
#bookname=shabda-sAgara (sa-en)
#stripmethod=keep
#sametypesequence=h
#description=Data from https://www.sanskrit-lexicon.uni-koeln.de/ as on 2026-09-26

अ|अं|अः
अ The first letter of the alphabet, and inherent short vowel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=001-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अ|अं|अः
अ ind.<BR>	 1. NO, not.<BR>	 2. A private, pr२ohibitive, and diminutive<BR>particle.<BR>	 3. An interjection of pity. It also implies degrees of<BR>difference, and similarity. As a negative prefix to words<BR>beginning with a vowel, अ is changed to अन्, as अ and अन्त<BR>form अनन्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=001-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अ|अं|अः
अ m. (अः) A name of VIṢṆU.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=001-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अऋणिन्
अऋणिन् mfn. (-णी-णिणी-णि) Free from debt or obligation; also<BR>अनृणिन्<BR> E. अ neg. ऋणिन् a debtor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=001-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंश|अंशः
अंश r. 10th cl. (अंशयति) To separate or divide. See अंस.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=001-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंश|अंशः
अंश m. (-शः)<BR>	 1. A share or portion.<BR>	 2. A part.<BR>	 3. A shoulder, the<BR>shoulder blade.<BR>	 4. (In arithmetic) a fraction.<BR>	 5. The nume-<BR>rator of a fraction.<BR>	 6. A degree of latitude or longitude, &c.<BR>See अंस.<BR> E. अंश to divide, अच् affix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=001-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंशक|अंशकं|अंशकः
अंशक m. (-कः) A kinsman, a relation, a co-heir.<BR>	 n. (-कं) A day. E.<BR>अंश to separate or divide, and वुन् affix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=001-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंशभाज्
अंशभाज् mfn. (भाक्) An heir, a co-heir, one who has a share or<BR>portion.<BR> E. अंश and भाज् who possesses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=001-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंशन|अंशनं
अंशन n. (-नं) Dividing, sharing.<BR> E. अंश and युच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=001-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंशनीय
अंशनीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) To be divided, divisible.<BR> E. अंश and.<BR>अनीयर aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=001-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंशमान
अंशमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Dividing, sharing.<BR> E. अंश and शानच् aff<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=001-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंशयत्
अंशयत् mfn. (-यन्-यती-यत्) Dividing, sharing.<BR> E. अंश and यति<BR>affix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=001-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंशयितव्य
अंशयितव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं) Divisible, to be divided.<BR> E. अंश and<BR>तव्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=001-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंशयितृ
अंशयितृ mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ) Dividing, sharing.<BR> E. अंश and शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=001-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंशल|अंशलः
अंशल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Strong, stout, lusty. See अंसल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=001-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंशहर
अंशहर mfn. (-रः-रा-री-रं) A sharer, a divider, a co-heir.<BR> E. अंश and<BR>हर who takes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=001-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंशहारिन्
अंशहारिन् mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि) A sharer, a co-heir.<BR> E. अंश and हारिन् who<BR>takes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=001-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंशांश|अंशांशः
अंशांश m. (-शः) Part of a portion or share.<BR> E. अंश repeated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=001-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंशांशि
अंशांशि ind. Share by share.<BR> E. अंश repeated and इ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=001-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंशित
अंशित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Divided, portioned, shared.<BR> E. अंश and<BR>क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=001-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंशिन्
अंशिन् mfn. (-शी-शिनी-शि) A sharer, a coheir.<BR> E. अंश and इनि<BR>poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=001-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंश्य
अंश्य mfn. (-श्यः-श्या-श्यं) Divisible, to be shared or divided.<BR> E. अंश<BR>and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=001-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंशु|अंशुः
अंशु m. (-शुः)<BR>	 1. A ray of light, a sun-beam.<BR>	 2. Light, splendor,<BR>effulgence.<BR>	 3. Dress, decoration.<BR>	 4. A small filament or end<BR>of thread.<BR>	 5. The sun.<BR>	 6. A minute particle or atom.<BR> E. अंश<BR>to divide, कु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=001-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंशुक|अंशुकं
अंशुक n. (-कं)<BR>	 1. Fine cloth, muslin.<BR>	 2. A mantle, a wrapper, a<BR>robe, a linen garment worn round the upper part of the body.<BR>3. Cloth in general.<BR>	 4. White cloth, 5. A leaf.<BR> E. अंश and कन्<BR>added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=001-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंशुजाल
अंशुजाल n. (-लं)<BR>	 1. A collection or blaze of light.<BR>	 2. A parcel or<BR>pencil of rays.<BR> E. अंशु and जाल a net.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=001-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंशुधर|अंशुधरः
अंशुधर m. (-रः) The sun.<BR> E. अंशु and धर who holds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=001-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंशुभर्तृ|अंशुभर्त्तृ
अंशुभर्तृ m. (-र्त्ता) The sun.<BR> E. अंशु and भर्तृ lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=001-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंशुमत्|अंशुमन्त्
अंशुमत् mfn. (-मान-मती-मत्)<BR>	 1. Radiant, luminous.<BR>	 2. Acuminated,<BR>pointed.<BR>	 m. (-मान्)<BR>	 1. The sun.<BR>	 2. A prince of the solar race, son<BR>of ASAMANJAS, grandson of SĀGARA. (-ती) A plant, (Hedysarum<BR>Gangeticum.)<BR> E. अंशु and मतुप् poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=001-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंशुमत्फला
अंशुमत्फला f. (-ला) The plantain, (Musa paradisiaca.)<BR> E. अंशुमत् and<BR>फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=001-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंशुमाला
अंशुमाला f. (-ला) A garland of light, a halo.<BR> E. अंशु and माला a<BR>garland.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=001-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंशुमालिन्
अंशुमालिन् m. (-ली) The sun.<BR> E. अंशुमाला and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=001-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंशुल|अंशुलः
अंशुल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Radiant, splendid.<BR> E. अंशु and लच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=001-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंशुबाण|अंशुबाणः
अंशुबाण m. (-णः) The sun.<BR> E. अंशु and बाण an arrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=001-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंशुहस्त|अंशुहस्तः
अंशुहस्त m. (-लः) The sun.<BR> E. अंशु and हस्त the hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=001-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंस|अंसः
अंस r. 10th cl. (-अंसयति) To separate or divide; also written अंश.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=001-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंस|अंसः
अंस m. (-सः)<BR>	 1. A shoulder, a scapula.<BR>	 2. A part, a portion.<BR> E. अंस to<BR>divide, अच् aff. it is also written अंश.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=001-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंसकूट|अंसकूटः
अंसकूट m. (-टः) A bull's hump, the protuberance between the shoul-<BR>ders of the Indian ox.<BR> E. अंस the shoulder, and कूट a peak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=001-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंसल|अंसलः
अंसल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Strong, stout, lusty.<BR> E. अंस the shoulder, and<BR>लच् aff. also written अंशल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=001-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंहति|अंहतिः
अंहति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. A gift, a donation.<BR>	 2. Sickness, disease.<BR>	 3. Leaving,<BR>abandoning.<BR>	 4. A gift.<BR> E. अहि to go, क्तिन् affix or अंह for हन to kill,<BR>and अति Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=001-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंहती
अंहती f. (-ती) A gift or donation. E. See अंहति, इ being made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=001-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंहस्
अंहस् n. (-हः) Sin. See अङ्घस्.<BR> E. अम to go, and the Uṇādi affix. असुन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=001-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंहिति|अंहितिः
अंहिति f. (-तिः) A gift or donation. E. See अंहति, इट् being inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=001-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंह्रि|अंह्रिः
अंह्रि m. (-ह्रिः)<BR>	 1. A foot.<BR>	 2. The root of a tree.<BR> E. अहि to go, and क्रिण्<BR>Uṇādi affix: also अङ्घ्रि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=001-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंह्रिप|अंह्रिपः
अंह्रिप m. (-पः) A tree.<BR> E. अंह्रि the root, and प from पा to drink.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=001-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंह्रिस्कन्ध|अंह्रिस्कंध|अंह्रिस्कन्धः
अंह्रिस्कन्ध m. (-न्धः) The heel.<BR> E. अंह्रि the foot, and स्कन्ध the shoulder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=002-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक|अकं
अक r. 1st. cl. (अकति)<BR>	 1. To wind or move tortuously. With an in-<BR>dicatory इ. अकि (अंकते)<BR>	 1. To mark or bespot.<BR>	 2. To go. See अङ्क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=002-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक|अकं
अक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. Moving tortuously.<BR>	 2. One who goes crookedly.<BR>	 3. Pain,<BR>affliction.<BR>	 4. Sin.<BR> E. अ priv. and क happiness, or अक to move<BR>crookedly, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=002-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकच|अकचः
अकच m. (-चः) Name of KETU, the dragon's tail, or descending node.<BR>mfn. (-चः-चा-चं) Bald, destitute of hair.<BR> E. अ priv. and कच hair;<BR>this applies to KETU, as the symbol of the asterism is a headless<BR>trunk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=002-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकण्टक
अकण्टक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Free from thorns, literally or metaphorically.<BR>E. अ priv. कण्टक a thorn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=002-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकथ्य|अकथ्यः
अकथ्य mfn. (-थ्यः-थ्या-थ्यं) Not to be mentioned or spoken of; also<BR>similar forms as अकथनीय &c.<BR> E. अ neg. कथ to speak, with the<BR>participle affixes यत् अनीयर् &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=002-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकनिष्ठ|अकनिष्ठः
अकनिष्ठ m. (-ष्ठः) A deified saint according to the Bauddhas.<BR>	 mfn.<BR>(-ष्ठः-ष्ठा-ष्ठं) Elder, superior.<BR> E. अ priv. and कनिष्ठ youngest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=002-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकनिष्ठग|अकनिष्ठगः
अकनिष्ठग m. (-ग) A deified saint according to the Bauddhas. E.<BR>अकनिष्ठ superior and गम to go affix ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=002-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकम्पित|अकंपित|अकम्पितः
अकम्पित m. (-तः) The name of a Jaina saint, one of the pupils of the<BR>last Tīrthaṅkara.<BR>	 mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Firm, unshaken, not agitated or<BR>trembling.<BR> E. अ priv. कपि to tremble; the participial affix क्त. and<BR>इट् inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=002-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकर
अकर mfn. (-रः-रा-री-रं)<BR>	 1. Maimed, handless.<BR>	 2. Privileged, exempt<BR>from tax or duty.<BR>	 3. One who does not act.<BR> E. अ priv. and कर the<BR>hand, tax, duty.<BR>	 f. (-रा) Emblic myrobalan, (Phyllanthus<BR>emblica.)<BR> E. अ priv. and कृञ to injure, अन् affix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=002-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकरणि|अकरणिः
अकरणि m. (-णिः) Failure, disappointment, (it is used only as an<BR>imprecation,) as तस्याकरणिरेवास्तु may he fail.<BR> E. अ priv. कृञ to do,<BR>and अनि affix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=002-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकरणीय
अकरणीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Not to be done, improper or impracticable.<BR>E. अ neg. करणीय to be done.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=002-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकरुण|अकरुणः
अकरुण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Unfeeling, void of compassion or tenderness.<BR>E. अ neg. करुणा tenderness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=002-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकर्क्कश|अकर्कश|अकर्कशः
अकर्क्कश mfn. (-शः-शा-शं) Soft, not hard.<BR> E. अ priv. and कर्क्कश hard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=002-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकर्ण|अकर्णः|अकर्ण्ण
अकर्ण mfn. (-र्ण-र्णा-र्णं) Deaf.<BR> E. अ priv. and कर्ण the ear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=002-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकर्त्तन|अकर्तन|अकर्त्तनः
अकर्त्तन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) A dwarf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=002-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकर्त्तव्य|अकर्तव्य|अकर्त्तव्यं
अकर्त्तव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं) Not to be done, improper, impracticable.<BR>E. अ neg. कर्त्तव्य to be done.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=002-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकर्म्मण्य|अकर्मण्य|अकर्म्मण्यं
अकर्म्मण्य mfn. (-ण्यः-ण्या-ण्यं) Not to be done, improper.<BR> E. अ neg. कर्म्मन्<BR>act, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=002-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकर्म्मन्|अकर्मन्
अकर्म्मन् mfn. (-र्म्मा-र्म्मा-र्म्म)<BR>	 1. Idle, unoccupied, without work.<BR>	 2. Degraded,<BR>no longer performing essential rites.<BR>	 n. (र्म्म)<BR>	 1. Absence of occupa-<BR>tion.<BR>	 2. Loss or neglect of essential observances.<BR>	 3. Improper act,<BR>crime, offence.<BR> E. अ neg. कर्म्मन् act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=002-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकर्म्मकृत्|अकर्मकृत्
अकर्म्मकृत् mfn. (-कृत्) Free from action, necessary as vital, or essential<BR>as religious.<BR> E. अ neg. कर्म्म act, कृत् who does.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=002-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकल्क
अकल्क mfn. (-ल्कः-ल्का-ल्कं)<BR>	 1. Clear, clean.<BR>	 2. Pure, sinless.<BR>	 3. Free from<BR>sediment.<BR>	 f. (-ल्का) Moonlight.<BR> E. अ priv and कल्क dirt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=002-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकल्कन|अकल्कनः
अकल्कन mfn. (न-ना-नं) Humble, not proud, (this word is sometimes<BR>written अकल्कलः)<BR> E. अ priv. कल्क pride, and न or ल aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=002-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकल्पित|अकल्पितः
अकल्पित mfn. (-तं-ता-तः) Natural, not artificial, not made.<BR> E. अ neg.<BR>कल्पित made.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=002-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकल्मष
अकल्मष mfn. (-षः-षा-षं) Faultless, sinless.<BR> E. अ priv. कल्मष sin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=002-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकल्य|अकल्यः
अकल्य mfn. (-ल्य-ल्या-ल्यं) Sick, diseased.<BR> E. अ priv. कल्य well.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=002-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकल्याण|अकल्याणं
अकल्याण mfn. (-ण-णी-णं) Unlucky, inauspicious.<BR> E. अ neg. कल्याण<BR>prosperous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=002-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकस्मात्
अकस्मात् ind.<BR>	 1. Immediately, instantly, presently.<BR>	 2. Without a cause,<BR>without a wherefore.<BR> E. अ neg. कस्मात् from what.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=002-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकाण्ड|अकांड
अकाण्ड mfn. (-ण्डः-ण्डा-ण्डं) Sudden, unexpected.<BR> E. अ neg. काण्ड a stem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=002-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकाण्डजात
अकाण्डजात mfn. (-तं-ता-तः) Suddenly born or produced.<BR> E. अकाण्ड<BR>and जात born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=002-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकाण्डपातजात
अकाण्डपातजात mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Perishing suddenly after birth, dying<BR>as soon as born<BR> E. अकाण्ड, अनद पात perishing, जात born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=002-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकारण|अकारणं
अकारण n. (-णं) Absence or nonexistence of a cause. (Used adverb<BR>ally,) Causelessly.<BR> E. अ neg. कारण cause.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=002-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकारणोत्पन्न
अकारणोत्पन्न mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं) Born or produced without a cause. E.<BR>अकारण and उत्पन्न born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=002-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकार्य्य|अकार्य|अकार्य्यं
अकार्य्य mfn. (-र्य्यः-र्य्या-र्य्यं) Improper not to be done.<BR>	 n. (र्य्यं) An impro-<BR>per act.<BR> E. अ neg. कार्य्य to be done.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=002-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकाल|अकालः
अकाल m. (-लः) Irregular or unusual, as time or season.<BR> E. अ neg.<BR>काल time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=002-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकालकुसुम
अकालकुसुम n. (मः) A flower budding out of season.<BR> E. अकाल and कुमुम<BR>a flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=002-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकालज|अकालजः
अकालज mfn. (-जः-जा-जं) Unseasonable, produced out of time or<BR>season; also अकालजात, अकालोत्पन्न and similar compounds.<BR> E. अकाल<BR>with ज or जात &c. born or produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=002-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकालजलदोदय|अकालजलदोदयः
अकालजलदोदय m. (यः)<BR>	 1. A fog, or mist.<BR>	 2. Unseasonable gathering<BR>of clouds,<BR> E. अ priv. and काल time, जलद a cloud, and उदय<BR>rising.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=002-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकालमेघोदय|अकालमेघोदयः
अकालमेघोदय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. Unseasonable cloudiness.<BR>	 2. A fog or mist. E.<BR>अकाल with मेघ a cloud, and उदय rising.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=002-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकालसह
अकालसह mfn. (-हः-हा-हं) Impatient, premature, not waiting for<BR>the proper season.<BR> E. अ neg. कालसह time-enduring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=002-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकिञ्चन|अकिंचन|अकिञ्चनः
अकिञ्चन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Poor, indigent.<BR> E. अ priv. and किञ्चन any<BR>thing, something.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=002-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकिञ्चनता|अकिंचनता
अकिञ्चनता f. (-ता) Voluntary poverty, one of the duties of a Jaina<BR>ascetic.<BR> E. अकिञ्चन and ता affix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=002-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकिल्विष|अकिल्विषः
अकिल्विष mfn. (-षः-षा-षं) Faultless, free from sin.<BR> E. अ priv. किल्विष<BR>fault.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=002-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकीर्त्ति|अकीर्ति|अकीर्तिः|अकीर्त्तिः
अकीर्त्ति f. (र्त्तिः) Infamy, disgrace.<BR> E. अ reverse, कीर्त्ति fame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=002-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकुत्सित
अकुत्सित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Unreproached, respectable.<BR> E. अ neg. कुत्सित<BR>bad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=002-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकुप्य|अकुप्यं
अकुप्य n. (-प्यं) Gold or silver.<BR> E. अ neg. and कुप्य base metal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=002-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकुल|अकुलः
अकुल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Low, mean, of low family.<BR> E. अ neg. कुल<BR>family.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=002-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकुलीन
अकुलीन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Low, mean, of low origin or race.<BR> E. अ neg.<BR>कुलीन of family.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=002-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकुशल
अकुशल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>	 1. Unlucky, inauspicious.<BR>	 2. Clumsy, not clever.<BR>E. अ neg. कुशल lucky, clever.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=002-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकूपार|अकूपारः
अकूपार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. The sea or ocean.<BR>	 2. A tortoise.<BR>	 3. The king of<BR>turtles, the tortoise supposed to uphold the world.<BR>	 4. A stone or<BR>rock. अ neg. कू the earth, and पृ to cherish. or अ neg. कू for कुत्सित<BR>contemptible, vile, and पार bank, boundary: there are other<BR>etymologies, and वृ being substituted for पृ the word is sometimes<BR>written अकूवार.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=002-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकूर्च्च|अकूर्च|अकूर्चः|अकूर्च्चः
अकूर्च्च m. (-र्च्चः) A deified saint, according to the Bauddhas.<BR>	 mfn.<BR>(-र्च्चः-र्च्चा-र्च्चं) Void of guile.<BR> E. अ priv. and कूर्च्च fraud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=002-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकृत|अकृतं
अकृत mfn. (तः-ता-तं) Undone neglected incomplete.<BR>	 n. (-तं) Any<BR>act unperformed.<BR> E. अ neg. कृत done.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=002-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकृतज्ञ|अकृतज्ञः
अकृतज्ञ mfn. (-ज्ञः-ज्ञा-ज्ञं) Ungrateful.<BR> E. अ neg. कृतज्ञ grateful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=002-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकृतज्ञता
अकृतज्ञता f. (-ता) Ingratitude.<BR> E. ता added to अकृतज्ञ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=002-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकृतज्ञत्व
अकृतज्ञत्व n. (-त्वं) Ingratitude.<BR> E. त्व added to अकृतज्ञ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=002-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकृतात्मन्
अकृतात्मन् mfn. (-त्मा-त्मा-त्म) Not identified or made one with oneself,<BR>especially in a spiritual sense, not one with spirit, or God. E.<BR>अकृत unmade, आत्मन् self.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=002-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकृतित्व|अकृतित्वं
अकृतित्व n. (त्वं,) Awkwardness, clumsiness, unfitness.<BR> E. अकृतिन् and<BR>त्व aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=002-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकृतिन्
अकृतिन् mfn. (-ती-तिनी-ति) Awkward, stupid, incapable of or unfit<BR>for doing any thing.<BR> E. अ neg. कृ to do, इन् aff. and त augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=002-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकृत्रिम|अकृत्रिमं
अकृत्रिम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं) Natural, inartificial, not made.<BR> E. अ neg.<BR>कृत्रिम artificial.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=003-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकृप|अकृपः
अकृप mfn. (-पः-पा-पं) Unmerciful, unkind.<BR> E. अ neg. कृपा mercy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=003-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकृपण|अकृपणः
अकृपण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Liberal, not miserly.<BR> E. अ neg. कृपण miserly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=003-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकृश
अकृश mfn. (-शः-शा-शं)<BR>	 1. Full, entire.<BR>	 2. Strong, fierce.<BR> E. अ neg. कृश<BR>little.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=003-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकृष्णकर्म्मन्|अकृष्णकर्मन्
अकृष्णकर्म्मन् mfn. (-र्म्मा-र्म्मा-र्म्मं) Innocent.<BR> E. अ neg. and कृष्णकर्म्मन् guilty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=003-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकेश|अकेशः
अकेश mfn. (-शः-शा-शं) Bald, hairless.<BR> E. अ neg. केश hair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=003-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकोट|अकोटः
अकोट m. (-टः) The betel-nut tree. (Areca faufel or catechu.)<BR> E. अ<BR>neg. and कुट to be crooked, because it grows with a straight<BR>stem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=003-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकोविद|अकोविदः
अकोविद mfn. (-दः-दा-दं) Stupid, ignorant.<BR> E. अ neg. कोविद clever.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=003-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्का
अक्का f. (-क्का) A mother.<BR> E. अक pain, कै to sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=003-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्त|अक्तः
अक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>	 1. Joined, combined.<BR>	 2. Gone.<BR>	 3. Spread abroad.<BR>4. Anointed.<BR> E. अञ्ज to go. and क्त affix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=003-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्तु|अक्तुः
अक्तु f. (क्तुः) Night, (on the authority of the Vedas.)<BR> E. अञ्ज to go, and<BR>क्तु affix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=003-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्रम|अक्रमः
अक्रम m. (मः) Want of order or arrangement, confusion, irregularity.<BR>E. अ priv. and क्रम order.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=003-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्रान्त|अक्रांत
अक्रान्त mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं)<BR>	 1. Unpassed, unsurpassed.<BR>	 2. Unconquered.<BR>(-न्तः) The egg-plant. (Solanum melongena.)<BR> E. अ neg. and क्रान्त<BR>passed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=003-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्रोध|अक्रोधः
अक्रोध m. (-धः) Dispassionateness, restraint of anger, one of the ten<BR>duties of an ascetic.<BR>	 mfn. (-धः-धा-धं) Dispassionate.<BR> E. अ neg.<BR>and क्रोध anger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=003-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्रिय|अक्रियः
अक्रिय mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>	 1. Inactive, dull, torpid.<BR>	 2. Abstaining from<BR>religious rites.<BR>	 f. (या) Inactivity, neglect of what ought to be<BR>done.<BR> E. अ neg. क्रिया act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=003-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्रियत्व
अक्रियत्व n. (-त्वं) Inactivity, torpor. त्व added to the preceding. also<BR>अक्रियता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=003-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्रूर|अक्रूरः
अक्रूर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Gentle, not cruel.<BR>	 m. (-रः) The paternal<BR>uncle and friend of KṚṢṆA.<BR> E. अ neg. क्रूर cruel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=003-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्लेद्य
अक्लेद्य mfn. (-द्यः-द्या-द्यं)<BR>	 1. Incapable of distress or pain.<BR>	 2. Unfit to be<BR>pained or distressed.<BR> E. अ neg. क्लेद्य to be pained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=003-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्लम
अक्लम m. (-मः) Absence of weariness or fatigue.<BR> E. अ priv. and क्लम<BR>fatigue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=003-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्लान्त|अक्लान्तः
अक्लान्त mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं) Unwearied.<BR> E. अ neg. and क्लान्त wearied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=003-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्लिष्ट
अक्लिष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>	 1. Unvexed, not distressed or annoyed.<BR>	 2.<BR>Unwearied, indefatigable.<BR> E. अ neg. क्लिष्ट wearied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=003-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्लेश|अक्लेशं|अक्लेशः
अक्लेश m. (-शः) Absence of weariness or vexation.<BR> E. अ neg. क्लेश<BR>distress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=003-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्लिका
अक्लिका f. (-का) The indigo plant. (Indigofera tinctoria.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=003-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्ष|अक्षं|अक्षः
अक्ष r. 1st and 3d cl. (अक्षति अक्ष्णति)<BR>	 1. To reach or obtain.<BR>	 2. To<BR>pervade.<BR>	 3. To accumulate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=003-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्ष|अक्षं|अक्षः
अक्ष m. (-क्षः)<BR>	 1. A die, cubic or oblong, for playing with.<BR>	 2. Part of a<BR>car.<BR>	 3. A wheel.<BR>	 4. A car.<BR>	 5. A snake.<BR>	 6. Law suit, legal proceedings<BR>7. Sacred knowledge, 8. The soul.<BR>	 9. A seed of which Rosaries are<BR>made, in which sense it occurs mostly in composition, as Rudrākṣa, Indrākṣa.<BR>10. A Karṣa or weight of sixteen māṣas.<BR>	 11.<BR>A tree bearing a medicinal fruit. (Terminalia belerica.)<BR>	 12. A<BR>proper name, the son of RAVANA.<BR>	 13. A name of GARUḌA.<BR>	 14. A<BR>person born blind.<BR>	 15. Terrestrial latitude.<BR>	 n. (-क्षं)<BR>	 1. An organ of<BR>sense.<BR>	 2. Sea, salt.<BR>	 3. Blue vitriol<BR> E. अशु to pervade, Uṇādi affix स.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=003-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षक|अक्षकः
अक्षक m. (-कः) A tree. (Dalbergia Oujeiniensis, Rox.)<BR> E. अक्ष Beleric<BR>myrobalan, and क affix: from its resembling that plant; or the<BR>termination being a pleonastic affix, the word may have all the<BR>senses of the preceding: also read अक्षिक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=003-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षकर्ण|अक्षकर्णः
अक्षकर्ण n. (-र्णः)<BR>	 1. The hypotenuse, especially of the triangle formed<BR>with the gnomon of a dial and its shadow.<BR>	 2. (In astronomy.)<BR>Argument of the latitude.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=003-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षत|अक्षतं|अक्षतः
अक्षत n. (-तं)<BR>	 1. Fried grain, (in this sense it is also used in the mas.<BR>plu. (-ताः)<BR>	 2. A eunuch.<BR>	 3. Whole grain.<BR>	 f. (-ता) A plant, named<BR>also Kankara Sringi.<BR>	 mfn. (-त-ता-तः)<BR>	 1. Uninjured, unhurt.<BR>	 2.<BR>Whole, unbroken.<BR> E. अ neg. and क्षत torn, broken &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=003-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षतयोनि|अक्षतयोनिः
अक्षतयोनि f. (-निः) A virgin.<BR> E. अक्षत and योनि pudendum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=003-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षदर्शक|अक्षदर्शकः
अक्षदर्शक m. (-कः) A judge.<BR> E. अक्ष a lawsuit, दर्शक who sees; from<BR>दृश to see.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=003-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षद्यू
अक्षद्यू m. (-द्यूः) A gambler, a dicer.<BR> E. अक्ष dice and द्यू who plays.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=003-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षद्यूत
अक्षद्यूत m. (-तः) A gambler, a dicer.<BR>	 n. (-तं) Gambling.<BR> E. अक्ष and<BR>द्यूत play or who plays: also अक्षद्यूत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=003-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षद्यूतिक
अक्षद्यूतिक n. (-कं) Dispute at play.<BR> E. अक्ष and द्यूत with टक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=003-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षदृश्
अक्षदृश् m. (-दृक्) A judge.<BR> E. अक्ष a lawsuit, and दृश् who sees.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=003-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षदेविन्
अक्षदेविन् m. (-वी) A gamester.<BR> E. अक्ष a dice, and देविन् a player.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=003-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षधर|अक्षधरः
अक्षधर m. (-रः) A plant, (Trophis aspera.) See साखोट.<BR>	 mfn. (-रः-रा-<BR>री-रं) One who holds dice &c.<BR> E. अक्ष and धर what holds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=003-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षधूर्त्त|अक्षधूर्त|अक्षधूर्तः|अक्षधूर्त्तः
अक्षधूर्त्त m. (-र्त्तः) A gamester, a gambler.<BR> E. अक्ष dice, and धूर्त्त a rogue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=003-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षधूर्त्तिल|अक्षधूर्तिल|अक्षधूर्तिलः
अक्षधूर्त्तिल m. (-लः) A bull, an ox.<BR> E. अक्ष a cart, धूर् its forepart, or<BR>धुर् a load, and तिल affix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=003-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षपाट|अक्षपाटः
अक्षपाट m. (-टः) An arena, a boxing or wrestling ground; also read<BR>अक्षवाट.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=003-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षपाटक|अक्षपाटकः
अक्षपाटक m. (-कः) A judge.<BR> E. अक्ष lawsuit, and पाट to arrange<BR>affix वुन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=003-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षपाटिक
अक्षपाटिक m. (-कः) A judge. E. as before with टक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=003-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षपाद|अक्षपादः
अक्षपाद m. (-दः) A follower of the Nyaya system of philosophy.<BR> E. अक्ष<BR>contest, and पाद who goes; the Nyaya is the logical school; also<BR>आक्षपाद.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=003-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षभाग|अक्षभागः
अक्षभाग m. (-गः) A degree of latitude.<BR> E. अक्ष and भाग a part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=003-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षम|अक्षमः
अक्षम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>	 1. Impatient, intolerant.<BR>	 2. Unable, incompet-<BR>ent, impotent f. (-मा)<BR>	 1. Impatience, intolerance.<BR>	 2. Envy,<BR>impatience of another's success.<BR>	 3. Inability, incapacity.<BR> E. अ neg.<BR>क्षमा patience.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=003-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षमता
अक्षमता f. (-ता) Impatience, &c. See the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=003-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षमत्व
अक्षमत्व n. (-त्वं) Impatience, &c. See अक्षम.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=003-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षमाला
अक्षमाला f. (-ला)<BR>	 1. A rosary, a string of beads, especially of the seeds<BR>of the Eleocarpus.<BR>	 2. The name of ARUNDHATĪ, wife of VASIṢṬHA,<BR>(from her wearing a rosary.)<BR> E. अक्ष a kind of seed or bead,<BR>and माला a necklace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=003-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षय|अक्षयः
अक्षय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Durable, permanent, imperishable.<BR>	 f. (-या)<BR>The seventh day of a lunar month, which happens on a Sunday<BR>or Monday, and the fourth, which falls on a Wednesday.<BR> E. अ<BR>neg. and क्ष to waste or decay, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=003-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षयता
अक्षयता f. (-ता) Durability, imperishableness.<BR> E. ता added to the<BR>preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=003-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षयतृतीया
अक्षयतृतीया f. (-या) The third day of the lunar half of the month of<BR>Vaiśākha. (April-May.)<BR> E. अक्षय durable, and तृतीया the third<BR>day: the consequences of meritorious actions performed on this<BR>day being permanent, as it is the first day of the Satya Yuga or<BR>the anniversary of creation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=003-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षयत्व
अक्षयत्व n. (-त्वं) Imperishableness.<BR> E. त्व added to अक्षय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=003-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षयलोक|अक्षयलोकः
अक्षयलोक m. (-कः) Heaven, the imperishable world or region.<BR> E. अक्षय<BR>and लोक world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=003-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षर|अक्षरं|अक्षरः
अक्षर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A name of ŚIVA.<BR>	 2. A name of VIṢṆU.<BR>	 n. (-रं)<BR>BRAHMĀ the supreme being, (in this sense it is sometimes mas.)<BR>2. Eternal beatitude, or exemption from further transmigration.<BR>	 3.<BR>Religious austerity.<BR>	 4. Moral merit.<BR>	 5. The sky or atmosphere.<BR>6. A letter of the alphabet.<BR>	 7. A plant. (Achyranthes aspera.)<BR>	 8.<BR>Water (in the dialect of the Vedas.)<BR>	 mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>	 1. Unal-<BR>terable.<BR>	 2. Unperishable, undecayable.<BR> E. अशू to pervade, and सर<BR>Uṇādi affix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=003-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षरचञ्च|अक्षरचञ्चः
अक्षरचञ्च m. (ञ्चः) A scribe, a writer.<BR> E. अक्षर letter, and चञ्च affix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=003-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षरचण|अक्षरचणः
अक्षरचण m. (-णः) A scribe.<BR> E. अक्षर a letter, and चण affix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=004-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षरचन|अक्षरचनः
अक्षरचन m. (-नः) A scribe. E. See the last word.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=004-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षरचुञ्चु|अक्षरचुंचु|अक्षरचुञ्चुः
अक्षरचुञ्चु m. (ञ्चुः) A scribe, a writer. See अक्षरचञ्च.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=004-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षरजननी
अक्षरजननी f. (-नी) A pen.<BR> E. अक्षर a letter, and जननी a mother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=004-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षरजीवक|अक्षरजीवकः
अक्षरजीवक m. (-कः) A scribe.<BR> E. अक्षर a letter, and जीवक who lives,<BR>i. e. who gets a livelihood by letters; also अक्षरजीविक and<BR>अक्षरजीविन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=004-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षरतूलिका
अक्षरतूलिका f. (-का) A pen.<BR> E. अक्षर a letter, and तूलिका a brush.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=004-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षरविन्यास|अक्षरविन्यासः
अक्षरविन्यास m. (सः)<BR>	 1. Scripture, a writing.<BR>	 2. The alphabet.<BR> E. अक्षर<BR>a letter, and विन्यास assemblage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=004-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षरमुख|अक्षरमुखः
अक्षरमुख m. (-खः) A scholar, a student.<BR> E. अक्षर a letter, and मुख<BR>commencement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=004-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षरसंस्थान|अक्षरसंस्थानं
अक्षरसंस्थान n. (-नं) Scripture, a writing.<BR> E. अक्षर a letter, and संस्थान<BR>placing, collecting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=004-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षवत्|अक्षवन्त्
अक्षवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Having a die, &c.<BR>	 f. (-ती) Gaming,<BR>playing with dice.<BR> E. अक्ष a die, and मतुप् possessive affix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=004-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षवाट|अक्षवाटः
अक्षवाट m. (-टः) An amphitheatre for wrestling, the arena of a gymna-<BR>sium.<BR> E. अक्ष contest, and वाट an enclosure, an area.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=004-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षविद्
अक्षविद् mfn. (-वित्) Versed in law, or in play.<BR> E. अक्ष law or dice, and<BR>विद् who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=004-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षसूत्र|अक्षसूत्रं
अक्षसूत्र n. (-त्रं) A rosary, a string of eleocarpus seeds so used.<BR> E. अक्ष<BR>and सूत्र a thread.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=004-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षांश|अक्षांशः
अक्षांश m. (-शः) A degree of latitude.<BR> E. अक्ष and अंश a part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=004-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षाग्र
अक्षाग्र n. (-ग्रं)<BR>	 1. The forepart of a car.<BR>	 2. The axle or bar to which<BR>the wheels are attached.<BR> E. अक्ष and अग्र forepart.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=004-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षाग्रकीलक|अक्षाग्रकीलकः
अक्षाग्रकीलक m. (-कः) The pin of the axle of a carriage, the linchpin,<BR>also one at the extremity of the pole.<BR> E. अक्ष a cart, अग्र forepart,<BR>and कीलक a pin or bolt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=004-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षान्ति|अक्षांति|अक्षांतिः|अक्षान्तिः
अक्षान्ति f. (-न्तिः)<BR>	 1. Impatience, intolerance.<BR>	 2. Envy, impatience of<BR>another's superiority or success.<BR> E. अ neg. and क्षान्ति sufferance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=004-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षारलवण|अक्षारलवणं
अक्षारलवण n. (-णं) Such food as may be eaten during a season of<BR>mourning, religious observance, &c. as cow's milk, ghee, rice,<BR>kidney-beans, barley, sesamum, and sea or river salt.<BR> E. अ neg<BR>क्षार alkali, लवण salt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=004-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षि
अक्षि n. (-क्षि) The eye.<BR>	 n. अश् to pervade, and सि affix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=004-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षिक|अक्षिकः
अक्षिक m. (-कः) A tree, (Dalbergia Oujeiniensis.) See also अक्ष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=004-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षिकूटक|अक्षिकूटकः
अक्षिकूटक n. (-कः) The eyeball.<BR> E. अक्षि the eye, and कूटक a globe<BR>or ball.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=004-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षिगोल|अक्षिगोलः
अक्षिगोल m. (-लः) The ball or globe of the eye.<BR> E. अक्षि and गोल ball.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=004-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षिगत|अक्षिगतः
अक्षिगत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Hateful, hated, disliked.<BR> E. अक्षि the eye,<BR>and गत gone,<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=004-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षितारा
अक्षितारा f. (-रा) The pupil of the eye.<BR> E. अक्षि and तारा a star.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=004-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षिपक्ष्मन्
अक्षिपक्ष्मन् n. (-क्ष्म) The eyelash.<BR> E. अक्षि and पक्ष्मन् lash.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=004-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षिपटल
अक्षिपटल n. (-लं) A coat of the eye.<BR> E. अक्षि and पटल a coat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=004-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षिभेषज|अक्षिभेषजः
अक्षिभेषज m. (-जः) A tree, (Pale Lodh.) See गालव.<BR>	 n. (-वं) Any medi-<BR>cament or collyrium for the eye.<BR> E. अक्षि the eye, and भेषज a remedy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=004-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षिव|अक्षिवः
अक्षिव m. (-वः) A plant. (Morunga.)<BR>	 n. (-वं) Sea-salt. See अक्षीव.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=004-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षिविकूशित
अक्षिविकूशित n. (-तं) A glance or side look; one with the eyelids<BR>partly closed.<BR> E. अक्षि the eye, and कूशित from कूश to contract,<BR>with वि prefixed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=004-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षीव|अक्षीवं|अक्षीवः
अक्षीव m. (-वः) A plant. (Guilandina or Hyperanthera morunga.)<BR>	 n.<BR>(वं) Sea-salt.<BR> E. अक्ष to pervade, ईव aff: it is also written अक्षिव<BR>and अक्षीव.<BR>	 mfn. (-वः-वा-वं) Sober, not intoxicated.<BR> E. अ neg. and<BR>क्षीव intoxicated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=004-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षुण्ण|अक्षुण्णः
अक्षुण्ण mfn. (-ण्णः-ण्णा-ण्णं)<BR>	 1. Unparted, uncut, not communicated.<BR>	 2.<BR>Inexpert.<BR>	 3. Unconquered.<BR> E. अ neg. क्षुण्ण cut.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=004-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षुण्णता
अक्षुण्णता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Entireness, fulness.<BR>	 2. Want of practice or con-<BR>versancy.<BR> E. अ neg. क्षुण्णता spareness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=004-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षुब्ध|अक्षुब्धः
अक्षुब्ध mfn. (-ब्धः-ब्धा-ब्धं) Unshaken, undisturbed, unagitated.<BR> E. अ<BR>neg. and क्षुब्ध shaken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=004-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षोट|अक्षोटः
अक्षोट m. (-टः)<BR>	 1. A tree, (described as a pilu, growing in the hills.)<BR>See पीलुः 2. A walnut.<BR>	 3. A tree bearing an oily nut, (Aleurites<BR>triloba) Also written आक्षोट,<BR> E. अक्ष to pervade, and ओट aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=004-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षोड|अक्षोडः
अक्षोड m. (-डः) See the preceding word, also आखोड,<BR> E. अक्ष to<BR>pervade, and ओड aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=004-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षोडक|अक्षोडकः
अक्षोडक m. (-कः) See अक्षोड,<BR> E. अक्षोड and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=004-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षोभ|अक्षोभः
अक्षोभ m. (-भः)<BR>	 1. Firmness, absence of agitation.<BR>	 2. The post to<BR>which an elephant is tied.<BR>	 mfn. (-भः-भा-भं) Unshaken, unagitated,<BR>E. अ priv. क्षोभ shaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=004-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षोभित
अक्षोभित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Unshaken, unagitated, firm.<BR> E. अ neg.<BR>and क्षोभित shaken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=004-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षौहिणी
अक्षौहिणी f. (-णी) A complete army, consisting of 1, 09, 350 foot,<BR>65, 610 horses, 21, 870 chariots, and 21, 870 elephants.<BR> E. अक्ष<BR>a carriage, ऊहिणी assemblage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=004-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्ष्ण|अक्ष्णं
अक्ष्ण n. (-क्ष्णं) Time.<BR> E. अश to eat, and क्स्न Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=004-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अखट्टिः|अखट्टि
अखट्टिः m. (-ट्टिः) Childish fancy, whim, caprice.<BR> E. अ neg. and खट to<BR>desire, undesirable by the wise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=004-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अखण्ड|अखंड|अखण्डः
अखण्ड mfn. (-ण्डः-ण्डा-ण्डं) All, entire.<BR> E. अ neg. and खण्ड a part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=004-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अखण्डन|अखंडन|अखण्डनः
अखण्डन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Time.<BR>	 2. Leaving entire.<BR>	 3. Admitting, non-refutation.<BR>E. अ neg. खडि to break, and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=004-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अखण्डित|अखंडित
अखण्डित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Unbroken, undivided.<BR>	 2. Undisturbed,<BR>uninterrupted, continuous.<BR>	 3. Unrefuted.<BR> E. अ neg. खण्डित divided.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=004-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अखण्डितर्त्तु|अखण्डितर्तु|अखण्डितर्तुः|अखण्डितर्त्तुः
अखण्डितर्त्तु mfn. (-र्त्तुः-र्त्तुः-र्त्तु) Fruitful, bearing fruit in due season.<BR>E. अ neg. खण्डित broken, and ऋतु season.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=004-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अखात|अखातं|अखातः
अखात mn. (-तः-तं)<BR>	 1. A natural pond or lake.<BR>	 2. A pool before a<BR>temple, Sometimes written आखात,<BR> E. अ neg. and खात dug.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=004-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अखाद्य|अखाद्यं
अखाद्य mfn. (-द्यः-द्या-द्यं) Improper to be eaten.<BR> E. अ neg. खाद्य to be eaten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=004-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अखादित
अखादित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Uneaten.<BR> E. अ neg. खादित eaten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=004-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अखिन्न
अखिन्न mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं) Unwearied, indefatigable.<BR> E. अ neg. खिन्न wearied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=004-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अखिल|अखिलं
अखिल mfn. (लः-ला-लं) All, entire,<BR> E. अ neg, and खिल separated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=004-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अख्यात|अख्यातः
अख्यात mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Unknown, obscure, not famous or notorious. E.<BR>अ neg. ख्यात famed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=004-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अख्याति|अख्यातिः
अख्याति f. (-तिः) Disrepute, want of fame.<BR> E. अ neg. ख्याति fame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=004-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग|अगः
अग r. 1st cl. (अगति) To wind or move tortuously. See अक, With an<BR>indicatory इ, अति (अंगति) To go, move or approach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=004-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग|अगः
अग m. (-गः)<BR>	 1. A tree.<BR>	 2. The sun.<BR>	 3. A mountain.<BR>	 4. A snake.<BR>	 5.<BR>Moving crookedly, twining, twisting<BR> E. अ neg. and ग who goes,<BR>from गम to go, or अग to go tortuously. अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=004-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अगच्छ|अगच्छः|अगछ
अगच्छ m. (-च्छः) A tree.<BR> E. अ neg. and गच्छ, from गम to go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=004-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अगज|अगजं
अगज mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>	 1. Mountainous, produced on a mountain.<BR>	 2.<BR>Vegetable, produced from a tree.<BR> E. अग and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=004-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अगणनीय
अगणनीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Not to be numbered or reckoned, also अगण्य,<BR>अगणितव्य, &c.<BR> E. अ neg. गणनीय to be numbered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=004-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अगणित
अगणित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Not reckoned, uncounted.<BR> E. अ neg. गणित<BR>counted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=004-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अगद|अगदः
अगद m. (-दः) A medicament, a medicine, a drug.<BR>	 mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>1. Well, healthy, free from disease.<BR>	 2. Wholesome, salubrious. E.<BR>अ neg. and गद disease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=004-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अगदङ्कार|अगदंकार|अगदंकारः|अगदङ्कारः
अगदङ्कार m. (-रः) A physician.<BR> E. अगद well, healthy, and कार who<BR>makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=004-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अगन्तव्य
अगन्तव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं) Not to be visited or approached, also अगमनीय,<BR>अगम्य, &c.<BR> E. अ neg. गन्तव्य to be gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=004-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अगम|अगमः
अगम m. (-मः)<BR>	 1. A tree.<BR>	 2. A mountain.<BR> E. अ priv. and गम who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=004-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अगम्य|अगम्यं
अगम्य mfn. (-म्यः-म्या-म्यं)<BR>	 1. Not to be visited or approached.<BR>	 2. Difficult<BR>of acquirement, unattainable.<BR>	 3. Unequalled, unsurpassable.<BR> E. अ<BR>neg. गम्य to be gone to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=004-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अगम्यरूप
अगम्यरूप mfn. (-पः-पा-पं) Of superior and unequalled form or nature.<BR>E. अगम्य and रूप form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=004-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अगरी
अगरी f. (-री) A kind of grass, vulg. Deotar. See देवताड,<BR> E. अ neg.<BR>and गर poison: an antidote.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=004-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अगरु
अगरु mn. (-रुः-रु) Agallochum, (Aquilaria agallocha, Rox) See अगुरु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=005-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अगर्व्व|अगर्व
अगर्व्व mfn. (-र्व्वः-र्व्वा-र्व्वं) Modest, humble, void of pride.<BR> E. अ neg. गर्ब्ब pride.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=005-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अगस्ति|अगस्तिः
अगस्ति m. (-स्तिः)<BR>	 1. The name of a saint, celebrated in Hindu mytho-<BR>logy, more usually entitled AGASTYA, the son of both MITRA and<BR>VARUṆA, by URVASI; he is represented of short stature, and is<BR>said by some to have been born in a water jar: he is famed for<BR>having swallowed the ocean, when it had given him offence; at<BR>his command also, the VINDHYA range of mountains prostrated<BR>itself, and so remains; hence his present appellation: he is also<BR>considered as the regent of the star Canopus.<BR>	 2. The name of a<BR>tree, (Sesbana grandiflora.)<BR> E. अग a mountain, and स्ति, with an<BR>adventitious meaning, to fix, or in the second instance, to be<BR>fixed; also अग as before, and स्ति Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=005-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अगस्तिद्रु|अगस्तिद्रुः
अगस्तिद्रु m. (-द्रुः) A tree, (Sesbana grandiflora.) See अगस्ति.<BR> E. अगस्ति,<BR>and द्रु a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=005-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अगस्त्य|अगस्त्यः
अगस्त्य m. (स्त्यः)<BR>	 1. The name of a saint.<BR>	 2. A tree.<BR>	 3. The star Cano-<BR>pus. See अगस्ति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=005-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अगात्मजा
अगात्मजा f. (-जा) A name of PĀRVATĪ, the daughter of the mountain<BR>or Himālaya.<BR> E. अग a mountain, and आत्मजा daughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=005-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अगाध|अगाधं|अगाधः
अगाध n. (-धः) A hole, a chasm.<BR>	 mfn. (-धः-धा-धं) Very deep, bottom-<BR>less.<BR> E. अ neg. गाध fixed place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=005-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अगाधजल|अगाधजलः
अगाधजल m. (-लः) A lake.<BR> E. अगाध deep, जल water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=005-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अगाधता
अगाधता f. (-ता) Depth.<BR> E. अगाध and ता aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=005-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अगाधत्व
अगाधत्व n. (-त्वं) Depth.<BR> E. अगाध and त्व aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=005-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अगार|अगारं
अगार n. (-रं) A house. See आगार<BR> E. अग a mountain, and ऋ to go;<BR>rising like a hill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=005-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अगिन|अगिनः
अगिन m. (-नः) The sun.<BR> E. अग to go, इन aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=005-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अगिर|अगिरः
अगिर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. The sun.<BR>	 2. Fire.<BR>	 3. A demon.<BR> E. अग to go, and<BR>इर aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=005-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अगुण|अगुणः
अगुण m. (-णः) A defect, a fault.<BR>	 mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>	 1. Void of good<BR>qualities, bad.<BR>	 2. Void of attributes.<BR> E. अ neg. गुण qualities.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=005-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अगुणता
अगुणता f. (-ता) Absence of all good qualities; also अगुणत्वं.<BR> E. अ neg.<BR>गुण with ता or त्व aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=005-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अगुणवादिन्
अगुणवादिन् mfn. (-दी-दिनी-दि) Censorious, pointing out defects.<BR> E. अगुण<BR>and वादिन् declaring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=005-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अगुरु|अगुरुः
अगुरु mn. (-रुः-रु)<BR>	 1. A fragrant wood, aloe wood, or agallochum,<BR>(Aquilaria agallocha, Rox.)<BR>	 2. Another tree which produces Bede-<BR>llium, (Amyris agallocha.)<BR>	 3. A timber tree, commonly Sisu,<BR>(Dalbergia sisu, Rox.)<BR>	 mfn. (-रुः-रुः-रू or -र्व्वी-रु) Light, not heavy.<BR>E. अ priv. and गुरु heavy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=005-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अगुप्त
अगुप्त mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं)<BR>	 1. Unhidden, unconcealed.<BR>	 2. One who cannot<BR>keep a secret.<BR> E. अ neg. गुप्त concealed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=005-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अगुरुशिंशपा
अगुरुशिंशपा f. (-पा) A timber tree. (Dalbergia sisu.) The best authori-<BR>ties consider this as formed of two distinct words. See अगुरु and<BR>शिंशपा ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=005-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अगूढ
अगूढ mfn. (ढः-ढा-ढं)<BR>	 1. Unhidden, unconcealed, manifest, evident.<BR>	 2.<BR>One who is not secret.<BR> E. अ neg. गूढ hidden.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=005-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अगूढगन्ध|अगूढगन्धं|अगूढगन्धः
अगूढगन्ध n. (-न्धं) Asafœtida.<BR> E. अगूढ and गन्ध smell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=005-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अगूढभाव
अगूढभाव mfn. (-वः-वा-वं) Open, honest, candid; one whose purpose or<BR>inclinations are evident.<BR> E. अगूढ and भाव nature.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=005-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अगोचर|अगोचरः
अगोचर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Covert, unseen, unwitnessed.<BR>	 n. (-रं)<BR>	 1. Absence,<BR>unconsciousness; not being witnessed or known.<BR>	 2. Any act or<BR>event not the object of the senses.<BR>	 3. The imperceptible, BRAHMĀ,<BR>or the invisible Supreme.<BR> E. अ neg. गोचर, object of sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=005-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अगौकस्
अगौकस् m. (-काः)<BR>	 1. A bird.<BR>	 2. A lion.<BR>	 3. The Sarabha, a fabulous ani-<BR>mal with eight legs.<BR> E. अग a tree or mountain, ओकस् a house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=005-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्नायी
अग्नायी f. (-यी)<BR>	 1. A goddess, the wife of AGNI, the deity of fire, and<BR>presiding over prayers accompanied with burnt offerings.<BR>	 2. The<BR>Treta or second age of the Hindus.<BR> E. अग्नि fire, and fem. aff. ङीप,<BR>with आय substituted for ऐ inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=005-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्नि|अग्निः
अग्नि m. (-ग्निः)<BR>	 1. Fire, always associated with the idea of the deity<BR>presiding over it, and who is worshipped by the Hindus. AGNI is<BR>also regent of the south-east quarter.<BR>	 2. A consecrated fire.<BR>	 3. The<BR>fire of the stomach, the digestive faculty, appetite.<BR>	 4. Bile.<BR>	 5.<BR>Gold.<BR>	 6. A plant of which the fruit has escharotic properties,<BR>(Semecarpus anacardium)<BR>	 7. Another plant, (Plumbago zeylanica.)<BR>E. अङ्ग to mark, and नि Uṇādi aff. ङ being dropped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=005-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निक|अग्निकः
अग्निक m. (-कः) An insect of a scarlet color, the ladybird.<BR> E. अग्नि fire<BR>and क aff. resembling fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=005-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निकण|अग्निकणः
अग्निकण m. (-णः) A spark.<BR> E. अग्नि fire, and कण a small particle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=005-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निकारिका
अग्निकारिका f. (-का) Maintaining a sacrificial fire, &c.<BR> E. अग्नि fire, and<BR>कारिका making, from कृ to do.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=005-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निकारित
अग्निकारित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Caused by fire.<BR> E. अग्नि and कारित caused.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=005-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निकार्य्य|अग्निकार्य|अग्निकार्य्यं
अग्निकार्य्य n. (-र्य्यं) Maintaining a sacred fire.<BR> E. अग्नि and कार्य्य act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=005-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निकाष्ठ|अग्निकाष्ठं
अग्निकाष्ठ n. (-ष्ठं) Agallochum. See अगुरु,<BR> E. अग्नि fire, and काष्ठ wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=005-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निकुक्कट
अग्निकुक्कट m. (-टः) A firebrand, a lighted wisp of straw.<BR> E. अग्नि fire,<BR>and कुक्कट a wisp of lighted straw.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=005-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निकृत|अग्निकृतः
अग्निकृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Done with or made by fire, offered with fire.<BR>E. अग्नि and कृत done.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=005-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निकोण|अग्निकोणं|अग्निकोणः
अग्निकोण m. (-णः) The east.<BR> E. अग्नि and कोण corner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=005-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निक्रीडा
अग्निक्रीडा f. (-डा) Illuminations, fireworks, &c.<BR> E. अग्नि and क्रीडा play.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=005-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निगर्भ|अग्निगर्भः
अग्निगर्भ m. (-र्भः)<BR>	 1. The sun-stone, crystal, or a fabulous gem; supposed<BR>to contain and impart solar heat.<BR>	 2. A plant.<BR>	 f. (-र्भा) The name of<BR>another plant.<BR> E. अग्नि, गर्भ the womb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=005-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निचित्
अग्निचित् m. (-चित्) A householder who has placed and consecrated a<BR>sacrificial fire.<BR> E. अग्नि fire, and चित् who collects.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=005-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निचित्या
अग्निचित्या f. (-त्या) Maintaining a sacred fire.<BR> E. अग्नि and चित्या<BR>collecting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=005-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निज|अग्निजः
अग्निज m. (-जः) A plant used in medicine, of stimulant properties.<BR>	 mfn.<BR>(-जः-जा-जं)<BR>	 1. Produced by or producing fire, also अग्निजात, 2. Digestive.<BR>E. अग्नि fire, and ज who or what is born, from जनः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=005-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निजार|अग्निजारः
अग्निजार m. (-रः) A medicinal plant. See अग्निज ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=005-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निजाल|अग्निजालः
अग्निजाल m. (-लः) A medicinal plant. See अग्निज ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=005-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निजिह्वा
अग्निजिह्वा f. (-ह्वा)<BR>	 1. A medicinal plant. See लाङ्गलिकी 2. A flame of fire.<BR>E. अग्नि, and जिह्वा the tongue, growing like a flame of fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=005-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निज्वाला
अग्निज्वाला f. (-ला)<BR>	 1. A flame of fire.<BR>	 2. A plant bearing red blossoms<BR>used by dyers, (Grislea tomentosa, Rox.)<BR>	 3. Another plant,<BR>commonly Jalapippalī.<BR> E. अग्नि and ज्वाला flame, from the fiery<BR>colour of its blossoms.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=005-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्नित्रेता
अग्नित्रेता f. (-ता) The aggregate of the three fires maintained by the<BR>Brahman householder, the Gārhapatya or domestic, Āhavanīya or<BR>consecrated, and Dakṣiṇa or southern.<BR> E. अग्नि and त्रेता triad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=005-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निद
अग्निद mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>	 1. Setting on fire, incendiary.<BR>	 2. Supplying with<BR>fire.<BR>	 3. Stomachic, tonic, digestive.<BR> E. अग्नि and द what gives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=005-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निदमनी
अग्निदमनी f. (-नी) A medicinal plant, of narcotic properties, (Solanum<BR>jacquini.) See कण्टकारिका,<BR> E. अग्नि bile, and दमनी what tames.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=005-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निदग्ध
अग्निदग्ध m. (-ग्धः) A Pitṛ or progenitor to whom oblations are made,<BR>mfn. (-ग्धः-ग्धा-ग्धं) Burnt.<BR> E. अग्नि and दग्ध burnt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=005-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निदीप्त
अग्निदीप्त mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं)<BR>	 1. Blazing on fire.<BR>	 2. Digestive.<BR>	 f. (-प्ता) The<BR>name of a plant.<BR> E. अग्नि and दीप्त inflamed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=005-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निदेव|अग्निदेवः
अग्निदेव m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. AGNI, the god of fire.<BR>	 2. A worshipper of fire.<BR>	 f. (-वा)<BR>A name of the third lunar mansion, identified with the Pleiades:<BR>AGNI being the ruling deity of the constellation. Also अग्निदेवता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=005-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निदैवत्य
अग्निदैवत्य n. (-त्यं) The supremacy or divinity of fire.<BR> E. अग्नि and दैवत्य<BR>divinity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=005-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निनिर्य्यास|अग्निनिर्यास|अग्निनिर्यासः|अग्निनिर्य्यासः
अग्निनिर्य्यास m. (-सः) The name of a plant, also अग्निजार<BR> E. अग्नि and निर्य्यास<BR>decoction or extract.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=005-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निपक्व
अग्निपक्व mfn. (क्वः-क्वा-क्वं) Cooked or dressed with fire.<BR> E. अग्नि and पक्क mature.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=005-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निपरिच्छद|अग्निपरिच्छदः
अग्निपरिच्छद n. (-दं) The implements and apparatus used in oblations<BR>to fire.<BR> E. अग्नि and परिच्छद accompaniments.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=005-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निपरीक्षा
अग्निपरीक्षा f. (-क्षा) The fiery ordeal, by a heated iron or boiling oil, or<BR>passing through fire.<BR> E. अग्नि and परीक्षा trial.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=006-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निप्रस्तर|अग्निप्रस्तरः
अग्निप्रस्तर m. (-रः) Fire-stone, flint, or any stone producing fire.<BR> E. अग्नि<BR>and प्रस्तर a stone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=006-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निभ|अग्निभं
अग्निभ m. (-भः) Gold.<BR> E. अग्नि and भ for भा lustre, brilliant as fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=006-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निभू
अग्निभू m. (-भूः) A name of SKANDA, the Hindu deity of war. See कार्त्तिकेय<BR>and स्कन्द.<BR> E. अग्नि and भू being; being, or born, from fire. ŚIVA<BR>having cast his seed into flame, for the purpose of generating a<BR>warrior, able to subdue TARĀKA, a demon, SKANDA was produced.<BR>n. (-भु) Water, which is generated, in the Hindu cosmogony,<BR>from fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=006-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निभूति|अग्निभूतिः
अग्निभूति m. (-तिः) A proper name. One of the pupils of the last Jaina<BR>saint.<BR> E. अग्नि and भूति superhuman power; equal to AGNI.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=006-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निमणि|अग्निमणिः
अग्निमणि m. (-णिः) The sun-stone.<BR> E. अग्नि and मणि a jewel or gem,<BR>brilliant as fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=006-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निमत्|अग्निमन्त्
अग्निमत् mfn. (-मान्-मती-मत्)<BR>	 1. Having a consecrated fire.<BR>	 2. Having<BR>fire in general.<BR> E. अग्नि and मतुप् poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=006-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निमन्थ|अग्निमन्थः
अग्निमन्थ m. (न्थः) A small tree, (Premna spinosa.)<BR> E. अग्नि and मन्थ chur-<BR>ning, because fire is produced by friction of two pieces of its wood<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=006-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निमारुति|अग्निमारुतिः
अग्निमारुति m. (-तिः) A name of the saint, AGASTYA.<BR> E. अग्नि fire, i. e. the<BR>fire of the stomach, the digestive faculty, and मारुति a name of<BR>HANUMAN; because the saint could digest as well as the monkey;<BR>the epithet alludes to a story of his devouring and digesting<BR>VĀTĀPI, a demon, who had assumed the form of a sheep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=006-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निमुख|अग्निमुखः
अग्निमुख m. (-खः)<BR>	 1. A deity.<BR>	 2. A Brahman.<BR> E. अग्नि and मुख the mouth;<BR>oblations to the gods passing through fire as their mouths.<BR>	 3. A<BR>plant, (Plumbago zeylanica.)<BR>	 4. Marking nut, (Semecarpus ana-<BR>cardium.) (In this sense it is also fem. -खी) E. as before, from its<BR>marking like fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=006-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निरक्षण|अग्निरक्षणं
अग्निरक्षण n. (-णं) Maintenance of a sacred fire; preserving a fire in a<BR>family for perpetuity, which supplies that lighted on occasions of<BR>worship.<BR> E. अग्नि and रक्षण Preserving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=006-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निरक्षित
अग्निरक्षित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Maintaining a sacred fire.<BR> E. अग्नि and रक्षित<BR>preserved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=006-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निरहित
अग्निरहित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Being without fire, especially a sacred fire.<BR>2. Devoid of appetite.<BR> E. अग्नि and रहित lost.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=006-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निरजस्
अग्निरजस् m. (-जाः) An insect of a scarlet color.<BR> E. अग्नि and रजस् dust or farina.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=006-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निरुहा
अग्निरुहा f. (-हा) The name of a plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=006-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निवर्ण|अग्निवर्ण्ण
अग्निवर्ण mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-र्णं) Hot, scalding, scorching.<BR> E. अग्नि and वर्ण<BR>quality; of the property of fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=006-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निवर्द्धक
अग्निवर्द्धक mfn. (-कः-का-की-कं)<BR>	 1. Tonic, stomachic.<BR>	 2. Feeding or exciting<BR>fire.<BR> E. अग्नि and वर्द्धक what augments.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=006-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निवर्द्धन
अग्निवर्द्धन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Exciting fire.<BR>	 2. Improving the appetite.<BR>	 m. (नः) A<BR>stomachic or any thing improving the appetite.<BR> E. अग्नि and वर्द्धन<BR>increasing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=006-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निवल्लभ|अग्निवल्लभः
अग्निवल्लभ m. (-भः) Resin, pitch.<BR> E. अग्नि and वल्लभ a friend, from its<BR>exciting or befriending fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=006-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निवाण
अग्निवाण m. (-णः) A fiery arrow, a rocket.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=006-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निवाह|अग्निवाहः
अग्निवाह m. (-हः) Smoke.<BR> E. अग्नि and वाह what bears.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=006-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निबाहु|अग्निबाहुः
अग्निबाहु m. (-हु) Smoke.<BR> E. अग्नि and बाहु the arm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=006-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निविसर्प|अग्निविसर्पः
अग्निविसर्प m. (-र्पः) Pain from a boil.<BR> E. अग्नि and विसर्प a boil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=006-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निवीज|अग्निवीजं
अग्निवीज n. (-जं) Gold.<BR> E. अग्नि and वीज seed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=006-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निवीर्य्य|अग्निवीर्य|अग्निवीर्य्यं
अग्निवीर्य्य n. (-र्य्यं) Gold.<BR> E. अग्नि and वीर्य्य power.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=006-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निवृद्धि
अग्निवृद्धि f. (-द्धिः)<BR>	 1. Improved digestion, appetite.<BR>	 2. Increase of fire. E.<BR>अग्नि and वृद्धि increase.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=006-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निशिख|अग्निशिखं|अग्निशिखः
अग्निशिख m. (-खः)<BR>	 1. A lamp.<BR>	 2. An arrow.<BR>	 3. A fiery arrow, a rocket.<BR>E. The Safflower plant, (Carthamus tinctorius.)<BR>	 mn. (-खः-खं)<BR>Safforn, the plant and die.<BR>	 f. (-खा)<BR>	 1. Flame.<BR>	 2. A plant. (Gloriosa<BR>superba.)<BR>	 3. A medicinal plant, (Menispermum cordifolium.) E.<BR>अग्नि and. शिखा a crest or flame or splendor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=006-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निशेखर|अग्निशेखरं|अग्निशेखरः
अग्निशेखर m. (-रः) Saffron.<BR> E. अग्नि and शेखर a crest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=006-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निष्टुत्
अग्निष्टुत् f. (-ष्टुत्) An expiatory sacrifice.<BR> E. अग्नि and ष्टु to sacrifice, aff.<BR>क्विप् with तुक् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=006-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निष्टोम|अग्निष्टोमः
अग्निष्टोम m. (-मः) A sacrifice, or rather a series of offerings to fire for<BR>five days to be celebrated in the spring.<BR> E. अग्नि and लोम oblation,<BR>burnt-offering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=006-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निष्ठ|अग्निष्ठः
अग्निष्ठ n. (-ष्ठं) An iron frying-pan.<BR>	 mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठा-ष्ठं) Placed in or on fire.<BR>E. अग्नि and ष्ठ what stays or remains, from स्था to stand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=006-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निष्वात्त|अग्निष्वात्तः
अग्निष्वात्त m. pl. (-त्ताः) Demigods or Manes to whom funeral oblations<BR>are presented. They are said to be the sons of MARĪCI, and<BR>progenitors especially of the gods.<BR> E. अग्नि, स्व own, and आत्त<BR>taken, who receive what is offered them by fire as their own.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=006-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निसंस्कार|अग्निसंस्कारः
अग्निसंस्कार m. (-रः) Any ceremony performed with the consecrated fire.<BR>E. अग्नि, संस्कार purification.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=006-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निसख|अग्निसखः
अग्निसख m. (-खः) The wind.<BR> E. अग्नि and सखा friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=006-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निसम्भव|अग्निसंभव|अग्निसम्भवः
अग्निसम्भव m. (-वः) Wild safflower.<BR>	 mfn. (-वः-वा-वं) Originating from fire.<BR>E. अग्नि and सम्भव born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=006-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निसहाय|अग्निसहायः
अग्निसहाय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. A pigeon.<BR>	 2. The wind.<BR> E. अग्नि and सहाय a friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=006-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निसार|अग्निसारं|अग्निसारः
अग्निसार n. (-रं) A medicinal application to the eyes, a collyrium from<BR>the calx of brass.<BR> E. अग्नि and सार strength, essence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=006-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निहोत्र|अग्निहोत्रं|अग्निहोत्रः
अग्निहोत्र n. (-त्रं)<BR>	 1. Maintenance of a perpetual or sacred fire.<BR>	 m. (-त्रः)<BR>1. Fire.<BR>	 2. Ghee.<BR> E. अग्नि and होत्र oblation with fire, burnt<BR>offerings.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=006-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निहोत्रिन्
अग्निहोत्रिन् m. (-त्री) One who maintains a perpetual and sacred fire;<BR>this is sometimes read अग्निहोतृ, nom. (-ता)<BR> E. अग्निहोत्र, and णिनि,<BR>or हृ to sacrifice, तृन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=006-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्नीध्
अग्नीध् m. (-ग्नीत्) A priest who attends the fire.<BR> E. अग्नि, इन्ध to excite,<BR>क्विप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=006-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्नीध्र|अग्नीध्रः
अग्नीध्र m. (-ध्रः) Officiating priest, whose duty is to attend the fire.<BR>	 f.<BR>(-ध्रा) Exciting the sacrificial fire<BR> E. अग्नि and इन्ध, to light or kindle;<BR>and the aff. रन्; the न of इन्ध being dropped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=006-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्नीन्धन|अग्नीन्धनं|अग्नीन्धनः
अग्नीन्धन n. (-नं) Exciting a sacrificial fire.<BR> E. अग्नि and इन्धन kindling,<BR>exciting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=006-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्न्यभाव
अग्न्यभाव m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. Loss or extinction of the sacred fire.<BR>	 2. Loss of<BR>appetite.<BR> E. अग्नि, अभाव nonexistence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=006-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्न्यस्त्र|अग्न्यस्त्रं
अग्न्यस्त्र n. (-स्त्रं) Firearms; in poetry, it is usually applied to a super-<BR>human power over the element of fire, but occasionally indicates,<BR>apparently, a rocket.<BR> E. अग्नि, अस्त्र a weapon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=006-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्न्यागार|अग्न्यागारः
अग्न्यागार m. (-रः) A fire-temple; a chamber or building where the<BR>sacred fire is kept.<BR> E. अग्नि, आगार house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=006-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्न्याधान|अग्न्याधानं
अग्न्याधान n. (-नं) Maintenance of a perpetual and sacred fire.<BR>	 n. अग्नि<BR>and आधान preserving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=006-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्न्याधेय|अग्न्याधेयः
अग्न्याधेय n. (-यं) Consecration of a perpetual fire.<BR> E. अग्नि, आधेय placing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=006-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्न्यालय|अग्न्यालयः
अग्न्यालय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. A place in which consecrated fire is kept.<BR>	 2. A hole<BR>with compartments of prescribed dimensions and shape, for the<BR>several sacred fires.<BR> E. अग्नि and आलय asylum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=006-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्न्याहित
अग्न्याहित m. (-तः) A householder who maintains a perpetual fire; also<BR>आहिताग्नि,<BR> E. अग्नि, आहित preserved by whom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=006-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्न्युत्पात|अग्न्युत्पातः
अग्न्युत्पात m. (-तः) A fiery meteor, a falling star, a comet.<BR> E. अग्नि and<BR>उत्पात portent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=006-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्र|अग्रं|अग्रः
अग्र mfn. (-ग्रः-ग्रा-ग्रं)<BR>	 1. Chief, principal. E. Prior, first.<BR>	 2. Excessive,<BR>more, much.<BR>	 4. Excellent, best.<BR>	 n. (-ग्रं)<BR>	 1. Front, forepart.<BR>	 2.<BR>Top, summit, upper part.<BR>	 3. End, point.<BR>	 4. Goal, resting place.<BR>5. Assemblage, multitude.<BR>	 6. A weight equal to one Pala.<BR>	 7. Limi-<BR>ted alms, (four mouthfuls.)<BR>	 8. (In astronomy) the sun's amp-<BR>litude.<BR> E. अगि to go, and the Uṇādi aff. रन्, the nasal of the<BR>derivative is dropped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=006-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्रकर|अग्रकरः
अग्रकर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. The tip of the extended hand.<BR>	 2. The right or<BR>better hand.<BR>	 3. The extremity of a ray of light; the focal point.<BR>E. अग्र, कर hand or ray.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=006-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्रगण्य|अग्रगण्यः
अग्रगण्य mfn. (-ण्यः-ण्या-ण्यं) Te be reckoned or considered as first or<BR>best.<BR> E. अग्र and गण्य to be counted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=007-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्रगामिन्
अग्रगामिन् mfn. (-मी-मिनी-मि) Preceding; going before.<BR> E. अग्र, गामिन्<BR>who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=007-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्रज|अग्रजः
अग्रज m. (-जः)<BR>	 1. An elder brother; the first-born.<BR>	 2. A Brahman.<BR>mfn. (-जः-जा-जं) First-born or produced.<BR> E. अग्र first, ज who is born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=007-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्रजङ्घा
अग्रजङ्घा f. (-ङ्घा) The forepart of the thigh.<BR> E. अग्र the first part and<BR>जङ्घा thigh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=007-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्रजन्मन्
अग्रजन्मन् m. (-न्मा)<BR>	 1. A priest or Brahman; a man of the sacerdotal<BR>tribe.<BR>	 2. An elder brother or first-born.<BR>	 3. BRAHMĀ, the first-born<BR>of the gods.<BR> E. अग्र first or best, and जन्मन् birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=007-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्रजातक|अग्रजातकः
अग्रजातक m. (-कः) A Brahman; a man of the first class.<BR> E. अग्र and<BR>जातक who is born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=007-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्रजाति|अग्रजातिः
अग्रजाति m. (-तिः) A Brahman; a man of the first class.<BR> E. अग्र and जाति<BR>race, class.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=007-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्रज्या
अग्रज्या f. (-ज्या) (In astronomy) Sine of the amplitude.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=007-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्रणी
अग्रणी mfn. (-णीः-णीः-णि) First, principal.<BR> E. अग्र and नी from नीञ to<BR>lead, aff. क्विप्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=007-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्रतःसर|अग्रतःसरः
अग्रतःसर mfn. (-र-रा-री-रं) Going before, preceding.<BR>	 m. (-रः) A leader. E.<BR>अग्रतस्, and सर, who goes, from सृ with अच् or ट aff. to go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=007-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्रतस्
अग्रतस् ind.<BR>	 1. Before, in front.<BR>	 2. Before in rank, &c.<BR> E. अग्र and तस् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=007-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्रदानिन्
अग्रदानिन् m. (-नी) A degraded Brahman; one who receives the pre-<BR>sents of Śūdras, or things first offered to the deceased.<BR> E. अग्र, दान<BR>gift, इनि poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=007-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्रनिरूपण
अग्रनिरूपण n. (-णं) Determining beforehand, prophecy, predestination.<BR>E. अग्र, निरूपण declaring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=007-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्रपणी
अग्रपणी f. (-र्णी) A plant, Cowhage, (Carpopogon pruriens.)<BR> E. अग्र, पर्ण<BR>leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=007-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्रपाणि|अग्रपाणिः
अग्रपाणि m. (-णिः)<BR>	 1. The tip of the hand.<BR>	 2. The right hand.<BR> E. अग्र,<BR>पाणि the hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=007-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्रभाग|अग्रभागः
अग्रभाग m. (-गः)<BR>	 1. Part of the top or end.<BR>	 2. Fore or top part.<BR>	 3. (In<BR>astronomy) Degree of amplitude, also अग्रांशः<BR> E. अग्र, भाग part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=007-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्रभूमि|अग्रभूमिः
अग्रभूमि mf. (-मिः) A goal, an object, the place or thing to be attained.<BR>E. अग्र before, भूमि earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=007-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्रमांस
अग्रमांस n. (-सं) The heart.<BR> E. अग्र principal, and मांस flesh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=007-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्रयान|अग्रयानं
अग्रयान n. (-नं) Advancing before an army, for the purpose of defiance;<BR>military ardor or daring.<BR> E. अग्र and यान going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=007-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्रवीज|अग्रवीजः
अग्रवीज m. (-जः) A viviparous plant, as the Gomphrœna globosa, &c.<BR>E. अग्र in front, and वीज seed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=007-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्रसन्धानी|अग्रसंधानी
अग्रसन्धानी f. (-नी) The register of human actions, kept by YAMA, the<BR>judge of the dead.<BR> E. अग्र first, and सं, preposition, with धा to<BR>take; recording all actions from the original birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=007-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्रसर|अग्रसरः
अग्रसर mfn. (-रः-रा-री-रं) Preceding, going before, a leader.<BR> E. अग्र and<BR>सर who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=007-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्रह|अग्रहः
अग्रह m. (-हः) An anchorite, a man who has retired from the world.<BR>E. अ neg. and ग्रह a house, being no longer householder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=007-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्रहणीय
अग्रहणीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Not to be taken, accepted or acquired.<BR> E. अ<BR>neg. ग्रहणीय to be taken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=007-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्रहस्त|अग्रहस्तः
अग्रहस्त m. (-स्तः)<BR>	 1. The tip of the extended hand.<BR>	 2. The tip of an<BR>elephant's trunk.<BR>	 3. The right or better hand.<BR> E. अग्र, हस्त hand &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=007-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्रहायण|अग्रहायणः
अग्रहायण m. (-णः) The name of a month; the eighth of the lunar of<BR>the Hindus, when the moon is full near the head of Orion, or<BR>about November-December.<BR> E. अग्र and हायन, year; according to<BR>the ancient system, the first month of the Hindu year; also<BR>आग्रहायण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=007-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्रहार|अग्रहारः
अग्रहार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. An endowment of lands or villages conferred upon<BR>Brahmans.<BR>	 2. A field of corn.<BR> E. अग्र chief (tribe) हृ to take, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=007-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्रांश
अग्रांश m. (-शः) See अग्रभाग.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=007-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्रांशु|अग्रांशुः
अग्रांशु m. (-शुः) The extreme ray or point of a ray of light, the focal<BR>point.<BR> E. अग्र, अंश a ray.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=007-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्राह्य|अग्राह्यं
अग्राह्य mfn. (-ह्यः-ह्या-ह्यं)<BR>	 1. Not fit or proper to be accepted.<BR>	 2. Not to<BR>be attained.<BR>	 3. Not to be trusted or consented to.<BR> E. अ neg. ग्राह्य<BR>to be taken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=007-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्रिम|अग्रिमः
अग्रिम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>	 1. Chief, principal, best.<BR>	 2. Elder, elder born.<BR>f. (मा) The name of a fruit, (Annona reticulata.) See लवनी<BR> E. अग्र<BR>and डिमच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=007-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्रिय|अग्रियं|अग्रियः
अग्रिय m. (-यः) An elder brother.<BR>	 mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Chief, principal. E.<BR>अग्र and इय or ईय aff. whence also अग्रीय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=007-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्रु|अग्रुः
अग्रु f. (-ग्रुः) A finger.<BR> E. अग to go, and रु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=007-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्रेगा
अग्रेगा m. (-गाः) A leader, a preceder.<BR> E. अग्रे in front, गा who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=007-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्रेगू
अग्रेगू m. (-गूः) A leader.<BR> E. अग्रे, ग from गम to go, and ऊ Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=007-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्रेदिधिषु|अग्रेदिधिषुः
अग्रेदिधिषु m. (-षुः) A man of either of the three first classes, whose<BR>wife has been before married, and has borne him children.<BR> E. अग्रे<BR>principal, and दिधिषु the husband of a twice married woman.<BR>	 f.<BR>(-षुः) A younger sister married before her elder; also अग्रेदिधिषू.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=007-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्रेवन
अग्रेवन n. (नं) The skirts of a wood<BR> E. अग्रे the forepart, and वन wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=007-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्रेसर|अग्रेसरः
अग्रेसर m. (-रः) A leader.<BR>	 mfn. (-रः-रा-री-रं) Preceding, going before. E.<BR>अग्रे in front, and सर who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=007-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्रेसरिक|अग्रेसरिकः
अग्रेसरिक m. (-कः) A leader.<BR> E. अग्रे in front, and सरिक who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=007-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्र्य|अग्र्यः
अग्र्य mfn. (-ग्य्रः-ग्य्रा-ग्य्रं) Chief, principal.<BR>	 m. (ग्य्रः) An elder brother. E.<BR>अग्र, and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=007-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अघ|अघं|अघः
अघ r. 1st cl. With an indicatory इ, अघि (अंघति.) 1. To go.<BR>	 2. To go<BR>swiftly.<BR>	 3. To being moving.<BR>	 4. To begin.<BR>	 5. To blame or censure<BR>r. 10th cl. (अघयति) To sin, to commit sin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=007-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अघ|अघं|अघः
अघ n. (-घं)<BR>	 1. Sin.<BR>	 2. Pain.<BR>	 3. Passion.<BR>	 m. (-घः) Name of a demon; the<BR>general name of KANSA. अ. अघ to go, and अच affix, removed by<BR>charity, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=007-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अघनाशक
अघनाशक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Purifying, freeing from sin.<BR> E. अघ, and नाशक<BR>what destroys.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=007-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अघनाशन|अघनाशनः
अघनाशन mfn. (-नः-नी-नं) Purifying, freeing from sin.<BR>	 m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. A name<BR>of VIṢṆU 2. An expiator. अ, अघ and नाशन destroyer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=007-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अघमय
अघमय mfn. (-यः-यी-यं) Sinful, identical with or fruitful in sin<BR> E. अघ<BR>and मयट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=007-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अघमर्षण|अघमर्षणं
अघमर्षण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) An expiatory prayer: reciting mentally a parti-<BR>cular passage from the Vedas while a little water, in the palm of<BR>the right hand, is held to the nose; this forms a part of the<BR>daily ceremonies of the Brahmans.<BR>	 m. (-णः) The author of the<BR>passage recited upon the above occasion.<BR> E. अघ sin, and सृष to<BR>bear with, or to sprinkle, युच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=007-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अघर्म्म|अघर्म
अघर्म्म mfn. (-र्म्म-र्म्मा-र्म्मं) Cool, not warm.<BR> E. अ neg. घर्म्म hot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=007-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अघर्म्मधामन्|अघर्मधामन्
अघर्म्मधामन् m. (-मा) The moon, as the source of coolness.<BR> E. अघर्म्म cool,<BR>धामन् vesture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=007-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अघवत्|अघवन्त्
अघवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Wicked, vicious, sinful.<BR> E. अघ sin. मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=007-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अघाह|अघाहः
अघाह n. (-हः) Time or day of impurity, consequent on the death of<BR>a relative, &c.<BR> E. अघ and अहन् day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=007-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अघृण
अघृण mfn. (-ण-णा-णं) Unkind, cruel.<BR> E. अ neg. घृणा compassion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=007-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अघोर|अघोरः
अघोर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Formidable, terrible.<BR>	 m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A name of ŚIVA.<BR>2. A worshipper of ŚIVA, and DeVĪ in their terrific forms.<BR>	 f. (-रा)<BR>The fourteenth day of the dark half of the month Bhadra, upon<BR>which ŚIVA is worshipped.<BR> E. अ implying resemblance, and घोर<BR>formidable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=007-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अघोरपथिन्
अघोरपथिन् m. (-पन्था) A worshipper of the terrific forms of ŚIVA and<BR>DURGĀ<BR> E. अघोर and पथिन् a road.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=007-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अघोष|अघोषः
अघोष mfn. (-षः-षा-षं)<BR>	 1. Without noise.<BR>	 2. Without cowherd, (a country)<BR>E. अ neg. घोष noise, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=007-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अघोस्
अघोस् ind. A vocative particle: the final स् is usually dropped in<BR>composition, as अघोयज ho, pay worship.<BR> E. अ neg. हन to kill, and<BR>ओस् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=007-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अघ्न
अघ्न m. (-घ्नः) A name of BRAHMĀ.<BR>	 f. (घ्ना) A cow.<BR>	 mfn. (-घ्नः-घ्ना-घ्नं)<BR>	 1. invi-<BR>olable, not to be slain.<BR> E. अ neg. हन to kill. and अक Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=007-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्क|अंक|अंकः|अङ्कः
अङ्क(क, त) r. 10th cl. (अङ्कयति)<BR>	 1. To number or count.<BR>	 2. To mark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=008-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्क|अंक|अंकः|अङ्कः
अङ्क n. (ङ्कं)<BR>	 1. A mark or spot.<BR>	 2. The flank or part above the hips.<BR>3. A species of dramatic entertainment.<BR>	 4. The act of a play, &c.<BR>5. Fault, offence.<BR>	 6. A line, a stroke.<BR>	 7. Mimic war or conflict.<BR>	 8.<BR>ornament, decoration.<BR>	 9. Place, abode.<BR>	 10. Proximity, proximate.<BR>11. A chapter or section.<BR>	 12. The body.<BR>	 13. A cypher, an arithme-<BR>tical sign.<BR> E. अञ्च to go, and the Uṇādi affix क; or अङ्क to stain or<BR>spot, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=008-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्कति|अंकति|अंकतिः|अङ्कतिः
अङ्कति m. (तिः)<BR>	 1. A Brahman who maintains a sacred fire 2. A name of<BR>BRAHMĀ.<BR>	 3. Fire.<BR>	 4. Air, wind.<BR> E. अञ्च to go, and the Uṇādi aff.<BR>अति; च being changed to क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=008-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्कन|अंकन|अंकनं|अङ्कनं
अङ्कन n. (नं)<BR>	 1. Cyphering, writing or making cyphers.<BR>	 2. Stamping,<BR>impressing, making marks,<BR> E. अङ्क to mark, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=008-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्कनीय
अङ्कनीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>	 1. To be marked.<BR>	 2. To be numbered.<BR> E. अङ्क<BR>to mark, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=008-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्कपरिवर्त्तन|अङ्कपरिवर्तन
अङ्कपरिवर्त्तन n. (-नः) Turning on the side.<BR> E. अङ्क and परिवर्त्तन turning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=008-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्कपालिका|अंकपालिका
अङ्कपालिका f. (का) An embrace, embracing.<BR> E. अङ्क the flank, and पालिका<BR>or पाली, nourishing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=008-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्कपाली|अंकपाली
अङ्कपाली f. (-ली)<BR>	 1. An embrace, embracing.<BR>	 2. A nurse.<BR>	 3. A plant,<BR>(Piring or Medicago esculenta.) E. See अङ्कपालिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=008-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्कभाज्|अंकभाज्
अङ्कभाज् mfn. (-भाक्) Resting or placed upon the side or hip.<BR> E. अङ्क and<BR>भाज् possessing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=008-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्कयितव्य
अङ्कयितव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>	 1. To be marked.<BR>	 2. To be numbered.<BR> E. अङ्क<BR>to mark, तव्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=008-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्कविद्या|अंकविद्या
अङ्कविद्या f. (-द्या) Arithmetic.<BR> E. अङ्क and विद्या science.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=008-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्कित|अङ्कितः
अङ्कित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Marked, spotted.<BR>	 2. Counted, numbered.<BR> E. अङ्क<BR>to mark, and participial aff क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=008-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्की|अंकी
अङ्की f. (-की) A small oblong drum.<BR> E. अङ्क the hip or flank, being<BR>carried upon that part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=008-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्कुट|अंकुट|अंकुटः|अङ्कुटः
अङ्कुट m. (-टः) A key.<BR> E. अकि to go, उटि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=008-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्कुर|अंकुर|अंकुरं|अंकुरः|अङ्कुरः
अङ्कुर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A Shoot or sprout.<BR>	 2. The hair of the body.<BR>	 3. Blood<BR>4. Water.<BR> E. अङ्क to stain. and Uṇādi aff. उरच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=008-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्कुरक|अंकुरकः|अङ्कुरकः
अङ्कुरक m. (-कः) A nest.<BR> E. अङ्कुर a shoot, and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=008-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्कुरित|अंकुरित
अङ्कुरित m. (-तः-ता-तं) Budded, sprouted, germinated.<BR> E. अङ्कुर and इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=008-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्कुश|अंकुश|अंकुशः|अङ्कुशः
अङ्कुश mn. (-शः-शं) The hook used to drive an elephant.<BR> E. अक to go,<BR>and उशच् Uṇādi aff. with नुम् inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=008-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्कुशग्रह|अंकुशग्रह|अङ्कुशग्रहः
अङ्कुशग्रह m. (-हः) An elephant-driver<BR> E. अङ्कुश्--, and ग्रह Who takes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=008-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्कुशदुर्द्धर
अङ्कुशदुर्द्धर m. (-रः) A restive elephant.<BR> E. अङ्कुश, and दुर् bad, difficult, धर<BR>who holds: who is ill restrained by the goad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=008-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्कुशी
अङ्कुशी f. (-शी) One of the twenty-four female deities peculiar to the<BR>Jainas, supposed to preside more immediately over human beings<BR>E. अङ्कुश, and ङीप् fem. aff. having or holding a hook.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=008-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्कूर|अंकूर|अंकूरः|अङ्कूरः
अङ्कूर m. (-रं) A sprout, a germin. E. See अङ्कुर, उ being made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=008-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्कूष|अंकूष|अंकूषः|अङ्कूषः
अङ्कूष mn. (-षः-षं) The hook or goad for driving an elephant. E. See<BR>अङ्कुश, उ being made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=008-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्कोट|अंकोट|अंकोटः|अङ्कोटः
अङ्कोट m. (टः) A plant: also अङ्कोठ<BR> E. अङ्क to mark or stain. ओट aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=008-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्कोठ|अंकोठ|अङ्कोठः
अङ्कोठ m. (-ठः) A plant. (Alangium hexapetalum.) E. See. अङ्कोट, ठ being<BR>used for ट.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=008-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्कोल|अंकोल|अङ्कोलः
अङ्कोल m. (-लः) A plant. See अङ्कोट; also अङ्कोलक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=008-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्कोल्लसार|अङ्कोल्लसारः
अङ्कोल्लसार m. (-रः) A kind of poison, probably prepared from the plant<BR>अङ्कोल, or अङ्कोट<BR> E. अङ्कोल, and सार essence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=008-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्कोल्लिका
अङ्कोल्लिका f. (-का) Embracing, an embrace.<BR> E. अङ्क the side उत् pre. and<BR>ल, from ला, to take.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=008-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्क्य|अंक्य|अङ्क्यः
अङ्क्य mfn. (ङ्क्यः-ङ्क्या-ङ्क्यं)<BR>	 1. To be counted.<BR>	 2. To be marked.<BR>	 m. (-ङ्क्यः)<BR>A small oblong drum. See अङ्की<BR> E. अङ्क to mark, aff. यत्; or अङ्क<BR>the hip, and य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=008-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्ग|अंग|अंगं|अङ्गं|अङ्गः
अङ्ग (-कत) r. 10th cl. (अङ्गयति)<BR>	 1. To mark.<BR>	 2. To count. See अङ्क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=008-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्ग|अंग|अंगं|अङ्गं|अङ्गः
अङ्ग n. (-ङ्गं)<BR>	 1. A limb or member.<BR>	 2. A division of Hindu learning,<BR>comprehending such science as is considered dependant upon<BR>the Vedas, hence also called Vedanga; works on six subjects<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=008-b" target="_blank">Page008-b+ 60</a>]<BR>come under this description, viz. pronounciation, grammar, pro-<BR>sody, explanation of obscure terms, description of religious rites,<BR>and astronomy.<BR>	 3. The body.<BR>	 4. An expedient, a means of success.<BR>5. Mind, understanding.<BR>	 6. A term in grammar, the inflective<BR>root, with the affix subjoined.<BR>	 7. (Sing. only), chief, principal.<BR>	 8.<BR>Inferior, secondary.<BR>	 9. All the dramatis personœ of a play, except<BR>the hero and heroine, the body of the characters.<BR>	 10. In rheto-<BR>ric.) An incidental passion or figure, illustrative of, but subor-<BR>dinate to the main object of the description.<BR>	 11. A scriptural work<BR>in the Jain religion; there are twelve works so named.<BR>	 m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>A country, Bengal proper, including Bhagalpur.<BR>	 mfn. (-ङ्गः-ङ्गा-ङ्ग)<BR>1. Corporeal, embodied.<BR>	 2. Near, proximate. Ind.<BR>	 1. A vocative<BR>article.<BR>	 2. Again, further, the rather.<BR>	 3. A particle of assent used<BR>in composition, with ई substituted for the vowel termination, as<BR>in अङ्गीकरण &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=008-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गक|अंगक|अंगकं
अङ्गक n. (-कं)<BR>	 1. The body, &c. See the preceding.<BR>	 f. (अङ्गिका) A bodice<BR>or jacket mfn. (-काः, का or -की-कं) Relating to the body, &c.<BR> E. अङ्ग,<BR>कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=008-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गग्रह|अङ्गग्रहः
अङ्गग्रह m. (-हः) Bodily pain.<BR> E. अङ्ग, and ग्रह what seizes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=008-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गज|अंगज|अङ्गजं|अङ्गजः
अङ्गज (-जः) mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>	 1. Produced or born of the body.<BR>	 n. (-जं)<BR>1. Blood.<BR>	 2. Love, desire.<BR>	 3. The hair of the head.<BR>	 4. Sickness,<BR>disease.<BR>	 5. A son f. (-जा) A daughter.<BR> E. अङ्ग the body, and ज<BR>what is born also similar compounds, as अङ्गजात, अङ्गजन्म, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=008-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गण|अंगण|अंगणं|अङ्गणं
अङ्गण n. (-णः) A court or yard. See अङ्गन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=008-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गति|अंगति|अंगतिः|अङ्गतिः
अङ्गति m. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. A name of BRAHMĀ.<BR>	 2. A name of KṚṢṆA.<BR>	 3. Fire.<BR>	 4. A<BR>Brahman, who has preserved a sacred fire.<BR> E. अगि to go, and अति aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=008-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गद|अंगद|अंगदं|अङ्गदं|अङ्गदः
अङ्गद m. (-दः)<BR>	 1. The name of a celebrated monkey, one of the heroes<BR>of the Rāmāyaṇa, the son of BALI.<BR>	 n. (-दं) A bracelet worn upon<BR>the upper arm.<BR>	 f. (-दा) The female elephant of the south<BR> E. अङ्ग<BR>the body, and दे to nourish, or दै to cleanse, aff. ड<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=008-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गन|अंगन|अंगनं|अङ्गनं
अङ्गन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. A court or yard.<BR>	 2. Going, moving.<BR>	 f. (-ना)<BR>	 1. A wo-<BR>man, a female.<BR>	 2. The sign Virgo.<BR>	 3. The female elephant of the<BR>north.<BR> E. अगि to go, and अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=008-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गनागण|अंगनागण
अङ्गनागण n. (-णं) A number of women.<BR> E. अङ्गना and गण troop.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=008-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गनाजन|अङ्गनाजनः
अङ्गनाजन m. (-नः) A female, a female person.<BR> E. अङ्गना and जन a being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=008-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गनाप्रिय|अंगनाप्रिय|अङ्गनाप्रियः
अङ्गनाप्रिय m. (-यः) A plant. (Jonesia asoka.) See अशोक,<BR> E. अङ्गना a<BR>woman, and प्रिय, beloved; worship being performed by woman<BR>to this plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=008-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गन्यास|अंगन्यास|अङ्गन्यासः
अङ्गन्यास m. (-सः) Touching various parts of the body, as a religious<BR>ceremony.<BR> E. अङ्ग, and न्यास arrangement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=008-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गपालि|अंगपालि|अङ्गपालिः
अङ्गपालि m. (-लिः) Embracing, an embrace.<BR> E. अङ्ग, and पाल to nourish,<BR>इन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=008-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गप्रायश्चित्त
अङ्गप्रायश्चित्त n. (-त्तं) Expiation for bodily impurity. especially the obla-<BR>tion offered by the heir at the first funeral obsequies, to remove<BR>the impurity contracted during the period of mourning.<BR> E. अङ्ग<BR>body and प्रायश्चित्त expiation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=008-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गमर्द्द|अङ्गमर्द|अंगमर्द|अङ्गमर्दः|अङ्गमर्द्दः
अङ्गमर्द्द m. (-र्द्दः) A servant, whose business it is to rub and knead the<BR>body.<BR> E. अङ्ग, मृद to rub, and अच् aff. Also अङ्गमर्द्दकः and अङ्गमर्द्दन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=008-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गरक्त|अङ्गरक्तः
अङ्गरक्त n. (-क्तं) A plant, vulg. Sundarochani. See रक्ताङ्ग<BR> E. अङ्ग and रक्त<BR>red, giving a red dye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=008-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गरक्षिणी|अंगरक्षिणी
अङ्गरक्षिणी f. (-णी)<BR>	 1. Armour, coat of mail, thick quilting, or an iron<BR>netting worn upon the body.<BR>	 2. A garment.<BR> E. अङ्ग, and रक्षिणी<BR>what preserves.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=008-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गराग|अंगराग|अङ्गरागः
अङ्गराग m. (-गः) Perfuming the body after cleansing; smearing it with<BR>unguents of sandal, &c.<BR> E. अङ्ग, and राग colouring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=008-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गराज्|अंगराज्
अङ्गराज् m. (-राट्) A name of KARṆA, king of Anga the son of KUNTI<BR>by SŪRYA. See कर्ण.<BR> E. अङ्ग the country so named, and राज् a king;<BR>also अङ्गराजा and अङ्गराज.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=008-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गरुह|अंगरुह
अङ्गरुह n. (-हं) Hair of the body, wool, fleece, down.<BR> E. अङ्ग and रुह<BR>what rises on.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=008-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गलीड्य
अङ्गलीड्य m. (-ड्यः) Ginger, (Amomum zinziber) See चिञ्चाटक<BR> E. अङ्ग, and<BR>लोड, to be mad, aff. यत्; exciting or stimulating the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=009-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गस्कन्ध|अङ्गस्कन्धः
अङ्गस्कन्ध m. (-न्धः) A subdivision of a branch of science or philosophy. E.<BR>अङ्ग a part of science, and स्कन्ध division.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=009-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गव|अंगवं|अङ्गवः
अङ्गव m. (-वः) A dried or withered fruit.<BR> E. अङ्ग and व, from वै to dry<BR>or wither.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=009-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गविकृति|अंगविकृति|अङ्गविकृतिः
अङ्गविकृति m. (तिः) Syncope, apoplexy.<BR> E. अङ्ग, and विकृति, change of<BR>condition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=009-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गविक्षेप|अंगविक्षेप|अङ्गविक्षेपः
अङ्गविक्षेप m. (-पः) Gesture, gesticulation.<BR> E. अङ्ग and विक्षेप throwing,<BR>moving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=009-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गवैकृत|अंगवैकृत|अङ्गवैकृतं
अङ्गवैकृत n. (-तं) Sign, token, hint.<BR> E. अङ्ग, and वैकृत change of from. &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=009-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गसंस्कार|अंगसंस्कार|अङ्गसंस्कारः
अङ्गसंस्कार m. (-रः) Embelishment of person, dressing, cleansing or perfuming it.<BR>E. अङ्ग and संस्कार making perfect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=009-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गसंहति|अंगसंहति|अङ्गसंहतिः
अङ्गसंहति f. (-तिः) Bodily strength or symmetry,<BR> E. अङ्ग, and संहति<BR>compactness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=009-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गसङ्ग|अङ्गसंग|अंगसंग|अङ्गसङ्गः
अङ्गसङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः) Bodily union or contact, coition.<BR> E. अङ्ग, and सङ्ग union.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=009-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गहार|अंगहार|अङ्गहारः
अङ्गहार m. (-रः) Gesture, gesticulation.<BR> E. अङ्ग, and हार taking, moving;<BR>also अङ्गहारि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=009-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गहारि|अङ्गहारिः
अङ्गहारि m. (-रिः) See अङ्गहार.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=009-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गहीन|अंगहीन|अङ्गहीनः
अङ्गहीन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Mutilated, maimed, defective.<BR> E. अङ्ग a limb, हीन<BR>deprived of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=009-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गाङ्गि|अंगांगि
अङ्गाङ्गि ind. Body and body, implying contact or cooperation.<BR> E. अङ्ग<BR>repeated with इ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=009-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गाङ्गिभाव|अंगांगिभाव|अङ्गाङ्गिभावः
अङ्गाङ्गिभाव m. (-वः) Personal relation or cooperation.<BR> E. अङ्गाङ्गि and भाव<BR>nature.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=009-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गाधिप|अंगाधिप|अङ्गाधिपः
अङ्गाधिप m. (-पः) A name of KARNĀ, king of Anga. See कर्ण<BR> E. अङ्ग the<BR>country, अधिप a ruler.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=009-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गार|अंगार|अंगारं|अंगारः|अङ्गारः
अङ्गार mn. (-रः-रं) Charcoal, whether burning or not, but more usually<BR>the latter.<BR>	 m. (-रः) A name of the planet Mars; from his fiery<BR>colour.<BR> E. अगि to go, and आरन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=009-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गारक|अंगारक|अंगारकं|अंगारकः|अङ्गारकः
अङ्गारक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. The planet Mars.<BR>	 2. Charcoal, burning or extingui-<BR>shed.<BR>	 3. Yellow or white amaranth. See कुरुण्टक 4. Another plant,<BR>(Eclipta or Verbesina prostrata.) See भृङ्गराज.<BR>	 n. (-कं) A medicated<BR>oil, prepared by boiling turmeric and various vegetable substances<BR>in common oil.<BR> E. अङ्गार and कन् affix; resembling a during brand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=009-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गारकमणि|अंगारकमणि|अङ्गारकमणिः
अङ्गारकमणि m. (-णिः) Coral.<BR> E. अङ्गारकः and मणि a gem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=009-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गारधानिका|अंगारधानिका
अङ्गारधानिका f. (-का) A small portable fireplace or fire-pan.<BR> E. अङ्गार,<BR>and धानिका what holds, from धा root, with the affs. ल्युट् कन्<BR>and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=009-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गारपरिपाचित|अङ्गारपरिपाचितं
अङ्गारपरिपाचित n. (-तं) Roasted food.<BR> E. अङ्गार, and परिपाचित cooked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=009-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गारपर्ण|अङ्गारपर्णः|अङ्गारपर्ण्ण
अङ्गारपर्ण m. (-र्णः) A name of CHITRARATHA, chief of the Gandharbas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=009-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गारपुष्प|अङ्गारपुष्पः
अङ्गारपुष्प m. (-पः) A. Plant, vulg. Ingua. See इङ्गुदी The seeds are used<BR>for rosaries. &c.<BR> E. अङ्गार and पुष्प a flower; the flowers supposed<BR>to resemble coals.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=009-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गारमञ्जी
अङ्गारमञ्जी f. (-ञ्जी) A tree, or shrub, (Cesalpinia bonducella.)<BR> E. अङ्गार<BR>and मञ्जी a pedicle, compared to a coal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=009-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गारवल्लरी
अङ्गारवल्लरी f. (-री)<BR>	 1. A species of Karañja, (Galedupa arborea)<BR>	 2. Ano-<BR>ther plant, (Ovieda verticallata, Rox.)<BR> E. अङ्गार and वल्लरी a com-<BR>pound pedicle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=009-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गारवल्ली|अंगारवल्ली
अङ्गारवल्ली f. (-ल्ली) See अङ्गारवल्लरी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=009-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गारशकटी|अंगारशकटी
अङ्गारशकटी f. (-टी) A small portable fire-pan.<BR> E. अङ्गार and शकटी a little<BR>cart.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=009-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गारि|अंगारिः|अङ्गारिः
अङ्गारि f. (-रिः) A small portable fire-pan<BR> E. अङ्गार and इन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=009-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गारिका|अंगारिका
अङ्गारिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. The stalk of the sugarcane.<BR>	 2. The bud of the<BR>Kiṃśuka, (Butea frondosa)<BR> E. अङ्गार, and कन् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=009-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गारिणी|अंगारिणी
अङ्गारिणी f. (-णी)<BR>	 1. A small portable fireplace.<BR>	 2. The quarter from<BR>which the sun has departed.<BR> E. अङ्गार and णिनि poss. aff. and<BR>fem. ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=009-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गारित|अंगारित|अङ्गारितं|अङ्गारितः
अङ्गारित n. (-तं) The early blossom of the Kiṃśuka. (Butea frondosa.)<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Burnt.<BR>	 2. Charred.<BR> E. अङ्गार, and इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=009-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गिका|अंगिका
अङ्गिका f. (-का) A kind of bodice or jacket.<BR> E. अङ्ग the body and इकन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=009-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गिन्|अंगिन्
अङ्गिन् mfn. (-ङ्गी-ङ्गिनी-ङ्गि)<BR>	 1. Corporal, bodily.<BR>	 2. Limbed, having limbs<BR>or members.<BR>	 3. Chief, principal.<BR> E. अङ्ग and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=009-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गिरस्|अंगिरस्
अङ्गिरस् m. (-राः) The name of a Ṛṣi or saint, born of BRAHMĀ, one<BR>of the seven principal sages; in one legend identified with fire,<BR>and apparently an astronomical personification, having for his<BR>sons UTATHYA and VṚHASPATI, and for daughters Sinīvālī,<BR>Kuhū, Rākā and Anumati.<BR> E. अगि to go, and आनि Uṇādi aff. with<BR>इरक् inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=009-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गीकरण|अंगीकरण|अंगीकरणं
अङ्गीकरण n. (-णं) Promising, agreeing, assenting,<BR> E. अङ्ग a particle of<BR>assent. करण doing, ची inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=009-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गीकार|अंगीकार|अंगीकारः|अङ्गीकारः
अङ्गीकार m. (-रः) An agreement, a promise.<BR> E. अङ्ग a particle of asseve-<BR>ration, and कार making, from कृ to do, घञ inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=009-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गीकृत|अङ्गीकृतं
अङ्गीकृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Agreed, promised.<BR> E. अङ्गी as before. and कृत<BR>participle of कृ<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=009-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गुरि|अंगुरिः|अङ्गुरिः
अङ्गुरि f. (-रिः)<BR>	 1. A finger 2. A toe, also written अङ्गुरी See अङ्गुलि.<BR> E. अङ्ग<BR>to count, and उरी Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=009-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गुरीय|अंगुरीय|अंगुरीयं|अङ्गुरीयः
अङ्गुरीय mn. (-यः-यं) A finger-ring. See अङ्गुलीयक<BR> E. अङ्गुरी a finger,<BR>and य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=009-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गुरीयक|अंगुरीयक|अंगुरीयकं|अङ्गुरीयकं
अङ्गुरीयक mn. (-कः-कं) A finger-ring. See अङ्गुरीय.<BR> E. कन् affixed to the<BR>preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=009-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गुल|अंगुल|अंगुलः|अङ्गुलः
अङ्गुल m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. The thumb.<BR>	 2. A finger.<BR>	 3. A measure of eight barley<BR>corns.<BR>	 4. The name of a saint. See वात्स्यायन.<BR>	 5. A digit, or one-<BR>twelvth part of any dimension.<BR> E. अङ्ग to count and उल aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=009-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गुलि|अंगुलि|अंगुलिः|अङ्गुलिः
अङ्गुलि f. (-लिः)<BR>	 1. A finger.<BR>	 2. The tip of an elephant's trunk.<BR>	 3. A toe;<BR>also अङ्गुली.<BR> E. अङ्ग to count, and उलि Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=009-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गुलितोरण|अंगुलितोरण|अङ्गुलितोरणं
अङ्गुलितोरण n. (-णं) Three semicircular lines drawn across the forehead,<BR>with sandal &c. a sectarial mark, especially of the followers of<BR>Śakti.<BR> E. अङ्गुलि a finger, and तोरण the ornamented arch of a<BR>gateway, to which the mark made by the fingers upon the fore-<BR>head may be compared.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=009-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गुलित्र|अंगुलित्र
अङ्गुलित्र n. (-त्रं) A guard for the finger, applied to the bow-string used<BR>by archers.<BR> E. अङ्गुलि and त्र what protects.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=009-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गुलित्राण|अंगुलित्राण
अङ्गुलित्राण n. (-णं) See the last<BR> E. अङ्गुलि and त्राण what protects.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=009-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गुलिमुख|अंगुलिमुख
अङ्गुलिमुख n. (-खं) The tip of the finger.<BR> E. अङ्गुलि and मुख end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=009-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गुलिमुद्रा|अंगुलिमुद्रा
अङ्गुलिमुद्रा f. (-द्रा) A seal ring.<BR> E. अङ्गुलि and मुद्रा a seal; also अङ्गुलिमुद्रिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=009-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गुलिमोटन|अंगुलिमोटन|अङ्गुलिमोटनं
अङ्गुलिमोटन n. (-नं) Cracking, or snapping the finger joints.<BR> E. अङ्गुलि,<BR>and मोटन rubbing, from मुट aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=009-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गुलिसन्देश|अङ्गुलिसंदेश|अंगुलिसंदेश|अङ्गुलिसन्देशः
अङ्गुलिसन्देश m. (-शः)<BR>	 1. Snapping the finger joints.<BR>	 2. Making signs,<BR>talking with the fingers.<BR> E. अङ्गुलि, and सन्देश information.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=009-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गुलिस्फोटन|अंगुलिस्फोटन
अङ्गुलिस्फोटन n. (नं) Snapping the fingers.<BR> E. अङ्गुलि and स्फोटन<BR>bursting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=009-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गुली|अंगुली
अङ्गुली f. (-ली)<BR>	 1. A finger.<BR>	 2. The tip of an elephant's trunk. See अङ्गुलि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=009-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गुलीक|अंगुलीक|अंगुलीकं|अङ्गुलीकः
अङ्गुलीक mn. (-कः-कं) A finger ring.<BR> E. अङ्गुली and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=009-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गुलीपञ्चक|अङ्गुलीपञ्चकं
अङ्गुलीपञ्चक n. (-कं) The five fingers collectively.<BR> E. अङ्गुली, and<BR>पञ्चक a five.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=009-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गुलीयक|अंगुलीयक|अंगुलीयकं|अङ्गुलीयकं
अङ्गुलीयक n. (-कं) A finger ring. E. See अङ्गुरीयक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=009-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गुलीसम्भूत|अङ्गुलीसंभूत|अङ्गुलीसम्भूतः
अङ्गुलीसम्भूत m. (-तः) A fingernail.<BR> E. अङ्गुली and सम्भूत born, produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=009-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गुष्ठ|अंगुष्ठ|अंगुष्ठः|अङ्गुष्ठः
अङ्गुष्ठ m. (-ष्ठः) The thumb.<BR> E. अङ्गु here said to be the hand, and ष्ठ,<BR>from स्था to stay.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=009-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंङ्गूष
अंङ्गूष m. (षः)<BR>	 1. An ichneumon.<BR>	 2. An arrow.<BR> E. अगि to go, and ऊषः<BR>Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=009-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्घस्|अंघस्
अङ्घस् n. (-घः) Sin.<BR> E. अघि to go, and असि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=009-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्घ्रि|अंघ्रि|अङ्घ्रिः
अङ्घ्रि m. (-ङ्घ्रिः)<BR>	 1. A foot.<BR>	 2. The root of a tree.<BR> E. हन to kill, and<BR>क्रिन् Uṇādi aff. the formative is irregular. See अंह्रि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=009-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्घ्रिनामक|अङ्घ्रिनामकः
अङ्घ्रिनामक m. (-कः) The root of a tree, being named from a foot;<BR>every synonym of a foot being also that of the root of a tree.<BR>E. अङ्घ्रि and नामक name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=009-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्घ्रिनामन्
अङ्घ्रिनामन् n. (-म) The root of a tree.<BR> E. अङ्घ्रि a foot or root and नामन्<BR>a name. See the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=009-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्घ्रिप|अंघ्रिप|अङ्घ्रिपः
अङ्घ्रिप m. (-पः) A tree. See अंह्रिप<BR> E. अङ्घ्रि, a root and प from पा<BR>to drink.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=010-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्घ्रिपर्णी
अङ्घ्रिपर्णी f. (-र्णी) A plant. See अङ्घ्रिवल्लिका.<BR> E. अङ्घ्रि and पर्ण a leaf,<BR>aff. ङीप्, the leaves rising from the root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=010-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्घ्रिवल्लिका
अङ्घ्रिवल्लिका f. (-का) A plant, (Hedysarum lagopidiodes, Rox.)<BR> E. अङ्घ्रि,<BR>and वल्लिका a pedicle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=010-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अच
अच r. 1st. cl. (उ) or (ञै) (अचति) (अञ्चति) (अञ्चते) 1. To go. to, go to or<BR>towards.<BR>	 2. To worship.<BR>	 3. To speak indistinctly. See अञ्च.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=010-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अचक्षुस्
अचक्षुस् n. (-क्षुः) A bad or contracted eye.<BR>	 mfn. (-क्षुः-क्षुः-क्षुः) Eyeless,<BR>sightless.<BR> E. अ priv. or dim, and चक्षुस् the eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=010-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अचण्ड|अचंड
अचण्ड mfn.<BR>	 f. (ण्ड-ण्डा-ण्डी-ण्डं) Gentle, not passionate. (-ण्डी)<BR>	 1. A tracta-<BR>ble cow.<BR>	 2. A mild and gentle woman.<BR> E. अ neg. and चण्ड<BR>passionate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=010-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अचपल
अचपल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Steady, not fickle<BR> E. अ neg. चपल A unsteady.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=010-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अचल|अचलः
अचल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Fixed, immoveable.<BR>	 m. (लः)<BR>	 1. A mountain.<BR>	 2.<BR>A pin or bolt.<BR>	 f. (-ला) The earth.<BR> E. अ not, and चल who, goes from<BR>चल and अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=010-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अचलकीला
अचलकीला f. (-ला) The earth.<BR> E. अचल a mountain, कील a bolt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=010-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अचलत्विष्
अचलत्विष् m. (त्विट) The Koil or Indian cuckoo.<BR> E. अचल mountain, and<BR>त्विष् light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=010-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अचलाधिप|अचलाधिपः
अचलाधिप m. (-पः) The king of mountains, the personified Himālaya;<BR>also analogous compounds, as अचलेन्द्रः अचलेश्वरः, &c.<BR> E. अचल and<BR>अधिप king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=010-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अचलभ्रातृ
अचलभ्रातृ m. (-ता) The name of a Jaina saint, one of the eleven pupils<BR>of the last pontiff.<BR> E. अचल and भ्रातृ brother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=010-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अचापल्य
अचापल्य n. (-ल्यं) Firmness, steadiness, consistency: also अचपलता, &c.<BR>E. अ neg. चापल्य inconstancy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=010-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अचिन्त
अचिन्त mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं) Insensible, inanimate.<BR> E. अ neg. चिन्ता reflexion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=010-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अचिन्तता
अचिन्तता f. (-ता) Insensibility, want of sense or intellect.<BR> E. ता added to<BR>the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=010-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अचिन्ता
अचिन्ता f. (-न्ता) Disregard, absence of thought or consideration.<BR> E. अ<BR>neg. चिन्ता thought.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=010-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अचिन्तित|अचिंतित
अचिन्तित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Unthought of, unexpected.<BR>	 2. Disregarded<BR>E. अ neg. चिन्तित considered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=010-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अचिन्त्य|अचिंत्य|अचिन्त्यः
अचिन्त्य mfn. (-न्त्य-न्त्या-न्त्यं) Inconceivable, unimaginable, incomprehensible.<BR>E. अ neg. चिन्त्य conceivable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=010-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अचिर
अचिर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Brief, momentary, not long. (-रा) A proper name.<BR>the mother of SĀNTI, the sixteenth Jaina saint.<BR> E. अ neg. चिर<BR>long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=010-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अचिरद्युति|अचिरद्युतिः
अचिरद्युति (-तिः) Lightning.<BR> E. अ neg. चिर long. and द्युति light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=010-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अचिरप्रभा
अचिरप्रभा f. (-भा) Lightning.<BR> E. अचिर as before, and प्रभा light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=010-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अचिररोचिस्
अचिररोचिस् f. (-चिः) Lightning.<BR> E. अचिर as before, and रोचिस् light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=010-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अचिरांशु|अचिरांशुः
अचिरांशु f. (-शुः) Lightning.<BR> E. अचिर and अंशु a ray.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=010-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अचिरात्
अचिरात् ind. Directly, without delay.<BR> E. अ neg. and चिरात् from length<BR>of time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=010-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अचिराभा
अचिराभा f. (भाः) Lightning.<BR> E. अचिर as above, and भा light, with आङ<BR>prefixed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=010-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अचेतन|अचेतनः
अचेतन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Insensible, unconscious, devoid of reason or<BR>feeling.<BR> E. अ neg. चेतना consciousness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=010-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अचैतन्य|अचैतन्यं
अचैतन्य n. (-न्यं)<BR>	 1. Unconsciousness, insensibility.<BR>	 2. The material<BR>universe, as opposed to spiritual being or God.<BR>	 3. Ignorance,<BR>especially spiritual.<BR> E. अ neg. चैतन्य intellect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=010-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अच्युत|अच्युतः
अच्युत m. (-तः)<BR>	 1. A name of VIṢṆU; also of KṚṢṆA, as a form of<BR>VIṢṆU.<BR>	 2. A shrub, (Morinda tinctoria.)<BR>	 mfn. (-तः-ताः-तं) Fixed,<BR>permanent.<BR> E. अ neg. and च्युत participle of च्युङ to go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=010-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अच्युतवास|अच्युतवासः
अच्युतवास m. (-सः) The religious fig tree, (Ficus religiosa.)<BR> E. अच्युत<BR>VIṢṆU वास abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=010-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अच्युताग्रज|अच्युताग्रजः
अच्युताग्रज m. (जः)<BR>	 1. A name of BALARĀMA, the elder brother of KṚṢṆA.<BR>2. A name of INDRA.<BR> E. अच्युत KṚṢṆA, as VIṢṆU, and अग्रज elder<BR>born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=010-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अच्छ|अच्छं|अच्छः|अछ
अच्छ mfn. (-च्छः-च्छा-च्छं) Clear, transparent.<BR>	 m. (च्छ)<BR>	 1. A bear.<BR>	 2. Crystal.<BR>ind. Fronting, before, in presence of.<BR> E. अ neg. or comparative,<BR>and च्छो to cut, aff. ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=010-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अच्छभल्ल|अच्छभल्लः
अच्छभल्ल m. (-ल्लः) A bear. This is sometimes considered as two words.<BR>See अच्छ and भल्ल<BR> E. अच्छ in front of, and भल्ल to kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=010-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अच्छेद्य|अछेद्य
अच्छेद्य mfn. (-द्यः-द्या-द्यं) Not to be cut, incapable of injury or comm-<BR>inution.<BR> E. अ neg. च्छेद्य to be cut.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=010-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अज|अजः
अज r. 1st cl. (अजति)<BR>	 1. To go.<BR>	 2. To blame. or censure: the root is<BR>irregular, वी being substituted for it before many of the inflecti-<BR>ons, as विवाय, वीयात् &c. with an indicatory इ अजि r. 10th cl.<BR>(अञ्जयति) To shine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=010-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अज|अजः
अज m. (-जः) A name of BRAHMĀ 2. Also of VIṢṆU 3. A name of ŚIVA.<BR>4. Also of KĀMA. CUPID.<BR>	 5. A proper name, the son of RAGHU,<BR>and father of DĀSARATHA.<BR>	 6. A he-goat.<BR>	 7. A sheep.<BR>	 8. A mineral<BR>substance. See माक्षिक f. (-जा)<BR>	 1. A she-goat.<BR>	 2. Illusion, the<BR>unreality of the universe, personified as Śakti.<BR>	 mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>Unborn.<BR> E. अ neg. and ज born. unborn; or अज to go, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=010-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजकर्ण|अजकर्णः
अजकर्ण m. (-र्णः)<BR>	 1. The ear of a goat.<BR>	 2. A tree, (Terminalia alata<BR>tomentosa, Rox.) See असन.<BR> E. अज a goat. कर्ण an ear; the leaf<BR>being compared to the ear of a goat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=010-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजकर्णक|अजकर्णकः|अजकर्ण्णक
अजकर्णक m. (-कः) A tree, vulg. Sāl (Shorea robusta, Rox.) See शाल E.<BR>क affixed to the preceding, denoting resemblance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=010-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजकव|अजकवं|अजकवः
अजकव m. (वः) The bow of ŚIVA, See अजकाव अजगव &c.<BR> E. अज VIṢṆU,<BR>and क BRAHMĀ with व aff. BRAHMĀ being placed in the centre,<BR>and VIṢṆU on the upper part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=010-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजकाव|अजकावं|अजकावः
अजकाव m. (व) See अजकव. E. as before, अ being made आ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=010-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजगन्धा
अजगन्धा f. (न्धा) A plant, (Ocymum gratissimum.)<BR> E. अज a goat, and गन्ध<BR>smell; smelling like a goat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=010-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजगन्धिका
अजगन्धिका f. (का) A plant, (Ocymum gratissimum.) See अजगन्धा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=010-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजगन्धिनी
अजगन्धिनी f. (नी) A plant, See अजशृङ्गी E. See अजगन्धा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=010-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजगर|अजगरः
अजगर m. (रः) The Bor, or Boa, a large serpent. (Boa constrictor. E.<BR>अज a goat, and गर who swallows. from गृ with अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=010-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजगव|अजगवं
अजगव n. (-वः) The bow of ŚIVA. See अजकव &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=010-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजगाव|अजगावं|अजगावः
अजगाव n. (-कः) See अजगव, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=010-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजजीविक|अजजीविकः
अजजीविक m. (-कः) A goatherd,<BR> E. अज and जीविक who lives or gets a<BR>livelihood by goats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=010-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजटा
अजटा f. (-टा) The name of a plant. (Flacourtia cataphracta.) Also<BR>written अजडा and अज्झटा<BR> E. अ neg. and जट a fibrous root; or अ<BR>and जडा foolish, brightening the intellects.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=010-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजथ्या
अजथ्या f. (-थ्वा) A plant, (Yellow jasmine.)<BR> E. अज, and थान् aff. of propriety<BR>or fitness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=010-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजनक|अजनकः
अजनक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) One not a parent or producer, unproductive,<BR>ungenerative.<BR> E. अ neg. जनक generator.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=010-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजननि|अजननिः
अजननि m. (-निः) Privation of birth, used as an imprecation. See अकरणि &c.<BR>Ex. अजननिरस्तु तस्य may he cease to exist.<BR> E. अ priv. and<BR>जननि birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=010-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजन्त
अजन्त m. (-न्त) (In grammar) A noun ending in a vowel.<BR> E. अच् the<BR>syllable including all the vowels, and अन्त end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=010-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजन्मन्
अजन्मन् mfn. (-न्मा-न्मा-न्म) Unborn.<BR> E. अ neg. जन्मन् birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=010-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजन्य|अजन्यं
अजन्य n. (-न्यं) A portent, an omen; any natural phenomenon, as an<BR>earthquake, &c. so considered.<BR>	 mfn. (-न्यः-न्या-न्यं) Not to be born or<BR>produced.<BR> E. अ neg. and जन्य birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=010-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजप|अजपः
अजप m. (-पः)<BR>	 1. A reader of works considered heterodox.<BR>	 2. A goatherd.<BR>f. (पा)<BR>	 1. A particular mantra or mystical formula employed by<BR>the Tantrikas, the essence of which is in the letters H and S,<BR>whence it is termed the Hansa mantra 2. ŚIVA and SAKTI com-<BR>bined, to which form, the mantra is particularly, addressed.<BR>	 mfn.<BR>(-पः-पा-पं)<BR>	 1. Who or what does not perform the Japa.<BR>	 1. Cherishing<BR>or feeding goats.<BR> E. अ not; and जप silent prayer; or अज a goat,<BR>and प who protects.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=010-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजमीढ|अजमीढः
अजमीढ m. (ढः) A name of YUDHIṢṬHIRA; the friend of AJA, i. e. E.<BR>अज VIṢṆU or KṚṢṆA, and ईह to seek, to love, with the parti-<BR>cipial क्त, the termination of the accusative is retained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=011-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजमोदा
अजमोदा f. (-दा)<BR>	 1. Common carroway, (Carum carui.)<BR>	 2. A kind of<BR>lovage, (Ligusticum ajwaen, Rox.)<BR>	 3. A sort of parsley, (Apium<BR>involucratum;) this latter application is the one used in the<BR>dialects.<BR> E. अज a goat, and मोद what pleases, from मुद.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=011-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजम्भ|अजंभ|अजम्भः
अजम्भ m. (-म्भः) A frog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=011-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजय|अजयः
अजय m. (-यः) Defeat.<BR>	 mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Unsurpassed, unsubdued, over<BR>whom or which no triumph is obtained.<BR>	 f. (-या) Hemp.<BR> E. अ neg.<BR>जय victory.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=011-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजय्य|अजय्यं
अजय्य mfn. (-य्यः-य्या-य्यं) Invincible, not to be subdued or surpassed. E.<BR>अ neg. जय्य conquerable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=011-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजर्य्य|अजर्य|अजर्य्यं
अजर्य्य n. (-र्य्यं)<BR>	 1. Friendship.<BR>	 2. Imperishableness, exemption from<BR>infirmity or decay.<BR>	 mfn. (-र्य्यः-र्य्या-र्य्यं) Imperishable, undecaying. E.<BR>अ neg. and जर्य्य from जॄ to decay.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=011-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजर|अजरः
अजर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Imperishable, undecaying.<BR>	 f. (-रा) Aloes.<BR> E. अ<BR>neg. जरा decay.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=011-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजलम्बन|अजलम्बनं
अजलम्बन n. (-नं) Antimony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=011-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजलोमन्
अजलोमन् m. (-मा) Cowach, (Carpopogon pruriens.)<BR> E. अज, and लोमन्<BR>the hair of the body, hair, wool.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=011-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजशृङ्गी
अजशृङ्गी f. (-ङ्गी) A plant; described as a milky and thorny plant, with<BR>a fruit of a crooked figure, like a ram's horn, and used as a medi-<BR>cine for the eyes; vulg, Mera Sṛngi, and Kankara Sṛngi. See<BR>कर्क्कटशृङ्गी.<BR> E. अज a ram, and शृङ्गी a horn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=011-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजस्र|अजस्रं
अजस्र n. Adverbial. (स्रं) Eternally, continually.<BR> E. अ neg. जस to let<BR>loose, and र aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=011-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजहत्स्वार्था
अजहत्स्वार्था f. (-र्था) A figure of speech, metonymy, one name being put<BR>for another, as ‘the spears enter’ for the spearmen.<BR> E. अ neg. जहत्<BR>leaving, स्वार्था sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=011-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजहल्लिङ्ग|अजहल्लिंग|अजहल्लिंगं|अजहल्लिङ्गः
अजहल्लिङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः) In grammar, a noun that does not vary its gender,<BR>even when it is used attributively.<BR> E. अजहत् not leaving, लिङ्ग<BR>gender.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=011-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजहा
अजहा mfn. (-हः-हा-हं) Not relinquishing, not leaving.<BR>	 f. (-हा) Cowach,<BR>(Carpopogon pruriens.)<BR> E. अज and ह, from हा to abandon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=011-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजागर|अजागरः
अजागर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Not wakeful, not awake.<BR>	 m. (-रः) A plant, (Ecli-<BR>pta, or verbesina prostrata.)<BR> E. अ neg. and जागर wakeful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=011-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजाजी
अजाजी f. (-जी) Cumin seed.<BR> E. अज, a goat, and अज to go, affix, ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=011-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजाजीव|अजाजीवः
अजाजीव m. (-वः) A goatherd; also अजाजीविन् अजापालकः, &c.<BR> E. अजा<BR>a she-goat, and जीव who lives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=011-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजात|अजातः
अजात mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Unborn, unproduced.<BR> E. अ neg. जात born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=011-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजातशत्रु|अजातशत्रुः
अजातशत्रु m. (-त्रुः) A name of YUDHIṢṬHIRA.<BR> E. अजात unborn, and शत्रु<BR>an enemy, who never made an enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=011-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजातारि|अजातारिः
अजातारि m. (-रिः) See अजातशत्रु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=011-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजादनी
अजादनी f. (-नी) A small species of prickly nightshade<BR> E. अज a goat,<BR>and अदन eating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=011-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजानय
अजानय m. (-यः) A horse of a good breed. See अजानेय.<BR>	 mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Fearless, undaunted. E. See अजानेय the initial being made short.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=011-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजान्त्री
अजान्त्री f. (-न्त्री) A potherb, (Convolvulus argenteus.) See female,<BR>छगलान्त्री.<BR> E. अज, and अन्त्र an entrail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=011-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजापालक|अजापालकः
अजापालक m. (-कः) A goatherd.<BR> E. अजा a she-goat, पाल to nourish, and<BR>वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=011-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजित|अजितं|अजितः
अजित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Unconquered.<BR>	 2. Unexcelled, unsurpassed.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-तः)<BR>	 1. The second of the twenty-four principal Jaina Tīrthakaras<BR>or deified sages.<BR>	 2. A name of VIṢṆU.<BR>	 3. A name of BUDDHA.<BR>4. A name of ŚIVA.<BR> E. अ neg. and जित, participle of जि to conquer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=011-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजिन|अजिनं
अजिन n. (-नं) A hide used as a seat, bed, &c. by the religious student;<BR>generally the hide of an antelope.<BR> E. अज to go, and the Uṇādi<BR>aff. इनच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=011-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजिनपत्रा
अजिनपत्रा f. (-त्रा-त्री) A bat.<BR> E. अजिन a hide, and पत्र a wing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=011-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजिनयोनि|अजिनयोनिः
अजिनयोनि m. (-निः) A deer, or antelope.<BR> E. अजिन a hide. and योनि<BR>place of origin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=011-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजिर|अजिरं|अजिरः
अजिर n. (-रं)<BR>	 1. A court or yard.<BR>	 2. Air, wind.<BR>	 3. The body.<BR>	 4. An<BR>object of sense 5. A frog.<BR> E. अज to go, and किरन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=011-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजिह्म|अजिह्मं|अजिह्मः
अजिह्म mfn. (-ह्मः-ह्मा-ह्मं) Straight, not crooked. literally or metaphorically;<BR>upright, sincere, honest, direct.<BR>	 m. (-ह्मः) A frog.<BR> E. अ neg. and<BR>जिह्म crooked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=011-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजिह्मग|अजिह्मगः
अजिह्मग m. (गः) An arrow.<BR>	 mfn. (-गः-गा-गं) Going or moving in<BR>a straight line.<BR> E. अजिह्म straight, direct, and ग what goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=011-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजिह्व|अजिह्वः
अजिह्व mfn. (-ह्वः-ह्वा-ह्वं) Tongueless, having no tongue.<BR>	 m. (-ह्वः) A frog.<BR>E. अ neg. and जिह्व from जिह्वा a tongue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=011-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजीगर्त्त|अजीगर्त|अजीगर्तः
अजीगर्त्त m. (-र्त्तः) A Ṛṣi, the father of Śunaḥśepa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=011-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजीर्ण|अजीर्णं
अजीर्ण n. (-र्णं)<BR>	 1. Flatulency, indigestion.<BR>	 2. Vigor, absence of old age<BR>or decay.<BR>	 mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-र्णं)<BR>	 1. Undigested.<BR>	 2. Undecayed, unimpai-<BR>red.<BR> E. अ neg, and जीर्ण old, digested.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=011-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजीव|अजीवः
अजीव m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. Death.<BR>	 2. Nonexistence.<BR>	 mfn. (-वः-वा-वं)<BR>	 1. Lifeless,<BR>dead.<BR> E. अ neg. and जीव life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=011-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजीवनि|अजीवनिः
अजीवनि f. (-निः) Nonexistence; used as an imprecation. See अकरणि,<BR>अजीवनिस्तस्य भूयात्.<BR> E. अ neg. जीव and अनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=011-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजेतव्य
अजेतव्य mfn. (-व्य-व्या-व्यं) Invincible, not to be conquered or overcome.<BR>E. अ neg. जेतव्य conquerable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=011-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजेय|अजेयः
अजेय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Invincible, insuperable, not to be overcome or<BR>surpassed.<BR> E. अ neg. जेय to be conquered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=011-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजैकपाद|अजैकपादः
अजैकपाद m. (-दः) One of the eleven Rudras or deities so named, forms<BR>of ŚIVA. Sometimes read अज एकपाद.<BR> E. अज ŚIVA, एक one, and पाद<BR>a quarter a part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=011-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अज्जुका
अज्जुका f. (-का) A courtezan, (in theatrical language.)<BR> E. अज to go,<BR>or here, to gain, and उकन् affix; sometimes read अर्ज्जुका, from<BR>अर्ज to earn, to gain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=011-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अज्झटा
अज्झटा f. (-टा) A plant. (Flacourtia cataphracta.)<BR> E. अत् particle of<BR>surprise, and झट to be entangled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=011-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अज्झल|अज्झलं
अज्झल n. (-लं) A shield.<BR> E. अझ् to join, and अलच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=011-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अज्ञ|अज्ञः
अज्ञ mfn. (-ज्ञः-ज्ञा-ज्ञं) Ignorant, unwise, foolish.<BR> E. अ priv. and ज्ञ who<BR>knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=011-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अज्ञता
अज्ञता f. (-ता) Ignorance; also अज्ञत्व<BR> E. ता added to अज्ञ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=011-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अज्ञत्व
अज्ञत्व n. (-त्वं) Ignorance.<BR> E. अज्ञ and त्व aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=011-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अज्ञात
अज्ञात mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Unknown.<BR>	 2. Unknowing.<BR> E. अ neg. ज्ञात known.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=011-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अज्ञान|अज्ञानं
अज्ञान n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Ignorance.<BR>	 2. Spiritual ignorance, worldly illusion or<BR>belief in external appearances.<BR>	 mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Ignorant, unwise.<BR>E. अ neg. and ज्ञान knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=011-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अज्ञानता
अज्ञानता f. (-ता) Ignorance, also अज्ञानत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=011-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अज्ञानिन्
अज्ञानिन् mfn. (-नी-निनी-नि) Ignorant, unwise.<BR> E. अ neg. ज्ञानिन् knowing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=011-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अज्ञेय
अज्ञेय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Incomprehensible.<BR> E. अ neg. ज्ञेय to be known.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=011-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अञ्च
अञ्च r. 1st. cl. (उ.) (अञ्चति) 1. To adore, to worship, to treat with respect.<BR>(ञ, उ.) (अंचति-ते) 2. To go, to approach.<BR>	 3. To ask or beg.<BR>	 4. To<BR>speak indistinctly. With प्र, to move in an eastern direction;<BR>with प्रति, to go westerly; with उत्, to go northerly; with अव,<BR>to move southerly; with परा, to turn aside or away. r. 1st and<BR>10th cl. (अंचति अंचयति) To discriminate, to individualize, to<BR>possess especially. See अच.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=011-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अञ्चति|अंचतिः|अञ्चतिः
अञ्चति m. (-तिः) Air, wind.<BR> E. अञ्च to go, and अति Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=011-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अञ्चल|अंचलं|अंचलः|अञ्चलः
अञ्चल m. (-लः) The end or border of a cloth, veil, shawl, &c.<BR> E. अञ्च to<BR>go, and अलच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=011-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अञ्चित|अंचित|अञ्चितः
अञ्चित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Worshipped, revered.<BR>	 2. Admired.<BR>	 3. Gone.<BR>E. the participial derivative cf अञ्च to worship, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=011-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अञ्चितभ्रू
अञ्चितभ्रू f. (-भ्रूः) A woman having beautiful eyebrows.<BR> E. अञ्चित, and भ्रू<BR>the brow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=011-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अञ्ज|अञ्जः
अञ्ज r. 7th cl. (ध, ऊ, ञि) (अनक्ति) 1. To make clear.<BR>	 2. To anoint.<BR>	 3. To<BR>be beautiful.<BR>	 4. To go: with अभि, to anoint: with वि, to make<BR>manifest, to call into being, to create, to mark or designate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=011-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अञ्जन|अञ्जनं|अंजनः|अञ्जनः
अञ्जन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Anointing.<BR>	 2. Going.<BR>	 3. Making clear, distinct.<BR>	 4. A<BR>collyrium or application to the eyelashes, to darken and improve<BR>them; a universal article of the eastern toilet.<BR>	 5. Particular<BR>applications, as lampblack, antimony, and another kind. See<BR>रसाञ्जन.<BR>	 6. Night.<BR>	 7. Ink.<BR>	 8. A term in rhetoric; the use of a<BR>word of several meanings in one specific sense, which is determi-<BR>ned by the context.<BR>	 m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. The elephant of the west 2. A<BR>species of lizard.<BR>	 f. (-ना)<BR>	 1. The mother of HANUMĀN.<BR>	 2. A green<BR>lizard. (-नी)<BR>	 3. A woman perfumed with sandal, &c.<BR>	 4. A medicinal<BR>plant. See. कटुका.<BR> E. अञ्ज to beautify or anoint, and ल्यु or ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=012-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अञ्जनकेशी
अञ्जनकेशी f. (-शी) A vegetable perfume. See हट्टविलासिनी.<BR> E. अञ्जन colly-<BR>rium, केश hair, and ङीप् fem. affix; the fibres being like the crys-<BR>tals, perhaps, of antimony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=012-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अञ्जनाधिका
अञ्जनाधिका f. (-का) A kind of lizard.<BR> E. अञ्जन, and अधिक much, excessive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=012-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अञ्जनाम्भस्
अञ्जनाम्भस् n. (-म्भः) Eye-water, liquid collyrium.<BR> E. अञ्जन collyrium, and<BR>अम्भस् water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=012-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अञ्जनावती|अंजनावती
अञ्जनावती f. (-ती) The female-elephant of the north-east.<BR> E. अञ्जन, and<BR>वतुप् poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=012-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अञ्जनिका|अंजनिका
अञ्जनिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. A species of lizard, (Lacerta anjaneya.)<BR>	 2. A small<BR>mouse.<BR> E. अञ्जन, and इकन् affix, with the fem. termination; also<BR>read अञ्जलिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=012-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अञ्जलि|अंजलिः|अञ्जलिः
अञ्जलि m. (-लिः)<BR>	 1. The cavity formed by putting the hands together,<BR>and hollowing the palms: being in this form carried to the<BR>forehead, it forms the appropriate salutation from inferiors of<BR>respectability to their superiors.<BR>	 2. A measure, a Kuḍava. See कुडव.<BR>E. अञ्ज to go, and लिच् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=012-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अञ्जलिका|अंजलिका
अञ्जलिका f. (-का) See अञ्जनिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=012-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अञ्जलिकारिका
अञ्जलिकारिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. A kind of sensitive plant, (Mimosa natans,) or<BR>according to some, a different plant, (Lycopodium imbricatum) E.<BR>अञ्जलि, and कारिका making; from the shape or closing of the<BR>petals, like the hollowed palms of the hand.<BR>	 2. A doll, a puppet. E.<BR>as before.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=012-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अञ्जलिकर्म्मन्|अञ्जलिकर्मन्
अञ्जलिकर्म्मन् n. (-र्म्म) Making salutations, civility, respect.<BR> E. अञ्जलि, and<BR>कर्म्मन् act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=012-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अञ्जलिबन्धन
अञ्जलिबन्धन n. (-नं) Making a salutation with the hands joined and<BR>applied to the forehead.<BR> E. अञ्जलि, and बन्धन binding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=012-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अञ्जस|अंजस|अञ्जसः
अञ्जस mfn. (-सः-सा-सं) Straight, even, upright, (in morals.)<BR> E. अञ्ज to<BR>make clear, असच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=012-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अञ्जसा|अंजसा
अञ्जसा ind.<BR>	 1. Soon, instantly.<BR>	 2. Truly, justly.<BR> E. अञ्ज as before, षै to<BR>destroy, and क्विप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=012-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अञ्जि|अंजि|अञ्जिः
अञ्जि m. (-ञ्जिः) A superior, a commander, a sender.<BR> E. अजि to go, and<BR>कि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=012-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अञ्जिष्ठ|अंजिष्ठः|अञ्जिष्ठः
अञ्जिष्ठ m. (-ष्ठः) The sun.<BR> E. अञ्ज to make manifest, and इष्ठन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=012-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अञ्जीर|अंजीर|अंजीरं|अञ्जीरं|अंजीरः|अञ्जीरः
अञ्जीर n. (-रं) The fig tree, also its fruit. In Bengal, the word derived<BR>from this implies the Guava; the term has, possibly, been<BR>borrowed from a Persian word.<BR> E. अञ्ज to make clear, and ईरन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=012-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अट
अट r. 1st cl. (अटति) To move, to go or approach: with पार prefixed,<BR>to go round about, to roam, to rove, to ramble, to wander about,<BR>especially as a religious mendicant. 10th cl. (अटयति) To slight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=012-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अट
अट mf. (-टः-टा)<BR>	 1. Going 2. Roaming, wandering<BR> E. अट, and अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=012-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अटन|अटनं
अटन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Going, 2. Roaming about, leading a vagrant life. E.<BR>अट, and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=012-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अटनि|अटनिः
अटनि f. (-निः or नी) The notched extremity of a bow.<BR> E. अट to go, अनि<BR>affix, also with ङीष् fem. termination.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=012-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अटरुष|अटरुषः
अटरुष m. (-षः) A tree, (Justicia adhatoda.)<BR> E. अट here, disease, from<BR>अट to go, and रुष to destroy; destroying disease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=012-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अटरूष|अटरूषः
अटरूष m. (-षः) See the last word.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=012-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अटवि|अटविः
अटवि f. (-विः) A forest, or wood.<BR> E. अट to go, and अटि affix, or ङीष्<BR>being added अटवी ut infra; birds, &c. resting there.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=012-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अटविक|अटविकः
अटविक m. (-कः) A woodman, a forester.<BR> E. अटवि a wood, वक aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=012-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अटल
अटल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Immoveable, unchangeable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=012-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अटवी
अटवी f. (-वी) A forest, or grove. See अटवि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=012-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अटाट्या
अटाट्या f. (-ट्या) Roaming about as a devotee or religious mendicant. E.<BR>अट to go, frequentative form, affs अच् and यप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=012-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अट्ट|अट्टं|अट्टः
अट्ट r. 1st cl. (उ.) (अट्टते) 1. To surpass or excel, to transgress or exceed.<BR>2. To kill or hurt. 10th cl. (अट्टयति)<BR>	 1. To slight.<BR>	 2. To be small.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=012-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अट्ट|अट्टं|अट्टः
अट्ट m. (-ट्ट)<BR>	 1. A room on the top of the house; but it is also applic-<BR>cable to other structures; as the black of an edifice, a fortified<BR>place in front of a building, a room on the top of a temporary<BR>hall, or a particular kind of building.<BR>	 2. Much, excessive.<BR>	 n. (-ट्टं)<BR>Food, boiled rice especially.<BR>	 mfn. (-ट्टः-ट्टा-ट्टं) Dry, dried.<BR> E. अट्ट to<BR>go, surpass or transcend and घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=012-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अट्टट्ट
अट्टट्ट ind. Very lofty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=012-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अट्टन|अट्टनं
अट्टन n. (-नं) A circular weapon, a kind of discus.<BR> E. अट्ट to kill or hurt,<BR>ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=012-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अट्टहास|अट्टहासः
अट्टहास m. (-सः) Violent laughter, a horselaugh.<BR> E. अट्ट excessive, and<BR>हास a laugh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=012-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अट्टहासक|अट्टहासकः
अट्टहासक m. (-कः) A plant, (Jasminum multiflorum.)<BR> E. अट्टहास, and<BR>कन्; resembling a laugh or smile on beauty's countenance; the<BR>comparison is common to the poets.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=012-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अट्टहासिन्
अट्टहासिन् mfn. (-सी-सिनी-सि) Laughing, loudly and violently.<BR>	 m. (-सी) A<BR>name of ŚIVA.<BR> E. अट्टहास, and णिनि poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=012-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अट्टाल|अट्टालः
अट्टाल m. (-लः) An upper room or pavilion, on the flat roof of an<BR>Indian house.<BR> E. अट्ट much, and अल to adorn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=012-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अट्टालक|अट्टालकः
अट्टालक m. (-कः) A room on the top of the house.<BR> E. अट्ट much, अल to<BR>adorn, and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=012-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अट्टालिका
अट्टालिका f. (-का) A palace, an upper-roomed house. E. as before, fem.<BR>form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=012-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अट्टालिकाकार|अट्टालिकाकारः
अट्टालिकाकार m. (-रः) A bricklayer, a mason, a builder; born of a Śūdra<BR>mother and painter father.<BR> E. अट्टालिका, and कार who enables.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=012-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अट्टा
अट्टा f. (-ट्टा) Wandering as a beggar or devotee.<BR> E. अट्ट to go. See अटा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=012-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अठ
अठ r. 1st cl. (अठति) with a redundant इ. अठि (अंठते) To go, to go to or<BR>towards.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=012-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अड
अड r. 1st cl. (अडति) To strive or endeavour. 5th cl. (अडोति) To occupy<BR>or possess, (peculiar to the Vedas.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=012-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अड्ड
अड्ड r. 1st cl. (अड्डति)<BR>	 1. To connect.<BR>	 2. To solve, or demonstrate.<BR>	 3. To<BR>strive, to endeavour. The radical penultimate is द, and the root<BR>is also written by VOPADEVA, अद्द.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=012-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अण
अण r. 1st. cl. (अणति) To sound. (ङ,) 4th cl. (अण्यते) To breathe, to live;<BR>with प्र, to exist, to live. See अन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=012-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अणक|अणकः
अणक mfn. (कः-का-कं) Inferior, low.<BR> E. अण to sound, अच् affix; and कन्<BR>affix of depreciation; also written अण्णक, and आणक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=012-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अणव्य|अणव्यं
अणव्य n. (-व्यं) A field bearing panic,<BR> E. अणु panic. and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=012-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अणि|अणिः
अणि m. (-णिः)<BR>	 1. A pin or bolt at the extremity of the pole of a<BR>carriage, the pin of the axle.<BR>	 2. The edge or point of a sharp<BR>weapon.<BR>	 3. A limit, a boundary; also अणी.<BR> E. अण to sound, and<BR>इन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=012-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अणिमन्
अणिमन् m. (-मा)<BR>	 1. Subtility, infinite minuteness, moleculism.<BR>	 2. The<BR>same considered as a superhuman faculty, to be acquired by<BR>austere devotion and the performance of magical rites, or as<BR>possessed by a deity.<BR> E. अण an atom, and इमनिच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=012-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अणीयस्
अणीयस् mfn. (-यान्-यसी-यः) Very small.<BR> E. अणु small, and इयसुन्<BR>comparative aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=012-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अणु|अणुः
अणु m. (-णुः)<BR>	 1. An atom, a minute and elementary particle of matter.<BR>2. A sort of grain, (Panicum miliaceum, Rox.)<BR>	 m. or mfn. (-णुः-ण्वी-णु)<BR>1. Atomic, small, minute.<BR> E. अण to sound, and उ Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=012-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अणुक|अणुकः
अणुक mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>	 1. Skilful, clever.<BR>	 2. Small, minute.<BR> E. अणु small,<BR>and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=012-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अणुत्व
अणुत्व n. (-त्वं) The state or being of an atom, also अणुता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=012-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अणुभा
अणुभा f. (-भा) Lightning.<BR> E. अणु minute, and भा light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=012-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अणुरेणु|अणुरेणुः
अणुरेणु f. (-णुः) Small particles of dust, a dust of atoms.<BR> E. अणु, and<BR>रेणु dust.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=013-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अणुरेणुजाल
अणुरेणुजाल n. (लं) The motes in a sunbeam.<BR> E. अणुरेणु, and जाल as-<BR>semblage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=013-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अणुरेवती
अणुरेवती f. (-ती) A tree. (Croton polyandrum.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=013-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अणुव्रीहि|अणुव्रीहिः
अणुव्रीहि m. (-हिः) Small grain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=013-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अण्ड|अंडं|अण्डं|अंडः|अण्डः
अण्ड n. (-ण्डं)<BR>	 1. An egg.<BR>	 2. A testicle or the scrotum.<BR>	 3. Semen geni-<BR>tale.<BR>	 4. The musk bag, regarded as the scrotum of the deer.<BR>E. अम to go, and ड Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=013-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अण्डक|अंडकः|अण्डकः
अण्डक m. (-कः) The scrotum.<BR> E. अण्ड scrotum. and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=013-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अण्डकोटरपुष्पी
अण्डकोटरपुष्पी f. (-ष्पा) A plant, (perhaps Convolvulus argenteus.) See<BR>अजान्त्री.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=013-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अण्डकोश|अण्डकोशः
अण्डकोश m. (-शः) See the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=013-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अण्डकोष|अण्डकोषः
अण्डकोष m. (-षः)<BR>	 1. The scrotum.<BR>	 2. The testicle.<BR>	 3. A boundary.<BR>	 4. the<BR>rind of a fruit.<BR>	 5. Fruit.<BR> E. अण्ड a testicle, and कोश or कोष a<BR>sheathe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=013-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अण्डकोषक|अण्डकोषकः
अण्डकोषक m. (-कः) The scrotum.<BR> E. कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=013-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अण्डज|अण्डजः
अण्डज mfn. (-जः-जा-जं) Oviparous.<BR>	 m. (-जः)<BR>	 1. A serpent.<BR>	 2. A fish<BR>3. A bird.<BR>	 4. A lizard.<BR>	 f. (जा Musk.<BR> E. अण्ड and egg, &c. and<BR>ज what is born, from जन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=013-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अण्डाकार|अण्डाकारः
अण्डाकार mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Egg-shaped, oval, elliptical.<BR>	 m. (-रः) An oval,<BR>an ellipsis; also अण्डाकृति, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=013-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अण्डालु|अंडालुः|अण्डालुः
अण्डालु m. (लुः) A fish.<BR> E. अण्ड, and आलु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=013-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अण्डीर|अंडीरः|अण्डीरः
अण्डीर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A man.<BR>	 2. Strong, powerful.<BR> E. अण्ड, and ईर aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=013-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अण्वी
अण्वी f. (-ण्वी) A finger, (from the Vedas.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=013-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत|अतः
अत r. 1st cl. (अतति) To go, to move or approach progressively and<BR>continually. With an indicatory इ. अति (अंतति) To bind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=013-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतएव
अतएव ind. Even, thus, or hence, so, from this cause, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=013-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतट|अतटः
अतट m. (-टः) A precipice.<BR> E. अ neg. and तट a back.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=013-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतथ्य
अतथ्य mfn. (-थ्यः-थ्या-थ्यं) Untrue, false, unreal.<BR> E. अ neg. तथ्य true.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=013-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतनु
अतनु mfn. (नुः-नुः-न्वी-नु) Large, great, not small or slight.<BR> E. अ neg. तनु<BR>minute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=013-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतन्द्र|अतंद्र
अतन्द्र mfn. (-न्द्रः-न्द्रा-न्द्रं) Awake, active, alert.<BR> E. अ neg. तन्द्रा sloth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=013-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतन्द्रित|अतंद्रित
अतन्द्रित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Smart, active, energetical.<BR> E. अ neg. तन्द्रित<BR>slothful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=013-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतप
अतप mfn. (-पः-पा-पं)<BR>	 1. Cool.<BR>	 2. Unanxious.<BR>	 3. Unemployed.<BR>	 4. Unos-<BR>tentatious.<BR> E. अ neg. तप ardor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=013-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतप्त
अतप्त mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं) Cool, not heated.<BR> E. अ neg. तप्त heated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=013-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतर्क|अतर्कः
अतर्क m. (-र्कः) Absence of reasoning, want of consideration.<BR> E. अ neg.<BR>तर्क consideration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=013-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतर्कित
अतर्कित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Unconsidered.<BR>	 2. Unexpected, unweighed.<BR>adv.<BR>	 n. (-तं) Unexpectedly, suddenly<BR> E. अ neg. अकित considered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=013-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतर्क्य
अतर्क्य mfn. (-र्क्यः-र्क्या-र्क्यं) Unsearchable, incomprehensible, inscrutable. E.<BR>अ neg. तर्क्य to be investigated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=013-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतर्पणीय
अतर्पणीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Insatiable.<BR> E. अ neg. तर्पणीय to be satisfied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=013-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतर्पित
अतर्पित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Unsatisfied.<BR> E. अ neg. तर्पित satisfied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=013-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतल|अतलं|अतलः
अतल n. (-लं) A particular hell or division of the infernal regions, the<BR>portion immediately below the earth.<BR> E. अ neg. and तल bottom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=013-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतलस्पर्श|अतलस्पर्शः
अतलस्पर्श mfn. (-र्शः-र्शा-र्शं) Very deep, bottomless.<BR> E. अ neg. तल bottom,<BR>and स्पर्श the touch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=013-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतलस्पृश्
अतलस्पृश् mfn. (स्पृक्) See the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=013-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतस्
अतस् ind.<BR>	 1. Hence, therefore, from this cause.<BR>	 2. An interjection of<BR>command.<BR> E. एतद् this, and तस् affix; irregular formation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=013-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतस|अतसः
अतस m. (-सः)<BR>	 1. Wind, air.<BR>	 2. The self, the soul.<BR>	 3. Cloth made from<BR>bark.<BR>	 4. A weapon.<BR>	 f. (-सी)<BR>	 1. Common flax, (Linum usitatissimum.)<BR>Śaṇa, Bengal sun, a kind of flax, (Crotolaria juncea.)<BR> E. अत to go,<BR>and the Uṇādi affix असच, when fem. with ङीष् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=013-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अति
अति ind. Over, beyond, exceeding, much, very much, &c. it implies<BR>generally excess, or preeminence.<BR> E. अत to go, and इन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=013-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिकथ|अतिकथः
अतिकथ mfn. (-थः-था-थं)<BR>	 1. Incredible, unworthy of belief or trust.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=013-b" target="_blank">Page013-b+ 60</a>]<BR>2. Erring, deviating from the duties of a profession or caste.<BR>	 f. (-था)<BR>Idle or unmeaning speech.<BR> E. अति excess or exceeding, and कथा<BR>speech: some words substitute for this word, इतिकथ q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=013-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिकन्दक|अतिकंदकः|अतिकन्दकः
अतिकन्दक m. (-कः) A tree. See हस्तिकन्द.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=013-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिकाय|अतिकायः
अतिकाय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Gigantic.<BR> E. अति, and काय body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=013-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिकृच्छ्र|अतिकृच्छ्रः
अतिकृच्छ्र n. (-च्छ्र)<BR>	 1. A kind of penance, eating a handful of food a day<BR>for six days, and fasting three.<BR>	 2. Extreme pain or suffering. E.<BR>अति, and कृच्छ्र penance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=013-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिकृति|अतिकृतिः
अतिकृति f. (-तिः) A kind of metre, a stanza of four lines, with twenty-<BR>five syllables to each line.<BR> E. अति, and कृति another metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=013-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिकृश
अतिकृश mfn. (-शः-शा-शी-शं) Very thin, emaciated.<BR> E. अति, and कृश thin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=013-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिक्रम|अतिक्रमः
अतिक्रम m. (-मः)<BR>	 1. Going over or beyond, lit. or fig.<BR>	 2. Surpassing,<BR>excelling.<BR>	 3. Transgressing.<BR>	 4. Contrariety, opposition.<BR>	 5. Neglect,<BR>aversion, disregard.<BR>	 6. Privation.<BR>	 7. A groundless demand.<BR>	 8. A<BR>gallant attack, advance of an army in front of an enemy. See अति-<BR>क्रम<BR> E. अति over, beyond, and क्रम to go; going beyond duty or<BR>daring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=013-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिक्रमिन्
अतिक्रमिन् mfn. (-मी-मिणी-मि)<BR>	 1. Transgressing.<BR>	 2. Exceeding, surpassing.<BR>E. अतिक्रम, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=013-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिक्रम्य
अतिक्रम्य ind. Having gone over or beyond. i. e. Exceeded, transgressed,<BR>surpassed, overcome, &c.<BR> E. अति before, क्रम to go, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=013-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिक्रश
अतिक्रश mfn. (-शः-शा-शी-शं) Thin, emaciated.<BR> E. अति, and क्रश spare; ऋ<BR>changed to र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=013-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिक्रान्त|अतिक्रांत|अतिक्रान्तः
अतिक्रान्त mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं)<BR>	 1. Transgressed, exceeded, passed the proper<BR>bounds.<BR>	 2. Excelled, surpassed.<BR>	 3. Passed in time.<BR>	 4. Attacked,<BR>assaulted.<BR>	 5. Excessive, unlimited.<BR>	 6. Prolix, diffuse.<BR>	 7. Disregarded,<BR>disliked.<BR> E. अति, and क्रम to go, aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=013-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिक्रामक|अतिक्रामकः
अतिक्रामक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Exceeding, one who oversteps due bounds.<BR>E. अति, and क्रम to go, स्खुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=013-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिगण्ड|अतिगंडः|अतिगण्डः
अतिगण्ड m. (-ण्डः) The sixth of the twenty-seven astrological yogas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=013-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिगन्ध|अतिगंध|अतिगन्धः
अतिगन्ध m. (-न्धः)<BR>	 1. A fragrant grass, lemon-grass, (Andropogon<BR>schœnanthus.)<BR>	 2. Champac, (Michelia champaca.)<BR>	 3. A kind of<BR>bean, (Phaseolus mungo)<BR>	 4. Sulphur.<BR>	 mfn. (-न्धः-न्धा-न्धं) Of strong<BR>or exceeding odour.<BR> E. अति, and गन्ध smell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=013-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिगन्धालु|अतिगंधालु|अतिगन्धालुः
अतिगन्धालु m. (-लुः) A creeper.<BR> E. अति, and गन्धालु a plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=013-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिगर्व्वित|अतिगर्वित|अतिगर्व्वितः
अतिगर्व्वित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Arrogant, proud.<BR> E. अति very, गर्व्व pride, and<BR>इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=013-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिगर्हित
अतिगर्हित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Despicable, vile.<BR> E. अति before, गर्हित reproached.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=013-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिगुप्त
अतिगुप्त mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं) Very secret, closely hidden or concealed. E.<BR>अति, and गुप्त hidden.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=013-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिगुहा
अतिगुहा f. (-हा) A plant, (Hemionites, cordifolia, Rox.) See पृष्णिपर्णी. E.<BR>अति surpassing, and गुहा a hole; rising above the ground.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=013-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिचर
अतिचर mfn. (-रः-रा-री-रं) Going over or beyond, lit. or fig.<BR>	 f. (-रा) A<BR>plant, (Hibiscus mutabilis.) See पद्मचारिणी.<BR> E. अतिचर to go beyond,<BR>अच् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=013-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिचार|अतिचारः
अतिचार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Going quickly.<BR>	 2. Going over or beyond.<BR>	 3. Sur-<BR>passing, excelling.<BR>	 4. The passage of a planet from one zodiacal<BR>sing to another, in a shorter than common period.<BR> E. अति before चर<BR>to go, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=013-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिच्छत्र|अतिच्छत्रः|अतिछत्र
अतिच्छत्र m. (-त्रः) A mushroom.<BR>	 f. (-त्रा)<BR>	 1. Anise, (Anethum pimpinella.)<BR>2. Barleria longifolia.<BR> E. अति, and च्छत्र an umbrella.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=013-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिच्छत्रक|अतिच्छत्रकः|अतिछत्रक
अतिच्छत्रक m. (-कः) A mushroom<BR> E. कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=013-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिजगती
अतिजगती f. (-ती) A form of metre, a stanza of four lines. with thirteen<BR>syllables in each line.<BR> E. अति, and जगती another metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=013-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिजव|अतिजवः
अतिजव mfn. (-वः-वा-वं) Marching fast or fleet.<BR> E. अति, and जव quick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=013-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिजागर|अतिजागरः
अतिजागर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Very wakeful, restless.<BR>	 m. (-रः) The black<BR>curlew.<BR> E. अति, and जागर wakeful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=013-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिजीर्ण
अतिजीर्ण mfn. (-र्ण-र्णा-र्णं) Very old.<BR> E. अति, and जीर्णं old.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=013-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिडीन|अतिडीनं
अतिडीन n. (-नं) Very lofty or very rapid flight of birds.<BR> E. अति, and<BR>डीन flying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=013-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतितराम्
अतितराम् ind. Much, excessively, exceedingly.<BR> E. अति, and तराम् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=014-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतितीव्र
अतितीव्र mfn. (-व्रः-व्रा-व्रं) Very sharp or pungent.<BR>	 f. (-व्रा) Doob grass. E.<BR>अति, and तीव्र sharp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=014-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतितीक्ष्ण|अतितीक्ष्णः
अतितीक्ष्ण mfn. (-क्ष्णः-क्ष्णा-क्ष्णं) Very pungent, sharp, hot or acrid<BR> E. अति,<BR>and तीक्ष्ण sharp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=014-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिथि|अतिथिः
अतिथि mfn. (-थिः-था) A guest, a person entitled to the rites of hospitality.<BR>m. (-थिः)<BR>	 1. A proper name, the son of KUŚA and grandson of<BR>RĀMA.<BR>	 2. Wrath.<BR> E. अत to go, and इथिन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=014-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिथिक्रिया
अतिथिक्रिया f. (-या) Hospitality considered as a religious duty.<BR> E. अतिथि,<BR>and क्रिया act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=014-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिथिद्वेष
अतिथिद्वेष m. (-षः) Inhospitality.<BR> E. अतिथि, and द्वेष dislike.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=014-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिथिपूजन|अतिथिपूजनं
अतिथिपूजन n. (-नं) Hospitality considered as one of the principal<BR>sacraments of the Hindus.<BR> E. अतिथि a guest, and पूजन worshipping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=014-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिथिसत्कार|अतिथिसत्कारः
अतिथिसत्कार m. (-रः) The rite of hospitality, hospitality.<BR> E. अतिथि, and<BR>सत्कार pious rite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=014-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिथिसेवा
अतिथिसेवा f. (-वा) Service of a guest, hospitality.<BR> E. अतिथि, and सेवा<BR>service.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=014-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिदातृ
अतिदातृ m. (-ता) A liberal man.<BR> E. अति, and दातृ who gives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=014-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिदान|अतिदानं
अतिदान n. (-नं) Munificence, giving largely.<BR> E. अति and दान gift.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=014-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिदाह|अतिदाहः
अतिदाह m. (-हः)<BR>	 1. Great heat.<BR>	 2. Violent inflammation.<BR> E. अति and<BR>दाह burning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=014-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिदिष्ट|अतिदिष्टः
अतिदिष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं) Substituted, supplementary.<BR> E. अति over, and<BR>दिष्ट enjoined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=014-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिदुःसह
अतिदुःसह mfn. (-हः-हा-हं) Intolerable, unbearable, not to be borne or<BR>endured.<BR> E. अति and दुःसह painful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=014-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिदुर्गत
अतिदुर्गत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) In great difficulty or distress.<BR> E. अति and दुर्गत<BR>badly off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=014-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिदुष्कर
अतिदुष्कर mfn. (-रः-रा-री-रं) Very arduous, very difficult.<BR> E. अति and<BR>दुष्कर difficult.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=014-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिदूर
अतिदूर n. (-रं) A great distance, afar off.<BR> E. अति, and दूर afar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=014-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिदेश|अतिदेशः
अतिदेश m. (-शः) Substitution, supplement.<BR> E. अति, and देश direction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=014-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिदोष
अतिदोष m. (-षः) A great fault.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=014-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिधृति|अतिधृतिः
अतिधृति f. (-तिः) A kind of metre, a stanza of four lines, with nineteen<BR>syllables in each line.<BR> E. अति and धृति another metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=014-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिनौ
अतिनौ mfn. (-नौः-नौः-नु) Landed from a boat.<BR> E. अति over, beyond, and<BR>नौ a boat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=014-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिपतन|अतिपतनं
अतिपतन n. (-नं) Exceeding, going beyond bounds.<BR> E. अति beyond and<BR>पत to go, ल्यट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=014-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिपथिन्
अतिपथिन् m. (-पन्था) A good road.<BR> E. अति, and पथिन् a road; a very<BR>road.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=014-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिपर|अतिपरः
अतिपर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A great enemy.<BR>	 2. One who has conquered his<BR>enemy.<BR> E. अति and परः a foe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=014-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिपात|अतिपातः
अतिपात m. (-तः)<BR>	 1. Neglect of duty.<BR>	 2. Transgression, deviation from<BR>laws or customs.<BR>	 3. Contrariety, opposition.<BR>	 4. Going beyond<BR>bounds. अति beyond, and पात from पत to go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=014-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिपातक|अतिपातकं
अतिपातक n. (-कं) Heinous sin, the worst of the great sins.<BR> E. अति,<BR>and पातक crime.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=014-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिपातकिन्
अतिपातकिन् mfn. (-की-किनी-कि) A great sinner, flagrantly criminal. E.<BR>अतिपातक and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=014-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिपारक
अतिपारक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Very capable, of great abilities.<BR> E. अति, and<BR>पारक who traverses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=014-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिपेशल
अतिपेशल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Very dexterous or clever.<BR> E. अति and पेशल<BR>clever.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=014-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिप्रसङ्ग|अतिप्रसंग|अतिप्रसंगः|अतिप्रसङ्गः
अतिप्रसङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः) Frequent repetition, uninterrupted continuance. E.<BR>अति, and प्रसाद connexion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=014-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिबल|अतिबलः
अतिबल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Strong, powerful.<BR>	 m. (-लः) An active soldier.<BR>	 f.<BR>(-ला) A plant, (Sida cordifolia, and rhombifolia.) See वाट्यपुष्पी E.<BR>अति and बल strong.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=014-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिभार|अतिभारः
अतिभार m. (-रः) A great or excessive burden.<BR> E. अति, and भार a load.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=014-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिभारग|अतिभारगः
अतिभारग m. (-गः) A mule.<BR> E. अतिभार, and ग who goes with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=014-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिभी
अतिभी m. (-भीः) Lightning, the flash accompanying thunder.<BR> E. अति,<BR>and भी dread.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=014-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिभूमि|अतिभूमिः
अतिभूमि f. (-मिः)<BR>	 1. Something more than was expected or aimed at.<BR>2. Extensive land or limits.<BR>	 3. Improper conduct, exceeding proper<BR>bounds.<BR> E. अति, and भूमि land.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=014-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिभृत
अतिभृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Carefully cherished or protected.<BR> E. अति and<BR>भृत cherished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=014-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिमङ्गल्य|अतिमंगल्य|अतिमङ्गल्यः
अतिमङ्गल्य mfn. (-ल्यः-ल्या-ल्यं) Very auspicious.<BR>	 m. (ल्यः) A fruit,<BR>(Ægle, or Cratœva marmelos) See विल्व.<BR> E. अत्ति, and मङ्गल<BR>auspicious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=014-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिमर्य्याद|अतिमर्याद|अतिमर्य्यादः
अतिमर्य्याद mfn. (-दः-दा-दं) or adverb n. (दं) Much, excessive, unlimited,<BR>unbounded.<BR> E. अति, and मर्य्यादा a limit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=014-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिमर्त्त्य
अतिमर्त्त्य mfn. (र्त्त्यः-र्त्त्य-र्त्त्यं) Superhuman, divine.<BR> E. अति and मत, mortal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=014-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिमात्र|अतिमात्रं
अतिमात्र mfn. (त्रः-त्रा-त्रं) or adverb.<BR>	 n. त्रं Much, excessive.<BR> E. अति, and मात्रा<BR>a minute quantity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=014-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिमानुष
अतिमानुष mfn. (-ष-षी-षं)<BR>	 1. Superhuman, more than mortal.<BR>	 2. Immortal,<BR>divine.<BR> E. अति, and मानुष human.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=014-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिमाय
अतिमाय mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>	 1. Free from illusion.<BR>	 2. Entirely liberated, or<BR>freed.<BR> E. अति and माया delusion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=014-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिमित
अतिमित mfn. (तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Dry, not wet.<BR>	 2. Over measured, exceeding.<BR>E. अ neg. तिमित moist, or अति and मित meted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=014-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिमुक्त|अतिमुक्तः
अतिमुक्त mfn. (-क्त-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>	 1. Seedless, barren.<BR>	 2. Entirely liberated or<BR>freed.<BR>	 m. (क्तः)<BR>	 1. A creeping plant, (Gœrtnera racemosa.) See<BR>माधवीलता 2. A tree, (Dalbergia oujeiniensis)<BR> E. अति, and मुक्त<BR>liberated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=014-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिमुक्तक|अतिमुक्तकः
अतिमुक्तक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A tree, (Dalbergia oujeiniensis.)<BR>	 2. Mountain<BR>ebony. See तिन्दुक.<BR>	 3. A creeper. (Gœrtnera racemosa, &c.) E. See<BR>अतिमुक्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=014-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिमोदा
अतिमोदा f. (-दा) A tree, (Jasmimum arboreum.)<BR> E. अति, and मोद<BR>delight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=014-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिरथ|अतिरथः
अतिरथ m. (-थः) A warrior of a particular order fighting in a car. E.<BR>अति, and रथ a chariot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=014-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिरथिन्
अतिरथिन् m. (-थी) A warrior of a particular class, fighting in a car. E.<BR>अति before रथ a car. and इनि aff. also अतिरथ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=014-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिरसा
अतिरसा f. (-सा) A creeper.<BR> E. अति, and रस flavour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=014-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिरिक्त|अतिरिक्तः
अतिरिक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं) Excessive, exceeding,<BR> E. अति, and रिव to flow,<BR>with the participial affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=014-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिरिक्तता
अतिरिक्तता f. (-ता) Increase of bulk or quantity, expansion, enlargement,<BR>elevation, &c.<BR> E. ता added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=014-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिरेक|अतिरेकः
अतिरेक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Much, excessive.<BR> E. अति, and रिच to flow,<BR>affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=014-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिरेकिन्
अतिरेकिन् mfn. (-की-किणी-कि) More, superior.<BR> E. अतिरेक and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=014-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिरोग|अतिरोगः
अतिरोग m. (-गः) Consumption, (Phthisis pulmonalis)<BR> E. अति and रोग<BR>disease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=014-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिरोमश|अतिरोमशः
अतिरोमश m. (-शः) A wild goat, or according to some, a large monkey.<BR>mfn. (-शः-शा-शं) Very hairy.<BR> E. अति, and रोमश hairy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=014-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिलुब्ध
अतिलुब्ध mfn. (-ब्धः-ब्धा-ब्धं) Very covetous.<BR> E. अति, and लुब्ध covetous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=014-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिलोमश
अतिलोमश mfn. (-शः-शा-शं) Very hairy.<BR> E. अति, and लोमश hairy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=014-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिवर्त्तन|अतिवर्तन|अतिवर्तनं
अतिवर्त्तन n. (-न) An accident, a circumstance not capable of being<BR>prevented or guarded against.<BR> E. अति, and वर्त्तन being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=014-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिवर्त्तुल|अतिवर्तुल|अतिवर्तुलः|अतिवर्त्तुलः
अतिवर्त्तुल m. (-लः) A kind of grain.<BR> E. अति, and वर्त्तूल round.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=014-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिवात|अतिवातः
अतिवात m. (-तः) A storm, a hurricane.<BR> E. अति, and वात wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=014-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिवाद|अतिवादः
अतिवाद m. (-दः) Opprobrious or unfriendly speech. See अभिवाद.<BR> E. अति<BR>overcoming, वद to speak, and घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=014-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिबालक|अतिबालकः
अतिबालक m. (-कः) An infant, mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Childish.<BR> E. अति and<BR>बालक a child.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=014-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिविकट|अतिविकटः
अतिविकट m. (-टः) A vicious elephant.<BR>	 mfn. (-टः-टा-टं) Very fierce, very<BR>formidable.<BR> E. अति, and विकट large or formidable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=014-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिविष
अतिविष mfn. (-षः-षा-षं) Antidote, exceeding or subduing poison.<BR>	 f. (-षा)<BR>A tree used in medicine, the bark is also employed in dyeing; it<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=015-a" target="_blank">Page015-a+ 60</a>]<BR>is of three kinds; white, red, and black. (Atis or Betula.)<BR> E. अति<BR>overcoming, and विष poison.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=014-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिवृष्टि|अतिवृष्टिः
अतिवृष्टि f. (-ष्टिः) Heavy rain.<BR> E. अति, and वृष्टि rain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=015-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिवेल|अतिवेलं
अतिवेल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) or adverb n. (-लं) Much, excessive, unlimited.<BR>E. अति, and वेला a limit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=015-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिव्यय
अतिव्यय m. (-यः) Extravagance, great expenditure.<BR> E. अति, and व्यय<BR>expenditure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=015-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिव्ययिन्
अतिव्ययिन् mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि) Extravagant, spendthrift.<BR> E. अतिव्यय, and<BR>इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=015-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिव्यथा
अतिव्यथा f. (-था) Excessive pain, agony.<BR> E. अति, and व्यथा pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=015-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिव्याप्ति|अतिव्याप्तिः
अतिव्याप्ति f. (-प्तिः)<BR>	 1. Extreme pervasion or extension.<BR>	 2. Going beyond<BR>the mark, drawing an inference unwarranted by the premises. E.<BR>अति, and व्याप्ति spreading.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=015-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिशक्करी
अतिशक्करी f. (-रो) A kind of metre; of four lines, with fifteen syllables<BR>to the line.<BR> E. अति beyond, शक्करी another metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=015-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिशक्त
अतिशक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं) Very powerful.<BR> E. अति, and शक्त powerful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=015-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिशक्ति|अतिशक्तिः
अतिशक्ति f. (-क्तिः) Great power.<BR> E. अति, and शक्ति power.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=015-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिशक्तिता
अतिशक्तिता f. (-ता) Heroic valor, prowess.<BR> E. अति, शक्ति power, and ता aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=015-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिशक्तिभाज्
अतिशक्तिभाज् m. (-क्) A man of gigantic power.<BR> E. अतिशक्ति, and भाज्<BR>who possesses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=015-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिशय|अतिशयः
अतिशय If an adj. mas. only. (-यः) If an adverb n. (-यं) much, excessive.<BR>E. शीङ to sleep; अति being prefixed, to excel; aff. अच्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=015-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिशयन|अतिशयनं
अतिशयन adv.<BR>	 n. (-नं) See अतिशय.<BR> E. ल्युट् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=015-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिशयिन्
अतिशयिन् mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि)<BR>	 1. Superior, exceeding.<BR>	 2. Increased,<BR>improved. &c.<BR> E. अतिशय, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=015-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिशयोक्ति|अतिशयोक्तिः
अतिशयोक्ति f. (-क्तिः)<BR>	 1. Hyperbole.<BR>	 2. Verbosity, prolixity.<BR> E. अतिशय<BR>excess, and उक्ति speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=015-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिशायन|अतिशायनं
अतिशायन adv.<BR>	 n. (-नं) adj.<BR>	 mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Much, excessive.<BR> E. अतिशय,<BR>and ल्युट् the ante-pen, lengthened.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=015-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिशायित
अतिशायित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Exceeded, surpassed, excelled.<BR>	 2. Increased.<BR>E. अति before शीङ, and क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=015-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिशोभन|अतिशोभनः
अतिशोभन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>	 1. Exellent.<BR>	 2. Chief, principal.<BR>	 3. Beautiful,<BR>splendid.<BR> E. अति, and शुभ to shine, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=015-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिसञ्चय|अतिसंचय
अतिसञ्चय m. (-यः) A hoard, a great accumulation.<BR> E. अति, and सञ्चय heap.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=015-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिसंहित
अतिसंहित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Cheated, deceived, imposed upon.<BR>2. Explained. declared.<BR> E. अति, before संहित combined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=015-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिसन्धान|अतिसंधान|अतिसंधानं
अतिसन्धान n. (-नं) Falsehood, deceit, fraud, cheating, overreaching. E.<BR>अति, before सन्धान combining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=015-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिसर्जन|अतिसर्जनं|अतिसर्ज्जनं
अतिसर्जन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Liberality, giving.<BR>	 2. Appointing, engaging.<BR>	 3. A<BR>gift, a donation.<BR>	 4. Slaughter, killing.<BR> E. अति, and सृज to create,<BR>ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=015-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिसान्तपन|अतिसांतपनं
अतिसान्तपन n. (-नं) Severe penance or expiation, especially for the guilt<BR>of eating unclean animals; taking as food nothing but cow's urine,<BR>cowdung, curds, milk, and ghee, each two days in succession. E.<BR>अति, and शान्तपन penance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=015-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिसाम्या
अतिसाम्या f. (-म्या) Liquorice plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=015-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिसार|अतिसारः
अतिसार m. (-रः) Diarrhœa or dysentery.<BR> E. अति, and सार what goes; from<BR>सृ to go, with घञ् affix; also अतीसार.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=015-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिसारकिन्
अतिसारकिन् mfn. (-की-किणी-कि) Dysenteric, afflicted with dysentery.<BR>E. अतिसार, and the affixes इनि and कुक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=015-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिसारिन्
अतिसारिन् mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>	 1. Afflicted with dysentery.<BR>	 2. Cathartic.<BR>E. अतिसार, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=015-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिस्फिर|अतिस्फिरः
अतिस्फिर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Very tremulous.<BR> E. अति, and स्फिर trembling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=015-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिहसित|अतिहसितं
अतिहसित n. (-तं) Violent laughter.<BR> E. अति, and हसित laughing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=015-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिहास|अतिहासः
अतिहास m. (-सः) A horselaugh, violent laughter.<BR> E. अति, and हास<BR>laughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=015-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतीन्द्रिय|अतींद्रिय|अतीन्द्रियं|अतीन्द्रियः
अतीन्द्रिय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Imperceptible, unattainable by the senses. E.<BR>अति beyond, and इन्द्रिय an organ of sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=015-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतीक्ष्ण
अतीक्ष्ण mfn. (-क्षणः-क्ष्णाः-क्ष्णं) Blunt, not sharp, dull, obtuse.<BR> E. अ neg.<BR>तीक्ष्ण sharp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=015-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतीक्ष्णता
अतीक्ष्णता f. (-ता) Bluntness, Se अतीक्ष्णत्व n. (-त्वं)<BR> E. ता or त्व added to<BR>the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=015-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतीच्छ
अतीच्छ mfn. (-छः-छा-छं) Very desirous, eager, ardent.<BR> E. अति, and<BR>इच्छा wish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=015-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतीत|अतीतं|अतीतः
अतीत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Passed, gone.<BR>	 2. Passed away, deceased, dead.<BR>3. Liberated from worldly restraint.<BR>	 4. Surpassed, gone over or<BR>beyond.<BR> E. अति, and इत gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=015-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतीतकाल
अतीतकाल m. (-लः) In gram. the preterite tense.<BR> E. अतीत and काल time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=015-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतीव
अतीव Ind. Much, very much, much indeed.<BR> E. अति, and इव as, so.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=015-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतीव्र
अतीव्र mfn. (-व्र-व्रा-व्रं) Blunt, dull, insipid.<BR> E. अ neg तीव्र sharp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=015-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतीसार|अतीसारः
अतीसार m. (रः) Diarrhœa or dysentery. See अतिसार.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=015-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतुङ्ग
अतुङ्ग mfn. (-ङ्गः-ङ्गा-ङ्गं)<BR>	 1. Short of stature, a dwarf.<BR>	 2. Low.<BR> E. अ neg.<BR>तुङ्ग tall or high.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=015-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतुन्द|अतुंद
अतुन्द mfn. (-न्दः-न्दा-न्दं) Lank, thin.<BR> E. अ neg. तुन्द fat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=015-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतुल|अतुलः
अतुल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Unequalled, m. (-लः) A plant that has an oily<BR>seed, (Sesamum orientale.)<BR> E. अ neg, तुल to be like, क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=015-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतुलनीय
अतुलनीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Incomparable.<BR> E. अ neg. तुलनीय comparable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=015-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतुल्य|अतुल्यं
अतुल्य mfn. (-ल्यः-ल्या-ल्यं) Unequalled, unparalleled.<BR> E. अ neg. तुल्य to be<BR>equalled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=015-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतुहिनरश्मि
अतुहिनरश्मि m. (-स्मिः) The sun, whose rays are not cold, i. e. hot: also<BR>analogous compounds, as अतुहिनधामन्, अतुहिनरुचि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=015-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतृप्त
अतृप्त mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं) Unsatisfied.<BR> E. अ neg. तृप्ति satisfied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=015-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतृप्ति|अतृप्तिः
अतृप्ति f. (-प्तिः) Insatiableness, voraciousness.<BR> E. अ neg. तृप्ति satisfaction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=015-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतेजस्
अतेजस् mfn. (-जाः-जाः-जः) Dark, dim, dull.<BR>	 n. (-जः)<BR>	 1. Shade, shadow.<BR>2. Insignificance, feebleness, imbecility.<BR> E. अ neg. तेजस light or spirit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=015-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतेजस्विन्
अतेजस्विन् mfn. (-स्वी-स्विनी-स्वि) Void of splendour or energy.<BR> E. अ neg.<BR>तेजस्विन् splendid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=015-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतोषणीय
अतोषणीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Implacable, not to be appeased.<BR> E. अ neg.<BR>तोषणीय to be pleased.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=015-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्क|अत्कः
अत्क m. (-त्कः) A limb, a member of the body.<BR>	 mfn. (-त्कः-त्का-त्कं) A<BR>traveller.<BR> E. अत to go, and कन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=015-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्ता
अत्ता f. (-त्ता)<BR>	 1. A mother, 2. an elder sister.<BR>	 3. A mother's elder sister.<BR>E. अत to go, अच, and टाप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=015-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्ति|अत्तिः
अत्ति f. (-त्तिः) In theatrical language, an elder sister.<BR> E. अत to go,<BR>क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=015-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्तिका
अत्तिका f. (-का) In theatrical language, an elder sister.<BR> E. अत्ता a<BR>mother, and कन् affix, who is, as it were, a mother; it is also<BR>written अन्तिका and अर्विका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=015-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्तृ
अत्तृ mfn. (-त्ता-त्त्वी-त्तृ) A feeder, one who eats.<BR> E. अद to eat. शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=015-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्नु|अत्नुः
अत्नु m. (-त्नुः) The sun.<BR> E. अत to go, क्नु Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=015-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्य|अत्यः
अत्य m. (-त्यः) A horse, from the Vedas.<BR> E. अत to go constantly. यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=015-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यजनीय
अत्यजनीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Not to be abandoned.<BR> E. अ neg. त्यजनीय to be<BR>abandoned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=015-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यन्त|अत्यंत|अत्यन्तं|अत्यन्तः
अत्यन्त mfn. or adv.<BR>	 n. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं) Much, excessive.<BR> E. अति beyond, and<BR>अन्त end or boundary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=015-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यन्तकोपन|अत्यन्तकोपनः
अत्यन्तकोपन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Very passionate.<BR> E. अत्यन्त, and कोपन<BR>passionate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=015-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यन्तगामिन्
अत्यन्तगामिन् mfn. (-मी-मिनी-मि) What goes much or quickly.<BR> E. अत्यन्त and<BR>गामिन् who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=015-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यन्तसुकुमार|अत्यन्तसुकुमारः
अत्यन्तसुकुमार m. (-रः) A species of grain, (Panicum Italicum.)<BR> E. अत्यन्त,<BR>and सुकुमार very soft.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=015-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यन्ताभाव|अत्यन्ताभावः
अत्यन्ताभाव m. (-वः) (In logic) absolute negation or nonexistence. E.<BR>अत्यन्त much, अभाव not being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=015-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यन्तिक|अत्यंतिक|अत्यन्तिकः
अत्यन्तिक m. (-कः) One who rambles much, a great rover.<BR>	 mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Much, exceeding.<BR> E. अत्यन्त, with ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=015-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यन्तीन|अत्यंतीन|अत्यन्तीनः
अत्यन्तीन m. (-नः) One who goes quickly or actively.<BR> E. अत्यन्त much,<BR>and ईन for गामिन् who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=015-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यम्ल|अत्यम्लं|अत्यम्लः
अत्यम्ल mfn. (-म्लः-म्ला-म्लं) Very sour.<BR>	 m. (-म्लः) A tree, (Spondias mangifera.)<BR>f. (-म्ला) Another plant and fruit; a species of citron. See मातुलुङ्गी<BR>E. अति, and अम्ल sour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=015-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यम्लपर्णी|अत्यम्लपर्ण्णी
अत्यम्लपर्णी f. (-र्णी) A creeper and medicinal plant.<BR> E. अति excessive, अम्ल<BR>sour; and पर्ण a leaf, with the fem. aff. ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=016-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यय|अत्ययः
अत्यय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. Death.<BR>	 2. Distress.<BR>	 3. Transgression.<BR>	 4. Vice, fault,<BR>guilt.<BR>	 5. Punishment.<BR>	 6. Going over or beyond.<BR>	 7. Absence.<BR>	 8. Loss,<BR>destruction.<BR> E. अति beyond, away, इण to go, and अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=016-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्ययित
अत्ययित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Exceeded, surpassed.<BR>	 2. Outraged.<BR> E. अति<BR>before इण to go, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=016-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यर्थ|अत्यर्थं
अत्यर्थ n. adv. or mfn. adj. (-र्थः-र्था-र्थं) Much, excessive.<BR> E. अति, and अर्थ<BR>substance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=016-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यल्प|अत्यल्पं
अत्यल्प mfn. (-ल्पः-ल्पा-ल्पं) Very small, very little.<BR> E. अति very, and अल्प<BR>small.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=016-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यष्टी
अत्यष्टी f. (-ष्टी) A kind of metre, a stanza of four lines, with seventeen<BR>syllables to the line.<BR> E. अति beyond, अष्टी another metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=016-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यसम
अत्यसम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं) Very rough, uneven, craggy.<BR> E. अति, and<BR>असम unequal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=016-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्याकार|अत्याकारः
अत्याकार m. (-रः) Censure, blame, contempt.<BR> E. अति and आङ prefixed<BR>to कृ to do, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=016-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्याचार|अत्याचारं|अत्याचारः
अत्याचार m. (-रः) Deviating from prescribed observances, contemning<BR>religious and moral laws.<BR> E. अति, and आचार observance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=016-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्याचारिन्
अत्याचारिन् mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि) Transgressing.<BR> E. अत्याचार, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=016-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्याज्य|अत्याज्यं
अत्याज्य mfn. (-ज्यः-ज्याः-ज्यं) Not to be abandoned.<BR> E. अ neg. त्याज्य to be<BR>abandoned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=016-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्याशा
अत्याशा f. (-शा) Unreasonable hope or desire.<BR> E. अति, and आशा hope.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=016-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्याहार
अत्याहार m. (-रः) Excessive food.<BR> E. अति, and आहार food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=016-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्याहारिन्
अत्याहारिन् mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि) Eating excessively, a glutton, a gorman-<BR>dizer.<BR> E. अत्याहार, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=016-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्याहित|अत्याहितं
अत्याहित n. (-तं)<BR>	 1. Great dread.<BR>	 2. Desperate or daring action.<BR> E. अति<BR>with धा to have; आङ prefixed. and the participial क्त; हि is substi-<BR>tuted for धा; what engrosses the mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=016-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्युक्ति|अत्युक्तिः
अत्युक्ति f. (-क्तिः)<BR>	 1. Idle or excessive talk.<BR>	 2. Expatiating, enlarging.<BR>	 3. A<BR>figure of rhetoric, description of any thing surprising or extraordi-<BR>nary, hyperbole.<BR> E. अति, and उक्ति speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=016-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्युक्था
अत्युक्था f. (-क्था) A kind of metre, a stanza of four lines, with two<BR>syllables to the line.<BR> E. अति, and उक्था another kind; it is also<BR>read अत्युक्ता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=016-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्युत्कट
अत्युत्कट mfn. (-टः-टा-टं) Extreme, exceeding great.<BR> E. अति, and उत्कट<BR>much.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=016-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्युत्कृष्ट
अत्युत्कृष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>	 1. Most excellent, best.<BR>	 2. Most valuable,<BR>precious.<BR> E. अति, and उत्कृष्ट excellent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=016-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यूह|अत्यूहः
अत्यूह m. (-हः) A gallinule.<BR>	 f. (-हा) A plant, (Jasminum villosum, Rox,<BR>or in Bengal, Nyctanthes tristis) See शेफालिका.<BR> E. अति, and ऊह<BR>to reason.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=016-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्र|अत्रः
अत्र ind. In this place, here, herein.<BR> E. त्र being substituted for the<BR>termination of the seventh case of इदम् this.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=016-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्रप
अत्रप mfn. (-पः-पा-पं) Shameless, immodest.<BR> E. अ neg. त्रपा shame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=016-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्रभवत्|अत्रभवन्त्
अत्रभवत् mfn. (-वान् वती-वत्) Respectable, venerable, (especially in thea-<BR>tical language.<BR> E. अत्र here, भू to be and the participial affix शतृ;<BR>being present or principal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=016-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्रास
अत्रास mfn. (-सः-सा-सं) Fearless.<BR> E. अ neg. त्रास fear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=016-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्रि|अत्रिः
अत्रि m. (-त्रिः) The name of one of one of the seven Ṛṣis or saints,<BR>born from the eye of RRAHMĀ, married to ANASŪYĀ, daughter<BR>of KARDAMA MUNI, and the father of DATTA or DATTĀTREYA,<BR>DURVĀSAS and CHANDRA.<BR> E. अद to eat and त्रिप् Unādi aff. The<BR>correct reading is अत्त्रि, but the word is always written with one त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=016-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्रिजात|अत्रिजातः
अत्रिजात m. (-तः)<BR>	 1. The moon.<BR>	 2. A man of the three first classes. E.<BR>अ neg. त्रि three, and जात born, not thrice born; born twice The<BR>moon, from the eye of ATRI, and from the ocean. The Brahman<BR>&c. from the womb and investiture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=016-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्रिदृग्ज|अत्रिदृग्जः
अत्रिदृग्ज m. (-जः) A name of CHANDRA or the moon.<BR> E. अत्रि a saint, दृश्<BR>the eye, and ज born, produced. Born from the eye of ATRI, “a<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=016-b" target="_blank">Page016-b+ 60</a>]<BR>flash of light from the eye of ATRI, was received by space, a<BR>goddess, the via lactea personified, who bore SOMA.” The following<BR>and other similar names refer to this legend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=016-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्रिन्
अत्रिन् m. (-त्री) A muni. See अत्रि,<BR> E. अद to eat, Unādi aff. त्रिन्;<BR>also अत्रिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=016-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्रिनेत्रज|अत्रिनेत्रजः
अत्रिनेत्रज m. (-जः) See अत्रिदृग्ज.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=016-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्रिनेत्रप्रसूत|अत्रिनेत्रप्रसूतः
अत्रिनेत्रप्रसूत m. (-तः) See अत्रिदृग्ज.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=016-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्रिनेत्रभू
अत्रिनेत्रभू m. (-भूः) See अत्रिदृग्ज.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=016-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्रिभारद्वाजिका
अत्रिभारद्वाजिका m. (-काः) The marriage union of ATRI and BHĀRA-<BR>DWĀJĪ.<BR> E. अत्रि, and भारद्वाजी; affix वुञ्. implying in this and similar<BR>compounds, union.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=016-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतुर
अतुर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Deliberate, not in haste.<BR> E. अ neg. तुर for त्वरा haste.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=016-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्त्रि
अत्त्रि m. (-त्त्रिः) A sage. See अत्त्रि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=016-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्त्रिन्
अत्त्रिन् m. (-त्त्री) A sage. See अत्त्रि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=016-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अथ
अथ ind. An auspicious and inceptive particle; it serves to introduce<BR>a remark, a question, an affirmation, &c. and corresponds to.<BR>	 1.<BR>After.<BR>	 2. And 3. Now, (inceptive or premising)<BR>	 4. What, (inter-<BR>rogatively)<BR>	 5. All, (comprehensively)<BR>	 6. Therefore, thus, further,<BR>moreover, &c. It also implies doubt or command, and is frequently<BR>redundant.<BR> E. अर्थ to ask, ड affix, and र is dropped, also अथो.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=016-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अथकिम्
अथकिम् ind. A particle of assent, how else, what else, assuredly. अथच<BR>ind. Also.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=016-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अथर्व्वण|अथर्वण|अथर्वणः|अथर्व्वणः
अथर्व्वण m. (-णः) A name of ŚIVA.<BR> E. अथर्ब्ब the name of a Veda, and ण aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=016-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अथर्व्वन्|अथर्वन्
अथर्व्वन् (-र्व्वा) 1. A Brahman.<BR>	 2. A name of VASIṢṬHA.<BR>	 n. (र्व्व) The name<BR>of the fourth Veda.<BR> E. अथ an auspicious particle ऋ to go, and<BR>वनिप aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=016-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अथर्व्वणि|अथर्वणि|अथर्वणिः|अथर्व्वणिः
अथर्व्वणि m. (-णिः)<BR>	 1. Brahman versed in the Atharva Veda.<BR>	 2. A<BR>family priest.<BR> E. अथर्व्व the Veda, and णि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=016-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अथवा
अथवा ind. Or.<BR> E. अथ, and वा sometimes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=016-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अथो
अथो ind. The same as अथ, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=016-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद|अदः
अद (औ) r. 2d cl. (अत्ति) To eat. The root is imperfect; घस being substituted<BR>for it in several inflections; as जघास, &c. Implying injury,<BR>it is not conjugated in the middle voice, although the action be<BR>reciprocal: as व्यत्यदन्ति they bite, or devour each other. With an<BR>indicatory इ, अदि (अन्दति) To bind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=016-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदक्ष
अदक्ष mfn. (-क्षः-क्षा-क्षं) Awkward, unskilful.<BR> E. अ neg. दक्ष clever.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=016-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदक्षिण
अदक्षिण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>	 1. Not clever, unskilful.<BR>	 2. Not comprehending<BR>the fee given to the Brahmans, a sacrifice, &c.<BR> E. अ neg. दक्षिण<BR>clever, or दक्षिणा a fee.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=016-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदग्ध
अदग्ध mfn. (-ग्धः-ग्धा-ग्धं) Unscorched, not burnt.<BR> E. अ neg. दग्ध burnt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=016-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदण्ड|अदंड
अदण्ड mfn. (-ण्डः-ण्डा-ण्डं) Unpunished.<BR>	 n. (-ण्डं) Impunity.<BR> E. अ neg. दण्ड<BR>punishment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=016-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदण्ड्य|अदंड्य
अदण्ड्य mfn. (-ण्ड्यः-ण्ड्या-ण्ड्यं) Unpunishable, unworthy of, or exempt from<BR>punishment.<BR> E. अ neg. दण्ड्या to be punished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=016-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदण्डनीय
अदण्डनीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Unpunishable, unfit to be punished, exempt<BR>from punishment.<BR> E. अ neg. दण्डनीय to be punished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=016-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदत्त|अदत्तं
अदत्त mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं) Not given.<BR>	 f. (त्ता) An unmarried girl.<BR> E. अ not,<BR>दत्त given.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=016-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदन|अदनं
अदन n. (नं)<BR>	 1. Food.<BR>	 2. Eating.<BR> E. अद to eat, and ल्युट aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=016-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदनीय
अदनीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) To be eaten, what may be eaten.<BR> E. अद to eat,<BR>अनीयर aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=016-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदन्त|अदंत|अदन्तः
अदन्त mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं) Toothless. So अदन्तक (-कः-का-कं)<BR> E. अ neg. दन्त<BR>a tooth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=016-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदम्य
अदम्य mfn. (-म्यः-म्या-म्यं) Uncontrollable, untameable.<BR> E. अ neg. दम्य to<BR>be tamed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=016-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदभ्र|अदभ्रः
अदभ्र mfn. (-भ्रः-भ्रा-भ्रं) Much, many.<BR> E. अ neg. दभ्र little, few.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=016-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदय
अदय mfn. (यः-या-यं) Unfeeling, unmerciful, destitute of pity.<BR> E. अ neg.<BR>दया clemency.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=016-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदर्शन|अदर्शनं
अदर्शन n. (-नं) Disappearance, not being visible or present.<BR> E. अ neg.<BR>दर्शन sight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=016-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदल|अदलः
अदल m. (-लः) A plant, (Eugenia acutangula) See हिज्जल.<BR>	 f. (-ला) Soco-<BR>torine aloe, (Aloes perfoliata.) See घृतकुमारी.<BR>	 mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Leafless.<BR>E. अ. and दल a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=017-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदस्
अदस् mfn. (-असौ-असौ-अदः)<BR>	 1. This.<BR>	 2. That.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=017-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदहनीय
अदहनीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Incombustible; so अदाहनीय<BR> E. अ neg. दाहनीय<BR>or दहनीय to be burnt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=017-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदातृ
अदातृ m. (-ता) A niggard, a miser.<BR> E. अ neg. दातृ who gives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=017-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदान
अदान n. (-नं) Not giving, withholding,<BR> E. अ neg. दान gift.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=017-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदान्त|अदांत|अदान्तः
अदान्त mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं) Untamed, unsubdued, undaunted.<BR> E. अ neg. दान्त<BR>daunted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=017-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदायिक
अदायिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>	 1. Unclaimed, as inheritance, lapsed.<BR>	 2. Not<BR>relating to inheritance.<BR> E. अ neg. दाय heritage, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=017-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदाह्य
अदाह्य mfn. (-ह्यः-ह्या-ह्यं) Inconsumable by fire, incombustible.<BR> E. अ neg.<BR>दाह्य to be burnt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=017-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदिति|अदितिः
अदिति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. The daughter of DAKṢA, wife of KAŚYAPA, and<BR>mother of the gods.<BR>	 2. The earth.<BR>	 3. Being entire.<BR> E. अ neg. दा to<BR>give, and दिति affix, not giving pain; or अ, दो to cut or break.<BR>क्तिच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=017-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदितिनन्दन|अदितिनंदन|अदितिनन्दनः
अदितिनन्दन m. (-नः) A deity, a divinity.<BR> E. अदिति, and नन्दन, a son of<BR>ADITI.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=017-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदुष्ट
अदुष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>	 1. Unspoiled, unvitiated.<BR>	 2. Good, virtuous<BR> E. अ<BR>neg. दुष्ट bad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=017-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदूषित
अदूषित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Undefiled, unvitiated.<BR>	 2. Virtuous, good.<BR> E. अ<BR>neg. दूषित corrupted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=017-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदृश्
अदृश् m. (-दृक्) Blind.<BR> E. अ priv. and दृश् the eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=017-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदृश्य|अदृश्यं
अदृश्य mfn. (-श्य-श्या-श्यं)<BR>	 1. Invisible, not be to seen.<BR>	 2. Improper to be-<BR>hold.<BR> E. अ neg. दृश्य to be seen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=017-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदृष्ट|अदृष्टं|अदृष्टः
अदृष्ट n. (-ष्टं)<BR>	 1. Casual and unseen danger, (as from conflagration,<BR>inundation, &c.)<BR>	 2. Fortune, destiny, fate.<BR>	 3. (In logic) Virtue or<BR>vice, as the eventual cause of pleasure or pain.<BR>	 mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>1. Unseen, unforeseen.<BR>	 2. Unknown, unfelt, not experienced.<BR> E. अ<BR>neg. and दृष्ट seen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=017-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदृष्टपुरुष|अदृष्टपुरुषः
अदृष्टपुरुष m. (-षः) A form of treaty, in which the parties treat direct<BR>without any mediator or surety also अदृष्टनर and similar compounds.<BR>E. अदृष्ट unseen, and पुरुष, &c. man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=017-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदृष्टपूर्व्व|अदृष्टपूर्व
अदृष्टपूर्व्व mfn. (-र्व्वः-र्व्वा-र्व्वं) Unseen previously, unseen till now.<BR> E. अदृष्ट,<BR>and पूर्व्व before.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=017-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदृष्टवत्
अदृष्टवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>	 1. Enjoying or undergoing good or bad<BR>fortune, more usually the former, fortunate.<BR> E. अदृष्ट, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=017-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदृष्टि|अदृष्टिः
अदृष्टि f. (-ष्टिः) A look of displeasure, evil eye.<BR> E. अ bad, and दृष्टि look.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=017-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदृष्टिका
अदृष्टिका f. (-का) An angry or displeased look, evil eye.<BR> E. अदृष्टि. and<BR>कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=017-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदेय
अदेय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Improper or unfit to be given.<BR> E. अ neg. देय to<BR>be given.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=017-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदेयदान
अदेयदान n. (-नं) Giving what ought not to be given, what is not<BR>one's own, &c.<BR> E. अदेय, and दान giving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=017-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्ग|अद्गः
अद्ग m. (-द्गः) Oiled butter.<BR> E. अद to eat, and गम् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=017-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्धा
अद्धा ind. Truly, verily.<BR> E. अत going constantly, धा to have, and विच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=017-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्भुत|अद्भुतं|अद्भुतः
अद्भुत n. (-तं)<BR>	 1. Surprise, astonishment.<BR>	 mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Wonderful,<BR>surprising.<BR> E. अत a particle of surprise, भू to be, and उतच् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=017-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्भुतश्वन
अद्भुतश्वन m. (-नः) A name of ŚIVA.<BR> E. अद्भुत astonishing, and श्वन who<BR>sounds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=017-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्मनि|अद्मनिः
अद्मनि m. (-निः) Fire.<BR> E. अद to eat, Uṇādi affix अनि, and म inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=017-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्मर|अद्मरः
अद्मर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Gluttonous.<BR> E. अद to eat, and क्मरच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=017-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्य
अद्य ind. Today.<BR> E. इदम् this; an irregular formation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=017-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्यतन|अद्यतनः
अद्यतन m. (-नः) The period of a current day, from midnight to midnight<BR>in the usual acceptation, but sometimes considered to begin and<BR>end with sunset.<BR>	 mfn. (-नः-नी-नं) Of or belonging to the current<BR>day, of today.<BR> E. अद्य, and द्युल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=017-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्यतनभूत
अद्यतनभूत m. (-तः) In grammar, the aorist past.<BR>	 mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Past or<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=017-b" target="_blank">Page017-b+ 60</a>]<BR>gone today, i. e. any time previous to today.<BR> E. अद्यतन of today,<BR>भूत been.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=017-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्यापि
अद्यापि ind. Even now, still.<BR> E. अद्य, and अपि certainly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=017-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्यावधि
अद्यावधि n. (-धि) Beginning or ending with the current day, from or<BR>till today.<BR> E. अद्य, and अवधि limit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=017-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्यश्वीन|अद्यश्वीनं
अद्यश्वीन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Near to any event, at the point of death &c.<BR>	 f.<BR>(-ना) A woman or any female animal near the time of delivery. E.<BR>अद्य, and श्व tomorrow. affix ख, what will happen today or to-<BR>morrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=017-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्रव्य|अद्रव्यं
अद्रव्य n. (-व्यं) A worthless or good for nothing object.<BR> E. अ neg. द्रव्य<BR>thing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=017-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्रि|अद्रिः
अद्रि m. (-द्रिः)<BR>	 1. A tree.<BR>	 2. A mountain.<BR>	 3. The sun.<BR>	 4. A measure. E.<BR>अद to eat, and क्रिन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=017-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्रिकीला
अद्रिकीला f. (-ला) The earth.<BR> E. अद्रि a mountain, and कील a pin or bolt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=017-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्रिज|अद्रिजं
अद्रिज mfn. (-जः-जा-जं) Produced or found in the hills.<BR>	 n. (जं) Red chalk.<BR>f. (-जा) A name of PĀRVATĪ or DURGĀ, the daughter of HIMĀLAYA,<BR>ruler of Himālaya mountain, and hence this her appellation,<BR>mountain-born.<BR> E. अद्रि, and ज, from जन to be born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=017-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्रितनया
अद्रितनया f. (-या) A name of PĀRVATĪ, the daughter of the mountain<BR>HIMĀLAYA.<BR> E. अद्रि, and तनया daughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=017-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्रिनन्दिनी
अद्रिनन्दिनी f. (-नी) PĀRVATĪ. See the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=017-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्रिपति|अद्रिपतिः
अद्रिपति m. (-तिः) Himālaya, lord of mountains: also similar compounds,<BR>as अद्रीन्द्र, अद्रिराज् &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=017-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्रिभिद्
अद्रिभिद् m. (-भित्) A name of INDRA.<BR> E. अद्रि, and भिद् who breaks;<BR>the splitter of mountains, (with his thunderbolt.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=017-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्रिभू
अद्रिभू mfn. (-भूः-भूः-भु) Mountaineer, mountain-born.<BR>	 m. (भूः) A Plant,<BR>(Salvinea cucullata.)<BR> E. अद्रि, and भू born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=017-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्रिराज्
अद्रिराज् m. (-राट्) The king of mountains, the HIMĀLAYA mountains;<BR>the snowy range on the north of Hindustan, confounded with the<BR>mythological ruler of them, and the father of PĀRVATĪ.<BR> E. अद्रि,<BR>and राज् a king, the king of mountains, deservedly so called, being<BR>the loftiest in the world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=017-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्रिवह्नि|अद्रिवह्निः
अद्रिवह्नि m. (-ह्निः) Fire on a mountain, a volcano.<BR> E. अद्रि, and वह्नि fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=017-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्रिशृङ्ग|अद्रिशृंग
अद्रिशृङ्ग n. (-ङ्गम्) A peak, the horn or summit of a mountain.<BR> E. अद्रि,<BR>and शृङ्ग a horn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=017-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्रिसार|अद्रिसारः
अद्रिसार m. (-रः) Iron.<BR> E. अद्रि, and सार essence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=017-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्रीश|अद्रीशः
अद्रीश m. (-शः)<BR>	 1. A name of ŚIVA.<BR>	 2. Also of HIMĀLAYA, as king of<BR>mountains.<BR> E. अद्रि, and ईश a master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=017-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्रोह|अद्रोहः
अद्रोह m. (-हः) Mildness, moderation, the absence of tyranny or<BR>oppression.<BR> E. अ neg. द्रोह tyranny.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=017-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्रोहिन्
अद्रोहिन् mfn. (-ही-हिणी-हि) Innocuous, mild.<BR> E. अ neg. द्रोहिन् violent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=017-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्वय|अद्वयः
अद्वय m. (-यः) A Bauddha.<BR> E. अ neg. द्वय two.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=017-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्वयवादिन्
अद्वयवादिन् m. (-दी)<BR>	 1. A Bauddha.<BR>	 2. A unitarian.<BR> E. अ neg. द्वय two,<BR>and वादिन् who speaks, one who acknowledges but one principle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=017-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्वितीय|अद्वितीयः
अद्वितीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Only, sole, without a second.<BR> E. अ neg. द्वितीय<BR>second.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=017-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्वेष|अद्वेषः
अद्वेष mfn. (-षः-षा-षं) Harmless, not malicious.<BR> E. अ neg. द्वेष malice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=017-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्वेषिन्
अद्वेषिन् mfn. (-षी-षिणी-षि) Harmless, inoffensive.<BR> E. अ neg. द्वेषिन् who<BR>hates.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=017-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्वैत|अद्वैतः
अद्वैत n. (-तं) Unity, not duality.<BR> E. अ neg. द्वैत duality.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=017-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्वैतवादिन्
अद्वैतवादिन् m. (-दी) A unitarian, one who maintains the existence of but<BR>one principle in the universe.<BR> E. अद्वैत unity, and वादिन् who speaks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=017-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधःकाय
अधःकाय m. (-यः) The lower part of the body, the lower extremities. E.<BR>अधस्, and काय body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=017-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधःकृत
अधःकृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Thrown or put down.<BR> E. अधस्, and कृत made.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=017-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधःक्षिप्त|अधःक्षिप्तः
अधःक्षिप्त (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं) Precipitated, thrown down.<BR> E. अधस् down, and क्षिप्त<BR>participle past of क्षिप् to throw.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=017-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधःपतित
अधःपतित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Fallen down.<BR> E. अधस्, and पतित fallen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=017-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधःप्रस्तर|अधःप्रस्तरः
अधःप्रस्तर m. (-रः) A seat or bed, made of grass,<BR> E. अधस्, and प्रस्तर a<BR>couch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=017-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधःपुष्पी
अधःपुष्पी f. (-ष्पी) A plant, (Hieracium.)<BR> E. अधस् downwards, and पुष्प<BR>a flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=018-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधःस्थ
अधःस्थ mfn. (-स्थ-स्था-स्थं)<BR>	 1. Below.<BR>	 2. Inferior.<BR> E. अधस्, and स्थ what stays.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=018-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधम|अधमः
अधम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>	 1. Inferior, low.<BR>	 2. Vile, despicable.<BR> E. अव to<BR>preserve, अम Unādi affix, and व changed to ध.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=018-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधमभृतक|अधमभृतकः
अधमभृतक mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>	 1. A porter, a bearer of burdens.<BR>	 2. Low,<BR>servile.<BR> E. अधम low, and भृतक a servant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=018-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधमर्ण|अधमर्णः
अधमर्ण mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-र्णं) A debtor.<BR> E. अधम low, and ऋण debt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=018-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधमर्णिक|अधमर्णिकः
अधमर्णिक m. (-कः) A debtor.<BR> E. अधम, and ऋण debt, with ठक् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=018-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधमर्णिन्
अधमर्णिन् m. (-र्णी) A debtor.<BR> E. अधम, and ऋण debt, with इनि added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=018-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधमाङ्ग|अधमांग|अधमाङ्गं
अधमाङ्ग n. (-ङ्गं) A foot.<BR> E. अधम low, and अङ्ग a limb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=018-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधर|अधरं|अधरः
अधर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>	 1. Low, inferior, below.<BR>	 2. Low, vile.<BR>	 3. Silenced,<BR>refuted, overcome in abuse or controversy.<BR>	 f. (-रा) The lower region.<BR>m. (-रः) The lower lip. (dual. रौ) The lips.<BR>	 mn. (-रः or रं) Puden-<BR>dum muliebre.<BR> E. अ neg. धृ to have or hold, and अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=018-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधरतस्
अधरतस् ind. Underneath.<BR> E. अधर, and तस् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=018-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधरमधु
अधरमधु n. (-धु) The moisture of the lips.<BR> E. अधर the lower lip, and मधु<BR>honey.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=018-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधरस्तात्
अधरस्तात् ind. Below, behind.<BR> E. स्तात् added to अधर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=018-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधरस्मात्
अधरस्मात् ind. Below, underneath. E. the form of the ablative.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=018-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधरात्
अधरात् ind. Underneath.<BR> E. अधर, with the termination आत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=018-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधरामृत|अधरामृतं
अधरामृत n. (-तं) The moisture, honey or nectar of the lips.<BR> E. अधर,<BR>and अमृत nectar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=018-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधरावलोप
अधरावलोप m. (-पः) Biting the lip.<BR> E. अधर, and अव before लुप to cut,<BR>affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=018-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधरीकृत
अधरीकृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Contradicted, invalidated.<BR> E. अधर, and कृत<BR>made with च्वी inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=018-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधरीण|अधरीणः
अधरीण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Reproached, censured.<BR> E. अधर, and ख aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=018-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधरीभूत
अधरीभूत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Contradicted, invalidated.<BR> E. अधर, and भूत<BR>become, with च्वी inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=018-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधरेण
अधरेण ind. Underneath.<BR> E. अधर, and the affix एन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=018-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधरेद्युस्
अधरेद्युस् ind. A future day, the day after the morrow.<BR> E. अधर, and<BR>एद्युस् irregular aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=018-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधर्म्म|अधर्म|अधर्मः|अधर्म्मः
अधर्म्म m. (-र्म्मः) Unrighteousness, injustice, all behaviour contrary to<BR>the Śruti and Smṛti, or religious and legal institutes.<BR> E. अ priv.<BR>and धर्म्मं virtue, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=018-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधर्म्मचारिन्|अधर्मचारिन्
अधर्म्मचारिन् mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि) Unrighteous, wicked.<BR> E. अधर्म्म, and चारिन्<BR>who follows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=018-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधर्म्मता|अधर्मता
अधर्म्मता f. (-ता) Unrighteousness; also अधर्म्मत्व n. (त्वं)<BR> E. ता or त्व added<BR>to अधर्म्म.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=018-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधर्म्मात्मन्|अधर्मात्मन्
अधर्म्मात्मन् mfn. (-त्म-त्मा-त्म) Wicked, unrighteous.<BR> E. अधर्म्म, and आत्मन्<BR>spirit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=018-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधर्म्मिन्|अधर्मिन्
अधर्म्मिन् mfn. (-र्म्मी-र्म्मिणी-र्म्मि) Wicked, sinful, unrighteous.<BR> E. अधर्म्म, and<BR>इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=018-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधर्म्मिष्ठ|अधर्मिष्ठ
अधर्म्मिष्ठ mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठा-ष्ठं) Very wicked.<BR> E. अधर्म्म, and इष्ठन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=018-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधश्चर|अधश्चरः
अधश्चर mfn. (-रः-रा-री-रं)<BR>	 m. (-रः) A thief.<BR> E. अधस् low, vile, and<BR>चर who goes down or below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=018-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधश्चौर|अधश्चौरः
अधश्चौर m. (-रः) A housebreaker.<BR> E. अधस् below, and चौर a thief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=018-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधस्
अधस् ind.<BR>	 1. Down, downwards, below.<BR>	 2. The lower or infernal<BR>regions.<BR>	 3. Pudendum muliebre.<BR> E. अधर with असि affix, and र<BR>dropped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=018-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधस्तन
अधस्तन mfn. (-नः-नी-नं) Below, underneath.<BR> E. अधस् and द्युल aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=018-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधस्तात्
अधस्तात् ind.<BR>	 1. Down, downwards, underneath.<BR>	 2. Behind.<BR>	 3. Puden-<BR>dum muliebre.<BR> E. अधर or अधस्, and तात् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=018-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधामार्गव|अधामार्गवः
अधामार्गव m. (-वः) A plant, (Achyranthes aspera)<BR> E. अधम vile, मार्ग a<BR>road, and व from वा to gain or possess.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=018-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधार्म्मिक|अधार्मिक|अधार्म्मिकः
अधार्म्मिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Unjust, unrighteous, wicked.<BR> E. अ neg. and<BR>धार्म्मिक virtuous, &c. from धर्म्म, affix ठञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=018-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधि|अधिः
अधि m. (-धिः) Anxiety, mental pain; more usually आधिः<BR> E. आङ<BR>before, धा to have, कि affix; आ is made short.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=018-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधि|अधिः
अधि ind. Over, above, upon, &c. a preposition and prefix to verbs<BR>implying superiority in place, quality, or quantity; as अधिष्ठातुं to<BR>stand in or on, अधिकर्त्तुं to rule over, अधिशयितुं to exceed: also<BR>used in the figurative sense of the same, as अधिगन्तुं to go to or<BR>attain; अधिकर्त्तुं to do over again, to repeat or recall; अधीतुं to go<BR>over or through, as a book; अधिवस्तुं to reside in or on, to perse-<BR>vere: forming also indeclinables with nouns, as अधिरात्रि in the<BR>night; अधिग्रहं in or over the house: and compounds with nouns,<BR>as अधिदेवता, &c. q. v.<BR> E. अ neg. धा to have, कि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=018-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिक|अधिकं|अधिकः
अधिक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Exceeding, more, over, more than, in addition<BR>to.<BR>	 n. (-कं) A figure in rhetoric, (Hyperbole.)<BR> E. अधि and क, from<BR>कै to sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=018-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिकतर
अधिकतर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) More, comparatively more.<BR> E. अधिक and तरप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=018-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिकतम
अधिकतम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं) Most, superlatively more.<BR> E. अधिक, and तमप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=018-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिकता
अधिकता f. (-ता) Excess, addition; also अधिकत्वं.<BR> E. ता or त्व added<BR>to अधिक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=018-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिकन्तु
अधिकन्तु ind. Moreover.<BR> E. अधिक, and तु but.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=018-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिकरण|अधिकरणं
अधिकरण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Superiority, supremacy.<BR>	 2. Title, right.<BR>	 3. In the<BR>Mīmāṃsā philosophy, a case or topic, comprehending five members,<BR>the subject, the doubt, the first side or prima facie argument, the<BR>answer or conclusion, the application.<BR>	 4. (In the Vedānta.) A case<BR>or question.<BR>	 5. (In grammar) Location, the sense of the seventh<BR>or locative case, defined to imply four kinds.<BR>	 1. Proximity, as, ‘a<BR>village on the Ganges.’ 2. Inclusion, as, ‘the gods in heaven.’<BR>3. End or object, as, ‘versed in the Sāstras; and 4. Integral<BR>existence, as, ‘the spirit is in all.’<BR> E. अधि over, कृ to do; and<BR>ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=018-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिकर्द्धि
अधिकर्द्धि mfn. (-र्द्धिः-र्द्धिः-र्द्धि) Prosperous, every way happy.<BR> E. अधिक<BR>excessive, and ऋद्धि prosperity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=018-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिकर्म्मन्|अधिकर्मन्
अधिकर्म्मन् n. (-र्म्म) Superintendence, Supervision.<BR> E. अधि, and कर्म्म<BR>business.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=018-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिकर्म्मिक|अधिकर्मिक|अधिकर्मिकः|अधिकर्म्मिकः
अधिकर्म्मिक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. Clerk or prefect of the market or fair.<BR>	 2. An<BR>overseer, a superintendent.<BR> E. अधि over, कर्म्म business, and इक aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=018-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिकाङ्ग|अधिकाङ्गं
अधिकाङ्ग mfn. (-ङ्गः-ङ्गा-ङ्गं) Having more members than natural or com-<BR>mon.<BR>	 n. (-ङ्गं) The girdle over the coat of mail, worn as a kind of<BR>scarf.<BR> E. अधिक exceeding and अङ्ग the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=018-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिकार|अधिकारः
अधिकार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Authority.<BR>	 2. Supremacy.<BR>	 3. Rule, government.<BR>4. Right, title.<BR>	 5. Property, ownership.<BR>	 6. Privilege.<BR>	 7. Duty,<BR>office.<BR>	 8. A chapter, a section.<BR>	 9. The use of royal insignia.<BR>	 10. (In<BR>grammar; Government, the dependence of a form on a previous<BR>one.<BR> E. अधि over, and कार what makes, from कृ with घञ् affix; what<BR>gives or exercises pre-eminence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=018-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिकारिता
अधिकारिता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Ownership, lordship.<BR>	 2. Right, title.<BR> E. अधिकारिन्<BR>with ता affix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=018-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिकारित्व|अधिकारित्वं
अधिकारित्व n. (-त्वं)<BR>	 1. Ownership.<BR>	 2. Right, title. E. See the last, affix त्व.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=018-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिकारिन्
अधिकारिन् m. (-री)<BR>	 1. A superintendent, a ruler, a director.<BR>	 2. A master,<BR>an owner.<BR>	 3. A sage, one who is perfect in principles and practice<BR>of the Vedānta.<BR>	 mf. (-री-रिणी) (In law) The possessor of a right<BR>or title, as. धनाधिकारी heir to property; संस्काराधिकारी one who has<BR>a right to the essential ceremonies of the Hindu religion.<BR> E. अधिकार,<BR>and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=018-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिकृत|अधिकृतः
अधिकृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Superintended, guided.<BR>	 2. Claimed or held<BR>as a right.<BR>	 3. Set over, superintendent.<BR>	 m. (-तः)<BR>	 1. A superinten-<BR>dent in general.<BR>	 2. Inspector of receipts and disbursements, an<BR>auditor of public accounts.<BR> E. अधि over, and कृत made.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=018-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिक्रम|अधिक्रमः
अधिक्रम m. (-मः) Invasion, assailing.<BR> E. अधि over, and क्रम to go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=018-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिक्रमण|अधिक्रमणं
अधिक्रमण n. (-णं) Invading, assailing, overrunning.<BR> E. अधि, and क्रमण<BR>going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=018-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिकृति|अधिकृतिः
अधिकृति f. (-तिः) A possession, a right.<BR> E. अधि, and कृति doing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=018-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिक्षिप्त|अधिक्षिप्तः
अधिक्षिप्त mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं)<BR>	 1. Censured, reviled, detracted from.<BR>	 2. Sent,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=019-a" target="_blank">Page019-a+ 60</a>]<BR>despatched.<BR>	 3. Placed, fixed.<BR> E. अधि, and क्षिप्त participle of क्षिप to<BR>send or throw.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=018-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिक्षेप|अधिक्षेपः
अधिक्षेप m. (-पः)<BR>	 1. Detraction, censure.<BR>	 2. Sending, despatching. E.<BR>अधि, and क्षेप throwing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=019-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिगत
अधिगत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Obtained.<BR>	 2. Gone through or over, lit. or<BR>fig. as read, studied.<BR> E. अधि, and गत gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=019-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिगम|अधिगमः
अधिगम m. (-मः)<BR>	 1. Obtaining, attaining, acquiring 2. Going through<BR>or over, lit or fig.<BR>	 3. Overpassing, overflowing: also<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=019-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिगमन|अधिगमनं
अधिगमन n. (-नं) &c<BR> E. अधि, and गम or गमन going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=019-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिगम्य
अधिगम्य mfn. (-म्यः-म्या-म्य) Unattainable, not to be reached or acquired.<BR>So अधिगमनीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) and अधिगन्तव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं) E.<BR>अधिगम with यत्, अनीयर or तव्य participial affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=019-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिजिह्व|अधिजिह्वः
अधिजिह्व m. (-ह्वः) A tumor on the tongue.<BR> E. अधि, and जिह्वा the tongue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=019-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिज्योतिष्
अधिज्योतिष् n. (-षं) The luminous parts of the creation.<BR> E. अधि supreme,<BR>ज्योतिष् light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=019-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधित्यका
अधित्यका f. (-का) Land on the upper part of a mountain.<BR> E. अधि over,<BR>above, and त्यकन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=019-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिदन्त|अधिदंतः|अधिदन्तः
अधिदन्त m. (-न्तः) A tooth growing over another.<BR> E. अधि, and दन्त a tooth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=019-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिदेव|अधिदेवः
अधिदेव m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. A supreme or superior deity.<BR>	 2. A tutelary deity. E.<BR>अधि, and देव a deity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=019-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिदेवता
अधिदेवता m. (-ता) A tutelary, or presiding divinity.<BR> E. अधि, and देवता<BR>a deity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=019-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिदैव|अधिदैवं
अधिदैव n. (-वं)<BR>	 1. The ruling deity, the active principle in creation:<BR>also अधिदैवतं.<BR>	 2. The collective body of gods, and superhuman<BR>beings.<BR> E. अधि, and दैव divine being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=019-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिप|अधिपः
अधिप m. (-पः)<BR>	 1. An owner, a lord or master.<BR>	 2. A king.<BR> E. अधि, and<BR>प who preserves, from पा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=019-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिपति|अधिपतिः
अधिपति m. (-तिः) A master, an owner, a ruler.<BR>	 2. A king.<BR> E. अधि, and<BR>पति a master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=019-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिप्रज
अधिप्रज n. (-जं) Continuation of the world by procreation.<BR> E. अधि, and<BR>प्रजा progeny.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=019-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिभू
अधिभू m. (-भूः) A master, a ruler.<BR> E. अधि, and भू who is from भू to be,<BR>affix विच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=019-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिभूत|अधिभूतं
अधिभूत n. (-तं) An essential element of matter, perishable matter,<BR>that of which the presence involves eventual dissolution.<BR> E. अधि<BR>over, and भूत an element.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=019-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिमन्थ|अधिमंथः|अधिमन्थः
अधिमन्थ m. (-न्थः) Acute pains in the balls of the eyes, with pain and<BR>swelling of one side of the head.<BR> E. अधि over, मन्थ what agitates.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=019-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिमांस|अधिमांसः
अधिमांस m. (-सः) Fleshy excrescences on the eye, cancer of the eye.<BR>E. अधि, and मांस flesh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=019-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिमांसक|अधिमांसकः
अधिमांसक m. (-कः) Inflammation of the tonsils.<BR> E. अधि, and मांस flesh,<BR>कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=019-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिमात्र
अधिमात्र n. (-त्रं) A knowledge of the properties of the letters forming<BR>the word for the Hindu triad ओम्<BR> E. अधि, and मात्र the whole.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=019-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिमास|अधिमासः
अधिमास m. (-सः) An intercalary month, formed of the aggregate days<BR>omitted in reckoning the lunar year.<BR> E. अधि, and मास a month.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=019-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिरथ|अधिरथः
अधिरथ m. (-थः) A charioteer.<BR> E. अधि, and रथ a car.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=019-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिराज्
अधिराज् m. (राट्) A supreme king, an emperor. So अधिराज m. (-जः)<BR>E. अधि, and राज्, राजन् a king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=019-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिराज्य|अधिराज्यं
अधिराज्य n. (ज्यं) Empire, supreme sway.<BR> E. अधि, and राज्य kingdom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=019-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिराज्यभाज्
अधिराज्यभाज् m. (-क्) An emperor, a paramount sovereign.<BR> E. अधिराज्य,<BR>and भाज् who possesses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=019-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिरूढ
अधिरूढ mfn. (-ढः-ढा-ढं) Elevated, exalted, surmounting.<BR> E. अधि,<BR>and रूढ mounted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=019-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिरोपित
अधिरोपित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Placed over, lit. or fig.<BR> E. अधि, and रोपित<BR>raised.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=019-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिरोह|अधिरोहः
अधिरोह m. (-हः) Surmounting, overtopping, elevation.<BR> E. अधि, and रोह<BR>mounting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=019-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिरोहणी
अधिरोहणी f. (-णी) A ladder, a pair of steps.<BR> E. अधि, and रुह to mount,<BR>with ल्युट् affix, and fem. ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=019-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिरोहिन्
अधिरोहिन् mfn. (-ही-हिणी-हि) Who rises on or above.<BR>	 f. (-णी) A ladder,<BR>a staircase.<BR> E. अधिरोह, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=019-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिलोक
अधिलोक m. (-कः) The universe, the material world.<BR> E. अधि, and<BR>लोक world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=019-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिवचन|अधिवचनं
अधिवचन n. (-नं) A name, an appellation.<BR> E. अधि, and वचन speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=019-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिवास|अधिवासः
अधिवास m. (-सः)<BR>	 1. A house, an abode.<BR>	 2. Place, situation.<BR>	 3. Continuance,<BR>perseverance.<BR>	 4. Perfuming the person, &c.<BR>	 5. A neighbour.<BR>6. Neighbourhood.<BR> E. अधि, and वस to dwell, with घञ् affix; or<BR>वास to fumigate, with अच्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=019-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिवासन|अधिवासनं
अधिवासन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Perfuming or scenting the person, &c.<BR>	 2. Abiding,<BR>staying.<BR>	 3. A religious ceremony; touching a vessel containing<BR>perfumes, flowers, and other things previously presented to an<BR>idol; or offering perfumes, &c. to idols, as a preliminary ceremony.<BR>E. अधि, and वास to fumigate, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=019-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिवासिता
अधिवासिता f. (-ता) Residence, staying or abiding in one place. E.<BR>अधिवास, with ता affix, and इट् augment; also with त्व, अधिवासित्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=019-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिविद्या
अधिविद्या f. (-द्या) The collective means and end of acquiring know-<BR>ledge.<BR> E. अधि, and विद्या knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=019-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिविन्ना
अधिविन्ना f. (-न्ना) A wife whose husband has subsequently married<BR>others; a superseded wife.<BR> E. अधि, and विन्न obtained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=019-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिवेत्तृ
अधिवेत्तृ m. (-त्ता) A man marrying other than his first wife.<BR> E. अधि,<BR>before विद to obtain, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=019-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिवेदन|अधिवेदनं
अधिवेदन n. (-नं) Marrying again, whilst a former wife is living.<BR> E. अधि<BR>before विद to obtain, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=019-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिवेदनीया
अधिवेदनीया f. (-या) A wife deserving or proper to be superseded. E.<BR>अधि before विद to obtain, अनीयर aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=019-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिश्रय|अधिश्रयः
अधिश्रय m. (-यः) A place, a receptacle.<BR> E. अधि before श्रि to serve,<BR>अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=019-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिश्रयणी
अधिश्रयणी f. (-णी) A furnace or fireplace.<BR> E. अधि, and श्रिङ to cook, ल्युट्<BR>affix and fem. termination.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=019-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिश्रित
अधिश्रित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Placed, deposited, received, included.<BR> E. अधि,<BR>before श्रि to serve, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=019-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिष्ठान|अधिष्ठानं
अधिष्ठान n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Abiding, resting; 2. Site, situation.<BR>	 3. Prescribed<BR>rule, fixed practice.<BR>	 5. A town.<BR>	 6. A wheel.<BR>	 7. Dignity.<BR> E. अधि,<BR>स्था to stand, and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=019-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिष्ठातृ
अधिष्ठातृ mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ) Governing, directing, fixing m. (-ता) A ruler, a<BR>governor, a director.<BR> E. अधि before स्था to stay, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=019-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिष्ठित
अधिष्ठित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Fixed, determined, established; literally or<BR>figuratively, as a house or a practice.<BR>	 2. Supervised, overseen.<BR>3. Guarded, surrounded.<BR>	 4. Appointed.<BR> E. अधि, and स्थित stationed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=019-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधीकार|अधीकारः
अधीकार m. (-रः) Superintendence, authority, &c. See अधिकार.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=019-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधीत|अधीतः
अधीत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Read, read through. E. the participial deriv.<BR>from अधी to read over, or study.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=019-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधीतवेद
अधीतवेद m. (-दः) A Brahman, who has read the Vedas; a student<BR>who has finished his course of study.<BR> E. अधीत, and वेद the Veda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=019-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधीति|अधीतिः
अधीति f. (-तिः) Study, perusal.<BR> E. अधी to read, and क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=019-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधीतिन्
अधीतिन् mfn. (-ती-तिनी-ति) A scholar, one who has finished his studies.<BR>E. अधीत, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=019-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधीन|अधीनः
अधीन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>	 1. Docile.<BR>	 2. Dependant.<BR> E. अधि, and ईन a<BR>master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=019-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधीनता
अधीनता f. (-ता) Subjection, dependence, slavery: so अधीनत्व (त्वं)<BR> E. ता<BR>or त्व added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=019-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधीयान|अधीयानः
अधीयान m. (-नः) A student. one going over or reading the Vedas, &c.<BR>E. अधि before इ to go, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=019-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधीर|अधीरः
अधीर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>	 1. Confused, perplexed.<BR>	 2. Unsteady, (lit. or<BR>met.)<BR>	 f. (-रा)<BR>	 1. Lightning.<BR>	 2. An offended, cross or capricious<BR>mistress or wife.<BR> E. अ neg, and धीर firm, steady.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=019-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधीरता
अधीरता f. (-ता) Fickleness, unsteadiness; also अधीरत्वं.<BR> E. ता or त्व added<BR>to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=019-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधीश|अधीशः
अधीश m. (-शः) A master, a lord.<BR> E. अधि, and ईश master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=019-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधीश्वर|अधीश्वरः
अधीश्वर m. (-रः) An emperor, a king paramount over all the neigh-<BR>bouring princes.<BR> E. अधि superior, and ईश्वर a lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=020-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधुना
अधुना ind. Now, at present.<BR> E. इदम् this, irregularly formed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=020-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधुनातन|अधुनातनं
अधुनातन mfn. (-नः-नी-नं) Of or belonging to the present<BR> E. अधुना, and<BR>द्युल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=020-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधृत|अधृतः
अधृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Upheld, undetained.<BR>	 m. (-तः) A name of VIṢṆU.<BR>E. अ neg. धृत held.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=020-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधृति|अधृतिः
अधृति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Laxity, want of firm hold.<BR>	 2. Want of steadiness or<BR>firmness.<BR> E. अ neg. धृति holding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=020-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधृष्ट|अधृष्टः
अधृष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं) Ashamed, modest, humble.<BR> E. अ neg. धृष्ट<BR>proud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=020-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधृष्टता
अधृष्टता f. (-ता) Modesty, diffidence: also अधृष्टत्व n. (-त्वं)<BR> E. ता or त्व<BR>added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=020-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधृष्य|अधृष्यः
अधृष्य mfn. (-ष्यः-ष्या-ष्यं) Proud, vain.<BR>	 f. (-ष्या) The name of a river.<BR> E. अ<BR>neg. and धृष to be proud; than whom nought is prouder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=020-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधेय
अधेय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Not to be held or taken.<BR> E. अ neg. धा to have,<BR>ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=020-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधैर्य्य|अधैर्य|अधैर्य्यः
अधैर्य्य mfn. (-र्य्यः-र्य्या-र्य्यं) Unsteady, feeble, irresolute. (-र्य्यं) Instability,<BR>want of firmness.<BR> E. अ not. धैर्य्य firmness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=020-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधोंशुक|अधोंशुकं
अधोऽंशुक n. (-कं) A lower garment.<BR> E. अधस् beneath, and अंशुक<BR>clothes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=020-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधोक्षज|अधोक्षजः
अधोक्षज m. (-जः) A name of VIṢṆU.<BR> E. अधस्, अक्ष an organ of sense,<BR>and ज who is produced; being produced by, or produced to such<BR>as have subdued or cast down their passions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=020-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधोगत
अधोगत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Descended, gone down.<BR> E. अधस् down. गत gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=020-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधोगति|अधोगतिः
अधोगति f. (-तिः) Going downwards, lit. or fig. descent, degradation.<BR>Also अधोगमः and अधोगमनं.<BR> E. अधस् and गति, &c. going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=020-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधोगामिन्
अधोगामिन् mfn. (-मी-मिनी-मि) Descending, going downwards.<BR> E. अधस्,<BR>and गामिन् who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=020-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधोघण्टा
अधोघण्टा f. (-ण्टा) A plant, (Acheranthes aspera.) See अपामार्ग.<BR> E. अधस्,<BR>and घटि to hurt, with अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=020-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधोङ्ग
अधोऽङ्ग n. (-ङ्गं)<BR>	 1. The anus.<BR>	 2. pudendum muliebre.<BR> E. अधस् and अङ्ग<BR>member.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=020-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधोजिह्विका
अधोजिह्विका f. (-का) The uvula or soft palate.<BR> E. अधस् below, and जिह्वा<BR>the tongue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=020-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधोदृष्टि|अधोदृष्टिः
अधोदृष्टि mfn. (-ष्टिः-ष्टिः-ष्टि) Downcast, one who looks down.<BR> E. अधस् and<BR>दृष्टि sight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=020-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधोपर
अधोपर n. (-रं)<BR>	 1. The anus.<BR>	 2. pudendum muliebre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=020-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधोबन्धन
अधोबन्धन n. (-नं) An under girth or strap.<BR> E. अधस्, and बन्धन binding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=020-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधोभव
अधोभव mfn. (-वः-वा-वं) placed below, inferior.<BR> E. अधस् and भ्व produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=020-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधोभाग|अधोभागः
अधोभाग m. (गः) The bottom, the lowest part.<BR> E. अधस्, and भाग part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=020-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधोभागहर
अधोभागहर n. (-रं) Purging.<BR> E. अधोभाग the lower part (of the body,) हर<BR>what affects.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=020-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधोभुवन|अधोभुवनं
अधोभुवन n. (-नं) The regions below the earth.<BR> E. अधस् beneath, and<BR>भुवन a world; the earth below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=020-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधोमर्म्मन्|अधोमर्मन्
अधोमर्म्मन् n. (-र्म्म) The anus.<BR> E. अधस्, and मर्म्मन् a member.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=020-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधोमुख|अधोमुखः
अधोमुख mfn. (-ख-खा-खी-खं)<BR>	 1. Down-looked, looking downwards.<BR>	 2.<BR>Inverted, turned upside down.<BR>	 3. Headlong.<BR>	 f. (-खा) A plant,<BR>(Premna esculenta.)<BR> E. अधस्, and मुख the face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=020-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधोयन्त्र
अधोयन्त्र n. (-न्त्रं) A still, or the lower of two vessels luted together for<BR>distilling, sublimation, &c.<BR> E. अधस्, and यन्त्र a vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=020-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधोलम्ब|अधोलम्बः
अधोलम्ब m. (-म्ब) A perpendicular.<BR> E. अधस् below, लम्ब a straight line.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=020-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधोलोक
अधोलोक m. (-कः) The regions below the earth.<BR> E. अधस् and लोक world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=020-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधोवदन
अधोवदन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Down-looked. See अधोमुख.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=020-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधोवश|अधोवशः
अधोवश m. (-शः)<BR>	 1. Bottom of a thing.<BR>	 2. Pudendum muliebre.<BR> E. अधस्,<BR>and वश dependence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=020-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधोवायु|अधोवायुः
अधोवायु m. (-युः) The vital air that passes downwards.<BR> E. अधस्, and<BR>वायु air.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=020-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधोस्रपित्त
अधोऽस्रपित्त n. (-त्तं) Discharge of blood from the anus, urethra. &c. E.<BR>अधस्, अस्त्रपित्त plethora.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=020-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यक्ष|अध्यक्षः
अध्यक्ष mfn. (-क्षः-क्षा-क्षं)<BR>	 1. Perceptible, present to the senses.<BR>	 2.<BR>Superintending, presiding over.<BR>	 m. (-क्षः)<BR>	 1. A superintendent in<BR>general, one of receipts and disbursements.<BR>	 2. A plant, (a species<BR>of Mimusops.) See क्षीरिका.<BR> E. अधि and अक्ष to pervade with<BR>अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=020-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यक्षता
अध्यक्षता f. (ता) Superintendence: also अध्यक्षत्व.<BR>	 n. (-त्वं)<BR> E. ता or त्व added<BR>to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=020-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यक्षर|अध्यक्षरं
अध्यक्षर n. (-रं) The mysterious word Om.<BR> E. अधि, and अक्षर letter:<BR>above all others in importance or in place; being often put at the<BR>head of various writings.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=020-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यग्नि
अध्यग्नि ind. Gifts made to a woman at the time of her marriage.<BR> E. अधि<BR>near, over, &c. and अग्रि fire, being presented at the time that<BR>burnt offering are made.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=020-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यण्डा|अध्यंडा
अध्यण्डा f. (-ण्डा) Cowach, (Carpopogon pruriens.)<BR> E. अधि, अम to be<BR>diseased, and ड affix; superior to disease. See अव्यङ्गा.<BR>अध्यय m. (-यः) A lecture, a chapter or section.<BR> E. अधि before इक्<BR>to go, घङ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=020-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्ययन|अध्ययनं
अध्ययन n. (-नं) Study, reading, especially of the sacred books; one of<BR>the six duties of a Brahman.<BR> E. अधि, इङ् to go, and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=020-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यवसाय|अध्यवसायः
अध्यवसाय m. (-यः) Effort, exertion, determined application.<BR> E. अधि, and<BR>अव before षो to destroy, with the affixes धञ् and यक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=020-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यवसायित
अध्यवसायित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Undertaken, attempted, as a difficult task. E.<BR>अधि, and अव before षो, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=020-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यवसायिन्
अध्यवसायिन् mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि) Resolute, determined.<BR> E. अध्यवसाय, and<BR>इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=020-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यशन|अध्यशनं
अध्यशन n. (-नं) Eating too often, taking food before that previously<BR>eaten is digested.<BR> E. अधि, and अशन eating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=020-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यस्तं|अध्यस्त
अध्यस्तं mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्त)<BR>	 1. Substituted.<BR>	 2. Placed over.<BR> E. अधि, and अस्त<BR>thrown.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=020-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यस्थि
अध्यस्थि n. (-स्थि) Bony exfoliation or deposit.<BR> E. अधि, and अस्थि a bone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=020-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यात्मन्
अध्यात्मन् m. (-त्मा)<BR>	 1. The soul, individuated spirit, or that which belongs<BR>to and presides over the body.<BR>	 2. The supreme spirit.<BR> E. अधि, and<BR>आत्मन् self or soul.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=020-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यात्मिक
अध्यात्मिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Spiritual, relating to the supreme spirit. E.<BR>अध्यात्मन् and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=020-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यात्मदृश्
अध्यात्मदृश् m. (दृक्) A holy sage, one who knows the nature of inherent<BR>spirit.<BR> E. अध्यात्मन्, and दृश् who sees.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=020-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यात्मरति
अध्यात्मरति m. (-तिः) An anchorite, one who diligently meditates on the<BR>supreme spirit.<BR> E. अध्यात्मन्, and रति pleasure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=020-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यापक|अध्यापकः
अध्यापक m. (-कः) A teacher, one who instructs in the sacred books. E.<BR>अधि, and इङ् to go, in the causal form, and वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=020-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यापन|अध्यापनं
अध्यापन n. (-नं) Instructing, teaching the sacred books; one of the six<BR>duties of a Brahman.<BR> E. अधि, इङ to go, in the causal form, and<BR>ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=020-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यापित
अध्यापित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Taught.<BR> E. अधीङ and क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=020-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्याय|अध्यायः
अध्याय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. The section, or division of a book.<BR>	 2. A chapter or<BR>lecture of the Vedas.<BR> E. अधि, इङ to go, and घञ् aff. proper to be<BR>gone through or read.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=020-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यारूढ|अध्यारूढः
अध्यारूढ mfn. (-ढः-ढा-ढं)<BR>	 1. Mounted on, riding upon.<BR>	 2. Exceeding, very<BR>much.<BR> E. अधि, and आङ before रुह to become manifest, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=020-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यारोप|अध्यारोपः
अध्यारोप m. (-पः) See the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=020-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यारोपण|अध्यारोपणं
अध्यारोपण n. (नं)<BR>	 1. Fixing in or upon.<BR>	 2. Transferring.<BR>	 3. Attaching<BR>erroneously the predicates of one object to another, as of eternity<BR>to matter, &c.<BR> E. अधि before रुह to grow, causal form ल्युट् affix,<BR>also with घञ् affix अध्यारोपः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=020-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यारोह
अध्यारोह m. (-हः) Mounting on, ascending.<BR> E. अधि, and आङ before रुह<BR>to rise, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=020-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यारोहण
अध्यारोहण n. (-णं) Ascending, mounting on or upon.<BR> E. अधि and आङ<BR>before रुह to rise, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=020-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यावाहनिक|अध्यावाहनिकं
अध्यावाहनिक n. (-कं) A woman's marriage portion, a dowry of such<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=021-a" target="_blank">Page021-a+ 60</a>]<BR>property as has descended to her lineally.<BR> E. अधि and आङ before<BR>वह to convey, ल्युट् affix, and ठक् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=020-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यास|अध्यासः
अध्यास n. (-सं)<BR>	 1. Inhabiting as chief, residing in, presiding over or<BR>ruling.<BR>	 2. Sitting on or upon.<BR>	 3. Transferring.<BR>	 4. Attributing<BR>erroneously the nature of one thing to another, as of eternity<BR>to matter, &c.<BR> E. अधि before, आस to sit, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=021-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यासित
अध्यासित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Seated in or on.<BR>	 2. Presiding over.<BR>	 3. In-<BR>habited<BR> E. अधि before, आस to sit, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=021-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यासीन
अध्यासीन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>	 1. Seated in or on.<BR>	 2. Placed or presiding<BR>over.<BR> E. अधि before, आसीन seated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=021-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्याहरण|अध्याहरणं
अध्याहरण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Supplying an ellipsis.<BR>	 2. Reasoning, discussing. E.<BR>अधि, आङ prefixed to हृञ to convey, with ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=021-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्याहार|अध्याहारः
अध्याहार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Adding a word or words to complete a sentence,<BR>supplying an ellipsis.<BR>	 2. Reasoning, argument. E. See अध्याहरण,<BR>घञ् being the aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=021-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्याहार्य्य|अध्याहार्य
अध्याहार्य्य mfn. (-र्य्यः-र्य्या-र्य्यं)<BR>	 1. Investigable.<BR>	 2. Requiring an ellipsis to<BR>be supplied.<BR> E. अधि, and आङ before हृ to take, ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=021-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्याहृत
अध्याहृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Supplied as an ellipsis.<BR>	 2. Argued, discussed.<BR>E. अधि and आङ before हृ to take, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=021-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्युषित
अध्युषित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Inhabited, settled.<BR> E. अधि before वस to dwell,<BR>affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=021-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्युष्ट्र|अध्युष्ट्रः
अध्युष्ट्र m. (-ष्ट्रः) A litter drawn or carried by a camel.<BR> E. अधि, and उष्ट्र<BR>camel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=021-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यूढ|अध्यूढः
अध्यूढ mfn. (-ढः-ढा-ढं)<BR>	 1. Very prosperous, thriving.<BR>	 2. Much.<BR>	 m. (-ढः) A<BR>name of ŚIVA.<BR>	 f. (-ढा) A superseded wife, one whose husband has<BR>married others.<BR> E. अधि, and ऊढ borne, from वह to bear, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=021-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्येतृ
अध्येतृ mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ) A student, reading, studying.<BR> E. अधि before, इङ<BR>to go, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=021-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्येषणा
अध्येषणा f. (-णा)<BR>	 1. Request, solicitation.<BR>	 2. Asking, begging.<BR> E. अधि, इष<BR>to wish, and ल्यु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=021-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्रुव
अध्रुव mfn. (-वः-वा-वं) Unstable, unfixed, uncertain, transient, perish-<BR>able.<BR> E. अ neg. ध्रुव fixed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=021-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्वग|अध्वगः
अध्वग mf. (-गः-गा) A traveller.<BR>	 m. (-गः)<BR>	 1. A camel.<BR>	 2. The sun.<BR>	 f. (-गा)<BR>A name of the river Ganges.<BR> E. अध्वन् a road, and ग who goes,<BR>from गम, with ड aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=021-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्वगमन
अध्वगमन n. (-नं) Journeying, travelling.<BR> E. अध्वन्, and गमन going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=021-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्वगामिन्
अध्वगामिन् mfn. (-मी-मिनी-मि) Travelling, a traveller.<BR> E. अध्वन् and गामिन्<BR>who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=021-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्वगभोग्य|अध्वगभोग्यः
अध्वगभोग्य m. (-ग्यः) A tree, (Spondias magnifera.)<BR> E. अध्वग a traveller,<BR>and भोग्य to be enjoyed by.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=021-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्वन्
अध्वन् m. (-ध्वा)<BR>	 1. A road.<BR>	 2. Fixing, placing.<BR>	 3. Time.<BR>	 4. Assault.<BR>	 5.<BR>Correcting viscidity, dilution of the phlegm and marrow.<BR> E. अत<BR>to go constantly, क्वनिप् affix; ध substituted for त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=021-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्वनीन|अध्वनीनः
अध्वनीन mf. (-नः-ना) A traveller.<BR> E. अध्वन्, and ख aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=021-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्वन्य|अध्वन्यः
अध्वन्य mf. (-न्यः-न्या) A traveller.<BR> E. अध्वन्, and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=021-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्वर|अध्वरः
अध्वर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A sacrifice.<BR>	 2. A Vasu, or a kind of demigod.<BR>	 3.<BR>Intent, attentive, careful.<BR> E. अ neg. ध्वॄ to bend or make crooked,<BR>and अच् affix; or अध्व a road, and र from रा to give; leading to<BR>heaven.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=021-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्वरथ|अध्वरथः
अध्वरथ m. (-थः) A travelling carriage or cart.<BR> E. अध्वन् a road, and रथ a<BR>carriage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=021-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्वर्य्यु|अध्वर्यु|अध्वर्युः|अध्वर्य्युः
अध्वर्य्यु m. (-र्य्युः) A Brahman versed in the Yajurveda.<BR> E. अध्वर a sacri-<BR>fice, क्यच् and उ affix, अ being dropped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=021-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्वशल्य|अध्वशल्यः
अध्वशल्य m. (-ल्यः) A tree, (Achyranthes aspera.) See अपमार्ग.<BR> E. अध्वन्,<BR>and शल्य a stake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=021-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्वान्त|अध्वांतं|अध्वान्तः
अध्वान्त n. (-न्तं) Gloom, twilight.<BR> E. अ neg. ध्वान्त darkness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=021-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्वान्तशात्रव|अध्वान्तशात्रवः
अध्वान्तशात्रव m. (-वः) A plant, (Cassia fistula.) See पत्रोर्ण.<BR> E. अ neg.<BR>ध्वान्त darkness, शात्रव inimical; blossoming in the shade.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=021-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन|अनः
अन (-घ) r. 2d. cl. (अनिति) Also of 4th cl. (ङ) (अन्यते) To breathe, to<BR>live. See अण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=021-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनंश
अनंश mfn. (-शः-शा-शं) Portionless, not entitled to a share or portion. E.<BR>अन् neg. अंश a part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=021-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनंशमत्फला
अनंशमत्फला f. (-ला) A plantain, (Musa sapientum.) See अंशुमत्फला.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=021-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनक|अनकः
अनक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) inferior, low. See अणक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=021-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनक्ष|अनक्षः
अनक्ष mfn. (-क्षः-क्षा-क्षं) Blind, eyeless.<BR> E. अन् neg. अक्षि the eye, the final<BR>dropped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=021-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनक्षर|अनक्षरं
अनक्षर n. (-रं)<BR>	 1. Blamable discourse, what is unfit to be uttered.<BR>	 2.<BR>Abuse.<BR> E. अन् neg. and अक्षर a letter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=021-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनक्षि
अनक्षि mfn. (-क्षि-क्षिः-क्षि) Having bad eyes.<BR> E. अन् neg. and अक्षि<BR>the eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=021-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनागार
अनागार m. (-रः) A saint, an anchorite.<BR> E. अन् neg. and आगार a house;<BR>living in woods.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=021-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनग्नि|अनग्निः
अनग्नि m. (-ग्निः) A Brahman who has not maintained his household<BR>fire.<BR> E. अन् neg. अग्नि fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=021-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनघ|अनघः
अनघ mfn. (-घः-घा-घं)<BR>	 1. Clean, clear.<BR>	 2. Pure, sinless.<BR>	 3. Handsome,<BR>pleasing.<BR> E. अन् neg. and अघ fault, faultless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=021-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनङ्ग|अनंग|अनङ्गं|अनङ्गः
अनङ्ग mfn. (-ङ्ग-ङ्गा-ङ्गं) Bodiless, incorporeal.<BR>	 m. (-ङ्गः) A name of KĀMA,<BR>the Hindu deity of love.<BR>	 n. (-ङ्गं)<BR>	 1. Heaven, æther or the atmos-<BR>phere.<BR>	 2. The mind or faculty of reasoning.<BR> E. अन् neg. and अङ्ग<BR>body; as applicable to KĀMA, it alludes to his having been re-<BR>duced to ashes, by the eye of ŚIVA, for having distributed his<BR>devotions, and rendered him enamoured of PĀRVATĪ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=021-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनङ्गक|अनंगकं|अनङ्गकं
अनङ्गक n. (-कं) The mind or faculty of reasoning.<BR> E. अनङ्ग, and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=021-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनङ्गासुहृद्
अनङ्गासुहृद् m. (-हृद् or -हृत्) A name of ŚIVA.<BR> E. अनङ्ग KĀMA, अ neg. and<BR>सुहृद् a friend, the foe of KĀMA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=021-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनच्छ|अनच्छः
अनच्छ mfn. (-च्छः-च्छा-च्छं) Turbid, muddy.<BR> E. अन् neg. and अच्छ clear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=021-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनञ्जन|अनंजन|अनञ्जनं
अनञ्जन n. (-नं) The sky, atmosphere, æther.<BR> E. अञ्ज to go, with the<BR>neg. prefix अन्, and affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=021-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनडुह्
अनडुह् m. (-ड्वान्) A bull or ox.<BR>	 f. (-डुही or -ड्वाही) A cow.<BR> E. अनस् a cart,<BR>वह to bear, and क्विप् affix, with ड inserted after अनस्, व is changed<BR>to उ in the mas., optionally in the fem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=021-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनणु|अनणुः
अनणु m. (-णुः) Small grain.<BR> E. अन् neg. अणु an atom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=021-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनत
अनत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Erect, not bowed down.<BR>	 2. Proud, haughty.<BR> E. अ<BR>neg. नत bowed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=021-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनतता
अनतता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Erectness, stiffness.<BR>	 2. Pride. Also अनतत्व n. (-त्वं)<BR> E. ता<BR>or त्व added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=021-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनतिक्रम
अनतिक्रम m. (-मः)<BR>	 1. Moderation, mediocrity, equality, not overstep-<BR>ping certain limits, not surpassing certain qualities, &c.<BR>	 2. Pro-<BR>priety, decorum.<BR> E. अन् neg. अतिक्रम exceeding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=021-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनतिक्रम्य
अनतिक्रम्य ind. Not having transgressed, &c.<BR>	 mfn. (-म्यः-म्या-म्यं) Incapable<BR>of being transgressed or exceeded.<BR> E. अन् neg. अतिक्रम्य having sur-<BR>passed, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=021-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनतिक्रान्त
अनतिक्रान्त mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं)<BR>	 1. Unsurpassed, unexceeded.<BR>	 2. Untrans-<BR>gressed, &c.<BR> E. अन् neg. अतिक्रान्त surpassed, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=021-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनतिरिक्त
अनतिरिक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं) Equal, not exceeded in quantity or quality.<BR>E. अन् neg. अतिरिक्त more.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=021-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनधिकार|अनधिकारः
अनधिकार m. (-रः) Absence of right, claim, interest or concern.<BR> E. अन्<BR>neg. अधिकार right.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=021-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनधिकारचर्च्चा|अनधिकारचर्चा
अनधिकारचर्च्चा f. (-र्च्चा) Officiousness, meddling with other people's busi-<BR>ness.<BR> E. अनधिकार, and चर्च्चा investigation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=021-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनधिकारिन्
अनधिकारिन् m. (-री) A non-heir, one who has no right or claim.<BR> E. अन्<BR>neg. अधिकारिन् an heir.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=021-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनधिकृत
अनधिकृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Uninherited, unclaimed.<BR>	 2. Not set over, or<BR>appointed.<BR> E. अन् neg. अधिकृत claimed, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=021-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनधिगत|अनधिगतः
अनधिगत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Not acquired.<BR>	 2. Not learnt or studied. E.<BR>अन् neg. अधिगत gone over.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=021-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनधिगम
अनधिगम m. (-मः)<BR>	 1. Non-acquirement.<BR>	 2. Non-perusal.<BR> E. अन् neg.<BR>अधिगम obtaining, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=021-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनधिगम्य
अनधिगम्य mfn. (-म्यः-म्या-म्यं)<BR>	 1. Unattainable.<BR>	 2. Incapable of being<BR>known.<BR> E. अन् neg. अधिगम्य so be attained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=021-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनधिष्ठित
अनधिष्ठित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Absent, not present.<BR>	 2. Not placed over,<BR>not appointed.<BR>	 3. Not ordered or enjoined.<BR> E. अन् neg. अधिष्ठित<BR>placed over.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=022-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनधीन|अनधीनः
अनधीन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Independent.<BR> E. अन् neg. अधीन dependent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=022-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनध्यक्ष|अनध्यक्षः
अनध्यक्ष mfn. (-क्षः-क्षा-क्षं)<BR>	 1. Imperceptible, unperceived, absent. See<BR>अप्रत्यक्ष.<BR>	 2. Having no superintendent.<BR> E. अन् neg. and अध्यक्ष percep-<BR>tible, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=022-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनध्याय|अनध्यायः
अनध्याय m. (-यः) Intermission of study.<BR> E. अन् neg. अध्याय reading.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=022-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनध्यायदिवस
अनध्यायदिवस m. (-सः) A day on which it is improper to study. E.<BR>अनध्याय, and दिवस a day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=022-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अननुज्ञात
अननुज्ञात mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Denied, refused, not assented to.<BR> E. अन् neg.<BR>अनुज्ञात assented to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=022-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्त|अनंत|अनन्तं|अनन्तः
अनन्त mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं)<BR>	 1. Eternal, endless.<BR>	 2. Unbounded, illimitable.<BR>3. Infinite, innumerable.<BR>	 m. (-न्तः)<BR>	 1. A name of VIṢṆU or<BR>KṚṢṆA.<BR>	 2. BALADEVA, the brother of KRISHNĀ.<BR>	 3. The chief of the<BR>NĀGAS or serpent race, that inhabit the infernal regions: the<BR>couch and constant attendant of VIṢṆU.<BR>	 4. The king of ser-<BR>pents, confounded with VĀSUKI. See वासुकि.<BR>	 5. The fourteenth<BR>of the Jaina Tīrthakaras or deified Saints: also called अनन्तजित्.<BR>	 f.<BR>(-न्ता)<BR>	 1. A name of PĀRVATĪ, the wife of SIVĀ.<BR>	 2. The earth.<BR>	 3.<BR>A synonym of several plants, (as Hedysarum alhagi.)<BR>	 4. A kind<BR>of potherb. See विशल्या.<BR>	 5. Bent grass, (Agrostis linearis.)<BR>	 6. Ano-<BR>ther plant, (Echites frutescens, Rox.) See श्यामा. Or according to<BR>others, (Asclepias pseudosarsa, Rox.) See शारिवा.<BR>	 7. Yellow myro-<BR>balan, (Terminalia citrina.)<BR>	 8. Emblic myrobalan, (Phyllanthus<BR>emblica).<BR>	 9. Another plant, (Menispermum glabrum.) See गुडुची.<BR>10. Long pepper. See कणा.<BR>	 n. (-न्तं) Sky or atmosphere, æther.<BR> E. अन्<BR>neg. and अन्त end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=022-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्तक|अनंतक
अनन्तक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Endless, eternal.<BR> E. कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=022-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्तचतुर्दशी|अनन्तचतुर्द्दशी
अनन्तचतुर्दशी f. (-शी) The fourteenth lunation of the light half of<BR>BHĀDRA, when ANANTA is worshipped.<BR> E. अनन्त, and चतुर्दशी the<BR>fourteenth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=022-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्तजित्
अनन्तजित् m. (-जित्) The fourteenth of the twenty-four Jaina defied<BR>Saints: also called अनन्त.<BR> E. अनन्त endless, and जित् who con-<BR>quers, who gains eternity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=022-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्तता
अनन्तता f. (-ता) Eternity: also अनन्तत्व n. (-त्वं)<BR> E. ता or त्व added to<BR>अनन्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=022-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्ततीर्थकृत्
अनन्ततीर्थकृत् m. (-कृत्) The fourteenth Jaina Saint, also अनन्त, &c.<BR> E. अनन्त<BR>endless, तीर्थ pilgrimage or virtue, and कृत् who has made.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=022-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्तमूल|अनन्तमूलः
अनन्तमूल m. (-लः) A plant, (Periploca Indica.)<BR> E. अनन्त, and मूल root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=022-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्तर|अनंतर|अनन्तरं
अनन्तर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>	 1. Next, immediately following.<BR>	 2. Next of kin or<BR>in succession.<BR>	 3. Close, compact.<BR>	 n. (-रं) Extreme propinquity E.<BR>अन् neg. and अन्तर between; having nothing intermediate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=022-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्तरज|अनन्तरजः
अनन्तरज mfn. (-जः-जा-जं) Born of the next in order; as of a Kṣatriya<BR>woman, by a Brahman; of a Vaiśya woman, by a Kṣatriya. E.<BR>अनन्तर, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=022-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्तराशि|अनन्तराशिः
अनन्तराशि f. (-शिः) In arithmetic; infinite quantity.<BR> E. अनन्त endless,<BR>राशि quantity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=022-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्तरूप
अनन्तरूप mfn. (-पः-पा-पं) Multiform.<BR> E. अनन्त, and रूप form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=022-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्तवात|अनन्तवातः
अनन्तवात m. (-तः) Rigidity or paralysis of the muscles of the face and<BR>neck.<BR> E. अनन्त, and वात wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=022-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्तविजय|अनन्तविजयः
अनन्तविजय m. (-यः) The shell of YUDHIṢṬHIRA.<BR> E. अनन्त, and विजय<BR>victory.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=022-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्तवीर्य्य|अनन्तवीर्य|अनन्तवीर्यः|अनन्तवीर्य्यः
अनन्तवीर्य्य m. (-र्य्यः) The twenty third Jaina Tīrthakara of a future age.<BR>E. अनन्त endless, and वीर्य्य power.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=022-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्तव्रत|अनन्तव्रतं
अनन्तव्रत n. (-तं) A ceremony performed in honour of VIṢṆU, on the<BR>day of the full moon in Bhādra.<BR> E. अनन्त, and व्रत a religious ob-<BR>servance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=022-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्तशीर्षा
अनन्तशीर्षा f. (-र्षा) The wife of VĀSUKI, the king of serpents.<BR> E. अनन्त<BR>many, and शीर्ष a head; many headed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=022-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्त्य|अनंत्य
अनन्त्य mfn. (-न्त्यः-न्त्या-न्त्यं) Infinite, unbounded, eternal n. (-न्त्यं)<BR>	 1. Im-<BR>mortality.<BR>	 2. Eternity.<BR>	 3. Infinity.<BR> E. अन् neg. अन्त्य final.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=022-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्य
अनन्य mfn. (-न्यः-न्या-न्यं)<BR>	 1. One, sole, without any other.<BR>	 2. Same, iden-<BR>tical.<BR> E. अन् neg. अन्य other.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=022-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्यगति|अनन्यगतिः
अनन्यगति mfn. (-तिः-तिः-ति) Having but one refuge.<BR>	 f. (-तिः) One only<BR>refuge or asylum.<BR> E. अनन्य, and गति motion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=022-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्यगतिक|अनन्यगतिकः
अनन्यगतिक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Having one refuge or hope alone.<BR> E. कन्<BR>added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=022-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्यज|अनन्यजः
अनन्यज m. (-जः) A name of KĀMA or love.<BR> E. अन् neg. अन्य other, and ज<BR>born; produced only in the heart.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=022-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्यता
अनन्यता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Singleness.<BR>	 2. Identity.<BR> E. अनन्य, and ता or त्व affix;<BR>also अनन्यत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=022-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्यपूर्व्व|अनन्यपूर्व|अनन्यपूर्वः
अनन्यपूर्व्व mfn. (-र्व्वः-र्व्वा-र्व्वं) Intact, virgin, never in the prior possession<BR>of another.<BR>	 f. (-र्व्वा) A virgin, a girl not previously wedded.<BR>E. अन् neg. अन्य another, पूर्व्व prior; also with कन् added<BR>अनन्यपूर्व्वक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=022-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्यभव
अनन्यभव mfn. (-वः-वा-वं) Produced or effected by one particular person or<BR>thing.<BR> E. अनन्य, and भव born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=022-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्यमनस्
अनन्यमनस् mfn. (-नः-नाः-नः) See the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=022-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्यमनस्क
अनन्यमनस्क mfn. (-स्कः-स्का-स्कं) Intent, attentive, having the mind fixed<BR>on one subject, not absent.<BR> E. अन् neg. अन्यमनस् or अन्यमनस्क think-<BR>ing of some thing else.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=022-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्यवृत्ति|अनन्यवृत्तिः
अनन्यवृत्ति mfn. (-त्तिः-त्तिः-त्ति) Closely attentive, having the mind fixed on<BR>one object.<BR> E. अन् neg. अन्य other, वृत्ति profession.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=022-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्यहृत
अनन्यहृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Not stolen or taken, safe.<BR> E. अन् neg. अन्य ano-<BR>ther, हृत taken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=022-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्यहार्य्य
अनन्यहार्य्य mfn. (-र्य्यः-र्य्या-र्य्यं) Incapable of being taken or stolen.<BR> E. अन्<BR>neg. अन्य another, हार्य्य to be taken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=022-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्वित
अनन्वित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Unconnected with, irrelevant.<BR>	 2. Devoid of,<BR>not possessing.<BR> E. अन् neg. अन्वित possessed of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=022-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनपकरण|अनपकरणं
अनपकरण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Non-requital, not retaliating.<BR>	 2. Non-resumption.<BR>3. Not doing ill.<BR> E. अन् before अपकरण evil doing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=022-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनपकर्म्मन्|अनपकर्मन्
अनपकर्म्मन् n. (-र्म्म)<BR>	 1. Non-retaliation. Non-resumption, (of a thing given<BR>or paid, &c.)<BR>	 3. Abstaining from evil.<BR> E. अन् before अपकर्म्मन्; also<BR>अनपाकर्म्मन्, अनपक्रिया, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=022-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनपकार|अनपकारः
अनपकार m. (-रः) Harmlessness, freedom from hatred and malice. E.<BR>अन् neg. अपकार evil doing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=022-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनपकारिन्
अनपकारिन् mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि) Innocuous.<BR> E. अनपकार, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=022-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनपक्रिया
अनपक्रिया f. (-या)<BR>	 1. Non-requital, non-retaliation.<BR>	 2. Non-acquittance<BR>(as of debt, &c.)<BR>	 3. Non-resumption.<BR>	 4. Abstaining from offence or<BR>evil.<BR> E. अन् before अपक्रिया offence, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=022-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनपचित
अनपचित mfn. (-नः-ता-तं) Dishonoured, disregarded.<BR> E. अन् neg. अपचित<BR>honoured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=022-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनपत्य
अनपत्य mfn. (-त्यः-त्या-त्यं) Childless, having no progeny: so अनपत्यक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR> E. अन् neg. अपत्य offspring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=022-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनपर
अनपर m. (-रः) Name of BRAHMĀ.<BR> E. अन् neg. अपर another.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=022-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनपराध|अनपराधः
अनपराध m. (-धः) Innocence.<BR>	 mfn. (-धः-धा-धं) Innocent, sinless.<BR> E. अन्<BR>neg. अपराध offence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=022-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनपराधिन्
अनपराधिन् mfn. (-धी-धिनी-धि) Innocent, sinless.<BR> E. अन् neg. अपराधिन्<BR>offending.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=022-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनपाय|अनपायः
अनपाय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Undiminished, unceasing.<BR>	 m. (-यः) Permanence,<BR>absence of loss or diminution.<BR> E. अन् neg. अपाय loss.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=022-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनपायिन्
अनपायिन् mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि)<BR>	 1. Firm, constant, durable, imperishable.<BR>2. Increasing.<BR> E. अनपाय permanence, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=022-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनपेक्ष|अनपेक्षं
अनपेक्ष mfn. (-क्षः-क्षा-क्षं) Disregarding, unheeding.<BR>	 f. (-क्षा) Carelessness,<BR>indifference, disregard.<BR> E. अन् neg. अपेक्षा regard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=022-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनपेक्षित
अनपेक्षित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Unheeded, disregarded.<BR> E. अन् neg. अपेक्षित<BR>regarded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=022-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनपेत
अनपेत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Present, not passed or gone.<BR>	 2. Possessed of,<BR>not devoid of.<BR> E. अन् neg. अपेत gone away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=022-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनभिमत
अनभिमत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Disagreeable, unpleasant, disastrous, unlucky.<BR>E. अन् neg. अभिमत liked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=023-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनभिज्ञ|अनभिज्ञः
अनभिज्ञ mfn. (-ज्ञः-ज्ञा-ज्ञं) Unwise, stupid.<BR> E. अन् neg. अभिज्ञ wise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=023-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनभिभव
अनभिभव m. (-वः) Freedom from obstruction or defeat.<BR> E. अन् neg. अभिभव<BR>defeat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=023-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनभिभूत
अनभिभूत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Unsubdued, unsurpassed.<BR>	 2. Unobstructed.<BR>E. अन् neg. अभिभूत subdued.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=023-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनभिलाष|अनभिलाषः
अनभिलाष m. (-षः) Indifference, absence of desire.<BR> E. अन् neg. अभिलाष<BR>desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=023-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनभिलाषिन्
अनभिलाषिन् mfn. (-षी-षिणी-षि) Indifferent.<BR> E. अनभिलाष, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=023-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनभिव्यक्त
अनभिव्यक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं) Indistinct, dim.<BR> E. अन् neg. अभिव्यक्त clear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=023-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनभिष्वङ्ग|अनभिष्वंग
अनभिष्वङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः) Detachment, disconnection, freedom from affection<BR>or attachment.<BR> E. अन् neg. अभिष्वङ्ग connection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=023-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनम|अनमः
अनम m. (-मः) A Brahman, one who does not salute a Brahman<BR>making obeisance to the gods only, and returning salutations,<BR>with his blessing.<BR> E. अ neg. and नम who salutes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=023-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनमस्य
अनमस्य mfn. (-स्यः-स्या-स्यं) Unworthy of being saluted.<BR> E. अ neg. नमस्य to<BR>be saluted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=023-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनय|अनयः
अनय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. Fate.<BR>	 2. Ill-luck, bad fortune.<BR>	 3. Calamity, distress.<BR>4. Vice, transgression.<BR> E. अन् neg. and अय good fortune.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=023-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनयङ्गत|अनयंगत
अनयङ्गत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Fallen into misfortune.<BR> E. अनय, and गत gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=023-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनर्गल|अनर्गलं
अनर्गल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Self-willed, unrestrained.<BR> E. अन् neg. and अर्गल a<BR>bolt or bar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=023-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनर्घ्य
अनर्घ्य mfn. (-र्घ्यः-र्घ्या-र्घ्यं) Invaluable, priceless, not to be bought.<BR> E. अन्<BR>neg. अर्घ्य price.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=023-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनर्घ्यत्व
अनर्घ्यत्व n. (-त्वं) Absence of price or cost, invaluableness; also अनर्घ्यता<BR>E. त्व or ता added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=023-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनर्च्चित|अनर्चित
अनर्च्चित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Unworshipped, unreverenced, disrespected. E.<BR>अन् neg. अर्च्चित worshipped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=023-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनर्थ|अनर्थः
अनर्थ mfn. (-र्थः-र्था-र्थं) Unmeaning, fruitless, nonsensical.<BR> E. अन् neg.<BR>अर्थ use.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=023-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनर्थक|अनर्थकं
अनर्थक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Unmeaning, idle, fruitless.<BR>	 n. (-कं) Unmeaning<BR>or nonsensical discourse.<BR> E. अन् neg. अर्थ meaning, and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=023-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनर्ह
अनर्ह mfn. (-र्हः-र्हा-र्हं) Unfit, unworthy, unsuitable.<BR> E. अन् neg. अर्ह fit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=023-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनल|अनलं|अनलः
अनल m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. A name of AGNI or fire.<BR>	 2. One of the eight Vasus or<BR>demigods so called.<BR>	 3. Bile.<BR>	 4. A plant, (Plumbago zeylanica and<BR>rosea.)<BR> E. अन् to be, कलच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=023-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनलप्रिया
अनलप्रिया f. (-या) The wife of AGNI,<BR> E. अनल, and प्रिया beloved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=023-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनलम्
अनलम् ind. Insufficient, unequal, unable, not enough.<BR> E. अन् neg. अलम्<BR>enough.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=023-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनलि|अनलिः
अनलि m. (-लिः) A plant, (Æschynomene grandiflora.) See अगस्तिद्रु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=023-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनवगीत
अनवगीत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Excellent, good, uncensured.<BR> E. अन् neg. अवगीत<BR>disparaged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=023-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनवग्रह
अनवग्रह mfn. (-हः-हा-हं) Resistless, not to be obstructed or impeded. E.<BR>अन् neg. अवग्रह obstruction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=023-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनवद्य
अनवद्य mfn. (-द्यः-द्या-द्यं)<BR>	 1. Blameless, irreproachable.<BR>	 2. Unobjection-<BR>able, allowable.<BR> E. अन् neg. अवद्य censurable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=023-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनवधान|अनवधानं
अनवधान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Careless, inattentive.<BR>	 n. (-नं) Inadvertence, in-<BR>attention, carelessness.<BR> E. अन् neg. अवधान care.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=023-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनवधानता
अनवधानता f. (-ता) Inadvertence, inattention.<BR> E. ता affix, subjoined to<BR>the preceding; or with त्व अनवधानत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=023-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनवर|अनवरः
अनवर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Equal or superior, not younger nor inferior. E.<BR>अन् neg. अवर inferior.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=023-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनवरत|अनवरतं
अनवरत adj.<BR>	 mfn. or adv.<BR>	 n. (-तः-ता-तं) Eternal, eternally.<BR> E. अन् neg.<BR>अवरत stopped, ceased.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=023-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनवरार्द्ध
अनवरार्द्ध mfn. (-र्द्धः-र्द्धा-र्द्धं) Chief, principal.<BR> E. अन् neg, अवरार्द्ध inferior.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=023-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनवलम्ब|अनवलंब|अनवलम्बः
अनवलम्ब mfn. (-म्बः-म्बा-म्बं) Without support or dependence.<BR> E. अन् neg.<BR>अवलम्ब support.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=023-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनवसर|अनवसरः
अनवसर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>	 1. Occupied, busy, having no leisure.<BR>	 2. Unseasonable,<BR>inopportune.<BR>	 m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Want of leisure or opportunity.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=023-b" target="_blank">Page023-b+ 60</a>]<BR>2. Unseasonableness, inopportuneness.<BR> E. अन् neg. अवसर<BR>leisure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=023-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनवस्कर|अनवस्करं
अनवस्कर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Clean.<BR> E. अन् priv. and अवस्कर dirt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=023-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनवस्थ
अनवस्थ mfn. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थं) Unstable, unsteady.<BR>	 2. Incontinent.<BR>	 f. (-स्था)<BR>1. Instability, absence of fixed state or condition.<BR>	 2. Uncertainty,<BR>doubt.<BR>	 3. Incontinence, dissoluteness.<BR>	 4. (In logic,) the abstract<BR>nature of a thing, independent of its existence.<BR> E. अन् neg. अवस्था<BR>condition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=023-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनवस्थान|अनवस्थानः
अनवस्थान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Unsteady, mutable, variable, not stationary.<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Instability.<BR>	 2. Wrong situation or direction.<BR>	 3. Mis-<BR>conduct.<BR>	 m. (-नः) Wind.<BR> E. अन् neg. अवस्थान fixture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=023-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनवस्थित
अनवस्थित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Unfixed, unsteady, unstable, inconstant.<BR>	 2.<BR>Loose, abandoned, violating moral and legal restraint.<BR> E. अन् neg.<BR>अवस्थित steady.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=023-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनवस्थिति|अनवस्थितिः
अनवस्थिति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Unsteadiness, instability.<BR>	 2. Dissoluteness, profli-<BR>gacy.<BR> E. अन् neg. and अवस्थिति stability.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=023-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनवाप्त
अनवाप्त mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं) Unobtained.<BR> E. अन् neg. अवाप्त obtained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=023-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनशन|अनशनं
अनशन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) One who fasts.<BR>	 n. (-नं) A fast, fasting.<BR> E. अन् neg.<BR>and अशन eating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=023-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनश्वर|अनश्वरं
अनश्वर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Eternal, imperishable.<BR> E. अ neg. and नश्वर tran-<BR>sient.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=023-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनस्
अनस् n. (-नः)<BR>	 1. A cart.<BR>	 2. Boiled rice.<BR>	 3. A mother.<BR>	 4. Birth.<BR>	 5. Life,<BR>breath<BR> E. अन् to live, असुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=023-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनसूय
अनसूय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Not envious.<BR>	 f. (-या)<BR>	 1. The wife of the sage<BR>ATRI.<BR>	 2. Exemption from envy.<BR> E. अन् neg. असूया envy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=023-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनसूयक
अनसूयक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Unenvious.<BR> E. अन् neg. असूया, and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=023-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनसूयु
अनसूयु mfn. (-युः-युः-यु) Free from envy.<BR> E. अन् neg. असूय to envy,<BR>उस् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=023-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनहङ्कार|अनहंकार
अनहङ्कार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Absence of pride, humility.<BR>	 2. The absence of the<BR>pride of individuality: one of the elements of creation, according<BR>to the Vedanta system.<BR> E. अन् neg. अहङ्कार pride.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=023-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनहङ्कारिन्|अनहंकारिन्
अनहङ्कारिन् mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि) Philosophical, humble, not proud, not<BR>selfish.<BR> E. अन् neg. अहङ्कारिन् proud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=023-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनहङ्कृति|अनहंकृति|अनहङ्कृतिः
अनहङ्कृति f. (-तिः) Content, satisfaction, the absence of care or vanity.<BR>E. अन् neg. अहङ्कृति pride.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=023-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाकार
अनाकार mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Shapeless, without form.<BR> E. अन् neg. आकार form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=023-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाकाल|अनाकालः
अनाकाल n. (-लं) Scarcity, famine.<BR> E. अन् neg. आङ् before काल time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=023-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाकालभृत|अनाकालभृतः
अनाकालभृत m. (-तः) A slave, one who has given himself to slavery, in a<BR>season of scarcity, for support.<BR> E. अनाकाल, and भृत nourished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=023-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाकुल|अनाकुलः
अनाकुल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Unperplexed, collected, composed.<BR> E. अन् neg.<BR>and आकुल perplexed, confused.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=023-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाक्रान्त|अनाक्रांत
अनाक्रान्त mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं) Unsurpassed, unsubdued.<BR>	 f. (-न्ता) A sort of<BR>prickly nightshade, (Solanum jacquini. WILD.) See कण्टकारी.<BR> E. अन्<BR>neg. आक्रान्त surpassed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=023-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाक्षारित
अनाक्षारित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Not calumniated, free from reproach or cen-<BR>sure.<BR> E. अन् neg. आक्षारित censured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=023-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनागत|अनागतं
अनागत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Not come, not arrived: (of a person, absent;)<BR>future, (of time.)<BR>	 2. Unknown, undistinguished.<BR>	 3. Not acquired,<BR>learned or obtained.<BR> E. अन् neg. आगत come, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=023-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनागतार्तवा|अनागतार्त्तवा
अनागतार्तवा f. (-वा) A young girl, one not arrived at puberty.<BR> E. अन्<BR>neg. आगत arrived, and आर्तव from ऋतु the menstrual flux, who has<BR>not menstruated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=023-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनागम|अनागमः
अनागम m. (-मः)<BR>	 1. Non-arrival of person or time.<BR>	 2. Non-acquisition.<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>	 1. Not arrived, not present.<BR>	 2. Not having or ob-<BR>taining.<BR>	 3. Not scriptural.<BR>	 4. Not having vouchers or deeds.<BR> E. अन्<BR>neg. आगम arrival, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=023-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनागम्य
अनागम्य mfn. (-म्यः-म्या-म्यं)<BR>	 1. Unapproachable, inaccessible.<BR>	 2. Unobtain-<BR>able.<BR> E. अन् neg. आगम्य to be approached.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=023-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाचरण
अनाचरण n. (-णं) Improper or immoral conduct.<BR> E. अन् neg. आचरण moral<BR>rule or practice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=023-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाचार|अनाचारः
अनाचार mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Immoral, ill-behaved, indecent.<BR>	 m. (-रः) impro-<BR>priety, violation of moral or civil rule or institute.<BR> E. अन् neg.<BR>आचार moral rule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=024-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाचारिन्
अनाचारिन् mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि) Immoral, indecorous, indecent.<BR> E. अन् neg.<BR>आचारिन् decent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=024-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाढ्य
अनाढ्य mfn. (-ढ्यः-ढ्या-ढ्यं) Poor, without wealth.<BR> E. अन् neg. आढ्य rich.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=024-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनातप|अनातपः
अनातप m. (-पः)<BR>	 1. Shade, shadow.<BR>	 2. Coolness.<BR> E. अन् neg. and आतप<BR>heat, moral or physical.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=024-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनातुर|अनातुरः
अनातुर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Well, vigorous, free from sickness or pain.<BR> E. अ<BR>neg. आतुर diseased.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=024-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनात्मनीन
अनात्मनीन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Disinterested, liberal, not regarding self alone.<BR>E. अन् neg. आत्मनीन selfish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=024-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाथ|अनाथः
अनाथ mfn. (-थः-था-थं) Without a master or protector, without a hus-<BR>band, &c.<BR> E. अ neg. नाथ master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=024-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनादर|अनादरः
अनादर m. (-रः) disrespect.<BR> E. अन् neg. and आदर respect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=024-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनादि|अनादिः
अनादि mfn. (-दिः-दिः-दि) Eternal, without any beginning, unborn, un-<BR>created.<BR> E. अन् neg. आदि beginning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=024-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनादित्व|अनादित्वं
अनादित्व n. (-त्वं) Eternity, exemption from commencement or birth.<BR>Also अनादिता.<BR> E. ता or त्व added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=024-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनादिष्ट
अनादिष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>	 1. Denied, refused, dissented.<BR>	 2. Not directed,<BR>advised or commanded.<BR> E. अन् neg. आदिष्ट directed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=024-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनादीनव
अनादीनव mfn. (-वः-वा-वं) Pure, faultless.<BR> E. अन् neg. आदीनव faulty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=024-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनादृत|अनादृतः
अनादृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Disrespected, despised.<BR> E. अन् neg. and आदृत<BR>respected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=024-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनादेय
अनादेय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Inadmissable, unacceptable, not to be taken or<BR>received<BR> E. अन् neg. आदेय to be taken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=024-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाधृष्य
अनाधृष्य mfn. (-ष्यः-ष्या-ष्यं) Unconquerable, indomitable.<BR> E. अन् neg. आधृष्य<BR>to be tamed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=024-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनापन्न
अनापन्न mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं) Unobtained, unattained.<BR> E. अन् neg. आपन्न ob-<BR>tained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=024-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाप्त|अनाप्तः
अनाप्त mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं)<BR>	 1. Unskilful, unapt.<BR>	 2. Uneffected, unobtained. E.<BR>अन् neg. आत fit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=024-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनामक|अनामकं|अनामकः
अनामक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Nameless, noteless.<BR>	 m. (-कः) The intercalary<BR>month.<BR>	 n. (-कं) Piles or hœmorrhoids.<BR> E. अ bad, नामक from नामन्<BR>a name, with कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=024-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनामन्
अनामन् m. (-मा) The ring finger. See अनामिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=024-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनामय|अनामयं|अनामयः
अनामय n. (-यं) Health.<BR> E. अन् neg. and आमय sickness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=024-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनामिका
अनामिका f. (-का) The ring finger.<BR> E. अ neg. and नामिका deriv. of नामन्<BR>a name, having no other name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=024-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनायत
अनायत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Unchecked, unrestrained.<BR>	 2. Close, continu-<BR>ous, unseparated.<BR>	 3. Unextended, having no length.<BR> E. अन् neg.<BR>आयत restrained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=024-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनायत्त|अनायत्तः
अनायत्त mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं) Independent, uncontrolled.<BR> E. अन् neg. आयत्त<BR>dependent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=024-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनायत्तवृत्तिता
अनायत्तवृत्तिता f. (-ता) Independence, self-subsistence.<BR> E. अनायत्त, and वृत्ति<BR>or वृत्तिता business.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=024-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनायास|अनायासः
अनायास m. (-सः) Exemption from pain or difficulty, facility, ease.<BR>	 2.<BR>Absence of exertion, idleness, neglect.<BR> E. अन् neg. आयास effort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=024-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनायासकृत|अनायासकृतं
अनायासकृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Done readly or easily.<BR>	 2. In medicine,<BR>prepared, extemporaneously simply decorated, (medicine or drugs.)<BR>E. अन् neg. आयास effort, pains, and कृत made, made without<BR>trouble.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=024-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनार्जव|अनार्जवं|अनार्ज्जव
अनार्जव n. (-वं)<BR>	 1. Crookedness, moral or physical.<BR>	 2. Disease.<BR> E. अन् neg.<BR>आर्जव straightness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=024-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनारत|अनारतं
अनारत adj.<BR>	 mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) adv.<BR>	 n. (-तं) Eternal, eternally.<BR> E. अन् neg.<BR>and आ prefixed to रम to be pleased, क्त affixed; having no rest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=024-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनारम्भ|अनारंभः|अनारम्भः
अनारम्भ m. (-म्भः)<BR>	 1. Defect of commencement, being without a beginning.<BR>2. Non-commencement, not attempting or undertaking.<BR> E. अन् neg.<BR>आरम्भ beginning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=024-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनारोग्य
अनारोग्य n. (-ग्यं) Sickness.<BR> E. अन् neg. आरोग्य health.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=024-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनारोग्यकर
अनारोग्यकर mfn. (-रः-रा-री-रं) Unwholesome, unhealthy, causing sickness.<BR>E. अनारोग्य, and कर what makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=024-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनार्य्य|अनार्य|अनार्यः|अनार्य्यः
अनार्य्य mfn. (-र्य्यः-र्य्या-र्य्यं) Unworthy, inferior, bad, vile.<BR> E. अन् neg. (-आर्य्य)<BR>respectable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=024-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनार्य्यक|अनार्यक|अनार्यकं|अनार्य्यकं
अनार्य्यक n. (-कं) Agallochum or aloe wood, (Aquila agallocha, Rox.)<BR>See the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=024-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनार्य्यज|अनार्यज|अनार्य्यजं
अनार्य्यज mfn. (-जः-जा-जं) Of vile or unworthy origin.<BR>	 n. (-जं) Agallo-<BR>chum or aloe wood, (Aquila agallocha.) See अगुरु.<BR> E. अन् priv. आर्य्य<BR>respectable, and ज produced; the perfume being brought from<BR>the country of Mlecchas or barbarians.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=024-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनार्य्यता|अनार्यता
अनार्य्यता f. (-ता) Vileness, unworthiness, baseness; also अनार्य्यत्वं E.<BR>ता or त्व added to अनार्य्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=024-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनार्य्यतिक्त|अनार्यतिक्त|अनार्यतिक्तः|अनार्य्यतिक्तः
अनार्य्यतिक्त m. (-क्तः) A medicinal plant, a kind of gentian, (Gentiana<BR>cherayta, Rox.)<BR> E. अनार्य्य inferior, and तिक्त bitter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=024-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनालम्ब|अनालंब|अनालम्बः
अनालम्ब mfn. (-म्बः-म्बा-म्बं) Unsupported, without stay or support.<BR> E. अन्<BR>neg. आलम्ब support.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=024-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनालाप|अनालापः
अनालाप mfn. (-पः-पा-पं) Silent, taciturn.<BR>	 m. (-पः) Taciturnity.<BR> E. अन् neg.<BR>आलाप conversing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=024-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनालोचित|अनालोचितः
अनालोचित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Unseen, unbeheld.<BR>	 2. Unweighed, uncon-<BR>sidered, rash, imprudent.<BR> E. अन् neg. आलोचित seen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=024-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाविल|अनाविलः
अनाविल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Clear, clean, pure.<BR> E. अन् neg. and आविल<BR>turbid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=024-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनावृत|अनावृतः
अनावृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Uncovered, undressed.<BR>	 2. Open, unenclosed.<BR>E. अन् neg. आवृत covered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=024-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनावृत्त
अनावृत्त mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं)<BR>	 1. Not stirred or turned round.<BR>	 2. Not retreating.<BR>E. अन् neg. and आवृत्त whirled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=024-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनावृष्टि|अनावृष्टिः
अनावृष्टि f. (-ष्टिः) Drought.<BR> E. अन् neg. आ before वृष्टि rain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=024-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाश्य|अनाश्यः
अनाश्य mfn. (-श्यः-श्या-श्यं) Indestructible.<BR> E. अ neg. नाश्य to be destroyed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=024-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाश्रय|अनाश्रयः
अनाश्रय m. (-यः) Detachment, absence of attachment or dependence. E.<BR>अन् neg. आश्रय asylum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=024-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाश्रित
अनाश्रित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Detached, disengaged, unconcerned in or un-<BR>connected with<BR> E. अन् neg. आश्रित dependent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=024-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाश्वस्
अनाश्वस् mfn. (-श्वान्-शुषी-श्वत्) Fasting, not eating.<BR> E. अन् neg. आश्वस्<BR>eating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=024-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनासादित
अनासादित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Not occurred, not having happened, nonexistent.<BR>E. अन् neg. आसादित effected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=024-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनासिक|अनासिकः
अनासिक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Noseless.<BR> E. अ neg. and नासिका the nose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=024-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनास्था
अनास्था f. (-स्था)<BR>	 1. Disrespect.<BR>	 2. Want of fixity or condition.<BR> E. अन् neg.<BR>आस्था station.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=024-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाहत|अनाहतं|अनाहतः
अनाहत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Unhurt, unbeaten, unwounded, intact.<BR>	 2. New<BR>and unbleached, (as cloth.)<BR>	 m. (-तः) The fourth of the mystical<BR>Chakras or circles of the body.<BR> E. अन् neg. and आहत beaten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=024-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाहार|अनाहारः
अनाहार n. (-रं)<BR>	 1. Abstinence, starvation.<BR>	 2. Non-production.<BR>	 3. Non-seizure.<BR>E. अन् neg. आहार food, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=024-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाहारिन्
अनाहारिन् mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>	 1. Not seizing.<BR>	 2. Fasting.<BR> E. अन् neg. and<BR>आहारिन् who takes food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=024-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाहार्य्य|अनाहार्य
अनाहार्य्य mfn. (-र्य्यः-र्य्या-र्य्यं)<BR>	 1. Not to be seized or taken, not producible.<BR>2. Not to be eaten.<BR> E. अन् neg. आहार्य्य to be taken, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=024-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाहुत
अनाहुत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Uncalled, unbidden: also अनाहूत.<BR> E. अन् neg.<BR>आहुत called.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=024-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिक्षु|अनिक्षुः
अनिक्षु m. (-क्षुः) A sort of long grass or reed, (Saccharum spontaneum.)<BR>E. अन् neg. and इक्षु sugar-cane; not it, but it's like.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=024-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिगीर्ण|अनिगीर्णः|अनिगीर्ण्ण
अनिगीर्ण mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-र्णं) Unuttered, unsaid.<BR> E. अ neg. निगीर्ण uttered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=024-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिग्रह|अनिग्रहः
अनिग्रह mfn. (-हः-हा-हं) Unrestrained.<BR> E. अ neg. निग्रह restraint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=024-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिच्छ
अनिच्छ mfn. (-च्छः-च्छा-च्छं) Undesirous, averse, indifferent: so अनिच्छक.<BR>E. अन्, and इच्छा wish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=024-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिच्छा
अनिच्छा f. (-च्छा) Indifference, absence of wish or desire.<BR> E. अन् neg.<BR>इच्छा desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=024-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिच्छु|अनिच्छुः|अनिछु
अनिच्छु mfn. (-च्छुः-च्छुः-च्छु)<BR>	 1. Disliking, not wishing.<BR>	 2. Indifferent. E.<BR>अन् neg. इच्छु who wishes: also अनिच्छक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=024-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनित्य|अनित्यः
अनित्य mfn. (-त्यः-त्या-त्यं)<BR>	 1. Transient, not everlasting.<BR>	 2. Occasional,<BR>incidental.<BR>	 3. Irregular, unusual.<BR> E. अ neg. नित्य constant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=025-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनित्यक्रिया
अनित्यक्रिया f. (-या) An occasional act of worship, sacrifice for a special<BR>purpose.<BR> E. अनित्य occasional, not constant, and क्रिया rite, also<BR>अनित्यकर्म्म, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=025-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनित्यता
अनित्यता f. (-ता) Transient or limited existence: also अनित्यत्व<BR> E. ता or त्व<BR>added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=025-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनित्यसम|अनित्यसमः
अनित्यसम m. (-मः) Arguing by illustration, not by logical rule.<BR> E. अनित्य<BR>unusual, and सम same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=025-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिदान
अनिदान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Causeless, groundless.<BR> E. अ neg. निदान.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=025-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिद्र
अनिद्र mfn. (-द्रः-द्रा-द्रं) Awake, sleepless.<BR> E. अ neg. निद्रा sleep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=025-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिन्दित|अनिन्दितः
अनिन्दित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Pious, virtuous, free, unreproachable.<BR> E. अ neg.<BR>and निन्दित reproached.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=025-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिन्द्य
अनिन्द्य mfn. (-न्द्यः-न्द्या-न्द्यं) Faultless.<BR> E. अ neg. निन्द्य blamable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=025-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिपुण|अनिपुणः
अनिपुण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Unskilled, unlearned, not conversant.<BR> E. अ neg.<BR>निपुण clever.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=025-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिबद्ध
अनिबद्ध mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>	 1. Unproduced, unseized.<BR>	 2. Unattached.<BR> E. अ neg.<BR>निबद्ध attached.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=025-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिभृत
अनिभृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Unsteady (as the mind), agitated.<BR>	 2. Tremulous,<BR>moving.<BR> E. अ neg. निभृत held firmly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=025-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिमिष|अनिमिषं|अनिमिषः
अनिमिष m. (-षः)<BR>	 1. A god.<BR>	 2. A fish.<BR>	 3. A person whose eyes are fixed,<BR>(as in disease), &c.<BR> E. अ neg. and निमिष what twinkles; the eyes<BR>being always fixed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=025-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिमिषाचार्य्य|अनिमिषाचार्य|अनिमिषाचार्यः|अनिमिषाचार्य्यः
अनिमिषाचार्य्य m. (-र्य्यः) A name of VṚHASPATI.<BR> E. अनिमिष a deity, and<BR>आचार्य्य a teacher; the preceptor of the gods.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=025-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिमेष|अनिमेषं|अनिमेषः
अनिमेष m. (-ष)<BR>	 1. A deity.<BR>	 2. A fish.<BR>	 3. A demon.<BR>	 4. A spirit or ghost.<BR>5. A person whose eyes are fixed. See अनिमिष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=025-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनियत|अनियतं
अनियत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Transitory, perishable.<BR>	 2. Unrestrained.<BR>	 3.<BR>Undefined, unprescribed.<BR> E. अ neg. नियत restrained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=025-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनियम|अनियमः
अनियम m. (-मः)<BR>	 1. Uncertainty, doubt.<BR>	 2. Absence of moral or religious<BR>obligation.<BR>	 3. Indecorous or improper conduct.<BR>	 mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Undetermined, undefined, unprovided for, by any rule or law.<BR> E. अ<BR>neg. नियम fixed observance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=025-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिराकृत|अनिराकृतः
अनिराकृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Unchecked, unobstructed.<BR> E. अ neg. निराकृत<BR>opposed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=025-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिरुद्ध|अनिरुद्धं|अनिरुद्धः
अनिरुद्ध mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>	 1. A spy, a secret emissary.<BR>	 2. Self willed, un-<BR>governable, headstrong.<BR>	 3. Unobstructed, unrestrained.<BR>	 m. (-द्धः)<BR>The son of PRADYUMNA, a form of KĀMA, and husband of<BR>UṢĀ.<BR>	 n. (-द्धं) The rope for fastening cattle.<BR> E. अ neg. निरुद्ध<BR>restrained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=025-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिरुद्धपथ|अनिरुद्धपथं
अनिरुद्धपथ n. (-थं)<BR>	 1. The atmosphere, æther.<BR>	 2. An unobstructed path.<BR>E. अनिरुद्ध unobstructed, and पथिन् a road.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=025-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिरुद्धभाविनी
अनिरुद्धभाविनी f. (-नी) A proper name. See उषा.<BR> E. अनिरुद्ध, and भाविनी a<BR>wife; the wife of ANIRUDDHA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=025-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिर्णय|अनिर्णयः
अनिर्णय m. (-यः) Uncertainty.<BR> E. अ neg. निर्णय certainty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=025-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिर्णीत
अनिर्णीत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Unascertained, undetermined.<BR> E. अ neg. निर्णीत<BR>ascertained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=025-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिर्णेय
अनिर्णेय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Undecidable, incapable of being decided.<BR> E. अ<BR>neg. निर्णेय decidable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=025-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिर्दिष्ट
अनिर्दिष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं) Unexplained, undefined.<BR> E. अ neg. निर्दिष्ट<BR>explained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=025-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिर्देश|अनिर्देशः
अनिर्देश m. (-शः) Absence of demonstration or direction.<BR> E. अ neg. निर्देश<BR>instruction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=025-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिर्द्धारित
अनिर्द्धारित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Unascertained, undetermined, undefined.<BR> E. अ<BR>neg. निर्द्धारित defined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=025-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिर्भर
अनिर्भर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Little, slight, light.<BR> E. अ neg. निर्भर bulky.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=025-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिर्मल|अनिर्म्मल|अनिर्म्मलः
अनिर्मल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Dirty, foul.<BR> E. अ neg. निर्मल clean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=025-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिर्माल्या|अनिर्म्माल्या
अनिर्माल्या f. (-ल्या) A plant, (Medicago esculenta, Rox.) See पृका.<BR> E. अ<BR>not, निर् out from, and माल्य from माला a necklace; not used in<BR>garlands.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=025-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिर्वचनीय|अनिर्व्वचनीयः
अनिर्वचनीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Not to be mentioned or described, indescrib-<BR>able.<BR> E. अ neg. निर्वचनीय describable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=025-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिर्वाह|अनिर्वाहः|अनिर्व्वाह|अनिर्व्वाहः
अनिर्वाह m. (-हः)<BR>	 1. Incoherence, want of connexion or consistency.<BR>	 2.<BR>Want of means of subsistence.<BR>	 3. Incompleteness.<BR> E. अ neg. निर्वाह<BR>connexion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=025-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिर्व्विण
अनिर्व्विण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>	 1. Disgusted.<BR>	 2. Poor, needy.<BR> E. अ neg. निर्व्विण<BR>satisfied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=025-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिर्व्विद|अनिर्विद
अनिर्व्विद mfn. (-वित्) Free from pain or trouble.<BR> E. अ neg. निर्व्विद what<BR>annoys.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=025-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिर्व्वृत|अनिर्वृत
अनिर्व्वृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Discontented.<BR>	 2. Unquiet, discomposed.<BR>	 3. Un-<BR>accomplished, unfulfilled.<BR> E. अ neg. निर्व्वृत effected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=025-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिर्व्वृति|अनिर्वृति|अनिर्वृतिः
अनिर्व्वृति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Poverty.<BR>	 2. Discontent.<BR>	 3. Incompleteness.<BR> E. अ neg.<BR>निर्व्वृति completion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=025-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिल|अनिलः
अनिल m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. Air or wind considered also as a deity.<BR>	 2. A subordinate<BR>deity, forty-nine of form whom a class, ANILAS or winds.<BR>	 3. One of<BR>another class demigods or Vasus.<BR>	 4. Wind, as one of the humors of<BR>the body.<BR>	 5. Rheumatism, paralysis, or any affection referred to dis-<BR>order of the wind.<BR> E. अन to breathe, इलट् aff.<BR>	 f. (-ली) The fifteenth<BR>Nakshatra or lunar mansion. See स्वाति.<BR> E. अनिल and the fem.<BR>termination: the wind being the ruling deity of the constellation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=025-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिलघ्नक|अनिलघ्नकः
अनिलघ्नक m. (-कः) A large tree, (Terminalia belerica.)<BR> E. अनिल, घ्न what<BR>removes, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=025-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिलपर्य्यय|अनिलपर्यय
अनिलपर्य्यय m. (-यः) Pain and swelling of the eyelids and outer parts of<BR>the eye.<BR> E. अनिल, and पर्य्यय pervasion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=025-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिलसख|अनिलसखः
अनिलसख m. (-खः) A name of fire.<BR> E. अनिल, and सखि a friend, the<BR>friend of the wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=025-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिलात्मज|अनिलात्मजः
अनिलात्मज m. (-जः) The son of the wind, HANUMAN or BHĪMA.<BR> E. अनिल,<BR>and आत्मज son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=025-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिलामय|अनिलामयः
अनिलामय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. Flatulence.<BR>	 2. Morbid affection of the wind, rheu-<BR>matism, &c.<BR> E. अनिल, and आमय sickness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=025-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिलाशिन्
अनिलाशिन् mfn. (-शी-शिनी-शि) Fasting, lit. feeding on the wind.<BR> E. अनिल,<BR>and अशिन् who eats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=025-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिलोचित
अनिलोचित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Unconsidered, inconsiderate, imprudent.<BR> E. अ<BR>neg. निलोचित regarded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=025-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिलोडित
अनिलोडित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Unconsidered, ill judged, undiscriminated. E.<BR>अ neg. निलोडित revolved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=025-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिवारित
अनिवारित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Unchecked, unimpeded, unopposed, unforbid-<BR>den.<BR> E. अ neg. निवारित checked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=025-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिश|अनिशं
अनिश n. (-शं) Eternally, eternal, (not employed as an adjective).<BR> E. अ<BR>neg. and निश from निशा night; having no night or end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=025-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिश्चित|अनिश्चितः
अनिश्चित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Unascertained, not certain.<BR> E. अ neg. निश्चित<BR>ascertained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=025-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिष्ट|अनिष्टः
अनिष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं) Unwished, undesirable, bad, unlucky.<BR>	 f. (-ष्टा) A<BR>plant, (Sida alba.)<BR> E. अन् neg. इष्ट wished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=025-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिष्ठा
अनिष्ठा f. (-ष्ठा) Unsteadfastness, unsteadiness.<BR> E. अ neg. निष्ठा fixedness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=025-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिष्णात|अनिष्णातः
अनिष्णात mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Unskilful, ignorant.<BR> E. अ neg. निष्णात clever.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=025-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिष्पन्न|अनिष्पन्नः
अनिष्पन्न mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं) Imperfect, incomplete.<BR> E. अ neg. निष्पन्न<BR>completed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=025-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिषिद्ध
अनिषिद्ध mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं) Unprohibited, unforbidden.<BR> E. अ neg. निषिद्ध<BR>prohibited.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=025-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिसर्ग
अनिसर्ग mfn. (-र्गः-र्गा-र्गं) Unnaturally elated or depressed.<BR> E. अ neg. निसर्ग<BR>natural condition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=025-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिस्तीर्ण
अनिस्तीर्ण mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-र्णं)<BR>	 1. Unanswered, unrefuted.<BR>	 2. Not set aside or<BR>got over.<BR> E. अ neg. निस्तीर्ण replied to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=025-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनीक|अनीकं|अनीकः
अनीक mn. (-कः-कं)<BR>	 1. An army, forces.<BR>	 2. War, combat.<BR> E. अन् to live,<BR>and ईकन् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=025-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनीकस्थ|अनीकस्थः
अनीकस्थ m. (-स्थः)<BR>	 1. An armed or royal guard, a sentinel.<BR>	 2. A warrior,<BR>a combatant.<BR>	 3. The trainer of an elephant, an elephant driver.<BR>4. A mark, a sign, a signal.<BR>	 5. A military drum.<BR> E. अनीक battle,<BR>and स्थ what stays.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=025-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनीकिनी
अनीकिनी f. (-नी)<BR>	 1. An army, a host, forces.<BR>	 2. A certain force;<BR>one-tenth of an Akṣauhiṇī, containing two thousand, one hundred<BR>and eighty-seven elephants, and as many cars, six thousand, five<BR>hundred and sixty-seven horses, and ten thousand, nine hundred<BR>and thirty-five foot.<BR>	 3. A lotus.<BR> E. अनीक an army, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=026-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनीच
अनीच mfn. (-चः-चा-चं) Decent, respectable.<BR> E. अ neg. नीच low.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=026-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनीचानुवर्त्तिन्|अनीचानुवर्तिन्
अनीचानुवर्त्तिन् mfn. (-र्त्ती-र्त्तिनी-र्त्ति) Not keeping low or improper com-<BR>pany.<BR>	 m. (-र्त्ती) A faithful lover or husband.<BR> E. अ neg. नीच low,<BR>अनुवर्त्तिन् following.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=026-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनीचदर्शिन्
अनीचदर्शिन् m. (-र्शी) A Bauddha saint.<BR> E. अ neg. नीच low, दर्शिन् who<BR>sees.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=026-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनीति|अनीतिः
अनीति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Impropriety, immorality.<BR>	 2. Impolicy, ill conduct. E.<BR>अ neg. नीति good conduct.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=026-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनीदृश
अनीदृश mfn. (-शः-शी-शं) Unlike, dissimilar.<BR> E. अ neg. ईदृश like.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=026-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनीश|अनीशः
अनीश mfn. (-शः-शा-शं) One who has not a lord or superior.<BR>	 m. (-शः)<BR>VIṢṆU.<BR> E. अन् neg. ईश lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=026-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनीश्वर
अनीश्वर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>	 1. Without a superior.<BR>	 2. Unchecked, uncon-<BR>trolled.<BR>	 3. Without power, powerless, unable.<BR>	 4. Atheist.<BR> E. अन्<BR>neg. ईश्वर a supreme.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=026-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनीश्वरता
अनीश्वरता f. (-ता) Absence of a supreme ruler.<BR> E. ता or त्व added to the<BR>last: also अनीश्वरत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=026-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनीश्वरवादिन्
अनीश्वरवादिन् m. (-दी) An atheist, one who denies a supreme ruler of<BR>the universe.<BR> E. अनीश्वर, and वादिन् who asserts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=026-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनीह|अनीहः
अनीह mfn. (-हः-हा-हं) Careless, indifferent.<BR> E. अन् neg. ईहा wish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=026-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनीहा
अनीहा f. (-हा) Indifference, apathy, disinclination.<BR> E. अन् neg. ईहा wish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=026-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनीहित
अनीहित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Disagreeable, displeasing, unwished.<BR>	 n. (-तं)<BR>Displeasure.<BR> E. अन्, and ईहित desired.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=026-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनु|अनुः
अनु ind. A preposition and prefix, implying 1. After.<BR>	 2. Like, in same<BR>manner.<BR>	 3. Under, inferior to.<BR>	 4. Along, lengthwise.<BR>	 5. With, to-<BR>gether with.<BR>	 6. In part of.<BR>	 7. Severally, each, by each.<BR>	 8. Near to.<BR>9 In regard to.<BR>	 10. To, out to, (calling.)<BR>	 11. Orderly, methodical.<BR>As अनुकर्त्तुं to act like; अनुगन्तुं to follow; अनुक्रमितुं to proceed in<BR>order; अनुशयितुं to repent, &c.; also, अनुरूपं according to the form;<BR>अनुविष्णु according to VIṢṆU; अनुगङ्गं upon or along the Ganges.<BR>See also the following words.<BR> E. अन् to live and ज aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=026-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुक|अनुकः
अनुक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Lustful, libidinous.<BR> E. अनु and क from कम to<BR>desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=026-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुकथन|अनुकथनं
अनुकथन n. (-नं) Discourse, conversation.<BR> E. अनु and कथन speaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=026-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुकम्पा|अनुकंपा
अनुकम्पा f. (-म्पा) Tenderness, compassion.<BR> E. अनु before कपि to tremble,<BR>and affix अच्, and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=026-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुकम्प्य|अनुकंप्य|अनुकम्प्यः
अनुकम्प्य mfn. (-म्प्यः-म्प्या-म्प्यं)<BR>	 1. Swift, expeditious.<BR>	 2. Pitiable, worthy of<BR>tenderness or compassion.<BR> E. अनु before कपि to tremble, य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=026-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुकरण|अनुकरणं
अनुकरण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Imitation, making or doing any thing like or in imita-<BR>tion of another, following an example.<BR>	 2. Resemblance, similarity.<BR>E. अनु, and करण making.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=026-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुकर्म्मन्|अनुकर्मन्
अनुकर्म्मन् n. (-र्म्म)<BR>	 1. Imitation.<BR>	 2. A subsequent rite or ceremony.<BR> E. अनु,<BR>and कर्म्मन् act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=026-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुकर्ष|अनुकर्षः
अनुकर्ष m. (-षः)<BR>	 1. The bottom of a carriage.<BR>	 2. Invoking, summoning<BR>by incantation.<BR>	 3. Attraction, drawing.<BR> E. अनु before, कृष to drag or<BR>furrow, and घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=026-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुकर्षण|अनुकर्षणं
अनुकर्षण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Invoking, summoning by incantations.<BR>	 2. Attracting,<BR>attraction.<BR>	 3. Including a subsequent in a preceding rule.<BR> E. अनु,<BR>and कृष to draw, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=026-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुकर्षन्
अनुकर्षन् m. (-ष) The bottom of a carriage. See अनुकर्ष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=026-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुकल्प|अनुकल्पः
अनुकल्प m. (-ल्पः)<BR>	 1. An alternative, a substitute.<BR>	 2. A secondary, subsi-<BR>diary or succedaneous injunction; as, instead Kūsā grass use Durba.<BR>E. अनु after and कल्प a principal precept.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=026-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुकामम्
अनुकामम् ind. According to wish or inclination.<BR> E. अनु and काम desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=026-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुकामीन|अनुकामीनः
अनुकामीन m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. One who goes as he lists.<BR>	 2. One who acts as<BR>he pleases.<BR> E. अनुकाम and ईन, for गामिन् who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=026-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुकार|अनुकारः
अनुकार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Imitation.<BR>	 2. Resemblance.<BR> E. अनु like, and कृञ् to do,<BR>with अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=026-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुकारिन्
अनुकारिन् mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि) Imitating, an imitator.<BR> E. अनुकार, and इनि<BR>aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=026-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुकूल|अनुकूलः
अनुकूल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Friendly, well disposed to, favourable or con-<BR>formable to.<BR>	 m. (-लः) A faithful husband.<BR>	 f. (-ला) Croton polyan-<BR>drum.<BR>	 n. (-लं) Favour, kindness.<BR> E. अनु, and कूल race, family.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=026-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुकूलता
अनुकूलता f. (-ता) Concord, good will, consent.<BR> E. अनुकूल, and ता affix;<BR>also with त्व, अनुकूलत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=026-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुकृत
अनुकृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Copied, imitated, made like or done in like<BR>manner.<BR> E. अनु, and कृत made.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=026-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुक्रकच
अनुक्रकच mfn. (-चः-चा-चं) Serrated, dentated.<BR> E. अनु like, क्रकच a saw.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=026-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुक्रम|अनुक्रमः
अनुक्रम m. (-मः) Order, method.<BR> E. अनु methodically, and क्रम to go, with<BR>घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=026-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुक्रमण|अनुक्रमणं
अनुक्रमण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Proceeding methodically or in order.<BR>	 2. Following.<BR>E. अनु, and क्रमण going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=026-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुक्रमणिका
अनुक्रमणिका f. (-का) A table or chapter of contents.<BR> E. कन् fem. form add-<BR>ed to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=026-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुक्रान्त
अनुक्रान्त mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं) Done methodically, passed over, read, &c. in<BR>due order.<BR> E. अनु, and क्रान्त gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=026-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुक्रिया
अनुक्रिया f. (-या)<BR>	 1. Imitation, doing any thing subsequently or in like<BR>manner.<BR>	 2. A subsequent rite or ceremony.<BR> E. अनु and क्रिया act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=026-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुक्रोश|अनुक्रोशः
अनुक्रोश m. (-शः) Tenderness, compassion.<BR> E. अनु, and क्रुश to bewail,<BR>घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=026-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुक्षण|अनुक्षणं
अनुक्षण n. adv. (-णं) Momentarily, perpetually.<BR> E. अनु, and क्षण a moment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=026-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुग|अनुगः
अनुग mfn. (-गः-गा-गं)<BR>	 1. Following.<BR>	 2. A follower, a servant.<BR>	 m. (-गः) A<BR>husband, a master.<BR> E. अनु after, and ग who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=026-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुगत|अनुगतः
अनुगत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Followed literally or figuratively, as by a de-<BR>pendent, &c.<BR>	 2. Following, a follower or a dependent.<BR>	 3. Acquired,<BR>obtained.<BR>	 4. Determined, defined.<BR> E. अनु, and गत gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=026-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुगम|अनुगमः
अनुगम m. (-मः)<BR>	 1. Following, going after in life or death.<BR>	 2. Imitating,<BR>approaching.<BR> E. अनु, and गम going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=026-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुगमन|अनुगमनं
अनुगमन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Going after, following.<BR>	 2. Dying after, as of a widow.<BR>See अनुमरण<BR> E. अनु, and गमन going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=026-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुगम्य
अनुगम्य mfn. (-म्यः-म्या-म्यं) Worthy of being followed or imitated.<BR> E. अनु,<BR>and गम्य to be gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=026-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुगवीन|अनुगवीनः
अनुगवीन m. (-नः) A cowherd.<BR> E. अनु and गवीन belonging to kine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=026-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुगामिन्
अनुगामिन् m. (-मी)<BR>	 1. A companion, a follower.<BR>	 2. One who goes behind<BR>or after.<BR> E. अनु after or with, and गामिन् who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=026-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुगुण|अनुगुणः
अनुगुण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) According or suitable to, according to merit or<BR>property.<BR> E. अनु, and गुण quality.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=026-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुगृहीत
अनुगृहीत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Favoured, obliged.<BR> E. अनु, and गृहीत taken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=026-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुग्र
अनुग्र mfn. (-ग्रः-ग्रा-ग्रं) Calm, gentle, not violent.<BR> E. अन् neg. उग्र<BR>fierce.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=026-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुग्रह|अनुग्रहः
अनुग्रह m. (-हः) Favour; conferring benefits, promoting good, and<BR>preventing ill.<BR> E. अनु afterwards, ग्रह to take, and अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=026-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुग्राहिन्
अनुग्राहिन् mfn. (-ही-हिणी-हि) Gracious, favourable.<BR> E. अनु, and ग्राहिन्<BR>who takes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=026-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुचर|अनुचरः
अनुचर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A companion, a follower.<BR>	 2. A servant.<BR>	 f. (-री) A fe-<BR>male companion.<BR> E. अनु with or after, and चर to go, ट aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=026-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुचारिन्
अनुचारिन् mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि) Following, attending.<BR> E. अनु before, चारिन्<BR>who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=026-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुचित
अनुचित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Improper, wrong.<BR> E. अन् neg. उचित proper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=026-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुचिन्ता|अनुचिंता
अनुचिन्ता f. (-न्ता) Thinking of, meditating upon, recalling, recollecting.<BR>E. अनु subsequent, चिन्ता thought.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=026-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुचिन्तित
अनुचिन्तित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Recollected, recalled, thought of.<BR> E. अनु and<BR>चिन्तित thought.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=026-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुच्च
अनुच्च mfn. (-च्चः-च्चा-च्चं) Low, not high, humble.<BR> E. अन् neg. उच्च high.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=026-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुच्छिष्ट|अनुच्छिष्टः
अनुच्छिष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं) Pure, purified by austerity and devotion E.<BR>अन् neg. and उच्छिष्ट rejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=026-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुज|अनुजं|अनुजः
अनुज mfn. (-जः-जा-जं) Born after, later, younger.<BR>	 m. (-जः) A younger<BR>brother.<BR>	 f. (-जा) A younger sister.<BR> E. अनु after, ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=027-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुजन्मन्
अनुजन्मन् mfn. (-न्मा-न्मा-न्म) Younger, junior.<BR> E. अनु after, and जन्मन्<BR>birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=027-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुजात|अनुजातः
अनुजात mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) After-born, later, younger.<BR>	 m. (-तः) A younger<BR>brother f. (-ता) A younger sister.<BR> E. अनु after, जात born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=027-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुज्झित
अनुज्झित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Undiminished, unimpaired, not left or lost. E.<BR>अन् neg. उज्झित left.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=027-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुजीविन्
अनुजीविन् mfn. (-वी-विनी-वि)<BR>	 1. Servant, dependent.<BR>	 2. A companion, a<BR>follower.<BR> E. अनु after or with, and जीविन् who lives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=027-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुज्ञा
अनुज्ञा f. (-ज्ञा)<BR>	 1. An order or command.<BR>	 2. Assent.<BR> E. अनु according to,<BR>ज्ञा to know, and क्विप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=027-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुज्ञात
अनुज्ञात mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Ordered, directed, instructed.<BR>	 2. Assented to,<BR>permitted, allowed.<BR>	 3. Accepted.<BR>	 4. Acknowleged, recognised.<BR> E. अनु<BR>and ज्ञात known.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=027-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुज्ञापक|अनुज्ञापकः
अनुज्ञापक m. (-कः) One who commands or enjoins.<BR> E. अनु, and ज्ञापक<BR>who makes known.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=027-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुतप्त
अनुतप्त mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं)<BR>	 1. Heated.<BR>	 2. Filled with regret or repentance. E.<BR>अनु, and तप्त heated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=027-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुतर|अनुतरं
अनुतर n. (-रं) Fare, freight.<BR> E. अनु, and तर what crosses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=027-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुतर्ष|अनुतर्षः
अनुतर्ष m. (-र्षः)<BR>	 1. Thirst.<BR>	 2. Wish.<BR>	 3. A drinking vessel, one used to<BR>drink spirituous liquors from. See अनुतर्षण.<BR> E. अनु and तर्ष, from तृष<BR>to thirst, and घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=027-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुतर्षण|अनुतर्षणं
अनुतर्षण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. A vessel from which spirituous liquor is drunk.<BR>	 2.<BR>Distributing liquor.<BR> E. अनु before तृष to be thirsty, and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=027-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुताप|अनुतापः
अनुताप m. (-पः)<BR>	 1. Repentance.<BR>	 2. Heat.<BR> E. अनु afterwards, and ताप<BR>heat, pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=027-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुतापिन्
अनुतापिन् mfn. (-पि-पिनी-पि) Penitent, regretting.<BR> E. अनुताप and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=027-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुत्क
अनुत्क mfn. (-त्कः-त्का-त्कं) Free from regret, possessed of self-compla-<BR>cency.<BR> E. अन् neg. उत्क sorry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=027-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुत्कर्ष
अनुत्कर्ष m. (-र्षः) Inferiority.<BR> E. अन् neg. उत्कर्ष superiority.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=027-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुत्तम|अनुत्तमः
अनुत्तम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>	 1. Chief, principal, best.<BR>	 2. Worse, inferior, not<BR>best.<BR> E. अन् neg. and उत्तम best.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=027-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुत्तर|अनुत्तरं
अनुत्तर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>	 1. Chief, principal.<BR>	 2. Best, excellent.<BR>	 3. Unable<BR>to answer, silent.<BR>	 4. Fixed, firm.<BR>	 5. Low, inferior.<BR>	 6. South,<BR>southern.<BR>	 n. (-रं) A reply which is incoherent or evasive, and is<BR>therefore held to be no answer.<BR> E. अन् neg. and उत्तर subse-<BR>quent, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=027-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुत्तान
अनुत्तान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Lying with the face to the ground.<BR> E. अन् neg.<BR>उत्तान sleeping, supine<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=027-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुत्पत्ति|अनुत्पत्तिः
अनुत्पत्ति f. (-त्तिः)<BR>	 1. Failure.<BR>	 2. Non-production.<BR> E. अन् neg. उत्पत्ति pro-<BR>duction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=027-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुत्पन्न
अनुत्पन्न mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>	 1. Uneffected, unaccomplished.<BR>	 2. Unborn, un-<BR>produced.<BR> E. अन् neg. उत्पन्न produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=027-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुदग्र|अनुदग्रः
अनुदग्र mfn. (-ग्रः-ग्रा-ग्रं)<BR>	 1. Very lofty.<BR>	 2. Not lofty, low.<BR> E. अन् neg.<BR>उदग्र lofty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=027-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुदर
अनुदर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Thin, lank.<BR> E. अन् neg. उदर belly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=027-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुदात
अनुदात mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं) Unaccented.<BR>	 m. (-त्तः) One of the three accents<BR>to be observed in reading the Vedas, the grave accent.<BR> E. अन्<BR>neg. उत् high, and आत्त pronounced, from दा to give, आङ् pre-<BR>fixed, to speak, and क्त affixed: pronouncing the vowels in a low<BR>and full tone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=027-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुदार|अनुदारः
अनुदार mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>	 1. Liberal, munificent.<BR>	 2. Niggardly, mean.<BR>	 3.<BR>Adhered to or followed by a wife.<BR> E. अन् neg. उदार liberal, or अनु,<BR>and दार wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=027-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुदित
अनुदित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Unrisen.<BR>	 2. Unsaid, unuttered.<BR> E. अन् neg.<BR>उदित risen or said.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=027-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुदिन|अनुदिनं
अनुदिन adv.<BR>	 n. (-नं) Daily.<BR> E. अनु and दिन day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=027-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुद्धत
अनुद्धत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Unsurpassed, unequalled.<BR>	 2. Unopposed.<BR>	 3.<BR>Humble.<BR> E. अन् neg. उद्धत proud, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=027-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुद्धरण|अनुद्धरणं
अनुद्धरण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Non-removal.<BR>	 2. Not offering.<BR>	 3. Not establishing or<BR>proving.<BR> E. अन् neg. उद्धरण taking away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=027-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुद्धार|अनुद्धारः
अनुद्धार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Non-partition, not taking a share.<BR>	 2. Non-removal.<BR>E. अन् neg. उद्धार partition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=027-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुद्धृत
अनुद्धृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Non-removed, not taken away.<BR>	 2. Uninjured,<BR>undestroyed.<BR>	 3. Unoffered.<BR>	 4. Undivided, unpartitioned.<BR>	 5. Un-<BR>established, unproved.<BR> E. अन् neg. उद्धृत removed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=027-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुद्युत
अनुद्युत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Inactive, idle, destitute of perseverance.<BR> E. अन्<BR>neg. उद्युत active.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=027-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुद्योग|अनुद्योगः
अनुद्योग m. (-गः) Absence of exertion or effort, laziness.<BR> E. अन् neg.<BR>उद्योग effort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=027-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुद्योगिन्
अनुद्योगिन् mfn. (-गी-गिनी-गि) Lazy, indifferent.<BR> E. अनुद्योग, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=027-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुद्रुत|अनुद्रुतं
अनुद्रुत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Followed, pursued.<BR>	 n. (-तं) A measure of time in<BR>music, half a Druta, or one fourth of a Matra or time taken to<BR>articulate a short vowel.<BR> E. अनु after, and द्रुत gone, escaped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=027-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुद्वाह|अनुद्वाहः
अनुद्वाह m. (-हः) Celibacy.<BR> E. अन् neg. उद्बाद्व marriage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=027-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुद्विग्न
अनुद्विग्न mfn. (-ग्नः-ग्ना-ग्नं) Easy, free from apprehension or perplexity. E.<BR>अन् neg. उद्विग्न anxious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=027-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुद्वेग|अनुद्वेगः
अनुद्वेग mfn. (-गः-गा-गं) Free from anxiety.<BR>	 m. (-गः) Freedom from<BR>anxiety.<BR> E. अन् neg. उद्वेग anxiety.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=027-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुधावन|अनुधावनं
अनुधावन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Chasing, pursuit, running after.<BR>	 2. Pursuit of any<BR>object, as of a mistress, &c.<BR> E. अनु, and धावन running.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=027-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुधावित
अनुधावित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Pursued, run after, literally or figuratively. E.<BR>अनु, and धावित run.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=027-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुनय|अनुनयः
अनुनय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. Salutation, courtesy, civility, showing respect or<BR>adoration to a guest or a deity.<BR>	 2. Regulation of conduct,<BR>discipline, tuition.<BR> E. अनु and नय, from णीञ् to guide or lead, and<BR>अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=027-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुनयिन्
अनुनयिन् mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि) Courteous, humble.<BR> E. अनुनय, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=027-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुनाद|अनुनादः
अनुनाद m. (-दः) Sound, consequent sound, vibration, echo.<BR> E. अनु, and<BR>नाद noise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=027-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुनासिक
अनुनासिक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Nasal, uttered through the nose.<BR> E. अनु and<BR>नासिका the nose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=027-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुनीत
अनुनीत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Trained, disciplined.<BR>	 2. Obtained, acquired.<BR>3. Taught.<BR>	 4. Respected.<BR>	 5. Pleased, pacified, appeased.<BR> E. अनु,<BR>and नीत brought.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=027-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुन्मत्त
अनुन्मत्त mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं) Sane, sober, not wild, not mad: so अनुन्माद. E.<BR>अन् neg. अन्मत्त mad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=027-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुप
अनुप mfn. (-पः-पा-पं) Watery, marshy; more usually अनूप.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=027-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपकारिन्
अनुपकारिन् mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि) Not assisting, neglecting, ungrateful. E.<BR>अन् neg. उपकारिन् assisting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=027-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपकृत
अनुपकृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Unassisted.<BR> E. अन् neg. उपकृत assisted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=027-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपतन|अनुपतनं
अनुपतन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Falling on or upon.<BR>	 2. Following.<BR> E. अनु, and पतन<BR>falling, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=027-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपतित
अनुपतित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Fallen, descended.<BR>	 2. Followed.<BR> E. अनु, and<BR>पतित fallen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=027-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपदिष्ट
अनुपदिष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं) Untaught, uninstructed.<BR> E. अन् neg. उपदिष्ट<BR>advised.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=027-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपदम्
अनुपदम् ind.<BR>	 1. Following.<BR>	 2. Step by step.<BR>	 3. Upon the foot.<BR>	 n. (-दं)<BR>A burthen, a word or passage repeated.<BR> E. अनु, and पद a foot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=027-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपदिन्
अनुपदिन् m. (-दी) A searcher, an inquirer, one who follows or seeks for.<BR>E. अनुपदम् following, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=027-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपदीना
अनुपदीना f. (-ना) A boot, a buskin.<BR> E. अनुपद upon the foot, and ख aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=027-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपन्यस्त
अनुपन्यस्त mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं) Undetermined, not established.<BR> E. अन् neg.<BR>उपन्यस्त fixed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=027-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपन्यास|अनुपन्यासः
अनुपन्यास m. (-सः) Failure of proof or determination, uncertainty,<BR>doubt.<BR> E. अन् neg. उपन्यास ascertainment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=027-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपपत्ति|अनुपपत्तिः
अनुपपत्ति f. (-त्तिः)<BR>	 1. Not supporting an assertion by good argument,<BR>inconclusive argumentation.<BR>	 2. Non-completion, not effecting or<BR>accomplishing, failure.<BR> E. अन् neg. उपपत्ति demonstration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=027-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपपन्न
अनुपपन्न mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>	 1. Not done, unaccomplished, uneffected.<BR>	 2.<BR>Unproved, undemonstrated.<BR> E. अन् neg. उपपन्न effected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=028-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुप्रपन्न
अनुप्रपन्न mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं) following, conforming to.<BR> E. अनु, and प्रपन्न done.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=028-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपभुक्त
अनुपभुक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं) Unenjoyed, unpossessed.<BR> E. अन् neg. उपभुक्त<BR>enjoyed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=028-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपम|अनुपमः
अनुपम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं) Excellent, best.<BR>	 f. (-मा) The female elephant of<BR>the south-east, or of the north-east.<BR> E. अन् neg. and उपमा resem-<BR>blance; above comparison.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=028-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपमेय
अनुपमेय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Incomparable: so अनुपमित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR> E. अन्<BR>neg. उपमित compared, or उपमेय comparable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=028-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपयुक्त
अनुपयुक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं) Useless, unnecessary, unserviceable.<BR> E. अन्<BR>neg. उपयुक्त serviceable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=028-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपयोग|अनुपयोगः
अनुपयोग m. (-गः) Unserviceableness, uselessness.<BR> E. अन् neg. उपयोग<BR>utility.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=028-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपलक्षित
अनुपलक्षित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Unmarked, undiscriminated.<BR> E. अन् neg.<BR>उपलक्षित marked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=028-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपलब्ध
अनुपलब्ध mfn. (-ब्धः-ब्धा-ब्धं)<BR>	 1. Unperceived, unascertained.<BR>	 2. Unob-<BR>tained.<BR> E. अन् neg. उपलब्ध obtained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=028-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपशय|अनुपशयः
अनुपशय m. (-यः) Any aggravating thing or circumstance, (in medi-<BR>cine) what increases the disease.<BR> E. अन् neg. उपशय a palliative.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=028-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपस्कृत
अनुपस्कृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Undressed, unprepared.<BR>	 2. Unfinished, un-<BR>polished.<BR>	 3. Unrequited.<BR> E. अन् neg. उपस्कृत finished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=028-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपस्थान|अनुपस्थानं
अनुपस्थान n. (-नं) Absence.<BR> E. अन् neg. उपस्थान vicinity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=028-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपस्थापन|अनुपस्थापनं
अनुपस्थापन n. (-नं) Not producing, not offering, not placing, not<BR>having ready or at hand.<BR> E. अन् neg. उप near, स्थापन placing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=028-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपस्थापित
अनुपस्थापित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Not ready, not at hand, not offered or<BR>produced.<BR> E. अन् neg. उपस्थापित placed near.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=028-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपस्थापिन्
अनुपस्थापिन् mfn. (-पी-पिनी-पि) Absent, distant.<BR> E. अन् neg. उपस्थापिन्<BR>near.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=028-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपस्थिति|अनुपस्थितिः
अनुपस्थिति f. (-तिः) Absence.<BR> E. अन् neg. उपस्थिति vicinity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=028-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपात|अनुपातः
अनुपात m. (-तः)<BR>	 1. Falling subsequently upon, alighting or descending<BR>upon in succession.<BR>	 2. Going, preceeding.<BR>	 3. Following.<BR>	 4. A<BR>degree of latitude opposite to one given, the antœci.<BR>	 5. Propor-<BR>tion, (in arithmetic.)<BR>	 6. Arithmetical progression.<BR> E. अनु, and<BR>पात falling, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=028-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपातक|अनुपातकं
अनुपातक n. (-कं) A heinous crime, as, falsehood, fraud, theft, adul-<BR>tery, &c. अनु, and पातक crime.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=028-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपान|अनुपानं
अनुपान n. (-नं) A fluid vehicle in medicine; drink taken with or after<BR>medicine.<BR> E. अनु after or with, and पान a drink.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=028-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपार्श्व
अनुपार्श्व mfn. (-र्श्वः-र्श्वा-र्श्वं) Lateral.<BR> E. अनु by or upon, पार्श्व the side.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=028-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुप्राप्त
अनुप्राप्त mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं) Obtained, attained, arrived at.<BR> E. अनु, and प्राप्त<BR>obtained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=028-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपुष्प|अनुपुष्पः
अनुपुष्प m. (-ष्पः) A kind of reed, (Saccharum sara.)<BR> E. अनु before पुष्प<BR>to put forth flowers, and अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=028-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपूर्व्व|अनुपूर्व|अनुपूर्वं
अनुपूर्व्व mfn. (-र्व्वः-र्व्वा-र्व्वं) Regular, orderly, successively, from the pre-<BR>ceding<BR> E. अनु after, पूर्व्व prior.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=028-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपूर्व्वम्|अनुपूर्वम्
अनुपूर्व्वम् ind. In regular order or succession, from the first, from above<BR>downwards.<BR> E. अनुपूर्व्व and शसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=028-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुप्त
अनुप्त mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं) Unsown, (as seed.)<BR> E. अन् neg. उप्त sown.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=028-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुप्तशस्य
अनुप्तशस्य mfn. (-स्यः-स्या-स्यं) Fallow, meadow, (ground, &c.)<BR> E. अन् neg.<BR>उप्त sown, शस्य grain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=028-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुप्रस्थ
अनुप्रस्थ mfn. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थं) Latitudinal.<BR> E. अनु neg. according to, प्रस्थ<BR>extending.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=028-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुप्रास|अनुप्रासः
अनुप्रास m. (-सः) Alilteration, repetition of similar letters, syllables<BR>and words.<BR> E. अनु and प्र before अस् to be, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=028-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुप्लव|अनुप्लवः
अनुप्लव m. (-वः) A companion or follower.<BR> E. अनु, प्लु to go, and अप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=028-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुबद्ध
अनुबद्ध mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं) Bound to, connected with.<BR> E. अनु, and बद्ध<BR>bound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=028-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुबन्ध|अनुबंधः|अनुबन्धः
अनुबन्ध m. (-न्धः)<BR>	 1. The inseparable adjunct or sign of any thing, the<BR>indication of guilt, symptom of disease, &c.<BR>	 2. An element of<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=028-b" target="_blank">Page028-b+ 60</a>]<BR>language, root, affix, &c.<BR>	 3. An indicatory letter not sounded or<BR>dropped in composition, but marking some peculiarity in inflecting<BR>the word to which it is attached; for instance, an indicatory इ,<BR>denotes that verbs require the insertion of a nasal before their<BR>final consonant.<BR>	 4. A child or pupil, who imitates an example set<BR>by the parent or preceptor.<BR>	 5. A child or infant in general.<BR>	 6. Com-<BR>mencement, beginning.<BR>	 7. Binding, confining.<BR>	 8. Any thing small<BR>or little, a part, a small part.<BR>	 9. The connexion between the<BR>agent and the cause or motive.<BR>	 10. Circumstance, case.<BR>	 11. The junc-<BR>tion of fractions.<BR>	 12. A secondary or symptomatic affection, one<BR>supervening on the principal disease.<BR>	 f. (न्धा)<BR>	 1. Hickup.<BR>	 2. Thirst.<BR>E. अनु after, and बन्ध to bind or confine, with घञ् affix; and in<BR>the fem. ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=028-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुबन्धिन्|अनुबंधिन्
अनुबन्धिन् mfn. (-न्धी-न्धिनी-न्धि) Connected with, attached.<BR> E. अनुबन्ध and<BR>इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=028-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुबन्ध्य|अनुबंध्य
अनुबन्ध्य mfn. (-न्ध्यः-न्ध्या-न्ध्यं) Principal, primary, what may receive an<BR>adjunct, as a root, a disease, &c.<BR> E. अनु and बन्ध to be attached<BR>to or by.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=028-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुबोध|अनुबोधः
अनुबोध m. (-धः)<BR>	 1. Reviving the scent of a faded perfume.<BR>	 2. Re-<BR>placing perfumes removed by bathing, &c.<BR>	 3. An afterthought.<BR>E. अनु, and बुध to understand, with घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=028-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुबोधित
अनुबोधित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Informed or convinced by reflection.<BR> E. अनु<BR>and बोधित made known.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=028-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुभव|अनुभवः
अनुभव m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. Conclusive judgment, understanding, impression,<BR>the exercise of the intellect, independent of memory; also अनुभूति.<BR>2. Result, consequence.<BR> E. अनु, भू to be, and अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=028-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुभाव|अनुभावः
अनुभाव m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. Indication of passion, by look or gesture.<BR>	 2. Dig-<BR>nity, authority, consequence.<BR>	 4. Firm opinion, belief, knowledge.<BR>4. Certainty, ascertainment.<BR> E. अनु, and भाव the essence or<BR>being; according to the internal feelings.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=028-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुभाविन्
अनुभाविन् mfn. (-वी-विनी-वि)<BR>	 1. Judging, knowing, understanding.<BR>	 2.<BR>Indicative of passion or feeling.<BR> E. अनु and भाविन् perceiving, or<BR>अनुभाव and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=028-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुभूत
अनुभूत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Understood, judged, apprehended.<BR>	 2. Result-<BR>ed, followed as a consequence.<BR>	 3. Perceiving, understanding. E.<BR>अनु, and भूत been.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=028-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुभूति|अनुभूतिः
अनुभूति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Judgment; knowledge, from four sources, percep-<BR>tion, inference, comparison and verbal information; or any source<BR>except memory.<BR>	 2. Dignity, consequence.<BR> E. अनु, and भूति<BR>being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=028-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुमत|अनुमतः
अनुमत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Accepted, assented to.<BR>	 2. Agreeable,<BR>pleasant.<BR>	 3. Loved, beloved.<BR>	 4. Concurred with, being of one<BR>opinion.<BR> E. अनु, and मत minded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=028-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुमति|अनुमतिः
अनुमति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Order or command.<BR>	 2. Assent, permission.<BR>	 3. A<BR>fifteenth day of the moon's age, on which she rises one digit<BR>less than full.<BR> E. अनु with, before मन to respect, and क्तिन् affix;<BR>in the last acceptation, because offerings made to the manes on<BR>this day are especially accepted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=028-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुमन्तृ|अनुमंतृ
अनुमन्तृ mfn. (-न्ता-न्त्री-न्तृ) Consenting to, concurring in, permitting. E.<BR>अनु, and मन् to mind, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=028-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुमरण|अनुमरणं
अनुमरण n. (-णं) Dying with or following in death; the term usually<BR>denotes the cremation of a Hindu widow, whose husband's corpse<BR>is not on the spot, and with part of whose dress she, therefore,<BR>ascends the pile: this is prohibited to Brahman women. It is<BR>also synonimous with सहमरण burning with the body.<BR> E. अनु with<BR>or after, and मरण dying: dying with her husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=028-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुमा
अनुमा f. (-मा) Inference (in logic,) drawing a conclusion from given<BR>premises.<BR> E. अनु after or according to, मा from माङ् to measure,<BR>affix अङ् and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=028-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुमान|अनुमानं
अनुमान n. (-नं) See अनुमा.<BR> E. अनु, and मा to measure, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=028-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुमानोक्ति|अनुमानोक्तिः
अनुमानोक्ति f. (-क्तिः) Reasoning, logic.<BR> E. अनुमान, and उक्ति saying, speak<BR>ing from inference.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=029-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुमित
अनुमित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Inferred.<BR> E. अनु, and मित measured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=029-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुमिति|अनुमितिः
अनुमिति f. (-तिः) Inference, conclusion from given premises.<BR> E. अनु,<BR>and मिति measuring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=029-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुमृता
अनुमृता f. (-ता) The woman who burns with a part of her husband's<BR>dress.<BR> E. अनु, and मृता deceased.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=029-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुमेय
अनुमेय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Inferable.<BR> E. अनु, and मेय to be measured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=029-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुमोदन|अनुमोदनं
अनुमोदन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Pleasing.<BR>	 2. Assent, acceptance.<BR>	 3. Sympathetic joy.<BR>E. अनु with, मोदन rejoicing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=029-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुमोदित|अनुमोदितं
अनुमोदित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Pleased, delighted.<BR>	 2. Agreeable, accept-<BR>able.<BR> E. अनु, and मोदित pleased.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=029-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुयात
अनुयात mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Followed, pursued.<BR>	 2. Practised.<BR> E. अनु after,<BR>यात gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=029-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुयायित्व
अनुयायित्व n. (-त्वं)<BR>	 1. Succession.<BR>	 2. Subsequence.<BR> E. अनुयायिन्, and त्व<BR>added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=029-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुयायिन्
अनुयायिन् mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि)<BR>	 1. Following, consequent upon.<BR>	 2. A<BR>follower, a dependent or attendant.<BR> E. अनु, and यायिन् who<BR>goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=029-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुयुक्त|अनुयुक्तः
अनुयुक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>	 1. Asked, inquired.<BR>	 2. Reprehended, censured.<BR>E. अनु, and युक्त joined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=029-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुयोक्तृ
अनुयोक्तृ m. (-क्ता) A hired teacher.<BR> E. अनु, and योक्तृ who joins.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=029-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुयोग|अनुयोगः
अनुयोग m. (-गः)<BR>	 1. A question.<BR>	 2. Asking, solicitation.<BR>	 3. Censure, re-<BR>proof.<BR>	 4. Religious meditation, spiritual union.<BR> E. अनु with, and<BR>योग union.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=029-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुयोगकृत्
अनुयोगकृत् m. (-कृत्) An Ācārya or spiritual teacher.<BR> E. अनुयोग, and कृत्<BR>who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=029-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुयोगिन्
अनुयोगिन् mfn. (-गी-गिनी-गि)<BR>	 1. Reproving, or a reprover.<BR>	 2. What<BR>combines or unites.<BR>	 3. Connected or combined with, situated in or<BR>on.<BR> E. अनुयोग, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=029-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुयोजन|अनुयोजनं
अनुयोजन n. (-नं) A question. E. See अनुयोग; the affix being ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=029-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुयोज्य|अनुयोज्यं|अनुयोज्यः
अनुयोज्य mfn. (-ज्यः-ज्या-ज्यं) Bad, censurable.<BR> E. अनु, and योज्य to be joined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=029-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुरक्त|अनुरक्तः
अनुरक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>	 1. Fond of, attached to, liking, esteeming,<BR>loving.<BR>	 2. Pleased.<BR> E. अनु, and रक्त affected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=029-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुरक्ति|अनुरक्तिः
अनुरक्ति f. (-क्तिः) Affection, love.<BR> E. अनु, and रक्ति affection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=029-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुरञ्जक|अनुरंजक
अनुरञ्जक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Gratifying, pleasing.<BR> E. अनु, and रञ्जक what<BR>pleases.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=029-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुरञ्जन|अनुरंजनं|अनुरञ्जनं
अनुरञ्जन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Loving, being attached to.<BR>	 2. Pleasing, giving delight<BR>to.<BR> E. अनु, and रञ्जन delighting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=029-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुरञ्जित|अनुरंजित
अनुरञ्जित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Pleased, delighted.<BR>	 2. Inspired with<BR>affection.<BR> E. अनु, and रञ्जित pleased.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=029-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुरत|अनुरतः
अनुरत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Fond of, attached to.<BR>	 2. Beloved.<BR> E. अनु and<BR>रत attached.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=029-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुरति|अनुरतिः
अनुरति f. (-तिः) Love, regard, esteem, attachment.<BR> E. अनु with, रम to<BR>play, and क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=029-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुरस|अनुरसः
अनुरस m. (-सः)<BR>	 1. (In poetry) a subordinate feeling or passion.<BR>	 2. (In<BR>medicine) a secondary flavour, as a little sweetness in a sour<BR>fruit, &c.<BR> E. अनु and रस flavour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=029-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुराग|अनुरागः
अनुराग m. (-गः) Attachment, love.<BR> E. अनु with, and रञ्ज to stain or<BR>colour, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=029-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुरागवत्|अनुरागवन्त्
अनुरागवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Loving, affectionate, in love with. E.<BR>अनुराग, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=029-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुरागिणी
अनुरागिणी f. (-णी) One of the personifications of musical notes.<BR> E. अनु<BR>subsequent, रागिणी a musical mode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=029-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुरागिन्
अनुरागिन् mfn. (-गी-गिणी-गि) Passion, impassioned, loving, in love. E.<BR>अनुराग, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=029-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुराधा
अनुराधा f. (-धा) The seventeenth Nakshatra or lunar mansion,<BR>designated by a row of oblation; (stars in Libra.)<BR> E. अनु, and राध<BR>to accomplish, अन् affix, and टाप् for the fem.; an auspicious sign<BR>for any thing to be undertaken in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=029-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुरुद्ध
अनुरुद्ध mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>	 1. Soothed, pacified.<BR>	 2. Checked, opposed.<BR> E. अनु<BR>and रुद्ध opposed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=029-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुरूप|अनुरूपः
अनुरूप mfn. (-पः-पा-पं)<BR>	 1. Like, resembling.<BR>	 2. Fit, suitable.<BR>	 3. According<BR>to.<BR>	 n. (-पं)<BR>	 1. Conformity.<BR>	 2. Assistance 3. Mediation, friendly<BR>interposition.<BR>	 4. Hindrance, check.<BR> E. अनु like, and रूप form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=029-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुरूपचेष्ट
अनुरूपचेष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं) Endeavouring to act becomingly.<BR> E. अनुरूप,<BR>and चेष्टा effort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=029-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुरोध|अनुरोधः
अनुरोध m. (-धः) The accomplishing of a desired object for another<BR>person, obligingness, service.<BR> E. अनु, and रुध to confine, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=029-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुरोधक
अनुरोधक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Complying with, complaisant.<BR> E. अनु before,<BR>रुध with, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=029-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुरोधिन्
अनुरोधिन् mfn. (-धी-धिनी-धि)<BR>	 1. Compliant, complaisant.<BR>	 2. Adverse. E.<BR>अनुरोध obliging, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=029-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुलाप|अनुलापः
अनुलाप m. (-पः) Tautology, repetition.<BR> E. अनु, and लप to speak, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=029-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुलिप्त
अनुलिप्त mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं) Smeared, anointed.<BR> E. अनु, and लिप्त smeared.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=029-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुलेप|अनुलेपः
अनुलेप m. (-पः) Unction, anointing.<BR> E. अनु, and लेप anointing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=029-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुलेपक
अनुलेपक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Anointing, who or what anoints.<BR> E. अनु, and<BR>लेपक who anoints.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=029-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुलेपन|अनुलेपनं
अनुलेपन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Anointing the body with unguents.<BR>	 2. Unguent so<BR>used.<BR>	 3. Oily or emollient application<BR> E. अनु, and लेपन anointing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=029-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुलेपिन्
अनुलेपिन् mfn. (-पी-पिनी-पि) Anointing the body with unguents. E.<BR>अनुलेप, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=029-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुलोम|अनुलोमः
अनुलोम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं) Regular, successive, with the hair or grain. E.<BR>अनु, and लोमन् hair of the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=029-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुलोमज|अनुलोमजः
अनुलोमज mfn. (-जः-जा-जं) Produced or born in due gradation; applied<BR>especially to the mixed tribes; as the offspring of a Brahman<BR>man and Kṣatriya woman, a Kṣatriya man and Vaiśya woman,<BR>and so on. See प्रतिलोमज.<BR> E. अनुलोमन्, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=029-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुलोमन|अनुलोमनं
अनुलोमन n. (-नं) (In medicine) Following the natural course or direc-<BR>tion.<BR> E. अनुलोम used as a nominal verb, and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=029-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुवचन|अनुवचनं
अनुवचन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Concordance, conformity to or concurrence with a<BR>previous text or authority.<BR>	 2. Subsidiary or similar doctrine.<BR> E. अनु,<BR>and वचन speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=029-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुवत्सर|अनुवत्सरं|अनुवत्सरः
अनुवत्सर m. (-रः) A year.<BR> E. अनु, and वत्सर a year.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=029-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुवर्त्तन|अनुवर्तन|अनुवर्तनं|अनुवर्त्तनं
अनुवर्त्तन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Obliging or serving another.<BR>	 2. Consequence, result.<BR>E. अनु, and वर्त्तन profession.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=029-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुवाक|अनुवाकः
अनुवाक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A chapter of the Vedas, a subdivision or section.<BR>2. A compilation from the Ṛc, or Yajur Vedas.<BR> E. अनु, वच to<BR>speak, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=029-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुवाक्या
अनुवाक्या f. (-क्या) A prayer or formula from the Vedas,<BR> E. अनु, and वाक्या<BR>a formula.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=029-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुवाद|अनुवादः
अनुवाद m. (-दः)<BR>	 1. Abuse, reviling.<BR>	 2. Tautology, repetition.<BR>	 3. Confor-<BR>mity to what has been previously said or explained.<BR> E. अनु low, or<BR>after, and वाद from वद् to speak, with घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=029-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुवादक
अनुवादक mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>	 1. Consenting to, replying.<BR>	 2. Conformable to,<BR>concurrent, corroborative.<BR> E. अनु, and वादक what says.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=029-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुवादत्व
अनुवादत्व n. (-त्वं) Consent, conformity, concurrence.<BR> E. त्व or ता added<BR>to अनुवाद; also अनुवादता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=029-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुवादिन्
अनुवादिन् mfn. (-दी-दिनी-दि) Consenting to, concurring with, conform-<BR>able to.<BR> E. अनुवाद and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=029-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुवाद्य
अनुवाद्य mfn. (-द्यः-द्या-द्यं) To be conformable or correspondent to.<BR>	 n. (-द्यं)<BR>The subject of a predicate.<BR> E. अनु before वद् to speak, ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=029-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुवारम्
अनुवारम् ind. Repeatedly.<BR> E. अनु, and वार time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=029-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुवास|अनुवासः
अनुवास m. (-सः)<BR>	 1. Scenting, perfuming.<BR>	 2. An oily enema.<BR> E. अनु and<BR>वास to perfume, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=029-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुवासन|अनुवासनं
अनुवासन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Affection, attachment.<BR>	 2. Perfuming the clothes,<BR>especially dipping the ends of the cloth in perfumes.<BR>	 3. Perfuming,<BR>scenting in general.<BR>	 4. An oily enema.<BR>	 5. Administering oily<BR>enemata.<BR> E. अनु after, वास to fumigate, and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=029-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुवासित
अनुवासित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Scented, perfumed.<BR>	 2. Fumigated.<BR>	 3.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=030-a" target="_blank">Page030-a+ 60</a>]<BR>Prepared or administered as an enema.<BR> E. अनु before, वास to<BR>fumigate, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=029-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुवास्य
अनुवास्य mfn. (-स्यः-स्या-स्यं)<BR>	 1. To be scented or fumigated.<BR>	 2. Requiring<BR>an enema.<BR> E. अनु before, वास and य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=030-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुविद्ध
अनुविद्ध mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>	 1. Variegated, ornamented.<BR>	 2. Obstructed,<BR>checked.<BR>	 3. Full of, abounding in.<BR>	 4. Set (as a jewel.)<BR> E. अनु, and<BR>विद्ध penetrated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=030-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुविधायिन्
अनुविधायिन् mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि) Conformable, compliant, obedient, atten-<BR>tive to.<BR> E. अनु and विधायिन् observing rules.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=030-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुवृत्ति|अनुवृत्तिः
अनुवृत्ति f. (-त्तिः)<BR>	 1. Complaisance, obliging or serving another. See<BR>अनुरोध.<BR>	 2. A subsequent or supplementary rule, completing what a<BR>preceding one has left to be explained.<BR>	 3. Imitating, doing or<BR>acting in like manner.<BR> E. अनु before, वृत् to serve, and क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=030-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुवेल्लित
अनुवेल्लित n. (-तं) Bandaging, securing with bandages, &c. (in surgery.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=030-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुव्रजन|अनुव्रजनं
अनुव्रजन n. (-नं) Complimentary attendance on a departing guest, fol-<BR>lowing him to a given distance; also अनुव्रज्या.<BR> E. अनु after and व्रजन<BR>or व्रज्या going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=030-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुशय|अनुशयः
अनुशय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. Repentance, regret.<BR>	 2. Ancient enmity.<BR>	 3. Hatred,<BR>resentment.<BR>	 4. Attachment to or pursuance of any object.<BR>	 f. (-यी)<BR>1. A disease of the feet, a boil or abscess on the upper part.<BR>	 2. A<BR>pimple on the head.<BR> E. अनु, शीङ् to sleep, and अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=030-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुशयितव्य
अनुशयितव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं) To be repented or regretted.<BR> E. अनु before<BR>शीङ् and तव्य affix; also अनुशयनीय, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=030-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुशयिन्
अनुशयिन् mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि)<BR>	 1. Devotedly attached to, faithful, adorn-<BR>ing.<BR>	 2. Repentant, penitent, sorry for.<BR> E. अनुशय, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=030-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुशर|अनुशरः
अनुशर m. (-रः) A Rākshasa, a sort of demon.<BR> E. अनु repeatedly, शृ to<BR>injure, and अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=030-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुशस्त्र|अनुशस्त्रं
अनुशस्त्र n. (-स्त्रं) A supplementary or subsidiary weapon or instrument.<BR>E. अनु, and शस्त्र a weapon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=030-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुशासक
अनुशासक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Ruling or one who governs or directs.<BR> E. अनु<BR>and शासक what governs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=030-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुशासन|अनुशासनं
अनुशासन n. (-नं) Command, order, precept, law.<BR> E. अनु, and शासन ruling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=030-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुशासित
अनुशासित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Directed, governed.<BR> E. अनु and शासित governed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=030-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुशासितृ
अनुशासितृ (-ता-त्री-तृ) Ruling, governing, commanding, directing, a ruler,<BR>&c.<BR> E. अनु and शासितृ who rules.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=030-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुशास्ति|अनुशास्तिः
अनुशास्ति f. (-स्तिः) Order, command, precept.<BR> E. अनु, and शास्ति order.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=030-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुशास्तृ
अनुशास्तृ m. (-स्ता) A governor, director, teacher.<BR> E. अनु, and शास्तृ who<BR>directs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=030-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुशीलन|अनुशीलनं
अनुशीलन n. (-नं) Repeated and devoted service.<BR> E. अनु according to,<BR>शीलन behaving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=030-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुशिष्ट
अनुशिष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>	 1. Taught, revealed.<BR>	 2. Done conformably to<BR>law, &c.<BR>	 3. Nearly completed.<BR> E. अनु according to, शिष्ट taught.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=030-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुशुचिका
अनुशुचिका f. (-का) Any ceremony enjoined by the Vedas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=030-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुशोक|अनुशोकः
अनुशोक m. (-कः) Sorrow, repentance, regret.<BR> E. अनु after, शोक sorrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=030-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुशोचक
अनुशोचक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Grieving, one who repents.<BR> E. अनु, and शोचक<BR>who sorrows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=030-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुशोचन|अनुशोचनं
अनुशोचन n. (-नं) Sorrow, repentance.<BR> E. अनु before, शुच to grieve, and<BR>ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=030-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुशोचित
अनुशोचित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Regretted, repented of.<BR> E. अनु before, शुच to<BR>sorrow, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=030-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुषङ्ग|अनुषंग|अनुषंगः|अनुषङ्गः
अनुषङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>	 1. Tenderness, compassion.<BR>	 2. Conjunction, coalition,<BR>connexion of word with word, or effects with causes.<BR>	 3. Necessary<BR>consequence, the connexion of a subsequent with a previous act.<BR>E. अनु, and षञ्ज to embrace, with घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=030-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुषङ्गिक|अनुषंगिक
अनुषङ्गिक mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>	 1. Consequent, following as a necessary<BR>result.<BR>	 2. Connected with, adhering to, inherent, concomitant. E.<BR>अनुषङ्ग, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=030-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुषङ्गिन्|अनुषंगिन्
अनुषङ्गिन् mfn. (-ङ्गी-ङ्गिनी-ङ्गि)<BR>	 1. Addicted or attached to.<BR>	 2. Embrac-<BR>ing.<BR>	 3. Connected with.<BR>	 4. Common, prevailing.<BR> E. अनुषङ्ग, and<BR>इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=030-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुषञ्जन|अनुषंजनं
अनुषञ्जन n. (-नं) Connection with what follows; concord.<BR> E. नुअ before,<BR>षञ्ज to embrace, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=030-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुषिक्त
अनुषिक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं) Rewatered or sprinkled.<BR> E. अनु, and षिक्त<BR>sprinkled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=030-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुषेचन
अनुषेचन n. (-नं) Watering or sprinkling over again.<BR> E. अनु, and षिच to<BR>sprinkle, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=030-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुष्टुभ्
अनुष्टुभ् f. (-ष्टुप्)<BR>	 1. A measure of verse, the stanza consisting four lines<BR>of eight syllables each, or three lines of eight, twelve, and twelve,<BR>making, in either case, thirty-two.<BR>	 2. A name of SARASWATI. E.<BR>अनु, and ष्टुभ् to stop, क्विप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=030-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुष्ण|अनुष्णं|अनुष्णः
अनुष्ण mfn. (-ष्णः-ष्णा-ष्णं)<BR>	 1. Lazy, sluggish.<BR>	 2. Cold, chilly.<BR> E. अन् neg.<BR>and उष्ण warm, alert.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=030-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुष्ठातव्य
अनुष्ठातव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं) To be done or accomplished.<BR> E. अनु according<BR>to, स्था to stay or be, तव्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=030-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुष्ठातृ
अनुष्ठातृ m. (-ता) The undertaker of any work.<BR> E. अनु before, स्था to stay,<BR>तृन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=030-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुष्ठान|अनुष्ठानं
अनुष्ठान n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Commencement or course of proceeding.<BR>	 2. Fixing<BR>or establishing, proof.<BR>	 3. Propriety, fitness.<BR>	 4. Doing or engaging<BR>in any thing.<BR> E. अनु according to, स्था to stay, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=030-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुष्ठित
अनुष्ठित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Effected, accomplished.<BR>	 2. Done, practised.<BR>	 3.<BR>Followed, observed.<BR>	 4. Appointed.<BR> E. अनु before स्था to stay, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=030-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुष्ठेय
अनुष्ठेय mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>	 1. To be proved or established, demonstrable.<BR>2. To be effected or accomplished.<BR> E. अनु before स्था to stay,<BR>य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=030-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुसन्धान|अनुसंधान|अनुसंधानं|अनुसन्धानं
अनुसन्धान n. (-नं) Inquiry, investigation, searching.<BR> E. अनु, and सम्<BR>before धा to have, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=030-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुसन्धानिन्|अनुसंधानिन्
अनुसन्धानिन् mfn. (-नी-निनी-नि) Investigating, searching; so अनुसन्धायिन्<BR>E. अनुसन्धान and इनि affix, or अनु and सम् before धा, and णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=030-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुसन्धेय|अनुसंधेय
अनुसन्धेय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Investigable, worthy of inquiry or scrutiny. E.<BR>अनु, and सम् before धा to have, य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=030-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुसरण|अनुसरणं
अनुसरण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Custom, habit, usage.<BR>	 2. Conformity to, conse-<BR>quence of.<BR>	 3. Following, going after.<BR> E. अनु before सृ to go, ल्युट्<BR>aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=030-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुसार|अनुसारः
अनुसार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Custom, usage.<BR>	 2. Nature, natural state or condition<BR>of any thing.<BR>	 3. Prevalence, currency.<BR>	 4. Received or established<BR>authority, especially of codes of law.<BR>	 5. Conformity to usage, &c.<BR>6. Consequence, result.<BR> E. अनु according to, सृ to go, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=030-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुसारिन्
अनुसारिन् mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>	 1. Following.<BR>	 2. According with or to. E.<BR>अनुसार, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=030-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुसूचक
अनुसूचक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Indicative of, pointing out.<BR> E. अनु before षूच<BR>to point out, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=030-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुस्मृति|अनुस्मृतिः
अनुस्मृति f. (-तिः) Cherished recollection, recalling some idea to the<BR>exclusion of all others.<BR> E. अनु before स्पृति memory. Also अनुस्मरणं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=030-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुस्वार|अनुस्वारः
अनुस्वार m. (-रः) The nasal letter (M) or dot above the line. E.<BR>अनु before, स्वर to sound, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=030-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुहार|अनुहारः
अनुहार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Imitation.<BR>	 2. Resemblance.<BR> E. अनु like, हृञ् to convey,<BR>and घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=030-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुहार्य्य|अनुहार्य|अनुहार्यः
अनुहार्य्य m. (-र्य्यः) Monthly obsequies.<BR> E. अनु before हृ to take, ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=030-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनूक|अनूकं|अनूकः
अनूक m. (-कः) A former state of existence.<BR>	 n. (-कं)<BR>	 1. Race, family.<BR>	 2.<BR>Disposition, temperament.<BR> E. अनु, उच to associate, and क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=030-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनूचान|अनूचानः
अनूचान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Well-behaved.<BR>	 m. (-नः) A learned Brahman;<BR>one versed in the Vedas and Vedāṇgas.<BR> E. अनू, and वच to speak;<BR>the form is irregular.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=030-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनूच्च
अनूच्च mfn. (-च्चः-च्छा-च्चं) Short, low.<BR> E. अन् neg. उच्च tall, high.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=030-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनूढ|अनूढः
अनूढ mfn. (-ढः-ढा-ढं) Unmarried.<BR> E. अन् neg. ऊढ married.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=030-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनूदित
अनूदित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Unuttered.<BR> E. अन् before ऊदित said.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=030-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनूद्य|अनूद्यं
अनूद्य mfn. (-द्यः-द्या-द्यं)<BR>	 1. Not to be addressed or spoken to.<BR>	 2. To be<BR>spoken to afterwards or in reply to.<BR>	 m. (-द्यः) A spiritual teacher,<BR>&c.<BR> E. अ before वद् to speak, यत् affix, form irregular, it is improper<BR>to address a Guru, &c. by name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=030-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनून|अनूनं
अनून mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>	 1. Whole, entire.<BR>	 2. Not less, not inferior. E.<BR>अन् neg. ऊन to diminish, and अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=031-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनूनक|अनूनकं
अनूनक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) See the preceding.<BR> E. कन् affixed to अनून.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=031-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनूप|अनूपं|अनूपः
अनूप mfn. (-पः-पा-पं) Watery, wet.<BR>	 m. (-पः) A buffalo.<BR> E. अनु near or<BR>with, and आप् water; ऊ is substituted for आ, and अच् is added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=031-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनूपज|अनूपजं
अनूपज n. (-जं) Ginger.<BR> E. अनूप, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=031-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनूरु|अनूरुः
अनूरु mfn. (-रुः-रुः-रु) Thighless.<BR>	 m. (-रुः) The charioteer of the sun,<BR>the dawn.<BR> E. अन् priv. and ऊरु a thigh; being represented with-<BR>out legs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=031-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनूरुसारथि|अनूरुसारथिः
अनूरुसारथि m. (-थिः) The sun.<BR> E. अनूरु, and सारथि a charioteer, whose<BR>coachman is ANŪRU.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=031-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनृजु|अनृजुः
अनृजु mfn. (-जुः-जुः-जु) Wicked, perverse, crooked, not straight, physi-<BR>cally or morally.<BR> E. अन् neg. ऋजु straight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=031-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनृण
अनृण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Free from debt.<BR> E. अन् neg. ऋण debt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=031-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनृणिन्
अनृणिन् mfn. (-णी-णिनी-णि) Unindebted, free from debt.<BR> E. अन् neg.<BR>ऋणिन् a debtor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=031-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनृत|अनृतं
अनृत n. (-तं)<BR>	 1. Falsehood.<BR>	 2. Agriculture.<BR> E. अन् neg. ऋत truth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=031-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनृतवादिन्
अनृतवादिन् mfn. (-दी-दिनी-दि) Speaking falsely, lying, a liar.<BR> E. अनृत,<BR>and वादिन् who speaks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=031-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनेक|अनेकं
अनेक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Many, much, not one.<BR> E. अन् neg. एक one.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=031-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनेककाल
अनेककाल adv.<BR>	 n. (-लं) A long time.<BR> E. अनेक, and काल time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=031-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनेकज|अनेकजः
अनेकज m. (-जः) A bird, born more than once; or in the shell, and<BR>upon being hatched.<BR> E. अनेक more than one, and ज what is born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=031-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनेकता
अनेकता f. (-ता) Muchness, manifold condition; also अनेकत्व.<BR> E. अनेक,<BR>and ता or त्व aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=031-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनेकाकार
अनेकाकार mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Multiform.<BR> E. अनेक and आकार form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=031-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनेकप|अनेकपः
अनेकप mf. (-पः-पा) An elephant.<BR> E. अनेक various, from अन् neg. एक<BR>one, and प from पा who drinks, who drinks with his trunk, and<BR>with his mouth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=031-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनेकरूप|अनेकरूपः
अनेकरूप mfn. (-पः-पा-पं)<BR>	 1. Multiform.<BR>	 2. Of various kinds or sorts.<BR>	 3.<BR>Fickle, of variable mind.<BR> E. अनेक, and रूप form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=031-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनेकविध
अनेकविध mfn. (-धः-धा-धं) Various, of many kinds, in different ways. E.<BR>अनेक, and विध sort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=031-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनेकश|अनेकशः
अनेकश ind. By large numbers or quantities.<BR> E. अनेक, and शसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=031-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनेकधा
अनेकधा ind. In various ways.<BR> E. अनेक and धाच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=031-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनेडमूक|अनेडमूकः
अनेडमूक mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>	 1. Deaf and dumb.<BR>	 2. Wicked, fraudulent. E.<BR>अन् here implying similarity, एड deaf, and मूक dumb. See एडमूक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=031-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनेनस्
अनेनस् mfn. (-नाः-नाः-नः) Blameless, sinless.<BR> E. अन् neg. एनस् fault.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=031-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनेव
अनेव ind. Otherwise, or.<BR> E. अन् neg. एव so.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=031-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनेहस्
अनेहस् m. (-हाः) Time.<BR> E. अन् neg. हन to kill or hurt, एहच् substitude,<BR>and असि Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=031-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनैक्य|अनैक्यं
अनैक्य n. (क्यं)<BR>	 1. Plurality, the existence of many.<BR>	 2. Want of union,<BR>anarchy.<BR> E. अनेक, and घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=031-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनैकान्त|अनैकांत
अनैकान्त mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं)<BR>	 1. Variable, unsteady.<BR>	 2. (In logic) Oc-<BR>casional, as a cause not invariably attended by the same effects. E.<BR>अनेक, अन्त end, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=031-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनैकान्तिक|अनैकांतिक
अनैकान्तिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Unsteady, variable, having many objects or<BR>purposes.<BR> E. अनेक, अन्त end, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=031-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनो
अनो ind. No, not; also नो.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=031-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनोकह|अनोकहः
अनोकह m. (-हः) A tree.<BR> E. अनस् a cart, उक going, and ह what injures;<BR>from हन with ड aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=031-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनोदित
अनोदित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Unquestioned, unaddressed, not spoken to.<BR> E. अन्<BR>neg. ओदित spoken to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=031-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तःकरण|अन्तःकरणं
अन्तःकरण n. (-णं) The internal and spiritual part of man, the seat of<BR>thought and feeling, the mind, the heart, the conscience, the soul.<BR>E. अन्तर् within, and करण an organ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=031-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तःपुर|अन्तःपुरं
अन्तःपुर n. (-रं)<BR>	 1. The female apartment.<BR>	 2. A queen.<BR>	 3. A palace. E.<BR>अन्तर् inner, and पुर a house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=031-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तःप्रकृति|अन्तःप्रकृतिः
अन्तःप्रकृति f. (-तिः) The heart, the soul, the internal nature or constitu-<BR>tion of man.<BR> E. अन्तर्, and प्रकृति nature.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=031-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तःप्रज्ञ
अन्तःप्रज्ञ mfn. (-ज्ञः-ज्ञा-ज्ञं) Acquainted with the heart, knowing one's<BR>self.<BR> E. अन्तर् and प्रज्ञा knowlege.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=031-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तःशरीर
अन्तःशरीर n. (-रं) The internal and spiritual part of man, the con-<BR>science, the soul.<BR> E. अन्तर् within, शरीर the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=031-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तःशल्य
अन्तःशल्य mfn. (-ल्यः-ल्या-ल्यं) Having some extraneous body, (a wound,<BR>&c.)<BR> E. अन्तर्, and शल्य a thorn, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=031-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तःसंज्ञा
अन्तःसंज्ञा f. (-ज्ञा) Internal consciousness.<BR> E. अन्तर्, and संज्ञा sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=031-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तःसत्त्वा
अन्तःसत्त्वा f. (-त्त्वा)<BR>	 1. A pregnant woman.<BR>	 2. Marking nut, (Semecarpus<BR>anacardium.)<BR> E. अन्तर् inner, and सत्त्वा having life or being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=031-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तःस्वेद|अन्तःस्वेदः
अन्तःस्वेद m. (-दः) An elephant.<BR> E. अन्तर् inner and स्वेद warmth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=031-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्त|अंत|अन्तं|अन्तः
अन्त mn. (-न्तः-न्तं)<BR>	 1. End, term.<BR>	 2. Final, ultimate, (continuing M. N.<BR>even with a fem. noun.)<BR>	 mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं)<BR>	 1. Near.<BR>	 2. Handsome.<BR>m. (-न्त)<BR>	 1. Death.<BR>	 2. A boundary, a limit.<BR>	 3. Certainty, ascertain-<BR>ment.<BR>	 4. A limb, a member.<BR>	 n. (-न्तं) Nature, diposition.<BR> E. अम to<BR>go, and तन् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=031-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तक|अंतक|अन्तकः
अन्तक m. (-कः) A name of YAMA.<BR> E. अन्त death, and क affix of agency.<BR>YAMA is the king or angel of death.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=031-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तकर
अन्तकर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Causing death, mortal, destructive.<BR> E. अन्त, and कर<BR>what makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=031-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तकाल|अन्तकालः
अन्तकाल m. (-लः) Time of death, death.<BR> E. अन्त end, and काल<BR>time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=031-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तग|अन्तगः
अन्तग mfn. (-गः-गा-गं)<BR>	 1. Dead, departed.<BR>	 2. Traversing, crossing, going<BR>to the end.<BR> E. अन्त, and ग who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=031-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्ततस्
अन्ततस् ind.<BR>	 1. From the end, from the term.<BR>	 2. Similarly, like.<BR>	 3. In<BR>part.<BR>	 4. Lastly, finally.<BR> E. अन्त, and तस् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=031-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्|अंतर्
अन्तर् ind. Within, between, amongst.<BR>	 2. To the end.<BR>	 3. Certainly,<BR>very well, a particle of assent.<BR> E. अन्त end, रा to receive, and<BR>क्विप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=031-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर|अंतर|अन्तरं
अन्तर (noun and adverb)<BR>	 n. (-रं)<BR>	 1. Interval, intermediate space.<BR>	 2.<BR>period, term.<BR>	 3. Clothing.<BR>	 4. Covering.<BR>	 5. Difference.<BR>	 6. Snake,<BR>behalf.<BR>	 7. A hole or rent.<BR>	 8. Own, the self.<BR>	 9. Without, except.<BR>	 10.<BR>Without, outside.<BR>	 11. Opportune time.<BR>	 12. Midst, the midst.<BR>	 13.<BR>The supreme soul.<BR>	 14. Like, similar.<BR>	 15. Other.<BR>	 16. (In arithmetic)<BR>Remainder, difference.<BR> E. अन्त end, and र from रा to obtain, and क<BR>aff. In consulting the meanings of the word, it is to be recollected,<BR>that vocables which are adverbs in English, are often nouns of the<BR>neuter gender in Sanskrit; this word is also a pronoun, in the 3d<BR>and 10th acceptations, when the latter means, without, or out<BR>of, any thing but a house or town: the whole of the interpretations<BR>may be referred to the ideas of, within and without.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=031-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तरङ्ग|अन्तरंग|अन्तरङ्गः
अन्तरङ्ग mfn. (-ङ्गः-ङ्गा-ङ्गं)<BR>	 1. Own, belonging to.<BR>	 2. Internal, interior.<BR>	 3.<BR>Of kin.<BR> E. अन्तर, and ग what goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=031-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तरतम|अंतरतम|अन्तरतमः
अन्तरतम mfn. (-मः-मा-मत्)<BR>	 1. Immediate, intimate, internal.<BR>	 2. Like,<BR>analogous.<BR>	 m. (-मः) A congenial letter, one of the same class. E.<BR>अन्तर inner, and डतम aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=031-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तरज्ञ
अन्तरज्ञ mfn. (-ज्ञः-ज्ञा-ज्ञं) Prudent, provident, foreseeing.<BR> E. अन्तर midst,<BR>and ज्ञ who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=031-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तरप्रभव|अन्तरप्रभवः
अन्तरप्रभव mfn. (-वः-वा-वं) Of mixed origin or caste.<BR> E. अन्तर different,<BR>प्रभव birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=031-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तरस्थ
अन्तरस्थ mfn. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थं)<BR>	 1. Internal, inward.<BR>	 2. Seperate, apart. E.<BR>अन्तर, and स्थ what stays.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=031-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तरा|अंतरा
अन्तरा ind.<BR>	 1. Without, except.<BR>	 2. In the middle, among, amidst.<BR>	 3.<BR>Near at hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=031-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तरात्मन्
अन्तरात्मन् m. (-त्मा)<BR>	 1. The soul, the inherent spirit.<BR>	 2. The internal<BR>feelings, the heart or mind.<BR> E. अन्तर्, and आत्मन् soul.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=031-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तरापत्या
अन्तरापत्या f. (-त्या) A pregnant woman.<BR> E. अन्तर, and अपत्य offspring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=031-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तराय|अंतरायः|अन्तरायः
अन्तराय m. (-यः) Obstacle, impediment.<BR> E. अन्तर between, इण to go,<BR>and घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=031-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तराल|अंतरालं|अन्तरालं
अन्तराल mn. (-लः-लं) Included space: also अन्तरालक.<BR> E. अन्तरा in the<BR>midst, ला to obtain, and क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=031-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तरिक्ष|अंतरिक्षं|अन्तरिक्षं
अन्तरिक्ष n. (-क्षं) The sky or atmosphere.<BR> E. अन्तर् within, and ऋक्ष a star;<BR>in which are the stars: or ईक्ष to see; seen by the world; the<BR>word is properly written with the long vowel, as अन्तरीक्ष, but the<BR>short is substituted in poetry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=032-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तरित|अंतरित|अन्तरितं
अन्तरित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Dead, departed, concealed, lost.<BR>	 2. Separated,<BR>detached.<BR>	 n. (-तं) Remainder, (in arithmetic.)<BR> E. अन्तर्, and इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=032-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तरीक्ष|अंतरीक्षं|अन्तरीक्षं
अन्तरीक्ष n. (-क्षं)<BR>	 1. Sky, heaven.<BR>	 2. Talc. E. See अन्तरिक्ष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=032-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तरीप|अन्तरीपं|अंतरीपः|अन्तरीपः
अन्तरीप mn. (-पः-पं) An island.<BR> E. अन्तर् in the midst of, and आप water;<BR>आ changed to ई.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=032-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तरीय|अंतरीयं|अन्तरीयं
अन्तरीय n. (-यं) A lower garment.<BR> E. अन्तर् inner, छ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=032-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तरे|अंतरे
अन्तरे ind. Amidst, among, between.<BR> E. अन्तर् with इण् to go, and<BR>विच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=032-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तरेण|अंतरेण
अन्तरेण ind.<BR>	 1. Except, without.<BR>	 2. Amidst, between.<BR> E. अन्तर्, इण् to<BR>go, and न aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=032-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्गडु
अन्तर्गडु mfn. (-डुः-डुः-डुं) Unprofitable, vain, idle.<BR> E. अन्तर् amidst, गडु to<BR>drop or distil, and उ affix: what runs to waste.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=032-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्गत|अंतर्गत|अन्तर्गतं
अन्तर्गत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Forgotten.<BR>	 2. Intermediate, interposed.<BR>	 3.<BR>Inner, internal, within.<BR> E. अन्तर् within, and गत gone, part. past<BR>of गम.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=032-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्गृह|अन्तर्गृहं
अन्तर्गृह n. (-हं) An inner apartment.<BR> E. अन्तर् within, and गृह a house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=032-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्जठर|अन्तर्जठरं
अन्तर्जठर n. (-रं) The stomach.<BR> E. अन्तर्, and जठर the belly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=032-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्ज्वलन|अन्तर्ज्वलनः
अन्तर्ज्वलन n. (-नं) Internal heat, inflammation.<BR> E. अन्तर्, and ज्वलन<BR>burning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=032-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्जात
अन्तर्जात mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Inborn, inbred, innate.<BR> E. अन्तर्, and जात born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=032-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्दहन
अन्तर्दहन n. (-नं) The distillation of spirituous liquor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=032-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्दाह|अन्तर्दाहः
अन्तर्दाह m. (-हः) Internal heat, or fever.<BR> E. अन्तर्, and दाह burning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=032-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्दुष्ट
अन्तर्दुष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं) Internally bad, wicked, vile.<BR> E. अन्तर्, and<BR>दुष्ट bad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=032-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्द्वार|अन्तर्द्वारं
अन्तर्द्वार n. (-रं) A private door within the house.<BR> E. अन्तर् inner, and द्वार<BR>a door.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=032-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्द्धा
अन्तर्द्धा f. (-र्द्धा) Disappearance, concealment, covering.<BR> E. अन्तर् within, धा<BR>to have or hold, क and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=032-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्द्धान
अन्तर्द्धान n. (-नं) Concealment, disappearance. E. As before, with ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=032-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्द्धिः|अन्तर्धि|अंतर्धिः|अन्तर्धिः
अन्तर्द्धिः f. (-र्द्धिः) See the preceding. E. as before, with कि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=032-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्ध्यान
अन्तर्ध्यान n. (-नं) Profound inward meditation.<BR> E. अन्तर्, and ध्यान meditation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=032-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्भव|अंतर्भव
अन्तर्भव mfn. (-वः-वा-वं) Inward, internal, generated internally.<BR> E. अन्तर्,<BR>and भव being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=032-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्भाव|अंतर्भावः|अन्तर्भावः
अन्तर्भाव m. (-वः) Internal or inherent nature or disposition.<BR> E. अन्तर्,<BR>and भाव disposition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=032-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्भावना|अंतर्भावना
अन्तर्भावना f. (-ना) Inward meditation or anxiety.<BR> E. अन्तर्, and भावना<BR>meditation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=032-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्भूत|अंतर्भूत|अन्तर्भूतः
अन्तर्भूत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Internal, inner, being within.<BR> E. अन्तर्, and भूत<BR>been.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=032-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्मनस्
अन्तर्मनस् mfn. (-नाः-नाः-नः) Sad, perplexed.<BR> E. अन्तर्, and मनस् the mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=032-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्यमन
अन्तर्यमन n. (-नं) Inward restraint, mental control.<BR> E. अन्तर्, and यमन<BR>restraining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=032-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्यामिन्
अन्तर्यामिन् mfn. (-मी-मिनी-मि)<BR>	 1. Checking or regulating the internal<BR>feelings.<BR>	 2. Heart-searching or pervading.<BR>	 m. (-मी)<BR>	 1. The soul.<BR>	 2.<BR>Providence, the Supreme spirit, as regulating and guiding man-<BR>kind.<BR>	 3. Conscience.<BR> E. अन्तर् within, and यामिन् who stops or<BR>refrains.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=032-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्लम्ब|अन्तर्लम्बः
अन्तर्लम्ब m. (-म्बः) An acute angular triangle.<BR> E. अन्तर् within, and लम्ब<BR>the perpendicular.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=032-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्वंशिक|अन्तर्वंशिकः
अन्तर्वंशिक m. (-कः) Superintendent of the women's apartments.<BR> E. अन्तर्<BR>within, वंश a race, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=032-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्वत्नी|अन्तर्व्वत्नी
अन्तर्वत्नी f. (-त्नी) A pregnant woman.<BR> E. अन्तर् within, मतुप् possessive<BR>affix, with an irregular formation of the fem. In the Vedas अन्तर्व्वती<BR>occurs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=032-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्वमि|अन्तर्वमिः|अन्तर्व्वमिः
अन्तर्वमि m. (-मिः) Flatulence, indigestion.<BR> E. अन्तर् inner, and वमि vo-<BR>miting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=032-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्वर्त्तिन्|अन्तर्वर्तिन्
अन्तर्वर्त्तिन् mfn. (-र्त्ती-र्त्तिनी-र्त्ति) Internal, included.<BR> E. अन्तर्, and वर्त्तिन् what<BR>abides.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=032-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्व्वाणि|अन्तर्वाणि|अन्तर्व्वाणिः
अन्तर्व्वाणि mfn. (-णिः-णिः-णि) Skilled in sacred sciences.<BR> E. अन्तर् inner,<BR>and वाणि speech: containing the essence of all knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=032-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्वासस्
अन्तर्वासस् n. (-सः) An inner garment.<BR> E. अन्तर् and वासस् clothes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=032-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्विगाहन|अन्तर्व्विगाहनं
अन्तर्विगाहन n. (-नं) Entrance, entering.<BR> E. अन्तर् within, and वि before,<BR>गाह to agitate, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=032-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्वेग|अन्तर्वेगः
अन्तर्वेग m. (-गः)<BR>	 1. Internal uneasiness or anxiety.<BR>	 2. Inward fever. E.<BR>अन्तर्, and वेग agitation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=032-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्वेदी|अन्तर्व्वेदी
अन्तर्वेदी f. (-दी) The name of a country.<BR> E. अन्तर् between, and वेदी level<BR>earth. The Doab or district between the Ganga and Yamuna rivers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=032-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्वेश्मन्
अन्तर्वेश्मन् n. (-श्म) The inner apartments, the interior of a building.<BR>E. अन्तर्, and वेश्मन् a house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=032-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्हास|अन्तर्हासः
अन्तर्हास mfn. (-सः-सा-सं) Laughing inwardly.<BR>	 m. (-सः) Self-satisfaction,<BR>conceit.<BR> E. अन्तर् inner, and हास laughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=032-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्हित|अंतर्हित|अन्तर्हितं
अन्तर्हित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Concealed, covered, hidden, disappeared.<BR> E. अन्तर्<BR>within, and धा to hold with क्त affix; हि substituted for धा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=032-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तवत्|अंतवत्|अन्तवन्त्
अन्तवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Finite, having a term or end.<BR> E. अन्त and<BR>मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=032-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तवासिन्
अन्तवासिन् m. (-सी) A pupil. See अन्तेवासिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=032-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तशय्या
अन्तशय्या f. (-य्या)<BR>	 1. Death.<BR>	 2. A bed or mat on the ground.<BR>	 3. The<BR>place for burial or burning.<BR> E. अन्त end, and शय्या a sleeping place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=032-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तावसायिन्
अन्तावसायिन् m. (-यी)<BR>	 1. A barber.<BR>	 2. A man of a low tribe or caste,<BR>the offspring of a Niṣādi woman by a Caṇḍāla, whose business<BR>is to attend in places where dead bodies are burned.<BR>	 3. The name<BR>of a saint.<BR> E. अन्त the end, अव and षो to cut, who pares the nails,<BR>&c. or षै to decay, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=032-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्ति|अंति|अन्तिः
अन्ति f. (-न्तिः) An elder sister, (in theatrical language.) ind. Near.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=032-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तिक|अंतिक|अन्तिकं|अन्तिकः
अन्तिक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Near, proximate.<BR>	 f. (-का)<BR>	 1. An elder sister,<BR>(in theatrical language.) See अत्तिका.<BR>	 2. A fireplace. See अन्दिका.<BR>	 3.<BR>A plant, (Echites scholaris.) See सप्तला.<BR>	 n. (-कं) Vicinity.<BR> E. अन्त<BR>the end, and कन् affix, इ inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=032-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तिकतम|अन्तिकतमः
अन्तिकतम mfn. (-मः-मा-मत्) Very near.<BR> E. अन्तिक, and डतम superlative aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=032-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तिकता
अन्तिकता f. (-ता) Nearness, vicinity, contiguity: also अन्तिकत्वं.<BR> E. अन्तिक<BR>with, ता or त्व aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=032-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तिकाश्रय|अन्तिकाश्रयः
अन्तिकाश्रय m. (-यः) Contiguous support, (as that given by a tree to a<BR>creeper, &c.)<BR> E. अन्तिक, and आश्रय support.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=032-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तिम|अंतिम|अन्तिमः
अन्तिम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>	 1. Final, ultimate, last.<BR>	 2. Very near.<BR> E. अन्त,<BR>and डिमच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=032-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तेवासिन्
अन्तेवासिन् m. (-सी)<BR>	 1. A pupil.<BR>	 2. A Caṇḍāla, or man of a low caste.<BR>mfn. (-सी-सिनी-सि) Final, ultimate.<BR> E. अन्त in the locative case, near<BR>or final; वस to abide, and णिनि affix: who dwells near his teacher,<BR>&c. See अन्तवासिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=032-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्त्य|अंत्य|अन्त्यं|अन्त्यः
अन्त्य mfn. (-न्त्यः-न्त्या-न्त्यं)<BR>	 1. Last, ultimate.<BR>	 2. Inferior, low.<BR>	 m. (-न्त्यः)<BR>	 1. A<BR>man of low caste.<BR>	 2. A fragrant grass, (Cyperus rotundus.) See<BR>मुस्त.<BR>	 n. (-न्त्यं) A measure of number, two Sāgaras, a very large<BR>number.<BR> E. अन्त, and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=032-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्त्यकर्म्मन्|अन्त्यकर्मन्
अन्त्यकर्म्मन् n. (-र्म्म) Funeral rites.<BR> E. अन्त्य and कर्म्मन् act; also अन्त्यक्रिया, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=032-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्त्यज|अन्त्यजः
अन्त्यज mfn. (-जः-जा-जं) Younger, latest born.<BR>	 m. (-जः)<BR>	 1. A Śūdra or<BR>man of the fourth tribe.<BR>	 2. A man of one of seven inferior<BR>tribes; a washerman, currier, mimic, Varuḍa, fisherman, Meda<BR>or attendant on women, and mountaineer or forester.<BR> E. अन्त्य in-<BR>ferior, and ज who is born: born from the feet of BRAHMĀ; also<BR>अन्त्यजात.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=032-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्त्यजन्मन्
अन्त्यजन्मन् mf. (-न्मा) A man or woman of Śūdra or fourth tribe, &c.,<BR>see the last.<BR> E. अन्त्य, and जन्मन् birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=032-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्त्यजातीय
अन्त्यजातीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Sprung from the last or lowest class.<BR> E. अन्त्य<BR>last, जाति class, affix छ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=032-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्त्यभ|अन्त्यभं
अन्त्यभ n. (-भं)<BR>	 1. The sign Pisces.<BR>	 2. The asterism Revatī.<BR>	 2. The last<BR>star or constellation.<BR> E. अन्त्य last, and भ a constellation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=032-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्त्यवर्ण|अन्त्यवर्णः|अन्त्यवर्ण्ण
अन्त्यवर्ण mf. (-र्णः-र्णा) A man or woman of the fourth tribe.<BR> E. अन्त्य, and<BR>वर्ण a tribe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=033-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्त्यावसायिन्
अन्त्यावसायिन् mf. (-यी-यिनी) A man or woman of low caste, especially one<BR>of seven classes: a Caṇḍāla, a Śvapaca or executioner, a Kṣattā<BR>or insect hunter, a charioteer, a bard, and a Vaideha or attendant<BR>on women.<BR>	 2. A man or a woman of a particular caste living by<BR>the chase. See अन्तावसायिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=033-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्त्येष्टि|अन्त्येष्टिः
अन्त्येष्टि f. (-ष्टिः) A funeral sacrifice.<BR> E. अन्त्य, and इष्टि sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=033-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्त्येष्टिक्रिया
अन्त्येष्टिक्रिया f. (-या) Obsequies.<BR> E. अन्त्येष्टि, and क्रिया rite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=033-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्त्र|अंत्रं|अन्त्रं
अन्त्र n. (-न्त्रं) An entrail.<BR> E. अम to be sick, and त्र Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=033-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्त्रकूज|अन्त्रकूजः
अन्त्रकूज m. (-जः) Grumbling of the bowels, borborygmi.<BR> E. अन्त्र, and कूज<BR>murmuring: also अन्त्रकूजनं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=033-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्त्रवृद्धि|अन्त्रवृद्धिः
अन्त्रवृद्धि f. (-द्धिः) Inguinal hernia, rupture.<BR> E. अन्त्य, and वृद्धि increase.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=033-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्त्राद|अन्त्रादः
अन्त्राद m. (-दः) A worm, ascarides, &c.<BR> E. अन्त्र, and अद what eats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=033-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्दिका|अंदिका
अन्दिका f. (-का) A fireplace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=033-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्दु|अंदुः|अन्दुः
अन्दु f. (-न्दुः) See अन्दू.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=033-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्दुक|अन्दुकः
अन्दुक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A ring or chain worn on the ancle.<BR>	 2. The chain for<BR>an elephant's feet.<BR> E. अदि to bind, कु affix, and कन् final.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=033-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्दू
अन्दू f. (-न्दूः)<BR>	 1. An ornament worn round the ancles.<BR>	 2. The chain for<BR>an elephant's feet.<BR>	 3. A chain, a fetter, a bond or tie.<BR> E. अदि<BR>to bind, and कू Unādi aff. or with कु affix अन्दु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=033-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्दूक|अन्दूकः
अन्दूक m. (-कः) The chain for an elephant's feet. See the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=033-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्दोल
अन्दोल (-त) r. 10th cl. (अन्दोलयति) To agitate, to swing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=033-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्ध|अंध|अन्धं|अन्धः
अन्ध (-त) r. 10th cl. (अन्धयति) To be or become blind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=033-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्ध|अंध|अन्धं|अन्धः
अन्ध mfn. (-न्धः-न्धा-न्धं) Blind.<BR>	 n. (-न्धं)<BR>	 1. Darkness.<BR>	 2. Water.<BR> E. अन्ध to be<BR>blind, and अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=033-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्धक|अंधक|अन्धकः
अन्धक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Blind.<BR>	 m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. The name of a country,<BR>apparently Behar.<BR>	 2. The name of a king.<BR>	 3. Of a Muni.<BR>	 4. Of an<BR>Asura.<BR> E. अन्ध to be blind, and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=033-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्धकरिपु|अन्धकरिपुः
अन्धकरिपु m. (-पुः)<BR>	 1. A name of ŚIVA, the enemy of the demon ANDHAKA.<BR>E. अन्धक a demon so named, and रिपु and enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=033-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्धकार|अन्धकारः
अन्धकार mn. (-रः-रं) Darkness.<BR> E. अन्ध blind, and कार what makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=033-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्धकासुहृद्
अन्धकासुहृद् m. (-द्) A name of ŚIVA.<BR> E. अन्धक, and असुहृद् the enemy.<BR>See अन्धकरिपु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=033-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्धकूप|अन्धकूपः
अन्धकूप m. (-पः) A blind well.<BR> E. अन्ध, and कूप a well: one of which the<BR>mouth is hidden.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=033-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्धतमस|अन्धतमसं
अन्धतमस n. (-सं) Great darkness.<BR> E. अन्ध to make blind, and तमस dark-<BR>ness: also written अन्धतामसं, अ being made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=033-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्धता
अन्धता f. (-ता) Blindness. Also n. अन्धत्वं.<BR> E. ता or त्व added to अन्ध.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=033-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्धतामिश्र|अन्धतामिश्रः
अन्धतामिश्र n. (-श्रं)<BR>	 1. A division of Tartarus, the second of the twenty-one hells.<BR>2. The doctrine of annihilation after death.<BR> E. अन्ध blind,<BR>great, and तामिश्र darkness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=033-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्धमूषा
अन्धमूषा f. (-षा) A small covered crucible, with a hole in the side. E.<BR>अन्ध, and मूषा a crucible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=033-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्धमूषिका
अन्धमूषिका f. (-का) The name of a grass. See देवताड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=033-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्धस्|अंधस्
अन्धस् n. (-न्धः) Boiled rice.<BR> E. अद to eat, नम् inserted, and असुन् Unādi<BR>affix, द changed to ध.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=033-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्धालजी
अन्धालजी f. (-जी) A blind boil, one that does not suppurate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=033-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्धाहि|अन्धाहिः
अन्धाहि mf. (-हिः-हिः) A kind of fish, vulg. kūñciyā; a species of eel?<BR>E. अन्ध blind, and अहि a snake: from its form and the smallness of<BR>its eyes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=033-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्धिका|अंधिका
अन्धिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. Night.<BR>	 2. Gambling.<BR>	 3. A small kind of mustard. See<BR>सर्षप.<BR>	 4. A woman.<BR>	 5. A disease of the eye.<BR> E. अन्ध dark or blind,<BR>and कन् affix in the fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=033-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्धीकृत
अन्धीकृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Made or become blind.<BR> E. अन्ध, and कृत made, च्वि<BR>augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=033-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्धीभूत
अन्धीभूत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Become blind.<BR> E. अन्ध, and भूत become, च्वि<BR>augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=033-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्धु|अंधुः|अन्धुः
अन्धु m. (-न्धुः) A Well.<BR> E. अम to go, and तुक् Unādi affix; ध is substituted<BR>for त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=033-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्धुल|अंधुलः|अन्धुलः
अन्धुल m. (-लः) A tree, (Mimosa sirisa, Rox.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=033-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्ध्र|अंध्र|अंध्रः|अन्ध्रः
अन्ध्र m. (-न्ध्रः) A hunter, one who lives by killing game; a man of low<BR>caste, the offspring of a Vaideha father and Kārāvara mother; not<BR>allowed to reside within a village or town.<BR>	 2. A country, modern<BR>Telingana; also आन्ध्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=033-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्न|अन्नं|अन्नः
अन्न mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं) Eaten.<BR>	 n. (-न्नं)<BR>	 1. Boiled rice.<BR>	 2. Food in general.<BR>3. Corn.<BR> E. अद to eat, and क्त affix of the part. past, त becoming न.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=033-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्नकाल|अन्नकालः
अन्नकाल m. (-लः) Meal time, proper hour for eating.<BR> E. अन्न, and काल<BR>time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=033-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्नकोष्ठ
अन्नकोष्ठ m. (-ष्ठः) A cupboard, a granary.<BR> E. अन्न, and कोष्ठ or receptacle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=033-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्नकोष्ठक|अन्नकोष्ठकः
अन्नकोष्ठक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. VIṢṆU.<BR>	 2. The sun.<BR>	 m. (-कः) A granary, a cupboard.<BR>E. अन्न food, कोष्ठक a repository.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=033-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्नगन्धि|अन्नगन्धिः
अन्नगन्धि m. (-न्धिः) Dysentery, diarrhœa.<BR> E. अन्न food, गन्ध smell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=033-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्नज
अन्नज mfn. (-जः-जा-जं) Springing from or occasioned by food.<BR> E. अन्न, and<BR>ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=033-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्नजल
अन्नजल n. (-लं) Support, subsistence.<BR> E. अन्न, and जल water, meat and<BR>drink.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=033-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्नद
अन्नद mfn. (-दः-दा-दं) One who gives food.<BR>	 f. (-दा) A goddess, a form of<BR>DURGĀ.<BR> E. अन्न, and द who gives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=033-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्नदातृ
अन्नदातृ m. (-ता) One who gives food, a charitable man.<BR> E. अन्न, and दातृ<BR>donor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=033-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्नदान
अन्नदान n. (-नं) The giving of rice or food, the maintenance of a person.<BR>E. अन्न, and दान giving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=033-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्नद्वेष|अन्नद्वेषः
अन्नद्वेष m. (-षः) Want of appetite, dislike of food.<BR> E. अन्न, and द्वेष dislike.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=033-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्नपरिवर्त्त|अन्नपरिवर्त
अन्नपरिवर्त्त m. (-र्त्तः) Change of diet.<BR> E. अन्न, and परिवर्त्त revolution.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=033-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्नपूर्णा|अन्नपूर्ण्णा
अन्नपूर्णा f. (-र्णा) A goddess, a form of DURGĀ.<BR> E. अन्न, and पूर्ण who fills<BR>with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=033-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्नपूर्व्वा|अन्नपूर्वा
अन्नपूर्व्वा f. (-र्व्वा) A goddess, a form of DURGĀ.<BR> E. अन्न, and पूर्व्व prior.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=033-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्नप्राशन|अन्नप्राशनं
अन्नप्राशन n. (-नं) A religious ceremony, in which after presenting obla-<BR>tions to fire, a little rice is, for the first time, put into the child's<BR>mouth; it should take place between the fifth and eighth month. E.<BR>अन्न, and प्राशन feeding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=033-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्नब्रह्मन्
अन्नब्रह्मन् n. (-ह्म) The deification of food, considering it in the light of<BR>BRAHMĀ, as the pervader and supporter of existence.<BR> E. अन्न, and<BR>ब्रह्म the Supreme.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=033-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्नभूमि
अन्नभूमि f. (-मिः) A large collection of food.<BR> E. अन्न, and भूमि a heap.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=033-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्नमय
अन्नमय mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>	 1. Composed of food, containing food.<BR>	 2. Derived<BR>or made from food.<BR>	 m. (-यः) The body.<BR> E. अन्न and मयट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=033-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्नमयकोष|अन्नमयकोषः
अन्नमयकोष m. (-षः) The gross material body, that which is sustained by<BR>food.<BR> E. अन्नमय, and कोष sheath, (of the spirit.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=033-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्नमल|अन्नमलं
अन्नमल n. (-लं) Spirituous liquor, the excrement or ferment of rice, &c.<BR>E. अन्न, and मल fœcula.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=033-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्नरस|अन्नरसः
अन्नरस m. (-सः) Chyle.<BR> E. अन्न, and रस juice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=033-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्नलिप्सा
अन्नलिप्सा f. (-प्सा) Hunger, craving.<BR> E. अन्न, and लिप्सा desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=033-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्नवाहिस्रोतस्
अन्नवाहिस्रोतस् n. (-तः) The œsophagus.<BR> E. अन्न, and वाहि what conveys,<BR>स्रोतस् canal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=033-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्नविकार|अन्नविकारः
अन्नविकार m. (-रः) The seminal secretion<BR> E. अन्न, and विकार change of<BR>form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=033-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्नशेष|अन्नशेषः
अन्नशेष m. (-षः) Leavings, offal.<BR> E. अन्न, and शेष remainder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=033-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्नाद|अन्नादः
अन्नाद mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>	 1. Feeding, eating.<BR>	 2. The partaker or eater of<BR>another's food.<BR>	 m. (-दः) VIṢṆU.<BR> E. अन्न, and अद who eats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=033-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्नायिन्
अन्नायिन् mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि) Hungry; desiring food.<BR> E. अन्न nominal verb<BR>to want food, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=033-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्नाहारिन्
अन्नाहारिन् mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि) Eating, feeding.<BR> E. अन्न, and आहारिन् who<BR>eats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=033-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्य|अन्यः
अन्य mfn. (-न्यः-न्या-न्यत्)<BR>	 1. Other, different.<BR>	 2. Unlike.<BR> E. अन्य to live, and<BR>यक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=033-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यत्
अन्यत् ind. Otherwise. E. See the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=033-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यगामिन्
अन्यगामिन् mfn. (-मी-मिनी-मि)<BR>	 1. Adulterous.<BR>	 2. Going to another (place,<BR>&c.)<BR> E. अन्य another (husband or wife,) गामिन् who goes to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=033-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यच्च
अन्यच्च ind.<BR>	 1. Again, moreover.<BR>	 2. On the contrary<BR> E. अन्यत्, and च added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=034-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यज
अन्यज mfn. (-जः-जा-जं) Born of another (family, &c.) of a different origin.<BR>E. अन्य, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=034-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यजन्मन्
अन्यजन्मन् n. (-न्म) Another birth, being born again, the metempsychosis.<BR>E. अन्य, and जन्मन् birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=034-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यतम|अन्यतमः
अन्यतम mfn. (-मः-मा-मत्)<BR>	 1. Either, any, any one of many.<BR>	 2. Different,<BR>distinct from many.<BR> E. अन्य, and डतम aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=034-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यतर|अन्यतरः
अन्यतर mfn. (-रः-रा-रत्)<BR>	 1. Other, different.<BR>	 2. Either of two.<BR> E. अन्य other,<BR>and डतर affix; applied to words that refer to but two things.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=034-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यतरेद्युस्
अन्यतरेद्युस् ind. Either of two days.<BR> E. अन्यतर, and एद्युस् affix, derived<BR>from द्युस् a day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=034-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यतस्
अन्यतस् ind. Elsewhere.<BR> E. अन्य, and तसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=034-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यत्र
अन्यत्र ind.<BR>	 1. Elsewhere, in another place.<BR>	 2. Except, unless, without. E.<BR>अन्य, and त्रल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=034-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यथा
अन्यथा ind.<BR>	 1. Otherwise, in a different manner.<BR>	 2. Inaccurately, untruly.<BR>3. Badly.<BR> E. अन्य, and थाल् affix, referring to manner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=034-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यथाख्याति|अन्यथाख्यातिः
अन्यथाख्याति f. (-तिः) Erroneous conception of spirit.<BR> E. अन्यथा and ख्याति<BR>declaring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=034-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यथात्व
अन्यथात्व n. (-त्वं) An opposite or different state of the case.<BR> E. अन्यथा and<BR>त्व aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=034-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यथासिद्धि|अन्यथासिद्धिः
अन्यथासिद्धि f. (-द्धिः) Disproving a cause or argument, by giving it a<BR>different effect or application, coming to a different conclusion<BR>from the same premises.<BR> E. अन्यथा otherwise, and सिद्धि proving,<BR>establishing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=034-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यदा
अन्यदा ind. Another time.<BR> E. अन्य, and दा affix, referring to time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=034-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यपुष्ट|अन्यपुष्टः
अन्यपुष्ट m. (-ष्टः) The koil or Indian cuckoo, supposed to be reared by<BR>the crow.<BR> E. अन्य, and पुष्ट nourished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=034-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यपूर्व्वा|अन्यपूर्वा
अन्यपूर्व्वा f. (-र्व्वा) A girl previously promised or betrothed to one and<BR>married to another.<BR> E. अन्य, and पूर्व्व prior.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=034-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यभृत्
अन्यभृत् m. (-त्) A crow.<BR> E. अन्य another, भृत् who nourishes: the crow is<BR>supposed to sit upon the eggs of the kokila: from भृ root, and क्विप्<BR>aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=034-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यभृत|अन्यभृतः
अन्यभृत m. (-तः) The kokila or Indian cuckoo.<BR> E. अन्य, and भृत nourished,<BR>from भृ with part. affix क्त; this bird, like the English cuckoo, being<BR>supposed to leave its eggs in the nests of other birds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=034-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यमनस्
अन्यमनस् mfn. (-नाः-नाः-नः)<BR>	 1. Fickle-minded.<BR>	 2. Absent.<BR> E. अन्य, and मनस्<BR>the mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=034-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यमनस्क|अन्यमनस्कः
अन्यमनस्क mfn. (-स्कः-स्का-स्कं)<BR>	 1. Absent, thinking of something else.<BR>	 2.<BR>Fickle, versatile.<BR> E. अन्य, and मनस्क minded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=034-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यमानस
अन्यमानस mfn. (-सः-सा-सं) Fickle-minded, otherwise-minded.<BR> E. अन्य, and<BR>मानस mental.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=034-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यवर्द्धित
अन्यवर्द्धित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Brought up by a stranger, fostered.<BR> E. अन्य, and<BR>वर्द्धित part. past of वृध् to grow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=034-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यवादिन्
अन्यवादिन् mfn. (-दी-दिनी-दि) Speaking inconsistently; (in law) prevaricat-<BR>ing or a prevaricator.<BR> E. अन्य otherwise, and वादिन् who speaks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=034-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यशाख|अन्यशाखः
अन्यशाख m. (-खः) An apostable.<BR> E. अन्य another, शाखा a branch or sect,<BR>or with कन् affix अन्यशाखकः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=034-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यादृश्
अन्यादृश् mfn. (-दृक्) Of another kind, like another.<BR> E. अन्य, दृश् to see,<BR>and क्विप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=034-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यादृश|अन्यादृशः
अन्यादृश mfn. (-शः-शी-शं) See the preceding. E. As before, with खञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=034-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्याधीन
अन्याधीन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Subject to others, dependent.<BR> E. अन्य, and अधीन<BR>dependent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=034-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्याय|अन्यायः
अन्याय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. Impropriety, indecorum.<BR>	 2. Irregularity, disorder. E.<BR>अ neg. न्याय propriety.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=034-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यायिन्
अन्यायिन् mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि)<BR>	 1. Unjust, unreasonable.<BR>	 2. Indecorous.<BR>	 3.<BR>Illogical.<BR> E. अ neg. न्यायिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=034-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यायवृत्त
अन्यायवृत्त mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं) Following evil courses.<BR> E. अन्याय improper, वृत्त<BR>practising.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=034-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्याय्य|अन्याय्यः
अन्याय्य mfn. (-य्यः-य्या-य्यं) Improper, indecorous, unbecoming, unfit.<BR> E. अ<BR>neg. न्याय्य right.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=034-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यासक्त
अन्यासक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं) Absent, intent on something else.<BR> E. अन्य, and<BR>आसक्त intent on.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=034-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यून|अन्यूनः
अन्यून mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Complete, entire.<BR> E. अ neg. and न्यून defective.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=034-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्येद्युस्
अन्येद्युस् ind. Another day.<BR> E. अन्य, and एद्युम् affix, from द्युस् a day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=034-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्येद्युस्क
अन्येद्युस्क mfn. (-स्कः-स्का-स्कं) Daily, diurnal, occurring every other day.<BR>m. (-स्कः) A quotidian fever.<BR> E. अन्येद्युस् and कत् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=034-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्योत्पन्न
अन्योत्पन्न mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं) Begotten by another, the progeny of another,<BR>than the reputed parent or husband.<BR> E. अन्य, and उत्पन्न born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=034-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्योदर्य्य|अन्योदर्य|अन्योदर्यः|अन्योदर्य्यः
अन्योदर्य्य m. (-र्य्यः) A stepmother's son.<BR> E. अन्य, and उदर belly, यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=034-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्योन्य|अन्योन्यं
अन्योन्य mfn. (-न्यः-न्या-न्यं) Mutual.<BR> E. अन्य repeated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=034-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्योन्यकलह
अन्योन्यकलह m. (-हः) Mutual quarrel.<BR> E. अन्योन्य, and कलह strife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=034-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्योन्यघात
अन्योन्यघात m. (-तः) Mutual conflict, striking, wounding or killing one<BR>another.<BR> E. अन्योन्य and घात striking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=034-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्योन्यभेद|अन्योन्यभेदः
अन्योन्यभेद m. (-दः) Mutual aversion or enmity.<BR> E. अन्योन्य, and भेद<BR>difference.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=034-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्योन्यापहृत
अन्योन्यापहृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Taken or secreted from one another, taken<BR>severally.<BR> E. अन्योन्य, and अपहृत removed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=034-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्योन्याभाव|अन्योन्याभावः
अन्योन्याभाव m. (-वः) Mutual negation, relative difference.<BR> E. अन्योन्य, and<BR>अभाव nonexistence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=034-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्योन्याश्रय|अन्योन्याश्रयः
अन्योन्याश्रय m. (-यः) Mutual or reciprocal connexion or dependence. E.<BR>अन्योन्य, and आश्रय support.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=034-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वक्ष|अन्वक्षः
अन्वक्ष mfn. (-क्षः-क्षा-क्षं) Following.<BR> E. अनु after, and अक्षि the eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=034-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वञ्च्|अन्वंच्
अन्वञ्च् mfn. (-न्वङ्-नूची-न्वक्) Following.<BR> E. अनु after, अञ्च to go, and क्विन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=034-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वय|अन्वयः
अन्वय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. Race, lineage, succession.<BR>	 2. Connexion, acquaintance,<BR>intercourse.<BR>	 3. the natural order or connexion of words in a sen-<BR>tence or stanza.<BR>	 4. The logical connexion of cause and effect, or<BR>proposition and conclusion.<BR> E. अनु after, इण् to go, and अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=034-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वयज्ञ|अन्वयज्ञः
अन्वयज्ञ m. (-ज्ञः) A genealogist.<BR> E. अन्वय. and ज्ञ who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=034-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वयिन्
अन्वयिन् mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि)<BR>	 1. Following, agreeing with.<BR>	 2. Belonging to<BR>race or family.<BR> E. अन्वय and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=034-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्ववाय|अन्ववायः
अन्ववाय m. (-यः) Race, lineage.<BR> E. अनु after, अव prefixed to इण to go,<BR>and अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=034-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वष्टका
अन्वष्टका f. (-का) A Śrāddha or funeral ceremony performed on the ninth<BR>day of the month's Pauṣa, Māgha, Phālguna or Āśvina. It is<BR>the maternal Śrāddha for those who preserve the sacred fire. E.<BR>अनु after, and अष्टका the eighth day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=034-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वहम्
अन्वहम् ind. Every day, daily.<BR> E. अनु, and अहन् a day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=034-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वाचय|अन्वाचयः
अन्वाचय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Connecting, uniting.<BR> E. अनु, and आङ् before, चि<BR>to collect, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=034-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वाधि|अन्वाधिः
अन्वाधि f. (-धिः)<BR>	 1. A bail or deposit to be delivered to a third person.<BR>2. Repentance.<BR> E. अनु according to, and आधि a pledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=034-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वाधेय|अन्वाधेयं
अन्वाधेय n. (-यं) Property presented after marriage to the wife by her<BR>husband's family.<BR> E. अनु subsequently, and आधेय to be taken or<BR>received.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=034-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वायतन
अन्वायतन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Latitudinal.<BR> E. अनु, and आयतन breadth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=034-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वारोहण|अन्वारोहणं
अन्वारोहण n. (-णं) Mounting the funeral pile after or with the body of<BR>the husband.<BR> E. अनु, and आरोहण ascending.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=034-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वासन|अन्वासनं
अन्वासन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. An unctuous or cooling enema.<BR>	 2. Service.<BR>	 3. Regret,<BR>affliction.<BR>	 4. A place where work is done, manufactory, a house<BR>of industry.<BR> E. अनु before, आस् to sit, and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=034-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वाहार्य्य|अन्वाहार्य|अन्वाहार्यः|अन्वाहार्य्यं
अन्वाहार्य्य m. (-र्य्यः)<BR>	 1. The monthly Śrāddha, or funeral repast in<BR>honour of the manes, held on the day of new moon; it should be,<BR>according to Menu, of meat eaten after the presentation of a piṇḍa<BR>or ball of rice.<BR>	 2. The monthly obsequies performed during the<BR>first year after the death of a parent.<BR> E. अनु after, and आहार्य्य to<BR>be taken or eaten; from हृ with आङ् prefixed, and ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=034-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वाहार्य्यक|अन्वाहार्यक|अन्वाहार्य्यकं
अन्वाहार्य्यक n. (-कं) See the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=034-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वाहिक
अन्वाहिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Daily, diurnal.<BR> E. अन्वह daily, ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=034-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वाहित|अन्वाहितं
अन्वाहित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Deposited with a person to be delivered ulti-<BR>mately to another.<BR> E. अनु and आहित placed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=034-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वित|अन्वितः
अन्वित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Joined, connected with.<BR>	 2. Having as an<BR>essential or inherent part, possessed of, possessing.<BR>	 3. Connected<BR>as in grammar, or construction.<BR> E. अनु with, and इत gone, part.<BR>of इण्; also अन्वीत.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=035-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्विष्ट|अन्विष्टः
अन्विष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं) Sought.<BR> E. अनु after, and इष desire, with the<BR>part. affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=035-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वीत|अन्वीतः
अन्वीत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Joined, connected with. See अन्वित.<BR> E. अनु with,<BR>and ईत from ई to go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=035-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वेषण|अन्वेषणं
अन्वेषण fn. (-णा-णं)<BR>	 1. Research, investigation of duty by reasoning.<BR>2. Research, enquiry in general.<BR> E. अनु, इष to desire and ल्यु aff. and<BR>in the fem. टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=035-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वेषित|अन्वेषितः
अन्वेषित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Sought. E. The part. past of इष, with अनु prefixed,<BR>and इ inserted before क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=035-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वेषिन्
अन्वेषिन् mfn. (-षी-षिणी-षि) Seeking, inquiring after.<BR> E. अनु before, इष to<BR>wish, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=035-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वेष्टृ
अन्वेष्टृ mfn. (-ष्टा-ष्ट्री-ष्टृ) An enquirer, a searcher.<BR> E. अनु before इष, and<BR>तृच् affix of agency.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=035-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपःसान्त
अपःसान्त n. (-न्तं) The offering or performance of sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=035-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्
अप् f. pl. only, (आपः) Water.<BR> E. आप to obtain, and क्विप् Unādi affix;<BR>the vowel of the radical becomes short.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=035-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप|अपः
अप ind. A particle and preposition implying.<BR>	 1. Inferiority, (below,<BR>worse.)<BR>	 2. Privation, (from.)<BR>	 3. Separation, (away, from.)<BR>	 4. Con-<BR>trariety, (against, opposite to.)<BR>	 5. Difference, (from.)<BR>	 6. Dis-<BR>honesty.<BR>	 7. Exultation: as अपकृष्टुं to revile, अपहर्त्तुं to take away,<BR>अपकर्त्तुं to do wrong, अपवक्तुं to contradict, अपकीर्त्ति infamy, &c.<BR> E. अ<BR>neg. and प from पा to preserve.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=035-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपकरण|अपकरणं
अपकरण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Acting improperly, doing wrong.<BR>	 2. Ill-treating,<BR>offending, injuring.<BR> E. अप before, कृ to do, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=035-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपकर्तृ|अपकर्त्तृ
अपकर्तृ mfn. (-र्ता-र्त्री-र्तृ) Injurious, offensive, hostile, inimical, an enemy.<BR>E. अप before, कृ to do, तृक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=035-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपकर्म्मन्|अपकर्मन्
अपकर्म्मन् n. (-र्म्म)<BR>	 1. Evil doing, wickedness.<BR>	 2. Oppression, violence.<BR>	 3.<BR>Laziness, incompetence.<BR>	 4. Any impure or degrading act or rite. E.<BR>अप before, कर्म्मन् act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=035-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपकलङ्क|अपकलंक|अपकलंकः|अपकलङ्कः
अपकलङ्क m. (-ङ्कः) An indelible disgrace.<BR> E. अप before, कलङ्क a stain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=035-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपकर्ष|अपकर्षः
अपकर्ष m. (-र्षः)<BR>	 1. Pulling down, bringing low, lowering, depressing.<BR>	 2.<BR>Inferiority, infamy, degradation. So अपकर्षण n. (-णं)<BR> E. अप before, कृष<BR>to attack, घञ् or ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=035-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपकार|अपकारः
अपकार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Injury, offence, wrong, mischief.<BR>	 2. Wickedness.<BR>	 3.<BR>Tyranny, oppression.<BR>	 4. Hatred, enmity.<BR> E. अप ill, and कार what<BR>does.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=035-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपकारक|अपकारकः
अपकारक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Injuring, pernicious.<BR> E. अप before, कृ to do,<BR>ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=035-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपकारगिर्
अपकारगिर् f. (-गीः) Reproach and menace.<BR> E. अपकार hatred, and गिर्<BR>speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=035-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपकारिन्
अपकारिन् mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>	 1. Offensive, oppressive.<BR>	 2. Wicked, doing<BR>ill.<BR>	 3. Mischievous, malicious.<BR>	 4. Inimical.<BR> E. अपकार, and<BR>इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=035-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपकारार्थिन्
अपकारार्थिन् mfn. (-र्थी-र्थिनी-र्थि) Malicious, malevolent.<BR> E. अपकार and<BR>अर्थिन् who aims at.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=035-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपकीर्त्ति|अपकीर्ति|अपकीर्तिः
अपकीर्त्ति f. (-र्त्तिः) Infamy, disgrace.<BR> E. अप before, कीर्त्ति fame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=035-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपकृत
अपकृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Done wrong, maliciously, offensively, or<BR>wickedly committed.<BR>	 2. Who does wrong.<BR>	 3. Ill-treated.<BR>	 4. Ob-<BR>served or practised as a degrading or impure act, as servile<BR>duties, funeral rites, &c.<BR> E. अप before, कृ to do, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=035-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपकृति|अपकृतिः
अपकृति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Oppression, wrong, injury.<BR>	 2. Enmity, opposition.<BR>3. Any degrading or impure act or rite.<BR> E. अप before, कृ to do,<BR>क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=035-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपकृष्ट|अपकृष्टं|अपकृष्टः
अपकृष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>	 1. Low, vile, inferior.<BR>	 2. Perplexed, distressed.<BR>3. Depressed, lowered, brought down. E. part. past of कृष्, with अप<BR>prefixed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=035-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपकृष्टता
अपकृष्टता f. (-ता) Inferiorty, vileness. So अपकृष्टत्व n. (-त्वं)<BR> E. तल् or त्व<BR>added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=035-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपक्ति|अपक्तिः
अपक्ति f. (-क्तिः)<BR>	 1. Immaturity.<BR>	 2. Indigestion.<BR> E. अ neg. पक्ति ripeness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=035-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपक्व|अपक्वः
अपक्व mfn. (-क्वः-क्वा-क्वं) Unripe, immature.<BR> E. अ neg. पक्व ripe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=035-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपक्वता
अपक्वता f. (-ता) Immaturity.<BR> E. अपक्व, and तल् affix: also with त्व, अपक्वत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=035-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपक्रम|अपक्रमः
अपक्रम m. (-मः)<BR>	 1. Flight, retreat.<BR>	 2. Passing off or away.<BR> E. अप from,<BR>and क्रम to go, with अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=035-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपक्रमण|अपक्रमणं
अपक्रमण n. (-णं) Retiring, passing off or away.<BR> E. अप before, क्रम to go,<BR>ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=035-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपक्रिया
अपक्रिया f. (-या)<BR>	 1. Oppression, offence.<BR>	 2. Evil doing, wickedness.<BR>	 3.<BR>Any impure act or rite.<BR> E. अप, and क्रिया action.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=035-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपक्रोश|अपक्रोशः
अपक्रोश m. (-शः) Reviling, abusing.<BR> E. अप against, क्रुश to call out, and<BR>घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=035-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपक्ष
अपक्ष mfn. (-क्षः-क्षा-क्षं) Adverse, opposed to, not of the same side or<BR>party.<BR> E. अ neg. पक्ष a party.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=035-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपक्षता
अपक्षता f. (-ता) Opposition, hostility.<BR> E. अपक्ष, and तल् affix: or with त्व<BR>affix अपक्षत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=035-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपगत|अपगतः
अपगत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Dead, deceased.<BR>	 2. Gone, departed, remote,<BR>gone off.<BR> E. अप away, and गत gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=035-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपगम|अपगमः
अपगम m. (-मः) Departure, separation, death.<BR> E. अप, and गम to go,<BR>affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=035-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपगा
अपगा f. (-गा) A river.<BR> E. अप down, below, or अप् water, and thence the<BR>sea; and गा what goes downward or into the sea; also आपगा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=035-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपघन|अपघनः
अपघन m. (-नः) A limb or member.<BR> E. अप, and घन from हन् to kill or<BR>hurt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=035-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपघात|अपघातः
अपघात m. (-तः) Striking or cutting off, killing.<BR> E. अप, and घात striking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=035-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपघातिन्
अपघातिन् mfn. (-ती-तिनी-ति) Murderous, killing.<BR> E. अपघात, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=035-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपचय|अपचयः
अपचय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. Loss, privation.<BR>	 2. Respect, obeisance.<BR> E. अप opposite<BR>to, and चय from चि to collect, with अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=035-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपचायित|अपचायितः
अपचायित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Saluted, reverenced.<BR> E. अप here implying<BR>much or highly; and चायित part. past of चाय to reverence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=035-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपचार|अपचारः
अपचार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Impropriety, defect, wickedness.<BR>	 2. Observing<BR>unwholesome or improper regimen.<BR> E. अप before, चर to go, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=035-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपचारिन्
अपचारिन् mfn. (-रि-रिणी-रि) Wicked, bad, one who acts wickedly. E.<BR>अपचार, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=035-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपचित|अपचितः
अपचित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Saluted, honoured.<BR>	 2. Diminished, expended,<BR>wasted.<BR> E. अप before, चाय to reverence, or चि to collect, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=035-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपचिति|अपचितिः
अपचिति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Loss.<BR>	 2. Expense.<BR>	 3. Annihilation.<BR>	 4. Worship,<BR>reverence.<BR> E. अप before चाय or चि, and क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=035-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपची
अपची f. (-ची)<BR>	 1. Enlargement of the glands of the neck, &c.<BR>	 2. Any<BR>indolent tumor.<BR> E. अ neg. पच to ripen, आङ् and ङीप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=035-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपचीयमान
अपचीयमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Wasting, perishing, departing.<BR> E. अप before,<BR>चि to collect, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=035-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपचेतृ
अपचेतृ m. (-ता) A spendthrift.<BR> E. अप, चि to collect, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=035-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपच्छाय|अपच्छायः
अपच्छाय mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>	 1. Shadowless, having no shadow, as a deity or<BR>celestial being.<BR>	 2. Having a bad or unlucky shadow.<BR>	 f. (-या) An<BR>unlucky shadow, a phantom.<BR> E. अप priv. छाया shadow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=035-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपञ्चीकृत|अपंचीकृत|अपंचीकृतं|अपञ्चीकृतं
अपञ्चीकृत n. (-तं) Simple elementary substance, not compounded of the<BR>five gross elements.<BR> E. अ neg. पञ्च five, कृत made, च्वि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=035-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपटान्तर|अपटांतर|अपटान्तरं
अपटान्तर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Adjoining, contiguous.<BR> E. अ neg. पट a screen, and<BR>अन्तर between.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=035-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपटी
अपटी f. (-टी) A screen or wall of cloth, especially the kenāt or screen<BR>surrounding a tent.<BR> E. अ priv. and पट to go, with fem. termination<BR>ङीप्; preventing admission.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=035-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपटीक्षेप|अपटीक्षेपः
अपटीक्षेप m. (-पः) Precipitate entrance on the stage, indicating hurry<BR>and agitation; also read अपटाक्षेप.<BR> E. अपटी curtain, and क्षेप tossing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=035-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपटु|अपटुः
अपटु mfn. (-टुः-टुः-ट्वी-टु)<BR>	 1. Sick, diseased.<BR>	 2. Awkward, not clever,<BR>uncouth.<BR>	 3. Ineloquent.<BR> E. अ neg. पटु clever.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=035-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपटुकरण
अपटुकरण n. (-णं) A defect in any of the senses.<BR> E. अपटु, and करण doing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=035-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपण्डित|अपंडित
अपण्डित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Unlearned, ignorant.<BR> E. अ neg. पण्डित learned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=035-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपतन्त्रक|अपतंत्रकः|अपतन्त्रकः
अपतन्त्रक m. (-कः) Spasmodic contraction of the body, emprosthotonos.<BR>E. अप away, तन्त्र will, कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=036-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपतर्पण|अपतर्पणं
अपतर्पण n. (-णं) Fasting, (in sickness.)<BR> E. अप bad, and तर्पण satisfaction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=036-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपतानक|अपतानकः
अपतानक m. (-कः) Spasmodic contraction: see the last.<BR> E. अप down, तन<BR>to spread, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=036-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपत्य|अपत्यं
अपत्य n. (-त्यं) Offspring, male or female.<BR> E. अ neg. पत to fall, and यत्<BR>affix; the family being upheld by them.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=036-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपत्यदा
अपत्यदा f. (-दा) A midwife.<BR> E. अपत्य offspring, and दा fem. deriv. who<BR>gives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=036-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपत्यपथ|अपत्यपथः
अपत्यपथ m. (-थः) The vulva.<BR> E. अपत्य, and पथ the road.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=036-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपत्यविक्रयिन्
अपत्यविक्रयिन् m. (-यी) A father who receives a gratuity from his son-in-law,<BR>a seller of his offspring.<BR> E. अपत्य, and विक्रयिन् who sells.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=036-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपत्यशत्रु|अपत्यशत्रुः
अपत्यशत्रु m. (-त्रुः) A crab.<BR> E. अपत्य offspring, and शत्रु an enemy. The crab<BR>being said to perish on producing young.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=036-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपत्रप|अपत्रपः
अपत्रप mfn. (-पः-पा-पं)<BR>	 1. Bashful, modest.<BR>	 2. Immodest.<BR>	 f. (-पा)<BR>	 1. Bashful-<BR>ness.<BR>	 2. Want of shame, immodesty.<BR> E. अप, and त्रपा shame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=036-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपत्रपिष्णु|अपत्रपिष्णुः
अपत्रपिष्णु mfn. (-ष्णुः-ष्णुः-ष्णु) Bashful.<BR> E. अप before, त्रप to be ashamed,<BR>and इष्णुच्र् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=036-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपथ|अपथं|अपथः
अपथ n. (-थं) The absence of a road.<BR> E. अ priv. and पथ for पथिन् a road.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=036-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपथिन्
अपथिन् m. (-न्था) See the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=036-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपथ्य|अपथ्यं
अपथ्य mfn. (-थ्यः-थ्या-थ्यं)<BR>	 1. Unsuitable, inconsistent.<BR>	 2. (In medicine)<BR>Contraindicated, unfit as food or drink in particular complaints.<BR>E. अ neg. पथ्य suitable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=036-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपद|अपदः
अपद mfn. (-द-दा or -दी-दं)<BR>	 1. Footless, having no feet.<BR>	 2. Having no<BR>place, no station. adv.<BR>	 n. (-दं) Unseasonably, inopportunely.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-दः) A reptile.<BR> E. अ neg. पद a foot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=036-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपदान|अपदानं
अपदान n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Approved occupation.<BR>	 2. Work well or completely<BR>done.<BR> E. अप before, दा to give, and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=036-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपदानक|अपदानकं
अपदानक n. (-कं) See the above.<BR> E. कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=036-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपदान्तर|अपदान्तरः
अपदान्तर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Adjoining, contiguous.<BR>	 n. (-रं) Proximity, close,<BR>contiguity.<BR> E. अ neg. पद a foot, and अन्तर between.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=036-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपदार्थ|अपदार्थः
अपदार्थ m. (-र्थः) Nonentity.<BR> E. अ neg. पदार्थ a thing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=036-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपदिश|अपदिशं
अपदिश n. or ind. (-शं) Intermediate space, half of a point of the com-<BR>pass.<BR> E. अप, and दिश to show, क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=036-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपदिश्य
अपदिश्य ind.<BR>	 1. Dispersing, going or having gone to various quarters.<BR>2. Having shown or stated.<BR> E. अप before, दिश to show, य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=036-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपदेवता
अपदेवता f. (-ता) An evil spirit, a goblin.<BR> E. अप, and देवता a deity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=036-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपदेश|अपदेशः
अपदेश m. (-शः)<BR>	 1. Evasion, prevarication.<BR>	 2. Disguise by dress, &c.<BR>	 3.<BR>Place, quarter.<BR>	 4. A butt or mark.<BR>	 5. Cause.<BR>	 6. Fame, reputation.<BR>7. A contrivance, a pretence, a pretext.<BR> E. अप ill, badly, &c. and<BR>दिश to show. with घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=036-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपद्रव्य|अपद्रव्यं
अपद्रव्य n. (-व्यं)<BR>	 1. An impurity, any bad thing.<BR>	 2. Alloy, adulteration.<BR>E. अप, and द्रव्य thing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=036-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपध्वंस|अपध्वंसः
अपध्वंस m. (-सः) Degradation, disgrace.<BR> E. अप, and ध्वंस loss.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=036-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपध्वंसज|अपध्वंसजः
अपध्वंसज m. (-जः) A man of a mixed or impure caste.<BR> E. अपध्वंस and ज<BR>born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=036-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपध्वस्त|अपध्वस्तः
अपध्वस्त mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं)<BR>	 1. Cursed, reviled.<BR>	 2. Abandoned.<BR>	 3. Pounded.<BR>E. अप implying contempt, &c. part. past of ध्वस to go, also अवध्वस्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=036-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपध्यान|अपध्यानं
अपध्यान n. (-नं) Evil thoughts, wickedness.<BR> E. अप, and ध्यान meditation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=036-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपनयन|अपनयनं
अपनयन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Taking away, withdrawing, removing.<BR>	 2. Destroying.<BR>3. Dying.<BR>	 4. Acquittance of a debt or obligation.<BR> E. अप from, णी to<BR>take, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=036-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपनीत
अपनीत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Taken away, removed.<BR>	 2. Paid, discharged. E.<BR>अप from, णी to take, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=036-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपनीय
अपनीय ind.<BR>	 1. Having taken away.<BR>	 2. Having discharged.<BR> E. अप before,<BR>णी to take, य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=036-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपनुत्ति|अपनुत्तिः
अपनुत्ति f. (-त्तिः) Removing, taking or sending away.<BR> E. अप, नुद to send,<BR>क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=036-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपनोद|अपनोदः
अपनोद m. (-दः) Removing, taking away.<BR> E. अप, and नुद to send,<BR>affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=036-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपनोदन|अपनोदनं
अपनोदन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Removing, destroying.<BR>	 2. Expiating.<BR> E. अप before,<BR>नुद to send, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=036-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपपात्र
अपपात्र mfn. (-त्रः-त्रा-त्रं) Of low caste, using separate vessels.<BR>	 n. (त्रं) A<BR>separate vessel, one from which no one else will eat.<BR> E. अप apart,<BR>पात्र a vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=036-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपपात्रित|अपपात्रितः
अपपात्रित m. (-तः) A person who has lost caste, one with whom his<BR>kindred will not eat or drink, from a common pātra or vessel. E.<BR>अपपात्र, and इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=036-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपभी
अपभी mfn. (-भीः-भीः-भि) Fearless, undaunted.<BR> E. अप away, भी fear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=036-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपभ्रंश|अपभ्रंशः
अपभ्रंश m. (-शः) Ungrammatical language.<BR> E. अप from, भ्रंश to fall, and<BR>अच् affix; also अपभ्रंस.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=036-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपम|अपमः
अपम m. (-मः) Declination, (in astronomy.)<BR> E. अप, मा to measure, ड aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=036-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपमान|अपमानं|अपमानः
अपमान n. (-नं) Disrespect, disgrace.<BR> E. अप reverse, and मन to respect,<BR>affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=036-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपमानित
अपमानित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Disrespect, disgraced.<BR> E. अपमान disgrace,<BR>इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=036-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपमान्य
अपमान्य mfn. (-न्यः-न्या-न्यं) Disreputable, dishonourable.<BR> E. अप before,<BR>मन to mind, ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=036-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपमित
अपमित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Neglect in dress or person, unadorned.<BR>	 2.<BR>Disrespected, disgraced.<BR> E. अप before, मा to measure, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=036-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपमित्यक|अपमित्यकं
अपमित्यक n. (-कं) Debt.<BR> E. अप from, मि to throw, and त्यकन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=036-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपमृत्यु|अपमृत्युः
अपमृत्यु m. (-त्युः) Sudden death, dying of some casualty, not of<BR>sickness or decay.<BR> E. अप, मृत्यु death.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=036-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपयशस्
अपयशस् n. (-शः) Disgrace, infamy.<BR> E. अप before, यशस् fame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=036-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपयशस्कर
अपयशस्कर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Disgraceful, occasioning infamy.<BR> E. अपयशस्<BR>and कर what makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=036-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपयान|अपयानं
अपयान n. (-नं) Retreat, flight.<BR> E. अप from, and यान going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=036-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपर|अपरं|अपरः
अपर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>	 1. Other.<BR>	 2. Opposite, contrary.<BR>	 3. Posterior, (in<BR>place or time.)<BR>	 4. Similar, same.<BR>	 5. Friendly, not adverse.<BR>	 n.<BR>(-रं) The hind quarter of an elephant.<BR>	 f. (-रा)<BR>	 1. The womb.<BR>	 2. Sup-<BR>pressed menstruation in pregnancy.<BR>	 3. The west.<BR> E. अ neg.<BR>and पर from पृ to nourish or fill, and अच् affix; or अ neg. and<BR>पर other.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=036-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरञ्च
अपरञ्च ind. Again, moreover.<BR> E. च the particle added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=036-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरत्व|अपरत्वं
अपरत्व n. (-त्वं)<BR>	 1. Opposition, contrariety.<BR>	 2. Posteriorly, (in place or<BR>time;) also अपरता f. (-ता.)<BR> E. त्व or तल् added to अपर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=036-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरति|अपरतिः
अपरति m. (-तिः) Stopping, ceasing.<BR> E. अप from, रम to please, and<BR>क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=036-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपररात्र|अपररात्रः
अपररात्र m. (-त्रः) The end of the night, the last watch.<BR> E. अपर the end,<BR>रात्र from रात्रि a night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=036-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरलोक|अपरलोकः
अपरलोक n. (-कं) Another world, paradise.<BR> E. अपर, and लोक world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=036-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरव|अपरवः
अपरव m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. Contest, dispute.<BR>	 2. Discord.<BR> E. अप, and रव sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=036-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरवक्त्र
अपरवक्त्र n. (-क्त्रं) A kind of metre of four lines, having every two lines<BR>the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=036-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरवोज्झित
अपरवोज्झित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Undisturbed, undisputed.<BR> E. अपरव, and उज्झित<BR>free from.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=036-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरस्पर|अपरस्परं
अपरस्पर adj.<BR>	 mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) or adv.<BR>	 n. (-रं)<BR>	 1. Continued, uninterrupted.<BR>2. Continually, (applied to action.)<BR> E. अ neg. and परस्पर mutual.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=036-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपराङ्मुख|अपराङ्मुखः
अपराङ्मुख mfn. (-खः-खी-खं) Not having the head downwards or reverted.<BR>2. Presenting a firm front in battle or danger.<BR> E. अ neg. पराङ्मुख<BR>reverted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=036-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपराजित|अपराजितः
अपराजित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Unconquered, unsurpassed.<BR>	 m. (-तः)<BR>	 1. A name<BR>of ŚIVA.<BR>	 2. Also of VIṢṆU.<BR>	 3. A sage.<BR>	 f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. A name applied to<BR>several plants.<BR>	 2. (Clitoria ternatea,) see गिरिकर्णी.<BR>	 3. Æschynomene<BR>sesban, see जया. and, 4. Another plant, see अशनपर्णी.<BR>	 5. A name of<BR>the goddess DURGĀ.<BR>	 6. A species of the शर्कर metre of four lines,<BR>with fourteen syllables in each line.<BR>	 7. The north-east quarter. E.<BR>अपर another, अ neg. and जित conquered, excelled, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=036-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपराजेय
अपराजेय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Unconquerable, invincible.<BR> E. अपर, and अजेय<BR>unconquerable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=036-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपराद्ध
अपराद्ध mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>	 1. Criminal, guilty.<BR>	 2. Erring.<BR> E. अप before,<BR>राध to accomplish, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=037-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपराद्धपृषत्क|अपराद्धपृषत्कः
अपराद्धपृषत्क m. (-त्कः) An archer or arrow always missing the butt. E.<BR>अपराद्ध erring, and पृषत्क an arrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=037-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपराद्धृ
अपराद्धृ mfn. (-द्धा-द्ध्री-द्धृ) Offending, an offender.<BR> E. अप before राध, with<BR>तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=037-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपराध|अपराधः
अपराध m. (-धः) Offence, transgression, fault.<BR> E. अप badly, and राध<BR>to accomplish, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=037-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपराधित
अपराधित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Criminated, condemned.<BR> E. अपराध and क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=037-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपराधिता
अपराधिता f. (-ता) Criminality, guilt. So अपराधित्व n. (-त्वं)<BR> E. तल् or त्व<BR>added to अपराधिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=037-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपराधिन्
अपराधिन् mfn. (-धी-धिनी-धि) Offending, culpable, criminal.<BR> E. अपराध,<BR>and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=037-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपराधीन
अपराधीन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Independent.<BR> E. अ neg. पराधीन dependent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=037-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपराह्ण|अपराह्णः
अपराह्ण m. (-ह्णः) Afternoon, the last watch of the day.<BR> E. अपर last, and<BR>अह्ण for अहन् a day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=037-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपराह्णतन|अपराह्णतनं
अपराह्णतन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Belonging to or produced in the close of the<BR>day, also अपराह्णेतन.<BR> E. अपराह्ण the end of a day, with द्यु or द्युल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=037-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरिकलित|अपरिकलितः
अपरिकलित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Unknown 2. Unseen.<BR> E. अ neg. परिकलित<BR>seen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=037-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरिक्लिन्न
अपरिक्लिन्न mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं) Dry, not moist, not liquid.<BR> E. अ neg. परिक्लिन्न<BR>moist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=037-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरिगत
अपरिगत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Unknown, unobtained.<BR> E. अ neg. परिगत ob-<BR>tained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=037-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरिग्रह|अपरिग्रहः
अपरिग्रह m. (-हः) Non-acceptance.<BR> E. अ neg. परिग्रह taking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=037-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरिग्राह्य
अपरिग्राह्य mfn. (-ह्यः-ह्या-ह्यं) Unfit or improper to be accepted, not to be<BR>taken.<BR> E. अ neg. परिग्राह्य to be taken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=037-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरिचयिन्
अपरिचयिन् mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि)<BR>	 1. Without acquaintance.<BR>	 2. Misanthropic.<BR>E. अ neg. परिचयिन् acquainted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=037-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरिचित
अपरिचित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Unacquainted with, unknown to.<BR> E. अ neg.<BR>परिचित known.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=037-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरिचेय
अपरिचेय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Unsociable.<BR> E. अ neg. परिचेय to be combined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=037-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरिच्छद
अपरिच्छद n. (-दं) Absence of clothing, nudity.<BR> E. अ neg. परिच्छद covering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=037-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरिच्छन्न|अपरिच्छन्नं
अपरिच्छन्न mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं) Uncovered, unclothed. So अपरिच्छादित mfn.<BR>(-तः-ता-तं)<BR> E. अ neg. परिच्छन्न or परिच्छादित clothed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=037-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरिच्छिन्न|अपरिच्छिन्नं
अपरिच्छिन्न mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं) Continuous, connected without interval. E.<BR>अ neg. परिच्छिन्न intersected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=037-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरिच्छेद|अपरिच्छेदः
अपरिच्छेद m. (-दः)<BR>	 1. Want of arrangement or order.<BR>	 2. Want of dis-<BR>tinction or division.<BR> E. अ neg. परिच्छेद section.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=037-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरिच्छेदित
अपरिच्छेदित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Unarranged, not distinguished or divided.<BR>E. अ neg. परिच्छेदित intersected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=037-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरिणयन
अपरिणयन n. (-नं) Celibacy.<BR> E. अ neg. परिणयन marrying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=037-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरिणीता
अपरिणीता f. (-ता) An unmarried woman.<BR> E. अ neg. परिणीता married<BR>woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=037-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरिपक्व|अपरिपक्वं
अपरिपक्व mfn. (-क्वः-क्वा-क्वं) Not quite mature.<BR> E. अ neg. परिपक्व ripe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=037-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरिपाटि
अपरिपाटि f. (-टिः-टी) Want of order, disarrangement.<BR> E. अ neg. परिपाटि<BR>order.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=037-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरिपूत
अपरिपूत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Unripe, immature, imperfect.<BR> E. अ neg. परिपूत<BR>perfect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=037-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरिमाण
अपरिमाण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Without measure, immense, immeasurable.<BR>E. अ neg. परिमाण measure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=037-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरिमित|अपरिमितं
अपरिमित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Unmeasured.<BR>	 2. Unlimited, unbounded. E.<BR>अ neg. परिमित measured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=037-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरिमेय
अपरिमेय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Unbounded, illimitable.<BR> E. अ neg. परिमेय mea-<BR>surable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=037-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरिम्लान|अपरिम्लानः
अपरिम्लान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Pure, clean.<BR> E. अ neg. परिम्लान dirty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=037-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरिवाद्य
अपरिवाद्य mfn. (-द्यः-द्या-द्यं) Not to be reprimanded.<BR> E. अ neg. परिवाद्य<BR>to be reproved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=037-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरिवृत
अपरिवृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Unenclosed, unsurrounded.<BR> E. अ neg. परिवृत<BR>surrounded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=037-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरिष्कार|अपरिष्कारः
अपरिष्कार m. (-रः) Coarseness, rudeness, want of polish or finish, moral<BR>or physical.<BR> E. अ neg. परिष्कार polish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=037-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरिष्कृत|अपरिष्कृतं
अपरिष्कृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Coarse, rude, unpolished, unadorned, morally<BR>or physically.<BR> E. अ neg. परिष्कृत finished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=037-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरिसर|अपरिसरः
अपरिसर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Distant, not contiguous.<BR> E. अ neg. परिसर near.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=037-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरिहरणीय
अपरिहरणीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Not to be abandoned or lost.<BR> E. अ neg. परिहृ<BR>to leave, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=037-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरिहार्य्य|अपरिहार्य|अपरिहार्य्यं
अपरिहार्य्य mfn. (-र्य्यः-र्य्या-र्य्यं)<BR>	 1. Not to be avoided, inevitable.<BR>	 2. Not to<BR>be abandoned.<BR>	 3. Not to be degraded.<BR> E. अ neg. परिहृ to leave, ण्यत्<BR>aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=037-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरीक्षित
अपरीक्षित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Untried, unproved.<BR> E. अ neg. परीक्षित tried.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=037-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरूप|अपरूपं
अपरूप mfn. (-पः-पा-पी-पं) Ugly, deformed, ill-looking, ill-made, mons-<BR>trous.<BR>	 n. (-पं) Monstrosity, deformity.<BR> E. अप bad, रूप form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=037-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपर्ण
अपर्ण mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-र्णं) Leafless.<BR>	 f. (-र्णा) A name of PĀRVATĪ.<BR> E. अ not,<BR>and पर्ण a leaf: the goddess not having even leaves for food,<BR>during her performance of religious austerities.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=037-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपर्य्याप्त|अपर्याप्त|अपर्य्याप्तं
अपर्य्याप्त mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं)<BR>	 1. Unlimited, unbounded.<BR>	 2. Incompetent, un-<BR>able, insufficient.<BR>	 3. Incomplete, not enough.<BR> E. अ neg. पर्य्याप्त ex-<BR>tended.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=037-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपर्य्याय|अपर्याय|अपर्यायः
अपर्य्याय m. (-यः) Want of order or method.<BR> E. अ neg. पर्य्याय order.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=037-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपल|अपलं
अपल n. (-लं) A pin or bolt.<BR> E. अप below, and ला to take, ड aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=037-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपलाप|अपलापः
अपलाप m. (-पः)<BR>	 1. Denial or concealment of knowledge, evasion.<BR>	 2.<BR>Affection, regard.<BR>	 3. Concealing, hiding.<BR> E. अप away or kindly,<BR>and लप to speak, घञ् affix; also अपलपन n. (-नं)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=037-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपलापिन्
अपलापिन् mfn. (-पी-पिनी-पि) One who denies or evades.<BR> E. अपलाप and<BR>इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=037-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपलाषिका
अपलाषिका f. (-का) Thirst.<BR> E. अप, लष to desire, कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=037-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवन|अपवनं
अपवन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Without air, sheltered from wind.<BR>	 n. (-नं) A gar-<BR>den, grove.<BR> E. अप, and वन a wood, or अ neg. पवन wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=037-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवरक|अपवरकः
अपवरक m. (-कः) An inner apartment, the lying-in chamber.<BR> E. अप be-<BR>fore, वृञ् to hide or close, अच् and कन् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=037-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवरण|अपवरणं
अपवरण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Covering, screening.<BR>	 2. A garment, a mantle.<BR> E. अप<BR>before, वृ to screen, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=037-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवर्ग|अपवर्गः
अपवर्ग m. (-र्गः)<BR>	 1. Final beatitude, the delivery of the soul from the body,<BR>and exemption from farther transmigration.<BR>	 2. Abandoning, quit-<BR>ting.<BR>	 3. The fruit or consequences of any completed act.<BR>	 4. The<BR>completion of any act.<BR>	 5. Any act brought to a conclusion.<BR>	 6.<BR>End, completion.<BR> E. अप from, वृज् to forsake, घञ् affix, and ग<BR>substituted for ज.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=037-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवर्गद
अपवर्गद mfn. (-दः-दा-दं) Conferring final beatitude.<BR> E. अपवर्ग, and द who<BR>gives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=037-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवर्जन|अपवर्जनं|अपवर्ज्जन|अपवर्ज्जनं
अपवर्जन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Gift or donation.<BR>	 2. Final emancipation or beatitude.<BR>3. Abandoning, abandonment.<BR> E. अप before, वृज् to forsake, and<BR>ल्युट् aff. See अपवर्ग.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=037-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवर्ज्जित|अपवर्जित
अपवर्ज्जित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Abandoned, quitted, got rid of, given cast<BR>away.<BR> E. अप before, वृज् to forsake, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=037-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवर्त्त|अपवर्त|अपवर्तः
अपवर्त्त m. (-र्त्तः)<BR>	 1. Taking away.<BR>	 2. A common measure in algebra. E.<BR>अप away, वृत to be, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=037-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवर्त्तन|अपवर्तन|अपवर्तनं
अपवर्त्तन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Agitating, shaking.<BR>	 2. Taking away, removal, resump-<BR>tion.<BR>	 3. Transferring, removing from one place to another.<BR>	 4.<BR>Abbreviation, abridging.<BR>	 5. Division by a common measure, re-<BR>duction of a fraction to its lowest terms.<BR> E. अप away, वृत to be,<BR>ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=037-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवाद|अपवादः
अपवाद m. (-दः)<BR>	 1. Censure, blame.<BR>	 2. An order, a command.<BR>	 3. Differ-<BR>ence, distinction, exception.<BR>	 4. Contradiction, opposition, denial.<BR>E. अप implying aversion, and वाद speech, from वद with घञ्; also<BR>अववाद.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=037-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवादक
अपवादक mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>	 1. Censuring, accusing.<BR>	 2. Opposing, object-<BR>ing to.<BR>	 3. Excepting, excluding.<BR> E. अप before, वद to speak, ण्वुल्<BR>aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=037-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवादित
अपवादित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Accused, censured.<BR>	 2. Opposed, objected to.<BR>E. अप before, वद to speak, causal form, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=038-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवादिन्
अपवादिन् mfn. (-दी-दिनी-दि)<BR>	 1. Accusing, defaming.<BR>	 2. Opposing, object-<BR>ing to.<BR> E. अपवाद and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=038-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवारण|अपवारणं
अपवारण n. (-णं) Disappearance, concealment, covering.<BR> E. अप before,<BR>वृञ् to hide, in the causal form, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=038-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवारित|अपवारितं
अपवारित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Covered, concealed, disappeared.<BR> E. अप before, वृञ्<BR>to hide, क्त affix, and the vowel is made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=038-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवार्य्य|अपवार्य
अपवार्य्य ind.<BR>	 1. (In theatrical language) Apart, aside.<BR>	 2. Having con-<BR>cealed.<BR> E. अप before, वृञ् to hide, ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=038-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवाह|अपवाहः
अपवाह m. (-हः) An inference or deduction.<BR> E. अप before, वह to bear,<BR>घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=038-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवित्र|अपवित्रं
अपवित्र mfn. (-त्रः-त्रा-त्रं) Impure, unclean.<BR> E. अ neg. पवित्र pure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=038-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवित्रता
अपवित्रता f. (-ता) Impurity, uncleanness. So अपवित्रत्व n. (-त्रं)<BR> E. तल् or त्व<BR>added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=038-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपविद्ध|अपविद्धः
अपविद्ध mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>	 1. Rejected, dismissed, removed.<BR>	 2. Thrown,<BR>sent.<BR>	 3. Broken to pieces.<BR> E. अप before. व्यध to strike, क्त the part.<BR>affix, and the semivowel changed to its corresponding vowel इ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=038-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपविद्धपुत्र|अपविद्धपुत्रः
अपविद्धपुत्र m. (-त्रः) A son rejected by his natural parents, and adopted<BR>by a stranger; one of the twelve objects of filiation in Hindu<BR>law.<BR> E. अपविद्ध as before and पुत्र a son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=038-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपविषा
अपविषा f. (-षा) A species of grass, (Kyllingia monocephala.)<BR> E. अप, and<BR>विष poison.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=038-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवृत्त
अपवृत्त mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं)<BR>	 1. Reversed, inverted, overturned.<BR>	 2. Deprived<BR>of 3. Uncovered<BR> E. अप, and वृत्त established.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=038-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवेध|अपवेधः
अपवेध m. (-धः) Piercing any thing in the wrong direction.<BR> E. अप, and<BR>वेध perforating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=038-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपव्यय|अपव्ययः
अपव्यय m. (-यः) Prodigality.<BR> E. अप, and व्यय expense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=038-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपव्ययमान
अपव्ययमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>	 1. Squandering.<BR>	 2. Denying a debt.<BR> E. अप<BR>away, व्यय expenditure, used as a verb, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=038-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपव्ययिन्
अपव्ययिन् mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि) Squandering, wasting, prodigal.<BR> E. अपव्यय<BR>and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=038-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपशङ्क|अपशंक
अपशङ्क mfn. (-ङ्कः-ङ्का-ङ्कं) Fearless, having no fear or hesitation. adv.<BR>	 n.<BR>(-ङ्कं) Fearlessly.<BR> E. अप, and शङ्क fear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=038-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपशद|अपशदः
अपशद m. (-दः) A low man. See अपसद.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=038-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपशब्द|अपशब्दः
अपशब्द m. (-ब्दः)<BR>	 1. Ungrammatical language.<BR>	 2. Common or vulgar<BR>speech, any form of language not Sanskrit.<BR> E. अप bad, and शब्द<BR>sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=038-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपशुच्
अपशुच् m. (-शुक्) The soul.<BR> E. अप, and शुच् sorrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=038-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपशोक|अपशोकः
अपशोक m. (-कः) A tree, (Jonesia asoca.)<BR> E. अप, and शोक sorrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=038-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपष्ट
अपष्ट n. (-ष्टं) The end or point of the hook for driving an elephant. E.<BR>अप before, ष्टे to surround, and ड aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=038-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपष्टम
अपष्टम m. (-मः) The point of the hook by which elephants are driven.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=038-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपष्ठु|अपष्ठुः
अपष्ठु m. (-ष्ठुः) Time.<BR>	 mfn. (-ष्ठुः-ष्ठुः-ष्ठु)<BR>	 1. Contrary, opposite.<BR>	 2. Left,<BR>(not right.) ind.<BR>	 1. Well, properly.<BR>	 2. Handsomely.<BR>	 3. Contrary,<BR>perversely.<BR> E. अप badly, स्थ what stays, with कु Unādi affix; स्थ<BR>becomes ष्ठ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=038-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपष्ठुर|अपष्ठुरं
अपष्ठुर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Opposite, contrary.<BR> E. अपष्ठु contrary, and र<BR>from रा to obtain, affix ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=038-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपष्ठुल|अपष्ठुलं
अपष्ठुल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Opposite, contrary, E. As before, ल substituted<BR>for र<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=038-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपस्
अपस् n. (-पः) Sacrificing.<BR> E. आप to obtain, अमुन् Unādi aff.; the radical<BR>vowel made short.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=038-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपसद|अपसदः
अपसद m. (-दः) A low man, an outcaste; it especially applies to the<BR>children of six degrading connexions, or of a Brāhman with the<BR>women of the three lower classes; of a Kṣatriya with<BR>women of two, the Vaiśya, and Śūdra; and of a Vaiśya with one<BR>of a lower class or a Śūdra.<BR> E. अप low, सद to abide, and अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=038-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपसर|अपसरः
अपसर m. (-रः) The removal of any thing from one place to another.<BR>E. अप before सृ to go, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=038-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपसर्जन|अपसर्जनं|अपसर्ज्जन|अपसर्ज्जनं
अपसर्जन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. A gift or donation.<BR>	 2. Killing.<BR>	 3. Final emancipa-<BR>tion.<BR>	 4. Abandonment.<BR> E. अप before, सृज to leave, and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=038-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपसरण|अपसरणं
अपसरण n. (-णं) Going out, egress.<BR> E. अप before, सरणं going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=038-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपसर्प|अपसर्पः
अपसर्प m. (-र्पः) A secret emissary or agent, a spy. So अपसर्पक m. (-कः) E.<BR>अप bad, &c. सर्प who goes; from सृप with अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=038-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपसलवि
अपसलवि ind. The space between the thumb and the forefinger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=038-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपसव्य|अपसव्यं|अपसव्यः
अपसव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>	 1. Opposite, contrary.<BR>	 2. Right, (not left.)<BR>	 n.<BR>(-व्यं) The space between the thumb and the forefinger.<BR> E. अप, and<BR>सव्य left.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=038-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपसव्यक
अपसव्यक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) See the above.<BR> E. कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=038-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपसार|अपसारः
अपसार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Egress, passage for going forth.<BR>	 2. Going out or away.<BR>E. अप before, सार a going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=038-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपसारित
अपसारित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Gone out, got out, escaped, fled.<BR> E. अप before,<BR>सारित gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=038-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपस्कर|अपस्करः
अपस्कर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Any part of a carriage.<BR>	 2. The anus.<BR>	 3. Fæces.<BR> E. अप,<BR>and कर from कृष to furrow, or कृ to do; स is inserted for the sake of<BR>euphony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=038-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपस्नात|अपस्नातः
अपस्नात mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Bathed or bathing after mourning, or upon the<BR>death of a connexion.<BR>	 2. Bathed after death. (the corpse,) prepara-<BR>tory to other ceremonies.<BR> E. अप, and स्नात bathed, from ष्णा, and<BR>क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=038-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपस्नान|अपस्नानं
अपस्नान n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Funereal bathing, upon the death of a connexion,<BR>after mourning, &c.<BR>	 2. Impure bathing, or bathing in water with<BR>which a person has previously washed.<BR> E. अप, and स्नान bathing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=038-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपस्पश
अपस्पश mfn. (-शः-शा-शं)<BR>	 1. Being without spies or emissaries.<BR>	 2. Want-<BR>ing the introduction or explanation, (grammar.)<BR> E. अप with स्पश<BR>a spy, or अ and पस्पश the first section of the Bhāṣya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=038-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपस्मार|अपस्मारः
अपस्मार m. (-रः) Epilepsy, falling sickness.<BR> E. अप privation, स्मृ to re-<BR>member, and घञ् affix; loss of memory or sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=038-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपस्मारिन्
अपस्मारिन् mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि) Epileptic, convulsed.<BR> E. इनि added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=038-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपहत
अपहत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Destroyed.<BR> E. अप, and हत killed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=038-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपहरण|अपहरणं
अपहरण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Taking away, carrying off, stealing, &c.<BR>	 2. Taking<BR>back, resuming.<BR> E. अप before, हृ to take, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=038-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपहरणीय
अपहरणीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>	 1. To be taken away, carried off, stolen, &c.<BR>2. To be taken back or resumed.<BR> E. अप before, हृ to take, अनीयर्<BR>affix; also अपहर्त्तव्य, and अपहार्य्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=038-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपहस्त|अपहस्तः
अपहस्त n. (-स्तं)<BR>	 1. Taking away or off.<BR>	 2. Stealing, plundering.<BR> E. अप,<BR>and हस्त the hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=038-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपहस्तित
अपहस्तित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Lost, gone, parted with or deprived of.<BR> E. अप,<BR>हस्त the hand, इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=038-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपहानि|अपहानिः
अपहानि f. (-निः)<BR>	 1. Exception, exclusion.<BR>	 2. Quitting, leaving.<BR>	 3. Leav-<BR>ing off, stopping.<BR> E. अप, and हानि abandoning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=038-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपहाय
अपहाय ind. Having left or abandoned.<BR>	 2. Except, excepting.<BR> E. अप<BR>before, हा to abandon, य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=038-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपहार|अपहारः
अपहार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Loss.<BR>	 2. Taking away.<BR>	 3. Theft, stealing.<BR>	 4. Secret-<BR>ing.<BR>	 5. Spending another person's property.<BR> E. अप before, हृ to<BR>take, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=038-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपहारक|अपहारकः
अपहारक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) One who takes away, seizing, taking, a thief.<BR>E. अपहृ to take away, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=038-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपहारिन्
अपहारिन् mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि) One who takes away, who seizes, steals, &c. a<BR>plunderer, a thief.<BR> E. अपहृ to steal, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=038-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपहास|अपहासः
अपहास m. (-सः) Silly or causeless laughter.<BR> E. अप before, हास laughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=038-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपहृत
अपहृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Taken away, carried aff, stolen, &c.<BR>	 2. Taken<BR>back, resumed.<BR> E. अप before, हृत taken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=038-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपह्नव|अपह्नवः
अपह्नव m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. Denial or concealment of knowledge.<BR>	 2. Affection. E.<BR>अप before, ह्नुङ् to conceal, and अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=038-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपह्नुत
अपह्नुत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Concealed, denied.<BR> E. अप before, ह्नु and क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=038-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपह्नुति|अपह्नुतिः
अपह्नुति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Denial or concealment of knowledge.<BR>	 2. A figure<BR>of rhetoric, applying a description or simile to other than its<BR>obvious application.<BR> E. अपह्नुङ् and क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=038-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपह्नोतृ
अपह्नोतृ mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ) One who conceals or denies.<BR> E. अपह्नुङ् and<BR>तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=039-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाक|अपाकः
अपाक mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>	 1. Immature, raw, undressed or unripe.<BR>	 2. Un-<BR>digested.<BR>	 m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. Immaturity.<BR>	 2. Indigestion.<BR> E. अ neg. पाक<BR>ripeness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=039-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाकरण|अपाकरणं
अपाकरण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Payment, liquidation.<BR>	 2. Removal, abstraction. E.<BR>अप and आङ् before कृ to make, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=039-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाकशाक|अपाकशाकं
अपाकशाक n. (-कं) Ginger.<BR> E. अपाक indigestion, and शाक herb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=039-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाकृत
अपाकृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Taken away, removed, destroyed, void of. 2<BR>Paid.<BR> E. अप and आ before, कृत made.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=039-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाकृति|अपाकृतिः
अपाकृति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Removal, taking away.<BR>	 2. Change of form or condi-<BR>tion.<BR> E. अप and आ before कृति doing, or अप with, आकृति form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=039-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाक्ष|अपाक्षं
अपाक्ष mfn. (-क्षः-क्षा-क्षं) Present, perceptible.<BR> E. अप before, and अक्ष an<BR>organ of sense, or अक्षि the eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=039-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाङ्क्त|अपांक्त
अपाङ्क्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>	 1. Not in a line or row.<BR>	 2. Not in the same<BR>degree or class, unworthy, inadmissible into society, excluded. E.<BR>अ neg. पङ्क्ति a line, अण् affix; also similar derivatives as अपाङ्क्त्य,<BR>&c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=039-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाङ्क्तेय|अपांक्तेय
अपाङ्क्तेय mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>	 1. Not in a line or row.<BR>	 2. Not in the same<BR>degree or order of society.<BR> E. अ neg. पंक्ति a line, ढक् aff. See अपाङ्कृत.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=039-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाङ्क्त्योपहत
अपाङ्क्त्योपहत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Defiled or contaminated by the presence of<BR>impure or improper persons.<BR> E. अपाङ्क्त्य excluded, उपहत affected by.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=039-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाङ्ग|अपांग|अपाङ्गः
अपाङ्ग n. (-ङ्गं)<BR>	 1. The outer corner of the eye.<BR>	 2. A sectarial mark or<BR>circlet on the forehead.<BR>	 mfn. (-ङ्गः-ङ्गी-ङ्गं) Maimed, crippled.<BR> E. अप<BR>before अगि to go, and अच् affix, or अङ्ग a limb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=039-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाङ्गक|अपांगक|अपाङ्गकः
अपाङ्गक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Maimed, mutilated.<BR>	 m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A plant,<BR>(Achyranthes aspera.)<BR>	 2. The outer angle of the eye.<BR> E. अप before<BR>the body, and क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=039-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाङ्गदर्शन|अपांगदर्शन|अपाङ्गदर्शनं
अपाङ्गदर्शन n. (-नं) A side glance, a leer, a wink.<BR> E. अपाङ्ग the corner of<BR>अङ्ग the eye, and दर्शन looking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=039-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाच्
अपाच् or अपाञ्च् mfn. (अपाङ् अपाची अपाक्) South, southern. E. See अवाच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=039-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाञ्च्|अपांच्
अपाच् or अपाञ्च् mfn. (अपाङ् अपाची अपाक्) South, southern. E. See अवाच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=039-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाच्य|अपाच्यं
अपाच्य mfn. (-च्यः-च्या-च्यं)<BR>	 1. Southern, southerly.<BR>	 2. Not to be ripened or<BR>digested.<BR> E. अपाच्, and यत् affix or अ neg. पाच्य to be ripened.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=039-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाचीन|अपाचीनं
अपाचीन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>	 1. South, southern.<BR>	 2. Opposite.<BR> E. अपाच् and ख<BR>aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=039-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाटव|अपाटवं
अपाटव n. (-वं)<BR>	 1. Sickness, disease.<BR>	 2. Awkwardness, inelegance.<BR> E. अ<BR>priv. and पाटव strength, cleverness, &c. See अपटु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=039-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाणिग्रहण
अपाणिग्रहण n. (-णं) Celibacy.<BR> E. अ neg. पाणिग्रहण taking the hand, as in<BR>marrying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=039-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपात्र|अपात्रं
अपात्र n. (-त्रं)<BR>	 1. A worthless or common utensil.<BR>	 2. An inferior or<BR>worthless person.<BR> E. अ neg. पात्र a vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=039-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपात्रीकरण|अपात्रीकरणं
अपात्रीकरण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Acting unbecomingly, doing degrading offices, as<BR>for a BRĀHMAN to receive wealth improperly acquired; to trade,<BR>to serve a SUDRA, and to utter an untruth.<BR>	 2. Excommunication,<BR>disqualification.<BR> E. अ neg. पात्र a vessel, करणं making, च्वि augment;<BR>disqualifying a person from eating out of the same vessel as<BR>another.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=039-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपादान|अपादानं
अपादान n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Removal, ablation, the sense of the fifth or ablative<BR>case.<BR>	 2. Taking away.<BR> E. अप from, आदान taking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=039-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपान|अपानं|अपानः
अपान n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. The anus.<BR>	 2. A fart, one of the five vital airs.<BR> E. अप<BR>below, अन to breathe, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=039-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपान्नाथ|अपांनाथ|अपांनाथः
अपान्नाथ m. (-थः) The ocean.<BR> E. अपाम् of water, नाथ lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=039-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपान्निधि|अपांनिधि|अपांनिधिः
अपान्निधि m. (-धिः) The ocean.<BR> E. अपां of water, निधि receptacle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=039-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाप|अपापः
अपाप mfn. (-पः-पा-पं) Sinless, virtuous, pure. So अपापिन् mfn. (-पी-पिनी-पि)<BR>E. अ neg. and पाप sin or पापिन् sinner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=039-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपामार्ग|अपामार्गः
अपामार्ग m. (-र्गः) A plant, (Achyranthes aspera.)<BR> E. अप, मृज to clean,<BR>with आङ् prefixed, and घञ् affix; the ashes are used in washing<BR>linen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=039-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाम्पति|अपांपति|अपांपतिः|अपाम्पतिः
अपाम्पति m. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. The ocean.<BR>	 2. A name of VARUṆA. See. अप्पति.<BR> E. अपाम्<BR>genitive case of अप water, and पति master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=039-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाम्पित्त|अपांपित्त|अपांपित्तं|अपाम्पित्तं
अपाम्पित्त n. (-त्तं) Fire.<BR> E. अपाम् of water, and पित्त bile; drying it up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=039-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाय|अपायः
अपाय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. Destruction, annihilation.<BR>	 2. Separation, disunion.<BR>	 3.<BR>Loss, injury.<BR>	 4. Departure, going away.<BR>	 5. Retreat, flight.<BR> E. अप<BR>away, अय going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=039-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपायिन्
अपायिन् mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि)<BR>	 1. Going away, departing, perishing.<BR> E. अपाय<BR>and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=039-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपार|अपारं|अपारः
अपार n. (-रं) The opposite bank of a river.<BR>	 mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Unbounded,<BR>boundless, interminable.<BR> E. अ neg. पार shore.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=039-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपारक
अपारक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Incompetent, impotent.<BR> E. अ neg. पारक who<BR>gets through or over.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=039-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपार्थ
अपार्थ mfn. (-र्थः-र्था-र्थं)<BR>	 1. Useless, unprofitable.<BR>	 2. Unmeaning.<BR> E. अप<BR>without, अर्थ object, also with कन् added अपार्थक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=039-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपार्थकरण
अपार्थकरण n. (-णं) A false plea in a lawsuit.<BR> E. अपार्थ, and करण making.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=039-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपावर्त्तन|अपावर्तन|अपावर्तनं
अपावर्त्तन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Turning away or from.<BR>	 2. Retreat, repulse.<BR>	 3. Re-<BR>turning.<BR> E. अप and आङ् before, वृत to be, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=039-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपावृत|अपावृतं
अपावृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Self-willed, unrestrained.<BR>	 2. Covered, conceal-<BR>ed.<BR>	 3. Surrounded, inclosed.<BR>	 4. Opened.<BR>	 5. Driven away. adv. (-तं)<BR>Immoderately, unreservedly.<BR> E. अप priv. वृञ् to hide, with आङ्<BR>prefixed, and क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=039-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपावृति|अपावृतिः
अपावृति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Enclosing, surrounding.<BR>	 2. Covering, screening. E.<BR>अप and आङ् before, वृ to hide, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=039-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपावृत्त|अपावृत्तं
अपावृत्त mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं)<BR>	 1. Rolling on the ground, (as a horse.)<BR>	 2. Un-<BR>covered.<BR>	 3. Driven back or to the rear, repelled.<BR> E. अप before, वृत<BR>to stand, and क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=039-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपावृत्ति|अपावृत्तिः
अपावृत्ति f. (-त्तिः)<BR>	 1. Retreat, repulse.<BR>	 2. Returning.<BR> E. अप and आङ् before.<BR>वृत to be, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=039-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाश्रय|अपाश्रयः
अपाश्रय m. (-यः) An awning spread over a court or yard.<BR>	 mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Helpless, destitute.<BR> E. अप, and आश्रय protection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=039-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपासङ्ग|अपासंग|अपासंगः|अपासङ्गः
अपासङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः) A quiver; also उपासङ्ग.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=039-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपासन|अपासनं
अपासन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Quitting, foregoing, discarding.<BR>	 2. Killing, slaughter.<BR>E. अप, अस to be, and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=039-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपासरण|अपासरणं
अपासरण n. (-णं) Departing, departure, removal.<BR> E. अप and आङ् before, सृ<BR>to go, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=039-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपासित
अपासित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Thrown or cut down, injured, destroyed.<BR> E. अप<BR>with अस to throw, क्त affix and इट् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=039-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपासृत
अपासृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Gone, departed, gone away.<BR> E. अप, and आङ्<BR>before, सृ to go, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=039-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपास्त|अपास्तं
अपास्त mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं)<BR>	 1. Thrown off, set aside.<BR>	 2. Driven away, expell-<BR>ed.<BR>	 3. Discarded, abandoned.<BR>	 4. Disregarded, contemned.<BR> E. अप<BR>and अस to throw, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=039-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपास्य
अपास्य ind.<BR>	 1. Having quitted or left.<BR>	 2. Having thrown away.<BR>	 3. Dis-<BR>regarding.<BR> E. अप, and अस to throw, य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=039-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपि
अपि ind. A preposition and particle corresponding to even, though,<BR>yet, assuredly, &c. and implying.<BR>	 1. Interrogation.<BR>	 2. Earnest inter-<BR>rogation or enquiry.<BR>	 3. Doubt.<BR>	 4. Possibility.<BR>	 5. Reproof; and.<BR>	 6.<BR>Conjunction.<BR>	 7. It is often an expletive.<BR> E. अ neg. and पि to go,<BR>with क्विप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=039-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपिगीर्ण|अपिगीर्णं
अपिगीर्ण mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-र्णं) Praised.<BR> E. अपि before, गीर्ण part. past, irregular-<BR>ly formed from गॄ to sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=039-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपिच
अपिच ind. Moreover, also.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=039-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपिच्छल
अपिच्छल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Clear, free from sediment or soil.<BR> E. अ neg.<BR>पिच्छल muddy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=039-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपितु
अपितु ind. If, if indeed, yet, but yet.<BR> E. अपि, and तु but, and, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=039-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपितृक
अपितृक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) See the next.<BR> E. अ neg. पितृ a father, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=039-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपित्र्य
अपित्र्य mfn. (-त्र्यः-त्रा-त्र्यं) Uninherited, acquired, not ancestral or pater-<BR>nal.<BR> E. अ neg. पितृ a father, क्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=039-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपिधान|अपिधानं
अपिधान n. (-नं) Covering, concealment, disappearance.<BR> E. अपि before धा<BR>to have or hold, and ल्युट् aff. See पिधान.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=039-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपिनद्ध|अपिनद्धं
अपिनद्ध mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं) Clothed, accoutred.<BR> E. अपि, and नद्ध part. past<BR>of नह to bind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=039-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपिशुन
अपिशुन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Upright, honest.<BR> E. अ neg. पिशुन dishonest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=040-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपीडन
अपीडन n. (-नं) Gentleness, kindness, giving pain to nothing.<BR> E. अ neg.<BR>पीडन paining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=040-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपीनस|अपीनसं|अपीनसः
अपीनस m. (-सः) Dryness of the nose, want of the pituitary secretion<BR>and loss of smell, cold.<BR> E. अ neg. पीनस the mucus of the nose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=040-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपीव्य|अपीव्यं
अपीव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं) Very handsome.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=040-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपुच्छ
अपुच्छ mfn. (-च्छः-च्छा-च्छं) Tailless.<BR>	 f. (-च्छा) A tree, (Dalbergia sisu.)<BR>See शिंशपा.<BR> E. अ neg. पुच्छ a tail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=040-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपुण्य
अपुण्य mfn. (-ण्यः-ण्या-ण्यं) Wicked, bad.<BR> E. अ, and पुण्य virtuous. So अपुण्यशील.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=040-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपुण्यकृत्
अपुण्यकृत् mfn. (-त्) Acting wickedly, wicked, bad.<BR> E. कृत् who does, with<BR>अपुण्य. So अपुण्यवत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=040-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपुत्र|अपुत्रः
अपुत्र m. (-त्रः) A man who has no son.<BR> E. अ neg. पुत्र a son, also with<BR>कन् added, अपुत्रकः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=040-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपुनरावृत्ति|अपुनरावृत्तिः
अपुनरावृत्ति f. (-त्तिः) Final exemption from life.<BR> E. अ neg. पुनरावृत्ति re-<BR>newed practice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=040-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपुनर्भव|अपुनर्भवः
अपुनर्भव m. (-वः) Final beatitude, exemption of the soul from further<BR>transmigration.<BR> E. अ neg. पुनर् again, and भव being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=040-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपुराण
अपुराण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Modern, new. So अपुरातन.<BR> E. अ neg. पुराण old.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=040-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपुरुष
अपुरुष mfn. (-षः-षा-षं) Unmanly.<BR> E. अ neg. पुरुष a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=040-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपुष्ट
अपुष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं) Lean.<BR> E. अ neg. पुष्ट nourished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=040-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपुष्प|अपुष्पः
अपुष्प mfn. (-ष्पः-ष्पा-ष्पं) Not flowering.<BR> E. अ neg. पुष्प a flower. So अपुष्पक<BR>and अपुष्पित.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=040-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपुष्पफलद|अपुष्पफलदः
अपुष्पफलद m. (-दः) Any tree which bears fruit, without flowering, as<BR>the jack tree.<BR> E. अपुष्प, फल fruit, and द what gives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=040-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपूजक
अपूजक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Irreligious, irreverent.<BR> E. अ neg. पूजक a wor-<BR>shipper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=040-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपूजा
अपूजा f. (-जा) Irreverence, disrespect.<BR> E. अ neg. पूजा worship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=040-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपूजित
अपूजित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Contemned, disregarded, not reverenced or<BR>worshipped.<BR> E. अ neg. पूजित worshipped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=040-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपूत
अपूत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Impure.<BR>	 2. Not having received the invocatory<BR>rite.<BR> E. अ neg. पूत pure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=040-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपूप|अपूपः
अपूप m. (-पः)<BR>	 1. Cake of flour, meal, &c.<BR>	 2. Wheat.<BR> E. पूय to split with<BR>अ neg. prefixed; प affixed, and य dropped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=040-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपूप्य|अपूप्यः
अपूप्य m. (-प्यः) Flour, meal.<BR> E. अपूप a cake, and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=040-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपूरणी
अपूरणी f. (-णी) The silk-cotton tree, (Bombax heptaphyllum.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=040-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपूर्ण
अपूर्ण mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-र्णं) Incomplete, not full or entire.<BR>	 m. (-णः) A fraction.<BR>2. An incomplete number.<BR> E. अ neg. पूर्ण full.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=040-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपूर्णकाल|अपूर्णकालः
अपूर्णकाल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Premature.<BR>	 m. (-लः) Incomplete time.<BR> E. अपूर्ण,<BR>and काल time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=040-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपूर्णकालज
अपूर्णकालज mfn. (-जः-जा-जं) Abortive, born before the proper time. E.<BR>अपूर्ण, and काल time, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=040-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपूर्णता
अपूर्णता f. (-ता) Incompleteness.<BR> E. अपूर्ण and तल् affix also with त्व, अपूर्णत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=040-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपूर्व्व|अपूर्व|अपूर्वः|अपूर्व्वं
अपूर्व्व mfn. (-र्व्वः-र्व्वा-र्व्वं)<BR>	 1. Wonderful, extraordinary.<BR>	 2. Unprecedented,<BR>unpreceded.<BR>	 3. Excellent, not exceeded.<BR>	 4. Not easterly.<BR>	 n. (-र्व्वं)<BR>The remote or unforeseen consequence of an act, as heaven of<BR>religious rites, a consequence not immediately preceded by its<BR>cause.<BR> E. अ neg. पूर्व्व prior.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=040-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपूर्व्ववत्|अपूर्ववत्
अपूर्व्ववत् ind. Singularly, unlike any thing else.<BR> E. अपूर्व्व and वति aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=040-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपृक्त|अपृक्तः
अपृक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं) Unmixed, uncombined.<BR>	 m. (-क्तः) (In grammar) an<BR>affix of a single letter.<BR> E. अ neg. पृक्त combined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=040-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपृथक्
अपृथक् ind. With, together with, collectively.<BR> E. अ not, पृथक् severally.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=040-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपृष्ट
अपृष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं) Unasked, unaddressed, not spoken to.<BR> E. अ neg.<BR>पृष्ट asked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=040-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपेक्षक
अपेक्षक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Expecting.<BR> E. अप before, ईक्ष to see, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=040-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपेक्षणीय|अपेक्षणीयं
अपेक्षणीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>	 1. To be regarded or considered.<BR>	 2. Desirable.<BR>E. अप before, ईक्ष to see, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=040-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपेक्षा
अपेक्षा f. (-क्षा)<BR>	 1. Expectation, hope.<BR>	 2. Regard, reference, consideration.<BR>3. Connexion of cause and effect.<BR>	 4. Absolute connexion, as of an<BR>individual with its species.<BR>	 5. Necessity, need, occasion.<BR> E. अप, ईक्ष<BR>to see, अङ्, and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=040-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपेक्षाबुद्धि|अपेक्षाबुद्धिः
अपेक्षाबुद्धि f. (-द्धिः) Clearness of understanding, the faculty of arranging<BR>and methodising a variety of considerations.<BR> E. अपेक्षा, and बुद्धि<BR>intellect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=040-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपेक्षित
अपेक्षित mfn. (तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Regarded, considered, referred to.<BR>	 2. Wished,<BR>hoped.<BR>	 3. Connected.<BR> E. अप, ईक्ष to see, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=040-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपेक्षितव्य
अपेक्षितव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>	 1. To be regarded or considered.<BR>	 2. Desir-<BR>able, estimable.<BR> E. अप, and ईक्ष to see, तव्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=040-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपेक्षिन्
अपेक्षिन् mfn. (-क्षी-क्षिणी-क्षि)<BR>	 1. Expecting, hoping, an expectant.<BR>	 2. Look-<BR>ing to.<BR> E. अपेक्षा and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=040-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपेक्ष्य
अपेक्ष्य mfn. (-क्ष्यः-क्ष्या-क्ष्यं)<BR>	 1. To be regarded or considered.<BR>	 2. To be<BR>wished or desired. ind. Having considered, having, or with, regard<BR>or reference to.<BR> E. अप, ईक्ष to see, यत् or य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=040-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपेत
अपेत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Gone, departed.<BR>	 2. Lost.<BR>	 3. Open, apart.<BR> E. अप,<BR>and इत gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=040-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपेशल
अपेशल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Inexpert.<BR> E. अ neg. पेशल clever.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=040-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपैशुन
अपैशुन n. (-नं) Integrity, honesty, uprightness.<BR> E. अ neg. पैशुन roguery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=040-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपोगण्ड|अपोगंडः|अपोगण्डः
अपोगण्ड mfn. (-ण्डः-ण्डा-ण्डं)<BR>	 1. Deformed, having a limb too many or too<BR>few, &c.<BR>	 2. Flaccid.<BR>	 3. A child or infant.<BR>	 4. Timid, fearful.<BR> E. अप<BR>before, गम to go, affix ड, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=040-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपोढ
अपोढ mfn. (-ढः-ढा-ढं)<BR>	 1. Removed, carried off.<BR>	 2. Lost, deprived of, taken<BR>away.<BR>	 3. Discussed, established by argument.<BR> E. अप, and ऊढ borne.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=040-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपोदिका
अपोदिका f. (-का) A potherb, (Basella, rubra or lucida.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=040-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपोह|अपोहः
अपोह m. (-हः)<BR>	 1. The removal of doubt by the exercise of the reasoning<BR>faculty.<BR>	 2. Reasoning, arguing.<BR> E. अप reverse, ऊह to reason, and<BR>घञ् affix; opposed to doubt or deliberation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=040-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपोहन|अपोहनं
अपोहन n. (-नं) Reasoning, exercise of reason.<BR> E. अप, and ऊह to reason,<BR>ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=040-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपोहित
अपोहित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Removed, taken away.<BR>	 2. Lost, deprived of.<BR>3. Established by reason.<BR> E. अप, and वह to bear, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=040-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपौरुष
अपौरुष n. (-षं) Unmanliness, cowardice.<BR> E. अ neg. पौरुष manhood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=040-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्तस्
अप्तस् n. (-प्तः) Sacrificing, offering oblations.<BR> E. आप to obtain, असुन् affix,<BR>and त inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=040-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्तु|अप्तुः
अप्तु m. (-प्तुः)<BR>	 1. The body.<BR>	 2. A limb or member.<BR> E. आप to obtain, and<BR>तुन् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=040-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्नस्
अप्नस् n. (-प्नः) Water, (in the language of the Vedas.)<BR> E. आप to obtain,<BR>असुन् affix, and नुम् inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=040-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्पति|अप्पतिः
अप्पति m. (-तिः) A name of VARUṆA.<BR> E. अप् water, and पति lord; regent<BR>of the water, also अपांपति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=040-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्पित्त|अप्पित्तं
अप्पित्त m. (-त्तः) Fire.<BR> E. अप् water, पित्त bile; see अपाम्पित्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=040-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्युत
अप्युत ind. Also, indeed.<BR> E. अपि, and उत or.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=040-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रकट|अप्रकटः
अप्रकट mfn. (-टः-टा-टं) Unmanifested, unapparent.<BR> E. अ neg. प्रकट evident.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=040-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रकम्प|अप्रकंप
अप्रकम्प mfn. (-म्पः-म्पा-म्पं)<BR>	 1. Unshaken, literally or figuratively, firm,<BR>steady.<BR>	 2. Unanswered, unrefuted.<BR> E. अ neg. प्रकम्प trembling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=040-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रकम्पता
अप्रकम्पता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Firmness, stability.<BR>	 2. Unanswerableness.<BR> E. तल्<BR>added to the preceding, also with त्व, अप्रकम्पत्व.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=040-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रकर्षित
अप्रकर्षित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Not exceeded, not more than.<BR>	 2. Unsurpassed.<BR>E. अ neg. प्रकर्षित bettered, exceeded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=040-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रकाश|अप्रकाशः
अप्रकाश mfn. (-शः-शा-शं) Hidden, private, not public or displayed, not<BR>manifest or evident.<BR> E. अ neg. प्रकाश light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=040-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रकाशित
अप्रकाशित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Not manifested, undivulged, unrevealed, not<BR>evident or public.<BR> E. अ neg. प्रकाशित manifested.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=040-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रकृत|अप्रकृतः
अप्रकृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Unusual, uncommon, occasional or incidental<BR>to.<BR> E. अ neg. प्र before, कृत made.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=040-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रकृति|अप्रकृतिः
अप्रकृति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Accidental property or nature, not the inherent or<BR>inseparable property.<BR>	 2. Spiritual being.<BR> E. अ neg. प्रकृति nature or<BR>matter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=040-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रकृष्ट|अप्रकृष्टः
अप्रकृष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं) Low, vile.<BR>	 m. (-ष्टः) A crow.<BR> E. अ neg. प्रकृष्ट<BR>excellent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=040-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रखर|अप्रखरः
अप्रखर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>	 1. Dull, obtuse.<BR>	 2. Bland, mild.<BR> E. अ neg. प्रखर<BR>sharp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=040-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रगल्भ
अप्रगल्भ mfn. (-ल्भः-ल्भा-ल्भं) Modest, unassuming.<BR> E. अ neg. प्रगल्भ arrogant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=041-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रगुण|अप्रगुणः
अप्रगुण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Confounded, perplexed.<BR> E. अ neg. प्रगुण direct.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=041-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रचुर
अप्रचुर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Little, few.<BR> E. अ neg. प्रचुर much.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=041-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रचोदित
अप्रचोदित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Undesired, not bidden or commanded.<BR>	 2.<BR>Undeclared, not said.<BR>	 3. Not promised.<BR>	 4. Unasked, declared.<BR> E. अ<BR>neg. प्रचोदित directed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=041-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रच्युत
अप्रच्युत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Observing, following, not fallen or deviating<BR>from.<BR> E. अ neg. प्रच्युत fallen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=041-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रज
अप्रज mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>	 1. Childless, without progeny.<BR>	 2. Unpeopled,<BR>destitute of subjects.<BR> E. अ neg. प्रजा offspring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=041-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रजात
अप्रजात mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Childless.<BR>	 f. (-ता) A barren woman.<BR> E. अ neg.<BR>प्रजात generated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=041-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रणीत
अप्रणीत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Unconsecrated, profane, common.<BR> E. अ neg. प्रणीत<BR>sacred.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=041-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रणोद्य
अप्रणोद्य mfn. (-द्यः-द्या-द्यं) Not to be turned away.<BR> E. अ neg. प्रणोद्य to be<BR>dismissed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=041-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतर्क्य
अप्रतर्क्य mfn. (-र्क्यः-र्क्या-र्क्यं) Not to be discussed, incomprehensible by<BR>reason.<BR> E. अ neg. प्रतर्क्य to be investigated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=041-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रताप|अप्रतापः
अप्रताप m. (-पः)<BR>	 1. Meanness, want of dignity.<BR>	 2. Dulness, want of<BR>brilliancy.<BR> E. अ neg. प्रताप splendor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=041-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतिकर|अप्रतिकरः
अप्रतिकर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>	 1. Trusted, confidential.<BR>	 2. One who does not<BR>requite or retaliate.<BR> E. अ neg. प्रति again, कर who does.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=041-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतिकार|अप्रतिकारः
अप्रतिकार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Non-requital, non-acquittal.<BR>	 2. Non-retaliation.<BR>	 3.<BR>Not remedying.<BR>	 mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>	 1. Helpless, defenceless.<BR>	 2. Irremedi-<BR>able.<BR> E. अ neg. प्रतिकार rendering again or the like.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=041-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतिग्राह्य
अप्रतिग्राह्य mfn. (-ह्यः-ह्या-ह्यं) Not to be taken, unacceptable.<BR> E. अ neg.<BR>प्रतिग्राह्य to be taken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=041-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतिय
अप्रतिय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Favourable, friendly.<BR> E. अ neg. प्रतिय adverse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=041-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतिपण्य
अप्रतिपण्य mfn. (-ण्यः-ण्या-ण्यं) Not to be bartered or exchanged.<BR> E. अ not,<BR>प्रति again, पण्य to be sold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=041-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतिपत्ति|अप्रतिपत्तिः
अप्रतिपत्ति f. (-त्तिः)<BR>	 1. Non-ascertainment.<BR>	 2. Non-performance, failure,<BR>3. Neglecting, disregard.<BR> E. अ neg. प्रतिपत्ति effecting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=041-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतिपन्न
अप्रतिपन्न mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>	 1. Unascertained.<BR>	 2. Unaccomplished.<BR>	 3. Neg-<BR>lected.<BR> E. अ neg. प्रतिपन्न effected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=041-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतिभ|अप्रतिभः
अप्रतिभ mfn. (-भः-भा-भं)<BR>	 1. Modest, bashful.<BR>	 2. Confounded, perplexed.<BR>3. Unreflected, (as an image.)<BR> E. अ neg. प्रतिभा light, reflexion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=041-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतिम
अप्रतिम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं) Unequalled, incomparable.<BR> E. अ neg. प्रतिमा simi-<BR>litude.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=041-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतियत्न|अप्रतियत्नः
अप्रतियत्न m. (-त्नः) Natural or spontaneous state or condition.<BR> E. अ neg.<BR>प्रतियत्न fabrication.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=041-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतियत्नपूर्व्व|अप्रतियत्नपूर्व
अप्रतियत्नपूर्व्व mfn. (-र्व्वः-र्व्वा-र्व्वं) Natural, not made or artificial.<BR> E. अ neg.<BR>प्रतियत्न fabrication.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=041-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतिबन्ध|अप्रतिबंध
अप्रतिबन्ध mfn. (-न्धः-न्धा-न्धं)<BR>	 1. Unobstructed, undisputed.<BR>	 2. Absolute,<BR>direct, (as inheritance,) not collateral or presumptive.<BR> E. अ neg.<BR>प्रतिबन्ध obstacle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=041-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतिरथ|अप्रतिरथं|अप्रतिरथः
अप्रतिरथ n. (-थं)<BR>	 1. A march or procession.<BR>	 2. The Sāma Veda.<BR>	 3.<BR>Auspicious, well, right.<BR>	 m. (-थः) A warrior.<BR> E. अ neg. प्रति against,<BR>रथ a car.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=041-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतिरूप
अप्रतिरूप mfn. (-पः-पा-पी-पं) Unequalled, incomparable.<BR> E. अ neg. प्रति<BR>against, रूप kind, form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=041-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतिरूपकथा
अप्रतिरूपकथा f. (-था) Unanswerable or incomparable discourse.<BR> E. अप्रतिरूप,<BR>and कथा speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=041-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतिकारित
अप्रतिकारित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Unimpeded, unobstructed.<BR> E. अ neg. प्रतिकारित<BR>hindered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=041-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतिविधान
अप्रतिविधान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Natural, unartificial.<BR> E. अ neg. प्रतिविधान fabrica-<BR>tion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=041-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतिष्ठ|अप्रतिष्ठः
अप्रतिष्ठ mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठा-ष्ठं)<BR>	 1. Infamous, disreputable.<BR>	 2. Thrown away,<BR>unprofitable.<BR>	 3. Undecided, fluctuating.<BR> E. अ neg. प्रतिष्ठा credit, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=041-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतिष्ठित|अप्रतिष्ठितः
अप्रतिष्ठित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Unconsecrated.<BR>	 2. Obscure, uncelebrated.<BR>3. Unsettled, unfixed.<BR> E. अ neg. प्रतिष्ठित celebrated, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=041-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतिषिद्ध
अप्रतिषिद्ध mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं) Unprohibited, unforbidden.<BR> E. अ neg. प्रतिषिद्ध<BR>forbidden.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=041-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतिहत
अप्रतिहत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Unaffected, uninjured, unimpaired.<BR>	 2. Not<BR>disappointed.<BR>	 3. Unobstructed.<BR> E. अ neg. प्रतिहत hurt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=041-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतीकार
अप्रतीकार mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>	 1. Unresisting, defenceless.<BR>	 2. Irremediable.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Non-retaliation.<BR>	 2. Want of remedy or relief.<BR> E. अ neg.<BR>प्रतीकार counteracting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=041-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतीति|अप्रतीतिः
अप्रतीति f. (-तिः) Mistrust, want of confidence.<BR> E. अ neg. प्रतीति faith.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=041-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतुल|अप्रतुलं|अप्रतुलः
अप्रतुल m. (-लः) Necessity, want.<BR> E. अ neg. प्रतुल sufficiency.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=041-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रत्यक्ष|अप्रत्यक्षः
अप्रत्यक्ष mfn. (-क्षः-क्षा-क्षं) Invisible, imperceptible, not present.<BR> E. अ neg.<BR>प्रत्यक्ष present.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=041-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रत्यय|अप्रत्ययः
अप्रत्यय m. (-यः) Doubt, distrust, disbelief.<BR> E. अ neg. प्रत्यय trust.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=041-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रत्ययिन्
अप्रत्ययिन् mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि) Doubtful, mistrusting, sceptical.<BR> E. अप्रत्यय<BR>and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=041-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रत्याख्यात
अप्रत्याख्यात mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Assented to, uncontradicted, unrefuted.<BR> E. अ<BR>neg. प्रत्याख्यात denied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=041-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रत्याख्येय
अप्रत्याख्येय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Not to be contradicted, undeniable.<BR> E. अ neg.<BR>प्रत्याख्येय deniable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=041-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रथित
अप्रथित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Unpublished.<BR>	 2. Unnoted, unknown.<BR> E. अ neg.<BR>प्रथित celebrated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=041-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रधान|अप्रधानं
अप्रधान n. (-नं) Subordinate, secondary.<BR> E. अ neg. प्रधान principal: (al-<BR>ways neuter.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=041-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रधानता
अप्रधानता f. (-ता) Inferiority, subordination.<BR> E. तल् added to the last, also<BR>with त्व, अप्रधानत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=041-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रबल
अप्रबल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Weak, inefficacious.<BR> E. अ neg. प्रबल potent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=041-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रभ
अप्रभ mfn. (-भः-भा-भं)<BR>	 1. Dull, obscure.<BR>	 2. Mean.<BR> E. अ neg. प्रभा radiance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=041-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रभूत
अप्रभूत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Insufficient, inadequate.<BR> E. अ neg. प्र before भूत<BR>been.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=041-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रमत्त|अप्रमत्तः
अप्रमत्त mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं) Careful, attentive, vigilant.<BR> E. अ neg. प्रमत्त care-<BR>less.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=041-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रमाद|अप्रमादः
अप्रमाद m. (-दः) Care, vigilance.<BR> E. अ neg. प्रमाद carelessness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=041-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रमादिन्
अप्रमादिन् mfn. (-दी-दिनी-दि) Careful, cautious, steady.<BR> E. अप्रमाद and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=041-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रमित
अप्रमित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Unbounded, unmeasured.<BR> E. अ neg. प्रमित measured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=041-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रमेय
अप्रमेय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Unbounded, immeasurable.<BR> E. अ neg. प्रमेय measur-<BR>able.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=041-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रयत्न|अप्रयत्नः
अप्रयत्न m. (-त्नः) Indifference, laziness.<BR>	 mfn. (-त्नः-त्ना-त्नं) Indifferent, apathe-<BR>tic, making no effort.<BR> E. अ neg. प्रयत्न energy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=041-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रलम्ब|अप्रलंब|अप्रलम्बं
अप्रलम्ब mfn. (-म्बः-म्बा-म्बं) Quick, expeditious.<BR> E. अ neg. प्रलम्ब slow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=041-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रवर्त्तक|अप्रवर्तक
अप्रवर्त्तक mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>	 1. Abstaining from action, inert.<BR>	 2. Not ex-<BR>citing to action.<BR> E. अ neg. प्रवर्त्तक what excites.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=041-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रवर्त्तन|अप्रवर्तन|अप्रवर्तनं
अप्रवर्त्तन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Refraining from, not engaging in.<BR>	 2. Not exciting<BR>to.<BR> E. अ neg. प्र before वृत to be, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=041-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रवीण
अप्रवीण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Unskilful.<BR> E. अ neg. प्रवीण skilful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=041-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रवृत्ति|अप्रवृत्तिः
अप्रवृत्ति f. (-त्तिः)<BR>	 1. Abstaining from action, inertia.<BR>	 2. Non-excitement.<BR>3. (In Medicine) Suppression of the natural evacuations, constipa-<BR>tion, ischury, &c.<BR> E. अ neg. प्रवृत्ति active exertion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=041-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रशक्त
अप्रशक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं) Moderate, temperate.<BR> E. अ neg. प्रशक्त intent or<BR>fond of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=041-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रशक्ति
अप्रशक्ति f. (-क्तिः) Moderation.<BR>	 mfn. (-क्तिः-क्तिः-क्ति) Moderate, temperate. E.<BR>अ neg. प्रशक्ति addiction to any thing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=041-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रशस्त|अप्रशस्तं
अप्रशस्त mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं) Bad, worthless.<BR> E. अ neg. प्रशस्त excellent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=041-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रसन्न|अप्रसन्नं
अप्रसन्न mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>	 1. Turbid, muddy.<BR>	 2. Displeased, dissatisfied,<BR>unfavourable.<BR> E. अ neg. प्रसन्न pleased.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=041-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रसाद|अप्रसादः
अप्रसाद m. (-दः) Disfavour, disapprobation.<BR> E. अ neg. प्रसाद favour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=041-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रसाद्य
अप्रसाद्य mfn. (-द्यः-द्या-द्यं)<BR>	 1. Not to be propitiated.<BR>	 2. Unappeasable, im-<BR>placable.<BR> E. अ neg. प्र before षद to go, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=041-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रसिद्ध|अप्रसिद्धं
अप्रसिद्ध mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>	 1. Unusual, uncommon.<BR>	 2. Uncelebrated.<BR> E. अ<BR>neg. प्रसिद्ध famous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=041-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रसूत
अप्रसूत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Not having offspring, barren, childless.<BR> E. अ neg.<BR>प्रसूत bearing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=041-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रस्तुत|अप्रस्तुतं
अप्रस्तुत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Uncommenced, not begun.<BR>	 2. Unconnected<BR>with, unattached to.<BR>	 3. Uncommon, unusual.<BR>	 4. Unpraised, not<BR>celebrated.<BR>	 5. Confounded, not prompt.<BR> E. अ neg. प्र before ष्टु to<BR>praise, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=042-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रहत|अप्रहतं
अप्रहत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Unhurt, intact.<BR>	 2. Untilled, waste, fallow. E.<BR>अ neg. प्रहत broken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=042-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्राकृत
अप्राकृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Special, particular, not common or generic.<BR>	 2.<BR>Not vulgar, (especially as dialect or speech.)<BR> E. अ neg. प्राकृत<BR>common, vulgar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=042-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्राग्र्य|अप्राग्र्यं
अप्राग्र्य mfn. (ग्र्यः-ग्र्या-ग्र्यं) Secondary, subordinate.<BR> E. अ neg. प्राग्र्य principal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=042-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्राचीन|अप्राचीनं
अप्राचीन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Modern, recent.<BR> E. अ neg. प्राचीन old.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=042-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्राज्ञ
अप्राज्ञ mfn. (-ज्ञः-ज्ञा-ज्ञं)<BR>	 1. Unlearned, ignorant.<BR>	 2. Unconscious, unwit-<BR>ting.<BR> E. अ neg. प्राज्ञ who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=042-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्राज्ञता
अप्राज्ञता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Unconsciousness.<BR>	 2. Ignorance.<BR> E. तल् added to the<BR>last, also with त्व, अप्राज्ञत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=042-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्राण|अप्राणः
अप्राण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Lifeless, inanimate.<BR>	 m. (-णः) Death.<BR> E. अ neg.<BR>प्राण life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=042-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्राणिन्
अप्राणिन् mfn. (-णी-णिनी-णि) Lifeless, inanimate.<BR> E. अप्राण and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=042-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्राप्त|अप्राप्तः
अप्राप्त mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं)<BR>	 1. Unobtained.<BR>	 2. Unarrived.<BR> E. अ neg. प्राप्त ac-<BR>quired.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=042-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्राप्तकाल
अप्राप्तकाल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>	 1. Inopportune, out of season.<BR>	 2. Under age,<BR>E. अप्राप्त, and काल time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=042-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्राप्तव्यवहार
अप्राप्तव्यवहार m. (-रः) A minor.<BR>	 mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Under age, not of years<BR>to engage in law or public business.<BR> E. अ neg. प्राप्त attained, व्यवहार<BR>legal affairs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=042-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्राप्ति|अप्राप्तिः
अप्राप्ति f. (-प्तिः) Non-attainment, non-acquisition.<BR> E. अ neg. प्राप्ति acqui-<BR>sition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=042-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्राथ
अप्राथ mfn. (-थः-था-थं) Unobtainable, unattainable. ind. Not having<BR>obtained.<BR> E. अ neg. प्राथ future or past part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=042-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रामाणिक|अप्रामाणिकः
अप्रामाणिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Unauthentic, unauthoritative.<BR> E. अ neg.<BR>प्रामाणिक of authority.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=042-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रामाण्य|अप्रामाण्यं
अप्रामाण्य n. (-ण्यं) Absence, or insufficiency of proof or authority.<BR> E. अ<BR>neg. प्रामाण्य proof.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=042-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रावृत
अप्रावृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Uncovered, unclothed.<BR> E. अ neg. प्रावृत covered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=042-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रिय|अप्रियं|अप्रियः
अप्रिय mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>	 1. Disliked, disagreeable.<BR>	 2. Unkind, unfriendly.<BR>m. (-यः) A foe, an enemy.<BR>	 f. (-या) A sort of skeat fish, (Silurus<BR>pungentissimus.)<BR> E. अ neg. प्रिय beloved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=042-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रियकर
अप्रियकर mfn. (-रः-रा-री-रं)<BR>	 1. Unfriendly, ill-disposed.<BR>	 2. Disagreeable.<BR>E. अप्रिय, and कर what makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=042-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रियंवद
अप्रियंवद mfn. (-दः-दा-दं) One who speaks harshly or unkindly.<BR> E. अ<BR>neg. प्रियंवद kind spoken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=042-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रियवादिन्
अप्रियवादिन् mfn. (-दी-दिनी-दि) Speaking unkindly.<BR> E. अप्रिय, and वादिन्<BR>who speaks; also अप्रियभाषिन्, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=042-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रीति|अप्रीतिः
अप्रीति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Dislike, aversion.<BR>	 2. Unfriendliness, enmity.<BR> E. अ neg.<BR>प्रीति love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=042-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रीतिकर
अप्रीतिकर mfn. (-रः-रा-री-रं)<BR>	 1. Unkind, adverse.<BR>	 2. Disagreeable, offen-<BR>sive.<BR> E. अप्रीति and कर what makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=042-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रेमन्
अप्रेमन् n. (-म) Dislike, aversion.<BR> E. अ neg. प्रेमन् affection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=042-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रौढ
अप्रौढ mfn. (-ढः-ढा-ढं)<BR>	 1. Timid, gentle.<BR>	 2. Immature.<BR>	 f. (-ढा) An un-<BR>married girl, or one very recently married, and not come to woman-<BR>hood<BR> E. अ neg. प्रौढ arrogant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=042-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्सरस्
अप्सरस् f. plur. always (-राः) The nymphs of Svarga, attendants on INDRA.<BR>E. अप् water, सृ to go, and असि Unādi affix: or अप्स in the waters,<BR>and रस flavour: from their fondness for bathing, or from their<BR>being produced at the churning of the ocean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=042-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्सरा
अप्सरा f. (-रा) an Apsarā or heavenly nymph.<BR> E. अप् and सृ as before,<BR>with अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=042-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अफल|अफलः
अफल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>	 1. Unfruitful, barren.<BR>	 2. Vain, unproductive.<BR>	 f.<BR>(-ला)<BR>	 1. The aloe plant, (Aloes perfoliata.)<BR>	 2. Another plant,<BR>(Flacoartia cataphracta.)<BR> E. अ neg. फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=042-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अफलता
अफलता f. (-ता) Barrenness, unprofitableness.<BR> E. अफल with तल् affix; also<BR>अफलत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=042-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अफलाकाङ्क्षिन्|अफलाकांक्षिन्
अफलाकाङ्क्षिन् mfn. (-क्षी-क्षिणी-क्षि) Disinterested, indifferent, not looking<BR>to beneficial consequences.<BR> E. अ neg. फल fruit, and आकाङ्क्षिन् who<BR>desires.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=042-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अफल्गु
अफल्गु mfn. (-ल्गुः-ल्गुः-ल्गु) Productive, profitable.<BR> E. अ neg. फल्गु worthless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=042-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अफुल्ल
अफुल्ल mfn. (-ल्लः-ल्ला-ल्लं) Unblown.<BR> E. अ neg. फुल्ल flowered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=042-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अफेन|अफेनं
अफेन n. (-नं) Opium.<BR>	 mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Frothless, without scum or foam.<BR>E. अ dim. and फेन froth; the word in the first sense is, no doubt,<BR>of modern date and foreign introduction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=042-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अब
अब r. 1st cl. With an indicatory इ, अबि (अंबते) To sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=042-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबद्ध|अबद्धं|अबद्धः
अबद्ध mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं) Unmeaning or nonsensical discourse.<BR>	 2. Unbound,<BR>at liberty.<BR> E. अ neg. बद्ध bound, connected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=042-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबद्धक|अबद्धकं
अबद्धक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) See the preceding.<BR> E. वुन् being added, which<BR>leaves क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=042-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबद्धमुख|अबद्धमुखः
अबद्धमुख mfn. (-खः-खा-खं) Foul-mouthed, scurrilous.<BR> E. अबद्ध unbound, and<BR>मुख the mouth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=042-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबध
अबध m. (-धः) Not killing.<BR>	 f. (-धा) The segment of the base of a triangle.<BR>E. अ neg. बध what kills.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=042-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबध्य|अबध्यं
अबध्य mfn. (-ध्यः-ध्या-ध्यं)<BR>	 1. Unmeaning or nonsensical, (as discourse.)<BR>	 2.<BR>Sacred, not to be put to death.<BR> E. अ neg. बन्ध to bind, or बध to kill,<BR>and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=042-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबध्यभाव
अबध्यभाव m. (-वः) Immunity, sacredness of character, as that of an<BR>ambassador.<BR> E. अबध्य, and भाव quality.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=042-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबन्धुर
अबन्धुर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Unlovely, displeasing.<BR> E. अ neg. बन्धुर handsome.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=042-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबन्ध्य|अबन्ध्यः
अबन्ध्य mfn. (-न्ध्यः-न्ध्या-न्ध्यं) Fruitfull, productive.<BR> E. अ neg. and बन्ध्य bound,<BR>barren.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=042-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबल|अबलं|अबलः
अबल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Weak, feeble, infirm.<BR>	 m. (-लः) A plant (Tapia<BR>cratœva.) See वरुण.<BR>	 f. (-ला) A woman.<BR> E. अ neg. and बल strong.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=042-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबाध|अबाधं|अबाधः
अबाध mfn. (-धः-धा-धं)<BR>	 1. Unobstructed, unrestrained.<BR>	 2. Free from pain.<BR>f. (-धा)<BR>	 1. Segment of the base of a triangle.<BR>	 2. Indistinctness, per-<BR>plexity.<BR> E. अ neg. and बाध to oppose, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=042-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबाधक
अबाधक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Not obstructing or opposing.<BR> E. अ neg. बाधक<BR>what opposes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=042-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबाध्य
अबाध्य mfn. (-ध्यः-ध्या-ध्यं) Improper to be pained or opposed.<BR> E. अ neg. बाध<BR>to oppose, यत् part. affix, also with अनीयर् and तव्य, अबाधनीय and<BR>अबाधितव्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=042-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबान्धव|अबांधव
अबान्धव mfn. (-वः-वी-वं) Having no relation or kindred, lone, unacknow-<BR>ledged, unowned.<BR> E. अ neg. बन्धु kindred, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=042-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबुद्धि|अबुद्धिः
अबुद्धि f. (-द्धिः) Ignorance.<BR>	 mfn. (-द्धिः-द्धिः-द्धि) Ignorant, stupid.<BR> E. अ neg. बुद्धि<BR>understanding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=042-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबुद्धिमत्|अबुद्धिमन्त्
अबुद्धिमत् mfn. (-मान्-मती-मत्) Unwise, ignorant, foolish.<BR> E. अ neg. बुद्धिमत्<BR>wise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=042-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबुध
अबुध mfn. (-धः-धा-धं) Stupid, foolish, a fool.<BR> E. अ neg. बुध wise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=042-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबोध|अबोधः
अबोध m. (-धः) Ignorance, stupidity.<BR>	 mfn. (-धः-धा-धं)<BR>	 1. Ignorant, stupid.<BR>2. Puzzled, perplexed.<BR> E. अ neg. बोध knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=042-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबोधगम्य
अबोधगम्य mfn. (-म्यः-म्या-म्यं) Incomprehensible.<BR> E. अ neg. बोध knowledge,<BR>गम्य to be attained by.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=042-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबोधनीय
अबोधनीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>	 1. Unintelligible.<BR>	 2. Not to be awakened or<BR>aroused.<BR> E. अ neg. बोधनीय to be understood, &c. also अबोधितव्य and<BR>अबोध्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=042-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अब्ज|अब्जः
अब्ज m. (-ब्जः)<BR>	 1. The moon.<BR>	 2. A kind of tree, (Barringtonia acutangula.)<BR>3. The physician of the gods. See धन्वन्तरि.<BR>	 mn. (-ब्जः-ब्जं) A conch.<BR>	 n.<BR>(-ब्जं)<BR>	 1. A lotus.<BR>	 2. A large number, a million of millions.<BR> E. अब् for<BR>अप् water, and ज who is born; from the situation of the things<BR>named, or their production at the churning of the ocean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=042-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अब्जज|अब्जजः
अब्जज m. (-जः) A name of Brahma.<BR> E. अब्ज a lotus, and ज born; BRAHMĀ,<BR>being said to have sprung at the creation from the lotus, which<BR>arose from the navel of VIṢṆU.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=042-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अब्जनयन
अब्जनयन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Having fine eyes.<BR> E. अब्ज, and नयन the eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=042-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अब्जनेत्र
अब्जनेत्र mfn. (-त्रः-त्रा-त्रं) Having fine eyes.<BR> E. अब्ज and नेत्र eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=043-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अब्जदृश्
अब्जदृश् mfn. (-दृक्) Lotus-eyed, having large fine eyes.<BR> E. अब्ज, and दृश् eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=043-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अब्जभोग|अब्जभोगः
अब्जभोग m. (-गः) The root of a lotus.<BR> E. अब्ज, and भोग enjoyment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=043-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अब्जयोनि|अब्जयोनिः
अब्जयोनि m. (-निः) A name of BRAHMAN (m.).<BR> E. अब्ज, and योनि the vulva; see<BR>अब्जज.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=043-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अब्जवाहन|अब्जवाहनः
अब्जवाहन m. (-नः) A name of ŚIVA.<BR> E. अब्ज the moon, and वाहन a vehicle:<BR>carrying or wearing the moon on his forehead.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=043-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अब्जहस्त|अब्जहस्तः
अब्जहस्त m. (-स्तः) The sun.<BR> E. अब्ज a lotus, and हस्त a hand: SŪRYA is re-<BR>presented holding this flower in one hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=043-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अब्जिनी
अब्जिनी f. (-नी) A multitude of lotus flowers.<BR> E. अब्ज and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=043-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अब्जिनीपति|अब्जिनीपतिः
अब्जिनीपति m. (-तिः) The sun.<BR> E. अब्जिनी, and पति a lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=043-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अब्द|अब्दः
अब्द m. (-ब्दः)<BR>	 1. A cloud.<BR>	 2. A year.<BR>	 3. A fragrant grass, (Cyperus<BR>rotundus.)<BR>	 4. The name of a mountain.<BR> E. अप् water, प changed to<BR>ब, and द what gives; or अब to preserve, &c. and दन् Unādi affix;<BR>hence the word is also written अब्द.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=043-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अब्दशत
अब्दशत n. (-तं) A century.<BR> E. अब्द, and शत a hundred.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=043-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अब्दसहस्र
अब्दसहस्र n. (-स्रं) A thousand years.<BR> E. अब्द, सहस्र a thousand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=043-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अब्दार्द्ध
अब्दार्द्ध n. (-र्द्धं) A half year.<BR> E. अब्द, and अर्द्ध half.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=043-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अब्दिक
अब्दिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Annual, yearly.<BR> E. अब्द and ठन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=043-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अब्दुर्ग|अब्दुर्गः
अब्दुर्ग n. (-र्गं) A fortress surrounded by a moat or lake.<BR> E. अप् water, and<BR>दुर्ग fort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=043-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अब्धि|अब्धिः
अब्धि m. (-ब्धिः) The ocean.<BR> E. अब् substituted for अप् water; धि from धा<BR>to have, and कि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=043-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अब्धिकफ|अब्धिकफः
अब्धिकफ m. (-फः) Cuttlefish bone.<BR> E. अब्धि, and कफ phlegm; being<BR>considered as the froth of the sea.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=043-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अब्धिज|अब्धिजः
अब्धिज m. du. (-जौ) The two sons of SŪRYA, and physicians of Svarga.<BR>f. (-जा) Wine.<BR> E. अब्धि, and ज born: the former are more usually<BR>termed the sons of AŚVINĪ, see आश्विनेय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=043-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अब्धिद्वीपा
अब्धिद्वीपा f. (-पा) The earth.<BR> E. अब्धि, and द्वीप in the fem. form; an island<BR>surrounded by the ocean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=043-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अब्धिनगरी
अब्धिनगरी f. (-री) A name of Dvārakā, the capital of KṚṢṆA, see<BR>द्वारका.<BR> E. अब्धि, and नगरी a city: the ocean-city.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=043-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अब्धिनवनीतक|अब्धिनवनीतकः
अब्धिनवनीतक m. (-कः) The moon.<BR> E. अब्धि, नवनीत fresh butter and क affix;<BR>produced by churning the ocean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=043-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अब्धिमण्डूकी
अब्धिमण्डूकी f. (-की) A pearl oyster.<BR> E. अब्धि the ocean, and मण्डूकी a female<BR>frog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=043-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अब्धिशयन|अब्धिशयनः
अब्धिशयन m. (-नः) A name of VIṢṆU.<BR> E. अब्धि, and शयन sleeping;<BR>sleeping on the ocean at the periods of the destruction and renova-<BR>tion of the world, having the serpent ANANTA for his couch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=043-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अब्ध्यग्नि|अब्ध्यग्निः
अब्ध्यग्नि m. (-ग्निः) Submarine fire.<BR> E. अब्धि, and अग्नि fire. See और्व्वस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=043-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अब्भक्ष|अब्भक्षः
अब्भक्ष m. (-क्षः) A snake.<BR> E. अब् for अप् water, and भक्ष to eat: living<BR>upon water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=043-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अब्भ्र|अब्भ्रं
अब्भ्र m. (-ब्भ्रः) The ocean. See अभ्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=043-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अब्भ्रि|अब्भ्रिः
अब्भ्रि n. (-ब्भ्रि)<BR>	 1. A baling vessel.<BR>	 2. An iron hoe.<BR>	 3. A stick tipped or<BR>shod with iron. See अभ्रि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=043-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अब्रह्मचर्य्य|अब्रह्मचर्य
अब्रह्मचर्य्य n. (-र्य्यं)<BR>	 1. Incontinence.<BR>	 2. Coition.<BR> E. अ neg. and ब्रह्मचर्य्य the<BR>duty of the religious student, i. e. chastity; also with कन् added<BR>अब्रह्मचर्य्यक n. (-कं.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=043-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अब्रह्मण्य|अब्रह्मण्यं
अब्रह्मण्य n. (-ण्यं) Sacred, not to be killed, (in theatrical language.)<BR> E. अ<BR>not, ब्रह्मण्य proper for a Brahman, i. e. death; also अब्राह्मण्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=043-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ
अभ r. 1st cl. With an indicatory इ, अभि (अंभते) To sound, (not generally<BR>admitted.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=043-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभक्त
अभक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं) Not believing, not attached to.<BR> E. अ neg. भक्त<BR>attached.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=043-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभक्तच्छन्द
अभक्तच्छन्द m. (-न्दः) Want of appetite.<BR> E. अ neg. भक्त food, छन्द inclination.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=043-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभक्तरुच्
अभक्तरुच् f. (-रुक्) Want of appetite.<BR> E. अ neg. भक्त food, रुच् inclination.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=043-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभक्ति|अभक्तिः
अभक्ति f. (-क्तिः) Incredulity, unbelief, want of devotion to.<BR> E. अ neg. भक्ति<BR>faith.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=043-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभक्तिमत्
अभक्तिमत् mfn. (-मान्-मती-मत्) Unbelieving, undevoted to.<BR> E. अ neg. भक्तिमत्<BR>believing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=043-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभक्षण|अभक्षणं
अभक्षण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Abstaining from, not eating any thing.<BR>	 2. Fasting. E.<BR>अ neg. भक्षण eating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=043-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभक्ष्य|अभक्ष्यं
अभक्ष्य mfn. (-क्ष्यः-क्ष्या-क्ष्यं) Not to be eaten.<BR> E. अ neg. भक्ष्य to be eaten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=043-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभक्ष्यत्व
अभक्ष्यत्व n. (-त्वं) Unfitness as food.<BR> E. अभक्ष्य and त्व affix; also अभक्ष्यता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=043-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभग्न
अभग्न mfn. (-ग्नः-ग्ना-ग्नं) Entire, unbroken.<BR>	 2. Uninturrupted.<BR> E. अ neg.<BR>भग्न broken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=043-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभङ्गुर|अभंगुर
अभङ्गुर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>	 1. Unbroken, entire.<BR>	 2. Undisturbed, un-<BR>interrupted.<BR> E. अ neg. भङ्गुर what breaks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=043-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभय|अभयं|अभयः
अभय n. (-यं)<BR>	 1. Absence or removal of fear.<BR>	 2. The root of a fragrant<BR>grass, (Andropogon muricatum.)<BR>	 f. (-या) Yellow myrobalan,<BR>(Terminalia citrina.)<BR>	 mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Fearless, undaunted.<BR> E. अ neg.<BR>and भय fear; the plant removing the dread of disease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=043-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभयडिण्डिम|अभयडिंडिम|अभयडिण्डिमः
अभयडिण्डिम m. (-मः) A war-drum.<BR> E. अभय, and डिण्डिम a drum: inspiring<BR>courage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=043-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभयद|अभयदः
अभयद m. (-दः) A protector, a defender.<BR>	 mfn. (-दः-दा-दं) Removing fear<BR>or danger.<BR> E. अभय fearlessness, द who gives; also with प्र prefix<BR>अभयप्रद.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=043-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभयदक्षिणा
अभयदक्षिणा f. (-णा) Promise or present of protection from danger. E.<BR>अभय, and दक्षिणा a gift to a Brahman, which, in this case he may<BR>receive from even a Śūdra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=043-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभयदान
अभयदान n. (-नं) Assurance of safety or protection.<BR> E. अभय and दान gift.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=043-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभयप्रद
अभयप्रद mfn. (-दः-दा-दं) One who grants safety.<BR> E. अभय fearlessness. प्रद<BR>who gives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=043-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभयप्रदान
अभयप्रदान n. (-नं) Assurance of safety or protection.<BR> E. अभय, and प्रदान<BR>giving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=043-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभयवाच्
अभयवाच् f. (-वाक्) Assurance of safety, encouragement.<BR> E. अभय, and वाच्<BR>speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=043-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभव|अभवः
अभव m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. End of the world, liberation from the world.<BR>	 2. Non-<BR>existence.<BR>	 mfn. (-वः-वा-वं) Nonexistent.<BR> E. अ neg. भव being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=043-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभवितव्य
अभवितव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं) What is not to be, what will not be.<BR> E. अ<BR>neg. भवितव्य to be.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=043-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभवितव्यता
अभवितव्यता f. (-ता) Fate, predestined non-occurrence.<BR> E. अ neg. भवितव्य<BR>what is to be, तल् affix; also अभवितव्यत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=043-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभव्य
अभव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>	 1. Not to be, not predestined.<BR>	 2. Improper, what<BR>ought not to be.<BR> E. अ neg. भव्य what is to be, also अभवनीय, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=043-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभाग
अभाग mfn. (-गः-गा-गं) Not sharing or dividing.<BR> E. अ neg. भाग a share.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=043-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभाग्य
अभाग्य mfn. (-ग्यः-ग्या-ग्यं) Unfortunate, wretched.<BR> E. अ neg. भाग्य fortunate.<BR>So अभाग्यवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=043-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभाव|अभावः
अभाव m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. Nonexistence, annihilation.<BR>	 2. Death.<BR>	 3. (In logic)<BR>Negation of two kinds, संसर्गाभाव universal negation, and अन्योन्याभाव<BR>relative or mutual negation.<BR>	 4. (In rhetoric) Absence of the essen-<BR>tial parts of poetical description of character, want of the pro-<BR>perties or temperaments.<BR> E. अ priv. भाव being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=043-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभावना
अभावना f. (-ना)<BR>	 1. Absence of judgement or right perception.<BR>	 2. Ab-<BR>sence of religious meditation or contemplation.<BR> E. अ neg. भावना<BR>perceiving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=043-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभावनीय|अभावनीयः
अभावनीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Not to be contemplated or inferred, uninfer-<BR>rible, inconceivable, unintelligible.<BR> E. अ neg. भावनीय to be perceived.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=043-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभाविन्
अभाविन् mfn. (-वी-विनी-वि)<BR>	 1. What is not to be, what will not be.<BR>	 2.<BR>Void of temperament or natural disposition.<BR> E. अ neg. भाविन् future,<BR>or having disposition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=043-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभाषण|अभाषणं
अभाषण n. (-णं) Silence.<BR> E. अ neg. and भाषण speaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=043-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभि
अभि ind. A preposition and particle implying.<BR>	 1. Superiority in place,<BR>rank, or power, (over, upon, against, above:)<BR>	 2. Proximity,<BR>(near:)<BR>	 3. Separation, (severally:)<BR>	 4. Wish, desire: 5. Conjunction,<BR>particularizing, (to, with respect to.) Thus अभिक्रमितुं to overpower;<BR>अभिगन्तुं to approach; अभिख्यातुं to speak to; अभिभव disgrace; अभिलाष<BR>desire; अभ्यग्निं on the fire, &c.<BR> E. अ neg. भा to shine, and कि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=043-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिक|अभिकः
अभिक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Lustful, libidinous.<BR> E. अभि and क from कम to<BR>desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=043-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिकाङ्क्षा|अभिकांक्षा
अभिकाङ्क्षा f. (-ङ्क्षा) Wish, desire.<BR> E. अभि, and काङ्क्षा desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=044-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिकाङ्क्षित
अभिकाङ्क्षित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Wished, desired.<BR> E. अभि and काङ्क्षित.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=044-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिकाङ्क्षिन्|अभिकांक्षिन्
अभिकाङ्क्षिन् mfn. (-क्षी-क्षिणी-क्षि) Wishing, desirous.<BR> E. अभि, and काङ्क्षिन्<BR>who wishes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=044-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिक्रम|अभिक्रमः
अभिक्रम m. (-मः) Assault, attack, invasion.<BR>	 2. Mounting, ascending. E.<BR>अभि before or beyond, क्रम to go, and घञ् affix, see अतिक्रम.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=044-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिख्या
अभिख्या f. (-ख्या)<BR>	 1. A name or appellation.<BR>	 2. Calling, addressing.<BR>	 3.<BR>Beauty.<BR>	 4. Fame, glory.<BR> E. अभि, ख्या to speak, अङ् affix, and टाप्<BR>fem. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=044-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिगत
अभिगत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Approached.<BR> E. अभि near to, गत gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=044-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिगम|अभिगमः
अभिगम m. (-मः) Approach, proximity.<BR> E. अभि to, गम going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=044-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिगमन|अभिगमनं
अभिगमन n. (-नं) Approaching, going near to.<BR> E. अभि, and गमन going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=044-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिगामिन्
अभिगामिन् mfn. (-मी-मिनी-मि) Approaching.<BR> E. अभि, and गामिन् who<BR>goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=044-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिग्रस्त|अभिग्रस्तः
अभिग्रस्त mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं) Overcome, subdued.<BR> E. अभि and ग्रस्त seized.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=044-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिग्रह|अभिग्रहः
अभिग्रह m. (-हः)<BR>	 1. Attack, onset.<BR>	 2. Challenge, going to fight.<BR>	 3. Plun-<BR>dering, robbing.<BR>	 4. Celebrity.<BR> E. अभि before, in presence of, ग्रह<BR>to take, and अप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=044-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिग्रहण|अभिग्रहणं
अभिग्रहण n. (-णं) Robbing, seizing any thing in presence of the owner.<BR>E. अभि before ग्रह to take, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=044-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिघर्षण|अभिघर्षणं
अभिघर्षण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Rubbing, friction.<BR>	 2. Possession by an evil spirit.<BR>E. अभि before घृष to pound, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=044-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिघात|अभिघातः
अभिघात m. (-तः)<BR>	 1. Striking, wounding, beating.<BR>	 2. Touching, contact.<BR>3. Pain, infliction, torture.<BR>	 4. Remedy, removal.<BR>	 n. (-तं) The<BR>combination of the fourth letter of any class with any of the other<BR>three preceding it.<BR> E. अभि before हन to strike, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=044-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिघातिन्
अभिघातिन् m. (-ती) An enemy.<BR>	 mfn. (-ती-तिनी-ति)<BR>	 1. Hostile, an assail-<BR>ant.<BR>	 2. Inflicting injury.<BR>	 3. Remedial.<BR> E. अभि before हन to strike<BR>or kill, and णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=044-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिघार|अभिघारः
अभिघार m. (-रः) Ghee or clarified butter.<BR> E. अभि, घृ to scatter, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=044-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिचर|अभिचरः
अभिचर m. (-रः) A servant.<BR> E. अभि after, and चर who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=044-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिचार|अभिचारः
अभिचार m. (-रः) Magic for a malevolent purpose, the spells and<BR>diagrams of the Atharva Veda and some of the Tantras, supposed<BR>to produce mental aberration, love, hatred, loss of feeling or<BR>paralysis, and death.<BR> E. अभि before चर to go, and घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=044-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिचारमन्त्र|अभिचारमन्त्रः
अभिचारमन्त्र m. (-न्त्रः) A formula or prayer for working a charm, an incan-<BR>tation.<BR> E. अभिचार, and मन्त्र a formula.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=044-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिचारिक
अभिचारिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Magical, magician, relating to spells or<BR>magic.<BR> E. अभिचार and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=044-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिचारित
अभिचारित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Inchanted, charmed.<BR> E. अभिचार and क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=044-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिचारिन्
अभिचारिन् mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>	 1. Magical, done by magic.<BR>	 2. Magician or<BR>one employing spells, a conjuror, a witch, &c.<BR> E. अभिचार, and इनि<BR>aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=044-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिचैद्य
अभिचैद्य m. (-द्यः) A name of ŚIŚUPĀLA.<BR> E. अभि over, चैद्य the people of<BR>Cedi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=044-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिजन|अभिजनः
अभिजन m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. Family, race.<BR>	 2. Native country.<BR>	 3. The head, or or-<BR>nament of a family.<BR>	 4. Fame, notoriety.<BR> E. अभि before जन who is<BR>born, from जन to be born, घञ् affix, the vowel remaining short.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=044-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिजात|अभिजातः
अभिजात mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Noble, well born.<BR>	 2. Wise, learned.<BR>	 3. Fit,<BR>proper.<BR>	 4. Handsome.<BR>	 5. Respectable.<BR> E. अभि before जात produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=044-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिजित्
अभिजित् f. (-जित्)<BR>	 1. One of the Nakshatras or lunar asterisms.<BR>	 2. The<BR>eighth muhurta or hour.<BR>	 3. An expiatory sacrifice.<BR> E. अभि, and जित्<BR>what conquers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=044-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिज्ञ|अभिज्ञः
अभिज्ञ mfn. (-ज्ञः-ज्ञा-ज्ञं)<BR>	 1. Skilful, clever.<BR>	 2. One who knows or under-<BR>stands.<BR> E. अभि, and ज्ञ who knows, from ज्ञा to know, क affix leaving<BR>अ; आ is dropped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=044-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिज्ञात
अभिज्ञात mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Known, understood.<BR>	 2. Detected, discovered.<BR>E. अभि, and ज्ञात known.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=044-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिज्ञान|अभिज्ञानं
अभिज्ञान n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. A mark, a spot or stain.<BR>	 2. A sign, a token.<BR>	 3.<BR>Ascertaining, knowledge.<BR> E. अभि before ज्ञा to know, and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=044-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभितप्त
अभितप्त mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं)<BR>	 1. Scorched, burnt.<BR>	 2. Afflicted.<BR> E. अभि, and तप्त<BR>burnt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=044-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभितस्
अभितस् ind.<BR>	 1. Quickly.<BR>	 2. Entirely.<BR>	 3. Before, in presence of.<BR>	 4. On<BR>both sides.<BR>	 5. Near.<BR> E. अभि and तसिल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=044-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिताप|अभितापः
अभिताप m. (-पः)<BR>	 1. Extreme heat.<BR>	 2. Agitation, affliction, emotion. E.<BR>अभि, and ताप heat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=044-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिद्रोह|अभिद्रोहः
अभिद्रोह m. (-हः)<BR>	 1. Oppression, cruelty.<BR>	 2. Abuse.<BR> E. अभि, and द्रोह<BR>violence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=044-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिधा
अभिधा f. (-धा)<BR>	 1. A name, an appellation.<BR>	 2. (In logic,) the power or<BR>sense of a word.<BR>	 3. The chief or common acceptation of a word. E.<BR>अभि before धा to have, क affix and टाप् fem.: what any thing is ob-<BR>tained by.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=044-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिधान|अभिधानं
अभिधान n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. A name, an appellation.<BR>	 2. Speaking, speech.<BR>	 3. A vo-<BR>cabulary, a dictionary. E. As before, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=044-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिधायिक
अभिधायिक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Denominative, relating to.<BR> E. अभिधायिन् with<BR>कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=044-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिधायिन्
अभिधायिन् mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि) Denominative, appellative.<BR> E. अभि before धा<BR>to have, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=044-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिधावन|अभिधावनं
अभिधावन n. (-नं) Pursuit, chase.<BR> E. अभि, and धावन running.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=044-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिधित्सा
अभिधित्सा f. (-त्सा)<BR>	 1. Direction, injunction.<BR>	 2. Desire, wish.<BR> E. अभि before<BR>धा to have, desiderative form, क and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=044-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिधेय|अभिधेयं
अभिधेय n. (-यं)<BR>	 1. A name or appellation.<BR>	 2. A significant word.<BR>	 mfn.<BR>(-यः-या-यं) To be named or mentioned.<BR> E. अभि before धा, and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=044-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिधेयरहित
अभिधेयरहित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Unmeaning, nonsensical, having no sense nor<BR>meaning.<BR> E. अभिधेय, and रहित void of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=044-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिध्या
अभिध्या f. (-ध्या)<BR>	 1. Coveting another's property.<BR>	 2. Desire, longing for in<BR>general.<BR> E. अभि, ध्यै to think, and अङ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=044-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिध्यान|अभिध्यानं
अभिध्यान n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Coveting, desiring, longing for.<BR>	 2. Meditation, profound<BR>thought.<BR> E. अभि before ध्यै to think of, ल्युट् affix, or ध्यान contempla-<BR>tion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=044-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनद्ध
अभिनद्ध mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं) Bound, tied round, fastened on or upon.<BR> E. अभि<BR>over, नद्ध tied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=044-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनन्दन|अभिनंदनं|अभिनन्दनः
अभिनन्दन m. (-नः) The fourth Jaina Tīrthakara or deified saint.<BR>	 n. (-नं)<BR>Delighting, rejoicing.<BR> E. अभि before नदि to please, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=044-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनन्दा
अभिनन्दा f. (-न्दा) Wish, expectation.<BR> E. अभि and नदि to please, affix अच्<BR>and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=044-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनन्दित
अभिनन्दित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Delighted, made happy.<BR> E. अभि and नन्दित<BR>pleased.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=044-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनय|अभिनयः
अभिनय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. Indication of a passion or purpose by look, gesture,<BR>&c.<BR>	 2. Acting, dramatic personification.<BR>	 3. Ornament, decoration.<BR>	 4.<BR>Civility, kindness.<BR> E. अभि, नीञ् to guide, and अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=044-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनव|अभिनवः
अभिनव mfn. (-वः-वा-वं)<BR>	 1. New.<BR>	 2. Young.<BR> E. अभि before नव new.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=044-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनवोद्भिद्
अभिनवोद्भिद् m. (-द् or -त्) A germin, a new bud.<BR> E. अभिनव new, and उद्भिद्<BR>produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=044-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनिर्म्मुक्त|अभिनिर्मुक्त|अभिनिर्मुक्तः
अभिनिर्म्मुक्त m. (-क्तः) One asleep at sunset.<BR>	 mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं) Left, quitted.<BR>E. अभि always, निर्म्मुक्त released.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=044-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनिर्याण|अभिनिर्याणं|अभिनिर्य्याण
अभिनिर्याण n. (-णं) Invasion, march of an assailant, or march in general.<BR>E. अभि, and निर् prefixed to या to go, and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=044-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनिर्वृत्ति|अभिनिर्वृत्तिः
अभिनिर्वृत्ति f. (-त्तिः) Accession of disease.<BR> E. अभि, and निर्वृत्ति inaction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=044-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनिविष्ट
अभिनिविष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>	 1. Conversant or familiar with, studied in.<BR>2. Attentive, engrossed.<BR> E. अभि, and निविष्ट entered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=044-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनिवेश|अभिनिवेशः
अभिनिवेश m. (-शः)<BR>	 1. Intentness, application, perseverance, determina-<BR>tion to effect a purpose, or attain an object.<BR>	 2. Tenacity.<BR>	 3. Study.<BR>4. Ignorant fear causing death.<BR> E. अभि and नि before विश to enter,<BR>घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=044-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनिष्क्रमण|अभिनिष्क्रमणं
अभिनिष्क्रमण n. (-णं) Going forth or out, issuing, exit.<BR> E. अभि and निर्<BR>before क्रम to go, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=044-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनिष्क्रान्त
अभिनिष्क्रान्त mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं) Gone out or forth.<BR> E. अभि, and निष्क्रान्त gone out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=044-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनिष्पतन|अभिनिष्पतनं
अभिनिष्पतन n. (-नं) Sallying, issuing, going forth.<BR> E. अभि before निष्पतन<BR>going out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=044-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनिष्पत्ति|अभिनिष्पत्तिः
अभिनिष्पत्ति f. (-त्तिः) End, termination.<BR> E. अभि, and निष्पत्ति discontinuance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=045-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनिष्पन्न
अभिनिष्पन्न mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं) Finished, completed.<BR> E. अभि, and निष्पन्न done,<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=045-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनिष्ठान|अभिनिष्ठानः
अभिनिष्ठान m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. The soft aspirate.<BR>	 2. A letter of the alphabet. E.<BR>अभि and नि before ष्ठा to stay or stand, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=045-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनीत|अभिनीतः
अभिनीत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Fit, proper.<BR>	 2. Friendly, kind.<BR>	 3. Highly<BR>finished, or ornamented.<BR>	 4. Patient.<BR>	 5. Impatient.<BR>	 6. Passionate. E.<BR>अभि and नीञ् to guide or obtain, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=045-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनीति|अभिनीतिः
अभिनीति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Friendship, civility, kindness.<BR>	 2. Gesture,<BR>expressive gesticulation.<BR> E. अभि, and नीति conduct.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=045-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनेय
अभिनेय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) To be represented dramatically.<BR> E. अभि before नी<BR>to guide, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=045-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनेतृ
अभिनेतृ mf. (-ता-त्री) An actor, an actress.<BR> E. अभि before नी to guide, तृच्<BR>aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=045-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिन्न
अभिन्न mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>	 1. Same, identical.<BR>	 2. One, undivided.<BR>	 3.<BR>Unchanged, unaltered.<BR>	 4. Uncut, unbroken.<BR>	 m. (-न्नः) An integer,<BR>a whole number.<BR> E. अ neg. भिन्न other.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=045-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिन्नता
अभिन्नता f. (-ता) Identity, wholeness.<BR> E. तल् added to the last, or with<BR>त्व, अभिन्नत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=045-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिपन्न|अभिपन्नः
अभिपन्न mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>	 1. Guilty.<BR>	 2. Unfortunate, calamitous.<BR>	 3. Sub-<BR>dued.<BR>	 4. Flown, fugitive.<BR>	 5. Seeking refuge.<BR> E. अभि before पद to go,<BR>in the part. past.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=045-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिप्रणय|अभिप्रणयः
अभिप्रणय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. Propitiation.<BR>	 2. Affection, favour.<BR> E. अभि and प्र be-<BR>fore णी, affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=045-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिप्रणीत
अभिप्रणीत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Invoked, propitiated.<BR>	 2. Consecrated.<BR>	 3.<BR>Brought, attracted.<BR> E. अभि and प्र before णी to conduct, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=045-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिप्राय|अभिप्रायः
अभिप्राय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. Meaning, intention, wish, purpose.<BR>	 2. Meaning, a<BR>sentence, sense.<BR>	 3. The main purport of a book.<BR> E. अभि, and प्रिञ् to<BR>satisfy, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=045-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिप्रेत|अभिप्रेतं
अभिप्रेत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Meant, intended.<BR>	 2. Wished.<BR>	 3. Wishing,<BR>desirous, ambitious of, pretending to.<BR> E. अभि, and प्र before इण to go,<BR>क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=045-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिप्रेत्य
अभिप्रेत्य ind. Intending, meaning.<BR> E. अभि and प्र before इण to go, क्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=045-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिप्रोक्षण|अभिप्रोक्षणं
अभिप्रोक्षण n. (-णं) Sprinkling, affusion.<BR> E. अभि and प्रोक्षण sprinkling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=045-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिप्लुत
अभिप्लुत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Overflowed, overrun, filled with.<BR>	 2. Attacked<BR>or affected by, labouring under.<BR> E. अभि before प्लु to go, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=045-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिभव|अभिभवः
अभिभव m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. Defeat, subjugation.<BR>	 2. Humiliation, disgrace.<BR> E. अभि<BR>implying inferiority, and भव being; from भू to be, and अप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=045-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिभवन|अभिभवनं
अभिभवन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Overpowering, overcoming.<BR>	 2. Being overpowered.<BR>E. अभि, भू to be, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=045-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिभूत|अभिभूतः
अभिभूत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Humbled, surpassed, defeated, subdued.<BR>	 2.<BR>Ignorant.<BR>	 3. Overcome with feelings or wants, with passion, with<BR>hunger, &c.<BR>	 4. Injured, aggrieved.<BR> E. अभि, and भूत been, being; part.<BR>past.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=045-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिभूति|अभिभूतिः
अभिभूति f. (-तिः) Disrespect, disgrace, humiliation.<BR> E. अभि before भू to be,<BR>and क्तिन् fem. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=045-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमत|अभिमतं|अभिमतः
अभिमत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Wished, desired.<BR>	 2. Agreed, accepted.<BR>	 3. Ad-<BR>mitted, assented to.<BR> E. अभि over, मत thought.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=045-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमतता
अभिमतता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Desire, love.<BR>	 2. Agreeableness, desirableness.<BR> E. तल्<BR>added to the preceding; also with त्व, अभिमतत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=045-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमन्त्रण|अभिमंत्रणं|अभिमन्त्रणं
अभिमन्त्रण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Calling to, addressing, inviting.<BR>	 2. Counselling.<BR>	 3.<BR>Consecrating any thing by a special formula.<BR> E. अभि in presence,<BR>मन्त्र to speak, and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=045-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमन्त्रित
अभिमन्त्रित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Charmed, consecrated, had a certain formula<BR>pronounced over it.<BR> E. अभि, मन्त्र to charm, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=045-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमन्तृ|अभिमंतृ
अभिमन्तृ m. (न्ता)<BR>	 1. A counsellor, a monitor.<BR>	 2. Conscience.<BR>	 mfn.<BR>(-न्ता-न्त्री-न्तृ) Who or what admonished or advices.<BR> E. अभि, and मन to<BR>mind, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=045-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमन्थ|अभिमंथः|अभिमन्थः
अभिमन्थ m. (-न्थः) Ophthalmia, disease of the eyes.<BR> E. अभि, and मन्थ to<BR>agitate, घञ् affix; also read अधिमन्थः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=045-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमन्यु|अभिमन्युः
अभिमन्यु m. (-न्युः) The son of ARJUNA by SUBHADRĀ.<BR> E. अभि and मन wrath.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=045-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमर|अभिमरः
अभिमर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Killing, slaughter.<BR>	 2. War, combat.<BR>	 3. Binding, con-<BR>finement.<BR>	 4. Treachery, danger from one's own party or friends.<BR>E. अभि before मर from मृ to die, and अप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=045-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमर्द्द|अभिमर्द|अभिमर्दः|अभिमर्द्दः
अभिमर्द्द m. (-र्द्दः)<BR>	 1. Rubbing, friction.<BR>	 2. Devastation of a country, &c.<BR>by an enemy.<BR>	 3. War, battle.<BR> E. अभि, and मृद् to tread down, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=045-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमर्शन|अभिमर्शनं
अभिमर्शन n. (-नं) Touching, rubbing.<BR> E. अभि before मृश to rub, with ल्युट्<BR>aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=045-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमर्षण|अभिमर्षणं
अभिमर्षण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Sprinkling upon or over.<BR>	 2. Licking the lips as an<BR>indication of guilt or prevarication.<BR> E. अभि, and मृष to sprinkle,<BR>ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=045-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमाति|अभिमातिः
अभिमाति m. (-तिः) An enemy.<BR> E. अभि against, and मा to measure, क्तिन्<BR>aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=045-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमान|अभिमानः
अभिमान m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. Pride, haughtiness.<BR>	 2. Knowledge.<BR>	 3. Affection.<BR>	 4.<BR>Injury, hurting, killing.<BR>	 5. Requesting.<BR> E. अभि, and मन to know,<BR>with घञ् affix, or मी to injure, and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=045-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमानता
अभिमानता f. (-ता) Pride, arrogance.<BR> E. तल् added to the last: also<BR>अभिमानत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=045-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमानवत्|अभिमानवन्त्
अभिमानवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Proud, arrogant.<BR>	 f. (-ती) pride.<BR> E. मतुप् poss.<BR>affix; added to अभिमान.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=045-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमानित|अभिमानितं
अभिमानित n. (-तं) Copulation.<BR> E. अभि, and मन to know, in the causal form,<BR>and क्त aff.<BR>	 f. (-ता) Pride, arrogance.<BR> E. अभिमानिन्, and तल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=045-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमानिन्
अभिमानिन् mfn. (-नी-निनी-नि) Proud, arrogant.<BR> E. अभिमान and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=045-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमाय|अभिमायः
अभिमाय mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>	 1. Subdued, reduced, broken or worn down.<BR>	 2.<BR>Stupid, ignorant.<BR> E. अभि before माया ignorance, illusion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=045-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमुख|अभिमुखं|अभिमुखः
अभिमुख mfn. (-खः-खा-खी-खं)<BR>	 1. Present.<BR>	 2. Near to, in front of.<BR>	 n. adv.<BR>(-खं) In front or presence of.<BR> E. अभि before, and मुख the face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=045-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमुखता
अभिमुखता f. (-ता) Presence, proximity.<BR> E. अभिमुख, and तल् affix or with<BR>त्व, अभिमुखत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=045-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमृष्ट
अभिमृष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं) Touched, rubbed, brought or passed close. E.<BR>अभि, and मृष्ट rubbed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=045-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभियाति|अभियातिः
अभियाति m. (-तिः) An enemy.<BR> E. अभि against, या to go, with अति affix,<BR>see अभियातिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=045-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभियातिन्
अभियातिन् m. (-ती) An enemy.<BR> E. अभि against, यत् to strive, and णिनि affix,<BR>see अभिघातिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=045-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभियुक्त|अभियुक्तः
अभियुक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं) Attacked by an enemy, assaulted, assailed.<BR>	 2.<BR>Diligent, intent.<BR>	 3. Said, spoken.<BR>	 4. Blamed, rebuked.<BR>	 5. (In law)<BR>Charged, prosecuted, defendant.<BR> E. अभि, and युक्त joined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=045-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभियुक्तता
अभियुक्तता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Diligence, application.<BR>	 2. Accusation, prosecution.<BR>E. अभियुक्त and तल् affix, also with त्व, अभियुक्तत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=045-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभियोक्तव्य
अभियोक्तव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>	 1. Blamable, to be reproved or rebuked.<BR>2. To be prevented or prohibited.<BR>	 3. To be prosecuted, indictable.<BR>4. To be pursued diligently.<BR> E. अभि before युज to join, तव्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=045-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभियोक्तृ
अभियोक्तृ m. (-क्ता) A plaintiff, an accuser.<BR>	 mfn. (-क्ता-क्त्री-क्तृ) One who<BR>assails another in any way.<BR> E. अभि before युज to join, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=045-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभियोग|अभियोगः
अभियोग m. (-गः)<BR>	 1. Attack, assault.<BR>	 2. Challenging to fight.<BR>	 3. War,<BR>battle.<BR>	 4. Energetic effort, exertion, perseverance.<BR>	 5. Reprimand,<BR>reproof.<BR>	 6. Prohibition, prevention.<BR>	 7. Contact, conjunction.<BR>	 8. (In<BR>law) A plaint, a charge, an accusation.<BR> E. अभि, युज to join, and<BR>घञ् affix, ज being changed to ग.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=045-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभियोगिन्
अभियोगिन् m. (-गी) A plaintiff, a prosecutor.<BR>	 mfn. (-गी-गिनी-गि) One who<BR>assails another in any way.<BR> E. अभियोग and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=045-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिरक्षा
अभिरक्षा f. (-क्षा) Universal protection, wide benevolence.<BR> E. अभि, and रक्षा<BR>preserving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=045-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिरक्षित
अभिरक्षित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Guarded, preserved, kept.<BR> E. अभि, and रक्षित<BR>preserved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=045-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिरक्षितृ
अभिरक्षितृ m. (-ता)<BR>	 1. A guardian.<BR>	 2. A controller.<BR>	 mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ) Who<BR>or what keeps or preserves.<BR> E. अभि, रक्षितृ who preserves.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=045-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिरत
अभिरत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Pleased or contended with, satisfied.<BR>	 2. Per-<BR>forming, practicing, engaged in, attentive to.<BR> E. अभिरम to sport,<BR>क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=045-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिरति|अभिरतिः
अभिरति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Pleasure, delight.<BR>	 2. Practice, occupation.<BR> E. अभि,<BR>and रति pleasure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=046-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिराद्ध
अभिराद्ध mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं) Propitiated, (by penance, &c.)<BR> E. अभि, and राद्ध<BR>accomplished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=046-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिराम|अभिरामः
अभिराम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं) Beautiful.<BR> E. अभि before रम to sport, and घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=046-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिरामता
अभिरामता f. (-ता) Beauty, splendour.<BR> E. तल् added to the last: also<BR>अभिरामत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=046-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिरुचि|अभिरुचिः
अभिरुचि f. (-चिः)<BR>	 1. Ambition, desire of fame.<BR>	 2. Desire in general.<BR>	 3.<BR>Taste, relish.<BR>	 4. Splendour.<BR> E. अभि, and रुचि light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=046-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिरूप|अभिरूपः
अभिरूप m. (-पः)<BR>	 1. A learned Brahman, a Pandit.<BR>	 2. A name of KĀMA.<BR>3. Of the moon.<BR>	 4. Of ŚIVA.<BR>	 5. Also of VIṢṆU.<BR>	 mfn. (-पः-पा-पी-पं)<BR>1. Learned.<BR>	 2. Pleasing.<BR>	 3. Handsome.<BR> E. अभि before रूप to have<BR>form, affix क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=046-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिलषणीय
अभिलषणीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Desirable.<BR> E. अभि before लष to wish, अनीयर्<BR>aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=046-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिलषित
अभिलषित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Desired, wished.<BR>	 n. (-तं) Desire.<BR> E. अभि before<BR>लष with क्त part. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=046-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिलाप|अभिलापः
अभिलाप m. (-पः)<BR>	 1. Speech, speaking.<BR>	 2. Declaration of the object of a<BR>vow or religious obligation.<BR> E. अभि before लप to speak, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=046-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिलाव|अभिलावः
अभिलाव m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. Reaping.<BR>	 2. Cutting.<BR> E. अभि, and लूञ to cut, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=046-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिलाष|अभिलाषः
अभिलाष m. (-षः) Wish, desire.<BR> E. अभि, and लष् to like, घञ् aff.; also<BR>अभिलास.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=046-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिलाषिन्
अभिलाषिन् mfn. (-षी-षिणी-षि) Wishing, desiring.<BR> E. अभिलाष and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=046-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिलाषुक|अभिलाषुकः
अभिलाषुक mfn. (-कः-का-की-कं)<BR>	 1. Covetous, greedy.<BR>	 2. Desirous, wishing.<BR>E. अभिलष to desire, उकन् affix, and the antepen. lengthened.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=046-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिलास|अभिलासः
अभिलास m. (-सः) Wish, desire. E. See अभिलाष; the root being लष, or लस.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=046-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिलिखित
अभिलिखित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Inserted in writing.<BR> E. अभि, and लिखित<BR>written.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=046-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिलेखन
अभिलेखन n. (-नं) Writing or inscribing.<BR> E. अभि, and लेखन writing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=046-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिवन्दन|अभिवंदनं
अभिवन्दन n. (-नं) Saluting respectfully.<BR> E. अभि before वदि to praise, affix<BR>युच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=046-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिवाद|अभिवादः
अभिवाद m. (-दः)<BR>	 1. Reverential salutation.<BR>	 2. Opprobrious, or unfriendly<BR>speech, abuse.<BR> E. अभि against, or adverse, and वाद speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=046-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिवादक|अभिवादकः
अभिवादक mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>	 1. Civil, polite.<BR>	 2. Uncivil, abusive.<BR> E. अभि<BR>to, or against, वादक who speaks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=046-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिवादन|अभिवादनं
अभिवादन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Respectful salutation, a bow or prostration; includ-<BR>ing sometimes the name or title of the person so addressed, and<BR>followed by the declaration of the person's own name.<BR>	 2. Saluta-<BR>tion of a superior or elder, by a junior or inferior, and especially of<BR>the teacher by his disciple.<BR>	 3. In general it is merely lifting the<BR>joined hands to the forehead, and saying, अहमभिवादये I salute. E.<BR>अभि in presence of, and वादन speaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=046-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिवाद्य|अभिवाद्यः
अभिवाद्य mfn. (-द्यः-द्या-द्यं) To be saluted.<BR> E. अभि, and वाद्य to be ad-<BR>dressed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=046-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिवाह्य
अभिवाह्य n. (-ह्यं)<BR>	 1. Presentation, offering.<BR>	 2. Conveyance, transmission.<BR>E. अभि to, वाह्य to be borne.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=046-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिविनीत
अभिविनीत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Pious, pure, devout.<BR> E. अभि, and विनीत well-<BR>behaved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=046-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिव्यक्त
अभिव्यक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>	 1. Plain, distinct, evident, manifest.<BR>	 2. De-<BR>clared, revealed.<BR> E. अभि, and व्यक्त plain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=046-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिव्याप्ति|अभिव्याप्तिः
अभिव्याप्ति f. (-प्तिः) Co-extending, pervading, omnipresence.<BR> E. अभि every<BR>where, and व्याप्ति spreading.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=046-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिव्याहार|अभिव्याहारः
अभिव्याहार m. (-रः) An articulate and significant word or phrase.<BR> E. अभि,<BR>and व्याहार speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=046-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिशङ्कित|अभिशंकित
अभिशङ्कित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Frightened, alarmed.<BR> E. अभि, and शङ्कित alarmed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=046-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिशपन|अभिशपनं
अभिशपन n. (-नं) False accusation, calumny. See अभिशाप.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=046-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिशप्त|अभिशप्तः
अभिशप्त mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं)<BR>	 1. Falsely accused, calumniated.<BR>	 2. Cursed,<BR>accursed.<BR> E. अभि before शप with क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=046-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिशंसन|अभिशंसनं
अभिशंसन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Calumny, abuse, calumniating, abusing.<BR> E. अभि re-<BR>verse, शंस to praise, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=046-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिशस्त|अभिशस्तः
अभिशस्त mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं)<BR>	 1. Calumniated, falsely accused.<BR>	 2. Defamed,<BR>infamous.<BR>	 3. Sinful, wicked.<BR>	 4. Asked, wanted.<BR> E. अभि implying<BR>opposition, शंस to praise, and affix of the part. past क्त; the nasal<BR>being dropped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=046-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिशस्तक
अभिशस्तक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Calumniating, a calumniator.<BR> E. अभिशस्त,<BR>and कृ to make, affix अच् or ट.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=046-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिशस्ताङ्क
अभिशस्ताङ्क m. (-ङ्कः) A brand, a mark of infamy on a criminal.<BR> E. अभिशस्त<BR>infamous, अङ्क mark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=046-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिशस्ति|अभिशस्तिः
अभिशस्ति f. (-स्तिः)<BR>	 1. Calumny, scandal, defamation.<BR>	 2. Asking, begging.<BR>E. अभि before शंस to praise or ask, and क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=046-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिशब्दित
अभिशब्दित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Declared, announced.<BR> E. अभि, and शब्दित<BR>sounded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=046-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिशाप|अभिशापः
अभिशाप m. (-पः)<BR>	 1. False accusation, calumny.<BR>	 2. Charge accusation.<BR>3. Suffering from anger or passion.<BR>	 4. Curse, imprecation.<BR> E. अभि,<BR>and शप to curse or swear, affix घञ्; or with ल्युट् affix अभिशपन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=046-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिशापन|अभिशापनं
अभिशापन n. (-नं) Pronouncing a curse or malediction.<BR> E. अभि with शप<BR>causal form, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=046-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिषङ्ग|अभिषंग|अभिषंगः|अभिषङ्गः
अभिषङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>	 1. Curse or imprecation.<BR>	 2. An oath.<BR>	 3. Defeat.<BR>	 4.<BR>False accusation, calumny.<BR>	 5. Association, company, connexion.<BR>	 6.<BR>Embracing.<BR>	 7. Possession by evil spirits.<BR>	 8. Accession of passion. E.<BR>अभि against, along with, &c. षञ्ज to embrace, to unite, and घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=046-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिषव|अभिषवं|अभिषवः
अभिषव m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. Religious bathing, ablution preparatory to religious<BR>rites.<BR>	 2. Sacrifice.<BR>	 3. Bathing in general.<BR>	 4. Drinking the juice of<BR>the acid Asclepias.<BR>	 5. Ferment, yeast, any substance producing<BR>vinous fermentation.<BR>	 n. (-वं) Sour gruel. See काञ्जिका.<BR> E. अभि, and मु<BR>to mix, to stir, अप् affix; and स is changed to ष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=046-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिषवण|अभिषवणं
अभिषवण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Bathing, ablution.<BR>	 2. Sacrificing, &c. See अभिषव. E.<BR>As before, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=046-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिषह्य
अभिषह्य ind. Insolently, violently, by force.<BR> E. अभि, षह to bear, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=046-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिषिक्त
अभिषिक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>	 1. Sprinkled.<BR>	 2. Anointed, installed, inaugu-<BR>rated, enthroned.<BR> E. अभि before सिच् to sprinkle, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=046-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिषुत|अभिषुतं
अभिषुत n. (-तं)<BR>	 1. Sour gruel. See काञ्जिका.<BR>	 2. The juice of the acid As-<BR>clepias.<BR> E. अभि before सु to mix, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=046-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिषेक|अभिषेकः
अभिषेक m. (-कः) Bathing, sprinkling.<BR> E. अभि before सिच् to sprinkle,<BR>and घञ् affix; the word is often used for initiation, royal unction,<BR>&c. sprinkling with the water of the Ganges, or water in which<BR>various articles have been immersed, being an essential part of the<BR>rites; also for a religious ceremony, including the presentation of<BR>a variety of articles, fruits, gems, &c. along with water or fluid<BR>substances for the bathing of the deity to whom worship is offered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=046-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिषेकशाला
अभिषेकशाला f. (-ला) The hall of coronation.<BR> E. अभिषेक, and शाला a hall.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=046-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिषेचन|अभिषेचनं
अभिषेचन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Initiation, inauguration.<BR>	 2. Sprinkling.<BR> E. अभि before<BR>षिच् to sprinkle, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=046-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिषेणन|अभिषेणनं
अभिषेणन n. (-नं) March to repel an enemy.<BR> E. अभि against, सेना an army,<BR>used as a verb, and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=046-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिष्टुत|अभिष्टुतं
अभिष्टुत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Praised.<BR> E. अभि before स्तु to praise, and क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=046-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिष्यन्द|अभिष्यंदः|अभिष्यन्दः
अभिष्यन्द m. (-न्दः)<BR>	 1. Great increase or enlargement.<BR>	 2. Oozing or flow-<BR>ing.<BR>	 3. Weakness of, or running at the eyes.<BR> E. अभि before स्यन्द to<BR>ooze or drop as a liquid, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=046-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिष्यन्दिन्|अभिष्यंदिन्
अभिष्यन्दिन् mfn. (-न्दी-न्दिनी-न्दि)<BR>	 1. Oozing, trickling.<BR>	 2. Having weak<BR>eyes.<BR>	 3. Causing defluxions or serious effusion.<BR> E. अभिष्यन्द and इनि<BR>aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=046-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिष्यन्दिरमण|अभिष्यन्दिरमणं
अभिष्यन्दिरमण n. (-णं) A suburb, a smaller city appended to a larger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=046-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसंहित
अभिसंहित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Attached to, interested, following any object<BR>eagerly.<BR>	 2. Agreed, contracted.<BR> E. अभि, and सम् before धा to have,<BR>क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=046-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसन्ताप|अभिसंताप|अभिसंतापः|अभिसन्तापः
अभिसन्ताप m. (-पः) War, battle.<BR> E. अभि much, and सन्ताप pain, heat, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=046-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसन्धान|अभिसंधान|अभिसंधानं|अभिसन्धानं
अभिसन्धान n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Cheating, deceiving.<BR>	 2. Attachment or interest in<BR>any object.<BR>	 3. Special agreement.<BR>	 4. Making peace or alliance. E.<BR>अभि, and सम् before, धा to have, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=046-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसन्धि|अभिसंधि|अभिसंधिः|अभिसन्धिः
अभिसन्धि f. (-न्धिः)<BR>	 1. Cheating, deceit.<BR>	 2. Purpose, object.<BR>	 3. Special<BR>agreement.<BR>	 4. Making peace or alliance.<BR>	 5. Joint, junction.<BR> E. अभि,<BR>and सन्धि agreement, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=047-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसम्पात|अभिसंपात|अभिसंपातः|अभिसम्पातः
अभिसम्पात m. (-तः)<BR>	 1. War, battle.<BR>	 2. Curse, imprecation.<BR> E. अभि before<BR>सम्पात going or falling; from पत to fall, with सं prefix, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=047-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसर|अभिसरः
अभिसर m. (-रः) A companion, a follower.<BR> E. अभि after or near, and सर<BR>who goes; from सृ to go, and अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=047-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसम्बन्ध|अभिसंबन्ध|अभिसंबंधः|अभिसंबन्धः
अभिसम्बन्ध m. (-न्धः)<BR>	 1. Relation, connexion.<BR>	 2. Sexual connexion.<BR>	 3.<BR>Contact, conjunction.<BR> E. अभि intensitive, सम्बन्ध connexion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=047-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसर्ज्जन|अभिसर्जन|अभिसर्जनं|अभिसर्ज्जनं
अभिसर्ज्जन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Gift, donation.<BR>	 2. Killing. See अतिसर्ज्जन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=047-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसायम्
अभिसायम् ind. About evening, at sunset.<BR> E. अभि towards, सायम् evening.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=047-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसार|अभिसारः
अभिसार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Strength.<BR>	 2. War, battle.<BR>	 3. A companion, a follower.<BR>4. The instrument or agent.<BR>	 5. An assignation, an appointment. E.<BR>अभि before सृ to go, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=047-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसारण|अभिसारणं
अभिसारण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Coming to or near, visiting, attending, following.<BR>2. Importuning.<BR> E. अभि, and सारण going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=047-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसारिका
अभिसारिका f. (-का) A woman who makes or keeps an assignation. E.<BR>अभि before सृ to go, वुन् affix which leaves क, and टाप् fem. do. also<BR>अभिसारिणी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=047-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसारिन्
अभिसारिन् mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>	 1. Going to or near to, visiting, attending.<BR>2. Going to an appointment or assignation.<BR> E. अभि, and सारिन्<BR>who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=047-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिहत
अभिहत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Humbled, subdued, broken down.<BR>	 2. Killed. E.<BR>अभि and हत part. past of हन् to kill or hurt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=047-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिहार|अभिहारः
अभिहार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Robbing, seizing any thing in the owner's pre-<BR>sence.<BR>	 2. A brisk attack.<BR>	 3. Arming, taking up arms.<BR> E. अभि before<BR>हृ to take, and घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=047-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिहित|अभिहितं
अभिहित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Spoken, said, declared.<BR> E. अभि before धा to have,<BR>the part. affix क्त, and हि substituted for the root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=047-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिहितत्व
अभिहितत्व n. (-त्वं) Text, authority, declaration.<BR> E. अभिहित said, त्व aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=047-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीक|अभीकः
अभीक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A poet.<BR>	 2. A husband.<BR>	 mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>	 1. Lustful,<BR>libidinous.<BR>	 2. Anxious, desirous.<BR>	 3. Cruel.<BR>	 4. Fearless.<BR> E. अभि before<BR>क, from कम to desire: the इ being made long irregularly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=047-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीक्ष्ण|अभीक्ष्णं
अभीक्ष्ण mfn. (-क्ष्णः-क्ष्णा-क्ष्णं)<BR>	 1. Repeated, frequent.<BR>	 2. Constant, perpetual.<BR>ind. (-क्ष्णम्)<BR>	 1. Repeatedly, again and again.<BR>	 3. Perpetually, con-<BR>stantly.<BR> E. अभि before क्ष्णा to whet, डम् affix, and the इ of अभि made<BR>long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=047-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीत
अभीत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Fearless, undaunted.<BR> E. अ neg. भीत afraid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=047-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीति|अभीतिः
अभीति f. (-तिः) Fearlessness.<BR> E. अ neg. भीति fear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=047-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीप्सित|अभीप्सितं
अभीप्सित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Wished, desired.<BR> E. अभि, आप to obtain, in the<BR>desiderative form, and क्त affix, इट् inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=047-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीप्सु
अभीप्सु mfn. (-प्सुः-प्सुः-प्सु) Wishing, desirous.<BR> E. अभि before ईप्सु wishing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=047-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीम|अभीमः
अभीम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं) Causing no fear or terror, unterrific. So अभीषण<BR>and अभीष्म and अभैरव.<BR> E. अ neg. भीम fearful, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=047-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीमान
अभीमान n. (-नं) Pride. E. See अभिमान, the इ being made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=047-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीर|अभीरः
अभीर m. (-रः) A cowherd.<BR> E. अभि and ईर to send, अच् affix; also आभीर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=047-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीरु|अभीरुः
अभीरु mfn. (-रुः-रुः-रु) Fearless, undaunted.<BR>	 m. (-रुः) A name of<BR>BHAIRAVA.<BR>	 f. (-रुः) A plant, (Asparagus recemosus.) See शतमूली. E.<BR>अ neg. भीरु timid: as applied to the plant, not fearful of breaking,<BR>from the number of its roots.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=047-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीरुपत्री
अभीरुपत्री f. (-त्री) A plant. See the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=047-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीलु
अभीलु mfn. (-लुः-लुः-लु) Fearless.<BR> E. अभीरु, र being changed to ल. Also<BR>अभीलुक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=047-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीशु|अभीशुः
अभीशु m. (-शुः)<BR>	 1. A ray of light.<BR>	 2. A rein.<BR>	 f. (-शुः) A finger.<BR> E. अभि<BR>before अशू to pervade, उ affix, derivative irregular. See अभीषु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=047-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीषङ्ग|अभीषंग|अभीषङ्गः
अभीषङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः) Curse, imprecation. See अभिषङ्ग. E. As before, the इ<BR>being here long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=047-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीषु|अभीषुः
अभीषु m. (-षुः)<BR>	 1. A ray of light.<BR>	 2. A rein.<BR>	 3. Love, lust.<BR>	 4. Passion. E.<BR>अभि before इष to desire, and उ affix or अश to pervade, &c. whence,<BR>अभिशु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=047-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीषुमत्|अभीषुमन्त्
अभीषुमत् mfn. (-मान्-मती-मत्)<BR>	 1. Splendid, brilliant.<BR>	 2. Enamoured,<BR>amorous.<BR> E. अभीषु and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=047-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीष्ट|अभीष्टं|अभीष्टः
अभीष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं) Wished, desired.<BR>	 f. (-ष्टा) A perfume. See रेणुका. E.<BR>अभि repeatedly, and इष्ट wished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=047-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभुक्त|अभुक्तः
अभुक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>	 1. Uneaten.<BR>	 2. Unenjoyed, unused, unexpended.<BR>3. One who has not eaten.<BR>	 4. One who has not enjoyed or possessed.<BR>E. अ neg. भुक्त eaten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=047-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभुग्न
अभुग्न mfn. (-ग्नः-ग्ना-ग्नं)<BR>	 1. Straight, not bent.<BR>	 2. Well, free from disease.<BR>E. अ neg. भुग्न broken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=047-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभुज
अभुज mfn. (-जः-जा-जं) Armless, maimed.<BR> E. अ neg. भुज the arm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=047-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभूत
अभूत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Nonexistent, absent, what is not or has not been.<BR>E. अ neg. भूत been.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=047-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभूमि|अभूमिः
अभूमि f. (-मिः) Want of place of refuge or support, destitution, priva-<BR>tion.<BR> E. अ neg. भूमि site.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=047-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभूयिष्ठ
अभूयिष्ठ mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठा-ष्ठं) Few, scanty.<BR> E. अ neg. भूयिष्ठ many.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=047-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभूरि
अभूरि mfn. (-रिः-रिः-रि) Few, some, several.<BR> E. अ neg. भूरि many.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=047-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभूषित
अभूषित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Unadorned.<BR> E. अ neg. भूषित adorned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=047-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभृशम्
अभृशम् ind. A little, a few.<BR> E. अ neg. भृशम् much.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=047-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभेद|अभेदः
अभेद m. (-दः) Identity, absence of difference or distinction.<BR>	 mfn.<BR>(-दः-दा-दं) Alike, identical.<BR> E. अ neg. भेद distinction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=047-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभेद्य|अभेद्यं
अभेद्य n. (-द्यं) A diamond.<BR>	 mfn. (-द्यः-द्या-द्यं)<BR>	 1. Hard, solid, not to be<BR>broken or divided.<BR>	 2. Not to be pierced, indivisible.<BR>	 3. Impene-<BR>trable.<BR> E. अ neg. भेद्य to be broken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=047-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभेद्यता
अभेद्यता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Indivisibility.<BR>	 2. Impenetrability.<BR>	 3. Inseparability.<BR>E. तल् added to the last, also with त्व, अभेद्यत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=047-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभोक्तव्य
अभोक्तव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>	 1. Not to be used or enjoyed.<BR>	 2. Not to be<BR>eaten.<BR> E. अ neg. भुज to eat, &c. तव्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=047-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभोक्तृ
अभोक्तृ m. (-क्ता) An abstemious person.<BR>	 mfn. (-क्ता-क्त्री-क्तृ) Not enjoying.<BR>not using.<BR> E. अ neg. भोक्तृ who enjoys.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=047-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभोग|अभोगः
अभोग m. (-गः) Non-enjoyment, not making use of.<BR> E. अ neg. भोग enjoy-<BR>ment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=047-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभोग्य
अभोग्य mfn. (-ग्यः-ग्या-ग्यं) Not to be used or enjoyed.<BR> E. अ neg. भोग्य to<BR>be used.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=047-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभोजन|अभोजनं
अभोजन n. (-नं) Abstinence, fasting.<BR> E. अ neg. भोजन food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=047-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभोजनीय
अभोजनीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>	 1. Not to be eaten.<BR>	 2. Not to be used.<BR> E. अ<BR>neg. भोजनीय to be eaten, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=047-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभोजिन्
अभोजिन् mfn. (-जी-जिनी-जि) Fasting.<BR> E. अ neg. भोजिन् who eats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=047-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभोज्य
अभोज्य mfn. (-ज्यः-ज्या-ज्यं) Impure, prohibited as food, not to be eaten.<BR>E. अ neg. भोज्य to be eaten, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=047-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यक्त
अभ्यक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं) Oiled, anointed.<BR> E. अभि, and अञ्ज to anoint, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=047-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यङ्ग|अभ्यंग|अभ्यंगः|अभ्यङ्गः
अभ्यङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>	 1. Rubbing the body with unctuous substances; smear-<BR>ing the body with oil, inunction.<BR>	 2. Unguent, liniment, oily applica-<BR>tion.<BR>	 3. Applying collyrium to the eyes.<BR>	 4. Sediment of oil, oil cake.<BR>E. अभि, and अञ्ज to anoint, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=047-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यञ्जन|अभ्यंजन|अभ्यंजनं|अभ्यञ्जनं
अभ्यञ्जन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Oil.<BR>	 2. Smearing the body with oil, inunction; see<BR>the preceding.<BR>	 3. Applying collyrium to the eyelashes, decorating<BR>the hair, &c. or any personal embellishment.<BR> E. अभि, अञ्ज to anoint,<BR>and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=047-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यधिक
अभ्यधिक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Exceeding, surpassing (in number, power, or<BR>kind, &c.)<BR> E. अभि, and अधिक more.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=047-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यधीन
अभ्यधीन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Dependent.<BR> E. अभि, and अधीन dependent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=047-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यनुज्ञा
अभ्यनुज्ञा f. (-ज्ञा)<BR>	 1. Order, command.<BR>	 2. Assent, permission. Also अभ्यनुज्ञानं<BR>E. अभि, and अनुज्ञा order.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=047-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यन्तर|अभ्यंतर|अभ्यन्तरं
अभ्यन्तर n. (-रं)<BR>	 1. Included space.<BR>	 2. Inner part, middle.<BR> E. अभि and<BR>अन्तर within.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=047-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यन्तरायाम|अभ्यन्तरायामः
अभ्यन्तरायाम m. (-मः) Curvature of the spine by spasm; emprosthonos. E.<BR>अभ्यन्तर middle, and आयाम length.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=047-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यनुज्ञात
अभ्यनुज्ञात mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Ordered.<BR>	 2. Permitted.<BR> E. अभि and अनु before<BR>ज्ञा to know, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=047-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यमित|अभ्यमितः
अभ्यमित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Sick, diseased.<BR> E. अभि, अम to be sick, part. affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=047-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यमित्रीण|अभ्यमित्रीणः
अभ्यमित्रीण m. (-नः) A soldier who faces the enemy valiantly.<BR> E. अभि be-<BR>fore, or against, अमित्र an enemy, and ख affix; the affix being छ or<BR>यत्, the word is also written अभ्यमित्रीय or अभ्यमित्र्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=048-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यर्च्चन|अभ्यर्चन|अभ्यर्चनं
अभ्यर्च्चन n. (-नं) Worship, reverence.<BR> E. अभि before अर्च्च to worship, affix<BR>ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=048-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यर्च्चा|अभ्यर्चा
अभ्यर्च्चा f. (-र्च्चा) Respect, worship.<BR> E. अभि, and अर्च्चा reverence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=048-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यर्ण|अभ्यर्णं|अभ्यर्ण्ण
अभ्यर्ण mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-र्णं) Near, proximate.<BR> E. अभि near, अर्ण irr. part. past,<BR>of अर्द to go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=048-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यर्थना
अभ्यर्थना f. (-ना) Petition, request.<BR> E. अभि before अर्थ to ask, युच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=048-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यर्थित
अभ्यर्थित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Asked, invited.<BR> E. अभि, and अर्थित asked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=048-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यर्हित
अभ्यर्हित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Fit, proper, becoming.<BR> E. अभि, and अर्हित proper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=048-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यवकर्षण|अभ्यवकर्षणं
अभ्यवकर्षण n. (-णं) Extraction, drawing out.<BR> E. अभि, and अव prefixed to<BR>कृष draw furrows, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=048-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यवस्कन्द|अभ्यवस्कंदः|अभ्यवस्कन्दः
अभ्यवस्कन्द m. (-न्दः)<BR>	 1. Striking so as to disable an enemy.<BR>	 2. Facing an<BR>enemy.<BR> E. अभि and अव before स्कन्द to go, affix घञ्; also with ल्युट्<BR>affix, अभ्यवस्कन्दनं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=048-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यवहरण|अभ्यवहरणं
अभ्यवहरण n. (-णं) Eating.<BR> E. अभि and अव before हृ to make, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=048-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यवहार|अभ्यवहारः
अभ्यवहार m. (-रः) Eating.<BR> E. अभि and अव before हृ to convey, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=048-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यवहृत|अभ्यवहृतं
अभ्यवहृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Eaten.<BR> E. अभि and अव before हृ to convey, and<BR>the part. affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=048-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यसन|अभ्यसनं
अभ्यसन n. (-नं) Frequent repetition, use, exercise, especially of the<BR>memory, learning by rote.<BR> E. अभि frequently, अस to throw or send,<BR>ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=048-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यसूय
अभ्यसूय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Angry, vexed.<BR>	 f. (-या) Detraction. Also असूया. E.<BR>अभि before असूया envy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=048-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यसूयक
अभ्यसूयक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Detracting, a detractor, a calumniator.<BR> E. अभि<BR>before असूय to envy or detract, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=048-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यस्य
अभ्यस्य mfn. (-स्यः-स्या-स्यं) To be studied. Also अभ्यसनीय.<BR> E. अभि before अस<BR>to throw, affix य or अनीयर्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=048-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यस्त|अभ्यस्तं
अभ्यस्त mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं)<BR>	 1. Exercised, practiced.<BR>	 2. Learnt by heart.<BR>	 3.<BR>Repeated as the radical syllable of a verb.<BR> E. अभि frequently, अस<BR>to throw or send, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=048-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्याकाङ्क्षित|अभ्याकांक्षित|अभ्याकांक्षितं|अभ्याकाङ्क्षितं
अभ्याकाङ्क्षित n. (-तं) A groundless complaint, a false accusation.<BR> E. अभि<BR>and आकाङ्क्षित desired.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=048-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्याख्यान|अभ्याख्यानं
अभ्याख्यान n. (-नं) A false accusation.<BR> E. अभि, and आख्यान saying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=048-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यागत|अभ्यागतः
अभ्यागत m. (-तः) A guest, a visitor.<BR>	 mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Arrived.<BR> E. अभि, and<BR>आगत come.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=048-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यागम|अभ्यागमः
अभ्यागम m. (-मः)<BR>	 1. War, battle.<BR>	 2. Striking, killing.<BR>	 3. Enmity.<BR>	 4.<BR>Vicinity.<BR>	 5. Rising, getting up.<BR>	 6. Coming, arrival, visit.<BR> E. अभि<BR>near, or before, &c. गम to go, with आ prefixed, and अच् affixed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=048-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यागमन|अभ्यागमनं
अभ्यागमन n. (-नं) Arrival, visitation.<BR> E. अभि, and आगमन coming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=048-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यागारिक|अभ्यागारिकः
अभ्यागारिक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Diligent in supporting a family.<BR> E. अभि be-<BR>fore आगार a house, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=048-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्याघात|अभ्याघातः
अभ्याघात m. (-तः) Assault, attack.<BR> E. अभि, and आघात assailing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=048-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यादान|अभ्यादानं
अभ्यादान n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Beginning, commencement.<BR>	 2. First beginning.<BR> E. अभि,<BR>and आदान taking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=048-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यान्त|अभ्यांत
अभ्यान्त mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं) Sick, diseased.<BR> E. अभि and आङ् before अम to be<BR>sick, and the affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=048-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यापात|अभ्यापातः
अभ्यापात m. (-तः) Calamity, misfortune.<BR> E. अभि and आङ् before पत to<BR>go, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=048-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यामर्द्द|अभ्यामर्द|अभ्यामर्दः
अभ्यामर्द्द m. (-र्द्दः) War, battle.<BR> E. अभि and आ before मृद to tread down,<BR>अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=048-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्याश|अभ्याशः
अभ्याश mfn. (-शः-शा-शं) Near, proximate.<BR>	 m. (-शः) Constant repetition. See<BR>अभ्यास.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=048-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यास|अभ्यासः
अभ्यास m. (-सः)<BR>	 1. Practice, exercise.<BR>	 2. Learning by rote.<BR>	 3. Practicing<BR>archery.<BR>	 4. (In arithmetic,) Multiplication.<BR>	 5. (In grammar,) The<BR>reduplicate syllable of a verb.<BR>	 mfn. (-सः-सा-सं) Near, proximate. E.<BR>अभि before अस to go, &c. घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=048-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यासता
अभ्यासता f. (-ता) Constant practice, use, habit.<BR> E. अभ्यास and तल् affix,<BR>also with त्व, अभ्यासत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=048-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यासयोग|अभ्यासयोगः
अभ्यासयोग m. (-गः) The practice of frequent and repeated contem-<BR>plation on any deity or abstract spirit, repeated recollection, &c.<BR>E. अभ्यास, and योग religious exercise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=048-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यासादन|अभ्यासादनं
अभ्यासादन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Striking so as to disable an enemy.<BR>	 2. Facing an<BR>enemy.<BR> E. अभि and आङ् before सद to go, in the causal form, and<BR>ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=048-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यासिन्
अभ्यासिन् mfn. (-सी-सिनी-सि) Practicing, exercising, repeating.<BR> E. अभ्यास<BR>and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=048-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्याहार|अभ्याहारः
अभ्याहार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Robbery. See अभिहार.<BR>	 2. Eating.<BR> E. अभि and आङ्<BR>before हृ to take, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=048-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्याहार्य्य|अभ्याहार्य
अभ्याहार्य्य m. (-र्य्यः) An eatable.<BR>	 mfn. (-र्य्यः-र्य्या-र्य्यं) Eatable, to be eaten. E.<BR>अभि and आहार्य्य to be eaten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=048-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युक्षण|अभ्युक्षणं
अभ्युक्षण n. (-णं) Sprinkling, wetting.<BR> E. अभि, and उक्ष to moisten, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=048-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युक्ष्य
अभ्युक्ष्य ind. Having sprinkled.<BR> E. अभि, and उक्ष to moisten, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=048-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युत्थान|अभ्युत्थानं
अभ्युत्थान n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Fame, reputation.<BR>	 2. Rising from off a seat, &c.<BR>	 3. Rise.<BR>4. Elevation.<BR>	 5. Sunrise.<BR> E. अभि and उत् before स्था to stay, ल्युट्<BR>aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=048-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युत्थित
अभ्युत्थित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Risen, arisen.<BR>	 2. Elevated, exalted.<BR> E. अभि and<BR>उत्थित lifted up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=048-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युदय|अभ्युदयः
अभ्युदय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. Prosperity, increase.<BR>	 2. Accident, occurrence.<BR>	 3. A<BR>festival, any religious celebration.<BR> E. अभि, and उदय rise, pros-<BR>perity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=048-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युदाहरण|अभ्युदाहरणं
अभ्युदाहरण n. (-णं) An example or illustration of a thing by its re-<BR>verse.<BR> E. अभि, and उदाहरण example.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=048-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युदित|अभ्युदितः
अभ्युदित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Asleep at sunrise.<BR>	 2. Celebrated as a festival.<BR>3. Risen, (as the sun.)<BR>	 4. Elevated, exalted.<BR>	 5. Arisen, happened.<BR>E. अभि, उत् up, and इत gone; part. past, of इण to go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=048-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युदीरित
अभ्युदीरित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Thrown over or upon.<BR> E. अभि and उत् before<BR>ईरित gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=048-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युद्यत
अभ्युद्यत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Brought or given unsolicited.<BR> E. अभि towards,<BR>उद्यत exerted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=048-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युद्धृत
अभ्युद्धृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Taken up, delivered.<BR> E. अभि, and उद्धृत taken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=048-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युपगत|अभ्युपगतः
अभ्युपगत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Promised, agreed, assented.<BR>	 2. Gone near<BR>to, approached, arrived at.<BR>	 3. Inferred, probable.<BR>	 4. Similar, ana-<BR>logous.<BR> E. अभि, उप over, गत gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=048-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युपगम|अभ्युपगमः
अभ्युपगम m. (-मः)<BR>	 1. A promise, an agreement, a contract.<BR>	 2. Ap-<BR>proaching, going near to.<BR>	 3. Probable ascertainment.<BR>	 4. Analogy,<BR>affinity.<BR> E. अभि, and उप implying association or vicinity, and गम<BR>going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=048-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युपगमित|अभ्युपगमितः
अभ्युपगमित m. (-तः) A slave for a fixed term.<BR>	 mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Obtained<BR>by assent or free will.<BR> E. अभ्युपगम and इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=048-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युपपत्ति|अभ्युपपत्तिः
अभ्युपपत्ति f. (-त्तिः)<BR>	 1. Favour, affection.<BR>	 2. Defence, protection.<BR>	 3.<BR>Agreement, assent.<BR>	 4. Impregnation of a woman, as of a brother's<BR>widow, as an act of duty.<BR> E. अभि and उप before पत to go, affix क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=048-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युपपन्न
अभ्युपपन्न mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं) Agreeing to.<BR> E. अभि and उप before पद to go,<BR>affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=048-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युपाय|अभ्युपायः
अभ्युपाय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. An agreement, a promise, an engagement.<BR>	 2. A<BR>means, an expedient.<BR> E. अभि and उप before इण to go, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=048-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युपायन|अभ्युपायनं
अभ्युपायन n. (-नं) A bribe, an inducement.<BR> E. अभि and उप before इण to<BR>go, causal form, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=048-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युपेत|अभ्युपेतं
अभ्युपेत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Contracted, promised, agreed.<BR>	 2. Approached.<BR>E. अभि and उप before इण to go, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=048-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युपेत्यशुश्रूषा
अभ्युपेत्यशुश्रूषा f. (-षा) A head or title of law, disputes between master<BR>and servant.<BR> E. अभ्युपेत्य having engaged, अ neg. शुश्रूषा service.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=048-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युष|अभ्युषः
अभ्युष m. (-षः)<BR>	 1. Grain, &c. half dressed, slightly scorched, or parched<BR>so as to be eaten from the hand.<BR>	 2. Bread.<BR> E. अभि before, उष to<BR>burn, क affix; the vowel may be made also long, which gives अभ्यूष,<BR>or may be changed to ओ, and form अभ्योष; some consider the root<BR>to be उष, to be sick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=048-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युषित|अभ्युषितः
अभ्युषित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Dwelling with.<BR> E. अभि before वस to dwell, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=048-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युह
अभ्युह m. (-हः)<BR>	 1. Discussion, reasoning.<BR>	 2. Supplying an ellipsis.<BR> E. अभि,<BR>and उह to reason, क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=049-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युह्य
अभ्युह्य ind.<BR>	 1. Having concluded or inferred, having reasoned.<BR>	 2. Hav-<BR>ing supplied as an ellipsis.<BR> E. अभि उह to reason, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=049-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यूष|अभ्यूषः
अभ्यूष m. (-षः) See अभ्युष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=049-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्योष|अभ्योषः
अभ्योष m. (-षः) See अभ्युष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=049-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्र|अभ्रं
अभ्र r. 1st. cl. (अभ्रति) To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=049-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्रंलिह|अभ्रंलिहः
अभ्रंलिह m. (-हः) Wind.<BR>	 mfn. (-हः-हा-हं) Cloud-touching, cloud-sweeping.<BR>E. अभ्र a cloud, लिह to lick, खश् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=049-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्र|अभ्रं
अभ्र n. (-भ्रं)<BR>	 1. The sky or atmosphere.<BR>	 2. A cloud.<BR>	 3. Gold.<BR>	 4. Talc.<BR> E. अभ्र<BR>to go, or अप् water, and भृ to have, क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=049-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्रक|अभ्रकं
अभ्रक n. (-कं) The mineral substance called talc.<BR> E. अभ्र the same, and<BR>कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=049-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्रङ्कष|अभ्रंकष|अभ्रंकषः|अभ्रङ्कषः
अभ्रङ्कष m. (-षः) Air, wind.<BR> E. अभ्र the sky, कष to plough, and खश् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=049-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्रपिशाच|अभ्रपिशाचः
अभ्रपिशाच m. (-चः) A name of RĀHU, the descending node personified.<BR>E. अभ्र the sky, and पिशाच a goblin; from the mischief he does to<BR>the moon, at the cause of its eclipse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=049-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्रपिशाचक|अभ्रपिशाचकः
अभ्रपिशाचक m. (-कः) See the preceding.<BR> E. कन् added to the former.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=049-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्रपुष्प|अभ्रपुष्पं|अभ्रपुष्पः
अभ्रपुष्प m. (-ष्पः) A kind of tree or cane. See वेतस.<BR> E. अभ्र a cloud and पुष्प<BR>a flower; flowering in the cloudy or rainy season.<BR>	 n. (-ष्पं) Water. E.<BR>As before; put forth as a flower from the clouds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=049-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्रम|अभ्रमः
अभ्रम m. (-मः) Steadiness, composure.<BR>	 mfn. (-मः-मा-मं) Steady, clear,<BR>not blundering.<BR> E. अ neg. भ्रम confusion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=049-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्रमातङ्ग|अभ्रमातंग|अभ्रमातङ्गः
अभ्रमातङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः) INDRA'S elephant.<BR> E. अभ्र a cloud, and मातङ्ग an ele-<BR>phant. The cloud-elephant, or that of the cloud-compelling king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=049-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्रमाला
अभ्रमाला f. (-ला) A line or succession of clouds.<BR> E. अभ्र and माला a garland.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=049-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्रमु|अभ्रमुः
अभ्रमु f. (-मुः) The female elephant of the east.<BR> E. अ neg. भ्रम to wander,<BR>and उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=049-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्रमुप्रिय|अभ्रमुप्रियः
अभ्रमुप्रिय m. (-यः) The male elephant of the east, also INDRA'S elephant.<BR>E. अभ्रमु, and प्रिय beloved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=049-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्रमुवल्लभ|अभ्रमुवल्लभः
अभ्रमुवल्लभ m. (-भः) See the preceding.<BR> E. अभ्रमु, and वल्लभ beloved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=049-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्ररोह|अभ्ररोहं
अभ्ररोह n. (-हं) The lapis lazuli.<BR> E. अभ्र a cloud, रोह what mounts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=049-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्रातृक
अभ्रातृक mf. (-कः-का) Brotherless.<BR> E. अ neg. भ्रातृ a brother, कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=049-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्रान्त|अभ्रांत|अभ्रान्तः
अभ्रान्त mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं) Clear, composed, unperplexed, not mistaken or<BR>in error.<BR> E. अ neg. भ्रान्त misled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=049-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्रान्ति|अभ्रांतिः|अभ्रान्तिः
अभ्रान्ति f. (-न्तिः) Absence of perplexity or error.<BR> E. अ neg. भ्रान्ति error.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=049-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्रावकाश|अभ्रावकाशः
अभ्रावकाश m. (-शः) Fall of rain.<BR> E. अभ्र cloud, अवकाश occasion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=049-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्रावकाशिक
अभ्रावकाशिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Exposed to the rain.<BR> E. अभ्रावकाश and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=049-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्रि|अभ्रिः
अभ्रि f. (-भ्रिः) A wooden scraper or shovel for cleaning a boat.<BR> E. अभ्र to<BR>go, and इन् affix, also अभ्री.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=049-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्रिय|अभ्रियः
अभ्रिय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Belonging to or produced from clouds.<BR> E. अभ्र a<BR>cloud, and इय affix, or technically य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=049-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्रेष|अभ्रेषः
अभ्रेष m. (-षः) Fitness, propriety.<BR> E. अ neg. and भ्रेष impropriety.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=049-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्रोत्थ|अभ्रोत्थं|अभ्रोत्थः
अभ्रोत्थ n. (-त्थं) INDRA'S thunderbolt.<BR> E. अभ्र a cloud, उत् before स्था to stand,<BR>to rise up, क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=049-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम|अमं|अमः
अम r. 1st cl. (अमति)<BR>	 1. To go, to go to or towards.<BR>	 2. To serve or honour.<BR>3. To sound. 10th cl. (आमयति) To afflict with sickness or pain<BR>from disease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=049-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम|अमं|अमः
अम ind. (-मं)<BR>	 1. Quickly.<BR>	 2. Little.<BR>	 mfn. (-मः-मा-मं) Unripe, (as fruit,<BR>&c.)<BR>	 m. (-मः) Sickness.<BR> E. अम to go or to be sick, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=049-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमङ्गल|अमंगल|अमङ्गलं|अमङ्गलः
अमङ्गल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Inauspicious, unlucky, evil.<BR>	 n. (-लं) Inauspicious-<BR>ness, ill luck.<BR>	 m. (-लः) The castor oil plant.<BR> E. अ neg. and मङ्गल<BR>auspicious: the wood has no sap, and is useless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=049-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमङ्गल्य|अमंगल्य|अमङ्गल्यः
अमङ्गल्य mfn. (-ल्यः-ल्या-ल्यं) Inauspicious, unlucky, productive of evil. E.<BR>अ neg. मङ्गल्य auspicious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=049-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमण्ड|अमंड|अमण्डः
अमण्ड m. (ण्डः) The castor oil tree, (Ricinus communis.)<BR> E. अ neg. मडि<BR>to adorn, and अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=049-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमण्डित
अमण्डित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Unadorned.<BR> E. अ neg. मण्डित adorned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=049-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमत|अमतः
अमत m. (-तः)<BR>	 1. Sickness, disease.<BR>	 2. Death.<BR>	 3. Time.<BR> E. अम to be sick,<BR>and अतच् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=049-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमति|अमतिः
अमति m. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Time.<BR>	 2. The moon.<BR>	 3. A cheat, a rogue.<BR>	 f. (-तिः) Un-<BR>consciousness, ignorance, absence of knowledge or intention.<BR> E. अम<BR>to go, and अति Unādi affix, or अ neg. मति understanding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=049-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमतिपूर्व्व|अमतिपूर्व
अमतिपूर्व्व mfn. (-र्व्वः-र्व्वा-र्व्वं) Unconscious, unintentional.<BR> E. अमति ignorance,<BR>पूर्व्व before.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=049-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमत्त
अमत्त mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं)<BR>	 1. Sober, not inebriated.<BR>	 2. Sane, not mad.<BR> E. अ<BR>neg. मत्त crazy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=049-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमत्र|अमत्रं
अमत्र n. (-त्रं) A vessel, a utensil.<BR> E. अम to go, अत्रन् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=049-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमत्सर|अमत्सरः
अमत्सर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Unenvious, charitable.<BR> E. अ neg. मत्सर envious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=049-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमनि|अमनिः
अमनि f. (-निः) A road.<BR> E. अम to go, अनि Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=049-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमन्तव्य
अमन्तव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं) Not to be regarded, inadmissible, unknowable.<BR>Also अमननीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR> E. अ neg. मन्तव्य or मननीय to be re-<BR>garded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=049-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमनुष्य|अमनुष्यः
अमनुष्य mfn. (-ष्यः-ष्या-ष्यं) Unmanly.<BR> E. अ neg. मनुष्य a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=049-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमनुष्यता
अमनुष्यता f. (-ता) Unmanliness.<BR> E. तल् added to the last: also with त्व,<BR>अमनुष्यत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=049-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमनोगत
अमनोगत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Unthought of, unknown.<BR> E. अ neg. मनोगत<BR>thought of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=049-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमनोज्ञ
अमनोज्ञ mfn. (-ज्ञः-ज्ञा-ज्ञं) Disagreeable, disliked.<BR> E. अ neg. मनोज्ञ agreeable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=049-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमनोनीत
अमनोनीत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Disapproved.<BR>	 2. Reprobate.<BR> E. अ neg. मनस्<BR>the mind, नीत led.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=049-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमनोयोग|अमनोयोगः
अमनोयोग m. (-गः) Inattentive.<BR> E. अ neg. मनोयोग attention.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=049-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमनोयोगिन्
अमनोयोगिन् mfn. (-गी-गिनी-गि) Inattentive.<BR> E. अ neg. मनोयोगिन् attentive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=049-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमनोहर
अमनोहर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Disagreeable, displeasing, unattractive.<BR> E. अ<BR>neg. मनोहर pleasant. So अमनोरम्य mfn. (-म्यः-म्या-म्यं) and अमनोहारिन्<BR>mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=049-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमन्त्र|अमंत्र
अमन्त्र mfn. (-न्त्रः-न्त्रा-न्त्रं) Unentitled to, or unaccompanied by holy texts,<BR>as a Śūdra, a female, certain ceremonies, &c.<BR> E. अ neg. मन्त्र a text<BR>of the Vedas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=049-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमन्त्रक|अमंत्रक
अमन्त्रक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Unentitled to, or unaccompanied by holy texts.<BR>E. अ neg. मन्त्र a text, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=049-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमन्द|अमंद|अमन्दः
अमन्द m. (-न्दः) A tree. (E. अम sickness, and द from दो to cut, or destroy.)<BR>mfn. (-न्दः-न्दा-न्दं)<BR>	 1. Fierce, violent.<BR>	 2. Active.<BR> E. अ neg. मन्द tardy<BR>or dull.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=049-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमम|अममः
अमम m. (-मः) One of the Jaina saints of a future age.<BR>	 mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>Devoid of all selfish or worldly attachment or desire.<BR> E. अ neg. and<BR>मम mine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=049-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अममता
अममता f. (-ता) Disinterestedness, indifference.<BR> E. अमम and तल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=049-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अममत्व|अममत्वं
अममत्व n. (-त्वं) Disinterestendess, philosophy, stoicism.<BR> E. अमम and त्व aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=049-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमर|अमरः
अमर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A deity, an immortal.<BR>	 2. A plant, (Heliotropium in-<BR>dicum.) See अस्थिसंहार.<BR>	 3. Also, (Euphorbia tirucalli, &c.)<BR>	 4. Quick-<BR>silver.<BR>	 f. (-रा)<BR>	 1. The residence of INDRA.<BR>	 2. A house post.<BR>	 3. The<BR>womb.<BR>	 4. The umbilical cord.<BR>	 5. A plant, (Menispermum glabrum.)<BR>See गुडूची.<BR>	 6. Bent grass, (Agrostis linearis.)<BR>	 mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Immortal.<BR>E. अ neg. and मर what dies, from मृ and अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=049-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमरणीय
अमरणीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) What cannot die, immortal.<BR> E. अ neg. मरणीय<BR>perishable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=049-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमरणीयता
अमरणीयता f. (-ता) Immortality.<BR> E. तल् added to the last; also अमरणीयत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=049-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमरता
अमरता f. (-ता) Immortality.<BR> E. अमर and तल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=049-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमरत्व|अमरत्वं
अमरत्व n. (-त्वं) Immortality.<BR> E. अमर and त्व aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=049-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमरदारु|अमरदारुः
अमरदारु m. (-रुः) Name of a tree, (Pinus longifolius.)<BR> E. अमर, and दारु<BR>a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=049-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमरद्विज|अमरद्विजः
अमरद्विज m. (-जः) A Brahman who lives by attending a temple or idol.<BR>E. अमर a god, and द्विज a Brahman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=049-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमरपति|अमरपतिः
अमरपति m. (-तिः) INDRA.<BR> E. अमर, and पति lord; also similar compounds,<BR>as अमराधिपतिः, अमरेशः, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=049-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमरपुष्प|अमरपुष्पः
अमरपुष्प m. (-ष्पः) A kind of grass, (Saccharum spontaneum.)<BR> E. अमर,<BR>and पुष्प a flower; also with कन् added, अमरपुष्पकः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=049-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमरपुष्पिका
अमरपुष्पिका f. (-का) A kind of anise, (Anethum sowa.)<BR> E. अमर perpetual,<BR>and पुष्पिका having flowers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=049-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमरभर्तृ|अमरभर्त्तृ
अमरभर्तृ m. (-र्त्ता) INDRA.<BR> E. अमर, and भर्तृ lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=050-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमरलोक|अमरलोकः
अमरलोक n. (-कं) Heaven, the abode of the gods.<BR> E. अमर, and लोक<BR>world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=050-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमरलोकता
अमरलोकता f. (-ता) Heaven.<BR> E. तल् added to अमरलोक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=050-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमरस्त्री
अमरस्त्री f. (-स्त्री) An Apsarā, or nymph of heaven.<BR> E. अमर, and स्त्री a fe-<BR>male.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=050-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमराङ्गना
अमराङ्गना f. (-ना) A nymph of INDRA'S heaven.<BR> E. अमर, and अङ्गना a fe-<BR>male.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=050-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमराद्रि|अमराद्रिः
अमराद्रि m. (-द्रिः) Mount Sumeru or Meru.<BR> E. अमर a deity, and अद्रि a<BR>mountain; being the residence of the gods.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=050-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमरापगा
अमरापगा f. (-गा) The heavenly Ganges.<BR> E. अमर, and आपगा river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=050-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमरावती
अमरावती f. (-ती) The capital of INDRA.<BR> E. अमर a deity, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=050-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमरुत
अमरुत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Calm, without wind.<BR> E. अ neg. मरुत wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=050-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमरेश|अमरेशः
अमरेश m. (-शः) INDRA the king of the gods.<BR> E. अमर, and ईश lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=050-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमरेश्वर|अमरेश्वरः
अमरेश्वर m. (-रः) INDRA.<BR> E. अमर, and ईश्वर chief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=050-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमर्त्य|अमर्त्यः
अमर्त्य m. (-र्त्यः) A deity.<BR>	 mfn. (-र्त्यः-र्त्या-र्त्यं) Immortal, divine.<BR> E. अ neg. मृ to<BR>die, क्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=050-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमर्त्यभुवन|अमर्त्यभुवनं
अमर्त्यभुवन n. (-नं) The heaven of INDRA, or Svarga, a kind of Mohamme-<BR>dan paradise.<BR> E. अमर्त्य a deity, and भुवन a world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=050-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमर्द्दित|अमर्दित
अमर्द्दित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Unthreshed, unsubdued, not trodden down. E.<BR>अ neg. मर्द्दित trampled on.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=050-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमर्य्यादा|अमर्यादा
अमर्य्यादा f. (-दा)<BR>	 1. Impropriety of conduct.<BR>	 2. Disrespect.<BR> E. अ neg.<BR>मर्य्यादा limit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=050-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमर्ष|अमर्षः
अमर्ष m. (-र्षः)<BR>	 1. Anger, passion.<BR>	 2. Impatience, impetuosity.<BR> E. अ neg.<BR>मृष to bear with, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=050-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमर्षण|अमर्षणः
अमर्षण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Passionate, wrathful. E. As before, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=050-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमर्षवत्
अमर्षवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>	 1. Hasty, impetuous, impatient.<BR>	 2. Wrathful,<BR>passionate.<BR> E. अमर्ष and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=050-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमर्षिन्
अमर्षिन् mfn. (-र्षी-र्षिणी-र्षि)<BR>	 1. Passionate, wrathful.<BR>	 2. Impetuous.<BR> E. अमर्ष<BR>and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=050-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमल|अमलं
अमल n. (-लं) Talc.<BR>	 f. (-ला)<BR>	 1. The goddess LAKṢMĪ.<BR>	 2. Emblic myroba-<BR>lan, (Phyllanthus emblica.)<BR>	 3. The umbilical cord.<BR>	 mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>	 1.<BR>Clean, pure.<BR>	 2. White.<BR> E. अ neg. and मल dirt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=050-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमलपतत्रिन्
अमलपतत्रिन् mf. (-त्री-त्रिणी) The wild goose.<BR> E. अमल white or grey, and<BR>पतत्रिन् a bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=050-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमलिन
अमलिन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Clean, pure.<BR> E. अ neg. मलिन dirty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=050-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमस|अमसः
अमस m. (-सः)<BR>	 1. Time.<BR>	 2. Stupidity.<BR>	 3. Disease.<BR> E. अम् to go, or be sick,<BR>and अस Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=050-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमसृण
अमसृण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>	 1. Harsh, hard.<BR>	 2. Violent, intense.<BR> E. अ neg.<BR>मसृण soft.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=050-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमस्तक
अमस्तक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Headless.<BR> E. अ neg. मस्तक the head.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=050-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमांस|अमांसः
अमांस mfn. (-सः-सा-सं) Feeble, thin.<BR> E. अ neg. and मांस flesh. Also अमांसल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=050-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमा
अमा ind.<BR>	 1. With, together with.<BR>	 2. Near.<BR>	 f. (-मा) Day of conjunction or<BR>new moon.<BR> E. अ neg. माङ् to measure, क्विप् affix, and टाप् fem. do.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=050-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमातृक
अमातृक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Motherless.<BR> E. अ neg. मातृ a mother, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=050-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमात्य|अमात्यः
अमात्य m. (-त्यः) A minister, a counsellor.<BR> E. अमा near, त्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=050-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमात्र|अमात्रः
अमात्र mfn. (-त्रः-त्रा-त्रं)<BR>	 1. Not whole or entire.<BR>	 2. Not elementary.<BR> E. अ<BR>neg. मात्र whole, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=050-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमात्रवत्त्व
अमात्रवत्त्व n. (-त्त्वं)<BR>	 1. Spirit, spiritual essence.<BR>	 2. Deficiency, defect.<BR> E. अ<BR>neg. मात्रवत् like elementary, त्व added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=050-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमानन|अमाननं
अमानन n. (-नं) Disrespect.<BR> E. अ neg. मन to mind, in the causal form,<BR>and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=050-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमानव
अमानव mfn. (-वः-वा-वं)<BR>	 1. Not human, animal.<BR>	 2. Superhuman.<BR> E. अ neg.<BR>मानव mortal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=050-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमानस्य|अमानस्यं
अमानस्य n. (-स्यं) Pain. See आमनस्य.<BR> E. अ neg. मनस् the mind, and ण्यत्<BR>aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=050-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमानिता
अमानिता f. (-ता) Modesty, humility.<BR> E. तल् added to अमानिन्, also with त्व,<BR>अमानित्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=050-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमानिन्
अमानिन् mfn. (-नी-निनी-नि) Humble, modest.<BR> E. अ neg. मान pride, इनि<BR>affix. Also अमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=050-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमानुष|अमानुषः
अमानुष mfn. (-षः-षी-षं) Not human, animal, superhuman.<BR> E. अ neg. मानुष<BR>human.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=050-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमानुष्य
अमानुष्य mfn. (-ष्यः-ष्यी-ष्यं) Superhuman.<BR> E. अ neg. मानुष्य human.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=050-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमान्य|अमान्यः
अमान्य mfn. (-न्यः-न्या-न्यं) To be disrespected.<BR> E. अ neg. मान्य to be respected.<BR>Also अमाननीय and अमानितव्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=050-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमामसी
अमामसी f. (-सी) The day of new moon.<BR> E. अमा with, मस to measure, अच्<BR>affix, and ङीप् fem. do or with घञ् affix अमामासी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=050-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमावसी
अमावसी f. (-सी) Day of new moon.<BR> E. अमा with, and वस to abide, अच्<BR>affix; being with, or in the same quarter as the sun; also अमावासी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=050-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमावास्य
अमावास्य mfn. (-स्यः-स्या-स्यं) Produced in the day of new moon.<BR> E. अमावास्या<BR>and अ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=050-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमावास्यक
अमावास्यक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Produced on the day of new moon. E.<BR>अमावास्या and वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=050-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमावास्या
अमावास्या f. (-स्या) Day of conjunction or new moon.<BR> E. अमा with, (the<BR>sun and moon,) वस to abide, ण्यत् affix: or with the penult. vowel<BR>short, अमावस्या; also अमावसी, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=050-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमाय
अमाय mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>	 1. True, wise.<BR>	 2. Sincere, guileless, free from error<BR>or deceit.<BR>	 f. (-या)<BR>	 1. Absence of delusion, knowledge of the truth.<BR>2. Sincerity, honesty.<BR> E. अ neg. माया deceit, delusion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=050-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमायिक|अमायिकः
अमायिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) True, real, honest, void of trick or guile.<BR> E. अ<BR>neg. मायिक deceptive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=050-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमायिन्
अमायिन् mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि) Acting without illusion or deceit.<BR> E. अ neg.<BR>मायिन् deceitful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=050-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमार्ग|अमार्गः
अमार्ग m. (-र्गः) Want of a road.<BR>	 mfn. (-र्गः-र्गा-र्गं) Without a road.<BR> E. अ neg.<BR>मार्ग a road.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=050-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमार्गित
अमार्गित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Unsought, not hunted after.<BR> E. अ neg. मार्गित<BR>sought.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=050-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमार्ज्जित|अमार्जित
अमार्ज्जित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Uncleansed.<BR>	 2. Unadorned.<BR> E. अ neg. मार्ज्जित<BR>cleaned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=050-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमित
अमित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Unmeasured, boundless, infinite.<BR>	 2. Neglected,<BR>unpolished, unclean.<BR> E. अ neg. मित measured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=050-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमितौजस्
अमितौजस् mfn. (-जाः-जाः-जः) Mighty, all-powerful, almighty.<BR> E. अमित<BR>boundless, ओजस् strength.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=050-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमित्र|अमित्रः
अमित्र m. (-त्रः) An enemy, an adversary.<BR>	 mfn. (-त्रः-त्रा-त्रं) Unfriendly,<BR>hostile.<BR> E. अम् to go, and इत्र Unādi affix, or अ neg. and मित्र a<BR>friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=050-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमिन्
अमिन् mfn. (-मी-मिनी-मि) Sick, diseased.<BR> E. अम sickness, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=050-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमिश्र
अमिश्र mfn. (-श्रः-श्रा-श्रं) Unmixed, unmixing.<BR> E. अ neg. मिश्र mixture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=050-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमिश्रणीय
अमिश्रणीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Immiscible.<BR> E. अ neg. मिश्रणीय to be mixed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=050-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमिश्रित
अमिश्रित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Unmixed.<BR> E. अ neg. मिश्रित mixed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=050-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमिष|अमिषं
अमिष n. (-षं)<BR>	 1. Luxury.<BR>	 2. Honesty, simplicity.<BR> E. अम to be sick, इषन्<BR>Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=050-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमीमांसा
अमीमांसा f. (-सा) Absence of reasoning or investigation.<BR> E. अ neg. मीमांसा<BR>investigation by reason.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=050-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमीव|अमीवं|अमीवः
अमीव n. (-वं)<BR>	 1. Sin.<BR>	 2. Pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=050-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमुक|अमुकं
अमुक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) A certain person or thing, any thing or person<BR>referred to without a name.<BR> E. अमु for अदस् this, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=050-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमुक्त|अमुक्तं
अमुक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>	 1. Not loosed, not let go.<BR>	 2. Not liberated from<BR>birth and death.<BR>	 n. (-क्तं) A weapon that is always grasped to be<BR>used, as a knife, &c. See मुक्तामुक्त, यन्त्रामुक्त, &c.<BR> E. अ neg. and मुक्त<BR>released.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=050-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमुक्तहस्त
अमुक्तहस्त mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं) Sparing, frugal, prudent.<BR> E. अमुक्त not loosed,<BR>हस्त the hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=050-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमुक्ति|अमुक्तिः
अमुक्ति f. (-क्तिः) Confinement, want of freedom or liberty.<BR> E. अ neg. मुक्ति<BR>liberation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=050-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमुख्य
अमुख्य mfn. (-ख्यः-ख्या-ख्यं) Inferior, ordinary.<BR> E. अ neg. मुख्य principal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=050-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमुतस्
अमुतस् ind. Hence, from this.<BR> E. अमु for अदस् and तसिल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=050-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमुत्र
अमुत्र ind. In the next life.<BR> E. अमु from अदस् this or that, and त्रल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=050-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमुत्रत्य
अमुत्रत्य mfn. (-त्यः-त्या-त्यं) Belonging to a future state, being of the next<BR>world.<BR> E. अमुत्र and त्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=050-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमुष्यपुत्र|अमुष्यपुत्रः
अमुष्यपुत्र mf. (-त्रः-त्री)<BR>	 1. Of a good family, of known origin.<BR>	 2. The son<BR>or daughter of such a one.<BR> E. अमुष्य the irr. gen. of अदस् this, and पुत्र<BR>a son, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=051-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमुष्यायण
अमुष्यायण mf. (-णः-णा)<BR>	 1. Of respectable birth, of known origin.<BR>	 2. The<BR>offspring of such a one, of a certain person, &c.<BR> E. अमुष्य as in the<BR>last, and फक् affix, also आमुष्यायण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=051-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमूदृश्
अमूदृश् mfn. (-दृक्) Of such form or kind.<BR> E. अमू for अदस् this, and क्विप्<BR>affix; also अमूदृश and अमूदृक्ष<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=051-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमूदृश|अमूदृशः
अमूदृश mfn. (-शः-शा-शं) Of such a form or kind. E. See the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=051-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमूदृक्ष
अमूदृक्ष mfn. (-क्षः-क्षा-क्षं) Such, like of such form or kind. E. See अमूदृश.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=051-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमूर्त्त|अमूर्त|अमूर्तः|अमूर्त्तः
अमूर्त्त mfn. (-र्त्तः-र्त्ता-र्त्तं) Formless, shapeless, unembodied.<BR> E. अ neg. मूर्त्ति<BR>form; the final changed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=051-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमूर्त्ति|अमूर्ति|अमूर्तिः
अमूर्त्ति f. (-र्त्तिः) Shapelessness, absence of shape or form.<BR> E. अ. neg. मूर्त्ति<BR>form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=051-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमूल
अमूल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Having no root. Also अमूलक.<BR>	 f. (-ला) A plant. See<BR>अग्निशिखा.<BR> E. अ neg. and मूल a root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=051-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमूल्य
अमूल्य mfn. (-ल्यः-ल्या-ल्यं) Invaluable, not to be purchased.<BR> E. अ neg. मूल्य<BR>price.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=051-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृणाल|अमृणालं
अमृणाल n. (-लं) The root of a fragrant grass, used in India for taties or<BR>screens against the hot winds, commonly called Kaskas,<BR>(Andropogon muricatum.)<BR> E. अ like, as it were, and मृणाल a fibrous<BR>root; also मृणाल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=051-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृत|अमृतं|अमृतः
अमृत n. (-तं)<BR>	 1. The food of the gods, Ambrosia or Nectar.<BR>	 2. Water.<BR>3. Butter, rice, &c. the residue of a sacrifice.<BR>	 4. Oiled butter or<BR>ghee.<BR>	 5. Unsolicited alms.<BR>	 6. Boiled rice.<BR>	 7. Food.<BR>	 8. Wealth,<BR>property.<BR>	 9. Gold.<BR>	 10. Buttermilk.<BR>	 11. Any thing sweet, a sweet-<BR>meat.<BR>	 12. Milk.<BR>	 13. Poison.<BR>	 14. A drug or medicament.<BR>	 15. Quick-<BR>silver.<BR>	 16. Final emancipation.<BR>	 m. (-तः)<BR>	 1. A god, an immortal.<BR>2. DHANWANTARI, the physician of the gods.<BR>	 f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Emblic<BR>myrobalan, (phyllanthus emblica.)<BR>	 2. The yellow sort., (Terminalia<BR>citrina.)<BR>	 3. Another plant, (Menispermum glabrum.)<BR>	 4. Long<BR>pepper.<BR>	 5. Holy basil, (Ocymum sanctum.)<BR>	 6. Spirituous liquor. It<BR>also occurs amongst the synonyms of several plants besides those<BR>enumerated.<BR>	 mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Beloved, desired.<BR>	 2. Beautiful.<BR>3. Immortal, imperishable.<BR> E. अ neg. मृङ् to die, and क्त affix; what<BR>is immortal or what makes so; what supports life, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=051-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृतकुण्ड
अमृतकुण्ड m. (-ण्डः) A vessel of nectar.<BR> E. अमृत and कुण्ड a hole.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=051-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृतता
अमृतता f. (-ता) Immortality.<BR> E. अमृत and तल् affix; also with त्व, अमृतत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=051-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृततरङ्गिणी|अमृततरंगिणी
अमृततरङ्गिणी f. (-णी) Moonlight.<BR> E. अमृत, and तरङ्गिणी a sea.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=051-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृतदीधिति|अमृतदीधितिः
अमृतदीधिति m. (-तिः) The moon.<BR> E. अमृत ambrosia, and दीधिति a ray.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=051-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृतद्रव|अमृतद्रवः
अमृतद्रव mfn. (-वः-वा-वं) Shedding ambrosia.<BR> E. अमृत, and द्रव dropping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=051-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृतधार
अमृतधार mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Shedding or distilling ambrosia.<BR> E. अमृत, and धारा<BR>a drop.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=051-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृतप|अमृतपः
अमृतप mfn. (-पः-पा-पं) Drinking ambrosia.<BR>	 m. (-पः) A deity.<BR> E. अमृत, and<BR>प who drinks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=051-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृतरस|अमृतरसः
अमृतरस m. (-सः) Nectar, ambrosia.<BR> E. अमृत, and रस juice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=051-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृतवर्ष
अमृतवर्ष m. (-र्षः) A fall of ambrosia from heaven.<BR> E. अमृत, and वर्ष rain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=051-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृतवल्ली
अमृतवल्ली f. (-ल्ली) A species moonseed, (Menispermun glabrum.) See<BR>गुडूची.<BR> E. अमृत, and वल्ली a pedicle; the plant flourishing for a long<BR>time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=051-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृतसारज|अमृतसारजः
अमृतसारज m. (-जः) Raw sugar, molasses.<BR> E. अमृत ambrosia, सार essence,<BR>and ज produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=051-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृतसू
अमृतसू m. (-सूः) The Moon, as the producer of ambrosia.<BR>	 f. (-सूः) A Mātṛ<BR>or a divine mother.<BR> E. अमृत the ambrosia, and सू who brings forth;<BR>from सूङ् to bear, and क्विप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=051-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृतस्रुत्
अमृतस्रुत् mfn. (-स्रूत्) Shedding ambrosia.<BR> E. अमृत, स्रू to distil, क्विप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=051-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृतसोदर|अमृतसोदरः
अमृतसोदर m. (-रः) A horse.<BR> E. अमृत, and सोदर brother: born with nectar<BR>at the churning of the ocean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=051-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृतान्धस्
अमृतान्धस् m. (-न्धाः) A deity.<BR> E. अमृत, and अन्धस् food; whose food is<BR>ambrosia.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=051-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृताफल|अमृताफलं|अमृताफलः
अमृताफल m. (-लः) The fruit of the Trichosanthes.<BR> E. अमृता, and फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=051-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृताशन|अमृताशनः
अमृताशन m. (-नः) A deity. E. As before, अशन eating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=051-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृतासङ्ग|अमृतासङ्गं|अमृतासङ्गः
अमृतासङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः) A collyrium, extracted from the Amomum anthoriza.<BR>See कर्परी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=051-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृताहरण|अमृताहरणः
अमृताहरण m. (-णः) A name of GARUḌA, the bird of VIṢṆU.<BR> E. अमृत, हृ<BR>to convey, with आङ् prefixed, and ल्युट् affix; GARŪDA having<BR>upon one occasion stolen the Amrita.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=051-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृतोत्पन्ना
अमृतोत्पन्ना f. (-न्ना) A fly.<BR> E. अमृत, and उत्पन्न born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=051-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृतोद्भव|अमृतोद्भवं
अमृतोद्भव m. (-वः) A kind of collyrium. See अमृतासङ्ग.<BR> E. अमृत, and उद्भव<BR>born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=051-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृत्ति
अमृत्ति f. (-त्तिः) A drinking vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=051-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृत्यु|अमृत्युः
अमृत्यु f. (-त्युः) Immortality.<BR> E. अ neg. मृत्यु death.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=051-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमेघ
अमेघ mfn. (-घः-घा-घं) Cloudless.<BR> E. अ. neg. मेघ a cloud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=051-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमेधस्
अमेधस् m. (-धाः) A food, an idiot.<BR> E. अ neg. मेध to understand, and असुन्<BR>aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=051-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमेध्य|अमेध्यं
अमेध्य mfn. (-ध्यः-ध्या-ध्यं) Impure, foul.<BR>	 n. (-ध्यं) Fæces, excrement.<BR> E. अ<BR>neg. and मेध्य pure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=051-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमेध्यत्व
अमेध्यत्व n. (-त्वं) Foulness, filthiness.<BR> E. त्व added to अमेध्य, also with तल्,<BR>अमेध्यता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=051-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमेध्ययुक्त
अमेध्ययुक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं) Filthy, foul.<BR> E. अमेध्य, and युक्त joined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=051-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमेध्यलिप्त
अमेध्यलिप्त mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं) Smeared with ordure, foul, defiled.<BR> E. अमेध्य,<BR>and लिप्त smeared.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=051-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमेध्यलेप|अमेध्यलेपः
अमेध्यलेप m. (-पः) Smearing with ordure.<BR> E. अमेध्य, and लेप plastering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=051-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमेध्याक्त
अमेध्याक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं) Soiled by ordure.<BR> E. अमेध्य, and अक्त smeared.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=051-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमेय
अमेय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Immense, immeasurable.<BR> E. अ neg. मेय to be measured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=051-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमेयात्मन्
अमेयात्मन् mfn. (-त्मा-त्मा-त्म) Magnanimous, possessing extraordinary powers<BR>of mind.<BR> E. अमेय, and आत्मन् self.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=051-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमोक्ष|अमोक्षः
अमोक्ष m. (-क्षः)<BR>	 1. Bondage, confinement.<BR>	 2. Confinement to life.<BR>	 mfn.<BR>(-क्षः-क्षा-क्षं) Unliberated, unloosed.<BR> E. अ neg. मोक्ष liberation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=051-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमोघ|अमोघः
अमोघ mfn. (-घः-घा-घं) Productive, fruitful, not vain or barren.<BR>	 m. (-घः)<BR>The name of a river.<BR>	 f. (-घा)<BR>	 1. Trumpet flower, (Bignonia suave-<BR>olens.)<BR>	 2. A plant of which the seed is used as a vermifuge, (Erycibe<BR>paniculata, Rox.) See विडङ्ग.<BR>	 3. Yellow myrobalan. See हरीतकी. E.<BR>अ not, मोघ vain, barren.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=051-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमोचन|अमोचनं
अमोचन n. (-नं) Non-liberation, not loosing or letting go.<BR> E. अ neg. मोचन<BR>loosing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=051-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमोचित
अमोचित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Confined, not liberated.<BR> E. अ neg. मोचित loosed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=051-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्ब|अंब|अंबः|अम्बः
अम्ब r. 1st. cl. (अंबति) To move, to go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=051-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बक|अंबक|अंबकं|अम्बकं
अम्बक n. (-कं)<BR>	 1. The eye.<BR>	 2. Copper.<BR> E. अम्ब to go, and वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=051-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बर|अंबर|अंबरं|अम्बरं|अम्बरः
अम्बर n. (-रं)<BR>	 1. The sky or atmosphere.<BR>	 2. Clothes, apparel.<BR>	 3. A perfume,<BR>(Ambergris.)<BR>	 4. Cotton.<BR>	 5. Talc.<BR> E. अम्ब to go, and अरन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=051-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बरयुग
अम्बरयुग n. (-गं) The two principal female garments, or upper and lower<BR>cloths or mantles<BR> E. अम्बर, and युग a pair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=051-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बरान्त|अंबरान्त|अम्बरान्तः
अम्बरान्त m. (-न्तः)<BR>	 1. The horizon.<BR>	 2. The end of a garment.<BR> E. अम्बर and<BR>अन्त end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=051-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बरिष|अम्बरिषं
अम्बरिष mn. (-षः-षं) A frying pan. See the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=051-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बरीष|अंबरीष|अंबरीषं|अम्बरीषं|अम्बरीषः
अम्बरीष mn. (-षः-षं)<BR>	 1. A frying pan.<BR>	 2. War, battle.<BR>	 m. (-षः)<BR>	 1. A name<BR>of ŚIVA.<BR>	 2. Also of VIṢṆU.<BR>	 3. A young animal. a colt, a boy.<BR>	 4.<BR>The name of a king of the solar race, celebrated as a worshipper of<BR>VIṢṆU.<BR>	 5. A division of hell.<BR>	 6. The sun.<BR>	 7. Repentance.<BR>	 8. A tree,<BR>(Spondias mangifera.)<BR> E. अबि to sound, and ईषन् Unādi affix, but<BR>irregularly formed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=051-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बष्ठ|अंबष्ठ|अंबष्ठः|अम्बष्ठः
अम्बष्ठ m. (-ष्ठः)<BR>	 1. The name of a country, stated to be in the eastern<BR>division of India, and supposed by Mr. WILFORD, to be the abode<BR>of the AMBASTŒ of Arrian.<BR>	 2. The offspring of a man of the Brah-<BR>man, and a woman of the Vaiśya tribe, a man of the medical cast.<BR>f. (-ष्ठा)<BR>	 1. A sort of jasmine, (Jasminum auriculatum.)<BR>	 2. A plant,<BR>(Cissampelos hexandra.) See वनतिक्तिका.<BR>	 3. Woodsorrel, (Oxalis<BR>corniculata, Rox.)<BR> E. अम्बा a mother, स्था to stand, and क affix, what<BR>cherishes like a mother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=051-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बष्ठकी|अंबष्ठकी
अम्बष्ठकी f. (-की) A creeper, (Cissampelos hexandra.) Also अम्बष्ठा and<BR>अम्बष्ठिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=052-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बा|अंबा
अम्बा f. (-म्बा)<BR>	 1. A mother.<BR>	 2. The same, (in theatrical language.)<BR>	 3. A<BR>name of DURGĀ. See अम्बिका.<BR> E. अबि to sound, अप् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=052-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बालिका|अंबालिका
अम्बालिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. A mother of PĀṆḌU.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=052-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बिका|अंबिका
अम्बिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. A mother.<BR>	 2. A name of PĀRVATĪ.<BR>	 3. The mother<BR>of DHṚTARĀṢṬRA.<BR>	 4. One of the female. domestic deities of the<BR>Jainas.<BR>	 5. A medicinal plant. See कटुकी.<BR> E. अम्बा a mother, and कन्<BR>affix; like a mother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=052-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बिकेय|अंबिकेय|अंबिकेयः|अम्बिकेयः
अम्बिकेय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. GANESA or KARTIKEYA both sons of PĀRVATĪ.<BR>	 2. A<BR>name of DHṚTARĀṢṬRA.<BR> E. अम्बिका as above; and ढक् affix, imply-<BR>ing family decent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=052-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बिकेयक|अंबिकेयकः|अम्बिकेयकः
अम्बिकेयक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. GANESA.<BR>	 2. DHṚTARĀṢṬRA. E. As the pre-<BR>ceding. कन् being added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=052-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बु|अंबु
अम्बु n. (-म्बु) Water.<BR> E. अबि to sound, and उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=052-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बुकणा
अम्बुकणा f. (-णा) A drop of water.<BR> E. अम्बु, and कण a particle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=052-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बुकण्टक|अम्बुकण्टकः
अम्बुकण्टक m. (-कः) The short-nosed alligator.<BR> E. अम्बु water, and कण्टक<BR>a thorn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=052-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बुकिरात|अम्बुकिरातः
अम्बुकिरात m. (-तः) An alligator.<BR> E. अम्बु, and किरात a savage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=052-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बुकीश|अम्बुकीशः
अम्बुकीश m. (-शः) A porpoise, especially of the kind common in the<BR>Ganges, (Delphinus gangeticus, Rox.)<BR> E. अम्बु, and कीश the water-<BR>monkey.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=052-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बुकूर्म्म|अम्बुकूर्म|अम्बुकूर्मः|अम्बुकूर्म्मः
अम्बुकूर्म्म m. (-र्म्मः) A porpoise, especially the gangetic.<BR> E. अम्बु, and कूर्म्म a<BR>tortoise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=052-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बुचर
अम्बुचर mfn. (-रः-रा-री-रं) Aquatical.<BR> E. अम्बु, and चर what moves in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=052-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बुचामर|अम्बुचामरं
अम्बुचामर n. (-रं) An aquatic plant, (Vallisneria.) See शैबाल.<BR> E. अम्बु, and<BR>चामर the Indian chowrie; the water-chowrie.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=052-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बुचारिन्
अम्बुचारिन् mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि) Aquatical, as a fish, &c.<BR> E. अम्बु, चर to go,<BR>णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=052-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बुज|अम्बुजं|अम्बुजः
अम्बुज m. (-जः) A plant, (Eugenia acutangula.) See हिज्जल.<BR>	 n. (-जं)<BR>	 1. A<BR>lotus, (Nymphæa nelumbo.)<BR>	 2. The thunderbolt of INDRA.<BR>	 mfn.<BR>(-जः-जा-जं) Aquatic, water-born.<BR> E. अम्बु, and ज what is produced;<BR>water-born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=052-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बुजन्म
अम्बुजन्म n. (-न्म) A lotus.<BR> E. अम्बु, and जन्म birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=052-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बुताल|अम्बुतालः
अम्बुताल m. (-लः) Vallisneria. See अम्बुचामर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=052-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बुद|अम्बुदः
अम्बुद m. (-दः) A cloud.<BR>	 mfn. (-दः-दा-दं) Shedding or giving water. E.<BR>अम्बु, and द what gives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=052-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बुधि|अम्बुधिः
अम्बुधि m. (-धिः) The ocean.<BR> E. अम्बु and धि what possesses; from धाञ्<BR>with कि affixed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=052-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बुनिधि|अम्बुनिधिः
अम्बुनिधि m. (-धिः) The ocean.<BR> E. अम्बु and निधि a treasure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=052-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बुप|अम्बुपः
अम्बुप m. (-पः) A plant, (Cassia tora, or alata.)<BR>	 mfn. (-पः-पा-पं) Drinking<BR>or imbibing water.<BR> E. अम्बु, and प what drinks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=052-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बुपत्रा
अम्बुपत्रा f. (-त्रा) A fragrant grass, (perhaps a Cyperus.) See उच्चटा. E.<BR>अम्बु, and पत्र a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=052-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बुपद्धति|अम्बुपद्धतिः
अम्बुपद्धति f. (-तिः) Current, stream, flow of water.<BR> E. अम्बु, and पद्धति<BR>distinction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=052-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बुप्रसादन|अम्बुप्रसादनं
अम्बुप्रसादन m. (-नः) The clearing nut tree, (Strychnos potatorum.) E.<BR>अम्बु water, प्रसद to cleanse, ल्युट् affix. The nuts of this plant are<BR>generally used in India, for purifying water; they are rubbed upon<BR>the inner surface of the vessel, and occasion the precipitation of<BR>the impurities of the fluid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=052-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बुभृत्
अम्बुभृत् m. (-भृत्)<BR>	 1. A cloud.<BR>	 2. The ocean.<BR>	 3. A grass, (Cyperus<BR>pertenuis.)<BR> E. अम्बु, and भृत् what nourishes, from भृञ् with क्विप्<BR>aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=052-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बुमत्|अंबुमत्|अम्बुमन्त्
अम्बुमत् m. (-मान्) The side of a river, or a bank, a shore.<BR>	 mfn.<BR>(-मान्-मती-मत्) Watery, having or containing water.<BR> E. अम्बु and मतुप्<BR>aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=052-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बुमात्रज|अम्बुमात्रजः
अम्बुमात्रज m. (-जः) A bivalve shell.<BR> E. अम्बु water, मात्र all, every kind,<BR>and ज produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=052-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बुमुच्
अम्बुमुच् m. (-मुक्) A cloud.<BR> E. अम्बु, and मुच् what lets go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=052-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बुर|अम्बुरः
अम्बुर m. (-रः) The lower limb of a door-frame, the threshold.<BR> E. अम्ब,<BR>and राज to shine, affix ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=052-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बुराशि|अम्बुराशिः
अम्बुराशि m. (-शिः) The ocean.<BR> E. अम्बु, and राशि a heap.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=052-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बुरुह्
अम्बुरुह् n. (-रुट्)<BR>	 1. Any aquatic plant.<BR>	 2. A lotus.<BR> E. अम्बु, and रुह् what<BR>grows on or in, क्विप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=052-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बुरोहिणी
अम्बुरोहिणी f. (-णी) A lotus.<BR> E. अम्बु, and रोहिन् what grows, or rises on<BR>or in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=052-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बुवाची
अम्बुवाची f. (-ची) Four days in Ashārha, the 10th to the 13th of the<BR>dark fortnight, when the earth is supposed to the unclean, and<BR>agriculture is prohibited.<BR> E. अम्बु and, वाच् speech, with ङीष् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=052-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बुवासी
अम्बुवासी f. (-सी) See the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=052-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बुवासिनी
अम्बुवासिनी f. (-नी) Trumpet flower, (Bignonia suave-olens.)<BR> E. अम्बु<BR>before वस to abide, णिनि and ङीप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=052-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बुवाह|अम्बुवाहः
अम्बुवाह m. (-हः)<BR>	 1. A cloud.<BR>	 2. The cyperus.<BR>	 3. A water-carrier.<BR> E. अम्बु<BR>water, and वाह what bears.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=052-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बुवाहिन्
अम्बुवाहिन् mfn. (-ही-हिनी-हि) Carrying or conveying water.<BR>	 f. (-नी) A<BR>wooden baling vessel.<BR> E. अम्बु, and (वाहिन्) what bears.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=052-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बुवेतस|अम्बुवेतसः
अम्बुवेतस m. (-सः) A kind of cane or reed growing in water. See वेतस.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=052-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बुसर्पिणी
अम्बुसर्पिणी f. (-णी) A leech.<BR> E. अम्बु before सृप् to go, णिनि affix; and ङीष्<BR>fem. do.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=052-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बुसादन
अम्बुसादन n. (-नं) The nut of the Strychnos. See अम्बुप्रसादन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=052-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बुसेचनी
अम्बुसेचनी f. (-नी) A vessel used for baling water out of a boat. E.<BR>अम्बु, षिच् to sprinkle, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=052-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बुकृत
अम्बुकृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Sputtered, (speech, discourse.)<BR> E. अम्बु water, and<BR>कृत made.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=052-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्ब्ल|अम्ब्लः
अम्ब्ल m. (-ब्लः) Sourness.<BR> E. अम्ब to go, and क्ल Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=052-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्भस्|अंभस्
अम्भस् n. (-म्भः) Water.<BR> E. अप् water, before असुन् Unādi affix; नुम् is<BR>inserted, and प becomes भ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=052-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्भस्स्थ
अम्भस्स्थ mfn. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थं)<BR>	 1. What holds or contains water.<BR>	 2. Abiding<BR>in water.<BR> E. अम्भस् and स्थ what abides or where it abides.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=052-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्भस्सू
अम्भस्सू m. (-स्सूः) Smoke, cloudiness.<BR> E. अम्भस् water, and सू what produces.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=052-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्भोज|अम्भोजं|अम्भोजः
अम्भोज n. (-जं) A lotus.<BR>	 m. (-जः)<BR>	 1. The moon.<BR>	 2. The Sārasa or Indian<BR>crane.<BR>	 mfn. (-जः-जा-जं) Aquatic, water-born.<BR> E. अम्भस्, and ज produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=052-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्भोजजनि
अम्भोजजनि m. (-निः) BRAHMĀ, being born secondarily from a lotus. E.<BR>अम्भोज, and जनि birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=052-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्भोजयोनि|अम्भोजयोनिः
अम्भोजयोनि m. (-निः) A name of BRAHMĀ.<BR> E. अम्भोज, and योनि womb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=052-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्भोजिनी|अंभोजिनी
अम्भोजिनी f. (-नी) An assemblage of lotus flowers, or a place where they<BR>abound.<BR> E. अम्भोज a lotus, णिनि and ङीप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=052-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्भोद|अम्भोदः
अम्भोद m. (-दः) A cloud.<BR> E. अम्भस्, and द what gives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=052-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्भोधर|अम्भोधरः
अम्भोधर m. (-रः) A cloud.<BR> E. अम्भस् water, and धर what has.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=052-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्भोधि|अम्भोधिः
अम्भोधि m. (-धिः) The ocean.<BR> E. अम्भस्, and धि what possesses, from धा<BR>with the affix कि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=052-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्भोनिधि|अम्भोनिधिः
अम्भोनिधि m. (-धिः) The ocean.<BR> E. अम्भस्, and निधि a treasure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=052-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्भोराशि|अम्भोराशिः
अम्भोराशि m. (-शिः) The ocean.<BR> E. अम्भस्, and राशि a heap.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=052-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्भोरुह|अम्भोरुहं
अम्भोरुह n. (-हं) A lotus.<BR> E. अम्भस्, and रुह what rises or grows from रुह्<BR>with अच् affix; also with क्विप् affix; अम्भोरुह् nom. (-रुट्)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=052-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्मय|अम्मयं
अम्मय mfn. (-यः-यी-यं) Watery, formed from, or consisting of water, (as<BR>froth, &c.)<BR> E. अप् water, and मयट् affix; प is changed to म, and the<BR>fem. takes ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=052-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्र|अम्रः
अम्र m. (-म्रः) The mango tree, (Mangifera Indica.)<BR>	 n. (-म्रं) A mango. E.<BR>अम to eat, and र aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=052-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्रात|अम्रातः
अम्रात m. (-तः) A species of spondias or hog plum, (Spondias mangi-<BR>fera.)<BR> E. अम्र the mango, and अत to go, अच् affix; resembling that<BR>fruit, also अम्रातक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=052-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्रातक|अम्रातकः
अम्रातक m. (-कः) A tree. See the preceding.<BR> E. कन् being added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=052-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्ल|अम्लं|अम्लः
अम्ल mfn. (-म्लः-म्ला-म्लं) Sour, acid.<BR>	 m. (-म्लः) Sourness, acidity.<BR>	 f. (-म्ली)<BR>Wood sorrel, (Oxalis monadelpha.)<BR>	 n. (-म्लं) Sour curds.<BR> E. अम to be<BR>sick, क्ल Unādi affix, and ङीप् for the fem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=052-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्लक|अम्लकः
अम्लक m. (-कः) A plant, (Artocarpus lacucha.) See लकुच.<BR> E. अम्ल sourness,<BR>and क affix; having a sour taste.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=052-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्लकेशर|अम्लकेशरः
अम्लकेशर m. (-रः) The citron.<BR> E. अम्ल, and केशर a filament.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=053-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्लता
अम्लता f. (-ता) Sourness.<BR> E. अम्ल and तल् affix, also with त्व aff. अम्लत्व n.<BR>(-त्वं)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=053-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्लपनस|अम्लपनसः
अम्लपनस m. (-सः) A tree, (Artocarpus lacucha.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=053-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्लपित्त
अम्लपित्त m. (-त्तः) Acidity of stomach.<BR> E. अम्ल, and पित्त bile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=053-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्लफल|अम्लफलं|अम्लफलः
अम्लफल m. (-लः) The tamarind tree.<BR>	 n. (-लं) The fruit.<BR> E. अम्ल, and फल<BR>fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=053-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्लरस|अम्लरसः
अम्लरस mfn. (-सः-सा-सं) Sour, having a sour taste.<BR>	 m. (-सः) Sourness,<BR>acidity.<BR> E. अम्ल, and रस flavour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=053-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्ललोणिका
अम्ललोणिका f. (-का) Wood-sorrel, (Oxalis corniculata,) also अम्ललोणी and<BR>अम्ललोलिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=053-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्ललोणी
अम्ललोणी f. (-णी) See the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=053-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्ललोलिका
अम्ललोलिका f. (-का) See अम्ललोणिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=053-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्लवर्ग|अम्लवर्गः
अम्लवर्ग m. (-र्गः) A class of plants with acid leaves or fruits, as the lime,<BR>orange, pomegranate, tamarind, wood-apple, sorrel, Lakucha,<BR>Spondias and others.<BR> E. अम्ल, and वर्ग a class.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=053-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्लवाडव
अम्लवाडव m. (-वः) See अम्रात above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=053-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्लवातक
अम्लवातक m. (-कः) Hog plum, (Spondias mangifera.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=053-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्लवेतस|अम्लवेतसः
अम्लवेतस m. (-सः) A kind of dock or sorrel, (Rumex vesicarius.)<BR> E. अम्ल<BR>sour, and वेतस a kind of reed; sour grass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=053-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्लवासुक
अम्लवासुक n. (-कं) A kind of sorrel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=053-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्लवृक्ष|अम्लवृक्षं|अम्लवृक्षः
अम्लवृक्ष m. (-क्षः) The tamarind tree.<BR> E. अम्ल, and वृक्ष a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=053-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्लशाक|अम्लशाकं|अम्लशाकः
अम्लशाक n. (-कं) A sort of sorrel, (Rumex vesicarius,) commonly used<BR>as a potherb.<BR> E. अम्ल, and शाक a potherb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=053-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्लसार|अम्लसारं|अम्लसारः
अम्लसार n. (-रं) Rice-water after fermentation.<BR>	 m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. The lime.<BR>	 2. A<BR>sort of sorrel.<BR> E. अम्ल, and सार essence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=053-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्लाक्त
अम्लाक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं) Acidulated.<BR> E. अम्ल, and अक्त mixed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=053-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्लान|अम्लानः
अम्लान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>	 1. Clean, clear.<BR>	 2. Bright, unclouded.<BR>	 m. (-नः)<BR>Globe amaranth, (Gomphrena globosa.)<BR> E. अ neg. and म्लान dirty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=053-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्लानि|अम्लानिः
अम्लानि mfn. (-निः-निः-नि)<BR>	 1. Vigorous.<BR>	 2. Unfading.<BR>	 f. (-निः)<BR>	 1. Vigour.<BR>2. Freshness, verdure.<BR> E. अ neg. म्लानि soil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=053-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्लानिन्
अम्लानिन् mfn. (-नी-निनी-नि) Clean, clear.<BR>	 f. (-नी) An assemblage of lotus<BR>flowers.<BR> E. अ neg. म्लानिन् soiled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=053-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्लिका
अम्लिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. The tamarind tree.<BR>	 2. Wood sorrel, (Oxalis corniculata.)<BR>3. A sour taste in the mouth, acidity of stomach.<BR> E. अम्ल sour, कन्<BR>and टाप् affixes; इ being substituted for अ; also अम्लीका and आम्लका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=053-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्लीका
अम्लीका f. (-का) See the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=053-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्लोद्गार|अम्लोद्गारः
अम्लोद्गार m. (-रः) Sour eructation.<BR> E. अम्ल, and उद्गार bringing up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=053-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अय|अयः
अय r. 1st cl. (अयते) To go, to go to or towards. With प्रति to believe, to<BR>rely on. A preposition containing र substitutes ल before this root,<BR>as प्र and पर make प्लायते, पलायते to fly, to run away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=053-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अय|अयः
अय m. (-यः) Good luck, favourable fortune.<BR> E. इण to go, and अच् affix;<BR>happiness proceeding by it.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=053-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयज्ञ|अयज्ञः
अयज्ञ mfn. (-ज्ञः-ज्ञा-ज्ञं) Not offering sacrifice.<BR> E. अ neg. यज्ञ sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=053-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयज्ञक
अयज्ञक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Unfit for sacrifice.<BR> E. अ neg. यज्ञक sacrificial.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=053-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयज्ञिय
अयज्ञिय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Not sacrificial, common, profane.<BR> E. अ neg. यज्ञिय<BR>sacrificial.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=053-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयतिन्
अयतिन् mfn. (-ती-तिनी-ति) Incontinent, of unsubdued appetite.<BR> E. अ neg.<BR>यतिन् self-restraining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=053-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयत्न|अयत्नः
अयत्न m. (-त्नः) Absence of effort or exertion.<BR> E. अ neg. यत्न effort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=053-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयत्नकारिन्
अयत्नकारिन् mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि) Idle, indifferent, making no exertion.<BR> E. अ<BR>neg. यत्न effort, and कारिन् who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=053-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयत्नकृत
अयत्नकृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Spontaneous, readily or easily produced.<BR> E. अयत्न,<BR>and कृत done. So अयत्नभूत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=053-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयत्नवत्
अयत्नवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Idle, inactive, indifferent,<BR> E. अ neg. यत्नवत्<BR>active.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=053-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयथा
अयथा ind. Unsuitably, unfitly, inconsistently, incongruously.<BR> E. अ neg.<BR>and यथा as, (it should be.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=053-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयथातथ
अयथातथ mfn. (-थः-था-थं)<BR>	 1. Unprofitable, useless, vain.<BR>	 2. Unfit, unsuitable,<BR>incompatible.<BR> E. अ neg. यथा as, तथा so.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=053-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयथातथ्य
अयथातथ्य n. (-थ्यं) Unprofitableness, unsuitableness, incompatibility. E.<BR>अयथातथ and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=053-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयथार्थ
अयथार्थ mfn. (-र्थः-र्था-र्थं)<BR>	 1. Not according to the sense or object, incongru-<BR>ous, nonsensical, unmeaning.<BR>	 2. Improper, unfitting.<BR>	 3. False, un-<BR>true.<BR> E. अ neg. यथा as, अर्थ sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=053-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयथावत्
अयथावत् ind. Inaccurately, erroneously.<BR> E. अ neg. यथा as, and वति aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=053-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयथाबलम्
अयथाबलम् ind. Unsuitably, imperfectly.<BR> E. अयथा, and बल strength.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=053-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयथाशास्त्रकारिन्
अयथाशास्त्रकारिन् mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि) Irreligious.<BR> E. अ neg. यथा according to,<BR>शास्त्र scripture, and कारिन् who acts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=053-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयथेष्ट
अयथेष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>	 1. Insufficient, not enough.<BR>	 2. Disliked, dis-<BR>approved of.<BR> E. अ neg. यथेष्ट wished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=053-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयन|अयनं
अयन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. A road, a path.<BR>	 2. The half year, that is, the sun's road<BR>north and south of the equator. See उत्तरायण, &c.<BR>	 3. The equinoctial<BR>and solstitial points.<BR>	 4. A Śāstra or inspired writing.<BR> E. इण to<BR>go, and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=053-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयनकाल|अयनकालः
अयनकाल m. (-लः) The interval between the equinoxes.<BR> E. अयन, and<BR>काल time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=053-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयनभाग|अयनभागः
अयनभाग m. (-गः) See अयनांश.<BR> E. अयन, and भाग a part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=053-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयनांश|अयनांशः
अयनांश m. (-शः) The arc between the vernal equinoctial point and the<BR>beginning of the fixed zodiac or first point in Aries.<BR> E. अयन, and<BR>अंश a part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=053-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयन्त्रित|अयंत्रित|अयन्त्रितः
अयन्त्रित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Unrestrained, self-willed.<BR> E. अ neg. यन्त्रित res-<BR>trained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=053-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयवत्|अयवन्त्
अयवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Lucky, fortunate.<BR> E. अय and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=053-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयशस्
अयशस् mfn. (-शाः-शाः-शः) Infamous.<BR>	 n. (-शः) Infamy.<BR> E. अ neg. यशस् fame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=053-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयशस्कर
अयशस्कर mfn. (-रः-रा-री-रं) Disgraceful, degrading.<BR> E. अयशस् and कर what<BR>makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=053-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयशस्य
अयशस्य mfn. (-स्यः-स्या-स्यं) Infamous. So अयशस्विन् mfn. (-स्वी-स्विनी-स्वि) E.<BR>अयशस् and य or विनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=053-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयस्
अयस् n. (-यः) Iron.<BR>	 m. (-याः) A name of VAHNI or fire.<BR> E. इण to go, and<BR>असुन् Unādi. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=053-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयस्कान्त|अयस्कान्तः
अयस्कान्त m. (-न्तः) A precious stone, the loadstone.<BR> E. अयस् and कान्त<BR>beautiful, implying a gem, after this word and others, as सूर्य्यकान्त,<BR>&c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=053-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयस्कार
अयस्कार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. The upper part of the thigh.<BR>	 2. A blacksmith. E.<BR>अयस्, and कार an agent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=053-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयस्कुम्भ
अयस्कुम्भ m. (-म्भः) An iron pot or boiler.<BR> E. अयस् and कुम्भ a jar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=053-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयाचक|अयाचकः
अयाचक mfn. (-काः-का-कं) One who does not ask or solicit.<BR> E. अ neg. याचक<BR>who solicits.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=053-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयाचित|अयाचितं|अयाचितः
अयाचित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Unasked, unsolicited.<BR>	 m. (-तः) The name of a<BR>Muni or saint, also उपवर्ष.<BR> E. अ neg. and याचित asked, solicited.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=053-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयाज्य
अयाज्य mfn. (-ज्यः-ज्या-ज्यं) Outcaste, degraded, not competent to offer sa-<BR>crifice.<BR> E. अ neg. याज्य to be sacrificed; by whom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=053-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयातपूर्व्व|अयातपूर्व
अयातपूर्व्व mfn. (-र्व्वः-र्व्वा-र्व्वं) Following, subsequent to succeeding.<BR> E. अ neg.<BR>यातपूर्व्व preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=053-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयाथार्थिक
अयाथार्थिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>	 1. Improper, unjust.<BR>	 2. Absurd, incongruous. E.<BR>अयथार्थ and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=053-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयाथार्थ्य|अयाथार्थ्यं
अयाथार्थ्य n. (-र्थ्यं)<BR>	 1. Impropriety, unfitness.<BR>	 2. Absurdity, nonsense.<BR> E. अयथार्थ<BR>and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=053-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयान|अयानं
अयान n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Natural disposition or temperament.<BR>	 2. Halt, stop.<BR> E. अ<BR>neg. या to go, ल्युट् affix; what never departs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=053-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयानय|अयानयं|अयानयः
अयानय m. (-यः) A country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=053-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयानयीन|अयानयीनः
अयानयीन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Produced in, or brought from Ayanaya. E.<BR>अयानय and ख aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=053-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयावक
अयावक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Unstained with lac-dye, naturally red.<BR> E. अ neg.<BR>यावक of lac.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=053-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयि
अयि ind. A particle of encouragement, and asking; also a vocative parti-<BR>cle.<BR> E. इ to go, and इन् affix. by which one goes; what leads or calls.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=053-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयुक्च्छद
अयुक्च्छद m. (-दः) A plant, (Echites scholaris.) See सप्तपर्ण.<BR> E. अयुज् separate,<BR>and छद a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=053-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयुक्त|अयुक्तं
अयुक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>	 1. Separate, disjoined.<BR>	 2. Improper.<BR> E. अ neg.<BR>युक्त joined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=054-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयुक्ति|अयुक्तिः
अयुक्ति f. (-क्तिः)<BR>	 1. Disunion, separation.<BR>	 2. Unreasonableness, want of<BR>conformity to correct principles or to analogy.<BR>	 3. Impropriety, unfit-<BR>ness.<BR> E. अ neg. युक्ति union.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=054-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयुग
अयुग mfn. (-गः-गा-गं)<BR>	 1. Single, separate.<BR>	 2. Odd.<BR> E. अ neg. युग a pair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=054-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयुगपत्
अयुगपत् ind. Gradually, seriatim, not at once.<BR> E. अ neg. युगपत् at once.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=054-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयुगल
अयुगल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Single.<BR> E. अ neg. युगल a pair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=054-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयुगार्च्चिस्|अयुगार्चिस्
अयुगार्च्चिस् m. (-र्च्चिः) Fire.<BR> E. अयुग uneven, (seven) अर्च्चिस् ray.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=054-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयुग्म
अयुग्म mfn. (-ग्मः-ग्मा-ग्मं)<BR>	 1. Separate, divided, single.<BR>	 2. Odd, uneven. E.<BR>अ not, युग्म a pair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=054-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयुग्मच्छद|अयुग्मच्छदः|अयुग्मछद
अयुग्मच्छद m. (-दः) A plant, (Echites scholaris.)<BR> E. अ neg. युग्म double, and<BR>छद a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=054-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयुज्
अयुज् mfn. (-युक्)<BR>	 1. Separate, single.<BR>	 2. Odd, uneven.<BR> E. अ neg. युज्<BR>what joins.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=054-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयुत|अयुतं|अयुतः
अयुत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Disjoined, detached.<BR>	 n. (-तं) Ten thousand.<BR> E. अ neg.<BR>and युत joined, counted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=054-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयुद्ध
अयुद्ध n. (-द्धं) Peace, absence of war.<BR> E. अ neg. युद्ध war.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=054-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अये
अये ind. Oh! ah! &c. an interjection of; 1. Recollection; 2. Fatigue;<BR>3. Fear; 4. Passion; and 5. Calling.<BR> E. इ to go, एच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=054-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयोग|अयोगः
अयोग m. (-गः)<BR>	 1. Separation, disjunction.<BR>	 2. A widower, an absent<BR>lover or husband.<BR>	 3. Unfitness, unsuitableness.<BR>	 4. Medical treatment,<BR>counter to the symptoms.<BR>	 5. Consistent treatment, non-mixture of<BR>opposite qualities.<BR>	 6. Dislike, aversion to any thing.<BR>	 7. Vigorous<BR>effort, exertion.<BR>	 8. An iron hammer.<BR> E. अ neg. and योग union; or<BR>अयस् iron, and ग what goes, or is.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=054-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयोगव|अयोगवः
अयोगव mf. (-वः-वा-वी) The offspring of a Śūdra man, and Vaiśya wo-<BR>man.<BR> E. अयोग disjoined, and व from वा to go; being one of the<BR>lowest castes or tribes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=054-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयोगुड|अयोगुडः
अयोगुड m. (-डः)<BR>	 1. A chalybeate pill, one made of some preparation of<BR>iron.<BR>	 2. An iron ball.<BR> E. अयस्, and गुड a ball.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=054-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयोग्य
अयोग्य mfn. (-ग्यः-ग्या-ग्यं)<BR>	 1. Unfit, unsuitable.<BR>	 2. Useless.<BR> E. अ neg. योग्य fit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=054-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयोग्यता
अयोग्यता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Unfitness, unsuitableness, incongruity, impropriety.<BR>E. अयोग्य and तल् affix; also अयोग्यत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=054-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयोग्र|अयोग्रं
अयोग्र n. (-ग्रं)<BR>	 1. A pestle for cleaning grain.<BR>	 2. A mace or club tipped<BR>with iron.<BR>	 3. A hammer, a forge hammer.<BR> E. अयस्, and अग्र the end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=054-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयोघन|अयोघनः
अयोघन m. (-नः) A hammer, a forge hammer.<BR> E. अयस्, and घन what strikes,<BR>from हन् to kill or strike.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=054-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयोजन
अयोजन nf. (-नं-ना) Disunion, separation, distinctness.<BR> E. अ not, योजन<BR>uniting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=054-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयोदत्
अयोदत् mfn. (-दत्-दती-दत्) Iron-toothed.<BR> E. अयस्, and दत् for दन्त a tooth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=054-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयोध्य
अयोध्य mfn. (-ध्यः-ध्या-ध्यं) Not to be warred against.<BR>	 f. (-ध्या) The capital<BR>of RĀMA, Ayodhyā, the modern Oude.<BR> E. अ neg. युद्ध to make war,<BR>and ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=054-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयोनिज|अयोनिजः
अयोनिज mfn. (-जः-जा-जं) Generated equivocally, not born from the<BR>womb.<BR> E. अ neg. योनि the womb, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=054-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयोमय
अयोमय mfn. (-यः-यी-यं) Made of iron.<BR> E. अयस् and मयट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=054-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयोमल|अयोमलं
अयोमल n. (-लं) Rust of iron.<BR> E. अयस्, and मल dirt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=054-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयोमुख|अयोमुखः
अयोमुख mfn. (-खः-खा-खं) Tipped or pointed with iron.<BR>	 m. (-खः) A kind<BR>of goblin with an iron face.<BR> E. अयस्, and मुख a mouth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=054-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयोहृदय
अयोहृदय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Stern, unrelenting, iron-hearted.<BR> E. अयस्, and<BR>हृदय the heart.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=054-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर|अरं|अरः
अर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Swift, speedy.<BR>	 n. (-रं)<BR>	 1. The spoke or radius of a<BR>wheel.<BR>	 2. adv. Swiftly.<BR>	 m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A Jaina division of time, the sixth<BR>of an Avasarpiṇī or Utsarpiṇī. See अवसर्पिणी, &c.<BR>	 2. The eighteenth<BR>Jaina Tīrthakara, or deified saint.<BR> E. ऋ to go, अप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=054-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरक|अरकः
अरक m. (-कः) An aquatic plant, (Vallisneria.) See शैवाल.<BR> E. अर what goes,<BR>and वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=054-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरक्षित
अरक्षित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Not preserved, not kept.<BR>	 2. Unprotected, undefended.<BR>E. अ neg. रक्षित kept.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=054-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरग्वध
अरग्वध m. (-धः) A tree, (Cassia fistula.) See आरग्वध.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=054-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरघट्ट|अरघट्टः
अरघट्ट m. (-ट्टः)<BR>	 1. A machine for raising water from a well.<BR>	 2. A deep well.<BR>E. अर quickly, and घट्ट to move, affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=054-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरघट्टक|अरघट्टकः
अरघट्टक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A wheel for drawing water with.<BR>	 2. A deep or large<BR>well.<BR> E. कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=054-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरङ्गर|अरंगर|अरंगरः
अरङ्गर m. (-रः) Factitious or made up poison.<BR> E. अरम् quick, and गर<BR>poison.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=054-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरजस्
अरजस् mfn. (-जाः-जाः-जः)<BR>	 1. Free from the quality of passion.<BR>	 2. Free from<BR>desire, &c.<BR>	 f. (-जाः) A young girl.<BR> E. अ neg. रजस् the menstrual flux,<BR>or passion, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=054-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरटु|अरटुः
अरटु m. (-टुः) A plant, (Bignonia Indica.) See अरलु.<BR> E. ऋ to go, and अटच्<BR>aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=054-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरणि|अरणिः
अरणि mf. (-णिः-णी) Wood used for kindling a fire, exciting it by attri-<BR>tion.<BR>	 m. (-णिः)<BR>	 1. The plant of which especially the wood is used for<BR>this purpose. (Premna spinosa, &c.) See गणिकारिका.<BR>	 2. A flint.<BR>	 3.<BR>The sun.<BR> E. ऋ to go, and अनि Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=054-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरण्य|अरण्यं|अरण्यः
अरण्य nf. (-ण्यं-णी) A forest.<BR>	 m. (-ण्यः) Kayaphal, a drug so named. See<BR>कट्फल.<BR> E. ऋ to go, and अन्य Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=054-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरण्यकदली
अरण्यकदली f. (-ली) The wood or wild plantain.<BR> E. अरण्य, and कदली the<BR>plantain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=054-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरण्यकार्प्पासी|अरण्यकार्पासी
अरण्यकार्प्पासी f. (-सी) The wild cotton.<BR> E. अरण्य, and कार्प्पासी cotton.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=054-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरण्यचटक|अरण्यचटकः
अरण्यचटक m. (-कः) A wood sparrow.<BR> E. अरण्य, and चटक a sparrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=054-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरण्यज
अरण्यज mfn. (-जः-जा-जं) Produced or born in a forest.<BR> E. अरण्य, and ज<BR>born; also similar compounds, as अरण्यजात, अरण्योत्पन्न, अरण्यभव,<BR>अरण्यसम्भव, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=054-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरण्यजार्द्रका
अरण्यजार्द्रका f. (-का) Wild ginger.<BR> E. अरण्यज, and आर्द्रका ginger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=054-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरण्यधान्य|अरण्यधान्यं
अरण्यधान्य n. (-न्यं) Wild rice.<BR> E. अरण्य, and धान्य grain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=054-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरण्यमक्षिका
अरण्यमक्षिका f. (-का) The gad fly.<BR> E. अरण्य, and मक्षिका a fly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=054-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरण्यरक्षक|अरण्यरक्षकः
अरण्यरक्षक m. (-कः) Keeper of a forest, superintendent of a forest dis-<BR>trict.<BR> E. अरण्य, and रक्षक who protects.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=054-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरण्यवायस|अरण्यवायसः
अरण्यवायस m. (-सः) A raven.<BR> E. अरण्य, and वायस a crow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=054-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरण्यवास|अरण्यवासः
अरण्यवास m. (-सः) A hermitage.<BR> E. अरण्य a wood, and वास abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=054-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरण्यवासिन्
अरण्यवासिन् m. (-सी) A hermit, an anchorite.<BR> E. अरण्य, and वासिन् who<BR>resides.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=054-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरण्यशालि|अरण्यशालिः
अरण्यशालि m. (-लिः) Wild rice.<BR> E. अरण्य, and शालि rice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=054-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरण्यशूकर
अरण्यशूकर m. (-रः) The wild hog.<BR> E. अरण्य, and शूकर hog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=054-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरण्यश्वन्
अरण्यश्वन् m. (-श्वा) A wolf.<BR> E. अरण्य, and श्वन् a dog, the forest dog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=054-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरण्याध्यक्ष|अरण्याध्यक्षः
अरण्याध्यक्ष m. (-क्षः) Keeper or ranger of the forests, a headman or<BR>superintendent of a forest district, an officer in the old Hindu go-<BR>vernment.<BR> E. अरण्य, and अध्यक्ष superintendent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=054-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरण्यानी
अरण्यानी f. (-नी) A large forest.<BR> E. अरण्य, आनुक and ङीष् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=054-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरत
अरत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Dull, languid, apathetic.<BR>	 2. Disgusted, discon-<BR>tented.<BR> E. अ neg. रत interested.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=054-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरतत्रप|अरतत्रपः
अरतत्रप m. (-पः) a dog. अ neg. रत copulation, and त्रप ashamed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=054-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरति|अरतिः
अरति mfn. (-तिः-तिः-ति)<BR>	 1. Dull, languid.<BR>	 2. Discontented, unhappy.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-तिः) Anger, passion.<BR>	 f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Dissatisfaction, discontent.<BR>	 2.<BR>Dullness, languor.<BR>	 3. Absence of pleasure, pain.<BR>	 4. Anxiety, dis-<BR>tress.<BR> E. अ neg. and रति pleasure, or ऋ to go, and अति Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=054-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरत्नि|अरत्निः
अरत्नि m. (-त्निः)<BR>	 1. A cubit of the middle length, from the elbow to the<BR>tip of the little finger.<BR>	 2. The elbow.<BR> E. ऋ to go, and कत्नि Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=054-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरम|अरमः
अरम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं) Low, inferior See अवम<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=054-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरम्य
अरम्य mfn. (-म्यः-म्या-म्यं) Disagreeable.<BR> E. अ neg. रम्य pleasing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=054-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरर|अररं|अररः
अरर mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>	 1. A door.<BR>	 2. A covering, a sheathe.<BR>	 3. The sheathe<BR>of the shoot of a bamboo.<BR> E. अर from ऋ to go, and अरण् Uṇādi<BR>affix, ङीष् in the fem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=054-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अररि|अररिः
अररि mn. (-रिः-रि) A door.<BR> E. ऋ to go, and अरिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=054-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अररु|अररुः
अररु m. (-रुः) A enemy.<BR> E. ऋ to go, अरु Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=054-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अररे
अररे ind. A vocative particle, expressing haste.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=054-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरलु|अरलुः
अरलु m. (-लुः) A plant, (Bignonia Indica) See शोणाक<BR> E. ऋ to go, अरु<BR>affix, and र is changed to ल, also अरटु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=054-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरव
अरव mfn. (-वः-वा-वं) Silent.<BR> E. अ neg. रव sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=055-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरविन्द|अरविंदं|अरविन्दं|अरविन्दः
अरविन्द n. (-न्दं)<BR>	 1. lotus, (Nymphæa nelumbo.)<BR>	 2. Copper.<BR> E. अर quickly,<BR>and विन्द to obtain, श affix; with reference to the lotus, as of<BR>quick growth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=055-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरविन्दनाभि|अरविन्दनाभिः
अरविन्दनाभि m. (-भिः) VIṢṆU.<BR> E. अरविन्द, and नाभि the navel, from which<BR>sprung the lotus that bore BRAHMĀ at the creation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=055-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरविन्दिनी|अरविंदिनी
अरविन्दिनी f. (-नी) An assemblage of lotus flowers.<BR> E. अरविन्द, इनि and<BR>ङीप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=055-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरस|अरसः
अरस mfn. (-सः-सा-सं)<BR>	 1. Insipid, tasteless.<BR>	 2. Dull, flat, (as a composi-<BR>tion.)<BR> E. अ neg. रस flavour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=055-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरसिक|अरसिकः
अरसिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>	 1. Unfeeling, dull, devoid of taste 2. Flavourless,<BR>insipid, liter. or fig.<BR> E. अ neg. रसिक flavoured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=055-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरहित
अरहित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Having, possessed of.<BR> E. अ neg. रहित left.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=055-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अराग
अराम mfn. (-गः-गा-गं) Cool, unimpassioned.<BR> E. अ neg. राग passion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=055-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरागिन्
अरागिन् mfn. (-गी-गिनी-गि) Cool, unimpassioned.<BR> E. अ neg. रागिन्<BR>impassioned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=055-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अराजक|अराजकः
अराजक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Anarchical, having no king or governor.<BR> E. अ<BR>neg. राजन् a king, कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=055-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अराति|अरातिः
अराति m. (-तिः) An enemy.<BR> E. अ neg. and रा to give, with ति affix; who<BR>does not give pleasure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=055-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरातिभङ्ग|अरातिभंग|अरातिभङ्गः
अरातिभङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः) Defeat or destruction of a foe.<BR> E. अराति, and भङ्ग<BR>breaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=055-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अराल|अरालं|अरालः
अराल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Crooked.<BR>	 m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. Resin.<BR>	 2. An elephant in rut.<BR>3. A bent or crooked arm.<BR>	 f. (-ला)<BR>	 1. A modest woman.<BR>	 2. A<BR>disloyal or unchaste one.<BR> E. अर what goes. आ before ला to take or<BR>give, and क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=055-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरि|अरिः
अरि m. (-रिः)<BR>	 1. An enemy.<BR>	 2. A wheel.<BR>	 3. A species of Khadira or<BR>Mimosa.<BR> E. ऋ to go, अच् affix, and इ substituted for अ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=055-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिकुल
अरिकुल n. (-लं) Family of an enemy.<BR> E. अरि, and कुल family.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=055-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिक्थभाज्
अरिक्थभाज् mfn. (-भाक्) Not entitled to a share of the property, a non-<BR>heir.<BR> E. अ neg. रिक्थभाज् a co-heir.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=055-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिता
अरिता f. (-ता) Enmity, hostility.<BR> E. अरि and तल् affix, also with त्व, अरित्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=055-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरित्र|अरित्रं|अरित्रः
अरित्र n. (-त्रं) A rudder.<BR> E. ऋ to go, and इत्रन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=055-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिनन्दन
अरिनन्दन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Gratifying an enemy, affording triumph to an<BR>enemy.<BR> E. अरि, and नन्दन what delights.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=055-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिन्दम|अरिंदम|अरिन्दमः
अरिन्दम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं) Conquering, victorious,<BR> E. अरि, and दम to tame,<BR>affix खच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=055-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिपुर
अरिपुर n. (-रं) An enemy's town or country.<BR> E. अरि, and पुर a city.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=055-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिमित्र
अरिमित्र m. (-त्रः) An ally or friend of an enemy.<BR> E. अरि, and मित्र a<BR>friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=055-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिमेद|अरिमेदः
अरिमेद m. (-दः) A fetid Mimosa, (M. Farnesiana.)<BR> E. अरि an enemy,<BR>and मेद what injures.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=055-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिराष्ट्र
अरिराष्ट्र n. (-ष्ट्रं) An enemy's country.<BR> E. अरि, and राष्ट्र a country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=055-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिलोक
अरिलोक m. (-कः) A hostile tribe or an enemy's country.<BR> E. अरि, and लोक<BR>a country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=055-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिष|अरिषं|अरिषः
अरिष m. (-षः)<BR>	 1. Disease arising from meat and drink.<BR>	 2. A stream of<BR>water from the clouds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=055-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिष्ट|अरिष्टं|अरिष्टः
अरिष्ट m. (-ष्टः)<BR>	 1. The soap-berry plant, (Sapindus saponaria, &c.)<BR>	 2.<BR>Garlick.<BR>	 3. The Nimb tree, (Melia azadaracta.)<BR>	 4. A crow.<BR>	 5. A<BR>heron.<BR>	 6. The name of an Asura or infernal spirit.<BR>	 n. (-ष्टं)<BR>	 1. A<BR>woman's apartment, the lying-in chamber.<BR>	 2. Good fortune, happi-<BR>ness.<BR>	 3. Bad or ill luck, misfortune.<BR>	 4. Buttermilk.<BR>	 5. Vinous spirit.<BR>6. Sign or symptom of approaching death.<BR>	 7. A portent, some<BR>natural phenomenon considered as indicating calamity.<BR> E. अ neg.<BR>and रिष्ट bad or good fortune.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=055-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिष्टक|अरिष्टकः
अरिष्टक m. (-कः) The soap-berry plant, (Sapindus saponaria, &c.)<BR> E. अ<BR>neg. and रिष्ट affliction, क affix; relieving sickness, &c. See the<BR>preceding, of which it may have all the meanings.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=055-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिष्टताति|अरिष्टतातिः
अरिष्टताति mfn. (-तिः-तिः-ति) Auspicious, making fortunate or happy. E.<BR>अरिष्ट, तन to spread, and डाति aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=055-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिष्टदुष्टधी
अरिष्टदुष्टधी mfn. (-धीः-धीः-धि) Apprehensive of death, alarmed at its<BR>approach.<BR> E. अरिष्ट sign of death, दुष्ट disturbed, and धी under-<BR>standing, mind; whose is so.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=055-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिष्टनेमि|अरिष्टनेमिः
अरिष्टनेमि m. (-मिः) The twenty-second of the twenty-four Jaina Tīrthakaras<BR>or saints. Also नेमि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=055-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिष्टसूदन|अरिष्टसूदनः
अरिष्टसूदन m. (-नः) A name of KṚṢṆA or VIṢṆU.<BR> E. अरिष्ट the Asura so<BR>named, and सूदन who destroys; having killed the demon ARIṢṬA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=055-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिष्टानक
अरिष्टानक m. (-कं) Consternation, defeat.<BR> E. अरि, and स्थानक being in place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=055-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिहिंसक|अरिहिंसकः
अरिहिंसक m. (-कः) An avenger.<BR> E. अरि, and हिंसक who injures.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=055-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुग्ण
अरुग्ण mfn. (-ग्णः-ग्णा-ग्णं) Healthy, well.<BR> E. अ neg. रुग्ण sick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=055-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुचि|अरुचिः
अरुचि f. (-चिः)<BR>	 1. Aversion, dislike.<BR>	 2. Want of appetite, disrelish, dis-<BR>gust.<BR> E. अ neg. रुचि light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=055-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुचिर
अरुचिर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Disagreeable, disgusting.<BR> E. अ neg. रुचिर agreeable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=055-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुच्य
अरुच्य mfn. (-च्यः-च्या-च्यं) Disagreeable.<BR> E. अ neg. रुच्य to be liked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=055-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुज्
अरुज् mfn. (-रुक् or रुग्) Sound, healthy, free from disease.<BR> E. अ neg. रुज् sick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=055-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुण|अरुणं|अरुणः
अरुण m. (-णः)<BR>	 1. A name of the sun.<BR>	 2. Also of his charioteer, or the dawn<BR>personified as the son of KAŚYAPA by VINATA.<BR>	 3. The colour of the<BR>dawn, dark red, or the mixture of red and black.<BR>	 4. Tawny, (the<BR>colour.)<BR>	 5. The redness of sunset.<BR>	 6. A kind of leprosy, with red spots<BR>and insensibility of the skin.<BR>	 7. A dumb man.<BR>	 4. (णा)<BR>	 1. A plant,<BR>(Betula.) See अतिविषा.<BR>	 2. Mader, (Rubia manjith.)<BR>	 3. Another plant,<BR>commonly Teori. See त्रिवृत्.<BR>	 4. A black kind of the same.<BR>	 5. Colocynth<BR>or bitter apple.<BR>	 6. The plant that yields the red and black berry<BR>from which the jeweller's weight, the Retti, is derived. See गुञ्जा.<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Tawny, dark red, &c.<BR> E. ऋ to go, and उनन् Udādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=055-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुणकमल|अरुणकमलं
अरुणकमल n. (-लं) The red lotus.<BR> E. अरुण, and कमल a lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=055-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुणलोचन|अरुणलोचनः
अरुणलोचन m. (-नः) A pigeon.<BR> E. अरुण, and लोचन the eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=055-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुणसारथि|अरुणसारथिः
अरुणसारथि m. (-थिः) The sun.<BR> E. अरुण, and सारथि a charioteer; whose<BR>charioteer is ARUṆA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=055-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुणाग्रज|अरुणाग्रजः
अरुणाग्रज m. (-जः) GARUḌA, the bird of VIṢṆU.<BR> E. अरुण, and अग्रज first<BR>born; having ARUṆA as his elder brother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=055-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुणात्मज|अरुणात्मजः
अरुणात्मज m. (-जः) A name of JAṬĀYU, a fabulous bird: said by some to<BR>be the son of ARUṆA, but more generally of GARUḌA.<BR> E. अरुण, and<BR>आत्मज the son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=055-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुणावरज|अरुणावरजः
अरुणावरज m. (-जः) A name of GARUḌA.<BR> E. अरुण, अवर after, and ज born;<BR>the younger brother of ARUṆA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=055-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुणित
अरुणित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Reddened.<BR>	 2. Dyed red, impurpled.<BR> E. अरुण and<BR>इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=055-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुणिमन्
अरुणिमन् m. (-मा) Redness.<BR> E. अरुण and इमनिच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=055-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुणीकृत
अरुणीकृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Reddened, turning or become red.<BR> E. अरुण, and<BR>कृत made, च्वि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=055-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुणोदय|अरुणोदयः
अरुणोदय m. (-यः) Break of day, dawn, the period preceding sunset. E.<BR>अरुण dawn, उदय rise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=055-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुणोपल|अरुणोपलः
अरुणोपल m. (-लः) A ruby.<BR> E. अरुण dark red, and उपल a stone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=055-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुदित
अरुदित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Unwept, unlamented.<BR>	 2. Not weeping.<BR> E. अ neg.<BR>रुदित wept.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=055-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुद्ध
अरुद्ध mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं) Free, unobstructed.<BR> E. अ neg. रुद्ध obstructed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=055-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुन्तुद|अरुंतुद|अरुन्तुदः
अरुन्तुद mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>	 1. Sharp, corrosive.<BR>	 2. Acrimonious, sharp, sour,<BR>(as disposition.)<BR> E. अरुस् a sore, and तुद what torments, from तुद<BR>and खश् affix; the final of अरुस् is dropped, and नुम् inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=055-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुन्तुदत्व
अरुन्तुदत्व n. (-त्वं)<BR>	 1. Infliction of pain.<BR>	 2. Acrimoniousness, causticity. E.<BR>त्व added to the last. Also अरुन्तुदता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=055-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुन्धती|अरुंधती
अरुन्धती f. (-ती) The daughter of KARDAMA and wife of VASIṢṬHA,<BR>one of the seven Ṛṣis; she is also one of the Pleiades.<BR> E. अ neg.<BR>रुध to confine, तन् and ङीप् affixes; who does not confine or hinder<BR>good works. ARUNDHATĪ is considered as pattern of conjugal ex-<BR>cellence, and is invoked at the marriage ceremony by the bridegroom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=055-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुन्धतीजानि|अरुन्धतीजानिः
अरुन्धतीजानि m. (-निः) VASIṢṬHA, one of the seven Ṛṣis or saints,<BR>and stars in the great bear.<BR> E. अरुन्धती and जानि from जाया a wife;<BR>whose wife is ARUNDHATĪ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=055-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुन्धतीनाथ|अरुन्धतीनाथः
अरुन्धतीनाथ m. (-थः) A name of VASIṢṬHA, as above.<BR> E. अरुन्धती and नाथ<BR>a lord or husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=056-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुश
अरुश mfn. (-शः-शा-शं) Smooth, liter. or fig.<BR> E. अ neg. रुश rough.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=056-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुष्क|अरुष्कः
अरुष्क m. (-ष्कः) The marking-nut plant, see the next word.<BR> E. अरुस् a<BR>sore, and क what makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=056-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुष्कर|अरुष्करं|अरुष्करः
अरुष्कर mfn. (-रः-री-रं) Corrosive, caustic, acrid.<BR>	 m. (-रः) The marking-<BR>nut plant, (Semecarpius anacardium.)<BR>	 n. (-रं) The nut.<BR> E. अरुस् a<BR>sore, कृ to make, ट aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=056-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुष्ट
अरुष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं) Calm, not angry.<BR> E. अ neg. रुष्ट angry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=056-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुस्
अरुस् mn. (-रुः) A sore or wound.<BR>	 m. (-रुः) The sun. ind. A joint.<BR> E. ऋ<BR>to go, and उसि Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=056-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुसिका
अरुसिका f. (-का) Eruptions on the scalp, with acute pain.<BR> E. अरुस् a sore,<BR>कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=056-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरूप|अरूपः
अरूप mfn. (-पः-पा-पी-पं)<BR>	 1. Formless, shapeless.<BR>	 2. Ugly, ill formed,<BR>misshapen.<BR>	 3. Dissimilar, unlike.<BR> E. अ neg. रूप beauty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=056-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरूपक
अरूपक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Literal, without figure or metaphor.<BR> E. अ neg.<BR>रूपक figurative.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=056-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरूपता
अरूपता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Ugliness.<BR>	 2. Shapelessness.<BR>	 3. Dissimilarity.<BR> E. तल्<BR>added to अरूप, also अरूपत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=056-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरूपवत्|अरूपवन्त्
अरूपवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Ugly, shapeless.<BR> E. अरूप and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=056-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरूष|अरूषः
अरूष m. (-षः)<BR>	 1. A kind of snake.<BR>	 2. The sun.<BR> E. ऋ to go, ऊषन् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=056-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरे
अरे ind. Interjection of calling to inferiors.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=056-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरेरे
अरेरे ind.<BR>	 1. Interjection of calling to inferiors.<BR>	 2. Also of calling angrily.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=056-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरोक|अरोकः
अरोक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Obscured, dimmed, darkened.<BR> E. रुच् to be light,<BR>घञ् affix; अ neg. prefix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=056-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरोकदत्|अरोकदन्त्
अरोकदत् mfn. (-दत्-दती-दत्) Having black or discoloured teeth.<BR> E. अरोक,<BR>and दत् for दन्त a tooth, also अरोकदन्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=056-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरोकदन्त|अरोकदंत
अरोकदन्त mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं) Having bad teeth; see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=056-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरोग|अरोगः
अरोग mfn. (-गः-गा-गं) Well, healthy, free from disease.<BR>	 m. (-गः) Health.<BR>E. अ neg. रोग sickness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=056-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरोगिता
अरोगिता f. (-ता) Health.<BR> E. अरोगिन् well, तल् affix, or with त्व अरोगित्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=056-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरोगिन्
अरोगिन् mfn. (-गी-गिणी-गि) Well, in health.<BR> E. अ neg. रोगिन् sick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=056-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरोचक|अरोचकः
अरोचक m. (-कः) Indigestion, loss of appetite.<BR> E. अ neg. रोचक digestion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=056-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरोचिष्णु
अरोचिष्णु mfn. (-ष्णुः-ष्णुः-ष्णुं)<BR>	 1. Disagreeable.<BR>	 2. Dark.<BR>	 3. Ugly.<BR> E. अ neg.<BR>रोचिष्णु splendid, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=056-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरोदन
अरोदन n. (-नं) Not weeping.<BR> E. अ neg. रोदन weeping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=056-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरोध्य
अरोध्य mfn. (-ध्यः-ध्या-ध्यं) Unobstructed, unobstructable.<BR> E. अ neg. रोध्य<BR>to be hindered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=056-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरोपण
अरोपण n. (-णं) Not planting or fixing.<BR> E. अ neg. रोपण setting up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=056-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरोष|अरोषः
अरोष m. (-षः) Calmness.<BR> E. अ neg. रोष wrath.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=056-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरौद्र
अरौद्र mfn. (-द्रः-द्री-द्रं) Not formidable or fierce.<BR> E. अ neg. रौद्र formidable<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=056-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्क|अर्कः|अर्क्क
अर्क r. 10th cl. (अर्कयति)<BR>	 1. To praise.<BR>	 2. To heat or warm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=056-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्क|अर्कः|अर्क्क
अर्क m. (-र्कः)<BR>	 1. The sun.<BR>	 2. Crystal.<BR>	 3. Swallow wort, (Calotropis<BR>gigantea)<BR>	 4. Copper.<BR>	 5. A name of INDRA.<BR>	 6. A Pandit or learned<BR>man.<BR>	 7. An elder brother.<BR>	 8. Sunday.<BR> E. अर्च to worship or respect,<BR>क Unādi affix, and the च is dropped; what is worshipped or res-<BR>pected: or अर्क to heat, affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=056-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्कज|अर्कजः
अर्कज du.<BR>	 m. (-जौ) The two sons of SŪRYA and AŚVINĪ, and physicians<BR>of Svarga<BR> E. अर्क the sun, and ज who is born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=056-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्कतनय|अर्कतनयः
अर्कतनय m. (-यः) The sons of SŪRYA or the sun, applicable to YAMA, to<BR>SANI, to the Munis VAIVASWATA and SAVARNI, to REVANTA, and<BR>to KARṆA.<BR>	 f. (-या) The daughter of the sun, applied to the river<BR>goddesses JAMUNA and TAPTI.<BR> E. अर्क, and तनय a son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=056-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्कत्विष्
अर्कत्विष् f. (-त्विट्)<BR>	 1. A ray of light.<BR>	 2. The light of the sun.<BR> E. अर्क, and<BR>त्विष् radiance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=056-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्कदिन
अर्कदिन n. (-नं) A solar day.<BR> E. अर्क, and दिन a day: also अर्कदिवसं, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=056-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्कनन्दन|अर्कनन्दनः
अर्कनन्दन m. (-नः) YAMA, &c. see अर्कतनय. E. As before, and नन्दन a son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=056-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्कपत्र|अर्कपत्रः
अर्कपत्र m. (-त्रः) Swallow wort, (Calotropis gigantea.)<BR>	 f. (-त्रा) A kind of<BR>birth wort, (Aristolochia Indica.)<BR> E. अर्क the swallow wort, and पत्र<BR>a leaf: the leaves of the two plants being similar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=056-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्कपर्ण|अर्कपर्णः|अर्क्कपर्ण
अर्कपर्ण m. (-र्णः) Swallow wort, (Asclepias gigantea,) or Calotropis.<BR> E. रक<BR>the sun, पर्ण a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=056-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्कपादप|अर्कपादपः
अर्कपादप m. (-पः) The Nimb tree, (Nimba or Melia azadaracta.)<BR> E. अर्क,<BR>and पादप a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=056-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्कपुष्पिका
अर्कपुष्पिका f. (-का) A plant, vulgarly Arkahuli, (Cleome pentaphylla.)<BR>Also अर्कपुष्पी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=056-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्कबन्धु|अर्कबन्धुः
अर्कबन्धु m. (-न्धुः) A name of BUDDHA, the founder of the BUDDHA sect<BR>of Hindus.<BR> E. अर्क the sun, and बन्धु a kinsman, being of the Surya<BR>Vansa's, or line of the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=056-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्कबान्धव|अर्कबान्धवः
अर्कबान्धव m. (-वः) See the preceding. E. As before, बान्धव a kinsman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=056-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्कमण्डल
अर्कमण्डल n. (-लं) The disc of the sun.<BR> E. अर्क and मण्डल a circle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=056-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्कमूला
अर्कमूला f. (-ला) Birthwort. See अर्कपत्रा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=056-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्करेतोज|अर्करेतोजः
अर्करेतोज m. (-जः) REVANTA the son of SŪRYA.<BR> E. अर्क, रेतस् the semen,<BR>and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=056-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्कवर्ष|अर्कवर्षः
अर्कवर्ष m. (-र्षः) A solar year.<BR> E. अर्क, and वर्ष a year; also अर्कवत्सर,<BR>&c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=056-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्कव्रत|अर्कव्रतं|अर्कव्रतः
अर्कव्रत n. (-तं)<BR>	 1. Levying taxes, subjecting the people to heavy imposts,<BR>drawing their wealth as the sun evaporizes water.<BR>	 2. Periodical wor-<BR>ship of the sun.<BR> E. अर्क the sun, and व्रत observance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=056-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्कसूनु|अर्कसूनुः
अर्कसूनु m. (-नः) YAMA, regent of the dead.<BR> E. अर्क, and सूनु a son: the son<BR>of SŪRYA. See अर्कतनय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=056-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्कसोदर|अर्कसोदरः
अर्कसोदर m. (-रः) The elephant of INDRA.<BR> E. अर्क, सोदर kinsman, from स<BR>with, and उदर womb; from their being alike engaged in maintain-<BR>ing the universe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=056-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्कांश|अर्कांशः
अर्कांश m. (-शः) A digit or twelfth of the sun's disc.<BR> E. अर्क, and अंश a<BR>part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=056-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्काश्मन्
अर्काश्मन् m. (-श्मा)<BR>	 1. A crystal lens. See सूर्य्यकान्त.<BR>	 2. A ruby.<BR> E. अर्क and<BR>अश्मन् a stone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=056-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्काह्न
अर्काह्न m. (-ह्नः) Swallow wort.<BR> E. अर्क, and अह्न application: bearing all<BR>the synonyms of the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=056-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्केन्दुसङ्गम|अर्केन्दुसंगम|अर्केन्दुसंगमः
अर्केन्दुसङ्गम m. (-मः) The instant of conjunction of the sun and moon. E.<BR>अर्क the sun, इन्दु the moon, and सङ्गम union.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=056-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्कोपल|अर्कोपलः
अर्कोपल m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. The sun-stone.<BR>	 2. A ruby.<BR>	 3. A crystal lens.<BR> E. अर्क,<BR>and उपल a stone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=056-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्गल|अर्गलं|अर्गलः
अर्गल mf. (-लः-ला or -ली) A wooden bolt or pin for fastening a door.<BR>	 mfn.<BR>(-लः-ला-लं) A surge or billow.<BR> E. अर्ज to gain. कलच् affix, ज becomes<BR>ग, and the fem. takes both टाप् and ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=056-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्गलिका
अर्गलिका f. (-का) A small door pin, a bolt. E. As before, कन् affix, टाप्<BR>for the fem. and इ substituted for अ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=056-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्घ|अर्घः
अर्घ r. 1st cl. (अर्घति) To hurt or injure. r. 10th cl. (अर्घयति) To cost, to<BR>be worth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=056-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्घ|अर्घः
अर्घ m. (-र्घः)<BR>	 1. Price, cost.<BR>	 2. Mode of worship or reverence.<BR>	 3. An obla-<BR>tion of various ingredients to a god or Brahman.<BR> E. अर्घ to cost, or<BR>अर्ह to worship, ह being changed to घ, affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=056-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्घदान
अर्घदान n. (-नं) Presentation of a respectful offering.<BR> E. अर्घ, and दान<BR>giving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=056-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्घबलाबल
अर्घबलाबल n. (-लं) Rate of price, proper price.<BR> E. अर्घ, and बल strength,<BR>अबल weakness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=056-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्घसंख्यापन
अर्घसंख्यापन n. (-नं) Fixing the price of commodities, appraising, assize.<BR>E. अर्घ, and संख्यापन fixing together with: it is the act of the king or<BR>ruler, in concert with the traders, and should be done once a week<BR>or once a fortnight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=056-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्घार्ह
अर्घार्ह mfn. (-र्हः-र्हा-र्हं) Worthy of or requiring a respectful offering, a<BR>superior.<BR> E. अर्घ, and अर्ह worthy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=056-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्घीश|अर्घीशः
अर्घीश m. (-शः) A name of ŚIVA.<BR> E. अर्घ oblation, and ईश lord: the lord<BR>of offerings.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=056-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्घ्य|अर्घ्यं
अर्घ्य mfn. (-र्घ्यः-र्घ्या-र्घ्यं) Venerable, deserving worship.<BR>	 n. (-र्घ्यं) A respect-<BR>ful oblation to gods or venerable men, of rice, durva grass, flowers,<BR>&c. with water only and of water in a small boat-shaped vessel.<BR>n. (-र्घ्यं) Wild honey. e. अर्घ, and य or यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=056-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्च|अर्च्च
अर्च r. 1st cl. (अर्चति) Also 1st and 10th cls. (अर्चति-ते अर्चयति-ते) To wor-<BR>ship, to honour or treat with respect: with सम् prefixed, to worship.<BR>This root and its derivatives are also read अर्च्च, &c. doubling the con-<BR>sonant after र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=057-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्चक|अर्चकः|अर्च्चक|अर्च्चकः
अर्चक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) A worshipper, one who worships.<BR> E. अर्च and वुन्.<BR>aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=057-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्चन|अर्च्चनं
अर्चन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) An article of worship.<BR>	 nf. (-नं-ना) Worship, the<BR>homage paid to deities and to superiors.<BR> E. अर्च to worship, युच्<BR>affix, and टाप् fem. do.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=057-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्चनीय
अर्चनीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Venerable, respectable.<BR> E. अर्च, and अनीयर् affix,<BR>also अर्च्य and अर्चयितव्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=057-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्चा|अर्च्चा
अर्चा f. (-र्चा)<BR>	 1. Worship, see अर्चन.<BR>	 2. An image.<BR> E. अर्च to worship, अच्<BR>affix, and टाप् fem. do.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=057-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्चि|अर्चिः|अर्च्चिः
अर्चि f. (-र्चिः) Flame.<BR> E. अर्च to worship, इन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=057-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्चित|अर्च्चितः
अर्चित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Worshipped, respected, saluted.<BR> E. अर्च in the<BR>part. past.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=057-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्चिष्मत्|अर्चिष्मन्त्
अर्चिष्मत् mfn. (-ष्मान्-ष्मती-ष्मत्) Brilliant, resplendent.<BR>	 m. (-ष्मान्)<BR>	 1. Fire.<BR>2. The sun.<BR> E. अर्चिस् flame, and मतुप् poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=057-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्चिस्|अर्च्चिस्
अर्चिस् m. (-र्चिः)<BR>	 1. Flame.<BR>	 2. A ray of light.<BR>	 3. Light, luster.<BR> E. अर्च to<BR>worship, and इसि Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=057-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्च्य
अर्च्य mfn. (-र्च्यः-र्च्या-र्च्यं) Reverend, respectable, worshipful.<BR> E. अर्च to<BR>worship, and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=057-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्ज|अर्ज्ज
अर्ज r. 1st cl. (-अर्जति) To earn, to gain or acquire, (commonly used with<BR>उप prefixed.) 10th cl. (अर्जयति)<BR>	 1. The same, and: 2. To work or<BR>manufacture.<BR>	 3. To make or prepare. This root and its derivatives<BR>are also read अर्ज्ज, &c. doubling the consonant after र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=057-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्जक|अर्जकः|अर्ज्जक|अर्ज्जकः
अर्जक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) An acquirer, one who gains or acquires.<BR>	 m. (-कः)<BR>Basil, the white sort, (Ocymum villosum.)<BR> E. अर्ज to gain, and वुन्<BR>aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=057-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्जन|अर्जनं|अर्ज्जनं
अर्जन n. (-नं) Gain, acquisition of wealth, &c.<BR> E. अर्ज, and ल्युट् affix, also<BR>written अर्ज्जन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=057-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्जित
अर्जित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Gained, acquired.<BR> E. अर्ज to gain, क्त affix, also<BR>written अर्ज्जित.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=057-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्जुन|अर्जुनं|अर्जुनः
अर्जुन m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. The third of the Pāndavas, the son of INDRA and<BR>friend of KṚṢṆA.<BR>	 2. The name of a king with a thousand arms.<BR>See कार्त्तवीर्य्य.<BR>	 3. A tree, (Pentaptera arjuna.)<BR>	 4. A peacock.<BR>	 5. The<BR>only son of his mother.<BR>	 6. White, (the colour.)<BR>	 nf. (-नं-नी)<BR>	 1. Grass.<BR>2. Slight inflammation of the conjunctiva or white of the eye.<BR>	 f.<BR>(-नी)<BR>	 1. A cow.<BR>	 2. UṢĀ, the wife of ANIRUDDHA.<BR>	 3. The Karatoyā<BR>river in the north of Bengal.<BR>	 4. A procuress, a bawd.<BR>	 mfn. (-नः-नी-नं)<BR>White.<BR> E. अर्ज to gain, उनन् Unādi affix, fem. ङीप्, also read अर्ज्जुन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=057-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्जुनक|अर्जुनकः
अर्जुनक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Belonging to ARJUNA.<BR> E. अर्जुन and वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=057-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्जुनतस्
अर्जुनतस् ind. On the side or party of ARJUNA.<BR> E. अर्जुन and तसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=057-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्जुनच्छवि|अर्जुनछवि
अर्जुनच्छवि mfn. (-विः-विः-वि) White, of a white colour.<BR> E. अर्जुन white, and<BR>छवि light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=057-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्जुनध्वज|अर्जुनध्वजः|अर्ज्जुनध्वजः
अर्जुनध्वज m. (-जः) The monkey HANUMAN.<BR> E. अर्जुन, and ध्वज a banner,<BR>being ARJUNA'S symbol.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=057-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्जुनोपम|अर्जुनोपमः|अर्ज्जुनोपम|अर्ज्जुनोपमः
अर्जुनोपम m. (-मः) The teak tree, (Tectona grandis.)<BR> E. अर्जुन a tree, &c.<BR>उपम like.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=057-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्ण|अर्णः
अर्ण m. (-र्णः)<BR>	 1. The teak tree.<BR>	 2. A letter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=057-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्णव|अर्णवः|अर्ण्णव
अर्णव m. (-वः) The ocean.<BR> E. अर्णस् water, व affix, and स is dropped: the<BR>ण in this and similar words is optionally doubled, as अर्ण्णव, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=057-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्णवज|अर्णवजः|अर्ण्णवज
अर्णवज mfn. (-जः-जा-जं) Sea-born, marine.<BR>	 mn. (-जः-जं) Cuttlefish. E.<BR>अर्णव, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=057-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्णवमन्दिर|अर्णवमन्दिरः
अर्णवमन्दिर m. (-रः) VARUṆA, regent of the water.<BR> E. अर्णव the ocean,<BR>and मन्दिर a house; whose dwelling is the deep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=057-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्णवपोत|अर्णवपोतः
अर्णवपोत m. (-तः) A boat or ship.<BR> E. अर्णव, and पोत a boat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=057-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्णवयान
अर्णवयान n. (-नं) A boat or ship.<BR> E. अर्णव, and यान vehicle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=057-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्णस्
अर्णस् n. (-र्णः) Water.<BR> E. ऋ to go, असुन् Unādi affix, and नट् inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=057-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्णोद|अर्णोदः|अर्ण्णोद
अर्णोद m. (-दः) A cloud.<BR> E. अणस्, and द what gives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=057-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्णोभव|अर्णोभवः|अर्ण्णोभव
अर्णोभव m. (-वः) A shell.<BR> E. अर्णस्, and भव being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=057-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्त्तगल|अर्तगल|अर्तगलः|अर्त्तगलः
अर्त्तगल m. (-लः) Blue barleria, (B. cærulea.)<BR> E. आर्त्त exhausted, and गल<BR>to drop, the आ is made short, also आर्त्तगल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=057-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्त्तन|अर्तन|अर्त्तनं
अर्त्तन n. (-नं) Censure, reproach, abuse.<BR> E. ऋति to blame, a sautra root<BR>and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=057-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्त्ति|अर्ति|अर्तिः|अर्त्तिः
अर्त्ति f. (-र्त्तिः)<BR>	 1. Pain.<BR>	 2. The end of a bow.<BR> E. अर्द to hurt, and क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=057-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्त्तिक
अर्त्तिक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Diseased, pained.<BR>	 m. (-कः) a kind of cake.<BR> E. अर्त्ति<BR>pain, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=057-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्त्तिका|अर्तिका
अर्त्तिका f. (-का) An elder sister, (in theatrical language.) See अत्तिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=057-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थ|अर्थः
अर्थ r. 10th el. (अर्थयते sometimes -ति) To ask or beg.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=057-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थ|अर्थः
अर्थ mfn. (-र्थः-र्था-र्थं)<BR>	 1. Rich.<BR>	 2. Learned.<BR>	 m. (-र्थः)<BR>	 1. Wealth, property,<BR>substance.<BR>	 2. Meaning, signification.<BR>	 3. Thing.<BR>	 4. fruit, conse-<BR>quence.<BR>	 5. Prohibition.<BR>	 6. A material substance or object of sense.<BR>7. Cause, origin.<BR>	 8. Request, asking, begging.<BR>	 9. Kind, sort, man-<BR>ner.<BR>	 10. Well, well-being.<BR>	 11. (In law) A suit, an action.<BR> E. ऋ to<BR>go, and थन् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=057-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थकर
अर्थकर mfn. (-रः-रा-री-रं) Producing yielding wealth, what enriches. E.<BR>अर्थ, and कर what makes, also similar compounds, as अर्थकारक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं) अर्थकारिन् mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि) and अर्थजनक mfn.<BR>(-कः-का-कं) &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=057-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थकाम
अर्थकाम m. (-मः) Avarice, desire of wealth<BR> E. अर्थ, and काम desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=057-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थगरीयस्
अर्थगरीयस् mfn. (-यान्-यसी-यः) Significant, meaning.<BR> E. अर्थ with गुरु heavy,<BR>ईयसुन् superlative aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=057-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थघ्न
अर्थघ्न mfn. (-घ्नः-घ्नी-घ्नं) Wasteful, extravagant.<BR> E. अर्थ, and घ्न who or what<BR>destroys.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=057-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थज्ञ
अर्थज्ञ mfn. (-ज्ञः-ज्ञा-ज्ञं) Wise, discriminating, understanding the various<BR>significations of a word, &c.<BR> E. अर्थ meaning, and ज्ञ who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=057-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थतस्
अर्थतस् ind. According to the sense.<BR> E. तसि added to अर्थ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=057-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थतत्त्व
अर्थतत्त्व n. (-त्त्वं) Truth, the real object, nature or cause of any thing. E.<BR>अर्थ, and तत्त्व truth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=057-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थद
अर्थद mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>	 1. Liberal, munificent.<BR>	 2. Compliant, favourable.<BR>E. अर्थ wealth or object, and द who or what gives. Also similar com-<BR>pounds, as अर्थदायक, अर्थदायिन् and अर्थदातृ, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=057-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थदूषण
अर्थदूषण n. (-णं) Waste, prodigality, extravagance.<BR> E. अर्थ, and दूषण spoil-<BR>ing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=057-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थना
अर्थना f. (-ना) Begging, asking.<BR> E. अर्थ to ask, and युच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=057-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थपति|अर्थपतिः
अर्थपति m. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. KUVERA, the Hindu PLUTUS.<BR>	 2. A king.<BR> E. अर्थ<BR>wealth, and पति lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=057-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थपर
अर्थपर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>	 1. Intent on gaining wealth.<BR>	 2. Persimonious,<BR>niggardly.<BR> E. अर्थ, and पर intent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=057-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थप्रयोग|अर्थप्रयोगः
अर्थप्रयोग m. (-गः)<BR>	 1. Application of wealth as to trade, usury, &c.<BR>	 2.<BR>The profession of usury.<BR> E. अर्थ, and प्रयोग application.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=057-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थप्राप्ति
अर्थप्राप्ति f. (-प्तिः)<BR>	 1. Acquisition of wealth.<BR>	 2. Attainment of an object.<BR>E. अर्थ, and प्राप्ति gaining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=057-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थभृत
अर्थभृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) A servant who has high wages.<BR> E. अर्थ, and भृत<BR>maintained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=057-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थभेद|अर्थभेदः
अर्थभेद m. (-दः) Distinction, difference of meaning.<BR> E. अर्थ meaning, and<BR>भेद dividing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=057-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थलाभ|अर्थलाभः
अर्थलाभ m. (-भः) Acquisition of wealth.<BR> E. अर्थ, and लाभ acquiring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=057-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थलुब्ध
अर्थलुब्ध mfn. (-ब्धः-ब्धा-ब्धं) Greedy of wealth, covetous, niggardly.<BR> E. अर्थ,<BR>and लुब्ध desirous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=057-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थलेश
अर्थलेश m. (-शः) A little wealth.<BR> E. अर्थ, and लेश a little.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=057-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थलोभ|अर्थलोभः
अर्थलोभ m. (-भः) Avarice, desire of wealth.<BR> E. अर्थ, and लोभ desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=057-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थवत्|अर्थवन्त्
अर्थवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>	 1. Wealthy, rich.<BR>	 2. Significant, having sense<BR>or meaning.<BR>	 3. Designed, intentional, having an object.<BR> E. अर्थ, and<BR>मतुप् poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=057-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थवाद|अर्थवादः
अर्थवाद m. (-दः)<BR>	 1. Praise, eulogium.<BR>	 2. Declaration of purpose or ob-<BR>ject, speech or expression having a certain object, as स्तुत्यर्थवादः<BR>speech implying praise, निन्दार्थवादः speech implying censure.<BR>	 3. Am-<BR>plification.<BR> E. अर्थ substance, thing, and वाद speaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=057-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थविज्ञान|अर्थविज्ञानं
अर्थविज्ञान n. (-नं) One of the six exercises of the understanding, the<BR>comprehension of meanings.<BR> E. अर्थ meaning, import, and विज्ञान<BR>knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=058-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थविद्
अर्थविद् mfn. (-वित् or विद्) Sagacious, sensible, wise.<BR> E. अर्थ, and विद् who<BR>knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=058-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थवृद्धि|अर्थवृद्धिः
अर्थवृद्धि f. (-द्धिः) Accumulation of wealth.<BR> E. अर्थ and वृद्धि increase.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=058-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थवैकल्य
अर्थवैकल्य n. (-ल्पं) Prevarication, evasion, deviation from truth, per-<BR>version or disguise of fact.<BR> E. अर्थ object, वैकल्य alteration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=058-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थव्यय|अर्थव्ययः
अर्थव्यय m. (-यः) Expenditure.<BR> E. अर्थ, and व्यय expenditure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=058-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थव्ययज्ञ|अर्थव्ययज्ञः
अर्थव्ययज्ञ mfn. (-ज्ञः-ज्ञा-ज्ञं) Liberal in giving and using.<BR> E. अर्थ wealth, व्यय<BR>expense, and ज्ञ who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=058-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थशास्त्र|अर्थशास्त्रं
अर्थशास्त्र n. (-स्त्रं) The science of polity or moral and political govern-<BR>ment.<BR> E. अर्थ possession, property, and शास्त्र institutes of a science.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=058-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थशौच
अर्थशौच n. (-चं)<BR>	 1. Honesty.<BR>	 2. Acquisition of wealth.<BR> E. अर्थ purpose or<BR>wealth, शौच purity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=058-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थसंग्रह
अर्थसंग्रह m. (-हः)<BR>	 1. Accumulation of wealth.<BR>	 2. A treasure.<BR> E. अर्थ, and<BR>संग्रह a collection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=058-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थसंस्थान
अर्थसंस्थान n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Accumulation of wealth.<BR>	 2. A treasury.<BR> E. अर्थ, and<BR>संस्थान assemblage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=058-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थसञ्चय|अर्थसंचय|अर्थसंचयः
अर्थसञ्चय m. (-यः) Accumulation of wealth.<BR> E. अर्थ, and सञ्चय heap.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=058-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थसम्बन्ध|अर्थसंबन्ध|अर्थसंबन्धः
अर्थसम्बन्ध m. (-न्धः) Connexion of the sense with the word or sentence.<BR>E. अर्थ, and सम्बन्ध connexion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=058-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थसिद्ध
अर्थसिद्ध mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>	 1. Effected by wealth.<BR>	 2. Successful, one whose<BR>aim is accomplished.<BR> E. अर्थ, and सिद्ध accomplished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=058-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थसिद्धि|अर्थसिद्धिः
अर्थसिद्धि f. (-द्धिः) Success.<BR> E. अर्थ, and सिद्धि accomplishment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=058-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थहर
अर्थहर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Inheriting or taking wealth.<BR> E. अर्थ, and हर who<BR>takes. So अर्थहारिन् mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=058-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थहीन
अर्थहीन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>	 1. Poor.<BR>	 2. Failing, disappointed.<BR>	 3. Unmean-<BR>ing, nonsensical.<BR> E. अर्थ and हीन wanting. So अर्थशून्य mfn. (-न्यः-न्या-न्यं)<BR>E. अर्थ, and शून्य empty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=058-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थागम|अर्थागमः
अर्थागम m. (-मः)<BR>	 1. Receipt or collection of property.<BR>	 2. Acquisition of<BR>wealth.<BR> E. अर्थ wealth and आगम coming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=058-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थाधिकार|अर्थाधिकारः
अर्थाधिकार m. (-रः) Stewardship, treasurership, charge of money or<BR>property.<BR> E. अर्थ and अधिकार superintendence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=058-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थाधिकारिन्
अर्थाधिकारिन् m. (-री) A treasurer, a paymaster.<BR> E. अर्थ, and अधिकारिन्<BR>superintendent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=058-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थान्तर
अर्थान्तर n. (-रं)<BR>	 1. Difference of meaning or purport.<BR>	 2. Another or<BR>second sense.<BR>	 3. Opposite or antithetical meaning.<BR> E. अर्थ, and<BR>अन्तर difference.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=058-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थान्तरन्यास
अर्थान्तरन्यास m. (-सः) Antithesis.<BR> E. अर्थान्तर, and न्यास position.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=058-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थान्वित
अर्थान्वित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Rich.<BR>	 2. Significant.<BR> E. अर्थ wealth, and अन्वित<BR>possessed of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=058-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थापत्ति|अर्थापत्तिः
अर्थापत्ति f. (-त्तिः)<BR>	 1. A figure of speech, a quibble, the use of one word<BR>in a double sense.<BR>	 2. An inference from circumstances.<BR> E. अर्थ,<BR>and आपति gaining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=058-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थार्थिन्
अर्थार्थिन् mfn. (-र्थी-र्थिनी-र्थि)<BR>	 1. One who solicits wealth.<BR>	 2. One endeavour-<BR>ing to gain any object.<BR> E. अर्थ, and अर्थिन् who seeks or solicits.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=058-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थिक|अर्थिकः
अर्थिक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A crier, a watchman, a minstrel, a servant whose<BR>duty it is to announce by song or music, fixed periods of the day,<BR>or those of getting up and of repose, &c.<BR>	 2. A beggar, a solicitor.<BR>E. अर्थि a rich man, and क from कै to call or sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=058-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थित
अर्थित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Asked, begged, sought.<BR> E. अर्थ to ask, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=058-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थिता
अर्थिता f. (-ता) Asking, begging. Also n. (-त्वं)<BR> E. तल् or त्व added to अर्थिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=058-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थिन्
अर्थिन् mfn. (-र्थी-र्थिनी-र्थि)<BR>	 1. One who asks or begs for any thing.<BR>	 2.<BR>One who seeks to effect or gain a purpose or object.<BR>	 m. (-र्थी)<BR>	 1. A<BR>servant.<BR>	 2. A follower, a companion or partizan.<BR>	 3. A plaintiff, a<BR>prosecutor.<BR>	 4. A beggar, a petitioner.<BR> E. अर्थ asking, &c. इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=058-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थोपार्ज्जन|अर्थोपार्जन
अर्थोपार्ज्जन n. (-नं) Acquiring wealth.<BR> E. अर्थ, and उपार्ज्जन acquiring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=058-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थोष्मन्
अर्थोष्मन् n. (-ष्म) Wealth, the condition of being wealthy.<BR> E. अर्थ, and<BR>उष्मन् warmth. So anglice, a warm man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=058-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थ्य|अर्थ्यं|अर्थ्यः
अर्थ्य mfn. (-र्थ्यः-र्थ्या-र्थ्यं)<BR>	 1. Intelligent, wise.<BR>	 2. Wealthy.<BR>	 3. Right, proper.<BR>4. Fit to be asked or sought.<BR>	 n. (-र्थ्यं) Red chalk.<BR> E. अर्थ and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=058-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्द|अर्द्द
अर्द r. 1st cl. (अर्दति)<BR>	 1. To ask or beg.<BR>	 2. To go. 1st and 10th cls.<BR>(अर्दति-ते अर्दयति-ते) To kill or to hurt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=058-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्दना|अर्द्दना
अर्दना f. (-ना)<BR>	 1. Begging, asking.<BR>	 2. Giving pain.<BR>	 3. Killing.<BR>	 4. Going.<BR>E. अर्द to ask, &c. युच् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=058-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्दनि|अर्दनिः
अर्दनि m. (-निः)<BR>	 1. Fire.<BR>	 2. Asking, begging.<BR>	 3. Sickness, disease.<BR> E. अर्द<BR>to pain, अनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=058-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्दित|अर्दितं|अर्द्दित|अर्द्दितः
अर्दित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Asked, requested, begged.<BR>	 2. Killed, injured.<BR>3. Pained, afflicted.<BR>	 4. Gone.<BR>	 n. (-तं) A disease, Hemiplegin,<BR>paralysis of the muscles on one side of the face and neck.<BR> E. अर्द to<BR>go, to ask, &c. affix क्त, and इट् inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=058-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्द्ध
अर्द्ध mfn. (-र्द्धः-र्द्धा-र्द्धं) Half, halved.<BR>	 m. (-र्द्धः) A part.<BR>	 n. (-र्द्धिं) A half.<BR> E. ऋध<BR>to increase, and घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=058-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्द्धकृत
अर्द्धकृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Halved, divided equally.<BR> E. अर्द्ध, and कृत made.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=058-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्द्धखार
अर्द्धखार nf. (-रं-री) A measure, half a khārī.<BR> E. अर्द्ध, and खारी a measure<BR>so called.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=058-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्द्धगङ्गा
अर्द्धगङ्गा f. (-ङ्गा) The Kāverī river, in the peninsula.<BR> E. अर्द्ध half, and गङ्गा<BR>the Ganges; being a sacred stream, having half the virtues of the<BR>great Ganges.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=058-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्द्धगुच्छ
अर्द्धगुच्छ m. (-च्छः) A necklace of twenty-four strings.<BR> E. अर्द्ध, and गुच्छ a<BR>bundle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=058-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्द्धचन्द्र
अर्द्धचन्द्र m. (-न्द्रः)<BR>	 1. A crescent or half moon.<BR>	 2. The hand bent into a<BR>semicircle or the shape of a claw, as for the purpose of seizing or<BR>clutching any thing.<BR>	 3. The semicircular marks on a peacock's<BR>tail.<BR>	 4. An arrow, with a head like a crescent.<BR>	 5. The semicircular<BR>scratch of the fingernail.<BR>	 f. (-न्द्रा) A plant, vulgarly Teori, the<BR>black kind.<BR> E. अर्द्ध half, and चन्द्र moon, or with कन् added अर्द्धचन्द्रकः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=058-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्द्धचन्द्राकार
अर्द्धचन्द्राकार mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Of the shape of the half moon.<BR>	 m. (-रः) A<BR>meniscus.<BR> E. अर्द्धचन्द्र, and आकार form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=058-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्द्धचन्द्राकृति
अर्द्धचन्द्राकृति mfn. (-तिः-तिः-ति) Half-mooned, of a crescent-shape, convex<BR>and concave.<BR>	 f. (-तिः) A meniscus.<BR> E. अर्द्धचन्द्र, and आकृति shape.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=058-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्द्धचोलक
अर्द्धचोलक m. (-कः) A short bodice.<BR> E. अर्द्ध, and चोलक a bodice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=058-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्द्धजाह्नवी
अर्द्धजाह्नवी f. (-वी) The Kāverī river. See अर्द्धगङ्गा, जाह्नवी being the Ganges.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=058-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्द्धधार
अर्द्धधार n. (-रं) A knife or lancet with a single edge, the blade two inches<BR>long, the heft six.<BR> E. अर्द्ध, and धारा an edge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=058-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्द्धनारीश
अर्द्धनारीश m. (-शः) A name of MAHĀDEVA.<BR> E. अर्द्ध, and नारी a woman, an<BR>ईश master; one of the forms of ŚIVA, to which this name applies<BR>being half male and half female.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=058-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्द्धनाव
अर्द्धनाव m. (-वः) A boat's half.<BR> E. अर्द्ध, and नाव, from नौ a boat, and टच<BR>aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=058-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्द्धनिशा
अर्द्धनिशा f. (-शा) Midnight.<BR> E. अर्द्ध, and निशा night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=058-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्द्धपण
अर्द्धपण n. (-णं) Half a Paṇa.<BR> E. अर्द्ध, and पण a measure of four Kākinīs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=058-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्द्धपारावत
अर्द्धपारावत m. (-तः)<BR>	 1. A pigeon, (with a spotted or painted throat.)<BR>	 2.<BR>The francoline partridge.<BR> E. अर्द्ध, and पारावत a pigeon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=058-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्द्धपुलायित
अर्द्धपुलायित n. (-तं) A half gallop, a canter.<BR> E. अर्द्ध, and पुलायित a gallop.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=058-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्द्धप्रहर
अर्द्धप्रहर m. (-रः) Half a watch, a period of an hour and a half.<BR> E. अर्द्ध, and<BR>प्रहर a watch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=058-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्द्धभाग
अर्द्धभाग m. (-गः) A half.<BR> E. अर्द्ध, and भाग part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=058-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्द्धभाज्
अर्द्धभाज् mf. (-भाक्) Taking or sharing half.<BR> E. अर्द्ध half. and माज् who<BR>possesses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=058-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्द्धभागिक
अर्द्धभागिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Taking or sharing half.<BR> E. अर्द्धभाग a half, ठक्<BR>aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=058-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्द्धभागिन्
अर्द्धभागिन् mfn. (-गी-गिनी-गि) Sharing or taking half.<BR> E. अर्द्धभाग and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=058-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्द्धमाणव
अर्द्धमाणव m. (-वः) A necklace of twelve strings. Also अर्द्धमाणवक.<BR> E. अर्द्ध,<BR>and माणव one of twenty-four strings.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=058-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्द्धयाम
अर्द्धयाम m. (-मः) Half a watch, an hour and a half.<BR> E. अर्द्ध, and याम a<BR>watch, also अर्द्धयामक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=058-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्द्धरथ
अर्द्धरथ m. (-थः) A warrior, who fights on a car with another.<BR> E. अर्द्ध,<BR>and रथ a car, having half a car.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=058-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्द्धरात्र
अर्द्धरात्र m. (-त्रः)<BR>	 1. Midnight.<BR>	 2. The period from two and a half to<BR>three and a half watches of the night.<BR> E. अर्द्ध, and रात्र night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्द्धर्च
अर्द्धर्च mn. (-चः-चं) Half a verse of the Vedas.<BR> E. अर्द्ध, and ऋच् a verse<BR>of a Veda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्द्धवीक्षण
अर्द्धवीक्षण n. (-णं) A side look, a glance, a leer.<BR> E. अर्द्ध, and वीक्षण looking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्द्धशत
अर्द्धशत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Fifty.<BR>	 2. One hundred and fifty.<BR> E. अर्द्ध, and<BR>शत a hundred, in the second sense it is more usually सार्द्धशत, &c.<BR>So अर्द्धपञ्चाशत्, अर्द्धसहस्र, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्द्धशन
अर्द्धशन n. (-नं) Half a meal.<BR> E. अर्द्ध, and अशन eating, also अर्द्धाशन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्द्धसफर
अर्द्धसफर m. (-रः) A small fish, (Cyprinus sophore, HAM:)<BR> E. अर्द्ध, and<BR>सफर another fish, to which it is compared.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्द्धसीरिन्
अर्द्धसीरिन् m. (-री) A cultivator, a ploughman who takes half the crop<BR>for his labour.<BR> E. अर्द्ध, and सीर a plough, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्द्धहार
अर्द्धहार m. (-रः) A necklace of sixty-four strings.<BR> E. अर्द्ध, and हार a<BR>necklace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्द्धांश
अर्द्धांश m. (-शः) A half.<BR> E. अर्द्ध, and अंश a share.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्द्धांशिन्
अर्द्धांशिन् mfn. (-शी-शिनी-शि) Sharing a half.<BR> E. अर्द्धांश and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्द्धाङ्ग
अर्द्धाङ्ग n. (-ङ्गं) Half the body.<BR> E. अर्द्ध, and अङ्ग the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्द्धार्द्ध
अर्द्धार्द्ध mfn. (-र्द्धः-र्द्धा-र्द्धं) Sharing equally.<BR>	 m. (-र्द्धः) A quarter.<BR> E. अर्द्ध<BR>repeated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्द्धावभेदक
अर्द्धावभेदक m. (-कः) Pain of half the head, hemicrania.<BR>	 n. (-कं) Dividing<BR>in equal parts.<BR> E. अर्द्ध, and अवभेदक cutting off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्द्धाशन
अर्द्धाशन n. (-नं) Half a meal. Also अर्द्धशन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्द्धासन
अर्द्धासन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Exemption from censure.<BR>	 2. Greeting kindly or with<BR>respect, placing on the same seat.<BR> E. अर्द्ध, and आस to remain,<BR>affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्द्धिक
अर्द्धिक mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>	 1. Measuring a half.<BR>	 2. Relating to a half. E.<BR>अर्द्ध and टिठन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्द्धिन्
अर्द्धिन् mfn. (-र्द्धी-र्द्धिनी-र्द्धि) Entitled to or sharing a half.<BR> E. अर्द्ध and इनि.<BR>aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्द्धेन्दु
अर्द्धेन्दु m. (-न्दुः)<BR>	 1. A half moon or crescent.<BR>	 2. The impression of a<BR>fingernail.<BR>	 3. The hand expanded in a semicircular form like a<BR>claw.<BR>	 4. An arrow with a crescent-shaped head.<BR> E. अर्द्ध, and इन्दु<BR>the moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्द्धोक्त
अर्द्धोक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं) Half uttered, said imperfectly or indistinctly.<BR>E. अर्द्ध, and उक्त said.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्द्धोक्ति
अर्द्धोक्ति f. (-क्तिः) Speaking indistinctly or incompletely, broken or in-<BR>terrupted speech.<BR> E. अर्द्ध, and उक्ति speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्द्धोदित
अर्द्धोदित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Half risen.<BR>	 2. Half uttered.<BR> E. अर्द्ध, and उदित<BR>risen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्द्धोरुक
अर्द्धोरुक n. (-कं) A short petticoat.<BR> E. अर्द्ध, and उरु the high, कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्पण|अर्पणं
अर्पण nf. (-णं-णा)<BR>	 1. Delivering, entrusting.<BR>	 2. Placing in or upon. E.<BR>ऋ to go, in the causal form, यच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्पणीय
अर्पणीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) To be delivered, deliverable.<BR> E. ऋ to go, causal<BR>form. अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्पित
अर्पित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Delivered, consigned.<BR>	 2. Placed in or upon.<BR>E. ऋ to go, in the causal form, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्पितकर
अर्पितकर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>	 1. Extending or giving the hand.<BR>	 2. Married.<BR>E. अर्पित, and कर the hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्पिस|अर्पिसः
अर्पिस m. (-सः) The heart.<BR> E. ऋ to go, in the causal form अर्प्य, and इसन्<BR>Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्प्य
अर्प्य mfn. (-र्प्यः-र्प्या-र्प्यं) To be delivered, consignable.<BR> E. ऋ to go, causal<BR>form, य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्ब्ब|अर्ब
अर्ब्ब r. 1st. cl. (अर्ब्बति)<BR>	 1. To go, to go to or towards.<BR>	 2. To kill or hurt.<BR>See अर्व्व.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्ब्बुद|अर्बुद|अर्बुदं|अर्बुदः|अर्ब्बुदः
अर्ब्बुद mn. (-दः-दं)<BR>	 1. Ophthalmia.<BR>	 2. A hundred millions.<BR>	 m. (-दः)<BR>	 1.<BR>The name of a mountain in the west of India, commonly Abu, a<BR>place of pilgrimage, especially to the Jainas.<BR>	 2. An indolent<BR>swelling.<BR> E. अर्ब्ब to injure. उदच् affix; the root and derivative are<BR>also written with the dental letter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्भ|अर्भः
अर्भ mfn. (-र्भः-र्भा-र्भं) Destitute of splendour.<BR>	 m. (-र्भः)<BR>	 1. A child, a pupil.<BR>2. Dew.<BR>	 3. Herbs.<BR> E. ऋ to go, and भन् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=059-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्भक|अर्भकः
अर्भक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A child, the young of any animal.<BR>	 2. A fool, an idiot.<BR>3. Small, minute.<BR>	 4. Emaciated.<BR>	 5. Like, similar.<BR> E. ऋध to grow,<BR>वुन् Unādi affix, and भ substituted for ध.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=059-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्म्म|अर्म|अर्मं|अर्मः|अर्म्मं
अर्म्म mn. (-र्म्मः-र्म्मं) A disease of the eyes.<BR> E. ऋ to go, and मन् Unādi<BR>affix, also read अर्म्मन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=059-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्म्मण|अर्मण|अर्मणं|अर्म्मणः
अर्म्मण m. (-णः) A measure of one Drona.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=059-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्म्मन्|अर्मन्
अर्म्मन् n. (-र्म्म) A disease of the eyes.<BR> E. ऋ to go, मनिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=059-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्य्य|अर्य|अर्यः|अर्य्यः
अर्य्य mfn. (-र्य्यः-र्य्या-र्य्यं) Excellent.<BR>	 m. (-र्य्यः)<BR>	 1. A master.<BR>	 2. A man of the<BR>third tribe, the Vaiśya.<BR>	 f. (-र्य्या)<BR>	 1. A woman of the third tribe.<BR>	 2. The<BR>wife of a Vaiśya.<BR> E. ऋ to go, यत् affix, and टाप् or ङीप् for the fem.;<BR>ङीप् is affixed, when the word is fem. with reference to the male.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=059-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्य्यमन्|अर्यमन्
अर्य्यमन् m. (-मा)<BR>	 1. The sun.<BR>	 2. A class of the Manes or deified proge-<BR>nitors.<BR>	 3. The asclepias plant.<BR> E. ऋ to go, कनिन् Unādi affix, and<BR>माङ् inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=059-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्य्यर्य्याणी
अर्य्यर्य्याणी f. (-णी) A multitude of woman of the Vaiśya tribe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=059-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्य्याणी|अर्याणी
अर्य्याणी f. (-णी) A woman of the Vaiśya tribe.<BR> E. अर्य्य, ङीप् affix, and<BR>आनुक् inserted. See अर्य्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=059-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्व्व|अर्व
अर्व्व r. 1st cl. (अर्व्वति) To kill or hurt, also written अर्ब्ब.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=059-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्व्वट|अर्वट|अर्वटं
अर्व्वट n. (-टं) Ashes.<BR> E. अर्व्व or अर्ब्ब to injure, hence the word may be<BR>also written अर्ब्बट.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=059-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्व्वन्|अर्वन्
अर्व्वन् mfn. (-र्व्वा-र्व्वती-र्व्वत्) Low, inferior, vile.<BR>	 m. (-र्व्वा)<BR>	 1. A horse.<BR>	 2. A<BR>name of INDRA.<BR>	 3. A short span.<BR>	 f. (-र्व्वती)<BR>	 1. A mare.<BR>	 2. A bawd, a<BR>procuress.<BR> E. ऋ to go, and वनिप् Unādi affix; it is sometimes derived<BR>from अर्ब्ब to go, and is then written अर्ब्बन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=059-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्व्वाच्|अर्वाच्
अर्व्वाच् mfn. (-र्व्वाङ्-र्व्वाची-र्व्वाक्) Following, subsequent. ind. (-र्व्वाच् or -र्व्वाक्)<BR>1. After, in time.<BR>	 2. Behind, in place.<BR>	 3. Near.<BR> E. अवर behind, अञ्च<BR>to go, क्विप् affix; the formation is irregular.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=059-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्व्वाचीन|अर्वाचीन|अर्व्वाचीनः
अर्व्वाचीन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>	 1. Reverse, contrary.<BR>	 2. Recent, modern. E.<BR>अर्व्वाच् and ख aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=059-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्व्वाचीनत्व
अर्व्वाचीनत्व n. (-त्वं) State of reverse.<BR> E. त्व added to the last; also with<BR>तल्, अर्व्वाचीनता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=059-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्श|अर्शं|अर्शः
अर्श n. (-र्शं) Hœmorrhoids, piles. Also अर्शस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=059-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्शस्
अर्शस् n. (-र्शः) Hœmorrhoids, piles.<BR> E. ऋ to go, असुन् Unādi affix, and<BR>शुट् inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=059-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्शस|अर्शसः
अर्शस mfn. (-सः-सा-सं) Afflicted with hœmorrhoids.<BR> E. अर्शस् and अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=059-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्शसान|अर्शसानः
अर्शसान m. (-नः) Fire.<BR> E. ऋ to go, शानच् affix, and शुट् inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=059-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्शिन्
अर्शिन् mfn. (-र्शी-र्शिनी-र्शि) Afflicted with hœmorrhoids.<BR> E. अर्श, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=059-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्शोघ्न|अर्शोघ्नः
अर्शोघ्न mfn. (-घ्नः-घ्ना-घ्नं) Destroying the hœmorrhoids.<BR>	 m. (-घ्नः) An es-<BR>culent root, (Arum campanulatum.)<BR>	 f. (-घ्नी) A plant, (Curculigo<BR>orchioides.)<BR> E. अर्शस्, and घ्न what destroys, from हन to kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=059-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्शोरोग
अर्शोरोग m. (-गः) The piles or hœmorrhoids.<BR> E. अर्शस्, and रोग disease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=059-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्शोरोगयुत
अर्शोरोगयुत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Afflicted with hœmorrhoids.<BR> E. अर्शोरोग and<BR>युत affected by.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=059-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्शोरोगिन्
अर्शोरोगिन् mfn. (-गी-गिणी-गि) Having hœmorrhoids.<BR> E. अर्शोरोग and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=059-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्शोहित|अर्शोहितः
अर्शोहित m. (-तः) The marking-nut plant, (Semecarpus anacardium.) E.<BR>अर्शस्, and हित proper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=059-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्सस्
अर्सस् m. (-र्सः) Hœmorrhoids. See अर्शस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=059-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्ह|अर्हः
अर्ह r. 1st cl. (अर्हति)<BR>	 1. To worship or honour.<BR>	 2. To be fit or worthy:<BR>in the first sense it is also. r. 10th cl. (अर्हयति.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=059-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्ह|अर्हः
अर्ह mfn. (-र्हः-र्हा-र्हं)<BR>	 1. Proper, fit, becoming.<BR>	 2. Deserving, entitled to,<BR>worthy, m. (-र्हः) INDRA.<BR>	 f. (-र्हा) Worship.<BR> E. अर्ह to worship, to be<BR>fit, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=059-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्हण|अर्हणं
अर्हण nf. (-णं-णा) Worship, adoration, respect, courtesy, treating with<BR>veneration or respect.<BR> E. अर्ह to worship, and युच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=059-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्हत्|अर्हन्त्
अर्हत् mfn. (-र्हन्-र्हन्ती-र्हत्)<BR>	 1. Venerable, respectable.<BR>	 2. Praised, celebrated.<BR>m. (-र्हन्)<BR>	 1. A Jina or Jaina saint and teacher.<BR>	 2. A Jaina, or follow-<BR>er of the doctrines of Jaina.<BR>	 3. A religious mendicant of that sect.<BR>E. अर्ह to worship, &c. and शतृ affix, of the present participle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=059-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्हत्तम
अर्हत्तम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं) Best, most worthy.<BR> E. अर्हत् respectable, डतम aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=060-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्हत्तर
अर्हत्तर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) More worthy, better.<BR> E. अर्हत् and डतर aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=060-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्हन्त|अर्हंत|अर्हन्तः
अर्हन्त m. (-न्तः)<BR>	 1. A Saugata or follower of the doctrines of Buddha.<BR>	 2.<BR>A religious mendicant of the same sect.<BR>	 3. A name of ŚIVA.<BR> E. अर्ह<BR>to worship, &c. and अन्त irregular aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=060-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्हित|अर्हितः
अर्हित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Saluted, honoured, worshipped.<BR> E. अर्ह to worship,<BR>&c. and क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=060-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्ह्य
अर्ह्य mfn. (-र्ह्यः-र्ह्या-र्ह्यं) Venerable, respectable, right, fit.<BR> E. अर्ह and यत्<BR>affix: also with अनीयर् affix, अर्हणीय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=060-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अल|अलं
अल r. 1st. cl. also read अलं (अलति-ते) 1. To adorn.<BR>	 2. To be competent<BR>or able.<BR>	 3. To prevent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=060-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अल|अलं
अल n. (-लं)<BR>	 1. The sting in the tail of the scorpion.<BR>	 2. Yellow orpiment.<BR>E. अल to adorn, &c. and अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=060-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलक|अलकं|अलकः
अलक mn. (-कः-कं) A curl.<BR>	 m. (-कः) A mad dog. See अलर्क f. (-का)<BR>	 1.<BR>Alaka, the capital of KUVERA.<BR>	 2. A young girl from eight to ten<BR>years of age.<BR> E. अल to adorn, &c. वुन् affix, and fem. टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=060-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलकनन्दा
अलकनन्दा f. (-न्दा)<BR>	 1. A young girl from eight to ten years old.<BR>	 2. A<BR>river, the Alakanandā, a stream that runs from the Himālaya<BR>mountains, and falls into the Ganges near Srinagara. It is also a<BR>name of the terrestrial Ganges.<BR> E. अलका, and नन्दा who delights,<BR>the final of the first dropped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=060-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलकप्रभा
अलकप्रभा f. (-भा) The capital of KUVERA.<BR> E. अलका, and प्रभा what shines.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=060-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलकप्रिय|अलकप्रियः
अलकप्रिय m. (-यः) A plant, (Pentaptera tomentosa.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=060-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलकसंहति|अलकसंहतिः
अलकसंहति f. (-तिः) Rows of curls.<BR> E. अलक, and संहति collection. So<BR>अलकावली.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=060-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलकाधिप|अलकाधिपः
अलकाधिप m. (-पः) A name of KUVERA.<BR> E. अलका the city, and अधिप a<BR>ruler.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=060-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलकाधिपति|अलकाधिपतिः
अलकाधिपति m. (-तिः) KUVERA.<BR> E. अलका, and अधिपति ruler.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=060-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलकान्त|अलकान्तः
अलकान्त m. (-न्तः) A ringlet, the end of a curl.<BR> E. अलक, and अन्त end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=060-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलक्त|अलक्तः
अलक्त m. (-क्तः) Lac, the red animal dye so called.<BR> E. अ neg. रक्त red, र<BR>being changed to ल; than what nothing is redder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=060-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलक्तक|अलक्तकः
अलक्तक n. (-कं) Lac, the dye; see the preceding. E. As before, कन्<BR>being added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=060-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलक्तरस|अलक्तरसः
अलक्तरस m. (-सः) Liquefied lac dye.<BR> E. अलक्त, and रस juice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=060-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलक्षण|अलक्षणं
अलक्षण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>	 1. Unfortunate, ill fated, having no good marks<BR>on the person.<BR>	 2. Undefined.<BR>	 n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. The absence of auspicious<BR>marks.<BR>	 2. Misfortune.<BR>	 3. The want of any predicate or definition.<BR>E. अ priv. and लक्षण a mark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=060-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलक्षित
अलक्षित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Unmarked, having no particular mark.<BR>	 2.<BR>Unobserved, unseen.<BR>	 3. Undefined.<BR> E. अ neg. and लक्षित marked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=060-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलक्ष्मी
अलक्ष्मी f. (-क्ष्मीः) Misfortune, poverty.<BR> E. अ priv. and लक्ष्मी fortune.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=060-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलक्ष्य
अलक्ष्य mfn. (-क्ष्यः-क्ष्या-क्ष्यं) Undistinguishable, undefinable. So अलक्षणीय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=060-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलगर्दः|अलगर्द|अलगर्द्द
अलगर्दः m. (-र्दः)<BR>	 1. The black variety of the Cobra de Capello, (Colu-<BR>ber naga.)<BR>	 2. A large black leech.<BR> E. अ neg. लग to be with or near,<BR>and क्विप् affix अलक; again, अर्द to go, and अच् affix; not trailing<BR>its whole length upon the ground: also अलगर्द्ध.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=060-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलग्न
अलग्न mfn. (-ग्नः-ग्ना-ग्नं) Not joined or connected.<BR> E. अ neg. लग्न attached<BR>to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=060-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलघु
अलघु mfn. (-घुः-घुः-घ्वी-घु)<BR>	 1. Heavy, weighty.<BR>	 2. Serious, solemn.<BR>	 3.<BR>Violent, intense.<BR> E. अ neg. लघु light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=060-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलघुप्रतिज्ञ
अलघुप्रतिज्ञ mfn. (-ज्ञः-ज्ञा-ज्ञं) Solemnly pledged or promised.<BR> E. अलघु, and<BR>प्रतिज्ञा agreement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=060-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलघूपल|अलघूपलः
अलघूपल m. (-लः) A rock.<BR> E. अलघु, and उपल a stone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=060-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलघूष्मन्
अलघूष्मन् m. (-ष्मा) Intense heat.<BR> E. अलघु, and उष्मन् heat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=060-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलङ्करण|अलंकरण|अलंकरणं|अलङ्करणं
अलङ्करण n. (-णं) Ornament, decoration.<BR> E. अलम् ornament, and करण what<BR>makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=060-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलङ्करिष्णु|अलंकरिष्णु|अलंकरिष्णुः|अलङ्करिष्णुः
अलङ्करिष्णु mfn. (-ष्णुः-ष्णुः-ष्णुं)<BR>	 1. Ornamented.<BR>	 2. Fond of ornament.<BR> E. अलम्<BR>ornament, कर from कृ, and इष्णुच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=060-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलङ्कर्तृ|अलंकर्तृ|अलङ्कर्त्तृ
अलङ्कर्तृ mfn. (-र्ता-र्त्री-र्तृ) Ornamented, ornamenting,<BR> E. अलम् as before,<BR>and कर्तृ who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=060-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलङ्कर्म्मीण|अलङ्कर्मीण|अलंकर्मीण|अलङ्कर्म्मीणः
अलङ्कर्म्मीण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Competent to an act, skilful, clever.<BR> E. अलम्<BR>able, fit for, कर्म्म act, business, ख aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=060-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलङ्कार|अलंकार|अलंकारः|अलङ्कारः
अलङ्कार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Ornament (of dress,) trinkets, jewels, &c.<BR>	 2. (Of<BR>language,) A figure or theoretical expression.<BR>	 3. The art of composi-<BR>tion.<BR> E. अलम् ornament, कार what makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=060-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलङ्कारहीन|अलंकारहीन
अलङ्कारहीन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Unadorned.<BR> E. अलङ्कार, and हीन void of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=060-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलङ्क्रिया|अलंक्रिया
अलङ्क्रिया f. (-या) Adorning, ornamenting.<BR> E. अलम्, and क्रिया act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=060-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलङ्कृत|अलंकृत|अलङ्कृतः
अलङ्कृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Ornamented, adorned, lit. or fig.<BR> E. अलम् as<BR>before, कृत made.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=060-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलङ्घन|अलंघन|अलंघनं
अलङ्घन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Not transgressing.<BR>	 2. Not passing over or beyond. E.<BR>अ neg. लङ्घन crossing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=060-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलङ्घनीय|अलंघनीय
अलङ्घनीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Impassable, not to be crossed.<BR>	 2. Venerable,<BR>inviolable, not to be transgressed.<BR> E. अ neg. लङ्घनीय to be passed,<BR>also अलङ्घ्यः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=060-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलङ्घनीयता|अलंघनीयता
अलङ्घनीयता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. The state of not being passable.<BR>	 2. Inviolability,<BR>respectability.<BR> E. तल् added to the last, also अलङ्घनीयत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=060-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलङ्घ्य|अलंघ्य
अलङ्घ्य mfn. (-ङ्घ्यः-ङ्घ्या-ङ्घ्यं)<BR>	 1. Inviolable.<BR>	 2. Impassable.<BR> E. अ neg. लङ्घ्य<BR>to be crossed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=060-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलङ्घ्यता
अलङ्घ्यता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Impassability, inaccessibility.<BR>	 2. Superiority.<BR>	 3.<BR>Authoritative or absolute rule.<BR> E. अलङ्घ्य not to crossed or trans-<BR>gressed, तल् affix, also अलङ्घ्यत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=060-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलज्ज
अलज्ज mfn. (ज्जः-ज्जा-ज्जं) Shameless.<BR> E. अ neg. लज्जा shame. So अलज्जित.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=060-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलजी
अलजी f. (-जी) Inflammation of the eye, at the edge of the cornea.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=060-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलञ्जर|अलंजरः|अलञ्जरः
अलञ्जर m. (-रः) An earthen water jar.<BR> E. अलम् able, and जॄ to decay,<BR>also अलिञ्जर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=060-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलति|अलतिः
अलति m. (-तिः) A kind of song.<BR> E. अलम् ornament, and अति Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=060-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलन्तराम्|अलंतराम्
अलन्तराम् ind. Quite enough, amply sufficient.<BR> E. अलं and तराम् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=060-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलब्ध
अलब्ध mfn. (-ब्धः-ब्धा-ब्धं) Unobtained.<BR> E. अ neg. and लब्ध attained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=060-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलन्धूम|अलंधूम|अलन्धूमः
अलन्धूम m. (-मः) A great smoke.<BR> E. अलम् much, and धूम smoke.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=060-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलभ्य
अलभ्य mfn. (-भ्यः-भ्या-भ्यं) Unattainable, unobtainable.<BR> E. अ neg. लभ्य to<BR>be got.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=060-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलम्
अलम् ind. Ornament.<BR>	 2. Enough, abundance.<BR>	 3. Able, adequate or<BR>equal to.<BR>	 4. Prohibition, no not.<BR>	 5. Unnecessary, no need of. It is<BR>chiefly used in composition, as अलञ्जीविकः having enough for sub-<BR>sistence; अलन्दत्त्वा refusing to give; इत्यलम् enough; अलङ्कार orna-<BR>ment, &c.<BR> E. अल to adorn. &c. and अम् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=060-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलम्पुरुषीण|अलंपुरुषीण|अलम्पुरुषीणः
अलम्पुरुषीण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Fit for a man, becoming a man.<BR> E. अलम्,<BR>पुरुष a man, and ख aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=060-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलम्बुष|अलंबुष|अलंबुषः|अलम्बुषः
अलम्बुष m. (-षः)<BR>	 1. The palm of the hand with the fingers extended.<BR>2. Vomiting, sickness.<BR>	 3. The name of a Rākshasa or goblin.<BR>	 f.<BR>(-षा)<BR>	 1. One of the Apsarās or nymphs of Svarga.<BR>	 2. Madder,<BR>(Rubia manjith.)<BR>	 3. A sort of sensitive plant.<BR>	 4. A barrier, a<BR>line or any thing not to be crossed.<BR> E. अलम्, and बुस to injure,<BR>affix क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=060-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलय|अलयः
अलय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Houseless, homeless.<BR> E. अ neg. and लय place of<BR>refuge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=060-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलर्क|अलर्कः
अलर्क m. (-र्कः)<BR>	 1. White swallow wort, (Calotropis gigantea alba.)<BR>	 2.<BR>A mad dog or one rendered furious.<BR>	 3. A fabulous animal, like a<BR>hog with eight legs.<BR>	 4. An Asura changed to such an animal. Also<BR>अलर्क्क.<BR> E. अल् to adorn, &c. क्विप् affix, and अर्क to inflame or heat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=060-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलले
अलले ind. A word of no import, occuring in the dialect or gibberish<BR>of Pisāchas, a class of imps or goblins, when they are introduced<BR>in plays, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=060-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलवाल|अलवालं
अलवाल n. (-लं) A basin for water at the root of a tree.<BR> E. अ neg. लू to<BR>cut, and आल affix; also आलवाल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=060-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलवालक|अलवालकं
अलवालक n. (-कं) See the preceding. E. As before, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=060-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलस|अलसः
अलस mfn. (-सः-सा-सं) Lazy, idle, indolent.<BR>	 m. (-सः)<BR>	 1. Swelling of the<BR>feet in elephantiasis.<BR>	 2. Chaps between the toes.<BR>	 3. Name of a<BR>tree.<BR>	 f. (-सा) A creeping plant, (Cissus pedata.)<BR> E. अ neg. लस to<BR>work, affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=060-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलसक|अलसकः
अलसक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Indolent.<BR>	 m. (-कः) Flatulence, Tympanitis, in-<BR>tumescence of the abdomen, with constipation and wind.<BR> E. कन्<BR>added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=061-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलसता
अलसता f. (-ता) Idleness.<BR> E. अलस and तल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=061-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलसत्व
अलसत्व n. (-त्वं) Idleness.<BR> E. अलस and त्वं aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=061-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलसेक्षणा
अलसेक्षणा f. (-णा) A woman with languishing looks.<BR> E. अलस idle, and<BR>ईक्षणा looking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=061-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलात|अलातं|अलातः
अलात n. (-तं) A firebrand, whether burning or extinguished.<BR> E. अ neg.<BR>ला to take, and क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=061-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलाबु|अलाबुः
अलाबु f. (-बुः) A long gourd. See the next word.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=061-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलाबू
अलाबू f. (-बूः) The bottle gourd, (Cucurbita lagenaris.)<BR> E. अ neg. लब to<BR>sink, ऊ Unādi affix, म् is dropped, and the preceding vowel length-<BR>ened: what does not sink in water; floats, &c. are made of this<BR>gourd, especially when hollowed: also अलबु and आलाबु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=061-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलाबूकट
अलाबूकट n. (-टं) The down of the gourd.<BR> E. अलाबू and कटच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=061-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलाभ|अलाभः
अलाभ m. (-भः)<BR>	 1. Non-acquirement, not getting.<BR>	 2. Loss.<BR> E. अ neg. लाभ<BR>gain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=061-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलार|अलारं
अलार m. (-रः) A door.<BR> E. अल able, and ऋ to go, अच् affix; by which<BR>one may go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=061-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलास|अलासः
अलास m. (-सः) Inflammation and abscess at the root of the tongue. E.<BR>अ neg. लास saliva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=061-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलि|अलिः
अलि m. (-लिः)<BR>	 1. A large black bee.<BR>	 2. A scorpion.<BR>	 3. The sign Scorpio.<BR>4. A crow.<BR>	 5. The Kokila or Indian cuckoo.<BR>	 6. Spirituous liquor. E.<BR>अल to be able, &c. इण् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=061-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलिक|अलिकं
अलिक n. (-कं) The forehead.<BR> E. अल to adorn, &c. and इकन् affix; also<BR>अलीक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=061-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलिकुल
अलिकुल n. (-लं) A flight or a number of bees.<BR> E. अलि, and कुल a<BR>number.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=061-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलिगर्द्ध
अलिगर्द्ध m. (-र्द्धः) A snake, the black Cobra.<BR> E. अलि, and गर्द्ध to sound, affix<BR>अच्; hissing like the scorpion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=061-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलिङ्गिन्|अलिंगिन्
अलिङ्गिन् mfn. (-ङ्गी-ङ्गिनी-ङ्गि) An impostor, a pretended ascetic or student,<BR>one wearing the usual marks, as the frontal marks, skin, staff, &c.<BR>without belonging in reality to a religious order.<BR> E. अ neg. लिङ्ग<BR>sectarial mark, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=061-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलिजिह्वा
अलिजिह्वा f. (-ह्वा) The uvula or soft palate. Also अलिजिह्विका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=061-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलिञ्जर|अलिंजर|अलिंजरः|अलिञ्जरः
अलिञ्जर m. (-रः) An earthen water jar.<BR> E. अलिम् strength, acc. of अलि<BR>and जॄ to waste, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=061-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलिन्
अलिन् m. (-ली)<BR>	 1. A large black bee.<BR>	 2. A scorpion.<BR> E. अल a sting, and<BR>इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=061-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलिन्द|अलिंदः|अलिन्दः
अलिन्द m. (-न्दः) A terrace before a house.<BR> E. अल to adorn, &c. and किन्दच्<BR>affix; also आलिन्द.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=061-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलिपक|अलिपकः
अलिपक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A large black bee.<BR>	 2. A scorpion.<BR>	 3. A dog. Also<BR>read अलिम्पक and अलिमक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=061-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलिपिज्ञ
अलिपिज्ञ mfn. (-ज्ञः-ज्ञा-ज्ञं) Ignorant of reading and writing.<BR> E. अ neg. लिपि<BR>writing, ज्ञ who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=061-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलिप्रिय|अलिप्रियं|अलिप्रियः
अलिप्रिय n. (-यं) The red lotus, (Nymphœa rubra.)<BR>	 f. (-या) The trumpet<BR>flower, (Bignonia suave-olens.)<BR> E. अलि a bee, and प्रिय beloved, the<BR>object of the bee's affections: the lotus especially is so described by<BR>the poets.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=061-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलिप्सा
अलिप्सा f. (-प्सा) Freedom from desire or cupidity.<BR> E. अ neg. and लिप्सा<BR>wish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=061-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलिमक|अलिमकः
अलिमक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A frog.<BR>	 2. The Kokila or Indian cuckoo.<BR>	 3. A large<BR>black bee.<BR>	 4. The filaments of the lotus.<BR>	 5. A tree, (Bassia latifolia.)<BR>E. अलि from अल to adorn, मकच् affix; also अलिपक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=061-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलिमाला
अलिमाला f. (-ला) A flight of bees.<BR> E. अलि and माला a necklace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=061-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलिम्पक|अलिंपक
अलिम्पक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A bee.<BR>	 2. The Kokila.<BR>	 3. A dog.<BR>	 4. The filaments<BR>of the lotus.<BR> E. अ neg. लिपि to smear, वुन् affix: also read अलिवकः<BR>and अलिम्बकः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=061-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलिविराव|अलिविरावः
अलिविराव m. (-वः) The hum of bees.<BR> E. अलि, and विराव sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=061-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलिविरुत
अलिविरुत n. (-तं) The song or hum of the bee.<BR> E. अलि, and विरुत sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=061-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलीक|अलीकं
अलीक mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>	 1. False.<BR>	 2. Unpleasing.<BR>	 3. Small, little.<BR>	 n. (-कं)<BR>1. Falsehood, untruth.<BR>	 2. Any thing displeasing.<BR>	 3. Heaven.<BR>	 4.<BR>The forehead.<BR> E. अल to adorn, &c. and कीकच् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=061-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलीकता
अलीकता f. (-ता) Falsehood, vanity: also अलीकत्व.<BR> E. तल् or त्व added to<BR>to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=061-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलीकमत्स्य|अलीकमत्स्यः
अलीकमत्स्य m. (-त्स्यः) A cake of beans fried with Sesamum oil.<BR> E. अलीक<BR>unreal, मत्स्य fish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=061-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलु|अलुः
अलु f. (-लुः) A small water pot.<BR> E. ऋ to go, and उच् affix, र becomes ल;<BR>also आलु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=061-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलुब्ध|अलुब्धः
अलुब्ध mfn. (-ब्धः-ब्धा-ब्धं) Moderated, content, not covetous.<BR> E. अ neg. and<BR>लुब्ध covetous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=061-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलून
अलून mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Uncut, unshorn.<BR> E. अ neg. लून cut.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=061-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अले
अले ind. An unmeaning word in the dialect of the demons or Pisāchas,<BR>when they are introduced in plays, &c. also अलले.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=061-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलेले
अलेले ind. See the preceding word.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=061-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलेश
अलेश mfn. (-शः-शा-शं) Much, large adv.<BR>	 n. (-शं) Not at all.<BR> E. अ neg. लेश<BR>small.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=061-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलेशैज
अलेशैज mfn. (-जः-जा-जं) Firm, steady.<BR> E. अलेश not at all, एज what<BR>shakes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=061-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलोकन|अलोकनं
अलोकन n. (-नं) Disappearance, invisibility, imperceptible.<BR> E. अ neg. लोकन<BR>seeing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=061-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलोकनीय
अलोकनीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Invisible.<BR> E. अ neg. लोकनीय visible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=061-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलोकित
अलोकित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Unseen.<BR> E. अ neg. लोकित seen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=061-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलोभ|अलोभः
अलोभ m. (-भः) Moderation, content, absence of cupidity.<BR> E. अ neg. and<BR>लोभ desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=061-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलोभिन्
अलोभिन् mfn. (-भी-भिनी-भि) Not wanting or desiring any thing, free<BR>from desire.<BR> E. अ neg. and लोभिन् desirous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=061-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलोल
अलोल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Firm, steady, tranquil, unagitated.<BR> E. अ neg.<BR>लोल moving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=061-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलोलु
अलोलु mfn. (-लुः-लुः-लु) Indifferent to sensual objects.<BR> E. अ neg. लोल to<BR>desire, affix उ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=061-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलोलुप
अलोलुप mfn. (-पः-पा-पं) Free from desire.<BR> E. अ neg, लोलुप libidinous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=061-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलोलुत्व
अलोलुत्व n. (-त्वं) Indifference to sensual objects.<BR> E. अलोलु and त्व affix: also<BR>अलोलुता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=061-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलोहित|अलोहितं
अलोहित n. (-तं) The red lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=061-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलौकिक|अलौकिकः
अलौकिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>	 1. Supernatural, not relating to this world.<BR>	 2.<BR>Not common, not current in the world.<BR>	 3. Indifferent to the world,<BR>unworldly.<BR> E. अ neg. लौकिक mundane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=061-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अल्क|अल्कः
अल्क n. (-ल्कं)<BR>	 1. A tree.<BR>	 2. A member of the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=061-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अल्प|अल्पं|अल्पः
अल्प mfn. (-ल्पः-ल्पा-ल्पं)<BR>	 1. Little, small.<BR>	 2. Inferior, low.<BR> E. अल् to be able.<BR>&c. प affix or with कन् added अल्पक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=061-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अल्पक|अल्पकः
अल्पक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Small, minute.<BR> E. अल्प and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=061-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अल्पकेशी
अल्पकेशी f. (-शी) The root of sweet flag.<BR> E. अल्प small, and केशी having<BR>filaments, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=061-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अल्पगन्ध|अल्पगन्धं
अल्पगन्ध n. (-न्धं) The red lotus.<BR> E. अल्प and गन्ध smell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=061-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अल्पज्ञ
अल्पज्ञ mfn. (-ज्ञः-ज्ञा-ज्ञं) Ignorant, shallow, superficial.<BR> E. अल्प, and ज्ञ who<BR>knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=061-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अल्पतनु|अल्पतनुः
अल्पतनु mfn. (-नुः-नुः-नु) Small, short, thin, pigmy, having a little body.<BR>E. अल्प, and तनु the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=061-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अल्पता
अल्पता f. (ता)<BR>	 1. Smallness, minuteness.<BR>	 2. Inferiority, insignificance. E.<BR>अल्प and तल् affix, or with त्व, अल्पत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=061-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अल्पदक्षिण
अल्पदक्षिण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Defective in present, (any ceremony, &c.)<BR>E. अल्प, and दक्षिणा gift to Brahmans.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=061-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अल्पधन
अल्पधन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Of little wealth, not affluent.<BR> E. अल्प, and धन wealth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=061-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अल्पधी
अल्पधी mfn. (-धीः-धीः-धि) Ignorant, foolish, of little sense.<BR> E. अल्प, and धी<BR>understanding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=061-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अल्पपत्र|अल्पपत्रः
अल्पपत्र m. (-त्रः) A species of the Tulasi.<BR> E. अल्प, and पत्र a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=061-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अल्पपद्म|अल्पपद्मं
अल्पपद्म n. (-द्मं) The red lotus.<BR> E. अल्प small, and पद्म lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=061-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अल्पप्रभाव
अल्पप्रभाव mfn. (-वः-वा-वं) Insignificant, of little weight or consequence.<BR>E. अल्प, and प्रभाव authority.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=061-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अल्पप्रमाण|अल्पप्रमाणः
अल्पप्रमाण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>	 1. Of little authority.<BR>	 2. Of little weight or<BR>measure.<BR> E. अल्प, and प्रमाण authority, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=062-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अल्पप्रमाणक|अल्पप्रमाणकः
अल्पप्रमाणक mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>	 1. Credulous, resting on little evidence.<BR>	 2.<BR>Of little weight or authority.<BR>	 3. Of short measure.<BR>	 m. (-कः) Common<BR>cucumber, (Cucumis sativus.)<BR> E. अल्प, and प्रमाण authority, &c. कन्<BR>added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=062-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अल्पबल
अल्पबल mfn. (-लः-लाः-लं) Feeble, of little strength.<BR> E. अल्प, and बल<BR>strength.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=062-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अल्पबाध
अल्पबाध mfn. (-धः-धा-धं) Causing little annoyance or inconvenience. E.<BR>अल्प, and बाधा pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=062-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अल्पबुद्धि
अल्पबुद्धि mfn. (-द्धिः-द्धिः-द्धि) Ignorant, silly, unwise.<BR> E. अल्प, बुद्धि understand-<BR>ing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=062-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अल्पमात्र
अल्पमात्र n. (-त्रं)<BR>	 1. A little, a little only.<BR>	 2. A short time, a few moments.<BR>E. अल्प, and मात्र only.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=062-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अल्पमारिष|अल्पमारिषः
अल्पमारिष m. (-षः) A kind of amaranth, (Amaranthus polygamus.) E.<BR>अल्प, मृष to hurt, and इमच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=062-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अल्पमूर्त्ति|अल्पमूर्ति|अल्पमूर्तिः
अल्पमूर्त्ति mfn. (-र्त्तिः-र्त्तिः-र्त्ति) Small, diminutive.<BR>	 f. (-र्त्तिः) A small figure<BR>or object.<BR> E. अल्प, and मूर्त्ति form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=062-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अल्पमेधस्
अल्पमेधस् mfn. (-धाः-धाः-धः) Ignorant, silly, of little understanding. E.<BR>अल्प, and मेधस् apprehension.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=062-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अल्पवयस्
अल्पवयस् mfn. (-याः-याः-यः) Young, of few years.<BR> E. अल्प, and वयस् life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=062-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अल्पवादिन्
अल्पवादिन् mfn. (-दी-दिनी-दि) Taciturn: also अल्पभाषिन्.<BR> E. अल्प, and वादिन्<BR>or भाषिन् who speaks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=062-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अल्पविषय
अल्पविषय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Meaning or directing a little.<BR> E. अल्प, and विषय<BR>object.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=062-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अल्पविद्य
अल्पविद्य mfn. (-द्यः-द्या-द्यं) Ill-taught, uneducated, ignorant.<BR> E. अल्प, and<BR>विद्या knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=062-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अल्पशक्ति
अल्पशक्ति mfn. (-क्तिः-क्तिः-क्ति) Weak, feeble,<BR> E. अल्प, and शक्ति power.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=062-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अल्पशस्
अल्पशस् ind.<BR>	 1. A little.<BR>	 2. To a few.<BR> E. अल्प and शसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=062-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अल्पसरस्
अल्पसरस् n. (-रः) A basin, a small pond, one which is shallow or dry in<BR>the hot season.<BR> E. अल्प, and सरस् a pool.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=062-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अल्पाकाङ्क्षिन्|अल्पाकांक्षिन्
अल्पाकाङ्क्षिन् mfn. (-ङ्क्षी-ङ्क्षिणी-ङ्क्षि) Contented, satisfied with little.<BR> E. अल्प,<BR>and आकाङ्क्षिन् who desires.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=062-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अल्पायुस्
अल्पायुस् mfn. (-युः-युः-युः)<BR>	 1. Short lived.<BR>	 2. Young of few years.<BR>	 m. (-युः)<BR>A goat.<BR> E. अल्प, and आयुस् life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=062-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अल्पाल्प
अल्पाल्प mfn. (-ल्पः-ल्पा-ल्पं)<BR>	 1. Very little, minute.<BR>	 2. Gradual, little at a<BR>time.<BR> E. अल्प repeated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=062-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अल्पाहार|अल्पाहारः
अल्पाहार mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Moderate, abstemious.<BR>	 m. (-रः) Moderation,<BR>abstinence.<BR> E. अल्प, and आहार food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=062-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अल्पाहारिन्
अल्पाहारिन् mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि) Abstemious, moderate.<BR> E. अल्प, and आहारिन्<BR>who feeds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=062-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अल्पिष्ठ|अल्पिष्ठः
अल्पिष्ठ mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठा-ष्ठं) Least, smallest, very small.<BR> E. अल्प, and इष्ठच् of<BR>the superlative.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=062-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अल्पीकृत
अल्पीकृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Reduced, comminuted, made little or few. E.<BR>अल्प and कृत with च्वि inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=062-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अल्पीभूत
अल्पीभूत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Reduced, diminished, become little or few. E.<BR>अल्प, and भूत become, च्वि inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=062-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अल्पीयस्
अल्पीयस् mfn. (-यान्-यसी-यः) Very small.<BR> E. अल्प and ईयसुन् affix. Also अल्पिष्ठ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=062-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अल्पोन
अल्पोन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Defective, not quite finished, not wholly entire.<BR>E. अल्प a little, ऊन less.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=062-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अल्ला
अल्ला f. (-ल्ला) A mother, in dramatic language.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=062-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव|अवः
अव r. 1st. cl. अवति 1. To keep, protect or defend.<BR>	 2. To please. (The<BR>following meanings, although found in lists of roots, are rarely<BR>used:)<BR>	 3. To move.<BR>	 4. To excite affection or be lovely.<BR>	 5. To<BR>satisfy.<BR>	 6. To know or apprehend.<BR>	 7. To enter.<BR>	 8. To be near.<BR>	 9. To<BR>own, to have a right.<BR>	 10. To obey.<BR>	 11. To act.<BR>	 12. To desire.<BR>	 13.<BR>To shine or be splendid.<BR>	 14. To obtain.<BR>	 15. To embrace.<BR>	 16. To<BR>kill or hurt.<BR>	 17. To take.<BR>	 18. To be.<BR>	 19. To grow. In place of 9,<BR>17, and 18. as above, some read; 9. To be able.<BR>	 17. To burn, and<BR>18. To divide or share.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=062-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव|अवः
अव ind. A preposition and prefix to words, corresponding to off, from,<BR>down from, out, away, &c. and implying; 1. Diminution.<BR>	 2. Depre-<BR>ciation.<BR>	 3. Diffusion.<BR>	 4. Support, resting.<BR>	 5. Commanding.<BR>	 6.<BR>Purifying, correcting.<BR>	 7. Knowledge.<BR>	 8. Disrespect.<BR>	 9. Nourishing.<BR>As अवगन्तु To go away; अवज्ञातुं To disrespect; अवतरितुं To come<BR>down, to descend; अवस्थातुं To remain in or on; अवहर्त्तुं To take<BR>off or away; also अवमः a low man; अवाक् reverse, behind; अवकोकिलः<BR>a koil with a bad voice, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=062-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवकट|अवकटं
अवकट mfn. (-टः-टा-टं)<BR>	 1. Opposite, contrary.<BR>	 2. Backwards.<BR>	 3. Down-<BR>wards.<BR>	 n. (-टं) Opposition, contrariety, reverse.<BR> E. अव down, and<BR>कटच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=062-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवकम्पित
अवकम्पित m. (-तः) A Buddha.<BR> E. अव, and कम्पित shaken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=062-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवकर|अवकरः
अवकर m. (-रः) Dust or sweepings.<BR> E. अव spreading, and कर what<BR>makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=062-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवकर्त्तन|अवकर्तन|अवकर्तनं
अवकर्त्तन n. (-नं) Excision, cutting off.<BR> E. अव and कर्त्तन cutting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=062-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवकर्षण|अवकर्षणं
अवकर्षण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Taking or pulling out, extraction, expulsion.<BR>	 2.<BR>Pulling, dragging.<BR> E. अव, and कर्षण pulling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=062-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवकलित|अवकलितः
अवकलित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Seen.<BR> E. अव and कलित part. past of कल to sound,<BR>&c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=062-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवकाश|अवकाशः
अवकाश m. (-शः)<BR>	 1. Leisure, opportunity.<BR>	 2. Interval, space.<BR>	 3. An open<BR>or wide space.<BR>	 4. A receptacle, a repository, a place in which any<BR>thing is kept.<BR>	 5. A place, a spot, a situation.<BR> E. अव between, &c.<BR>काश to shine, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=062-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवकीर्ण|अवकीर्णः
अवकीर्ण mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-र्णं) I. Coarsely pounded.<BR>	 2. Scattered.<BR>	 3. Dis-<BR>regarded, violated.<BR> E. अव implying separation, कॄ to scatter in the<BR>irregular part. past.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=062-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवकीर्णिन्|अवकीर्ण्णिन्
अवकीर्णिन् mfn. (-र्णी-र्णिनी-र्णि) Violating a vow or engagement to be<BR>chaste, abstemious, &c.<BR>	 m. (-र्णी) The religious student who has com-<BR>mitted an act of incontinency.<BR> E. अव before, कॄ to scatter, क्त the<BR>part. past, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=062-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवकीर्णिव्रत
अवकीर्णिव्रत n. (-तं) Penance for an act of incontinency.<BR> E. अवर्कीर्णि and<BR>व्रत religious obligation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=062-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवकुञ्चन|अवकुंचन|अवकुंचनं
अवकुञ्चन n. (-नं) Bending, curving, flexure, contraction.<BR> E. अव and कुञ्चन<BR>curving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=062-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवकुटार|अवकुटारं
अवकुटार mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>	 1. Opposite, contrary.<BR>	 2. Backwards.<BR>	 3. Down-<BR>wards.<BR>	 n. (-रं) Reverse, contrariety.<BR> E. अव and कुटार aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=062-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवकुट्टित
अवकुट्टित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Vexed.<BR>	 2. Inflamed.<BR>	 3. Cut off.<BR> E. अव, and<BR>कुट्ट to heat, &c. क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=062-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवकुण्ठन|अवकुंठनं
अवकुण्ठन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Investing, surrounding.<BR>	 2. Attracting.<BR> E. अव before<BR>कुठ to surround, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=062-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवकुण्ठित|अवकुंठित
अवकुण्ठित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Affected.<BR>	 2. Surrounded, attracted.<BR> E. अव<BR>before कुठ to surround, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=062-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवकृष्ट|अवकृष्टः
अवकृष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>	 1. Expelled, turned out.<BR>	 2. Removed, sent away,<BR>drawn aside.<BR>	 3. Extracted.<BR>	 4. Pulled.<BR>	 5. Inferior, low.<BR>	 6. Degraded,<BR>outcaste.<BR>	 m. (-ष्टः) A servant who performs the lowest office, a<BR>sweeper, a waterman, &c.<BR> E. अव out of, and कृष्ट drawn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=062-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवकृष्य
अवकृष्य ind.<BR>	 1. Having drawn out or extracted.<BR>	 2. Having drawn to-<BR>gether or contracted.<BR> E. अव, and कृष to draw, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=062-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवकेशिन्
अवकेशिन् mfn. (-शी-शिनी-शि) Barren.<BR> E. अव privative, केश properly hair,<BR>in this instance fruit, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=062-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवक्तव्य|अवक्तव्यं
अवक्तव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>	 1. Not to be said, improper.<BR>	 2. Indescribable.<BR>E. अ neg. वक्तव्य to be said.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=062-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवक्र
अवक्र mfn. (-क्रः-क्रा-क्रं)<BR>	 1. Straight.<BR>	 2. Upright, honest.<BR> E. अ neg. वक्र<BR>crooked liter. and metaph.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=062-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवक्रन्दन|अवक्रंदनं
अवक्रन्दन n. (-नं) Weeping aloud.<BR> E. अव, and क्रन्दन crying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=062-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवक्रय|अवक्रयः
अवक्रय m. (-यः) Price.<BR> E. अव, and क्री to buy, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=062-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवक्रान्ति|अवक्रांतिः|अवक्रान्तिः
अवक्रान्ति f. (-न्तिः)<BR>	 1. Descent, descending.<BR>	 2. Approaching, going near<BR>to.<BR> E. अव, and क्रान्ति passing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=062-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवक्रिया
अवक्रिया f. (-या) Neglect, omission. non-performance of prescribed acts.<BR>E. अव priv. क्रिया act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=062-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवक्रुष्ट
अवक्रुष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं) Sounded ill or badly.<BR>	 2. Reviled, abused.<BR> E. अव,<BR>and क्रुष्ट sounded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=063-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवक्रोश|अवक्रोशः
अवक्रोश m. (-शः)<BR>	 1. A disagreeable noise.<BR>	 2. A curse, an imprecation.<BR>	 3.<BR>Abuse.<BR> E. अव and क्रुश to sound, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=063-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवक्लेद|अवक्लेदः
अवक्लेद m. (-दः)<BR>	 1. Ichor, malignant or fetid discharge.<BR>	 2. Trickling,<BR>descent of moisture.<BR> E. अव, and क्लेद what wets.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=063-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवक्लेदन|अवक्लेदनं
अवक्लेदन n. (-नं) Trickling, falling, as dew or moisture.<BR> E. अव, and क्लेदन<BR>wetting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=063-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवक्वण|अवक्वणः
अवक्वण m. (-णः) A discord, a false note.<BR> E. अव, and क्वण a sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=063-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवक्वाथ|अवक्वाथः
अवक्वाथ m. (-थः) Imperfect digestion or decoction.<BR> E. अव, and क्वाथ a<BR>decoction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=063-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवक्षय|अवक्षयः
अवक्षय m. (-यः) Loss, waste, destruction.<BR> E. अव, and क्षय waste.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=063-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवक्षिप्त
अवक्षिप्त mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं) Said sarcastically, imputed, insinuated.<BR>	 2. Ill<BR>thrown.<BR>	 3. Thrown down.<BR> E. अव, and क्षिप्त thrown.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=063-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवक्षीण
अवक्षीण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Emaciated, wasted.<BR> E. अव, and क्षीण wasted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=063-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवक्षुत|अवक्षुतं
अवक्षुत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Sneezed upon.<BR> E. अव, and क्षुत sneezed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=063-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवक्षेप|अवक्षेपः
अवक्षेप m. (-पः)<BR>	 1. Sarcasm, irony.<BR>	 2. Throwing wrong or improperly.<BR>	 3.<BR>Throwing down.<BR> E. अव, and क्षेप throwing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=063-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवगणित|अवगणितं
अवगणित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Disregarded, despised.<BR> E. अव, गण to count or<BR>reckon in the past part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=063-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवगण्ड|अवगंडः|अवगण्डः
अवगण्ड m. (-ण्डः) A boil or pimple upon the face.<BR> E. अव, गडि to affect the<BR>cheek, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=063-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवगत|अवगतं
अवगत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Known, understood.<BR>	 2. Gone, gone off or away.<BR>3. Assented, promised.<BR> E. अव implying knowledge, and गत part. past<BR>of गम to go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=063-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवगति|अवगतिः
अवगति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Knowledge in general.<BR>	 2. Departure, removal.<BR> E. अव,<BR>गम to go, and क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=063-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवगथ|अवगथः
अवगथ mfn. (-थः-था-थं) Bathing or bathed early in the morning.<BR> E. अव, ग<BR>from गम to go, and थक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=063-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवगदित|अवगदितः
अवगदित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Unsaid, unuttered.<BR> E. अव reverse, गदित<BR>said.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=063-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवगन्तव्य
अवगन्तव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>	 1. Meant, intended to be known or understood.<BR>2. To be quitted. So अवगम्य.<BR> E. अव, and गन्तव्य to be gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=063-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवगम|अवगमः
अवगम m. (-मः)<BR>	 1. Knowledge, certainty.<BR>	 2. Removal, departure.<BR> E. अव,<BR>गम going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=063-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवगाढ
अवगाढ mfn. (-ढः-ढा-ढं)<BR>	 1. Immersed, plunged, bathed.<BR>	 2. Deep.<BR> E. अवगाह<BR>and क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=063-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवगाढवत्
अवगाढवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Bathing, plunging, diving.<BR> E. अवगाढ and वतुप्<BR>aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=063-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवगाद|अवगादः
अवगाद m. (-दः) A small wooden basin for baling water out of a boat.<BR>E. अव for अप water, ग from गम to go, and आदक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=063-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवगाह|अवगाहः
अवगाह m. (-हः)<BR>	 1. Bathing.<BR>	 2. Bathing place, bath.<BR> E. अव before, गाह to<BR>agitate: also वगाह.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=063-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवगाहन|अवगाहनं
अवगाहन n. (-नं) Bathing.<BR> E. अवगाह and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=063-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवगाहित
अवगाहित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Bathed, immersed.<BR> E. अवगाह, and क्त affix, with<BR>इट् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=063-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवगीत|अवगीतं|अवगीतः
अवगीत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Reproached, abused, censured.<BR>	 2. Wicked, vile.<BR>3. Sung depreciatingly, satirised in song.<BR>	 4. Sung badly.<BR>	 n. (-तं)<BR>	 1.<BR>Reproach, blame.<BR>	 2. Satire in song.<BR>	 3. Bad singing.<BR> E. अव bad, &c.<BR>गीत sounded, sung.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=063-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवगुण्ठन|अवगुंठनं|अवगुण्ठनं
अवगुण्ठन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. A veil.<BR>	 2. Sweeping.<BR>	 3. Hiding, veiling.<BR> E. गुठि to<BR>enclose, with अव prefixed, and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=063-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवगुण्ठिका|अवगुंठिका
अवगुण्ठिका f. (-का) See the preceding. E. As before, with वुन् and टाप्<BR>aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=063-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवगुण्ठित|अवगुंठित|अवगुण्ठितं
अवगुण्ठित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Concealed, covered, veiled, screened.<BR> E. अवगुठ<BR>to enclose, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=063-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवगुण्डित|अवगुंडित
अवगुण्डित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Pounded, ground, pulverulent.<BR> E. अव prefixed<BR>to गुण्डित pounded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=063-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवगोरण|अवगोरणं
अवगोरण n. (-णं) Assailing with weapons, assaulting with intent to kill.<BR>E. अव, गुर् or गूर् to assault, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=063-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवग्रह|अवग्रहः
अवग्रह m. (-हः)<BR>	 1. Taking, acceptance.<BR>	 2. Taking off or away, seizure.<BR>	 3.<BR>Disrespect.<BR>	 4. Drought.<BR>	 5. Obstacle, impediment.<BR>	 6. An elephant's<BR>forehead.<BR>	 7. A herd of elephants.<BR>	 8. Nature, original tempera-<BR>ment.<BR>	 9. A sort of knowledge, a false idea.<BR>	 10. An imprecation or<BR>term of abuse.<BR> E. अव before, ग्रह to take or seize, अप् affix: also<BR>अवग्राह.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=063-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवग्रहण|अवग्रहणं
अवग्रहण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Obstacle, impediment.<BR>	 2. Disrespect.<BR> E. अव, ग्रह to<BR>take, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=063-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवग्राह|अवग्राहः
अवग्राह m. (-हः)<BR>	 1. An imprecation or term of abuse, as अवग्राहस्ते स्यात्,<BR>may disappointment befall you.<BR>	 2. Drought.<BR>	 3. Disgrace, discom-<BR>fiture: see अवग्रह. E. As before, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=063-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवगृह्य
अवगृह्य n. (-ह्यं) An inflection, and inflective termination.<BR> E. अव before<BR>ग्रह to take, क्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=063-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवघट्ट|अवघट्टः
अवघट्ट m. (-ट्टः) A hole in the ground, a cave, a cavern.<BR> E. अव down,<BR>low, घट्ट to move, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=063-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवघर्षण|अवघर्षणं
अवघर्षण n. (-णं) Rubbing, scrubbing.<BR> E. अव, and घर्षण rubbing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=063-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवघर्षित
अवघर्षित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Rubbed, scrubbed.<BR> E. अव, and घर्षित rubbed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=063-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवघात|अवघातः
अवघात m. (-तः)<BR>	 1. Threshing corn, by bruising it with a wooden pestle<BR>in a mortar of the same material.<BR>	 2. Sudden or violent death.<BR>	 3.<BR>Striking, killing.<BR>	 4. A violent or fatal blow.<BR> E. अव, and घात<BR>struck.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=063-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवघातिन्
अवघातिन् mfn. (-ती-तिनी-ति) Striking, killing.<BR> E. अव before हन to strike,<BR>णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=063-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवघुष्ट
अवघुष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं) Proclaimed, denounced.<BR> E. अव, and घुष्ट cried.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=063-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवघूर्ण|अवघूर्णः
अवघूर्ण m. (-र्णः)<BR>	 1. A whirling round.<BR>	 2. A whirlpool.<BR> E. अव before घूर्ण<BR>to roll round, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=063-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवघूर्णन|अवघूर्णनं|अवघूर्ण्णन
अवघूर्णन n. (-नं) Rolling or whirling round.<BR> E. अव, and घूर्णन rolling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=063-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवघूर्णित
अवघूर्णित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Whirled round.<BR> E. अव, and घूर्णित whirled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=063-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवघोषण|अवघोषणं
अवघोषण n. (-णं) Crying, proclaiming, denouncing.<BR> E. अव and घोषण<BR>proclamation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=063-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवचन
अवचन n. (-नं) Silence, not speaking.<BR> E. अ neg. वचन word.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=063-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवचनीय
अवचनीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Not to be spoken, improper.<BR> E. अ neg. वचनीय<BR>to be said.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=063-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवचनीयता
अवचनीयता f. (-ता) Impropriety of speech.<BR> E. अवचनीय and तल् affix; also<BR>अवचनीयत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=063-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवचय|अवचयः
अवचय m. (-यः) Gathering, especially flowers, fruits, &c.<BR> E. अव, and चय<BR>collecting; also अवचाय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=063-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवचस्कर|अवचस्करः
अवचस्कर mfn. (-रः-रा-री-रं) Silent, not speaking.<BR> E. अ neg. वच speech,<BR>कर who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=063-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवचार्य्य|अवचार्य
अवचार्य्य mfn. (-र्य्यः-र्य्या-र्य्यं)<BR>	 1. To be cast down.<BR>	 2. To be given.<BR>	 3. To be<BR>put on or applied.<BR> E. अव, चर to go, causal form, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=063-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवचूड|अवचूडः
अवचूड m. (-डः) The crest or ornamented top of a standard, hanging<BR>downwards.<BR> E. अव, चूडा a crest; also अवचूडक and अवचूल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=063-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवचूर्णन|अवचूर्णनं|अवचूर्ण्णन
अवचूर्णन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Pounding, grinding, reducing to powder.<BR>	 2. Sprinkling<BR>absorbent powders on sores.<BR> E. अव, चूर्ण to pound, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=063-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवचूर्णित|अवचूर्णितं|अवचूर्ण्णित
अवचूर्णित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Coarsely pounded.<BR> E. अव, चूर्ण to pound, in<BR>the part. past.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=063-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवचूल|अवचूलः
अवचूल m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. The ornamented head of a standard, when the<BR>ornaments, streamers, peacock's tails, &c. hang downward.<BR>	 2. A<BR>chouri.<BR> E. अव inferior, and चूडा crest, ड changed to ल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=063-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवचूलक|अवचूलकं|अवचूलकः
अवचूलक n. (-कं) A chouri or brush formed of a cow's tail, peacock's<BR>feathers, &c. for fanning off flies.<BR> E. कन् affixed to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=063-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवच्छात
अवच्छात mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Emaciated by abstinence.<BR>	 2. Reaped.<BR>	 3. Cut<BR>off.<BR> E. अव before, छो to destroy, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=063-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवच्छिन्न|अवच्छिन्नं
अवच्छिन्न mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>	 1. Cut off.<BR>	 2. Divided, separated, detached.<BR>3. In logic, predicated. i. e. separated from every thing else by<BR>the properties especially predicated of any thing.<BR>	 4. Bounded. E.<BR>अव, affix छिन्न cut.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=063-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवच्छुरित|अवच्छुरितं|अवछुरित
अवच्छुरित n. (-तं) A horselaugh.<BR> E. अत्र, छुर to cut or split, and the affix<BR>of the part. past: what splits, (one's sides).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=063-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवच्छुरितक|अवच्छुरितकं
अवच्छुरितक n. (-कं) A horselaugh. E. See the preceding word, कन् being<BR>added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=064-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवच्छेद|अवच्छेदः
अवच्छेद m. (-दः)<BR>	 1. A predicate, the property of a thing by which it is<BR>distinguished from every other.<BR>	 2. A part, a portion.<BR>	 3. A bound-<BR>ary, a barrier.<BR>	 4. Amputation, excision.<BR> E. अव off, छेद cutting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=064-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवच्छेदक|अवच्छेदकं|अवच्छेदकः
अवच्छेदक mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>	 1. Peculiar, distinguishing, that which se-<BR>parates.<BR>	 2. Bounding, separating one thing from another.<BR>	 m. (-कः)<BR>1. A predicate, a property.<BR>	 2. A barrier, a boundary.<BR> E. कन् added<BR>to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=064-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवच्छेदन|अवच्छेदनं
अवच्छेदन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Cutting off.<BR>	 2. Separating, dividing.<BR>	 3. Discrimi-<BR>nating, distinguishing.<BR> E. अव, and छेदन cutting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=064-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवच्छेदावच्छेद|अवच्छेदावच्छेदः
अवच्छेदावच्छेद m. (-दः) Generalising, removing distinctions.<BR> E. अवच्छेद<BR>a distinction, and cutting off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=064-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवजनित
अवजनित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Born.<BR> E. अव, and जनित born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=064-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवजय|अवजयः
अवजय m. (-यः) Overcoming, victory.<BR> E. अव, and जय conquer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=064-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवजित
अवजित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Conquered.<BR>	 2. Contemned, disregarded.<BR> E. अव,<BR>and जित conquered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=064-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवज्ञा
अवज्ञा f. (-ज्ञा) Disrespect.<BR> E. अव, ज्ञा to know, अङ् affix, and टाप् for the<BR>fem. also अवज्ञता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=064-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवज्ञात|अवज्ञातं
अवज्ञात mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Disrespected.<BR> E. अव, ज्ञात part. past of ज्ञा to know.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=064-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवज्ञान|अवज्ञानं
अवज्ञान n. (-नं) Disrespect.<BR> E. अव before ज्ञान knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=064-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवज्ञेय
अवज्ञेय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Contemptible, disreputable, to be treated with<BR>disrespect: so अवज्ञातव्य.<BR> E. अव, and ज्ञा to know, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=064-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवज्ञोपहत
अवज्ञोपहत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Degraded, humiliated.<BR> E. अवज्ञा, and उपहत<BR>wounded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=064-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवट|अवटः
अवट m. (-टः)<BR>	 1. A hole, a vacuity.<BR>	 2. A hole in the ground, a chasm, a<BR>pit.<BR>	 3. Any depressed part of the body, a cavity, a fosse, a sinus.<BR>4. A well.<BR>	 5. A juggler.<BR> E. अव to preserve, अटन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=064-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवटङ्क
अवटङ्क m. (-ङ्कः) A mart; also अवटङ्ग.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=064-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवटि|अवटिः
अवटि m. (-टिः)<BR>	 1. A hole in the ground.<BR>	 2. (In anatomy) A sinus, a hollow,<BR>a cavity. E. As before, अटिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=064-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवटीट|अवटीटः
अवटीट mfn. (-टः-टा-टं) Flat-nosed.<BR> E. अव implying lowness, flatness, and<BR>टीटच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=064-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवटु|अवटुः
अवटु f. (-टुः)<BR>	 1. The back of the neck.<BR>	 2. A hole in the ground.<BR>	 3. A<BR>well.<BR>	 4. The name of a tree.<BR> E. अव down, and टीक to go, irregular<BR>affix डु; or अ neg. वट to surround, and उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=064-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवटुज|अवटुजः
अवटुज m. (-जः) A hind curl, the hair on the back of the head.<BR> E. अवटु<BR>and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=064-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवडीन|अवडीनं
अवडीन n. (-नं) The flight of a bird, or a particular act of such flight;<BR>flying down.<BR> E. अव down, &c. and डीन flying: see प्रडीन, उड्डीन, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=064-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवतंस|अवतंसं|अवतंसः
अवतंस mn. (-सः-सं)<BR>	 1. An ear-ring.<BR>	 2. A crest.<BR> E. अव, तसि a Sautra root<BR>to adorn, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=064-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवतंसित
अवतंसित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Having an ear-ring.<BR>	 2. Crested.<BR> E. अवतंस and<BR>इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=064-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवतति|अवततिः
अवतति f. (-तिः) Stretching, extending.<BR> E. अव, and तन to spread, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=064-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवतमस|अवतमसं
अवतमस n. (-सं) Slight darkness, obscurity.<BR> E. अव implying deficiency,<BR>and तमस् darkness, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=064-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवतरण|अवतरणं
अवतरण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Descending, alighting.<BR>	 2. Crossing.<BR>	 3. Translating.<BR>4. Quoting, citing.<BR> E. अव down, तॄ to cross, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=064-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवतान|अवतानः
अवतान m. (-नः) Stretching, extension.<BR> E. अव before तन to stretch, affix ण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=064-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवतार|अवतारः
अवतार n. (-रं)<BR>	 1. Descent, especially of a deity from heaven; the appear-<BR>ance of any deity upon earth, but more particularly the incarna-<BR>tions of VIṢṆU in ten principal forms which are well known, viz.<BR>1. The fish.<BR>	 2. The tortoise.<BR>	 3. The boar.<BR>	 4. The man-lion.<BR>	 5. The<BR>dwarf.<BR>	 6. and 7. The two RĀMAS.<BR>	 8. KṚṢṆA.<BR>	 9. BUDDHA and<BR>10. KALKI. A pious or distinguished person, in the language of<BR>respect or flattery, is also called an Avatāra, a descent or incarna-<BR>tion of the deity.<BR>	 2. A Tirtha or sacred place.<BR>	 3. Translation,<BR>translating 4. Descent.<BR>	 5. Crossing.<BR> E. अव before, तॄ to cross,<BR>affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=064-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवतारण|अवतारणं
अवतारण n. (णं)<BR>	 1. Possession by an evil spirit.<BR>	 2. The ends or border<BR>of a garment.<BR>	 3. Worship, adoration.<BR>	 4. Taking out.<BR> E. अव, तॄ to<BR>pass, in the causal form, and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=064-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवतारित
अवतारित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Taken off or out, laid down or aside.<BR>	 2.<BR>Descended.<BR> E. अव and तॄ causal form, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=064-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवतीर्ण|अवतीर्णः|अवतीर्ण्ण
अवतीर्ण mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-र्णं)<BR>	 1. Descended, alighted.<BR>	 2. Crossed, passed over.<BR>3. Translated.<BR> E. अव and तॄ with क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=064-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवतोका
अवतोका f. (-का) A cow miscarrying from accident.<BR> E. अव, implying cen-<BR>sure, and तोक offspring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=064-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवदंश|अवदंशः
अवदंश m. (-शः) A relish, or what excites thirst.<BR> E. अव, दंश to bite, to be<BR>pungent, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=064-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवदत्त
अवदत्त mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं) Given away.<BR>	 2. Finished, accomplished.<BR> E. अव<BR>before दा to give, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=064-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवदात|अवदातं|अवदातः
अवदात mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. White.<BR>	 2. Yellow.<BR>	 3. Clean, clear.<BR>	 4. Beautiful.<BR>m. (-तः) White, (the colour.)<BR> E. अव, दै to cleanse, क्त affix of the<BR>part. past.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=064-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवदातक
अवदातक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) As above.<BR>	 m. (-कः) White.<BR> E. कन् added to the<BR>last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=064-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवदान|अवदानं
अवदान n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Approved occupation.<BR>	 2. An act accomplished.<BR>	 3.<BR>Achievement, a great or glorious act.<BR>	 4. Breaking, dividing.<BR>	 5.<BR>The root of a fragrant grass; see अवदाह. An oblation.<BR> E. अव, दै to<BR>cleanse, to purify, or दा to give, and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=064-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवदारण|अवदारणं
अवदारण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. A spade or hoe.<BR>	 2. Tearing, dividing.<BR> E. अव down, दॄ<BR>to tear or rend, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=064-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवदारित
अवदारित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Torn, rent.<BR> E. अव before दॄ to tear, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=064-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवदाह|अवदाहं|अवदाहः
अवदाह n. (-हं) The root of a fragrant grass, (Andropogon muricatum.)<BR>E. अव reverse, and दाह heat, burning, heat-preventing, from its<BR>being used in Tātis or screens, placed before doors, &c. kept con-<BR>stantly wet: the air passing through these, blows into a room cool<BR>and refreshing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=064-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवदाहेष्ट|अवदाहेष्टं
अवदाहेष्ट n. (-ष्टं) See the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=064-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवदाहेष्टकापथ|अवदाहेष्टकापथं
अवदाहेष्टकापथ n. (-थं) See अवदाह. See also इष्टकापथ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=064-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवदीर्ण|अवदीर्णं
अवदीर्ण mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-र्णं)<BR>	 1. Melted, fused, liquefied.<BR>	 2. Torn, rent,<BR>sundered.<BR> E. अव, दॄ to separate, irregular part. past.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=064-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवदून
अवदून mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Regretted.<BR> E. अव, दू to be sorry, affix. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=064-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवदोह|अवदोहः
अवदोह m. (-हः) Milk.<BR> E. अव, दुह to milk, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=064-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवद्य|अवद्यं
अवद्य mfn. (-द्यः-द्या-द्यं)<BR>	 1. Low, inferior.<BR>	 2. Disagreeable, disliked.<BR>	 n. (-द्यं)<BR>Sin, vice.<BR> E. अ neg. वद to speak, and यत् affix of the part. future;<BR>not to be spoken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=064-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवद्रङ्ग|अवद्रंगः|अवद्रङ्गः
अवद्रङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः) A market or fair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=064-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवधातव्य
अवधातव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं) To be attended to, deserving attention and care.<BR>So अवधानीय and अवधेय.<BR> E. अव before धा to have, तव्य, अनीयर् or यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=064-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवधान|अवधानं
अवधान n. (नं)<BR>	 1. Attention, attentiveness, intentness.<BR>	 2. Care, careful-<BR>ness.<BR> E. अव, धा to have or hold, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=064-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवधानता
अवधानता f. (-ता) Attentiveness.<BR> E. अवधान attention, तल् added, also with<BR>त्व, अवधानत्व n. (-त्वं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=064-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवधारण|अवधारणं
अवधारण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Determining, certainty, ascertainment.<BR>	 2. Emphasis.<BR>E. अव before धृ to hold ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=064-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवधारणीय
अवधारणीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) To be ascertained.<BR> E. अव before धृ to hold,<BR>causal form, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=064-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवधारित|अवधारितः
अवधारित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Certain, known, ascertained.<BR> E. अव before धृ to<BR>hold, causal form, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=064-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवधार्य्य|अवधार्य|अवधार्य्यः
अवधार्य्य mfn. (-र्य्यः-र्य्या-र्य्यं) To be ascertained, known.<BR> E. अव before धृ to hold,<BR>causal form, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=064-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवधावन|अवधावनं
अवधावन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Running after, pursuing.<BR>	 2. Taking, seizure.<BR>	 3.<BR>Cleaning.<BR> E. अव, धाव to run, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=064-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवधावनीय
अवधावनीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>	 1. To be run after.<BR>	 2. To be seized.<BR> E. अव<BR>after, धाव to run, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=064-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवधावित
अवधावित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Chased, pursued.<BR>	 2. Cleaned.<BR> E. अव before<BR>धाव to run, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=064-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवधि|अवधिः
अवधि m. (-धिः)<BR>	 1. Limit, division 2. Period. time.<BR>	 3. A hole, a pit.<BR>	 4.<BR>Agreement, engagement.<BR>	 5. Conclusion, termination.<BR>	 6. Attention,<BR>application.<BR>	 7. Care.<BR> E. अव, धा to have, कि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=065-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवधिता
अवधिता f. (-ता) Limit, limitation.<BR> E. अवधि with तल् affix; also with त्व,<BR>अवधित्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=065-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवधीर
अवधीर r. 10th cl. (अवधीरयति) To disregard, to disrespect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=065-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवधीरण|अवधीरणं
अवधीरण n. (-णं) Treating with disrespect.<BR> E. अवधीर and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=065-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवधीरित
अवधीरित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Disrespected, disregarded.<BR> E. अवधीर and क्त<BR>aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=065-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवधूत|अवधूतः
अवधूत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Compelled.<BR>	 2. Discarded.<BR>	 3. Shaken, removed,<BR>tossed.<BR>	 4. Trodden upon.<BR>	 5. Separated from worldly feeling and<BR>obligation.<BR> E. अव, and धूत shaken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=065-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवधूनन|अवधूननं
अवधूनन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Shaking, causing to shake.<BR>	 2. Expelling.<BR>	 3. Being in<BR>agitation, trembling.<BR>	 4. Trembling on, treading on.<BR> E. अव before<BR>धूनन shaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=065-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवध्वंस|अवध्वंसः
अवध्वंस m. (-सः)<BR>	 1. Censure, blame.<BR>	 2. Abandoning, quitting.<BR>	 3. Pound-<BR>ing, grinding.<BR> E. अव before ध्वंस to go, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=065-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवध्वस्त|अवध्वस्तः
अवध्वस्त mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं)<BR>	 1. Pounded coarsely.<BR>	 2. Abandoned.<BR>	 3. Censured.<BR>E. अव separate, &c. ध्वंस to go, part. affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=065-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवन|अवनं
अवन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Satisfaction, (given or received.)<BR>	 2. Preserving, protecting.<BR>3. Kindness.<BR>	 4. Speed.<BR>	 5. Going.<BR>	 6. Obtaining.<BR>	 7. Asking.<BR>	 8. Seizing.<BR>9. Killing.<BR>	 10. Strength, power.<BR>	 11. Increase.<BR>	 12. Existence, being.<BR>13. Doing.<BR>	 14. Desire.<BR>	 15. Beautifying, adorning.<BR>	 16. Embracing.<BR>17. Bearing.<BR>	 18. Entrance.<BR> E. अव to go, to preserve, &c. ल्युट्<BR>aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=065-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवनत|अवनतं
अवनत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Bending, stooping, bowed.<BR> E. अव down, नम to<BR>bow, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=065-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवनति|अवनतिः
अवनति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Bowing, stooping.<BR>	 2. Setting.<BR> E. अव, and नति<BR>bowing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=065-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवनद्ध|अवनद्धं
अवनद्ध mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-धं) Bound on, tied, fastened.<BR>	 n. (-द्धं) A drum: see<BR>आनद्ध.<BR> E. अव, and नद्ध bound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=065-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवनय|अवनयः
अवनय m. (-यः) Causing to descend, throwing down.<BR> E. अव down, नय for<BR>नाय causing to get: see अवनाय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=065-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवनाट|अवनाटः
अवनाट mfn. (-टः-टा-टं) Flat-nosed.<BR> E. अव flatness, नाटच् affix, in this<BR>sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=065-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवनाम|अवनामः
अवनाम m. (-मः) Causing to bend, bending, bowing.<BR> E. अव before नम to<BR>bow, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=065-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवनामक
अवनामक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) What depresses or causes to bow or bend. E.<BR>अव and नम in the causal form, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=065-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवनामिन्
अवनामिन् mfn. (-मी-मिनी-मि) Bending or bowing down.<BR> E. अव, and नामिन्<BR>what bends.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=065-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवनाय|अवनायः
अवनाय m. (-यः) Causing to descend, throwing down, precipitating. E.<BR>अव down, नीञ् to obtain, in the causal form, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=065-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवनायक
अवनायक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Causing to descend.<BR> E. अव before नीञ् to obtain,<BR>causal form, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=065-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवनाह|अवनाहः
अवनाह m. (-हः) Binding, grinding, putting on.<BR> E. अव before नह to bind,<BR>घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=065-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवनि|अवनिः
अवनि f. (-निः) The earth.<BR> E. अव to preserve, अनि Unādi affix; it is also<BR>written अवनी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=065-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवनिपति|अवनिपतिः
अवनिपति m. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. A king.<BR>	 2. VIṢṆU.<BR>	 3. YUDHISTHIRA.<BR> E. अवनि, and<BR>पति lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=065-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवनिपाल|अवनिपालः
अवनिपाल m. (-लः) A king.<BR> E. अवनि and पाल who protects.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=065-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवनिरुह
अवनिरुह m. (-रुट्) A tree.<BR> E. अवनि, and रुह what mounts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=065-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवनिष्ठीवन|अवनिष्ठीवनं
अवनिष्ठीवन n. (-नं) Spitting upon.<BR> E. अव, and निष्ठीवन spitting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=065-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवनी
अवनी f. (-नी) The earth: see अवनि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=065-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवनीपति|अवनीपतिः
अवनीपति m. (-तिः) A king, or sovereign.<BR> E. अवनी the earth, and पति a<BR>master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=065-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवनीश|अवनीशः
अवनीश m. (-शः) A king.<BR> E. अवनी, and ईश lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=065-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवनीश्वर|अवनीश्वरः
अवनीश्वर m. (-रः) A king, an emperor.<BR> E. अवनी, and ईश्वर lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=065-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवनेजन|अवनेजनं
अवनेजन n. (-नं) Washing.<BR> E. अव, and नेजन ablution.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=065-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवन्ति|अवंति|अवंतिः|अवन्तिः
अवन्ति m. (-न्तिः)<BR>	 1. The name of a city, the modern Oujein.<BR>	 2. The name<BR>of a river.<BR> E. अव to preserve, Unādi affix झिच्; the derivative is<BR>irregular. Avanti, is one of the seven sacred cities of the Hindus, to<BR>die at which secures eternal happiness: the word is also written अवन्ती<BR>and अवन्तिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=065-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवन्तिसोम|अवन्तिसोमं|अवन्तिसोमः
अवन्तिसोम n. (-मं) Sour gruel, prepared from the fermentation of rice-water.<BR>E. अवन्ति the city, षू to produce, मन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=065-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवन्ती|अवंती
अवन्ती f. (-न्ती) A city: see अवन्ति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=065-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवपतन|अवपतनं
अवपतन n. (-नं) Alighting, descending.<BR> E. अव down, पतन falling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=065-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवपन्न
अवपन्न mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>	 1. Alighted, descended.<BR>	 2. Fallen on or into.<BR>	 3.<BR>Thrown down.<BR> E. अव, and पन्न gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=065-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवपात|अवपातः
अवपात m. (-तः)<BR>	 1. A hole or pit for catching game in.<BR>	 2. Descent, descend-<BR>ing.<BR> E. अव below, पत to go or fall, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=065-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवपातन|अवपातनं
अवपातन n. (-नं) Felling, knocking or cutting down.<BR> E. अव down, पातन<BR>causing to fall.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=065-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवपालित
अवपालित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Neglected, not protected.<BR> E. अव before पालित<BR>protected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=065-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवपीड|अवपीडः
अवपीड m. (-डः) A sternutatory, any drug producing sneezing.<BR> E. अव,<BR>पीड to pain, affix. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=065-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवबधा
अवबधा f. (-धा) Segment of the base of a triangle.<BR> E. अव, and बध what kills.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=065-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवबोध|अवबोधः
अवबोध m. (-धः)<BR>	 1. Judgment, discrimination, knowledge.<BR>	 2. Waking,<BR>being awake.<BR>	 3. Teaching.<BR> E. अव, and बोध knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=065-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवबोधक|अवबोधकः
अवबोधक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A teacher.<BR>	 2. An awakener.<BR> E. अव before बुध to be<BR>wise, causal form, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=065-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवबोधकत्व
अवबोधकत्व n. (-त्वं) Instruction, guidance, explanation.<BR> E. अववोधक who<BR>teaches, and त्व aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=065-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवभास|अवभासः
अवभास m. (-सः)<BR>	 1. Light.<BR>	 2. Manifestation.<BR> E. अव, and भास light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=065-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवभासित
अवभासित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Illumined, lighted, radiant.<BR>	 2. Evident,<BR>manifest.<BR> E. अव, and भासित splendid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=065-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवभासिन्
अवभासिन् mfn. (-सी-सिनी-सि) Shining, bright.<BR>	 f. (-नी) The outer skin or<BR>cuticle.<BR> E. अव, and भासिन् shines.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=065-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवभिन्न
अवभिन्न mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं) Broken, pierced, divided.<BR> E. अव affix, भिन्न cut or<BR>broken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=065-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवभुग्न
अवभुग्न mfn. (-ग्नः-ग्ना-ग्नं) Contracted, bent.<BR> E. अव, and भूग्र bent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=065-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवभृथ|अवभृथः
अवभृथ m. (-थः)<BR>	 1. A supplementary sacrifice made to atone for any de-<BR>fects in a principal and preceding one.<BR>	 2. Bathing after a sacrifice.<BR>E. अव, भृ to screen, क्थन् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=065-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवभृथस्नान
अवभृथस्नान n. (-नं) Bathing after any sacrifice or ceremony.<BR> E. अवभृथ as<BR>before, and स्नान bathing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=065-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवभ्रट|अवभ्रटः
अवभ्रट mfn. (-टः-टा-टं) Flat-nosed.<BR> E. अव and भ्रटच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=065-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवम|अवमं|अवमः
अवम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं) Low, vile, inferior, base.<BR>	 n. (-नं) A lunar day, exactly<BR>coinciding with a solar one.<BR> E. अव to preserve, &c. अम Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=065-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवमत|अवमतं
अवमत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Despised, disregarded, contemned.<BR> E. अव imply-<BR>ing contempt, and मत known, minded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=065-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवमताङ्कुश|अवमतांकुश|अवमताङ्कुशः
अवमताङ्कुश m. (-शः) A restive elephant, or one in rut.<BR> E. अवमत disre-<BR>garded, and अङ्कुश the goad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=065-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवमति|अवमतिः
अवमति m. (-तिः) A master, an owner.<BR>	 f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Aversion, dislike.<BR>	 2.<BR>Disregard, contempt.<BR> E. अव, मन to heed, and क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=065-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवमन्तव्य|अवमंतव्य
अवमन्तव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं) To be contemned, to be treated with disres-<BR>pect.<BR> E. अव before मन and तव्य affix. So अवमन्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=065-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवमन्तृ|अवमंतृ
अवमन्तृ mfn. (-न्ता-न्त्री-न्तृ) Proud, contemptuous, disrespectful.<BR> E. अव be-<BR>fore मन, with तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=065-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवमर्द्द|अवमर्द|अवमर्दः
अवमर्द्द m. (-र्द्दः)<BR>	 1. Devastation, inflicting pain or punishment on an<BR>enemy, by laying his country waste, &c.<BR>	 2. Giving pain.<BR> E. अव, मृद<BR>to tread down, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=065-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवमर्षण|अवमर्षणं
अवमर्षण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Intolerance, impatience.<BR>	 2. Effacing, obliterating.<BR>	 3.<BR>Banishing from recollection.<BR> E. अव away, &c. मृष to endure, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=065-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवमान|अवमानः
अवमान n. (-नं) Disrespect, contempt.<BR> E. अव before मान respect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=065-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवमानता
अवमानता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Dishonourableness.<BR>	 2. Contempt.<BR> E. तल् added to the<BR>last; also with त्व, अवमानत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=065-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवमानना
अवमानना f. (-ना) Disrespect.<BR> E. अव before मन to mind, युच् affix and<BR>टाप् fem. do.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=066-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवमाननीय
अवमाननीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) To be disrespected, to be contemned.<BR> E. अव<BR>before मन, with अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=066-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवमानित|अवमानितः
अवमानित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Disrespected, despised.<BR> E. अव before the part.<BR>past of मन to respect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=066-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवमानिता
अवमानिता f. (-ता) Disrespectfulness.<BR> E. तल् added to अवमानिन्; also with<BR>त्व, अवमानित्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=066-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवमानिन्
अवमानिन् mfn. (-नी-निनी-नि) Behaving disrespectfully, contemning, des-<BR>pising.<BR> E. अवमान and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=066-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवमान्य|अवमान्यः
अवमान्य mfn. (-न्यः-न्या-न्यं) To be treated with disrespect.<BR> E. अव before मन<BR>with ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=066-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवमूत्रयत्
अवमूत्रयत् mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्) Urining upon.<BR> E. अव on, मूत्र nominal v. to<BR>make water, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=066-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवमूर्द्धशय
अवमूर्द्धशय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Prostrate.<BR> E. अव down, मूर्द्धन् the forehead, शय<BR>who sleeps.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=066-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवमोचन|अवमोचनं
अवमोचन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Letting forth, emitting.<BR>	 2. Setting at liberty.<BR> E. अव<BR>before मुच to set free, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=066-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवयव|अवयवः
अवयव m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. A limb, a member.<BR>	 2. A part, a portion.<BR>	 3. Division<BR>of a logical argument or syllogism.<BR> E. अव, यु to join, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=066-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवयविन्
अवयविन् mfn. (-वि-विनी-वि)<BR>	 1. Limbed, having limbs.<BR>	 2. Having portions<BR>or subdivisions.<BR>	 m. (-वी) A syllogism, a logical argument.<BR> E. अवयव<BR>and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=066-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवर|अवरं|अवरः
अवर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>	 1. Posterior, hinder, last.<BR>	 2. Younger.<BR>	 3. Inferior.<BR>	 n.<BR>(-रं) The hind thigh of an elephant.<BR>	 f. (-रा) A name of DURGĀ.<BR> E. अ<BR>neg. and वर preferable; not the best, or than which nothing is better.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=066-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरज|अवरजः
अवरज mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>	 1. Younger, junior.<BR>	 2. Inferior, of low birth.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-जः) A younger brother.<BR> E. अवर after, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=066-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरत|अवरतः
अवरत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Stopped, ceased, desisted from.<BR> E. अव, रम to sport,<BR>affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=066-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरतस्
अवरतस् ind. Hinder, posterior.<BR> E. अवर and अतसुच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=066-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरति|अवरतिः
अवरति f. (-तिः) Stopping, ceasing, cessation, end.<BR> E. अव bad, &c. रम to<BR>play, and क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=066-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरवर्ण|अवरवर्णः
अवरवर्ण mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा or -र्णी) A Śūdra, a man or woman of the fourth tribe.<BR>E. अवर last, and वर्ण a tribe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=066-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरवर्णक|अवरवर्णकः
अवरवर्णक mf. (-र्णकः-र्णिका) See the preceding.<BR> E. कन् added to अवरवर्ण,<BR>also अवरवर्णज.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=066-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरव्रत|अवरव्रतः
अवरव्रत m. (-तः) The sun.<BR> E. अ neg. वर best, than what nought is better,<BR>and व्रत worship: whose worship is of the first importance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=066-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरस्तात्
अवरस्तात् ind. Hinder, posterior.<BR> E. अवर and अस्तात् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=066-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरार्द्ध
अवरार्द्ध n. (-र्द्धं) The last half.<BR> E. अवर and अर्द्ध half.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=066-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरार्द्ध्य|अवरार्द्ध्यः
अवरार्द्ध्य mfn. (-र्द्ध्यः-र्द्ध्या-र्द्ध्यं) Belonging to the last half.<BR> E. यत् affix to the<BR>last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=066-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरीण|अवरीणं
अवरीण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Censured, blamed.<BR> E. अव, री to flow, the irre-<BR>gular part. past.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=066-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरुग्ण
अवरुग्ण mfn. (-ग्णः-ग्णा-ग्णं)<BR>	 1. Broken, torn.<BR>	 2. Diseased.<BR> E. अव before रुज<BR>to be sick, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=066-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरुद्ध
अवरुद्ध mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>	 1. Checked, stopped, hindered.<BR>	 2. Shut up or in,<BR>inclosed.<BR>	 3. Secluded, as in a harem.<BR> E. अव, and रुद्ध hindered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=066-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरूढ
अवरूढ mfn. (-ढः-ढा-ढं) Descended, alighted.<BR> E. अव down, रुह to go, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=066-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरोध|अवरोधः
अवरोध m. (-धः)<BR>	 1. The seraglio of a palace, the queen's apartment.<BR>	 2. A<BR>queen.<BR>	 3. A palace.<BR>	 4. A covering.<BR>	 5. Hindrance, obstruction.<BR>	 6. A<BR>fence, a pen, an inclosure, confinement.<BR>	 7. Restraint.<BR> E. अव, रुध to<BR>inclose or shut up, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=066-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरोधक|अवरोधकः
अवरोधक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) What impedes or obstructs.<BR>	 m. (-कः) A guard.<BR>f. (-धिका) A female of the harem.<BR>	 n. (-कं) A barrier, a fence.<BR> E. अव<BR>before रोधक what opposes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=066-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरोधन|अवरोधनं
अवरोधन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. The inner or women's apartments in a royal palace.<BR>2. Hindering, obstructing.<BR>	 3. Obstacle, impediment.<BR> E. अव, रुघ to<BR>enclose, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=066-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरोधायन
अवरोधायन n. (-नं) A seraglio.<BR> E. अवरोध hindrance, and अयन going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=066-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरोधिक|अवरोधिकः
अवरोधिक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Obstructive, impeding.<BR>	 m. (-कः) A guard of<BR>the queen's apartments.<BR> E. अवरोध with ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=066-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरोधिन्
अवरोधिन् mfn. (-धी-धिनी-धि) Obstructing.<BR> E. अवरोध and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=066-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरोपण|अवरोपणं
अवरोपण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Taking away, depriving, diminishing.<BR>	 2. Descending.<BR>3. Setting, (as of the sun.)<BR> E. अव affix, and रोपण placing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=066-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरोपित
अवरोपित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Deprived of, curtailed, diminished, lost.<BR> E. अव<BR>aff. रोपित placed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=066-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरोह|अवरोहः
अवरोह m. (-हः)<BR>	 1. Mounting, ascending.<BR>	 2. Descent, passing from or<BR>over.<BR>	 3. The growth of a creeping plant or vine.<BR>	 4. A pendant<BR>branch, one that strikes fresh root into the earth, as those of the<BR>Indian fig tree.<BR>	 5. Heaven or Svarga.<BR> E. अव up or down, &c. रुह to<BR>mount, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=066-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरोहण|अवरोहणं
अवरोहण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Alighting, descending.<BR>	 2. Mounting.<BR> E. अव before<BR>रुह to mount, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=066-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरोहिन्
अवरोहिन् mfn. (-ही-हिणी-हि)<BR>	 1. What descends.<BR>	 2. What ascends.<BR>	 m. (-ही)<BR>The Indian fig tree.<BR> E. अवरोह a branch, &c. and इनि poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=066-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवर्ण|अवर्णः
अवर्ण mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-र्णी-र्णं)<BR>	 1. Colourless.<BR>	 2. Bad, low, destitude of good<BR>qualities.<BR>	 m. (-र्णः) Censure, blame.<BR> E. अ neg. and वर्ण praise, colour,<BR>&c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=066-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवर्त्तमान|अवर्तमान
अवर्त्तमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>	 1. Nonexistent.<BR>	 2. Not present.<BR> E. अ neg.<BR>वर्त्तमान existing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=066-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवर्द्धमान
अवर्द्धमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Not increasing. not growing.<BR> E. अ neg. वर्द्धमान<BR>increasing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=066-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलक्ष|अवलक्षः
अवलक्ष m. (-क्षः) or attributively.<BR>	 mfn. (-क्षः-क्षा-क्षं) White: see वलक्ष.<BR> E. अव,<BR>and लक्ष to mark, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=066-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलग्न|अवलग्नः
अवलग्न mn. (-ग्नः-ग्नं) The waist.<BR>	 mfn. (-ग्नः-ग्ना-ग्नं) Placed contiguously, im-<BR>pressed, attached, &c.<BR> E. अव, and लग्न part. past of लग to be near or<BR>with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=066-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलम्ब|अवलंबः|अवलम्बः
अवलम्ब m. (-म्बः)<BR>	 1. Asylum, dependence, support.<BR>	 2. Depending,<BR>hanging on or from.<BR>	 3. A prop, a stay.<BR>	 4. A suspender.<BR>	 5. A perpen-<BR>dicular.<BR> E. अव before लवि to go, &c. अच् affix; also अवलम्बनं<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=066-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलम्बन|अवलंबनं|अवलम्बनं
अवलम्बन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Depending upon, dependence.<BR>	 2. Hanging on or<BR>from.<BR>	 3. A prop.<BR> E. अव before लबि to go, &c. and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=066-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलम्बित|अवलंबित|अवलम्बितं
अवलम्बित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Quick, expeditious.<BR>	 2. Alighting, descending.<BR>3. Protected, cherished.<BR>	 4. Hanging on or upon, suspended from,<BR>clinging to.<BR>	 5. Depending upon, trusting to, supported by.<BR> E. अव,<BR>and the part. past of लवि to go, to fall, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=066-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलम्बिन्|अवलंबिन्
अवलम्बिन् mfn. (-म्बी-म्बिनी-म्बि) Depending on.<BR> E. अवलम्ब and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=066-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलिप्त|अवलिप्तः
अवलिप्त mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं)<BR>	 1. Anointed, plastered, smeared.<BR>	 2. Proud,<BR>arrogant.<BR> E. अव before लिप्त smeared.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=066-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलिप्तता
अवलिप्तता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Pride, arrogance.<BR>	 2. Unction.<BR> E. अवलिप्त plastered,<BR>smeared, and तल् affix; also with त्व, अवलिप्तत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=066-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलीढ|अवलीढं
अवलीढ mfn. (-ढः-ढा-ढं)<BR>	 1. Licked.<BR>	 2. Devoured, destroyed.<BR> E. अव and लीढ<BR>licked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=066-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलीला
अवलीला f. (-ला) Sport, play.<BR> E. अव, and लीला sport.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=066-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलुञ्चन|अवलुंचन|अवलुंचनं
अवलुञ्चन n. (-नं) Tearing, tearing or cutting off.<BR> E. अव, लुच to separate,<BR>affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=066-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलुण्ठन|अवलुंठनं|अवलुण्ठनं
अवलुण्ठन n. (-नं) Rolling on the ground.<BR> E. अव, and लुण्ठन rolling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=066-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलुण्ठित
अवलुण्ठित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Rolled on the ground.<BR> E. अव, and लुण्ठित rolling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=066-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलून
अवलून mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Cut off.<BR> E. अव, and लून cut.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=066-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलेप|अवलेपः
अवलेप m. (-पः)<BR>	 1. Pride.<BR>	 2. Smearing, anointing.<BR>	 3. Ornament.<BR>	 4. Union,<BR>association.<BR> E. अव, लिप to smear, &c. अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=066-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलेपन|अवलेपनं
अवलेपन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Daring, proud or arrogant purpose.<BR>	 2. Anointing. E.<BR>अव, लिप to smears, &c. ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=066-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलेह|अवलेहः
अवलेह m. (-हः) An extract, and electuary, confection.<BR> E. अव, and लेह lick-<BR>ing, what is to be licked with the tongue, not masticated or drank.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=066-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलेहन|अवलेहनं
अवलेहन n. (-नं) Licking with the tongue.<BR> E. अव, and लेहन licking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=066-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलेह्य
अवलेह्य mfn. (-ह्यः-ह्या-ह्यं) Thick, viscid.<BR> E. अव, and लेह्य to be licked with<BR>the tongue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=066-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलोक|अवलोकः
अवलोक m. (-कः) Sight, seeing.<BR> E. अव, and लोकृ to see, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=067-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलोकन|अवलोकनं
अवलोकन n. (-नं) Sight, seeing.<BR> E. अव, लोकृ to see, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=067-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलोकित|अवलोकितं|अवलोकितः
अवलोकित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Seen.<BR>	 m. (-तः) A Bauddha.<BR> E. अव, and the part.<BR>past of लोकृ to see.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=067-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवल्गुज|अवल्गुजः
अवल्गुज m. (-जः) A plant, (Serratula anthelmintica:) see सोमराजी.<BR> E. अ<BR>neg. वल्गु handsome, and ज produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=067-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अववाद|अववादः
अववाद m. (-दः)<BR>	 1. A command, an order.<BR>	 2. Censure, reproach.<BR>	 3.<BR>Trust, confidence.<BR> E. अव implying disrespect, and वाद speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=067-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवश
अवश mfn. (-शः-शा-शं)<BR>	 1. Independent, unsubjected, unrestrained.<BR>	 2.<BR>Necessary, certain.<BR> E. अ neg. वश subjection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=067-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवशक्थिका
अवशक्थिका f. (-का) A cloth tied round the legs and knees of a person<BR>sitting on his hams: see अवसक्थिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=067-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवशिष्ट|अवशिष्टः
अवशिष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं) Left, rest, remainder.<BR> E. अव, and शिष्ट left.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=067-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवशीन|अवशीनः
अवशीन m. (-नः) A scorpion.<BR> E. अव before श्यै to go, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=067-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवशीभूत
अवशीभूत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Unrestrained, independent.<BR>	 2. Uninfluenced<BR>by magic.<BR> E. अवश and भूत been, with च्वि inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=067-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवशेष|अवशेषः
अवशेष m. (-षः)<BR>	 1. Leavings, remainder.<BR>	 2. End, close, termination. E.<BR>अव, and शेष remainder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=067-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवश्य|अवश्यं
अवश्य mfn. (-श्यः-श्या-श्यं) Untameable, ungovernable. ind. (-श्य) Certainly,<BR>necessarily.<BR> E. अव, श्यै to go, डम् affix; irregularly formed: it occurs<BR>in composition with or without the nasal, as अवश्यङ्कारी who does<BR>what is necessary, अवश्यपाच्यः to be necessarily cooked, &c.<BR> E. अ neg.<BR>वश to subdue, affix यत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=067-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवश्यक
अवश्यक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Necessary, inevitable, indispensable.<BR> E. अवश्य and<BR>कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=067-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवश्यकता
अवश्यकता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Necessity, obligation.<BR>	 2. Certainty.<BR> E. तल् added to<BR>अवश्यक; also अवश्यकत्वं with त्व aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=067-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवश्या
अवश्या f. (-श्या) A fog or mist.<BR> E. अव, श्यै to go, ड affix and fem. टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=067-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवश्याय|अवश्यायः
अवश्याय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. Frost.<BR>	 2. Pride.<BR> E. अव, श्यै to go, and यङ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=067-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवष्कयणी
अवष्कयणी f. (-णी) A cow that bears a calf after a long interval: see<BR>वष्कयणी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=067-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवष्टब्ध|अवष्टब्धं
अवष्टब्ध mfn. (-ब्धः-ब्धा-ब्धं)<BR>	 1. Near.<BR>	 2. Protected, supported.<BR>	 3. Surpassed,<BR>overcome.<BR>	 4. Bound, tied.<BR>	 5. Opposed.<BR>	 6. Wrapped up, enfolded.<BR>	 7.<BR>Hanging from or upon.<BR>	 8. Stopped, stayed.<BR>	 9. Paralysed.<BR> E. अव,<BR>स्तभि to stop, to stand, in the part. past.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=067-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवष्टभ्य
अवष्टभ्य ind.<BR>	 1. Leaning upon, holding.<BR>	 2. Stopping, arresting.<BR> E. अव be-<BR>fore स्तभि to stop, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=067-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवष्टम्भ|अवष्टंभः|अवष्टम्भः
अवष्टम्भ m. (-म्भः)<BR>	 1. Gold.<BR>	 2. Commencement, beginning.<BR>	 3. A post or<BR>pillar.<BR>	 4. Excellence.<BR>	 5. Impediment.<BR>	 6. Support, stay.<BR>	 7. Paralysis.<BR>E. अव, स्तभि to stay or stop, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=067-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवष्टम्भन|अवष्टंभनं
अवष्टम्भन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Supporting, protecting.<BR>	 2. A pillar, a post.<BR>	 3. Stop-<BR>ping, staying.<BR>	 4. Paralysing.<BR> E. अव before स्तभि to stay, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=067-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवष्वाण|अवष्वाणं|अवष्वाणः
अवष्वाण n. (-णं) Eating.<BR> E. अव, स्वन to sound, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=067-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवस|अवसं|अवसः
अवस ind. (-वस) Without, on the outside.<BR>	 m. (-सः)<BR>	 1. A king.<BR>	 2. The sun.<BR>n. (-सं) Preserving, protecting, (in the language of the Vedas.) E.<BR>अव to preserve, &c. असच् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=067-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसक्त
अवसक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>	 1. Attached to or by, in contact with.<BR>	 2. En-<BR>gaged or eager.<BR>	 3. Ound round, begirt.<BR>	 4. Placed or thrown upon.<BR>E. अव, and सक्त joined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=067-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसक्तिका
अवसक्तिका f. (-का) A wrapper, a girth or band.<BR> E. अव about, सक्त joined,<BR>कन् affix, and the fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=067-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसक्थिका
अवसक्थिका f. (-का)1. A wrapper, a mantle.<BR>	 2. A cloth drawn round<BR>the knees and legs of a person sitting on his hams.<BR> E. अव round,<BR>सक्थि the thigh, कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=067-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसज्जन|अवसज्जनं
अवसज्जन n. (-नं) Embracing, clinging.<BR> E. अव before सज्ज to embrace, ल्युट्<BR>aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=067-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसथ|अवसथः
अवसथ m. (-थः)<BR>	 1. A village.<BR>	 2. A college, a school.<BR>	 n. (-थं) A house. E.<BR>अ neg. वस to dwell, and अथच् affix; than which there is no other<BR>or better abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=067-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसथ्य|अवसथ्यः
अवसथ्य m. (-थ्यः) A college, a school. E. See the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=067-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसन्न|अवसन्नः
अवसन्न mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>	 1. Melancholy, dispirited, unhappy.<BR>	 2. Ended,<BR>terminated.<BR>	 3. Languid, enervated.<BR>	 4. Separated.<BR>	 5. Bowed, bent.<BR>6. Non-suited.<BR> E. अव before सन to faint, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=067-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसन्नता
अवसन्नता f. (-ता) Low spirits, affliction.<BR>	 2. Termination, completion. E.<BR>तल् added to अवसन्न; also with त्व affix अवसन्नत्वं<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=067-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसर|अवसरः
अवसर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Occasion, opportunity.<BR>	 2. Rain, raining.<BR>	 3. Consulta-<BR>tion in private.<BR>	 4. A year.<BR>	 5. A moment.<BR> E. अव, सृ to go, अप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=067-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसर्ग|अवसर्गः
अवसर्ग m. (-र्गः) Following one's own inclinations.<BR> E. अव, सृज to create, घञ्<BR>affix; ज becomes ग.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=067-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसर्प|अवसर्पः
अवसर्प m. (-र्पः) A spy, a secret emissary: see अपसर्प.<BR> E. अव, सृप to go,<BR>अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=067-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसर्पिणी
अवसर्पिणी f. (-णी) A Jaina division of time; ten Crores of crores of<BR>Sāgaras or oceans of years.<BR> E. अव, सृप to go, णिनि and ङीप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=067-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसव्य|अवसव्यं
अवसव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं) Right, (not left.)<BR> E. अव reverse, सव्य left; also<BR>अपसव्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=067-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसाद|अवसादः
अवसाद m. (-दः)<BR>	 1. Lassitude, want of energy or spirit, especially as<BR>proceeding from doubtful or unsuccessful love.<BR>	 2. Exhaustion,<BR>fatigue.<BR>	 3. In law, badness of a cause.<BR>	 4. End, termination.<BR> E. अव,<BR>षद to go, to sink, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=067-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसादक
अवसादक mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>	 1. Exhausting, wearisome.<BR>	 2. Ending, finish-<BR>ing.<BR> E. अव before षद to go, &c. causal form, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=067-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसादन|अवसादनं
अवसादन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Finishing.<BR>	 2. An escharotic.<BR>	 3. Removing proud flesh<BR>by escharotic applications.<BR> E. अव before षद to go, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=067-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसादित
अवसादित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Languid, exhausted, faint.<BR> E. अव, षद to go, क्त<BR>aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=067-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसान|अवसानं
अवसान n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Conclusion, termination, cessation.<BR>	 2. Death.<BR>	 3.<BR>Boundary, limit.<BR>	 4. (In grammar,) Disjunction of letters.<BR> E. अव, षो<BR>to finish, ल्युट् affix; ओ is changed to आ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=067-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसाय|अवसायः
अवसाय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. End, conclusion.<BR>	 2. Termination, completion.<BR>	 3.<BR>Certainty, ascertainment.<BR> E. अव, षो to finish, affix ण, and युक्<BR>inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=067-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसारण
अवसारण n. (-णं) Removing, causing to move.<BR> E. अव before सृ to go,<BR>causal form, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=067-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसित|अवसितं
अवसित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Ended, terminated.<BR>	 2. Finished, com-<BR>pleted.<BR>	 3. Known, understood.<BR>	 4. Stored, (as grain, &c.)<BR> E. अव, षो<BR>to finish, and क्त part. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=067-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसेक|अवसेकः
अवसेक m. (-कः) Sprinkling.<BR> E. अव, विच to sprinkle, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=067-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसेकिम|अवसेकिमः
अवसेकिम m. (-मः) A kind of cake, pulse ground and fried with oil or<BR>butter.<BR> E. अव, सेकृ to sprinkle, इमच् affix; what is sprinkled with<BR>oil, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=067-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसेचन|अवसेचनं
अवसेचन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Sprinkling.<BR>	 2. Bleeding.<BR> E. अव before षिच to sprinkle,<BR>affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=067-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसेय
अवसेय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) To be destroyed, destructible.<BR> E. अव before षो to<BR>destroy, affix यत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=067-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवस्कन्द|अवस्कंदः|अवस्कन्दः
अवस्कन्द m. (-न्दः)<BR>	 1. A camp.<BR>	 2. Assault, attack, storm.<BR>	 3. Bathing.<BR>	 4.<BR>Going down, descending.<BR> E. अव against, &c. स्कन्द to go, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=067-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवस्कन्दन|अवस्कंदनं|अवस्कन्दनं
अवस्कन्दन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Attacking, assaulting, storm.<BR>	 2. Bathing.<BR>	 3.<BR>Descending.<BR> E. अव before स्कन्दन going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=067-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवस्कन्दित|अवस्कंदित
अवस्कन्दित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Attacked.<BR>	 2. Bathed, bathing.<BR>	 3. Gone<BR>down.<BR> E. अव, स्कन्द to go, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=067-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवस्कर|अवस्करः
अवस्कर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A privity, a part to be concealed.<BR>	 2. Ordure, fæces.<BR>3. Dirt.<BR>	 4. Sweepings.<BR> E. अव down, away, &c. क to throw, अप् affix,<BR>स prefixed to क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=067-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवस्करक|अवस्करकः
अवस्करक m. (कः)<BR>	 1. A sweeper.<BR>	 2. A brush, broom, &c.<BR> E. अवस्कर and<BR>वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=067-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवस्तात्
अवस्तात् ind.<BR>	 1. Posterior, latter.<BR>	 2. Finally.<BR> E. अव and स्ताव् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=067-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवस्तार|अवस्तारः
अवस्तार m. (-रः) A screen or wall of cloth surrounding a tent, &c.<BR> E. अव<BR>round, स्तॄ to spread, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=067-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवस्तु
अवस्तु n. (-स्तु) Insubstantiality, the unreality of matter.<BR> E. अ priv. वस्तु<BR>thing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=067-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवस्तुता
अवस्तुता f. (-ता) Insubstantiality, unreality.<BR> E. तल् added to the last;<BR>also with त्व, अवस्तुत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=068-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवस्था
अवस्था f. (-स्था) State, condition, situation, circumstance of age or<BR>position.<BR> E. अव, स्था to stand or stay, अङ् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=068-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवस्थाचतुष्टय|अवस्थाचतुष्टयं
अवस्थाचतुष्टय n. (-यं) The periods of human life, viz. childhood, youth,<BR>manhood, and old age.<BR> E. अवस्था, and चतुष्टय fourfold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=068-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवस्थाद्वय
अवस्थाद्वय n. (-यं) Two states of life, viz. happiness or misery.<BR> E. अवस्था,<BR>and द्वय two.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=068-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवस्थान|अवस्थानं
अवस्थान n. (-नं) Situation, station, abode, place or period of abiding<BR>or staying.<BR> E. अव before स्था to stay, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=068-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवस्थापन|अवस्थापनं
अवस्थापन n. (-नं) Fixing, settling.<BR> E. अव before स्था to stay, causal form,<BR>ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=068-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवस्थापित
अवस्थापित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Fixed. E. See the last, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=068-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवस्थायिन्
अवस्थायिन् mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि) Staying, residing in.<BR> E. अव before स्था to<BR>stay, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=068-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवस्थित|अवस्थितः
अवस्थित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Occupying place or period, abiding, residing<BR>remaining firm or fixed, &c.<BR>	 2. Firm of purpose, steady.<BR>	 3.<BR>Engaged in, prosecuting, following.<BR> E. अव before स्था to stay,<BR>affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=068-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवस्थिति|अवस्थितिः
अवस्थिति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Abiding.<BR>	 2. A residence.<BR>	 3. Following, practising.<BR>E. अव, and स्थिति staying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=068-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवहत
अवहत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Bruised, beaten.<BR>	 2. Threshed, winnowed. E.<BR>अव, and हत struck.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=068-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवहरण|अवहरणं
अवहरण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Redeeming, taking back.<BR>	 2. Fining, muleting.<BR>	 3.<BR>Taking away, stealing, plundering.<BR> E. अव, and हरण taking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=068-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवहस्त|अवहस्तः
अवहस्त m. (-स्तः) The back of the hand.<BR> E. अव reverse, &c. and हस्त the<BR>hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=068-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवहार|अवहारः
अवहार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A shark 2. A water-elephant.<BR>	 3. A thief.<BR>	 4. Truce,<BR>suspension or cessation of gambling, fighting, &c.<BR>	 5. Summoning,<BR>inviting.<BR>	 6. Any approximatable object, fit or able to be brought<BR>near.<BR>	 7. Apostacy, abandoning a sect or cast.<BR>	 8. Re-delivery.<BR> E. अव,<BR>हृ to take or convey, घञ् or ण aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=068-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवहारक|अवहारकः
अवहारक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) One who stops fighting, &c.<BR>	 m. (-कः) A shark,<BR>a marine monster.<BR> E. अवहार, कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=068-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवहार्य्य|अवहार्य|अवहार्य्यः
अवहार्य्य mfn. (-र्य्यः-र्य्या-र्य्यं)<BR>	 1. Recoverable, redeemable.<BR>	 2. Finable, pun-<BR>ishable.<BR> E. अव, and हार्य्य to be taken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=068-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवहालिका
अवहालिका f. (-का) A wall, a bound hedge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=068-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवहित|अवहितं
अवहित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Known, celebrated.<BR>	 2. Done with care.<BR>	 3. Care-<BR>ful.<BR>	 4. Attentive.<BR> E. अव, धा to have or hold, part. affix क्त; ध becomes<BR>ह and इट् is inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=068-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवहित्थ|अवहित्थं
अवहित्थ nf. (-त्थं-त्था) Dissimulation.<BR> E. अ neg. वहिर् outer, स्था to stand; an<BR>irregular form: what does not show outwardly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=068-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवहृत
अवहृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Taken off, back, or away, seized, stolen.<BR>	 2.<BR>Fined.<BR> E. अव off, हृत taken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=068-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवहेल|अवहेलं|अवहेलः
अवहेल nf. (-लं-ला) Disrespect.<BR> E. अव, हेड to despise, घञ् affix; ड becomes<BR>ल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=068-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवहेलन|अवहेलनं
अवहेलन n. (-नं) Disrespect. E. As अवहेल, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=068-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवहेलित|अवहेलितं
अवहेलित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Disrespected.<BR>	 n. (-तं) Disrespect.<BR> E. अवहेल and<BR>इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=068-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवाक्पुष्पी
अवाक्पुष्पी f. (-ष्पी) A plant, (Pimpinella Anisum.)<BR> E. अवाक् downwards, and<BR>पुष्पी having flowers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=068-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवाक्शिरस्
अवाक्शिरस् mfn. (-राः-राः-रः) Having the head downwards.<BR> E. अवाक् down,<BR>and शिरस् the head.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=068-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवाक्ष|अवाक्षः
अवाक्ष mfn. (-क्षः-क्षी-क्षं) Who protects or defends, a guarding, a keeper.<BR>E. अव under. and अक्षि the eye, अ final.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=068-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवाग्र|अवाग्रं
अवाग्र mfn. (-ग्रः-ग्रा-ग्रं) Stooping, bending, bowed.<BR> E. अव reverse, and अग्र<BR>front.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=068-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवाङ्मुख|अवाङ्मुखं|अवाङ्मुखः
अवाङ्मुख mfn. (-खः-खा-खं) Downlooked, headlong. अवाच्, and मुख the<BR>face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=068-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवाच्
अवाच् mfn. (-वाक्) Dumb.<BR> E. अ priv. वाच् speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=068-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवाच्
अवाच् or अवाञ्च् mfn. (-वाङ्-वाची-वाक्)<BR>	 1. Downlooked, headlong.<BR>	 2. South.<BR>ind. (-वाक्)<BR>	 1. South, southern.<BR>	 2. Downwards.<BR>	 f. (-वाची)<BR>	 1. The south<BR>quarter.<BR>	 2. The lower regions.<BR> E. अव down, downwards, अञ्च् to go,<BR>क्विप् affix; the south being considered as below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=068-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवाञ्च्|अवांच्
अवाच् or अवाञ्च् mfn. (-वाङ्-वाची-वाक्)<BR>	 1. Downlooked, headlong.<BR>	 2. South.<BR>ind. (-वाक्)<BR>	 1. South, southern.<BR>	 2. Downwards.<BR>	 f. (-वाची)<BR>	 1. The south<BR>quarter.<BR>	 2. The lower regions.<BR> E. अव down, downwards, अञ्च् to go,<BR>क्विप् affix; the south being considered as below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=068-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवाचीन|अवाचीनं
अवाचीन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>	 1. South, southern.<BR>	 2. Downlooked, headlong.<BR>	 3.<BR>Descended, gone down.<BR> E. अवाच् and ख aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=068-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवाच्य|अवाच्यं|अवाच्यः
अवाच्य mfn. (-च्यः-च्या-च्यं)<BR>	 1. Vile, bad.<BR>	 2. Improper to be uttered.<BR>	 3.<BR>Southern, southerly.<BR> E. अ neg. and वाच्य to be spoken, or अवाच् and<BR>यत् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=068-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवाच्यता
अवाच्यता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Reproach, calumny.<BR>	 2. Impropriety.<BR> E. तल् added to<BR>the preceding; also with त्व, अवाच्यत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=068-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवाच्यदेश|अवाच्यदेशः
अवाच्यदेश m. (-शः) The vulva.<BR> E. अवाच्य not to be named, देश a place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=068-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवाज्ज्ञान
अवाज्ज्ञान n. (-नं) Disrespect.<BR> E. अवाच्, ज्ञान knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=068-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवादिन्
अवादिन् mfn. (-दी-दिनी-दि) One who does not speak, who does not dis-<BR>pute, who does not bring an action, peaceable.<BR> E. अ neg. वादिन् who<BR>speaks, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=068-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवान|अवानं|अवानः
अवान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Dried, dry, (fruit.)<BR> E. अ neg. and वान dry: than<BR>which nothing is drier.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=068-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवान्तर|अवांतर|अवान्तरं
अवान्तर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Included, involved.<BR> E. अव, and अन्तर inner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=068-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवापित
अवापित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Unsown, (as grain,) planted.<BR> E. अ neg. and वापित<BR>sown.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=068-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवाप्त
अवाप्त mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं) Received, got, obtained.<BR> E. अव before आप to ob-<BR>tain, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=068-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवाप्तवत्
अवाप्तवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>	 1. Receiving, obtaining, taking.<BR>	 2. Entertain-<BR>ing, (as a belief.)<BR> E. अवाप to get, क्तवतु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=068-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवाप्ति|अवाप्तिः
अवाप्ति f. (-प्तिः) Obtaining, getting, receiving.<BR> E. अव, and आप to attain,<BR>क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=068-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवाप्य
अवाप्य mfn. (-प्यः-प्या-प्यं) Unattainable, unobtainable. ind. Having ob-<BR>tained.<BR> E. अ neg. वाप्य procurable, or अव before आप to obtain, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=068-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवार|अवारं|अवारः
अवार n. (-रं) The near bank of a river.<BR> E. अव down, ऋ to go, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=068-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवारपार|अवारपारः
अवारपार m. (-रः) The ocean.<BR> E. अवार the near and पार the opposite<BR>bank; embanked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=068-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवारपारीण|अवारपारीणः
अवारपारीण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Crossing a river.<BR> E. अवारपार both banks,<BR>and ख aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=068-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवारिका
अवारिका f. (-का) Coriander seed; also अवरिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=068-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवारित|अवारितं
अवारित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Unimpeded, unobstructed.<BR>	 2. Innumerable.<BR>E. अ neg. and वारित hindered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=068-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवारितव्य
अवारितव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं) Not to be impeded.<BR> E. अ neg. and वारितव्य to<BR>be hindered; also अवारणीय and अवार्य्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=068-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवारीण|अवारीणः
अवारीण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Crossing a river.<BR> E. अवार and ख aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=068-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवार्य्य|अवार्य|अवार्य्यं
अवार्य्य mfn. (-र्य्यः-र्य्या-र्य्यं) Unrestrainable, irresistible.<BR> E. अ neg. वार्य्य to be<BR>hindered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=068-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवावट|अवावटः
अवावट m. (-टः) The son of a woman by any other man than her first<BR>husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=068-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवावन्
अवावन् m. (-वा) A thief.<BR> E. ओण to take away, वनिप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=068-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवासस्
अवासस् mfn. (-साः-साः-सः) Naked.<BR> E. अ priv. वासस् clothes<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=068-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवास्तव|अवास्तवं
अवास्तव mfn. (-वः-वी-वं)<BR>	 1. Unsubstantial, unreal.<BR>	 2. Unfounded, ir-<BR>rational, (as an argument.)<BR> E. अ neg. and वास्तव substance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=068-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवास्तविक
अवास्तविक mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>	 1. Insubstantial, unreal.<BR>	 2. Unfounded, (as<BR>an argument.)<BR> E. अ neg. वास्तविक substantial.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=068-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवि|अविः
अवि m. (-विः)<BR>	 1. The sun.<BR>	 2. A mountain.<BR>	 3. A sheep.<BR>	 4. A master.<BR>	 5.<BR>A blanket.<BR>	 6. A rat.<BR>	 7. A wall or enclosure.<BR>	 8. Air, wind.<BR>	 9. The<BR>shawl goat.<BR>	 f. (-विः) A woman in her courses; also अवी.<BR> E. अव to go,<BR>to preserve, &c. इन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=068-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविक|अविकं|अविकः
अविक n. (-कं) A diamond.<BR> E. अवि the sun, &c. कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=068-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविकच
अविकच mfn. (-चः-चा-चं) Closed, shut.<BR> E. अ neg. विकच open.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=068-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविकचित
अविकचित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Unblown.<BR> E. अ neg. विकचित blown.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=068-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविकट|अविकटः
अविकट m. (-टः) A flock of sheep.<BR> E. अवि a sheep, कटच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=068-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविकथ
अविकथ mfn. (-थः-था-थं) Not boasting, not talking vainly or idly.<BR> E. अ<BR>neg. and विकथा boasting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=068-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविकथन
अविकथन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) One who does not boast.<BR>	 n. (-नं) Not boasting.<BR>E. अ neg. विकथन talking idly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=069-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविकल
अविकल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>	 1. Entire, perfect, unimpaired.<BR>	 2. Regular,<BR>orderly, consistent.<BR> E. अ neg. and विकल defective.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=069-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविकल्प|अविकल्पः
अविकल्प m. (-ल्पः) Positive act or precept, absence of doubt or alter-<BR>native.<BR> E. अ neg. विकल्प alternative.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=069-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविकार|अविकारः
अविकार mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Immutable, permanent.<BR> E. अ neg. विकार change.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=069-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविकार्य्य|अविकार्य
अविकार्य्य mfn. (-र्य्यः-र्य्या-र्य्यं) Immutable, unchangeable.<BR> E. अ neg. विकार्य्य<BR>liable to change of form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=069-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविकृत
अविकृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Unchanged, permanent.<BR> E. अ neg. विकृत changed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=069-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविक्रम|अविक्रमः
अविक्रम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं) Powerless, feeble.<BR>	 m. (-मः) Cowardice.<BR> E. अ neg.<BR>विक्रम prowess.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=069-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविक्रय
अविक्रय m. (-यः) Want of sale.<BR> E. अ neg. विक्रय sale.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=069-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविक्रान्त|अविक्रांत
अविक्रान्त mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं)<BR>	 1. Unsurpassed.<BR>	 2. Feeble, powerless.<BR> E. अ neg.<BR>वि before क्रम to go, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=069-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविक्रीत
अविक्रीत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Unsold.<BR> E. अ neg. विक्रीत sold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=069-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविक्रेय
अविक्रेय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Unsaleable, not to be sold.<BR> E. अ neg. विक्रेय to<BR>be sold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=069-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविक्लम|अविक्लमः
अविक्लम m. (-मः) Vigour, freshness, absence of fatigue.<BR> E. अ neg. विक्लम<BR>fatigue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=069-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविक्लव
अविक्लव mfn. (-वः-वा-वं) Calm, composed, firm.<BR> E. अ neg. विक्लव confounded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=069-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविक्लान्त
अविक्लान्त mfn. (-न्तः-ता-न्तं) Unwearied.<BR> E. अ neg. विक्लान्त wearied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=069-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविक्षत
अविक्षत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Entire, undiminished.<BR>	 2. Unhurt.<BR> E. अ neg.<BR>विक्षत wounded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=069-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविक्षिप्त
अविक्षिप्त mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं)<BR>	 1. Attentive, composed.<BR>	 2. Retained.<BR> E. अ neg.<BR>विक्षिप्त tossed, agitated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=069-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविक्षोभ
अविक्षोभ m. (-भः) Quiet, quiescence.<BR> E. अ neg. विक्षोभ agitation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=069-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविक्षोभित
अविक्षोभित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Tranquil, undisturbed.<BR> E. अ neg. विक्षोभित<BR>agitated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=069-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविगत
अविगत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Retained, present, unseparated.<BR> E. अ neg. विगत<BR>gone away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=069-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविगम|अविगमः
अविगम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं) Unseparated, unremoved.<BR>	 m. (-मः) Presence,<BR>inherence, association, non-separation.<BR> E. अ neg. विगम separation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=069-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविगर्हित
अविगर्हित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Unreproached.<BR> E. अ neg. विगर्हित reproached.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=069-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविगीत|अविगीतं
अविगीत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Unreproached.<BR> E. अ neg. विगीत censure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=069-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविगुण
अविगुण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>	 1. Compatible, consistent with, not contrary<BR>to.<BR>	 2. Worthy, good.<BR> E. अ neg. वि without, गुण property.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=069-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविग्न|अविग्नः
अविग्न m. (-ग्नः) A fruit tree, commonly Caronda, (Carissa Carondas.)<BR>E. अ neg. विज to fear, part. past, irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=069-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविग्रह|अविग्रहः
अविग्रह mfn. (-हः-हा-हं) Bodiless, incorporeal.<BR> E. अ neg. विग्रह body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=069-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविघ्न
अविघ्न mfn. (-घ्नः-घ्ना-घ्नं) Unimpeded, uninterrupted.<BR> E. अ neg. विघ्न<BR>obstacle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=069-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविचक्षण
अविचक्षण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Unlearned, ignorant.<BR> E. अ neg. विचक्षण learned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=069-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविचार|अविचारः
अविचार mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>	 1. Undiscriminating, ill-judging, unwise.<BR>	 2.<BR>Prompt, unhesitating.<BR>	 m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Want of judgment or discrimina-<BR>tion, error, folly.<BR>	 2. Promptitude.<BR> E. अ neg. विचार discussion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=069-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविचारित|अविचारितः
अविचारित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Ill-judged or investigated, unconsidered.<BR>2. Determined, certain, clear, not requiring deliberation.<BR> E. अ neg.<BR>विचारित discussed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=069-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविचालित
अविचालित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Victorious, triumphant.<BR>	 2. Unmoved.<BR> E. अ<BR>neg. विचालित shaken, resisted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=069-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविच्युत
अविच्युत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Undeviated from, observed, followed.<BR>	 2.<BR>Eternal, permanent.<BR> E. अ neg. विच्युत fallen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=069-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविच्छिन्न|अविच्छिन्नं|अविछिन्न
अविच्छिन्न mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं) Unseparated, undivided.<BR> E. अ neg. विच्छिन्न cut<BR>off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=069-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविच्छेद|अविच्छेदः|अविछेद
अविच्छेद mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>	 1. Entire, whole, undivided.<BR>	 2. Uninterrupted.<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>	 1. Entireness.<BR>	 2. Connexion, continuity.<BR> E. अ neg. विच्छेद<BR>separation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=069-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविजातीय
अविजातीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Of the same species.<BR> E. अ neg. विजातीय of a<BR>different kind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=069-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविज्ञ|अविज्ञः
अविज्ञ mfn. (-ज्ञः-ज्ञा-ज्ञं)<BR>	 1. Clumsy, stupid.<BR>	 2. Ignorant, untaught.<BR> E. अ<BR>neg. विज्ञ wise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=069-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविज्ञता
अविज्ञता f. (-ता) Ignorance, folly.<BR> E. अविज्ञ and तल् affix; also अविज्ञत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=069-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविज्ञात
अविज्ञात mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Unknown.<BR>	 2. Undistinguished.<BR> E. अ neg.<BR>विज्ञात known.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=069-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविज्ञेय|अविज्ञेयं|अविज्ञेयः
अविज्ञेय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Undiscernible, not to be recognized or known.<BR>E. अ neg. विज्ञेय to be known.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=069-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविडीन|अविडीनं
अविडीन n. (-नं) A direct flight.<BR> E. अ neg. विडीन flying deviously.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=069-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवित|अवितं
अवित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Preserved, protected.<BR> E. अव to preserve, क्त affix<BR>of part. past.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=069-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवितथ|अवितथं
अवितथ mfn. (-थः-था-थं) True.<BR>	 n. (-थं) Truth.<BR> E. अ neg. and वितथ untrue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=069-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवित्त
अवित्त mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं)<BR>	 1. Unknown.<BR>	 2. Poor.<BR> E. अ neg. वित्त known, or<BR>wealth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=069-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवित्यज|अवित्यजं|अवित्यजः
अवित्यज mfn. (-जः-जा-जं) Quicksilver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=069-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविथ्य
अविथ्य mfn. (-थ्यः-थ्या-थ्यं) Fit for or suited to a sheep.<BR> E. अवि and थ्यन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=069-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविदग्ध
अविदग्ध mfn. (-ग्धः-ग्धा-ग्धं)<BR>	 1. Unlearned.<BR>	 2. Stupid.<BR> E. अ neg. विदग्ध clever.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=069-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविदाहिन्
अविदाहिन् mfn. (-ही-हिनी-हि) Imperfectly digested, producing heart-<BR>burn.<BR> E. अ neg. वि free from, दाहिन् what burns.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=069-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविदित|अविदितः
अविदित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Unknown.<BR> E. अ neg. विदित known.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=069-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविदूर
अविदूर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Near, contiguous.<BR> E. अ neg. विदूर distant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=069-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविदूरतस्
अविदूरतस् ind. Near, not far off.<BR> E. अविदूर and तसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=069-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविदूस|अविदूसं
अविदूस n. (-सं) The milk of a ewe.<BR> E. अवि and दूस aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=069-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविद्धकर्णा
अविद्धकर्णा f. (-र्णा-र्णी) A plant, (Cissampelos hexandra.)<BR> E. अ neg. विद्ध<BR>broken, divided, and कर्ण the ear; the leaf being compared to the<BR>ear; also अविद्धकर्णी and विद्धकर्णी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=069-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविद्य|अविद्यः
अविद्य mfn. (-द्यः-द्या-द्यं)<BR>	 1. Foolish, unwise.<BR>	 2. Not relating to knowlege.<BR>f. (-द्या)<BR>	 1. Ignorance.<BR>	 2. Spiritual ignorance.<BR>	 3. Illusion.<BR>	 4. Per-<BR>sonified illusion or Māyā.<BR> E. अ priv. and विद्या knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=069-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविद्यमान|अविद्यमानः
अविद्यमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>	 1. Nonexistent.<BR>	 2. Not present, absent.<BR> E. अ<BR>neg. and विद्यमान being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=069-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविद्वस्
अविद्वस् mfn. (-द्वान्-दुषी-द्वः) Unwise, unlearned.<BR> E. अ neg. विद्वस् learned,<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=069-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविधान
अविधान n. (-नं) Irregularity, deviation from or absence of fixed rule. E.<BR>अ neg. and विधान rule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=069-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविधानतस्
अविधानतस् ind. Irregularly.<BR> E. अविधान and तसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=069-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविधि|अविधिः
अविधि mfn. (-धिः-धिः-धि) Irregular, void of or contrary to rule.<BR>	 f. (-धिः)<BR>Irregularity.<BR> E. अ neg. and विधि rule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=069-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविन|अविनः
अविन m. (-नः) A sacrificer, one who makes a sacrifice or causes it to<BR>be made.<BR> E. अव to preserve, इतच् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=069-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविनय|अविनयः
अविनय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Indecorous, ill-behaved.<BR>	 m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. Indecorum,<BR>impropriety, fault.<BR>	 2. Incivility, disrespect.<BR>	 3. Offence, crime. E.<BR>अ neg. and विनय modest behaviour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=069-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविनश्वर|अविनश्वरः
अविनश्वर mfn. (-रः-री-रं) Indestructible: so अविनाश्य.<BR> E. अ neg. विनश्वर<BR>destructible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=069-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविनाभाव|अविनाभावः
अविनाभाव m. (-वः) Inherent and essential character.<BR> E. अ, and विना<BR>without, भाव property.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=069-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविनिगम|अविनिगमः
अविनिगम m. (-मः) An illogical conclusion.<BR> E. अ neg. विनिगम accurate<BR>deduction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=069-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविनिवर्त्तिन्|अविनिवर्तिन्
अविनिवर्त्तिन् mfn. (-र्त्ती-र्त्तिनी-र्त्ति) Holding on, advancing, one who does<BR>not turn back.<BR> E. अ neg. विनिवर्त्तिन् who retreats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=069-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविनिर्मोक
अविनिर्मोक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Without an exception.<BR> E. अ neg. विनिर्मोक<BR>exception.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=069-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविनीत|अविनीतः
अविनीत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Misbehaving, acting ill or improperly, wicked,<BR>vile.<BR>	 f. (-ता) An unchaste or disloyal woman.<BR> E. अ neg. विनीत<BR>virtuous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=069-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविपक्ष
अविपक्ष mfn. (-क्षः-क्षा-क्षं) Unopposed, having no adversary.<BR> E. अ neg. विपक्ष<BR>an adversary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=069-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविपट|अविपटः
अविपट m. (-टः) Woolen cloth.<BR> E. अवि a sheep, and पटच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=069-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविपद्
अविपद् f. (-पत्) Prosperity, ease.<BR> E. अ neg. विपद् misfortune.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=069-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविपन्न
अविपन्न mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>	 1. Uninjured, unhurt.<BR>	 2. Not soiled or contami-<BR>nated, pure, clean.<BR> E. अ neg. विपन्न destroyed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=069-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविपश्चिद्
अविपश्चिद् mfn. (-श्चित्) Unwise, ignorant.<BR> E. अ neg. विपश्चिद् learned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=070-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविपाक|अविपाकः
अविपाक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. Immaturity.<BR>	 2. Not suffering the consequence of<BR>actions in a former life.<BR>	 3. Indigestion.<BR> E. अ neg. विपाक ripening.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=070-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविपुल
अविपुल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Small, insignificant, slender.<BR> E. अ neg. विपुल large.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=070-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविप्रकृष्ट
अविप्रकृष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं) Near, not remote.<BR> E. अ neg. विप्रकृष्ट remote.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=070-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविप्लुत
अविप्लुत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Undeviating, following or observing steadily.<BR>2. Observed, unviolated.<BR> E. अ neg. विप्लुत transgressed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=070-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविफल
अविफल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Fruitful, productive.<BR> E. अ neg. विफल unfruitful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=070-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविफुल्ल
अविफुल्ल mfn. (-ल्लः-ल्ला-ल्लं) Unblown.<BR> E. अ neg. विफुल्ल blown.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=070-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविभक्त|अविभक्तः
अविभक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>	 1. Undivided, unpartitioned.<BR>	 2. Joint, unsepa-<BR>rated, (as coparceners.)<BR> E. अ neg. विभक्त divided.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=070-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविभाग|अविभागः
अविभाग mfn. (-गः-गा-गं) Unportioned, unpartitioned.<BR>	 m. (-गः) Undivided<BR>inheritance.<BR> E. अ neg. विभाग division.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=070-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविभागिन्
अविभागिन् mfn. (-गी-गिनी-गि)<BR>	 1. One who does not share.<BR>	 2. Not sharing,<BR>not dividing.<BR> E. अ neg. विभागिन् who divides.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=070-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविभाज्य|अविभाज्यं
अविभाज्य mfn. (-ज्यः-ज्या-ज्यं) Not to be divided, not to be partitioned.<BR> E. अ<BR>neg. विभाज्य partible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=070-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविभाज्यत्व
अविभाज्यत्व n. (-त्वं) Indivisibility, unfitness for partition.<BR> E. अविभाज्य and<BR>त्व affix; also with तल्, अविभाज्यता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=070-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविभावन|अविभावनं
अविभावन nf. (-नं-ना) Disappearance, imperceptibility.<BR> E. अ neg. विभावन<BR>perception.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=070-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविभावनीय
अविभावनीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Imperceptible, undistinguishable.<BR> E. अ neg.<BR>विभावनीय perceptible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=070-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविमरीस|अविमरीसं
अविमरीस n. (-सं) The milk of a ewe.<BR> E. अवि and मरीसच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=070-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविमल
अविमल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Foul, turbid.<BR> E. अ neg. विमल clear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=070-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविमुक्त|अविमुक्तं|अविमुक्तः
अविमुक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं) Unloosed, not quitted.<BR>	 m. (-क्तः) A name of<BR>Benares.<BR> E. अ neg. and विमुक्त loosed: the last is never to be lost<BR>view of by those seeking salvation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=070-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविमुक्तेश्वर|अविमुक्तेश्वरः
अविमुक्तेश्वर m. (-रः) A celebrated Siva Linga, at Benares.<BR> E. अविमुक्त, and<BR>ईश्वर lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=070-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवियुक्त
अवियुक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>	 1. Undivided, conjoined.<BR>	 2. Not separated or<BR>absent.<BR> E. अ neg. वियुक्त disjoined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=070-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवियोग|अवियोगः
अवियोग m. (-गः)<BR>	 1. Conjunction, association.<BR>	 2. Presence, not being<BR>parted or absent.<BR> E. अ neg. वियोग disunion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=070-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविरक्त
अविरक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं) Interested in, attached to.<BR> E. अ neg. विरक्त<BR>unattached.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=070-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविरत|अविरतं
अविरत adj.<BR>	 mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Eternal, continual, uninterrupted.<BR>	 2.<BR>Abandoned, or adv.<BR>	 n. (-तं) Eternal, continual.<BR> E. अ neg. विरत stop-<BR>ping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=070-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविरल|अविरलं
अविरल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>	 1. Coarse, gross, substantial.<BR>	 2. Close, con-<BR>tiguous.<BR>	 3. Uninterrupted.<BR> E. अ neg. and विरल fine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=070-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविराम|अविरामः
अविराम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं) Continuous, uninterrupted.<BR>	 m. (-मः) Continu-<BR>ance, uninterrupted succession.<BR>	 n. adv. (-मं) Uninterruptedly.<BR> E. अ<BR>neg. विराम rest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=070-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविरुद्ध
अविरुद्ध mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>	 1. Unimpeded, unobstructed.<BR>	 2. Allowed, per-<BR>mitted, proper.<BR>	 3. Compatible, consistent with.<BR> E. अ neg. विरुद्ध hin-<BR>dered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=070-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविरेचन|अविरेचनं
अविरेचन n. (-नं) Constipating, stopping dejection.<BR> E. अ neg. विरेचन purg-<BR>ing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=070-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविरेच्य
अविरेच्य mfn. (-च्यः-च्या-च्यं) Improper to be purged.<BR> E. अ neg. विरेच्य to be<BR>purged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=070-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविरोध|अविरोधः
अविरोध m. (-धः)<BR>	 1. Absence of impediment.<BR>	 2. Assent, concurrence,<BR>non-opposition.<BR>	 3. Consistency, compatibility.<BR> E. अ neg. विरोध<BR>hindrance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=070-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविरोधित
अविरोधित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Unimpeded, unobstructed.<BR> E. अ neg. विरोधित<BR>hindered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=070-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविलङ्घन|अविलंघनं
अविलङ्घन n. (-नं) Not exceeding, not trespassing.<BR> E. अ neg. विलङ्घन<BR>trespassing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=070-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविलङ्घनीय|अविलंघनीय
अविलङ्घनीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Prescribed, fixed, not to be transgressed or<BR>exceeded.<BR> E. अ neg. विलङ्घनीय to be past over or beyond.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=070-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविलम्ब|अविलंब|अविलम्बः
अविलम्ब mfn. (-म्बः-म्बा-म्बं) Prompt, quick, without delay.<BR> E. अ neg. विलम्ब<BR>delay.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=070-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविलम्बन|अविलम्बनं
अविलम्बन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Quick, expeditious: also अविलम्बित.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=070-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविलम्बित|अविलंबित|अविलम्बितं|अविलम्बितः
अविलम्बित mfn. adj. (-तः-ता-तं) Quick, expeditious.<BR>	 n. adv. (-तं) Quickly,<BR>expeditiously.<BR> E. अ neg. and विलिम्बित slow, tedious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=070-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविलम्बितक्रम
अविलम्बितक्रम m. (-मः) Going quickly, swift pace.<BR> E. अविलम्बित, and क्रम<BR>motion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=070-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविला
अविला f. (-ला) A sheep, a ewe.<BR> E. अ neg. विल to break, अच् and टाप्<BR>affixes; not able to wound, &c. having no horns.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=070-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविलास|अविलासः
अविलास mfn. (-सः-सा-सं) Faithful, constant.<BR> E. अ neg. विलास sport,<BR>caprice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=070-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविवक्षित
अविवक्षित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Unasserted, undeclared.<BR> E. अ neg. विवक्षित said.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=070-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविवाद|अविवादः
अविवाद m. (-दः) Concurrence, consent, non-disagreement.<BR> E. अ neg.<BR>विवाद dispute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=070-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविवादिन्
अविवादिन् mfn. (-दी-दिनी-दि) Quiet, peaceable.<BR> E. अ neg. विवादिन् conten-<BR>tious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=070-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविवाहित|अविवाहितः
अविवाहित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Unmarried.<BR> E. अ neg. and विवाहित married.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=070-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविवाहिन्
अविवाहिन् mfn. (-ही-हिनी-हि)<BR>	 1. Interdicted as to marriage.<BR>	 2. Not<BR>relating to marriage.<BR>	 3. Single, not marrying.<BR> E. अ neg. विवाहिन्<BR>marrying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=070-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविविक्त
अविविक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>	 1. Uninvestigated, undiscriminated.<BR>	 2.<BR>Indiscriminate, confounded.<BR>	 3. Common, public.<BR> E. अ neg. विविक्त<BR>discriminated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=070-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविवेक|अविवेकः
अविवेक m. (-कः) Ignorance, absence of discrimination or judgment. E.<BR>अ neg. and विवेक discrimination.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=070-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविवेकता
अविवेकता f. (-ता) Inconsiderateness, imprudence, want of judgment. E.<BR>अविवेक and तल् added: also अविवेकत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=070-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविवेकिन्
अविवेकिन् mfn. (-की-किनी-कि) Ignorant, undiscriminating, defective in<BR>judgment, superficial, short-sighted.<BR> E. अविवेक as above, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=070-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविवेचक|अविवेचकः
अविवेचक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Ignorant, undiscriminating.<BR> E. अ neg. and<BR>विवेचक who judges.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=070-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविवेचना
अविवेचना f. (-ना) Want of judgment.<BR> E. अ neg. विवेचना discriminating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=070-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविशङ्का
अविशङ्का f. (-ङ्का) Unapprehensiveness, confidence, certainty.<BR> E. अ neg.<BR>विशङ्का fear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=070-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविशङ्कित|अविशंकित
अविशङ्कित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Confiding, trusting, unapprehensive.<BR> E. अ<BR>neg. विशङ्कित alarmed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=070-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविशुद्ध
अविशुद्ध mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>	 1. Not pure, clear, free from fault or defect.<BR>	 2.<BR>Not valid, perfect, or unimpeached.<BR> E. अ neg. विशुद्ध pure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=070-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविशेष|अविशेषः
अविशेष mfn. (-षः-षा-षं) Uniform, alike, without any difference.<BR>	 n. (-षं)<BR>Equality, uniformity.<BR> E. अ neg. विशेष variation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=070-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविशेषज्ञ
अविशेषज्ञ mfn. (-ज्ञः-ज्ञा-ज्ञं) Indiscriminating, not perceiving the difference<BR>in things.<BR> E. अ neg. विशेष variation, and ज्ञ who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=070-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविश्रान्त|अविश्रांत|अविश्रान्तः
अविश्रान्त mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं) Unwearied.<BR> E. अ neg. विश्रान्त tired.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=070-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविश्वस्त|अविश्वस्तः
अविश्वस्त mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं) Suspected, doubted, not trusted.<BR> E. अ neg. and<BR>विश्वस्त trusted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=070-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविश्वास|अविश्वासः
अविश्वास mfn. (-सः-सा-सं) Mistrusted.<BR>	 m. (-सः) Suspicion, mistrust.<BR> E. अ<BR>neg. विश्वास trust.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=070-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविश्वासा
अविश्वासा f. (-सा) A cow calving after long intervals.<BR> E. अ neg. विश्वास<BR>trust.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=070-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविश्वासिन्
अविश्वासिन् mfn. (-सि-सिनी-सि) Mistrustful, unbelieving.<BR> E. अ neg.<BR>विश्वासिन् who trusts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=070-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविष|अविषः
अविष mfn. (-षः-षा-षं) Anti-venomous, antidote, not poisonous.<BR> E. अ<BR>neg. and विष poison.<BR>	 m. (-षः) The ocean, sky.<BR>	 f. (-षी)<BR>	 1. A river.<BR>	 2.<BR>The earth.<BR>	 3. Heaven.<BR> E. अव to go, &c. टिषच् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=070-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविषक्त
अविषक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं) Unchecked, unopposed, unimpeded.<BR> E. अ neg.<BR>विषक्त restrained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=070-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविषय|अविषयः
अविषय mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>	 1. Unperceived, invisible.<BR>	 2. Insensible, disregard-<BR>ing objects of sense.<BR>	 m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. Disappearance, absence.<BR>	 2. Disre-<BR>gard of objects of sense.<BR> E. अ neg. विषय an object of sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=070-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविस्
अविस् m. (-विः) An extender or enlarger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=070-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविसर्गिन्
अविसर्गिन् mfn. (-र्गी-र्गिणी-र्गि) Adhering to, retaining, not quitting.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-र्गी) A continued fever.<BR> E. अ neg. विसर्गिन् quitting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविसोढ|अविसोढं
अविसोढ n. (-ढं) Ewe's milk.<BR> E. अवि and सोढ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविस्तृत
अविस्तृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Compact, compressed, close.<BR> E. अ neg. विस्तृत<BR>spread.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविस्पष्ट|अविस्पष्टं
अविस्पष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं) Obscure, not clear or plain.<BR>	 n. (-ष्टं) Indistinct<BR>speech.<BR> E. अ neg. विस्पष्ट plain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविस्मरण
अविस्मरण n. (-णं) Remembering, not forgetting.<BR> E. अ neg. विस्मरण forget-<BR>ting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविस्मृति
अविस्मृति f. (-तिः) Remembering, recollection.<BR> E. अ neg. विस्मृति forgetful-<BR>ness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविहित
अविहित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Undone, uneffected.<BR>	 2. Unprescribed, not<BR>directed or ruled.<BR> E. अ neg. विहित established.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविह्वल
अविह्वल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Calm, composed, unagitated.<BR> E. अ neg. विह्वल<BR>agitated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवी
अवी f. (-वी) A woman in her courses: see अवि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवीक्षण
अवीक्षण n. (-णं) Not regarding, not looking at.<BR> E. अ neg. वीक्षण seeing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवीक्षित
अवीक्षित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Unseen, unbeheld.<BR> E. अ neg. वीक्षित seen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवीचि|अवीचिः
अवीचि m. (-चिः) A hell.<BR>	 mfn. (-चिः-चिः-चि) Waveless.<BR> E. अ neg. वीचि a<BR>wave.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवीचिमय|अवीचिमयः
अवीचिमय m. (-यः) A hell, the place of punishment for liars.<BR> E. अवीचि<BR>without waves, मयट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवीज|अवीजः
अवीज mfn. (-जः-जा-जं) Seedless.<BR>	 n. (-जं)<BR>	 1. Bad seed.<BR>	 2. Absence of<BR>seed.<BR> E. अ neg. वीज seed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवीजक
अवीजक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Seedless.<BR> E. अवीज and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवीर|अवीरः
अवीर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Weak, impotent, helpless.<BR>	 f. (-रा) A woman who<BR>has neither husband nor son.<BR> E. अ neg. वीर strong.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवृत
अवृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Unselected.<BR>	 2. Uncovered.<BR>	 3. Unprotected.<BR> E. अ<BR>neg. वृत chosen, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवृत्ति|अवृत्तिः
अवृत्ति f. (-त्तिः) Inadequate support, absence of subsistence or allowance.<BR>E. अ neg. वृत्ति maintenance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवृथा
अवृथा ind. Successfully, profitably.<BR> E. अ not, वृथा vainly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवृथार्थ
अवृथार्थ mfn. (-र्थः-र्था-र्थं) Succeeding, gaining one's object.<BR> E. अवृथा not in<BR>vain, अर्थ object.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवृद्धिक
अवृद्धिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>	 1. Not bearing interest.<BR>	 2. Not augmentative.<BR>E. अ neg. वृद्धि increase, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवेक्षण|अवेक्षणं
अवेक्षण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Seeing.<BR>	 2. Attention, observation.<BR> E. अव, and ईक्षण<BR>seeing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवेक्षमाण
अवेक्षमाण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Inspecting, examining.<BR> E. अव, ईक्ष to see, शानच्<BR>aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवेक्षा
अवेक्षा f. (-क्षा)<BR>	 1. Attention, observation.<BR>	 2. Seeing, looking at.<BR>	 3. Agree-<BR>ment, engagement.<BR> E. अव upon or to, ईक्ष to see, अ affix, and टाप्<BR>feminine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवेक्षित|अवेक्षितं
अवेक्षित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Seen, regarded.<BR> E. अव before ईक्ष to see and क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवेदयान
अवेदयान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Not enquiring or ascertaining.<BR> E. अ neg. विद् to<BR>know, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवेदविद्
अवेदविद् m. (-विद्) A Brahman who has not studied the Vedas.<BR> E. अ neg.<BR>वेद and विद् who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवेदविहित
अवेदविहित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Unscriptural, not enjoined in the Vedas. E.<BR>अ neg. वेद and विहित declared.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवेद्य|अवेद्यः
अवेद्य mfn. (-द्यः-द्या-द्यं)<BR>	 1. Unascertainable, secret, not to be known.<BR>	 2.<BR>Not to be pained or hurt.<BR>	 m. (-द्यः) A calf.<BR> E. अ neg. वेद्य to be hurt<BR>or known.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवेल|अवेलः
अवेल m. (-लः) Denial or concealment of knowledge.<BR>	 f. (-ला) Chewed betel.<BR>E. अव and इला speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवैध|अवैधं
अवैध mfn. (-धः-धी-धं) Irregular, heterodox, contrary or not conformable<BR>to rule.<BR> E. अ neg. विधि rule, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवोद|अवोदं|अवोदः
अवोद mfn. (-दः-दा-दं) Wet, moist.<BR> E. अव ill, उन्द to moisten, and क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्द
अव्द m. (-व्दः)<BR>	 1. A cloud.<BR>	 2. A year.<BR> E. अव to preserve, दन् Unādi affix,<BR>see अब्द.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यक्त|अव्यक्तं|अव्यक्तः
अव्यक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>	 1. Indistinct, unapparent, invisible, impercepti-<BR>ble.<BR>	 2. (In algebra,) Unknown as quantity or number.<BR>	 m. (-क्तः)<BR>	 1.<BR>VIṢṆU.<BR>	 2. ŚIVA.<BR>	 3. KANDARPA or CUPID.<BR>	 4. A fool.<BR>	 n. (-क्तं)<BR>	 1. The<BR>Supreme Being or universal spirit.<BR>	 2. Any invisible principle<BR>according to the Sānkhya philosophy.<BR>	 3. The soul.<BR>	 4. Nature,<BR>temperament.<BR> E. अ neg. व्यक्त evident, distinct.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=071-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यक्तक्रिया
अव्यक्तक्रिया f. (-या)<BR>	 1. Algebraic calculation.<BR>	 2. Any act of an indistinct<BR>character or aim.<BR> E. अव्यक्त, and क्रिया act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=071-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यक्तराग|अव्यक्तरागः
अव्यक्तराग m. (-गः) Dark-red, the colour of the dawn.<BR> E. अव्यक्त indistinct,<BR>and राग colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=071-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यक्तराशि|अव्यक्तराशिः
अव्यक्तराशि f. (-शिः) An unknown number or indistinct quantity, (in<BR>algebra.)<BR> E. अव्यक्त and राशि quantity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=071-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यक्तसाम्य
अव्यक्तसाम्य n. (-म्यं) Equation of unknown quantities.<BR> E. अव्यक्त, and साम्य<BR>equality.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=071-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यग्र
अव्यग्र mfn. (-ग्रः-ग्रा-ग्रं)<BR>	 1. Steady, cool, deliberate.<BR>	 2. Indifferent, undis-<BR>turbed.<BR> E. अ neg. व्यग्र hurried.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=071-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यङ्ग|अव्यंग|अव्यङ्गः
अव्यङ्ग mfn. (-ङ्गः-ङ्गा-ङ्गं)<BR>	 1. Plain, not figurative.<BR>	 2. Perfect, not<BR>mutilated.<BR>	 f. (-ङ्गा) Cowach, (Carpopogon pruriens, Rox.)<BR> E. अ neg.<BR>वि priv. and अङ्ग the body, or व्यङ्ग figure of speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=071-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यङ्गाङ्ग
अव्यङ्गाङ्ग mfn. (-ङ्गः-ङ्गी-ङ्गं) Well made, symmetrical, perfect, entire. E.<BR>अव्यङ्ग not defective, अङ्ग a limb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=071-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यञ्जन|अव्यंजन|अव्यञ्जनः
अव्यञ्जन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>	 1. Indistinct.<BR>	 2. Plain, not figurative.<BR>	 m. (-नः)<BR>An animal without horns, though of an age to have them.<BR> E. अ<BR>neg. व्यञ्जन a mark or figure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=071-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यण्डा|अव्यंडा
अव्यण्डा f. (-ण्डा) A plant, (Carpopogon pruriens.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=071-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यतिकीर्ण|अव्यतिकीर्ण्ण
अव्यतिकीर्ण mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-र्णं) Distinct, specific, separate, unmixed.<BR> E. अ<BR>neg. व्यतिकीर्ण confounded, mixed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=071-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यथ|अव्यथः
अव्यथ mfn. (-थः-था-थं)<BR>	 1. Free from pain.<BR>	 2. Merciful, not inflicting pain.<BR>m. (-थः) A snake.<BR>	 f. (-था)<BR>	 1. Yellow myrobalan.<BR>	 2. Another plant,<BR>(Hibiscus mutabilis.) See पद्मचारिणी.<BR> E. अ neg. व्यथा pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=071-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यथि|अव्यथिः
अव्यथि m. (-थिः) A horse, (in the dialect of the Vedas.)<BR> E. अ neg. व्यथ to<BR>pain, and इन् affix; who does not tire in war, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=071-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यथिधी
अव्यथिधी m. (-धीः)<BR>	 1. The earth.<BR>	 2. Night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=071-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यथिन्
अव्यथिन् mfn. (-थी-थिनी-थि)<BR>	 1. Free from pain.<BR>	 2. Not inflicting pain. E.<BR>अ neg. व्यथा pain, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=071-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यथिष|अव्यथिषः
अव्यथिष m. (-षः)<BR>	 1. The ocean.<BR>	 2. The sun.<BR>	 f. (-षी)<BR>	 1. The earth.<BR>	 2.<BR>Midnight.<BR> E. अ neg. व्यथ to suffer pain, and टिषच् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=071-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यथ्य|अव्यथ्यः
अव्यथ्य mfn. (-थ्यः-थ्या-थ्यं)<BR>	 1. Free from pain.<BR>	 2. Not paining, not giving<BR>pain.<BR> E. अ neg. व्यथ to feel pain, and क्यप् affix irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=071-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यभिचार|अव्यभिचारः
अव्यभिचार m. (-रः) Steadiness, consistency, constancy.<BR> E. अ neg. व्यभिचार<BR>irregularity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=071-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यभिचारिन्
अव्यभिचारिन् mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>	 1. Constant.<BR>	 2. Virtuous, moral.<BR>	 3.<BR>Steady, permanent, faithful.<BR> E. अ neg. व्यभिचारिन् variable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=071-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यय|अव्ययं|अव्ययः
अव्यय mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>	 1. Economical, parsimonious.<BR>	 2. Unexpended,<BR>unwasted.<BR>	 3. Imperishable, immutable, eternal.<BR>	 m. (-यः) A name<BR>of VIṢṆU.<BR>	 mn. (-यः-यं) An indeclinable word, a particle.<BR> E. अ neg.<BR>and व्यय expenditure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=071-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्ययात्मन्
अव्ययात्मन् mfn. (-त्मा-त्मा-त्म) Eternal, imperishable.<BR>	 m. (-त्मा) Soul, spirit.<BR>E. अव्यय undecayed, आत्मन् self.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=071-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्ययीभाव|अव्ययीभावः
अव्ययीभाव m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. Imperishableness.<BR>	 2. An indeclinable compound.<BR>E. अव्यय and भाव disposition, with च्वि inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=071-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यर्थ|अव्यर्थः
अव्यर्थ mfn. (-र्थः-र्था-र्थं)<BR>	 1. Profitable, fruitful.<BR>	 2. Effectual, efficacious.<BR>E. अ neg. व्यर्थ useless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=071-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यलीक
अव्यलीक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) True, veracious.<BR> E. अ neg. व्यलीक false.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=071-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यवधान
अव्यवधान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>	 1. Close, contiguous.<BR>	 2. Careless.<BR> E. अ neg.<BR>व्यवधान any thing interposed, or carefulness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=071-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यवधानता
अव्यवधानता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Contiguity.<BR>	 2. Carelessness.<BR> E. तल् added to with<BR>the last; also with त्व, अव्यवधानत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=071-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यवसाय|अव्यवसायः
अव्यवसाय m. (-यः) Negligence, inactivity.<BR> E. अ neg. व्यवसाय employ-<BR>ment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=071-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यवसायवत्|अव्यवसायवन्त्
अव्यवसायवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Negligent, remiss in practice.<BR> E. अ neg.<BR>व्यवसाय practice, profession, मतुप् poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यवसायिन्
अव्यवसायिन् mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि) Negligent, inactive, remiss.<BR> E. अ neg.<BR>व्यवसाय business, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यवस्था
अव्यवस्था f. (-स्था)<BR>	 1. Irregularity, deviation from established rule.<BR>	 3.<BR>Incorrect legal opinion.<BR> E. अ neg. व्यवस्था law.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यवस्थित|अव्यवस्थितः
अव्यवस्थित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Not conformable to law or practice.<BR>	 2.<BR>Unacquainted with the law or custom.<BR>	 3. Ill regulated.<BR>	 4.<BR>Displaced, disordered.<BR> E. अ neg. and व्यवस्थित ordained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यवहार्य्य|अव्यवहार्य|अव्यवहार्य्यं
अव्यवहार्य्य mfn. (-र्य्यः-र्य्या-र्य्यं) Unactionable, not to be discussed in law.<BR>E. अ neg. व्यवहार्य्य actionable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यवहित|अव्यवहितं
अव्यवहित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Adjoining, contiguous.<BR> E. अ neg. and व्यवहित<BR>divided.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यवहृत|अव्यवहृतः
अव्यवहृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Not determined or investigated by law.<BR>	 2.<BR>Not spoken.<BR> E. अ neg. व्यवहृत tried.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यसन
अव्यसन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Moral, correct, free from vice.<BR> E. अ neg. व्यसन<BR>evil practice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यसनिन्
अव्यसनिन् mfn. (-नी-निनी-नि) Free from evil practices, steady, correct.<BR>E. अ neg. व्यसन evil practices, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यस्त
अव्यस्त mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं)<BR>	 1. Simple, undecomposed.<BR>	 2. Undispersed,<BR>collected.<BR> E. अ neg. व्यस्त scattered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्याकुल
अव्याकुल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Calm, firm, composed.<BR> E. अ neg. व्याकुल<BR>flurried.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्याकृत
अव्याकृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Undecomposed.<BR>	 n. (-तं) Elementary substance<BR>from which all things were created, considered as one with the<BR>substance of BRAHMĀ.<BR> E. अ neg. व्याकृत separated, decomposed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्याख्या
अव्याख्या f. (-ख्या) Obscurity, want of clearness or explanation.<BR> E. अ neg.<BR>व्याख्या explanation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्याख्यात
अव्याख्यात mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Unexplained, obscure.<BR> E. अ neg. व्याख्यात ex-<BR>plained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्याख्यान|अव्याख्यानं
अव्याख्यान n. (-नं) Absence of explicitness, want of explanation.<BR> E. अ<BR>neg. व्याख्यान explanation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्याख्येय
अव्याख्येय mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>	 1. Unintelligible, inexplicable.<BR>	 2. Easy, not<BR>requiring to be explained.<BR> E. अ neg. व्याख्येय to be explained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्याज|अव्याजं|अव्याजः
अव्याज m. (-जः) Absence of fraud, simplicity, honesty.<BR> E. अ neg. व्याज<BR>disguise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यापक
अव्यापक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Special, individual, peculiar.<BR> E. अ neg. व्यापक<BR>generick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यापकत्व
अव्यापकत्व n. (-त्वं) Speciality, individuality, non-comprehensiveness or<BR>generalization.<BR> E. अव्यापक special, and त्व affix; also अव्यापकता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यापार|अव्यापारः
अव्यापार mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Inexpert, inexperienced.<BR>	 m. (-रः) Business not<BR>practised or understood.<BR> E. अ not, व्यापार business.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यापित्व
अव्यापित्व n. (-त्वं) Speciality, non-generalization.<BR> E. अ neg. व्यापिन् what<BR>pervades, त्व affix; also अव्यापिता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यापिन्
अव्यापिन् mfn. (-पी-पिनी-पि)<BR>	 1. Special, individual.<BR>	 2. Limited, partial, not<BR>comprehensive.<BR> E. अ neg. व्यापिन् pervading.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्याप्त
अव्याप्त mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं) Peculiar, individual, limited.<BR> E. अ neg. व्याप्त<BR>diffused.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्याप्य|अव्याप्यं
अव्याप्य mfn. (-प्यः-प्या-प्यं) Peculiar, not to be extended generally.<BR> E. अ neg.<BR>व्याप्य to be extended.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्याप्यवृत्ति|अव्याप्यवृत्तिः
अव्याप्यवृत्ति mfn. (-त्तिः-त्तिः-त्ति) (In logic) A category of individual appli-<BR>cation, and influenced by place and time, as pain, pleasure, love,<BR>hatred, virtue, vice, &c.<BR> E. अ neg. व्याप्य diffusive, general, and<BR>वृत्ति being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यायाम|अव्यायामः
अव्यायाम m. (-मः) Absence of lassitude or fatigue.<BR> E. अ neg. व्यायाम exer-<BR>tion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यावर्त्तन|अव्यावर्तन
अव्यावर्त्तन n. (-नं) Not returning, not coming back, not circulating.<BR> E. अ<BR>neg. व्यावर्त्तन returning, revolving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्याहत|अव्याहतं
अव्याहत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Unresisted, unimpeded.<BR>	 2. Not disappointed.<BR>E. अ neg. व्याहत baffled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्याहित
अव्याहित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Undisputed.<BR> E. अ neg. व्याहित disputed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=072-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्रण
अव्रण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Sound, unhurt, unscarred.<BR> E. अ neg. व्रण a wound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=072-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्रत
अव्रत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Not observing religious rites or obligations, un-<BR>initiated.<BR> E. अ neg. व्रत a vow, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=072-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश
अश r. 5th cl. (ऊ) अशू (अश्नुते) 1. To pervade or occupy.<BR>	 2. To heap or<BR>crowd. r. 9th cl. (अश्नाति) To eat, to eat hungrily. With प्र prefixed,<BR>to begin to eat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=072-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशक्त|अशक्तं
अशक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं) Unable, incompetent.<BR> E. अ neg. शक्त able, strong.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=072-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशक्तता
अशक्तता f. (-ता) Weakness, inability.<BR> E. तल् added to the last; also with<BR>त्व, अशक्तत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=072-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशक्ति|अशक्तिः
अशक्ति f. (-क्तिः) Inability, incapability, weakness, impotence.<BR> E. अ neg.<BR>शक्ति power.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=072-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशक्य|अशक्यं
अशक्य mfn. (-क्यः-क्या-क्यं)<BR>	 1. Impossible, impracticable.<BR>	 2. Not to be<BR>made.<BR> E. अ neg. शक्य possible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=072-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशङ्क|अशंक
अशङ्क mfn. (-ङ्कः-ङ्का-ङ्कं)<BR>	 1. Fearless, undaunted.<BR>	 2. Secure, certain.<BR> E. अ<BR>neg. शङ्का fear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=072-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशङ्कित|अशंकित
अशङ्कित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Certain, undoubted.<BR>	 2. Fearless.<BR> E. अ neg. शङ्कित<BR>alarmed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=072-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशठ
अशठ mfn. (-ठः-ठा-ठं) Virtuous, good.<BR> E. अ neg. शठ wicked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=072-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशत्रु|अशत्रुः
अशत्रु mfn. (-त्रुः-त्रुः-त्रु) Friendly.<BR>	 m. (-त्रुः) A name of the moon.<BR> E. अ neg.<BR>and शत्रु an enemy; who has.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=072-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशन|अशनं|अशनः
अशन m. (-नः) A plant, (Pentaptera tomentosa, Rox.)<BR>	 n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Food.<BR>2. Eating: also असन.<BR> E. अश to eat, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=072-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशनपर्णी
अशनपर्णी f. (-र्णी) A plant: also असनपर्णी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=072-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशनाया
अशनाया f. (-या) Hunger.<BR> E. अशन food, क्यच् affix, अ and टाप् added, and<BR>the penultimate made long: wishing for food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=072-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशनायित|अशनायितं
अशनायित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Hungry. E. As before, इतच् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=072-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशनि|अशनिः
अशनि mf. (-निः-निः) INDRA'S thunderbolt.<BR> E. अश to eat, अनि Unādi affix;<BR>what eats or consumes rocks, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=072-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशरीर|अशरीरः
अशरीर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Bodiless, incorporeal m. (-रः) A name of KĀMA or<BR>love.<BR> E. अ neg. शरीर body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=072-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशरीरिन्
अशरीरिन् mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि) Incorporeal.<BR> E. अ neg. शरीरिन् embodied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=072-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशर्म्मन्|अशर्मन्
अशर्म्मन् n. (-र्म्म) Pain, affliction.<BR>	 mfn. (-र्म्मा-र्म्मा-र्म्म) Unhappy, afflicted. E.<BR>शर्म्मन् happiness, &c. with the priv. prefix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=072-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशान्त|अशांत
अशान्त mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं) Restless, anxious, unresigned.<BR> E. अ neg. शान्त<BR>tranquil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=072-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशान्ति
अशान्ति f. (-न्तिः) Anxiety, restlessness.<BR> E. अ neg. शान्ति tranquillity. So<BR>अशान्तता f. (-ता).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=072-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशाम्य
अशाम्य mfn. (-म्यः-म्या-म्यं) Unappeasable, not to be pacified.<BR> E. अ neg. शम<BR>to appease, ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=072-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशारीरिक
अशारीरिक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Not relating to or endowed with body.<BR> E. अ<BR>neg. शारीरिक bodily.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=072-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशाश्वत
अशाश्वत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Perishable, transient, temporary.<BR> E. अ neg. शाश्वत<BR>eternal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=072-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशासन
अशासन n. (-नं) Want of government, anarchy, disorder.<BR> E. अ neg. शासन<BR>governing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=072-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशासनीय
अशासनीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Ungovernable: so अशास्य<BR> E. अ neg. शासनीय or<BR>शास्य to be ruled, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=072-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशासित
अशासित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Ungoverned, undisciplined.<BR> E. अ neg. शासित<BR>governed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=072-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशास्त्र
अशास्त्र mfn. (-स्त्रः-स्त्रा-स्त्रं) Not conformable to sacred authority, hetero-<BR>dox, unscriptural.<BR> E. अ neg. शास्त्र scripture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=072-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशास्त्रीय
अशास्त्रीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Not conformable to sacred authority, hetero-<BR>dox, immoral, irreligious.<BR> E. अ neg. शास्त्रीय scriptural.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=072-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशिक्षित|अशिक्षितं
अशिक्षित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Untaught, ignorant.<BR> E. अ neg. शिक्षित taught.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=072-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशित|अशितं
अशित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Eaten.<BR>	 2. Satisfied.<BR> E. अश to eat, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=072-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशितङ्गवीन|अशितंगवीन|अशितङ्गवीनं
अशितङ्गवीन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Formerly grazed by cattle, (a field, &c.) E.<BR>अशित eaten, and गवीन relating to cattle; also आशितङ्गवीन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=072-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशित्र|अशित्रः
अशित्र m. (-त्रः) A thief.<BR> E. अशू to pervade, इत्र Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=072-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशिथिल
अशिथिल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Firm, tight, hard.<BR> E. अ neg. शिथिल loose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=072-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशिर|अशिरं|अशिरः
अशिर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A name of the sun.<BR>	 2. Fire.<BR>	 3. A goblin or demon.<BR>	 f.<BR>(-रा) The wife of a goblin.<BR>	 n. (-रं) A diamond.<BR> E. अश to eat, and<BR>इर affix; what eats sacrifices, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=073-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशिरस्
अशिरस् mfn. (-राः-राः-रः) Headless.<BR> E. अ neg. शिरस् the head.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=073-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशिरःस्नान
अशिरःस्नान n. (-नं) Bathing the body with exception of the head.<BR> E. अ<BR>neg. शिरस् the head, स्नान bathing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=073-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशिव|अशिवः
अशिव mfn. (-वः-वा-वं) Unlucky, unfortunate.<BR> E. अ neg. शिव propitious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=073-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशिवी
अशिवी f. (-वी) A female demon or goblin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=073-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशिश्विका
अशिश्विका f. (-का) See the following.<BR> E. कन् added to अशिश्वी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=073-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशिश्वी
अशिश्वी f. (-श्वी) A childless woman.<BR> E. अ priv. शिशु a child, and ङीप् fem.<BR>affix: उ becomes व.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=073-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशिष्ट
अशिष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं) Ill regulated, ill-behaved, rude, barbarous,<BR>profligate<BR> E. अ neg. शिष्ट regulated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=073-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशिष्टता
अशिष्टता f. (-ता) Rudeness, &c.<BR> E. तल् added to the last; also with त्व,<BR>अशिष्टत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=073-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशिष्टाचार
अशिष्टाचार m. (-रः) Rudeness, profligacy.<BR> E. अशिष्ट, and आचार practice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=073-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशीत|अशीतः
अशीत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Warm, hot.<BR> E. अ not, शीत cold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=073-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशीतकर|अशीतकरः
अशीतकर m. (-रः) The sun.<BR> E. अ neg. शीत cold, and कर a ray, and similar<BR>compounds, as अशीतदीधितिः, अशीतमरीचिः, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=073-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशीति|अशीतिः
अशीति f. sing. always (-तिः) Eighty. du. (-ती) Two eighties. pl. (-तयः)<BR>Many eighties.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=073-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशीतिक
अशीतिक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Octagenarian, of eighty years of age, &c. E.<BR>अशीति and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=073-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशीर्ण
अशीर्ण mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-र्णं) Undecayed, unimpaired.<BR> E. अ neg. शीर्ण decayed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=073-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशील
अशील mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>	 1. Ill behaved, vulgar, offensive.<BR>	 2. Indifferent.<BR>E. अ neg. शील polite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=073-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशुष्क
अशुष्क mfn. (-ष्कः-ष्का-ष्कं) Green, fresh, moist.<BR> E. अ neg. शुष्क dry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=073-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशुचि|अशुचिः
अशुचि f. (-चिः)<BR>	 1. Impurity.<BR>	 2. Disgrace, degradation.<BR>	 mfn. (-चिः-चिः-चि)<BR>Foul, impure.<BR> E. अ neg. शुचि purity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=073-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशुचित्व
अशुचित्व n. (-त्वं) Impurity.<BR> E. त्व added to अशुचि; also अशुचिता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=073-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशुद्ध|अशुद्धं
अशुद्ध mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>	 1. Impure.<BR>	 2. Inaccurate.<BR>	 3. Unknown, unascer-<BR>tained.<BR> E. अ neg. शुद्ध pure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=073-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशुद्धवासक|अशुद्धवासकः
अशुद्धवासक m. (-कः) A vagrant, a suspicious character.<BR> E. अशुद्ध unknown,<BR>वास abode, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=073-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशुद्धि|अशुद्धिः
अशुद्धि f. (-द्धिः) Impurity.<BR>	 mfn. (-द्धिः-द्धिः-द्धि) Impure.<BR> E. अ neg. शुद्धि<BR>purity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=073-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशुभ|अशुभं
अशुभ n. (-भं)<BR>	 1. Sin.<BR>	 2. Misfortune.<BR>	 mfn. (-भः-भा-भं) Unlucky.<BR> E. अ priv.<BR>शुभ good.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=073-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशुश्रूषा
अशुश्रूषा f. (-षा) Inattention, neglect of service or respect.<BR> E. अ neg. शुश्रूषा<BR>service.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=073-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशृत|अशृतं
अशृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Unripe.<BR> E. अ neg. and शृत ripe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=073-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशेष|अशेषं|अशेषः
अशेष mfn. (-षः-षा-षं)<BR>	 1. Entire, all the whole.<BR>	 2. Infinite, endless.<BR> E. अ<BR>neg. and शेष remainder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=073-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशेषतस्
अशेषतस् ind. Entirely, wholly.<BR> E. अशेष whole, तसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=073-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशोक|अशोकं|अशोकः
अशोक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Cheerful, not sorrowful.<BR>	 m. (-कः) A tree com-<BR>monly Asoka (Jonesia Asoca.)<BR>	 n. (-कं) Quicksilver.<BR>	 f. (-का)<BR>	 1. A<BR>medicinal plant, see कटुकी.<BR>	 2. One of the female domestic deities<BR>of the jainas.<BR> E. अ neg. and शोक sorrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=073-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशोकरोहिणी
अशोकरोहिणी f. (-णी) A medicinal plant, see कटुकी.<BR> E. अशोक, and रोहिणी<BR>the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=073-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशोकारि|अशोकारिः
अशोकारि m. (-रिः) A tree, (Nauclea Cadamba:) see कदम्ब.<BR> E. अशोक, and<BR>अरि an enemy: choking the Asoca.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=073-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशोच|अशोचः
अशोच m. (-चः) Content, tranquillity, the absence of care or vanity.<BR> E. अ<BR>priv. शोच sorrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=073-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशोच्य|अशोच्यं
अशोच्य mfn. (-च्यः-च्या-च्यं) Not to be sorrowed for.<BR> E. अ neg. शोच्य to be<BR>regretted; also अशोचनीय and अशोचितव्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=073-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशोधन
अशोधन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Uncleanness.<BR>	 2. Inaccuracy.<BR> E. अ neg. शोधन cleaning,<BR>&c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=073-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशोधित
अशोधित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Unclean, uncleansed.<BR>	 2. Inaccurate, unrevised,<BR>uncorrected.<BR> E. अ neg. शोधित purified.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=073-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशोष्य
अशोष्य mfn. (-ष्यः-ष्या-ष्यं) Not to be dried up.<BR> E. अ neg. शोष्य to be dried<BR>up; so अशोषणीय, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=073-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशौच|अशौचं
अशौच n. (-चं)<BR>	 1. Foulness, impurity.<BR>	 2. Legal impurity, contamination,<BR>defilement contracted by the death of a relation, the commission of<BR>prohibited acts, &c.<BR> E. अ neg. शौच purification.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=073-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशौचत्व
अशौचत्व n. (-त्वं)<BR>	 1. Impure or abandoned nature or diposition.<BR>	 2. Defile-<BR>ment, contamination.<BR> E. त्व added to अशौच.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=073-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशौर्य्य|अशौर्य
अशौर्य्य n. (-र्य्यं) Want of heroism, cowardice.<BR> E. अ neg. शौर्य्य valour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=073-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्म|अश्मः
अश्म m. (-श्मः)<BR>	 1. A mountain, a rock.<BR>	 2. A cloud, (in the language of<BR>the Vedas:) see अश्मन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=073-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्मकुट्ट|अश्मकुट्टः
अश्मकुट्ट mfn. (-ट्टः-ट्टा-ट्टं) Who or what breaks with a stone.<BR>	 2. Bruised or<BR>broken by stones.<BR> E. अश्म and कुट्ट what bruises or breaks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=073-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्मकुट्टक|अश्मकुट्टकः
अश्मकुट्टक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Breaking or bruising any thing with a stone.<BR>E. अश्म and कुट्टक who breaks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=073-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्मगर्भ|अश्मगर्भः
अश्मगर्भ m. (-र्भः) An emerald.<BR> E. अश्मन् a stone, and गर्भ the womb; the<BR>primary stone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=073-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्मगर्भज|अश्मगर्भजं|अश्मगर्भजः
अश्मगर्भज n. (-जं) An emerald.<BR> E. अश्म and गर्भ before ज produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=073-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्मज|अश्मजं|अश्मजः
अश्मज n. (-जं)<BR>	 1. Red chalk.<BR>	 2. Iron.<BR> E. अश्मन् a stone, &c. and ज pro-<BR>duced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=073-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्मजतुक|अश्मजतुकं
अश्मजतुक n. (-कं) Bitumen.<BR> E. अश्म and जतुक lac.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=073-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्मदारण|अश्मदारणः
अश्मदारण m. (-णः) An axe or crow for breaking stones, &c.<BR>	 n. (-णं) Split-<BR>ting stones or rocks.<BR> E. अश्मन् a stone, &c. दॄ to split. ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=073-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्मन्
अश्मन् m. (-श्मा) A stone or rock.<BR> E. अश to spread, &c. मनिन् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=073-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्मन्त|अश्मंत|अश्मन्तं|अश्मन्तः
अश्मन्त mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं)<BR>	 1. Unbounded, unlimited.<BR>	 2. Inauspicious, un-<BR>lucky.<BR>	 n. (-न्तं)<BR>	 1. A fireplace.<BR>	 2. Death.<BR>	 3. A field, a plain.<BR> E. अश्मन्<BR>a stone, &c. and अन्त the end; it is also written अश्वन्त and अस्मन्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=073-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्मन्तक|अश्मंतकं|अश्मन्तकं|अश्मंतकः|अश्मन्तकः
अश्मन्तक n. (-कं)<BR>	 1. A fireplace.<BR>	 2. A shade for a lamp.<BR>	 3. A species of<BR>oxalis.<BR> E. कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=073-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्मपुष्प|अश्मपुष्पं
अश्मपुष्प n. (-ष्पं) Benzoin, (Styrax benzoin.)<BR> E. अश्मन् stone, and पुष्प a<BR>flower: supposed to exude from rocks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=073-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्मभाल|अश्मभालं
अश्मभाल m. (-लः) A mortar of stone or iron.<BR> E. अश्मन् a stone, and भाल<BR>the skull.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=073-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्मभिद्
अश्मभिद् m. (-द्) The name of a plant, (Plectranthus scutellaroides, Rox.)<BR>E. अश्मन् a stone, and भिद् what breaks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=073-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्मभेद|अश्मभेदः
अश्मभेद m. (-दः) See the preceding. E. As before, अश्मन् and भेद.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=073-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्ममय
अश्ममय mfn. (-यः-यी-यं) Made or consisting of stone, stony.<BR>	 n. (-यं) A<BR>mineral.<BR> E. अश्म and मयट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=073-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्मयोनि|अश्मयोनिः
अश्मयोनि m. (-निः) An emerald. E. See अश्मगर्भ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=073-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्मर|अश्मरः
अश्मर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Stony, rocky, appertaining to stone or rock. E.<BR>अश्मन् and र aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=073-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्मरी
अश्मरी f. (-री)<BR>	 1. Strangury.<BR>	 2. Stone or gravel, (the disease.)<BR> E. अश्मर<BR>stony, and ङीप् fem. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=073-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्मरीघ्न|अश्मरीघ्नः
अश्मरीघ्न m. (-घ्नः) A tree, (Tapia cratœva.)<BR> E. अश्मरी gravel, and घ्न what<BR>destroys; a lithonthriptic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=073-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्मरीहर|अश्मरीहरः
अश्मरीहर m. (-रः) A tree, (Pentaptera arjuna.) E. See the last word, हर<BR>from हृ to carry away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=073-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्मसार|अश्मसारः
अश्मसार mn. (-रः-रं) Iron.<BR> E. अश्मन् a stone, and सार essence, &c. the<BR>hardest stone, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=073-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्मान्तक
अश्मान्तक m. (-कः) A plant, from the fibres of which the girdle of a<BR>Brahman may be made; also अश्मन्तक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=073-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्मीर|अश्मीरं|अश्मीरः
अश्मीर mn. (-रः-रं) Stone or gravel, (the disease.)<BR> E. अश्मन् a stone, ईर<BR>aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=073-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्र|अश्रं|अश्रः
अश्र n. (-श्रं)<BR>	 1. A tear.<BR>	 2. Blood.<BR> E. अशू to spread, &c. and र affix; see<BR>अश्रु and अस्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=073-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्रद्ध
अश्रद्ध mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं) Unbelieving.<BR>	 f. (-द्धा) Unbelief.<BR> E. अ neg. श्रद्धा faith.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=073-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्रद्दधान|अश्रद्दधानः
अश्रद्दधान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Unbelieving, incredulous, having no faith.<BR> E. अ<BR>neg. श्रद्दधान believing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=073-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्रद्धेय|अश्रद्धेयं
अश्रद्धेय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Incredible, not to be believed.<BR> E. अ neg. and श्रद्धेय<BR>worthy of faith.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=073-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्रप|अश्रपः
अश्रप m. (-पः) A fiend, a cannibal.<BR> E. अश्र blood, and प who drinks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=073-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्रवण|अश्रवणः
अश्रवण n. (-णं) Deafness, loss of hearing.<BR> E. अ neg. श्रवण hearing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=074-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्रम|अश्रमः
अश्रम m. (-मः)<BR>	 1. Freshness, freedom from fatigue.<BR>	 2. Laziness, want of<BR>exertion.<BR> E. अ neg. श्रम fatigue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=074-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्राद्ध|अश्राद्धः
अश्राद्ध mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>	 1. Not performing exequial rites, not entitled<BR>to them, not belonging or relating to them.<BR>	 m. (-द्धः) Non-perform-<BR>ance of exequial rites.<BR> E. अ neg. श्राद्ध funereal ceremony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=074-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्रान्त|अश्रांत|अश्रान्तं|अश्रान्तः
अश्रान्त adv.<BR>	 n. (-न्तं) adj.<BR>	 mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं)<BR>	 1. Eternal, continual.<BR>	 2.<BR>Unwearied.<BR> E. अ neg. and श्रान्त wearied, part. past of श्रम.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=074-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्रि|अश्रिः
अश्रि f. (-श्रिः)<BR>	 1. The edge of a sword.<BR>	 2. A corner, the angle of a room<BR>or house.<BR> E. श्रिञ् to serve, आङ् prefixed, आ becomes अ; also अश्री<BR>and आश्रि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=074-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्रीक
अश्रीक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Unlucky, unpropitious.<BR> E. अ neg. श्री fortune,<BR>and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=074-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्रीमत्|अश्रीमन्त्
अश्रीमत् mfn. (-मान्-मती-मत्) Inglorious, unfortunate.<BR> E. अ neg. श्रीमत्<BR>fortunate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=074-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्रील
अश्रील mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Unlucky, unprosperous.<BR> E. अ neg. श्री prosperity,<BR>ला to have, affix क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=074-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्रु
अश्रु n. (-श्रु) A tear.<BR> E. अ neg. श्रि to serve, डुन् Unādi affix; it is also<BR>written अश्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=074-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्रुत|अश्रुतं
अश्रुत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Unheard.<BR>	 2. Not directed by or contrary to the<BR>Vedas.<BR> E. अ neg. and श्रुत heard, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=074-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्रुनाली
अश्रुनाली f. (-ली) Fistula lachrymalis.<BR> E. अश्रु and नाली a channel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=074-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्रुपात|अश्रुपातः
अश्रुपात m. (-तः) A flow of tears.<BR> E. अश्रु, and पात fall.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=074-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्रेयस्
अश्रेयस् mfn. (-यान्-यसी-यः)<BR>	 1. Worthless, useless, unprofitable, bad.<BR>	 2.<BR>Inferior, worse.<BR> E. अ neg. श्रेयस् excellent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=074-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्रेष्ठ
अश्रेष्ठ mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठा-ष्ठं)<BR>	 1. Inferior, worse.<BR>	 2. Bad, vile.<BR> E. अ neg. श्रेष्ठ<BR>best.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=074-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्रोत्रिय
अश्रोत्रिय m. (-यः) A Brahman who has not read the Vedas.<BR> E. अ neg.<BR>श्रोत्रिय a learned Brahman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=074-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्लाघ्य
अश्लाघ्य mfn. (-घ्यः-घ्या-घ्यं) Worthless, undeserving of honour or praise. E.<BR>अ neg. श्लाघ्य to be praised.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=074-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्लाघनीय
अश्लाघनीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Undeserving of honour or praise, base, mean,<BR>worthless.<BR> E. अ neg. श्लाघनीय to be praised.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=074-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्लीक
अश्लीक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Unlucky, unpropitious. E. As अश्रीक, the र being<BR>changed to ल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=074-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्लील
अश्लील mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>	 1. Coarse, vulgar.<BR>	 2. Abusive, blackguard.<BR>	 n. (-लं)<BR>1. Rustic language.<BR>	 2. Untruth.<BR>	 3. Low abuse.<BR> E. अ neg. श्लील<BR>elegant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=074-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्लेषा
अश्लेषा f. (-षा)<BR>	 1. The ninth Nakshatra or lunar mansion, containing<BR>five stars.<BR>	 2. Disunion, disjunction.<BR> E. अ neg. and श्लेष union.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=074-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्लेषाभव|अश्लेषाभवः
अश्लेषाभव m. (-वः) A mane of KETU or the dragon's head: see केतु. E.<BR>अश्लेषा the asterism, and भव born, born under the sign Aslehā; or<BR>अश्लेषा disjunction, and भव produced; as KETU was formed of the<BR>lower extremities which had been sundered by VIṢṆU from RĀHU.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=074-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्लेषाभू
अश्लेषाभू m. (-भूः) A name of KETU. E. As the preceding, भू to be born,<BR>with क्विप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=074-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्व|अश्वः
अश्व m. (-श्वः)<BR>	 1. A horse.<BR>	 2. A set or cast of men horse-like in strength.<BR>du. (-श्वौ) A horse and a mare.<BR>	 f. (-श्वा) A mare.<BR> E. अश to pervade, क्वन्<BR>Unādi affix, and टाप् fem. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=074-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वक|अश्वकः
अश्वक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Horse-like, acting like a horse, &c.<BR>	 m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A<BR>bad horse, a hack.<BR>	 2. A stray horse, one whose owner is not known.<BR>3. Any horse.<BR> E. अश्व and कन् added in different senses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=074-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वकन्दिका
अश्वकन्दिका f. (-का) A plant, (Physalis flexuosa.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=074-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वकर्ण|अश्वकर्णः|अश्वकर्ण्ण
अश्वकर्ण m. (-र्णः) A timber tree, commonly Sakwa or Sal (Shorea robusta.)<BR>E. अश्व a. horse, and कर्ण an ear, the leaves being compared to the<BR>ears of a horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=074-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वकर्णक|अश्वकर्णकः
अश्वकर्णक m. (-कः) The Sal-tree, (Shorea robusta.)<BR> E. कन् added to<BR>अश्वकर्ण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=074-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वकिनी
अश्वकिनी f. (-नी) The first Nakshatra or lunar mansion.<BR> E. अश्वक a horse,<BR>इनि and ङीप् affixes: see अश्विनी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=074-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वखुर|अश्वखुरः
अश्वखुर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A horse's hoof.<BR>	 2. A perfume, apparently a dried<BR>shell-fish: see नखी.<BR>	 f. (-रा-री) A plant, (Clitoria ternatea.)<BR> E. अश्व and<BR>खुर his hoof: which the perfume and leaves of the plant are sup-<BR>posed to resemble.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=074-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वगन्धा
अश्वगन्धा f. (-न्धा) A plant, (Physalis flexuosa.)<BR> E. अश्व, and गन्ध smell;<BR>having the smell of a horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=074-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वगोयुग|अश्वगोयुगं|अश्वगोयुगः
अश्वगोयुग n. (-गं) A pair of horses.<BR> E. अश्व and गोयुगच् affix implying a pair,<BR>a brace. &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=074-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वगोष्ठ|अश्वगोष्ठं
अश्वगोष्ठ n. (-ष्ठं) A stable.<BR> E. अश्व, and गोष्ठ abode, place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=074-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वग्रीव|अश्वग्रीवः
अश्वग्रीव m. (-वः) The name of a demon, more commonly named Hayagrīva.<BR> E. अश्व and ग्रीवा a neck; horse-necked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=074-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वघ्न|अश्वघ्नः
अश्वघ्न m. (-घ्नः) Oleander, (Nerium odorum.)<BR> E. अश्व and घ्न what kills or<BR>hurts, from हन; horse-destroying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=074-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वचिकित्सक|अश्वचिकित्सकः
अश्वचिकित्सक m. (-कः) A farrier.<BR> E. अश्व and चिकित्सक who heals.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=074-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वचिकित्सा
अश्वचिकित्सा f. (-त्सा) Farriery.<BR> E. अश्व and चिकित्सा medical treatment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=074-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वतर|अश्वतरः
अश्वतर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Swift, speedy.<BR>	 mf. (-रः-री) A mule.<BR>	 m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. One<BR>of the chiefs of the Nagas or serpent race, inhabiting the regions<BR>under the earth.<BR>	 2. A Gandharba or celestial chorister.<BR>	 3. A male<BR>calf.<BR> E. अश्व and तर from तॄ to pass, to go, affix अप्; or ष्टरच् diminu-<BR>tive aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=074-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वत्थ|अश्वत्थः
अश्वत्थ m. (-त्थः)<BR>	 1. The holy fig tree, (Ficus religiosa.)<BR>	 2. The fruit of<BR>the tree 3. The time at which it bears.<BR>	 f. (-त्था) Day of fullmoon. E.<BR>अ neg. श्व a future period, and थ from स्था to remain; of less dura-<BR>tion than the Vata or Indian fig; there are several other etymolo-<BR>gies.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=074-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वत्थक|अश्वत्थकः
अश्वत्थक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) To be given, to be done, &c. when the Aswat-<BR>the tree bears.<BR>	 n. (-कं) The petals of the Arabian jasmine. E.<BR>अश्वत्थ and वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=074-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वत्थामन्
अश्वत्थामन् m. (-मा) The name of a saint and warrior, the son of DRONA.<BR>E. अश्व, स्था to stand or stay, and मनिन् affix; the story is that at his<BR>birth he made a noise like a horse; also with a final vowel<BR>अश्वत्थाम.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=074-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वदंष्ट्रा
अश्वदंष्ट्रा f. (-ष्ट्रा) A plant, (Tribulus lanuginosus.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=074-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वन्त|अश्वंत|अश्वन्तं|अश्वन्तः
अश्वन्त n. (-न्तं)<BR>	 1. Death.<BR>	 2. Termination, limit.<BR>	 3. A fireplace.<BR>	 4. A field<BR>5. Unlucky, inauspicious.<BR> E. अशु vital air, अन्त end: also अश्मन्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=074-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वपाल|अश्वपालः
अश्वपाल m. (-लः) A groom.<BR> E. अश्व, and पाल who takes care of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=074-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वबाल|अश्वबालः
अश्वबाल m. (-लः) A kind of reed, (Saccharum spontaneum.)<BR>	 2. Horse hair.<BR>E. अश्व and बाल a tail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=074-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वभा
अश्वभा f. (-भा) Lightning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=074-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वमहिषिका
अश्वमहिषिका f. (-का) The natural enmity of a horse and a buffalo.<BR> E. अश्व,<BR>and महिष a buffalo, वुन् affix of enmity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=074-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वमार|अश्वमारः
अश्वमार m. (-रः) Oleander, (Nerium odorum.)<BR> E. अश्व and मार what kills;<BR>the plant is conceived to be deleterious to the horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=074-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वमारक|अश्वमारकः
अश्वमारक m. (-कः) See the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=074-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वमाल|अश्वमालः
अश्वमाल m. (-लः) A kind of serpent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=074-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वमुख|अश्वमुखः
अश्वमुख m. (-खः) A Kinnara or celestial chorister.<BR> E. अश्व and मुख a face;<BR>this kind of demigod being represented with a horse's head.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=074-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वमेध|अश्वमेधः
अश्वमेध m. (-धः) The actual or emblematic sacrifice of a horse.<BR> E. अश्व and<BR>मेध sacrifice; this sacrifice is one of the highest order, and performed<BR>a hundred times, entitles the sacrificer to the dominion of Svarga<BR>or paradise: it appears to have been originally typical; the horse,<BR>and other animals being simply bound during the performance<BR>of certain ceremonies; the actual sacrifice is an introduction of a<BR>later period. See As. R. Vol. viii. p. 442, COLEBROOKE on the Vedas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=074-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वमेधिक|अश्वमेधिकः
अश्वमेधिक m. (-कः) A horse fit for the sacrifice called Aswamedha. E.<BR>अश्वमेध as above, कन् added, and इ inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=074-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वमेधीय|अश्वमेधीयः
अश्वमेधीय m. (-यः) A horse fit for an Aswamedha.<BR> E. अश्वमेध and छ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=074-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वयुज्
अश्वयुज् f. (-युक्) The first lunar mansion: see अश्विनी.<BR>	 m. (-युक् or -युजः)<BR>The month Aswin, (Sept.-Oct.) See आश्वयुज.<BR> E. अश्व, युज to join,<BR>affix क्विप्; also with अ added in the last sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=074-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वरक्ष|अश्वरक्षः
अश्वरक्ष m. (-क्षः) The keeper or rider of a horse.<BR> E. अश्व and रक्ष who pre-<BR>serves.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=075-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वलाल
अश्वलाल m. (-लः) A kind of snake.<BR> E. अश्व and लाल spittle, whose foam is<BR>like that of a horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=075-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वलोमन्
अश्वलोमन् m. (-मा)<BR>	 1. A kind of snake.<BR>	 2. Horse-hair.<BR> E. अश्व and लोमन्<BR>hair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=075-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्ववक्त्र|अश्ववक्त्रः
अश्ववक्त्र m. (-क्त्रः) A chorister of Svarga, a Kinnara or Gandharba.<BR> E. अश्व<BR>and वक्त्र face, horse-faced: these demigods being so represented.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=075-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्ववडव|अश्ववडवं
अश्ववडव n. (-वं) A stud of horses and mares.<BR>	 m. du. or plu. only (-वौ-वाः)<BR>1. A horse and a mare.<BR>	 2. Horses and mares<BR> E. अश्व and वडवा a mare.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=075-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्ववह|अश्ववहः
अश्ववह m. (-हः) A horseman.<BR> E. अश्व and वह what bears; whom a horse<BR>carries.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=075-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्ववार|अश्ववारः
अश्ववार m. (-रः) A horseman.<BR> E. अश्व and वृञ् to nourish, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=075-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्ववारण|अश्ववारणः
अश्ववारण m. (-णः) The Gayal, a sort of ox, (Bos gavœus.)<BR> E. अश्व, वृ to<BR>screen or hide, in the causal form, युच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=075-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वविद्
अश्वविद् m. (-वित्)<BR>	 1. A name of NALA, a king and hero of several poems.<BR>2. A jockey.<BR> E. अश्व and विद् who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=075-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्ववैद्य|अश्ववैद्यः
अश्ववैद्य m. (-द्यः) A farrier, a horse-doctor.<BR> E. अश्व and वैद्य physician.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=075-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वशाला
अश्वशाला f. (-ला)<BR>	 1. A stable.<BR>	 2. A riding house.<BR> E. अश्व and शाला a hall.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=075-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वशाव|अश्वशावः
अश्वशाव m. (-वः) A foal, a colt.<BR> E. अश्व and शाव young.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=075-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वशृगालिका
अश्वशृगालिका f. (-का) The natural enmity between a horse and a jackal.<BR>E. अश्व and शृगाल a jackal, affix वुन् implying hostility.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=075-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वषड्गव|अश्वषड्गवं
अश्वषड्गव n. (-वं) A set of six horses.<BR> E. अश्व and षड्गवच् a set of six.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=075-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वसादिन्
अश्वसादिन् m. (-दी) A horseman, a rider, a horse-soldier.<BR> E. अश्व and<BR>सादिन् who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=075-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वसारथ्य
अश्वसारथ्य n. (-थ्यं) Management of horses and cars, coachmanship, cha-<BR>rioteership.<BR> E. अश्व and सारथि a driver, यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=075-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वसेन|अश्वसेनः
अश्वसेन m. (-नः) A proper name, a king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=075-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वसेननृपनन्दन|अश्वसेननृपनन्दनः
अश्वसेननृपनन्दन m. (-नः) A king and saint; also SANATKUMARA.<BR> E. अश्वसेन<BR>a proper name, नृप a king, and नन्दन a son: the son of the king ASWA-<BR>SENA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=075-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वस्तन
अश्वस्तन mfn. (-नः-नी-नं) Of today, not of or for tomorrow.<BR> E. अ neg.<BR>श्वस् tomorrow, द्यु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=075-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वस्तनिक
अश्वस्तनिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Not of or for tomorrow.<BR> E. अश्वस्तन and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=075-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वहारक|अश्वहारकः
अश्वहारक m. (-कः) A horse-stealer.<BR> E. अश्व and हारक who takes away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=075-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वहृदय
अश्वहृदय n. (-यं) Horsemanship.<BR> E. अश्व and हृदय heart, affection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=075-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वारि|अश्वारिः
अश्वारि m. (-रिः) A buffalo.<BR> E. अश्व and अरि an enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=075-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वारूढ|अश्वारूढः
अश्वारूढ mfn. (-ढः-ढा-ढं) Mounted, set on horse-back.<BR> E. अश्व and आरूढ<BR>mounted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=075-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वारोह|अश्वारोहः
अश्वारोह mfn. (-हः-हा-हं) Riding or carried on a horse.<BR>	 m. (-हः) A horse-<BR>man.<BR>	 f. (-हा) A plant; also Aśwagandha, (Physalis flexuosa.)<BR> E. अश्व<BR>and आरोह what mounts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=075-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वावरोहक|अश्वावरोहकः
अश्वावरोहक m. (-कः) A plant, (Physalis flexuosa.)<BR> E. अश्व, अव on, &c. रोहक<BR>what grows; growing to the length of a horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=075-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वारोहिन्
अश्वारोहिन् mfn. (-ही-हिणी-हि) Mounted or riding on horse-back.<BR> E. अश्व and<BR>आरोहिन् what mounts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=075-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्विक
अश्विक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Drawn by horses, carried by horses, &c.<BR> E. अश्व<BR>and ष्ठन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=075-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्विन्
अश्विन् m. du. (-नौ) The twin sons of AŚVINĪ by SŪRYA, and physicians<BR>of Svarga.<BR> E. अश्विनी and अण् affix, the fem. termination is dropped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=075-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्विनी
अश्विनी f. (-नी)<BR>	 1. The first of the twenty-eight Nakshatras or constella-<BR>tions in the moons path, hence considered its mansions.<BR>	 2. In my-<BR>thology, a nymph, the asterism personified.<BR>	 3. The wife of SŪRYA,<BR>who concealed herself in the form of a mare.<BR> E. अश्व a horse, इन् and<BR>ङीप् affixes; the symbol of the Nakshatra is a horse's head, figured<BR>by three stars in the head of ARIES.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=075-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्विनीकुमार
अश्विनीकुमार m. du. (-रौ) The twin sons of SŪRYA the sun, by his wife<BR>SANJNA transformed to a mare; they are endowed with perpetual<BR>youth and beauty, and are the physicians of the gods.<BR> E. अश्विनी the<BR>wife of SŪRYA, and कुमार a youth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=075-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्विनीपुत्र
अश्विनीपुत्र m. du. (-त्रौ) The Aswins: see the last.<BR> E. अश्विनी and पुत्र a son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=075-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्विनीसुत
अश्विनीसुत m. du. (-तौ) The twin sons of AŚVINĪ by SŪRYA.<BR> E. अश्विनी<BR>and सुत a son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=075-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्विसालोक्य
अश्विसालोक्य n. (-क्यं) The heaven or station of the Aswins, to which the<BR>giver of a horse is raised.<BR> E. अश्विन् and सालोक्य interview.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=075-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वीन|अश्वीनः
अश्वीन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Distant, a day's journey for a horse, more usually<BR>आश्वीन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=075-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वीय|अश्वीयं|अश्वीयः
अश्वीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Belonging or relating to a horse.<BR>	 n. (-यं) A number<BR>of horses.<BR> E. अश्व and छ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=075-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वोरस
अश्वोरस mfn. (-सः-सी-सं) Broad-chested.<BR> E. अश्व and उरस् the breast, टच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=075-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष
अष r. 1st cl. (असति-ते)<BR>	 1. To go or move.<BR>	 2. To take or receive.<BR>	 3. To<BR>shine: see अस.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=075-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अषडक्षीण|अषडक्षीणः
अषडक्षीण m. (-णः) A secret.<BR> E. अ neg. षट् six, अक्षि in eye, and ख affix;<BR>what is not seen by six eyes, that is known or determined by two<BR>persons to the exclusion of a third.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=075-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अषाढ|अषाढः
अषाढ mfn. (-ढः-ढा-ढं) Produced or occurring in the month Āshāḍha.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-ढः)<BR>	 1. The month Āshāḍha, commencing with the sun's entrance<BR>into Gemini, (June-July.)<BR>	 2. A student's staff.<BR>	 f. (-ढा) A name com-<BR>mon to the twentieth and twenty-first lunar mansion: see पूर्व्वाषाढा<BR>and उत्तराषाढा. E. See आषाढ, the initial being made short.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=075-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अषाढक|अषाढकः
अषाढक m. (-कः) The month Āshāḍha; also आषाढक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=075-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टक|अष्टकः
अष्टक mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>	 1. Eight.<BR>	 2. Eighth.<BR>	 n. (-कं) The eight sections<BR>of PĀṆINI'S Grammar.<BR>	 m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. The formulæ of the Rig Veda<BR>as collected into eight portions, thence called Ashtakas.<BR>	 2. One<BR>acquainted with PĀṆINI'S rules or the formulæ of the Veda.<BR> E. कन्<BR>added to अष्ट.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=075-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टकर्ण|अष्टकर्णः
अष्टकर्ण m. (-र्णः) A name of BRAHMĀ.<BR> E. अष्ट eight, and कर्ण an ear; eight-<BR>eared, being four-headed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=075-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टका
अष्टका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. Worship of the manes or progenitors performed on<BR>certain days.<BR>	 2. The eighth day of three months on which the<BR>progenitors are worshipped. E. (अश) to ear, and तकन् affix; vegetables,<BR>flesh, and cake, being severally offered upon these occasions, and<BR>the Brahmins feasted; in this sense it is also अष्टिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=075-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टकाङ्ग|अष्टकांग|अष्टकाङ्गं|अष्टकाङ्गः
अष्टकाङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः) A kind of board or cloth for playing with dice on. E.<BR>अष्टक eight, and अङ्ग body, having eight divisions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=075-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टकोण|अष्टकोणः
अष्टकोण m. (-णः) An octagon.<BR> E. अष्ट and कोण angle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=075-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टगाध्
अष्टगाध् m. (-द् or -त्)<BR>	 1. A fabulous animal supposed to have eight legs:<BR>see शरभ.<BR>	 2. A spider.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=075-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टगव
अष्टगव n. (-वं) A flock of eight cows.<BR> E. अष्ट and गव kine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=075-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टगुण
अष्टगुण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Eightfold.<BR> E. अष्ट eight, गुण number.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=075-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टदिक्पाल
अष्टदिक्पाल m. plu. (-लाः) The regents of the cardinal points, as INDRA of<BR>the East; VAHNI of the S. E.; YAMA of the South; NAIRRIT of<BR>the S. W.; VARUṆA of the West; MARUT of the N. W.; KUVERA<BR>of the North; and ISA of the N. E.<BR> E. अष्टदिश् the eight points, and<BR>पाल who protects.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=075-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टदिश्
अष्टदिश् f. (-दिक्) The eight cardinal points of the compass collectively.<BR>E. अष्ट eight, दिश् quarter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=075-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टधा
अष्टधा ind. Eightfold, eight times.<BR> E. अष्ट eight, धा aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=075-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टधातु|अष्टधातुः
अष्टधातु n. (-तु) The eight metals collectively, as gold, silver, copper, tin,<BR>lead, brass, iron and steel.<BR> E. अष्ट and धातु a mineral.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=075-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टन्
अष्टन् mfn. plu. only (अष्ट or अष्टौ) Eight.<BR> E. असू to pervade, कनिन्<BR>Unādi affix, and तुद् inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=075-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टपाद|अष्टपादः
अष्टपाद m. (-पात् or -पाद्)<BR>	 1. A spider.<BR>	 2. A fabulous animal with eight<BR>legs: see शरभ.<BR>	 m. (-दः) A kind of spider with a small body and<BR>long legs.<BR> E. अष्ट eight, and पाद a foot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=075-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टी
अष्टी f. (-ष्टी) A metre consisting of four lines, and having sixteen sylla-<BR>bles in each; there are nine species of it.<BR> E. अष्टन् eight, ङीप् fem. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=075-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टम|अष्टमः
अष्टम mfn. (-मः-मी-मं) Eight.<BR>	 f. (-मी)<BR>	 1. The eighth day of the fortnight.<BR>2. A medicinal plant: see क्षीरकाकोली, the last of a class of eight<BR>medicinal plants: see अष्टवर्ग.<BR> E. अष्टन् with डट् affix and मट् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=075-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टमङ्गल|अष्टमंगल|अष्टमङ्गलं|अष्टमङ्गलः
अष्टमङ्गल m. (-लः) A horse with a white face, tail, mane, breast, and<BR>hoofs.<BR>	 n. (-लं) A Collection of eight lucky things to be assembled<BR>on certain occasions, as at a coronation, &c. as a lion, a bull, an<BR>elephant, a water-jar, a fan, a flag, a trumpet, and a lamp; or a<BR>Brahman, a cow, fire, gold, ghee, the sun, water, and a king. E.<BR>अष्ट eight, and मङ्गल auspicious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=076-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टमांश|अष्टमांशः
अष्टमांश m. (-शः) An eighth.<BR> E. अष्टम and अंश a part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=076-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टमान|अष्टमानं
अष्टमान n. (-नं) A measure, one Kuḍava.<BR> E. अष्ट eight, and मान measure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=076-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टमिका
अष्टमिका f. (-का) A weight of four tolas.<BR> E. अष्टम eighth, कन् added, fem.<BR>form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=076-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टमूर्त्ति|अष्टमूर्ति|अष्टमूर्तिः|अष्टमूर्त्तिः
अष्टमूर्त्ति m. (-र्त्तिः) A name of ŚIVA.<BR> E. अष्ट eight, and मूर्त्ति form: evident<BR>in the earth, water, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=076-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टमूर्त्तिधर|अष्टमूर्तिधर
अष्टमूर्त्तिधर m. (-रः) A name of ŚIVA.<BR> E. अष्टमूर्त्ति an assemblage of eight<BR>forms, and धर who has, being identical with the five elements and<BR>with the mind, individuality and crude matter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=076-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टलोहक|अष्टलोहकं
अष्टलोहक n. (-कं) A class of eight metals, gold, silver, copper, tin, lead,<BR>and iron of three sorts, including steel.<BR> E. अष्ट eight, लोहक metal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=076-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टवर्ग|अष्टवर्गः
अष्टवर्ग m. (-र्गः) A class of eight principal medicaments, they are mostly<BR>the roots of plants from the hills, which have not been determined,<BR>and are named: Rishabha, Jivāka, Meda, Mahameda, Riddhi,<BR>Vriddhi, Kākoli, and Kṣirakākoli.<BR> E. अष्ट eight, and वर्ग a class.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=076-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टविध
अष्टविध mfn. (-धः-धा-धं) Eightfold, of eight kinds.<BR> E. अष्ट eight, and विध<BR>sort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=076-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टश्रवस्
अष्टश्रवस् m. (-वाः) A name of BRAHMĀ.<BR> E. अष्ट and श्रवस् an ear; eight-<BR>eared.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=076-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टाकपाल|अष्टाकपालः
अष्टाकपाल mfn. (-लः-ली-लं) Prepared in eight pans.<BR>	 m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. A sacrifice<BR>in which ghee, is offered in eight vessels.<BR> E. अष्ट and कपाल the<BR>convexity of a jar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=076-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टागव
अष्टागव n. (-वं) A car or wain, one drawn by eight oxen.<BR> E. अष्ट and गो a<BR>cow, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=076-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टाङ्ग|अष्टांग
अष्टाङ्ग n. (-ङ्गं)<BR>	 1. Eight parts of the body, the hands, breast, forehead,<BR>eyes, throat and middle of the back; or four first, with the knees<BR>and feet; or these six, with the words and mind.<BR>	 2. Any whole con-<BR>sisting of eight parts or members.<BR>	 3. The eight parts of a court, or<BR>the law, the judge, assessors, scribe and astrologer, gold, fire and<BR>water.<BR>	 4. A die, dice.<BR> E. अष्ट eight, and अङ्ग a limb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=076-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टाङ्गनय
अष्टाङ्गनय m. (-यः) See the above.<BR> E. अष्टाङ्ग and नय taking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=076-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टाङ्गपात|अष्टांगपात
अष्टाङ्गपात m. (-तः) Prostration as in reverence.<BR> E. अष्टाङ्ग eight members.<BR>and पात falling, touching the ground with the hands, knees, and<BR>feet, forehead and breast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=076-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टाङ्गप्रणाम|अष्टांगप्रणाम
अष्टाङ्गप्रणाम m. (-मः) Profound reverence, prostration with the hands,<BR>feet, thighs, breast, eyes, head, words and mind.<BR> E. अष्टाङ्ग and<BR>प्रणाम bowing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=076-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टाङ्गार्घ्य|अष्टाङ्गार्घ्यः
अष्टाङ्गार्घ्य m. (-र्घ्यः) An offering of eight articles, water, milk, Kusa<BR>grass, curds, ghee, rice, barley and mustard: or honey, red olean-<BR>der flowers, and sandal, are substituted for the three last.<BR> E. अष्ट<BR>eight, अङ्ग member, अर्घ्य offering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=076-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टादशन्
अष्टादशन् mfn. plu. only (-दश) Eighteen.<BR> E. अष्ट eight, and दशन् ten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=076-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टापद|अष्टापदं|अष्टापदः
अष्टापद mn. (-दः-दं)<BR>	 1. A kind of chequered cloth or board for drafts,<BR>dice, &c.<BR>	 2. Gold.<BR>	 m. (-दः)<BR>	 1. A spider.<BR>	 2. A fabulous animal with<BR>eight legs, the Sarabha.<BR>	 3. The mountain Kailasa or abode of<BR>KUVERA.<BR>	 4. A worm.<BR>	 5. A pin or bolt.<BR>	 f. (-दी) A wild sort of jas-<BR>min.<BR> E. अष्ट eight, and पद a quarter, place, foot, &c. अ being made<BR>long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=076-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टापदपत्र
अष्टापदपत्र n. (-त्रं) Gold-leaf, a sheet of gold.<BR> E. अष्टापद and पत्र a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=076-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टापाद
अष्टापाद mfn. (-दः-दा-दं) Quartered by eight, having eight for the root. E.<BR>अष्टन् and पाद a quarter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=076-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टारचक्रवत्|अष्टारचक्रवन्त्
अष्टारचक्रवत् m. (-वान्) A Jaina saint and ruler.<BR> E. अष्ट, अर a period, and<BR>चक्रवत् a ruler; such for eight Aras.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=076-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टास्र|अष्टास्रः
अष्टास्र n. (-स्रं) An octagon.<BR> E. अष्ट and अस्र angle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=076-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टास्रय
अष्टास्रय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Octangular.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=076-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्ठि|अष्ठिः
अष्ठि f. (-ष्ठिः) A kernel, a stone.<BR> E. अ neg. स्था to remain, इन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=076-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्ठीला
अष्ठीला f. (-ला)<BR>	 1. A round pebble or stone.<BR>	 2. A globular swelling be-<BR>low the navel, produced by wind.<BR>	 3. Contusion.<BR> E. अस्थि a bone, ला<BR>to bring (to resemble,) क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=076-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्ठीवत्|अष्ठीवन्त्
अष्ठीवत् mn. (-वान्-वत्) The knee.<BR> E. अस्थि a bone, and मतुप् poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=076-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्ठीलिका
अष्ठीलिका f. (-का) A pebble.<BR> E. कन् added to the last, fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=076-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंयम|असंयमः
असंयम m. (-मः) Absence of check or restraint, specially of the senses.<BR>E. अ neg. संयम restraint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=076-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंयोग|असंयोगः
असंयोग m. (-गः) Absence of union or connection.<BR> E. अ neg. संयोग connec-<BR>tion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=076-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंलग्न
असंलग्न mfn. (-ग्नः-ग्ना-ग्नं) Disjoined, detached, separate.<BR> E. अ neg. सम् with<BR>लग्न connected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=076-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंविदान
असंविदान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>	 1. Ignorant, unwise.<BR>	 2. Not promising or con-<BR>tracting.<BR> E. अ neg. सं before विद् to know, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=076-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंवृत
असंवृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Uncovered, exposed.<BR> E. अ neg. संवृत covered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=076-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंशय
असंशय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Free from doubt, certain.<BR>	 n. adv. (-यं) Certainly,<BR>verily.<BR> E. अ neg. संशय doubt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=076-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंश्रव
असंश्रव mfn. (-वः-वा-वं) Out of hearing.<BR> E. अ neg. सं with श्रव hearing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=076-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंसक्त
असंसक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं) Indifferent to, not attached to.<BR> E. अ neg. सम्<BR>with सक्त attached.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=076-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंसृष्ट
असंसृष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>	 1. Unmixed with.<BR>	 2. Separate, not living in com-<BR>mon.<BR> E. अ neg. संसृष्ट united.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=076-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंस्कृत|असंस्कृतः
असंस्कृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Not perfect, unpolished, rude, common.<BR>	 2.<BR>Uninitiated, not having gone through the proper rites of caste,<BR>state, sex or age.<BR> E. अ neg. संस्कृत perfect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=076-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंस्तुत
असंस्तुत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Unknown, unacquainted, not known as ac-<BR>quaintances.<BR>	 2. Not friends.<BR> E. अ neg. संस्तुत known.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=076-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंस्थान|असंस्थानं
असंस्थान n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Want, destitution.<BR>	 2. Disorder, confusion.<BR> E. अ neg.<BR>संस्थान station.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=076-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंस्थित
असंस्थित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Disordered, irregular, not arranged or arrayed.<BR>2. Not collected or assembled.<BR>	 3. Destitute.<BR> E. अ neg. संस्थित placed<BR>together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=076-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंस्थिति|असंस्थितिः
असंस्थिति f. (-तिः) See असंस्थान. E. As before, स्थिति stay.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=076-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंहत|असंहतः
असंहत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Scattered, loose, straggling, uncompressed.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-तः) A form of array, loose or open order of troops.<BR> E. अ neg. संहत<BR>compact.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=076-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंहार्य्य|असंहार्य
असंहार्य्य mfn. (-र्य्यः-र्य्या-र्य्यं) Irresistible.<BR> E. अ neg. संहार्य्य to be repelled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=076-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस
अस (ञ) r. 1st. cl. (असति-ते)<BR>	 1. To go or move.<BR>	 2. To take or receive.<BR>	 3.<BR>To shine. (ल) r. 2d cl. (अस्ति) To be. (य, उ, इर्) r. 4th cl. (अस्यति-ते) To<BR>throw or direct. With अनु prefixed, to sit down: with अप, to quit<BR>or abandon: with नि, to deposit: with निर्, to expel: with परि and<BR>उप, to sit around: with प्र, to throw away, to reject, to confute:<BR>with वि, to divide: with वि and आङ्, to class, to arrange: with सम्<BR>and नि, to abandon the world: with सम्, to collect, to combine or<BR>compound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=076-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असकल
असकल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Part, not all, unentire.<BR> E. अ neg. सकल all.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=076-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असकृत्
असकृत् ind. Repeatedly, again and again.<BR> E. अ neg. सकृत् once.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=076-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असकृद्गर्भवास|असकृद्गर्भवासः
असकृद्गर्भवास m. (-सः) Repeated birth.<BR> E. असकृत् repeatedly, गर्भ the womb,<BR>वास abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=076-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असक्त
असक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>	 1. Detached, disunited.<BR>	 2. Not interested in, in-<BR>different to, unattached to.<BR>	 3. Detached from worldly feelings and<BR>passions.<BR> E. अ neg. सक्त united.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=076-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असक्थ
असक्थ mfn. (-क्थः-क्था-क्थं) Without thighs.<BR> E. अ neg. सक्थि a thigh, अच्<BR>affix; also without the affix, असक्थि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=076-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असखि|असखिः
असखि m. (-खा) An enemy, an adversary.<BR> E. अ neg. सखिन् a friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=076-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असगोत्र
असगोत्र mfn. (-त्रः-त्रा-त्रं) Of a different family.<BR> E. अ neg. स with गोत्र<BR>family.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=076-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असङ्कल्प|असंकल्प
असङ्कल्प mn. (-ल्पः-ल्पं)<BR>	 1. Sincerity.<BR>	 2. Absence of predetermination. E.<BR>अ neg. सङ्कल्प will, vow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=076-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असङ्कल्पित|असंकल्पित|असङ्कल्पितः
असङ्कल्पित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Not purposed, not resolved or determined<BR>on.<BR> E. अ neg. सङ्कल्पित purposed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=077-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असङ्कसुक|असंकसुक
असङ्कसुक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Firm, steady.<BR> E. अ neg. सङ्कसुक mutable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=077-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असङ्कीर्ण|असंकीर्ण
असङ्कीर्ण mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-र्णं) Uncompounded, uncollected, unmixed.<BR> E. अ neg.<BR>सङ्कीर्ण collected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=077-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असङ्कुल|असंकुल|असंकुलः|असङ्कुलः
असङ्कुल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Clear, open, broad.<BR>	 m. (-लः) A broad road.<BR> E. अ<BR>neg. and सङ्कुल crowded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=077-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असङ्केत
असङ्केत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Not appointed, not agreed upon.<BR> E. अ neg. सङ्केत<BR>an agreement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=077-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंख्य|असङ्ख्य|असंख्यः|असङ्ख्यः
असंख्य mfn. (-ख्यः-ख्या-ख्यं) Innumerable, exceedingly numerous.<BR> E. अ neg.<BR>and संख्य to be numbered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=077-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंख्यता|असङ्ख्यता
असंख्यता f. (-ता) Innumerability, immensity, infinity.<BR> E. तल् added to the<BR>preceding; or with त्व, असंख्यत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=077-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंख्यात|असङ्ख्यात|असंख्यातं
असंख्यात mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Uncounted.<BR> E. अ neg. संख्यात numbered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=077-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंख्येय|असङ्ख्येय|असंख्येयः
असंख्येय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Innumerable.<BR> E. अ neg. संख्येय to be counted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=077-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असङ्ग|असंग|असंगः
असङ्ग mfn. (-ङ्गः-ङ्गा-ङ्गं) Solitary, unassociated.<BR> E. अ neg. सङ्ग with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=077-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असङ्गत|असंगत
असङ्गत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Uneven, unequal.<BR>	 2. Unattached.<BR>	 3. Unpre-<BR>ferred, disesteemed.<BR>	 4. Improbable, inconsistent.<BR>	 5. Unaccompa-<BR>nied, unassociated with.<BR> E. अ neg. सङ्गत connected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=077-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असङ्गति|असंगति|असंगतिः
असङ्गति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Improbability, incongruity.<BR>	 2. Not associating with.<BR>E. अ neg. सङ्गति congruity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=077-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असङ्गम|असंगम|असंगमः
असङ्गम m. (-मः)<BR>	 1. Separation, disunion.<BR>	 2. Inequality.<BR>	 3. Incongruity.<BR>4. Not associating with.<BR> E. अ neg. सङ्गम union.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=077-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असच्छास्त्र
असच्छास्त्र n. (-स्त्रं) Heretical or heterodox doctrine.<BR> E. असत् untrue, शास्त्र<BR>a scripture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=077-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असज्जन|असज्जनः
असज्जन m. (-नः) A wicked or contemptible person.<BR> E. असत् bad, जन a<BR>person.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=077-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंज्ञ
असंज्ञ mfn. (-ज्ञः-ज्ञा-ज्ञं) Insensible.<BR> E. अ neg. संज्ञा sign of life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=077-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असत्|असन्त्
असत् mfn. (-सन्-सती-सत्)<BR>	 1. Nonexistent, not being.<BR>	 2. Untrue, unreal.<BR>3. Bad, vile.<BR> E. अ neg. and सत् being, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=077-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असतायी
असतायी f. (-यी) Wickedness.<BR> E. असत् bad, ङीप् affix, and आय inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=077-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असती
असती f. (-ती) A disloyal or unchaste woman.<BR> E. अ neg. and सती vir-<BR>tuous, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=077-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असतीसुत|असतीसुतः
असतीसुत m. (-तः) A bastard.<BR> E. असती and सुत a son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=077-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असत्कर्म्मन्|असत्कर्मन्
असत्कर्म्मन् mfn. (-र्म्मा-र्म्मा-र्म्म) Wicked.<BR>	 n. (-र्म्म) Wickedness.<BR> E. असत् and कर्म्म<BR>act: also असत्कार्य्य, असत्क्रिया, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=077-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असत्कृत
असत्कृत mfn. (तः-ता-तं) Ill done, done from improper motives, or in an<BR>unbecoming manner.<BR> E. अ neg. सत् good, कृत done.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=077-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असत्ता
असत्ता f. (-त्ता)<BR>	 1. Nonexistence.<BR>	 2. Untruth.<BR>	 3. Wickedness.<BR> E. असत्<BR>and तल् added; also with त्व, असत्त्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=077-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असत्पथ|असत्पथः
असत्पथ m. (-थः)<BR>	 1. A bad road.<BR>	 2. Evil practice or doctrine.<BR> E. अ neg.<BR>सत् good, and पथिन् a road.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=077-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असत्परिग्रह|असत्परिग्रहः
असत्परिग्रह m. (-हः) Receiving unfit presents, or from improper per-<BR>sons.<BR> E. असत् and परिग्रह acceptance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=077-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असत्पुत्र|असत्पुत्रः
असत्पुत्र m. (-त्रः)<BR>	 1. A childless man.<BR>	 2. A wicked or disreputable son.<BR>E. असत् and पुत्र a son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=077-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असत्य|असत्यः
असत्य mfn. (-त्यः-त्या-त्यं)<BR>	 1. False, untrue.<BR>	 2. Lying, a liar.<BR>	 n. (-त्यं) Un-<BR>truth.<BR> E. अ neg. सत्य true.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=077-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असत्यवादिन्
असत्यवादिन् mfn. (-दी-दिनी-दि) A liar, speaking falsely, giving false evi-<BR>dence.<BR> E. असत्य and वादिन् who speaks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=077-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असत्यसन्ध|असत्यसंध
असत्यसन्ध mfn. (-न्धः-न्धा-न्धं) Treacherous, base, wicked.<BR> E. असत्य untrue,<BR>सन्धि combination, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=077-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असत्यसन्निभ
असत्यसन्निभ mfn. (-भः-भा-भं) Improbable, unlikely.<BR> E. असत्य and सन्निभ<BR>like.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=077-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असत्संसर्ग|असत्संसर्गः
असत्संसर्ग m. (-र्गः) Evil company.<BR> E. असत् wicked, and संसर्ग association.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=077-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असद्
असद् m. (-द् or -त्) A name of INDRA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=077-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असदध्येतृ
असदध्येतृ m. (-ता) A heterodox student.<BR> E. असत् untrue, bad, अधि before<BR>इङ् to go, to read or study, and तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=077-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असदाचार|असदाचारः
असदाचार mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Wicked, following evil practices.<BR>	 m. (-रः) Evil<BR>practice.<BR> E. असत् and आचार observance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=077-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असदाचारिन्
असदाचारिन् mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि) Wicked, vile, one who follows bad or<BR>heterodox practices.<BR> E. असदाचार and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=077-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असदृश|असदृशः
असदृश mfn. (-शः-शी-शं) Unlike, dissimilar.<BR> E. अ neg. सदृश like.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=077-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असद्ग्रह|असद्ग्रहः
असद्ग्रह m. (-हः) Caprice, idle or childish desire.<BR> E. अ neg. सत् good,<BR>wise, &c. and ग्रह what is taken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=077-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असद्भाव|असद्भावः
असद्भाव m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. An evil temperament or disposition.<BR>	 2. Nonexistence.<BR>E. असत् and भाव nature.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=077-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असद्वृत्ति|असद्वृत्तिः
असद्वृत्ति f. (-त्तिः)<BR>	 1. Low or degrading occupation or profession.<BR>	 2.<BR>Wickedness.<BR> E. असत् wicked, वृत्ति practice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=077-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असद्व्यवहार|असद्व्यवहारः
असद्व्यवहार mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Following evil practices.<BR>	 m. (-रः) Evil prac-<BR>tices.<BR> E. असत् and व्यवहार practice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=077-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असद्व्यवहारिन्
असद्व्यवहारिन् mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि) Following evil courses.<BR> E. असद्व्यवहार<BR>and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=077-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असन|असनं|असनः
असन m. (-नः) A tree, (Pentaptera tomentosa.)<BR>	 n. (-नं) Throwing, send-<BR>ing.<BR> E. अस to expel (disease), to send, to throw, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=077-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असनपर्णी
असनपर्णी f. (-र्णी) The name of a plant, (Marsilea quadrifolia.)<BR> E. असन<BR>and पर्ण a leaf; having leaves like the Asana.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=077-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असन्तति|असंतति|असन्ततिः
असन्तति mfn. (-तिः-तिः-ति) Childless.<BR>	 f. (-तिः) Want of posterity.<BR> E. अ<BR>neg.सन्तति descendants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=077-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असन्तान|असंतान|असन्तानः
असन्तान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Childless, having no posterity.<BR>	 m. (-नः) Want<BR>of posterity.<BR> E. अ neg. सन्तान progeny.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=077-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असन्तुष्ट|असंतुष्ट|असन्तुष्टः
असन्तुष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं) Displeased.<BR> E. अ neg. सन्तुष्ट pleased.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=077-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असन्तोष|असंतोष|असंतोषः
असन्तोष m. (-षः) Displeasure.<BR> E. अ neg. सन्तोष pleasure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=077-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असन्दिग्ध|असंदिग्ध
असन्दिग्ध mfn. (-ग्धः-ग्धा-ग्धं)<BR>	 1. Undoubted, unsuspected.<BR>	 2. Certain, confi-<BR>dent.<BR> E. अ neg. सन्दिग्ध doubted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=077-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असन्दिष्ट
असन्दिष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>	 1. Unapprised.<BR>	 2. Uncommunicated.<BR> E. अ neg.<BR>सन्दिष्ट informed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=077-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असन्धान|असंधान
असन्धान n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Want of an aim or object.<BR>	 2. Disjunction.<BR> E. अ neg.<BR>सन्धान holding together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=077-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असन्धि|असंधि|असंधिः
असन्धि f. (-न्धिः) Want of union or connection.<BR> E. अ neg. सन्धि junction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=077-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असन्धित|असंधित
असन्धित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Untied, unbound, at liberty, loose.<BR> E. अ neg.<BR>सन्धित tied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=077-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असन्नद्ध|असंनद्ध|असन्नद्धः
असन्नद्ध mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>	 1. Born, produced.<BR>	 2. Affecting knowledge, con-<BR>ceited as a Pandit or teacher.<BR>	 3. Proud.<BR>	 4. Unarmed.<BR> E. अ neg. सम्<BR>with, &c. नद्ध the part. past, of नह to bind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=077-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असन्निकर्ष|असंनिकर्ष|असंनिकर्षः
असन्निकर्ष m. (-र्षः)<BR>	 1. Non-perception of objects, not bringing them to<BR>the mind.<BR>	 2. Remoteness.<BR> E. अ neg. सन्निकर्ष attraction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=077-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असन्निकृष्ट|असंनिकृष्ट
असन्निकृष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>	 1. Unperceived, undistinguished.<BR>	 2. Remote,<BR>not near.<BR> E. अ neg. सन्निकृष्ट drawn near to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=077-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असन्निधि|असंनिधि|असंनिधिः
असन्निधि f. (-धिः)<BR>	 1. Absence, distance.<BR>	 2. Confidence, absence of doubt.<BR>E. अ neg. सन्निधि proximity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=077-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असन्निहित|असंनिहित
असन्निहित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Far, not near.<BR> E. अ neg. सन्निहित placed near.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=077-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असम्मान|असंमान|असम्मानं|असंमानः
असम्मान n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Disrespect.<BR>	 2. Impropriety.<BR> E. अ neg. सम्मान respect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=077-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असपिण्ड|असपिंड
असपिण्ड mfn. (-ण्डः-ण्डा-ण्डं) Unconnected by obsequial offerings.<BR> E. अ neg.<BR>सपिण्ड offering a common cake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=077-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असभ्य|असभ्यः
असभ्य mfn. (-भ्यः-भ्या-भ्यं)<BR>	 1. Unfit for an assembly.<BR>	 2. Vulgar, low.<BR> E. अ<BR>neg. सभ्य belonging to a company.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=077-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असम|असमः
असम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>	 1. Unequalled, individual, without a fellow or<BR>equal.<BR>	 2. Uneven, unequal either in surface or number.<BR>	 m. (-मः) A<BR>name of Buddha or a Buddha.<BR> E. अ neg. and सम like, same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=077-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असमक्ष
असमक्ष mfn. (-क्षः-क्षा-क्षं) Absent, not present or visible.<BR> E. अ neg. समक्ष<BR>before the eyes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=077-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असमग्र
असमग्र mfn. (-ग्रः-ग्रा-ग्रं) Part, partial, incomplete, unentire.<BR> E. अ neg. समग्र<BR>all.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=077-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असमञ्जस|असमंजस|असमञ्जसं
असमञ्जस mfn. (-सः-सा-सं) Unequal, unlike.<BR>	 n. (-सं) Unconformity, disparity,<BR>difference.<BR> E. अ neg. समञ्जस equal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=077-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असमय|असमयः
असमय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. Unseasonableness.<BR>	 2. Unfit or unfavourable time. E.<BR>अ neg. समय season.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=077-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असमवायिकारण|असमवायिकारणं
असमवायिकारण n. (-णं) (In logic,) Incidental cause, as the simple conjunc-<BR>tion of two different objects.<BR> E. असमवायिन् and कारण cause.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=077-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असमवायिन्
असमवायिन् mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि) Accidental, not inherent and inseparable.<BR>E. अ neg. समवाय intimate union, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=078-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असमर्थ|असमर्थः
असमर्थ mfn. (-र्थः-र्था-र्थं)<BR>	 1. Unable, incompetent.<BR>	 2. Feeble, weak.<BR> E. अ<BR>neg. समर्थ able.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=078-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असमर्पण
असमर्पण n. (-णं) Non-delivery, not committing or intrusting any thing to<BR>another.<BR> E. अ neg. समर्पण delivering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=078-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असमर्पित
असमर्पित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Unconsigned, unintrusted, undelivered.<BR> E. अ<BR>neg. समपित delivered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=078-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असमस्त
असमस्त mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं)<BR>	 1. Separate, several, uncollected, uncompounded.<BR>2. Incomplete, imperfect.<BR> E. अ neg. समस्त assembled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=078-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असमान|असमानं
असमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>	 1. Different.<BR>	 2. Unlike.<BR>	 3. Unequal.<BR> E. अ neg.<BR>समान same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=078-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असमापित
असमापित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Unfinished, unaccomplished.<BR> E. अ neg. समापित<BR>completed, simple.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=078-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असमाप्त|असमाप्तं
असमाप्त mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं) Unfinished, incomplete.<BR> E. अ neg. समाप्त finished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=078-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असमाप्ति
असमाप्ति f. (-प्तिः) Incompleteness.<BR> E. अ neg. समाप्ति completion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=078-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असमावर्त्तक|असमावर्तक|असमावर्तकः
असमावर्त्तक m. (-कः) A religious student, whose studies are not complet-<BR>ed.<BR> E. अ neg. समावर्त्तक who completes his course.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=078-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असमाहार|असमाहारः
असमाहार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Non-recovery of any thing.<BR>	 2. Disjunction, discon-<BR>nection.<BR> E. अ neg. सम् and आङ् before हृ to take, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=078-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असमाहार्य्य|असमाहार्य
असमाहार्य्य mfn. (-र्य्यः-र्य्या-र्य्यं) Irrecoverable.<BR>	 2. Not to be combined or<BR>united.<BR> E. अ neg. सम् and आङ् before हृ to take, ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=078-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असमीक्ष्य
असमीक्ष्य ind. Not having considered.<BR> E. अ neg. समीक्ष्य having seen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=078-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असमीक्ष्यकारिन्
असमीक्ष्यकारिन् mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि) Acting inconsiderately.<BR> E. असमीक्ष्य and<BR>कारिन् who acts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=078-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असमीचीन
असमीचीन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Improper, incorrect.<BR> E. अ neg. समीचीन proper,<BR>right.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=078-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असमृद्धि|असमृद्धिः
असमृद्धि mfn. (-द्धिः-द्धिः-द्धि) Unfortunate.<BR>	 f. (-द्धिः) Non-increase.<BR> E. अ neg.<BR>अमृद्धि increase.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=078-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असम्पत्ति|असंपत्ति|असंपत्तिः
असम्पत्ति f. (-त्तिः)<BR>	 1. Ill luck, non-increase.<BR>	 2. Non-accomplishment, fail-<BR>ure.<BR> E. अ neg. सम्पत्ति prosperity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=078-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असम्पन्न|असंपन्न
असम्पन्न mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं) Uneffected, unaccomplished.<BR> E. अ neg. सम्पन्न effected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=078-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असम्पर्क|असंपर्क
असम्पर्क mfn. (-र्कः-र्का-र्कं) Destitute of connexion or relation.<BR> E. अ neg.<BR>सम्पर्क connexion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=078-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असम्पर्कीय
असम्पर्कीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Unconnected with, not belonging to.<BR> E. अ neg.<BR>सम्पर्कीय related to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=078-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असम्पूर्ण|असंपूर्ण|असम्पूर्ण्ण
असम्पूर्ण mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-र्णं) Incomplete, not entire.<BR> E. अ neg. सम्पूर्ण complete.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=078-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असम्बद्ध|असंबद्ध|असम्बद्धं
असम्बद्ध mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>	 1. Unconnected, unmeaning, incoherent, (dis-<BR>course, &c.)<BR>	 2. Improper, wrong.<BR> E. अ neg. सम् with, and बध to bind,<BR>affix of the part. past.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=078-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असम्बन्ध|असंबंध|असंबन्ध|असंबन्धः
असम्बन्ध mfn. (-न्धः-न्धा-न्धं) Unconnected, not relating or belonging to.<BR> E. अ<BR>neg. सम्बन्ध connexion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=078-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असम्बाध|असंबाध
असम्बाध mfn. (-धः-धा-धं) Open, accessible.<BR>	 f. (-धा) A species of the Sarkari<BR>metre.<BR> E. अ neg. सम्बाध contracted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=078-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असम्भव|असंभव|असंभवः
असम्भव mfn. (-वः-वा-वं)<BR>	 1. Improbable, unlikely, inconsistent.<BR>	 2. Non-<BR>existent.<BR>	 nf. (-वं-वा)<BR>	 1. Any extraordinary event.<BR>	 2. Non existence. E.<BR>अ neg. सम्भव production.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=078-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असम्भावना|असंभावना
असम्भावना f. (-ना) Difficulty or impossibility of conceiving or comprehend-<BR>ing.<BR> E. अ neg. सम्भावना conception.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=078-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असम्भावनीय|असंभावनीय
असम्भावनीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Inconceivable, incomprehensible.<BR> E. अ neg.<BR>सम्भावनीय conceivable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=078-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असम्भूत|असंभूत
असम्भूत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Unproduced.<BR> E. अ neg. सम्भूत born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=078-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असम्भोग|असंभोग
असम्भोग m. (-गः) Non-enjoyment, not using or enjoying.<BR> E. अ neg. सम्भोग<BR>enjoyment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=078-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असम्भ्रम|असंभ्रम|असंभ्रमः
असम्भ्रम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं) Cool, composed.<BR>	 m. (-मः) Calmness, steadiness.<BR>E. अ neg. सम्भ्रम flurry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=078-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असम्मत|असंमत|असंमतः|असम्मतः
असम्मत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Dissentient, differing from.<BR>	 2. Averse, con-<BR>trary.<BR> E. अ neg. सम् with, मत minded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=078-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असम्मति|असंमति|असंमतिः
असम्मति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Dissent, difference of opinion.<BR>	 2. Dislike, aversion.<BR>E. अ neg. सम् with, मति mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=078-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असम्मान|असंमान|असम्मानं|असंमानः
असम्मान n. (-नं) Disrespect, disgrace.<BR> E. अ neg. सम् with, मान respect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=078-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असम्मूढ|असंमूढ
असम्मूढ mfn. (-ढः-ढा-ढं) Clear-seeing, judging well, cool, calm.<BR> E. अ neg.<BR>सम्मूढ beguiled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=078-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असम्मोह|असंमोह|असंमोहः
असम्मोह m. (-हः) Steadiness, calmness, composure.<BR> E. अ neg. सम्मोह fas-<BR>cination.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=078-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असम्यक्कारिन्
असम्यक्कारिन् mfn. (-रि-रिणी-रि)<BR>	 1. Inexpert, incompetent.<BR>	 2. Ill conduct-<BR>ed, profligate.<BR> E. अ neg. सम्यक् properly, कारिन् who does any thing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=078-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असम्यञ्च्|असम्यंच्
असम्यञ्च् mfn. (-म्यङ्-मीची-म्यक्)<BR>	 1. Improper, incorrect.<BR>	 2. Imperfect,<BR>incomplete.<BR> E. अ neg. सम्यञ्च् right.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=078-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असरु|असरुः
असरु m. (-रुः) The name of a medicinal plant, vulg. Kukursonga,<BR>(Conyza lacera.)<BR> E. अस to reject or be rejected, अरु affix; thrown<BR>away from its bad smell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=078-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असल|असलं
असल n. (-लं)<BR>	 1. Iron.<BR>	 2. Arms.<BR>	 3. A mantra.<BR> E. अस to be, लच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=078-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असवर्ण|असवर्ण्ण
असवर्ण mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-र्णं)<BR>	 1. Of a different caste.<BR>	 2. Of a different colour. E.<BR>अ neg. सवर्ण of one caste, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=078-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असह
असह mfn. (-हः-हा-हं) Impatient, intolerant, not enduring.<BR> E. अ neg. सह<BR>who bears.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=078-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असहन|असहनः
असहन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Unable to endure.<BR>	 m. (-नः) An enemy.<BR>	 n. (-नं) In-<BR>tolerance, impatience.<BR> E. अ neg. सह to bear, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=078-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असहनीय
असहनीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Unbearable, insufferable.<BR> E. अ neg. सहनीय to be<BR>borne; also असहितव्य and असह्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=078-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असहमान
असहमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Impatient, not bearing, not enduring.<BR> E. अ neg.<BR>सहमान bearing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=078-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असहाय
असहाय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Lonely, solitary, friendless.<BR> E. अ neg. सहाय an<BR>associate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=078-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असहायता
असहायता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Loneliness, solitude, the life of a hermit.<BR>	 2. Friend-<BR>lessness, being without a friend or patron.<BR> E. असहाय and तल् affix;<BR>also असहायत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=078-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असहित
असहित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Unassociated, unaccompanied.<BR> E. अ neg. सहित<BR>accompanied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=078-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असहिष्णु
असहिष्णु mfn. (-ष्णुः-ष्णुः-ष्णु) Impatient, unenduring.<BR> E. अ neg. and सहिष्णु<BR>bearing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=078-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असह्य|असह्यः
असह्य mfn. (-ह्यः-ह्या-ह्यं) Intolerable, unbearable.<BR> E. अ neg. सह्य to be<BR>borne.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=078-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असाक्षात्
असाक्षात् ind.<BR>	 1. Invisible, imperceptible.<BR>	 2. Not present.<BR> E. अ neg. साक्षात्<BR>before one's eyes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=078-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असाक्षिक
असाक्षिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Unattested, unwitnessed.<BR> E. अ neg. साक्षिन् a<BR>witness, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=078-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असाक्षिन्
असाक्षिन् mfn. (-क्षी-क्षिणी-क्षि) Incompetent as evidence.<BR> E. अ neg. साक्षिन् a<BR>witness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=078-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असाक्ष्य|असाक्ष्यं
असाक्ष्य n. (-क्ष्यं) Want of evidence, sufficient evidence.<BR> E. अ neg. साक्ष्य testi-<BR>mony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=078-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असात्म्य
असात्म्य mfn. (-त्म्यः-त्म्या-त्म्यं) Unwholesome, disagreeing with, (as food,<BR>&c.)<BR> E. अ neg. सात्म्य suitable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=078-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असाधन
असाधन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Without means.<BR>	 n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Non-accomplishment.<BR>2. Not proving or establishing.<BR> E. अ neg. and साधन implement or<BR>means.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=078-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असाधनीय
असाधनीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Unaccomplishable, not to be effected or com-<BR>pleted.<BR> E. अ neg. साधनीय to be effected; also असाध्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=078-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असाधारण|असाधारणं|असाधारणः
असाधारण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Special, specific, not common.<BR>	 n. (-णं)<BR>	 1.<BR>Speciality, species.<BR>	 2. Special property.<BR> E. अ neg. साधारण common.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=078-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असाधित
असाधित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Unaccomplished.<BR> E. अ neg. साधित accomplished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=078-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असाधु
असाधु mfn. (-धुः-धुः-ध्वी-धु) Wicked, bad.<BR>	 f. (-ध्वी) An unchaste wife.<BR> E. अ<BR>neg. साधु virtuous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=078-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असाधुता
असाधुता f. (-ता) Wickedness.<BR> E. असाधु and तल् affix; or with त्व, असाधुत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=078-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असाधुवृत्ता
असाधुवृत्ता f. (-त्ता) An unchaste woman.<BR> E. असाधु impurity, and वृत्त pro-<BR>fessed or practised.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=078-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असाध्य|असाध्यं
असाध्य mfn. (-ध्यः-ध्या-ध्यं)<BR>	 1. Not to be effected, not proper or able to be<BR>accomplished.<BR>	 2. Incurable, irremediable.<BR>	 3. Not susceptible of proof.<BR>E. अ neg. साध्य to be done.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=078-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असान्द्र|असान्द्रं
असान्द्र mfn. (-न्द्रः-न्द्रा-न्द्रं) Fine, delicate but with interstices.<BR> E. अ priv. and<BR>सान्द्र coarse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=079-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असामयिक
असामयिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Unseasonable.<BR> E. अ neg. समय time, ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=079-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असामान्य
असामान्य mfn. (-न्यः-न्या-न्यं) Peculiar, not common.<BR>	 n. (-न्यं) Peculiar or<BR>special property.<BR> E. अ neg. सामान्य common.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=079-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असाम्प्रतम्|असांप्रतम्
असाम्प्रतम् ind. Unfitly, improperly, inopportunely.<BR> E. अ priv. and साम्प्रतं<BR>fitly, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=079-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असाम्य|असाम्यं
असाम्य n. (-म्यं)<BR>	 1. Difference, dissimilarity.<BR>	 2. Unsuitableness, (in medicine<BR>or diet,) Unwholesomeness.<BR>	 3. Disagreeableness.<BR> E. अ neg. साम्य<BR>sameness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=079-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असार|असारं|असारः
असार mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>	 1. Sapless, pithless.<BR>	 2. Vain, unprofitable.<BR>	 3. Weak,<BR>feeble.<BR>	 n. (-रं) The castor oil tree.<BR> E. अ priv. and सार juice, sap, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=079-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असावधान
असावधान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Careless, inadvertent.<BR> E. अ neg. सावधान care-<BR>ful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=079-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असावधानता
असावधानता f. (-ता) Carelessness.<BR> E. तल् added to the last, or with त्व,<BR>असावधानत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=079-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असाहस|असाहसं
असाहस n. (-सं) Gentleness, absence of violence.<BR> E. अ neg. साहस violence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=079-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असाहसिक
असाहसिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Gentle, peaceable, not violent.<BR> E. अ neg.<BR>साहसिक violent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=079-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असाहाय्य
असाहाय्य n. (-य्यं) Want of assistance or cooperation.<BR> E. अ neg. साहाय्य<BR>alliance, friendship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=079-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असि|असिः
असि m. (-सिः) A sword, a scymitar.<BR> E. अस to cast, and इन् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=079-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असिक|असिकं
असिक n. (-कं) The part of the face between the under-lip and the chin.<BR>E. अस to throw, to shine, &c. and इकन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=079-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असिक्निका
असिक्निका f. (-का) A woman servant: see असिक्नी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=079-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असिक्नी
असिक्नी f. (-क्नी)<BR>	 1. A girl attending upon the inner or women's apart-<BR>ments.<BR>	 2. A river.<BR> E. अ neg. and सित white, because her hair is not<BR>whitened by age: क्न is substituted for त, and the affix is ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=079-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असिगण्ड|असिगण्डः
असिगण्ड m. (-ण्डः) A small pillow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=079-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असित|असितः
असित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Black or dark blue.<BR>	 m. (-तः)<BR>	 1. Black, (the colour.)<BR>2. A name of the planet Saturn.<BR>	 3. The dark fortnight of a lunar<BR>month.<BR>	 f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. The indigo-plant.<BR> E. अ neg. and सित white.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=079-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असिताभ्रशेखर|असिताभ्रशेखरः
असिताभ्रशेखर m. (-रः) A Jaina or Buddha saint.<BR> E. असित black, अभ्र a<BR>cloud, and शेखर a crest: cloud-crested.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=079-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असिताम्बुरुह
असिताम्बुरुह n. (-हं) The blue lotus.<BR> E. असित black or dark blue, and<BR>अम्बुरुह a lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=079-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असितार्चिस्|असितार्च्चिस्
असितार्चिस् m. (-र्चिः) A name of VAHNI or fire.<BR> E. असित dark, smoky,<BR>अचिस् a ray of light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=079-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असिताश्मन्
असिताश्मन् n. (-श्म)<BR>	 1. The lapis lazuli.<BR>	 2. Any black or dark blue stone.<BR>E. असित black, and अशमन् a stone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=079-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असितोत्पल|असितोत्पलं
असितोत्पल n. (-लं) The blue lotus.<BR> E. असित and उत्पल lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=079-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असितोपल
असितोपल n. (-लं) The lapis lazuli.<BR> E. असित blue, उपल stone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=079-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असिदंष्ट्र|असिदंष्ट्रः
असिदंष्ट्र m. (-ष्ट्रः) A marine monster, the Makara, considered as the<BR>emblem of KĀMADEVA.<BR> E. असि and दंष्ट्र a tooth: sword-toothed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=079-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असिदंष्ट्रक|असिदंष्ट्रकः
असिदंष्ट्रक m. (-कः) See the preceding. E. As before, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=079-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असिदन्त|असिदंत|असिदन्तः
असिदन्त m. (-न्तः) A crocodile: see मकर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=079-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असिधारा
असिधारा f. (-रा) The edge of a sword.<BR> E. असि and धारा edge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=079-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असिद्ध|असिद्धं|असिद्धः
असिद्ध mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>	 1. Unripe.<BR>	 2. Imperfect, incomplete.<BR>	 3. Unaccom-<BR>plished, uneffected.<BR>	 4. Unproven.<BR> E. अ neg. and सिद्ध perfect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=079-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असिद्धि|असिद्धिः
असिद्धि f. (-द्धिः)<BR>	 1. Failure, imperfect or incomplete accomplishment.<BR>	 2.<BR>(In logic,) Want of proof, conclusion not warranted by the premises.<BR>E. अ neg. सिद्धि completion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=079-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असिधाव|असिधावः
असिधाव m. (-वः) An armourer, a furbisher, a sword or tool cleaner. E.<BR>असि and धाव who polishes; to धाव clean, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=079-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असिधावक|असिधावकः
असिधावक m. (-कः) See the preceding.<BR> E. कन् added to the above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=079-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असिधेनु|असिधेनुः
असिधेनु f. (-नुः) A knife.<BR> E. असि and धेनु a bow; the sword-like bow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=079-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असिधेनुका
असिधेनुका f. (-का) See the preceding. E. As before.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=079-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असिपत्र|असिपत्रः
असिपत्र m. (-त्रः)<BR>	 1. The sugar-cane.<BR>	 2. A hell paved with swords.<BR>	 n. (-त्रं)<BR>1. A sheathe, a scabbard.<BR>	 2. The blade of a sword.<BR> E. असि and पत्र a<BR>leaf; sharp as a sword, or enclosing it.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=079-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असिपत्रक|असिपत्रकः
असिपत्रक m. (-कः) The sugar-cane. E. As the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=079-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असिपत्रवन|असिपत्रवनं
असिपत्रवन n. (-नं) A hell where the trees have leaves as sharp as swords.<BR>E. असि and पत्र a leaf, वन a wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=079-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असिपुच्छक|असिपुच्छकः
असिपुच्छक m. (-कः) The gangetic porpoise, (Delphinus gangeticus, Rox.)<BR>E. असि, पुच्छ a tail, and कन् affix; sword-tailed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=079-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असिपुत्रिका
असिपुत्रिका f. (-का) A knife.<BR> E. असि and पुत्रिका a daughter, an infant<BR>sword; from its smallness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=079-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असिपुत्री
असिपुत्री f. (-त्री) A knife. E. See the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=079-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असिमेद|असिमेदः
असिमेद m. (-दः) A fetid Mimosa: see विट्खदिर.<BR> E. असि and मेद marrow,<BR>essence; the plant being described with many thorns, and a decoc-<BR>tion of it being demulcent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=079-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असिहेति|असिहेतिः
असिहेति m. (-तिः) A swordsman or soldier armed with a sword.<BR> E. असि<BR>and हेति a weapon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=079-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असु|असुः
असु m. pl. always, (असवः) The five vital breaths or airs of the body.<BR>	 n.<BR>(-सु)<BR>	 1. Reflexion, thought, or the heart as the seat of it.<BR>	 2. Afflic-<BR>tion.<BR> E. अस to be, &c. and उ Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=079-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुकर
असुकर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Difficult, arduous.<BR> E. अ neg. सुकर easy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=079-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुक्षण|असुक्षणं
असुक्षण n. (-णं) See असूक्षण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=079-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुख|असुखं
असुख n. (-खं) Sorrow, pain, affliction, &c.<BR> E. अ neg. and सुख pleasure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=079-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुखावह
असुखावह mfn. (-हः-हा-हं) Producing unhappiness.<BR> E. असुख and आवह what<BR>bears.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=079-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुखिन्
असुखिन् mfn. (-खी-खिनी-खि) Unhappy, sorrowful, afflicted.<BR> E. असुख and<BR>इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=079-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुखोदय
असुखोदय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Causing or ending in unhappiness.<BR> E. असुख and<BR>उदय rising.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=079-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुखोदर्क
असुखोदर्क mfn. (-र्कः-र्का-र्कं) Productive of or ending in unhappiness. E.<BR>असुख and उदर्क subsequent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=079-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुगम
असुगम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>	 1. Difficult of attainment or accomplishment,<BR>hard, unattainable.<BR>	 2. Difficult to be understood.<BR> E. अ neg. सु easily,<BR>गम going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=079-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुत
असुत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Childless.<BR> E. अ neg. सुत a son, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=079-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुधारण|असुधारणं
असुधारण n. (-णं) Life, existence.<BR> E. असु vital air, and धारण possession.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=079-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुनिरस
असुनिरस mfn. (-सः-सा-सं) Disagreeable, unpleasant, offensive.<BR> E. अ neg.<BR>सुनिरस agreeable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=079-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुन्दर
असुन्दर mfn. (-रः-रा-री-रं)<BR>	 1. Plain, ugly.<BR>	 2. Improper, unbecoming.<BR> E. अ<BR>neg. सुन्दर handsome.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=079-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुभृत्
असुभृत् mfn. (-भृत्) Living, alive.<BR> E. असु and भृत् possessing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=079-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुमत्|असुमन्त्
असुमत् mfn. (-मान्-मती-मत्) Living, breathing.<BR>	 m. (-मान्) Life, the prin-<BR>ciple of vitality, the portion of spirit connected with the attributes<BR>of existence.<BR> E. असु vital air, मतुप् poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=079-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुर|असुरः
असुर mf. (-रः-रा) An Asura or demon: the Asuras are children of DITI<BR>by KAŚYAPA; they are demons of the first order, and in perpetual<BR>hostility with the gods.<BR>	 m. (-रः) The sun.<BR>	 f. (-रा)<BR>	 1. Night.<BR>	 2. A<BR>zodiacal sign.<BR>	 3. A prostitute.<BR>	 f. (-री)<BR>	 1. Black mustard, (Sinapis<BR>ramosa.)<BR>	 2. The wife of an Asura.<BR> E. अ neg. and मुर a deity; or अस्<BR>to send, to cast, &c. and उरन् Unādi affix, टाप् and ङीप् for the<BR>fem. or अ neg. and सुरा spirituous liquor, personified as a dam-<BR>sel produced at the churning of the ocean, who was rejected by the<BR>demons and received by the gods.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=079-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुरक्ष
असुरक्ष mfn. (-क्षः-क्षा-क्षं) Perishable, volatile, transitory.<BR> E. अ neg. सु easy<BR>रक्षा preservation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=079-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुरक्ष्य
असुरक्ष्य mfn. (-क्ष्यः-क्ष्या-क्ष्यं) Difficult of retention or preservation.<BR> E. अ<BR>neg. सु easily, रक्ष्य to be kept.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=079-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुररिपु|असुररिपुः
असुररिपु m. (-पुः) A name of VIṢṆU.<BR> E. असुर and रिपु an enemy, the foe<BR>of the Asuras.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=079-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुरसा
असुरसा f. (-सा) A sort of basil, (Ocymun pilosum.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=079-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुराह्व|असुराह्वं
असुराह्व n. (-ह्वं) Bell metal.<BR> E. असुर and आह्वा a name; named after an<BR>Asura; struck at seasons of worship, and deterring his approach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=079-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुर्क्षण|असुर्क्षणं
असुर्क्षण n. (-णं) See असूर्क्षण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=079-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुलभ
असुलभ mfn. (-भः-भा-भं) Difficult of attainment.<BR> E. अ neg. सुलभ easily got.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=079-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुसम|असुसमः
असुसम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं) Dearly beloved.<BR>	 m. (-मः)<BR>	 1. A husband.<BR>	 2. A<BR>lover.<BR> E. असु life, सम equal to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=080-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुस्थ|असुस्थः
असुस्थ mfn. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थं) Unwell, uncomfortable.<BR> E. अ neg. सुस्थ well.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=080-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुहृद्
असुहृद् m. (-हृत्) An enemy.<BR> E. अ neg. सुहृद् a friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=080-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असूक
असूक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Calumnious, scandalous, detracting, depreciating.<BR>E. असूञ् to calumniate, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=080-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असूक्षण|असूक्षणं
असूक्षण n. (-णं) Disrespect.<BR> E. अ implying modification, सूर्क्ष to disrespect,<BR>affix ल्युट्, the र is rejected; it is also written असुक्षण and असूर्क्षण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=080-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असूक्ष्म
असूक्ष्म mfn. (-क्ष्मः-क्ष्मा-क्ष्मं) Large, thick, gross.<BR> E. अ neg. सूक्ष्म fine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=080-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असूति|असूतिः
असूति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Non-production, obstruction, removal.<BR>	 2. Barrenness.<BR>E. अ neg. सूति bringing forth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=080-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असूयन|असूयनं
असूयन n. (-नं) Calumny, detraction.<BR> E. असूय to detract from, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=080-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असूया
असूया f. (-या)<BR>	 1. Calumny, detraction.<BR>	 2. The wife of the sage ATRI.<BR>E. असूञ् to detract from, a nominal root, and उक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=080-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असूयु|असूयुः
असूयु m. (-युः) Calumny.<BR> E. असूय to calumniate, उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=080-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असूर्क्षण
असूर्क्षण n. (-णं) Disrespect. E. See असूक्षण; it is also written असुर्क्षण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=080-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असूर्य्यम्पश्या|असूर्यम्पश्या|असूर्यंपश्या
असूर्य्यम्पश्या f. (-श्या) The wife of a king or a great man.<BR> E. अ neg. सूर्य्य the<BR>sun, and पश्या who sees; who never sees the sun being shut up in<BR>the Zenana.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=080-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असृक्कर|असृक्करः
असृक्कर m. (-रः) The juice or essence of the body, lymph, serum, &c. E.<BR>असृज् blood, and कर what makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=080-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असृक्प|असृक्पः
असृक्प mf. (-क्पः-क्पा) A Rākṣasa, an imp or goblin of malicious pro-<BR>pensities.<BR> E. असृज् blood, and प who drinks: these demons eat flesh,<BR>human or animal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=080-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असृक्पात|असृक्पातः
असृक्पात m. (-तः) Drops of blood, as from a wound.<BR> E. अमृज् and पात fal-<BR>ling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=080-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असृक्श्राव
असृक्श्राव m. (-वः) Bleeding, letting blood.<BR> E. असृज् and श्राव causing to<BR>flow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=080-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असृक्श्राविन्
असृक्श्राविन् mfn. (-वी-विणी-वि) Bleeding, who or what takes away blood.<BR>E. असृज् and श्राविन् what causes to flow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=080-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असृग्दरा
असृग्दरा f. (-रा) Irregular or excessive menstruation, mœnorrhagia. E.<BR>असृज्, दॄ to tear, affix अप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=080-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असृग्धरा
असृग्धरा f. (-रा) The skin.<BR> E. असृज् and धरा what contains: blood-con-<BR>taining; also असृग्धारा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=080-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असृग्धारा
असृग्धारा f. (-रा)<BR>	 1. The skin.<BR>	 2. A stream of blood.<BR> E. असृज् and धारा a<BR>stream.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=080-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असृग्वहा
असृग्वहा f. (-हा) A blood-vessel.<BR> E. असृज् and वह what bears.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=080-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असृज्विमोक्षण
असृज्विमोक्षण n. (-णं) Bleeding.<BR> E. असृज् and विमोक्षण letting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=080-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असृज्
असृज् n. (-सृक्) Blood.<BR> E. अ neg. सृज् to create, क्विप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=080-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असृपाट|असृपाटः
असृपाट mf. (-टः-टी) A stream of blood.<BR> E. अ neg. सृप् to go, काट aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=080-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असृष्ट
असृष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>	 1. Uncreated.<BR>	 2. Undistributed, not presented. E.<BR>अ neg. सृष्ट created, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=080-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असेचनक|असेचनकं
असेचनक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Charming, lovely.<BR> E. अ neg. सेचन satisfaction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=080-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असेवन
असेवन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Disregarding, neglecting.<BR>	 2. Avoiding, shunning.<BR>	 3.<BR>Disobedience, inattention.<BR> E. अ neg. सेवन service.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=080-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असेवा
असेवा f. (-वा)<BR>	 1. Avoiding, not following or practising.<BR>	 2. Disregard.<BR>	 3.<BR>Disobedience.<BR> E. अ neg. सेवा service: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=080-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असेवित
असेवित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Neglected, unattended to, disobeyed.<BR>	 2. Ab-<BR>stained from, disused.<BR> E. अ neg. सेवित served, used.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=080-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असेव्य
असेव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>	 1. Not to be served or attended to.<BR>	 2. Not to be<BR>used or practised, not to be eaten, drank, &c.<BR> E. अ neg. सेव्य to be<BR>followed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=080-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असौन्दर्य्य|असौन्दर्य
असौन्दर्य्य n. (-र्य्यं) Ugliness.<BR> E. अ neg. सौन्दर्य्य beauty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=080-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असौम्य
असौम्य mfn. (-म्यः-म्या-म्यं)<BR>	 1. Ugly, unlovely.<BR>	 2. Disagreeable, displeasing.<BR>E. अ neg. सौम्य pleasing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=080-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असौम्यस्वर|असौम्यस्वरः
असौम्यस्वर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Having a bad or croaking voice.<BR> E. असौम्य dis-<BR>agreeable, and स्वर a note or sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=080-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असौष्ठव|असौष्ठवं
असौष्ठव n. (-वं)<BR>	 1. Ugliness, deformity.<BR>	 2. Demerit, worthlessness.<BR> E. अ<BR>neg. सौष्ठव beauty, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=080-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्कन्न
अस्कन्न mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं) Permanent, durable.<BR> E. अ neg. स्कद to flow, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=080-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्खलित
अस्खलित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Firm, permanent, unshaken, unyielding.<BR>	 2.<BR>Not slipping or fallen.<BR>	 3. Undeviating.<BR> E. अ neg. स्खलित slipped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=080-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्त|अस्तं|अस्तः
अस्त Sautra root. 10th cl. (अस्तयति) To obscure or eclipse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=080-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्त|अस्तं|अस्तः
अस्त mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं)<BR>	 1. Thrown, cast.<BR>	 2. Sent, dispatched.<BR>	 3. Set, ob-<BR>scured.<BR>	 4. Removed, set aside.<BR>	 m. (-स्तः)<BR>	 1. The western mountain,<BR>behind which the sun is supposed to set.<BR>	 2. Sun-set.<BR>	 n. (-स्तं) Death,<BR>end.<BR> E. अस्त to obscure or eclipse, अच् affix, or अस to throw, &c. and<BR>क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=080-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्तक|अस्तकः
अस्तक m. (-कः) Beautitude, eternal felicity.<BR> E. अस्तम् disappearance, and<BR>कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=080-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्तगत
अस्तगत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Set, as the sun.<BR> E. अस्त and गत gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=080-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्तगिरि|अस्तगिरिः
अस्तगिरि m. (-रिः) The western mountain.<BR> E. अस्त and गिरि a mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=080-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्तब्ध
अस्तब्ध mfn. (-ब्धः-ब्धा-ब्धं) Unconfounded.<BR> E. अ neg. स्तब्ध astounded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=080-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्तब्धत्व
अस्तब्धत्व n. (-त्वं) Self-possession, not being confused or confounded.<BR> E. त्व<BR>added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=080-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्तम्
अस्तम् ind. Disappearance, setting, vanishing.<BR> E. अस् to send or cast, तम्<BR>aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=080-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्तमती
अस्तमती f. (-ती) A plant, (Hedysarum gangeticum:) see सालपर्णी.<BR> E. अस्तम्<BR>the mountain, and अत to go, अच् and ङीप् affixes; abounding in<BR>the west.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=080-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्तमयन
अस्तमयन n. (-नं) Disappearance, setting.<BR> E. अस्तम्, and अयन going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=080-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्तमित
अस्तमित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Set, (as the sun.)<BR> E. अस्तम् and इत gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=080-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्तवत्
अस्तवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>	 1. Obstructed, hindered, opposed.<BR>	 2. Set. E.<BR>अस्त thrown, &c. मतुप् poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=080-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्तव्यस्त
अस्तव्यस्त mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं) Confused, disordered, irrelevant.<BR> E. अस्त and व्यस्त<BR>scattered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=080-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्तसङ्ख्य|अस्तसंख्य
अस्तसङ्ख्य mfn. (-ङ्ख्यः-ङ्ख्या-ङ्ख्यं) Innumerable.<BR> E. अस्त gone, सङ्ख्या number.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=080-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्ताघ|अस्ताघः
अस्ताघ mfn. (-घः-घा-घं) Very deep: see अस्थाघ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=080-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्ताचल|अस्ताचलः
अस्ताचल m. (-लः) The western mountain.<BR> E. अस्त, and अचल a mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=080-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्ताद्रि|अस्ताद्रिः
अस्ताद्रि m. (-द्रिः) The western mountain.<BR> E. अस्त and अद्रि a mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=080-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्तावलम्बन|अस्तावलंबन
अस्तावलम्बन n. (-नं) The resting of a heavenly body on the western part<BR>of the horizon.<BR> E. अस्त and अवलम्बन depending.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=080-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्तावलम्बिन्
अस्तावलम्बिन् mfn. (-म्बी-म्बिनी-म्बि) Setting as the sun, on the point of<BR>setting.<BR> E. अस्त and अवलम्बिन् impending.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=080-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्ति|अस्तिः
अस्ति ind. Now being, existent, present.<BR> E. अस to be, and क्तिन् affix, or<BR>the third person sing. present tense, it is, used as a particle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=080-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्तिनास्ति
अस्तिनास्ति ind.<BR>	 1. Doubtful.<BR>	 2. Partly true and partly not.<BR> E. अस्ति and<BR>नास्ति it is not.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=080-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्तिनास्तित्व
अस्तिनास्तित्व n. (-त्वं)<BR>	 1. Uncertain or doubtful existence.<BR>	 2. Partial<BR>existence.<BR> E. त्व added to the last; also अस्तिनास्तिता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=080-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्तिमत्|अस्तिमन्त्
अस्तिमत् mfn. (-मान् मती-मत्) Wealthy, opulent.<BR> E. अस्ति what is, and मतुप्<BR>poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=080-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्तु
अस्तु ind. Be it so, let it be, implying assent, also reluctance and pain. E.<BR>अस to be, तुम् affix or the third person sing. imperative used as a<BR>particle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=080-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्तुत
अस्तुत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Not praised.<BR> E. अ neg. स्तुत praised.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=080-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्तेन
अस्तेन n. (-नं) Honesty.<BR> E. अ neg. स्तेन theft.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=080-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्तेय|अस्तेयं
अस्तेय n. (-यं) Honesty.<BR> E. अ neg. स्तेय theft.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=080-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्त्यान|अस्त्यानं
अस्त्यान n. (-नं) Reproach, blame.<BR> E. अ deteriorative and स्त्यै to sound,<BR>ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=080-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्त्र|अस्त्रं
अस्त्र n. (-स्त्रं)<BR>	 1. A weapon in general.<BR>	 2. A sword.<BR>	 3. A bow.<BR>	 4. A missile<BR>weapon.<BR> E. अस to throw, ष्ट्रन् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=080-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्त्रकण्टक|अस्त्रकंटक|अस्त्रकण्टकः
अस्त्रकण्टक m. (-कः) An arrow.<BR> E. अस्त्र and कण्टक a thorn, a thorn-like<BR>weapon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=080-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्त्रकारक|अस्त्रकारकः
अस्त्रकारक m. (-कः) An armourer.<BR> E. अस्त्र and कारक who makes: so<BR>अस्त्रकारः and अस्त्रकारिन् m. (-री.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=080-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्त्रचिकित्सक|अस्त्रचिकित्सकः
अस्त्रचिकित्सक m. (-कः) A surgeon.<BR> E. अस्त्र and चिकित्सक healing; who uses<BR>instruments as means of cure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=080-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्त्रचिकित्सा
अस्त्रचिकित्सा f. (-त्सा) Surgery.<BR> E. अस्त्र a knife, a lancet, and चिकित्सा<BR>healing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=080-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्त्रजीव|अस्त्रजीवः
अस्त्रजीव m. (-वः) A soldier, a warrior.<BR> E. अस्त्र a weapon, and जीव who<BR>lives by.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=081-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्त्रधारिन्
अस्त्रधारिन् m. (-री) A soldier.<BR> E. अस्त्र and धारिन् who bears; so अस्त्रधारक<BR>m. (-कः.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=081-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्त्रनिवारण
अस्त्रनिवारण n. (-णं) Guarding off a blow.<BR> E. अस्त्र and निवारण guarding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=081-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्त्रमार्ज्ज|अस्त्रमार्ज|अस्त्रमार्ज्जः
अस्त्रमार्ज्ज m. (-र्ज्जः) An armourer, a sword or tool cleaner.<BR> E. अस्त्र and<BR>मार्ज्ज who cleans, from मृज and अण् affix; also अस्त्रमार्ज्जक m. (-कः.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=081-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्त्रयुद्ध
अस्त्रयुद्ध m. (-द्धः) Fighting with weapons.<BR> E. अस्त्र and युद्ध battle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=081-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्त्रविद्या
अस्त्रविद्या f. (-द्या) The military science.<BR> E. अस्त्र and विद्या knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=081-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्त्रवेद|अस्त्रवेदः
अस्त्रवेद n. (-दं) The science of arms and war.<BR> E. अस्त्र a weapon, and वेद<BR>a Veda or scripture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=081-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्त्रसायक|अस्त्रसायकः
अस्त्रसायक m. (-कः) An iron arrow.<BR> E. अस्त्र, षो to destroy, वुन् affix; what<BR>destroys all other weapons.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=081-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्त्रहीन
अस्त्रहीन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Unarmed, defenceless.<BR> E. अस्त्र and हीन deprived of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=081-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्त्रागार|अस्त्रागारं|अस्त्रागारः
अस्त्रागार m. (-रः) An arsenal, an armoury.<BR> E. अस्त्र and आगार house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=081-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्त्राघात|अस्त्राघातः
अस्त्राघात m. (-तः) A wound, a cut.<BR> E. अस्त्र and आघात a blow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=081-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्त्राहत
अस्त्राहत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Struck, wounded, killed.<BR> E. अस्त्र and आहत<BR>struck.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=081-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्त्रीक
अस्त्रीक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Having no female.<BR> E. अ neg. स्त्री female, कन्<BR>added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=081-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थाग|अस्थागं
अस्थाग mfn. (-गः-गा-गं) Very deep.<BR> E. अ neg. स्था to stand, with क्विप्<BR>affix, and ग from गम to go; where there is no proceeding to an<BR>end; it is also written अस्ताग, अस्थाघ, अस्थान and अस्थार.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=081-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थाघ|अस्थाघं|अस्थाघः
अस्थाघ mfn. (-घः-घा-घं) See the preceding. E. As before, with घ, from<BR>हन् to kill or hurt, and अप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=081-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थान|अस्थानं
अस्थान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) See अस्थाग.<BR>	 n. (-नं) A place where there is no firm<BR>footing. adv. Unsuitably, unseasonably.<BR> E. अ neg. and स्थान<BR>stopping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=081-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थाने
अस्थाने ind. Unseasonably, inopportunely.<BR> E. अ neg. स्थाने in place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=081-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थाय|अस्थायं|अस्थायः
अस्थाय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) See अस्थाग; also अस्थाव and अस्थास.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=081-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थायिन्
अस्थायिन् mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि) Perishable, transient.<BR> E. अ neg. and स्थायिन्<BR>staying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=081-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थार|अस्थारं|अस्थारः
अस्थार mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) See अस्थाग.<BR> E. अस्था as above. and र from रा to<BR>obtain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=081-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थावर|अस्थावरं
अस्थावर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>	 1. Moveable, moving, not fixed.<BR>	 2. (In law)<BR>Personal, (as property,) money, cattle, &c. opposed to land.<BR> E. अ<BR>neg. स्थावर stable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=081-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थि
अस्थि n. (-स्थि) A bone.<BR> E. अस to throw, &c. and क्थिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=081-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थिक
अस्थिक n. (-कं) A bone.<BR> E. कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=081-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थिकृत्
अस्थिकृत् mfn. (-कृत्) Marrow.<BR> E. अस्थि a bone, and कृत् what makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=081-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थिज|अस्थिजः
अस्थिज m. (-जः) Marrow.<BR> E. अस्थि and ज what is produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=081-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थिज्ञ
अस्थिज्ञ m. (-ज्ञः) Marrow.<BR> E. अस्थि and ज्ञ what knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=081-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थिति|अस्थितिः
अस्थिति f. (-तिः) Want of place or condition, want of firm continuance.<BR>E. अ neg. स्थिति staying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=081-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थितुण्ड|अस्थितुंड|अस्थितुण्डः
अस्थितुण्ड mf. (-ण्डः-ण्डा) A bird.<BR> E. अस्थि and तुण्ड a mouth; whose<BR>mouth or beak is of bone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=081-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थितोद|अस्थितोदः
अस्थितोद m. (-दः) Pain in the bones.<BR> E. अस्थि and तोद torturing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=081-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थित्वच्
अस्थित्वच् f. (-त्वक्) The periosteum.<BR> E. अस्थि and त्वच् skin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=081-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थिधन्वन्
अस्थिधन्वन् m. (-न्वा) A name of ŚIVA.<BR> E. अस्थि, धनु a bow, and अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=081-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थिपञ्जर|अस्थिपंजर|अस्थिपञ्जरः
अस्थिपञ्जर m. (-रः) A skeleton.<BR> E. अस्थि and पञ्जर a cage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=081-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थिभक्ष|अस्थिभक्षः
अस्थिभक्ष m. (-क्षः) A dog.<BR> E. अस्थि and भक्ष who eats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=081-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थिभङ्ग|अस्थिभंग|अस्थिभङ्गः
अस्थिभङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>	 1. Fracture.<BR>	 2. A plant of supposed efficacy in<BR>fractures, (Cissus quadrangularis.)<BR> E. अस्थि and भङ्ग a breaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=081-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थिभुज्
अस्थिभुज् m. (-भुक्) A dog.<BR> E. अस्थि a bone, भुज् who eats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=081-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थिभेद|अस्थिभेदः
अस्थिभेद m. (-दः)<BR>	 1. Fracturing, breaking or wounding a bone.<BR>	 2. A<BR>sort of bone, a bone.<BR> E. अस्थि and भेद breaking, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=081-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थिभेदक|अस्थिभेदकः
अस्थिभेदक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) A bone-breaker, who or what breaks bones.<BR>E. अस्थि and भेदक what breaks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=081-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थिमत्|अस्थिमन्त्
अस्थिमत् mfn. (-मान्-मती-मत्) Having bones, vertebrated, &c.<BR> E. अस्थि and<BR>मतुप् poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=081-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थिमाला
अस्थिमाला f. (-ला) A necklace of bones.<BR> E. अस्थि and माला a garland.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=081-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थिमालिन्
अस्थिमालिन् m. (-ली) A name of ŚIVA.<BR> E. अस्थि a bone, माला a garland, इनि<BR>affix; ŚIVA is commonly represented with a necklace of skulls.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=081-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थिर|अस्थिरः
अस्थिर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>	 1. Trembling, shaken, unsteady.<BR>	 2. Uncertain,<BR>unascertained.<BR>	 3. Unworthy of confidence.<BR> E. अ neg. and स्थिर firm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=081-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थिरता
अस्थिरता f. (-ता) Unsteadiness, fickleness, mutability.<BR> E. अस्थिर and तल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=081-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थिरत्व
अस्थिरत्व n. (-त्वं) Unsteadiness, mutability.<BR> E. अस्थिर and त्व aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=081-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थिवत्
अस्थिवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Bony, osseous.<BR> E. अस्थि and वतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=081-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थिविग्रह|अस्थिविग्रहः
अस्थिविग्रह m. (-हः) A name of BHRINGI, one of ŚIVA'S attendants.<BR> E. अस्थि<BR>and विग्रह a part, &c. who carries ŚIVA'S decorations.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=081-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थिशोष|अस्थिशोषः
अस्थिशोष m. (-षः) Dryness and decay of the bones.<BR> E. अस्थि and शोष dry-<BR>ing up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=081-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थिसंहार|अस्थिसंहारः
अस्थिसंहार m. (-रः) A plant, a species of turnsole, (Heliotropium indicum:)<BR>see हस्तिशुण्डी<BR> E. अस्थि and सं before हृ to take, to collect, seize, &c.<BR>(it is an ingredient in philtres, &c.) घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=081-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थिसंहारक|अस्थिसंहारकः
अस्थिसंहारक m. (-कः) The adjutant bird.<BR> E. अस्थि and संहारक who seizes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=081-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थिसञ्चय|अस्थिसंचय|अस्थिसंचयः
अस्थिसञ्चय m. (-यः) Collecting the bones or their ashes after burning a<BR>corpse.<BR> E. अस्थि and सञ्चय assemblage; also अस्थिसञ्चयनं<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=081-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थिसन्धि|अस्थिसंधि|अस्थिसन्धिः
अस्थिसन्धि f. (-न्धिः)<BR>	 1. A joint, and articulation.<BR>	 2. Uniting of a broken<BR>bone.<BR> E. अस्थि and सन्धि connection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=081-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थिसमर्पण
अस्थिसमर्पण n. (-णं) Throwing the bones of a dead body into the Ganges.<BR>E. अस्थि and समर्पण consigning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=081-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थिसार|अस्थिसारः
अस्थिसार m. (-रः) Marrow.<BR> E. अस्थि bone, and सार essence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=081-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थिस्थूण|अस्थिस्थूणः
अस्थिस्थूण m. (-णः) The body, or that of which the bones are the sup-<BR>porters.<BR> E. अस्थि and स्थूण a post.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=081-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थूल
अस्थूल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Small, delicate.<BR> E. अ neg. स्थूल gross.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=081-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थैर्य्य|अस्थैर्य|अस्थैर्य्यं
अस्थैर्य्य n. (-र्य्यं) Instability, unsteadiness.<BR> E. अ neg. सथैर्य्य steadiness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=081-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्निग्ध
अस्निग्ध mfn. (-ग्धः-ग्धा-ग्धं)<BR>	 1. Harsh, hard, dry.<BR>	 2. Harsh, unkind.<BR> E. अ neg.<BR>and स्निग्ध unctuous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=081-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्नेह|अस्नेहः
अस्नेह mfn. (-हः-हा-हं)<BR>	 1. Harsh, unkind.<BR>	 2. Harsh, hard, dry.<BR>	 m. (-हः)<BR>	 1.<BR>Unkindness, want of affection.<BR>	 2. Absence of oiliness.<BR> E. अ neg. स्नेह<BR>affection, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=081-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्पर्श|अस्पर्शः
अस्पर्श mfn. (-र्शः-र्शा-र्शं) What does not touch or is not touched.<BR>	 m. (-र्शः)<BR>Not touching, non-contact.<BR> E. अ neg. स्पर्श contact.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=081-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्पर्शन|अस्पर्शनं
अस्पर्शन n. (-नं) Non-contact, avoiding the contact of any thing or per-<BR>son, especially of one who is impure.<BR> E. अ neg. स्पर्शन touching.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=081-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्पर्शनीय
अस्पर्शनीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Impure, not to be touched.<BR> E. अ neg. स्पर्शनीय<BR>to be touched.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=081-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्पर्शित
अस्पर्शित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Untouched.<BR> E. अ neg. स्पर्शित touched.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=081-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्पष्ट|अस्पष्टं
अस्पष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं) Indistinct.<BR> E. अ neg. and स्पष्ट clear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=081-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्पृश्य
अस्पृश्य mfn. (-श्यः-श्या-श्यं) Not to be touched.<BR> E. अ neg. स्पृश्य tangible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=081-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्पृष्ट
अस्पृष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं) Untouched.<BR> E. अ neg. स्पृष्ट touched.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=081-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्पृष्टि|अस्पृष्टिः
अस्पृष्टि f. (-ष्टिः) Not touching, avoiding contact.<BR> E. अ neg. स्पृष्टि touching.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=081-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्पृह
अस्पृह mfn. (-हः-हा-हं) Undesirous, content, indifferent.<BR> E. अ neg. स्पृहा<BR>desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=081-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्पृहणीय
अस्पृहणीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Undesirable.<BR> E. अ neg. स्पृहणीय desirable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=081-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्फुट|अस्फुटं
अस्फुट n. (-टं) Indistinct speech.<BR>	 mfn. (-टः-टा-टं)<BR>	 1. Indistinct, obscure.<BR>2. Invisible.<BR>	 3. Unblown.<BR> E. अ neg. and स्फुट open, clear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=081-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्फुटफल
अस्फुटफल n. (-लं)<BR>	 1. Indistinct result.<BR>	 2. (In Geometry,) Gross area of a<BR>triangle, &c.<BR> E. अस्फुट and फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=081-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्फुटवाच्
अस्फुटवाच् mfn. (-वाक्) Lisping, speaking indistinctly.<BR> E. अस्फुट and वाच् who speaks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=081-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्मद्
अस्मद् First person pronoun, (अहं) I. (आवां) We two. (वयं) We.<BR> E. अस to<BR>be, and मदिक् Unādi affix: the inflexions of this pronoun are very<BR>irregular.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=081-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्मदीय
अस्मदीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Our, ours.<BR> E. अस्मद् I, and छ affix in the sense of<BR>the second case plur.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=081-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्मन्त|अस्मंतं|अस्मन्तं
अस्मन्त n. (-न्तं) A furnace or fireplace: see अश्मन्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=081-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्मरण|अस्मरणं
अस्मरण n. (-णं) Forgetfulness, forgetting.<BR> E. अ neg. स्मरण remembering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=081-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्मरणीय
अस्मरणीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Not to be recollected.<BR> E. अ neg. स्मरणीय to be<BR>remembered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=081-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्मार्त्त|अस्मार्त
अस्मार्त्त mfn. (-र्त्तः-र्त्ती-र्त्तं)<BR>	 1. Immemorial, not within memory.<BR>	 2. Illegal,<BR>not according to law.<BR>	 3. Not belonging to Hindu institutes.<BR> E. अ<BR>neg. स्मार्त्त relating to law, &c. from स्मृति with अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=082-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्मृत
अस्मृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Forgotten.<BR> E. अ neg. स्मृत remembered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=082-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्मृति|अस्मृतिः
अस्मृति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Want of memory, forgetfulness.<BR>	 2. Not being part of<BR>the institutes.<BR> E. अ neg. स्मृति memory or code of law.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=082-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्व|अस्वः
अस्व mfn. (-स्वः-स्वा-स्वं) Not one's own.<BR> E. अ neg. स्व own.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=082-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्वक
अस्वक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Not one's own, belonging to another.<BR> E. अ neg.<BR>स्वक own.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=082-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्वकीय
अस्वकीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Not one's own, belonging to another.<BR> E. अ neg.<BR>स्वकीय own.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=082-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्वच्छ
अस्वच्छ mfn. (-च्छः-च्छा-च्छं) Opaque, not clear.<BR> E. अ neg. स्वच्छ clear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=082-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्वच्छन्द|अस्वच्छंद|अस्वच्छन्दः
अस्वच्छन्द mfn. (-न्दः-न्दा-न्दं)<BR>	 1. Docile.<BR>	 2. Dependent.<BR> E. अ priv. स्व own,<BR>and च्छन्द intention; not self-willed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=082-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्वजाति
अस्वजाति mfn. (-तिः-तिः-ति)<BR>	 1. Of a different caste.<BR>	 2. Of a different<BR>species.<BR> E. अ neg. स्व own, जाति caste.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=082-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्वतन्त्र|अस्वतंत्र|अस्वतन्त्रः
अस्वतन्त्र mfn. (-न्त्रः-न्त्रा-न्त्रं)<BR>	 1. Docile, humble.<BR>	 2. Dependent, subject. E.<BR>अ neg. स्वतन्त्र self-willed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=082-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्वत्व|अस्वत्वं
अस्वत्व n. (-त्वं) Want of claim or right to any thing, having no<BR>indefeasible property in it, absence of ownership.<BR> E. अ neg. स्व<BR>own, with त्व affix: also with तल्, अस्वता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=082-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्वन्त|अस्वंत|अस्वन्तः
अस्वन्त mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं)<BR>	 1. Ending ill, leading to or having an<BR>unfavourable close.<BR>	 2. Approaching the end of life.<BR>	 m. (-न्तः) A<BR>fire place: see अश्वन्त.<BR> E. अ neg. and सु good, or असु breath, and<BR>अन्त end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=082-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्वप्न|अस्वप्नः
अस्वप्न m. (-प्नः) A deity.<BR> E. अ neg. and स्वप्न sleep; who never sleeps.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=082-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्वभाव|अस्वभावः
अस्वभाव m. (-वः) Unnatural or unusual character or temperament.<BR>	 mfn.<BR>(-वः-वा-वं) Of a different nature.<BR> E. अ neg. स्वभाव nature.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=082-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्वर|अस्वरः
अस्वर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Having a bad or croaking voice.<BR> E. अ neg. and<BR>स्वर a note or the voice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=082-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्वरूप
अस्वरूप mfn. (-पः-पा-पं) Essentially different or unlike.<BR> E. अ neg. स्वरूप of<BR>one nature.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=082-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्वर्ग्य
अस्वर्ग्य mfn. (-र्ग्यः-र्ग्या-र्ग्यं) Not leading to heaven.<BR> E. अ neg. स्वर्ग्य para-<BR>disiacal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=082-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्वस्थ
अस्वस्थ mfn. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थं)<BR>	 1. Unwell, indisposed.<BR>	 2. Unfortunate,<BR>badly off.<BR> E. अ neg. स्वस्थ being well happy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=082-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्वादु
अस्वादु mfn. (-दुः-दुः-दु) Tasteless, insipid.<BR> E. अ neg. स्वादु sapid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=082-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्वाध्याय|अस्वाध्यायः
अस्वाध्याय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. A Brahman who has not made his studies, who<BR>has not read the Vedas previous to his investiture.<BR>	 2. Interrup-<BR>tion or interval of study, prohibited on certain days of the<BR>moon, at eclipses, &c.<BR> E. अ neg. स्व own, and अध्याय a lecture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=082-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्वामिक|अस्वामिकं
अस्वामिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Unowned, unclaimed.<BR> E. अ neg. स्वामिन् a mas-<BR>ter, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=082-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्वामिन्
अस्वामिन् mfn. (-मी-मिनी-मि)<BR>	 1. Having no right or title to any thing,<BR>not being master of it.<BR>	 2. That which has no master or owner.<BR>E. अ neg. स्वामिन् a master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=082-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्वामिविक्रय|अस्वामिविक्रयः
अस्वामिविक्रय m. (-यः) Sale without ownership.<BR> E. अ neg. स्वामिन् a master,<BR>&c. विक्रय sale.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=082-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्वाम्य|अस्वाम्यं
अस्वाम्य n. (-म्यं) Absence or right or title to property.<BR> E. अ neg. स्वाम्य<BR>ownership.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=082-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्वार्थ
अस्वार्थ mfn. (-र्थः-र्था-र्थं)<BR>	 1. Not for one's self.<BR>	 2. Not for a proper object.<BR>3. Having a different meaning.<BR> E. अ neg. स्व own, अर्थ end or sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=082-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्वास्थ्य|अस्वास्थ्यं
अस्वास्थ्य n. (-स्थ्यं) Indisposition, discomfort, indigence.<BR> E. अ neg. स्वास्थ्य<BR>well-being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=082-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्वीकार
अस्वीकार m. (-रः) Dissent, non-acquiescence.<BR> E. अ neg. स्वीकार promise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=082-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्वीकृत
अस्वीकृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Dissented from, refused, not promised.<BR> E. अ<BR>neg. स्वीकृत promised.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=082-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्वेद
अस्वेद m. (-दः) Suppressed perspiration.<BR> E. अ neg. स्वेद sweat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=082-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्र|अस्रं|अस्रः
अस्र m. (-स्रः)<BR>	 1. A corner, an angle.<BR>	 2. Hair.<BR>	 n. (-स्रं)<BR>	 1. Blood.<BR>	 2. A<BR>tear.<BR> E. अस to cast or throw, &c. affix रक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=082-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्रकण्ठ|अस्रकंठ|अस्रकण्ठः
अस्रकण्ठ m. (-ण्टः) An arrow.<BR> E. अस्र and कण्ठ throat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=082-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्रज|अस्रजं
अस्रज n. (-जं) Flesh.<BR> E. अस्र blood, and ज produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=082-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्रजित्
अस्रजित् m. (-जित्) A plant, commonly Kabātabentu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=082-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्रप|अस्रपः
अस्रप mf. (-पः-पा) A Rākṣasa or goblin.<BR>	 f. (-पा) A leech.<BR> E. अस्र blood,<BR>and प who drinks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=082-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्रपित्त
अस्रपित्त n. (-त्तं) Plethora, hœmorrhage, epistaxis, involuntary dis-<BR>charge of blood from the mouth, nostrils, anus, &c.<BR> E. अस्र and<BR>पित्त bile: both humors being supposed to be affected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=082-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्रमातृका
अस्रमातृका f. (-का) Chyle, chyme.<BR> E. अस्र blood, मातृ the parent, कन् affix<BR>of similitude.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=082-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्ररोधिनी
अस्ररोधिनी f. (-नी) A plant, (Mimosa pudica.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=082-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्रार्ज्जक|अस्रार्जक|अस्रार्जकः|अस्रार्ज्जकः
अस्रार्ज्जक m. (-कः) The white Tulasi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=082-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्रि|अस्रिः
अस्रि f. (-स्रिः) Ten millions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=082-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्रु
अस्रु n. (-स्रु) A tear.<BR> E. अत to cast or reject, and रु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=082-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्रुव
अस्रुव n. (-वं) A granulation, (of flesh.)<BR> E. अ neg. स्रु to distil, अप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=082-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अह|अहं|अहः
अह r. 5th cl. (अहति) To pervade or occupy. (इ) अहि r. 1st. cl. (अंहते) To<BR>go or move: also 10th cl. (अंहयति) To shine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=082-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अह|अहं|अहः
अह ind. A particle and interjection implying; 1. Commendation: 2.<BR>Rejecting, sending: 3. Deviation from custom, (improperly:)<BR>	 4.<BR>Certainty, ascertainment.<BR> E. अ neg. ह from हन् to hurt, affix ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=082-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहंयु|अहंयुः
अहंयु mfn. (-युः-युः-यु) Proud.<BR>	 m. (-युः) A warrior.<BR> E. अहम् I, and युस्<BR>affix: self-opinioned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=082-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहःपति|अहःपतिः
अहःपति m. (-तिः) The sun.<BR> E. अहन् a day, and पति a master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=082-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहःशेष|अहःशेषः
अहःशेष n. (-षं) Evening.<BR> E. अहन् and शेष end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=082-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहङ्कार|अहंकार|अहङ्कारः
अहङ्कार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Pride.<BR>	 2. Individuality, sense of self.<BR>	 3. One of the<BR>elements of creation, consciousness, individualization.<BR> E. अहम् 1,<BR>and कार what makes; thinking highly of one's self.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=082-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहङ्कारवत्|अहंकारवत्|अहंकारवन्त्
अहङ्कारवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Proud.<BR> E. अहङ्कार pride, मतुप् poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=082-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहङ्कारिन्|अहंकारिन्
अहङ्कारिन् mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि) Proud, self-important.<BR> E. अहङ्कार and इनि<BR>poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=082-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहङ्कृत|अहंकृत
अहङ्कृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Proud.<BR> E. अहम् I, and कृत made: see अहङ्कार.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=082-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहङ्कृति|अहंकृति|अहङ्कृतिः
अहङ्कृति f. (-तिः) Pride.<BR> E. अहम् and कृति action: see अहङ्कार.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=082-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहत|अहतं
अहत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Unhurt, uninjured, not struck or killed.<BR>	 2.<BR>Unblemished, unsoiled.<BR>	 n. (-तं) New clothes.<BR> E. अ neg. and हत hurt,<BR>part. past of हन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=082-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहन्
अहन् m. (-हः) A day.<BR> E. अ neg. हा to leave, and कनिन् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=082-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहननीय
अहननीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Not to be killed.<BR> E. अ neg. हननीय to be killed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=082-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहन्तव्य
अहन्तव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं) Not to be killed.<BR> E. अ neg. हन्तव्य to be killed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=082-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहमहमिका
अहमहमिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. Military vaunting.<BR>	 2. Assertion or conceit of<BR>superiority, boasting, egotism.<BR> E. अहम् I, reiterated, क and टाप्<BR>affixed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=082-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहम्पूर्व्विका|अहम्पूर्विका|अहंपूर्विका
अहम्पूर्व्विका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. Emulative onset, the running forward of soldiers<BR>with emulation.<BR>	 2. Conceit, vaunting.<BR> E. अहम् I, पूर्व्व first; affixes<BR>as in the last; I will be foremost.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=082-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहम्मति|अहंमति|अहम्मतिः
अहम्मति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Spiritual ignorance.<BR>	 2. Conceit.<BR>	 3. Self-love.<BR> E. अहम्<BR>and मति understanding; self-love, or worldly mindedness, opposed<BR>to abstract meditation on the deity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=082-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहरणीय
अहरणीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Not to be taken away.<BR> E. अ neg. हरणीय to be<BR>taken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=082-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहरहर्
अहरहर् ind. Daily, day by day.<BR> E. अहन् repeated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=082-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहर्गण|अहर्गणः
अहर्गण m. (-णः)<BR>	 1. A month.<BR>	 2. Any calculated term.<BR> E. अहन् a day,<BR>and गण a number or class.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=082-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहर्निशम्
अहर्निशम् ind. Day and night.<BR> E. अहन् day, निशा night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=082-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहर्पति|अहर्पतिः
अहर्पति m. (-तिः) The sun.<BR> E. अहन् and पति a master; also अहःपति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=082-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहर्बान्धव|अहर्बान्धवः|अहर्ब्बान्धवः
अहर्बान्धव m. (-वः) The sun.<BR> E. अहन् and बान्धव a friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=082-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहर्मणि|अहर्मणिः|अहर्म्मणिः
अहर्मणि m. (-णिः) The sun.<BR> E. अहन् and मणि a gem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=082-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहर्मुख|अहर्मुखं
अहर्मुख n. (-खं) Morning, the dawn.<BR> E. अहन् and मुख the commence-<BR>ment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=082-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहल
अहल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Unploughed, unfurrowed.<BR> E. अ neg. हलि a furrow,<BR>अच् affix: also with the final unchanged, अहलि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=082-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहल्य|अहल्यः
अहल्य mfn. (-ल्यः-ल्या-ल्यं) Unploughed, (a field, &c.)<BR>	 f. (-ल्या)<BR>	 1. The name<BR>of an Apsaras or heavenly courtezan.<BR>	 2. The wife of GAUTAMA, a<BR>saint and philosopher.<BR> E. अ neg. हल to plough, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=083-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहर्ष
अहर्ष mfn. (-र्षः-र्षा-र्षं) Unhappy, gloomy, sorrowful.<BR> E. अ neg. हर्ष happi-<BR>ness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=083-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहर्षित
अहर्षित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Unhappy, sorrowful.<BR> E. अ neg. हर्षित rejoiced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=083-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहवनीय
अहवनीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>	 1. Not to be offered, not fit or proper to be<BR>sacrificed.<BR> E. अ neg. हवनीय to be offered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=083-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहस्कर|अहस्करः
अहस्कर m. (-रः) The sun.<BR> E. अहन् and कर who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=083-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहस्पति|अहस्पतिः
अहस्पति m. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. The sun.<BR>	 2. Swallow wort.<BR> E. अहन् and पति<BR>master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=083-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहह
अहह ind. A particle or interjection, as ah! aha! &c. implying: 1.<BR>Surprise: 2. Fatigue: 3. Pain: 4. Pleasure: 5. Calling.<BR> E. अह<BR>from अहम् I, and ह from हा to abandon: self or pride-abandon-<BR>ment; also अहहा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=083-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहहा
अहहा ind. See the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=083-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहार्य्य|अहार्य|अहार्यः|अहार्य्यं|अहार्य्यः
अहार्य्य mfn. (-र्य्यः-र्य्या-र्य्यं) Not to be stolen or taken away.<BR>	 m. (-र्य्यः) A<BR>mountain.<BR> E. अ neg. and हार्य्य future part. of हृञ् to take or con-<BR>vey.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=083-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहार्य्यत्व|अहार्यत्व
अहार्य्यत्व n. (-त्वं) Security, not being liable to be stolen or taken away.<BR>E. अहार्य्य and त्व affix; also अहार्य्यता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=083-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहि|अहिः
अहि m. (-हिः)<BR>	 1. A snake or serpent.<BR>	 2. The sun.<BR>	 3. A traveller.<BR>	 4.<BR>Lead.<BR>	 5. The name of a demon: see वृत्रासुर.<BR>	 6. A name of RĀHU,<BR>the ascending node.<BR> E. आङ् prefixed to हन् to hurt, इन् Unādi affix;<BR>injuring all or every thing, the आ of आङ् is made short.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=083-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहिंसक
अहिंसक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Harmless, innocuous.<BR> E. अ neg. हिंसक mis-<BR>chievous: so अहिंस्र and अहिंस्रक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=083-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहिंसा
अहिंसा f. (-सा) Harmlessness, doing injury to nothing, one of the car-<BR>dinal virtues of most Hindu sects, but particularly of the Baud-<BR>dhas and Jainas.<BR> E. अ neg. हिंसा hurt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=083-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहिंसित
अहिंसित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Uninjured.<BR> E. अ neg. हिंसित hurt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=083-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहिंस्र|अहिंस्रः
अहिंस्र mfn. (-स्रः-स्रा-स्रं) Innocuous, innocent, harmless.<BR>	 f. (-स्रा) The name<BR>of a plant, commonly Kurkavali: see कर्कटा.<BR> E. अ neg. and हिंस्रा in-<BR>jurious: than which there is none more so.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=083-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहिका
अहिका f. (-का) The silk-cotton tree, (Bombax heptaphyllum.)<BR> E. अ<BR>neg. and हा to go or abandon, ङिक् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=083-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहिकान्त|अहिकांत|अहिकान्तः
अहिकान्त m. (-न्तः) Air, wind.<BR> E. अहि a serpent, and कान्त beloved;<BR>snakes being supposed to feed upon air.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=083-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहिच्छत्र|अहिच्छत्रः
अहिच्छत्र m. (-त्रः)<BR>	 1. The name of a country.<BR>	 2. A milky or thorny<BR>plant: see मेषशृङ्गी.<BR>	 f. (-त्रा)<BR>	 1. Sugar.<BR>	 2. A city.<BR> E. अहि a snake,<BR>and छत्र a parasol.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=083-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहिजित्
अहिजित् m. (-जित्)<BR>	 1. A name of KṚṢṆA.<BR>	 2. Also of INDRA.<BR> E. अहि<BR>and जित् who conquers, from जि with क्विप् affix; subduing a demon<BR>in the form of a snake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=083-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहित|अहितः
अहित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Hostile, inimical.<BR>	 2. Hurtful, prejudicial.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-तः) An enemy.<BR>	 n. (-तं) Food, &c. contraindicated in a disease.<BR>E. अ neg. and हित friendly, fit, proper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=083-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहितकारिन्
अहितकारिन् mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि) Adverse, inimical, acting unkindly. E.<BR>अहित unkind, कारिन् acting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=083-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहितमनस्
अहितमनस् mfn. (-नाः-नाः-नः) Hating, adverse, inimical.<BR> E. अहित and मनस्<BR>mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=083-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहितुण्डिक|अहितुंडिक|अहितुण्डिकः
अहितुण्डिक m. (-कः) A snake-catcher or exhibiter.<BR> E. अहि and तुण्ड face,<BR>इकन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=083-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहिद्विष्
अहिद्विष् m. (-द्विट्)<BR>	 1. A name of INDRA.<BR>	 2. GARUḌA the bird of VIṢṆU.<BR>3. A peacock.<BR>	 4. An ichneumon.<BR> E. अहि and द्विष् who hates, from<BR>द्विष् to hate with क्विप् affix; serpent-hater or enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=083-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहिनकुलिका
अहिनकुलिका f. (-का) The natural enmity subsisting between a snake<BR>and an ichneumon.<BR> E. अहि, नकुल a mungoose, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=083-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहिनिर्म्मोक|अहिनिर्मोक|अहिनिर्मोकः
अहिनिर्म्मोक m. (-कः) The slough of a snake.<BR> E. अहि and निर्म्मोक the<BR>same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=083-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहिपति|अहिपतिः
अहिपति m. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. A name of SHESHA, the sovereign of the snakes;<BR>also of VĀSUKI and others.<BR>	 2. Any large serpent.<BR> E. अहि a snake,<BR>and पति lord; also similar compounds, as अहिनाथः, अहीन्द्रः, अहीशः,<BR>अहीश्वरः, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=083-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहिपुत्रक|अहिपुत्रकः
अहिपुत्रक m. (-कः) A kind of boat.<BR> E. अहि and पुत्रक a son, resembling a<BR>snake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=083-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहिफेन|अहिफेनं|अहिफेनः
अहिफेन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Opium.<BR>	 2. The saliva or venom of a snake.<BR> E. अहि a<BR>snake, and फेन foam.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=083-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहिब्रध्न|अहिब्रध्नः
अहिब्रध्न m. (-ध्नः)<BR>	 1. A name of ŚIVA.<BR>	 2. One of the demigods called<BR>RUDRAS.<BR> E. अहि and ब्रधि to bind, नक् Unādi affix; having his<BR>neck bound with snakes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=083-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहिब्रध्नदेवता
अहिब्रध्नदेवता f. (-ता) The twenty-sixth constellation.<BR> E. अहिब्रध्न and देवता<BR>presiding deity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=083-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहिभय|अहिभयं
अहिभय n. (-यं) Mistrust or apprehension of treachery.<BR> E. अहि and भय<BR>fear; fear of a lurking snake as it were.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=083-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहिभुज्
अहिभुज् m. (-भुक्) GARUḌA the bird of VIṢṆU.<BR>	 2. A peacock.<BR> E. अहि<BR>and भुज् who eats, from भुज् and क्विप् affix; snake-eater.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=083-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहिमांशु|अहिमांशुः
अहिमांशु m. (-शुः) The sun.<BR> E. अ neg. हिम cold, and अंशु a ray; also si-<BR>milar compounds, as अहिमकर, अहिमरुचि, अहिमतेजस्, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=083-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहिविद्विष्
अहिविद्विष् m. (-द्विट्)<BR>	 1. GARUḌA.<BR>	 2. INDRA.<BR> E. अहि a snake or VRITRA-<BR>SURA, and विद्विष् foe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=083-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहीन|अहीनः
अहीन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>	 1. Possessed of, not deprived of.<BR>	 2. Not out-caste<BR>or vile.<BR> E. अ neg. हीन deprived of.<BR>	 m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. A large snake, a<BR>serpent.<BR>	 2. A particular sacrifice, one lasting twelve days.<BR> E. अहि<BR>a snake, and इन superior, or अहन् a day, and ख aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=083-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहीनवादिन्
अहीनवादिन् m. (-दी) A witness who is not unfit to give evidence.<BR> E. अ<BR>neg. हीनवादी a defective witness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=083-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहीरणि|अहीरणिः
अहीरणि m. (-णिः) A kind of snake, said to be two-headed.<BR> E. अहि, इर<BR>to move, and अणि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=083-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहुत|अहुतः
अहुत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Unoffered, unsacrificed.<BR>	 2. Uncalled, unsummoned.<BR> m. (-तः) Religious meditation and prayer, considered as one<BR>of the five great sacraments.<BR> E. अ neg. हु to sacrifice, or ह्वे to call,<BR>क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=083-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहे
अहे ind. A particle implying, 1. Rejection.<BR>	 2. Separation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=083-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहेतु|अहेतुः
अहेतु m. (-तुः) Absence of cause or reason.<BR> E. अ neg. हेतु cause.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=083-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहेतुक
अहेतुक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Causeless, groundless.<BR> E. अ neg. हेतुक having<BR>cause.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=083-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहेतुता
अहेतुता f. (-ता) Absence of cause or necessity.<BR> E. तल् added to अहेतु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=083-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहेतुत्व
अहेतुत्व n. (-त्वं) Absence of reason or cause.<BR> E. त्व added to अहेतु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=083-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहेरु|अहेरुः
अहेरु f. (-रुः) A plant, (Asparagus racemosus:) see शतमूली.<BR> E. अ neg.<BR>हि to go, and रु affix; immoveable; alluding to the number of its<BR>roots.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=083-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहो
अहो ind. A particle and interjection of, 1. Reproach, (fie !)<BR>	 2.<BR>Compassion.<BR>	 3. Regret, (ah ! oh !)<BR>	 4. Calling, (ho ! hola !)<BR>	 5.<BR>Praise, flattery, approbation.<BR>	 6. Fatigue, weariness.<BR>	 7. Surprise,<BR>(ah !)<BR>	 8. Doubt, deliberation, (either, or.)<BR>	 9. Contempt, sneer-<BR>ing.<BR>	 10. An expletive.<BR> E. अ neg. हा to go, and डो aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=083-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहोरात्र|अहोरात्रः
अहोरात्र m. (-त्रः) A day of twenty-four hours or thirty Muhūrtas, from<BR>sunrise to sunrise.<BR>	 n. or ind. (-त्रम्) Day and night, continually,<BR>always.<BR> E. अहन् a day, and रात्रि a night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=083-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहोवत
अहोवत ind.<BR>	 1. A particle of calling; 2. Of compassion; 3. Of<BR>fatigue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=083-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहोही
अहोही ind. In a variegated or wonderful manner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=083-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अह्नाय
अह्नाय ind. Soon, instantly.<BR> E. अ neg. ह्नाय from ह्नु to take away or<BR>secrete, with घञ् affix, and य substituted for the व to which the<BR>radical त is changed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=083-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अह्रीक|अह्रीकः
अह्रीक m. (-कः) A Bauddha mendicant.<BR> E. अ neg. and ह्रीक bashful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=083-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अह्वला
अह्वला f. (-ला) The marking nut-plant, (Semecarpus anacardium.)<BR> E. अ<BR>neg. ह्वे to emulate, and डल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=083-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आ
आ The second letter of the alphabet, corresponding to A long, as in<BR>far, and written in the Roman character Ā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=084-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आ
आ ind.<BR>	 1. A particle of reminiscence, (ah! oh!)<BR>	 2. A conjunction<BR>disjunctive, (but)<BR>	 3. A particle of compassion, (ah! alas!)<BR>	 4.<BR>A conjunction copulative, (and.) This particle remains unaltered<BR>in orthography even before vowels.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=084-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आ
आ or आङ् A particle, and prefix to words, implying; 1. Diminu-<BR>tion, (a little.)<BR>	 2. Limit inceptive, (from, from thence, or that<BR>time.)<BR>	 3. Limit conclusive, (until, unto, as far as.)<BR>	 4. Prefixed to<BR>verbs it extends or reverses their meaning, as रुह to rise, आरुह<BR>to ascend, to mount, and गम to go, आगम to come.<BR>	 5. In composi-<BR>tion with nouns it forms indeclinables, either crude, as आजानु to<BR>the knee, or with the terminations of the objective or ablative<BR>case, as आसमुद्रं or आसमुद्रात् as far as to the ocean.<BR>	 6. A particle<BR>of menace or of pain, (ah! alas!) this is more correctly written<BR>आस्<BR> E. आप् to pervade, to obtain, and डाङ् affix, प is dropped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=084-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आङ्
आ or आङ् A particle, and prefix to words, implying; 1. Diminu-<BR>tion, (a little.)<BR>	 2. Limit inceptive, (from, from thence, or that<BR>time.)<BR>	 3. Limit conclusive, (until, unto, as far as.)<BR>	 4. Prefixed to<BR>verbs it extends or reverses their meaning, as रुह to rise, आरुह<BR>to ascend, to mount, and गम to go, आगम to come.<BR>	 5. In composi-<BR>tion with nouns it forms indeclinables, either crude, as आजानु to<BR>the knee, or with the terminations of the objective or ablative<BR>case, as आसमुद्रं or आसमुद्रात् as far as to the ocean.<BR>	 6. A particle<BR>of menace or of pain, (ah! alas!) this is more correctly written<BR>आस्<BR> E. आप् to pervade, to obtain, and डाङ् affix, प is dropped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=084-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आ
आ m. (आः) A name of MAHĀDEVA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=084-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आ
आ ind. A particle of assent, yes, verily.<BR> E. अम to go, क्विप् affix, अ be-<BR>comes आ<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=084-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकम्पन|आकंपन
आकम्पन n. (-नं) Shaking, trembling.<BR> E. आङ् before कपि to tremble, ल्युट्<BR>aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=084-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकम्पित|आकंपित|आकम्पितं
आकम्पित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Shaken, trembling.<BR> E. आङ् prefixed, कपि to<BR>shake, and क्त participial aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=084-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकम्प्र|आकंप्र
आकम्प्र mfn. (-म्प्रः-म्प्रा-म्प्रं) Trembling, shaking, agitated.<BR> E. आङ् before<BR>कपि to shake, रक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=084-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकर|आकरः
आकर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A mine.<BR>	 2. A multitude.<BR>	 3. Best, excellent.<BR> E. आङ्<BR>prefixed, कृ to make, &c. अप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=084-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकरिन्
आकरिन् mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि) Mineral, produced in a mine, &c.<BR> E. आकर<BR>and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=084-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकर्णन|आकर्णनं
आकर्णन n. (-नं) Hearing.<BR> E. आङ् before कर्ण to hear, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=084-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकर्णित
आकर्णित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Heard.<BR> E. आङ्, कर्ण to hear, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=084-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकर्ष|आकर्षः
आकर्ष m. (-र्षः)<BR>	 1. Pulling, hawling.<BR>	 2. Pulling to or towards, dragging,<BR>attracting.<BR>	 3. Attraction, fascination.<BR>	 4. Magnetic attraction.<BR>	 5. A<BR>magnet, a loadstone.<BR>	 6. A dice or die.<BR>	 7. Playing with dice.<BR>	 8. A<BR>board of such a game.<BR>	 9. Drawing the bow.<BR>	 10. An organ of sense.<BR>11. Spasm.<BR> E. आङ्, कृष् to draw or make furrows, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=084-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकर्षक|आकर्षकः
आकर्षक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Attractive, what draws or attracts.<BR>	 m. (-कः) A<BR>magnet or loadstone.<BR> E. आकर्ष attraction, and वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=084-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकर्षण|आकर्षणं
आकर्षण n. (-णं) Pulling, drawing, attracting.<BR>	 f. (-णी)<BR>	 1. A crooked stick,<BR>for pulling down fruit, &c.<BR>	 2. Any instrument for pulling.<BR> E. आङ्<BR>before कृष् to pull, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=084-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकर्षिक
आकर्षिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Magnetic, attractive.<BR> E. आकर्ष and ष्ठल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=084-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकर्षित
आकर्षित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Drawn, attracted.<BR> E. आङ् before कृष् to draw, क्त<BR>aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=084-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकर्षिन्
आकर्षिन् mfn. (-र्षी-र्षिणी-र्षि) Attractive.<BR>	 f. (-णी) A rod with a hook at the<BR>end to pull down the boughs of trees, for the purpose of gathering<BR>the fruit.<BR> E. आङ् before कृष् to draw, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=084-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकलन|आकलनं
आकलन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Wish, desire.<BR>	 2. Counting, reckoning.<BR>	 3. Confinement,<BR>binding.<BR>	 4. Laying hold of.<BR> E. आङ्, कल to count, sound, &c. and<BR>ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=084-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकलित
आकलित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Counted, reckoned.<BR>	 2. Seized, held,<BR>bound.<BR> E. आङ् before कल to count, &c. क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=084-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकल्प|आकल्पः
आकल्प m. (-ल्पः)<BR>	 1. Ornament, decoration.<BR>	 2. Increasing, adding to,<BR>improving.<BR>	 3. Sickness, disease.<BR> E. आङ् before कृप् to be able, to<BR>be weak, &c. घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=084-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकल्पक|आकल्पकः
आकल्पक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. Remembering with regret, missing.<BR>	 2. Fainting,<BR>loss of sense or perception.<BR>	 3. Darkness.<BR>	 4. A knot or joint.<BR> E. आङ्,<BR>कल्प from कृप् to be able, to be weak, &c. and ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=084-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकष|आकषः
आकष m. (-षः) A touchstone.<BR> E. आङ्, कष to injure, and अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=084-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकषक
आकषक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Touching, assaying.<BR> E. वुन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=084-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकषिक
आकषिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Touching, testing.<BR> E. आकष and ष्ठल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=084-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकस्मिक|आकस्मिकं
आकस्मिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Sudden, unexpected, causeless.<BR> E. अकस्मात्<BR>and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=084-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकाङ्क्षत्
आकाङ्क्षत् mfn. (-ङ्क्षन्-ङ्क्षन्ती-ङ्क्षत्)<BR>	 1. Wishing, expecting.<BR>	 2. Looking at, to,<BR>or towards.<BR> E. आङ् before काङ्क्षि to desire, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=084-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकाङ्क्षणीय
आकाङ्क्षणीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Desirable, to be desired or expected.<BR> E. आङ्<BR>before काङ्क्षि to desire, अनीयर् affix; also आकाङ्क्षितव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>and आकाङ्क्ष्य mfn. (-ङ्क्ष्यः-ङ्क्ष्या-ङ्क्ष्यं) with तव्य and यत् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=084-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकाङ्क्षा|आकांक्षा
आकाङ्क्षा f. (-ङ्क्षा)<BR>	 1. Wish, desire.<BR>	 2. Purpose, intention.<BR>	 3. Looking at,<BR>to, or towards.<BR>	 4. Enquiry, asking.<BR>	 5. The presence of a word in<BR>a sentence indispensable to the sense.<BR>	 6. The significancy of a<BR>word.<BR> E. आङ् prefixed to काङ्क्षि to desire, अच् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=084-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकाङ्क्षित|आकांक्षित
आकाङ्क्षित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Wished, desired.<BR>	 2. Asked, enquired.<BR>	 3.<BR>Regarded, looked at.<BR>	 4. Wanted, necessary.<BR> E. आङ् before काङ्क्षि to<BR>desire, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=084-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकाङ्क्षिन्|आकांक्षिन्
आकाङ्क्षिन् mfn. (-ङ्क्षी-ङ्क्षिणी-ङ्क्षि)<BR>	 1. Wishing, wishful.<BR>	 2. Asking, enquiring,<BR>expectant.<BR> E. आकाङ्क्षा and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=084-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकाय|आकायः
आकाय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. A funeral pile.<BR>	 2. Abode, residence.<BR> E. आङ् before चि<BR>to collect, घञ् affix, च changed to क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=084-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकार|आकारः
आकार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Hint, sign, token.<BR>	 2. Form.<BR>	 3. The letter आ<BR> E. आङ्,<BR>कृ to make, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=084-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकारगुप्ति|आकारगुप्तिः
आकारगुप्ति f. (-प्तिः) Dissimulation.<BR> E. आकार and गुप्ति concealment,<BR>suppressing all sign or indication of the feelings.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=084-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकारगोपन|आकारगोपनं
आकारगोपन n. (-नं) See the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=084-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकारण|आकारणं
आकारण nf. (-णं-णा) Calling, a call or summons.<BR> E. आङ्, कृ to make or<BR>do in the causal form, and ल्युट् affix, fem. affix टाप्; sometimes<BR>written आकरण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=084-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकारवत्|आकारवन्त्
आकारवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Symmetrical, handsome, well formed. E.<BR>आकार form, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=084-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकारित
आकारित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Called or summoned.<BR>	 2. Stipulated, agreed.<BR>3. Demanded, exacted.<BR> E. आङ् before कृ to make, causal form, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=084-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकालिक|आकालिकं
आकालिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>	 1. Momentary, instantaneous.<BR>	 2. Unseason-<BR>able, improper with respect to time.<BR>	 f. (-की) Lightning.<BR> E. अ neg.<BR>काल time, ठक् affix, fem. ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=084-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकालिकत्व
आकालिकत्व n. (-त्वं) Unseasonableness, suddenness.<BR> E. त्व added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=084-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकाश|आकाशं|आकाशः
आकाश mn. (-शः-शं)<BR>	 1. The fifth element, æther, the sky or atmosphere.<BR>2. Brahma as identical with æther.<BR>	 3. Space, vacuity.<BR> E. आङ्<BR>and काशृ to shine, घञ् affix; every where shining; Akash is the<BR>subtle and æthereal fluid, supposed to fill and pervade the<BR>universe, and to be the peculiar vehicle of life and sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=084-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकाशकक्षा
आकाशकक्षा f. (-क्षा) The horizon.<BR> E. आकाश and कक्षा girdle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=084-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकाशज
आकाशज mfn. (-जः-जा-जं) Produced in the sky.<BR> E. आकाश and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=084-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकाशजननिन्
आकाशजननिन् m. (-नी) A loophole, a casement, an embrasure.<BR> E. आकाश<BR>and जननिन् what generates, giving air and light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=084-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकाशदीप
अकाशदीप m. (-पः)<BR>	 1. A lamp or torch lighted in honour of LAKṢMĪ or<BR>VIṢṆU, and elevated on a pole in the open air at the Dewali<BR>festival, in the month Kartik.<BR>	 2. A beacon, a lantern on a pole.<BR>E. आकाश and दीप a lamp; also आकाशप्रदीपः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=084-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकाशभाषित
आकाशभाषित n. (-तं)<BR>	 1. Speaking outside or of the stage, or a supposi-<BR>tious speech, which is replied to as if it had been spoken, (in<BR>dramatic language.)<BR>	 2. A voice or sound in the air.<BR> E. आकाश and<BR>भाषित spoken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=084-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकाशमण्डल
आकाशमण्डल n. (-लं) The celestial sphere.<BR> E. आकाश and मण्डल a circle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=084-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकाशमांसी
आकाशमांसी f. (-सी) A plant, small Jatāmānsi, (Valeriana Jatamansi.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=084-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकाशमूली
आकाशमूली f. (-ली) An aquatic plant, (Pistia stratiotes.)<BR> E. आकाश and<BR>मूली having roots; having its root in air.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=084-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकाशयान
आकाशयान n. (-नं) A heavenly car, one moving through the air. E.<BR>आकाश and यान vehicle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=084-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकाशरक्षिन्
आकाशरक्षिन् m. (-क्षी) A warder, a watchman on the outer battlements.<BR>E. आकाश and रक्षिन् a guard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=085-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकाशवर्त्मन्
आकाशवर्त्मन् n. (-र्त्म) The atmosphere, the firmament, the air.<BR> E. आकाश<BR>and वर्त्मन् a road.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=085-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकाशवल्ली
आकाशवल्ली f. (-ल्ली) A sort of creeper, a parasite. (Cassyta filiformis.) E.<BR>आकाश and वल्ली pedicle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=085-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकाशवाणी
आकाशवाणी f. (-णी) A voice from heaven.<BR> E. आकाश and वाणी speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=085-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकाशसलिल|आकाशसलिलं
आकाशसलिल n. (-लं) Rain.<BR> E. आकाश and सलिल water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=085-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकाशस्थ
आकाशस्थ mfn. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थं) Abiding in the sky.<BR> E. आकाश and स्थ what<BR>stays.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=085-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकाशीय
आकाशीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Atmospherical. Also आकाशिन् mfn. (-शी-शिनी-शि)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=085-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकाशे
आकाशे ind. In the air, a stage direction, implying something said by<BR>or to a person out of sight. E. 7th case of आकाश.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=085-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकाशेश|आकाशेशः
आकाशेश m. (-शः)<BR>	 1. INDRA, as ruler of the firmament.<BR>	 2. (In law) A<BR>helpless person, as a child, a woman, a pauper or invalid.<BR> E. आकाश<BR>and ईश lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=085-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकिञ्चन|आकिंचन|आकिंचनं|आकिञ्चनं
आकिञ्चन n. (-नं) Poverty.<BR> E. अकिञ्चन poor, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=085-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकीर्ण|आकीर्णं|आकीर्ण्ण
आकीर्ण mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-र्णं)<BR>	 1. Filled, overspread.<BR>	 2. Crowded.<BR>	 3. Impervious.<BR>4. Spread.<BR>	 5. Scattered.<BR> E. आङ्, कॄ to scatter, part. affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=085-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकीर्णता
आकीर्णता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Fulness.<BR>	 2. Crowd, multitude.<BR> E. आकीर्ण filled, तल्<BR>affix; also आकीर्णत्वं<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=085-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकुञ्चन|आकुंचनं|आकुञ्चनं
आकुञ्चन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Compression, contraction, shrinking.<BR>	 2. Collecting,<BR>heaping.<BR>	 3. Curving, flexure.<BR>	 4. Contortion.<BR> E. आङ् before कुचि to<BR>contract, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=085-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकुञ्चित
आकुञ्चित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Bent, contracted.<BR>	 2. Twisted, contorted. E.<BR>आङ् before कुचि to contract, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=085-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकुण्ठित
आकुण्ठित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Confounded, abashed.<BR> E. आङ् before कुण्ठित<BR>abashed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=085-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकुल|आकुलं
आकुल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>	 1. Confounded, confused, flurried.<BR>	 2. Confused<BR>(in order), disordered.<BR>	 3. Incoherent, contradictory.<BR> E. आङ्, कुल to<BR>accumulate, and क affix; not self-possessed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=085-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकुलत्व|आकुलत्वं
आकुलत्व n. (-त्वं) Confusion, perplexity, bewilderment.<BR> E. आकुल and त्व<BR>affix; also with तल् affix आकुलता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=085-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकुलित
आकुलित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Bewildered, flurried, agitated.<BR>	 2. Distressed.<BR>E. आङ् before कुल, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=085-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकुलीकृत
आकुलीकृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Bewildered, perplexed.<BR> E. आकुल and कृत made<BR>with च्वि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=085-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकुष्ट
आकुष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं) Expelled, extracted.<BR> E. आकुष to extract, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=085-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकूत|आकूतं
आकूत n. (-तं)<BR>	 1. Meaning, intention.<BR>	 2. Wish, desire.<BR> E. आङ्, कूङ् to<BR>cry, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=085-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकृति|आकृतिः
आकृति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Form, figure.<BR>	 2. The body.<BR>	 3. Tribe, species.<BR>	 4. A<BR>metre: a stanza of four lines, with twenty-two syllables to each<BR>line.<BR> E. आङ् before कृ to make or do, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=085-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकृतिच्छत्रा
आकृतिच्छत्रा f. (-त्रा) A plant, (Achyranthes aspera.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=085-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकृष्ट|आकृष्टं
आकृष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>	 1. Pulled, drawn.<BR>	 2. Attracted.<BR> E. आङ् before<BR>कृष् to drag, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=085-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकृष्यमाण
आकृष्यमाण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Drawing, attracting.<BR> E. आकृष to draw, शानच्<BR>aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=085-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकृष्टवत्
आकृष्टवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>	 1. Pulling, dragging, pulling up or out.<BR>	 2.<BR>Pulling to, attracting.<BR>	 3. Charming, fascinating.<BR> E. आकृष्ट and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=085-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकृष्टि|आकृष्टिः
आकृष्टि f. (-ष्टिः)<BR>	 1. Pulling, dragging.<BR>	 2. Drawing, attraction.<BR> E. आङ्<BR>before कृष् to drag, affix क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=085-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकोकेर|आकोकेरः
आकोकेर m. (-रः) The constellation Capricornus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=085-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकौशल
आकौशल n. (-लं) Inexpertness, want of skill or practice.<BR> E. अकुशल un-<BR>skilful, affix अण् and the initial optionally long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=085-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्रन्द|आक्रंदः|आक्रन्दः
आक्रन्द mfn. (-न्दः-न्दा-न्दं) Who checks or restrains.<BR>	 m. (-न्दः)<BR>	 1. Crying,<BR>crying out.<BR>	 2. Calling.<BR>	 3. Weeping, sobbing.<BR>	 4. Sound.<BR>	 5. Vio-<BR>lence.<BR>	 6. Furious or violent combat.<BR>	 7. A friend.<BR>	 8. A brother.<BR>	 9. A<BR>king, a lord.<BR>	 10. A usurper.<BR>	 11. A king who prevents an ally from<BR>aiding another.<BR> E. आङ्, क्रन्द to cry, to sound, &c. अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=085-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्रन्दिक|आक्रंदिक
आक्रन्दिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Going where sounds of distress are heard. E.<BR>आक्रन्द and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=085-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्रम|आक्रमः
आक्रम m. (-मः)<BR>	 1. Going over or beyond.<BR>	 2. Surpassing.<BR>	 3. Spreading<BR>over or upon.<BR>	 4. Overleading.<BR>	 5. Attaining, overcoming, obtaining.<BR>6. Invading, attacking, falling upon.<BR>	 7. Might, valour.<BR> E. आङ् be-<BR>fore क्रम to go, to mount, ascend, surpass, &c. affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=085-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्रमण|आक्रमणं
आक्रमण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Going over or beyond.<BR>	 2. Overpowering, subduing.<BR>3. Spreading or extending over or upon.<BR>	 4. Attacking, marching<BR>against, invading.<BR> E. आङ् before क्रम to go, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=085-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्रमणीय
आक्रमणीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>	 1. To be attacked.<BR>	 2. To be surpassed or over-<BR>come.<BR>	 3. To be seized.<BR> E. आङ् before क्रम to go, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=085-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्रान्त|आक्रांत|आक्रान्तः
आक्रान्त mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं)<BR>	 1. Surpassed, surmounted.<BR>	 2. Overcome, over-<BR>run.<BR>	 3. Pained, distressed.<BR>	 4. Accompanied, attended.<BR>	 5. Over-<BR>spread.<BR>	 6. Obtained, possessed.<BR>	 7. Agitated or overcome by, as a<BR>feeling.<BR> E. आक्रम to mount, surpass, &c. and part. affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=085-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्रान्ति|आक्रांतिः|आक्रान्तिः
आक्रान्ति f. (-न्तिः)<BR>	 1. Going over or beyond.<BR>	 2. Overpowering.<BR>	 3. Might,<BR>valour.<BR> E. आङ् before क्रम to go, affix क्तिन्; see आक्रम.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=085-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्रामक|आक्रामकः
आक्रामक mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>	 1. Invading, assailing 2. Overrunning.<BR> E. आङ्<BR>before क्रम to go, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=085-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्रीड|आक्रीडः
आक्रीड m. (-डः)<BR>	 1. A royal garden.<BR>	 2. Sport, pleasure.<BR> E. आङ्, क्रीड to<BR>play, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=085-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्रीडन|आक्रीडनं
आक्रीडन n. (-नं) Sporting, taking pleasure.<BR> E. आक्रीड to sport, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=085-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्रीडिन्
आक्रीडिन् mfn. (-डी-डिनी-डि) Sporting, playing.<BR> E. आक्रीड to play, घिनुण्<BR>aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=085-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्रुष्ट
आक्रुष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>	 1. Cursed.<BR>	 2. Accused, calumniated.<BR>	 3. Abused.<BR>4. Vociferated.<BR> E. आङ् before क्रुश to call, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=085-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्रोश|आक्रोशः
आक्रोश m. (-शः)<BR>	 1. Abuse, censuring, a curse or oath.<BR>	 2. Vociferousness,<BR>calling aloud.<BR> E. आङ्, क्रुश to call, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=085-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्रोशक|आक्रोशकः
आक्रोशक mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>	 1. Abusing, abusive.<BR>	 2. Vociferous.<BR> E. आक्रुश<BR>to call, वुञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=085-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्रोशन|आक्रोशनं
आक्रोशन n. (-नं) Curse, imprecation.<BR> E. आङ्, क्रुश to call, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=085-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्रोशनीय
आक्रोशनीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) To be accursed, censurable, reprovable.<BR> E. आङ्<BR>before क्रुश to cry, अनीयर् affix; also आक्रुश्य and आक्रोशितव्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=085-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्षद्यूतिक
आक्षद्यूतिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Effected or completed by gambling.<BR> E. अक्षद्यूत<BR>and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=085-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्षपण|आक्षपणं
आक्षपण n. (-णं) Fasting, or purification by fasting.<BR> E. आङ् before क्षप to<BR>endure, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=085-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्षपाटिक|आक्षपाटिकः
आक्षपाटिक m. (-कः) A judge.<BR> E. अक्ष a law-suit, पट to go, causal form, उक<BR>affix; also अक्षपाटिक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=085-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्षपाद|आक्षपादः
आक्षपाद m. (-दः) A logician.<BR> E. अक्ष dispute, पाद a division, अण् affix;<BR>also अक्षपाद.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=085-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्षार|आक्षारः
आक्षार m. (-रः) Accusation, calumny.<BR> E. आङ् before क्षर to go, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=085-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्षारण|आक्षारणं
आक्षारण nf. (-णं-णा)<BR>	 1. Calumnious accusation.<BR>	 2. Abuse, reviling. E.<BR>आङ्, क्षर to go, with युच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=085-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्षारित|आक्षारितं
आक्षारित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Calumniated, falsely accused.<BR>	 2. Accused of<BR>adultery or fornication.<BR>	 3. Falsely accused, of such crimes in parti-<BR>cular.<BR>	 4. Guilty, criminal.<BR>	 5. Reviled, abused.<BR> E. आङ्, क्षर to go,<BR>part. affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=085-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्षिक|आक्षिकः
आक्षिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>	 1. Relating or belonging to a die, to gambling,<BR>&c.<BR>	 2. Won at dice.<BR>	 m. (-कः) A tree, (Morinda tinctoria.)<BR>	 n. (-कं) A<BR>gambling debt, money lost at play.<BR> E. अक्ष a die, &c. and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=085-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्षिकपण|आक्षिकपणः
आक्षिकपण m. (-णः) A stake, a wager, a bet.<BR> E. आक्षिक and पण a wager.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=085-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्षिपत्
आक्षिपत् mfn. (-पन्-पती-पत्)<BR>	 1. Excelling, so as to reproach or put to<BR>shame others.<BR>	 2. Reviling, abusing.<BR>	 3. Tossing.<BR>	 4. Sending.<BR> E. आङ्<BR>before क्षिप to throw, affix शतृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=085-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्षिप्त
आक्षिप्त mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं)<BR>	 1. Cast, thrown, tossed.<BR>	 2. Thrown down or away.<BR>3. Borne, carried.<BR>	 4. Reviled, abused, blamed, ridiculed.<BR>	 4. Equal<BR>or equivalent to.<BR> E. आङ् before क्षिप् to throw, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=085-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्षीव
आक्षीव m. (-वः) A plant, (Morunga guilandina and hyperanthera:) see<BR>अक्षीव.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=085-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्षेप|आक्षेपः
आक्षेप m. (-पः)<BR>	 1. Throw, toss.<BR>	 2. Abuse, reviling.<BR>	 3. Censure, blame, re-<BR>proach.<BR>	 4. Attraction.<BR>	 5. A figure in rhetoric, (irony.)<BR> E. आङ्, क्षिप्<BR>to throw or send, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=086-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्षेपक|आक्षेपकः
आक्षेपक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. Sickness, disease.<BR>	 2. Convulsion, spasm.<BR>	 3. A de-<BR>tractor, a calumniator or accuser.<BR>	 4. A thrower.<BR> E. आङ् before क्षिप्<BR>to toss, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=086-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्षैत्रज्ञ्य|आक्षैत्रज्ञ्यं
आक्षैत्रज्ञ्य n. (-ज्ञं) Spiritual ignorance.<BR> E. अ neg. क्षेत्रज्ञ wise, and ष्यञ् affix,<BR>the initial optionally long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=086-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्षोट|आक्षोटः
आक्षोट m. (-टः) A tree, (see पीलु,) growing in mountains: in Hindi, the<BR>corresponding name implies the walnut: see अक्षोट and आक्षोड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=086-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्षोड|आक्षोडः
आक्षोड m. (-डः) A kind of Pilu, a tree so named, (Careya arborea:) see<BR>अक्षोड, अक्षोट and पीलु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=086-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्क्षोद
आर्क्षोद m. (-दः) A Brahman of the Ṛkṣoda mountain.<BR> E. ऋक्षोद and अण्<BR>aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=086-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्षोदन|आक्षोदनं
आक्षोदन n. (-नं) Hunting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=086-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आख|आखः
आख m. (-खः) A spade, a hoe.<BR> E. आङ्, खन् to dig, ड aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=086-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आखण्डल|आखंडलः|आखण्डलः
आखण्डल m. (-लः) A name of INDRA.<BR> E. आङ् and खण्ड to break, अलच्<BR>affix; mountain-breaking, foe-destroying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=086-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आखन|आखनः
आखन m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. A spade.<BR>	 2. A digger.<BR> E. आङ्, खन् to dig, घ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=086-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आखनिक|आखनिकः
आखनिक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A thief.<BR>	 2. A rat.<BR>	 3. A hog.<BR>	 4. A spade.<BR>	 5. A digger,<BR>a ditcher, a miner.<BR> E. आङ्, खन् to dig, and इकन् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=086-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आखनिकवक
आखनिकवक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A spade.<BR>	 2. A digger.<BR> E. आङ् before खन् to dig,<BR>इकवक aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=086-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आखर|आखरः
आखर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A spade.<BR>	 2. A digger.<BR> E. आङ्, खन् to dig, डर aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=086-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आखात|आखातं|आखातः
आखात mn. (-तः-तं) A natural pond: see अखात.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=086-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आखान|आखानः
आखान m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. A spade.<BR>	 2. A digger.<BR> E. आङ्, खन् to dig. घञ्<BR>aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=086-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आखु|आखुः
आखु m. (-खुः)<BR>	 1. A rat, a mouse.<BR>	 2. A hog.<BR>	 3. A thief.<BR>	 4. A sort of tree:<BR>see देवताड.<BR> E. आङ्, खन् to dig, and कु Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=086-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आखुकर्णी
आखुकर्णी f. (-र्णी) The name of a plant, (Salvinia cucullata.)<BR> E. आखु a<BR>mouse, and कर्ण an ear; the leaves are compared to the ears of a<BR>mouse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=086-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आखुग|आखुगः
आखुग m. (-गः)<BR>	 1. A name of GANESA.<BR>	 2. A name of KĀRTIKEYA. E.<BR>आखु a rat, and ग who goes; GANESA is represented riding on a rat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=086-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आखुघात|आखुघातः
आखुघात m. (-तः) A Śūdra or man of low caste and profession, lit. a ratcatcher.<BR>E. आखु and घात a blow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=086-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आखुपर्णिका
आखुपर्णिका f. (-का) A plant: see आखुकर्णी.<BR> E. आखु and पर्ण a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=086-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आखुपर्णी
आखुपर्णी f. (-र्णी) See the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=086-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आखुपाषाण|आखुपाषाणः
आखुपाषाण m. (-णः) A kind of mineral, a loadstone.<BR> E. आखु and पाषाण a<BR>stone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=086-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आखुभुज्
आखुभुज् m. (-भुक्) A cat.<BR> E. आखु and भुज् who eats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=086-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आखुरथ|आखुरथः
आखुरथ m. (-थः) A name of GANESA.<BR> E. आखु, and रथ a carriage; whose<BR>vehicle is a rat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=086-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आखुविषहा
आखुविषहा f. (-हा) A kind of grass, (Andropogon serratum.)<BR> E. आखु, विष<BR>venom, and हा what destroys; considered as a remedy for the bite<BR>of a rat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=086-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आखूत्थ|आखूत्थः
आखूत्थ m. (-त्थः) The rising up or coming of rats, a swarm of rats. E.<BR>आखु and उत्थ from उत् and स्था with क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=086-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आखेट|आखेटः
आखेट m. (-टः)<BR>	 1. Chase, hunting.<BR>	 2. Terror, fright.<BR> E. आङ्, खिट to<BR>alarm, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=086-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आखेटक|आखेटकः
आखेटक mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>	 1. Hunting, a hunter.<BR>	 2. Frightening, fright-<BR>ful.<BR>	 n. (-कं) Hunting.<BR> E. आखेट and कन् pleonastic affix; or आङ्<BR>with खिट and ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=086-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आखेटशीर्षक|आखेटशीर्षकं
आखेटशीर्षक n. (-कं) A cavern, a mine.<BR> E. आखेट terrifying, and शीर्ष the<BR>head or principal, क affix: very gloomy and terrifying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=086-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आखेटिक|आखेटिकः
आखेटिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>	 1. Who or what hunts.<BR>	 2. Terrible, frightful.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A hound.<BR>	 2. A hunter.<BR> E. आखेट chase, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=086-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आखोट|आखोटः
आखोट m. (-टः) The walnut tree. E. See अक्षोट. &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=086-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आख्या
आख्या f. (-ख्या) A name or appellation.<BR> E. ख्या to say, आङ् prefixed, अङ्<BR>and टाप् fem. affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=086-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आख्यात|आख्यातं
आख्यात mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Said, spoken.<BR>	 2. Called, declared.<BR>	 3. Made<BR>known.<BR>	 4. Inflected, declined, conjugated. E. part. past of आख्या to<BR>say, to speak, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=086-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आख्यान|आख्यानं
आख्यान n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. A tale, a legend.<BR>	 2. Saying, declaring.<BR> E. आङ् before<BR>ख्या to tell, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=086-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आख्यायक|आख्यायकः
आख्यायक m. (-कः) A messenger, a teller, an announcer or relater.<BR>	 f.<BR>(-यिका) A tale, a true or probable story.<BR> E. आख्या to say, खुल् affix,<BR>य inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=086-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आख्येय
आख्येय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Fit or proper to be said.<BR> E. आङ् before ख्या to say,<BR>affix यत्; also आख्यातव्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=086-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगत|आगतं
आगत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Arrived, come.<BR>	 2. Received, obtained.<BR>	 3. Living<BR>or residing in.<BR> E. आङ् before गम् to go, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=086-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगत्य
आगत्य ind. Having arrived.<BR> E. आङ् before गम् to go, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=086-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगन्तव्य|आगंतव्य
आगन्तव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं) What will come, what is likely to arrive. E.<BR>आङ् and गम् to go, तव्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=086-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगन्तु|आगंतु|आगन्तुः
आगन्तु mfn. (-न्तुः-न्तुः-न्तु)<BR>	 1. Coming, arriving.<BR>	 2. Incidental, adventi-<BR>tious.<BR>	 m. (-न्तुः)<BR>	 1. A guest.<BR>	 2. A stranger, a newcomer.<BR>	 3. An<BR>accident, any accidental hurt or wound.<BR> E. आङ् before गम् to go,<BR>to come, तु affix; म becomes न; also आगान्तु and आगन्तुक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=086-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगन्तुक|आगंतुक|आगन्तुकं
आगन्तुक mfn. (-कः-का-की-कं)<BR>	 1. Incidental, adventitious. (as pleasure,<BR>pain, ornament, &c.)<BR>	 2. Stray.<BR>	 m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A stranger, a newcomer.<BR>2. A guest.<BR> E. आगन्तु and कन् affix, what comes and goes: what is<BR>not inseparably inherent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=086-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगम|आगमं|आगमः
आगम m. (-मः)<BR>	 1. Arrival, coming, approach.<BR>	 2. A Śāstra or work on<BR>sacred science in general, supposed to be of divine origin.<BR>	 3. A<BR>Tantra or any work inculcating the mystical worship of ŚIVA and<BR>SAKTI.<BR>	 4. A grammatical augment, a syllable or letter inserted in<BR>any part of the radical word.<BR>	 5. Record, title deed, legal title, a<BR>voucher or written testimony, &c.<BR> E. आङ् before गम् to go, to come,<BR>अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=086-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगमन|आगमनं
आगमन n. (-नं) Arriving, coming.<BR> E. आङ् before गम् to go, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=086-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगमनिरपेक्ष
आगमनिरपेक्ष mfn. (-क्षः-क्षा-क्षं) Independent of a written voucher or title.<BR>E. आगम and निरपेक्षा disregard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=086-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगमय्य
आगमय्य ind. Having explored or discovered.<BR> E. आङ् before गम् to go,<BR>causal form, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=086-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगमरहित
आगमरहित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Devoid of a written title or voucher.<BR>	 2.<BR>Without a Śāstra.<BR> E. आगम and रहित devoid of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=086-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगमसापेक्ष
आगमसापेक्ष mfn. (-क्षः-क्षा-क्षं) With or supported by legal vouchers. E.<BR>आगम and सापेक्ष regard to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=086-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगमापायिन्
आगमापायिन् mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि) Transient, of short duration.<BR> E. आगम and<BR>अपायिन् separating, going at the time of arrival.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=086-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगमित|आगमितं
आगमित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Read over, perused, studied.<BR> E. आङ् prefixed to<BR>गम् in the causal form; participial affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=086-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगम्य
आगम्य mfn. (-म्यः-म्या-म्यं)<BR>	 1. To be approached, accessible.<BR>	 2. To be acquired.<BR>E. आङ् before गम् with यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=086-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगस्
आगस् n. (-गः)<BR>	 1. Sin.<BR>	 2. Transgression, offence, fault.<BR> E. आग substituted<BR>for इण् to go, असुन् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=086-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगाध|आगाधं
आगाध mfn. (-धः-धा-धं) Very deep: see अगाध.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=086-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगान्तु|आगान्तुः
आगान्तु mfn. (-न्तुः-न्तुः-न्तु) A guest: see आगन्तु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=086-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगामिन्
आगामिन् mfn. (-मी-मिनी-मि)<BR>	 1. Arriving, coming.<BR>	 2. Future.<BR> E. आङ्<BR>before गम् to go, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=086-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगार|आगारं
आगार n. (-रं) A house, a dwelling: see अगार.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=086-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगारदाह|आगारदाहः
आगारदाह m. (-हः) Arson, setting a house on fire.<BR> E. आगार and दाह burn-<BR>ing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=086-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगारदाहिन्
आगारदाहिन् m. (-ही) An incendiary.<BR> E. आगारदाह arson, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=086-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगुर्
आगुर् f. (-गूः) An agreement: see आगू.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=086-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगुरव
आगुरव mfn. (-वः-वी-वं)<BR>	 1. Consisting of or containing Agallochum.<BR>	 2.<BR>Very heavy.<BR> E. अगुरु and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=086-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगू
आगू f. (-गूः) An agreement.<BR> E. आगम to come, डू affix or आङ् prefixed to<BR>गू to come and क्विन् affix; also आगुर्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=086-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आग्नीध्र|आग्नीध्रं|आग्नीध्रः
आग्नीध्र n. (-ध्रं) The place where a sacrificial fire is kindled.<BR> E. अग्नि fire,<BR>and इन्ध to kindle; see अग्नीध्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=087-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आग्नेय|आग्नेयं|आग्नेयः
आग्नेय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Belonging or relating to fire or its deity.<BR>	 n. (-यं)<BR>1. The name of a city, (Devikotta, on the Coromandel Coast.)<BR>	 2.<BR>Blood.<BR>	 3. Ghee or boiled butter.<BR>	 m. (-यः) A name of the saint<BR>AGASTI.<BR>	 f. (-यी)<BR>	 1. The wife of AGNI.<BR>	 2. The south-east quarter, of<BR>which AGNI is the regent.<BR> E. अग्नि fire or its deity, ढक् affix which<BR>leaves एय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=087-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आग्रह|आग्रहः
आग्रह m. (-हः)<BR>	 1. Favour, patronage.<BR>	 2. Seizing, taking.<BR>	 3. Surpassing,<BR>surmounting.<BR>	 4. Power, ability.<BR> E. आङ्, ग्रह to take, अप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=087-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आग्रहायण|आग्रहायणः
आग्रहायण m. (-णः) A month so called, the first of the Hindu year ac-<BR>cording to some systems, (November-December.)<BR> E. अग्र beginning,<BR>and हायन a year; also अग्रहायण, the अ being unchanged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=087-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आग्रहायणिक|आग्रहायणिकः
आग्रहायणिक m. (-कः) The month Āgrahayana.<BR> E. अग्रहायण and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=087-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आग्रहायणी
आग्रहायणी f. (-णी)<BR>	 1. The name of a constellation consisting of three<BR>stars, one of which is Orionis, figured by an antelope's head,<BR>hence also मृगशिरस्.<BR>	 2. The day of full moon in the month<BR>Āgrahayana.<BR> E. अग्रहायण and ङीप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=087-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आग्रायण
आग्रायण n. (-णं) A sacrifice offered when the new rice or wheat ripens.<BR>E. अग्र chief, अयन coming, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=087-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आग्रायणेष्टि
आग्रायणेष्टि f. (-ष्टिः) A particular ceremony: see the last.<BR> E. आग्रायण and<BR>इष्टि a sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=087-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आघट्टक|आघट्टकः
आघट्टक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A tree, (the red sort of Achyranthes.)<BR>	 2. A rubber,<BR>what effects friction.<BR> E. आङ् before घट्ट to move, and वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=087-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आघट्टन
आघट्टन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Friction, rubbing, contact.<BR>	 2. Shaking.<BR> E. आङ् before<BR>घट्ट to move, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=087-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आघट्टित
आघट्टित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Touched, rubbed.<BR>	 2. Shaken.<BR> E. आङ् before<BR>घट्ट to move, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=087-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आघर्ष|आघर्षः
आघर्ष m. (-र्षः) Rubbing, friction.<BR> E. आङ् before घृष् to rub, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=087-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आघर्षण|आघर्षणं
आघर्षण n. (-णं) Rubbing, friction.<BR>	 f. (-णी) A brush, a rubber.<BR> E. आङ्<BR>before घृष् to rub, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=087-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आघर्षित
आघर्षित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Rubbed.<BR> E. आङ् before घृष् to rub, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=087-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आघाट|आघाटः
आघाट m. (-टः)<BR>	 1. A limit, a boundary.<BR>	 2. A tree, (Achyranthes aspera.)<BR>E. आङ्, घट to endeavour, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=087-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आघात|आघातः
आघात m. (-तः)<BR>	 1. Killing, striking.<BR>	 2. A blow, a wound.<BR>	 3. A slaughter-<BR>house, a place for killing animals or victims.<BR> E. आङ्, हन to kill or<BR>injure, in the participial form; घ is substituted for ह.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=087-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आघातन|आघातनं
आघातन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Striking, killing.<BR>	 2. A slaughter-house.<BR> E. आङ्, हन to<BR>kill or injure, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=087-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आघार|आघारः
आघार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Ghee or boiled butter.<BR>	 2. Sprinkling.<BR>	 3. Sprinkling<BR>ghee at certain sacrifices.<BR> E. आङ्, घृ to sprinkle, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=087-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आघूर्णन|आघूर्णनं
आघूर्णन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Rolling, tossing.<BR>	 2. Whirling.<BR> E. आङ् before घूर्ण to<BR>roll, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=087-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आघूर्णित|आघूर्णितं
आघूर्णित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Rolled, rolling.<BR>	 2. Whirled round.<BR> E. आङ्<BR>before घूर्ण to roll, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=087-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आघोषण|आघोषणं
आघोषण n. (-णं) A crying or proclaiming.<BR> E. आङ् before घुष to sound,<BR>affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=087-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आघ्नत्
आघ्नत् mfn. (-घ्नन्-घ्नती-घ्नत्) Striking, beating.<BR> E. आङ् before हन् to kill,<BR>affix शतृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=087-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आघ्राण|आघ्राणं
आघ्राण m. (-णः)<BR>	 1. Smelling.<BR>	 2. Satisfaction, satiety.<BR> E. आङ्, घ्रा to<BR>smell, युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=087-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आघ्रात|आघ्रातः
आघ्रात mfn. (-ताः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Smelled, scented.<BR>	 2. Surmounted, surpassed.<BR>	 3.<BR>Satisfied, satiated.<BR> E. क्त participial affix after आघ्रा to smell, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=087-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आङ्क्षी|आंक्षी
आङ्क्षी f. (-ङ्क्षी) A musical instrument, a tabor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=087-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आङ्ग|आंग|आङ्गं|आङ्गः
आङ्ग mfn. (-ङ्गः-ङ्गी-ङ्गं)<BR>	 1. Bodily, corporeal.<BR>	 2. Having limbs or parts,<BR>or relating to them.<BR>	 3. Relating to the inferior persons of a drama,<BR>to a portion of the Vedas, &c.: see अङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः) A soft delicate<BR>form or body.<BR> E. अङ्ग a body, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=087-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आङ्गक|आंगक|आङ्गकः
आङ्गक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. The ruler of the country Anga.<BR>	 2. An inhabitant of<BR>the same.<BR> E. अङ्ग and वुञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=087-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आङ्गार|आंगार|आंगारं|आङ्गारं
आङ्गार n. (-रं) A multitude of firebrands.<BR> E. आङ्गार a torch, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=087-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आङ्गिक|आंगिक|आङ्गिकः
आङ्गिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>	 1. Bodily, corporeal.<BR>	 2. Gesticulated, expressed<BR>by bodily action, (dramatic sentiment, passion, &c. exhibited by<BR>attitude, gesture, &c.)<BR>	 m. (-कः) A player on a tabor or drum. E.<BR>अङ्ग the body, ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=087-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आङ्गिरस|आंगिरस|आङ्गिरसः
आङ्गिरस m. (-सः) A name of VṚHASPATI, preceptor of the gods. E.<BR>अङ्गिरस् a saint so named, patronymic affix अण्; ANGIRAS being<BR>the father of VṚHASPATI.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=087-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आङ्गुलिक
आङ्गुलिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Like a finger.<BR> E. अङ्गुली and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=087-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचक्षमाण
आचक्षमाण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Saying, declaring.<BR> E. आङ् before चक्ष to speak,<BR>शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=087-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचक्षुस्
आचक्षुस् m. (-क्षुः) A learned man, a Pandit.<BR> E. आङ् before चक्ष् to speak,<BR>उसि Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=087-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचतुर्य्य|आचतुर्य
आचतुर्य्य n. (-र्य्यं) Clumsiness, stupidity.<BR> E. अचतुर and यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=087-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचम|आचमः
आचम m. (-मः) Rincing the mouth: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=087-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचमन|आचमनं
आचमन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Rincing the mouth, sipping water before religious<BR>ceremonies, meals, &c. from the palm of the hand, and spitting it<BR>out again; the ceremony also includes touching the body in various<BR>parts.<BR>	 2. Gargling the throat, &c.<BR> E. आङ् before चम् to eat, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=087-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचमनक|आचमनकं|आचमनकः
आचमनक m. (-कः) A spitting pot.<BR> E. आचमन, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=087-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचमनीय|आचमनीयं
आचमनीय n. (-यं)<BR>	 1. Water for rinsing the mouth.<BR>	 2. A gargle.<BR> E. आङ्<BR>before चम् to eat, affix अनीयर्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=087-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचम्य
आचम्य ind. Having rinsed the mouth, having sipped and rejected a lit-<BR>tle water.<BR> E. आङ् before चम् to eat, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=087-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचरण|आचरणं
आचरण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Following, observing, usage, practice.<BR>	 2. An insti-<BR>tuted rite or rule of conduct.<BR> E. आङ् before चर् to go, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=087-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचरणीय
आचरणीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Right, proper, what is to be followed or ob-<BR>served.<BR> E. आङ् before चर to go, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=087-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचरत्
आचरत् mfn. (-रन्-रन्ती-रत्) Following, practising, observing.<BR> E. आङ्<BR>before चर् to go, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=087-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचरित|आचरितं
आचरित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Observed, practised, either as a rite or usage.<BR>2. Usual, customary.<BR>	 3. Enjoined, fixed by rule.<BR> E. आङ् before चर<BR>to go, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=087-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचर्य्य|आचर्य
आचर्य्य mfn. (-र्य्यः-र्य्या-र्य्यं) To be gone to or approached.<BR> E. आङ् before चर्<BR>to go, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=087-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचान्त|आचांत|आचान्तः
आचान्त mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं)<BR>	 1. Sipped and ejected, (as water.)<BR>	 2. One who has<BR>rinsed his mouth, &c.<BR> E. आङ् before चम् to eat, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=087-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचाम|आचामः
आचाम m. (-मः) Sipping water, rincing the mouth.<BR> E. आङ् before चम्<BR>to eat, affix. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=087-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचाम्य
आचाम्य n. (-म्यं)<BR>	 1. Rincing the mouth, &c.<BR>	 2. Water so used.<BR>	 3. A gar-<BR>gle.<BR> E. आङ् before चम् to eat, ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=087-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचार|आचारः
आचार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. An established rule of conduct, an ordinance, an in-<BR>stitute, a precept.<BR>	 2. Custom, practice, usage.<BR> E. आङ् before चर्<BR>to go, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=087-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचारवर्ज्जित|आचारवर्जित|आचारवर्ज्जितः
आचारवर्ज्जित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Irregular, out or rule.<BR>	 2. Outcaste. E.<BR>आचार an institute, and वर्ज्जित abandoned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=087-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचारहीन
आचारहीन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Outcaste, void of decent or established<BR>practices, unauthorised.<BR> E. आचार and हीन deprived of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=087-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचारिक
आचारिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>	 1. Conformable to rule or practice.<BR>	 2. Pre-<BR>scriptive.<BR> E. आचार and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=087-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचारिन्
आचारिन् mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि) Following established rites or practice. E.<BR>आचार and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=087-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचार्य्य|आचार्य|आचार्यः|आचार्य्यः
आचार्य्य m. (-र्य्यः)<BR>	 1. A spiritual guide or teacher; he who invests the<BR>student with the sacrificial thread, and instructs him in the Vedas,<BR>the law of sacrifice, and religious mysteries.<BR>	 2. A name of DRONA,<BR>the teacher of the Pandus.<BR>	 f. (-र्य्या) A spiritual preceptress.<BR>	 f.<BR>(-र्य्याणी) The wife of an Ācharya or holy teacher.<BR> E. आङ् before चर्<BR>to go, ण्यत् affix, in the fem. टाप् or ङीप् with आनुक् inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=087-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचार्य्यत्व|आचार्यत्व|आचार्यत्वं
आचार्य्यत्व n. (-त्वं) The office or proficiency of a holy teacher.<BR> E. आचार्य्य<BR>and त्व affix; also with तल्, आचार्य्यता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=087-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचार्य्यमिश्र|आचार्यमिश्र
आचार्य्यमिश्र mfn. (-श्रः-श्रा-श्रं) Venerable, honourable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=088-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचार्य्योपासन|आचार्योपासन
आचार्य्योपासन n. (-नं) Waiting upon or serving the spiritual preceptor. E.<BR>आचार्य्य and उपासना worship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=088-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचित|आचितं|आचितः
आचित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Heaped, accumulated.<BR>	 2. Covered.<BR>	 3. Spread,<BR>diffused.<BR>	 mn. (-तः-तं)<BR>	 1. A measure of ten Bhāras.<BR>	 2. A cart-load.<BR>E. आङ् and the past participle of चिञ् to collect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=088-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचितिक
आचितिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Holding an Āchita.<BR> E. आचित and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=088-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचितीन
आचितीन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Holding or equal to an Āchita.<BR> E. आचित and ख<BR>aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=088-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचूषण|आचूषणं
आचूषण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Suction.<BR>	 2. Application of cupping glasses or horns<BR>to the skin, &c.<BR> E. आङ् before चूष to suck, ल्युट्. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=088-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आच्छ|आछ
आच्छ r. 1st. cl. (-इ) आच्छि (आच्छति) To lengthen or stretch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=088-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आच्छन्न|आच्छन्नं
आच्छन्न mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>	 1. Covered.<BR>	 2. Clothed.<BR> E. आङ् before छद to cover,<BR>affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=088-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आच्छाक|आच्छाकः
आच्छाक m. (-कः) A tree, (Morinda tinctoria.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=088-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आच्छाद|आच्छादः|आछाद
आच्छाद m. (-दः) Cloth, clothes.<BR> E. आङ् before छद to cover, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=088-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आच्छादन|आच्छादनं|आछादन
आच्छादन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Cloth, clothes.<BR>	 2. Covering, disappearance.<BR>	 3. A co-<BR>vering, a sheath, mantle, cloak, &c. E. See the last, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=088-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आच्छादित|आच्छादितं
आच्छादित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Covered.<BR>	 2. Clothed.<BR> E. आङ् before छद to<BR>cover, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=088-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आच्छाद्य
आच्छाद्य mfn. (-द्यः-द्या-द्यं) To be covered or clothed. ind. Having clothed<BR>or put on.<BR> E. आङ् before छद to cover, causal form, यत् or ल्यप् affix;<BR>also आच्छादनीय and आच्छादितव्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=088-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आच्छिन्न
आच्छिन्न mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं) Cut, cut off.<BR> E. आङ् before छद to cut, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=088-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आच्छुरित|आच्छुरितं|आछुरित
आच्छुरित n. (-तं)<BR>	 1. A horselaugh.<BR>	 2. Making a noise with the finger<BR>nails by rubbing them on one another.<BR> E. आङ् before छुर to cut, क्त<BR>affix; also आच्छुरितक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=088-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आच्छुरितक|आच्छुरितकं|आछुरितक
आच्छुरितक n. (-कं) See the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=088-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आच्छेद|आच्छेदः
आच्छेद m. (-दः) Cutting, cutting off, excision.<BR> E. आङ् before छिद to cut,<BR>घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=088-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आच्छेदन|आच्छेदनं
आच्छेदन n. (-नं) Excision.<BR> E. आङ् before छिद to cut, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=088-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आच्छोदन|आच्छोदनं|आछोदन
आच्छोदन n. (-नं) Hunting, the chase.<BR> E. आङ् before चुद to command,<BR>with ल्युट् affix, च becomes छ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=088-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आज|आजं|आजः
आज n. (-जं) Oiled butter.<BR> E. आङ् before अज to go, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=088-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आजक|आजकं
आजक n. (-कं) A flock of goats.<BR> E. अज a goat, and वुञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=088-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आजकार|आजकारः
आजकार m. (-रः) ŚIVA'S bull.<BR> E. आज from अज to go, and कार what<BR>makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=088-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आजगव|आजगवं
आजगव n. (-वं) The bow of ŚIVA. E. See अजकाव.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=088-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आजानेय|आजानेयः
आजानेय m. (-यः) A horse of a good breed.<BR> E. अज to go, घञ् affix, आज<BR>going: आनेय to be taken: who carries the rider through all opposi-<BR>tion, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=088-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आजि|आजिः
आजि f. (-जिः)<BR>	 1. War, battle.<BR>	 2. Level ground.<BR>	 3. An instant.<BR>	 4. Abuse,<BR>reviling.<BR>	 5. Going.<BR> E. अज to go, इन् Unādi affix, and आङ् prefixed<BR>or अज with इण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=088-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आजिक्रिया
आजिक्रिया f. (-या) Fighting, making war.<BR> E. आजि and क्रिया act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=088-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आजिगीषु
आजिगीषु mfn. (-षुः-षुः-षु) Ambitious, desirous to excel or overcome. E.<BR>आङ् before जि to conquer, in the desiderative form, affix उस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=088-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आजिग्रह
आजिग्रह mfn. (-हः-हा-हं) What takes or seizes.<BR> E. आङ् before ग्रह to<BR>take, श aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=088-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आजीव|आजीवः
आजीव m. (-वः) Livelihood, subsistence.<BR> E. आङ् before जीव to live, घञ्<BR>aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=088-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आजीवन|आजीवनं
आजीवन n. (-नं) Livelihood.<BR> E. आङ् before जीव to live, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=088-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आजीवनार्थ
आजीवनार्थ n. (-र्थं) Means of livelihood or subsistence, business, profes-<BR>sion.<BR> E. आजीवन and अर्थ means.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=088-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आजीव्य
आजीव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>	 1. Habitable, fertile.<BR>	 2. To be practised as a<BR>means of living.<BR> E. आङ् before जीव्य to be lived, in or by.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=088-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आजुर्
आजुर् f. (-जूः) Working without wages.<BR> E. आङ् before जुर to become<BR>old, क्विप् affix; also आजू.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=088-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आजू
आजू f. (-जूः) See the preceding.<BR> E. आङ् before जु to be quick, क्विप् affix<BR>and the final lengthened; or जन to be born, and डू aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=088-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आज्ञप्त|आज्ञप्तः
आज्ञप्त mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं) Ordered, commanded.<BR> E. आङ् before ज्ञप causal<BR>of ज्ञा and क्त affix; also आज्ञापित.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=088-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आज्ञप्ति|आज्ञप्तिः
आज्ञप्ति f. (-प्तिः) Order, command.<BR> E. आङ् before ज्ञा to know with क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=088-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आज्ञा
आज्ञा f. (-ज्ञा) An order, a command.<BR> E. आङ् before ज्ञा to know, and<BR>अङ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=088-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आज्ञाकर|आज्ञाकरः
आज्ञाकर mfn. (-रः-री-रं) Obeying, obedient, performing an order.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-रः) A servant.<BR> E. आज्ञा and कर who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=088-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आज्ञाकरण
आज्ञाकरण n. (-णं) Obedience, execution of orders.<BR> E. आज्ञा and करण<BR>doing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=088-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आज्ञाकारिन्
आज्ञाकारिन् mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि) Obedient, ministrant, one who obeys or<BR>executes orders.<BR> E. आज्ञा and कारिन् who acts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=088-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आज्ञाचक्र|आज्ञाचक्रं
आज्ञाचक्र n. (-क्रं) A mystical circle or diagram, one of six described by<BR>the Tantras.<BR> E. आज्ञा and चक्र a circle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=088-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आज्ञात
आज्ञात mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Ordered, commanded.<BR> E. आङ् before ज्ञा to know,<BR>affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=088-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आज्ञानुयायिन्
आज्ञानुयायिन् mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि) Obeying or executing orders, obedient. E.<BR>आज्ञा, अनु according to, यायिन् who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=088-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आज्ञानुवर्त्तिन्|आज्ञानुवर्तिन्
आज्ञानुवर्त्तिन् mfn. (-र्त्ती-र्त्तिनी-र्त्ति) Obeying or executing orders.<BR> E. आज्ञा,<BR>अनु according to, and वर्त्तिन् who abides.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=088-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आज्ञानुसारिन्
आज्ञानुसारिन् mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि) Obedient, obeying or executing orders.<BR>E. आज्ञा, अनु according to, सारिन् who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=088-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आज्ञापक|आज्ञापकः
आज्ञापक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Giving orders, a commander, commanding. E.<BR>आङ् before ज्ञा to know, causal form, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=088-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आज्ञापत्र|आज्ञापत्रं
आज्ञापत्र n. (-त्रं) An edict, a written order.<BR> E. आज्ञा and पत्र a page.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=088-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आज्ञापन|आज्ञापनं
आज्ञापन n. (-नं) Ordering, commanding.<BR> E. आङ् before ज्ञा to know,<BR>causal from, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=088-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आज्ञाप्रतिघात|आज्ञाप्रतिघातः
आज्ञाप्रतिघात m. (-तः) Disobedience, rebellion.<BR> E. आज्ञा and प्रतिघात re-<BR>belling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=088-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आज्ञाभङ्ग|आज्ञाभंग|आज्ञाभङ्गः
आज्ञाभङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः) Disobedience, insubordination, disloyalty.<BR> E. आज्ञा<BR>and भङ्ग breaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=088-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आज्ञावह
आज्ञावह mfn. (-हः-हा-हं) Obedient, subject, ministrant.<BR> E. आज्ञा and वह<BR>who bears.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=088-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आज्ञासम्पादिन्|आज्ञासंपादिन्
आज्ञासम्पादिन् mfn. (-दी-दिनी-दि) Obedient, submissive.<BR> E. आज्ञा and सम्पा-<BR>दिन् who executes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=088-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आज्यप
आज्यप m. (-पः) A Pitṛ or progenitor of a class of Pitṛs who are the<BR>sons of PULASTYA, and the ancestors of the Vaiśya order.<BR> E. आज्य<BR>ghee, and प who drinks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=088-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आज्यभास
आज्यभास m. (-सः) Offering ghee at certain ceremonies.<BR> E. आज्य and भास<BR>what shines.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=088-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आञ्चन|आंचनं
आञ्चन n. (-नं) Partial extraction of thorns or arrows and the like from<BR>the body.<BR> E. आङ् before अञ्च् to go, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=088-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आञ्जनेय|आंजनेयः|आञ्जनेयः
आञ्जनेय m. (-यः) A name of the monkey HANUMĀN.<BR> E. अञ्जना the mother<BR>of HANUMĀN, and ढक् patronymic affix which leaves एय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=088-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आञ्जिनेय|आंजिनेयः|आञ्जिनेयः
आञ्जिनेय m. (-यः) An insect, a kind of lizard.<BR> E. अञ्जन antimony, ढक्<BR>affix, and इट् inserted; from the blue tint of the animal's back.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=088-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आटविक|आटविकः
आटविक m. (-कः) A woodman.<BR> E. अटवी a wood, and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=088-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आटरूष|आटरूषः
आटरूष m. (-पः) A tree, (Justicia adhenatoda, &c.) E. See अटरुष. the अ<BR>being made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=088-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आटि|आटिः
आटि m. (-टिः) The Śarali, a bird so called, (Turdus ginginianus.) E.<BR>आङ् before अट to go, इन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=088-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आटीकन|आटीकनं
आटीकन n. (-नं) The leaping motion of a calf.<BR> E. आङ् prefixed to टीक<BR>to go, ल्युट् affix; also written आटीकर and आटीलक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=088-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आटीकर|आटीकरः
आटीकर m. (-रः) A bull.<BR> E. आटीक leaping, and र who gets or uses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=088-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आटोप|आटोपः
आटोप m. (-पः)<BR>	 1. Pride.<BR>	 2. Flatulence, borborygmi.<BR> E. आङ् before टुप<BR>a Sautra root, to be proud, and घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=088-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आडम्बर|आडंबरः|आडम्बरः
आडम्बर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Charge sounded by musical instruments.<BR>	 2. The<BR>roaring of elephants.<BR>	 3. A drum used in battle.<BR>	 4. Commencement.<BR>5. The eyelid.<BR>	 6. Pride, arrogance.<BR>	 7. Anger, passion.<BR>	 8. Happi-<BR>ness, pleasure.<BR>	 n. (-रं) Rubbing and moulding the body.<BR> E. आङ्<BR>before दम to tame or subdue, वरच् affix; द is changed to ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=088-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आडम्बरिन्|आडंबरिन्
आडम्बरिन् mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि) Proud, arrogant.<BR> E. आडम्बर and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=089-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आडि|आडिः
आडि f. (-डिः) A bird, the Śarali, (Turdus ginginianus.)<BR> E. आङ् before<BR>अड to go, इन् affix; also आटि, आडिका and आटी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=089-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आडू
आडू m. (-डूः) A raft, a float.<BR> E. अ neg. अण to sound, ड and ऊ Unādi affixes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=089-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आढक|आढकं|आढकः
आढक mfn. (-कः-की-का-कं) A measure of grain equal to four Prasthas<BR>or containing nearly 7lbs. 11 oz. avoirdupois: in Bengal an<BR>Araka is equal to two mons or 164lbs. avds.<BR>	 f. (-की)<BR>	 1. A kind<BR>of pulse, (Cytisus cajan.)<BR>	 2. A fragrant earth: see तुवरी.<BR> E. आङ्,<BR>ढोक to go, irregularly अच्, fem. ङीप् or टाप् with इक् inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=089-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आढकिक|आढकिकः
आढकिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>	 1. Sown with an Āḍhaka of seed, (a field,<BR>&c.)<BR>	 2. Holding or containing the same.<BR> E. आढक the measure, and<BR>ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=089-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आढकीन|आढकीनः
आढकीन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) See the preceding.<BR> E. आढक, ख aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=089-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आढ्य|आढ्यः
आढ्य mfn. (-ढ्यः-ढ्या-ढ्यं)<BR>	 1. Opulent, wealthy, rich.<BR>	 2. Abounding in, pro-<BR>ductive.<BR>	 3. Having, being possessed of.<BR> E. आङ्, ध्यै to consider,<BR>to meditate, क irregular aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=089-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आढ्यङ्करण|आढ्यंकरण
आढ्यङ्करण n. (-णं) Enriching, or the means of enriching, wealth, pros-<BR>perity.<BR> E. आढ्य and ख्युन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=089-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आढ्यचर
आढ्यचर mfn. (-रः-री-रं) Formerly opulent.<BR> E. आढ्य and चरट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=089-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आढ्यम्भविष्णु|आढ्यंभविष्णु
आढ्यम्भविष्णु mfn. (-ष्णुः-ष्णु-ष्णु) Becoming rich or eminent.<BR> E. आढ्य and भू<BR>to be, खिष्णुच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=089-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आढ्यम्भावुक|आढ्यंभावुक
आढ्यम्भावुक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Becoming rich or eminent.<BR> E. आढ्य and भू<BR>to be, with खकञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=089-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आणक|आणकः
आणक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Low, inferior: see आणक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=089-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आणवीन|आणवीनं
आणवीन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Bearing or fit to bear panic.<BR> E. अणु panic, and<BR>खञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=089-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आणि|आणिः
आणि mf. (-णिः)<BR>	 1. The edge of a sword.<BR>	 2. The pin of the axle of a<BR>cart.<BR>	 3. A limit, a boundary.<BR> E. अण to sound, इन् affix, the pen.<BR>long; also अणि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=089-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आण्ड|आंड|आण्डः
आण्ड n. (-ण्डं) A multitude of eggs, &c.<BR> E. अण्ड and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=089-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आण्डीर|आंडीर
आण्डीर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Having many eggs, &c.<BR> E. आण्ड and ईरच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=089-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतङ्क|आतंक|आतंकः|आतङ्कः
आतङ्क m. (-ङ्कः)<BR>	 1. Fear, apprehension.<BR>	 2. Disease, sickness.<BR>	 3. Afflic-<BR>tion, pain.<BR>	 4. Fever.<BR>	 5. The sound of a drum or tabor.<BR> E. आङ्,<BR>तकि to live in distress, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=089-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतञ्चन|आतंचनं|आतञ्चनं
आतञ्चन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Calcining, adding a powder or flux to metals in fusion.<BR>2. The flux so used.<BR>	 3. Casting any thing into another to effect<BR>some change, as butter milk into fresh milk to turn it.<BR>	 4. Casting<BR>away, destroying.<BR>	 5. Danger, calamity, as a pestilence or epidemic.<BR>6. Speed, velocity.<BR>	 7. Gratifying, satisfying.<BR> E. आङ्, तञ्चु to go,<BR>and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=089-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतत
आतत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Spread, extended.<BR> E. आङ् before तन to spread, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=089-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आततायिता
आततायिता f. (-ता) Stealing, persecuting, murdering, destroying. E.<BR>आततायिन् and तल् affix; also with त्व affix, आततायित्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=089-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आततायिन्
आततायिन् mfn. (-यि-यिनी-यि) A felon, a thief, a murderer, incendiary,<BR>ravisher, &c.<BR> E. आतत extended, every where, ई to go, and णिनि<BR>affix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=089-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतन|आतनं
आतन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Sight, view.<BR>	 2. Spreading, expanding.<BR> E. आङ् be-<BR>fore तन to spread, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=089-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतप|आतपः
आतप m. (-पः) Sun-shine.<BR> E. आङ् before तप to heat, to shine, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=089-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतपत्र|आतपत्रं
आतपत्र n. (-त्रं) A large umbrella of silk or leaves, used in the east as<BR>a parasol.<BR> E. आतप sun-shine, त्र what preserves.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=089-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतपत्रक|आतपत्रकं
आतपत्रक n. (-कं) A small umbrella, a mat or basket carried on the<BR>head as one.<BR> E. आतपत्र a parasol, and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=089-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतपवारण|आतपवारणं
आतपवारण n. (-णं) A Chattah or Indian parasol.<BR> E. आतप sun-shine,<BR>and वारण preventing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=089-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतपशुष्क
आतपशुष्क mfn. (-ष्कः-ष्का-ष्कं) Dried in the sun, evaporated by the solar<BR>heat.<BR> E. आतप and शुष्क dry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=089-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतपाभाव|आतपाभावः
आतपाभाव m. (-वः) Shade.<BR> E. आतप and अभाव nonexistence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=089-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतर|आतरः
आतर m. (-रः) Fare, freight.<BR> E. आङ्, तृ to cross or pass over, अप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=089-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतर्पण|आतर्पणं
आतर्पण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Satisfying, satisfaction.<BR>	 2. Whitening the wall or<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=089-b" target="_blank">Page089-b+ 60</a>]<BR>floor or seat on festival occasions.<BR> E. आङ्, तृप to satisfy or to be<BR>satisfied, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=089-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतापिन्
आतापिन् m. (-पी) A kite. E. See the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=089-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतायिन्
आतायिन् m. (-यी) A kite.<BR> E. आङ् before ताय to spread, णिनि affix; it is<BR>also read आतापिन्, from तप to be warm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=089-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतार|आतारः
आतार m. (-रः) Fare, freight.<BR> E. आङ्, तृ to cross, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=089-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आति|आतिः
आति m. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. A bird.<BR>	 2. Going.<BR> E. अत् to go, इण् affix: or Unādi<BR>affix इन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=089-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतिथेय|आतिथेयः
आतिथेय mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>	 1. Proper for a guest.<BR>	 2. Hospitable, attentive<BR>to a guest.<BR> E. अतिथि a guest, and ढञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=089-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतिथ्य|आतिथ्यं|आतिथ्यः
आतिथ्य mfn. (-थ्यः-थ्या-थ्यं)<BR>	 1. Proper for a guest.<BR>	 2. Hospitable, attent-<BR>ive to a guest.<BR>	 n. (-थ्यं) Hospitality.<BR>	 m. (-थ्यः) A guest.<BR> E. अतिथि<BR>and ज्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=089-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतिरेक्य|आतिरेक्यं
आतिरेक्य n. (-क्यं) Excess, superfluity.<BR> E. अतिरेक exceeding, ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=089-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतिशय्य|आतिशय्यं
आतिशय्य n. (-य्यं) Excess, quantity.<BR> E. अतिशय much, and यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=089-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतु|आतुः
आतु m. (-तुः) A raft, a float.<BR> E. आङ्, तृ to cross, and डु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=089-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतुर|आतुरः
आतुर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Diseased.<BR> E. आङ् before तुर to hasten, क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=089-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतृप्य|आतृप्यं|आतृप्यः
आतृप्य mfn. (-प्यः-प्या-प्यं) Satisfiable, to be satisfied.<BR>	 m. (-प्यः) The custard<BR>apple tree, (Annona reticulata.)<BR>	 n. (-प्यं) The fruit.<BR> E. आङ् before<BR>तृप् to satisfy, क्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=089-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतोद्य|आतोद्यं
आतोद्य n. (-द्यं) A musical instrument.<BR> E. आङ् before तुद to torment, ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=089-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्त
आत्त mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं)<BR>	 1. Taken, accepted.<BR>	 2. Assumed.<BR>	 3. Attracted. E.<BR>आङ before दा to give, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=089-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्तगन्ध|आत्तगन्धः
आत्तगन्ध mfn. (-न्धः-न्धा-न्धं)<BR>	 1. Humbled, degraded.<BR>	 2. Perfumed.<BR> E. आत्त<BR>taken, and गन्ध pride; whose pride is taken down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=089-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्तगर्व्व|आत्तगर्व|आत्तगर्व्वः
आत्तगर्व्व mfn. (-र्व्वः-र्व्वा-र्व्वं) Humbled, &c. see the preceding. E. As before,<BR>गर्व्व pride.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=089-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मकर्म्मन्|आत्मकर्मन्
आत्मकर्म्मन् n. (-र्म्म) One's own act.<BR> E. आत्मन् and कर्म्म act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=089-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मकृत
आत्मकृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Self-executed, done of one's self.<BR> E. आत्मन् and<BR>कृत done.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=089-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मगुप्ता
आत्मगुप्ता f. (-प्ता) A plant, Cowach, (Carpopogon pruriens.)<BR> E. आत्मन् self,<BR>गुप्त hidden; self-preserved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=089-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मग्राहिन्
आत्मग्राहिन् mfn. (-ही-हिणी-हि) Selfish, greedy, taking care of one's self,<BR>appropriating, taking for one's self.<BR> E. आत्मन् and ग्राहिन् who seizes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=089-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मघात|आत्मघातः
आत्मघात m. (-तः)<BR>	 1. Suicide.<BR>	 2. Heresy, schism.<BR> E. आत्मन् and घात killing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=089-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मघातिन्
आत्मघातिन् mfn. (-ती-तिनी-ति)<BR>	 1. A suicide.<BR>	 2. A heretic, a schismatic,<BR>one who disregards the moral or religious institutions of the code.<BR>E. आत्मन् and घातिन् who kills.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=089-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मघोष|आत्मघोषः
आत्मघोष m. (-षः)<BR>	 1. A crow.<BR>	 2. A cock.<BR> E. आत्मन्, घुषि to sound, and घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=089-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मज|आत्मजः
आत्मज m. (-जः) A son.<BR>	 f. (-जा)<BR>	 1. A daughter.<BR>	 2. The understanding. E.<BR>आत्मन् the body or soul, and ज born, produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=089-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मजन्मन्
आत्मजन्मन् m. (-न्मा) A son.<BR> E. आत्मन् and जन्मन् birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=089-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मज्ञ|आत्मज्ञः
आत्मज्ञ m. (-ज्ञः) A sage, one who knows his own nature and that of<BR>spirit.<BR> E. आत्मन् and ज्ञ who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=089-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मज्ञान
आत्मज्ञान n. (-नं) Spiritual knowledge, true wisdom.<BR> E. आत्मन् and ज्ञान<BR>knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=089-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मगत|आत्मगतं
आत्मगत ind. (-तं) Apart, to one's self, (in theatrical language.)<BR> E. आत्मन्<BR>and गत gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=089-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मतत्त्व|आत्मतत्त्वं
आत्मतत्त्व n. (-त्वं) The nature of spirit.<BR> E. आत्मन् and तत्त्व truth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=089-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मतत्त्वज्ञ
आत्मतत्त्वज्ञ m. (-ज्ञः) A sage, especially one versed in the Vedanta doc-<BR>trines.<BR> E. आत्मतत्त्व and ज्ञ who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=089-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मता
आत्मता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Identity with self.<BR>	 2. Spirituality.<BR> E. आत्मन् and तल्<BR>affix; also with त्व affix, आत्मत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=089-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मत्यागिन्
आत्मत्यागिन् m. (-गी)<BR>	 1. A suicide.<BR>	 2. A heretic, an unbeliever.<BR> E. आत्मन्<BR>and त्यागिन् who deserts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=089-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मदर्श|आत्मदर्शः
आत्मदर्श m. (-र्शः) A mirror.<BR> E. आत्मन् and दर्श sight, seeing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=089-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मदर्शन
आत्मदर्शन n. (-नं) Knowledge of man's real nature, spiritual knowledge.<BR>E. आत्मन् and दर्शन seeing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=089-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मद्रोहिन्
आत्मद्रोहिन् mfn. (-ही-हिणी-हि) Self-tormenting, fretful, miserable.<BR> E. आत्मन्<BR>and द्रोहिन् who torments.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=089-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मन्
आत्मन् m. (-त्मा)<BR>	 1. The soul.<BR>	 2. The natural temperament or disposition.<BR>3. BRAHM, the supreme deity and soul of the universe, or more<BR>usually in this sense परमात्मा.<BR>	 4. Life, spirit, the vivifying soul in<BR>opposition to the sentient; commonly also जीवात्मा.<BR>	 5. Body.<BR>	 6.<BR>Care, effort, pains.<BR>	 7. Firmness.<BR>	 8. The understanding, the intellect.<BR>9. The mind or faculty of reason.<BR>	 10. The sun.<BR>	 11. Fire.<BR>	 12. Wind,<BR>air.<BR>	 13. A son.<BR>	 14. The self, the abstract individual.<BR> E. आङ्, अत to<BR>go, मनिन् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=090-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मनीन|आत्मनीनं|आत्मनीनः
आत्मनीन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>	 1. Existent, sentient.<BR>	 2. Appropriate, good<BR>for, fit for.<BR>	 3. Suitable. (as diet, &c.)<BR>	 m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. A son.<BR>	 2. A wife's<BR>brother.<BR>	 3. A jester.<BR> E. आत्मन् and ख aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=090-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मनेपद|आत्मनेपदं
आत्मनेपद n. (-दं) The middle voice, the proper form of the verb.<BR> E. आत्मने<BR>to one's self, पद inflected word.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=090-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मबन्धु|आत्मबन्धुः
आत्मबन्धु m. (-न्धुः) One's own kinsman, a first cousin or father's sister's<BR>son, mother's brother's son, mother's sister's son.<BR> E. आत्मन् own,<BR>and बन्धु relative.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=090-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मबुद्धि
आत्मबुद्धि f. (-द्धिः)<BR>	 1. Self-knowledge.<BR>	 2. One's own knowledge.<BR> E. आत्मन्<BR>and बुद्धि knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=090-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मबोध|आत्मबोधः
आत्मबोध m. (-धः) Spiritual instruction.<BR> E. आत्मन् and बोध causing to<BR>know.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=090-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मभाव|आत्मभावः
आत्मभाव m. (-वः) Proper or peculiar nature.<BR> E. आत्मन् and भाव disposition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=090-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मभू
आत्मभू mfn. (-भू-भूः-भु) Self-born, self-existent.<BR>	 m. (-भूः)<BR>	 1. A name of<BR>BMAHMĀ.<BR>	 2. Of KĀMADEVA.<BR>	 3. Of VIṢṆU, and 4. Of ŚIVA. E.<BR>आत्मन् self, and भू being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=090-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मभूत|आत्मभूतः
आत्मभूत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Self-produced.<BR>	 2. Own, peculiar, belonging to.<BR>3. Attached to, faithful.<BR> E. आत्मन् and भूत become.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=090-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्ममानिन्
आत्ममानिन् mfn. (-नी-निनी-नि) Respecting one's self, decorous, respect-<BR>able.<BR> E. आत्मन् and मानिन् respecting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=090-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्ममूली
आत्ममूली f. (-ली) A plant, (Hedysarum alhagi:) see दुरालभा.<BR> E. आत्मन् and मूल a root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=090-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मम्भरि|आत्मंभरि|आत्मम्भरिः
आत्मम्भरि mfn. (-रिः-रिः-रि) Selfish, greedy.<BR> E. आत्मन् self and भरि who-<BR>nourishes, from भृ to nourish, with खि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=090-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मयाजिन्
आत्मयाजिन् m. (-जी) A wise or learned man, one who studies his own<BR>nature and that of the soul.<BR> E. आत्मन् and याजिन् who worships.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=090-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मयोनि|आत्मयोनिः
आत्मयोनि m. (-निः)<BR>	 1. A name of BRAHMĀ.<BR>	 2. Of ŚIVA.<BR>	 3. Of VIṢṆU,<BR>and 4. Of KĀMADEVA.<BR> E. आत्मन् self, and योनि the place of birth:<BR>see आत्मभू.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=090-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मलोमन्
आत्मलोमन् n. (-म)<BR>	 1. The beard.<BR>	 2. The hair of the body.<BR> E. आत्मन् and<BR>लोमन् hair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=090-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मवत्|आत्मवन्त्
आत्मवत् ind. Like one's self.<BR> E. आत्मन् and वति aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=090-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मवत्|आत्मवन्त्
आत्मवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>	 1. Prudent, considerate.<BR>	 2. Self-possessed,<BR>composed, calm.<BR> E. आत्मन् and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=090-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मवत्ता
आत्मवत्ता f. (-त्ता)<BR>	 1. Self-resemblance.<BR>	 2. Proportion, analogy.<BR>	 3. Pru-<BR>dence, self-regard.<BR> E. तल् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=090-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मवश|आत्मवशः
आत्मवश m. (-शः) Subjection of the mind, self-control, self-government.<BR>E. आत्मन् and वश subjection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=090-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मविद्
आत्मविद् m. (-विद्)<BR>	 1. A sensible man, one who knows himself.<BR>	 2. A wise<BR>man, a sage, one who knows the nature of the soul or spirit. E.<BR>आत्मन् and विद् who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=090-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मविद्या
आत्मविद्या f. (-द्या) Spiritual knowledge.<BR> E. आत्मन् and विद्या science.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=090-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मविवृद्धि|आत्मविवृद्धिः
आत्मविवृद्धि f. (-द्धिः) Self-advantage.<BR> E. आत्मन् and विवृद्धि increase.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=090-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मवीर|आत्मवीरः
आत्मवीर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>	 1. Existent, sentient.<BR>	 2. Appropriate, good for<BR>one's self.<BR>	 3. Suitable, (as diet, &c.)<BR>	 m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A wife's brother.<BR>	 2.<BR>A jester.<BR> E. आत्मन् and वीर heroic, strong.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=090-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मवृत्ति|आत्मवृत्तिः
आत्मवृत्ति f. (-त्तिः) Practising one's duties or occupation.<BR> E. आत्मन् and<BR>वृत्ति profession.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=090-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मशक्ति|आत्मशक्तिः
आत्मशक्ति f. (-क्तिः) Inherent or own power.<BR> E. आत्मन् self, and शक्ति power.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=090-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मशुद्धि|आत्मशुद्धिः
आत्मशुद्धि f. (-द्धिः) Self-purification.<BR> E. आत्मन् and शुद्धि purity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=090-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मश्लाघा
आत्मश्लाघा f. (-घा) Boasting.<BR> E. आत्मन् self, श्लाघा praise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=090-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मसंयम|आत्मसंयमः
आत्मसंयम m. (-मः) Self-restraint, stoicism.<BR> E. आत्मन् self, and संयम restraint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=090-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मसन्देह|आत्मसंदेह|आत्मसंदेहः
आत्मसन्देह m. (-हः) Internal doubt.<BR> E. आत्मन् and सन्देह doubt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=090-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मसम्भव|आत्मसंभव|आत्मसंभवः
आत्मसम्भव m. (-वः) A son.<BR> E. आत्मन् and सम्भव birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=090-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मसात्
आत्मसात् ind. One's own.<BR> E. आत्मन् and सात् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=090-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मसात्कृत
आत्मसात्कृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Appropriated, made one's own.<BR> E. आत्मसात् and कृत made.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=090-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मसिद्धि|आत्मसिद्धिः
आत्मसिद्धि f. (-द्धिः) Self-advantage.<BR> E. आत्मन् and सिद्धि accomplishment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=090-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्महत्या
आत्महत्या f. (-त्या) Suicide, self-destruction.<BR> E. आत्मन् and हत्या killing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=090-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्महन्
आत्महन् m. (-हा)<BR>	 1. A suicide, a self-murderer.<BR>	 2. A heretic, an unbeliever.<BR>3. A priest in a temple, a servant or attendant upon an idol. E.<BR>आत्मन् and हन् who kills or destroys, self-destroying; the priest<BR>subsisting by appropriating to himself offerings to deities, for<BR>which future punishment is assigned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=090-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्महनन
आत्महनन n. (-नं) Suicide.<BR> E. आत्मन् and हनन killing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=090-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्महित
आत्महित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Beneficial to one's self.<BR> E. आत्मन् and हित good for.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=090-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मादिष्ट|आत्मादिष्टः
आत्मादिष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं) Self-counselled.<BR>	 m. (-ष्टः) A treaty dictated by<BR>the party wishing it himself.<BR> E. आत्मन् and आदिष्ट directed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=090-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्माधीन|आत्माधीनः
आत्माधीन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Sentient, existent.<BR>	 m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. A wife's brother.<BR>2. A censorious man.<BR>	 3. A son.<BR> E. आत्मन् and अधीन dependent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=090-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मापहारक|आत्मापहारकः
आत्मापहारक m. (-कः) An impostor, one who pretends to belong to a<BR>higher class than his own.<BR> E. आत्मन् and अपहारक a plunderer: who<BR>steals himself.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=090-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मार्थ
आत्मार्थ mfn. (-र्थः-र्था-र्थं) For one's own sake, for the sake of one's self. E.<BR>आत्मन् and अर्थ object.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=090-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्माशिन्
आत्माशिन् m. (-शी) A fish.<BR> E. आत्मन्, अश् to eat, णिनि affix; supposed to<BR>eat its young.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=090-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्माश्रय|आत्माश्रयः
आत्माश्रय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. Self-dependence.<BR>	 2. Innate idea, abstract knowledge,<BR>independent of the thing to be known.<BR> E. आत्मन् self, and आश्रय<BR>asylum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=090-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मीय|आत्मीयः
आत्मीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>	 1. Cognate, related, of kin.<BR>	 2. Own.<BR> E. आत्मन् and छण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=090-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मोदय|आत्मोदयः
आत्मोदय m. (-यः) Self-advantage or elevation.<BR> E. आत्मन् and उदय rising.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=090-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मोपम|आत्मोपमः
आत्मोपम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं) Like one's self.<BR> E. आत्मन् and उपमा resemblance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=090-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मोपजीविन्
आत्मोपजीविन् mfn. (-वी-विनी-वि)<BR>	 1. A public performer, actor, singer,<BR>dancer, &c.<BR>	 2. A day-labourer.<BR> E. आत्मन् self, उपजीविन् who subsists:<BR>who lives by his own exertions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=090-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मोद्भव|आत्मोद्भवः
आत्मोद्भव mfn. (-वः-वा-वं) Born or produced from one's self.<BR>	 m. (-वः) A<BR>son.<BR>	 f. (-वा)<BR>	 1. A daughter.<BR>	 2. A plant, (Glycine debilis.)<BR> E. आत्मन्<BR>and उद्भव born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=090-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्यन्तिक|आत्यंतिक
आत्यन्तिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>	 1. Supreme.<BR>	 2. Excessive, abundant.<BR>	 3. In-<BR>finite.<BR> E. अत्यन्त exceeding, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=090-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्ययिक
आत्ययिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>	 1. Ill-omened, unpropitious.<BR>	 2. Destructive.<BR>	 3.<BR>Disastrous.<BR>	 4. Distressing, painful.<BR> E. अत्यय destruction, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=090-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्यूह|आत्यूहः
आत्यूह m. (-हः) A gallinule: see दात्यूह.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=090-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्रेय|आत्रेयः
आत्रेय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. The name of a Muni or saint, the son of ATRI, applica-<BR>ble to DATTA, DURVASAS, and SOMA.<BR>	 2. An essential humor or<BR>juice of the body.<BR>	 f. (-यिका or -यी) A woman during her courses.<BR>	 f.<BR>(-यी)<BR>	 1. The name of a river in the north of Bengal.<BR>	 2. The wife of<BR>ATRI.<BR>	 3. Any woman of the Brahmanical order.<BR> E. अत्रि a saint so<BR>called, ढक् patronymic aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=090-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आथर्व्वण|आथर्वण|आथर्वणः|आथर्व्वणं|आथर्व्वणः
आथर्व्वण m. (-णः)<BR>	 1. A family priest.<BR>	 2. A Brahman versed in the Athar-<BR>van Veda.<BR>	 n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. A collection of prayers, &c. delivered by ATHAR-<BR>VAN, a sage.<BR>	 2. A private apartment in which after sacrifice, the<BR>sacrificer receives absolution from the officiating Brahman. E.<BR>अथर्व्वण a Veda, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=090-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आथर्व्वणिक|आथर्वणिक|आथर्वणिकः
आथर्व्वणिक m. (-कः) A Brahman who has studied the Atharva Veda.<BR>E. अथर्व्वण and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=090-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदत्त
आदत्त mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं) Taken, received.<BR> E. आङ् before दा to give, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=090-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आददान
आददान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Taking, accepting.<BR> E. आङ् before दा to give,<BR>affix शानच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=090-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदधान
आदधान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Having, possessing.<BR> E. आङ् before धा to have,<BR>शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=090-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदर|आदरः
आदर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Respect, reverence.<BR>	 2. Commencement, beginning. E.<BR>आङ्, दृ to have, अप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=090-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदरणीय
आदरणीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>	 1. Venerable, respectable.<BR>	 2. To be attended to.<BR>E. आङ् before दृ to have, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=091-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदर्त्तव्य|आदर्तव्य
आदर्त्तव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं) To be respected or regarded.<BR> E. आङ्, दृ and तव्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=091-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदर्य्य|आदर्य|आदर्य्यः
आदर्य्य mfn. (-र्य्यः-र्य्या-र्य्यं) Venerable, respectable.<BR> E. आङ् before दृ to<BR>have, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=091-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदर्श|आदर्शः
आदर्श m. (-र्शः)<BR>	 1. A Mirror.<BR>	 2. A commentary.<BR>	 3. The original manus-<BR>cript from which a copy is taken.<BR> E. आङ्, दृशि to see, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=091-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदर्शन|आदर्शनं
आदर्शन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Showing, making apparent or seen.<BR>	 2. A mirror. E.<BR>आङ् before दृश to see, causal form, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=091-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदर्शित
आदर्शित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Shown, made apparent.<BR> E. आङ् before दृश to<BR>see, causal form, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=091-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदान|आदानं
आदान n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Taken, receipt, acceptance.<BR>	 2. A horse's trappings.<BR>3. A symptom.<BR>	 f. (-नी) A plant: see हस्तिघोषा.<BR> E. आङ् reversing the<BR>sense, and दा to give, ल्युट् affix, fem. ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=091-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदाय|आदायः
आदाय ind. Having taken.<BR> E. आङ् before दा to give, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=091-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदायचर
आदायचर mfn. (-रः-री-रं) Who goes away after taking any thing.<BR> E. आदाय,<BR>चर to go, ट aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=091-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदि|आदिः
आदि m. only (-दिः)<BR>	 1. First, prior.<BR>	 2. First, pre-eminent. ind. (In<BR>composition,) Other, et-cetera, as स्वादि the affix सु et-cetera. E.<BR>आङ् before दा to give, and कि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=091-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदिकर|आदिकरः
आदिकर m. (-रः) BRAHMĀ, the creator.<BR> E. आदि and कर who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=091-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदिकर्त्तृ|आदिकर्तृ
आदिकर्त्तृ m. (-र्त्ता) BRAHMĀ, as the creator.<BR> E. आदि and कर्त्तृ who<BR>makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=091-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदिकवि|आदिकविः
आदिकवि m. (-विः)<BR>	 1. A name of BRAHMĀ.<BR>	 2. A name of VALMIKI, the<BR>first mortal poet.<BR> E. आदि the first, and कवि a poet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=091-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदिकारण|आदिकारणं
आदिकारण n. (-णं) A primary cause.<BR> E. आदि and कारण cause.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=091-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदितस्
आदितस् ind. From the first, from the beginning.<BR> E. आदि and तसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=091-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदितेय|आदितेयः
आदितेय m. (-यः) A deity, a divinity.<BR> E. अदिति the mother of the gods.<BR>and ढक् derivative aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=091-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदित्य|आदित्यः
आदित्य m. (-त्यः)<BR>	 1. A deity in general.<BR>	 2. A deity of a particular class;<BR>the ADITYAS are twelve in number, they are forms of SŪRYA or the<BR>sun, and appear to represent him as distinct in each month of<BR>the year.<BR>	 3. The sun.<BR> E. अदिति the mother of the gods, and घञ्<BR>derivative aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=091-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदित्यपुष्पिका
आदित्यपुष्पिका f. (-का) Red swallow wort.<BR> E. आदित्य the sun, and पुष्पिका<BR>having a flower, the flower of the sun, from its red colour: see<BR>अर्कपुष्पिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=091-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदित्यमण्डल
आदित्यमण्डल n. (-लं) The disc or orb of the sun.<BR> E. आदित्य and मण्डल a circle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=091-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदित्यसूनु|आदित्यसूनुः
आदित्यसूनु m. (-नुः)<BR>	 1. A name of SUGRĪVA, a monkey king; 2. of YAMA;<BR>3. of SANI or SATURN.<BR> E. आदित्य the sun, and सूनु a son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=091-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदित्व|आदित्वं
आदित्व n. (-त्वं) Priority, precedence.<BR> E. आदि and त्व added; also आदिता<BR>with तल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=091-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदित्सा
आदित्सा f. (-ता) Wish to seize.<BR> E. आङ् before दा to give, desiderative<BR>from, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=091-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदित्सु
आदित्सु mfn. (-त्सुः-त्सुः-त्सु) Wishing to take or have.<BR> E. आङ् before दा<BR>to give, desiderative form, उस् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=091-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदिदेव|आदिदेवः
आदिदेव m. (-वः) Name of VIṢṆU or NARAYANA.<BR> E. आदि the first, and<BR>देव a god, the first god, the creator.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=091-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदिपुरुष|आदिपुरुषः
आदिपुरुष m. (-षः) The first male, usually applied to VIṢṆU.<BR> E. आदि the<BR>first, and पुरुष a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=091-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदिभूत|आदिभूतः
आदिभूत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) First born or existent.<BR>	 m. (-तः) BRAHMĀ.<BR> E. आदि<BR>and भूत been.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=091-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदिम|आदिमं
आदिम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं) First, prior.<BR> E. आदि and डिमच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=091-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदिराज|आदिराजः
आदिराज m. (-जः) The name of a king; also पृथु.<BR> E. आदि and राजन् a king,<BR>the first king; he was a form of VIṢṆU, and husband of Prithivi<BR>or the earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=091-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदिवराह|आदिवराहः
आदिवराह m. (-हः) A name of VIṢṆU.<BR> E. आदि and वराह a boar; the<BR>first boar, alluding to VIṢṆU'S avatara or incarnation in that<BR>form; also similar compounds, as आदिशूकरः, आद्यकोलः, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=091-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदिष्ट|आदिष्टं|आदिष्टः
आदिष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>	 1. Commanded, directed.<BR>	 2. Appointed.<BR>	 3. Ad-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=091-b" target="_blank">Page091-b+ 60</a>]<BR>viced, enjoined.<BR>	 4. Said.<BR>	 n. (-ष्टं) Fragments or leavings of a meal.<BR>E. आङ् before दिश् to point or show, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=091-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदिष्टिन्
आदिष्टिन् m. (-ष्टी)<BR>	 1. A student, a Brahman in the first order.<BR>	 2. A<BR>penite, one engaged in any expiatory rite.<BR> E. आदिष्ट what is in-<BR>structed, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=091-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदीनव|आदीनवं|आदीनवः
आदीनव m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. Distress, pain, uneasiness.<BR>	 2. Fault, transgression.<BR>3. An inflictor of distress.<BR> E. आङ् before दीङ् to decay, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=091-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदीपन|आदीपनं
आदीपन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Whitening the wall, floor, or seat, &c. upon festi-<BR>val occasions.<BR>	 2. Embellishing.<BR>	 3. Inflaming, exciting.<BR> E. आङ्, दीप्<BR>to beautify, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=091-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदीपित
आदीपित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Illuminated.<BR> E. आङ् before दीप् to inflame, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=091-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदृत|आदृतः
आदृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Respectful.<BR>	 2. Respected, honoured, worship-<BR>ped.<BR>	 3. Zealous, diligent.<BR> E. आङ् before दृञ् to have, and क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=091-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदृत्य|आदृत्यः
आदृत्य mfn. (-त्यः-त्या-त्यं) Venerable, respectable.<BR> E. आङ् before दृ to have,<BR>क्यप् affix; तुक् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=091-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदेय
आदेय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Receivable, leviable, what may be taken or re-<BR>ceived.<BR> E. आङ् before दा to give, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=091-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदेवक
आदेवक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) One who sports or plays.<BR> E. आङ् before दिन to<BR>sport, वुञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=091-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदेश|आदेशः
आदेश m. (-शः)<BR>	 1. An order, a command.<BR>	 2. Advice, instruction.<BR>	 3. (In<BR>grammar,) A substitute.<BR>	 4. (In astrology,) Event, result, conse-<BR>quence of stellar conjunctions, &c.<BR> E. आङ् before दिश् to point or<BR>show, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=091-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदेशिन्
आदेशिन् m. (-शी)<BR>	 1. A commander, a director.<BR>	 2. An astrologer, a for-<BR>tune-teller.<BR> E. आङ् before दिश to point or show, and णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=091-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदेष्टृ
आदेष्टृ m. (-ष्टा)<BR>	 1. An adviser, a director, a commander.<BR>	 2. An employer<BR>of priests.<BR> E. आङ् before दिश to show, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=091-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आद्य|आद्यं|आद्यः
आद्य mfn. (-द्यः-द्या-द्यं)<BR>	 1. First, initial.<BR>	 2. Edible, what is to be or may<BR>be eaten.<BR>	 n. (-द्यं)<BR>	 1. Grain.<BR>	 2. Food.<BR>	 f. (-द्या) A name of DURGĀ. E.<BR>आदि and ण्यत् affix, fem. टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=091-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आद्यकवि|आद्यकविः
आद्यकवि m. (-विः) A name of VALMIKI, author of the Rāmāyaṇa. E.<BR>आद्य first, and कवि a poet, being the first who wrote Sanskrit verse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=091-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आद्यन्त
आद्यन्त mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं) From the beginning to the end.<BR>	 n. (-न्तं) Be-<BR>ginning and end, first and last.<BR> E. आदि first, and अन्त last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=091-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आद्यन्तवत्|आद्यन्तवन्त्
आद्यन्तवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Finite, having beginning and end.<BR> E. आदि<BR>beginning, अन्त end, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=091-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आद्यमाषक|आद्यमाषकः
आद्यमाषक m. (-कः) A Masha, a weight equal to five Gunja or Retti<BR>seeds, about 17(1/2) grains troy.<BR> E. आद्य and माषक a Masha, the pri-<BR>mary Masha; also माष and मास.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=091-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आद्यवीज|आद्यवीजं
आद्यवीज n. (-जं) A primary cause.<BR> E. आद्य and वीज seed, cause.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=091-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आद्यून|आद्यूनः
आद्यून mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>	 1. Shamelessly voracious.<BR>	 2. Without the begin-<BR>ning.<BR> E. आङ्, दिव to play or enjoy in the part. past, or आदि first,<BR>and ऊन minus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=091-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आद्योपान्त|आद्योपान्तं
आद्योपान्त adv. (-न्तं) From first to last.<BR> E. आद्य and उप near, अन्त end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=091-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधमन|आधमनं
आधमन n. (-नं) A pledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=091-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधर्म्मिक|आधर्मिक
आधर्म्मिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Unjust, unrighteous.<BR> E. अ neg. धर्म्म virtue, &c. ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=091-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधर्षण|आधर्षणं
आधर्षण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Conviction, (of crime or of error.)<BR>	 2. Sentence,<BR>refutation.<BR>	 3. Injuring, annoying.<BR> E. आङ् before धृष to be bold,<BR>ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=091-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधर्षित
आधर्षित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Convicted, sentenced.<BR>	 2. Refuted, disproved.<BR>3. Injured, aggrieved.<BR> E. आङ् before धृष to be bold, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=091-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधान|आधानं
आधान n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Taking, having.<BR>	 2. Receiving, recovering.<BR>	 3. A cere-<BR>mony performed with consecrated fire.<BR>	 4. A pledge, a deposit.<BR>	 5. A<BR>surety.<BR>	 6. A ceremony performed pervious to conception: see<BR>गर्भाधान.<BR> E. आङ् before धा to have, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=091-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधानिक|आधानिकं|आधानिकः
आधानिक n. (-कं) A ceremony performed after cohabitation to procure<BR>or favour conception.<BR> E. आधान and ठक् affix: see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=091-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधाय|आधायः
आधाय ind. Having deposited or placed.<BR> E. आङ् before धा to have, ल्यप्<BR>aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=091-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधार|आधारः
आधार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Support, prop, stay.<BR>	 2. Receptacle.<BR>	 3. Comprehension,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=092-a" target="_blank">Page092-a+ 60</a>]<BR>location, the sense of the locative in or on.<BR>	 4. A dike, a<BR>canal.<BR>	 5. A basin round the foot of a tree.<BR> E. आङ् and धृ to hold<BR>or contain, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=091-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधाराधेयभाव|आधाराधेयभावः
आधाराधेयभाव m. (-वः) The influence or action of the support or recipi-<BR>ent upon the thing received or supported.<BR> E. आधार support,<BR>&c. आधेय what is to be held, and भाव quality.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=092-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधि|आधिः
आधि m. (-धिः)<BR>	 1. Mental agony, anxiety.<BR>	 2. Exception.<BR>	 3. Defini-<BR>tion.<BR>	 4. A pledge, a pawn, a mortgage.<BR>	 5. Location, fixing, scite,<BR>&c.<BR>	 6. Engagement.<BR> E. आङ् before ध्यै to reflect, and कि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=092-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधिक्य|आधिक्यं
आधिक्य n. (-क्यं) Excess.<BR> E. अधिक more, ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=092-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधिज
आधिज mfn. (-जः-जा-जं) Produced by pain, &c.<BR> E. आधि pain, and ज<BR>produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=092-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधिज्ञ|आधिज्ञः
आधिज्ञ mfn. (-ज्ञः-ज्ञा-ज्ञं)<BR>	 1. Crooked.<BR>	 2. Pained, distressed.<BR> E. आधि<BR>pain, &c. and ज्ञ who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=092-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधिकारण्य|आधिकारण्यं
आधिकारण्य n. (-ण्यं)<BR>	 1. Possession.<BR>	 2. Location.<BR> E. अधिकरण, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=092-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधिकारिक
आधिकारिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>	 1. Supreme, superior, relating or belong-<BR>ing to any thing or person of importance or sway.<BR>	 2. Official, re-<BR>lating to any office or duty.<BR> E. अधिकार and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=092-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधित्व|आधित्वं
आधित्व n. (-त्वं) Nature or circumstance of a pledge.<BR> E. अधि and त्व aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=092-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधित्वोपाधि
आधित्वोपाधि m. (-धिः) The object or purpose with which a pledge is<BR>given, the conditions or terms of a mortgage.<BR> E. आधित्व and उपाधि<BR>condition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=092-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधिदैविक|आधिदैविकं
आधिदैविक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Relating to, a tutelary or presiding deity.<BR>E. अधिदैव and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=092-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधिपत्य|आधिपत्यं
आधिपत्य n. (-त्यं) Power, supremacy, sovereignty.<BR> E. अधिपति a lord or<BR>master, &c. ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=092-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधिभोग|आधिभोगः
आधिभोग m. (-गः) Usufruct, enjoyment or use of a deposit, use of a<BR>horse, cow, &c. pledged.<BR> E. आधि a pledge, and भोग enjoyment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=092-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधिभौतिक|आधिभौतिकं
आधिभौतिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Elementary, derived or produced from the<BR>primitive elements.<BR> E. अधिभूत a material cause, ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=092-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधिमन्यव|आधिमन्यवः
आधिमन्यव m. (-वः) Feverish heat or burning.<BR> E. आधि and मन्यु distress,<BR>अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=092-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधिराज्य|आधिराज्यं
आधिराज्य n. (-ज्यं) Supreme sway, royalty, royal government.<BR> E. अधिराज<BR>and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=092-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधिवेदनिक|आधिवेदनिकं
आधिवेदनिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Property, &c. given to a first wife upon<BR>marrying a second.<BR> E. अधि before विद् to know, and ल्युट affix,<BR>अधिवेदन, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=092-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधीकरण|आधीकरणं
आधीकरण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Pledging, mortgaging.<BR>	 2. A pledge.<BR> E. आधि and<BR>करण making, &c. with च्वि inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=092-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधीकृत
आधीकृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Pledged, pawned, mortgaged.<BR> E. आधि and कृत<BR>made, with च्वि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=092-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधीकृत्य
आधीकृत्य ind. Having pledged.<BR> E. आधि with कृत्य having done, च्वि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=092-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधुत|आधुतः
आधुत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Shaken, trembling.<BR> E. आङ् before धु or धू to trem-<BR>ble, affix क्त; it is also long, आधूत.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=092-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधुनिक|आधुनिकः
आधुनिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) New, recent, of the present moment. E.<BR>अधुना now, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=092-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधूत|आधूतः
आधूत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Shaken, agitated, trembling.<BR> E. आङ् before धूत<BR>shaken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=092-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधूर्य्य|आधूर्य
आधूर्य्य n. (-र्य्यं) Weakness, infirmity.<BR> E. अ neg. धूर्य्य to be borne, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=092-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधृत
आधृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Contained, supported.<BR> E. आङ् before धृ to have,<BR>क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=092-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधेय|आधेयं
आधेय mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>	 1. Placed, deposited or to be deposited.<BR>	 2. To be<BR>received or supported.<BR>	 3. To be pledged or mortgaged.<BR> E. आङ् be-<BR>fore धा to have or hold, and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=092-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधोरण|आधोरणः
आधोरण m. (-णः) The rider or driver of an elephant.<BR> E. आङ् before धोर to<BR>move well, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=092-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आध्मात|आध्मातः
आध्मात mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Sounded, sounding.<BR>	 2. Inflated.<BR>	 3. Burnt.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-तः)<BR>	 1. Flatulence, borborygmi, swelling of the abdomen with<BR>noise.<BR>	 2. War, battle.<BR> E. आङ् before ध्मा to blow, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=092-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आध्मान|आध्मानं
आध्मान n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Blowing, inflation.<BR>	 2. A bellow.<BR>	 3. Intumescence,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=092-b" target="_blank">Page092-b+ 60</a>]<BR>swelling of the belly, dropsy.<BR> E. आङ् before ध्मा to blow, and ल्युट<BR>aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=092-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आध्या
आध्या f. (-ध्या) Recollection, remembering especially with regret.<BR> E. आङ्<BR>before ध्यै to reflect, अच् affix, and टाप् fem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=092-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आध्यात्मिक|आध्यात्मिकं
आध्यात्मिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Relating to the supreme spirit, spiritual,<BR>holy.<BR> E. अध्यात्म the soul, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=092-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आध्यान|आध्यानं
आध्यान n. (-नं) Remembering, pensive or sorrowful recollection, dwel-<BR>ling or meditating upon, &c.<BR> E. आङ् before ध्यै to consider, and ल्युट<BR>aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=092-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आध्यापक|आध्यापकः
आध्यापक m. (-कः) A teacher, a scriptural preceptor.<BR> E. आङ् prefixed to<BR>the causal of अधि to peruse, affix वुन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=092-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आध्युपभोग
आध्युपभोग m. (-गः) Usufruct of a pledge.<BR> E. आधि and उपभोग enjoyment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=092-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आध्वर्य्यव|आध्वर्यव
आध्वर्य्यव mfn. (-वः-वी-वं) Belonging to the officiating priest.<BR> E. अध्वर्य्यु<BR>and अञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=092-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आन|आनः
आन m. (-नः) Breath inspired.<BR> E. अन् to be, अण् affix; existing by it.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=092-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनक|आनकः
आनक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A large military drum, beaten at one end.<BR>	 2. A<BR>double drum.<BR>	 3. A small drum or tabor.<BR>	 4. A thunder-cloud, or a<BR>cloud to which the noise of the thunder is ascribed.<BR> E. आङ before<BR>अन to sound, and वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=092-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनकदुन्दुभि|आनकदुन्दुभिः
आनकदुन्दुभि m. (-भिः) A name of VASUDEVA the father of KṚṢṆA. E.<BR>अनकदुन्दुभ the parent of VASUDEVA, इञ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=092-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनकदुन्दुभि|आनकदुन्दुभिः
आनकदुन्दुभि mf. (-भिः-भी) A large drum beaten at one end, a large dhol,<BR>a kettle drum.<BR> E. आनक what sounds and दुन्दुभि a drum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=092-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनक्य
आनक्य m. (-क्यः) Name of a Muni or sage: see कौण्डिन्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=092-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनत|आनतः
आनत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Bending, stooping, bowed.<BR>	 2. Pacified, conci-<BR>liated.<BR>	 3. Humbled.<BR>	 4. Submissive, obedient.<BR> E. आङ् before नम्<BR>to bow or bend, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=092-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनति|आनतिः
आनति f. (-तिः) Bending, bowing, stooping.<BR> E. आङ before नम to bow, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=092-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनद्ध|आनद्धं|आनद्धः
आनद्ध mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>	 1. Bound, tied.<BR>	 2. Costive.<BR>	 n. (-द्धं)<BR>	 1. A drum in<BR>general: also अवनद्ध.<BR>	 2. Dressing, Putting on clothes or ornaments.<BR>E. आङ्, before नह to bind, and क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=092-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनन|आननं
आनन n. (-नं) The mouth, (and by syncope) the face.<BR> E. आङ before अन<BR>to live or breathe, ल्युट aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=092-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनन्तर्य्य|आनन्तर्य|आनंतर्यं
आनन्तर्य्य n. (-र्य्यं) Proximity, absence of interval.<BR>	 2. Immediate conse-<BR>quence or succession.<BR> E. अनन्तर and यञ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=092-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनन्त्य|आनंत्यं
आनन्त्य n. (-न्त्यं)<BR>	 1. Infinity.<BR>	 2. Immortality, future happiness.<BR> E. अनन्त<BR>endless, यञ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=092-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनन्द|आनंदः|आनन्दः
आनन्द m. (-न्दः)<BR>	 1. Happiness, joy.<BR>	 2. BALARĀMA according to the Jaina<BR>system of many KṚṢṆAS and many BALARĀMAS.<BR>	 n. (-न्दं) GOD,<BR>Supreme spirit, according to the Vedanta.<BR>	 f. (-न्दी) A plant, vul-<BR>garly Ākanpata.<BR> E. आङ् before नदि to be or make happy, घञ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=092-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनन्दथु|आनंदथु|आनन्दथुः
आनन्दथु mfn. (-थुः-थुः-थु) Happy, joyful.<BR>	 m. (-थुः) Happiness, joy.<BR> E. आङ्<BR>before नदि to be happy, and अथुच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=092-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनन्दद
आनन्दद mfn. (-दः-दा-दं) Exhilarating, delighting: so आनन्दकर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=092-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनन्ददत्त|आनन्ददत्तः
आनन्ददत्त m. (-त्तः) Membrum virile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=092-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनन्दन|आनंदन|आनन्दनं
आनन्दन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Civility, courtesy, the treatment of a friend or guest<BR>at meeting and parting.<BR>	 2. Delighting, making happy.<BR>	 3. What<BR>gives or occasions delight.<BR> E. आङ् before नदि to make happy, and<BR>ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=092-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनन्दपट|आनन्दपटं|आनन्दपटः
आनन्दपट n. (-टं) Bridal clothes.<BR> E. आनन्द making happy, and पट cloth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=092-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनन्दप्रभव|आनन्दप्रभवं|आनन्दप्रभवः
आनन्दप्रभव m. (-वः) The seminal fluid.<BR> E. आनन्द pleasure, and प्रभव what is<BR>manifest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=092-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनन्दमय|आनंदमय|आनन्दमयः
आनन्दमय mfn. (-यः-यी-यं) Blissful, made up or consisting of happiness.<BR>n. (-यं) The Supreme Spirit.<BR> E. आनन्द and मयट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=092-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनन्दमयकोष|आनन्दमयकोषः
आनन्दमयकोष m. (-षः) The innermost case of the body, or causal frame<BR>enshrining the soul.<BR> E. आनन्दमय and कोष sheath.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=092-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनन्दानन्दन
आनन्दानन्दन m. (-नः) A king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=092-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनन्दि|आनंदिः|आनन्दिः
आनन्दि m. (-न्दिः) Happiness, pleasure; also आनन्दी f. (-न्दी)<BR> E. आङ् before<BR>नदि to be happy, and कि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=092-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनन्दित|आनन्दितः
आनन्दित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Happy, rejoiced, delighted.<BR> E. आङ before नदि to be happy affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=092-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनन्दिन्|आनंदिन्
आनन्दिन् mfn. (-न्दी-न्दिनी-न्दि) Happy, joyful.<BR> E. आनन्द and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=093-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनमित
आनमित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Bent, bowed down.<BR> E. आङ् before नम् with क्त<BR>aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=093-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनम्र
आनम्र mfn. (-म्रः-म्रा-म्रं) Bowing, stooping, bent, bowed down.<BR> E. आङ् be-<BR>fore नम् to bow, रक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=093-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनय|आनयः
आनय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. Bringing.<BR>	 2. Investiture with the sacred thread. E.<BR>आङ् before णीञ् to obtain, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=093-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनयन|आनयनं
आनयन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Bringing.<BR>	 2. Investiture with the sacred thread. E.<BR>आङ् before णीञ् to get, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=093-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनर्त्त|आनर्त|आनर्तः|आनर्त्तः
आनर्त्त m. (-र्त्तः)<BR>	 1. A country on the north of the Malabar Coast.<BR>	 2.<BR>A stage, a theatre.<BR>	 3. War.<BR>	 4. Water.<BR>	 5. An inhabitant of<BR>Ānarta.<BR> E. आङ् before नृत् to dance, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=093-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनर्थक्य|आनर्थक्यं
आनर्थक्य n. (-क्यं)<BR>	 1. Unfitness, impropriety.<BR>	 2. Uselessness, unprofit-<BR>ableness.<BR> E. अनर्थ unprofitable, ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=093-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनाय|आनायः
आनाय m. (-यः) A net.<BR> E. आङ् before णीञ् to obtain, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=093-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनाय्य|आनाय्यः
आनाय्य mfn. (-य्यः-य्या-य्यं) To be brought.<BR>	 m. (-य्यः) Consecrated fire,<BR>taken from the household fire, and placed on the south side. E.<BR>आङ् before णीञ् to obtain, ण्यत् affix: deriv. irregular.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=093-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनाह|आनाहः
आनाह m. (-हः)<BR>	 1. Epistasis, suppression of urine, or constipation.<BR>	 2.<BR>Length, especially of cloth.<BR> E. आङ् before नह to bind, affix<BR>घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=093-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनिल|आनिलः
आनिल m. (-लः) Name of HANUMAN and BHIMA.<BR> E. अनिल and अण्<BR>patronymic affix; see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=093-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनिलि|आनिलिः
आनिलि m. (-लिः)<BR>	 1. A name of the monkey HANUMAN.<BR>	 2. BHIMA. E.<BR>अनिल the wind, patronymic affix इञ्; HANUMAN and BHIMA being<BR>the sons of ANILA or the wind.<BR>	 f. (-लिः) A name of SWATI, the<BR>fifteenth Nakshatra or lunar mansion.<BR> E. अनिल and अण् affix, fem.<BR>ङीप्; ANILA being the ruling deity of the asterism.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=093-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनीत
आनीत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Taken.<BR>	 2. Brought.<BR>	 3. Obtained.<BR> E. आङ् before<BR>णीञ् to obtain, and क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=093-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनीय
आनीय ind.<BR>	 1. Having taken.<BR>	 2. Having brought.<BR> E. आङ् before णीञ् to<BR>obtain, and ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=093-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनील|आनीलः
आनील mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Darkish.<BR>	 m. (-लः) A black horse.<BR> E. आङ् dimi-<BR>nutive, and नील black or dark blue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=093-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनुकूल्य|आनुकूल्यं
आनुकूल्य n. (-ल्यं) Favour, kindness.<BR> E. अनुकूल favourable, ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=093-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनुगत्य|आनुगत्यं
आनुगत्य n. (-त्यं) Acquintance, familiarity.<BR> E. अनुगत followed, ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=093-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनुग्रामिक
आनुग्रामिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) About or belonging to the village, rustic,<BR>rural, &c.<BR> E. अनुग्राम and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=093-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनुपदिक
आनुपदिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Following, pursuing, tracking.<BR> E. अनुपद and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=093-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनुपूर्व्व|आनुपूर्व|आनुपूर्वं
आनुपूर्व्व nf. (-र्व्वं-र्व्वीं)<BR>	 1. Order, series, succession.<BR>	 2. (In law) Direct<BR>order of the castes.<BR>	 3. (In logic) A conclusion, regularly or syllogis-<BR>tically deduced.<BR> E. अनु subsequent, पूर्व्व first, अण् affix; also आनुपूर्व<BR>and आनुपूर्व्वक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=093-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनुमानिक|आनुमानिकः
आनुमानिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Inferrable, inferred, subject to inference,<BR>derived from inference, &c.<BR> E. अनुमान inference, and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=093-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनुरक्ति|आनुरक्तिः
आनुरक्ति f. (-क्तिः) Passion, affection.<BR> E. अनुरक्ति the same, the first vowel<BR>made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=093-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनुलोम्य
आनुलोम्य n. (-म्यं) Direct order, regular series or succession.<BR> E. अनुलोम<BR>direct, and यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=093-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनुलोमिक
आनुलोमिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Regular, orderly, in due course or series. E.<BR>अनुलोम and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=093-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनुविधित्सा
आनुविधित्सा f. (-त्सा) Ingratitude.<BR> E. अनु and वि before धा to have, desi-<BR>derative form, affixes अङ् and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=093-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनुषङ्गिक|आनुषंगिक
आनुषङ्गिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>	 1. Proportionate, like, analogous, relative.<BR>2. Necessary, (as result, consequence.)<BR>	 3. Connected, concomitant<BR>with, adherent, inherent.<BR>	 4. (In grammar) Elliptical, including<BR>or agreeing with words not comprised in the sentence.<BR> E. अनुषङ्ग<BR>relation or connexion, ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=093-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनूप|आनूपः
आनूप m. (-पः) Any animal frequenting marshy places, as a buffalo,<BR>&c.<BR> E. अनूप marshy ground, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=093-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनूपमांस
आनूपमांस m. (-सः) Flesh or meat of animals frequenting marshes, &c.<BR>E. आनूप and मांस flesh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=093-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनृण्य|आनृण्यं
आनृण्य n. (-ण्यं) Acquittance of debt or obligation.<BR> E. अनृणी out of<BR>debt, ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=093-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनृशंस्य|आनृशंस्यं
आनृशंस्य n. (-स्यं)<BR>	 1. Mildness.<BR>	 2. Cruelty.<BR> E. अनृशंस mild, and यञ् affix,<BR>or आङ् intensitive, and नृशंस्य cruelty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=093-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनेतव्य
आनेतव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं) To be brought or taken.<BR> E. आङ् before णीञ्<BR>to take, तव्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=093-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनेय
आनेय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) To be taken or brought.<BR> E. आङ् before णी to take ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=093-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनैपुण|आनैपुणं
आनैपुण n. (-णं) Clumsiness, stupidity.<BR> E. अनिपुण not dexterous, अण्<BR>affix; and the initial optionally long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=093-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनैश्वर्य्य|आनैश्वर्य|आनैश्वर्यं
आनैश्वर्य्य n. (-र्य्यं) Absence of power or supremacy.<BR> E. अनैश्वर्य्य the same,<BR>and the initial optionally long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=093-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आन्त|आंत
आन्त mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं) Gone.<BR> E. अम् to go, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=093-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आन्त|आंत
आन्त mfn. (-न्तः-न्ती-न्तं) Final, terminal, relating to the end.<BR> E. अन्त and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=093-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आन्तर्गणिक|आंतर्गणिक
आन्तर्गणिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Included, comprehended, (in a class or<BR>troop.)<BR> E. अन्तर् and गण a class, ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=093-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आन्तरीक्ष|आंतरीक्ष|आन्तरीक्षं
आन्तरीक्ष mfn. (-क्षः-क्षी-क्षं) Heavenly, celestial, produced in the sky.<BR>	 n.<BR>(-क्षं) The firmament.<BR> E. अन्तरीक्ष the same, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=093-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आन्तर्वेश्मिक
आन्तर्वेश्मिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Produced or occurring within a house. E.<BR>अन्तर्वेश्मन् and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=093-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आन्तिका|आंतिका
आन्तिका f. (-का) An elder sister: see अन्तिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=093-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आन्त्रिक|आंत्रिक|आन्त्रिकः
आन्त्रिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Visceral, relating to the bowels.<BR> E. अन्त्र an<BR>entrail, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=093-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आन्दोल|आंदोलः|आन्दोलः
आन्दोल r. 10th cl. (-त) आन्दोलयति To swing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=093-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आन्दोल|आंदोलः|आन्दोलः
आन्दोल m. (-लः) Swinging.<BR> E. आन्दोल to swing and घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=093-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आन्दोलन|आंदोलनं|आन्दोलनं
आन्दोलन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Swinging.<BR>	 2. A swing.<BR>	 3. Trembling, oscillation. E.<BR>आन्दोल to swing, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=093-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आन्दोलित|आन्दोलितं
आन्दोलित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Swung, shaken. E. Participle past of आन्दोल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=093-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आन्धस|आंधसः|आन्धसः
आन्धस m. (-सः) The scum of boiled rice.<BR> E. अन्धस and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=093-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आन्धसिक|आंधसिकः|आन्धसिकः
आन्धसिक m. (-कः) A cook.<BR> E. अन्धस् boiled rice, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=093-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आन्न
आन्न mfn. (-न्नः-न्नी-न्नं)<BR>	 1. Fed, having food.<BR>	 2. Relating to food, derived<BR>from it, &c.<BR> E. अन्न and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=093-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आन्ध्र|आंध्र|आन्ध्रः
आन्ध्र m. (-न्ध्रः) A native of Telengana.<BR> E. अन्ध्र country, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=093-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आन्वयिक|आन्वयिकः
आन्वयिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>	 1. Of a good family, well born.<BR>	 2. Orderly,<BR>according to order or arrangement.<BR> E. अन्वय race, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=093-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आन्वीक्षिकी
आन्वीक्षिकी f. (-की) Logical philosophy, metaphysics.<BR> E. अनु according<BR>to, ईक्ष् to see, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=093-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप|आपः
आप r. 1st, 5th & 10th cls. (ऌ) आपॢ (आपति, आप्नोति or -नुते and आपयति)<BR>1. To pervade or occupy.<BR>	 2. To obtain, to gain. In the first<BR>sense it is usually employed with वि prefixed, and in the second<BR>with अव or प्र; also with अभि and वि prefixed, to spread one place<BR>to another; with परि and वि or सं and वि, to obtain completely;<BR>with सं and वि to meet with, light upon or fall into; with उप, सं<BR>and प्र, to arrive at, to enter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=093-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप|आपः
आप m. (-पः) One of the eight demigods called Vasus.<BR> E. आप् to ob-<BR>tain, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=093-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपकर
आपकर mfn. (-रः-री-रं) Offensive, mischievous, unfriendly.<BR> E. अपकर<BR>offence, अञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=093-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपक्व|आपक्वं
आपक्व mfn. (-क्वः-क्वा-क्वं)<BR>	 1. Half baked, crude, raw.<BR>	 2. Nearly ripe, not<BR>quite ripe.<BR>	 3. Undressed, what is eaten without further prepa-<BR>ration, (as bread, &c.)<BR> E. आङ् diminutive, पक्व dressed, cooked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=093-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपगा
आपगा f. (-गा) A river, a stream.<BR> E. आप् a quantity of water, the ocean,<BR>and गा fem. derivative from गम् to go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=093-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपण|आपणः
आपण m. (-णः)<BR>	 1. A market.<BR>	 2. A shop.<BR> E. आङ् before and पणि to trade,<BR>affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=093-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपणिक|आपणिकः
आपणिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Mercantile, relating to traffic, to a market,<BR>&c.<BR>	 m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A merchant, a dealer, a shop-keeper.<BR>	 2. Tax on<BR>markets or shops.<BR>	 3. Assize, market-rate.<BR> E. आङ् before पणि to<BR>negociate, इकण् Unādi affix; or आपण and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=093-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपतन|आपतनं
आपतन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Coming, approaching.<BR>	 2. Descending, alighting.<BR>3. Happening.<BR> E. आङ् before पत् to go, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=094-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपतिक|आपतिकः
आपतिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Accidental, unforeseen, sent from heaven.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-कः) A hawk, a falcon.<BR> E. आङ् before पत् to go, to fall, इकन्<BR>Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=094-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपतित
आपतित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Happened, befallen.<BR>	 2. Alighted, descended.<BR>E. आङ् before पत् to go, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=094-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपत्काल|आपत्कालः
आपत्काल m. (-लः) Season of distress.<BR> E. आपद् and काल time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=094-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपत्कालिक
आपत्कालिक mfn. (-कः-की-का-कं) Occurring in a time of calamity, be-<BR>longing to it.<BR> E. आपत्काल and ठक् or ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=094-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपत्ति|आपत्तिः
आपत्ति f. (-त्तिः)<BR>	 1. Misfortune, calamity.<BR>	 2. Obtaining, procuring.<BR>	 3.<BR>Fault, Transgression.<BR>	 4. Remonstrance, expostulation.<BR> E. आङ् be-<BR>fore पद् to go, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=094-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपत्प्राप्त|आपत्प्राप्तः
आपत्प्राप्त mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं) Unfortunate, unhappy, afflicted.<BR> E. आपद् mis-<BR>fortune, and प्राप्त obtained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=094-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपद्
आपद् f. (-पद्-पत्) Misfortune, calamity.<BR> E. आङ् before पद् to go, क्लिप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=094-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपद्ग्रस्त
आपद्ग्रस्त mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं) Unfortunate, unhappy, in misfortune. E.<BR>आपद् and ग्रस्त seized.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=094-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपद्धर्म्म|आपद्धर्म|आपद्धर्मः
आपद्धर्म्म n. (-र्म्मं) Practice or profession other than that proper to<BR>caste, but allowable in time of distress.<BR> E. आपद् and धर्म्म<BR>virtue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=094-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपदा
आपदा fn. (-दा-दं) Misfortune, calamity.<BR> E. आङ् before पद् to go, अङ् and<BR>टाप् affs.; also आपद्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=094-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपन|आपनं
आपन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Obtaining.<BR>	 2. Pepper.<BR> E. आप to obtain, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=094-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपनिक|आपनिकः
आपनिक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. An emerald.<BR>	 2. A barbarian.<BR> E. आङ् before पन् to<BR>praise, and इकन् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=094-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपन्न|आपन्नः
आपन्न mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>	 1. Unfortunate, afflicted.<BR>	 2. Gained, obtained,<BR>acquired.<BR> E. आङ् before पद् to go, क्त participial aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=094-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपन्नसत्व
आपन्नसत्व mfn. (-त्वः-त्वा-त्वं) Impregnated, pregnant.<BR>	 f. (-त्वा) A pregnant<BR>woman.<BR> E. आपन्न obtained, सत्व thing, substance, टाप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=094-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपमित्यक|आपमित्यकं
आपमित्यक n. (-कं) Property, &c. obtained by barter.<BR> E. अपमित्य having<BR>changed, ककन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=094-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपराह्णिक
आपराह्णिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Occurring in the afternoon, &c.<BR> E. अपराह्ण and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=094-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपव|आपवः
आपव m. (-वः) A name of VASIṢṬHA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=094-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपस्
आपस् n. (-पः)<BR>	 1. Water.<BR>	 2. Sin.<BR> E. आप to obtain, असुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=094-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपस्कार|आपस्कारं
आपस्कार n. (-रं) The root or extremity of the trunk or body.<BR> E. अपस्कर<BR>filth, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=094-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपस्तम्ब
आपस्तम्ब m. (-म्बः) The name of a sage and legislator.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=094-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपाक|आपाकः
आपाक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A potter's kiln.<BR>	 2. A baking oven.<BR> E. आङ् before<BR>पच to bake, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=094-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपाण्डुर
आपाण्डुर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Slightly pale, palish.<BR> E. आङ् dimin. पाण्डुर pale.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=094-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपात|आपातः
आपात m. (-तः)<BR>	 1. Throwing down, causing to descend.<BR>	 2. Falling, de-<BR>scending.<BR>	 3. The instant, the current moment.<BR> E. आङ् before पत्<BR>to go, to fall, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=094-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपाततस्
आपाततस् ind. Immediately, instantly.<BR> E. तसि added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=094-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपान|आपानं
आपान m. (-नः) A tavern, a liquor-shop, a place for drinking in society.<BR>E. आङ् before पा to drink, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=094-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपालि|आपालिः
आपालि m. (-लिः) A louse.<BR> E. आङ् before पल to go, इन् affix; the penul-<BR>timate irregularly long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=094-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपी
आपी f. (-पी) The twentieth Nakshatra or lunar mansion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=094-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपीड|आपीडः
आपीड m. (-डः)<BR>	 1. Squeezing, compressing.<BR>	 2. Giving pain, hurting.<BR>	 3.<BR>A chaplet tied on the crown of the head.<BR> E. आङ् before पीड to pain,<BR>अच् affix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=094-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपीडन|आपीडनं
आपीडन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Squeezing, compressing, tying or drawing tightly.<BR>	 2.<BR>Embracing, clasping.<BR>	 3. Giving pain, hurting.<BR> E. आङ् before पीड to<BR>pain, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=094-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपीडित
आपीडित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Squeezed, compressing.<BR>	 2. Bound tightly.<BR>3. Embraced.<BR>	 4. Hurt.<BR> E. आङ् before पीडित pressed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=094-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपीत|आपीतं|आपीतः
आपीत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Drank up.<BR>	 2. Very yellow.<BR>	 n. (-तं) A pyritic<BR>mineral.<BR> E. आङ् before पीत drank or yellow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=094-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपीन|आपीनं|आपीनः
आपीन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Stout, fat.<BR>	 m. (-नः) A well.<BR>	 n. (-नं) An udder. E.<BR>आङ् and पीन fat, large.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=094-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपूपिक|आपूपिकं|आपूपिकः
आपूपिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>	 1. A baker.<BR>	 2. A confectioner.<BR>	 3. One who<BR>eats cakes, one for whom they are good, &c.<BR>	 n. (-कं) A multitude<BR>of cakes.<BR> E. अपूप a cake, ठक् or ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=094-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपूप्य|आपूप्यः
आपूप्य m. (-प्यः) Flour, meal.<BR> E. अपूप a cake, यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=094-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपूर्त्ति|आपूर्ति|आपूर्तिः|आपूर्त्तिः
आपूर्त्ति f. (-र्त्तिः)<BR>	 1. Filling.<BR>	 2. Satisfaction, fulness.<BR> E. आङ् before पूर्त्ति fulness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=094-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपूष|आपूषं
आपूष n. (-षं) Tin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=094-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपृच्छा
आपृच्छा f. (-च्छा) Conversation, speaking to or with.<BR> E. आङ् before<BR>प्रच्छ to ask, अङ् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=094-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्त|आप्तः
आप्त mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं)<BR>	 1. Trusted, confidential.<BR>	 2. Gained, obtained.<BR>	 3.<BR>True.<BR>	 4. Apt, fit.<BR>	 5. A friend.<BR>	 6. Appointed.<BR>	 7. Authentic.<BR>8. Accused, prosecuted.<BR>	 f. (-प्ता) A twisted band or lock of hair.<BR>	 n.<BR>(-प्तं)<BR>	 1. Quotient.<BR>	 2. Equation of a degree.<BR> E. आप to obtain, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=094-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्तकारिन्
आप्तकारिन् m. (-री) A trusty agent, a confidential servant.<BR> E. आप्त trust-<BR>ed, and कारिन् who acts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=094-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्तगर्व्व|आप्तगर्व|आप्तगर्व्वः
आप्तगर्व्व mfn. (-र्व्वः-र्व्वा-र्व्वं) Proud, arrogant.<BR> E. आप्त and गर्व्व pride.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=094-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्तगर्भा
आप्तगर्भा f. (-र्भा) A pregnant woman.<BR> E. आप्त and गर्भ embryo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=094-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्तवचन
आप्तवचन n. (-नं) A received text, an authority.<BR> E. आप्त and वचन text.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=094-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्ति|आप्तिः
आप्ति f. (-प्तिः)<BR>	 1. Gain, acquisition.<BR>	 2. Binding, joining.<BR>	 3. Connexion,<BR>relation.<BR>	 4. Fitness, aptitude.<BR> E. आप to obtain, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=094-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्तोक्ति|आप्तोक्तिः
आप्तोक्ति f. (-क्तिः)<BR>	 1. An augment, or affix, (in grammar.)<BR>	 2. A word<BR>of received acceptation, and established by usage only.<BR> E. आप्त<BR>received, उक्ति speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=094-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्प
आप्प m. (-प्पः) The sign Aquarius.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=094-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्य|आप्यं|आप्यः
आप्य mfn. (-प्यः-प्या-प्यं)<BR>	 1. Watery, consisting of water, as froth, &c.<BR>	 2.<BR>Obtainable, to be obtained.<BR>	 n. (-प्यं) A plant, a kind of costus. E.<BR>अप् water, यञ् affix; or आप to get, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=094-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्यान
आप्यान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>	 1. Stout, robust.<BR>	 2. Fat.<BR> E. आङ् before स्फाय to<BR>grow, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=094-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्यायन|आप्यायनं
आप्यायन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Pleasing, satisfying.<BR>	 2. Satiety, satisfaction.<BR>	 3. Ad-<BR>vancing.<BR>	 4. Corpulency, growing or being fat or stout.<BR> E. आङ् be-<BR>fore स्फाय to increase, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=094-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्यायित|आप्यायितः
आप्यायित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Pleased.<BR>	 2. Satisfied.<BR>	 3. Increased, improv-<BR>ed.<BR>	 4. Stout, fat.<BR> E. आङ् before स्फाय to increase, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=094-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्रच्छन|आप्रच्छनं
आप्रच्छन n. (-नं) Civility upon receiving or parting with a visitor, wel-<BR>come, adieu, &c.<BR> E. आङ् before प्रच्छ to ask, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=094-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्रपद|आप्रपदं
आप्रपद n. (-दं) A dress reaching to the feet.<BR> E. आङ् and प्र before पद a foot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=094-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्रपदीन|आप्रपदीनं
आप्रपदीन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) A dress reaching from the shoulders to the<BR>feet.<BR> E. आङ् and प्र prefixed to पद a foot, ख aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=094-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्रपदीनक
आप्रपदीनक n. (-कं) See the preceding.<BR> E. कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=094-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्लव|आप्लवः
आप्लव m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. Bathing.<BR>	 2. Sprinkling with water.<BR> E. आङ् before प्लुङ्<BR>to swim, अप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=094-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्लवन|आप्लवनं
आप्लवन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Sprinkling with water.<BR>	 2. Bathing.<BR> E. आङ् before<BR>प्लुङ् to swim, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=094-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्लवव्रतिन्
आप्लवव्रतिन् m. (-ती) An initiated householder, one who has passed<BR>through the first order, that of the Brahmachari, and is admitted<BR>into the second.<BR> E. आङ् before प्लव bathing, व्रतिन् performer of a<BR>व्रत, or religious obligation; bathing being part of the prescribed<BR>ceremony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=094-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्लाव|आप्लावः
आप्लाव m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. Bathing.<BR>	 2. Sprinkling, wetting.<BR>	 3. A submerging.<BR>4. A flood, an inundation.<BR> E. आङ् before प्लुङ् to swim, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=094-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्लावित
आप्लावित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Inundated, overflowed.<BR> E. आङ् before प्लुङ् to<BR>bathe, causal form, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=094-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्लाव्य
आप्लाव्य ind. Having wetted or sprinkled.<BR> E. आङ् before प्लुङ् to swim,<BR>ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=094-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्लुत|आप्लुतः
आप्लुत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Bathed.<BR>	 2. Wetted, sprinkled.<BR>	 m. (-तः) An ini-<BR>tiated householder: see आप्लवव्रतिन्.<BR>	 n. (-तं) Bathing.<BR> E. आङ् before<BR>प्लुङ् to bathe, affix of the participle past.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=094-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्लुतव्रतिन्
आप्लुतव्रतिन् m. (-ती) See आप्लवव्रतिन्.<BR> E. आप्लुत bathed, &c. as before.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=094-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्लुत्य
आप्लुत्य ind. Having bathed.<BR> E. आङ् before प्लुङ् to bathe, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=095-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्वन्
आप्वन् m. (-प्वा) Air, wind.<BR> E. आप to obtain, वुन् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=095-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आबद्ध|आबद्धः
आबद्ध mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं) Tied, bound.<BR>	 m. (-द्धः)<BR>	 1. A binding.<BR>	 2. A yoke.<BR>3. Ornament.<BR>	 4. Affection.<BR> E. आङ् before बन्ध to bind, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=095-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आबन्ध|आबंधः|आबन्धः
आबन्ध mfn. (-न्धः-न्धा-न्धं) Bound or tied firmly.<BR>	 m. (-न्धः)<BR>	 1. The tie of a<BR>yoke, that which fastens the ox to the yoke, or the latter to the<BR>plough.<BR>	 2. Affection.<BR>	 3. Ornament, decoration.<BR>	 4. A tie or bound.<BR>E. आङ्, बन्ध a binding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=095-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आबाधा
आबाधा f. (-धा) Segment of the base of a triangle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=095-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आबुत्त|आबुत्तः
आबुत्त m. (-त्तः) A sister's husband, (in theatrical language.)<BR> E. आप<BR>to obtain, क्विप्, उत् and तन् to stretch, ड affix, प is changed to ब;<BR>according to another etymology the word is आवुत्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=095-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आबोधन|आबोधनं
आबोधन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Knowledge, understanding.<BR>	 2. Instructing, inform-<BR>ing.<BR> E. आङ् before बुद्ध to know, causal, form, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=095-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभरण|आभरणं
आभरण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Ornament decoration, as jewels, &c.<BR>	 2. Nourishing. E.<BR>आङ् before भृञ् to fill or nourish, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=095-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभा
आभा f. (-भा)<BR>	 1. Light.<BR>	 2. Splendour.<BR>	 3. Beauty.<BR> E. आङ् before भा to<BR>shine, अङ् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=095-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभाति|आभातिः
आभाति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Shade.<BR>	 2. Light.<BR> E. आङ् before भा to shine, affix क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=095-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभाष|आभाषः
आभाष m. (-षः) Introduction, preface.<BR> E. आङ् before भाष to speak, aff.<BR>अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=095-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभाषण|आभाषणं
आभाषण n. (-णं) Addressing, speaking to.<BR> E. आङ् before भाष to speak, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=095-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभास|आभासः
आभास m. (-सः)<BR>	 1. Light.<BR>	 2. Reflexion.<BR>	 3. Intention, purpose.<BR>	 4. (In<BR>logic) Fallacy, semblance of a reason, an argument that is erro-<BR>neous though plausible: it is classed as of various kinds.<BR> E. आङ्<BR>before भास shining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=095-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभास्वर|आभास्वरः
आभास्वर m. (-रः) A demigod, of a class consisting of sixty-four.<BR> E. आङ्<BR>before भास to shine, वरच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=095-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभिजन|आभिजनः
आभिजन n. (-नं) Loftiness of birth.<BR> E. अभिजन family, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=095-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभिजात्य|आभिजात्यं
आभिजात्य n. (-त्यं)<BR>	 1. Birth, family, rank.<BR>	 2. Learning.<BR> E. अभिजाति family,<BR>&c. यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=095-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभिधा
आभिधा f. (-धा) Sound.<BR> E. अभिधा a compound root, to name, आङ् and<BR>टाप् affixes, and आङ् prefix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=095-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभिधानक
आभिधानक n. (-कं) See the preceding. E. As before, क्त and कन् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=095-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभिधानीयक
आभिधानीयक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Relating or belonging to a name or word.<BR>n. (-कं) The property of a name, &c.<BR> E. अभिधानीय and वुञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=095-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभिमुख्य|आभिमुख्यं
आभिमुख्य n. (-ख्यं) Presence, being in front of or face to face.<BR> E. अभि-<BR>मुख and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=095-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभिहारिक
आभिहारिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Taken by force or fraud.<BR> E. अभिहार seizure, ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=095-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभीक्ष्ण|आभीक्ष्णं
आभीक्ष्ण adj.<BR>	 mfn. (-क्ष्णः-क्ष्णा-क्ष्णं) or adv.<BR>	 n. (-क्ष्णं)<BR>	 1. Much, exceeding.<BR>2. Eternal, eternally.<BR> E. अभीक्ष्ण frequent, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=095-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभीर|आभीरः
आभीर m. (-रः) A cowhered, sprung from a Brahman and female of the<BR>medical tribe or the Ambaṣṭha.<BR>	 f. (-री) A cowherd's wife, or a<BR>woman of that tribe.<BR> E. आङ्, अभि and ईर to send, affix अच् and<BR>fem. ङीष्, or without the first prefix अभीर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=095-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभीरपल्लि|आभीरपल्लिः
आभीरपल्लि f. (-ल्लिः) A station of herdsmen, a village inhabited by them<BR>only, an abode of cowherds, &c.<BR> E. आभीर a cowherd, and पल्लि a<BR>house, a village, &c. also with the final long -पल्ली.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=095-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभीरपल्ली
आभीरपल्ली f. (-ल्ली) See the preceding. E. As above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=095-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभील|आभीलं|आभीलः
आभील mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>	 1. Formidable, fearful.<BR>	 2. Suffering pain.<BR>	 n. (-लं)<BR>Bodily pain.<BR> E. अभि before इल to sleep, क affix; अ is made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=095-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभेरी
आभेरी f. (-री) One of the Rāgiṇīs or modes of music, femininely per-<BR>sonified.<BR> E. आङ् before, भेरी a drum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=095-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभोग|आभोगः
आभोग m. (-गः)<BR>	 1. Completion, fulness.<BR>	 2. Enjoyment.<BR>	 3. Effort, pains.<BR>4. The expanded hood of the Cobra capella, used by VARUṆA<BR>as his umbrella.<BR> E. आङ् before भुज to eat, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=095-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभ्यासिक
आभ्यासिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Resulting from practice, practicing, repeat-<BR>ing.<BR> E. अभ्यास and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=095-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभ्युदयिक|आभ्युदयिकं
आभ्युदयिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>	 1. Relating to prosperity, &c.<BR>	 2. High,<BR>exalted.<BR>	 3. Important.<BR>	 n. (-कं) A Sraddha or offering to ancestors<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=095-b" target="_blank">Page095-b+ 60</a>]<BR>on occasions of rejoicing.<BR> E. अभ्युदय elevation, prosperity, ठक्<BR>affix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=095-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आम|आमं|आमः
आम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>	 1. Raw, undressed, unripe.<BR>	 2. Unbaked, unan-<BR>nealed.<BR>	 m. (-मः)<BR>	 1. Sickness, disease.<BR>	 3. Constipation, passing<BR>hard and unhealthy excretions.<BR>	 4. Grain freed from the chaff.<BR>E. अम् to be sick, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=095-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमकुम्भ|आमकुम्भः
आमकुम्भ m. (-म्भः) A water-jar of unbaked clay.<BR> E. आम and कुम्भ a jar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=095-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमगन्धि
आमगन्धि n. (-न्धि) A bad and cadaverous smell, like that of raw meat<BR>or burning corpse.<BR> E. आम raw, &c. and गन्धि smell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=095-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमण्ड|आमंडः|आमण्डः
आमण्ड m. (-ण्डः) The castor oil plant.<BR> E. आङ् dim. मडि to adorn, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=095-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमनस्य|आमनस्यं
आमनस्य n. (-स्यं) Pain.<BR> E. अ priv. मनस् the mind, यत् affix and the first<BR>vowel made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=095-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमन्त्रण|आमंत्रणं|आमन्त्रणं
आमन्त्रण nf. (-णं-णा)<BR>	 1. Calling or calling to.<BR>	 2. Courtesy, welcome, adieu,<BR>&c.<BR>	 3. Inviting, invitation.<BR>	 4. Interrogation.<BR>	 5. The vocative case.<BR>E. आङ् before मत्रि to consult, affix युच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=095-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमन्त्रयितृ|आमंत्रयितृ
आमन्त्रयितृ mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ) Asking, inviting, calling.<BR>	 m. (-ता) An inviter,<BR>an entertainer, especially of Brahmans.<BR> E. आङ् before मत्रि to<BR>counsel, causal form, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=095-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमन्त्रित|आमंत्रित
आमन्त्रित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Invited, summoned, called.<BR> E. आङ् before मत्रि to<BR>consult, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=095-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमपीनस
आमपीनस n. (-सं) Running at the nose, defluxion.<BR> E. आम and पीनस<BR>pituitary excretion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=095-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आममांस
आममांस m. (-सः) Raw flesh.<BR> E. आम and मांस flesh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=095-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आममांसाशिन्
आममांसाशिन् m. (-शी) A cannibal.<BR> E. आममांस and अशिन् who eats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=095-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमय|आमयं|आमयः
आमय m. (-यः) Sickness, disease.<BR>	 n. (-यं) A grass, (Costus.)<BR> E. अम् to be<BR>sick, घञ् affix, आम, and य, from या to obtain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=095-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमयाविन्
आमयाविन् mfn. (-वी-विनी-वि)<BR>	 1. Sick, diseased.<BR>	 2. Affected with indiges-<BR>tion, dyspeptic.<BR> E. आमय, अव to go, and णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=095-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमयावित्व
आमयावित्व n. (-त्वं) Dyspepsia, indigestion.<BR> E. आमयाविन् and त्व aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=095-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमरक्त
आमरक्त m. (-क्तः) Dysentery.<BR> E. आम and रक्त blood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=095-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमरणान्तिक|आमरणांतिक
आमरणान्तिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Lasting for life, continuing till death. E.<BR>आङ् before मरण dying, and अन्त end, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=095-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमरस|आमरसः
आमरस m. (-सः) Imperfect chyme.<BR> E. आम and रस juice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=095-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमर्श|आमर्शः
आमर्श m. (-र्शः) Advice, counsel.<BR> E. आङ् before मृश् to advice, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=095-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमर्ष|आमर्षः
आमर्ष m. (-र्षः)<BR>	 1. Wrath or rage.<BR>	 2. Impatience.<BR> E. अ before मृष to bear,<BR>affix घञ्, the prefix made long: also अमर्ष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=095-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमर्षण|आमर्षणं
आमर्षण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Rubbing, wiping.<BR>	 2. Anger.<BR> E. आङ् before मृष to rub,<BR>&c. ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=095-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमलक|आमलकं|आमलकः
आमलक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Emblic myrobalan, (Phyllanthus emblica.)<BR>	 m.<BR>(-कः) Another plant, (Justicia adhenatoda, &c.)<BR>	 n. (-कं) The fruit<BR>of the myrobalan.<BR> E. आङ् and मल् to hold, वुन् aff. fem. ङीष् having<BR>all medicinal virtues.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=095-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमवात|आमवातः
आमवात m. (-तः) Constipation or torpor of the bowels, with flatulence<BR>and intumescence.<BR> E. आम and वात wind, the wind being supposed<BR>to be chiefly affected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=095-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमशूल|आमशूलः
आमशूल m. (-लः) The cholic, pain arising from indigestion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=095-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमातिसार|आमातिसारः
आमातिसार m. (-रः) Dysentery, the excretion being mixed with hard<BR>and fœtid matter.<BR> E. आम and अतिसार dysentery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=095-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमात्य|आमात्यः
आमात्य m. (-त्यः)<BR>	 1. A minister, a counseller, an adviser.<BR>	 2. A general.<BR>E. See अमात्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=095-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमाद्
आमाद् mfn. (-मात्) Eating raw food.<BR> E. आम, अद to eat, ञिट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=095-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमानस्य|आमानस्यं
आमानस्य n. (-स्यं) Pain. E. See आमनस्य, the antepen. being made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=095-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमान्न|आमान्नं
आमान्न n. (-न्नं) Undressed rice.<BR> E. आम and अन्न boiled rice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=095-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमालक|आमालकः
आमालक mn. (-कः-कं) Land near a mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=095-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमावास्य
आमावास्य mfn. (-स्यः-स्या-स्यं) Occurring on the day of conjunction, &c.<BR>E. अमावास्य and अञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=095-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमाशय|आमाशयः
आमाशय m. (-यः) The stomach.<BR> E. आम hardness of the fæces, &c. and<BR>आशय a station.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=095-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमिक्षा
आमिक्षा f. (-क्षा) Curd of two milk whey.<BR> E. आङ् before मिष to sprinkle,<BR>सक् affix; also आमीक्षा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=095-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमिक्ष्य|आमिक्ष्यं
आमिक्ष्य mfn. (-क्ष्यः-क्ष्या-क्ष्यं) Made of curds, &c.<BR> E. आमिक्षा and यत् affix;<BR>also with छ, आमिक्षीय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=096-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमिष|आमिषं
आमिष mn. (-षः-षं)<BR>	 1. Flesh.<BR>	 2. Enjoyment.<BR>	 3. An object of enjoyment,<BR>a pleasing or beautiful object, &c.<BR>	 4. A bribe.<BR>	 5. Coveting, longing<BR>for.<BR>	 6. Form.<BR>	 7. Lust, desire.<BR>	 8. Food.<BR> E. अम् to be sick, to go, ष्टिसच्<BR>Unādi aff. and the antepen. lengthened.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=096-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमिषप्रिय|आमिषप्रियः
आमिषप्रिय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Carnivorous, fond of flesh meat.<BR>	 m. (-यः) A<BR>heron.<BR> E. आमिष flesh, and प्रिय fond of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=096-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमिषभुज्
आमिषभुज् mfn. (-भुक्) Carnivorous.<BR> E. आमिष and भुज what eats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=096-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमिषाशिन्
आमिषाशिन् mfn. (-शी-शिनी-शि) Carnivorous, eating flesh and fish.<BR> E. आमिष<BR>flesh, अश to eat, and णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=096-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमुक्त|आमुक्तः
आमुक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>	 1. Loosed, let go.<BR>	 2. Discharged, cast, shot.<BR>	 3.<BR>Put on as clothes or armour.<BR>	 4. Dressed, accoutred.<BR> E. आङ् before<BR>मुच to release, unbind, &c. क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=096-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमुक्ति|आमुक्तिः
आमुक्ति f. (-क्तिः)<BR>	 1. Liberation, being let loose.<BR>	 2. Final liberation. ind.<BR>(-क्ति) To be end of existence.<BR> E. आङ् and मुक्ति liberation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=096-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमुख|आमुखं
आमुख n. (-खं)<BR>	 1. Prelude, prologue.<BR>	 2. Commencement. ind. To the<BR>face.<BR> E. आङ् before मुख face or beginning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=096-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमुप|आमुपः
आमुप m. (-पः) A thorny kind of bambu, (Bambusa spinosa, Rox.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=096-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमुष्यायण|आमुष्यायणः
आमुष्यायण mfn. (-णः-णी-णं) Of an illustrious family, well born, well<BR>descended.<BR> E. अमुष्य the genitive of अदस् this, and फक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=096-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमूल|आमूलं
आमूल adv.<BR>	 n. (-स्तं) To the root, by the root, entirely, radically.<BR> E. आङ्<BR>particle, and मूल root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=096-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमृष्ट
आमृष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं) Wiped, rubbed.<BR> E. आङ् before मृज to wipe, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=096-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमोचन|आमोचनं
आमोचन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Loosing, liberating.<BR>	 2. Emitting, shedding, letting<BR>forth or out.<BR> E. आङ् before मुच to liberate, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=096-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमोद|आमोदः
आमोद m. (-दः)<BR>	 1. A fragrancy, a diffusive perfume.<BR>	 2. Strong smell.<BR>	 3.<BR>Pleasure.<BR> E. आङ् before मुद् to be pleased, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=096-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमोदन|आमोदनं
आमोदन n. (-नं) Delighting, rejoicing.<BR> E. आङ् before मुद् to please,<BR>causal form, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=096-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमोदित|आमोदितः
आमोदित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Pleased, delighted.<BR>	 2. Fragrant.<BR> E. आङ् be-<BR>fore मुद् with क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=096-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमोदिन्
आमोदिन् mfn. (-दी-दिनी-दि)<BR>	 1. Fragrant.<BR>	 2. Happy, delighted.<BR>	 m. (-दी)<BR>A perfume for the mouth, made up in the form of a pill or bolus<BR>of camphor, &c.<BR> E. आमोद and णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=096-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमोषिन्
आमोषिन् mfn. (-षी-षिणी-षि) A thief, who or what steals.<BR> E. आङ् before<BR>मुष to steal, घिनुण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=096-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आम्नाय|आम्नायः
आम्नाय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. A Veda, or the Vedas in the aggregate.<BR>	 2. Received<BR>doctrine, traditional and right.<BR>	 3. Traditional usage, family or<BR>national customs.<BR>	 4. Advice, instruction in past and present<BR>usage.<BR>	 5. A Tantra.<BR>	 6. An element of being, a property of sub-<BR>stance.<BR> E. आङ् before म्रा to learn, to remember, घञ् and युक् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=096-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आम्नायसारिन्
आम्नायसारिन् mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि) Pious, observing the Vedas and national<BR>customs.<BR> E. आम्नाय and सारिन् who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=096-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आम्बिकेय|आंबिकेयः|आम्बिकेयः
आम्बिकेय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. A name of DHRITARĀSHTRA.<BR>	 2. Also of KĀR-<BR>TIKEYA.<BR> E. अम्बिका the mother of DHRITARASHTRA or a name of<BR>DURGĀ and ढक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=096-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आम्भसिक|आंभसिक|आम्भसिकः
आम्भसिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Aquatic.<BR>	 m. (-कः) A fish.<BR> E. अम्भस् water, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=096-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आम्र|आम्रः
आम्र m. (-म्रः) The mango tree, (Mangifera Indica.)<BR> E. अम् to be sick,<BR>रक् Unādi affix, and अ made आ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=096-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आम्रपेशी
आम्रपेशी f. (-शी) A piece of dried mango.<BR> E. आम्र and पेशी a piece of<BR>flesh, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=096-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आम्रमय
आम्रमय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Made of mangoes, (sauce, &c.)<BR> E. आम्र and मयट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=096-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आम्रात|आम्रातः
आम्रात m. (-तः) The hog-plum, (Spondias mangifera).<BR> E. आम्र the<BR>mango, and अत् to go, the affix अच्; the fruit resembling the<BR>mango: also आम्रातक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=096-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आम्रातक|आम्रातकः
आम्रातक m. (-कः) See the preceding. E. As before, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=096-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आम्रावर्त्त|आम्रावर्त|आम्रावर्त्तः
आम्रावर्त्त m. (-र्त्तः) Inspissated mango juice.<BR> E. आम्र and आवर्त्त stirring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=096-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आम्रेडन|आम्रेडनं
आम्रेडन n. (-नं) Tautology, reiteration of words or sounds.<BR> E. आङ् be-<BR>fore म्रेडृ to be mad, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=096-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आम्रेडित|आम्रेडितं
आम्रेडित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Reiterated, repeated.<BR>	 n. (-तं) Repetition of a<BR>sound or word.<BR> E. आङ् before म्रिडृ to be mad, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=096-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आम्ल|आम्लः
आम्ल mfn. (-म्लः-म्ला-म्लं) The tamarind tree.<BR>	 n. (-म्लं) Sourness, acidity. E.<BR>अम्ल sour, with आङ् prefixed, or अम्ल sour and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=096-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आम्लवेतस|आम्लवेतसः
आम्लवेतस m. (-सः) A plant, (Rumex vesicatorius.)<BR> E. आम्ल sourness, and<BR>वेतस a cane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=096-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आम्लिका
आम्लिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. The tamarind tree.<BR>	 2. Sourness in the mouth, acidity<BR>of the stomach: see अम्लिका.<BR> E. आम्ल sour, and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=096-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आम्लीका
आम्लीका f. (-का) The tamarind tree.<BR> E. अम्ल and ठक् affix, the pen made<BR>long: otherwise अम्लिका as before.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=096-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आय|आयः
आय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. Income, revenue.<BR>	 2. Gain, profit.<BR>	 3. The guard of the<BR>women's apartments.<BR> E. आङ् before या to obtain, ड aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=096-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयःशूलिक|आयःशूलिकः
आयःशूलिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Active, diligent, indefatigable.<BR> E. अयस् iron<BR>शूल a sharp weapon, affix ठञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=096-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयत्
आयत् mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्) Coming, approaching.<BR> E. आङ् before इण् to<BR>go, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=096-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयत|आयतः
आयत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Long.<BR>	 2. Diffuse, prolix.<BR>	 m. (-तः) An oblong<BR>figure, (in geometry.)<BR> E. आङ् before यम् to cease, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=096-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयतच्छदा
आयतच्छदा f. (-दा) The plantain tree, (Musa sapientum.)<BR> E. आयत long,<BR>and छद a leaf, long-leaved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=096-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयतस्तू
आयतस्तू m. (-स्तूः) A panegyrist.<BR> E. आयत diffuse, ष्टू to praise, and क्विप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=096-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयतार्द्ध
आयतार्द्ध m. (-र्द्धः) (In geometry,) Half an oblong.<BR> E. आयत and अर्द्ध half.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=096-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयतन|आयतनं
आयतन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Abode, house.<BR>	 2. An altar, also a shed for sacrifices.<BR>3. A ground plot, the site of a house, &c.<BR>	 4. The cause of disease.<BR>E. आयत nominal root, to lengthen, affix ल्युट्; extending from the<BR>house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=096-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयताक्षी
आयताक्षी f. (-क्षी) A woman with large eyes or long eyelids.<BR> E. आयत and<BR>अक्षि the eye, fem. affix ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=096-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयतायति|आयतायतिः
आयतायति f. (-तिः) Long continuance, remote futurity.<BR> E. आयत and<BR>आयति future time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=096-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयति|आयतिः
आयति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Future time.<BR>	 2. Majesty, dignity.<BR>	 3. Restraint of<BR>mind.<BR>	 4. Length.<BR>	 5. Meeting, junction.<BR>	 6. Obtaining.<BR> E. आङ् be-<BR>fore यम् to cease, affix क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=096-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयतिमत्
आयतिमत् mfn. (-मान्-मती-मत्)<BR>	 1. Long, extended.<BR>	 2. Stately, dignified.<BR>3. Self-restrained.<BR> E. आयति and मतुप aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=096-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयतेक्षण
आयतेक्षण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Long-eyed, having large eyes.<BR> E. आयत and<BR>ईक्षण sight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=096-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयत्त|आयत्तः
आयत्त mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं) Docile, tractable, dependent.<BR> E. आङ् before यम्<BR>to restrain, and क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=096-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयत्तता
आयत्तता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Docility, tractableness, humility.<BR> E. आयत्त तल् affix<BR>of the abstract: also with त्व, आयत्तत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=096-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयत्ति|आयत्तिः
आयत्ति f. (-त्तिः)<BR>	 1. A day.<BR>	 2. Affection.<BR>	 3. Subjection, subjecting.<BR>	 4. A<BR>boundary, a limit.<BR>	 5. Power, strength.<BR>	 6. Continuance in the right<BR>way, steadiness of conduct.<BR>	 7. Sleeping.<BR>	 8. Length.<BR>	 9. Majesty,<BR>dignity.<BR>	 10. Future time.<BR> E. आङ् before यति to endeavour, and<BR>क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=096-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयथातथ्य|आयथातथ्यं
आयथातथ्य n. (-थ्यं) Unfitness, unsuitableness, incompatibility.<BR> E. अयथा-<BR>तथ and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=096-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयम्य
आयम्य ind. Having restrained or suppressed.<BR> E. आङ् before यम् to res-<BR>train, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=096-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयव्यय
आयव्यय m. (-यः) Receipt and disbursement, income and expenditure. E.<BR>आय and व्यय expense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=096-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयल्लक|आयल्लकं|आयल्लकः
आयल्लक n. (-कं) Missing, regretting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=096-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयस|आयसं
आयस mfn. (-सः-सी-सं)<BR>	 1. Of iron, iron.<BR>	 2. Armed with an iron weapon.<BR>	 3.<BR>Zealous.<BR>	 n. (-सं)<BR>	 1. Iron.<BR>	 2. A weapon.<BR>	 f. (-सी) Armour for the body,<BR>a breastplate, a coat of mail.<BR> E. अयस iron, अण् and ङीप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=096-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयस्त|आयस्तः
आयस्त mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं)<BR>	 1. Sharpened, whetted.<BR>	 2. Thrown, cast, sent.<BR>3. Pained, distressed.<BR>	 4. Vexed, angry.<BR>	 5. Hurt, killed.<BR>	 6. Managed<BR>or effected with difficulty.<BR>	 7. Labouring, toiling, making effort or<BR>exertion.<BR> E. आङ्, यस to endeavour, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=096-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयानभूत
आयानभूत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Obtained by sacrifice.<BR> E. आङ् before याग sacri-<BR>fice, भूत become.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=097-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयाचित
आयाचित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Urgently requested or desired.<BR> E. आङ् before<BR>याच् to ask, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=097-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयात|आयातं
आयात mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Come.<BR> E. आङ् before यात gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=097-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयान|आयानं
आयान n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. The natural temperament or disposition.<BR>	 2. Coming,<BR>arrival.<BR> E. आङ् before या to obtain, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=097-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयाम|आयामः
आयाम m. (-मः)<BR>	 1. Length, either in space or time.<BR>	 2. Breadth, (in<BR>mensuration.)<BR>	 3. Restraint, restraining.<BR> E. आङ् before यम to cease,<BR>घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=097-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयामिन्
आयामिन् mfn. (-मी-मिनी-मि)<BR>	 1. Long in space or time.<BR>	 2. One who<BR>restrains.<BR> E. आयाम and इनि affix or आङ् before यम् to cease and<BR>घिनुण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=097-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयास|आयासः
आयास m. (-सः)<BR>	 1. Fatigue, weariness.<BR>	 2. Effort, exertion.<BR>	 3. Trouble,<BR>labour.<BR> E. आङ् before यस् to endeavour, to make exertion, and घञ्<BR>affix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=097-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयासिन्
आयासिन् mfn. (-सी-सिनी-सि)<BR>	 1. Making exertion, active, laborious.<BR>	 2.<BR>Exhausted by labour, wearied.<BR> E. आङ् before यस् to endeavour,<BR>घिनुण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=097-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयुःशेष|आयुःशेषः
आयुःशेष m. (-षः) End of life, death.<BR> E. आयुस् and शेष end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=097-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयु|आयुः
आयु mn. (-युः-यु) Age, duration of life.<BR> E. अय् to go, Unādi affix डु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=097-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयुक्त|आयुक्तः
आयुक्त m. (-क्तः) A minister, an agent or deputy.<BR> E. आङ् before युज्<BR>to join, and क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=097-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयुध|आयुधं|आयुधः
आयुध m. (-धः) A weapon in general.<BR> E. आङ् before युध् to fight, क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=097-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयुधधर्म्मिणी|आयुधधर्मिणी
आयुधधर्म्मिणी f. (-णी) A plant, (Œschynomene sesban): see जयन्ती. E.<BR>आयुध a weapon and धर्म्मिणी possessing virtue: having the virtues<BR>of a weapon against disease, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=097-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयुधागार|आयुधागारं
आयुधागार n. (-रं) An arsenal, an armoury.<BR> E. आयुध and आगार a house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=097-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयुधिक|आयुधिकः
आयुधिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Relating to arms.<BR>	 m. (-कः) A soldier, a war-<BR>rior.<BR> E. आयुध a weapon, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=097-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयुधीय|आयुधीयः
आयुधीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Relating to or connected with weapons.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-यः) A warrior.<BR> E. आयुध and छण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=097-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयुर्द्रव्य|आयुर्द्रव्यं
आयुर्द्रव्य n. (-व्यं) A medicament.<BR> E. आयुस् life, and द्रव्य thing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=097-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयुर्वेद|आयुर्वेदः|आयुर्व्वेदः
आयुर्वेद m. (-दः)<BR>	 1. The science of medicine.<BR>	 2. The collective writings<BR>of authority on medicine, or medical Śāstra.<BR> E. आयुस् life, and वेद<BR>a Veda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=097-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयुर्वेदमय
आयुर्वेदमय mfn. (-यः-यी-यं) Acquainted with medical science.<BR> E. आयुर्वेद and मयट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=097-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयुर्वेदिन्
आयुर्वेदिन् mfn. (-दी-दिनी-दि) Belonging to medicine, of the medical pro-<BR>fession, medical, medicinal, &c.<BR>	 m. (-दी) A practicer of physic, a<BR>physician or surgeon.<BR> E. आयुवेंद and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=097-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयुष्मत्|आयुष्मन्त्
आयुष्मत् mfn. (-ष्मान्-ष्मती-ष्मत्)<BR>	 1. Alive, living.<BR>	 2. Long lived.<BR>	 m. (-ष्मान्)<BR>One of the twenty-seven Yogas or divisions of the ecliptic.<BR> E. आयुस्<BR>age, and मतुप् possessive aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=097-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयुष्टोम|आयुष्टोमः
आयुष्टोम m. (-मः) A sacrifice to obtain longevity.<BR> E. आयुस् and ष्टोम a<BR>sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=097-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयुष्य|आयुष्यं
आयुष्य mfn. (-ष्यः-ष्या-ष्यं) Vital, preservative of life, for the sake of life,<BR>relating or belonging to it.<BR> E. आयुस् and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=097-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयुस्
आयुस् n. (-युः) Age, duration of life.<BR> E. इ to go, उसि Unādi affix, the<BR>pen. lengthened.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=097-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयुस्कर|आयुस्करः
आयुस्कर mfn. (-रः-रा-री-रं) Promoting longevity, supporting life. E.<BR>आयुस् and कर what makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=097-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आये
आये ind. An interjection of calling, expressive of affection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=097-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयोग|आयोगः
आयोग m. (-गः)<BR>	 1. Presenting or offering flowers, perfumes, &c.<BR>2. Action, the performance of an act.<BR>	 3. A shore or bank.<BR> E. आङ्<BR>before युज् to join, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=097-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयोगव|आयोगवः
आयोगव m. (-वः) A man of a mixed tribe sprung from a Śūdra man and<BR>Vaiśya woman; his business is carpentry, &c.<BR>	 f. (-वी) A woman of<BR>the tribe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=097-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयोजन|आयोजनं
आयोजन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Effort, exertion.<BR>	 2. Taking, seizing.<BR>	 3. Collecting. E.<BR>आङ् before युज् to join, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=097-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयोजित
आयोजित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Collected together.<BR> E. आङ् before युज् to join,<BR>क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=097-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयोधन|आयोधनं
आयोधन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. War, battle, slaughter.<BR> E. आङ् before युध to make<BR>war, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=097-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर|आरं|आरः
आर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. The planet MARS.<BR>	 2. The planet SATURN.<BR>	 n. (-रं)<BR>	 1. An<BR>angle, a corner.<BR>	 2. End, extremity.<BR>	 3. Brass.<BR>	 4. Oxide of iron.<BR>	 f.<BR>(-रा)<BR>	 1. A shoe-maker's awl or knife.<BR>	 2. A probe.<BR> E. ऋ to go, affix<BR>घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=097-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरकूट|आरकूटः
आरकूट mn. (-टः-टं) Brass.<BR> E. आर what goes, and कूट a heap; composed<BR>of various materials.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=097-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरक्ष|आरक्षं|आरक्षः
आरक्ष mfn. (-क्षः-क्षा-क्षं)<BR>	 1. Preserved, defended.<BR>	 2. Proper or worthy to<BR>be preserved, &c.<BR>	 m. (-क्षः)<BR>	 1. Protection, guard, preservation.<BR>	 2.<BR>The junction of the frontal sinuses of an elephant.<BR> E. आङ् before<BR>रक्ष to preserve, &c. घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=097-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरक्षक|आरक्षकः
आरक्षक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Who or what guards or protects.<BR>	 m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A<BR>watchman, a patrol.<BR>	 2. A village or police magistrate.<BR> E. आङ् be-<BR>fore रक्ष् to preserve, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=097-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरग्बध
आरग्बध m. (-धः) A plant, (Cassia fistula.)<BR> E. आङ्, रुज् sickness, बध what destroys.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=097-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरट्ट|आरट्टः
आरट्ट m. (-ट्टः) The name of a country, north-west of India.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=097-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरट्टज|आरट्टजः
आरट्टज m. (-जः) A horse from the Āraṭṭa country.<BR> E. आरट्ट and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=097-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरणि|आरणिः
आरणि m. (-णिः) An eddy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=097-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरण्य|आरण्यः
आरण्य mfn. (-ण्यः-ण्यी-ण्यं) Forest, wild, forest-born, &c.<BR> E. अरण्य a wood,<BR>अण् affix of derivation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=097-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरण्यक|आरण्यकः
आरण्यक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Forest, wild, forest-born or produced.<BR>	 m. (-कः)<BR>A forester, an inhabitant of the woods.<BR> E. आरण्य and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=097-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरण्यपशु|आरण्यपशुः
आरण्यपशु m. (-शुः) A wild or forest animal, as a buffalo, a monkey, &c.<BR>E. आरण्य forest, and पशु an animal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=097-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरण्यराशि|आरण्यराशिः
आरण्यराशि m. (-शिः) The sign LEO.<BR> E. आरण्य a forest beast, and राशि a sign.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=097-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरति|आरतिः
आरति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Stopping, ceasing.<BR>	 2. Waving lights before an image.<BR>E. आङ् before रम् to play, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=097-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरनाल|आरनालं
आरनाल n. (-लं) Sour gruel made from the fermentation of boild rice. E.<BR>आर what goes, from ऋ to go, and नाल smell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=097-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरनालक|आरनालकं
आरनालक n. (-कं) See the preceding. E. As before, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=097-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरब्ध|आरब्धं
आरब्ध mfn. (-म्भः-म्भा-म्भं) Begun, commenced.<BR> E. आङ् before रभि to com-<BR>mence, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=097-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरभट|आरभटः
आरभट mfn. (-टः-टी) Boldness, confidence.<BR>	 f. (-टी) A branch of the dra-<BR>matic art, the machinery of the drama, the representation of magi-<BR>cal incantations, &c.<BR> E. आर quickly, भट to nourish, अच् and ङीप्<BR>affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=097-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरभमाण
आरभमाण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Beginning, beginning resolutely with a de-<BR>termination to finish.<BR> E. आङ् before रभि to commence, शानच aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=097-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरम्भ|आरंभः|आरम्भः
आरम्भ m. (-म्भः)<BR>	 1. A beginning, a thing begun.<BR>	 2. Haste, speed.<BR>	 3. Effort,<BR>exertion.<BR>	 4. Pride.<BR>	 5. Killing, slaughter.<BR>	 6. An introduction, a<BR>prologue, &c.<BR> E. आङ् before रभि to commence, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=097-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरभ्य
आरभ्य ind. Having begun, beginning from.<BR> E. आङ् before रभि to com-<BR>mence, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=097-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरव|आरवः
आरव m. (-वः) Sound.<BR> E. आङ् before रु to sound, अप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=097-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरस्य|आरस्यं
आरस्य n. (-स्यं) Insipidity, want of favour or spirit.<BR> E. अरस and यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=097-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आराग्र|आराग्रं
आराग्र n. (-ग्रं) The edge of a semicircular arrow head.<BR> E. आर what goes,<BR>and अग्र edge, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=097-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरात्
आरात् ind.<BR>	 1. Near.<BR>	 2. Distant, far from.<BR> E. आङ् before रा to get, आत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=097-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आराति|आरातिः
आराति m. (-तिः) An enemy.<BR> E. आङ् before रा to take or receive, आति aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=097-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरातीय
आरातीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>	 1. Near, proximate.<BR>	 2. Remote.<BR> E. आरात् and छ<BR>aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=097-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरात्रिक|आरात्रिकं
आरात्रिक n. (-कं) Waving lamps at night before an image.<BR> E. आङ् before<BR>रात्रि night, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=097-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आराधक
आराधक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Who or what worships, a worshipper.<BR> E. आङ्<BR>before राध् to finish, and वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=097-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आराधन|आराधनं
आराधन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Accomplishment.<BR>	 2. Acquirement, attainment.<BR>	 3.<BR>Gratifying, propitiating.<BR>	 4. Worshipping.<BR>	 5. Cooking.<BR>	 f. (-ना) Ser-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=098-a" target="_blank">Page098-a+ 60</a>]<BR>vice. (-नी) Worship, adoration, propitiation of the deities.<BR> E. आङ्<BR>before राध् to finish, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=097-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आराधनीय
आराधनीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) To be worshipped or adored.<BR> E. आङ् before<BR>राध् to finish, अनीयर् affix; also with तव्य and य, आराधितव्य and आराध्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=098-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आराधित
आराधित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Worshipped, honoured, reverenced.<BR>	 2. Propi-<BR>tiated, pleased.<BR>	 3. Accomplished, effected.<BR> E. आङ् before राध् to<BR>finish, क्त affix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=098-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आराध्यमान
आराध्यमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>	 1. Being worshipped, receiving worship, &c.<BR>2. Being in course of fulfilment.<BR> E. आङ् before राध् and शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=098-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आराम|आरामः
आराम m. (-मः) A garden, a grove.<BR> E. आङ् before रम् to please, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=098-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरालिक|आरालिकः
आरालिक mf. (-कः-की) A cook.<BR> E. अराल crooked, ठक् affix; always bend-<BR>ing over the dishes, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=098-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आराव|आरावः
आराव m. (-वः) Sound.<BR> E. आङ् before रु to sound, affix घञ्; also आरव.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=098-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरु|आरुः
आरु m. (-रुः)<BR>	 1. The name of a tree, (Lagerstrœmia regina.)<BR>	 2. A crab.<BR>3. A hog.<BR>	 4. A pitcher.<BR> E. ऋ to go, उण् affix, the pen. made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=098-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरुक|आरुकः
आरुक n. (-कं) A drug brought from the hills, of cooling properties.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=098-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरुरुक्षु
आरुरुक्षु mfn. (-क्षुः-क्षुः-क्षु) Desirous to rise or ascend, to advance, &c. E.<BR>आङ् before रुह् to rise, desiderative form, उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=098-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरू
आरू mfn. (-रूः-रूः-रु) Of a tawny colour.<BR>	 m. (-रूः) Tawny, (the colour.)<BR>E. ऋ to go, ऊ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=098-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरूढ|आरूढः
आरूढ mfn. (-ढः-ढा-ढं)<BR>	 1. Mounted, ascended, risen.<BR>	 2. Raised up, elevat-<BR>ed on high.<BR> E. आङ् before रुह् to grow, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=098-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरूढवत्|आरूढवन्त्
आरूढवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Mounting, rising.<BR> E. आङ् before रुह् to<BR>mount, क्तवतु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=098-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरेवत|आरेवतं|आरेवतः
आरेवत m. (-तः) A plant, (Cassia fistula.)<BR> E. आङ् before रेव, आरेव trust,<BR>तन् to stretch, ड affix; inspiring confidence during sickness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=098-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरोग्य|आरोग्यं
आरोग्य n. (-ग्यं) Health.<BR> E. आङ् reverse, रुज् to be sick, यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=098-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरोढृ
आरोढृ mfn. (-ढा-ढ्री-ढृ) Who or what mounts or rides, &c.<BR> E. आङ् be-<BR>fore रुह् to mount, affix तृच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=098-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरोप|आरोपः
आरोप m. (-पः)<BR>	 1. Placing in or on.<BR>	 2. Assigning or attributing to. E.<BR>आङ् before रुह् to mount, causal form, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=098-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरोपण|आरोपणं
आरोपण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Trusting, delivering.<BR>	 2. Placing or fixing in or on.<BR>3. Elevating.<BR>	 4. Planting.<BR>	 5. The bending of a bow.<BR> E. आङ्<BR>before रुह् to ascend, causal form, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=098-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरोपित|आरोपितं
आरोपित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Deposited, intrusted.<BR>	 2. Placed, fixed.<BR>3. Made.<BR>	 4. Raised, elevated.<BR>	 5. Consecrated.<BR>	 6. Accidental, ad-<BR>ventitious.<BR> E. आङ् before रुह् to ascend, causal form, part past.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=098-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरोह|आरोहः
आरोह m. (-हः)<BR>	 1. Length.<BR>	 2. A woman's waist.<BR>	 3. Ascent, rising, creep-<BR>ing up.<BR>	 4. Mounting, riding.<BR>	 5. The rider of a horse or elephant.<BR>6. Weight.<BR>	 7. A measure.<BR>	 8. The buttocks.<BR>	 9. A mine.<BR> E. आङ् be-<BR>fore रुह् to rise, to mount, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=098-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरोहक|आरोहकः
आरोहक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Lifting or raising up.<BR> E. आङ् before रुह् to rise,<BR>to mount, affix वुन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=098-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरोहण|आरोहणं
आरोहण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Rising, ascending.<BR>	 2. The rising or growing of new<BR>shoots.<BR>	 3. A ladder, a staircase.<BR>	 4. Riding on.<BR> E. आङ् before रुह्<BR>to ascend, affix ल्युट्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=098-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरोहिन्
आरोहिन् mfn. (-ही-हिणी-हि) One who mounts or rides.<BR> E. आङ् before<BR>रुह् to mount, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=098-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्कि|आर्किः
आर्कि m. (-र्किः) A son of the sun, as SANI and the rest.<BR> E. अर्क the sun,<BR>and इञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=098-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्क्ष|आर्क्षः
आर्क्ष mfn. (-र्क्षः-र्क्षी-र्क्षं) Stellar, regulated by the stars or constellations.<BR>E. ऋक्ष and अण aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=098-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्क्षवर्ष|आर्क्षवर्षः
आर्क्षवर्ष m. (-र्षः) A stellar year, or revolution of a constellation.<BR> E. आर्क्ष and वर्ष a year.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=098-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्गल|आर्गलः
आर्गल mf. (-लः-ली) A bolt or bar: see अर्गल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=098-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्ग्बध
आर्ग्बध m. (-धः) A plant, (Cassia fistula.)<BR> E. ऋ to go, and बध to de-<BR>stroy or prevent, deriv. irr. see आरग्बध.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=098-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्घा
आर्घा f. (-र्घा) A sort of yellow bee.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=098-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्घ्य|आर्घ्यं
आर्घ्य n. (-र्घ्यं) Wild honey.<BR> E. आर्घा and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=098-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्च्च|आर्च
आर्च्च mfn. (-र्च्चः-र्च्ची-र्च्चं)<BR>	 1. Devout, worshipping.<BR>	 2. Relating to the Ṛc<BR>or Ṛk Veda.<BR> E. अर्च्चा worship, and ण affix or ऋच् and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=098-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्च्चिक|आर्चिक
आर्च्चिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Relating to the Rig Veda, &c.<BR> E. ऋच् and ठक्<BR>aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=098-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्जव|आर्जवं
आर्जव n. (-वं)<BR>	 1. Straightness.<BR>	 2. Rectitude, propriety of act or observ-<BR>ance.<BR>	 3. Sincerity.<BR> E. ऋजु straight, अण aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=098-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्त्त|आर्त|आर्त्तः
आर्त्त mfn. (-र्त्तः-र्त्ता-र्त्तं)<BR>	 1. Pained, afflicted.<BR>	 2. Disturbed, confounded. E.<BR>ऋत to hate, to move, participial affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=098-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्त्तगल|आर्तगल|आर्तगलः|आर्त्तगलः
आर्त्तगल m. (-लः) A plant, blue Barleria, (Barleria cœrulea.)<BR> E. आर्त्त<BR>pained, गल् to eat, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=098-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्त्तनाद|आर्तनाद|आर्तनादः
आर्त्तनाद m. (-दः) A cry of pain.<BR> E. आर्त्त and नाद sound. So आर्त्तस्वर m. (-रः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=098-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्त्तव|आर्तव|आर्तवः|आर्त्तवं|आर्त्तवः
आर्त्तव mfn. (-वः-वा or -वी-वं)<BR>	 1. Menstrual, relating to or produced<BR>by this discharge.<BR>	 2. Seasonable, produced in season.<BR>	 n. (-वं)<BR>	 1. The<BR>menstrual discharge.<BR>	 2. A flower.<BR>	 f. (-वी) A mare.<BR> E. ऋतु the<BR>menses or a season, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=098-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्त्ति|आर्ति|आर्तिः|आर्त्तिः
आर्त्ति f. (-र्त्तिः)<BR>	 1. Pain.<BR>	 2. Sickness.<BR>	 3. The end of a bow.<BR> E. आङ् be-<BR>fore ऋत to move, क्तिन् affix; also अत्ति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=098-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्त्तिज्य
आर्त्तिज्य n. (-ज्यं) The office of a sacrificing priest.<BR> E. ऋत्विज् a priest, and यञ affix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=098-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्त्त्यपहरण
आर्त्त्यपहरण n. (-णं) Consoling or relieving distress, pain, &c.<BR> E. आर्त्ति<BR>and अपहरण taking away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=098-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्थिक
आर्थिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>	 1. Wise.<BR>	 2. Rich.<BR>	 3. Significant.<BR> E. अर्थ and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=098-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्द्र|आर्द्रं
आर्द्र mfn. (-र्द्रः-र्द्रा-र्द्रं)<BR>	 1. Wet, moist, damp.<BR>	 2. Fresh, not dry.<BR>	 3. Loose,<BR>flaccid.<BR>	 4. Tender, soft.<BR>	 f. (-र्द्रा) The sixth Nakshatra or lunar man-<BR>sion.<BR> E. अद् to go, रक् Unādi affix, and the pen. lengthened.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=098-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्द्रक|आर्द्रकं
आर्द्रक n. (-कं) Ginger in the undried state.<BR> E. आर्द्र moist, and वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=098-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्द्रकाष्ठ
आर्द्रकाष्ठ n. (-ष्ठं) Green wood, timber not dry.<BR> E. आर्द्र and काष्ठ wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=098-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्द्रता
आर्द्रता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Moisture, wetness.<BR>	 2. Tenderness, softness.<BR>	 3. Freshness,<BR>greenness.<BR> E. आर्द्र and तल् affix; also आर्द्रत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=098-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्द्रनयन
आर्द्रनयन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Weeping, suffused with tears.<BR> E. आर्द्र and<BR>नयन the eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=098-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्द्रमाषा
आर्द्रमाषा f. (-षा) A leguminous shrub, (Glycine debilis.)<BR> E. आर्द्र moist,<BR>and माष a sort of bean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=098-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्द्रशाक|आर्द्रशाकं
आर्द्रशाक n. (-कं) Ginger.<BR> E. आर्द्र and शाक a potherb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=098-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्द्रालुब्धक|आर्द्रालुब्धकः
आर्द्रालुब्धक m. (-कः) The dragon's tail or descending node.<BR> E. आर्द्रा the<BR>lunar mansion, and लुब्धक who desires.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=098-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्द्धद्रौणिक
आर्द्धद्रौणिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Bought with half a Drona, containing it,<BR>&c.<BR> E. अर्द्धद्रोण a measure, ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=098-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्द्धधातुक
आर्द्धधातुक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Belonging to a part of a verb, (the inflexions<BR>of six tenses.)<BR> E. अर्द्ध and धातु a root, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=098-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्द्धप्रस्थिक
आर्द्धप्रस्थिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Bought, &c. with half a Prastha.<BR> E. अर्द्धप्रस्थ<BR>a measure, and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=098-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्द्धमासिक
आर्द्धमासिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>	 1. Lasting, &c. for half a month.<BR>	 2. Observ-<BR>ing or practicing (continence, &c.) for a fortnight.<BR> E. अर्द्धमास and<BR>ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=098-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्द्धिक
आर्द्धिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>	 1. Sharing half, an equal partner.<BR>	 2. Relating<BR>to half.<BR>	 m. (-कः) One who ploughs the ground for half the crop.<BR>E. अर्द्ध half, ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=098-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्य्य|आर्य|आर्यः|आर्य्यः
आर्य्य mfn. (-र्य्यः-र्य्या-र्य्यं)<BR>	 1. Of a good family.<BR>	 2. Respectable, venerable.<BR>3. Apposite, proper.<BR>	 4. To be sought or obtained.<BR>	 m. (-र्य्यः)<BR>	 1. A<BR>master, an owner.<BR>	 2. A name of BUDDHA.<BR>	 3. A friend.<BR>	 f. (-र्य्या)<BR>1. A name of PARVATI.<BR>	 2. A kind of metre, measured by feet,<BR>each foot being equal to four short syllables, or two long and two<BR>short; there are seven and a half feet in each verse of the<BR>couplet, equal to thirty and to twenty-seven syllabic instants: the<BR>regular form consists of alternate long and short verses, but it<BR>admits of eighty principal variations.<BR> E. ऋ to go, ण्यत् affix; also<BR>अर्य्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=098-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्य्यक|आर्यक|आर्यकः|आर्य्यकं|आर्य्यकः
आर्य्यक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A grandfather.<BR>	 2. Any respectable man.<BR>	 n. (-कं)<BR>The vessel, &c. used in sacrifices made to the manes.<BR>	 f. (आर्य्यका or<BR>आर्य्यिका) A respectable woman.<BR> E. आर्य्य respectable, &c. and वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=098-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्य्यगृह्य|आर्यगृह्य
आर्य्यगृह्य mfn. (-ह्यः-ह्या-ह्यं) Decorous, respectable, right.<BR> E. आर्य्य and गृह्य<BR>to be accepted by.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=098-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्य्यपुत्र|आर्यपुत्र|आर्यपुत्रः|आर्य्यपुत्त्रः
आर्य्यपुत्र m. (-त्रः)<BR>	 1. A husband, (in theatrical language.)<BR>	 2. The son of<BR>a spiritual preceptor.<BR> E. आर्य्य a respectable person and पुत्र a son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=099-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्य्यप्राय|आर्यप्राय
आर्य्यप्राय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Abounding with respectable persons.<BR> E. आर्य्य and<BR>प्राय quantity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=099-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्य्यमिश्र|आर्यमिश्र|आर्यमिश्रः|आर्य्यमिश्रः
आर्य्यमिश्र mfn. (-श्रः-श्रा-श्रं) Distinguished, respectable.<BR>	 m. (-श्रः) A gentle-<BR>man, a man of consequence.<BR> E. आर्य्य and मिश्र mixed, joined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=099-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्य्यरूप|आर्यरूप
आर्य्यरूप mfn. (-पः-पा-पं) A hypocrite, an impostor.<BR> E. आर्य्य and रूप sem-<BR>blance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=099-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्य्यलिङ्गिन्|आर्यलिङ्गिन्
आर्य्यलिङ्गिन् mfn. (-ङ्गी-ङ्गि-नी-ङ्गि) A hypocrite, an impostor; a Śūdra,<BR>wearing the dress of a Brahman, &c.<BR> E. आर्य्य and लिङ्गिन् who bears<BR>insignia.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=099-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्य्यवृत्त|आर्यवृत्त
आर्य्यवृत्त mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं) Good, pious, virtuous.<BR> E. आर्य्य and वृत्त practised.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=099-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्य्यवेश|आर्यवेश
आर्य्यवेश mfn. (-शः-शा-शं) Well clothed, fine.<BR> E. आर्य्य and वेश vesture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=099-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्य्यागीति|आर्यागीति
आर्य्यागीति f. (-तिः) A variety of the Āryā metre, containing eight equal<BR>feet or thirty-two syllabic instants in each verse of the couplet. E.<BR>आर्य्या and गीति another metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=099-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्य्यावर्त्त|आर्यावर्त|आर्यावर्तः|आर्यावर्त्त|आर्य्यावर्त्तः
आर्य्यावर्त्त m. (-र्त्तः) The holy land, the country extending from the<BR>eastern to the western sea, and bounded on the north and south,<BR>by the Himalya and Vindhya mountains.<BR> E. आर्य्य venerable, आवर्त्त<BR>abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=099-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्व्वाक्|आर्वाक्
आर्व्वाक् ind.<BR>	 1. After, afterwards.<BR>	 2. Behind.<BR> E. अर्व्वाक् and अण् pleonastic aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=099-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्ष|आर्षः
आर्ष mfn. (-र्षः-र्षी-र्षं) Relating or belonging to or derived from a Ṛṣi.<BR>m. (-र्षः) A form of marriage, the father of the bride receiving one<BR>or two pair of kine from the bridegroom.<BR>	 n. (-र्षं) The Vedas.<BR>	 f. (-र्षा)<BR>One of the orders of the metres of the Vedas.<BR> E. ऋषि and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=099-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्षभि|आर्षभिः
आर्षभि m. (-भिः) A name of BHARATA, emperor of India.<BR> E. ऋषभ ex-<BR>cellent, and इञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=099-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्षभ्य|आर्षभ्यः
आर्षभ्य m. (-भ्यः) A steer fit to be let loose.<BR> E. ऋषभ an ox, यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=099-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्षेय
आर्षेय mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>	 1. Relating or belonging to or derived from a<BR>Ṛṣi.<BR>	 2. Venerable, respectable.<BR> E. ऋषि a sage, ढक् affix; also आर्ष<BR>and आर्ष्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=099-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्षोढा
आर्षोढा f. (-ढा) A wife married according to the Arsha form.<BR> E. आर्ष and<BR>ऊढ married.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=099-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्हत|आर्हतः
आर्हत m. (-तः) A Jaina, a follower of the doctrines of a Jaina or Arhata.<BR>E. अर्हत् a Jaina, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=099-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्हत्य|आर्हत्यं
आर्हत्य nf. (-त्यं-न्ती) The quality or practice of an Arhata or Jaina saint. E.<BR>अर्हत् a Jaina, ष्यञ् affix fem. ङीष् with the nasal inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=099-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आल|आलं|आलः
आल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Large, extensive.<BR>	 n. (-लं) Yellow orpiment.<BR> E. अल<BR>to adorn, in the causal form, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=099-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलगर्द्द|आलगर्द|आलगर्दः|आलगर्द्दः
आलगर्द्द m. (-र्द्धः) A species of Cobra. E. See अलगर्द्द.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=099-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलभ्य
आलभ्य ind. Having received or obtained.<BR> E. आङ् before लभि to gain, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=099-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलम्भ|आलंभः|आलम्भः
आलम्भ m. (-म्भः)<BR>	 1. Slaughter, killing.<BR>	 2. Embracing.<BR> E. आङ् before लभि<BR>to kill, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=099-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलम्भ्य
आलम्भ्य mfn. (-म्भ्यः-म्भ्या-म्भयं)<BR>	 1. Fit or proper to be killed.<BR>	 2. Obtainable,<BR>to be obtained.<BR> E. आङ् before लभि with ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=099-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलम्ब|आलंब|आलम्बः
आलम्ब m. (-म्बः)<BR>	 1. A receptacle, a prop, an asylum or support.<BR>	 2. De-<BR>pending on or from.<BR>	 3. A perpendicular.<BR> E. आङ् before लम्बि to go,<BR>affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=099-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलम्बन|आलंबनं|आलम्बनं
आलम्बन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Depending on or resting upon, hanging from.<BR>	 2. The<BR>natural and necessary connexion of feeling with the cause by which<BR>it is excited.<BR>	 3. Supporting, sustaining.<BR> E. आङ् before लबि to go,<BR>ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=099-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलम्बित|आलंबित
आलम्बित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Pendant, suspended, hanging from or on.<BR>	 2.<BR>Supported, upheld.<BR>	 3. Protected.<BR> E. आङ् before लबि to go, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=099-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलम्बिन्|आलंबिन्
आलम्बिन् mfn. (-म्बी-म्बिनी-म्बि)<BR>	 1. Depending on or from, hanging from,<BR>&c.<BR>	 2. Supporting, maintaining.<BR> E. आलम्ब support, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=099-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलय|आलयं|आलयः
आलय m. (-यः) A house, a dwelling, a receptacle, an asylum.<BR> E. आङ्<BR>before लीङ् to enfold, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=099-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलवण्य|आलवण्यं
आलवण्य n. (-ण्यं)<BR>	 1. Ugliness.<BR>	 2. Insipidity.<BR> E. अ neg. लवण handsome,<BR>affix यञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=099-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलवाल|आलवालं
आलवाल n. (-लं) A basin for water round the root of a tree.<BR> E. आङ् be-<BR>fore लू to cut or dig, and आलच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=099-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलस|आलसः
आलस mfn. (-सः-सी-सं) Idle, slothful, lazy.<BR> E. अलस idle, अण् affix: see<BR>अलस.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=099-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलस्य|आलस्यं|आलस्यः
आलस्य mfn. (-स्यः-स्यी-स्यं) Idle, slothful, apathetic.<BR>	 n. (-स्यं) Idleness,<BR>sloth.<BR> E. अलस idle, and यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=099-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलात|आलातं
आलात n. (-तं) A firebrand, a coal burning or extinguished.<BR> E. अलात and<BR>अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=099-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलान|आलानं
आलान n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. The post to which an elephant is lied.<BR>	 2. The rope that<BR>ties him.<BR>	 3. A fetter, a tie.<BR>	 4. Tying, binding.<BR>	 5. A rope or string.<BR>E. आङ् before ला to take, आला to tie or fasten, affix ल्युट.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=099-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलाप|आलापः
आलाप m. (-पः)<BR>	 1. Speaking to, addressing, conversation.<BR>	 2. Enumera-<BR>tion of the questions in an arithmetical or algebraic sum.<BR> E. आङ्<BR>before लप् to speak, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=099-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलापन
आलापन n. (-नं) Speaking to, conversing with.<BR> E. आङ before लप् to<BR>speak, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=099-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलापनीय
आलापनीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>	 1. To be said or spoken.<BR>	 2. To be spoken to<BR>or addressed.<BR> E. आङ् before लप् to speak, अनीयर affix; also आलाप्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=099-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलापिन्
आलापिन् mfn. (-पी-पिनी-पि) Who speaks or converses.<BR> E. आङ before लप्<BR>to speak, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=099-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलाबु|आलाबुः
आलाबु f. (-बुः) A pumpkin gourd: also आलाबू, अलाबु and अलाबू, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=099-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलावर्त्त|आलावर्त|आलावर्तं|आलावर्त्तं
आलावर्त्त n. (-र्त्तं) A fan made of cloth.<BR> E. आल orpiment, and आवर्त्त abode:<BR>stained or painted with some such substance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=099-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलास्य|आलास्यः
आलास्य m. (-स्यः) A crocodile.<BR> E. आल wide, large, and आस्य a mouth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=099-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलि|आलिः
आलि mfn. sub. (-लिः-लिः or ली-लि)<BR>	 1. Pure, honest, sincere.<BR>	 2. Useless,<BR>idle, unmeaning.<BR>	 f. (-लिः-ली)<BR>	 1. A woman's female friend.<BR>	 2. A row<BR>or range, a continuous line.<BR>	 3. A ridge or mound of earth, crossing<BR>ditches, dividing fields, &c.<BR>	 2. A line, a race or family.<BR>	 m. (-लिः)<BR>1. A scorpion.<BR>	 2. A bee; see अलि.<BR> E. अल to adorn, to be able, &c.<BR>affix इण् and the pen. made long; also आली, affix ङीप.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=099-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलिङ्गन|आलिंगन|आलिंगनं|आलिङ्गनं
आलिङ्गन n. (-नं) Embracing, an embrace.<BR> E. आङ् before लिगि to ap-<BR>proach, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=099-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलिङ्गित|आलिंगित|आलिङ्गितः
आलिङ्गित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Embraced.<BR> E. आङ् before लिगि to approach, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=099-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलिङ्गिन्|आलिंगिन्
आलिङ्गिन् mfn. (-ङ्गी-ङ्गिनी-ङ्गि) Embracing.<BR>	 m. (-ङ्गी) A small drum shaped<BR>like a barley corn, and carried upon the breast.<BR> E. आलिङ्ग an em-<BR>brace, and इनि affix; also आलिङ्गी fem. ङीप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=099-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलिङ्ग्य|आलिंग्य|आलिङ्ग्यः
आलिङ्ग्य mfn. (-ङ्ग्यः-ङ्ग्या-ङ्ग्यं) To be embraced.<BR>	 m. (-ङ्ग्यः) A small drum:<BR>see the preceding.<BR> E. आलिङ्ग and ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=099-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलिञ्जर|आलिंजर|आलिंजरः|आलिञ्जरः
आलिञ्जर m. (-रः) A large clay water jar.<BR> E. अलिञ्जर a jar. अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=099-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलिन्
आलिन् m. (-ली) A scorpion. E. See आलि, affix इनि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=099-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलिन्द|आलिंद|आलिंदः|आलिन्दः
आलिन्द m. (-न्दः)<BR>	 1. A terrace before a house.<BR>	 2. A raised place or<BR>terrace for sleeping upon.<BR> E. अलिन्द the same, and अण् affix: see<BR>अलिन्द also आलिन्दक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=099-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलिप्त
आलिप्त mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं) Smeared, plastered, anointed.<BR> E. आङ् before लिप<BR>to smear, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=099-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलिम्पन|आलिंपनं|आलिम्पनं
आलिम्पन m. (-नः) Whitening or painting the floor, wall, &c. on festival<BR>occasions.<BR> E. आङ् before लिपि to plaster, and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=099-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आली
आली f. (-ली)<BR>	 1. A female friend.<BR>	 2. A row or range.<BR>	 3. A field, boundary<BR>or mound: see आलि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=099-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलीढ|आलीढं
आलीढ mfn. (-ढः-ढा-ढं)<BR>	 1. Eaten.<BR>	 2. Licked.<BR>	 n. (-ढं) An attitude in<BR>shooting, the right knee advanced, the left leg retracted.<BR> E. आङ<BR>before लिह् to lick, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=099-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलीढक|आलीढकं
आलीढक n. (-कं) The frolicking of a calf. Sometimes written आढीलक<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=099-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलीन
आलीन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Melted, fused.<BR> E. आङ् before ली to melt, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=099-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलीनक|आलीनकं
आलीनक n. (-कं) Tin.<BR> E. आलीन and affix वुन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=099-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलु|आलुः
आलु f. (-लुः) A pitcher, a small water jar.<BR>	 mn. (-लुः-लु)<BR>	 1. An esculent<BR>root, (Arum campanulatum:) in the modern dialects this name is<BR>applied to the yam, potatoe, &c.<BR>	 2. A raft, a float.<BR>	 m. (-लुः) An owl.<BR>E. ऋ to go, and उण् affix, आरु what goes, (in the earth, water, &c.)<BR>the initial is lengthened, and र is changed to ल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=099-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलुक|आलुकं|आलुकः
आलुक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A name of the chief of the Nagas or serpent race:<BR>see शेष.<BR>	 2. An esculent root: see आलु.<BR> E. कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=100-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलून
आलून mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Cut, out off.<BR> E. आङ् before लून cut.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=100-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलेखन|आलेखनं|आलेखनः
आलेखन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Writing.<BR>	 2. Painting.<BR>	 f. (-नी) A brush, a pencil. E.<BR>आङ before लिख् to write, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=100-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलेख्य|आलेख्यं
आलेख्य mfn. (-ख्यः-ख्या-ख्यं)<BR>	 1. To be written.<BR>	 2. To be delineated or painted.<BR>n. (-ख्यं)<BR>	 1. A painting.<BR>	 2. A writing.<BR> E. आङ् before लिख् to write,<BR>ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=100-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलेख्यशेष|आलेख्यशेषः
आलेख्यशेष mfn. (-षः-षा-षं) Dead, deceased.<BR> E. आलेख्य painting, writing, and शेष final.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=100-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलेप|आलेपः
आलेप m. (-पः)<BR>	 1. Smearing, plastering, anointing.<BR>	 2. Liniment.<BR> E. आङ्<BR>before लिपि to anoint, घञ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=100-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलेपन
आलेपन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Smearing, plastering, anointing.<BR>	 2. Liniment.<BR> E. आङ्<BR>before लिप् to smear, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=100-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलोक|आलोकः
आलोक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. Sight, seeing, looking.<BR>	 2. Light.<BR>	 3. Flattery, compli-<BR>mentary language, panegyric.<BR> E. आङ् before लोकृ to see, घञ affix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=100-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलोकन|आलोकनं
आलोकन n. (-नं) Sight, seeing, looking.<BR> E. आङ् before लोकृ to see, ल्युट<BR>affix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=100-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलोकित
आलोकित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Seen, beheld.<BR> E. आङ् before लोकृ to see, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=100-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलोचक
आलोचक n. (-कं) The faculty of vision or the cause of sight.<BR> E. आङ् be-<BR>fore लोच to see and वुञ् affix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=100-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलोचन|आलोचनं
आलोचन nf. (-नं-ना) Sight, seeing.<BR> E. आङ् before लोच to see, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=100-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलोचित
आलोचित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Seen, beheld.<BR>	 2. Considered.<BR> E. आङ् before<BR>लोच to see, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=100-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलोच्य
आलोच्य mfn. (-च्यः-च्या-च्यं) To be seen, thought of or considered; also<BR>आलोचनीय.<BR> E. आङ् before लोच to see, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=100-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलोडन|आलोडनं
आलोडन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Mixing, blending.<BR>	 2. Stirring, shaking, agitating. E.<BR>आङ before लुड to stir, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=100-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलोडित
आलोडित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Mixed, blended.<BR>	 2. Shaken, agitated.<BR> E. आङ्<BR>before लुड to stir, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=100-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलोल|आलोलः
आलोल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Shaken, agitated.<BR>	 m. (-लः) Trembling, agitation.<BR>E. आङ् before लुड to shake, affix घञ्, ड changed to ल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=100-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलोलित
आलोलित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Shaken, agitated.<BR> E. आङ् before लुल to shake, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=100-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवनेय|आवनेयः
आवनेय m. (-यः) The planet MARS.<BR> E. अवनी the earth, ठक् patronymic aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=100-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवन्त्य|आवंत्य|आवन्त्यः
आवन्त्य m. (-न्त्यः)<BR>	 1. The offspring of a degraded Brahman.<BR>	 2. An in-<BR>habitant. &c. of Avanti or Ougein.<BR> E. अवन्ती and ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=100-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवपन|आवपनं
आवपन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Any vessel.<BR>	 2. Weaving.<BR>	 3. Sowing seed.<BR> E. आङ् be-<BR>fore वप् to sow, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=100-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवरक
आवरक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) A cover, a veil, what covers or conceals.<BR> E. आङ<BR>before वृ with वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=100-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवरण|आवरणं
आवरण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Covering.<BR>	 2. A covering, a garment.<BR>	 3. A shield.<BR>	 4. An<BR>outer bar or fence, a wall.<BR>	 5. An obstruction.<BR>	 6. Mental blindness. E.<BR>आङ् before वृ to screen, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=100-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवरणशक्ति|आवरणशक्तिः
आवरणशक्ति f. (-क्तिः) The power of illusion, that which veils the real na-<BR>ture of things.<BR> E. आवरण and शक्ति power.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=100-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवर्त्त|आवर्त|आवर्तः|आवर्त्तं|आवर्त्तः
आवर्त्त m. (-र्त्तः)<BR>	 1. Revolving, turning round.<BR>	 2. A whirlpool.<BR>	 3. A lock<BR>of hair that curls backwards, especially on a horse.<BR>	 4. Deliberation,<BR>revolving.<BR>	 5. A mineral substance, pyrites, marcasite.<BR> E. आङ् be-<BR>fore वृत् to choose, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=100-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवर्त्तक|आवर्तक|आवर्तकः
आवर्त्तक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A revolution, a whirl.<BR>	 2. A whirlpool.<BR>	 3. A curl of<BR>hair, especially on a horse.<BR>	 4. Revolution of the mind from the in-<BR>fluence of the senses.<BR>	 5. The depression above the frontal ridge or<BR>over the eyebrows.<BR>	 f. (-की) The name of a creeping plant.<BR> E. कन्<BR>added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=100-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवर्त्तन|आवर्तन|आवर्तनः|आवर्त्तनं
आवर्त्तन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Turning, turning round.<BR>	 2. Churning.<BR>	 3. Stirring any<BR>thing in fusion.<BR>	 4. Melting metals together, alligation.<BR>	 5. The time<BR>when shadows are cast in an opposite direction.<BR>	 6. Repeating, doing<BR>over again.<BR>	 7. Study, practicing.<BR>	 f. (-नी) A crucible.<BR> E. आवर्त्त, ल्युट्<BR>affix; and ङीप् for the fem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=100-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवर्त्तनमणि|आवर्तनमणि|आवर्त्तनमणिः
आवर्त्तनमणि m. (-णिः) A gem of a secondary order, commonly Rajavatta.<BR>E. आवर्त्तन the same, and मणि a jewel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=100-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवर्त्तनीय|आवर्तनीय
आवर्त्तनीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>	 1. To be whirled or turned round.<BR>	 2. To be<BR>reversed.<BR>	 3. To be repeated.<BR> E. आङ् before वृत् to be, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=100-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवर्त्तमान|आवर्तमान
आवर्त्तमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>	 1. Advancing, proceeding.<BR>	 2. Revolving, going<BR>round.<BR> E. आङ् before वृत् to be, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=100-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवर्त्तिन्|आवर्तिन्
आवर्त्तिन् mfn. (-र्त्ती-र्त्तिनी-र्त्ति) What whirls or turns upon itself.<BR>	 m. (-र्त्ती)<BR>A horse having curls of hair on various parts of his body: it is<BR>considered as a lucky mark.<BR>	 f. (-नी) A whirlpool.<BR> E. आवर्त्त and इनि<BR>aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=100-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवर्हित|आवर्हितः
आवर्हित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Eradicated, plucked up by the roots.<BR> E. आङ् be-<BR>fore वर्ह to hurt, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=100-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवलि|आवलिः
आवलि f. (-लिः)<BR>	 1. A row, a range, a continuous line.<BR>	 2. A series, dynasty,<BR>a lineage.<BR> E. आङ् before वल to move, इन् affix; also आवली, taking ङीप्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=100-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवल्य
आवल्य n. (-ल्यं) Weakness.<BR> E. अवल weak, यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=100-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवश्य|आवश्यं
आवश्य n. (-श्यं) Necessity, inevitable act or conclusion.<BR> E. अवश्य and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=100-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवश्यक|आवश्यकं
आवश्यक n. (-कं) Mecessity, inevitable act or conclusion.<BR> E. अवश्य certain,<BR>affs. अण् and कन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=100-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवश्यकत्व|आवश्यकत्वं
आवश्यकत्व n. (-त्वं) Necessity, inevitability.<BR> E. त्व added to आवश्यक, also<BR>with तल्, आवश्यकता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=100-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवसथ|आवसथं|आवसथः
आवसथ mn. (-थः-थं)<BR>	 1. A house.<BR>	 2. A fire temple or place where sacrificial<BR>fire is preserved.<BR>	 m. (-थः)<BR>	 1. A treatise on the poetical metre called<BR>Ārya. (आर्य्याकोषः) see आर्य्या.<BR>	 2. A particular religious observance.<BR>E. आङ् before वस् to dwell, अथ Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=100-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवसथिक|आवसथिकः
आवसथिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Inhabiting a house, household, domestic. E.<BR>अवसथ and ष्ठल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=100-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवसथ्य|आवसथ्यः
आवसथ्य n. (-थ्यं) A house.<BR> E. अवसथ and यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=100-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवसित|आवसितं
आवसित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Stored, (as grain.)<BR>	 2. Winnowed.<BR>	 3. Ripe, full<BR>grown.<BR> E. आङ् before अव reverse, and षो to destroy, participial<BR>affix क्त; also अवसित.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=100-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवह|आवहः
आवह mfn. (-हः-हा-हं) What bears or conveys.<BR>	 m. (-हः) One of the seven<BR>winds.<BR> E. आङ् before वह to bear, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=100-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवहत्
आवहत् mfn. (-हन्-हन्ती-हत्) Obtaining, receiving.<BR> E. आङ् before वह् to<BR>bear, affix शतृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=100-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवहमान|आवहमानं
आवहमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Followed, succeeded, come in succession. E.<BR>आङ् before वह् to bear, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=100-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवहित
आवहित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Rooted up, extirpated.<BR> E. आङ् before वह् to bear, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=100-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवात्
आवात् mfn. (-वान्-वान्ती-वात्) Blowing.<BR> E. आङ् before वा to blow, aff. शतृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=100-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवाधा
आवाधा f. (-धा)<BR>	 1. Pain.<BR>	 2. Distress.<BR>	 3. Segment of the base of a triangle.<BR>E. आङ् before वाधा the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=100-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवाप|आवापः
आवाप m. (-पः)<BR>	 1. A basin for water round the root of a tree.<BR>	 2. A bracelet.<BR>3. Hostile purpose, intention of going to war, (as a king.)<BR>	 4. Throw-<BR>ing, casting, directing.<BR>	 5. Sowing seed.<BR>	 6. Throwing additional<BR>ingredients into any compound, (in pharmacy, &c.) in course of<BR>preparation.<BR>	 7. Mixing, inserting.<BR>	 8. Uneven ground.<BR>	 9. A vessel.<BR>10. Principal sacrifice with fire.<BR> E. आङ्, वप् to sow, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=100-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवापक|आवापकः
आवापक m. (-कः) A bracelet of gold, &c.<BR> E. कन् added the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=100-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवापन|आवापनं
आवापन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. A loom, an implement for weaving.<BR>	 2. A reel or<BR>frame for winding thread.<BR> E. आङ् before वप् to weave, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=100-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवारि|आवारिः
आवारि m. (-रिः) A shop, a stall.<BR> E. आङ् before वृ to nourish, in the<BR>causal form, इ affix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=100-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवार्य|आवार्य्य
आवार्य ind. Covering, hiding, concealing.<BR> E. आङ् before वृ to screen,<BR>ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=100-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवाल|आवालं
आवाल n. (-लं) A basin for water round the foot of a tree.<BR> E. आङ् before<BR>वल to move, घञ् affix; also आलवाल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=100-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवाल्य|आवाल्यं
आवाल्य n. (-ल्यं) Age or time ending with infancy.<BR> E. आङ् unto, वाल्य<BR>childhood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=100-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवास|आवासः
आवास m. (-सः) A house, a dwelling.<BR> E. आङ्, वस् to dwell, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=100-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवाहन|आवाहनं
आवाहन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Calling.<BR>	 2. Inviting.<BR>	 3. Offering oblations with fire.<BR>f. (-नी) A particular position of the hands or the palms put to-<BR>gether, and the thumbs put at the root of the ring finger.<BR> E. आङ्<BR>before वह् to bear, causal form, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=100-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवाहित
आवाहित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Invoked, invited.<BR> E. आङ् before वह् to bear,<BR>causal form, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=101-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आविक|आविकः
आविक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Woollen, &c. or anything relating to or derived<BR>from a sheep.<BR>	 m. (-कः) A blanket, woollen cloth.<BR> E. अवि a sheep,<BR>वुज् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=101-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आविकसौत्रिक
आविकसौत्रिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Made of woollen thread.<BR> E. आविक and<BR>सूत्र a thread, ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=101-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आविग्न|आविग्नः
आविग्न m. (-ग्नः) A small fruit tree, vulgarly Carinda, (Carissa carondas.) Also अविग्न.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=101-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आविद्ध
आविद्ध mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>	 1. Pierced, wounded.<BR>	 2. Crooked.<BR>	 3. Cast, thrown,<BR>sent.<BR>	 4. Disappointed.<BR>	 5. Stupid, foolish.<BR> E. आङ् before व्यध to hurt,<BR>क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=101-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आविद्धकर्णी
आविद्धकर्णी f. (-र्णी) A plant, (Aknidhi:) also आविद्धकर्णिका f. (-का.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=101-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आविध|आविधः
आविध m. (-धः) An awl, a drill, a kind of gimlet worked by a string.<BR>E. आङ् before व्यध to pierce, घञ् or क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=101-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आविर्भाव|आविर्भावः
आविर्भाव m. (-वः) Manifestation, presence, becoming visible.<BR> E. आविस्<BR>manifestly, and भाव condition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=101-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आविर्भूत|आविर्भूतः
आविर्भूत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Appeared manifest, become visible.<BR> E. आविस्<BR>and भूत become.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=101-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आविल
आविल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Foul, turbid.<BR> E. आङ् before विल to break, and क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=101-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आविष्करण|आविष्करणं
आविष्करण n. (-णं) Manifestation, making visible<BR> E. आविस् and करण<BR>making.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=101-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आविष्कार|आविष्कारः
आविष्कार m. (-रः) Becoming or making visible.<BR> E. आविस् and कार making.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=101-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आविष्कृत|आविष्कृतः
आविष्कृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Made or become visible, evident, manifest. E.<BR>आविस् apparent, and कृत made.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=101-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आविष्ट|आविष्टः
आविष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>	 1. Entered.<BR>	 2. Possessed, (by a demon, &c.)<BR>	 3.<BR>Possessed, engrossed, (by any sentiment or feeling.)<BR> E. आविश to<BR>enter, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=101-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आविस्
आविस् ind. Manifest, evident.<BR> E. आङ् before उङ् to sound, इर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=101-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवी
आवी f. (-वी) Pain of child-birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=101-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवीत
आवीत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Passed, gone.<BR>	 2. Placed, hung.<BR>	 m. (-तः) The<BR>sacrificial cord worn in any particular manner.<BR> E. आङ् before वीत<BR>gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=101-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवीतिन्
आवीतिन् m. (-ती) A Brahman who wears the cord in any particular<BR>manner.<BR> E. इनि added to the last: see प्राचीनावीतिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=101-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवूक
आवूक m. (-कः) A father, (in theatrical language.)<BR> E. अव to preserve,<BR>ऊकन् affix, and the initial lengthened.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=101-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवृत्
आवृत् f. (-वृत्) Order, method.<BR> E. आङ् before वृत् to choose, affix क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=101-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवृत|आवृतः
आवृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Enclosed, surrounded, (by a ditch, wall, &c.)<BR>2. Covered, screened.<BR>	 3. Invested, inclosed, involved.<BR>	 4. Spread,<BR>overspread, overcast.<BR>	 5. Filled with, abounding with.<BR>	 m. (-तः) A<BR>man of mixed origin, the son of a Brahman, by a woman of the<BR>Ugra caste.<BR> E. आङ् before वृञ् to screen, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=101-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवृत्त|आवृत्तः
आवृत्त mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं)<BR>	 1. Whirled, stirred, turned round.<BR>	 2. Reverted,<BR>averted.<BR>	 3. Retreated, fled.<BR> E. आङ् before वृत् to be, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=101-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवृत्ति|आवृत्तिः
आवृत्ति f. (-त्तिः)<BR>	 1. Reversion, turning back or from.<BR>	 2. Flight, retreat.<BR>3. Revolving, going round.<BR>	 4. Worldly existence, the revolution of<BR>births.<BR>	 5. Use, employment, application.<BR> E. आङ् before वृत् to be,<BR>क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=101-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवेग|आवेगः
आवेग m. (-गः)<BR>	 1. Hurry, haste.<BR>	 2. Flurry, agitation.<BR>	 f. (-गी) A potherb,<BR>(Convulvulus argenteus.)<BR> E. आङ् before विज् to be alarmed, घञ्<BR>and ङीप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=101-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवेदक|आवेदकः
आवेदक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) One who makes known.<BR>	 m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. An ap-<BR>pellant, a suitor.<BR>	 2. An informer.<BR> E. आङ् before विद् to know,<BR>causal form, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=101-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवेदन|आवेदनं
आवेदन n. (-नं) Representing, addressing or apprising respectfully.<BR> E. आङ् and वेदन informing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=101-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवेदित|आवेदितः
आवेदित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Made known, communicated, represented. E.<BR>आङ् before विद् to know, causal form, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=101-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवेद्य
आवेद्य mfn. (-द्यः-द्या-द्यं) To be represented or made known. ind. Having<BR>made known.<BR> E. आङ् before विद् to know, causal form, यत् or ल्यप्<BR>affix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=101-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवेद्यमान
आवेद्यमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Stating, representing.<BR> E. आङ् before विद् to<BR>know, causal form, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=101-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवेश|आवेशः
आवेश m. (-शः)<BR>	 1. Entrance, entering.<BR>	 2. Pride, arrogance.<BR>	 3. Indis-<BR>tinctness of idea, apoplectic or epileptic giddiness.<BR>	 4. Absorp-<BR>tion of the faculties in one wish or idea, devotedness to an ob-<BR>ject.<BR>	 5. Demoniac frenzy, possession, &c.<BR> E. आङ् before विश् to<BR>enter, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=101-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवेशन|आवेशनं
आवेशन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Entrance, entering.<BR>	 2. A house in which work is<BR>carried on, a workshop, a manufactory, &c.<BR>	 3. Possession by devils,<BR>&c.<BR>	 4. Passion, fury.<BR>	 5. The disk of the sun.<BR> E. आङ् before विश् to<BR>enter, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=101-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवेशिक|आवेशिकः
आवेशिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>	 1. A guest, a visitor.<BR>	 2. Entering into.<BR>	 3.<BR>Own, peculiar, unparticipated.<BR>	 4. Inherent.<BR> E. आङ् before विश् to<BR>enter, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=101-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवेष्टक|आवेष्टकः
आवेष्टक m. (-कः) A wall, a fence, an enclosure.<BR> E. आङ् before वेष्ट to sur-<BR>round, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=101-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवेष्टन|आवेष्टनं
आवेष्टन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Wrapping round, binding, tying.<BR>	 2. A wrapper, an<BR>envelope, a bandage.<BR>	 3. An inclosure.<BR> E. आङ् before वेष्ट to surround,<BR>ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=101-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवेष्टित
आवेष्टित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Surrounded, enveloped, inclosed, bound or tied.<BR>E. आङ् before वेष्ट to inclose, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=101-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशंसन|आशंसनं
आशंसन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Expecting, wishing.<BR>	 2. Declaring, asserting.<BR> E. आङ्<BR>before शसि to wish, &c. ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=101-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशंसा
आशंसा f. (-सा)<BR>	 1. wish, desire.<BR>	 2. Speech, declaration.<BR> E. आङ् before<BR>शसि to desire, अङ् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=101-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशंसित
आशंसित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Wished, expected.<BR>	 2. Declared, said.<BR> E. आङ् be-<BR>fore शसि to desire, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=101-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशंसितृ
आशंसितृ mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ)<BR>	 1. Wishing, desiring.<BR>	 2. Asserting.<BR> E. आङ्<BR>before शसि to wish, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=101-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशंसु|आशंसुः
आशंसु mfn. (-सुः-सुः-सु) Wishing, desiring.<BR> E. आङ् before शसि to wish,<BR>and उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=101-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशक्त|आशक्तः
आशक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं) Able, powerful.<BR> E. आङ् before and शक्त able.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=101-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशक्ति|आशक्तिः
आशक्ति f. (-क्तिः) Power, ability, might.<BR> E. आङ् before शक्ति power.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=101-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशङ्कनीय|आशंकनीय
आशङ्कनीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>	 1. To be doubted, questionable.<BR>	 2. To be<BR>apprehended.<BR> E. आङ् before शकि to doubt, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=101-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशङ्का|आशंका
आशङ्का f. (-ङ्का)<BR>	 1. Fear, apprehension.<BR>	 2. Doubt, uncertainty.<BR> E. आङ्<BR>before शकि to doubt, अच् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=101-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशङ्कान्वित
आशङ्कान्वित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Afraid.<BR>	 2. Doubting, uncertain.<BR> E. आशङ्का<BR>and अन्वित having.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=101-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशङ्कित|आशंकित
आशङ्कित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Feared, dreaded.<BR>	 2. Doubted.<BR> E. आङ् before<BR>शकि to doubt, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=101-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशन|आशनः
आशन m. (-नः) A tree, (Pentaptera tomentosa.) See असन and आसन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=101-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशय|आशयः
आशय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. Meaning, intention.<BR>	 2. Free will or pleasure.<BR>	 3. An<BR>asylum, an abode or retreat.<BR>	 4. receptacle, a recipient.<BR>	 5. Any re-<BR>cipient or containing vessel or viscus of the body, as रक्ताशय the<BR>heart, आमाशय the stomach, &c.<BR>	 6. The stomach in particular.<BR>7. The mind.<BR>	 8. Property, possessions.<BR>	 9. A miser, a niggard.<BR>	 10.<BR>Virtue and vice.<BR>	 11. Fate, fortune.<BR>	 12. The Jack, a kind of bread-<BR>fruit tree.<BR> E. आङ् before शीङ् to rest, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=101-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशयाश|आशयाशः
आशयाश m. (-शः) A name of fire: see आश्रयास.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=101-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशयितृ
आशयितृ mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ)<BR>	 1. Feeding, a feeder, one who gives food.<BR>	 2. Pro-<BR>tecting, a protector.<BR>	 3. Recipient, a receiver.<BR> E. अश् to eat, causal<BR>form, affix शतृ or आङ् before शीङ् to rest, with the same aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=101-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशर|आशरः
आशर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Fire.<BR>	 2. An imp, a goblin.<BR> E. आङ् before शृ to injure,<BR>अप् affix; also आशिर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=101-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशल|आशलः
आशल m. (-लः) A tree: see जीवक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=101-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशव|आशवं
आशव n. (-वं) A spirit distilled from molasses: see आसव.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=101-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशा
आशा f. (-शा)<BR>	 1. Hope, desire.<BR>	 2. Length.<BR>	 3. A quarter, a region. E.<BR>आङ् before अशू to expand, अच् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=101-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशाढ|आशाढः
आशाढ m. (-ढः)<BR>	 1. The month Ashaḍha, (June-July.)<BR>	 2. A staff of Palasa<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=102-a" target="_blank">Page102-a+ 60</a>]<BR>wood carried by ascetics.<BR>	 f. (-ढा) The name of two of the lunar<BR>mansions: see पूर्व्वाषाढा and उत्तराषाढा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=101-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशान्वित
आशान्वित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Having hope.<BR> E. आशा and अन्वित possessed of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=102-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशाप्राप्त
आशाप्राप्त mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं) Successful, possessing the object hoped for. E.<BR>आशा and प्राप्त obtained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=102-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशाबन्ध|आशाबन्धः
आशाबन्ध m. (-न्धः)<BR>	 1. Confidence, trust, expectation.<BR>	 2. A spider's web. E.<BR>आशा hope, &c. and बन्ध a binding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=102-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशाभङ्ग|आशाभंग|आशाभङ्गः
आशाभङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः) Disappointment.<BR> E. आशा and भङ्ग breaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=102-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशावत्|आशावन्त्
आशावत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Hoping, having hope.<BR> E. आशा and मतुप् poss.<BR>affix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=102-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशाहीन
आशाहीन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Desponding, despairing.<BR> E. आशा and हीन des-<BR>titude of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=102-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशिञ्जित|आशिंजित
आशिञ्जित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Tinkling, applied to the ornaments worn on<BR>the hands and feet.<BR> E. आङ् before शिजि to tinkle, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=102-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशित|आशितं
आशित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Eaten.<BR> E. आङ् before अश् to eat, affix क्त; also<BR>अशित.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=102-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशितङ्गवीन|आशितंगवीन|आशितङ्गवीनं
आशितङ्गवीन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Formerly grazed by cattle.<BR> E. आशित eaten,<BR>गवीन irregular derivative of गो a cow, and खश् affix; also अशितङ्गवीन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=102-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशितम्भव|आशितंभव|आशितम्भवं
आशितम्भव n. (-वं) Food, victuals.<BR>	 m. (-वः) Satisfaction, satiety.<BR> E. आशित<BR>and भव produced by, from भ and खश् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=102-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशितृ
आशितृ mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ) Voracious, gluttonous, eating excessively.<BR> E. अश्<BR>to eat, and तृच् affix, इ inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=102-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशिर|आशिरः
आशिर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Fire.<BR>	 2. A goblin or imp.<BR> E. आङ् before अश् to eat,<BR>किरच् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=102-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशिस्
आशिस् f. (-शीः)<BR>	 1. Blessing, benediction, bestowing or wishing, a bles-<BR>sing upon others.<BR>	 2. A serpent's fang.<BR> E. आङ् before शास् to rule,<BR>क्विप् affix, and आ is changed to इ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=102-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशी
आशी f. (-शीः)<BR>	 1. Wishing or bestowing a blessing.<BR>	 2. A serpent's fang.<BR>3. A kind of venom, the venom of a snake.<BR> E. आङ् before अश् to<BR>eat, अच् and ङीप् affixes: see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=102-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशीर्वचन
आशीर्वचन n. (-नं) A blessing, a benediction.<BR> E. आशिस् and वचन speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=102-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशीर्वाद|आशीर्वादः|आशीर्व्वादः
आशीर्वाद m. (-दः) A blessing, a benediction.<BR> E. आशिस् and वाद speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=102-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशीविष|आशीविषः
आशीविष m. (-षः) A snake.<BR> E. आशी a fang, and विष poison; in whose<BR>fang is venom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=102-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशु|आशुः
आशु mfn. (-शुः-शुः-शु) Going quickly, fleet, fast.<BR>	 mn. (-शुः-शु) Rice ripen-<BR>ing in the rainy season.<BR>	 n. adv. (-शु) Quick, quickly.<BR> E. अशू to per-<BR>vade, उण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=102-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशुकारिन्
आशुकारिन् mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>	 1. Doing anything quickly, smart, active.<BR>2. (In medicine) Operating speedily.<BR> E. आशु quick and कारिन् what<BR>acts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=102-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशुग|आशुगः
आशुग mfn. (-गः-गा-गं) Going or moving quickly, swift, fleet.<BR>	 m. (-गः)<BR>	 1.<BR>The wind.<BR>	 2. An arrow.<BR> E. आशु quick, and ग who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=102-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशुपत्री
आशुपत्री f. (-त्री) A tree which yields frankincense, (Boswellia serrata.)<BR>See शल्लकी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=102-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशुव्रीहि|आशुव्रीहिः
आशुव्रीहि m. (-हिः) Rice ripening in the rainy season.<BR> E. आशु quick, and<BR>व्रीहि rice; that is, of rapid growth; also आशु. So आशुधान्य n. (-न्यं) and<BR>other compounds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=102-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशुशुक्षणि|आशुशुक्षणिः
आशुशुक्षणि m. (-णिः)<BR>	 1. Fire.<BR>	 2. Wind, air.<BR> E. आशु before शुष् to dry in<BR>the reiterative form, and अनि Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=102-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशेकुटिन्
आशेकुटिन् m. (-टी) A mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=102-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशौच|आशौचं
आशौच n. (-चं) Impurity.<BR> E. अशुचि impure, अञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=102-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्चर्य्य|आश्चर्य|आश्चर्य्यं
आश्चर्य्य mfn. (-र्य्यः-र्य्या-र्य्यं) Astonishing, wonderful.<BR>	 m. (-र्य्यः) Surprise, as-<BR>tonishment.<BR> E. आङ् before चर् to go, deriv. irregular.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=102-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्चर्य्यत्व|आश्चर्यत्व|आश्चर्यत्वं
आश्चर्य्यत्व n. (-त्वं)<BR>	 1. Wonderfulness.<BR>	 2. Wonder, astonishment.<BR> E. आश्चर्य्य<BR>and त्व affix; or with ता, आश्चर्य्यता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=102-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्चोतन
आश्चोतन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Aspersion, sprinkling.<BR>	 2. Applying ghee, &c. to the<BR>eyelids.<BR> E. आङ् before श्चुत् to sprinkle, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=102-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्म|आश्मः
आश्म mfn. (-श्मः-श्मा-श्मं) Stony, made of stone, &c.<BR> E. अश्मन् stone, and<BR>अण् affix: with the final rejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=102-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्मन|आश्मनः
आश्मन mfn. (-नः-नी-नं) Made of stone, stony, stone.<BR> E. अश्मन् and अञ् aff.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=102-b" target="_blank">Page102-b+ 60</a>]<BR>m. (-नः) A name of ARUṆA, the charioteer of the sun.<BR> E. अश्मन्<BR>stone, अण् affix: immoveable as a stone, having no legs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=102-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्मिक
आश्मिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Made of stone, consisting of stone, &c.<BR> E. अश्मन्<BR>and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=102-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्यान
आश्यान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Dried partially, consolidated, coagulated.<BR> E. आङ्<BR>dimin. श्यान dry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=102-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्रम|आश्रमं|आश्रमः
आश्रम m. (-मः)<BR>	 1. A religious order, of which there are four kinds re-<BR>ferable to the different periods of life; 1st, that of the student or<BR>Brahmachari; 2d, that of the householder or Grihastha; 3d, that<BR>of the anchorite or Vanaprastha; and 4th, that of the beggar or<BR>Bhikshu; see ब्रह्मचारी, &c.<BR>	 2. A college, a school.<BR>	 3. A hermitage,<BR>the abode of retired saints or sages.<BR>	 4. A wood or thicket.<BR> E. आङ्<BR>before श्रम to perform religious austerities, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=102-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्रमगुरु|आश्रमगुरुः
आश्रमगुरु m. (-रुः) The head of a religious order, a preceptor, a principal.<BR>E. आश्रम a convent, and गुरु senior.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=102-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्रमधर्म्म|आश्रमधर्म|आश्रमधर्मः
आश्रमधर्म्म m. (-र्म्मः) The special duty or duties of each order of life. E.<BR>आश्रम and धर्म्म duty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=102-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्रमिक|आश्रमिकः
आश्रमिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Belonging to one of the four orders, see आश्रम.<BR>E. आश्रम as above, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=102-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्रमिन्
आश्रमिन् mfn. (-मी-मिणी-मि)<BR>	 1. Belonging to one of the four orders.<BR>	 2.<BR>Belonging to a hermitage, a hermit, an anchorite, &c.<BR> E. आश्रम and<BR>इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=102-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्रय|आश्रयः
आश्रय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. Being inclined or addicted to following, practising.<BR>	 2.<BR>A recipient, the person or thing in which any quality or article<BR>is inherent, retained or received.<BR>	 3. An asylum, a place of refuge.<BR>4. A patron, a protector.<BR>	 5. Having recourse to a protector or<BR>asylum.<BR>	 6. A dwelling.<BR>	 7. Contiguity, vicinity.<BR>	 8. Source, origin.<BR>9. A plea, an excuse.<BR>	 10. Appropriate act, one consistent with the<BR>character of the agent.<BR> E. आङ् before श्रि to serve, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=102-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्रयण
आश्रयण n. (-णं) Refuge, asylum, means of protection or security.<BR> E. आङ्<BR>before श्रि to serve, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=102-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्रयणीय
आश्रयणीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>	 1. To be had recourse to.<BR>	 2. To be practised or<BR>followed.<BR> E. आङ् before श्रि to serve, affix अनीयर्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=102-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्रयभूत
आश्रयभूत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Protecting, supporting, one who is the refuge<BR>of any other.<BR> E. आश्रय and भूत become.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=102-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्रयाश|आश्रयाशः
आश्रयाश mfn. (-शः-शा-शं) A forfeiter of an asylum, one who by misconduct<BR>&c loses patronage or protection.<BR>	 m. (-शः) A name of fire.<BR> E. आश्रय<BR>a house, &c. अश् to eat or consume, and अण् affix: similar com-<BR>pounds occur frequently, as आश्रयध्वंसिन्, आश्रयभज्, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=102-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्रव|आश्रवं|आश्रवः
आश्रव mfn. (-वः-वा-वं) Compliant, obedient.<BR>	 m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. A promise, an<BR>engagement.<BR>	 2. Distress, fatigue.<BR>	 3. Fault, transgression.<BR> E. आङ्<BR>before श्रु to hear, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=102-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्रि|आश्रिः
आश्रि f. (-श्रिः) The edge of a sword: see अश्रि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=102-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्रित|आश्रितः
आश्रित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Inhabiting, dwelling in, resorting to as a re-<BR>treat or asylum.<BR>	 2. Following, practising, observing.<BR>	 3. Using,<BR>employing, having recourse to.<BR>	 4. Receiving anything, as an in-<BR>herent or integral part.<BR>	 5. Taking one's station at or on, as at win-<BR>dow or a seat, &c.<BR>	 6. A dependent.<BR> E. आङ् before श्रि to serve, क्त<BR>affix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=102-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्रित्य
आश्रित्य ind.<BR>	 1. Having sought or obtained an asylum.<BR>	 2. Having re-<BR>course to, employing, practising.<BR> E. आङ् before श्रि to serve, ल्यप्<BR>affix, तुक् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=102-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्रुत|आश्रुतः
आश्रुत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Promised, agreed.<BR>	 2. Heard.<BR> E. आङ् before श्रु to hear, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=102-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्लिष्ट
आश्लिष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>	 1. Embraced.<BR>	 2. Embracing, who or what em-<BR>braces.<BR>	 3. Connected, interwoven, blended.<BR>	 4. Attaching to, joining,<BR>who or what adheres to.<BR>	 5. Invested, spread.<BR>	 6. Connected as a<BR>consequence, deduced, concluded.<BR> E. आङ् before श्लिष् to fold. क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=102-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्लेष|आश्लेषः
आश्लेष m. (-षः)<BR>	 1. Embracing, an embrace.<BR>	 2. Site of any act.<BR>	 3. Intimate<BR>connexion.<BR> E. आङ् before श्लिष् to fold, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=102-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्व|आश्वं
आश्व mfn. (-श्वः-श्वी-श्वं) Relating to a horse, drawn by horses, equestrian,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=103-a" target="_blank">Page103-a+ 60</a>]<BR>&c.<BR>	 n. (-श्वं)<BR>	 1. A number of horses.<BR>	 2. A chariot drawn by horses. E.<BR>अश्व a horse, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=102-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्वत्थ|आश्वत्थं
आश्वत्थ m. (-त्थः) The fruit of the holy fig tree.<BR> E. अश्वत्थ and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=103-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्वत्थिक
आश्वत्थिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Relating to or produced by the Aswattha<BR>tree.<BR>	 2. Flowering of the Aswattha (the time when.)<BR> E. अश्वत्थ and<BR>ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=103-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्वयुज|आश्वयुजः
आश्वयुज mfn. (-जः-जी-जं) Belonging to or occurring in the same month<BR>of Aswin.<BR>	 m. (-जः) The month Aswin, (September-October.)<BR>	 f. (-जी)<BR>The day of full moon in Aswin.<BR> E. अश्वयुज the first lunar mansion,<BR>affix अण् and fem. ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=103-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्वरथ
आश्वरथ mfn. (-थः-थी-थं) Belonging to a chariot.<BR> E. अश्वरथ and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=103-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्वलक्षणिक|आश्वलक्षणिकः
आश्वलक्षणिक m. (-कः) A farrier, a groom.<BR> E. अश्व, लक्षण a mark, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=103-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्वलायन|आश्वलायनः
आश्वलायन m. (-नः) The name of a sage and legislator, &c.<BR> E. अश्वलायन<BR>and अण् patronymic aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=103-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्वसत्
आश्वसत् mfn. (-सन्-सन्ती-सत्)<BR>	 1. Breathing, alive.<BR>	 2. Recovering, reviving.<BR>E. आङ् before श्वस् to breathe, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=103-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्वसित
आश्वसित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Encouraged, cheered, consoled.<BR> E. आङ् be-<BR>fore श्वस् to breathe, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=103-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्वास|आश्वासः
आश्वास m. (-सः)<BR>	 1. Completion, cessation.<BR>	 2. A chapter or section, the<BR>division of a book.<BR>	 3. A probable story.<BR>	 4. Breathing.<BR> E. आङ् be-<BR>fore श्वस् to breathe, to live, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=103-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्वासक|आश्वासकः
आश्वासक m. (-कः) Clothing.<BR>	 mfn. (-कः-सिका-कं) Consoling, comforting.<BR>E. आङ् before श्वस् to breathe, causal form, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=103-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्वासन|आश्वासनं
आश्वासन n. (-नं) Consoling, encouraging, reviving.<BR> E. आङ् before श्वस् to<BR>breathe, causal form, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=103-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्वासित
आश्वासित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Encouraged, comforted.<BR> E. आङ् before श्वस् to<BR>breathe, causal form, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=103-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्वास्य
आश्वास्य ind. Having recovered or revived.<BR> E. आङ् before श्वस् to breathe, causal form, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=103-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्विक|आश्विकः
आश्विक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Equestrian, cavalier, relating to a horse, drawn<BR>by horses, &c.<BR> E. अश्व and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=103-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्विन|आश्विनः
आश्विन m. (-नः) The month Aswin, (September-October.)<BR> E. अश्विनी the<BR>constellation, अण् deriv. affix: when the moon is in Aswini.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=103-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्वीन|आश्वीनं|आश्वीनः
आश्वीन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) A day's journey for a horse.<BR> E. अश्व a horse, and<BR>खञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=103-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्विनेय|आश्विनेयः
आश्विनेय m. du. (-यौ) The two twin sons of AŚVINĪ by SŪRYA, and<BR>physicians of Svarga; one of them is named NĀSATYA, the other<BR>DASRA. or the patronymic may be used in the singular to designate<BR>either one of them.<BR> E. अश्विनी and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=103-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्वीय|आश्वीयं
आश्वीय n. (-यं) A number of horses.<BR> E. अश्व a horse, and छ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=103-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आषाढ|आषाढः
आषाढ m. (-ढः)<BR>	 1. The name of a month, (June-July.)<BR>	 2. A staff of the<BR>wood of the Palasa, carried by an ascetic in the month Ashaḍha.<BR>3. The Malaya mountain.<BR> E. आषाढा the constellation, and अण् affix.<BR>f. (-ढी) The day of full moon in the month Ashaḍha.<BR>	 f. (-ढा) The<BR>twenty-first and twenty-second lunar mansion; it is most commonly<BR>compounded with पूर्व्व and उत्तरः see पूर्व्वाषाढा and उत्तराषाढा.<BR> E. अ<BR>neg. सह to bear, अण् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=103-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आषाढक|आषाढकः
आषाढक m. (-कः) The month Ashaḍha: see the preceding, also अषाढक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=103-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आषाढभव|आषाढभवः
आषाढभव mfn. (-वः-वा-वं) Produced in the month Ashaḍha.<BR>	 m. (-वः) The<BR>planet MARS.<BR> E. आषाढ the month, and भव produced, from भू and अच्<BR>aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=103-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आषाढाभू
आषाढाभू m. (-भूः) See the preceding.<BR> E. आषाढा the sign, and भू produced,<BR>from भू to be, affix क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=103-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आष्ट्र|आष्ट्रं
आष्ट्र n. (-ष्ट्रं) Æther, the sky or atmosphere.<BR> E. अस् to throw, to send, ष्ट्रन् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=103-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस|आसः
आस r. 2d cl. (आस्ते or आस्स्ते)<BR>	 1. To sit.<BR>	 2. To be present.<BR>	 3. To be or<BR>exist. With अधि prefixed.<BR>	 1. To inhabit, to dwell in.<BR>	 2. To sit over<BR>or upon.<BR>	 3. To mistake or err by taking one thing for another from<BR>similarity of appearance. With अभि, to sit or apply to, to study, to<BR>learn. With उत्, 1. To leave, to abandon.<BR>	 2. To shake, agitate, &c.<BR>(as wind.) With उप, to worship, to do homage. With निर्, to<BR>expel. With प्र and निर्, to reject, to refute, to invalidate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=103-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्
आस् ind. (-आः) An interjection, ah! oh! &c. implying.<BR>	 1. Recollection.<BR>2. Anger.<BR>	 3. Menace.<BR>	 4. Pain.<BR>	 5. Affliction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=103-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस|आसः
आस m. (-सः) A bow.<BR> E. अस् to send or throw, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=103-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसक्त|आसक्तं|आसक्तः
आसक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>	 1. Zealously following or pursuing, intent or<BR>attached strongly to.<BR>	 2. Trusting to, confiding in.<BR>	 3. Eternal. adv.<BR>n. (-क्तं) Eternally.<BR> E. आङ् before षञ्ज् to embrace, to move, parti-<BR>cipial affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=103-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसक्तचित्त
आसक्तचित्त mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं) Of a fixed mind, intent on, devoted to,<BR>absorbed in.<BR> E. आसक्त and चित्त mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=103-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसक्तचेतस्
आसक्तचेतस् mfn. (-ताः-ताः-तः) Having the mind fixed or intent on any<BR>object.<BR> E. आसक्त and चेतस् the understanding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=103-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसक्तमनस्
आसक्तमनस् mfn. (-नाः-नाः-नः) Having the mind fixed upon any object. E.<BR>आसक्त and मनस् the mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=103-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसक्ति|आसक्तिः
आसक्ति f. (-क्तिः) Attachment to one object or pursuit, diligence, applica-<BR>tion.<BR> E. आङ् before षञ्ज् to embrace, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=103-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसङ्ग|आसंग|आसङ्गं|आसङ्गः
आसङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>	 1. Attachment to any object.<BR>	 2. Association, connexion.<BR>3. Proximity, contact. adv.<BR>	 n. (-ङ्गं) Eternally. adj.<BR>	 mfn. (-ङ्गः-ङ्गा-ङ्गं)<BR>Eternal.<BR> E. आङ् always, षञ्ज् to move, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=103-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसङ्गत्य|आसंगत्य|आसंगत्यं
आसङ्गत्य n. (-त्यं) Detachment, disunion.<BR> E. अ neg. सङ्गति union, ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=103-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसङ्गिनी|आसंगिनी
आसङ्गिनी f. (-नी) A whirlwind.<BR> E. आसङ्ग eternal, इनि and ङीप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=103-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसज्जन
आसज्जन n. (-नं) Putting on dress, armour, ornaments, &c.<BR> E. आङ् be-<BR>fore षज्ज् to dress, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=103-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसज्ज्य
आसज्ज्य ind. Having put on.<BR> E. आङ् before षज्ज् to dress, affix ल्यप्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=103-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसत्ति|आसत्तिः
आसत्ति f. (-त्तिः)<BR>	 1. Intimate union, meeting, junction.<BR>	 2. Gain, profit,<BR>acquirement.<BR>	 3. In logic, connexion or relation between two or<BR>more proximate terms and the sense they convey.<BR> E. आङ् before<BR>षद् to go, affix क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=103-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसन|आसनं|आसनः
आसन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. A stool, a seat.<BR>	 2. Maintaining a post against an<BR>enemy.<BR>	 3. The withers of an elephant, the part where the driver<BR>sits.<BR>	 4. Halting, stopping.<BR>	 5. Sitting in some peculiar posture,<BR>as is the custom of devotees, &c. eighty-four kinds are enumerated:<BR>see पद्मासन, &c.<BR>	 m. (-नः) A tree, (Pentapheca tomentosa.) Also<BR>असन.<BR>	 f. (-ना-नी) Stay, abiding, sitting. (-नी)<BR>	 1. A shop, a stall.<BR>2. A small seat, a stool.<BR> E. आस् to abide, and युच or ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=103-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसन्द|आसंदः|आसन्दः
आसन्द m. (-न्दः) A name of VIṢṆU.<BR>	 mfn. (-न्दः-न्दी-न्दं) A small couch or<BR>oblong chair, having the seat made of basket work.<BR> E. आस sitting,<BR>and द what gives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=103-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसन्न|आसन्नः
आसन्न mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं) Near, proximate.<BR>	 m. (-न्नः) A setting sun.<BR> E. आङ<BR>before षद् to go, and क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=103-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसन्नकाल|आसन्नकालः
आसन्नकाल m. (-लः) Hour of death.<BR> E. आसन्न and काल time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=103-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसव|आसवः
आसव n. (-वं)<BR>	 1. Rum, spirit distilled from sugar or molasses.<BR>	 2. Spi-<BR>rituous liquor in general.<BR> E. आङ् before षूञ् to be generated, and<BR>अप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=103-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसवद्रु|आसवद्रुः
आसवद्रु m. (-द्रुः) The palmyra tree.<BR> E. आसव spirit, and द्रु a tree; the<BR>juice of the palmyra upon fermenting affording a spirituous<BR>liquor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=103-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसादन|आसादनं
आसादन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Obtaining, attaining.<BR>	 2. Accomplishing.<BR>	 3. Going<BR>to or toward.<BR> E. आङ् before षद् to go, causal form, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=103-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसादित|आसादितः
आसादित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Obtained.<BR>	 2. Reached, gone to.<BR>	 3. Spread,<BR>extended, overspread.<BR>	 4. Effected, completed.<BR> E. आङ् before षद् to<BR>go, in the causal form, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=103-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसाद्य
आसाद्य ind.<BR>	 1. Having attained or reached.<BR>	 2. Having obtained.<BR> E. आङ्<BR>before षद् to go, causal form, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=103-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसाधन|आसाधनं
आसाधन n. (-नं) Accomplishment, attainment.<BR> E. आङ् before षाध् to<BR>succeed, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=103-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसार|आसारः
आसार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A hard shower.<BR>	 2. Surrounding an enemy.<BR>	 3. The<BR>army of an ally, or of a king whose dominions are separated by<BR>other intervening states.<BR> E. आङ् before सृ to go, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=103-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसाव्य
आसाव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं) To be born.<BR> E. षु to bear, affix ण्यत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=103-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसिक|आसिकः
आसिक m. (-कः) A swordsman.<BR> E. असि a sword, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=103-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसिक|आसिकः
आसिक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) One who sits.<BR> E. आस् to sit, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=104-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसिक्त
आसिक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं) Sprinkled.<BR> E. आङ् before षिच् to sprinkle, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=104-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसित
आसित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Sat down.<BR>	 2. Who sits or is seated.<BR>	 n. (-तं)<BR>1. Place of abode, a city.<BR>	 2. A seat.<BR> E. आस् to sit, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=104-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसिद्ध
आसिद्ध mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>	 1. Accomplished, effected.<BR>	 2. Put under<BR>restraint: see आसेध.<BR> E. आङ् before षिध् to go, &c. affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=104-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसीन|आसीनः
आसीन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Sitting, seated.<BR> E. आस् to sit, शानच् affix, form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=104-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसीनप्रचलायित|आसीनप्रचलायितं
आसीनप्रचलायित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Nodding, rocking as seated, falling asleep.<BR>E. आसीन and प्रचलायित set in motion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=104-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसुति|आसुतिः
आसुति m. (-तिः) Distilling, distillation.<BR> E. आङ before षूञ. to produce, affix क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=104-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसुतीबल
आसुतीबल m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. A sacrificer at the full and change of the moon.<BR>2. A distiller.<BR> E. आसुति and बलच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=104-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसुर|आसुरं|आसुरः
आसुर mfn. (-रः-री-रं) Infernal, demoniac, belonging or relating to the<BR>Asuras.<BR>	 m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. An Asura or demon.<BR>	 2. A form of marriage, in<BR>which the bridegroom gives to the bride, her father and paternal<BR>kinsmen, as much as he can afford.<BR>	 n. (-रं) Black salt.<BR>	 f. (-री)<BR>	 1. A<BR>division of medicine, surgery, curing by cutting with instruments,<BR>applying the actual cautery, &c.<BR>	 2. Mustard.<BR> E. असुर a demon, अण्<BR>aff. and in the fem. ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=104-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसेक|आसेकः
आसेक m. (-कः) Sprinkling.<BR> E. आङ् before षिच् to sprinkle, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=104-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसेचन|आसेचनः
आसेचन n. (-नं) Sprinkling.<BR>	 mfn. (-नः-नी-नं) Beloved, desired.<BR> E. आङ्<BR>before षिच् to sprinkle, ल्युट् affix; also असेचनक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=104-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसेचनक|आसेचनकः
आसेचनक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) See the preceding.<BR> E. आङ् before षिच् to<BR>sprinkle, ल्युट् and कन् affs. also असेचनक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=104-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसेद्धृ
आसेद्धृ m. (-द्धा) One who confines or arrests another.<BR> E. आङ् before षिध्<BR>to go, and तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=104-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसेध|आसेधः
आसेध m. (-धः) Arrest, legal restraint of four kinds; कालासेधः limit of<BR>time, स्थानासेधः confinement to a place, प्रवासासेधः prohibition<BR>against removal or departure, कर्म्मासेधः restriction from employment.<BR>E. आङ् before षिध् to go, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=104-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसेध्य
आसेध्य mfn. (-ध्यः-ध्या-ध्यं) To be interrupted, prohibited or restrained. E.<BR>आङ् before षिध् to go, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=104-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्कन्दन|आस्कंदनं|आस्कन्दनं
आस्कन्दन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Going, going to, approaching.<BR>	 2. Effacing, de-<BR>stroying.<BR>	 3. Reproach, abuse.<BR>	 4. War, battle.<BR>	 5. Drying.<BR> E. आङ्<BR>before स्कन्द to go, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=104-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्कन्दित|आस्कंदितं|आस्कन्दितं
आस्कन्दित n. (-तं) The walk of a horse.<BR> E. आङ् before स्कन्द to go, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=104-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्कन्दितक|आस्कंदितकं|आस्कन्दितकं
आस्कन्दितक n. (-कं) See the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=104-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्तर|आस्तरः
आस्तर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A covering, a coverlet, a blanket thrown over the<BR>back of a horse or elephant.<BR>	 2. Spreading clothes, &c.<BR>	 3. A car-<BR>pet, a bed.<BR> E. आङ् before स्तृञ् to spread, and अप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=104-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्तरण|आस्तरणं
आस्तरण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. A carpet, a rug, a quilt, bed-clothes.<BR>	 2. A bed.<BR>	 3. A<BR>layer of sacred grass spread out at a sacrifice.<BR>	 4. An elephant's<BR>housings, a painted cloth or blanket worn on his back. E. As the<BR>preceding, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=104-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्तिक|आस्तिकः
आस्तिक m. (-कः) The name of a Muni or saint.<BR> E. अस्ति who is and वुञ्<BR>affix; from an expression of his father, (he is in the womb,) pro-<BR>nouncing his conception to have taken place before there were any<BR>external indications of it.<BR>	 mfn. (-कः-की-कं) A believer, pious, faith-<BR>ful.<BR> E. अस्ति as before, saying that there is a God, &c. in opposition<BR>to the नास्तिक an atheist, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=104-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्तिकता
आस्तिकता f. (-ता) Belief in God.<BR> E. आस्तिक and तल् affix; also with<BR>त्व affix आस्तिकत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=104-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्तिकार्थद|आस्तिकार्थदः
आस्तिकार्थद m. (-दः) A name of a king, also called JANAMEJAYA.<BR>E. आस्तिक the Muni, अर्थ a request, and द who gives or grants;<BR>having at his request spared the Naga TAKSHAKA, from the<BR>destruction to which he had devoted the race.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=104-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्तीक|आस्तीकः
आस्तीक m. (-कः) The name of a Muni or saint, the son of JARATKĀRU,<BR>also a Muni: see आस्तिक.<BR> E. अस्ति and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=104-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्तीकजननी
आस्तीकजननी f. (-नी) The wife of JARATKĀRU, a saint.<BR> E. आस्तीक as<BR>above, and जननी a mother, the mother of that saint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=104-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्तीक्य
आस्तीक्य n. (-क्यं) Belief in Providence and a future world.<BR> E. आस्तीक a<BR>believer, and यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=104-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्तीर्ण|आस्तीर्ण्ण
आस्तीर्ण mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-र्णं) Spread, strewed, scattered.<BR> E. आङ् before स्तृ to<BR>spread, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=104-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्तृत
आस्तृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Spread.<BR>	 2. Covered.<BR> E. आङ् before स्तृ to spread, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=104-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्था
आस्था f. (-स्था)<BR>	 1. Prop, stay, place or means of abiding.<BR>	 2. An assembly.<BR>3. Effort, pains, care.<BR>	 4. Consideration, regard.<BR> E. आङ् before स्था<BR>to stay, to stand, अङ् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=104-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्थान|आस्थानं
आस्थान nf. (-नं-नी) An assembly.<BR>	 n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Place, site.<BR>	 2. Staying, abid-<BR>ing.<BR>	 5. Pains, care.<BR> E. आङ् before स्था to stay or stand, ल्युट् and<BR>ङीप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=104-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्थापन|आस्थापनं
आस्थापन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Placing, fixing, causing to stay or remain.<BR>	 2. An<BR>enema of oil, ghee, &c.<BR> E. आङ् before स्था to stay, causal form. ल्युट्<BR>aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=104-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्थित
आस्थित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Stayed, dwelt, abiding, abode.<BR>	 2. Applied to,<BR>having recourse to.<BR>	 3. Occupied, engrossed by, engaged in.<BR>	 4.<BR>Spread, overspread.<BR>	 5. Obtained.<BR>	 6. Observing, adhering to, follow-<BR>ing, practising.<BR> E. आङ् before स्था to stay, and क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=104-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्पद|आस्पदं
आस्पद n. (-दं)<BR>	 1. Business, affair.<BR>	 2. Office, rank, station.<BR>	 3. Dignity.<BR>	 4.<BR>Authority.<BR>	 5. Place, site.<BR> E. आङ् before पद् to go, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=104-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्पन्दन|आस्पन्दनं
आस्पन्दन n. (-नं) Trembling, throbbing.<BR> E. आङ् before स्पदि to shake, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=104-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्पर्द्धा
आस्पर्द्धा f. (-र्द्धा) Emulation, rivalry.<BR> E. आङ् before स्पर्द्ध to vie with, अच्<BR>and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=104-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्पर्द्धिन्
आस्पर्द्धिन् mfn. (-र्द्धी-र्द्धिनी-र्द्धि) Emulous.<BR> E. आस्पर्द्धा and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=104-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्फाल|आस्फालः
आस्फाल m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. Striking, rubbing, causing to move gently.<BR>	 2. Flap-<BR>ping, clapping.<BR>	 3. The flapping motion of an elephant's ear.<BR> E. आङ्<BR>before स्फल to move, causal form, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=104-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्फालन|आस्फालनं
आस्फालन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Pride, arrogance.<BR>	 2. Rubbing, stirring, moving<BR>gently.<BR> E. आङ् before स्फल to move, causal form, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=104-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्फालित
आस्फालित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Struck gently, rubbed, touched, stirred.<BR>	 2.<BR>Flapped, clapped, struck together.<BR> E. आङ् before स्फल to move,<BR>causal form, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=104-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्फुजित्
आस्फुजित् m. (-जित्) A name of a SUKRA, regent of the planet VENUS,<BR>and teacher of the Asuras.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=104-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्फोट|आस्फोटः
आस्फोट m. (-टः)<BR>	 1. A plant, (Swallow wort.)<BR>	 2. The sound of striking<BR>on the arms, as made by combatants, wrestlers, &c.<BR>	 f. (-टा) A wild<BR>variety of jasmine.<BR> E. आङ् before स्फुट to expand, and अच् affix; also<BR>आस्फोन and आस्फोता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=104-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्फोटक|आस्फोटकः
आस्फोटक m. (-कः) A tree, (Careya arborea.)<BR> E. आङ् before स्फुट् to blow,<BR>&c. and वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=104-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्फोटन|आस्फोटनं
आस्फोटन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Blowing, expanding.<BR>	 2. Contracting, closing.<BR>	 3.<BR>Slapping the arms, or the noise made by it.<BR>	 f. (-नी) A gimlet or<BR>auger.<BR> E. आङ् before स्फुट् to blow or expand, and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=104-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्फोत|आस्फोतः
आस्फोत m. (-तः)<BR>	 1. Swallow wort, (Asclepias gigantea.)<BR>	 2. Mountain<BR>ebony, (Bauhinia variegata, &c.)<BR>	 3. A kind of echites or savanna<BR>flower, (E. dichotoma, Rox.)<BR>	 f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. A wild variety of jasmine.<BR>	 2.<BR>Clitoria ternatea.<BR> E. आङ् before स्फुट् to blow or expand, अच् affix<BR>and ट changed to त; or स्फै to increase, with क्त affix, and आ con-<BR>verted to ओ; also sometimes आस्फोट and आस्फोटा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=104-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्य|आस्यं
आस्य n. (-स्यं)<BR>	 1. the face.<BR>	 2. The mouth.<BR>	 mfn. (-स्यः-स्या-स्यं) Belonging or<BR>relating to the mouth or face.<BR> E. अस् to throw or direct, and ण्यत्<BR>affix, or आङ् before स्यन्द to go, and ड affix; to which food goes or<BR>is directed.<BR>	 f. (-स्या) Stay, abiding, resting.<BR> E. आस् to sit, and ण्यत्<BR>affix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=104-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्यपत्र|आस्यपत्रं
आस्यपत्र n. (-त्रं) A lotus.<BR> E. आस्य a face, पत्र a leaf; this flower is com-<BR>monly compared to a beautiful face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=104-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्यलाङ्गल|आस्यलांगल|आस्यलाङ्गलः
आस्यलाङ्गल m. (-लः) A hog, a boar.<BR> E. आस्य and लाङ्गल a plough; whose<BR>face is as it were a plough.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=104-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्यलोमन्
आस्यलोमन् n. (-म) The beard.<BR> E. आस्य and लोमन् hair; the hair of the<BR>face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=104-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्यासव|आस्यासवः
आस्यासव m. (-वः) Spittle, saliva.<BR> E. अस्य the mouth, आसव liquor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=105-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्रप|आस्रपः
आस्रप m. (-पः) The nineteenth lunar mansion.<BR> E. अस्रप a Rākṣasa or<BR>goblin, and अण् aff. one of this race being the deity of the asterism.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=105-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्रव|आस्रवः
आस्रव m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. Distress, pain, affliction.<BR>	 2. Flow, issue, running, discharge.<BR>E. आङ् before स्रु to go, and अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=105-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्राव|आस्रावः
आस्राव m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. Pain, affliction.<BR>	 2. Flow, issue, running, discharge.<BR>E. आङ् before स्रु to ooze, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=105-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्वनित
आस्वनित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Sounded.<BR> E. आङ् before स्वन् to sound, क्त affix,<BR>with इट् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=105-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्वान्त
आस्वान्त mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं) Sounded.<BR> E. आङ् before स्वन् to sound, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=105-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्वाद|आस्वादः
आस्वाद m. (-दः)<BR>	 1. Tasting, eating.<BR>	 2. Enjoying.<BR>	 3. Flavour.<BR> E. आङ् be-<BR>fore ष्वद् to taste, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=105-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्वादन|आस्वादनं
आस्वादन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Tasting, eating.<BR>	 2. Enjoying.<BR> E. आङ् before ष्वद् to taste, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=105-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्वादित
आस्वादित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Tasted.<BR>	 2. Enjoyed, possessed.<BR>	 3. Eaten. E.<BR>आङ् before ष्वद् to taste, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=105-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आह
आह ind. An interjection, aha! ah! implying.<BR>	 1. Casting, sending.<BR>	 2.<BR>Severity, reproof.<BR>	 3. Commanding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=105-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहक|आहकः
आहक m. (-कः) A disease of the nose, inflammation of the Schneideri-<BR>an membrane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=105-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहत|आहतं|आहतः
आहत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Struck, beaten.<BR>	 2. Injured, killed.<BR>	 3. Multiplied.<BR>4. Known, understood.<BR>	 5. Uttered falsely.<BR>	 n. (-तं)<BR>	 1. Old cloth or<BR>raiment.<BR>	 2. New cloth or clothes.<BR>	 3. Assertion of an impossibility.<BR>m. (-तः) A drum.<BR> E. आङ्, before हन् to hurt or injure, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=105-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहतलक्षण|आहतलक्षणः
आहतलक्षण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Noted for good qualities.<BR> E. आहत known,<BR>and लक्षण a mark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=105-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहर|आहरः
आहर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Breath inspired, inspiration.<BR>	 2. Taking, seizing. E.<BR>आङ् before हृ to take, अप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=105-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहरण|आहरणं
आहरण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Taking, seizing.<BR>	 2. Causing, inducing.<BR>	 3. Extracting,<BR>removing.<BR> E. आङ् before हृ to take, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=105-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहर्त्तृ|आहर्तृ
आहर्त्तृ mfn. (-र्त्ता-र्त्त्री-र्त्तृ) One who takes or seizes.<BR>	 m. (-र्त्ता) (In law,) A<BR>copy-holder.<BR> E. आङ् before हृ to take, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=105-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहव|आहवः
आहव m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. War, battle.<BR>	 2. Sacrificing.<BR> E. आङ् before हु to sacrifice<BR>or ह्वेञ् to call, and अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=105-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहवन|आहवनं
आहवन n. (-नं) Sacrifice, offering sacrifice<BR> E. आङ् before हु to sacrifice, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=105-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहवनीय|आहवनीयः
आहवनीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) To be offered as an oblation.<BR>	 m. (-यः) A con-<BR>secrated fire taken from the house-holder's perpetual fire, and<BR>prepared for receiving oblations.<BR> E. आङ् before हु to offer abla-<BR>tions, and अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=105-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहवनीयक|आहवनीयकः
आहवनीयक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Fit for a burnt offering.<BR>	 m. (-कः) A con-<BR>secrated fire.<BR> E. कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=105-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहार|आहारः
आहार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Food.<BR>	 2. Taking, conveying.<BR> E. आङ् before हृ to convey, घञ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=105-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहारसम्भव|आहारसंभव|आहारसंभवः|आहारसम्भवः
आहारसम्भव m. (-वः) The juice of the body, chyle, lymph, serum, &c. E.<BR>आहार food, and सम्भव what is produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=105-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहारार्थिन्
आहारार्थिन् mfn. (-र्थी-र्थिनी-र्थि) Begging or seeking for food.<BR> E. आहार food<BR>and अर्थिन् who asks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=105-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहार्य्य|आहार्य|आहार्यः|आहार्य्यं|आहार्य्यः
आहार्य्य mfn. (-र्य्यः-र्य्या-र्य्यं)<BR>	 1. Adventitious, accessory, incidental.<BR>	 2. To<BR>be taken or seized.<BR>	 3. To be eaten.<BR>	 m. (-र्य्यः) The ornamentative<BR>part of the drama, the dress, decorations, &c.<BR> E. आङ् before हृञ्<BR>to convey, ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=105-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहार्य्यशोभा|आहार्यशोभा
आहार्य्यशोभा f. (-भा) Adventitious beauty, beauty not natural but the<BR>effect of paint, ornaments, &c.<BR> E. आहार्य्य incidental, and शोभा<BR>splendor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=105-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहाव|आहावः
आहाव m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. A trough near a well for watering cattle.<BR>	 2. War,<BR>battle.<BR>	 3. Calling.<BR> E. आङ् before ह्वे to call, घञ् affix, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=105-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहिक|आहिकः
आहिक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A name of the inspired grammarian PĀṆINI.<BR>	 2.<BR>The descending node.<BR> E. अहि a snake, or the constellation Aslesha,<BR>and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=105-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहिण्डिक|आहिंडिकः|आहिण्डिकः
आहिण्डिक m. (-कः) A man of fixed origin, the son of a Nishada father<BR>and Vaidehī mother, employed as a watchman on the outside of<BR>jails, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=105-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहित|आहितः
आहित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Placed, deposited.<BR>	 2. Entertained, felt.<BR>	 3.<BR>Comprising, containing.<BR>	 4. Made, done.<BR> E. आङ् before धा to have<BR>or hold, part. affix क्त, form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=105-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहितलक्षण|आहितलक्षणः
आहितलक्षण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Noted for good qualities. E. See आहतलक्षण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=105-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहितव्यथ
आहितव्यथ mfn. (-थः-था-थं) Pained, grieved.<BR> E. आहित felt, व्यथा pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=105-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहितस्वन
आहितस्वन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Noisy, uttering or making sound.<BR> E. आहित<BR>made, स्वन a sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=105-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहिताङ्क|आहितांक
आहिताङ्क mfn. (-ङ्कः-ङ्का-ङ्कं) Marked, spotted, stained.<BR> E. आहित made, अङ्क a spot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=105-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहिताग्नि|आहिताग्निः
आहिताग्नि m. (-ग्निः) A Brahman who has preserved a sacred fire kept<BR>alive perpetually in a family, &c.<BR> E. आहित placed, and अग्नि a fire;<BR>by whom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=105-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहितुण्डिक|आहितुंडिकः|आहितुण्डिकः
आहितुण्डिक m. (-कः) A juggler, a snake-catcher.<BR> E. अहि a snake, तुण्ड a<BR>mouth, and ठक् affix; playing with the mouth of a snake: the<BR>poisonous fangs being extracted, the snakes are suffered to bite<BR>their exhibitors.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=105-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहुत|आहुतं
आहुत n. (-तं) The nourishment of all created beings, considered as one<BR>of the five sacraments or principal sacrifices of the Hindus. E.<BR>आङ् before हु to offer oblations, and क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=105-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहुति|आहुतिः
आहुति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Offering oblations with fire to the deities.<BR>	 2. Any<BR>solemn rite accompanied with oblations. E. As the preceding,<BR>affix क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=105-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहुल्य|आहुल्यं
आहुल्य n. (-ल्यं) A leguminous shrub.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=105-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहूत|आहूतं|आहूतः
आहूत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Called, summoned, invoked, invited.<BR> E. आङ be-<BR>fore ह्वे to call, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=105-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहूतप्रपलायिन्
आहूतप्रपलायिन् m. (-यी) A defendant or witness absconding, or not ap-<BR>pearing when summoned.<BR> E. आहूत and प्रपलायिन् who runs away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=105-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहूति|आहूतिः
आहूति f. (-तिः) Calling.<BR> E. आङ् before ह्वे to call, affix क्तिन्; ए is<BR>dropped, and व is changed to its analogous vowel उ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=105-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहृत
आहृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Brought, taken, collected.<BR> E. आङ् before हृ to<BR>take, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=105-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहृत्य
आहृत्य ind. Having taken or received, having brought.<BR> E. आङ् before<BR>हृ to take, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=105-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहेय|आहेयं
आहेय mfn. (-यः-यी-यं) Belonging or relating to a snake.<BR> E. अहि a snake,<BR>and ढञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=105-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहो
आहो ind.<BR>	 1. An interjection of doubt; 2. Of asking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=105-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहोपुरुषिका
आहोपुरुषिका f. (-का) Boasting, military vaunting.<BR> E. आहो, पुरुष a man,<BR>and affix कन्; doubting another's manhood, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=105-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहोस्वित्
आहोस्वित् ind. A particle implying doubt.<BR> E. आहो and स्वित् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=105-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आह्न|आह्नः
आह्न n. (-ह्नं) Many days.<BR> E. अहन् a day, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=105-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आह्निक|आह्निकं
आह्निक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Daily, diurnal, of or belonging to a day.<BR>	 n.<BR>(-कं)<BR>	 1. Constant occupation, daily work.<BR>	 2. The division or section<BR>of a book.<BR>	 3. Food.<BR> E. अहन् a day, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=105-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आह्निकाचार
आह्निकाचार m. (-रः) Daily observance, the prayers and practices neces-<BR>sary for bodily and mental purification.<BR> E. आह्निक daily and आचार<BR>observance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=105-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आह्लाद|आह्लादः
आह्लाद m. (-दः) Joy, delight.<BR> E. आङ् before ह्लद् to be pleased, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=105-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आह्लादित|आह्लादितः
आह्लादित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Delighted, rejoiced.<BR> E. आङ् before ह्लद् to be<BR>delighted, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=105-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आह्व
आह्व m. (-ह्वः) A crier, who or what calls.<BR>	 f. (-ह्वा)<BR>	 1. A name, an ap-<BR>pellation.<BR>	 2. A call, a summons.<BR> E. आङ् before ह्वे to call, क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=105-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आह्वय|आह्वयः
आह्वय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. A name or appellation.<BR>	 2. A lawsuit arising from a<BR>dispute about games with animals, as cock-fighting, &c.<BR> E. आङ्<BR>before ह्वेञ् to call, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=105-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आह्वान|आह्वानं
आह्वान n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Calling, a call or summons.<BR>	 2. Legal summons.<BR>	 3. A<BR>name, an appellation.<BR>	 4. Invocation, invitation.<BR> E. आङ् before ह्वेञ्<BR>to call, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=105-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आह्वानदर्शन
आह्वानदर्शन n. (-नं) Day of trial.<BR> E. आह्वान summons, and दर्शन seeing,<BR>investigating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=105-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आह्वाय|आह्वायः
आह्वाय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. A name.<BR>	 2. A summons.<BR> E. आङ्ह्वे to call, घ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=105-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आह्वायक|आह्वायकः
आह्वायक m. (-कः) A messenger, a courier.<BR> E. आङ्ह्वे to call, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=105-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इ|इः
इ The third vowel of the alphabet, corresponding to I short, and pro-<BR>nounced as that letter in kill, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=106-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इ|इः
इ m. (इः) A name of KĀMADEVA. Ind. An interjection.<BR>	 1. Of anger.<BR>	 2.<BR>Of calling.<BR>	 3. Of sorrow or distress.<BR>	 4. Of compassion.<BR> E. इ to go,<BR>क्विप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=106-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इ|इः
इ r. 1st cl. (अयति) To go, to go to or towards: with उत् prefixed, to<BR>rise or ascend, as the sun, &c. with अभि and उत् the same, or to<BR>rise in the world, to prosper. (ङ) इङ् and अधि always prefixed<BR>अधीङ् r. 2nd cl. (अधीते) To study, to learn, to read over or through.<BR>(क) इक् and अधि prefixed r. 2nd cl. (अध्येति) To remember, to think<BR>of. (ण) इण् r. 2nd cl. (एति) To go. This root takes many prefixes,<BR>implying with अति, 1. To surpass, to surmount.<BR>	 2. To pass, to<BR>spend time or to elapse as time. With अनु, 1. To go after, to<BR>follow.<BR>	 2. To go like, to imitate in going.<BR>	 3. To succeed. With अभि,<BR>1. To obtain, to get.<BR>	 2. To proceed, to go on.<BR>	 3. To go.<BR>	 4. To ap-<BR>proach.<BR>	 5. To serve or worship. With अप, 1. To go away, to depart.<BR>2. To perish. With अभि and उप, To arrive. With उप, 1. To<BR>receive.<BR>	 2. To aid or assist.<BR>	 3. To approach or go near to. With<BR>निर्, To go forth or out from. With प्रति, 1. To trust, to confide.<BR>	 2.<BR>To follow, to be added or subjoined to.<BR>	 3. (In the passive verb,) To<BR>become evident or manifest. With वि, To expend, to waste, to de-<BR>part. With सम् and उप, To obtain, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=106-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इक्कट|इक्कटः
इक्कट m. (-टः) A kind of reed: see इत्कट.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=106-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इक्षव
इक्षव m. (-वः) The sugar-came.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=106-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इक्षु|इक्षुः
इक्षु m. (-क्षुः) The sugar-cane.<BR> E. इष् to desire, and क्सु affix or ईक्ष् to see,<BR>असुन् affix and ई made short.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=106-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इक्षुकाण्ड|इक्षुकाण्डः
इक्षुकाण्ड m. (-ण्डः)<BR>	 1. A species of sugar-cane, (Saccharum munja, Rox.)<BR>See मुञ्ज.<BR>	 2. A sort of grass, (Kas,) (Saccharum spontaneum.)<BR>	 3.<BR>The stem or cane of the Saccharum officinale, the sugar-cane. E.<BR>इक्षु and काण्ड a stem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=106-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इक्षुगन्धा
इक्षुगन्धा f. (-न्धा)<BR>	 1. A kind of reed, (Saccharum spontaneum.)<BR>	 2. Bar-<BR>leria longifolia, (this and its synonyms are also applied to Cap-<BR>paris spinosa and Tribulus lanuginosus: see कोकिलाक्ष and गोक्षुरक.)<BR>3. Convolvulus paniculatus: भूमिकुष्माण्ड.<BR> E. इक्षु and गन्ध smell;<BR>having the odor of the sugar-cane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=106-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इक्षुगन्धिका
इक्षुगन्धिका f. (-का) Convolvulus paniculatus. E. See the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=106-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इक्षुतुल्या
इक्षुतुल्या f. (-ल्या) A species of grass or reed.<BR> E. इक्षु and तुल्या like, like<BR>sugar-cane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=106-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इक्षुदण्ड|इक्षुदण्डः
इक्षुदण्ड n. (-ण्डं) The stem or cane of the Saccharum officinale, the<BR>sugar-cane.<BR> E. इक्षु and दण्ड a staff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=106-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इक्षुदर्भा
इक्षुदर्भा f. (-र्भा) A kind of grass; also वंशमूल, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=106-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इक्षुनेत्र|इक्षुनेत्रं
इक्षुनेत्र n. (-त्रं) A kind of tree.<BR> E. इक्षु and नेत्र an eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=106-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इक्षुपत्र|इक्षुपत्रः
इक्षुपत्र m. (-त्रः) A species of grain, Jower, (Panicum spicatum.)<BR> E. इक्षु<BR>and पत्र a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=106-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इक्षुप्र|इक्षुप्रः
इक्षुप्र m. (-प्रः) A sort of grass, (Saccharum sara.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=106-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इक्षुबालिका
इक्षुबालिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. A kind of reed: see इक्ष्वालिका.<BR>	 2. Saccharum spon-<BR>taneum.<BR> E. इक्षु and बालिका an infant; a young sugar-cane, from<BR>its smaller size.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=106-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इक्षुभक्षिका
इक्षुभक्षिका f. (-का) A meal of sugar or molasses.<BR> E. इक्षु, भक्ष to eat, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=106-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इक्षुमती
इक्षुमती f. (-ती) The name of a river in Bengal.<BR> E. इक्षु and मतुप् aff. in<BR>this sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=106-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इक्षुमूल|इक्षुमूलं
इक्षुमूल n. (-लं)<BR>	 1. A sort of tree; also इक्षुनेत्र.<BR>	 2. The root of sugar-cane.<BR>E. इक्षु and मूल a root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=106-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इक्षुमेह|इक्षुमेहः
इक्षुमेह m. (-हः) Diabetes, or D. mellitus.<BR> E. इक्षु and मेह urine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=106-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इक्षुमेहिन्
इक्षुमेहिन् mfn. (-हि-हिनी-हि) Diabetic.<BR> E. इक्षुमेह and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=106-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इक्षुयन्त्र|इक्षुयंत्र
इक्षुयन्त्र n. (-न्त्रं) A sugar-mill.<BR> E. इक्षु and यन्त्र a machine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=106-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इक्षुयोनि|इक्षुयोनिः
इक्षुयोनि m. (-निः) The common sugar-cane.<BR> E. इक्षु and योनि origin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=106-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इक्षुर|इक्षुरः
इक्षुर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Sugar-cane.<BR>	 2. Barleria longifolia or Tribulus lanugi-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=106-b" target="_blank">Page106-b+ 60</a>]<BR>nosus.<BR>	 3. Saccharum spontaneum.<BR> E. इक्षु sugar-cane and र what<BR>gives, from रा and ड aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=106-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इक्षुरक|इक्षुरकः
इक्षुरक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. Saccharum spontaneum.<BR>	 2. Barleria longifolia:<BR>see the preceding, कन् being added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=106-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इक्षुरस|इक्षुरसः
इक्षुरस m. (-सः)<BR>	 1. The juice of the sugar-cane 2. Molasses, unrefined<BR>sugar.<BR>	 3. A sort of grass, (Saccharum spontaneum.)<BR> E. इक्षु sugar-<BR>cane and रस juice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=106-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इक्षुरसक्वाथ|इक्षुरसक्वाथः
इक्षुरसक्वाथ m. (-थः) Raw or unrefined sugar, molasses.<BR> E. इक्षुरस and क्वाथ<BR>a decoction, the boiled or inspissated juice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=106-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इक्षुरसोद|इक्षुरसोदः
इक्षुरसोद m. (-दः) The sea of syrup.<BR> E. इक्षुरस and उद water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=106-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इक्षुवाटिका
इक्षुवाटिका f. (-का) A kind of sugar-cane, common yellow cane; also<BR>इक्षुवाटी; see पुण्ड्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=106-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इक्षुविकार|इक्षुविकारः
इक्षुविकार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Sugar, molasses.<BR>	 2. Any sweetmeat<BR> E. इक्षु and<BR>विकार change of form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=106-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इक्षुवेष्टन|इक्षुवेष्टनः
इक्षुवेष्टन m. (-नः) A sort of grass, (Saccharum munja.)<BR> E. इक्षु and वेष्टन surrounding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=106-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इक्षुशाकट|इक्षुशाकटं
इक्षुशाकट n. (-टं) A field of sugar-cane.<BR> E. इक्षु and शाकट a field.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=106-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इक्षुशाकिन|इक्षुशाकिनं
इक्षुशाकिन n. (-नं) A field of sugar-cane.<BR> E. इक्षु and शाकिन a field in this<BR>compound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=106-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इक्षुसार|इक्षुसारः
इक्षुसार m. (-रः) Molasses, raw or unrefined sugar.<BR> E. इक्षु and सार es-<BR>sence, the essence of the sugar-cane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=106-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इक्ष्वाकु|इक्ष्वाकुः
इक्ष्वाकु m. (-कुः) The son of the Manu NAIVASWATA, the son of SŪRYA<BR>or the sun, and first prince of the solar dynasty: he reigned at<BR>Ajodhya in the commencement of the second Yuga or age.<BR>	 f.<BR>(-कुः) A bitter gourd.<BR> E. इक्षु and अक to obtain, and कु or उण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=106-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इक्ष्वालिक|इक्ष्वालिकः
इक्ष्वालिक m. (-कः) A kind of reed, (Saccharum spontaneum.)<BR>	 f. (-का)<BR>Another sort, (Saccharum fuscum;) the native pens are made<BR>from its stem.<BR> E. इक्षु and आलिका for आली a line; it grows like the<BR>sugar-cane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=106-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इख
इख r. 1st cl. (एखति) and (इ) इखि (इंखति) To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=106-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इग
इग r. 1st cl. (इ) इगि (इङ्गति) 1. To go, to go to or towards.<BR>	 2. To move or agitate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=106-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इङ्ग|इंग|इङ्गं|इङ्गः
इङ्ग mfn. (-ङ्गः-ङ्गा-ङ्गं)<BR>	 1. Moveable, locomotive.<BR>	 2. Surprising, wonder-<BR>ful.<BR>	 m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>	 1. A hint or sign, an indication of sentiment by<BR>gesture, &c.<BR>	 2. Knowledge.<BR> E. इगि to go, affix क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=106-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इङ्गित|इंगित|इङ्गितं
इङ्गित n. (-तं)<BR>	 1. Hint, sign, gesture.<BR>	 2. Going, motion.<BR>	 3. Intention,<BR>purpose.<BR> E. इगि to go, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=106-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इङ्गितज्ञ|इंगितज्ञ
इङ्गितज्ञ mfn. (-ज्ञः-ज्ञा-ज्ञं) Understanding signs.<BR> E. इङ्गित and ज्ञ who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=106-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इङ्गुद|इंगुद|इंगुदः|इङ्गुदः
इङ्गुद mf. (-दः-दी) The name of a plant, commonly Ingua<BR> E. इङ्गु going,<BR>and द what gives; the pen. अ is changed to उ and the fem. affix<BR>is ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=106-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इङ्गुल|इंगुलः|इङ्गुलः
इङ्गुल mf. (-लः-ली) See the preceding. E. As before, द being changed to ल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=106-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इच्छक|इच्छकः
इच्छक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Wishing, desirous.<BR>	 m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. Citron, (Citrus<BR>medica.)<BR>	 2. (In arithmetic,) Demand, the sum sought.<BR> E. इच्छा<BR>wish, and वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=106-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इच्छत्
इच्छत् mfn. (-च्छन्-च्छन्ती-च्छत्) Wishing, wishful, desirous.<BR> E. इष् to wish, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=106-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इच्छत्व
इच्छत्व n. (-त्वं) Desire, wishfulness.<BR> E. इच्छा and त्व affix; also with तल्,<BR>इच्छता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=106-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इच्छा
इच्छा f. (-च्छा) Wish, desire.<BR> E. इष् to desire, affixes श and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=106-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इच्छानिवृत्ति|इच्छानिवृत्तिः
इच्छानिवृत्ति f. (-त्तिः) Suppression of desire.<BR> E. इच्छा and निवृत्ति cessation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=106-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इच्छान्वित
इच्छान्वित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Having desire, wishing, wishful.<BR> E. इच्छा and<BR>अन्वित possessed of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=106-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इच्छावत्|इच्छावन्त्
इच्छावत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Wishing, wishful, desirous.<BR>	 f. (-ती) A woman<BR>desirous of anything.<BR> E. इच्छा, मतुप् poss. affix, and ङीप् fem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=106-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इच्छावसु|इच्छावसुः
इच्छावसु m. (-सुः) A name of KUVERA.<BR> E. इच्छा desire and वसु wealth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=106-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इच्छु|इच्छुः
इच्छु mfn. (-च्छुः-च्छुः-च्छु) Wishing, desiring.<BR> E. इष् to wish, and उस् affix,<BR>deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=106-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इच्छुक|इच्छुकः
इच्छुक mfn. (-कः-का-की-कं) Wishing, desirous.<BR> E. कन् added to the last,<BR>or इच्छु and उकन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=106-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इज्जल|इज्जलः
इज्जल m. (-लः) A small tree growing in wet and saline soil, or on low<BR>grounds near the sea, (Barringtonia acutangula.) See हिज्जल.<BR> E. इण्<BR>to go, क्विप् affix, and जल water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=106-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इज्य|इज्यः
इज्य mfn. (-ज्यः-ज्या-ज्यं) A teacher.<BR>	 m. (-ज्यः) VṚHASPATI, the teacher<BR>or Guru of the gods.<BR>	 f. (-ज्या)<BR>	 1. A gift, a donation.<BR>	 2. Sacrificing,<BR>making offerings to the gods or manes.<BR>	 3. Worship, reverence.<BR>	 4.<BR>Meeting, union.<BR>	 5. A cow.<BR>	 6. A bawd or procuress. R. यज् to sacri-<BR>fice, &c. क्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=107-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इज्याशील|इज्याशीलः
इज्याशील m. (-लः) A frequent sacrificer.<BR> E. इज्या sacrifice, and शील to be<BR>frequent, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=107-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इञ्चाक|इंचाकः|इञ्चाकः
इञ्चाक m. (-कः) A shrimp or prawn.<BR> E. इ love, चक् to satisfy, and घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=107-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इट|इटः
इट r. 1st cl. (एटति) To go, to go to or towards.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=107-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इट्चर|इट्चरः
इट्चर m. (-रः) A bull or steer allowed to go at liberty.<BR> E. इष to wish, क्विप्<BR>affix, and चर् who goes, going at will; also इड्वर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=107-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इडा
इडा f. (-डा)<BR>	 1. The wife of BUDDHA, daughter of IKSHAKU.<BR>	 2. The earth.<BR>3. A cow.<BR>	 4. Speed.<BR>	 5. A tubular vessel, one of the principal<BR>channels of the vital spirit, that which is on the right side of the<BR>body.<BR>	 6. Heaven.<BR>	 7. The goddess of speech.<BR> E. इल् to direct or send,<BR>क affix, and टाप् fem. ल and ड are interchangeable: see इला.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=107-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इडाचिका
इडाचिका f. (-का) A wasp.<BR> E. इडा the earth, चर् to go, and ड्वन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=107-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इडिका
इडिका f. (-का) The earth.<BR> E. इल् to direct, and वुन् affix; ल becomes ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=107-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इडिक्क|इडिक्कः
इडिक्क m. (-कः) A wild goat.<BR> E. इडिक् an imitative sound, and क who<BR>utters, from कै, aff. ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=107-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इड्वर|इड्वरः
इड्वर m. (-रः) A bull fit to be let at liberty.<BR> E. इष् to wish, affix क्विप्,<BR>and वृ to choose, अप् affix: see इट्चर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=107-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इण्यीन्थ
इण्यीन्थ m. (-न्थः) A knife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=107-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इण्वीन्दु
इण्वीन्दु m. (-न्दुः) A tree, (Trochis aspera.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=107-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इत्
इत् ind. A grammatical term, implying a letter in the inflective par-<BR>ticles that is to be rejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=107-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इत|इतः
इत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Gone.<BR>	 2. Remembered.<BR>	 3. Obtained.<BR> E. इण् to go,<BR>affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=107-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इतःइतस्
इतःइतस् ind. Here here, come here.<BR> E. इतस् repeated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=107-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इतर|इतरः
इतर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>	 1. Other, different.<BR>	 2. Low, vile.<BR> E. इ desire, तृ to<BR>pass over, and अप aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=107-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इतरथा
इतरथा ind. In another manner, otherwise, differently.<BR> E. था added to<BR>इतर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=107-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इतरेतर|इतरेतरं
इतरेतर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>	 1. Mutual, one with another.<BR>	 2. Respective,<BR>several.<BR> E. इतर repeated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=107-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इतरेतरकाम्या
इतरेतरकाम्या f. (-म्या) Respective or several fancies or inclinations. E.<BR>इतरेतर and काम्य to be desired.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=107-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इतरेतराश्रय
इतरेतराश्रय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Affecting or concerning mutually.<BR> E. इतरेतर<BR>and आश्रय object or receptacle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=107-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इतरेद्युस्
इतरेद्युस् ind. Another or different day.<BR> E. इतर and एद्युस् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=107-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इतश्चेतस्
इतश्चेतस् ind. Hither and thither.<BR> E. इतस् repeated, with च and, inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=107-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इतस्
इतस् ind. Hence, from hence. E. irr. deriv. from इदम् this, with तसिल<BR>aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=107-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इतस्ततस्
इतस्ततस् ind. Here and there, hither and thither.<BR> E. इतस् hence, ततस् thence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=107-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इति|इतिः
इति ind. A particle implying, 1. Cause, (thus, therefore.)<BR>	 2. Manifesta-<BR>tion, (lo! behold!)<BR>	 3. Something additional, (etcetera.)<BR>	 4. The<BR>meanings of एवम्^1, (so, thus, even, in this manner.)<BR>	 5. Conclusion,<BR>enough, (finis.)<BR>	 6. Reference, (so says, this is, &c.) It also implies,<BR>7. Order, arrangement, specific or distinctive, and 8. Identity<BR>(of this or similar form.)<BR>	 9. A grammatical copulative, indicating a<BR>preceding sound or sense, to be again intented.<BR> E. इ to go, क्तिच् aff.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20260703. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/285.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=107-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इतिकथ|इतिकथं
इतिकथ mfn. (-थः-था-थं)<BR>	 1. Unworthy of trust, not fit to be credited.<BR>	 2.<BR>Wicked, lost.<BR>	 f. (-था) Unmeaning or nonsensical discourse.<BR> E. इति<BR>this, so, and कथा a saying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=107-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इतिकर्त्तव्य|इतिकर्तव्य
इतिकर्त्तव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं) What is proper or necessary to be done. E.<BR>इति so, कर्त्तव्य to be done.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=107-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इतिकर्त्तव्यता|इतिकर्तव्यता
इतिकर्त्तव्यता f. (-ता) Proper and right measures.<BR> E. इतिकर्त्तव्य with तल्<BR>added, or with त्व, इतिकर्त्तव्यत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=107-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इतिह
इतिह ind. Traditional instruction, advice, &c. mutually imparted. E.<BR>इति so, thus, and ह tidings.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=107-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इतिहास|इतिहासः
इतिहास m. (-सः) History, traditional accounts of former events, heroic<BR>history, as the Mahabharata and Rāmāyaṇa.<BR> E. इतिह traditional<BR>instruction, अस् to be, and घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=107-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इत्कट|इत्कटः
इत्कट mf. (-टः-टा) A kind of reed or grass; also बहुमूल.<BR> E. उत् and कट<BR>to go, उ is changed to इ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=107-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इत्किला
इत्किला f. (-ला) A perfume: see रोचना.<BR> E. इत obtained, and किल to play.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=107-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इत्थम्
इत्थम् ind. Thus.<BR> E. इदम् this, deriv. irr. with थमु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=107-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इत्थम्भूत|इत्थंभूत
इत्थम्भूत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Become thus or in such manner.<BR> E. इत्थम् and<BR>भूत become.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=107-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इत्य|इत्यः
इत्य mfn. (-त्यः-त्या-त्यं) To be gone to or towards.<BR>	 f. (-त्या) A litter, a<BR>palankeen.<BR> E. इत् to go, क्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=107-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इत्यादि
इत्यादि ind. Etcetera, and so forth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=107-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इत्वर|इत्वरः
इत्वर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>	 1. Low, vile.<BR>	 2. Cruel, harsh.<BR>	 3. A traveller.<BR>	 4.<BR>Poor, indigent.<BR>	 5. Going, moving, what goes.<BR>	 f. (-री) A disloyal or<BR>unchaste woman.<BR> E. इत and क्वरप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=107-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इद|इदं
इद r. 1st cl. (इ) इदि (इन्दति) To have supreme power and superhuman<BR>faculties.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=107-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इदम्
इदम् pron.<BR>	 mfn. (-अयं-इयं-इदं) This.<BR> E. इन्द् to have power, कमिन् Unādi<BR>affix, and the radical न rejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=107-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इदंकार्य्या|इदङ्कार्या|इदंकार्या|इदङ्कार्य्या
इदंकार्य्या f. (-र्य्या) A plant, (Hedysarum alhagi.)<BR> E. इदम् this, and कार्य्य<BR>business; applied to this and that use.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=107-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इदानीन्तन|इदानींतन|इदानीन्तनं
इदानीन्तन mfn. (-नः-नी-नं) Present, momentary, of the present moment.<BR>E. इदानीम् and द्यु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=107-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इदानीम्
इदानीम् ind.<BR>	 1. Now, at present.<BR>	 2. An expletive, affecting however<BR>slightly the sense. E. irr. deriv. from इदम् this, with दानीम् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=107-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इदावत्सर|इदावत्सरः
इदावत्सर m. (-रः) A year, one of the five sorts of years in which gifts.<BR>of clothes and food are productive of great rewards.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=107-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इद्ध|इद्धं|इद्धः
इद्ध mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>	 1. Lighted, alight.<BR>	 2. Shining, glowing, blazing.<BR>	 3.<BR>Clean, clear, bright.<BR>	 4. Wonderful.<BR>	 5. Obeyed, unresisted.<BR>	 n. (-द्धं)<BR>1. Sunshine, light, heat.<BR> E. इन्ध to shine, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=107-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इध्म|इध्मं|इध्मः
इध्म n. (-ध्मं) Fuel.<BR> E. इन्धी to kindle, to burn, मक् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=107-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इध्मप्रव्रश्चन|इध्मप्रव्रश्चनः
इध्मप्रव्रश्चन n. (-नं) A hatchet, an axe.<BR> E. इध्म and प्रव्रश्चन what cuts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=107-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन|इनः
इन m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. The sun.<BR>	 2. A master, a lord.<BR>	 3. A king.<BR>	 4. The as-<BR>terism Hasta.<BR> E. इण् to go, नक् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=107-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इनसभ
इनसभ n. (-भं) A royal court or assembly.<BR> E. इन and सभा assembly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=107-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्दंवर
इन्दंवर n. (-रं) The blue lotus. (Nymphæa cœrulea.)<BR> E. इन्दं from इदि to<BR>possess great power, and वर what chooses, preeminent above other<BR>flowers: see इन्दीवर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=107-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्दिन्दिर|इंदिंदिरः|इन्दिन्दिरः
इन्दिन्दिर m. (-रः) A large bee.<BR> E. इदि to possess great power, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=107-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्दिरा|इंदिरा
इन्दिरा f. (-रा) A name of LAKṢMĪ, the wife of VIṢṆU.<BR> E. इदि as above,<BR>and रा who gives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=107-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्दिरालय|इन्दिरालयं
इन्दिरालय n. (-यं) The lotus, (Nymphæa lotus.)<BR> E. इन्दिरा LAKṢMĪ, and<BR>आलय an abode; this goddess issued at the creation from the<BR>petals of the flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=107-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्दिरावर|इन्दिरावरं
इन्दिरावर n. (-रं) The blue lotus.<BR> E. इन्दिरा the goddess, and वर what is<BR>best; a flower beloved by LAKṢMĪ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=107-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्दिवर|इंदिवर|इंदिवरं|इन्दिवरं
इन्दिवर n. (-रं) The blue lotus. (Nymhæa cœrulea)<BR> E. इन्दि for इन्दिरा q.<BR>v. the rest as in the preceding; also इन्दिवर and इन्दीवार.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=107-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्दीवर|इंदीवर|इंदीवरं|इन्दीवरं
इन्दीवर n. (-रं) See the preceding.<BR>	 f. (-री) A plant, (Asparagus racemo-<BR>sus.) E. As before.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=107-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्दीवार|इन्दीवारं|इंदीवारः|इन्दीवारः
इन्दीवार n. (-रं) See इन्दिवर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=107-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्दु|इंदुः|इन्दुः
इन्दु m. (-न्दुः)<BR>	 1. The moon.<BR>	 2. Camphor.<BR> E. उन्द् to wet or moisten; उ<BR>Unādi affix and the initial changed to इ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=107-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्दुकमल|इन्दुकमलं
इन्दुकमल n. (-लं) The white lotus.<BR> E. इन्दु the moon, and कमल the lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=107-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्दुकला
इन्दुकला f. (-ला) A digit of the moon.<BR> E. इन्दु and कला a digit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=107-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्दुकलिका
इन्दुकलिका f. (-का) The Ketaki flower.<BR> E. इन्दु and कलिका a bud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=107-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्दुकान्त|इन्दुकान्तः
इन्दुकान्त m. (-न्तः) The lunar gem, the moonstone.<BR>	 f. (-न्ता) Night.<BR> E. इन्दु<BR>and कान्त a master or husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=107-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्दुजनक|इन्दुजनकः
इन्दुजनक m. (-कः) The ocean.<BR> E. इन्दु and जनक a parent; the moon was<BR>produced amongst other things at the churning of the ocean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=107-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्दुजा
इन्दुजा f. (-जा) The Narmada or commonly Narbudda river in the<BR>Dakhin.<BR> E. इन्दु and जा born; the daughter of the moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=108-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्दुदल|इन्दुदलः
इन्दुदल m. (-लः) A portion of the moon, a digit, a crescent, &c.<BR> E. इन्दु<BR>and दल a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=108-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्दुपुत्र|इन्दुपुत्रः
इन्दुपुत्र m. (-त्रः) A name of BUDHA, regent of the planet MERCURY. E.<BR>इन्दु and पुत्र the son: the son of CHANDRA or the moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=108-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्दुभृत्
इन्दुभृत् m. (-भृत्) A name of ŚIVA.<BR> E. इन्दु and भृत् who nourishes; ŚIVA<BR>wears a half moon on his forehead.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=108-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्दुमण्डल
इन्दुमण्डल n. (-लं) The orb or disc of the moon.<BR> E. इन्दु and मण्डल sphere.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=108-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्दुमती|इंदुमती
इन्दुमती f. (-ती)<BR>	 1. Day of full moon.<BR>	 2. Name of a princess married to<BR>AJA the son of RAGHU.<BR> E. इन्दु and मतुप् poss. affix, fem. ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=108-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्दुर
इन्दुर m. (-रः) A rat.<BR> E. उन्द to moisten, उरच् affix, the initial is changed<BR>to इ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=108-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्दुरत्न|इन्दुरत्नं
इन्दुरत्न n. (-त्नं) A pearl.<BR> E. इन्दु and रत्न a gem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=108-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्दुरेखा
इन्दुरेखा f. (-खा) A digit of the moon.<BR> E. इन्दु and रेखा a line.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=108-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्दुलेखा
इन्दुलेखा f. (-खा)<BR>	 1. A digit of the moon.<BR>	 2. A plant, (Menispermum<BR>glabrum.)<BR>	 3. The moon plant, (Asclepias acida.)<BR>	 4. A kind of<BR>lovage, (Ligusticum ajwaen:) see अनामिका.<BR> E. इन्दु and लेखा a line.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=108-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्दुलोहक|इन्दुलोहकं
इन्दुलोहक n. (-कं) Silver.<BR> E. इन्दु and लोह iron, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=108-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्दुवल्ली
इन्दुवल्ली f. (-ल्ली) The moon plant, (Asclepias acida.)<BR> E. इन्दु and वल्ली a creeper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=108-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्दुव्रत|इन्दुव्रतं
इन्दुव्रत n. (-तं) A religious observance depending on the age of the<BR>moon; diminishing the quantity of food by a certain portion<BR>daily, for a fortnight or a month, &c.<BR> E. इन्दु and व्रत a religious<BR>obligation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=108-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्र|इंद्रः|इन्द्रः
इन्द्र m. (-न्द्रः)<BR>	 1. The deity presiding over Svarga or the Hindu para-<BR>dise, and the secondary divinities; he is also regent of the east<BR>quarter, and is more particularly the deity of the atmosphere,<BR>corresponding in many respects with the Grecian JOVE.<BR>	 2. The<BR>Supreme Being, (according to the Vedanta,) or the deity INDRA in<BR>that capacity.<BR>	 3. Supremacy, supreme power or authority.<BR>	 4. An<BR>Aditya, one of the twelve demigods so called.<BR>	 5. One of the Yogas.<BR>or divisions of a circle on the plane of the ecliptic.<BR>	 6. The human<BR>or animal soul, the portion of spirit residing in the body.<BR>	 7. Night.<BR>8. A plant, (Wrightea antidysenterica, &c.) see कुटज.<BR>	 9. An organ<BR>of sense.<BR>	 10. (In composition) Best, excellent.<BR>	 11. The 14th luna-<BR>tion of the month Jyeshtha.<BR>	 12. One of the nine divisions of<BR>Jambu Dwipa, or the known continent.<BR>	 f. (-न्द्रा)<BR>	 1. The name of a<BR>plant, (Marjoram?) see फणिज्झक.<BR>	 2. The wife of INDRA.<BR> E. इदि to<BR>possess supreme power, and रन् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=108-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रक|इंद्रकं|इन्द्रकं
इन्द्रक n. (-कं) An assembly room, a hall.<BR> E. इन्द्र excellent, and क what<BR>sounds, from कै and ड aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=108-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रकील|इन्द्रकीलः
इन्द्रकील m. (-लः) The mountain Mandara, a fabulous mountain with<BR>which the ocean was churned.<BR> E. इन्द्र and कील a pin or bolt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=108-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रकुञ्जर|इन्द्रकुञ्जरः
इन्द्रकुञ्जर m. (-रः) INDRA'S elephant.<BR> E. इन्द्र and कुञ्जर an elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=108-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रकोष|इन्द्रकोषः
इन्द्रकोष m. (-षः)<BR>	 1. A platform, a scaffold.<BR>	 2. A projection of the roof of a<BR>house, forming a kind of balcony or terrace.<BR>	 2. A pin or bracket<BR>projecting from the wall.<BR> E. इन्द्र best, and कोष a place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=108-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रगोप|इन्द्रगोपः
इन्द्रगोप m. (-पः) An insect, (Coccinella of various kinds.)<BR> E. इन्द्र best,<BR>गो light, and प from पा who nourishes or possesses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=108-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रच्छन्दस्|इन्द्रछन्दस्
इन्द्रच्छन्दस् n. (-न्दः) A necklace of a thousand strings.<BR> E. इन्द्र best, and<BR>छन्दस् a necklace, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=108-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रजाल|इन्द्रजालं
इन्द्रजाल n. (-लं)<BR>	 1. Conjuring, juggling.<BR>	 2. Deception, cheating.<BR>	 3.<BR>Trick or stratagem in war.<BR> E. इन्द्र an organ of sense, and जाल a net.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=108-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रजालिक|इन्द्रजालिकः
इन्द्रजालिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>	 1. A juggler, a conjuror.<BR>	 2. Deceptive, un-<BR>real.<BR> E. इन्द्रजाल illusion, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=108-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रजित्
इन्द्रजित् m. (-जित्) The son of RAVANA.<BR> E. इन्द्र and जित् who conquers: the conqueror of INDRA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=108-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रजिद्विजयिन्
इन्द्रजिद्विजयिन् m. (-यी) LAKSHMANA, the brother of RAMA.<BR> E. इन्द्रजित्<BR>and विजयिन् a victor, the conqueror of INDRAJIT.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=108-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रतूल|इन्द्रतूलं
इन्द्रतूल n. (-लं) A flock of cotton, a flocculent seed, &c. blown about in<BR>the air.<BR> E. इन्द्र and तूल cotton: INDRA'S cotton.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=108-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रतूलक|इन्द्रतूलकं
इन्द्रतूलक n. (-कं) See the preceding. E. As before, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=108-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रदारु|इन्द्रदारुः
इन्द्रदारु m. (-रुः) A tree, (Pinus devadaru.)<BR> E. इन्द्र and दारु tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=108-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रद्रु|इन्द्रद्रुः
इन्द्रद्रु m. (-द्रुः) A tree, (Pentaptera arjuna, Rox.)<BR> E. इन्द्र and द्रु a tree<BR>a staff of which is fit to carry the banner of INDRA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=108-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रद्रुम|इन्द्रद्रुमः
इन्द्रद्रुम m. (-मः) See the preceding. E. As before.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=108-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रनील|इन्द्रनीलः
इन्द्रनील m. (-लः) A sapphire.<BR> E. इन्द्र best, and नील blue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=108-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रनीलक|इन्द्रनीलकः
इन्द्रनीलक m. (-कः) An emerald. E. See the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=108-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रपुष्पा
इन्द्रपुष्पा f. (-ष्पा) A medicinal plant; also अग्निजिह्वा.<BR> E. इन्द्र and पुष्पा a<BR>flower; also इन्द्रपुष्पिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=108-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रपुरोहिता
इन्द्रपुरोहिता f. (-ता) The asterism Pushya.<BR> E. इन्द्र and पुरोहिता priest, INDRA presiding over it.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=108-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रप्रस्थ|इंद्रप्रस्थ|इन्द्रप्रस्थं
इन्द्रप्रस्थ m. (-स्थः) Ancient Delhi.<BR> E. इन्द्र the deity, and प्रस्थ who presides.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=108-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रप्रहरण|इन्द्रप्रहरणं
इन्द्रप्रहरण n. (-णं) INDRA'S thunderbolt.<BR> E. इन्द्र and प्रहरण a weapon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=108-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रभेषज|इन्द्रभेषजं
इन्द्रभेषज n. (-जं) Dried ginger.<BR> E. इन्द्र best, and भेषज medicament.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=108-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रमहकामुक|इन्द्रमहकामुकः
इन्द्रमहकामुक m. (-कः) A dog.<BR> E. इन्द्र, मह a sacrifice and कामुक desirous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=108-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रमूल
इन्द्रमूल n. (-लं) A flock of cotton: see इन्द्रतूल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=108-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रयव|इन्द्रयवः
इन्द्रयव mn. (-वः-वं) The seed of the Wrightea antidysenterica.<BR> E. इन्द्र the<BR>plant, and यव seed: it is used medicinally in cases of diarrhœa,<BR>dysentery, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=108-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रलुप्त|इन्द्रलुप्तं|इन्द्रलुप्तः
इन्द्रलुप्त mn. (-प्तः-प्तं) Morbid, baldness, falling of the hair of the head:<BR>according to some authorities, loss of beard.<BR> E. इन्द्र best, लुप्त lost.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=108-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रलुप्तक|इन्द्रलुप्तकं
इन्द्रलुप्तक m. (-कः) See the preceding. E. As before, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=108-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रलोक|इन्द्रलोकः
इन्द्रलोक m. (-कः) Svarga or paradise, the heaven of INDRA.<BR> E. इन्द्र and<BR>लोक world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=108-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रलोकेश|इन्द्रलोकेशः
इन्द्रलोकेश m. (-शः)<BR>	 1. INDRA.<BR>	 2. A guest, hospitality to whom secures<BR>paradise.<BR> E. इन्द्रलोक and ईश lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=108-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रवारुणिका
इन्द्रवारुणिका f. (-का) Colocynth, a wild bitter gourd, (Cucumis colo-<BR>cynthis.)<BR> E. कन् added to इन्द्रवारुणी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=108-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रवारुणी
इन्द्रवारुणी f. (-णी) See the preceding.<BR> E. इन्द्र and वरुण the two deities so<BR>called, affixes अण् and ङीप्; the favourite plant of INDRA and<BR>VARUṆA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=108-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रवृक्ष|इन्द्रवृक्षः
इन्द्रवृक्ष m. (-क्षः) A kind of fir: see देवदारु.<BR> E. इन्द्र for any god, वृक्ष a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=108-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रव्रत
इन्द्रव्रत n. (-तं) One of the duties of a king, to distribute gratification,<BR>as INDRA pours down rain.<BR> E. इन्द्र and व्रत observance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=108-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रवृद्धा
इन्द्रवृद्धा f. (-द्धा) A sore, an ulcer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=108-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रशक्ति|इन्द्रशक्तिः
इन्द्रशक्ति f. (-क्तिः) INDRĀṆĪ, the wife or personified energy of INDRA. E.<BR>इन्द्र and शक्ति power.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=108-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रसावर्णि|इन्द्रसावर्णिः
इन्द्रसावर्णि m. (-र्णिः) The last of the fourteen Menus.<BR> E. इन्द्र and सावर्णि the son of the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=108-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रसुत|इन्द्रसुतः
इन्द्रसुत m. (-तः) The monkey king BALI.<BR> E. इन्द्र and सुत a son; the son<BR>of INDRA: the epithet is also applied to ARJUNA and JAYANTA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=108-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रसुरस|इन्द्रसुरसः
इन्द्रसुरस m. (-सः) A shrub, the leaves of which are used in discutient<BR>applications, (Vitex negundo;) also सिन्दुवार.<BR> E. इन्द्र best, सु good,<BR>and रस juice; whose juice is excellent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=108-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रसुरिस|इन्द्रसुरिसः
इन्द्रसुरिस m. (-सः) See the preceding. E. As before, the pen. being changed to इ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=108-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रसूनु|इन्द्रसूनुः
इन्द्रसूनु m. (-नुः) The son of INDRA: see इन्द्रसुत<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=108-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्राग्निधूम|इन्द्राग्निधूमः
इन्द्राग्निधूम m. (-मः) Frost.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=108-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्राणिका|इंद्राणिका
इन्द्राणिका f. (-का) Vitex negundo: see इन्द्रसुरस.<BR> E. कन् added to the next word.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=108-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्राणी|इंद्राणी
इन्द्राणी f. (-णी)<BR>	 1. The wife of INDRA.<BR>	 2. A plant, (Vitex negundo:) see<BR>the preceding.<BR> E. इन्द्र, ङीष् affix, and आनुक् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=108-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रानुज|इन्द्रानुजः
इन्द्रानुज m. (-जः) A name of VIṢṆU.<BR> E. इन्द्र and अनुज younger born:<BR>the younger brother of INDRA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=108-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रायुध|इन्द्रायुधं|इन्द्रायुधः
इन्द्रायुध m. (-धः) The rainbow.<BR>	 f. (-धा) A kind of leech of various tints<BR>on the back.<BR> E. इन्द्र and आयुध a weapon; INDRA'S weapon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=108-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रारि|इन्द्रारिः
इन्द्रारि m. (-रिः) An Asura or demon.<BR> E. इन्द्र and अरि an enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=108-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रावरज|इन्द्रावरजः
इन्द्रावरज m. (-जः) VIṢṆU.<BR> E. इन्द्र and अवरज after-born: the younger<BR>brother of INDRA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=108-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्राशन|इन्द्राशनः
इन्द्राशन m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. Hemp, dried and chewed.<BR>	 2. The shrub which bears<BR>the seed used as a jeweller's weight, (Abrus precatorius.)<BR> E. इन्द्र<BR>and अशन food: the food of INDRA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=108-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रासन
इन्द्रासन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. The throne of INDRA.<BR>	 2. Any throne.<BR> E. इन्द्र and असन<BR>a seat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=108-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रिय|इंद्रिय|इन्द्रियं|इन्द्रियः
इन्द्रिय n. (-यं)<BR>	 1. An organ of sense divided into three classes, Jananendri-<BR>yas, Karmendriyas, and Antarindriyas, or organs of percep-<BR>tion and action, and the internal organs; the first are the eye, ear,<BR>nose, tongue, and skin; the second, the organ of speech or larynx,<BR>hand, foot, anus, and parts of generation; the last are, Manas<BR>the mind or organ of thought; Buddhi the organ of apprehension;<BR>Ahankara the organ of selfishness; and Chitta the heart or organ<BR>of feeling.<BR>	 2. Semen virile.<BR>	 mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Done, seen, given, &c.<BR>by INDRA.<BR> E. इन्द्र the soul or self, and इयच् affix, deriv. irr. what is<BR>with difficulty restrained by the soul, or इन्द्र the deity, and घ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=109-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रियगोचर|इन्द्रियगोचरः
इन्द्रियगोचर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Perceptible, capable of being ascertained by<BR>the senses.<BR> E. इन्द्रिय and गोचर perceptible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=109-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रियग्राम|इन्द्रियग्रामः
इन्द्रियग्राम m. (-मः) The senses or organs of sense collectively.<BR> E. इन्द्रिय<BR>and ग्राम here, assemblage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=109-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रियज्ञान
इन्द्रियज्ञान n. (-नं) The faculty of perception, sense, consciousness. E.<BR>इन्द्रिय and ज्ञान knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=109-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रियनिग्रह|इन्द्रियनिग्रहः
इन्द्रियनिग्रह m. (-हः) Restraining the organs of sense.<BR> E. इन्द्रिय and<BR>निग्रह restraint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=109-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रियबुद्धि|इन्द्रियबुद्धिः
इन्द्रियबुद्धि f. (-द्धिः) Perception, the exercise of any sense, the faculty of<BR>any organ.<BR> E. इन्द्रिय and बुद्धि knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=109-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रियबोधन
इन्द्रियबोधन n. (-नं) Any excitement of sense, an object of perception, a<BR>stimulus, &c.<BR> E. इन्द्रिय and बोधन waking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=109-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रियवर्ग|इन्द्रियवर्गः
इन्द्रियवर्ग m. (-र्गः) the organs of sense collectively.<BR> E. इन्द्रिय and वर्ग a class.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=109-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रियविप्रतिपत्ति|इन्द्रियविप्रतिपत्तिः
इन्द्रियविप्रतिपत्ति f. (-त्तिः) Erroneous or vicious perception.<BR> E. इन्द्रिय and<BR>विप्रतिपत्ति perversion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=109-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रियस्वाप|इन्द्रियस्वापः
इन्द्रियस्वाप m. (-पः)<BR>	 1. Unconsciousness, insensibility.<BR>	 2. The end of the<BR>world.<BR> E. इन्द्रिय and स्वाप sleep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=109-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रियागोचर
इन्द्रियागोचर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Imperceptible.<BR> E. इन्द्रिय and अगोचर im-<BR>perceptible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=109-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रियायतन|इन्द्रियायतनं
इन्द्रियायतन n. (-नं) The body.<BR> E. इन्द्रिय and आयतन a mansion: the resi-<BR>dence of the senses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=109-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रियार्थ|इन्द्रियार्थः
इन्द्रियार्थ m. (-र्थः) An object of sense, as sound, smell, &c.<BR> E. इन्द्रिय and<BR>अर्थ an object.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=109-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रियासङ्ग|इन्द्रियासङ्गः
इन्द्रियासङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः) Stoicism, philosophy, detachment from sensual<BR>objects.<BR> E. इन्द्रिय and असङ्ग detachment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=109-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रेज्य|इन्द्रेज्यः
इन्द्रेज्य m. (-ज्यः) The name of VṚHASPATI, the preceptor of the gods.<BR>E. इन्द्र and इज्य to be worshipped; venerable to the deities.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=109-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्ध|इंध|इन्धः
इन्ध r. 7th cl. (ई and ञि) ञिइन्धी (इन्धे) 1. To shine.<BR>	 2. To kindle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=109-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्धन|इंधन|इन्धनं
इन्धन n. (-नं) Fuel; wood, grass, &c. used for that purpose.<BR> E. इन्ध to<BR>kindle, and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=109-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्वका
इन्वका f. plu. (-काः) Stars in the head of Orion.<BR> E. इवि to please, क्वुन्<BR>affix: see इल्वला and इल्वका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=109-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इभ|इभः
इभ r. 10th cl. (इ) इभि (इम्भयते) To collect or accumulate. {sic}<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=109-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इभ|इभः
इभ m. (-भः)<BR>	 1. An elephant.<BR>	 2. Best (in composition.)<BR> E. इण् to go, भन्<BR>Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=109-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इभकणा
इभकणा f. (-णा) A plant with an arometic seed, (Pothos officinalis,) E.<BR>इभ an elephant, and कणा pepper; being considered by Hindu<BR>writers, as a large species of pepper; see गजपिप्पली.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=109-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इभदन्ता
इभदन्ता f. (-न्ता) A plant: see नागदन्ती.<BR> E. इभ an elephant and दन्त a<BR>tooth: this and similar names are given, from its supposed resem-<BR>blance to an elephant's tooth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=109-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इभनिमीलिका
इभनिमीलिका f. (-का) Smartness, shrewdness, wittiness.<BR> E. इभ and निमी-<BR>लिका winking; winking knowingly like an elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=109-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इभपालक|इभपालकः
इभपालक m. (-कः) The driver or keeper of an elephant.<BR> E. इभ, पालक a<BR>nourisher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=109-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इभपोटा
इभपोटा f. (-टा) A young elephant, a cub.<BR> E. इभ and पोटा any young<BR>animal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=109-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इभमाचल|इभमाचलः
इभमाचल m. (-लः) A lion.<BR> E. इभ an elephant, in the second case, आ and<BR>चल who attacks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=109-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इभयुवति|इभयुवतिः
इभयुवति f. (-तिः) An elephant's cub.<BR> E. इभ and युवति young.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=109-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इभाख्य|इभाख्यः
इभाख्य m. (-ख्यः) A plant, (Mesua ferrea:) see नागकेशर.<BR> E. इभ and आख्या<BR>an appellation; named from the elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=109-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इभोषणा
इभोषणा f. (-णा) A kind of aromatic plant: see इभकणा.<BR> E. इभ and उषणा<BR>pepper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=109-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इभ्य|इभ्यः
इभ्य mfn. (-भ्यः-भ्या-भ्यं) Wealthy, opulent.<BR>	 f. (-भ्या)<BR>	 1. A female elephant.<BR>2. The olibanum tree, (Boswellia thurifera.)<BR> E. इभ an elephant;<BR>here also implying excellence, and यत् affix of appropriation or<BR>fitness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=109-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इयत्|इयन्त्
इयत् mfn. (-यान्-यती-यत्) So much, this much.<BR> E. इदम् this, and वतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=109-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इयत्ता
इयत्ता f. (-त्ता) Fixed measure or quantity, so much.<BR> E. इयत् and तल्<BR>affix; also with त्व, इयत्त्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=109-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इरण|इरणं
इरण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>	 1. Desert.<BR>	 2. Salt or barren, (soil.) E. See इरिण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=109-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इरम्मद|इरंमद|इरम्मदः
इरम्मद m. (-दः)<BR>	 1. A flash of lightning, or the fire attending the fall of<BR>a thunderbolt.<BR>	 2. Submarine fire.<BR> E. इरा water, here also watery<BR>clouds, and मद what plays or shines.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=109-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इरा
इरा f. (-रा)<BR>	 1. The earth.<BR>	 2. Water.<BR>	 3. Speech.<BR>	 4. The goddess of<BR>speech, &c.<BR>	 5. Ardent spirits.<BR> E. इण् to go, and रन् Unādi affix, fem.<BR>affix टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=109-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इराचर|इराचरं
इराचर m. (-रः) Hail.<BR>	 mfn. (-रः-रा-री-रं)<BR>	 1. Earth-born, terrestrial.<BR>	 2.<BR>Aquatic.<BR> E. इरा water, &c. and चर what goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=109-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इराज|इराजः
इराज m. (-जः) A name of KANDARPA the Hindu CUPID.<BR> E. इरा water,<BR>and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=109-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इरावत्|इरावन्त्
इरावत् m. (-वान्)<BR>	 1. The ocean.<BR>	 2. A cloud.<BR>	 3. A king.<BR>	 mfn. (-वान्-वती-<BR>वत्) Watery, having or yielding water, &c.<BR> E. इरा and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=109-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इरावेल्लिका
इरावेल्लिका f. (-का) Pimples or pustules on the head.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=109-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इरिण|इरिणं|इरिणः
इरिण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. A desert, an inhospitable region.<BR>	 2. Salt or barren soil.<BR>E. ऋ to go, इनन् Unādi affix, and the initial changed to इ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=109-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इरिमेद|इरिमेदः
इरिमेद m. (-दः) A fetid mimosa: see विट्खदिर. E. See अरिमेद, अ being<BR>changed to इ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=109-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इरु
इरु m. (-रुः) Seed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=109-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इरेश|इरेशः
इरेश m. (-शः)<BR>	 1. A name of VIṢṆU.<BR>	 2. A king, a sovereign.<BR>	 3.<BR>VARUṆA.<BR> E. इरा SARASWATI, &c. ईश lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=109-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इर्व्वारु|इर्वारु|इर्वारुः|इर्व्वारुः
इर्व्वारु mf. (-रुः-रुः)<BR>	 1. A cucumber, (Cumumis utilatissimus, Rox.)<BR>2. Another kind, (Cucumis colocynthis.)<BR> E. इरु a seed, and आरु<BR>what goes to or gets, from ऋ and उण् affix, or आलु, र becoming ल;<BR>also written इर्व्वालु, ईर्व्वारु, उर्व्वारु, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=109-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इर्व्वारुशुक्तिका|इर्वारुशुक्तिका
इर्व्वारुशुक्तिका f. (-का) A kind of melon; commonly Sphuti or Sphut,<BR>(Cucumis momordica.)<BR> E. इर्व्वारु and शुक्तिका an oyster-shaped cu-<BR>cumber.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=109-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इर्व्वालु|इर्वालु|इर्व्वालुः
इर्व्वालु m. (-लुः) See इर्व्वारु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=109-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इल
इल r. 6th cl. (इलति)<BR>	 1. To sleep.<BR>	 2. To go.<BR>	 3. To throw, send or direct:<BR>in this last sense, it is also r. 10th cl. (एलयति.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=109-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इलविला
इलविला f. (-ला) The mother of KUVERA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=109-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इला
इला f. (-ला)<BR>	 1. The wife of BUDDHA, and daughter of IKSHWAKU.<BR>	 2.<BR>The earth.<BR>	 3. A cow.<BR>	 4. Speech.<BR> E. इल् to send, क and टाप् affixes;<BR>also इडा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=109-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इलागोल
इलागोल n. (-लं) The earth, the globe.<BR> E. इला and गोल a sphere.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=109-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इलातल
इलातल n. (-लं)<BR>	 1. The fourth place in the circle of the zodiac.<BR>	 2. The<BR>surface of the earth.<BR> E. इला and तल below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=109-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इलावृत|इलावृतं
इलावृत n. (-तं) One of the nine Varṣas or divisions of the known world,<BR>comprehending the highest and most centrical part of the old<BR>continent.<BR> E. इला the earth, and आवृत chosen: the fairest part of the<BR>globe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=109-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इलिका
इलिका f. (-का) The earth.<BR> E. इल् to go, कन् and टाप् affixes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=109-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इली
इली f. (-ली) A cudgel, a stick shaped like a sword or a short sword: see ईली.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=109-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इलीश|इलीशः
इलीश m. (-शः) A fish, commonly the Hilsa or Sable, (Clupea alosa.) E.<BR>इल् to go, (in the water,) and ईश chief, principal. The fish being<BR>one of high flavour, and very abundant at certain seasons, it is<BR>generally eaten both by the natives of Bengal, and by Europeans<BR>residing there.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=109-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इल्लल|इल्ललः
इल्लल m. (-लः) A bird.<BR> E. इल् to go, and अल who is able.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=110-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इल्लिश|इल्लिशः
इल्लिश m. (-शः) The Hilsa fish: see इलीश also ईल्लीश.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=110-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इल्वका
इल्वका f. plu. (-काः) Stars in Orion's head: see इल्वल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=110-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इल्वड
इल्वड m. (-डः) See the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=110-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इल्वल|इल्वलः
इल्वल m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. The name of a demon.<BR>	 2. Of a fish.<BR>	 f. plu. (-लाः) Stars<BR>in Orin's head.<BR> E. इल् to send or go, and वल Unādi affix; the last<BR>is also written इल्वका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=110-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इव
इव r. 1st cl. (इ) इवि (इंवति) 1. To pervade.<BR>	 2. (According to some,) to<BR>please.<BR>	 3. To be satisfied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=110-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इव
इव ind. So, even, as, like, in the same manner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=110-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इशीका
इशीका f. (-का) An elephant's eyeball: see इषीका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=110-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष|इषः
इष r. 4th cl. (इष्यति) To go. r. 6th cl. (इच्छति)<BR>	 1. To wish, to desire.<BR>	 2.<BR>To accept, to receive. With अभि, to desire: with प्रति, to engage,<BR>to promise. r. 9th cl. (इष्णाति) To repeat an act, to do anything<BR>again and again. With अनु prefixed, to search after, to investigate<BR>or enquire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=110-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष|इषः
इष m. (-षः) The month Āswin, (September-October.)<BR> E. इष् to go, क<BR>affix; also ईष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=110-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इषिका
इषिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. An elephant's eyeball.<BR>	 2. A painter's brush, &c. also<BR>इषीका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=110-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इषिर|इषिरः
इषिर m. (-रः) Fire.<BR> E. इष् to go, किरच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=110-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इषीका
इषीका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. An elephant's eyeball.<BR>	 2. A painter's brush, &c. also<BR>इषिका.<BR>	 3. A kind of reed, (Saccharum spontaneum.)<BR> E. इष् to go,<BR>ईकन् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=110-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इषु|इषुः
इषु mf. (-षुः-षुः)<BR>	 1. An arrow.<BR>	 2. A versed sine.<BR> E. इष् to go, and उ Unādi<BR>aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=110-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इषुधर|इषुधरः
इषुधर m. (-रः) An archer.<BR> E. इषु and धर who bears.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=110-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इषुधि|इषुधिः
इषुधि mf. (-धिः-धिः) A quiver.<BR> E. इषु and धि what holds, from धा root,<BR>and कि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=110-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्ट|इष्टं|इष्टः
इष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>	 1. Wished, desired.<BR>	 2. Cherished, beloved.<BR>	 3. Wor-<BR>shipped, reverenced, respected.<BR>	 m. (-ष्टः)<BR>	 1. A lover, a husband.<BR>	 2.<BR>The Castor-oil tree.<BR>	 n. (-ष्टं)<BR>	 1. An act of sacrifice, an oblation, &c.<BR>2. An essential ceremony, as ablution, investiture, &c. ind. (-ष्टम्)<BR>Voluntarily.<BR> E. इष् to desire, or इष् substituted for यज् to sacrifice,<BR>and क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=110-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्टकर्म्मन्|इष्टकर्मन्
इष्टकर्म्मन् n. (-र्म्म) (In arithmetic,) Rule of supposition, operation with an<BR>assumed number.<BR> E. इष्ट wished, and कर्म्मन् act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=110-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्टका
इष्टका f. (-का) A brick; also इष्टिका.<BR> E. इष् to wish, तकक् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=110-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्टकान्यास|इष्टकान्यासः
इष्टकान्यास m. (-सः) Laying the foundation of a house.<BR> E. इष्टका and न्यास<BR>order.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=110-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्टकापथ|इष्टकापथं|इष्टकापथः
इष्टकापथ n. (-थं) The root of a fragrant grass, (Andropogon muricatum.)<BR>E. इष्ट wished, and कापथ a bad road, growing in or preferring<BR>unfrequented places: this word is sometimes divided, कापथ being<BR>one name, and इष्ट added to अवदाह, another name: see अवदाहेष्ट and<BR>अवदाह.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=110-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्टकाराशि|इष्टकाराशिः
इष्टकाराशि f. (-शिः) A pile of bricks.<BR> E. इष्टका and राशि a heap.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=110-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्टगन्ध|इष्टगन्धं|इष्टगन्धः
इष्टगन्ध mfn. (-न्धः-न्धा-न्धं) Fragrant, any fragrant substance.<BR>	 n. (-न्धं) Sand.<BR>E. इष्ट and गन्ध a smell; of a desirable odor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=110-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्टतम
इष्टतम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं) Beloved, best beloved, dearest, most desired. E.<BR>इष्ट and तमप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=110-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्टतर
इष्टतर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Dearer, more dear, more desired.<BR> E. इष्ट and तरप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=110-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्टत्व
इष्टत्व n. (-त्वं)<BR>	 1. Desirableness.<BR>	 2. Reverence, &c. also इष्टता.<BR> E. तल् or त्व<BR>added to इष्ट.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=110-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्टदेव|इष्टदेवः
इष्टदेव m. (-वः) A tutelary deity, one particularly worshipped.<BR> E. इष्ट and<BR>देव a deity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=110-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्टदेवता
इष्टदेवता f. (-ता) A person's chosen or tutelary.<BR>	 2. divinity.<BR> E. इष्ट and<BR>देवता divinity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=110-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्टापूर्त्त|इष्टापूर्त|इष्टापूर्तं|इष्टापूर्त्तं
इष्टापूर्त्त n. (-र्त्तं) Any religious duty, as oblation, sacrifice, penance, holy<BR>study, digging a well, planting a tree, &c.<BR> E. इष्ट a sacrifice, and<BR>पूर्त्त liberal act, religiously considered; आङ् prefixed to the latter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=110-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्टार्थोद्युक्त|इष्टार्थोद्युक्तः
इष्टार्थोद्युक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं) Zealously active, diligent for a desired object.<BR>E. इष्ट wished, अर्थ intention, and उद्युक्त diligent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=110-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्टि|इष्टिः
इष्टि f. (-ष्टिः)<BR>	 1. Wish, desire.<BR>	 2. A sacrifice, any sacrificial rite.<BR>	 3. A<BR>compendious verse easily committed to memory.<BR> E. इष् to wish, or<BR>इष् substituted for यज्, to sacrifice; affix क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=110-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्टिका
इष्टिका f. (-का) A brick. E. More usually इष्टका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=110-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्टिन्
इष्टिन् mfn. (-ष्टी-ष्टिनी-ष्टि) Who wishes or desires, desirous, wishing. E.<BR>इष्ट and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=110-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्टिपच|इष्टिपचः
इष्टिपच m. (-चः) A demon.<BR> E. इष्टि a sacrifice or oblation, and पच who<BR>digests: stealing oblations to the deities, and eating them.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=110-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्टिमुष्
इष्टिमुष् m. (-मुट्) A demon.<BR> E. इष्टि an oblation, and मुष् who steals; from<BR>मुष root, and क्विप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=110-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्टु|इष्टुः
इष्टु f. (-ष्टुः) Desire, wish.<BR> E. इष् to wish, तु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=110-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्ट्वा
इष्ट्वा ind.<BR>	 1. Having sacrificed or worshipped.<BR>	 2. Having wished.<BR> E. इष<BR>with क्त्वाच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=110-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्म|इष्मः
इष्म m. (-ष्मः)<BR>	 1. Love or the deity KĀMA^1.<BR>	 2. Spring.<BR> E. इष् to desire, and मक् Unādi aff.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20260617. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/264.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=110-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्य|इष्यं|इष्यः
इष्य m. (-ष्यः) The spring season.<BR> E. इष् to wish, and क्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=110-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्व|इष्वः
इष्व m. (-ष्वः) A spiritual preceptor.<BR> E. इष् to wish, वुन् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=110-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्वास|इष्वासं|इष्वासः
इष्वास mfn. (-सः-सा-सं) A thrower of arrows.<BR>	 m. (-सः)<BR>	 1. A bow.<BR>	 2. An<BR>archer, a warrior.<BR> E. इषु an arrow, and आस who throws.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=110-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इस्
इस् ind. (इः) An interjection of anger, pain, or sorrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=110-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इह
इह ind.<BR>	 1. Here, in this place.<BR>	 2. Now, at this time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=110-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इहकाल|इहकालः
इहकाल m. (-लः) This life.<BR> E. इह and काल time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=110-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इहलोक|इहलोकः
इहलोक m. (-कः) This life, the world.<BR> E. इह and लोक world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=110-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इहामूत्र
इहामूत्र ind. Here and there, in this world and in the next.<BR> E. इह here,<BR>अमूत्र there or in that.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=110-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ई
ई The fourth letter of the alphabet, corresponding to I long, having<BR>the sound of ee in feel, and distinguished by an accent from the<BR>former, as ī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=110-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ई
ई m. (ईः) A name of KANDARPA.<BR>	 f. (ईः) A name of LAKṢMĪ. ind.<BR>An interjection of, 1. Pain.<BR>	 2. Anger.<BR>	 3. Consciousness or percep-<BR>tion.<BR>	 4. Consideration.<BR>	 5. Compassion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=110-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ई
ई r. 2nd cl. (एति)<BR>	 1. To go.<BR>	 2. To pervade.<BR>	 3. To conceive or become<BR>pregnant.<BR>	 4. To desire.<BR>	 5. To throw or direct.<BR>	 6. To eat. This root<BR>is not generally admitted, though it occurs in composition, as with<BR>उत् (उदीते) To appear. r. 4th cl. (ङ) ईङ् (ईयते) To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=110-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईक्ष
ईक्ष r. 1st cl. (ईक्षते) To see. It most usually occurs compounded with<BR>one or other of the prepositions, as with अप, to expect; with अभि,<BR>to gaze at; with अव, to inspect; with उत् or उप, to expect or<BR>await; with उप, to abandon; with निर्, to see; with परि, to try,<BR>to test, to assay; with प्र, to see, to resemble, or look like; with<BR>वि, to inspect; with प्रति, 1. to look for, to expect, 2. to venerate;<BR>with सम्, to compare, to contrast, to select; with प्रति and उत्, to<BR>look up at.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=110-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईक्षण|ईक्षणं
ईक्षण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Sight, seeing.<BR>	 2. An eye.<BR> E. ईक्ष् to see, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=110-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईक्षणिका
ईक्षणिका f. (-का) A female fortuneteller.<BR> E. ईक्षण seeing, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=110-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईक्षमाण
ईक्षमाण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Looking at, surveying.<BR> E. ईक्ष् to see, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=110-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईक्षित
ईक्षित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Seen, beheld.<BR> E. ईक्ष् and क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=110-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईख
ईख r. 1st cl. (ङ) (ईखति) To go.; also (इ) ईखि (ईंखति.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=110-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईज
ईज r. 1st cl. (ङ) (ईजते) 1. To go.<BR>	 2. To blame or censure; also (इञ्)<BR>ईजिञ् (ईंजति-ते.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=110-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईड
ईड r. 2nd cl. (ईट्टे) also 10th cl. (ईडयति) To praise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=110-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईडन|ईडनं
ईडन n. (-नं) Praising.<BR> E. ईड and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=110-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईडा
ईडा f. (-डा) Praise.<BR> E. ईड् to praise, क and टाप affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=110-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईडित|ईडितः
ईडित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Praised, commended.<BR> E. ईड् to praise, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=111-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईड्य
ईड्य mfn. (-ड्यः-ड्या-ड्यं) To be praised, to be glorified.<BR> E. ईड् to praise,<BR>क्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=111-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईढ
ईढ mfn. (-ढः-ढा-ढं) Sought.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=111-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईत
ईत r. 1st cl. (इ) ईति (ईंतति) To bind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=111-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईत
ईत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Gone.<BR> E. ई to go, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=111-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईति|ईतिः
ईति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Calamity of season, as drought, excessive rain, rats,<BR>foreign invasion, &c.<BR>	 2. Travelling in foreign countries, sojourning.<BR>3. An affray.<BR> E. ईङ् to go. affix क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=111-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईदृक्ष|ईदृक्षः
ईदृक्ष mfn. (-क्षः-क्षा-क्षं) Such.<BR> E. ई for इदम् this, दृश् to see, क्विन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=111-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईदृश्
ईदृश् mfn. (-दृक्) Such, so like.<BR> E. ई for इदम् this, दृश् with क्विप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=111-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईदृश|ईदृशः
ईदृश mfn. (-शः-शी-शं) Such, so like. E. As the last, with कञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=111-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईप्सन
ईप्सन n. (-नं) Desiring, wishing to obtain.<BR> E. आप् to obtain, desiderative<BR>form, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=111-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईप्सित
ईप्सित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Wished, desired.<BR> E. आप् to obtain, desiderative<BR>form, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=111-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईप्सु
ईप्सु mfn. (-प्सुः-प्सुः-प्सु) Desirous, wishing to get or obtain.<BR> E. आप् to ob-<BR>tain, desiderative form, उस् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=111-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईर|ईरः
ईर r. 2nd cl. (ईर्त्ते)<BR>	 1. To go.<BR>	 2. To shake. r. 1st and 10th cls. (ईरति,<BR>ईरयति)<BR>	 1. To go.<BR>	 2. To throw or direct, to drive or force on; with<BR>उत् prefixed, to say or speak; with प्र, to send, to make to go;<BR>with सम्, to go like the wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=111-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईयिवस्
ईयिवस् mfn. (-वान्-युषी-वस्)<BR>	 1. Gone, having gone.<BR>	 2. Having obtained.<BR>E. ईण् to go, क्वसु aff. form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=111-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईरिण|ईरिणं
ईरिण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>	 1. Desert.<BR>	 2. Saline and barren (soil.)<BR> E. ऋ to go,<BR>and इरन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=111-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईरित|ईरितं
ईरित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Sent, dispatched.<BR>	 2. Said, uttered.<BR>	 3. Gone.<BR>4. Made.<BR> E. ईर् to send, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=111-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईरिताकूत
ईरिताकूत n. (-तं) Declared purpose or intention.<BR> E. ईरित and आकूत<BR>purpose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=111-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईर्क्ष्य
ईर्क्ष्य r. 1st cl. (ईर्क्ष्यति) To envy, to feel impatient at another's<BR>prosperity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=111-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईर्म्म|ईर्म|ईर्मः
ईर्म्म n. (-र्म्मं) A sore or wound.<BR> E. ईर् to send, and मक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=111-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईर्य्या|ईर्या
ईर्य्या f. (-र्य्या) Wandering about as a religious mendicant.<BR> E. ईर् to go,<BR>affix क्यप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=111-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईर्व्वारु|ईर्वारु|ईर्वारुः|ईर्व्वारुः
ईर्व्वारु m. (-रुः) A cucumber, (Cucumis utilatissimus;) also ईर्व्वालु and<BR>ईर्व्वारु, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=111-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईर्षा
ईर्षा f. (-र्षा) Impatience, envy of another's success; more properly read ईर्ष्या.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=111-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईर्षालु|ईर्षालुः
ईर्षालु mfn. (-लुः-लुः-लु) Impatient of another's success, envious.<BR> E. ईर्षा<BR>and आलुच् affix: see ईर्ष्यालु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=111-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईर्षित
ईर्षित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Envied.<BR>	 n. (-तं) Envy.<BR> E. ईर्षा and इतच् affix, or<BR>ईर्ष् with क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=111-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईर्ष्य
ईर्ष्य r. 1st. cl. (ईर्ष्यति) To envy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=111-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईर्ष्य
ईर्ष्य mfn. (-र्ष्यः-र्ष्या-र्ष्यं) Envious, envying.<BR>	 f. (-र्ष्या)<BR>	 1. Envy or impatience<BR>of another's success.<BR>	 2. Spite, malice.<BR> E. ईर्ष्य to envy, and अच् and<BR>टाप affixes; also, but according to the best writers, inaccurately<BR>written ईर्षा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=111-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईर्ष्यक
ईर्ष्यक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Envious, envying.<BR> E. ईर्ष्य and वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=111-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईर्ष्यमाण
ईर्ष्यमाण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Envying, envious.<BR> E. ईर्ष्य and शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=111-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईर्ष्यालु|ईर्ष्यालुः
ईर्ष्यालु mfn. (-लुः-लुः-लु) Envious.<BR> E. ईर्ष्य and आलुच् affix; also written<BR>ईर्षालु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=111-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईर्ष्यावश
ईर्ष्यावश mfn. (-शः-शा-शं) Being overcome with envy.<BR> E. ईर्ष्या and वश<BR>subjection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=111-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईर्ष्यिन्
ईर्ष्यिन् mfn. (-र्ष्यी-र्ष्यिणी-र्ष्यि) Envious, spiteful.<BR> E. ईर्ष्या and इनि affix. So<BR>ईर्ष्यावत् (-वान्-वती-वत्) and ईर्ष्यामय (-यः-यी-यं.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=111-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईलि|ईलिः
ईलि f. (-लिः) See ईली.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=111-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईलित|ईलितः
ईलित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Praised.<BR> E. इड् to praise, affix क्त, and ड changed to ल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=111-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईली
ईली f. (-ली) A weapon, sometimes considered as a cudgel, and some-<BR>times as a short sword, or a stick shaped like a sword.<BR> E. ईर् to go,<BR>&c. क and ङीप् affixes, and र changed to ल; see इली; also ईलि, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=111-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईश|ईशं|ईशः
ईश r. 2nd cl. (ङ) ईशङ् (ईष्टे) To possess power, property, or authority.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=111-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईश|ईशं|ईशः
ईश m. (-शः)<BR>	 1. A name of ŚIVA.<BR>	 2. Also of the same deity as regent of<BR>the north-east quarter.<BR>	 3. A ruler, a master.<BR>	 f. (-शा) The shaft of a<BR>plough.<BR> E. ईश् to rule, क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=111-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईशसखि
ईशसखि m. (-खा) A name of KUVERA.<BR> E. ईश ŚIVA, and सखि a friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=111-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईशादन्त|ईशादन्तः
ईशादन्त m. (-न्तः)<BR>	 1. An elephant with large tusks.<BR>	 2. The tusk of an<BR>elephant.<BR> E. ईशा and दन्त a tooth; whose tooth is of the size of a<BR>plough-shaft, or the tooth which is so.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=111-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईशान|ईशानं|ईशानः
ईशान m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. A name of ŚIVA.<BR>	 2. Also of the same deity as regent of<BR>the north-east quarter.<BR>	 3. One of the Rudras.<BR>	 4. The sun as a form<BR>of ŚIVA.<BR>	 mf. (-नः-नी) The silk-cotton tree, (Bombax heptaphyllum.)<BR>	 n.<BR>(-नं) Light, splendor.<BR>	 f. (-नी) A name of DURGĀ.<BR> E. ईश a master, &c.<BR>and आनच् affix, and fem. ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=111-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईशिता
ईशिता f. (-ता) Superiority, supremacy, one of the eight attributes of<BR>divinity.<BR> E. ईश a master, and तल् abstract affix; also ईशित्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=111-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईशितृ
ईशितृ m. (-ता)<BR>	 1. A master, an owner or proprietor.<BR>	 2. A king.<BR> E. ईश् to<BR>rule, and तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=111-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईशित्व|ईशित्वं
ईशित्व n. (-त्वं) See ईशिता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=111-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईश्वर|ईश्वरं|ईश्वरः
ईश्वर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. The supreme ruler of the universe, GOD; it is therefore<BR>applied to all the different divinities, but mostly designates ŚIVA,<BR>in mythological and popular acceptation. According to the Sank-<BR>hyas, Iswara is the liberated spirit; finite, according to KAPILA;<BR>infinite, according to PATANJALI. In the Nyaya system, Iswara is<BR>also a finite spirit endowed with attributes. In the Vedanta, Iswara<BR>is infinite and universal spirit, the cause and substance of creation.<BR>2. A name of ŚIVA, especially in a compound, when the form<BR>of the deity implied is a Linga, as Visweswara, Someswara,<BR>Rameswara, &c.<BR>	 3. KĀMADEVA.<BR>	 mfn. (-रः-रा-री-रं)<BR>	 1. An owner,<BR>a proprietor, a chief or head.<BR>	 2. Able, competent.<BR>	 f. (-रा or -री)<BR>1. A name of DURGĀ.<BR>	 2. Of LAKṢMĪ, or of any other of the<BR>Śaktis or female energies of the deities.<BR> E. ईश् to rule, and वरट्<BR>or वरच् affix, consequently ङीप् or टाप् for the feminine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=111-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईश्वरभाव|ईश्वरभावः
ईश्वरभाव m. (-वः) Royal or imperial nature.<BR> E. ईश्वर a sovereign, and भाव<BR>disposition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=111-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईश्वरसभा
ईश्वरसभा f. (-भा) Royal court or assembly.<BR> E. ईश्वर and सभा an assembly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=111-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईश्वराधीन
ईश्वराधीन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Subject to a king, dependent on a master or<BR>on GOD, &c.<BR> E. ईश्वर, अधि over, ख aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=111-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईश्वराधीनता
ईश्वराधीनता f. (-ता) Dependence upon GOD, subjection to a ruler. E.<BR>ईश्वराधीन and तल् added; also with त्व, ईश्वराधीनत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=111-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईष|ईषः
ईष r. 1st cl. (ङ) ईषङ् (ईषते) 1. To go or move.<BR>	 2. To kill or hurt.<BR>	 3. To<BR>see.<BR>	 4. To give. (उ) ईषु (ईषति) To glean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=111-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईष|ईषः
ईष m. (-षः) The month Aswin: see इष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=111-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईषज्जल
ईषज्जल n. (-लं) Shallow water, a little water.<BR> E. ईषत् and जल water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=111-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईषत्
ईषत् ind. A little.<BR> E. ईष् to go, अत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=111-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईषत्कर|ईषत्करः
ईषत्कर mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>	 1. Diminutive, delicate.<BR>	 2. Doing little.<BR>	 3. What<BR>little is done to or made of.<BR> E. ईषत् a little, and कर what makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=111-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईषत्पान
ईषत्पान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) What is little drank or drank little of.<BR> E. ईषत्<BR>and पान drink.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=111-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईषत्प्रलम्भ
ईषत्प्रलम्भ mfn. (-म्भः-म्भा-म्भं) What is little gained of.<BR> E. ईषत् and प्रलम्भ profit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=111-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईषदुष्ण|ईषदुष्णं
ईषदुष्ण mfn. (-ष्णः-ष्णा-ष्णं) Tepid, slightly warm.<BR> E. ईषत् and उष्ण warm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=111-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईषद्गुण
ईषद्गुण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Of little merit.<BR> E. ईषत् and गुण quality.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=111-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईषत्पाण्डु|ईषत्पाण्डुः
ईषत्पाण्डु m. (-ण्डुः) A pale or light brown colour.<BR> E. ईषत् a little, and पाण्डु pale.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=111-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईषत्पुरुष|ईषत्पुरुषः
ईषत्पुरुष m. (-षः) A mean man.<BR> E. ईषत् and पुरुष a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=111-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईषदून
ईषदून mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Not quite complete or entire.<BR> E. ईषत् and ऊन less.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=111-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईषद्दर्शन
ईषद्दर्शन n. (-नं) A glance at, a slight inspection.<BR> E. ईषत् and दर्शन seeing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=111-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईषद्धास|ईषद्धासः
ईषद्धास m. (-सः) A smile.<BR> E. ईषत् a little, and हास laughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=111-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईषद्रक्त|ईषद्रक्तः
ईषद्रक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं) Of a pale red (colour.)<BR> E. ईषत् and रक्त red.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=111-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईषन्निमय
ईषन्निमय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Exchanged for a little.<BR> E. ईषत् and नियम barter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=111-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईषल्लभ
ईषल्लभ mfn. (-भः-भा-भं) What little is or can be gained of.<BR> E. ईषत and<BR>लभ what gets.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=111-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईषा
ईषा f. (-षा) The pole or shaft of a plough.<BR> E. ईष् to go, affixes क and<BR>टाप्; also ईशा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=112-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईषादण्ड|ईषादण्डः
ईषादण्ड m. (-ण्डः) The handle of a plough.<BR> E. ईषा the staff, and दण्ड a<BR>stick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=112-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईषादन्त|ईषादन्तः
ईषादन्त m. (-न्तः) An elephant with a large tusk or tooth.<BR> E. ईषा and दन्त<BR>a tooth: see ईशादन्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=112-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईषिका
ईषिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. An elephant's eyeball: see ईषीका.<BR>	 2. A painter's brush,<BR>&c. see ईषीका.<BR>	 3. A weapon, a dart or arrow.<BR> E. ईष् to hurt, किकन्<BR>affix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=112-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईषिर|ईषिरः
ईषिर m. (-रः) Fire.<BR> E. ईष् to injure, and किरच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=112-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईषीका
ईषीका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. A painter's brush, a fibrous stick used as one.<BR>	 2. An<BR>ingot mould.<BR>	 3. A dipping-rod, or something cast into a crucible to<BR>examine if the metal it contains is in fusion: see ईषिका.<BR> E. ईष् to<BR>go, ईकन् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=112-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईष्म|ईष्मः
ईष्म m. (-ष्मः)<BR>	 1. KĀMADEVA.<BR>	 2. Spring: see इष्म.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=112-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईह|ईहः
ईह r. 1st cl. (ङ) ईहङ् (ईहते) To endeavour, to aim or attempt. With<BR>सम् prefixed, to wish, to desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=112-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईहमान
ईहमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Performing, undertaking.<BR> E. ईह् to make effort,<BR>शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=112-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईहा
ईहा f. (-हा)<BR>	 1. Wish, desire.<BR>	 2. Effort, exertion.<BR> E. ईह् to desire, अङ् and<BR>टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=112-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईहातस्
ईहातस् ind. Diligently, energetically, by or with labour or exertion. E.<BR>तसि substituted for the regular case.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=112-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईहामृग|ईहामृगः
ईहामृग m. (-गः)<BR>	 1. A wolf.<BR>	 2. A division of the drama.<BR> E. ईहा wish,<BR>and मृग a deer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=112-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईहार्थिन्
ईहार्थिन् mfn. (-र्थी-र्थिनी-र्थि)<BR>	 1. Aiming at any object.<BR>	 2. Seeking wealth.<BR>E. इह् to seek, अर्थ wealth, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=112-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईहावृक|ईहावृकः
ईहावृक m. (-कः) A wolf.<BR> E. ईहा and वृक a wolf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=112-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईहित
ईहित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Sought, attempted, made effort for.<BR>	 2. Wished,<BR>desired.<BR> E. ईह् to wish, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=112-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उ|उः
उ The third short vowel of the Sanskrit alphabet, corresponding to<BR>the letter U, and pronounced as that is in the word full.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=112-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उ|उः
उ r. 1st cl. (ङ) उङ् (उवते) To sound, to make a particular sound or<BR>noise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=112-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उ|उः
उ ind. An interjection, 1. of assent; 2. of calling; 3. of compas-<BR>sion; 4. anger; and 5. of command.<BR>	 6. An expletive.<BR>	 m. (-उः)<BR>	 1.<BR>A name of ŚIVA.<BR>	 2. Of BRAHMĀ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=112-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उकनाह|उकनाहः
उकनाह m. (-हः) A horse of a red and yellow, or red and black colour,<BR>a bay or chesnut horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=112-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उकुण|उकुणः
उकुण m. (-णः) A bug. Also उत्कुण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=112-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उक्त|उक्तं|उक्तः
उक्त n. (-क्तं) A sentence.<BR>	 nf. (-क्तं-क्ता) A stanza of four lines with one<BR>syllabic instant, one long or two short syllables in each.<BR>	 mfn.<BR>(-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं) Spoken, said.<BR> E. वच् to speak, affix क्त and व changed<BR>to उ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=112-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उक्तवत्|उक्तवन्त्
उक्तवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Said, was saying.<BR> E. वच् to speak, क्तवतु affix<BR>of the past part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=112-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उक्तवाक्य
उक्तवाक्य mfn. (-क्यः-क्या-क्यं) One who has borne testimony or given an<BR>opinion.<BR>	 n. (-क्यं) A dictum, a decree.<BR> E. उक्त and वाक्य dictum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=112-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उक्ति|उक्तिः
उक्ति f. (-क्तिः) Speech, speaking.<BR> E. वच् to speak, and क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=112-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उक्तोपसंहार|उक्तोपसंहारः
उक्तोपसंहार m. (-रः) Any brief or compendious phrase or description. E.<BR>उक्त what is said, उपसंहार compendiousness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=112-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उक्त्वा
उक्त्वा ind. Having spoken or said.<BR> E. वच् to speak, क्त्वाच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=112-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उक्थ|उक्थं|उक्थः
उक्थ n. (-क्थं) The second or Sama Veda.<BR>	 f. (-क्था) A kind of metre,<BR>a stanza of four lines of one syllable each, the syllable may be<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=112-b" target="_blank">Page112-b+ 60</a>]<BR>one long or two short in quantity.<BR> E. वच् to speak, and थक् Uṇādi<BR>affix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=112-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उक्ष|उक्षः
उक्ष r. 1st. cl. (उक्षति)<BR>	 1. To sprinkle or wet.<BR>	 2. To clean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=112-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उक्ष|उक्षः
उक्ष mfn. (-क्षः-क्षा-क्षं)<BR>	 1. Cleansed, washed.<BR>	 2. Wet, moist.<BR> E. उक्ष् to wet, affix अप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=112-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उक्षतर|उक्षतरः
उक्षतर m. (-रः) A large bull or ox.<BR> E. उक्षन् an ox, and तरप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=112-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उक्षन्
उक्षन् m. (-क्षा) An ox or bull.<BR> E. उक्ष् to sprinkle, and कनिन् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=112-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उक्षाल|उक्षालः
उक्षाल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>	 1. Swift.<BR>	 2. Excellent.<BR>	 3. Terrible.<BR>	 4. High.<BR>5. Much.<BR>	 m. (-लः) A monkey.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=112-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उक्षित
उक्षित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Sprinkled.<BR>	 2. Cleansed, perfumed.<BR> E. उक्ष् to<BR>wet, and क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=112-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उख|उखः
उख r. 1st cl. (ओखति) (इ) उखि (उंखति) 1. To go, to move or approach.<BR>2. To dry, to wither.<BR>	 3. To adorn. The first retains the diphthong<BR>with a prefix ending in अ, as प्र and ओखति make प्रोखति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=112-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उखर्व्वल|उखर्वल|उखर्वलः|उखर्व्वलः
उखर्व्वल m. (-लः) A kind of grass, a sort of Andropogon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=112-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उखल|उखलः
उखल m. (-लः) A kind of grass, a sort of Andropogon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=112-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उखा
उखा f. (-खा) A pot or saucepan, &c.<BR> E. उख् to go, क affix, and टाप्,<BR>also उघा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=112-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उख्य|उख्यं|उख्यः
उख्य mfn. (-ख्यः-ख्या-ख्यं) Boiled, dressed in a pot, (flesh, &c.)<BR> E. उखा a pot and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=112-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उग्र|उग्रं|उग्रः
उग्र mfn. (-ग्रः-ग्रा-ग्रं)<BR>	 1. Angry, wrathful.<BR>	 2. Hot, sharp, pungent,<BR>acrid.<BR>	 3. Formidable, terrible.<BR>	 4. Cruel, flerce, savage.<BR>	 m. (-ग्रः)<BR>	 1. A<BR>name of ŚIVA.<BR>	 2. A name of a mixed tribe, from a Kṣatriya father<BR>and Śūdra mother: the employment of this caste according to<BR>Menu, is the killing or catching of animals that live in holes, as<BR>a snake-catcher, &c.; according to the Tantras, the Ugra is an en-<BR>comiast or bard.<BR>	 3. A tree, (Morunga hyperanthera, &c.)<BR>	 4. A<BR>class of asterisms, Magha Rharani, Purvaphalguni, Purvasharha,<BR>Purvabhadrapada.<BR>	 5. A name of Malabar.<BR>	 f. (-ग्रा)<BR>	 1. Orris root.<BR>	 2.<BR>A medicinal plant.<BR>	 3. An Ugra woman.<BR>	 n. (-ग्रं) Wrath, anger.<BR> E. उच्<BR>to accumulate, रन् Unādi affix, च is changed to ग.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=112-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उग्रकर्म्मन्|उग्रकर्मन्
उग्रकर्म्मन् mfn. (-र्म्मा-र्म्मा-र्म्म) Fierce, violent, cruel.<BR> E. उग्र and कर्म्मन् act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=112-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उग्रकाण्ड|उग्रकाण्डः
उग्रकाण्ड m. (-ण्डः) A sort of gourd, (Momordica charantia.)<BR> E. उग्र and<BR>काण्ड a stem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=112-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उग्रगन्ध|उग्रगंध|उग्रगन्धं|उग्रगन्धः
उग्रगन्ध mfn. (-न्धः-न्धा-न्धं) Strong smelling.<BR>	 m. (-न्धः)<BR>	 1. A plant,<BR>(Michelia champaca.)<BR>	 2. Garlic.<BR>	 n. (-न्धं) Asafœtida.<BR>	 f. (-न्धा)<BR>	 1. Com-<BR>mon caraway, (Carum carui, &c.) see अजमोदा.<BR>	 2. Orris root.<BR>	 3. A<BR>medicinal plant.<BR> E. उग्र violent, &c. and गन्ध scent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=112-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उग्रगन्धिन्
उग्रगन्धिन् mfn. (-न्धी-न्धिनी-न्धि) Strong smelling.<BR> E. उग्रगन्ध and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=112-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उग्रचय|उग्रचयः
उग्रचय m. (-यः) Desire.<BR> E. उग्र fierce, चय a heap.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=112-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उग्रत्व|उग्रत्वं
उग्रत्व n. (-त्वं)<BR>	 1. Violence, passionateness.<BR>	 2. Pungency acrimony.<BR> E. उग्र<BR>angry, and त्व; also with तल् affix. उग्रता f. (-ता.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=112-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उग्रदण्ड
उग्रदण्ड mfn. (-ण्डः-ण्डा-ण्डं) Relentless, remorseless.<BR> E. उग्र and दण्ड<BR>punishment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=112-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उग्रधन्वन्
उग्रधन्वन् m. (-न्वा) A name of INDRA.<BR> E. उग्र fierce, and धन्वन् a bowyer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=112-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उग्रनासिक|उग्रनासिकः
उग्रनासिक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Large-nosed.<BR> E. उग्र formidable, and नासिका<BR>a nose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=112-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उग्रम्पश्य|उग्रंपश्य
उग्रम्पश्य mfn. (-श्यः-श्या-श्यं)<BR>	 1. Frightful, hideous, fierce looking.<BR>	 2. Malig-<BR>nant, wicked.<BR> E. उग्र fierce, पश्य looking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=112-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उग्रशेखरा
उग्रशेखरा f. (-रा) A name of GANGA.<BR> E. उग्र ŚIVA, and शेखरा a crest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=112-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उग्रसेन|उग्रसेनः
उग्रसेन m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. The name of a prince, the father of DEVAKI and<BR>KANSA, and king of Mathura.<BR>	 2. The name of another prince,<BR>the son of PARIKSHIT.<BR> E. उग्र fierce, and सेना an army.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=112-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उग्रसेनज|उग्रसेनजः
उग्रसेनज m. (-जः) A name of KANSA, the uncle and enemy of KṚṢṆA.<BR>E. उग्रसेन and ज born; also उग्रसेनतनयः, उग्रसेनपुत्रः, उग्रसेनसुतः, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=112-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उङ्कुण|उंकुणः|उङ्कुणः
उङ्कुण m. (-णः) A bug: see उत्कुण.<BR> E. उ fear, and कुण a sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=112-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच
उच r. 4th cl. (उच्यति) To be conglomerate, to be gathered or assembled<BR>together, to unite or associate with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=112-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उचित|उचितं
उचित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Proper, suitable, convenient.<BR>	 2. Receivable, fit<BR>or right to be taken.<BR>	 3. Known, understood.<BR>	 4. Intrusted, deposited.<BR>5. Measured, adjusted, accurate.<BR> E. वच् to speak, and कितच् Unādi<BR>aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=112-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्च|उच्चं|उच्चः
उच्च mfn. (-च्चः-च्चा-च्चं) High, tall.<BR>	 m. (-च्चः) The apex of the orbit of a<BR>planet.<BR> E. उत् upwards, चि to gather, and ड aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=113-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चकैस्
उच्चकैस् ind. Excessively lofty, tall, loud, &c.<BR> E. उच्च high, कैस् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=113-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चघन|उच्चघनं
उच्चघन n. (-नं) Laughter in the mind not expressed in the countenance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=113-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चटा
उच्चटा f. (-टा)<BR>	 1. Pride, arrogance.<BR>	 2. Habit, usage.<BR>	 3. A kind of garlic.<BR>4. A species of grass, (a cyperus.)<BR>	 5. A shrub, (Abrus precatorius.)<BR>6. A sort of sorrel.<BR> E. उत् and चट् to injure, अच् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=113-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चण्ड|उच्चंड|उच्चण्डः
उच्चण्ड mfn. (-ण्डः-ण्डा-ण्डं)<BR>	 1. Quick, expeditious.<BR>	 2. Passionate, violent. E.<BR>उत् implying excess, चडि to be angry, and अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=113-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चतम
उच्चतम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं) Highest.<BR> E. उच्च and तमप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=113-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चतर
उच्चतर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Higher, more lofty.<BR> E. उच्च and तरप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=113-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चतरु|उच्चतरुः
उच्चतरु m. (-रुः)<BR>	 1. The cocoanut tree.<BR>	 2. Any lofty tree.<BR> E. उच्च and तरु<BR>a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=113-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चता
उच्चता f. (-ता) Height; also उच्चत्व n. (-त्वं)<BR> E. तल् or त्व added to उच्च.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=113-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चताल|उच्चतालं|उच्चतालः
उच्चताल n. (-लं) Music and dancing at feasts, drinking parties, &c.<BR> E. उच्च<BR>high sounding, and ताल tune.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=113-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चदेव|उच्चदेवः
उच्चदेव m. (-वः) A name of KṚṢṆA.<BR> E. उच्च high, above, and देव a deity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=113-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चदेवता
उच्चदेवता f. (-ता) Time personified, Chronos.<BR> E. उच्च high, and देवता divi-<BR>nity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=113-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चन्द्र|उच्चंद्र|उच्चंद्रः|उच्चन्द्रः
उच्चन्द्र m. (-न्द्रः) The end of the night, the last watch of the night.<BR> E. उत्<BR>priv. and चन्द्र the moon; moonset.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=113-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चभाषण
उच्चभाषण n. (-णं) Speaking loud.<BR> E. उच्च and भाषण speaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=113-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चय|उच्चयः
उच्चय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. The knot of the string or of the cloth which fastens<BR>the lower garments round the loins tied in front.<BR>	 2. The opposite<BR>leg of a triangle.<BR> E. उत् up, above, त्रि to gather, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=113-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चरण|उच्चरणं
उच्चरण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Uttering, articulating.<BR>	 2. Going up or out.<BR> E. उत् be-<BR>fore चर् to go, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=113-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चरित
उच्चरित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Uttered, articulated.<BR>	 2. Gone up or out.<BR> E. उत्<BR>before चर् to go, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=113-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चल|उच्चलं
उच्चल n. (-लं) The mind, the understanding.<BR> E. उत् above and चल what<BR>goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=113-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चलन|उच्चलनं
उच्चलन n. (-नं) Going up or out.<BR> E. उत् before चल् to go, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=113-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चललाटा
उच्चललाटा f. (-टा) A woman with a high or projecting forehead.<BR> E. उच्च<BR>high, and ललाट a forehead; also उच्चललाटिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=113-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चलित
उच्चलित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Gone up or out.<BR>	 2. Winnowed.<BR> E. उत् before<BR>चल् to go, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=113-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चाटन|उच्चाटनं|उच्चाटनः
उच्चाटन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Eradicating as a plant.<BR>	 2. Ruining, (as an individual.)<BR>3. Causing a person's ruin by magical incantations.<BR> E. उच्च up, and<BR>अटन going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=113-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चार|उच्चारः
उच्चार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Fœces, excrement.<BR>	 2. Pronounciation, utterance.<BR> E. उत्<BR>before चर् to go, and घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=113-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चारण|उच्चारणं
उच्चारण n. (-णं) Articulating, enunciation.<BR> E. उत् before चर् to go, causal<BR>form, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=113-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चारणज्ञ|उच्चारणज्ञः
उच्चारणज्ञ m. (-ज्ञः) A linguist, one skilled in languages or sounds. E.<BR>उच्चारण and ज्ञ who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=113-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चारणस्थान
उच्चारणस्थान n. (-नं) The part of the throat, &c. whence certain sounds,<BR>as nasals, gutturals, and the like proceed.<BR> E. उच्चारण and स्थान place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=113-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चारणार्थ
उच्चारणार्थ mfn. (-र्थः-र्था-र्थं) Necessary for pronounciation, a superfluous<BR>letter, &c. उच्चारण and अर्थ object.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=113-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चारित
उच्चारित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Pronounced, uttered, articulated.<BR> E. उत् before<BR>चर् to go, causal form, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=113-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चार्य्य|उच्चार्य
उच्चार्य्य ind. Having spoken or uttered.<BR>	 mfn. (-र्य्यः-र्य्या-र्य्यं) To be spoken, to<BR>be pronounced.<BR> E. उत् before चर् to go, causal form, affix ल्यप् or यत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=113-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चार्य्यमाण|उच्चार्यमाण
उच्चार्य्यमाण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Being uttered or pronounced.<BR> E. उच्चर, causal<BR>form, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=113-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चावच|उच्चावचः
उच्चावच mfn. (-चः-चा-चं)<BR>	 1. Various, multiform.<BR>	 2. Uneven, irregular,<BR>undulating.<BR>	 3. High and low.<BR> E. उदक् upper, and अवाक् lower,<BR>great and small, &c.; the compound is irregular.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=113-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चिकीर्षा
उच्चिकीर्षा f. (-र्षा) Desire or wish to collect.<BR> E. उत् before चि to collect,<BR>desiderative form, अङ् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=113-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चिङ्गट|उच्चिंगटः|उच्चिङ्गटः
उच्चिङ्गट m. (-टः)<BR>	 1. A sort of cricket.<BR>	 2. A passionate man.<BR> E. उत् like,<BR>and चिङ्गट a shrimp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=113-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चूल|उच्चूलः
उच्चूल m. (-लः) The flag or pennon of a banner.<BR> E. उत् above, and चूड to<BR>be high; ल is substituted for ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=113-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चैःश्रवस्
उच्चैःश्रवस् m. (-वाः) The horse of INDRA.<BR> E. उच्चैस् high, and श्रवस् an ear,<BR>long-eared; it is sometimes written with a final vowel, nom. (-सः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=113-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चैःस्वर|उच्चैःस्वरः
उच्चैःस्वर m. (-रः) A loud sound or voice.<BR> E. उच्चैस् and स्वर sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=113-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चैर्घुष्ट|उच्चैर्घुष्टं
उच्चैर्घुष्ट n. (-ष्टं) Making a loud noise, clamour.<BR> E. उच्चैस् high, loud,<BR>and घुष्ट sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=113-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चैस्
उच्चैस् ind. High, loud, great, much, &c.<BR> E. उत् much, चि to collect,<BR>डैस् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=113-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चैस्तम
उच्चैस्तम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>	 1. Very high, tall or lofty.<BR>	 2. Very loud. E.<BR>उच्चैस् and तमप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=113-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चैस्तमाम्
उच्चैस्तमाम् ind.<BR>	 1. Loudly, aloud.<BR>	 2. On high, high.<BR> E. आमु added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=113-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चैस्तर|उच्चैस्तरं
उच्चैस्तर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>	 1. Loftier.<BR>	 2. Louder.<BR> E. उच्चैस् and तरप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=113-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्यमान
उच्यमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) To be said.<BR> E. वच् to speak, pass. v. शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=113-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छ|उछ
उच्छ r. 1st and 6th cls. (इ) उच्छि (उञ्छतिः) 1. To glean.<BR>	 2. To gather<BR>little by little. (ई) उच्छी (उच्छति) or usually with वि prefixed (व्युच्छति)<BR>1. To end or terminate, to leave off.<BR>	 2. To finish or conclude.<BR>	 3. To<BR>pass or quit.<BR>	 4. To bind. With प्र, to wipe off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=113-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छन्न|उच्छन्नं
उच्छन्न mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं) Destroyed.<BR>	 m. (-न्नः) Peace obtained by ceding<BR>valuable lands.<BR> E. उत् before छद् to go, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=113-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छलत्|उच्छलन्त्
उच्छलत् mfn. (-लन्-लन्ती-लत्) Going or moving on or against.<BR> E. उत्, शक to<BR>go, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=113-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छलन|उच्छलनं
उच्छलन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Going upon.<BR>	 2. Having over, or above, or against. E.<BR>उत् before शल to go, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=113-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छादन|उच्छादनं
उच्छादन n. (-नं) Cleaning with perfumes.<BR> E. उत् before छद् to cover, in<BR>the causal form, and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=113-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छालित
उच्छालित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Waved, waved above.<BR>	 2. Gone, went.<BR>	 3.<BR>Shaken.<BR> E. उत् before शल् to go, causal form, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=113-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छास्त्रवर्त्तिन्|उच्छास्त्रवर्तिन्
उच्छास्त्रवर्त्तिन् mfn. (-र्त्ती-र्त्तिनी-र्त्ति) Transgressing, deviating from the<BR>ritual.<BR> E. उत् before शास्त्र scripture, वर्त्तिन् who abides.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=113-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छिख
उच्छिख mfn. (-खः-खा-खं)<BR>	 1. Flaming, blazing up.<BR>	 2. Radiant.<BR>	 3. High-<BR>crested.<BR> E. उत् up, शिखा a flame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=113-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छिङ्घन|उच्छिंघनं
उच्छिङ्घन n. (-नं) Breathing through the nostrils, snuffing, snoring.<BR> E. उत्<BR>before शिघि to smell, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=113-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छिद्य
उच्छिद्य ind. Having cut off, destroyed, killed, &c.<BR> E. उत् before छिद् to<BR>cut, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=113-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छिन्न|उच्छिन्नः
उच्छिन्न mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>	 1. Cut, cut off or out.<BR>	 2. Destroyed, killed.<BR> E. उद् before छिन्न cut.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=113-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छिलीन्ध्र|उच्छिलींध्र
उच्छिलीन्ध्र n. (-न्ध्रं) A mushroom.<BR> E. उत् and शिलीन्ध्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=113-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छिष्ट|उच्छिष्टं
उच्छिष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>	 1. Left, rejected as food; (i. e. spit out of the<BR>mouth, or orts, crumbs, fragments, &c.)<BR>	 2. Left, abandoned.<BR> E. उत्<BR>up, शिष् to leave as a residue, and क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=113-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छिष्टभोजन|उच्छिष्टभोजनः
उच्छिष्टभोजन m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. One who eats another's leavings.<BR>	 2. The at-<BR>tendant upon an idol, whose food is the leavings of the deities.<BR>E. उच्छिष्ट orts, and भोजन food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=113-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छिष्टभोजिन्
उच्छिष्टभोजिन् mfn. (-जी-जिनी-जि) Who eats the remains of a meal. E.<BR>उच्छिष्ट and भोजिन् who eats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=113-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छिष्टमोदन|उच्छिष्टमोदनं
उच्छिष्टमोदन n. (-नं) Wax.<BR> E. उच्छिष्ट and मोदन pleasing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=113-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छिष्टान्न
उच्छिष्टान्न n. (-न्नं) Leavings, offal.<BR> E. उच्छिष्ट and अन्न food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=113-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छीर्षक|उच्छीर्षकं
उच्छीर्षक n. (-कं) A pillow.<BR> E. उत् upon, and शीर्षक the head: on which<BR>rests the head.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=113-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छुष्क
उच्छुष्क mfn. (-ष्कः-ष्का-ष्कं) Dry, dried up, withered.<BR> E. उत् before शुष्क dried.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=113-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छूडा
उच्छूडा f. (-डा) The head of a banner or part above the flag with erect<BR>ornaments.<BR> E. उत् up, छूडा crest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=113-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छून|उच्छूनं
उच्छून mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>	 1. Swollen, turgid.<BR>	 2. Lofty, high.<BR>	 3. Fat, bulky.<BR>E. उत् up, श्वि to increase, क्त affix, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=113-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छृङ्खल|उच्छृंखल|उच्छृङ्खलं
उच्छृङ्खल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>	 1. Unrestrained, perverse, self-willed.<BR>	 2. Irre-<BR>gular, desultory, unmethodical.<BR> E. उत् priv. and शृङ्खला a chain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=113-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छेद|उच्छेदः
उच्छेद m. (-दः)<BR>	 1. Cutting off or out.<BR>	 2. Destroying, destruction.<BR>	 3.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=114-a" target="_blank">Page114-a+ 60</a>]<BR>Cutting short, putting an end to 4. Excision.<BR> E. उत् and छिद् to<BR>cut, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=113-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छेषण|उच्छेषणं
उच्छेषण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Rest, remainder.<BR>	 2. Leavings.<BR> E. उत् and शेषण remaining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=114-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छोषण
उच्छोषण mfn. (-णः-णी-णं) What dries up or withers.<BR>	 n. (-णं) Drying up,<BR>parching.<BR> E. उत् and शोषण drying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=114-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छ्रय|उच्छ्रयः
उच्छ्रय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. Height, elevation of a tree, mountain, &c.<BR>	 2. Rising<BR>of a planet, &c.<BR>	 3. Upright side of a triangle.<BR> E. उत् up, श्रिञ् to<BR>serve, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=114-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छ्राय|उच्छ्रायः
उच्छ्राय m. (-यः) Height, elevation.<BR> E. उत् before श्रि to serve, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=114-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छ्रायिन्
उच्छ्रायिन् mfn. (-यी-यिणी-यि) High, raised, lofty.<BR> E. उच्छ्राय and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=114-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छ्रित|उच्छ्रितं
उच्छ्रित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Born, produced.<BR>	 2. High, tall.<BR>	 3. Lifted up,<BR>raised.<BR>	 4. Prosperous, advancing, increasing, rising.<BR>	 5. Left, aban-<BR>doned.<BR>	 6. Increased in size or bulk, grown.<BR> E. उत् before श्रिञ् to<BR>serve, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=114-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छ्रिति|उच्छ्रितिः
उच्छ्रिति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Height, elevation.<BR>	 2. The upright side of a triangle.<BR>E. उत् before श्रि to serve, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=114-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छ्रेय
उच्छ्रेय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) High, lofty.<BR> E. उत् before श्रि to serve, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=114-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छ्वसन|उच्छ्वसनं
उच्छ्वसन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Breathing.<BR>	 2. Sighing.<BR> E. उत् before श्वस् to breathe,<BR>affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=114-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छ्वसित|उच्छ्वसितं
उच्छ्वसित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Blown, expanded.<BR>	 2. Breathed, inspired.<BR>	 3.<BR>Sighing.<BR> E. उत् much, &c. श्वसित breathed, blown.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=114-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छ्वास|उच्छ्वासः
उच्छ्वास m. (-सः)<BR>	 1. Breath, breathing, inspiration.<BR>	 2. A sigh.<BR>	 3. Consola-<BR>tion, encouragement.<BR>	 4. Division of a book.<BR> E. उत् up, and श्वस् to<BR>breathe, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=114-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उज्जयनी
उज्जयनी f. (-नी) Ujjayani or Oujein, a city so called in Malabar, formerly<BR>the capital of VIKRAMADITYA. It is one of the seven sacred cities<BR>of the Hindus, and the first meridian of their geographers: the<BR>modern Oujein is about a mile south of the ancient city.<BR> E. उत्<BR>much, जयनी victorious or place of victory; from the military cha-<BR>racter of its people; also अवन्ती and उज्जयिनी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=114-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उज्जयन्त|उज्जयन्तः
उज्जयन्त m. (-न्तः) The name of a mountain, part of the chain in the<BR>west of India, part of the Vindhyan range: see रैवत.<BR> E. उत priv. and<BR>जयन्ति a banner, or जयन्त the son of INDRA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=114-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उज्जयिनी
उज्जयिनी f. (-नी) The city Oujein. E. See उज्जयनी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=114-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उज्जासन|उज्जासनं
उज्जासन n. (-नं) Killing, slaughter.<BR> E. उत् before जस् to kill, and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=114-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उज्जिहीर्षा
उज्जिहीर्षा f. (-र्षा) Wishing to take or seize.<BR> E. उत् before हृ to take, desid.<BR>form, अङ् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=114-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उज्जृम्भ|उज्जृंभ|उज्जृम्भं|उज्जृम्भः
उज्जृम्भ mfn. (-म्भः-म्भा-म्भं)<BR>	 1. Blown, expanded.<BR>	 2. Open, apart.<BR> E. उत् up,<BR>and जृभि to gape, अप् affix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=114-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उज्जृम्भित|उज्जृंभित|उज्जृम्भितं
उज्जृम्भित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Blown, expanded.<BR>	 2. Opened, stretched.<BR>	 n.<BR>(-तं) Effort, exertion.<BR> E. उत् before जृभि to yawn, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=114-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उज्ज्वल|उज्ज्वलं|उज्ज्वलः
उज्ज्वल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>	 1. Luminous, splendid, light.<BR>	 2. Lovely, beauti-<BR>ful.<BR>	 3. Clean, clear.<BR>	 4. Blown, expanded.<BR>	 5. Burning, blazing.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-लः) Love, passion.<BR>	 n. (-लं) Gold.<BR> E. उत् much, ज्वल to shine, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=114-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उज्ज्वलता
उज्ज्वलता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Splendour, radiance.<BR>	 2. Beauty.<BR> E. तल added to the<BR>last; also with त्व, उज्ज्वलत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=114-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उज्ज्वलन|उज्ज्वलनं
उज्ज्वलन n. (-नं) Burning or shining.<BR> E. उत् before ज्वल to shine, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=114-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उज्ज्वलित
उज्ज्वलित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Lighted, shining, flaming, &c.<BR> E. उत् before<BR>ज्वल to shine, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=114-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उञ्छ|उञ्छं|उंछः|उञ्छः
उञ्छ n. (-ञ्छं) Gathering grains.<BR> E. उछि to glean, and घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=114-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उञ्छन|उंछनं|उञ्छनं
उञ्छन n. (-नं) Gathering grains of corn in market places, &c. gleaning.<BR>E. उछि to glean, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=114-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उञ्छवृत्ति
उञ्छवृत्ति mfn. (-त्तिः-त्तिः-त्ति) A gleaner, one who lives by gleaning. E.<BR>उञ्छ and वृत्ति practice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=114-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उञ्छशिल|उञ्छशिलं
उञ्छशिल n. (-लं) Gleaning corn or grains.<BR> E. उञ्छ gathering grain, and<BR>शिल gleaning corn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=114-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उञ्छशील|उञ्छशीलः
उञ्छ-शील mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) One who lives by gleaning, &c.<BR> E. उञ्छ and शील who practices.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=114-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उज्झ|उज्झः
उज्झ r. 6th cl. (उज्झति) To quit or abandon. This is sometimes read<BR>उद्झ. With प्र, to escape or avoid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=114-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उज्झ|उज्झः
उज्झ m. (-ज्झः) Abandoning, leaving.<BR> E. उज्झ and क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=114-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उज्झित|उज्झितं
उज्झित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Left, abandoned.<BR>	 2. Left off, discontinued. E.<BR>उज्झ to leave, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=114-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उज्झितृ
उज्झितृ mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ) Who or what leaves.<BR> E. उज्झ and तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=114-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उट|उटं|उटः
उट m. (-टः) Leaves, grass, &c. used in making huts, thatches, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=114-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उटज|उटजः
उटज m. (-जः)<BR>	 1. A hut made of leaves, the residence of hermits or<BR>saints.<BR>	 2. A house in general.<BR> E. उट thatch, &c. and ज made.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=114-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उठ
उठ r. 1st cl. (ओठति) To strike or knock down; also ऊठ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=114-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उडु|उडुः
उडु fn. (-डुः-डु) A lunar mansion or constellation in the moon's path.<BR>	 n.<BR>(डु) Water.<BR> E. उत् above, डीङ् to go or fly, डु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=114-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उडुप|उडुपः
उडुप mn. (-पः-पं) A raft or float.<BR>	 m. (-पः) The moon.<BR> E. उडु as above,<BR>and प from पा to preserve, affix ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=114-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उडुपति|उडुपतिः
उडुपति m. (-तिः) The moon.<BR> E. उडु and पति lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=114-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उडुपथ|उडुपथः
उडुपथ m. (-थः) The firmament.<BR> E. उडु a constellation, and पथ a path.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=114-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उडुम्बर|उडुंबर|उडुम्बरं|उडुंबरः|उडुम्बरः
उडुम्बर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Glomerous fig tree, (Ficus glomerata, Rox.)<BR>	 2. The<BR>threshold of a house.<BR>	 3. A eunuch.<BR>	 4. A species of leprosy with<BR>coppery spots.<BR>	 5. A kind of worm, supposed to be generated in<BR>the blood, and to produce leprosy.<BR>	 n. (-र)<BR>	 1. Copper.<BR>	 2. A Karṣa,<BR>a measure of two Tolas.<BR> E. उडु a constellation in the second case, वृ<BR>to screen, and अप् affix; it is also written ऊडुम्बर and उदुम्बर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=114-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उडुम्बरपर्णी
उडुम्बरपर्णी f. (-र्णी) The name of a plant: see दन्ती.<BR> E. उडुम्बर and पर्ण a<BR>leaf: whose leaves are of the color of copper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=114-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उडूप|उडूपः
उडूप mn. (-पः-पं) A raft, a float.<BR>	 m. (-पः) The moon: see उडुप.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=114-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उड्डयन|उड्डयनं
उड्डयन n. (-नं) Flying, soaring.<BR> E. उत् before डी to fly, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=114-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उड्डामर|उड्डामरं
उड्डामर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Excellent, respectable, of rank or consequence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=114-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उड्डीन|उड्डीनं
उड्डीन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Flown up, flying up.<BR>	 n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Flying as a bird.<BR>2. Flying up, soaring.<BR> E. उत् up, and डी to fly, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=114-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उड्डीयमान|उड्डीयमानः
उड्डीयमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Flying, soaring, who flies or soars.<BR> E. उत् up,<BR>डी to fly, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=114-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उड्डीश|उड्डीशः
उड्डीश m. (-शः)<BR>	 1. A work so called, containing charms and incanta-<BR>tions.<BR>	 2. A name of ŚIVA.<BR> E. उत् up, and डी to fly, Unādi affix श.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=114-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उण्डेरक|उंडेरक|उंडेरकः|उण्डेरकः
उण्डेरक m. (-कः) A ball of flour, a roll, a loaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=114-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उण्डेरकस्रज्
उण्डेरकस्रज् f. (-स्रक्) A string of rolls, balls of meal or flour upon a string.<BR>E. उण्डेरक and स्रज् a chaplet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=114-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उढ्र
उढ्र m. (-ढ्रः)<BR>	 1. Water.<BR>	 2. The China rose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=114-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्
उत् ind. An interjection of, 1. asking, (how, what?)<BR>	 2. of deliberation,<BR>(either, or;)<BR>	 3. of extreme doubt, (hey! what!)<BR>	 4. Up, above, on,<BR>upon; see उद्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=114-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत|उतं
उत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Sewn, woven.<BR> E. ऊय to sew, affix क्त. Ind. A particle<BR>of, 1. doubt, (what!)<BR>	 2. of interrogation, (what, how?)<BR>	 3. of con-<BR>nexion, (also, and;)<BR>	 4. of deliberation, (either, or.)<BR>	 5. It is also an<BR>expletive.<BR> E. ऊङ् to sound, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=114-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उतथ्य|उतथ्यः
उतथ्य m. (-थ्यः) The name of a Muni, son of ANGIRAS.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=114-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उतथ्यानुज|उतथ्यानुजः
उतथ्यानुज m. (-जः) A name of VṚHASPATI, regent of the planet Jupiter.<BR>E. उतथ्य and अनुज younger born; the younger brother of UTATHYA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=114-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उतथ्यानुजन्मन्
उतथ्यानुजन्मन् m. (-न्मा) VṚHASPATI. E. See the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=114-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उताहो
उताहो ind. A particle implying, 1. deliberation, (either or;)<BR>	 2. asking<BR>(how, what?)<BR> E. उत् and आहो meaning as before.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=114-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उताहोस्वित्
उताहोस्वित् ind. A particle of doubt or deliberation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=114-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्क|उत्कः
उत्क mfn. (-त्कः-त्का-त्कं)<BR>	 1. Regretting, sad, sorrowful.<BR>	 2. Absent, think-<BR>ing of something else.<BR>	 4. Wishing for, desirous of.<BR>	 m. (-त्कः) Op-<BR>portunity, occasion.<BR> E. उत् up, away, and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=114-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कट|उत्कटं|उत्कटः
उत्कट mfn. (-टः-टा-टं)<BR>	 1. Much, excessive.<BR>	 2. Drunk, mad, furious.<BR>3. Proud, haughty.<BR>	 4. Uneven.<BR>	 5. Difficult.<BR>	 6. Superior, high.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-टः)<BR>	 1. Intoxication, pride.<BR>	 2. An elephant in rut.<BR>	 3. Sara grass,<BR>(Saccharum sara.)<BR>	 n. (-टं)<BR>	 1. Woody cassia or its bark.<BR>	 2. Sarsapa-<BR>rilla.<BR> E. उत् high, great, and कटच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=114-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कटुकासन|उत्कटुकासनं
उत्कटुकासन n. (-नं) Sitting on the hams, squatting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=114-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कण्ठा|उत्कंठा
उत्कण्ठा f. (-ण्ठा) Regretting, missing anything or person.<BR> E. उत् much,<BR>कठि to be sad, अङ् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=114-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कण्ठित|उत्कंठित|उत्कण्ठितं
उत्कण्ठित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Regretting, wishing or sorrowing for, distress-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=115-a" target="_blank">Page115-a+ 60</a>]<BR>ed, sorrowful.<BR>	 f. (-ता) A Woman whose husband or lover is absent.<BR>E. उत् much, कठि to be sad, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=114-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कता
उत्कता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. A plant with aromatic seeds. (Pothos officinalis, Rox.)<BR>See गजपिप्पली.<BR>	 2. Regretting, sorrowing for.<BR> E. उत्क regretting, and<BR>तल् abstract aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=115-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कन्धरम्
उत्कन्धरम् ind. Bending back the neck.<BR> E. उत् up, कन्धर the neck.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=115-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कर|उत्करः
उत्कर mfn. (-रः-रा-री-रं)<BR>	 1. What lifts or raises.<BR>	 2. What piles or heaps,<BR>what makes up.<BR>	 m. (-रः) A heap, a pile, a stack, &c.<BR> E. उत् up, and<BR>कर what makes, from कृ and ट or अप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=115-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्करिका
उत्करिका f. (-का) A sort of sweetmeat made with milk, treacle, and<BR>ghee.<BR> E. उत्कर and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=115-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्करीय
उत्करीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Relating or belonging to a heap, &c.<BR> E. उत्कर<BR>and छ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=115-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कर्त्तन|उत्कर्तन|उत्कर्तनं
उत्कर्त्तन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Cutting over or on.<BR>	 2. Cutting to pieces.<BR>	 3. Cutting<BR>off.<BR> E. उत् before कृत् to cut, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=115-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कर्ष|उत्कर्षः
उत्कर्ष mfn. (-र्षः-र्षा-र्षं)<BR>	 1. Superior, eminent.<BR>	 2. Much, excessive.<BR>	 3. At-<BR>tractive, drawing.<BR>	 m. (-र्षः)<BR>	 1. Excellence, eminence.<BR>	 2. Excess.<BR>3. Increase.<BR>	 4. Pulling, pulling up or to.<BR> E. उत् much, कृष् to mark<BR>घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=115-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कल|उत्कलं|उत्कलः
उत्कल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) A porter, one who travels with a burden or load.<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. A country in the south of India, part of Orissa.<BR>	 2. A<BR>fowler, a bird-catcher.<BR> E. उत् before and कल् to go, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=115-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कलिका
उत्कलिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. Regretting, missing anything or person.<BR>	 2. A bud,<BR>an unblown flower.<BR>	 3. A wave.<BR>	 4. Wanton sportfulness, dalliance.<BR>E. उत् before कल् to go, वुन् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=115-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कलित|उत्कलितः
उत्कलित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Regretting, grieving for.<BR>	 2. Prosperous,<BR>rising, increasing.<BR> E. उत् up, and कल् to go or count; part.<BR>affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=115-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्काका
उत्काका f. (-का) A cow calving every year.<BR> E. उत्क regretting, and अक्<BR>to go, अच् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=115-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कार|उत्कारः
उत्कार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Winnowing corn.<BR>	 2. Piling it up.<BR> E. उत् up, and कॄ to<BR>scatter, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=115-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कारिका
उत्कारिका f. (-का) A poultice.<BR> E. उत् before कृ to make, causal form,<BR>वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=115-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कासन|उत्कासनं
उत्कासन n. (-नं) Hemming, clearing the throat of mucus.<BR> E. उत् up, and<BR>कासन coughing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=115-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कुञ्चिता|उत्कुंचिता
उत्कुञ्चिता f. (-ता) Kalonji, (Nigella Indica, Rox.)<BR> E. उत् up, कुञ्च् to<BR>go crookedly, क्त affix, or with वुन् affix उत्कुञ्चिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=115-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कीर्त्तन|उत्कीर्तन|उत्कीर्तनं
उत्कीर्त्तन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Praising, celebrating.<BR>	 2. Crying, proclaiming. E.<BR>उत् before कीर्त्त to praise, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=115-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कीर्त्तित|उत्कीर्तित
उत्कीर्त्तित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Praised, renowned.<BR>	 2. Proclaimed, pro-<BR>mulgated.<BR> E. उत् aloud, कीर्त्त to praise, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=115-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कुट|उत्कुटं
उत्कुट n. (-टं) Sleeping with the head erect.<BR> E. उत् neg. and कुट् to be<BR>crooked, क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=115-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कुण|उत्कुणः
उत्कुण m. (-णः) A bug.<BR> E. उत् high, loud, and कुण् to call, क affix; also<BR>उङ्कुण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=115-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कूट|उत्कूटं|उत्कूटः
उत्कूट m. (-टः) An umbrella or parasol.<BR> E. उत् priv. कूट् to heat, क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=115-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कूलित
उत्कूलित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Brought to the bank or shore.<BR> E. उत् before कूल<BR>a bank, nominative verb, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=115-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कृति|उत्कृतिः
उत्कृति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Cutting up.<BR>	 2. A form of metre, a stanza of four<BR>lines of twenty-six syllables each.<BR> E. उत् and कृति another metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=115-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कृत्य
उत्कृत्य ind. Having cut off, or up.<BR> E. उत् before कृत् to cut, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=115-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कृत्यमान
उत्कृत्यमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Being cut to pieces.<BR> E. उत् before कृत् to cut,<BR>शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=115-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कृष्ट|उत्कृष्टं
उत्कृष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>	 1. Excellent, eminent.<BR>	 2. Superior, best.<BR>	 3.<BR>Much, most, excessive.<BR>	 4. Drawn, attracted.<BR> E. उत् before कृष् to<BR>drag, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=115-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कृष्टता
उत्कृष्टता f. (-ता) Excellence, superiority, eminence.<BR> E. उत्कृष्ट with तल्<BR>added; also त्व, उत्कृष्टत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=115-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कृष्टभूम|उत्कृष्टभूमः
उत्कृष्टभूम m. (-मः) A good soil.<BR> E. उत्कृष्ट excellent and भूमि earth, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=115-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कृष्टवेदन
उत्कृष्टवेदन n. (-नं) The best or most respectable form of marriage. E.<BR>उत्कृष्ट and वेदन marrying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=115-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कोच|उत्कोचः
उत्कोच mf. (-चः-चा) A bribe.<BR> E. उत् before कुच् to be crooked, क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=115-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कोचक|उत्कोचकः
उत्कोचक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. The receiver of a bribe.<BR>	 2. A bribe.<BR> E. उत् before<BR>कुच् to be crooked, वुन् affix or कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=115-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्क्रम|उत्क्रमः
उत्क्रम m. (-मः)<BR>	 1. Going up or out.<BR>	 2. Progressive increase.<BR>	 3. Going<BR>astray, acting improperly, deviation, transgression.<BR> E. उत् before<BR>क्रम् to go, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=115-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्क्रमण|उत्क्रमणं
उत्क्रमण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Going up or out.<BR>	 2. Surpassing, exceeding.<BR> E. उत्<BR>before क्रम् to go, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=115-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्क्रान्त|उत्क्रांत
उत्क्रान्त mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं)<BR>	 1. Passed, surpassed, gone over or beyond.<BR>	 2.<BR>Gone forth or out.<BR>	 3. Trespassing, exceeding.<BR> E. उत् before क्रम् to<BR>go, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=115-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्क्रान्तिन्|उत्क्रांतिन्
उत्क्रान्तिन् mfn. (-न्ती-न्तिनी-न्ति) Passing, passing away, gone, departed.<BR> E. उत्क्रान्त and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=115-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्क्राम|उत्क्रामः
उत्क्राम m. (-मः)<BR>	 1. Opposition, contrariety.<BR>	 2. Going, going above, sur-<BR>passing.<BR>	 3. Going from or out.<BR>	 4. Deviating from propriety, trans-<BR>gressing.<BR> E. उत् out, क्रम् to go, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=115-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्क्रामत्
उत्क्रामत् mfn. (-मन्-मन्ती-मत्)<BR>	 1. Going over or above, surpassing.<BR>	 2. Coing out.<BR>E. उत् before क्रम् to go, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=115-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्क्रुष्ट
उत्क्रुष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं) Crying, speaking out or aloud, (who or what<BR>does so.)<BR>	 n. (-ष्टं)<BR>	 1. Crying out, calling, exclaiming.<BR>	 2. Conversa-<BR>tion.<BR> E. उत् before क्रुश् to cry, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=115-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्क्रोश|उत्क्रोशः
उत्क्रोश m. (-शः)<BR>	 1. An osprey.<BR>	 2. Clamour, proclamation.<BR> E. उत् loud,<BR>क्रुश् to cry, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=115-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्क्लेद|उत्क्लेदः
उत्क्लेद m. (-दः) Nausea, sickness.<BR> E. उत् before and क्लेद moisture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=115-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्क्लेश|उत्क्लेशः
उत्क्लेश m. (-शः) Nausea, sickness.<BR> E. उत् before क्लेश distress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=115-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्क्षिप्त|उत्क्षिप्तः
उत्क्षिप्त mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं)<BR>	 1. Thrown upwards, tossed.<BR>	 2. Thrown out,<BR>ejected.<BR>	 3. Vomited.<BR>	 4. Rejected, dismissed.<BR>	 m. (-प्तः) Thorn apple,<BR>(Datura metel and fastuosa.)<BR> E. उत् up, and क्षिप्त thrown; in the<BR>last sense it alludes to the intoxicating qualities of the plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=115-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्क्षिप्तिका
उत्क्षिप्तिका f. (-का) An ornament in the shape of a crescent worn in the<BR>upper part of the ear.<BR> E. उत् up, क्षिप् to send, affix क्तिन्; to which<BR>कन् and टाप् are then added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=115-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्क्षेप|उत्क्षेपः
उत्क्षेप m. (-पः)<BR>	 1. Throwing or tossing up.<BR>	 2. Throwing away.<BR>	 3. Send-<BR>ing, dispatching.<BR>	 4. Bringing up, vomiting.<BR> E. उत् before क्षिपि to<BR>throw, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=115-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्क्षेपक|उत्क्षेपकः
उत्क्षेपक mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>	 1. Throwing, a thrower, what or who elevates<BR>or raises.<BR>	 2. Who sends or orders.<BR>	 m. (-कः) A stealer of clothes,<BR>&c.<BR> E. उत् before क्षिप् to throw, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=115-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्क्षेपण|उत्क्षेपणं
उत्क्षेपण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. A fan.<BR>	 2. A kind of basket or bowl used for clean-<BR>ing corn.<BR>	 3. Throwing upwards, tossing.<BR>	 4. Sending, sending away.<BR>5. Vomiting.<BR>	 6. Taking up.<BR>	 7. A measure of sixteen Paṇas<BR> E. उत<BR>up, क्षिप् to throw or send, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=115-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्खला
उत्खला f. (-ला) A kind of perfume: see मुरा.<BR> E. उत् before खल् to<BR>gather, अच् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=115-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्खात|उत्खातं
उत्खात mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Eradicated, pulled up by the roots.<BR>	 2. De-<BR>stroyed, annihilated.<BR> E. उत् up, खन् to dig, and क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=115-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्त|उत्तं
उत्त mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं) Wet, moistened.<BR> E. उन्द् to wet, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=115-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तंस|उत्तंसः
उत्तंस mn. (-सः-सं)<BR>	 1. An earring.<BR>	 2. A crest.<BR> E. उत् much, and तसि a<BR>Sautra root, to ornament, affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=115-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तप्त|उत्तप्तं|उत्तप्तः
उत्तप्त mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं)<BR>	 1. Burnt, seared.<BR>	 2. Bathed, washed.<BR>	 3. Anxious,<BR>excited.<BR>	 n. (-प्तं) Dried flesh.<BR> E. उत् much, or in the last sense priv.<BR>and तप्त heated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=115-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तम|उत्तमः
उत्तम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>	 1. Chief, principal, first, best.<BR>	 2. Greatest, high-<BR>est.<BR>	 m. (-मः)<BR>	 1. The third Manu, son of PRIYAVRATA.<BR>	 2. The best<BR>kind of lover or hero.<BR>	 f. (-मा)<BR>	 1. An excellent woman: one who is<BR>handsome, healthy, and affectionate.<BR>	 4. A plant, (Asclepias rosea.)<BR>E. उत् much, तम् to desire, affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=115-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तमपुरुष|उत्तमपुरुषः
उत्तमपुरुष m. (-षः)<BR>	 1. The first person, (in grammar.)<BR>	 2. An excellent<BR>man.<BR> E. उत्तम and पुरुष man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=115-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तमफलिनी
उत्तमफलिनी f. (-नी) A plant, (Asclepias rosea, Rox.) See दुग्धिका.<BR> E. उत्तम<BR>best, फल fruit, इनि affix, and ङीप् fem. do.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=116-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तमर्ण|उत्तमर्णः
उत्तमर्ण mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-र्णं) A creditor.<BR> E. उत्तम chief, and ऋण a debt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=116-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तमर्णिक
उत्तमर्णिक m. (-कः) A creditor.<BR> E. उत्तम, ऋण a debt, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=116-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तमर्णिन्
उत्तमर्णिन् m. (-र्णी) A creditor.<BR> E. उत्तम, ऋण a debt, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=116-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तमलाभ|उत्तमलाभः
उत्तमलाभ m. (-भः) Great profit, a double return.<BR> E. उत्तम and लाभ gain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=116-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तमसंग्रह
उत्तमसंग्रह m. (-हः) Intriguing with another man's wife, addressing her<BR>privately, casting amorous looks, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=116-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तमसाहस|उत्तमसाहसः
उत्तमसाहस n. (-सं)<BR>	 1. The highest of the three fixed mulcts or fines;<BR>a fine of 1,000 or of 80,000 Paṇas.<BR>	 2. Capital punishment, brand-<BR>ing, banishment, confiscation, mutilation and death.<BR> E. उत्तम the<BR>best or greatest, साहस infliction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=116-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तमाङ्ग|उत्तमांग|उत्तमाङ्गं
उत्तमाङ्ग n. (-ङ्गं) The head.<BR> E. उत्तम chief, and अङ्ग member.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=116-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तमार्द्ध्य
उत्तमार्द्ध्य n. (-र्द्ध्यं) The best half.<BR> E. उत्तम, अर्द्ध half, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=116-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तमाह|उत्तमाहः
उत्तमाह m. (-मः) A fine day, a lucky day.<BR> E. उत्तम best, अहन् a day, ट aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=116-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तमोपपद
उत्तमोपपद mfn. (-दः-दा-दं) Best, good.<BR> E. उत्तम and उपपद secondary<BR>term, to whom or what the best term is applicable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=116-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तमौजस्
उत्तमौजस् m. (-जाः) A proper name, one of the warriors of the Maha-<BR>bharata.<BR> E. उत्तम and ओजस् strength.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=116-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तम्भन|उत्तंभन|उत्तंभनं
उत्तम्भन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Upholding, supporting, staying.<BR>	 2. Stopping, arrest-<BR>ing.<BR> E. उत् before ष्टभि to stop, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=116-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तम्भित
उत्तम्भित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Upheld, supported.<BR>	 2. Stopped, arrested.<BR>3. Erect, (as the hair of the head,) standing on end.<BR> E. उत् before<BR>ष्टभि to stop, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=116-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तर|उत्तरं|उत्तरः
उत्तर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>	 1. Superior, high, lofty.<BR>	 2. Northern.<BR>	 3. Best,<BR>excellent.<BR>	 4. (In composition) Fit, appertaining to.<BR>	 5. Subse-<BR>quent, posterior.<BR>	 n. (-रं)<BR>	 1. An answer, a reply.<BR>	 2. (In law) A<BR>defence, a rejoinder.<BR>	 3. A consequence, a result.<BR>	 4. Remainder,<BR>difference, (in arithmetic.)<BR>	 m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. The son of VIRATA.<BR>	 f. (-रा)<BR>1. The wife of ABHIMANYU, the son of ARJUNA.<BR>	 2. The north. E.<BR>उत् above, and तर from तृ to pass, affix अप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=116-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरकाल|उत्तरकालः
उत्तरकाल m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. Furture time.<BR>	 2. Time reckoned from full moon<BR>to full moon.<BR> E. उत्तर subsequent, काल time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=116-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरकुरु|उत्तरकुरुः
उत्तरकुरु mn. (-रुः-रु) Uttarakuru, the country about the north pole. E.<BR>उत्तर northern, and कुरु the northern part of the globe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=116-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरकोशला
उत्तरकोशला f. (-ला) The city of Ayodhya, the modern Oude.<BR> E. उत्तर<BR>north, कोशला a district so called.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=116-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरक्रिया
उत्तरक्रिया f. (-या) Obsequial ceremonies.<BR> E. उत्तर last, क्रिया rite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=116-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरङ्ग|उत्तरंग|उत्तरंगं|उत्तरङ्गं
उत्तरङ्ग mfn. (-ङ्गः-ङ्गा-ङ्गं)<BR>	 1. Flooded, inundated, washed over by waves.<BR>n. (-ङ्गं) A wooden arch surmounting the door frame.<BR> E. उत्तर<BR>above, ग what goes, affix खश्; or उत् and तरङ्ग a wave.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=116-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरज
उत्तरज mfn. (-जः-जा-जं) Born subsequently or afterwards, posterity. E.<BR>उत्तर and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=116-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरज्या
उत्तरज्या f. (-ज्या) The versed sine of an arc.<BR> E. उत्तर and ज्या an arc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=116-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरण|उत्तरणं
उत्तरण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Crossing rivers, &c.<BR>	 2. Coming forth or out of, (espe-<BR>cially water,) landing.<BR> E. उत् over, तरण passing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=116-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरत्
उत्तरत् mfn. (-रन्-रन्ती-रत्)<BR>	 1. Crossing, going over.<BR>	 2. Coming out of<BR>(water.)<BR> E. उत् before तृ to cross, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=116-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरतस्
उत्तरतस् ind.<BR>	 1. Northward.<BR>	 2. Afterwards.<BR>	 3. Behind.<BR> E. उत्तर and अतसुच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=116-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरत्र
उत्तरत्र ind.<BR>	 1. After, subsequent.<BR>	 2. Northward.<BR> E. उत्तर and त्रल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=116-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरदायक
उत्तरदायक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Replying, answering.<BR> E. उत्तर and दायक a<BR>giver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=116-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरदिश्
उत्तरदिश् f. (-दिक्) The north quarter.<BR> E. उत्तर and दिश् region.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=116-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरधेय
उत्तरधेय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) To be done subsequently.<BR> E. उत्तर afterwards, धि<BR>to have, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=116-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरपक्ष|उत्तरपक्षः
उत्तरपक्ष m. (-क्षः)<BR>	 1. A demonstrated truth, a direct conclusion.<BR>	 2.<BR>Course of argument, according to established truths.<BR>	 3. Second<BR>part of an argument, reply, refutation.<BR>	 4. The minor proposition<BR>in a syllogism.<BR> E. उत्तर subsequent, and पक्ष subject of an inference;<BR>also adding क, उत्तरपक्षक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=116-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरपक्षता
उत्तरपक्षता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Conclusion, demonstration.<BR>	 2. Replication, reply.<BR>E. तल् added to the preceding; also with त्व, उत्तरपक्षत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=116-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरपद
उत्तरपद n. (-दं) The last member of a compound word.<BR> E. उत्तर and पद<BR>word.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=116-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरपदिक
उत्तरपदिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Belonging or relating to the last word or<BR>term.<BR> E. उत्तरपद and ठक् affix; also with छ added उत्तरपदकीय mfn.<BR>(-यः-या-यं.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=116-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरपाद|उत्तरपादः
उत्तरपाद m. (-दः) A division of legal practice, that part which relates<BR>to the reply or defence.<BR> E. उत्तर a reply, and पाद a quarter; four<BR>divisions being admitted in every suit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=116-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरपुरुष|उत्तरपुरुषः
उत्तरपुरुष m. (-षः) (In grammar,) The third person.<BR> E. उत्तर last, and<BR>पुरुष man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=116-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरप्रच्छद|उत्तरप्रच्छदः
उत्तरप्रच्छद m. (-दः) A coverlid, a quilt.<BR> E. उत्तर and प्रच्छद what covers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=116-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरफाल्गुनी
उत्तरफाल्गुनी f. (-नी) The twelfth lunar mansion containing two stars,<BR>figured by a bed.<BR> E. उत्तर subsequent, and फाल्गुनी or फल्गुनी an<BR>asterism; hence it also occurs उत्तरफल्गुनी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=116-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरभाद्रपद्
उत्तरभाद्रपद् f. (-द्) The twenty-seventh lunar mansion, figured dy a<BR>couch, and comprehending two stars, of which one is a Andro<BR>medœ.<BR> E. उत्तर subsequent, and भाद्रपद् properly the constellation;<BR>also with a final vowel, उत्तरभाद्रपदा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=116-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरमात्र
उत्तरमात्र n. (-त्रं) Any reply, some reply.<BR> E. उत्तर and मात्र only.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=116-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तररहित
उत्तररहित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Unable to reply, having no answer.<BR> E. उत्तर<BR>and रहित devoid of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=116-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरलक्षण
उत्तरलक्षण n. (-णं) The indication of an actual reply.<BR> E. उत्तर and लक्षण<BR>mark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=116-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरवस्ति
उत्तरवस्ति f. (-स्तिः) A small syringe, a urethra injection pipe.<BR> E. उत्तर<BR>best, वस्ति syringe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=116-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरवादिन्
उत्तरवादिन् m. (-दी) A defendant, a replicant.<BR> E. उत्तर a reply, and वादिन्<BR>who speaks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=116-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरसंज्ञित
उत्तरसंज्ञित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Designated in the reply, (a witness, &c.) E.<BR>उत्तर and संज्ञित named.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=116-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरसाक्षिन्
उत्तरसाक्षिन् m. (-क्षी) Witness for the defence.<BR> E. उत्तर reply, साक्षिन् a<BR>witness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=116-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरसाधक|उत्तरसाधकः
उत्तरसाधक mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>	 1. Befriending, assisting, a help, a friend.<BR>2. Who or what establishes a reply.<BR> E. उत्तर and साधक what accom-<BR>plishes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=116-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरा
उत्तरा ind. North, northerly, northward.<BR> E. उत्तर and आच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=116-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरात्
उत्तरात् ind. Northward.<BR> E. उत्तर and आति aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=116-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तराधर
उत्तराधर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Superior and inferior, higher and lower. E.<BR>उत्तर upper, अधर lower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=116-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तराधिकार|उत्तराधिकारः
उत्तराधिकार m. (-रः) Right to property, &c. in succession to another<BR>person, heirship, inheritance.<BR> E. उत्तर and अधिकार right.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=116-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तराधिकारिन्
उत्तराधिकारिन् mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि) An heir, a claimant, subsequent to the<BR>death, &c. of the original owner.<BR> E. उत्तराधिकार and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=116-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तराधिकारिता
उत्तराधिकारिता f. (-ता) Right of succession.<BR> E. तल् added to उत्तराधिकारिन्;<BR>also with त्व, उत्तराधिकारित्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=116-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरापथ
उत्तरापथ m. (-थः) The north, a northern road or direction.<BR> E. उत्तर and<BR>पथिन् a road, the final of उत्तर lengthened.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=116-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तराभास|उत्तराभासः
उत्तराभास m. (-सः) A false, indirect, or prevaricating reply, (in law.) E.<BR>उत्तर a defence, and आभास what resembles: apparently a defence,<BR>but not so in fact.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=116-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तराभासता
उत्तराभासता f. (-ता) Inadequacy of a reply, the semblance without the<BR>reality.<BR> E. तल् added to the last; also with त्व, उत्तराभासत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=116-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरायण|उत्तरायणं
उत्तरायण n. (-णं) The period of the sun's progress to the north of the<BR>equator, the summer solstice.<BR> E. उत्तर the north, and अयन going,<BR>progress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=116-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तराशा
उत्तराशा f. (-शा) The north.<BR> E. उत्तर and आशा region.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=116-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तराशाढा
उत्तराशाढा f. (-ढा) One of the lunar mansions. E. See उत्तराषाढा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=116-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तराशापति|उत्तराशापतिः
उत्तराशापति m. (-तिः) A name of KUVERA.<BR> E. उत्तर, आशा a quarter,<BR>पति a master; regent of the north.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=116-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तराषाढा
उत्तराषाढा f. (-ढा) The twenty-first of the lunar mansions, figured by<BR>an elephant's tooth or a bed, and containing two stars, one of<BR>which is in Sagittarius.<BR> E. उत्तर subsequent, and आषाढा the<BR>constellation; to distinguish it from asterism, twentieth: see<BR>पूर्व्वाषाढा and आषाढा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=117-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरासङ्ग|उत्तरासंग|उत्तरासङ्गः
उत्तरासङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः) An upper and outer garment.<BR> E. उत्तर upper, आङ्<BR>prefixed to षञ्ज् to surround, and घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=117-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तराहि
उत्तराहि ind. Northerly, from the north, implying distance.<BR> E. उत्तर<BR>and आहिच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=117-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरीय|उत्तरीयं
उत्तरीय n. (-यं) An upper or outer garment.<BR> E. उत्तर upper, and छ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=117-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरेण
उत्तरेण ind. Northward, posterior, subsequent.<BR> E. उत्तर with एनप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=117-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरेद्युस्
उत्तरेद्युस् ind. A subsequent day, a day following tomorrow.<BR> E. उत्तर<BR>subsequent, and एद्युस् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=117-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरोत्तर
उत्तरोत्तर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) More and more, further and further, &c.<BR>	 n. (-रं)<BR>1. A rejoinder, a reply to an answer.<BR>	 2. Excess, exceeding quanti-<BR>ty or degree.<BR>	 3. Succession, gradation, descending.<BR> E. उत्तर re-<BR>peated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=117-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तान|उत्तानं
उत्तान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>	 1. Shallow.<BR>	 2. Sleeping supinely or with the face<BR>upwards.<BR>	 3. Upright.<BR>	 4. Concave.<BR> E. उत् upwards, तन् to stretch,<BR>and घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=117-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तानक|उत्तानकः
उत्तानक m. (-कः) A species of grass, (a cyperus:) see उच्चटा.<BR> E. उत् much, तन् to spread, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=117-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तानपाद|उत्तानपादः
उत्तानपाद m. (-दः)<BR>	 1. A prince, son of SWAYAMBHU the Menu.<BR>	 2. One of<BR>the stars of the little bear, (Ursi minoris.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=117-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तानपादज|उत्तानपादजः
उत्तानपादज m. (-जः) A name of DHRUVA.<BR> E. उत्तानपाद, ज born: the son of UTTANAPADA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=117-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तानशय|उत्तानशयः
उत्तानशय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) One who sleeps with the face upwards.<BR>	 mf.<BR>(-यः-या) An infant.<BR> E. उत्तान and शय who sleeps.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=117-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्ताप|उत्तापः
उत्ताप m. (-पः)<BR>	 1. Great heat.<BR>	 2. Affliction, distress.<BR>	 3. Anxiety, excite-<BR>ment.<BR>	 4. Effort, energy.<BR> E. उत् before तप् to be hot, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=117-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तापित
उत्तापित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Heated, made hot.<BR>	 2. Pained, distressed.<BR>	 3.<BR>Roused, excited.<BR> E. उत् before तप् to be hot, causal form, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=117-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तार|उत्तारः
उत्तार mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Excellent, pre-eminent.<BR>	 m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Vomiting.<BR>	 2.<BR>Passing away, instability.<BR>	 3. Ejecting, getting rid of.<BR> E. उत् above,<BR>and तार who passes, from तृ and घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=117-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तारिन्
उत्तारिन् mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>	 1. Unsteady, changing, shaking.<BR>	 2. Sick. E.<BR>उत् before तृ to go, णिनि affix; or उत्तार and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=117-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तार्य्य|उत्तार्य
उत्तार्य्य mfn. (-र्य्यः-र्य्या-र्य्यं) To be ejected, to be thrown up by vomiting. E.<BR>उत् before तृ to pass, ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=117-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्ताल|उत्तालः
उत्ताल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>	 1. Best, excellent.<BR>	 2. Arduous, difficult.<BR>	 3. For-<BR>midable 4. Swift, speedy.<BR>	 5. Lofty, tall.<BR>	 m. (-लः) An ape.<BR> E. उत्<BR>before तल् to fix, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=117-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तिष्ठमान
उत्तिष्ठमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>	 1. Getting up, rising.<BR>	 2. Increasing, augment-<BR>ing.<BR> E. उत् before स्था to stay, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=117-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तीरम्
उत्तीरम् ind. On the bank, ashore.<BR> E. उत् and तीर a bank.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=117-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तीर्ण|उत्तीर्णं|उत्तीर्ण्ण
उत्तीर्ण mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-र्णं)<BR>	 1. Crossed, traversed.<BR>	 2. Loosed, liberated.<BR>	 3.<BR>Thrown off.<BR> E. उत् over, तीर्ण crossed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=117-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तुङ्ग|उत्तुंग|उत्तुङ्गः
उत्तुङ्ग mfn. (-ङ्गः-ङ्गा-ङ्गं) High, lofty, tall.<BR> E. उत् very, and तुङ्ग high.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=117-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तुङ्गता
उत्तुङ्गता f. (-ता) Height, elevation.<BR> E. तल् added to the last, or with त्व,<BR>उत्तुङ्गत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=117-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तुण्डित|उत्तुंडितं
उत्तुण्डित n. (-तं) The head of a thorn, &c. which has entered the skin.<BR>E. उत before तुडि to hurt, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=117-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तुष|उत्तुषः
उत्तुष m. (-षः) Fried grain.<BR> E. उत् priv. and तुष husk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=117-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तेजन|उत्तेजनं
उत्तेजन nf. (-नं-ना)<BR>	 1. Sending, dispatching.<BR>	 2. Urging, driving.<BR>	 3.<BR>Whetting, sharpening, polishing.<BR>	 4. Exciting, animating.<BR>	 5. An<BR>inspiring or exciting speech.<BR> E. उत् and तेजन giving light or energy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=117-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तेजित|उत्तेजितं
उत्तेजित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Sent, dispatched.<BR>	 2. Animated, excited.<BR>	 3.<BR>Whetted, sharpened, polished.<BR>	 m. (-तः) Moving in the longe,<BR>sidling, one of a horse's five paces.<BR> E. उत्, before तिज् to sharpen,<BR>and क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=117-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तेरित|उत्तेरितं
उत्तेरित n. (-तं) A horse's walk, one of his five paces in Hindu jockey-<BR>ship.<BR> E. उत्, तृ to pass, क्त irr. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=117-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तोलन|उत्तोलनं
उत्तोलन n. (-नं) Lifting up, raising, elevating.<BR> E. उत् and तोलन weighting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=117-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तोलित
उत्तोलित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Raised, lifted up.<BR> E. उत् before तुल to be equal,<BR>causal form, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=117-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्त्यक्त|उत्त्यक्तः
उत्त्यक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>	 1. Abandoned, left.<BR>	 2. Thrown, tossed.<BR>	 3. Free<BR>from passion or affection.<BR> E. उत् and त्यक्त abandoned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=117-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्त्याग|उत्त्यागः
उत्त्याग m. (-गः)<BR>	 1. Abandonment, quitting.<BR>	 2. Throwing, throwing up.<BR>3. Secession from worldly feelings.<BR> E. उत् and त्याग leaving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=117-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्त्रास
उत्त्रास m. (-सः) Fear, terror.<BR> E. उत much, and त्रास fear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=117-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्थ|उत्थः
उत्थ mfn. (-त्थः-त्था-त्थं) Standing or being up.<BR> E. उत् and स्था to stay, क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=117-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्थान|उत्थानं
उत्थान n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Effort, exertion.<BR>	 2. Manhood, manly exertion.<BR>	 3. An<BR>army.<BR>	 4. War, battle.<BR>	 5. A book.<BR>	 6. Joy, pleasure.<BR>	 7. Rising,<BR>getting up.<BR>	 8. A courtyard.<BR>	 9. A shed where sacrifices are made.<BR>10. A term, a limit.<BR>	 11. Evacuating by stool, &c.<BR>	 12. Business of<BR>a family or realm, as the care of subjects or dependents.<BR>	 13. Re-<BR>flexion.<BR>	 14. Proximate cause of disease.<BR> E. उत् above, स्था to stand,<BR>and ल्युट् affix, स is dropped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=117-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्थानैकादशी
उत्थानैकादशी f. (-शी) The eleventh lunation of the light half of Kartik<BR>or Agrahayana, when VIṢṆU rises from his sleep.<BR> E. उत्थान rising,<BR>एकादशी eleventh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=117-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्थापक|उत्थापकः
उत्थापक mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>	 1. Lifting, causing to get up, who or what<BR>raises, &c.<BR>	 2. Exciting, animating,<BR> E. उत् before स्था to stay causal<BR>form, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=117-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्थापन|उत्थापनं
उत्थापन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Raising, elevating.<BR>	 2. Causing to rise or get up.<BR>	 3.<BR>Exciting, instigating.<BR>	 4. (In arithmetic) Substitution of a value.<BR>E. उत् and स्था causal form, affix ल्युट्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=117-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्थापित
उत्थापित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Raised, lifted up, elevated.<BR>	 2. Made to get<BR>up, aroused from a seat, a bed, &c.<BR>	 3. Instigated.<BR> E. उत् and स्था<BR>causal form, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=117-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्थाप्य
उत्थाप्य ind.<BR>	 1. Having raised or caused to rise.<BR>	 2. Having roused or<BR>instigated.<BR> E. उत् before स्था to stay, causal form, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=117-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्थाय
उत्थाय ind.<BR>	 1. Having risen (from a seat, &c.)<BR>	 2. Having risen (in<BR>rank, &c.)<BR> E. उत् before स्था to stand, affix ल्यप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=117-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्थित|उत्थितं
उत्थित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Born, produced.<BR>	 2. Endeavouring, striving.<BR>3. Happened, occurring.<BR>	 4. Increasing, advancing, rising.<BR>	 5. High,<BR>risen or rising as from a seat, &c.<BR> E. उत् up, स्था to stay, and क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=117-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्थिताङ्गुलि|उत्थितांगुलि|उत्थिताङ्गुलिः
उत्थिताङ्गुलि m. (-लिः) The palm of the hand with the fingers extended.<BR>E. उत्थित increased, and अङ्गुलि a finger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=117-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्थिति|उत्थितिः
उत्थिति f. (-तिः) Elevation, rising up.<BR> E. उत् before स्था to stay, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=117-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पत|उत्पतः
उत्पत m. (-तः)<BR>	 1. A bird.<BR>	 2. Going upwards, or up.<BR> E. उत् up, and पत<BR>who goes, from पत् to go, and अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=117-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पतन|उत्पतनं
उत्पतन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Birth, production.<BR>	 2. Going up, rising, ascending. E.<BR>उत्, पत् to go, and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=117-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पतितृ
उत्पतितृ mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ) Jumping up, rising, going upwards.<BR> E. उत्, पत to rise, and तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=117-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पतित
उत्पतित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Risen, ascended.<BR> E. उत् up, पत् to go, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=117-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पतिष्णु|उत्पतिष्णुः
उत्पतिष्णु mfn. (-ष्णुः-ष्णुः-ष्णु) Rising, jumping up.<BR> E. उत्पत and इष्णुच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=117-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पत्ति|उत्पत्तिः
उत्पत्ति f. (-त्तिः)<BR>	 1. Birth, production.<BR>	 2. Producing as an effect or re-<BR>sult, giving rise to or generating as a consequence.<BR>	 3. Production<BR>in general.<BR> E. उत् up, पत् to go, and क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=117-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पत्तिप्रयोग|उत्पत्तिप्रयोगः
उत्पत्तिप्रयोग m. (-गः)<BR>	 1. Purport, meaning.<BR>	 2. Production by the joint<BR>operation of cause and effect.<BR> E. उत्पत्ति and प्रयोग act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=117-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पत्तिव्यञ्जक|उत्पत्तिव्यंजक|उत्पत्तिव्यञ्जकः
उत्पत्तिव्यञ्जक m. (-कः) A type of birth, (as investiture.)<BR> E. उत्पत्ति and<BR>व्यञ्जक figurative indication.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=117-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पथ|उत्पथः
उत्पथ m. (-थः) Error, bad way, evil.<BR> E. उत् from, पथ for पथिन् a path.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=117-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पथम्
उत्पथम् ind. Astray, on the wrong road.<BR> E. उत् from, पथिन् a path, अ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=117-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पन्न|उत्पन्नः
उत्पन्न mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>	 1. Born, produced.<BR>	 2. Known, ascertained.<BR>	 3.<BR>Risen, gone up.<BR>	 4. Acquired, gained.<BR>	 5. Effected, accomplished.<BR>	 6.<BR>Occurred, happened.<BR> E. उत्, पद् to go, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=117-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पन्नतन्तु
उत्पन्नतन्तु mfn. (-न्तुः-न्तुः-न्तु) Having progeny.<BR> E. उत्पन्न and तन्तु line; des-<BR>cendants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=117-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पल|उत्पलं|उत्पलः
उत्पल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Thin.<BR>	 n. (-लं)<BR>	 1. A blue lotus, (Nymphæa cærula.)<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=118-a" target="_blank">Page118-a+ 60</a>]<BR>2. A plant, (a Costus:) see कुष्ट.<BR>	 3. A water-lily in general.<BR>	 4. A<BR>flower in general.<BR>	 f. (-ली)<BR>	 1. A kind of cake made with unwinnowed<BR>corn.<BR> E. उत् up, पल् to go or grow, अच् affix, and fem. टाप् or ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=117-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पलगन्धिक|उत्पलगन्धिकं
उत्पलगन्धिक n. (-कं) A species of sandal of the colour of brass, and very<BR>fragrant.<BR> E. उत्पल the lotus, गन्ध a smell, कन् affix of similitude.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=118-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पलचक्षुस्
उत्पलचक्षुस् mfn. (-क्षुः-क्षुः-क्षुः) Lotus-eyed, fine-eyed.<BR> E. उत्पल and चक्षुस् the<BR>eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=118-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पलपत्र|उत्पलपत्रं
उत्पलपत्र n. (-त्रं)<BR>	 1. The leaf of the lotus.<BR>	 2. The impression of a female<BR>nail.<BR>	 3. The Tilaka or mark on the forehead, made with sandal,<BR>&c. by the Hindus.<BR>	 4. A broad-bladed knife or lancet.<BR> E. उत्पल a<BR>lotus, and पत्र a leaf; similarly shaped, &c. also कन् added उत्पल-<BR>पत्रक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=118-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पलशारिवा
उत्पलशारिवा f. (-वा) A plant, (Echites frutescens.)<BR> E. उत्पल a flower,<BR>शारिवा irregular deriv. of शृ to harm: whose flower injures or de-<BR>stroys, (disease.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=118-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पलाभ
उत्पलाभ mfn. (-भः-भा-भं) Lotus-like, resembling a lotus.<BR> E. उत्पल and<BR>आङ before भा to shine, ड aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=118-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पलिनी
उत्पलिनी f. (-नी) An assemblage of lotus flowers.<BR> E. उत्पल a lotus, इनि<BR>affix, and ङीप fem. do.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=118-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पवन|उत्पवनं
उत्पवन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Straining liquids before using for domestic or religious<BR>purposes.<BR>	 2. Sprinkling ghee or other fluids on the sacrificial fire,<BR>with two blades of Kusa grass, the ends of which are held in<BR>either hand, and the centre dipped into the liquid, which is then<BR>dropped upon the fire.<BR> E. उत् above, &c. पुङ् to purify, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=118-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पश्य|उत्पश्यः
उत्पश्य mfn. (-श्यः-श्या-श्यं) Looking up or upwards.<BR> E. उत् up, and पश्य<BR>looking, irr. formative, from दृश् to see.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=118-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पाट|उत्पाटः
उत्पाट m. (-टः)<BR>	 1. Pulling up by the roots.<BR>	 2. Destroying.<BR> E. उत् up,<BR>पट् to go, causal from, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=118-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पाटन|उत्पाटनं
उत्पाटन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Eradicating, pulling up by the roots.<BR>	 2. Destroying.<BR>E. उत before पट् to go, causal form, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=118-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पाटित|उत्पाटितं
उत्पाटित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Eradicated, pulled up by the roots.<BR> E. उत् up,<BR>or out, पट् to go, in the causal form, and क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=118-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पाटिन्
उत्पाटिन् mfn. (-टी-टिनी-टि) Eradicating, extirpating.<BR> E. उत्पाट and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=118-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पात|उत्पातः
उत्पात m. (-तः)<BR>	 1. A portent, some natural prodigy or phœnomenon.<BR>2. Any public calamity, as an eclipse, a meteor, an earthquake,<BR>&c.<BR> E. उत् accidentally, पत् to happen, and घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=118-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पातवात|उत्पातवातः
उत्पातवात m. (-तः) A whirlwind, a hurricane.<BR> E. उत्पात a portent, and वात<BR>wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=118-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पादक|उत्पादकः
उत्पादक mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>	 1. A producer, a generator.<BR>	 2. What gives<BR>origin or production to, causative.<BR>	 m. (-कः) A fabulous animal<BR>with eight legs; written also उत्पातक n. (-कं) Origin, cause.<BR>	 f.<BR>(-दिका)<BR>	 1. A white ant, (termes.)<BR>	 2. A potherb, (Hilancha repens.)<BR>3. Also, Basella, (rubra or lucida.)<BR> E. उत् much, पद a foot, or पद्<BR>to go, in the causal form, and वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=118-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पादन|उत्पादनं
उत्पादन n. (-नं) Producing, generating, begetting.<BR> E. उत् before पद् to<BR>go, causal form, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=118-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पादशयन|उत्पादशयनः
उत्पादशयन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) The Francoline partridge.<BR> E. उत् upon, पाद a foot, शयन sleeping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=118-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पादित
उत्पादित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Produced, effected.<BR>	 2. Generated, begotten.<BR>E. उत् before पद् to go, causal form, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=118-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पाद्य
उत्पाद्य ind.<BR>	 1. Having begotten.<BR>	 2. Having produced, having inspired.<BR>E. उत् before पद् to go, causal form, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=118-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पाली
उत्पाली f. (-ली) Health.<BR> E. उत् before, पल to preserve, अङ् and ङीष् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=118-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पाव|उत्पावः
उत्पाव m. (-वः) Purifying ghee, &c. see उत्पवन.<BR> E. उत् before पू to make<BR>pure, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=118-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पिञ्जर|उत्पिंजर
उत्पिञ्जर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Uncaged, unconfined.<BR> E. उत् out of, पिञ्जर a cage;<BR>also उत्पिञ्जल, ल being substituted for र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=118-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पिञ्जल|उत्पिंजल|उत्पिञ्जलः
उत्पिञ्जल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>	 1. Confounded, confused.<BR>	 2. Uncaged. E. See<BR>the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=118-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पित्सु
उत्पित्सु mfn. (-सुः-सुः-सु) Desirous of going, going, proceeding.<BR> E. उत्<BR>before पत to go, desiderative form, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=118-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पिष्ट
उत्पिष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं) Ground, rubbed.<BR>	 n. (-ष्टं) A disease, a grating of<BR>the bones of the joints upon each other.<BR> E. उत् and पिष्ट ground.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=118-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पीड|उत्पीडः
उत्पीड m. (-डः) Froth.<BR> E. उत् on, पीड् to go, क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=118-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्प्रासन|उत्प्रासनं
उत्प्रासन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Ridicule, derision.<BR>	 2. Hurling, throwing afar.<BR> E. उत<BR>and प्र before अस् to throw, affix ल्युट.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=118-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्प्रेक्षा
उत्प्रेक्षा f. (-क्षा)<BR>	 1. Indifference, carelessness.<BR>	 2. Ironical comparison.<BR>	 3.<BR>Comparison in general, poetical or rhetorical.<BR> E. उत् and प्र prefixed<BR>to ईक्ष् to see, अङ् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=118-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्प्लवन|उत्प्लवनं
उत्प्लवन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Taking up oil or ghee when it has been defiled in<BR>any way, by dipping a blade of Kusa grass into it, and dropping<BR>it from them upon the fire.<BR>	 2. Jumping, springing upon.<BR> E. उत्<BR>over, प्लवन jumping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=118-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्प्लवा
उत्प्लवा f. (-वा) A boat.<BR> E. उत् over, प्लु to go, अच् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=118-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्प्लुत
उत्प्लुत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Jumped upon, approached suddenly.<BR> E. उत् before<BR>प्लु to go, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=118-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्प्लुत्य
उत्प्लुत्य ind. Having sprung or jumped upon.<BR> E. उत् before प्लु to go, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=118-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्फल|उत्फलं
उत्फल n. (-लं) Excellent fruit.<BR> E. उत् and फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=118-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्फाल|उत्फालः
उत्फाल m. (-लः) A jump, a leap.<BR> E. उत् before स्फुल् to move, affix घञ्<BR>the vowel and final changed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=118-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्फुल्ल|उत्फुल्लः
उत्फुल्ल mfn. (-ल्लः-ल्ला-ल्लं)<BR>	 1. Blown as a flower.<BR>	 2. Swollen, increased in<BR>bulk.<BR>	 3. Sleeping supinely.<BR> E. उत् and फुल्ल blown.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=118-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्स|उत्सः
उत्स m. (-त्सः) A fountain, a spring.<BR> E. उन्द् to wet, and स Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=118-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सङ्ग|उत्संग|उत्संगः|उत्सङ्गः
उत्सङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>	 1. The haunch or part above the hip.<BR>	 2. The acclivity<BR>or slope of a hill.<BR>	 3. Association, union.<BR>	 4. Embrace.<BR>	 5. The bot-<BR>tom or deep part of an ulcer.<BR> E. उत् before षञ्ज् to embrace, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=118-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सङ्गित|उत्संगित
उत्सङ्गित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Associated, combined, joined.<BR> E. उत् before षञ्ज्<BR>to be joined with, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=118-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सङ्गिन्|उत्संगिन्
उत्सङ्गिन् mfn. (-ङ्गी-ङ्गिनी-ङ्गि) Associating or combining with, an associate,<BR>a partner.<BR>	 m. (-ङ्गी) An ulcer, a deep sore.<BR>	 f. (-ङ्गिनी) Pimples on<BR>the inner edge of the eyelids.<BR> E. उत्सङ्ग and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=118-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सन्न
उत्सन्न mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>	 1. Destroyed, overturned.<BR>	 2. Decayed, in ruins.<BR>3. Risen, increased.<BR> E. उत् before षद् to go, affix क्त<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=118-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सर्ग|उत्सर्गः
उत्सर्ग m. (-र्गः)<BR>	 1. Abandoning, quitting.<BR>	 2. Resigning, retiring from.<BR>	 3.<BR>Giving, donation.<BR>	 4. Any precept or rule.<BR>	 5. Presentation of any<BR>thing promised to a god or Brahman, with suitable ceremonies.<BR>6. A particular ceremony preparatory to a course of the Vedas.<BR>	 7.<BR>Dejection, excretion, voiding by stool, &c.<BR> E. उत् before सृज् to quit,<BR>to leave, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=118-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सर्जन|उत्सर्जनं
उत्सर्जन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Gift, donation.<BR>	 2. Abandoning, leaving, &c.<BR> E. उत् be-<BR>fore सृज् to leave, and ल्युट् affix: see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=118-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सर्पिणी
उत्सर्पिणी f. (-णी) A Jaina division of time, a long period described as<BR>10 crores of oceans of years; this period alternates with one of<BR>similar duration: see अवसर्पिणी.<BR> E. उत् much, सृप् to go, णिनि and<BR>ङीष् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=118-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सर्प्प|उत्सर्प|उत्सर्पः
उत्सर्प्प m. (-र्प्पः)<BR>	 1. Going or gliding upwards.<BR>	 2. Swelling, heaving. E.<BR>उत् before सृप् to go, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=118-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सर्प्पण|उत्सर्पण|उत्सर्पणं
उत्सर्प्पण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Gliding upwards.<BR>	 2. Swelling, heaving.<BR> E. उत् before<BR>सृप् to go gently, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=118-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सर्प्पिन्|उत्सर्पिन्
उत्सर्प्पिन् mfn. (-र्प्पी-र्प्पिणी-र्प्पि)<BR>	 1. What glides upwards.<BR>	 2. Rising gently;<BR>heaving, &c.<BR> E. उत्सर्प्प and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=118-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सर्य्या|उत्सर्या
उत्सर्य्या f. (-र्य्या) A cow fit to take the bull.<BR> E. उत्, सृ to go, and ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=118-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सव|उत्सवः
उत्सव m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. A festival, a jubilee.<BR>	 2. Height, elevation.<BR>	 3. Impa-<BR>tience.<BR>	 4. Wish.<BR>	 5. Passion, wrath.<BR> E. उत्, षू to bear, to bring<BR>forth, affix अच; happiness, &c. is produced by it.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=118-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सादन|उत्सादनं
उत्सादन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Going up, ascending, rising.<BR>	 2. Raising, elevating.<BR>	 3.<BR>Destroying, overturning.<BR>	 4. Cleaning the person with perfumes.<BR>5. Rubbing or chafing the limbs.<BR>	 6. Ploughing a field twice or<BR>thoroughly.<BR>	 7. Healing a sore, causing it to fill up.<BR> E. उत् much,<BR>षद् to destroy, in the causal form, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=118-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सादनीय
उत्सादनीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>	 1. To be gone up or ascended.<BR>	 2. To be effect-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=119-a" target="_blank">Page119-a+ 60</a>]<BR>ed.<BR>	 3. To be destroyed.<BR>	 n. (-यं) Any application to a sore produc-<BR>ing granulations.<BR> E. उत् before षद् to go, causal form, affix अनीयर्;<BR>also उत्सादितव्य and उत्साद्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=118-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सादित|उत्सादितं
उत्सादित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Risen, ascended.<BR>	 2. Raised, elevated.<BR>	 3. De-<BR>stroyed.<BR>	 4. Cleansed, purified with oil, perfumes, &c. E. As above,<BR>affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=119-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सारक|उत्सारकः
उत्सारक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A doorkeeper, a porter.<BR>	 2. A guard, a guardian. E.<BR>उत्, सृ to go, in the causal form and वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=119-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सारण|उत्सारणं
उत्सारण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Removing, keeping at a distance.<BR>	 2. Moving, causing<BR>to move.<BR> E. उत्, सृ to go, causal form, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=119-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्साह|उत्साहः
उत्साह m. (-हः)<BR>	 1. Effort, perseverance, strenuous and continued exer-<BR>tion.<BR>	 2. A thread.<BR>	 3. Happiness.<BR>	 4. Firmness, fortitude.<BR> E. उत्<BR>much, सह् to bear, to be able, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=119-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्साहवत्|उत्साहवन्त्
उत्साहवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Active, energetic, persevering.<BR> E. उत्साह and वतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=119-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्साहवर्द्धन
उत्साहवर्द्धन n. (-नं) Heroism.<BR> E. उत्साह exertion, and वर्द्धन increasing, from<BR>वृध् and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=119-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्साहसम्पन्न|उत्साहसंपन्न
उत्साहसम्पन्न mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं) Active, persevering.<BR> E. उत्साह and सम्पन्न effected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=119-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्साहिन्
उत्साहिन् mfn. (-ही-हिनी-हि) Active, persevering.<BR> E. उत्साह and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=119-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सिक्त|उत्सिक्तः
उत्सिक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>	 1. Haughty, proud, rude.<BR>	 2. Elevated, raised.<BR>3. Enlarged, increased.<BR>	 4. Sprinkled.<BR>	 5. Disordered, disturbed (in<BR>mind, &c.)<BR>	 m. (-क्तः) A king's wrestler.<BR> E. उत् before षिच् to<BR>sprinkle, and क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=119-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सिच्यमान|उत्सिच्यमानः
उत्सिच्यमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>	 1. Augmenting, growing.<BR>	 2. Sprinkling. E.<BR>उत् before षिच् to sprinkle, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=119-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सुक|उत्सुकः
उत्सुक mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>	 1. Zealously active, making exertions for a gra-<BR>tifying object.<BR>	 2. Regretting, missing, sorrowing for.<BR>	 3. Fond of,<BR>attached to.<BR> E. उत् much, सु to produce, क्विप् and कन् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=119-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उतसुकता
उतसुकता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Sorrow, regret.<BR>	 2. Attachment, affection.<BR> E. उत्सुक<BR>and तल् affix; also with त्व affix उत्सुकत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=119-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सूत्र
उत्सूत्र mfn. (-त्रः-त्रा-त्रं)<BR>	 1. Loose, detached, unstrung.<BR>	 2. Irregular, out<BR>of rule.<BR> E. डत् before सूत्र a thread, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=119-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सूर|उत्सूरः
उत्सूर m. (-रः) Evening, twilight.<BR> E. उत् priv. सूर the sun; sunset.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=119-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सृज्य
उत्सृज्य ind. Having quitted.<BR> E. उत् before सृज् to leave, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=119-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सृष्ट|उत्सृष्टः
उत्सृष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>	 1. Left, abandoned.<BR>	 2. Given, presented.<BR>	 3.<BR>Cast into or upon.<BR> E. उत् and सृज् so leave, affix क्त, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=119-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सृष्टपशु
उत्सृष्टपशु m. (-शुः) A bull set at liberty upon particular occasions, as a<BR>marriage, &c. and allowed to go about at will.<BR> E. उत्सृष्ट loosed,<BR>and पशु an animal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=119-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सेक|उत्सेकः
उत्सेक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. Increase, enlargement.<BR>	 2. Pride, haughtiness.<BR>	 3.<BR>Casting water, &c. on anything, sprinkling.<BR>	 4. Flying out or up,<BR>foaming or spouting. over, showering.<BR> E. उत् on, षिच् to sprinkle,<BR>घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=119-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सेचन|उत्सेचनं
उत्सेचन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Showering or spouting upwards.<BR>	 2. Boiling or foam-<BR>ing over.<BR> E. उत् and सेचन sprinkling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=119-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सेध|उत्सेधः
उत्सेध m. (-धः)<BR>	 1. Height, elevation.<BR>	 2. The body.<BR>	 3. Fatness, obesity.<BR>4. Intumescence 5. Thickness.<BR>	 n. (-धं) Killing, slaughter.<BR> E. उत्<BR>up, षिध् to go, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=119-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्स्मय|उत्स्मयः
उत्स्मय m. (-यः) A smile.<BR> E. उत् and स्मय a smile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=119-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्
उद् or उत् ind. A particle and prefix to words implying, 1. Superiority<BR>in degree; (over, above.)<BR>	 2. In place, (over, above, on, upon.)<BR>3. Pride.<BR>	 4. Publicity.<BR>	 5. Power.<BR>	 6. Separation, disjunction,<BR>(off, from, out of.)<BR>	 7. Emancipation.<BR>	 8. Binding.<BR>	 9. Helplessness,<BR>weakness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=119-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्
उद् or उत् ind. A particle and prefix to words implying, 1. Superiority<BR>in degree; (over, above.)<BR>	 2. In place, (over, above, on, upon.)<BR>3. Pride.<BR>	 4. Publicity.<BR>	 5. Power.<BR>	 6. Separation, disjunction,<BR>(off, from, out of.)<BR>	 7. Emancipation.<BR>	 8. Binding.<BR>	 9. Helplessness,<BR>weakness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=119-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद|उदं
उद n. (-दं) Water.<BR> E. उन्द् to wet, deriv. irr.: see उदक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=119-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदक्
उदक् ind. Northern, upper, subsequent: see उदच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=119-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदक|उदकं
उदक n. (-कं) Water.<BR> E. उन्द् to wet, deriv. irr.; this is sometimes con-<BR>sidered as two words, उद and क, each having the same meaning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=119-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदकक्रिया
उदकक्रिया f. (-या) Presentation of water to ancestors as far as the four-<BR>teenth degree.<BR> E. उदक and क्रिया rite; so उदकर्म्म, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=119-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदकद|उदकदः
उदकद mfn. (-दः-दा-दं) A giver of water, yielding water, offering<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=119-b" target="_blank">Page119-b+ 60</a>]<BR>water to the manes, &c.<BR>	 m. (-दः) An heir, a near kinsman.<BR> E. उदक<BR>and द who gives; also उदकदातृ and उदकदायिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=119-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदकदान
उदकदान n. (-नं) Gift of water, especially to the manes, as a religious<BR>or obsequial rite.<BR> E. उदक् and दान giving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=119-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदकदायिन्
उदकदायिन् mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि) Giving water.<BR>	 m. (-यी) An heir or kins-<BR>man, one who presents libations of water.<BR> E. उदक् and दायिन् who<BR>gives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=119-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदकपूर्व्वकम्|उदकपूर्वकम्
उदकपूर्व्वकम् ind. Pouring water on the hand as preparatory to or con-<BR>firmatory of a gift or promise.<BR> E. उदक and पूर्व्वक prior.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=119-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदकप्रतीकाश
उदकप्रतीकाश mfn. (-शः-शा-शं) Watery, fluid like water.<BR> E. उदक and<BR>प्रतीकाश what resembles.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=119-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदकमेह|उदकमेहः
उदकमेह m. (-हः) A variety of Diabetes, passing watery urine.<BR> E. उदक् and मेह urining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=119-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदकशाक
उदकशाक n. (-कं) Any aquatic herb.<BR> E. उदक and शाक a potherb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=119-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदकस्पर्श|उदकस्पर्शः
उदकस्पर्श m. (-र्शः)<BR>	 1. Touching different parts of the body with<BR>water.<BR>	 2. Touching water in confirmation of a promise, &c. F. उदक<BR>and स्पर्श touch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=119-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदकाधार|उदकाधारः
उदकाधार m. (-रः) A reservoir, a cistern, a well, &c.<BR> E. उदक and आधार receptacle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=119-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदकार्थिन्
उदकार्थिन् mfn. (-र्थी-र्थिनी-र्थि) Thirsty, desirous of water.<BR> E. उदक and<BR>अर्थिन् who seeks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=119-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदकीर्य्य|उदकीर्य|उदकीर्यः|उदकीर्य्यः
उदकीर्य्य m. (-र्य्यः) A plant, (Galedupa, arborea &c.) See करञ्जक.<BR> E. उद्<BR>water, and कॄ to scatter, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=119-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदकुम्भ|उदकुंभ|उदकुम्भः
उदकुम्भ m. (-म्भः) A water-jar.<BR> E. उद् and कुम्भ a jar; also उदककुम्भ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=119-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदकोदञ्चन
उदकोदञ्चन m. (-नः) A water-jar.<BR> E. उदक् and उदञ्चन what goes up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=119-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदकोदर
उदकोदर n. (-रं) Dropsy.<BR> E. उदक and उदर the belly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=119-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदक्त
उदक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं) Gone up, risen, ascended.<BR> E. उत् before अञ्च् to<BR>go, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=119-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदक्या
उदक्या f. (-क्या) A woman in her courses.<BR> E. उदक् water, and यत् affix of<BR>fitness: requiring water for purification.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=119-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदगद्रि|उदगद्रिः
उदगद्रि m. (-द्रिः) The Himālaya mountains on the north of Hindustan.<BR>E. उदक् north, and अद्रि a mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=119-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदगयन|उदगयनं
उदगयन n. (-नं) The sun's progress north of the equator: see उत्तरायण.<BR>E. उदक् north, and अयन going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=119-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदग्भूम|उदग्भूमः
उदग्भूम m. (-मः) Good soil.<BR> E. उदक् north, भूमि earth, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=119-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदग्भूमि|उदग्भूमिः
उदग्भूमि m. (-मिः) Fertile soil: see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=119-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदग्र|उदग्रं
उदग्र mfn. (-ग्रः-ग्रा-ग्रं)<BR>	 1. High, tall.<BR>	 2. Large, vast.<BR>	 3. Projecting.<BR>	 4.<BR>Pointing upwards.<BR>	 5. Fierce, intense.<BR> E. उत् up, and अग्र end,<BR>point.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=119-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदग्रदत्|उदग्रदन्त्
उदग्रदत् mfn. (-दन्-दती-दत्) Large-toothed.<BR>	 m. (-दन्) An elephant with a<BR>large tusk.<BR> E. उदग्र large, and दत् for दन्त a tooth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=119-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदङ्मुख
उदङ्मुख mfn. (-खः-खा-खी-खं) Facing the north.<BR> E. उदच् and मुख face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=119-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदच्
उदच् or उदञ्च् mfn. (उदङ् उदीची उदक्)<BR>	 1. North, northern.<BR>	 2. Upper,<BR>upwards.<BR>	 3. Subsequent, posterior.<BR>	 f. (-दीची) The north.<BR> E. उद् up,<BR>अञ्च् to go, affix क्विप्; the neuter is used as a particle: see उदक्;<BR>the noun is irregular.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=119-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदञ्च्|उदंच्
उदच् or उदञ्च् mfn. (उदङ् उदीची उदक्)<BR>	 1. North, northern.<BR>	 2. Upper,<BR>upwards.<BR>	 3. Subsequent, posterior.<BR>	 f. (-दीची) The north.<BR> E. उद् up,<BR>अञ्च् to go, affix क्विप्; the neuter is used as a particle: see उदक्;<BR>the noun is irregular.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=119-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदज|उदजः
उदज mfn. (-जः-जा-जं) Aquatic, watery, produced in or by water.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-जः) Driving cattle.<BR> E. उद् water, and ज born, or उत् up, and अज to<BR>go, affix अप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=119-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदञ्चन|उदंचन|उदंचनं|उदञ्चनं
उदञ्चन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. A lid or cover.<BR>	 2. Directing or throwing upwards.<BR>	 3.<BR>Rising, ascending.<BR> E. उत् above, अञ्च् to go, and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=119-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदञ्चित|उदञ्चितं
उदञ्चित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Thrown up, tossed.<BR>	 2. Worshipped.<BR> E. उद् up,<BR>अञ्च् to go or worship, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=119-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदण्डपाल|उदंडपाल|उदंडपालः|उदण्डपालः
उदण्डपाल m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. A kind of fish.<BR>	 2. A sort of snake.<BR> E. उद् much,<BR>अण्ड an egg, and पाल what nourishes; laying many eggs at once.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=119-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदधि|उदधिः
उदधि m. (-धिः)<BR>	 1. The ocean.<BR>	 2. A water-jar.<BR>	 3. A cloud.<BR> E. उद् water,<BR>and धि having, from धा, with कि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=119-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदधिक्रम
उदधिक्रम m. (-मः) A voyager, a mariner.<BR> E. उदधि, क्रम् to go, विट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=119-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदधिमल|उदधिमलः
उदधिमल m. (-लः) Cuttlefish bone.<BR> E. उदधि and मल soil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=119-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदधिमेखला
उदधिमेखला f. (-ला) The earth.<BR> E. उदधि and मेखला a girdle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=119-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदधिसुता
उदधिसुता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. LAKṢMĪ.<BR>	 2. Dwaraka, the capital of KṚṢṆA. E.<BR>उदधि the ocean, and सुता daughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=119-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदन्त|उदंत|उदन्तः
उदन्त m. (-न्तः)<BR>	 1. Pure and virtuous man.<BR>	 2. Tidings, intelligence.<BR>	 3.<BR>One who gets a livelihood by a trade, &c.<BR> E. उद् disjunctive, and<BR>अन्त end, term.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=120-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदन्तक|उदंतक|उदंतकः|उदन्तकः
उदन्तक m. (-कः) News, tidings, intelligence.<BR> E. कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=120-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदन्तिका|उदंतिका
उदन्तिका f. (-का) Satisfaction, satiety.<BR> E. उद् complete, अन्त end, कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=120-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदन्या
उदन्या f. (-न्या) Thirst.<BR> E. उदक् water, क्यच् affix, the final क is changed<BR>to न.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=120-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदन्वत्|उदन्वन्त्
उदन्वत् m. (-न्वान्) The ocean.<BR> E. उद् water, and मतुप् possessive aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=120-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदपात्र
उदपात्र n. (-त्रं) A water-cup, a ewer.<BR> E. उद् water and पात्र a vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=120-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदपान|उदपानं|उदपानः
उदपान mn. (-नः-नं) A well.<BR> E. उद् water, पा to drink, and ल्युट् affix; the<BR>place where water is drunk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=120-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदपेष
उदपेष n. (-षं) A paste, anything ground with water.<BR> E. उद् water and<BR>पेष grinding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=120-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदभार|उदभारः
उदभार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A cloud.<BR>	 2. A water carrier.<BR> E. उद् water and भार<BR>a load.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=120-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदमन्थ|उदमन्थः
उदमन्थ m. (-न्थः) Barley water.<BR> E. उद् and मन्थ scum; also उदकमन्थ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=120-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदमेघ|उदमेघः
उदमेघ m. (-घः) A watery cloud.<BR> E. उद् and मेघ a cloud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=120-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदय|उदयः
उदय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. The rising of the sun and planets in general.<BR>	 2. The<BR>eastern mountain, behind which the sun is supposed to rise.<BR>	 3.<BR>Rising, ascending.<BR>	 4. Light, splendor.<BR>	 5. Prosperity, good fortune.<BR>6. Creation, the rising of the world.<BR>	 7. (In law) Income.<BR> E. उद् up,<BR>इण् to go, and अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=120-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदयन|उदयनं|उदयनः
उदयन n. (-नं) Rising, ascending.<BR>	 m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. A name of AGASTYA: see<BR>अगस्त्य.<BR>	 2. The name of a sovereign, king of Kausambi, and hero of<BR>the Vasavadatta, a dramatic poem; also, of part of the Vrihat<BR>Katha.<BR> E. उद् above, इण् to go, and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=120-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदयपर्व्वत|उदयपर्वत|उदयपर्वतः
उदयपर्व्वत m. (-तः) The eastern mountain behind which the sun rises.<BR>E. उदय and पर्व्वत a mountain; also similar compounds, as उदयगिरिः,<BR>उदयशैलः, उदयाचलः, उदयाद्रिः, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=120-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदयिन्
उदयिन् mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि)<BR>	 1. Rising, ascending.<BR>	 2. Prosperous, flourish-<BR>ing.<BR> E. उदय and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=120-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदर|उदरं|उदरः
उदर n. (-रं)<BR>	 1. The belly.<BR>	 2. War.<BR>	 3. Any morbid abdominal affection,<BR>as liver, spleen, &c.<BR>	 f. (-री) Enlargement of the abdomen from<BR>dropsy or flatulency.<BR> E. उद् up, ऋ to go, अप् affix; what goes up<BR>or swells with food, slaughter, &c. or उद् prefixed to दृ to burst,<BR>and अच् or अल् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=120-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदरक
उदरक mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>	 1. Rubbing the belly, &c.<BR>	 2. Abdominal.<BR> E. उदर<BR>and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=120-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदरग्रन्थि|उदरग्रन्थिः
उदरग्रन्थि m. (-न्थिः) The spleen, (the disease; a chronic affection of this<BR>organ not uncommon in India.)<BR> E. उदर abdomen, and ग्रन्थि a knot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=120-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदरत्राण|उदरत्राणं
उदरत्राण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. A cuirass, armour covering the front.<BR>	 2. A girth, a<BR>belly-band.<BR> E. उदर the belly, and त्राण what preserves.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=120-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदरथि|उदरथिः
उदरथि m. (-थिः)<BR>	 1. The ocean.<BR>	 2. The sun.<BR> E. उद् freely, ऋ to go, and<BR>अथिर् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=120-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदरपिशाच|उदरपिशाचः
उदरपिशाच mfn. (-चः-चा-चं) A glutton, voracious, one who devours every<BR>thing, flesh, fish, &c.<BR> E. उदर and पिशाच a demon, who is a devil<BR>for his belly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=120-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदरम्भरि|उदरंभरि|उदरम्भरिः
उदरम्भरि mfn. (-रिः-रिः-रि) Selfishly voracious, gluttonous.<BR> E. उदर, भृ to<BR>nourish, इन् affix, and मुम् is inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=120-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदरशय|उदरशयः
उदरशय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Sleeping on the face or belly.<BR> E. उदर and शय<BR>who sleeps.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=120-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदरामय|उदरामयः
उदरामय m. (-यः) Dysentery, diarrhæa.<BR> E. उदर the belly, and आमय sickness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=120-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदरावर्त्त|उदरावर्त|उदरावर्तः|उदरावर्त्तः
उदरावर्त्त m. (-र्त्तः) The navel.<BR> E. उदर and आवर्त्त whirl.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=120-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदरावेष्ट|उदरावेष्टः
उदरावेष्ट m. (-ष्टः) Tape worm.<BR> E. उदर and आवेष्ट what surrounds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=120-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदरिन्
उदरिन् mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>	 1. Fat, corpulent.<BR>	 2. Abdominal.<BR>	 f. (-णी) A<BR>pregnant woman.<BR> E. उदर the belly, इनि possessive aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=120-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदरिल|उदरिलः
उदरिल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Fat, corpulent.<BR> E. उदर the belly, and इलच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=120-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदर्क|उदर्कः
उदर्क m. (-र्कः)<BR>	 1. Future or remote consequence.<BR>	 2. Future time.<BR>	 3. A<BR>plant (Vangueria spinosa:) see मदन.<BR> E. उद् much, ऋच् to praise,<BR>affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=120-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदर्च्चिस्|उदर्चिस्
उदर्च्चिस् mfn. (-र्च्चिः-र्च्चिः-र्च्चिः) Luminous and ascending.<BR>	 m. (-र्च्चिः)<BR>	 1. A<BR>name of VAHNI or fire.<BR>	 2. ŚIVA.<BR>	 3. KANDARPA.<BR> E. उद् upwards, and<BR>अर्च्चिस् flame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=120-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदर्द|उदर्दः|उदर्द्द
उदर्द m. (-र्दः) Erysipelas.<BR> E. उद् up, अर्द to go, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=120-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदर्द्ध
उदर्द्ध m. (-र्द्धः) Scarlet fever.<BR> E. उद् and ऋध to increase, अच aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=120-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदलावणिक|उदलावणिकः
उदलावणिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Salted, prepared with brine.<BR> E. उद् water,<BR>लवण salt and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=120-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदवज्र|उदवज्रः
उदवज्र m. (-ज्रः) A thunderbolt of water, a water spout.<BR> E. उद् and वज्र<BR>a thunderbolt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=120-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदवसित|उदवसितं
उदवसित n. (-तं) A house.<BR> E. उद् water, and वसित covered, defended, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=120-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदवास|उदवासः
उदवास n. (-सं)<BR>	 1. A house in the margin of a stream or pond.<BR>	 2. A<BR>marine grotto, &c.<BR> E. उद् and वास abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=120-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदवाहन
उदवाहन m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. A cloud.<BR>	 2. Any water vessel.<BR> E. उद् and वाहन<BR>vehicle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=120-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदविन्दु
उदविन्दु m. (-न्दुः) A drop of water.<BR> E. उद् and विन्दु a drop.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=120-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदश्वित्
उदश्वित् n. (-श्वित्) Buttermilk, with an equal proportion of water.<BR> E. उद्<BR>water, श्वि to increase, affixes क्विप् and तुक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=120-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदस्त
उदस्त mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं)<BR>	 1. Cast, thrown.<BR>	 2. Expelled, cast out.<BR>	 3. Cast<BR>up.<BR>	 4. Humbled, shamed.<BR>	 5. Scattered.<BR>	 6. Removed.<BR> E. उद् before<BR>अस् to throw, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=120-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदस्थाली
उदस्थाली f. (-ली) A caldron, a kettle.<BR> E. उद् water and स्थाली a pot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=120-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदस्य
उदस्य ind.<BR>	 1. Having taken pains, made an effort, &c.<BR>	 2. Having<BR>thrown, having cast up or tossed.<BR>	 3. Having scattered.<BR>	 4. Having<BR>expelled.<BR> E. उद् before अस् to be or throw, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=120-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदहार|उदहारः
उदहार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A water carrier.<BR>	 2. A cloud.<BR> E. उद and हार who<BR>takes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=120-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदाज|उदाजः
उदाज m. (-जः) Commanding, directing bodies of men.<BR> E. उद् before अज्<BR>to go, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=120-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदात्त|उदात्तं|उदात्तः
उदात्त mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं)<BR>	 1. Generous, gentle and bountiful.<BR>	 2. Giving, a<BR>donor.<BR>	 3. Great, illustrious.<BR>	 4. Dear, beloved.<BR>	 5. Accented.<BR>	 m. (-त्तः)<BR>1. The acute accent, a high or sharp tone.<BR>	 2. Gift, donation.<BR>	 3. A<BR>musical instrument, a large drum.<BR>	 4. An ornament, (in rhetoric)<BR>E. उद् high, up, and आत्त pronounced, sounded; or from दा to give<BR>or have, with आङ् prefixed, affix क्तः see अनुदात्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=120-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदान|उदानः
उदान m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. One of the five vital airs, that which rises up the<BR>throat and passes into the head.<BR>	 2. The navel.<BR>	 3. A snake.<BR>	 4. An<BR>eyelash.<BR> E. उद् above, आङ prefixed to अण to breathe, to be, affix<BR>घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=120-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदार|उदारः
उदार mfn. (-रः-रा-री-रं)<BR>	 1. Generous, liberal, munificent.<BR>	 2. Great.<BR>	 3.<BR>Unperplexed.<BR>	 4. Gentle.<BR>	 5. Upright, honest, sincere.<BR>	 6. Eloquent.<BR>7. Proper, right.<BR> E. उद् well, आङ् prefixed to ऋ to go, and अप्<BR>affixed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=120-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदारचेतस्
उदारचेतस् mfn. (-ताः-ताः-तः) High-minded, magnanimous.<BR> E. उदार and<BR>चेतस् the mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=120-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदारधी
उदारधी mfn. (-धीः-धीः-धि) Wise, sagacious, noble-minded.<BR> E. उदार and<BR>धी understanding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=120-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदावत्सर|उदावत्सरः
उदावत्सर m. (-रः) A year, one of the five sorts of years astrologically<BR>considered.<BR> E. उद् and आङ् before वत्सर a year.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=120-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदावर्त्त|उदावर्त|उदावर्तः|उदावर्त्तः
उदावर्त्त m. (-र्त्तः) A disease of the bowels, iliac passion.<BR>	 f. (-ता) Difficult<BR>menstruation.<BR> E. उद् upper, आवर्त्त abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=120-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदास|उदासः
उदास m. (-सः)<BR>	 1. Throwing or directing upwards.<BR>	 2. Elevation, being<BR>above or over.<BR>	 3. A stoic, a philosopher.<BR>	 4. Stoicism.<BR>	 mfn. (-सः-सा-सं)<BR>Indifferent, unconcerned, apathetic.<BR> E. उद् and आस who casts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=120-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदासितृ
उदासितृ mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ) Indifferent, disregarding, void of concern or<BR>affection.<BR> E. उद् before आस् to cast, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=120-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदासिन्
उदासिन् mfn. (-सी-सिनी-सि) Indifferent, disregarding.<BR>	 m. (-सी) A stoic, a<BR>philosopher, one who has no passion nor affection for anything:<BR>in popular acceptation, a religious mendicant in general, or one<BR>of a particular order.<BR> E. उदास and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=120-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदासीन|उदासीनः
उदासीन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>	 1. Indifferent, free from affection. (In law,) One<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=121-a" target="_blank">Page121-a+ 60</a>]<BR>not involved in the dispute.<BR>	 m. (-नः) A stranger, a neutral, a com-<BR>mon acquaintance, a person neither a friend, nor a foe.<BR> E. उद्<BR>above, आसीन seated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=120-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदास्थित|उदास्थितः
उदास्थित m. (-तः)<BR>	 1. A spy, an emissary.<BR>	 2. A doorkeeper.<BR>	 3. superin-<BR>tendent.<BR>	 mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Set over.<BR> E. उद् over, आङ् before स्था to<BR>stay, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=121-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदाहरण|उदाहरणं
उदाहरण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. An example or illustration, an opposite argument,<BR>one of five modes of logical reasoning.<BR>	 2. Declaring, saying.<BR> E. उद्<BR>over, आङ् before हृ to convey, and ल्युट् affix, or with घञ् affix<BR>उदाहार.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=121-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदाहार|उदाहारः
उदाहार m. (-रः) See the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=121-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदाहृत
उदाहृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Called, named, entitled.<BR>	 2. Said.<BR>	 3. Illustrat-<BR>ed.<BR> E. उद् and आङ् before हृ to take, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=121-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदित|उदितः
उदित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Said, spoken.<BR>	 2. Bound, tied.<BR>	 3. Risen, ascended.<BR>4. Grown, augmented.<BR>	 5. Born, produced.<BR>	 6. Incurred, experienced.<BR>7. High, tall, lofty.<BR> E. वद् to speak, and क्त affix; or उद् up, and इत<BR>gone, past part. of इण् to go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=121-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदितोदित|उदितोदितः
उदितोदित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Well acquainted with the Śāstras.<BR> E. उदित<BR>said, (by law and religion,) and उदित risen, &c. eminent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=121-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदीक्षण|उदीक्षणं
उदीक्षण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Seeing, beholding.<BR>	 2. Looking up.<BR> E. उद् and ईक्ष् to<BR>see, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=121-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदीक्ष्य
उदीक्ष्य ind. Having seen.<BR> E. उद् and ईक्ष् to see, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=121-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदीची
उदीची f. (-ची) The north: see उदच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=121-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदीचीन|उदीचीनं
उदीचीन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Northern.<BR> E. उदच् north, ख aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=121-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदीच्य|उदीच्यं|उदीच्यः
उदीच्य m. (-च्यः) The country to the north and west of the river Sarasvatī,<BR>the northern region.<BR>	 n. (-च्यं) A perfume: see बाला.<BR> E. उदीची<BR>the north, and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=121-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदीरण|उदीरणं
उदीरण n. (-णं) Speaking, saying.<BR> E. उद् up, out, ईर् to go, and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=121-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदीरित
उदीरित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Said, uttered.<BR> E. उद् and ईर to go, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=121-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदीर्ण|उदीर्णः
उदीर्ण mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-र्णं)<BR>	 1. Generous, great, excellent.<BR>	 2. Intense.<BR> E. उद्<BR>above, ऋ to go, affix क्त, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=121-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदीर्णवेग
उदीर्णवेग mfn. (-गः-गा-गं) Impetuous (as a torrent), violent.<BR> E. उदीर्ण and वेग speed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=121-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदीर्य्य|उदीर्य
उदीर्य्य mfn. (-र्य्यः-र्य्या-र्य्यं) To be spoken.<BR> E. उत् before ईर् to go, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=121-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदीर्य्यमाण|उदीर्यमाण
उदीर्य्यमाण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>	 1. Speaking.<BR>	 2. Spoken.<BR> E. उद् before ईर् to<BR>go, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=121-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदुम्बर|उदुंबर|उदुम्बरं|उदुंबरः|उदुम्बरः
उदुम्बर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. The glomerous fig tree, (Ficus glomerata.)<BR>	 2. A kind<BR>of leprosy.<BR>	 3. A threshold.<BR>	 4. A eunuch.<BR>	 n. (-रं) Copper; see<BR>उडुम्बर, it is also written ऊडुम्बर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=121-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदुम्बरपर्णी|उदुम्बरपर्ण्णी
उदुम्बरपर्णी f. (-र्णी) A plant: see दन्तिका; also उडुम्बरपर्णी and ऊडुम्बरपर्णी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=121-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदूखल|उदूखलं
उदूखल n. (-लं) A gum-resin, Bdellium.<BR>	 mn. (-लः-लं) A wooden mortar<BR>used for freeing rice from the husk, by pounding it with a pestle.<BR>2. Any mortar.<BR> E. उदू for उद् up, and खल what goes, affix अच्; also<BR>उडूखल and उलूखल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=121-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदूढ|उदूढः
उदूढ mfn. (-ढः-ढा-ढं)<BR>	 1. Married.<BR>	 2. Coarse, gross, heavy.<BR>	 3. Material,<BR>substantial.<BR>	 4. Much, exceeding.<BR> E. उद् up, वह् to bear, and क्त<BR>affix, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=121-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदेजय
उदेजय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Shaking, making tremble.<BR> E. उद् before एज् to<BR>tremble, श aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=121-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्ग
उद्ग r. 6th cl. (उद्गति) To cast off or quit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=121-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्गत|उद्गतं
उद्गत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Risen, ascended.<BR>	 2. Vomited, cast up.<BR>	 3. De-<BR>parted, gone.<BR>	 4. Proceeded forth or from.<BR> E. उद् up, and गत gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=121-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्गता
उद्गता f. (-ता) A stanza of four lines, with ten syllables in the three first,<BR>and thirteen in the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=121-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्गतासु
उद्गतासु mfn. (-सुः-सुः-सु) Deceased, dead.<BR> E. उद्गत gone, असु breath.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=121-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्गति|उद्गतिः
उद्गति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Going up, rising, ascending.<BR>	 2. Bringing up, vomit-<BR>ing.<BR> E. उद् and गति going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=121-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्गम|उद्गमः
उद्गम m. (-मः)<BR>	 1. Going up, rising, ascending.<BR>	 2. Bringing up, vomit-<BR>ing; also उद्गमनं.<BR> E. उद् up, गम or गमन going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=121-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्गमनीय|उद्गमनीयं
उद्गमनीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) To be gone up, or ascended.<BR>	 n. (-यं) A pair of<BR>bleached clothes.<BR> E. उद् up, गम् to go, and अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=121-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्गाढ|उद्गाढं
उद्गाढ n. adv. (-ढं) or. adj.<BR>	 mfn. (-ढः-ढा-ढं) Much, excessive.<BR> E. उद् excess,<BR>and गाढ much.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=121-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्गातृ
उद्गातृ m. (-ता) A reciter of the prayers, &c. of the Sama Veda.<BR> E. उद्<BR>up, and गातृ who sings, (the prayers being chanted,) from गै to<BR>sing, and तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=121-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्गाथा
उद्गाथा f. (-था) A variety of the Āryā measure, the same as the Gīti, a<BR>stanza of four lines containing alternately 12 and 18 instants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=121-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्गार|उद्गारः
उद्गार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Vomiting.<BR>	 2. Ejecting anything from the mouth.<BR>3. Sound.<BR>	 4. Speaking in the throat.<BR> E. उद् up, गॄ to vomit,<BR>&c. घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=121-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्गिरण|उद्गिरणं
उद्गिरण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Vomiting.<BR>	 2. Ejecting anything, as saliva, &c. from<BR>the mouth.<BR> E. उद् before गॄ to vomit, ल्युट् affix; also उद्गरणं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=121-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्गीति|उद्गीतिः
उद्गीति f. (-तिः) A variety of the Āryā metre, a verse of four lines con-<BR>taining 12, 15--12, and 14 feet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=121-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्गीथ|उद्गीथः
उद्गीथ m. (-थः)<BR>	 1. A portion of the Sama Veda.<BR>	 2. Designation of the<BR>triliteral name of God.<BR>	 3. Chaunting the Sama Veda.<BR> E. उद् up,<BR>aloud, गै to sing, and थक् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=121-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्गुर्ण
उद्गुर्ण mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-र्णं)<BR>	 1. Raised, lifted, held up.<BR>	 2. Erected.<BR>	 3. Excited.<BR>E. उद् up, गुर् to make effort, irr. participle past.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=121-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्ग्रह|उद्ग्रहः
उद्ग्रह m. (-हः)<BR>	 1. Taking up.<BR>	 2. An object that may be accomplished by<BR>religious or other acts.<BR> E. उद् before ग्रह् to take, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=121-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्ग्रहण|उद्ग्रहणं
उद्ग्रहण n. (-णं) Taking up, lifting up<BR> E. उद् and ग्रहण taking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=121-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्ग्राह|उद्ग्राहः
उद्ग्राह m. (-हः)<BR>	 1. Taking up.<BR>	 2. Replying in argument.<BR> E. उत् up, ग्रह्<BR>to take, and घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=121-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्ग्राहित|उद्ग्राहितः
उद्ग्राहित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Excellent, exalted.<BR>	 2. Bound, tied.<BR>	 3. Seized,<BR>4. Deposited, delivered.<BR>	 5. Taken or lifted up.<BR>	 6. Recalled, re-<BR>membered.<BR> E. उद् up, and ग्राहित taken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=121-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्घ|उद्घः
उद्घ m. (-द्घः) Excellence, happiness.<BR> E. उत् much, घण् to shine, affix ड or<BR>उद् before हन् to strike, अप् aff. and the final rejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=121-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्घन|उद्घनः
उद्घन m. (-नः) A carpenter's work-bench, a plank on which he works. E.<BR>उत् above, हन् to injure, अप् affix, ह changed to घ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=121-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्घट्टन|उद्घट्टनं
उद्घट्टन n. (-नं) Opening, opening up as a lid.<BR> E. उत् up, and घट्टन fastening.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=121-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्घट्टित
उद्घट्टित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Opened, unlocked.<BR> E. उत् up, and घट्टित fastened.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=121-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्घर्षण|उद्घर्षणं
उद्घर्षण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Rubbing, rubbing up.<BR>	 2. Rubbing the skin with hard<BR>substances, as vitrified brick, &c.<BR> E. उद् and घर्षण friction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=121-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्घस|उद्घसं
उद्घस n. (-सं) Flesh.<BR> E. उत्, घस substituted for अद् to eat, affix अप्; what<BR>is eaten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=121-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्घाट|उद्घाटः
उद्घाट m. (-टः) A watch or guard house.<BR> E. उत् up, घट् to endeavour, &c. घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=121-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्घाटक|उद्घाटकं|उद्घाटकः
उद्घाटक mn. (-कः-कं)<BR>	 1. A key.<BR>	 2. A bucket, &c. see the next.<BR>	 3. An<BR>opener, the instrument or agent of opening anything.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=121-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्घाटन|उद्घाटनं
उद्घाटन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. The rope and bucket of a well, a leather bucket<BR>used for drawing water.<BR>	 2. Opening, unlocking.<BR>	 3. An opener, the<BR>instrument or means of opening, a key, &c.<BR>	 4. Hoisting, raising,<BR>lifting up.<BR> E. उत् up, घट् to strive, affix ल्युट्; also with वुन् affix<BR>उद्घाटक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=121-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्घाटित|उद्घाटितः
उद्घाटित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Done with effort, exerted.<BR>	 2. Opened.<BR>	 3.<BR>Raised, hoisted or lifted up.<BR> E. उद् much, घट् to exert, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=121-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्घाटितज्ञ|उद्घाटितज्ञः
उद्घाटितज्ञ mfn. (-ज्ञः-ज्ञा-ज्ञं) Wise, intelligent.<BR> E. उत् much, घट् to endeav-<BR>our, affix क्त, and ज्ञ who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=121-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्घाटिताङ्ग
उद्घाटिताङ्ग mfn. (-ङ्गः-ङ्गा-ङ्गं)<BR>	 1. Intelligent.<BR>	 2. Naked.<BR> E. उद्घाटित and<BR>अङ्ग the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=121-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्घात|उद्घातः
उद्घात m. (-तः)<BR>	 1. A beginning, a thing begun.<BR>	 2. A weapon.<BR>	 3. A club,<BR>a mallet.<BR>	 4. Striking, wounding, inflicting a hurt.<BR>	 5. A wound, a<BR>blow.<BR>	 6. The division of a book, a chapter, a section.<BR>	 7. Breathing<BR>through the nostrils as a religious exercise.<BR>	 8. Slipping, tripping.<BR>9. High, tall.<BR> E. उत् before हन् to kill or destroy, and घञ् affix,<BR>त is substituted for न.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=121-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्ज
उद्ज r. 6th cl. (उज्जति) To be straight: see उज्ज.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=121-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्झ
उद्झ r. 6th cl. See उञ्झ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=121-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्घुष्ट
उद्घुष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं) Sounded out.<BR> E. उत् before घुष् to sound, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=121-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्दंश|उद्दंशः
उद्दंश m. (-शः) A bug.<BR> E. उत् much, and दंश who bites, from दशि and<BR>अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=122-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्दण्ड|उद्दंड|उद्दण्डः
उद्दण्ड mfn. (-ण्डः-ण्डा-ण्डं) Raised on a staff or pole.<BR> E. उत् and दण्ड a stick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=122-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्दण्डपाल|उद्दंडपाल|उद्दण्डपालः
उद्दण्डपाल m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. A sort of snake.<BR>	 2. A kind of fish.<BR>	 3. A punisher,<BR>whether king or magistrate.<BR> E. उत् above, दण्डपाल a punisher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=122-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्दन्तुर|उद्दंतुर|उद्दन्तुरः
उद्दन्तुर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>	 1. High, tall.<BR>	 2. Terrific, formidable.<BR>	 3. Large<BR>toothed.<BR> E. उत् high, long, and दन्तुर large toothed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=122-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्दान|उद्दानं
उद्दान n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Binding, confinement.<BR>	 2. Taming, subduing.<BR>	 3. A fire-<BR>place.<BR>	 4. Submarine fire.<BR>	 5. The middle, the waist.<BR>	 6. The en-<BR>trance of the sun into a sign of the zodiac.<BR> E. उत् reverse, and दा<BR>to give, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=122-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्दान्त|उद्दांत
उद्दान्त mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं)<BR>	 1. Energetic.<BR>	 2. Humble.<BR>	 3. Elevated.<BR>	 4. Vomit-<BR>ed by an elephant.<BR> E. उत् and दान्त tamed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=122-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्दाम|उद्दामः
उद्दाम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>	 1. Set free, unbound.<BR>	 2. Unconstrained, self-willed.<BR>3. Large, great.<BR>	 4. Proud, haughty.<BR>	 m. (-मः) A name of<BR>VARUṆA.<BR> E. उत् priv. दम् to tame, and घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=122-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्दाल|उद्दालः
उद्दाल m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. A plant, (Cordia myxa or latifolia.)<BR>	 2. A kind of<BR>grain, (Paspalum frumentaceum.)<BR> E. उत् high, large. दल् to pierce,<BR>affix घञ्; also उद्दालक, क being added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=122-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्दित|उद्दितः
उद्दित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Bound, tied.<BR> E. उद् up, दो to cut, and क्त affix; also उदित.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=122-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्दिन|उद्दिनं
उद्दिन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Mid-day.<BR>	 2. Every day.<BR> E. उत् and दिन day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=122-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्दिश्य
उद्दिश्य ind. Having shown or explained.<BR>	 2. Stipulating for, demanding.<BR>E. उत्, दिश् to show, य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=122-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्दिष्ट
उद्दिष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>	 1. Mentioned, particularised, described.<BR>	 2. Pro-<BR>mised.<BR> E. उत् before दिश् to show, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=122-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्दीप|उद्दीपः
उद्दीप n. (-पं) A gummy and resinous substance, Bdellium.<BR>	 m. (-पः)<BR>	 1.<BR>Inflaming, lighting.<BR>	 2. An enflamer.<BR>	 3. Animating, or who or<BR>what animates.<BR> E. उत्, दीप् to shine, क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=122-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्दीपक|उद्दीपकः
उद्दीपक mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>	 1. Exciting, inflaming, rendering more intense.<BR>2. Lighting, setting alight.<BR> E. उद् and दीपक what lights.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=122-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्दीपन|उद्दीपनं
उद्दीपन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Exciting, inflaming as passion.<BR>	 2. Illuminating.<BR>	 3.<BR>Burning of a body, &c.<BR>	 4. Any aggravating thing or circumstance,<BR>calculated to give poignancy to feeling or passion.<BR> E. उद् much,<BR>दीप् to inflame, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=122-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्दीपमान
उद्दीपमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Lighting up, brightening, becoming light. E.<BR>उद् before दीप् and शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=122-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्दीप्त|उद्दीप्तः
उद्दीप्त mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं)<BR>	 1. Lighted, set on fire or alight.<BR>	 2. Inflamed,<BR>aggravated, as passion.<BR> E. उद् and दीप्त lighted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=122-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्दीप्र|उद्दीप्रं|उद्दीप्रः
उद्दीप्र n. (-प्रं) Bdellium.<BR> E. उद् before दीप् to shine, रक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=122-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्देश|उद्देशः
उद्देश m. (-शः)<BR>	 1. Illustration, explanation, exemplification.<BR>	 2.<BR>Search, enquiry.<BR>	 3. Stipulation, bargain.<BR>	 4. An object, a motive.<BR>mfn. (-शः-शा-शं) Relative to.<BR> E. उद् and देश showing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=122-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्देशक|उद्देशकः
उद्देशक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) What explains or shows, illustrative, explana-<BR>tory.<BR>	 m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. An illustration, an example.<BR>	 2. An illustrator.<BR>3. A guide.<BR> E. उद् before दिश् to show, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=122-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्देश्य|उद्देश्यः
उद्देश्य mfn. (-श्यः-श्या-श्यं) To be illustrated or explained.<BR> E. उद्, दिश् to<BR>show, ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=122-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्देहिका
उद्देहिका f. (-का) The white ant, termes; also उत्यादिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=122-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्द्योत|उद्द्योतः
उद्द्योत m. (-तः) Light, lustre.<BR> E. उद्, द्युत् to shine, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=122-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्द्राव|उद्द्रावः
उद्द्राव m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. Flight, retreat.<BR>	 2. Going upwards.<BR> E. उद् up, द्रु to run,<BR>and घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=122-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्द्रुत
उद्द्रुत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Fled, retreated, run away.<BR>	 2. Ascended, gone<BR>up or upwards.<BR> E. उद् and द्रुत gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=122-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्धत|उद्धतं|उद्धतः
उद्धत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Rude, ill-behaved.<BR>	 2. Haughty, vain, puffed<BR>up.<BR>	 3. Raised, elevated.<BR>	 4. Excited, intense.<BR>	 m. (-तः) A king's<BR>wrestler.<BR> E. उद् above, हन् to hurt or injure, affix क्त; ह becomes ध.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=122-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्धतमनस्क
उद्धतमनस्क mfn. (-स्कः-स्का-स्कं) Haughty, proud, high-minded.<BR> E. उद्धत<BR>raised, मनस्क minded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=122-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्धतमनस्कत्व|उद्धतमनस्कत्वं
उद्धतमनस्कत्व n. (-त्वं) Pride, arrogance.<BR> E. उद्धत, मनस्क having a mind,<BR>and त्व abstract aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=122-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्धति|उद्धतिः
उद्धति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Pride, haughtiness.<BR>	 2. Elevation.<BR> E. उद् before हन् to<BR>strike, affix क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=122-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्धम|उद्धमः
उद्धम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं) Who or what blows.<BR>	 m. (-मः)<BR>	 1. Breathing hard,<BR>panting.<BR>	 2. Blowing, sounding.<BR> E. उद् before ध्मा to blow, affix श.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=122-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्धय
उद्धय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Who or what drinks.<BR> E. उद् before धे to drink,<BR>श aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=122-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्धर्तृ|उद्धर्त्तृ
उद्धर्तृ mfn. (-र्ता-र्त्री-र्तृ)<BR>	 1. Who raises or lifts up.<BR>	 2. A sharer, a coheir.<BR>3. Who recovers property.<BR> E. उद् before हृ to take, तृन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=122-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्धरण|उद्धरणं
उद्धरण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Raising or lifting anything.<BR>	 2. Eradicating a tree, &c.<BR>3. Exterminating, destroying.<BR>	 4. Taking a part or share.<BR>	 5. Vomit-<BR>ing, bringing up.<BR>	 6. Final emancipation.<BR> E. उद् up, हृ to take, and<BR>ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=122-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्धरणीय
उद्धरणीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>	 1. To be raised up.<BR>	 2. To be given up.<BR> E. उत्<BR>before हरणीय to be taken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=122-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्धर्ष|उद्धर्षः
उद्धर्ष m. (-र्षः)<BR>	 1. A festival, especially religious.<BR>	 2. Great joy.<BR> E. उत्<BR>much, हर्ष happiness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=122-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्धर्षण|उद्धर्षणं
उद्धर्षण n. (-णं) Erection of the hair of the body.<BR> E. उद् much, हृष् to be<BR>happy, and ल्युट् affix; occasioned by great pleasure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=122-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्धव|उद्धवः
उद्धव m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. A festival, a holiday.<BR>	 2. Sacrificial fire.<BR>	 3. The name of<BR>a person, the friend and counsellor of KṚṢṆA.<BR> E. उद् reverse, धु<BR>to feel pain, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=122-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्धान|उद्धानं|उद्धानः
उद्धान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>	 1. Gone up, ascended.<BR>	 2. Vomited.<BR>	 n. (-नं) A fur-<BR>nace or fireplace.<BR> E. उद्, धा to have or hold, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=122-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्धान्त|उद्धांत|उद्धान्तः
उद्धान्त mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं) Vomited.<BR>	 m. (-न्तः) An elephant out of rut.<BR> E. उद्<BR>up, and ध्मा to breathe or blow, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=122-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्धार|उद्धारं|उद्धारः
उद्धार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Raising, elevating, lifting up.<BR>	 2. Debt, especially a debt<BR>not bearing interest.<BR>	 3. A portion, a share.<BR>	 4. A deduction, a part<BR>to be set aside.<BR>	 5. Recovering property.<BR>	 6. Extracting, quoting.<BR>	 n.<BR>(-रं) A fireplace.<BR>	 f. (-रा) A plant, (Menispermum glabrum); see<BR>गुडूची.<BR> E. उत् up, धृ to have, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=122-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्धारक
उद्धारक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Who or what raises or lifts.<BR> E. उत् before हृ to<BR>take, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=122-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्धारण|उद्धारणं
उद्धारण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Raising, elevating.<BR>	 2. Sharing, dividing.<BR> E. उद् be-<BR>fore धृ to have, causal form, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=122-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्धारविभाग|उद्धारविभागः
उद्धारविभाग m. (-गः) Partition, division of shares.<BR> E. उद्धार and विभाग<BR>dividing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=122-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्धुर
उद्धुर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>	 1. Heavy.<BR>	 2. Thick, gross.<BR>	 3. Firm.<BR> E. उत् and धुर<BR>a burden.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=122-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्धूत
उद्धूत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Shaken off, fallen from or off.<BR>	 2. Tossed up,<BR>scattered above.<BR> E. उत् and धूत trembling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=122-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्धूषण|उद्धूषणं
उद्धूषण n. (-णं) Horripilation.<BR> E. उत up, धूष to shine, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=122-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्धृत|उद्धृतः
उद्धृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Raised, drawn up, as water from a well, &c.<BR>	 2.<BR>Pulled up or out, eradicated or broken off.<BR>	 3. Lifted up.<BR>	 4. Raised,<BR>elevated.<BR>	 5. Thrown up or upwards.<BR>	 6. Vomited.<BR>	 7. Separated,<BR>set apart.<BR>	 8. Divided, partitioned.<BR>	 9. Recovered.<BR>	 10. Uncovered.<BR>11. Dispersed, scattered.<BR>	 12. Extracted, selected, taken from or out<BR>of.<BR>	 13. Holding, containing.<BR> E. उत् up, धृ to take, and क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=122-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्धृतोद्धार
उद्धृतोद्धार mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>	 1. One who has received his share.<BR>	 2. That<BR>from which a share has been deducted.<BR> E. उद्धृत and उद्धार a share.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=122-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्ध्य|उद्ध्यः
उद्ध्य m. (-द्ध्यः) A river.<BR> E. उञ्झ to go, क्यप् affix, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=122-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्ध्मान|उद्ध्मानं
उद्ध्मान n. (-नं) A furnace or fireplace.<BR> E. उत्, ध्मा to blow, and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=122-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्बन्धन|उद्बंधन
उद्बन्धन n. (-नं) Tying up, hanging.<BR> E. उत् and बन्धन tying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=122-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्बाहु
उद्बाहु mfn. (-हुः-ह्वी-हु)<BR>	 1. Having the arms lifted up.<BR>	 2. Having the<BR>trunk upraised (as an elephant.)<BR> E. उत् and बाहु the arm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=122-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्बुद्ध|उद्बुद्धः
उद्बुद्ध mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>	 1. Blown, budded.<BR>	 2. Reminded, made to think of<BR>or recalled.<BR>	 3. Awaked.<BR> E. उत् forth, up, and बुद्ध known.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=122-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्बुद्धसंस्कार|उद्बुद्धसंस्कारः
उद्बुद्धसंस्कार m. (-रः) Association of ideas recalling anything to remem-<BR>brance.<BR> E. उद्बुद्ध and संस्कार faculty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=122-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्बोध|उद्बोधः
उद्बोध m. (-धः)<BR>	 1. Incipient knowledge.<BR>	 2. Awaking.<BR>	 3. Reminding. E.<BR>उत् and बोध knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=122-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्बोधक|उद्बोधकः
उद्बोधक mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>	 1. Discovering, exhibiting.<BR>	 2. What reminds, or<BR>calls to remembrance.<BR> E. उत् and बोधक making known.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=123-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्बोधन|उद्बोधनं
उद्बोधन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Recalling, reminding.<BR>	 2. Awaking, arousing.<BR> E. उत्<BR>before बुध to know, causal form, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=123-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्भट|उद्भटः
उद्भट mfn. (-टः-टा-टं)<BR>	 1. Excellent.<BR>	 2. Exalted, magnanimous.<BR>	 m. (-टः)<BR>	 1.<BR>A tortoise.<BR>	 2. The sun.<BR> E. उत् lofty, भट् to desire, and अच् affix;<BR>high-minded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=123-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्भव|उद्भवः
उद्भव m. (-वः) Birth, production.<BR> E. उत् forth, भू to be or become, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=123-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्भवकर
उद्भवकर mfn. (-रः-रा-री-रं) Productive.<BR> E. उद्भव, and कर what makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=123-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्भाव|उद्भावः
उद्भाव m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. Production, generation.<BR>	 2. Magnanimity.<BR> E. उत्, भाव<BR>causing to be, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=123-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्भावन|उद्भावनं
उद्भावन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Inattention, neglect, disregard.<BR>	 2. Saying, speaking.<BR>E. उत् away or up, भावन observing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=123-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्भावित
उद्भावित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Neglected, disregarded.<BR>	 2. Said, declared. E.<BR>उत् and भावित made known.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=123-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्भास|उद्भासः
उद्भास m. (-सः) Radiance, splendor.<BR> E. उत् and भास shining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=123-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्भासयत्
उद्भासयत् mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्) Lighting up, irradiating.<BR> E. उत् before भास<BR>to shine, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=123-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्भासित
उद्भासित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Lighting up, illuminated, splendid.<BR>	 2. Orna-<BR>mented, graced, beautified.<BR> E. उत् before भास to shine, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=123-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्भिज|उद्भिजः
उद्भिज mfn. (-जः-जा-जं) See the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=123-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्भिज्ज|उद्भिज्जं|उद्भिज्जः
उद्भिज्ज mfn. (-ज्जः-ज्जा-ज्जं) Sprouting, germinating. (as a vegetable.) E.<BR>उद्भिद् a vegetable, and ज produced; also उद्भिज one ज being drop-<BR>ped; also उद्भिद्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=123-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्भिद्
उद्भिद् mfn. (-द्भिद् or -द्भित्) Sprouting, germinating.<BR> E. उत् up, भिद to<BR>break or burst, affix क्विप्, or with क affix उद्भिद (दः-दा-दं) n. (-दं)<BR>Culinary salt.<BR> E. उत् forth, भिद् to break, and क affix; breaking<BR>from the soil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=123-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्भिद|उद्भिदं
उद्भिद n. (-दं) Sprouting, &c. E. See the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=123-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्भिन्न
उद्भिन्न mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>	 1. Opened, burst.<BR>	 2. Budded.<BR> E. उत् up, and भिन्न broken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=123-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्भूत|उद्भूतः
उद्भूत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Born, produced.<BR>	 2. Lofty, literally or figura-<BR>tively.<BR>	 3. Visible, perceptible, present.<BR> E. उत् before भू to be, affix<BR>क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=123-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्भूतरूप|उद्भूतरूपं
उद्भूतरूप n. (-पं) Visible shape or form.<BR> E. उद्भूत and रूप form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=123-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्भ्रम|उद्भ्रमः
उद्भ्रम n. (-मं)<BR>	 1. Regret.<BR>	 2. Whirling, flourishing.<BR> E. उत् much, भ्रम to<BR>wander, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=123-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्भ्रान्त|उद्भ्रांत|उद्भ्रान्तं
उद्भ्रान्त mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं)<BR>	 1. Agitated, bewildered, distressed.<BR>	 2. Whirled,<BR>flourished, waved (as a sword).<BR> E. उत् and भ्रान्त revolved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=123-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्य|उद्यः
उद्य m. (-द्यः) A river.<BR> E. उद् water, and य what goes, from या to go,<BR>and ड aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=123-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्यत|उद्यतं|उद्यतः
उद्यत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Raised, held up.<BR>	 2. Active, persevering, labouring<BR>diligently and incessantly.<BR>	 3. Trained, exercised, disciplined.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-तः) A section, a chapter, the division of a book.<BR> E. उत् before यम्<BR>to cease, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=123-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्यम|उद्यमः
उद्यम m. (-मः)<BR>	 1. Strenuous and continued effort, exertion, persever-<BR>ance.<BR>	 2. Taking or lifting up.<BR> E. उद् reverse, यम् to cease, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=123-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्यमिन्
उद्यमिन् mfn. (-मी-मिनी-मि) Persevering, active, making effort.<BR> E. उद्यम<BR>and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=123-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्यम्य
उद्यम्य mfn. (-म्यः-म्या-म्यं) Requiring exertion. ind. Having lifted or<BR>taken up.<BR>	 2. Having made exertion.<BR> E. उत् before यम् to cease,<BR>यत् and ल्यप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=123-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्यान|उद्यानं|उद्यानः
उद्यान n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. A garden.<BR>	 2. A royal garden, a park.<BR>	 3. Going forth,<BR>exit.<BR>	 4. Purpose, motive.<BR> E. उद् up, या to go, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=123-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्यानपाल|उद्यानपालः
उद्यानपाल m. (-लः) A gardener.<BR>	 2. The master or owner of a garden. E.<BR>उद्यान and पाल who takes care of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=123-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्याव|उद्यावः
उद्याव m. (-वः) Mixing, joining.<BR> E. उद् before यु to mix, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=123-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्युक्त|उद्युक्तः
उद्युक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं) Zealously active, labouring for some desired<BR>end.<BR> E. उद्, युज् to join, क्त affix; also उद्यत.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=123-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्योग|उद्योगः
उद्योग m. (-गः) Exertion, perseverance, strenuous and continued endeav-<BR>our.<BR> E. उद्, युज् to join, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=123-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्योगिन्
उद्योगिन् mfn. (-गी-गिनी-गि) Active, laborious, persevering, one who makes<BR>effort.<BR> E. उद्योग and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=123-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्र|उद्रः
उद्र m. (-द्रः) An otter.<BR> E. उन्दी to wet, and रक् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=123-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्रङ्ग|उद्रंगः|उद्रङ्गः
उद्रङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः) An imaginary city, one floating in the air.<BR> E. उद् above,<BR>and द्रङ्ग a town, one द rejected; also read उद्रङ्क, see<BR>हरिश्चन्द्रपूर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=123-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्रथ|उद्रथः
उद्रथ m. (-थः)<BR>	 1. The pin of the axle of a carriage.<BR>	 2. A cock.<BR> E. उद् up,<BR>and रथ a carriage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=123-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्राव|उद्रावः
उद्राव m. (-वः) A loud noise.<BR> E. उत् before रु to cry, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=123-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्रिक्त|उद्रिक्तं
उद्रिक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>	 1. Distinct, evident.<BR>	 2. Increased, augmented.<BR>E. उद्, रिच् to flow, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=123-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्रुज
उद्रुज mfn. (-जः-जा-जं) Destroying, breaking down.<BR> E. उद् on, रुज् to<BR>injure, क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=123-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्रेक|उद्रेकः
उद्रेक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. Commencement.<BR>	 2. Increase.<BR>	 3. Excess.<BR> E. उत्, रिच् to flow, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=123-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वत्सर|उद्वत्सरः
उद्वत्सर m. (-रः) A year.<BR> E. उत्, वत्सर a year.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=123-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वमन|उद्वमनं
उद्वमन n. (-नं) Vomiting, bringing up.<BR> E. उत्, and वमन vomiting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=123-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वर्त्त|उद्वर्त|उद्वर्तः|उद्वर्त्तः
उद्वर्त्त mfn. (-र्त्तः-र्त्ता-र्त्तं)<BR>	 1. Abundant, plentiful.<BR>	 2. Left over.<BR>	 m. (-र्त्तः) A<BR>remainder, a surplus.<BR> E. उत् much, वृत् to be, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=123-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वर्त्तक|उद्वर्तक|उद्वर्तकः
उद्वर्त्तक mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>	 1. Rubbing and cleaning the body, (who or what<BR>does so.)<BR>	 2. Causing increase.<BR>	 m. (-कः) (In algebra,) An assumed<BR>quantity.<BR> E. उद् over, वृत् to be, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=123-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वर्त्तन|उद्वर्तन|उद्वर्तनं|उद्वर्त्तनं
उद्वर्त्तन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Going up, rising, ascending.<BR>	 2. Grinding, pounding.<BR>3. Rubbing or kneading the body.<BR>	 4. Rubbing and cleaning it with<BR>fragrant unguents.<BR>	 5. Unguents. used for that purpose, or to<BR>relieve pains in the limbs, &c.<BR>	 6. Rising, (figuratively) prosperity,<BR>elevation.<BR>	 7. Misbehaving.<BR>	 8. Springing up of plants or grain, &c.<BR>9. Drawing out metal, laminating, wire drawing, &c.<BR> E. उद् up,<BR>and वर्त्तन abiding, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=123-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वर्त्तित|उद्वर्तित
उद्वर्त्तित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Perfumed, scented.<BR>	 2. Risen, elevated.<BR>	 3.<BR>Sprung up.<BR>	 4. Drawn out.<BR> E. उत् before वृत् to be, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=123-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वर्द्धन
उद्वर्द्धन n. (-नं) A sly or suppressed laugh.<BR> E. उत् priv. वृध् to increase, and<BR>ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=123-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वर्हित|उद्वर्हितः
उद्वर्हित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Raised, drawn or lifted up.<BR>	 2. Eradicated. E.<BR>उत् up, and वर्हित injured; also उद्वाहित, from वाह् to endeavour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=123-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वह|उद्वहः
उद्वह mf. (-हः-हा) A son or a daughter.<BR>	 m. (-हः)<BR>	 1. The vital air that<BR>conveys nourishment, &c. upwards.<BR>	 2. A chief, a leader, the head<BR>of a family or force.<BR>	 mfn. (-हः-हा-हं)<BR>	 1. Who or what takes up or<BR>away.<BR>	 2. Best, most eminent.<BR> E. उत् further, वह what bears; crrry-<BR>ing on one's name, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=123-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वहत्
उद्वहत् mfn. (-हन्-हन्ती-हत्)<BR>	 1. Upholding, supporting, bearing, contain-<BR>ing.<BR>	 2. Having, possessing, assuming.<BR> E. उत् before वह् to bear, शतृ<BR>affix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=123-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वान|उद्वानः
उद्वान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Vomited.<BR> E. उद् up, वम् to vomit, क्त affix: see<BR>उद्वान्त and उद्धान.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=123-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वान्त|उद्वांत|उद्वान्तं|उद्वान्तः
उद्वान्त mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं) Vomited.<BR>	 m. (-न्तः) An elephant out of rut. E.<BR>उत्, वम् to vomit, affix क्त, deriv. irr. see उद्धान्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=123-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वाप|उद्वापः
उद्वाप m. (-पः) (In logic,) nonexistence of a subsequent consequent on<BR>the absence of an antecedent.<BR> E. उद् before वप् to sow, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=123-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वास|उद्वासः
उद्वास m. (-सः)<BR>	 1. Abandoning, letting loose or free.<BR>	 2. Exile.<BR>	 3. Kill-<BR>ing.<BR> E. उद् away, वस् to abide, causal form, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=123-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वासन|उद्वासनं
उद्वासन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Quitting, abandoning.<BR>	 2. Expelling, banishing.<BR>	 3.<BR>Killing, slaughter.<BR> E. उत् forth, out, वस् to abide, in the causal<BR>form, and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=123-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वाह|उद्वाहः
उद्वाह m. (-हः) Marriage.<BR> E. उत् up, वह् to bear, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=123-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वाहकर्म्मन्|उद्वाहकर्मन्
उद्वाहकर्म्मन् n. (-र्म्म) The marriage ceremony.<BR> E. उद्वाह and कर्म्मन् act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=123-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वाहन|उद्वाहनं
उद्वाहन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Marriage.<BR>	 2. Ploughing a field twice.<BR>	 3. Anxiety,<BR>anxious regret.<BR>	 f. (-नी) The small shell used as a coin, a Cowri. E.<BR>उत् up, वाह् to endeavour, ल्युट् affix, and ङीष् fem. do.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=123-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वाहिक|उद्वाहिकः
उद्वाहिक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Relating to marriage, matrimonial.<BR> E. उद्वाह<BR>marriage, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=123-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वाहित|उद्वाहितः
उद्वाहित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Raised, lifted or pulled up, &c.<BR>	 2. Eradicated.<BR>E. उत् before वह् to bear, causal form, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=124-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वाहिन्
उद्वाहिन् mfn. (-ही-हिनी-हि)<BR>	 1. What raises or draws up.<BR>	 2. Who or what<BR>marries, relating to marriage.<BR>	 f. (-नी) A rope.<BR> E. उत्, वाह to endeav-<BR>our, णिनि and ङीष् affixes, or उद्वाह and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=124-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्विग्न|उद्विग्नः
उद्विग्न mfn. (-ग्नः-ग्ना-ग्नं) Sorrowful, anxious, grieving for an absent lover,<BR>&c.<BR> E. उत्, विज् to shake, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=124-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्विग्नमनस्
उद्विग्नमनस् mfn. (-नाः-नाः-नः) Sorrowful, depressed in spirits, anxious,<BR>distressed.<BR> E. उद्विग्न and मनस् the mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=124-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वीक्षण|उद्वीक्षणं
उद्वीक्षण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Looking up or upwards.<BR>	 2. Seeing, looking at.<BR> E. उत्<BR>and वि before ईक्ष् to see, affix ल्युट.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=124-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वृत्त|उद्वृत्तः
उद्वृत्त mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं)<BR>	 1. Raised, elevated.<BR>	 2. Exalted, prosperous.<BR>3. Unrestrained, ill-behaved.<BR>	 4. Vomited.<BR>	 5. Left, as a remainder. E.<BR>उत् above, and वृत्त placed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=124-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वेग|उद्वेगं|उद्वेगः
उद्वेग mfn. (-गः-गा-गं)<BR>	 1. One going swiftly, a runner, a courier, &c.<BR>2. Steady, composed, tranquil.<BR>	 m. (-गः)<BR>	 1. Regret.<BR>	 2. Fear.<BR>	 3. An-<BR>xiety, agitation.<BR>	 4. Distress occasioned by separation from a<BR>beloved object.<BR>	 5. Admiration, astonishment.<BR>	 6. Ascending,<BR>mounting, going up or upwards.<BR>	 7. An ascetic whose arms, by<BR>long habit, continue always raised above his head.<BR>	 n. (-गं) The fruit<BR>of the Areca catechu, the betel nut.<BR> E. उत् up, विज् to fear, to<BR>shake, &c. घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=124-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वेगिन्
उद्वेगिन् mfn. (-गी-गिनी-गि) Suffering distress, anxious, unhappy.<BR> E. उद्वेग<BR>and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=124-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वेजक
उद्वेजक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Distressing, annoying, what causes pain or sor-<BR>row.<BR> E. उत् before विज् to fear, causal form, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=124-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वेजन|उद्वेजनं
उद्वेजन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Anxiety, regret, sorrowing for one absent.<BR>	 2. Cor-<BR>poral infliction, mutilation, torture.<BR> E. उत् before विज् to shake,<BR>affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=124-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वेजनकर
उद्वेजनकर mfn. (-रः-रा-री-रं)<BR>	 1. Inflecting pain, punishing, torturing.<BR>	 2.<BR>Painful.<BR> E. उद्वेजन and कर what makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=124-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वेजित
उद्वेजित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Grieved, pained, afflicted.<BR> E. उत् before विज् to<BR>fear, causal, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=124-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वेष्ट|उद्वेष्टः
उद्वेष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं) What surrounds, &c.<BR>	 m. (-ष्टः)<BR>	 1. Investing a town,<BR>besieging or surrounding it.<BR>	 2. Capturing, taking.<BR>	 3. Surrounding,<BR>enclosing.<BR> E. उत् before वेष्ट to surround, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=124-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वेष्टन
उद्वेष्टन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Surrounding.<BR>	 2. An enclosure.<BR>	 3. Pain in the but-<BR>tocks.<BR> E. उत् before वेष्ट to surround, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=124-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वेष्टित
उद्वेष्टित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Surrounded, invested, enclosed.<BR> E. उत् before वेष्ट<BR>to surround, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=124-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उधस
उधस n. (-सं) An udder; see ऊधस.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=124-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उध्य
उध्य m. (-ध्यः) A name of a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=124-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उध्रस्
उध्रस् r. 9th cl. (उध्रस्नाति) r. 10th cl. (उध्रासयति)<BR>	 1. To glean or gather by<BR>little at a time.<BR>	 2. To throw or cast upwards. The initial उ is con-<BR>sidered by some as an indicatory letter, the root being then ध्रस; q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=124-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्द
उन्द r. 7th cl. (ई) उन्दी (उनत्ति) 1. To wet or moisten.<BR>	 2. To be or be-<BR>come wet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=124-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्दर
उन्दर m. (-रः) A rat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=124-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्दुर|उंदुर|उंदुरः|उन्दुरः
उन्दुर m. (-रः) A rat: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=124-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्दुरु|उंदुरु|उंदुरुः|उन्दुरुः
उन्दुरु m. (-रुः) A rat.<BR> E. उन्दी to wet, and उरु affix; it is also written<BR>उन्दरु, उन्दर, as above, and ऊन्दुरु, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=124-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्न|उन्नः
उन्न mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>	 1. Wet, moist.<BR>	 2. Kind, humane.<BR> E. उन्द् to be moist,<BR>क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=124-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्नत|उन्नतः
उन्नत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. High, tall.<BR>	 2. Raised, held or lifted up.<BR>	 3.<BR>Plump, full.<BR>	 4. Great, eminent.<BR> E. उत् high, नत bent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=124-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्नतनाभि|उन्नतनाभिः
उन्नतनाभि mfn. (-भिः-भिः-भि) Corpulent.<BR> E. उन्नत high, and नाभि the navel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=124-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्नतशिरस्
उन्नतशिरस् mfn. (-राः-राः-रः) Holding up the head, carrying the head<BR>high.<BR> E. उन्नत and शिरस् the head.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=124-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्नतानत|उन्नतानतं
उन्नतानत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Uneven, undulating, wavy.<BR> E. उन्नत high, and<BR>आनत low.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=124-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्नति|उन्नतिः
उन्नति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Increase, advancement, prosperity.<BR>	 2. Rising, ascend-<BR>ing.<BR>	 3. The wife of GARUḌA.<BR> E. उत् up, नम् to bend, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=124-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्नतीश|उन्नतीशः
उन्नतीश m. (-शः) A name of GARUḌA.<BR> E. उन्नति and ईश husband: the hus-<BR>band of UNNATI.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=124-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्नद्ध
उन्नद्ध mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>	 1. Swelled, increased.<BR>	 2. Tied upon or over.<BR>	 3.<BR>Unbound.<BR> E. उत् before नह् to bind, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=124-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्नमन|उन्नमनं
उन्नमन n. (-नं) Raising, lifting up.<BR> E. उत् before नम् to bow, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=124-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्नमित|उन्नमितः
उन्नमित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Raised, elevated, lifted or pulled up.<BR>	 2. Height-<BR>ened, increased.<BR> E. उत् before नम् to bow, क्त affix, with इट् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=124-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्नमय्य
उन्नमय्य ind. Having raised.<BR> E. उत् before नम् to bow, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=124-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्नम्र
उन्नम्र mfn. (-म्रः-म्रा-म्रं) Lofty, high, elevated.<BR> E. उत् before नम् to bow, रक्<BR>aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=124-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्नय|उन्नयः
उन्नय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. Raising, elevating, hoisting.<BR>	 2. Analogy, resemblance.<BR>E. उत् up, नी to obtain, and अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=124-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्नयन|उन्नयनं
उन्नयन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Deliberation, discussion, logic, reasoning.<BR>	 2. Inference.<BR>3. Raising, elevating, lifting up.<BR> E. उत् up, नी to obtain, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=124-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्नस
उन्नस mfn. (-सः-सा-सं) Having a prominent nose.<BR> E. उत् up, नस for नासिका<BR>the nose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=124-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्नाम|उन्नामः
उन्नाम m. (-मः) Raising, lifting up.<BR> E. उत् and नम् to bow, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=124-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्नाय|उन्नायः
उन्नाय m. (-यः) Raising. E. See उन्नय, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=124-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्नायक
उन्नायक mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>	 1. What raises.<BR>	 2. What leads to an inference<BR>or conclusion.<BR> E. उत् before नी to get, causal form, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=124-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्नाह|उन्नाहं|उन्नाहः
उन्नाह n. (-हं) Sour gruel made from the fermentation of rice.<BR> E. उत् and<BR>नह् to bind, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=124-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्निद्र|उन्निद्रः
उन्निद्र mfn. (-द्रः-द्रा-द्रं)<BR>	 1. Awake.<BR>	 2. Blown, expanded as flower.<BR> E. उत्<BR>priv. and निद्रा sleep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=124-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मत्त|उन्मत्तः
उन्मत्त mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं)<BR>	 1. Insane, frantic, mad.<BR>	 2. Drunk, intoxicated.<BR>m. (-त्तः)<BR>	 1. The thorn apple, (Datura metel and fastuosa)<BR>	 2. A<BR>plant, (Pterospermum acerifolium.)<BR> E. उत् much, मत्त drunk or mad:<BR>applied to the plants, it alludes to their deleterious properties.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=124-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मत्तता
उन्मत्तता f. (-ता) Insanity, intoxication.<BR> E. तल् added to the last: also<BR>उन्मत्तत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=124-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मद|उन्मदः
उन्मद mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>	 1. Mad, furious, extravagant, intoxicated.<BR>	 m. (-दः)<BR>Insanity, either morbid or as the effect of temporary excitement,<BR>intoxication, ecstacy.<BR> E. उत् very, मद् to be mad, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=124-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मदिष्णु|उन्मदिष्णुः
उन्मदिष्णु mfn. (-ष्णुः-ष्णुः-ष्णु)<BR>	 1. Mad, insane, crazed.<BR>	 2. Intoxicated.<BR>	 3. In<BR>rut, (as an elephant.)<BR> E. उन्मद to be mad, इष्णुच् attributive aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=124-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मनस्
उन्मनस् mfn. (-नाः-नाः-नः) Regretting, missing, sorrowing for a lost or<BR>departed friend, &c.<BR> E. उत् up, upset, disturbed, and मनस् the mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=124-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मन्थ|उन्मंथ|उन्मंथः|उन्मन्थः
उन्मन्थ m. (-न्थः)<BR>	 1. Killing, slaughter.<BR>	 2. Agitation.<BR> E. उत् before मथि to<BR>kill, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=124-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मन्थक|उन्मंथक|उन्मन्थकः
उन्मन्थक mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>	 1. What moves or stirs.<BR>	 2. Throbbing, beating.<BR>m. (-कः) Inflammation of the outer ear.<BR> E. उत् before मथि to hurt,<BR>वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=124-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मन्थन|उन्मंथन|उन्मंथनं
उन्मन्थन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Shaking, agitating.<BR>	 2. Hurting, killing.<BR>	 3. Probing,<BR>stirring a weapon, &c. lodged in the body.<BR> E. उत् before उथि to<BR>hurt, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=124-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मन्थित
उन्मन्थित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Moved, agitated, distressed.<BR> E. उत् and मन्थित<BR>agitated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=124-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्माथ|उन्माथः
उन्माथ m. (-थः)<BR>	 1. A snare or trap.<BR>	 2. Killing, slaughter.<BR>	 3. A killer, a<BR>slaughterer.<BR>	 4. Pride, disdain.<BR> E. उत्, मथ् to agitate, and घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=124-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्माद|उन्मादः
उन्माद mfn. (-दः-दा-दं) Mad, insane, extravagant.<BR>	 m. (-दः)<BR>	 1. Madness,<BR>extravagance.<BR>	 2. (In medicine,) Mania.<BR> E. उत् much, मद् to be<BR>mad, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=124-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मादन|उन्मादनः
उन्मादन m. (-नः) Maddening, exciting, intoxicating.<BR>	 2. One of five<BR>arrows borne by KĀMADEVA, the Hindu CUPID.<BR> E. उत् before मद्<BR>to be mad or intoxicated, causal form, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=124-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मादवत्|उन्मादवन्त्
उन्मादवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Mad, insane, wild, extravagant.<BR> E. उन्माद<BR>madness, &c. and मतुप् poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=124-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मादिन्
उन्मादिन् mfn. (-दी-दिनी-दि) Mad, intoxicated.<BR> E. उन्माद and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=124-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मान|उन्मानं|उन्मानः
उन्मान m. (-नः) A measure of size or quantity.<BR> E. उत् and मा to measure,<BR>ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=125-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मार्ग|उन्मार्गः
उन्मार्ग m. (-र्गः)<BR>	 1. A wrong road.<BR>	 2. Improper conduct, an evil course,<BR>error.<BR> E. उत् and मार्ग way.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=125-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मार्गगत
उन्मार्गगत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Erred, erring, going wrong.<BR> E. उन्मार्ग and गत gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=125-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मार्गगमन
उन्मार्गगमन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Going a wrong road.<BR>	 2. Following evil courses. E.<BR>उन्मार्ग and गमन going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=125-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मार्गगामिन्
उन्मार्गगामिन् mfn. (-मी-मिनी-मि)<BR>	 1. Going wrong, erring, following evil<BR>courses.<BR>	 2. Taking a wrong road.<BR> E. उन्मार्ग and गामिन् who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=125-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मित
उन्मित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Meted, measured.<BR> E. उत् before मा to measure, क्त<BR>affix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=125-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मिषत्
उन्मिषत् mfn. (-षन्-षन्ती-षत्) Opening the eye, drawing up the eyelid,<BR>looking at, seeing.<BR> E. उत् before मिष to scatter, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=125-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मिषित|उन्मिषितः
उन्मिषित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Opened, (as the eye.)<BR>	 2. Blown as a flower. E.<BR>उत् up, मिष् to scatter, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=125-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मीलन|उन्मीलनं
उन्मीलन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Winking, twinkling of the eye.<BR>	 2. Blowing, expand-<BR>ing.<BR> E. उत् and मील to twinkle, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=125-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मीलित|उन्मीलितः
उन्मीलित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Opened, (as the eyes.)<BR>	 2. Blown as a flower.<BR>E. उत्, मील् to wink, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=125-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मुख|उन्मुखः
उन्मुख mfn. (-खः-खा-खं) Looking upwards.<BR> E. उत् up, मुख the face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=125-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मुद्र|उन्मुद्रः
उन्मुद्र mfn. (-द्रः-द्रा-द्रं)<BR>	 1. Blown as a flower.<BR>	 2. Unsealed, opened.<BR> E. उत्<BR>up, open, and मुद्रा a seal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=125-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मूलित|उन्मूलितं
उन्मूलित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Eradicated, pulled up by the roots.<BR> E. उत् up,<BR>मूल nominal verb, to take root, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=125-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मृष्ट
उन्मृष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं) Worn off, blotted out.<BR> E. उत् out, मृष्ट rubbed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=125-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मेदा
उन्मेदा f. (-दा) Corpulency, fatness.<BR> E. उत् much, मिद् to anoint, अच and<BR>टाप् affixes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=125-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मेष|उन्मेषं|उन्मेषः
उन्मेष m. (-षः)<BR>	 1. Winking, twinkling of the eyelids, the upward mo-<BR>tion.<BR>	 2. Opening the eye, looking at.<BR> E. उत् up, मिष् to scatter, affix<BR>घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=125-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उप
उप ind. A particle and prefix to verbs and other words implying, 1.<BR>Excess, (over, above, &c.;)<BR>	 2. Vicinity or assemblage, (near,<BR>by the side of, with, together with;)<BR>	 3. Inferiority. (lesser, secondary,<BR>&c.;)<BR>	 4. Likeness, resemblance; 5. Disease, extinction; 6. Orna-<BR>ment; 7. Command; 8. Reproof; 9. Astonishing; 10.<BR>Giving; 11. Killing; 12. Diffusion; 13. Wish, desire; 14.<BR>Effort, exertion, &c. as उपकर्त्तुं to assist; उपगन्तुं to approach; उपदेष्टुं<BR>to advise; उपलब्धुं to revile; उपस्थातुं to worship; also उपपुराणं an in-<BR>ferior or minor Purana, उपकुम्भं near the water-pot, उपगङ्गं upon the<BR>Ganges, उपकान्तं near or with a lover, उपाग्नि in the vicinity of fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=125-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकण्ठ|उपकंठ|उपकण्ठं|उपकण्ठः
उपकण्ठ mfn. (-ण्ठः-ण्ठा-ण्ठं) Near, proximate.<BR>	 n. (-ण्ठं)<BR>	 1. Space near a vil-<BR>lage or its boundary.<BR>	 2. One of a horse's paces, his walk. ind. (-ण्ठं)<BR>Upon the neck, near the throat.<BR> E. उप near, कण्ठ the neck.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=125-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकरण|उपकरणं
उपकरण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Apparatus, paraphernalia, as the vessels and offer-<BR>ings at a sacrifice.<BR>	 2. Implements, machines.<BR>	 3. The insignia of<BR>royalty.<BR>	 4. Sauces, condiments.<BR>	 5. Helping, assisting.<BR>	 6. Object of<BR>art or science, fabricating, composing, &c.<BR>	 7. Means of subsistence,<BR>any thing supporting life.<BR> E. उप implying command or help, कृ to<BR>make, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=125-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकर्णम्
उपकर्णम् ind. Close to the ear, into the ear, (whispered, &c. )<BR> E. उप near, कर्ण the ear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=125-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकर्तृ|उपकर्त्तृ
उपकर्तृ mfn. (-र्ता-र्त्री-र्तृ) Assisting, befriending, one who helps or be-<BR>friends.<BR> E. उप before कृ to do, affix तृन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=125-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकल्पन|उपकल्पनं
उपकल्पन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Preparing articles of food, medicine, &c.<BR>	 2. Fabricat-<BR>ing, making.<BR>	 3. Substituting.<BR> E. उप and कल्पन making.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=125-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकल्पित
उपकल्पित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Prepared, made.<BR>	 2. Secondary, substituted.<BR>E. उप and कल्पित prepared.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=125-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकार|उपकारः
उपकार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Favour, protection, help, assistance.<BR>	 2. Use, ad-<BR>vantage.<BR>	 3. A flower, &c. full blown.<BR>	 4. Garlands suspended, at<BR>gateways, as an embellishment on festivals.<BR> E. उप near or over, कृ<BR>to make, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=125-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकारक
उपकारक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) A friend, a protector, one who befriends. E.<BR>उप and कृ to do, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=125-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकारकत्व
उपकारकत्व n. (-त्वं)<BR>	 1. Protection, assistance.<BR> E. उपकारक and त्व aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=125-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकारपर
उपकारपर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Beneficent, diligent in doing good.<BR> E. उपकार<BR>and पर diligent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=125-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकारिका
उपकारिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. A protectress, a governess.<BR>	 2. A palace, a cara-<BR>vansera.<BR>	 3. A kind of cake.<BR> E. उपकारी as below, &c. कन् affix, and<BR>the fem. form, or the fem. of उपकारक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=125-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकारिता
उपकारिता f. (-ता) Aid, succour, protection.<BR> E. तल् added to उपकारिन्; also<BR>with त्व, उपकारित्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=125-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकारिन्
उपकारिन् mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>	 1. Helping, assisting, a benefactor.<BR>	 2. Sub-<BR>sidiary, subservient.<BR> E. उपकार and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=125-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकारी
उपकारी f. (-री) A palace, a caravansera.<BR> E. उपकार aid, asylum, affixes<BR>अण् and ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=125-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकार्य्य|उपकार्य|उपकार्य्यः
उपकार्य्य mfn. (-र्य्यः-र्य्या-र्य्यं) Deserving assistance or favour.<BR>	 f. (-र्य्या)<BR>	 1. A<BR>king's house, a palace, a caravansera.<BR>	 2. A tent.<BR> E. उपकार aid, &c.<BR>and ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=125-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकुञ्चि|उपकुंचिः|उपकुञ्चिः
उपकुञ्चि f. (-ञ्चिः) A plant, (Nigella Indica.)<BR> E. उप very, कुञ्च् to be small, and कि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=125-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकुञ्चिका|उपकुंचिका
उपकुञ्चिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. Small cardamoms: see एला.<BR>	 2. A sort of fennel<BR>flower, (Nigella Indica, Rox.)<BR> E. वुन् affixed to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=125-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकुम्भ|उपकुंभ|उपकुम्भं
उपकुम्भ mfn. (-म्भः-म्भा-म्भं)<BR>	 1. Near, proximate.<BR>	 2. Solitary, lonely, retired.<BR>n. or ind. (-म्भं) Near the water-jar.<BR> E. उप and कुम्भ a jar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=125-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकुल्या
उपकुल्या f. (-ल्या)<BR>	 1. A canal, a trench, a ditch.<BR>	 2. Long pepper, (Piper<BR>longum.)<BR> E. उप near, कुल् to accumulate, and क्यप् affix, fem. टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=125-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकुश|उपकुशः
उपकुश m. (-शः) Gum-boil.<BR> E. उप before कुश् to enclose, क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=125-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकूपजलाशय|उपकूपजलाशयः
उपकूपजलाशय m. (-यः) A trough near a well for watering cattle.<BR> E. उप<BR>near, कूप a well, and जलाशय a place for water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=125-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकृत
उपकृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Benefited, assisted.<BR>	 2. Done kindly or benefi-<BR>cently, rendered as assistance.<BR>	 n. (-तं) A favour, a benefit.<BR> E. उप<BR>before कृ to do, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=125-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकृति|उपकृतिः
उपकृति f. (-तिः) Aid, assistance, kindness.<BR> E. उप and कृ to do, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=125-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपक्रन्तृ|उपक्रंतृ
उपक्रन्तृ mfn. (-न्ता-न्त्री-न्तृ) Beginning, one who begins.<BR> E. उप before क्रम् to<BR>go, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=125-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपक्रम|उपक्रमः
उपक्रम m. (-मः)<BR>	 1. Deliberate commencement or undertaking; providing<BR>means, and anticipating consequences.<BR>	 2. A beginning in general.<BR>3. A particular ceremony preparatory to reading the Vedas.<BR>	 4. A<BR>stratagem.<BR>	 5. A means, an expedient.<BR>	 6. Trying the fidelity, &c.<BR>of a counselor or friend.<BR>	 7. Valor.<BR>	 8. Practice of medicine, physick-<BR>ing.<BR>	 9. Flight, retreat.<BR>	 10. Approach.<BR> E. उप over, &c. क्रम् to go,<BR>affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=125-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपक्रमणीय
उपक्रमणीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>	 1. Necessary, to be commenced or undertaken.<BR>2. To be gone to near.<BR> E. उप before क्रम् to go, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=125-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपक्रमितृ
उपक्रमितृ mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ) One who begins, &c. see उपक्रम.<BR> E. उप before<BR>क्रम् to go, तृच् affix, with इट् augment; also उपक्रर्तृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=125-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपक्रोश|उपक्रोशः
उपक्रोश m. (-शः) Censure, reproach.<BR> E. उप reproach, inferiority, क्रुश् to<BR>cry, to sound, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=125-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपक्रोष्टृ
उपक्रोष्टृ m. (-ष्टा)<BR>	 1. An ass.<BR>	 2. A reviler, reprover.<BR> E. उप implying cen-<BR>sure, क्रुश् to cry, तृन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=125-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकॢप्त
उपकॢप्त mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं) Consecrated, dedicated, prepared or set apart for<BR>use.<BR> E. उप and कॢप्त made.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=125-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपक्वण|उपक्वणं|उपक्वणः
उपक्वण m. (-णः) The sound of a lute.<BR> E. उप well, क्वण् to sound, affix अप्<BR>or with घञ् affix उपक्वाण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=125-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपक्षय|उपक्षयः
उपक्षय m. (-यः) Loss.<BR> E. उप before क्षि to lose, affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=125-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपक्षेप|उपक्षेपः
उपक्षेप m. (-पः) Poetical or figurative style or composition.<BR> E. उप and क्षिप्<BR>to throw, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=125-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपगण|उपगणः
उपगण m. (-णः) A small number, less than a troop or number.<BR> E. उप<BR>and गण a troop.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=125-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपगत|उपगतः
उपगत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Promised, agreed.<BR>	 2. Near, approached, gone<BR>to.<BR>	 3. Feeling, suffering, entertaining.<BR>	 4. Becoming, being, become.<BR>5. Having, obtained.<BR> E. उप with, गत gone, part. past of गम् to go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=125-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपगतवत्
उपगतवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>	 1. Going to, gone to.<BR>	 2. Feeling, suffering,<BR>(as sorrow, &c.)<BR>	 3. Promising.<BR>	 4. Possessing.<BR> E. उप before गम् to<BR>go, क्तवतु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=126-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपगन्ध|उपगंधः|उपगन्धः
उपगन्ध m. (-न्धः) Perfume.<BR> E. उप and गन्ध smell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=126-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपगम|उपगमः
उपगम m. (-मः)<BR>	 1. Agreement, promise.<BR>	 2. Approach, approximation.<BR>3. Suffering, feeling.<BR>	 4. Acquaintance, society, intercourse.<BR>	 5. Get-<BR>ting, having, obtaining.<BR> E. उप near, गम् to go, and अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=126-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपगिरि|उपगिरिः
उपगिरि ind. Near a mountain; also with टच् added उपगिरम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=126-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपगीत
उपगीत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Celebrated, proclaimed, sung, (by bards, &c.) E.<BR>उप and गीत sung.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=126-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपगीति|उपगीतिः
उपगीति f. (-तिः) A variety of the Āryā metre, a stanza of four lines,<BR>containing 12--15 and 12--15 syllabic instants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=126-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपगीय
उपगीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) To be sung. ind. Having sung.<BR> E. उप before गै to<BR>sing, यत् or ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=126-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपगूढ
उपगूढ mfn. (-ढः-ढा-ढं)<BR>	 1. Hidden, concealed.<BR>	 2. Lulled, suppressed.<BR> E. उप<BR>before गुह् to hide, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=126-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपगूहन|उपगूहनं
उपगूहन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. An embrace, embracing.<BR>	 2. Astonishment, surprise.<BR>E. उप near, गुह् to hide, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=126-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपग्रह|उपग्रहः
उपग्रह m. (-हः)<BR>	 1. A prisoner, a man or animal in confinement.<BR>	 2. Fa-<BR>vour, encouragement.<BR>	 3. Assistance.<BR>	 4. Peace purchased by the<BR>cession of every thing.<BR>	 5. Seizure.<BR>	 6. The presiding spirit or cause<BR>directing a planet's motion.<BR>	 7. A minor planet or any heavenly<BR>body of a secondary kind, as a comet, a meteor, a falling star, &c.<BR>8. A heap of kusa grass.<BR> E. उप near, ग्रह् to take, अप् affix or ग्रह a<BR>planet, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=126-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपग्रहण|उपग्रहणं
उपग्रहण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Taking, seizing.<BR>	 2. Holy study, reading the Vedas<BR>after initiation.<BR> E. उप much, ग्रह् to take, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=126-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपग्राह्य|उपग्राह्यः
उपग्राह्य m. (-ह्यः) A present, an offering to a king or great man, a Nezar.<BR>E. उप much, &c. ग्रह् to take, affix ण्यत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=126-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपघात|उपघातः
उपघात m. (-तः)<BR>	 1. Disease, sickness.<BR>	 2. Touch, contact, especially with<BR>an intent to injure.<BR>	 3. Personal violence, assault.<BR> E. उप much, हन्<BR>to injure, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=126-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपघ्न|उपघ्नः
उपघ्न m. (-घ्नः)<BR>	 1. Contiguous support.<BR>	 2. Support, stay, protection.<BR>3. What rests upon or is supported by.<BR> E. उप near, हन् to destroy,<BR>and अप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=126-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपचक्र|उपचक्रः
उपचक्र m. (-क्रः) A variety of the ruddy goose.<BR> E. उप minor, and चक्र the Chakwa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=126-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपचतुर
उपचतुर m. plu. (-राः) Almost four.<BR> E. उप minor and चतुर four.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=126-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपचय|उपचयः
उपचय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. Quantity, heap.<BR>	 2. Elevation.<BR>	 3. Prosperity.<BR>	 4. Excess.<BR>5. The third, sixth, tenth, and eleventh degrees from the first of a<BR>zodiacal sign.<BR> E. उप above, चि to collect, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=126-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपचरित|उपचरितं
उपचरित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Served, adored.<BR> E. उप near or with, चर् to go,<BR>affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=126-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपचर्य्य|उपचर्य
उपचर्य्य mfn. (-र्य्यः-र्य्या-र्य्यं) To be served or waited on.<BR>	 f. (-र्य्या)<BR>	 1. Service,<BR>attendance.<BR>	 2. Practice of medicine, physicking.<BR> E. उप implying<BR>help, चर् to go, क्यप् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=126-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपचाय्य|उपचाय्यः
उपचाय्य m. (-य्यः) A place for holding sacrificial fire, a hearth, an altar.<BR>E. उप, चिञ् to collect, ण्यत् affix, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=126-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपचार|उपचारः
उपचार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Service, attendance.<BR>	 2. Physicking, the practice of<BR>medicine.<BR>	 3. Practice, profession, usage.<BR>	 4. A present, a bribe.<BR>	 5.<BR>Presenting delicacies or necessaries, water, betel, &c.<BR>	 6. Tending<BR>the sick, nursing.<BR>	 7. Solicitation, request.<BR>	 8. Incomplete act, one in<BR>progress.<BR>	 9. A form of speech, a phrase that leaves something to be<BR>inferred ellipsis, &c.<BR> E. उप well, much, &c. चर् to go, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=126-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपचारकरण
उपचारकरण n. (-णं) Offering presents, especially of perfumes, flowers,<BR>&c. attention, service.<BR> E. उपचार and करण making; also उपचारकर्म्मन्,<BR>उपचारक्रिया, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=126-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपचारपर
उपचारपर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Waiting upon, serving diligently.<BR> E. उपचार ser-<BR>vice, and पर diligent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=126-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपचार्य्य|उपचार्य|उपचार्यः|उपचार्य्यः
उपचार्य्य m. (-र्य्यः) Practice of medicine<BR> E. उप, चर् in the causal form,<BR>and ण्यत् affix, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=126-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपचित|उपचितः
उपचित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Collected, assembled.<BR>	 2. Heaped.<BR>	 3. Thriving,<BR>increasing.<BR>	 4. Burnt.<BR>	 5. Plastered, smeared.<BR> E. उप much, and चित<BR>collected, from चिञ् to gather, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=126-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपचित्रा
उपचित्रा f. (-त्रा) A plant, (Salvinia cucullata, Rox.) See मूषिकपर्णी.<BR> E. उप<BR>much, चित्र variegated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=126-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपचूलन|उपचूलनं
उपचूलन n. (-नं) Heating, burning.<BR> E. उप much, चूर् to burn, affix ल्युट्,<BR>र changed to ल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=126-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपचेय
उपचेय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) To be collected or heaped up.<BR> E. उप before चि to<BR>gather, ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=126-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपच्छन्न|उपछन्न
उपच्छन्न mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं) Secret, concealed.<BR> E. उप and छद् to cover, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=126-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपजात
उपजात mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Produced, engendered, aroused.<BR> E. उप and जात<BR>born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=126-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपजाति|उपजातिः
उपजाति f. (-तिः) A metre or stanza of four lines, with eleven syllables<BR>in each.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=126-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपजाप|उपजापः
उपजाप m. (-पः)<BR>	 1. Disunion, separation.<BR>	 2. Treason, treachery.<BR> E. उप<BR>separation, जप् to meditate, ण aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=126-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपजापक
उपजापक mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>	 1. A mischief-maker, one who foments quar-<BR>rels.<BR>	 2. A traitor, treacherous.<BR> E. उप before जप् to meditate, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=126-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपजिह्वा
उपजिह्वा f. (-ह्वा)<BR>	 1. A kind of insect.<BR>	 2. The uvula or soft palate.<BR>	 3. En-<BR>largement of the tongue.<BR> E. उप privation or similitude, and जिह्वा<BR>the tongue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=126-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपजिह्विका
उपजिह्विका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. A species of insect.<BR>	 2. The soft palate; see the<BR>preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=126-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपजीवक
उपजीवक n. (-कं)<BR>	 1. Act, object.<BR>	 2. Means of subsistence.<BR> E. उप before जीव्<BR>to live, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=126-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपजीविका
उपजीविका f. (-का) Subsistence, livelihood.<BR> E. उप and जीविका the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=126-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपजीवन|उपजीवनं
उपजीवन n. (-नं) Subsistence, means of living.<BR> E. उप and जीवन living.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=126-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपजीविन्
उपजीविन् mfn. (-वी-विनी-वि) Dependent, living by or on.<BR> E. उप and जीविन्<BR>who lives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=126-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपजीव्य|उपजीव्यः
उपजीव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं) Affording a livelihood.<BR>	 n. (-व्यं) Cause.<BR> E. उप be-<BR>fore जीव् to live, य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=126-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपजोषम्
उपजोषम् ind. An expression indicative of joy.<BR> E. उप much, जुष् to be kind,<BR>and अम् affix; also उपयोषम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=126-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपज्ञा
उपज्ञा f. (-ज्ञा) Untaught knowledge.<BR> E. उप near, with ज्ञा knowledge,<BR>from ज्ञा to know, अङ् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=126-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपढौकन|उपढौकनं
उपढौकन n. (-नं) A respectful offering or present, a Nezer.<BR> E. उप and<BR>ढौकन seeking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=126-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपतप्त
उपतप्त mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं)<BR>	 1. Heated, parched.<BR>	 2. Distressed, pained.<BR> E. उप<BR>and तप्त heated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=126-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपतप्तृ
उपतप्तृ m. (-प्ता)<BR>	 1. Morbid heat.<BR>	 2. Any cause of heat, burning or inflam-<BR>mation.<BR> E. उप excess, तप् to heat, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=126-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपताप|उपतापः
उपताप m. (-पः)<BR>	 1. Disease.<BR>	 2. Haste, hurry.<BR>	 3. Heat, heatedness.<BR>	 4.<BR>Pain.<BR>	 5. Misfortune.<BR> E. उप much, तप् to heat, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=126-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपतापिन्
उपतापिन् mfn. (-पी-पिनी-पि)<BR>	 1. Inflaming, exciting.<BR>	 2. Heating.<BR>	 3. Suffer-<BR>ing heat or pain.<BR>	 4. Sick.<BR> E. उपताप and इनि affix, or उप before तप<BR>with णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=126-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपत्यका
उपत्यका f. (-का) Land near the foot of a hill or mountain.<BR> E. उप near,<BR>त्यकन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=126-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदंश|उपदंशः
उपदंश m. (-शः)<BR>	 1. A relish, or something to promote drinking.<BR>	 2. The<BR>venereal disease, chancre.<BR>	 3. Biting, stinging.<BR>	 4. A tree, the scraped<BR>root of which is used for horse-radish, (Morunga hyperanthera.) E.<BR>उप much, &c. दंश biting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=126-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदर्शक|उपदर्शकः
उपदर्शक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A doorkeeper.<BR>	 2. A guide.<BR> E. उप and दर्शक who shows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=126-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदर्शित
उपदर्शित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Perceived, distinguished.<BR> E. उप before दर्शित seen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=126-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदा
उपदा f. (-दा) A present, an offering to a king or great man, &c. a<BR>Nezer.<BR> E. उप, दा a gift, from दा to give, अङ् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=126-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदानक|उपदानकं
उपदानक n. (-कं) A present, &c. see the preceding.<BR> E. उप implying help,<BR>&c. दान a gift, and क affix: a gift which is for the purpose of pro-<BR>curing favour or protection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=126-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदिश्य
उपदिश्य ind. Having advised or instructed.<BR> E. उप before दिश to show, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=126-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदिष्ट|उपदिष्टः
उपदिष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>	 1. Instructed, advised.<BR>	 2. Initiated.<BR>	 3. Specified,<BR>particularised.<BR>	 4. Assigned as a plea or reason.<BR>	 n. (-ष्टं) Council,<BR>advice.<BR> E. उप before दिश् to show, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=127-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदी
उपदी f. (-दी) A parasitic plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=127-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदेवता
उपदेवता f. (-ता) A minor divinity, as a Yakṣa, Gandharva, Apsara,<BR>&c.<BR> E. उप and देवता a divinity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=127-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदेश|उपदेशः
उपदेश m. (-शः)<BR>	 1. Advice, information, instruction.<BR>	 2. Plea, pretext.<BR>	 3.<BR>Specification.<BR>	 4. Initiation, communication of the initiatory Man-<BR>tra or formula.<BR>	 5. (In grammar,) An elementary term.<BR> E. उप before<BR>दिश् to show, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=127-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदेशक|उपदेशकः
उपदेशक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Giving instruction, instructing, instructive.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-कः) An instructor, a guide, specially a spiritual guide.<BR> E. उप be-<BR>fore दिश् to show, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=127-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदेशन|उपदेशनं
उपदेशन n. (-नं) Advising, instructing.<BR> E. उप before दिश् to show, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=127-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदेशिन्
उपदेशिन् mfn. (-शी-शिनी-शि) Advising, an adviser.<BR> E. उपदेश advice, and<BR>इनि affix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=127-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदेष्टव्य
उपदेष्टव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं) To be advised. (fit, proper, &c.)<BR> E. उप before<BR>दिश् to show, तव्य affix; also उपदेश्य, उपदेशनीय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=127-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदेष्टृ
उपदेष्टृ mfn. (-ष्टा-ष्ट्री-ष्टृ) One who points out, who orders or advises.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-ष्टा) A Guru, a spiritual guide.<BR> E. उप prefixed to दिश to show,<BR>affix तृच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=127-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदेह|उपदेहः
उपदेह m. (-हः)<BR>	 1. Liniment, ointment.<BR>	 2. A minor or secondary body.<BR>E. उप and दिह plaster, or देह the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=127-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदेहिका
उपदेहिका f. (-का) A kind of insect.<BR> E. उप with, &c. देह the body, affixes<BR>कन् and टाप्; also उत्पादिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=127-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपद्रव|उपद्रवः
उपद्रव m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. Tyranny, oppression.<BR>	 2. National distress, whether<BR>the act of the seasons or the king, famine, exaction, &c.<BR>	 3. National<BR>commotion, rebellion.<BR>	 4. Violence.<BR>	 5. A supervenient disease, one<BR>brought on whilst a person labours under another.<BR> E. उप, द्रु to go,<BR>अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=127-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपद्रविन्
उपद्रविन् mfn. (-वी-विणी-वि)<BR>	 1. Tyrannical.<BR>	 2. Violent, factious.<BR>	 m. (-वी)<BR>1. A tyrant, an oppressor.<BR>	 2. A rebel.<BR> E. उपद्रव and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=127-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपद्रष्टृ
उपद्रष्टृ mfn. (-ष्टा-ष्ट्री-ष्टृ) Supervisor, inspector, overseeing, overlooking.<BR>E. उप before दृश् to see, तृच् affix, the vowel changed to र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=127-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपद्रुत
उपद्रुत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Tyrannized over, oppressed, visited by calamities,<BR>&c.<BR> E. उप before द्रु to go, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=127-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपधर्म्म|उपधर्म|उपधर्मः|उपधर्म्मः
उपधर्म्म m. (-र्म्मः)<BR>	 1. A heretic, a schismatic.<BR>	 2. A minor or inferior duty.<BR>E. उप and धर्म्म duty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=127-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपधा
उपधा f. (-धा)<BR>	 1. A false pretence.<BR>	 2. Trial or test of honesty, &c. of four<BR>kinds, of loyalty, disinterestedness, continence, and courage.<BR>	 3. A<BR>penultimate letter.<BR> E. उप, धा having, from धा to have, with अङ्<BR>and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=127-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपधातु|उपधातुः
उपधातु m. (-तुः)<BR>	 1. An inferior mineral, a semi-metal: seven are speci-<BR>fied; pyrites, sulphate of copper, talc, antimony, red orpiment,<BR>yellow orpiment, and calx of brass.<BR>	 2. Secondary secretion, as the<BR>milk, menses, adeps, sweet, teeth, hair, and lymph.<BR> E. उप minor,<BR>and घातु mineral, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=127-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपधान|उपधानं
उपधान n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. A pillow.<BR>	 2. Kindness, affection.<BR>	 3. Poison.<BR>	 4. Reli-<BR>gious observance or obligation.<BR>	 5. Excellence, excellent quality.<BR>	 6.<BR>Resting or placing upon.<BR> E. उप, धा to have or hold, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=127-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपधानीय|उपधानीयं
उपधानीय n. (-यं) A pillow.<BR> E. उपधान a pillow, and छ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=127-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपधाय
उपधाय ind. Having placed or rested upon.<BR> E. उप before धा to hold, ल्यप्<BR>affix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=127-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपधाशुचि
उपधाशुचि mfn. (-चिः-चिः-चि) Approved, tried, of approved loyalty, &c.<BR>E. उपधा and शुचि pure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=127-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपधि|उपधिः
उपधि m. (-धिः)<BR>	 1. Fraud, circumvention.<BR>	 2. The wheel of a carriage.<BR>	 3.<BR>Fear, terror.<BR> E. उप, धा to have, and कि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=127-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपधिक|उपधिकः
उपधिक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A cheat, a knave, especially one who extorts money<BR>by threats.<BR>	 2. Fraud.<BR> E. उपधि and कृ to make, ड affix or कन्<BR>pleonasm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=127-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपधूपित|उपधूपितः
उपधूपित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Being at the point of death.<BR>	 2. Suffering<BR>extreme pain.<BR> E. उप near or much, धूपित pained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=127-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपधृति|उपधृतिः
उपधृति f. (-तिः) A ray of light.<BR> E. उप much, धृ to have, क्तिन् affix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=127-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनत|उपनतः
उपनत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Approached, approximate, near, (either in time<BR>or place.)<BR> E. उप near, नम् to bow, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=127-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनय|उपनयः
उपनय m. (-यः) The initiation of the three first classes; investiture<BR>with a peculiar thread or cord worn over the left shoulder, and<BR>under the right: the cord of the Brahman is of cotton, Munja, or<BR>Kusa grass; of the Kṣatriya, of Sana or flax; and of the Vaiśya,<BR>of wool: the youths should be invested respectively, from eight to<BR>sixteen, from eleven to twenty-two, and from twelve to twenty-four<BR>years of age.<BR>	 n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Attaining, gaining.<BR>	 2. Bringing to E.<BR>उप over, नीञ् to obtain, अच् affix; also with घञ् affix उपनाय, and<BR>with ल्युट् affix उपनयन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=127-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनयन|उपनयनं
उपनयन n. (-नं) See the preceding. E. As before, affix ल्युट्; also with<BR>अण् added उपनायन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=127-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनाय|उपनायः
उपनाय m. (-यः) See उपनय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=127-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनाह|उपनाहः
उपनाह m. (-हः)<BR>	 1. A plaster, an unguent applied to a wound or sore.<BR>2. The tie of a lute, the lower part of the tail piece where the wires<BR>are fixed.<BR>	 3. Inflammation of the ciliary glands, stye.<BR> E. उप, नह् to<BR>bind, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=127-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनाहन|उपनाहनं
उपनाहन n. (-नं) Unction, anointing, plastering.<BR> E. उप before नह् to tie, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=127-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनिक्षेप|उपनिक्षेपः
उपनिक्षेप m. (-पः) A deposit, sealed or in a cover so that the contents<BR>are unknown.<BR> E. उप and निक्षेप the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=127-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनिधान|उपनिधानं
उपनिधान n. (-नं) A deposit: see the next.<BR> E. उप and नि before धा to have,<BR>ल्युट् affix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=127-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनिधि|उपनिधिः
उपनिधि m. (-धिः) A deposit, a pledge, property put into the care of a<BR>creditor, friend, &c.<BR> E. उप and नि before धा to have, क affix; in law<BR>this word ordinarily implies more especially a sealed or enclosed<BR>deposit, but according to some, it is any article entrusted to a<BR>friend which he may use whilst in his keeping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=127-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनिषद्
उपनिषद् f. (-षद् or -षत्)<BR>	 1. A portion of the religious writings of the<BR>Hindus; the theological part, and the Vedanta or argumentative<BR>part of the Vedas, either detached from or comprised in the princi-<BR>pal work.<BR>	 2. Virtue, moral merit.<BR>	 3. Truth as the principle of<BR>divine being.<BR>	 4. A neighbouring mansion.<BR>	 5. A lonely place.<BR> E. उप<BR>and नि prefixed to षद् to go, affix क्विप्; in which abide the essential<BR>parts of religion, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=127-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनिष्कर|उपनिष्करं|उपनिष्करः
उपनिष्कर n. (-रं)<BR>	 1. A street.<BR>	 2. A principal or royal road.<BR> E. उप and नि<BR>before कृ to make, affix अप्, and स inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=127-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनिष्क्रमण|उपनिष्क्रमणं
उपनिष्क्रमण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. A main or royal road.<BR>	 2. An instituted observance<BR>or Sanskara, taking a child in the fourth month of its age into the<BR>open air.<BR>	 3. Going forth.<BR> E. उप and नि before क्रम् to go, affix ल्युट्,<BR>and स inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=127-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनिहित
उपनिहित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Deposited with, entrusted to.<BR>	 2. Placed<BR>near to.<BR>	 3. Offered, presented.<BR> E. उप and नि before धा to to have,<BR>क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=127-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनीत|उपनीतः
उपनीत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Brought near to, approximated.<BR>	 2. Obtained,<BR>attained.<BR>	 3. Citing, adducing.<BR>	 4. Presented.<BR>	 5. Known.<BR>	 m. (-तः) The<BR>youth invested with the characteristic string; see उपनय.<BR> E. उप be-<BR>fore नी to obtain, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=127-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनीय
उपनीय ind.<BR>	 1. Having brought.<BR>	 2. Having invested.<BR> E. उप before नी<BR>to bring, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=127-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनुन्न
उपनुन्न mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>	 1. Sent or dispatched.<BR>	 2. Wafted, driven, (by<BR>the wind.)<BR> E. उप before नुद् to send, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=127-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपन्यस्त
उपन्यस्त mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं)<BR>	 1. Pledged, deposited.<BR>	 2. Given, communicated.<BR>3. Brought forward, (as an example, &c.) adduced.<BR>	 4. Placed near<BR>to, or in, or upon.<BR> E. उप and नि before अस् to throw, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=127-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपन्यास|उपन्यासः
उपन्यास m. (-सः)<BR>	 1. A pledge, a pawn, a hostage.<BR>	 2. An exordium or in-<BR>troduction.<BR>	 3. A precept, a law.<BR>	 4. Giving, imparting.<BR>	 5. Juxta-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=128-a" target="_blank">Page128-a+ 60</a>]<BR>position.<BR>	 6. A suggestion, a hint.<BR> E. उप and नि prefixed to अस् to<BR>throw or send, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=127-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपन्यास्य
उपन्यास्य mfn. (-स्यः-स्या-स्यं) To be pledged.<BR> E. उप and न्यास्य to be adduced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=128-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपपति|उपपतिः
उपपति m. (-तिः) A paramour, a gallant.<BR> E. उप in place of, पति a<BR>husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=128-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपपत्ति|उपपत्तिः
उपपत्ति f. (-त्तिः)<BR>	 1. Birth, production.<BR>	 2. Association, connexion.<BR>	 3. Fit-<BR>ness, propriety.<BR>	 4. Cessation, end.<BR>	 5. Possessing, having.<BR>	 6. As-<BR>certained or demonstrated conclusion.<BR>	 7. Cause, reason.<BR>	 8. Effect-<BR>ing, doing.<BR>	 9. Religious abstraction.<BR>	 10. (In arithmetic or geo-<BR>metry,) Proof, demonstration.<BR> E. उप before पद् to go, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=128-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपपत्तिमत्|उपपत्तिमन्त्
उपपत्तिमत् mfn. (-मान्-मती-मत्)<BR>	 1. Right, fit, reasonable, proper.<BR>	 2. Unit-<BR>ed, associated.<BR> E. उपपत्ति and मतुप् poss aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=128-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपपद|उपपदं
उपपद n. (-दं)<BR>	 1. Small, diminutive.<BR>	 2. The subsidiary term in a com-<BR>pound word.<BR>	 3. The first member of a compound word.<BR>	 4. An<BR>aptote a word sometimes used as an adverb and sometimes as an<BR>inflected noun.<BR>	 5. A secondary noun in a sentence in conjunction<BR>or apposition.<BR> E. उप before पद a foot, or an inflected word.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=128-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपपन्न
उपपन्न mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>	 1. Manifested.<BR>	 2. Fit, suited to the occasion,<BR>adequate.<BR>	 3. Done, shown, proved, effected.<BR>	 4. Endowed with,<BR>possessed of.<BR>	 5. Produced from or by.<BR>	 6. Physicked, cured.<BR> E. उप<BR>before पद् to go, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=128-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपपातक|उपपातकं
उपपातक n. (-कं) A great crime, as killing a cow, selling a daughter,<BR>atheism, &c.; it is considered as criminality in the second or third<BR>degree, and is of various kinds: see महापातक.<BR> E. उप much, and<BR>पातक a crime.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=128-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपपातकिन्
उपपातकिन् m. (-की) A sinner in any but the first degree.<BR> E. उपपातक<BR>and इनि affix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=128-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपपादन|उपपादनं
उपपादन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Effecting, doing.<BR>	 2. Giving, delivering, presenting.<BR>3. Proving or establishing by argument.<BR> E. उप before पद् to go,<BR>causal form, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=128-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपपादित
उपपादित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Done, effected.<BR>	 2. Given delivered, present-<BR>ed.<BR>	 3. Proved, accomplished.<BR> E. उप before पद् to go, causal form,<BR>क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=128-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपपादुक|उपपादुकः
उपपादुक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Shod.<BR>	 m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A superhuman being,<BR>a god, a demon, &c.<BR>	 2. Hell.<BR> E. उप before पद् to go, उकञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=128-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपपाप|उपपापं
उपपाप m. (-पः) A heinous crime, as killing a cow, &c.<BR> E. उप excess,<BR>and पाप sin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=128-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपपालित
उपपालित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Protected, nurtured.<BR> E. उप and पालित<BR>protected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=128-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपपीडन|उपपीडनं
उपपीडन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Pain, agony, torture.<BR>	 2. Inflicting pain.<BR>	 3. Devas-<BR>tating, laying waste.<BR> E. उप before पीड to give pain, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=128-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपपीडित
उपपीडित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Tortured, pained, distressed.<BR>	 2. Devastated.<BR>E. उप before पीड to give pain, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=128-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपपुर|उपपुरं
उपपुर n. (-रं) A suburb.<BR> E. उप near, पुर a city.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=128-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपपुराण|उपपुराणं
उपपुराण n. (-णं) A Purana, one not included in the eighteen principal:<BR>a similar number is reckoned, or 1. Adi.<BR>	 2. Nrishinha.<BR>	 3. Vayu.<BR>4. Sivadhermma.<BR>	 5. Durvasa.<BR>	 6. Nārada.<BR>	 7. Nandikeswara.<BR>8. Usanas.<BR>	 9. Kapila.<BR>	 10. Varuna.<BR>	 11. Sāmba.<BR>	 12. Kālikā.<BR>	 13.<BR>Maheswara.<BR>	 14. Padma.<BR>	 15. Deva.<BR>	 16. Parāsara.<BR>	 17. Marīcha.<BR>18. Bhaskara.<BR> E. उप minor, पुराण a Purāna.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=128-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपपुष्पिका
उपपुष्पिका f. (-का) Yawning, gaping.<BR> E. उप much, पुष्प to flower, to open<BR>as a flower, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=128-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपप्रदान|उपप्रदानं
उपप्रदान n. (-नं) A bribe.<BR> E. उप for assistance, प्र before दा to give, affix<BR>ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=128-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपप्लव|उपप्लवः
उपप्लव m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. Rahu, the ascending node.<BR>	 2. A portent or natural<BR>phænomenon so considered.<BR>	 3. An affray, or assault, a conflict<BR>without weapons.<BR>	 4. Eclipse.<BR>	 5. Misfortune.<BR> E. उप over, &c. प्लु to<BR>go, अप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=128-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपप्लुत
उपप्लुत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Distressed, pained.<BR>	 2. Harassed (by Rāhu,<BR>&c.) eclipsed.<BR>	 3. Assailed, beset.<BR>	 4. Marked by prodigies.<BR>	 5. Wet,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=128-b" target="_blank">Page128-b+ 60</a>]<BR>moistened.<BR>	 f. (-ता) Morid sensibility of the uterus.<BR> E. उप before<BR>प्लु to go, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=128-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपभुक्त
उपभुक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं) Used, enjoyed, possessed.<BR> E. उप before भुज् to<BR>enjoy, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=128-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपभुञ्जान
उपभुञ्जान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Using, enjoying.<BR> E. उप before भुज् to enjoy, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=128-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपभृत्
उपभृत् f. (-भृत्) A cup of a round shape, made of the wood of the<BR>banian tree, and used in sacrifices.<BR> E. उप, भृ to fill, क्विप् and तुक् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=128-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपभोग|उपभोगः
उपभोग m. (-गः)<BR>	 1. Pleasure, satisfaction.<BR>	 2. Enjoyment, use.<BR>	 3. Cohabi-<BR>tation.<BR>	 4. Use, usufruct.<BR> E. उप excess, भुज् to eat, &c. affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=128-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपभोग्य
उपभोग्य mfn. (-ग्यः-ग्या-ग्यं) To be used, to be enjoyed.<BR> E. उप before भुज् to<BR>enjoy, य aff.; also उपभोजनीय and उपभोक्तव्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=128-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपमर्द्द|उपमर्द|उपमर्दः
उपमर्द्द m. (-र्द्दः)<BR>	 1. Reproach, abuse.<BR>	 2. Refuting a charge.<BR> E. उप, मृद् to<BR>tread down, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=128-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपमर्द्दक|उपमर्दक|उपमर्दकः
उपमर्द्दक m. (-कः) The refuting of a charge.<BR> E. कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=128-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपमा
उपमा f. (-मा)<BR>	 1. Likeness, (but used only in composition.)<BR>2. Resemblance, a resemblance as a picture, an image, &c.<BR>	 3. A<BR>simile.<BR> E. उप like, मा to measure, affixes अङ् and टाप्; also with<BR>ल्युट् aff. उपमान.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=128-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपमातृ
उपमातृ mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ) An image-maker, a portrait-painter.<BR> E. उप be-<BR>fore मा to measure, तृच् aff.<BR>	 f. (-त्री)<BR>	 1. A wet nurse.<BR>	 2. A near female<BR>relative.<BR> E. उप like, मातृ a mother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=128-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपमान|उपमानं
उपमान n. (-नं) See उपमा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=128-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपमित
उपमित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Compared.<BR> E. उप and मा to measure, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=128-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपमिति|उपमितिः
उपमिति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Resemblance, comparison, a likeness, a picture,<BR>image, &c.<BR>	 2. Analogy.<BR>	 3. Knowledge of things derived from ana-<BR>logy or resemblances.<BR> E. उप like, मा to measure, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=128-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपमेत|उपमेतः
उपमेत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Compared with.<BR>	 m. (-तः) The Sal, a timber tree,<BR>(Shorea robusta.)<BR> E. उपमा like, इत gone: high as a mountain, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=128-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपमेय
उपमेय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) To be compared with or to.<BR>	 n. (-यं) The subject<BR>of a comparison, as the face is of the moon.<BR> E. उप before मा to<BR>measure, य affix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=128-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपमेयोपमा
उपमेयोपमा f. (-मा) The resemblance of any object to that compared with<BR>it, as of the moon to a beautiful face.<BR> E. उपमेय and उपमा likeness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=128-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपयन्तृ|उपयंतृ
उपयन्तृ m. (-न्ता) A husband, a master.<BR> E. उप, यम् to cease, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=128-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपयन्त्र|उपयंत्र|उपयंत्रं
उपयन्त्र n. (-न्त्रं)<BR>	 1. A small instrument or implement.<BR>	 2. An application<BR>of a similar nature, as actual cautery, escharotics, &c.<BR> E. उप and<BR>यन्त्र instrument.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=128-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपयम|उपयमः
उपयम m. (-मः) Marriage.<BR> E. उप and यम् to stop, affix अप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=128-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपयाचक|उपयाचकः
उपयाचक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) A present solicitor, one who asks or begs. E.<BR>उप before याच् to beg, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=128-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपयाचित|उपयाचितं
उपयाचित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Requested, solicited.<BR>	 2. Offered especially to<BR>the deities to render them propitious.<BR> E. उप much, याच् to ask or<BR>beg, affix क्त, or with कन् added उपयाचितक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=128-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपयाम|उपयामः
उपयाम m. (-मः) Marriage.<BR> E. उप, यम् to refrain, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=128-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपयुक्त|उपयुक्तः
उपयुक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>	 1. Proper, right.<BR>	 2. Adapted to, suitable, appro-<BR>priate, useful.<BR>	 3. Touched by.<BR>	 4. Taken.<BR>	 5. Eaten.<BR> E. उप before युज्<BR>to join, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=128-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपयुञ्जान
उपयुञ्जान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Taking, appropriating, attaching.<BR> E. उप before<BR>युजि to join, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=128-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपयोग|उपयोगः
उपयोग m. (-गः)<BR>	 1. Good conduct, observing established practices.<BR>	 2. Any<BR>act tending to effect a desired object.<BR>	 3. Fitness, suitableness.<BR>	 4.<BR>Service, utility.<BR>	 5. Use, application.<BR>	 6. Contact, proximity.<BR>	 7. Ad-<BR>minstration of medicines.<BR>	 8. Preparation of them.<BR> E. उप before युज्<BR>to join, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=128-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपयोगिता
उपयोगिता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Fitness, suitableness.<BR>	 2. Usefulness.<BR>	 3. Occasion,<BR>need.<BR>	 4. Favour, propitiousness.<BR> E. उपयोगिन् and तल् affix, or with<BR>त्व, उपयोगित्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=128-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपयोगिन्
उपयोगिन् mfn. (-गी-गिनी-गि)<BR>	 1. Appropriate, suitable.<BR>	 2. Conducive or<BR>contributing to, serviceable, useful.<BR>	 3. Favourable, propitious.<BR>	 4.<BR>Touching, in contact with<BR> E. उपयोग and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=128-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपयोषम्
उपयोषम् ind. A word expressing great pleasure: see उपजोषम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=129-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपरक्त|उपरक्तः
उपरक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं) Afflicted with pain or calamity.<BR>	 m. (-क्तः)<BR>	 1.<BR>Eclipsed, (the sun or moon.)<BR>	 2. Rahu, (the ascending node.)<BR> E. उप<BR>implying distress, रञ्ज् to colour, and क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=129-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपरक्षण|उपरक्षणं
उपरक्षण n. (-णं) A guard, an outpost.<BR> E. उप, रक्ष् to defend or protect,<BR>aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=129-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपरचित
उपरचित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Made, prepared.<BR> E. उप and रचित made.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=129-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपरत|उपरतः
उपरत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Stopped, ceased.<BR>	 2. Dead.<BR> E. उप before रम् to<BR>please, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=129-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपरतस्पृह|उपरतस्पृहः
उपरतस्पृह mfn. (-हः-हा-हं) Void of desire.<BR> E. उपरत and स्पृहा desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=129-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपरति|उपरतिः
उपरति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Stopping, ceasing.<BR>	 2. Refraining from sensual enjoy-<BR>ment.<BR>	 3. Abstaining from prescribed acts.<BR>	 4. Great or exquisite<BR>pleasure.<BR>	 5. Death.<BR> E. उप reverse or excess, रम् to please, क्तिन्<BR>affix; also with घञ् affix उपरम or उपराम.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=129-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपरम|उपरमः
उपरम m. (-मः) See the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=129-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपरमण|उपरमणं
उपरमण n. (-णं) Abstaining from ceremonial acts or from the pleasures<BR>of sense, &c.<BR>	 2. Ceasing, discontinuance.<BR> E. उप before रम् to please,<BR>affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=129-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपरस|उपरसः
उपरस m. (-सः)<BR>	 1. A secondary mineral, as red chalk, bitumen, &c.<BR>	 2. A<BR>secondary passion.<BR>	 3. A subordinate flavour.<BR> E. उप minor, रस<BR>flavour, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=129-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपराग|उपरागः
उपराग m. (-गः)<BR>	 1. An eclipse of the sun or moon.<BR>	 2. Rahu or the<BR>ascending node.<BR>	 3. Calamity, affliction.<BR>	 4. Misbehaviour, ill con-<BR>duct.<BR>	 5. Reproach, abuse.<BR> E. उप, रञ्ज् to colour, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=129-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपराम|उपरामः
उपराम m. (-मः) Stopping, ceasing: see उपरति.<BR> E. उप, रम् to please, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=129-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपरि
उपरि ind. On, upon, above.<BR> E. उप and रि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=129-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपरिगत
उपरिगत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Gone up, ascended.<BR> E. उपरि and गत gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=129-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपरिचित
उपरिचित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Piled over or above.<BR> E. उपरि and चित collected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=129-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपरिज
उपरिज mfn. (-जः-जा-जं) High, elevated, produced above.<BR> E. उपरि and<BR>ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=129-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपरिष्टात्
उपरिष्टात् ind. Up, above.<BR> E. उप and रिष्टातिल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=129-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपरुद्ध|उपरुद्धः
उपरुद्ध mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>	 1. Obstructed, impeded.<BR>	 2. Covered, spread.<BR>	 3.<BR>Favoured.<BR> E. उप and रुद्ध checked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=129-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपरोध|उपरोधः
उपरोध m. (-धः)<BR>	 1. Impediment, opposition, check, refusal.<BR>	 2. Favour,<BR>protection.<BR>	 3. Surrounding, blockading.<BR>	 4. Binding, tying.<BR>	 5. Tak-<BR>ing hold of.<BR> E. उप before रुध् to confine, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=129-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपरोधक|उपरोधकं
उपरोधक n. (-कं) An inner room, a private apartment.<BR> E. उप near, रुध्<BR>to enclose, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=129-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपर्य्युपरि
उपर्य्युपरि ind.<BR>	 1. Over, upon, above, what is above.<BR>	 2. Near, neigh-<BR>bouring.<BR> E. उपरि repeated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=129-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपल|उपलः
उपल m. (-लः) A rock or stone, a precious stone or jewel.<BR>	 f. (-ला) Re-<BR>fined or candied sugar.<BR> E. उप near, ला to give or take; affix ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=129-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपलक्ष्य|उपलक्ष्यः
उपलक्ष्य mfn. (-क्ष्यः-क्ष्या-क्ष्यं) Inferable.<BR>	 m. (-क्ष्यः)<BR>	 1. A prop, a stay, a<BR>support, an asylum.<BR>	 2. An inference.<BR> E. उप near, लक्ष्य to be mark-<BR>ed or sought.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=129-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपलक्षण|उपलक्षणं
उपलक्षण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Designating or implying any analogous object<BR>where only one is specified, using a term in a generic sense.<BR>	 2.<BR>Metaphorical or elliptical expression.<BR> E. उप comprehensive, लक्षण<BR>a mark or designation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=129-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपलक्षित
उपलक्षित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Comprehended, included, implied, understood.<BR>E. उप before लक्ष् to designate, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=129-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपलब्ध
उपलब्ध mfn. (-ब्धः-ब्धा-ब्धं)<BR>	 1. Obtained, received.<BR>	 2. Understood, known.<BR>3. Perceived.<BR> E. उप before लभ् to get, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=129-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपलब्धार्था
उपलब्धार्था f. (-र्था) A tale, a true or probable story.<BR> E. उपलब्ध under-<BR>stood, अर्थ meaning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=129-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपलब्धि|उपलब्धिः
उपलब्धि f. (-ब्धिः)<BR>	 1. Mind, understanding.<BR>	 2. Knowledge, especially reli-<BR>gious.<BR>	 3. Gain, acquisition.<BR>	 4. Perceptibility, appearance.<BR> E. उप,<BR>लभ् to obtain, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=129-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपलम्भ|उपलंभ|उपलंभः|उपलम्भः
उपलम्भ m. (-म्भः) Apprehension, conception, comprehension otherwise<BR>than from memory.<BR> E. उप near, लभि to obtain, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=129-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपलभ्य
उपलभ्य mfn. (-भ्यः-भ्या-भ्यं)<BR>	 1. To be obtained.<BR>	 2. To be understood. ind.<BR>Having observed.<BR> E. उप before लभ् to get, यत् or ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=129-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपलम्भ्य|उपलम्भ्यः
उपलम्भ्य mfn. (-म्भ्यः-म्भ्या-म्भ्यं) Commendable, praise-worthy, respectable.<BR>E. उप before लभ् to get, ण्यत् affix, and म augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=129-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपलालिका
उपलालिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. Thirst.<BR>	 2. Oppression.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=129-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपलिङ्ग|उपलिंग|उपलिंगं|उपलिङ्गं
उपलिङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः) A portent, a natural phænomenon considered as an-<BR>nouncing evil.<BR> E. उप over, लिगि to go, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=129-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपलिप्त
उपलिप्त mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं) Smeared, plastered.<BR> E. उप and लिप्त smeared.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=129-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपलिप्सित
उपलिप्सित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Wishing to take or seize.<BR> E. उप before लभ् to<BR>gain, desider. form, क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=129-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपलेप|उपलेपः
उपलेप m. (-पः) Plastering, smearing, anointing.<BR> E. उप, लिप् to smear,<BR>affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=129-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपलेपन|उपलेपनं
उपलेपन n. (-नं) Smearing, plastering with cow-dung, &c.<BR> E. उप, लिप् to smear, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=129-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपवन|उपवनं
उपवन n. (-नं) A garden, a grove.<BR> E. उप like, and वन a wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=129-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपवर्णन|उपवर्णनं
उपवर्णन n. (-नं) Minute description.<BR> E. उप and वर्णन describing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=129-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपवर्त्तन|उपवर्तन|उपवर्तनं|उपवर्त्तनं
उपवर्त्तन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. A country inhabited or not.<BR>	 2. An uninhabited<BR>country.<BR>	 3. A division, a district or Pargana.<BR>	 4. A kingdom.<BR> E. उप,<BR>वृत् to abide, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=129-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपवर्ष|उपवर्षः
उपवर्ष m. (-र्षः) The name of a saint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=129-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपवर्ह|उपवर्हः
उपवर्ह m. (-र्हः) A pillow.<BR> E. उप over, वर्ह to excel, &c. घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=129-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपवसथ|उपवसथः
उपवसथ m. (-थः) A village.<BR> E. उप, वस् to abide, थक् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=129-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपवस्त|उपवस्तं
उपवस्त n. (-स्तं) A fast, fasting.<BR> E. उप, वस् to abide, क्त affix; or with घञ्<BR>affix उपवास.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=129-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपवास|उपवासः
उपवास m. (-सः)<BR>	 1. A fast, fasting: when observed as a religious act,<BR>it comprises abstinence from all sensual gratification, from per-<BR>fumes, flowers, unguents, ornaments, betel, music and dancing,<BR>&c.<BR>	 2. A fire-alter.<BR> E. उप before वस् to abide, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=129-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपवासिन्
उपवासिन् mfn. (-सी-सिनी-सि) Fasting, one who observes a fast.<BR> E. उपवास<BR>and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=129-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपवाहन|उपवाहनं
उपवाहन n. (-नं) Carrying, bringing back.<BR> E. उप and वाहन bearing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=129-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपवाह्य|उपवाह्यः
उपवाह्य m. (-ह्यः)<BR>	 1. A king's elephant.<BR>	 2. Any royal vehicle.<BR> E. उप above,<BR>वह् to bear, ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=129-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपविद्या
उपविद्या f. (-द्या) Profane science, inferior sort of knowledge.<BR> E. उप and<BR>विद्या knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=129-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपविष|उपविषं|उपविषः
उपविष n. (-षं)<BR>	 1. Factitious poison.<BR>	 2. A narcotic, any deleterious drug,<BR>as opium, &c.<BR> E. उप like, विष poison.<BR>	 f. (-षा) A plant, Atis.<BR> E. उप<BR>reverse, and विष poison: an antidote.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=129-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपविष्ट|उपविष्टः
उपविष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>	 1. Seated, sitting.<BR>	 2. Arrived, entered.<BR> E. उप<BR>upon, विष्ट placed, entered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=129-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपवीत|उपवीतं
उपवीत n. (-तं) The thread or cord worn by the three first classes of<BR>Hindus, over the left shoulder and under the right.<BR> E. उप much, वी<BR>to shine, affix क्त; see उपनय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=129-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपवीतिन्
उपवीतिन् m. (-ती) The Brahman who wears the string in the usual<BR>manner, or on the left shoulder and under the right arm.<BR> E. उपवीत<BR>and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=129-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपवृंहित
उपवृंहित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Collected from, possessed of.<BR> E. उप and वृंहित<BR>collected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=129-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपवेद|उपवेदः
उपवेद m. (-दः) A minor Veda, of which four are reckoned, treating of<BR>the military art, medicine, music, and mechanics.<BR> E. उप and वेद a<BR>Veda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=129-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपवेश|उपवेशः
उपवेश m. (-शः)<BR>	 1. Sitting, resting.<BR>	 2. A seat.<BR>	 3. Voiding by stool.<BR> E. उप<BR>before विश् to enter, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=129-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपवेशन|उपवेशनं
उपवेशन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Sitting, resting.<BR>	 2. Voiding by stool.<BR> E. उप before विश्<BR>to enter, active or causal form, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=129-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपवेश्य
उपवेश्य ind. Having seated or caused to sit.<BR> E. उप before विश् to enter,<BR>causal form, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=129-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपव्याघ्र|उपव्याघ्रः
उपव्याघ्र m. (-घ्रः) The hunting leopard.<BR> E. उप and व्याघ्र a tiger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=129-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपशम|उपशमः
उपशम m. (-मः)<BR>	 1. Tranquillity, calmness, patience.<BR>	 2. Intermission,<BR>cessation.<BR> E. उप much, शम् to be tranquil, अप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=129-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपशय|उपशयः
उपशय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Productive of happiness or rest.<BR>	 m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. As-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=130-a" target="_blank">Page130-a+ 60</a>]<BR>certainment of disease or diagnosis by the effect of certain arti-<BR>cles of food or medicine.<BR>	 2. Allaying disease by diet, regimen, &c.<BR>E. उप before शी to sleep, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=129-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपशल्य|उपशल्यं|उपशल्यः
उपशल्य n. (-ल्यं) A space near a village.<BR> E. उप near, शल् to go, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=130-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपशान्त|उपशांत
उपशान्त mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं)<BR>	 1. Calm, tranquil.<BR>	 2. Appeased, pacified.<BR>	 3.<BR>Diminished, intermitted.<BR> E. उप before शम् to be tranquil, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=130-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपशान्ति|उपशांति|उपशांतिः|उपशान्तिः
उपशान्ति f. (-न्तिः)<BR>	 1. Tranquillity, calm.<BR>	 2. Appeasing, allaying.<BR>	 3. Cessa-<BR>tion, intermission.<BR> E. उप before शम् to be quiet, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=130-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपशान्तिन्|उपशांतिन्
उपशान्तिन् mfn. (-न्ती-न्तिनी-न्ति) Tranquil, calm, appeased, tame.<BR>	 f. (-न्तिनी)<BR>A tame elephant.<BR> E. उपशान्त and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=130-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपशाय|उपशायः
उपशाय m. (-यः) Watching and sleeping alternately.<BR> E. उप alternately,<BR>शी to sleep, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=130-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपशायिता
उपशायिता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Tranquillizing, calming.<BR>	 2. Secondary means of<BR>cure, as diet, &c.<BR> E. उपशायिन् and तल् affix; also with त्व, उपशायित्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=130-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपशायिन्
उपशायिन् mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि)<BR>	 1. Allaying, tranquillizing, what calms, &c.<BR>2. (In medicine,) Composing, narcotic.<BR> E. उप before शी to sleep,<BR>causal form, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=130-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपशोभित
उपशोभित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Adorned.<BR> E. उप and शोभित beautified.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=130-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपश्रुत|उपश्रुतं
उपश्रुत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) promised, agreed.<BR> E. उप with श्रु to hear, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=130-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपश्रुति|उपश्रुतिः
उपश्रुति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Promise, assent.<BR>	 2. Judicial astrology, aspect of the<BR>stars, fortune-telling.<BR> E. उप above, श्रु to hear, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=130-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसंक्षेप
उपसंक्षेप m. (-पः) An abstract or compendium.<BR> E. उप and संक्षेप abridgement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=130-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसंख्यान
उपसंख्यान n. (-नं) (In grammar,) A substitute in form or sense, a con-<BR>significant term or aff.<BR> E. उप near, संख्या to number, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=130-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसंग्रह
उपसंग्रह m. (-हः) Obeisance, civil address, respectful salutation of a<BR>person by name.<BR>	 2. Taking, holding.<BR> E. उप near, सम् with, ग्रह् to<BR>take, aff. घञ्, or with ल्युट् aff. उपसंग्रहणं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=130-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसंग्राह्य
उपसंग्राह्य mfn. (-ह्यः-ह्या-ह्यं)<BR>	 1. Respectable, venerable.<BR>	 2. To be saluted<BR>reverentially.<BR> E. उप and सम् before ग्रह् to take, ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=130-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसंगृह्य
उपसंगृह्य ind. Having taken, holding.<BR> E. उप and सम् before ग्रह् to take, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=130-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसंव्यान|उपसंव्यानं
उपसंव्यान n. (-नं) A lower garment.<BR> E. उप and सं before व्येञ् to cover,<BR>ल्युट् affix; what covers the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=130-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसंहरण|उपसंहरणं
उपसंहरण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Refusing, withholding.<BR>	 2. Excluding.<BR>	 3. Taking<BR>away.<BR>	 4. Attacking, invading.<BR> E. उप and सम् before हरण taking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=130-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसंहरत्
उपसंहरत् mfn. (-रन्-रन्ती-रत्)<BR>	 1. Taking away.<BR>	 2. Refusing, excepting.<BR>	 3.<BR>Going against, invading.<BR> E. उप and सं before हृ to take, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=130-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसंहार|उपसंहारः
उपसंहार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Withholding, refusing.<BR>	 2. Taking away.<BR>	 3. Except-<BR>ing, excluding.<BR>	 4. Destruction, death, end.<BR>	 5. Collection, assem-<BR>blage.<BR>	 6. Compendium.<BR>	 7. Brevity, conciseness.<BR>	 8. Attacking, in-<BR>vasion.<BR>	 9. (In logic,) Refutation.<BR> E. उप and सम् before हृ to take,<BR>घञ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=130-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसंहृत
उपसंहृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Withheld, denied, refused.<BR>	 2. Excepted.<BR>	 3.<BR>Compressed, comprehended, excluded.<BR> E. उप and सं before हृ to<BR>take, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=130-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसंहृति|उपसंहृतिः
उपसंहृति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. A compound expressive of various meanings.<BR>	 2.<BR>Comprehension.<BR>	 3. Seizing, taking.<BR> E. उप and सम् before हृ to take,<BR>क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=130-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसत्ति|उपसत्तिः
उपसत्ति f. (-त्तिः)<BR>	 1. Meeting, union.<BR>	 2. Service.<BR>	 3. Gift, donation.<BR> E. उप<BR>with, षद् to go, &c., क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=130-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसद|उपसदः
उपसद mfn. (-दः-दा-दं) Who goes near to.<BR>	 m. (-दः)<BR>	 1. Gift, donation.<BR>	 2.<BR>Approach.<BR> E. उप and षद् to go, affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=130-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसदन|उपसदनं
उपसदन n. (-नं) A neighbouring abode, a neighbourhood.<BR> E. उप near,<BR>and सदन a dwelling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=130-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसन्ध्यम्|उपसंध्यम्
उपसन्ध्यम् ind. Near evening.<BR> E. उप near, सन्ध्या evening.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=130-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसन्न|उपसन्नः
उपसन्न mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं) Approached, approximate.<BR> E. उप over, षद् to<BR>go, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=130-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसन्नता
उपसन्नता f. (-ता) Proximity, approach.<BR> E. उपसन्न and तल् affix; also<BR>उपसन्नत्वं with त्व aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=130-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसमाधान|उपसमाधानं
उपसमाधान n. (-नं) Placing, putting in or on.<BR> E. उप and सम् with आङ्<BR>before धा to have, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=130-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसम्पन्न|उपसंपन्न|उपसम्पन्नः
उपसम्पन्न mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>	 1. Dressed, cooked.<BR>	 2. Immolated, sacrificed,<BR>(as a victim, &c.)<BR>	 3. Dead, deceased.<BR>	 4. Gained, obtained.<BR>	 5.<BR>Enough, sufficient.<BR>	 6. Perfected, finished.<BR> E. उप and सम् prefixed<BR>to पद् to go, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=130-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसर|उपसरः
उपसर mfn. (-रः-रा-री-रं)<BR>	 1. The first pregnancy or impregnation of a<BR>cow, &c.<BR>	 2. Who or what approaches.<BR> E. उप before सृ to go, and<BR>अप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=130-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसर्ग|उपसर्गः
उपसर्ग m. (-र्गः)<BR>	 1. A portent, a natural phænomenon supposed to an-<BR>nounce future evil, an eclipse, &c.<BR>	 2. A particle prefixed to roots,<BR>&c., a preposition.<BR>	 3. A disease, possession by an evil spirit.<BR>4. Change occasioned by any disease.<BR>	 5. A disease brought on<BR>whilst a person labours under another.<BR>	 6. Indication or symptom<BR>of death.<BR> E. उप near or with, सृज् to go, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=130-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसर्जन|उपसर्जनं|उपसर्ज्जन|उपसर्ज्जनं
उपसर्जन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. A representative, a substitute, any person or thing<BR>subordinate or subsidiary.<BR>	 2. Portent, eclipse.<BR>	 3. Approaching.<BR>E. उप inferior, सृज् to go, ल्युट् aff. In the first sense, though used<BR>as an attributive, it is always neuter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=130-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसर्पण|उपसर्पणं
उपसर्पण n. (-णं) Approaching, advancing to.<BR> E. उप near, सृप् to go, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=130-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसर्य्या|उपसर्या
उपसर्य्या f. (-र्य्या) A cow, (fit for the bull.)<BR> E. उप, सृ to go, यत् aff. deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=130-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसार्य्य|उपसार्य|उपसार्य्यः
उपसार्य्य mfn. (-र्य्यः-र्य्या-र्य्यं) To be approached or gone to.<BR> E. उप before<BR>सृ to go, ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=130-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसुन्द|उपसुंदः|उपसुन्दः
उपसुन्द m. (-न्दः) The name of a demon.<BR> E. उप, and सुन्द another demon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=130-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसूर्य्यक|उपसूर्यक|उपसूर्यकं|उपसूर्यकः|उपसूर्य्यकं
उपसूर्य्यक n. (-कं) The disk of the sun or moon.<BR> E. उप near, or with, सूर्य्य<BR>the sun, कन् aff. of identity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=130-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसृत्य
उपसृत्य ind. Having approached.<BR> E. उप before सृ to go, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=130-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसृष्ट|उपसृष्टं|उपसृष्टः
उपसृष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>	 1. Attended by or accompanied with, joined,<BR>attached, connected to or with.<BR>	 2. Eclipsed, (as the sun or moon.)<BR>3. Seized by, possessed by, (evil demons, &c.)<BR>	 n. (-ष्टं) Coition, co-<BR>pulation.<BR> E. उप, सृज् to create, &c. aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=130-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसेवन|उपसेवनं
उपसेवन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Service.<BR>	 2. Addiction to.<BR> E. उप and सेव् to serve, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=130-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्कर|उपस्करः
उपस्कर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A condiment, a spice or seasoning, mustard, pepper,<BR>&c.<BR>	 2. An article of household use, as a broom, a basket, &c.<BR>	 3.<BR>Blame, censure.<BR> E. उप complete, and कर what makes, स inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=130-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्कृत
उपस्कृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Blamed, censured.<BR> E. उप and कृत made, स inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=130-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्तम्भ|उपस्तंभ|उपस्तंभः|उपस्तम्भः
उपस्तम्भ m. (-म्भः) Support of life, as food, sleep, and government of the<BR>passions.<BR> E. उप and स्तभि to stop, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=130-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्त्री
उपस्त्री f. (-स्त्री) A concubine.<BR> E. उप and स्त्री a female, a wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=130-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्थ|उपस्थः
उपस्थ mfn. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थं) Near, proximate.<BR>	 m. (-स्थः)<BR>	 1. The male or<BR>female organs of generation.<BR>	 2. The haunch or hip.<BR>	 3. The anus.<BR>E. उप near, and स्थ what is or stays, ड aff. after स्था.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=130-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्थपत्र|उपस्थपत्रः
उपस्थपत्र m. (-त्रः) Indian fig tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=130-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्थनिग्रह|उपस्थनिग्रहः
उपस्थनिग्रह m. (-हः) Continence.<BR> E. उपस्थ an organ of generation, and<BR>निग्रह restraining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=130-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्थातृ
उपस्थातृ mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ) A servant.<BR> E. उप before स्था to remain, तृच aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=130-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्थान|उपस्थानं
उपस्थान n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Proximity, nearness.<BR>	 2. Obtaining, getting.<BR>	 3. An<BR>assembly.<BR> E. उप near, स्था to stay, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=130-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्थानीय
उपस्थानीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>	 1. To be stayed with or near.<BR>	 2. What ought<BR>to be near or with.<BR> E. उप before स्था to stay, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=130-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्थापक
उपस्थापक mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>	 1. Placing or bringing near to.<BR>	 2. Explaining,<BR>teaching, a teacher.<BR>	 3. Causing to obtain.<BR> E. उप before स्था to be,<BR>causal form, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=130-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्थापन|उपस्थापनं
उपस्थापन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Placing near.<BR>	 2. Attendance, service.<BR> E. उप and स्थापन placing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=130-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्थापयितव्य
उपस्थापयितव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं) To be placed near.<BR> E. उप before स्था to<BR>stay, causal form, तव्य aff.; also उपस्थापनीय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=130-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्थापित
उपस्थापित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Placed near to.<BR>	 2. Attended.<BR> E. उप before<BR>स्था to stay, causal form, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=130-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्थाय
उपस्थाय ind.<BR>	 1. Having approached.<BR>	 2. Having brought near to or<BR>assembled.<BR> E. उप near, and स्था to stay, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=130-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्थायिन्
उपस्थायिन् mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि) Standing near, being present.<BR> E. उप before<BR>स्था to stay. णिनि aff. and युक् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=130-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्थित|उपस्थितः
उपस्थित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Approached, arrived.<BR>	 2. Staying by or near<BR>to.<BR>	 3. Caused, occasioned.<BR>	 4. Got, received.<BR>	 5. Felt.<BR>	 6. Clean,<BR>cleansed.<BR>	 7. Done, accomplished.<BR>	 8. Known.<BR> E. उप before स्था to<BR>stay, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=131-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्थिति|उपस्थितिः
उपस्थिति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Proximity.<BR>	 2. Obtaining, getting.<BR>	 3. Effecting, ac-<BR>complishing.<BR>	 4. Arrival.<BR>	 5. Knowledge.<BR> E. उप before स्था to be,<BR>aff. क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=131-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्पर्श|उपस्पर्शः
उपस्पर्श m. (-र्शः)<BR>	 1. Touching, contact.<BR>	 2. Bathing, ablution.<BR>	 3. Rincing<BR>the mouth, sipping water and ejecting it.<BR> E. उप like, स्पर्श touch,<BR>from स्पृश् to touch, and अच् aff.; or with ल्युट् aff. उपस्पर्शन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=131-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्पर्शन|उपस्पर्शनं
उपस्पर्शन n. (-नं) See the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=131-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्पृष्ट
उपस्पृष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>	 1. Touched.<BR>	 2. Sipped.<BR> E. उप and स्पृष्ट touched.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=131-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्वत्व|उपस्वत्वं
उपस्वत्व n. (-त्वं) Revenue, profit, what is derived from land or other<BR>capital.<BR> E. उप and स्वत्व ownership.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=131-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहत|उपहतः
उपहत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Destroyed.<BR>	 2. Injured, impaired, evilly affected<BR>by.<BR>	 3. Struck by lightning, &c.<BR>	 4. Pained, hurt.<BR>	 5. Impure.<BR>	 6.<BR>Infected, polluted, vitiated.<BR> E. उप and हत struck.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=131-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहतदृश्
उपहतदृश् mfn. (-दृक्) Dazzled, blinded.<BR> E. उपहत struck, दृश् the eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=131-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहतात्मन्
उपहतात्मन् mfn. (-त्मा-त्मा-त्म) Agitated, affected as by passion, &c. E.<BR>उपहत and आत्मन् the soul.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=131-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहरण|उपहरणं
उपहरण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Offering gifts to superiors.<BR>	 2. Presenting victims.<BR>	 3.<BR>Distributing or serving out food.<BR>	 4. Taking, seizing.<BR> E. उप before<BR>हृ to take, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=131-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहर्त्तव्य|उपहर्तव्य
उपहर्त्तव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>	 1. To be offered as a victim.<BR>	 2. To be pre-<BR>sented.<BR> E. उप before हृ take, तव्य aff.; also उपहरणीय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=131-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहर्तृ|उपहर्त्तृ
उपहर्तृ mfn. (-र्ता-त्री-र्तृ) Offering victims, serving out food, &c.<BR> E. उप<BR>before हृ to take, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=131-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहव|उपहवः
उपहव m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. Calling to.<BR>	 2. Summoning, invoking.<BR> E. उप before हु to<BR>call, अप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=131-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहसित|उपहसितं
उपहसित n. (-तं) Laughter, laughing.<BR> E. उप up, हसित laughing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=131-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहार|उपहारः
उपहार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A complimentary gift, a present to a superior, &c.<BR>2. A victim, an offering to a deity.<BR>	 3. Tribute, indemnification,<BR>presents as the price of peace.<BR>	 4. Food distributed to guests, &c. E.<BR>उप before हृ to convey, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=131-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहारिन्
उपहारिन् mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>	 1. Giving, presenting.<BR>	 2. Sacrificing.<BR> E. उप-<BR>हार and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=131-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहालक|उपहालकः
उपहालक m. (-कः) The name of a country, part of the peninsula: see<BR>कुन्तल.<BR> E. उप, हाल a king so named, aff. क, the country over which<BR>HALA reigned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=131-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहास|उपहासः
उपहास m. (-सः) Ridicule, laughing at any one.<BR> E. उप before हस् to<BR>laugh, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=131-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहास्य
उपहास्य mfn. (-स्यः-स्या-स्यं) Rediculous, laughable.<BR> E. उप and हास्य to be<BR>laughed at.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=131-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहित
उपहित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Placed, deposited, placed in or upon.<BR>	 2. Laid<BR>aside.<BR>	 3. Joined.<BR>	 4. Mixed.<BR> E. उप before हा to quit, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=131-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहूय
उपहूय ind Having called or addressed.<BR> E. उप near, ह्वे to call, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=131-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहृत
उपहृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Taken, collected, gathered.<BR>	 2. Offered,<BR>presented.<BR>	 3. Immolated, offered as a victim.<BR>	 4. Served out as<BR>food.<BR> E. उप before हृ to take, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=131-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपह्वर|उपह्वरं|उपह्वरः
उपह्वर n. (-रं)<BR>	 1. Solitary, private.<BR>	 2. Near.<BR>	 m. (-रः) A car, a carriage. E.<BR>उपह्वृ to bend, अप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=131-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपांशु|उपांशुः
उपांशु m. (-शुः) Muttering prayers, reciting them in a low voice so as<BR>not to be overheard. ind.<BR>	 1. Solitary, private.<BR>	 2. Secretely, in a<BR>whisper.<BR> E. उप, अंशु a ray.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=131-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाकरण|उपाकरणं
उपाकरण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Performance of a preparatory rite before reading<BR>the Vedas.<BR>	 2. Immolation, sacrifice of an animal duly consecrated.<BR>E. उप and आङ् prefixed to कृ to do, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=131-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाकर्म्मन्|उपाकर्मन्
उपाकर्म्मन् n. (-र्म्म)<BR>	 1. Preparation.<BR>	 2. A ceremony performed before read-<BR>ing the Vedas.<BR>	 3. Beginning to read the Vedas. E. See the preced-<BR>ing, the aff. being मनिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=131-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाकृत|उपाकृतं|उपाकृतः
उपाकृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Attended with evil omens, disastrous, calamitous.<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>	 1. A victim slain or to be slain.<BR>	 2. A portent, a phæno-<BR>menon announcing calamity.<BR> E. उप and आङ् before कृत made.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=131-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाख्यान|उपाख्यानं
उपाख्यान n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. A tale, a narrative.<BR>	 2. Telling, narration.<BR> E. उप and<BR>आख्यान a tale.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=131-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपागत
उपागत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Suffering, feeling.<BR>	 2. Promised.<BR>	 3. Approached<BR>arrived.<BR>	 4. Occurred, happened.<BR> E. उप and आङ् before गम् to go,<BR>aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=131-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपागम|उपागमः
उपागम m. (-मः)<BR>	 1. Promise, agreement.<BR>	 2. Approach.<BR>	 3. Occurrence, ar-<BR>rival.<BR>	 4. Feeling, suffering.<BR> E. उप near, आङ् before गम् to come, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=131-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाग्रहण|उपाग्रहणं
उपाग्रहण n. (-णं) Reading the Vedas after initiation.<BR> E. उप and आङ् be-<BR>fore ग्रह् to take, ल्युट् aff.: see उपाकरण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=131-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाङ्ग|उपांग|उपांगः|उपाङ्गः
उपाङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>	 1. The sectarial mark made with Sandal, &c. on the<BR>forehead.<BR>	 2. Any minor limb or member.<BR>	 3. Secondary portion of<BR>science.<BR> E. उप and अङ्ग the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=131-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाञ्जन|उपांजन|उपांजनं
उपाञ्जन n. (-नं) Plastering the ground with cow-dung, &c.<BR> E. उप and<BR>अञ्जन anointing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=131-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपात्त|उपात्तं|उपात्तः
उपात्त mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं) Taken, received, gained, got.<BR>	 m. (-त्तः) An ele-<BR>phant out of rut.<BR> E. उप near, आत्त taken, seized.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=131-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपात्तरंहस्
उपात्तरंहस् mfn. (-हाः-हाः-हः) Quick, fleet.<BR> E. उपात्त acquired, रंहस् speed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=131-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपात्तशस्त्र
उपात्तशस्त्र mfn. (-स्त्रः-स्त्रा-स्त्रं) Armed, taking up arms.<BR> E. उपात्त and शस्त्र<BR>a weapon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=131-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपात्यय|उपात्ययः
उपात्यय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. Neglect or disobedience of ordinances or customs.<BR>2. Disorder or disorderly behaviour.<BR> E. उप and अति prefixed to इण्<BR>to go, अच aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=131-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपादान|उपादानं
उपादान n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Taking away, abduction, taking.<BR>	 2. Abstraction, res-<BR>training the organs of sense and perception.<BR>	 3. Cause, motive.<BR>4. Immediate or proximate cause.<BR>	 5. The formal or distinct form,<BR>the material cause.<BR>	 6. A double meaning, an expression convey-<BR>ing a sense besides that which appears intended.<BR>	 7. Saying, speak-<BR>ing.<BR> E. उप near, आदा to take, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=131-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपादानकारण
उपादानकारण n. (-णं) A proximate cause.<BR> E. उपादान and कारण cause.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=131-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपादिका
उपादिका f. (-का) A potherb, (Basella lucida.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=131-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपादेय|उपादेयः
उपादेय mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>	 1. Acceptable, admissible, to be taken or<BR>received.<BR>	 2. Excellent, admirable.<BR> E. उप and आङ् before दा to<BR>give, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=131-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाधि|उपाधिः
उपाधि m. (-धिः)<BR>	 1. Virtuous reflection.<BR>	 2. A discriminative or dis-<BR>tinguishing property, an attribute.<BR>	 3. Deception, disguise. (In<BR>the Vadanta this is especially applied to certain natural forms or<BR>properties, considered as disguises of the spirit.)<BR>	 4. A title, a dis-<BR>criminative appellation, a nickname.<BR>	 5. Careful or diligent for<BR>the support of a family, (always masculine, though with a<BR>feminine or neuter substantive.)<BR>	 6. A purpose, an occasion, an<BR>object.<BR>	 7. (In logic,) A special cause for a general effect.<BR>	 8. (In<BR>rhetoric,) The natural character of species, quality, or action. E.<BR>उप and आङ् before धा to have, aff. कि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=131-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाध्याय|उपाध्यायः
उपाध्याय m. (-यः) A spiritual preceptor.<BR>	 f. (-या) A female preceptor.<BR>	 f.<BR>(-यी or -यानी) The wife of a teacher.<BR> E. उप and अधि before इण to<BR>go, घञ् aff. for the fem. टाप् aff. in the first instance, in the second<BR>ङीष् with or without आनुक् inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=131-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपानह्
उपानह् f. (-नत्) A shoe.<BR> E. उप and आङ् before नह् to bind, aff. क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=131-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपान्त|उपांत|उपान्तः
उपान्त mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं) Near.<BR>	 m. (-न्तः) The angle of the eye.<BR> E. उप near,<BR>अन्त end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=131-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपान्तिक|उपांतिक
उपान्तिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Near, proximate, neighbouring.<BR> E. उपान्त and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=131-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपान्त्य|उपांत्य|उपान्त्यः
उपान्त्य m. (-न्त्यः) The corner of the eye.<BR>	 n. (-न्त्यं) Vicinity.<BR> E. उप and<BR>अन्त्य end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=131-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाय|उपायः
उपाय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. A means, an expedient, a way.<BR>	 2. A means of success<BR>against an enemy; four are usually enumerated, as, sowing<BR>dissension, chastisement, conciliation and gifts.<BR>	 3. Approaching,<BR>approach.<BR> E. उप and आङ् before इण् to go, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=131-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपायज्ञ
उपायज्ञ mfn. (-ज्ञः-ज्ञा-ज्ञं) Fertile in expedients, contriving, providing<BR>for.<BR> E. उपाय and ज्ञ who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=132-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपायन|उपायनं
उपायन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. A present, a complementary or respectful gift.<BR>	 2.<BR>Approaching, going near to.<BR>	 3. Engaging in a religious observance.<BR>E. उप before अय् to go, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=132-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपायिन्
उपायिन् mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि) Expert in the use of means.<BR> E. उपाय and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=132-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाययोग|उपाययोगः
उपाययोग m. (-गः) Application of means, or combination of expedients.<BR>E. उपाय and योग union.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=132-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपार्ज्जन|उपार्जन|उपार्जनं|उपार्ज्जनं
उपार्ज्जन n. (-नं) Acquiring property, earning.<BR> E. उप and अर्ज्जन gaining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=132-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपार्ज्जित|उपार्जित
उपार्ज्जित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Gained, acquired, earned.<BR> E. उप and अर्ज्जित<BR>gained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=132-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपारत
उपारत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Engaged in, occupied by.<BR>	 2. Frequenting,<BR>resorting to.<BR> E. उप and आङ् before रम् to sport, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=132-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपारम|उपारमः
उपारम m. (-मः)<BR>	 1. Engaging in.<BR>	 2. Going to or in.<BR> E. उप and आङ् be-<BR>fore रम् to sport, affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=132-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपालब्ध
उपालब्ध mfn. (-ब्धः-ब्धा-ब्धं) Reproached, reviled.<BR> E. उप and आङ् before<BR>लभि to hurt, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=132-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपालम्भ|उपालंभ|उपालंभः|उपालम्भः
उपालम्भ m. (-म्भः)<BR>	 1. Abuse, reviling.<BR>	 2. Deferring, delaying.<BR> E. उप and<BR>आङ् before लभि to injure, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=132-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपावर्त्तन|उपावर्तन|उपावर्तनं
उपावर्त्तन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Turning round, revolving.<BR>	 2. Ceasing.<BR>	 3. Turning<BR>back, returning.<BR>	 4. Approaching.<BR> E. उप and आङ् before वृत् to be,<BR>ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=132-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपावृत्त|उपावृत्तः
उपावृत्त mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं)<BR>	 1. Rolling on the ground.<BR>	 2. Ceased, ceasing,<BR>refraining.<BR>	 m. (-त्तः) A horse rolling himself on the ground.<BR> E. उप<BR>and आङ् before वृत् to be, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=132-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाश्रय|उपाश्रयः
उपाश्रय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. Asylum, support.<BR>	 2. Reliance, dependence upon. E.<BR>उप and आङ् before श्री to serve, affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=132-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाश्रित
उपाश्रित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Supporting, (literally or figuratively) bearing,<BR>holding, protecting.<BR>	 2. Relying or depending upon.<BR> E. उप near,<BR>and आश्रित giving support.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=132-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपासक|उपासकः
उपासक mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>	 1. Worshipping, a worshipper.<BR>	 2. Serving, a<BR>servant.<BR>	 3. A Śūdra.<BR> E. उप before अस् to be, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=132-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपासङ्ग|उपासंग|उपासंगः|उपासङ्गः
उपासङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः) A quiver.<BR> E. उप and आङ् before षञ्ज to embrace, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=132-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपासन|उपासनं
उपासन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Archery.<BR>	 2. Service.<BR>	 3. A seat.<BR>	 4. Assembling.<BR>	 5. In-<BR>juring, hurting.<BR>	 f. (-ना)<BR>	 1. Service.<BR>	 2. Worship, adoration.<BR> E. उप<BR>before आस् to sit, or आङ् before अस् to throw or send, affix युच्<BR>and fem. टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=132-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपासित|उपासितः
उपासित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Served, honoured, worshipped.<BR>	 2. Serving,<BR>paying worship or service.<BR> E. उप inferiority, आस् to sit or remain,<BR>affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=132-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपासितृ
उपासितृ m. (-ता) A worshipper.<BR> E. उप and आङ् before आस् to sit, तृन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=132-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपासीन
उपासीन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>	 1. Sitting with or near to.<BR>	 2. Occupying.<BR> E. उप<BR>before आसीन seated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=132-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपास्ति|उपास्तिः
उपास्ति f. (-स्तिः) Service, especially of a deity, worship.<BR> E. उप before आस्<BR>to sit, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=132-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपास्य
उपास्य mfn. (-स्यः-स्या-स्यं) To be worshipped or served. ind.<BR>	 1. Having<BR>served or worshipped.<BR>	 2. Having associated or called together. E.<BR>उप before आस् to sit, यत् or ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=132-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपास्यमान
उपास्यमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Being served or worshipped, receiving hom-<BR>age.<BR> E. उप before आस् to sit, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=132-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाहित|उपाहितः
उपाहित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Joined, annexed.<BR>	 2. Deposited, placed.<BR>	 3.<BR>Put on, worn.<BR>	 4. Agreed upon, made or done mutually.<BR>	 m. (-तः)<BR>A fiery potent, a meteor, a comet.<BR> E. उप and आङ् before धा to<BR>have or hold, affix क्त, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=132-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाहृत
उपाहृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Prepared.<BR>	 2. Taken, seized.<BR> E. उप and आङ्<BR>before हृ to take, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=132-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपेक्षक
उपेक्षक mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>	 1. Disregarding, neglecting, disdaining.<BR>	 2.<BR>Patient, enduring.<BR> E. उप before ईक्ष् to see, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=132-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपेक्षण|उपेक्षणं
उपेक्षण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Leaving, abandoning.<BR>	 2. Disregarding, neglecting,<BR>disdaining.<BR> E. उप and ईणक्ष seeing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=132-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपेक्षा
उपेक्षा f. (-क्षा)<BR>	 1. Trick, deceit, one of the minor expedients in war.<BR>	 2.<BR>Abandoning, leaving.<BR>	 3. Dissent.<BR>	 4. Negligence, neglect.<BR>	 5. En-<BR>durance, patience.<BR>	 6. Contempt, disdain.<BR> E. उप before ईक्ष् to see,<BR>अङ् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=132-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपेक्षित
उपेक्षित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Disregarded, disesteemed, neglected, disdained.<BR>E. उप before ईक्ष् to see, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=132-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपेत
उपेत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Endowed with, possessed of, having, possessing.<BR>2. Arrived at, come to, come near to.<BR>	 3. Invested.<BR> E. उप and इत<BR>gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=132-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपेतृ
उपेतृ mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ)<BR>	 1. Contriving, contriver, one who employs expedi-<BR>ents.<BR>	 2. Approaching, going near to.<BR> E. उप before इण् to go, तृच्<BR>aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=132-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपेन्द्र|उपेंद्र|उपेंद्रः|उपेन्द्रः
उपेन्द्र m. (-न्द्रः) A name of VIṢṆU or KṚṢṆA.<BR> E. उप after, इन्द्र INDRA:<BR>born subsequently to INDRA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=132-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपेन्द्रवज्रा
उपेन्द्रवज्रा f. (-ज्रा) A species of the Trishtubh metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=132-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपेय|उपेयः
उपेय mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>	 1. To be sought, to be had recourse to.<BR>	 2. To be<BR>gone to or approached.<BR>	 3. To be effected by any means.<BR> E. उप be-<BR>fore इण् to go, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=132-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपेयिवस्
उपेयिवस् mfn. (-वान्-युषी-वत्)<BR>	 1. Accompanied or followed by, associated<BR>with, united.<BR>	 2. Obtained, got.<BR> E. उप near, इण् to go, क्वसु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=132-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपेयुस्
उपेयुस् mfn. (-यूः-यूः-युः) Arrived at, gone to.<BR> E. उप before इण् to go, उस् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=132-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपोढ|उपोढः
उपोढ mfn. (-ढः-ढा-ढं)<BR>	 1. Near, proximate.<BR>	 2. Married.<BR>	 3. Arrayed, ar-<BR>ranged.<BR> E. उप before वह् to bear, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=132-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपोती
उपोती f. (-ती) A potherb, (Basella rubra or lucida.)<BR> E. उप much, and<BR>उद water, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=132-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपोदकी
उपोदकी f. (-की) See the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=132-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपोदिका
उपोदिका f. (-का) A potherb, (Basella rubra or lucida.)<BR> E. उप and उद<BR>water, कन् and टाप् affs. and इ substituted for the pen. or ई being<BR>substituted उपोदीका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=132-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपोद्घात|उपोद्घातः
उपोद्घात m. (-तः)<BR>	 1. A beginning, a thing begun.<BR>	 2. An introduction,<BR>a preface.<BR>	 3. An example, an apposite argument or illustration.<BR>4. Analysis, the ascertainment of the elements of which a thing<BR>consists.<BR> E. उप before हन् to injure, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=132-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपोषण|उपोषणं
उपोषण n. (-णं) A fast, fasting.<BR> E. उप before वस to abide, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=132-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपोषित|उपोषितं|उपोषितः
उपोषित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Fasted, fasting.<BR>	 n. (-तं) Fast, fasting.<BR> E. उप<BR>before वस् to abide, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=132-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उप्त|उप्तः
उप्त mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं) Sown, (as seed.)<BR> E. वप् to sow, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=132-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उप्तकृष्ट|उप्तकृष्टं
उप्तकृष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं) Ploughed after sowing.<BR> E. उप्त and कृष्ट ploughed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=132-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उप्ति|उप्तिः
उप्ति f. (-प्तिः) Sowing seeds.<BR> E. वप् to sow, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=132-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उप्तिविद्
उप्तिविद् m. (-वित् or -विद्) An agriculturist.<BR> E. उप्ति and विद् who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=132-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उप्त्रिम
उप्त्रिम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं) Sown, cultivated.<BR> E. वप् to sow, क्त्रि aff. and मप्<BR>added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=132-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उब्ज
उब्ज r. 6th cl. (उब्जति) To be straight: with नि prefixed, (न्युब्जति) To be<BR>crooked: this root is also written उज्ज and उद्ज.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=132-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उभ
उभ r. 6th cl. (उभति) To fill; also उम्भ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=132-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उभ
उभ pron.<BR>	 m. and dual only, (उभौ) Both.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=132-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उभय|उभयं|उभयः
उभय pron. (sing. and plu. only,) (-यः-ये) Both.<BR> E. उभ and य from या to<BR>obtain, aff. ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=132-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उभयतस्
उभयतस् ind. On both sides.<BR> E. उभय both, and तसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=132-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उभयतोदत्|उभयतोदन्त्
उभयतोदत् mfn. (-दन्-दती-दत्) Having a double row of teeth, (man,<BR>animal, &c.)<BR> E. उभयतस् and दत् for दन्त a tooth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=132-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उभयतोमुख
उभयतोमुख mfn. (-खः-खी-खं) Looking either way, two-faced.<BR> E. उभयतस्<BR>and मुख face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=132-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उभयत्र
उभयत्र ind. In both places, on both sides.<BR> E. उभय and त्रल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=132-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उभयथा
उभयथा ind. In both ways.<BR> E. उभय and थाल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=132-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उभयद्युस्
उभयद्युस् ind. Both days, the day past and to come.<BR> E. उभय both, द्युस्<BR>aff.; or with एद्युस् aff. उभयेद्युस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=132-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उभयभागहर
उभयभागहर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>	 1. Applicable to two purposes.<BR>	 2. Taking<BR>two shares or parts.<BR>	 n. (-रं) A medicine that acts in two ways, as<BR>an emetic and a purge.<BR> E. उभय, भाग a part, and हर what takes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=132-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उभयवेतन
उभयवेतन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Serving two masters, being in the pay of<BR>both.<BR> E. उभय and वेतन wages.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=133-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उभयसम्भव|उभयसंभव|उभयसंभवः
उभयसम्भव m. (-वः) A dilemma.<BR> E. उभय both, (conclusions,) सम्भव<BR>production.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=133-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उभयानुमत
उभयानुमत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Agreed to or accepted mutually, or on both<BR>sides.<BR> E. उभय and अनुमत assented to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=133-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उभयार्थम्
उभयार्थम् ind. For a double object, (as for prosperity in earth and happi-<BR>ness in heaven.)<BR> E. उभय and अर्थ an object.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=133-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उम्
उम् ind. An interjection, 1. Of anger.<BR>	 2. Interrogation.<BR>	 3. Promise or<BR>assent; and 4. Of cordiality or pacification.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=133-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उम|उमः
उम m. (-मः)<BR>	 1. A city, a town.<BR>	 2. A wharf, a landing place.<BR>	 f. (-मा)<BR>	 1.<BR>A name of the goddess PARVATI or DURGĀ.<BR>	 2. Light, splendor.<BR>	 3.<BR>Fame, reputation.<BR>	 4. Turmeric.<BR>	 5. Flax, (Linum usilatissimum.)<BR>6. Quiet, tranquillity.<BR> E. उ particle of calling, and मा prohibition;<BR>i. e. “Practise not austerities,” the exclamation addressed to<BR>DURGĀ by her mother: in the other, senses it may be derived from<BR>मा to measure, or मा lustre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=133-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उमाकट|उमाकटः
उमाकट m. (-टः) The cluster of flax.<BR> E. उमा flax, कच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=133-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उमागुरु|उमागुरुः
उमागुरु m. (-रुः) The mountain Himālaya.<BR> E. उमा the goddess, and गुरु<BR>a spiritual teacher: in mythology the personified mountain is the<BR>father of UMA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=133-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उमापति|उमापतिः
उमापति m. (-तिः) A name of ŚIVA.<BR> E. उमा and पति master; the husband<BR>of UMA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=133-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उमावन|उमावनं
उमावन n. (-नं) A name of Vanapura or Devi Kota, (Devi Cote.)<BR> E. उमा<BR>and वन a grove; the residence of UMA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=133-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उमासुत|उमासुतः
उमासुत m. (-तः) A name KARTIKEYA.<BR> E. उमा and सुत a son, the son<BR>of PARVATI.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=133-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उमेश|उमेशः
उमेश m. (-शः) A title of ŚIVA.<BR> E. उमा and ईश a lord: see उमापति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=133-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उम्भ
उम्भ r. 6th cl. (प) (उम्भति) To fill; also उभ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=133-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उम्य|उम्यं
उम्य n. (-म्यं) A field of linseed, (Linum utilatissimum.)<BR> E. उमा flax, and<BR>यत् affix; also औमीन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=133-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उम्बर|उंबर|उंबरः|उम्बरः
उम्बर m. (-रः) The upper-timber of a door-frame.<BR> E. उद् up, above, वृ to<BR>screen, अप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=133-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उम्बी|उंबी
उम्बी f. (-म्बी) The stalks of wheat or barley fried over a fire of wet grass,<BR>considered as a tonic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=133-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरःक्षत
उरःक्षत n. (-तं) Injury of the lungs, breaking a blood-vessel, consumption.<BR>E. उरस् and क्षत lesion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=133-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरःस्थल
उरःस्थल n. (-लं) The breast, the bosom.<BR> E. उरस् the breast, and स्थल place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=133-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरःसूत्रिका
उरःसूत्रिका f. (-का) A pearl-necklace.<BR> E. उरस् the breast, and सूत्र thread,<BR>टच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=133-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उर|उरः
उर Sautra root. (उरति) to go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=133-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरग|उरगः
उरग m. (-गः) A snake.<BR> E. उरस् the breast, and ग who goes, from गम् to<BR>go, affix ड; also उरङ्ग and उरङ्गम.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=133-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरगस्थान|उरगस्थानं
उरगस्थान n. (-नं) The infernal regions below the earth.<BR> E. उरग and स्थान<BR>a place or country: the abode of the Nagas or serpents.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=133-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरगारि|उरगारिः
उरगारि m. (-रिः)<BR>	 1. GARUḌA the bird of VIṢṆU.<BR>	 2. A large crane. E.<BR>उरग a snake, and अरि the enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=133-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरगाशन|उरगाशनः
उरगाशन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. A name of GARUḌA the bird of VIṢṆU.<BR>	 2. The<BR>gigantic crane.<BR> E. उरग and अशन food; whose food is of serpents.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=133-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरगेन्द्र|उरगेन्द्रः
उरगेन्द्र m. (-न्द्रः) The king of snakes, SESHA or VĀSUKI.<BR> E. उरग and इन्द्र<BR>chief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=133-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरङ्ग|उरंग|उरंगः|उरङ्गः
उरङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः) A snake, a serpent: see उरग, the affix being खच्; also उरङ्गम.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=133-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरण|उरणः
उरण m. (-णः)<BR>	 1. A ram.<BR>	 2. A cloud.<BR>	 f. (-णी) A ewe.<BR> E. ऋ to go, क्यु affix,<BR>leaving ण, and उ substituted for the antepenultimate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=133-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरणाक्ष|उरणाक्षः
उरणाक्ष m. (-क्षः) Cassia, (Alata.)<BR> E. उरण ram, अक्ष an eye: the flower<BR>being so compared: क being added, also उरणाक्षक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=133-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरणाख्य|उरणाख्यः
उरणाख्य m. (-ख्यः) Cassia: see the preceding.<BR> E. उरण and आख्या a name;<BR>named from the ram; also उरणाख्यक, क being added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=133-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरभ्र|उरभ्रः
उरभ्र m. (-भ्रः) A ram.<BR> E. उरु much, भ्रम् to wander, ड affix, and the final<BR>of उरु dropped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=133-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उररी
उररी ind. A particle implying, 1. Assent.<BR>	 2. Expansion: (it chiefly<BR>occurs in composition.)<BR> E. वे to weave, ररीक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=133-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उररीकार|उररीकारः
उररीकार m. (-रः) A promise, an agreement.<BR> E. उररी, कार what makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=133-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उररीकृत|उररीकृतः
उररीकृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Promised, agreed.<BR>	 2. Spread, diffused. E.<BR>उररी and कृत made.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=133-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरश्छद|उरश्छदः
उरश्छद m. (-दः) Armour, mail.<BR> E. उरस् the breast, and छद a covering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=133-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरस्
उरस् mfn. (-राः-राः-रः) Best, excellent.<BR>	 n. (-रः) The breast, the<BR>bosom.<BR> E. ऋ to go, Unādi affix असुन्, the pen. changed to उ; also<BR>उर a Soutra root, to go, and असुन् as before.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=133-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरसिज|उरसिजः
उरसिज m. (-जः) The female breast.<BR> E. उरस् the breast, in the 7th case,<BR>ज produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=133-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरसिरुह|उरसिरुहः
उरसिरुह m. (-हः) The female breast.<BR> E. उरसि on the breast, and रुह<BR>what grows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=133-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरसिल|उरसिलः
उरसिल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Broad-chested, having a full or broad breast.<BR>E. उरस् and इलच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=133-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरस्कट|उरस्कटः
उरस्कट m. (-टः) The sacrificial thread hung round the neck and upon the<BR>breast, as it is sometimes worn.<BR> E. उरस् the breast, कट् to encom-<BR>pass, अल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=133-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरस्तस्
उरस्तस् ind. From the breast.<BR> E. उरस् and तसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=133-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरस्त्राण|उरस्त्राणं
उरस्त्राण n. (-णं) Mail, the breastplate or cuirass.<BR> E. उरस्, त्रै to pre-<BR>serve, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=133-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरस्य|उरस्यः
उरस्य mfn. (-स्यः-स्या-स्यं) From the breast.<BR>	 mf. (-स्यः-स्या) A legitimate son<BR>or daughter, that is, one born from a married couple of the same<BR>tribe or cast.<BR> E. उरस् the breast, and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=133-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरस्वत्|उरस्वन्त्
उरस्वत् mfn. (-स्वान्-स्वती-स्वत्) Broad-chested, full-breasted, strong. E.<BR>उरस् and मतुप् poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=133-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उराह|उराहः
उराह m. (-हः) A horse of a pale colour, with dark legs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=133-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरी
उरी ind. A particle, implying, (especially in composition.)<BR>	 1. Promise,<BR>assent.<BR>	 2. Expansion; also उररी and ऊरी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=133-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरीकार
उरीकार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Promise.<BR>	 2. Extension.<BR> E. उरी, and कार what makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=133-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरीकृत|उरीकृतः
उरीकृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Promised.<BR>	 2. Expanded, spread.<BR> E. उरी and<BR>कृत made; also उररीकृत and ऊरीकृत.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=133-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरु|उरुः
उरु mfn. (-रुः-रुः-र्व्वी-रु)<BR>	 1. Large, great.<BR>	 2. Much, excessive.<BR>	 3. Long.<BR>4. Valuable, precious.<BR> E. ऊर्णु to cover, कु Unādi affix; ऊ is made<BR>short, and ण dropped by special rule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=133-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरुकाल|उरुकालः
उरुकाल m. (-लः) A creeper, (Cucumis colocynthis.)<BR> E. उरु and काल time,<BR>of long growth; also with कन् added उरुकालकः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=133-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरुगाय|उरुगायः
उरुगाय m. (-यः) A name of KṚṢṆA.<BR> E. उरग a snake, इ to go, and<BR>अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=133-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरुतर
उरुतर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Greater, larger.<BR> E. उरु and तरप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=133-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरुतम
उरुतम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं) Greatest.<BR> E. उरु and तमप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=133-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरुताप|उरुतापः
उरुताप m. (-पः) Great heat.<BR> E. उरु much, ताप heat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=133-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरुत्व|उरुत्वं
उरुत्व n. (-त्वं) Magnitude, vastness.<BR> E. उरु and त्व affix; also उरुता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=133-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरुमार्ग|उरुमार्गः
उरुमार्ग m. (-र्गः) A long road.<BR> E. उरु and मार्ग a road.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=133-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरुरी
उरुरी ind. A particle, of 1. Assent.<BR>	 2. Expansion: see उररी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=133-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरुवुक|उरुवुकः
उरुवुक m. (-कः) The castor-oil tree, (Palma christi or Ricinus commu-<BR>nis.)<BR> E. उरु great or much, (disease,) वै to wither or dry, affix उक<BR>deriv. irr. or with ऊक affix उरुवूक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=133-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरुवूक|उरुवूकः
उरुवूक m. (-कः) See the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=133-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरुव्यचस्
उरुव्यचस् m. (-चाः) A malignant sprite, an imp or goblin.<BR> E. उरु much,<BR>व्यच् to deceive, असुन् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=133-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरुसत्त्व
उरुसत्त्व mfn. (-त्त्वः-त्त्वा-त्त्वं) Magnanimous, of a lofty nature.<BR> E. उरु and<BR>सत्त्व disposition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=133-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरुहार|उरुहारः
उरुहार m. (-रः) A valuable necklace.<BR> E. उरु and हार a necklace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=133-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरोगामिन्
उरोगामिन् mfn. (-मी-मिनी-मि)<BR>	 1. Creeping, crawling, going on the belly<BR>as a reptile.<BR> E. उरस् and गामिन् who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=133-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरोग्रह|उरोग्रहः
उरोग्रह m. (-हः) Pain of the chest, pleurisy.<BR> E. उरस् and ग्रह what seizes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=133-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरोघात|उरोघातः
उरोघात m. (-तः)<BR>	 1. Striking or beating the breast.<BR>	 2. Pain in the chest.<BR>E. उरस् and घात a wound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=133-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरोज|उरोजः
उरोज m. (-जः) The female breast.<BR> E. उरस् the breast, and ज produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=133-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उर्ज्जित|उर्जित|उर्ज्जितं
उर्ज्जित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Abandoned, left.<BR> E. वर्ज्ज to abandon, क्त affix, and<BR>the vowel substituted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=134-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उर्णनाभ|उर्णनाभः|उर्ण्णनाभ
उर्णनाभ m. (-भः) A spider.<BR> E. उर्ण wool, नाभि a navel, affix ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=134-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उर्णा
उर्णा f. (-र्णा)<BR>	 1. Wool, felt, the hair of camels, &c.<BR>	 2. A circle of hair<BR>between the eyebrows.<BR> E. उर्णु to cover, ड affix; the word is proper-<BR>ly ऊर्णा, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=134-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उर्द|उर्द्द
उर्द r. 1st cl. (उर्दते)<BR>	 1. To measure.<BR>	 2. To play.<BR>	 3. To be easy or cheerful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=134-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उर्द्र|उर्द्रः
उर्द्र m. (-र्द्रः) An otter.<BR> E. उर्द् to play, रन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=134-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उर्व्व|उर्व
उर्व्व r. 1st cl. (ई,) उर्वी (उर्वति) To kill or hurt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=134-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उर्व्वट|उर्वट|उर्वटः|उर्व्वटः
उर्व्वट m. (-टः) A year.<BR> E. उरु much, and अट् to go, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=134-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उर्व्वरा|उर्वरा
उर्व्वरा f. (-रा)<BR>	 1. Fertile soil, yielding every kind of crop.<BR>	 2. Land in<BR>general.<BR> E. उरु much, ऋ to go, अप् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=134-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उर्व्वशी|उर्वशी
उर्व्वशी f. (-शी) The name of one of the courtezans of Svarga or<BR>INDRA'S heaven.<BR> E. उरु great, वश् to tame, अच् and ङीष् affixes;<BR>also उर्व्वसी and ऊर्व्वसी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=134-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उर्व्वशीरमण|उर्वशीरमण|उर्वशीरमणः|उर्व्वशीरमणः
उर्व्वशीरमण m. (-णः) The name of AILA or PURURAVA, the second king<BR>of the line of the moon.<BR> E. उर्व्वशी, and रमण the gallant or husband<BR>of the Apsara URVASI.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=134-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उर्व्वशीवल्लभ|उर्वशीवल्लभ|उर्वशीवल्लभः|उर्व्वशीवल्लभः
उर्व्वशीवल्लभ m. (-भः) A name of AILA: see the preceding. E. As before,<BR>वल्लभ a friend, a lover, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=134-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उर्व्वारु|उर्वारु|उर्वारुः|उर्व्वारुः
उर्व्वारु m. (-रुः) A kind of cucumber, (Cucumis utilatissimus.) See इर्व्वारु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=134-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उर्व्वी|उर्वी
उर्व्वी f. (-र्व्वी) The earth.<BR> E. उरु great, ङीष् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=134-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उर्व्वीधर|उर्वीधर|उर्वीधरः
उर्व्वीधर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A mountain.<BR>	 2. The serpent SESHA.<BR> E. उर्व्वी the<BR>earth, and धर what holds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=134-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उर्व्वीरुह|उर्वीरुह|उर्वीरुहः
उर्व्वीरुह m. (-हः) A tree.<BR> E. उर्व्वी and रुह what grows on.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=134-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल|उलः
उल Sautra root, (उलति) to burn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=134-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उलप|उलपः
उलप mn. (-पः-पं)<BR>	 1. A creeping plant, a spreading creeper.<BR>	 m. (-पः) A<BR>kind of grass or reed, (Saccharum cylindricum.)<BR> E. बल् to be strong,<BR>अपच् affix; also उलुप.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=134-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उलिन्द|उलिंदः|उलिन्दः
उलिन्द m. (-न्दः) The name of a country.<BR> E. उल् to burn, किन्दच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=134-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उलुप|उलुपः
उलुप mn. (-पः-पं) A spreading creeper.<BR>	 m. (-पः) A reed, (Saccharum<BR>cylindricum.)<BR> E. बल् to be strong, उपच् affix; also उलप and उलूप.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=134-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उलुपिन्
उलुपिन् m. (-पी) A porpoise, or fish resembling it.<BR> E. उ for उत् up, लुप्<BR>to disturb, &c. णिनि affix; also उलूपिन्, ऊलुपिन्, उल्लुपिन्, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=134-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उलूक|उलूकं|उलूकः
उलूक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. An owl.<BR>	 2. A name of INDRA.<BR>	 3. One of the heroes<BR>of the Mahabharata.<BR>	 n. (-कं) A kind of reed, (Saccharum cylindri-<BR>cum.)<BR> E. बल् to be strong, ऊक aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=134-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उलूखल|उलूखलं|उलूखलः
उलूखल n. (-लं)<BR>	 1. A wooden mortar used for cleaning rice.<BR>	 2. Bdel-<BR>lium, a gummy substance.<BR> E. उद् up, ख empty, and ल what takes:<BR>or उदू for उद्, and खल what goes; द is changed to लः see उदूखल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=134-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उलूखलक|उलूखलकं
उलूखलक m. (-कः) A name of Bdellium, a gummy substance, or the<BR>plant which produces it.<BR> E. कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=134-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उलूखलिक
उलूखलिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Pounded in a mortar, cleansed.<BR> E. उलूखल<BR>and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=134-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उलूत|उलूतः
उलूत m. (-तः) A large snake, the Boa.<BR> E. उद् much, लू to cut, and क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=134-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उलूप
उलूप m. (-पः) A spreading creeper.<BR>	 n. (-पं) A sort of grass.<BR>	 f. (-पी) A<BR>nymph of Pātāla married to ARJUNA. E. See उलुप.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=134-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उलूपिन्
उलूपिन् m. (-पी) A porpoise, or fish resembling it: see उलुपिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=134-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्का
उल्का f. (-ल्का)<BR>	 1. A fire-brand.<BR>	 2. Fire falling from heaven, a meteor,<BR>&c.<BR>	 3. Flame.<BR>	 4. Fire.<BR> E. उष् to burn, कक् Unādi affix, ल substi-<BR>tuted for ष; or the root is a Sautra root, उल to burn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=134-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्कामुख|उल्कामुखः
उल्कामुख m. (-खः) A ghost or goblin, with a face of fire, who eats what<BR>is vomited, and who was a negligent Brahman in his life-time.<BR>	 f.<BR>(-खी) A fox.<BR> E. उल्का a flame, मुख a mouth, ङीष् affix; the latter<BR>from the redness of his mouth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=134-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्मुक|उल्मुकं|उल्मुकः
उल्मुक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A fire-brand, wood burning or burnt as charcoal.<BR>	 2.<BR>The name of a prince.<BR> E. उष् to burn, मुक Unādi affix, ष is chang-<BR>ed to ल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=134-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्लकसन|उल्लकसनं
उल्लकसन n. (-नं) Horripilation, erection of the hair of the body.<BR> E. उद्<BR>up, लष् to injure, ल्युट् affix, and क inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=134-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्लग्न
उल्लग्न m. (-ग्नः) The Lagna of any particular place.<BR> E. उत् over, लग्न the<BR>entrance of the sun into a sign.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=134-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्लङ्घन|उल्लंघन|उल्लंघनं|उल्लङ्घनं
उल्लङ्घन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Leaping or passing over or beyond.<BR>	 2. Exceeding,<BR>transgression.<BR> E. उद् before लघि to go, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=134-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्लङ्घित|उल्लंघित
उल्लङ्घित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Passed over or beyond, jumped across.<BR>	 2.<BR>Exceeded, transgressed.<BR> E. उद् before लघि to go, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=134-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्लङ्घ्य|उल्लंघ्य
उल्लङ्घ्य mfn. (-ङ्घ्यः-ङ्घ्या-ङ्घ्यं)<BR>	 1. To be crossed, to be passed over or<BR>beyond.<BR>	 2. To be disregarded or neglected.<BR> E. उद् before लघि to go,<BR>and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=134-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्लङ्घितशासन|उल्लंघितशासन
उल्लङ्घितशासन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Refractory, rebellious, disobedient.<BR> E. उल्लङ्घित<BR>and शासन order.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=134-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्लल|उल्ललः
उल्लल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Shaking, trembling.<BR> E. उद् much, लल् to tremble, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=134-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्ललत्
उल्ललत् mfn. (-लन्-लन्ती-लत्) Shaking, trembling.<BR>	 2. Moving irregularly<BR>or convulsively.<BR> E. उद् before लल् to tremble, affix शतृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=134-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्ललित|उल्ललितः
उल्ललित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Shaken, trembling, agitated.<BR> E. उद् much, लल् to<BR>tremble, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=134-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्लस
उल्लस mfn. (-सः-सा-सं)<BR>	 1. Bright, shining.<BR>	 2. Sporting, merry, happy.<BR>	 3.<BR>Going out, issuing.<BR> E. उद् before लस् to shine, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=134-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्लसत्
उल्लसत् mfn. (-सन्-सन्ती-सत्)<BR>	 1. Brilliant, shining.<BR>	 2. Sporting, wanton-<BR>ing.<BR> E. उद् before लस् to shine, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=134-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्लसता
उल्लसता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Splendor, brilliancy.<BR>	 2. Mirth, happiness.<BR>	 3. Going<BR>forth, issuing.<BR> E. उल्लस what shines, तल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=134-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्लसित
उल्लसित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Bright, splendid, shining.<BR>	 2. Happy.<BR>	 3. Eject-<BR>ed, brought to the top or surface.<BR>	 4. Drawn up.<BR> E. उद् before लस्<BR>to shine, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=134-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्लाघ|उल्लाघः
उल्लाघ mfn. (-घः-घा-घं)<BR>	 1. Recovered from sickness, convalescent.<BR>	 2. Dex-<BR>trous, clever, intelligent.<BR>	 3. Pure.<BR>	 4. Happy, delighted.<BR> E. उद्<BR>much, लाघ to be able, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=134-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्लाप|उल्लापः
उल्लाप m. (-पः) Change of voice in grief, sickness, &c.<BR> E. उद् implying<BR>alteration, लप् to speak, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=134-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्लास|उल्लासः
उल्लास m. (-सः)<BR>	 1. Joy, happiness.<BR>	 2. Light, splendor.<BR>	 3. Increase.<BR>	 4. The<BR>division of a book, a chapter, a section.<BR> E. उद् much, लस् to shine,<BR>&c. घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=134-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्लासित
उल्लासित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Delighted, rejoicing.<BR> E. उद् before लस् to shine,<BR>causal form, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=134-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्लिखत्
उल्लिखत् mfn. (-खन्-खन्ती-खत्)<BR>	 1. Painting, writing.<BR>	 2. Making lines or<BR>streaks, above or on high.<BR>	 3. Scratching, scraping.<BR>	 4. Bearing,<BR>raising.<BR> E. उद् before लिख् to write, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=134-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्लिखित|उल्लिखितः
उल्लिखित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Thrown up, tossed.<BR>	 2. Pared, made thin.<BR>3. Scraped, scratched.<BR>	 4. Painted, delineated.<BR>	 5. Written over or<BR>above.<BR> E. उद् and लिखित written.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=134-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्लिङ्गित|उल्लिंगित
उल्लिङ्गित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Discriminated, distinguished, known.<BR> E. उद्<BR>before लिगि to mark, and क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=134-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्लुञ्चन|उल्लुंचन|उल्लुंचनं
उल्लुञ्चन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Plucking out hair.<BR>	 2. Cutting the hair.<BR> E. उद् up,<BR>लुचि to cut, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=134-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्लेख|उल्लेखः
उल्लेख m. (-खः)<BR>	 1. Utterance, pronunciation.<BR>	 2. Speaking.<BR> E. उद् before<BR>लिख् to write, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=134-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्लेखन|उल्लेखनं
उल्लेखन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Raising up, elevating.<BR>	 2. Vomiting.<BR>	 3. Digging.<BR>4. Scraping, paring.<BR>	 5. Uttering, utterance.<BR>	 6. Writing, painting.<BR>E. उद् before लिखि to write, &c. ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=134-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्लोच|उल्लोचः
उल्लोच m. (-चः) An awning, a canopy.<BR> E. उद् above, लोच् to see, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=134-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्लोल|उल्लोलः
उल्लोल m. (-लः) A surge, a large wave or billow.<BR> E. उद् up, लोड् to be<BR>furious, अच् affix, and ड becomes ल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=134-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्व|उल्वं
उल्व n. (-ल्वं)<BR>	 1. The womb.<BR>	 2. The embryo.<BR>	 3. The membranes investing<BR>the fœtus.<BR>	 4. A cavity.<BR> E. उच् to accumulate, कन् Unādi affix, and<BR>च becomes ल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=134-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्वण|उल्वणं
उल्वण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>	 1. Apparent, evident.<BR>	 2. Much, exceeding.<BR>	 n. (-णं)<BR>An excess of either of the humors of the body, bile, phlegm or<BR>wind.<BR> E. उद् up, ल्वी to join, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=134-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उब्ज
उब्ज r. 6th cl. (उब्जति) To be straight: see ऊब्ज.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=134-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उशत्|उशन्त्
उशत् mfn. (-शन्-शती-शत्) Inauspicious, (as discourse.)<BR> E. उष् to burn,<BR>शतृ part. affix; also उषत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=135-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उशनस्
उशनस् m. (-नाः) A name of SUKRA, regent of the planet Venus.<BR> E. वस्<BR>to wish, कनसि Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=135-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उशिज्
उशिज् m. (-शिक्)<BR>	 1. Fire.<BR>	 2. Ghee or boiled butter.<BR> E. वश् to wish, Unādi<BR>affix इज्, and व changed to उ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=135-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उशी
उशी f. (-शी) Wish, desire.<BR> E. वश् to wish, ई Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=135-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उशीनर|उशीनरः
उशीनर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. The name of a country, (Candahar.)<BR>	 2. A king, the<BR>father of SIVI.<BR> E. उशी desire, नर a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=135-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उशीर|उशीरं|उशीरः
उशीर mn. (-रः-रं) The root of a fragrant grass, (Androdogon muricatum.)<BR>f. (-री) A sort of grass, a small sort of Saccharum.<BR> E. वश् ta desire,<BR>ईरन् Unādi affix; also with कन् added उशीरक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=135-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उष|उषं|उषः
उष r. 1st cl. (ओषति) To burn. (उ,) उषु (ओषति) To kill or injure: with प्र<BR>prefixed, this root makes प्रोषति, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=135-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उष|उषं|उषः
उष m. (-षः)<BR>	 1. Early morning, dawn, day-break.<BR>	 2. A libidinous man.<BR>3. Bdellium.<BR>	 4. Saline earth.<BR>	 f. (-षा)<BR>	 1. A cow.<BR>	 2. Burning, scorch-<BR>ing.<BR>	 3. A proper name, the wife of ANIRUDDHA.<BR>	 4. Night.<BR>	 5. A<BR>pot; also उखा. ind. The end of night or day-break.<BR> E. उष् to burn,<BR>क affix and fem. do टाप्; the affix of the particle is का.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=135-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उषण|उषणं
उषण n. (-णं) Black pepper.<BR>	 f. (-णा)<BR>	 1. Long pepper.<BR>	 2. Chai, (Piper<BR>Chaba.)<BR>	 3. Dried ginger.<BR> E. उष् to burn, कनच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=135-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उषत्|उषन्त्
उषत् mfn. (-षन्-षती-षत्) Inauspicious, (as discourse:) see उशत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=135-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उषप|उषपः
उषप m. (-पः)<BR>	 1. The sun.<BR>	 2. Fire.<BR> E. उष् to burn, पच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=135-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उषर्बुध|उषर्बुधः
उषर्बुध m. (-धः) Fire.<BR> E. उषस् dawn, बुध् to know, क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=135-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उषस्
उषस् n. (-षः)<BR>	 1. The dawn, morning.<BR>	 f. (-सी) The end of the day, twi-<BR>light.<BR> E. उष् to burn, असि Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=135-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उषस्य
उषस्य mfn. (-स्यः-स्या-स्यं) Belonging to the dawn.<BR> E. उषस् and य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=135-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उषाकल|उषाकलः
उषाकल m. (-लः) A cock.<BR> E. उषा dawn, कल् to sound, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=135-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उषापति|उषापतिः
उषापति m. (-तिः) A name of ANIRUDDHA, the son of KĀMADEVA. E.<BR>उषा and पति a lord, a master: the husband of USHA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=135-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उषारमण|उषारमणः
उषारमण m. (-णः) ANIRUDDHA: see the preceding.<BR> E. उषा and रमण a<BR>husband, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=135-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उषित|उषितः
उषित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Stale.<BR>	 2. Burnt.<BR>	 3. Quick, expeditious.<BR>	 4. Fixed,<BR>remaining in or on.<BR>	 5. Inhabited, dwelt.<BR> E. उष् to burn, or वस् to<BR>abide, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=135-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उषितङ्गवीन|उषितंगवीन|उषितङ्गवीनः
उषितङ्गवीन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Formerly inhabited by cattle.<BR> E. उषित inhabit-<BR>ed, गवीन appertaining to cattle, form गो with खश् affix: see<BR>अशितङ्गवीन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=135-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उषित्वा
उषित्वा ind. Having resided in.<BR> E. वस् to abide, क्त्वा aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=135-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उषीर|उषीरं|उषीरः
उषीर mn. (-रः-रं) The root of the Andropogon muricatum.<BR> E. वश् to<BR>desire, ईरन् affix, श becomes षः see उशीर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=135-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उषेश|उषेशः
उषेश m. (-शः) A name ANIRUDDHA.<BR> E. उषा and ईश lord, husband: see उषापति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=135-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उष्य
उष्य mfn. (-ष्यः-ष्या-ष्यं) Fit to be dressed in a pot, or boiled, (meat, &c.)<BR>E. उषा a pot, यत् affix; also उख्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=135-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उष्ट्र|उष्ट्रः
उष्ट्र m. (-ष्ट्रः)<BR>	 1. A camel.<BR>	 2. A cart, a vehicle of burthen.<BR>	 f. (-ष्ट्री or<BR>-ष्ट्रिका) An earthen vessel.<BR>	 2. A she camel.<BR> E. उष् to burn, and ष्ट्रन्<BR>Unādi affix, fem. affix ङीष् or टाप् with इक् inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=135-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उष्ट्रकाण्डी
उष्ट्रकाण्डी f. (-ण्डी) A flower of a red colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=135-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उष्ट्रक्रोशिन्
उष्ट्रक्रोशिन् mfn. (-शी-शिनी-शि) Making a noise like a camel.<BR> E. उष्ट्र and क्रुश्<BR>to cry, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=135-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उष्ट्रगोयुग
उष्ट्रगोयुग n. (-गं) A pair of camel.<BR> E. उष्ट्र and गोयुग a couple.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=135-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उष्ट्रग्रीव|उष्ट्रग्रीवः
उष्ट्रग्रीव m. (-वः) Hemorrhoids.<BR> E. उष्ट्र and ग्रीवा the neck.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=135-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उष्ट्रधूसरपुच्छिका
उष्ट्रधूसरपुच्छिका f. (-का) A tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=135-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उष्ट्रपादिका
उष्ट्रपादिका f. (-का) Arabian jasmine.<BR> E. उष्ट्र and पाद a foot: from the<BR>shape of its flowers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=135-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उष्ट्रयान
उष्ट्रयान n. (-नं) A camel litter, a vehicle drawn or borne by camels. E.<BR>उष्ट्र and यान a carriage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=135-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उष्ट्रशिरोधर|उष्ट्रशिरोधरं|उष्ट्रशिरोधरः
उष्ट्रशिरोधर m. (-रः) Piles, hemorrhoids, bleeding piles.<BR> E. उष्ट्र a camel,<BR>शिरस् head, and धर what has.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=135-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उष्ण|उष्णः
उष्ण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>	 1. Hot, warm.<BR>	 2. Pungent, acrid.<BR>	 3. Sharp, active.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=135-b" target="_blank">Page135-b+ 56</a>]<BR>4. Impetuous, warm, passionate.<BR>	 m. (-ष्णः)<BR>	 1. The hot season, (June<BR>and July.)<BR>	 2. Heat, warmth.<BR>	 3. Sunshine.<BR>	 4. An onion.<BR>	 5. A sigh.<BR>f. (-णा)<BR>	 1. Consumption.<BR>	 2. Bile.<BR> E. उष् to burn, णक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=135-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उष्णक|उष्णकः
उष्णक mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>	 1. Sharp, smart, active.<BR>	 2. Suffering pain.<BR>2. Bent, inclining, stooping.<BR>	 4. Warming, heating.<BR>	 m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. The<BR>hot season, two months about June and July.<BR>	 2. Revolving, turn-<BR>ing round.<BR> E. वुन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=135-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उष्णता
उष्णता f. (-ता) Heat, warmth.<BR> E. तल् added to उष्ण; also with त्व, उष्णत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=135-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उष्णनदी
उष्णनदी f. (-दी) The river of hell.<BR> E. उष्ण hot, नदी a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=135-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उष्णरश्मि|उष्णरश्मिः
उष्णरश्मि m. (-श्मिः) The sun.<BR> E. उण and रश्मि a ray.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=135-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उष्णवारण|उष्णवारणः
उष्णवारण mn. (-णः-णं) An umbrella or parasol, a Chattah.<BR> E. उष्ण heat,<BR>and वृ to screen, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=135-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उष्णवाष्प
उष्णवाष्प m. (-ष्पः)<BR>	 1. Hot vapour, steam.<BR>	 2. Tears.<BR> E. उष्ण and वाष्प vapour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=135-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उष्णवीर्य्य|उष्णवीर्य|उष्णवीर्यः|उष्णवीर्य्यः
उष्णवीर्य्य m. (-र्य्यः)<BR>	 1. The gangetic porpoise.<BR>	 2. Any hot or pungent sub-<BR>stance.<BR> E. उष्ण heat, वीर्य्य power, strength.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=135-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उष्णांशु|उष्णांशुः
उष्णांशु m. (-शुः) The sun.<BR> E. उष्ण and अंशु a ray.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=135-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उष्णागम|उष्णागमः
उष्णागम m. (-मः) The hot season, consisting of two months, about June<BR>and July.<BR> E. उष्ण heat, and आगम arrival.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=135-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उष्णाभिगम|उष्णाभिगमः
उष्णाभिगम m. (-मः) The hot season, as above.<BR> E. उष्ण and अभिगम approach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=135-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उष्णालु
उष्णालु mfn. (-लुः-लुः-लु) Suffering from heat.<BR> E. उष्ण and आलु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=135-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उष्णासह|उष्णासहः
उष्णासह m. (-हः) The cold season.<BR> E. उष्ण warmth, असह intolerant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=135-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उष्णिका
उष्णिका f. (-का) Rice gruel.<BR> E. उष्ण warm (rice,) वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=135-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उष्णिह्
उष्णिह् f. (-ष्णिक्) A verse of four lines, each line being of seven syllables:<BR>it is used chiefly in the Vedas.<BR> E. उत् prefixed to ष्णिह् to be unctu-<BR>ous or bland, क्विन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=135-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उष्णीष|उष्णीषं|उष्णीषः
उष्णीष mn. (-षः-षं)<BR>	 1. A turban.<BR>	 2. A diadem.<BR>	 3. A distinguishing cog-<BR>nate mark.<BR>	 4. The curly hair with which a Buddha is born, and<BR>which indicates his future sanctity.<BR> E. उष्ण heat, ईष् to oppose or<BR>injure, क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=135-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उष्णीषधारिन्
उष्णीषधारिन् mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि) Turbaned.<BR> E. उष्णीष and धारिन् who wears.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=135-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उष्णोदक|उष्णोदकं
उष्णोदक n. (-कं) Warm or hot water.<BR> E. उष्ण and उदक water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=135-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उष्णोपगम|उष्णोपगमः
उष्णोपगम m. (-मः) The hot season, summer.<BR> E. उष्ण, उपगम arrival.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=135-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उष्म|उष्मं|उष्मः
उष्म m. (-ष्मः)<BR>	 1. The hot season, (June and July.)<BR>	 2. Spring, (April and<BR>May.)<BR>	 3. Heat.<BR>	 4. Anger, warmth of temper.<BR>	 5. Ardor, eagerness.<BR>E. उष् to burn, मक् affix; also with कन् affix उष्मक, also उष्ण and<BR>उष्णक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=135-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उष्मन्
उष्मन् m. (-ष्मा)<BR>	 1. The hot season.<BR>	 2. Heat.<BR> E. उष् to burn, and मनिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=135-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उष्मपा
उष्मपा m. (-पाः) A heavenly spirit of an inferior order.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=135-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उष्मभास्
उष्मभास् m. (-भाः) The sun.<BR> E. उष्म and भास् what shines.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=135-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उष्मस्वेद|उष्मस्वेदः
उष्मस्वेद m. (-दः) A vapour bath.<BR> E. उष्म and स्वेद sweat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=135-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उष्मागम|उष्मागमः
उष्मागम m. (-मः) The hot season: see उष्णागम.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=135-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उस्र|उस्रः
उस्र m. (-स्रः)<BR>	 1. A bull.<BR>	 2. A ray of light.<BR>	 f. (-स्रा)<BR>	 1. A cow.<BR>	 2. A plant,<BR>(Anthericum tuberosum, Rox.)<BR> E. वस् to dwell, रक् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=135-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उस्रधन्वन्
उस्रधन्वन् m. (-न्वा) INDRA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=135-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उह
उह r. 1st cl. (इर्) उहिर् (ओहति) or (इ) उहि (उंहति) 1. To hurt or give<BR>pain.<BR>	 2. To kill, to destroy. With वि and अप, pre. to destroy, to<BR>remove.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=135-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उहान|उहानः
उहान m. (-नः) The name of a country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=135-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊ
ऊ The sixth vowel of the Sanskrit alphabet, corresponding to U long,<BR>and having the sound of that letter in the word rule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=135-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊ
ऊ ind.<BR>	 1. An incipient particle.<BR>	 2. An interjection of compassion.<BR>	 3. Of<BR>regard.<BR>	 m. (ऊः) The moon.<BR> E. अव् to go, क्विप् affix, व becomes ऊ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=135-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊढ|ऊढः
ऊढ mfn. (-ढः-ढा-ढं)<BR>	 1. Married.<BR>	 2. Carried as load or burthen.<BR>	 f. (-ढा) A<BR>bride, a wife espoused according to the ritual.<BR> E. वह् to bear, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=135-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊढकङ्कट|ऊढकंकट|ऊढकङ्कटः
ऊढकङ्कट mfn. (-टः-टा-टं) Armed, mailed.<BR> E. ऊढ borne, कङ्गट armour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=135-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊत|ऊतं
ऊत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Woven.<BR> E. वेञ् to weave, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=136-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊति|ऊतिः
ऊति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Preserving, protecting.<BR>	 2. Sewing, weaving.<BR>	 3. Distil-<BR>ling.<BR>	 4. Speed.<BR>	 5. Sport, play.<BR> E. वेञ् to weave, &c. affix क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=136-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊधन्य|ऊधन्यं
ऊधन्य mfn. (-न्यः-न्या-न्यं) Produced from the udder, milk, &c.<BR> E. ऊधस्, यत्<BR>affix, and न substituted for स.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=136-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊधस्
ऊधस् n. (-धः) An udder.<BR> E. वह् to bear, असि affix, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=136-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊधस्य|ऊधस्यं
ऊधस्य n. (-स्यं) Milk.<BR> E. ऊधस् and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=136-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊन|ऊनं
ऊन r. 10th cl. (न) ऊनत् (ऊनयति) 1. To deduct or lessen.<BR>	 2. To mete out<BR>in small quantities.<BR>	 3. To measure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=136-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊन|ऊनं
ऊन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Less in number, size or degree, as fewer, smaller,<BR>inferior, &c.<BR> E. ऊन to deduct, &c. affix क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=136-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊम्
ऊम् ind. An interjection of, 1. Interrogation.<BR>	 2. Anger.<BR>	 3. Reproach,<BR>abuse.<BR>	 4. Arrogance.<BR>	 n. (-मं) A city.<BR> E. अव् to preserve, &c. मन्<BR>Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=136-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊय
ऊय r. 1st cl. (ई) ऊयी (ऊयते) To sew, to weave.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=136-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊररी
ऊररी ind.<BR>	 1. A particle of assent.<BR>	 2. Of expansion.<BR> E. ऊय् to sew, &c.<BR>ररीक् affix: see उररी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=136-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊरव्य|ऊरव्यः
ऊरव्य m. (-व्यः) A man of the third caste or tribe, the merchant or hus-<BR>bandman, the Vaiśya.<BR> E. ऊरु a thigh, and यत् affix; being born<BR>from the thighs of BRAHMĀ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=136-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊरी
ऊरी ind. A particle of, 1. Assent.<BR>	 2. Of expansion: see उरी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=136-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊरीकृत|ऊरीकृतः
ऊरीकृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Promised.<BR>	 2. Expanded.<BR> E. ऊरी and कृत made:<BR>see उरीकृत.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=136-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊरु|ऊरुः
ऊरु m. (-रुः) The thigh.<BR> E. ऊर्णु to cover, कु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=136-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊरुग्लानि|ऊरुग्लानिः
ऊरुग्लानि f. (-निः) Weakness of the thigh.<BR> E. ऊरु and ग्लानि debility.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=136-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊरुज|ऊरुजः
ऊरुज m. (-जः) A Vaiśya or man of the third tribe.<BR> E. ऊरु and ज born;<BR>from the thigh of BRAHMĀ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=136-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊरुदघ्न
ऊरुदघ्न mfn. (-घ्नः-घ्ना-घ्नं) As high as the thigh.<BR> E. ऊरु and दघ्नच् affix; also<BR>ऊरुद्वयस and ऊरुमात्र, with द्वयसच् and मात्रच् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=136-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊरुपर्व्वन्|ऊरुपर्वन्
ऊरुपर्व्वन् n. (-र्व्व) The knee.<BR> E. ऊरु and पर्व्वन् a joint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=136-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊरुरी
ऊरुरी ind. A particle of, 1. Promise.<BR>	 2. Of expansion: see ऊररी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=136-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊरुस्तम्भ|ऊरुस्तम्भः
ऊरुस्तम्भ m. (-म्भः)<BR>	 1. Paralysis of the lower extremities.<BR>	 2. Rheumatism<BR>of the thigh.<BR>	 f. (-म्भा) The plantain tree.<BR> E. ऊरु and स्तम्भ a post.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=136-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्ज्
ऊर्ज् f. (-ऊर्क्) Strength, vigour.<BR> E. ऊर्ज् to be strong, क्विप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=136-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्ज|ऊर्जः|ऊर्ज्ज|ऊर्ज्जं|ऊर्ज्जः
ऊर्ज r. 10th cl. (ऊर्जयति)<BR>	 1. To be strong.<BR>	 2. To live.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=136-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्ज|ऊर्जः|ऊर्ज्ज|ऊर्ज्जं|ऊर्ज्जः
ऊर्ज m. (-र्जः)<BR>	 1. The month Kartik, (Oct.-Nov.)<BR>	 2. Effort, exertion.<BR>	 3.<BR>Power, strength.<BR>	 4. Breath, breathing.<BR>	 5. Procreative power.<BR>	 n.<BR>(-र्जं) Water.<BR> E. ऊर्ज to live, क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=136-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्जस्वत्|ऊर्जस्वन्त्|ऊर्ज्जस्वत्
ऊर्जस्वत् mfn. (-स्वान्-स्वती-स्वत्) Strong, vigorous.<BR> E. ऊर्ज and मतुप् affix,<BR>with स inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=136-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्जस्वल|ऊर्ज्जस्वलः
ऊर्जस्वल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Strong, powerful.<BR> E. ऊर्ज strength, वलच् affix,<BR>and स inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=136-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्जस्विन्
ऊर्जस्विन् mfn. (-स्वी-स्विनी-स्वि) Very strong.<BR>	 n. (-स्वि) Speaking of any<BR>thing with disdain, (a figure of rhetoric.)<BR> E. ऊर्ज and विनि affix, स<BR>inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=136-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्जित|ऊर्ज्जित
ऊर्जित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Powerful, mighty, great, excellent.<BR>	 2. Exceed-<BR>ing, much.<BR> E. ऊर्ज to be strong, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=136-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्जिताश्रय|ऊर्ज्जिताश्रय
ऊर्जिताश्रय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Spirited, magnanimous.<BR> E. ऊर्जित great,<BR>आश्रय receptacle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=136-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्णनाभ|ऊर्णनाभः|ऊर्ण्णनाभ
ऊर्णनाभ m. (-भः) A spider.<BR> E. ऊर्ण wool, नाभि the navel, ड affix; also<BR>ऊर्णनाभि, the final being retained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=136-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्णा
ऊर्णा f. (-र्णा)<BR>	 1. Wool, felt, &c., the hair of sheep, deer, camels, &c.<BR>	 2.<BR>A circle of the hair between the eyebrows, considered as a token<BR>of greatness.<BR> E. ऊर्णु to cover, ड and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=136-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्णामय|ऊर्ण्णामय
ऊर्णामय mfn. (-यः-यी-यं) Woolen, made of wool.<BR> E. ऊर्णा and मयट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=136-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्णायु|ऊर्णायुः|ऊर्ण्णायु
ऊर्णायु m. (-युः)<BR>	 1. A woollen blanket.<BR>	 2. A ram.<BR>	 3. A spider.<BR> E. ऊर्णा<BR>wool, युस् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=136-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्णु|ऊर्ण्णु
ऊर्णु r. 2nd cl. (ञ) ऊर्णुञ् (ऊर्णौति ऊर्णोति or ऊर्णुते) To cover, hide, con-<BR>ceal, &c. with प्र prefixed प्रोर्णौति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=136-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्णुत
ऊर्णुत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Covered.<BR> E. ऊर्णु and क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=136-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्द्दर|ऊर्दर|ऊर्दरं|ऊर्दरः|ऊर्द्दरः
ऊर्द्दर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A hero, a champion.<BR>	 2. A Rākṣasa, a goblin or fiend.<BR>E. ऊर्ज to be strong, दरल Unādi affix; ज is dropped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=136-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्द्ध
ऊर्द्ध mfn. (-र्द्धः-र्द्धा-र्द्धं)<BR>	 1. Above, upper.<BR>	 2. High, elevated.<BR>	 3. Abandoned:<BR>see ऊर्द्ध्व.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=136-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्द्धक
ऊर्द्धक m. (-कः) A kind of drum: see ऊर्द्ध्वक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=136-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्द्ध्व
ऊर्द्ध्व mfn. (-र्द्ध्वः-र्द्ध्वा-र्द्ध्वं)<BR>	 1. Above, superior, upper.<BR>	 2. High.<BR>	 3. Aban-<BR>doned.<BR>	 4. After, subsequent.<BR> E. ऊर् substituted for उद्<BR>above, हा to leave, and ड्व affix, or with ड only ऊर्द्ध.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=136-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्द्ध्वक
ऊर्द्ध्वक m. (-कः) A kind of drum.<BR> E. ऊर्द्ध्व or ऊर्द्ध्व up, and क what sounds;<BR>from its making a loud noise, or being elevated in playing; also<BR>ऊर्द्धक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=136-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्द्ध्वकाय
ऊर्द्ध्वकाय m. (-यः) The upper part of the body.<BR> E. ऊर्द्ध्व and काय body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=136-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्द्ध्वग
ऊर्द्ध्वग mfn. (-गः-गा-गं) Going up or above; ascending, hovering.<BR> E. ऊर्द्ध्व<BR>and ग what goes; also ऊर्द्ध्वगामिन्, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=136-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्द्ध्वगत
ऊर्द्ध्वगत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Gone up, risen, ascended.<BR> E. ऊर्द्ध्व, गत gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=136-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्द्ध्वगति
ऊर्द्ध्वगति f. (-तिः) Ascent, elevation.<BR> E. ऊर्द्ध्व and गति going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=136-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्द्ध्वगपुर
ऊर्द्ध्वगपुर n. (-रं) The city of HARISCHANDRA, who with his subjects is<BR>supposed to be suspended in the atmosphere.<BR> E. ऊर्द्ध्वग going above,<BR>and पुर a city: see हरिश्चन्द्रपुर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=136-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्द्ध्वगम
ऊर्द्ध्वगम m. (-मः) Upward motion of any kind<BR> E. ऊर्द्ध्व and गम going;<BR>also ऊर्द्ध्वगति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=136-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्द्ध्वचरण
ऊर्द्ध्वचरण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Supine, heels upwards.<BR> E. ऊर्द्ध्व and चरण the<BR>foot; also ऊर्द्ध्वपाद, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=136-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्द्ध्वजानु
ऊर्द्ध्वजानु mfn. (-नुः-नुः-नु)<BR>	 1. Thick-kneed, long-shanked.<BR>	 2. Sitting on the<BR>hams.<BR> E. ऊर्द्ध्व high, large, जानु the knee, and with कन् added<BR>ऊर्द्ध्वजानुक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=136-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्द्ध्वज्ञ
ऊर्द्ध्वज्ञ mfn. (-ज्ञः-ज्ञा-ज्ञं) Thick-kneed: see the preceding.<BR> E. ऊर्द्ध्व and<BR>ज्ञ substituted for जानु; also ऊर्द्ध्वज्ञु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=136-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्द्ध्वज्ञु
ऊर्द्ध्वज्ञु mfn. (-ज्ञुः-ज्ञुः-ज्ञु) See the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=136-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्द्ध्वत्व
ऊर्द्ध्वत्व n. (-त्वं) Height, elevation.<BR> E. त्व added to ऊर्द्ध्व; also with तल् ऊर्द्ध्वता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=136-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्द्ध्वदृष्टि
ऊर्द्ध्वदृष्टि mfn. (-ष्टिः-ष्टिः-ष्टि) Looking up or upwards.<BR> E. ऊर्द्ध्व and दृष्टि sight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=136-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्द्ध्वदेव
ऊर्द्ध्वदेव m. (-वः) A name of VIṢṆU.<BR> E. ऊर्द्ध्व superior, and देव deity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=136-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्द्ध्वन्दम
ऊर्द्ध्वन्दम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं) Exalted, elevated.<BR> E. ऊर्द्ध्व upper, दम् to tame.<BR>अप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=136-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्द्ध्वपातन
ऊर्द्ध्वपातन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Causing to ascend.<BR>	 2. Sublimation.<BR> E. ऊर्द्ध्व and पातन<BR>Causing to go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=136-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्द्ध्वपात्र
ऊर्द्ध्वपात्र n. (-त्रं) A sacrificial vessel.<BR> E. ऊर्द्ध्व and पात्र a vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=136-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्द्ध्वपाद
ऊर्द्ध्वपाद mfn. (-दः-दा-दं) Heels upwards.<BR>	 m. (-दः) A fabulous animal with<BR>eight legs.<BR> E. ऊर्द्ध्व superior, exceeding, पाद a foot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=136-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्द्ध्वपुण्ड्र
ऊर्द्ध्वपुण्ड्र m. (-ण्ड्रः) A perpendicular line on the forehead made with<BR>Sandal, &c. a Vaishnava mark.<BR> E. ऊर्द्ध्व above, पुण्ड्र a similar mark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=136-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्द्ध्वबाहु
ऊर्द्ध्वबाहु m. (-हुः) An ascetic, one who holds his arms above his head<BR>constantly till they are fixed in that position.<BR> E. ऊर्द्ध्व and बाहु the<BR>arm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=136-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्द्ध्वरेतस्
ऊर्द्ध्वरेतस् m. (-ताः)<BR>	 1. A name of ŚIVA.<BR>	 2. Of BHISHMA.<BR>	 3. A description<BR>of saint, one who lives in perpetual chastity.<BR> E. ऊर्द्ध्व up, above, and<BR>रेतस् semen virile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=136-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्द्ध्वलिङ्ग
ऊर्द्ध्वलिङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः) A name of ŚIVA.<BR> E. ऊर्द्ध्व and लिङ्ग the generative organ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=136-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्द्ध्वलोक
ऊर्द्ध्वलोक m. (-कः) Svarga, the heaven of INDRA or paradise.<BR> E. ऊर्द्ध्व and<BR>लोक a world; the world above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=136-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्द्ध्ववर्त्मन्
ऊर्द्ध्ववर्त्मन् m. (-त्मा) The atmosphere, heaven.<BR> E. ऊर्द्ध्व above, and वर्त्मन् a<BR>path.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=136-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्द्ध्ववायु
ऊर्द्ध्ववायु m. (-युः) The wind in the upper part of the body.<BR> E. ऊर्द्ध्व and वायु wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=136-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्द्ध्ववृत
ऊर्द्ध्ववृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Put on, above or over the head.<BR> E. ऊर्द्ध्व and वृत<BR>worn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=136-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्द्ध्वशोधन
ऊर्द्ध्वशोधन n. (-नं) Vomiting.<BR> E. ऊर्द्ध्व and शोधन purifying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=136-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्द्ध्वस्थ
ऊर्द्ध्वस्थ mfn. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थं) Above, superior, placed on high; also ऊर्द्ध्वस्थित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR> E. ऊर्द्ध्व and स्थ what stays or is.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=136-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्द्ध्वस्थिति
ऊर्द्ध्वस्थिति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. A horse's back, the part where the rider sits.<BR>	 2.<BR>Elevation, superiority.<BR> E. ऊर्द्ध्व above, and स्थिति being, staying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=136-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्द्ध्वासित
ऊर्द्ध्वासित m. (-तः) The name of a vegetable, (Momordica charantia.) E.<BR>ऊर्द्ध्व above, आसित thrown: raised above other fruits.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=137-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्म्मि|ऊर्मि|ऊर्मिः|ऊर्म्मिः
ऊर्म्मि mf. (-र्म्मिः) or f. only, (-र्म्मी)<BR>	 1. A wave.<BR>	 2. A current, the flowing<BR>of water.<BR>	 3. A fold or plait in a garment.<BR>	 4. A Light, manifesta-<BR>tion.<BR>	 5. Speed, velocity.<BR>	 6. Mental suffering, distress, uneasiness.<BR>	 7.<BR>Pain.<BR>	 8. Missing, regretting.<BR>	 9. Human infirmity, as grief, illusion,<BR>hunger, thirst, decay, death.<BR>	 10. Association.<BR>	 11. Number, quanti-<BR>ty.<BR> E. ऋ to go, मि Unāadi affix, ऊ substituted for the initial letter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=137-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्म्मिका|ऊर्मिका
ऊर्म्मिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. A finger-ring.<BR>	 2. A plait or fold in a garment.<BR>	 3. A<BR>wave.<BR>	 4. Regret, sorrowing for anything lost.<BR>	 5. The buzzing of<BR>a bee. E. As the preceding, कन् &c. added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=137-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्म्मिमत्|ऊर्मिमत्|ऊर्मिमन्त्
ऊर्म्मिमत् mfn. (-मान्-मती-मत्)<BR>	 1. Crooked.<BR>	 2. Wavy, billowy.<BR> E. ऊर्म्मि a<BR>wave, and मतुप् poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=137-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्म्मिमत्ता|ऊर्मिमत्ता
ऊर्म्मिमत्ता f. (-त्ता)<BR>	 1. Undulation.<BR>	 2. Crookedness.<BR> E. ऊर्म्मिमत् and तल् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=137-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्म्मिमालिन्|ऊर्मिमालिन्
ऊर्म्मिमालिन् m. (-ली) The ocean.<BR> E. ऊर्म्मि a wave, माला a necklace, and इनि<BR>affix; whose necklace is the surge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=137-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्व्वरा|ऊर्वरा
ऊर्व्वरा f. (-रा) Fertile soil, land bearing any and every crop: see उर्व्वरा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=137-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्व्वष्टीवत्
ऊर्व्वष्टीवत् n. (-वत्) The thigh and knee.<BR> E. ऊरु and अष्ठीवत् the knee pan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=137-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्व्वसी
ऊर्व्वसी f. (-सी) A nymph of Svarga: see उर्व्वशी. Also written ऊर्व्वशी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=137-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्व्व्यङ्ग|ऊर्व्यङ्ग|ऊर्व्यंगं|ऊर्व्यङ्गं
ऊर्व्व्यङ्ग n. (-ङ्गं) A mushroom.<BR> E. ऊर्व्वी for उर्व्वी the earth, and अङ्ग body:<BR>earth-born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=137-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्षा
ऊर्षा f. (-र्षा) A kind of grass, (Andropogon serratum:) see देवताडक. E.<BR>वृष् to rain, अङ् and टाप् affixes, व changed to ऊ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=137-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊलूक|ऊलूकः
ऊलूक m. (-कः) An owl.<BR> E. बल् to be strong, and ऊक affix; ब become ऊ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=137-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊलूपिन्
ऊलूपिन् m. (-पी) A porpoise: see ऊलपिन्, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=137-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊष|ऊषं|ऊषः
ऊष r. 1st cl. (ऊषति) To be diseased or disordered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=137-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊष|ऊषं|ऊषः
ऊष m. (-षः) Salt-ground, soil impregnated with saline particles.<BR>	 n. (-षं)<BR>Dawn, day-break.<BR>	 f. (-षा) The wife of ANIRUDDHA.<BR> E. ऊष् to be or<BR>make sick, क affix, fem. टाप्: see उषा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=137-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊषक|ऊषकं
ऊषक n. (-कं) Dawn, day-break. E. As before, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=137-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊषण|ऊषणं|ऊषणः
ऊषण n. (-णं) Black pepper.<BR>	 f. (-णा) Long pepper: see उषण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=137-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊषर|ऊषरः
ऊषर mfn. (-रः-रा-री-रं) A spot with saline soil.<BR> E. ऊष such soil, रच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=137-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊषवत्|ऊषवन्त्
ऊषवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Consisting of saline soil, (a place, &c.)<BR> E. ऊष<BR>and poss. affix मतुप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=137-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊह|ऊहः
ऊह r. 1st cl. (ऊहते) To reason, to apprehend and infer: with प्र and वि<BR>to intermit; with वि, to array in order of battle; with सम् prefixed,<BR>(समूहति or -ते) to assemble or to be assembled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=137-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊह|ऊहः
ऊह mfn. (-हः-हा-हं)<BR>	 1. Reasoning.<BR>	 2. Completing a defective sentence<BR>or verse, supplying an ellipsis.<BR> E. ऊह् to deliberate, घञ् affix, or<BR>with ल्युट् affix, ऊहन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=137-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊहन|ऊहनं
ऊहन n. (-नं) Reasoning, inferring, concluding.<BR> E. ऊह् to deliberate,<BR>affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=137-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊहनी
ऊहनी f. (-नी) A broom.<BR> E. वह् to carry, ल्युट् and ङीष् affixes; व is chang-<BR>ed to ऊ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=137-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊहिन्
ऊहिन् mfn. (-ही-हिनी-हि)<BR>	 1. Who or what reasons.<BR>	 2. Who or what<BR>assembles.<BR>	 f. (-णी) An assemblage, a collection.<BR> E. ऊह reasoning,<BR>इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=137-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊह्य
ऊह्य mfn. (-ह्यः-ह्या-ह्यं) To be investigated, to be supplied.<BR> E. ऊह् to<BR>reason, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=137-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋ
ऋ The seventh vowel of the Sanskrit alphabet, and peculiar to it. It<BR>corresponds in sound with RI, in merrily.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=137-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋ
ऋ f. (आ) A name of ADITI, the mother of the gods. ind.<BR>	 1. An expres-<BR>sion of abuse.<BR>	 2. An articulate sound.<BR>	 3. An expression of laugh-<BR>ter.<BR>	 4. A sound inarticulate or reiterated as in stammering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=137-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋ
ऋ r. 1st cl. (ऋच्छति)<BR>	 1. To go, to approach.<BR>	 2. To gain, to acquire;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=137-b" target="_blank">Page137-b+ 60</a>]<BR>(the radical is changed to ऋछ before an initial mute श.) r. 3rd cl.<BR>(ईयर्त्ति) To go; (some confine this root to the Vedas.) r. 5th cl.<BR>(ऋणोति) To kill, to injure; also रि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=137-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋक्थ|ऋक्थं
ऋक्थ n. (-थं)<BR>	 1. Wealth, possessions, property.<BR>	 2. Gold.<BR> E. ऋच् to<BR>praise, थक् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=137-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋक्थग्रहण
ऋक्थग्रहण n. (-णं) Receiving or inheriting property.<BR> E. ऋक्थ wealth<BR>and ग्रहण taking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=137-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋक्थग्राह|ऋक्थग्राहः
ऋक्थग्राह mfn. (-हः-हा-हं) Who inherits or takes property.<BR>	 m. (-हः) in-<BR>heriting or receiving property.<BR> E. ऋक्थ and ग्रह् to take, with घञ्<BR>affix; also with णिनि, ऋक्थग्राहिन् mfn. (-ही-हिणी-हि.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=137-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋक्थजात
ऋक्थजात mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Accumulated, added, (as property.)<BR> E. ऋक्थ<BR>wealth and जात produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=137-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋक्थभाग|ऋक्थभागः
ऋक्थभाग m. (-गः)<BR>	 1. Division of property, inheritance, partition.<BR>	 2. A<BR>share.<BR> E. ऋक्थ property and भाग division.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=137-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋक्थभागिन्
ऋक्थभागिन् mfn. (-गी-गिनी-गि) An heir, a coheir, inheriting or sharing<BR>property.<BR> E. ऋक्थ and भागिन् who shares.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=137-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋक्थहर
ऋक्थहर mfn. (-रः-री-रं) An heir, a coheir.<BR> E. ऋक्थ and हर who takes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=137-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋक्थहारिन्
ऋक्थहारिन् mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि) An heir, inheriting or sharing property.<BR>E. ऋक्थ and हारिन् who takes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=137-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋक्शत
ऋक्शत n. (-तं) A hundred texts.<BR> E. ऋच् a prayer, and शत a century.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=137-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋक्संहिता
ऋक्संहिता f. (-ता) The collection of the prayers and hymns of the Rik<BR>Veda.<BR> E. ऋच् and संहिता compendium.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=137-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋक्ष|ऋक्षं|ऋक्षः
ऋक्ष r. 5th cl. (ऋक्ष्णोति) To kill, to hurt or seek to hurt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=137-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋक्ष|ऋक्षं|ऋक्षः
ऋक्ष mfn. (-क्षः-क्षा-क्षं) Pierced, cut, divided.<BR>	 mn. (-क्षः-क्षं) A star, a con-<BR>stellation.<BR>	 m. (-क्षः)<BR>	 1. A mountain in the peninsula, the temporary<BR>residence of RAMA.<BR>	 2. A bear.<BR>	 3. A plant, (Bignonia Indica.)<BR> E. ऋष्<BR>to go, Unādi affix स, the radical final then becomes क, and स be-<BR>comes ष; and क and ष form the compound letter क्ष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=137-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋक्षगन्धा
ऋक्षगन्धा f. (-न्धा)<BR>	 1. A kind of potherb, (Convolvulus argenteus.)<BR>	 2.<BR>Another sort, (Convolvulus paniculatus.)<BR> E. ऋक्ष a bear, and गन्ध<BR>smell, smelling like a bear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=137-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋक्षगन्धिका
ऋक्षगन्धिका f. (-का) A kind of potherb, (Convolvulus paniculatus, the<BR>pale sort:) see the preceding. E. As before, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=137-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋक्षर|ऋक्षरं|ऋक्षरः
ऋक्षर n. (-रं) A shower, a stream.<BR>	 m. (-रः) A family priest.<BR> E. ऋष् to go,<BR>and सर Unādi affix: see the derivation of ऋक्ष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=137-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋक्षविभावन
ऋक्षविभावन n. (-नं) Observing or seeing the stars.<BR> E. ऋक्ष and विभावन<BR>noticing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=137-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋक्षेश|ऋक्षेशः
ऋक्षेश m. (-शः) The moon.<BR> E. ऋक्ष a star, ईश lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=137-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋक्षेष्टि|ऋक्षेष्टिः
ऋक्षेष्टि m. (-ष्टिः) Offering worship to the planets and stars.<BR> E. ऋक्ष and<BR>इष्टि worship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=137-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋग्वेद|ऋग्वेदः
ऋग्वेद m. (-दः) The Ṛc or Ṛk Veda, the first of the four Vedas. E.<BR>ऋच् and वेद a Veda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=137-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋग्वेदविद्
ऋग्वेदविद् m. (-वित् or -विद्) A Brahman familiar with the Ṛk Veda. E.<BR>ऋग्वेद and विद् who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=137-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋच्
ऋच् r. 6th cl. (ऋचति)<BR>	 1. To praise.<BR>	 2. To cover, to screen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=137-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋच्
ऋच् f. (ऋक्)<BR>	 1. Rik or Rig Veda, one of the four principal religious<BR>books of the Hindus.<BR>	 2. A stanza of a prayer or hymn of the Rig<BR>Veda.<BR>	 3. A mantra, a magical invocation, a mystical prayer. E.<BR>ऋच् to praise, affix क्विप्, celebrating the praises of the gods.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=137-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋचीष|ऋचीषं|ऋचीषः
ऋचीष n. (-षं) A frying pan.<BR>	 m. (-षः) A hell.<BR> E. ऋज् to fry, ईषन् affix, च<BR>substituted for ज; also ऋजीष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=137-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋच्छ
ऋच्छ r. 6th cl. (ऋच्छति)<BR>	 1. To go, to move.<BR>	 2. To fail in faculties.<BR>	 3. To<BR>become hard or stiff, to congeal.<BR>	 4. To incur.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=137-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋच्छरा
ऋच्छरा f. (-रा) A harlot, a courtezan.<BR> E. ऋच्छ् to go, अर Unādi affix,<BR>and टाप् for the fem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=137-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋज
ऋज r. 1st cl. (अर्जते)<BR>	 1. To go.<BR>	 2. To stand or be firm.<BR>	 3. To be strong.<BR>4. To acquire, to gain or earn.<BR>	 5. To live. With a prefix ending in<BR>अ, the radical vowel is changed to आर्, as in the pass. voice,<BR>(प्रार्ज्यते) (इ) ऋनि (ऋजते) To fry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=137-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋजीक|ऋजीकः
ऋजीक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. INDRA.<BR>	 2. Smoke.<BR> E. ऋज and कीकन् Uṇadi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=137-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋजीष|ऋजीषं
ऋजीष n. (-षं)<BR>	 1. A frying pan.<BR>	 2. A hell.<BR> E. ऋज् to fry, ईषन् Unādi<BR>affix: see ऋचीष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=138-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋजु
ऋजु mfn. (-जुः-जुः-जु)<BR>	 1. Straight.<BR>	 2. Straight metaphorically, as in<BR>morals, upright, honest.<BR> E. ऋज् to go, affix कु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=138-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋजुकाय|ऋजुकायः
ऋजुकाय m. (-यः) A name of the saint KAŚYAPA.<BR> E. ऋजु straight, काय body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=138-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋजुता
ऋजुता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Uprightness, sincerity.<BR>	 2. Straightness.<BR> E. ऋजु with तल्<BR>affix; also with त्व, ऋजुत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=138-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋजूकरण
ऋजूकरण n. (-णं) Straightening.<BR> E. ऋजु and करण making; the vowel<BR>lengthened.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=138-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋजूकृत
ऋजूकृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Made straight.<BR> E. ऋजु and कृत made; the vowel<BR>lengthened.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=138-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋज्र|ऋज्रः
ऋज्र m. (-ज्रः) A leader.<BR> E. ऋज् to go, रन् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=138-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋञ्जसान|ऋंजसान|ऋञ्जसानः
ऋञ्जसान m. (-नः) A cloud.<BR> E. ऋजि to go, शानच् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=138-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋण|ऋणं
ऋण r. 8th cl. (उ) ऋणु (अर्णोति or अर्णुते, ऋणोति or -णुते) To go; according<BR>to some it is ऋन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=138-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋण|ऋणं
ऋण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Debt.<BR>	 2. A fort, a strong hold.<BR>	 3. (In algebra,) Ne-<BR>gative quantity, minus.<BR> E. ऋ to go, क्त affix, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=138-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋणकर्तृ|ऋणकर्त्तृ
ऋणकर्तृ mfn. (-र्ता-त्री-र्तृ) Getting into debt, indebted.<BR> E. ऋण and कर्तृ<BR>who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=138-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋणग्रस्त
ऋणग्रस्त mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं) Indebted, involved in debt.<BR> E. ऋण and ग्रस्त seized.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=138-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋणग्रह|ऋणग्रहः
ऋणग्रह m. (-हः)<BR>	 1. Borrowing.<BR>	 2. A borrower.<BR> E. ऋण and ग्रह taking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=138-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋणग्राहिन्
ऋणग्राहिन् mfn. (-ही-हिणी-हि) Borrowing, a borrower.<BR> E. ऋण and ग्राहिन्<BR>who takes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=138-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋणदातृ
ऋणदातृ mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ) One who pays a debt.<BR> E. ऋण and दातृ who gives.<BR>Also ऋणद mfn. (-दः-दा-दं) and ऋणदायिन् mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=138-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋणदान
ऋणदान n. (-नं) Payment of debt.<BR> E. ऋण and दान giving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=138-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋणमत्कुण|ऋणमत्कुणः
ऋणमत्कुण m. (-णः) A security, a bail.<BR> E. ऋण debt, मत्कुण an insect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=138-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋणमार्गण|ऋणमार्गणः
ऋणमार्गण m. (-णः) A security.<BR> E. ऋण, मृग् to cleanse, in the causal, and<BR>ल्युट् affix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=138-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋणमुक्ति|ऋणमुक्तिः
ऋणमुक्ति f. (-क्तिः) Discharge of a debt.<BR> E. ऋण and मुक्ति emancipation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=138-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋणमोक्ष|ऋणमोक्षः
ऋणमोक्ष m. (-क्षः) Paying a debt.<BR> E. ऋण and मोक्ष released.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=138-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋणवत्|ऋणवन्त्
ऋणवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Owing, in debt.<BR> E. ऋण and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=138-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋणशोधन
ऋणशोधन n. (-नं) Payment or discharge of a debt.<BR> E. ऋण and शोधन<BR>purifying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=138-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋणादान|ऋणादानं
ऋणादान n. (-नं) Recovery of a debt, receipt of money, &c. lent. It is<BR>one of the eighteen titles or subjects of judicial procedure.<BR> E. ऋण<BR>and आदान receiving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=138-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋणान्तक|ऋणान्तकः
ऋणान्तक m. (-कः) The planet MARS.<BR> E. ऋण, अन्त end, and क affix of<BR>agency: being the patron of debtors.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=138-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋणापनयन
ऋणापनयन n. (-नं) Discharge of a debt.<BR> E. ऋण and अपनयन removing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=138-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋणापनोदन|ऋणापनोदनं
ऋणापनोदन n. (-नं) Payment of a debt.<BR> E. ऋण and अपनोदन removing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=138-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋणापाकरण
ऋणापाकरण n. (-णं) Paying off a debt.<BR> E. ऋण and अपाकरण acquittance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=138-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋणिक|ऋणिकः
ऋणिक m. (-कः) A debtor.<BR> E. ऋण debt. वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=138-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋणिन्
ऋणिन् mfn. (-णी-णिनी-णि)<BR>	 1. Indebted.<BR>	 2. Of or belonging to a debt.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-णी) A debtor.<BR> E. ऋण and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=138-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋणोद्ग्रहण
ऋणोद्ग्रहण n. (-णं) Recovering a debt in any way from the creditor, by<BR>friendly or legal proceedings, by stratagem, or by arrest.<BR> E. ऋण<BR>and उद्ग्रहण taking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=138-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋत|ऋतं|ऋतः
ऋत r. 6th cl. (ऋतति)<BR>	 1. To go.<BR>	 2. To have power.<BR>	 3. To domineer.<BR>	 4.<BR>To hate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=138-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋत|ऋतं|ऋतः
ऋत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Gone.<BR>	 2. Enlightened, luminous.<BR>	 3. Worshipped,<BR>respected.<BR>	 4. True.<BR>	 n. (-तं)<BR>	 1. Gleaning.<BR>	 2. Water.<BR>	 3. Truth.<BR> E. ऋ<BR>to go, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=138-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋतधामन्
ऋतधामन् m. (-मा) A name of VIṢṆU.<BR> E. ऋत luminous, धामन् abode;<BR>whose residence is brilliant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=138-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋतव्य
ऋतव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं) Seasonable, in season, relating to a season. E.<BR>ऋतु and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=138-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋति|ऋतिः
ऋति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Prosperity, felicity.<BR>	 2. A road, a way.<BR>	 3. Abuse, cen-<BR>sure, reproach.<BR>	 4. Envy, emulation.<BR>	 5. Going, motion.<BR>	 6. Ill for-<BR>tune.<BR> E. ऋ and क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=138-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋतिङ्कर|ऋतिंकर
ऋतिङ्कर mfn. (-रः-री-रं) Propitions, fortunate.<BR> E. ऋति and कर what<BR>makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=138-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋतीया
ऋतीया f. (-या)<BR>	 1. Censure, reproach, (according to some.)<BR>	 2. Shame. E.<BR>ऋत Sautra root, to abuse, ईयच् affix, fem. टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=138-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋतु|ऋतुः
ऋतु m. (-तुः)<BR>	 1. A season, (the Hindu year is divided into six seasons,<BR>each consisting of two months.)<BR>	 2. The menstrual evacuation.<BR>3. The time favourable for procreation, or sixteen days in each<BR>month.<BR>	 4. A month.<BR>	 5. A kind of collyrium.<BR>	 6. Light.<BR> E. ऋ to go,<BR>तु Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=138-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋतुकाल|ऋतुकालः
ऋतुकाल m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. The duration of a season.<BR>	 2. The period of menstru-<BR>ation.<BR>	 3. The period favourable for procreation, sixteen days in<BR>each month.<BR> E. ऋतु and काल time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=138-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋतुगण|ऋतुगणः
ऋतुगण m. (-णः) The seasons collectively.<BR> E. ऋतु and गण a class.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=138-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋतुपर्य्याय|ऋतुपर्याय|ऋतुपर्यायः
ऋतुपर्य्याय m. (-यः) The revolution of the season.<BR> E. ऋतु and पर्य्याय<BR>revolution.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=138-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋतुप्राप्त|ऋतुप्राप्तः
ऋतुप्राप्त mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं) Fruitful, fertile, &c. productive in due season.<BR>E. ऋतु season, and प्राप्त attained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=138-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋतुमती
ऋतुमती f. (-ती) A woman during menstruation.<BR> E. ऋतु, मतुष् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=138-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋतुवृत्ति|ऋतुवृत्तिः
ऋतुवृत्ति m. (-त्तिः) A year.<BR> E. ऋतु a season, वृत्ति being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=138-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋतुराज|ऋतुराजः
ऋतुराज m. (-जः) Spring.<BR> E. ऋतु and राजा king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=138-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋतुलिङ्ग|ऋतुलिंग
ऋतुलिङ्ग n. (-ङ्गं)<BR>	 1. A sign of the season.<BR>	 2. A symptom of menstrua-<BR>tion.<BR> E. ऋतु and लिङ्ग a mark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=138-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋतुसन्धि|ऋतुसंधि|ऋतुसन्धिः
ऋतुसन्धि f. (-न्धिः) The interval or junction between two seasons: the last<BR>seven days of one season and the first seven of the next.<BR> E. ऋतु<BR>and सन्धि union.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=138-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋतुसात्म्य
ऋतुसात्म्य n. (-त्म्यं) Diet, &c. suited to the season.<BR> E. ऋतु and सात्म्य suitableness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=138-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋतुस्नाता
ऋतुस्नाता f. (-ता) A woman who has bathed after menstruation.<BR> E. ऋतु<BR>and स्राता bathed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=138-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋते
ऋते ind. Besides, except.<BR> E. ऋत Sautra root, to except, के aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=138-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋतोक्ति
ऋतोक्ति f. (-क्तिः) Speaking truth.<BR> E. ऋत and उक्ति saying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=138-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋत्वन्त|ऋत्वन्तः
ऋत्वन्त m. (-न्तः) The close of a season.<BR>	 2. The termination of menstru-<BR>ation.<BR> E. ऋतु and अन्त term.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=138-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋत्विज्
ऋत्विज् m. (-त्विक्)<BR>	 1. A domestic chaplain, a family priest.<BR> E. ऋतु a<BR>season, यज् to worship, affix क्विन्, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=138-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋद्ध|ऋद्धं|ऋद्धः
ऋद्ध mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं) Prosperous, thriving, rising, &c.<BR>	 n. (-द्धं)<BR>	 1. Stored<BR>grain.<BR>	 2. A demonstrated conclusion, a distinct result.<BR> E. ऋघ् to<BR>grow, &c. affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=138-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋद्धि|ऋद्धिः
ऋद्धि f. (-द्धिः)<BR>	 1. A medicinal plant; also सिद्धि.<BR>	 2. Increase, growth.<BR>3. Fortune, prosperity.<BR>	 4. A name of the goddess PARVATI.<BR> E. ऋध<BR>to grow, &c., क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=138-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋद्धिमत्|ऋद्धिमन्त्
ऋद्धिमत् mfn. (-मान्-मती-मत्) Rich, prosperous.<BR> E. ऋद्धि and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=138-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋध
ऋध r. 4th cl. (उ) ऋधु (ऋध्यति) To increase, to grow, to flourish, to<BR>prosper. r. 5th cl. (ऋध्नोति)<BR>	 1. To increase, &c.<BR>	 2. To augment or<BR>make increase.<BR>	 3. To please.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=138-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋफ
ऋफ r. 6th cl. (ऋफति) To injure, to kill; also रिफ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=138-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋभु|ऋभुः
ऋभु m. (-भुः)<BR>	 1. A deity.<BR>	 2. A divinity of a particular order.<BR> E. ऋ the<BR>mother of the gods, भू to be, डु affix; also रिभु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=138-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋभुक्ष|ऋभुक्षः
ऋभुक्ष m. (-क्षः)<BR>	 1. A name of INDRA.<BR>	 2. INDRA'S heaven or paradise.<BR>	 3.<BR>The thunderbolt of INDRA.<BR> E. ऋभु a deity, क्षि to waste, to go, ड aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=138-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋभुक्षिन्
ऋभुक्षिन् m. (-क्षा) INDRA.<BR> E. ऋभुक्ष paradise, &c. इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=138-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋम्फ
ऋम्फ r. 6th cl. (ऋम्फति) To injure, to kill; also रिम्फ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=138-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋश्य|ऋश्यः
ऋश्य m. (-श्यः) The painted or white-footed antelope.<BR> E. ऋष् to go, क्यप्<BR>affix; also ऋष्य and रिश्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=138-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋष
ऋष r. 1st cl. (अर्षति) To take, to receive, to choose. (ई) ऋषी r. 6th cl.<BR>(ऋषति) To go, to approach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=138-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋषभ|ऋषभः
ऋषभ m. (-भः)<BR>	 1. (In composition,) best, excellent.<BR>	 2. A bull.<BR>	 3. A<BR>dried plant, one of the eight principal medicaments.<BR>	 4. The<BR>second of the seven notes of the Hindu gamut, in abbreviation,<BR>Ri.<BR>	 5. The first of the twenty-four principal Jinas or Jaina saints.<BR>6. The hollow of the ear.<BR>	 7. The name of a mountain.<BR>	 8. A croco-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=139-a" target="_blank">Page139-a+ 56</a>]<BR>dile's tail.<BR>	 9. A boar's tail.<BR>	 f. (-भी)<BR>	 1. A masculine woman, a woman<BR>with a beard, &c.<BR>	 2. A widow.<BR>	 3. Cowach, (Carpopogon pruriens.)<BR>E. ऋष् to go, अभच् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=138-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋषभध्वज|ऋषभध्वजः
ऋषभध्वज m. (-जः) A name of ŚIVA.<BR>	 2. A Jaina saint.<BR> E. ऋषभ and ध्वज a<BR>sign: he whose symbol is a bull.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=139-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋषि|ऋषिः
ऋषि m. (-षिः) A Ṛṣi or sanctified personage so called: there are seven<BR>orders of these saints, as the Srutarshi, Kandarshi, Paramarshi,<BR>Maharshi, Rajarshi, Brahmarshi and Devarshi: the uncompounded<BR>name is especially applied to seven sages, of the Brahmarshi order,<BR>cotemporary with each MANU; those of the present Manwantara,<BR>are MARICHI, ATRI, ANGIRAS, PULASTYA, PULAHA, KRATU and<BR>VASIṢṬHA: the names of each series differ: specified also form, in<BR>astronomy, the asterism of the greater bear: the Ṛṣi of a Mantra<BR>or mystic prayer in the Vedas, is the saint by whom it is supposed<BR>to have been remembered or recited.<BR>	 2. A Veda.<BR>	 3. A ray of light.<BR>	 4.<BR>A saint or sanctified sage in general.<BR>	 f. (-षी) The wife of a Ṛṣi. E.<BR>ऋष् to go, इन् Unādi affix, fem. affix ङीष्; who goes beyond the<BR>limits of earthly life and wisdom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=139-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋषिकुल्या
ऋषिकुल्या f. (-ल्या) A river<BR> E. ऋषि a saint, कुल्या an artificial canal: a ca-<BR>nal made by the saints.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=139-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋषिगण
ऋषिगण m. (-णः) A company or number of sages.<BR> E. ऋषि and गण a<BR>number.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=139-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋषिजाङ्गल|ऋषिजाङ्गलः
ऋषिजाङ्गल m. (-लः) See the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=139-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋषिजाङ्गलिकी
ऋषिजाङ्गलिकी f. (-की) A potherb, (Convolvulus argenteus:) see वृद्धताडक.<BR>E. ऋषि and जाङ्गलिक a dealer in antidotes, affix ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=139-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋषिप्रोक्ता
ऋषिप्रोक्ता f. (-क्ता) A plant: see माषपर्णी.<BR> E. ऋषि, प्रोक्त mentioned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=139-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋषियज्ञ|ऋषियज्ञः
ऋषियज्ञ m. (-ज्ञः) The study of Scripture.<BR> E. ऋषि a sage, and यज्ञ sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=139-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋषीवह
ऋषीवह mfn. (-हः-हा-हं) Bearing or conveying a Ṛṣi.<BR> E. ऋषि and वह<BR>what bears, the final made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=139-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋष्टि|ऋष्टिः
ऋष्टि f. (-ष्टिः) A sword.<BR> E. ऋष् to go, affix क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=139-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋष्य|ऋष्यः
ऋष्य m. (-ष्यः) The painted or white-footed antelope.<BR>	 n. (-ष्यं) A sort of<BR>leprosy.<BR> E. ऋष् to go, क्यप् affix: also ऋश्य, रिश्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=139-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋष्यकेतु|ऋष्यकेतुः
ऋष्यकेतु m. (-तुः) A name of ANIRUDDHA the son of KANDARPA.<BR> E. ऋष्य<BR>and केतु a sign; having a deer for his symbol: some read this<BR>रिश्वकेतु, and others ऋश्यकेतु, ऋष्यकेतन, रिष्यकेतु, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=139-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋष्यगता
ऋष्यगता f. (-ता) A plant, (Asparagus racemosus.)<BR> E. ऋषि and अ before<BR>गत gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=139-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋष्यगन्धा
ऋष्यगन्धा f. (-न्धा) A potherb, (Convolvulus argenteus:) see वृद्धताडक. E.<BR>ऋषि, अ priv. and गन्ध smell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=139-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋष्यजिह्व
ऋष्यजिह्व n. (-ह्वं) A sort of leprosy.<BR> E. ऋष्य the deer and जिह्वा the tongue;<BR>to which the blotches are compared.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=139-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋष्यप्रोक्ता
ऋष्यप्रोक्ता f. (-क्ता)<BR>	 1. Cowach, (Carpopogon pruriens.)<BR>	 2. Asparagus<BR>racemosus.<BR>	 3. Sida, (cordifolia and rhombifolia.) E. See ऋषिप्रोक्ता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=139-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋष्यमूक|ऋष्यमूकः
ऋष्यमूक m. (-कः) A mountain in the Dakshin, the temporary abode of<BR>RAMA with the monkey-chief SUGRĪVA.<BR> E. ऋष्य a deer, मूक dumb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=139-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋष्यशृङ्ग|ऋष्यशृङ्गः
ऋष्यशृङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः) The name of a holy sage celebrated in the first book<BR>of the Rāmāyaṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=139-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ॠ
ॠ The long vowel corresponding to the short one preceding, and<BR>having the sound of RI long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=139-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ॠ
ॠ r. 9th cl. (गि) (ऋणाति) To go or move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=139-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ॠ
ॠ f. (री)<BR>	 1. The mother of the gods.<BR>	 2. Also of the demons.<BR>	 3. Re-<BR>collection.<BR>	 m. (आ)<BR>	 1. A name of BHAIRAVA.<BR>	 2. An Asura or demon.<BR>3. The breast.<BR>	 4. Motion, going. ind.<BR>	 1. Incipient particle.<BR>	 2. An<BR>interjection of compassion.<BR>	 3. Of reproach.<BR>	 4. Of terror.<BR>	 5. A mys-<BR>tical letter used in the Tantras.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=139-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऌ
ऌ The ninth vowel of the Nagari Alphabet, having the power of Lri,<BR>but more usually considered to be expressed by Li as in Lily.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=139-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऌ
ऌ aptote.<BR>	 1. The divine nature.<BR>	 2. The earth.<BR>	 3. A mountain. ind. A<BR>mystical letter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=139-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ॡ
ॡ The long vowel corresponding to the preceding short one, Lri or Li.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=139-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ॡ
ॡ aptote.<BR>	 1. A divine female.<BR>	 2. The female nature.<BR>	 3. A mother.<BR>	 m.<BR>(ॡः) A name of ŚIVA.<BR>	 f. (ॡः)<BR>	 1. The mother of the demons.<BR>	 2.<BR>The mother of the all-bestowing cow. ind. A mystical letter used<BR>once or repeatedly in many Mantras or mystical formulæ. The<BR>letters ॠ and ॡ are employed in the same manner: they have ap-<BR>parently no signification, but are personified and invested with<BR>marvellous properties in the Tantras.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=139-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ए
ए The eleventh vowel of the alphabet, corresponding to the letter E<BR>as pronounced in most languages except the English, and having<BR>the sound of A in amiable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=139-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ए
ए ind. An interjection of, 1. Remembering, (ha.)<BR>	 2. Censure or con-<BR>tempt.<BR>	 3. Compassion, (ah!)<BR>	 4. Addressing, (eh! hey.)<BR>	 5. Calling,<BR>(hey, ho.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=139-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ए
ए m. (-एः) A name of VIṢṆU.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=139-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एक|एकं|एकः
एक mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>	 1. One.<BR>	 2. Alone, solitary.<BR>	 3. Other, different.<BR>	 4.<BR>Chief, pre-eminent.<BR> E. इण् to go, Unādi affix कन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=139-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकऋक्थिन्
एकऋक्थिन् m. (-थी) A coheir.<BR> E. एक one (father,) ऋक्थिन् heir.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=139-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकक|एककः
एकक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Alone, solitary.<BR> E. एक one, &c. कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=139-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एककर
एककर mfn. (-रः-रा-री-रं)<BR>	 1. Making one.<BR>	 2. One-handed.<BR>	 3. One-rayed.<BR>E. एक and कर making, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=139-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एककार्य्य|एककार्य
एककार्य्य mfn. (-र्य्यः-र्य्या-र्य्यं) Performing the same office, answering the<BR>same end.<BR> E. एक and कार्य्य act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=139-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एककाल|एककालः
एककाल m. (-लः) One or the same time.<BR> E. एक and काल time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=139-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एककालभोजन
एककालभोजन n. (-नं) Eating but one meal in any given time.<BR> E. एककाल<BR>and भोजन food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=139-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एककालीन
एककालीन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Coeval, contemporary.<BR> E. एक and कालीन relating to time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=139-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एककुण्डल|एककुण्डलः
एककुण्डल m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. A name of BALARĀMA.<BR>	 2. An epithet of KUVERA.<BR>E. एक and कुण्डल an ear-ring: wearing it in one ear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=139-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकक्षीर
एकक्षीर n. (-रं) The milk of one (nurse; &c.)<BR> E. एक and क्षीर milk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=139-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकगुरु|एकगुरुः
एकगुरु m. (-रुः) A spiritual brother, pupil of the same preceptor.<BR> E. एक<BR>and गुरु a religious preceptor; also with कन् added एकगुरुक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=139-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकग्रामीण
एकग्रामीण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Of the same town or village.<BR> E. एक one,<BR>ग्रामीण villager.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=139-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकचक्र|एकचक्रं|एकचक्रः
एकचक्र m. (-क्रः) The name of a city: see हरिगृह.<BR> E. एक, चक्र a circle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=139-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकचर|एकचरः
एकचर mfn. (-रः-रा-री-रं)<BR>	 1. Solitary, alone.<BR>	 2. Having one follower.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-रः) A rhinoceros.<BR> E. एक alone, and चर who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=139-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकचारिन्
एकचारिन् mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि) Going alone or with one follower only.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-री) A follower of BUDDHA.<BR> E. एक one, चर् to go, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=139-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकचित्त
एकचित्त mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं)<BR>	 1. Thinking of one thing only, intent upon,<BR>absorbed in.<BR>	 2. Of one mind, agreeing, concurring.<BR> E. एक one, चित्त<BR>the mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=139-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकजन्मन्
एकजन्मन् m. (-न्मा)<BR>	 1. A king, a sovereign.<BR>	 2. A Śūdra.<BR> E. एक best or one,<BR>जन्मन् birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=140-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकजात
एकजात mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Of one parentage, born of the same parents. E.<BR>एक and जात born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=140-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकजाति|एकजातिः
एकजाति mfn. (-तिः-तिः-ति)<BR>	 1. Of the same caste.<BR>	 2. Once born.<BR>	 m. (-तः)<BR>A Śūdra.<BR> E. एक one, and जाति birth or caste: not being regenerat-<BR>ed by investiture, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=140-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकज्या
एकज्या f. (-ज्या)<BR>	 1. The chord of an arc.<BR>	 2. Sine of 30° or of the radius.<BR>E. एक and ज्या a cord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=140-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकतम|एकतमः
एकतम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं) One of many.<BR> E. एक and डतमच् affix of the<BR>superlative.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=140-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकतर|एकतरः
एकतर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>	 1. Either, one of two.<BR>	 2. Other, different.<BR> E. एक<BR>and डतरच् affix of the comparative.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=140-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकतस्
एकतस् ind. On one side, on one part.<BR> E. एक and तसिल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=140-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकता
एकता f. (-ता) Unity, oneness.<BR> E. एक and तल् affix. or with त्व aff. एकत्व n. (-त्वं)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=140-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकतान|एकतानः
एकतान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Closely attentive, having the mind fixed on one<BR>only object.<BR>	 m. (-नः) Musical unison: see the next.<BR> E. एक, तन् to<BR>stretch or spread, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=140-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकताल|एकतालः
एकताल m. (-लः) Harmony, unison, the accurate adjustment of song,<BR>dance, and instrumental music.<BR>	 f. (-ली) An instrument for beating<BR>time, any instrument having but one note.<BR> E. एक one, uniform,<BR>and ताल musical measure or time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=140-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकतीर्थिन्
एकतीर्थिन् m. (-र्थी) A spiritual brother, an associate in religious offices<BR>or objects.<BR> E. एक one, the same, तीर्थ place of pilgrimage, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=140-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकत्र
एकत्र ind. Together, in one, in one place.<BR> E. एक and त्रल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=140-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकदंष्ट्र|एकदंष्ट्रः
एकदंष्ट्र m. (-ष्ट्रः) A name of GANESA.<BR> E. एक and दंष्ट्र a tooth, single<BR>toothed or tusked; the fellow being broken off in a scuffle by<BR>KARTIKEYA, or according to another legend by PARSURAMA; also<BR>एकदन्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=140-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकदन्त|एकदंत|एकदन्तः
एकदन्त m. (-न्तः) A name of GANESA: see the preceding.<BR> E. एक and दन्त a tooth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=140-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकदा
एकदा ind. At the same time, at once.<BR> E. एक and दाच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=140-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकदुःखसुख
एकदुःखसुख mfn. (-खः-खा-खं) Sympathizing, having the same joys and<BR>sorrows.<BR> E. एक, and दुःख pain, सुख pleasure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=140-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकदृश्
एकदृश् mfn. (-दृक्) One-eyed.<BR>	 m. (-दृक्)<BR>	 1. A name of MAHADEVA.<BR>	 2. A<BR>crow.<BR> E. एक and दृश् an eye: ŚIVA is termed one-eyed, from the eye<BR>in his forehead.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=140-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकदेश|एकदेशः
एकदेश m. (-शः) A part, a portion, a division.<BR> E. एक and देश place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=140-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकदेह|एकदेहः
एकदेह mfn. (-हः-हा-हं)<BR>	 1. Elegatnly formed.<BR>	 2. Single bodied.<BR>	 m. (-हः)<BR>The planet MERCURY.<BR> E. एक best or one, and देह body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=140-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकधा
एकधा ind. In one way.<BR> E. एक and धाच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=140-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकधुर्
एकधुर् f. (-धूः) A particular burthen or conveyance.<BR> E. एक and धुर् a load.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=140-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकधुर|एकधुरः
एकधुर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Cattle for special burthen, fit for but one kind of<BR>labour. E. See एकधुरीण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=140-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकधुरावह|एकधुरावहः
एकधुरावह mfn. (-हः-हा-हं) See the preceding.<BR> E. एक, धुर burthen, and<BR>आवह who bears.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=140-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकधुरीण|एकधुरीणः
एकधुरीण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Cattle of special burthen.<BR> E. एक, धुर a burthen,<BR>ख affix which leaves ईण, or with अ affix forming एकधुर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=140-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकनट|एकनटः
एकनट m. (-टः) The principal actor in a drama, the manager.<BR> E. एक<BR>chief, and नट an actor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=140-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकनाथ|एकनाथः
एकनाथ mfn. (-थः-था-थं) Having one master.<BR>	 m. (-थः) Sole master or lord.<BR>E. एक and नाथ lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=140-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकपक्ष|एकपक्षः
एकपक्ष mfn. (-क्षः-क्षा-क्षं) An associate, a firm ally or partizan.<BR> E. एक one,<BR>पक्ष part: of the same side or party.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=140-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकपत्नी
एकपत्नी f. (-त्नी)<BR>	 1. A faithful wife, one devoted to her husband.<BR>	 2. The<BR>wife of a man who has no other wives.<BR> E. एक one or excellent, पति<BR>a husband, न substituted for the final, and ङीप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=140-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकपत्रिका
एकपत्रिका f. (-का) A plant, white basil,<BR> E. एक end, पत्र a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=140-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकपद|एकपदं|एकपदः
एकपद adv.<BR>	 n. (-दं) Then, at that time, at once.<BR>	 m. (-दः) A single inflec-<BR>tion of a verb or noun.<BR>	 f. (-दी) A road, a path or way.<BR> E. एक one,<BR>पद a foot, fem. affix ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=140-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकपरि
एकपरि ind. One over, a term at dice.<BR> E. एक and परि over, against.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=140-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकपात
एकपात mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Sudden, rapid, coming suddenly or at once. E.<BR>एक and पात falling upon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=140-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकपाद्
एकपाद् m. (-त्) A name of ŚIVA.<BR> E. एक best, and पाद् a ray.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=140-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकपिङ्ग|एकपिंग|एकपिङ्गः
एकपिङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः) A name of KUVERA.<BR> E. एक one, and पिङ्ग tawny: hav-<BR>ing a yellow mark in the place of one of his eyes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=140-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकपिङ्गल|एकपिंगल|एकपिङ्गलः
एकपिङ्गल m. (-लः) See the preceding. E. As before.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=140-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकपिण्ड|एकपिंड
एकपिण्ड mfn. (-ण्डः-ण्डा-ण्डं) Related, near of kin, united by the offering<BR>of the funeral cake.<BR> E. एक and पिण्ड a funeral cake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=140-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकपिण्डता
एकपिण्डता f. (-ता) Connexion by the funeral cake, consanguinity.<BR> E. एक-<BR>पिण्ड and तल् affix; also with त्व, एकपिण्डत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=140-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकफल
एकफल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Having one or a principal result or object. E.<BR>एक and फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=140-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकभक्त
एकभक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>	 1. Attached to a common master.<BR>	 2. Wor-<BR>shipping one deity.<BR>	 3. Eating together.<BR>	 4. Eating but one meal,<BR>(a day.)<BR> E. एक and भक्त attached to, or भक्त food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=140-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकभक्तव्रत|एकभक्तव्रतं
एकभक्तव्रत n. (-तं) Eating but once a day as a religious obligation.<BR> E. एक,<BR>भक्त food, व्रत vow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=140-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकभक्ति
एकभक्ति mfn. (-क्तिः-क्तिः-क्ति)<BR>	 1. Of one faith.<BR>	 2. Believing in one deity. E.<BR>एक and भक्ति faith.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=140-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकभाव|एकभावः
एकभाव mfn. (-वः-वा-वं) Of a simple or single nature or temperament. E.<BR>एक and भाव disposition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=140-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकभुक्त
एकभुक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>	 1. Eating but one meal, (a day, &c.)<BR>	 2. Eating<BR>together.<BR> E. एक and भुक्त eaten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=140-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकभोजन
एकभोजन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Eating in common, feeding together.<BR>	 2. Eating one<BR>meal a day, &c.<BR> E. एक and भोजन food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=140-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकमुख
एकमुख mfn. (-खः-खा-खी-खं)<BR>	 1. Having one chief or head.<BR>	 2. Onefaced. E.<BR>एक and मुख the mouth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=140-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकमूला
एकमूला f. (-ला)<BR>	 1. A plant, (Asparagus racemosa.)<BR>	 2. Flax, (Linum.) E.<BR>एक and मूल root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=140-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकयष्टिका
एकयष्टिका f. (-का) A single string of flowers, pearls, &c.<BR> E. एक and<BR>यष्टिका a necklace, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=140-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकयोनि
एकयोनि mfn. (-निः-निः-नि) Uterine, of the same mother.<BR> E. एक and<BR>योनि womb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=140-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकरज|एकरजः
एकरज m. (-जः) A plant, (Verbesina scandens:) see भृङ्गराज.<BR> E. एक excel-<BR>lent, and रजस् farina.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=140-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकरस|एकरसः
एकरस mfn. (-सः-सा-सं) Of one flavour.<BR> E. एक and रस flavour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=140-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकरात्र|एकरात्रः
एकरात्र n. (-त्रं) One night, a night.<BR> E. एक and रात्रि night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=140-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकरात्रिक
एकरात्रिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) For a night, of a night.<BR> E. एक and रात्रि<BR>night, with ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=140-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकराशि|एकराशिः
एकराशि f. (-शिः) A heap, a crowd.<BR> E. एक and राशि a heap.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=140-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकराशिभूत
एकराशिभूत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Heaped or collected together.<BR> E. एकराशि and<BR>भूत become.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=140-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकल|एकलः
एकल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Alone, solitary; a various reading of एकक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=140-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकलिङ्ग|एकलिंग|एकलिङ्गं|एकलिङ्गः
एकलिङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>	 1. A name of KUVERA.<BR>	 2. A place or district in which<BR>for five Cos there is but one Phallus.<BR> E. एक one or best, लिङ्ग a<BR>mark, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=140-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकवद्भाव
एकवद्भाव m. (-वः) An aggregate of many, as in grammar, the formation<BR>of a compound noun of several nouns.<BR> E. एक, वत् like, भाव<BR>property.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=140-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकवर्ण|एकवर्णः
एकवर्ण mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-र्णं)<BR>	 1. Of one caste or tribe.<BR>	 2. Of one colour.<BR>	 3.<BR>Of one quality.<BR>	 m. (-र्णः) One unknown quantity, (in algebra.)<BR>	 f.<BR>(-र्णी) Beating time, marking musical measure by clapping the<BR>hands, or the instrument which does so, a castanet: see एकताली.<BR>E. एक, वर्ण a quality, a note, and ङीष् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=140-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकवर्णसमीकरण
एकवर्णसमीकरण n. (-णं) Uniliteral equation.<BR> E. एकवर्ण and समीकरण equation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=140-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकवर्षिका
एकवर्षिका f. (-का) A heifer one year old.<BR> E. एक, वर्ष a year, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=140-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकवाद|एकवादः
एकवाद m. (-दः) A musical instrument, a kind of drum or tabor.<BR> E. एक<BR>principal, वाद sound: high-sounding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=140-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकवीर|एकवीरः
एकवीर m. (-रः) A chief warrior.<BR> E. एक and वीर a hero.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=140-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकवृक्ष|एकवृक्षः
एकवृक्ष m. (-क्षः) A desert-place, in which but one tree is seen for four<BR>Cos.<BR> E. एक and वृक्ष a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=141-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकवेणी
एकवेणी f. (-णी)<BR>	 1. A single braid of hair.<BR>	 2. A woman whose hair is tied<BR>in one braid.<BR> E. एक and वेणी a tress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=141-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकशफ|एकशफः
एकशफ m. (-फः)<BR>	 1. A horse.<BR>	 2. Any animal whose hoof is not cloven. E.<BR>एक one, uniform, and शफ a hoof.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=141-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकशरण
एकशरण n. (-णं) One only hope or refuge, especially applied to a deity.<BR>E. एक and शरण protection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=141-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकशरीर
एकशरीर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>	 1. Consanguineous, of one body or blood.<BR>	 2.<BR>Of one or the same body.<BR> E. एक, शरीर body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=141-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकशरीरान्वय
एकशरीरान्वय m. (-यः) Consanguineous descent.<BR> E. एकशरीर and अन्वय<BR>lineage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=141-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकशरीरारम्भ
एकशरीरारम्भ m. (-म्भः) Commencement of consanguinity by the union of<BR>father and mother.<BR> E. एकशरीर and आरम्भ beginning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=141-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकशरीरावयव
एकशरीरावयव m. (-वः) A descendant in a right line, a kinsman by blood.<BR>E. एकशरीर and अवयव a member.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=141-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकशरीरावयवत्व
एकशरीरावयवत्व n. (-त्वं) Consanguineous descent or connexion.<BR> E. त्व<BR>added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=141-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकशाख|एकशाखः
एकशाख m. (-खः) A Brahman of the same branch or school.<BR> E. एक and<BR>शाखा a branch, (of the Vedas.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=141-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकशृङ्ग|एकशृंग|एकशृङ्गः
एकशृङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>	 1. A title of VIṢṆU or KṚṢṆA.<BR>	 2. A unicorn, a<BR>rhinoceros, &c.<BR> E. एक and शृङ्ग a mark or horn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=141-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकसर्ग|एकसर्गः
एकसर्ग mfn. (-र्गः-र्गा-र्गं) Closely attentive, having the mind intent upon<BR>one object.<BR> E. एक one, and सृज् to create, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=141-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकसूत्र|एकसूत्रः
एकसूत्र m. (-त्रः) A small double drum, played by a string and ball at-<BR>tached to the body of it: see वृषाङ्कज.<BR> E. एक and सूत्र a thread.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=141-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकसूनु
एकसूनु m. (-नुः) An only son.<BR> E. एक, and सूनु a son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=141-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकस्थ
एकस्थ mfn. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थं) Collected, assembled, conjoined, in one site or<BR>place.<BR> E. एक and स्थ what stays.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=141-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकस्थान
एकस्थान n. (-नं) One place, the same place.<BR> E. एक and स्थान place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=141-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकहायनी
एकहायनी f. (-नी) A heifer one year old.<BR> E. एक, हायन a year, affix ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=141-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकाकिन्
एकाकिन् mfn. (-की-किनी-कि) Alone, solitary.<BR> E. एक and आकिनिच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=141-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकाक्ष|एकाक्षः
एकाक्ष mfn. (-क्षः-क्षा-क्षं) One-eyed.<BR>	 m. (-क्षः) A crow.<BR> E. एक and अक्षि an<BR>eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=141-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकाक्षर
एकाक्षर n. (-रं) A monosyllable, especially the sacred monosyllable Om.<BR>E. एक and अक्षर a letter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=141-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकाग्र|एकाग्रः
एकाग्र mfn. (-ग्रः-ग्रा-ग्रं)<BR>	 1. Intent, closely attentive, fixed on one object.<BR>2. Undisturbed, unperplexed.<BR>	 3. Known, celebrated.<BR>	 4. Single-<BR>pointed.<BR>	 m. (-ग्रः) The whole of a long line which is subdivided. E.<BR>एक and अग्र chief, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=141-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकाग्रता
एकाग्रता f. (-ता) Close and undisturbed attention.<BR> E. तल् added to the<BR>preceding; also with त्व, एकाग्रत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=141-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकाग्र्य|एकाग्र्यः
एकाग्र्य mfn. (-ग्र्यः-ग्र्या-ग्र्यं) Closely attentive: see the preceding. E.<BR>एक, अग्र्य chief, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=141-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकाङ्ग|एकांग|एकाङ्गं|एकाङ्गः
एकाङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः) The planet MERCURY.<BR>	 n. (-ङ्गं) Sandal.<BR> E. एक best, pre-<BR>eminent, and अङ्ग body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=141-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकादश
एकादश mfn. (-शः-शी-शं) Eleven, eleventh.<BR>	 f. (-शी) The eleventh day of<BR>the half month: it is especially sacred to VIṢṆU and fasting on<BR>it is most efficacious.<BR> E. एकादशन् eleven, affix ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=141-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकादशन्
एकादशन् plur.<BR>	 mfn. (-श) Eleven.<BR> E. एक one, दशन् ten, with आङ्<BR>inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=141-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकानंशा
एकानंशा f. (-शा) A name of PĀRVATĪ.<BR> E. अंश a part, with the neg.<BR>pref. and एक pre-eminent: chief and undivided.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=141-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकानुदिष्ट
एकानुदिष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं) Left, as a funeral feast, one who has recent-<BR>ly partaken of it.<BR> E. एक one, (ancestor,) अनु after, दिष्ट shown.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=141-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकान्त|एकान्तं|एकान्तः
एकान्त mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं)<BR>	 1. Excessive.<BR>	 2. Solitary, lonely, retired.<BR>	 3.<BR>Aside, apart. adv.<BR>	 n. (-न्तं)<BR>	 1. Much, excessive.<BR>	 2. Apart.<BR> E. एक one<BR>and अन्त end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=141-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकान्तकरुण
एकान्तकरुण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Very compassionate, weakly charitable. E.<BR>एकान्त and करुण charitable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=141-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकान्ततस्
एकान्ततस् ind.<BR>	 1. Alone, apart, privately.<BR>	 2. Much, exceedingly. E.<BR>एकान्त and तसिल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=141-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकान्तर|एकान्तरः
एकान्तर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Next but one.<BR> E. एक and अन्तर between.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=141-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकान्तस्थित
एकान्तस्थित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Staying alone or apart.<BR> E. एकान्त and स्थित<BR>staying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=141-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकाब्दा
एकाब्दा f. (-ब्दा) A heifer one year old.<BR> E. एक and अब्द a year.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=141-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकायन|एकायनः
एकायन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Closely attentive, intent.<BR> E. एक, अयन going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=141-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकायनगत|एकायनगतः
एकायनगत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) See the preceding.<BR> E. एकायन and गत being,<BR>having gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=141-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकावली
एकावली f. (-ली) A single string of beads, flowers, &c.<BR> E. एक and आवली a row.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=141-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकार्थ|एकार्थः
एकार्थ mfn. (-र्थः-र्था-र्थं)<BR>	 1. Having one sense or meaning.<BR>	 2. Having one<BR>or the same object.<BR> E. एक and अर्थ meaning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=141-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकाश्रितगुण|एकाश्रितगुणः
एकाश्रितगुण m. (-णः) A simple attribute or predicate, as form, taste,<BR>smell, &c.<BR> E. एक one, आश्रित invested, गुण property.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=141-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकाष्टी
एकाष्टी f. (-ष्टी) A pod or seed of cotton.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=141-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकाष्टील
एकाष्टील m. (-लः) A plant: see वकपुष्प; the flowers are sacred to ŚIVA.<BR>f. (-ली) A medicinal plant, (Cissampelos hexandra.)<BR> E. एक best,<BR>अष्टि seed, and ल what gives or takes, from ला with क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=141-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकाह|एकाहः
एकाह n. (-हं) The period of one day.<BR> E. एक and अहन् a day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=141-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकाहगम
एकाहगम m. (-मः) A day's journey.<BR> E. एकाह and गम going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=141-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकीभाव|एकीभावः
एकीभाव m. (-वः) Common nature or property.<BR> E. एक with च्वि augment,<BR>and भाव nature.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=141-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकीय|एकीयः
एकीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) A companion, a partizan or associate.<BR> E. एक one,<BR>and छण् affix. also एकपक्ष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=141-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकैक
एकैक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Single, one by one<BR> E. एक repeated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=141-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकैकशस्
एकैकशस् ind. One by one, severally, seriatim.<BR> E. एक repeated, with<BR>शसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=141-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकोद्दिष्ट|एकोद्दिष्टं
एकोद्दिष्ट n. (-ष्टं) The Sraddha or funeral rite offered to one person<BR>only.<BR> E. एक and उद्दिष्ट addressed to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=141-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकोशिका
एकोशिका f. (-का) A plant, (Cissampelos hexandra:) see एकाष्टील.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=141-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकौघभूत
एकौघभूत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Heaped, crowded together.<BR> E. एक one, ओघ<BR>quantity, भूत become.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=141-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एज
एज r. 1st cl. (ऋ) (एजृ) (एजते) To shine. (एजति) To shake or tremble.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=141-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एजन|एजनं
एजन n. (-नं) Shaking, trembling.<BR> E. एज् and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=141-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एजयत्
एजयत् mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्) Causing to shake or tremble.<BR> E. एज् to shake,<BR>causal form, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=141-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एजित
एजित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Shaken, trembling.<BR> E. एज् to shake, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=141-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एजितव्य
एजितव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं) To be shaken.<BR> E. एज and तव्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=141-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एजितृ
एजितृ mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ) Shaking, trembling.<BR> E. एज् and तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=141-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एठ
एठ r. 1st cl. (एठते) To annoy, to resist or oppose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=141-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एड|एडः
एड mfn. (-डः-डा-डं) Deaf.<BR> E. ईड् to praise, आङ् prefixed, अच् or घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=141-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एडक|एडकः
एडक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A ram.<BR>	 2. A wild goat.<BR>	 f. (-का) A ewe.<BR> E. ईल् to go,<BR>ण्वुल् affix; and ल changed to ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=141-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एडगज|एडगजः
एडगज m. (-जः) A medicinal plant, used for the cure of ring-worms,<BR>(Cassia tora.)<BR> E. एड a sheep, गज to sound, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=141-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एडमूक|एडमूकः
एडमूक mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>	 1. Deaf and dumb.<BR>	 2. Wicked, perverse.<BR> E. एड<BR>deaf, and मूक dumb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=141-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एडुक|एडुकं|एडुकः
एडुक n. (-कं)<BR>	 1. A building constructed of rubbish, bones, &c.<BR>	 2. A<BR>wall enclosing bones, a tomb, &c.<BR>	 3. A building of hard subs-<BR>tances resembling bones.<BR> E. ईड to throw or send, deriv. irr.; also<BR>एडूक and एडोक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=141-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एण|एणः
एण mf. (-णः-णी) A kind of deer or antelope, described as being of a<BR>black colour, with beautiful eyes, and short legs.<BR> E. इण् to go,<BR>ण aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=141-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एणक|एणकः
एणक m. (-कः) A species of deer or antelope: see the preceding.<BR> E. कन्<BR>added to एण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=141-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एणतिलक|एणतिलकः
एणतिलक m. (-कः) The moon.<BR> E. एण an antelope, and तिलक the secta-<BR>rial mark; a deer being fancifully visible in the moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=141-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एणभृत्
एणभृत् m. (-त्) The moon.<BR> E. एण and भृत् who nourishes: see the<BR>preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=141-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एणाजिन
एणाजिन n. (-नं) A deer-skin.<BR> E. एण and अजिन the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=142-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एत|एतं|एतः
एत mfn. (-तः-ता or -ती-तं) Of a variegated colour. (-तः-ता-तं) Arrived,<BR>come.<BR>	 m. (-तः)<BR>	 1. A deer or antelope.<BR>	 2. A variegated colour.<BR> E. इण्<BR>to go, तन् affix; when signifying colour, the fem. affix is either<BR>टाप् or ङीप्, and before the latter, त is changed to न.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=142-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एतद्
एतद् pron.<BR>	 mfn. (एषः एषा एतद् or एतत्) This.<BR> E. एत derived from इण् to<BR>go, and तद् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=142-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एतन|एतनः
एतन m. (-नः) Expiration, breathing out, discharging air from the<BR>lungs.<BR> E. इण् to go, तनन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=142-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एतर्हि
एतर्हि ind. Now, at this time.<BR> E. एत substituted for इदम्. and र्हिल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=142-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एतश|एतशः
एतश m. (-शः) A Brahman.<BR> E. इण् to go, and तश Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=142-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एतशस्
एतशस् m. (-शाः) A Brahman or man of the first class.<BR> E. इण् to go, तशस् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=142-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एतादृश्
एतादृश् mfn. (-दृक्) Such, such like.<BR> E. एतद् this. दृश् to see, क्विप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=142-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एतादृश
एतादृश mfn. (-शः-शी-शं) Such, such like.<BR> E. एतद् this, दृश् to see, कञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=142-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एतावत्|एतावन्त्
एतावत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) So many, so much, so far. ind. (-वत्) So far,<BR>thus far, so much, &c.<BR> E. एतद्, and मतुप् or वति aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=142-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एत्य
एत्य ind. Having gone to or approached.<BR> E. इण् to go, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=142-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एध|एधः
एध r. 1st cl. (एधते) To grow or increase.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=142-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एध|एधः
एध m. (-धः) Fuel, as wood, grass, &c.<BR> E. एध् to increase, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=142-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एधतु|एधतुः
एधतु mfn. (-तुः-तुः-तु) Increased, grown.<BR>	 m. (-तुः)<BR>	 1. Man.<BR>	 2. Fire.<BR> E. एध्<BR>to increase, तु Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=142-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एधनीय
एधनीय mfn. (-तः-या-यं) To be enlarged or increased.<BR> E. एध् to grow, and<BR>अनीयर् affix; also एधितव्य and एध्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=142-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एधस्
एधस् n. (-धः) Fuel: see एध.<BR> E. एध् to grow, Unādi affix असुन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=142-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एधित|एधितः
एधित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Increased, grown.<BR> E. एध् to increase, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=142-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एधितृ
एधितृ mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ) Increasing, growing, enlarging.<BR> E. एध् to grow,<BR>and तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=142-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एनस्
एनस् n. (एनः)<BR>	 1. Sin, fault, offence.<BR>	 2. Censure, blame.<BR> E. इण् to go,<BR>असुन् Unādi affix, and नुम् inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=142-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एनस्विन्
एनस्विन् mfn. (-स्वी-स्विनी-स्वि) Sinful, a sinner.<BR> E. एनस् and विनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=142-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एरका
एरका f. (-का) A sort of grass of emollient and diluent properties.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=142-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एरङ्ग|एरंगः|एरङ्गः
एरङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः) A kind of fish; also एलङ्ग.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=142-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एरण्ड|एरंडः|एरण्डः
एरण्ड m. (-ण्डः) The castor-oil plant, (Palma christi or Ricinus com-<BR>munis. )<BR>	 f. (-ण्डी) Long pepper.<BR> E. इर् to go, &c. आङ् prefixed, अण्डच्<BR>affix, fem. affix ङीष्; also with कन् added एरण्डक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=142-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एरण्डक|एरंडकः|एरण्डकः
एरण्डक m. (-कः) Palma christi: see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=142-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एरण्डपत्रिका
एरण्डपत्रिका f. (-का) A plant, commonly Danti.<BR> E. एरण्ड, and पत्र leaf,<BR>having similar leaves.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=142-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एरण्डफला
एरण्डफला f. (-ला) A plant: see the preceding.<BR> E. एरण्ड, and फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=142-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एर्वारु|एर्वारुः|एर्व्वारुः
एर्वारु m. (-रुः) A kind of cucumber, (Cucumis utilatissimus.) E. See<BR>ईर्व्वारु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=142-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एलक|एलकः
एलक m. (-कः) A ram: see एडक.<BR> E. ड and ल being interchanged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=142-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एलङ्ग|एलंगः|एलङ्गः
एलङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः) A sort of fish, (Cyprinus marginatus, BUCH.) Also एरङ्ग.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=142-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एलवालु
एलवालु n. (-लु) The name of a perfume: see the next word.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=142-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एलवालुक
एलवालुक n. (-कं) A granular substance apparently vegetable, of a red-<BR>dish brown colour, and used as a drug and as a perfume.<BR> E. एला<BR>cardamoms, वल् to breathe, उण् affix, and कन् added, or without<BR>कन्, एलवालु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=142-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एलविल|एलविलः
एलविल m. (-लः) A name of KUVERA: see ऐलविल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=142-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एला
एला f. (-ला) Cardamoms, the seed of the Eletteria cardamomum, or<BR>Alpinia Cardamomum: it applies to both the large and small<BR>cardamom, but most commonly to the former.<BR> E. इल् to send, &c.<BR>अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=142-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एलापत्र|एलापत्रः
एलापत्र m. (-त्रः) One of the chiefs of the Nagas or serpent-race.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=142-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एलापर्णी|एलापर्ण्णी
एलापर्णी f. (-र्णी) A plant, (Mimosa octandra.)<BR> E. एला cardamoms, and<BR>पर्ण a leaf, ङीष् fem. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=142-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एलीका
एलीका f. (-का) Small cardamoms.<BR> E. एला, and ईकन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=142-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एव|एवं|एवः
एव mfn. (एवः एवा एवं) Going, moving. ind. As, like, &c.: see एवम्.<BR> E. इण्<BR>to go, Uṇādi affix वन्: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=142-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एवम्
एवम् ind. A particle implying, 1. Likeness, (as, so, like.)<BR>	 2. Assent,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=142-b" target="_blank">Page142-b+ 55</a>]<BR>(yes, verily.)<BR>	 3. Sameness of manner, (thus, in this way.)<BR>	 4.<BR>Certainly, (indeed, assuredly, even so.)<BR>	 5. Command, (so, thus,<BR>&c.)<BR>	 6. An expletive.<BR> E. इण् to go, वम् affix; also एव.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=142-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एवम्भूत|एवंभूत
एवम्भूत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) So such, in such manner.<BR> E. एवम्, and भूत been.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=142-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एवम्विध
एवम्विध mfn. (-धः-धा-धं) Such, in such form or manner, of such a kind<BR>E. एवम्, and विध sort, way.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=142-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एष|एषः
एष r. 1st. cl. (ऋ) एषृ (एषते) To go or approach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=142-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एषण|एषणः
एषण m. (-णः) An iron arrow.<BR>	 f. (-णी)<BR>	 1. A goldsmith's balance, assay<BR>scales.<BR>	 2. An iron or steel probe.<BR> E. एष् to go, ल्युट् and ङीष् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=142-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एषणिका
एषणिका f. (-का) A goldsmith's balance. E. As before, with कन् and टाप्<BR>added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=142-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एषणीय
एषणीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>	 1. To be desired, desirable.<BR>	 2. To be aimed at.<BR>E. इष् to wish, affix अनीयर्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=142-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एषा
एषा f. (-षा) Desire.<BR> E. इष् to wish, अङ् and टाप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=142-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एषितृ
एषितृ mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ) Wishing, desirous.<BR> E. इष् to wish, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=142-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एष्टृ
एष्टृ mfn. (-ष्टा-ष्ट्री-ष्टृ) Wishing, desirous.<BR> E. इष् to wish, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=142-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐ
ऐ The twelfth vowel of the Nagari alphabet, or more properly a<BR>diphthong; corresponding in sound to Ei in height.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=142-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐ
ऐ ind. An interjection of, 1. Remembering, (aye, ha)<BR>	 2. Calling,<BR>summoning, (hola, ho, heigh.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=142-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐ
ऐ m. (ऐः) A name of ŚIVA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=142-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐकध्य|ऐकध्यं
ऐकध्य n. (-ध्यं) Singleness of time or occurrence.<BR> E. एक, and ध्यमुञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=142-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐकमत्य|ऐकमत्यं
ऐकमत्य n. (-त्यं) Consent, concurrence, sameness of doctrine or opinion.<BR>E. एक one, मत minded, ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=142-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐकशफ
ऐकशफ mfn. (-फः-फा-फं) Produced by or belonging to animals with<BR>single hoofs.<BR> E. एकशफ, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=142-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐकागारिक|ऐकागारिकः
ऐकागारिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>	 1. A thief, a robber.<BR>	 2. The possessor of one<BR>residence.<BR> E. एक one, अगार a house, affix ठक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=142-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐकाग्र्य|ऐकाग्र्यं
ऐकाग्र्य n. (-ग्र्यं) Intentness on one object.<BR> E. एकाग्र, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=142-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐकान्यिक|ऐकान्यिकः
ऐकान्यिक m. (-कः) One who commits a single error in reading.<BR> E. एक<BR>and अन्य other, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=142-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐकाहिक|ऐकाहिकं
ऐकाहिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Ephemeral, quotidian, of one day, of the<BR>same day.<BR> E. एक and अहन् a day, ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=142-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐक्य|ऐक्यं
ऐक्य n. (-क्यं)<BR>	 1. Unity, oneness.<BR>	 2. A whole of various parts, an aggre-<BR>gate, a total.<BR> E. एक, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=142-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐक्षव|ऐक्षवं
ऐक्षव mfn. (-वः-वी-वं) Sugar, sugary, produced from or relating to the<BR>sugar-cane.<BR> E. इक्षु sugar-cane, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=142-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐक्षुक|ऐक्षुकः
ऐक्षुक m. (-कः) A carrier of sugar-canes.<BR> E. इक्षु, and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=142-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐक्षुभारिक
ऐक्षुभारिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Carrying sugar-canes.<BR> E. इक्षु, and भार a load,<BR>ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=142-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐक्ष्वाक|ऐक्ष्वाकः
ऐक्ष्वाक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Of the family of IKSHWAKU.<BR> E. ईक्ष्वाकु, and अञ्<BR>affix, the final rejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=142-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐक्ष्वाकव
ऐक्ष्वाकव mfn. (-वः-वी-वं) Of the family of IKSHWAKU.<BR> E. ईक्ष्वाकु, and<BR>अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=142-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐङ्गुद|ऐंगुद|ऐङ्गुदं
ऐङ्गुद n. (-दं) The fruit of the plant called Inguda.<BR> E. इङ्गुद the plant,<BR>affix अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=142-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐच्छिक
ऐच्छिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Optional, voluntary, at will.<BR> E. इच्छा wish, ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=142-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐडुक|ऐडुकं
ऐडुक n. (-कं) A wall, &c. of bones and rubbish: see एडुक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=142-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐण|ऐणं
ऐण mfn. (-णः-णी-णं) Belonging to a male antelope.<BR> E. एण an antelope,<BR>अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=142-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐणिक|ऐणिकः
ऐणिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Belonging to a deer, &c.<BR>	 m. (-कः) A hunter, a<BR>deer-killer.<BR> E. एण, and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=142-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐणेय|ऐणेयं|ऐणेयः
ऐणेय mfn. (-यः-यी-यं) Appertaining to a doe or the female antelope. E.<BR>एणी a doe, affix ढक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=142-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐतरेयोपनिषद्
ऐतरेयोपनिषद् f. (-षद् or -षत्) One of the Upanishads of the Vedas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=143-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐतिहासिक|ऐतिहासिकः
ऐतिहासिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Historical.<BR>	 m. (-कः) A historian.<BR> E. इतिहास<BR>a story, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=143-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐतिह्य|ऐतिह्यं
ऐतिह्य n. (-ह्यं) Traditional instruction.<BR> E. इतिहा tradition, ञ्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=143-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐन्दव|ऐंदव|ऐन्दवं|ऐन्दवः
ऐन्दव mfn. (-वः-वी-वं) Lunar.<BR>	 n. (-वं) The asterism Mrigasiras.<BR>	 f. (-वी) A<BR>plant, (Serratula anthelmintica.)<BR> E. इन्दु the moon, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=143-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐन्द्र|ऐंद्र|ऐन्द्रं|ऐन्द्रः
ऐन्द्र mfn. (-न्द्रः-न्द्रा-न्द्रं) Sacred, or relating to the god INDRA.<BR>	 m. (-न्द्रः)<BR>1. A name of the monkey king BALI.<BR>	 2. A name of ARJUNA.<BR>	 f.<BR>(-न्द्री)<BR>	 1. The wife of INDRA.<BR>	 2. The goddess DURGĀ.<BR>	 3. Misfortune,<BR>misery, (personified.)<BR>	 4. The name of a plant, a kind of cucumber,<BR>(Cucumis madraspatanus.)<BR>	 5. The constellation Jyeṣṭha.<BR>	 6. The<BR>east quarter, of which INDRA is regent.<BR> E. इन्द्र, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=143-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐन्द्रजालिक|ऐंद्रजालिक|ऐन्द्रजालिकः
ऐन्द्रजालिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Deceptive, illusory.<BR>	 m. (-कः) A juggler. E.<BR>इन्द्रजाल Deception, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=143-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐन्द्रलुप्तिक|ऐंद्रलुप्तिक|ऐन्द्रलुप्तिकः
ऐन्द्रलुप्तिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Afflicted with falling of the hair or morbid<BR>baldness.<BR> E. इन्द्रलुप्त falling of the hair, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=143-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐन्द्राग्न|ऐंद्राग्न
ऐन्द्राग्न m. (-ग्नः) A ceremony, &c. addressed to INDRA and AGNI.<BR> E. इन्द्र,<BR>and अग्नि, with अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=143-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐन्द्रायुध
ऐन्द्रायुध mfn. (-धः-धा-धं) Relating to INDRA'S bow or the rainbow. E.<BR>इन्द्रायुध, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=143-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐन्द्रावरुण
ऐन्द्रावरुण mfn. (-णः-णी-णं) Sacred to INDRA and VARUṆA.<BR> E. इन्द्र, and<BR>वरुण with अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=143-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐन्द्रि|ऐंद्रिः|ऐन्द्रिः
ऐन्द्रि m. (-न्द्रिः)<BR>	 1. The patronymick of JAYANTA the son of INDRA.<BR>	 2.<BR>A name of the monkey BALI.<BR>	 3. A name of ARJUNA.<BR>	 4. A crow.<BR>E. इन्द्र, इञ् patronymick aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=143-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐन्द्रियक|ऐंद्रियक|ऐन्द्रियकं
ऐन्द्रियक mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>	 1. Perceptible, perceived, present.<BR>	 2. Of or<BR>belonging to the sense.<BR> E. इन्द्रिय an organ of sense, and वुञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=143-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐरावण|ऐरावणः
ऐरावण m. (-णः) INDRA'S elephant.<BR> E. इरावत् the ocean, अण् affix of<BR>descent; ocean-born: न is changed irregularly to ण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=143-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐरावत|ऐरावतं|ऐरावतः
ऐरावत m. (-तः)<BR>	 1. INDRA'S elephant.<BR>	 2. The same, considered as the<BR>elephant of the north quarter.<BR>	 3. An orange.<BR>	 4. A fruit, (Arto-<BR>carpus lacucha.)<BR>	 5. A serpent, one of the chiefs of the Naga or<BR>serpent race, inhabiting the infernal regions.<BR>	 f. (-ती)<BR>	 1. Lightning.<BR>2. A particular kind of it.<BR>	 3. The female of INDRA'S elephant.<BR>	 4.<BR>The Ravi river in the Panjab.<BR>	 n. (-तं) INDRA'S bow unbent, the<BR>rainbow.<BR> E. इरावत् water-having; that is, the ocean, a cloud, &c.<BR>अण् affix implying origin or descent; born from the ocean, (the<BR>elephant,) proceeding from watery clouds, (lightning, &c.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=143-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐरिण|ऐरिणं
ऐरिण n. (-णं) Fossil or rock salt.<BR> E. इरिन् earthly, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=143-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐरेय|ऐरेयं
ऐरेय n. (-यं) A spirituous liquor.<BR> E. इरा wine, ढक् affix: see मैरेय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=143-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐल|ऐलः
ऐल m. (-लः) The name of a king, also PURURAVA.<BR> E. इला the wife of<BR>BUDDHA, अण् patronymick affix; the son of ILA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=143-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐलवालुक|ऐलवालुकः
ऐलवालुक n. (-कं) A perfume: see एलवालुक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=143-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐलविल|ऐलविलः
ऐलविल m. (-लः) A title of KUVERA.<BR> E. इलविला the wife of PULASTYA,<BR>and the paternal grand-mother of the deity, affix अण्; also ऐड-<BR>विल, ऐडविड, एलविल, &c. ल and ड being interchanged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=143-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐलेय|ऐलेयं|ऐलेयः
ऐलेय n. (-यं) A perfume: see एलवालुक.<BR> E. एला cardamoms, ढक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=143-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐश
ऐश mfn. (-शः-शी-शं)<BR>	 1. Divine.<BR>	 2. Regal.<BR> E. ईश, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=143-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐशानी
ऐशानी f. (-नी) The north-east quarter.<BR> E. ईशान ŚIVA, as regent of the<BR>north-east, अण् and ङीष् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=143-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐशिक|ऐशिकः
ऐशिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>	 1. Divine, heavenly.<BR>	 2. Regal, royal.<BR> E. ईश,<BR>and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=143-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐश्वर
ऐश्वर mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>	 1. Divine, relating to god, &c.<BR>	 2. Royal, supreme.<BR>E. ईश्वर, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=143-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐश्वर्य्य|ऐश्वर्य|ऐश्वर्यं|ऐश्वर्य्यं
ऐश्वर्य्य n. (-र्य्यं)<BR>	 1. Super-human power, the divine faculties of omni-<BR>presence, omnipotence, invisibility, &c.<BR>	 2. Supremacy, dominion,<BR>sway, power, might.<BR> E. ईश्वर a master, a deity, ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=143-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐषमस्
ऐषमस् ind. The present year.<BR> E. इदम् this, समसण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=143-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐषमस्त्य|ऐषमस्त्यः
ऐषमस्त्य mfn. (-स्त्यः-स्त्या-स्त्यं) Of or belonging to the present year. E.<BR>ऐषमस्, and त्यय affix; or with द्यु affix, ऐषमस्तन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=143-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐष्टिक
ऐष्टिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Sacrificial, ceremonial.<BR> E. इष्टि a sacrifice, ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=143-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐष्टिकपौर्त्तिक|ऐष्टिकपौर्तिक
ऐष्टिकपौर्त्तिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Ceremonial and meritorious, (any act,<BR>&c.)<BR> E. इष्टापूर्त्त any pious act, ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=143-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐहलौकिक
ऐहलौकिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Of this world, terrestrial, sublunary. E.<BR>इह here, लोक world, ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=143-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐहिक|ऐहिकं
ऐहिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Worldly, local, of this world, of this place. E.<BR>इह here, and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=143-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओ
ओ The vowel O, and the thirteenth of the Nagari alphabet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=143-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओ
ओ ind.<BR>	 1. A vocative particle, (ho.)<BR>	 2. An interjection of calling, (ho,<BR>hola.)<BR>	 3. Of reminiscence, (ho, ah.)<BR>	 4. Of compassionating,<BR>(ah, oh.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=143-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओ
ओ m. (ओः) BRAHMĀ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=143-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओं
ॐ ind. The mystical monosyllable Om: see ओम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=143-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओक|ओकं|ओकः
ओक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A house.<BR>	 2. An asylum, a refuge: see ओकस्.<BR>	 3. A bird<BR>E. उच् to assemble, क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=143-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओकण|ओकणः
ओकण m. (-णः) A bug; also ओकणि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=143-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओकस्
ओकस् n. (-कः)<BR>	 1. An asylum, a place of refuge.<BR>	 2. A house.<BR> E. उच् to<BR>collect, असुन् Uṇādi affix, च becomes क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=143-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओकुल|ओकुलः
ओकुल m. (-लः) A cake of flour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=143-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओकोदनी
ओकोदनी f. (-नी) A bug.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=143-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओक्कणी
ओक्कणी f. (-णी) A bug.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=143-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओख
ओख r. 1st. cl. (ऋ) ओखृ (ओखति) and with a prefix, as प्र प्रोखति)<BR>	 1. To<BR>dry or arid.<BR>	 2. To adorn.<BR>	 3. To be able or competent, to suffice.<BR>4. To refuse or prevent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=143-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओघ|ओघः
ओघ m. (-घः)<BR>	 1. A heap or quantity, flock or multitude.<BR>	 2. A stream,<BR>a torrent, rapid flow of water, an inundation.<BR>	 3. Quick time in<BR>music.<BR>	 4. Tradition.<BR>	 5. Advice, instruction.<BR> E. उच् to collect, घञ्<BR>affix, and च is changed to घ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=143-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओङ्कार|ओंकार|ओंकारः|ओङ्कारः
ओङ्कार m. (-रः) The mysterious name of the deity: see ओम्.<BR>	 f. (-रा) A<BR>Bauddha Śakti, or female personification of divine energy.<BR> E. ओम्<BR>and कार affix implying a letter, the compound letter ओ; other-<BR>wise ओम्, signifying assent, and कार who makes; what complies<BR>with our wishes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=143-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओज|ओजः
ओज (त) r. 1st. cl. (ओजति)<BR>	 1. To live, to have the vital faculties and<BR>organs.<BR>	 2. To be strong or able.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=143-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओज|ओजः
ओज m. (-जः) See the following.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=143-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओजस्
ओजस् n. (-जः)<BR>	 1. Light, splendor.<BR>	 2. Manifestaion, appearance.<BR>	 3.<BR>Strength.<BR>	 4. Support, stay.<BR>	 5. Metallic lustre.<BR>	 6. Vitality, the<BR>principle of vital warmth and action diffused throughout the<BR>body.<BR>	 7. Virility, the generative faculty.<BR>	 8. A form of style, elabo-<BR>rate style, abounding with compounds.<BR>	 9. (In astrology,) Each<BR>alternate sign of the zodiac, first, third, fifth, &c.<BR> E. ओज to live,<BR>and असुन् affix; or with अच् affix ओज.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=143-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओजस्विन्
ओजस्विन् mfn. (-स्वि-स्विनी-स्वि)<BR>	 1. Mighty, powerful, strong.<BR>	 2. Splendid,<BR>bright.<BR> E. ओजस् and विनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=143-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओडक
ओडक m. (-कः) A musical mode, which omits two of the notes of the<BR>scale, Ri and Pa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=143-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओडिका
ओडिका f. (-का) Wild rice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=143-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओडी
ओडी f. (-डी) Wild rice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=143-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओड्र|ओड्रः
ओड्र m. (-ड्रः)<BR>	 1. The China rose, (Hibiscus mutabilis.)<BR>	 2. The name of<BR>of a country, the northern part of Orissa.<BR> E. उड to embrace, रक<BR>affix, and उ is changed to ओ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=143-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओड्रपुष्प|ओड्रपुष्पं
ओड्रपुष्प n. (-ष्पं) The China rose, the plant or its flower.<BR> E. ओड्र China<BR>rose, and पुष्प a flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=143-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओण
ओण r. 1st cl. (ऋ) ओणृ (ओणति) To remove, to take away or abstract.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=144-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओतु|ओतुः
ओतु m. (-तुः) A cat.<BR> E. अव् to go, &c. and तु Uṇādi affix, the radical is<BR>changed to ओ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=144-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओदन|ओदनं|ओदनः
ओदन mn. (-नः-नं) Boiled rice.<BR>	 f. (-निका-नी) A plant, (Sida cordifolia,<BR>&c.) see वला<BR> E. उन्द् to be wet, ल्युट् Uṇādi affix, and न dropped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=144-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओद्म|ओद्मः
ओद्म m. (-द्मः) Wetting, moistening.<BR> E. उन्द् to be wet, मम् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=144-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओम्
ओम् ind.<BR>	 1. The mystic name of the deity, prefacing all the prayers<BR>and most of the writings of the Hindus.<BR> E. अ a name of VIṢṆU,<BR>उ of ŚIVA, and म of BRAHMĀ; it therefore implies the Indian triad,<BR>and expresses the three in one.<BR>	 2. A particle of command or in-<BR>junction.<BR>	 3. Of assent, (verily, amen.)<BR>	 4. Of auspiciousness.<BR>	 5. Of<BR>removal, (away, hence,) and, 6. It is an inceptive particle.<BR> E. अव्<BR>to go, to preserve, &c. मन् Uṇādi affix, the radical being convert-<BR>ed into ओ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=144-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओल|ओलं|ओलः
ओल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Wet, damp; also ओल्ल.<BR>	 m. (-लः) An esculent root,<BR>(Arum campanulatum.)<BR> E. वल or वल्ल to destroy, (complaints, es-<BR>pecially hœmorrhoids,) अच् affix, व changed to ओ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=144-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओलड
ओलड r. 1st and 10th cls. (इ) ओलडि (ओलण्डति or ओलण्डयति) To dart or<BR>throw up: some consider the initial vowel to be indicatory, and<BR>make the root लडि q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=144-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओष|ओषं|ओषः
ओष m. (-षः) Burning, combustion.<BR> E. उष् to burn, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=144-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओषण|ओषणः
ओषण m. (-णः) Pungency, pungent taste or flavour.<BR>	 f. (-णी) A potherb,<BR>commonly Purya.<BR> E. उष् to burn, and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=144-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओषधि|ओषधिः
ओषधि f. (-धिः) An annual plant or herb, one that dies after becoming<BR>ripe.<BR> E. ओष heat, and धा to have, कि affix; or with ङीष्, ओषधी;<BR>or with इञ् affix, औषधि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=144-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओषधी
ओषधी f. (-धी) An annual plant or deciduous herb: see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=144-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओषधीपति|ओषधीपतिः
ओषधीपति m. (-तिः) The moon.<BR> E. ओषधी and पति lord: presiding over<BR>annual plants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=144-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओषधीश|ओषधीशः
ओषधीश m. (-शः) The moon. E. See the preceding; ईश meaning lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=144-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओष्ठ|ओष्ठः
ओष्ठ m. (-ष्ठः) The lip, especially the upper, &c. du.<BR>	 m. (ओष्ठौ or ओष्ठाधरौ)<BR>The lips: see अधर.<BR>	 f. (-ष्ठी) A creeper, bearing a red flower, to<BR>which the lip is commonly compared, (Bryonia grandis.)<BR> E. उष् to<BR>burn, थन् Uṇādi affix, fem. affix ङीष्: see विम्ब.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=144-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओष्ठपल्लव|ओष्ठपल्लवः
ओष्ठपल्लव n. (-वं) A lip or the lips.<BR> E. ओष्ठ and पल्लव a new shoot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=144-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओष्ठरोग|ओष्ठरोगः
ओष्ठरोग m. (-गः) Any morbid affection of the lips.<BR> E. ओष्ठ and रोग<BR>disease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=144-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओष्ठोपमफला
ओष्ठोपमफला f. (-ला) The creeper, (Bryonia grandis:) see ओष्ठी.<BR> E. ओष्ठ a<BR>lip, उपम like, फल a flower, अच् and टाप् affixes; whose flower<BR>resembles a lip.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=144-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औ
औ The diphthong Au or Ou, having the same sound as in Our, and<BR>considered as the fourteenth vowel of the Nagari alphabet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=144-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औ
औ ind. An interjection of, 1. Calling, (ho! hola.)<BR>	 2. Of addressing,<BR>(the vocative particle oh.)<BR>	 3. A particle of prohibition, and 4. Of<BR>asseveration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=144-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औ
औ m. (औः) The serpent ANANTA.<BR>	 f. (औः) The earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=144-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औ
औ ind. The mystical prefix proper for Śūdras: see ओम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=144-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औक्थिक|औक्थिकः
औक्थिक m. (-कः) A Brahman acquainted with the Uktha portion of<BR>the Sama Veda.<BR> E. उक्थ and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=144-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औक्ष|औक्षं
औक्ष mfn. (-क्षः-क्षी-क्षं) Relating to an ox, derived from one, &c.<BR> E. उक्षन्,<BR>and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=144-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औक्षक|औक्षकं
औक्षक m. (-कः) A herd of oxen.<BR> E. उक्ष an ox, वुञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=144-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औख्य|औख्यं
औख्य mfn. (-ख्यः-ख्या-ख्यं) Boiled or dressed in a pot.<BR> E. उखा a cauldron,<BR>a saucepan, यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=144-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औचित्य|औचित्यं
औचित्य nf. (-त्यं-ती) Propriety, aptness, fitness.<BR> E. उचित proper, ष्यञ्<BR>affix in the abstract sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=144-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औजसिक|औजसिकः
औजसिक m. (-कः) A hero.<BR> E. ओजस् strength, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=144-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औडुपिक|औडुपिकः
औडुपिक m. (-कः) A passenger, one going in a raft or boat.<BR> E. उडुप<BR>and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=144-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औडुम्बर|औडुंबर|औडुम्बरं|औडुम्बरः
औडुम्बर mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>	 1. Coppery, made of copper, &c.<BR>	 2. Made of the<BR>wood of the Udumbara fig tree.<BR>	 m. (-रः) A name of YAMA the<BR>regent of death.<BR>	 n. (-रं)<BR>	 1. A kind of leprosy.<BR>	 2. Copper.<BR> E. उडुम्बर<BR>and अण् affix: see उडुम्बर, उदुम्बर, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=144-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औड्र|औड्रः
औड्र m. (-ड्रः) An Uriya, an inhabitant of Urissa.<BR> E. ओड्र, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=144-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औत्कर्ष्य|औत्कर्ष्यं
औत्कर्ष्य n. (-र्ष्यं) Excellence, superiority.<BR> E. उकर्ष, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=144-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औत्तमि|औत्तमिः
औत्तमि m. (-मिः) The third MANU.<BR> E. उत्तम, and इञ् patronymic. k. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=144-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औत्तरपथिक
औत्तरपथिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Going or coming in a northerly direction.<BR>E. उत्तर, पथ for पथिन् a road, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=144-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औत्तानपादि|औत्तानपादिः
औत्तानपादि m. (-दिः) A name of DHRUVA, in mythology the son of<BR>UTTANAPADA, and grandson of the first MANU; in astronomy,<BR>the polar star, or the north pole itself.<BR> E. उत्तानपाद, and इञ् patro-<BR>nymick aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=144-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औत्पातिक
औत्पातिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Portentous, calamitous.<BR> E. उत्पात, and<BR>ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=144-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औत्सङ्गिक|औत्संगिक
औत्सङ्गिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Carried or placed upon the hip or flank. E.<BR>उत्सङ्ग, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=144-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औत्सर्गिक|औत्सर्गिकः
औत्सर्गिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>	 1. Omitting, leaving.<BR>	 2. Terminative, com-<BR>pleting, relating or belonging to a final ceremony, by which the<BR>rite is dismissed.<BR>	 3. Natural, inherent.<BR>	 4. Derivative, produced<BR>from or of, directly and naturally.<BR> E. उत्सर्ग abandoned, and<BR>ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=144-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औत्सुक्य|औत्सुक्यं
औत्सुक्य n. (-क्यं) Anxiety, perturbation, regret.<BR> E. उत्सुक anxious, ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=144-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औदक
औदक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Watery, aquatic, of or belonging to water. E.<BR>उदक, and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=144-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औदनिक|औदनिकः
औदनिक m. (-कः) A cook.<BR> E. ओदन boiled rice, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=144-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औदरिक|औदरिकः
औदरिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Selfishly voracious.<BR> E. उदर the belly, and<BR>ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=144-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औदश्वित|औदश्वितं
औदश्वित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Made of buttermilk, &c.<BR>	 n. (-तं) Buttermilk<BR>with an equal proportion of water.<BR> E. उदश्वित् the same, and अण्<BR>affix; or with कस् added औदश्वित्क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=144-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औदार्य्य|औदार्य|औदार्यं|औदार्य्यं
औदार्य्य n. (-र्य्यं) Magnanimity, generosity, greatness.<BR> E. उदार liberal,<BR>and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=144-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औदास्य|औदास्यं
औदास्य n. (-स्यं) Philosophy, stoicism, indifference.<BR> E. उदास, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=144-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औद्दालक|औद्दालकं
औद्दालक n. (-कं) A bitter and acrid substance like honey, said to be<BR>found in the nest of the white ant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=144-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औद्धत्य|औद्धत्यं
औद्धत्य n. (-त्यं) Arrogance, disdain.<BR> E. उद्धत haughty, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=144-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औद्धारिक
औद्धारिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Heritable, portionable, belonging to a share<BR>or portion.<BR>	 n. (-कं) A portion or inheritance.<BR> E. उद्धार a share,<BR>ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=144-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औद्वाहिक|औद्वाहिकं
औद्वाहिक n. (-कं) A gift made to a woman at her marriage.<BR> E. उद्वाहिक,<BR>and अण् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=144-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औद्भिज्ज|औद्भिज्जं
औद्भिज्ज n. (-ज्जं) Fossil salt.<BR> E. उद्भिज् the same, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=144-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औद्भिद|औद्भिदं
औद्भिद n. (-दं) Rock or Sambher salt.<BR> E. उद्भिद्, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=144-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औपकार्य्या|औपकार्या
औपकार्य्या f. (-र्य्या) A booth, a residence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=144-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औपगवक|औपगवकं
औपगवक n. (-कं) A multitude of the descendants of Upagu.<BR> E. औपगव<BR>the patronymick of उपगु, and वुन् aggregate aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=144-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औपग्रस्तिक|औपग्रस्तिकः
औपग्रस्तिक m. (-कः) An eclipse, or the sun or moon in eclipse.<BR> E. उपग्रस्त<BR>eclipsed, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=144-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औपग्रहिक|औपग्रहिकः
औपग्रहिक m. (-कः) An eclipse, or the sun or moon in eclipse.<BR> E. उपग्रह<BR>an eclipse, ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=144-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औपजानुक
औपजानुक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Upon or near the knees.<BR> E. उपजानु, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=144-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औपधेय
औपधेय n. (-यं) The wheel of a carriage.<BR> E. उपधि, and ढञ् pleonasm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=144-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औपनायनिक
औपनायनिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Relating to the rite of investiture. E.<BR>उपनयन, and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=144-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औपनिधिक|औपनिधिकं
औपनिधिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Relating to a deposit.<BR>	 n. (-कं) A deposit, the<BR>thing pledged or deposited.<BR> E. उपनिधि, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=145-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औपनिषद|औपनिषदः
औपनिषद mfn. (-दः-दी-दं) Scriptural, theological.<BR> E. उपनिषद्, and<BR>अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=145-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औपम्य|औपम्यं
औपम्य n. (-म्यं) Resemblance, similitude.<BR> E. उपमा, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=145-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औपयिक|औपयिकः
औपयिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Right, fit, proper.<BR>	 n. (-कं) A means, an expe-<BR>dient.<BR> E. उपाय an expedient, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=145-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औपरिष्ट
औपरिष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं) Being or produced above.<BR> E. उपरिष्ट, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=145-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औपरोधिक|औपरोधिकः
औपरोधिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>	 1. Proceeding from or relating to kindness<BR>or favour.<BR>	 2. Opposing, impeding, connected with or relating to a<BR>check or hindrance.<BR> E. उपरोध, and ठक् affix.<BR>	 m. (-कः) A staff of<BR>the wood of a particular tree, (the Pilu.)<BR> E. उपरोध willingness to<BR>oblige, &c. टक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=145-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औपल
औपल mfn. (-लः-ली-लं) Stony, of stone.<BR> E. उपल, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=145-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औपवस्त|औपवस्तं
औपवस्त n. (-स्तं) Fasting, a fast.<BR> E. उपवस्त, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=145-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औपवाह्य|औपवाह्यः
औपवाह्य mfn. (-ह्यः-ह्या-ह्यं) Drawn for pleasure, (a carriage.)<BR> E. उपवह a<BR>conveyance, यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=145-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औपसर्गिक|औपसर्गिकः
औपसर्गिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>	 1. Portentous.<BR>	 2. Prepositive, connected<BR>with a preposition.<BR>	 3. Relating to change, &c.<BR>	 m. (-कः) Irregular<BR>action of the humors of the body, producing cold sweats, &c. E.<BR>उपसर्ग a portent, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=145-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औपस्थ्य|औपस्थ्यं
औपस्थ्य n. (-स्थ्यं) Cohabitation, sexual enjoyment.<BR> E. उपस्थ, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=145-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औपाध्यायक
औपाध्यायक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Preceptral, of or relating to a spiritual<BR>teacher.<BR> E. उपाध्याय and वुञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=145-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औपानह्य
औपानह्य mfn. (-ह्यः-ह्या-ह्यं) To be tied or bound on (grass, leather, &c.)<BR>E. उपानह्, and ञ्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=145-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औपासन|औपासनः
औपासन mfn. (-नः-नी-नं) Devotional, holy, connected with or belonging<BR>to worship or service.<BR> E. उपासना, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=145-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औम
औम mfn. (-मः-मी-मं) Flaxen, made of flax, &c.<BR> E. उमा and अञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=145-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औमक
औमक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Flaxen, made of flax, &c.<BR> E. उमा and वुञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=145-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औमीन|औमीनं
औमीन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Flax, (a field of, &c.)<BR> E. उमा flax, and ख aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=145-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औरग|औरगं
औरग mfn. (-गः-गी-गं) Serpent, serpentine, relating or belonging to a<BR>snake.<BR>	 n. (-गं) The constellation Aslesha.<BR> E. उरग a snake, and अण्<BR>affix; a serpent in the regent of this constellation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=145-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औरभ्र|औरभ्रः
औरभ्र mfn. (-भ्रः-भ्रा-भ्रं) Belonging to, &c., a sheep.<BR>	 m. (-भ्रः) A coarse<BR>woollen blanket.<BR>	 n. (-भ्रं)<BR>	 1. Mutton, the flesh of sheep.<BR>	 2. Woollen<BR>cloth.<BR> E. उरभ्र a sheep, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=145-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औरभ्रक|औरभ्रकं
औरभ्रक n. (-कं) A flock of sheep.<BR> E. उरभ्र and वुञ् affix of multitude.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=145-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औरभ्रिक|औरभ्रिकः
औरभ्रिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Relating to, produced by, &c. sheep.<BR>	 m. (-कः)<BR>A shepherd.<BR> E. उरभ्र a sheep, and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=145-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औरस|औरसः
औरस mf. (-सः-सी) A legitimate child, i. e. by a wife of the same tribe.<BR>E. उरस् the best, and अण affix; the best of the twelve sons; also<BR>उरस्य and औरस्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=145-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औरस्य|औरस्यः
औरस्य mf. (-स्यः-स्यं) See the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=145-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

और्ण|और्ण्ण
और्ण mfn. (-र्णः-र्णी-र्णं) Woollen (cloth, &c.)<BR> E. ऊर्णा wool, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=145-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

और्णक|और्ण्णक
और्णक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Made woollen, &c.<BR> E. ऊर्णा, and वुञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=145-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

और्द्धदेहिक
और्द्धदेहिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Obsequial, funeral.<BR>	 n. (-कं) Obsequies of a<BR>deceased person; whatever is given or performed on a person's<BR>decease, as burning, offering cakes, giving alms, &c.<BR> E. ऊर्द्ध or<BR>ऊर्द्ध्व above, देह the body, and ठक् affix; hence also और्द्ध्वदेहिक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=145-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

और्द्धश्रोतसिक
और्द्धश्रोतसिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) A Saiva or adherent of that doctrine,<BR>which gives ŚIVA the pre-eminence in the Hindu triad.<BR> E. ऊर्द्धश्रोतस्<BR>a name of ŚIVA, viz. above whom or in whose head is the river,<BR>(श्रीतस्) (the Ganges,) and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=145-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

और्व्व|और्व|और्वः|और्व्वं|और्व्वः
और्व्व m. (-र्व्वः) Submarine fire.<BR> E. उर्व्व a saint so named, from whose<BR>thighs sprang a being of flame, which was received by the ocean;<BR>the affix is अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=145-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

और्व्वशेय|और्वशेय|और्वशेयः|और्व्वशेयः
और्व्वशेय m. (-यः) A name of the saint AGASTYA.<BR> E. उर्व्वशी the celestial<BR>courtezan, and ठक् affix; his birth being ascribed indirectly to<BR>this lady.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=145-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

और्व्वानल|और्वानल
और्व्वानल m. (-लः) Submarine fire.<BR> E. और्व्व, and अनल fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=145-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औलूक|औलूकं
औलूक n. (-कं) A flock of owls.<BR> E. उलूक, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=145-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औलूक्य|औलूक्यः
औलूक्य m. (-क्यः) A follower of the Vaiseshika doctrine.<BR> E. उलूक an<BR>owl, and ष्यञ् affix, like an owl: this etymology, and perhaps the<BR>word, owes its origin probably to controversial animosity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=145-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औलूखल
औलूखल mfn. (-लः-ली-लं) Ground or pounded in a mortar.<BR> E. उलूखल, and<BR>अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=145-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औशनस
औशनस n. (-सं) The code, &c. of USANAS.<BR> E. उशनस्, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=145-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औशीर|औशीरं|औशीरः
औशीर mn. (-रः-रं)<BR>	 1. The cow's tail used as a fan, the Chowri.<BR>	 2. A<BR>stick, or, according to some, the stick which serves as a handle to<BR>the preceding.<BR>	 3. A bed.<BR>	 4. A seat, a chair or stool.<BR>	 5. The root<BR>of a fragrant grass, (Andropogon muricatum.)<BR> E. उशीर the root of<BR>the Andropogon muricatum, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=145-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औषण|औषणं
औषण n. (-णं) Pungency.<BR> E. उषण pepper, &c. अण् affix; also उषण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=145-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औषध|औषधं
औषध n. (-धं) A medicament, a drug, any herb, mineral, &c. used in<BR>medicine.<BR> E. औषधि an annual plant, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=145-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औषधि|औषधिः
औषधि f. (-धि) A deciduous plant, an annual as grass, &c. E. See ओषधि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=145-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औषधीय
औषधीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Medicinal.<BR> E. औषध and छ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=145-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औषर|औषरं
औषर n. (-रं)<BR>	 1. Fossile salt.<BR>	 2. Iron stone.<BR> E. ऊषरा desert soil, अण् affix;<BR>also with कन् added औषरक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=145-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औषस
औषस mfn. (-सः-सी-सं) Early, matutinal.<BR> E. उषस् the dawn, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=145-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औषिक
औषिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Early, morning, &c. with the dawn.<BR> E. उषा,<BR>and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=145-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औष्ट्र
औष्ट्र mfn. (-ष्ट्रः-ष्ट्री-ष्ट्रं) Derived from or relating to a camel.<BR>	 n. (-ष्ट्रं) The<BR>camel genus or species.<BR> E. उष्ट्र and अञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=145-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औष्ट्रक|औष्ट्रकं
औष्ट्रक n. (-कं) A herd of camels.<BR> E. उष्ट्र a camel, and वुञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=145-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औष्म्य|औष्म्यं
औष्म्य n. (-ष्म्यं) Heat, warmth.<BR> E. उष्म warm, यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=145-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क|कं|कः
क The first consonant of the Nagari Alphabet, and the first of the<BR>guttural letters, corresponding to K or C in can, designated by<BR>the latter in Sir. WM. JONES'S system, but in this work by the<BR>former.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=145-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क|कं|कः
क m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A name of BRAHMĀ.<BR>	 2. Of VIṢṆU.<BR>	 3. Of KĀMADEVA.<BR>4. Of fire.<BR>	 5. Air or wind.<BR>	 6. A title of YAMA.<BR>	 7. The sun.<BR>	 8. The<BR>soul.<BR>	 9. A clever or dexterous man.<BR>	 10. A king, a prince.<BR>	 11. A<BR>knot or joint.<BR>	 12. A peacock.<BR>	 13. The mind.<BR>	 14. The body.<BR>	 15.<BR>Time.<BR>	 16. Wealth, property.<BR>	 17. Sound.<BR>	 18. Light, splendor.<BR>	 n.<BR>(कं)<BR>	 1. The head.<BR>	 2. Water.<BR>	 3. Pleasure, happiness.<BR>	 4. Hair.<BR>	 5. A<BR>head of hair. pron.<BR>	 mfn. (-कः-का-किम्) Who or what: see किम्.<BR> E. कै<BR>to sound, or कच् to shine, &c. affix ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=145-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कंय्य
कंय्य mfn. (-य्यः-य्या-य्यं) Happy.<BR> E. कं happiness, यस् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=145-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कंय्यु
कंय्यु mfn. (-य्युः-य्युः-य्यु) Happy, prosperous.<BR> E. कं happiness and युस् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=145-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कंश|कंशः
कंश m. (-शः) A goblet: see कंस.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=145-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कंस|कंसं|कंसः
कंस m. (-सः) A proper name; KANSA king of Mathura the uncle and<BR>enemy of KṚṢṆA, by whom he was slain; as the foe of the<BR>deity, he is considered an Asura or demon.<BR>	 mn. (-सः-सं)<BR>	 1. A goblet,<BR>a drinking vessel; also कंश and कांस्य.<BR>	 2. A metal, tutanag or<BR>white copper; also bell metal.<BR>	 3. A measure.<BR> E. कमु to desire, स<BR>Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=145-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कंसक|कंसकं
कंसक n. (-कं) A mineral substance, (a salt of iron?) used as an appli-<BR>cation to the eyes: see पुष्पकासीस.<BR> E. कंस, and क affix of similarity;<BR>of similar white colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=145-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कंसकार|कंसकारः
कंसकार m. (-रः) A worker in pewter or white brass.<BR> E. कंस and कार who<BR>makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=145-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कंसजित्
कंसजित् m. (-जित्) A title of KṚṢṆA.<BR> E. कंस, and जित् who conquers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=145-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कंसहन्
कंसहन् m. (-हा) A name of KṚṢṆA or VIṢṆU.<BR> E. हन् from हन to<BR>kill; the destroyer of KANSA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=146-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कंसाराति|कंसारातिः
कंसाराति m. (-तिः) KṚṢṆA, or VIṢṆU in that character.<BR> E. कंस, and<BR>अराति an enemy, the foe of KANSA; hence also कंसारि and other<BR>similar epithets: see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=146-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कंसारि|कंसारिः
कंसारि m. (-रिः) See the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=146-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कंसास्थि
कंसास्थि n. (-स्थि) Tutanag, white copper, any alloy of tin and copper. E.<BR>कंस white metal, and अस्थि bone, fig. substance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=146-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कंसिक
कंसिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Made of bellmetal, &c.<BR> E. कंस, and ठन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=146-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कंसीय
कंसीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Fit for or relating to a cup.<BR> E. कंस, and छ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=146-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कंसोद्भवा
कंसोद्भवा f. (-वा) A fragrant earth: see तुवरी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=146-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कक
कक r. 1st cl. (ककते)<BR>	 1. To be proud.<BR>	 2. To be unsteady.<BR>	 3. To be<BR>thirsty. (इ) ककि (कंकते) To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=146-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ककन्द|ककंदः|ककन्दः
ककन्द m. (-न्दः) Gold.<BR> E. कनी to shine, affix द, and the initial repeated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=146-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ककुञ्जल|ककुंजल|ककुंजलः|ककुञ्जलः
ककुञ्जल m. (-लः) A bird, the Chataka.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=146-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ककुत्स्थ|ककुत्स्थः
ककुत्स्थ m. (-स्थः) A prince, the grandson of IKSHWAKU, and ancestor<BR>of RAMA.<BR> E. ककुद् an emblem of royalty, and स्थ who resides.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=146-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ककुद्
ककुद् f. (-त्) or ककुद mn. (-दः-दं)<BR>	 1. The hump on the shoulders of the<BR>Indian bull.<BR>	 2. An ensign or symbol of royalty, as the white<BR>parasol, &c.<BR>	 3. Chief, pre-eminent.<BR>	 4. The peak or summit of a<BR>mountain.<BR> E. क happiness, कु to sound, affixes क्विप् and तुक्; त<BR>becomes द; or with a final vowel, taking an additional affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=146-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ककुद्मत्|ककुद्मन्त्
ककुद्मत् m. (-द्मान्)<BR>	 1. A bull.<BR>	 2. A mountain.<BR>	 f. (-द्मती) The hip and lions.<BR>E. ककुद् a bull's hump, &c. affix मतुप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=146-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ककुद्मिकन्या
ककुद्मिकन्या f. (-न्या) A river.<BR> E. ककुद्मिन् a mountain, कन्या a daughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=146-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ककुद्मिन्
ककुद्मिन् mfn. (-द्मी-द्मिनी-द्मि)<BR>	 1. Peaked.<BR>	 2. Humped.<BR>	 m. (-द्मी)<BR>	 1. A moun-<BR>tain.<BR>	 2. A bull.<BR> E. ककुद, and मिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=146-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ककुन्दर|ककुंदर|ककुंदरं|ककुन्दरं
ककुन्दर n. (-रं) The cavities of the loins: see कुकुन्दर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=146-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ककुभ्
ककुभ् f. (-प)<BR>	 1. Space, region or quarter, as east, west, &c.<BR>	 2. Beauty,<BR>splendor.<BR>	 3. Unornamented hair, or the hair hanging down as a<BR>tail.<BR>	 4. A wreath of Champaka flowers.<BR>	 5. A Rāgiṇī or personified<BR>mode of music.<BR>	 6. A Śāstra or sacred treatise.<BR> E. क wind, स्कुभ् to<BR>spread, क्विप् affix and the स is dropped; or कक् to be proud,<BR>उभ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=146-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ककुभ|ककुभः
ककुभ m. (-भः)<BR>	 1. A tree, (Pentaptera Arjuna, Rox.)<BR>	 2. A part of a lute,<BR>the belly, a wooden vessel covered with leather placed under its<BR>neck to render the sound deeper, or a crooked piece of wood at<BR>the end of the lute.<BR>	 3. One of the Ragas or personified musical<BR>modes.<BR>	 f. (-भा)<BR>	 1. Space, region, quarter: see ककुभ् 2. One of the<BR>Rāgiṇīs or female personifications of music.<BR> E. ककुभ् space, and<BR>अच् affix; or क wind, स्कुभ् to spread, क affix and स rejected, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=146-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ककुभादनी
ककुभादनी f. (-नी) A kind of perfume: see नली.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=146-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ककेरुक|ककेरुकः
ककेरुक m. (-कः) A worm in the stomach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=146-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कक्क
कक्क r. 1st cl. (कक्कति) To laugh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=146-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कक्कोल|कक्कोलः
कक्कोल m. (-लः) A perfume, a plant bearing a berry, the inner part of<BR>which is a waxy and arometic substance.<BR>	 n. (-लं) The berry, possibly<BR>the fruit of the Cocculus Indicus.<BR> E. कक् to be proud, with क्विप्<BR>affix, कुल् to accumulate, अच् affix; also with कन् added कक्कोलक<BR>mn. (-कः-कं.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=146-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कक्ख
कक्ख(ए) r. 1st cl. (कक्खति) To laugh, to laugh at, to deride; see खक्ख.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=146-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कक्खट|कक्खटः
कक्खट mfn. (-टः-टा-टं) Hard, solid.<BR>	 f. (-टी) chalk.<BR> E. कक्ख to deride,<BR>अटन् affix, fem. affixes टाप् and ङीष्; also खक्खट.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=146-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कक्खटपत्रक|कक्खटपत्रकः
कक्खटपत्रक m. (-कः) A plant of the fibres of which a kind of rope is<BR>made, (Corchorus olitorius, Rox.)<BR> E. कक्खट hard, पत्र a leaf, and<BR>कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=146-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कक्व
कक्व r. 1st cl. (कक्वति) To laugh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=146-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कक्ष|कक्षः
कक्ष m. (-क्षः)<BR>	 1. The armpit.<BR>	 2. A spreading creeper, a climbing plant.<BR>3. Grass.<BR>	 4. Dry grass.<BR>	 5. A wood, a forest.<BR>	 6. A forest of dead<BR>trees, a dry wood.<BR>	 7. A private or inner chamber or part of a<BR>house.<BR>	 8. Sin.<BR>	 9. A buffalo.<BR>	 10. The side or flank.<BR>	 11. (In astro-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=146-b" target="_blank">Page146-b+ 60</a>]<BR>nomy,) The orbit of a planet, or the circle anciently termed a<BR>deferent.<BR>	 12. A gate.<BR>	 13. The beleric myrobalan, (Terminalia bele-<BR>rica.)<BR>	 mf. (-क्षः-क्षा)<BR>	 1. A wall.<BR>	 2. The end of the lower garment, which<BR>after the cloth is carried round the body, is brought up behind,<BR>and tucked into the waistband.<BR>	 f. (-क्षा)<BR>	 1. An elephant's rope, the<BR>string round his neck, also his girth.<BR>	 2. A woman's girdle or zone.<BR>3. An enclosure, a part or division of an edifice.<BR>	 4. A part of a car.<BR>5. Objection or reply in argument.<BR>	 6. Similarity, parity.<BR>	 7. Emula-<BR>tion, rivalship.<BR>	 8. The jeweller's weight, the Retti.<BR>	 9. Painful boils<BR>in the armpit, side, shoulder, &c.<BR>	 n. (-क्षं) A constellation, a star:<BR>see कक्ष्या, कच्छ, काञ्चि, &c.<BR> E. कष् to hurt or kill, स Uṇādi affix,<BR>fem. टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=146-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कक्षरुहा
कक्षरुहा f. (-हा) A fragrant grass, (Cyperus.)<BR> E. कक्ष an enclosure, and<BR>रुह what grows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=146-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कक्षशाय|कक्षशायः
कक्षशाय m. (-यः) A dog.<BR> E. कक्ष an inner room, शाय who sleeps.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=146-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कक्षान्तर|कक्षांतर
कक्षान्तर n. (-रं) The inner or private apartment.<BR> E. कक्ष and अन्तर<BR>interior.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=146-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कक्षापट|कक्षापटः
कक्षापट m. (-टः) A cloth passed between the legs to cover the privities.<BR>E. कक्षा a girdle, and पट a cloth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=146-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कक्षावेक्षक|कक्षावेक्षकः
कक्षावेक्षक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A doorkeeper.<BR>	 2. A guard of the queen's apart-<BR>ments.<BR>	 3. Keeper of royal garden.<BR>	 4. A painter.<BR>	 5. A poet.<BR>	 6. A<BR>debauchee.<BR>	 7. Eagerness of feeling, strength of sentiment.<BR> E. कक्षा<BR>an enclosure, and अवेक्ष to see, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=146-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कक्षीवत्|कक्षीवन्त्
कक्षीवत् m. (-वान्) The name of a saint.<BR> E. कक्षा a reply, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=146-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कक्षोत्था
कक्षोत्था f. (-त्था) A fragrant grass, (Cyperus.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=146-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कक्ष्य|कक्ष्यं
कक्ष्य n. (-क्ष्यं) The cup or receptacle of a balance.<BR>	 f. (-क्ष्या)<BR>	 1. The girth<BR>of an elephant, of rope or leather.<BR>	 2. A woman's girdle or zone.<BR>	 3.<BR>The enclosure of an edifice; that is, either the wall, &c. so enclos-<BR>ing, or the court or chamber constituting the enclosure.<BR>	 4. The<BR>inner apartment of a palace.<BR>	 5. Similarity.<BR>	 6. Effort, exertion.<BR>	 7.<BR>An upper garment.<BR>	 8. A shrub, yielding the black and red berry,<BR>that serves as a jeweller's weight; the Ratti or Gunga, (Abrus<BR>precatorius.)<BR> E. कक्ष the flank, &c. यत् affix; see कक्ष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=146-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कख
कख r. 1st cl. (ए) कखे (कखति) To laugh, to laugh at or deride; also<BR>कक्ख and खक्ख q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=146-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कख्या
कख्या f. (-ख्या) An enclosure, a division of a large building: see कक्ष्या. E.<BR>कख् to deride, यत् aff. and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=146-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कग
कग r. 1st cl. (ए) कगे (कगति) To perform any action: the meaning of<BR>this root is not given in many lists, from its application being<BR>indefinitely various.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=146-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कङ्क|कंक|कंकः|कङ्कः
कङ्क m. (-ङ्कः)<BR>	 1. A heron.<BR>	 2. YAMA or death.<BR>	 3. A false or pretended<BR>Brahman.<BR>	 4. A title of YUDISHṬHIRA, from his assuming the dis-<BR>guise of a Brahman.<BR>	 5. A man of the second or military tribe.<BR>	 6.<BR>One of the eighteen divisions of the continent.<BR>	 7. The brother of<BR>KANSA.<BR>	 8. A kind of mango.<BR>	 f. (-ङ्का)<BR>	 1. A daughter of UGRASENA.<BR>2. A sort of sandal.<BR> E. ककि to go, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=146-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कङ्कट|कंकट|कंकटः|कङ्कटः
कङ्कट m. (-टः) Mail, defensive armour.<BR> E. ककि to go, Uṇādi affix अटन्,<BR>and with कन् added कङ्कटक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=146-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कङ्कटेरी
कङ्कटेरी f. (-री) Turmerick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=146-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कङ्कण|कंकण|कंकणं|कङ्कणं|कंकणः|कङ्कणः
कङ्कण mn. (-णः-णं)<BR>	 1. A bracelet or ornament of the wrist.<BR>	 2. A string<BR>or ribband tied round the wrist.<BR>	 3. An ornament or trinket.<BR>	 4. A<BR>crest.<BR>	 f. (-णी) A small bell or tinkling ornament; also किङ्किणी and<BR>कङ्कणीका.<BR> E. कं happily, agreeably, कण् to sound, or the reiterative<BR>form of कण and अच् affix, fem. affix ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=146-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कङ्कणीका|कंकणीका
कङ्कणीका f. (-का) See कङ्कणी.<BR> E. कण् to sound in the reiterative form, and<BR>ईकन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=146-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कङ्कत|कंकत|कंकतं|कङ्कतं|कंकतः|कङ्कतः
कङ्कत mfn. (-तः-तिका or -ती-तं) A comb, an instrument for cleaning the<BR>hair.<BR>	 m. (-तः) A tree.<BR> E. ककि to go, अतच् affix, fem. ङीष् or कन्<BR>added in the fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=146-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कङ्कत्रोट|कङ्कत्रोटः
कङ्कत्रोट m. (-टः) A kind of fish commonly Kanila (Esox Cancila,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=147-a" target="_blank">Page147-a+ 60</a>]<BR>HAM.)<BR> E. कङ्क a heron, and त्रोटि the throat; whose long snout re-<BR>sembles the beak of a heron: also कङ्कत्रोटि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=146-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कङ्कत्रोटि|कङ्कत्रोटिः
कङ्कत्रोटि m. (-टिः) A kind of a fish: see the preceding; also जलसूचि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=147-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कङ्कपत्र|कंकपत्र|कङ्कपत्रः
कङ्कपत्र m. (-त्रः) An arrow.<BR> E. कङ्क and पत्र leaf, (feather.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=147-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कङ्कमाला
कङ्कमाला f. (-ला) Beating time by clapping the hands: see करताली.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=147-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कङ्कमुख|कंकमुख|कङ्कमुखः
कङ्कमुख m. (-खः) A pair of tongs.<BR>	 n. (-खं) A sort of forceps.<BR> E. कङ्क and<BR>मुख the mouth; heron-mouthed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=147-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कङ्कर|कंकर|कङ्करं|कङ्करः
कङ्कर mfn. (-रः-री-रं) Vile, bad.<BR>	 n. (-रं) Buttermilk mixed with water.<BR>See कञ्जर.<BR> E. क implying bad, or कं water, कर what does or makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=147-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कङ्करोल|कंकरोलः|कङ्करोलः
कङ्करोल m. (-लः) A small tree, (Alangium hexapetalum:) see निकोचक;<BR>the word in the dialects Kankarol is applied to a species of gourd,<BR>(Momordica mixta.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=147-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कङ्कलोड्य|कंकलोड्यं|कङ्कलोड्यं
कङ्कलोड्य n. (-ड्यं) A kind of drug.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=147-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कङ्कशत्रु|कङ्कशत्रुः
कङ्कशत्रु m. (-त्रुः) A plant, (Hedysarnm gangeticum:) see शालपर्णी.<BR> E. कङ्क<BR>a heron, and शत्रु an enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=147-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कङ्कशाय|कंकशाय|कङ्कशायः
कङ्कशाय m. (-यः) A dog.<BR> E. कङ्क a heron, and शाय sleeping, sleeping<BR>like a heron, from शीङ् and घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=147-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कङ्का|कंका
कङ्का f. (-ङ्का) Scent of the lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=147-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कङ्काल|कंकाल|कंकालं|कंकालः|कङ्कालः
कङ्काल m. (-लः) The skeleton.<BR> E. ककि to go, कालच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=147-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कङ्कालमालिन्|कंकालमालिन्
कङ्कालमालिन् m. (-ली) A title of ŚIVA.<BR> E. कङ्काल, माला a necklace, and इनि<BR>affix; whose necklace is formed of bones.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=147-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कङ्कु|कंकुः|कङ्कुः
कङ्कु m. (-ङ्कुः)<BR>	 1. The brother of KANSA.<BR>	 2. A sort of panic. E.<BR>ककि to go, उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=147-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कङ्कुष्ठ|कंकुष्ठं|कङ्कुष्ठं|कंकुष्ठः|कङ्कुष्ठः
कङ्कुष्ठ n. (-ष्टं) A medicinal earth, described as of two colours, one of a<BR>silvery and one of a gold colour, or one of a light and one of a<BR>dark yellow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=147-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कङ्केरु|कंकेरुः|कङ्केरुः
कङ्केरु m. (-रुः) A kind of crow.<BR> E. कङ्क an imitative sound, ईर् to send,<BR>to utter, उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=147-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कङ्केलि|कंकेलि|कङ्केलिः
कङ्केलि m. (-लिः) The Asoka tree, (Jonesia asoca;) also कङ्केल्लि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=147-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कङ्केल्ल|कंकेल्लः|कङ्केल्लः
कङ्केल्ल m. (-ल्लः) A kind of potherb, (Chenopodium esculentum, Rox.)<BR>See वास्तुक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=147-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कङ्केल्लि|कंकेल्लिः|कङ्केल्लिः
कङ्केल्लि m. (-ल्लिः) A tree (Jonesia asoca, Rox.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=147-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कङ्ख|कंखं|कङ्खं
कङ्ख m. (-ङ्खः) Enjoyment, fruition.<BR> E. कखि to deride, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=147-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कङ्गु|कंगु|कङ्गुः
कङ्गु f. (-ङ्गुः) A kind of Panick seed, (Panicum Italicum;) several<BR>varieties of it are cultivated, and form articles of food for the poor.<BR>E. क water, अनि to go, कु affix; also with ऊङ् affix कङ्गू, and with<BR>कन् added कङ्गुका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=147-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कङ्गुनी
कङ्गुनी f. (-नी) A sort of Panick; see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=147-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कङ्गुनीपत्रा
कङ्गुनीपत्रा f. (-त्रा) A kind of grass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=147-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कङ्गुल|कंगुल|कंगुलः|कङ्गुलः
कङ्गुल m. (-लः) The hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=147-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कच|कचः
कच r. 1st cl. (कचते)<BR>	 1. To bind.<BR>	 2. To shine.<BR>	 3. To sound. (इ) कचि r.<BR>1st cl. (कञ्चते)<BR>	 1. To shine.<BR>	 2. To bind; also काचि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=147-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कच|कचः
कच m. (-चः)<BR>	 1. The hair.<BR>	 2. A proper name, the son of VṚHASPATI.<BR>3. Binding or a binding.<BR>	 4. A cicatrix, a dry or healed sore.<BR>	 5. A<BR>cloud.<BR>	 f. (-चा)<BR>	 1. A female elephant.<BR>	 2. Beauty, brilliance.<BR> E. कच् to<BR>bind, &c. अच् affix, fem. टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=147-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कचङ्गन|कचंगन|कचंगनं|कचङ्गनं
कचङ्गन n. (-नं) A free market, a place of sale that pays no duty or custom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=147-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कचङ्गल|कचंगल|कचंगलः|कचङ्गलः
कचङ्गल m. (-लः) The ocean.<BR> E. कच a cloud, अङ्ग the body, and ल what<BR>takes or receives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=147-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कचप|कचपं|कचपः
कचप m. (-पः)<BR>	 1. Grass.<BR>	 2. A leaf.<BR> E. कच a cloud, and प what drinks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=147-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कचपक्ष|कचपक्षः
कचपक्ष m. (-क्षः) Much or ornamented hair, and कच hair, and पक्ष, in this<BR>combination, abundance; similar compounds are made with पाश<BR>and हस्त, कचपाश, कचहस्त; also with केश hair, as केशपक्ष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=147-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कचपाश|कचपाशः
कचपाश m. (-शः) See the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=147-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कचमाल|कचमालः
कचमाल m. (-लः) Smoke.<BR> E. कच a cloud, and माला a necklace, ड affix;<BR>also खतमाल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=147-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कचरिपुफला
कचरिपुफला f. (-ला) The Sami tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=147-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कचहस्त|कचहस्तः
कचहस्त m. (-स्तः) See कचपक्ष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=147-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कचाकु|कचाकुः
कचाकु mfn. (-कुः-कुः-कु)<BR>	 1. Ill disposed, wicked.<BR>	 2. Intolerable, difficult<BR>to be borne.<BR>	 m. (-कुः) A snake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=147-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कचाचित
कचाचित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Having long or dishevelled hair.<BR> E. कच, and<BR>अचित not gathered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=147-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कचाटुर|कचाटुरः
कचाटुर m. (-रः) A gallinule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=147-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कचु|कचुः
कचु f. (-चुः) An esculent root, (Arum colocasia and other kinds, many<BR>of which are cultivated for food:) see कच्वी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=147-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कच्चट|कच्चटं
कच्चट n. (-टं) An aquatic plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=147-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कच्चर|कच्चरं
कच्चर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>	 1. Dirty, foul.<BR>	 2. Soiled, spoiled by dirt.<BR>	 3. Vile,<BR>wicked, bad.<BR>	 n. (-रं) Buttermilk diluted with water.<BR> E. कुत् bad,<BR>vile, चर what goes or is, from चर with अच् affix; कत् is substituted<BR>for कुत्, and the त changed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=147-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कच्चित्
कच्चित् ind.<BR>	 1. A particle implying wish or desire, (may it be so;) also<BR>introducing a kind enquiry, (I hope that it is so, &c.)<BR>	 2. A particle<BR>implying an alternative, whether, whether or not.<BR> E. कत् for कुत्<BR>bad, and चित् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=147-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कच्छ|कच्छं|कच्छः
कच्छ mfn. (-च्छः-च्छा-च्छं) Contiguous to water, (land, &c.)<BR>	 m. (-च्छः)<BR>	 1.<BR>Marshy ground, a marsh, a morass.<BR>	 2. Ground bordering water or<BR>watery soil, as the bank of a river, the margin of a lake or tank,<BR>a mound or causeway, &c.<BR>	 3. Level land skirting mountains.<BR>	 4. A<BR>tree, the timber of which is used for making furniture, &c. com-<BR>monly Tun, (Cedrela Tuna, Rox.)<BR>	 5. Another tree, (Hibiscus<BR>Populneoides.)<BR>	 6. A part of a boat.<BR>	 mf. (-च्छः-च्छा) The hem of a<BR>garment tucked into the waistband: see कक्ष.<BR>	 f. (-च्छा)<BR>	 1. A plant,<BR>(Lycopodium imbricatum, Rox.) See वाराही.<BR>	 2. A cricket.<BR> E. क<BR>water, छो to cut or break, क affix; or कच् to bind, छ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=147-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कच्छटिका
कच्छटिका f. (-का) The end or hem of a lower garment or cloth gather-<BR>ed up behind, and tucked into the waistband; also कक्षा and<BR>कच्छाटिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=147-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कच्छप|कच्छपः
कच्छप m. (-पः)<BR>	 1. A turtle, a tortoise.<BR>	 2. One of KUVERA'S Nidhis or<BR>treasures.<BR>	 2. An attitude in wrestling.<BR>	 4. A flat kind of still.<BR>	 f.<BR>(-पी)<BR>	 1. A female tortoise, also a small one.<BR>	 2. A kind of lute, also<BR>the lute of SARASWATI.<BR>	 3. A cutaneous disease, wart or blotch. E.<BR>कच्छ a morass, and प who cherishes, who inhabits watery places:<BR>the lute, &c. are so named from being similar in shape to the<BR>tortoise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=147-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कच्छपिका
कच्छपिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. A pimple, a blotch or wart.<BR>	 2. A wart accompany-<BR>ing gonorrhœa.<BR> E. कच्छप a tortoise, कन् added, fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=147-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कच्छभू
कच्छभू f. (-भूः) Marshy ground, a swamp, a morass.<BR> E. कच्छ, and<BR>भू land.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=147-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कच्छरुहा
कच्छरुहा f. (-हा) A kind of grass, Durva or Dub, (Agrostis linearis<BR>Lin. Panicus dactilon, Rox.)<BR> E. कच्छ marshy ground, and रुह who<BR>grows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=147-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कच्छाटिका
कच्छाटिका f. (-का) See कच्छटिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=147-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कच्छान्त|कच्छांत|कच्छान्तः
कच्छान्त m. (-न्तः) The border of a lake or stream.<BR> E. कच्छ, and अन्त term.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=147-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कच्छु|कच्छुः
कच्छु f. (-च्छुः) Itch, formation of watery pustules on the hands, &c. E.<BR>कष् to hurt, उ affix; also कच्छू.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=147-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कच्छुघ्नी
कच्छुघ्नी f. (-घ्नी) A vegetable, (Trichosanthes.)<BR> E. कच्छु, and घ्नी what<BR>removes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=147-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कच्छुर|कच्छुरः
कच्छुर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>	 1. Scabby, itchy.<BR>	 2. Unchaste, libidinous.<BR>	 f. (-रा)<BR>1. A plant, (a species of Hedysarum?)<BR>	 2. Cowach, (Dolichos car-<BR>popogon.)<BR>	 3. Another plant: see शठु.<BR> E. कच्छु itch or scab,<BR>and र aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=147-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कच्छू
कच्छू f. (-च्छूः) Scab or itch.<BR> E. कष् to injure, ऊ Uṇādi affix, and छ<BR>substituted for ष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=147-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कच्छूमती
कच्छूमती f. (-ती) Cowach, (Dolichos carpopogon.)<BR> E. कच्छू itch, and<BR>मतुप् affix; producing an itching upon application to the skin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=147-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कच्छोटिका
कच्छोटिका f. (-का) The fastening of the lower garment: see कच्छटिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=147-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कच्वी
कच्वी f. (-च्वी) An esculent root, (Arum colocasia and other kinds,<BR>several of which are cultivated for food;) also written कचु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=147-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कज|कजं
कज r. 1st cl. (कजति) To be disturbed or confused with joy, pride, or<BR>sorrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=147-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कज|कजं
कज mfn. (-जः-जा-जं) Watery, aquatic, produced in or by water.<BR>	 n. (-जं)<BR>A lotus.<BR> E. क water, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=148-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कज्जल|कज्जलं|कज्जलः
कज्जल m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. A cloud.<BR>	 n. (-लं) Lampblack, considered as a colly-<BR>rium, being applied upon the eyelashes or eyelids, medicinally<BR>or ornamentatively; also sulphuret of lead or antimony, when so<BR>used.<BR>	 f. (-ली) Sulphuret of mercury, Æthiop's mineral.<BR>	 f. (-ला or<BR>-ली) A kind of fish, (Cyprinus atratus,) or any kind peculiar to<BR>stagnant waters, whence the name.<BR> E. कत् for कुत् bad, and जल water<BR>or juice, as the moisture of the collyrium, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=148-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कज्ज्वल|कज्ज्वलं
कज्ज्वल n. (-लं) Lampblack, especially considered as an application to<BR>the eyes: see the preceding.<BR> E. कत् bad, and ज्वल flame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=148-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कज्ज्वलध्वज
कज्ज्वलध्वज m. (-जः) A lamp.<BR> E. कज्ज्वल, and ध्वज a sign; also कज्जलध्वज.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=148-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कज्ज्वलरोचक
कज्ज्वलरोचक mn. (-कः-कं) The wooden stand or tripod on which the<BR>lamp is placed, a candlestick.<BR> E. कज्ज्वल and रुच् to shine; affixes<BR>घञ् and कन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=148-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कञ्चट|कञ्चटं|कञ्चटः
कञ्चट m. (-टः) A plant: see लाङ्गली, (Commelina salicifolia.)<BR>	 n. (-टं) An-<BR>other species of the same, (Commedina Bengalensis.)<BR> E. कं water,<BR>and चट् to divide; alluding to the habits of the plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=148-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कञ्चड|कञ्चडः
कञ्चड m. (-डः) A plant, (Commelina Bengalensis:) see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=148-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कञ्चार|कंचार|कंचारः|कञ्चारः
कञ्चार m. (-रः) The sun.<BR> E. कं heaven, and चर् to go, affix अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=148-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कञ्चिका|कंचिका
कञ्चिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. The branch of a bamboo.<BR>	 2. A small boil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=148-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कञ्चुक|कंचुक|कंचुकः|कञ्चुकः
कञ्चुक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. The skin of a snake.<BR>	 2. Armour, mail.<BR>	 3. A bodice or<BR>jacket.<BR>	 4. Cloth, clothes.<BR>	 5. A kind of drawers or short breeches.<BR>f. (-की) The name of a plant.<BR> E. कचि to bind or shine, affix उकन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=148-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कञ्चुकालु|कंचुकालु|कंचुकालुः|कञ्चुकालुः
कञ्चुकालु m. (-लुः) A snake.<BR> E. कञ्चुक a serpent's skin, and आलुक्<BR>poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=148-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कञ्चुकिन्|कंचुकिन्
कञ्चुकिन् m. (-की)<BR>	 1. An attendant on the women's apartments.<BR>	 2. A<BR>libidinous man, a debauchee.<BR>	 3. A serpent.<BR>	 4. Agallochum.<BR>	 5. Bar-<BR>ley.<BR>	 6. A sort of pulse, (Chenna.)<BR> E. कञ्चुक armour, &c. इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=148-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कञ्चुलिका|कंचुलिका
कञ्चुलिका f. (-का) A bodice or jacket.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=148-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कञ्ज|कंज|कञ्जं|कंजः|कञ्जः
कञ्ज mfn. (-ञ्जः-ञ्जा-ञ्जं) Produce in or from water.<BR>	 m. (-ञ्जः)<BR>	 1. A name<BR>of BRAHMĀ.<BR>	 2. The hair.<BR>	 n. (-ञ्जं)<BR>	 1. Nectar, the food of the<BR>immortals.<BR>	 3. A lotus.<BR> E. कं happiness, water, &c. and ज what is<BR>born or produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=148-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कञ्जक|कंजक|कंजकः|कञ्जकः
कञ्जक m. (-कः) A kind of bird, the Mayana: see कञ्जन<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=148-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कञ्जज|कंजज|कञ्जजः
कञ्जज m. (-जः) A name of BRAHMĀ.<BR> E. कञ्ज a lotus, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=148-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कञ्जन|कंजन|कंजनः|कञ्जनः
कञ्जन m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. The Mayana or Maina, (Gracula religiosa.)<BR>	 2. A name<BR>of KANDARPA, the deity of love.<BR> E. कचि to go, युच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=148-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कञ्जर|कंजर|कंजरः|कञ्जरः
कञ्जर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A name of BRAHMA.<BR>	 2. The sun.<BR>	 3. The belly.<BR>	 4. An<BR>elephant.<BR> E. कञ्ज a lotus, &c. ऋ to hate or injure, अच् or घञ् affix<BR>कञ्जार, the pen. made short; also derived by some from कजि, a<BR>Sautra root, to produce or grow, and अर Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=148-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कञ्जल|कंजल|कंजलः|कञ्जलः
कञ्जल m. (-लः) The Maina: see कञ्जन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=148-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कञ्जार|कंजार|कंजारः|कञ्जारः
कञ्जार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Muni or holy sage.<BR>	 2. BRAHMĀ, &c. see कञ्जर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=148-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कञ्जिका|कंजिका
कञ्जिका f. (-का) A Plant, (Siphonanthus Indica:) see ब्रह्मयष्टिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=148-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कट|कटः
कट r. 1st cl. (कटति)<BR>	 1. To go, to move.<BR>	 2. To live with difficulty. (इ)<BR>कटि (कण्टति) To go. (ए) कटे (कटति) 1. To rain.<BR>	 2. To encompass, to<BR>cover or screen. (ई) कटी (कटति) To go or approach: with प्र pre-<BR>fixed, verb 10th cl. (प्रकटयति) To appear, to become apparent or<BR>manifest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=148-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कट|कटः
कट mfn. (-टः-टी-टं) An agent in any action.<BR>	 mf. (-टः-टी)<BR>	 1. The hip.<BR>2. The hollow above the hip or the loins, also the hip and loins.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-टः)<BR>	 1. The temples of the elephant.<BR>	 2. A mat.<BR>	 3. A twist of straw<BR>or grass.<BR>	 4. A screen of the same.<BR>	 5. A corpse.<BR>	 6. A time or sea-<BR>son.<BR>	 7. Much, excessive.<BR>	 8. Grass.<BR>	 9. A place where dead bodies are<BR>burnt or buried, a place of sepulture.<BR>	 10. A hearse, a bier, a bed,<BR>&c. used for conveying a dead body.<BR>	 11. An annual plant.<BR>	 12. A<BR>thin piece of wood, a plank.<BR>	 f. (-टी) Long pepper.<BR> E. कट् to rain or<BR>encompass, अच् affix, fem. ङीष्; also कटि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=148-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटक|कटकं|कटकः
कटक mn. (-कः-कं)<BR>	 1. The side or ridge of a hill or mountain.<BR>	 2. Table<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=148-b" target="_blank">Page148-b+ 60</a>]<BR>land.<BR>	 3. Sea-salt.<BR>	 4. A ring placed as an ornament upon an ele-<BR>phant's tusk.<BR>	 5. A bracelet of gold, shell, &c.<BR>	 6. A zone.<BR>	 7. A<BR>royal metropolis.<BR>	 8. A city or town.<BR>	 9. A village.<BR>	 10. A house or<BR>dwelling.<BR>	 11. A camp.<BR>	 12. An army.<BR>	 13. A circle.<BR>	 14. A wheel. E.<BR>कट to encompass, कन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=148-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटकिन्
कटकिन् m. (-की) A mountain.<BR> E. कटक land on a hill, &c. and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=148-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटकोल|कटकोलः
कटकोल(-लः) A spitting vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=148-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटखादक|कटखादकं|कटखादकः
कटखादक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) An eater, one who eats voraciously.<BR>	 m. (-कः)<BR>1. A glass vessel, a tumbler or bowl.<BR>	 2. A crow.<BR>	 3. A jackal. E.<BR>कट much, or corpse, खाद् to eat, affix वुन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=148-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटङ्कट|कटंकट|कटंकटः|कटङ्कटः
कटङ्कट m. (-टः) A name of GANESA.<BR> E. कट a mat, &c. कट who goes,<BR>खच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=148-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटङ्कटेरी|कटंकटेरी
कटङ्कटेरी f. (-री)<BR>	 1. Turmeric.<BR>	 2. Yellow saunders.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=148-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटन|कटनं
कटन n. (-नं) Roof or thatch of a house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=148-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटपूतन|कटपूतनः
कटपूतन m. (-नः) A kind of goblin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=148-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटप्रू
कटप्रू m. (-प्रूः)<BR>	 1. A name of MAHADEVA.<BR>	 2. A kind of demigod, one of<BR>the class of Vidyadharas.<BR>	 3. A Rākṣasa, an imp or demon.<BR>	 4.<BR>Gambling, playing with dice.<BR>	 5. A worm.<BR> E. कट much, प्रु to go, क्विप्<BR>affix, and the final is made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=148-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटप्रोथ|कटप्रोथः
कटप्रोथ m. (-थः) The buttocks: see कटिप्रोथ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=148-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटभङ्ग|कटभंग|कटभङ्गः
कटभङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>	 1. Gleaning, plucking or gathering corn by the hand.<BR>2. Royal misfortune, as deposure, defeat, &c.<BR> E. कट, &c. भञ्ज् to<BR>break, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=148-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटभी
कटभी f. (-भी)<BR>	 1. A plant, (Heartpea, Cardiaspermum halicacabum.)<BR>2. Another creeper, (Clitoria ternata.)<BR> E. कट् to encompass, and<BR>भज् to serve, ड and ङीष् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=148-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटमालिनी
कटमालिनी f. (-नी) Wine or any vinous liquor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=148-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटम्ब|कटंबः|कटम्बः
कटम्ब m. (-म्बः)<BR>	 1. A kind of musical instrument.<BR>	 2. An arrow.<BR> E. कट्<BR>to go, and अम्ब Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=148-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटम्बरा
कटम्बरा f. (-रा) A medicinal plant: see कटुकी.<BR> E. कट् to surround, अच्<BR>affix; what invests the body, as sickness; वृ to screen or defend,<BR>मुम् inserted, and अच् and टाप् affixes; also कटम्भरा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=148-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटम्भरा|कटंभरा
कटम्भरा f. (-रा)<BR>	 1. A plant, (Pœderia fetida.)<BR>	 2. A medicinal plant,<BR>कटुकीः see the preceding.<BR>	 3. A sort of cucumber, (Cucumis Ma-<BR>draspatanus.)<BR>	 4. A female elephant.<BR>	 5. Red arsenic.<BR>	 6. A plant,<BR>(Aletris hyacinthoides:) see मुर्व्वा.<BR>	 7. Hog-weed. E. As before, भृ to<BR>nourish, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=148-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटव्रण|कटव्रणः
कटव्रण m. (-णः) A name of BHIMASENA, one of the five Pandava<BR>brothers.<BR> E. कट much, व्रण who wounds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=148-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटशर्करा
कटशर्करा f. (-रा) A plant: see गाङ्गेष्टी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=148-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटस्थल
कटस्थल n. (-लं)<BR>	 1. The hip and loins.<BR>	 2. An elephant's temples.<BR> E. कट,<BR>and स्थल place; also कटभू, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=148-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटाकु|कटाकुः
कटाकु m. (-कुः) A bird.<BR> E. कट् to go, काकु Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=148-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटाक्ष|कटाक्षः
कटाक्ष m. (-क्षः) A leer, a glance or side look.<BR> E. कट् to go, and अक्षि<BR>the eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=148-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटाक्षावेक्षण
कटाक्षावेक्षण n. (-णं) Casting lewd or amorous glances, ogling.<BR> E. कटाक्ष<BR>a leer, and अवेक्षण looking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=148-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटाग्नि|कटाग्निः
कटाग्नि m. (-ग्निः)<BR>	 1. A fire of grass or straw.<BR>	 2. Straw, &c. investing<BR>a criminal who is to be burnt and set on fire.<BR> E. कट, and अग्नि fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=148-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटायन|कटायनं
कटायन n. (-नं) A fragrant grass, (Andropogon muricatum.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=148-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटार|कटारः
कटार m. (-रः) A libidinous man, a lecher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=148-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटाह|कटाहः
कटाह m. (-हः)<BR>	 1. A shallow boiler for oil or butter.<BR>	 2. A frying pan.<BR>3. A winnowing basket.<BR>	 4. A turtle's shell.<BR>	 5. A young buffalo<BR>whose horns are just appearing.<BR>	 6. A Dwipa or division of the<BR>known continent, so called.<BR>	 7. Hell, the infernal regions.<BR>	 8. A<BR>well.<BR> E. कट much, &c. हन् to destroy, with आङ् prefixed, and ड aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=148-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटि|कटिः
कटि mf. (-टिः-टी)<BR>	 1. The hip.<BR>	 2. The buttocks.<BR>	 3. An elephant's cheek.<BR>E. कट् to go, कि affix, fem. ङीष्ः see कट and कटिप्रोथ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=148-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटितट
कटितट n. (-टं) The loins, the hip.<BR> E. कटि and तट shore.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=148-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटित्र|कटित्रं
कटित्र m. (-त्रः)<BR>	 1. An ornament of small bells worn round the loins.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=149-a" target="_blank">Page149-a+ 60</a>]<BR>2. A cloth so worn.<BR>	 3. Armour for the hip and loins.<BR> E. कटि the<BR>hip, and त्र what preserves, from त्रै with ड aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=148-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटिदेश|कटिदेशः
कटिदेश m. (-शः) The loins.<BR> E. कटि and देश place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=149-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटिन्
कटिन् mfn. (-टी-टिनी-टि)<BR>	 1. Matted, screened.<BR>	 2. Loined, having<BR>handsome loins, &c.<BR>	 m. (-टी) An elephant.<BR> E. कट an elephant's<BR>temples, &c. इनि pos. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=149-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटिप्रोथ|कटिप्रोथः
कटिप्रोथ m. (-थः) The buttocks.<BR> E. कटि the hip or loins, and प्रोथ to be<BR>equal to; also written कटप्रोथ, कटीप्रोथ and severally कटि and प्रोथ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=149-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटिरोहक|कटिरोहकः
कटिरोहक m. (-कः) The rider of an elephant, as distinct from the driver,<BR>the person that sits upon the loins.<BR> E. कटि the loins, रुह् to mount,<BR>and वुञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=149-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटिल्लक|कटिल्लकः
कटिल्लक m. (-कः) A species of the balsam apple, (Momordica charantia.)<BR>E. कट् to go, &c. इल्ल affix, कन् added; also कठिल्लक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=149-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटिशीर्षक|कटिशीर्षकः
कटिशीर्षक m. (-कः) The hip and loins, or the hollow above the hip. E.<BR>कटि, शीर्ष the head or superior part, कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=149-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटिशृङ्खला|कटिशृंखला
कटिशृङ्खला f. (-ला) A girdle of small bells.<BR> E. कटि the loins, and शृङ्कला<BR>a chain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=149-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटिसूत्र|कटिसूत्रं
कटिसूत्र n. (-त्रं) A female zone or waist-band.<BR> E. कटि the loins, and सूत्र<BR>a thread.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=149-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटी
कटी f. (-टी) See कटि and कट.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=149-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटीतल|कटीतलः
कटीतल m. (-लः) A crooked sword, a sabre or scymitar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=149-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटीर|कटीरं|कटीरः
कटीर mn. (-रः-रं)<BR>	 1. The cavity of the loins, or the iliac regions.<BR>	 m. (-रः)<BR>1. Mons veneris.<BR>	 2. A cave.<BR> E. कट् to go, and ईर् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=149-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटीरक|कटीरकं|कटीरकः
कटीरक m. (-कः) The posteriors.<BR> E. कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=149-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटु|कटुः
कटु mfn. (-टुः-टुः or -ट्वी-टु)<BR>	 1. Pungent.<BR>	 2. Envious.<BR>	 3. Fierce, impetuous,<BR>hot.<BR>	 4. Fragrant.<BR>	 5. Bad scented, ill smelling.<BR>	 6. Displeasing, dis-<BR>agreeable.<BR>	 m. (-टुः)<BR>	 1. Pungency or a pungent taste.<BR>	 2. A flower,<BR>(Michelia champaca.)<BR>	 3. Champhor.<BR>	 4. A sort of gourd, (Trichosan-<BR>thes.)<BR>	 n. (-टु)<BR>	 1. An improper action, an act which ought not to<BR>have been done.<BR>	 2. Blaming, reviling, scandal.<BR>	 f. (-टुः)<BR>	 1. The name<BR>of a medicinal plant; also कटुका and कटुकी.<BR>	 2. A plant which<BR>bears a fragrant seed: see प्रियङ्गु.<BR>	 3. Mustard.<BR> E. कट् to go, &c. and<BR>उ Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=149-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटुक|कटुकं|कटुकः
कटुक mf. (-कः-की)<BR>	 1. A plant, the bark and seed of which have an acrid<BR>and bitter taste, and are used in medicine for worms, dysentery, &c.<BR>(Wrightea antidysenterica.)<BR>	 2. Gigantic swallow wort, (Colotropis<BR>gigantea.<BR>	 3. A fragrant kind of grass.<BR>	 4. Mustard.<BR>	 5. A gourd:<BR>see पटोल f. (-का or -की) A medicinal plant, used as a sedative and<BR>laxative; also कटुरोहिणी.<BR>	 n. (-कं) A compound of three pungent<BR>substances, a black pepper, long pepper, and dry ginger: see<BR>त्रिकटु.<BR> E. कटु pungent, and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=149-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटुकन्द|कटुकन्दः
कटुकन्द mn. (-न्दः-न्द्रं)<BR>	 1. A plant, (Morunga guilandina, and Hyperan-<BR>thera.)<BR>	 2. Ginger, the fresh root or the plant.<BR>	 3. Garlic.<BR> E. कटु, and<BR>कन्द a root; having a pungent root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=149-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटुकालावु|कटुकालावुः
कटुकालावु m. (-वुः) A bitter gourd.<BR> E. कटुक pungent and acrid, अलावु<BR>a gourd.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=149-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटुकीट|कटुकीटः
कटुकीट m. (-टः) A gnat or musquito.<BR> E. कटु, and कीट an insect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=149-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटुकीटक|कटुकीटकः
कटुकीटक m. (-कः) A gnat or musquito.<BR> E. कटु fierce, and कीटक a<BR>worm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=149-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटुक्वाण|कटुक्वाणः
कटुक्वाण m. (-णः) A bird, jacana, (Parra goensis.)<BR> E. कटु disagreeable,<BR>क्वाण sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=149-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटुग्रन्थि|कटुग्रन्थिः
कटुग्रन्थि m. (-न्थिः) Ginger, the root.<BR> E. कटु pungent, and ग्रन्थि joint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=149-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटुच्छद|कटुच्छदः
कटुच्छद m. (-दः) The name of a plant; also तगर.<BR> E. कटु and छद a leaf:<BR>having a pungent leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=149-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटुता
कटुता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Pungency, sharpness.<BR>	 2. Testiness, irritability.<BR> E. कटु<BR>and तल् affix; also with त्व, कटुत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=149-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटुतिक्तिका
कटुतिक्तिका f. (-का) A bitter gourd.<BR> E. कटु, and तिक्त bitter, कन् affix with<BR>the fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=149-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटुतुम्बी
कटुतुम्बी f. (-म्बी) See the preceding.<BR> E. कटु pungent, here meaning bitter-<BR>ly so, and तुम्बी a gourd.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=149-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटुत्रय|कटुत्रयं
कटुत्रय n. (-यं) The aggregate of three spices, ginger, and long and<BR>black pepper<BR> E. कटु, and त्रय three.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=149-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटुनिष्प्लाव|कटुनिष्प्लावः
कटुनिष्प्लाव m. (-वः) Grain not inundated.<BR> E. कटु, and निष्प्लाव non-<BR>inundation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=149-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटुपत्र|कटुपत्रः
कटुपत्र m. (-त्रः) A medicinal plant, (Oldenlandia biflora)<BR> E. कटु pungent,<BR>and पत्र leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=149-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटुफल|कटुफलः
कटुफल m. (-लः) A sort of cucumber, (Trichosanthes diœca.)<BR> E. कटु and<BR>फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=149-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटुभङ्ग|कटुभङ्गः
कटुभङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः) Dried ginger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=149-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटुभद्र|कटुभद्रं|कटुभद्रः
कटुभद्र n. (-द्रं) Ginger either fresh or dry.<BR> E. कटु, and भद्र auspicious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=149-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटुर|कटुरं|कटुरः
कटुर n. (-रं) Buttermilk.<BR> E. कटु and रा to give, affix ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=149-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटुरव|कटुरवः
कटुरव m. (-वः) A frog.<BR> E. कटु, and रव sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=149-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटुरोहिणी
कटुरोहिणी f. (-णी) A medicinal plant: see कटुकी.<BR> E. कटु pungent, and<BR>रोहिणी that grows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=149-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटुवार्त्ताकी|कटुवार्ताकी
कटुवार्त्ताकी f. (-की) A variety of solanum.<BR> E. कटु and वार्त्ताकी the eggplant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=149-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटुवीजा
कटुवीजा f. (-जा) Long pepper.<BR> E. कटु and वीज seed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=149-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटुस्नेह|कटुस्नेहः
कटुस्नेह m. (-हः) The mustard sea plant, (Sinapis dichotoma.)<BR> E. कटु,<BR>and स्नेह oily substance: yielding a pungent oil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=149-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटूत्कट|कटूत्कटं
कटूत्कट n. (-टं) Ginger.<BR> E. कटु, and उत्कट best, and with कन् added<BR>कटूत्कटक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=149-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटोरा
कटोरा f. (-रा) A shallow cup.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=149-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटोल|कटोलः
कटोल m. (-लः) A man of an inferior and degraded tribe, a Chandala,<BR>a Pariah, &c.<BR>	 2. A pungent flavour.<BR> E. कट् to go, ओलच् Uṇādi<BR>affix; also कटोलक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=149-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटोलवीणा
कटोलवीणा f. (-णा) A kind of lute played by the common people. E.<BR>कटोल a Chandala, and वीणा a lute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=149-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कट्टार|कट्टारः
कट्टार m. (-रः) A weapon, a dagger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=149-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कट्फल|कट्फलः
कट्फल m. (-लः) A small tree found in the north-west of Hindustan,<BR>the bark and seeds of which are used in medicine, and as aroma-<BR>tics; the fruit also is eaten; the common name is Kayaphala.<BR>	 f.<BR>(-ला)<BR>	 1. A plant, (Gmelina arborea, Rox.)<BR>	 2. The egg plant, &c.<BR>E. कट instead of कटु acrid, and फल fruit, fem. affix टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=149-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कट्वङ्ग|कट्वङ्गः
कट्वङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>	 1. A plant, (Bignonia Indica.)<BR>	 2. A name of DILIPA a<BR>king of Ayodhya.<BR> E. कटु pungent, &c. अङ्ग bark, body, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=149-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कट्वर|कट्वरं
कट्वर n. (-रं)<BR>	 1. Sauce, condiment.<BR>	 2. Buttermilk.<BR>	 3. The skim or whey<BR>of curds.<BR> E. कट् to rain, &c. वरच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=149-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कठ|कठः
कठ r. 1st cl. (कठति) To live in distress. (इ) कठि r. 1st and 10th cls.<BR>(कण्ठति-ते, कण्ठयति)<BR>	 1. To grieve.<BR>	 2. To recollect. With उद् prefixed,<BR>to regret or miss, to lament, to bewail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=149-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कठ|कठः
कठ m. (-ठः)<BR>	 1. The name of a Muni or saint.<BR>	 2. A note or simple<BR>sound.<BR>	 3. A portion of the Yajur Veda.<BR>	 4. A Mantra or mystical<BR>prayer.<BR>	 5. A Brahman.<BR>	 6. A Brahman versed in the Vedas, especi-<BR>ally in the Rig Veda.<BR>	 7. A student of the same.<BR>	 8. Trouble, dis-<BR>tress.<BR>	 f. (-ठी) The wife of a Brahman.<BR> E. कठ् to be confused, and<BR>अप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=149-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कठधूर्त्त|कठधूर्त|कठधूर्तः
कठधूर्त्त m. (-र्त्तः) A BRAHMAN skilled in the Katha branch of the Vedas.<BR>E. कठ, and धूर्त्त cunning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=149-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कठमर्द्द|कठमर्द|कठमर्दः|कठमर्द्दः
कठमर्द्द m. (-र्द्दः) A name of ŚIVA.<BR> E. कठ distress, मर्द्द who dissipates.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=149-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कठर|कठरः
कठर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Hard.<BR> E. कठ trouble, and र from रा to take or give,<BR>affix ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=149-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कठश्रोत्रिय|कठश्रोत्रियः
कठश्रोत्रिय m. (-यः) A BRAHMAN who has studied the Katha portion of<BR>the Vedas.<BR> E. कठ, and श्रोत्रिय a BRAHMAN.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=149-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कठाध्यापक|कठाध्यापकः
कठाध्यापक m. (-कः) A teacher of the Katha portion of the Veda.<BR> E. कठ,<BR>and अध्यापक a teacher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=149-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कठाहक|कठाहकः
कठाहक m. (-कः) A gallinule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=149-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कठिका
कठिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. Chalk.<BR>	 2. The Tulasi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=149-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कठिञ्जर|कठिंजरः|कठिञ्जरः
कठिञ्जर m. (-रः) A plant worshipped by the Hindus, commonly Tulasi,<BR>(Ocymum sanctum, or sacred basil.)<BR> E. कठिन hard, and जृ to<BR>destroy, affix अच्, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=149-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कठिन|कठिनं|कठिनः
कठिन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>	 1. Hard, solid.<BR>	 2. Unkind, severe.<BR>	 3. Paralysed,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=150-a" target="_blank">Page150-a+ 60</a>]<BR>rendered stiff or rigid.<BR>	 4. Difficult, obscure.<BR>	 nf. (-नं-ना) An earthen<BR>vessel.<BR>	 f. (-ना) A sweetmeat made with refined sugar. (-नी or -निका)<BR>Chalk.<BR> E. कठ् to be confounded, and इनच् Uṇādi affix, fem. affixes<BR>ठाप् and ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=149-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कठिनता
कठिनता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Firmness, hardness.<BR>	 2. Severity.<BR>	 3. Difficulty, ob-<BR>scurity.<BR> E. तल् added to the last; also with त्व. कठिनत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=150-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कठिनपृष्ठ|कठिनपृष्ठः
कठिनपृष्ठ m. (-ष्ठः) A tortoise.<BR> E. कठिन, and पृष्ठ back; also कठिनपृष्ठक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=150-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कठिनहृदय
कठिनहृदय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Hard-hearted, cruel, unkind.<BR> E. कठिन, and<BR>हृदय the heart.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=150-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कठिनान्तःकरण
कठिनान्तःकरण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Harsh, cruel, severe.<BR> E. कठिन, and अन्तः-<BR>करण disposition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=150-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कठिल्ल|कठिल्लः
कठिल्ल m. (-ल्लः) A plant, (Momordica charantia:) see कटिल्ल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=150-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कठिल्लक|कठिल्लकः
कठिल्लक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A plant: see the preceding.<BR>	 2. A name of Tulasi<BR>or holy basil.<BR>	 3. Hogweed.<BR> E. कन् added to the preceding: see<BR>कटिल्ल and कटिल्लक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=150-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कठेर|कठेरः
कठेर m. (-रः) A needy or distressed man, a pauper.<BR> E. कठ् to be dis-<BR>tressed, and एरक् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=150-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कठेरु
कठेरु m. (-रुः) The Indian Plutus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=150-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कठोर|कठोरः
कठोर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>	 1. Hard, solid.<BR>	 2. Severe, cruel.<BR>	 3. Full, com-<BR>plete, full-grown.<BR>	 4. Full, (as the moon.)<BR> E. कठ् to be distressed,<BR>&c. आरन् Uṇādi affix; also कठोल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=150-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कठोरता
कठोरता f. (ता)<BR>	 1. Hardness, firmness.<BR>	 2. Severity, rigor.<BR> E. तल् added<BR>to the preceding; also कठोरत्वं with त्व aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=150-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कठोल|कठोलः
कठोल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) See कठोर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=150-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कड|कडः
कड r. 1st and 6th cls. (कडति) To be confused or disturbed by pleasure<BR>or pain, to be proud or mad, (the roots differ in some of the in-<BR>flections). (इ) कडि r. 1st cl. (कण्डते) The same as the preceding; also<BR>r. 1st and 10th cls. (कण्डति, कण्डयति)<BR>	 1. To break off a part, to tear,<BR>to separate or detach.<BR>	 2. To remove the chaff or husk of grain,<BR>&c.<BR>	 3. To preserve.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=150-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कड|कडः
कड mfn. (-डः-डा-डं) Ignorant, stupid.<BR> E. कड् to be perplexed, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=150-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कडक|कडकं
कडक n. (-कं) Sea salt obtained by evaporation.<BR> E. कड् to separate,<BR>वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=150-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कडङ्कर|कडंकर|कडंकरः|कडङ्करः
कडङ्कर m. (-रः) Straw, the stalks of various sorts of pulse, &c.<BR> E. कड<BR>mad, कृ to make, खच् affix; also कडङ्गर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=150-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कडङ्करीय|कडंकरीय
कडङ्करीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) To be fed with straw.<BR> E. कडङ्कर, and छ affix;<BR>also with यत्, कडङ्कर्य्य; and from कडङ्ग, कडङ्गरीय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=150-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कडङ्ग|कडंगः|कडङ्गः
कडङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः) A spirituous liquor, a kind of rum.<BR> E. कड् to be intoxi-<BR>cated, अङ्ग aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=150-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कडङ्गर|कडंगर|कडंगरः|कडङ्गरः
कडङ्गर m. (-रः) Straw, chaff.<BR> E. कड, रक affix, अङ्गच् inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=150-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कडत्र|कडत्रं
कडत्र n. (-त्रं) A vessel.<BR> E. गड् to distil, अत्रन् Uṇādi affix, and क substi-<BR>tuted for ग; also कलत्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=150-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कडम्ब|कडंब|कडंबः|कडम्बः
कडम्ब m. (-म्बः)<BR>	 1. The stalk of a potherb.<BR>	 2. The end or point.<BR> E. कड्<BR>to separate, &c. अम्बच् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=150-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कडम्बी
कडम्बी f. (-म्बी) A potherb, (Convolvulus repens:) see कलम्बी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=150-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कडार|कडारः
कडार mfn. (-रः-री-रं) Tawny.<BR>	 m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Tawny, (the colour.)<BR>	 2. A<BR>servant.<BR> E. कड् to be confused, आरण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=150-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कडितुल|कडितुलः
कडितुल m. (-लः) A sword, a scymitar, a sacrificial knife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=150-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कड्ड
कड्ड r. 1st cl. (कड्डति) To be rough, to be harsh or severe: the pen.<BR>is originally द.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=150-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण|कणः
कण(म) r. 1st cl. (कणति)<BR>	 1. To sound.<BR>	 2. To cry as in distress. (ऋ) कण<BR>r. 1st cl. (कणति) To go or approach. r. 10th cl. (कणयति) To wink,<BR>to cover or close the eye with the lids or lashes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=150-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण|कणः
कण mf. (-णः-णी or -णिका)<BR>	 1. Small, minute.<BR>	 2. An atom, a minute<BR>particle.<BR>	 m. (-णः)<BR>	 1. An eye of corn.<BR>	 2. The spark or facet of gem.<BR>3. A spark of fire.<BR>	 4. A drop of water, &c.<BR>	 f. (-णा)<BR>	 1. Cummin seed.<BR>2. Long pepper.<BR>	 3. A kind of fly, (कुम्भीरमक्षिका) the crocodile fly? E.<BR>कण् to contract, अच् affix, fem. टाप् or ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=150-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कणजीर|कणजीरः
कणजीर n. (-रं) A white kind of cummin seed.<BR> E. कण small, जीर<BR>cummin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=150-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कणजीरक|कणजीरकं
कणजीरक n. (-कं) Small cummin seed.<BR> E. कण minute, and जीरक<BR>cummin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=150-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कणभक्षक|कणभक्षकः
कणभक्षक m. (-कः) A kind of bird.<BR> E. कण pepper, and भक्षक who eats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=150-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कणलाभ|कणलाभः
कणलाभ m. (-भः) A whirlpool.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=150-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कणाटीन|कणाटीनः
कणाटीन m. (-नः) A wagtail.<BR> E. कण little, अट् to go, and ईनच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=150-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कणाटीर|कणाटीरः
कणाटीर m. (-रः) A wagtail; also कणाटीरक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=150-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कणाद|कणादः
कणाद m. (-दः)<BR>	 1. The name of a Muni, also called Kasyapa: the author<BR>of the Vaisheshika philosophy.<BR>	 2. A goldsmith.<BR> E. कण a little, and<BR>अद् to eat, referring to the abstemiousness of the saint; or आदा to<BR>take, alluding the proverbial dishonesty of the artificer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=150-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कणिक|कणिकः
कणिक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A small particle, as a crystal, an eye of corn, &c.<BR>	 2.<BR>An enemy.<BR>	 3. Whirling round a set of lamps at sacrificial ceremo-<BR>nies.<BR>	 4. The heart of wheat, commonly Suji, sharps or semoule.<BR>	 f.<BR>(-का)<BR>	 1. An atom, a small particle.<BR>	 2. Small, minute: see कण.<BR>	 3. A<BR>plant, (Premna spinosa:) see गणिकारिका 4. A kind of rice.<BR> E. कण<BR>small, वुन् affix, and इट् inserted, fem. affix टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=150-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कणित|कणितं
कणित n. (-तं) A cry or sound uttered through pain.<BR> E. कण् to sound, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=150-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कणिश|कणिशं|कणिशः
कणिश n. (-शं) An ear or spike of corn.<BR> E. कण small, &c. affix श.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=150-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कणीक|कणीकं|कणीकः
कणीक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Small, diminutive.<BR> E. कण to be small, ईकन्<BR>Uṇādi affix; it is also written कनीक and कणिक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=150-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कणीचि|कणीचिः
कणीचि f. (-चिः)<BR>	 1. A creeper in flower.<BR>	 2. A cart.<BR>	 3. The Abrus precato-<BR>rius.<BR> E. कण to wink, ईचि Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=150-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कणीयस्
कणीयस् mfn. (-यान्-यसी-यः)<BR>	 1. Very small.<BR>	 2. Young, younger.<BR> E. कण<BR>small, and ईयसुन् superlative affix; also कनीयस.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=150-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कणेर|कणेरः
कणेर m. (-रः) A tree, (Cascaria ovata, &c.)<BR>	 f. (-रा) A courtezan.<BR>	 2. A<BR>she-elephant.<BR> E. कण् to go, एर affix, or with एरु affix कणेरु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=150-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्टक|कंटक|कंटकं|कंटकः|कण्टकः
कण्टक mn. (-कः-कं)<BR>	 1. A thorn.<BR>	 2. A paltry foe.<BR>	 3. A fish bone.<BR>	 4. Hor-<BR>ripilation, or the erection of the hair of the body.<BR>	 5. Any annoy-<BR>ance or source of vexation.<BR>	 6. A term in the Nyaya philosophy, im-<BR>plying refutation of argument, detection of error, &c.<BR>	 m. (-कः)<BR>	 1.<BR>A work-shop, a manufactory.<BR>	 2. Fault, defect.<BR>	 3. The point of<BR>a pin or needle.<BR>	 4. A fish or marine monster, the symbol of<BR>KĀMADEVA: see मकर.<BR>	 5. A bamboo.<BR> E. कटि to divide, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=150-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्टकद्रुम|कंटकद्रुम|कण्टकद्रुमः
कण्टकद्रुम m. (-मः) The Salmali or silk-cotton tree.<BR> E. कण्टक, and द्रुम a<BR>tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=150-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्टकफल|कंटकफल|कण्टकफलः
कण्टकफल m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. The Jaka, or bread-fruit tree, (Artocarpus in-<BR>tegrifolia.)<BR>	 2. Another plant: see गोक्षुर.<BR>	 3. The castor oil tree.<BR>	 4. The<BR>Datura.<BR> E. कण्टक a spike, and फल fruit: the term is applicable to<BR>any plant, the fruit of which is invested with a hairy or thorny<BR>coat; also कण्टकिफल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=150-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्टकभुज्|कंटकभुज्
कण्टकभुज् m. (-भुक्) A camel.<BR> E. कण्टक and भुज् who eats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=150-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्टकमर्द्दन|कण्टकमर्दन
कण्टकमर्द्दन mfn. (-नः-नी-नं)<BR>	 1. What treads down or extracts thorns.<BR>	 2.<BR>What bridles or suppresses disturbances, annoyances, &c.<BR>	 n. (-नं)<BR>1. Beating down thorns.<BR>	 2. Suppressing disturbances, &c.<BR> E. कण्टक,<BR>and मर्द्दन trampling on.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=150-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्टकश्रेणी
कण्टकश्रेणी f. (-णी) A porcupine.<BR> E. कण्टक and श्रेणी a row.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=150-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्टकागार|कण्टकागारः
कण्टकागार m. (-रः) A porcupine.<BR> E. कण्टक and अगार or आगार a house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=150-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्टकारिका|कंटकारिका
कण्टकारिका f. (-का) A sort of prickly nightshade, (Solanum jacquini.)<BR>E. कण्टक a thorn, ऋ to go, अण् affix, कन् added with the feminine<BR>termination; also कण्टकारी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=150-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्टकारी
कण्टकारी f. (-री)<BR>	 1. A prickly nightshade: see the preceding.<BR>	 2. The<BR>silk-cotton tree, (Bombax heptaphyllum.)<BR>	 3. Another plant, com-<BR>monly Buinchhi, (Flacourtia sapida, Rox.) E. As before.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=150-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्टकाल|कंटकालः|कण्टकालः
कण्टकाल m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. The bread-fruit tree or Jaka: see कण्टकफल.<BR>	 2.<BR>Species of the coral tree, (Erythrina Indica.)<BR> E. कण्टक a thorn,<BR>आला to take, affix ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=150-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्टकाशन|कंटकाशन|कण्टकाशनः
कण्टकाशन m. (-नः) A camel.<BR> E. कण्टक, and अशन food; whose food is of<BR>thorns, thistles, &c.; also कण्टकभुज्, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=150-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्टकाष्ठील|कण्टकाष्ठीलः
कण्टकाष्ठील m. (-लः) A kind of fish, one which has many bones.<BR> E. कण्टक,<BR>अस्थि a bone, and ईलच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=150-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्टकिज
कण्टकिज mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>	 1. Produced from a fish.<BR>	 2. Borne by the mi-<BR>mosa tree.<BR> E. कण्टकिन्, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=151-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्टकिन्|कंटकिन्
कण्टकिन् mfn. (-की-किनी-कि)<BR>	 1. Thorny, prickly.<BR>	 2. Vexatious, annoying.<BR>m. (-की)<BR>	 1. A fish.<BR>	 2. A tree, (Mimosa catechu.)<BR>	 3. A plant. (Van-<BR>gueria spinosa.)<BR>	 4. A bamboo.<BR>	 5. The jujube.<BR> E. कण्टक a thorn or<BR>small bone, and इनि poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=151-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्टकिफल|कंटकिफल|कण्टकिफलः
कण्टकिफल m. (-लः) The Indian bread-fruit tree or Jaka. (Artocarpus<BR>integrifolia:) see कण्टकफल; also कण्टकीफल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=151-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्टकिल|कंटकिल|कंटकिलः|कण्टकिलः
कण्टकिल m. (-लः) A thorny kind of bamboo, (Bambusa spinosa, Rox.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=151-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्टकीफल|कण्टकीफलः
कण्टकीफल m. (-लः) See कण्टकिफल, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=151-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्टकोद्धरण
कण्टकोद्धरण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Weeding, extracting thorns, &c.<BR>	 2. Removing<BR>annoyances.<BR>	 3. Extirpating thieves, rogues, &c. or all national or<BR>public nuisances.<BR> E. कण्टक and उद्धरण extracting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=151-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्टपत्र|कण्टपत्रः
कण्टपत्र m. (-त्रः) A plant, commonly Buinchhi, (Flacourtia sapida,<BR>Rox.) and कण्टपत्रक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=151-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्टफल
कण्टफल m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. The jack tree.<BR>	 2. The Datura plant.<BR>	 3. The castor<BR>oil plant.<BR> E. कण्ट for कण्टक a thorn or spike, फल fruit: see कण्टकफल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=151-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्टल|कंटलः|कण्टलः
कण्टल m. (-लः) The Babul, a tree yielding a species of gum arabic,<BR>(Acacia Arabica,) the branches are prickly, whence the name. E.<BR>कण्ट for कण्टक a thorn, and ल from ला to take or have.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=151-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्टाकारिन्
कण्टाकारिन् m. (-री) The jack tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=151-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्टाफल|कण्टाफलः
कण्टाफल m. (-लः) The Jaca or Jack tree: see कण्टकफल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=151-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्ठ|कंठ|कंठं|कंठः|कण्ठः
कण्ठ mfn. (-ण्ठः-ण्ठा or -ण्ठी-ण्ठं)<BR>	 1. The throat.<BR>	 2. Sound, especially gut-<BR>tural sound.<BR>	 3. Near, proximate.<BR>	 m. (-ण्ठः)<BR>	 1. A tree, (Vangueria<BR>spinosa.)<BR>	 2. The space of an inch from the edge of the hole in<BR>which sacrificial fire is deposited f. (-ण्ठी)<BR>	 1. A rope or leather<BR>round the neck of a horse.<BR>	 2. A necklace, a collar.<BR> E. कण् to sound,<BR>ठ Uṇādi affix, fem. affix टाप् or ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=151-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्ठकूणिका|कंठकूणिका
कण्ठकूणिका f. (-का) The Vina or Indian lute.<BR> E. कण्ठ the throat, कूण् to<BR>sound, and ठक् affix; sounded like the larynx.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=151-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्ठग
कण्ठग mfn. (-गः-गा-गं) Extending to the throat or swallow.<BR> E. कण्ठ and<BR>ग what goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=151-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्ठतलासिका
कण्ठतलासिका f. (-का) The leather or rope passing round the neck of<BR>a horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=151-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्ठनीडक|कंठनीडक|कण्ठनीडकः
कण्ठनीडक m. (-कः) A kite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=151-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्ठनीलक|कंठनीलक|कण्ठनीलकः
कण्ठनीलक m. (-कः) A torch, a whisp of lighted straw, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=151-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्ठपाशक|कंठपाशक|कण्ठपाशकः
कण्ठपाशक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A halter.<BR>	 2. A rope passing round an elephant's<BR>neck.<BR> E. कण्ठ, and पाशक a fetter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=151-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्ठभूषा|कंठभूषा
कण्ठभूषा f. (-षा) A collar or short necklace.<BR> E. कण्ठ the throat, and भूषा<BR>an ornament.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=151-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्ठमणि|कंठमणि|कण्ठमणिः
कण्ठमणि m. (-णिः) A jewel worn on the throat.<BR> E. कण्ठ, and मणि a gem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=151-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्ठलग्न
कण्ठलग्न mfn. (-ग्नः-ग्ना-ग्नं)<BR>	 1. Fastened or suspended round the throat.<BR>2. Clinging to, embracing.<BR> E. कण्ठ, and लग्न attached to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=151-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्ठलता
कण्ठलता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. A collar.<BR>	 2. A horse's halter.<BR> E. कण्ठ, and लता a<BR>creeper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=151-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्ठसज्जन|कंठसज्जन
कण्ठसज्जन n. (-नं) Hanging on or round the throat.<BR> E. कण्ठ, and सज्जन<BR>equipping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=151-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्ठस्थ
कण्ठस्थ mfn. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थं)<BR>	 1. Sticking in the throat.<BR>	 2. Being in or upon<BR>the throat.<BR>	 3. Guttural.<BR>	 4. Having by rote, ready to repeat.<BR> E. कण्ठ,<BR>and स्थ what stays.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=151-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्ठागत
कण्ठागत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Come in to the throat, (breath, &c.)<BR> E. कण्ठ,<BR>and आगत come.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=151-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्ठाग्नि|कण्ठाग्निः
कण्ठाग्नि m. (-ग्निः) A bird.<BR> E. कण्ठ, and अग्नि fire, and figuratively di-<BR>gestive faculty; digesting in the throat or gizzard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=151-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्ठाल|कंठाल|कंठालः|कण्ठालः
कण्ठाल m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. A boat.<BR>	 2. A hoe, a spade.<BR>	 3. War.<BR>	 4. An esculent<BR>root, (Arum.)<BR>	 5. A camel.<BR>	 f. (-ला) A churning vessel.<BR> E. कण्ठ the<BR>throat, अल् to ornament, &c अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=151-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्ठावसक्त
कण्ठावसक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं) Embracing, clinging to the neck.<BR> E. कण्ठ,<BR>and अवसक्त fastened to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=151-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्ठिका|कंठिका
कण्ठिका f. (-का) A necklace of one string or row.<BR> E. कण्ठी and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=151-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्ठीरव|कंठीरव|कण्ठीरवः
कण्ठीरव m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. A lion, elephant in rut.<BR>	 2. A pigeon.<BR> E. कण्ठ the<BR>throat, and रव sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=151-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्ठेकाल|कंठेकाल|कंठेकालः|कण्ठेकालः
कण्ठेकाल m. (-लः) A name of ŚIVA.<BR> E. कण्ठे in the throat, काल black,<BR>black-necked; see नीलकण्ठ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=151-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्ठ्य|कंठ्य|कण्ठ्यः
कण्ठ्य mfn. (-ण्ठ्यः-ण्ठ्या-ण्ठ्यं) Guttural, belonging to the throat, pro-<BR>nounced from the throat, &c.<BR> E. कण्ठ and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=151-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्डन|कंडन|कंडनं|कण्डनं
कण्डन n. (-नं) Threshing, separating the chaff from grain.<BR>	 f. (-नी) A<BR>wooden bowl or mortar, in which the cleaning or threshing of<BR>grain is performed.<BR> E. कडि to divide, ल्युट् affix, fem. do. ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=151-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्डरा|कंडरा
कण्डरा f. (-रा) A principal vessel of the body, a large artery, vein, &c.<BR>E. कडि to divide, अरन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=151-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्डु|कंडु|कंडुः|कण्डुः
कण्डु f. (-ण्डुः)<BR>	 1. The itch, itching.<BR>	 2. Scratching: see कण्डू.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=151-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्डुरा
कण्डुरा f. (-रा) Cowach: see कण्डूरा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=151-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्डू|कंडू
कण्डू n. (ञ) कण्डूञ् Sautra root, (कण्डूयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To itch.<BR>	 2. To scratch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=151-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्डू|कंडू
कण्डू f. (-ण्डूः)<BR>	 1. The itch, itching.<BR>	 2. Scratching.<BR> E. कण्डूञ् to itch,<BR>affix क्विप्; also with the final short, कण्डु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=151-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्डूकरी
कण्डूकरी f. (-री) Cowach, (Carpopogon pruriens.)<BR> E. कण्डू itching, and<BR>कर what makes, ङीप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=151-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्डूघ्न|कण्डूघ्नः
कण्डूघ्न m. (-घ्नः) Cassia, (fistula.)<BR> E. कण्डू and घ्न what destroys.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=151-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्डूति|कंडूति|कंडूतिः|कण्डूतिः
कण्डूति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Itching, the itch.<BR>	 2. Scratching.<BR> E. कण्डू and क्तिन्<BR>affix; also कण्डू, कण्डूयन, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=151-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्डूयत्
कण्डूयत् mfn. (-यन्-यती-यत्) Scratching, rubbing.<BR> E. कण्डू to itch, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=151-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्डूयन|कंडूयन|कण्डूयनं
कण्डूयन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Itching.<BR>	 2. Scratching; also कण्डूया and कण्डू. E. As<BR>before, affixes यक् and ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=151-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्डूयनक|कंडूयनक|कण्डूयनकः
कण्डूयनक m. (-कः) A tickler, one who ticklace or scratches.<BR> E. कण्डूतन<BR>and क who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=151-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्डूया|कंडूया
कण्डूया f. (-या)<BR>	 1. Itching.<BR>	 2. Scratching.<BR> E. कण्डू to itch, affixes यक्<BR>and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=151-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्डूरा|कंडूरा
कण्डूरा f. (-रा) Cowach, (Carpopogon pruriens.)<BR> E. कण्डू itching, and रा<BR>what makes, from रा to take or give, affixes क and टाप्; alluding<BR>to the irritating property of the leaves of this plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=151-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्डूल|कंडूल|कण्डूलः
कण्डूल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Itchy, having the itch.<BR>	 m. (-लः) An esculent<BR>root, (Arum.)<BR> E. कण्डू and ला to have, ड aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=151-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्डोल|कंडोल|कंडोलः|कण्डोलः
कण्डोल m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. A basket, a safe, any place in which provisions are<BR>kept.<BR>	 2. A camel.<BR> E. कडि to divide, ओलच् Uṇādi affix; also with<BR>कन् added कण्डोलक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=151-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्डोलक|कंडोलकः|कण्डोलकः
कण्डोलक m. (-कः) A safe, a store room: see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=151-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्डोलवीणा
कण्डोलवीणा f. (-णा) A vulgar lute.<BR> E. कण्डोल here implying a Chandala,<BR>and वीणा the Vina or Indian lute; also कटोल वीणा and कण्डोली.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=151-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्डोली|कंडोली
कण्डोली f. (-ली) See the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=151-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्ड्वोघ|कण्ड्वोघः
कण्ड्वोघ m. (-घः) A caterpillar.<BR> E. कण्डु itching, and ओघ and abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=151-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्व|कण्वं|कण्वः
कण्व m. (-ण्वः) The name of a celebrated Muni or saint.<BR>	 n. (-ण्वं) Sin. E.<BR>कण् to sound, क्वन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=151-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कत|कतः
कत m. (-तः)<BR>	 1. The name of a Muni or saint.<BR>	 2. The clearing nut plant.<BR>E. कै to sound, अत Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=151-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कतक|कतकः
कतक m. (-कः) The clearing nut plant, (Strychnos potatorum:) one of<BR>the seeds of this plant being rubbed upon the inside of the water<BR>jars used in Bengal, occasions a precipitation of the earthy par-<BR>ticles diffused through the water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=151-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कतम
कतम mfn. (-मः-मा-मत्) Which, (of many.)<BR> E. किम् and डतमच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=151-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कतमाल|कतमालः
कतमाल m. (-लः) A name of AGNI or fire; this word is perhaps a<BR>corruption: see कचमाल and खतमाल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=151-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कतर
कतर mfn. (-रः-रा-रत्) Which, (of two,) whether.<BR> E. किम् and डतरच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=151-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कति
कति mfn. (-ति-ति-ति)<BR>	 1. How many.<BR>	 2. How much.<BR> E. किम् what, and<BR>डति aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=151-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कतिचित्
कतिचित् ind.<BR>	 1. In any way, in some way.<BR>	 2. For some time.<BR> E. कति<BR>how many, and चित् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=151-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कतिथ
कतिथ mfn. (-थः-था-थं) What, how much.<BR> E. थुक् added to कति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=151-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कतिपय|कतिपयः
कतिपय mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>	 1. How many.<BR>	 2. A certain number, so many.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=151-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कतिपयथ
कतिपयथ mfn. (-थः-था-थं) What, how much.<BR> E. थक् added to कतिपय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=151-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कतिविध
कतिविध mfn. (-धः-धा-धं)<BR>	 1. Of how many sorts.<BR>	 2. Of various kinds. E.<BR>कति, and विध sort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=152-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कत्तृण|कत्तृणं
कत्तृण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. A fragrant grass.<BR>	 2. A plant, commonly Chakulia<BR>(Hemionites cordifolia, Rox.)<BR> E. कत् for कुत् bad, तृण grass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=152-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कत्तोय|कत्तोयं
कत्तोय n. (-यं) Wine or vinous spirit.<BR> E. कत् for कुत् bad, and तोय water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=152-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कत्थ
कत्थ r. 1st cl. (कत्थते)<BR>	 1. To praise or celebrate.<BR>	 2. To flatter or coax.<BR>3. To boast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=152-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कत्र
कत्र r. 10th cl. (कत्रयति) To loosen, to slacken, to remove.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=152-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कत्सवर|कत्सवरं
कत्सवर n. (-रं) The shoulder, the shoulder blade.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=152-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथ|कथं
कथ r. 10th cl. (कथयति) To speak, to tell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=152-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथक|कथकः
कथक mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>	 1. A narrator, a relator, one who recites a story,<BR>or who publicly reads and expounds the Puranas, &c.<BR>	 2. One who<BR>speaks or tells.<BR>	 mf. (-कः-का) The speaker of a prologue or a mono-<BR>logue.<BR>	 3. A professional story teller.<BR> E. कथ to speak, to relate,<BR>वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=152-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथङ्कथिक|कथंकथिक|कथङ्कथिकः
कथङ्कथिक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) An interrogant, one who asks or questions.<BR>E. कथम् how, कथ to speak, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=152-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथङ्कथिकता|कथंकथिकता
कथङ्कथिकता f. (-ता) A question, asking, enquiring.<BR> E. तल् affix of the<BR>abstract added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=152-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथङ्कथित
कथङ्कथित m. (-तः) An interrogant, one who questions.<BR> E. कथम् how,<BR>कथित said.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=152-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथञ्चन
कथञ्चन ind. In some way, in any way, by any means.<BR> E. कथम् and चन<BR>aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=152-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथञ्चित्
कथञ्चित् ind. In any way, by some means or other.<BR> E. कथम् and चित् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=152-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथन|कथनं
कथन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Talkative.<BR>	 n. (-नं) Saying, narrating, relating. E.<BR>कथ to say, &c. युच् or ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=152-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथनीय
कथनीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) To be said, to be told or declared.<BR> E. कथ to<BR>tell, अनीयर् affix; also with तव्य कथितव्य and with यत् कथ्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=152-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथन्ता|कथंता
कथन्ता f. (-न्ता) Enquiry, question, demand.<BR> E. कथ to speak, झश् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=152-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथम्
कथम् ind.<BR>	 1. A particle of interrogation, (how, what.)<BR>	 2. Also imply-<BR>ing mode, (how, in what manner.)<BR>	 3. A particle of amazement or<BR>surprise.<BR>	 4. Of pleasure.<BR>	 5. Of abuse.<BR>	 6. Of interrogation, implying<BR>doubt.<BR> E. किम् what, and थमु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=152-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथा
कथा f. (-था) A feigned story, a tale or fable.<BR> E. कथ to tell, &c. अङ् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=152-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथानुराग|कथानुरागः
कथानुराग m. (-गः) Attention, taking pleasure in a discourse.<BR> E. कथा, and<BR>अनुराग inclination.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=152-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथाप्रबन्ध|कथाप्रबंध|कथाप्रबन्धः
कथाप्रबन्ध m. (-न्धः) A narrative, a tale, a fiction.<BR> E. कथा, and प्रबन्ध<BR>connexion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=152-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथाप्रसङ्ग|कथाप्रसंग|कथाप्रसङ्गः
कथाप्रसङ्ग mfn. (-ङ्गः-ङ्गा-ङ्गं)<BR>	 1. Talkative, talking much and foolishly.<BR>2. Half-witted, foolish.<BR>	 3. A conjuror, a dealer in antidotes, &c.<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>	 1. Talking, conversation, speaking to or with.<BR>	 2.<BR>Rumour, report.<BR> E. कथा a fable, and प्रसङ्ग who relates.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=152-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथाप्राण|कथाप्राणः
कथाप्राण m. (-णः)<BR>	 1. An actor, the speaker of a prologue or monologue,<BR>the introducer of a drama.<BR>	 2. A professed story teller.<BR> E. कथा and<BR>प्राण life, livelihood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=152-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथायोग|कथायोगः
कथायोग m. (-गः) Conversation, talk, discourse.<BR> E. कथा, and योग uniting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=152-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथारम्भ|कथारंभ|कथारम्भः
कथारम्भ m. (-म्भः)<BR>	 1. Narration, narrative, story telling.<BR>	 2. Beginning of<BR>a story.<BR> E. कथा, and आरम्भ beginning, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=152-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथाविरक्त
कथाविरक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं) Reserved, taciturn, disliking conversation.<BR>E. कथा, and विरक्त disliking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=152-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथासंग्रह
कथासंग्रह m. (-हः) A collection of tales or fables.<BR> E. कथा, and संग्रह collection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=152-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथिक|कथिकः
कथिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) A story-teller by profession, a narrator, a relator.<BR>E. कथा a tale, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=152-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथित|कथितः
कथित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Said, told, related.<BR> E. कथ to tell, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=152-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथितपद
कथितपद n. (-दं) Repetition, tautology.<BR> E. कथित said, पद a word.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=152-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथोद्घात|कथोद्घातः
कथोद्घात m. (-तः) The opening of a drama, by the character that first<BR>enters overhearing and repeating the last words of the prelude. E.<BR>कथा, and उद्घात beginning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=152-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथोपकथन
कथोपकथन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Conversation, conference.<BR>	 2. Narration.<BR> E. कथा,<BR>and उपकथन speaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=152-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथोपाख्यान
कथोपाख्यान n. (-नं) Narration, narrative, relation, telling a story. E.<BR>कथा, and उपाख्यान telling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=152-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथ्य
कथ्य mfn. (-थ्यः-थ्या-थ्यं) To be spoken or said.<BR> E. कथ and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=152-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कद|कदः
कद or (इ) कदि r. 1st. cl. (कदते and कन्दते)<BR>	 1. To be confused, to suffer<BR>mentally, to grieve.<BR>	 2. To confound.<BR>	 3. To kill or hurt; also कदि<BR>(कंदति) 1. To call.<BR>	 2. To cry or shed tears.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=152-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कद|कदः
कद m. (-दः) A cloud.<BR> E. क water, and द what gives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=152-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कदक|कदकं|कदकः
कदक m. (-कः) An awning.<BR> E. कद a cloud, and क what makes; yielding<BR>a shade as a cloud; also fem. कदका and कदकी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=152-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कदक्षर|कदक्षरं
कदक्षर n. (-रं) A bad letter.<BR> E. कत् for कुत् bad and अक्षर a letter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=152-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कदध्वन्
कदध्वन् m. (-ध्वा) A bad road.<BR> E. कत् for कुत् bad, and अध्वन् a road.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=152-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कदन|कदनं
कदन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Killing, destroying.<BR>	 2. Sin.<BR>	 3. War.<BR> E. कद् to kill or<BR>injure, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=152-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कदन्न|कदन्नं
कदन्न n. (-न्नं) Bad food.<BR> E. कत् for कुत् bad, अन्न food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=152-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कदम्ब|कदंब|कदम्बं|कदंबः|कदम्बः
कदम्ब m. (-म्बः)<BR>	 1. A plant, commonly Kadamba (Nauclea kadamba.)<BR>2. The mustard seed plant, (Sinapis dichotoma.)<BR>	 3. A kind of grass,<BR>(Andropogon serratum:) see देवताडक.<BR>	 4. Turmeric.<BR>	 n. (-म्बं) A multi-<BR>tude, an assemblage or collection.<BR> E. कद् to confound, &c. अम्बच<BR>Uṇādi affix; also with कन् added कदम्बक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=152-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कदम्बक|कदंबक|कदम्बकं|कदंबकः|कदम्बकः
कदम्बक mn. (-कः-कं) See the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=152-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कदम्बद|कदंबदः|कदम्बदः
कदम्बद m. (-दः) Mustard seed plant: it seems to be a variety of read-<BR>ing for कदम्बक, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=152-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कदम्बपुष्पी
कदम्बपुष्पी f. (-ष्पी) A plant, the flowers of which resemble those of the<BR>Kadamba, commonly called Mundiri.<BR> E. कदम्ब, and पुष्प a flower,<BR>fem. affix ङीष्; also with टाप् कदम्बपुष्पा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=152-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कदम्बवायु|कदंबवायु|कदम्बवायुः
कदम्बवायु m. (-युः) A fragrant breeze.<BR> E. कदम्ब the plant, and वायु wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=152-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कदम्बानिल|कदंबानिल|कदम्बानिलः
कदम्बानिल m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. A fragrant breeze.<BR>	 2. Spring.<BR> E. कदम्ब and<BR>अनिल wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=152-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कदर|कदरं|कदरः
कदर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A white sort of mimosa.<BR>	 2. A corn, a callosity.<BR>	 3. A<BR>saw.<BR>	 4. An iron goad for an elephant.<BR>	 n. (-रं) Coagulated milk.<BR>E. क water, &c. दृ to tear, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=152-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कदर्थ|कदर्थः
कदर्थ mfn. (-र्थः-र्था-र्थं)<BR>	 1. Useless.<BR>	 2. Unmeaning.<BR> E. कत् for कुत्, and<BR>अर्थ object.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=152-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कदर्थित
कदर्थित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Despised, disdained, rejected.<BR>	 2. Rendered<BR>useless.<BR> E. कत् for कुत् bad, अर्थित sought.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=152-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कदर्थीकृत
कदर्थीकृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Despised, disdained.<BR>	 2. Rendered useless<BR>and unavailing.<BR> E. कदर्थ and कृत made, with च्वि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=152-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कदर्य्य|कदर्य|कदर्यः|कदर्य्यः
कदर्य्य mfn. (-र्य्यः-र्य्या-र्य्यं)<BR>	 1. Avaricious, miserly.<BR>	 2. Little, insignificant,<BR>mean.<BR>	 3. Bad, disagreeable.<BR>	 m. (-र्य्यः) A miser.<BR> E. कत् bad, vile,<BR>and अर्य्य possessor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=152-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कदर्य्यत्व|कदर्यत्व
कदर्य्यत्व n. (-त्वं)<BR>	 1. Avarice.<BR>	 2. Insignificance.<BR>	 3. Badness.<BR> E. त्व added<BR>to the last; also with तल् कदर्य्यता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=152-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कदल|कदलः
कदल mf. (-लः-ली)<BR>	 1. The plantain tree, (Musa sapientum.)<BR>	 2. Another<BR>plant, (Pistia stratiotes:) see पृष्णी.<BR>	 f. (-ला) The silk-cotton tree;<BR>also (-ली-लिका)<BR>	 1. A kind of deer, the hide of which is used as a<BR>seat, &c.<BR>	 2. A flag, a banner.<BR>	 3. A flag carried by an elephant. E.<BR>क water, air, &c. दल् to pierce, to divide, &c. affix अच्, and टाप्<BR>or ङीष् fem. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=152-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कदलक|कदलकः
कदलक m. (-कः) The plantain or banana tree: see the preceding. E.<BR>कन् added to कदल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=152-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कदलीक्षता
कदलीक्षता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. A sort of cucumber.<BR>	 2. A fine woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=152-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कदश्व|कदश्वः
कदश्व m. (-श्वः) A hack, a bad horse.<BR> E. कत् for कुत्, and अश्व a horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=152-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कदा
कदा ind. When, at what time.<BR> E. किम् what, दा aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=152-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कदाकार|कदाकारः
कदाकार mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Ill formed, ugly.<BR> E. कत् for कुत्, and आकार form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=152-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कदाख्य|कदाख्यं
कदाख्य n. (-ख्यं) A plant, commonly Kurh or Kudh, (Costus<BR>speciosus.)<BR> E. कत् bad, आख्या name, ill named: having a bad name<BR>or reputation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=152-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कदाचन
कदाचन ind. Sometime or other, ever; न कदाचन never.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=152-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कदाचार|कदाचारः
कदाचार mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Wicked, abandoned, following evil practices.<BR>E. कत् for कुत्, आचार observance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=152-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कदाचित्
कदाचित् ind. Sometimes, at sometime or other, ever; न कदाचित्<BR>never.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=153-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कदापि
कदापि ind. Sometimes, now and then.<BR> E. कदा when, अपि certainly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=153-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कदुष्ण|कदुष्णं
कदुष्ण mfn. (-ष्णः-ष्णा-ष्णं) Tepid, warm.<BR>	 n. (-ष्णं) Warmth, gentle warmth.<BR>E. कत् instead of कुत् bad, inferior, उष्ण heat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=153-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कद्रु|कद्रुः
कद्रु mfn. (-द्रुः-द्रुः-द्रूः-द्रु) Tawny.<BR>	 f. (-द्रूः) The wife of CASYAPA the<BR>saint, and mother of the Nāgas or the serpent race, inhabiting<BR>the regions below the earth.<BR>	 m. (-द्रुः) Tawny, (the colour.)<BR> E. कम्<BR>to desire, डु affix, and र inserted; the final of the radical is<BR>irregularly changed to द; fem. affix ऊञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=153-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कद्रुपुत्र|कद्रुपुत्रः
कद्रुपुत्र m. (-त्रः) A serpent.<BR> E. पुत्र a son, joined to the preceding; also<BR>other compounds of similar import, as कद्रुसुत, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=153-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कद्रुसुत|कद्रुसुतः
कद्रुसुत m. (-तः) A serpent: see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=153-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कद्वद|कद्वदः
कद्वद mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>	 1. Speaking ill, inaccurately, indistinctly, &c.<BR>2. Vile, base, contemptible.<BR> E. कत् for कुत् bad, and वद who<BR>speaks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=153-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन
कन(ई ञि)ञिकनी r. 1st cl. (कनति)<BR>	 1. To shine.<BR>	 2. To desire or love.<BR>3. To go or approach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=153-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कनक|कनकं|कनकः
कनक n. (-कं) Gold.<BR>	 m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. The name of a tree which bears red<BR>flowers, (Butea frondosa:) see पलाश.<BR>	 2. Thorn apple, (Datura<BR>metel, &c.)<BR>	 3. Another plant, (Mesua ferrea:) see नागकेशर.<BR>	 4.<BR>Mountain ebony, (Bauhinia variegata, &c.) see काञ्चनाल.<BR>	 5. A<BR>black sort of agallochum.<BR>	 6. A shrub yielding a yellow fragrant<BR>flower, (Michelia champaca.)<BR> E. कन to shine, अक Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=153-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कनकक्षार|कनकक्षारः
कनकक्षार m. (-रः) Borax.<BR> E. कनक, and क्षार flux.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=153-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कनकटङ्क|कनकटंक|कनकटङ्कः
कनकटङ्क m. (-ङ्कः) A golden hatchet.<BR> E. कनक, and टङ्क a hatch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=153-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कनकदण्डक|कनकदंडक
कनकदण्डक n. (-कं) The royal parasol.<BR> E. कनक gold, दण्ड a staff, and<BR>कन् affix; golden-sticked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=153-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कनकपराग|कनकपरागः
कनकपराग m. (-गः) Gold-dust.<BR> E. कनक, and पराग pollen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=153-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कनकपल|कनकपलः
कनकपल m. (-लः) A Pala, a weight of gold and silver equal to sixteen<BR>Mashas, or about 280 grains troy: see पल.<BR> E. कनक, and पल a<BR>Pala.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=153-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कनकभङ्ग|कनकभङ्गः
कनकभङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः) A piece of gold.<BR> E. कनक, भङ्ग what is broken off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=153-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कनकमय
कनकमय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Golden, consisting or made of gold.<BR> E. कनक and<BR>मयट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=153-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कनकरस|कनकरसः
कनकरस m. (-सः) Yellow orpiment.<BR> E. कनक, and रस juice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=153-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कनकलोद्भव|कनकलोद्भवः
कनकलोद्भव m. (-वः) Resin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=153-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कनकसूत्र
कनकसूत्र n. (-त्रं) A gold cord.<BR> E. कनक, and सूत्र string.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=153-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कनकस्थली
कनकस्थली f. (-ली) A gold-mine, golden soil.<BR> E. कनक, and स्थल place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=153-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कनकाचल|कनकाचलः
कनकाचल m. (-लः) The mountain Sumeru.<BR> E. कनक, and अचल a<BR>mountain; the golden mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=153-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कनकाध्यक्ष|कनकाध्यक्षः
कनकाध्यक्ष m. (-क्षः) The treasurer or superintendent of the gold. E.<BR>कनक, and अध्यक्ष a superintendent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=153-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कनकालुका
कनकालुका f. (-का) A golden jar or vase.<BR> E. कनक, आलु a water jar, कन्<BR>and टाप् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=153-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कनकाह्व|कनकाह्वं|कनकाह्वः
कनकाह्व m. (-ह्वः) A tree with golden or yellow blossoms, (Mesua ferrea.)<BR>E. कनक, and आह्वा appellation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=153-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कनन|कननः
कनन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) One-eyed.<BR> E. कन् to shine, युच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=153-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कनिष्ठ|कनिष्ठः
कनिष्ठ mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठा-ष्ठं)<BR>	 1. Small, little.<BR>	 2. Younger, younger born.<BR>	 3.<BR>Young.<BR>	 f. (-ष्ठा) The little finger.<BR> E. कन् to shine, &c. and इष्ठच्<BR>affix, or कण small, the ण being changed, or कन substituted for<BR>युवन् and अल्प.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=153-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कनिष्ठता
कनिष्ठता f. (-ता) The state of being younger or smaller<BR> E. तल् added to<BR>the last; also with त्व, कनिष्ठत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=153-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कनी
कनी f. (-नी) A girl, a maiden.<BR> E. कन् to shine, अच् and ङीष् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=153-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कनीक
कनीक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Very small: see कणिक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=153-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कनीचि|कनीचिः
कनीचि f. (-चिः)<BR>	 1. A creeping plant which bears flowers.<BR>	 2. The Gunja,<BR>a shrub bearing a red and black berry, (Abrus precatorios.)<BR>	 3. A<BR>cart.<BR> E. कनी to shine, ईचि Unādi affix; also according to some<BR>कणीचि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=153-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कनीनक|कनीनकः
कनीनक m. (-कः) The caruncula lacrymalis.<BR>	 f. (-निका)<BR>	 1. The pupil of<BR>the eye.<BR>	 2. The little finger.<BR> E. कन् to shine, ईकन् affix, कन् added;<BR>also with ङीष् only कनीनी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=153-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कनीनी
कनीनी f. (-नी)<BR>	 1. The little finger.<BR>	 2. The pupil of the eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=153-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कनीयस्
कनीयस् mfn. (-यान्-यसी-यः)<BR>	 1. Very young, youngest.<BR>	 2. Very small,<BR>least.<BR>	 3. Younger born, a younger brother or sister.<BR> E. कण small,<BR>ईयसुन् affix, the ण being changed; or कन् to shine, &c.: or कन<BR>substituted for युवन् and अल्प.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=153-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कनीयस|कनीयसं
कनीयस n. (-सं) Copper.<BR> E. कन् to shine, ईयसच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=153-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कनेरा
कनेर f. (-रा)<BR>	 1. A female elephant.<BR>	 2. A harlot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=153-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्त|कंत
कन्त mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं) Happy.<BR> E. कं and त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=153-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्ति
कन्ति mfn. (-न्तिः-न्तिः-न्ति) Happy.<BR> E. कम् and ति aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=153-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्तु|कंतु|कन्तुः
कन्तु mfn. (-न्तुः-न्तुः-न्तु) Happy.<BR>	 m. (-न्तुः)<BR>	 1. KĀMADEVA, the deity of<BR>love.<BR>	 2. The heart, as the seat or faculty of perception and<BR>feeling.<BR> E. कम् to desire, तु Unādi affix; or कं and तु possessive aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=153-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्था|कंथा
कन्था f. (-न्था)<BR>	 1. A rag, a patched cloth or garment, a quilt of grass.<BR>2. A wall: this word in composition may be used as neuter, if<BR>the compound imply a town in the province of Uśīnara as<BR>सोसिमकन्थं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=153-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्थाधारण|कंथाधारण
कन्थाधारण n. (-णं) Wearing a garment of patch-work, the practice of<BR>some Yogis.<BR> E. कन्था, and धारण wearing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=153-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्थाधारिन्|कंथाधारिन्
कन्थाधारिन् mf. (-री-रिणी) A Yogi, a religious mendicant.<BR> E. कन्था, and<BR>धारिन् who wears.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=153-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्द|कंद|कंदं|कन्दं|कंदः|कन्दः
कन्द mn. (-न्दः-न्दं)<BR>	 1. A bulbous or tuberous root.<BR>	 2. One of an esculent<BR>sort, (Arum campanulatum.)<BR>	 3. Garlic.<BR>	 m. (-न्दः)<BR>	 1. A cloud.<BR>	 2.<BR>An affection of the feminine organ, considered as a fleshy<BR>excrescence, but apparently prolapsus uteri.<BR> E. कदि to wet, &c.<BR>अच् affix, कं water, and दा to give.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=153-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्दट|कंदट|कन्दटं
कन्दट n. (-टं) The white esculent water lily.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=153-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्दमूल|कंदमूल|कन्दमूलं
कन्दमूल n. (-लं) A radish.<BR> E. कन्द, and मूल root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=153-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्दर|कंदर|कंदरं|कन्दरं|कंदरः|कन्दरः
कन्दर mfn. (-रः-रा or -री-रं)<BR>	 1. An artificial or natural cave.<BR>	 2. A glen, a<BR>defile, a valley.<BR>	 m. (-रः) A hook for driving an elephant with.<BR>	 n.<BR>(-रं) Dry ginger.<BR> E. कं water or the head, and दृ to divide, to<BR>pierce, अप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=153-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्दराकर|कंदराकर|कन्दराकरः
कन्दराकर m. (-रः) A mountain.<BR> E. कन्दर a cave, आकर having, making.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=153-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्दराल|कन्दरालः
कन्दराल m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. A plant, (Hibiscus populneoides.)<BR>	 2. A species of<BR>fig tree, (Ficus venosa:) see प्लक्ष.<BR>	 3. The walnut tree.<BR> E. कन्दरा a<BR>cave, and लच् affix; growing in desolate places: also with कन्<BR>added कन्दरालक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=153-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्दरालक|कन्दरालकः
कन्दरालक m. (-कः) A species of fig tree: see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=153-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्दर्प|कंदर्प|कंदर्पः|कन्दर्पः
कन्दर्प m. (-र्पः) A name of the deity KĀMA^1, the CUPID of the Hiudu<BR>mythology.<BR> E. कं BRAHMĀ, दर्प to inflame, अच् affix; the inflamer<BR>even of the first of the gods; corresponding in this respect with<BR>his Grecian prototype.<BR>	 f. (-र्पा) One of the presiding female deities<BR>of the Jainas.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20260617. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/264.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=153-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्दर्पकूप|कंदर्पकूप|कन्दर्पकूपः
कन्दर्पकूप m. (-पः) Pudendum muliebre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=153-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्दर्पज्वर|कंदर्पज्वर|कन्दर्पज्वरः
कन्दर्पज्वर m. (-रः) Passion, desire.<BR> E. कन्दर्प, and ज्वर fever.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=153-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्दर्पमुषल|कंदर्पमुषल|कन्दर्पमुषलः
कन्दर्पमुषल m. (-लः) Membrum virile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=153-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्दल|कंदल|कंदलं|कन्दलं|कंदलः|कन्दलः
कन्दल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>	 1. The cheek, or the cheek and temple.<BR>	 2. A<BR>portent, a natural phœnomenon supposed to announce evil.<BR>	 3. A<BR>new shoot or sprig.<BR>	 4. A low minute tone.<BR>	 5. Reproach, censure.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-लः)<BR>	 1. Gold.<BR>	 2. War, battle.<BR>	 f. (-ली)<BR>	 1. A species of deer of which<BR>the hide is used.<BR>	 2. A sort of tree, the banana: see कदली.<BR>	 3. A<BR>flag.<BR> E. कन्द a root, &c. and ल from ला to take, fem. affix ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=153-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्दलित|कंदलित
कन्दलित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Budden, blown.<BR>	 2. Put forth, emitted. E.<BR>कन्दल a bud, इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=153-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्दलीकुसुम|कंदलीकुसुम|कन्दलीकुसुमं
कन्दलीकुसुम n. (-मं) A mushroom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=153-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्दवर्द्धन
कन्दवर्द्धन m. (-नः) An esculent root.<BR> E. कन्द, and वर्द्धन increasing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=153-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्दशूरण|कन्दशूरणः
कन्दशूरण m. (-णः) A sort of Arum, (A. campanula tum.)<BR> E. कन्द, and<BR>शूरण the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=153-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्दसंज्ञ
कन्दसंज्ञ n. (-ज्ञं) Prolapsus uteri, see कन्द.<BR> E. कन्द a root, and संज्ञा a<BR>name, affix ड; every संज्ञा or name for a bulbous root, being a<BR>term for this complaint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=154-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्दसार|कंदसार|कन्दसारं
कन्दसार n. (-रं) The garden or grove of INDRA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=154-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्दालु|कन्दालुः
कन्दालु m. (-लुः) An esculent root, a sort of Arum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=154-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्दिन्|कंदिन्
कन्दिन् mfn. (-न्दी-न्दिनी-न्दि) Having a bulbous root.<BR>	 m. (-न्दी) A sort of<BR>Arum, (A. campanulatum, or any similar bulb.)<BR> E. कन्द and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=154-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्दु|कंदुः|कन्दुः
कन्दु mfn. (-न्दुः-न्दुः-न्दु)<BR>	 1. A boiler, a saucepan or other cooking utensil<BR>of iron.<BR>	 2. An oven or vessel serving for one.<BR> E. स्कन्द to go, उ<BR>Uṇādi affix, and the initial स rejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=154-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्दुक|कंदुक|कंदुकं|कंदुकः|कन्दुकः
कन्दुक m. (-कः) A ball of wood or pith for playing with.<BR>	 n. (-कं) A<BR>germ.<BR> E. कदि to cry, to call, &c. उ affix, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=154-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्दुपक्व|कन्दुपक्वं
कन्दुपक्व mfn. (-क्वः-क्वा-क्वं) Parched, roasted, (as grain,) fried, &c. dressed<BR>without water.<BR> E. कन्दु, and पक्व dressed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=154-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्दोट|कंदोट|कन्दोटं|कंदोटः|कन्दोटः
कन्दोट m. (-टः) The white esculent water lily.<BR>	 n. (-टं) The blue lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=154-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्दोत|कंदोतः|कन्दोतः
कन्दोत m. (-तः) The white lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=154-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्ध|कंध|कंधः|कन्धः
कन्ध m. (-न्धः) A cloud.<BR> E. कं water, and ध from धा to have.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=154-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्धर|कंधर|कंधरः|कन्धरः
कन्धर mf. (-रः-रा) The neck.<BR>	 m. (-रः) A cloud.<BR> E. कं water or the head<BR>and धर having, from धृञ्, affix खच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=154-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्धि|कंधि|कंधिः|कन्धिः
कन्धि m. (-न्धिः) The ocean.<BR>	 f. (-न्धिः) The neck.<BR> E. कं water or the head,<BR>धा to have, कि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=154-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्न|कन्नं
कन्न n. (-न्नं) Fainting, falling in a fit or state of insensibility; in some<BR>copies this word is read कल्ल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=154-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्यका
कन्यका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. A girl, a maiden.<BR>	 2. A daughter.<BR>	 3. The Socotrine<BR>aloe, (Aloes perfoliata.)<BR> E. कन्या a girl, कन् pleonastic affix, fem.<BR>affix टाप्ः see कन्या and कन्याका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=154-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्यकाच्छल|कन्यकाच्छलः|कन्यकाछल
कन्यकाच्छल n. (-लं) Beguiling a maiden, seduction, betrayal.<BR> E. कन्यका,<BR>and छल deceit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=154-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्यकाजात|कन्यकाजातः
कन्यकाजात m. (-तः) The son of an unmarried woman.<BR> E. कन्यका, and जात born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=154-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्यकापति|कन्यकापतिः
कन्यकापति m. (-तिः) A daughter's husband.<BR> E. कन्यका, and पति a husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=154-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्यस|कन्यसः
कन्यस m. (-सः)<BR>	 1. A younger brother.<BR>	 f. (-सा) The little finger: see<BR>कनिष्ठ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=154-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्या
कन्या f. (-न्या)<BR>	 1. A girl nine years old, a virgin.<BR>	 2. A name of DURGĀ.<BR>	 3.<BR>The sign of the zodiac, Virgo.<BR>	 4. The socotrine aloe (Aloes per-<BR>foliata.)<BR>	 6. Large cardamoms.<BR>	 7. A species of metre of four lines,<BR>with four syllables in each.<BR>	 3. A parasite plant.<BR> E. कन् to shine,<BR>Uṇādi affix यक्, fem. टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=154-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्याका
कन्याका f. (-का) A young girl or virgin: see कन्या and कन्यका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=154-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्याकुब्ज|कन्याकुब्जः
कन्याकुब्ज m. (-ब्जः) Kanyakubja or Kinnoge, an ancient city of great<BR>note, in the north of Hindustan, known to classical geography<BR>as Cannogyza: the name also applies to its dependencies or the<BR>surrounding district; also कान्यकुब्ज.<BR> E. कन्या a girl, and कुब्ज round-<BR>shouldered, crooked; the etymology, alludes to a legend relating<BR>to the one hundred daughters of KUŚANĀBHA the king of this<BR>city, who were all rendered crooked by Vayu, for non-compliance<BR>with his licentious desires.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=154-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्याग्रहण
कन्याग्रहण n. (-णं) Taking a girl in marriage.<BR> E. कन्धा and ग्रहण taking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=154-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्याट|कन्याटः
कन्याट m. (-टः) The middle of a house, the inner or private apart-<BR>ments.<BR> E. कन्या a girl, अट् to go, and अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=154-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्यादान|कन्यादानं
कन्यादान n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Giving a girl in marriage.<BR>	 2. Receiving the same.<BR>E. कन्या, and दान gift, or आदान acceptance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=154-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्यादातृ
कन्यादातृ m. (-ता) A father, one who gives a girl in marriage.<BR> E. कन्या,<BR>and दातृ donor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=154-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्यादूषक|कन्यादूषकः
कन्यादूषक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A violator or defiler of a virgin.<BR>	 2. A calumniator<BR>of a girl.<BR> E. कन्या, and दूषक who defiles; also कन्यादूषिन् m. (-षी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=154-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्यादूषण
कन्यादूषण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Defiling a virgin.<BR>	 2. Calumniating a girl.<BR> E. कन्या,<BR>and दूषण spoiling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=154-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्यादोष|कन्यादोषः
कन्यादोष m. (-षः) A blemish in a virgin, disease, bad repute, &c. E.<BR>कन्या, and दोष fault.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=154-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्यापति|कन्यापतिः
कन्यापति m. (-तिः) A daughter's husband: see कन्यकापति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=154-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्यापाल|कन्यापालः
कन्यापाल m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. A dealer in slave girls.<BR>	 2. The father of a<BR>daughter.<BR> E. कन्या, and पाल who cherishes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=154-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्यापुत्र|कन्यापुत्रः
कन्यापुत्र m. (-त्रः) The offspring of an unmarried daughter.<BR> E. कन्या,<BR>and पुत्र a son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=154-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्याप्रदान
कन्याप्रदान n. (-नं) Giving a daughter in marriage.<BR> E. कन्या, and प्रदान<BR>a gift.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=154-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्याराम|कन्यारामः
कन्याराम m. (-मः) A Bauddha or Jaina saint.<BR> E. कन्या a girl, रम् to<BR>please, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=154-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्यावेदिन्
कन्यावेदिन् m. (-दी) A son-in-law.<BR> E. कन्या, and वेदिन् who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=154-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्याशुल्क
कन्याशुल्क n. (-ल्कं) The purchase money of a maiden, money given to<BR>the bride's father.<BR> E. कन्या and शुल्क tax.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=154-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्यासमुद्भव
कन्यासमुद्भव m. (-वः) The son of an unmarried girl.<BR> E. कन्या, and समुद्भव<BR>born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=154-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्याहरण
कन्याहरण n. (-णं) Carrying off girl, rape, ravishment.<BR> E. कन्या, and हरण<BR>taking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=154-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्यिका
कन्यिका f. (-का) A young girl, a virgin: see कन्यका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=154-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्युष|कन्युषं
कन्युष n. (-षं) The hand below the wrist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=154-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कप
कप(इ)कपि r. 1st cl. (कंपते) To shake, to tremble: with अनु prefixed, to<BR>feel tenderness or compassion, to pity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=154-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपट|कपटं|कपटः
कपट mn. (-टः-टं) Fraud, deceit, cheating, circumvention.<BR> E. क BRAHMĀ,<BR>पट् to go, अच् affix; what extends even to BRAHMĀ,; or क the head,<BR>and पट a covering, screening the head as it were.<BR>	 f. (-टी) A<BR>measure equal to the capacity of the hollows of the two hands<BR>joined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=154-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपटता
कपटता f. (-ता) Deceitfulness.<BR> E. तल् added to कपटः also with त्व कपटत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=154-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपटप्रबन्ध|कपटप्रबंध|कपटप्रबन्धः
कपटप्रबन्ध m. (-न्धः) Fraud, trick, fraudulent plot or contrivance.<BR> E. कपट,<BR>and प्रबन्ध procedure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=154-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपटलेख्य
कपटलेख्य n. (-ख्यं) A forged document, a false or fraudulent statement.<BR>E. कपट, and लेख्य a writing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=154-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपटवेश|कपटवेशः
कपटवेश mfn. (-शः-शा-शं) Masked, disguised, assuming a false dress or<BR>appearance.<BR>	 m. (-शः) Disguise.<BR> E. कपट, and वेश costume.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=154-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपटवेशिन्
कपटवेशिन् mfn. (-शी-शिनी-शि) Disguised, in masquerade.<BR> E. कपटवेश and<BR>इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=154-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपटिक|कपटिकः
कपटिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) A rogue, a cheat, fraudulent, dishonest. E.<BR>कपट and ठक aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=154-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपटिन्
कपटिन् mfn. (-टी-टिनी-टि) Fraudulent, dishonest, a cheat, &c.<BR> E. कपट<BR>and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=154-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपर्द्द|कपर्द|कपर्दः|कपर्द्दः
कपर्द्द m. (-र्द्दः)<BR>	 1. The braided hair of ŚIVA.<BR>	 2. A small shell used as<BR>a coin, a Cowri.<BR>	 3. A name of ŚIVA.<BR> E. क water, (that of the<BR>Ganges,) पृ in the deriv. form, nourishing, and द from दा to give;<BR>or क happiness, &c. which will apply to both senses; also with<BR>कन् added कपर्द्दक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=154-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपर्द्दक|कपर्दक|कपर्दकः|कपर्द्दकः
कपर्द्दक m. (-कः) See the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=154-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपर्द्दिन्|कपर्दिन्
कपर्द्दिन् m. (-र्द्दी) A name of ŚIVA.<BR> E. कपर्द्द his braided hair, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=154-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपाट|कपाटं|कपाटः
कपाट mfn. (-टः-टी-टं) A door, the leaf or pannel of a door.<BR> E. क the<BR>the head or wind, पट् to go, अण् affix; also कवाट.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=154-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपाटघ्न
कपाटघ्न m. (-घ्नः) A thief, a housebreaker.<BR> E. कपाट, and घ्न who breaks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=154-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपाटसन्धि|कपाटसंधि|कपाटसंधिः
कपाटसन्धि m. (-न्धिः)<BR>	 1. The junction of the leaves of a door.<BR>	 2. A mode<BR>of multiplying, (in arithmetic.)<BR> E. कपाट, and सन्धि junction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=154-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपाल|कपालं|कपालः
कपाल mn. (-लः-लं)<BR>	 1. The skull, the cranium.<BR>	 2. Either half of a<BR>water jar.<BR>	 3. Any flat bone.<BR>	 4. A beggar's bowl.<BR>	 5. Multitude as-<BR>semblage, collection.<BR>	 6. A species of leprosy.<BR>	 7. A treaty of peace<BR>on equal terms.<BR> E. कपि to tremble, and कालन् Uṇādi affix; or क<BR>the head, and पाल what cherishes or protects.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=154-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपालनालिका
कपालनालिका f. (-का) A sort of pin or spindle for winding cotton,<BR>thread, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=154-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपालभृत्
कपालभृत् m. (-भृत्) A name of MAHADEVA.<BR> E. कपाल a skull, and भृत्<BR>who cherishes; being represented with a necklace of skulls.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=154-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपालसन्धि|कपालसंधि|कपालसंधिः
कपालसन्धि f. (-न्धिः) Treaty of peace on equal terms.<BR> E. कपाल, and सन्धि<BR>peace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=154-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपालिका
कपालिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. The tartar of the teeth.<BR>	 2. A potsherd.<BR> E. कपाल<BR>and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=155-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपालिन्
कपालिन् m. (-ली)<BR>	 1. A title of ŚIVA.<BR>	 2. A man of low caste, from a<BR>Brahman mother and fisherman father.<BR>	 f. (-लिनी) The goddess<BR>DURGĀ.<BR> E. कपाल a skull, इनि affix; and ङीष् fem. do.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=155-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपि|कपिः
कपि m. (-पिः)<BR>	 1. An ape or monkey.<BR>	 2. The monkey HANUMAN.<BR>	 3. A<BR>title of VIṢṆU or KṚṢṆA.<BR>	 4. Incense, storax or impure ben-<BR>zoin.<BR>	 5. Emblic myrobalan, (Phyllanthus emblica.)<BR>	 6. A kind of<BR>Bonduc or Bonducella.<BR> E. कपि to tremble, इ Uṇādi affix, the<BR>nasal rejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=155-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपिकच्छु|कपिकच्छुः
कपिकच्छु f. (-च्छुः) Cowach, (Dolichos carpopogon.)<BR> E. कपि a monkey,<BR>and कच्छु itching; also with final vowel long कपिकच्छू.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=155-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपिकच्छुरा
कपिकच्छुरा f. (-रा) Cowach: see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=155-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपिकन्दुक|कपिकन्दुकं
कपिकन्दुक n. (-कं) The skull, the cranium.<BR> E. कपि, and कन्दुक a ball.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=155-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपिचूत|कपिचूतः
कपिचूत m. (-तः) A tree, (Spondias mangifera:) see आम्रातक.<BR> E. कपि, and<BR>चूत the mango tree, the monkey's mango.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=155-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपिज|कपिजः
कपिज mfn. (-जः-जा-जं) Born of a monkey, &c.<BR>	 m. (-जः) Incense, ben-<BR>zoin.<BR> E. कपि, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=155-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपिञ्जल|कपिंजल|कपिंजलः|कपिञ्जलः
कपिञ्जल m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. A bird, the francoline partridge.<BR>	 2. The Chataka.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=155-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपितैल|कपितैलं
कपितैल n. (-लं) Benzoin or storax.<BR> E. कपि, and तैल oil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=155-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपित्थ|कपित्थः
कपित्थ m. (-त्थः) The elephant or wood apple, (Feronia elephantum.) E.<BR>कपि, and त्थ from स्था to stay or abide; the residence of apes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=155-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपित्थपर्णी
कपित्थपर्णी f. (-र्णी) A plant, commonly कपित्थानी, the leaves of which are<BR>compared to those of the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=155-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपित्थानी
कपित्थानी f. (-नी) A plant: see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=155-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपित्थास्य|कपित्थास्यः
कपित्थास्य m. (-स्यः) A kind of monkey.<BR> E. कपित्थ, and आस्य a face; having<BR>a roundish face, in shape like the wood apple.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=155-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपिध्वज|कपिध्वजः
कपिध्वज m. (-जः) A name of ARJUNA.<BR> E. कपि a monkey, and ध्वज a<BR>sign; having a monkey as his symbol, his ensign or arms.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=155-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपिनामन्
कपिनामन् m. (-मा) Incense: see कपि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=155-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपिप्रभा
कपिप्रभा f. (-भा) Cowach: see कपिकच्छु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=155-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपिप्रभु|कपिप्रभुः
कपिप्रभु m. (-भुः) A name of the first RAMA.<BR> E. कपि and प्रभु master;<BR>general of the monkey force with which he invaded Lanka or<BR>Ceylon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=155-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपिप्रिय|कपिप्रियः
कपिप्रिय m. (-यः) The elephant or wood apple: see कपित्थ.<BR> E. कपि, and<BR>प्रिय beloved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=155-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपिरथ|कपिरथः
कपिरथ m. (-थः) A title of RAMA.<BR> E. कपि and रथ a car; having been<BR>carried by his monkies.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=155-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपिल|कपिलः
कपिल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Tawny.<BR>	 m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. KAPILA, a celebrated Muni or<BR>saint, the founder of the Sankhya system of philosophy: the son<BR>of KERDDAMA by DEVAHUTI, and according to some, an avatar of<BR>VIṢṆU.<BR>	 2. A title of AGNI the deity of fire.<BR>	 3. A dog.<BR>	 4. Tawny,<BR>(in colour.)<BR>	 f. (-ला)<BR>	 1. The female elephant of the south-east.<BR>	 2. A<BR>kind of Sisu, or timber tree so called: see शिंशपा.<BR>	 3. A sort of per-<BR>fume: see रेणुका 4. The aloe plant.<BR>	 5. A fabulous cow, celebrated<BR>in the Puranas.<BR>	 6. The common leech.<BR> E. कम् to desire, इलच् Uṇādi<BR>affix, and प substituted for म; or कपि a monkey, and ल to take,<BR>&c. being of such a colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=155-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपिलद्युति|कपिलद्युतिः
कपिलद्युति m. (-तिः) A name of SŪRYA or the sun.<BR> E. कपिल, and द्युति<BR>light; being of a dull red or tawny hue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=155-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपिलद्राक्षा
कपिलद्राक्षा f. (-क्षा) The brown or tawny grape.<BR> E. कपिल, and द्राक्षा a grape.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=155-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपिलद्रुम|कपिलद्रुमः
कपिलद्रुम m. (-मः) The name of a perfume or sweet scented wood:<BR>see काक्षी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=155-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपिलधारा
कपिलधारा f. (-रा)<BR>	 1. The Ganges.<BR>	 2. A holy place, a place of pil-<BR>grimage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=155-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपिलाश्व|कपिलाश्वः
कपिलाश्व m. (-श्वः) A title of the god INDRA.<BR> E. कपिल tawny, and अश्व<BR>horse; such being the colour of INDRA'S steed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=155-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपिलोह|कपिलोहं
कपिलोह n. (-हं) Brass.<BR> E. कपि for कपिल brown, and लोह iron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=155-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपिल्लिका
कपिल्लिका f. (-का) A plant, which bears a seed resembling pepper,<BR>(Pothos officinalis.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=155-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपिवक्त्र|कपिवक्त्रः
कपिवक्त्र m. (-क्त्रः) A name of NĀRADA^1, a saint and philosopher, and<BR>friend of KṚṢṆA.<BR> E. कपि and वक्त्र a face; the saint having a face<BR>like a monkey.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20260517. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/225.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=155-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपिवल्ली
कपिवल्ली f. (-ल्ली) The elephant or wood apple: see कपित्थ.<BR> E. कपि, and वल्ली<BR>a pedicle; that being invested with a downy coat, resembling the<BR>hair of an ape.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=155-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपिश|कपिशः
कपिश mfn. (-शः-शा-शं) Brown, of a brown colour.<BR>	 m. (-शः)<BR>	 1. Brown,<BR>(the colour,) a compound of black and yellow.<BR>	 2. Incense,<BR>storax or coarse benzoin.<BR>	 f. (-शी) A spirit, a sort of rum.<BR>	 f.<BR>(-शा) The mother of the demons called Pisachas.<BR> E. कपि an ape,<BR>and श affix; of the colour of an ape.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=155-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपिशाञ्जन|कपिशाञ्जनः
कपिशाञ्जन m. (-नः) A title of ŚIVA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=155-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपिशायन|कपिशायनः
कपिशायन m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. A deity.<BR>	 2. A sort of spirit or rum.<BR> E. कपिशा, affix फक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=155-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपिशापुत्र
कपिशापुत्र m. (-त्रः) A Pisacha, an imp or goblin.<BR> E. कपिशा the mother of<BR>these beings, and पुत्र a son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=155-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपिशित
कपिशित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Embrowned, made brown or dusky red.<BR> E. कपिश<BR>and इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=155-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपिशीका
कपिशीका f. (-का) Spirituous liquor.<BR> E. कपिश, and ईकन् affix: see कपिश.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=155-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपिशीर्ष|कपिशीर्षं
कपिशीर्ष m. (-र्षः) The upper part or coping of a wall.<BR> E. कपि, and शीर्ष<BR>the head; a monkey's head.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=155-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपिशीर्षक|कपिशीर्षकं
कपिशीर्षक n. (-कं) Vermilion, the red sulphuret of mercury.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=155-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपिस्थल
कपिस्थल n. (-लं) A place frequented by monkies.<BR> E. कपि, and स्थल place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=155-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपीकच्छु|कपीकच्छुः
कपीकच्छु f. (-च्छुः) Cowach: see कपिकच्छ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=155-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपीज्य|कपीज्यः
कपीज्य m. (-ज्यः) A plant, (a species of mimusops:) see क्षीरिका.<BR> E. कपि,<BR>and इज्य respected, liked; a favourite plant with the monkies;<BR>also कपीज्यक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=155-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपीतन|कपीतनः
कपीतन m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. A tree bearing an acid fruit, (Spondias mangifera:)<BR>see आम्रातक.<BR>	 2. Another tree, (Hibiscus populneoides:) see गर्द्दभाण्ड.<BR>3. A species of Mimosa, (Mimosa sirisha, Rox.)<BR>	 4. The holy fig<BR>tree, (Ficus religiosa.)<BR>	 5. The betel nut tree, (Areca faufel or<BR>Catechu.)<BR>	 6. The name of another plant, (Cratæva marmelos.) E.<BR>कपि an ape, and तन what spreads; sheltering or feeding monkies;<BR>the vowel is made long irregularly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=155-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपीन्द्र|कपींद्र|कपीन्द्रः
कपीन्द्र m. (-न्द्रः)<BR>	 1. A name of the celebrated monkey HANUMAN.<BR>	 2. Also<BR>of SUGRĪVA, &c.<BR> E. कपि, and इन्द्र the chief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=155-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपुष्टिका
कपुष्टिका f. (-का) A patch of hair on each side of the head.<BR> E. क the<BR>head, पुष्टि cherishing, कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=155-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपुच्छल|कपुच्छलं
कपुच्छल n. (-लं) Hair hanging down to the ground.<BR> E. क the head,<BR>पुच्छ a tail, and ल what resembles.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=155-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपोत|कपोतः
कपोत m. (-तः)<BR>	 1. A dove or pigeon, especially the spotted necked<BR>pigeon.<BR>	 2. A bird in general.<BR> E. कब to tinge, to be of various hues,<BR>आतच् Uṇādi affix, ब changed to प.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=155-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपोतक|कपोतकं|कपोतकः
कपोतक n. (-कं) Antimony.<BR> E. कपोत and कन् affix, implying resemblance,<BR>(in colour.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=155-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपोतचरणा
कपोतचरणा f. (-णा) A perfume: see नली.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=155-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपोतपालिका
कपोतपालिका f. (-का) A dove cot, an aviary or pigeon house.<BR> E. कपोत a<BR>bird, &c. पाल to nourish, and वुन् affix, fem. termination टाप्; also<BR>with the affixes अण् and ङीप् कपोतपाली.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=155-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपोतपाली
कपोतपाली f. (-ली) See the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=155-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपोतसार|कपोतसारं
कपोतसार n. (-रं) Antimony.<BR> E. कपोत and सार essence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=155-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपोताङ्घ्रि|कपोतांघ्रि|कपोताङ्घ्रिः
कपोताङ्घ्रि f. (-ङ्घ्रिः) A perfume: see नली.<BR> E. कपोत and अङ्घ्रि a foot; of a<BR>red colour, like the claw of a pigeon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=155-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपोताभ|कपोताभः
कपोताभ m. (-भः) A pale or dirty white colour.<BR> E. कपोत, an आङ् before<BR>भा to shine, affix ड; of the colour of a pigeon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=155-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपोतारि|कपोतारिः
कपोतारि m. (-रिः) A hawk, a falcon.<BR> E. कपोत, and अरि an enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=155-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपोतिका
कपोतिका f. (-का) A dove.<BR> E. कपोत a pigeon, कन् affix. fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=155-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपोल|कपोलः
कपोल m. (-लः) A cheek.<BR>	 f. (-ली) The forepart of the knee, the knee-cap<BR>or pan.<BR> E. कपि to quiver, and ओलच् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=155-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपोलकाष|कपोलकाषः
कपोलकाष m. (-षः) The elephant's temples and cheeks.<BR> E. कपोल and काष<BR>touchstone; being of the like dark colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=155-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपोलभित्ति|कपोलभित्तिः
कपोलभित्ति m. (-त्तिः) The temples and cheek, the upper part of the<BR>face.<BR> E. कपोल, and भित्ति a wall.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=156-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपोलराग|कपोलरागः
कपोलराग m. (-गः) Colour or flush in the cheek.<BR> E. कपोल, and राग colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=156-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपोलफलक|कपोलफलकः
कपोलफलक m. (-कः) The cheek.<BR> E. कपोल, and फलक a plank.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=156-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कप्याख्य|कप्याख्यः
कप्याख्य m. (-ख्यः) Incense.<BR> E. कपि and आख्या aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=156-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कफ|कफः
कफ m. (-फः)<BR>	 1. Phlegm, one of the three humours of the body.<BR>	 2.<BR>Watery froth or foam in general.<BR> E. क water, and फल to bud or<BR>flower, ड aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=156-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कफकर
कफकर mfn. (-रः-रा-री-रं) Producing phlegm.<BR> E. कफ and कर what<BR>makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=156-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कफकूर्च्चिका|कफकूर्चिका
कफकूर्च्चिका f. (-का) Saliva, spittle.<BR> E. कफ, and कूर्च्चिका cream.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=156-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कफघ्न
कफघ्न mfn. (-घ्नः-घ्नी-घ्नं) Removing phlegm, antiphlegmatic, (an epithet of<BR>many plants, &c.)<BR> E. कफ, and घ्न what destroys.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=156-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कफणि|कफणिः
कफणि mf. (-णिः-णी) The elbow.<BR> E. क pleasure, फण् to go, इन् and ङीष्<BR>affixes; also कफोणि<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=156-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कफनाशन
कफनाशन mfn. (-नः-नी-नं) Antiphlegmatic.<BR> E. कफ, and नाशन destroying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=156-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कफवर्द्धक
कफवर्द्धक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Exciting phlegm.<BR> E. कफ, and वर्द्ध्वक what<BR>increases.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=156-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कफवर्द्धन
कफवर्द्धन mfn. (-नः-नी-नं) Exciting phlegm.<BR>	 m. (-नः) The name of a<BR>plant; also पिण्डितगर.<BR> E. कफ phlegm, वृध् to augment, and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=156-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कफारि|कफारिः
कफारि m. (-रिः) Ginger.<BR> E. कफ and अरि foe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=156-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कफिन्
कफिन् mfn. (-फी-फिनी-फि) Phlegmatic.<BR>	 m. (-फी) An elephant.<BR> E. कफ and<BR>इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=156-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कफेलू
कफेलू mfn. (-लूः-लूः-लु) Phlegmatic, causing or exciting phlegm.<BR> E. कफ,<BR>लू from ला to take or give, and कू Uṇādi affix; the deriv. is irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=156-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कफोणि|कफोणिः
कफोणि mf. (-णिः-णी) The elbow.<BR> E. क pleasure, स्फुर् to go, &c. इन् and<BR>ङीष् affixes; the form is irregular: see कफणि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=156-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कब
कब(ऋ)कबृ r. 1st cl. (कबते)<BR>	 1. To colour, to tinge with various hues.<BR>2. To praise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=156-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कबन्ध|कबंध|कबंधं|कबन्धं|कबंधः|कबन्धः
कबन्ध mn. (-न्धः-न्धं) A headless trunk, especially retaining vitality.<BR>	 n.<BR>(-न्धं) Water.<BR>	 m. (-न्धः)<BR>	 1. A name of RAHU.<BR>	 2. Also of a demon de-<BR>stroyed by RAMA.<BR>	 3. The belly.<BR> E. कं the head, and बध् to injure,<BR>to lop, affix अच्; also कं water, and बन्ध binding, attaching.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=156-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कबन्धता
कबन्धता f. (-ता) Headlessness, decapitation.<BR> E. कबन्ध and तल् affix; also<BR>with त्व कबन्धत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=156-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कबित्थ|कबित्थः
कबित्थ m. (-त्थः) The elephant or wood apple: see कपित्थ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=156-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कबिल|कबिलः
कबिल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Tawny, (of such a hue.)<BR>	 m. (-लः) Tawny (the<BR>colour:) see कपिल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=156-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कम
कम(उ)कमु r. 1st cl. (कामयति) To desire: this root is irregular.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=156-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कम्
कम् ind.<BR>	 1. Water.<BR>	 2. The head.<BR>	 3. Happiness or happily.<BR>	 4. An exple-<BR>tive.<BR> E. कम् to desire, विच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=156-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कमठ|कमठं|कमठः
कमठ mn. (-ठः-ठं)<BR>	 1. A water jar, especially one made of a hollow<BR>gourd or cocoanut, and used by ascetics.<BR>	 m. (-ठः)<BR>	 1. A turtle,<BR>a tortoise.<BR>	 2. A bamboo.<BR>	 3. The name of a Daitya or de-<BR>mon.<BR>	 4. A porcupine.<BR>	 f. (-ठी) A female tortoise, a small one. E.<BR>कम् to desire, &c. अठ Uṇādi affix, fem. affix. ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=156-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कमण्डलु|कमंडलु|कमंडलुः|कमण्डलुः
कमण्डलु mn. (-लुः-लु) An earthen or wooden water pot, used by the<BR>ascetic and religious student.<BR>	 2. The waved-leaf fig tree: see प्लक्ष.<BR>E. क BRAHMĀ or water, and मण्ड ornament or essence, ल from ला<BR>to get or give, and डु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=156-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कमन|कमनं|कमनः
कमन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>	 1. Libidinous, desirous.<BR>	 2. Beautiful, desirable.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. A name of BRAHMĀ.<BR>	 2. KĀMA^1 or love.<BR>	 3. A tree, (Jone-<BR>sia asoca.)<BR> E. कम् to desire, affix युच् or ल्युट्.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20260617. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/264.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=156-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कमनच्छद|कमनच्छदः|कमनछद
कमनच्छद m. (-दः) A heron.<BR> E. कमन beautiful, and छद plumage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=156-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कमनीय|कमनीयं
कमनीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Pleasing, beautiful, desirable.<BR> E. कम् and अनीयर्<BR>affix of the future participle, to be desired.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=156-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कमनीयता
कमनीयता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Loveliness, beauty.<BR>	 2. Desirableness.<BR> E. तल् added<BR>to the last, or with त्व कमनीयत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=156-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कमन्ध|कमन्धं
कमन्ध m. (-न्धः) Water. See कबन्ध; also according to some, this is an<BR>orthographical compound, of कं and अन्ध, both synonyms of water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=156-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कमर|कमरः
कमर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Desirous, lustful.<BR> E. कम् and अरन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=156-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कमल|कमलं|कमलः
कमल n. (-लं)<BR>	 1. A lotus, (Nelumbium speciosum or Nymphæa nelum-<BR>bo.)<BR>	 2. Water.<BR>	 3. Copper.<BR>	 4. A medicament, a drug.<BR>	 5. The blad-<BR>der.<BR>	 m. (-लः) A species of deer.<BR>	 f. (-ला)<BR>	 1. A name of LAKṢMĪ.<BR>2. An excellent woman.<BR> E. कम् water, and अल what adorns, or कम्<BR>to desire, with कलच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=156-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कमलच्छद
कमलच्छद m. (-दः)<BR>	 1. A heron: see कङ्क 2. Petal of the lotus.<BR> E. कमल,<BR>and छद a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=156-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कमलाकर|कमलाकरः
कमलाकर m. (-रः) A lake, &c. where lotuses abound.<BR> E. कमल, and आकर<BR>a mine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=156-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कमलासन|कमलासनः
कमलासन m. (-नः) An epithet of BRAHMĀ.<BR> E. कमल a lotus, and आसन<BR>seat or abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=156-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कमलिनी
कमलिनी f. (-नी) A number of lotus flowers, or a place abounding with<BR>them.<BR> E. कमल, इनि and ङीष् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=156-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कमलोत्तर|कमलोत्तरं
कमलोत्तर n. (-रं) Safflower, (Carthamus tinctorius.)<BR> E. कमल, and उत्तर<BR>best, excellent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=156-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कमा
कमा f. (-मा) Beauty, radiance.<BR> E. कम् to desire, अङ् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=156-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कमितृ
कमितृ mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ) Lustful, desirous, cupidinous.<BR> E. कम् to desire,<BR>तृच् affix; and इ inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=156-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कम्प|कंप|कंपः|कम्पः
कम्प m. (-म्पः) Tremour, trembling, shaking.<BR> E. कपि to shake, and अच्<BR>affix; also कम्पन, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=156-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कम्पन|कंपन|कम्पनं|कम्पनः
कम्पन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Trembling, unsteady, shaken.<BR>	 n. (-नं) Trembling,<BR>quivering.<BR>	 m. (-नः) The dewy season. (Nov.-Dec.)<BR> E. कपि to<BR>tremble, and युच् or ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=156-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कम्पमान
कम्पमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Trembling.<BR> E. कपि to tremble, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=156-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कम्पलक्ष्मन्|कंपलक्ष्मन्
कम्पलक्ष्मन् m. (-क्ष्मा) Air, wind.<BR> E. कम्प trembling, and लक्ष्मन् mark or<BR>sign.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=156-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कम्पाक|कंपाक|कंपाकः|कम्पाकः
कम्पाक m. (-कः) Wind, air.<BR> E. काकुन् affixed to कपि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=156-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कम्पान्वित
कम्पान्वित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Trembling, agitated.<BR> E. कम्प, and अन्वित pos-<BR>sessed of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=156-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कम्पित|कंपित|कम्पितं
कम्पित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Shaking, shaken, trembling.<BR>	 n. (-तं) Trembling,<BR>a trembling, a tremor<BR> E. कपि and क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=156-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कम्पिल|कम्पिलः
कम्पिल m. (-लः) A plant: see रोचनी; see काम्पिल्ल; also कम्पिल्ल and कम्पील.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=156-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कम्प्र|कंप्र
कम्प्र mfn. (-म्प्रः-म्प्रा-म्प्रं) Trembling, shaken.<BR> E. कपि, and र aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=156-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कम्ब
कम्ब r. 1st. cl. (कम्बति) To go, to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=156-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कम्बर|कंबर|कम्बरः
कम्बर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Variegated.<BR>	 m. (-रः) Variegated, (the colour.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=156-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कम्बल|कंबल|कम्बलं|कंबलः|कम्बलः
कम्बल m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. A blanket.<BR>	 2. A chief of the Nagas or serpents.<BR>	 3. A<BR>small worm.<BR>	 4. A dewlap.<BR>	 5. An upper cloth or garment.<BR>	 6. A<BR>sort of deer.<BR>	 n. (-लं) Water.<BR> E. कम् to desire, कल Uṇādi affix,<BR>and ब inserted; or कम् the head, water, &c. and बल् to be strong,<BR>affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=156-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कम्बलकारक
कम्बलकारक m. (-कः) Woollen cloth manufacturer.<BR> E. कम्बल, and कारक<BR>who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=156-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कम्बलवाह्यक|कंबलवाह्यक
कम्बलवाह्यक n. (-कं) A kind of carriage, covered with a coarse blanket<BR>or woollen cloth, and drawn by oxen.<BR> E. कम्बल and वह् to bear,<BR>affixes ण्यत् and कन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=156-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कम्बलायिन्
कम्बलायिन् m. (-यी) A sort of kite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=156-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कम्बि|कंबिः|कम्बिः
कम्बि f. (-म्बिः)<BR>	 1. A ladle or spoon.<BR>	 2. A shoot, a branch or joint of a<BR>bamboo.<BR> E. कम् to desire, बिन् affix, or with ङीष् added कम्बी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=156-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कम्बु|कंबु|कम्बुः
कम्बु mfn. (-म्बुः-म्बूः-म्बु) Speckled, variegated.<BR>	 mn. (-म्बुः-म्बु)<BR>	 1. A conch,<BR>a shell.<BR>	 m. (-म्बुः)<BR>	 1. A bracelet, a ring.<BR>	 2. A bivalve shell.<BR>	 3. An<BR>elephant.<BR>	 4. The neck.<BR>	 5. A vein or tubular vessel of the body,<BR>&c.<BR> E. कम्ब् to go, उ affix, or कम् to desire; the form is irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=156-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कम्बुक|कंबुकः|कम्बुकः
कम्बुक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) A mean person.<BR>	 m. (-कः) A conch.<BR>	 f. (-का) A<BR>tree (Physais flexuosa.)<BR> E. कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=156-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कम्बुग्रीवा|कंबुग्रीवा
कम्बुग्रीवा f. (-वा) A neck marked with three lines like a shell, and con-<BR>sidered to be indicative of exalted fortune.<BR> E. कम्बु a shell, and ग्रीवा<BR>the neck.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=156-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कम्बू|कंबू
कम्बू mfn. (-म्बूः-म्बूः-म्बु) A thief, a plunderer.<BR>	 m. (-म्बूः) A bracelet. E.<BR>कम् to desire, ऊ Uṇādi affix, and बुक् inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=156-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कम्बोज|कंबोज|कंबोजः|कम्बोजः
कम्बोज m. (-जः)<BR>	 1. The name of a country in the north of India, Cam-<BR>boja or Camboya.<BR>	 2. A kind of shell.<BR>	 3. A description of<BR>elephant: see काम्बोज.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=157-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कम्भारी
कम्भारी f. (-री) A plant, (Gmelina arborea.)<BR> E. कम् water, भार a burthen,<BR>ङीष् affix; also गम्भारी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=157-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कम्भु|कंभु
कम्भु n. (-म्भु) The root of the Andropogon muricatum.<BR> E. कं water, भू<BR>produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=157-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कम्र|कम्रः
कम्र mfn. (-म्रः-म्रा-म्रं)<BR>	 1. Desirous, cupidinous.<BR>	 2. Beautiful, desirable. E.<BR>कम् to desire, रन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=157-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कयस्था
कयस्था f. (-स्था) A medicinal plant, commonly Kakoli; also कायस्था, or<BR>more accurately, perhaps, वयस्था.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=157-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर|करः
कर mfn. (-रः-रा-री-रं) Who or what does, makes or causes, as किङ्करः a<BR>servant, who does anything; भयङ्करः frightful, what causes fear;<BR>उपकरः who gives aid: अपकरः who does ill, &c.<BR>	 m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A ray of<BR>light, a sun or moonbeams.<BR>	 2. Royal revenue toll, tax, impost, &c.<BR>3. The hand.<BR>	 4. Hail.<BR>	 5. An elephant's trunk.<BR> E. कृञ् to do, &c. ट<BR>or अप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=157-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करक|करकं|करकः
करक mf. (-कः-का) Hail.<BR>	 mn. (-कः-कं)<BR>	 1. The water-pot of the student<BR>or ascetic.<BR>	 2. The shell of the cocoanut hollowed to form a vessel.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. The pomegranate tree.<BR>	 2. Toll, tax.<BR>	 3. A particular<BR>sort of bird.<BR>	 4. A plant, (Galedupa arborea, &c.) See करञ्ज.<BR>	 5. A<BR>tree, (Butea frondosa.)<BR> E. कन् added to the preceding, or कृ to in-<BR>jure, &c. and वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=157-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करकण्टक|करकंटक|करकण्टकः
करकण्टक m. (-कः) The finger-nail.<BR> E. कर the hand, and कण्टक a thorn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=157-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करकमल
करकमल n. (-लं) The hand, especially of a lover, a mistress, &c.<BR> E. कर,<BR>and कमल a lotus; also similar compounds, as करपद्म, करपङ्कज,<BR>करपल्लव, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=157-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करकलश|करकलशः
करकलश m. (-शः) The hand hollowed to receive water.<BR> E. कर, and कलश a ewer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=157-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करकाम्भस्|करकांभस्
करकाम्भस् m. (-म्भाः) The cocoanut tree, (Cosos nucifera.)<BR> E. करक the<BR>shell, and अम्भस् the water, the nut containing a serous fluid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=157-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करकुद्मल
करकुद्मल n. (-लं) A finger.<BR> E. कर, and कुद्मल a bud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=157-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करकोष|करकोषः
करकोष m. (-षः) The hollow of the hand.<BR> E. कर, and कोष receptacle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=157-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करग्रह|करग्रहः
करग्रह m. (-हः)<BR>	 1. Marriage.<BR>	 2. Levying or gathering a tax.<BR>	 3. A tax-<BR>gatherer.<BR>	 4. Taking the hand.<BR> E. कर, and ग्रह taking: one part of<BR>the ceremony of marriage is the placing of the right hand of the<BR>bride with the palm uppermost, in the right hand of the bride-<BR>groom; also करग्राह.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=157-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करग्रहण
करग्रहण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Levying or gathering a tax.<BR>	 2. Taking the hand.<BR>	 3.<BR>Marriage.<BR> E. कर, and ग्रहण taking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=157-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करग्राहिन्
करग्राहिन् mfn. (-ही-हिणी-हि)<BR>	 1. Levying a tax.<BR>	 2. Taking the hand. E.<BR>कर, and ग्राहिन् who takes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=157-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करघर्षण|करघर्षणः
करघर्षण m. (-णः) The churning stick.<BR>	 n. (-णं) Rubbing the hands to-<BR>gether.<BR> E. कर the hand, and घर्षण rubbing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=157-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करघर्षिन्
करघर्षिन् m. (-र्षी) The churning stick.<BR> E. कर the hand, घृष् to rub,<BR>णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=157-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करङ्क|करंक|करंकः|करङ्कः
करङ्क m. (-ङ्कः)<BR>	 1. The head.<BR>	 2. A cocoanut hollowed so as to form a cup<BR>or vessel.<BR>	 3. Any bone of the body.<BR>	 4. A kind of sugar-cane.<BR> E. कॄ<BR>to send or throw, &c. अंक aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=157-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करङ्कशालि|करङ्कशालिः
करङ्कशालि m. (-लिः) A sort of sugar-cane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=157-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करङ्गण
करङ्गण n. (-णं) A market or fair.<BR> E. कर tax, and गण collection, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=157-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करच्छद|करच्छदः
करच्छद m. (-दः) The teak tree.<BR> E. कर, and छद a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=157-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करज|करजं|करजः
करज mfn. (-जः-जा-जं) Produced in or from a hand, a ray, &c.<BR>	 m. (-जः)<BR>1. A finger-nail.<BR>	 2. The name of a timber tree, commonly Karañja,<BR>(Galedupa arborea, Rox.)<BR>	 n. (-जं) A perfume, commonly Nakhi<BR>resembling a nail in appearance.<BR> E. कर the hand, and ज produced;<BR>or कं pleasure, रञ्ज् to colour, &c. अच् affix; see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=157-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करजाल
करजाल n. (-लं) A pencil of rays, a stream of light.<BR> E. कर, and जाल<BR>multitude.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=157-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करञ्ज|करंज|करंजः|करञ्जः
करञ्ज m. (-ञ्जः) The name of a plant, commonly Karañja (Galedupa<BR>arborea, Rox.)<BR> E. क water, and रञ्ज् to colour, अच् affix: see करज.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=157-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करञ्जक|करञ्जकः
करञ्जक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. Karañja: see the preceding.<BR>	 2. Another plant,<BR>(Verbesina scandens, Rox.) Sea भृङ्गराज.<BR> E. कन् added to the fore-<BR>going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=157-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करट|करटः
करट m. (-टः)<BR>	 1. A crow.<BR>	 2. An elephant's cheek.<BR>	 3. Safflower or car-<BR>thamus.<BR>	 4. A man of a low or degraded profession.<BR>	 5. The first<BR>Śrāddha or ceremony performed in honour of a deceased relation.<BR>6. An atheist, an unbeliever, an oppugner of the doctrines of<BR>the Vedas.<BR>	 7. A musical instrument, (Castanets?)<BR>	 f. (-टा) A cow<BR>difficult to be milked.<BR> E. क pleasure, &c. रट् to sound, and अच्<BR>affix; or कृ to do, and अटन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=157-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करटक|करटकः
करटक m. (-कः) A crow.<BR> E. कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=157-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करटिन्
करटिन् m. (-टी) An elephant.<BR> E. करट and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=157-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करटु|करटुः
करटु m. (-टुः) The numidian crane.<BR> E. कर् for कुत् bad, अट् to go, and<BR>डु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=157-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करण|करणं|करणः
करण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. An instrument or means of action.<BR>	 2. Making, doing.<BR>3. Action, act.<BR>	 4. Cause, motive.<BR>	 5. Business, occupation, as trade.<BR>&c.<BR>	 6. An organ of sense.<BR>	 7. The body.<BR>	 8. The mind or heart.<BR>	 9.<BR>A field.<BR>	 10. Grain.<BR>	 11. The posture, abstinence, &c. of an ascetic.<BR>12. Copulation, (seu modus coeundi.)<BR>	 13. The usage or practice of the<BR>writer caste.<BR>	 14. Acting, dramatic action.<BR>	 15. Song, singing.<BR>	 16. The<BR>particular business of any tribe or caste.<BR>	 17. Plaistering, spreading<BR>any thing with the hand.<BR>	 18. A Karana, an astrological division<BR>of time; the Karanas are eleven: 7 moveable and 4 fixed, and<BR>two are equal to a lunar day; or the time during which the moon's<BR>motion from the sun amounts to 6°.<BR>	 19. (In grammar) The instru-<BR>mental case, or noun in that case.<BR>	 m. (-णः) A man of a mixed<BR>class, the son of a Śūdra woman by a Vaiśya; or, according to<BR>some, of an outcaste Kṣatriya, by a Kṣatriya female; the<BR>occupation of this class is writing, accounts, &c. a writer, a scribe.<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>	 1. A woman of the same caste.<BR>	 2. (In arithmetic, &c.) A<BR>surd or irrational quantity.<BR> E. कृ to do, to act, &c. ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=157-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करणत्राण|करणत्राणं
करणत्राण n. (-णं) The head.<BR> E. करण an organ of sense, and त्राण preserving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=157-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करणत्व
करणत्व n. (-त्वं) Instrumentality, mediate agency.<BR> E. त्व added to करण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=157-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करणनियम
करणनियम m. (-मः) Suppression or restraint of the organs of sense. E.<BR>करण, and नियम restraint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=157-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करणि
करणि f. (-णिः) Doing, making, effecting.<BR> E. कृ to do, अमि affix; also with<BR>कन् added करणिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=157-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करणीय|करणीयं
करणीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) To be done or made.<BR> E. कृ to do, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=157-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करणीसुता
करणीसुता f. (-ता) An adopted daughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=157-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करण्ड|करंड|करंडः|करण्डः
करण्ड m. (-ण्डः)<BR>	 1. A basket or covered box of bamboo wicker work.<BR>	 2.<BR>A bee-hive, a honey-comb.<BR>	 3. A sword.<BR>	 4. A sort of duck.<BR>	 5. An<BR>aquatic weed, (Vallisneria.)<BR> E. कृ to do, अण्डन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=157-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करण्डिन्|करंडिन्
करण्डिन् m. (-ण्डी) A fish in general.<BR> E. करण्ड Vallisneria, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=157-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करतल|करतलः
करतल n. (-लं) The palm of the hand.<BR> E. कर, and तल lower part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=157-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करतलधृत
करतलधृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Held in the hand.<BR> E. करतल, and धृत held.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=157-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करतलस्थ
करतलस्थ mfn. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थं) Held in the hand, what is in or under the<BR>hand.<BR> E. करतल, and स्य what is.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=157-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करताल|करतालं|करतालः
करताल nf. (-लं-ली)<BR>	 1. A musical instrument, a cymbal.<BR>	 2. Beating time<BR>by clapping the hands.<BR> E. कर the hand, ताल musical time, and<BR>ङीष् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=157-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करतोया
करतोया f. (-या) The Karatoya river, a river in the north-east of Bengal.<BR>E. कर the hand, and तोय water: at the wedding of ŚIVA and<BR>PARVATI, the water which had been poured into the hand of the<BR>former, constituted, upon its being thrown on the ground, the<BR>source of this river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=157-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करद
करद mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>	 1. Subject to tax or duty.<BR>	 2. Tributary.<BR>	 3. Who<BR>gives his hand, &c.<BR> E. कर, and द who gives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=157-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करदक्ष
करदक्ष mfn. (-क्षः-क्षा-क्षं) Handy, dexterous, ready.<BR> E. कर, and दक्ष clever.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=157-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करदीकृत
करदीकृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Subjugated, made tributary.<BR> E. करद, and कृत<BR>made with च्वि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=157-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करधृत
करधृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Held, supported by the hand.<BR> E. कर, and धृत held.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=158-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करनिहित
करनिहित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Held in the hand.<BR> E. कर, and निहित placed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=158-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करपत्र|करपत्रं
करपत्र n. (-त्रं)<BR>	 1. A saw.<BR>	 2. Splashing water about while bathing, playing<BR>or gamboling in water.<BR> E. कर, and पत्र a leaf; being in the hand<BR>as a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=158-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करपत्रवत्|करपत्त्रवन्त्|करपत्रवन्त्
करपत्रवत् m. (-वान्) The palmyra tree (Borassus flabelliformis.)<BR> E. करपत्र<BR>a saw, and मतुप् affix, the spatha being compared to a saw.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=158-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करपत्रिका
करपत्रिका f. (-का) Playing with water, gamboling in it, splashing it<BR>about; also करपत्र, करपात्र and करपत्रिक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=158-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करपर्ण|करपर्णः|करपर्ण्ण
करपर्ण m. (-र्णः) A species of castor oil tree.<BR> E. कर, and पर्ण a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=158-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करपल्लव|करपल्लवः
करपल्लव m. (-वः) A finger.<BR> E. कर, and पल्लव a shoot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=158-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करपात्र|करपात्रं
करपात्र n. (-त्रं)<BR>	 1. The hand hollowed so as to hold anything.<BR>	 2. The<BR>throwing of water in sport.<BR> E. कर, and पात्र a cup.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=158-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करपाल|करपालः
करपाल m. (-लः) A sword, a scymitar.<BR> E. कर the hand, and पल protect-<BR>ing, or with बल to be strong, करबाल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=158-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करपालिका
करपालिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. A cudgel, a short club or wooden sword.<BR>	 2. A<BR>sword or one edged knife.<BR> E. कर the hand, पाल to nourish, ण्वुल्<BR>affix, and the fem. termination.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=158-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करपुट|करपुटः
करपुट n. (-टं)<BR>	 1. Joining the palms of the hands to show respect.<BR>	 2. The<BR>hands joined and hollowed to receive anything.<BR> E. कर, and पुट<BR>a bag.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=158-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करपृष्ठ
करपृष्ठ n. (-ष्ठं) Back of the hand.<BR> E. कर, and पृष्ठ back.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=158-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करप्रचेय
करप्रचेय mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>	 1. To be held, to be taken hold of.<BR>	 2. To be<BR>collected by taxes.<BR> E. कर, and प्रचेय to be accumulated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=158-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करप्राप्त
करप्राप्त mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं) Held in hand, got, secured.<BR> E. कर, and प्राप्त obtained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=158-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करबाल|करबालः
करबाल n. (-लं)<BR>	 1. A finger-nail.<BR>	 2. A sword, a scymitar; see करपाल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=158-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करबालिका
करबालिका f. (-का) A small sword, &c. see करपालिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=158-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करभ|करभः
करभ m. (-भः)<BR>	 1. The metacarpus, the hand from the wrist to the root<BR>of the fingers.<BR>	 2. A young camel or any young animal.<BR>	 3. A young<BR>elephant.<BR>	 4. A perfume, commonly Nakhi.<BR>	 f. (-भी) A she camel. E.<BR>कृ to reject, अभच् Uṇādi affix: see कलभ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=158-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करभप्रिया
करभप्रिया f. (-या) A plant, a sort of Hedysarum.<BR> E. करभ, and प्रिय fond<BR>of; fodder for camels.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=158-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करभिन्
करभिन् m. (-भी) An elephant.<BR> E. करभ and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=158-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करभीर|करभीरः
करभीर m. (-रः) A lion.<BR> E. करभ a young animal, and ईर who destroys.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=158-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करभूषण|करभूषणं
करभूषण n. (-णं) A bracelet, an ornament worn round the wrist.<BR> E. कर<BR>the hand, and भूषण an ornament.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=158-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करमट्ट|करमट्टः
करमट्ट m. (-ट्टः) The betel nut tree: see गुवाक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=158-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करमरिन्
करमरिन् m. (-री) A prisoner, a captive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=158-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करमर्द्द|करमर्द|करमर्दः|करमर्द्दः
करमर्द्द m. (-र्द्दः) A small tree (bearing an acid fruit, commonly Karonda<BR>or Karinda, (Carissa carondas.)<BR> E. कर the hand, and मृद् to destroy,<BR>अण् affix; what is pulled by the hand; also with कन् affix,<BR>करमर्द्दक and fem. with ङीष् affix करमर्द्दी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=158-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करमर्द्दक|करमर्दक|करमर्दकः|करमर्द्दकः
करमर्द्दक m. (-कः) See the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=158-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करमाल|करमालः
करमाल m. (-लः) Smoke, probably an error or corruption for खतमाल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=158-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करमाला
करमाला f. (-ला) The hand used as a rosary, the joints of the fingers<BR>corresponding to the beads.<BR> E. कर, and माला a rosary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=158-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करमुक्त|करमुक्तं
करमुक्त n. (-क्तं) A missile weapon, but thrown by the hand, a dart,<BR>javelin, &c.<BR> E. कर, and मुक्त released.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=158-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कराग्रपल्लव
कराग्रपल्लव m. (-वः) A finger.<BR> E. कर, and अग्र to the point, पल्लव a shoot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=158-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करम्ब|करंब|करंबः|करम्बः
करम्ब mfn. (-म्बः-म्बा-म्बं)<BR>	 1. Mixed, intermingled.<BR>	 2. Set, inlaid.<BR>	 m. (-म्बः)<BR>Flour or meal mixed with curds: see करम्भ.<BR> E. कृ to do, अम्बच्<BR>Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=158-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करम्बित|करंबित|करम्बितः
करम्बित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Intermingled, mixed, blended, &c.<BR>	 2. Pound-<BR>ed, reduced to grains or dust.<BR>	 3. Set, inlaid.<BR> E. करम्ब and इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=158-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करम्भ|करंभ|करंभः|करम्भः
करम्भ m. (-म्भः) A cake, flour or meal mixed with curds.<BR> E. क water, and<BR>रभि to send. &c. अच् affix; also with कन् added करम्भक; also with<BR>रवि to sound, &c. करम्ब, &c. as above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=158-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कररुद्ध
कररुद्ध mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं) Stopped by the hand, held tight or fast.<BR> E. कर,<BR>and रुद्ध stopped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=158-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कररुह|कररुहः
कररुह m. (-हः) A finger-nail.<BR> E. कर the hand, and रुह to grow, to rise,<BR>affix क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=158-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करर्द्धि|करर्द्धिः
करर्द्धि m. (-र्द्धिः) A small musical instrument used for marking time,<BR>(a castanet,) or clapping the hands together for that purpose. E.<BR>कर the hand, ऋद्धि property.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=158-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करवालिका
करवालिका f. (-का) A small club, &c. see करबालिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=158-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करवी
करवी f. (-वी) The leaf of the Asafœtida plant, Hingupatri: see कवरी<BR>and कारवी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=158-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करवीर|करवीरः
करवीर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A fragrant plant, (Oleander or Nerium odorum.)<BR>	 2. The<BR>name of a demon.<BR>	 3. A sword or scymitar.<BR>	 4. A cemetery, a place<BR>for burning or interring the dead.<BR>	 f. (-रा) Red arsenic.<BR>	 f. (-री)<BR>	 1. A<BR>name of ADITI, the mother of the gods.<BR>	 2. A good cow.<BR>	 3. A wo-<BR>man who has borne a son, a mother.<BR> E. कर here said to mean a<BR>root, वीर to become evident, and अच् affix; or कर hand, वि prefixed<BR>to ईर् to go, &c. affix क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=158-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करवीरक|करवीरकः
करवीरक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A sword.<BR>	 2. A poison, the poisonous root of the<BR>Oleander.<BR>	 3. A tree, (Pentaptera arjuna.)<BR> E. कन् added to the<BR>preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=158-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करशाखा
करशाखा f. (-खा) A finger.<BR> E. कर the hand, and शाखा a branch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=158-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करशीकर|करशीकरः
करशीकर m. (-रः) Water expelled by an elephant's trunk.<BR> E. कर his<BR>trunk, and शीकर drizzling rain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=158-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करशूक|करशूकः
करशूक m. (-कः) A finger-nail.<BR> E. कर the hand, शूक the beard of corn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=158-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करशोथ|करशोथः
करशोथ m. (-थः) Œdematous swelling of the hands.<BR> E. कर, and शोथ<BR>swelling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=158-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करहाट|करहाटः
करहाट m. (-टः)<BR>	 1. The fibrous root of a lotus.<BR>	 2. A tree, (Vangueria<BR>spinosa.)<BR> E. क water, and रह् to abandon, करह a lotus, अट what<BR>goes, or by what it goes; or कर the hand, हट् to illuminate or<BR>adorn, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=158-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करहाटक|करहाटकः
करहाटक m. (-कः) The name of a tree, (Vangueria spinosa.)<BR> E. कन्<BR>added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=158-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कराघात|कराघातः
कराघात m. (-तः) A thump, a blow with the hand.<BR> E. कर, and आघात a blow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=158-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करामर्द्द|करामर्द|करामर्दः|करामर्द्दः
करामर्द्द m. (-र्द्दः) A fruit-tree, (Carissa carondas:) see करमर्द्ध.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=158-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कराम्बुक|कराम्बुकः
कराम्बुक m. (-कः) A plant, (Flacourtia cataphracta, Rox.) See कृष्णपाक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=158-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कराम्लक|कराम्लकः
कराम्लक m. (-कः) A fruit-tree, (Carissa carondas.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=158-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करायिका
करायिका f. (-का) A bird, a small kind of crane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=158-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करारोट|करारोटः
करारोट m. (-टः) A finger ring.<BR> E. कर the hand, रुट् to shine, with आङ्<BR>prefixed, affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=158-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कराल|करालं|करालः
कराल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>	 1. Great, large.<BR>	 2. High, lofty.<BR>	 3. Formidable,<BR>terrible.<BR>	 4. Having projecting teeth.<BR>	 m. (-लः) Resin, pitch, or a<BR>mixture of oil and the resin of the Sal tree.<BR>	 n. (-लं) A dark kind<BR>of Tulasi or Basil.<BR>	 f. (-ला) A kind of swallow wort, commonly<BR>Anantamul, (Hemisdemus Indicus.) See शारिवा.<BR>	 f. (-ली) One of<BR>the seven tongues of AGNI or fire.<BR> E. कर the hand, &c. ला with आङ्<BR>prefixed to take, and क affix; or कर, and अल् to be able, &c. affix<BR>अण्, fem. do टाप् or ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=158-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करालक|करालकः
करालक m. (-कः) A sort of Basil, the dark kind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=158-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करालकर
करालकर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>	 1. Having a large trunk, (an elephant.)<BR>	 2.<BR>Having a powerful arm or hand.<BR> E. कराल, and कर a hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=158-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करालम्ब|करालंब|करालम्बः
करालम्ब mfn. (-म्बः-म्बा-म्बं) One who stretches out his hand to support<BR>or pick up another, &c.<BR> E. कर, and आलम्ब what supports.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=158-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करालम्बन
करालम्बन n. (-नं) Extending the hand, taking by the hand, helping,<BR>sustaining.<BR> E. कर, and आलम्बन supporting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=158-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करालवदन
करालवदन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Of hideous aspect, ugly, frightful.<BR>	 f. (-ना) A<BR>form or emanation of DURGĀ.<BR> E. कराल, and वदन countenance; also<BR>करालानन, करालमुख, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=158-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करालिक|करालिकः
करालिक m. (-कः) A tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=158-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करालित
करालित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Afraid of, alarmed by or at.<BR>	 2. Rendered<BR>formidable.<BR>	 3. Magnified.<BR> E. कराल and इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=158-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करिकणवल्ली
करिकणवल्ली f. (-ल्ली) A species of pepper, (Piper chavya.)<BR> E. करिकण<BR>elephant-pepper, वल्ली a vine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=158-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करिकुम्भ|करिकुंभ|करिकुम्भः
करिकुम्भ m. (-म्भः) The frontal globe of an elephant.<BR> E. करि, and कुम्भ the<BR>same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=159-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करिकुसुम्भ|करिकुसुम्भः
करिकुसुम्भ m. (-म्भः) A fragrant powder prepared from the flowers of the<BR>Nāgakesara, (Mesua ferrea;) also करिकुमुम्भक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=159-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करिगर्ज्जित|करिगर्जित|करिगर्ज्जितं
करिगर्ज्जित n. (-तं) The roaring of elephants.<BR> E. करिन् an elephant, and<BR>गर्ज्जित sounding, thundering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=159-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करिचर्म्मन्|करिचर्मन्
करिचर्म्मन् n. (-र्म्म) An elephant's hide.<BR> E. करिन्, and चर्म्मन् skin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=159-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करिज|करिजः
करिज m. (-जः) A young elephant.<BR> E. करि an elephant, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=159-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करिदन्त|करिदंत|करिदन्तः
करिदन्त m. (-न्तः)<BR>	 1. An elephant's tusk.<BR>	 2. Ivory.<BR> E. करिन्, and दन्त a<BR>tooth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=159-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करिदारक|करिदारकः
करिदारक m. (-कः) A lion.<BR> E. करिन् an elephant, दॄ to tear or rend, ण्वुल्<BR>affix; or with युच् affix करिदारण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=159-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करिन्
करिन् m. (-री) An elephant.<BR> E. कर the proboscis of this animal, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=159-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करिनासिका
करिनासिका f. (-का) A musical instrument.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=159-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करिपिप्पली
करिपिप्पली f. (-ली) A plant bearing a pungent fruit, (Pothos officinalis,<BR>Rox.)<BR> E. करि, and पिप्पली long-pepper; Elephant-pepper; consi-<BR>dered by native writers as a large species of that condiment; also<BR>गजपिप्पली, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=159-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करिपोत|करिपोतः
करिपोत m. (-तः) A young elephant, one under ten years old.<BR> E. करि,<BR>and पोत a young animal; also करिशावक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=159-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करिबन्ध|करिबंध|करिबन्धः
करिबन्ध m. (-न्धः) The post to which an elephant is tied.<BR> E. करि, and बन्ध<BR>a binding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=159-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करिमाचल|करिमाचलः
करिमाचल m. (-लः) A lion.<BR> E. करि, मा splendor, and चल् to go; the lion<BR>being considered as the natural enemy and destroyer of the<BR>elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=159-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करिमुख|करिमुखः
करिमुख m. (-खः) A title of GANESA.<BR> E. करि, and मुख a face: this diety<BR>being represented with an elephant's head.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=159-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करियादस्
करियादस् n. (-दः) A water-elephant, a hippopotamus.<BR>	 n. करि, and यादस्<BR>any aquatic animal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=159-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करिर|करिरः
करिर m. (-रः) The shoot of a bamboo: see करीर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=159-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करिशावक|करिशावकः
करिशावक m. (-कः) A young elephant under five years old; according<BR>to some, also until ten years. E. See करिपोत, शावक meaning a<BR>young animal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=159-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करिष्ठ
करिष्ठ mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठा-ष्ठं) Doing much.<BR> E. कर who does, इष्ठन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=159-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करिष्यत्|करिष्यन्त्
करिष्यत् mfn. (-ष्यन्-ष्यन्ती-ष्यत्) Doing, (with a future sense,) about to do.<BR>E. कृ to do, शतृ affix of the future.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=159-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करिष्यमाण
करिष्यमाण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) About to do, going to do.<BR> E. कृ to do, शानच्<BR>affix of the future.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=159-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करीन्द्र|करींद्र|करीन्द्रः
करीन्द्र m. (-न्द्रः)<BR>	 1. A large, or a state elephant.<BR>	 2. INDRA'S<BR>elephant.<BR> E. करि, and इन्द्र chief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=159-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करीयस्
करीयस् mfn. (-यान्-यसी-यः) Who does much.<BR> E. कर who does, ईथसुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=159-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करीर|करीरः
करीर mn. (-रः-रं) The shoot of a bamboo; also करिर.<BR>	 m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A<BR>thorny plant, described as growing in deserts, and fed upon by<BR>camels, commonly Karil, (Capparis aphylla, Rox.)<BR>	 2. A water jar.<BR>f. (-रा or -री)<BR>	 1. The root of an elephant's tusk.<BR>	 2. A cricket, a<BR>small grasshopper, &c.<BR> E. कॄ to injure, to throw or send, &c. and<BR>ईरण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=159-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करीरिका
करीरिका f. (-का) The root of an elephant's tusk: see करीरी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=159-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करीष|करीषं|करीषः
करीष mn. (-षः-षं) Dry cowdung.<BR> E. कॄ to throw, send, &c. and ईषन्<BR>Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=159-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करीषङ्कषा|करीषंकषा
करीषङ्कषा f. (-षा) A strong wind, a gale.<BR> E. करीष, कष् to disturb, खच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=159-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करीषाग्नि|करीषाग्निः
करीषाग्नि m. (-ग्निः) A fire of dry cowdung.<BR> E. करीष, and अग्नि fire; this<BR>substance is very generally used as fuel in Hindustan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=159-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करुण|करुणः
करुण mf. (-णः-णा) Tenderness, pity, compassion, the feeling or<BR>sentiment. adv. (-णं) Pitifully, in distress.<BR>	 m. (-णः)<BR>	 1. Sorrow,<BR>affliction, one of the eight sentiments.<BR>	 2. The name of a fruit-tree,<BR>the pamplemousse, (Citrus decumana.)<BR>	 3. A Jina or Jaina saint. E.<BR>कॄ to send or cast, उनन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=159-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करुणात्मक
करुणात्मक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Compassionate, tender-hearted.<BR> E. करुणा,<BR>आत्म self, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=159-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करुणापर|करुणापरः
करुणापर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Compassionate, tender.<BR> E. करुणा, पर excellent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=159-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करुणामल्ली
करुणामल्ली f. (-ल्ली) Double jasmine: see नवमल्ली.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=159-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करुणामय
करुणामय mfn. (-यः-यी-यं) Gentle, compassionate.<BR> E. करुणा and मयट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=159-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करुणार्द्र
करुणार्द्र mfn. (-र्द्रः-र्द्रा-र्द्रं) Tender-hearted, soft, sensitive.<BR> E. करुणा; and<BR>आर्द्र moist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=159-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करुणाविप्रलम्भ
करुणाविप्रलम्भ m. (-म्भः) Grief of separation with the uncertainty of meet-<BR>ing again, fears occurring in absence.<BR> E. करुणा sorrow, and विप्रलम्भ<BR>separation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=159-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करुणावेदिता
करुणावेदिता f. (-ता) Charitableness, kindliness.<BR> E. करुणा, वेदिन् who knows,<BR>तल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=159-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करेट|करेटः
करेट m. (-टः) A finger-nail.<BR> E. कर, and इट् to go, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=159-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करेटव्या
करेटव्या f. (-व्या) The numidian crane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=159-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करेटु|करेटुः
करेटु mf. (-टुः-टुः) The numidian crane.<BR> E. क for कुत् bad, or क water,<BR>and रेट् to sound, उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=159-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करेणु|करेणुः
करेणु mf. (-णुः-णुः) A male or female elephant.<BR>	 m. (-णुः) A plant: see<BR>कर्णिकार.<BR> E. कृ to do, &c. एणु Uṇādi affix; also with a final long<BR>vowel, करेणू.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=159-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करेणुभू
करेणुभू m. (-भूः) The name of a Muni or saint; also पालकाप्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=159-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करेणुवर्य्य|करेणुवर्य
करेणुवर्य्य m. (-र्य्यः) A large or powerful elephant.<BR> E. करेणु, and वर्य्य<BR>excellent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=159-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करेणुसुत|करेणुसुतः
करेणुसुत m. (-तः) The name of a Muni.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=159-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करेणू
करेणू mf. (-णूः-णूः) A male or female elephant: see करेणु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=159-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करेनर|करेनरः
करेनर m. (-रः) Benzoin or storax.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=159-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करोट|करोटं
करोट mf. (-टः-टिः or -टी) The bones of the head, the scull.<BR> E. क the<BR>head, रुट् to oppose, to defend, &c. affixes अच् and इन् or ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=159-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करोत्कर
करोत्कर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A bundle of rags.<BR>	 2. A heavy tax.<BR> E. कर, and उत्कर<BR>plenty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=159-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करोदक
करोदक n. (-कं) Water held in, or poured into the hand.<BR> E. कर, and<BR>उदक water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=159-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्क|कर्कः
कर्क mfn. (-र्कः-र्का-र्कं)<BR>	 1. White.<BR>	 2. Good, excellent.<BR>	 m. (-र्कः)<BR>	 1. A white<BR>horse.<BR>	 2. A mirror.<BR>	 3. A water jar.<BR>	 4. A crab.<BR>	 5. A sign of the<BR>zodiac, (Cancer.)<BR>	 6. A fire.<BR>	 7. A long gourd.<BR>	 8. Beauty.<BR> E. कृ to do,<BR>&c. क Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=159-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्कचिर्भिटी
कर्कचिर्भिटी f. (-टी) A small cucumber.<BR> E. कर्क, and चिर्भिटी the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=159-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्कट|कर्कटः
कर्कट m. (-टः)<BR>	 1. A crab.<BR>	 2. The sign of the zodiac, (Cancer.)<BR>	 3. A kind<BR>of bird, the numidian crane.<BR>	 4. A long gourd: see तुम्बी.<BR>	 5. The<BR>fibrous root of the lotus.<BR>	 6. The curved end of the beam of a<BR>balance, to which the strings supporting the scale are attached.<BR>7. A compass.<BR>	 8. The radius of a circle.<BR>	 f. (-टा) A plant, common-<BR>ly Kurkavali, (Momordica mixta.)<BR>	 f. (-टी)<BR>	 1. A kind of cucumber,<BR>(Cucumis utilatissimus, Rox.)<BR>	 2. The fruit of the silk-cotton<BR>tree.<BR>	 3. A snake.<BR>	 4. A water jar.<BR> E. कर्क a Sautra root, to laugh or<BR>smile, and अटन् affix, fem. affix टाप् or ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=159-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्कटक|कर्कटकः
कर्कटक m. (-कः) A crab.<BR> E. कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=159-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्कटशृङ्गिका
कर्कटशृङ्गिका f. (-का) A plant, commonly Kankarasringi: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=159-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्कटशृङ्गी
कर्कटशृङ्गी f. (-ङ्गी) A plant, the fruit of which is compared to the claw<BR>or feelers of a crab, the horn of a goat, &c. see अजशृङ्गी.<BR> E. कर्कट,<BR>शृङ्ग a horn, इनि and ङीष् affixes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=159-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्कटाख्या
कर्कटाख्या f. (-ख्या) See the preceding.<BR> E. कर्कट, and आख्या an appellation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=159-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्कटि|कर्कटिः
कर्कटि f. (-टिः) A sort of cucumber, (Cucumis utilatissimus:) see कर्कट.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=159-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्कटु|कर्कटुः
कर्कटु m. (-टुः) The numidian crane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=159-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्कन्धु|कर्कंधु|कर्कंधुः|कर्कन्धुः
कर्कन्धु mf. (-न्धुः-न्धूः) A tree, the jujube: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=159-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्कन्धू|कर्कंधू
कर्कन्धू mf. (-न्धूः-न्धूः) The jujube (Zizyphus jujuba.)<BR> E. कर्क excellent,<BR>धा to have, and कु Uṇādi affix, fem. affix ऊञ्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=159-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्कर|कर्करं|कर्करः
कर्कर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Hard, firm.<BR>	 n. (-रं) Stone, lime-stone, especially<BR>the nodule found in Bengal under the name of Kankar.<BR>	 m. (-रः) A<BR>mirror.<BR>	 f. (-री) A small water-jar.<BR> E. कर्क beauty, from कर्क to smile,<BR>र from रा to give, fem. affix ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=159-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्कराक्ष|कर्कराक्षः
कर्कराक्ष m. (-क्षः) A wag-tail.<BR> E. कर्कर a mirror, and अक्ष an eye:<BR>bright-eyed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=159-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्कराङ्ग|कर्करांग|कर्कराङ्गः
कर्कराङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः) A gallinule.<BR> E. कर्कर firm, and अङ्ग body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=160-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्कराटु|कर्कराटुः
कर्कराटु m. (-टुः) A glance, a side look.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=160-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्कराटुक|कर्कराटुकः
कर्कराटुक m. (-कः) The numidian crane: see कर्करेटु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=160-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्करान्धक
कर्करान्धक m. (-कः) A blind well, one of which the mouth is overgrown<BR>with grass, &c. so as to be hidden.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=160-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्कराल|कर्करालः
कर्कराल mn. (-लः-लं) A curl, a ringlet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=160-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्करी
कर्करी f. (-री) A water-jar with a spout.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=160-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्करीका
कर्करीका f. (-का) A small water jar.<BR> E. कॄ to scatter, in the reiterative<BR>form, and ईक Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=160-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्करेट|कर्करेटं
कर्करेट n. (-टं) The hand curved as a claw or half moon, for the pur-<BR>pose of grasping anything.<BR> E. कर्कर hard, firm, इट् to go, to be,<BR>affix अप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=160-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्करेटु|कर्करेटुः
कर्करेटु mf. (-टुः-टुः) The numidian crane: see करेटु.<BR> E. कर्कश hard, &c.<BR>रेट् to sound, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=160-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्कश|कर्कशः
कर्कश mfn. (-शः-शा-शं)<BR>	 1. Violent.<BR>	 2. Hard.<BR>	 3. Intangible.<BR>	 4. Cruel.<BR>	 5.<BR>Unfeeling, unmerciful.<BR>	 6. Harsh, unkind.<BR>	 7. Miserly.<BR>	 m. (-शः)<BR>	 1. A<BR>plant, commonly Sunda rochani, (Crinum?)<BR>	 2. A kind of cassia,<BR>(Cassia esculenta.)<BR>	 3. Sugar-cane.<BR>	 4. A sword, a scymitar.<BR>	 f. (-शी)<BR>Wild jujube; also कर्कशिका.<BR> E. कॄ to injure, विच् affix, कश with the<BR>same meaning, and अच्, highly injurious: or कर्क a Sautra root,<BR>and श aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=160-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्कशच्छद|कर्कशच्छदः
कर्कशच्छद m. (-दः)<BR>	 1. A plant, (Trophis aspera.)<BR>	 2. A kind of gourd,<BR>(Trichosanthes diœca.)<BR> E. कर्कश hard, and छद a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=160-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्कशदल|कर्कशदलः
कर्कशदल m. (-लः) A gourd (Trichosanthes diœca.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=160-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्कशवाक्य|कर्कशवाक्यं
कर्कशवाक्य n. (-क्यं) Harsh or contumelious speech.<BR> E. कर्कश, and वाक्य<BR>speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=160-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्कसार|कर्कसारं
कर्कसार n. (-रं) Flour or meal mixed with curds.<BR> E. कर्क, and सार essence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=160-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्कारु|कर्कारुः
कर्कारु m. (-रुः) A pumpkin gourd, (Cucurbita pepo.)<BR> E. कक white, ऋ<BR>to go, or to be, ऊण् affix; also कर्कारू.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=160-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्कारुक|कर्कारुकः
कर्कारुक m. (-कः) A plant, (Convolvulus paniculatus.)<BR> E. कन् added to<BR>the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=160-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्कि|कर्किः|कर्क्कि
कर्कि m. (-र्किः) The sign Cancer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=160-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्केतन|कर्केतनं|कर्केतनः
कर्केतन m. (-नः) A kind of gem or precious stone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=160-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्कोट|कर्कोटः
कर्कोट m. (-टः) One of the principle serpents or Nagas of Pātāla.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=160-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्कोटक|कर्कोटकः
कर्कोटक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A plant, (Ægle marmelos:) see मालूर.<BR>	 2. A Naga<BR>or serpent: see the preceding.<BR>	 3. A kind of gourd, (Momordica<BR>charantia:) in this sense; also कर्कोटिका.<BR>	 4. Sugar-cane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=160-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्कोटकी
कर्कोटकी f. (-की) A plant, a Ghosha with yellow flowers: see घोष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=160-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्घ
कर्घ r. 1st. cl. (कर्घति) To go, to move. Probably a variant misreading for 'karba'^1<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20260702. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/283.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=160-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्चूर|कर्चूरः|कर्च्चूरं|कर्च्चूरः
कर्चूर m. (-रः) A plant, (Curcuma reclinata, Rox.)<BR>	 n. (-रं) Gold: see कर्बूर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=160-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्चूरक|कर्चूरकः|कर्च्चूरकः
कर्चूरक m. (-कः) Zedoary, (Curcuma zerumbet:) see कर्बूरक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=160-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्ज|कर्ज्ज
कर्ज r. 1st cl. (कर्जति) To pain or make uneasy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=160-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्ण|कर्णः|कर्ण्ण
कर्ण r. 10th cl. (कर्णयति) To pierce or bore: with the prefix आङ्, समा,<BR>(सम् and आङ्) or उप, to hear or listen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=160-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्ण|कर्णः|कर्ण्ण
कर्ण m. (-र्णः)<BR>	 1. The ear.<BR>	 2. KARṆA a prince, sovereign of Angadesha,<BR>and elder brother, by the mother's side, to the Pandu princes,<BR>being the son of SŪRYA by KUNTI, before the marriage with<BR>PĀṆḌU.<BR>	 3. The helm or rudder of a vessel.<BR>	 4. (In prosody,) A<BR>spondee, a foot of two long syllables.<BR>	 5. (In geometry,) The hypo-<BR>thenuse of a triangle, or the diagonal of a tetragon.<BR>	 6. A plant,<BR>(Cassia fistula.)<BR>	 7. A kind of swallow wort, (Colotropis gigantea.)<BR>E. कर्ण to hear, घञ् affix; or कृ to do, &c. न Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=160-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णकण्डु|कर्णकण्डुः
कर्णकण्डु m. (-ण्डुः) Itching of the ear.<BR> E. कर्ण, and कण्डु itching.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=160-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णकीटी
कर्णकीटी f. (-टो)<BR>	 1. An insect or worm with many feet, and of a reddish<BR>colour, (Julus cornifex.)<BR>	 2. A small centipede.<BR> E. कर्ण the ear, and<BR>कीट an insect, being supposed to attack the ear especially.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=160-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णक्ष्वेड|कर्णक्ष्वेडः|कर्ण्णक्ष्वेड
कर्णक्ष्वेड m. (-डः) An affection of the ear, a roaring or constant noise<BR>in it.<BR> E. कर्ण, and क्ष्वेड a buzzing in the ear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=160-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णग
कर्णग mfn. (-गः-गा-गं)<BR>	 1. Hanging on the ear, next to the ear.<BR>	 2. Ex-<BR>tending to the ear.<BR> E. कर्ण, and ग what goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=160-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णगूथ|कर्णगूथं|कर्णगूथः
कर्णगूथ m. (-थः) The wax of the ear.<BR> E. कर्ण, and गूथ fœces, excrement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=160-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णगोचर
कर्णगोचर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Capable of being heard, perceptible to the ear.<BR>E. कर्ण, and गोचर perceptible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=160-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णग्राह|कर्णग्राहः
कर्णग्राह m. (-हः) A helmsman.<BR> E. कर्ण, the helm, and ग्राह who holds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=160-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णग्राहवत्|कर्णग्राहवन्त्
कर्णग्राहवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Having a helmsman.<BR> E. कर्णग्राह and<BR>मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=160-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णच्छिद्र|कर्णछिद्र
कर्णच्छिद्र n. (-द्रं) The outer auditory passage.<BR> E. कर्ण, and छिद्र hole.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=160-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णजप|कर्णजपः
कर्णजप m. (-पः) An informer.<BR> E. कर्ण, and जप who whispers; also<BR>कर्णेजप.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=160-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णजलूका
कर्णजलूका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. An insect, (Julus.)<BR>	 2. A small centipede: see<BR>कर्णकीटी.<BR> E. कर्ण, and जलूका a leech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=160-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णजलौकस्
कर्णजलौकस् f. (-का) A worm: see the preceding; also कर्णजलौका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=160-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णजलौका
कर्णजलौका f. (-काः) A kind of insect, (Julus cornifex, &c.)<BR>	 2. A small<BR>centipede; also कर्णजलौकस् and कर्णजलूका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=160-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णजाह|कर्णजाहं|कर्ण्णजाह
कर्णजाह n. (-हं) The root of the ear.<BR> E. कर्ण, and जाह affix in this<BR>sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=160-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णजित्
कर्णजित् m. (-जित्) A title of ARJUNA.<BR> E. कर्ण, and जित् conqueror;<BR>KARṆA having taken the part of the KURUS, was killed by<BR>ARJUNA in the great battle between them and the Pandus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=160-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णताल|कर्णतालः|कर्ण्णताल
कर्णताल m. (-लः) The flapping of an elephant's ears.<BR> E. कर्ण, and ताल<BR>tune.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=160-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णदर्पण|कर्णदर्पणः|कर्ण्णदर्पण
कर्णदर्पण m. (-णः) An ear-ring, an ornament of the ear.<BR> E. कर्ण, and<BR>दर्पण a mirror.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=160-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णदुन्दुभि|कर्णदुन्दुभिः|कर्ण्णदुन्दुभि
कर्णदुन्दुभि f. (-भिः) A kind of worm: see कर्णकीटी.<BR> E. कर्ण, and दुन्दुभि a<BR>sort of drum; making a noise in the ear like a drum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=160-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णधार|कर्णधारः|कर्ण्णधार
कर्णधार m. (-रः) A pilot, a helmsman.<BR> E. कर्ण the helm, धृञ् to have or.<BR>hold, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=160-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णनाद|कर्ण्णनाद
कर्णनाद m. (-दः) Ringing in the ear.<BR> E. कर्ण, and नाद sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=160-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णन्दु
कर्णन्दु f. (-न्दुः) A woman's ear-ring: see कर्णान्दु and कर्णेन्दु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=160-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णपाक|कर्णपाकः|कर्ण्णपाक
कर्णपाक m. (-कः) Inflamation of the outer ear.<BR> E. कर्ण, and पाक ripening.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=160-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णपाली|कर्ण्णपाली
कर्णपाली f. (-ली) An ornament of the ear, a garland or string of jewels<BR>pendent from it.<BR> E. कर्ण, and पाल् to cherish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=160-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णपुर|कर्ण्णपुर
कर्णपुर m. (-रः) The capital of KARṆA, the ancient name of Bhagalpur.<BR>E. कर्ण, and पुर city; also कर्णपुर् f. (-पूः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=160-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णपूर|कर्णपूरः|कर्ण्णपूर
कर्णपूर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A tree, (Mimosa sirisha.)<BR>	 2. The blue lotus.<BR>	 3. An<BR>ear-ring.<BR>	 4. The Asoka tree.<BR> E. कर्ण. and पूर to make full, to<BR>complete.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=160-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णपूरक|कर्णपूरकः|कर्ण्णपूरक
कर्णपूरक m. (-कः) The Kadamba tree, (Nauclea kadamba.)<BR> E. कर्णपूर<BR>an ear-ring, and कन् resembling, like the large round drop or<BR>pendant of a Hindustani ear-ring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=160-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णप्रतिनाह|कर्णप्रतिनाहः|कर्ण्णप्रतिनाह
कर्णप्रतिनाह m. (-हः) A disease of the ear, suppression of the excretion<BR>or wax, which is supposed to have dissolved and pass by the nose<BR>and mouth.<BR> E. कर्ण, and प्रतिनाह suppression.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=160-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णफल|कर्णफलः|कर्ण्णफल
कर्णफल m. (-लः) A sort of fish, (Ophiocephalus kurrawey.)<BR> E. कर्ण, and<BR>फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=160-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णमद्गुर
कर्णमद्गुर m. (-रः) A sort of sheat fish, (Silurus unitus.)<BR> E. कर्ण, and मद्गुर<BR>a sheat fish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=160-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णमल|कर्णमलं|कर्ण्णमल
कर्णमल m. (-लः) The excretion or wax of the ear.<BR> E. कर्ण, and मल dirt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=160-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णमुकुर|कर्णमुकुरः
कर्णमुकुर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. An ornament of the ear.<BR>	 2. An ear-ring.<BR> E. कर्ण,<BR>and मुकुर a mirror; reflecting its beauty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=160-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णमोटी|कर्ण्णमोटी
कर्णमोटी f. (-टी) A name of DEVI or DURGĀ in one of her forms or in-<BR>carnations<BR> E. कर्ण the ear, मुट् to rub, घञ् and ङीप् affixes; this<BR>is sometimes written कर्णमोटि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=160-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णलतिका
कर्णलतिका f. (-का) The lobe of the ear.<BR> E. कर्ण, लता a creeping plant,<BR>कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=160-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णवंश|कर्णवंशः|कर्ण्णवंश
कर्णवंश m. (-शः) An elevated platform.<BR> E. कर्ण, and वंश a bamboo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=160-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णवत्|कर्णवन्त्
कर्णवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>	 1. Having ears.<BR>	 2. Long-eared.<BR>	 3. Having a<BR>helm.<BR> E. कर्ण and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=160-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णवर्जित|कर्णवर्जितः|कर्णवर्ज्जितः|कर्ण्णवर्ज्जित
कर्णवर्जित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Earless.<BR>	 m. (-तः) A snake.<BR> E. कर्ण, and वर्जित्<BR>deprived.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=160-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णविद्रधि
कर्णविद्रधि f. (-धिः) Ulceration of the ear.<BR> E. कर्ण, and विद्रधि a sore.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=161-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णवेध|कर्णवेधः|कर्ण्णवेध
कर्णवेध m. (-धः)<BR>	 1. Boaring the ears: as a religious ceremony it is per-<BR>formed where there are three sons, to prevent one of them from<BR>dying.<BR>	 2. Piercing the ear in general.<BR> E. कर्ण, and वेध piercing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=161-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णवेधनिका
कर्णवेधनिका f. (-का) An instrument for perforating the ear.<BR> E. कर्ण, विध्<BR>to pierce, ल्युट् and ङीष् affixes, with कन् added, and the fem. termina-<BR>tion टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=161-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णवेधनी
कर्णवेधनी f. (-नी) See the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=161-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णवेष्टक|कर्णवेष्टकं
कर्णवेष्टक n. (-कं) An ear-ring: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=161-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णवेष्टन|कर्णवेष्टनं
कर्णवेष्टन n. (-नं) An ear-ring.<BR> E. कर्ण, and वेष्टन surrounding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=161-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णशष्कुली|कर्ण्णशष्कुली
कर्णशष्कुली f. (-ली) The outer part of the ear, the cartilage and depres-<BR>sions leading to the auditory passage.<BR> E. कर्ण, and शष्कुल the hol-<BR>lows of the ear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=161-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णशूल|कर्णशूलः|कर्ण्णशूल
कर्णशूल n. (-लं) Ear-ache.<BR> E. कर्ण, and शूल pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=161-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णश्रव|कर्ण्णश्रव
कर्णश्रव mfn. (-वः-वा-वं) Audible, loud.<BR> E. कर्ण, and श्रव hearing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=161-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णसंस्राव|कर्णसंस्रावः|कर्ण्णसंस्राव
कर्णसंस्राव m. (-वः) Discharge of pus from the ear.<BR> E. कर्ण, and संस्राव<BR>suppuration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=161-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णस्राव
कर्णस्राव m. (-वः) Discharge of ichorous matter from the ear.<BR> E. कर्ण,<BR>and स्राव running.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=161-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णस्फोटा|कर्ण्णस्फोटा
कर्णस्फोटा f. (-टा) A sort of creeper.<BR> E. कर्ण, and स्फोट a boil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=161-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णाट|कर्णाटः
कर्णाट m. (-टः) A country, Karṇāṭa, whence the modern Karnatic: the<BR>name however was anciently applied to the central districts of the<BR>peninsula, including Mysur.<BR>	 f. (-टी)<BR>	 1. One of the Rāgiṇīs or fe-<BR>male personification of the musical modes, the bride of the Rāga<BR>MĀLAVA.<BR>	 2. A plant.<BR> E. कर्ण the ear, a prince, &c. and अट् to go,<BR>affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=161-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णानुज|कर्णानुजः
कर्णानुज m. (-जः) A name of Yudhiṣṭhira, the elder brother of the<BR>five Pandu princes.<BR> E. कर्ण, and अनुज younger born; the younger<BR>brother of KARṆA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=161-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णान्तिक|कर्णांतिक
कर्णान्तिक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Near or close to the ear.<BR> E. कर्ण, and अन्तिक<BR>near.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=161-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णान्दु|कर्णांदु|कर्णान्दुः
कर्णान्दु f. (-न्दुः)<BR>	 1. An ornament of the ear.<BR>	 2. An ear-ring: see the next,<BR>and कर्णेन्दु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=161-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णान्दू|कर्णांदू
कर्णान्दू f. (-न्दूः) An ornament of the ear, an ear-ring, &c.<BR> E. कर्ण, and अन्दू<BR>a chain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=161-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णारा
कर्णारा f. (-रा) An instrument for perforating the ear.<BR> E. कर्ण the ear, ऋ<BR>to go, अच् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=161-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णारि|कर्णारिः
कर्णारि m. (-रिः) A name of ARJUNA.<BR> E. कर्ण, and अरि an enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=161-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णालङ्कार|कर्णालंकार
कर्णालङ्कार m. (-रः) An ear-ring, an ornament of the ear.<BR> E. कर्ण, and<BR>अलङ्कार ornament; also कर्णालङ्क्रिया, कर्णालङ्कृति, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=161-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णास्फाल|कर्णास्फालः
कर्णास्फाल m. (-लः) The flapping of an elephant's ear.<BR> E. कर्ण, and आस्फाल<BR>with the same import.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=161-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णिक|कर्णिकः
कर्णिक mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>	 1. Having large or long ears.<BR>	 2. Having ears.<BR>3. Having a helm.<BR>	 m. (-कः) A steersman.<BR>	 f. (-का)<BR>	 1. An ear-ring or<BR>ornament of the ear.<BR>	 2. The pericarp of a lotus.<BR>	 3. The middle<BR>finger.<BR>	 4. The tip of an elephant's trunk.<BR>	 5. A fruit-stalk.<BR>	 6. A pen<BR>or small brush.<BR>	 7. A plant, (Premna spinosa, &c.) see अग्निमन्थ. E.<BR>कर्ण the ear, &c. इक affix; or कन् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=161-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णिकाचल|कर्णिकाचलः|कर्ण्णिकाचल
कर्णिकाचल m. (-लः) The fabulous mountain Sumeru.<BR> E. कर्णिका the seed<BR>vessel of a lotus, and अचल a mountain, Meru being in the centre of<BR>the world, the divisions of which are delineated as the leaves of a<BR>lotus; also other compounds, as कर्णिकाद्रि, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=161-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णिकार|कर्णिकारः|कर्ण्णिकार
कर्णिकार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. The name of a tree, commonly Kaniyar, (Pteros-<BR>permum acerifolium.)<BR>	 2. A sort of Cassia, (Cassia fistula.)<BR>	 3. The<BR>pericarp of a lotus.<BR> E. कर्णिका an ornament of the ear, ऋ to go, अण्<BR>affix; also with कन् added कर्णिकारक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=161-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णिकिन्
कर्णिकिन् m. (-की) An elephant.<BR> E. कर्णिका the tip of his trunk, and<BR>इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=161-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णिन्
कर्णिन् mfn. (-र्णी-र्णिनी-र्णि)<BR>	 1. Having an ear, relating to the ear, &c.<BR>	 2.<BR>Long-eared.<BR>	 3. Barbed, (as an arrow.)<BR>	 4. Having a helm.<BR>	 m. (-र्णनी)<BR>	 1.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=161-b" target="_blank">Page161-b+ 60</a>]<BR>The name of a mountain, one of the seven principal ranges of the<BR>mountains, dividing the universe.<BR>	 2. The neck, the part near the<BR>ear.<BR>	 3. A steersman.<BR>	 f. (-र्णिनी) A disease of the uterus, prolapsus<BR>or polypus uteri.<BR> E. कर्ण, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=161-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णिल
कर्णिल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Long-eared.<BR> E. कर्ण, and इलच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=161-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णीरथ|कर्णीरथः|कर्ण्णीरथ
कर्णीरथ mf. (-थः-था) A covered car, or according to some, a litter for the<BR>conveyance of woman, &c. borne on men's shoulders.<BR> E. कर्णी the<BR>part near the ear, and रथ a carriage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=161-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णीसुत|कर्णीसुतः|कर्ण्णीसुत
कर्णीसुत m. (-तः) A name of KANSA the enemy of KṚṢṆA.<BR> E. कर्णी the<BR>mother of this prince, and सुत a son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=161-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णेजप|कर्णेजपः
कर्णेजप mfn. (-पः-पा-पं) An informer, a tale-bearer.<BR> E. कर्णे in the ear,<BR>and जप् to recite in a low voice, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=161-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णेन्दु|कर्णेन्दुः|कर्ण्णेन्दु
कर्णेन्दु f. (-न्दुः)<BR>	 1. A semicircular ornament of the ear.<BR>	 2. An ear-ring. E.<BR>कर्ण, and इन्दु the moon, a crescent, &c. see कर्णान्दु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=161-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्त्त|कर्त|कर्तः|कर्त्तः
कर्त्त r. 10th. cl. (कर्त्तयति) To slacken or unloose, to remove; also कत्र<BR>and कर्त्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=161-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्त्तन|कर्तन|कर्त्तनं
कर्त्तन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Cutting, cutting off or in pieces.<BR>	 2. Spinning cotton or<BR>thread.<BR>	 f. (-नी) Scissors.<BR> E. कृत् to cut, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=161-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्त्तरिका|कर्तरिका
कर्त्तरिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. A knife.<BR>	 2. A small sword or cutlass.<BR>	 3. A hunter's<BR>knife or sword, a couteau de chasse.<BR>	 4. A scissors.<BR> E. कर्त्तरी, and<BR>कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=161-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्त्तरी|कर्तरी
कर्त्तरी f. (-री)<BR>	 1. A scissors or shears.<BR>	 2. A knife.<BR>	 3. A small sword or<BR>cutlass.<BR> E. कृत् to cut, अरन् affix, and ङीप् fem. do.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=161-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्त्तव्य|कर्तव्य|कर्त्तव्यं|कर्त्तव्यः
कर्त्तव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>	 1. To be done or made.<BR>	 2. What ought to be<BR>done.<BR> E. कृ to make, तव्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=161-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्त्तव्यता|कर्तव्यता
कर्त्तव्यता f. (-ता) Necessity, obligation, propriety, fitness.<BR> E. कर्त्तव्य, and<BR>तल् affix; also with त्व affix कर्त्तव्यत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=161-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्त्तित|कर्तित
कर्त्तित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Cut, cut off.<BR> E. कृत् to cut, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=161-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्त्तिष्यत्|कर्तिष्यत्
कर्त्तिष्यत् mfn. (-ष्यन्-ष्यन्ती-ष्यत्) Intending or wishing to cut.<BR> E. कृत् to<BR>cut, शतृ affix to future participle; also कर्त्तिष्यमाण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>with शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=161-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्त्तुकाम|कर्तुकाम
कर्त्तुकाम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं) Desirous or intending to do.<BR> E. कर्त्तुम् to do, काम<BR>desire, the final of the first rejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=161-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्त्तृ|कर्तृ
कर्त्तृ mfn. (-र्त्ता-र्त्त्री-र्त्तृ)<BR>	 1. An agent, a doer, a maker, one who makes or<BR>does.<BR>	 2. One who practises what he knows.<BR>	 m. (-र्त्ता)<BR>	 1. A name of<BR>BRAHMĀ.<BR>	 2. (In grammar,) The active noun, the nominative case.<BR>E. कृ to do, and तृच् affix: it may also be read कर्तृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=161-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्त्तृक|कर्तृक
कर्त्तृक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) An agent, one who does anything.<BR> E. कन् added<BR>to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=161-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्त्तृकत्व|कर्तृकत्व
कर्त्तृकत्व n. (-त्वं) Agency, action.<BR> E. कर्त्तृक, and त्व aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=161-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्त्तृका|कर्तृका
कर्त्तृका f. (-का) A small sword.<BR> E. कृत् to cut, कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=161-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्त्तृत्व|कर्तृत्व|कर्तृत्वं
कर्त्तृत्व n. (-त्वं) Agency, the act or property of an agent.<BR> E. कर्त्तृ, and त्व<BR>affix; also with तल् affix कर्त्तृता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=161-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्त्तृवाच्य|कर्तृवाच्य|कर्तृवाच्यः
कर्त्तृवाच्य m. (-च्यः) (In grammar,) The active voice.<BR> E. कर्त्तृ agent, and<BR>वाच्य to be said.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=161-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्त्र|कर्त्रं
कर्त्र r. 10th cl. (कर्त्रयति) To unloose, to remove: see कर्त्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=161-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्त्री
कर्त्री f. (-र्त्री) A scissors.<BR> E. कृत् to cut, तृच् and ङीष् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=161-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्द|कर्दः|कर्द्द|कर्द्दः
कर्द r. 1st cl. (कर्दति) To grumble, as the bowels; to caw as a crow; or<BR>to make any such noise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=161-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्द|कर्दः|कर्द्द|कर्द्दः
कर्द m. (-र्दः) Mud, clay.<BR> E. कर्द् to sound ill, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=161-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्दट|कर्दटः|कर्द्दट|कर्द्दटः
कर्दट m. (-टः)<BR>	 1. The fibrous root of the lotus.<BR>	 2. Mud, dirt.<BR>	 3. Any<BR>aquatic weed, as Vallisneria, &c.<BR> E. कर्द mud, and अट what goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=161-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्दन|कर्दनं|कर्द्दन|कर्द्दनं
कर्दन n. (-नं) Grumbling of the bowels, borborygmi.<BR> E. कर्द् to make<BR>such noise, and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=161-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्दम|कर्दमः|कर्द्दम|कर्द्दमं|कर्द्दमः
कर्दम m. (-मः)<BR>	 1. Mud, mire, clay.<BR>	 2. Sin.<BR>	 3. A Prajāpati, the son of<BR>BRAHMĀ by CHĀYĀ, and the father of Kapila: (this personage<BR>appears to be an innovation in Hindu mythology.)<BR>	 f. (-मी) A plant.<BR>n. (-मं) Flesh.<BR> E. कर्द् to sound badly, and अम Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=161-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्दमाटक|कर्दमाटकः|कर्द्दमाटक|कर्द्दमाटकः
कर्दमाटक m. (-कः) A receptacle for filth, a sewer, a necessary.<BR> E. कर्दम<BR>filth, अट to go, and वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=161-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्पट|कर्पटं|कर्पटः
कर्पट m. (-टः) Old and patched or ragged garments.<BR> E. कृप् to be able,<BR>and अटन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=162-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्पटधारिन्
कर्पटधारिन् m. (-री) A religious mendicant, a Fakir, a beggar in patched<BR>or ragged clothes, or sometimes with merely a cloth to cover the<BR>privities.<BR> E. कर्पट as above, धृ to have, and णिनि affix; also कर्पटिक<BR>and कर्पटिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=162-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्पटिक|कर्पटिकः|कर्प्पटिक
कर्पटिक m. (-कः) See the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=162-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्पटिन्
कर्पटिन् m. (-टी) See कर्पटधारिन्. This and the two preceding words may<BR>also be used in three genders, meaning, beggar in general, or any<BR>one in beggarly raiment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=162-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्पर|कर्परः
कर्पर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. The skull, the cranium.<BR>	 2. An iron saucepan or frying<BR>pan.<BR>	 3. A kind of weapon.<BR>	 4. The Glomerous fig tree: see उडुम्बर.<BR>f. (-री) A collyrium extracted from the Amomum anthorhiza, Rox.<BR>E. कृप् to be able, अरन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=162-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्पराल|कर्परालः
कर्पराल m. (-लः) A tree, described as a Pilu growing in the hills. E.<BR>कर्पर the skull, &c. and अल् to adorn, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=162-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्पराश
कर्पराश m. (-शः) Sand, gravel, a sandy soil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=162-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्परिकातुत्थ|कर्परिकातुत्थं
कर्परिकातुत्थ n. (-त्थं) A collyrium extracted from the Amomum author-<BR>hiza: see कर्परा.<BR> E. कर्परिका for कर्परी, and तुत्थ any collyrium.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=162-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्पास|कर्पासं|कर्पासः
कर्पास mn. (-सः-सं) Cotton.<BR>	 f. (-सी) The cotton tree; also कार्पासी.<BR> E. कृ<BR>to do, &c. पास Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=162-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्पूर|कर्पूरं|कर्पूरः
कर्पूर mn. (-रः-रं) Camphor.<BR> E. कृप् to be able, ऊर Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=162-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्पूरक|कर्पूरकः
कर्पूरक m. (-कः) Zedoary, (Curcuma zerumbet, Rox.) See कर्पूरक and<BR>कर्चूरक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=162-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्पूरतिलका
कर्पूरतिलका f. (-का) One of DURGĀ'S female attendants or confidantes;<BR>see जया.<BR> E. कर्पूर camphor, and तिलक the sectarial spot on the fore-<BR>head; having the Tilaka of camphor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=162-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्पूरतैल|कर्पूरतैलं|कर्प्पूरतैल
कर्पूरतैल n. (-लं) Camphor-liniment.<BR> E. कर्पूर, and तैल oil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=162-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्पूरनालिका|कर्प्पूरनालिका
कर्पूरनालिका f. (-का) Rice dressed with spices, camphor and ghee.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=162-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्पूरमणि|कर्पूरमणिः|कर्प्पूरमणि
कर्पूरमणि m. (-णिः) A white mineral used medicinally.<BR> E. कर्पूर, and<BR>मणि a gem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=162-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्फर|कर्फरः
कर्फर m. (-रः) A mirror.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=162-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्ब|कर्ब्ब
कर्ब r. 1st cl. (कर्बति) To go, to move or approach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=162-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्बर
कर्बर m. (-रः) See कर्वर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=162-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्बुदार|कर्ब्बुदारः
कर्बुदार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Mountain ebony: see कोबिदार.<BR>	 2. Blue barleria: see नीलझिण्टी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=162-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्बुर|कर्बुरः|कर्ब्बुरं|कर्ब्बुरः
कर्बुर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Variegated, of a spotted or variegated colour.<BR>	 f.<BR>(-रा)<BR>	 1. Trumpet flower, (Bignonia suave-olens.)<BR>	 2. A sort of basil,<BR>(Ocymum gratissimum:) see वर्वरी.<BR>	 f. (-री) A name of the goddess<BR>DURGĀ.<BR>	 n. (-रं)<BR>	 1. Gold.<BR>	 2. Water.<BR>	 3. Datura, (the fruit.)<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A demon, an imp or goblin.<BR>	 2. A variegated<BR>colour.<BR>	 3. A plant, (Curcuma reclinata, Rox.) See शठी.<BR>	 4. Sin.<BR>	 5.<BR>Rice growing amidst inundation.<BR> E. कब to tinge or dye, उरच्<BR>Uṇādi affix and र inserted, or कर्ब to go, &c. and उरन् affix, also<BR>long कर्बूर; it is also often read with the dental व, but perhaps<BR>erroneously.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=162-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्बूर|कर्बूरः|कर्ब्बूरं|कर्ब्बूरः
कर्बूर mn. (-रः-रं) Gold.<BR>	 m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A species of curcuma, (C. reclinata,<BR>Rox.)<BR>	 2. Zedoary, (Curcuma zerumbet.)<BR>	 3. A demon.<BR>	 f. (-रा) A<BR>leech.<BR>	 n. (-रं) Yellow orpiment. See कर्बुर and कर्बूरक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=162-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्बूरक|कर्ब्बूरकः
कर्बूरक m. (-कः) Zedoary, (Curcuma zerumbet, Rox.)<BR> E. कन् added to<BR>the preceding: also कर्चूरक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=162-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्बूरित|कर्ब्बूरित
कर्बूरित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Variegated, many coloured.<BR> E. कर्बूर, and इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=162-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्म|कर्म
कर्म्म mn. (-र्म्मः-र्म्मं) Act, action; see कर्म्मन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=162-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मकर|कर्मकर|कर्मकरः|कर्म्मकरः
कर्म्मकर mfn. (-रः-रा-री-रं)<BR>	 1. A hired laborer.<BR>	 2. A servant of any kind,<BR>(as a pupil, &c.) not a slave.<BR>	 3. An agent, any one who does work or<BR>business.<BR>	 m. (-रः) A name of YAMA, regent of the dead.<BR>	 f. (-री)<BR>	 1.<BR>A plant, (Aletris hyacinthoides.) See मूर्ब्बा.<BR>	 2. Bryonia grandis: see<BR>निम्बिका.<BR>	 3. A female servant or slave.<BR> E. कर्म्म work, act, and कर who<BR>does or performs; also कर्म्मकार.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=162-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मकार|कर्मकार|कर्मकारः|कर्म्मकारः
कर्म्मकार mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>	 1. A worker, one who does any business, an<BR>artisan, a mechanic.<BR>	 2. One who performs any act.<BR>	 m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=162-b" target="_blank">Page162-b+ 60</a>]<BR>blacksmith, one of the progeny of the divine artist VISWAKARMA.<BR>2. A bull.<BR> E. कर्म्म an act, कृञ् to perform, affix अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=162-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मकारक|कर्मकारक
कर्म्मकारक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) One who does any work, one who performs<BR>any act.<BR> E. कर्म्म, and कारक who does.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=162-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मकारिन्|कर्मकारिन्
कर्म्मकारिन् mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि) Working, doing any work, who performs<BR>any act.<BR> E. कर्म्म, and कारिन् who does.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=162-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मकार्म्मुक|कर्मकार्मुक|कर्मकार्मुकः
कर्म्मकार्म्मुक m. (-कः) A strong bow.<BR> E. कर्म्म used to action, कार्म्मुक a bow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=162-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मकीलक|कर्मकीलक|कर्मकीलकः|कर्म्मकीलकः
कर्म्मकीलक m. (-कः) A washerman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=162-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मकृत्|कर्मकृत्
कर्म्मकृत् mfn. (-कृत्)<BR>	 1. Having done work.<BR>	 2. A workman, an artisan. E.<BR>कर्म्म, and कृत् who does.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=162-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मकृतवत्|कर्मकृतवत्
कर्म्मकृतवत् m. (-वान्) The director of a religious rite, the reciter of the<BR>Mantras or formula.<BR> E. कर्म्म, and कृतवत् doing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=162-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मक्षम|कर्मक्षम|कर्म्मक्षमः
कर्म्मक्षम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं) Competent to an act.<BR> E. कर्म्म, and क्षम to be<BR>patient, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=162-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मचेष्टा|कर्मचेष्टा
कर्म्मचेष्टा f. (-ष्टा) Active exertion, action.<BR> E. कर्म्म, and चेष्टा effort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=162-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मचोदना|कर्मचोदना
कर्म्मचोदना f. (-ना) The object of acts, the inducement to ritual acts, or<BR>the combination of knowledge, the thing to be known, and the<BR>person who acquires knowledge.<BR> E. कर्म्म, and चोदना impelling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=162-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मज|कर्मज|कर्मजः|कर्म्मजः
कर्म्मज mfn. (-जः-जा-जं) Resulting from or produced by any act, especi-<BR>ally religious or moral, or unrighteous or immoral actions.<BR>	 m. (-जः)<BR>The Kali-yug or fourth and present age of the world, the age of<BR>iniquity.<BR>	 2. The holy fig tree, (Ficus religiosa.)<BR> E. कर्म्म, and ज<BR>produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=162-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मजगुण|कर्मजगुण|कर्म्मजगुणः
कर्म्मजगुण m. (-णः) A predicate or property resulting from human acts,<BR>as separation, reunion, &c.<BR> E. कर्म्मज, and गुण quality.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=162-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मज्ञ|कर्मज्ञ
कर्म्मज्ञ mfn. (-ज्ञः-ज्ञा-ज्ञं)<BR>	 1. Skilled in any work.<BR>	 2. Acquainted with reli-<BR>gious rites.<BR> E. कर्म्म, and ज्ञ who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=162-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मठ|कर्मठ|कर्मठः|कर्म्मठः
कर्म्मठ mfn. (-ठः-ठा-ठं)<BR>	 1. Finishing carefully.<BR>	 2. Accomplishing any<BR>rite.<BR>	 m. (-ठः) The director and performer of a sacrifice.<BR> E. कर्म्म,<BR>and ठच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=162-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मणिवाच्य
कर्म्मणिवाच्य m. (-च्यः) The passive voice, (in grammar.)<BR> E. कर्म्मणि in the<BR>act or object, and वाच्य to be said.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=162-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मण्य|कर्मण्य|कर्म्मण्यः
कर्म्मण्य mfn. (-ण्यः-ण्या-ण्यं) Proper to any act, suitable to or fit for it.<BR>	 f.<BR>(-ण्या) Wages, hire.<BR>	 n. (-ण्यं) Energy, activity.<BR> E. कर्म्मन्, and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=162-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मण्यभुज्|कर्मण्यभुज्
कर्म्मण्यभुज् mfn. (-भुक्) Working for hire.<BR> E. कर्म्मण्य wages, and भुज् to<BR>eat, affix क्विप्ः see भरण्यभुज्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=162-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मत्याग|कर्मत्याग|कर्मत्यागः
कर्म्मत्याग m. (-गः) Abandonment of worldly duties or ceremonial rites.<BR>E. कर्म्म, and त्याग abandonment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=162-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मत्व|कर्मत्व
कर्म्मत्व n. (-त्वं)<BR>	 1. Act, action, the active discharge of the duties and<BR>functions of life.<BR>	 2. Any act.<BR> E. कर्म्म, and त्व affix; also with तल्,<BR>कर्म्मता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=162-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मदुष्ट|कर्मदुष्ट
कर्म्मदुष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्ट) Following wicked or degrading practices<BR>immoral, disreputable.<BR> E. कर्म्म, and दुष्ट defiled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=162-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मदोष|कर्मदोष|कर्मदोषः
कर्म्मदोष m. (-षः)<BR>	 1. Error, blunder.<BR>	 2. Sin, vice.<BR>	 3. The evil consequence<BR>of human acts.<BR>	 4. Discreditable conduct or business.<BR> E. कर्म्म, and<BR>दोष fault.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=162-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मध्वंस|कर्मध्वंस|कर्मध्वंसः
कर्म्मध्वंस m. (-सः)<BR>	 1. Loss of benefits arising from religious acts.<BR>	 2. De-<BR>struction of any work.<BR>	 3. Disappointment.<BR> E. कर्म्म, and ध्वंस loss.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=162-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मन्|कर्मन्
कर्म्मन् mn. (-र्म्मा-र्म्म)<BR>	 1. Action in general.<BR>	 2. The object of an action.<BR>3. The subject of action in grammar, considered of three kinds,<BR>प्राप्य or व्याप्य when it is simple, as ग्रामं गच्छति he goes to the village;<BR>सूर्य्यं पश्यति he sees the sun; विकार्य्य when change of form is implied,<BR>as सुवर्णं कुण्डलं करोति gold forms the ear-ring; and निर्वर्त्य when<BR>some new product is evolved, as कटं करोति he makes a mat; पुत्रं<BR>प्रसूते she bears a son.<BR>	 4. The objective noun.<BR>	 5. Action specific,<BR>moral duty, the obligation imposed by peculiarities of tribe,<BR>occupation, &c.<BR>	 6. Natural, active property, as maturity, of heat;<BR>support, of earth; dispersion, of wind, &c.<BR>	 7. Religious action, as<BR>sacrifice, ablution, &c. especially as originating in the hope of<BR>future recompense, and as opposed to speculative religion or<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=163-a" target="_blank">Page163-a+ 60</a>]<BR>knowledge of spirit.<BR>	 8. (In Logic.) Substantial action or motion of<BR>five kinds, upwards, downwards, extension, contraction, and going<BR>in general.<BR>	 9. Action or act involving retribution or reward, virtue,<BR>vice, &c.<BR>	 10. Fate, the certain consequence of previous acts.<BR> E. कृञ्<BR>to do, मनिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=162-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मनिष्ठ|कर्मनिष्ठ
कर्म्मनिष्ठ mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठा-ष्ठं) Engaged in active duties.<BR>	 m. (-ष्ठः) A Brahman<BR>who performs sacrifices, &c.<BR> E. कर्म्म, and निष्ठ who stays in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=163-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मन्दिन्|कर्मन्दिन्|कर्मंदिन्
कर्म्मन्दिन् m. (-न्दी) The beggar, the religious mendicant, the member of<BR>the fourth order; see आश्रम, &c.<BR> E. कर्म्म work, अन्द to abandon, or<BR>कर्म्मन्द the name of a saint, the founder of the sect, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=163-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मफल|कर्मफल|कर्म्मफलं
कर्म्मफल n. (-लं)<BR>	 1. Pain, pleasure, &c. considered as the consequence or<BR>fruit of human actions.<BR>	 2. The name of a fruit; see कर्म्मरङ्ग.<BR> E. कर्म्म,<BR>and फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=163-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मफलोदय|कर्मफलोदय
कर्म्मफलोदय m. (-यः) The occurrence of consequences.<BR> E. कर्म्मफल, and<BR>उदय rising.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=163-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मबन्धन|कर्मबन्धन|कर्मबंधन
कर्म्मबन्धन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Bound by acts.<BR>	 n. (-नं) Confinement to repeated<BR>existence, as the consequence of acts.<BR> E. कर्म्म, and बन्धन binding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=163-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मभू|कर्मभू
कर्म्मभू f. (-भूः) Tilled or cultivated ground.<BR> E. कर्म्म, and भू earth, ground,<BR>&c. it may also mean the same as the next word.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=163-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मभूमि|कर्मभूमि|कर्मभूमिः|कर्म्मभूमिः
कर्म्मभूमि f. (-मिः) Āryāvarta or the central part of India, Bharata<BR>Varṣa, the whole of India, or any similar place considered as holy<BR>land.<BR> E. कर्म्म, and भूमि earth: where men perform the ceremonies<BR>of the Hindu faith.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=163-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्ममूल|कर्ममूल|कर्म्ममूलं
कर्म्ममूल n. (-लं) Kusa or sacrificial grass, see कुश.<BR> E. कर्म्म, and मूल a root:<BR>it being used in many religious and essential Karmas or sacred<BR>rites.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=163-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मयुग|कर्मयुग|कर्म्मयुगं
कर्म्मयुग m. (-गः) The fourth and present age of the world, the iron<BR>age, the Kali-yug: see कलि, and above, कर्म्मज.<BR> E. कर्म्म, and युग a<BR>Yuga or age.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=163-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मयोग|कर्मयोग|कर्मयोगः|कर्म्मयोगः
कर्म्मयोग m. (-गः)<BR>	 1. Performance of worldly functions or duties.<BR>	 2. The<BR>same, considered as equivalent to a religious duty.<BR>	 3. Active<BR>exertion, industry.<BR> E. कर्म्म, and योग union or observances.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=163-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मरङ्ग|कर्मरङ्ग|कर्म्मरङ्गः
कर्म्मरङ्ग n. (-ङ्गं) A plant bearing an acid fruit, (Averrhoa carambola.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=163-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मरी|कर्मरी
कर्म्मरी f. (-री) The manna of the bamboo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=163-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मवज्र|कर्मवज्र|कर्मवज्रः|कर्म्मवज्रः
कर्म्मवज्र m. (-ज्रः) A Śūdra.<BR> E. कर्म्म, and वज्र the thunderbolt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=163-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मवश|कर्मवश|कर्मवशः
कर्म्मवश m. (-शः)<BR>	 1. The necessary influence of acts.<BR>	 2. Fate, considered<BR>as the inevitable consequence of actions done in a former life. E.<BR>कर्म्म, and वश subjection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=163-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मवाटी|कर्मवाटी
कर्म्मवाटी f. (-टी) A lunar day, or the 30th division of a lunar month. E.<BR>कर्म्म, and वाटी a road, &c. regulating all ceremonies and observ-<BR>ances, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=163-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मविघ्न|कर्मविघ्न
कर्म्मविघ्न m. (-घ्नः)<BR>	 1. Impediment, obstruction.<BR> E. कर्म्म, and विघ्न hindrance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=163-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मविधि|कर्मविधि
कर्म्मविधि f. (-धिः)<BR>	 1. Rule of action, observance, practice.<BR>	 2. Mode of<BR>conducting any ceremony.<BR> E. कर्म्म, and विधि precept; also कर्म्मविधान.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=163-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मविपर्य्यय|कर्मविपर्यय
कर्म्मविपर्य्यय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. Succession of office or employment, revolving or<BR>alternating duty.<BR>	 2. Contrariety or reverse of any act or business.<BR>E. कर्म्म, and विपर्य्यय contrariety.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=163-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मविपाक|कर्मविपाक|कर्म्मविपाकः
कर्म्मविपाक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. Future reward or punishment, the consequence<BR>of human acts in a subsequent birth.<BR>	 2. A work on this subject,<BR>explaining expiatory rites to be performed in cases of disease, &c.<BR>supposed to be the punishment of offences in a previous existence.<BR>E. कर्म्म, and विपाक maturity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=163-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मविशेष|कर्मविशेष
कर्म्मविशेष m. (-षः) Variety of act or actions.<BR> E. कर्म्म, and विशेष difference.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=163-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मशील|कर्मशील|कर्म्मशीलः
कर्म्मशील mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>	 1. Assiduous, laborious.<BR>	 2. One who perseveres<BR>in his duties without looking forward to their reward.<BR> E. कर्म्म, and<BR>शील attached.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=163-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मशुद्ध|कर्मशुद्ध
कर्म्मशुद्ध n. (-द्धं) Approved occupation.<BR> E. कर्म्म, and शुद्ध pure, correct.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=163-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मशूर|कर्मशूर|कर्म्मशूरः
कर्म्मशूर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Assiduous, laborious.<BR> E. कर्म्म, and शूर dexterous,<BR>able.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=163-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मशौच|कर्मशौच
कर्म्मशौच n. (-चं) Humility.<BR> E. कर्म्म, and शौच purity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=163-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मसंग्रह|कर्मसङ्ग्रह
कर्म्मसंग्रह m. (-हः) Collective acts, comprising the act, its performance,<BR>and the performer.<BR> E. कर्म्म, and संग्रह assemblage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=163-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मसचिव|कर्मसचिव|कर्मसचिवः|कर्म्मसचिवः
कर्म्मसचिव m. (-वः) A minister, a subordinate one employed upon active<BR>duties, as a judge, a deputy, &c.<BR> E. कर्म्म, and सचिव an adviser, a<BR>friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=163-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मसन्न्यासिक|कर्मसन्न्यासिक|कर्मसंन्यासिकः|कर्म्मसंन्यासिक|कर्म्मसन्न्यासिकः
कर्म्मसन्न्यासिक m. (-कः) An ascetic, a religious person who has withdrawn<BR>from the world.<BR> E. कर्म्म, and सन्न्यासिक a Sannyasi or religious men-<BR>dicant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=163-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मसमाधि
कर्म्मसमाधि m. (-धिः) Devotion, abstruction.<BR> E. कर्म्म, and समाधि abstruction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=163-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मसम्भव|कर्मसम्भव
कर्म्मसम्भव mfn. (-वः-वा-वं) Produced by, or the consequence of acts. E.<BR>कर्म्म, and सम्भव born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=163-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मसाक्षिन्|कर्मसाक्षिन्
कर्म्मसाक्षिन् m. (-क्षी) The sun<BR> E. कर्म, and साक्षिन् an evidence; who<BR>beholds all deeds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=163-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मसाधन|कर्मसाधन
कर्म्मसाधन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Implement, means.<BR>	 2. Articles essential to the<BR>performance of a religious act.<BR> E. कर्म्म, and साधन means of effecting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=163-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मसिद्धि|कर्मसिद्धि|कर्मसिद्धिः
कर्म्मसिद्धि f. (-द्धिः) Success, accomplishment.<BR> E. कर्म्म, and सिद्धि com-<BR>pletion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=163-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्महेतु|कर्महेतु
कर्म्महेतु mfn. (-तुः-तुः-तु) Arising from acts, caused by acts.<BR> E. कर्म्म, and<BR>हेतु cause; also with कन् added कर्म्महेतुक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=163-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्माङ्ग|कर्माङ्ग|कर्मांग
कर्म्माङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>	 1. Part or progress of any act.<BR>	 2. Part of a sacrificial<BR>rite.<BR> E. कर्म्म, and अङ्ग member.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=163-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मात्मन्|कर्मात्मन्
कर्म्मात्मन् mfn. (-त्मा-त्मा-त्म) Endowed with principles of action, active,<BR>acting.<BR> E. कर्म्म, and आत्मन् self.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=163-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मानुबन्ध|कर्मानुबन्ध
कर्म्मानुबन्ध m. (-न्धः) Connexion with or dependence upon acts.<BR> E. कर्म्म,<BR>and अनुबन्ध attachment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=163-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मानुबन्धिन्|कर्मानुबन्धिन्
कर्म्मानुबन्धिन् mfn. (-न्धी-न्धिनी-न्धि) Connected or confined by works.<BR> E. कर्म्म,<BR>and अनुबन्धिन् what connects.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=163-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मानुरूप|कर्मानुरूप
कर्म्मानुरूप mfn. (-पः-पा-पं)<BR>	 1. According to action or act.<BR>	 2. According to<BR>function or duty.<BR> E. कर्म्म, and अनुरूप according to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=163-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मानुरूपतस्|कर्मानुरूपतस्
कर्म्मानुरूपतस् ind. Conformably to act, function, &c.<BR> E. तसि added to<BR>the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=163-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मानुष्ठान|कर्मानुष्ठान
कर्म्मानुष्ठान n. (-नं) Practising one's duties; discharging peculiar func-<BR>tions.<BR> E. कर्म्म, and अनुष्ठान following.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=163-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मानुसार|कर्मानुसार|कर्मानुसारः
कर्म्मानुसार m. (-रः) Consequence of or conformity to acts.<BR> E. कर्म्म, and<BR>अनुसार consequence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=163-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मानुसारतस्|कर्मानुसारतस्
कर्म्मानुसारतस् ind. According to one's deeds.<BR> E. कर्म्म, and अनुसार com-<BR>formity, तसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=163-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मानुष्ठायिन्|कर्मानुष्ठायिन्
कर्म्मानुष्ठायिन् mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि) Practising duties, performing rites, &c.<BR>E. कर्म्म, and अनुष्ठायिन् following.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=163-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मान्त|कर्मान्त|कर्मांत|कर्मान्तः|कर्म्मान्तः
कर्म्मान्त m. (-न्तः)<BR>	 1. Tilled or cultivated land.<BR>	 2. The end or abandon-<BR>ment of ritual acts.<BR>	 3. The end of any task or act.<BR> E. कर्म्म, and अन्त<BR>an end or limit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=163-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मान्तर|कर्मान्तर|कर्मांतर
कर्म्मान्तर n. (-रं) Difference or contrariety of action, re-action.<BR>	 2. Penance,<BR>expiation.<BR>	 3. Suspense, interval of action.<BR> E. कर्म्म, and अन्तर differ-<BR>ence, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=163-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मान्तिक|कर्मान्तिक|कर्मांतिक|कर्मान्तिकः
कर्म्मान्तिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Final, completing.<BR>	 m. (-कः) A servant, one<BR>who finishes work.<BR> E. कर्म्मान्त. and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=163-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्माभिधायक|कर्माभिधायक
कर्म्माभिधायक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Enjoining, or prescribing duties or acts.<BR>E. कर्म्म, and अभिधायक what shows: also कर्म्माभिधायिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=163-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मार|कर्मार|कर्मारः|कर्म्मारः
कर्म्मार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. An artificer, a mechanic, a blacksmith, a brazier, a<BR>carpenter, &c.<BR>	 2. A bamboo.<BR>	 3. An acid fruit: see कर्म्मरङ्ग.<BR> E. कर्म्म,<BR>ऋ to go. घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=163-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मारम्भ|कर्मारम्भ
कर्म्मारम्भ m. (-म्भः) Commencement of any act.<BR> E. कर्म्म, and आरम्भ beginning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=163-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मार्ह|कर्मार्ह|कर्मार्हः|कर्म्मार्हः
कर्म्मार्ह mfn. (-र्हः-र्हा-र्हं)<BR>	 1. Fit for work, able to do anything.<BR>	 2. Suitable<BR>to any rite, &c.<BR>	 m. (-र्हः) A man.<BR> E. कर्म्म, and अर्ह fit for.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=163-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मिन्|कर्मिन्
कर्म्मिन् mfn. (-र्म्मी-र्म्मिणी-र्म्मि)<BR>	 1. Busy, active, engaged in any work.<BR>	 2.<BR>Belonging or relating to any act.<BR> E. कर्म्म, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=163-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मिष्ठ|कर्मिष्ठ|कर्म्मिष्ठः
कर्म्मिष्ठ mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठा-ष्ठं) Active, assiduous, diligent.<BR> E. कर्म्म, and इष्ठन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=163-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मीर|कर्मीर|कर्म्मीरः
कर्म्मीर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Variegated: see किर्म्मीर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=163-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मीरक|कर्मीरक
कर्म्मीरक m. (-कः) A small tree, (Trophis aspera.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=163-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मेन्द्रिय|कर्मेन्द्रिय|कर्मेंद्रिय|कर्म्मेन्द्रियं
कर्म्मेन्द्रिय n. (-यं) An organ of action; five are reckoned, the hand, the<BR>foot, the larynx or organ of the voice, the organ of generation,<BR>and that of fœculent excretion.<BR> E. कर्म्म, and इन्द्रिय an organ of<BR>sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=164-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मोदार|कर्मोदार
कर्म्मोदार n. (-रं) Any honourable or valiant act, magnanimity, prowess.<BR>E. कर्म्म, and उदार lofty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=164-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मोद्युक्त|कर्मोद्युक्त
कर्म्मोद्युक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं) Actively labouring, busily engaged.<BR> E. कर्म्म,<BR>and उद्युक्त exerting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=164-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मोद्योग|कर्मोद्योग
कर्म्मोद्योग m. (-गः) Engaging actively in any work.<BR> E. कर्म्म, and उद्योग effort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=164-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्व|कर्वः|कर्व्व|कर्व्वः
कर्व r. 1st cl. (कर्वति) To be proud, to boast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=164-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्व्व|कर्व|कर्वः|कर्व्वः
कर्व्व m. (-र्व्वः)<BR>	 1. Love, desire.<BR>	 2. A rat.<BR> E. कृ to injure, and व Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=164-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्व्वट|कर्वट|कर्वटः|कर्व्वटं|कर्व्वटः
कर्व्वट mn. (-टः-टं)<BR>	 1. The capital of a district, (of two or four hundred<BR>villages,) in a pleasant site and of handsome construction, a<BR>market town, &c.<BR>	 n. (-टं) A city.<BR> E. कर्व्व to be proud, and अटच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=164-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्व्वर|कर्वर|कर्वरः
कर्व्वर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A demon or imp.<BR>	 2. A tiger.<BR>	 f. (-री)<BR>	 1. A name of<BR>DURGĀ.<BR>	 2. The leaf of the asafœtida plant: see हिङ्गुपत्री.<BR> E. कृ to in-<BR>jure, क्वरच् Uṇādi affix; if derived from कर्ब्ब to go, &c. this word is<BR>read कर्ब्बर, but such a reading is probably inaccurate: see कर्ब्बर,<BR>also कर्ब्बुर; it is sometimes considered as a various reading of this<BR>last, meaning, variegated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=164-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्ष|कर्षः
कर्ष mn. (-र्षः-र्षं) A weight of gold or silver, a Karṣa equal to sixteen<BR>Mashas; this, according to the ancient division of five Rettis to<BR>the Masha, would make the Karṣa equal to about 176 grains troy;<BR>in common use, eight Rettis are given to the Masha and the Karṣa<BR>is therefore about 280 grains troy: see मास and रक्तिक.<BR>	 m. (-षः)<BR>	 1.<BR>Drawing, dragging, pulling.<BR>	 2. Ploughing.<BR>	 3. Attracting.<BR>	 4. Beleric<BR>myrobalan: see विभीतक.<BR> E. कृष् to plough, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=164-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्षक|कर्षकः
कर्षक mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>	 1. A cultivator of the soil, one who lives by til-<BR>lage.<BR>	 2. What draws or drags.<BR>	 3. Attractive, what attracts.<BR> E. कृष् to<BR>plough, बुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=164-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्षण|कर्षणं
कर्षण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Ploughing, cultivating the ground.<BR>	 2. Pulling, drag-<BR>ging.<BR>	 3. Attracting.<BR> E. कृष् to plough, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=164-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्षणि|कर्षणिः
कर्षणि f. (-णिः) A dishonest woman.<BR> E. कृष्, and अनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=164-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्षणीय
कर्षणीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>	 1. To be drawn or pulled.<BR>	 2. To be attracted, to<BR>be conciliated or won.<BR> E. कृष् to plough, with अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=164-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्षफल|कर्षफलः
कर्षफल m. (-लः) Beleric myrobalan, (Terminalia belerica.)<BR> E. कर्ष the<BR>same, and फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=164-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्षयत्
कर्षयत् mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्)<BR>	 1. Dragging, pulling.<BR>	 2. Attracting.<BR>	 3. Haras-<BR>sing, annoying.<BR> E. कृष् to attract, causal form, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=164-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्षाह्व
कर्षाह्व n. (-ह्वं) A Tola, a weight of sixteen Mashas.<BR> E. कर्ष, and आह्वा<BR>appellation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=164-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्षित
कर्षित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Drawn.<BR>	 2. Attracted.<BR>	 3. Ploughed.<BR> E. कृष् to<BR>draw, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=164-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्षिन्
कर्षिन् mfn. (-र्षी-र्षिणी-र्षि)<BR>	 1. What pulls or draws.<BR>	 2. What ploughs or<BR>furrows.<BR>	 3. Attractive, what attracts.<BR>	 f. (-र्षिणी)<BR>	 1. A medicinal sort<BR>of moon-plant: see क्षीरिणी.<BR>	 2. The bit of a bridle.<BR> E. कृष् to plough,<BR>&c. णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=164-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्षू
कर्षू m. (-र्षूः)<BR>	 1. A fire of dried cowdung.<BR>	 2. Agriculture, cultivating,<BR>cultivation.<BR>	 3. Livelihood.<BR>	 f. (-र्षूः)<BR>	 1. A river.<BR>	 2. A canal.<BR>	 3. A<BR>shallow trench for receiving the sacrificial fire.<BR> E. कृष् to plough,<BR>&c. Uṇādi affix ऊ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=164-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्हि
कर्हि ind. When, at what time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=164-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्हिचित्
कर्हिचित् ind. Sometimes, occasionally, ever; न कर्हिचित् never.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=164-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल|कलं|कलः
कल r. 1st cl. (कलति) To sound. 1st and 10th cls. (कलति, कालयति) To<BR>throw or cast, to send; also 1st and 10th cls. (कलति, कलयति)<BR>	 1. To<BR>go.<BR>	 2. To count or reckon: with आङ् prefixed, 1. To take, 2. To<BR>bind or tie; with परि, To keep in mind, to think or remember;<BR>with वि, To maim, to separate a part, to make defective; with सम्,<BR>To sum up, to add.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=164-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल|कलं|कलः
कल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>	 1. Crude, undigested.<BR>	 2. Weak.<BR>	 m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. A low<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=164-b" target="_blank">Page164-b+ 60</a>]<BR>or soft tone, as humming, buzzing, &c.<BR>	 2. The Sal tree.<BR>	 3. In poetry,<BR>time equal to four matras or instants.<BR>	 n. (-लं)<BR>	 1. Semen virile.<BR>	 2.<BR>The jujube, Zizyphus jujuba.)<BR>	 f. (-ला)<BR>	 1. A small part of anything.<BR>2. A digit or one sixteenth of the moon's diameter.<BR>	 3. A division<BR>of time, equal to thirty Kashhas or about eight seconds.<BR>	 4. The<BR>60th part of one thirtieth of a zodiacal sign, a minute of a degree.<BR>5. Interest on a capital.<BR>	 6. Any practical art, mechanical or fine,<BR>sixty-four such are enumerated, as carpentering, architecture, jewel-<BR>lery, farriery, acting, dancing, music, medicine, poetry, &c.<BR>	 7. The<BR>menstrual discharge.<BR>	 8. A boat 9. Fraud, deceit.<BR> E. कल् to sound,<BR>to count, &c. अच् affix or क pleasure, and ल what gives, from ला<BR>to bring, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=164-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलक|कलकः
कलक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A kind of fish: see शकुल.<BR>	 2. Name of species of prose<BR>composition.<BR> E. कल् to count, &c. वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=164-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलकण्ठ|कलकंठ|कलकण्ठः
कलकण्ठ m. (-ण्ठः)<BR>	 1. A low murmuring tone.<BR>	 2. The Indian cuckoo.<BR>	 3.<BR>A dove, a pigeon.<BR>	 4. A goose.<BR> E. कल low tone, and कण्ठ the throat;<BR>in whose throat it is made.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=164-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलकल|कलकलः
कलकल m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. A confused noise, the murmuring or buzz of a<BR>crowd.<BR>	 2. Resin, pitch, the resin of the Sal tree.<BR> E. कल् to sound,<BR>as above; the root reiterated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=164-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलकूजिका
कलकूजिका f. (-का) A wanton, a lascivious woman.<BR> E. कल, and कूज to coo,<BR>affix कन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=164-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलघोष|कलघोषः
कलघोष m. (-षः) The Kokila or Indian cuckoo.<BR> E. कल, घुष् to sound, and<BR>घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=164-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलङ्क|कलंक|कलंकः|कलङ्कः
कलङ्क m. (-ङ्कः)<BR>	 1. A spot or mark.<BR>	 2. Defamation, abuse.<BR>	 3. The rust of<BR>iron.<BR> E. क BRAHMĀ, water, &c. लकि to deface, and घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=164-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलङ्ककर
कलङ्ककर mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>	 1. Censorious, calumniating, defaming.<BR>	 2. Spot-<BR>ting, staining,<BR> E. कलङ्क, and कर what makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=164-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलङ्ककला
कलङ्ककला f. (-ला) A digit of the moon in shadow.<BR> E. कलङ्क, and कला<BR>a digit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=164-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलङ्कमय
कलङ्कमय mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>	 1. Spotted, stained.<BR>	 2. Calumniated, defamed.<BR>E. कलङ्क, and मयट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=164-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलङ्कष|कलंकष|कलंकषः|कलङ्कषः
कलङ्कष m. (-षः) A lion.<BR>	 f. (-षा) A musical instrument: see करताली. E.<BR>कल a murmuring sound, and कष् to make a sound, affix. खच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=164-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलङ्कित|कलंकित
कलङ्कित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Spotted, soiled, stained.<BR>	 2. Calumniated, de-<BR>famed.<BR> E. कलङ्क, and इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=164-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलङ्किन्
कलङ्किन् mfn. (-ङ्की-ङ्किनी-ङ्कि)<BR>	 1. Soiled, stained.<BR>	 2. Disgraced, reviled.<BR>	 3.<BR>Rusty.<BR> E. कलङ्क, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=164-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलङ्कुर|कलंकुर|कलंकुरः|कलङ्कुरः
कलङ्कुर m. (-रः) An eddy, a whirlpool.<BR> E. कल a sound, and कुर to emit<BR>sound, क affix, and the termination of the 2nd case retained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=164-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलञ्ज|कलंज|कलंजः|कलञ्जः
कलञ्ज mfn. (-ञ्जः-ञ्जा-ञ्जं) An animal struck with a poisoned weapon.<BR>2. Tobacco.<BR>	 3. Ten tolas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=164-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलट|कलटं
कलट n. (-टं) The thatch of a house; other read this कुटल q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=164-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलता
कलता f. (-ता) Melody, music.<BR> E. कल, and तल् affix; also with त्व कलत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=164-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलत्र|कलत्रं
कलत्र n. (-त्रं)<BR>	 1. The hip and loins.<BR>	 2. A wife.<BR>	 3. A royal citadel, a<BR>strong hold or fastness.<BR> E. गड to distil, &c. अत्रच् affix, क is sub-<BR>stituted for ग, and ड and ल are interchangeable: see कडत्र; or कल<BR>weak, feeble, and त्र, from त्रै to preserve, affix ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=164-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलधूत|कलधूतं
कलधूत n. (-तं)<BR>	 1. Gold.<BR>	 2. Silver: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=164-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलधौत|कलधौतं
कलधौत n. (-तं)<BR>	 1. Gold.<BR>	 2. Silver.<BR>	 3. A low or pleasing tone; also कलधूत.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=164-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलधौतलिपि
कलधौतलिपि f. (-पिः)<BR>	 1. A streak of gold.<BR>	 2. Illumination of a manu-<BR>script with gold.<BR> E. कलधौत, and लिपि writing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=164-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलध्वनि|कलध्वनिः
कलध्वनि m. (-निः)<BR>	 1. The turtle dove.<BR>	 2. The Kokila^1 or Indian cuckoo.<BR>3. A peacock.<BR>	 4. A low sweet tone.<BR> E. कल, and ध्वनि a sound.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20260511. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/217.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=164-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलन|कलनं|कलनः
कलन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. A spot, a stain.<BR>	 2. An offence, fault, defect.<BR>	 3. Mur-<BR>muring, sounding.<BR>	 4. An embryo or the first vestige of the fœtus.<BR>m. (-नः) A sort of cane.<BR>	 f. (-ना)<BR>	 1. Subjection, submission.<BR>	 2. Chat-<BR>tering, talking.<BR>	 3. Shedding, emitting.<BR> E. कल् to count, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=164-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलन्दर|कलंदरः|कलन्दरः
कलन्दर m. (-रः) A man of a mixed caste.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=164-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलन्दिका|कलंदिका
कलन्दिका f. (-का) Knowledge, intelligence, wisdom in general.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=164-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलभ|कलभः
कलभ m. (-भः)<BR>	 1. A young elephant: see कल.<BR>	 2. The Datura plant. E.<BR>कल् to cast, अभच् Uṇādi affix; or according to some authorities, कृ<BR>to cast, अभच् affix, making करभ, and र is then changed to ल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=165-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलम|कलमः
कलम m. (-मः)<BR>	 1. Rice which is sown in May and June, and ripens in<BR>December or January; a white rice growing in deep water: see<BR>शालि.<BR>	 2. A pen, a reed for writing with.<BR>	 3. A thief, a rogue. E.<BR>कल् to count, &c. and अम Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=165-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलम्ब|कलंब|कलंबः|कलम्बः
कलम्ब m. (-म्बः)<BR>	 1. An arrow.<BR>	 2. The stalk of a potherb.<BR>	 3. The<BR>Kadamba, (Nauclea cadamba:) see कदम्ब.<BR>	 n. (-म्बं) Calamba-<BR>root, (Menispermum calumba.)<BR>	 f. (-म्बी) or m. and f. (-म्बः-म्बी) A<BR>kind of potherb, (Convolvulus repens, &c.) see कडम्बी.<BR> E. कड्<BR>to delight, अम्बच् affix, ल substituted for ड, fem. affix ङीष्; also<BR>कलम्बक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=165-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलम्बिका|कलंबिका
कलम्बिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. A potherb: see the preceding.<BR> E. कन् added to<BR>कलम्बी.<BR>	 2. The nape of a neck.<BR> E. क the head, and लबि to be, to<BR>rest, ण्वुल् affix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=165-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलम्बुट|कलंबुट|कलम्बुटं
कलम्बुट m. (-टः) Fresh butter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=165-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलम्बू
कलम्बू f. (-म्बूः) A potherb: see कलम्बी, the fem. affix being ऊञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=165-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलयत्
कलयत् mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्) Computing, calculating.<BR> E. कल् to count, शतृ<BR>affix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=165-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलरव|कलरवः
कलरव m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. A dove, a pigeon.<BR>	 2. The Indian cuckoo.<BR>	 3. A low or<BR>pleasing tone, a humming, buzzing, &c.<BR> E. कल a low tone and रव<BR>what utters.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=165-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलल|कललं|कललः
कलल mn. (-लः-लं) The womb, the uterus; according to some, the em-<BR>bryo one month after conception.<BR> E. कल् to reckon, अलच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=165-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कललज|कललजः
कललज m. (-जः) Resin, the extract of the Sal tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=165-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कललजोद्भव|कललजोद्भवः
कललजोद्भव m. (-वः) The Sal tree, (Shorea robusta.)<BR> E. कललज, and उद्भव<BR>birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=165-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलविङ्क|कलविंक|कलविंकः|कलविङ्कः
कलविङ्क m. (-ङ्कः)<BR>	 1. A sparrow.<BR>	 2. A plant, (Echites antidysenterica:)<BR>see कलिङ्गक.<BR>	 3. A spot, a stain.<BR>	 4. A white Chowri.<BR> E. कल a low<BR>tone, chirping, &c. वकि to go, &c. अच् affix, the deriv. is irr.; also<BR>कलविङ्कक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=165-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलश|कलशः
कलश mfn. (-शः-शी-शं) An earthen water-pot; also कलस, कलशि, &c.<BR> E. क<BR>water, लश् to labour, क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=165-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलशि|कलशिः
कलशि f. (-शिः)<BR>	 1. A plant, (Hemionites cordifolia.)<BR>	 2. A water-jar.<BR> E. क<BR>water, लश् to labour, &c. कि affix; also कलशी and कलसि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=165-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलशी
कलशी f. (-शी)<BR>	 1. A plant.<BR>	 2. A water-jar: see the preceding, and कलश.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=165-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलस|कलसः
कलस mfn. (-सः-सी-सं) A water-jar: see कलश.<BR>	 m. (-सः)<BR>	 1. A measure, a<BR>Drona: see द्रोण.<BR>	 2. A rounded pinnacle or ball on the top of a<BR>temple.<BR>	 f. (-सी) A plant: see कलशि, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=165-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलसि|कलसिः
कलसि f. (-सिः) See कलशि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=165-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलसीसुत|कलसीसुतः
कलसीसुत m. (-तः) A name of the saint AGASTYA: see घटोद्भव and अगस्त्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=165-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलसोदधि|कलसोदधिः
कलसोदधि m. (-धिः) The ocean.<BR> E. कलस, and उदधि the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=165-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलस्वर
कलस्वर n. (-रं) A low musical sound.<BR> E. कल, स्वर a note.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=165-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलह|कलहं|कलहः
कलह mn. (-हः-हं)<BR>	 1. War, battle.<BR>	 2. Strife, contention.<BR>	 m. (-हः)<BR>	 1. The<BR>sheath of a sword, a scabbard.<BR>	 2. A road, a way.<BR>	 3. Deceit, false-<BR>hood.<BR>	 4. Violence without murderous weapons, abuse, beating,<BR>kicking, &c.<BR> E. कल a pleasing sound, and ह what destroys, from<BR>हन् with ड aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=165-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलहंस|कलहंसः
कलहंस m. (-सः)<BR>	 1. A drake, or according to some, a teal.<BR>	 2. A gander.<BR>3. Another bird, (Gallinula porphyria.)<BR>	 4. BRAHMĀ or the Supreme<BR>Being.<BR>	 5. An emperor.<BR>	 6. A species of the Atijagatī^1 metre.<BR> E. कल<BR>pleasing sound, and हस a goose.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by 2026-05-22 on Scott Rhodes. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/221.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=165-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलहकार|कलहकारः
कलहकार mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>	 1. Contending with, fighting.<BR>	 2. Quarrelsome,<BR>turbulent.<BR> E. कलह, and कार who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=165-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलहकारिन्
कलहकारिन् mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि) Assailing, contending or fighting with.<BR>	 2.<BR>Quarrelsome, fractious, turbulent.<BR> E. कलह, and कारिन् who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=165-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलहनाशन|कलहनाशनः
कलहनाशन m. (-नः) Febrifuge nut-plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=165-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलहप्रिय|कलहप्रियः
कलहप्रिय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Quarrelsome.<BR>	 m. (-यः) NĀRADA^1.<BR>	 f. (-या) The<BR>Maina, a bird.<BR> E. कलह, and प्रिय fond of.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20260517. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/225.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=165-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलहान्तरिता|कलहांतरिता
कलहान्तरिता f. (-ता) An appeased wife, one who has been angry and is<BR>sorry for it.<BR> E. कलह strife, अन्तरित covered, &c. fem. affix टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=165-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलहापहृत
कलहापहृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Taken by force.<BR> E. कलह, and अपहृत taken<BR>away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=165-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलाकुल
कलाकुल n. (-लं) Poison.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=165-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलाकुशल
कलाकुशल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Skilled in the elegant arts; singing, dancing,<BR>&c.<BR> E. कला, and कुशल clever.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=165-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलाकेलि|कलाकेलिः
कलाकेलि mfn. (-लिः-लिः-लि) Gay, frolicsome, wanton.<BR>	 m. (-लिः) A name<BR>of KĀMA^1 or love.<BR> E. कला deceit, and केलि who sports.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20260617. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/264.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=165-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलाङ्कुर|कलांकुर|कलांकुरः|कलाङ्कुरः
कलाङ्कुर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A crane.<BR>	 2. A name of KANSA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=165-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलाचिका
कलाचिका f. (-का) The fore arm, the arm below the elbow; also कलाची.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=165-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलाची
कलाची f. (-ची) See the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=165-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलाद|कलादः
कलाद m. (-दः) A gold-smith: see कणाद.<BR> E. कला an art, and दा to give,<BR>ड aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=165-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलानिधि|कलानिधिः
कलानिधि m. (-धिः) The moon.<BR> E. कला a digit, निधि a treasure; contain-<BR>ing many digits.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=165-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलानुनादिन्
कलानुनादिन् m. (-दी)<BR>	 1. A bee, but particularly one of a very large kind.<BR>2. A sparrow.<BR>	 3. The Chataka, a bird so called.<BR> E. कल a buzz, &c.<BR>अनुनद् to sound, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=165-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलान्तर|कलांतर|कलान्तरं
कलान्तर n. (-रं) Interest, profit.<BR> E. कला a part, अन्तर over.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=165-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलाप|कलापः
कलाप m. (-पः)<BR>	 1. An ornament in general.<BR>	 2. A zone, a string of bells<BR>worn by woman round the waist.<BR>	 3. A peacock's tail.<BR>	 4. Assem-<BR>blage, multitude.<BR>	 5. A quiver.<BR>	 6. The moon.<BR>	 7. A clever and in-<BR>telligent man.<BR>	 8. The name of a grammar of the Sanskrit<BR>language, ascribed to the god KARTIKEYA.<BR>	 9. A village where the<BR>destroyer KALKI is to be born.<BR>	 10. A poem written in one metre.<BR>E. अला an art, a division of time, &c. आप् to obtain, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=165-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलापक|कलापकं|कलापकः
कलापक m. (-कः) A rope on an elephant's neck.<BR>	 n. (-कं)<BR>	 1. A number of<BR>verses in one metre.<BR>	 2. A series of four stanzas on one subject.<BR>	 3.<BR>A loan to be repaid when the peacocks spread their tails.<BR> E. कलाप,<BR>and वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=165-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलापिन्
कलापिन् m. (-पी)<BR>	 1. A peacock.<BR>	 2. The Indian cuckoo.<BR>	 3. Waved leaf fig<BR>tree.<BR>	 4. The author of the Kalāpa grammar.<BR>	 f. (-नी)<BR>	 1. The moon.<BR>2. A species of cyperus.<BR> E. कलाप a peacock's tail, &c. इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=165-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलापूर्ण|कलापूर्णः|कलापूर्ण्ण
कलापूर्ण m. (-र्णः) The moon.<BR> E. कला a digit, and पूर्ण filled, complete.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=165-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलाभृत्
कलाभृत् m. (-भृत्)<BR>	 1. The moon.<BR>	 2. An artist, a mechanic, &c.<BR> E. कला a<BR>digit, &c. and भृत् who cherishes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=165-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलामक|कलामकः
कलामक m. (-कः) A kind of rice ripening in the cold season: see कलम.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=165-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलाम्बि|कलांबिः|कलाम्बिः
कलाम्बि f. (-म्बिः) Lending, a loan: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=165-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलाम्बिका
कलाम्बिका f. (-का) Lending, a loan.<BR> E. कला a part, and अम्ब to go, वुन् affix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=165-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलाय|कलायः
कलाय m. (-यः) The name of various leguminous seeds, chiefly<BR>of the order Plaseolus, particular kinds of pulse or vetches.<BR> E. क<BR>wind, ला to bring or give, and युक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=165-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलायखञ्ज
कलायखञ्ज m. (-ञ्जः) One who trembles and totters as he walks.<BR> E. कलाय,<BR>and खञ्ज a wagtail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=165-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलायन|कलायनः
कलायन m. (-नः) A tumbler, a dancer, but especially one who dances<BR>or walks on a sharp edge, as the edge of a sword. &c.<BR> E. कला a<BR>part, and अयन going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=165-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलालाप|कलालापः
कलालाप m. (-पः) A bee, &c.<BR> E. कल buzz, and आलाप speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=165-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलावत्|कलावन्त्
कलावत् m. (-वान्) A name of Chandra or the moon.<BR>	 f. (-ती)<BR>	 1. A celes-<BR>tial lute or Vina.<BR>	 2. The mother of RĀDHĀ^1.<BR>	 3. An Apsara.<BR>	 4. A<BR>mystical ceremony, initiation of the Tantrika student, in which<BR>the goddess DURGĀ is supposed to be transferred from the water-<BR>jar to the body of the novice.<BR> E. कला a digit, or कल a sweet tone,<BR>and मतुप् aff.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by 2026-05-15 on Scott Rhodes. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/222.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=165-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलाविक|कलाविकः
कलाविक m. (-कः) A cock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=165-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलाविकल|कलाविकलः
कलाविकल m. (-लः) A sparrow: see कलविङ्क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=165-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलाहक|कलाहकः
कलाहक m. (-कः) A musical instrument; also काहल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=165-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलि|कलिः
कलि m. (-लिः)<BR>	 1. The fourth age of the world, according to the<BR>Hindus, the iron age, or that of vice: the commencement of the<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=166-a" target="_blank">Page166-a+ 60</a>]<BR>Kali-yug or age, is placed 3,101 years anterior to the Christian<BR>æra, so that in A. D. 1896, the Kali year is 4,997, the number<BR>of its years is 432,000, at the expiration of which, the world is<BR>to be destroyed.<BR>	 2. The age personified.<BR>	 3. War, battle.<BR>	 4. Strife,<BR>dissension.<BR>	 5. An arrow.<BR>	 6. Beleric myrobalan.<BR>	 f. (-लिः or -ली) An<BR>unblown flower: see कलिका.<BR> E. कल् to count or reckon, इन्<BR>Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=165-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलिक|कलिकः
कलिक m. (-कः) A curlew.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=166-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलिका
कलिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. An unblown flower.<BR>	 2. The bottom or peg of a lute.<BR>E. कल् to count, इन् affix कलि, and with ङीष्, कली as above; again,<BR>कन् pleonastic affix, and टाप् fem. do.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=166-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलिकापूर्व्व|कलिकापूर्व|कलिकापूर्व्वं
कलिकापूर्व्व n. (-र्व्वं) Acts leading to future consequences, not connected<BR>with those of a previous birth.<BR> E. कलिका a bud, अपूर्व्व not<BR>preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=166-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलिकार|कलिकारः
कलिकार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A plant bearing a nut, which is used as a febrifuge.<BR>(Grey bonduc.) see पूतिकरञ्ज.<BR>	 2. The fork-tailed shrike.<BR>	 3.<BR>Another bird, a small one with a yellow head, (Loxia philippensis.)<BR>4. A name of NĀRADA^1.<BR>	 f. (-री) A poisonous plant: see लाङ्गली. E.<BR>कलि strife, &c. कृञ् to make, affix अण्; also with कन् added कलि-<BR>कारक.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20260517. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/225.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=166-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलिकारक|कलिकारकः
कलिकारक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. Grey bonduc; also कलिमारक.<BR>	 2. The name of<BR>NĀRADA^1 a divine sage, and great mischief maker: see कलिकार.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20260517. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/225.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=166-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलिङ्ग|कलिंग|कलिङ्गं|कलिङ्गः
कलिङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>	 1. The febrifuge nut-plant, (Cæsalpinia bunduccella.)<BR>2. The fork-tailed shrike, (Lanius forficatus, Lath.)<BR>	 3. The name<BR>of a country; the name of Kalinga is applied in the Puranas to<BR>several places, but it especially signifies a district on the Coro-<BR>mandel coast, extending from below Cuttack to the vicinity of<BR>Madras, (in this sense, like some other names of countries, it is<BR>usually confined to the plural number (-ङ्गाः) confounding the<BR>place with the people inhabiting it.<BR>	 nf. (-ङ्गं-ङ्गा) A medicinal seed,<BR>that of Echites antidysenterica.<BR>	 f. (-ङ्गा)<BR>	 1. A woman of a good<BR>shape.<BR>	 2. A plant, commonly Teori, (Convolvulus turpethum:)<BR>see त्रिवृत्.<BR> E. कलि strife, &c. ग from गम् to go, खच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=166-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलिङ्गक|कलिङ्गकः
कलिङ्गक m. (-कः) The seed of the Coraiya, (Echites antidysenterica:)<BR>see इन्द्रयव.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=166-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलिञ्ज|कलिंज|कलिंजः|कलिञ्जः
कलिञ्ज m. (-ञ्जः) A mat, a screen of grass, a tati, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=166-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलित|कलितं
कलित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Gained, acquired.<BR>	 2. Known, understood.<BR>	 3.<BR>Numbered, reckoned.<BR>	 4. Separated, divided.<BR>	 5. Made, done.<BR>	 6.<BR>Held, laid hold of.<BR>	 7. Sounded indistinctly, buzzed, murmured,<BR>&c.<BR> E. कल् to count, &c. affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=166-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलिद्रुम|कलिद्रुमः
कलिद्रुम m. (-मः) Beleric myrobalan, (Terminalia belerica,) also कलि the<BR>tree of strife; being supposed to be favourite haunt of imps or<BR>goblins.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=166-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलिन्द|कलिंद|कलिंदः|कलिन्दः
कलिन्द m. (-न्दः)<BR>	 1. The sun.<BR>	 2. A mountain.<BR>	 3. Beleric myrobalan. E.<BR>कलि strife, दा to give, खश् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=166-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलिन्दकन्या|कलिंदकन्या
कलिन्दकन्या f. (-न्या) The Yamuna.<BR> E. कलिन्द the sun or a mountain, कन्या<BR>daughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=166-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलिन्दनन्दिनी|कलिंदनंदिनी
कलिन्दनन्दिनी f. (-नी) The Yamuna or Jumna river.<BR> E. कलिन्द the name<BR>of a mountain, part of the Himālaya range, and नन्दिनी a daugh-<BR>ter; the source of the river being in the mountain Kalinda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=166-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलिन्दशैलजाता
कलिन्दशैलजाता f. (-ता) The Yamuna river: see the preceding.<BR> E. कलिन्द-<BR>शैल the mountain, and जाता born; also कलिन्दसू, कालिन्दी, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=166-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलिप्रिय|कलिप्रियः
कलिप्रिय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Quarrelsome, mischievous, mischief making.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-यः)<BR>	 1. A monkey, an ape.<BR>	 2. NĀRADA^1.<BR> E. कलि strife, and प्रिय<BR>fond of.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20260517. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/225.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=166-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलिमारक|कलिमारकः
कलिमारक m. (-कः) A plant, (Bonduccella:) see पूतिकरञ्ज^1.<BR> E. कलि strife,<BR>मृ to destroy or remove, affixes अण् and कन्; some copies read<BR>कलिकारक.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20260517. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/225.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=166-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलियुग|कलियुगं
कलियुग n. (-गं) The Kali, the present or iron age: see कलि.<BR> E. कलि, and<BR>युग an age.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=166-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलिल|कलिलः
कलिल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>	 1. Impervious, impenetrable.<BR>	 2. Mixed, blended.<BR>E. कल् to count, &c. इलच् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=166-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलिवृक्ष|कलिवृक्षः
कलिवृक्ष m. (-क्षः) Beleric myrobalan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=166-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलुक्क|कलुक्कः
कलुक्क m. (-क्कः) A musical instrument; a cymbal.<BR>	 f. (-क्का)<BR>	 1. A tavern.<BR>2. A meteor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=166-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलुष|कलुषं|कलुषः
कलुष mfn. (-षः-षा-षं)<BR>	 1. Turbid, foul, muddy.<BR>	 2. Wicked, bad.<BR>	 mf.<BR>(-षः-षी) A buffalo.<BR>	 n. (-षं)<BR>	 1. Sin.<BR>	 2. Wrath.<BR> E. कल् to go, &c. उषन्<BR>Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=166-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलुषत्व
कलुषत्व n. (-त्वं)<BR>	 1. Foulness, turbidness.<BR>	 2. Opacity.<BR>	 3. Agitation,<BR>trouble, anger.<BR> E. कलुष foul, &c. त्व affix; also with तल् कलुषता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=166-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलुषयोनि
कलुषयोनि mfn. (-निः-निः-नि) Of impure origin.<BR> E. कलुष, and योनि<BR>womb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=166-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलुषित
कलुषित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Defiled, contaminated.<BR>	 2. Foul, impure.<BR>3. Wicked.<BR> E. कलुष, and इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=166-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलुषिन्
कलुषिन् mfn. (-षी-षिणी-षि)<BR>	 1. Foul, impure.<BR>	 2. Depraved, wicked.<BR>	 3. De-<BR>filed.<BR> E. कलुष, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=166-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलेवर|कलेवरं|कलेवरः
कलेवर n. (-रं) The body.<BR> E. कल semen, and वर best; formed from the<BR>seminal fluid; the termination of the locative^1 is retained.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20260518. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/226.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=166-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलोत्ताल
कलोत्ताल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) High sharp.<BR> E. कल, and उत्ताल loud, high<BR>sounding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=166-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्क|कल्कः
कल्क mfn. (-ल्कः-ल्का-ल्कं) Sinful, wicked.<BR>	 mn. (-ल्कः-ल्कं)<BR>	 1. Sediment, the<BR>deposit of oil, ghee, &c.<BR>	 2. Dirt, filth.<BR>	 3. Ordure, fæces.<BR>	 4. Sin.<BR>	 5.<BR>Hypocrisy.<BR>	 6. Pride.<BR>	 7. The beleric myrobalan.<BR>	 8. The wax of the<BR>ear.<BR>	 9. Levigated powder.<BR> E. कल् to count, &c. क Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=166-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्कफल|कल्कफलः
कल्कफल m. (-लः) The pomegranate plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=166-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्कि|कल्किः
कल्कि m. (-ल्किः) A name of VIṢṆU, in his future capacity of destroyer<BR>of the world, the tenth and last Avatara of descent of the deity,<BR>in the four ages of Kalpa.<BR> E. कल् to count, कि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=166-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्किन्
कल्किन् mfn. (-ल्की-ल्किनी-ल्कि)<BR>	 1. Foul, turbid, having sediment.<BR>	 2.<BR>Dirty.<BR>	 3. Wicked.<BR>	 m. (-ल्की) The last descent of VIṢṆU: see the<BR>preceding.<BR> E. कल्क, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=166-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्प|कल्पः
कल्प mfn. (-ल्पः-ल्पा-ल्पं) In composition; Like, but with a degree of in-<BR>feriority.<BR>	 m. (-ल्पः)<BR>	 1. A Śāstra or sacred work; one of the six<BR>Vedangas, and comprehending the description of religious rites.<BR>2. A day and night of BRAHMĀ, a period of 4,320,000,000 Solar-<BR>sydereal-years or years of mortals, measuring the duration of the<BR>world, and as many, the interval of its annihilation.<BR>	 3. A destruc-<BR>tion of the world.<BR>	 4. A sacred precept, practice prescribed by the<BR>Vedas for effecting certain consequences.<BR>	 5. Propriety, fitness.<BR>	 6.<BR>Optionality, alternative, doubt.<BR>	 7. Resolve, purpose, any act of<BR>determination.<BR>	 8. One of the trees of INDRA'S paradise of Svarga.<BR>E. कृप् to be able, घ affix, ऋ is changed to अल्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=166-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्पक|कल्पकः
कल्पक m. (-कः) A barber.<BR> E. कृप् to cut, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=166-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्पक्षय|कल्पक्षयः
कल्पक्षय m. (-यः) The destruction of all things, the end of the world. E.<BR>कल्प, and क्षय destruction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=166-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्पद्रुम|कल्पद्रुमः
कल्पद्रुम m. (-मः) A fabulous tree, one granting every thing desired. E.<BR>कल्प purpose, and द्रुम a tree; also कल्पद्रु, कल्पवृक्ष, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=166-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्पन|कल्पनं
कल्पन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Cutting.<BR>	 2. Making, manufacturing.<BR>	 3. Making as a<BR>poem or tale, inventing, composing.<BR>	 nf. (-नं-ना)<BR>	 1. Inference.<BR>	 2.<BR>Invention, fabrication.<BR>	 3. Caparisoning or decorating an elephant.<BR>f. (-नी) A scissors or shears.<BR> E. कृप् to be able, &c. ल्यु or ल्युट् affix,<BR>and consequently टाप् or ङीप् fem. do.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=166-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्पनीय
कल्पनीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>	 1. To be made or contrived.<BR>	 2. To be substitut-<BR>ed or supplied.<BR> E. कृप् to be able, अनीयर् affix; also कल्प्य and<BR>कल्पितव्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=166-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्पवायु
कल्पवायु m. (-युः) The wind that is to blow at the end of all things. E.<BR>कल्प, and वायु wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=166-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्पवृक्ष|कल्पवृक्षः
कल्पवृक्ष m. (-क्षः) One of the fabulous trees of INDRA'S heaven; a tree<BR>which yields whatever may be desired.<BR> E. कल्प purpose, and वृक्ष a<BR>tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=166-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्पादि|कल्पादिः
कल्पादि m. (-दिः) The beginning of a Kalpa, the renovation of all<BR>things.<BR> E. कल्प, and आदि beginning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=167-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्पान्त|कल्पांत|कल्पान्तः
कल्पान्त m. (-न्तः) The destruction of the world, the end of the Kalpa,<BR>or four ages of its existence.<BR> E. कल्प the period, and अन्त the end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=167-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्पान्तस्थायिन्|कल्पांतस्थायिन्
कल्पान्तस्थायिन् mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि) Lasting, permanent.<BR> E. कल्पान्त, and<BR>स्थायिन् what stays.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=167-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्पित|कल्पितः
कल्पित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Made, fabricated, artificial.<BR>	 2. Composed, in-<BR>vented.<BR>	 3. Arranged, put in order.<BR>	 4. Prepared at once, put<BR>together extempore.<BR>	 5. Brought, conducted.<BR>	 6. Inferred.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-तः) An elephant armed or caparisoned for war.<BR> E. कृप् to be able,<BR>&c. क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=167-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्पितार्घ
कल्पितार्घ mfn. (-र्घः-र्घा-र्घं) One for whom or what a respectful offering is<BR>prepared.<BR> E. कल्पित made, and अर्घ an offering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=167-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्प्य
कल्प्य mfn. (-ल्प्यः-ल्प्या-ल्प्यं)<BR>	 1. To be made or contrived.<BR>	 2. To be substi-<BR>tuted.<BR> E. कृप् to be able, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=167-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्मष|कल्मषं|कल्मषः
कल्मष mfn. (-षः-षा-शं) Dirty, foul.<BR>	 m. (-षः) A kind of hell, a division of<BR>the infernal regions.<BR>	 n. (-षं)<BR>	 1. Sin.<BR>	 2. The hand bellow the wrist.<BR>E. कर्म्म virtuous or pious action, षो to destroy, and क affix; the<BR>form is irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=167-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्माष|कल्माषः
कल्माष mfn. (-षः-षा or -षी-षं) Of a mixed or variegated colour.<BR>	 m. (-षः)<BR>1. A variegated colour.<BR>	 2. A mixture of black and white.<BR>	 3. Black.<BR>4. A demon or goblin.<BR>	 f. (-षी) The spotted cow of Jamadagni, the<BR>giver of all desires.<BR> E. कल् to go, &c. क्विप् affix, कल्, मष् to injure,<BR>अण् affix माष; what injures or triumphs over other colours.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=167-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्माषकण्ठ|कल्माषकंठ|कल्माषकण्ठः
कल्माषकण्ठ m. (-ण्ठः) A name of ŚIVA.<BR> E. कल्माष black, and कण्ठ throat;<BR>form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=167-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्माषपाद|कल्माषपादः
कल्माषपाद m. (-दः) The name of a king, also SAUDĀSA; transformed<BR>to a Rākṣasa by VASIṢṬHA.<BR> E. कल्माष, and पाद a foot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=167-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्य|कल्यं|कल्यः
कल्य mfn. (-ल्यः-ल्या-ल्यं)<BR>	 1. Ready, prepared, armed.<BR>	 2. Healthy, free from<BR>sickness.<BR>	 3. Clever, dexterous.<BR>	 4. Deaf and dumb.<BR>	 5. Auspicious,<BR>(speech or discourse.)<BR>	 6. Counselling, monitory.<BR>	 7. Sound, perfect,<BR>free from mental or bodily imperfections.<BR>	 n. (-ल्यं)<BR>	 1. The dawn or<BR>break of day.<BR>	 2. Yesterday.<BR>	 3. Tomorrow.<BR>	 nf. (-ल्यं-ल्या)<BR>	 1. Spirituous<BR>liquor.<BR>	 2. Congratulation, good wishes, annunciation of good<BR>tidings.<BR>	 f. (-ल्या) Emblic myrobalan: see हरीतकी.<BR> E. कल् to count,<BR>&c. यक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=167-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्यजग्धि|कल्यजग्धिः
कल्यजग्धि f. (-ग्धिः) The morning meal, breakfast.<BR> E. कल्य dawn, and<BR>जग्धि eating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=167-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्यत्व|कल्यत्वं
कल्यत्व n. (-त्वं)<BR>	 1. Health.<BR>	 2. Recovery, convalescence.<BR> E. कल्य being<BR>well, and त्व affix of the abstract; also कल्यता with तल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=167-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्यपाल|कल्यपालः
कल्यपाल m. (-लः) A distiller.<BR> E. कल्य vinous liquor, and पाल who<BR>nourishes; also with कन् added, कल्यपालक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=167-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्यवर्त्त|कल्यवर्त|कल्यवर्तः|कल्यवर्त्तः
कल्यवर्त्त m. (-र्त्तः) Breakfast.<BR> E. कल्य, and वर्त्त, from वृत् to be or abide,<BR>affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=167-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्याण|कल्याणं|कल्याणः
कल्याण mfn. (-णः-णी-णं) Happy, well, right, prosperous, lucky.<BR>	 f. (-णी)<BR>1. A cow.<BR>	 2. A leguminous shrub, (Glycine debilis.)<BR>	 n. (-णं)<BR>	 1.<BR>Good fortune, happiness, prosperity.<BR>	 2. Gold.<BR> E. कल्य healthy, &c.<BR>अ to be, to sound, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=167-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्याणकर
कल्याणकर mfn. (-रः-री-रं) Propitious, auspicious, conferring good<BR>fortune, &c.<BR> E. कल्याण, and कर what makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=167-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्याणकृत्
कल्याणकृत् mfn. (-कृत्)<BR>	 1. Virtuous, good.<BR>	 2. Propitious, lucky.<BR> E. कल्याण,<BR>and कृत् who does.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=167-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्याणचार
कल्याणचार mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>	 1. Following virtuous courses.<BR>	 2. Lucky,<BR>fortunate.<BR> E. कल्याण, चर् to go, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=167-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्याणधर्मन्|कल्याणधर्म्मन्
कल्याणधर्मन् mfn. (-र्मा-र्मा-र्म) Good, virtuous.<BR> E. कल्याण, धर्म duty,<BR>अनिच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=167-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्याणपञ्चमीक
कल्याणपञ्चमीक m. (-कः) A fortnight which has the fifth lunation lucky.<BR>E. कल्याण, पञ्चमी the fifth, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=167-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्याणवचन
कल्याणवचन n. (-नं) Friendly speech, good wishes.<BR> E. कल्याण, and वचन<BR>speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=167-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्याणवीज|कल्याणवीजः
कल्याणवीज m. (-जः) A sort of pulse, (Ervum hirsutum.)<BR> E. कल्याण, and<BR>वीज seed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=167-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्याणाचार
कल्याणाचार mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Virtuous, following good practices.<BR> E. कल्याण,<BR>and आचार rule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=167-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्याणिका
कल्याणिका f. (-का) Red arsenic.<BR> E. कल्याणी, and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=167-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्याणिन्
कल्याणिन् mfn. (-णी-णिनी-णि)<BR>	 1. Happy, lucky, prosperous.<BR>	 2. Auspici-<BR>ous, propitious.<BR> E. कल्याण, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=167-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्यापाल|कल्यापालः
कल्यापाल m. (-लः) A distiller.<BR> E. कल्या spirituous liquor, and पाल who<BR>preserves.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=167-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्युष
कल्युष n. (-षं) The wrist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=167-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्ल|कल्लः
कल्ल r. 1st cl. (कल्लते)<BR>	 1. To sound ill or indistinctly.<BR>	 2. To sound.<BR>	 3. To<BR>be mute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=167-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्ल|कल्लः
कल्ल mfn. (-ल्लः-ल्ला-ल्लं) Deaf.<BR> E. कल्ल to sound indistinctly, affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=167-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्लत्व|कल्लत्वं
कल्लत्व n. (-त्वं)<BR>	 1. Indistinct articulation, hoarseness.<BR>	 2. Deafness.<BR> E. कल्ल<BR>to sound indistinctly, and त्व affix; also with तल् affix कल्लता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=167-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्लि
कल्लि ind. To-morrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=167-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्लोल|कल्लोलः
कल्लोल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) An enemy, hostile, inimical.<BR>	 m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. A surge,<BR>a billow.<BR>	 2. Joy, happiness, pleasure.<BR> E. कल्ल to sound, ओलच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=167-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कव
कव(ऋ)ववृ r. 1st cl. (कवते)<BR>	 1. To describe, (as a poet.)<BR>	 2. To paint, to<BR>picture; also कब.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=167-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवक|कवकं|कवकः
कवक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A mouthful.<BR>	 2. A fungus, a mushroom, &c.<BR> E. कु to<BR>sound, अक aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=167-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवच|कवचं|कवचः
कवच mn. (-चः-चं)<BR>	 1. Armour, mail.<BR>	 2. A drum used in battle, a kettle<BR>drum.<BR>	 3. An amulet, a charm.<BR>	 4. A tree, (Hibiscus populneoides.)<BR>see गर्द्दभाण्ड.<BR>	 3. The mystical syllable Hum, forming part of a<BR>Mantra, and considered as a preservative like armour; it is also<BR>inscribed on a Birch leaf, &c. and worn as an amulet; being car-<BR>ried about the person as a charm: see the next.<BR> E. कु to sound, अच्<BR>Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=167-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवचपत्र|कवचपत्रं|कवचपत्रः
कवचपत्र n. (-त्रं) The Birch tree, commonly Bhojpatra: see भूर्जपत्र. E.<BR>कवच an amulet, and पत्र a leaf: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=167-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवचहर|कवचहरः
कवचहर mfn. (-रः-रा-री-रं) Wearing armour or amulets.<BR>	 m. (-रः) A boy,<BR>a child.<BR> E. कवच, and हृ to take, अच् or ट aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=167-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवटी
कवटी f. (-टी) A door: see कवाट.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=167-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवयी
कवयी f. (-यी) A kind of flat fish, commonly Kavay or Kay; remark-<BR>able for going by land from one spot to another, (Coiuscoboius,<BR>Ham.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=167-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवर|कवरं|कवरः
कवर sub.<BR>	 mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) A braid or fillet of hair, adj. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>	 1.<BR>Mixed, intermingled, blended.<BR>	 2. Set, inlaid.<BR>	 mn. (-रः-रं)<BR>	 1. Salt.<BR>	 2.<BR>Sourness or acidity.<BR>	 f. (-रा or -री) A plant, (Mimosa octandra.)<BR>	 f.<BR>(-री) The leaf of the asafœtida plant, Hingupatri.<BR> E. क the head,<BR>&c. वृ to screen, अच् affix, fem. do. टाप् or ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=167-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवरकी
कवरकी f. (-की) A captive, a prisoner: see वन्दी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=167-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवरीभार|कवरीभारः
कवरीभार m. (-रः) A fine head of hair.<BR> E. कवरी, and भार a load; also<BR>कवरीभर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=167-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवरीभृत्
कवरीभृत् mfn. (-भृत्) Wearing a fillet of hair.<BR> E. कवरी, and भृत् who has.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=167-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवल|कवलं|कवलः
कवल m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. A mouthful.<BR>	 2. A kind of fish, commonly Baliya.<BR>	 3.<BR>An astringent wash for cleaning the mouth, a gargle.<BR> E. क the<BR>head, water, &c. and वल to be strong, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=167-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवलिका
कवलिका f. (-का) A piece of cloth over a sore, a bandage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=167-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवलित|कवलितः
कवलित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Eaten<BR> E. कवल nominal verb, to eat, and क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=167-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवस|कवसः
कवस m. (-सः) Armour, mail.<BR> E. कु to sound, and अस Uṇādi affix; also<BR>कवच.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=167-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवाट|कवाटः
कवाट sub.<BR>	 mfn. (-टः-टा-टं) A door, the leaf or pannel of the door.<BR> E. क<BR>wind, air, वट् to exclude, and अण् affix; also कपाट.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=167-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवाटवक्र|कवाटवक्रं
कवाटवक्र n. (-क्रं) A plant, commonly Kapata ventu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=167-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवार|कवारं
कवार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A lotus.<BR>	 2. A bird, (Tantalus falcinellus, BUCH.) E.<BR>क water, वर to prefer, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=167-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवि|कविः
कवि mfn. (-विः-विः or -वी-वि) Learned, wise.<BR>	 m. (-विः)<BR>	 1. A poet.<BR>	 2. The<BR>sun.<BR>	 3. SUKRA, the regent of the planet Venus, and preceptor of<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=168-a" target="_blank">Page168-a+ 60</a>]<BR>the demons.<BR>	 4. A name of VALMIKI, the author of the Rāmāyaṇa,<BR>the inventor of poesy.<BR>	 5. A name of BRAHMĀ.<BR>	 f. (-विः-वी) The bit<BR>of a bridle, or the reins altogether; also कविका.<BR> E. कु to sound, to<BR>celebrate, and इन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=167-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कविक|कविकं|कविकः
कविक mf. (-कः-का) The bit of a bridle, or the reins altogether.<BR>	 f. (-का)<BR>A sort of fish, the Kay.<BR> E. कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=168-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कविज्येष्ठ|कविज्येष्ठः
कविज्येष्ठ m. (-ष्ठः) A name of VALMIKI, author of the Rāmāyaṇa.<BR> E. कवि<BR>a poet, and ज्येष्ठ elder or superior.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=168-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कविता
कविता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Poesy, poetical style or composition.<BR>	 2. A poem. E.<BR>कवि, and तल् affix; also with त्व affix, कवित्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=168-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवितावेदिन्
कवितावेदिन् mfn. (-दी-दिनी-दि) Wise, learned, a genius, a poet.<BR> E. कविता<BR>poetry, &c. वेदिन् who understands.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=168-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कविय|कवियं
कविय mn. (-यः-यं) The bit of a bridle, or the reins.<BR> E. कु to sound, affix<BR>यः see कवि and कविक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=168-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कविरामायण|कविरामायणः
कविरामायण m. (-णः) A name of VALMIKI.<BR> E. कवि a poet, &c. and रामायण<BR>the epic poem so called; the poet of the Rāmāyaṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=168-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कविलाशिका
कविलाशिका f. (-का) A musical instrument, a kind of lute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=168-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कविवाल्मीकि|कविवाल्मीकिः
कविवाल्मीकि m. (-किः) The poet VALMIKI.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=168-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवीय|कवीयं
कवीय n. (-यं) The bit of a bridle, or the reins.<BR> E. कु to sound, छ affix;<BR>also कविय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=168-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवेल|कवेलं
कवेल n. (-लं) A lotus.<BR> E. क water, विल् to send, &c. घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=168-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवोष्ण|कवोष्णं
कवोष्ण mfn. (-ष्णः-ष्णा-ष्णं) Slightly warm, tepid.<BR>	 n. (-ष्णं) A slight warmth.<BR>E. कु indifferent, and उष्ण warm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=168-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कव्य|कव्यं|कव्यः
कव्य n. (-व्यं) An oblation or offering of food to deceased ancestors. E.<BR>कु to sound or praise, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=168-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कव्यवाल|कव्यवालः
कव्यवाल m. (-लः) A class of the manes or deified ancestors.<BR> E. कव्य an<BR>offering to the manes, वा occasionally, and ल who receives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=168-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कव्यवाहन
कव्यवाहन m. (-नः) Fire.<BR> E. कव्य, and वाहन vehicle; also कव्यवाह.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=168-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कश|कशः
कश r. 1st cl. (कशति-ते) To kill, to hurt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=168-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कशा
कशा f. (-शा)<BR>	 1. A whip.<BR>	 2. Whipping, flogging.<BR> E. कश् to hurt, अच् and<BR>टाप् affixes: also कष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=168-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कशात्रय
कशात्रय n. (-यं) Three modes of whipping (a horse,) good, bad, and<BR>middling.<BR> E. कशा, and त्रयम् threefold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=168-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कशार्ह|कशार्हः
कशार्ह mfn. (-र्हः-र्हा-र्हं) Deserving a whipping.<BR> E. कशा a whip, and अर्ह to<BR>be fit or proper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=168-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कशिपु|कशिपुः
कशिपु m. (-पुः)<BR>	 1. Food.<BR>	 2. Clothing. du.<BR>	 m. (-पू) Food and clothing. E.<BR>कश् to injure, to remove, (pain, hunger, &c.) पु affix, the form<BR>is irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=168-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कशेरु|कशेरुः
कशेरु mn. (-रुः-रु) The back bone.<BR>	 f. (-रूः) A kind of grass, (Scirpus<BR>kysoor.)<BR>	 m. (-रुः) One of the nine divisions of Jambu Dwipa.<BR> E. क<BR>sound, शृ to harm, ऊ or उ Uṇādi affix, and एरङ् substituted for the<BR>radical vowel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=168-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कशेरुक|कशेरुकं|कशेरुकः
कशेरुक f. (-का) The back bone.<BR>	 n. (-कं) A sort grass, (Scirpus kysoor.)<BR>E. कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=168-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कशेरुस्
कशेरुस् n. (-रुः) A grass, (Scirpus kysoor:) see कशेरु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=168-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कश्चन
कश्चन ind. Some body, a certain person; the first member of com-<BR>pound is declinable. as कश्चन, कस्यचन, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=168-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कश्चित्
कश्चित् ind. Some body, some one, a certain one: the first member of<BR>the compound is declinable, as कश्चित्, कस्मैचित्, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=168-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कश्मल|कश्मलं
कश्मल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Foul, dirty.<BR>	 m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. Fainting, syncope.<BR>	 2.<BR>Sin.<BR> E. कश् to go, क्मलच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=168-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कश्मीर|कश्मीरः
कश्मीर m. (-रः) The name of a country, Kashmir.<BR> E. कश् to go, ईरन्<BR>Uṇādi affix, and मुद् inserted: see काश्मीर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=168-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कश्मीरजन्मन्
कश्मीरजन्मन् m. (-न्मा) Saffron: see काश्मीरजन्मन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=168-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कश्य|कश्यं
कश्य mfn. (-श्यः-श्या-श्यं) Deserving a whipping.<BR>	 n. (-श्यं)<BR>	 1. Spirituous<BR>liquor.<BR>	 2. A horse's flank.<BR> E. कश् to beat, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=168-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कश्यप|कश्यपः
कश्यप m. (-पः)<BR>	 1. The name of a Muni or deified sage, the son of<BR>MARICHI, and father of the gods, demons, animals, fishes, reptiles,<BR>&c. by the seventeen daughters of DAKṢA.<BR>	 2. A kind of deer.<BR>	 3.<BR>A sort of fish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=168-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कश्यपनन्दन|कश्यपनन्दनः
कश्यपनन्दन m. (-नः) A name of GURUDA the bird of VIṢṆU.<BR> E. कश्यप,<BR>and नन्दन a son, the son of KAŚYAPA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=168-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कष|कषः
कष r. 1st cl. (कषति) 10th cl. (कषयति)<BR>	 1. To injure, to hurt, to destroy,<BR>to kill.<BR>	 2. To try, to test: with नि, to try metals.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=168-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कष|कषः
कष m. (-षः) The touchstone.<BR>	 f. (-षा) A whip; also कशा.<BR> E. कष् to hurt,<BR>to test or try, अच् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=168-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कषण|कषणः
कषण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Unripe, immature.<BR>	 n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Touch or test of<BR>gold by the touchstone.<BR>	 2. Rubbing, marking.<BR> E. कष् to hurt,<BR>affix युच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=168-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कषपाषाण|कषपाषाणः
कषपाषाण m. (-णः) A touchstone.<BR> E. कष्, and पाषाण a stone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=168-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कषाकु|कषाकुः
कषाकु m. (-कुः)<BR>	 1. The sun.<BR>	 2. Fire.<BR> E. कष् to injure, आकु Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=168-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कषाघात
कषाघात m. (-तः) A cut, a stroke with a whip.<BR> E. कषा, and आघात a<BR>blow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=168-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कषाय|कषायः
कषाय mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>	 1. Astringent.<BR>	 2. Fragrant.<BR>	 3. Red, dull red.<BR>	 4.<BR>Brown, of a colour composed of red and yellow.<BR>	 mn. (-यः-यं)<BR>	 1.<BR>An astringent flavour or taste.<BR>	 2. A decoction or infusion.<BR>	 3. Gum,<BR>resin, extract, exudation from a tree, &c.<BR>	 4. Plastering, anointing.<BR>5. Colouring or perfuming the person.<BR>	 6. Attachment to worldly<BR>objects.<BR>	 m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. A plant, (Bignonia Indica.)<BR>	 2. Passion,<BR>emotion.<BR>	 f. (-या) A plant, a small sort of Hedysarum.<BR> E. कष् to<BR>injure, आय aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=168-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कषायकृत्
कषायकृत् m. (-कृत्) Red Lodh, a tree the bark of which is used in<BR>dyeing.<BR> E. कषाय red, कृत् what makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=168-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कषायचित्र
कषायचित्र mfn. (-त्रः-त्रा-त्रं) Dyed or stained of a dull red colour.<BR> E. कषाय,<BR>and चित्र painted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=168-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कषायान्वित
कषायान्वित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Astringent, harsh.<BR> E. कषाय, and अन्वित having.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=168-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कषायित
कषायित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Prepared for dyeing or colouring.<BR> E. कषाय<BR>nominal verb, to astringe, and क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=168-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कषायिन्
कषायिन् mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि)<BR>	 1. Yielding a resinous exudation.<BR>	 2. Astrin-<BR>gent.<BR>	 3. Dyed of a red colour.<BR>	 4. Worldly minded.<BR>	 m. (-यी) The<BR>Sal tree.<BR> E. कषाय, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=168-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कषि|कषिः
कषि mfn. (-षिः-षिः-षि) Injurious, mischievous.<BR> E. कष् to hurt, and<BR>इन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=168-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कषिका
कषिका f. (-का) A bird in general.<BR> E. कष् to hurt, and इकन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=168-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कषित
कषित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Hurt, injured.<BR> E. कष् to hurt, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=168-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कषेरुका
कषेरुका f. (-का) The back-bone, the spine: see कशेरुका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=168-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कष्ट|कष्टं|कष्टः
कष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>	 1. Pained, suffering pain.<BR>	 2. Impervious, impene-<BR>trable.<BR>	 n. (-ष्टं) Bodily pain or uneasiness. ind. (-ष्टं) An exclama-<BR>tion of regret or sorrow, ah, alas!<BR> E. कष् to hurt, participle<BR>affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=168-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कष्टकर
कष्टकर mfn. (-रः-री-रं) Giving pain or trouble.<BR> E. कष्ट, and कर what<BR>makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=168-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कष्टकारक|कष्टकारकः
कष्टकारक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Causing trouble or annoyance.<BR>	 m. (-कः) The<BR>world.<BR> E. कष्ट pain, and कारक the maker, the cause.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=168-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कष्टश्रित
कष्टश्रित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Suffering pain or misfortune, under-going hard-<BR>ships, performing penance.<BR> E. कष्ट, and श्रित subjected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=168-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कष्टस्थान|कष्टस्थानं
कष्टस्थान n. (-नं) A bad or disagreeable place or scite.<BR> E. कष्ट, and स्थान<BR>place, situation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=168-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कष्टि|कष्टिः
कष्टि f. (-ष्टिः)<BR>	 1. Test, trial.<BR>	 2. Pain, trouble.<BR> E. कष् to hurt, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=168-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कस|कसः
कस r. 1st cl. (कसति) To move, to go or approach: with वि prefixed,<BR>to open or expand as a flower, to blow. (इ) कसि r. 2nd cl. (कंस्ते)<BR>1. To go.<BR>	 2. To command.<BR>	 3. To destroy: the root is also read by<BR>some authorities, कस (कस्ते) or कशि (कंष्टे.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=168-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कस|कसः
कस m. (-सः) A touchstone: see कष.<BR>	 f. (-सा) A whip: see कशा and कषा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=168-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कसनोत्पाटन|कसनोत्पाटनः
कसनोत्पाटन m. (-नः) A plant, (Justicia, &c.) see वासक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=168-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कसिपु|कसिपुः
कसिपु m. (-पुः) Food, boiled rice: see कशिपु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=168-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कसेरु|कसेरुः
कसेरु m. (-रुः) A sort of grass: see कशेरु, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=168-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कसेरुका
कसेरुका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. A sort of grass.<BR>	 2. The back bone: see कशेरुका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=168-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कस्तीर|कस्तीरं
कस्तीर n. (-रं) Tin.<BR> E. कस् to go, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=168-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कस्तुरिका
कस्तुरिका f. (-का) Musk; also कस्तूरी and कस्तूरिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=168-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कस्तूरीमल्लिका
कस्तूरीमल्लिका^1 f. (-का) The musk-bag.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20250526. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/237.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=169-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कस्तूरिका
कस्तूरिका f. (-का) See कस्तूरी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=169-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कस्तूरिकाण्डज
कस्तूरिकाण्डज m. (-जः) Musk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=169-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कस्तूरी
कस्तूरी f. (-री)<BR>	 1. Musk, the animal perfume so called, as brought from<BR>Kashmir, Napal, and western Asam or Bhutan, the latter is said<BR>to be the best.<BR>	 2. A plant, (Hibiscus abelmoschus.)<BR>	 3. Another<BR>plant, (Amaryllis zeylanica.)<BR> E. कस् to go, and तूरच् affix; its<BR>scent going or spreading; the deriv. is irr.; also कन् being added<BR>कस्तूरिका and कस्तुरिका as above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=169-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कस्मल|कस्मलं
कस्मल n. (-लं)<BR>	 1. Fainting, syncope.<BR>	 2. Sin: see कश्मल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=169-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कस्वर
कस्वर mfn. (-रः-री-रं) Who or what goes or moves.<BR> E. कस् to go, वरच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=169-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कह्लार|कह्लारं
कह्लार n. (-रं) The white esculent water-lily, (Nymphæa lotus.)<BR> E. क<BR>water, हार a necklace or ornament, and ल irregularly inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=169-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कह्व|कह्वः
कह्व m. (-ह्वः) A kind of crane, (Ardea nivea.)<BR> E. क water, ह्वेञ् to call,<BR>&c. ड aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=169-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कांसीय|कांसीयं
कांसीय n. (-यं) White copper: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=169-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कांस्य|कांस्यं|कांस्यः
कांस्य mn. (-स्यः-स्यं) A goblet, a drinking vessel.<BR>	 n. (-स्यं)<BR>	 1. White cop-<BR>per or brass, queen's metal, any amalgam zinc and copper.<BR>	 2. A<BR>musical instrument, a sort of gong or plate of bell-metal struck<BR>with a stick or rod.<BR>	 3. A measure: see कंस, &c.<BR> E. कसि to injure,<BR>ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=169-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कांस्यक|कांस्यकं
कांस्यक n. (-कं) See the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=169-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कांस्यकार|कांस्यकारः
कांस्यकार m. (-रः) A brazier, a pewterer, a worker in white or bell-<BR>metal.<BR> E. कांस्य, and कार a workman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=169-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कांस्यनील|कांस्यनीलः
कांस्यनील m. (-लः) Blue vitriol considered as a collyrium.<BR> E. कांस्य<BR>bell-metal, and नील blue or black; also written occasionally कांश्यनील.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=169-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काक|काकं|काकः
काक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A crow.<BR>	 2. A plant, (Ardisia solanacea?)<BR>	 3. A lame<BR>man, a cripple, one whose legs are wanting or useless.<BR>	 4. One of<BR>the divisions of the world or Dwipas.<BR>	 5. A measure.<BR>	 6. Washing the<BR>head, bathing by dipping the head only into the water.<BR>	 7. A sec-<BR>tarial mark, the Tilaka? 8. Shameless, arrogant.<BR>	 n. (-कं)<BR>	 1. Modus<BR>coeundi.<BR>	 2. A multitude or assemblage of crows.<BR>	 f. (-का) An appel-<BR>lation of several plants, as, 1. The common Vakapushpa: see वक;<BR>2. Kakjhangi, (Leea hirta;) also in this sense काकी; 3. A medici-<BR>nal plant, vulg. Kakoli; 4. The Retti or Gunja, (Abrus precatori-<BR>us;)<BR>	 5. Opposite-leaved fig-tree: see उडुम्बर; 6. A potherb, (Sola-<BR>num Indicum, &c.) see काकमाची.<BR> E. कै to sound, Uṇādi affix कन्;<BR>or क for कु bad, ill, and अक to go, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=169-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काककङ्गु|काककङ्गुः
काककङ्गु f. (-ङ्गुः) A kind of panick, (P. miliaceum.)<BR> E. काक, and कङ्गु<BR>another species of the same grass; the Kengu of the crows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=169-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काककला
काककला f. (-ला) A plant, (Leea hirta:) see काकजङ्घा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=169-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकघ्नी
काकघ्नी f. (-घ्नी) A tree, said to be a large kind of Karañja, (Galedupa<BR>arborea.)<BR> E. काक, and घ्नी what kills.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=169-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकचिञ्चा|काकचिंचा
काकचिञ्चा f. (-ञ्चा) The shrub which yields the red and black berry, used<BR>in India as a jeweller's weight, (Abrus precatorius:) see गुञ्जा. E.<BR>काक, and चिञ्चा extremity; the point being as black as a crow; also<BR>काकचिञ्चि and काकचिञ्ची.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=169-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकचिञ्चि|काकचिञ्चिः
काकचिञ्चि f. (-ञ्चिः) See the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=169-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकचिञ्ची
काकचिञ्ची f. (-ञ्ची) See काकचिञ्चा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=169-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकच्छद|काकच्छदः|काकछद
काकच्छद m. (-दः)<BR>	 1. A wagtail.<BR>	 2. Side locks of the head of hair.<BR> E. काक<BR>a crow, and छद plumage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=169-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकच्छर्द्दि|काकच्छर्दि|काकछर्द्दि
काकच्छर्द्दि m. (-र्द्दिः)<BR>	 1. A wagtail.<BR>	 2. What is ejected by a crow. E.<BR>काक, and छर्द्दि vomiting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=169-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकजङ्घा|काकजंघा
काकजङ्घा f. (-ङ्घा) A plant, (Leea hirta, Rox. Catalogue; elsewhere de-<BR>scribed as Leea æquata.)<BR> E. काक, and जङ्घा a thigh; compared to a<BR>crow's leg.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=169-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकजम्बु|काकजम्बुः
काकजम्बु f. (-म्बुः) A plant, commonly Bhuinjamb, (Ardisia solanacea:)<BR>see भूमिजम्बु; also काकजम्बू.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=169-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकण|काकणं
काकण n. (-णं) A leprosy with black and red spots, considered incur-<BR>able.<BR> E. काक the Gunja berry, deriv. irr. also with कन् affix काकणक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=169-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकणन्तिका
काकणन्तिका f. (-का) The Abrus precatorius: see काकचिञ्चा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=169-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकता
काकता f. (-ता) The state or nature of a crow.<BR> E. काक, and तल् affix;<BR>also काकत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=169-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकतालीय
काकतालीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Accidental, unexpected, opportune.<BR> E. काक,<BR>and ताली the fruit of the palm: it alludes to a story of the fruit of<BR>the palm falling in the way of a crow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=169-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकतालीयवत्
काकतालीयवत् ind. Suddenly, opportunely.<BR> E. काकतालीय, and वत् like.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=169-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकतालुकिन्
काकतालुकिन् mfn. (-की-किनी-कि) Contemptible, vile.<BR> E. काक, तालु palate,<BR>कन् affix of similitude, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=169-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकतिक्ता
काकतिक्ता f. (-क्ता) The Gunja-plant: see काकचिञ्चा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=169-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकतिन्दुक|काकतिन्दुकः
काकतिन्दुक m. (-कः) A kind of ebony, (Diospyros tomentosa, Rox.) E.<BR>काक, and तिन्दुक ebony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=169-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकतुण्ड|काकतुण्डः
काकतुण्ड m. (-ण्डः) A dark sort of Agallochum: see कालागुरु.<BR>	 f. (-ण्डी)<BR>	 1.<BR>The Gunja-plant.<BR>	 2. A sort of brass.<BR>	 3. A tree, commonly Kuwa<BR>dori.<BR> E. काक, and तुण्ड face; of the colour of a crow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=169-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकतुण्डिका
काकतुण्डिका f. (-का) The Gunja-plant: see काकचिञ्चा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=169-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकध्वज|काकध्वजः
काकध्वज m. (-जः) Submarine fire, a personage in Hindu mythology:<BR>see और्व्व.<BR> E. काक, and ध्वज a banner, whose symbol is a crow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=169-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकनाशा
काकनाशा f. (-शा) A plant, commonly Vakapushpa: see वकपुष्प.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=169-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकनासा
काकनासा f. (-सा) A plant: see काकजङ्घा; also काकनासिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=169-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकनासिका
काकनासिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. A plant, (Leea hirta.)<BR>	 2. Red Teori.<BR> E. काक a<BR>crow, and नासिका a nose; the root being fancifully compared to the<BR>beak of the bird; also काकनासा and काकनासिकी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=169-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकन्दी
काकन्दी f. (-न्दी) Emblick myrobalan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=169-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकपक्ष|काकपक्षः
काकपक्ष m. (-क्षः) The side locks of the head of hair; three or five on<BR>each side left when the head is first shaved, and which may be al-<BR>lowed to remain, especially in persons of the military caste.<BR> E. काक,<BR>and पक्ष a feather, a wing, a crow's wing; the word is also used as<BR>an epithet of a warrior, a name of RAMA, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=169-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकपीलु|काकपीलुः
काकपीलु m. (-लुः) A kind of ebony: see काकतिन्दुक; also with कन् add-<BR>ed काकपीलुकः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=169-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकपुच्छ|काकपुच्छः
काकपुच्छ m. (-च्छः) The Kokila or Indian cuckoo.<BR> E. काक, and पुच्छ a<BR>tail; crow-tailed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=169-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकपुष्ट|काकपुष्टः
काकपुष्ट m. (-ष्टः) The Koil or Kokil, as before.<BR> E. काक, and पुष्ट nourish-<BR>ed; this bird like the English cuckoo, being said to leave its eggs<BR>in the nests of other birds, as in that of the crow, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=169-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकफल|काकफलः
काकफल m. (-लः) The Nimb tree.<BR> E. काक, and फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=169-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकबन्ध्या
काकबन्ध्या f. (-न्ध्या) A woman that bears only one child.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=169-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकभीरु|काकभीरुः
काकभीरु m. (-रुः) An owl.<BR> E. काक, and भीरु fearful; afraid of the crows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=169-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकमद्गु|काकमद्गुः
काकमद्गु m. (-द्गुः) A water-hen, gallinule.<BR> E. काक, and मद्गु another kind<BR>of bird, a Shag; resembling a crow in colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=169-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकमर्द्द|काकमर्द|काकमर्दः|काकमर्द्दः
काकमर्द्द m. (-र्द्दः) The colocynth or bitter apple.<BR> E. काक, and मर्द्दक de-<BR>stroying; the fruit of which destroys crows; also काकमर्द्दक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=169-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकमाचिका
काकमाचिका f. (-का) A plant: see the next word.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=169-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकमाची
काकमाची f. (-ची) An esculent vegetable, commonly Gurkamai, (Sola-<BR>num Indicum.)<BR> E. काक, मच् to respect, &c. अण् and ङीष् affixes;<BR>also with कन् and टाप् added, काकमाचिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=169-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकमुद्गा
काकमुद्गा f. (-द्गा) A plant, commonly Mugani, according to some, a wild<BR>kind of beam.<BR> E. काक, and मुद्ग Moong.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=169-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकयव|काकयवः
काकयव m. (-वः) Barren corn, the ear of which has no grain.<BR> E. काक, and<BR>यव barley.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=169-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकरुक|काकरुकः
काकरुक mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>	 1. Naked.<BR>	 2. Timid, fearful.<BR>	 3. Poor, indigent.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. Fraud, deceit.<BR>	 2. An owl.<BR>	 3. A henpecked husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=169-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकरुहा
काकरुहा f. (-हा) A parasite plant, (Epidendrum tesseloides, &c.) see<BR>वन्दा.<BR> E. काक, and रुह what mounts; on which crows rest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=169-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकल|काकलं|काकलः
काकल n. (-लं) A jewel worn upon neck.<BR>	 f. (-लिः or -ली) A low and<BR>sweet tone, the song of a bird, &c.<BR> E. का instead of कु diminutive,<BR>कल् to sound, इन् or ङीप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=169-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकलक|काकलकः
काकलक m. (-कः) An ornament of the neck.<BR> E. कन् added the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=169-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकलीद्राक्षा
काकलीद्राक्षा f. (-क्षा) A grape with a very small stone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=169-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकलीरव|काकलीरवः
काकलीरव m. (-वः) The Kokila.<BR> E. काकली a sweet tone, and रव sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=170-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकशब्द
काकशब्द m. (-ब्दः) The cawing of a crow.<BR> E. काक, and शब्द sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=170-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकशीर्ष|काकशीर्षः
काकशीर्ष m. (-र्षः) A tree, commonly Vakapushpa; (Æschynomene<BR>grandiflora.)<BR> E. काक, and शीर्ष a head.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=170-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकस्त्री
काकस्त्री f. (-स्त्री) See the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=170-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकाङ्गा
काकाङ्गा f. (-ङ्गा) A plant, (Leea æquata.)<BR> E. काक, and अङ्ग form, body,<BR>टाप् affix; or with ङीष् affix, काकाङ्गी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=170-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकाङ्गी
काकाङ्गी f. (-ङ्गी) See the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=170-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकाञ्ची
काकाञ्ची f. (-ञ्ची)<BR>	 1. A plant, (Leea æquata.)<BR>	 2. An esculent vegetable,<BR>(Solanum Indicum.)<BR> E. काक, अञ्च् to go, अच् and ङीप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=170-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकादनी
काकादनी f. (-नी) The Gunja-plant: see काकचिञ्चा.<BR> E. काक, अदन food,<BR>ङीप् fem. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=170-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकार
काकार mfn. (-रः-री-रं) Scattering water.<BR> E. क water, कॄ to scatter; with<BR>आङ् prefixed, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=170-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकारि|काकारिः
काकारि m. (-रिः) An owl.<BR> E. काक, and अरि a foe; whose enemy is the crow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=170-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकाल|काकालः
काकाल m. (-लः) A raven.<BR> E. काक, and अल् to be able, affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=170-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकिणी
काकिणी f. (-णी)<BR>	 1. A cubit, the forth part of a Danda or short pole.<BR>2. The quarter of a Paṇa, a weight or a tale of shells equal to twenty<BR>Cowries.<BR>	 3. A quarter of a Masha, a weight of silver or gold.<BR>	 4. A<BR>Retti or small seed used as a weight.<BR>	 5. A Cowri or shell used<BR>as a coin.<BR> E. कक to be unsteady, ल्युट् and ङीप् affixes; deriv. irr.;<BR>also the dental न being substituted, काकिनी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=170-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकिनी
काकिनी f. (-नी) See the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=170-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकिल|काकिलः
काकिल m. (-लः) The central jewel in a necklace, &c. see काकल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=170-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकु|काकुः
काकु f. (-कुः)<BR>	 1. Change of voice in fear, grief, &c.<BR>	 2. Muttering,<BR>murmuring.<BR>	 3. The tongue.<BR> E. कक् to deride, उण् affix, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=170-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकुत्स्थ|काकुत्स्थः
काकुत्स्थ m. (-त्स्थः)<BR>	 1. A name of RAMA.<BR>	 2. The name of a sovereing,<BR>also Purañjaya^1.<BR> E. ककुद् pre-eminent, अण् affix, and स्थ who stays or is.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20260603. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/248.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=170-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकुद|काकुदं
काकुद m. (-दः) The palate.<BR> E. ककुद् the head, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=170-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकेक्षु|काकेक्षुः
काकेक्षु m. (-क्षुः) A kind of reed, (Saccharum spontaneum.)<BR> E. काक, and<BR>इक्षु sugar-cane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=170-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकेन्दु|काकेन्दुः
काकेन्दु m. (-न्दुः) A species of ebony, (Diospyros melanoxylon.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=170-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकोचिक|काकोचिकः
काकोचिक m. (-कः) A kind of fish, commonly Cacochi; also काकोचि<BR>(Cyprinus cachius, HAM.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=170-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकोडुम्बर|काकोडुम्बरः
काकोडुम्बर m. (-रः) Opposite-leaved fig-tree, (Ficus oppositifolia.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=170-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकोडुम्बरिका
काकोडुम्बरिका f. (-का) See the preceding.<BR> E. काक, and उडुम्बर glomerous<BR>fig, कन् affix, and the feminine termination; also काकोदुम्बरिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=170-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकोदर|काकोदरः
काकोदर m. (-रः) A snake.<BR> E. काक going ill or tortuously, (derived from<BR>का for कु, and अक to go,) and उदर the belly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=170-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकोल|काकोलं|काकोलः
काकोल mn. (-लः-लं) A poisonous substances of a black colour, or<BR>the colour of a raven, whence its name; possibly the berry of the<BR>Cocculus Indicus.<BR>	 n. (-ल) A division of the infernal regions or<BR>hell.<BR>	 m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. A raven.<BR>	 2. A potter.<BR>	 3. A snake.<BR>	 4. A boar.<BR>5. A drug; as follows.<BR>	 f. (-ली) The name of a vegetable substance<BR>used in medicine, described as sweet and cooling, allaying fever,<BR>removing phlegm, &c.: it it said to be a root brought from Nepal<BR>or Morung.<BR> E. काक to be unsteady, &c. and ओलच् affix, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=170-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकोलूकिका
काकोलूकिका f. (-का) The natural enmity of the owl and crow.<BR> E. काक<BR>a crow, उलूक an owl, वुन् affix, implying enmity in this and similar<BR>compounds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=170-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काक्ष|काक्षः
काक्ष r. 1st. cl. (इ) काक्षि (कांक्षति) To desire; it is most frequently used<BR>with आङ् prefixed, in the same sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=170-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काक्ष|काक्षः
काक्ष mfn. (-क्षः-क्षा-क्षं) Frowning, looking, scornfully or in displeasure.<BR>m. (-क्षः) A glance, a wink or leer.<BR>	 n. (-क्षं) A frown, a look of dis-<BR>pleasure.<BR> E. का for कु diminutive or depreciative, and अक्षि the eye.<BR>f. (-क्षी)<BR>	 1. A sort of trefoil, (Cytisus cojan.)<BR>	 2. A perfume, a fra-<BR>grant kind of earth.<BR> E. कक्ष a creeping plant, अण् and ङीप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=170-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काक्षीव|काक्षीवः
काक्षीव m. (-वः) A plant, (Morunga hyperanthera, &c.) see शोभाञ्जन. E.<BR>का or कु diminutive, and क्षीव to be intoxicated: see अक्षीव; also<BR>with कन् added काक्षीवक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=170-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काग|कागः
काग m. (-गः) A crow: (in the dialects, a raven.)<BR> E. का an imitative<BR>sound, and ग who sings, from गै with ड or क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=170-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काङ्क्षत्
काङ्क्षत् mfn. (-ङ्क्षन्-ङ्क्षन्ती-ङ्क्षत्) Wishing, desiring, hoping.<BR> E. काक्षि to desire,<BR>शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=170-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काङ्क्षा|कांक्षा
काङ्क्षा f. (-ङ्क्षा) Wish, inclination, desire.<BR> E. काक्षि to wish, अच् and टाप्<BR>affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=170-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काङ्क्षित|कांक्षित
काङ्क्षित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Wished, desired.<BR> E. काक्षि to wish, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=170-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काङ्क्षारु
काङ्क्षारु m. (-रुः) A heron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=170-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काङ्गा
काङ्गा f. (-ङ्गा) Orris root.<BR> E. का bad, crooked, and अङ्ग body, shape.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=170-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काच|काचं|काचः
काच r. 1st cl. (इ) काचि (काञ्चते^1) 1. To shine.<BR>	 2. To bind.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20260619. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/265#issuecomment-4742856865.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=170-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काच|काचं|काचः
काच m. (-चः)<BR>	 1. Alkaline ashes, any salt of potash or soda in a glassy<BR>or crystalline state.<BR>	 2. Crystal, quartz or glass, considered as a<BR>natural production, and used as a jewel or ornament.<BR>	 3. A loop,<BR>swinging shelf, a string so contrived as to hold or support<BR>burthens, &c.<BR>	 4. A disease of the eyes, affection of the optic nerve<BR>or gutta serena.<BR>	 n. (-चं)<BR>	 1. Alkaline salt, black salt.<BR>	 2. Wax. E.<BR>कच् to shine or bind, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=170-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काचक|काचकः
काचक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A stone 2. Alkaline ashes, &c. see the preceding. E.<BR>कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=170-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काचकूपी
काचकूपी f. (-पी) A glass-bottle.<BR> E. काच, and कूपी bottle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=170-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काचघटी
काचघटी f. (-टी) A glass-ewer.<BR> E. काच, and घटी a small jar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=170-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काचन|काचनं
काचन n. (-नं) An enclosure, a string or tape which ties a parcel or<BR>bundle of papers, &c.<BR> E. कच् to tie, ल्युट् affix; also with कन् added<BR>काचनक m. (-कः.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=170-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काचन|काचनं
काचन ind. Some one, any one, (applied to feminine objects,) the first<BR>member is declinable.<BR> E. का fem. of किम्, चन added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=170-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काचनक|काचनकं
काचनक n. (-कं) A binding or rope for binding.<BR> E. कन् added to काचन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=170-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काचनकिन्
काचनकिन् m. (-की) A writing, a written paper.<BR> E. काचनक a<BR>binding, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=170-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काचभाजन|काचभाजनं
काचभाजन n. (-नं) A vessel of glass or crystal, a cup, a goblet, &c. E.<BR>काच, and भाजन a vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=170-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काचमणि|काचमणिः
काचमणि m. (-णिः) Crystal, quartz.<BR> E. काच, and मणि a gem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=170-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काचमल|काचमलं
काचमल n. (-लं) Black salt or soda: see काचलवण.<BR> E. काच glass, and<BR>मल soil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=170-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काचलवण|काचलवणं
काचलवण n. (-णं) Black salt, a medicinal salt, prepared by calcining<BR>fossile salt and the fruit of the emblic myrobalan together. It<BR>consists chiefly of muriate of soda, with a small quantity of iron,<BR>lime and sulphur, and is a tonic aperient.<BR> E. काच alkaline ashes,<BR>and लवण salt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=170-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काचवकयन्त्र
काचवकयन्त्र n. (-न्त्रं) A glass-retort.<BR> E. काच, and वकयन्त्र a retort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=170-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काचसम्भव|काचसंभव|काचसम्भवं
काचसम्भव n. (-वं) Black salt: see the last.<BR> E. काच, and सम्भव produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=170-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काचसौवर्च्चल|काचसौवर्चल|काचसौवर्चलं
काचसौवर्च्चल n. (-लं) Black salt: see काचलवण.<BR> E. काच, and सौवर्च्चल salt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=170-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काचस्थाली
काचस्थाली f. (-ली) The trumpet flower, (Bignonia sauveolens^1.)<BR> E. काच<BR>glass, and स्थाली a goblet, &c. to which its colour is compared.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20260608. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/253.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=170-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काचिघ|काचिघः
काचिघ m. (-घः)<BR>	 1. A legume.<BR>	 2. A rat.<BR>	 3. Gold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=170-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काचित्
काचित् ind. Some one, any one, (a female person or object,) the first<BR>member is declinable, as काञ्चित्, &c.<BR> E. का fem. of किम्, and चित् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=170-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काचित|काचितं
काचित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Suspended by a swing or in a loop.<BR> E. काच a<BR>nominal root, to hang by a loop or in a swing, and क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=170-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काचिम|काचिमः
काचिम m. (-मः) A tree considered as sacred, one growing near a<BR>temple, and an object of religious veneration or worship, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=170-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काञ्चन|कांचन|काञ्चनं|काञ्चनः
काञ्चन mfn. (-नः-नी-नं) Golden, of gold.<BR>	 n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Gold.<BR>	 2. Wealth.<BR>	 3.<BR>A filament of the lotus.<BR>	 m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. Mountain ebony, (Bauhinia<BR>variegata, &c.)<BR>	 2. A tree bearing a yellow fragrant flower,<BR>(Michelia champaca.)<BR>	 3. Another plant, (Mesua ferrea:) see<BR>नागकेसर.<BR>	 4. Glomerous fig-tree: see उडुम्बर.<BR>	 5. Common thorn<BR>apple, (Datura metel.)<BR>	 f. (-नी)<BR>	 1. Turmeric.<BR>	 2. A yellow pigment.<BR>E. कचि to shine, &c. ल्युट् affix, the radical vowel lengthened; this<BR>etymology gives the meaning gold, the others refer to their colour,<BR>&c. in which they resemble the metal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=170-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काञ्चनक|काञ्चनकं|कांचनकः|काञ्चनकः
काञ्चनक m. (-कः) Mountain ebony, &c.<BR>	 n. (-कं) Yellow orpiment. E.<BR>काञ्चन gold, &c. and कन् affix, implying resemblance or identity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=171-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काञ्चनकन्दर|कांचनकंदर|काञ्चनकन्दरः
काञ्चनकन्दर m. (-रः) A gold-mine.<BR> E. काञ्चन, and कन्दर a cave.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=171-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काञ्चनकारिणी
काञ्चनकारिणी f. (-णी) a plant, (Asparagus racemosus:) see शतमूली.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=171-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काञ्चनगिरि|कांचनगिरि|काञ्चनगिरिः
काञ्चनगिरि m. (-रिः) Mount Sumeru.<BR> E. काञ्चन, and गिरि a mountain;<BR>the golden mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=171-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काञ्चनचय
काञ्चनचय m. (-यः) A heap of gold.<BR> E. काञ्चन, and चय assemblage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=171-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काञ्चनभू|कांचनभू
काञ्चनभू f. (-भूः)<BR>	 1. Gold-dust.<BR>	 2. A Golden or yellow soil.<BR> E. काञ्चन,<BR>and भू soil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=171-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काञ्चनमय
काञ्चनमय mfn. (-यः-यी-यं) Golden.<BR> E. काञ्चन, and मयट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=171-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काञ्चनवप्र
काञ्चनवप्र m. (-प्रः) A hill or mound of gold.<BR> E. काञ्चन, and वप्र a mound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=171-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काञ्चनसन्धि|काञ्चनसंधि|कांचनसंधि|काञ्चनसन्धिः
काञ्चनसन्धि f. (-न्धिः) A treaty of friendship between two parties on<BR>equal terms.<BR> E. काञ्चन, and सन्धि alliance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=171-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काञ्चनाल|कांचनाल|कांचनालः|काञ्चनालः
काञ्चनाल m. (-लः) Mountain ebony, (Bauhinia variegata, &c.)<BR> E. काञ्चन<BR>gold, and अल् to be able or like; some copies read काञ्चनार.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=171-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काञ्चनीया
काञ्चनीया f. (-या) A yellow pigment, commonly Gorochana.<BR> E. काचि to<BR>shine, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=171-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काञ्चि|कांचि|कांचिः|काञ्चिः
काञ्चि f. (-ञ्चिः) See काञ्ची.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=171-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काञ्चिक|कांचिकं|काञ्चिकं
काञ्चिक n. (-कं) Sour gruel: see काञ्जिक<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=171-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काञ्ची|कांची
काञ्ची f. (-ञ्ची)<BR>	 1. A woman's zone or girdle.<BR>	 2. The name of an ancient<BR>city situated in the peninsula, and one of the seven sacred cities<BR>of the Hindus.<BR>	 3. A plant, (Abrus precatorius:) see गुञ्जा.<BR> E. कचि<BR>to bind or shine, इन् or ङीष् affixes; whence also काञ्चि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=171-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काञ्चीपद|कांचीपद|काञ्चीपदं
काञ्चीपद n. (-दं) Mons veneris, the public region.<BR> E. काञ्ची the zone,<BR>and पद place, site.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=171-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काञ्जिक|कांजिक|कांजिकं|काञ्जिकं
काञ्जिक nf. (-कः-का) Sour gruel, the water of boiled rice in a state of<BR>spontaneous fermentation.<BR> E. क water, अञ्ज् to go, &c. and affix<BR>इक; also the vowel being lengthened काञ्चीक, or without the final,<BR>काञ्ची.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=171-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काठ|काठः
काठ m. (-ठः) A stone, a rock.<BR> E. कठ् to be hard, &c. अण् affix; also<BR>with कन् added, काठक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=171-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काठक
काठक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) According to the Katha portion of the Vedas.<BR>E. कठ, and वुञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=171-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काठिन|काठिनं|काठिनः
काठिन m. (-नः) The date fruit.<BR>	 n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Hardness.<BR>	 2. Sternness. E.<BR>कठिन, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=171-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काठिन्य|काठिन्यं
काठिन्य n. (-न्यं)<BR>	 1. Hardness.<BR>	 2. Difficulty, obscurity.<BR>	 3. Sternness,<BR>severity.<BR> E. कठिन hard, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=171-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काण|काणः
काण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) One-eyed, monoculous.<BR>	 m. (-णः) A crow<BR> E. कण्<BR>to sound, &c. अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=171-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काणूक|काणूकः
काणूक m. (-कः) A crow.<BR> E. कण् to sound, &c. and ऊकन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=171-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काणेय|काणेयः
काणेय mfn. (-यः-यी-यं) One-eyed.<BR> E. काण, and ढक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=171-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काणेर|काणेरः
काणेर mfn. (-रः-री-रं) One-eyed.<BR> E. काण, and ढ्रक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=171-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काण्ड|कांड|कांडं|काण्डं|कांडः|काण्डः
काण्ड mn. (-ण्डः-ण्डं)<BR>	 1. A stalk or stem.<BR>	 2. The part of the trunk of a<BR>tree whence the branches proceed.<BR>	 3. A cluster, a clump.<BR>	 4. An<BR>arrow.<BR>	 5. Opportunity, season.<BR>	 6. Water.<BR>	 7. A kind of reed,<BR>(Saccharum sara.)<BR>	 8. A multitude, a heap, a quantity.<BR>	 9. A horse.<BR>10. A chapter, a section.<BR>	 11. The part in a sacrifice appropriated<BR>to different objects, as the gods or manes.<BR>	 12. A long bone, a<BR>bone of the extremities.<BR>	 13. Praise, flattery.<BR>	 14. Private, privacy.<BR>15. Low, vile, bad.<BR>	 16. Sinful, wicked.<BR> E. कन् to shine, &c. ड<BR>Uṇādi affix, and the radical vowel made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=171-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काण्डकाण्डक|काण्डकाण्डकः
काण्डकाण्डक m. (-कः) A species of grass.<BR> E. काण्ड repeated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=171-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काण्डकार|कांडकार|काण्डकारं|काण्डकारः
काण्डकार n. (-रं) The betel-nut, the fruit of the areca.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=171-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काण्डगोचर|कांडगोचर|काण्डगोचरः
काण्डगोचर m. (-रः) An iron-arrow.<BR> E. काण्ड a stem or stalk, and गोचर an<BR>object of sense; it is fired from a stock like the arrow of the cross<BR>bow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=171-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काण्डणी
काण्डणी f. (-णी) A plant, commonly Ramaduti: see सूक्ष्मपर्णी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=171-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काण्डतिक्तक|काण्डतिक्तकः
काण्डतिक्तक m. (-कः) A kind of gentian, (Gentiana cherayta, Rox.) E.<BR>काण्ड the stem, and तिक्त sharp, bitter, कन् added to this and similar<BR>compounds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=171-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काण्डनील|काण्डनीलः
काण्डनील m. (-लः) A plant with an astringent bark, commonly Lodh.<BR>E. काण्ड, and नील blue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=171-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काण्डपट|कांडपट|काण्डपटः
काण्डपट m. (-टः) An outer tent, a screen surrounding a tent.<BR> E. काण्ड a<BR>stem, &c. and पट a cloth; also with कन् added काण्डपटकः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=171-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काण्डपुष्प|काण्डपुष्पं
काण्डपुष्प n. (-ष्पं) A small fragrant flower, commonly Dona, (Artemisia.)<BR>E. काण्ड the stem, and पुष्प flower; flowering from the stalk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=171-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काण्डपृष्ठ|कांडपृष्ठ|काण्डपृष्ठं|काण्डपृष्ठः
काण्डपृष्ठ mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठा-ष्ठं) Of the military profession, a soldier.<BR>	 m. (-ष्ठः)<BR>1. The husband of a Vaiśya female.<BR>	 2. An adopted or any other<BR>than the natural son.<BR>	 n. (-ष्ठं) The bow of KĀMA^1.<BR> E. काण्ड an arrow,<BR>and पृष्ठ the back: see काण्डस्पृष्ट.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20260617. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/264.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=171-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काण्डभग्न
काण्डभग्न n. (-ग्नं) A fracture of either of the extremities.<BR> E. काण्ड, and भग्न breaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=171-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काण्डरुहा
काण्डरुहा f. (-हा) A medicinal plant: see कटुकी.<BR> E. काण्ड the stem of a<BR>tree, and रुहा what ascends; hence it appears to be a creeper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=171-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काण्डर्षि|काण्डर्षिः
काण्डर्षि m. (-र्षिः) Ṛṣi or divine saint of a peculiar class; Jaimini and<BR>others who teach a particular Kanda or section of Vedas.<BR> E. काण्ड<BR>a section, and ऋषि a saint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=171-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काण्डवत्|कांडवत्|काण्डवन्त्
काण्डवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Armed with an arrow, an archer.<BR> E. काण्ड an<BR>arrow, and मतुप् poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=171-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काण्डसन्धि|कांडसंधि|काण्डसंधि|काण्डसन्धिः
काण्डसन्धि m. (-न्धिः) A knot, a joint in the stem of a tree, &c.<BR> E. काण्ड a<BR>stem, and सन्धि union.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=171-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काण्डस्पृष्ट|कांडस्पृष्ट|काण्डस्पृष्टः
काण्डस्पृष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं) Of the military profession, living by arms, a<BR>soldier.<BR> E. काण्ड an arrow, &c. स्पृश् to touch, and क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=171-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काण्डहीन|काण्डहीनं
काण्डहीन n. (-नं) A fragrant grass, a sort of cyperus: see भद्रमुस्तक. E.<BR>काण्ड a stem, and हीन deprived.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=171-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काण्डीर|कांडीर|कांडीरः|काण्डीरः
काण्डीर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Armed with an arrow, an archer.<BR>	 m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A<BR>creeping plant, commonly Kanda Bel, (Momordica charantia.)<BR>	 2.<BR>A plant, (Achyranthes aspera.)<BR>	 f. (-रा) Bengal madder, (Rubia<BR>manjith:) see मञ्जिष्ठा.<BR> E. काण्ड an arrow, a stem, &c. and ईरच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=171-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काण्डेक्षु|काण्डेक्षुः
काण्डेक्षु m. (-क्षुः)<BR>	 1. A plant, (Barleria longifolia.)<BR>	 2. A kind of reed,<BR>(Saccharum spontaneum:) see काश.<BR> E. काण्ड, and इक्षु sugar-cane;<BR>having a similar stem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=171-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कातर|कातरः
कातर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>	 1. Confused, perplexed, disordered.<BR>	 2. Timid,<BR>gentle.<BR>	 m. (-रः) A large kind of fish, commonly Katala (Cyprinus<BR>catla, HAM.)<BR> E. का a little or badly, and तर what crosses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=171-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कातरता
कातरता f. (-ता) Timidity, agitation.<BR> E. तल् added to कातर; also with त्व,<BR>कातरत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=171-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कातल|कातलः
कातल m. (-लः) The name of a fish, commonly Katala, (Cyprinus catla,<BR>HAM.) E. See कातर, र changed to ल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=171-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कातीय|कातीयः
कातीय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. A name of KATYAYANA.<BR>	 2. A pupil of the same. E.<BR>कात्यायन with फक् affix and the middle syllable dropped; also कात्या-<BR>यनीय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=171-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कात्त्रयक
कात्त्रयक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Produced from any bad triad.<BR> E. कत्त्रय, and ढकञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=171-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कात्य|कात्यः
कात्य m. (-त्यः) The name of a saint; also कात्यायन.<BR> E. कत a proper name,<BR>and यञ् affix implying descent or lineage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=171-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कात्यायन|कात्यायनः
कात्यायन m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. The name of a celebrated lawgiver and divine<BR>sage.<BR>	 2. An appellation of VARARUCHI a poet.<BR> E. कात्य, and फक्<BR>pleonastic affix.<BR>	 f. (-नी)<BR>	 1. A name of DURGĀ.<BR>	 2. A middle-aged<BR>widow.<BR> E. ङीष् added to कात्यायन; the daughter of the saint KATYA-<BR>YANA, (DURGĀ,) or resembling the wife of a sage in dress and aus-<BR>terity, (the widow.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=171-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कात्यायनीय|कात्यायनीयः
कात्यायनीय m. (-यः) A pupil of KATYAYANA.<BR> E. कात्यायन, and फक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=171-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काथिक|काथिकः
काथिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Belonging to a story, told in it, &c.<BR>	 m. (-कः)<BR>A narrator.<BR> E. कथा, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=171-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कादम्ब|कादंब|कादंबः|कादम्बः
कादम्ब n. (-म्बं)<BR>	 1. A tree, (Nauclea cadamba.)<BR>	 2. A drake, or, accord-<BR>ing to some, a teal.<BR>	 3. An arrow.<BR>	 f. (-म्बा) A plant, commonly<BR>Mundiri: see कदम्बपुष्प.<BR> E. अण् added to कदम्ब.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=171-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कादम्बक|कादंबकः|कादम्बकः
कादम्बक m. (-कः) An arrow.<BR> E. कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=171-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कादम्बर|कादंबर|कादंबरं|कादम्बरं|कादम्बरः
कादम्बर n. (-रं) The surface or skim of coagulated milk.<BR>	 m. (-रः) A<BR>spirituous liquor distilled from the flowers of the Kadamba.<BR>	 f.<BR>(-री)<BR>	 1. Wine, spirituous liquor in general.<BR>	 2. A name of SARAS-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=172-a" target="_blank">Page172-a+ 60</a>]<BR>WATI.<BR>	 3. The female Koil or Indian cuckoo.<BR>	 4. The female of an-<BR>other bird, (Turdus salica, BUCH.)<BR> E. कदम्ब the Kadamba flower, र<BR>what gains or gets, from रा, affix ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=171-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कादम्बरीवीज|कादम्बरीवीजं
कादम्बरीवीज n. (-जं) Ferment, yeast, whatever occasions fermentation.<BR>E. कादम्बरी, and वीज seed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=172-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कादम्बर्य्य|कादम्बर्य|कादम्बर्य्यः
कादम्बर्य्य m. (-र्य्यः) The Kadamba tree: see कादम्ब.<BR> E. कादम्बरी a spirit,<BR>and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=172-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कादम्बिनी|कादंबिनी
कादम्बिनी f. (-नी) A long line of clouds.<BR> E. कादम्ब the Kadamba flower,<BR>इनि and ङीप् affixes, implying a multitude; the clouds being com<BR>pared with the large white flowers of the Nauclea cadamba.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=172-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कादाचित्क|कादाचित्कं
कादाचित्क mfn. (-त्कः-त्की-त्कं) Produced sometimes, occasional, inciden-<BR>tal.<BR> E. कदाचित् sometimes, with कन् added, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=172-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काद्रवेय|काद्रवेयः
काद्रवेय m. (-यः) A Naga or serpent of the race that is supposed to people<BR>the lower regions.<BR> E. कद्रु the mother of these beings, and ढक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=172-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कानक|कानकं
कानक n. (-कं) The seed of the croton.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=172-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कानन|काननं
कानन nf. (-नं-नी)<BR>	 1. A forest, a grove.<BR>	 2. The face of BRAHMĀ.<BR>	 3. A<BR>house.<BR> E. कनि to shine, in the causal form, and ल्युट् affix, or क<BR>BRAHMĀ, and आनन a face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=172-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काननारि|काननारिः
काननारि m. (-रिः) The Śami or Śain tree, (Mimosa albida:) see समी.<BR>E. कानन, and अरि enemy; injurious to a wood; being a thorny tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=172-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कानीन|कानीनः
कानीन mf. (-नः-नी) The son or daughter of a young and unmarried<BR>woman.<BR>	 m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. A name of VYASA.<BR>	 2. Also of KARṆA, (being<BR>both born of mothers who were unmarried.)<BR> E. कन्या a virgin or<BR>young girl, changed to कनीन् and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=172-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कान्त|कांत|कान्तं|कान्तः
कान्त mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं)<BR>	 1. Pleasing, agreeable.<BR>	 2. Lovely, beautiful.<BR>3. Dear, beloved.<BR>	 m. (-न्तः)<BR>	 1. A name of KṚṢṆA.<BR>	 2. The moon.<BR>3. A husband.<BR>	 4. Spring.<BR>	 5. A precious stone; in which case it is<BR>compounded with सूर्य्य, चन्द्र or अयस्, as सूर्य्यकान्त a crystal lens, &c.<BR>f. (-न्ता)<BR>	 1. A wife, a mistress, any beloved or lovely woman.<BR>2. A plant, commonly Priyangu: see प्रियङ्गु.<BR>	 3. A grass, (Cyperus<BR>pertenuis.)<BR>	 n. (-न्तं)<BR>	 1. Iron.<BR>	 2. Saffron.<BR> E. कम् to desire, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=172-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कान्तता
कान्तता f. (-ता) Loveliness, beauty, splendor.<BR> E. कान्त pleasing, &c. तल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=172-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कान्तपक्षिन्|कांतपक्षिन्
कान्तपक्षिन् m. (-क्षी) A peacock.<BR> E. कान्त beautiful, पक्षिन् a bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=172-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कान्तपुष्प|कान्तपुष्पः
कान्तपुष्प m. (-ष्पः) Mountain ebony, &c. (Bauhinia variegata.)<BR> E. कान्त<BR>and पुष्प flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=172-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कान्तलक|कान्तलकः
कान्तलक m. (-कः) A tree, the wood of which something resembles<BR>mahogany, commonly Toon, (Cedrela tunna, Rox.)<BR> E. कान्त beauty,<BR>and र what gives, कन् added, and र changed to ल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=172-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कान्ताङ्घ्रिदोहद|कांतांघ्रिदोहद|कान्ताङ्घ्रिदोहदः
कान्ताङ्घ्रिदोहद m. (-दः) A tree, commonly Asoka, (Jonesia asoca.)<BR>E. कान्ता a woman, अङ्घ्रि a foot, and दोहद desire; the tree being<BR>supposed to blossom upon coming in contact with the foot of a<BR>handsome female.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=172-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कान्ताचरणदोहद|कान्ताचरणदोहदः
कान्ताचरणदोहद m. (-दः) The tree Asoka: see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=172-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कान्तायस|कांतायस|कान्तायसं
कान्तायस n. (-सं) Iron-stone: see अयस्कान्त.<BR> E. कान्त, and अयस् iron, अण् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=172-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कान्तार|कांतार|कांतारं|कान्तारं|कांतारः|कान्तारः
कान्तार mn. (-रः-रं)<BR>	 1. A bad or difficult road.<BR>	 2. A wood, a forest.<BR>	 3.<BR>A hole, a cavity.<BR>	 m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A red variety of the sugar-cane.<BR>2. A bamboo.<BR>	 3. Mountain ebony.<BR>	 n. (-रं)<BR>	 1. A symptom or sympto-<BR>matic disease.<BR>	 2. A lotus.<BR>	 f. (-री) A sort of sugar-cane.<BR> E. कान् for<BR>कञ्चित् any one, here meaning no one, तृ to go, in the causal,<BR>form, अच् affix; allowing none to pass; or क pleasure, &c. अन्त<BR>end, ऋ to go, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=172-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कान्तारक|कांतारकः|कान्तारकः
कान्तारक m. (-कः) A sort of sugar-cane.<BR> E. कान्त good, excellent (juice,)<BR>ऋ to go, to gain, अण् and कन् affixes: see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=172-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कान्तारग
कान्तारग mfn. (-गः-गा-गं) Who or what goes into or in a wood.<BR> E. कान्तार,<BR>and ग who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=172-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कान्ति|कांति|कांतिः|कान्तिः
कान्ति f. (-न्तिः)<BR>	 1. Beauty, splendor, light.<BR>	 2. Female beauty.<BR>	 3. Wish,<BR>desire.<BR>	 4. A lovely or desirable woman.<BR>	 5. Personal decoration or<BR>embellishment.<BR> E. कम् to desire or be desired, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=172-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कान्तिकर|कांतिकर
कान्तिकर mfn. (-रः-री-रं) Beautifying, illumining, making handsome or<BR>splendid.<BR> E. कान्ति, and कर what makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=172-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कान्तिद|कांतिद|कान्तिदं
कान्तिद mfn. (-दः-दा-दं) Beautifying, illuminating.<BR>	 n. (-दं) Bile, the<BR>bilious humour.<BR> E. कान्ति light, splendor, &c. and द what gives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=172-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कान्तिदायक|कांतिदायक|कान्तिदायकं
कान्तिदायक mfn. (-यकः-यिका-यकं) Beautifying, adorning.<BR>	 n. (-कं) A kind<BR>of Curcuma, from the root of which a yellow die is prepared,<BR>(C. Zanthorhiza.)<BR> E. कान्ति beauty, &c. दायक distributor, giver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=172-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कान्तिभृत्|कांतिभृत्
कान्तिभृत् mfn. (-भृत्)<BR>	 1. Handsome, beautiful.<BR>	 2. Bright, shining. E.<BR>कान्ति, and भृत् what has.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=172-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कान्तिमत्|कांतिमत्|कान्तिमन्त्
कान्तिमत् mfn. (-मान्-मती-मत्)<BR>	 1. Splendid.<BR>	 2. Beautiful.<BR> E. कान्ति, and<BR>मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=172-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कान्तिहर
कान्तिहर mfn. (-रः-री-रं) Dimming, dulling, making dull or ugly. E.<BR>कान्ति, and हर what removes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=172-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कान्दव|कांदव|कांदवं
कान्दव mfn. (-वः-वी-वं) Roasted or baked, (in an iron pan or oven, as<BR>bread, cakes, &c.)<BR> E. कन्दु, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=172-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कान्दविक|कांदविक|कांदविकः|कान्दविकः
कान्दविक m. (-कः) A baker.<BR> E. कान्दव baked bread, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=172-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कान्दिशीक|कांदिशीक|कान्दिशीकः
कान्दिशीक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Flying, running away, put to flight.<BR> E. कदि<BR>to fear, घञ् and इन् affixed, कन्दि; शीक् to go, to ooze. घञ् affix,<BR>कन्दिशीक; and again, अण् affix, कान्दिशीक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=172-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कान्यकुब्ज|कान्यकुब्जं|कान्यकुब्जः
कान्यकुब्ज m. (-ब्जः) A country, the modern Konouj; also कन्याकुब्ज.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=172-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कान्यजा
कान्यजा f. (-जा) A kind of perfume, commonly Nali.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=172-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कापटिक|कापटिकः
कापटिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>	 1. Wicked, bad, perverse.<BR>	 2. Fraudulent, dis-<BR>honest.<BR>	 m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A student, a scholar.<BR>	 2. A flatterer, a para-<BR>site.<BR> E. कपट fraud, &c. ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=172-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कापट्य|कापट्यं
कापट्य n. (-ट्यं) Wickedness, fraud, dishonesty.<BR> E. कपट, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=172-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कापथ|कापथः
कापथ m. (-थः) A bad road.<BR> E. का for कु bad, vile, and पथिन् a road.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=172-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कापाल|कापालं|कापालः
कापाल mfn. (-लः-ली-लं) Cranial, relating to the skull.<BR>	 m. (-लः) A kind<BR>of cucumber, (Cucumis utilatissimus.)<BR>	 n. (-लं) A sort of leprosy.<BR>E. कपाल, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=172-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कापालिक|कापालिकः
कापालिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Relating or belonging to the skull.<BR>	 m. (-कः)<BR>A worshipper of ŚIVA of the left-hand order, characterised by<BR>carrying a half of the skull as a cup, drinking spirituous liquors,<BR>&c.<BR> E. कपाल, and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=172-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कापिल|कापिलः
कापिल mfn. (-लः-ली-लं) Of a tawny colour.<BR>	 m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. A follower of<BR>the Sankhya system of philosophy.<BR> E. कपिल the founder of the<BR>school, and अण् affix.<BR>	 2. Tawny, (the colour.)<BR> E. अण् pleonastic<BR>added to कपिल, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=172-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कापिश|कापिशं
कापिश n. (-शं) A spirituous liquor, wine.<BR>	 f. (-शी) A country.<BR> E. कपिश<BR>brown, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=172-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कापिशायन|कापिशायनं
कापिशायन m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. A deity.<BR>	 2. A kind of vinous liquor.<BR>	 n. (-नं)<BR>Honey.<BR>	 f. (-नी) A grape.<BR> E. कपिश brown, or कापिशी a country, and<BR>ष्फक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=172-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कापिशेय|कापिशेयः
कापिशेय m. (-यः) A Pisacha, an imp or goblin.<BR> E. कपिश, and ढक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=172-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कापुरुष|कापुरुषः
कापुरुष m. (-षः) A mean contemptible man, a coward, a wretch.<BR> E. का<BR>for कु bad, vile, पुरुष a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=172-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कापुरुषत्व
कापुरुषत्व n. (-त्वं) Meanness, cowardliness.<BR> E. त्व added to the preced-<BR>ing: also with तल्, कापुरुषता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=172-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कापेय|कापेयं|कापेयः
कापेय mfn. (-यः-यी-यं) Belonging to or relating to a monkey.<BR> E. कपि a<BR>monkey, and ढक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=172-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कापोत|कापोतं|कापोतः
कापोत mfn. (-तः-ती-तं) Of a dirty white colour.<BR>	 m. (-तः)<BR>	 1. Natron,<BR>fossile alkali.<BR>	 2. Antimony, considered as a collyrium or applica-<BR>tion to the eyes.<BR>	 3. A pale or dirty white colour.<BR>	 n. (-तं) A flock<BR>of pigeons,<BR> E. कपोत a pigeon, &c. अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=172-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कापोताञ्जन|कापोतांजन|कापोताञ्जनं
कापोताञ्जन n. (-नं) Antimony, especially considered as a collyrium. E.<BR>कापोत a pigeon, and अञ्जन a collyrium.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=172-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काप्यकर|काप्यकरः
काप्यकर m. (-रः) A penitent, one who acknowledges his faults.<BR>E. का for कु bad, आप्य having obtained, and कर who does; from कृ.<BR>and अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=172-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काप्यकार|काप्यकारः
काप्यकार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Avowal or confession of sin.<BR>	 2. A penitent, one<BR>who confesses a crime. E. As before, affix अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=172-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काफल|काफलः
काफल m. (-लः) A bitter seed; see कट्फल.<BR> E. का bad, and फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=172-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काम|कामं|कामः
काम m. (-मः)<BR>	 1. KĀMA^1 the Hindu Cupid or deity of love.<BR>	 2. Wish,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=173-a" target="_blank">Page173-a+ 60</a>]<BR>desire.<BR>	 3. BALARĀMA the brother of KṚṢṆA.<BR>	 4. The mango tree.<BR>f. (-मा) Love, desire.<BR>	 n. (-मं)<BR>	 1. Semen virile.<BR>	 2. An object of desire.<BR>3. Willingly, voluntarily.<BR>	 4. A particle of assent or agreement: see<BR>कामम्. ind. (in composition.) Following one's own desire, as कामवाद<BR>speaking what one lists; कामभक्ष eating whatever one likes; कामचार<BR>doing whatever one chuses; in law, a child previous to the imposi-<BR>tion of the characteristic cord is all these.<BR> E. कम् to desire, घञ् aff.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20260617. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/264.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=172-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामकला
कामकला f. (-ला) RATI the wife of KĀMA^1.<BR> E. काम, and कला a part.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20260617. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/264.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=173-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामकामिन्
कामकामिन् mfn. (-मी-मिनी-मि) Following the dictates of passion of<BR>desire.<BR> E. काम, and कामिन् desirous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=173-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामकार|कामकारः
कामकार mfn. (-रः-री-रं) Following one's inclinations.<BR>	 m. (-रः) Desire,<BR>the operation or influence of desire.<BR> E. काम, and कार act, who acts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=173-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामकारतस्
कामकारतस् ind. According to one's desires, following one's inclinations,<BR>indulging desire.<BR> E. कामकार, and तसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=173-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामकूट|कामकूटः
कामकूट m. (-टः)<BR>	 1. The paramour of a harlot, a cully.<BR>	 2. Wanton cares-<BR>ses, harlotry.<BR> E. काम desire, and कूट a peak or summit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=173-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामकेलि|कामकेलिः
कामकेलि mfn. (-लिः-लिः-लि) Libidinous, wanton.<BR>	 m. (-लिः)<BR>	 1. Copulation.<BR>2. Amorous sport.<BR> E. काम love, desire, केलि play, sport.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=173-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामग
कामग mfn. (-गः-गा-गं) Acting as one pleases.<BR> E. काम, and ग who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=173-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामगामिन्
कामगामिन् mfn. (-मी-मिनी-मि) Going as one lists.<BR> E. काम the wish, and<BR>गामिन् who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=173-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामगुण|कामगुणः
कामगुण m. (-णः)<BR>	 1. Passion, affection.<BR>	 2. An object of sense.<BR>	 3. Com-<BR>pletion, satiety, perfect enjoyment.<BR> E. काम desire, and गुण a quality<BR>or property.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=173-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामङ्गामिन्|कामंगामिन्
कामङ्गामिन् mfn. (-मी-मिनी-मि) Going as one lists.<BR> E. कामम् at will, and<BR>गामिन् who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=173-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामचार|कामचारः
कामचार mfn. (-रः-री-रं) Following one's own pleasure, unchecked, un-<BR>restrained.<BR>	 m. (-रः) Following one's own wishes or pleasure,<BR>sensuality, selfishness.<BR> E. काम, and चार practice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=173-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामचारतस्
कामचारतस् ind. According to one's own inclinations.<BR> E. तसि added to the<BR>last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=173-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामचारिन्
कामचारिन् mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>	 1. Desirous, libidinous.<BR>	 2. Self-willed.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-री)<BR>	 1. A sparrow.<BR>	 2. A name of GARUḌA the bird of VIṢṆU. E.<BR>काम desire, and चारिन् who goes, from चर् with णिनि affix; also<BR>with ण्बुल् affix, कामचारक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=173-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामज|कामजः
कामज mfn. (-जः-जा-जं) Produced or caused by passion or desire.<BR>	 m. (-जः)<BR>The son of KĀMA^1.<BR> E. काम, and ज born: also कामजनित, कामोत्पन्न, &c.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20260617. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/264.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=173-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामजान|कामजानः
कामजान m. (-नः) The Kokila or Indian cuckoo.<BR> E. काम, and<BR>जान what produces, from जन् in the causal form, and घञ् affix;<BR>also read कामजनि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=173-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामजाल
कामजाल m. (-लः) See कामताल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=173-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामठ
कामठ m. (-ठः) A tortoise.<BR> E. कमठ the same, अण् pleonasm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=173-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामतस्
कामतस् ind.<BR>	 1. Willingly, consentingly.<BR>	 2. Passionately.<BR> E. काम, and तसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=173-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामताल|कामतालः
कामताल m. (-लः) The Kokila, or Koil, the Inidian cuckoo.<BR> E. काम,<BR>and ताल a musical strain; the song of the Koil being poetically<BR>considered as an incentive to love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=173-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामद|कामदः
कामद mfn. (-दः-दा-दं) Giving what is wished, granting one's desires.<BR>f. (-दा) A fabulous cow, the cow of plenty<BR> E. काम desire, and द<BR>what gives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=173-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामदुघा
कामदुघा f. (-घा) The cow of plenty.<BR> E. काम, and दुह् to yield milk, affix कप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=173-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामदुह्
कामदुह् f. (-धुक्)<BR>	 1. The cow of plenty.<BR> E. काम, and दुह् to give<BR>milk, क्विप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=173-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामदूती
कामदूती f. (-ती)<BR>	 1. Trumpet flower, (Bignonia suave-olens.)<BR>	 2. The<BR>female koil.<BR> E. काम desire, and दूती a messenger; also कामदूति and<BR>कामदूतिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=173-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामध्वंसिन्
कामध्वंसिन् m. (-सी) A name of ŚIVA.<BR> E. काम CUPID, and ध्वंसिन् an enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=173-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामन|कामनः
कामन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Lustful, libidinous, desirous.<BR>	 f. (-ना) Wish,<BR>desire.<BR> E. कम् to desire, and युच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=173-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामन्धमिन्|कामंधमिन्
कामन्धमिन् m. (-मी) A brazier.<BR> E. काम willingly, ध्मा to blow, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=173-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामपत्नी
कामपत्नी f. (-त्नी) A name of RATI.<BR> E. काम KANDARPA, and पत्नी a wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=173-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामपाल|कामपालः
कामपाल m. (-लः) A name of BALARĀMA, the brother of KṚṢṆA. E.<BR>काम KĀMA^1, and पाल who cherishes; being by one legend the pa-<BR>ternal uncle of that deity.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20260617. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/264.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=173-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामप्रद|कामप्रदः
कामप्रद mfn. (-दः-दा-दं) Granting what is desired.<BR> E. काम, and प्रद what yields.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=173-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामबद्ध
कामबद्ध mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं) Bound by love.<BR>	 n. (-द्धं) A wood.<BR> E. काम, and<BR>बद्ध tied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=173-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामभक्ष
कामभक्ष mfn. (-क्षः-क्षा-क्षं) Eating anything or every thing.<BR> E. काम, and<BR>भक्ष who eats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=173-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामभक्ष्य
कामभक्ष्य mfn. (-क्ष्यः-क्ष्या-क्ष्यं) Eating anything.<BR> E. काम, and भक्ष्य to be eaten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=173-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामम्
कामम् ind. A particle, 1. Of reluctant assent, (well, very well.)<BR>	 2. Of<BR>assent, (willingly, readily.)<BR>	 3. Of agreement, (very well, so be it.)<BR>	 4.<BR>Of contempt or invidious remark.<BR>	 5. Agreeably to desire, follow-<BR>ing the inclination: see काम.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=173-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काममह|काममहः
काममह m. (-हः) The day of full moon in the month Chaitra, (March-<BR>April.)<BR> E. काम the deity, and मह worship; a festival in honour of<BR>KĀMA^1.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20260617. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/264.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=173-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काममालिन्
काममालिन् m. (-ली) A name of GANESA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=173-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामयितृ
कामयितृ mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ) Libidinous, lustful, desirous.<BR> E. कम् to desire,<BR>in the causal form, and तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=173-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामरूप|कामरूपः
कामरूप mfn. (-पः-पी-पं)<BR>	 1. Pleasing, beautiful.<BR>	 2. Taking any or every<BR>shape at will.<BR>	 m. (-पः) A district lying east of Bengal, the west-<BR>ern portion of Asam.<BR> E. काम desire, and रूप form or figure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=173-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामरूपिन्
कामरूपिन् mfn. (-पी-पिणी-पि)<BR>	 1. Pleasing, beautiful.<BR>	 2. Taking any<BR>shape at will.<BR>	 m. (-पी)<BR>	 1. A Vidyadhara, a kind of subordinate<BR>deity.<BR>	 2. A pole cat.<BR> E. काम desire, will, रूप form, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=173-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामरेखा
कामरेखा f. (-खा) A harlot, a courtezan.<BR> E. काम desire, and रेखा a line.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=173-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामल|कामलः
कामल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Libidinous, cupidinous.<BR>	 mf. (-लः-ला) A com-<BR>plaint, jaundice, excessive secretion or obstruction of bile.<BR>	 m. (-लः)<BR>1. Spring.<BR>	 2. A dry and sterile soil.<BR> E. काम desire, ला to bring,<BR>ड aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=173-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामलता
कामलता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Membrum virile.<BR>	 2. A plant, (Ipomæa quamoclit.) E.<BR>काम, and लता creeper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=173-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामलोल
कामलोल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Overcome with desire or passion.<BR> E. काम, and<BR>लोल agitated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=173-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामवल्लभ|कामवल्लभः
कामवल्लभ m. (-भः)<BR>	 1. The mango tree.<BR>	 2. Spring.<BR>	 f. (-भा) Moonlight. E.<BR>काम, and वल्लभ friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=173-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामवाद
कामवाद mfn. (-दः-दा-दं) Saying anything at pleasure.<BR> E. काम, and वाद speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=173-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामविहन्तृ|कामविहंतृ
कामविहन्तृ mfn. (-न्ता-न्त्री-न्तृ) Disappointing, preventing.<BR> E. काम, and विहन्तृ<BR>who destroys.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=173-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामवृत्त
कामवृत्त mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं) Licentious, dissipated, debauched.<BR> E. काम, and<BR>वृत्त practising.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=173-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामवृद्धि|कामवृद्धिः
कामवृद्धि f. (-द्धिः)<BR>	 1. A shrub, commonly Kamaja, of supposed aphro-<BR>disial properties.<BR>	 2. Increase of passion or desire.<BR> E. काम, and वृद्धि<BR>increase.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=173-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामवृन्ता
कामवृन्ता f. (-न्ता) Trumpet flower, (Bignonia suave-olens,)<BR> E. काम, and<BR>वृन्ता a flower-stalk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=173-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामशर|कामशरः
कामशर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. The shaft of KĀMADEVA.<BR>	 2. The mango.<BR> E. काम,<BR>and शर an arrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=173-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामसंयोग|कामसंयोगः
कामसंयोग m. (-गः) Attainment of desired objects.<BR> E. काम, and संयोग union.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=173-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामसख|कामसखः
कामसख m. (-खः)<BR>	 1. Spring.<BR>	 2. The mango.<BR> E. काम, and सखि a friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=173-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामसुत|कामसुतः
कामसुत m. (-तः) A name of ANIRUDDHA.<BR> E. काम, and सुत a son; also<BR>similar compounds, as कामपुत्र, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=173-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामहैतुक
कामहैतुक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Of one's own accord.<BR> E. काम, and हेतु cause, वुञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=173-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामाग्नि|कामाग्निः
कामाग्नि m. (-ग्निः) Passion, lust, violent desire.<BR> E. काम, and अग्नि fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=173-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामाङ्कुश|कामांकुश|कामाङ्कुशः
कामाङ्कुश m. (-शः)<BR>	 1. A finger-nail.<BR>	 2. Membrum virile.<BR> E. काम, and अङ्कुश<BR>shoot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=173-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामाङ्ग|कामांग|कामाङ्गः
कामाङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः) The mango tree, (Mangifera Indica.)<BR> E. काम, and अङ्ग<BR>the body or form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=173-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामातुर|कामातुरः
कामातुर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) In love, affected by love or desire.<BR> E. काम, and<BR>आतुर diseased.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=173-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामात्मन्
कामात्मन् mfn. (-त्मा-त्मा-त्म)<BR>	 1. Licentious, libidinous.<BR>	 2. Desiring, wishing<BR>for.<BR> E. काम, and आत्मन् self.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=174-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामात्मता
कामात्मता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Passion, lust.<BR>	 2. Wish, desire.<BR> E. कामात्म, and तल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=174-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामाधिष्ठित
कामाधिष्ठित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Influenced or overcome by love.<BR> E. काम, and<BR>अधिष्ठित placed over.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=174-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामाधिकार|कामाधिकारः
कामाधिकार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. The influence of passion or desire.<BR>	 2. The as-<BR>piration of the will.<BR>	 3. The part of the Śāstra which relates to<BR>human wishes or desires.<BR> E. काम, and अधिकार superintendence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=174-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामानल|कामानलः
कामानल m. (-लः) Passion, lust, violent desire.<BR> E. काम, and अनल fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=174-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामान्ध|कामांध|कामान्धः
कामान्ध m. (-न्धः) The Kokila or indian cuckoo.<BR> E. काम, and अन्ध blind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=174-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामायुध|कामायुधः
कामायुध n. (-धं) An arrow of KĀMADEVA.<BR>	 m. (-धः)<BR>	 1. Membrum virile.<BR>	 2.<BR>The mango tree.<BR> E. काम, and आयुध a weapon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=174-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामायुस्
कामायुस् m. (-युः) Name of GARUḌA the bird of VIṢṆU.<BR> E. काम, and<BR>आयुस् life; existing at will.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=174-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामारण्य|कामारण्यं
कामारण्य n. (-ण्यं) A handsome grove or wood.<BR> E. काम desirable, and अरण्य<BR>a forest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=174-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामारि|कामारिः
कामारि m. (-रिः) A mineral substance used in medicine, a sort of<BR>pyrites: see विट्माक्षिक.<BR> E. काम love, and अरि an enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=174-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामार्त्त|कामार्त|कामार्त्तः
कामार्त्त mfn. (-र्त्तः-र्त्ता-र्त्तं) In love, afflicted by love or passion.<BR> E. काम,<BR>and आर्त्त pained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=174-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामालु|कामालुः
कामालु m. (-लुः) A red sort of mountain ebony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=174-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामावसाय|कामावसायः
कामावसाय m. (-यः) Coldness, stoicism, mortification or suppression of<BR>the passions.<BR> E. काम, and अवसाय destruction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=174-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामावसायिता
कामावसायिता f. (-ता) The power of suppressing desire, self-denial or<BR>mortification.<BR> E. कामावसायिन्, and तल् affix, or with त्व, कामावसायित्व<BR>n. (-त्वं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=174-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामावसायितृ
कामावसायितृ mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ) Who or what suppresses or destroys<BR>passion or desire.<BR> E. काम, and अवसायितृ destroying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=174-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामावसायिन्
कामावसायिन् mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि) Destructive of love or desire, one who<BR>suppresses desire, &c.<BR> E. कामावसाय, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=174-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामासक्त
कामासक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं) Impassioned, in love, overcome with desire or<BR>passion.<BR> E. काम, and आसक्त attached.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=174-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामासक्ति
कामासक्ति f. (-क्तिः) Passion, desire.<BR> E. काम, and आसक्ति attachment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=174-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामि|कामिः
कामि m. (-मिः) A libidinous man, a lecher.<BR>	 f. (-मिः) A name of RATI<BR>the wife of KĀMA^1.<BR> E. कम् to desire, कि affix; the pen. becomes<BR>long.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20260617. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/264.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=174-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामिक|कामिकः
कामिक m. (-कः) A kind of wild duck.<BR> E. कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=174-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामिता
कामिता f. (-ता) Love, desire.<BR> E. कामिन्, and तल् affix; also with त्व<BR>कामित्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=174-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामिन्
कामिन् mfn. (-मी-मिनी-मि)<BR>	 1. Impassioned, fond, loving, wanton.<BR>	 2. Cu-<BR>pidinous, desirous.<BR>	 m. (-नी)<BR>	 1. The moon.<BR>	 2. A lover, an uxorious<BR>husband.<BR>	 3. The ruddy goose.<BR>	 4. A pigeon.<BR>	 5. A sparrow.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>	 1. A loving or affectionate woman.<BR>	 2. A timid woman.<BR>	 3. A<BR>woman in general.<BR>	 4. Spirituous liquor.<BR>	 5. A climbing plant.<BR> E. कम्<BR>to desire, and णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=174-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामिनीश|कामिनीशः
कामिनीश m. (-शः) A plant, (Morunga guilandina, &c.) see शोभाञ्जन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=174-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामील|कामीलः
कामील m. (-लः) A kind of betel, commonly रामगुवाक.<BR> E. काम desire,<BR>ईलच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=174-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामुक|कामुकः
कामुक mfn. (-कः-का-की-कं) Cupidinous, desirous, lustful, libidinous.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-कः)<BR>	 1. A plant, Asoka, (Jonesia asoca.)<BR>	 2. A creeping plant,<BR>(Gærtnera racemosa.)<BR>	 3. A sparrow.<BR>	 4. A bow.<BR>	 f. (-का) A woman<BR>desirous of wealth, food, &c.<BR>	 f. (-की) A woman libidinous or lust-<BR>ful.<BR> E. कम् to desire, उकञ् affix, fem. टाप् or ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=174-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामोदक|कामोदकं
कामोदक n. (-कं) Oblation of water to deceased friends, &c. exclusive<BR>of those for whom it is directed by law.<BR> E. काम will, and उदक<BR>water; being given according to the inclination of the giver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=174-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामोदा
कामोदा f. (-दा) A Rāgiṇī, one of the female personifications of the<BR>musical modes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=174-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामोपहत
कामोपहत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Overcome with passion or desire.<BR> E. काम, and<BR>उपहत struck.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=174-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काम्पिल|कांपिलः|काम्पिलः
काम्पिल m. (-लः) A country believed to be situated in the north of<BR>India: see काम्पिल्ल, &c.<BR>	 f. (-ली) The capital city of that region.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=174-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काम्पिल्य|काम्पिल्यः
काम्पिल्य m. (-ल्यः)<BR>	 1. A perfume, commonly Sunda Rochani.<BR>	 2. A<BR>country: see the preceding; also काम्पिल्ल, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=174-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काम्पिल्ल|कांपिल्ल|कांपिल्लः|काम्पिल्लः
काम्पिल्ल m. (-ल्लः)<BR>	 1. Sunda Rochani, a perfume and drug so called.<BR>2. The name of a country said to be in the north-west of India. E.<BR>कपि to tremble or shake, इल्ल affix; also काम्पिल or काम्पील, काम्पिल्य, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=174-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काम्पिल्लका
काम्पिल्लका f. (-का) See the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=174-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काम्पील|काम्पीलः
काम्पील m. (-लः) See काम्पिल and काम्पिल्ल; also काम्पीलक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=174-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काम्बल|कांबल|कांबलः|काम्बलः
काम्बल mfn. (-लः-ली-लं) Clothed with a blanket, &c.<BR>	 m. (-लः) A car<BR>covered with a woollen cloth or blanket.<BR> E. कम्बल a blanket, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=174-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काम्बलिक|काम्बलिकः
काम्बलिक m. (-कः) Gruel, barley-water, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=174-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काम्बविक|कांबविक|कांबविकः|काम्बविकः
काम्बविक m. (-कः) A dealer in shells, a vender of ornaments made of<BR>them, &c.<BR> E. कम्बु a shell, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=174-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काम्बुका
काम्बुका f. (-का) A plant, (Physalis flexuosa:) see अश्वगन्धा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=174-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काम्बोज|कांबोज|कांबोजः|काम्बोजः
काम्बोज m. (-जः)<BR>	 1. A native of Kamboja, a foreign race going like<BR>the Yavanas, with the whole of the head shaved, one of the tribes<BR>originally Kṣatriya, but degraded by omission of the essential<BR>rites.<BR>	 2. A horse of the bread of Kamboya or Kamboja.<BR>	 3. A white<BR>mimosa.<BR>	 4. A tree, commonly Punnaga, (Rottleria tinctoria)<BR>	 f. (-जी)<BR>1. A plant, commonly Mashani: see माषपर्णी.<BR>	 2. A white mimosa,<BR>as above.<BR>	 3. The Gunja-plant.<BR> E. कम्बोज Kamboja or Kamboya, a<BR>country in the north of India, अण् and ङीष् affixes: the plants, &c.<BR>being supposed indigenous to that district.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=174-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काम्य|काम्यं
काम्य mfn. (-म्यः-म्या-म्यं)<BR>	 1. Agreeable, desirable, amiable.<BR>	 2. Performed<BR>through the desire of some advantage, (a religious ceremony, &c.)<BR>2. Optional, supererogatory, performed for some particular object<BR>and opposed to the नित्यकर्म्म or fixed and indispensable observance.<BR>4. Relating to desire, will, &c.<BR>	 5. Done through lust or passion. E.<BR>काम desire, love, &c. and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=174-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काम्यगिर्
काम्यगिर् f. (-गीः) A pleasing sound, an agreeable speech or song. E.<BR>काम्य, and गिर् speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=174-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काम्यत्व
काम्यत्व n. (-त्वं)<BR>	 1. Supererogation, will, pleasure.<BR>	 2. Love, desire. E.<BR>काम्य, and त्व affix; also with तल्, काम्यता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=174-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काम्यदान|काम्यदानं
काम्यदान n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. An acceptable or desirable gift.<BR>	 2. A voluntary gift.<BR>E. काम्य, and दान a gift.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=174-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काम्यमरण
काम्यमरण n. (-णं) Voluntary death, suicide.<BR> E. काम्य, and मरण dying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=174-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काम्याभिप्राय|काम्याभिप्रायः
काम्याभिप्राय m. (-यः) The purpose of deriving benefit from any act. E.<BR>काम्य, and अभिप्राय intention.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=174-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काम्ल
काम्ल mfn. (-म्लः-म्ला-म्लं) Slightly acid, acidulous.<BR> E. का dimin, अम्ल sour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=174-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काय|कायं|कायः
काय mn. (-यः-यं) The body.<BR>	 n. (-यं)<BR>	 1. Part of the hand sacred to the<BR>creator; the root of the little finger.<BR>	 2. Clarified butter or any ob-<BR>lation to BRAHMĀ.<BR>	 m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. One of the eight modes of marriage,<BR>the same as प्राजापत्य.<BR>	 2. Assemblage, collection.<BR>	 3. A butt or mark,<BR>an object to be hit or attained.<BR>	 4. Natural temperament of any<BR>thing or being.<BR>	 5. A house, a habitation.<BR>	 6. Principal, capital.<BR> E. क<BR>a name of BRAHMĀ, and अण् deriv. affix, इ is added to क, and अय<BR>is substituted for the short vowel; proceeding from or relating to<BR>BRAHMĀ, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=174-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कायक
कायक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Belonging to the body.<BR> E. काय, and कन्<BR>added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=174-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कायक्लेश|कायक्लेशः
कायक्लेश m. (-शः) Bodily suffering, toil or pain.<BR> E. काय, and क्लेश<BR>distress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=174-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कायचिकित्सा
कायचिकित्सा f. (-त्सा) Treatment of disease, administering medicines. E.<BR>काय, and चिकित्सा remedying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=174-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कायबलन
कायबलन n. (-नं) Armour, mail.<BR> E. काय the body, and बलन protecting;<BR>from बल् to be strong, affix ल्युट.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=174-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कायमान|कायमानं
कायमान n. (-नं) A hut of grass or thatch.<BR> E. कै to sound, and शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=174-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कायस्थ|कायस्थः
कायस्थ m. (-स्थः)<BR>	 1. The Supreme Being.<BR>	 2. A caste or tribe, or man of<BR>that tribe; the Kayeth or writer caste, proceeding from a Kṣatriya<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=175-a" target="_blank">Page175-a+ 60</a>]<BR>father and Śūdra mother.<BR>	 f. (-स्था)<BR>	 1. Yellow myrobalan: see<BR>हरीतकी.<BR>	 2. Emblic myrobalan.<BR>	 3. A drug, commonly Kakoli.<BR>	 4. A<BR>woman of the Kayeth caste.<BR>	 f. (-स्थी) The wife of a Kayeth or<BR>scribe.<BR> E. काय the body or house. and स्थ who stays, or resides.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=174-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कायाग्नि|कायाग्निः
कायाग्नि m. (-ग्निः) The digestive faculty.<BR> E. काय, and अग्नि fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=175-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कायिक|कायिकः
कायिक mfn. (-कः-का-की-कं) Corporeal, relating to the body.<BR> E. काय the<BR>body, and कन् or ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=175-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कायिकावृद्धि|कायिकावृद्धिः
कायिकावृद्धि f. (-द्धिः) Interest arising from service drawn from the body<BR>of an animal, (as a cow, &c,) pledged; or according to some, in-<BR>terest of which the payment does not effect the principal.<BR> E. कायिका<BR>corporeal, &c. वृद्धि interest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=175-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार|कारः
कार mfn. (-रः-री-रं) Who or what does any act, (but used chiefly in<BR>composition with other words:) the agent, a maker or doer; as<BR>कुम्भकार a potter, a maker of earthen vessels. स्वर्णकार a goldsmith,<BR>&c.<BR>	 m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Act, action.<BR>	 2. Killing, slaughter.<BR>	 3. Certainty.<BR>4. Effort, exertion.<BR>	 5. Religious austerity.<BR>	 6. A heap of snow, or a<BR>mountain covered with it.<BR>	 7. Tax, toll, royal revenue.<BR>	 8. A master,<BR>a lord.<BR>	 f. (-रा)<BR>	 1. A prison.<BR>	 2. Binding, confinement.<BR>	 3. A female<BR>messenger.<BR>	 4. The part of a lute below the neck.<BR>	 5. A female work-<BR>er in gold, (हेमकारिका.)<BR>	 6. Pain, affliction.<BR> E. कृञ् to make, to<BR>do, with घञ् or अण् affix, in the latter case the fem. affix is ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=175-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारक|कारकं|कारकः
कारक mfn. (-रकः-रिका-रकं) An agent, acting, doing, who or what does,<BR>acts, makes, &c.<BR>	 m. (-कः) A noun of action.<BR>	 n. (-कं)<BR>	 1. Action,<BR>especially in grammar.<BR>	 2. That part of grammar comprising all<BR>nouns which imply the agent, object, instrument, &c. or anything<BR>except the simple and radical idea; it also includes the use and<BR>government of the cases or syntax.<BR> E. कृञ् to do, and ण्वुल् affix of<BR>agency.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=175-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारकर
कारकर mfn. (-रः-री-रं) Working, doing work, acting as agent.<BR> E. कार,<BR>and कर who does.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=175-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारकहेतु|कारकहेतुः
कारकहेतु m.^1 (-{{तु->तुःळ्ह्ळ्ह्२०२६०६२४ळ्ह्श्चोत्त् ण्होदेस्ळ्ह्ह्त्त्प्स्:॑꣡गित्हुब्।चोम्॑सन्स्क्रित्-लेऌइचोन्॑च्स्ल्-चोर्रेच्तिओन्स्॑इस्सुएस्॑२७४}}}) Efficient or active cause.<BR> E. कारक what produces, हेतु<BR>cause.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20260624. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/274.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=175-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारकुक्षीय|कारकुक्षीयः
कारकुक्षीय m. (-यः) The name of a country, that of king SALWA; or plu.<BR>(-याः) The people of that country.<BR> E. कार a snowy mountain, कुक्ष<BR>the flank, and छ affix; being on the skirts of the Himālaya ridge<BR>in the north-west of Hindustan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=175-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारज
कारज mfn. (-जः-जी-जं) Of or relating to the finger-nail.<BR>	 m. (-जः) A<BR>young elephant.<BR> E. करज a nail, &c. अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=175-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारण|कारणं
कारण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Cause, motive, origin, principle: in logic, cause is of<BR>three kinds; Samavayi inherent or direct; Asamavāyi proximate<BR>or indirect; and Nimitta instrumental or incidental.<BR>	 2. Action,<BR>agency.<BR>	 3. Killing, injuring.<BR>	 4. An organ of sense.<BR>	 5. An instru-<BR>ment or means.<BR>	 6. An element, elementary matter.<BR>	 7. A deity, as the<BR>remote or proximate cause of creation.<BR>	 8. A number of scribes.<BR>9. A kind of musical instrument.<BR>	 10. A sort of song, &c. see करण.<BR>11. The origin of a story (of a play or poem.)<BR>	 f. (-णा).<BR>	 1. Pain,<BR>agony.<BR>	 2. Casting into hell.<BR>	 3. An astronomical period.<BR> E. कृञ् to<BR>do or act, in the causal form, and युच् or ल्युट् affix, or करण, and अण्<BR>added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=175-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारणकारण
कारणकारण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. A primary cause 2. An elementary cause, an<BR>atom.<BR> E. कारण repeated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=175-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारणगुण|कारणगुणः
कारणगुण m. (-णः) An elementary or causal property.<BR> E. कारण, and गुण<BR>property.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=175-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारणगुणोद्भवगुण|कारणगुणोद्भवगुणः
कारणगुणोद्भवगुण m. (-णः) A secondary or derivative property, as form,<BR>taste, smell, &c. produced by combinations of elementary or causal<BR>particles.<BR> E. कारणगुण, and उद्भवगुण produced property.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=175-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारणत्व
कारणत्व n. (-त्वं) Causality, causation.<BR> E. त्व added to कारण, and त्व affix,<BR>or with तल्, कारणता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=175-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारणमाला
कारणमाला f. (-ला) A series or chain of events.<BR> E. कारण, and माला a<BR>wreath.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=175-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारणवादिन्
कारणवादिन् m. (-दी) A complainant, a plaintiff.<BR> E. कारण the cause, and<BR>वादिन् who declares.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=175-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारणशरीर|कारणशरीरं
कारणशरीर n. (-रं) The inner rudiment of the body or causal frame, the<BR>seat of the soul.<BR> E. कारण, and शरीर body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=175-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारणाभाव
कारणाभाव m. (-वः) Absence of cause.<BR> E. कारण, and अभाव nonentity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=175-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारणिक|कारणिकः
कारणिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>	 1. Investigating, trying, ascertaining the<BR>cause.<BR>	 2. Causal, causative.<BR> E. कारण action, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=175-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारणोत्तर|कारणोत्तरं
कारणोत्तर n. (-रं) Special plea, denial of the cause of complaint, admis-<BR>sion of the charge generally, but denial of the issue; as to a de-<BR>mand of debt, acknowledgement that it was incurred, but assertion<BR>that the loan has been repaid, &c.<BR> E. कारण the cause, and उत्तर<BR>answer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=175-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारण्डव|कारंडव|कारंडवः|कारण्डवः
कारण्डव mf. (-वः-वी) A sort of duck.<BR> E. करण्ड Vallisneria, अण् pleonastic aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=175-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारण्डव्यूह|कारण्डव्यूहः
कारण्डव्यूह m. (-हः) A Buddha or sanctified being according to the<BR>Bauddhas.<BR> E. कारण्ड the same, वै to go, and ड aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=175-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारन्धमिन्|कारंधमिन्
कारन्धमिन् m. (-मी)<BR>	 1. A brazier, a worker in mixed or white metal.<BR>	 2. A<BR>mineralogist, an assayer.<BR> E. कारं work, and धमिन् who blows; from<BR>ध्मा to blow, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=175-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारम्भा|कारंभा
कारम्भा f. (-म्भा) A plant bearing a fragrant seed, commonly Priyangu.<BR>का for कु bad, आरम्भ beginning; very diminutive while young.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=175-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारमिहिका
कारमिहिका f. (-का) Camphor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=175-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारयत्
कारयत् mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्) Causing to do, conferring any power or<BR>authority to do, &c. कृ to do, causal form, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=175-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारयमाण
कारयमाण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Doing what is appointed, carrying into effect<BR>what has been ordered.<BR> E. कृ to do, causal form, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=175-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारयितृ
कारयितृ mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ) Causing to act or do.<BR> E. कृ to do, causal form,<BR>तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=175-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारव|कारवः
कारव m. (-वः) A crow.<BR> E. का an imitative sound, रव who sounds.<BR>	 f. (-वी)<BR>1. A kind of Anise, (Anethum sowa.)<BR>	 2. Another plant, (Celosia<BR>cristata.)<BR>	 3. The asafœtida plant or its leaf, Hinguparni.<BR>	 4. A kind<BR>of fennel, (Nigella Indica.)<BR>	 4. A small gourd.<BR> E. क water, आङ् be-<BR>fore रु to go, अण् and ङीप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=175-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारवेल्ल|कारवेल्लं|कारवेल्लः
कारवेल्ल m. (-ल्लः) A kind of gourd, (Momordica charantia.)<BR> E. कार cer-<BR>tainty, and वेल्ल what goes; also with कन् added कारवेल्लक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=175-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारवेल्लक|कारवेल्लकः
कारवेल्लक m. (-कः) See the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=175-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारस्कर|कारस्करः
कारस्कर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A medicinal plant.<BR>	 2. A tree.<BR> E. कार toll, revenue,<BR>and कर what makes; स is inserted in this sense, for the sake of<BR>euphony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=175-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारस्कराटिका
कारस्कराटिका f. (-का) A centipede or worm resembling it, (Julus.) E.<BR>कारस्कर a tree, and अट what goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=175-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारागार|कारागारं
कारागार n. (-रं) A gaol, a place of confinement.<BR> E. कारा confinement, and<BR>अगार or आगार a house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=175-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारागुप्त|कारागुप्तः
कारागुप्त mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं) Captive, imprisoned, confined, a prisoner. E.<BR>कारा confinement, and गुप्त concealed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=175-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारायिका
कारायिका f. (-का) A female crane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=175-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारावर|कारावरः
कारावर m. (-रः) A man of a mixed and low caste, a man born of a<BR>Nishadha father and Vaidehī mother, employed in working in lea-<BR>ther or hides.<BR> E. कार, and अवर low.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=175-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारावेश्मन्
कारावेश्मन् n. (-श्म) A prison, a gaol.<BR> E. कारा confinement, and वेश्मन् a house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=175-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारि|कारिः
कारि mfn. (-रिः-रिः-रि) An artist, an artificer.<BR>	 f. (-रिः) Action, act,<BR>agency.<BR> E. कृञ् to do, and इन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=175-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारिका
कारिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. An actress, a dancing woman.<BR>	 2. Action, agency.<BR>	 3.<BR>Comment, gloss.<BR>	 4. An art, a profession.<BR>	 5. Sharp pain.<BR>	 6. Inter-<BR>est at any stipulated rate.<BR> E. कृञ् to do, and वुन् affix, fem. termina-<BR>tion टाप् and इ substituted for the penultimate vowel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=175-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारित|कारितः
कारित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Caused to be made or done, brought about, effect-<BR>ed.<BR>	 f. (-ता) Stipulated interest; also कारिका, and कारितावृद्धि.<BR> E. कृ<BR>to do, in the causal form, and क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=175-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारितवत्
कारितवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>	 1. Making, doing.<BR>	 2. Calling, appointing.<BR>E. कृ to do, क्तवतु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=175-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारिन्
कारिन् mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि) An actor, acting, doing.<BR> E. कृ to do, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=176-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारीष|कारीषं
कारीष n. (-षं) A great quantity of dried cow-dung.<BR> E. करीष, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=176-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारु|कारुः
कारु mfn. (-रुः-रुः-रु)<BR>	 1. An artist, an artificer, an agent, a maker, a<BR>doer.<BR>	 m. (-रुः) A name of VISWAKARMA, the artist of the gods.<BR>2. An art, a science.<BR> E. कृञ् to do, and उण् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=176-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारुक|कारुकः
कारुक m. (-कः) An artisan, an artificer.<BR> E. कारु, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=176-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारुचौर|कारुचौरः
कारुचौर m. (-रः) One who commits burglary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=176-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारुज|कारुजः
कारुज m. (-जः)<BR>	 1. A piece of mechanism, any product of manufacture.<BR>2. An ant-hill, a hillock.<BR>	 3. A young elephant.<BR>	 4. Sesamum grow-<BR>ing spontaneously.<BR>	 5. A plant, (Mesua ferrea.)<BR>	 6. Froth, foam.<BR>	 7.<BR>Red orpiment.<BR> E. कारु an art or artist, and ज what is born or<BR>produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=176-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारुणिक|कारुणिकः
कारुणिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Compassionate, tender, kind.<BR> E. करुणा com-<BR>passion, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=176-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारुण्डी|कारुंडी
कारुण्डी f. (-ण्डी) A leech; also कारुण्डिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=176-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारुण्य|कारुण्यं
कारुण्य n. (-ण्यं) Compassion, tenderness.<BR> E. करुणा compassion, &c.<BR>ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=176-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारूष
कारूष m. (-षः)<BR>	 1. The offspring of the degraded or outcaste Vaiśya<BR>tribe.<BR>	 2. A country; plu.<BR>	 m. (-षाः) Its inhabitants; also वृहद्गुहाः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=176-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारूहस्त
कारूहस्त m. (-स्तः) The hand of the artisan or artificer.<BR> E. कारू, and हस्त<BR>hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=176-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारोत्तम|कारोत्तमः
कारोत्तम m. (-मः) Yeast, barm, froth.<BR> E. कार action, and उत्तम first, best,<BR>chief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=176-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारोत्तर|कारोत्तरः
कारोत्तर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Barm, yeast: see the preceding.<BR>	 2. A well. E. As<BR>before, उत्तर best, instead of उत्तम.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=176-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्क्कण|कार्कण
कार्क्कण mfn. (-णः-णी-णं) Done by or relating to a pheasant.<BR> E. कृकणा, and<BR>अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=176-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्क्कवाकव|कार्कवाकव
कार्क्कवाकव mfn. (-वः-वी-वं) Produced or done by a cock, &c.<BR> E. कृकवाकु,<BR>and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=176-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्क्कश्य|कार्कश्य|कार्कश्यं
कार्क्कश्य n. (-श्यं)<BR>	 1. Hardness, firmness, solidity.<BR>	 2. Sternness, inflexi-<BR>bility.<BR> E. कर्क्कश, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=176-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्क्कीक|कार्कीक
कार्क्कीक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Like a white horse.<BR> E. कर्क्क, and ईकन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=176-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्ण|कार्णः|कार्ण्ण
कार्ण mfn. (-र्णः-र्णी-र्णं) Relating to the ear, auricular, &c.<BR>	 n. (-र्णं) An<BR>ear-ring.<BR> E. कर्ण, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=176-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्णच्छिद्रक|कार्णछिद्रक
कार्णच्छिद्रक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) A sort of well.<BR> E. कर्णच्छिद्र the opening of<BR>the ear, कन् affix of similitude, अण् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=176-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्णवेष्टकिक
कार्णवेष्टकिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Ornamented with ear-ring.<BR> E. कर्णवेष्टक,<BR>and ठक् affix; also read कार्णवेष्टनिक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=176-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्त्तवीर्य्य|कार्तवीर्य|कार्तवीर्यः|कार्त्तवीर्य्यः
कार्त्तवीर्य्य m. (-र्य्यः)<BR>	 1. The name of a king, also called ARJUNA, killed by<BR>PARASURAMA.<BR>	 2. The name of one of the Jaina chakravartis or<BR>emperors of the world.<BR> E. कृतवीर्य्य the father of this prince, अण्<BR>patronymic aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=176-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्त्तस्वर|कार्तस्वर|कार्तस्वरं|कार्त्तस्वरं
कार्त्तस्वर n. (-रं)<BR>	 1. Gold.<BR>	 2. Thorn apple.<BR> E. कृतस्वर a kind of mine, and<BR>अण् affix, implying production: or कृतस्वर a reader of the Vedas,<BR>(from कृत made, and स्वर a sound;) to whom gold is given as a<BR>reward.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=176-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्त्तान्तिक|कार्तान्तिक|कार्तांतिक|कार्तांतिकः|कार्तान्तिकः|कार्त्तान्तिकः
कार्त्तान्तिक m. (-कः) An astrologer.<BR> E. कृतान्त fortune, luck, and ठक् affix;<BR>acquainted with the fates.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=176-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्त्तिक|कार्तिक|कार्तिकः|कार्त्तिकः
कार्त्तिक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. The month Kartik, (October-November,) when the<BR>moon is full near the Pleiades.<BR>	 2. The deity KARTIKEYA.<BR> E. कृत्तिका<BR>the Pleiades, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=176-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्त्तिकिक|कार्तिकिक|कार्त्तिकिकः
कार्त्तिकिक m. (-कः) See the preceding, ठक् affix added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=176-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्त्तिकेय|कार्तिकेय|कार्तिकेयः|कार्त्तिकेयः
कार्त्तिकेय m. (-यः) KARTIKEYA, the deity of war and son of ŚIVA. E.<BR>कृत्तिका the personified Pleiades, and ढक् affix: according to the<BR>legend, having been fostered and brought up by the nymphs so<BR>called.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=176-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्त्तिकेयप्रसू|कार्तिकेयप्रसू
कार्त्तिकेयप्रसू f. (-सूः) A name of DURGĀ.<BR> E. कार्त्तिकेय, and प्रसू the mother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=176-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्त्तिकोत्सव|कार्तिकोत्सव|कार्त्तिकोत्सवः
कार्त्तिकोत्सव m. (-वः) The day of full moon in the month KARTIK, a<BR>festival.<BR> E. कार्त्तिक the month, and उत्सव festival.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=176-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्त्स्न
कार्त्स्न n. (-र्त्स्नम्) The whole, all, entire.<BR> E. कृत्स्न, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=176-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्त्स्न्य|कार्त्स्न्यं
कार्त्स्न्य n. (-र्त्स्न्यम्) The whole, all, entire.<BR> E. कृत्स्न, and यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=176-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्द्दम|कार्दम
कार्द्दम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं) Made of mud, filled with it, &c.<BR> E. कर्द्दम, and अण्<BR>affix; also with ठक्, कार्द्दमिक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=176-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्पट|कार्पटः
कार्पट m. (-टः)<BR>	 1. Lac, the animal dye.<BR>	 2. A petitioner, a suitor, one<BR>who begs for employment, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=176-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्पटिक|कार्पटिकः
कार्पटिक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A parasite.<BR>	 2. A pilgrim, one who spends his life<BR>in pilgrimage, or who subsists by carrying water from holy<BR>rivers.<BR> E. कृप् to be able, अटन् affix, ठञ् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=176-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्पण्य|कार्पण्यं
कार्पण्य n. (-ण्यं)<BR>	 1. Poverty, indigence.<BR>	 2. Poorness of spirit, weakness,<BR>imbecility.<BR> E. कृपण poor, ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=176-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्पास|कार्पासं|कार्पासः
कार्पास mfn. (-सः-सी-सं) Made of cotton, cottony, &c.<BR>	 nf. (-सं-सी)<BR>	 1. The<BR>cotton plant, (Gossypium hirsutum-)<BR>	 n. (-सं)<BR>	 1. Cotton cloth, &c.<BR>2. Paper.<BR> E. कृ to make, to do, पास Uṇādi affix, the vowel of the<BR>radical being lengthened.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=176-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्पासनासिका
कार्पासनासिका f. (-का) A spindle.<BR> E. कार्पास, and नासिका the nose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=176-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्पासास्थि
कार्पासास्थि n. (-स्थि) The seed of the cotton plant.<BR> E. कार्पास, and अस्थि<BR>a bone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=176-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्पासिक
कार्पासिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Made of or from cotton.<BR>	 f. (-का) The cotton<BR>plant: see कार्पास.<BR> E. कार्पास, and ठञ् affix; or कार्पास with कन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=176-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्म्म|कार्म|कार्म्मः
कार्म्म mfn. (-र्म्म-र्म्मी-र्म्मं) Laborious, industrious, occupied.<BR> E. कर्म्म an<BR>act, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=176-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्म्मण|कार्मण|कार्म्मणं
कार्म्मण mfn. (-णः-णी-णं) Finishing a work, doing it well or completely.<BR>n. (-णं) Magic, performing anything by means of magical<BR>incantations.<BR> E. कर्म्मन् work, act, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=176-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्म्मणत्व|कार्मणत्व
कार्म्मणत्व n. (-त्वं) Magic, fascination.<BR> E. त्व added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=176-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्म्मिक|कार्मिक|कार्म्मिकः
कार्म्मिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>	 1. Manufactured, made.<BR>	 2. Worked, em-<BR>broidered, intermixed with coloured thread, (cloth, &c.)<BR> E. कर्म्म<BR>work, art, affix ठक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=176-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्म्मुक|कार्मुक|कार्म्मुकं|कार्म्मुकः
कार्म्मुक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Finishing a work, doing it well or completely.<BR>nm. (-कं-कः) A bamboo.<BR>	 n. (-कं) A bow.<BR> E. कर्म्म act, action, and<BR>उकञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=176-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्म्मुकभृत्|कार्मुकभृत्
कार्म्मुकभृत् m. (-भृत्) A soldier, an archer.<BR> E. कार्म्मुक, and भृत् who has.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=176-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्य्य|कार्य|कार्य्यं
कार्य्य mfn. (-र्य्यः-र्य्या-र्य्यं)<BR>	 1. To be done.<BR>	 2. What ought to be done, fit,<BR>right.<BR>	 n. (-र्य्यं)<BR>	 1. Cause, origin.<BR>	 2. Motive, object.<BR>	 3. Effect, result<BR>of a cause.<BR>	 4. Affair, business.<BR>	 5. Law-suit, dispute.<BR>	 6. The<BR>denouement^1 of a drama.<BR>	 7. In grammar, an adjunct, either as<BR>an affix, augment or substitute^2.<BR> E. कृञ् to do, and ण्यत् aff.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20260701. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/282.<BR>[2] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20260701. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/282.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=176-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्य्यकारण|कार्यकारण
कार्य्यकारण n. (-णं) Cause of a special or incidental kind, originating in<BR>some act or occasion.<BR> E. कार्य्य, and कारण cause.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=176-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्य्यकारणतस्|कार्यकारणतस्
कार्य्यकारणतस् ind. Incidentally, from some special cause.<BR> E. कार्य्यकारण,<BR>and तसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=176-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्य्यकाल|कार्यकाल|कार्यकालः
कार्य्यकाल m. (-लः) Time for action, appointed time, season, opportuni-<BR>ty.<BR> E. कार्य्य, and काल time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=176-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्य्यकुशल|कार्यकुशल|कार्य्यकुशलः
कार्य्यकुशल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Finishing a work, doing it well or com-<BR>pletely.<BR> E. कार्य्य business, and कुशल prosperous, successful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=176-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्य्यक्षम|कार्यक्षम
कार्य्यक्षम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं) Competent, fit, able.<BR> E. कार्य्य, and क्षम able.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=176-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्य्यगुरुता|कार्यगुरुता
कार्य्यगुरुता f. (-ता) Necessity or importance of any act.<BR> E. कार्य्य, and<BR>गुरुता weight; also कार्य्यगुरुत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=176-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्य्यचिन्तक|कार्यचिन्तक|कार्यचिंतक|कार्यचिन्तकः
कार्य्यचिन्तक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Prudent, considerate, cautious.<BR> E. कार्य्य,<BR>and चिन्तक who reflects.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=176-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्य्यचिन्ता|कार्यचिन्ता
कार्य्यचिन्ता f. (-न्ता) Prudence, caution, consideration.<BR> E. कार्य्य, and चिन्ता<BR>reflexion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=176-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्य्यतस्|कार्यतस्
कार्य्यतस् ind. Consequently, necessarily, actually.<BR> E. कार्य्य act, and<BR>तसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=176-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्य्यदर्शन|कार्यदर्शन
कार्य्यदर्शन n. (-नं) Inspection, supervision.<BR> E. कार्य्य, and दर्शन seeing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=176-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्य्यनिर्णय|कार्यनिर्णय|कार्यनिर्णयः
कार्य्यनिर्णय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. Judgment, ascertainment of the fact.<BR>	 2. Set-<BR>tlement of an affair.<BR> E. कार्य्य affair, cause, and निर्णय ascertain-<BR>ment; also कार्य्यविनिर्णय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=176-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्य्यपुट|कार्यपुट|कार्यपुटः|कार्य्यपुटः
कार्य्यपुट m. (-टः)<BR>	 1. An impudent or shameless fellow.<BR>	 2. An idler, one<BR>who follows unprofitable pursuits.<BR>	 3. A madman, a crazy or<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=177-a" target="_blank">Page177-a+ 60</a>]<BR>hair-brained man.<BR> E. कार्य्य object, cause, &c. पुट् to rub, to-destroy,<BR>क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=176-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्य्यप्रद्वेष|कार्यप्रद्वेष|कार्यप्रद्वेषः|कार्य्यप्रद्वेषः
कार्य्यप्रद्वेष m. (-षः) Idleness.<BR> E. कार्य्य, and प्रद्वेष aversion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=177-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्य्यभाजन|कार्यभाजन
कार्य्यभाजन n. (-नं) Any one engaged in active life, one fit for business<BR>or conducting affairs.<BR> E. कार्य्य, and भाजन a vessel; also कार्य्यपात्रं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=177-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्य्यवत्|कार्यवत्|कार्यवन्त्
कार्य्यवत् ind. Actually, according to act or motive.<BR> E. कार्य्य, and वति aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=177-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्य्यवत्|कार्यवत्|कार्यवन्त्
कार्य्यवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>	 1. Engaged in business.<BR>	 2. Having a cause<BR>or motive.<BR>	 3. Doing one's duty<BR> E. कार्य्य and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=177-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्य्यवत्ता|कार्यवत्ता
कार्य्यवत्ता f. (-त्ता) Act, action.<BR> E. कार्य्यवत् and तल् affix; also कार्य्यवत्त्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=177-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्य्यवश|कार्यवश
कार्य्यवश m. (-शः) Necessary consequence.<BR> E. कार्य्य cause, and वश sub-<BR>jection to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=177-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्य्यवस्तु|कार्यवस्तु
कार्य्यवस्तु n. (-स्तु) End, object.<BR> E. कार्य्य, and वस्तु thing, what is to be done.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=177-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्य्यविपत्ति|कार्यविपत्ति|कार्यविपत्तिः
कार्य्यविपत्ति f. (-त्तिः) Failure, reverse, misfortune.<BR> E. कार्य्य, and विपत्ति<BR>misfortune.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=177-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्य्यशेष|कार्यशेष|कार्यशेषः
कार्य्यशेष m. (-षः) The completion of a business or affair begun.<BR> E. कार्य्य,<BR>and शेष rest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=177-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्य्यसन्देह|कार्यसन्देह
कार्य्यसन्देह m. (-हः) Embarrassment, difficulty.<BR> E. कार्य्य, and सन्देह doubt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=177-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्य्यसागर|कार्यसागर
कार्य्यसागर m. (-रः) Business, heavy business, weighty affairs.<BR> E. कार्य्य,<BR>and सागर ocean; also similar compounds, as कार्य्याब्धि, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=177-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्य्यसाधक|कार्यसाधक
कार्य्यसाधक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Accomplishing any object.<BR> E. कार्य्य, and साधक<BR>what completes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=177-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्य्यसाधन
कार्य्यसाधन n. (-नं) Means of effecting any object, instrument, imple-<BR>ment, aid.<BR> E. कार्य्य, and साधन means.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=177-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्य्यसिद्धि|कार्यसिद्धि|कार्यसिद्धिः
कार्य्यसिद्धि f. (-द्धिः) Accomplishment, success, fulfilment of any ob-<BR>ject or purpose.<BR> E. कार्य्य, and सिद्धि success.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=177-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्य्यहन्तृ|कार्यहन्तृ|कार्यहंतृ
कार्य्यहन्तृ mfn. (-न्ता-न्त्री-न्तृ) Foiling, counteracting, opposing all one's<BR>aims.<BR> E. कार्य्य, and हन्तृ who destroys.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=177-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्य्याक्षम|कार्याक्षम
कार्य्याक्षम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं) Unfit, incompetent, unable.<BR> E. कार्य्य, and अक्षम<BR>unable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=177-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्य्यान्त|कार्यान्त
कार्य्यान्त n. (-न्तं) The end of a business.<BR> E. कार्य्य, and अन्त end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=177-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्य्यार्थ|कार्यार्थ|कार्यार्थः
कार्य्यार्थ m. (-र्थः)<BR>	 1. An object or purpose.<BR>	 2. Application for employ-<BR>ment, n. or ad. (-र्थं)<BR>	 1. For the sake of any particular object.<BR>	 2. To<BR>perform any work or duty.<BR> E. कार्य्य, and अर्थ object.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=177-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्य्यार्थसिद्धि|कार्यार्थसिद्धि
कार्य्यार्थसिद्धि f. (-द्धिः) The accomplishment of any object or purpose. E.<BR>कार्य्यार्थ, and सिद्धि fulfilment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=177-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्य्यार्थिन्|कार्यार्थिन्
कार्य्यार्थिन् mfn. (-र्थी-र्थिनी-र्थि)<BR>	 1. Having an object or purpose.<BR>2. Applying for employment.<BR> E. कार्य्यार्थ, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=177-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्य्यिक|कार्यिक
कार्य्यिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Having business, transacting business.<BR>	 2.<BR>Seeking employment, &c.<BR>	 3. Engaged in a suit at law.<BR> E. कार्य्य,<BR>and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=177-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्य्यिन्|कार्यिन्
कार्य्यिन् mfn. (-र्य्यी-र्य्यिणी-र्य्यि)<BR>	 1. Seeking for employment.<BR>	 2. One who<BR>transacts business, active, assiduous.<BR>	 3. Having an object.<BR>	 4. A<BR>party to a suit, either as plaintiff or defendant.<BR>	 5. Requiring an<BR>affix, &c.<BR> E. कार्य्य, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=177-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्य्येक्षण|कार्येक्षण
कार्य्येक्षण n. (-णं) Superintendance of public affairs, &c.<BR> E. कार्य्य, and<BR>ईक्षण seeing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=177-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्य्योद्धार|कार्योद्धार|कार्योद्धारः
कार्य्योद्धार m. (-रः) Discharge of any duty, performance of any act. E.<BR>कार्य्य, and उद्धार extrication.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=177-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्य्योद्युक्त|कार्योद्युक्त
कार्य्योद्युक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं) Engaged in any business, intent upon any<BR>object.<BR> E. कार्य्य, and उद्युक्त active.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=177-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्य्योद्योग|कार्योद्योग|कार्योद्योगः
कार्य्योद्योग m. (-गः) Active engagement in any business.<BR> E. कार्य्य, and<BR>उद्योग exertion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=177-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्शानव
कार्शानव mfn. (-वः-वी-वं) Fiery, hot, glaring, relating to fire.<BR> E. कृशानु fire,<BR>अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=177-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्श्य|कार्श्यं|कार्श्यः
कार्श्य m. (-र्श्यः) The Sal tree, (Shorea robusta:) see कार्ष्य.<BR>	 n. (-र्ष्यं) Thin-<BR>ness, emaciation.<BR> E. कृश thin, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=177-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्श्मरी
कार्श्मरी f. (-री) A plant, commonly Gambhari: see काश्मरा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=177-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्षक|कार्षकः
कार्षक m. (-कः) A husbandman.<BR> E. कृष् to draw furrows, क्वुन् unadi affix,<BR>and the vowel made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=177-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्षापण|कार्षापणं|कार्षापणः
कार्षापण mn. (-णः-णं) A weight or measure of different values, as syno-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=177-b" target="_blank">Page177-b+ 60</a>]<BR>nimous with Karṣa; it is of gold, weighing sixteen Mashas, or<BR>about 176 grains; of silver, it is in value sixteen Paṇas of kow-<BR>ries, or in tale 1280 commonly termed a Kahan: of copper it<BR>weighs eighty Retis, or the same as of gold, about 176 grains;<BR>according to some, it is the same as a Pan of Kowries, or in tale<BR>eighty.<BR>	 n. (-णं) Money, gold and silver.<BR>	 m. (-णः) A husbandman. E.<BR>कर्ष a Karṣa of silver, आपण custom, habit, and the vowel of कर्ष<BR>lengthened; also with कन् added कार्षापणकः see कर्षपण and कार्षिक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=177-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्षापणवर
कार्षापणवर n. (-रं) The Karṣa of the lowest value.<BR> E. कार्षापण, and अवर<BR>low.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=177-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्षापणिक
कार्षापणिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Bought, &c. with a Karṣa.<BR> E. कार्षापण, and<BR>टिठन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=177-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्षि|कार्षिः
कार्षि f. (-र्षिः)<BR>	 1. Ploughing, cultivation.<BR>	 2. Drawing, attracting.<BR> E. कृष्<BR>to draw, इन् affix, and the vowel. made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=177-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्षिक|कार्षिकः
कार्षिक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A weight: see the preceeding.<BR>	 2. A husbandman. E.<BR>कर्ष a measure, ploughing, &c. and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=177-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्ष्ण
कार्ष्ण mfn. (-र्ष्णः-र्ष्णी-र्ष्णं)<BR>	 1. Black.<BR>	 2. Of or belonging to the black an-<BR>telope.<BR>	 m. (-र्ष्णः) The black antelope.<BR> E. कृष्ण, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=177-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्ष्णायस
कार्ष्णायस mfn. (-सः-सी-सं) Made of black iron.<BR> E. कृष्णायस, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=177-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्ष्णि|कार्ष्णिः
कार्ष्णि m. (-र्ष्णिः) A name of KĀMADEVA.<BR> E. कृष्ण the deity KṚṢṆA, and<BR>इञ् affix; the son of KṚṢṆA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=177-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्ष्य|कार्ष्यः
कार्ष्य m. (-र्ष्यः) The Sal tree, (Shorea robusta)<BR> E. कृष् to make furrows,<BR>ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=177-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्ष्यवण
कार्ष्यवण n. (-णं) A forest of Sal trees.<BR> E. कार्ष्य, and वन a wood the final<BR>changed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=177-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काल|कालं|कालः
काल r. 10th cl. (कालयति) To count time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=177-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काल|कालं|कालः
काल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Black, of a dark colour, dark blue especially,<BR>which is usually confounded with black.<BR>	 m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. Time.<BR>	 2. A<BR>name of YAMA, regent of the dead.<BR>	 3. A black colour.<BR>	 4. Death.<BR>5. A form of ŚIVA.<BR>	 6. The planet Saturn.<BR>	 7. The Koil.<BR>	 8. Cassia<BR>fistula.<BR>	 9. Resin.<BR>	 10. A plant, a red kind of plumbago.<BR>	 n. (-लं)<BR>	 1.<BR>Iron.<BR>	 2. A black agallochum: see कालीयक.<BR>	 3. A vegetable poison,<BR>perhaps the fruit of the Cocculus Indicus.<BR>	 f. (-ला)<BR>	 1. Indigo,<BR>(Indigofera tinctoria.)<BR>	 2. A black sort of Teori.<BR>	 3. Calonji, (Nigella<BR>Indica.)<BR>	 4. Madder, (Rubia manjith.) (-ला or -ली) A name of the<BR>goddess DURGĀ the wife ef ŚIVA. (-ली)<BR>	 1. The wife of SANTANU a<BR>king.<BR>	 2. One of the Matris or divine mothers.<BR>	 3. A female deity of<BR>the Bauddhas.<BR>	 4. A row or succession of clouds.<BR>	 5. Ink or black-<BR>ing.<BR>	 6. A worm or animalcule generated in the acetous fermen-<BR>tation of milk.<BR>	 7. Abuse, censure, defamation.<BR>	 8. Night.<BR>	 9. Trum-<BR>pet flower, (Bignonia suave-olens.)<BR>	 10. One of the seven tongues<BR>or flames of fire.<BR> E. कल् to count or reckon, &c. in the causal form,<BR>अच् affix, fem. affix टाप् or ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=177-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालक|कालकं|कालकः
कालक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Black, dark coloured.<BR>	 m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A freckle, a<BR>mark.<BR>	 2. A water snake.<BR>	 f. (-का) The mother of a class Asuras.<BR>	 n.<BR>(-कं) The liver.<BR> E. कल् to reckon, (good or bad fortune,) वुञ् affix;<BR>or काल black, and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=177-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालकचु
कालकचु f. (-चुः) A sort of Arum, (A. colooasia.)<BR> E. काल black and कचु<BR>Arum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=177-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालकण्ठ|कालकंठ|कालकण्ठः
कालकण्ठ m. (-ण्ठः)<BR>	 1. A name of ŚIVA.<BR>	 2. A water fowl, a gallinule.<BR>	 3.<BR>A sparrow.<BR>	 4. A peacock.<BR>	 5. A wagtail.<BR>	 6. A tree, (Pentaptera<BR>tomentosa:) see असन.<BR> E. काल black, and कण्ठ the throat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=177-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालकण्ठक|कालकण्ठकः
कालकण्ठक m. (-कः) A gallinule.<BR> E. कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=177-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालकर्णिका
कालकर्णिका f. (-का) Misfortune, misery; also कालकर्णी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=177-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालकन्दक|कालकन्दकः
कालकन्दक m. (-कः) A water snake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=177-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालकलाय|कालकलायः
कालकलाय m. (-यः) A sort of pulse, (Phaseolus max.)<BR> E. काल black,<BR>कलाय pulse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=177-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालकरण
कालकरण n. (-ष्णं) Appointing a time.<BR> E. काल, and करण making.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=177-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालकल्प
कालकल्प mfn. (-ल्पः-ल्पा-ल्पं) Like death, fatal, deadly.<BR> E. काल, and<BR>कल्प Loike.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=177-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालकस्तूरी
कालकस्तूरी f. (-री) A plant, (Hibiscus abelmoschus.)<BR> E. काल black, and<BR>कस्तूरी musk; the seeds having a smell of musk when rubbed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=178-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालकारित
कालकारित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Effected or brought about by or in time. E.<BR>काल, and कारित occasioned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=178-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालकील|कालकीलः
कालकील m. (-लः) A confused or mingled sound, a tumult; also<BR>कालकीलक m. (-कः.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=178-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालकुण्ठ|कालकुंठ|कालकुण्ठः
कालकुण्ठ m. (-ण्ठः) A name of YAMA.<BR> E. काल time, and कुण्ठ confusing,<BR>distressing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=178-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालकुष्ठ|कालकुष्ठः
कालकुष्ठ n. (-ष्ठं) A sort of earth from the mountains.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=178-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालकूट|कालकूटं|कालकूटः
कालकूट mn. (-टः-टं) A kind of poison.<BR> E. काल YAMA, कूट to destroy,<BR>अप् affix; destroying even the regent of death.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=178-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालकूटङ्कट
कालकूटङ्कट m. (-टः) A name of ŚIVA.<BR> E. कालकूट poison, and कट who<BR>takes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=178-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालकृत्
कालकृत् m. (-कृत्) The sun.<BR> E. काल time, and कृत् who makes; who<BR>marks the time; also कालकृत.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=178-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालकृत|कालकृतः
कालकृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Fixed, appointed, (as to time.)<BR>	 2. Lent or<BR>deposited by a giver.<BR>	 3. Produced or effected by time.<BR>	 m. (-तः)<BR>	 1.<BR>The sun: see the preceding.<BR>	 2. Time.<BR> E. काल and कृत done.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=178-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालक्षेप|कालक्षेपः
कालक्षेप m. (-पः) Spending or passing time.<BR> E. काल and क्षेप throwing<BR>away; also कालक्षेपण^1.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20260711. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/300.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=178-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालखञ्जन|कालखंजन|कालखञ्जनं
कालखञ्जन n. (-नं) The liver.<BR> E. काल black, and खजि to go, युच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=178-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालखण्ड|कालखंड|कालखण्डं
कालखण्ड n. (-ण्डं) The liver.<BR> E. काल black, and खण्ड part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=178-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालगन्ध
कालगन्ध m. (-न्धः) Kind of Cobra (de copella): see अलगर्द.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=178-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालग्रन्थि|कालग्रंथि|कालग्रन्थिः
कालग्रन्थि m. (-न्थिः) A year.<BR> E. काल time, and ग्रन्थि a knot or joint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=178-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालङ्कत|कालङ्कतः
कालङ्कत m. (-तः) A plant, (Cassia fistula.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=178-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालचक्र|कालचक्रं|कालचक्रः
कालचक्र n. (-क्रं)<BR>	 1. A cycle, a given revolution of time.<BR>	 2. A period,<BR>according to the Jainas, of twelve Aras: see अर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=178-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालञ्जर|कालंजर|कालंजरः|कालञ्जरः
कालञ्जर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A name of ŚIVA.<BR>	 2. The name of a rock in Bun-<BR>delkhand, the modern Kallinjer.<BR>	 3. The adjacent country.<BR>	 4. An<BR>assembly or collection of religious mendicants; Kallinjer is one<BR>of the places at which such assemblies meet, being enumerated in<BR>the Vedas amongst the Tapasyasthanas, or spots adapted to pra-<BR>ctices of austere devotion.<BR>	 f. (-रा or -री) An appellation of DURGĀ,<BR>E. काल in the second case, time or death, and जर who makes old,<BR>or causes to decay; irregularly deduced from the causal of जॄ to<BR>become old.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=178-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालज्ञ|कालज्ञः
कालज्ञ mfn. (-ज्ञः-ज्ञा-ज्ञं) One who knows times or season.<BR>	 m. (-ज्ञः)<BR>	 1. An<BR>astrologer.<BR>	 2. A cock.<BR> E. काल, and ज्ञ who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=178-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालदण्ड|कालदंड|कालदण्डः
कालदण्ड m. (-ण्डः) The staff of death, death.<BR> E. काल, and दण्ड staff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=178-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालधर्म्म|कालधर्म|कालधर्मः|कालधर्म्मः
कालधर्म्म m. (-र्म्मः)<BR>	 1. Death, dying.<BR>	 2. Influence of time, seasonableness,<BR>effects proper to the time or season.<BR> E. काल time, and धर्म्म virtue,<BR>property.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=178-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालनियोग|कालनियोगः
कालनियोग m. (-गः) Fate, destiny.<BR> E. काल and नियोग will.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=178-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालनिर्य्यास|कालनिर्यास|कालनिर्यासः|कालनिर्य्यासः
कालनिर्य्यास m. (-सः) A fragrant and resinous substance, (Bdellium): see<BR>गुग्गुल.<BR> E. काल black, and निर्य्यास an extract.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=178-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालनेमि|कालनेमिः
कालनेमि m. (-मिः)<BR>	 1. A demon, the son of HIRAṆYAKAŚIPU.<BR>	 2. A Rak-<BR>shasa described in the Rāmāyaṇa<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=178-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालनेमिन्
कालनेमिन् m. (-मी) A demon: see कालनेमि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=178-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालनेमिरिपु|कालनेमिरिपुः
कालनेमिरिपु m. (-पुः) An epithet of KṚṢṆA.<BR> E. कालनेमि the name of a<BR>demon who undertook to destroy the deity in his youth, and रिपु<BR>the foe: see similar names.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=178-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालनेमिहन्
कालनेमिहन् m. (-हा) KṚṢṆA or VIṢṆU. see the preceding.<BR> E. कालनेमि,<BR>and हन् who kills or destroys.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=178-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालनेम्यरि|कालनेम्यरिः
कालनेम्यरि m. (-रिः) See कालनेमिरिपु. E. As above, अरि a foe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=178-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालपक्व
कालपक्व mfn. (-क्वः-क्वाः-क्वं) Spontaneously ripened.<BR> E. काल and पक्व matured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=178-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालपर्ण|कालपर्णः|कालपर्ण्ण
कालपर्ण m. (-र्णः) A tree bearing dark coloured leaves, (Tabernæ<BR>montana coronaria,) commonly Tagara: see<BR> E. गत काल black, and<BR>पर्ण a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=178-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालपरिवास|कालपरिवासः
कालपरिवास m. (-सः) Standing for a time, (as to get stale or fermented,<BR>&c.)<BR> E. काल and परिवास abiding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=178-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालपाश|कालपाशः
कालपाश m. (-शः) The noose of YAMA or death.<BR> E. काल, and पाश a noose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=178-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालपुरुष|कालपुरुषः
कालपुरुष m. (-षः)<BR>	 1. One of YAMA'S attendants or ministers.<BR>	 2. An as-<BR>trological figure of a man, with the positions of the constella-<BR>tions, &c. inscribed on different parts of the body for the purpose<BR>of predicting his fortunes; also कालनर, &c.<BR> E. काल black, and पुरुष<BR>a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=178-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालपृष्ठ|कालपृष्ठं|कालपृष्ठः
कालपृष्ठ n. (-ष्ठं)<BR>	 1. The bow of KARṆA.<BR>	 2. A bow in general.<BR>	 m. (-ष्ठः)<BR>	 1.<BR>The black antelope.<BR>	 2. A heron.<BR> E. काल black. and पृष्ठ the back;<BR>black-backed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=178-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालप्रभात|कालप्रभातं
कालप्रभात n. (-तं) The sultry season, autumn, the two months follow-<BR>ing the rainy season.<BR> E. काल time, and प्रभात shining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=178-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालप्ररूढ
कालप्ररूढ mfn. (-ढः-ढा-ढं) Over-blown, over-ripe.<BR> E. काल, and प्ररूढ<BR>blown.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=178-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालबलन
कालबलन m. (-नः) Armour, mail.<BR> E. काल death, and बलन strengthen-<BR>ing, defending; perhaps a wrong reading for कायबलम, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=178-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालमान|कालमानः
कालमान m. (-नः) Black Tulasi; also read कालमाल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=178-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालमुष्कक|कालमुष्ककः
कालमुष्कक m. (-कः) A plant, (Bignonia Indica.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=178-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालमशिका
कालमशिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. Bengal madder, (Rubia manjith.)<BR>	 2. A black sort<BR>of Teori, a plant so called, a species of convolvulus: see काल-<BR>मेषिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=178-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालमेशी
कालमेशी f. (-शी) See कालमेषी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=178-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालमेषिका
कालमेषिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. Bengal madder.<BR>	 2. Black Teori: see त्रिवृता.<BR> E. काल<BR>black, मिष् to posses, अन् and ङीष् affixes, and कन् added; or with-<BR>out this affix, कालमेषी; also being derived from मिश् to sound.<BR>कालमेशिका and कालमेशी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=178-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालमेषी
कालमेषी f. (-षी)<BR>	 1. A plant, (Serratula anthelmintica.)<BR>	 2. Bengal<BR>madder, (Rubia manjith:) see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=178-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालयवन|कालयवनः
कालयवन m. (-नः) An Asura, an enemy of KṚṢṆA, destroyed by him<BR>by stratagem.<BR> E. काल black, यवन् a Yavana.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=178-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालयाप|कालयापः
कालयाप m. (-पः)<BR>	 1. Procrastination, putting off, delaying.<BR>	 2. Passing<BR>away time.<BR> E. काल, and या to go, causal form, घञ् affix; also<BR>with ल्युट्, कालयापनं; also यापः and यापनं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=178-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालरात्रि|कालरात्रिः
कालरात्रि m. (-त्रिः)<BR>	 1. A particular night, one which occurs on the 7th<BR>day of the 7th month of every 77th years; after such a period of<BR>life, a man is exempt from attention to the usual ordinances.<BR>	 2.<BR>The last night of a Kalpa 3. A dark night.<BR>	 4. A form of Śakti<BR>or DURGĀ.<BR> E. काल black, time, and रात्रि a night: see भीमरथी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=178-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काललवण|काललवणं
काललवण n. (-णं) A factitious and purgative salt, commonly Bitlavan<BR>or Bitnaban.<BR> E. काल black, and लवण salt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=178-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काललौह|काललौहं
काललौह n. (-हं) Iron.<BR> E. काल black, and लौह a metal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=178-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालवृक्ष
कालवृक्ष m. (-क्षः) A kind of vetch: see कालवृन्त.<BR> E. काल black, वृक्ष tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=178-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालवृद्धि|कालवृद्धिः
कालवृद्धि f. (-द्धिः) Periodical interest, payable monthly, &c.<BR> E. काल, and<BR>वृद्धि interest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=178-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालवृन्त|कालवृन्तः
कालवृन्त m. (-न्तः) A kind of vetch, (Dolichos biflorus.)<BR>	 f. (-न्ती) Trumpet<BR>flower.<BR> E. काल black, and वृन्त stalk: see कुलथ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=178-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालवेला
कालवेला f. (-ला) A season at which any act is improper, half a watch<BR>in every day.<BR> E. काल and वेला time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=178-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालशाक
कालशाक n. (-कं) A sort of potherb.<BR> E. काल black, शाक a potherb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=178-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालशेय|कालशेयं
कालशेय n. (-यं) Buttermilk.<BR> E. कलशी a jar, and ढक् affix; produced in<BR>a jar or pitcher by churning; also कालसेय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=178-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालसंरोध|कालसंरोधः
कालसंरोध m. (-धः) Lapse of a long period of time.<BR> E. काल time, संरोध<BR>impediment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=178-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालसदृश
कालसदृश mfn. (-शः-शी-शं)<BR>	 1. Opportune, seasonable.<BR>	 2. Deathlike.<BR> E. काल<BR>and सदृश like.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=178-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालसम्पन्न|कालसंपन्न
कालसम्पन्न mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>	 1. Dated, bearing a date.<BR>	 2. Effected by<BR>time.<BR> E. काल, and सम्पन्न produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=178-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालसर्प|कालसर्पः
कालसर्प m. (-र्पः) The black and most deadly variety of the cobra,<BR>(Coluber naga)<BR> E. काल black, and सर्प a serpent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=178-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालसार|कालसारं|कालसारः
कालसार m. (-रः) The black antelope, n. (-रं) A sort of Sandal.<BR> E. काल<BR>black, and सार essence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=178-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालसूत्र|कालसूत्रं
कालसूत्र n. (-त्रं) One of the twenty-one hells.<BR> E. काल from कल् to count,<BR>a reckoning, and सूत्र a thread, a rule; also with कन् added काल-<BR>सूत्रक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=179-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालसेय|कालसेयं
कालसेय n. (-यं) Buttermilk: see कालशेय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=179-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालस्कन्ध|कालस्कंध|कालस्कन्धः
कालस्कन्ध m. (-न्धः)<BR>	 1. A sort of ebony, (Diospyros melanoxylon, Rox.)<BR>2. The Tamala, a tree bearing dark blossoms.<BR>	 3. Another plant:<BR>see जीवक.<BR>	 4. The glomerous fig tree.<BR> E. काल black and स्कन्ध the<BR>trunk of a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=179-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालाकृष्ट
कालाकृष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>	 1. Led to death or destruction, drawn to or<BR>by one's fate.<BR>	 2. Produced or brought about by time.<BR> E. काल, and<BR>आकृष्ट attracted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=179-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालाक्षरिक|कालाक्षरिकः
कालाक्षरिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) A scholar, a pupil.<BR> E. काल time, अक्षर a<BR>letter. and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=179-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालागुरु
कालागुरु n. (-रु) A black kind of aloe wood or agallochum: see अगुरु. E.<BR>काल black, and अगुरु agallochum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=179-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालाग्नि|कालाग्निः
कालाग्नि m. (-ग्निः) The fire that is to destroy the world.<BR> E. काल, and<BR>अग्नि fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=179-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालाञ्जनी
कालाञ्जनी f. (-नी) A small shrub, used as a purgative.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=179-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालात्यय|कालात्ययः
कालात्यय m. (-यः) Loss or destruction by lapse of time.<BR> E. काल, and<BR>अत्यय destruction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=179-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालानुनादिन्
कालानुनादिन् m. (-दी)<BR>	 1. A large black bee.<BR>	 2. A sparrow.<BR>	 3. The fran-<BR>coline partridge.<BR> E. काल season, and अनुनादिन् who sings or sounds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=179-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालानुसारक|कालानुसारकं|कालानुसारकः
कालानुसारक n. (-कं)<BR>	 1. A tree, commonly Tagara 2. Yellow Sandal. E.<BR>काल, and अनुसार being like or conforming to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=179-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालानुसारि|कालानुसारिः
कालानुसारि m. (-रिः)<BR>	 1. Benzoin or benjamin.<BR> E. काल black, अनुसार<BR>resembling, being, and कि affix; also कालानुसार्य्य the affix being यत.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=179-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालानुसार्य्य|कालानुसार्य|कालानुसार्यः|कालानुसार्य्यं
कालानुसार्य्य n. (-र्य्यं)<BR>	 1. Gum benjamin or benzoin.<BR>	 2. A yellow fragrant<BR>wood from which a perfume is prepared.<BR>	 3. A timber tree, com-<BR>monly Sisu: see शिंशपा.<BR>	 4. A tree, commonly Tagara. E. See the<BR>preceding; also with कन् added कालानुसार्य्यक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=179-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालान्तक|कालांतक|कालान्तकः
कालान्तक m. (-कः) YAMA, death.<BR> E. काल and अन्तक destroyer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=179-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालान्तर|कालांतर
कालान्तर n. (-रं)<BR>	 1. Interval, intermediate time.<BR>	 2. Period, process of<BR>time.<BR>	 3. A former or another time.<BR> E. काल and अन्तर between &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=179-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालान्तरविष|कालांतरविष|कालान्तरविषः
कालान्तरविष m. (-षः) A poisonous animal, venomous only when enraged<BR>or alarmed, as a rat, &c.<BR> E. काल time, अन्तर after or at, and विष<BR>poison; having venom only at times.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=179-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालान्तरावृत|कालांतरावृत
कालान्तरावृत^1 mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Hidden or concealed by times.<BR> E. कालान्तर,<BR>and आवृत्त covered.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20260716. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/305.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=179-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालाप|कालापः
कालाप m. (-पः)<BR>	 1. A serpent's hood.<BR>	 2. A demon, an imp or goblin.<BR>	 3.<BR>A student of the Kalāpa grammar.<BR> E. कलाप, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=179-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालायस|कालायसं
कालायस n. (-सं) Iron.<BR> E. काल, and अयस् iron, टच aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=179-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालावधि|कालावधिः
कालावधि m. (-धिः) A fixed or appointed time.<BR> E. काल, and अवधि limit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=179-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालाशौच
कालाशौच n. (-चं) Season of mourning or impurity.<BR> E. काल and अशौच<BR>impurity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=179-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालिक|कालिकं|कालिकः
कालिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>	 1. Relating to time.<BR>	 2. Seasonable.<BR>	 3. Of long<BR>standing.<BR>	 4. Of a dark colour, black, blackish, &c.<BR>	 m. (-कः) The<BR>curlew.<BR>	 n. (-कं) A black kind of Sandal: see कालीयक.<BR>	 f. (-का)<BR>	 1.<BR>Cloudiness, a multitude or succession of clouds.<BR>	 2. A dark cloud<BR>threatening rain.<BR>	 3. A fog or mist, &c.<BR>	 4. The goddess GAURI.<BR>	 5.<BR>A terrific goddess, a form of CHANDI or DURGĀ.<BR>	 6. A female<BR>singer of Svarga.<BR>	 7. Blackness, a black colour.<BR>	 8. A fault or flaw<BR>in gold, &c.<BR>	 9. Spirituous liquor.<BR>	 10. A plant: see बृश्चिकपत्र.<BR>11. A kind of potherb.<BR>	 12. The branch of a cucumber plant.<BR>	 13.<BR>Spikenard.<BR>	 14. A line of hair extending to the navel.<BR>	 15. A female<BR>crow.<BR>	 16. Price of a commodity on credit, or a price to be paid at<BR>a fixed period, or by instalments.<BR>	 17. Periodical interest paid by<BR>the month, &c.<BR>	 18. An animalcule formed by the fermentation of<BR>milk.<BR>	 19. Ink or blacking.<BR>	 20. A small bird, commonly Śyama.<BR>21. A medicinal plant: see काकोलि.<BR> E. काल black, &c. ठक् or कन्<BR>affix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=179-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालिकता
कालिकता f. (-ता) Time, date, season.<BR> E. कालिक, and तल् affix; also with<BR>त्व, कालिकत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=179-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालिङ्ग|कालिंग|कालिङ्गं|कालिङ्गः
कालिङ्ग mfn. (-ङ्गः-ङ्गी-ङ्गः) Produced in or belonging to the Kalinga<BR>country.<BR>	 m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>	 1. An elephant.<BR>	 2. A snake.<BR>	 3. A species of<BR>cucumber, (Cucumis utilatissimus.)<BR>	 4. A sort of iron.<BR>	 f. (-ङ्गी) A<BR>gourd or cucumber.<BR>	 n. (-ङ्गं) The water melon.<BR> E. कलिङ्ग a country,<BR>and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=179-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालिदास|कालिदासः
कालिदास m. (-सः) The name of a celebrated poet, author of Sakuntala,<BR>Vikramorvasi, the Megha Duta, the Raghu Vansa, the Nalodoya<BR>and other poems: he was one of nine poets or gems of VIKRAMA-<BR>DITYA'S court, and is supposed to have flourished in the century<BR>preceding the Christian æra; the name is however applied to<BR>more persons than one, and seems, in measure, to have been<BR>used as an honorary title; the work attributed to this author are<BR>amongst the most elegant compositions in the Sanskrit language.<BR>E. काली the goddess DURGĀ, and दास a slave, the final of काली<BR>being made short.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=179-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालिदासक|कालिदासकः
कालिदासक m. (-कः) The poet KALIDASA: see the preceding.<BR> E. कन्<BR>added to कालिदास.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=179-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालिनी
कालिनी f. (-नी) One of the lunar mansions: see आर्द्रा.<BR> E. काल time affixes<BR>इनि and ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=179-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालिन्दक|कालिन्दकं
कालिन्दक n. (-कं) The water melon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=179-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालिन्दी|कालिंदी
कालिन्दी f. (-न्दी) The YAMUNĀ or JUMNA river.<BR> E. कालिन्द. A mountain,<BR>part of the Himālaya range, and the seat of the river's source,<BR>अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=179-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालिन्दीकर्षण|कालिंदीकर्षण|कालिन्दीकर्षणः
कालिन्दीकर्षण m. (-णः) A name of BALARĀMA.<BR> E. कालिन्दी the YAMUNĀ,<BR>and कर्षण the plougher; having diverted the stream into a new<BR>and devious channel, marked out by his ploughshare.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=179-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालिन्दीभेदन|कालिंदीभेदन|कालिन्दीभेदनः
कालिन्दीभेदन m. (-नः) BALARĀMA.<BR> E. कलिन्दी, and भिद् to break, affix<BR>ल्युट्ः see the preceding word.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=179-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालिन्दीसू|कालिंदीसू
कालिन्दीसू f. (-सूः) The wife of SŪRYA and mother of YAMUNĀ the per-<BR>sonified river.<BR> E. कालिन्दी, and सू who bears, from सू to bear child-<BR>ren, and क्विप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=179-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालिन्दीसोदर|कालिंदीसोदर|कालिन्दीसोदरः
कालिन्दीसोदर m. (-रः) YAMA.<BR> E. कालिन्दी, and सोदर brother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=179-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालिमन्
कालिमन् m. (-मा) Blackness.<BR> E. काल black, इमनिच aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=179-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालिय|कालियः
कालिय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Relating to time, &c.<BR>	 m. (-यः) A serpent des-<BR>troyed by KṚṢṆA.<BR> E. काल, and घ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=179-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालीक|कालीकः
कालीक m. (-कः) A curlew, a sort of heron: see कालिक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=179-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालीची
कालीची f. (-ची) The court of judgment of YAMA, regent and judge of<BR>the dead.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=179-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालीतनय|कालीतनयः
कालीतनय m. (-यः) A buffalo.<BR> E. काली the goddess, and तनय a son: i. e.<BR>a favourite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=179-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालीन
कालीन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Timely, seasonable, relating to time.<BR> E. काल,<BR>and ख aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=179-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालीय|कालीयं
कालीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Relating to time, to blackness, &c.<BR>	 n. (-यं) A<BR>dark of kind of Sandal, or perhaps of Agallochum: see कालीयक.<BR>E. काल black, and छ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=179-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालीयक|कालीयकं|कालीयकः
कालीयक n. (-कं)<BR>	 1. A yellow fragrant wood, perhaps a species of aloe<BR>wood.<BR>	 2. A dark kind of Sandal wood.<BR>	 m. (-कः) A species of tur-<BR>meric. (Curcuma zanthorhiza:) see दारुहरिद्रा.<BR> E. कन् added to the<BR>last, of a black or blackish hue; also कालीय, कालेय, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=179-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालुष्य|कालुष्यं
कालुष्य n. (-ष्यं) Foulness, dirtiness, turbidness, opacity. F. कलुष, and<BR>यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=179-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालेय|कालेयं|कालेयः
कालेय mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>	 1. Belonging to the Kali age, &c.<BR>	 2. Dark<BR>coloured.<BR>	 n. (-यं)<BR>	 1. A yellow fragrant wood: see कालीयक and<BR>कालेयक.<BR>	 2. The liver.<BR>	 m. (-यः) The name of a demon or imp. E.<BR>काल or कलि, and ढक् affix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=179-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालेयक|कालेयकं|कालेयकः
कालेयक m. (-कः) A sort of curcuma, (C. zanthorhiza, Rox.) see काली-<BR>यक.<BR>	 n. (-कं) A yellow fragrant wood.<BR> E. कन् added to the preceding<BR>word.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=179-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालोत्पादित
कालोत्पादित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Produced in due season.<BR> E. काल, उत्पादित<BR>engendered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=180-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालोप्त
कालोप्त mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं) Sown in due season.<BR> E. काल, and उप्त sown.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=180-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काल्प|काल्पः
काल्प mfn. (-ल्पः-ल्पा-ल्पं)<BR>	 1. Preceptive, ritual.<BR>	 2. Relating to a Kalpa or<BR>period so called.<BR>	 m. (-ल्पः) Zedoary, (Curcuma zerumbet.)<BR> E. कल्प<BR>a precept, and अण् affix; the plant forms a part of oblations<BR>offered upon certain occasions to fire; also with कन् added<BR>काल्पक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=180-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काल्पक|काल्पकः
काल्पक m. (-कः) Zedoary: see the preceding; also काल्यक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=180-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काल्पनिक|काल्पनिकः
काल्पनिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>	 1. Artificial, fabricated.<BR>	 2. Fictitious, in-<BR>vented.<BR> E. कल्पना and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=180-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काल्य|काल्यं
काल्य mfn. (-ल्यः-ल्या-ल्यं) Timely, seasonable.<BR>	 n. (-ल्यं) Dawn, day-break,<BR>see कल्य f. (-ल्या)<BR>	 1. A cow fit for the bull.<BR>	 2. (by confusion with kalyā)^1 Pleasant or auspicious<BR>discourse: see कल्या.<BR> E. काल time, and यत् aff.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20260718. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/309.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=180-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काल्यक|काल्यकः
काल्यक m. (-कः) Zedoary: see काल्पक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=180-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काल्याणिनेय
काल्याणिनेय mfn. (-यः-यी-यं) Sprung from a virtuous or fortunate woman.<BR>E. कल्याणी, and ढक् affix, इनञ inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=180-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कावचिक|कावचिकं
कावचिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Relating to armour, armorial.<BR>	 n. (-कं) A<BR>multitude of men in armour.<BR> E. कवच armour, and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=180-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कावरुक
कावरुक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Fearful, henpecked.<BR>	 m. (-कः) An owl.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=180-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कावाद
कावाद m. (-दः) Indistinct sound.<BR> E. का for कु bad वाद, speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=180-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कावार|कावारं
कावार n. (-रं) An aquatic plant, (Vallisneria,)<BR>	 f. (-री) An umbrella,<BR>Chattah, especially one without a stick, and worn like a broad<BR>brimmed hat.<BR> E. क the head, and आवार what covers or protects,<BR>from वृ to screen, and घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=180-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कावृक|कावृकः
कावृक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A gallinaceous fowl 2. The ruddy goose.<BR>	 3. A small<BR>singing bird, (Loxia philippensis:) see पीतमस्तक.<BR> E. क water, or क<BR>for कु bad, आङ् before वृ to cover, and कक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=180-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कावेर|कावेरं
कावेर n. (-रं) Saffron, (Crocus sativus.)<BR>	 f. (-री)<BR>	 1. A river in the Dekhin,<BR>the Kaveri.<BR>	 2. A courtezan, a harlot.<BR>	 3. Turmeric.<BR> E. कव to colour<BR>एरक् affix, and the radical vowel made long, fem. affix ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=180-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काव्य|काव्यं|काव्यः
काव्य m. (-व्यः) A name of SUKRACHARYA, the preceptor of the demons.<BR>f. (-व्या)<BR>	 1. Understanding, intelligence.<BR>	 2. A female fiend: see<BR>पूतना.<BR>	 3. A Pitṛ of a particular order, the son of KAVI or SUKRA.<BR>n. (-व्यं) A poem, poetical composition.<BR> E. कवि a poet, &c. ञ्यत्<BR>derivative or pleonastic aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=180-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काव्यचौर|काव्यचौरः
काव्यचौर m. (-रः) A plagiarist.<BR> E. काव्य a poem, and चौर a thief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=180-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काश|काशं|काशः
काश(ऋ)काशृ r. 1st cl. (काशते) also (उ ऋ) (उकाशृ) r. 4th cl. (काश्यते)<BR>1. To shine. With निर् prefixed. To expel.<BR>	 2. To hide or obscure;<BR>with प्र, To make or become manifest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=180-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काश|काशं|काशः
काश m. (-शः)<BR>	 1. Cough, catarrh: see कास.<BR>	 2. Sneezing.<BR>	 n. (-शं)<BR>	 1. A<BR>species of grass, (Saccharum spontaneum.)<BR>	 2. Irritation in the<BR>throat.<BR>	 f. (-शी) Kasi or Benares, the holy city so called. (-शी or -शा)<BR>Saccharum spontaneum, as above.<BR> E. कश् to sound, in the causal<BR>form, अच् affix; or काश् to shine, अच् and ङीष् fem. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=180-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काशक|काशकः
काशक m. (-कः) A species of long grass, (Saccharum, spontaneum.)<BR>E. कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=180-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काशमर्द्द|काशमर्द|काशमर्द्दः
काशमर्द्द m. (-र्द्दः) See कासमर्द्द.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=180-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काशाल्मलि|काशाल्मलिः
काशाल्मलि f. (-लिः) A kind of silk-cotton tree.<BR> E. का bad, inferior, and<BR>शाल्मलि the Simul tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=180-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काशि|काशिः
काशि f. (-शिः) Kasi a celebrated city and place of pilgrimage, the<BR>modern Benares.<BR> E. काश् to shine, to be beautiful or renowned,<BR>and इन् Uṇādi affix; also काशीः see काश and काशिका, काशिकी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=180-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काशिका
काशिका f. (-का) Kasi or Benares: see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=180-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काशिकाप्रिय|काशिकाप्रियः
काशिकाप्रिय m. (-यः) A name of DHANWANTARI, as king of Benares E.<BR>काशिका the city Kasi, and प्रिय a friend; also काशिराज.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=180-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काशिन्
काशिन् mfn. (-शी-शिनी-शि)<BR>	 1. Having a cold or cough.<BR>	 2. Shining bri-<BR>lliant.<BR> E. काश cough, and इनि affix, or काश् to shine, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=180-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काशिराज|काशिराजः
काशिराज m. (-जः) A name of DHANWANTARI or DIVODASA, a king of<BR>Benares, and an author of medical works; he is often confound-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=180-b" target="_blank">Page180-b+ 60</a>]<BR>ed with his celestial namesake, the physician of the gods.<BR> E. काशि<BR>the city, and राज a king or ruler; also काशीराज.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=180-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काशिल
काशिल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Made of kas grass, abounding with it, &c. E.<BR>काश and इल aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=180-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काशीनाथ|काशीनाथः
काशीनाथ m. (-थः) A name of ŚIVA.<BR> E. काशी Kasi or Benares, and भाव<BR>lord or master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=180-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काशीराज|काशीराजः
काशीराज m. (-जः) DIVODASA: see काशिराज.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=180-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काशीश|काशीशं
काशीश m. (-शः)<BR>	 1. ŚIVA.<BR>	 2. DIVODASA, or any king of Beuares.<BR>	 n. (-शं)<BR>Sulphate of iron.<BR> E. काशी and ईश lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=180-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काशूकार
काशूकार m. (-रः) The betel nut tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=180-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काश्मरो
काश्मरो f. (-री) A plant commonly Gambhari, (Gmelina arborea, Rox.)<BR>see गम्भारी.<BR> E. काश् to shine, and अर affix, formative irr.; also<BR>कार्श्मरो and काश्मर्य्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=180-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काश्मर्य्य|काश्मर्य|काश्मर्यः|काश्मर्य्यः
काश्मर्य्य mn. (-र्य्य-र्य्यं) Gambhari, a plant: see the preceding.<BR> E. यत्<BR>added to काश्मरी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=180-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काश्मीर|काश्मीरं|काश्मीरः
काश्मीर n. (-रं)<BR>	 1. A plant with a tuberous root, a sort of costus, (Cus-<BR>tus speciosus.)<BR>	 2. A country, Kashmir, or in the plu. (-राः) its<BR>inhabitants.<BR>	 f. (-री) A tree, (Ficus elastica.)<BR> E. कश्मीर Kashmir,<BR>and अण् affix; produced in that place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=180-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काश्मीरज|काश्मीरजं
काश्मीरज n. (-जं)<BR>	 1. A costus.<BR>	 2. Saffron: see कश्मीर.<BR>	 f. (-जः) Atis or<BR>Betula: see अतिविषा<BR> E. काश्मीर and ज born; produced in Kashmir.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=180-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काश्मीरजन्मन्
काश्मीरजन्मन् n. (-न्म) Saffron.<BR> E. काश्मीर, and जन्मन् birth produced in<BR>Kashmir.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=180-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काश्य|काश्यं
काश्य n. (-श्यं) Spirituous liquor.<BR>काश्यप m. (-पः)<BR>	 1. The name of a saint; also called KANADA, the<BR>son of KASYABA.<BR>	 2. A name of ARUṆA: see the next.<BR>	 3. A sort<BR>of deer.<BR>	 4. A tribe or Brahmans pretending to descend from<BR>KAŚYAPA.<BR> E. कश्यप a saint, and अण् affix of descent.<BR>	 n. (-पं) Flesh.<BR>E. काश्य spirituous liquor, and प from पा to drink or cherish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=180-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काश्यपि|काश्यपिः
काश्यपि m. (-पिः)<BR>	 1. A name of ARUṆA.<BR>	 2. A name of GARUḌA the bird<BR>of VIṢṆU.<BR> E. कश्यप the saint, and इञ् affix of descent, being both<BR>sons of KAŚYAPA.<BR>	 f. (-पी) The earth. E. As before: alluding to a<BR>legend from the Puranas, in which PARASURAMA, after the des-<BR>truction of the Kṣatriya race, and performance of an Aswame-<BR>dha, presented the sovereignty of the world to his Guru,<BR>KASYARA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=180-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काश्यपेय|काश्यपेयः
काश्यपेय m. (-यः) The sun.<BR> E. कश्यप the saint, and ढक् affix of decent,<BR>the son of KAŚYAPA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=180-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काश्वरी
काश्वरी f. (-री) A plant: see काश्मरी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=180-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काषाय
काषाय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Red, dyed of a reddish colour.<BR> E. कषाय and अण्<BR>aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=180-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काष्ठ|काष्ठं
काष्ठ n. (-ष्ठा-ष्ठं) Wood f.<BR>	 1. A quarter or region of the world space.<BR>tract.<BR>	 2. Place, site.<BR>	 3. Limit, boundary.<BR>	 4. A measure of,<BR>time the thirteenth part of a Kala, or eighteen twinkling.<BR>of the eye.<BR>	 5. Excellence, superiority.<BR>	 6. A plant, (Curcum zan-<BR>thorhiza, Rox.)<BR> E. काश् to shine, Uṇādi affix क्थन् changed to ष, and<BR>थ after ष becomes ठ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=180-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काष्ठक|काष्ठकं
काष्ठक n. (-क) Aloe wood or agallochum.<BR> E. कन् added to काष्ठ wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=180-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काष्ठकदली
काष्ठकदली f. (-ली) The wild plantain.<BR> E. काष्ठ, and कदली a plantain; the<BR>fruit being hard and woody.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=180-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काष्ठकीट|काष्ठकीटः
काष्ठकीट m. (-टः) A small insect or worm found in decayed wood. E.<BR>काष्ठ wood, and कीठ a worm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=180-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काष्ठकुट्ट|काष्ठकुट्टः
काष्ठकुट्ट m. (-ट्टः) A bird, a sort of woodpecker, (Picus Bengalensis) E.<BR>काष्ठ, and कुट्ट to cut, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=180-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काष्टकुद्दाल
काष्टकुद्दाल m. (-लः) A kind of wooden shovel or scraper used for baling<BR>water out of a boat. or for scraping and cleaning its bottom, &c.<BR>E. काष्ठ wood, and कुद्दाल shovel; also with the first vowel long<BR>कूद्दाल, काष्ठकूद्दाल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=180-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काष्ठखण्ड
काष्ठखण्ड n. (-ण्डं) A stick, a spar, a piece of wood.<BR> E. काष्ठ and खण्ड<BR>piece.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=180-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काष्ठतक्ष्
काष्ठतक्ष् m. (-ट्) A carpenter.<BR> E. काष्ठ wood, and तक्ष् to cut or pare,<BR>affix क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=181-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काष्ठाक्षक
काष्ठाक्षक m. (-कः) A carpenter: see the preceding. E. As before वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=181-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काष्ठतन्तु|काष्ठतंतु|काष्ठतन्तुः
काष्ठतन्तु m. (-न्तुः) A small worm that is found in timber.<BR> E. काष्ठ wood,<BR>and तन्तु what spreads, from तन् with तुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=181-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काष्ठदारु|काष्ठदारुः
काष्ठदारु m. (-रुः) The Deodar tree, (Uvaria longifolia.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=181-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काष्ठद्रु|काष्ठद्रुः
काष्ठद्रु m. (-द्रुः) A tree, (Butea frondosa.)<BR> E. काष्ठ, and द्रु a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=181-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काष्ठमठी
काष्ठमठी f. (-ठी) A funeral pile.<BR> E. काष्ठ wood, and मठी a pile, an edifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=181-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काष्ठमय
काष्ठमय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Wooden, made of wood.<BR> E. काष्ठ and मयट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=181-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काष्ठमल्ल|काष्ठमल्लः
काष्ठमल्ल m. (-ल्लः) A bier, a plank, &c. on which dead bodies are carried.<BR>E. काष्ठ wood, and मल्ल a vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=181-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काष्ठलेखक|काष्ठलेखकः
काष्ठलेखक m. (-कः) A small worm found in wood.<BR> E. काष्ठ and लेखक who<BR>writes or inscribes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=181-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काष्ठलौहिन्
काष्ठलौहिन् m. (-ही) A club, a short cudgel, especially if armed with<BR>iron.<BR> E. काष्ठ, लौह iron, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=181-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काष्ठवत्|काष्ठवन्त्
काष्ठवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Having wood for fuel, &c. ind. Like a piece<BR>of wood.<BR> E. काष्ठ, and मतुप् or वति aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=181-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काष्ठागार|काष्ठागारः
काष्ठागार m. (-रः) A wooden house or enclosure.<BR> E. काष्ठ and आगार a<BR>house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=181-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काष्ठाम्बुवाहिनी|काष्ठांबुवाहिनी
काष्ठाम्बुवाहिनी f. (-नी) A wooden bucket or baling vessel: see अम्बुवाहिनी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=181-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काष्ठिन्
काष्ठिन् mfn. (-ष्ठी-ष्ठिनी-ष्ठि)<BR>	 1. Of wood, wooden.<BR>	 2. Having wood.<BR> E. काष्ठ,<BR>and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=181-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काष्ठीला
काष्ठीला m. (-ला) A large kind of Colotropis.<BR>	 f. (-ला) A plantain: see<BR>रम्भा.<BR> E. का for कु small, अस्थि bone or stalk, and ला to get or posses<BR>क and टाप् affixes; having a stem which is good for nothing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=181-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कास|कासः
कास r. 1st cl. (ऋ) कासृ (कासते) 1. To make a bad sound, or one indi-<BR>cating disease; to cough.<BR>	 2. To shine: see काश.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=181-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कास|कासः
कास m. (-सः)<BR>	 1. Cough, catarrh.<BR>	 2. A species of reed or long grass,<BR>(Saccharum spontaneum.)<BR>	 3. Morunga, (Hyperanthera, &c.) see<BR>शीभाञ्जन.<BR> E. कास् to cough, to make an unpleasant sound, अच् affix:<BR>also काश् to shine, &c. see काश.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=181-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कासकुण्ठ|कासकुंठ|कासकुण्ठः
कासकुण्ठ mfn. (-ण्ठः-ण्ठा-ण्ठं) Afflicted with cough.<BR>	 m. (-ण्ठः) YAMA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=181-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कासघ्न|कासघ्नः
कासघ्न mfn. (-घ्नः-घ्नी-घ्नं) Removing or alleviating cough, pectoral.<BR>	 f. (-घ्नी)<BR>A short or prickly nightshade: see कण्टकारी.<BR> E. कास catarrh and घ्न<BR>from हन् to kill, removing cough.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=181-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कासनाशिनी
कासनाशिनी f. (-नी) A thorny plant: see कर्कटशृङ्गी.<BR> E. कास catarrh, and<BR>नाशिनी removing, remedying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=181-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कासुन्दीवटिका
कासुन्दीवटिका f. (-का) An acid drink.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=181-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कासमर्द्द|कासमर्द|कासमर्दः|कासमर्द्दः
कासमर्द्द m. (-र्द्दः)<BR>	 1. A plant, (Cassia or Senna esculenta.)<BR>	 2. An acid<BR>preparation, a mixture of tamarinds and mustard.<BR> E. कास or काश<BR>cough, and मर्द्द what destroys; also काशमर्द्द.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=181-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कासमर्द्दन|कासमर्दन|कासमर्द्दनः
कासमर्द्दन m. (-नः) A sort of cucumber, (Trichosanthes dioeca.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=181-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कासर|कासरः
कासर m. (-रः) A buffalo.<BR> E. क water, and आङ् prefixed to सृ to go,<BR>affix अप्; who frequents water, this animal being partial to<BR>marshy places.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=181-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कासार|कासारं|कासारः
कासार m. (-रः) A pond, a pool.<BR> E. क water, सृ to go, आङ् prefix, and<BR>घञ् affix, or कास् to shine, आरन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=181-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कासारि|कासारिः
कासारि m. (-रिः) A plant, (Cassia esculenta:) see कासमर्द्द्र<BR> E. कास cough,<BR>and अरि a foe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=181-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कासालु|कासालुः
कासालु m. (-लुः) An esculent root, a sort of Yam.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=181-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कासीस|कासीसं
कासीस n. (-सं) Green vitriol, green sulphate of iron.<BR> E. कास् to go, ईसण्<BR>aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=181-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कासू
कासू f. (-सूः)<BR>	 1. Indistinct speech.<BR>	 2. Speech in general.<BR>	 3. Understand-<BR>ing.<BR>	 4. Devotion.<BR>	 5. Light, lustre.<BR>	 6. A sort of spear or lance.<BR> E. कस्<BR>to go, to shine, or कास् to make a bad sound, क Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=181-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कासूतरी
कासूतरी f. (-री) A short spear, a javelin.<BR> E. कासू, and ष्टरच् diminutive<BR>aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=181-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काहका
काहका f. (-का) A musical instrument: see काहला.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=181-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काहल|काहलं|काहलः
काहल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>	 1. Dry, withered.<BR>	 2. Mischievous.<BR>	 3. Large,<BR>excessive.<BR>	 f. (-ली)<BR>	 1. One of the Apsaras or courtezans of INDRA'S<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=181-b" target="_blank">Page181-b+ 60</a>]<BR>heaven.<BR>	 2. The sound of any tube, pipe or musical instrument. (-ला)<BR>A young woman.<BR>	 mf. (-लः-ला) A horn, either a cow horn, or an<BR>instrument of that shape.<BR>	 m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. A cock.<BR>	 2. Sound in<BR>general.<BR>	 3. A cat.<BR>	 n. (-लं) Indistinct speech. adv. Much, excessive-<BR>ly.<BR> E. क pleasure, the head, &c. हल् to plough or divide, with आङ्<BR>prefixed, affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=181-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काहलापुष्प|काहलापुष्पः
काहलापुष्प m. (-ष्पः) Thorn apple, (Datura metel.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=181-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कि
कि r. 3rd cl. (चिकेति) To know: with निर् prefixed, to attain certainly,<BR>to ascertain positively. किं See किम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=181-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किंशारु|किंशारुः
किंशारु m. (-रुः)<BR>	 1. The beard of corn.<BR>	 2. An arrow.<BR>	 3. A heron.<BR> E. किं<BR>what, or sometimes, शृ to injure, &c. रुण् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=181-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किंशुक|किंशुकः
किंशुक m. (-कः) A tree bearing beautiful red blossoms, and hence often<BR>alluded to by the poets, (Butea frondośa;) also पलाश<BR> E. किं what,<BR>something, शुक a parrot; its red flowers being of the colour of a<BR>parrot's beak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=181-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किंशुलुक|किंशुलुकः
किंशुलुक m. (-कः) A species of the Kiṃśuka. see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=181-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किकि|किकिः
किकि m. (-किः) A blue jay,<BR> E. कि an imitative sound; the word being<BR>repeated; or कै to emit a sound, and कि affix; also किकीदीवि,<BR>किकी, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=181-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किकिदिवि|किकिदिविः
किकिदिवि m. (-विः) The blue jay.<BR> E. किकि, an imitative sound and दिव् to<BR>play, कि affix; also in other forms किकि, किकिदिव, किकिदीवि,<BR>किकीदिवी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=181-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किकीदिव|किकीदिवः
किकीदिव m. (-वः) See the preceding. E. As before, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=181-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किकीदीवि|किकीदीविः
किकीदीवि m. (-विः) See किकिदिवि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=181-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किखि|किखिः
किखि m. (-खिः) A monkey, an ape.<BR>	 f. (-खिः) A small jackal, a fox.<BR> E. कु<BR>to sound, डिखि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=181-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किङ्कर|किंकर|किङ्करः
किङ्कर mfn. (-रः-रा or -री-रं) A servant.<BR> E. किं what or something, and<BR>कर who does.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=181-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किङ्किणि
किङ्किणि f. (-णिः or -णी)<BR>	 1. A girdle of small bells, or any tinkling orna-<BR>ment.<BR>	 2. An acid sort of grape.<BR> E. किं some, and किण an imitative<BR>sound, affix क, with इन् or ङीष् fem. affix; also with कन् added<BR>किङ्किणीका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=181-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किङ्किर|किंकिर|किङ्किरं|किंकिरः|किङ्किरः
किङ्किर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. The Indian cuckoo, the Koil or Kokila.<BR>	 2. A large<BR>black bee.<BR>	 3. A horse.<BR>	 4. KĀMADEVA.<BR>	 f. (-रा) Blood.<BR>	 n. (-रं) The<BR>frontal sinus of an elephant.<BR> E. किं something, कॄ to scatter, क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=181-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किङ्किरात|किंकिरात|किंकिरातः|किङ्किरातः
किङ्किरात m. (-तः)<BR>	 1. A name of KĀMADEVA.<BR>	 2. A parrot.<BR>	 3. The Koil or<BR>Indian cuckoo.<BR>	 4. A tree, (Jonesia asoka.)<BR>	 5. A species of barleria:<BR>see झिण्टी.<BR> E. किङ्किर as above, and अत who goes or is.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=181-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किङ्किरिन्
किङ्किरिन् m. (-री) A plant, commonly Buinchhi, (Flacourtia sapida,<BR>Rox.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=181-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किञ्च|किंच
किञ्च ind.<BR>	 1. An inceptive or continuative particle, (moreover further,<BR>again.)<BR>	 2. A particle of comprehension.<BR> E. किं what, च and.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=181-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किञ्चन|किंचन|किञ्चनः
किञ्चन m. (-नः) A species of the Palasa or Butea frondosa. ind. Some-<BR>what something.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=181-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किञ्चनता|किंचनता
किञ्चनता f. (-ता) Somewhat, something.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=181-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किञ्चित्|किंचित्
किञ्चित् ind.<BR>	 1. Something somewhat.<BR>	 2. A part, a little.<BR>	 n. किं what,<BR>चित् to think, affix क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=181-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किञ्चिलिक|किंचिलिकः|किञ्चिलिकः
किञ्चिलिक m. (-कः) See the following.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=181-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किञ्चलुक
किञ्चलुक m. (-कः) A worm.<BR> E. किञ्चित् a little, and चल् to go, or चुल् to be<BR>high, वुन् affix, deriv. irr.; it is sometimes written किञ्चिलिक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=181-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किञ्ज|किंज|किंजं|किञ्जं
किञ्ज n. (-ञ्जं) The filament of a lotus: see किञ्जल्क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=181-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किञ्जल|किंजल|किंजलः|किञ्जलः
किञ्जल m. (-लः) The filament of a lotus: see किञ्जल्क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=181-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किञ्जल्क|किंजल्क|किञ्जल्कं|किंजल्कः|किञ्जल्कः
किञ्जल्क m. (-ल्कः) The filament of a lotus, great numbers of which sur-<BR>round the pericarp.<BR>	 n. (-ल्कं) The flower of the Mesua ferrea. E.<BR>किञ्चित् somewhat, जक् to hide or cover, क affix, and the form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=181-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किट
किट r. 1st cl. (केटति)<BR>	 1. To go or approach.<BR>	 2. To alarm or terrify.<BR>	 3. To<BR>dread, to fear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=181-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किटि|किटिः
किटि m. (-टिः) A hog.<BR> E. किट् to go, and कि affix; also किटि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=181-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किटिभ|किटिभः
किटिभ m. (-भः) A bug.<BR> E. किटि a hog, भ who resembles, from भा to<BR>shine, affix ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=181-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किट्ट|किट्टं
किट्ट n. (-ट्टं) Excrement, excretion, dirt.<BR> E. किट् to go, here implying to<BR>go out of, (the body, &c.) and क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=182-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किट्टवर्जित|किट्टवर्ज्जित|किट्टवर्ज्जितं
किट्टवर्जित n. (-तं) Semen virile.<BR> E. किट्ट dirt, &c. वर्जित deprived.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=182-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किट्टाल|किट्टालः
किट्टाल m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. A copper vessel.<BR>	 2. Scoria, rust of iron, &c.<BR> E. किट्ट<BR>dirt, अल् to be able, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=182-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किण|किणः
किण m. (-णः)<BR>	 1. A wart, a mole.<BR>	 2. A scar.<BR>	 3. A corn, a callosity.<BR>4. An insect found in wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=182-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किणि|किणिः
किणि f. (-णिः) A tree, (Achyranthes aspera:) see अपामार्ग.<BR> E. किण् a<BR>scar, and कि affix; making scars; that is cicatrizing wounds,<BR>sores, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=182-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किणिही
किणिही f. (-ही) Achyranthes aspera.<BR> E. किणि a sore, and ह what re-<BR>moves, fem. affix ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=182-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किण्व|किण्वं|किण्वः
किण्व mn. (-ण्वः-ण्वं) Ferment, a drug or seed used to produce fermenta-<BR>tion, in the manufacture of spirits from sugar, bassia, &c.<BR>	 n. (-ण्वं)<BR>Sin.<BR> E. कण् to sound, &c. क्वन् Uṇādi affix, and the इ irregularly in-<BR>serted: see कण्व.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=182-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कित
कित r. 1st cl. (चिकित्सति)<BR>	 1. To cure, to administer remedies, to practise<BR>physic.<BR>	 2. To remove, to destroy.<BR>	 3. To chastise.<BR>	 4. (Usually with<BR>वि prefixed,) To doubt; this root is regular. r. 3rd cl. (चिकेति) To<BR>know. r. 10th cl. (केतयति)<BR>	 1. To dwell.<BR>	 2. To desire; some authori-<BR>ties make it a regular root of the 1st cl. in these senses, and others<BR>deny its admitting of any conjugation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=182-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कितव|कितवः
कितव mfn. (-वः-वा-वं)<BR>	 1. A gamester, a gambler.<BR>	 2. A cheat, cheating,<BR>fraudulent.<BR>	 3. Mad, crazy.<BR>	 4. Mischievous, malicious.<BR>	 m. (-वः)<BR>	 1.<BR>Thorn apple, (Datura metel.)<BR>	 2. A kind of perfume, commonly<BR>Rochana.<BR> E. किं what, तव your, (what is your stake or wager?) he<BR>who asks such a question, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=182-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किन्तनु|किंतनु|किन्तनुः
किन्तनु m. (-नुः) An insect described as having eight legs and a very<BR>slender body, a species of spider.<BR> E. किं for किञ्चित् a little, and तनु<BR>the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=182-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किन्तमाम्|किंतमाम्
किन्तमाम् ind. Whether, either of any.<BR> E. किं, and तमप् with आमु added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=182-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किन्तराम्|किंतराम्
किन्तराम् ind. Whether, either of two.<BR> E. किं, and तरप् with आमु added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=182-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किन्तु|किंतु
किन्तु ind.<BR>	 1. But.<BR>	 2. Moreover, further. E. A compound particle of किं<BR>and तु disjunctive particle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=182-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किन्तुघ्न|किंतुघ्न|किन्तुघ्नः
किन्तुघ्न m. (-घ्नः) One of the eleven periods called Karanas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=182-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किन्धिन्|किंधिन्
किन्धिन् m. (-न्धी) A horse: see किल्किन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=182-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किन्नर|किंनर|किन्नरः
किन्नर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A demigod attached to the service of KUVERA, a<BR>celestial chorister or musician.<BR>	 2. A kind of flower or attendant on<BR>a Jina or Jaina saint.<BR>	 f. (-री) A female Kinnara, or chorister.<BR> E. किं<BR>what, used contemptuously, (what kind of) नर a man: the Kinnara<BR>having, with the human figure, the head of a horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=182-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किन्नरेश|किंनरेश|किन्नरेशः
किन्नरेश m. (-शः) A name of KUVERA.<BR> E. किन्नर a Kinnara, and ईश master,<BR>lord; also other similar compounds, as किन्नरेश्वर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=182-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किन्नु|किंनु
किन्नु ind.<BR>	 1. A particle of interrogation, (what?)<BR>	 2. Doubt, (how, what?)<BR>3. Comparison, (thus, as, like, how much less)<BR>	 4. Conjunction,<BR>(again, further.)<BR>	 5. Place, location, and 6. Agency.<BR> E. किम् and नु<BR>conjoined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=182-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किम्
किम् ind. (-किम् or किं)<BR>	 1. What, how.<BR>	 2. Either, or; a particle of doubt<BR>or interrogation.<BR>	 3. A particle of contempt. The relative pronoun.<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-किं) What, who, which expressing, 1. Doubt.<BR>	 2. In-<BR>terrogation.<BR>	 3. Disdain.<BR>	 4. Reproach, (as in English, Who are you,<BR>&c.)<BR>	 5. Kind, sort.<BR> E. कै to sound, डिमि Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=182-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किमर्थम्
किमर्थम् ind. What for, wherefore, why.<BR> E. किम् and अर्थ object.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=182-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किमु
किमु ind. Either, or, whether implying doubt or discrimination: see किम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=182-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किमुत
किमुत ind.<BR>	 1. Either, or, whether, implying.<BR>	 2. Doubt or discrimina-<BR>tion.<BR>	 3. Much, exceeding; a particle of magnitude or quantity.<BR>	 4.<BR>An interrogative, how, what, &c. see किम्.<BR> E. किम् and the particle उत.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=182-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किम्पच|किंपच|किम्पचः
किम्पच mfn. (-चः-चा-चं) Miserly, avaricious.<BR> E. किम् what, (nothing,) पच<BR>who cooks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=182-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किम्पचान|किंपचान|किम्पचानः
किम्पचान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Miserly, niggardly, avaricious.<BR> E. किं what,<BR>used contemptuously, पच् to cook, and शानच् affix, or with अच् only,<BR>किम्पचः see मितम्पच, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=182-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किम्पाक|किंपाक|किम्पाकः
किम्पाक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Mother-led, infantine, childish.<BR>	 m. (-कः) A cu-<BR>curbitaceous plant, (Trichosanthes palmata; also Cucumis colocyn-<BR>thus.)<BR> E. किं depreciative, and पाक what is ripe or mature.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=182-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किम्पुरुव
किम्पुरुव m. (-षः)<BR>	 1. A heavenly musician: see किन्नर.<BR>	 2. A division of<BR>the universe, one of the nine Khandas or portions into which the<BR>world is divided, and described as the country between the<BR>Himachala and Hemakuta mountains.<BR>	 3. A despicable or low man.<BR>E. किम् what, contemptuously, and पुरुष a man; also with the first<BR>vowel of that word lengthened, किम्पूरुष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=182-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किम्पुरुषेश्वर|किंपुरुषेश्वर|किम्पुरुषेश्वरः
किम्पुरुषेश्वर m. (-रः) An epithet of KUVERA: see किन्नरेश.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=182-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किम्पूरुष|किंपूरुष|किम्पूरुषं
किम्पूरुष n. (-षं) The division of the world, called by this name: see<BR>किम्पुरुष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=182-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किम्भरा|किंभरा
किम्भरा f. (-रा) A kind of perfume, commonly Nali: see नली.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=182-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किम्भूत|किंभूत
किम्भूत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) or n. only, (-तं) How, in what manner or degree,<BR>like what.<BR> E. किम्, and भूत become.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=182-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किंवत्|किंवन्त्
किंवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Poor, mean, insignificant.<BR> E. किं a little, मतुप्<BR>possessive aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=182-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किंवदन्ति|किंवदंति|किंवदन्तिः
किंवदन्ति f. (-न्तिः) Rumour, report.<BR> E. किं what, वद् to say, and झिच् Uṇādi<BR>affix, or with झच् and ङीष् affixes किंवदन्ती.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=182-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किंवा
किंवा ind. Or, else, moreover.<BR> E. किं what, वा or.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=182-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कियत्|कियन्त्
कियत् mfn. (-यान्-यती-यत्)<BR>	 1. How much, how many, ind. (-यत्)<BR>	 1. A little.<BR>2. How much, used chiefly in composition; as कियत्काल how long,<BR>for a short time; कियदवधि or कियत्पर्य्यन्तं how far, or for a little way.<BR>E. किं and मतुप् affix, and य is substituted for the व.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=182-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कियदेतिका
कियदेतिका f. (-का) Effort, vigorous and persevering exertions. E.<BR>कियत् used contemptuously, and इति from इदम् this, affix ठक्; (how<BR>great a task is this, that it should not be effected, &c.) इह here,<BR>being employed in place of इति, the word is written कियदेहिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=182-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कियद्दूर
कियद्दूर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) For a short distance, a little way.<BR> E. कियत्, and<BR>दूर far.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=182-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कियाह|कियाहः
कियाह m. (-हः) A horse of a red or bay colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=182-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किर|किरः
किर m. (-रः) A hog.<BR> E. कॄ to scatter, क affix; also किरि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=182-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किरक|किरकः
किरक m. (-कः) A scribe.<BR> E. कॄ to scatter, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=182-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किरण|किरणः
किरण m. (-णः)<BR>	 1. A ray of light, a sun or moon beam.<BR>	 2. The sun.<BR>E. क to scatter, (light,) and क्यु Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=182-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किरणमय
किरणमय mfn. (-यः-यी-यं) Radiant, bright, refulgent.<BR> E. किरण and<BR>मयट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=182-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किरणमालिन्
किरणमालिन् m. (-ली) The sun.<BR> E. किरण, माला a garland, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=182-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किरत्
किरत् mfn. (-रन्-रन्ती-रत्)<BR>	 1. Scattering, spreading.<BR>	 2. Lighting, shedd-<BR>ing light.<BR> E. कॄ to scatter शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=182-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किरात|किरातः
किरात m. (-तः)<BR>	 1. A savage, one of the barbarous tribes who inhabit<BR>woods and mountains and live by the chase, the Kirrhadœ of<BR>Arrian.<BR>	 2. ŚIVA as a mountaineer opposed to ARJUNA, the account<BR>of which is the subject of the poem, the Kiratarjuniya.<BR>	 3. A kind<BR>of gentian: see किराततिक्त.<BR>	 4. A pigmy a dwarf.<BR>	 5. A groom, a<BR>horseman.<BR>	 f. (-ती)<BR>	 1. The river GANGES or its goddess.<BR>	 2. A name<BR>of DURGĀ.<BR>	 3. A bawd, a procuress.<BR>	 4. The celestial GANGES or<BR>river of Svarga.<BR> E. कॄ to scatter, (speech, &c.) and अत who goes;<BR>also किरातक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=182-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किराततिक्त|किराततिक्तः
किराततिक्त m. (-क्तः) A kind of gentian, (Gentiana cherayta.)<BR> E. किरात a<BR>savage, तिक्त pungent, bitter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=182-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किराताशिन्
किराताशिन् m. (-शी) A name of GURUDA the bird of VIṢṆU.<BR> E. किरात a<BR>pigmy, and अशिन् who eats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=182-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किराति|किरातिः
किराति f. (-तिः) A name of the GANGES.<BR> E. कॄ to scatter, (sound, &c.)<BR>to make a murmuring noise, अत who goes, and इन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=182-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किरातिनी
किरातिनी f. (-नी) Indian spikenard; see जटामांसी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=182-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किरि|किरिः
किरि m. (-रिः) A hog.<BR> E. कॄ to scatter, (dirt, &c.) and इ Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=182-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किरिटि|किरिटिः
किरिटि n. (-टिः) The fruit of the marshy date tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=183-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किरीट|किरीटं|किरीटः
किरीट mn. (-टः-टं) A crest, a diadem.<BR> E. कॄ to scatter, (pearls, &c.) and<BR>कीटन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=183-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किरीटधारण
किरीटधारण n. (-णं) Wearing a tiara, assuming the crown.<BR> E. किरीट, and<BR>धारण bearing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=183-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किरीटधारिन्
किरीटधारिन् mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि) Crowned, having a tiara.<BR>	 m. (-री) A king.<BR>E. किरीट, and धारिन् who wears.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=183-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किरीटिन्
किरीटिन् mfn. (-टी-टिनी-टि) Crested, crowned.<BR>	 m. (-टी)<BR>	 1. A king.<BR>	 2. A<BR>name of ARJUNA.<BR> E. किरीट a crest, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=183-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किर्म्मी|किर्मी
किर्म्मी f. (-र्म्मी) The Palasa tree: see षलाश.<BR>	 2. A hall, a building, an<BR>apartment.<BR>	 3. An image of gold.<BR>	 4. A figure of iron.<BR> E. कृ to<BR>make, मन् and ङीप् affixes, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=183-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किर्म्मीर|किर्मीर|किर्मीरः|किर्म्मीरः
किर्म्मीर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Variegated.<BR>	 m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. The orange tree.<BR>	 2. The<BR>name of a Rākṣasa or goblin.<BR>	 3. A variegated colour.<BR> E. क to<BR>scatter, ईरन् affix; and मुट् inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=183-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किर्म्मीरजित्|किर्मीरजित्
किर्म्मीरजित् m. (-जित्) A name of BHIMA, one of the Pandu princes.<BR>E. किर्म्मीर a demon, and जित् who conquers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=183-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किर्म्मीरत्वच्|किर्मीरत्वच्
किर्म्मीरत्वच् f. (-त्वक्) The orange tree.<BR> E. किर्म्मीर variegated, and त्वच्<BR>bark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=183-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किर्म्मीरभिद्
किर्म्मीरभिद् m. (-भित् or -भिद्) A name of BHIMA: see किर्म्मीरजित्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=183-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किर्म्मीरसूदन|किर्मीरसूदन|किर्मीरसूदनः|किर्म्मीरसूदनः
किर्म्मीरसूदन m. (-नः) A name of BHIMA: see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=183-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किल|किलः
किल r. 6th cl. (किलति)<BR>	 1. To be or become white.<BR>	 2. To play. r. 10th<BR>cl. (केलयति) To send, to throw or cast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=183-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किल|किलः
किल ind. An aptote signifying.<BR>	 1. News, (so said, so reported.)<BR>	 2.<BR>Likelihood, (probably, possibly.)<BR>	 3. Conciliatory expression.<BR>	 4.<BR>Assertion, certainty, (indeed, verily, assuredly.)<BR>	 5. Falsehood,<BR>inaccuracy.<BR> E. किल् to send or order, affix क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=183-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किलकिञ्चित|किलकिंचित|किलकिञ्चितं
किलकिञ्चित n. (-तं) Armorous agitation, weeping, laughing, being angry,<BR>being pleased, &c. in the society of a lover.<BR> E. किल play, sport, किं<BR>what, some, and चित collected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=183-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किलकिला
किलकिला f. (-ला) Sound expressing joy, or the expression or pleasure<BR>by any sound or cry.<BR> E. किल play, sport, repeated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=183-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किलाट|किलाटः
किलाट mf. (-टः-टी) Inspissated milk, curds or coagulated milk; it<BR>may be applied to cheese.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=183-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किलाटिन्
किलाटिन् m. (-टी) A bamboo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=183-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किलास|किलासं
किलास m. (-सः)<BR>	 1. A blotch, a scab.<BR>	 2. A white leprous spot.<BR> E. किल् to<BR>play, affix क; आस from आस् to reject or throw, with अच् affix; or<BR>अस् to be, with अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=183-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किलासघ्न|किलासघ्नः
किलासघ्न m. (-घ्नः) A sort of gourd, (Momordica mixta:) see काकरोल. E.<BR>किलास a blotch, and घ्न what removes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=183-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किलासिन्
किलासिन् mfn. (-सी-सिनी-सि) Having blotches.<BR> E. किलास, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=183-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किलिञ्च|किलिञ्चं
किलिञ्च mn. (-ञ्चः-ञ्चं) A thin plank: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=183-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किलिञ्ज|किलिंज|किलिंजं|किलिञ्जः
किलिञ्ज mn. (-ञ्जः-ञ्जं)<BR>	 1. A thin plank of green wood.<BR>	 2. A mat: see the<BR>next; also read किलिञ्च.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=183-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किलिञ्जक|किलिंजकः|किलिञ्जकः
किलिञ्जक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A mat.<BR>	 2. A screen or twist of grass or straw. E.<BR>किल to be white, इ added किलि, ज what overcomes, from जि with ड<BR>affix, and वुन् added; deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=183-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किलिम|किलिमं
किलिम m. (-मः) A tree, a kind of fir or pine, (Pinus deodar.)<BR>	 n. (-मं)<BR>Resin, the extract of the pine.<BR> E. किल् to cast, किमन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=183-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किल्विन्
किल्विन् m. (-ल्वी) A horse; read also किन्धिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=183-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किल्विष|किल्विषं
किल्विष n. (-षं)<BR>	 1. Sin, 2. Fault, offence.<BR>	 3. Disease, sickness.<BR> E. किल् to<BR>play sport, टिषच् Uṇādi affix, and वुक् inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=183-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किल्विषिन्
किल्विषिन् mfn. (-षी-षिणी-षि) Wicked, culpable, criminal.<BR> E. किल्विष, and<BR>इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=183-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किशल|किशलं
किशल mn. (-लः-लं) A sprout, a shoot: see किसल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=183-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किशलय|किशलयं|किशलयः
किशलय mn. (-यः-यं) A young shoot: see किसलय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=183-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किशलयतल्प
किशलयतल्प m. (-ल्पः) A bed of young leaves, &c.<BR> E. किशलय and तल्प a<BR>couch; also किशलयशय्या किशलयशयनं, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=183-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किशोर|किशोरः
किशोर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Young, infantine.<BR>	 m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A colt.<BR>	 2. The sun.<BR>3. Benjamin, (Styrax benzoin.)<BR>	 4. A youth, a lad, one from his<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=183-b" target="_blank">Page183-b+ 60</a>]<BR>birth to the end of his fifteenth year: a minor in law अजातव्यवहारः<BR>becoming, after his fifteenth year, subject to suits at law or<BR>जातव्यवहार<BR> E. किम् what, used contemptuously, श to go, and ओरन्<BR>Uṇādi affix; also कन् added किशोरकः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=183-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किष्क
किष्क r. 10th cl. (किष्कयते) To kill. to injure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=183-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किष्किन्ध|किष्किंध|किष्किंधः|किष्किन्धः
किष्किन्ध m. (-न्धः) A mountain in the south of India, in Mysore, the<BR>residence of the monkey prince BALI.<BR>	 f. (-न्धा) A cave in the moun-<BR>tain; also किष्किन्ध्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=183-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किष्किन्ध्य|किष्किंध्य|किष्किंध्यः|किष्किन्ध्यः
किष्किन्ध्य m. (-न्ध्यः) The mountain Kishkindhya, situated in the peninsula<BR>in the northern part of Mysore, near the sources of the pampa<BR>river, the territory of BALI. the monkey, from whom it was con-<BR>quered by RAMA, and transferred to SUGRĪVA, another monkey<BR>chief.<BR>	 f. (-न्ध्या) A cave in the mountain of Kishkindhya, the pecu-<BR>liar residence of BALI; also किष्किन्ध.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=183-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किष्किन्ध्याधिप|किष्किन्ध्याधिपः
किष्किन्ध्याधिप m. (-पः) A name of BALI, a monkey king slain by RAMA.<BR>E. किष्किन्ध्य and अधिप ruler.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=183-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किष्कु|किष्कुः
किष्कु mfn. (-ष्कुः-ष्कुः-ष्कु) Vile, bad, contemptible.<BR>	 mf. (-ष्कुः)<BR>	 1. A cubit.<BR>2. A span.<BR>	 3. The fore-arm.<BR> E. कै to sound, डिष्कु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=183-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किष्कुपर्व्वन्|किष्कुपर्वन्
किष्कुपर्व्वन् m. (-र्व्वा)<BR>	 1. Sugar-cane.<BR>	 2. A bamboo.<BR>	 3. A reed, (Arundo<BR>tibialis.)<BR> E. किष्कु a span or cubit, and पर्व्वन् a joint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=183-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किसल|किसलं|किसलः
किसल mn. (-लः-लं) A sprout or shoot, the extremity of a branch bearing<BR>new leaves.<BR> E. किं diminutive, सल् to go, अच् affix; also किशल and<BR>किशलय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=183-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किसलय|किसलयं|किसलयः
किसलय mn. (-यः-यं) A sprout, a young shoot: see the preceding. E. As<BR>before, affix कयञ्; also किशलय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=183-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीकट|कीकटः
कीकट mfn. (-टः-टी-टं)<BR>	 1. Miserly, avaricious.<BR>	 2. Poor, needy.<BR>	 m. (-टः)<BR>	 1.<BR>A country, (Behar;) or m. plu. (-टाः) its inhabitants.<BR>	 2. A horse. E.<BR>ककि to go, अटच् affix, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=183-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीकस|कीकसं|कीकसः
कीकस mfn. (-सः-सा-सं) Hard, firm.<BR>	 n. (-सं) A bone.<BR>	 m. (-सः) A worm, an<BR>insect.<BR> E. की derived from किम् what, a depreciating particle, before<BR>कस् to go, affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=183-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीकसास्य|कीकसास्यः
कीकसास्य m. (-स्यः) A bird in general.<BR> E. कीकस a bone, and आस्य face or<BR>or mouth; alluding to the osseous structure of the beak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=183-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीकि|कीकिः
कीकि m. (-किः) A blue jay: see किकि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=183-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीचक|कीचकः
कीचक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A bamboo whistling or rattling in the wind.<BR>	 2. Any<BR>hollow bamboo.<BR>	 3. A reed.<BR>	 4. A Daitya or infernal demon so<BR>named.<BR>	 5. A particular Rākṣasa or goblin.<BR>	 6. A kind of tree.<BR>	 7. A<BR>prince, the son of KEKAYA.<BR> E. चीक to touch, to sound, वुन् Uṇādi<BR>affix, and the radical consonants transposed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=183-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीचकजित्
कीचकजित् m. (-जित्) A name of BHIMA.<BR> E. कीचक a goblin, and जित् who conquers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=183-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीचकनिसूदन|कीचकनिसूदनः
कीचकनिसूदन m. (-नः) BHIMA: see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=183-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीचकभिद्
कीचकभिद् m. (-भित्) See the two words preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=183-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीट|कीटः
कीट r. 11th cl. (कीटयति)<BR>	 1. To tinge or colour.<BR>	 2. To bind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=183-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीट|कीटः
कीट m. (-टः) A worm, an insect.<BR> E. कीट् to colour or dye, क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=183-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीटक|कीटकः
कीटक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Harsh, hard, unfeeling.<BR>	 m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A worm, an<BR>insect.<BR>	 2. A bird, panegyrist, descended from a Kṣatriya father<BR>and Vaiśya mother.<BR> E. कीट a worm, and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=183-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीटघ्न|कीटघ्नः
कीटघ्न m. (-घ्नः) Sulphur.<BR> E. कीट a worm, and घ्न what destroys.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=183-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीटज
कीटज n. (-जं) Silk.<BR>	 f. (-जा) Lac, an animal dye of a red colour.<BR> E. कीट a<BR>worm, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=183-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीटपक्षोद्भव
कीटपक्षोद्भव m. (-वः) The change from the chrysalis or larva to the but-<BR>terfly.<BR> E. कीट, पक्ष a wing, and उद्भव evolution.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=183-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीटपादिका
कीटपादिका f. (-का) A plant, (Cissus pedata.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=183-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीदृश्
कीदृश् mfn. (-दृक्) Who or what like.<BR> E. किम् what, दृश् to see, and क्विन्<BR>affix; also with कञ् affix; कीदृश mfn. (-शः-शी-शं.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=183-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीनाश|कीनाशः
कीनाश mfn. (-शः-शी-शं)<BR>	 1. A labourer or cultivator of the soil.<BR>	 2. Small,<BR>little.<BR>	 3. Covetous, niggardly.<BR>	 4. A slayer of cattle.<BR>	 m. (-शः)<BR>	 1. A<BR>name of YAMA.<BR>	 2. A particular monkey.<BR> E. की for का or कु bad,<BR>vile, नाश who destroy, the causal form of नश् to destroy, with<BR>अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=183-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीर|कीरं|कीरः
कीर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A parrot.<BR>	 2. Kashmir.<BR>	 m. plu. (-राः) The people of<BR>Kashmir, n. (-रं) Flesh.<BR> E. की bad, vile, ईर् to send or order, क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=184-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीरक|कीरकः
कीरक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A tree.<BR>	 2. A Buddha.<BR>	 3. Obtaining, gaining.<BR> E. कन्<BR>added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=184-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीरेष्ट|कीरेष्टः
कीरेष्ट m. (-ष्टः)<BR>	 1. A tree, a species of mountain Pilu: see अक्षोड 2. The<BR>mango tree.<BR> E. कीर a parrot, and इष्ट wished, desired.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=184-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीर्ण|कीर्णः|कीर्ण्ण
कीर्ण mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-र्णं)<BR>	 1. Covered, secreted, hidden.<BR>	 2. Scattered,<BR>thrown, cast.<BR>	 3. Injured, hurt.<BR>	 4. Full.<BR> E. कॄ to scatter, affix क्त<BR>formation irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=184-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीर्णि|कीर्णिः|कीर्ण्णि
कीर्णि f. (-र्णिः)<BR>	 1. Scattering, throwing.<BR>	 2. Covering, concealing.<BR> E. कॄ to<BR>scatter, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=184-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीर्त्तन|कीर्तन|कीर्तनं|कीर्त्तनं
कीर्त्तन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Saying, telling.<BR>	 2. Repeating.<BR>	 3. Celebrating, praising.<BR>f. (-ना) Fame, glory.<BR> E. कृत् to praise or celebrate, युच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=184-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीर्त्तयत्|कीर्तयत्
कीर्त्तयत् mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्) Praising, celebrating.<BR> E. कृत् to praise, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=184-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीर्त्ति|कीर्ति|कीर्तिः|कीर्त्तिः
कीर्त्ति f. (-र्त्तिः)<BR>	 1. Fame, renown, glory.<BR>	 2. Favour, approbation.<BR>	 3.<BR>Sound.<BR>	 4. Light, lustre.<BR>	 5. Mud, dirt.<BR>	 6. Diffusing, expansion.<BR>	 7.<BR>One of the Matrikas or personified divine energies of KṚṢṆA. E.<BR>कृत् to celebrate, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=184-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीर्त्तिकर|कीर्तिकर
कीर्त्तिकर mfn. (-रः-री-रं) Conferring fame.<BR> E. कीर्त्ति, and कर what<BR>makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=184-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीर्त्तित|कीर्तित|कीर्त्तितः
कीर्त्तित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Said, asserted.<BR>	 2. Known, notorious.<BR>	 3. Cele-<BR>brated; praised.<BR> E. कृत् to celebrated, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=184-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीर्त्तिभाज्|कीर्तिभाज्
कीर्त्तिभाज् mfn. (भाक्) Celebrated, famous.<BR>	 m. (-भाक्) A name of DRO-<BR>NACHARYA, the military preceptor of the PĀṆḌUS and KURUS.<BR>E. कीर्त्ति fame, and भाज् to serve or honour, affix क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=184-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीर्त्तिमत्|कीर्तिमत्|कीर्तिमन्त्
कीर्त्तिमत् mfn. (-मान्-मती-मत्) Praised, famous, celebrated.<BR>	 m. (-मान्) The<BR>elder brother of VASUDEVA.<BR> E. कीर्त्ति, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=184-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीर्त्तिशेष|कीर्तिशेष|कीर्तिशेषः|कीर्त्तिशेषः
कीर्त्तिशेष m. (-षः) Death, dying.<BR> E. कीर्त्ति fame, and शेष end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=184-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीर्त्त्य
कीर्त्त्य mfn. (-र्त्त्यः-र्त्त्या-र्त्त्यं) To be praised or celebrated.<BR> E. कृत् to praise,<BR>क्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=184-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीर्म्मी|कीर्मी
कीर्म्मी f. (-र्म्मी) A house for straw; also हेमपुत्री.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=184-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीर्य्यमाण|कीर्यमाण
कीर्य्यमाण mfn. (-णः-णाः-णं) Covered, bestrewed.<BR> E. कॄ to scatter, passive<BR>form, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=184-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कील|कीलः
कील r. 10th cl. (कीलयति) To bind, to fasten, to stake, to pin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=184-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कील|कीलः
कील mf. (-लः-ला)<BR>	 1. Flame, lambent flame.<BR>	 2. Small, minute.<BR>	 m. (-लः)<BR>1. A stake, a pin, a bolt, a wedge, &c.<BR>	 2. A lance, a spike.<BR>	 3. A<BR>gnomon.<BR>	 4. A weapon.<BR>	 5. A post, a piller.<BR>	 6. The elbow.<BR>	 7. A<BR>blow or punch with the elbow.<BR>	 8. A blow, a thump; (in the three<BR>last senses some make this also fem.)<BR>	 9. A post in a cow-house;<BR>see the next.<BR> E. कील् to bind, and क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=184-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीलक|कीलकः
कीलक m. (-कः) A piller for cows, &c. to rub themselves against, or<BR>one to which they are tied.<BR>	 2. A pin, a bolt, a wedge.<BR> E. कन्<BR>added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=184-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीलसंस्पर्श|कीलसंस्पर्शः
कीलसंस्पर्श m. (-र्शः) A plant, the fruit of which yields a turpentinous<BR>substance that has been used in India as pitch, &c. commonly<BR>Gab; (Embryopteris glutinifera, Rox.)<BR> E. कील a bolt, सम् with,<BR>and स्पर्श touch, the fruit being invested with a hard coat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=184-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीलाल|कीलालं|कीलालः
कीलाल n. (-लं)<BR>	 1. Water.<BR>	 2. Blood.<BR>	 3. Amrita, the food of the gods.<BR>	 4.<BR>Honey.<BR> E. कील flame, and अल what opposes, &c. or कील a stake,<BR>&c. and अल what adorns; from अल् with अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=184-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीलालधि|कीलालधिः
कीलालधि m. (-धिः) The ocean.<BR> E. कीलाल water, and धि what contains.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=184-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीलालप|कीलालपः
कीलालप m. (-पः) A Rākṣasa, a sort of goblin or imp.<BR> E. कीलाल blood,<BR>and प who drinks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=184-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीलित|कीलितः
कीलित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Bound, tied, confined.<BR>	 2. Pierced, transfixed.<BR>3. Staked, impaled.<BR>	 4. Pinned, fastened by a stake, &c.<BR>	 5. Set up<BR>as a stake or pole.<BR> E. कील् to bind. affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=184-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीश|कीशः
कीश mfn. (-शः-शा-शं) Naked.<BR>	 m. (-शः)<BR>	 1. A monkey, an ape.<BR>	 2. The sun.<BR>E. क air, water, &c. ईश who has power over, and क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=184-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीशपर्ण|कीशपर्णः|कीशपर्ण्ण
कीशपर्ण mf. (-र्णः-र्णी) A tree, (Achyranthes aspera:) see अपामार्गः also<BR>कीशपर्णक.<BR>	 m. (-कः)<BR> E. कीश a monkey, पर्ण a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=184-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कु|कुः
कु r. 1st cl. (ङ) कुङ् (कवते) r. 2nd cl. (टु) टुकु (कौति) r. 6th cl. (शिं) कुशि<BR>(कुवते) r. 9th cl. (ञ) कुञ् (कुनाति, कुनीते) 1. To sound, to sound<BR>indistinctly, to moan, to groan.<BR>	 2. To cry as a bird, to coo, to<BR>hum as a bee, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=184-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कु|कुः
कु f. (-कुः) The earth. ind. A particle of depreciation, and implying.<BR>1. Sin, guilt.<BR>	 2. Reproach, contempt.<BR>	 3. Diminution, littleness.<BR>4. Prevention, hindrance, as कुपथ a bad road, &c.<BR> E. कु to sound,<BR>क्विप् affix, or कुङ् to sound, with the affix ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=184-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुक
कुक r. 1st cl. (कोकते) To take, to accept.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=184-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुक
कुक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Taking, accepting.<BR> E. कुक and क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=184-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुकभ|कुकभं
कुकभ n. (-भं) Spirituous liquor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=184-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुकर|कुकरः
कुकर mfn. (-रः-रा-री-रं)<BR>	 1. Having a crooked or withered arm.<BR>	 2.<BR>Wicked, acting wickedly.<BR> E. कु bad, and कर the hand; or कृ to do,<BR>ट aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=184-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुकर्म्मन्|कुकर्मन्
कुकर्म्मन् mfn. (-र्म्मा-र्म्मा-र्म्म) Wicked, bad.<BR>	 n. (-र्म्म) Wickedness, depravity,<BR>villainy.<BR> E. कु bad, कर्म्मन् act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=184-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुकर्म्मकारिन्|कुकर्मकारिन्
कुकर्म्मकारिन् mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि) Wicked, depraved.<BR> E. कुकर्म्म, and कारिन्<BR>who does.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=184-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुकील|कुकीलः
कुकील m. (-लः) A mountain.<BR> E. कु earth, and कील a pin or bolt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=184-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुकुद|कुकुदः
कुकुद mfn. (-दः-दा-दं) One who gives a girl, decorated with fit orna-<BR>ments and with the prescribed ceremonies, in marriage.<BR> E. कुक to<BR>take and द who gives: see कूकुद.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=184-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुकुन्दर|कुकुंदर|कुकुन्दरं|कुकुंदरः|कुकुन्दरः
कुकुन्दर n. (-रं) or n du. (-रे) the cavities of the loins.<BR> E. कुन्दर a hollow.<BR>a cave, from कु the earth, and दृ to rend or tear, कु bad, vile, pre-<BR>fixed; it is also written ककुन्दर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=184-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुकुभा
कुकुभा f. (-भा) One of the female personifications of music or Rāgiṇīs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=184-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुकुर|कुकुरः
कुकुर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A dog.<BR>	 2. A branch of the Yadu race: see कुक्कुर.<BR>3. A plant and perfume: see ग्रन्थिपर्णी.<BR>	 m. plu. (-राः) A country: see<BR>दशार्ह.<BR> E. कुक् to take, उरच् Uṇādi affix; also कुक्कुर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=184-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुकुराधिनाथ
कुकुराधिनाथ m. (-थः) KṚṢṆA.<BR> E. कुकुर a Yadu, and अधिनाथ chief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=184-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुकूणक
कुकूणक m. (-कः) Weakness, of the eyes in infants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=184-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुकूल|कुकूलं|कुकूलः
कुकूल n. (-लं)<BR>	 1. A hole filled with stakes.<BR>	 2. Conflagration of chaff.<BR>	 3.<BR>Armour, mail.<BR> E. कु the earth, and कूल a bank, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=184-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुकृत्य
कुकृत्य n. (-त्यं) Wickedness, evil.<BR> E. कु, and कृत्य act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=184-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुकोल|कुकोलं
कुकोल n. (-लं) The jujube: see कोलि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=184-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुक्कुट|कुक्कुटः
कुक्कुट m. (-टः)<BR>	 1. A cock.<BR>	 2. A wild cock.<BR>	 3. The offspring of a Śūdra<BR>or man of the fourth caste, by a Chandala woman.<BR>	 4. A whisp of<BR>of lighted straw, a firebrand.<BR>	 5. A spark of fire.<BR>	 f. (-टिः or टी)<BR>Hypocrisy, interested observance of religious duties.<BR>	 f. (-टी)<BR>	 1. A<BR>hen.<BR>	 2. A small house lizard.<BR>	 3. The silk-cotton tree, (Bombax<BR>heptaphyllum.)<BR> E. कुक् taking, from कुक with क्विप् affix, and कुट् to<BR>cut or scratch, with क affix; scratching up the earth, &c. or कु<BR>bad, कुट् to cut, &c. and क inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=184-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुक्कुटक|कुक्कुटकः
कुक्कुटक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A cock.<BR>	 2. A wild cock.<BR>	 3. A man of a mixed caste,<BR>one sprung from a Śūdra and the female of a barbarian.<BR> E. कन्<BR>added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=184-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुक्कुटमण्डप|कुक्कुटमण्डपः
कुक्कुटमण्डप m. (-पः) A place where final emancipation may be attained;<BR>also मुक्तिमण्डप.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=184-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुक्कुटमस्तक|कुक्कुटमस्तकं|कुक्कुटमस्तकः
कुक्कुटमस्तक n. (-कं) A sort of pepper, (Piper chavya.)<BR> E. कुक्कुट, and मस्तक<BR>head; to what the flower may be compared.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=184-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुक्कुटव्रत|कुक्कुटव्रतं
कुक्कुटव्रत n. (-तं) A religious observation, (worship of ŚIVA,) on the<BR>seventh of the light fortnight of Bhadra, by women, especially<BR>for the sake of obtaining offspring.<BR> E. कुक्कुट a howl, and व्रत religious<BR>rite; alluding to the fruitfulness of the hen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=184-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुक्कुटशिख|कुक्कुटशिखः
कुक्कुटशिख m. (-खः) Safflower, (Carthamus tinctorius.)<BR> E. कुक्कुट a cock, and<BR>शिख a crest; cockscomb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=184-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुक्कुटाण्ड
कुक्कुटाण्ड n. (-ण्डं) A fowl's egg.<BR> E. कुक्कुटी and अण्ड an egg.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=184-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुक्कुटाभ|कुक्कुटाभः
कुक्कुटाभ m. (-भः) A kind of snake, compared to a fowl, in some res-<BR>pects, perhaps from having a crest or comb.<BR> E. कुक्कुट a cock, and<BR>आभ who is or resembles, from भा to shine, prefix आङ् and affix क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=184-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुक्कुटाहि|कुक्कुटाहिः
कुक्कुटाहि m. (-हिः) A kind of snake: see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=185-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुक्कुभ|कुक्कुभः
कुक्कुभ m. (-भः)<BR>	 1. A wild cock, (Phasianus gallus.)<BR>	 2. Varnish, oiling<BR>or oily gloss; also कुक्कुभक m. (-कः)<BR> E. कुक् imitative sound, कु to<BR>utter sound, and भक् irr. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=185-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुक्कुर|कुक्कुरं|कुक्कुरः
कुक्कुर m. (-रः) A dog.<BR>	 n. (-रं) A vegetable perfume, commonly Gant-<BR>hiala: see ग्रन्थिपर्णी.<BR>	 f. (-री) A bitch.<BR> E. कुक् to take. उरन् Uṇādi affix,<BR>and क inserted; also कुकुर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=185-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुक्कुवाच्
कुक्कुवाच् m. (-क) A sort of deer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=185-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुक्ष|कुक्षः
कुक्ष m. (-क्षः) The belly.<BR> E. कुष् to extract, and स affix; by which the<BR>fœces are excreted; also कुक्षि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=185-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुक्षि|कुक्षिः
कुक्षि m. (-क्षिः) The belly, the cavity of the abdomen.<BR> E. कुषि to extract,<BR>and क्सि affix; see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=185-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुक्षिम्भरि|कुक्षिंभरि|कुक्षिम्भरिः
कुक्षिम्भरि mfn. (-रिः-रिः-रि) Voracious, gluttonous, filling or pampering<BR>the belly.<BR> E. कुक्षि the belly, भृ to nourish, affix खि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=185-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुक्षिरन्ध्र|कुक्षिरन्ध्रः
कुक्षिरन्ध्र m. (-न्ध्रः) A reed.<BR> E. कुक्षि and रन्ध्र a hole.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=185-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुख्याति
कुख्याति f. (-तिः) Evil report, infamy.<BR> E. कु bad, and ख्याति fame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=185-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुङ्कुम|कुंकुम|कुंकुमं|कुङ्कुमं
कुङ्कुम m. (-मः) Saffron, (Crocus sativus.)<BR> E. कुकि to take, and उमक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=185-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुङ्कुमताम्र
कुङ्कुमताम्र mfn. (-म्रः-म्रा-म्रं) Red, coppery red.<BR> E. कुङ्कुम and ताम्र copper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=185-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुङ्कुमरेणु
कुङ्कुमरेणु f. (-णुः) the dust or pollen of saffron. M. कुङ्कुम and रेणु dust<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=185-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुङ्कुमाक्त
कुङ्कुमाक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं) Dyed or stained with saffron, orange, yellow.<BR>E. कुङ्कुम and अक्त anointed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=185-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुङ्कुमाङ्क
कुङ्कुमाङ्क mfn. (-ङ्कः-ङ्का-ङ्कं) Marked with saffron, dyed or stained of an<BR>orange colour.<BR> E. कुङ्कुम and अङ्क a mark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=185-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुङ्कुमारुण
कुङ्कुमारुण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Red, ruddy.<BR> E. कुङ्कुम and अरुण purple.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=185-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुच|कुचः
कुच r. 1st cl. (कोचति)<BR>	 1. To sound high, to utter a loud, shrill cry, as<BR>a bird.<BR>	 2. To go.<BR>	 3. To polish.<BR>	 4. To touch.<BR>	 5. To furrow or mark<BR>with lines.<BR>	 6. To be crooked.<BR>	 7. To write.<BR>	 8. To oppose.<BR>	 9. To<BR>contend.<BR>	 10. To be restricted or confined, to contract. r. 6th cl. (शि)<BR>शिकुच (कुचति) or with सं prefixed, (संकोचति or संकुचति)<BR>	 1. To straiten,<BR>to narrow or contract.<BR>	 2. To be straitened, to shrink, to contract.<BR>With उत् to bribe; with वि, and आ, to expand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=185-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुच|कुचः
कुच m. (-चः) A breast, a pap.<BR> E. कुच् to bind or confine, क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=185-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुचकुम्भ|कुचकुम्भः
कुचकुम्भ m. (-म्भः) The female breast.<BR> E. कुच and कुम्भ vase.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=185-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुचण्डिका
कुचण्डिका f. (-का) A plant, (Aletris hyacinthoides:) see मूर्व्वा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=185-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुचतट
कुचतट n. (-टं) The female breast.<BR> E. कुच, and तट bank.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=185-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुचटताग्र
कुचटताग्र n. (-ग्रं) A nipple.<BR> E. कुचतट and अग्र tip.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=185-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुचन्दन
कुचन्दन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Red sanders, (Pterocarpus santolinus.)<BR>	 2. Sappan or<BR>log wood: see पत्राङ्ग.<BR>	 3. Saffron.<BR>	 4. A leguminous plant, (Adenan-<BR>thera pavonina.)<BR> E. कु bad, inferior, and चन्दन Sandal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=185-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुचफल|कुचफलः
कुचफल m. (-लः) The pomegranate.<BR> E. कुच, and फल fruit of the shape of<BR>the breast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=185-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुचर|कुचरः
कुचर mfn. (-रः-रा-री-रं)<BR>	 1. Censorious, detracting.<BR>	 2. Following evil<BR>practices, low, vile, wicked.<BR> E. कु vile, and चर who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=185-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुचर्य्या|कुचर्या
कुचर्य्या f. (-र्य्या) Impropriety, wickedness.<BR> E. कु bad, चर्य्या practice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=185-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुचाग्र|कुचाग्रं
कुचाग्र n. (-ग्रं) A nipple.<BR> E. कुव a breast, and अग्र point, end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=185-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुचाङ्गेरी
कुचाङ्गेरी f. (-री) Wood sorrel, (Oxalis monadelpha:) see चाङ्गेरी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=185-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुचिक|कुचिकः
कुचिक mf. (-कः-का) A kind of fish, in shape like an eel, commonly<BR>Kunchiya, (Unibranchapertura Cuchiya, Ham.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=185-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुचित
कुचित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Closed, contracted.<BR>	 2. Measured.<BR> E. कुच् to<BR>contract, कितच् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=185-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुचेल|कुचेलः
कुचेल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Ill clothed, dressed in dirty or tattered garments.<BR>f. (-लः-ली) A plant, (Cissampelos hexandra:) see विद्ध्वकर्णी.<BR> E. कु bad,<BR>and चेला a garment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=185-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुच्छ|कुच्छं
कुच्छ n. (-च्छं) The white water lily.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=185-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुज|कुजः
कुज r. 1st cl. (उ) कुजु (कोजति) 1. To steal or rob. (इ) कुजि (कुञ्जति) To<BR>sound inarticulately.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=185-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुज|कुजः
कुज m. (-जः)<BR>	 1. The plant MARS.<BR>	 2. A demon; also called Naraka.<BR>	 3. A<BR>tree.<BR>	 f. (-जा)<BR>	 1. A name of DURGĀ.<BR>	 2. Of SITA.<BR> E. कु the earth, and<BR>ज born, earth-born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=185-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुजम्भल|कुजंभलः|कुजम्भलः
कुजम्भल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) A housebreaker; also कुजम्भिल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=185-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुजम्भिल|कुजंभिल|कुजंभिलः|कुजम्भिलः
कुजम्भिल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) A thief, a housebreaker; also कुजम्भल and<BR>कुजम्भर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=185-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुज्झिश
कुज्झिश m. (-शः) A sort of fish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=185-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुज्झटि|कुज्झटिः
कुज्झटि f. (-टिः-टी) A fog or mist.<BR> E. कु the earth, and झट् to be entan-<BR>gled, affix कि; also कुज्झटिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=185-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुज्झटिका
कुज्झटिका f. (-का) A fog or mist: see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=185-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुञ्च
कुञ्च r. 1st cl. (-उ) कुञ्चु (कुञ्चति) 1. To go, to go to or towards.<BR>	 2. To move<BR>crookedly.<BR>	 3. To make crooked.<BR>	 4. To be crooked.<BR>	 5. To lessen, to<BR>make small.<BR>	 6. To be or become small, to shrink as a substance.<BR>	 7.<BR>To contract or draw in, (as the thoughts,) Some read this root कुचि<BR>but needlessly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=185-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुञ्चन|कुंचन|कुंचनं|कुञ्चनं
कुञ्चन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Curving, bending.<BR>	 2. Contracting.<BR>	 3. Contraction of the<BR>eyelids.<BR> E. कुञ्च् to go crookedly, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=185-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुञ्चि|कुंचि|कुंचिः|कुञ्चिः
कुञ्चि f. (-ञ्चिः) A measure of quantity equal to eight handfuls.<BR> E. कुञ्च् to<BR>be curved. इन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=185-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुञ्चिका|कुंचिका
कुञ्चिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. A plant bearing a red and black seed, used as a<BR>weight, (Abrus precatorious:) see गुञ्जा 2. The branch or shoot of a<BR>bamboo.<BR>	 3. A plant bearing a pungent seed, (Nigella Indica:) see<BR>कृष्णजीरक.<BR>	 4. A fish, commonly Cunchiya, in shape like an eel and<BR>eaten as one, (Unibranchapertura cunchiya.)<BR>	 5. A key.<BR> E. कुञ्च् to go<BR>crookedly, &c. क्वुन् affix, with the fem. termination.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=185-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुञ्चित|कुंचित|कुञ्चितं
कुञ्चित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Crooked, curved, bent.<BR> E. कुञ्च to go crookedly,<BR>affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=185-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुञ्ज|कुंज|कुंजं|कुंजः|कुञ्जः
कुञ्ज mn. (-ञ्जः-ञ्जं)<BR>	 1. A place overgrown with creeping plants, a bower,<BR>an arbour.<BR>	 2. An elephant's tusk or ivory.<BR>	 3. The lower jaw.<BR> E. कु<BR>the earth, and ज produced, म inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=185-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुञ्जकुटीर|कुंजकुटीर|कुञ्जकुटीरः
कुञ्जकुटीर m. (-रः) A bower, an arbour.<BR> E. कुञ्ज and कुटीर a small house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=185-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुञ्जर|कुंजर|कुंजरः|कुञ्जरः
कुञ्जर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. An elephant.<BR>	 2. (In composition,) Pre-eminent, as<BR>पुरुषकुञ्जर an excellent. man.<BR>	 3. Hair.<BR>	 4. A country.<BR>	 f. (-रा or -री)<BR>	 1. A<BR>female elephant. (-रा)<BR>	 1. A plant, (Bignonia suave-olens.)<BR>	 2. A<BR>shrub, (Grislea tomentosa)<BR> E. कुञ्ज a tusk, an arbour, &c. and र<BR>what forms or possesses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=185-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुञ्जरपिप्पली
कुञ्जरपिप्पली f. (-ली) A plant described as bearing a fruit which resembles<BR>long pepper: see गजपिप्पली.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=185-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुञ्जराराति|कुंजराराति|कुञ्जरारातिः
कुञ्जराराति m. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. The Sarabha, a fabulous animal.<BR>	 2. A lion. E.<BR>कुञ्जर an elephant, and अराति an enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=185-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुञ्जरालुक|कुञ्जरालुकं
कुञ्जरालुक n. (-कं) A species of esculent root, a sort of yam.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=185-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुञ्जराशन|कुंजराशन|कुञ्जराशनः
कुञ्जराशन m. (-नः) The holy fig tree, (Ficus religiosa.)<BR> E. कुञ्जर an ele-<BR>phat, and अशन food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=185-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुञ्जल|कुंजलं|कुञ्जलं
कुञ्जल m. (-लः) Sour gruel: see काञ्जिक.<BR> E. कु bad, and जल water. form<BR>irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=185-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुञ्जिका
कुञ्जिका f. (-का) Kalonji, (Nigella Indica:) see कुञ्चिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=185-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुट|कुटं|कुटः
कुट(शि) r. 6th cl. (कुटति)<BR>	 1. To make crooked.<BR>	 2. To be or become<BR>crooked.<BR>	 3. To be dishonest, to cheat or deceive. (इ) कुटि (कुण्टति)<BR>1. To be stopped or obstructed, to be prevented from moving.<BR>	 2.<BR>To confound or disorder from pain or grief: see कुडि r. 10th cl.<BR>(कुटयते, कोटयति)<BR>	 1. To cut: see त्रुट् 2. To heat: see कुट्ट.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=185-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुट|कुटं|कुटः
कुट mn. (-टः-टं)<BR>	 1. A water pot.<BR>	 mf. (-टः-टी) A house; also कुटि.<BR>	 m. (-टः)<BR>1. A fort, a strong hold.<BR>	 2. A tree: see कुठ.<BR>	 3. A hammer, a mallet<BR>for breaking small stones.<BR>	 4. A mountain.<BR>	 f. (-टी)<BR>	 1. A kind of<BR>perfume, commonly Mura.<BR>	 2. A bawd, a procuress or go-between.<BR>3. A nosegay, a bundle or tuft of flowers or vegetables.<BR> E. कुट् to<BR>go crookedly, &c. क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=185-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुटङ्क|कुटंक|कुटंकः|कुटङ्कः
कुटङ्क m. (-ङ्कः) A roof, a thatch.<BR> E. कुट a house, in the third case, and क<BR>what makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=185-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुटङ्गक|कुटंगक|कुटंगकः|कुटङ्गकः
कुटङ्गक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. An arbour formed by creeping plants overrunning a<BR>tree.<BR>	 2. A roof or thatch.<BR>	 3. A house, small house, a hut or cot-<BR>tage: see कुटुङ्गक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=185-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुटच|कुटचः
कुटच m. (-चः) Coraya: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=185-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुटज|कुटजः
कुटज m. (-जः) A medicinal plant, commonly Coraya, (Echites antidy-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=186-a" target="_blank">Page186-a+ 60</a>]<BR>senterica, Rox.) the seeds are used as a vermifuge: see इन्द्रयव.<BR>	 2.<BR>A name of the saint AGASTYA.<BR>	 3. Also of DRONA a sage and<BR>warrior: see द्रोण<BR> E. कूट a mountain peak, and ज what is produced;<BR>the vowel of कूट being made short.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=185-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुटन्नक
कुटन्नक n. (-कं) a fragrant grass: see मुस्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=186-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुटन्नट|कुटन्नटं|कुटन्नटः
कुटन्नट m. (-टः) A plant, (Bignonia Indica.)<BR>	 n. (-टं) A fragrant grass,<BR>(Cyperus rotundus.)<BR> E. कुटन् being crooked, नट् to dance or wave,<BR>and अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=186-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुटप|कुटपः
कुटप m. (-पः)<BR>	 1. A saint, a divine sage or Muni.<BR>	 2. A garden or grove<BR>near a house.<BR>	 3. A measure of grain, &c. see कुडप n. (-पं) A lotus.<BR>E. कुट a house, and प what nourishes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=186-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुटर|कुटरं|कुटरः
कुटर m. (-रः) A post round which the string passes that works the<BR>churning stick: see कुठर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=186-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुटरु|कुटरुः
कुटरु n. (-रु) A tent, a house of cloth or canvas.<BR> E. कुट् to be crooked<BR>अरु Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=186-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुटरुणा
कुटरुणा f. (-णा) A plant commonly Teori, (Convolvulus turpethum.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=186-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुटल|कुटलं
कुटल n. (-लं) A roof, a thatch: see कुटङ्क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=186-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुटहारिका
कुटहारिका f. (-का) A female slave or servant.<BR> E. कुट a water pot, and<BR>हारिका who carries.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=186-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुटि|कुटिः
कुटि mf. (-टिः-टिः or -टी) A house.<BR>	 m. (-टिः)<BR>	 1. A tree.<BR>	 2. The body.<BR>	 3.<BR>Curvature, a curve.<BR> E. कुट् to be crooked, इ Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=186-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुटिचर|कुटिचरः
कुटिचर m. (-रः) A porpoise.<BR> E. कुटि a curve, चर who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=186-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुटित|कुटितं
कुटित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Crooked, bent.<BR> E. कुट् to be curved, इत Uṇādi<BR>affix; also कुटिल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=186-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुटितृ
कुटितृ mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ)<BR>	 1. Being bent.<BR>	 2. Acting dishonestly.<BR> E. कुट् to<BR>be crooked, तृच्, aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=186-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुटिर|कुटिरं
कुटिर n. (-रं) A hut, a cottage.<BR> E. कुटि a house, रा to be like, ड aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=186-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुटिल|कुटिलं
कुटिल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>	 1. Crooked, bent.<BR>	 2. Dishonest, fraudulent.<BR>	 n.<BR>(-लं) Tin.<BR>	 f. (-ला) The name of a river, the Kutila river, according<BR>to some, a name of the SARASWATI.<BR> E. कुट् to be crooked, किलच्<BR>Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=186-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुटिलगामिन्
कुटिलगामिन् mfn. (-मी-मिनी-मि) Tortuous, going crookedly.<BR> E. कुटिल, and<BR>गामिन् what goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=186-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुटिलता
कुटिलता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Crookedness.<BR>	 2. Guile, dishonesty.<BR> E. कुटिल and तल्<BR>affix; also with त्व, कुटिलत्वं.<BR>	 n. (-त्वं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=186-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुटिलिका
कुटिलिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. A blacksmith's forge.<BR>	 2. Crouching, coming steal-<BR>thily as a hunter on his prey.<BR> E. कुटिल, and इकन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=186-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुटीचक|कुटीचकः
कुटीचक m. (-कः) One who lives at his son's expense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=186-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुटीचर|कुटीचरः
कुटीचर m. (-रः) An ascetic of a particular order, one who consigns the<BR>care of his family to his son, and remains at home engaged solely<BR>in devotion.<BR> E. कुटी a house, and चर who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=186-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुटीर|कुटीरं|कुटीरः
कुटीर m. (-रः) A small house, a hut, a hovel.<BR> E. कुटी a house, and र aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=186-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुटुङ्कक
कुटुङ्कक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. An arbour or bower, formed of creeping plants.<BR>	 2.<BR>A thatch, a roof.<BR>	 3. A hut, a cottage.<BR>	 4. A creeper winding round<BR>a tree.<BR> E. कुट् to be crooked, क affix, कुट and अङ्ग the body, with<BR>कन् added; the form is irr.; also कुटङ्कक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=186-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुटुम्ब|कुटुंब|कुटुंबं|कुटुम्बः
कुटुम्ब r. 10th cl. (कुटुम्बयते) To support a family.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=186-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुटुम्ब|कुटुंब|कुटुंबं|कुटुम्बः
कुटुम्ब m. (-म्बः)<BR>	 1. A name.<BR>	 2. A kinsman, a relation by descent 3. A<BR>connexion, a relation by the mother's side, by marriage, &c.<BR>	 4.<BR>Offspring, progeny.<BR>	 5. Family, race.<BR> E. कुटुम्ब to support a family,<BR>and अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=186-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुटुम्बक|कुटुंबक|कुटुंबकं
कुटुम्बक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Being of one family.<BR>	 n. (-कं) A family, a kind-<BR>red.<BR> E. कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=186-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुटुम्बव्यापृत|कुटुंबव्यापृत|कुटुम्बव्यापृतः
कुटुम्बव्यापृत m. (-तः) A provident and attentive father of a family. E.<BR>कुटुम्ब kindred, and व्यापृत one who manages.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=186-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुटुम्बिता
कुटुम्बिता f. (-ता) Family connexion or union, living as one family. E.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=186-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुटुम्बिन्|कुटुंबिन्
कुटुम्बिन् and तल् affix; also with त्व, कुटुम्बित्व.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=186-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुटुम्बिन्|कुटुंबिन्
कुटुम्बिन् mfn. (-म्बी-म्बिनी-म्बि)<BR>	 1. A peasant, a cultivator of the soil.<BR>	 2.<BR>One who supports or has a family.<BR>	 m. (-म्बी) A householder, a pater-<BR>familias.<BR>	 f. (-म्बिनी)<BR>	 1. The wife of a householder and mother of a<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=186-b" target="_blank">Page186-b+ 60</a>]<BR>family, a matron.<BR>	 2. A small shrub used in medicine, a kind of<BR>moon plant: see क्षीरिणी.<BR> E. कुटुम्ब kindred, &c. and इनि poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=186-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुटुम्बार्थ
कुटुम्बार्थ n. adj. (-र्थं) For the support or on account of a family.<BR> E. कुटुम्ब,<BR>and अर्थ object.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=186-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुटुम्बौकस्
कुटुम्बौकस् n. (-कः) Apartments, &c. appropriated to the accommodation<BR>of relations, &c.<BR> E. कुटुम्ब kindred, and औकस् a house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=186-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुटेर
कुटेर m. (-रः) A hut, a cottage.<BR> E. कुट् to be crooked, एरक् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=186-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुट्ट|कुट्टः
कुट्ट r. 10th cl. (कुट्टयति)<BR>	 1. To cut, to divide.<BR>	 2. To grind or pound.<BR>	 3.<BR>To censure. 1st cl. (कुट्टति) 10th cl. (कुट्टयति) To heat, some make<BR>this root कुट.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=186-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुट्टक|कुट्टकः
कुट्टक mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>	 1. What cuts.<BR>	 2. What pounds or grinds.<BR>	 m. (-कः)<BR>1. A power in arithmetic or algebra, a quantity such, that a given<BR>number being multiplied by it, and the product added to a given<BR>quantity, the sum may be divisible without remainder by a given<BR>divisor.<BR>	 2. A kingfisher.<BR> E. कुट्ट् to pound, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=186-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुट्टकव्यवहार
कुट्टकव्यवहार m. (-रः) That branch of arithmetic which treats of the<BR>Kuttaka: see the last.<BR> E. कुट्टक, and व्यवहार practice; also कुट्टकाध्याय<BR>or chapter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=186-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुट्टन|कुट्टनं
कुट्टन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Pounding, grinding, cutting, dividing.<BR>	 2. Abusing.<BR>	 f.<BR>(-नी) A bawd, a procuress, a go-between.<BR> E. कुट्ट् to cut, ल्युट् and ङीष्<BR>affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=186-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुट्टमित|कुट्टमितं
कुट्टमित n. (-तं) One of the ten graces of women, affected repulse of a<BR>lover's caresses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=186-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुट्टाक
कुट्टाक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) What cuts or divides.<BR> E. कुट्ट् to cut, षाकन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=186-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुट्टार|कुट्टारं|कुट्टारः
कुट्टार m. (-रः) A mountain.<BR>	 n. (-रं)<BR>	 1. Pleasure.<BR>	 2. A blanket. adv.<BR>Only, merely. (केवले) This word is also written कुट्टीर and कुठार, but<BR>perhaps inaccurately.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=186-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुट्टिन्
कुट्टिन् mfn. (-ट्टी-ट्टिनी-ट्टि) What cuts or pounds.<BR>	 f. (-नी) A bawd, a pro-<BR>curess.<BR> E. कुट्ट cutting, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=186-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुट्टिम|कुट्टिमः
कुट्टिम mn. (-मः-मं)<BR>	 1. A jewel mine.<BR>	 2. Ground smoothed and plastered.<BR>3. Ground prepared for the site of a mansion.<BR>	 4. A hut, a cott-<BR>age.<BR>	 5. The pomegranate.<BR> E. कुट्ट् to cut or pierce, and इमच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=186-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुट्टिहारिका
कुट्टिहारिका f. (-का) A female servant, a slave: see कुटहारिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=186-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुट्टीर|कुट्टीरः
कुट्टीर m. (-रः) A mountain: कुट्टार.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=186-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुद्मल|कुद्मलं|कुद्मलः
कुद्मल mn. (-लः-लं) An opening bud.<BR>	 n. (-लं) One of the hells in which<BR>sinners are punished, where they are bound with ropes.<BR> E. कुट् to<BR>be curved, and क्मलच् Uṇādi affix, or कल affix. with मुट् inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=186-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुठ|कुठः
कुठ(इ,)कुठि r. 1st cl. (कुण्ठति) To be idle. r. 10th cl. (कुण्ठयति) To sur-<BR>round; अप् is usually prefixed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=186-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुठ|कुठः
कुठ m. (-ठः) A tree.<BR> E. कु the earth, and स्था to abide, ड affix; earth-<BR>abiding; the deriv. is irregular, and is sometimes written कुट,<BR>derived from कुट् to be crooked, to bend or wave, affix क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=186-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुठर|कुठरः
कुठर m. (-रः) The post round which the string of the churning stick<BR>winds: see कुटर.<BR> E. कुठ् to surround, करन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=186-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुठाकु|कुठाकुः
कुठाकु m. (-कुः) A bird; the woodpecker.<BR> E. कुठ for कुट to cut, and आकु<BR>Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=186-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुठाटङ्क|कुठाटंकः|कुठाटङ्कः
कुठाटङ्क m. (-ङ्कः) An axe.<BR> E. कुठ a tree, आङ् prefixed to टकि to bind, and<BR>अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=186-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुठार|कुठारः
कुठार mf. (-रः-री)<BR>	 1. An axe.<BR>	 2. A sort of hoe or spade.<BR>	 m. (-रः) A tree.<BR>E. कुठ a tree, and ऋ to go, affix अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=186-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुठारिका
कुठारिका f. (-का) A small one or adze; also a similarly shaped instru-<BR>ment used in surgery for scarification.<BR> E. कन् added to the prece-<BR>ding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=186-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुठारु|कुठारुः
कुठारु m. (-रुः)<BR>	 1. A tree.<BR>	 2. A monkey, an ape.<BR>	 3. An armourer.<BR> E. कुठ a<BR>tree, ऋ to go, affix ञुण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=186-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुठि|कुठिः
कुठि m. (-ठिः)<BR>	 1. A mountain.<BR>	 2. A tree.<BR> E. कुठ् to surround, and इ<BR>Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=186-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुठिक|कुठिकः
कुठिक m. (-कः) A kind of costus, commonly, cutṭh, (Costus speciosus.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=186-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुठेर|कुठेरः
कुठेर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A name of fire.<BR>	 2. Tulasi or basil: see the next.<BR> E. कुठ्<BR>to surround, एरक् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=186-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुठेरक|कुठेरकः
कुठेरक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. Holy basil, (Ocimum sanctum;) see पणसा.<BR>	 2. A<BR>white sort of the same, (Ocimum gratissimum.)<BR> E. कन् added to the<BR>preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=187-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुठेरज|कुठेरजः
कुठेरज m. (-जः) A white species of basil; also कुठेरक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=187-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुठेरु|कुठेरुः
कुठेरु m. (-रुः) The wind of a fan or Chowrie.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=187-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुड
कुड(शि) r. 6th cl. (कुडति)<BR>	 1. To play or act as a child, to trifle.<BR>	 2.<BR>To eat.<BR>	 3. To heap. (इ,) कुडि r. 1st cl. (कुण्डति)<BR>	 1. To confound<BR>or disorder with grief or pain.<BR>	 2. To form, to make.<BR>	 3. (कुण्डते) To<BR>burn, to heat. r. 1st and 10th cls. (कुण्डति, कुण्डयति) To preserve.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=187-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुडप|कुडपः
कुडप m. (-पः) A measure: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=187-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुडव|कुडवः
कुडव m. (-वः) A measure of grain, wood, iron, &c. the fourth part of a<BR>Prastha, described by some as a vessel four fingers wide, and<BR>as many deep, and containing twelve Prakritis or handfuls: it is<BR>also said to contain thirteen and a half cubic Angulas; or to be a<BR>finger and half deep, and three fingers each length and breadth.<BR>In medicine it is equal to two Prakritis or thirty-two Tolakas. E.<BR>कुड् to heap, कवन् affix; also कुडप and कुटप.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=187-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुडि|कुडिः
कुडि m. (-डि) The body.<BR> E. कुड् to born, इ Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=187-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुडिका
कुडिका f. (-का) An earthen or wooden water pot used by ascetics.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=187-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुडिश|कुडिशः
कुडिश m. (-शः) A fish, commonly Kurchi, (Cyprinus curchius, HAM.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=187-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुडुप|कुडुपः
कुडुप m. (-पः) The clasp or fastening of a necklace or bracelet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=187-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुड्मल|कुड्मलः
कुड्मल m. (-लः) A new bud; see कुद्मल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=187-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुड्मलित
कुड्मलित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Budded, blossomed.<BR>	 2. Cheerful, smiling,<BR>(as the countenance.)<BR> E. कुल्मल and इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=187-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुड्य|कुड्यं
कुड्य n. (-ड्यं)<BR>	 1. A wall.<BR>	 2. Anointing, plastering.<BR>	 3. Eagerness, curiosi-<BR>ty.<BR> E. कु to sound, and ड्यन् affix, or कुड् to heap, &c. and क्यप् affix;<BR>also कूड्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=187-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुड्यक|कुड्यकं
कुड्यक n. (-कं) A wall: see the preceding, कन् being added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=187-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुड्यच्छेदिन्
कुड्यच्छेदिन् m. (-दी) A thief, a housebreaker,<BR> E. कुड्य a wall, and छेदिन्<BR>who cuts or breaks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=187-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुड्यच्छेद्य|कुड्यच्छेद्यं|कुड्यच्छेद्यः
कुड्यच्छेद्य n. (-द्यं) An opening, a hole in a wall, a breach.<BR> E. कुड्य a<BR>wall, and छेद्य to be broken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=187-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुड्यमत्स्य|कुड्यमत्स्यः
कुड्यमत्स्य mf. (-त्स्यः-त्स्यी) A house lizard.<BR> E. कुड्य a wall, and मत्स्य a fish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=187-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुण
कुण r. 6th cl. (कुणति)<BR>	 1. To sound.<BR>	 2. To cherish, to support or aid with<BR>gifts, &c.<BR>	 3. To be in pain. r. 10th cl. (कुणयति)<BR>	 1. To converse<BR>with, to speak to or address.<BR>	 2. To counsel or advise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=187-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुणप|कुणपः
कुणप mfn. (-पः-पी-पं) Foul smelling, stinking.<BR>	 mn. (-पः-पं)<BR>	 1. A dead<BR>body, a corpse.<BR>	 m. (-पः)<BR>	 1. A stink, a foul smell.<BR>	 2. A spear.<BR>	 f. (-पी)<BR>A small bird, a kind of Maina or Salik: see विट्सारिका.<BR> E. कृण् to<BR>sound, कपन affix, व is changed to its congener उ; sound proceeding<BR>from the corpse, &c. by the escape of the vital air, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=187-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुणाल|कुणालः
कुणाल m. (-लः) The name of a country.<BR> E. क्वण् to sound, कालन् Uṇādi<BR>affix; व becomes उ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=187-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुणि|कुणिः
कुणि m. (-णिः)<BR>	 1. A cripple with a crooked or withered arm, or with<BR>out a hand or finger; कूणि 2. The Tun tree, (Cedrela tunna:) also<BR>तुणि.<BR>	 3. A whitlow.<BR> E. कुण् to sound. कि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=187-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुणिन्द|कुणिन्दः
कुणिन्द m. (-न्दः) Sound, sounding.<BR> E. क्वण to sound, किन्दच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=187-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुण्टक|कुंटक|कुण्टकः
कुण्टक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Fat, corpulent.<BR> E. कुटि to be crooked,<BR>क्वन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=187-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुण्ठ|कुंठ|कुण्ठः
कुण्ठ mfn. (-ण्ठः-ण्ठा-ण्ठं)<BR>	 1. Indolent, lazy, slow.<BR>	 2. Stupid, foolish, a fool<BR>E. कुठि to be slothful, &c. affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=187-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुण्ठक|कुंठक|कुंठकः|कुण्ठकः
कुण्ठक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) A fool, stupid, ignorant.<BR> E. कन् added to the<BR>former.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=187-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुण्ठित|कुंठित|कुण्ठितः
कुण्ठित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Grasped, held.<BR>	 2. Encircled.<BR>	 3. Stupid.<BR> E. कुठि<BR>and क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=187-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुण्ड|कुंड|कुंडं|कुण्डं|कुंडः|कुण्डः
कुण्ड m. (-ण्डः) A son born in adultery, the son of a woman by another<BR>man than her husband, while the husband is alive.<BR>	 n. (-ण्डं)<BR>	 1. A<BR>hole in the ground for receiving and preserving consecrated fire.<BR>2. A pool, a well, a spring of basin of water, especially consecrated<BR>to some holy purpose or person.<BR>	 3. A measure.<BR>	 mf. (-ण्डः-ण्डी) A<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=187-b" target="_blank">Page187-b+ 60</a>]<BR>pitcher.<BR>	 f. (-ण्डी) A student's water-pot, made of a hollow cocoanut,<BR>&c.<BR> E. कुडि to preserve, ड aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=187-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुण्डकीट|कुंडकीट|कुण्डकीटः
कुण्डकीट m. (-टः)<BR>	 1. A follower of the Charvaka doctrine, or the tenets<BR>of those sects who deny the authority of the Vedas.<BR>	 2. The son of<BR>a woman of the Brahminical tribe born in adultery, particularly<BR>with a man of an inferior caste.<BR>	 3. A keeper of concubines, a man<BR>who has female slaves.<BR> E. कुण्ड a pool, &c. and कीट a worm, a reptile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=187-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुण्डकील|कुंडकील|कुण्डकीलः
कुण्डकील m. (-लः) A low, vile man: see नागर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=187-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुण्डगोल|कुंडगोल
कुण्डगोल m. (-लः) Sour rice gruel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=187-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुण्डगोलक|कुंडगोलक|कुण्डगोलकं
कुण्डगोलक m. (-कः) Sour rice gruel: see काञ्जिक.<BR> E. कुण्ड a pitcher, गुड् to<BR>preserve, ण्वुल् affix, ड is changed to ल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=187-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुण्डङ्ग|कुण्डङ्गः
कुण्डङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः) An arbour, a bower,<BR> E. कुडि to preserve, अङ्गच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=187-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुण्डपाय्य|कुण्डपाय्यः
कुण्डपाय्य m. (-य्यः) A sacrifice, an oblation.<BR> E. कुण्ड, and पाय्य to be<BR>imbibed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=187-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुण्डल|कुंडल|कुंडलं|कुण्डलं|कुंडलः|कुण्डलः
कुण्डल n. (-लं)<BR>	 1. An earring.<BR>	 2. A bracelet.<BR>	 3. A fetter, a tie, a collar.<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>	 1. Mountain ebony: see काञ्चन.<BR>	 2. Guruchi, a plant, (Menis-<BR>permum glabrum.) see गुडूची.<BR>	 3. Cowach.<BR> E. कुडि to preserve,<BR>कलच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=187-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुण्डलधारण
कुण्डलधारण n. (-णं) Wearing earrings.<BR> E. कुण्डल, and धारण having.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=187-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुण्डलधारिन्
कुण्डलधारिन् mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि) Wearing earrings.<BR> E. कुण्डल, and धारिन् who<BR>has.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=187-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुण्डलिन्|कुंडलिन्
कुण्डलिन् mfn. (-ली-लिनी-लि) Having an earring.<BR>	 m. (-ली)<BR>	 1. A name of<BR>VARUṆA regent of the water.<BR>	 2. A snake.<BR>	 3. A peacock.<BR>	 4. The<BR>spotted or painted deer.<BR>	 f. (-नी)<BR>	 1. A Śakti or form of DURGĀ, wor-<BR>shipped by the Tantrikas.<BR>	 2. A plant, (Meanispermum glabrum.)<BR>3. Curds boiled with Ghee and spices.<BR> E. कुण्डल and earring, and<BR>इनि affix; the rings on the snake, the eyes in the peacock's tail, &c.<BR>being compared to this ornament.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=187-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुण्डाशिन्|कुंडाशिन्
कुण्डाशिन् m. (-शी)<BR>	 1. A pander, a pimp.<BR>	 2. One who is supported by a<BR>bastard.<BR> E. कुण्ड, अश् to eat, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=187-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुण्डिका|कुंडिका
कुण्डिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. A student's waterpot, the Kamandalu.<BR>	 2. A pitcher.<BR>E. कुण्ड a pitcher, &c. कन् added with the fem. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=187-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुण्डिन|कुंडिन|कुंडिनं|कुण्डिनं|कुण्डिनः
कुण्डिन n. (-नं) A city; also Vidarbha, the capital of Vidarbha the<BR>father-in-law of Nala Raja, apparently the modern Condavir.<BR>	 m.<BR>plur. (-नाः) The people of Kundina.<BR>	 m. (-नः) The name of a saint. E.<BR>कुडि to preserve, इनच् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=187-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुण्डिन्|कुंडिन्
कुण्डिन् m. (-ण्डी) A bastard: see कुण्ड.<BR> E. कुण्ड and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=187-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुण्डीर|कुंडीर|कुण्डीरः
कुण्डीर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Able, powerful.<BR>	 m. (-रः) A man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=187-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुतनु|कुतनुः
कुतनु mfn. (-नुः-न्वी-नु) Deformed.<BR>	 m. (-नुः) A name of KUVERA.<BR> E. कु bad,<BR>vile, and तनु body, this deity being of a monstrous appearance,<BR>having three legs and but eight teeth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=187-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुतप|कुतपः
कुतप mfn. (-पः-पा-पं) Slightly hot, mild, tepid.<BR>	 mn. (-पः-पं)<BR>	 1. The eight<BR>Muhurta or portion of the day, from the last Danda of the second<BR>watch to the first of the third or about noon; an eligible time for<BR>the performance of sacrifices to the manes.<BR>	 2. A daughter's son.<BR>3. A musical instrument.<BR>	 4. A sort of blanket made of the hair of<BR>the mountain goat.<BR>	 5. Sacrificial grass, (Poa cynosuroides.)<BR>	 m. (-पः)<BR>1. The sun.<BR>	 2. Fire.<BR>	 3. A twice born man, one of the three first<BR>classes.<BR>	 4. A guest.<BR>	 5. A sister's son.<BR>	 6. An ox.<BR> E. कु the earth,<BR>and तप what warms, or कु diminutive, and तप heat; the sun being<BR>on the decline, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=187-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुतपसप्तक
कुतपसप्तक n. (-कं) A Sraddha in which seven constituents occur, noon,<BR>a horn platter, a Nepal blanket, silver, sacrificial grass, sesamum<BR>and kine.<BR> E. कुतप, and सप्तक sevenfold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=187-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुतश्चन
कुतश्चन ind. Anywhere, somewhere.<BR> E. चन added to. कुतस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=187-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुतश्चित्
कुतश्चित् ind. Somewhere or other.<BR> E. चित् added to कुतस्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=187-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुतस्
कुतस् ind. Implying interrogation, 1. How, what.<BR>	 2. How, in what<BR>way, how should it be thus, &c. implying denial or concealment<BR>of knowledge.<BR>	 3. Whence, for what place.<BR> E. कु for किम् what,<BR>and तसिल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=187-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुतस्त्य
कुतस्त्य mfn. (-स्त्यः-स्त्या-स्त्यं) Whence come, how happened.<BR> E. त्यप् added to<BR>the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=188-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुतुक|कुतुकं
कुतुक n. (-कं)<BR>	 1. Eagerness, vehemence.<BR>	 2. Desire, inclination.<BR>	 3.<BR>Curiosity.<BR> E. कुत a particular sound, कै to emit sound, ड affix; also<BR>कौतुक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=188-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुतुप|कुतुपं|कुतुपः
कुतुप m. (-पः) A small leathern oil bottle.<BR>	 mn. (-पः-पं) The eighth hour of<BR>of the day: see कुतप<BR> E. कुतु as below, and उपच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=188-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुतू
कुतू f. (-तूः) A leathern oil bottle.<BR> E. कु bad, and तन् to spread, डु affix,<BR>and the final lengthened.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=188-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुतूणक|कुतूणकः
कुतूणक m. (-कः) Weakness of the eyes in infants; also read कुकूणक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=188-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुतूहल|कुतूहलं|कुतूहलः
कुतूहल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>	 1. Excellent, best, praised, celebrated.<BR>	 2. Sur-<BR>prising, wonderful.<BR>	 n. (-लं)<BR>	 1. Eagerness, vehemence, impetuosity.<BR>	 2.<BR>Desire, inclination.<BR>	 3. Curiosity.<BR> E. कु bad तूल् to send forth, क affix,<BR>and ह inserted; or कुतू an oil bottle, and हल् to make limes or<BR>furrows; or कु the earth, and तुद् to vex or tease; the etymologies<BR>however are all fanciful; the word is also written कौतूहल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=188-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुतूहलिन्
कुतूहलिन् mfn. (-ली-लिनी-लि)<BR>	 1. Curious, inquisitive.<BR>	 2. Eager, impatient.<BR>E. कुतूहल, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=188-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुतृण|कुतृणं
कुतृण n. (-णं) An aquatic plant, water-house leek, (Pistia stratiotes.) E.<BR>bad, तृण grass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=188-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुत्र
कुत्र ind. Where, wherein, in what place.<BR> E. कु substituted for किं what,<BR>and त्रल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=188-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुत्रचित्
कुत्रचित् ind. Somewhere.<BR> E. चित् added to कुत्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=188-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुत्रापि
कुत्रापि ind. Wherever, somewhere.<BR> E. कुत्र, and अपि certainly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=188-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुत्स
कुत्स r. 10th cl. (कुत्सयते-ति) To despise, to abuse, to revile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=188-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुत्सन|कुत्सनं
कुत्सन n. (-नं) Abuse, contempt, reproach, reviling.<BR> E. कुत्स to revile, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=188-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुत्सला
कुत्सला f. (-ला) The indigo plant: see नीली.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=188-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुत्सा
कुत्सा f. (-त्सा) Reproach, contempt, censure.<BR> E. कुत्स् to despise, अङ् and<BR>टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=188-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुत्सावादीन्
कुत्सावादीन् mfn. (-दी-दिनी-दि) Censorious, abusive.<BR> E. कुत्सा and वादिन्<BR>who speaks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=188-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुत्सित|कुत्सितं|कुत्सितः
कुत्सित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Low, vile, contemptible, contemned, reviled, &c.<BR>n. (-तं) A grass. (Cyperus.)<BR> E. कुत्स् to reproach. &c., and क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=188-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुथ|कुथं|कुथः
कुथ r. 4th cl. (कुथ्यति) To stink. r. 9th cl. (कुथ्नाति)<BR>	 1. To be distressed;<BR>see कुन्थ(इ)कुथि r. 1st cl. (कुन्थति)<BR>	 1. To hurt or kill.<BR>	 2. To afflict,<BR>to give pain.<BR>	 3. To be afflicted, to suffer pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=188-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुथ|कुथं|कुथः
कुथ mf. (-थः-था) A painted or variegated cloth or blanket, serving as an<BR>elephant's housings.<BR>	 m. (-थः) Sacrificial or Kusa grass, (Poa<BR>cynosuroides.)<BR> E. कुथ् to be connected, &c. अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=188-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुद
कुद r. 10th cl. (ऋ) कुदृ (कोदयति) To lie, to speak falsely: see कुद्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=188-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुदाल|कुदालः
कुदाल m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. Mountain ebony.<BR>	 2. A kind of spade: see कुद्दाल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=188-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुदृष्टि|कुदृष्टिः
कुदृष्टि mfn. (-ष्टिः-ष्टिः-ष्टि) Having bad eyes.<BR>	 f. (-ष्टिः)<BR>	 1. Heterodox doc-<BR>trine, as that of the Sankkyas. &c.<BR>	 2. Weak sight.<BR>	 3. Evil eye.<BR> E. कु<BR>bad, दृष्टि sight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=188-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुद्दल
कुद्दल m. (-लः) Mountain ebony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=188-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुद्दार|कुद्दारः
कुद्दार m. (-रः) See the next; sometimes also written कुदार.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=188-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुद्दाल|कुद्दालः
कुद्दाल m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. A mountain ebony, (Bauhinia variegata, &c.) also<BR>काञ्चन.<BR>	 2. A kind of spade or hoe.<BR> E. कु the earth, and दल to divide,<BR>with उत् prefixed, and अण् affix or with दॄ to divide, कुद्दार; also<BR>कुदाल, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=188-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुद्मल|कुद्मलं|कुद्मलः
कुद्मल n. (-लं) An opening bud: see कुद्मल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=188-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुद्य|कुद्यं
कुद्य n. (-द्यं) A wall: see कुड्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=188-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुद्र
कुद्र r. 10th cl. (इ) कुद्रि (कुंद्रयति) To speak falsely, to lie: some read<BR>this root कुदृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=188-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुद्रङ्ग|कुद्रंग|कुद्रंगः|कुद्रङ्गः
कुद्रङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः) A dwelling raised on a platform or scaffold. It is some-<BR>times written कुद्रङ्क<BR> E. कु the earth, and द्रङ्ग what goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=188-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुद्रव|कुद्रवः
कुद्रव m. (-वः) A kind of grass, the grain of which is eaten by the poor,<BR>(Paspalum scrobiculatum;) also कीद्रव.<BR> E. कु the earth, and द्रु to be<BR>fixed, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=188-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुध्र|कुध्रः
कुध्र m. (-ध्रः) A mountain.<BR> E. कु the earth, ध्रु to be fixed, affix ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=188-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुनख|कुनखः
कुनख mfn. (-खः-खी-खं) Having ugly nails.<BR>	 n. (-खं) A disease of the<BR>nails.<BR> E. कु bad, नख a nail; also with इनि added, कुनखिन्. See<BR>the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=188-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुनखिन्
कुनखिन् mfn. (-खी-खिनी-खि) Having bad or diseased nails.<BR> E. कुनख, and<BR>इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=188-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुनट|कुनटः
कुनट m. (-टः) A sort of trumpet flower.<BR>	 f. (-टी)<BR>	 1. Red arsenic.<BR>	 2. Corian-<BR>der.<BR> E. कु the earth, and नट् to dance, also कुनटी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=188-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुनलिन्
कुनलिन् m. (-ली) A tree, (Æschynomence grandiflora.)<BR> E. कु bad, नल a<BR>stalk, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=188-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुनाभि|कुनाभिः
कुनाभि m. (-भिः)<BR>	 1. A whirlwind.<BR>	 2. KUVERA'S aggregate treasure: see<BR>निधि<BR> E. कु the world, and नाभि the navel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=188-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुनाशक|कुनाशकः
कुनाशक m. (-कः) A plant, commonly Jawasa: see यवास.<BR> E. कु the earth,<BR>and नाशक what injures.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=188-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुनीति
कुनीति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Impolicy, misgovernment.<BR>	 2. Ill conduct, mis-<BR>behaviour.<BR> E. कु bad, नीति policy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=188-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुन्त|कुंत|कुंतः|कुन्तः
कुन्त mf. (-न्तः-न्ती)<BR>	 1. A bearded dart, a lance.<BR>	 m. (-न्तः)<BR>	 1. A species of<BR>grain, (Coix barbata, Rox.)<BR>	 2. A small animal, an insect.<BR>	 3. Pass-<BR>ionateness.<BR>	 f. (-न्तिः or -न्ती)<BR>	 1. A wife af PĀṆḌU, and mother of the<BR>three elder PANDAVA princes, by as many gods.<BR>	 2. The gum oliba-<BR>num tree, (Boswelia thurifera.)<BR>	 3. Beellium, a fragrant resin.<BR>	 4.<BR>The wife of a Brahman.<BR> E. कु bad, and अन्त end, destroying ill, ene-<BR>mies, &c. or क the head, and उन्द to give pain, त substituted for द<BR>fem. affix इन् or ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=188-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुन्तल|कुंतल|कुंतलः|कुन्तलः
कुन्तल m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. Hair.<BR>	 2. A drinking cup.<BR>	 3. Barley.<BR>	 4. A plough 5.<BR>The name of a country in the north-west of the peninsula.<BR>	 m.<BR>plu. (-लाः) The people of the inhabitants of Kuntala.<BR> E. कुन्त a dart,<BR>and ला to bring or gain, क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=188-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुन्तलिका|कुंतलिका
कुन्तलिका f. (-का) A butter-knife or scoop.<BR> E. कुन्तल a cup, &c, and<BR>इकन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=188-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुन्थ
कुन्थ r. 9th cl. (कुथ्नाति)<BR>	 1. To cling to, to twine round or be connected<BR>with.<BR>	 2. To be distressed.<BR>	 3. To suffer pain, want, &c. see कुथ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=188-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुन्थु|कुन्थुः
कुन्थु m. (-न्थुः)<BR>	 1. The seventeenth of the Jinas or deified Jaina saints.<BR>2. One of the Jaina emperors of the world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=188-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुन्द|कुंद|कुंदं|कुंदः|कुन्दः
कुन्द mn. (-न्दः-न्दं) A kind of jasmine, (J. multiflorum or pubescens.)<BR>	 m.<BR>(-न्दः)<BR>	 1. A turner's lathe.<BR>	 2. Olibanum, the resin of the Boswellia<BR>thurifera: see कुन्दरु 3. One of KUVERA'S nine treasures.<BR>	 4. The<BR>Nerium plant.<BR> E. कु to sound, दन Uṇādi affix, and नुम् inserted, or<BR>कु the earth, उन्द् to hurt, and अण् affix; also with कन् added कुन्दक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=188-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुन्दम|कुंदम|कुंदमः|कुन्दमः
कुन्दम m. (-मः) A cat,<BR> E. कु vile, (animals, as mice,) and दम who tames.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=188-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुन्दर|कुंदरः|कुन्दरः
कुन्दर m. (-रः) A sort of grass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=188-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुन्दिनी|कुंदिनी
कुन्दिनी f. (-नी) An assemblage of lotus flowers.<BR> E. कुन्द the jasmine, and<BR>इनि affix, fem. affix ङीप् an assemblage like that of Kunda flowers,<BR>from the similar whiteness of the lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=188-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुन्दु|कुंदु|कुंदुः|कुन्दुः
कुन्दु f. (-न्दूः) Frankincense or olibanum: see कुन्दुरु.<BR>	 m. (-न्दुः) A rat, a<BR>mouse.<BR> E. कु the earth, and दृ to tear or divide, डु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=188-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुन्दुर|कुन्दुरः
कुन्दुर m. (-रः) Olibanum: see कुन्दुरु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=188-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुन्दुरु|कुन्दुरुः
कुन्दुरु mf. (-रुः) The resin of the Boswellia thurifera, gum olibanum or<BR>frankincense.<BR> E. क BRAHMĀ, उन्द to moisten, (to bedew with incense<BR>in sacrifice,) रु affix, उक inserted.<BR>	 m. (-रुः) A rat: see कुन्दु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=188-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुन्दरुक
कुन्दरुक mf. (-कः-की) The olibanum tree, commonly Sali or Sale (Boswel-<BR>lia thurifera.)<BR>	 m. (-कः) The gum.<BR> E. कन् possessive or pleonastic<BR>added to कुन्दुरु, fem. affix ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=188-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुप|कुपः
कुप(इर)कुपिर r. 4th cl. (कुप्यति) To be angry, to be flushed with wrath.<BR>With प्र, to be very much enraged. r. 10th cl. (कोपयति)<BR>	 1. To shine:<BR>see कूप.<BR>	 2. To speak. (इ)कुपि r. 1st and 10th cls. (कुम्पति कुम्पयति)<BR>1. To spread.<BR>	 2. To remember.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=188-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुपङ्क
कुपङ्क m. (-ङ्कः) A slough, a heap of filth and mud.<BR> E. कु vile, पङ्क mud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=188-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुपत
कुपत ind. Excellently.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=188-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुपथ|कुपथः
कुपथ n. (-थं)<BR>	 1. A bad road.<BR>	 2. Immorality, profligacy.<BR>	 3. Heterodox<BR>doctrine.<BR> E. कु bad, and पथिन् a road; also कापथ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=188-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुपथगामिन्
कुपथगामिन् mfn. (-मी-मिनी-मि) Wicked, going in a bad or wrong read. E.<BR>कुपथ, and गामिन् who goes; also कुपथग, कृपथचर, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=189-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुपथ्य
कुपथ्य mfn. (-थ्यः-थ्या-थ्यं)<BR>	 1. Relating to a bad road, literally or figurative-<BR>ly.<BR>	 2. Counterindicated, improper, unwholesome, (as regimen, &c.)<BR>E. कु and पथ्य proper, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=189-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुपाणि|कुपाणिः
कुपाणि mfn. (-णिः-णिः-णि) Crooked-handed, having a deformed or maimed<BR>hand.<BR> E. कु bad and पाणि, the hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=189-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुपित
कुपित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Incensed, angry, offended.<BR> E. कुप् to be angry,<BR>क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=189-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुपितवायु|कुपितवायुः
कुपितवायु m. (-युः) Flatulence or hypochondria.<BR> E. कुपित, and वायु wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=189-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुपितान्तक
कुपितान्तक m. (-कः) Imminent or threatening death.<BR> E. कुपित, and अन्तक<BR>destroyer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=189-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुपिनिन्
कुपिनिन् m. (-नी) A fisherman<BR> E. कुपिनी a net, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=189-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुपिनी
कुपिनी f. (-नी) A kind of net or snare, for catching small fish, made of<BR>bamboos or rushes,<BR> E. गुप् to cover or conceal, इनि and ङीष् affixes;<BR>ग is changed to क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=189-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुपिन्द|कुपिंद|कुपिंदः|कुपिन्दः
कुपिन्द m. (-न्दः) A weaver.<BR> E. कुप् or कुय् to spread out, किन्दच् Uṇādi<BR>affix; also कुविन्द.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=189-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुपीलु|कुपीलुः
कुपीलु m. (-लुः) A sort of ebony tree<BR> E. कु bad, पीलु a tree, so called.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=189-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुपुत्र|कुपुत्रः
कुपुत्र m. (-त्रः)<BR>	 1. A son of an inferior degree, as one adopted, &c.<BR>	 2. A<BR>disobedient or wicked son.<BR> E. कु, and पुत्र a son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=189-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुपुरुष|कुपुरुषः
कुपुरुष m. (-षः)<BR>	 1. A low or vile man.<BR>	 2. A poltroon.<BR> E. कु bad, and पुरुष<BR>a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=189-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुपूय|कुपूयः
कुपूय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Inferior, low, vile.<BR> E. कु bad, and पूय् to divide, अच्<BR>aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=189-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुप्य|कुप्यं
कुप्य n. (-प्यं) Base metal, copper, brass, &c. or any metal except gold<BR>and silver.<BR> E. गुप् to conceal or preserve, क्यप् affix; ग is changed<BR>irregularly to क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=189-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुप्यशाला
कुप्यशाला f. (-ला) A braziery, a foundery, a place where metallic vessels,<BR>&c. are made or sold.<BR> E. कुप्य base metal, शाला a dwelling, a shop,<BR>&c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=189-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुप्रिय|कुप्रियः
कुप्रिय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Low, vile, last, worst.<BR> E. कु reverse, and प्रिय be-<BR>loved; disagreeable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=189-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुप्लव|कुप्लवः
कुप्लव m. (-वः) A weak or frail raft or float.<BR> E. कु, and प्लव a raft.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=189-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुब
कुब r. 1st and 10th cls. (इ) कुबि (कुम्बति कुम्बयति) To cover, to hide, to<BR>clothe, to screen, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=189-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुबेर|कुबेरः
कुबेर m. (-रः) The deity KUVERA: see कुवेर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=189-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुब्ज|कुब्जः
कुब्ज mfn. (-ब्जः-ब्जा-ब्जं) Humpbacked, crooked.<BR>	 m. (-ब्जः)<BR>	 1. A tree,<BR>(Achyranthes aspera:) see अपामार्ग.<BR>	 2. A scymitar.<BR>	 3. A sort of fish.<BR>(Bola cuja, HAM.)<BR> E. कु the earth, or कु ill badly, and उब्ज् to be<BR>straight, affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=189-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुब्जक|कुब्जकः
कुब्जक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Humpbacked.<BR>	 m. (-कः) An aquatic plant, (Trapa<BR>bispinosa:) see वारिकण्टक.<BR> E. क water, and उब्ज् to be straight, affix<BR>अच्, and कन् added, or कुब्ज and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=189-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुब्जकण्टक|कुब्जकण्टकः
कुब्जकण्टक m. (-कः) A white mimosa.<BR> E. कुब्ज, and कण्टक a thorn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=189-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुव्र
कुव्र n. (-व्रं)<BR>	 1. A forest.<BR>	 2. A hole for sacrificial fire.<BR>	 3. An ear-ring.<BR>	 4.<BR>A thread.<BR>	 5. A cart.<BR> E. कुवि to hide, रक् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=189-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुब्रह्म|कुब्रह्मः
कुब्रह्म m. (-ह्मः) A degraded or contemptible Brahman, one who officiates<BR>for Śūdras.<BR> E. कु bad, ब्रह्मन् a Brahman, टच् affix; also retaining the<BR>final, कुव्रह्मन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=189-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुभ
कुभ r. 10th cl. (इ) कुभि (कुम्भयति) To cover, to clothe, to veil or hide:<BR>see कुब.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=189-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुमार|कुमारं|कुमारः
कुमार r. 10th cl. (कुमारयति) To play, especially as a child also कुमाल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=189-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुमार|कुमारं|कुमारः
कुमार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A boy, one under five years of age.<BR>	 2. A name of<BR>KARTIKEYA.<BR>	 3. A prince, the heir apparent, and who is associated<BR>to the empire, (in theatrical language.)<BR>	 4. A horse-man, a caval-<BR>ier.<BR>	 5. A parrot.<BR>	 6. One of the attendants on the twenty-four Jinas,<BR>and also a sanctified character amongst the Jaina sect.<BR>	 7. A tree,<BR>(Tapia cratæva) see वरुण 8. A name of Sindhu river or Indus.<BR>	 n.<BR>(-रं) Pure gold.<BR>	 f. (-री)<BR>	 1. A young girl, one from ten to twelve<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=189-b" target="_blank">Page189-b+ 60</a>]<BR>years old, a virgin: or in the Tantras any virgin to the age of<BR>sixteen, or as long as menstruation has not commenced.<BR>	 2. A<BR>name of DURGĀ.<BR>	 3. The central part of the universe according to<BR>Hindu geography, Jambu Dwipa or India.<BR>	 4. The most southerly<BR>of the nine portions of the known continent, or of Jambu Dwipa,<BR>the southern extremity of the peninsula, whence Cape Comorin<BR>or Kumari.<BR>	 5. The name of a river flowing from the mountain<BR>Sactiman.<BR>	 6. A plant, (Clitoria ternatea:) see अपराजिता.<BR>	 7. Double<BR>jasmine.<BR>	 8. The aloe tree, (Aloes perfoliata:) see घृतकुमारी.<BR>	 9. The<BR>Syama, a bird so named.<BR> E. कुमार to play as a child, affix अच् fem.<BR>affix ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=189-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुमारक|कुमारकः
कुमारक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A boy, a lad.<BR>	 2. A tree: see वरुण.<BR> E. कन् added to<BR>the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=189-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुमारघातिन्
कुमारघातिन् m. (-ती) The slayer of a child.<BR> E. कुप्तार, हन् to kill, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=189-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुमारपाल|कुमारपालः
कुमारपाल m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. A name of Raja SALIVAHANA.<BR>	 2. Name of a king<BR>of Guzerat.<BR> E. कुमार a child, and पाल a cherisher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=189-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुमारभृत्या
कुमारभृत्या f. (-त्या) Care of a pregnant or lying-in woman, midwifery. E.<BR>कुमार a child, and भृत्या cherishing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=189-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुमारयु|कुमारयुः
कुमारयु m. (-युः) A prince.<BR> E. कुमार prince, या to go or be, and उ Uṇādi<BR>aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=189-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुमारवाहिन्
कुमारवाहिन् m. (-ही) A peacock.<BR> E. कुमार KARTIKEYA, and वाहिन् what<BR>bears; this god being usually represented riding on a peacock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=189-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुमारसू
कुमारसू f. (-सूः) A name of GANGA, the river goddess.<BR> E. कुमार the god<BR>KARTIKEYA, and मू a mother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=189-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुमारिका
कुमारिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. A girl from ten to twelve years old, or generally a<BR>virgin.<BR>	 2. Double jasmine.<BR>	 3. A division of the known continent.<BR>4. Large cardamoms.<BR>	 5. An insect, (Spex Asiatica:) see कुमारी,<BR>कन् being added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=189-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुमाल
कुमाल r. 10th cl. (कुमालयति) To play as a child, &c. see कुमार.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=189-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुमालक|कुमालकः
कुमालक m. (-कः) The name of a district, part of Malwa: also termed<BR>Sauvira.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=189-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुमुद्
कुमुद् mfn. (-त् or -द्)<BR>	 1. Niggardly, avaricious.<BR>	 2. Unkind, unfriendly.<BR>n. (-त् or -द्)<BR>	 1. The esculent white water lily.<BR>	 2. The red lotus. E.<BR>कु the earth, or bad, vile, मुद् to be pleased, and क्विप् affix; also<BR>कुमुद.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=189-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुमुद|कुमुदं|कुमुदः
कुमुद n. (-दं)<BR>	 1. The white esculent water lily, (Mymphæa escu-<BR>lenta.)<BR>	 2. The red lotus, (Nrubra.)<BR>	 3. silver.<BR>	 m. (-दः)<BR>	 1. The ele-<BR>phant of the south-west quarter.<BR>	 2. One of the monkey heroes of<BR>the Rāmāyaṇa.<BR>	 3. One of the Naga or serpent race.<BR>	 4. A Danava<BR>or infernal deity.<BR>	 5. Camphor.<BR>	 f. (-दा)<BR>	 1. An aquatic plant, (Pistia<BR>stratiotes.)<BR>	 2. A tree, (Gmelina arborea:) see गम्भारी. (-दी) A medi-<BR>cinal and aromatic shrub, commonly Kayaphal.<BR> E. कु the earth<BR>&c. मुद् to be pleased, and क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=189-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुमुदबान्धव|कुमुदबांधव|कुमुदबान्धवः
कुमुदबान्धव m. (-वः) The moon.<BR> E. कुमुद a lotus, and बान्धव the friend;<BR>the white esculent lotus expanding its petals during the night,<BR>and closing them in the day time; hence other similar appella-<BR>tions of the moon, as कुमुदबन्धु, कुमुदप्रिय, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=189-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुमुदवती
कुमुदवती f. (-ती) A place abounding in water lilies, &c. see कुमुद्वती.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=189-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुमुदाकर|कुमुदाकरः
कुमुदाकर m. (-रः) A number of water lilies or place abounding with<BR>them.<BR> E. कुमुद, and आकर a mine; also कुमुदवनं, कुमुदिनी, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=189-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुमुदावास|कुमुदावासः
कुमुदावास m. (-सः) A pool abounding in lotuses.<BR> E. कुमुद, and आवास a<BR>residence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=189-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुमुदिक
कुमुदिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Abounding with water lilies.<BR> E. कुमुद, and<BR>ठच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=189-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुमुदिका
कुमुदिका f. (-का) A small tree, the seeds of which are aromatic, com-<BR>monly Kayaphal: see कुमुदी, and कट्फल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=189-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुमुदिनी
कुमुदिनी f. (-नी) A place abounding in lotuses, &c. see कुमुद्वती.<BR> E. कुमुद,<BR>इनि and ङीष् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=189-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुमुदिनीपति|कुमुदिनीपतिः
कुमुदिनीपति m. (-तिः) The moon.<BR> E. कुमुदिनी, and पति lord: see कुमुदबान्धव.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=189-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुमुदेश|कुमुदेशः
कुमुदेश m. (-शः) The moon: see कुमुदबान्धब.<BR> E. कुमुद, and ईश a master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=189-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुमुद्वत्|कुमुद्वन्त्
कुमुद्वत् mfn. (-द्वान्-द्वती-द्वत्) A place abounding in the flowers of the<BR>Nymphæa esculenta.<BR>	 f. (-ती)<BR>	 1. The same.<BR>	 2. A multitude of lotus<BR>flowers.<BR>	 3. The flexible stalk of a water lily.<BR>	 4. A sort of water<BR>lily, (Menyanthes Indica or cristata.)<BR> E. कुमुद the water lily, and<BR>मतुप् poss. affix, or वति affix of comparison, fem. ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=190-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुमेरु|कुमेरुः
कुमेरु m. (-रुः) The southern hemisphere or pole, the region of the<BR>demons and Titans.<BR> E. कु, and मेरु the mountain where the gods<BR>reside.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=190-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुमोदक|कुमोदकः
कुमोदक m. (-कः) A name of VIṢṆU.<BR> E. कु the earth, मुद् to delight,<BR>वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=190-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुम्प|कुम्पः
कुम्प mfn. (-म्पः-म्पा-म्पं) Crooked-armed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=190-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुम्बा|कुंबा
कुम्बा f. (-म्बा) An enclosure round a place of sacrifice, to prevent profane<BR>intrusion.<BR> E. कुवि to cover, to screen or conceal, अङ् and टाप्<BR>affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=190-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुम्भ|कुंभ|कुम्भं|कुंभः|कुम्भः
कुम्भ m. (-म्भः)<BR>	 1. A small water jar.<BR>	 2. The frontal globe on the upper<BR>part of the forehead of an elephant; there are two of these projec-<BR>tion, which swell in the rutting season.<BR>	 3. A sign of the zodiac,<BR>(Aquarius.)<BR>	 4. A proper name, the nephew of Ravana considered<BR>as a Rākṣasa or demon.<BR>	 5. The paramour of a harlot, a<BR>bully, a flash or fancy man.<BR>	 6. (In Yoga phil) A religious<BR>exercise, closing the nostrils and mouth so as to suspend<BR>breathing.<BR>	 7. A measure of grain equal to twenty Dronas,<BR>a little more than three bushels and three gallons, or a<BR>Comb: some make it to Dronas or sixty-four Seers.<BR>	 n. (-म्भं)<BR>	 1. A<BR>fragrant resin or the plant which bears it, (Bdellium.)<BR>	 2. A plant<BR>commonly Teori: see त्रिवृत्.<BR>	 f. (-म्भी)<BR>	 1. A pot, an earthen cooking<BR>vessel, a small jar.<BR>	 2. Kayaphal, a small tree, the seeds of which<BR>are used in medicine: see कट्फल 3. An aquatic plant, (Pistia<BR>stratiotes.)<BR>	 4. Trumpet flower, (Bignonia suave-olens.) (-म्भा) A<BR>harlot, a whore.<BR> E. कु the earth, or base, vile, &c. उम्भ् to fill, and<BR>अण् or अच् affix, deriv, irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=190-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुम्भक|कुंभक|कुंभकः|कुम्भकः
कुम्भक m. (-कः) Stopping the breath by shutting the mouth and close-<BR>ing both nostrils with the fingers of the right hand.<BR> E. कन् added<BR>to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=190-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुम्भकर्ण|कुम्भकर्णः
कुम्भकर्ण m. (-र्णः) The gigantic brother of RAVANA.<BR> E. कुम्भ and कर्ण the ear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=190-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुम्भकामला
कुम्भकामला f. (-ला) A bilious affection, a sort of jaundice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=190-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुस्मकार
कुस्मकार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A potter.<BR>	 2. A kind of wild fowl.<BR>	 f. (-री)<BR>	 1. A min-<BR>eral substance, used as an application to strengthen the eyes<BR>and beautify the eye lashes.<BR>	 2. Red arsenic.<BR>	 3. The wife of a<BR>potter.<BR> E. कुम्भ a jar, &c. and कार what makes, from कृ to make,<BR>and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=190-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुम्भकारक
कुम्भकारक m. (-कः) A potter.<BR>	 f. (-रिका)<BR>	 1. Collyrium.<BR>	 2. A woman of the<BR>potter caste.<BR> E. कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=190-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुम्भतुम्बी
कुम्भतुम्बी f. (-म्बी) A large round gourd.<BR> E. कुम्भ, and तुम्बी a gourd.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=190-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुम्भदासी|कुंभदासी
कुम्भदासी f. (-सी) A bawd, a procuress.<BR> E. कुम्भ a bully, and दासी a fe-<BR>male slave.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=190-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुम्भपदी
कुम्भपदी f. (-दी) A woman with an enlarged leg.<BR> E. कुम्भ and पद् for पाद a<BR>foot, fem. affix ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=190-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुम्भपाद
कुम्भपाद m. (-दः) A man with an enlarged leg.<BR> E. कुम्भ and पाद a foot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=190-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुम्भयोनि|कुंभयोनि|कुम्भयोनिः
कुम्भयोनि m. (-निः)<BR>	 1. A name of AGASTYA, a saint so called.<BR>	 2. Also<BR>of VASIṢṬHA; and of DRONA, the military preceptor of the<BR>Kurus and Pandus.<BR> E. कुम्भ a jar, and योनि a womb; born in a<BR>water jar, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=190-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुम्भला
कुम्भला f. (-ला) A plant, the flowers of which are compared to those of<BR>the Naucleacadamba: see कुण्डिरि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=190-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुम्भशाला
कुम्भशाला f. (-ला) A pottery, a potter's kiln.<BR> E. कुम्भ a jar, and शाला a<BR>hall, a shop.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=190-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुम्भसन्धि|कुम्भसंधि|कुंभसंधि|कुम्भसन्धिः
कुम्भसन्धि m. (-न्धिः) The hollow on the top of an elephant's head, be-<BR>tween the frontal globes.<BR> E. कुम्भ the frontal globe, and सन्धि<BR>junction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=190-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुम्भसम्भव|कुम्भसंभव|कुंभसंभव|कुम्भसंभवः|कुम्भसम्भवः
कुम्भसम्भव m. (-वः) The saint AGASTYA: see अगस्थ<BR> E. कुम्भ a jar, and<BR>सम्भव born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=190-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुम्भाण्ड|कुम्भाण्डः
कुम्भाण्ड m. (-ण्डः) A minister of the Asura, BANA, mf (ण्डः-ण्डी) A pump-<BR>kin gourd: see कुम्भाण्ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=190-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुम्भिका|कुंभिका
कुम्भिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. An aquatic plant, (Pistia stratiotes.)<BR>	 2. Trumpet<BR>flower.<BR>	 3. A disease of the eyes, hordeolum or stye.<BR> E. कुम्भी as<BR>above, and कन् affix, in the fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=190-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुम्भिन्|कुंभिन्
कुम्भिन् mfn. (-म्भी-म्भिनी-म्भि)<BR>	 1. Having a water jar.<BR>	 2. Shaped like a<BR>water jar, &c.<BR> E. कुम्भ, and इनि affix.<BR>	 m. (-म्भी)<BR>	 1. An elephant.<BR>	 2. A<BR>crocodile.<BR>	 3. A fish.<BR>	 4. A plant bearing a fragrant resin, Bdellium.<BR>E. कुम्भ as above, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=190-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुम्भिनीवीज|कुम्भिनीवीजं
कुम्भिनीवीज n. (-जं) The croton nut.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=190-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुम्भिमद|कुंभिमद|कुम्भिमदः
कुम्भिमद m. (-दः) The juice that exudes from an elephant's temples at<BR>certain seasons.<BR> E. कुम्भि, and मद the exudation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=190-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुम्भिल|कुंभिल|कुंभिलः|कुम्भिलः
कुम्भिल m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. A thief.<BR>	 2. A plagiarist, a paraphrast.<BR>	 3. A wife's<BR>brother.<BR>	 4. A fish, the gilt-head.<BR>	 5. A child begotten at undue<BR>seasons, or of an imperfect impregnation.<BR> E. कुम्भ as above, and<BR>इलच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=190-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुम्भीक|कुंभीक|कुंभीकः|कुम्भीकः
कुम्भीक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A plant. the bark of which furnishes a yellow dye,<BR>(Rottleria tinctoria:) see पुन्नाग.<BR>	 2. An aquatic plant.<BR>	 3. An affec-<BR>tion of the eyes, hordeolum or stye: see कुम्भिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=190-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुम्भीधान्य
कुम्भीधान्य m. (-न्यः) Grain stored in jars sufficient, according to some, for<BR>six days, or to others for one year's consumption.<BR> E. कुम्भ, and धान्य<BR>grain, च्वि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=190-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुम्भीधान्यक|कुम्भीधान्यकः
कुम्भीधान्यक m. (-कः) A householder, preserving grain in store for six<BR>days, &c.<BR> E. कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=190-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुम्भीनस|कुंभीनस|कुम्भीनसः
कुम्भीनस m. (-सः) A large, and venomous snake.<BR>	 f. (-सी) The mother of<BR>LAVANA, a Rākṣasa or fiend.<BR> E. कुम्भी a pitcher, and नस derived<BR>from नासा the nose; having wide nostrils.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=190-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुम्भीपाक|कुंभीपाक|कुम्भीपाकः
कुम्भीपाक m. (-कः) A hell.<BR> E. कुम्भी a pot, and पाक what cooks: in which<BR>the wicked are baked like potters' vessels.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=190-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुम्भीर|कुंभीर|कुंभीरः|कुम्भीरः
कुम्भीर m. (-रः) The crocodile of the ganges; the long nosed alligator.<BR>E. कुम्भी an elephant, and ईर what resembles; or कुम्भी a fish, and<BR>र who seized, from रा to take or gain: or ल from ला, whence also<BR>कुम्भील.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=190-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुम्भीरमक्षिका
कुम्भीरमक्षिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. A sort of fly or aquatic insect.<BR> E. कुम्भी a croco-<BR>dile, and मक्षिका a fly, the crocodile fly, alluding, perhaps, to<BR>its size.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=190-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुम्भील|कुंभील|कुंभीलः|कुम्भीलः
कुम्भील m. (-लः) A crocodile: see कुम्भीर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=190-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुम्भीवीज|कुम्भीवीजं
कुम्भीवीज n. (-जं) The nut of the croton.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=190-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुर
कुर r. 6th cl. (कुरति) To sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=190-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुरका
कुरका f. (-का) The olibanum tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=190-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुरङ्कर|कुरंकर|कुरंकरः|कुरङ्करः
कुरङ्कर m. (-रः) The Indian crane.<BR> E. कुर् to sound, क affix, a sound,<BR>and कर what makes; also कुरङ्कुर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=190-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुरङ्ग|कुरंग|कुरंगः|कुरङ्गः
कुरङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः) A deer, an antelope.<BR> E. कुर् to sound, अङ्गच् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=190-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुरङ्गक|कुरंगकः|कुरङ्गकः
कुरङ्गक m. (-कः) A deer.<BR> E. कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=190-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुरङ्गनयना|कुरंगनयना
कुरङ्गनयना f. (-ना) A handsome woman.<BR> E. कुरङ्ग, and नयना the eye,<BR>fawn-eyed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=190-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुरङ्गम|कुरंगम|कुरंगमः|कुरङ्गमः
कुरङ्गम m. (-मः) A deer, an antelope.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=190-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुरचिल्ल|कुरचिल्लः
कुरचिल्ल m. (-ल्लः) A crab.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=190-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुरट|कुरटः
कुरट m. (-टः) A currier, a leather-seller, a shoe-maker.<BR> E. कु bad, रट्<BR>to speak, अच् affix; being described as a man of low occupation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=190-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुरण्टक|कुरंटक|कुरंटकः|कुरण्टकः
कुरण्टक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. Yellow amaranth.<BR>	 2. Yellow barleria: see कुरुण्टक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=190-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुरण्ड|कुरंड|कुरंडः|कुरण्डः
कुरण्ड m. (-ण्डः) Enlargement of the testicles or rather of the scrotum,<BR>including inguinal hernia, hydrocele, &c.<BR> E. कु bad, ill, रम् to play,<BR>and ड aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=190-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुरण्डक|कुरंडकः|कुरण्डकः
कुरण्डक m. (-कः) Yellow amaranth: see कुरुण्टक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=190-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुरर|कुररः
कुरर mf. (-रः-रा) An osprey; also another species of eagle.<BR>	 f. (-री) A<BR>sheep, an ewe.<BR>	 2. A female osprey.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=190-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुररीगण|कुररीगणः
कुररीगण m. (-णः) A flight of ospreys.<BR> E. कुररी, and गण a troop.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=190-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुरल|कुरलः
कुरल m. (-लः) A curl, a lock of hair.<BR>	 2. An osprey, see कुरुल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=191-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुरव|कुरवः
कुरव mfn. (-वः-वा-वं) Having a bad voice.<BR>	 m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. A bad or harsh<BR>sound.<BR>	 2. Red or yellow amaranth: see कुरवक.<BR> E. कु bad or ill, and<BR>रव what sounds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=191-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुरवक|कुरवकः
कुरवक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Having a bad voice, making a disagreeable<BR>sound.<BR>	 m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A purple sort of Jhinti or Barleria.<BR>	 2. A crim-<BR>son species of amaranth.<BR> E. कु bad, रव to sound, क्वन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=191-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुरस|कुरसः
कुरस mfn. (-सः-सा-सं) Bad-juiced, of bad essence.<BR>	 m. (-सः) Sprituous or<BR>vinous liquor.<BR>	 f. (-सा) A wild creeping plant, a species of hiera-<BR>cium; see गोजिह्वा.<BR> E. कु bad, and रस juice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=191-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुराल|कुरालः
कुराल m. (-लः) A light bay horse with black legs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=191-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुरी
कुरी f. (-री) A kind of grass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=191-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुरीर|कुरीरं
कुरीर n. (-र) Copulation.<BR> E. कृ to do, ईरन् Uṇādi affix, उद् inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=191-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुरु|कुरुः
कुरु m. (-रुः)<BR>	 1. Kuru or Uttara Kuru, the most northerly of the four<BR>Maha Dwipas, or principal divisions of the known world, by other<BR>systems it is considered as one of nine divisions of Varṣas of the<BR>same; in both cases it is the country beyond the northern-most<BR>range of mountains, extending to the frozen ocean.<BR>	 2. A proper<BR>name, son of AGNIDHRA, and grandson of PRIYAVRATA.<BR>	 3. A proper<BR>name, a prince of the lunar race, son of SAMVARANA by TAPATI;<BR>sovereign of the north-west of India or the country about Delhi,<BR>and ancestor of both PĀṆḌU and DHRITARASHTRA; the patrony-<BR>mic however derived from his name is most usually applied to the<BR>sons of the latter.<BR>	 4. A holy place: see कुरुक्षेत्र.<BR>	 5. Boiled rice.<BR>	 6.<BR>Pricklynightshade: see कण्टकारिका.<BR> E. कृ to make, कु affix, and ऋ<BR>becomes. उ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=191-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुरुकन्दक|कुरुकन्दकं
कुरुकन्दक n. (-कं) Horseradish, (Raphanus sativus.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=191-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुरुक्षेव
कुरुक्षेव n. (-त्रं) The country near Delhi, the scene of the great battle<BR>between the Kurus and Pandus.<BR> E. कुरु the Kuru race, and क्षेत्र a<BR>field.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=191-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुरुक्षेत्रीयोग|कुरुक्षेत्रीयोगः
कुरुक्षेत्रीयोग m. (-गः) A solar day, in the course of which three lunar days,<BR>three asterisms and three Yogas occur.<BR> E. कुरुक्षेत्र, and योग<BR>conjunction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=191-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुरुण्ट|कुरुंट|कुरुंटः|कुरुण्टः
कुरुण्ट m. (-ण्टः)<BR>	 1. Yellow amaranth.<BR>	 2. Yellow Barleria.<BR>	 f. (-ण्टी)<BR>	 1. A<BR>doll, a puppet.<BR>	 2. The wife of a Brahman or teacher.<BR> E. कु bad, रुटि<BR>to shine, affix अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=191-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुरुण्टक|कुरुंटकः|कुरुण्टकः
कुरुण्टक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. Yellow or white amaranth.<BR>	 2. A yellow species of<BR>Barleria, (B. prionitis.)<BR> E. कु bad, रुटि to shine, &c. ण्वुल् affix; also<BR>कुरण्टक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=191-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुरुम्ब|कुरुंबं|कुरुम्बं
कुरुम्ब n. (-म्बं) A large species of orange.<BR>	 f. (-म्बा) Trumpet flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=191-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुरुराज्
कुरुराज् m. (-ट्) A name of DURYODHANA.<BR> E. कुरु the Kuru race, राज् to<BR>shine, and क्विप् affix; the Kuru chief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=191-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुरुरी
कुरुरी f. (-री) A kind of bird with a warbling note.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=191-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुरुल|कुरुलः
कुरुल m. (-लः) A curl or lock of hair, especially on the forehead.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=191-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुरुवक|कुरुवकः
कुरुवक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. The crimson amaranth.<BR>	 2. A purple species of<BR>Barleria.<BR>	 3. Also a yellow kind.<BR> E. कु a little, रु to sound, क्वुन्<BR>affix, and उवङ् substituted for उ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=191-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुरुविन्द|कुरुविंद|कुरुविंदं|कुरुविन्दं|कुरुविंदः|कुरुविन्दः
कुरुविन्द mn. (-न्दः-न्दं)<BR>	 1. A fragrant grass, (Cyperus rotundus.)<BR>	 2. A<BR>kind of barley: see कल्माष.<BR>	 3. A ruby: see कुरुविल्ल.<BR>	 4. Black salt.<BR>5. Vermilion.<BR>	 6. A mirror.<BR> E. कुरु Kurudesa, विन्द् to gain, and श<BR>affix; found in that country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=191-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुरुविन्दक
कुरुविन्दक m. (-कः) A kind of Dolichos biflorus, a wild variety.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=191-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुरुविल्ल|कुरुविल्लः
कुरुविल्ल m. (-ल्लः) A ruby; also कुरुविल्ल, and कुरुविन्द.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=191-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुरुविल्व|कुरुविल्वः
कुरुविल्व m. (-ल्वः) A ruby; also कुरुविन्द.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=191-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुरुविस्त|कुरुविस्तः
कुरुविस्त m. (-स्तः) A Pala of gold, a weight of gold equal to about 700<BR>Tory grains.<BR> E. कुरु the country, and विस्त abundant; abounding in<BR>Kurudesa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=191-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुरूप
कुरूप mfn. (-पः-पी-पं) Ugly, ill made, deformed.<BR>	 n. (-षं) Ugliness.<BR> E. कु,<BR>and रूप form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=191-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुरूपता
कुरूपता f. (-ता) Ugliness.<BR> E. तल् added to the last; also कुरूपत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=191-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुरूपिन्
कुरूपिन् mfn. (-पी-पिणी-पि) Ugly, ill made, frightful, deformed.<BR> E. कुरूप,<BR>and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=191-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुरूप्य|कुरूप्यं
कुरूप्य n. (-प्यं) Tin.<BR> E. कु base, रूप्य silver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=191-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुर्क्कुर|कुर्कुर|कुर्कुरः
कुर्क्कुर mf. (-रः-री) A dog or bitch.<BR> E. कुर् instead of कु bad, prefixed to कु<BR>to sound, and रक् affix: see कुक्कुर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=191-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुर्द|कुर्द्द
कुर्द r. 1st cl. (कूर्दते or कुर्दते) To play; also कूर्द.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=191-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुर्दन|कुर्द्दन|कुर्द्दनं
कुर्दन n. (-नं) Play, playing, sport: see कूर्दन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=191-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुर्पर|कुर्परः
कुर्पर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. The knee.<BR>	 2. The elbow; also कूर्पर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=191-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुर्पास|कुर्पासः
कुर्पास m. (-सः) A sort of bodice or jacket: see कूर्पास; also with कन्<BR>added कुर्पासक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=191-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुर्व्वाण|कुर्वाण
कुर्व्वाण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Doing, making.<BR> E. कृ to make, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=191-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुर्व्वत्|कुर्वत्|कुर्वन्त्
कुर्व्वत् mfn. (-र्व्वन्-र्व्वन्ती-र्व्वत्)<BR>	 1. Doing, acting, an agent.<BR>	 2. A servant. E.<BR>कृ to do, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=191-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुर्व्वद्रूप|कुर्वद्रूप
कुर्व्वद्रूप n. (-पं)<BR>	 1. Cause according to the Chravakas.<BR>	 2. grain.<BR> E. कुर्व्वत्,<BR>and रूप nature.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=191-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुल|कुलं|कुलः
कुल r. 1st cl. (कोलति)<BR>	 1. To accumulate.<BR>	 2. To be of kin, to act as of<BR>kin.<BR>	 3. To flow homogeneously.<BR>	 4. To count. With आङ् prefixed,<BR>to be attentive; with वि to be bewildered, flurried or distressed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=191-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुल|कुलं|कुलः
कुल n. (-लं)<BR>	 1. Family, race, tribe or caste.<BR>	 2. A herd, a flock, &c. of ani-<BR>mals of the same species.<BR>	 3. An inhabited country.<BR>	 4. A house,<BR>an abode.<BR>	 5. The body.<BR>	 6. The front or forepart.<BR>	 7. A blue stone:<BR>see कुलत्थ m. (-लः) An artist of celebrated descent.<BR>	 f. (-लिः or -ली) A<BR>prickly nightshade: see कण्टकारी, &c. (-ली) A wife's elder sister. E.<BR>कुल् to accumulate, क affix, or कुङ् to sound, and लक् affix, or कु<BR>the earth, and ल who takes or possesses, from ला with ड aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=191-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलक|कुलकं|कुलकः
कुलक mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>	 1. Of a good family, of eminent birth.<BR>	 m. (-कः)<BR>1. A species of ebony, (Diospyros tomentosa, Rox.) See काकेन्दु.<BR>	 2.<BR>An artist of eminent birth.<BR>	 3. An ant or mole hill.<BR>	 4. A green<BR>snake.<BR>	 n. (-कं)<BR>	 1. A sort of gourd, (Trichosanthes diæca.)<BR>	 2. The<BR>connexion of several stanzas, protraction of the government of<BR>the noun or verb through several verses, contrary to the practice<BR>of closing the sense with each verse.<BR> E. कन् added to the prece-<BR>ding, or कुल race, and क who sounds. declares, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=191-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलकन्या
कुलकन्या f. (-न्या) A girl of good family.<BR> E. कुल and कन्या a maiden.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=191-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलकर्म्मन्|कुलकर्मन्
कुलकर्म्मन् n. (-र्म्म) The proper duty of a race or family, any observance<BR>customarily held by one.<BR> E. कुल, and कर्म्म act; also कुलक्रिया and<BR>कुलकार्य्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=191-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलक्क|कुलक्कः
कुलक्क m. (-क्कः) Beating time in music.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=191-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलक्षय|कुलक्षयः
कुलक्षय m. (-यः) Decay or disappearance of a family.<BR>	 f. (-या) Cowach,<BR>(Carpopogon pruriens.)<BR> E. कुल the body, and क्षय injurious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=191-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलगिरि|कुलगिरिः
कुलगिरि m. (-रिः) A mountain, any one of the seven principal moun-<BR>tains of Bhāratavarṣa.<BR> E. कुल and गिरि mountain: see कुलाचल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=191-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलङ्गी
कुलङ्गी f. (-ङ्गी) A thorny plant: see कर्कटशृङ्गी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=191-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलज|कुलजः
कुलज mfn. (-जह्-जा-जं)<BR>	 1. Well-born, of a good family.<BR>	 2. Ancestral,<BR>hereditary,<BR> E. कुल, and ज born; also कुलजात, कुलोत्पन्न, and similar<BR>compounds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=191-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलञ्ज|कुलञ्जः
कुलञ्ज m. (-ञ्जः) See the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=191-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलञ्जन|कुलञ्जनः
कुलञ्जन m. (-नः) An aromatic plant, (Alpinia galanga;) also कुलञ्ज and गन्धमूल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=191-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलट|कुलटः
कुलट m. (-टः) Any son except the one begotten, as one adopted,<BR>bought, &c.<BR>	 f. (-टा) An unchaste woman.<BR> E. कुल race, and अट who<BR>goes, deriv. irr.; by whom the family honour is injured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=191-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलटापति
कुलटापति m. (-तिः) The husband of an unchaste woman, a cuckold. E.<BR>कुलटा, and पति husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=191-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलटी
कुलटी(-टी) Red arsenic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=191-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलतिथि|कुलतिथिः
कुलतिथि mf. (-थिः) The fourth, eighth, twelvth, or fourteenth lunar<BR>day.<BR> E. कुल, and तिथि a lunation, respectable days.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=191-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलतिलक|कुलतिलकः
कुलतिलक m. (-कः) The chief of a family, one who does honour to a<BR>family.<BR> E. कुल and तिलक frontal mark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=191-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलत्थ|कुलत्थः
कुलत्थ m. (-त्थः) A kind of pulse, (Dlichos biflorus.)<BR>	 f. (-त्था)<BR>	 1. A blue<BR>stone used in medicine, and applied as a collyrium to the eyes;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=192-a" target="_blank">Page192-a+ 60</a>]<BR>also an astringent to sores, &c.)<BR>	 2. A wild kind of Dolichos.<BR> E. कुल<BR>a bank, and स्था to stand or stay, affix ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=191-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलत्थिका
कुलत्थिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. A blue stone used as a collyrium. &c.<BR>	 2. A sort of<BR>vetch, considered as a wild sort of the Dolichos biflorus. E. See<BR>the preceding, कन् added to कुलत्थ in the fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=192-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलधर्म्म|कुलधर्म|कुलधर्मः|कुलधर्म्मः
कुलधर्म्म m. (-र्म्मः) Practice or observance peculiar to a tribe or family,<BR>peculiar duty of caste or race.<BR> E. कुल family, and धर्म्म virtue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=192-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलधारक|कुलधारकः
कुलधारक m. (-कः) A son.<BR> E. कुल a race, and धृ to hold, in the causal<BR>form वुन् affix; upholding a family.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=192-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलनक्षत्र|कुलनक्षत्रं
कुलनक्षत्र n. (-त्रं) Any propitious asterism.<BR> E. कुल, and नक्षत्र asterism.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=192-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलनायिका
कुलनायिका f. (-का) A girl who is worshipped at the celebration of the<BR>orgies of the left hand Saktas.<BR> E. कुल society, and नायिका a<BR>female.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=192-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलनारी
कुलनारी f. (-री) A woman of good family.<BR> E. कुल and नारी a woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=192-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलनाश|कुलनाशः
कुलनाश ml. (-शः)<BR>	 1. camel.<BR>	 2. A reprobate, an outcaste.<BR> E. कुल a family,<BR>नाश who hurts or destroys.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=192-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलनिन्दा
कुलनिन्दा f. (-न्दा) Family disgrace.<BR> E. कुल, and निन्दा reproach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=192-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलपति|कुलपतिः
कुलपति m. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Head or chief of a family.<BR>	 2. A sage who teaches<BR>10000 pupils with free board & lodging.<BR> E. कुल a family, and पति<BR>master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=192-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलपर्व्वत|कुलपर्वत|कुलपर्वतः
कुलपर्व्वत m. (-तः) A principal mountain of India, any one of seven so<BR>considered: see कुलाचल.<BR> E. कुल, and पर्व्वत a mountain; also similar<BR>compounds, as कुलगिरि, कुलशैल, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=192-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलपांसुला
कुलपांसुला f. (-ला) An unchaste woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=192-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलपालक|कुलपालकं
कुलपालक mfn. (-लकः-लिका-लकं) Nourishing or providing for a family.<BR>n. (-कं) A kind of orange.<BR> E. कुल a race, &c. पाल् to nourish, and<BR>वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=192-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलपालि|कुलपालिः
कुलपालि f. (-लिः) A chaste woman.<BR> E. कुल race, and पाल who nourishes,<BR>इन् fem. affix; also कुलपालिका and कुलपाली.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=192-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलपालिका
कुलपालिका f. (-का) See कुलपालि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=192-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलबधू
कुलबधू f. (-धूः) A virtuous or respectable woman.<BR> E. कुल, and बधू a wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=192-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलभृत्या
कुलभृत्या f. (-त्या) A midwife, a nurse.<BR> E. कुल family, and भृत्या a servant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=192-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलभ्रष्ट
कुलभ्रष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं) Expelled from a family.<BR> E. कुल, and भ्रष्ट fallen<BR>from.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=192-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलमर्य्यादा|कुलमर्यादा
कुलमर्य्यादा f. (-दा) Family honour or respectability.<BR> E. कुल, and मर्य्यादा propriety.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=192-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलमित्र
कुलमित्र n. (-त्रं) A friend of the family.<BR> E. कुल, and मित्र a friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=192-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलम्भर|कुलंभर|कुलंभरः|कुलम्भरः
कुलम्भर m. (-रः) A thief: see कुजम्भल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=192-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलयोषित्
कुलयोषित् f. (-त्) A virtuous woman.<BR> E. कुल, and योषित् a woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=192-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलवार|कुलवारः
कुलवार m. (-रः) Tuesday or Friday.<BR> E. कुल, and वार a day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=192-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलविप्र|कुलविप्रः
कुलविप्र m. (-प्रः) The family priest.<BR> E. कुल race, and विप्र a Brahman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=192-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलव्यापिन्
कुलव्यापिन् mfn. (-पो-पिनी-पि) Attaching or applicable to tribe or caste.<BR>E. कुल, and व्यापिन् prevailing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=192-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलश्रेष्ठिन्
कुलश्रेष्ठिन् mfn. (-ष्ठी-ष्ठिनी-ष्ठि)<BR>	 1. An artificer or artist of eminent birth.<BR>2. Well-born, of good family. Eminent in a family.<BR> E. कुल race, and<BR>श्रेष्ठ best, poss. affix इनि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=192-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलसंख्या|कुलसङ्ख्या
कुलसंख्या f. (-ख्या) Ranking or being reckoned as a family respectability.<BR>E. कुल, and संख्या enumeration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=192-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलसन्तति|कुलसंतति|कुलसंततिः
कुलसन्तति f. (-तिः) Bosterity, descendants.<BR> E. कुल, and सन्तति continuance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=192-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलसन्निधि|कुलसंनिधि|कुलसन्निधिः
कुलसन्निधि f. (-धिः)<BR>	 1. Kindred, relations.<BR>	 2. Presence of witnesses. E.<BR>कुल, and सन्निधि proximity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=192-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलसम्भव|कुलसंभव|कुलसम्भवः
कुलसम्भव mfn. (-वः-वा-वं) Sprung from family.<BR> E. कुल race, and सम्भव born,<BR>produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=192-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलसौरभ|कुलसौरभं
कुलसौरभ n. (-भं) A plant, commonly Marua: see मरूवक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=192-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलस्थिति|कुलस्थितिः
कुलस्थिति f. (-तिः) Antiquity or prosperity of a family.<BR> E. कुल, and स्थिति<BR>duration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=192-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलस्त्री
कुलस्त्री f. (-स्त्री)<BR>	 1. A chaste woman.<BR>	 2. A woman of a good family, a<BR>respectable woman.<BR> E. कुल a family, and स्त्री a woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=192-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलहण्टक
कुलहण्टक m. (-कः) An eddy: see कूलहण्टक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=192-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलाकुल
कुलाकुल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Of mixed origin, of a mixed character.<BR> E. कुल<BR>propitious, and आकुल bewildered, or कुल with a neg. prefix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=192-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलाकुलतिथि|कुलाकुलतिथिः
कुलाकुलतिथि mf. (-थिः-थिः) The second, sixth or tenth lunar days. E.<BR>कुलाकुल, and तिथि a lunation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=192-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलाकुलनक्षत्र|कुलाकुलनक्षत्रं
कुलाकुलनक्षत्र n. (-त्रं) An asterism of mixed character, as Varuni, Ardra,<BR>Mula and Abhijit.<BR> E. कुलाकुल, and नक्षत्र asterism.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=192-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलाकुलवार|कुलाकुलवारः
कुलाकुलवार m. (-रः) Wednesday.<BR> E. कुलाकुल and वार a day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=192-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलाक्षुता
कुलाक्षुता f. (-ता) A bitch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=192-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलाचल|कुलाचलः
कुलाचल m. (-लः) A mountain, one of a class of seven principal moun-<BR>tains, which are supposed to exist in each Varṣa or division of a<BR>continent: those of Bhāratavarṣa, India are Mohendra, Malaya,<BR>Sahya, Śuktimān, Riksha, Vindyha, and Pāripātra.<BR> E. कुल a race,<BR>and अचल a mountain; also कुलाद्रि, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=192-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलाचार|कुलाचारः
कुलाचार m. (-रः) The proper duty or practice of a caste or family. E.<BR>कुल, and आचार observance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=192-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलाचार्य्य|कुलाचार्य|कुलाचार्यः|कुलाचार्य्यः
कुलाचार्य्य m. (-र्य्यः)<BR>	 1. A family priest.<BR>	 2. A genealogist.<BR> E. कुल and<BR>आचार्य्य teacher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=192-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलाट|कुलाटः
कुलाट m. (-टः) A small fish.<BR> E. कुल for कूल a bank, and अट who goes;<BR>burrowing in the sand and mud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=192-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलाधारक|कुलाधारकः
कुलाधारक m. (-कः) A son. E. See कुलधारक, आङ् being here inserted<BR>signifying extension.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=192-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलाभि|कुलाभिः
कुलाभि m. (-भिः) A treasure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=192-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलाभिमान|कुलाभिमानः
कुलाभिमान n. (-नं) Pride of birth, family pride.<BR> E. कुल, and अभिमान pride.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=192-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलाभिमानिन्
कुलाभिमानिन् mfn. (-नी-निनी-नि) Proud of birth or of family descent. E.<BR>कुल, and अभिमानिन् proud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=192-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलाय|कुलायं|कुलायः
कुलाय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. A nest.<BR>	 2. A place, a spot in general.<BR>	 n. (-यं) The<BR>body.<BR> E. कुल family, and अय् to go, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=192-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलायनिलाय|कुलायनिलायः
कुलायनिलाय m. (-यः) The act of sitting in a nest, brooding.<BR> E. कुलाय, and<BR>निलाय abiding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=192-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलायनिलायिन्
कुलायनिलायिन् mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि) Brooding, hatching, (as a bird.)<BR> E. कुलाय,<BR>and निलायिन् who abides in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=192-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलायनिलायिता
कुलायनिलायिता f. (-ता) The act or condition of hatching, &c.<BR> E. तल्<BR>added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=192-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलायस्थ|कुलायस्थः
कुलायस्थ m. (-स्थः) A bird.<BR> E. कुलाय a nest, and स्थ who abides.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=192-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलायिका
कुलायिका f. (-का) An aviary.<BR> E. कुलाय a nest, and कन् affix in the fem.<BR>form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=192-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलाल|कुलालः
कुलाल m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. A potter.<BR>	 2. A wild cock.<BR>	 f. (-ली)<BR>	 1. A species of<BR>bluestone, applied as a collyrium to the eyes.<BR>	 2. The wife of a pot-<BR>ter.<BR> E. कुल् to accumulate, and कालन Uṇādi affix, or कुल family, अल्<BR>to adorn, &c. अण् and ङीप् or ङीष् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=192-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलालम्बिन्|कुलालंबिन्
कुलालम्बिन् mfn. (-म्बी-म्बिनी-म्बि) Supporting or maintaining a family. E.<BR>कुल, and आलम्बिन् what upholds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=192-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलालिका
कुलालिका f. (-का) An aviary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=192-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलाह|कुलाहः
कुलाह m. (-हः) A horse of a light brown colour, with black knees.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=192-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलाहल|कुलाहलः
कुलाहल m. (-लः) A small tree, (Conyza terebinthina.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=192-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलाहक|कुलाहकः
कुलाहक m. (-कः) A chamelion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=192-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलि|कुलिः
कुलि m. (-लिः) A hand.<BR>	 f. (-लिः) A prickly nightshade: see कुल<BR> E. कुल्<BR>to accumulate, &c. कि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=192-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलिक|कुलिकः
कुलिक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Of a good family, well-born.<BR>	 m. (-कः) One of<BR>the eight chiefs of the Nagas or serpent race, described as having<BR>a half moon on the top of his head, and being of a monkey hue.<BR>2. An artist or artificer of eminent birth.<BR>	 3. A thorny plant,<BR>(Ruellia longifolia)<BR>	 4. The chief or headman of a tribe or caste.<BR>E. कुल family, &c. कन् affix, and इ substituted for अ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=192-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलिकवेला
कुलिकवेला f. (-ला) Certain portions of each day, on which it is impro-<BR>per to begin any business.<BR> E. कुलिक, and वेला time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=192-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलिङ्ग|कुलिंग|कुलिंगः|कुलिङ्गः
कुलिङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>	 1. The fork-tailed shrike.<BR>	 2. A sparrow; also कलिङ्ग.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=192-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलिङ्गक|कुलिङ्गकः
कुलिङ्गक m. (-कः) A sparrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=192-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलिर|कुलिरं|कुलिरः
कुलिर m. (-रः) A crab; also कुलीर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=192-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलिश|कुलिशं|कुलिशः
कुलिश mn. (-शः-शं)<BR>	 1. The thunderbolt of INDRA.<BR>	 2. A kind of fish. E.<BR>कुलि for कुल a bank, and श what rests, from शीञ् to sleep, &c. and<BR>क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=192-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलिशभृत्
कुलिशभृत् m. (-भृत्) INDRA.<BR> E. कुलिश and भृत् who has.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=193-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलिशाङ्कुश
कुलिशाङ्कुश f. (-श) A kind of female deity.<BR> E. कुलिश the thunderbolt,<BR>and अङ्कुश a goad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=193-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलिशासन|कुलिशासनः
कुलिशासन m. (-नः) A name of Sakya, a Buddha or Bauddha saint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=193-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलीन|कुलीनः
कुलीन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Well-born, of high or eminent descent, of a good<BR>family.<BR>	 m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. A horse of a good breed.<BR>	 2. A Brahman of one<BR>of the twenty-two Rarhiya divisions of the five principal tribes, as<BR>established by Balal Sen kind of Bengal.<BR>	 3. A worshipper of<BR>SAKTI, according to the left hand ritual: see कौलीन.<BR> E. कुल a<BR>family, and ख aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=193-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलीनक|कुलीनकः
कुलीनक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Of a good family.<BR>	 m. (-कः) A kind of wild<BR>kidney bean.<BR> E. कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=193-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलीनता
कुलीनता f. (-ता) Birth, rank, family respectability.<BR> E. कुलीन, and तल्<BR>affix; also with त्व, कुलीनत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=193-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलीनस|कुलीनसं
कुलीनस n. (-सं) Water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=193-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलीर|कुलीरः
कुलीर mn. (-रः-रं) A crab.<BR> E. कुल् to accumulate, and ईरन् affix; also<BR>कुलिर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=193-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलीरशृङ्गी
कुलीरशृङ्गी f. (-ङ्गी) A plant: see कर्क्कटशृङ्गी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=193-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलीराद्
कुलीराद् m. (-द् or -त्) A young crab.<BR> E. कुलीर a crab. and अद् to eat,<BR>affix क्विप्; destroying its parent; the old crab being supposed to<BR>perish on producing young.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=193-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलीश|कुलीशं|कुलीशः
कुलीश mn. (-शः-शं) INDRA'S thunderbolt: see कुलिश.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=193-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलुक|कुलुकं
कुलुक n. (-कं) The fur or foulness of the tongue.<BR> E. कुल् to accumulate,<BR>and उक aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=193-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलक्वगुञ्जा
कुलक्वगुञ्जा 1. (-ञ्जा) A firebrand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=193-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलेश्वर|कुलेश्वरः
कुलेश्वर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A name of ŚIVA.<BR>	 2. The chief of a family or race. E.<BR>कुल a race, ईश्वर lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=193-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलोत्कट|कुलोत्कटः
कुलोत्कट mfn. (-टः-टा-टं) High-born.<BR>	 m. (-टः) A horse of a good breed.<BR>E. कुल race, and उत्कट eminent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=193-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलोत्कर्ष
कुलोत्कर्ष m. (-र्षः) Family respectability.<BR> E. कुल and उत्कर्ष excellence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=193-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलोद्गत
कुलोद्गत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Of good family.<BR> E. कुल and उद्गत exalted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=193-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलोत्पन्न
कुलोत्पन्न mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>	 1. Of a good family, well-born.<BR>	 2. Family, be-<BR>longing to, inherited by, &c.<BR> E. कुल and उत्पन्न born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=193-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलोद्भव
कुलोद्भव mfn. (-वः-वा-वं)<BR>	 1. Well-born, of good family.<BR>	 2. Produced in a<BR>family.<BR> E. कुल and उद्भव birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=193-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलोद्भूत
कुलोद्भूत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Well-born, of family.<BR> E. कुल and उद्भूत born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=193-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलोद्वह|कुलोद्वहः
कुलोद्वह m. (-हः) A chief, a leader, the head of a family.<BR> E. कुल and उद्वह<BR>who upholds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=193-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुल्फ|कुल्फं|कुल्फः
कुल्फ mn. (-ल्फः-ल्फं) A disease.<BR>	 m. (-ल्फः) The ankle; also गुल्फ.<BR> E. कल्<BR>to count, फ Uṇādi affix, and उ inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=193-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुल्मल|कुल्मलं
कुल्मल n. (-लं) Sin.<BR> E. कुष् to extract, क्मलन् Uṇādi affix, and ष changed<BR>to ल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=193-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुल्माष|कुल्माषं|कुल्माषः
कुल्माष mn. (-षः-षं) Sour gruel prepared by the spontaneous fermenta-<BR>tion of the water of boiled rice.<BR>	 n. (-षं)<BR>	 1. Half ripe barley.<BR>	 2.<BR>Forced rice.<BR>	 3. A sort of Phaseolus: see राजमाष.<BR>	 4. A species of<BR>Dolichos, (D. beflorus.) See यावक.<BR>	 5. A disease.<BR>	 m. (-षः) A dish<BR>consisting of half boiled rice, with pulse, &c. commonly Khichri. E.<BR>कुल a class or race, मष् or मस् to hurt or kill, अण् affix; hence the<BR>word is also written कुल्मास.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=193-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुल्माषाभिमुत
कुल्माषाभिमुत n. (-तं) Sour gruel. See कुल्मास.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=193-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुल्मास|कुल्मासं
कुल्मास mn. (-सः-सं) See कुल्माष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=193-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुल्य|कुल्यं|कुल्यः
कुल्य mfn. (-ल्यः-ल्या-ल्यं)<BR>	 1. Of a good family, well-born, well descended.<BR>2. Of or relating to a family or race.<BR>	 m. (-ल्यः) A counsellor.<BR>	 f.<BR>(-ल्या)<BR>	 1. A river in general.<BR>	 2. A canal, a channel for irrigation.<BR>3. A ditch, a dyke or trench.<BR>	 4. A drug or medicinal plant, (Cel-<BR>tis orientalis:) see जीवन्ती.<BR>	 5. A chaste or virtuous woman, n. (-ल्यं)<BR>1. A bone.<BR>	 2. A measure of eight Dronas: see द्रोण 3. A win-<BR>nowing basket.<BR>	 4. Flesh.<BR>	 5. Friendly inquiry after family affairs or<BR>domestic accidents, condolence, congratulation, &c.<BR> E. कुल् to<BR>accumulate, and यत् affix, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=193-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुल्वक|कुल्वकं
कुल्वक n. (-कं) Fur upon the tongue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=193-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुव|कुवं
कुव n. (-वं) A water lily, a lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=193-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुवङ्ग|कुवंग|कुवङ्गं|कुवङ्गः
कुवङ्ग n. (-ङ्गं) Lead.<BR> E. कु bad वङ्ग tin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=193-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुवच|कुवचः
कुवच mfn. (-चः-चा-चं) Abusive, censorious, detracting.<BR> E. कु bad, वच् to<BR>speak, क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=193-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुवज्रक|कुवज्रकं
कुवज्रक n. (-कं) Crystal, a stone resembling a diamond.<BR> E. कु inferior,<BR>वज्र the diamond, कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=193-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुवद
कुवद mfn. (-दः-दा-दं) Censorious.<BR> E. कु bad, वद् to speak, क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=193-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुवर|कुवरः
कुवर m. (-रः) An astringent taste; see तुवर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=193-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुवल|कुवलं
कुवल mfn. (-लः-ली-लं)<BR>	 1. The jujube, the tree.<BR>	 2. The fruit.<BR>	 n. (-लं)<BR>	 1.<BR>A water lily.<BR>	 2. A pearl.<BR> E. कु the earth, and वल् to cover, affix<BR>अच् see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=193-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुवलय|कुवलयं
कुवलय n. (-यं)<BR>	 1. Any water lily.<BR>	 2. The blue lotus.<BR> E. कु the earth, वल<BR>to cover, and कयन् affix; also कुवल, and कुव.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=193-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुवलयिनी
कुवलयिनी f. (-नी) A place abounding in water lilies.<BR> E. कुवलय, and<BR>इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=193-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुवलाश्व|कुवलाश्वः
कुवलाश्व m. (-श्वः) A proper name of a king, also धुन्धुमार.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=193-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुवाद|कुवादः
कुवाद mfn. (-दः-दा-दं) Detracting, censorious.<BR> E. कु evil, वद् to speak,<BR>अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=193-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुबाहुल
कुबाहुल m. (-लः) A camel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=193-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुविन्द|कुविंद|कुविंदः|कुविन्दः
कुविन्द m. (-न्दः) A weaver.<BR> E. कुप् to spread, किन्दच् Uṇādi affix, and प<BR>changed to व; also कुपिन्द.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=193-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुविवाह|कुविवाहः
कुविवाह m. (-हः) A degrading or improper marriage.<BR> E. कु bad, and<BR>विवाह marriage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=193-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुवृत्तिकृत्
कुवृत्तिकृत् m. (-कृत्) A plant, (Cæsalpinia ponduccella:) see पूतिक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=193-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुवेणी
कुवेणी f. (-णी)<BR>	 1. A fish basket.<BR>	 2. An ill braided tress of hair.<BR>	 3. A<BR>woman with her hair ill braided.<BR> E. कु bad, बेण् to go, घञ् affix and<BR>ङीष् fem. affix; also with टाप् or इन् affixed, कुवेणा and कुवेणि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=193-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुवेर|कुवेरः
कुवेर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>	 1. Deformed, monstrous.<BR>	 2. Slow, lazy m. (-रः)<BR>KUVERA the son of VISRAVAS by IRAVIRA, the chief of the Yakṣas,<BR>god of wealth and regent of the north.<BR> E. कु vile, and वेर body,<BR>alluding to the deformity of the god. who is represented as having<BR>three legs and but eight teeth.<BR>	 2. The Tun tree: see नन्दिवृक्ष 3. One<BR>of the attendants of a Jaina saint. E. As above, or कुवि to cover,<BR>&c. and एरच् Uṇādi affix; in this case the word may be read कुबेर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=193-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुवेरक|कुवेरकः
कुवेरक m. (-कः) The Tun tree, (Cedrala tunna.)<BR> E. कन् added to the<BR>preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=193-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुवेराक्षी
कुवेराक्षी f. (-क्षी) The trumpet flower, (Bignonia suave olens.)<BR> E. कुवेर,<BR>and अक्षि the eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=193-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुवेराचल|कुवेराचलः
कुवेराचल m. (-लः) Mount Kailasa.<BR> E. कुवेर and अचल a mountain; the<BR>capital of KUVERA, being situated in Kailasa, which is supposed to<BR>be in the Himālaya range.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=193-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुवेराद्रि|कुवेराद्रिः
कुवेराद्रि m. (-द्रिः) See the preceding. E. As above, अद्रि being a mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=193-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुवेल|कुवेलं
कुवेल n. (-लं) Any water lily.<BR> E. कु the earth, वेल् to shake, अच् affix:<BR>see कुवलय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=193-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुव्र
कुव्र n. (-व्रं) A forest or wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=193-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुश|कुशं|कुशः
कुश(इर)कुशिर r. 4th cl. (कुश्यति)<BR>	 1. To embrace, to enfold.<BR>	 2. To take<BR>out or from. (इ)कुशि r. 1st and 10th cls. (कुंशति कुंशयति) To shine:<BR>see कुस.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=193-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुश|कुशं|कुशः
कुश mfn. (-शः-शा-शं)<BR>	 1. Wicked, deprave.<BR>	 2. Mad, inebriate.<BR>	 mn. (-शः-शं)<BR>A species of grass used in many solemn and religious observances,<BR>hence called sacrificial grass, (Poa cynosuroides.)<BR>	 m. (-शः)<BR>	 1. The<BR>yoke of a plough.<BR>	 2. A proper name, one of the sons of RAMA.<BR>	 3.<BR>One of the great Dwipas or divisions of the universe, surrounded<BR>by the sea of spirituous liquor.<BR>	 f. (-शा)<BR>	 1. A rope.<BR>	 2. A plant, com-<BR>monly Maukatha.<BR>	 n. (-शं) Water.<BR>	 f. (-शी)<BR>	 1. A ploughshare.<BR>	 2.<BR>Wrought iron.<BR>	 mf. (-शः-शी) A bridle, a horse's head rope.<BR> E. कु the<BR>earth. शीञ् to sleep or rest, and ड affix, or कु bad, and शी to des-<BR>troy, again कुश् to embrace or enfold, and क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=193-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुशनामन्
कुशनामन् m. (-मा) A camel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=193-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुशय|कुशयः
कुशय m. (-यः) A drinking vessel, a cup, a goblet.<BR> E. कुश् to extract,<BR>and अय Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=194-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुशपुष्प|कुशपुष्पं
कुशपुष्प n. (-ष्पं) A perfume, commonly Ganthiala.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=194-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुशल|कुशलं|कुशलः
कुशल mfn. (-लः-ला or -ली-लं)<BR>	 1. Happy, well, right.<BR>	 2. Expert, skilful.<BR>3. Clever.<BR>	 4. Eloquent.<BR>	 n. (-लं)<BR>	 1. Adequacy, ability.<BR>	 2. Virtue,<BR>virtuous action.<BR>	 3. Well-being, happiness.<BR> E. कु the earth. and शल्<BR>to go, affix अच्; also कुषल and कुसल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=194-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुशलता
कुशलता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Cleverness, ability.<BR>	 2. Eloquence.<BR>	 3. Well-being. E.<BR>तल् added to the last; also with त्व, कुशलत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=194-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुशलप्रश्न|कुशलप्रश्नः
कुशलप्रश्न m. (-श्नः) Salutation, greeting, friendly inquiry respecting a<BR>person's health or welfare.<BR> E. कुशल well-being, and प्रश्न asking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=194-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुशलव
कुशलव du.<BR>	 m. (-वौ) The two sons of RAMA or KUSA, and LAVA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=194-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुशलबुद्धि
कुशलबुद्धि mfn. (-द्धिः-द्धिः-द्धि)<BR>	 1. Wise, able, intelligent.<BR> E. कुशल and बुद्धि<BR>understanding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=194-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुशलिन्
कुशलिन् mfn. (-ली-लिनी-लि)<BR>	 1. Auspicious, favourable.<BR>	 2. Virtuous,<BR>good.<BR>	 3. Happy, prosperous.<BR>	 4. Clever.<BR> E. कुशल, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=194-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुशवारि
कुशवारि n. (-रिः) Water in which Kusa grass has been boiled.<BR> E. कुश,<BR>and वारि water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=194-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुशस्तव
कुशस्तव m. (-वः) A bundle of Kusa grass.<BR> E. कुश, and स्तव a cluster.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=194-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुशस्थल|कुशस्थलं
कुशस्थल nf. (-लं-ली) The country of Kanyakubja or Kanouj.<BR>	 f. (-ली) The<BR>residence of KṚṢṆA: see द्वारका.<BR>	 2. A name of Oujein or Avanti<BR>during the Treta Yug or second age.<BR> E. कुश sacred grass, and स्थल<BR>place; abounding in Kusa grass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=194-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुशाकर|कुशाकरः
कुशाकर m. (-रः) Fire.<BR> E. कुश the grass, &c. आकर a mine; the sacrifi-<BR>cial fire being made upon a tuft of this grass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=194-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुशाक्ष|कुशाक्षः
कुशाक्ष m. (-क्षः) A monkey, an ape.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=194-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुशाग्र
कुशाग्र mfn. (-ग्रः-ग्रा-ग्रं) Sharp, shrewd, intelligent.<BR>	 n. (-ग्रं) The sharp<BR>point of the Kusa grass.<BR> E. कुश, and अग्र point.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=194-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुशाग्रबुद्धि
कुशाग्रबुद्धि mfn. (-द्धिः-द्धिः-द्धि) Sharp, shrewd, intelligent.<BR>	 f. (-द्धिः) Shrewd-<BR>ness, subtlety.<BR> E. कुशाग्र, and बुद्धि understanding; also similar com-<BR>pounds, कुशाग्रधी, कुशाग्रीयमति, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=194-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुशाग्रीय
कुशाग्रीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Subtile, penetrating: see the next.<BR> E. कुश the<BR>grass, अग्र point, छ affix; implying resemblance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=194-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुशाग्रीयमति|कुशाग्रीयमतिः
कुशाग्रीयमति mfn. (-तिः-तिः-ति) Inspecting minutely, subtile, sharp sight-<BR>ed, intelligent, possessing mental acumen.<BR> E. कुश the grass,<BR>अग्रीय point, and मति mind; also other similar compounds, as<BR>कुशाग्रीयधी, कुशाग्रीयबुद्धि, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=194-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुशाङ्गुरीय|कुशांगुरीय
कुशाङ्गुरीय n. (-यं) A ring of Kusa grass, worn at religious ceremonies. E.<BR>कुश, and अङ्गुरीय a ring; also कुशाङ्गुरीयकं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=194-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुशाल्मलि|कुशाल्मलिः
कुशाल्मलि m. (-लिः) A tree, (Andersonia rohitaka.)<BR> E. कु and शाल्मलि silk-cotton tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=194-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुशारणि|कुशारणिः
कुशारणि m. (-णिः) The name of a sage celebrated for his irascibility:<BR>see दुर्व्वासा.<BR> E. कुश the grass, and अरणि wood whose attrition pro-<BR>duces fire; using Kusa for this purpose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=194-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुशासन
कुशासन n. (-नं) A seat of Kusa grass.<BR> E. कुश, and आसन a seat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=194-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुशिंशपा
कुशिंशपा f. (-पा) A kind of Sisu tree, (Dalbergia Sisu.)<BR> E. कु inferior, and<BR>शिंशपा the Sisu tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=194-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुशिक|कुशिकः
कुशिक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Squint-eyed.<BR>	 m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A Muni or divine sage<BR>so named, the father of JAMADAGNI.<BR>	 2. A ploughshare.<BR>	 3. The Sal<BR>tree, (Shorea robusta.)<BR>	 4. Beleric myrobalan: see विभीतक.<BR>	 5. The<BR>sediment of oil.<BR> E. कुश the grass, &c. इकन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=194-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुशित|कुशितं
कुशित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Mixed, combined with water, &c.<BR> E. कुश् or कुष to<BR>embrace, to mix, and इतच् Uṇādi affix; hence also कुषित.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=194-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुशिन्
कुशिन् m. (-शी) A name of VALMIKI, the author of the Rāmāyaṇa.<BR> E. कुश<BR>the son of RAMA, affix इनि; the poem is supposed to be recited by<BR>KUSA, and LAVA, the sons of the hero.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=194-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुशीद|कुशीदं
कुशीद n. (-दं)<BR>	 1. The profession of usury.<BR>	 2. Red saunders: see कुसीद.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=194-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुशील
कुशील mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>	 1. Ill-behaved, rude, wicked.<BR>	 2. Evil disposed,<BR>ill-tempered.<BR> E. कु and शील temper, conduct.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=194-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुशीलता
कुशीलता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Misbehaviour, misconduct.<BR>	 2. Bad disposition, ill-<BR>temper.<BR> E. तल् added to the preceding; also with त्व, कुशीलत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=194-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुशीलव|कुशीलवः
कुशीलव m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. An actor, a dancer, a mime.<BR>	 2. A bard, a herald.<BR>	 3.<BR>A newsmonger.<BR> E. कु bad, शील practice, and व affix, from वा to<BR>go, &c. with क affix, du.<BR>	 m. (वौ) The two sons of RAMA: see<BR>कुशलव.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=194-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुशीवश|कुशीवशः
कुशीवश m. (-शः) A name of VALMIKI: see कुशिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=194-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुशूल|कुशूलः
कुशूल m. (-लः) A granary, a cupboard, a place in which rice or other<BR>grain is kept.<BR>	 2. Conflagration of chaff.<BR> E. कुश् to enfold, कुल affix;<BR>also कुसूल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=194-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुशूलधान्य
कुशूलधान्य m. (-न्यः) Grain stored for three year's consumption.<BR> E. कुशूल,<BR>and धान्य grain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=194-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुशूलधान्यक|कुशूलधान्यकः
कुशूलधान्यक m. (-कः) A householder, &c. who has three year's grain in<BR>store.<BR> E. कुशूलधान्य, and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=194-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुशेशय|कुशेशयं|कुशेशयः
कुशेशय n. (-यं) A lotus in general.<BR>	 m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. A tree, commonly Kani-<BR>yar: see कर्णिकार.<BR>	 2. The Indian crane.<BR> E. कुश water, in the seventh<BR>case, शीञ् to sleep or rest, with the affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=194-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुशेशयकर
कुशेशयकर m. (-रः) The sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=194-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुशोत्तर
कुशोत्तर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Having, or being covered with grass.<BR> E. कुश<BR>and उत्तर beyond.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=194-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुशोदक
कुशोदक n. (-कं) Water in which Kusa grass has been infused.<BR> E. कुश,<BR>and उदक water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=194-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुष
कुष r. 9th cl. (कुष्णाति)<BR>	 1. To expel, to force or draw out, to extract.<BR>	 2.<BR>To test, to assay.<BR>	 3. To shine. With अव to prove, to display; with<BR>निर to extract.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=194-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुषल|कुषलः
कुषल mfn. (-लः-ला or -ली-लं) Clever, expert, skilful: see कुशल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=194-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुषाकु|कुषाकुः
कुषाकु mfn. (-कुः-कुः-कु)<BR>	 1. Burning, scorching, inflaming.<BR>	 2. Wicked,<BR>detestable.<BR>	 m. (-कुः)<BR>	 1. A monkey.<BR>	 2. The sun.<BR>	 3. Fire.<BR> E. कुष् to<BR>shine, काकु Uṇādi affix; also कषाकु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=194-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुषित्
कुषित् ind. Execllently.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=194-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुषित|कुषितः
कुषित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Mixed with water, &c. see कुशित.<BR>	 n. (-तं) Happy,<BR>well, right, fortunate, auspicious, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=194-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुषीद|कुषीदं
कुषीद mfn. (-दः-दा-दं) Indifferent, apathetic, inert.<BR>	 n. (-दं) Usury: see<BR>कुसीद<BR> E. कु vile, षद् to move, &c, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=194-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुष्ठ|कुष्ठं|कुष्ठः
कुष्ठ n. (-ष्ठं)<BR>	 1. Leprosy, of which eighteen varieties are enumerated,<BR>seven great or severe, and eleven of minor importance.<BR>	 2. A plant,<BR>a kind of costus, (Costus speciosus:)<BR>	 3. A sort of poison.<BR> E. कुष्<BR>to extract, and क्थम् Uṇādi affix, or कु bad, ill and स्थ being,<BR>staying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=194-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुष्ठघ्न|कुष्ठघ्नः
कुष्ठघ्न m. (-घ्नः) A medicinal plant, commonly Hiyavali: see हितावली.<BR>	 f.<BR>(-घ्नी)<BR>	 1. An esculent root, (Solanum Indicum:) see काकमाची 2.<BR>Opposite leaved fig tree; also काकोडुम्बरिका.<BR> E. कुष्ठ the leprosy,<BR>and घ्न what destroys.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=194-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुष्ठनाशन|कुष्ठनाशनः
कुष्ठनाशन m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. White mustard.<BR>	 2. A sort of yam: see वाराही.<BR> E. कुष्ठ<BR>the leprosy, and नाशन what destroys.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=194-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुष्ठनाशिनी
कुष्ठनाशिनी f. (-नी) A plant, commonly Hakucha, (Psoralia corylifolia.)<BR>E. As above: see कुष्ठनाशन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=194-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुष्ठल|कुष्ठलं
कुष्ठल n. (-लं)<BR>	 1. A bad place or spot.<BR>	 2. The surface of the earth.<BR> E. कु<BR>bad or the earth, and स्थल place; स becomes ष, and थ is then<BR>changed to ठ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=194-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुष्ठसूदन|कुष्ठसूदनः
कुष्ठसूदन m. (-नः) The cassia tree, (C. fistula.)<BR> E. कुष्ठ and सूदन des-<BR>troying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=194-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुष्ठहृत्
कुष्ठहृत् m. (-हृत्) Catechu, (Mimosa catechu:) see खदिर.<BR> E. कुष्ठ leprosy,<BR>and हृत् what takes away, from हृ to convey, affix क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=194-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुष्ठहन्तृ
कुष्ठहन्तृ m. (-न्ता) A large esculent root, described as possessed of<BR>medicinal virtue in leprosy, and other cutaneous affections,<BR>(Arum campanulatum:) see हस्तिकन्द.<BR> E. कुष्ठ leprosy, and हन्तृ what<BR>kills or destroys.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=194-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुष्ठारि|कुष्ठारिः
कुष्ठारि m. (-रिः)<BR>	 1. A fetid mimosa, (M. Farnesiana.)<BR>	 2. The Khayar or<BR>Catechu: (M. catechu.)<BR>	 3. A kind of Aristolochia: see अर्कपत्र.<BR>	 4.<BR>A sort of gourd, (Trichosanthes diœca.)<BR>	 5. Sulphur.<BR> E. कुष्ठ the<BR>leprosy, and अरि an enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=194-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुष्ठिन्
कुष्ठिन् mfn. (-ष्ठी-ष्ठिनी-ष्ठि) Leprous, a leper, &c.<BR> E. कुष्ठ and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=195-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुष्मल|कुष्मलं
कुष्मल n. (-लं) Cutting, dividing.<BR> E. कुष् to extract, and क्मलन् Uṇādi<BR>aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=195-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुष्माण्ड|कुष्मांड|कुष्मांडः|कुष्माण्डः
कुष्माण्ड mf. (-ण्डः-ण्डा or -ण्डी) A pumpkin gourd, (Cucurbita pepo.)<BR>	 m.<BR>(-ण्डः)<BR>	 1. One of a class of demigods attached to ŚIVA.<BR>	 2. State of<BR>the womb in gestation.<BR>	 f. (-ण्डी)<BR>	 1. A name of DURGĀ.<BR>	 2. A drug.<BR>A religious ceremony, a certain rite performed as a penance or<BR>expiation; also कुष्माण्डक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=195-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुष्माण्डक|कुष्मांडक|कुष्मांडकः|कुष्माण्डकः
कुष्माण्डक m. (-कः) A pumpkin gourd, (Cucurbita pepo.)<BR> E. कु the earth,<BR>उष्म heat, अन् to exist or be, ड affix, and the vowel irregularly<BR>short, कन् added; also कुष्माण्ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=195-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुस
कुस(इर)कुसिर r. 4th cl. (कुस्यति) To embrace. (इ) कुसि r. 1st and 10th<BR>cls. (कुंसति, कुंसयति)<BR>	 1. To shine.<BR>	 2. To talk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=195-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुसरित्
कुसरित् f. (-रित्) A shallow stream.<BR> E. कु bad, सरित् A river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=195-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुसल|कुसलं
कुसल adv.<BR>	 n. (-लं) Well, happy, &c. see कुशल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=195-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुसित|कुसितः
कुसित m. (-तः) An inhabited country.<BR> E. कुस् to shine, and इत Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=195-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुसीतायी
कुसीतायी f. (-यी) The wife of a money-lender. See कुसीदायी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=195-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुसीद|कुसीदं|कुसीदः
कुसीद n. (-दं)<BR>	 1. Usury, the profession of usury.<BR>	 2. Any loan of thing<BR>lent to be repaid with interest.<BR>	 mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>	 1. A money lender.<BR>2. Slothful, inert.<BR> E. कुस् to embrace, ईद Uṇādi affix; or कु bad,<BR>and षद् to go, affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=195-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुसीदपथ|कुसीदपथः
कुसीदपथ m. (-थः) Usury, usurous interest, any exceeding five per<BR>cent.<BR> E. कुसीद and पथ for पथिन् road.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=195-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुसीदवृद्धि|कुसीदवृद्धिः
कुसीदवृद्धि f. (-द्धिः) Interest on money.<BR> E. कुसीद and वृद्धि increase.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=195-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुसीदायी
कुसीदायी f. (-यी) The wife of a usurer.<BR> E. कूसीद A usurer, ऐ substituted<BR>for its final, and, ङीष् affix; also कुसीतायी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=195-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुसीदिक|कुसीदिकः
कुसीदिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) One who follows the profession of usury. E.<BR>कुसीद usury, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=195-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुसुम|कुसुमं|कुसुमः
कुसुम n. (-मं)<BR>	 1. A flower in general.<BR>	 2. Fruit.<BR>	 3. The menstrual dis-<BR>charge.<BR>	 4. Ophthalmia, disease of the eyes.<BR> E. कुस् to shine, उम<BR>Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=195-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुसुमकार्म्मुक|कुसुमकार्मुक|कुसुमकार्मुकः
कुसुमकार्म्मुक m. (-कः) KĀMA^1.<BR> E. कुसुम and कार्म्मुक a bow.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20260617. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/264.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=195-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुसुमचित
कुसुमचित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Heaped with flowers.<BR> E. कुसुम, and चित<BR>gathered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=195-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुसुमपुर|कुसुमपुरं
कुसुमपुर n. (-रं) A city, the vicinity of the modern Patna: see पाटलिपुत्र.<BR>E. कुसुम a flower, and पुर a city.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=195-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुसुममध्य|कुसुममध्यं
कुसुममध्य n. (-ध्यं) The name of tree, bearing a large acid fruit, (Dilenia<BR>Indica.)<BR> E. कुसुम a flower, and मध्य the centre; the flower blosso-<BR>ming from the fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=195-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुसुमयत्
कुसुमयत् mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्) Producing flowers, causing to flower. E.<BR>कुसुम nom. verb, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=195-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुसुमवत्|कुसुमवन्त्
कुसुमवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) In flower, flowering.<BR>	 f. (-ती)<BR>	 1. A female<BR>during menstruation.<BR>	 2. A town: see कुसुमपुर.<BR> E. कुसुम and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=195-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुसुमस्तवक|कुसुमस्तवकः
कुसुमस्तवक m. (-कः) A collection of flowers, a garland, nosegay a bouquet,<BR>E. कुसुम, and स्तवक a cluster.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=195-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुसुमाकर|कुसुमाकरः
कुसुमाकर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Spring, the vernal season.<BR>	 2. A quantity of flowers<BR>or place abounding with them, a parterre, a garden.<BR> E. कुसुम, and<BR>आकर a mine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=195-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुसुमाञ्जन|कुसुमांजन|कुसुमाञ्जनं
कुसुमाञ्जन m. (-नं) The calx of brass, used as a collyrium.<BR> E. कुसुम a flow-<BR>er, and अञ्जन application to the eyes; resembling a flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=195-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुसुमात्मक|कुसुमात्मकं
कुसुमात्मक n. (-कं) Saffron.<BR> E. कुसुम, and आत्मक self; the essential part of<BR>the flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=195-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुमुमाधिप
कुमुमाधिप m. (-पः) The champa, a tree which bears a yellow fragrant<BR>flower, (Michelia champaca.)<BR> E. कुसुम a flower, and अधिप a king;<BR>royal amongst flowers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=195-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुसुमाधिराज्
कुसुमाधिराज् m. (-राट्) See the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=195-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुसुमायुध|कुसुमायुधः
कुसुमायुध m. (-धः) A name of KĀMADEVA.<BR> E. कुसुम a flower, and आयुध a<BR>weapon: his shafts being tipped with flowers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=195-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुसुमाल|कुसुमालः
कुसुमाल m. (-लः) A thief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=195-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुसुमावचाय|कुसुमावचायः
कुसुमावचाय m. (-यः) Gathering flowers.<BR> E. कुसुम, and अवचाय gathering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=195-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुसुमावतंसक
कुसुमावतंसक n. (-कं) A chaplet, a crown of flowers.<BR> E. कुसुम, and अवतंसक<BR>a tiara.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=195-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुसुमासव|कुसुमासवं
कुसुमासव n. (-वं) Honey.<BR> E. कुसुम, and आसव spirit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=195-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुसुमित
कुसुमित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Flowered, budded, in flower.<BR> E. कुसुम, and इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=195-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुसुमितलता
कुसुमितलता f. (-ता) A species of the Dhriti metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=195-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुसुमेषु|कुसुमेषुः
कुसुमेषु m. (-षुः) A name of the god KĀMA^1.<BR>	 n. (-षु) The bow of KĀMA^2. E.<BR>कुसुम, and इषु an arrow; whose shafts are flowers.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20260617. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/264.<BR>[2] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20260617. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/264.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=195-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुसुम्भ|कुसुंभ|कुसुंभं|कुसुम्भं|कुसुंभः|कुसुम्भः
कुसुम्भ n. (-म्भं)<BR>	 1. Safflower, (Carthamus tinctorius.)<BR>	 2. Gold.<BR>	 m. (-म्भः)<BR>The water pot of the student and Sanyasi.<BR> E. कुस् to shine, and उम्भ<BR>Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=195-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुसू
कुसू m. (-सूः) An earth-worm.<BR> E. कु the earth, सू produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=195-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुसूल|कुसूलः
कुसूल m. (-लः) A granary, &c. see कुशूल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=195-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुसृति|कुसृतिः
कुसृति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Wickedness, depravity.<BR>	 2. Conjuring, slight of hand,<BR>&c.<BR> E. कु vile, सृ to go, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=195-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुस्तुभ|कुस्तुभः
कुस्तुभ m. (-भः)<BR>	 1. A name of VIṢṆU.<BR>	 2. The ocean<BR> E. कु the earth, ष्टुभ<BR>to stop, क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=195-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुस्तुम्बरी
कुस्तुम्बरी f. (-री) A pungent seed used in condiments, coriander: see the<BR>next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=195-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुस्तुम्बुरु|कुस्तुम्बुरुः
कुस्तुम्बुरु f. (-रुः) Coriander, a pungent seed.<BR> E. कु bad, vile, तुवि to take,<BR>उरु affix, deriv. irr.; also कुस्तुम्बरी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=195-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुस्वप्न
कुस्वप्न m. (-प्नः) A bad dream, nightmare.<BR> E. कु, and स्वप्न a vision.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=195-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुस्म
कुस्म r. 10th cl. (कुस्मयति)<BR>	 1. To smile improperly or blamably.<BR>	 2. To see<BR>mentally, to perceive, to imagine: this is considered by some as<BR>a denominative, and to be classed improperly amongst the roots.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=195-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुह|कुहः
कुह r. 10th cl, (कुहयते)<BR>	 1. To surprise, to astonish, to excite wonder.<BR>	 2.<BR>To cheat, to impose upon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=195-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुह|कुहः
कुह m. (-हः) A name of KUVERA, f. (-हा) A medicinal drug: see कटुकी<BR>ind. Where, whither, used in Vedas in place of कुत्र.<BR> E. कु vile, and<BR>हा to leave, affix ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=195-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुहक|कुहकं|कुहकः
कुहक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) A cheat, a rogue, a juggler.<BR>	 m. (-कः) Juggling,<BR>deception, slight-of-hand, &c.<BR> E. कुह् to astonish, क्वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=195-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुहककार
कुहककार mfn. (-रः-री-रं) Juggling, conjuring, cheating.<BR> E. कुहक, and<BR>कार who makes; also कुहककारक and कुहककारिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=195-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुहकचकित
कुहकचकित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Suspicious, cautious, wary.<BR> E. कुहक and<BR>चकित fearful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=195-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुहकजीविन्
कुहकजीविन् mfn. (-वी-विनी-वि) Living by slight-of-hand. a conjuror, a<BR>cheat, &c.<BR> E. कुहक deception, and जीविन् who lives by.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=195-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुहकवृत्ति|कुहकवृत्तिः
कुहकवृत्ति f. (-त्तिः)<BR>	 1. Juggling, conjuring, slight-of-hand.<BR>	 2. Hypocrisy.<BR>E. कुहक, and वृत्ति practice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=195-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुहकस्वन|कुहकस्वनः
कुहकस्वन m. (-नः) A wild cock.<BR> E. कुहक deception, and स्वन who sounds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=195-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुहकस्वर|कुहकस्वरः
कुहकस्वर m. (-रः) A wild cock: see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=195-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुहन|कुहनं|कुहनः
कुहन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>	 1. Envious.<BR>	 2. Hypocritical.<BR>	 m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. A rat.<BR>	 2.<BR>A snake.<BR>	 f. (-ना) Hypocrisy, assumed and false sanctity, the inter-<BR>ested performance of religious austerities.<BR>	 n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. A small earth-<BR>en vessel.<BR>	 2. A glass vessel.<BR> E. कुह् to surprise, युच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=195-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुहनिका
कुहनिका f. (-का) Hypocrisy: see the preceding.<BR> E. कुहन, and इकन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=195-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुहर|कुहरं|कुहरः
कुहर n. (-रं)<BR>	 1. A cavity, a hollow.<BR>	 2. A hole, a rent, &c.<BR>	 3. The ear.<BR>4. A guttural sound.<BR>	 5. The throat or larynx.<BR>	 m. (-रः) A kind of<BR>snake.<BR> E. कु the earth, &c. and हर what takes, &c. from हृ with the<BR>aff अप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=195-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुहरित|कुहरितं
कुहरित n. (-तं)<BR>	 1. The song, or cry of the Kokila, or the Indian cuckoo.<BR>2. Vox congressus in coitu.<BR>	 3. A sound in general.<BR> E. कुहर, and<BR>इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=195-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुहलि|कुहलिः
कुहलि m. (-लिः) A Pan the leaf of the Piper betel, with small pieces<BR>of the Areca nut, and Catechu and a little lime, which are chewed<BR>and eaten by the Oriental nations.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=195-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुहु|कुहुः
कुहु f. (-हुः) See the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=195-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुहू
कुहू f. (-हूः)<BR>	 1. New moon; the first day of the first quarter on which<BR>the moon rises invisible.<BR>	 2. The cry of the Kokila or Indian cuckoo.<BR>E. कूह् to astonish, ऊ affix, or with कु affix कुहु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=195-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुहूक
कुहूक m. (-कः) The Indian cuckoo.<BR> E. कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=196-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुहूकण्ठ|कुहूकंठ|कुहूकण्ठः
कुहूकण्ठ m. (-ण्ठः) The Kokila or Indian cuckoo.<BR> E. कुहू the Kokila's<BR>cry, and कण्ठ the throat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=196-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुहूपाल
कुहूपाल m. (-लः) The king of turtles, the tortoise supposed to uphold<BR>the world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=196-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुहूमुख|कुहूमुखः
कुहूमुख m. (-खः) The Kokila: see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=196-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुहूरव|कुहूरवः
कुहूरव m. (-वः) The Kokila.<BR> E. कुहू, and रव sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=196-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुहूल|कुहूलं
कुहूल n. (-लं) A pit, filled with stakes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=196-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुहेडिका
कुहेडिका f. (-का) A fog, a mist, haze, haziness.<BR> E. कु the earth, हेड्. to<BR>surround, वुन् affix; also कुहेलिक and कुहेडी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=196-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुहेडी
कुहेडी f. (-डी) See the preceding: also कुहेली.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=196-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुहेलिका
कुहेलिका f. (-का) Fog, mist: see कुहेडिका ल being changed to ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=196-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कू
कू r. 6th cl. (ङ) कूङ् (कुवते) To sound, especially as if in pain, to<BR>moan, to groan, &c. (ञ) कूञ r. 9th cl. (कुनाति-नीते) To sound &c.<BR>As before.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=196-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कू
कू f. (-कूः) A female Pisacha or goblin.<BR> E. कू to sound, क्विप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=196-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूकुद|कूकुदः
कूकुद mfn. (-दः-दा-दं) One who gives a girl in marriage with due cere-<BR>mony, and suitable decorations.<BR> E. कुक् to take, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=196-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूच|कूचः
कूच m. (-चः) A breast, A female breast, especially that of a young or<BR>unmarried woman: see कुच.<BR>	 f. (-ची) A painting brush or pencil. E.<BR>कू to sound, चट् Uṇādi affix, and the vowel made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=196-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूचिका
कूचिका f. (-का) A small brush or hair pencil.<BR> E. कुच् to be curved, and<BR>क्वुन् affix, with the fem. affix टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=196-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूज|कूजः
कूज r. 1st cl. (कूजति) To make any inarticulate sound, to utter a cry<BR>as a bird, to coo as a pigeon, to caw as a crow, &c. With परि<BR>prefixed, to moan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=196-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूजत्
कूजत् mfn. (-जन्-जन्ती-जत्) Cooing.<BR> E. कूज् to coo, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=196-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूजन|कूजनं
कूजन n. (-नं) Cooing, moaning, uttering an inarticulate sound.<BR> E. कूज् and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=196-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूजित|कूजितं
कूजित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Cooed, uttered inarticulately.<BR>	 n. (-तं) The cry of<BR>a bird, cooing.<BR> E. कूज् to sound, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=196-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूट|कूटः
कूट r. 10th cl. (कूटयते)<BR>	 1. To avoid or decline giving, to not give.<BR>	 2. To<BR>render indistinct or unintelligible, to muddle or render confused or<BR>foul. (कूटयति)<BR>	 1. To give pain.<BR>	 2. To burn.<BR>	 3. To call or invite, to<BR>counsel or advise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=196-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूट|कूटः
कूट mf. (-टः-टी) A house, a dwelling: see कुट mn. (-टः-टं)<BR>	 1. The peak or<BR>summit of a mountain.<BR>	 2. A water-jar.<BR>	 3. A heap of grain, &c.<BR>	 4.<BR>Uniform and elementary substance.<BR>	 5. A hammer, a mallet.<BR>	 6. A<BR>plough-share.<BR>	 7. The body of a plough.<BR>	 8. A trap for catching deer.<BR>9. A concealed weapon, as a dagger in a wooden case, a sword-<BR>cane, &c.<BR>	 10. Illusion.<BR>	 11. Fraud, trick, deceit, 12. Untruth,<BR>Falsehood (or attributively,) false, untrue.<BR>	 13. Vile, low.<BR>	 14. An ox<BR>whose horns are broken.<BR>	 m. (-टः) The name of a saint, also named<BR>AGASTYA.<BR> E. कूट् to confuse, to withhold, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=196-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूटक|कूटकं|कूटकः
कूटक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Unfair, fraudulent.<BR>	 n. (-कः) A ploughshare.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-कः)<BR>	 1. A braid or tress of hair.<BR>	 2. A perfume: see मुरा.<BR> E. कूट् to<BR>cut, and क्वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=196-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूटकार|कूटकारः
कूटकार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A rogue.<BR>	 2. A cheat, a false witness.<BR> E. कूट, and कार<BR>who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=196-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूटकारक|कूटकारकः
कूटकारक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A false witness.<BR>	 2. A rogue, a cheat.<BR> E. कूट, and<BR>कारक who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=196-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूटकृत्
कूटकृत् mfn. (-कृत्) Fraudulent, dishonest.<BR>	 m. (-कृत्)<BR>	 1. A name of ŚIVA.<BR>2. A Kāyastha or man of the writer caste.<BR> E. कूट illusion, &c. and<BR>कृत् who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=196-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूटज|कूटजः
कूटज m. (-जः) A medicinal plant: see कुटज.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=196-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूटता
कूटता f. (-ता) falsehood, fraud.<BR> E. तल् added to कुट; also with त्व,<BR>कुटत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=196-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूटपर्व्व|कूटपर्व|कूटपर्वः
कूटपर्व्व m. (-र्व्वः) Fever occurring in an elephant from vitiation of the<BR>three humors; also read कूटपूर्ब्ब.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=196-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूटपाकल|कूटपाकलः
कूटपाकल m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. A bilious fever in an elephant.<BR>	 2. A potter's kiln.<BR>E. कूट a heap, and पाक what ripens, लच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=196-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूटयन्त्र|कूटयंत्र|कूटयन्त्रं
कूटयन्त्र n. (-न्त्रं) A trap or snare for deer, birds, &c.<BR> E. कूट a trap, and<BR>यन्त्र an implement; also simply कूट.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=196-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूटशाल्मलि|कूटशाल्मलिः
कूटशाल्मलि m. (-लिः) A species of the Simul silk-cotton tree.<BR> E. कूट false<BR>and शाल्मलि the Simul.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=196-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूटशासन
कूटशासन n. (-नं) A forged or false grant or decree.<BR> E. कूट, and शासन a<BR>grant, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=196-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूटसाक्षिन्
कूटसाक्षिन् m. (-ची) A false witness.<BR> E. कूट falsehood, and साक्षिन् a<BR>witness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=196-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूटस्थ|कूटस्थं|कूटस्थः
कूटस्थ mfn. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थं) Uniform, perpetually and universally the same<BR>as spirit, elementary matter, æther &c.<BR>	 n. (-स्थं)<BR>	 1. The soul 2. A<BR>sort of perfume, a species of dried shell fish, commonly Nakhi. E.<BR>कूट fixed, and स्थ what remains.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=196-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूटस्वर्ण
कूटस्वर्ण n. (-र्णं) Alloyed or counterfeit gold.<BR> E. कूट, and स्वर्ण gold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=196-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूटाक्ष|कूटाक्षः
कूटाक्ष m. (-क्षः) Loaded or false dice.<BR> E. कूट. and अक्ष a die.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=196-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूटागार|कूटागारं
कूटागार n. (-रं) An upper room, an apartment on the top of a house. E.<BR>कूट a peak, आगार a house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=196-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूटार्थभाषिता
कूटार्थभाषिता f. (-ता) A tale, a story, a fiction.<BR> E. कूट false, अर्थ meaning,<BR>and भाषिता spoken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=196-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूड
कूड r. 6th cl. (कूडति)<BR>	 1. To be or become firm or solid.<BR>	 2. To eat.<BR>	 3. To<BR>graze.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=196-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूड्य|कूड्यं
कूड्य n. (-ड्यं) A wall: see कुड्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=196-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूण
कूण r. 10th cl. (कूणयते-ति) To contract or close.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=196-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूणि|कूणिः
कूणि mfn. (-णिः-णिः-णि) Crooked-armed, having a curved or withered<BR>arm: see कुणि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=196-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूणिका
कूणिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. The horn of any animal.<BR>	 2. The peg of a lute.<BR> E. कूण्<BR>to sound or to be crooked, वुन् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=196-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूणित
कूणित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Contracted, shut, closed.<BR> E. कूण् to contract,<BR>affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=196-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूदर|कूदरः
कूदर m. (-रः) The offspring of a Brahman woman by a Ṛṣi, begotten<BR>during menstruation.<BR> E. कु bad, उदर belly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=196-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूद्दाल|कूद्दालः
कूद्दाल m. (-लः) Mountain ebony: see कुद्दाल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=196-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कून
कून r. 10th cl. (कूनयति) To contract or close.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=196-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूप|कूपः
कूप r. 10th cl. (कूपयति)<BR>	 1. To be weak.<BR>	 2. To weaken: see कुप.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=196-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूप|कूपः
कूप m. (-पः)<BR>	 1. A well.<BR>	 2. A hole, a hollow.<BR>	 3. A mast.<BR>	 4. A tree or rock<BR>in the midst of a river.<BR>	 f. (-पी)<BR>	 1. A small well.<BR>	 2. The navel.<BR>	 3. A<BR>flask, a bottle.<BR> E. कु to sound, (frogs croaking in a well, &c.) and<BR>प Uṇādi affix: the vowel is made long; also कूपक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=196-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूपक|कूपकः
कूपक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. The mast of a vessel.<BR>	 2. A stake, &c. to which a boat<BR>is moored.<BR>	 3. A leather oil vessel.<BR>	 4. The hollow below the loins.<BR>5. A funeral pile.<BR>	 6. A well.<BR>	 7. A temporary well, a hole dug for<BR>water in the dry bed of a rivulet.<BR>	 8. A tree or rock in the middle<BR>of a stream.<BR> E. कन् added the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=196-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूपमण्डूक
कूपमण्डूक m. (-कः) A frog in a well, applied to a person of no enterprise,<BR>one who never leaves his home.<BR> E. कूप, and मण्डूक a frog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=196-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूपाङ्ग|कूपांग|कूपाङ्गः
कूपाङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः) Horripilation, erection of the hairs of the body,<BR> E. कूप<BR>a well, and अङ्ग the body; some copies read कूपाङ्क, from अङ्ख a mark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=196-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूपार|कूपारः
कूपार m. (-रः) The ocean; also कूवार, and अकूपार, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=196-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूपिका
कूपिका f. (-का) A stone or rock in the middle of a stream: see कूपक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=196-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूभ
कूभ n. (-भं) A lake, a pool, a pond.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=196-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूर|कूरं|कूरः
कूर m. (-रः) Boiled rice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=196-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूर्च्च|कूर्च|कूर्चं|कूर्चः|कूर्च्चं|कूर्च्चः
कूर्च्च mn. (-र्च्चः-र्च्चं)<BR>	 1. The upper part of the nose, the part between the<BR>eyebrows.<BR>	 2. The beard.<BR>	 3. Deceit, fraud, circumvention.<BR>	 4. Hard,<BR>solid.<BR>	 5. The tip of the thumb and middle finger brought in contact,<BR>as to pinch, &c.<BR>	 6. A handful of Kusa grass or peacock's feathers.<BR>7. A bunch, a bundle, as of grass &c.<BR>	 8. A brush of the same.<BR>9. The head.<BR>	 10. False praise, unmerited commendation, either of<BR>one's self or another person, boasting, flattery.<BR>	 11. Hypocrisy.<BR>	 12.<BR>The mystic syllable Hum. (In Tan: shas.)<BR> E. कूर् to sound, चङ् affix,<BR>or कृ to do, उर्च्च affix or कूर्च्च Sautra root, to praise, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=196-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूर्च्चक|कूर्चक|कूर्चकः
कूर्च्चक n. (-कं) A brush for cleaning the teeth, &c.<BR> E. कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=196-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूर्च्चशिरस्|कूर्चशिरस्
कूर्च्चशिरस् n. (-रः) The heel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=197-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूर्च्चशीर्ष|कूर्चशीर्ष|कूर्चशीर्षः|कूर्च्चशीर्षः
कूर्च्चशीर्ष m. (-र्षः) A drug, commonly Jivaka, one of the eight principal<BR>medicaments.<BR> E. कूर्च्च the beard, &c. and शीर्ष the head; being bear-<BR>ded; or from कूर्च्च praise, and शीर्ष chief commendable amongst<BR>medicines; also with कन् added कूर्च्चशीर्षक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=197-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूर्च्चशेखर|कूर्चशेखर|कूर्चशेखरः|कूर्च्चशेखरः
कूर्च्चशेखर m. (-रः) The cocoa-nut tree.<BR> E. कूर्च्च a bunch, and शेखर summit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=197-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूर्च्चिका|कूर्चिका
कूर्च्चिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. Inspissated milk.<BR>	 2. A key.<BR>	 3. A bud, a blossom.<BR>	 4.<BR>A painting brush or pencil.<BR>	 5. A needle.<BR> E. कूर्च्च् to praise, &c. वुन्<BR>affix, and the fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=197-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूर्द|कूर्द्द
कूर्द r. 1st cl. (कुर्दते) To play: see कुर्द.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=197-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूर्दन|कूर्दनं|कूर्द्दन|कूर्द्दनं
कूर्दन n. (-नं) Playing, sport, pastime.<BR>	 f. (-नी) A festival in honour of<BR>KĀMADEVA, held on the day of full moon, in the month Chaitra. E.<BR>कूर्द् to play, ल्युट् affix, fem. ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=197-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूर्प्प|कूर्प|कूर्पं|कूर्पः
कूर्प्प n. (-र्प्पं) The space between the eyebrows.<BR> E. कॄ to scatter. &c. deriv.<BR>irr.: see कूर्च्च.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=197-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूर्प्पर|कूर्पर|कूर्परः
कूर्प्पर mf. (-रः-रा)<BR>	 1. The elbow.<BR>	 2. The knee.<BR> E. कुर to sound, with क्विप्<BR>affix कुर् पर from पृ to nourish, the first vowel is made long;<BR>sometimes also कुर्पर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=197-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूर्प्पास|कूर्पास|कूर्पासः
कूर्प्पास m. (-सः) A cuirass or quilted jacket worn as armour see कूर्प्पासक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=197-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूर्प्पासक|कूर्पासक|कूर्पासकः
कूर्प्पासक mn. (-कः-कं) A bodice, a jacket with short sleeves worn next<BR>the body, by woman especially.<BR> E. कूर्पर the elbow, आस् to abide,<BR>घञ् affix, and र dropped, कूर्प्पास, see the preceding: again, कन्<BR>pleonastic affix added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=197-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूर्म्म|कूर्म|कूर्मः|कूर्म्मः
कूर्म्म mf. (-र्म्मः-र्म्मी)<BR>	 1. A tortoise, a turtle.<BR>	 2. The descent of VIṢṆU as a<BR>tortoise to support the mountain Mandar at the churning of the<BR>ocean.<BR>	 3. A peculiar gesticulation with the fingers.<BR> E. कु implying<BR>reverse, ऊर्म्मी speed, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=197-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूर्म्मचक्र|कूर्मचक्र|कूर्म्मचक्रं
कूर्म्मचक्र n. (-क्रं) An astrological diagram.<BR> E. कूर्म्म, and चक्र circle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=197-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूर्म्मपृष्ठ|कूर्मपृष्ठ|कूर्म्मपृष्ठः
कूर्म्मपृष्ठ n. (-ष्ठं)<BR>	 1. Globe amaranth, (Gomphrena globosa.)<BR>	 2. The back<BR>or shell of a tortoise.<BR> E. कूर्म्म a tortoise, and पृष्ट the back.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=197-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूर्म्मपृष्ठक|कूर्मपृष्ठक|कूर्म्मपृष्ठकं
कूर्म्मपृष्ठक n. (-कं) The cover of a dish, a lid.<BR> E. कन् added to the preced-<BR>ing, implying resemblance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=197-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूर्म्मराज|कूर्मराज|कूर्मराजः|कूर्म्मराजः
कूर्म्मराज m. (-जः) The king of turtles, the tortoise supposed to uphold<BR>the world.<BR> E. कूर्म्म tortoise, and राज a king, from राजन् with टच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=197-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूल|कूलं
कूल r. 1st cl. (कूलति) To cover, to hide, to screen, to enclose: with अनु<BR>prefixed, to protect, to be kind to, as to a follower or dependent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=197-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूल|कूलं
कूल n. (-लं)<BR>	 1. A bank, a shore.<BR>	 2. A heap, a mound.<BR>	 3. A pond or pool.<BR>4. The rear of an army.<BR> E. कूल् to cover, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=197-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूलक|कूलकं|कूलकः
कूलक m. (-कः) An ant hill.<BR>	 n. (-कं)<BR>	 1. A mound of earth, a heap, a pile.<BR>2. A bank, a dyke.<BR> E. कन् added to the former.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=197-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूलङ्कष|कूलंकष|कूलंकषः|कूलङ्कषः
कूलङ्कष m. (-षः)<BR>	 1. The ocean, the sea.<BR>	 2. The stream or current of a<BR>river.<BR>	 f. (-षा) A river.<BR> E. कूल a bank, कष् to injure, affix खच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=197-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूलचर
कूलचर mfn. (-रः-री-रं) Frequenting the banks of rivers, grazing there,<BR>&c.<BR> E. कूल, चर what goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=197-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूलभू
कूलभू f. (-भूः) A bank, the land upon the bank or shore.<BR> E. कूल, and भू<BR>earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=197-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूलमुद्रुज
कूलमुद्रुज mfn. (-जः-जा-जं) Breaking down banks (as a river, &c.)<BR> E. कूल<BR>रुज् to make sick, with उत् pre. and खश् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=197-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूलमुद्वह
कूलमुद्वह mfn. (-हः-हा-हं) Carrying away the banks, (a river, &c.)<BR> E. कूल,<BR>वह् to bear, उत् pre. खश् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=197-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूलवती
कूलवती f. (-ती) A river.<BR> E. कूल a bank, and मतुप् poss. affix, fem. ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=197-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूलहण्डक|कूलहंडक|कूलहण्डकः
कूलहण्डक m. (-कः) An eddy.<BR> E. कूल a bank, and हुडि to collect, वुन् affix,<BR>deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=197-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूलिका
कूलिका f. (-का) Base or bottom part of the Indian lute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=197-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूवर|कूवरः
कूवर mfn. (-रः-री-रं) Beautiful, agreeable, pleasing.<BR>	 mn. (-रः-रं) The pole<BR>of a carriage or wood to which the yoke is fixed.<BR>	 m. (-रः) A hump-<BR>backed man.<BR>	 f. (-री) A carriage covered with a cloth or blanket. E.<BR>कू to sound, and वर from वृ to cherish, with अप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=197-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूवरिन्
कूवरिन् m. (-री) A carriage.<BR> E. कूवर the pole, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=197-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूष्माण्ड|कूष्मांड|कूष्मांडः|कूष्माण्डः
कूष्माण्ड mf. (-ण्डः-ण्डी) A pumpkin gourd, (Cucurbita pepo.)<BR>	 m. (-ण्डः) A<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=197-b" target="_blank">Page197-b+ 60</a>]<BR>kind of spirit or imp, of which there exists a Gana or class.<BR>	 f. (-ण्डी)<BR>A name of DURGĀ; also कुष्माण्ड and कूष्माण्डक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=197-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूष्माण्डक|कूष्माण्डकः
कूष्माण्डक m. (-कः) A pumpkin gourd: see कूष्माण्ड.<BR> E. कु bad, उष्म warm<BR>and अण्ड an egg here put for seed, कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=197-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूहना
कूहना f. (-ना) Hypocrisy, affectation of religious zeal or austerity: see,<BR>कुहना.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=197-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूहा
कूहा f. (-हा) A fog, a mist.<BR> E. कुह् to astonish, अङ् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=197-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृ
कृ r. 5th cl. (ञ) कृञ् (कृणोति, कृणुते) To hurt, to injure, to kill. (डु, ञ,)<BR>डुकृञ् r. 8th cl. (करोति, कुरुते) To do, to make, to perform any kind<BR>of action: this root admits most of the prepositions and a variety<BR>of significations; it is also active or deponent, according to its pre-<BR>fix and import; as, 1. With अति, (अतिकुरुते) To exceed, to do more.<BR>2. With अधि, (अधिकुरुते) a. To surpass or overcome. b. To superint-<BR>end, to govern. c. To hold of right. d. To bear patiently. e. To re-<BR>frain from.<BR>	 3. With अनु (अनुकरोति) To copy, to imitate, to act like<BR>or after.<BR>	 4. With अप (अपकुरुते) a. To wrong, to injure. b. To do evil.<BR>5. With आङ् (आकुरुते) a. To call. b. To take shape or form.<BR>	 6. With<BR>उत् (उत्कुरुते) a. To kill or hurt dangerously. b. To collect, to assem-<BR>ble.<BR>	 7. With उद्, and आङ् (उदाकुरुते) To reproach.<BR>	 8. With उप<BR>(उपकुरुते) To befriend, to serve or assist.<BR>	 9. With उप, and स inserted<BR>(उपस्कुरुते, or उपस्करोति) To alter. (उपस्करोति) a. To polish, to adorn.<BR>b. To assemble. c. To reply.<BR>	 10. With तिरस् (तिरस्करोति) To abuse, to<BR>revile.<BR>	 11. With दुर (दुष्करोति) To do evil.<BR>	 12. With निर् and आङ<BR>(निराकुरुते) a. To make light of, to contemn. b. To expel. c. To<BR>annihilate.<BR>	 13. With परि, and स inserted (परिष्करोति) To polish,<BR>to refine, to make elegant or perfect.<BR>	 14. With पर and आङ्<BR>(पराकरोति) To act well.<BR>	 15. With प्र (प्रकुरुते) a. To begin. b. To<BR>do anything quickly. c. To serve. d. To allot, to portion. e. To vio-<BR>late.<BR>	 f. To chant, to recite.<BR>	 16. With प्रति (प्रतिकुरुते) a. To counter-<BR>act. b. To retaliate. c. To remedy.<BR>	 17. With प्रति and उप (प्रत्युपकुरुते)<BR>To requite, to return a kindness; with वि (विकुरुते) a. To utter, to<BR>sound. b. To seek, strive for. (विकरोति) a. To alter, to change in<BR>form. b. To disturb or agitate.<BR>	 18. With वि and आङ् (व्याकुरुते) a.<BR>To explain, to expound. b. To make manifest or public.<BR>	 19. With<BR>सम् (संस्करोति) a. To polish, to perfect. b. To assemble, to bring to-<BR>gether.<BR>	 20. With सु (सुकरोति) To do well.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=197-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृक|कृकः
कृक m. (-कः) The throat, the larynx.<BR> E. कृ to make, and क्कुन् affix, what<BR>makes or produces sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=197-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृकण|कृकणः
कृकण m. (-णः)<BR>	 1. A kind of partridge, commonly Kaer, (Perdix sylva-<BR>tica.)<BR>	 2. A worm.<BR> E. कृक the throat, and अण् to sound, affix अच्,<BR>the deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=197-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृकणीय
कृकणीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Belonging or relating to a partridge.<BR> E. कृकण<BR>and छ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=197-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृकर|कृकरः
कृकर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A name of ŚIVA.<BR>	 2. One of the five vital airs, that<BR>which assists in digestion.<BR>	 3. A kind of partridge: see कृकण.<BR>	 4. A<BR>sort of pepper, (P. chavya.)<BR>	 5. The oleander tree.<BR> E. कृक the throat,<BR>and र what gets or receives; or कृ imitative sound, and कर what<BR>makes, from कृ to make or do, affix अप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=197-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृकलाश|कृकलाशः
कृकलाश m. (-शः) See the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=197-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृकलास|कृकलासः
कृकलास m. (-सः) A lizard, chameleon.<BR> E. कृक the throat, and लस् to<BR>play, &c. affix अण्; also कृकलाश.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=197-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृकवाकु|कृकवाकुः
कृकवाकु m. (-कुः)<BR>	 1. A cock, a gallinaceous fowl.<BR>	 2. A peacock.<BR>	 3. A li-<BR>zard, a chameleon.<BR> E. कृक the throat, वच् to speak, Uṇādi affix ञुण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=197-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृकवाकुध्वज|कृकवाकुध्वजः
कृकवाकुध्वज m. (-जः) A name of KĀRTTIKEYA.<BR> E. कृकवाकु a peacock, and<BR>ध्वज a standard or symbol; the peacock is the vehicle and standard<BR>of SKANDA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=197-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृकाटिका
कृकाटिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. The back of the neck.<BR>	 2. The raised and straight<BR>part of the neck.<BR> E. कृक the throat, अट् to go, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=197-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृकुलास
कृकुलास m. (-सः) A lizard, a chameleon: see कृकलास.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=197-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृच्छ्र|कृच्छ्रं|कृच्छ्रः|कृछ्र
कृच्छ्र mfn. (-च्छ्रः-च्छ्रा-च्छ्रं)<BR>	 1. Attended with pain, painful.<BR>	 2. Wicked,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=198-a" target="_blank">Page198-a+ 60</a>]<BR>sinful.<BR>	 mn. (-च्छ्रः-च्छ्रं) Bodily pain. Penance, expiation.<BR>	 3. Sin.<BR>	 4.<BR>difficulty, labour, trouble.<BR>	 5. A kind of religious penance, accord-<BR>ing to some, the same as the Prajapatya: see प्राजापत्य; (according<BR>to others, as the Santapana: (see सान्तपन.)<BR> E. कृत् to cut, रक् Uṇādi<BR>affix, and छ substituted for the final.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=197-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृच्छ्रगत
कृच्छ्रगत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Embarrassed, distressed.<BR>	 2. Pained, suffering<BR>pain.<BR> E. कृच्छ्र, and गत gone to or in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=198-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृच्छ्रातिकृच्छ्र|कृच्छ्रातिकृच्छ्रः
कृच्छ्रातिकृच्छ्र m. (-च्छ्रः) A kind of penance, taking no sustenance but water<BR>for three, nine, twelve, or twenty-one days.<BR> E. कृच्छ्र one kind of<BR>penance. and अतिकृच्छ्र another; the substance of both.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=198-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृच्छ्रार्द्ध्व
कृच्छ्रार्द्ध्व m. (-र्द्ध्वः) An inferior penance lasting six days.<BR> E. कृच्छ्र and अर्द्ध्व half.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=198-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृड
कृड r. 6th cl. (कृडति)<BR>	 1. To be thick or coarse, to be gross, to be solid.<BR>2. To eat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=198-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृणु|कृणुः
कृणु m. (-णुः) A painter.<BR> E. कृ to do or make, क्नु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=198-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत|कृतं
कृत(-ई)कृती r. 6th cl. (कृन्तति) To cut, to divide. r. 7th cl. (कृणति) To<BR>surround, to encompass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=198-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत|कृतं
कृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Done, made, performed.<BR>	 2. Injured, hurt.<BR>	 3. Fit,<BR>proper.<BR>	 n. (-तं)<BR>	 1. The first of the four ages of the world, the Satya-<BR>yug.<BR>	 2. Fruit, consequence. adv.<BR>	 1. Enough, sufficient.<BR>	 2. Enough,<BR>completely finished.<BR>	 3. Enough, have done, no more.<BR> E. कृ to do, to<BR>injure, &c. affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=198-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतक|कृतकं|कृतकः
कृतक mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>	 1. Artificial, factitious, made, not produced spon-<BR>taneously.<BR>	 2. Assumed, simulated, not natural.<BR>	 n. (-कं) Factitious<BR>salt, produced by boiling and evaporating from saline soils.<BR> E. कृत्<BR>to cut or divide, Uṇādi affix अक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=198-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतकपट
कृतकपट mfn. (-टः-टा-टं) Deceiving, beguiling, fraudulent.<BR> E. कृत, and<BR>कपट deceit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=198-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतकर्त्तव्य|कृतकर्तव्य
कृतकर्त्तव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं) Having done or discharged, or being done,<BR>(a duty.) कृत done, कर्त्तव्य what was to be done.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=198-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतकर्म्मन्|कृतकर्मन्
कृतकर्म्मन् mfn. (-र्म्मा-र्म्मा-र्म्मं) Skilful, clever, able.<BR> E. कृत made, कर्म्मन् act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=198-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतकार्य्य|कृतकार्य
कृतकार्य्य mfn. (-र्य्यः-र्य्या-र्य्यं) See कृतकृत्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=198-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतकाल|कृतकालः
कृतकाल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>	 1. Fixed, settled as to time.<BR>	 2. Sent or deposit-<BR>ed, &c. for a certain time.<BR> E. कृत, and काल time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=198-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतकूर्च्छक
कृतकूर्च्छक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Tied up as a small bundle or brush.<BR> E. कृत-<BR>कूर्च्छ a bundle, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=198-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतकृत्य|कृतकृत्यः
कृतकृत्य mfn. (-त्यः-त्या-त्यं)<BR>	 1. Having done or discharged anything to be<BR>done.<BR>	 2. Having accomplished or attained any object.<BR>	 3. Contented,<BR>satisfied.<BR> E. कृत done, and कृत्य what was to be done; also कृतकर्त्तव्य,<BR>कृतकार्य्य, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=198-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतकृत्यता
कृतकृत्यता f. (-ता) Success, attainment, accomplishment, the full dis-<BR>charge of any duty or realisation of any object.<BR> E. कृतकृत्य and तल्<BR>affix; also with त्व affix, कृतकृत्यत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=198-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतकोटि|कृतकोटिः
कृतकोटि m. (-टिः)<BR>	 1. A name of the saint KAŚYAPA.<BR>	 2. A name of UPA-<BR>VERSHA, another divine sage.<BR> E. कृत made, कोटि excellence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=198-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतकोप
कृतकोप mfn. (-पः-पा-पं) Angry, indignant.<BR> E. कृत, and कोप anger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=198-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतक्रय|कृतक्रयः
कृतक्रय m. (-यः) A purchaser, a buyer.<BR> E. कृत, and क्रय purchase.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=198-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतक्रिय|कृतक्रियः
कृतक्रिय mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>	 1. having finished or completed anything in<BR>which one was engaged.<BR>	 3. Having attained any end or accomplish-<BR>ed any object.<BR>	 3. Having fulfilled one's duty.<BR> E. कृत done, क्रिया<BR>work, duty. &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=198-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतक्रुध
कृतक्रुध mfn. (-धः-धा-धं) Angry, resentful.<BR> E. कृत, and क्रुधा wrath.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=198-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतघातयत्न
कृतघातयत्न mfn. (-त्नः-त्ना-त्नं) Assaulting, attacking, one who tries to kill.<BR>E. कृत, घात a blow, यत्न effort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=198-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतघ्न|कृतघ्नः
कृतघ्न mfn. (-घ्नः-घ्नी-घ्नं)<BR>	 1. Ungrateful, not acknowledging former good<BR>offices.<BR>	 2. Defeating or rendering vain all previous measures.<BR> E. कृत<BR>what has been done, घ्न killing, destroying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=198-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतघ्नता
कृतघ्नता f. (-ता) Ingratitude.<BR> E. तल् added to the last; also with त्व, कृतघ्नत्वं,<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=198-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतचूड|कृतचूडः
कृतचूड m. (-डः) A boy on whom the ceremony of tonsure has been per-<BR>formed.<BR> E. कृत, and चूडा a crest, a lock of hair being left on the top<BR>of the head.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=198-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतजन्मन्
कृतजन्मन् mfn. (-न्मा-न्मा-न्म)<BR>	 1. Born, produced.<BR>	 2. Generated.<BR> E. कृत, and<BR>जन्मन् birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=198-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतज्ञ|कृतज्ञः
कृतज्ञ mfn. (-ज्ञः-ज्ञा-ज्ञं)<BR>	 1. Grateful, remembering former aid or favours.<BR>2. Observant of propriety, correct in conduct.<BR>	 m. (-ज्ञः) A dog. E.<BR>कृत what is done, and ज्ञ who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=198-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतज्ञता
कृतज्ञता f. (-ता) Gratitude.<BR> E. कृतज्ञ, and तल् affix; also कृतज्ञत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=198-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृततीर्थ
कृततीर्थ m. (-र्थः)<BR>	 1. A guide to holy places, &c. one who frequents them.<BR>2. A councillor, one fertile in expedients.<BR> E. कृत, तीर्थ pilgrimage, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=198-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतत्व
कृतत्व n. (-त्वं) Being done or effected.<BR> E. त्व, added to कृत.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=198-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतदार
कृतदार m. (-रः) A married man.<BR> E. कृत, and दारा a wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=198-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतदास|कृतदासः
कृतदास mf. (-सः-सी) A self-engaged servant, a hired servant.<BR> E. कृत made,<BR>(spontaneously,) and दास a slave.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=198-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतधी
कृतधी mfn. (-धीः-धीः-धि)<BR>	 1. Prudent, considerate.<BR>	 2. Learned, educated.<BR>E. कृत, and धी understanding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=198-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृवध्वंस
कृवध्वंस mfn. (-सः-सा-सं)<BR>	 1. Defeated, overpowered.<BR>	 2. Injured, destroyed.<BR>3. Recollecting past transactions.<BR> E. कृत, and ध्वंस loss.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=198-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतध्वस्त
कृतध्वस्त mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं) Loss after being one possessed or acquired. E.<BR>कृत made, gained, ध्वस्त destroyed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=198-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतनाशक
कृतनाशक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Ungrateful.<BR> E. कृत, and नाशक who destroys.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=198-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतनिर्णेजन|कृतनिर्णेजनः
कृतनिर्णेजन m. (-नः) A penitent, one who has performed penance or made<BR>expiation.<BR> E. कृत, and निर्णेजन cleansing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=198-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतनिश्चय
कृतनिश्चय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Confident, sure, certain.<BR> E. कृत, and निश्चय<BR>certainly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=198-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतपुङ्ख|कृतपुंख|कृतपुङ्खः
कृतपुङ्ख mfn. (-ङ्खः-ङ्खा-ङ्खं) Skilled in archery.<BR> E. कृत done, made, पुङ्ख the<BR>feather of an arrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=198-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतपूर्ब्ब
कृतपूर्ब्ब mfn. (-र्ब्बः-र्ब्बा-र्ब्बं) Done formerly or precedingly.<BR> E. कृत, and पूर्ब्ब<BR>prior.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=198-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतपूर्ब्बनाशन
कृतपूर्ब्बनाशन n. (-नं) Ingratitude, forgetting past services.<BR> E. कृतपूर्ब्ब, and<BR>नाशन destroying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=198-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतपूर्ब्बिन्
कृतपूर्ब्बिन् mfn. (-र्ब्बी-र्ब्बिणी-र्ब्बि) One by whom anything was done in<BR>time past.<BR> E. कृत done, पूर्ब्ब formerly, इनि affix of agency.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=198-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतपौरुष
कृतपौरुष mfn. (-षः-षा-षं) Behaving gallantly.<BR> E. कृत, and पौरुष manhood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=198-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतप्रणाम
कृतप्रणाम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं) Saluting, making or having made obeisance. E.<BR>कृत, and प्रणाम salute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=198-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतप्रयत्न
कृतप्रयत्न mfn. (-त्नः-त्ना-त्नं) Active, industrious, persevering.<BR> E. कृत, and<BR>प्रयत्न effort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=198-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतफल|कृतफलं
कृतफल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Successful, fruitful.<BR>	 n. (-लं)<BR>	 1. Result, conse-<BR>quence of an act.<BR>	 2. A poisonous substance: see कृक्वोल.<BR> E. कृत, and<BR>फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=198-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतबाहु
कृतबाहु mfn. (-हुः-हुः-हु) Laying hand upon, touching.<BR> E. कृत, and बाहु<BR>the arm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=198-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतबुद्धि
कृतबुद्धि mfn. (-द्धिः-द्धिः-द्धि) Informed of one's duty, having acquired<BR>knowledge.<BR> E. कृत, and बुद्धि understanding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=198-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतभय
कृतभय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Alarmed, apprehensive.<BR> E. कृत, and भय fear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=198-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतमङ्गल
कृतमङ्गल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Blessed, consecrated.<BR> E. कृत and मङ्गल auspicious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=198-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतमन्यु
कृतमन्यु mfn. (-न्युः-न्यु-न्यु) Angry, offended, indignant.<BR> E. कृत, and मन्यु<BR>anger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=198-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतमाल|कृतमालः
कृतमाल m. (-लः) A tree, (Cassia fistula.)<BR> E. कृत made, माल a garland,<BR>garlands being made of its flowers; also आरग्बध.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=198-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतमुख|कृतमुखः
कृतमुख mfn. (-खः-खा-खं) Skilled, clever, conversant.<BR> E. कृत done, and<BR>मुख chief, principal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=198-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतरव
कृतरव mfn. (-वः-वा-वं) Sounding, singing.<BR> E. कृत, and रव a sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=198-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतरुच्
कृतरुच् mfn. (-रुक्) Splendid, brilliant.<BR> E. कृत, and रुच् light; also कृतरुचि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=198-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतरुष
कृतरुष mfn. (-षः-षा-षं) Angry, displeased.<BR> E. कृत, and रुषा wrath.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=198-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतलक्षण|कृतलक्षणः
कृतलक्षण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Excellent, amiable, &c. noted for good qualities.<BR>2. Defined, discriminated.<BR>	 3. Marked, stamped.<BR>	 4. Branded.<BR> E. कृत<BR>made, लक्षण a mark, a sign.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=198-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतवत्|कृतवन्त्
कृतवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Making, was making, made.<BR> E. कृत, and क्तवतु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=198-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतवाप|कृतवापः
कृतवाप m. (-पः) A penitent who has shaven his head and chin.<BR> E. कृत,<BR>and वाप tonsure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=198-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतविक्रिय
कृतविक्रिय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Altered, changed.<BR> E. कृत and विक्रिय change;<BR>also कृतविकार.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=199-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतविद्य
कृतविद्य mfn. (-द्यः-द्या-द्यं) Scientific, a philosopher.<BR> E. कृत and विद्या<BR>knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=199-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतविस्मय
कृतविस्मय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Surpassing, astonishing.<BR> E. कृत, and विस्मय<BR>wonder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=199-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतवेतन|कृतवेतनः
कृतवेतन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Hired as a servant or labourer.<BR> E. कृत made,<BR>appointed, and वेतन wages.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=199-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतवेदिन्
कृतवेदिन् mfn. (-दी-दिनी-दि)<BR>	 1. Grateful.<BR>	 2. Knowing, observant.<BR> E. कृत,<BR>and वेदिन् who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=199-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतवेधन
कृतवेधन m. (-नः) A plant, a sort of Ghosha with white flowers: see घोष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=199-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतवेपथु
कृतवेपथु mfn. (-थुः-थुः-थु) Trembling.<BR> E. कृत, and वेपथु trembling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=199-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतवेश
कृतवेश mfn. (-शः-शा-शं) Decorating, adorning.<BR> E. कृत, and वेश dress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=199-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतव्यलीक
कृतव्यलीक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Annoyed, vexed, irritated.<BR> E. कृत, and व्यलीक<BR>pain, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=199-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतशक्ति
कृतशक्ति mfn. (-क्तिः-क्तिः-क्ति) Putting forth one's strength or courage. E.<BR>कृत, and शक्ति power.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=199-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतशोभ
कृतशोभ mfn. (-भः-भा-भं)<BR>	 1. Splendid, brilliant.<BR>	 2. Beautiful, beautified.<BR>3. Dexterous, handy.<BR> E. कृत, and शोभा splendor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=199-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतशौच
कृतशौच mfn. (-चः-चा-चं) Purified, cleansed, freed from the natural de-<BR>jections, released from conventional defilement, &c.<BR> E. कृत, and<BR>शौच purification.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=199-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतश्रम|कृतश्रमः
कृतश्रम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं) Laborious, assiduous, persevering, pains-taking<BR>making great or continuous exertions.<BR> E. कृत made, श्रम fatigue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=199-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतसङ्केत|कृतसंकेत
कृतसङ्केत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Making an agreement or appointment,<BR> E. कृत,<BR>and सङ्केत agreement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=199-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतसंसर्ग
कृतसंसर्ग mfn. (-र्गः-र्गा-र्गं) Approximate, united.<BR> E. कृत, and संसर्ग union.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=199-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतसंस्कार
कृतसंस्कार mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Initiated, having undergone all the purificatory<BR>ceremonies.<BR> E. कृत, and संस्कार rite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=199-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतसंज्ञ
कृतसंज्ञ mfn. (-ज्ञः-ज्ञा-ज्ञं) Distinguished by appropriate marks, devices,<BR>&c.<BR> E. कृत, and संज्ञा a signal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=199-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतसन्निधान|कृतसंनिधान
कृतसन्निधान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Contracted, approximated.<BR> E. कृत, and सन्नि-<BR>धान proximity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=199-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतसम्बन्ध
कृतसम्बन्ध mfn. (-न्धः-न्धा-न्धं) Connected, allied.<BR> E. कृत, and सम्बन्ध<BR>alliance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=199-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतसापत्निका
कृतसापत्निका f. (-का) A woman whose husband has taken another wife.<BR>E. कृत made, स with, together with, पत्नी a wife, affix कन्ः or derived<BR>from सापत्नक, कृतसापत्नका; also कृतसापत्नी, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=199-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतस्थिति
कृतस्थिति mfn. (-तिः-तिः-ति) Abiding, staying, taking up an abode in or<BR>with.<BR> E. कृत, and स्थिति stay.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=199-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतस्वस्त्ययन
कृतस्वस्त्ययन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Recommended to the protection of gods pre-<BR>vious to any journey or undertaking.<BR> E. कृत, स्वस्त्ययन benediction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=199-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतहस्त|कृतहस्तः
कृतहस्त mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं)<BR>	 1. Skilled in archery.<BR>	 2. Clever, skilful, dexter-<BR>ous.<BR> E. कृत exercised, हस्त the hand; also कृतहस्तक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=199-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृताकृत|कृताकृतः
कृताकृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Done in part, not completed.<BR>	 2. Committed<BR>and omitted.<BR> E. कृत, and अकृत undone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=199-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतागम
कृतागम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं) Advanced, proficient,<BR> E. कृत, and आगम coming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=199-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतागस्
कृतागस् mfn. (-गाः-गाः-गः) Criminal, offending, in fault.<BR> E. कृत done, आगस्<BR>crime.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=199-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृताग्निकार्य्य|कृताग्निकार्य
कृताग्निकार्य्य m. (-र्य्यः) A Brahman who has offered the usual oblations<BR>with fire.<BR> E. कृत, and अग्निकार्य्य fire-sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=199-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृताङ्क|कृतांक|कृताङ्कः
कृताङ्क mfn. (-ङ्कः-ङ्का-ङ्कं)<BR>	 1. Marked.<BR>	 2. Numbered.<BR>	 3. Branded.<BR> E. कृत,<BR>and अङ्क a mark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=199-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृताञ्जलि|कृतांजलि|कृताञ्जलिः
कृताञ्जलि mfn. (-लिः-लिः-लि) One who joins the palms of the hands,<BR>making such a sign of reverence or solicitation, reverent, respect-<BR>ful.<BR>	 m. (-लिः) A shrub used in medicine, also in magical portions,<BR>&c.<BR> E. कृत made, अञ्जलि the hand joined, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=199-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृताञ्जलिपुट
कृताञ्जलिपुट mfn. (-टः-टा-टं) Joining the palms of the hands for the pur-<BR>pose of doing obeisance, also for holding water &c.<BR> E. कृत, and अञ्जलि-<BR>पुट the palms joined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=199-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतात्मन्
कृतात्मन् mfn. (-त्मा-त्मा-त्म) Subdued, tranquil, of a self-governed spirit.<BR>E. कृत, and आत्मन् self.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=199-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतानति
कृतानति mfn. (-तिः-तिः-ति) Bending, bowed, paying homage or respect.<BR>E. कृत, and आनति bowing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=199-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतानुकूल्य
कृतानुकूल्य mfn. (-ल्यः-ल्या-ल्यं) Kind, favouring, compliant.<BR> E. कृत, आनुकूल्य<BR>favour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=199-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतानुव्याध
कृतानुव्याध mfn. (-धः-धा-धं) Mixed, combined, united.<BR> E. कृत, and अनुव्याध<BR>mixture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=199-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतानुसार|कृतानुसारः
कृतानुसार m. (-रः) Established practice, usage, custom, rate.<BR> E. कृत, and<BR>अनुसार custom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=199-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतान्त|कृतांत|कृतान्तः
कृतान्त m. (-न्तः)<BR>	 1. A name of YAMA, son of SŪRYA, and regent of the<BR>dead, or death personified.<BR>	 2. Destiny, that is, the inevitable<BR>result of actions done in a past existence.<BR>	 3. A demonstrated con-<BR>clusion, proved or established doctrine.<BR>	 4. Sinful or inauspicious<BR>action.<BR>	 5. Saturday, which is considered as an unlucky day.<BR>	 f. (-न्ता)<BR>A perfume: see रेणुका.<BR> E. कृत act, (actum) done, अन्त end, destruction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=199-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतान्तक
कृतान्तक m. (-कः) See the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=199-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतान्तजनक|कृतांतजनक|कृतान्तजनकः
कृतान्तजनक m. (-कः) A name of the sun.<BR> E. कृतान्त YAMA, and जनक pro-<BR>genitor; being the father of YAMA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=199-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतापकार
कृतापकार mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>	 1. Injured, wronged.<BR>	 2. Discomfited, overpower-<BR>ed.<BR>	 3. Doing wrong, offending.<BR> E. कृत, and अपकार offence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=199-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतापदान
कृतापदान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Completing a task, effecting an object.<BR> E. कृत,<BR>and अपदान accomplishment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=199-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतापराध
कृतापराध mfn. (-धः-धा-धं) Guilty, culpable, an offender.<BR> E. कृत, and अप-<BR>राध offence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=199-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृताभिषेक|कृताभिषेकः
कृताभिषेक mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>	 1. Sprinkled.<BR>	 2. Inaugurated.<BR>	 m. (-कः) A<BR>prince, &c. who has been inaugurated.<BR> E. कृत, and अभिषेष sprinkling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=199-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतार्थ|कृतार्थः
कृतार्थ mfn. (-र्थः-र्था-र्थं) Successful, having attained an end, having accom-<BR>plished a purpose or desire.<BR> E. कृत done, अर्थ object.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=199-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतार्थता
कृतार्थता f. (-ता) Success, fruitfulness, accomplishment of an object. E.<BR>तल् added to the last; also कृतार्थत्व.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=199-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतार्थीकृत
कृतार्थीकृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Rendered successful.<BR> E. कृतार्थ, and कृत made, च्वि<BR>augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=199-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतार्थीभूत
कृतार्थीभूत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Become successful.<BR> E. कृतार्थ, and भूत been, च्वि<BR>augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=199-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतालय|कृतालयः
कृतालय m. (-यः) A frog.<BR> E. कृत made, आलय abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=199-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतावधान
कृतावधान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Careful, cautious, prudent, attentive.<BR> E. कृत,<BR>and अवधान care.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=199-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतावधि
कृतावधि mfn. (-धिः-धिः-धि)<BR>	 1. Fixed, appointed, agreed upon.<BR>	 2. Bounded,<BR>limited.<BR> E. कृत, and अवधि term, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=199-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतावमर्ष
कृतावमर्ष mfn. (-र्षः-र्षा-र्षं)<BR>	 1. Disregarding, effacing from recollection.<BR>	 2.<BR>Intolerant.<BR> E. कृत, and अवमर्ष impatience.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=199-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृताबशक्थिक
कृताबशक्थिक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Seated on the hams with the knees tied<BR>together, or the hips and knees surrounded by a cloth.<BR> E. कृत, and<BR>अवशक्थिका the cloth so used.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=199-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतावस्थ
कृतावस्थ mfn. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थं)<BR>	 1. Summoned, called.<BR>	 2. Made present.<BR>	 3.<BR>Fixed, settled.<BR> E. कृत, and अवस्था condition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=199-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतावास
कृतावास m. (-सः) A lodging, a temporary a accommodation, an apart-<BR>ment.<BR> E. कृत, and आवास abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=199-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृताशन
कृताशन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Feeding upon.<BR> E. कृत, and अशन eating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=199-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतास्कन्दन
कृतास्कन्दन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>	 1. Assailing, attacking.<BR>	 2. Effacing from re-<BR>collection.<BR> E. कृत, and आस्कन्दन going to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=199-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतास्त्र
कृतास्त्र mfn. (-स्त्रः-स्त्रा-स्त्रं) Armed.<BR> E. कृत, and अस्त्र weapon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=199-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतास्पद
कृतास्पद mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>	 1. Governed, ruled.<BR>	 2. Supporting, rested upon<BR>by anything.<BR>	 3. Residing in or on, taking one's abode.<BR> E. कृत, and<BR>आस्पद place, rule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=199-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृताहक
कृताहक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Having performed the daily ceremonies, or de-<BR>votions.<BR> E. कृत, अहन् a day, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=199-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृताह्वान
कृताह्वान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>	 1. Summoned, called.<BR>	 2. Challenged.<BR> E. कृत,<BR>and आह्वान calling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=199-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृति|कृतिः
कृति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Act, action, acting, doing, &c.<BR>	 2. Injuring, hurt, hurt-<BR>ing.<BR>	 3. A sort of metre, a stanza of four lines, with twenty sylla-<BR>bles in each.<BR> E. कृ to do, to injure, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=200-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतिकर|कृतिकरः
कृतिकर m. (-रः) A name of RĀVANA.<BR> E. कृति injuring, कृ to do, ट aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=200-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतिन्
कृतिन् mfn. (-ती-तिनी-ति)<BR>	 1. Wise, learned.<BR>	 2. Clever, skilful.<BR>	 3. Good,<BR>virtuous.<BR>	 4. Pure, pious, 5. Following, obeying, doing what is<BR>enjoined.<BR> E. कृत done, performed, इनि affix; by whom proper acts<BR>are done.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=200-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृते
कृते ind. For, on account of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=200-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतेर्ष्य
कृतेर्ष्य mfn. (-र्ष्यः-र्ष्या-र्ष्य) Envious, jealous.<BR> E. कृत, and ईर्ष्या envy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=200-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतोच्चैस्
कृतोच्चैस् ind. Raised on high.<BR> E. कृत, and उच्चैस् high.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=200-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतोदक
कृतोदक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Having performed ablutions.<BR> E. कृत, and उदक<BR>water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=200-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतोद्वाह
कृतोद्वाह mfn. (-हः-हा-हं) Performing penance by standing with uplifted<BR>hands.<BR>	 2. Married.<BR> E. कृत, and उद्वाह marriage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=200-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतोपकार
कृतोपकार mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>	 1. Assisted, befriended.<BR>	 2. Friendly, giving<BR>aid.<BR> E. कृत, and उपकार help.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=200-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतोपनयन
कृतोपनयन m. (-नः) The student invested with the sacrificial cord.<BR> E. कृत<BR>and उपनयन investiture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=200-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतोपभोग
कृतोपभोग mfn. (-गः-गा-गं) Used, enjoyed.<BR> E. कृत, and उपभोग use.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=200-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्त|कृत्तं
कृत्त mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं)<BR>	 1. Cut, divided.<BR>	 2. Desired, sought, wished for. E.<BR>कृत् to cut, &c. affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=200-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्ति|कृत्तिः
कृत्ति f. (-त्तिः)<BR>	 1. The hide upon which the religious student sits, sleeps,<BR>&c. usually the skin of an antelope.<BR>	 2. The skin.<BR>	 3. The bark of<BR>the Bhūrjpatra, used for writing upon, for making hooka snakes,<BR>&c.<BR>	 4. One of the lunar mansions: see the next.<BR> E. कृत् to cut, क्तिन्<BR>aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=200-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्तिका
कृत्तिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. The third of the lunar mansions, or constellations in<BR>the moon's path, consisting of six stars, and corresponding to the<BR>Pleiades.<BR>	 2. (In mythology,) a nymph; one of six, the nurses of<BR>KARTTIKEYA.<BR> E. कृत् to cut, क्तिन् and कन् affixes; the figure of the<BR>asterism is a razor or knife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=200-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्तिकाभव|कृत्तिकाभवः
कृत्तिकाभव m. (-वः) A name of CHANDRA or the moon.<BR> E. कृत्तिका the<BR>constellation, and भव who is born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=200-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्तिकासुत|कृत्तिकासुतः
कृत्तिकासुत m. (-तः) A name of SKANDA or KARTTIKEYA.<BR> E. कृत्तिका and<BR>सुत the son; the nymphs so named being his foster mothers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=200-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्तिवास|कृत्तिवासः
कृत्तिवास m. (-सः) ŚIVA: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=200-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्तिवासस्
कृत्तिवासस् m. (-साः) An appellation of MAHADEVA.<BR> E. कृत्ति a skin or<BR>hide, and वासस् clothes; clothed with a tyger's skin; also कृत्तिवास.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=200-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्नु|कृत्नुः
कृत्नु mfn. (-त्नुः-त्नुः-त्नु) An artist, an artificer or mechanic.<BR> E. कृ to make,<BR>कृत्नु Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=200-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्य|कृत्यं|कृत्यः
कृत्य mfn. (-त्यः-त्या-त्यं)<BR>	 1. To be done or performed.<BR>	 2. To be rendered<BR>murderous or mischievous, hired as an assassin, seduced from<BR>allegiance or alliance, hostile through covetousness, &c.<BR>	 f. (-त्या)<BR>	 1.<BR>Action, act.<BR>	 2. A female deity, to whom sacrifices are offered for<BR>destructive and magical purposes.<BR>	 3. Magic.<BR>	 4. A pestilence.<BR>	 n.<BR>(-त्यं)<BR>	 1. Motive, cause.<BR>	 2. The class of affixes in grammar forming<BR>nouns corresponding to gerunds and supines, chiefly with a passive<BR>signification, but sometimes active, and sometimes abstract nouns.<BR>E. कृत्, to injure, to divide &c. क्यप् or यत् affixed, or कृत्, to injure,<BR>वुन् affix, and य inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=200-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्यक
कृत्यक m. (-कः) An injurer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=200-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्यज्ञ
कृत्यज्ञ mfn. (-ज्ञः-ज्ञा-ज्ञं) Learned, wise, who knows what is to be done. E.<BR>कृत्य, and ज्ञ who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=200-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्यवर्त्मन्
कृत्यवर्त्मन् n. (-र्त्म) The right way, the manner in which any object is to<BR>be effected.<BR> E. कृत्य, and वर्त्मन् a road.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=200-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्यविद्
कृत्यविद् mf. (-विद्) Learned, wise who knows what is to be done.<BR> E. कृत्य,<BR>and विद् who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=200-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्यविधि|कृत्यविधिः
कृत्यविधि f. (-धिः) The way to do anything, a rule or precept.<BR> E. कृत्य, and<BR>विधि rule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=200-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्रिम|कृत्रिमं|कृत्रिमः
कृत्रिम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं) Made, factitious, artificial, the reverse of what is<BR>naturally or spontaneously produced.<BR>	 m. (-मः)<BR>	 1. Incense, olibanum.<BR>2. An adopted son, used for कृत्रिमपुत्र.<BR>	 n. (-मं) A kind of salt, the<BR>common Bit Noban or Bit Lavan.<BR> E. कृ to make, क्त्रि Uṇādi affix,<BR>and मम् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=200-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्रिमधूप|कृत्रिमधूपः
कृत्रिमधूप m. (-पः) A compound perfume, containing ten or eighteen in-<BR>gredients.<BR> E. कृत्रिम artificial, and धूप resin; also with कन् added<BR>कृत्रिमधूपक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=200-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्रिमपुत्र|कृत्रिमपुत्त्रः|कृत्रिमपुत्रः
कृत्रिमपुत्र m. (-त्रः) An adopted son; one of the twelve kinds recognized<BR>in law, the son made.<BR> E. कृत्रिम, and पुत्र a son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=200-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्रिममित्र|कृत्रिममित्रः
कृत्रिममित्र m. (-त्रः) An acquired friend; one on whom benefits have<BR>been conferred, or from whom they have been received.<BR> E. कृत्रिम<BR>made, and मित्र a friend; also similar compounds in this or other<BR>senses, कृत्रिमशत्रु an acquired enemy, कृत्रिमौदासीन one who is indiffer-<BR>ent to benefits or injuries, neither an acquired friend nor foe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=200-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्वा
कृत्वा ind. Having done, made, &c.<BR> E. कृ to do, क्त्वाच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=200-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्स|कृत्सं|कृत्सः
कृत्स n. (-त्सं)<BR>	 1. Water.<BR>	 2. Entire, whole.<BR> E. कृत् to surround, and<BR>Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=200-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्स्न|कृत्स्नं|कृत्स्नः
कृत्स्न mfn. (-त्स्नः-त्स्ना-त्स्नं) All, whole, entire.<BR>	 n. (-त्स्नं)<BR>	 1. Water.<BR>	 2. The<BR>flank or hip.<BR> E. कृत् to encompass, कस्न Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=200-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्स्नविद्
कृत्स्नविद् mfn. (-वित् or -विद्) Omniscient, acquainted with all things. E.<BR>कृत्स्न all, and विद् who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=200-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्स्नशस्
कृत्स्नशस् ind. Wholly, entirely, altogether.<BR> E. कृत्स्न, and शस् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=200-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृदर|कृदरं|कृदरः
कृदर m. (-रः) A granary, a cup-board, &c. for holding corn, grain, &c.<BR>E. कृत् to contain, Uṇādi affix अर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=200-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृदन्त
कृदन्त m. (-न्तः) A noun formed by the application of the affixes termed<BR>कृत् to the root,<BR> E. कृत्, and अन्त a final.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=200-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृन्तत्र|कृंतत्र|कृंतत्रं|कृन्तत्रं
कृन्तत्र n. (-त्रं) A plough.<BR> E. कृत् to divide or cut, कत्रन् Uṇādi affix, and<BR>नुम् inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=200-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृन्तन|कृंतन|कृंतनं|कृन्तनं
कृन्तन n. (-नं) Cutting.<BR> E. कृति to cut, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=200-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृन्तनिका
कृन्तनिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. A knife.<BR>	 2. The edge of a knife.<BR> E. कन् added to<BR>the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=200-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृप|कृपः
कृप(ऊ, ऌ)ऊकृपॢ r. 1st cl. (कल्पते) to be able. r. 1st and 10th cls.<BR>(कल्पति, कल्पयति)<BR>	 1. To think or imagine.<BR>	 2. To mix.<BR>	 3. To paint or<BR>colour. r. 1st cl. (कृपति) To have pity or mercy. r. 10th cl. (कृपयति)<BR>To be weak. In the first roots ल or ऌ is substituted for ऋ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=200-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृप|कृपः
कृप m. (-पः)<BR>	 1. The name of a sage, the brother-in-law of DRONA.<BR>	 2. A<BR>name of VYASA, the compiler of Vedas and Puranas.<BR>	 f. (-पा) Ten-<BR>derness, compassionateness f. (-पी) The wife of the sage DRONA. E.<BR>कृप् to be able, &c. अङ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=200-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृपण|कृपणः
कृपण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>	 1. Miserly, avaricious.<BR>	 2. Low, vile.<BR>	 3. Poor,<BR>feeble, miserable, pitiable.<BR>	 m. (णः) A worm.<BR> E. कृप् to be able, क्वुन्<BR>or ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=200-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृपाण|कृपाणः
कृपाण m. (-णः) A sword, a scymitar or sacrificial knife.<BR>	 f. (-णी)<BR>	 1. A<BR>knife.<BR>	 2. A shears or scissors.<BR>	 3. A dagger.<BR> E. कृपा mercy, नुद् to<BR>destroy, ड aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=200-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृपाणक|कृपाणकः
कृपाणक m. (-कः) A sword, a scymitar: see the preceding.<BR> E. कन् added<BR>to कृपाण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=200-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृपाणिका
कृपाणिका f. (-का) A knife.<BR> E. कन् added to कृपाण, and the fem. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=200-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृपाद्वैत|कृपाद्वैतः
कृपाद्वैत m. (-तः) One of the Buddhas or deified saints of the Buddhas.<BR>E. कृपा compassion, and अद्वैत not second; unequalled for tender-<BR>ness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=200-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृपालु|कृपालुः
कृपालु mfn. (-लुः-लुः-लु) Compassionate, tender.<BR> E. कृपा tenderness, आलुक्<BR>aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=200-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृपामय
कृपामय mfn. (-यः-यी-यं) Compassionate; so कृपावत् (-वान्-वती-वत्) कृपान्वित<BR>(-तः-ता-तं) &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=200-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृपाहीन
कृपाहीन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Unfeeling, unkind, hardhearted.<BR> E. कृपा, हीन<BR>devoid of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=200-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृपीट|कृपीटं
कृपीट n. (-टं)<BR>	 1. The belly.<BR>	 2. Water.<BR>	 3. A wood, a forest.<BR>	 4. Wood,<BR>timber.<BR> E. कृप् to be able, कीटन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=200-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृपीटपाल|कृपीटपालः
कृपीटपाल m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. The ocean.<BR>	 2. A rudder or large oar used as one.<BR>3. Air, wind.<BR> E. कृपीट water, पाल what preserves, &c. अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=201-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृपीटयोनि|कृपीटयोनिः
कृपीटयोनि m. (-निः) Fire.<BR> E. कृपीट water, योनि source, place of origin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=201-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृपीपति|कृपीपतिः
कृपीपति m. (-तिः) A name of DRONĀCHĀRYA.<BR> E. कृपी the wife of the sage,<BR>and पति master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=201-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृपीपुत्र
कृपीपुत्र m. (-त्रः) ASWATTHAMA a sage, the son of KRIPI and DRONA. E.<BR>कृपी, and पुत्र a son, or with other synonyms of a son, as कृपीसुत, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=201-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृव
कृव r. 1st cl. or 5th cl. (इ) कृवि (कृणोति) 1. To kill, to hurt or injure in<BR>any way.<BR>	 2. To act, to do.<BR>	 3. To go, to move.<BR>	 4. To be in pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=201-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृमि|कृमिः
कृमि m. (-मिः)<BR>	 1. A worm, an insect in general.<BR>	 2. Lac, the red dye,<BR>which is in fact an insect.<BR>	 3. An Asura or demon.<BR>	 4. One subject to<BR>worms.<BR> E. क्रम् to go, इन् Uṇādi affix, and the corresponding vowel<BR>substituted for र; also क्रिमि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=201-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृमिकण्टक|कृमिकण्टकं
कृमिकण्टक n. (-कं)<BR>	 1. A plant used in medicine: see विडङ्ग.<BR>	 2. Opposite<BR>leaved fig tree.<BR>	 3. A plant, (Salvinia cucullata:) see मूषिकपर्णी. E.<BR>कृमि a worm, and कण्टक a thorn, a foe; also क्रिमिकण्ठक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=201-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृमिकर्ण|कृमिकर्णः|कृमिकर्ण्ण
कृमिकर्ण m. (-र्णः) Worms or lice generating in the external ear.<BR> E. कृमि,<BR>and कर्ण the ear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=201-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृमिकोशोत्थ
कृमिकोशोत्थ mfn. (-त्थः-त्था-त्थं) Silken, silk.<BR> E. कृमि a worm, कोश a ball,<BR>and उत्थ what comes or rises from.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=201-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृमिग्रन्थि|कृमिग्रन्थिः
कृमिग्रन्थि m. (-न्थिः) Insects generated at the roots of the eyelashes.<BR> E. कृमि<BR>and ग्रन्थि a joint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=201-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृमिघ्न|कृमिघ्नः
कृमिघ्न mfn. (-घ्नः-घ्नी-घ्नं) Vermifuge, anthelmintic.<BR>	 m. (-घ्नः)<BR>	 1. A shrub<BR>used in medicine, as an anthelmintic, commonly Biranga, (Erycibe<BR>paniculata, Rox.) See विडङ्ग.<BR>	 2. The onion.<BR>	 3. The root of the ju-<BR>jube.<BR>	 4. The marking nut plant.<BR>	 f. (-घ्नी) Turmeric.<BR> E. कृमि a worm,<BR>हन् to kill, and ठक् affix; also क्रिमिघ्न.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=201-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृमिज|कृमिजं
कृमिज n. (-जं) Agallochum; see कृमिज.<BR>	 f. (-जा) Lac, a red dye so called.<BR>E. कृमि an insect, and ज born, produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=201-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृमिदन्तक|कृमिदन्तकः
कृमिदन्तक m. (-कः) Toothache with decay of the teeth,<BR> E. कृमि, and दन्त a<BR>tooth, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=201-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृमिन्
कृमिन् mfn. (-मी-मिनी-मि) Affected with worms.<BR> E. कृमि, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=201-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृमिरिपु|कृमिरिपुः
कृमिरिपु m. (-पुः) An anthelmintic plant: see कृमिघ्न.<BR> E. कृमि, and रिपु an<BR>enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=201-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृमिल
कृमिल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Having worms, wormy.<BR>	 f. (-ला) A fruitful woman,<BR>one bearing many children.<BR> E. कृमि a worm, and ला to receive, to<BR>get, affix ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=201-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृमिशङ्ख|कृमिशंख|कृमिशङ्खः
कृमिशङ्ख m. (-ङ्खः) The fish of the conch.<BR> E. कृमि a worm, and शङ्ख a shell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=201-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृमिशुक्ति|कृमिशुक्तिः
कृमिशुक्ति f. (-क्तिः) An oyster.<BR> E. कृमि an insect, and शुक्ति oyster-shell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=201-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृमिशैल|कृमिशैलः
कृमिशैल m. (-लः) An ant or mole hill.<BR> E. कृमि a worm, and शैल a hill;<BR>also with कन् added, कृमिशैलक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=201-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृमिहर
कृमिहर mfn. (-रः-री-रं) Anthelmintic, vermifuge.<BR> E. कृमि, and हर what<BR>removes; so कृमिहन्तृ (-न्ता-न्त्री-न्तृ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=201-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृमीलक|कृमीलकः
कृमीलक m. (-कः) A wild sort of kidney bean: see वनमुद्ग.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=201-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृवि|कृविः
कृवि r. 5th cl. (कृविणोति) To want to hurt or kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=201-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृवि|कृविः
कृवि m. (-विः) A loom.<BR> E. कृ to make, (cloth,) and क्विन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=201-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृश|कृशः
कृश r. 4th cl. (इर) कृशिर (कृश्यति) To make thin or small.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=201-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृश|कृशः
कृश mfn. (-शः-शा-शं)<BR>	 1. Small, thin, tittle, minute.<BR>	 2. Thin, spare,<BR>emaciated.<BR>	 3. Weak, feeble.<BR> E. कृश् to pare or make thin, क्त affix,<BR>deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=201-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृशता
कृशता f. (-ता) Leanness, thinness.<BR> E. तल् added to the last; also with<BR>त्व, कृशत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=201-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृशर|कृशरः
कृशर mf. (-रः-रा)<BR>	 1. A dish composed of milk, sesamum, and rise.<BR>	 2.<BR>Rice and pease boiled together with a few spices, commonly<BR>Khichree: also कृसर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=201-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृशला
कृशला f. (-ला) The hair of the head.<BR> E. कृश minute, ल what receives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=201-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृशाकु
कृशाकु m. (-कुः)<BR>	 1. Heating.<BR>	 2. Grieving.<BR> E. कृश् to make small, and काकु<BR>aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=201-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृशाक्ष|कृशाक्षः
कृशाक्ष m. (-क्षः) A spider.<BR> E. कृश, अक्षि eye, टच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=201-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृशाङ्ग|कृशाङ्गः
कृशाङ्ग mfn. (-ङ्गः-ङ्गी-ङ्गं) Spare, thin, emaciate.<BR>	 f. (-ङ्गी)<BR>	 1. A woman with<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=201-b" target="_blank">Page201-b+ 60</a>]<BR>a slender shape.<BR>	 2. A plant, commonly Priyangu: see प्रियङ्गु<BR> E. कृश<BR>thin, अङ्ग the body, अण् and ङीष् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=201-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृशानु|कृशानुः
कृशानु m. (-नुः)<BR>	 1. A name of fire 2. A plant, (Plumbago zeylanica.) E.<BR>कृश् to make thin, आनुक Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=201-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृशानुरेतस्
कृशानुरेतस् m. (-ताः) A name of ŚIVA<BR> E. कृशानु fire, and रेतस् semen virile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=201-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृशाश्व
कृशाश्व m. (-श्वः) The name of a sage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=201-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृशाश्विन्
कृशाश्विन् m. (-श्वी) A dancer, an actor, a tumbler.<BR> E. कृशाश्व the name of a<BR>saint, the author of directions to players, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=201-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष
कृष r. 1st. cl. (आ) औकृश (कर्षति) and 6th cl (कृषति-ते)<BR>	 1. To draw or make<BR>furrows.<BR>	 2. To plough. With अप, 1. To draw down.<BR>	 2. To debase.<BR>	 3.<BR>To disregard. with अव, 1. To draw out or off.<BR>	 2. To disregard or<BR>contemn. With आङ्, To attract, to draw to. With उत्, 1. To raise,<BR>to draw up.<BR>	 2. To raise, to excite, to make high, proud, loud, &c.<BR>With सम्, To draw together. With सम and नि, To bring near or<BR>close to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=201-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृषक|कृषकः
कृषक mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>	 1. What or who makes furrows or ploughs.<BR>	 2.<BR>Attractive, attrahent.<BR>	 m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. The plough-share.<BR>	 2. A husband-<BR>man, a peasant. कृष् to plough, &c. Uṇādi affix, क्वन्; also कृषिक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=201-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृषाण|कृषाणः
कृषाण m. (-णः) A husbandman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=201-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृषाणु|कृषाणुः
कृषाणु m. (-णुः) A name of fire: see कृशानु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=201-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृषि|कृषिः
कृषि f. (-षिः)<BR>	 1. Husbandry, agriculture.<BR>	 2. Ploughing, cultivating the<BR>soil, &c.<BR> E. कृष् to plough, इक् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=201-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृषिक|कृषिकः
कृषिक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. The plough-share.<BR>	 2. A husband-man a cultivator. E.<BR>कृष् to plough, Uṇādi affix किकन्; also कृषक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=201-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृषिजीविन्
कृषिजीविन् m. (-वी) A cultivator, a farmer.<BR> E. कृषि, and जीविन् who lives by.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=201-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृषिफल
कृषिफल n. (-लं) Agricultural produce or profit.<BR> E. कृषि, and फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=201-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृषीबल
कृषीबल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) One who lives by agriculture, &c.<BR>	 m. (-लः) A<BR>husband-man.<BR> E. कृषि agriculture, बलच् affix, and इ made ई.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=201-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्कर|कृष्करः
कृष्कर m. (-रः) An appellation of ŚIVA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=201-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्ट|कृष्टं
कृष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं) Ploughed or tilled, a field, &c.<BR> E. कृष् to plough,<BR>affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=201-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्टपच्य|कृष्टपच्यः
कृष्टपच्य mfn. (-च्यः-च्या-च्यं) Sown or ripening after ploughing. (rice, &c.)<BR>E. कृष्ट ploughed, पच् to ripen, and क्यप् affix; in some places the<BR>grain is sown without previous ploughing, whence it is called<BR>अकृष्टपच्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=201-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्टपाक्य|कृष्टपाक्यं
कृष्टपाक्य mfn. (-क्यः-क्या-क्यं) Sown or rather ripening after ploughing: see<BR>कृष्टपच्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=201-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्टि|कृष्टिः
कृष्टि m. (ष्टिः) A teacher, a learned man or Pandit.<BR>	 f. (-ष्टिः) ploughing,<BR>cultivating the soil.<BR>	 2. Attracting, drawing.<BR> E. कृष् to plough, to<BR>trace, ति or क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=201-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णंश्रित
कृष्णंश्रित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Devoted to Krishna.<BR> E. कृष्णं second case, श्रित<BR>serving; also कृष्णश्रित.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=201-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्ण|कृष्णं|कृष्णः
कृष्ण mfn. (-ष्णः-ष्णा-ष्णं) Black or dark blue.<BR>	 m. (-ष्णः)<BR>	 1. Black, the colour,<BR>or dark blue, which is often confounded with it by the Hindus.<BR>	 2.<BR>KṚṢṆA, the most celebrated form of VIṢṆU, or rather VIṢṆU<BR>himself; he is distinct from the ten Avatars or incarnations, be-<BR>ing identified with the deity.<BR>	 3. VYASA, a sage, the compiler of<BR>the Vedas.<BR>	 4. A name of ARJUNA.<BR>	 5. The Kokila or Indian cuckoo<BR>6. A crow.<BR>	 7. A fruit, Karonda or Karinda, (Carissa carondas.)<BR>	 8.<BR>The dark half of the lunar month from full to new moon.<BR>	 n. (-ष्णं)<BR>1. Black pepper.<BR>	 2. Iron.<BR>	 3. Blue vitriol.<BR>	 4. Black agallochum.<BR>	 f.<BR>(-ष्णा)<BR>	 1. name of DRAUPADI wife of the PANDAVAS.<BR>	 2. The indigo<BR>plant 3. Long pepper.<BR>	 4. A grape.<BR>	 5. A drug, commonly Kakoli.<BR>	 6.<BR>Kalonji, (Nigella Indica:) see कृष्णजीरक.<BR>	 7. Black mustard, (the<BR>name is applied to other vegetable substances of a dark colour.)<BR>	 8.<BR>The Krishna river in the Deccan.<BR>	 9. A black leech, considered<BR>poisonous.<BR> E. कृष् to attract. as the minds of men, &c नक् Uṇādi<BR>affix; (this is applied to KṚṢṆA, &c.) else, कृष् to tinge, affix the<BR>same; again कृष्ण black, &c. and अच् affix, fem. affix टाप.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=201-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णकन्द|कृष्णकंद|कृष्णकन्दं
कृष्णकन्द n. (-न्दः) The red lotus, (Nymphæa rubra.)<BR> E. कृण black, and कन्द stalk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=201-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णकर्म्मन्|कृष्णकर्मन्
कृष्णकर्म्मन् mfn. (-र्म्मा-र्म्मा-र्म्म) Criminal, guilty.<BR>	 n. (-र्म्म)<BR>	 1. Making black.<BR>	 2.<BR>Cauterising.<BR> E. कृष्ण black. and कर्म्मन् action.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=202-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णकाक|कृष्णकाकः
कृष्णकाक m. (-कः) A raven.<BR> E. कृष्ण black, and काक a crow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=202-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णकाष्ठ|कृष्णकाष्ठं
कृष्णकाष्ठ n. (-ष्ठं) A black variety of agallochum.<BR> E. कृष्ण, and काष्ठ<BR>wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=202-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णकेलि|कृष्णकेलिः
कृष्णकेलि m. (-लिः) A plant, (Mirabilis jalapa.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=202-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णकोहल|कृष्णकोहलः
कृष्णकोहल m. (-लः) A gamester, a gambler.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=202-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णचतुर्दशी|कृष्णचतुर्द्दशी
कृष्णचतुर्दशी f. (-शी) The fourteenth day in the dark half of a month. E.<BR>कृष्ण dark, चतुर्दशी fourteenth; it is the day preceding new moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=202-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णचर|कृष्णचरः
कृष्णचर mfn. (-रः-री-रं) Formerly or in a former existence, KṚṢṆA. E.<BR>कृष्ण, and चरट् affix, implying former state of being; also कृष्णरुप्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=202-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णचूडा
कृष्णचूडा f. (-डा) A shrub, (Poinciana pulcherrima.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=202-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णचूर्ण|कृष्णचूर्णं|कृष्णचूर्ण्ण
कृष्णचूर्ण n. (-र्ण) Rust of iron, iron filings<BR> E. कृष्ण black, and चूर्ण powder,<BR>dust.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=202-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णजटा
कृष्णजटा f. (-टा) Indian spikenard: see जटामांसी.<BR> E. कृष्ण black, जटा twis-<BR>ted hair, to which its entangled stalks are compared.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=202-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णजीरक|कृष्णजीरकः
कृष्णजीरक m. (-कः) Kalongi, a plant having a small black seed, which<BR>is used for medical and culinary purposes, (Nigella Indica, Rox.)<BR>E. कृष्ण black, and जीरक cummin seed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=202-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णता
कृष्णता f. (-ता) Blackness.<BR> E. तल् added to कृष्ण; with त्व, कृष्णत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=202-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णताम्र|कृष्णताम्रं
कृष्णताम्र n. (-म्रं) A kind of Sandal wood.<BR> E. कृष्ण, and ताम्र copper, of a<BR>dusky copper hue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=202-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णतार|कृष्णतारः
कृष्णतार m. (-रः) A deer, an antelope.<BR> E. कृष्ण black, and तार the pupil of<BR>the eye, black-eyed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=202-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णत्रिवृता
कृष्णत्रिवृता f. (-ता) A plant, black Teori: see त्रिवृता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=202-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णदशन
कृष्णदशन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Having bad or discoloured teeth.<BR> E. कृष्ण, and<BR>दशन a tooth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=202-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णदेह|कृष्णदेहः
कृष्णदेह mfn. (-हः-हा-हं) Black-bodied.<BR>	 m. (-हः) A large black bee.<BR> E. कृष्ण<BR>black, and देह the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=202-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णद्वैपायन|कृष्णद्वैपायनः
कृष्णद्वैपायन m. (-नः) A name of VYASA, the compiler of the Vedas, and<BR>Puranas. E. A compound of two other names of the sage: see कृष्ण,<BR>and द्वैपायन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=202-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णधत्तूर
कृष्णधत्तूर m. (-रः) A dark species of Dhatura or thron apple, (Dhatura<BR>fastuosa:) see धत्तूर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=202-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णपक्ष|कृष्णपक्षः
कृष्णपक्ष m. (-क्षः) The dark half of a month, the fifteen days during<BR>which the moon is in the wane.<BR> E. कृष्ण dark, and पक्ष fortnight or<BR>half month.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=202-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णपाक|कृष्णपाकः
कृष्णपाक m. (-कः) A tree bearing a small fruit, which when ripe, is of a<BR>black colour, commonly Carinda or karonda, (Carissa carondas) E.<BR>कृष्ण black and पाक what is ripe, from पच् to ripen, to cook, and<BR>घञ् affix; also कृष्णफल, and कृष्णपाकफल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=202-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णपाकफल|कृष्णपाकफलः
कृष्णपाकफल m. (-लः) The Karonda: see the preceding.<BR> E. फल fruit,<BR>added to कृष्णपाक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=202-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णपिङ्गला
कृष्णपिङ्गला f. (-ला) A name of DURGĀ.<BR> E. कृष्ण black, and पिङ्गल tawny;<BR>being of such a colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=202-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णपिण्डीतक|कृष्णपिण्डीतकः
कृष्णपिण्डीतक m. (-कः) A dark kind of Mayana, (Vangueria spinosa.) E.<BR>कृष्ण black, and पिण्डीतक the Mayan or Mayana tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=202-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णपिण्डीर|कृष्णपिण्डीरः
कृष्णपिण्डीर m. (-रः) A dark kind of Mayana: see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=202-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णपिपीली
कृष्णपिपीली f. (-ली) The black ant.<BR> E. कृष्ण, and पिपीली an ant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=202-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णपुष्प|कृष्णपुष्पः
कृष्णपुष्प m. (-ष्पः) A black kind of Dhatura.<BR>	 f. (-ष्पी) Another plant: see<BR>प्रियङ्गु<BR> E. कृष्ण black and पुष्प a flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=202-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णफल|कृष्णफलः
कृष्णफल m. (-लः) A fruit tree, the Karinda: see कृष्णपाक. (ला) A shrub,<BR>(Serratula anthelmintica:) see सोमराजी.<BR> E. कृष्ण black, and फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=202-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णफलपाक|कृष्णफलपाकः
कृष्णफलपाक m. (-कः) A fruit: see the preceding; also कृष्णपाकफल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=202-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णभूमि
कृष्णभूमि f. (-मिः) A country with a dark soil, one of mould, blue clay,<BR>&c.<BR> E. कृष्ण black, and भूमि earth; also with a final अ, कृष्णभूमः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=202-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णभूमिजा
कृष्णभूमिजा f. (-जा) A species of grass, described as a nourishing food<BR>for cattle.<BR> E. कृष्णभूमि black earth, and ज born, produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=202-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णभेदी
कृष्णभेदी f. (-दी) A medicinal plant: see कटुकी.<BR> E. कृष्ण black, hence, dirt<BR>or excrement, and भेदी what breaks, or dissipates.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=202-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णमुद्ग|कृष्णमुद्गः
कृष्णमुद्ग m. (-द्गः) A sort of pulse, (Phaseolus max.)<BR> E. कृष्ण black, मुद्ग<BR>phaseolus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=202-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णमृत्
कृष्णमृत् f. (-मृत्) A country with a soil of a dark colour.<BR> E. कृष्ण black,<BR>and मृत् earth: see कृष्णभूमि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=202-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णमृत्तिका
कृष्णमृत्तिका f. (-का) See the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=202-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णरूप्य|कृष्णरूप्यः
कृष्णरूप्य mfn. (-प्यः-प्या-प्यं) Formerly KṚṢṆA: see कृष्णचर.<BR> E. कृष्ण, and<BR>रूप्य affix, implying past state of being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=202-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णलवण|कृष्णलवणं
कृष्णलवण n. (-णं) A factitious salt, either that prepared by evaporation<BR>from saline soil, or the medicinal kind, called Bit Laban or Bit<BR>Naban, a muriate of soda with a proportion of sulphur and iron.<BR>E. कृष्ण black, and लवण salt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=202-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णल|कृष्णलः
कृष्णल m. (-लः) A Retti, a weight, the berry so used; or an artificial<BR>weight derived from it, the berry averaging about 1 (1/4) grain, the<BR>weight 2 3-16 grains.<BR>	 f. (-ला) A shrub bearing a small black and<BR>red berry, the Ratti or Gunza: see गुञ्जा.<BR> E. कृष्ण blackness, and ल<BR>what gets, from ला to obtain, affix ड and fem. affix टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=202-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णलक|कृष्णलकः
कृष्णलक m. (-कः) A Ratti, the jeweller's weight, the fifth of a Masha.<BR>E. कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=202-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णलोह|कृष्णलोहं|कृष्णलोहः
कृष्णलोह n. (-हं) The loadstone.<BR> E. कृष्ण what attracts, and लोह iron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=202-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णलोहित|कृष्णलोहितः
कृष्णलोहित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Of a purple colour.<BR> E. कृष्ण black, and लोहित<BR>red; of which two colours purple is supposed to consist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=202-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णवक्त्र|कृष्णवक्त्रः
कृष्णवक्त्र m. (-क्त्र) The black faced monkey.<BR> E. कृष्ण black, and वक्त्र the<BR>face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=202-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णवर्ण|कृष्णवर्णः|कृष्णवर्ण्ण
कृष्णवर्ण mfn. (-र्ण-र्णा-र्णं)<BR>	 1. Black or dark blue, A SUDRA.<BR>	 2. A name of<BR>RAHU n, (-र्णं) The colour black.<BR> E. कृष्ण and वर्ण colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=202-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णवर्त्मन
कृष्णवर्त्मन m. (-र्त्मा)<BR>	 1. Fire.<BR>	 2. RAHU or the personified ascending noda.<BR>3. A low man, an outcaste, a profligate, a blackguard.<BR>	 4. The<BR>marking nut plant.<BR> E. कृष्ण black, and वर्त्मन् a path or way; whose<BR>way is darkness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=202-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णवल्ली
कृष्णवल्ली f. (-ल्ली) A plant, a dark kind of Babul, (Ocymum pilosum.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=202-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णवानर|कृष्णवानरः
कृष्णवानर m. (-रः) A black monkey.<BR> E. कृष्ण black, and वानर an ape.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=202-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णवीज|कृष्णवीजं|कृष्णवीजः
कृष्णवीज m. (-जः) A red variety of the Morunga: see रक्तशीग्र.<BR> E. कृष्ण<BR>black, वीज the seed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=202-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णवृन्ता
कृष्णवृन्ता f. (-न्ता)<BR>	 1. The trumpet flower, (Bignonia suave-olens.)<BR>	 2. A<BR>leguminous plant, (Glycine debilis.)<BR> E. कृष्ण black, and वृन्त foot-<BR>stalk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=202-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णवृन्तिका
कृष्णवृन्तिका f. (-का) A tree, (Gmelina arborea:) see गम्भारी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=202-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णशार|कृष्णशारः
कृष्णशार m. (-रः) The black antelope: see कृष्णसार.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=202-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णशालि|कृष्णशालिः
कृष्णशालि m. (-लिः) A sort of rice of a dark colour.<BR> E. कृष्ण, and शालि rice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=202-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णशिम्बी
कृष्णशिम्बी f. (-म्बी) A sort of bean, (Dolichos virosus.)<BR> E. कृष्ण, and शिम्बी<BR>a Dolichos.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=202-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णशृङ्ग|कृष्णशृंग|कृष्णशृङ्गः
कृष्णशृङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः) A buffalo.<BR> E. कृष्ण black, and शृङ्ग a horn, black horned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=202-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णश्रित
कृष्णश्रित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Worshipping or devoted to KRISNA.<BR> E. कृष्ण,<BR>and श्रित attached.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=202-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णसख|कृष्णसखः
कृष्णसख m. (-खः) A friend or follower of KṚṢṆA, especially ARJUNA<BR>E. कृष्ण, and सखि a friend, टच् affix in this class of compounds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=202-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णसखि
कृष्णसखि f. (-खी) Cummin-seed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=202-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णसर्प
कृष्णसर्प m. (-र्पः) A black snake.<BR> E. कृष्ण, and सर्प a snake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=202-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णसर्षप|कृष्णसर्षपः
कृष्णसर्षप m. (-पः) Black mustard.<BR> E. कृष्ण, and सर्षप mustard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=202-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णसार|कृष्णसारः
कृष्णसार mf. (-रः-रा) A timber tree, Sisu, (Dalbergia Sisu, Rox.)<BR>	 m.<BR>(-रः)<BR>	 1. The black antelope.<BR>	 2. Khayar, (Mimosa catechu.)<BR>	 3. A<BR>thorny plant, (Euphorbia tirucalli, &c.)<BR> E. कृष्ण black, and सार<BR>essence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=202-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णसारङ्ग|कृष्णसारङ्गः
कृष्णसारङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः) The black antelope.<BR> E. कृष्ण black, and सारङ्ग a deer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=202-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णसारथि|कृष्णसारथिः
कृष्णसारथि m. (-थिः) ARJUNA.<BR> E. कृष्ण, and सारथि charioteer, driven by<BR>KṚṢṆA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=202-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णस्कन्ध|कृष्णस्कन्धः
कृष्णस्कन्ध m. (-न्धः) A tree which bears black blossoms, the Tamala tree.<BR>E. कृष्ण black, and स्कन्ध the shoulder: see कालस्कन्ध.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=202-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णागुरु
कृष्णागुरु n. (-रुः) Agallochum or aloe wood, the black variety.<BR> E. कृष्ण,<BR>and अगुरु aloe wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=202-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णाचल|कृष्णाचलः
कृष्णाचल m. (-लः) The mountain Raivata, part of the western portion<BR>of the Vindhya chain; it is also one of the nine principal moun-<BR>tains. that separate the same divisions or Varṣas of the known<BR>world.<BR> E. कृष्ण black, and अचल a mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=203-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णानदी
कृष्णानदी f. (-दी) The name of a river, possibly the Krishna in the<BR>Deccan.<BR> E. कृष्ण and नदी a river, river of KṚṢṆA; also other<BR>analogous names, as कृष्णसमुद्भवा, कृष्णवेण्या, कृष्णगङ्गा &c; also कृष्णा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=203-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णामिष|कृष्णामिषं
कृष्णामिष n. (-षं) Iron.<BR> E. कृष्ण black, and आमिष flesh substance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=203-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णायस|कृष्णायसं
कृष्णायस n. (-सं) Iron, crude or black iron.<BR> E. कृष्ण black, and अयस iron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=203-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णार्च्चिस्|कृष्णार्चिस्
कृष्णार्च्चिस् m. (-र्च्चिः) A name of fire.<BR> E. कृष्ण black, and अर्च्चिस् flame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=203-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णार्जक|कृष्णार्जकः
कृष्णार्जक m. (-कः) A black species of basil: see कृष्णवल्ली<BR> E. कृष्ण black,<BR>and अर्जक basil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=203-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृणावास
कृणावास m. (-सः) The holy fig tree, (Ficus religiosa.)<BR> E. कृष्ण the deity,<BR>and आवास abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=203-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णाश्रित|कृष्णाश्रितः
कृष्णाश्रित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Devoted to or the votary of KṚṢṆA.<BR> E. कृष्ण<BR>and आश्रित attached or devoted to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=203-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णिका
कृष्णिका f. (-का) Black mustard.<BR> E. कृष्ण black, कन् affix, the fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=203-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णिमन्
कृष्णिमन् m. (-मा) Blackness.<BR> E. कृष्ण and इमनिच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=203-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णीकरण|कृष्णीकरणं
कृष्णीकरण n. (-णं) Blackening, making black.<BR> E. कृष्ण and करण making,<BR>च्वि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=203-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णीकृत
कृष्णीकृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Blackened, made black.<BR> E. कृष्ण, कृत made, च्वि<BR>augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=203-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णीभूत
कृष्णीभूत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Being or become black, &c.<BR> E. कृष्ण भूत become<BR>च्वि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=203-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णेक्षु|कृष्णेक्षुः
कृष्णेक्षु m. (-क्षुः) A sort of sugar cane.<BR> E. कृष्ण black, and इक्षु sugar cane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=203-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृसर|कृसरः
कृसर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A dish consisting of sesamum and grain.<BR>	 2. A mix-<BR>ture of rice and peas with a few spices.<BR> E. कॄ to scatter, सर Uṇādi<BR>affix; also कृशर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=203-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कॄ
कॄ r. 6th cl. (किरति) To throw, to scatter. r. 9th cl. (कृणाति) or (गि, ञ)<BR>गिकॄञ् (कृणाति-कृणीते) To hurt, to injure, r. 10th cl. (कारयते) To<BR>know. With अप prefixed, To draw furrows, to make lines.<BR>	 1.<BR>To disperse.<BR>	 2. With अव, To throw, to cast.<BR>	 3. With आङ्, To fill<BR>up. to cover over.<BR>	 4. With प्रति, To hurt, to injure.<BR>	 5. With वि. To<BR>throw, to cast, to send, to scatter widely.<BR>	 6. With सम, To gather,<BR>to collect.<BR>	 7. With अभि in the passive voice, to be upset, over-<BR>come, or overwhelmed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=203-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कॄत
कॄत r. 10th cl. (कीर्त्तयति) To celebrate, to glorify. to render renowned<BR>or notorious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=203-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कॢप्त|कॢप्तः
कॢप्त mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं)<BR>	 1. Made, formed.<BR>	 2. Fixed, appointed.<BR>	 3. Ascertai-<BR>ned, determined.<BR>	 4. Cut, pared, shorn.<BR> E. कृप् to be able. &c. affix<BR>क्त, and the augment इट् omitted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=203-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कॢप्तकीला
कॢप्तकीला f. (-ला) A Tittle-deed, a lease of a house, a document &c. E.<BR>कॢप्त fixed, कील a bolt or pin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=203-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कॢप्तधूप|कॢप्तधूपः
कॢप्तधूप m. (-पः) Frankincense, olibanum.<BR> E. कॢप्त made, धूप incense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=203-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कॢप्तिक|कॢप्तिकः
कॢप्तिक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Bought, purchased.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=203-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केकय|केकयः
केकय m. (-यः) A prince of the lunar race.<BR>	 f. (-यी) daughter of the prece-<BR>ding and one of the wives of DAŚARATHA: the mother of<BR>BHARATA: see केकेयी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=203-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केकर|केकरः
केकर mfn. (-रः-री-रं) Squint-eyed.<BR> E. के in the head. कृ to make, टच्<BR>affix; also compounded with अक्ष an eye, as केकराक्ष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=203-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केकल
केकल m. (-लः) A dancer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=203-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केका
केका f. (-का) The cry of a peacock.<BR> E. के an imitative sound and क<BR>what sounds, from कै to sound, affixes ड and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=203-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केकाबल|केकाबलः
केकाबल m. (-लः) A peacock.<BR> E. केका his cry, and बलच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=203-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केकिन्
केकिन् m. (-की) A peacock.<BR> E. केका the cry of the bird, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=203-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केकेयी
केकेयी f. (-यी) One of DASARAT'HA'S three wives, the mother of<BR>BHARATA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=203-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केचन
केचन ind. Some, some or certain persons.<BR> E. के plural of किम्, and<BR>चन aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=203-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केचित्
केचित् ind. Some, some persons. E. See the last; चिति aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=203-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केचुक|केचुकं
केचुक m. (-कः) An esculent root, (Arum colocasia:) see कचु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=203-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केणिका
केणिका f. (-का) A tent.<BR> E. किण् to cover (a Sautra root), ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=203-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केत|केतः
केत r. 10th cl. (केतयति)<BR>	 1. To call or invite.<BR>	 2. To counsel or advise;<BR>some authorities substitute सङ्केत for this root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=203-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केत|केतः
केत m. (-तः) A house, an abode.<BR> E. कित् to abide, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=203-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केतक|केतकः
केतक mf. (-कः-की) A fragrant plant, (Pandanus odoratissimus.)<BR> E. किति<BR>to abide, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=203-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केतन|केतनं
केतन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. A flag, a banner.<BR>	 2. Business, indispensable act.<BR>	 3.<BR>Invitation.<BR>	 4. A spot or mark, a sign, a symbol.<BR>	 5. A house, an<BR>abode.<BR>	 6. Place, site, situation. &c.<BR> E. कित् to abide, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=203-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केतित
केतित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Called, summoned.<BR>	 2. Dwelt, inhabited.<BR> E. केत्<BR>to call, or कित् to dwell, क्त affix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=203-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केतु|केतुः
केतु m. (-तुः) KETU the dragon's tail or descending node; in astronomy,<BR>the ninth of the planets; in mythology, a demon: the body of<BR>SAINHIKEYA severed from the head (RAHU), by VIṢṆU, at the<BR>churning of the ocean, but immortal, by having tasted the Amrita.<BR>2. A banner, a flag.<BR>	 3. A mark, a sign, a symbol, &c.<BR>	 4. Light.<BR>5. A comet, falling star, &c.<BR>	 6. Disease.<BR>	 7. A pigmy race inhabit-<BR>ing Kusa Dwipa, the progeny of JAIMINI.<BR> E. चाय् to worship, तु<BR>Uṇādi affix, कि substituted for the root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=203-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केतुतारा
केतुतारा f. (-रा) A comet.<BR> E. केतु, and तारा a star.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=203-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केतुभ|केतुभः
केतुभ m. (-भः) A cloud.<BR> E. केतु the plant, and भ what resembles it in<BR>darkness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=203-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केतुमाल|केतुमालं|केतुमालः
केतुमाल n. (-लं) One of nine great divisions of the known world, the<BR>western portion or Varṣa of Jambu Dwipa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=203-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केतुयष्टि|केतुयष्टिः
केतुयष्टि f. (-ष्टिः) A flag-staff<BR> E. केतु, and यष्टि a stick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=203-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केतुरत्न|केतुरत्नं
केतुरत्न n. (-त्नं) Lapis lazuli.<BR> E. केतु, and रत्न a gem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=203-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केतुवसन
केतुवसन m. (-नः) A flag.<BR> E. केतु a standard, and वसन cloth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=203-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केदर|केदरः
केदर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Squint-eyed.<BR>	 m. (-रः) The name of a plant.<BR> E. क<BR>the earth or the head, दृ to divide, affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=203-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केदार|केदारः
केदार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A field, a meadow, a plain.<BR>	 2. A mountain.<BR>	 3. A name<BR>of ŚIVA.<BR>	 4. A particular place, the modern Kedar, part of the<BR>Himālaya mountains.<BR>	 5. A basin for water round the root of a<BR>tree.<BR>	 6. A bed in a garden or field.<BR> E. क water, earth, &c. दृ to<BR>tear or rend, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=203-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केदारखण्ड|केदारखंड
केदारखण्ड n. (-ण्डं) A small dyke or mound, earth raised to keep out<BR>water.<BR> E. केदार, and खण्ड a portion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=203-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केनार|केनारः
केनार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. The head.<BR>	 2. The temples, the upper part of the<BR>cheek.<BR>	 3. A joint.<BR>	 4. A division of hell, a hell like a potter's kiln.<BR>E. क the head, &c. नृ to guide, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=203-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केनिपात|केनिपातः
केनिपात m. (-तः) The helm, a rudder, a large oar used as one.<BR> E. क<BR>water, निपात who goes or falls; also केनिपातक m. (-कः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=203-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केन्दु|केन्दुः
केन्दु m. (-न्दुः) A sort of ebony, (Diospyros tomentosa, Rox.)<BR> E. क the<BR>earth, इन्द् to moisten, उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=203-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केन्दुक|केन्दुकः
केन्दुक m. (-कः) A sort of ebony, that yields a species of tar, (Diospyros<BR>glutinosa.)<BR> E. कन् implying resemblance, affixed to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=203-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केन्द्र|केंद्र|केंद्रं|केन्द्रं
केन्द्र n. (-न्द्रं)<BR>	 1. The centre of a circle.<BR>	 2. The argument of an equation.<BR>3. The distance of a planet from the first point of its orbit in the<BR>fourth, seventh, or tenth degree. (In astronomy.) It is variously<BR>applied in combination, as पतनकेन्द्रं argument of the latitude;<BR>द्वितीयकेन्द्रं the distance of the higher apsis from a planet in any<BR>point of its orbit; शीघ्रकेन्द्रं commutation, the distance of the sun<BR>from a superior planet or of an inferior planet from the sun;<BR>मन्दकेन्द्रं argument of anomaly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=203-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केप
केप r. 1st cl. (ऋ) केपृ (केपते) 1. To shake or tremble.<BR>	 2. To go, to move<BR>or approach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=203-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केयूर|केयूरं|केयूरः
केयूर n. (-रं) A bracelet worn on the upper arm.<BR> E. क the head, here<BR>implying the head of the arm, यु to join, ऊर aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=203-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केरल|केरलः
केरल m. (-लः) The appellation of a country, Keraladesha or the modern<BR>Malabar.<BR>	 f. (-ली)<BR>	 1. Astronomical science.<BR>	 2. Astronomical Sas-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=204-a" target="_blank">Page204-a+ 60</a>]<BR>tra or treatise.<BR>	 3. A Hora or period of time equal to about one<BR>hour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=203-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केल
केल r. 1st cl. (ऊ) केलू (केलति) 1. To shake.<BR>	 2. To go or move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=204-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केलक|केलकः
केलक m. (-कः) A dancer, a tumbler, one who walks or dances on the<BR>edge of a sword.<BR> E. किल् to sport, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=204-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केलास|केलासः
केलास m. (-सः) Crystal.<BR> E. के in water, लस् to shine, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=204-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केलि|केलिः
केलि mf. (-लिः-लिः or -ली) Play, sport, pastime, amusement.<BR>	 f. (-लिः)<BR>The earth.<BR> E. किल् to sport, Uṇādi affix इ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=204-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केलिक|केलिकः
केलिक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Sportive, sporting.<BR>	 m. (-कः) The Asoka tree. E.<BR>केलि and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=204-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केलिकला
केलिकला f. (-ला)<BR>	 1. The Vina or lute of SARASWATI.<BR>	 2. Amorous or<BR>sportive accent or address.<BR>	 3. Sportive skill, wantonness.<BR> E. केलि<BR>sport, कल् to sound, affix अङ् and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=204-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केलिकिल|केलिकिलः
केलिकिल m. (-लः) One of ŚIVA'S attendant demigods.<BR>	 2. The confiden-<BR>tial companion of the hero of a drama, in general a sort of<BR>buffoon.<BR>	 f. (-ला) A name of RATI the wife of KĀMADEVA.<BR> E. केलि<BR>sport, किल who plays, from किल् to sport, affix क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=204-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केलिकीर्ण|केलिकीर्णः|केलिकीर्ण्ण
केलिकीर्ण m. (-र्णः) A camel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=204-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केलिकुञ्चिका|केलिकुंचिका
केलिकुञ्चिका f. (-का) A wife's younger sister.<BR> E. केलि play, कुचि to be<BR>crooked, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=204-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केलिकोष|केलिकोषः
केलिकोष m. (-षः) An actor, a dancer or tumbler: see केलक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=204-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केलिगृह
केलिगृह n. (-हं) A pleasure house. a private apartment.<BR> E. केलि sport,<BR>and गृह a house; also केलिनिकेतन &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=204-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केलिनागर|केलिनागरः
केलिनागर m. (-रः) A sensualist, an enjoyer of worldly pleasures.<BR> E. केलि<BR>sport, and नागर a libertine, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=204-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केलिपर
केलिपर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Wanton, sportive.<BR> E. केलि, and पर intent on.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=204-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केलिमुख|केलिमुखः
केलिमुख m. (-खः) Pastime, sport.<BR> E. केलि play, and मुख chief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=204-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केलिवृक्ष|केलिवृक्षः
केलिवृक्ष m. (-क्षः) A species of the Kadamba, commonly Keli Kadamba,<BR>(Nauclea cordifolia.)<BR> E. केलि sport, and वृक्ष a tree; being abun-<BR>dant in the scene of KṚṢṆA'S sports with the Gopis.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=204-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केलिशयन
केलिशयन n. (-नं) A couch, a sofa.<BR> E. केलि, and शयन a bed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=204-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केलिशुषि|केलिशुषिः
केलिशुषि f. (-षिः) The earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=204-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केलिसचिव|केलिसचिवः
केलिसचिव m. (-वः) Minister of the sports, master of revels.<BR> E. केलि play<BR>सचिव a counsellor, a minister.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=204-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केव
केव r. 1st cl. (ऋ) केवृ (केवते) To serve.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=204-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केवर्त्त|केवर्त|केवर्तः|केवर्त्तः
केवर्त्त m. (-र्त्तः) A fisherman: see कैवर्त्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=204-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केवल|केवलं|केवलः
केवल mfn. (-लः-ला or -ली-लं)<BR>	 1. One, alone, only.<BR>	 2. All, entire, whole.<BR>m. (-लः) An envious or selfish man.<BR>	 n. adv. (-लं)<BR>	 1. Absolutely,<BR>certainly.<BR>	 2. Only, alone. Subst.<BR>	 3. A species of knowledge, that<BR>of the unity of spirit.<BR> E. केव् to sprinkle, कल aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=204-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केवलज्ञानिन्
केवलज्ञानिन् m. (-नी) One of the Jaina saints of the last age.<BR> E. केवल<BR>unity, and ज्ञानिन् who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=204-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केवलद्रव्य|केवलद्रव्यं
केवलद्रव्य n. (-व्यं) Black pepper.<BR> E. केवल one, only, द्रव्य thing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=204-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केवलवैयाकरण
केवलवैयाकरण m. (-णः) A grammarian, a mere grammarian, one not<BR>versed in any other science.<BR> E. केवल only, and वैयाकरण a grammari-<BR>an; also similar compounds, as केवलनैयायिक a mere logician, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=204-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केवलिन्
केवलिन् mfn. (-ली-लिनी-लि) One, only, alone.<BR>	 m. (-ली) A Jaina who has<BR>acquired holy knowledge.<BR> E. केवल one, इनि affix; a unitarian.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=204-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केविका
केविका f. (-का) The name of a flower, commonly Keber.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=204-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केश|केशः
केश m. (-शः)<BR>	 1. Hair.<BR>	 2. A name of VARUṆA.<BR>	 3. A kind of perfume:<BR>see वाला, 4. The name of a demon.<BR>	 5. A name of VIṢṆU.<BR>	 f. (-शो)<BR>1. A lock of hair on the crown of the head.<BR>	 2. The indigo plant<BR>3. Indian spikenard.<BR> E. क्लिश् to bind, अण् affix, and ल rejected;<BR>or क the head, and ईश् to rule, affix अच्; again, क water or hap-<BR>piness, and ईश the lord or master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=204-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केशक|केशकः
केशक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Skilful in dressing hair, taking pains with it,<BR>&c.<BR> E. केश and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=204-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केशकलाप|केशकलापः
केशकलाप m. (-पः) A quantity of hair.<BR> E. केश hair, and कलाप in this<BR>compound implying quantity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=204-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केशकार|केशकारः
केशकार m. (-रः) A sort of sugar cane.<BR> E. केश, and कार what makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=204-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केशकीट|केशकीटः
केशकीट m. (-टः) A louse.<BR> E. केश, and कीट an insect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=204-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केशगर्भ|केशगर्भः
केशगर्भ m. (-र्भः)<BR>	 1. A braid of hair 2. Varuna.<BR> E. केश, and गर्भ origin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=204-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केलगर्भक
केलगर्भक m. (-कः) A braid or tress of hair.<BR> E. केश hair, and गर्भक a<BR>chaplet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=204-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केशगृहीत
केशगृहीत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Pulled or seized by the hair.<BR> E. केश, and गृहीत<BR>seized.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=204-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केशग्रह|केशग्रहः
केशग्रह m. (-हः) Pulling the hair.<BR> E. केश, and ग्रह seizing; also केशग्रहणं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=204-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केशघ्न|केशघ्नं
केशघ्न n. (-घ्नं) Morbid baldness, falling of the hair.<BR> E. केश the hair, and<BR>घ्न what destroys, from हन् to injure, affix टच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=204-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केशच्छिद्
केशच्छिद् m. (च्छिद् or -च्छित्) A barber, a hair-dresser.<BR> E. केश the hair<BR>छिद् to cut, affix क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=204-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केशट|केशटः
केशट m. (-टः)<BR>	 1. A name of VIṢṆU.<BR>	 2. A goat.<BR>	 3. A louse.<BR>	 4. A broth-<BR>er.<BR>	 5. One of KAmA'S arrows.<BR>	 6. A tree, commonly Sonapat, (शोणक.)<BR>E. केश hair, अट् to go, affix अच्, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=204-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केशधृत्
केशधृत् m. (-धृत्) The root of sweet flag.<BR> E. केश hair, and धृ to hold, affix<BR>क्विप्; resembling hair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=204-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केशपक्ष|केशपक्षः
केशपक्ष m. (-क्षः) Much or ornamented hair.<BR> E. केश hair, पक्ष quantity, in<BR>this compound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=204-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केशपङ्क्ति
केशपङ्क्ति f. (-क्तिः)<BR>	 1. A row or line of hair.<BR>	 2. A quantity of hair.<BR> E. केश,<BR>and पंक्ति a line.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=204-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केशपर्णी|केशपर्ण्णी
केशपर्णी f. (-र्णी) A plant, (Achyranthes aspera;) also अपामार्ग.<BR> E. केश hair,<BR>पर्ण a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=204-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केशपाश|केशपाशः
केशपाश m. (-शः) Much or ornamented hair.<BR>	 f. (-शी) A lock of hair on<BR>the top of the head.<BR> E. केश hair, पाश quantity, in this compound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=204-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केशभू
केशभू m. (-भूः) The head.<BR> E. केश, and भू place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=204-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केशमार्जक|केशमार्जकं|केशमार्ज्जक
केशमार्जक m. (-कः) A comb.<BR> E. केश hair, मृज् to clean, ण्वुल् affix; also<BR>केशमार्जन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=204-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केशमार्जन|केशमार्जनं|केशमार्ज्जन
केशमार्जन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. A comb.<BR>	 2. Cleaning the hair. E. See the preceding,<BR>ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=204-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केशमुष्टि|केशमुष्टिः
केशमुष्टि m. (-ष्टिः)<BR>	 1. A large species of Nimb tree.<BR>	 2. A handful of hair.<BR>E. केश, and मुष्टि the fist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=204-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केशर|केशरं|केशरः
केशर mn. (-रः-रं) The filament of a lotus or of any vegetable.<BR>	 m. (-रः)<BR>1. A plant, commonly Nageswar, (Mesua ferrea.)<BR>	 2. A tree bearing<BR>a white strong smelling flower, (Mimusops elengi:) see वकुल.<BR>	 3. A<BR>shrub used in dying, (Rottleria tinctoria;) also पुन्नाग.<BR>	 4. A lion's<BR>mane.<BR>	 n. (-रं) Asafœtida.<BR> E. क water, &c. in the seventh case के, शृ<BR>to go, अप् affix; also with सृ to go केसर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=204-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केशरञ्जन|केशरञ्जनः
केशरञ्जन m. (-नः) A plant: see भृङ्गराज (Verbesina prostrata.)<BR> E. केश the<BR>hair, and रञ्जन what colours.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=204-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केशराज|केशराजः
केशराज m. (-जः) A species of Bhringaraja: see the preceding.<BR> E. केश<BR>hair, राज् to shine, टच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=204-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केशराम्ल|केशराम्लः
केशराम्ल m. (-म्लः) A citron tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=204-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केशरिन्
केशरिन् m. (-री)<BR>	 1. A lion.<BR>	 2. A horse.<BR>	 3. A plant used in dying: see<BR>पुन्नाग.<BR>	 4. Nageswar, (Mesua ferrea.)<BR>	 5. The citron tree.<BR> E. केशर a<BR>name, a filament, &c. इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=204-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केशव|केशवः
केशव mfn. (-वः-वा-वं) Having much or handsome hair.<BR>	 m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. A<BR>name of KṚṢṆA or VIṢṆU.<BR>	 2. A plant, commonly Punnaga: see<BR>पुन्नाग<BR> E. क BRAHMĀ, and ईश ŚIVA, व who goes, &c. from वा with ड<BR>affix; again केश hair, व who possesses: fine-haired.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=204-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केशवत्|केशवन्त्
केशवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Having a fine head of hair.<BR> E. केश and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=204-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केशवभक्ति
केशवभक्ति f. (-क्तिः) Devotion to KṚṢṆA.<BR> E. केशव and भक्ति faith.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=204-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केशवायुध|केशवायुधः
केशवायुध m. (-धः)<BR>	 1. The mango tree.<BR>	 2. Any weapon of KṚṢṆA. E.<BR>केशव KṚṢṆA, and आयुध a weapon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=204-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केशवालय|केशवालयः
केशवालय m. (-यः) The holy fig tree, (Ficus religiosa.)<BR> E. केशव KṚṢṆA,<BR>and आलय abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=204-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केशवाबाल
केशवाबाल m. (-लः) See the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=204-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केशवावास|केशवावासः
केशवावास m. (-सः) See the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=204-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केशवेश|केशवेशः
केशवेश m. (-शः) A tress or fillet of hair.<BR> E. केश hair, and वेश ornament.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=204-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केशहस्त|केशहस्तः
केशहस्त m. (-स्तः) Much ornamented hair.<BR> E. केश hair, and हस्त here im-<BR>plying much.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=204-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केशाकेशि
केशाकेशि n. (-शि) Pulling the hair mutually, hair to hair.<BR> E. केश hair,<BR>repeated, affix इञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=205-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केशान्त|केशांत|केशान्तः
केशान्त m. (-न्तः)<BR>	 1. Cutting off the hair finally as a religious ceremony,<BR>performed upon Brahmans at sixteen years of age; Kṣatriyas at<BR>twenty-two; and Vaiśyas at twenty-four.<BR>	 2. The tip or end of hair.<BR>E. केश and अन्त end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=205-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केशान्तिक
केशान्तिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>	 1. Extending to the hair.<BR>	 2. Relating to the<BR>ceremony of final tonsure.<BR> E. केशान्त, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=205-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केशारि|केशारिः
केशारि m. (-रिः) A tree, (Mesua ferrea.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=205-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केशावमर्षण
केशावमर्षण n. (-णं) Pulling the hair, especially amorously, playing with<BR>it, rubbing it, &c.<BR> E. केश the hair, अव implying improperly, and<BR>मर्षण rubbing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=205-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केशिक|केशिकः
केशिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>	 1. Having fine or luxuriant hair.<BR>	 2. Relating to<BR>the hair.<BR> E. केश hair. ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=205-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केशिन्
केशिन् mfn. (-शी-शिनी-शि) Having fine hair.<BR>	 m. (-शी)<BR>	 1. A name of<BR>VIṢṆU or KṚṢṆA.<BR>	 2. The name of a Daitya or demon killed by<BR>KṚṢṆA.<BR>	 3. A lion.<BR>	 f. (-शिनी)<BR>	 1. A kind of grass, (Andropogon<BR>aculeatum.)<BR>	 2. Spikenard, (Valeriana jatamansi.)<BR> E. केश hair,<BR>इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=205-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केशिसूदन|केशिसूदनः
केशिसूदन m. (-नः) A name of KṚṢṆA.<BR> E. केशि a demon, सूदन destroyer<BR>also similar compounds, as केशिहन्, केशिनिसूदन, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=205-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केशिहन्
केशिहन् m. (-हा) See the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=205-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केशोच्चय|केशोच्चयः
केशोच्चय m. (-यः) Much or handsome hair.<BR> E. केश hair, उच्चय heap, abundance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=205-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केसर|केसरं|केसरः
केसर mn. (-रः-रं) A filament.<BR>	 m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A lion.<BR>	 2. A horse.<BR>	 3. The name<BR>of a horse or lion, &c., see केशर.<BR>	 4. A plant, (Mimusops elengi.)<BR>	 5.<BR>A tree used in dying, (Rottleria Tinctoria.)<BR>	 nf. (-रं-री) Asafœtida.<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>	 1. Gold.<BR>	 2. Sulphate of iron.<BR>	 3. The flower of the Nageswar.<BR>E. के on the head, सृ to go, ट aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=205-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केसरवर|केसरवरं
केसरवर n. (-रं) Saffron.<BR> E. केसर and वर best.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=205-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केसराम्ल|केसराम्लः
केसराम्ल m. (-म्लः) A citron.<BR> E. केसर, and अम्ल sour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=205-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केसरिन्
केसरिन् m. (-री)<BR>	 1. A lion.<BR>	 2. A horse.<BR>	 3. A plant used in dying: see<BR>पुन्नाग.<BR>	 4. Nageswar, (Mesua ferrea.)<BR>	 5. A monkey the father of<BR>HANUMAN.<BR> E. केसर a filament, a mane, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=205-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केसरिसुत|केसरिसुतः
केसरिसुत m. (-तः) The monkey HANUMAN.<BR> E. केसरि, and सुत son कै r.<BR>1st cl. (कायति) To sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=205-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कैकेयी
कैकेयी f. (-यी) One of the wives of DAŚARATHA, and the mother of<BR>BHARATA.<BR> E. केकय a king, father of this lady, and ढक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=205-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कैङ्कर्य्य|कैङ्कर्य|कैंकर्यं|कैङ्कर्य्यं
कैङ्कर्य्य n. (-र्य्यं) Service, servitude.<BR> E. किङ्कर a servant, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=205-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कैटभ|कैटभः
कैटभ m. (-भः) A demon slain by VIṢṆU.<BR>	 f. (-भा) A name of DURGĀ.<BR>E. कैटभ a demon in whose death the goddess was instrumental,<BR>by having at the prayers of BRAHMĀ roused VIṢṆU from his<BR>slumbers, during which two demons, Kaitabha and Madhu, were<BR>about to demolish BRAHMĀ; also कैटभी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=205-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कैटभजित्
कैटभजित् m. (-जित्) A name of VIṢṆU.<BR> E. कैटभ the name of an Asur<BR>killed by the deity, and जित् who conquers; also similar com-<BR>pounds, as कैटभहन्, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=205-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कैटभारि|कैटभारिः
कैटभारि m. (-रिः) A name of VIṢṆU: see कैटभजित्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=205-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कैटर्य्य|कैटर्य|कैटर्यः|कैटर्य्यः
कैटर्य्य m. (-र्य्यः) A plant used in medicine, commonly Kayaphal.<BR>	 2.<BR>The Nimb tree.<BR>	 3. Mayana, (Vangueria spinosa.)<BR> E. कैटर from किट्<BR>to fear, and रा to cause, alarming by its pungency; pleonastic<BR>affix ष्यञ्; also कैडर्य्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=205-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कैतव|कैतवं|कैतवः
कैतव n. (-वं)<BR>	 1. Deceit, fraud, cheating, roguery.<BR>	 2. Gambling 3. The<BR>lapis lazuli.<BR> E. कितव a cheat, &c. अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=205-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कैतवप्रयोग|कैतवप्रयोगः
कैतवप्रयोग m. (-गः) A trick, a device.<BR> E. कैतव and प्रयोग application.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=205-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कैतववाद|कैतववादः
कैतववाद m. (-दः) Evasion, falsehood.<BR> E. कैतव and वाद speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=205-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कैदार|कैदारं|कैदारः
कैदार mfn. (-रः-री-रं) Belonging to a field, a meadow, &c.<BR>	 m. (-रः) Rice,<BR>corn.<BR>	 n. (-रं) A multitude of fields.<BR> E. केदार a field, and अण् affix;<BR>also कैदारक, and कैदारिक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=205-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कैदारक|कैदारकं
कैदारक n. (-कं) A multitude of fields.<BR> E. केदार, and वुञ् affix; also with<BR>ठञ् affix कैदारिक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=205-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कैदार्य्य|कैदार्य|कैदार्य्यं
कैदार्य्य mfn. (-र्य्यः-र्य्यी-र्य्यं) Belonging to a field, &c.<BR>	 n. (-र्य्यं) A number<BR>of fields.<BR> E. केदार and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=205-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कैरव|कैरवं|कैरवः
कैरव m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. A rogue, a cheat.<BR>	 2. An enemy.<BR>	 f. (-वी) Moonlight.<BR>	 n.<BR>(वं)<BR>	 1. The white esculent water lily.<BR>	 2. Fraud, trick.<BR> E. केरव here<BR>said to mean, a goose, from के in water, and रु to sound, with अप्<BR>affix; again, अण् affix, liked by the geese; or किरव a cheat, &c. or<BR>कैरव a lotus, and अण् affix, implying identity or resemblance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=205-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कैरविणी
कैरविणी f. (-णी) A place abounding in lotus flowers, or an assemblage<BR>of lotuses.<BR> E. कैरव a white lotus, इनि and ङीष् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=205-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कैरविन्
कैरविन् m. (-वी) The moon.<BR> E. कैरवी moonlight, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=205-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कैराटक|कैराटकः
कैराटक m. (-कः) A species ef poison, one of the fixed kinds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=205-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कैरात|कैरातं|कैरातः
कैरात n. (-तं)<BR>	 1. A sort of gentian, commonly Cherayta, (Gentiana<BR>cherayta, Rox)<BR>	 2. A kind of Sandal.<BR>	 m. (-तः) A strong man. E.<BR>किरात gentian, &c. अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=205-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कैल|कैलं
कैल n. (-लं) Sport, pleasure.<BR> E. केलि, and अञ् pleonasm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=205-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कैलास|कैलासः
कैलास m. (-सः) The mountain Kailasa, the fabulous residence of KUVERA,<BR>and favourite haunt of ŚIVA; it is placed by the Hindus amongst<BR>the Himālaya mountains, and the name is given to one of the lof-<BR>tiest peaks lying on the north of the Manasa lake.<BR> E. कैलास crys-<BR>tal, and the affix अण् implying nature or consistence; or कैल plea-<BR>sure, आस् to abide, affix यञ्; the place where beings reside in<BR>bliss.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=205-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कैलासनिकेतन|कैलासनिकेतनः
कैलासनिकेतन m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. ŚIVA.<BR>	 2. KUVERA.<BR> E. कैलास, and निकेतन dwell-<BR>ing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=205-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कैलासौकस्
कैलासौकस् m. (-काः) A name of KUVERA.<BR> E. कैलास the mountain, औकस्<BR>abode; whose abode is mount Kailasa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=205-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कैवर्त्त|कैवर्त|कैवर्तः|कैवर्त्तः
कैवर्त्त m. (-र्त्तः) A fisherman born of a prostitute by a Kṣatriya, or of<BR>an Ayogava female by a Nisada father.<BR>	 f. (-र्त्ती) The wife of a<BR>fisherman.<BR> E. क water, the seventh case, के and वर्त्त who abides,<BR>केवर्त्त a fish, अण् affix, implying enmity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=205-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कैवर्त्तक|कैवर्तक|कैवर्तकः
कैवर्त्तक m. (-कः) See the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=205-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कैवर्त्तमुस्त|कैवर्तमुस्त|कैवर्त्तमुस्तं
कैवर्त्तमुस्त n. (-स्तं) See the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=205-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कैवर्त्तमुस्तक|कैवर्तमुस्तक|कैवर्त्तमुस्तकं
कैवर्त्तमुस्तक n. (-कं) A fragrant grass: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=205-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कैवर्त्तिमुस्तक|कैवर्तिमुस्तक|कैवर्त्तिमुस्तकं
कैवर्त्तिमुस्तक n. (-कं) A fragrant kind of grass, (Cyperus rotundus.) E.<BR>कैवर्त्त as above, water-abiding, and मुस्तक cyperus; also कैवर्त्तीमुस्तक,<BR>कैवर्त्तमुस्त, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=205-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कैवल्य|कैवल्यं
कैवल्य mfn. (-ल्यः-ल्यी-ल्यं) Sole, only.<BR>	 n. (-ल्यं)<BR>	 1. Eternal emancipation,<BR>future happiness.<BR>	 2. Exclusiveness, individuality.<BR> E. केवल alone,<BR>free from all fetters, ष्यञ् affix of the abstract.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=205-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कैशिक|कैशिकं|कैशिकः
कैशिक m. (-कः) Love, passion, lust.<BR>	 f. (-की) One of the four varieties of<BR>dramatic style, the graceful style, suited especially to the passion<BR>of love.<BR>	 n. (-कं) A quantity of hair, the head of hair.<BR> E. केशिक hav-<BR>ing much hair. &c. affix अण् fem. affix ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=205-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कैशोर|कैशोरं
कैशोर n. (-रं) Youth, boyhood, from the age of ten to that of fifteen.<BR>E. किशोर a child, and अञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=205-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कैश्य|कैश्यं
कैश्य n. (-श्यं) A head of hair, much or ornamented hair.<BR> E. केश hair,<BR>यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=205-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोक|कोकः
कोक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A wolf.<BR>	 2. The ruddy goose.<BR>	 3. A frog.<BR>	 4. A lizard,<BR>a chameleon.<BR>	 5. The wild date tree.<BR>	 6. A name of VIṢṆU.<BR> E. कुक्<BR>to seize or take, or क water, उक् to go, affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=205-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोकड|कोकडः
कोकड m. (-डः) An animal said to be a kind of deer, of a brown<BR>colour, with a bushy tail, and lurking in holes, perhaps a hare.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=205-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोकदेव|कोकदेवः
कोकदेव m. (-वः) A pigeon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=205-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोकनद|कोकनदं
कोकनद n. (-दं)<BR>	 1. The red lotus.<BR>	 2. The red water-lily.<BR> E. कोक a goose,<BR>and नद् to sound, affix क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=205-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोकनदच्छवि|कोकनदच्छविः
कोकनदच्छवि mfn. (-विः-विः-वि) Red, the colour, or of that colour. E.<BR>कोकनद the red lotus, and छवि light, splendor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=205-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोकबन्धु|कोकबन्धुः
कोकबन्धु m. (-न्धुः) The sun.<BR> E. कोक the ruddy goose, and बन्धु a friend:<BR>see चक्रवाक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=205-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोकाह|कोकाहः
कोकाह m. (-हः) A white horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=205-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोकिल|कोकिलः
कोकिल m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. The Kokila or Koil, the black or Indian cuckoo,<BR>(Cuculus Indicus.)<BR>	 2. A firebrand, a lighted coal.<BR> E. कुक् to seize,<BR>(the heart,) and इलच् affix: the Kokila makes a prominent figure<BR>in Hindu poetry, and is supposed, by his musical cry, to inspire<BR>pleasing and tender emotions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=206-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोकिलनयन|कोकिलनयनः
कोकिलनयन m. (-नः) A plant bearing a dark black flower, (Capparis<BR>spinosa;) it is also applied to Barleria longifolia.<BR> E. कोकिल the<BR>Koil, and नयन an eye, to which the flower is compared; also other<BR>similar compounds, as कोकिलाक्ष &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=206-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोकिलाक्ष|कोकिलाक्षः
कोकिलाक्ष m. (-क्षः) A shrub: see the preceding.<BR> E. कोकिल, and अक्ष the<BR>eye, or with कन् added, कोकिलाक्षक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=206-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोकिलावास|कोकिलावासः
कोकिलावास m. (-सः) The mango tree.<BR> E. कोकिल, and आवास abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=206-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोकिलेक्षु|कोकिलेक्षुः
कोकिलेक्षु m. (-क्षुः) The black variety of sugar cane. कोकिल and इक्षु<BR>sugar cane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=206-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोकिलोत्सव|कोकिलोत्सवः
कोकिलोत्सव m. (-वः) The mango tree.<BR> E. कोकिल and उत्सव festival.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=206-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोच|कोचः
कोच m. (-चः) A man of degraded caste, the offspring of a fisherman<BR>by a female of the butcher tribe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=206-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोङ्कण|कोंकण|कोङ्कणं|कोंकणः|कोङ्कणः
कोङ्कण m. (-णः) The name of a country, Konkan in the peninsula. The<BR>hilly strip of land between the Sahyadri and the ocean.<BR>	 n. (-णं) A<BR>kind of weapon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=206-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोङ्कणासुत|कोंकणासुत|कोङ्कणासुतः
कोङ्कणासुत m. (-तः) A name of PARASURAMA.<BR> E. कोङ्कणा the mother of<BR>the hero, or the woman of Konkan, and सुत a son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=206-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोजागर|कोजागरः
कोजागर m. (-रः) The day of full-moon in the month of Ashwin, (Septm-<BR>ber-October.)<BR> E. कः who जागर wakeful; who is awake the call of<BR>LAKṢMĪ, who descending on this night, promised wealth to all<BR>that were awake: hence the night is spent in festivity, and<BR>games of chance in honour of the goddess.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=206-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोट|कोटः
कोट m. (-टः)<BR>	 1. A fort, a strong hold.<BR>	 2. A shed, a hut.<BR>	 3. Crooked-<BR>ness, (Physical and moral) curvature.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=206-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोटक|कोटकः
कोटक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Who or what curves or bends.<BR>	 m. (-कः) A<BR>thatcher, a builder of huts, &c.<BR> E. कुट् to be crooked, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=206-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोटर|कोटरं|कोटरः
कोटर mn. (-रः-रं) The hollow of a tree.<BR>	 f. (-री)<BR>	 1. A name of the goddess<BR>DURGĀ, 2. A naked woman: see कोटवी.<BR> E. कोट and र, from रा<BR>to get, to possess, with the affix ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=206-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोटरावण|कोटरावणं
कोटरावण n. (-णं) A wood in which there are hollow trees.<BR> E. कोटर the<BR>hollow of a tree, and वन a wood; by special rules, the final vowel<BR>of the first word is made long, and न in the second is changed<BR>to ण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=206-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोटवी
कोटवी f. (-वी)<BR>	 1. A naked woman.<BR>	 2. A name of DURGĀ.<BR> E. कोट crook-<BR>edness, and वा to get or receive, क and ङीष् affixes; also कोट्टवी,<BR>and कोटरी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=206-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोटि|कोटिः
कोटि f. (-टिः)<BR>	 1. The edge or point of a sword.<BR>	 2. The curved end of a<BR>bow.<BR>	 3. A number, a Krore or ten millions.<BR>	 4. Eminence, excell-<BR>ence.<BR>	 5. The upright side of a triangle.<BR>	 6. The complement of an<BR>arc to 90°.<BR>	 7. A plant, Piring or Asparac, (Medicago esculenta.)<BR>8. A department.<BR>	 9. The horn of the moon 10. one side of a deba-<BR>table question.<BR> E. कुट् to be crooked, and इण् Uṇādi affix; also<BR>कोटी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=206-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोटिक|कोटिकः
कोटिक m. (-कः) An insect, coccinella of various kinds; this is most<BR>usually read कोटिर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=206-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोटिजित्
कोटिजित् m. (-जित्) A name of the poet KALIDASA.<BR> E. कोटि a Krore,<BR>(of competitors,) and जित् conqueror.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=206-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोटिज्या
कोटिज्या f. (-ज्या) The cosine of an angle in a right-angled triangle. E.<BR>कोटि and ज्या a sine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=206-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोटिपात्र|कोटिपात्रः
कोटिपात्र m. (-त्रः) A rudder or large oar used as one.<BR> E. कोटि an edge,<BR>and पात्र a plank.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=206-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोटिर|कोटिरः
कोटिर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. An ichneumon, (Viverra ichneumon.)<BR>	 2. An insect,<BR>coccinella of various kinds: see इन्द्रगोप.<BR>	 3. A name of INDRA. E.<BR>कोटि excellence, and र what possesses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=206-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोटिवर्ष|कोटिवर्षं
कोटिवर्ष n. (-र्ष) The name of a city, Vanapuri or Devikote, on the<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=206-b" target="_blank">Page206-b+ 60</a>]<BR>Koromandel coast.<BR>	 f. (-र्षा) A plant used as a medicinal vegetable.<BR>(Medicago esculenta:) see पिडिङ्ग,<BR> E. कोटि excellence, वर्ष what<BR>diffuses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=206-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोटश
कोटश m. (-शः) A harrow.<BR> E. कोटि an edge, शी to cut or pare, क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=206-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोटिशस्
कोटिशस् ind. In multitudes, by millions.<BR> E. कोटि, and शसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=206-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोटी
कोटी f. (-टी)<BR>	 1. The edge or point of a sword.<BR>	 2. A medicinal plant,<BR>(Medicago esculenta.)<BR>	 3. A Krore, &c.: see कोटि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=206-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोटीर|कोटीरः
कोटीर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Long entangled hair.<BR>	 2. A crest, a diadem.<BR> E. कुट् to<BR>be crooked, इरन् affix and the radical vowel converted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=206-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोटीवर्ष|कोटीवर्षं
कोटीवर्ष n. (-र्षं) A name of Vanapura.<BR>	 f. (-र्षा) Piring, a plant: see<BR>कोटिवर्ष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=206-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोटीश|कोटीशः
कोटीश m. (-शः) A harrow: see कोटिश.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=206-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोट्ट|कोट्टं|कोट्टः
कोट्ट m. (-ट्टः-ट्टं) A fort, a castle, a stronghold.<BR> E. कुट्ट् to cut or divide,<BR>affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=206-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोट्टवी
कोट्टवी f. (-वी)<BR>	 1. A naked woman with dishevelled hair.<BR>	 2. A name of<BR>DURGĀ.<BR>	 3. The mother of Vana, an Asura: see कोटवी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=206-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोट्टवीपुर|कोट्टवीपुरं
कोट्टवीपुर n. (-रं) Vanapur or Devicotta.<BR> E. कोट्टवी the mother of Vana,<BR>and पुर a city.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=206-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोट्टार|कोट्टारः
कोट्टार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A well a pond.<BR>	 2. The stairs of a pond.<BR>	 3. A fortified<BR>town, a strong hold.<BR>	 4. A libertine.<BR> E. कोट्ट a fort, &c. ऋ to go,<BR>affix अप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=206-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोठ|कोठः
कोठ m. (-ठः)<BR>	 1. A species of leprosy with large round spots.<BR>	 2. Ring-<BR>worm, impetigo.<BR> E. कुठ् to surround, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=206-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोण|कोणः
कोण m. (-णः)<BR>	 1. A corner, an angle.<BR>	 2. The quill or bow of a lute, a<BR>fiddle-stick, &c.<BR>	 3. A drum stick.<BR>	 4. A sort of stringed musical<BR>instrument.<BR>	 5. The sharp edge of a sword.<BR>	 6. A stick, a staff, a<BR>club.<BR>	 7. A name of Mangala, the planet MARS.<BR>	 8. A name of the<BR>planet SATURN.<BR>	 9. An intermediate point of the compass.<BR> E. कुण,<BR>to sound, &c. घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=206-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोणकुण|कोणकुणः
कोणकुण m. (-णः) A bug.<BR> E. कुण् to cut, affix क, added to कीण the edge<BR>of a sword.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=206-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोणाघात|कोणाघातः
कोणाघात m. (-तः) A mixed sound of several musical instruments “ढक्का-<BR>शतसहस्राणि भेरीशतशतानि च । एकदा यत्र हन्यन्ते कोणाघातः स उच्यते” ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=206-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोणि|कोणिः
कोणि mfn. (-णिः-णिः-णि) Having a crooked arm: see कुणि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=206-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोथ|कोथः
कोथ mfn. (-थः-था-थं)<BR>	 1. Afflicted with pain.<BR>	 2. Churned.<BR>	 m. (-थः)<BR>	 1. In-<BR>flamation, and ulceration of the angles of the eyelids.<BR>	 2. Gan-<BR>grene.<BR>	 3. Churning.<BR> E. कुथ् to afflict or be afflicted. affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=206-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोदण्ड|कोदंड|कोदंडं|कोदण्डं|कोदंडः|कोदण्डः
कोदण्ड mn. (-ण्डः-ण्डं) A bow.<BR>	 m. (-ण्डः)<BR>	 1. An eyebrow.<BR>	 2. The name of<BR>a country.<BR> E. कुण् to sound, अण्ड Uṇādi affix, &c. दन inserted; the<BR>final radical consonant is rejected; otherwise, कुद् to speak false,<BR>अण्डच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=206-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोद्रव|कोद्रवः
कोद्रव n. (-वं) A species of grain eaten by the poorer people. (Paspalum<BR>kora.)<BR> E. क wind, उद्रव to go, affix अच्; sown by the wind, or<BR>growing wild in many places.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=206-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोप|कोपः
कोप m. (-पः)<BR>	 1. Wrath, rage.<BR>	 2. Morbid irritation or disorder of the<BR>humours of the body.<BR> E. कुप् to be angry, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=206-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोपक्रम|कोपक्रमं|कोपक्रमः
कोपक्रम m. (-मः) An angry or passionate man.<BR> E. कोप rage, and क्रम who<BR>goes or has.<BR>	 n. (-मं) The creation by BRAHMĀ.<BR> E. क BRAHMĀ, and<BR>उपक्रम order, method; also similar compounds, as कोपज्ञ, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=206-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोपज्वलित
कोपज्वलित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Enraged, inflamed with wrath.<BR> E. कोप, and<BR>ज्वलित inflamed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=206-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोपदीप्त
कोपदीप्त mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं) Incensed, inflamed with anger.<BR> E. कोप, and दीप्त<BR>shining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=206-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोपन|कोपनः
कोपन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Passionate, wrathful.<BR>	 f. (-ना) A passionate woman.<BR>E. कुप् to be angry, युच् affix, fem. affix टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=206-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोपपद
कोपपद n. (-दं) Appearance of anger, pretended wrath.<BR> E. कोप, and पद<BR>place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=206-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोपवत्|कोपवन्त्
कोपवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Passionate, angry.<BR> E. कोप, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=206-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोपवेग|कोपवेगः
कोपवेग m. (-गः) Violence, impetuousity of passion.<BR> E. कोप, and वेग speed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=206-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोपाकुल
कोपाकुल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Furious, enraged.<BR> E. कोप, and आकुल bewildered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=206-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोपित
कोपित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Angry, enraged.<BR> E. कोप, and इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=207-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोपिन्
कोपिन् mfn. (-पी-पिनी-पि) Angry, passionate, wrathful.<BR>	 m. (-पी) A bird<BR>called the water-pigeon.<BR> E. कुप् to be angry, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=207-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोमल|कोमलं|कोमलः
कोमल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>	 1. Soft, bland.<BR>	 2. Soft, low, sweet.<BR>	 3. Beautiful,<BR>pleasing, agreeable.<BR>	 f. (-ला) A plant: see क्षीरिका.<BR>	 n. (-लं) Water. E.<BR>कुट् to be curved, कल Uṇādi affix; and मुट् inserted, formative<BR>irregular; or कम् to desire, कलच् affix, and उ inserted with con-<BR>version.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=207-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोमलक|कोमलकं
कोमलक n. (-कं) The fibres of the stalk of a lotus.<BR> E. कोमल soft, कन्<BR>added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=207-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोमलगीत
कोमलगीत n. (-तं) A pleasing song.<BR> E. कोमल, and गीत a song; also with<BR>कन् added, कोमलगीतकः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=207-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोमलता
कोमलता f. (-ता) Softness, tenderness, agreeableness; also with त्व, कोमलत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=207-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोमासिका
कोमासिका f. (-का) A budding fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=207-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोयष्टि|कोयष्टिः
कोयष्टि m. (-ष्टिः) The lapwing: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=207-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोयष्टिक|कोयष्टिकः
कोयष्टिक m. (-कः) The lapwing.<BR> E. क water, यष्टि a line or row, कन् ad-<BR>ded, deriv. irr.; also कोयष्टि. These birds are found in the vicinity<BR>of marshes, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=207-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोर|कोरः
कोर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Union with little or no motion, as that of the fingers<BR>with another, amphiarthrosis.<BR>	 2. A bud.<BR> E. कुर sound, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=207-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोरक|कोरकं|कोरकः
कोरक mn. (-कः-कं)<BR>	 1. A bud, unblown flower; any thing partially deve-<BR>loped but not full-grown.<BR>	 2. A sp१ecies of perfume commonly<BR>Chor.<BR>	 3. Another perfume, a berry containing a resinous and<BR>fragrant substance: see कक्कोलक 4. The fibres of the stalk of the<BR>lotus.<BR> E. कुर् to sound, affix वुन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=207-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोरङ्गी
कोरङ्गी f. (-ङ्गी) Small cardamoms: see एला.<BR> E. कुर् to sound, अङ्गच् and<BR>ङीष् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=207-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोरदूष|कोरदूषः
कोरदूष m. (-षः) A kind of grain, (Paspalum frumentaceum.)<BR> E. कोर a<BR>bud, दूष् to change, अण् affix; also कन् being added कोरदूषक<BR>m. (-कः.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=207-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोरित
कोरित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Pounded, ground, comminuted.<BR>	 2. Budded,<BR>sprouted.<BR> E. कोर and इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=207-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोल|कोलं|कोलः
कोल m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. A hog.<BR>	 2. A raft, a float.<BR>	 3. The haunch, the hip or<BR>flank.<BR>	 4. Embracing, an embrace.<BR>	 5. The planet Sani or SATURN.<BR>	 6.<BR>Plumbago, (Zenlanica &c.)<BR>	 7. A country, Kalinga, the modern sea<BR>coast from Cuttack to Madras.<BR>	 8. A kind of weapon.<BR>	 9. An outcast,<BR>one of a tribe degraded by SAGARA from the military order.<BR>	 10. A<BR>man of a mixed caste.<BR>	 11. A barbarian, a Kol, people inhabiting<BR>the hills and forests in Central India.<BR>	 n. (-लं)<BR>	 1. The fruit of the<BR>jujube.<BR>	 2. The weight of one Tola.<BR>	 3. Black pepper.<BR>	 f. (-ला or -ली)<BR>1. The jujube tree.<BR>	 2. Long pepper.<BR>	 3. A kind of pepper, (Piper<BR>chavya, Rox.)<BR> E. कुल् to accumulate, affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=207-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोलक|कोलकं|कोलकः
कोलक n. (-कं)<BR>	 1. A kind of perfume: see कक्कोलक 2. Long pepper.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-कः) A plant, (Cordia myxta.)<BR> E. कुल् to accumulate, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=207-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोलदल|कोलदलं
कोलदल n. (-लं) A kind of perfume: see नखो<BR> E. कोल the jujube, दल a<BR>leaf; having a similar leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=207-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोलनासिका
कोलनासिका f. (-का) A plant; also वङ्किनी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=207-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोलपुच्छ|कोलपुच्छः
कोलपुच्छ m. (-च्छः) A heron.<BR> E. कोल a hog, पुच्छ a tail; hogtailed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=207-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोलमूल|कोलमूलं
कोलमूल n. (-लं) The root of long pepper.<BR> E. कोल and मूल root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=207-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोलम्बक|कोलंबक|कोलंबकः|कोलम्बकः
कोलम्बक m. (-कः) The body of a lute, the whole of it except the<BR>strings.<BR> E. कुल् to accumulate, अम्बच् and कन् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=207-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोलवल्ली
कोलवल्ली f. (-ल्ली) A plant, with a pungent fruit resembling pepper: see<BR>गजपिप्पली (Pothos officinalis.)<BR> E. कोल a hog, वल्ली a creeper; res-<BR>embling a hog's bristle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=207-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोलाञ्च|कोलांच|कोलाञ्चः
कोलाञ्च m. (-ञ्चः) A name of Kalinga the Coromandel coast, from<BR>Cuttack to Madras; according to some, it is in Gangetic Hindu-<BR>stan, with Konouj for the capital.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=207-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोलाहल|कोलाहलं|कोलाहलः
कोलाहल m. (-लः) A loud and confused sound, an uproar, a great and<BR>indistinct noise.<BR> E. कोल accumulation, from कुल with घञ्; again,<BR>हल् to make or plough, आङ् prefixed, and अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=207-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोलि|कोलिः
कोलि f. (-लिः or ली) The jujube tree,) (Zizyphus jujuba.) E. See कोल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=207-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोविद|कोविदः
कोविद mfn. (-दः-दा-दं) Wise, learned.<BR> E. को who sounds or teaches (the<BR>Shastras,) विद divine knowledge from विद् to know, affix क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=207-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोविदार|कोविदारं|कोविदारः
कोविदार m. (-रः) A species of ebony, (Bauhinia variegata.)<BR> E. कु the<BR>earth, दॄ to tear or divide, with वि prefixed deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=207-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोश|कोशं|कोशः
कोश m. (-शः)<BR>	 1. An egg.<BR>	 2. Wrought or unwrought gold or silver plate,<BR>jewellery.<BR>	 3. An ordeal, &c.<BR>	 f. (-शी)<BR>	 1. shoe, a sandal.<BR>	 2. The bread<BR>of corn.<BR> E. कुश् or कुष् to issue, घञ् affix, fem. affix ङीष्; see कोष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=207-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोशकार|कोशकारः
कोशकार m. (-रः) The sugar cane; also कोषकार.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=207-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोशफल|कोशफलं
कोशफल n. (-लं) A berry containing a waxy and fragrant substance:<BR>see कक्कोल.<BR> E. कोश an egg, फल fruit; the berry being egg-shaped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=207-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोशल|कोशलः
कोशल mf. (-लः-ला)<BR>	 1. A man of the city Ayodhya (Oude), or the<BR>neighbouring district.<BR>	 2. The name of a prince.<BR> E. कुश् to shine,<BR>अल Uṇādi affix; also कोषल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=207-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोशलात्मजा
कोशलात्मजा f. (-जा) The wife of DAŚARATHA the mother of RAMA. E.<BR>कोशल the name of a king, and आत्मजा a daughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=207-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोशवासिन्
कोशवासिन् mfn. (-सो-सिनी-सि) Wrapped up in a sheathe or shell, &c.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-सी)<BR>	 1. A shelled animal.<BR>	 2. A chrysalis or pupa.<BR> E. कोश, and वासिन्<BR>what abides.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=207-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोशस्थ|कोशस्थः
कोशस्थ mfn. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थं) Sheathed, enveloped in a sheathe, a shell, &c.<BR>m. (-स्थः)<BR>	 1. Any shelled insect or animal, as a snail, &c.<BR>	 2. A<BR>pupa or chrysalis.<BR>	 3. The silk worm in its cocoon.<BR> E. कोश and स्थ<BR>what abides.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=207-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोशलिक|कोशलिकं
कोशलिक n. (-कं) A bribe.<BR> E. कोश or कोष wealth, and ल what takes, ष्ठक्<BR>affix; also कोषलिक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=207-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोशाङ्ग|कोशाङ्गं
कोशाङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः) A kind of reed or grass, commonly Ikada.<BR> E. कोश or<BR>कोष a sheathe, and अङ्ग body; also कोषाङ्ग.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=207-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोशातक|कोशातकः
कोशातक m. (-कः) Hair.<BR>	 f. (-की) Several sorts of cucurbitaceous plants:<BR>see कोषातक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=207-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोशातकिन्
कोशातकिन् m. (-की)<BR>	 1. Trade, business.<BR>	 2. A trader, a merchant.<BR>	 3.<BR>Submarine fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=207-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोष|कोषं|कोषः
कोष mn. (-षः-षं)<BR>	 1. A bud 2. A sheathe, a scabbard, &c.<BR>	 3. A coat, a<BR>surrounding cover, any investing sheathe.<BR>	 4. Judicial trial by<BR>oath or ordeal, or by fire, water, poison, the balance, heated balls<BR>of iron, boiling oil, &c. attesting a deity, and touching or drinking<BR>water three times in which some idol has been washed.<BR>	 5. Gold or<BR>silver, wrought or unwrought as plate, jewellery, &c.<BR>	 6. Wealth.<BR>7. Accumulated wealth, treasure.<BR>	 8. A treasury, the apartment<BR>where money or plate is kept.<BR>	 9. A sacrificial vessel or any drink-<BR>ing vessel.<BR>	 10. The vulva, the womb.<BR>	 11. The penis.<BR>	 12. A test-<BR>icle or the scrotum.<BR>	 13. An egg.<BR>	 14. (In composition) A ball or<BR>globe, as सूत्रकोष a ball of thread, नेत्रकोष the eyeball, &c.<BR>	 15. The<BR>inner part of the Jack-fruit or its like.<BR>	 16. A nutmeg.<BR>	 17. A dic-<BR>tionary or vocabulary.<BR>	 18. A term for the five sheathes or cases<BR>which successively make up the body enveloping the soul. (In<BR>Vedanta Philosophy.)<BR>	 f. (-षी)<BR>	 1. A shoe, a sandal.<BR>	 2. The beard<BR>of corn: see कोश<BR> E. कुष् or कोश् to issue, affix घञ् hence the word<BR>is optionally कोष or कोश; the meanings may be mostly resolved<BR>into that, from which something issues or evolves.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=207-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोषक|कोषकः
कोषक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. An egg.<BR>	 2. A testicle.<BR> E. कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=207-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोषकार|कोषकारः
कोषकार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Sugar cane, or a variety.<BR>	 2. The silk worm, or the<BR>insect while in its cocoon.<BR>	 3. A lexicographer.<BR>	 4. A chrysalis, or<BR>(pupa.)<BR> E. कोष a sheathe, and कार what makes; also कोशकार or<BR>with कन् added कोशकारक and कोषकारक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=207-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोषग्रहण
कोषग्रहण n. (-णं) Undergoing an ordeal.<BR> E. कोषो and ग्रहण taking; also<BR>कोशग्रहणं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=207-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोषचञ्चु|कोषचंचु|कोषचञ्चुः
कोषचञ्चु m. (-ञ्चुः) The Indian crane.<BR> E. कोष a sheathe, &c. and चञ्चु<BR>a beak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=207-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोषनायक
कोषनायक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. The Indian Plutus.<BR>	 2. A treasurer.<BR> E. कोष, and<BR>नायक chief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=207-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोषफल|कोषफलं|कोषफलः
कोषफल n. (-लं) A berry having a fragrant pulp: see कक्कोल m. (-लः) A<BR>kind of creeping plant: see घोषक f. (-ला) A sort of Ghosha with<BR>yellow flowers,<BR> E. कोष a sheathe, and फल fruit; also कोशफल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=208-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोषभूत
कोषभूत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Treasured, stored, accumulated.<BR> E. कोष, and<BR>भूत been.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=208-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोषला
कोषला f. (-ला) The country south of Ayodhya (Oude) or Ayodhyā<BR>itself: see कोशला.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=208-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोषवत्
कोषवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Rich, wealthy.<BR> E. कोष, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=208-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोषवृद्धि|कोषवृद्धिः
कोषवृद्धि f. (-द्धिः) Swelled testicle, enlargement of the scrotum, from<BR>hernia or hydrocele, &c.<BR> E. कोष a testicle, and वृद्धि increase.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=208-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोषशायिका
कोषशायिका f. (-का) A knife.<BR> E. कोष a scabbard, and शी to sleep, ण्Vअल aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=208-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोषशुद्धि
कोषशुद्धि f. (-द्धिः) Purification by ordeal.<BR> E. कोष, and शुद्धि purity; also<BR>कोशशुद्धि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=208-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोषहीन
कोषहीन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Poor, without treasure.<BR> E. कोष, and हीन<BR>deprived of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=208-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोषांश
कोषांश m. (-शः) Part of a treasure, a portion of a person's wealth. E.<BR>कोष, and अंश part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=208-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोषातक|कोषातकः
कोषातक m. (-कः) Hair.<BR>	 f. (-की)<BR>	 1. A small species of cucumber, (Tri-<BR>chosanthes diæca:)<BR>	 2. A cucurbitaceous plant, commonly called<BR>Turai, (Luffa acutangula.)<BR>	 3. Another kind. (L. pentangula.)<BR>	 4.<BR>A kind of creeper: see घोष.<BR>	 5. A plant, (Achyranthes aspera;)<BR>also अपामार्ग.<BR>	 6. Night.<BR> E. कोष a sheathe, &c. अत् to go, affixes क्वुन्<BR>and ङीष्; also कोशातक and कोषातकी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=208-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोषाध्यक्ष
कोषाध्यक्ष m. (-क्षः)<BR>	 1. A treasurer. A minister of finance.<BR>	 2. KUVERA. E.<BR>कोष, and अध्यक्ष superintendent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=208-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोषापहरण
कोषापहरण n. (-णं) Carrying off treasure.<BR> E. कोष, and अपहरण taking<BR>away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=208-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोषिन्
कोषिन् m. (-षी) The mango tree.<BR> E. कोष a sheathe, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=208-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोष्ठ|कोष्ठः
कोष्ठ mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठा-ष्ठं) Own.<BR>	 m. (-ष्ठः)<BR>	 1. A granary, a place in which<BR>grain is kept.<BR>	 2. A treasury.<BR>	 3. An apartment.<BR>	 4. Any viscus, as the<BR>heart, lungs, stomach, bowels, &c.<BR> E. कुष् to issue, थन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=208-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोष्ठक|कोष्ठकः
कोष्ठक n. (-कं)<BR>	 1. A granary 2. A treasury.<BR>	 3. A brick-trough for<BR>watering cattle at.<BR> E. कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=208-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोष्ठपाल|कोष्ठपालः
कोष्ठपाल m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. A municipal officer, a constable.<BR>	 2. A watch, a<BR>guard.<BR>	 3. A store-keeper, a treasurer.<BR> E. कोष, the granary, &c. and<BR>पाल who protects.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=208-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोष्ठागार
कोष्ठागार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A store.<BR>	 2. A treasury.<BR> E. कोष्ठ, and आगार a house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=208-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोष्ठाग्नि|कोष्ठाग्निः
कोष्ठाग्नि m. (-ग्निः) The digestive faculty, the gastric juice.<BR> E. कोष्ठ sto-<BR>mach, and अग्नि fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=208-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोष्ण|कोष्णं
कोष्ण mfn. (-ष्णः-ष्णा-ष्णं) Warm, moderately warm, tepid.<BR>	 n. (-ष्णं) Warmth.<BR>E. का diminutive, and उष्ण warm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=208-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोहल|कोहलः
कोहल m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. The name of a saint or Muni, the inventor or first<BR>preceptor of the drama.<BR>	 2. A kind of musical instrument.<BR>	 3. A sort<BR>of spirituous liquor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=208-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौकृत्य|कौकृत्यं
कौकृत्य n. (-त्यं)<BR>	 1. Evil doing, wickedness.<BR>	 2. Repentance,<BR> E. कु bad, कृत्या<BR>action, affix अण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=208-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौक्कुटिक|कौक्कुटिकः
कौक्कुटिक m. (-अः)<BR>	 1. A hypocrite.<BR>	 2. A kind of mendicant, one who<BR>does not look far before him, or who proceeds with his eyes fixed<BR>upon the ground, for fear of treading upon insects, &c.<BR> E. कुक्कुटी<BR>hypocrisy, or a small part, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=208-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौक्कुटिकन्दल|कौक्कुटिकन्दलः
कौक्कुटिकन्दल m. (-लः) A species of snake, the Boa or Bor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=208-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौक्ष
कौक्ष mfn. (-क्षः-क्षा-क्षं) Abdominal, ventral.<BR> E. कुक्षि the belly, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=208-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौक्षेयक|कौक्षेयकः
कौक्षेयक m. (कः) A sword, scymitar.<BR> E. कुक्षि the belly, and ढकञ् affix;<BR>in any other sense the affix is अण्, making कौक्ष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=208-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौङ्क|कौंक|कौंकः|कौङ्कः
कौङ्क m. (-ङ्कः) the country, the Konkan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=208-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौङ्किण|कौङ्किणः
कौङ्किण m. (-णः) The district of Konkan in the peninsula: see कोङ्कन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=208-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौञ्च|कौञ्चः
कौञ्च m. (-ञ्चः) The name of a mountain, part of the Himālaya range:<BR>see क्रौञ्च.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=208-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौञ्जायनी
कौञ्जायनी f. (-नी)<BR>	 1. The wife of a Brahman or any venerable personage.<BR>2. A female descendant of Kunja.<BR> E. कुञ्ज, and फक् affix, fem. affix<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=208-b" target="_blank">Page208-b+ 60</a>]<BR>ङीष् this word may be masculine, कौञ्जायन m. (-नः) meaning a<BR>male descendant of Kunja; also कौञ्जायन्य formed from कुञ्ज by ष्यञ्<BR>affix m. sing. (-न्यः) sense; also plur. (-नाः.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=208-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौट|कौटः
कौट mfn. (-टः-टी-टं)<BR>	 1. Fraudulent, dishonest.<BR>	 2. Snared, wired.<BR>	 3.<BR>Domestic, homely, home-born, home bred.<BR>	 4. Independent.<BR>	 n. (-टं)<BR>Fraud, falsehood.<BR>	 m. (-टः) A medicinal shrub, &c. कुटज.<BR> E. कूट<BR>fraud, or कुटि a house, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=208-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौटकिक|कौटकिकः
कौटकिक m. (-कः) A vender of the flesh of birds or beasts, a poacher,<BR>a butcher, &c.; also कौटिक.<BR> E. कूट or कूटक a snare, a trap, and<BR>ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=208-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौटज|कौटजः
कौटज m. (-जः) A medicinal shrub, (Echites antidysenterica:) see कुटज.<BR>E. अण् pleonastic affix to कुटज the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=208-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौटतक्ष|कौटतक्षः
कौटतक्ष m. (-क्षः) An independent carpenter, one who works at home on<BR>his own account, and not for the village or the corporation, &c. E.<BR>कौट domestic, and तक्ष a carpenter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=208-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौटल्य|कौटल्यः
कौटल्य m. (-ल्यः) The name of a saint; also called Vatsyayana.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=208-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौटसाक्षिन्
कौटसाक्षिन् m. (-क्षी) A false witness.<BR> E. कौट fraud, and साक्षिन् a witness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=208-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौटसाक्ष्य
कौटसाक्ष्य n. (-क्ष्यं) False evidence.<BR> E. कौट, and साक्ष्य testimony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=208-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौटिक|कौटिकः
कौटिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>	 1. Fraudulent, dishonest.<BR>	 2. Relating to a<BR>snare to trap.<BR>	 m. (-कः) One who kills animals, and sells their flesh<BR>for his own subsistence, a hunter, a poacher, a mountaineer, &c. E.<BR>कूट a trap for catching birds, &c. affix ष्ठक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=208-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौटिलिक|कौटिलिकः
कौटिलिक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A hunter.<BR>	 2. A blacksmith.<BR> E. कुटिलिका derived<BR>from कुटिल crooked, said to mean a forge, or the stooping approach<BR>of a hunter on his prey, affix अण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=208-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौटिल्य|कौटिल्यं|कौटिल्यः
कौटिल्य n. (-ल्यं)<BR>	 1. Crookedness.<BR>	 2. Dishonesty.<BR>	 2. An Epithet of<BR>Chanakya.<BR> E. कुटिल, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=208-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौटुम्बिक|कौटुंबिक|कौटुम्बिकः
कौटुम्बिक m. (-कः) The father or master of a family.<BR> E. कुटुम्ब, and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=208-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौडविक|कौडविकं
कौडविक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Sown with a certain measure, (a Kuḍava) of<BR>grain; (a field, &c.)<BR> E. कुडव a measure, and ठक aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=208-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौणप|कौणपः
कौणप m. (-पः) A Rākṣasa or goblin.<BR> E. कुणप a corpse, and अण affix;<BR>these beings are supposed to eat human flesh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=208-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौणपदन्त|कौणपदंत|कौणपदन्तः
कौणपदन्त m. (-न्तः) A name of BHISHMA uncle of the Pandus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=208-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौण्डिन्य|कौण्डिन्यः
कौण्डिन्य m. (-न्यः) The name of a Muni or divine sage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=208-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौण्य|कौण्यं
कौण्य n. (-ण्यं) Being maimed, being handless.<BR> E. कुणि a cripple, यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=208-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौतुक|कौतुकं
कौतुक n. (-कं)<BR>	 1. Eagerness, vehemence, impatience.<BR>	 2. Joy, pleasure,<BR>happiness.<BR>	 3. Sport, pastime.<BR>	 4. A festivity.<BR>	 5. Wish, inclination.<BR>6. Curiosity.<BR>	 7. Kind or friendly greeting, civility, salutation.<BR>	 8.<BR>The marriage thread or ring.<BR>	 9. The enjoyment of public diver-<BR>sions.<BR>	 10. Song, dance, show or spectacle.<BR>	 11. Season of enjoyment.<BR>E. कुतुक, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=208-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौतूहल|कौतूहलं
कौतूहल n. (-लं)<BR>	 1. Eagerness, vehemence.<BR>	 2. Curiosity.<BR> E. कुतूहल and<BR>अण् pleonastic affix; also with ष्यञ् affix, कौतूहल्य n. (-ल्यं.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=208-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौतूहलान्वित
कौतूहलान्वित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Eager, vehement.<BR>	 2. Curious.<BR> E. कौतूहल,<BR>and अन्वित having.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=208-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौदालिक|कौदालिकः
कौदालिक m. (-कः) A man of a mixed caste, the son of a fisherman by<BR>a woman of the washerman caste.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=208-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौद्रविक|कौद्रविकं
कौद्रविक n. (-कं) Social salt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=208-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौद्रवीण|कौद्रवीणं
कौद्रवीण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) A field, &c. of a particular grain, (Paspalum<BR>frumentaceum.)<BR> E. कोद्रव a species of grain, and खञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=208-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौनख्य|कौनख्यं
कौनख्य n. (-ख्यं) Ugliness of the nails.<BR> E. कुनख, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=208-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौनख्यादिक
कौनख्यादिक n. (-कं) Neglect of personal decoration.<BR> E. कु bad, नखी a<BR>nail, आदि et cetera, कन् added, and अण् affix; allowing the nails to<BR>grow, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=208-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौन्तिक|कौंतिक|कौंतिकः|कौन्तिकः
कौन्तिक m. (-कः) A spearman, a soldier armed with a spear.<BR> E. कुन्त a<BR>spear, affix ठक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=208-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौन्ती
कौन्ती f. (-न्ती) A sort of perfume, commonly Renuka.<BR> E. कुन्ति here said<BR>to mean a country, affixes अण् and ङीष्; produced in that district.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=208-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौन्तेय|कौंतेय|कौंतेयः|कौन्तेयः
कौन्तेय m. (-यः) Either of the Pandu princes.<BR> E. कुन्ती, and ढक् affix, son<BR>of KUNTI.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=208-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौन्द
कौन्द mfn. (-न्दः-न्दी-न्दं) Relating to the jasmine.<BR> E. कुन्द, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=209-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौप|कौपं
कौप n. (-पं) Water of a well.<BR> E. कूप, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=209-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौपीन|कौपीनं
कौपीन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. A small piece of cloth worn over the privities.<BR>	 2. A<BR>privity, a privy part.<BR>	 3. A wrong or improper act.<BR>	 4. Sin.<BR> E. कूप a<BR>well, &c. खञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=209-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौपोदकी
कौपोदकी f. (-की) The mace of KṚṢṆA: see कौमोदकी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=209-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौमार|कौमारं
कौमार mfn. adj. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>	 1. Maiden, virgin.<BR>	 2. Juvenile.<BR>	 3. Soft, ten-<BR>der.<BR>	 f. (-री) One of the seven Matris, the divine mothers or perso-<BR>nified energies of the gods; the energy or Śakti of KUMARA or<BR>KARTIKEYA.<BR>	 n. (-रं)<BR>	 1. Youth, childhood, from birth to the age of<BR>five.<BR>	 2. Maidenhood to the age of sixteen.<BR> E. कुमार a youth, and<BR>अञ् aff.; or कुमार the deity KARTIKEYA, अण् and ङीष् affixes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=209-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौमुद|कौमुदः
कौमुद m. (-दः) The month Kartik, (Oct.-Nov.)<BR>	 f. (-दी)<BR>	 1. Moonlight.<BR>2. A festival in honour of KARTIKEYA, held on the full moon<BR>of the month Kartik.<BR>	 3. Day of full moon in the month<BR>Aswin.<BR>	 4. The same in the month Kartik.<BR>	 5. Elucidation (at the<BR>end of titles of works. e. g. सांख्यतत्त्वकौमुदी.)<BR> E. कुमुद a white lotus,<BR>अण् and ङीष् affixes, कौमुदी moonlight, equally white or brilliant;<BR>the other senses come from this.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=209-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौमुदिक
कौमुदिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Relating to a water lily, abounding with them,<BR>&c.<BR> E. कुमुद, and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=209-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौमुदिका
कौमुदिका f. (-का) A companion and confidant of DURGĀ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=209-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौमुदीचार|कौमुदीचारः
कौमुदीचार mn. (-रः-रं) Day of full moon in the month of Aswin. E.<BR>कौमुदी a festival, and चार what proceeds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=209-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौमुदीपति|कौमुदीपतिः
कौमुदीपति m. (-तिः) The moon.<BR> E. कौमुदी moonlight, and पति lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=209-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौमुदीवृक्ष|कौमुदीवृक्षः
कौमुदीवृक्ष m. (-क्षः) The stick or stand of a lamp.<BR> E. कौमुदी here light in<BR>general, and वृक्ष a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=209-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौमोदकी
कौमोदकी f. (-की) The club or mace of KṚṢṆA.<BR> E. कुमुदक what gives<BR>the earth pleasure, here said to be VIṢṆU or KṚṢṆA, affixes<BR>अण् and ङीष्; also कौमुदी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=209-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौरव|कौरवः
कौरव m. (-वः) A Kaurava, a descendant of KURU.<BR> E. कुरु, and अण् affix;<BR>also with वुञ् affix कौरवक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=209-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौरव्य|कौरव्यः
कौरव्य m. (-व्यः) An ancestor or descendant of KURU.<BR> E. कुरु, and ण्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=209-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौर्म्म|कौर्म|कौर्मः
कौर्म्म mfn. (-र्म्मः-र्म्मी-र्म्मं)<BR>	 1. Relating to a tortoise.<BR>	 2. Acting as a tortoise<BR>3. Belonging or relating to the Avatar of VIṢṆU, as a tortoise,<BR>as the Kaurmma or Kurma Purana.<BR> E. कुर्म्म, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=209-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौर्प्य|कौर्प्यः
कौर्प्य m. (-र्प्यः) The sign Scorpio.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=209-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौल|कौलः
कौल mfn. (-लः-ली-लं) Of a good family, well-born.<BR>	 m. (-लः) A worship-<BR>per of Śakti according to the left hand ritual, n. (-लं). The doctrine<BR>and practices of the left hand Saktas.<BR> E. कुल a family, and अञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=209-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौलकेय|कौलकेयः
कौलकेय mfn. (-यः-यी-यं) Of a good family, well-born.<BR>	 m. (-यः) The son<BR>of an unchaste woman.<BR> E. कुलक family, and ढक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=209-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौलटिनेय|कौलटिनेयः
कौलटिनेय mf. (-यः-यी) 1, The son or daughter of a female beggar.<BR>	 2. A<BR>bastard.<BR> E. कुलटा a female beggar, ढक् affix, and इनञ् inserted;<BR>also without the augment कौलटेय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=209-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौलटेय|कौलटेयः
कौलटेय mf. (-यः-यी)<BR>	 1. The child of a female beggar.<BR>	 2. A bastard, the<BR>child of an unchaste wife: see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=209-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौलटेर|कौलटेरः
कौलटेर mf. (-रः-रा)<BR>	 1. A bastard son or daughter of a disloyal wife.<BR>	 2.<BR>The child of a beggar.<BR> E. कुलटा an unchaste woman, ढ्रक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=209-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीलत्थ
कीलत्थ mfn. (-त्थः-त्था-त्थं) Made, prepared, consisting of a kind of vetch.<BR>E. कुलत्थ Dolichos biflorus, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=209-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौलत्थीन|कौलत्थीनं
कौलत्थीन mfn. (-नः-नी-नं) A field, &c. of Dolichos bifloros.<BR> E. कुलत्थ, and<BR>खञ् affix; see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=209-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौलव|कौलवः
कौलव m. (-वः) One of the astrological periods called Karanas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=209-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौलालक
कौलालक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) made by a potter.<BR>	 n. (-कं) Earthen-ware,<BR>porcelain.<BR> E. कुलाल, and वुञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=209-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौलिक|कौलिकः
कौलिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Ancestral, heritable in the family, belonging<BR>to it, &c.<BR>	 m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A heretic, an impostor.<BR>	 2. A weaver.<BR>	 3. A<BR>follower of the left hand Sakta ritual.<BR> E. कुल race, affix ठक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=209-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौलीन|कौलीनं|कौलीनः
कौलीन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. High birth, family descent.<BR>	 2. Rumour, report.<BR>	 3.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=209-b" target="_blank">Page209-b+ 60</a>]<BR>Evil report, detraction.<BR>	 4. Combat of animals, of birds, snakes, &c.<BR>5. Cock-fighting, &c. contention of animals as a species of gamb-<BR>ling.<BR>	 6. A privity, a privy part.<BR>	 7. An improper act.<BR>	 m. (-नः)<BR>	 1.<BR>The son of a female beggar.<BR>	 2. A follower of the left hand Sakta<BR>ritual.<BR> E. कुलीन of a good family, affix श्वण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=209-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौलेय|कौलेयः
कौलेय mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>	 1. Of a good family, well-born.<BR>	 2. Of the left<BR>hand Sakta sect.<BR> E. कुल family, ढक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=209-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौलेयक|कौलेयकः
कौलेयक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Of good parentage.<BR> E. कुल family, ढकञ् affix.<BR>m. (-कः) A dog.<BR> E. कुल a house. affix as before; a domestic animal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=209-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौल्माषीण|कौल्माषीणं
कौल्माषीण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) A field, &c. fit for or sown with a kind of<BR>been.<BR> E. कुल्माष q. v. and खञ् affix; also with अञ् affix, कौल्माष mfn.<BR>(-षः-षी-षं.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=209-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौल्य|कौल्यः
कौल्य mfn. (-ल्यः-ल्या-ल्यं)<BR>	 1. Of good family or parentage.<BR>	 2. Of the left<BR>hand Sakta sect.<BR> E. कुल family, and घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=209-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौवल|कौवलं
कौवल n. (-लं) The jujube tree: see कुवल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=209-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौवेर|कौवेरं
कौवेर mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>	 1. Relating or referable to KUVERA.<BR>	 2. Situated<BR>in the north.<BR>	 f. (-री)<BR>	 1. The Śakti or female energy of KUVERA.<BR>	 2.<BR>The north quarter.<BR>	 n. (-रं) A sort of costus, (C. speciosus:) see कुष्ठ<BR>E. कुवेर the deity, affix अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=209-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौश|कौशं
कौश mfn. (-शः-शी-शं) Silk, silken.<BR>	 n. (-शं) Kanyakubja or Kanouj the<BR>ancient city so called.<BR> E. कोश and अण् affix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=209-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौशल|कौशलं
कौशल nf. (-लं-ली)<BR>	 1. Greeting, salutation, friendly inquiry.<BR>	 2. A respect-<BR>ful present, a Nezar.<BR>	 3. Happiness, welfare, &c.<BR> E. कुशल good for-<BR>tune, well-being, अण् and ङीष् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=209-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौशलिका
कौशलिका f. (-का) A present, a respectful gift or offering.<BR> E. कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=209-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौशलेय|कौशलेयः
कौशलेय m. (-यः) A name of RAMA.<BR> E. कौशल्या the wife of DAŚARATHA,<BR>ढक् affix of descent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=209-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौशल्य|कौशल्यं
कौशल्य n. (-ल्यं)<BR>	 1. Good fortune, well-being, &c.<BR>	 2. Cleverness, talent.<BR>f. (-ल्या) The mother of RAMA.<BR> E. कुशल and यञ् affix, or कोशल a<BR>name of the father of this princess, affix ण्यत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=209-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौशल्यानन्दन|कौशल्यानन्दनः
कौशल्यानन्दन m. (-नः) A name of RAMA.<BR> E. नन्दन a son, and कौशल्या<BR>R'AMA'S mother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=209-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौशल्यायनि|कौशल्यायनिः
कौशल्यायनि m. (-निः) RAMA: see the preceding.<BR> E. कौशल्या and फिञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=209-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौशाम्बर
कौशाम्बर n. (-रं) Silk cloth.<BR> E. कौश, and अम्बर vesture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=209-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौशाम्बी|कौशांबी
कौशाम्बी f. (-म्बी) The name of an ancient city on the Ganges in the<BR>lower part of the Doab, in the vicinity of Kurrah; also वत्सपत्तन. E.<BR>कुशाम्ब a proper name, (the founder,) अण् and ङीप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=209-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौशिक|कौशिकः
कौशिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>	 1. Silk, silken.<BR>	 2. Of the family of Kusika, &c.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A name of INDRA.<BR>	 2. A fragrant substance, (Bdellium)<BR>3. An owl.<BR>	 4. A snake-catcher.<BR>	 5. An ichneumon. (Viverra ichneu-<BR>mon.)<BR>	 6. A title of VISWAMITRA.<BR>	 7. One skilled in dictionaries.<BR>	 8.<BR>A dictionary compiler.<BR>	 9. Love, the passion.<BR>	 10. The marrow.<BR>	 f.<BR>(-की)<BR>	 1. A river in Bahar, the Kosi or Koosa.<BR>	 2. A name of the<BR>goddess DURGĀ, n. (-कं) Silk.<BR> E. कोश a sheathe, &c. ठक् affix, and<BR>ङीप् for the feminine; also कौषिक, and कौशिकी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=209-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौशिकप्रिय|कौशिकप्रियः
कौशिकप्रिय m. (-यः) A name of RAMA.<BR> E. कौशिक the sage VISWAMITRA,<BR>and प्रिय a friend or favourite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=209-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौशिकफल|कौशिकफलः
कौशिकफल n. (-लं) A cocoanut.<BR> E. कौशिक the saint VISWAMTRA, and फल<BR>fruit, being said to have been created by the sage in his progress<BR>to make human being in rivalry to BRAHMĀ, the nut being the<BR>first rudiment of the head.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=209-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौशिका
कौशिका f. (-का) A drinking vessel, a cup or goblet.<BR> E. कुश् to sur-<BR>round or contain, affixes ण्वुल् and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=209-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौशिकात्मज|कौशिकात्मजः
कौशिकात्मज m. (-जः) A name of ARJUNA.<BR> E. कौशिक INDRA, and आत्मज<BR>a son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=209-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौशिकायुध|कौशिकायुधं
कौशिकायुध n. (-धं) The rainbow,<BR> E. कौशिक INDRA, and आयुध a weapon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=209-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौशिकाराति|कौशिकारातिः
कौशिकाराति m. (-तिः) A crow.<BR> E. कौशिक an owl, अराति enemy; also<BR>कौशिकारि &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=209-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौशितकी
कौशितकी f. (-की) The wife of the saint AGASTYA.<BR> E. कुश् to retract,<BR>(wrath,) इतक् and ङीष् affixes; this lady being an anti-xantippe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=209-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौशीलव्य
कौशीलव्य n. (-व्यं) The profession of an actor, a dancer, &c.<BR> E. कुशीलव<BR>and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=210-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौशेय|कौशेयं
कौशेय mfn. (-यः-यी-यं) Silken, of silk.<BR>	 n. (-यं)<BR>	 1. Silk.<BR>	 2. A silk petticoat<BR>or trowsers; a woman's lower garment of silk.<BR> E. कोश or कोष the<BR>cocoon, and ढक् affix; also कौषेय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=210-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौषिक|कौषिकः
कौषिक m. (-कः) A name of INDRA, &c.: see above, कौशिक.<BR>	 f. (-की)<BR>DURGĀ, &c. see कौशिकी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=210-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौषेय|कौषेयं
कौषेय mfn. (-यः-यी-यं) Silken: see कौशेय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=210-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौसीद
कौसीद mfn. (-दः-दा-दं) Usurious.<BR> E. कुसीद, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=210-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौसीद्य|कौसीद्यं
कौसीद्य n. (-द्यं)<BR>	 1. Sloth, indolence.<BR>	 2. The practice of usury.<BR> E. कुसीद<BR>usury, &c. affix यञ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=210-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौसुम|कौसुमं
कौसुम mfn. (-मः-मी-मं) Flowering.<BR> E. कुसुम and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=210-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौसुम्भ|कौसुंभ|कौसुम्भः
कौसुम्भ mfn. (-म्भः-म्भा-म्भ) Dyed with safflower, orange, red.<BR> E. कुसुम्भ<BR>safflower, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=210-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौसृतिक|कौसृतिकः
कौसृतिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) A juggler, a conjuror.<BR> E. कुसृति wickedness,<BR>affix ठक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=210-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौस्तुभ|कौस्तुभः
कौस्तुभ m. (-भः) The jewel of KṚṢṆA suspended on his breast.<BR> E. कुस्तुभ<BR>a name of VIṢṆU or KṚṢṆA, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=210-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौस्तुभलक्षक
कौस्तुभलक्षक m. (-कः) A name of VIṢṆU.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=210-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौस्तुभवक्षस्
कौस्तुभवक्षस् m. (-क्षाः) A name of VIṢṆU or KṚṢṆA.<BR> E. कौस्तुभ the<BR>jewel, and वक्षस् the breast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=210-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्नथ
क्नथ r. 1st and 10th cls. (क्नथति, क्नथयति) To hurt, to injure, to kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=210-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्नस
क्नस (उ) क्नसु r. 4th cl. (क्नस्यति)<BR>	 1. To be crooked (in mind or body.)<BR>	 2.<BR>To shine, (इ) क्नसि r. 10th cl. (क्नंसयति) To shine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=210-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्नु
क्नु r. 9th cl. (ञ) क्नुञ् (क्नुनाति-नीते) To sound; also क्नू.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=210-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्नू
क्नू r. 9th cl. (ञ) क्नूञ् (क्नूनाति-नीते) To sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=210-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्नूय
क्नूय r. 1st cl. (इ) क्नूया (क्नुयते) 1. To sound.<BR>	 2. To be wet.<BR>	 3. To stink.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=210-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्नूयितृ
क्नूयितृ mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ) What stinks, &c.<BR> E. क्रुय, and तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=210-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्मर
क्मर r. 1st cl. (क्मरति) To be crooked in person, to be crooked in mind,<BR>to be fraudulent or crafty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=210-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रकच|क्रकचः
क्रकच mn. (-चः-चं)<BR>	 1. A saw.<BR>	 2. A thorny plant: see करीर.<BR>	 f. (-चा) The<BR>Ketaki: see the next.<BR> E. क्र an imitative sound, कच् to emit sound,<BR>affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=210-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रकचच्छद|क्रकचच्छदः
क्रकचच्छद m. (-दः) A plant with a strong smelling flower, (Pandanus<BR>odoratissimus.)<BR> E. क्रकच a saw, and छद a leaf; having serrated<BR>leaves.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=210-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रकचपाद्
क्रकचपाद् m. (-पाद्-पात्) A chameleon, a lizard.<BR> E. क्रकच a saw, पाद् a foot,<BR>saw-footed, or with a final vowel, क्रकचपाद m. (-दः.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=210-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रकचपृष्ठी
क्रकचपृष्ठी f. (-ष्ठी) A small fish with numerous small spines in the back,<BR>(Coius cobojius, Ham.)<BR> E. क्रकच a saw, and पृष्ठ the back, saw-backed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=210-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रकण|क्रकणः
क्रकण m. (-णः) A kind of partridge, commonly Kayar; also कृकण and<BR>क्रकर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=210-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रकर|क्रकरः
क्रकर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A sort of partridge, called Kaer, (perdix sylvatica;)<BR>also कृकर.<BR>	 2. A thorny plant, vulgarly Karil: see करीर.<BR>	 3. A saw.<BR>4. A poor man.<BR> E. क्र an imitative sound, कर what makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=210-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रतु|क्रतुः
क्रतु m. (-तुः)<BR>	 1. Sacrifice, offering, worship.<BR>	 2. An Aswamedha, the sacri-<BR>fice.<BR>	 3. The name of a Muni, one of the seven principal Ṛṣis or<BR>saints, the offspring of BRAHMĀ, married to Kriya and the father<BR>of the 60,000 Balikhilyas.<BR>	 4. One of the ten VISWADEVAS.<BR> E. कृञ्<BR>to do क्तु Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=210-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रतुच्छद
क्रतुच्छद m. (-दः)<BR>	 1. A Jina.<BR>	 2. One skilled in sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=210-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रतुतुल्य
क्रतुतुल्य mfn. (-ल्यः-ल्या-ल्यं) Equal to an Aswamedha in merit.<BR> E. क्रतु and<BR>तुल्य equal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=210-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रतुद्रुह्
क्रतुद्रुह् m. (-द्रुक् or -द्रुग्-द्रुट् or द्रुड्) An Asur, a demon.<BR> E. क्रतु sacrifice,<BR>and द्रुह who hates, affix क्किप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=210-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रतुद्विष्
क्रतुद्विष् m. (-द्विट्) A Daitya or demon.<BR> E. क्रतु a sacrifice, and द्विष् who hates.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=210-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रतुध्वंसिन्
क्रतुध्वंसिन् m. (-सी) A name of ŚIVA.<BR> E. क्रतु a sacrifice, ध्वंसि to destroy,<BR>affix णिनि, the destroyer of DAKṢA'S sacrifice: see दक्ष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=210-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रतुपशु|क्रतुपशुः
क्रतुपशु m. (-शुः) A horse, especially such a one, as is fit for an Aswa-<BR>medha.<BR> E. क्रतु sacrifice, and पशु animal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=210-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रतुपुरुष|क्रतुपुरुषः
क्रतुपुरुष m. (-षः) A name of VIṢṆU.<BR> E. क्रतु, and पुरुष man or male.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=210-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रतुफल
क्रतुफल n. (-लं) The reward of a sacrifice, the object for which it is per-<BR>formed.<BR> E. क्रतु, and फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=210-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रतुभुज्
क्रतुभुज् m. (-भुक्) A god, a deity.<BR> E. क्रतु sacrifice, and भुज् who eats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=210-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रतुराज|क्रतुराजः
क्रतुराज m. (-जः) A particular sacrifice, the Rajasuya: one performed by<BR>a monarch who has subdued all the princes of the world.<BR> E. क्रतु<BR>sacrifice, and राज a king; a royal or pre-eminent ceremony: see<BR>राजसूय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=210-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रतुविक्रयिन्
क्रतुविक्रयिन् m. (-यी) A Brahman who sells to another the possible bene-<BR>fits of a sacrifice which he has performed.<BR> E. क्रतु, and विक्रयिन् who<BR>sells; also क्रतुविक्रायकः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=210-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रतुसिद्धि
क्रतुसिद्धि f. (-द्धिः) Completion of a sacrifice, attainment of the object for<BR>which it is performed.<BR> E. क्रतु, and सिद्धि completion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=210-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रतूत्तम|क्रतूत्तमः
क्रतूत्तम m. (-मः) The Rajasuya sacrifice: see the preceeding<BR> E. क्रतु, and<BR>उत्तम best: the pre-eminent sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=210-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रथ
क्रथ r. 1st and 10th cls. (क्रथयति-ते क्राथयति-ते) To kill, to hurt or injure.<BR>r. 10th cl. (क्रथयति) To amuse, to delight repeatedly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=210-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रथन|क्रथनं
क्रथन n. (नं)<BR>	 1. Slaughter, killing.<BR>	 2. Snoring, stertor.<BR> E. क्रथ् to kill,<BR>affix ल्यट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=210-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रथनक|क्रथनकं
क्रथनक n. (-कं) A white sort of Agallochum: see अगुरु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=210-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रद
क्रद r. 1st cl. (क्रदते) or (इ) क्रदि (क्रन्दति) 1. To confound, to confuse.<BR>	 2. To<BR>To grieve, to be confused; also (क्रन्दति)<BR>	 1. To call, to cry out.<BR>	 2.<BR>To weep, to shed tears: see क्रन्द.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=210-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रन्तृ
क्रन्तृ mfn. (-न्ता-न्त्री-न्तृ) Going, who or what goes.<BR> E. क्रम, and तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=210-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रन्द|क्रंदः|क्रन्दः
क्रन्द r. 1st and 10th cls. generally used with आङ prefixed, आक्रन्द<BR>(आक्रन्दति, आक्रन्दयति) 1. To weep, to shed tears.<BR>	 2. To call continu-<BR>ally.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=210-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रन्दन|क्रंदन|क्रन्दनं|क्रंदनः|क्रन्दनः
क्रन्दन m. (-नः) A cat n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Weeping, lamenting, sobbing.<BR>	 2. Crying<BR>out, calling.<BR>	 3. Mutual daring or defiance, challenging, braving. E.<BR>क्रदि to cry out, to call, sob, &c. affix ल्युट्; also with क्र affix क्रन्दित.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=210-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रन्दित|क्रंदित|क्रन्दितं
क्रन्दित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Wept.<BR>	 2. Called or cried out.<BR>	 n. (-त 1. Weep-<BR>ing.<BR>	 2. Calling.<BR>	 3. Mutual daring: see the preceding.<BR> E. क्रन्द to<BR>call, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=210-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रप
क्रप r. 1st cl. (क्रपते)<BR>	 1. To compassionate, to pity.<BR>	 2. To go or move:<BR>see कृप.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=210-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रम|क्रमः
क्रम r. 1st cl. (उ) क्रमु (क्रामति, क्राम्यति or क्रम्यति) To go, to walk, to step:<BR>(in the following senses it is optionally deponent:) (क्रमते, क्रम्यते)<BR>	 1.<BR>To proceed uninterruptedly.<BR>	 2. To grow or increase.<BR>	 3. To preserve.<BR>It is also active or deponent according to various prefixes and in<BR>various senses, as, with अति (अतिक्रामति) 1. To go over or beyond,<BR>to leap over.<BR>	 2. To transgress, to pass beyond the bounds of virtue.<BR>With अनु (अनुक्रमते) To proceed regularly or in order. With अभि<BR>(अभिक्रामति) 1. To overcome, to surpass.<BR>	 1. To assail. With अप (अप-<BR>क्रमते) To go away, to depart. With आङ्, (आक्रमते) To rise as the<BR>sun. &c. or (आक्रामति) To rise, to mount, to overcome. With उत्,<BR>(उत्क्रामति) To transgress. With उप, (उपक्रामति) To depart. (उपक्रमते)<BR>to begin. With निर् (निष्क्रामति) To go forth. With पर and आङ् (परा-<BR>क्रमति) To display valour, to surpass or overcome. With प्र, (प्रक्रामति)<BR>To depart, to go or approach, (प्रक्रमते) To begin. With परि, (परि-<BR>क्रामति) To wander about, to ramble. With वि (विक्रामति) 1. To over-<BR>come.<BR>	 2. To mount or ascend. (विक्रमते) Th pace, to proceed by steps,<BR>to move with the feet. With वि and आङ् (व्याक्रमते) To transgress.<BR>With सम्, (संक्रामति) to remove.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=210-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रम|क्रमः
क्रम m. (-मः)<BR>	 1. Going, proceeding.<BR>	 2. A sacred precept or practice pre-<BR>scribed by the Vedas.<BR>	 3. Order, method.<BR>	 4. Power, strength, 5.<BR>Overcoming, surpassing, subduing, &c.<BR>	 6. A foot.<BR>	 7. Uninterrupt-<BR>ed progress.<BR> E. क्रम् to go, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=210-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रमक|क्रमकः
क्रमक mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>	 1. Orderly, methodical.<BR>	 2. Proceeding, going.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-कः) A student who goes through a regular course of study, one<BR>who proceeds methodically.<BR> E. क्रम् to go, affix वुन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=210-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रमज्या
क्रमज्या f. (-ज्या) (In astronomy,) The sine of a planet's declination.<BR> E. क्रम्<BR>going, and ज्या sine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=211-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रमण|क्रमणः
क्रमण m. (-णः) A foot.<BR>	 n. (-णं) Going, proceeding.<BR> E. क्रम् to go, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=211-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रमतस्
क्रमतस् ind. Gradually, successively, in order.<BR> E. क्रम्, and तस् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=211-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रममाण
क्रममाण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Going, proceeding.<BR> E. क्रम् to go, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=211-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रमयोग|क्रमयोगः
क्रमयोग m. (-गः) Successive or methodical practice.<BR> E. क्रम, and योग union.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=211-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रमशस्
क्रमशस् ind.<BR>	 1. Gradually, by degrees.<BR>	 2. Regularly, seriatim.<BR> E. क्रम,<BR>and शसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=211-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रमागत|क्रमागतं
क्रमागत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Descended to or inherited lineally, what comes<BR>from one's ancestors in regular succession.<BR>	 2. Arrived in due<BR>course or succession.<BR> E. क्रम, and आगत come.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=211-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रमागतत्व
क्रमागतत्व n. (-त्वं) Hereditary succession or possession.<BR> E. त्व added to<BR>the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=211-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रमायात|क्रमायातः
क्रमायात mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Proceeding in regular order.<BR>	 2. Descended<BR>lineally, (estate, &c.)<BR> E. क्रम order, and आयात come, obtained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=211-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रमि|क्रमिः
क्रमि m. (-मिः) A worm; see क्रिमि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=211-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रमितृ
क्रमितृ mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ) Going, who or what goes, &c.<BR> E. क्रम् to go, तृच<BR>affix, with इट् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=211-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रमु|क्रमुः
क्रमु m. (-मुः) The betel-nut tree, (Areca faufel or catechu;) also क्रमुक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=211-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रमुक|क्रमुकः
क्रमुक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. The areca or betel nut, (Areca faufel or catechu.)<BR>	 2.<BR>A kind of tree, a red sort of Lodh: see लोध्र.<BR>	 3. A kind of fragrant<BR>grass; see भद्रमुस्तक.<BR>	 4. The mulberry tree, (Morus Indica.)<BR>	 5. The<BR>fruit of the cotton tree.<BR>	 f. (-की) The areca tree.<BR> E. क्रम to go, उक aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=211-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रमुकफल|क्रमुकफलं
क्रमुकफल n. (-लं) The areca nut.<BR> E. क्रमुक, and फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=211-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रमेल|क्रमेलः
क्रमेल m. (-लः) A camel: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=211-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रमेलक|क्रमेलकः
क्रमेलक m. (-कः) A camel.<BR> E. क्रम् to go. एलप् Uṇādi affix, and कन् add-<BR>ed; or क्रम order, इल् to go, क affix, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=211-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रमोद्वेग|क्रमोद्वेगः
क्रमोद्वेग m. (-गः) An ox.<BR> E. क्रम a foot, उद्वेग who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=211-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रय|क्रयः
क्रय m. (-यः) Buying, purchase.<BR> E. क्री to buy, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=211-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रयक्रीत
क्रयक्रीत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Bought, purchased.<BR> E. क्रय, and क्रीत bought.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=211-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रयलेख्य|क्रयलेख्यं
क्रयलेख्य n. (-ख्यं) Deed of sale, conveyance, &c.<BR> E. क्रय, and लेख्य writing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=211-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रयविक्रय|क्रयविक्रयः
क्रयविक्रय m. (-यः) Trade, traffic, buying and selling.<BR> E. क्रय purchase,<BR>विक्रय sale.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=211-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रयविक्रयानुशय|क्रयविक्रयानुशयः
क्रयविक्रयानुशय m. (-यः) Rescission of sale. title of civil judicature.<BR> E. क्रय-<BR>विक्रय, and अनुशय doubt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=211-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रयविक्रयिक|क्रयविक्रयिकः
क्रयविक्रयिक m. (-कः) A trader or merchant, a dealer.<BR> E. क्रय buying,<BR>विक्रय sale, and ठन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=211-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रयशीर्ष|क्रयशीर्षं
क्रयशीर्ष m. (-र्षः) The coping of a wall.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=211-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रयारोह|क्रयारोहः
क्रयारोह m. (-हः) A market, a fair.<BR> E. क्रय purchase, and रुह to rise, आङ्<BR>prefix, and घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=211-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रयिक|क्रयिकः
क्रयिक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A trader, a dealer.<BR>	 2. A purchaser, a buyer.<BR> E. क्री<BR>to buy, Uṇādi affix इकन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=211-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रयिन्
क्रयिन् mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि) A buyer or purchaser,<BR> E. क्री to buy इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=211-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रय्य|क्रय्यं
क्रय्य mfn. (-य्यः-य्या-य्यं) Purchasable.<BR> E. क्री to buy, यत् affix, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=211-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रव्य|क्रव्यं
क्रव्य n. (-व्यं)<BR>	 1. Flesh.<BR>	 2. Raw flesh.<BR> E. कृप to be able, यत् affix. and प.<BR>changed to व; the latter becomes dental before य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=211-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रव्यघातन|क्रव्यघातनः
क्रव्यघातन m. (-नः) A deer.<BR> E. क्रव्य flesh, and घातन killing for its flesh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=211-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रव्यभुज्
क्रव्यभुज् mfn. (-भुक्) Carnivorous.<BR>	 m. (-भुक्) A Rākṣasa.<BR> E. क्रव्य, भुज्.<BR>who eats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=211-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रव्याद्
क्रव्याद् m. or mfn. (-व्याद् or -व्यात्)<BR>	 1. An imp or goblin, a Rākṣasa.<BR>	 2.<BR>A flesh-eater.<BR>	 3. A beast of prey, a carnivorous animal.<BR> E. क्रव्य flesh,<BR>अद् to eat, विद् affix, or with अण् affix क्रव्याद.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=211-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रव्याद|क्रव्यादः
क्रव्याद mfn. (-दः-दा-दं) An eater of flesh or meat, carnivorous.<BR>	 m. (-दः)<BR>	 1.<BR>A goblin, a Rākṣasa.<BR>	 2. A lion.<BR>	 3. A hawk. Funeral fire. E. See<BR>the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=211-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रव्याशिन्
क्रव्याशिन् mfn. (-शी-शिनो-शि) Carnivorous.<BR>	 m. (-शी) A demon, an anthro-<BR>popphagus.<BR> E. क्रव्य, and अशिन् who eats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=211-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्राकचिक|क्राकचिकः
क्राकचिक m. (-कः) A sawyer.<BR> E. क्रकच् and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=211-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रान्त|क्रांत|क्रान्तः
क्रान्त mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं)<BR>	 1. Overcome, surpassed.<BR>	 2. Attacking, invading,<BR>gone to or against.<BR>	 3. Spread, extended 4. Going, going over or<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=211-b" target="_blank">Page211-b+ 60</a>]<BR>across.<BR>	 m. (-न्तः)<BR>	 1. A horse.<BR>	 2. (In astronomy,) Declination.<BR>	 n. (-न्तं)<BR>An astrological element, the conjunction of any planet with the<BR>moon.<BR> E. क्रम् to go, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=211-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रान्ति|क्रांति|क्रांतिः|क्रान्तिः
क्रान्ति f. (-न्तिः)<BR>	 1. Going, proceeding.<BR>	 2. Overcoming, surpassing.<BR>	 3. The<BR>sun's course on the globe, the ecliptic.<BR>	 4. Declination of a planet.<BR>E. क्रम् to go, affix क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=211-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रान्तिकक्ष|क्रांतिकक्ष|क्रान्तिकक्षः
क्रान्तिकक्ष m. (-क्षः) The ecliptic.<BR> E. क्रान्ति and कक्ष girdle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=211-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रान्तिज्या
क्रान्तिज्या f. (-ज्या) Sine of the declination<BR> E. क्रान्ति, and ज्या sine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=211-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रान्तिपात|क्रांतिपात|क्रान्तिपातः
क्रान्तिपात m. (-तः) The nodes of the ecliptic, or the equinoctial points.<BR>E. क्रान्ति and पात going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=211-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रान्तिपातगति
क्रान्तिपातगति f. (-तिः) Motion of the nodes of the ecliptic precession of<BR>the equinox.<BR> E. क्रान्तिपात, and गति going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=211-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रान्तिभाग|क्रान्तिभागः
क्रान्तिभाग m. (-गः) Declination of a point of the ecliptic.<BR> E. क्रान्ति, and<BR>भाग division.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=211-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रान्तिमण्डल|क्रांतिमंडल
क्रान्तिमण्डल n. (-लं) The ecliptic.<BR> E. क्रान्ति, and मण्डल circle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=211-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रान्तिवलय|क्रांतिवलय|क्रान्तिवलयः
क्रान्तिवलय m. (-यः) The space within the tropics.<BR> E. क्रान्ति, and वलय<BR>bracelet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=211-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रान्तु|क्रांतुः|क्रान्तुः
क्रान्तु m. (-न्तुः) A bird in general.<BR> E. क्रम् to go, वुन् Uṇādi affix, and the<BR>pen. made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=211-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रामत्
क्रामत् mfn. (-मन्-मन्ती-मत्)<BR>	 1. Going, proceeding over or through.<BR>	 n. क्रम्<BR>to go, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=211-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रायक|क्रायकः
क्रायक mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>	 1. A buyer or purchaser.<BR>	 2. A dealer, a trader.<BR>E. क्री to buy, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=211-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रिमि|क्रिमिः
क्रिमि m. (-मिः)<BR>	 1. A worm, an insect.<BR>	 2. Lac, which is the accumula-<BR>tion of an insect.<BR>	 3. A worm in the intestines.<BR> E. क्रम् to go, इन्<BR>Uṇādi affix, and इट् inserted; also कृमि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=211-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रिमिकण्टक|क्रिमिकण्टकं
क्रिमिकण्टक m. (-कः) A medicinal plant, commonly Biranga: see<BR>कृमिकण्टक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=211-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रिमिघ्न|क्रिमिघ्नः
क्रिमिघ्न mfn. (-घ्नः-घ्नी-घ्नं) Vermifuge, anthelmintic.<BR>	 m. (-घ्नः) An anthel-<BR>mintic shurb: see कृमिघ्न. f, (-घ्नी) Somraj, (Serratula or Conyza an-<BR>thelmintica)<BR> E. कृमि or क्रिमि a worm, and घ्न what kills: see कृमिघ्न.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=211-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रिमिज|क्रिमिजं
क्रिमिज n. (-जं) Aguru or aloe wood: see अगुरु f. (-जा) The red dye called<BR>Lac.<BR> E. क्रिमि a worm, and ज born; also कृमिज.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=211-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रिमिशत्रु|क्रिमिशत्रुः
क्रिमिशत्रु m. (-त्रुः) The coral tree, (Erythrina fulgens.)<BR> E. क्रिमि a worm,<BR>and शत्रु an enemy; the leaves yield, by expression, an acrid<BR>anthelmintic juice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=211-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रिमिशात्रव|क्रिमिशात्रवः
क्रिमिशात्रव m. (-वः) A fetid mimosa, (M. farnesiana.)<BR> E. क्रिमि a worm,<BR>and शात्रव inimical; an anthelmintic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=211-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रिमिशैल|क्रिमिशैलः
क्रिमिशैल m. (-लः) An ant-hill.<BR> E. क्रिमि a worm, and शैल a hill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=211-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रिय|क्रियः
क्रिय m. (-यः) The sign Aries.<BR> E. कृ to do, श aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=211-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रियमाण
क्रियमाण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Doing, making, engaged in.<BR> E. कृ to do<BR>शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=211-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रिया
क्रिया f. (-या)<BR>	 1. An act, action, acting.<BR>	 2. Means, expedient.<BR>	 2. Begin-<BR>ning, undertaking.<BR>	 4. Atonement.<BR>	 4. Study.<BR>	 6. Worship.<BR>	 7. Dis-<BR>quisition.<BR>	 1. Bodily action.<BR>	 9. Remedying, physical treatment or<BR>practice.<BR>	 10. Instrument, implement.<BR>	 11. A religious or initiatory<BR>ceremony.<BR>	 12. Obsequies, rites performed immediately after death.<BR>13. Purificatory rites, as ablution, &c.<BR>	 14. Judicial investigation, by<BR>human means, as witnesses, documents, &c. or by superhuman or<BR>ordeals of various kinds.<BR>	 15. In grammar, a verb of two kinds<BR>सकर्म्मक्रिया active or अकर्म्मक्रिया intransitive: 16. A noun of action. E.<BR>कृ to act, to do, श affix, fem. aff टाप्; the above meanings may be<BR>all resolved into the first.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=211-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रियाकर
क्रियाकर m. (-रः) See the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=211-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रियाकार|क्रियाकारः
क्रियाकार mfn. (-रः-री-रं) One who does any act, an agent, a performer.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-रः) A student, a novice, a tyro.<BR> E. क्रिया study, and कर or कार,<BR>who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=211-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रियाद्वेषिन्
क्रियाद्वेषिन् mfn. (-षी-षिणी-षि) Opposed or averse to any act.<BR>	 m. (-षी) One<BR>of the five kinds of witnesses, he whose testimony is hurtful to<BR>the cause.<BR> E. क्रिया a suit, and द्वेषिन् injuring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=211-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रियानिर्देश|क्रियानिर्देशः|क्रियानिर्द्देश
क्रियानिर्देश m. (-शः) Evidence<BR> E. क्रिया, and निर्देश proof.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=212-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रियानुरुप
क्रियानुरुप mfn. (-पः-पा-पं) Conformably to the act, according to the ac-<BR>tion.<BR> E. क्रिया, and अनुरूप like to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=212-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रियापटु
क्रियापटु mfn. (-टुः-टुः-टु) Clever, dexterous.<BR> E. क्रिया, and पटु clever.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=212-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रियापर
क्रियापर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Attentive to or diligent in the performance of<BR>their duties.<BR> E. क्रिया, and पर engaged in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=212-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रियापवर्ग|क्रियापवर्गः
क्रियापवर्ग m. (-र्गः)<BR>	 1. End of an affair.<BR>	 2. Liberation from ceremonial<BR>acts.<BR> E. क्रिया, and अपवर्ग end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=212-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रियापाद|क्रियापादः
क्रियापाद m. (-दः) The third division of a suit at law, the proof or re-<BR>joinder of the plaintiff.<BR> E. क्रिया an affair, and पाद a fourth part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=212-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रियाप्रसङ्ग|क्रियाप्रसंग
क्रियाप्रसङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः) Course of proceeding.<BR> E. क्रिया, and प्रसङ्ग procedure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=212-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रियाफल
क्रियाफल n. (-लं) Result or consequence of acts.<BR> E. क्रिया, and फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=212-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रियाभ्युपगम|क्रियाभ्युपगमः
क्रियाभ्युपगम m. (-मः) Special compact or agreement.<BR> E. क्रिया business,<BR>अभि and उप prefixed to गम् to go, affix अच्; going through with<BR>any thing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=212-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रियालोप|क्रियालोपः
क्रियालोप m. (-पः) Discontinuance or loss of any of the essential cere-<BR>monies of the Hindu religion.<BR> E. क्रिया, and लोप loss.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=212-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रियावत्|क्रियावन्त्
क्रियावत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>	 1. Engaged in business.<BR>	 2. Understanding<BR>business, fit for it, possessed of worldly knowledge.<BR>	 3. Celebrating<BR>religious rites.<BR> E. क्रिया, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=212-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रियावश|क्रियावशः
क्रियावश mfn. (-शः-शा-शं) Subject to the influence of acts.<BR>	 m. (-शः)<BR>Necessity, necessary influence of acts done or to be done.<BR> E. क्रिया,<BR>and वश Subjection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=212-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रियावसन्न|क्रियावसन्नः
क्रियावसन्न mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं) One who loses his cause in a lawsuit.<BR> E. क्रिया<BR>affair, अवसन्न ended.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=212-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रियावादिन्
क्रियावादिन् m. (-दी) A plaintiff.<BR> E. क्रिया affair, and वादिन् who declares.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=212-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रियाविधि|क्रियाविधिः
क्रियाविधि f. (-धिः)<BR>	 1. Conduct of affairs.<BR>	 2. Mode of performing any rite.<BR>E. क्रिया, and विधि rule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=212-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रियाविधिज्ञ
क्रियाविधिज्ञ mfn. (-ज्ञः-ज्ञा-ज्ञं)<BR>	 1. Conversant with business.<BR>	 2. Under-<BR>standing the ritual, &c.<BR> E. क्रियाविधि, and ज्ञ who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=212-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रियासमभिहार|क्रियासमभिहारः
क्रियासमभिहार m. (-रः) Repetition of any act, doing any thing repeated-<BR>ly.<BR> E. क्रिया, and समभिहार repetition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=212-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रियेन्द्रिय|क्रियेंद्रिय|क्रियेन्द्रियं
क्रियेन्द्रिय m. (-यः) An organ of action, as the hand, foot, voice, organ of<BR>generation and that of excretion.<BR> E. क्रिया acting, and इन्द्रिय an or-<BR>gan; also कर्म्मेन्द्रिय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=212-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्री
क्री (डु, ङ,) डुक्रीङ r. 9th cl. (क्रीणाति, क्रीणीते) To buy, to barter or ex-<BR>change; with वि prefixed, to sell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=212-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रीड|क्रीडः
क्रीड r. 1st cl. (ऋ) क्रीडृ (क्रीडति) To play, to sport; with अनु, अव, आङ्<BR>परि, or सम् prefixed, it is deponent, as अनुक्रीडते, &c. unless अनु<BR>requires the accusative case, and the compound with सम् implies<BR>inarticulate sound, as तमनुक्रीडति सा she plays with him, संक्रीडति<BR>चक्रं the wheel creaks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=212-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रीड|क्रीडः
क्रीड mf. (-डः-डा)<BR>	 1. Sport, play, pastime, pleasure, amusement.<BR>	 f. (-डा)<BR>1. Playing, as a ball, &c.<BR>	 2. Disrespect.<BR> E. क्रीड्. to play, अ affix,<BR>and fem. do टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=212-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रीडन|क्रीडनं
क्रीडन n. (-नं) Play, sport, &c.<BR> E. क्रीड to play, affix युच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=212-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रीडत्
क्रीडत् mfn. (-डन्-डन्ती-डत्) Playing, gamboling, sporting.<BR> E. क्रीड and<BR>शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=212-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रीडमान
क्रीडमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Sporting, playing.<BR> E. क्रीड, and शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=212-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रीडाकूत
क्रीडाकूत n. (-त) Sportive or wanton purpose or desire.<BR> E. क्रीडा, and आकूत<BR>wish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=212-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रीडाकोप|क्रीडाकोपः
क्रीडाकोप m. (-पः) Assumed anger, anger in sport.<BR> E. क्रीडा, and कोप<BR>anger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=212-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रीडारत्न|क्रीडारत्नं
क्रीडारत्न n. (-त्नं) Compulation.<BR> E. क्रीडा, and रत्न a gem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=212-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रीडारथ|क्रीडारथः
क्रीडारथ m. (-थः) A car, a carriage.<BR> E. क्रीडा sport, pleasure, and रथ a car.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=212-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रीडावत्
क्रीडावत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्), Sporting, sportive.<BR> E. क्रीडा, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=212-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रीडासरस्
क्रीडासरस् n. (-रः) A reservoir, a basin.<BR> E. क्रीडा, pleasure, सरस् a lake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=212-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रीत|क्रीतः
क्रीत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Bought, purchased.<BR>	 m. (-तः) A son, one of the<BR>twelve kinds acknowledged by the ancient Hindu law; he who is<BR>purchased from his natural parents.<BR> E. कृ to buy, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=212-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रीतक|क्रीतकः
क्रीतक m. (-कः) A son bought from his natural parents, and adopted as<BR>male issue; also क्रीत and क्रीतपुत्त्रः see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=212-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रीतानुशय|क्रीतानुशयः
क्रीतानुशय m. (-यः) Returning a purchase upon the seller, admissible in<BR>some cases by law.<BR> E. क्रीत bought, अनुशय repentance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=212-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रुञ्च|क्रुंच|क्रुंचः|क्रुञ्चः
क्रुञ्च (उ) क्रुञ्चु r. 1st cl. (क्रुञ्चति)<BR>	 1. To go, to approach towards or<BR>arrive at.<BR>	 2. To move crookedly.<BR>	 3. To be crooked.<BR>	 4. To curve or<BR>make crooked.<BR>	 5. To become small, to shrink.<BR>	 6. To make small, to<BR>lessen; also कुञ्च.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=212-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रुञ्च|क्रुंच|क्रुंचः|क्रुञ्चः
क्रुञ्च mf. (क्रुङ् क्रुञ्चा) A curlew.<BR> E. क्रुञ्च् to go crookedly, affix क्विन्, fem.<BR>affix टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=212-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रुञ्च|क्रुंच|क्रुंचः|क्रुञ्चः
क्रुञ्च m. (-ञ्चः) A name of the mountain Krouncha.<BR>	 f. (-ञ्चा) A kind of<BR>Vina or lute.<BR> E. क्रुञ्च् to be crooked, affixes क and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=212-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रुड
क्रुड r. 6th cl. (क्रुडति)<BR>	 1. To sink.<BR>	 2. To be childish.<BR>	 3. To eat.<BR>	 4. To<BR>be thick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=212-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रुद्ध|क्रुद्धः
क्रुद्ध mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>	 1. Angry, wrathful.<BR>	 2. Fierce, cruel.<BR>	 n. (-द्धं) Anger.<BR>E. क्रुध् to be angry, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=212-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रुध
क्रुध (औ, ऌ) औक्रुधॢ r. 4th cl. (क्रुध्यति) To be wrathful, to be flushed<BR>with anger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=212-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रुध
क्रुध f. (-क्रुत् or -क्रुद्) Anger, passion.<BR> E. क्रुध् to be angry, affix क्विप्; also<BR>with अङ and टाप् affixes, क्रुधा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=212-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रुधा
क्रुधा f. (-धा) Anger: see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=212-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रुध्यत्
क्रुध्यत् mfn. (-ध्यन्-ध्यन्ती-ध्यत्) Being angry.<BR> E. क्रुध, and शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=212-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रुन्थ
क्रुन्थ r. 9th cl. (क्रुथ्नाति)<BR>	 1. To be connected with, to cling or adhere to<BR>2. To be distressed, to suffer pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=212-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रुश
क्रुश r. 1st cl. (क्रोशति)<BR>	 1. To call.<BR>	 2. To cry, to weep. With अनु prefixed,<BR>To feel for, to sympathise with. With आङ्, To revile, to abuse or<BR>censure. With उप, To reproach. With प्र, To cry aloud, to shout.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=212-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रुश्वन्
क्रुश्वन् m. (-श्वा) A jackal<BR> E. कुश्. to cry or howl, Uṇādi affix क्वनिप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=212-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रुष्ट|क्रुष्टं
क्रुष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>	 1. Wept, cried.<BR>	 2. Cried aloud, bawled.<BR>	 n. (-ष्टं)<BR>	 1.<BR>Weeping, sobbing.<BR>	 2. Noise, sound.<BR> E. क्रुश् to weep, affix क्त<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=212-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रूर|क्रूरः
क्रूर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>	 1. Cruel, pitiless.<BR>	 2. Hard, harsh.<BR>	 3. Hard, solid.<BR>4. Mischievous, destructive.<BR>	 5. Formidable, terrible.<BR>	 6. Hot, sharp.<BR>7. Disagreeable.<BR>	 m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. An odd sign of the zodiac, as the<BR>first, third, fifth, &c. which are, of malignant influences.<BR>	 2. A<BR>hawk.<BR>	 3. A heron.<BR>	 4. Red oleander.<BR> E. कृत् to cut, रक् Uṇādi affix,<BR>and क्रू substituted for कृत.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=212-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रूरकर्म्मन्|क्रूरकर्मन्
क्रूरकर्म्मन् mfn. (-र्म्मा-र्म्मा-र्म्म) Fierce, cruel, unrelenting.<BR> E. क्रूर and<BR>कर्म्मन् act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=212-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रूरकोष्ठ
क्रूरकोष्ठ m. (-ष्ठः) Torpid or costive bowels unaffected by strong purga-<BR>tives.<BR> E. क्रूर, and कोष्ठ the alimentary canal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=212-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रूरगन्ध|क्रूरगंध|क्रूरगन्धः
क्रूरगन्ध m. (-न्धः) Sulphur.<BR> E. क्रूर, and गन्ध smell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=212-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रूरचरित
क्रूरचरित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Cruel, ferocious, addicted to cruel practices. E.<BR>क्रूर and चरित who practices.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=212-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रूरता
क्रूरता f. (-ता) Cruelty, fierceness.<BR> E. तल् added to the last; also with<BR>त्व, क्रूरत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=212-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रूगटृश्
क्रूगटृश् mfn. (-टृक्)<BR>	 1. Mischievous, villainous.<BR>	 2. Evil-eyed.<BR>	 m. (-टृक्)<BR>A name of the planet Sani or Saturn.<BR> E. क्रूर cruel, &c. and दृश्<BR>who sees, from दृश् to see, affix क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=212-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रूरराविन्
क्रूरराविन् m. (-वी) A raven.<BR> E. क्रूर formidable, राविन् who cries.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=212-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रूरलोचन|क्रूरलोचनः
क्रूरलोचन m. (-नः) A name of Saturn.<BR> E. क्रूर evil, and लोचन an eye; of<BR>an evil or inauspicious aspect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=212-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रूरव
क्रूरव m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. A jackal.<BR>	 2. Any thing bad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=212-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रूराकृति|क्रूराकृतिः
क्रूराकृति m. (-तिः) A name of RAVANA, the ruler of Lanka.<BR> E. क्रूर evil,<BR>and आकृति figure, form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=212-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रूराचार
क्रूराचार mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Following barbarous or savage practices.<BR> E. क्रूर,<BR>and आचार observance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=212-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रूर्च्च|क्रूर्च
क्रूर्च्च mn. (-र्च्चः-र्च्च) The beard: see क्रूर्च्च.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=212-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रेणि|क्रेणिः
क्रेणि m. (-णिः) Buying, purchase.<BR> E. क्री to buy, णि Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=212-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रेतव्य|क्रेतव्यं
क्रेतव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं) Purchasable. E. future participle of क्री to buy,<BR>affix तव्यत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=212-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रेतृ
क्रेतृ m. (-ता) A purchaser, a buyer,<BR> E. क्री to buy, affix तृच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=213-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रेय|क्रेयं
क्रेय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Purchasable.<BR> E. क्री to buy, affix यत्; to be bought.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=213-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रोञ्च|क्रोंच|क्रोंचः|क्रोञ्चः
क्रोञ्च m. (-ञ्चः) A mountain: see क्रौञ्च.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=213-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रोञ्चपदा
क्रोञ्चपदा f. (-दा) A species of metre of four lines, and twenty-five<BR>syllables in each.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=213-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रोञ्चदारण
क्रोञ्चदारण m. (-णः) A name of KARTIKEYA.<BR> E. क्रोञ्च or क्रौञ्च a mountain,<BR>and दारण the render or tearer; also क्रौञ्चदारण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=213-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रोड|क्रोडं|क्रोडः
क्रोड nf. (-डं-डा)<BR>	 1. The breast, the chest.<BR>	 2. The haunch, the flank, the<BR>hollow above the hip.<BR>	 m. (-डः)<BR>	 1. A name of Sani or Saturn.<BR>	 2. A<BR>hog.<BR> E. क्रुड्. to be thick, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=213-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रोडपर्णी|क्रोडपर्ण्णी
क्रोडपर्णी f. (-र्णी) A prickly nightshade: see कण्टकारिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=213-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रोडपाद|क्रोडपादः
क्रोडपाद m. (-दः) A turtle, a tortoise.<BR> E. क्रोड the breast, and पाद a foot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=213-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रोडाङ्क|क्रोडांक|क्रोडाङ्कः
क्रोडाङ्क m. (-ङ्कः) A tortoise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=213-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रोडाङ्घ्रि|क्रोडांघ्रि|क्रोडाङ्घ्रिः
क्रोडाङ्घ्रि m. (-ङ्घ्रि) A turtle or tortoise.<BR> E. क्रोड and अङ्घ्रि a foot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=213-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रोडीकरण|क्रोडीकरणं
क्रोडीकरण n. (-णं) Embracing.<BR> E. क्रोड breast or side, करण making,<BR>and च्वि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=213-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रोडीकृति|क्रोडीकृतिः
क्रोडीकृति f. (-तिः) Embracing, mutual embrace. E. See the preceding;<BR>कृति making.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=213-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रोथ|क्रोथः
क्रोथ m. (-थः) Killing, slaying.<BR> E. क्रुथ् to kill or hurt, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=213-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रोध|क्रोधः
क्रोध m. (-धः) Anger, wrath.<BR> E. क्रुध् to be angry, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=213-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रोधज|क्रोधजः
क्रोधज mfn. (-जः-जा-जं) Proceeding from or engendered by wrath; it<BR>especially applies to eight vices, hatred, envy, oppression, violence<BR>&c.<BR> E. क्रोध passion, and ज produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=213-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रोधन|क्रोधनः
क्रोधन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Passionate, angry, wrathful. (-ना) A passionate<BR>woman, a vixen.<BR> E. क्रुध् to be angry affix युच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=213-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रोधनीय
क्रोधनीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Provocative.<BR>	 n. (-यं) An injury.<BR> E. क्रुध् to be<BR>angry, (on account of,) अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=213-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रोधमय
क्रोधमय mfn. (-यः-यी-यं) Angry, passionate.<BR> E. क्रोध and मयट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=213-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रोधमूर्च्छित
क्रोधमूर्च्छित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Passionate, angry, overcome with rage.<BR>	 m. (-तः)<BR>A kind of perfume, commonly Chor.<BR> E. क्रोध wrath, and मूर्च्छित<BR>confused, overcome.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=213-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रोधवर्जित|क्रोधवर्ज्जित
क्रोधवर्जित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Free from wrath, mild, calm.<BR> E. क्रोध and वर्जित<BR>devoid of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=213-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रोधवश
क्रोधवश mfn. (-शः-शा-शं) Passionate, violent.<BR> E. क्रोध, and वश subject to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=213-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रोधिन्
क्रोधिन् mfn. (-धी-धिनी-धि) Angry, passionate.<BR> E. क्रोध anger, affix इनि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=213-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रोधोञ्झित
क्रोधोञ्झित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Calm, composed, free from wrath.<BR> E. क्रोध,<BR>and उञ्झित abandoned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=213-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रोश|क्रोशः
क्रोश m. (-शः) A measure of distance, a league, a Kos, containing 4000<BR>cubits; some double this, and make the Kos 8000 cubits.<BR> E. क्रुश्<BR>to call, &c, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=213-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रोशत्
क्रोशत् mfn. (-शन्-शन्ती-शत्) Crying, calling out.<BR> E. क्रुश् to cry, शत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=213-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रोशताल|क्रोशतालः
क्रोशताल m. (-लः) A large or double drum.<BR> E. क्रोश a Kos, and ताल a<BR>tune; whose sound may be heard for a league.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=213-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रोशध्वनि|क्रोशध्वनिः
क्रोशध्वनि m. (-निः) A large drum.<BR> E. क्रोश, and ध्वनि sound: see the<BR>preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=213-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रोशयुग|क्रोशयुगं
क्रोशयुग n. (-गं) A measure of two Kos, 4000 yards, or about 2(1/2) miles;<BR>this seems to correspond to the modern Kos, but the standard<BR>varies.<BR> E. क्रोश a Kos, and युग a pair also गव्यूति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=213-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रोष्टु
क्रोष्टु mf. (-ष्टा-ष्ट्री) A jackal. क्रुश् to cry or call, and तुन् aff; the noun<BR>declined in many cases like nouns in ऋ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=213-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रोष्टुकपुच्छिका
क्रोष्टुकपुच्छिका f. (-का) A plant, commonly Chaculiya, (Hemionites<BR>cordifolia, Rox.) or according to some, Ramvasac, a different plant<BR>see क्रोष्टुविन्ना.<BR> E. क्रोष्टु a jackal, कन् affix, and पुच्छिका tail; the<BR>flower being compared to the tail of the animal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=213-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रोष्टुकमेखला
क्रोष्टुकमेखला f. (-ला) The plant Chacaliya; see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=213-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रोष्टुपुच्छिका
क्रोष्टुपुच्छिका f. (-का) See क्रोष्टुकपुच्छिका; also क्नोष्टुपुच्छी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=213-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रोष्टुविन्ना
क्रोष्टुविन्ना f. (-न्ना) The name of a plant, either Chaculiya, (Hemionites<BR>cordifolia, Rox) or a different plant called Ramvasac.<BR> E. क्रोष्टु a<BR>jackal, and विन्न known; known by being compared to the animal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=213-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रोष्टेक्षु|क्रोष्टेक्षुः
क्रोष्टेक्षु m. (-क्षुः) The white sugar cane.<BR> E. क्रोष्ट and इक्षु cane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=213-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रोष्ट्री
क्रोष्ट्री f. (-ष्ट्री)<BR>	 1. The black or white Bhuincaonra, (Convolvulus pani-<BR>culatus:) see भूमिकुष्माण्डक.<BR>	 2. Chaculiya: see क्रोष्टुविन्ना.<BR>	 3. A she<BR>jackal: see क्रोष्टु.<BR> E. क्रुश् to cry, affix ष्ट्रन् and fem. ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=213-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रौञ्च|क्रौंच|क्रौंचः|क्रौञ्चः
क्रौञ्च m. (-ञ्चः)<BR>	 1. A kind of heron. (Ardea jaculator, BUCH.)<BR>	 2. One of<BR>the Dwipas or principal divisions of the world, surrounded by the<BR>sea of curds.<BR>	 3. A mountain, part of the Himālaya range, situated in<BR>the eastern part of the chain on the north of Asam.<BR>	 4. A Jaina<BR>emblem, the figure of the curlew, used as a symbol.<BR>	 5. The name<BR>of a demon, f. (-ञ्चा) The female of the curlew.<BR> E. क्रुञ्च to go crook-<BR>edly, affix अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=213-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रौञ्चदारण|क्रौंचदारण|क्रौञ्चदारणः
क्रौञ्चदारण m. (-णः) A name of KARTIKEYA.<BR> E. क्रौञ्च the name of a moun-<BR>tain; also of an Asur, and दारण the tearer or destroyer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=213-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रौञ्चादान
क्रौञ्चादान m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. Long pepper.<BR>	 2. The fibres of the stalk of the lotus.<BR>3. An esculent root, commonly Ghenchu.<BR>	 4. An acquatic plant,<BR>commonly Chinchata.<BR> E. क्रौञ्च the heron, and अदन eating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=213-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रौञ्चाराति|क्रौंचाराति|क्रौञ्चारातिः
क्रौञ्चाराति m. (-तिः) A name of KARTIKEYA.<BR> E. क्रौञ्च the Asur, and अराति<BR>an enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=213-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रौञ्चारि|क्रौंचारि|क्रौञ्चारिः
क्रौञ्चारि m. (-रिः)<BR>	 1. The deity KARTIKEYA.<BR>	 2. The hero and Avatar<BR>PARASURAMA.<BR> E. क्रौञ्च the Asura or the mountain, and अरि a foe:<BR>PARASU RAMA is said to have made with his arrows a pass or defile<BR>through the Krauncha mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=213-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रौर्य्य|क्रौर्य|क्रौर्यं
क्रौर्य्य n. (-र्य्यं) Cruelty, fierceness, passion.<BR> E. क्रूर cruel. &c. ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=213-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रौशशतिक|क्रौशशतिकः
क्रौशशतिक m. (-कः) One who goes a hundred Kos, or leagues.<BR> E. क्रोश<BR>a Kos, शत a hundred, and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=213-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लथ
क्लथ (म) r. 1st. cl. (क्लथति) To kill or hurt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=213-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लद
क्लद r. 1st cl. (क्लदते) or (इ) क्लदि (क्लन्दते) 1. To be confused, to grieve.<BR>2. To confound; also क्लदि (क्लदडि) 1. To call.<BR>	 2. To shed tears.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=213-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लप
क्लप r. 10th cl. (क्लापयति) To speak, to speak barbarously.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=213-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लम|क्लमः
क्लम (उ, भ, ञ, इर) क्लमु r. 4th cl. (क्लाम्यति) To be fatigued, to be weary or<BR>exhausted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=213-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लम|क्लमः
क्लम m. (-मः) Fatigue, weariness, exhaustion.<BR> E. क्लम् to be weary, affix<BR>घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=213-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लमथ|क्लमथः
क्लमथ m. (-थः) Fatigue, exhaustion.<BR> E. क्लम् to be weary, Uṇādi affix अथ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=213-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लमित्व
क्लमित्व n. (-त्वं) Exhaustion, languor fatigue.<BR> E. क्लमिन्, and त्व affix; also<BR>with तल्, क्लमिता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=213-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लमिन्
क्लमिन् mfn. (-मी-मिनी मि) Weary, exhausted.<BR> E. क्लम्, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=213-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लव
क्लव r. 1st cl. (क्लवते) To fear, to be afraid: वि is usually prefixed in this<BR>sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=213-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लान्त|क्लांत|क्लान्तः
क्लान्त mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं)<BR>	 1. Wearied.<BR>	 2. Depressed in spirits or exhausted.<BR>E. क्लम् to be weary, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=213-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लान्तमनस्
क्लान्तमनस् mfn. (-नाः-नाः-नः) Low-spirited, languid, melancholy.<BR> E. क्लान्त,<BR>and मनस् the mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=213-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लान्ति|क्लांति|क्लांतिः|क्लान्तिः
क्लान्ति f. (-न्तिः) Fatigue, weariness.<BR> E. क्लम् to be weary, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=213-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लान्तिच्छिद्|क्लांतिच्छिद्
क्लान्तिच्छिद् mfn. (-च्छित् or च्छिद्) Relieving fatigue, refreshing, invigora-<BR>ting.<BR> E. क्लान्ति, and च्छिद् what cuts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=213-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लान्तिच्छेद
क्लान्तिच्छेद m. (-दः) Refreshing, restoring, removing fatigue.<BR> E. क्लान्ति,<BR>and च्छेद cutting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=213-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लिद
क्लिद (इ) क्लिदि r. 1st cl. (क्लिन्दते-ति) To bewail, to lament, to weep. (ऊ, इर;)<BR>इर क्लिदू r. 4th cl. (क्लिद्यति) To be or become wet, damp, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=213-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लिन्न|क्लिन्नं
क्लिन्न mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं) Wet, moistened.<BR> E. क्लिद् to be or become wet, irr.<BR>participle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=213-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लिन्नवर्त्मन्
क्लिन्नवर्त्मन् m. (-त्मा) Excess of the lachrymal discharge, watering of the<BR>eyes.<BR> E. क्लिन्न, and वर्त्मन् the eyelid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=213-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लिन्नाक्ष|क्लिन्नाक्षः
क्लिन्नाक्ष mfn. (-क्षः-क्षा-क्षं) Blear-eyed.<BR> E. क्लिन्न wet, and अक्ष the eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=213-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लिश
क्लिश (उ) क्लिशु r. 4th cl. (क्लिश्यते)<BR>	 1. To suffer distress.<BR>	 2. To inflict or<BR>cause distress; (ऊ,) क्लिशू r. 9th cl. (क्लिश्नाति)<BR>	 1. To oppose 2. To<BR>afflict, to distress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=213-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लिशित|क्लिशितः
क्लिशित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Distrest, afflicted, wearied,<BR> E. क्लिश to be distressed,<BR>&c. affix क्त with इट inserted; also without इट्, क्लिष्ट.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=213-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लिशितवत्
क्लिशितवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Suffering pain or distress.<BR> E. क्लिश, and क्तवतु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=213-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लिष्ट|क्लिष्टः
क्लिष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>	 1. Distressed, afflicted, &c.<BR>	 2. Inconsistent, contra-<BR>dictory.<BR> E. क्लिश् to be distressed, &c. affix क्त, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=214-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लिष्टि|क्लिष्टिः
क्लिष्टि f. (-ष्टिः)<BR>	 1. Calamity, distress.<BR>	 2. Service.<BR> E. क्लिश् to afflict, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=214-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लीतक
क्लीतक n. (-कं) Liquorice, (Glycirrbiza glabra)<BR> E. क्लीव् to be weak, affix<BR>क्त, व being dropped; क्लीत weakness, कल् to remove, and ल drop-<BR>ped by affixing ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=214-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लीतकिक
क्लीतकिक f. (-का) The indigo plant, (Indigofera Indica.)<BR> E. क्रीतक traffic,<BR>कन् pleonastic, the fem. form; र is changed to ल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=214-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लीव|क्लीवः
क्लीव (ऋ) क्लीवृ r. 1st. cl. (क्लीवते)<BR>	 1. To be impotent.<BR>	 2. To be timorous,<BR>to be modest or unassuming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=214-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लीव|क्लीवः
क्लीव (ऋ) क्लीवृ r. 1st cl. (क्लीवते)<BR>	 1. To be impotent.<BR>	 2. To be timid or<BR>modest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=214-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लीव|क्लीवः
क्लीव mfn. (-वः-वा-वं)<BR>	 1. Weak, impotent.<BR>	 2. Idle, slothful.<BR>	 mn. (-वः-वं)<BR>1. The neuter gender.<BR>	 2. A eunuch.<BR> E. क्लीव् to be weak or timid,<BR>affix क; also read क्लीवक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=214-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लेद|क्लेदः
क्लेद n. (-दं)<BR>	 1. Wetness, dampness, moisture, &c.<BR>	 2. Running, discharge<BR>from a sore.<BR> E. क्लिद् to be wet, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=214-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लेदक|क्लेदकः
क्लेदक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Wetting, moistening, making wet or moist.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-कः) Phlegm in the stomach, excess of saliva.<BR> E. क्लिद् to be wet,<BR>causal form, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=214-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लेदन्
क्लेदन् m. (-दा) The moon.<BR> E. क्लिद् to be damp, कनिन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=214-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लेदन|क्लेदनः
क्लेदन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Wetting, moistening.<BR>	 2. Oozing, trickling.<BR>	 m. (-नः)<BR>Phlegm, the phlegmatic or watery humor.<BR> E. क्लिद् to be moist,<BR>ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=214-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लेदु|क्लेदुः
क्लेदु m. (-दुः)<BR>	 1. The moon.<BR>	 2. Complication of disorders.<BR> E. क्लिद् to be<BR>wet or damp, उण् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=214-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लेश|क्लेशः
क्लेश r. 1st cl. (क्लेशते)<BR>	 1. To speak articulately, 2. To distress.<BR>	 3. To im-<BR>pede or obstruct.<BR>	 4. To kill, to strike.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=214-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लेश|क्लेशः
क्लेश m. (-शः)<BR>	 1. Pain, affliction or distress.<BR>	 2. Pain from disease, an-<BR>guish. Worldly occupation, care, trouble.<BR>	 4. Wrath, anger.<BR> E. क्लिश्<BR>to suffer or inflict pain, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=214-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लेशक
क्लेशक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Giving pain, annoying, afflicting.<BR> E. क्लिश, and<BR>वुञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=214-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लेशप्रहाण
क्लेशप्रहाण n. (-णं) Termination of distress, especially of worldly cares,<BR>passions, &c.<BR> E. क्लेश, and प्रहाण destruction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=214-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लेशापह|क्लेशापहः
क्लेशापह mfn. (-हः-हा-हं)<BR>	 1. Consolatory, consoling.<BR>	 2. Palliative,<BR>allaying pain.<BR>	 m. (-हः) A son.<BR> E. क्लेश, and अपह what removes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=214-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लेशित|क्लेशितः
क्लेशित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Pained, distressed, afflicted.<BR> E. क्लिश् to suffer<BR>pain, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=214-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लैतकिक|क्लैतकिकं
क्लैतकिक n. (-कं) Wine, spirituous liquor.<BR> E. क्लीतक liquorice, ठक् affix;<BR>a fermented liquor being prepared from this root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=214-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लैव्य|क्लैव्यं
क्लैव्य n. (-व्यं)<BR>	 1. Absence of virility, impotence.<BR>	 2. The neuter gender.<BR>3. Unmanliness, cowardice, &c.<BR> E. क्लीव and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=214-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लोमन्
क्लोमन् n. (म) The bladder.<BR> E. क्लु to go, कनिन् affix; also with a final<BR>vowel; क्लोम n. (-मं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=214-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्व
क्व ind. Where, in what place or degree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=214-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्वङ्गु|क्वङ्गुः
क्वङ्गु m. (-ङ्गुः) A sort of Panick: see कङ्गु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=214-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्वचित्
क्वचित् ind. Somewhere.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=214-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्वण|क्वणः
क्वण r. 1st cl. (क्वणति) To sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=214-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्वण|क्वणः
क्वण m. (-णः)<BR>	 1. The sound or tone of any musical instrument 2. Sound<BR>in general.<BR> E. क्वण् to sound, अप् affix; also क्वाण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=214-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्वणत्
क्वणत् mfn. (-णन्-णन्ती-णत्) Sounding.<BR> E. क्वण, and शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=214-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्वणन|क्वणनं|क्वणनः
क्वणन n. (-नं) The sound of any musical instrument.<BR>	 m. (-नः) A small<BR>earthen pot or boiler.<BR> E. क्वण् to sound, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=214-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्वणित|क्वणितं
क्वणित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Sounded, twanged,<BR> E. क्वण् to sound, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=214-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्वत्य
क्वत्य mfn. (-त्यः-त्या-त्यं) Of or belonging to where or what place<BR> E. त्यप्<BR>added to क्व.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=214-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्वथ|क्वथः
क्वथ r. 1st cl. (-ए,) क्वथे (क्वथति) To decoct, to boil, to prepare by heat, to<BR>digest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=214-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्वथन|क्वथनं
क्वथन n. (-नं) Boiling, decocting.<BR> E. क्वथ् to boil, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=214-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्वथित|क्वथितः
क्वथित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Boiled, decocted, stewed, digested.<BR> E. क्वथ् to<BR>decoct, &c. affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=214-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्वाण|क्वाणः
क्वाण m. (-णः) The sound of musical instruments.<BR> E. क्वण् to sound, affix<BR>घञ्ः see क्वण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=214-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्वाथ|क्वाथः
क्वाथ m. (-थः)<BR>	 1. A decoction, any solution or infusion prepared with a<BR>continued and gentle heat.<BR>	 2. Pain, sorrow.<BR>	 3. Calamity, distress.<BR>4. The mixture of the materials for a decoction.<BR> E. क्वथ to decoct,<BR>घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=214-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्वाथोद्भव|क्वाथोद्भवं|क्वाथोद्भवः
क्वाथोद्भव n. (-वं) Blue vitriol used as a collyrium.<BR> E. क्वाथ and उद्भव produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=214-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्वेल
क्वेल r. 1st. cl. (ऊ) क्वेलू (क्वेलति) To shake or move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=214-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्ष|क्षः
क्ष m. (-क्षः)<BR>	 1. A destruction of the world.<BR>	 2. A demon, a goblin.<BR>	 3. The<BR>third incarnation of VIṢṆU, the Narasinha Avatar.<BR>	 4. Lightning.<BR>5. A field.<BR>	 6. A peasant, a husbandman.<BR>	 7. Loss, disappearance. E.<BR>क्षि or क्षै to waste, &c. affix क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=214-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षज
क्षज (म, ष) r. 1st. cl. (क्षजते)<BR>	 1. To go or approach.<BR>	 2. To give. (इ, ष, म)<BR>क्षजि r. 1st cl. (क्षञ्जते)<BR>	 1. To go.<BR>	 2. To give. r. 1st. and 10th cls. (इ)<BR>क्षजि (क्षञ्जति, क्षञ्जयति) To live in distress, to live in pain or want.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=214-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षण|क्षणं|क्षणः
क्षण (उ) क्षणु r. 8th cl. (क्षणति, क्षणुते) To kill, to injure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=214-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षण|क्षणं|क्षणः
क्षण m. (-णः)<BR>	 1. A measure of time equal to thirty Kalas or four minu-<BR>tes.<BR>	 2. A moment.<BR>	 3. A festival.<BR>	 4. Vacation from work, state of<BR>being unemployed.<BR>	 5. Leisure, opportunity.<BR>	 6. A certain day of<BR>the fortnight, as the full, change, &c. see पर्ब्बन् 7. Dependence,<BR>servitude.<BR>	 8. The centre, the middle.<BR>	 n. adv. (-णं) For a moment.<BR>E. क्षण् to injure, affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=214-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षणक्षेप|क्षणक्षेपः
क्षणक्षेप m. (-पः) A short delay.<BR> E. क्षण, and क्षेप throwing (away.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=214-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षणतु|क्षणतुः
क्षणतु m. (-तुः) A wound or sore.<BR> E. क्षण् to hurt, अतु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=214-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षणद|क्षणदं|क्षणदः
क्षणद m. (-दः) An astrologer.<BR>	 n. (-दं) Water.<BR>	 f. (-दा)<BR>	 1. Night.<BR>	 2. Tur-<BR>meric.<BR> E. क्षण leisure, a moment, &c. and द who gives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=214-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षणदाचार
क्षणदाचार mfn. (-रः-री-रं) Nocturnal, nightwalker.<BR>	 mf. (-रः-री) A fiend,<BR>a goblin,<BR> E. क्षणदा night, and चर who or what goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=214-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षणदान्ध्य|क्षणदांध्य
क्षणदान्ध्य n. (-न्ध्यं) Night blindness, nyctalopsis.<BR> E. क्षणदा, and आन्ध्य<BR>blindness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=214-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षणदृष्ट
क्षणदृष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं) Momentarily visible, seen for an instant.<BR> E. क्षण,<BR>and दृष्ट seen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=214-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षणद्युति|क्षणद्युतिः
क्षणद्युति f. (-तिः) Lightning.<BR> E. क्षण, and द्युति Light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=214-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षणन|क्षणनं
क्षणन n. (-नं) Killing, slaughter.<BR> E. क्षण to hurt, to kill, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=214-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षणनिश्वास|क्षणनिश्वासः
क्षणनिश्वास m. (-सः) A porpoise, the Gangetic porpoise.<BR> E. क्षण a moment<BR>and निश्वास breath, breathing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=214-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षणप्रकाश
क्षणप्रकाश f. (-शः) Lightning.<BR> E. क्षण and प्रकाश manifest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=214-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षणप्रभ
क्षणप्रभ mfn. (-भः-भा-भं) Gleaming, flashing.<BR>	 f. (भा) Lightning,<BR> E. क्षण a<BR>moment, and प्रभा light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=214-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षणभङ्गुर|क्षणभंगुर|क्षणभङ्गुरः
क्षणभङ्गुर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Transient, frail, perishable.<BR> E. क्षण, and भङ्गुर<BR>breaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=214-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षणभूत
क्षणभूत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Momentary, short-lived.<BR> E. क्षण and भूत been.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=214-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षणमात्र
क्षणमात्र adv.<BR>	 n. (-त्रं) Momentary, but for a moment.<BR> E. क्षण, and मात्र<BR>only.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=214-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षणरामिन्
क्षणरामिन् m. (-मी) A pigeon.<BR> E. क्षण a moment, and रम् to play, affix<BR>णिनि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=214-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षणविध्वंसिन्
क्षणविध्वंसिन् mfn. (-सी-सिनी-सि) Transient, frail.<BR> E. क्षण and विध्वंसिन् what<BR>is destroyed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=214-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षणान्तर
क्षणान्तर adv.<BR>	 n. (-रं) A minute afterwards, the next moment.<BR> E. क्षण,<BR>and अन्तर interval.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=214-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षणिक|क्षणिकः
क्षणिक mfn. (-कः-का-की-कं) Momentary, transient.<BR>	 f. (-का) Lightning. E.<BR>क्षण a moment, affix कन् or ठक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=214-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षणिन्
क्षणिन् mfn. (-णी-णिनी-णि) Momentary, transient.<BR>	 f. (-णी) Night.<BR> E. क्षण,<BR>इनि and ङीप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=214-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षत|क्षतं
क्षत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Hit, hurt, wounded, &c.<BR>	 2. Broken, torn, rent.<BR>	 3.<BR>Trodden or broken down.<BR>	 4. Impaired, diminished.<BR>	 5. Destroyed.<BR>n. (-तं) A wound, sore, a hurt.<BR> E. क्षण् to hurt. affix क्त, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=214-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षतघ्न|क्षतघ्नः
क्षतघ्न m. (-घ्नः) The name of a plant, (Conyza lacera.)<BR>	 f. (-घ्नी) Lac, the<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=215-a" target="_blank">Page215-a+ 60</a>]<BR>animal dye.<BR> E. क्षत a wound, and घ्न what destroys or removes;<BR>from हन् to kill, affix ठक्, fem. affix ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=214-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षतज|क्षतजं
क्षतज n. (-जं)<BR>	 1. Blood.<BR>	 2. Pus, matter.<BR> E. क्षत a wound, and ज<BR>produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=215-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षततेजस्
क्षततेजस् mfn. (-जाः-जाः-जः) Dimmed, obscured, (as light or power.)<BR> E. क्षत<BR>and तेजस् splendour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=215-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षतविक्षत
क्षतविक्षत mfn. (-तः-ता-तंः) Mangled, wounded.<BR> E. क्षत and विक्षत wounded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=215-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षतविध्वंसिन्
क्षतविध्वंसिन् m. (-सी) A sort of potherb, (Convolvulus argenteus:) see<BR>वृद्धदार.<BR> E. क्षत a wound &c. ध्वंसि to attack, with वि prefix, and णिनि<BR>aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=215-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षतवृत्ति|क्षतवृत्तिः
क्षतवृत्ति f. (-त्तिः) Destitution, being without the means of support, liv-<BR>ing on what one can get.<BR> E. क्षत and वृत्ति maintenance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=215-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षतव्रत|क्षतव्रतः
क्षतव्रत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) A violator of a vow or religious engagement. E.<BR>क्षत broken. and व्रत a religious obligation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=215-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षतहर|क्षतहरं
क्षतहर n. (-रं) Agallochum or aloe wood: see अगुरु.<BR> E. क्षत a wound, and<BR>हर what removes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=215-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षतारि
क्षतारि mfn. (-रिः-रिः-रि) Victorious, triumphant.<BR> E. क्षत struck, and अरि<BR>a foe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=215-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षति|क्षतिः
क्षति f. (-तिः) A wound.<BR> E. क्षण् to hurt, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=215-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षतौजस्
क्षतौजस् mfn. (-जा-जाः-जं) Weakened, reduced, impaired.<BR> E. क्षत, and<BR>ओजस् strength.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=215-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षत्तृ
क्षत्तृ mfn. (-त्ता-त्त्री-त्तृ) Occupied, engaged in work.<BR>	 m. (-त्ता)<BR>	 1. A chario-<BR>teer, a coachman.<BR>	 2. A doorkeeper, a porter.<BR>	 3. The son of a<BR>Śūdra by Kṣatriya woman, whose employment is catching ani-<BR>mals that live in holes.<BR>	 4. The son of a female slave.<BR>	 5. A name<BR>of BRAHMĀ.<BR>	 6. The son of a Śūdra man and Vaiśya woman. E.<BR>क्षद a Sautra root, to screen or defend, to join or mix, Uṇādi affix<BR>तृच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=215-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षत्त्र
क्षत्त्र m. (-त्त्रः) A man of the second or military and regal class.<BR>	 n. (-त्त्रं)<BR>The body.<BR> E. क्षद Sautra root, to divide or eat, Uṇādi affix त्र; this<BR>word and its derivatives are commonly, for the sake of con-<BR>venience, written with one त, क्षत्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=215-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षत्त्रधर्म्म
क्षत्त्रधर्म्म m. (-र्म्मः) The duty of a Kṣatriya, bravery, military conduct.<BR>E. क्षत्त्र and धर्म्म duty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=215-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षत्त्रधर्म्मानुम
क्षत्त्रधर्म्मानुम mfn. (-गः-गा-गं) Following or observing the duty of a soldier.<BR>E. क्षत्त्रधर्म्म, and अनुग who follows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=215-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षत्त्रबन्धु
क्षत्त्रबन्धु mfn. (-न्धुः-न्धू or न्धुः-न्धु)<BR>	 1. A mere Kṣatriya, a certain Kṣatriya.<BR>2. A Kṣatriya, one of the military tribe: see ब्रह्मबन्धु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=215-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षत्त्रिन्
क्षत्त्रिन् m. (-त्त्री) A man of the military class.<BR> E. क्षत्त्र and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=215-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षत्त्रिय
क्षत्त्रिय mf. (-यः-या or याणी) A man or woman of the second or military<BR>tribe.<BR>	 f. (-यी) The wife of a Kṣatriya.<BR> E. क्षत्र, affix घ, fem. टाप् or<BR>ङीष्, in one form, with आनुक inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=215-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षत्त्रियजाति
क्षत्त्रियजाति f. (-तिः) The military tribe or caste.<BR> E. क्षत्त्रिय, and जाति caste.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=215-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षत्त्रियधर्म्म
क्षत्त्रियधर्म्म m. (-र्म्मः) The duty or occupation of the warrior tribe, war,<BR>government, &c.<BR> E. क्षत्त्रिय, and धर्म्म duty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=215-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षत्तियप्राय
क्षत्तियप्राय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Full of or abounding with the military tribe.<BR>E. क्षत्त्रिय, and प्राय most.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=215-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षद
क्षद Sautra r. 1st cl. (क्षदति)<BR>	 1. To eat.<BR>	 2. To pull to pieces, to divide.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=215-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षदत्
क्षदत् mfn. (-दन्-दन्ती-दत्)<BR>	 1. Eating.<BR>	 2. Dividing, tearing.<BR> E. क्षद् to eat,<BR>&c. v. शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=215-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षदन|क्षदनं
क्षदन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Eating.<BR>	 2. Tearing, dividing.<BR> E. क्षद् to eat, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=215-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षन्तव्य|क्षंतव्य
क्षन्तव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं) To be endured, to be suffered or submitted to<BR>patiently.<BR> E. क्षम् to bear, and तव्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=215-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षन्तृ|क्षंतृ
क्षन्तृ mfn. (-न्ता-न्त्री-न्तृ) Patient, resigned.<BR> E. क्षम् to bear, to be patient,<BR>तृच aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=215-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षप|क्षपः
क्षप r. 10th cl. (क्षपयति)<BR>	 1. To send, to throw, to cast, to direct, &c.<BR>	 2.<BR>To bear patiently. (इ) क्षपि r. 1st and 10th cls. (क्षम्पति, क्षम्पयति)<BR>	 1.<BR>To bear patiently, to endure.<BR>	 2. To compassionate.<BR>	 3. To shine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=215-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षपण|क्षपणः
क्षपण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Shameless, impudent.<BR>	 n. (-णं) Defilement, impuri-<BR>ty.<BR> E. क्षप् to throw away (shame), affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=215-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षपणक|क्षपणकः
क्षपणक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A Buddha.<BR>	 2. A Buddha mendicant.<BR>	 3. A Jaina<BR>mendicant.<BR> E. कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=215-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षपणी
क्षपणी f. (-णी)<BR>	 1. An oar.<BR>	 2. A net: see क्षेपणि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=215-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षपण्यु|क्षपण्युः
क्षपण्यु m. (-ण्युः) Offence, transgression.<BR> E. क्षप् to bear, अण्यु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=215-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षपयत्
क्षपयत् mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्)<BR>	 1. Bearing patiently, enduring.<BR>	 2. Casting,<BR>sending.<BR> E. क्षप् to send, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=215-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षपा
क्षपा f. (-पा) Night.<BR> E. क्षप् to send or reject, अ affix, and टाप् fem. do.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=215-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षपाकर|क्षपाकरः
क्षपाकर m. (-रः) The moon.<BR> E. क्षपा night, and कर who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=215-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षपाघन|क्षपाघनः
क्षपाघन m. (-नः) A dark cloud or clouds of night.<BR> E. क्षपा, and घन a<BR>cloud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=215-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षपाचर|क्षपाचरः
क्षपाचर m. (-रः) A fiend, a goblin.<BR> E. क्षपा, and चर who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=215-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षपाट|क्षपाटः
क्षपाट m. (-टः) A Rākṣasa, an imp or goblin.<BR> E. क्षपा night, and अट who<BR>goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=215-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षपानाथ|क्षपानाथः
क्षपानाथ m. (-थः) The moon.<BR> E. क्षपा, and नाथ lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=215-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षपान्त
क्षपान्त m. (-न्तः) Dawn, day-break.<BR> E. क्षपा, and अन्त end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=215-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षपाह
क्षपाह n. (-हं) A day and night.<BR> E. क्षपा. and अहन् a day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=215-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षपित
क्षपित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Submitted to, borne, endured.<BR>	 2. Sent, cast,<BR>directed.<BR> E. क्षप, and क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=215-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षम|क्षमं|क्षमः
क्षम (उ, ष, ञि) ञिक्षमुष r. 1st cl. (क्षमते) To bear or endure. (उ, इर, भ<BR>इर्क्षमुभ r. 4th. cl. (क्षाम्यति) To bear or endure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=215-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षम|क्षमं|क्षमः
क्षम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>	 1. Patient, resigned, enduring.<BR>	 2. Refraining from,<BR>forbearing.<BR>	 3. Able, adequate.<BR>	 4. Benevolent, friendly.<BR>	 5. Fit, ap-<BR>propriate, suitable, proper.<BR>	 f. (-मा)<BR>	 1. Patience.<BR>	 2. The earth.<BR>	 3.<BR>Night.<BR>	 4. A name of DURGĀ.<BR>	 n. (मं) Propriety, fitness.<BR> E. क्षम as<BR>above, affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=215-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षमान्वित
क्षमान्वित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Patient, enduring.<BR>	 2. Forgiving.<BR> E. क्षमा, and<BR>अन्वित possessed of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=215-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षमापर
क्षमापर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Patient, forbearing.<BR> E. क्षमा, पर practising.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=215-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षमाभुज|क्षमाभुजः
क्षमाभुज mfn. (-क्) Patient.<BR>	 m. (-क्) A king, a prince.<BR> E. क्षमा, the earth,<BR>&c. and भुज् who possesses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=215-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षमायुक्त
क्षमायुक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं) Patient, enduring,<BR> E. क्षमा. and युक्त joined with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=215-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षमावत्|क्षमावन्त्
क्षमावत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Patient, enduring.<BR> E. क्षमा, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=215-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षमितृ
क्षमितृ mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ) Patient, enduring.<BR> E. क्षम् to bear, affix तृच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=215-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षमिन्
क्षमिन् mfn. (-मी-मिनी-मि)<BR>	 1. Patient.<BR>	 2. Capable, able.<BR> E. क्षम् to bear,<BR>घिनुण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=215-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षय|क्षयः
क्षय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. Loss, waste, destruction, removal, &c.<BR>	 2. A destruction<BR>of the universe.<BR>	 3. Consumption, Phthisis pulmonalis.<BR>	 4. A house,<BR>an abode.<BR>	 5. Sickness in general.<BR>	 6. Decay, wasting away.<BR>	 7. In<BR>algebra, negative quantity, minus.<BR> E. क्षि to waste or destroy, affix<BR>अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=215-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षयकर
क्षयकर mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>	 1. Destroying, terminating. Liberating from<BR>existence.<BR> E. क्षय, and कर who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=215-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षयकाल|क्षयकालः
क्षयकाल m. (-लः) The end of all things, the period of destruction. E.<BR>क्षय, and काल time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=215-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षयकास|क्षयकासः
क्षयकास m. (-सः) A consumptive or phthisical cough.<BR> E. क्षय, and कास cough.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=215-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षयथु|क्षयथुः
क्षयथु m. (-थुः) Cough, consumption.<BR> E. क्षि to waste, अथुच् affix; some<BR>copies read this क्षवथु, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=215-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षयनाशिनी
क्षयनाशिनी f. (-नी) A plant, (Celtis Orientalis:) see जीवन्ती.<BR> E. क्षय con-<BR>sumption, and नाशिनी what removes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=215-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षयपक्ष|क्षयपक्षः
क्षयपक्ष m. (-क्षः) The dark fortnight, that of the moon's wane,<BR> E. क्षय<BR>and पक्ष half month.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=215-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षयवायु|क्षयवायुः
क्षयवायु m. (युः) The wind that is to blow at the end of the world. E.<BR>क्षय, and वायु wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=215-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षययुक्ति|क्षययुक्तिः
क्षययुक्ति f. (क्तिः) Necessity or opportunity of destroying.<BR> E. क्षय, and युक्त,<BR>fitness; also क्षययोग.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=215-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षयरोग|क्षयरोगः
क्षयरोग m. (-गः) Consumption.<BR> E. क्षय, and रोग disease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=215-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षयरोगित्व
क्षयरोगित्व n. (-त्वं) Consumption.<BR> E. क्षयरोगिन् and त्व affix; also with तल<BR>क्षयरोगिता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=215-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षयरोगिन्
क्षयरोगिन् mfn. (-गी-गिणी-गि) Consumptive, hectic.<BR> E. क्षय, and रोगिन्<BR>diseased.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=215-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षयसम्पद्|क्षयसंपद्
क्षयसम्पद् f. (-त् or -द्) Total loss, ruin, destruction.<BR> E. क्षय, and सम्पद्<BR>increase.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=216-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षयिन्
क्षयिन् mfn. (-यी-यिणी-यि)<BR>	 1. Wasting, decaying.<BR>	 3. Consumptive,<BR> E. क्षय,<BR>and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=216-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षयिष्णु
क्षयिष्णु mfn. (-ष्णुः-ष्णुः-ष्णु) Wasting, decaying perishing.<BR> E. क्षि to perish,<BR>इष्णुच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=216-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षर|क्षरं|क्षरः
क्षर r. 1st. cl. (क्षरति)<BR>	 1. To drop or let fall.<BR>	 2. To distil, to ooze, to<BR>trickle. With सं, To flow. With आ, r. of the 10th cl. (आक्षारयति) To<BR>accuse, to abuse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=216-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षर|क्षरं|क्षरः
क्षर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A cloud.<BR>	 2. Trickling oozing.<BR>	 n. (-रं) Water.<BR> E. क्षर् to<BR>drop, and अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=216-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षरज|क्षरजः
क्षरज mfn. (-जः-जा-जं) Produced by distillation, &c.<BR> E. क्षर, and ज born;<BR>also क्षरेज.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=216-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षरण|क्षरणं
क्षरण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Tricking, running.<BR>	 3. Distilling, dropping,<BR> E. क्षर and<BR>ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=216-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षरत्
क्षरत् mfn. (-रन्-रन्ती-रत्) Trickling, oozing. running<BR> E. क्षर् to trickle शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=216-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षरपत्रा
क्षरपत्रा f. (-त्रा) The Dronapushpa plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=216-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षरभाव
क्षरभाव mfn. (-वः-वा-व) Mutable, dissoluble.<BR> E. क्षर flowing, भाव property.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=216-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षरित
क्षरित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Oozed, trickling, dropped, flowing, liquified. E.<BR>क्षर, and क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=216-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षरिन्
क्षरिन् mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि) Dropping, flowing, trickling.<BR>	 m. (-री) The rainy<BR>season.<BR> E. क्षर water, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=216-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षरेज
क्षरेज mfn. (-जः-जा-जं) Produced by distilling, &c.<BR> E. क्षर in the seventh<BR>case, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=216-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षल
क्षल r. 1st cl. (क्षलति)<BR>	 1. To shake.<BR>	 2. To move, (some consider this as<BR>interchangeable with क्षर.) r. 10th cl. (क्षालयति) To purify, to clean-<BR>se or make clean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=216-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षव|क्षवः
क्षव m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. Sneezing.<BR>	 2. Cough, catarrh 2. A species of Mustard<BR>(Sinapis dichotoma, Rox,)<BR> E. क्षु to sneeze, affix अप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=216-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षवकृत्
क्षवकृत् mfn. (-त्) Sneezing, coughing.<BR> E. क्षव, and कृत् who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=216-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षविका
क्षविका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. A kind of rice.<BR>	 2. A woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=216-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षवथु|क्षवथुः
क्षवथु m. (-थुः)<BR>	 1. Cough, catarrh.<BR>	 2. Sneezing.<BR>	 3. Irritation of the throat,<BR>sore throat.<BR> E. क्षु to sneeze, &c. अथुच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=216-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षात्त्र
क्षात्त्र mfn. (-त्त्रः-त्त्री-त्त्रं) Belonging or relating to the military tribe. E.<BR>क्षत्त्र, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=216-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षान्त|क्षांत|क्षान्तः
क्षान्त mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं) Patient, enduring.<BR> E. क्षम् to bear, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=216-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षान्ति|क्षांति|क्षांतिः|क्षान्तिः
क्षान्ति f. (-न्तिः) Patience, forbearance, endurance.<BR> E. क्षम् to be patient,<BR>affix क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=216-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षान्तु|क्षांतु|क्षान्तुः
क्षान्तु mfn. (-न्तुः-न्तुः-न्तु) Patient, enduring.<BR> E. क्षम् to bear, Uṇādi affix तुन्<BR>the vowel is made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=216-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षाम|क्षामः
क्षाम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>	 1. Slender, slim, emaciated.<BR>	 2. Weak, infirm. E.<BR>क्षै to waste, affix क्त, form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=216-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षामता
क्षामता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Slenderness.<BR>	 2. Thinness, emaciation.<BR>	 3. Debility. E.<BR>क्षाम, and तल् affix: also with त्व, क्षामत्व.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=216-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षामास्य|क्षामास्यं
क्षामास्य n. (-स्यं) Improper regimen, diet. &c. Contraindicated in disease.<BR>E. क्षाम debilitating, and आस्य to be eaten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=216-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षार|क्षारं|क्षारः
क्षार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Glass.<BR>	 2. Juice, essence.<BR>	 3. Molasses, treacle.<BR>	 4. Salt.<BR>5. Ashes.<BR>	 5. A rogue, a cheat.<BR>	 7. Borax, borate of soda.<BR>	 8. Alkali,<BR>either soda or potash.<BR>	 9. Caustic Alkali, one species of cautery.<BR>	 n.<BR>(-रः) A factitious or medicinal salt, commonly black salt: see कृष्ण-<BR>लवण.<BR> E. क्षर् to prop, or distil, affix अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=216-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षारक|क्षारकः
क्षारक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A blossom, a new blown flower.<BR>	 2. A cage or basket<BR>for birds or fish.<BR>	 3. A washerman.<BR>	 4. Juice, essence.<BR> E. क्षर् to fall<BR>or drop, affix ण्वुल्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=216-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षारकर्म्मन्|क्षारकर्मन्
क्षारकर्म्मन् n. (-र्म्म) Applying caustic alkali (lapis infernalis) to proud<BR>flesh, &c.<BR> E. क्षार, and कर्म्मन् act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=216-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षारण|क्षारणं
क्षारण nm. (-णं-णः) Accusing, calumniating.<BR>	 n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Distilling.<BR>	 2.<BR>Converting to alkali or ashes.<BR> E. क्षार् to drop, causal form, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=216-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षारदला
क्षारदला f. (-ला) A potherb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=216-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षारद्रु|क्षारद्रुः
क्षारद्रु m. (-द्रुः) A tree, commonly Ghantaparali; see घण्टापाटलि; also क्षारवृक्ष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=216-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षारपत्र|क्षारपत्रः
क्षारपत्र n. (-त्रं) A potherb, (Chenopodium album.)<BR> E. क्षार juice, and प्रत्र<BR>a leaf; also क्षारपत्रक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=216-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षारमध्य|क्षारमध्यः
क्षारमध्य m. (-ध्यः) A shrub, (Achyranthes aspera:) also अपामार्ग.<BR> E. क्षार.<BR>alkali:, and मध्य middle; its alkaline ashes make it useful in wash-<BR>ing clothes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=216-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षारमृत्तिका
क्षारमृत्तिका f. (-का) Saline soil, especially an impure sulphate of soda. E.<BR>क्षार salt. and मृत्तिका earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=216-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षाररस|क्षाररसः
क्षाररस m. (-सः) A salt or alkaline flavour.<BR> E. क्षार, and रस flavour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=216-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षारवृक्ष|क्षारवृक्षः
क्षारवृक्ष m. (-क्षः) Any tree yielding abundant potash, as the plantain, &c.<BR>E. क्षार, and वृक्ष a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=216-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षारषट्क|क्षारषट्कं
क्षारषट्क n. (-ट्कं) Six kinds of trees distinguished by their juice, as<BR>the Butea frondosa, Grislea tomentosa, Achyranthes aspera, Cow-<BR>ach, Ghantaparali, Coraya.<BR> E. क्षार, and षट्क six.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=216-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षाराच्छ|क्षाराच्छं
क्षाराच्छ n. (-च्छं) Sea-salt.<BR> E. क्षार salt, and अच्छ clear, pure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=216-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षारिका
क्षारिका f. (-का) Hunger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=216-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षारित|क्षारितः
क्षारित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Guilty.<BR>	 2. Calumniated, falsely accused, speci-<BR>ally of adultery.<BR>	 3. Accused of crime.<BR>	 4. Distilled from saline mat-<BR>ter, strained through alkaline ashes, &c.<BR> E. क्षर् to go or fall, in<BR>the causal form, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=216-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षालन|क्षालनं
क्षालन n. (-नं) Washing, sprinkling, cleaning with water.<BR> E. क्षाल् to<BR>wash, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=216-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षालनीय
क्षालनीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) To be washed, to be cleaned with water. क्षल,<BR>and अनीयर् affix; also with तव्य and यत् क्षालितव्य and क्षाल्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=216-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षालयत्
क्षालयत् mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्) Washing, sprinkling,<BR> E. क्षल् to wash शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=216-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षालित|क्षालितं
क्षालित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Cleared, cleaned, washed.<BR> E. क्षाल् to cleanse,<BR>affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=216-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षि|क्षिः
क्षि r. 1st cl. (क्षयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To wane or decrease.<BR>	 2. To diminish, to disap-<BR>pear, to waste, to perish.<BR>	 3. To rule or possess with unlimited<BR>power. r. 5th cl. (क्षिणोति) To hurt or injure, to wound or kill. r.<BR>6th cl. (क्षियति)<BR>	 1. To dwell.<BR>	 2. To go or approach. (ष) क्षिष r. 9th cl.<BR>(क्षिणाति) To injure or kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=216-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षि|क्षिः
क्षि f. (-क्षिः) Residence, abode.<BR>	 2. Going, moving.<BR>	 3. Waste, loss, des-<BR>truction.<BR> E. क्षि to decrease, &c. कि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=216-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षिण
क्षिण (उ) क्षिणु r. 8th cl. (क्षिणोति or क्षिणुते or क्षेणोति-णुते) To hurt, to injure, to kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=216-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षित|क्षितः
क्षित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Wasted, decayed.<BR>	 2. Poor, miserable.<BR> E. क्षि to<BR>waste, affix क्त; also क्षीण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=216-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षिति|क्षितिः
क्षिति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. The earth.<BR>	 2. An abode, a dwelling, a house.<BR>	 3. Loss,<BR>destruction, wane.<BR>	 4. The period of the destruction of the universe.<BR>5. A perfume, commonly called Rochana.<BR> E. क्षि to waste, to dwell,<BR>&c, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=216-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षितिकण|क्षितिकणः
क्षितिकण mf. (-णः-णा) dust.<BR> E. क्षिति the earth, and कण a particle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=216-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षितिक्षम|क्षितिक्षमः
क्षितिक्षम m. (-मः) A tree, (Mimosa khayar.)<BR> E. क्षिति, and क्षम able.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=216-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षितिक्षित्
क्षितिक्षित् m. (-त्) A kind, a prince.<BR> E. क्षिति, and क्षि to dwell, affix क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=216-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षितिखण्ड
क्षितिखण्ड m. (-ण्डः) A clod or lump of earth.<BR> E. क्षिति, and खण्ड earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=216-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षितिज|क्षितिजं|क्षितिजः
क्षितिज mfn. (-जः-जा-जं) Earth-born, produced of or in the earth.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-जः)<BR>	 1. Mars.<BR>	 2. The demon NARAKA.<BR>	 3. An earthworm.<BR>	 f. (-जा)<BR>SITA.<BR> E. क्षिति, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=216-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षितिजन्तु|क्षितिजन्तुः
क्षितिजन्तु m. (-न्तुः) An earth. worm.<BR> E. क्षिति, and जन्तु animal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=216-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षितितल
क्षितितल n. (-लं)<BR>	 1. The region below the earth.<BR>	 2. The surface of the<BR>earth.<BR> E. क्षिति, and तल beneath.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=216-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षितिधर|क्षितिधरः
क्षितिधर m. (-रः) A mountain.<BR> E. क्षिति the earth. and धर what holds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=216-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षितिधारिन्
क्षितिधारिन् mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि) Carrying soil or earth.<BR> E. क्षिति, and धारिन्<BR>bearing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=216-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षितिनाग|क्षितिनागः
क्षितिनाग m. (-गः) An earth-worm.<BR> E. क्षिति, and नाग a serpent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=216-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षितिप|क्षितिपः
क्षितिप m. (-पः) A king.<BR> E. क्षिति, and प who protects; also क्षितिपाल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=216-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षितिपति|क्षितिपतिः
क्षितिपति m. (-तिः) king, a sovereign.<BR> E. क्षिति, and पति lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=216-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षितिपाल|क्षितिपालः
क्षितिपाल m. (-लः) A king, a prince.<BR> E. क्षिति, and पाल who protects.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=216-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षितिपीठ
क्षितिपीठ n. (-ठं) The surface of the earth.<BR> E. क्षिति, and पीठ a stool.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=216-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षितिप्रतिष्ठ
क्षितिप्रतिष्ठ mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठा-ष्ठं) Dwelling on the earth.<BR> E. क्षिति, and प्रतिष्ठ<BR>established.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=216-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षितिभृत्
क्षितिभृत् m. (-भृत्)<BR>	 1. A prince, a king.<BR>	 2. A mountain.<BR> E. क्षिति, and भृत्<BR>who nourishes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=217-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षितिमण्डल|क्षितिमंडल
क्षितिमण्डल n. (-लं) The earth, the globe.<BR> E. क्षिति, and मण्डल circle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=217-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षितिरुह|क्षितिरुहः
क्षितिरुह m. (-हः) A tree.<BR> E. क्षिति the earth, and रुह what mounts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=217-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षितिवर्द्धन
क्षितिवर्द्धन m. (-नः) A corpse.<BR> E. क्षिति the earth, and वर्द्धन what increases.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=217-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षितिसुत|क्षितिसुतः
क्षितिसुत m. (-तः)<BR>	 1. A name of the demon NARAKA, also of 2. Mars. E.<BR>क्षिति and सुत a son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=217-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षितीश|क्षितीशः
क्षितीश m. (-शः) A king.<BR> E. क्षिति, and ईश a prince.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=217-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षितीश्वर|क्षितीश्वरः
क्षितीश्वर m. (-रः) A king.<BR> E. क्षिति and ईश्वर a king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=217-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षित्यदिति|क्षित्यदितिः
क्षित्यदिति f. (-तिः) The mother of KṚṢṆA.<BR> E. क्षिति the earth, and अदिति<BR>the mother of the gods; the terrestrial parent of divinity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=217-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षित्वन्
क्षित्वन् m. (-त्वा) Air, wind.<BR> E. क्षि to go, Uṇādi affix, क्वनिप्, त inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=217-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षिद
क्षिद r. 1st cl. (क्षेदति) To utter an inarticulate sound, to moan as in<BR>grief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=217-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षिप|क्षिपः
क्षिप (औ) औक्षिप r. 4th cl. (क्षिप्यति) (ञ, आ) औक्षिञ् r. 6th cl. (क्षिपति-ते)<BR>To throw or cast, to direct or send. With अधि, prefixed, To abuse,<BR>to censure or reproach. With अव, To throw down. With आङ् 1. To<BR>attract.<BR>	 2. To ridicule. With उत्, To raise up, &c. With नि, To<BR>place, to deposit. With प्र, To throw far or violently. With वि To<BR>scatter, to disperse. with वि and नि, To deliver over, to resign, to<BR>leave. With सम and आङ् To remove, to send away. With सम्, 1. To<BR>abridge, to compress or contract.<BR>	 2. To disappear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=217-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षिप|क्षिपः
क्षिप m. (-पः)<BR>	 1. Throwing, casting.<BR>	 2. Reviling.<BR>	 3. One who throws,<BR>&c.<BR>	 f. (-पा)<BR>	 1. Sending, casting, throwing, &c.<BR>	 2. Night see क्षपा E.<BR>क्षिप् to throw, affix क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=217-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षिपक|क्षिपकः
क्षिपक m. (-कः) A warrior, a fighter.<BR> E. क्षिप throwing or directing,<BR>(darts, &c.) क Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=217-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षिपण|क्षिपणं
क्षिपण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Sending, dismissing, throwing, casting, &c.<BR>	 2. Revi-<BR>ling, abusing.<BR> E. क्षिप् to throw, &c. affix ल्यट् the radical vowel<BR>unchanged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=217-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षिपणि|क्षिपणिः
क्षिपणि m. (-णिः) A missile weapon f. (-णिः-णी) An oar.<BR> E. क्षिप् to throw<BR>to cast, Uṇādi affix अणि, and the radical vowel unchanged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=217-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षिपणु|क्षिपणुः
क्षिपणु m. (-णुः) Air, wind.<BR> E. क्षिप् to throw or send, to waft, Uṇādi<BR>affix अनु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=217-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षिपण्यु|क्षिपण्युः
क्षिपण्यु mfn. (-ण्युः-ण्युः-ण्यु)<BR>	 1. fragrant, sweet-smelling.<BR>	 2. Diffusive,<BR>what may be sent or scattered.<BR>	 m. (-ण्युः)<BR>	 1. The body.<BR>	 2. Spring,<BR>the season of spring.<BR> E. क्षिप् to send, &c. कन्युच् Uṇādi affix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=217-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षिपत्
क्षिपत् mfn. (-पत्-पन्ती-पत्)<BR>	 1. Throwing, casting.<BR>	 2. Abusing, reproaching<BR>E. क्षिप् to throw, affix शतृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=217-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षिप्नु|क्षिप्नुः
क्षिप्नु mfn. (-प्नुः-प्नुः-प्नु) Obstructive, throwing obstacles in the way;<BR>also क्षिप्णु<BR> E. क्षिप् to cast, &c. क्रु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=217-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षिप्त|क्षिप्तः
क्षिप्त mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं)<BR>	 1. Thrown, cast.<BR>	 2. Sent, despatched 3. Dismissed.<BR>f. (-प्ता) Night; also क्षिपा and क्षपा<BR> E. क्षिप् to throw, &c. affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=217-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षिप्तदेह
क्षिप्तदेह mfn. (-हः-हा-हं) Prostrate, lying down.<BR> E. क्षिप्त, and देह the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=217-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षिप्ति|क्षिप्तिः
क्षिप्ति f. (-प्तिः)<BR>	 1. Throwing.<BR>	 2. Sending, ordering.<BR>	 3. Solving a riddle,<BR>explaining or understanding a hidden meaning.<BR> E. क्षिप् to throw,<BR>क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=217-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षिप्यत्
क्षिप्यत् mfn. (-प्यन्-प्यन्ती-प्यत्)<BR>	 1. Throwing.<BR>	 2. Sending.<BR> E. क्षिप 4th cl. to send, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=217-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षिप्यमाण
क्षिप्यमाण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>	 1. Tossing, throwing 2. Casting aside, thro-<BR>wing off.<BR>	 3. Sending, directing.<BR> E. क्षिप and शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=217-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षिप्र|क्षिप्रं
क्षिप्र mfn. (-प्रः-प्रा-प्रं) Quickly, speedily, quick, swift. adv.<BR>	 n. (-प्रं)<BR>Quickly.<BR> E. क्षिप् to send or despatch, Uṇādi affix रक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=217-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षिप्रपाकिन्
क्षिप्रपाकिन् m. (-की) A kind of tree, (Hibiscus populneoides:) see<BR>गर्द्ध्वभाण्ड<BR> E. क्षिप्र quick, and पाकिन् what ripens.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=217-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षिया
क्षिया f. (-या) Loss, waste, destruction.<BR> E. क्षि to waste, अङ् and टाप् affix<BR>es, इ substituted for the penultimate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=217-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षिव
क्षिव (उ) क्षिवु r. 4th cl. (क्षीव्यति) To eject from the mouth, to vomit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=217-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षी
क्षी r. 1st cl. (क्षयति-ते) To hurt or injure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=217-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीज
क्षीज r. 1st cl. (क्षीजति) To sound inarticulately, to sigh or groan as in<BR>distress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=217-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीजन|क्षीजनं
क्षीजन n. (-नं) The whistling of hollow reeds or bamboos.<BR> E. क्षीज् to<BR>sound inarticulately, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=217-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीण|क्षीणः
क्षीण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>	 1. Thin, emaciated, feeble.<BR>	 2. Thin, slender.<BR>	 3.<BR>Wasted, diminished, worn away, expended.<BR>	 4. Destroyed, lost.<BR>	 5.<BR>Injured, broken, torn.<BR>	 6. Subdued, suppressed.<BR>	 7. Poor, miserable.<BR>E. क्षि to waste, affix क्त, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=217-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीणता
क्षीणता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. slenderness, delicacy.<BR>	 2. Thinness, emaciation.<BR>	 3.<BR>Diminution, decay.<BR> E. तल् added to the last; also with त्व, क्षीणत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=217-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीणपाप
क्षीणपाप mfn. (-पः-पा-पं) Purified, having suffered the consequences of<BR>sin.<BR> E. क्षीण, and पाप sin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=217-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीणपुण्य
क्षीणपुण्य mfn. (-ण्यः-ण्या-ण्यं)<BR>	 1. Abandoned.<BR>	 2. Having enjoyed the fruits<BR>of virtue, and being doomed by another birth to labour for more.<BR>E. क्षीण, and पुण्य virtue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=217-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीणमध्य
क्षीणमध्य mfn. (-ध्यः-ध्या-ध्यं) Slender-waisted.<BR> E. क्षीण, and मध्य middle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=217-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीणवत्
क्षीणवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Wasted, decayed.<BR> E. क्षि to waste, and<BR>क्तवतु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=217-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीणवासिन्
क्षीणवासिन् mfn. (-सी-सिनी-सि) Inhabiting a destructible house.<BR>	 m. (-सी)<BR>A dove or pigeon.<BR> E. क्षीण, and वासिन् abiding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=217-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीणविक्रान्त|क्षीणविक्रांत
क्षीणविक्रान्त mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं) Cowed, deprived of courage or prowess.<BR>E. क्षीण, and विक्रान्त valiant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=217-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीणवृत्ति
क्षीणवृत्ति mfn. (-त्तिः-त्तिः-त्ति) Out of employ. out of bread, having no<BR>maintenance.<BR> E. क्षीण lost, and वृत्ति practice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=217-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीणशक्ति
क्षीणशक्ति mfn. (-क्तिः-क्तिः-क्ति) Weak, feeble, impotent.<BR> E. क्षीण, and शक्ति<BR>vigour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=217-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीणाज्यकर्म्मन्|क्षीणाज्यकर्मन्
क्षीणाज्यकर्म्मन् m. (-र्म्मा) A Bauddha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=217-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीणाष्टकर्म्मन्|क्षीणाष्टकर्मन्
क्षीणाष्टकर्म्मन् m. (-र्म्मा) A Jina, an inspired teacher according to the<BR>Jainas.<BR> E. क्षीण, and अष्टकर्म्मन् eight natural acts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=217-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीब|क्षीबः
क्षीब (ऋ) क्षीबृ r. 1st cl. (क्षीबते) To be intoxicated, (literally or meta-<BR>phorically.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=217-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीब|क्षीबः
क्षीब mfn. (-बः-बा-बं) Drunk, intoxicated.<BR> E. क्षीब् to be drunk, affix क्त,<BR>deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=217-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीबता
क्षीबता f. (-ता) Intoxication.<BR> E. तल् added to the last; also with त्व, क्षीबत्वं<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=217-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीयमाण
क्षीयमाण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Perishing, wasting away.<BR> E. क्षि to perish,<BR>शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=217-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीर|क्षीरः
क्षीर n. (-रं)<BR>	 1. Water.<BR>	 2. Milk.<BR>	 f. (-री) A small shrub (Asclepia rosea;)<BR>also दुग्धिका.<BR>	 2. A tree, a species of Mimosa, (M. kauki, Rox) also<BR>क्षीरिका.<BR>	 3. Gigantic swallow-wort.<BR>	 4. Euphorbia; several kinds,<BR>particularly, E. hirta. E. thymifolia, and E. chamæsyce.<BR> E. घस् to<BR>eat, ईरन् Uṇādi affix; the fem. nouns are derived from क्षीर milk.<BR>the plants yielding a milky juice or sap, upon expression or<BR>incision.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=217-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीरकण्ठ|क्षीरकंठ|क्षीरकण्ठः
क्षीरकण्ठ m. (-ण्ठः) An infant, a young child. F. क्षीर milk, and कण्ठ<BR>throat; also with कन् added क्षीरकण्ठक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=217-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीरकन्दा
क्षीरकन्दा f. (-न्दा) A kind of potherb, black Bhuincaonra, (Convolvulus<BR>paniculatus.)<BR> E. क्षीर water, and कन्द root: having a watery root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=217-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीरकाकोलिका
क्षीरकाकोलिका f. (-का) A drug, and one of the eight principal medica-<BR>ments of the Hindus; it is a root from the Himālaya.<BR> E. क्षीर milk,<BR>and काकोलि a drug, कन् added; yielding, when fresh, a milky<BR>juice; also क्षीरकाकोली.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=217-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीरकाकोली
क्षीरकाकोली f. (-ली) See the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=217-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीरकीट|क्षीरकीटः
क्षीरकीट m. (-टः) An insect or animalcule generated by the fermenta-<BR>tion of milk<BR> E. क्षीर milk, and कीट a worm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=217-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीरज|क्षीरजं
क्षीरज n. (-जं) Coagulated or curdled milk.<BR> E. क्षीर milk, and ज pro-<BR>duced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=217-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीरद
क्षीरद mfn. (-दः-दा-दं) What gives or yields milk.<BR> E. क्षीर. and द what<BR>gives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=217-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीरदल|क्षीरदलः
क्षीरदल m. (-लः) Gigantic swallow-wort.<BR> E. क्षीर milk, and दल leaf; the<BR>leaves, &c. yielding, on expression or incision, a milky juice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=217-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीरनीर|क्षीरनीरं
क्षीरनीर n. (-रं) Embracing, embrace.<BR> E. क्षीर milk, and नीर water; mix-<BR>ing like milk and water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=217-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीरप|क्षीरपः
क्षीरप mfn. (-पः-पा-पं) Drinking milk. who or what drinks it.<BR> E. क्षीर, and<BR>प who drinks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=218-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीरपर्णी
क्षीरपर्णी f. (-र्णी) See क्षीरदल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=218-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीरपाण|क्षीरपाणं|क्षीरपाणः
क्षीरपाण n. (-णं) drinking milk; also क्षीरपान.<BR>	 m. plu. (-णाः) The name of<BR>a people, the milk-drinkers.<BR> E. क्षीर, and पान drink; in the second<BR>sense, न is changed always to ण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=218-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीरपायिन्
क्षीरपायिन् mfn. (-यी-यिणी-यि)<BR>	 1. Drinking milk, sucking, &c.<BR>	 2. Drinking<BR>or imbibing water repeatedly.<BR> E. क्षीर, and पायिन् who drinks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=218-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीरपायिन्
क्षीरपायिन् m. plu. (-यिणः) The people calld Usinaras, the milk-drink-<BR>ers.<BR> E. क्षीर, पा to drink, णिनि affix, य inserted, and न final changed<BR>to ण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=218-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीरमोचक
क्षीरमोचक m. (-कः) A tree, (Morunga hyperanthera.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=218-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीरमोरट|क्षीरमोरटः
क्षीरमोरट m. (-टः) A plant, a kind of Murva: see मूर्व्वा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=218-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीरयष्टिक
क्षीरयष्टिक n. (-कं) A dish of liquorice and milk.<BR> E. क्षीर, and यष्टिक made<BR>of liquorice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=218-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीरबल्ली
क्षीरबल्ली f. (-ल्ली) The dark Bhuincaonra, (Convolvulus paniculatus) E.<BR>क्षीर water, and वल्ली pedicle: see क्षीरकन्दा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=218-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीरविकृति|क्षीरविकृतिः
क्षीरविकृति f. (-तिः) Inspissated milk.<BR> E. क्षीर milk, and विकृति change of<BR>form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=218-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीरविदारिका
क्षीरविदारिका f. (-का) The dark Bhuincaonra; also क्षीरविदारी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=218-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीरविदारी
क्षीरविदारी f. (-री) The white or black Bhuincaonra, (Convolvulus pani-<BR>culatus:) see भूमिकुष्माण्डक.<BR> E. क्षीर water, and विदारी the same<BR>plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=218-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीरवृक्ष|क्षीरवृक्षः
क्षीरवृक्ष m. (-क्षः) Glomerous fig tree, (Ficus glomerata;) also उडुम्बर. E.<BR>क्षीर, milk. and बृक्ष a tree, the leaves and bark yielding a white<BR>milky juice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=218-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीरशर|क्षीरशरः
क्षीरशर m. (-रः) Cream, the surface or skim of milk.<BR> E. क्षीर milk, and<BR>शर what goes over or on.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=218-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीरशुक्ल|क्षीरशुक्लः
क्षीरशुक्ल m. (-क्लः) An aquatic plant, (Trapa bispinosa, Rox.)<BR>	 f. (-क्ला) The<BR>pale Bhuincaonra: see भूमिकुष्माण्डक.<BR> E. क्षीर milk, and शुक्ल white;<BR>white as milk, the fruit, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=218-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीरसार|क्षीरसारः
क्षीरसार m. (-रः) Butter.<BR> E. क्षीर, and सार essence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=218-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीरस्फटिक|क्षीरस्फटिकः
क्षीरस्फटिक m. (-कः) A precious stone, described as a milky crystal, (opal<BR>or cat's eye)<BR> E. क्षीर milk, and स्फटिक crystal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=218-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीराद|क्षीरादः
क्षीराद m. (-दः) An infant at the breast.<BR> E. क्षीर, and अद who feeds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=218-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीराब्धि|क्षीराब्धिः
क्षीराब्धि m. (-ब्धिः) The sea of milk, one of the seven seas surrounding<BR>as many worlds.<BR> E. क्षीर milk, and अब्धि the ocean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=218-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीराब्धिज|क्षीराब्धिजं|क्षीराब्धिजः
क्षीराब्धिज m. (-जः) The moon.<BR>	 f. (-जा) A name of the goddess LAKṢMĪ.<BR>n. (-जं)<BR>	 1. Sea salt.<BR>	 2. A pearl.<BR> E. क्षीराब्धि the sea of milk, and ज<BR>born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=218-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीराब्धितनया
क्षीराब्धितनया f. (-या) A name of LAKṢMĪ:<BR> E. क्षीराब्धि the sea of milk,<BR>and तनया daughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=218-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीरान्नाद
क्षीरान्नाद m. (-दः) An infant both fed and suckled.<BR> E. क्षीर, and अन्न food,<BR>अद who eats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=218-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीराविका
क्षीराविका f. (-का) A sort of Asclepias; see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=218-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीरावी
क्षीरावी f. (-वी) A sort of Asclepias, (A. rosia, Rox;) also दुग्धिका<BR> E. क्षीर<BR>milk or milky juice, अव् to contain, affixes अण् and ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=218-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीराह्व|क्षीराह्वः
क्षीराह्व m. (-ह्वः) The Saral, a kind of pine.<BR> E. क्षीर milk, and आह्व what<BR>is named; or it may mean that the tree is also named simply क्षीर,<BR>that which yields a milky juice or sap.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=218-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीरिका
क्षीरिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. A tree bearing an edible fruit, (Mimusops kauki,<BR>Rox.)<BR>	 2. A potherb, Bhuicaonra, (Convolvulus paniculatus.)<BR> E. क्षीर<BR>milk, affix ठक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=218-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीरिणी
क्षीरिणी f. (-णी)<BR>	 1. A milch cow.<BR>	 2. A tree bearing an edible fruit, (Mi-<BR>musops kauki.)<BR>	 3. A medicinal kind of the moon plant or acid<BR>Asclepias.<BR> E. क्षीर milk, and इनि affix, alluding to its juice, fem.<BR>affix ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=218-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीरिन्
क्षीरिन् mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>	 1. Milky, yielding milk.<BR>	 2. Having milk.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-री) A sort of Mimusops: see क्षीरिका.<BR> E. क्षीर milk, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=218-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीरेयी
क्षीरेयी f. (-यी) An oblation of milk, rice, and sugar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=218-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीरोद|क्षीरोदः
क्षीरोद m. (-दः) The sea of milk.<BR> E. क्षीर milk, and उद water: it also<BR>implies the sea in general.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=218-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीरोदतनया
क्षीरोदतनया f. (-या) A name of LAKṢMĪ.<BR> E. क्षीरोद the sea of milk, and<BR>तनया daughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=218-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीरोदनन्दन|क्षीरोदनन्दनः
क्षीरोदनन्दन m. (-नः) The moon.<BR> E. क्षीरोद the ocean in general, and नन्दन<BR>a son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=218-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीव|क्षीवः
क्षीव (उ) क्षीवु r. 1st cl. (क्षीवति)<BR>	 1. To spit or sputter, to eject from the<BR>mouth. 2, To be drunk: see क्षिव, also क्षीब.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=218-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीब|क्षीबः
क्षीब mfn. (-बः-बा-बं) Drunk, intoxicated.<BR> E. क्षीव, and क्त affix; also क्षीव.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=218-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीवता
क्षीवता f. (-ता) Drunkenness, intoxication.<BR> E. तल् added to the last; also<BR>with त्व, क्षीवत्वं; also क्षीवता, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=218-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षु|क्षुः
क्षु (टु) टुक्षु r. 2d cl. (क्षौति) To sneeze, to make any such sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=218-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुण|क्षुणः
क्षुण m. (-णः) The soap berry plant, (Sapindus saponaria.)<BR> E. क्षुद् to<BR>bruise, डुण aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=218-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुण्ण|क्षुण्णं
क्षुण्ण mfn. (-ण्णः-ण्णा-ण्णं)<BR>	 1. Bruised, pounded.<BR>	 2. Exercised, practiced, skil-<BR>ful.<BR>	 3. One versed in sacred science, but described as unable to<BR>explain or teach it.<BR>	 4. Defeated, overcame.<BR> E. क्षुद् to bruise, &c.<BR>affix क्त, form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=218-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुत्
क्षुत् f. (-क्षुत्)<BR>	 1. Sneezing; also क्षुत.<BR> E. क्षु to sneeze, affix क्किप्, तुक् is add-<BR>ed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=218-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुत|क्षुतं|क्षुतः
क्षुत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Sneezed, sneezing.<BR>	 mf. (-तः-ता)<BR>	 1. Sneezing.<BR>	 2.<BR>Cough.<BR> E. क्षु to sneeze, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=218-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुतवत्
क्षुतवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Sneezing.<BR> E. क्षु to sneeze, क्तवतु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=218-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुताभिजनन|क्षुताभिजननः
क्षुताभिजनन m. (-नः) Black-mustard.<BR> E. क्षुत sneezing, and अभिजनन what<BR>produces; also क्षुधाभिजनन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=218-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुत्करी
क्षुत्करी f. (-री) Black-mustard.<BR> E. क्षुत् sneezing, करी making.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=218-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुत्तृणोपपीडित
क्षुत्तृणोपपीडित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Hungry and thirsty.<BR> E. क्षुध् with तृष्णा<BR>thirst, and उपपीडित distressed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=218-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुत्पिपासित
क्षुत्पिपासित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Hnngry and thirsty,<BR> E. क्षुध्, and पिपासा<BR>thirst, इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=218-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुत्प्रतीकार
क्षुत्प्रतीकार m. (-रः) Allaying hunger, eating.<BR> E. क्षुध्, and प्रतीकार counter-<BR>acting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=218-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुद|क्षुदः
क्षुद (ञ, इर, औ) औ क्षुदिर r. 7th cl. (क्षुणत्ति, क्षुत्ते) To pound, to bruise, to<BR>reduce, to powder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=218-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुद्र|क्षुद्रः
क्षुद्र mfn. (-द्रः-द्रा-द्रं)<BR>	 1. Small, little.<BR>	 2. Mean, low.<BR>	 3. Mean, niggardly,<BR>avaricious.<BR>	 4. Cruel.<BR>	 5. Poor, indigent.<BR>	 f. (-द्रा)<BR>	 1. A woman maim-<BR>ed or crippled, wanting a limb, &c.<BR>	 2. A dancing girl.<BR>	 3. A whore,<BR>a harlot.<BR>	 4. A fly.<BR>	 5. A bee or wasp.<BR>	 6. A gnat, &c.<BR>	 7. A prickly<BR>nightshade: see कण्टकारी.<BR>	 8. The egg plant, (Solanum melongena.)<BR>9. Sorrel, (Oxalis monadelpha.)<BR> E. क्षुद् to bruise or pound, Uṇādi<BR>affix रक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=218-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुद्रकम्बु|क्षुद्रकंबु|क्षुद्रकम्बुः
क्षुद्रकम्बु m. (-म्बुः) A small shell.<BR> E. क्षुद्र small, and कम्बु a shell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=218-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुद्रघण्टिका|क्षुद्रघंटिका
क्षुद्रघण्टिका f. (-का) A tinkling ornament, a girdle of small bells, &c. E.<BR>क्षुद्र small, घण्टा a clock or bell, affix कन्, and the fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=218-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुद्रचूड|क्षुद्रचूडः
क्षुद्रचूड m. (-डः) A kind of small bird.<BR> E. क्षुद्र small, and चूडा a crest,<BR>small-crested.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=218-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुद्रजन्तु|क्षुद्रजंतु|क्षुद्रजन्तुः
क्षुद्रजन्तु m. (-न्तुः)<BR>	 1. Any small animal.<BR>	 2. A kind of worm, (Julus.) E.<BR>क्षुद्र small, and जन्तु animal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=218-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुद्रजीर|क्षुद्रजीरः
क्षुद्रजीर m. (-रः) Small cummin.<BR> E. क्षुद्र small, and जीर cummin seed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=218-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुद्रता
क्षुद्रता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Smallness, minuteness.<BR>	 2. Inferiority, insignificance,<BR>meanness.<BR> E. तल् added to क्षुद्र; also with त्व, क्षुद्रत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=218-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुद्रदंशिका
क्षुद्रदंशिका f. (-का) A small gadfly.<BR> E. क्षुद्र, and दंशिका a gadfly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=218-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुद्रदंशी
क्षुद्रदंशी f. (-शी) A small gadfly.<BR> E. क्षुद्र, and दंशी a gadfly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=218-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुद्रनासिक|क्षुद्रनासिकः
क्षुद्रनासिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Having a little nose.<BR> E. क्षुद्र, and नासिका the<BR>nose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=218-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुद्रपत्रा
क्षुद्रपत्रा f. (-त्रा) Wood-sorrel, (Oxalis monadelpha.)<BR> E. क्षुद्र, and पत्र a leaf,<BR>small-leaved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=218-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुद्रफलक|क्षुद्रफलकः
क्षुद्रफलक m. (-कः) A tree, (Celtis orientalis:) see जीवन.<BR> E. क्षुद्र, and फल<BR>fruit, कन् added, bearing a small fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=218-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुद्रफला
क्षुद्रफला f. (-ला) A plant. (Ardisia solanacea.)<BR> E. क्षुद्र, and फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=218-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुद्रबुद्धि|क्षुद्रबुद्धिः
क्षुद्रबुद्धि mfn. (-द्धिः-द्धिः-द्धि) Simple, silly, ignorant.<BR> E. क्षुद्र, and बुद्धि under-<BR>standing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=219-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुद्ररोग|क्षुद्ररोगः
क्षुद्ररोग m. (-गः) A minor disease, one of little importance.<BR> E. क्षुद्र, and<BR>रोग disease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=219-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुद्रवंशा
क्षुद्रवंशा f. (-शा) A plant (Dioscorea:) see वराहक्रान्ता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=219-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुद्रशङ्ख|क्षुद्रशंख|क्षुद्रशङ्खः
क्षुद्रशङ्ख m. (-ङ्खः) A small shell.<BR> E. क्षुद्र, and शङ्ख a shell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=219-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुद्रशीर्ष|क्षुद्रशीर्षः
क्षुद्रशीर्ष m. (-र्षः) A tree, (Celosia cristata.)<BR> E. क्षुद्र, and शीर्ष the head,<BR>having a small head.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=219-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुद्रसहा
क्षुद्रसहा f. (-हा) A plant, commonly Mugai: see मुद्गपर्णी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=219-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुद्रहिङ्गुलिका
क्षुद्रहिङ्गुलिका f. (-का) A prickly nightshade, (Solanum jacquini.)<BR>a small species.<BR> E. क्षुद्र small, and हिङ्गुली the plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=219-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुद्रहिङ्गुली
क्षुद्रहिङ्गुली f. (-ली) See the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=219-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुद्राण्डमत्स्यसङ्घात|क्षुद्राण्डमत्स्यसंघात|क्षुद्राण्डमत्स्यसंघातः
क्षुद्राण्डमत्स्यसङ्घात m. (-तः) Small fly.<BR> E. क्षुद्र small, अण्ड an egg, मत्स्य a fish,<BR>and सङ्घात a heap.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=219-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुद्राम्लपनस|क्षुद्राम्लपनसः
क्षुद्राम्लपनस m. (-सः) A tree, (Artocarpus lacucha:) see लकुच.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=219-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुद्राम्ला
क्षुद्राम्ला f. (-म्ला) Wood-sorrel, (Oxalis monadelpha.)<BR> E. क्षुद्र, and अम्ल<BR>sour; a small and acid plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=219-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुध
क्षुध (ऌ औ) औक्षधॢ r. 4th cl. (क्षुध्यति) To be hungry, to hunger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=219-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुध्
क्षुध् f. (-क्षुत् or क्षुद्) Hunger.<BR> E. क्षुध् to be hungry, affix क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=219-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुधा
क्षुधा f. (-धा) Hunger.<BR> E. क्षुध् to be hungry, affixes अङ् and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=219-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुधाकर
क्षुधाकर mfn. (-रः-री-रं) Causing hunger, improving the appetite<BR> E. क्षुधा,<BR>and कर what makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=219-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुधाध्वंस
क्षुधाध्वंस m. (-सः) Allaying hunger.<BR> E. क्षुधा, and ध्वंस destruction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=219-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुधापीडित
क्षुधापीडित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Hungry, starving.<BR> E. क्षुधा, and पीडित pained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=219-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुधाभिजनन|क्षुधाभिजननः
क्षुधाभिजनन m. (-नः) Black mustard.<BR> E. क्षुधा hunger, and अभिजनन caus-<BR>ing, promoting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=219-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुधार्त्त|क्षुधार्त|क्षुधार्त्तः
क्षुधार्त्त m. (-र्त्तः-र्त्ता-र्त्तं) Hungry, hungered.<BR> E. क्षुधा and आर्त्त pained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=219-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुधाशान्ति
क्षुधाशान्ति f. (-न्तिः) Satisfaction, satiety, allaying hunger.<BR> E. क्षुधा, and<BR>शान्ति appeasing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=219-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुधित|क्षुधितः
क्षुधित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Hungered, hungry.<BR> E. क्षुध् to be hungry, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=219-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुधुन|क्षुधुनः
क्षुधुन m. (-नः) A savage, a barbarian.<BR> E. क्षुध् to be hungry, Uṇādi affix<BR>उनन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=219-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुप|क्षुपः
क्षुप m. (-पः) A small tree, one with short branches and roots, a bush,<BR>a shurb.<BR> E. क्षु to sound, aff. प.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=219-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुब्ध|क्षुब्धः
क्षुब्ध mfn. (-ब्धः-ब्धा-ब्धं)<BR>	 1. Agitated, tossed, stirred.<BR>	 2. Agitated men-<BR>tally, anxious, disturbed.<BR>	 m. (-ब्धः) The churning stick.<BR> E. क्षुभ् to<BR>stir, to agitate, affix क्त, form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=219-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुभ|क्षुभः
क्षुभ r. 1st cl. (क्षोभति)<BR>	 1. To be confused or agitated.<BR>	 2. To stir or dis-<BR>turb. r. 4th cl. and 9th cl. (क्षुभ्यति and क्षुभ्नाति)<BR>	 2. To shake, to-<BR>tremble, to be unsteady.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=219-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुभित|क्षुभितः
क्षुभित mfn. (-तः-ता-त)<BR>	 1. Frightened, alarmed, afraid.<BR>	 2. Agitated,<BR>tossed, set in motion.<BR>	 3. Agitated mentally, disturbed, anxious.<BR>	 4.<BR>Angry, enraged.<BR> E. क्षुभ् to shake, to be agitated, to stir, &c. affix क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=219-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुमा
क्षुमा f. (-मा)<BR>	 1. Linseed, (Linum usitatissimum.)<BR>	 2. A sort of flax, Ben-<BR>gal San.<BR>	 3. The indigo plant.<BR>	 4. A sort or creeper.<BR> E. क्षु to sound,<BR>affix मक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=219-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुर|क्षुरः
क्षुर r. 6th cl. (क्षुरति)<BR>	 1. To cut.<BR>	 2. To scratch, to make lines or furrows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=219-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुर|क्षुरः
क्षुर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A razor.<BR>	 2. A plant, (Barleria longifolia.)<BR>	 3. Also<BR>Tribulus lanuginosus: see गोक्षुर.<BR>	 4. A horse's hoof; also खुर 5.<BR>The hoof of a cow, &c.<BR>	 6. The foot of a bedstead.<BR>	 f. (-री) A knife.<BR>E. क्षुर् to scratch or cut, Uṇādi affix रन् and the final consonant<BR>rejected; also खुर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=219-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुरक|क्षुरकः
क्षुरक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A plant, commonly Tila.<BR>	 2. Barleria longifolia.<BR>	 3.<BR>Tribulus lanuginosus.<BR> E. क्षुर् to scratch, &c. क्कुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=219-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुरप्र|क्षुरप्रः
क्षुरप्र m. (-प्रः)<BR>	 1. kind of arrow, one with a sharp-horse-shoe-shaped<BR>head.<BR>	 2. A sort of hoe or weeding spade.<BR> E. क्षुर a hoof, and प्रथ् to<BR>go, ड affix; also खुरप्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=219-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुरभाण्ड|क्षुरभांड|क्षुरभाण्डं
क्षुरभाण्ड n. (-ण्डं) A razor case.<BR> E. क्षुर, and भाण्ड a vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=219-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुरमर्द्दिन्|क्षुरमर्दिन्
क्षुरमर्द्दिन् m. (-र्दी) A barber.<BR> E. क्षुर a razor, and मृद् to destroy, affix<BR>णिनि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=219-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुरिणी
क्षुरिणी f. (-णी) A kind of yam: see वराहक्रान्ता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=219-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुरिन्
क्षुरिन् mf. (-री-रिणी) A male or female barber.<BR> E. क्षुर a razor, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=219-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुल्ल|क्षुल्लः
क्षुल्ल mfn. (-ल्लः-ल्ला-ल्लं) Little, small.<BR> E. क्षुद् to pound, affix क्विप्, क्षुद<BR>powder, dust, ल from ला to get, to be, affix ड; also खुल्ल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=219-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुल्लक|क्षुल्लकः
क्षुल्लक mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>	 1. Little; small.<BR>	 2. Hard.<BR>	 3. Poor, indigent.<BR>	 4.<BR>Low, vile.<BR>	 5. Wicked, malicious, abandoned.<BR>	 6. Young, youngest.<BR>7. Pained, distressed, m. (-कः) A small shell.<BR> E. क्षुल्ल as above, कन्<BR>added, also खुल्लक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=219-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुल्लतात|क्षुल्लतातः
क्षुल्लतात m. (-तः) Sce the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=219-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुल्लतातक|क्षुल्लतातकः
क्षुल्लतातक m. (-कः) A paternal uncle.<BR> E. क्षुल्ल youngest, and तात a father,<BR>कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=219-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुवत्
क्षुवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Sneezing.<BR> E. क्षु, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=219-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षेड
क्षेड r. 10th cl. (क्षेडयति) To eat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=219-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षेड
क्षेड m. (-डः)<BR>	 1. Disease in the ear.<BR>	 2. Poison.<BR>	 3. Sound: see क्षेड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=219-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षेडित
क्षेडित m. (-तः) Roar of a lion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=219-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षेत्र|क्षेत्रं
क्षेत्र n. (-त्रं)<BR>	 1. A field.<BR>	 2. The body.<BR>	 3. A wife.<BR>	 4. A pure or sacred<BR>spot, a place of pilgrimage, as Puri, &c.<BR>	 5. Plane figure, geo-<BR>metry.<BR>	 6. A diagram.<BR> E. क्षि to dwell, &c. affix ष्ट्रन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=219-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षेत्रकर|क्षेत्रकरः
क्षेत्रकर mfn. (-रः-री-रं) Making a field, cultivating it, &c.<BR> E. क्षेत्र, कर<BR>who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=219-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षेत्रज|क्षेत्रजः
क्षेत्रज mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>	 1. Produced in a field, (as corn, &c.)<BR>	 2. Born of<BR>the body, &c.<BR>	 m. (-जः) A son, the offspring of the wife by a kins-<BR>man or person duly appointed to procreate issue to the husband.<BR>E. क्षेत्र wife, and ज born, born of the wife only; this is one of the<BR>twelve kinds of issue acknowledged by the old Hindu law.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=219-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षेत्रज्ञ|क्षेत्रज्ञः
क्षेत्रज्ञ mfn. (-ज्ञः-ज्ञा-ज्ञं)<BR>	 1. Clever, dexterous, skilful.<BR>	 2. A husbandman,<BR>&c.<BR>	 m. (-ज्ञः)<BR>	 1. The soul, the emanation of divinity residing in the<BR>body.<BR>	 2. A libertine, a whore-monger.<BR> E. क्षेत्र a field, the body,<BR>&c, and ज्ञ who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=219-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षेत्रपति|क्षेत्रपतिः
क्षेत्रपति m. (-तिः) A land-owner, a farmer, the master of a field.<BR> E. क्षेत्र,<BR>and पति master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=219-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षेत्रभूमि|क्षेत्रभूमिः
क्षेत्रभूमि f. (-मिः) Cultivated and.<BR> E. क्षेत्र, and भूमि land.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=219-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षेत्रविद्
क्षेत्रविद् m. (-वित्)<BR>	 1. A sage, one who possesses spiritual knowledge.<BR>2. A husbandman.<BR> E. क्षेत्र, and विद् who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=219-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षेत्रराशि|क्षेत्रराशिः
क्षेत्रराशि f. (-शिः) Figurate quantity.<BR> E. क्षेत्र, and राशि number.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=219-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षेत्रसीमा
क्षेत्रसीमा f. (-मा) The boundaries of a meadow or field, or holy place.<BR>E. क्षेत्र, and सीमा limit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=219-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षेत्राजीव|क्षेत्राजीवः
क्षेत्राजीव mfn. (-वः-वा-वं) A cultivator, a peasant.<BR> E. क्षेत्र a field, and जीव<BR>who lives, with आङ् prefixed; who gets a livelihood by the<BR>labours of the field.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=219-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षेत्रामलकी
क्षेत्रामलकी f. (-की) A plant commonly Bhumiamalaki, Flacourtia cata-<BR>phracta, Rox)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=219-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षेत्रिक|क्षेत्रिकः
क्षेत्रिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Having a field, relating to a field, &c.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A farmer, a cultivator.<BR>	 2. A husbandman.<BR> E. क्षेत्र, and<BR>ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=219-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षेत्रिन्
क्षेत्रिन् mfn. (-त्री-त्रिणी-त्रि) Owning or having a field, cultivating it, &c.<BR>m. (-त्री)<BR>	 1. A husband.<BR>	 2. A cultivator, a husbandman.<BR> E. क्षेत्र a<BR>field, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=219-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षेत्रिय|क्षेत्रियं|क्षेत्रियः
क्षेत्रिय n. (-यं)<BR>	 1. Meadow grass, herbage, pasturage.<BR>	 2. Physicking,<BR>operating.<BR>	 m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. An adulterer.<BR>	 2. A medicament, what is fit<BR>to be administered in medicine.<BR>	 3. An incurable disease.<BR> E. क्षेत्र a<BR>field, the body, घ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=219-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षेद
क्षेद m. (-दः) Sorrowing, moaning.<BR> E. क्षि to moan, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=219-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षेप|क्षेपः
क्षेप m. (-पः)<BR>	 1. Sending, dismissing.<BR>	 2. Throwing, casting.<BR>	 3. Pride,<BR>haughtiness.<BR>	 4. Delay, dilatoriness.<BR>	 5. Disrespect, contempt.<BR>	 6. Pas-<BR>sing away time, 7. Abuse, reviling.<BR>	 8. A clump of flowers, &c.<BR>	 9.<BR>(In arithmetic, &c.) Additive quantity, addendum.<BR> E. क्षिप् to throw<BR>affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=219-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षेपक|क्षेपकः
क्षेपक mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>	 1. Who or what throws or sends.<BR>	 2. Abusing<BR>disrespectful.<BR> E. क्षिप् to throw, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=219-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षेपण|क्षेपणं
क्षेपण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Sending, directing.<BR>	 2. Throwing, casting.<BR>	 3. Passing<BR>away time.<BR>	 4. Abusing.<BR> E. क्षिप् to throw, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=220-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षेपणि|क्षेपणिः
क्षेपणि f. (-णिः or णी)<BR>	 1. An oar.<BR>	 2. A net, a fishing net.<BR> E. क्षिप् to cast<BR>or throw, अण् and ङीष् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=220-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षेपिमन्
क्षेपिमन् m. (-मा) Great velocity.<BR> E. क्षिप्र quick, and इमनिच् affix, deriv irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=220-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षेपिष्ठ|क्षेपिष्ठः
क्षेपिष्ठ mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठा-ष्ठं) Very quick, quickest.<BR> E. क्षिप्र quick, and इष्ठन्<BR>superlative affix, र rejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=220-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षेपीयस्
क्षेपीयस् mfn. (-यान्-यसी-यः) Very quick.<BR> E. क्षिप्र, and ईयसुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=220-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षेप्तृ
क्षेप्तृ mfn. (-प्ता-प्त्री-प्तृ) Who or what throws, sends, orders, &c.<BR> E. क्षिप् to<BR>throw, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=220-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षेम|क्षेमं|क्षेमः
क्षेम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं) Happy, well, prosperous, right, &c.<BR>	 mn. (-मः-मं)<BR>	 1.<BR>Happiness, well-being.<BR>	 2. Preserving, protecting, keeping what is<BR>acquired.<BR>	 3. Final emancipation or eternal happiness.<BR>	 4. The pro-<BR>per term of civil address to Vaiśya, as क्षेममस्ति क्षेमं भवतु Is it well,<BR>or may it be well, &c.<BR>	 f. (-मा) A name of DURGĀ.<BR> E. क्षि to remove,<BR>and मन् Uṇādi affix; what removes or destroys sorrow, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=220-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षेमक|क्षेमकः
क्षेमक m. (-कः) A perfume, commonly Chor.<BR> E. कन् added to क्षेम.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=220-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षेमकर|क्षेमकरः
क्षेमकर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Propitious, conferring happiness or good for-<BR>tune.<BR> E. क्षेम and कृ to make, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=220-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षेमकार|क्षेमकारः
क्षेमकार mfn. (-रः-री-रं) Auspicious, propitious, conferring happiness or<BR>good fortune.<BR> E. क्षेम happiness, and कृ to make, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=220-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षेमङ्कर|क्षेमंकर|क्षेमङ्करः
क्षेमङ्कर mfn. (-रः-री-रं) Propitious, &c.: see the preceding.<BR>	 f. (-री) The<BR>Brahmani kite or Coromandel eagle, which is considered as a bird<BR>of good omen, (Falco ponticerianus.)<BR> E. क्षेम and कृ to make, with<BR>खच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=220-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षेमवत्|क्षेमवन्त्
क्षेमवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Happy, prosperous.<BR> E. क्षेम and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=220-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षेमफला
क्षेमफला f. (-ला) Opposite leaved fig tree.<BR> E. क्षेम auspicious, and फल<BR>fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=220-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षेम्य|क्षेम्यं|क्षेम्यः
क्षेम्य mfn. (-म्यः-म्याम्यं)<BR>	 1. Lucky, prosperous, thriving.<BR>	 2. Healthy,<BR>salubrious.<BR> E. क्षेम and यत् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=220-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षेव
क्षेव (ड) क्षेवु r. 1st cl. (क्षेवति) To spit, to eject form the mouth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=220-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षै
क्षै r. 1st cl. (क्षायति) To wane, to waste or decline.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=220-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षैत्र|क्षैत्रं
क्षैत्र n. (-त्रं) A multitude of fields &c.<BR> E. क्षेत्र a field, &c. and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=220-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षैत्रज्ञ|क्षैत्रज्ञं
क्षैत्रज्ञ n. (-ज्ञं) Spirituality, the nature of the soul.<BR> E. क्षेत्रज्ञ and अण्<BR>aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=220-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षैत्रज्ञ्य|क्षैत्रज्ञ्यं
क्षैत्रज्ञ्य n. (ज्ञ्यं) Spirituality, the nature of the soul, the knowledge of<BR>it, &c.<BR> E. क्षेत्रज्ञ and यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=220-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षैरेयी
क्षैरेयी f. (-यी) Milk and rice, or any preparation of milk.<BR> E. क्षीर milk,<BR>aff. ठञ् fem. affix ङीप्; some copies read this word क्षीरेयी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=220-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षोड|क्षोडः
क्षोड m. (-डः) The post to which an elephant is bound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=220-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षोजन
क्षोजन n. (-नं) Sound of the flute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=220-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षोणि|क्षोणिः
क्षोणि f. (-णिः or -णी) The earth.<BR> E. क्षु to sound, अणि affix, fem affix<BR>optionally ङीप् also क्षौणि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=220-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षोद|क्षोदः
क्षोद m. (-दः)<BR>	 1. Powder, pulverized substance.<BR>	 2. A piece, a small<BR>piece or particle.<BR>	 3. The stone or slab on which any thing is<BR>ground or powdered, a mortar, &c.<BR>	 4. Dust.<BR> E. क्षुद् to bruise or<BR>pound, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=220-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षोदारज
क्षोदारज mfn. (-जः-जा-जं) Ground, pulverized.<BR> E. क्षोद and रज for<BR>रजस् dust.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=220-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षोदित|क्षोदितं
क्षोदित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Pounded, ground, comminuted.<BR>	 n. (-तं) Powder,<BR>dust, substance pulverized or ground<BR> E. क्षुद् to bruise or pound,<BR>affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=220-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षोदिमन्
क्षोदिमन् m. (-मा) Minuteness, exceeding smallness or inferiority.<BR> E. क्षुद्र<BR>small, &c. affix इमनिच् deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=220-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षोदिष्ठ|क्षोदिष्ठः
क्षोदिष्ठ mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठा-ष्ठं) Finely pounded or levigated, very small or<BR>minute.<BR> E. क्षुद्र small, इष्ठन् affix of the superlative, र rejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=220-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षोदीयस्
क्षोदीयस् mfn. (-यान्-यसी-यः) Very fine or small.<BR> E. क्षुद्र and ईयसुन् affix<BR>of the superlative.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=220-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षोभ|क्षोभः
क्षोभ m. (-भः)<BR>	 1. Agitation, emotion.<BR>	 2. Shaking, trembling, tossing. E.<BR>क्षुभ् to be agitated, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=220-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षोम|क्षोमं|क्षोमः
क्षोम mn. (-मः-मं) A room on the top of a house: see क्षौम n. (-मं) Wove<BR>silk<BR> E. क्षु to make a sound, Uṇādi affix मन्; also क्षौम.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=220-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षौणि|क्षौणिः
क्षौणि f. (-णिः or -णी) The earth,<BR> E. क्षोणि the earth, and अण् pleonastic,<BR>with इन् or ङीष् fem. terminations added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=220-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षौणीप्राचीर|क्षौणीप्राचीरः
क्षौणीप्राचीर m. (-रः) The ocean.<BR> E. क्षौणी the earth, and प्राचीर an enclosure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=220-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षौद्र|क्षौद्रं|क्षौद्रः
क्षौद्र n. (-द्रं)<BR>	 1. Honey.<BR>	 2. Water.<BR>	 m. (-द्रः) A flower, (Michelia cham-<BR>paca.)<BR> E. क्षुद्रा a fly, &c. affix अञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=220-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षौद्रक्य|क्षौद्रक्यं
क्षौद्रक्य mfn. (-क्यः-क्यी-क्यं) Small, minute.<BR> E. क्षुद्र small, ञाट् pleonastic aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=220-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षौम|क्षौमं|क्षौमः
क्षौम mfn. (-मः-मी-मं) Linen, made of linen, coverd with it, &c.<BR>	 f. (-मी)<BR>Lin or flax, (Linum usitatissimum.)<BR>	 mn. (-मः-मं)<BR>	 1. An airy room<BR>on the top of a house.<BR>	 2. An apartment on the top of a hall.<BR>	 3.<BR>The back of an edifice.<BR>	 4. A fortified place in front of a building.<BR>5. A building of a particular form.<BR>	 6. Wove silk: 7. Linen cloth E.<BR>क्षोम q. v. अण् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=220-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षौमक|क्षौमकः
क्षौमक m. (-कः) Chor, a species of perfume.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=220-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षौर|क्षौरं
क्षौर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Shaving the head.<BR>	 2. Shaving in general.<BR>	 f. (-री) A<BR>razor.<BR> E. क्षुर a razor, affix अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=220-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षौरिक|क्षौरिकः
क्षौरिक m. (-कः) A barber.<BR> E. क्षुर a razor, affix ठक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=220-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्ष्णु
क्ष्णु r. 2nd cl. (क्ष्णोति or with सम् prefixed संक्ष्णुते) To whet, to sharpen.<BR>(क्ष्णोते) To take away, to remove.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=220-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्ष्णुत|क्ष्णुतः
क्ष्णुत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Whetted, sharpened.<BR> E. क्ष्णु to whet, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=220-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्ष्मा
क्ष्मा f. (-क्ष्मा) The earth.<BR> E. क्षम् to bear, Uṇādi affix अच्, and the penul-<BR>timate dropped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=220-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्ष्मातल|क्ष्मातलं
क्ष्मातल n. (-लं) The surface of the earth.<BR> E. क्ष्मा, and तल below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=220-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्ष्माभुज्
क्ष्माभुज् m. (-क्) A king.<BR> E. क्ष्मा, and भुज् who enjoys.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=220-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्ष्माभृत्
क्ष्माभृत् m, (-सृत्)<BR>	 1. A king, a prince.<BR>	 2. A mountain.<BR> E. क्ष्मा the earth,<BR>and भृत् who nourishes, from भृ, affix क्विप्, तुक added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=220-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्ष्माय
क्ष्माय (इ) क्ष्मायी r. 1st. (क्ष्मायते) To shake, to make tremble.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=220-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्ष्मायित|क्ष्मायितः
क्ष्मायित mfd. (-तः-ता-तं) Shaken, trembling.<BR> E. क्ष्माय, and क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=220-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्ष्मायितृ
क्ष्मायितृ mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ) Trembling, shaking.<BR> E. क्ष्माय, and तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=220-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्ष्मील
क्ष्मील r. 1st cl. (क्ष्मीलति) To wink or twinkle, to close as the eye lids.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=220-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्ष्विण्ण|क्ष्विण्णः
क्ष्विण्ण mfn. (-ण्णः-ण्णा-ण्णं)<BR>	 1. Sounded.<BR>	 2. Soft, unctuous.<BR> E. क्ष्विद् to sound,<BR>&c. क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=220-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्ष्विद
क्ष्विद (-ञि, आ) ञिक्ष्विदा r. 1st cl. (क्ष्वेदति) To sound inarticulately. r. 4th<BR>cl. (क्षिद्यति)<BR>	 1. To be unctuous, to be soft or bland.<BR>	 2. To liberate,<BR>to free: some consider these roots as more properly read क्ष्विड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=220-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्ष्वेड|क्ष्वेडं|क्ष्वेडः
क्ष्वेड mfn. (-डः-डा-डं)<BR>	 1. Crooked, bent.<BR>	 2. Wicked, depraved.<BR>	 m. (-डः)<BR>1. Venom, poison.<BR>	 2. Sound, noise.<BR>	 3. Tingling or buzzing in the<BR>ear, from hardening of the wax, &c.<BR>	 4. Ghosha, with yellow flow-<BR>ers; see घोष.<BR>	 n. (-डं)<BR>	 1. The flower of the Ghosha plant.<BR>	 2. The<BR>fruit of a red kind of swallow wort.<BR>	 f. (डा)<BR>	 1. A war whoop, a<BR>battle cry.<BR>	 2. A bamboo rod or stake.<BR> E. क्ष्विद् to sound inarticu-<BR>lately, to be soft or bland, &c. affix घ, and ड substituted for द,<BR>or क्ष्वेल् to shake, &c. अच् affix, and ल changed to ड<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=220-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्ष्वेडित|क्ष्वेडितं|क्ष्वेडितः
क्ष्वेडित n. (-तं) A battle cry, a war whoop.<BR> E. क्ष्विद् to sound inarticu-<BR>lately, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=220-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्ष्वेल
क्ष्वेल (ऋ) क्ष्वेऌ r. 1st cl. (क्ष्वेलति)<BR>	 1. To shake, to tremble.<BR>	 2. To go, to<BR>move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=220-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ख|खं|खः
ख The second consonant of the Deva Nagari alphabet, being the<BR>aspirate of the proceding; it is written in the Roman character<BR>Kh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=220-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ख|खं|खः
ख n. (-खं)<BR>	 1. Heaven.<BR>	 2. Sky or ether.<BR>	 3. An organ of sense.<BR>	 4. Know-<BR>ledge.<BR>	 5. Happiness, pleasure.<BR>	 6. vacuity.<BR>	 7. A dot, a cypher.<BR>	 8.<BR>A city, a field.<BR>	 9. Action.<BR>	 10. Auspiciousness.<BR>	 11. Tale.<BR>	 12. The<BR>tenth constellation from any given one, or the sun's entrance in-<BR>to it.<BR>	 13. Brahma the supreme spirit.<BR>	 m. (-खः) A name of the<BR>sun.<BR> E. खन् to dig, to penetrate, affix ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=220-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खकुन्तल|खकुंतल|खकुन्तलः
खकुन्तल m. (-लः) A name of ŚIVA.<BR> E. ख ether, कुन्तल hair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=221-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खक्ख
खक्ख r. 1st cl. (-खक् खति) To laugh, to laugh at or deride; also कख.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=221-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खक्खट|खक्खटः
खक्खट mfn. (-टः-टा-टं) Hard, solid: see कक्खट.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=221-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खखोल्क|खखोल्कः
खखोल्क m. (-ल्कः) The sun.<BR> E. ख the sky, and खोल्क a meteor, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=221-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खग|खगः
खग m. (-गः)<BR>	 1. A bird.<BR>	 2. An arrow.<BR>	 3. The sun.<BR>	 4. A planet.<BR>	 5. deity.<BR>6. Air, wind.<BR>	 7. A grasshopper.<BR> E. ख the sky, &c. and ग who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=221-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खगपति|खगपतिः
खगपति m. (-तिः) A name of GARUḌA, the bird or vehicle of VIṢṆU.<BR>E. खग a bird. and पति lord or chief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=221-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खगम|खगमः
खगम m. (-मः) A bird.<BR> E. ख, and गम what goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=221-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खगवक्त्र|खगवक्त्रः
खगवक्त्र m. (-क्त्रः) A tree, commonly Lakucha, (Artocarpus lacucha.) E.<BR>खग a bird, and वक्त्र face, bird-faced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=221-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खगवती
खगवती f. (-तिः) The earth.<BR> E. खग a bird, &c. मतुप् poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=221-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खगशत्रु|खगशत्रुः
खगशत्रु m. (-त्रुः) A plant, commonly Chakuliya, (Hemionitis cordifolia,<BR>Rox.)<BR> E. खग a bird, and शत्रु an enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=221-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खगस्थान
खगस्थान n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. The hollow of a tree.<BR>	 2. A bird's nest.<BR> E. खग a bird,<BR>स्थान place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=221-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खगान्तक|खगांतक|खगान्तकः
खगान्तक m. (-कः) A hawk, falcon.<BR> E. खग, and अन्तक destroyer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=221-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खगासन|खगासनः
खगासन m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. The eastern mountain over which the sun rises.<BR>	 2. A<BR>name of VIṢṆU.<BR> E. खग a bird or the sun, and आसन seat or place<BR>of abiding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=221-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खगेन्द्र|खगेंद्र|खगेन्द्रः
खगेन्द्र m. (-न्द्रः) A name of GARUḌA.<BR> E. खग, and इन्द्र chief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=221-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खगेन्द्रध्वज|खगेन्द्रध्वजः
खगेन्द्रध्वज m. (-जः) VIṢṆU.<BR> E. खगेन्द्र, and ध्वज emblem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=221-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खगेश्वर|खगेश्वरः
खगेश्वर m. (-रः) GARUḌA the bird of VIṢṆU; also खगेश. K. खग, and ईश्वर<BR>king of birds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=221-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खगोड
खगोड m. (-डः) A kind of reed, (Saccharum spontaneum.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=221-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खगोल|खगोलः
खगोल m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. The vault or circle of the heavens, the planisphere.<BR>	 2.<BR>The same represented artificially, the armillary sphere.<BR> E. ख, and<BR>गोल sphere.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=221-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खगोलविद्या
खगोलविद्या f. (-द्या) Astronomy.<BR> E. खगोल and विद्या knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=221-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खङ्कर|खंकर|खंकरः|खङ्करः
खङ्कर m. (-रः) A curl, a lock of hair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=221-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खच
खच r. 1st cl. (खचति) also r. 9th cl. (खच्नाति)<BR>	 1. To be past birth.<BR>	 2. To<BR>cause prosperity.<BR>	 3. To purify. r. 10th cl. (खचयति) To fasten, to<BR>bind, to set.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=221-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खचमस|खचमसः
खचमस m. (-सः) The moon.<BR> E. ख the sky, चम् to eat, and अस aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=221-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खचर|खचरः
खचर mfn. (-रः-री-रं) Moving in the sky, flying in the air.<BR>	 m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A<BR>cloud.<BR>	 2. An aerial spirit.<BR>	 3. Air, wind.<BR>	 4. A demon.<BR>	 5. The sun.<BR>	 6.<BR>A bird.<BR> E. ख the sky, and चर who goes, from चर् to go, affix ट;<BR>see also खेचर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=221-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खचित|खचितं
खचित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Mixed, blended, inlaid.<BR>	 2. Joined, combined.<BR>E. खच् to fasten, &c. affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=221-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खज|खजः
खज r. 1st cl. (खजति) To churn or agitate. (इ,) खजि (खञ्जति) To limp, to<BR>halt, to walk lame or ill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=221-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खज|खजः
खज m. (-जः) A ladle, a spoon.<BR>	 f. (-जा)<BR>	 1. Churning, stirring.<BR>	 2. Killing,<BR>destroying.<BR>	 3. The palm with the fingers extended.<BR> E. खज् to agi-<BR>tate, &c. affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=221-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खजक|खजकः
खजक m. (-कः) The churning stick.<BR>	 f. (-जिका) A ladle or spoon.<BR> E. खज्<BR>to churn or agitate, affix. ण्वुल्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=221-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खजप|खजपं
खजप m. (-पः) Ghee or clarified butter.<BR> E. खज् to stir or agitate, Uṇādi<BR>affix अप.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=221-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खजल|खजलं
खजल n. (-लं)<BR>	 1. Frost, hoar frost.<BR>	 2. Dew, rain.<BR> E. ख the sky, and जल<BR>water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=221-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खजाक|खजाकः
खजाक mf. (-कः-का) A spoon, a ladle.<BR>	 m. (-कः) A bird.<BR> E. खज to agitate,<BR>and आक Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=221-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खजित्
खजित् m. (-जित्) A Buddha, one of the seven teachers or saints of the<BR>Buddha sect.<BR> E. ख heaven, and जित् who subdues.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=221-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खज्योतिस्
खज्योतिस् m. (-तिः) A fire-fly.<BR> E. ख, and ज्योतिस् light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=221-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खञ्ज|खंज|खञ्जः
खञ्ज mfn. (-ञ्जः-ञ्जा-ञ्जं) Lame, crippled, limping.<BR>	 f. (-ञ्जा) A species of<BR>metre, a stanza of two lines, one of thirty-two, the other of thirty<BR>feet.<BR> E. खजि to limp or go lame, affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=221-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खञ्जक|खंजक|खञ्जकः
खञ्जक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Lame, limping.<BR> E. खजि to limp, affix वुन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=221-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खञ्जखेट|खंजखेट|खञ्जखेटः
खञ्जखेट m. (-टः) A wag-tail.<BR> E. खञ्ज lame, and खेट who moves.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=221-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खञ्जखेल|खंजखेल|खञ्जखेलः
खञ्जखेल m. (-लः) A wag-tail.<BR> E. खञ्ज lame, and खेल who moves, from<BR>खेल् to move, affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=221-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खञ्जन|खंजन|खञ्जनं|खंजनः|खञ्जनः
खञ्जन m. (-नः) A small bird, the wag-tail, (Motacilla alba.)<BR>	 f. (-ना)<BR>	 1.<BR>A small kind of wag-tail.<BR>	 2. Mustard.<BR>	 n. (-नं) Going, moving. E.<BR>खजि to go lamely, affix ल्यु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=221-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खञ्जनरत|खंजनरत|खञ्जनरतं
खञ्जनरत n. (-तं) The cohabitation of saints.<BR> E. खञ्जन a wag-tail, and रत<BR>cohabitation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=221-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खञ्जनाकृति|खञ्जनाकृतिः
खञ्जनाकृति f. (-तिः) A sort of wag-tail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=221-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खञ्जनिका|खंजनिका
खञ्जनिका f. (-का) A kind of wag-tail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=221-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खञ्जरीट|खंजरीट|खंजरीटः|खञ्जरीटः
खञ्जरीट m. (-टः) A wag-tail.<BR> E. खञ्ज lame, ऋ to go, कीटन् affix, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=221-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खट|खटः
खट r. 1st cl. (खटति) To desire, to wish, to seek or inquire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=221-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खट|खटः
खट m. (-टः)<BR>	 1. Grass.<BR>	 2. Phlegm, the phlegmatic or watery humor.<BR>	 3.<BR>A blind well.<BR>	 4. An axe, a hatchet.<BR>	 5. A closed or doubled fist, as<BR>for striking.<BR>	 6. A plough.<BR>	 7. A fragrant kind of grass: see कत्तृण.<BR>E. खट् to seek, to wish, affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=221-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खटक|खटकः
खटक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A go-between, a man whose business it is to nego-<BR>ciate marriages: see घटक.<BR>	 2. The doubled fist of wrestlers or box-<BR>ers.<BR> E. खट् to seek, to wish, affix वुन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=221-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खटकामुख|खटकामुखं|खटकामुखः
खटकामुख m. (-खः) A man in the attitude of shooting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=221-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खटखादक|खटखादकः
खटखादक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. An eater.<BR>	 2. A glass vessel.<BR>	 3. A jackal.<BR>	 4. an<BR>animal.<BR>	 5. A crow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=221-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खटिक|खटिकः
खटिक m. (-कः) The fist, the hand closed.<BR>	 f. (-का)<BR>	 1. Chalk.<BR>	 2. The<BR>external opening of the ear.<BR>	 3. A fragrant grass: (Andropogon<BR>muricatus.)<BR> E. खट् to seek or wish, वुन् affix, and इट् inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=221-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खटिनी
खटिनी f. (-नी) Chalk.<BR> E. खट् to seek, इनि affix, fem. affix ङीष्; also<BR>कठिनी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=221-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खटी
खटी f. (-टी) Chalk.<BR> E. खट् to seek, अच् and ङीष् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=221-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खट्ट
खट्ट r. 10th cl. (खट्टयति) To cover, to screen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=221-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खट्टन|खट्टनः
खट्टन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Dwarfish, short of stature.<BR> E. खट्ट् to cover or<BR>hide, affix ल्यु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=221-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खट्टा
खट्टा f. (-ट्टा) A kind of grass, (Andropogon serratus.)<BR> E. खट्ट् to screen,<BR>अङ् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=221-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खट्टाश|खट्टाशः
खट्टाश mf. (-शः-शी) The civet or zebet cat, (Viverra zibetha.)<BR> E. खट्टा the<BR>grass, and अश who eats; also खट्टास.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=221-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खट्टास|खट्टासः
खट्टास m. (-सः) The civet: see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=221-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खट्टि|खट्टिः
खट्टि m. (-ट्टिः) A bier, the bed on which the corpse is carried to the<BR>pile; also खट्टी.<BR> E. खट्ट् to screen, affix कि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=221-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खट्टिक|खट्टिकः
खट्टिक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) A hunter, a fowler, one who lives by killing<BR>and selling game.<BR>	 f. (-का)<BR>	 1. A small bedstead, a cot.<BR>	 2. A bier or<BR>bed on which the corpse is carried.<BR> E. खट्ट् to screen, इकन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=221-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खट्टेरक|खट्टेरकः
खट्टेरक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Dwarf, dwarfish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=221-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खट्वा
खट्वा f. (-ट्वा)<BR>	 1. A bedstead, a cot, a couch.<BR>	 2. A hammock, a swing E.<BR>खट्ट् to hide, Uṇādi affix कन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=221-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खट्वाङ्ग|खट्वांग|खट्वाङ्गं|खट्वाङ्गः
खट्वाङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः) A king of the solar line.<BR>	 n. (-ङ्गं)<BR>	 1. Part of a bed.<BR>	 2. A.<BR>club or staff with a skull at the top of it, considered as a weapon<BR>of Siva, and carried by penitents and Yogis.<BR>	 3. Wood from a fun-<BR>eral pile.<BR> E. खट्वा a cot, and अङ्ग body or form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=221-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खट्वाङ्गभृत्
खट्वाङ्गभृत् m. (-भृत्) A name of ŚIVA.<BR> E. खट्वाङ्ग one of his weapons, भृत्<BR>who maintains.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=221-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खट्वाङ्गिन्|खट्वांगिन्
खट्वाङ्गिन् m. (-ङ्गी) A name of ŚIVA.<BR> E. खट्वाङ्ग, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=221-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खट्वारूढ|खट्वारूढः
खट्वारूढ mfn. (-ढः-ढा-ढं)<BR>	 1. Low, vile, abandoned, iniquitous.<BR>	 2. Erring,<BR>going wrong.<BR>	 3. Stupid, silly.<BR>	 4. Laid or lying on a bed.<BR> E. खट्वा a<BR>bed, and आरूढ mounted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=221-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खट्विका
खट्विका f. (-का) A small bedstead.<BR> E. खट्वा a bedstead, and कन् affix. fem.<BR>form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=221-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खड|खडं|खडः
खड r. 10th cl. (खाडयति) also (इ,) खडि r. 1st and 10th cls. (खण्डति,<BR>खण्डयति) and (इ ङ) खडिङ् r. 1st cl. (खण्डते) To divide, ‘to tear, to<BR>break off a part or piece.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=221-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खड|खडं|खडः
खड m. (-डः)<BR>	 1. Breaking, dividing.<BR>	 2. Buttermilk boiled with acid<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=222-a" target="_blank">Page222-a+ 60</a>]<BR>vegetables and spices.<BR>	 3. A small grass.<BR>	 f. (-डी) Chalk.<BR> E. खड्. to<BR>break, &c. affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=221-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खडक्किका
खडक्किका f. (-का) A private or back door, a small venetian door or<BR>window.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=222-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खडिका
खडिका f. (-का) Chalk.<BR> E. खड्. to break, affix वुन्, fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=222-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खडु|खडुः
खडु m. (-डुः) A bier.<BR> E. खड्. to break, affix उ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=222-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खड्ग|खड्गं|खड्गः
खड्ग m. (-ड्गः) A rhinoceros.<BR>	 2. A rhinocero's horn.<BR>	 3. A sword, a scymi-<BR>tar.<BR>	 4. A large sacrificial knife.<BR>	 5. One of the Buddhas or Baud-<BR>dha saints.<BR>	 n. (-ड्गं) Iron.<BR> E. खड्. to tear or rend, Uṇādi affix गन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=222-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खड्गकोष|खड्गकोषः
खड्गकोष m. (-षः)<BR>	 1. A creeping plant, (Scripus maximus.)<BR>	 2. A scab-<BR>bard, a sheathe.<BR> E. खड्ग a sword. and कोष a sheathe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=222-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खड्गचर्म्मधर|खड्गचर्मधर
खड्गचर्म्मधर m. (-रः) A soldier armed with a sword and shield.<BR> E. खड्ग,<BR>and चर्म्म a shield, धर who bears.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=222-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खड्गट|खड्गटः
खड्गट m. (-टः) A large kind of Kas, (Saccharum spontaneum.)<BR> E. खड्ग the<BR>rhinoceros, and अट who goes; these animals being usually found<BR>amongst high grass or reeds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=222-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खड्गधर|खड्गधरः
खड्गधर m. (-रः) A swordsman.<BR> E. खड्ग, and धर who holds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=222-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खड्गधेनु|खड्गधेनुः
खड्गधेनु f. (-नुः)<BR>	 1. A small knife.<BR>	 2. A female rhinoceros.<BR> E. खड्ग a sword<BR>&c. धेनु a cow, used here as a diminutive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=222-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खड्गपत्र|खड्गपत्रः
खड्गपत्र m. (-त्रः) The name of a creeper. (Scirpus maximus.)<BR>	 n. (-त्रं) The<BR>blade of a sword.<BR> E. खड्ग a sword, and पत्र leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=222-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खड्गपाणि
खड्गपाणि mfn. (-णिः-णिः-णि) Holding a sword.<BR> E. खड्ग, and पाणि the hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=222-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खड्गपात्र
खड्गपात्र n. (-त्रं) A vessel of buffalo's horn.<BR> E. खड्ग and पात्र a vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=222-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खड्गपिधान|खड्गपिधानं
खड्गपिधान n. (-नं) A scabbard, a sheathe.<BR> E. खड्ग a sword, and पिधान a<BR>sheathe; also with कन् added, खड्गपिधानक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=222-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खड्गपुत्रिका
खड्गपुत्रिका f. (-का) A knife, a small sword.<BR> E. खड्ग, and पुत्तिका infant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=222-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खड्गप्रहार|खड्गप्रहारः
खड्गप्रहार m. (-रः) A sword cut.<BR> E. खड्ग, and प्रहार a stroke.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=222-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खड्गमांस
खड्गमांस m. (-सः) Buffalo-beef.<BR> E. खड्ग, and मांस flesh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=222-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खड्गलेखा
खड्गलेखा f. (-खा) A row of sabres. खड्ग, and लेखा a line.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=222-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खड्गराट
खड्गराट m. (-टः)<BR>	 1. A shield. One who observes a peculiar religious obli-<BR>gation, rubbing the feet backwards and forwards on the edge of a<BR>sword made red hot, this is a penance peculiar to the Bauddhas.<BR>E. खड्ग a sword, रट् to speak, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=222-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खड्गाघात|खड्गाघातः
खड्गाघात m. (-तः) A sword cut.<BR> E. खड्ग, and आघात a blow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=222-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खड्गाधार|खड्गाधारः
खड्गाधार m. (-रः) A sheathe, a scabbard.<BR> E. खड्ग, and आधार what receives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=222-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खड्गाभिहत
खड्गाभिहत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Cut or struck with a sword.<BR> E. खड्ग, and अभि-<BR>हत struck.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=222-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खड्गामिष
खड्गामिष n. (-षं) Buffalo's flesh.<BR> E. खड्ग, and आमिष flesh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=222-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खड्गिक|खड्गिकः
खड्गिक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. The cream or froth of buffalo's milk.<BR>	 2. A vender of<BR>flesh meat.<BR> E. खड्ग a sword, &c. affix ठक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=222-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खड्गिन्
खड्गिन् mfn. (-ड्गी-ड्गिनी-ड्गि) Armed with a sword.<BR>	 m. (-ड्गी)<BR>	 1. A rhinoceros.<BR>2. A Jina or Jaina saint.<BR> E. खड्ग a horn, &c. affix इनि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=222-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खड्गिमार|खड्गिमारः
खड्गिमार m. (-रः) A kind of creeper: see खड्गकोष.<BR> E. खड्गि a rhinoceros,<BR>and मार what destroys.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=222-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खड्गीक|खड्गीकं
खड्गीक m. (-कः) A sickle, a scythe.<BR> E. खड्ग a scymitar, and इकन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=222-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खण्ड|खंड|खण्डं|खण्डः
खण्ड mn. (-ण्डः-ण्डं)<BR>	 1. A piece, a part, a fragment, a portion.<BR>	 2. A chap-<BR>ter, a section.<BR>	 3. A term in an equation.<BR>	 m. (-ण्डः)<BR>	 1. A flaw in a<BR>jewel.<BR>	 2. Treacle or molasses partially dried or candied.<BR>	 n. (-ण्डं)<BR>	 1.<BR>A sort of sugar cane.<BR>	 2. Black salt.<BR> E. खडि to break, and घञ् affix<BR>or खन् to tear, affix ड, and न changed to ण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=222-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खण्डक|खंडक|खण्डकः
खण्डक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. Pared or clipped fingernails.<BR>	 2. A part, a piece. E.<BR>खण्ड् to tear, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=222-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खण्डकर्ण|खण्डकर्णः
खण्डकर्ण m. (-र्णः) Sweet potato.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=222-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खण्डकथा|खंडकथा
खण्डकथा f. (-था) A tale or story divided into sections.<BR> E. खण्ड a section,<BR>and कथा a story.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=222-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खण्डकालु
खण्डकालु n. (-लु) An esculent root, sweet potatoe: also खण्डकालुक n. (-कं)<BR>E. खण्डक a portion, and आलु any esculent root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=222-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खण्डकाव्य|खंडकाव्य
खण्डकाव्य (-व्यं)<BR>	 n. A poem interspersed with prose.<BR> E. खण्ड, and काव्य a<BR>poem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=222-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खण्डज|खंडज|खण्डजः
खण्डज m. (-जः) Treacle, molasses.<BR> E. खण्ड, and ज what is produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=222-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खण्डधारा|खंडधारा
खण्डधारा f. (-रा) Shears, scissors.<BR> E. खण्ड a part, and and धृ to have or<BR>hold, in the causal from.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=222-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खण्डन|खंडन|खण्डनं
खण्डन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Breaking, dividing, cutting, reducing to pieces.<BR>	 2.<BR>Destroying, annihilating.<BR>	 3. Refuting, (in argument.)<BR>	 4. Rebellion,<BR>opposition.<BR> E. खण्ड् to break, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=222-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खण्डनरत
खण्डनरत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Destructive, skilful in cutting or destroying. E.<BR>खण्डन, and रत engaged in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=222-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खण्डनीय|खंडनीय
खण्डनीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>	 1. Brittle, fragile.<BR>	 2. Refutable.<BR>	 3. Destruct-<BR>ible, &c.<BR> E. खडि, and अनीयर् affix; also खण्ड्य, and खण्डितव्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=222-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खण्डपत्र
खण्डपत्र n. (-त्रं) A bundle of various leaves.<BR> E. खण्ड, and पत्र a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=222-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खण्डपरशु|खंडपरशु|खण्डपरशुः
खण्डपरशु m. (-शुः) A name of ŚIVA.<BR> E. खण्ड a part, and परशु a hatchet;<BR>cutting his foes to pieces.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=222-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खण्डपर्शु|खंडपर्शु|खण्डपर्शुः
खण्डपर्शु m. (-र्शुः)<BR>	 1. A name of PARASURAMA.<BR>	 2. A name of ŚIVA.<BR>	 3.<BR>Rahu, the personified ascending node.<BR>	 4. A spreader of unguents,<BR>fragrant powders, &c.<BR>	 5. A drug, commonly Chandamalaki.<BR>	 6.<BR>An elephant with a broken tusk.<BR> E. खण्ड a part, and पर्शु an axe;<BR>whose axe or arms cut every thing to pieces.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=222-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खण्डपाल|खंडपाल|खण्डपालः
खण्डपाल m. (-लः) A confectioner, a seller of sweetmeats.<BR> E. खण्ड molasses,<BR>and पाल who cherishes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=222-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खण्डप्रलय|खंडप्रलय|खण्डप्रलयः
खण्डप्रलय m. (-यः) Partial destruction of the universe, the destruction<BR>of the division of the terrestrial world.<BR> E. खण्ड, and प्रलय destruc-<BR>tion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=222-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खण्डमण्डल|खंडमंडल
खण्डमण्डल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>	 1. Gibbous, not full or round.<BR>	 n. (-लं) A<BR>segment of a circle, part of a circle or an incomplete sphere. E.<BR>खण्ड, and मण्डल sphere.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=222-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खण्डमोदक|खंडमोदक|खण्डमोदकः
खण्डमोदक m. (-कः) Granulated sugar.<BR> E. खण्ड, and मोदक a sweetmeat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=222-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खण्डलवण|खंडलवण|खण्डलवणं
खण्डलवण n. (-णं) Black salt.<BR> E. खण्ड, and लवण salt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=222-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खण्डशस्|खंडशस्
खण्डशस् ind. Piece meal, in or by pieces.<BR> E. खण्ड, and शसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=222-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खण्डसर|खण्डसरः
खण्डसर m. (-रः) Granulated sugar.<BR> E. खण्ड, and सर what goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=222-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खण्डाभ्र|खंडाभ्र|खण्डाभ्रं
खण्डाभ्र n. (-भ्रं)<BR>	 1. Scattered clouds.<BR>	 2. A bite, the impression of the<BR>teeth.<BR> E. खण्ड a part, and अभ्र a cloud, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=222-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खण्डाली|खंडाली
खण्डाली f. (-ली)<BR>	 1. A measure for oil.<BR>	 2. A pond.<BR>	 3. A woman whose<BR>husband has been guilty of infidelity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=222-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खण्डिक|खंडिकः|खण्डिकः
खण्डिक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. Pease.<BR>	 2. The armpit<BR> E. खडि to break, इकन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=222-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खण्डित|खंडित|खण्डितं
खण्डित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Cut, torn, broken in pieces.<BR>	 2. Destroyed.<BR>	 3.<BR>Broken as allegiance, disobeyed against, rebelled.<BR>	 4. Refuted, con-<BR>troverted.<BR>	 5. Scattered, dispersed.<BR>	 6. Disappointed.<BR>	 7. Betrayed,<BR>abandoned, (as a lover.)<BR>	 f. (-ता) A woman whose husband or lover<BR>has been guilty of infidelity.<BR> E. खडि to cut. affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=222-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खण्डितव्य
खण्डितव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं) To be broken, what may or ought to be<BR>broken, confuted, destroyed, &c.<BR> E. खडि, and तव्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=222-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खण्डितविग्रह|खंडितविग्रह
खण्डितविग्रह mfn. (-हः-हा-हं) Maimed, mutilated.<BR> E. खण्डित, and विग्रह<BR>body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=222-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खण्डिताशंस
खण्डिताशंस mfn. (-सः-सा-सं) Disappointed, foiled, frustrated.<BR> E. खण्डित,<BR>and आशंस expectation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=222-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खण्डिन्|खंडिन्
खण्डिन् mfn. (-ण्डी-ण्डिनी-ण्डि)<BR>	 1. In pieces or parts, divided, comminuted,<BR>&c.<BR>	 2. Consisting of pieces or parts.<BR>	 m. (-ण्डः) A wild kind kidney<BR>bean: see वनमुद्ग.<BR>	 f. (-नी) The earth.<BR> E. खण्ड a portion, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=222-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खण्डीर|खण्डीरः
खण्डीर m. (-रः) A kind of kidney bean: see पीतमुद्भ<BR> E. खण्ड a part, ईरन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=222-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खण्ड्य|खंड्य
खण्ड्य mfn. (-ण्ड्यः-ण्ड्या-ण्ड्यं) What may or ought to be broken, &c. see<BR>खण्डितव्य<BR> E. खडि and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=222-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खतमाल|खतमालः
खतमाल m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. Smoke.<BR>	 2. cloud.<BR> E. ख the sky, तमाल a tree with<BR>dark blossoms; the etherial Tamāla.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=222-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खद
खद r. 1st cl. (खादति)<BR>	 1. To be steady or firm.<BR>	 2. To hurt or kill.<BR>	 3. To<BR>eat. r. 10th cl. (खदयति) To cover.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=222-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खदिका
खदिका f. (-का) Fried or parched grain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=222-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खदिर|खदिरः
खदिर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A tree, the resin of which is used in medicine, Khayar<BR>Terra japonica or catechu, (Mimosa catechu.)<BR>	 2. A name of INDRA.<BR>3. The moon.<BR>	 f. (-री) A sensitive plant, (Mimosa pudica.)<BR> E. खद् to<BR>hurt, Uṇādi affix इरच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=222-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खदिरपत्री
खदिरपत्री f. (-त्री) The sensitive plant.<BR> E. खदिर, and पत्र, a leaf, affix ङीप्<BR>also with कन् added खदिरपत्रिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=223-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खदिरोपम|खदिरोपमं
खदिरोपम n. (-मं) The Babul, Acacia Arabica.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=223-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खदूरक
खदूरक n. (-कं) A dwarf.<BR> E. ख, and दूर afar, कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=223-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खदूरवासिनी
खदूरवासिनी f. (-नी) One of the female deities or Śaktis of the Buddhas.<BR>E. ख heaven, दूर ill, and वासिनी who abides.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=223-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खद्योत|खद्योतः
खद्योत m. (-तः)<BR>	 1. A fire-fly.<BR>	 2. The sun.<BR> E. ख the sky, and द्योत what is<BR>luminous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=223-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खद्योतन|खद्योतनः
खद्योतन m. (-नः) The sun.<BR> E. ख heaven, and द्युत to shine, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=223-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खधूप|खधूपः
खधूप m. (-पः) A rocket, a fire work.<BR> E. ख, and धूप incense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=223-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खन
खन (उ,) खनु r. 1st cl. (खनति-ते)<BR>	 1. To dig or delve.<BR>	 2. To hurt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=223-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खनक|खनकः
खनक mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>	 1. Tearing, dividing.<BR>	 2. Digging, &c.<BR>	 m. (-कः)<BR>	 1.<BR>A rat.<BR>	 2. A housebreaker.<BR>	 3. A miner.<BR> E. खन् to dig, affix ण्वुल्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=223-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खनत्
खनत् mfn. (-नन्-नन्ती-नत्) Digging.<BR> E. खन्, and शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=223-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खनि|खनिः
खनि f. (-निः or -नी) A mine, especially of precious stones; when used<BR>in composition with आकर, more commonly a mine of the precious<BR>metals.<BR> E. खन् to dig, इन् affix, and ङीष् optionally added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=223-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खनितृ
खनितृ mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ) Who or what digs or delves, a digger, a ditcher,<BR>&c.<BR> E. खन् to dig, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=223-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खनित्र|खनित्रं
खनित्र n. (-त्रं) A spade or hoe.<BR> E. खन् to dig, इत्रच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=223-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खपुर|खपुरं|खपुरः
खपुर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. The betel tree, (Areca faufel or catechu.)<BR>	 2. A fragrant<BR>grass, (Cyperus pertenuis.)<BR>	 3. Garlic.<BR>	 4. Flatulence.<BR>	 n. (-रं)<BR>	 1. A<BR>water jar.<BR>	 2. A city in the sky, the city of HARISCHANDRA.<BR> E. ख<BR>the heavens, &c. पृ to nourish, affix क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=223-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खभ्रान्ति|खभ्रांति|खभ्रान्तिः
खभ्रान्ति m. (-न्तिः) A kite.<BR> E. ख the sky, भ्रम् to roam, affix क्तिन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=223-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खमणि|खमणिः
खमणि m. (-णिः) The sun.<BR> E. ख the sky, and मणि a jewel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=223-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खमीलन|खमीलनं
खमीलन n. (-नं) Lassitude, weariness, sleepiness.<BR> E. ख the sky, and मीलन<BR>twinkling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=223-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खमूर्त्ति|खमूर्ति|खमूर्तिः
खमूर्त्ति f. (-र्त्तिः) A celestial appearance or person.<BR> E. ख, and मूर्त्ति<BR>form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=223-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खमूर्त्तिमत्|खमूर्तिमत्|खमूर्तिमन्त्
खमूर्त्तिमत् mfn. (-मान्-मती-मत्) Having a divine or celestial person or<BR>form.<BR> E. खमूर्त्ति, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=223-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खमूलि|खमूलिः
खमूलि f. (-लिः or -ली or -लिका) An aquatic plant, (Pistia stratiotes.)<BR> E. ख<BR>ether, मूल a root, affixes इन् or ङीष्; also खमूलिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=223-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खम्ब
खम्ब r. 1st cl. (खम्बति) To go or move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=223-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खर|खरं|खरः
खर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>	 1. Hot.<BR>	 2. Sharp, pungent.<BR>	 3. Sharp, sharp-edged,<BR>cutting.<BR>	 4. Cruel, harsh.<BR>	 mn. (-रः-रं) Heat.<BR>	 m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. An ass.<BR>	 2.<BR>A Rākṣasa, the brother of RAVANA.<BR>	 3. A Daitya or demon in<BR>general.<BR>	 4. A sort of prickly nightshade.<BR>	 5. A crow.<BR>	 6. A heron.<BR>	 7.<BR>An osprey.<BR>	 f. (-रा) A kind of grass, (Andropogon serratus.<BR> E. ख an<BR>organ of sense, and रा to get or give, affix क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=223-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खरकुटि
खरकुटि f. (-टिः or -टी) A barber's shop.<BR> E. खर heat, and कुटि a dwelling;<BR>also written खरकुट्टि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=223-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खरकोण|खरकोणः
खरकोण m. (-णः) The francoline partridge.<BR> E. खर heat, कुण् to sound,<BR>affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=223-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खरक्वाण|खरक्वाणः
खरक्वाण m. (-णः) The francoline partridge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=223-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खरगन्धनिभा
खरगन्धनिभा f. (-भा) A plant, (Hedysarum lagopodioides.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=223-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खरगृह|खरगृहं
खरगृह n. (-हं) An ass's stable.<BR> E. खर an ass, and गृह a house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=223-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खरगेह|खरगेहं
खरगेह n. (-हं) A stable for asses.<BR> E. खर, and गेह a house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=223-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खरग्रह|खरग्रहः
खरग्रह n. (-हः) A stable for asses.<BR> E. खर, and ग्रह a house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=223-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खरघातन|खरघातनः
खरघातन m. (-नः) A plant, commonly Nagesar, (Mesua ferrea.)<BR> E. खर<BR>an ass, and घातन mischievous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=223-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खरच्छद|खरच्छदः
खरच्छद m. (-दः)<BR>	 1. A kind of reed or grass, (Saccharum cylindricum.)<BR>2. Also another kind, commonly Okera.<BR> E. खर warm, sharp, छद a<BR>leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=223-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खरणस्
खरणस् mfn. (-णाः-णाः-णः) Sharp-nosed.<BR> E. खर sharp, नस् from नासिका a<BR>nose; also with a final vowel खरणस mfn. (-सः-सा-सं.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=223-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खरदण्ड|खरदंड|खरदण्डं
खरदण्ड n. (-ण्डं) A lotus, (Nymphæa lotus.)<BR> E. खर sharp, and दण्ड stick<BR>or stem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=223-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खरदला
खरदला f. (-ला) Opposite leaved fig tree.<BR> E. खर hot, दल leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=223-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खरदूषण|खरदूषणः
खरदूषण m. (-णः) Thron apple, (Datura metel.)<BR> E. खर an ass and दूषण<BR>hurting; by its narcotic properties.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=223-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खरध्वंसिन्
खरध्वंसिन् m. (-सी) A name of RAMA.<BR> E. खर an imp or goblin so called,<BR>and ध्वंसिन् the destroyer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=223-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खरनाद|खरनादः
खरनाद m. (-दः) The braying of an ass.<BR> E. खर, and नाद noise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=223-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खरनादिन्
खरनादिन् m. (-दी-दिनी-दि) Braying as an ass.<BR>	 f. (-नी) A kind of perfume:<BR>see रेणुका.<BR> E. खरनाद and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=223-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खरपत्र|खरपत्रः
खरपत्र m. (-त्रः)<BR>	 1. A. red sort of Tulasi or basil.<BR>	 2. The teak tree, (Tec-<BR>tona grandis.)<BR> E. खर hot, and पत्र a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=223-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खरपत्रक|खरपत्रकः
खरपत्रक m. (-कः) A plant: see तिलक.<BR> E. कन् added to खरपत्र hot leaved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=223-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खरपात्र|खरपात्रं
खरपात्र n. (-त्रं) An iron pot or vessel.<BR> E. खर an ass, and पात्र a vessel;<BR>fit for such an animal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=223-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खरपादाद्य
खरपादाद्य m. (-द्यः) The elephant or wood apple, (Ferenia elephantium:)<BR>see कपित्थ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=223-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खरपाल|खरपालः
खरपाल m. (-लः) A wooden vessel.<BR> E. खर, and पाल what cherishes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=223-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खरपुष्प|खरपुष्पः
खरपुष्प m. (-ष्पः) A plant, commonly Marua: see मरुवक f. (-ष्पा or -ष्पिका)<BR>A kind of Tulasi, (Ocymum gratissimum;) also वर्वर.<BR> E. खर sharp,<BR>hot, पुष्प a flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=223-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खरप्रिय|खरप्रियः
खरप्रिय m. (-यः) A pigeon.<BR> E. खर hot, and प्रिय fond, dear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=223-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खरमञ्जरी
खरमञ्जरी f. (-री) A plant, (Achyranthes aspera:) see अपामार्ग.<BR> E. खर sharp,<BR>pungent, and मञ्जरी a pedicle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=223-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खरयान
खरयान n. (-नं) A vehicle drawn by asses<BR> E. खर, and यान a carriage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=223-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खरलोमन्
खरलोमन् m. (-मा) One of the chiefs of the Naga or serpent race inhabi-<BR>ing hell.<BR> E. खर an ass, and लोमन् hair of the body; having the skin<BR>of an ass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=223-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खरवल्लिका
खरवल्लिका f. (-का) A plant, commonly Goraksha Chakuliya, (Hedysarum<BR>lagopodioides.)<BR> E. खर hot, sharp, वल्लिका a pedicle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=223-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खरशब्द|खरशब्दः
खरशब्द m. (-ब्दः)<BR>	 1. An osprey.<BR>	 2. The braying of an ass.<BR> E. खर, and शब्द<BR>sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=223-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खरशाल
खरशाल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Born or produced in an asse's stall.<BR>	 f. (-ला) A n<BR>asse's stable or stall.<BR> E. खर, and शाला a hall; in the first sense the<BR>final is dropped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=223-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खरसोल्ल
खरसोल्ल m. (-ल्लः) An iron vessel; also read खरसोनि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=223-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खरांशु|खरांशुः
खरांशु m. (-शुः) The sun<BR> E. खर hot, and अंशु a ray.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=223-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खरागरी
खरागरी f. (-री) A kind of grass, (Andropogon Serratus;) also देवताड E.<BR>खर venom गृ to take, with आङ् prefixed. अच् and ङीष् affixes; an-<BR>tivenomous, an antidote.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=223-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खरालक
खरालक m. (-कः) An iron arrow; also खरालिक m. (-कः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=223-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खराश्वा
खराश्वा f. (-श्वा) A plant, (Celosia cristata.)<BR> E. खर an ass, अश to be eaten,<BR>and व and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=223-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खरिका
खरिका f. (-का) Musk in powder.<BR> E. खर, कन् added, fem form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=223-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खरिन्धय|खरिंधय
खरिन्धय mfn. (-यः-यी-यं) Drinking ass's milk.<BR> E. खरी and धे to drink,<BR>खश् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=223-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खरु|खरुः
खरु mfn. (-रुः-रुः or -रूः-रु)<BR>	 1. White.<BR>	 2. Desirous of improper or prohi-<BR>bited things.<BR>	 3. A fool, foolish, idiotic.<BR>	 4. Harsh, cruel.<BR>	 m. (-रुः)<BR>	 1.<BR>A name of ŚIVA.<BR>	 2. A horse.<BR>	 3. A tooth.<BR>	 4. pride.<BR>	 5. Love or the<BR>deity KaMA.<BR>	 6. White, the colour. खन् to dig, &c. Uṇādi affix कु<BR>and र substituted for the final.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=223-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खर्ब्ब|खर्ब|खर्ब्बः
खर्ब्ब r. 10th cl. (खर्ब्बति) To go or move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=223-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खर्ज|खर्ज्ज
खर्ज r. 1st. cl. (-खर्जति)<BR>	 1. To worship, to treat with respect or courtesy.<BR>2. To pain or make clean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=223-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खर्जिका|खर्ज्जिका
खर्जिका f. (-का) A relish, a provocative to drink.<BR> E. खर्ज् to pain,<BR>and वुन् affix. fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=223-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खर्ज्जुर|खर्जुर|खर्जुरं|खर्ज्जुरं
खर्ज्जुर n. (-रं) Silver: see खर्ज्जूर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=223-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खर्ज्जू|खर्जू
खर्ज्जू f. (-र्ज्जूः)<BR>	 1. Cutaneous eruption, itch, scab, &c.<BR>	 2. A worm, an<BR>insect.<BR> E. खर्ज्जि to give pain, Uṇādi affix ऊ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=223-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खर्ज्जूर|खर्जूर|खर्जूरः|खर्ज्जूरं|खर्ज्जूरः
खर्ज्जूर n. (-रं)<BR>	 1. Silver.<BR>	 2. The fruit of the date.<BR>	 3. Yellow orpiment.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-रः)<BR>	 1. The date tree. (Phœnix sylvestris.<BR>	 2. A scorpion.<BR>	 f. (-री)<BR>The wild date tree.<BR> E. खर्ज् to give pain, &c. Uṇādi affix ऊर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=223-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खर्ज्जूररस|खर्जूररस|खर्जूररसः
खर्ज्जूररस m. (-सः) The juice or extract of the wild date, Tari, used to<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=224-a" target="_blank">Page224-a+ 60</a>]<BR>leaven bread, and as an intoxicating liquor, when in a state of<BR>spontaneous fermentation.<BR> E. खर्ज्जूर and रस juice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=223-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खर्द|खर्द्द
खर्द r. 1st cl. (खर्दति) To bite, to sting venomously.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=224-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खर्प्पर|खर्पर|खर्परः
खर्प्पर mf. (-रः-री) A kind of collyrium or application to the eyes: see<BR>कर्प्पर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A thief.<BR>	 2. A rogue, a cheat.<BR>	 3. A beggar's bowl<BR>or dish.<BR>	 4. The half of a skull.<BR>	 5. An umbrella or parasol.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=224-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खर्द्ध्व
खर्द्ध्व r. 1st cl. (खर्द्ध्वति) To go, to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=224-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खर्पराल
खर्पराल m. (-लः) A plant: see कन्दराल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=224-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खर्प्परीतूत्थ
खर्प्परीतूत्थ n. (-त्थं) A sort of collyrium.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=224-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खर्ब|खर्ब्ब|खर्ब्बः
खर्ब r. 1st cl. (खर्वति) To go, to move to or towards.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=224-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खर्ब्ब|खर्ब|खर्ब्बः
खर्ब्ब mfn. (-र्ब्बः-र्ब्बा-र्ब्बं) A dwarf, short, low, of little size or stature.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-र्ब्बः) One of KUVERAS nine Nidhis or treasures.<BR>	 n. (-र्ब्बं) A large<BR>number, ten million-millions.<BR> E. खर्ब्ब or खर्ब्ब to be small, to go, to<BR>move, affix अच; also खर्व्व.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=224-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खर्व्वशाख|खर्वशाख
खर्व्वशाख mfn. (-खः-खा-खं) Small, short, dwarfish.<BR> E. खर्ब्ब short, and शाखा<BR>a branch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=224-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खर्म्म|खर्म|खर्म्मः
खर्म्म n. (-र्म्मं)<BR>	 1. Virility, manliness.<BR>	 2. Wovesilk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=224-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खर्ब्ब|खर्ब|खर्ब्बः
खर्ब्ब r. 1st. cl. (खर्व्वति) To be proud, or haughty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=224-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खर्व्व|खर्व|खर्वः|खर्व्वः
खर्व्व mfn. (-र्व्वः-र्व्वा-र्व्वं) A dwarf, &c.: see खर्व्व.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=224-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खर्ब्बट|खर्बट
खर्ब्बट mn. (-टः-टं)<BR>	 1. The capital of a district of four hundred villages,<BR>a market or country town.<BR>	 2. A village at the foot of a mountain.<BR>E. खर्ब्ब being proud, and अट what goes or is.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=224-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खल|खलं|खलः
खल r. 1st. cl. (खलति)<BR>	 1. To gather.<BR>	 2. To move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=224-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खल|खलं|खलः
खल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>	 1. Low, vile. base.<BR>	 2. Low, inferior.<BR>	 3. Cruel.<BR>mischief-making.<BR>	 4. Bad, wicked.<BR>	 mn. (-लः-लं)<BR>	 1. Earth, mould or<BR>soil.<BR>	 2. Place, site.<BR>	 3. Sediment, deposit of oil, &c.<BR>	 4. A granary,<BR>a threshing floor.<BR>	 5. A mill.<BR>	 m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. The sun.<BR>	 2. A tree with<BR>black blossoms: see तमाल.<BR>	 3. The Dhatura plant.<BR> E. खल् to gather,<BR>(misfortune, &c.) affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=224-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खलता
खलता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Wickedness, villainy.<BR>	 2. Filthiness.<BR> E. खल and तल्<BR>affix; also with त्वा affix खलत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=224-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खलति|खलतिः
खलति mfn. (-तिः-तिः or -ती-ति) Bald, baldheaded.<BR> E. स्खल् to fall, Uṇādi<BR>affix अतच् इ inserted, and स rejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=224-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खलपू
खलपू mf. (-पूः) A sweeper, a cleaner, Mehter or Farash.<BR> E. खल place,<BR>and पू who cleans, from पूञ् to cleanse or purify, affix क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=224-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खलप्रीति
खलप्रीति f. (-तिः) The friendship or favour of wicked or low persons. E.<BR>खल and प्रीति affection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=224-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खलमूर्त्ति|खलमूर्ति|खलमूर्त्तिः
खलमूर्त्ति m. (-र्त्तिः) Quicksilver.<BR> E. खल place, and मूर्त्ति form; taking<BR>the form of the place it lies in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=224-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खलसंसर्ग|खलसंसर्गः
खलसंसर्ग m. (-र्गः) Associating with bad company.<BR> E. खल, संसर्ग asso-<BR>ciating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=224-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खलाधारा
खलाधारा f. (-रा) A cockroach.<BR> E. खल the sediment of oil, and आधार<BR>having.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=224-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खलि|खलिः
खलि m. (-लिः) Sediment of oil or oil-cake.<BR> E. खल् to gather, इन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=224-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खलिन्
खलिन् mfn. (-ली-लिनी-लि) Having sediment, &c.<BR>	 f. (-नी)<BR>	 1. A multitude<BR>of threshing floors.<BR>	 2. A plant, (Anthericum tuberosum.)<BR> E. खल,<BR>and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=224-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खलिन|खलिनं|खलिनः
खलिन mn. (-नः-नं) The bit of a bridle: see खलीन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=224-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खलिश|खलिशः
खलिश mf. (-शः-शा) A kind of fish, (Trichopodus colisa, Ham.)<BR>also खलेश.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=224-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खलीकार|खलीकारः
खलीकार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Mischief, evil.<BR>	 2. Leaving or reducing to sedi-<BR>ment.<BR> E. खल mischievous, and कार who makes; च्वि inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=224-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खलीन|खलीनं|खलीनः
खलीन mn. (-नः-नं) The bit of a bridle.<BR> E. ख the mouth, and लीन what<BR>is fixed; also the vowel being made short खलिन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=224-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खलु
खलु ind.<BR>	 1. A particle of prohibition.<BR>	 2. An expletive.<BR>	 3. An expres-<BR>sion of endearment or conciliation.<BR>	 4. An expression indicating<BR>inquiry.<BR>	 5. An expression of asseveration or ascertainment,<BR>(certainly, indeed.)<BR>	 6. Only. खल् to gather, affix उ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=224-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खलुज
खलुज m. (-लुक्) Darkness.<BR> E. ख the sky, लुक् dropped, lost, from लुज्<BR>to efface, affix क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=224-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खलुरेष|खलुरेषः
खलुरेष m. (-षः) A kind of wild animal; also खलुरेषक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=224-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खलूरिका
खलूरिका f. (-का) A parade, a place for military exercise.<BR> E. खडि to<BR>break, ऊरच् affix, ड changed to ल, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=224-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खलेधानी
खलेधानी (-नी) Tho post of a threshing floor, round which the oxen<BR>pass who tread out grain; also खलेवाली.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=224-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खलेबाली
खलेबाली f. (-ली) A post: see the preceding.<BR> E. खल् a threshing floor<BR>in the seventh case, and बाली what is firm, a post, &c. from खल<BR>to be strong, अण् and ङीष् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=224-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खलेश|खलेशः
खलेश m. (-शः) A kind of fish, (commonly Trichopodus colisa, HAM.)<BR>see खलिश.<BR> E. खले in dirt, and श from शी to sleep; burrowing in<BR>the mud of the banks, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=224-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खलेशय|खलेशयः
खलेशय m. (-यः) The Khalisa fish: see the preceding. E. As before.<BR>शी, and अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=224-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खलोक्ति|खलोक्तिः
खलोक्ति f. (-क्तिः) Abuse, low or wicked language.<BR> E. खल, and उक्ति<BR>speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=224-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खल्या
खल्या mfn. (-ल्यः-ल्या-ल्यं) Fit for oil cake, for a threshing floor, &c.<BR>(-ल्या) A multitude of threshing floors.<BR> E. खल a threshing floor<BR>affix क्यप्, यत् or य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=224-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खल्ल|खल्लः
खल्ल m. (-ल्लः)<BR>	 1. A kind of cloth or clothes, leather garments.)<BR>	 2. A<BR>canal, a cut, a creek, a trench, a deep hole.<BR>	 3. The Chataka, a<BR>kind of cuckoo.<BR>	 4. Leather.<BR>	 5. A leather water bag.<BR>	 6. A mill,<BR>a stone or vessel for grinding drugs, &c.<BR>	 f. (-ल्ली) Shooting pain<BR>in the extremities.<BR> E. खल collecting, &c. and ल what gets;<BR>also खल्लक m. (-कः)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=224-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खल्लिका
खल्लिका f. (-का) A frying pan.<BR> E. कन् added to the preceding,<BR>fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=224-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खल्लिट|खल्लिटः
खल्लिट mfn. (-टः-टा-टं) Bald, morbidly troubled with falling of the<BR>hair; also खल्लीट.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=224-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खल्लीट|खल्लीटः
खल्लीट mfn. (-टः-टा-टं) Becoming morbidly bald: see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=224-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खल्वट
खल्वट m. (-टः) A severe cough.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=224-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खल्विका
खल्विका f. (-का) A frying pan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=224-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खव
खव r. 9th cl. (खौनाति)<BR>	 1. To be past birth.<BR>	 2. To cause or procure<BR>prosperity.<BR>	 3. To produce purity, to purify.<BR>	 4. To produce or<BR>manifest wealth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=224-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खवल्ली
खवल्ली f. (-ल्ली) A parasitic plant.<BR> E. ख, वल्ली a pedicle<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=224-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खवारि
खवारि n. (-रिः) Rain water, dew, vapour, &c.<BR> E. ख heaven, and वारि<BR>water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=224-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खवाष्प
खवाष्प m. (-प्पः) Snow, hoar frost, dew.<BR> E. ख sky, and वाष्प vapour or tears.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=224-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खश|खशः
खश m. (-शः)<BR>	 1. A mountainous country to the north of India.<BR>	 2. A<BR>native of that country, considered as a degraded Kṣatriya.<BR>	 f. (-शा)<BR>A kind of perfume, commonly Mura.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=224-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खशय
खशय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Resting or dwelling in the air.<BR> E. ख and शी to<BR>sleep, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=224-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खशरीर
खशरीर n. (-रं) A celestial or immortal body.<BR> E. ख and शरीर body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=224-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खशरीरिन्
खशरीरिन् mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि) Of a heavenly body.<BR> E. खशरीर and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=224-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खशेट|खशेटः
खशेट m. (-टः) The Khalisa, a kind of fish: see खलेश.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=224-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खश्वास|खश्वासः
खश्वास m. (-सः) Air or wind.<BR> E. ख the atmosphere, and श्वास breath.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=224-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खष
खष r. 1st cl. (खषति) To kill, to hurt or injure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=224-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खष्प|खष्पं|खष्पः
खष्प n. (-ष्यं)<BR>	 1. Anger, passion. Violence, oppression.<BR> E. खन् to hurt, to<BR>dig, प Uṇādi affix, न changed to ष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=224-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खस|खसः
खस m. (-सः) Itch, scab.<BR>	 2. A man of a country or tribe considered to be<BR>a degraded Kṣatriya: the Khasas inhabit the mountains surroun-<BR>ding Kashmir.<BR>	 f. (-सा) The mother of the imps or goblins.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=224-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खसगन्ध
खसगन्ध m. (-न्धः) A plant, commonly Kṣirakakolic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=224-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खसम|खसमः
खसम m. (-मः) A Buddha or Bauddha deified saint.<BR> E. ख heaven, and<BR>सम equal, the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=224-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खसम्भव|खसंभव
खसम्भव mfn. (-वः-वा-वं) Produced in the sky, aerial, ethereal.<BR> E. ख, and<BR>सम्भव birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=224-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खसर्पण|खसर्पणः
खसर्पण m. (-णः) One of the Buddha or Bouddha saints.<BR>	 n. (-णं) Gliding<BR>through the air.<BR> E. ख heaven, and सर्पण who goes to or in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=224-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खसात्मज|खसात्मजः
खसात्मज m. (-जः) An imp or goblin.<BR> E. खसा the mother of these beings,<BR>आत्मज a son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=225-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खस्तनी
खस्तनी f. (-नी) The earth.<BR> E. ख earth, स्तन a breast, affix ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=225-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खस्खस|खस्खसः
खस्खस m. (-सः) The poppy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=225-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खस्खसरस|खस्खसरसः
खस्खसरस m. (-सः) Poppy juice, opium.<BR> E. खस्खस and रस juice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=225-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खस्फटिक
खस्फटिक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. Crystal, the sun gem.<BR>	 2. The moon gem: see सूर्य्यकान्त<BR>and चन्द्रकान्त<BR> E. ख heaven, and स्फटिक crystal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=225-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खहर
खहर m. (-रः) (In arithmetic.) A fraction having a cypher for its deno-<BR>minator.<BR> E. ख a cypher, हर divisor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=225-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खाजिक|खाजिकः
खाजिक m. (-कः) Fried or parched grain.<BR> E. खज् to go, &c. affix ण्वुल्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=225-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खाट|खाटः
खाट mf. (-टः-टा)<BR>	 1. A bier, a cot or bedstead on which dead bodies are<BR>conveyed to the pile.<BR> E. खट् to screen, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=225-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खाटि|खाटिः
खाटि f. (-टिः)<BR>	 1. Caprice, whim.<BR>	 2. A scar.<BR>	 3. A bier.<BR> E. खट् to screen,<BR>&c. इञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=225-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खाटिका
खाटिका f. (-का) A bier: see खाट also खाटी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=225-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खाण्डव|खांडव|खाण्डवं|खांडवः|खाण्डवः
खाण्डव n. (-वं) A wood, sacred to INDRA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=225-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खाण्डिक|खांडिक|खांडिकः|खाण्डिकः
खाण्डिक m. (-कः) A confectioner, a seller of sweetmeats.<BR> E. खण्ड molasses<BR>or coarse sugar, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=225-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खात|खातं
खात mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Dug, excavated.<BR>	 2. Torn, rent.<BR>	 n. (-टं)<BR>	 1. A square<BR>or oblong pond.<BR>	 2. Any excavation.<BR> E. खन् to dig, affix क्त and<BR>the pen. lengthened.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=225-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खातक|खातकं|खातकः
खातक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A delver, a digger.<BR>	 2. A debtor; more correctly<BR>खादक.<BR>	 n. (-कं) A moat, a ditch.<BR> E. खात a pond, affix कन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=225-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खातभू
खातभू f. (-भूः) A moat, a ditch.<BR> E. खात a pond, भू earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=225-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खात्र|खात्रं
खात्र n. (-त्रं)<BR>	 1. A square or large pond.<BR>	 2. A spade, a hoe.<BR>	 3. A wood<BR>4. A thread.<BR> E. खन् to dig, ष्ट्रन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=225-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खाद|खादः
खाद (ऋ) खादृ r. 1st cl. (खादति) To eat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=225-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खादक|खादकः
खादक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A borrower, a user, (in law,) literally, an eater.<BR>	 2. A<BR>feeder, one who eats or feeds.<BR> E. खाद् to eat, affix वुन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=225-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खादन|खादनं|खादनः
खादन m. (-नः) A tooth.<BR>	 n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Eating.<BR>	 2. Food, victuals.<BR> E. खाद् to<BR>eat, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=225-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खादनीय
खादनीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Edible, to be eaten.<BR> E. खाद and अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=225-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खादित|खादितं
खादित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Eaten.<BR> E. खाद् to eat, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=225-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खादितवत्
खादितवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Eating, feeding.<BR> E. खाद and क्तवतु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=225-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खादितव्य
खादितव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं) To be eaten, what may be or must be eaten,<BR>&c.<BR> E. खाद and तव्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=225-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खादिर|खादिरः
खादिर mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>	 1. Derived from the Khayar tree.<BR>	 2. made of its<BR>wood.<BR> E. खदिर, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=225-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खादिरसार|खादिरसारः
खादिरसार m. (-रः) Catechu, the resinous extact of the Mimosa catechu.<BR>E. खदिर and सार essence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=225-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खादुक|खादुकः
खादुक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Mischievous, injurious, malignant.<BR> E. खाद् to eat, उकन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=225-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खाद्य|खाद्यं
खाद्य mfn. (-द्य-द्या-द्यं) Edible, to be eaten, what is to be or may be<BR>eaten.<BR>	 n. (-द्यं) Food, victuals.<BR> E. खाद् to eat, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=225-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खानि|खानिः
खानि mf. (-निः-नी) A mine.<BR> E. खन् to dig, इञ् affix, fem. affix ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=225-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खानिक|खानिकं|खानिकः
खानिक n. (-कं) An opening or hole in a wall, a breach.<BR> E. खन् to dig affix ठञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=225-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खानिल|खानिलः
खानिल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) A housebreaker.<BR> E. खन् to dig, इलच् affix, deriv<BR>irr.; this is sometimes read खानिन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=225-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खानोदक|खानोदकः
खानोदक m. (-कः) A cocoanut.<BR> E. खान rending, and उदक water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=225-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खापगा
खापगा f. (-गा) A name of GANGA or the Ganges.<BR> E. ख heaven, and अपगा<BR>a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=225-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खार|खारः
खार mf. (-रः-रिः or -री) A Khari, a measure of grain containing six-<BR>teen Dronas, or about three bushels: it is also reckoned at three<BR>or four Dronas; also at five Gonis, which is considered equal to<BR>512 Ser's f. (-री) A scar.<BR> E. खन् to dig, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=225-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खारिम्पच|खारिंपच|खारिम्पचः
खारिम्पच mfn. (-चः-चा-चं) Cooking a Khari, by measure (a vessel, &c.)<BR>E. खारी as above, पच् to cook, affix खश्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=225-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खारीक|खारीकं
खारीक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) A field, &c. equal to or sown with a Khari of<BR>grain.<BR> E. खारी the measure, and इकन् or ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=225-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खारीवाप|खारीवापः
खारीवाप mfn. (-पः-पा-पं) A field sown with a Khari of grain, &c. E.<BR>खारी, and वाप sowing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=225-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खालित्य
खालित्य n. (-त्यं) Morbid baldness.<BR> E. खलति and यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=225-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खाशि
खाशि m. (-शिः) Name of a country to the east of Bengal: the Cossya<BR>hills; also खाशिक m. (-कः.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=225-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खाश्मरी
खाश्मरी f. (-री) A plant: see काश्मरी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=225-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खिखि|खिखिः
खिखि f. (-खिः) A fox; also in some copies, किखि q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=225-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खिङ्खिर|खिंखिर|खिंखिरः|खिङ्खिरः
खिङ्खिर mf. (-रः-रा) A fox.<BR>	 m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. One of ŚIVA'S weapons, 2. A kind<BR>of perfume, commonly Hala.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=225-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खिट
खिट r. 1st cl. (खेटति)<BR>	 1. To terrify, to alarm or surprise.<BR>	 2. To be ter-<BR>rified, to fear or dread.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=225-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खिद
खिद r. 4th and 7th cls. (खिद्यते and खिंते) To be distressed, to suffer pain<BR>or misery. (औ, प) औखिदप् r. 6th cl. (खिन्दति) To afflict or distress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=225-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खिदिर|खिदिरः
खिदिर m. (-रः) The moon.<BR>	 2. An ascetic, a penitent, 3. A pauper, E.<BR>खिद् to suffer pain, किरच् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=225-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खिद्यमान|खिद्यमानः
खिद्यमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Suffering pain or distress.<BR> E. खिद्, with शानच्<BR>aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=225-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खिद्र|खिद्रः
खिद्र m. (-द्रः)<BR>	 1. Disease, sickness.<BR>	 2. A pauper, a poor man<BR> E. खिद् to be<BR>in pain, रक् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=225-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खिन्न|खिन्नः
खिन्न mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>	 1. Distrest, suffering pain or uneasiness.<BR>	 2. Weari-<BR>ed, exhausted.<BR> E. खिद् to be pain, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=225-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खिल|खिलं|खिलः
खिल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>	 1. Waste or unploughed land.<BR>	 2. Empty, vacant.<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. A name of BRAHMĀ.<BR>	 2. VIṢṆU.<BR>	 mn. (-लः-लं) A com-<BR>pendium, a compilation, especially of hymns and prayers.<BR> E. ख<BR>vacuity, &c. ल what gets or possesses, affix ड, and इ substituted<BR>for the penultimate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=225-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खु
खु (ङ) खुङ् r. 1st cl. (खुवते) To sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=225-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खुङ्गाह|खुंगाह|खुंगाहः|खुङ्गाहः
खुङ्गाह m. (-हः) A black horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=225-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खुज
खुज r. 1st cl. (-उ) खुजु (खोजति) To steal or rob.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=225-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खुञ्जाक
खुञ्जाक m. (-कः) A kind of grass: see देवताडक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=225-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खुड
खुड r. 6th cl. (-खडति) To cover. r. 1st. and 10th cls. (खोडति खोडयति)<BR>also (इ,) खुडि r. 1st. and 10th cls. (खुण्डति, खुण्डयति) To break<BR>in pieces, to sunder, to divide, tear, rend, &c. (इङ्) खुडिङ् r. 1st cl.<BR>(खुण्डते) To limp, to be lame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=225-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खुर|खुरः
खुर r. 6th cl. (खुरति) To cut, to scratch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=225-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खुर|खुरः
खुर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A hoof, a horse's hoof, &c.<BR>	 2. A razor.<BR>	 3. The foot of a<BR>bedstead; also क्षुर 4. A sort of perfume, commonly Nakhi, ap-<BR>parently a dried shell fish, and of the shape of a hoof.<BR> E. खुर् to<BR>cut, रन् Uṇādi affix, the radical र is dropped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=225-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खुरक|खुरकः
खुरक m. (-कः) A plant commonly Tila.<BR> E. कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=225-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खुरक्षेप|खुरक्षेपः
खुरक्षेप m. (-पः) A kick, kicking.<BR> E. खुर, and क्षेप throwing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=225-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खुरणस्
खुरणस् mfn. (-णाः-णाः-णः) Flat-nosed, having a nose like a horse's hoof,<BR>E. खुर a hoof, and नस् deriv. of नासिका a nose; also with a final<BR>vowel खुरणस mfn. (-सः-सा-सं.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=225-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खुरपदवी
खुरपदवी f. (-वी) A horse's foot marks.<BR> E. खुर, and पदवी vestige.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=225-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खुरप्र|खुरप्रः
खुरप्र m. (-प्रः) An arrow with a semicircular head: see क्षुरप्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=225-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खुरली
खुरली f. (-ली) Military exercise, practising archery, &c.<BR> E. खुर् to cut,<BR>अलच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=225-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खुराक|खुराकः
खुराक m. (-कः) An animal in general.<BR> E. खुर् to cut, and आक aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=225-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खुराघात|खुराघातः
खुराघात m. (-तः) A kick.<BR> E. खुर, and आघात a blow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=225-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खुराभिघात
खुराभिघात m. (-तः)<BR>	 1. A kick.<BR>	 2. Kicking, pawing, (as a horse.)<BR> E. खुर,<BR>and अभिघात striking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=225-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खुरालक|खुरालकः
खुरालक m. (-कः) An iron arrow.<BR> E. खुर a razor, and अल what is able,<BR>affix कन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=225-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खुरालिक|खुरालिकः
खुरालिक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A barber's case.<BR>	 2. An iron arrow.<BR>	 3. A pillow. E.<BR>खुर a razor, &c. अल् to be equal to, affix ठक्; some read this खरा-<BR>लक, but to all appearance erroneously.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=225-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खुर्द|खुर्द्द
खुर्द r. 1st cl. (खुर्दते or खूर्दते) To play, to sport.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=225-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खुल्ल|खुल्लं
खुल्ल mfn. (-ल्लः-ल्ला-ल्लं) Small, little, low, mean, &c.<BR>	 n. (-ल्लं) A kind of<BR>perfume: see खुर.<BR> E. खुद् to divide, &c. and ल from ला to get, the<BR>radical द becomes ल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=225-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खुल्लक|खुल्लकः
खुल्लक mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>	 1. Low, vile.<BR>	 2. Little, small.<BR>	 3. Poor, indigent.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=226-a" target="_blank">Page226-a+ 60</a>]<BR>4. Cruel, harsh.<BR>	 5. Wicked, mischievous, malignant: see क्षुल्ल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=225-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खुल्लतात|खुल्लतातः
खुल्लतात m. (-तः) A father's younger brother; also क्षुल्लतात.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=226-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खुल्लम|खुल्लमः
खुल्लम m. (-मः) A road.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=226-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खूर्द|खूर्द्द
खूर्द r. 1st cl. (खूर्दते) To play: see खुर्द.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=226-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खेखीरक|खेखीरकः
खेखीरक m. (-कः) A hollow or sounding reed, or cane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=226-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खेगमन|खेगमनः
खेगमन m. (-नः) A gallinule.<BR> E. खे in the air, and गमन going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=226-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खेचर|खेचरः
खेचर mfn. (-रः-री-रं) Aerial, moving in the air.<BR>	 m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A name of<BR>ŚIVA.<BR>	 2. A Vidyadhara or kind of demigod.<BR>	 3. Quicksilver.<BR> E. खे<BR>in heaven, and चर who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=226-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खेट|खेटं|खेटः
खेट r. 1st cl. (खेटति) To alarm. r. 10th cl. (खेटयति) To eat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=226-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खेट|खेटं|खेटः
खेट mfn. (-टः-टा-टं)<BR>	 1. Vile, bad, low.<BR>	 2. Armed, having a weapon or<BR>weapons.<BR>	 mn. (-टः-टं) Hunting, the chase; also आखेट m. (-टः)<BR>	 1.<BR>A shield.<BR>	 2. A village, the residence of peasants or farmers.<BR>	 3. A<BR>small town, half the Pura or town.<BR>	 4. The club of BALARĀMA.<BR>	 5.<BR>Phlegm, the phlegmatic or watery humour.<BR>	 6. The ascending node<BR>or RAHU.<BR>	 7. A horse.<BR>	 n. (-टं) Grass.<BR> E. खिट् to terrify, &c. affix घञ्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=226-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खेटक|खेटकः
खेटक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A village, the residence of agricultural peasants.<BR>	 2. A<BR>shield.<BR>	 3. The club of BALARĀMA.<BR> E. खिट् to terrify, &c. अच् affix,<BR>and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=226-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खेटिताल|खेटितालः
खेटिताल m. (-लः) A minstrel, a family bard or piper, whose business it<BR>is to awaken the Laird, with music and singing.<BR> E. खेटि derived<BR>from खिट् to disturb, and ताल tune.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=226-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खेटिन्
खेटिन् m. (-टी) A lecher, a libertine.<BR> E. खेट sport, affix इनि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=226-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खेड
खेड r. 10th cl. (खेडयति) To eat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=226-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खेडिताल
खेडिताल m. (-लः) A minstrel: see खेटिताल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=226-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खेद|खेदः
खेद m. (-दः)<BR>	 1. Sorrow, affliction, distress. Lassitude, depression.<BR>	 3.<BR>Pain.<BR>	 4. Proverty.<BR> E. खिद् to be distressed, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=226-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खेदन|खेदनं
खेदन n. (-नं) See the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=226-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खेदान्वित
खेदान्वित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Distressed, pained.<BR> E. खेद, and अन्वित having.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=226-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खेदित
खेदित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Annoyed, harassed.<BR>	 2. Afflicted, distressed,<BR>pained.<BR> E. खिद् to give pain, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=226-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खेदिनी
खेदिनी f. (-नी)<BR>	 1. A plant, (Marsilea quadrifolia:) see असनपर्णी.<BR>	 2. A<BR>creeper, a creeping plant.<BR> E. खिद् to be distressed, affixes णिनि and<BR>ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=226-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खेय|खेयं
खेय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) To be dug.<BR>	 n. (-यं) A ditch, a moat.<BR> E. खन् to dig,<BR>affix क्यप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=226-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खेल
खेल (ऋ) खेऌ r. 1st cl. (खेलति) To shake to tremble, to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=226-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खेलन|खेलनं
खेलन n. (-नं) Play, sport, pastime.<BR>	 f. (-नी) A piece or man at drafts,<BR>chess, &c.<BR> E. खेल् to shake or move, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=226-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खेला
खेला f. (-ला) Play, pastime, sport<BR> E. खेल् to shake, अङ् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=226-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खेलि|खेलिः
खेलि f. (-लिः)<BR>	 1. A song, a hymn.<BR>	 2. An arrow.<BR>	 3. The sun.<BR>	 4. A bird.<BR>	 5.<BR>Any animal.<BR> E. खेल् to shake, कि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=226-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खेव
खेव (ऋ) खेवृ r. 1st cl. (खेवते) To serve.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=226-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खेसर|खेसरः
खेसर m. (-रः) A mule.<BR> E. खे in air, सर who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=226-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खै
खै r. 1st cl. (खायति)<BR>	 1. To be firm or steady.<BR>	 2. To kill, to injure or<BR>hurt.<BR>	 3. To dig.<BR>	 4. To mourn, to sorrow for.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=226-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खोङ्काह|खोङ्काहः
खोङ्काह m. (-हः) A white and brown horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=226-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खोट
खोट r. 1st cl. (ऋ) खोट्ट (खोटति) To be lame or lamed. r. 10th cl. (खोटयति)<BR>1. To eat.<BR>	 2. To throw or cast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=226-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खोटि|खोटिः
खोटि f. (-टिः) A cunning or scheming woman; also read खोरि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=226-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खोटी
खोटी f. (-टी) The gum olibanum tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=226-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खोड|खोडः
खोड (ऋ) खोडृ r. 1st cl. (खोडति) To be or become lame. r. 10th cl. (खोड-<BR>यति) To throw or cast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=226-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खोड|खोडः
खोड mfn. (-डः-डा-डं) Lame, limping.<BR> E. खोड्. to be lame, affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=226-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खोडकशीर्ष
खोडकशीर्ष n. (-र्ष) The arched roof of a house, the coping of a wall, &c.<BR>also खोडकशीर्षक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=226-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खोर|खोरः
खोर (ऋ) खोरृ r. 1st cl. (खोरति) To be lame, to be prevented from<BR>moving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=226-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खोर|खोरः
खोर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Lame.<BR> E. खोर् to be lame, affix अच्; also खोड<BR>and खोल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=226-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खोल|खोलः
खोल (ऋ) खोऌ r. 1st cl. (खोलति) To be lame, to limp, to be prevented<BR>from moving. खोड, खोर, &c. are conceived by some authorities to<BR>be mere variations in the form of this root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=226-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खोल|खोलः
खोल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Lame.<BR> E. खोल् to be lame, affix अच्; also खोर, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=226-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खोलक|खोलकः
खोलक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A helmet, armour for the head.<BR>	 2. A pot, a sauce-<BR>pan.<BR>	 3. An ant-hill.<BR>	 4. The shell of the betel nut.<BR> E. खुड्. to cover,<BR>affix ण्वुल्, ड changed to ल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=226-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खोलि|खोलिः
खोलि f. (-लिः) A quiver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=226-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खोल्क|खोल्कः
खोल्क m. (-ल्कः)<BR>	 1. A meteor.<BR>	 2. A planet.<BR> E. ख, and उल्का torch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=226-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खोल्मुक|खोल्मुकः
खोल्मुक m. (-कः) The planet MARS.<BR> E. ख heaven, उल्मुक a hot coal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=226-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ख्या
ख्या r. 2nd cl. (ख्याति)<BR>	 1. To relate, to recount, to say or tell.<BR>	 2. To<BR>celebrate, to make known. With अभि prefixed, To shine or be<BR>glorious. With आ, To be famous. With वि, to celebrate. With सु,<BR>To be approved. With कु, To be infamous. With प्रति and आ, To<BR>reject, to refuse. With सम्, To count, to reckon. With सं and आ to<BR>denominate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=226-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ख्यात|ख्यातः
ख्यात mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Famous, celebrated, notorious.<BR> E. ख्या to relate,<BR>affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=226-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ख्यातगर्हण|ख्यातगर्हणः
ख्यातगर्हण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Notoriously vile, infamous.<BR> E. ख्यात famous,<BR>गर्हण abuse; also ख्यातगर्हित.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=226-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ख्यातगर्हित|ख्यातगर्हितः
ख्यातगर्हित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Infamous: see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=226-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ख्याति|ख्यातिः
ख्याति f. (-तिः) Fame, celebrity.<BR> E. ख्या to tell, affix क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=226-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ख्यापक
ख्यापक mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>	 1. Declaring, making known, one who tells or<BR>declares.<BR>	 2. One who confesses.<BR> E. ख्या to say, causal form, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=226-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ख्यापन|ख्यापनं
ख्यापन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Declaring, divulging.<BR>	 2. Saying, avowing.<BR>	 3. Confess-<BR>ing.<BR>	 4. Explaining.<BR> E. ख्या causal form, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=226-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग|गं|गः
ग The third consonant of the Nagri alphabet, the letter G.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=226-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग|गं|गः
ग mfn. (-गः-गा-गं) Who or what goes, used chiefly in composition: as<BR>अध्वगः a traveller, who goes a road; अपगा what goes down, (a<BR>river, &c.)<BR>	 m. (-गः)<BR>	 1. A name of the deity GANESHA.<BR>	 2. A Gand-<BR>harba or celestial musician.<BR>	 f. (-गा) A song.<BR>	 n. (-गं) Song, singing.<BR>E. गम् to go or गै to sing, affix ड, fem. affix टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=226-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गगण|गगणं
गगण n. (-णं) Sky, atmosphere, heaven.<BR> E. गम् to go. Uṇādi affix युच्<BR>and the radical final changed to ग; the word and its derivatives<BR>are also sometimes read गगन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=226-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गगणध्वज
गगणध्वज (-जः) 1. A cloud.<BR>	 2. The sun.<BR> E. गगण the sky, and ध्वज a stand-<BR>ard or symbol.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=226-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गगणाध्वग
गगणाध्वग m. (-गः)<BR>	 1. The sun.<BR>	 2. A planet.<BR>	 3. A heavenly spirit. E.<BR>गगण the sky, अध्वन् a road, and ग who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=226-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गगणपुष्प
गगणपुष्प m. (-ष्पः) A flower in the sky. i. e. an impossibility.<BR> E. गगण, and<BR>पुष्प a flower; alse गगणकुसुम, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=226-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गगणविहारिन्
गगणविहारिन् mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि) Sporting in heaven.<BR>	 m. (-री)<BR>	 1. The sun.<BR>2. A heavenly luminary.<BR>	 3. A divinity or celestial being,<BR> E. गगण,<BR>and विहारिन् who sports.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=226-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गगणसद्
गगणसद् mf. (-सत् or -सद्) Going in the air.<BR>	 m. (-सद्) A celestial being.<BR>E. गगण, and षद् to go, क्विप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=226-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गगणस्थ
गगणस्थ mfn. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थं) Situated in the sky.<BR> E. गगण and स्थ what stays<BR>in; also गगणस्थित, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=226-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गगणस्पर्शन
गगणस्पर्शन m. (-नः) Air, wind.<BR> E. गगण, and स्पर्शन who touches.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=226-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गगणाग्र
गगणाग्र n. (-ग्रं) The highest heavens, the summit or highest part of<BR>heaven.<BR> E. गगण, and अग्र end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=226-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गगणेचर
गगणेचर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A planet 2. An asterism.<BR>	 3. A heavenly spirit. E.<BR>गगणे in the sky, चर who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=226-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गगणोल्मुक
गगणोल्मुक m. (-कः) The planet Mars.<BR> E. गगण the sky, and उल्मुका a<BR>torch or coal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=226-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गग्घ
गग्घ r. 1st cl. (गग्घति) To laugh, to laugh at or deride: see घग्घ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=226-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गङ्गा|गंगा
गङ्गा f. (-ङ्गा) The river Ganges, or its personification as a goddess. E.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=227-a" target="_blank">Page227-a+ 60</a>]<BR>गम् to go, Uṇādi affix गन्, or गां the accusative of गो the earth, and<BR>ग who goes, form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=226-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गङ्गाका|गंगाका
गङ्गाका f. (-का) The river Ganges.<BR> E. कन् added to the preceding; also<BR>read गङ्गका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=227-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गङ्गाक्षेत्र|गंगाक्षेत्र
गङ्गाक्षेत्र n. (-त्रं) The river Ganges, and two Krosh on either of its<BR>banks.<BR> E. गङ्गा, and क्षेत्र holy place; all dying within such limits<BR>going to heaven, whatever their crimes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=227-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गङ्गाचिल्ली|गंगाचिल्ली
गङ्गाचिल्ली f. (-ल्ली) The black headed gull, (Larus ridibundus.)<BR> E. गङ्गा the<BR>Ganges, and चिल्ली a kite, considered by the Hindus as a species of<BR>that bird; the Gangetic kite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=227-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गङ्गाज|गंगाज|गङ्गाजः
गङ्गाज m. (-जः)<BR>	 1. A name of BHISHMA.<BR>	 2. A name of the deity KARTI-<BR>KEYA.<BR> E. गङ्गा the river goddess, and ज born; the son of GANGA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=227-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गङ्गाजल
गङ्गाजल n. (-लः) The water of the Ganga.<BR> E. गङ्गा, and जल water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=227-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गङ्गाटेय|गङ्गाटेयः
गङ्गाटेय mfn. (-यः-यी-यं) Going in or to the Ganges.<BR>	 m. (-यः) A shrimp or<BR>prawn; also गलाविल.<BR> E. गङ्गा the river, and अट् to go, अच् affix,<BR>गङ्गाट, and ढक् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=227-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गङ्गाद्बार
गङ्गाद्बार n. (-रं) The place where the Ganga enters the plains; also<BR>Haridwar.<BR> E. गङ्गा, and द्वार gate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=227-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गङ्गातीर
गङ्गातीर n. (-रं) The bank of the Ganga.<BR> E. गङ्गा, and तीर a bank.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=227-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गङ्गाधर|गंगाधर|गङ्गाधरः
गङ्गाधर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. An epithet of ŚIVA.<BR>	 2. The ocean.<BR> E. गङ्गा the Ganges,<BR>and धर who possesses or receives; according to the legend, the<BR>Ganges in its descent first alighted on the head of ŚIVA, and con-<BR>tinued for some period entangled in his hair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=227-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गङ्गापार
गङ्गापार n. (-रं) The bank of the Ganges.<BR> E. गङ्गा, and पार the bank.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=227-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गङ्गापुत्र|गंगापुत्र|गङ्गापुत्रः
गङ्गापुत्र m. (-त्रः)<BR>	 1. BHISHMA.<BR>	 2. A man of a mixed and vile caste, em-<BR>ployed to remove dead bodies.<BR>	 3. A Brahman who conducts the<BR>ceremonies of pilgrimage at some places on the Ganges, especially<BR>at Benares.<BR> E. गङ्गा, and पुत्र a son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=227-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गङ्गामध्य|गंगामध्य
गङ्गामध्य n. (-ध्यं) The bed or stream of the Ganges.<BR> E. गङ्गा, and मध्य<BR>centre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=227-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गङ्गाम्बु|गंगांबु
गङ्गाम्बु n. (-म्बु)<BR>	 1. Pure rain water, such as falls in Aswin.<BR>	 2. Ganges<BR>water.<BR> E. गङ्गा, and अम्बु water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=227-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गङ्गायात्रा|गंगायात्रा
गङ्गायात्रा f. (-त्रा)<BR>	 1. Pilgrimage to the Ganga.<BR>	 2. Carrying a sick per-<BR>son to the river side to die there.<BR> E. गङ्गा, and यात्रा going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=227-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गङ्गासुत|गंगासुत|गङ्गासुतः
गङ्गासुत m. (-तः)<BR>	 1. A name of KARTIKEYA.<BR>	 2. A name of the hero<BR>BHISHMA: see गङ्गाज.<BR> E. गङ्गा, and सुत a son; the son of GANGA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=227-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गङ्गिका|गंगिका
गङ्गिका f. (-का) The Ganges.<BR> E. गङ्गा, and कन् affix fem. from; also गङ्गका,<BR>and गङ्गाका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=227-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गङ्गीभूत|गंगीभूत
गङ्गीभूत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Become as the Ganges, as sacred, &c.<BR> E. गङ्गा,<BR>and भूत become, च्वि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=227-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गच्छ|गच्छः
गच्छ m. (-च्छः) A tree.<BR> E. गम् to go, and स Uṇādi affix, what goes or<BR>grows; also अगच्छ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=227-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गच्छत्
गच्छत् mfn. (-च्छन्-च्छन्ती-च्छत्) Going.<BR> E. गम् to go, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=227-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गज|गजः
गज r. 1st cl. (गजति) To be drunk, to be confused or inebriated; r. 1st<BR>and 10th cls. (गजति, गजयति) also (इ) गजि r. 1st cl. (गञ्जति) To<BR>sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=227-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गज|गजः
गज m. (-जः)<BR>	 1. An elephant.<BR>	 2. A measure of length, the Gaz, a yard,<BR>a measure of two cubits.<BR>	 3. A mound of earth sloping on both<BR>sides, on which a house may be created.<BR>	 4. A small hole in the<BR>ground for a fire, over which to prepare medicines.<BR> E. गज् to<BR>sound, to roar, affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=227-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गजकन्द|गजकंद|गजकन्दः
गजकन्द m. (-न्दः) A large esculent root, a sort of arum.<BR> E. गज, and<BR>कन्द root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=227-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गजकूर्म्माशिन्|गजकूर्माशिन्
गजकूर्म्माशिन् m. (-शी) A name of GARUḌA the bird and vehicle of<BR>VIṢṆU.<BR> E. गज an elephant, कूर्म्म a tortoise, and अशिन् who eats;<BR>alluding to a legend of his swallowing both animals whilst engaged<BR>in a contest with each other.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=227-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गजविर्भट
गजविर्भट mf. (-टः-टा) A kind of cucumber, (Cucumis Madraspatanus.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=227-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गजच्छाया
गजच्छाया f. (-या) A portion of time proper for a Sraddha,<BR> E. गज, and<BR>छाया shadow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=227-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गजढक्का
गजढक्का f. (-क्का) A kettle-drum carried on an elephant.<BR> E. गज an ele-<BR>phant, and ढक्का a large drum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=227-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गजता
गजता f. (-ता) A multitude of elephants.<BR> E. गज an elephant, तल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=227-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गजदघ्न|गजदघ्नः
गजदघ्न mfn. (-घ्नः-घ्नी-घ्नं) As high or tall as an elephant<BR> E. गज, and<BR>दघ्नच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=227-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गजदन्त|गजदंत|गजदन्तः
गजदन्त m. (-न्तः)<BR>	 1. A name of GANESHA.<BR>	 2. Ivory, the elephant's tooth.<BR>3. A bracket or pin projecting from the wall.<BR> E. गज a elephant,<BR>and दन्त a tooth; GANESHA is represented with an elephant's head.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=227-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गजदान|गजदानं
गजदान n. (-नं) The liquor exuding from an elephant's temples.<BR> E. गज<BR>and दान the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=227-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गजद्वयस|गजद्वयसः
गजद्वयस mfn. (-सः-सी-सं) As high as an elephant.<BR> E. गज, and द्वयसच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=227-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गजपति|गजपतिः
गजपति m. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. A large state elephant.<BR>	 2. A king.<BR> E. गज, and पति<BR>a master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=227-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गजपिप्पली
गजपिप्पली f. (-ली) A plant bearing a seed which resembles pepper, (Poth-<BR>os officinalis)<BR> E. गज an elephant, and पिप्पली long pepper; consi-<BR>dered to be a large species of pepper: see similar names, as करि-<BR>पिप्पली, इभकणा, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=227-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गजपुङ्गव|गजपुंगव|गजपुङ्गवः
गजपुङ्गव m. (-वः) A large and excellent elephant.<BR> E. गज, and पुङ्गव<BR>implying eminence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=227-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गजपुट|गजपुटः
गजपुट m. (-टः) A small hollow for a fire, over which to prepare medi-<BR>cal decoctions, extracts, &c.<BR> E. गज, and पुट a hollow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=227-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गजप्रिया
गजप्रिया f. (-या) The gum olibanum tree, (Boswellia serrata.)<BR> E. गज an<BR>elephant, and प्रिय beloved; also वल्लकी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=227-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गजबन्धनी|गजबंधनी
गजबन्धनी f. (-नी) A post to which an elephant is bound.<BR> E. गज, and<BR>बन्धन a binding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=227-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गजभक्षक|गजभक्षकः
गजभक्षक m. (-कः) The sacred fig tree.<BR> E. गज, and भक्षक eater; the<BR>young branches of the Pipal being the elephant's favourite<BR>food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=227-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गजभक्षा
गजभक्षा f. (-क्षा) The gum olibanum tree: see गजप्रिय.<BR> E. गज an ele-<BR>phant and भक्षा food; also गजभक्ष्या.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=227-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गजमण्डलिका|गजमंडलिका
गजमण्डलिका f. (-का) A ring or circle of elephants surrounding a car.<BR>&c.<BR> E. गज, मण्डल a circle, कन् affix fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=227-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गजमाचल|गजमाचलः
गजमाचल m. (-लः) A lion.<BR> E. गज an elephant, मा fortune, and चल<BR>what goes: the destroyer of the elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=227-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गजमात्र|गजमात्रः
गजमात्र mfn. (-त्रः-त्री-त्रं) As tall as an elephant.<BR> E. गज, and मात्रच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=227-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गजमुक्ता
गजमुक्ता f. (-क्ता) A pearl, supposed to be found in the head of an ele-<BR>phant.<BR> E. गज, and मुक्ता a pearl.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=227-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गजमोटन|गजमोटनः
गजमोटन m. (-नः) A lion.<BR> E. गज an elephant, मुट् to run away, in the<BR>causal from, affix ल्युट्; or with मुच् to go, गजमोचन as it is some-<BR>times read.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=227-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गजयूथ
गजयूथ m. (-थः) A herd of elephants.<BR> E. गज, and यूथ a herd.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=227-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गजवदन|गजवदनः
गजवदन m. (-नः) A name of GANESHA, who is represented always with<BR>the head of an elephant.<BR> E. गज. and वदन a face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=227-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गजव्रज|गजव्रजः
गजव्रज mfn. (-जः-जा-जं) Who walks like an elephant.<BR>	 n. (-जं)<BR>	 1. A troop<BR>of elephants. 2, The pace of an elephant.<BR> E. गज, and व्रज a number<BR>or going, who goes, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=227-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गजसाह्वय|गजसाह्वयं
गजसाह्वय n. (-यं) A famous city, Hastinapur the capital of the KuRUS.<BR>E. गज, स for सम् with, and आह्वय an appellation; named from its<BR>elephants; also गजाह्व, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=227-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गजाग्रणी
गजाग्रणी m. (-णी) The elephant of INDRA.<BR> E. गज and अग्रणी pre-eminent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=227-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गजाजीव|गजाजीवः
गजाजीव m. (-वः) An elephant keeper or driver.<BR> E. गज and आजीव who<BR>lives; who gets his livelihood by elephants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=227-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गजानन|गजाननः
गजानन m. (-नः) The deity GANESHA.<BR> E. गज an elephant, and आनन a face;<BR>see गजवदन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=227-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गजारि|गजारिः
गजारि m. (-रिः)<BR>	 1. A lion.<BR>	 2. A particular tree.<BR> E. गज and अरि a foe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=227-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गजारूढ
गजारूढ mfn. (-ढः-ढा-ढं) Mounted or riding on an elephant.<BR> E. गज and<BR>and आरूढ mounted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=227-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गजाशन|गजाशनः
गजाशन m. (-नः) The religious fig tree.<BR>	 f. (-ना)<BR>	 1. Hemp, (Cannabis<BR>sativa.)<BR>	 2. The gum olibanum tree.<BR>	 3. The root of a lotus.<BR> E. गज<BR>and अशन food; the food of elephants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=227-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गजास्य|गजास्यः
गजास्य m. (-स्यः) GANESHA: see गजानन.<BR> E. गज an elephant, and आस्य a<BR>face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=228-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गजाह्व|गजाह्वं
गजाह्व n. (-ह्वं) The city Hastinapur.<BR>	 f. (-ह्वा) A plant: see गजपिप्पली. E.<BR>गज, and आह्वा a name: see गजसाह्वय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=228-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गजाह्वय|गजाह्वयं
गजाह्वय n. (-यं) Hastinapur, the ancient Delhi: see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=228-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गजेन्द्र|गजेंद्र|गजेन्द्रः
गजेन्द्र m. (-न्द्रः)<BR>	 1. A large and excellent elephant.<BR>	 2. INDRA'S elephant<BR>E. गज, and इन्द्र chief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=228-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गजोषणा
गजोषणा f. (-णा) A short of pepper: see गजपिप्पली.<BR> E. गज, and उषणा<BR>pepper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=228-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गञ्ज|गंज|गंजः|गञ्जः
गञ्ज mfn. subst. (-ञ्जः-ञ्जा-ञ्जं) A mine, a jewel mine mn. (-ञ्जः-ञ्जं)<BR>	 1. A cow-<BR>house or station of cowherds.<BR>	 2. A treasury, a jewel room, the<BR>place where plate, &c. is preserved.<BR>	 3. A mart, a place where<BR>grain, &c. is stored for sale.<BR>	 m. (-ञ्जः) Disrespect, contempt.<BR>	 f. (ञ्जा)<BR>1. A tavern.<BR>	 2. A drinking vessel.<BR>	 3. A hut, a hovel, the abode of<BR>low people.<BR>	 4. The Gunja or Ratti, (Abrus precatorious:) see गुञ्जा.<BR>E. गजि to sound, अच् affix; fem. affix टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=228-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गञ्चिका
गञ्चिका f. (-का) A tavern.<BR> E. कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=228-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गड|गडः
गड r. 1st cl. (गडति) To distil or drop, to run as a liquid; also, गल (इ)<BR>गडि r. 1st cl. (गण्डति) To affect the cheek, to be rough as the cheek,<BR>(obsolete.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=228-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गड|गडः
गड m. (-डः)<BR>	 1. A kind of fish, the young of the Ophiocephaluslata,<BR>Ham.<BR>	 2. Another species, (Cyprinus garra. Ham.) see गल.<BR>	 3. An<BR>impediment, an obstacle.<BR>	 4. A screen, a covering, a fence.<BR>	 5. A<BR>moat, a ditch.<BR>	 6. A country, part of Malwa, Gerha or Gera Men-<BR>dela.<BR> E. गड्. to drop, affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=228-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गडक|गडकः
गडक m. (-कः) A kind of fish: see the last.<BR> E. गड्. to drop, affix क्वुन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=228-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गडयन्त|गडयंत|गडयंतः|गडयन्तः
गडयन्त m. (-न्तः) A cloud.<BR> E. गड् to drop (water), Uṇādi affix झच् and<BR>अय substituded for the penultimate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=228-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गडलवण|गडलवणं
गडलवण n. (-णं) Rock or fossile salt, especially that found in the dis-<BR>trict of Sambhar in the province of Ajmere.<BR> E. गड a country, and<BR>लवण salt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=228-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गडि|गडिः
गडि m. (-डिः)<BR>	 1. A steer.<BR>	 2. A lazy ox.<BR> E. गड् to drop, इन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=228-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गडु|गडुः
गडु mfn. (-डुः-डुः-डु) Crooked, humpbacked, &c.<BR>	 m. (-डुः)<BR>	 1. A hump<BR>on the back.<BR>	 2. Goitre or Bronchocele.<BR>	 3. A humpbacked man.<BR>	 4.<BR>A Javelin, a spear.<BR>	 5. An earth-worm. 6, A water pot.<BR> E. गड् to<BR>drop, Uṇādi affix उ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=228-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गडुक|गडुकः
गडुक n. (-कं)<BR>	 1. A water pot.<BR>	 2. A finger ring.<BR> E. कन् added to the<BR>last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=228-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गडुकण्ठ
गडुकण्ठ mfn. (-ण्ठः-ण्ठी-ण्ठं) Having a goitre.<BR> E. गडु, and कण्ठ the throat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=228-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गडुर|गडुरः
गडुर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Crooked, bent, humpbacked.<BR> E. गडु a hump, and<BR>र substituted for लः see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=228-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गडुल|गडुलः
गडुल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Crooked, humpbacked.<BR> E. गडु hump, and लच्<BR>affix; also गडुर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=228-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गडेर|गडेरः
गडेर m. (-रः) A cloud.<BR> E. गड् to drop (water), and एरक् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=228-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गडोत्थ|गडोत्थं
गडोत्थ n. (-त्थं) Fossile salt.<BR> E. गड the country, and उत्थ produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=228-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गडोल|गडोलः
गडोल m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. A mouthful.<BR>	 2. Raw sugar.<BR> E. गड् to drop, ओलच्<BR>Uṇādi affix; also गण्डोल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=228-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गड्डरिका
गड्डरिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. A sudden rush of water of which the source is<BR>unknown.<BR>	 2. A single ewe preceding a flock of sheep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=228-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गड्डुक|गड्डुकः
गड्डुक m. (-कः) A golden vase.<BR> E. गड् to sprinkle, डुक Uṇādi affix; also<BR>गड्डूक and occasionally कडूक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=228-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गड्डूक|गड्डूकः
गड्डूक m. (-कः) A golden water vessel: see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=228-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गण|गणः
गण r. 10th cl. (गणयति) To count, to reckon up by: number, to<BR>calculate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=228-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गण|गणः
गण m. (-णः)<BR>	 1. A flock, a multitude, a troop, a tribe or class, &c.<BR>	 2. A<BR>body of troops equal to three Gulmas or twenty-seven chariots<BR>and as many elephants, eighty-one horses, and 135 foot.<BR>	 3. Troops<BR>of inferior deities considered as ŚIVA'S attendants, and under the<BR>especial superintendance of GANESHA.<BR>	 4. A name of GANESHA.<BR>	 5. A<BR>number (in arithmetic.)<BR>	 6. A kind of perfume, commonly Chor.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=228-b" target="_blank">Page228-b+ 60</a>]<BR>7. A sect in philosophy or religion.<BR>	 8. A conjugation, a class or<BR>radicals.<BR>	 2. Series of asterisms which are classed under three heads<BR>human, infernal, and divine.<BR> E. गण् to count to reckon, affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=228-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गणक|गणकः
गणक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. An astrologer, a calculator of nativities. &c.<BR>	 2. An<BR>arithmetician.<BR>	 f. (-की) The wife of an astrologer.<BR> E. गण् to calcul-<BR>ate, affix क्वुन्, fem. affix ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=228-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गणकार|गणकारः
गणकार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A name of BHIMASENA.<BR>	 2. A classifier, one who<BR>arranges into classes.<BR> E. गण a troop, and कार who forms.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=228-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गणचक्रक|गणचक्रकं
गणचक्रक n. (-कं) A dinner in common by a party of virtuous men. E.<BR>गण a number, चक्र a wheel or circle, and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=228-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गणता
गणता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Classification.<BR>	 2. Multitude, assemblage.<BR>	 3. Following<BR>a part or fraction.<BR>	 4. Arithmetic.<BR> E. गण a class, तल् affix; also<BR>with त्व, गणत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=228-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गणदीक्षा
गणदीक्षा f. (-क्षा)<BR>	 1. Initiation of a particular kind in which GANESA<BR>is especially worshipped.<BR>	 2. Initiation of a number or class.<BR>	 3. Per-<BR>formance of religious rites for a number of persons.<BR> E. गण, and<BR>दीक्षा a religious rite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=228-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गणदीक्षिन्
गणदीक्षिन् m. (-क्षी)<BR>	 1. A priest who officiates for various castes and<BR>people.<BR>	 2. One who has been initiated into the worship of GANESHA.<BR>E. गण, दीक्षा a rite, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=228-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गणदेवता
गणदेवता f. (-ता) A deity of a class, as an Aditya a Vasu, a Rudra, &c.<BR>E. गण, and देवता a divinity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=228-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गणद्रव्य|गणद्रव्यं
गणद्रव्य n. (-व्यं)<BR>	 1. Public property, common stock.<BR>	 2. A variety of<BR>articles.<BR> E. गण a class, and द्रव्य thing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=228-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गणधर|गणधरः
गणधर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. The head of a class or number, the teacher of a<BR>school.<BR>	 2. A title of the first diciples of the Jaina Mahavira. E.<BR>गण a class, and धर who holds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=228-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गणन|गणनं
गणन nf. (-नं-ना)<BR>	 1. Counting, enumerating.<BR>	 2. Arithmetic.<BR> E. गण् to<BR>count, युच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=228-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गणनाथ|गणनाथः
गणनाथ m. (-थः) A name of GANESHA.<BR> E. गण, and नाथ lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=228-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गणनायक|गणनायकः
गणनायक m. (-कः) A name of GANESHA.<BR>	 f. (-यिका) A name of DURGĀ. E.<BR>गण, and नायक a leader; see गणेश.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=228-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गणनीय|गणनीयं
गणनीय mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>	 1. Numerable, to be counted or reckoned.<BR>	 2.<BR>To be classed.<BR> E. गण् to count, and अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=228-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गणपति|गणपतिः
गणपति m. (-तिः) GANESHA.<BR> E. गण् and पति lord: see गणेश.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=228-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गणपर्व्वत|गणपर्वत|गणपर्व्वतः
गणपर्व्वत m. (-तः) The fabulous mountain Kailasha.<BR> E. गण ŚIVA'S attend-<BR>ant demigods, and पर्व्वत a mountain; this mountain being the<BR>residence of the Kinnaras, Yakṣas, and other subordinate<BR>deities.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=228-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गणपीठक|गणपीठकं
गणपीठक n. (-कं) The breast or bosom.<BR> E. गण the aggregate, (of quali-<BR>ties,) and पीठक a seat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=228-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गणरात्र|गणरात्रं
गणरात्र n. (-त्रं) A multitude of nights.<BR> E. गण, and रात्र night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=228-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गणरूप|गणरूपः
गणरूप m. (-पः) Swallow wort, (Colotropis gigantea;) also अर्क.<BR> E. गण<BR>a number, and रूप form, multiform.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=228-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गणरूपिन्
गणरूपिन् m. (-पी) Swallow wort, the white sort: see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=228-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गणवतीसुत|गणवतीसुतः
गणवतीसुत m. (-तः) The name of a sage and physician, also called DHAN-<BR>WANTARI or KASIRAJA.<BR> E. गणवती a proper name, and सुत a son, the<BR>son of GANAVATI.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=228-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गणहासक|गणहासकः
गणहासक m. (-कः) Chor, a species of perfume,<BR> E. गण many, and हासक<BR>what causes to smile, what de-lights.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=228-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गणाग्रणी
गणाग्रणी m. (-णीः) A name of GANESHA.<BR> E. गण the troops of deities, and<BR>अग्रणी principal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=228-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गणाचल|गणाचलः
गणाचल m. (-लः) The mountain Kailasha.<BR> E. गण, and अचल a mountain,<BR>the residence of the GANAS or troops of demi-gods.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=228-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गणाधिप|गणाधिपः
गणाधिप m. (-पः)<BR>	 1. A name of GANESHA.<BR>	 2. A title of ŚIVA.<BR>	 3. The chief<BR>of a troop of soldiers, of a class of diciples, of a body of men or<BR>animals, &c.<BR> E. गण, and अधिप Master; also गणाधिपति, and other<BR>similar epithets: see गणेश.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=228-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गणान्न
गणान्न n. (-न्नं) A mess, food prepared for a number of Persons in com-<BR>mon.<BR> E. गण and अन्न food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=228-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गणाभ्यन्तर|गणाभ्यंतर|गणाभ्यन्तरः
गणाभ्यन्तर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) One of a troop or number.<BR>	 m. (-रः) A member<BR>of a religious convent or association.<BR> E. गण, and अभ्यन्तर included<BR>गणि f. (-णिः) Counting, enumerating<BR> E. गण् to count, इञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=229-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गणिका
गणिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. A courtezan, a harlot.<BR>	 2. A sort of Jasmin. (J.<BR>auriculatum.)<BR>	 3. A tree, commonly Ganiyari, (Premnaspinosa.)<BR>4. A female elephant.<BR>	 5. Counting, enumerating.<BR> E. गण to reckon,<BR>&c. ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=229-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गणिकारिका
गणिकारिका f. (-का) The name of a small tree with a very fetid leaf,<BR>commonly called Ganiyari, the wood of which is used in attrition,<BR>for the purpose of producing flame, (Premna spinosa.)<BR> E. कन् added<BR>to गणिकारी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=229-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गणिकारी
गणिकारी f. (-री) The name of a tree: see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=229-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गणित|गणितं
गणित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Numbered, counted, reckoned, calculated.<BR>	 n. (-तं)<BR>1. The science of computation, comprising arithmetic, algebra,<BR>and geometry, distinguished as पाटीगणितं, वीजगणितं and रेखागणितं.<BR>	 2.<BR>Calculating, numbering.<BR> E. गण to count, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=229-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गणितव्य
गणितव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>	 1. To be counted or numbered.<BR>	 2. To be cal-<BR>culated.<BR> E. गण and तव्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=229-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गणिपिटका
गणिपिटका f. (-का) A division of science peculiar to the Jainas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=229-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गणीभूत
गणीभूत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Included in any class or troop.<BR>	 2. Calculated.<BR>E. गण, and भूत become, with च्वि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=229-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गणेय|गणेयः
गणेय mfn. (-यः-यी-यं) Numberable, calculable, what may be reckoned<BR>or counted.<BR> E. गण to count, and यत् affix, form irr. see गण्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=229-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गणेरु|गणेरुः
गणेरु m. (-रुः) A plant, (Pterospermum acerifolium, &c.) see कर्णिकार.<BR>f. (-रुः)<BR>	 1. A harlot, a whore.<BR>	 2. A female elephant.<BR> E. गण a<BR>number, ईर्, to go, &c. affix उ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=229-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गणेरुका
गणेरुका f. (-का) A bawd, a procuress.<BR> E. कन् added to the pre-<BR>ceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=229-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गणेश|गणेशः
गणेश m. (-शः)<BR>	 1. A name of ŚIVA.<BR>	 2. GANESA, the son of ŚIVA and<BR>PARVATI; he is the deity of wisdom, and remover of obstacles,<BR>whence in the commencement of all undertakings, the opening<BR>of all compositions. &c. he receives the reverential homage of<BR>the Hindus. He is represented as a short fat man with the head<BR>of an elephant; and the present appellation, with other similar<BR>compounds, alludes to his office as chief of the various classes of<BR>subordinate gods, who are regarded as ŚIVA'S attendants.<BR> E. गण a<BR>troop or class (of deities attendant upon ŚIVA,) and ईश lord or<BR>master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=229-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गणेशकुसुम|गणेशकुसुमं
गणेशकुसुम m. (-मः) A shrub, Oleander with red flowers.<BR> E. गणेश and<BR>कुसुम a flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=229-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गणेशपूजा
गणेशपूजा f. (-जा) Worship of GANESA.<BR> E. गणेश and पूजा worship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=229-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गणेशभूषण|गणेशभूषणं
गणेशभूषण n. (-णं) Red lead.<BR> E. गणेश and भूषण ornament.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=229-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गणोत्साह|गणोत्साहः
गणोत्साह m. (-हः) A rhinoceros.<BR> E. गण a herd, and उत्साह toil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=229-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गण्ड|गंड|गंडः|गण्डः
गण्ड m. (-ण्डः)<BR>	 1. A cheek, the whole side of the face including the tem-<BR>ple.<BR>	 2. An elephant's temple or cheek.<BR>	 3. A boil, a pimple.<BR>	 4. A<BR>mark, a spot.<BR>	 5. A bubble.<BR>	 6. A knot.<BR>	 7. A rhinoceros: (see गण्डक)<BR>	 8.<BR>Part of a horse's trappings, a stud or button fixed as an orna-<BR>ment upon the harness.<BR>	 9. A hero.<BR>	 10. The abrupt interchange of<BR>question and answer, as one of the characteristics of the dramatic<BR>composition called Vithi.<BR>	 11. The tenth Yoga, or one of the<BR>twenty-seven portions of a circle on the plane of the ecliptic: see<BR>योग.<BR>	 12. An astronomical period.<BR> E. गडि to affect the cheek, अच्<BR>affix, or गम् to go, ड Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=229-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गण्डक|गंडक|गंडकः|गण्डकः
गण्डक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A rhinoceros.<BR>	 2. A mode of reckoning by fours.<BR>	 3. An<BR>obstacle or impediment.<BR>	 4. Separation, disjunction.<BR>	 5. Astrologi-<BR>cal science or a part of it.<BR>	 f. (-की) The name of a river in the north<BR>of India, the Gandaki.<BR>	 f. (-का) A lump, a ball.<BR> E. गडि to affect the<BR>cheek, &c ण्वुल् affix, fem. affix ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=229-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गण्डकारी
गण्डकारी f. (-री) A sensitive plant, (Mimosa pudica.)<BR> E. गण्ड a boil, and<BR>कारी what occasions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=229-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गण्डकाली
गण्डकाली f. (-ली) See the preceding.<BR> E. गण्ड a knot, and काली black;<BR>black with many joints and knots.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=229-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गण्डकुसुम|गंडकुसुम|गण्डकुसुमं
गण्डकुसुम n. (-मं) The juice that exudes from the elephant's temples in<BR>time of rut.<BR> E. गण्ड an elephant's temples, and कुसुम a flower,<BR>from its supposed fragrance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=229-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गण्डकूप|गंडकूप|गण्डकूपः
गण्डकूप m. (-पः) The peak or summit of a mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=229-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गण्डगात्र|गण्डगात्रं
गण्डगात्र n. (-त्रं) fruit, custard apple, (Annona squamosa)<BR> E. गण्ड a<BR>boil, and गात्र a body; the inside being compared to purulent<BR>pustules.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=229-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गण्डफलक|गंडफलक
गण्डफलक n. (-कं) The cheek.<BR> E. गण्ड and फलक a layer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=229-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गण्डमाला|गंडमाला
गण्डमाला f. (-ला) Inflammation of the glands of the neck, &c.<BR> E. गण्ड a<BR>boil. and माला a necklace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=229-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गण्डमालिन्
गण्डमालिन् mfn. (-ली-लिनी-लि) Having the glands of the neck inflamed.<BR>E. इनि added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=229-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गण्डशैल|गंडशैल|गण्डशैलः
गण्डशैल m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. A rock or rocky fragment fallen from a height thrown<BR>down by an earthquake, a storm, &c.<BR>	 2. The forehead.<BR> E. गण्ड a<BR>cheek, and शैल a rock, the cheek of the mountain, or in the second<BR>instance, vice-versa, the mountain as it were of the cheek or face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=229-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गण्डस्थल|गंडस्थल
गण्डस्थल nf. (-लः-ली) The cheek.<BR> E. गण्ड and स्थल place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=229-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गण्डाङ्ग|गंडांग|गण्डाङ्गः
गण्डाङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः) A rhinoceros.<BR> E. गण्ड a stud, and अङ्ग a body; from the<BR>studded appearance of his hide.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=229-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गण्डाली|गंडाली
गण्डाली f. (-ली) A bent grass with white blossoms, a white sort of<BR>Durva, (Agrostis linearis.)<BR> E. गण्ड a boil, अल् to be adequate to<BR>or fit for, affixes अण् and ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=229-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गण्डि|गंडि|गंडिः|गण्डिः
गण्डि m. (-ण्डिः)<BR>	 1. Goitre or Bronchocele.<BR>	 2. The trunk of a tree. E.<BR>गण्डि to affect the cheek, &c. Uṇādi affix इन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=229-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गण्डीर|गंडीर|गंडीरः|गण्डीरः
गण्डीर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A kind of potherb, described as growing in watery<BR>ground, and according to some, a species of cucumber.<BR>	 2. A hero,<BR>a champion.<BR>	 f. (-री) A milky plant, (Euphorbia.)<BR> E. गडि to affect<BR>a part. &c. इरन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=229-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गण्डु|गंडु|गंडुः|गण्डुः
गण्डु mf. (-ण्डुः) A pillow.<BR>	 f. (-ण्डूः) A knot or joint.<BR> E. गडि to sup-<BR>port the cheek, Uṇādi affix उ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=229-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गण्डूपद|गंडूपद|गण्डूपदः
गण्डूपद m. (-दः) An earth-worm.<BR>	 f. (-दी) A small or female worm.<BR>E. गण्डू a knot, and पद a foot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=229-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गण्डूपदभव|गंडूपदभव|गण्डूपदभवं
गण्डूपदभव m. (-वः) Lead.<BR> E. गण्डूपद a worm, and भव produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=229-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गण्डूष|गंडूष|गंडूषः|गण्डूषः
गण्डूष mf. (-षः-षा)<BR>	 1. A mouthful.<BR>	 2. A handful.<BR>	 3. A handful of water,<BR>&c. held in the hollowed palm of the hand for rincing the mouth,<BR>&c.<BR>	 4. Filling the mouth, rincing it, &c.<BR>	 5. The tip of an elephant's<BR>trunk.<BR> E. गड् to drop, ऊषण् Uṇādi affix and नुम् inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=229-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गण्डोल|गंडोल|गंडोलः|गण्डोलः
गण्डोल m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. Raw sugar.<BR>	 2. A mouthful.<BR> E. गड् to drop, or गडि<BR>to affect the cheek, ओलच् affix; also गडोल<BR> E. गण् to count, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=229-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गण्य|गण्यं
गण्य mfn. (-ण्यः-ण्या-ण्यं) To be counted or calculated.<BR> E. गण् to count, affix<BR>of the future participle यत्; also irregularly गणेय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=229-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गत|गतं
गत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Gone.<BR>	 2. Known, understood.<BR>	 3. Obtained,<BR>gained.<BR>	 4. Lost.<BR>	 n. (-तं)<BR>	 1. Going, motion.<BR>	 2. Any thing past or<BR>done, an event.<BR> E. गम् to go, in the participle past.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=229-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गतकाल
गतकाल n. (-लं) Time past.<BR> E. गत, and काल time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=229-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गतक्लम
गतक्लम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं) Rested, refreshed.<BR> E. गत and क्लम fatigue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=229-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गतचेतन
गतचेतन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Senseless, swooned.<BR> E. गत and चेतना conscious-<BR>ness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=229-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गतज्वर
गतज्वर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Well, recovered, free from fever or sickness. E.<BR>गत and ज्वर fever.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=229-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गततोयद
गततोयद mfn. (-दः-दा-दं) Cloudless, cleared up, fair.<BR> E. गत, and तोयद a<BR>cloud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=229-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गतप्रत्यागत
गतप्रत्यागत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Returned, come back again after having<BR>gone away.<BR> E. गत and प्रत्यागत come back.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=229-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गतदिन
गतदिन n. (-नं) Yesterday.<BR> E. गत and दिन day; also गतदिवसं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=229-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गतधृति
गतधृति mfn. (-तिः-तिः-ति) Agitated, discomposed, unsteady.<BR> E. गत and<BR>धृति firmness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=229-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गतनासिक|गतनासिकः
गतनासिक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Noseless.<BR> E. गत gone, lost, and नासिका the nose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=229-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गतमाय
गतमाय mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>	 1. Reformed, without deceit.<BR>	 2. Cruel without<BR>compassion.<BR> E. गत and माया deceit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=230-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गतलक्ष्मीक
गतलक्ष्मीक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Unfortunate, suffering losses; so गतश्रीक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=230-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गतबत्
गतबत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>	 1. Going, passing.<BR>	 2. Obtaining.<BR>	 3. Falling<BR>into.<BR>	 4. Feeling, entertaining.<BR> E. गम and क्तवतु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=230-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गतवित्त
गतवित्त mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं) Beggared, impoverished.<BR> E. गत and वित्त wealth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=230-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गतविभव
गतविभव mfn. (-वः-वा-वं) Poor, indigent.<BR> E. गत and विभव wealth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=230-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गतव्यथ
गतव्यथ mfn. (-थः-था-थं)<BR>	 1. Free from pain.<BR>	 2. Unanxious.<BR> E. गत and व्यथ<BR>pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=230-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गतशैशव
गतशैशव mfn. (-वः-वा-वं) Grown up, above eight years of age.<BR> E. गत and<BR>शैशव infancy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=230-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गतसङ्कल्प|गतसंकल्प
गतसङ्कल्प mfn. (-ल्पः-ल्पा-ल्पं) Bereft of sense, foolish.<BR> E. गत and सङ्कल्प<BR>purpose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=230-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गतसङ्ग
गतसङ्ग mfn. (-ङ्गः-ङ्गा-ङ्गं)<BR>	 1. Detached from, dissevered.<BR>	 2. Adverse or<BR>indifferent to.<BR> E. गत, and सङ्ग union.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=230-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गतसत्व
गतसत्व mfn. (-त्वः-त्वा-त्वं)<BR>	 1. Base.<BR>	 2. Lifeless, dead, &c.<BR> E. गत, and सत्व<BR>being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=230-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गतसन्नक|गतसन्नकः
गतसन्नक m. (-कः) An elephant out of rut.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=230-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गताक्ष
गताक्ष mfn. (-क्षः-क्षा-क्षं) Blind, sightless.<BR> E. गत gone, and अक्ष for अक्षि<BR>the eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=230-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गतागत|गतागतं
गतागत m. (-तं)<BR>	 1. The flight of a bird backward and forward.<BR>	 2. Going<BR>and coming, reiterated motion in general.<BR> E. गत going, आगत<BR>coming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=230-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गतानुगतिक
गतानुगतिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Following, imitative, doing as others do. E.<BR>गत, and अनुगतिक who goes after.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=230-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गतायुस्
गतायुस् mfn. (-युः-युः-युः)<BR>	 1. Very old, infirm, decrepid, decayed.<BR>	 2. Dead.<BR>E. गत, and आयुस् life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=230-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गतार्त्तवा|गतार्तवा
गतार्त्तवा f. (-वा)<BR>	 1. A woman past child-bearing.<BR>	 2. A barren woman. E.<BR>गत, and आर्त्तवा a woman menstruating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=230-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गतार्थ
गतार्थ mfn. (-र्थः-र्था-र्थं)<BR>	 1. Unmeaning, nonsensical.<BR>	 2. Poor.<BR>	 3. Void of<BR>an object.<BR> E. गत, and अर्थ sense, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=230-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गतासु
गतासु mfn. (-सुः-सुः-सु) Dead, expired.<BR> E. गत, and असु breath.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=230-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गति|गतिः
गति m. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Going, moving, motion in general.<BR>	 2. March, proces-<BR>sion.<BR>	 3. A road, a way, a path.<BR>	 4. A period of life, as age, youth,<BR>&c.<BR>	 5. An expedient, a means of success.<BR>	 6. Knowledge, wisdom.<BR>7. A sinus, a fistular sore.<BR>	 8. Worldly vanity or wickedness.<BR>	 9.<BR>Course of events, fate, fortune.<BR>	 10. Resource, refuge, asylum.<BR>	 11.<BR>The diurnal motion of a planet in its orbit, 12. State, mode of<BR>existence.<BR> E. गम् to go, affix क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=230-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गतिक|गतिकं
गतिक n. (-कं)<BR>	 1. Going, motion.<BR>	 2. Refuge, asylum.<BR>	 3. Course.<BR>	 4. Con-<BR>dition.<BR> E. कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=230-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गतिला
गतिला f. (-ला)<BR>	 1. A name of river, the Gatila.<BR>	 2. Mutual separation.<BR>E. गम् to go, इल Uṇādi affix, and त substituted for the radical<BR>final.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=230-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गत्वर|गत्वरः
गत्वर mfn. (-रः-री-रं) Going, moving, locomotive.<BR> E. गम् to go affix क्वरप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=230-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गत्वा
गत्वा ind. Having gone, gone to or attained, &c.<BR> E. गम् to go, क्त्वा aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=230-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गत्यून
गत्यून mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>	 1. Impassable, difficult of access.<BR>	 2. Desert.<BR>	 3.<BR>Helpless.<BR> E. गति and ऊन् defective.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=230-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गद|गदं|गदः
गद r. 10th cl. (गदति) To speak articulately.<BR>	 2. To be sick. r. 10th cl.<BR>(गदयति) To thunder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=230-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गद|गदं|गदः
गद m. (-दः)<BR>	 1. Disease, sickness.<BR>	 2. Speech, speaking.<BR>	 3. GADA the<BR>younger brother of KṚṢṆA.<BR>	 f. (-दा)<BR>	 1. A mace, a club.<BR>	 2. Trum-<BR>pet flower, (Bigonia suave-olens.)<BR> E. गद् to speak, &c. अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=230-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गदयित्नु|गदयित्नुः
गदयित्नु mfn. (-त्नुः-त्नुः-त्नु)<BR>	 1. Loquacious, talkative, talking much or idly.<BR>2. Libidinous, lustful, desirous.<BR>	 m. (-त्नुः) A name of KANDARPA,<BR>the deity of love.<BR> E. गद् to speak, Uṇādi affix इत्नुच्, and अय in-<BR>serted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=230-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गदाख्य|गदाख्यं
गदाख्य n. (-ख्यं) A kind of Costus, (C. speciosus:) see कुष्ठ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=230-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गदागद
गदागद m. (always dual -दौ) The two physicians of Svarga, the sons of<BR>AŚVINĪ by SŪRYA.<BR> E. गद disease in general, and अगद health.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=230-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गदाग्रज|गदाग्रजः
गदाग्रज m. (-जः) A name of VIṢṆU or KṚṢṆA<BR> E. गद, and अग्रज an<BR>elder brother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=230-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गदाधर|गदाधरः
गदाधर m. (-रः) A name of KṚṢṆA.<BR> E. गदा E. club, and धर who holds;<BR>KṚṢṆA or VIṢṆU is represented holding a mace in one of his<BR>hands.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=230-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गदाभृत्
गदाभृत् m. (-भृत्)<BR>	 1. A name of KṚṢṆA.<BR>	 2. A mace or club bearer.<BR>	 3.<BR>One who fights with a mace.<BR> E. गदा a club, and भृत् who nourishes.<BR>see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=230-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गदाम्बर|गदांबर|गदाम्बरः
गदाम्बर m. (-रः) A cloud.<BR> E. गद sound, अम्बर the sky.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=230-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गदाराति|गदारातिः
गदाराति m. (-तिः) A drug, a medicament.<BR> E. गद and अराति an enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=230-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गदाह्व|गदाह्वं
गदाह्व n. (-ह्वं) A kind of grass, (Costus speciosus:) see कुष्ठ.<BR> E. गद disease,<BR>and आह्वा a name; named by many of the same terms as disease:<BR>see व्याधि, &c. also गदाख्य, गदाह्वय, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=230-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गदित|गदितः
गदित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Spoken, said.<BR> E. गद् to speak, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=230-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गदितवत्
गदितवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Saying, speaking, having spoken.<BR> E. गद, and<BR>क्तवतु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=230-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गदिन्
गदिन् m. (-दी)<BR>	 1. A name of VIṢṆU.<BR>	 2. A mace bearer.<BR>	 3. One armed<BR>with a club.<BR>	 4. A sick man.<BR> E. गदा a mace, and इनि poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=230-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गद्गद्
गद्गद् m. (-दः) Indistinct or convulsive utterance, as sobbing, &c.<BR> E. गद्<BR>to speak, क्विप् affix, root repeated with अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=230-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गद्गदध्वनि|गद्गदध्वनिः
गद्गदध्वनि m. (-निः) low inarticulate expression of joy or grief.<BR> E. गद्गद<BR>inarticulate utterance. and ध्वनि sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=230-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गद्गदपद
गद्गदपद n. (-दं) Inarticulate speech.<BR> E. गद्गद and पद a word.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=230-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गद्गदवाच्
गद्गदवाच् f. (-वाक्) Inarticulate or convulsive speech, interrupted by sob-<BR>bing, &c.<BR> E. गद्गद, and वाच् speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=230-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गद्य|गद्यं
गद्य mfn. (-द्यः-द्या-द्यं) To be spoken or uttered.<BR>	 n. (-द्यं) Prose<BR> E. गद् to<BR>speak, affix यत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=230-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गद्यानक|गद्यानकं|गद्यानकः
गद्यानक n. (-कं) A weight either of sixty-four or forty-eight Rattis;<BR>also read गद्यालक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=230-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्तव्य|गंतव्य
गन्तव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं) To be gone, to be gone to or attained.<BR> E. गम,<BR>and तव्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=230-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्तु|गंतुः|गन्तुः
गन्तु m. (-न्तुः) A traveller, a way-farer.<BR> E. गम् to go, Uṇādi affix तुन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=230-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्तृ|गंतृ
गन्तृ mfn. (-न्ता-न्त्री-न्तृ) Who or what goes or moves.<BR> E. गम् to go, तृच्<BR>aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=230-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्त्री|गंत्री
गन्त्री f. (-न्त्री) A cart or car drawn by oxen.<BR> E. गम् to go, इन् affix, fem.<BR>affix ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=230-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्त्रीरथ|गंत्रीरथ|गन्त्रीरथः
गन्त्रीरथ m. (-थः) A cart.<BR> E. गन्त्री a carriage drawn by oxen, and रथ a<BR>vehicle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=230-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्ध|गंध|गन्धं|गंधः|गन्धः
गन्ध r. 10th cl. (गन्धयते)<BR>	 1. To injure, to hurt or kill.<BR>	 2. To move, to go.<BR>3. To ask or beg.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=230-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्ध|गंध|गन्धं|गंधः|गन्धः
गन्ध m. (-न्धः)<BR>	 1. Smell, odour.<BR>	 2. A perfume, a fragrance or fragrant<BR>substance.<BR>	 3. A diffusive fragrance.<BR>	 4. Sulphur.<BR>	 5. Connexion,<BR>relationship.<BR>	 6. A neighbour.<BR>	 7. A plant, (Morunga hyperanthera,<BR>&c.)<BR>	 8. Pride, arrogance.<BR>	 9. Small, diminutive, a little, a small<BR>quantity, &c.<BR>	 10. Pounded Sandal.<BR>	 f. (-न्धा) The bud of the Cham-<BR>paca flower, (Michelia Champaca.)<BR>	 n. (-न्धं) Aloe-wood.<BR> E. गन्ध् to<BR>hurt, to move, &c. affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=230-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धक|गंधक|गंधकः|गन्धकः
गन्धक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. Sulphur.<BR>	 2. The morunga tree, (M. hyperanthera,<BR>&c.) see शोभाञ्जन.<BR> E. कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=230-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धकारिका|गंधकारिका
गन्धकारिका f. (-का) A female artisan, living in the house of another<BR>woman.<BR> E. गन्ध perfume, and कारिका who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=230-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धकालिका|गंधकालिका
गन्धकालिका f. (-का) The mother ef VYASA.<BR> E. कन् added to the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=230-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धकाली|गंधकाली
गन्धकाली f. (-ली) The mother of the poet VYASA.<BR> E. गन्ध perfume, कल् to<BR>make, affixes अण् and ङीष् having a strong scent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=230-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धकाष्ठ|गंधकाष्ठ|गन्धकाष्ठं
गन्धकाष्ठ n. (-ष्ठं) A fragrant wood, as Sandal, aloewood, &c.<BR> E. गन्ध<BR>smell, and काष्ठ timber.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=230-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धकुटी|गंधकुटी
गन्धकुटी f. (-टी) A kind of perfume, commonly Mura.<BR> E. गन्ध smell, &c.<BR>कुटी abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=230-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धखेड|गन्धखेडं
गन्धखेड n. (-डं) A fragrant grass.<BR> E. गन्ध, and खेड grass; also with कन्<BR>added गन्धखेडकं: see गन्धतृण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=230-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धगज|गंधगज|गन्धगजः
गन्धगज m. (-जः) An elephant of the best kind.<BR> E. गन्ध odour, गज an<BR>elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=231-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धगुण|गंधगुण
गन्धगुण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Having the property of odour.<BR> E. गन्ध, and गुण<BR>quality.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=231-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धघ्राण|गंधघ्राण
गन्धघ्राण n. (-णं) Smelling any odour.<BR> E. गन्ध, and घ्राणं smelling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=231-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धचेलिका|गंधचेलिका
गन्धचेलिका f. (-का) Musk.<BR> E. गन्ध fragrance, चेलि clothes, affix कन्; being<BR>used for scenting clothes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=231-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धजात|गन्धजातं
गन्धजात n. (-तं) The leaf of the Laurus cassia.<BR> E. गन्ध smell, जात produc-<BR>ed; fragrant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=231-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धज्ञा|गंधज्ञा
गन्धज्ञा f. (-ज्ञा) The nose.<BR> E. गन्ध scent, and ज्ञा who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=231-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धतूर्य्य|गन्धतूर्य|गंधतूर्य|गन्धतूर्य्यं
गन्धतूर्य्य n. (-र्य्यं) A musical instrument, one of a loud sound used in<BR>battle: (a drum or trumpet.)<BR> E. गन्ध pride, and तूर्य्य a musical ins-<BR>trument.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=231-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धतृण|गन्धतृणं
गन्धतृण n. (-णं) A fragrant grass, (Andropogon schœnanthus.)<BR> E. गन्ध,<BR>and तृण grass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=231-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धत्वच्
गन्धत्वच् f. (-त्वक्) A sort of perfume, commonly Elabaluka.<BR> E. गन्ध and<BR>त्वच् skin, rind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=231-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धद्विप|गंधद्विप|गन्धद्विपः
गन्धद्विप m. (-पः) An elephant of the best class, supposed to emit a par-<BR>ticular smell at all times.<BR> E. गन्ध, and द्विप an elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=231-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धधूलि|गंधधूलि|गन्धधूलिः
गन्धधूलि f. (-लिः) Musk, the fragrant secretion of the musk-deer.<BR> E. गन्ध<BR>fragrant, and धूलि dust.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=231-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धन|गंधन|गंधनं|गन्धनं
गन्धन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Continued effort, perseverance.<BR>	 2. Injury, hurting, kill-<BR>ing.<BR>	 3. Intimation, information.<BR>	 4. Manifestation.<BR> E. गन्ध् to hurt,<BR>to move, &c. affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=231-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धनकुल|गंधनकुल|गन्धनकुलः
गन्धनकुल m. (-लः) The musk-rat of Bengal. (Sorex moschata.)<BR> E. गन्ध<BR>scented, and नकुल an ichneumon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=231-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धनाकुली
गन्धनाकुली f. (-ली) A plant, possibly the serpent Ophioxylon: see राम्ना,<BR>E. गन्ध smelling, and नाकुली the same plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=231-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धनामन्
गन्धनामन् m. (-मा) A fragrant kind of basil.<BR> E. गन्ध fragrance, and नामन्<BR>a name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=231-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धनाली|गंधनाली
गन्धनाली f. (-ली) The nose.<BR> E. गन्ध scent, and नाली tubular canal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=231-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धनिलया|गंधनिलया
गन्धनिलया f. (-या) Double jasmine, (J. Zambac floribus multiplicatis.) E.<BR>गन्ध smell, and निलय a house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=231-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धपत्र|गन्धपत्रः
गन्धपत्र m. (-त्रः) A white sort of basil, (Ocymum gratissimum:) see<BR>श्वेतपर्णास.<BR>	 f. (-त्री)<BR>	 1. A sort of zedoary. (-त्रा) Ajwaen, (Ligusticam<BR>ajwaen.)<BR>	 2. Another plant, (Physalis flexuosa.)<BR> E. गन्ध, and पत्र a<BR>leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=231-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धपलाशिका|गंधपलाशिका
गन्धपलाशिका f. (-का) Turmeric.<BR> E. गन्ध smell, पलाश a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=231-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धपलाशी|गंधपलाशी
गन्धपलाशी f. (-शी) Zedoary, (Curcuma zerumbet.)<BR> E. गन्ध and पलाश a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=231-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धपाषाण|गंधपाषाण|गन्धपाषाणः
गन्धपाषाण m. (-णः) Sulphur.<BR> E. गन्ध smelling, and पाषाण a stone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=231-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धपिशाचिका|गंधपिशाचिका
गन्धपिशाचिका f. (-का) The smell of incense, diffusive incense.<BR> E. गन्ध smell<BR>पिशाचिका female demon; imp-like, from its dark colour or cloudy<BR>nature; or attracting demons by its fragrance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=231-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धपीता
गन्धपीता f. (-ता) A species of zedoary.<BR> E. गन्ध and पीत yellow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=231-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धपुष्प|गंधपुष्प|गन्धपुष्पः
गन्धपुष्प m. (-ष्पः)<BR>	 1. A kind of cane, (Calamus rotang.)<BR>	 2. Another plant,<BR>(Alangium hexapetalum:) see अङ्कोट.<BR>	 3. Sebesten. (Cordia myxa.)<BR>f. (-ष्पा)<BR>	 1. The indigo plant.<BR>	 2. Ganiyari, (Premna spinosa, &c.) see<BR>गणिकारी.<BR>	 n. (-ष्पं) Flowers and Sandal presented together at seasons<BR>of worship.<BR> E. गन्ध smell, and पुष्प flower; having odoriferous flowers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=231-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धफल|गन्धफलः
गन्धफल m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. Elephant or wood apple: see कपित्थ.<BR>	 2. The Bel,<BR>(Ægle cratæva.)<BR>	 f. (-ला or -ली)<BR>	 1. A plant bearing a fragrant seed.<BR>see प्रियङ्गु 2. The gum olibanum tree.<BR>	 f. (-ली) The blossom of the<BR>champaca: see चम्पक.<BR> E. गन्ध smell, and फल a fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=231-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धबन्धु|गंधबंधु|गन्धबन्धुः
गन्धबन्धु m. (-न्धुः) The mango tree.<BR> E. गन्ध a smell, and बन्धु a friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=231-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धभद्रा
गन्धभद्रा f. (-द्रा) A creeper commonly Gandhabhadali or Ghandali, (Pœ-<BR>deria fetida)<BR> E. गन्ध smell, and भद्र auspicious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=231-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धभाण्ड|गन्धभाण्डः
गन्धभाण्ड m. (-ण्डः) A tree, (Hibiscus populneoides:) see गर्द्धभाण्ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=231-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धमांसी
गन्धमांसी f. (-सी) A kind of Indian spikenard: see जटामांसी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=231-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धमातृ|गंधमातृ
गन्धमातृ f. (-ता) The earth.<BR> E. गन्ध scent, and मातृ the mother; the pro-<BR>perty of fragrance. residing in the earth or earthy atoms.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=231-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धमादन|गंधमादन|गन्धमादनं|गन्धमादनः
गन्धमादन mn. (-नः-नं) The name of a particular mountain, forming the<BR>division between Ilavritta and Bhadraswa or to the east of Mern.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. A large black bee.<BR>	 2. Sulphur.<BR>	 3. The name of one of<BR>the monkey chiefs.<BR>	 f. (-नी) Spirituous liquor; also in some books<BR>read गन्धमादिनी.<BR> E. गन्ध smell, मद् to inebriate in the causal form and<BR>ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=231-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धमादिन्
गन्धमादिन् mfn. (-दी-दिनी-दि) Strong scented, of intoxicating odour.<BR>	 f.<BR>(-नी)<BR>	 1. Lac, 2. A sort of perfume.<BR>	 3. Wine or spirituous liquor. E.<BR>गन्ध and मादिन् what intoxicates.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=231-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धमार्जार|गंधमार्जार|गन्धमार्जारः|गन्धमार्ज्जार|गन्धमार्ज्जारः
गन्धमार्जार m. (-रः) The civet-cat.<BR> E. गन्ध smell, and मार्जार a cat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=231-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धमालिनी
गन्धमालिनी f. (-नी) Mura, a perfume so called.<BR> E. गन्ध smell, माला a neck-<BR>lace, affixes इनि and ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=231-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धमुण्ड|गन्धमुण्डः
गन्धमुण्ड m. (-ण्डः) A creeper, (Hibiscus populneoides;) also गन्धभाण्ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=231-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धमूल|गन्धमूलः
गन्धमूल m. (-लः) A plant with a fragrant and tuberous root, one of the<BR>Scitaminea, (Alpinia galanga:) see कुलञ्जन.<BR>	 f. (-ला or -ली)<BR>	 1. A species<BR>of Cucumber, (C. reclinata, Rox.)<BR>	 2. The olibanum tree.<BR> E. गन्ध<BR>smell and मूल a root, fem. affix टाप् or ङीष् also with कन् affix<BR>गन्धमूलक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=231-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धमूलक|गन्धमूलकः
गन्धमूलक m. (-कः) A sort of Cucumber also गन्धमूली; see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=231-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धमूषिक|गंधमूषिक|गन्धमूषिकः
गन्धमूषिक mf. (-कः-का) The musk-rat or shrew, (Sorex moschata;) also<BR>in the fem. गन्धमूषी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=231-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धमृग|गंधमृग|गन्धमृगः
गन्धमृग m. (-गः) The civet-cat.<BR> E. गन्ध smell, and मृग a deer; the name<BR>also may be applied to the musk-deer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=231-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धमोदन|गंधमोदन|गन्धमोदनः
गन्धमोदन n. (-नं) Sulphur,<BR> E. गन्ध, and मोदन pleasing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=231-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धमैथुन|गंधमैथुन|गन्धमैथुनः
गन्धमैथुन m. (-नः) A bull.<BR> E. गन्ध smell, and मैथुन copulation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=231-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धमोहिनी|गंधमोहिनी
गन्धमोहिनी f. (-नी) The champaca flower.<BR> E. गन्ध smell, and मोहिनी de-<BR>lighting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=231-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धरस|गन्धरसः
गन्धरस m. (-सः) Myrrh.<BR> E. गन्ध smell, and रस essence; also रसगन्ध.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=231-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धराज|गंधराज|गन्धराजं|गन्धराजः
गन्धराज n. (-जं)<BR>	 1. Sandal.<BR>	 2. Any sweet smelling flower.<BR>	 f. (-जी)<BR>	 1. A<BR>sort of perfume, commonly, Nakhi: see नखी.<BR> E. गन्ध smell, and<BR>राज what excels, from राज् to shine, affix अच्; fem. affix ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=231-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धर्ब्ब
गन्धर्ब्ब m. (-र्ब्बः)<BR>	 1. A Gandharba or celestial musician; these demigods<BR>inhabit INDRA'S heaven, and form the orchestra at all the banquets<BR>of the principal deities.<BR>	 2. A horse.<BR>	 3. A kind of deer; according<BR>to some authorities, the musk-deer.<BR>	 4. The soul after death, and<BR>previous to its being born again, corresponding, in some respects,<BR>to the western notion of ghosts.<BR>	 5. A singer in general.<BR>	 6. The<BR>Kokila or black cuckoo.<BR>	 7. The sun.<BR>	 8. A sage, a pious man.<BR> E. गन्ध<BR>smell, injury, &c. अर्ब्ब to go, affix अच् the अ final of गन्ध is reject-<BR>ed; the root is also sometimes written with the dental letter अर्व्व,<BR>when the compound will be गन्धर्व्व; the best authorities however<BR>write it with the final labial letter ब as above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=231-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धर्ब्बविद्या
गन्धर्ब्बविद्या f. (-द्या) Music, dancing, &c.<BR> E. गन्धर्ब्ब, and विद्या science.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=231-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धर्ब्बविवाह
गन्धर्ब्बविवाह m. (-हः) Marriage by mutual consent, without any ceremo-<BR>nies, allowable between persons of the second class.<BR> E. गन्धर्ब्ब and<BR>विवाह marriage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=231-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धर्ब्बवेद
गन्धर्ब्बवेद m. (-दः) The science of music considered as a branch of the<BR>Sama Veda.<BR> E. गन्धर्ब्ब and वेद a Veda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=231-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धर्ब्बहस्त
गन्धर्ब्बहस्त m. (-स्तः) The castor-oil tree, (Palma christi or Ricinus com-<BR>munis.)<BR> E. गन्धर्ब्ब a deer, and हस्त hand or food; the leaves being<BR>compared to the foot of the deer: also with कन् added गन्धर्ब्बहस्तक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=231-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धलोलुपा|गंधलोलुपा
गन्धलोलुपा f. (-पा) A fly or gnat.<BR> E. गन्ध smell, &c. लोलुप unsteady.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=231-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धवणिज्
गन्धवणिज् m. (-णिक्) A perfumer, a dealer in perfumes.<BR> E. गन्ध and वणिज्<BR>a dealer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=231-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धवत्|गंधवत्|गन्धवन्त्
गन्धवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Scented, smelling, odoriferous.<BR>	 f. (-ती)<BR>	 1.<BR>The earth.<BR>	 2. The name of a city.<BR>	 4. Wine or vinous liquor.<BR>	 4. A<BR>kind of perfume: see मुरा.<BR>	 5. The mother of VYASA.<BR>	 6. A wild<BR>species of Ajwaen: see the यमानी.<BR> E. गन्ध smell, मतुप् poss. affix fem.<BR>aff. ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=231-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धवल्कल|गन्धवल्कलं
गन्धवल्कल n. (-लं)<BR>	 1. Cassia bark.<BR>	 2. Sarsaparilla.<BR> E. गन्ध, and वल्कल bark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=231-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धवल्लरी
गन्धवल्लरी f. (-री) A plant, also सहदेवी<BR> E. गन्ध smell, and वल्लर a pedicle,<BR>or with वल्ली the same, गन्धवल्ली.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=232-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धवह|गंधवह|गन्धवहः
गन्धवह mfn. (-हः-हा-हं) Smelling, fragrant, &c.<BR>	 m. (-हः) The wind.<BR>	 f.<BR>(-हा) The nose.<BR> E. गन्ध smell, and वह what conveys, from वह् to bear<BR>&c., and अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=232-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धवाह|गंधवाह|गन्धवाहः
गन्धवाह m. (-हः)<BR>	 1. The wind.<BR>	 2. A deer, the musk-deer.<BR>	 f. (-हा) The<BR>nose.<BR> E. गन्ध smell, वह् to convey, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=232-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धविह्वल|गंधविह्वल|गन्धविह्वलः
गन्धविह्वल m. (-लः) Wheat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=232-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धवृक्ष|गंधवृक्ष|गन्धवृक्षः
गन्धवृक्ष n. (-क्षः) The Sal tree, (Shorea robusta.)<BR> E. गन्ध, perfume, and बृक्ष<BR>a tree, yielding a fragrant resin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=232-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धव्याकुल|गंधव्याकुल|गन्धव्याकुलं
गन्धव्याकुल n. (-लं) A perfume, a fragrant berry: see कक्कोल<BR> E. गन्ध smell<BR>and व्याकुल disturbed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=232-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धशटी
गन्धशटी f. (-टी) A sort of Cucumber: see शटी.<BR> E. गन्ध smell, and शटी the<BR>same plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=232-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धशालि|गन्धशालिः
गन्धशालि m. (-लिः) A sweet smelling kind of rice.<BR> E. गन्ध, and शालि rice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=232-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धशुण्डिनी|गंधशुंडिनी
गन्धशुण्डिनी f. (-नी) The musk-rat or shrew.<BR> E. गन्ध and शुण्डिनी a rat; also<BR>गन्धाशुण्डिनी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=232-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धशेखर|गंधशेखर|गन्धशेखरः
गन्धशेखर m. (-रः) Musk.<BR> E. गन्ध, and शेखर chief, a principal perfume.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=232-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धसार|गंधसार|गन्धसारः
गन्धसार m. (-रः) Sandal.<BR> E. गन्ध and सार essence, the essence of perfume.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=232-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धसूयी
गन्धसूयी f. (-यी) The musk shrew or small musk-rat.<BR> E. गन्ध smell, and<BR>सू to produce, affixes युक् and ङीप्; also sometimes read गन्धसुखी,<BR>from गन्ध and सुख pleasure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=232-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धसोम|गंधसोम|गन्धसोमं
गन्धसोम n. (-मं) The white esculent water lily.<BR> E. गन्ध smell, and सोम the<BR>moon; opening its petals at night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=232-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धहारिका|गंधहारिका
गन्धहारिका f. (-का) A female artisan working in another person's<BR>house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=232-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धाखु|गंधाखु|गन्धाखुः
गन्धाखु m. (-खुः) A musk-rat.<BR> E. गन्ध smell, and आखु a rat: see गन्धसूयी, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=232-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धाजीव|गंधाजीव|गन्धाजीवः
गन्धाजीव m. (-वः) A vender of perfumes.<BR> E. गन्ध, and आजीव who gets a<BR>livelihood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=232-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धाढ्य|गंधाढ्य|गन्धाढ्यं|गन्धाढ्यः
गन्धाढ्य m. (-ढ्यः) The orange tree.<BR>	 f. (-ढ्या) A plant: see गन्धाली.<BR> E. गन्ध, and<BR>आढ्य wealth, rich in odour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=232-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धापकर्षण|गंधापकर्षण
गन्धापकर्षण n. (-णं) Removing any smell.<BR> E. गन्ध, and अपकर्षण taking away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=232-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धाला
गन्धाला f. (-ला) A plant, commonly Jati or Chameli, (Celtis orientalis.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=232-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धाली|गंधाली
गन्धाली f. (-ली)<BR>	 1. Gandhali or Gandhavaduliya, a plant, (Pæderia fetida.)<BR>2. A wasp: see गन्धोली.<BR> E. गन्ध smell, and आली a line, a quantity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=232-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धाश्मन्|गंधाश्मन्
गन्धाश्मन् m. (-श्मा) Sulphur.<BR> E. गन्ध smell, and अश्मन् a stone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=232-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धाष्टक|गंधाष्टक|गन्धाष्टकं
गन्धाष्टक n. (-कं) A class of eight fragrant articles used in worship, &c.<BR>as a sandal, agallochum, camphor, saffron, valerian, and some fra-<BR>grant grasses.<BR> E. गन्ध, and अष्टक eight collectively.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=232-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धिक|गंधिक|गन्धिकः
गन्धिक m. (-कः) Sulphur.<BR> E. गन्ध smell, and ठक् affix; also गन्धक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=232-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धिन्|गंधिन्
गन्धिन् mfn. (-न्धी-न्धिनी-न्धि) Smelling, odoriferous.<BR>	 m. (-न्धि)<BR>	 1. A bug; also<BR>the flying bug.<BR>	 2. A tree, (Xanthophyllum virens.)<BR>	 f. (-नी) A kind<BR>of perfume: see Mura,<BR> E. गन्ध smelling, इनि poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=232-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धोतु|गन्धोतुः
गन्धोतु m. (-तुः) The civet-cat.<BR> E. गन्ध smell, and ओतु a cat; also गन्धौतु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=232-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धोत्तमा|गंधोत्तमा
गन्धोत्तमा f. (-मा) Spirituous or vinous liquor.<BR> E. गन्ध odour, and उत्तम<BR>excellent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=232-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धोपजोविन्
गन्धोपजोविन् m. (-वी) A perfumer.<BR> E. गन्ध, and उपजीविन् who lives by.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=232-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धोलि|गन्धोलिः
गन्धोलि f. (-लिः or -ली) A kind of cucumber, (C. reclinata, Rox.) (-ली)<BR>1. A wasp.<BR>	 2. A fragrant grass, (Cyperus rotundus.)<BR> E. गन्ध to smell<BR>or injure<BR> E. ओलच affix, इन् or ङीष् fem. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=232-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गभस्ति|गभस्तिः
गभस्ति mf. (-स्तिः) A ray light, a sun or moon-beam.<BR>	 m. (-स्तिः) The sun.<BR>f. (-स्तिः) A name of SWAHA the wife of AGNI.<BR> E. ग for गो the<BR>heaven, भस् to shine, and क्तिच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=232-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गभस्तिमत्|गभस्तिमन्त्
गभस्तिमत् m. (-मान्) The sun.<BR>	 n. (-मत्) One of the seven divisions of<BR>Pātāla or regions below the earth.<BR> E. गभस्ति a ray of light, and मतुप्<BR>poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=232-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गभस्तिहस्त|गभस्तिहस्तः
गभस्तिहस्त m. (-स्तः) The sun.<BR> E. गभस्ति a ray, and हस्त a hand; yielding<BR>the sun-beams.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=232-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गभीर|गभीरं
गभीर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>	 1. Deep.<BR>	 2. Thick, impervious, (as a forest.)<BR>	 3.<BR>Profound, sagacious.<BR>	 4. Deep in sound, hollow-toned.<BR> E. गम् to go<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=232-b" target="_blank">Page232-b+ 60</a>]<BR>भ substituted for the final, इरन् Uṇādi affix; also with नुम् inser-<BR>ted गम्भीर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=232-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गभीरध्वनि
गभीरध्वनि m. (-निः)<BR>	 1. Deep sound.<BR>	 2. A low note or tone<BR> E. गभीर and<BR>ध्वनि sound; also गभीरनाद गभीरशब्द &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=232-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गभीरिका
गभीरिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. A large drum.<BR>	 2. A gong.<BR> E. गभीर deep, (as sound.)<BR>कन् affix, and the fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=232-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गभीलिक
गभीलिक m. (-कः) A small round pillow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=232-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गम|गमः
गम (औ, ऌ) औगमॢ r. 1st. cl. (गच्छति)<BR>	 1. To go, to move or approach.<BR>2. To arrive at, to accomplish or attain. With अनु prefixed, To<BR>follow, to imitate, With आङ् (आगच्छति) 1. To come, to arrive.<BR>	 2.<BR>To go to entertain.<BR>	 3. (आगमयते) To wait, to delay. With अधि, 1. To<BR>obtain, to gain or acquire.<BR>	 2. To go over, as a book or set of rules<BR>to peruse, to learn.<BR>	 3. To pass over, to omit. With अप, To go back<BR>or away, to separate. With अव, To know, to understand. With उत्,<BR>1. To approach, to go near to.<BR>	 2. To go up, to rise. With उप, 1.<BR>To produce.<BR>	 2. To go near.<BR>	 3. To consent to. With उप and आङ्,<BR>To approach. With दुर्, To go with difficulty. With नि, To acquire<BR>knowledge. With निर्, To go forth or out. With परि and उत्, To<BR>rise, as from a seat, &c. With परि, 1. To surround.<BR>	 2. To go away.<BR>With प्रति and आङ्, To return to arrive at. With वि, To go against<BR>as an enemy. With सम्, (संगच्छते) 1. To go with, to accompany.<BR>	 2.<BR>To meet, to encounter, (संगच्छति) To go to, (in a transitive sense.)<BR>With सम् and आङ्, To meet, to unite. With सम् and उप, To sub-<BR>mit to, to yield. With सु, 1. To go easily or well.<BR>	 2. To arrive at.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=232-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गम|गमः
गम m. (-मः)<BR>	 1. Going, moving.<BR>	 2. March, especially the march of an<BR>assailant.<BR>	 3. A road.<BR>	 4. A game played with dice and men, as<BR>backgammon, &c.<BR>	 5. Acting inconsiderately, looking at any thing<BR>hastily and superficially.<BR>	 6. Reading lightly, hasty or careless<BR>perusal, running over a book, &c.<BR> E. गम् to go, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=232-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गमकारित्व|गमकारित्वं
गमकारित्व n. (-त्वं) Rashness, inconsiderateness.<BR> E. गम् as above, कारिन्<BR>who does or acts, and त्व abstract aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=232-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गमथ|गमथः
गमथ m. (-थः)<BR>	 1. A road.<BR>	 2. A traveller.<BR> E. गम् to go, अथ Uṇādi<BR>aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=232-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गमन|गमनं
गमन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Going in general, 2. March in general, or the march of<BR>an assailant.<BR>	 3. Cohabitation.<BR>	 4. Obtaining, attaining.<BR> E. गम् to<BR>go or move, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=232-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गमनार्ह
गमनार्ह mfn. (-र्हः-र्हा-र्हं) To be sought, fit, suitable, desirable.<BR> E. गमन<BR>and अर्ह worthy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=232-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गमनीय
गमनीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>	 1. What may be gone to or reached, attainable,<BR>accessible.<BR>	 2. What ought to be followed, to be practised or ob-<BR>served.<BR> E. गम् and अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=232-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गमयत्
गमयत् mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्) Causing or making to go.<BR> E. गम् to go, causal<BR>form, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=232-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गमागम|गमागमः
गमागम m. (-मः) Going and coming.<BR> E. गम, and आगम going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=232-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गमित
गमित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Caused to go, sent, brought, reduced, driven to<BR>&c.<BR> E. गम् to go, causal form, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=232-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गमिन्
गमिन् m. (-मी) A passenger.<BR> E. गम् to go, इनि Uṇādi affix, otherwise<BR>with णिनि. affix, गामिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=232-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गम्ब
गम्ब r. 1st cl. (गम्बति) To go or move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=232-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गम्भारी|गंभारी
गम्भारी f. (-री) The name of tree, commonly called by the same name<BR>Gambhari, (Gmelina arborea.)<BR> E. क water, भृ to nourish, affixes<BR>अण् and ङीष् क is changed to ग and into the second case.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=232-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गम्भीर|गंभीर|गम्भीरं|गम्भीरः
गम्भीर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>	 1. Deep, (as water, but applied metaphorically<BR>to sound, intellect, &c. as in English.)<BR>	 2. Dull, slow.<BR>	 m. (-रः) A<BR>Mantra or magical incantation written in prose in the Rig Veda.<BR>2. A lotus.<BR>	 3. The citron.<BR>	 f. (-रा) Hiccup, violent singultus.<BR> E. गम्<BR>to go, इरन् Uṇādi affix, म changed to भ, and नुम् inserted see गभीर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=232-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गम्भीरता
गम्भीरता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Depth, (of water.)<BR>	 2. Depth of thought, profoundness.<BR>3. Depth of sound.<BR> E. गम्भीर, and तल् affix; also गम्भीरत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=232-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गम्भीरनाद
गम्भीरनाद m. (-दः) A deep or hollow sound, thundering, roaring, &c. E.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=233-a" target="_blank">Page233-a+ 60</a>]<BR>गग्भीर, and णाद sound; also similar compounds, as गम्भीरध्वनि, गम्भीर-<BR>शब्द; also with गभीर, गभीरनाद, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=232-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गम्भीरवेदिन्|गंभीरवेदिन्
गम्भीरवेदिन् m. (-दी) A restive elephant.<BR> E. गम्भीर dull, and विद् to know,<BR>affix णिनि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=233-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गम्भीरार्थ
गम्भीरार्थ n. (-र्थं) Profound sense or meaning.<BR> E. गम्भीर, and अर्थ sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=233-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गम्य|गम्यं|गम्यः
गम्य mfn. (-म्यः-म्या-म्यं)<BR>	 1. Attainable, accessible.<BR>	 2. To be gone, to be<BR>gone to.<BR>	 3. Perceptible.<BR>	 4. Desirable, suitable, fit.<BR> E. गम् to go,<BR>यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=233-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गम्यता
गम्यता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Accessibility.<BR>	 2. Perceptibility.<BR>	 3. Being capable of<BR>attainment.<BR> E. तल् added to the last; also with त्व गम्यत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=233-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गम्यमान|गम्यमानः
गम्यमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) To be gone, to be traversed, to be gone to, &c.<BR>E. गम् to go, passive v., शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=233-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गय|गयः
गय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. A species of ox, the Gayal or Bos Gavœus.<BR>	 2. The name<BR>of a royal or military saint.<BR>	 3. The name of an Asura.<BR>	 4. One of<BR>the monkey chiefs of the Rāmāyaṇa.<BR>	 f. (-या) Gaya, a city in Behar<BR>still so called, and a place of pilgrimage; the capital of the saint<BR>of the same name; it was made holy by the benediction of VIṢṆU,<BR>who granted its sancity to the piety of Gaya the Rajarshi; or ac-<BR>cording to another legend to Gaya the Asura, who was overwhel-<BR>med here by the deities with rocks; sacrifices should be offered<BR>once at least in the life of every Hindu to his progenitors at Gaya.<BR>E. गै to sing, डय aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=233-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर|गरं|गरः
गर mn. (-रः-रं)<BR>	 1. Poison.<BR>	 2. An antidote.<BR>	 m. (-रः) Sickness, disease.<BR>	 n. (-रं)<BR>1. Sprinkling, wetting.<BR>	 2. The fifth of the eleven Karanas.<BR>	 f. (-रा)<BR>Swallowing. (-री) A species of grass, (Andropogon serratus); also<BR>गरागरी.<BR> E. गर् to hurt, and अच् affix, or गृ to wet or sprinkle, or<BR>again गॄ to swallow, affix अप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=233-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गरघ्न|गरघ्नः
गरघ्न mfn. (-घ्नः-घ्नी-घ्नं)<BR>	 1. Antidotic, an antidote.<BR>	 2. Sanative, healthy.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-घ्नः) A species of Basil.<BR>	 f. (-घ्नी) A fish (the young of the Ophioce-<BR>phalus lata, HAM.)<BR> E. गर, and घ्न what destroys.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=233-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गरण|गरणं
गरण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Wetting, sprinkling.<BR>	 2. Swallowing.<BR> E. गृ to wet, or गॄ<BR>to swallow, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=233-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गरद|गरदं|गरदः
गरद mfn. (-द-दा-दं)<BR>	 1. A poisoner. poisoning.<BR>	 2. Unwholesome, occasion-<BR>ing sickness.<BR>	 n. (-दं) Poison.<BR> E. गर poison, and द who gives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=233-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गरव्रत|गरव्रतः
गरव्रत m. (-तः) A peacock.<BR> E. गर sprinkling, (of rain,) and व्रत religious<BR>observance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=233-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गरभ|गरभः
गरभ m. (-भः) The fœtus or embryo: see गर्भ.<BR> E. गृ to drop, &c. अभच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=233-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गरल|गरलं|गरलः
गरल n. (-लं)<BR>	 1. The venom of a snake or venom in general.<BR>	 2. A<BR>bundle of grass, or hay.<BR>	 3. Measure in general.<BR> E. गर poison, &c.<BR>and ल what gets or possesses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=233-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गरलिन्
गरलिन् mfn. (-ली-लिनी-लि) Venomous, poisonous.<BR> E. गरल, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=233-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गरागरी
गरागरी f. (-री) A kind of grass, (Andropogon serratus:) see खरा and<BR>गरी; also अगरी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=233-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गरात्मक|गरात्मकं
गरात्मक n. (-कं) The seed of the Sobhanjan or Morunga.<BR> E. गर poison,<BR>and आत्मक nature.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=233-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गराधिका
गराधिका f. (-का) Lac, the animal red dye so called.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=233-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गरिमन्
गरिमन् m. (-मा)<BR>	 1. Weight, heaviness.<BR>	 2. Venerableness.<BR> E. गुरु and<BR>इमनिच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=233-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गरिष्ठ|गरिष्ठः
गरिष्ठ mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठा-ष्ठं)<BR>	 1. Heaviest, excessively heavy.<BR>	 2. Very vener-<BR>able.<BR> E. गुरु heavy, इष्ठच् superlative affix, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=233-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गरीयस्
गरीयस् mfn. (-यान्-यसी-यः)<BR>	 1. Heaviest, very heavy.<BR>	 2. Highly venerable<BR>3. Worst. E. See the last, affix ईयसुन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=233-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गरुड|गरुडः
गरुड m. (-डः) The bird and vehicle of VIṢṆU; he is generally re-<BR>presented as being something between a man and a bird, and<BR>considered as sovereign of the feathered race; he is the son of<BR>KAŚYAPA and VINATA, and younger brother of ARUṆA.<BR> E. गरुत् a<BR>wing, डी, to fly, affix ड, and the त of the noun dropped, who flies<BR>like a bird, or गृ to moisten, and उडच् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=233-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गरुडध्वज|गरुडध्वजः
गरुडध्वज m. (-जः) A name of VIṢṆU.<BR> E. गरुड, and ध्वज a symbol; whose<BR>symbol is GARUḌA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=233-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गरुडरुत
गरुडरुत n. (-तं) A species of metre having four lines to the stanza, and<BR>sixteen syllables to each line.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=233-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गरुडाग्रज|गरुडाग्रजः
गरुडाग्रज m. (-जः) ARUṆA, the charioteer of the sun.<BR> E. गरुड, and अग्रज<BR>elder born; the elder brother of GARUḌA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=233-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गरुडाङ्कित|गरुडांकित|गरुडाङ्कितं
गरुडाङ्कित n. (-तं) An emerald.<BR> E. गरुड, GARUḌA, and अङ्कित marked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=233-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गरुडाश्मन्
गरुडाश्मन् m. (-श्मा) An emerald.<BR> E. गरुड, and अश्मन् a stone: see the<BR>preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=233-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गरुडोत्तीर्ण|गरुडोत्तीर्णं|गरुडोत्तीर्ण्ण
गरुडोत्तीर्ण n. (-र्णं) The emerald.<BR> E. गरुत् and उत्तीर्ण्ण passed over.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=233-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गरुत्
गरुत् m. (-रुत्) A wing.<BR> E. गृ to moisten, and उति Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=233-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गरुत्मत्|गरुत्मन्त्
गरुत्मत् m. (-त्मान्)<BR>	 1. The bird of VIṢṆU.<BR>	 2. A bird in general.<BR> E. गरुत् a<BR>wing, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=233-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गरुद्योधिन्
गरुद्योधिन् m. (-धी) A quail.<BR> E. गरुत् a wing, and योधिन् who fights.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=233-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्ग|गर्गः
गर्ग m. (-र्गः) One of the ten principal Munis or saints, a son of BRAHMĀ.<BR>f. (गार्गी) Wife of GARGA.<BR> E. गृ to sprinkle, ग Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=233-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्गर|गर्गरः
गर्गर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A kind of fish, (Pimelodus gagora, HAM.)<BR>	 f. (-री)<BR>	 1. A<BR>churn.<BR>	 2. A water vessel, a goblet.<BR> E. गर्ग an imitative sound, a<BR>gurgling, and र what makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=233-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्गाट|गर्गाटः
गर्गाट m. (-टः) A kind of fish, (Pimelodus gagora, HAM.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=233-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्गीय
गर्गीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) A descendant of GARGA.<BR> E. गर्ग, and छ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=233-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्घ
गर्घ r. 1st cl. (गर्घति) To go or move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=233-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्ज|गर्जः|गर्ज्ज|गर्ज्जं
गर्ज r. 10th cl. (गर्जयति) To sound. r. 1st cl. (गर्जति) To emit a deep or<BR>full sound, to sound as distant thunder, to roar as a lion, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=233-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्ज|गर्जः|गर्ज्ज|गर्ज्जं
गर्ज n. (-र्जं)<BR>	 1. The roaring of elephants.<BR>	 2. The grumbling of clouds,<BR>&c.<BR> E. गर्ज् to roar or growl, affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=233-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्जक|गर्जकः|गर्ज्जक|गर्ज्जकः
गर्जक m. (-कः) A fish, commonly Gajar.<BR> E. गर्ज् to grumble, affi वुन्.<BR>गर्जन n. (-र्न)<BR>	 1. Sound, noise.<BR>	 2. Passion, wrath.<BR>	 3. Excessive indig-<BR>nation.<BR>	 4. Reproach, menace.<BR>	 5. War, battle, conflict.<BR>	 6. The<BR>grumbling of clouds, &c.<BR> E. गर्ज् to grumble or roar, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=233-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्जनीय
गर्जनीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) To be sounded or roared.<BR> E. गर्ज् to sound<BR>अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=233-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्जर|गर्ज्जर|गर्ज्जरं
गर्जर n. (-रं) A carrot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=233-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्जि|गर्जिः|गर्ज्जिः
गर्जि m. (-र्जिः) The muttering of clouds or distant thunder.<BR> E. गर्ज् to<BR>sound as thunder, कि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=233-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्जित|गर्जितः|गर्ज्जितं
गर्जित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Sounded, roared, bellowed.<BR>	 m. (-तः) Roaring of an<BR>elephant in rut.<BR>	 n. (-तं) The muttering of clouds or roaring of<BR>distant thunder.<BR> E. गर्ज् to roar. &c. affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=233-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्ज्य
गर्ज्य mfn. (-र्ज्यः-र्ज्या-र्ज्यं) To be roared or sounded.<BR> E. गर्ज् to sound.<BR>ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=233-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्त्त|गर्त|गर्तं|गर्तः|गर्त्तः
गर्त्त m. (-र्त्तः)<BR>	 1. A hole in general.<BR>	 2. The hollow of the lions.<BR>	 3. The<BR>name of a country; also त्रिगर्त्त, in the north-west of India.<BR>	 4. A<BR>kind of disease.<BR> E. गृ to drop, Uṇādi affix तन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=233-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्त्तिका|गर्तिका
गर्त्तिका f. (-का) A weaver's workshop.<BR> E. गर्त्त a hole, affix ठन्, the weav-<BR>er sits at his loom with his feet in a hollow or hole below the<BR>level of the floor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=233-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्द|गर्द्द
गर्द r. 1st and 10th cls. (गर्दति, गर्दयति) To sound, to roar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=233-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्द्दभ|गर्दभ|गर्दभः|गर्द्दभं|गर्द्दभः
गर्द्दभ m. (-भः)<BR>	 1. Smell, odour.<BR>	 2. An ass.<BR>	 f. (-भी)<BR>	 1. A she ass.<BR>	 2. An in-<BR>sect, a kind of beetle springing from cowdung.<BR>	 3. A disease of<BR>the skin, eruption of round, red, and painful spots; also गर्द्दभिका.<BR>4. A creeper, (Clitoria ternata.)<BR>	 n. (-भं) The white lotus.<BR> E. गर्द्द् to<BR>sound, Uṇādi affix अभच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=233-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्द्दभाजिन
गर्द्दभाजिन n. (-नं) The skin or hide of an ass.<BR> E. गर्द्दभ, and अजिन a skin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=233-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्द्दभशाक|गर्दभशाक|गर्द्दभशाकः
गर्द्दभशाक mf. (-कः-का) A plant, (Ovieda verticellata.)<BR> E. गर्द्दभ an ass,<BR>and शाक a vegetable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=233-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्द्दभाण्ड|गर्दभाण्ड|गर्दभांड|गर्दभाण्डः|गर्द्दभाण्डः
गर्द्दभाण्ड m. (-ण्डः) A kind of tree, commonly Parspipal, (Hibiscus<BR>populneoides.)<BR> E. गर्द्दभ smell, अम् to go, and ड aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=233-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्द्दभाह्वय|गर्दभाह्वय|गर्द्दभाह्वयः
गर्द्दभाह्वय m. (-यः) The white lotus.<BR> E. गर्द्दभ smell, and आह्वय an appellation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=233-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्द्दभिका|गर्दभिका
गर्द्दभिका f. (-का) An cutaneous disease, a blotch, an eruption.<BR> E. कन्<BR>fem. form added to गर्द्दभ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=233-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्द्ध
गर्द्ध m. (-र्द्धः)<BR>	 1. Eagerness, greediness.<BR>	 2. The Parspipal: see गर्द्धभाण्ड. E.<BR>गृध् to desire, to be greedy, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=233-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्द्धन
गर्द्धन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) covetous. Greedy.<BR> E. गृध् to be greedy, affix युच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=234-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्द्धिन्
गर्द्धिन् mfn. (-र्द्धी-र्द्धिनी-र्द्धि) Greedy, covetous.<BR> E. गर्द्ध, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=234-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्ध|गर्द्धः|गर्धः
गर्ध r. 10th cl. (गर्धयति) To desire or covet: see गृध.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=234-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्ब्ब|गर्ब|गर्ब्बः
गर्ब्ब r. 1st cl. (गर्ब्बति) To move, to go or approach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=234-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्ब्ब|गर्ब|गर्ब्बः
गर्ब्ब m. (-र्ब्बः) Pride, haughtiness.<BR> E. गर्ब्ब् to be proud, अच् affix; also<BR>read गर्ब्भ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=234-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्ब्भ
गर्ब्भ m. (-र्ब्भः) A fœtus, &c.; see the next.<BR>	 f. (-र्ब्भा) Interval of time,<BR>division of time or place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=234-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्भ|गर्भः
गर्भ m. (-र्भः)<BR>	 1. A fœtus or embryo.<BR>	 2. A child.<BR>	 3. The belly.<BR>	 4. The in-<BR>side, the middle.<BR>	 5. Joining, union.<BR>	 6. The rough coat of the fruit<BR>of the Jaka.<BR>	 7. An inner apartment, a lying-in chamber.<BR>	 8. Any<BR>interior chamber, the adytum of a temple, &c.<BR>	 9. The bed of the<BR>Ganges, when the river is fullest; that is, on the fourteenth day of<BR>of the dark half of the month Bhadra, or in the height of the<BR>rains; as high as the river flows at this period, so far extends the<BR>Garbha, after which the Tir or proper bank begins, and extends<BR>for 150 cubits; this space is holy ground.<BR>	 10. The calyx of the<BR>lotus. The interior or inner part of any thing.<BR> E. गृ to drop, or<BR>गॄ to swallow, Uṇādi affix मन्; also read गर्भ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=234-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्भक|गर्भकं|गर्भकः
गर्भक m. (-कः) A chaplet of flowers, &c. worn in the hair.<BR>	 n. (-कं) A<BR>period of a day and two nights.<BR> E. कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=234-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्भकर|गर्भकरः
गर्भकर mfn. (-रः-री-रं) Impregnating, fecundatory, procreative, produc-<BR>ing impregnation.<BR>	 m. (-रः) A plant, (Nagelia putranjiva.)<BR> E. गर्भ,<BR>and कर what makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=234-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्भकोश|गर्भकोशः
गर्भकोश m. (-शः) The uterus.<BR> E. गर्भ, and कोश sheathe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=234-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्भगृह
गर्भगृह n. (-हं)<BR>	 1. An inner chamber.<BR>	 2. A lying-in chamber.<BR>	 3. The<BR>sanctuary or adytum of a temple.<BR> E. गर्भ and गृह a house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=234-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्भग्रहण
गर्भग्रहण n. (-णं) Conception, impregnation.<BR> E. गर्भ, and ग्रहण taking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=234-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्भघातिन्
गर्भघातिन् mfn. (-ती-तिनी-ति) Producing abortion.<BR> E. गर्भ, and घातिन्<BR>what destroys.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=234-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्भचलन
गर्भचलन n. (-नं) Quickening, motion of the fœtus in utero.<BR> E. गर्भ, and<BR>चलन moving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=234-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्भच्युत
गर्भच्युत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Bearing a child.<BR>	 2. Miscarrying.<BR> E. गर्भ, and<BR>च्युत falling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=234-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्भच्युति|गर्भच्युतिः
गर्भच्युति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Birth, delivery.<BR>	 2. Miscarriage.<BR> E. गर्भ, and च्युति<BR>falling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=234-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्भण्ड|गर्भंड|गर्भंडः|गर्भण्डः
गर्भण्ड m. (-ण्डः) Enlargement of the navel.<BR> E. गर्भ the belly, and अण्ड an<BR>egg, the penultimate made short.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=234-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्भद|गर्भदः
गर्भद mfn. (-दः-दा-दं) Impregnating, procreative.<BR>	 m. (-दः) A tree, (Nagelia<BR>putranjiva.)<BR>	 f. (-दा) A shrub so called.<BR> E. गर्भ a fœtus, and द what<BR>gives, with reference to the supposed virtue of the plant; also गर्भ-<BR>दतृ mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=234-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्भद्रुह
गर्भद्रुह mfn. (-द्रुक् or द्रुट्) Causing abortion.<BR> E. गर्भ, and द्रुह what injures.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=234-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्भधारण
गर्भधारण n. (-णं) Impregnation, gestation.<BR> E. गर्भ, and धारण holding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=234-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्भनाडी
गर्भनाडी f. (-डी) The umbilical cord.<BR> E. गर्भ, and नाडी a vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=234-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्भपरिस्रव|गर्भपरिस्रवः
गर्भपरिस्रव m. (-वः) Secundines.<BR> E. गर्भ, and परिस्रव what exudes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=234-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्भपाकिन्
गर्भपाकिन् m. (-की) Rice ripening after two months.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=234-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्भपातक|गर्भपातकः
गर्भपातक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Producing abortion.<BR>	 m. (-कः) A red kind of<BR>morunga.<BR> E. गर्भ the fœtus, पत् to fall, in the causal form, and<BR>वुञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=234-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्भपातन|गर्भपातनः
गर्भपातन n. (-नं) Producing abortion.<BR>	 f. (-नी) Any plant or drug supposed<BR>to have that effect.<BR> E. गर्भ, and पातन causing to fall.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=234-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्भपातिन्
गर्भपातिन् mfn. (-ती-तिनी-ति) Producing abortion f. (-नी) A kind of<BR>potherb: see विशल्या. E. As in the last, affixes णिनि and ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=234-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्भपोषण
गर्भपोषण n. (-णं) Gestation.<BR> E. गर्भ, and पोषण nourishing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=234-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्भरूप|गर्भरूपः
गर्भरूप mfn. (-पः-पी-पं) A child, an infant.<BR> E. गर्भ an embryo, and रूप<BR>form; also गर्भरूपकः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=234-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्भवती
गर्भवती f. (-ती) A pregnant female.<BR> E. गर्भ a fœtus, and मतुप् poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=234-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्भशङ्कु|गर्भशंकु|गर्भशङ्कुः
गर्भशङ्कु m. (-ङ्कुः) A kind of vectis or instrument for extracting the dead<BR>fœtus.<BR> E. गर्भ and शङ्कु a probe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=234-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्भशय्या
गर्भशय्या f. (-य्या) The uterus.<BR> E. गर्भ, and शय्या a bed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=234-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्भस्थ
गर्भस्थ mfn. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थं)<BR>	 1. Situated in the womb.<BR>	 2. Centrical, internal,<BR>within the centre of any thing.<BR> E. गर्भ, and स्थ what abides.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=234-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्भस्राव|गर्भस्रावः
गर्भस्राव m. (-वः) Abortion, miscarriage.<BR> E. गर्भ the embryo, and स्राव<BR>expulsion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=234-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्भस्राविन्
गर्भस्राविन् mfn. (-वी-विणी-वि) Producing or occasioning abortion.<BR> E. गर्भ,<BR>and स्राविन् what causes to issue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=234-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्भागार|गर्भागारं
गर्भागार n. (-रं)<BR>	 1. An inner and private room, the female apartments, the<BR>lying-in chamber.<BR>	 2. The sanctuary of a temple. The chamber where<BR>the object of worship is placed.<BR> E. गर्भ the fœtus, and आगार an<BR>abode, hence it is applied to the womb: see गर्भाशय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=234-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्भाधान|गर्भाधानं
गर्भाधान n. (-नं) A ceremony performed prior to conception.<BR> E. गर्भ the<BR>embryo, and आधान taking, being supposed conductive to future<BR>impregnation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=234-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्भाशय|गर्भाशयः
गर्भाशय m. (-यः) The womb, the uterus.<BR> E. गर्भ the embryo, and आशय asy-<BR>lum or abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=234-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्भाष्टम|गर्भाष्टमः
गर्भाष्टम m. (-मः) The eighth month of uterine gestation.<BR>	 2. The eighth<BR>year reckoning from conception.<BR> E. गर्भ the fœtus, and अष्टम eighth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=234-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्भिणी
गर्भिणी f. (-णी)<BR>	 1. A pregnant woman.<BR>	 2. A plant, (Asclepias rosea)<BR> E. गर्भ<BR>embryo, and इनि poss. affix, fem. affix ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=234-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्भिण्यवेक्षण|गर्भिण्यवेक्षणं
गर्भिण्यवेक्षण n. (-णं) Midwifery, attendance and care of pregnant women<BR>and new born infants.<BR> E. गर्भिणी, and अवेक्षण care, looking to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=234-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्भोपघातिनी
गर्भोपघातिनी f. (-नी) A cow (or female), miscarrying from going unseason-<BR>ably.<BR> E. गर्भ the fœtus, उप intensitive preffix, हन् to destroy, affixes<BR>णिनि and ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=234-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्म्मुटिका|गर्मुटिका
गर्म्मुटिका f. (-का) A species of rice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=234-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्म्मुत्|गर्मुत्
गर्म्मुत् f. (-र्म्मुत्)<BR>	 1. A kind of grass.<BR>	 2. Gold.<BR>	 3. A reed.<BR> E. गॄ to swallow,<BR>&c. Uṇādi affix उति, and म inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=234-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्व्व|गर्व|गर्वः|गर्व्वः
गर्व्व r. 1st cl. (गर्व्वति) To be proud or haughty; also (ङ) गर्वङ् r. 10th<BR>cl. (गर्व्वयते) To grow proud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=234-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्व्व|गर्व|गर्वः|गर्व्वः
गर्व्व m. (-र्व्वः) Pride, arrogance.<BR> E. गर्व्व् to be proud, affix अच् or गॄ to<BR>swallow, &c. and व Uṇādi affix; this word is sometimes written गर्ब्ब.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=234-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्व्वर|गर्वर
गर्व्वर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Proud, haughty, arrogant.<BR> E. गॄ to reject, &c. Uṇādi<BR>affix खरच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=234-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्व्वाट|गर्वाट|गर्वाटः|गर्व्वाटः
गर्व्वाट m. (-टः) A watchman, a doorkeeper, a sort of village constable, a<BR>headborough or beadle.<BR> E. गर्व्व pride, अट् to go, and अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=234-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्व्वित|गर्वित|गर्व्वितः
गर्व्वित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Proud, haughty.<BR>	 2. Conceited.<BR> E. गर्व्व pride,<BR>and इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=234-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्ह
गर्ह r. 1st and 10th cls. (गर्हति-ते, गर्हयति) To blame, to censure to despise<BR>or contemn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=234-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्हण|गर्हणं
गर्हण n. (-णं) Censuring, censure, blame, reproach.<BR> E. गर्ह् reprove, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=234-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्हणीय
गर्हणीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Censurable, contemptible, vile, bad.<BR> E. गर्ह् to<BR>abuse, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=234-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्हा
गर्हा f. (-र्हा) Abuse, censure, reproach.<BR> E. गर्ह् to revile, affixes अङ् and<BR>टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=234-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्हित|गर्हितं
गर्हित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Blamed, censured.<BR>	 2. Contemned, despised.<BR>3. Bad, vile.<BR> E. गर्ह् to blame, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=234-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्ह्य|गर्ह्यः
गर्ह्य mfn. (-र्ह्यः-र्ह्या-र्ह्यं) Low, vile, contemptible.<BR> E. गर्ह् to abuse, affix<BR>यत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=234-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्ह्यवादिन्
गर्ह्यवादिन् mfn. (-दी-दिनी-दि) Speaking ill, speaking vilely or inaccurate-<BR>ly.<BR> E. गर्ह्य vile, and वादिन् who speaks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=234-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गल|गलः
गल r. 1st cl. (गलति)<BR>	 1. To eat.<BR>	 2. To ooze; also (ङ्) गलङ् r. 10th cl.<BR>(गलयते) To drop, to ooze or distil. With अव prefixed, To fall, to<BR>fall down or off; With वि, 1. To go, to approach.<BR>	 2. To bear or<BR>support.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=234-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गल|गलः
गल m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. The throat.<BR>	 2. The resin of the Sal tree.<BR>	 3. A reed, a<BR>large kind of the Saccharum cylindricum.<BR>	 4. A rope.<BR>	 5. A musical<BR>instrument.<BR>	 6. A kind of fish, a small kind of cyprinus, a subgenus<BR>of that class, (Cyprinus garra. HAM.)<BR> E. गल् to eat, to drop, &c. affix<BR>अच्, or गॄ to swallow, with अच्, गर, and र changed to ल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=234-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गलक|गलकः
गलक m. (-कः) A kind of fish.<BR> E. कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=235-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गलकम्बल|गलकंबल|गलकम्बलः
गलकम्बल m. (-लः) A bull's dewlap.<BR> E. गल the neck, and कम्बल a soft<BR>substance as a blanket, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=235-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गलगण्ड|गलगंड|गलगण्डः
गलगण्ड m. (-ण्डः) Inflammation, enlargement of the glands of the neck.<BR>E. गल throat and गण्ड a swelling or boil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=235-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गलग्रह|गलग्रहः
गलग्रह m. (-हः)<BR>	 1. A sauce of fish ground up with salt, pepper, Ghee,<BR>&c.<BR>	 2. A day on which a course of study is commenced, but imme-<BR>diately preceding a day on which study is prohibited.<BR>	 3. The fourth<BR>lunation of the dark fortnight, the seventh eighth, and ninth, the<BR>thirteenth and three days following.<BR>	 4. Seizing any one by the<BR>throat, throttling, choking.<BR> E. गल the throat, and ग्रह what takes,<BR>&c.; also गलग्रहण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=235-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गलत्
गलत् mfn. (-लन्-लन्ती-लत्)<BR>	 1. Falling, dropping.<BR>	 2. Oozing, trickling,<BR>flowing.<BR>	 3. Melting.<BR> E. गल् to flow, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=235-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गलन|गलनं
गलन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Melting, fusing.<BR>	 2. Trickling, dropping, oozing.<BR>	 3. Fall-<BR>ing. down or off.<BR>	 4. Leaking.<BR> E. गल् to drop, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=235-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गलनीय
गलनीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Fusible, liquefiable, to be melted, &c.<BR> E. गल् to<BR>melt, अनीयर् affix; also गलितव्य and गल्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=235-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गलन्तिका|गलंतिका
गलन्तिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. A small pitcher.<BR>	 2. A small water jar with small<BR>holes in the bottom, from which the water drops upon a Linga<BR>or Tulasi plant, placed beneath.<BR> E. गड् to drop, affix झच्, गडन्ति कन्<BR>in the fem. form added, and ड changed to ल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=235-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गलमेखला
गलमेखला f. (-ला) A thread worn round the neck, a necklace.<BR> E. गल the<BR>throat, and मेखला a girdle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=235-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गलव्रत|गलव्रतः
गलव्रत m. (-तः) A peacock.<BR> E. गल the throat, व्रत holy observance.<BR>also the same as गरव्रत q. v. ल being substituted for र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=235-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गलशुण्डिका|गलशुंडिका
गलशुण्डिका f. (-का) The uvula or soft palate.<BR> E. गल the throat, and<BR>शुण्डिका the elephant's trunk, resembling it in being a pendulous,<BR>roundish, and fleshy substance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=235-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गलस्तनी
गलस्तनी f. (-नी) A she-goat.<BR> E. गल the throat, and स्तन the breast; some<BR>species of the Bengal goat have small fleshy processes, resembling<BR>nipples depending from the throat; also गलस्तनी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=235-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गलहस्त|गलहस्तः
गलहस्त m. (-स्तः) Throttling.<BR> E. गल, and हस्त the hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=235-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गलाङ्कुर|गलांकुर|गलाङ्कुरः
गलाङ्कुर m. (-रः) A disease of the throat, inflammation of the fauces,<BR>and enlargement of the tonsils.<BR> E. गल the throat, and अङ्कुर a new<BR>sprout.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=235-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गलाविल
गलाविल m. (-लः) A prawn or shrimp: see गङ्गाटेय. Some books read this<BR>गलानिल, and others गलानिक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=235-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गलि|गलिः
गलि m. (-लिः) A strong and lazy ox.<BR> E. गल् to eat, and इन् affix; who<BR>is good for nothing but eating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=235-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गलित|गलितः
गलित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Fallen, dropped.<BR>	 2. Liquefied, melted.<BR>	 3. Dis-<BR>tilled, oozing, flowing.<BR>	 4. Decayed, impaired.<BR>	 5. Lost, deprived.<BR>6. Untied, loosed.<BR> E. गल् to drop, to ooze, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=235-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गलितकुष्ठ
गलितकुष्ठ n. (-ष्ठं) Advanced and incurable leprosy, when the fingers and<BR>toes fall off.<BR> E. गलित, and कुष्ठ leprosy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=235-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गलितदन्त
गलितदन्त mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं) Toothless.<BR> E. गलित, and दन्त tooth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=235-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गलितनख
गलितनख mfn. (-खः-खा-खी-खं) Having no nails.<BR> E. गलित, and नख the nail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=235-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गलितनयन
गलितनयन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Blind.<BR> E. गलित, and नयन the eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=235-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गलेगण्ड|गलेगंड|गलेगंडः|गलेगण्डः
गलेगण्ड m. (-ण्डः) A kind of bird, (the Adjutant or Ardea argala.)<BR> E. गल<BR>the throat, in the seventh case, and गण्ड a boil; alluding to a pen-<BR>dulous fleshy purse hanging from the throat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=235-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गलेस्तनी
गलेस्तनी f. (-नी) A she-goat; see गलस्तनी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=235-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गलू
गलू m. (-लूः) A sort of gem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=235-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गल्भ
गल्भ r. 1st cl. (गल्भते) To be bold or confident.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=235-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गल्भ
गल्भ mfn. (-ल्भः-ल्भा-ल्भं)<BR>	 1. Proud, haughty.<BR>	 2. Confident, bold, auda-<BR>cious.<BR> E. गल्भ् to be proud, &c. अच् affix, more commonly प्रगलभ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=235-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गल्या
गल्या f. (-ल्या)<BR>	 1. A multitude of throats.<BR>	 2. A quantity of a kind of<BR>grass, or ropes made of it.<BR> E. गल a throat, &c. य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=235-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गल्ल|गल्लः
गल्ल m. (-ल्लः) The cheek.<BR> E. गल् to eat, and ल affix; from ला to get or<BR>receive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=235-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गल्लचातुरी
गल्लचातुरी f. (-री) A small round pillow to put underneath the cheek. E.<BR>गल्ल the cheek, and चातुर a pillow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=235-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गल्वर्क|गल्वर्कः
गल्वर्क m. (-र्कः)<BR>	 1. A goblet, a vessel for drinking spirituous liquor.<BR>	 2.<BR>Lapis lazuli.<BR> E. गल् to drop, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=235-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गल्ह
गल्ह r. 1st cl. (गल्हते) To blame, to censure or despise: see गर्ह.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=235-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गवय|गवयः
गवय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. A species of ox, the Gayal, erroneously classed by<BR>Hindu writers amongst the kinds of deer, (Bos gavæus.)<BR>	 2. A<BR>monkey chief: the son of VAIVASWATA.<BR>	 f. (-यी) The female Gayal.<BR>E. गु to sound, and अय affix, form irregular; or गो a cow, and य<BR>from या to obtain. affix ड, resembling a cow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=235-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गवराज|गवराजः
गवराज m. (-जः) A bull.<BR> E. गो a cow, affix अण् गव relating to a cow, and<BR>राजन् king, chief; the more direct compound makes गोराज.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=235-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गवल|गवलं|गवलः
गवल m. (-लः) A wild buffalo.<BR>	 n. (-लं) Buffalo's horn.<BR> E. गु to sound,<BR>अलच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=235-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गवाक्ष|गवाक्षः
गवाक्ष m. (-क्षः)<BR>	 1. An air hole, a loop hole, a round window, a bull's<BR>eye, &c.<BR>	 2. A monkey chief; one of the sons of VAIVASWATA. E.<BR>गो a ray of light, अक्ष् to spread, affix घञ्, or गो an ox, and अक्ष an<BR>eye; ox eyed.<BR>	 f. (क्षी) A sort of cucumber, (Cucumis madraspata-<BR>nus.)<BR>	 2. A plant, (Clitoria ternatea:) see अपराजिता.<BR> E. गो the earth,<BR>अक्ष् to spread, affix अण् or ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=235-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गवाक्षजाल
गवाक्षजाल n. (-लं) A lattice, a jalousie, trellice work.<BR> E. गवाक्ष, and जाल<BR>a net.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=235-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गवाची
गवाची f. (-ची) A fish, (Macrognathus pancalus.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=235-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गवादन|गवादनं
गवादन n. (-नं) Pasture or meadow grass.<BR>	 f. (-नी)<BR>	 1. A hay rack, a trough<BR>for holding grass out of which cattle feed.<BR>	 2. A species of cucum-<BR>ber, (Cucumis madraspatanus, or, according to some, C. coloquin-<BR>tida.)<BR>	 3. A plant, (Clitoria ternatea:) see the preceding.<BR> E. गो a<BR>cow, अदन food, fem. affix ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=235-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गवालूक|गवालूकः
गवालूक m. (-कः) The Gayal, (Bos gavæus:) see गवय.<BR> E. गो a cow, लोक<BR>to see, with आङ् prefixed, deriv. irr.; in appearance a cow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=235-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गवाशन|गवाशनः
गवाशन m. (-नः) An outcaste.<BR> E. गव, and अशन who eats, eating beef.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=235-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गवाषिका
गवाषिका f. (-का) Lac, the dye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=235-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गवाह्निक
गवाह्निक n. (-कं) A day's feed for a cow.<BR> E. गो and आह्निक daily.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=235-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गवीश्वर|गवीश्वरः
गवीश्वर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Owner of kine.<BR> E. गो a cow, ईश्वर a lord or master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=235-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गवेडु|गवेडुः
गवेडु m. (-डुः) A cloud.<BR>	 f. (-डुः) A kind of grain, (Coix barbata.)<BR> E. गो a<BR>cow or the earth, एड् to preserve, उ affix, or with कन् added गवेडुका<BR>also गवेधु, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=235-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गवेधु|गवेधुः
गवेधु f. (-धुः) Coix barbata: see the preceding; also with कन् added<BR>गवेधुका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=235-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गवेरुक|गवेरुकं
गवेरुक n. (-कं) Red chalk.<BR> E. गो light or colour, ईर् to send, affix वुन्,<BR>and the penultimate changed to उ irregularly; also read गवेधुक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=235-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गवेशका
गवेशका f. (-का) A plant, (Hedysarum lagopodioides.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=235-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गवेष|गवेषः
गवेष r. 10th cl. (गवेषयति)<BR>	 1. To seek, to hunt for, to search or inquire.<BR>2. To make an effort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=235-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गवेषण|गवेषणं
गवेषण nf. (-णं-णा) Research, inquiry after any thing, (physical or phi-<BR>losophical, &c.)<BR> E. गवेष to inquire, affix युच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=235-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गवेषित|गवेषितं
गवेषित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Sought, inquired for.<BR> E. गवेष to search or hunt, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=235-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गवोद्व
गवोद्व m. (-द्वः) An excellent cow.<BR> E. गो a cow, and उद्व implying excel-<BR>lence; the compound remains masculine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=235-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गव्य|गव्यं
गव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>	 1. Of or belonging to a cow, (as milk, curds, &c.)<BR>2. Proper or fit for cattle.<BR>	 nf. (-व्यं-व्या) A bowstring.<BR>	 f. (-व्या)<BR>	 1. A<BR>multitude of cows.<BR>	 2. A measure of two Kos: see गव्यूति.<BR>	 n. (-व्यं) A<BR>colouring substance, a yellow pigment or dye.<BR> E. गो a cow, &c.<BR>and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=235-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गव्यूत|गव्यूतं
गव्यूत n. (-तं)<BR>	 1. A Kos, a measure of length equal 4000 cubits.<BR>	 2. A<BR>measure of two Kos: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=235-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गव्यूति|गव्यूतिः
गव्यूति mf. (-तिः) A measure of two Kos, a league measured by 2000<BR>Dands or fathoms.<BR> E. गो the earth, यु to join, क्तिन् affix, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=235-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गह
गह r. 10th cl. (-गहयति) To be thick or impervious as a forest, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=235-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गह
गह m. (-ह) A cave.<BR>	 2. A forest.<BR> E. गह् to be impervious अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=235-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गहन|गहनं|गहनः
गहन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Impervious, inaccessible.<BR>	 n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. A wood, a<BR>thicket.<BR>	 2. A cave.<BR>	 3. Pain, distress.<BR> E. गाह् to tremble, &c. affix<BR>युच्, and the radical vowel made short; or गह् to be thick, affix as<BR>before.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=236-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गहीय
गहीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Relating to a cave or a thicket, which is deep<BR>and difficult of access, impervious.<BR> E. गह a thicket, छ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=236-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गह्वर|गह्वरं|गह्वरः
गह्वर nf. (-रं-री) A cave, a cavern, a grotto, a recess in a rock or moun-<BR>tain, &c.<BR>	 n. (-रं)<BR>	 1. A thicket, a wood.<BR>	 2. Hypocrisy.<BR>	 3. Weeping,<BR>crying, but not violently.<BR>	 m. (-रः) An arbour, a bower.<BR> E. गाह to<BR>be agitated, and ष्वरच् Uṇādi affix, the radical vowel made short.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=236-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गा
गा r. 1st cl. (ङ) गाङ् (गाते) To go, to go to or towards. r. 3rd. cl. but<BR>restricted to the Vedas. (जगाति) To praise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=236-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गा
गा f. (-गा) A verse or metrical composition.<BR> E. गै to sing, क and टाप्<BR>affixes: see ग.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=236-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गाङ्ग|गांग|गाङ्गं|गाङ्गः
गाङ्ग mfn. (-ङ्गः-ङ्गी-ङ्गं) Belonging or relating to the river Ganges.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-ङ्गः)<BR>	 1. A name of KARTIKEYA.<BR>	 2. A name of BHISHMA<BR> E. गङ्गा<BR>the GANGA, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=236-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गाङ्गट|गांगट|गांगटः|गाङ्गटः
गाङ्गट m. (-टः) A prawn or shrimp.<BR> E. गाङ्ग relating to the Ganges, and<BR>अट what goes, form irr.; also गाङ्गाट or with कन् affix गाङ्गाटक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=236-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गाङ्गटय
गाङ्गटय m. (-यः) A shrimp or prawn.<BR> E. गङ्गा, अट् to go, and ढक् affix<BR>also गङ्गाटेय, and गाङ्गाट, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=236-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गाङ्गायनि|गांगायनि|गांगायनिः|गाङ्गायनिः
गाङ्गायनि f. (-निः)<BR>	 1. A name of BHISHMA.<BR>	 2. A name of KARTIKEYA, E.<BR>गङ्गा the personified river, (as the wife of SANTANU, in the first<BR>instance, and mother of the hero; and in the second, as the receiver<BR>of KARTIKEYA, the son of ŚIVA, from AGNI, the god of fire.) and<BR>फिञ् patronymic aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=236-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गाङ्गेय|गांगेय|गाङ्गेयं|गाङ्गेयः
गाङ्गेय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. BHISHMA.<BR>	 2. KARTIKEYA: see the preceding.<BR>	 3. The<BR>Hilsa or Illias fish, (Cluponodon ilisha, HAM.)<BR>	 n. (-यं)<BR>	 1. Gold.<BR>	 2.<BR>A grass: see कशेरु.<BR>	 3. A fragrant grass, (Cyperus rotundus.) E.<BR>गङ्गा the Ganges, ढक् affix of descent, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=236-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गाङ्गेरुकी
गाङ्गेरुकी f. (-की) A plant, (Hedysarum lagopodioides, but it is vari-<BR>ously described.)<BR> E. गाङ्ग Ganges water, ईर् to go or grow, उकन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=236-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गाङ्गेष्ठी
गाङ्गेष्ठी f. (-ष्ठी) A plant, (Guilandina bonducella.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=236-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गाङ्गौघ
गाङ्गौघ n. (-घं) The current of the Ganges.<BR> E. गाङ्ग Gangetic, and ओघ<BR>heap.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=236-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गाञ्जिकाय|गांजिकाय|गांजिकायः|गाञ्जिकायः
गाञ्जिकाय m. (-यः) A quail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=236-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गाढ|गाढं
गाढ adv.<BR>	 n. (-ढं) adj.<BR>	 mfn. (ढः-ढा-ढं)<BR>	 1. Excessive, much, very much,<BR>heavy, oppressive, &c.<BR>	 2. Firm, strong.<BR>	 3. Hard.<BR>	 4. Close.<BR> E. गाह्<BR>to agitate, affix क्त, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=236-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गाढता
गाढता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Firmness, hardness.<BR>	 2. Excess.<BR> E. गाढ, and तल affix;<BR>also with त्व, गाढत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=236-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गाढमुष्टि|गाढमुष्टिः
गाढमुष्टि mfn. (-ष्टिः-ष्टिः-ष्टि) Miserly, niggard, avaricious, close-fisted m.<BR>(-ष्टिः) A scymitar, a large sacrificial knife.<BR> E. गाढ heavy or close,<BR>and मुष्टि gripe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=236-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गाणपत
गाणपत mfn. (-तः-ती-तं) Relating to GANESHA, or the leader of a troop,<BR>&c.<BR> E. गणपति, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=236-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गाणपत्य|गाणपत्यः
गाणपत्य mfn. (-त्यः-त्यी-त्यं) Relating to GANAPATI or GANESHA.<BR>	 m. (-त्यः) A<BR>worshipper of him.<BR>	 n. (-त्यं)<BR>	 1. Worship of him.<BR>	 2. Chieftainship,<BR>presidency.<BR> E. गणपति, and ष्यण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=236-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गाणिक्य|गाणिक्यं
गाणिक्य n. (-क्यं) An assembly of harlots.<BR> E. गणिका a whore, यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=236-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गाण्डिव|गांडिव|गांडिवं|गांडिवः|गाण्डिवः
गाण्डिव mn. (-वः-वं)<BR>	 1. The bow of ARJUNA.<BR>	 2. Any bow; also गाण्डीव.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=236-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गाण्डीव|गांडीव|गांडीवं|गांडीवः|गाण्डीवः
गाण्डीव mn. (-वः-वं)<BR>	 1. The bow of ARJUNA.<BR>	 2. Any bow.<BR> E. गाण्डी what<BR>affects the cheek, from गण्ड with इञ् affix, then व added, and इ<BR>final lengthened; or continuing short, गाण्डिव.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=236-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गाण्डीविन्|गांडीविन्
गाण्डीविन् m. (-वी) A name of ARJUNA.<BR> E. गाण्डीव ARJUNA'S bow, and<BR>इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=236-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गातु|गातुः
गातु mfn. (-तुः-तुः-तु) Angry, wrathful.<BR>	 m. (-तुः)<BR>	 1. A Gandharba or<BR>celestial chorister.<BR>	 2. The Kokila or Indian cuckoo.<BR>	 3. A large black<BR>bee.<BR>	 4. A singer.<BR> E. गै to sing, Uṇādi affix तु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=236-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गातृ
गातृ mf. (-ता-त्री) A male or female singer.<BR> E. गै to sing, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=236-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गात्र|गात्रं
गात्र n. (-त्रं)<BR>	 1. The body.<BR>	 2. The fore quarter of an elephant.<BR>	 3. A limb,<BR>a member.<BR> E. गम् to go, ष्ट्रन् Uṇādi affix, the radical final is reject-<BR>ed, and the vowel made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=236-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गात्रभङ्गा
गात्रभङ्गा f. (-ङ्गा) Cowach, (Carpopogon pruriens.)<BR> E. गात्र the body, and<BR>भङ्गा what breaks or hurts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=236-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गात्रमार्जनी|गात्रमार्ज्जनी
गात्रमार्जनी f. (-नी) A towel.<BR> E. गात्र, and मार्जनी a wiper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=236-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गात्रसङ्कोचिन्|गात्रसंकोचिन्
गात्रसङ्कोचिन् m. (-ची) The pole-cat, (Viverra putorius)<BR> E. गात्र the body,<BR>and सङ्कोचिन् who draws up or contracts in order to spring upon prey.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=236-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गात्रसम्प्लव|गात्रसंप्लव|गात्रसंप्लवः
गात्रसम्प्लव m. (-वः) A small bird, the diver.<BR> E. गात्र the body, and सम्प्लव<BR>who plunges, from सम् entirely, प्लुङ to go, and अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=236-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गात्रानुलेपनी
गात्रानुलेपनी f. (-नी) Fragrant unguents, &c. smeared upon the body,<BR>perfume for the person.<BR> E. गात्र the body, अनु upon लिप् to plaster<BR>or smear, and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=236-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गात्रोत्सादन
गात्रोत्सादन n. (-नं) Cleaning the person with perfumes, &c.<BR> E. गात्र and<BR>उत्सादन cleaning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=236-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गाथक|गाथकः
गाथक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A musician, a singer.<BR>	 2. A chanter of the Puranas<BR>or sacred poems.<BR> E. गै to sing. स्थकन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=236-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गाथा
गाथा f. (-थां)<BR>	 1. A verse, a stanza.<BR>	 2. Metre, rhythm.<BR>	 3. A song, a chant<BR>or verse to be chanted or sung.<BR>	 4. Prakrita or any language not<BR>Sanskrit.<BR>	 5. The same as the Aryya Metre, in which the verse con-<BR>tains sixty syllabic instants, variously arranged.<BR> E. गै to sing, थन्<BR>Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=236-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गाथाकार|गाथाकारः
गाथाकार m. (-रः) A singer. A reciter.<BR> E. गाथा, कृ to make, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=236-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गाथिक|गाथिकः
गाथिक m. (-कः) One who recites Gathas, verses or hymns.<BR> E. गाथा, and<BR>ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=236-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गाध|गाधः
गाध (ऋ) गाधृ r. 1st. cl. (गाधते)<BR>	 1. To stand, to stay, to remain.<BR>	 2. To<BR>seek, to search or enquire for.<BR>	 3. To compile. string or heap<BR>together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=236-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गाध|गाधः
गाध mfn. (-धः-धा-धं) Not very deep.<BR>	 m. (-धः)<BR>	 1. Place, site.<BR>	 2. Desire<BR>of gain, cupidity, covetousness.<BR>	 3. Bottom, soundings.<BR> E. गाध् to<BR>stand, &c. affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=236-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गाधि|गाधिः
गाधि m. (-धिः) The name of a king sovereign of Kanyakubja, father<BR>of ViSWAMITRA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=236-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गाधिज|गाधिजः
गाधिज m. (-जः)<BR>	 1. A name of the celebrated saint VISWAMITRA.<BR> E. गाधि<BR>as above, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=236-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गाधिपुर|गाधिपुरं
गाधिपुर n. (-रं) Kanyakubja the ancient Kanouj.<BR> E. गाधि a proper name<BR>an पुर a city; the capital of GADHI.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=236-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गाधिभू
गाधिभू m. (-भूः) The saint VISWAMITRA.<BR> E. गाधि, and भू born, the<BR>son of GADHI.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=236-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गाधेय|गाधेयः
गाधेय m. (-यः) VISWAMITRA.<BR> E. गाधि and ढक् patronymic affix: see the<BR>preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=236-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गान|गानं
गान n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Singing, song in general, or a song.<BR>	 2. Sound.<BR> E. गै to<BR>sing affix ल्युट्;<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=236-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गानिनी
गानिनी f. (-नी) Orris root.<BR> E. गान song, इनि and ङीप् affixes; supposed<BR>to be of use in clearing the voice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=236-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गानीय
गानीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Musical.<BR> E. गान and छ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=236-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गान्तु|गांतुः|गान्तुः
गान्तु mfn. (-न्तुः-न्तुः-न्तु) A goer, a traveller, one who goes or moves E.<BR>गम् to go, Uṇādi affix तु, and the radical vowel made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=236-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गान्त्री|गांत्री
गान्त्री f. (-न्त्री) A carriage drawn by oxen.<BR> E. गम् to go, ष्ट्रन्. affix, fem.<BR>do. ङीष् and the pen. made long; also गन्त्रा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=236-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गान्दिनी|गांदिनी
गान्दिनी f. (-नी)<BR>	 1. The river Ganges, or the goddess Ganga.<BR>	 2. The<BR>mother of AkRURA.<BR> E. गो paradise, in the accusative case, द who<BR>gives, इनि and ङीप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=236-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गान्दिनीसुत|गांदिनीसुत|गान्दिनीसुतः
गान्दिनीसुत m. (-तः)<BR>	 1. A name of BHISHMA, &c.<BR>	 2. AkRURA.<BR> E. गान्दिनी<BR>GANGA, and सुत a son: see गङ्गासुत.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=236-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गान्धर्ब्ब
गान्धर्ब्ब mfn. (-र्ब्बः-र्ब्बी-र्ब्बं) Relating or belonging to a Gandharba.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-र्ब्बः) A heavenly chorister: see गन्धर्ब्बं n. र्ब्बं 1. Song; singing.<BR>	 2. A<BR>form of marriage, that which require only mutual and amorous<BR>agreement.<BR> E. गन्धर्ब्ब a Gandharba, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=236-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गान्धार|गांधार|गान्धारं|गांधारः|गान्धारः
गान्धार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. One of the seven primary notes of music.<BR>	 2. Minium<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=237-a" target="_blank">Page237-a+ 60</a>]<BR>or red lead.<BR>	 3. A country, (Candahar, between the north of India<BR>and Persia).<BR>	 n. (-रं) Gum myrrh f. (-री)<BR>	 1. The wife of DHRITARASH-<BR>TRA mother of DURYODHANA.<BR>	 2. One of the tutelary female deities of<BR>the Jainas.<BR>	 3. A plant (Hedysarum alhagi.)<BR>	 4. Prickly nightshade.<BR>E. गान्ध the aggregate of गन्ध smell, &c. ऋ to go and अण् affix; the<BR>note being said to be produced by pure and fragrant breath, &c.<BR>गान्धारेय m. (-यः) A name of DURYODHANA, the son of DHRI-<BR>TARASHTRA.<BR> E. गान्धारी the name of the mother of this chief, and<BR>ढक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=236-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गान्धिक|गांधिक|गांधिकः|गान्धिकः
गान्धिक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A scribe, a clerk.<BR>	 2. A vender of perfumes, a per-<BR>fumer.<BR>	 3. A kind of worm, having a strong fetid smell.<BR> E. गन्ध<BR>smell, and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=237-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गामुक|गामुकः
गामुक mfn. (-कः-का or -की-कं) Going, locomotive.<BR> E. गम् to go, उकञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=237-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गाम्भीर्य्य|गाम्भीर्य|गांभीर्य|गांभीर्यं|गाम्भीर्य्यं
गाम्भीर्य्य n. (-र्य्यं)<BR>	 1. Depth, (of water, sound, &c.)<BR>	 2. The deep sound of<BR>the voice of a jaina saint, like distant thunder or the muttering of<BR>clouds.<BR> E. गम्भीर deep, affix ष्यञ् or ज्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=237-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गायक|गायकः
गायक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Singing, one who sings.<BR>	 m. (-कः) A singer.<BR> E. गै<BR>to sing, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=237-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गायत्
गायत् mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्) Singing.<BR> E. गै to sing. affix शतृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=237-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गायत्रिन्
गायत्रिन् m. (-त्री) A tree that yields the resin formerly called Terra<BR>Japonica, (Mimosa catechu;) also गायत्री fem. noun, as below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=237-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गायत्री
गायत्री f. (-त्री)<BR>	 1. A measure of verse in the Vedas, a stanza usually of<BR>twenty-four syllables, variously arranged, but most commonly in<BR>three lines.<BR>	 2. A sacred verse from the Vedas to be recited only men-<BR>tally; this is usually personified and considered as a goddess, the<BR>wife of BRAHMĀ; the metaphorical mother of the three first clas-<BR>ses, in their capacity of twice born, investiture with the sacred and<BR>distinguishing string, &c. being regarded as a new birth; there is<BR>but one Gayatri of the Vedas, but according to the system of the<BR>Tantrikas, a number of mystical verses are called Gayatris; each<BR>deity has one in particular.<BR>	 3. A kind of mimosa, (M. catechu:)<BR>see the preceding, &c.<BR> E. गायन् who sings, and त्रै to preserve, affix-<BR>es क and ङीष्; this applies especially to the mystical verse, the<BR>repetition of which is necessary for salvation; the word is also writ-<BR>ten गायत्त्री.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=237-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गायन|गायनः
गायन mfn. (-नः-नी-नं) Singing, a singer.<BR>	 m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. A singer.<BR>	 2. A<BR>chatterer, a gossip.<BR>	 n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Singing 2. Professing or practising<BR>singing as a livelihood.<BR> E. गै to sing. aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=237-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गारित्र|गारित्रं
गारित्र m. (-त्रः) Rice, grain, corn.<BR> E. ग to swallow, Uṇādi affix<BR>णित्रन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=237-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गारुड|गारुडं|गारुडः
गारुड m. (-डः)<BR>	 1. Gold.<BR>	 2. A Mantra or charm against poison.<BR>	 3. An<BR>emerald.<BR> E. गरुड the vehicle of VIṢṆU, and अण् affix; of or rela-<BR>ting to GARUḌA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=237-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गारुडिक|गारुडिकः
गारुडिक m. (-कः) A charmer, a dealer in antidotes.<BR> E. गारुड the mantra<BR>of GARUḌA, or a charm against venom, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=237-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गारुडी
गारुडी f. (-डी) Hog-weed, (Boerhavia diffusa alata.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=237-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गारुत्मत्
गारुत्मत् n. (-त्) The emerald.<BR> E. गरुत्मत् GARUḌA, and अण् affix; derived<BR>from or relating to GARUḌA; the gem is supposed to be generated<BR>from his voided phlegm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=237-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गार्ग्ग|गार्ग|गार्गः
गार्ग्ग mfn. (-र्ग्गः-र्ग्गी-र्ग्गं) Descended from the sage GARGA.<BR> E. गर्ग्ग, and<BR>अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=237-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गार्ग्गक|गार्गक|गार्गकः
गार्ग्गक n. (-कं) A multitude of the descendents of the saint GARGA. E.<BR>गार्ग्ग a descendant of GARGA, and वुञ् affix of multitude; also with<BR>ठञ्, गार्ग्गिक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=237-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गार्ग्गीपुत्रकायनि|गार्गीपुत्रकायनि
गार्ग्गीपुत्रकायनि m. (-निः) A descendant of the son of GARGI.<BR> E. गार्ग्गी the<BR>wife of the saint GARGA, पुत्र a son, and फिञ् affix, कुक् augment;<BR>also without the augment गार्ग्गीपुत्रायनि, or with इञ् affix, गार्ग्गीपुत्रि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=237-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गार्ग्ग्य
गार्ग्ग्य mfn. (-र्ग्ग्यः-र्ग्ग्यी-र्ग्ग्यं) Descended from the GARGA, son, daughter,<BR>&c.<BR> E. गर्ग्ग and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=237-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गार्द्ध
गार्द्ध mfn. (-र्द्धः-र्द्धी-र्द्धं)<BR>	 1. Derived from a vulture.<BR>	 2. Greedy.<BR>	 m. (-र्द्धः)<BR>	 1.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=237-b" target="_blank">Page237-b+ 60</a>]<BR>Desire, greediness, cupidity.<BR>	 2. An arrow.<BR> E. गृध greedy, affix अण्<BR>or गृध्र with अण् affix, and र rejected optionally.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=237-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गार्द्धपक्षं|गार्धपक्ष|गार्द्धपक्षः
गार्द्धपक्षं m. (-क्षः) An arrow.<BR> E. गार्द्ध and पक्ष a wing; formed with vulture's<BR>feathers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=237-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गार्द्धपत्र
गार्द्धपत्र m. (-त्रः) An arrow. E. As before, पत्र a leaf, a wing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=237-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गार्द्ध्य
गार्द्ध्य n. (-र्द्ध्यं)<BR>	 1. Greediness.<BR>	 2. Desire.<BR> E. गृध्र greedy, यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=237-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गार्द्ध्र
गार्द्ध्र mfn. (-र्द्ध्रः-र्द्ध्री-र्द्ध्रं) Derived from a vulture,<BR> E. गृद्ध्र and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=237-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गार्द्ध्रपक्ष
गार्द्ध्रपक्ष m. (-क्षः) An arrow.<BR> E. गार्द्ध्र, and पक्ष a wing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=237-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गार्भ
गार्भ mfn. (-र्भः-र्भी-र्भं)<BR>	 1. Uterine, fœtal.<BR>	 2. Relating to conception, (any<BR>act or ceremony, &c.)<BR> E. गर्भ and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=237-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गार्भिक
गार्भिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>	 1. Fœtal, uterine.<BR>	 2. Relating to or connected<BR>with gestation or the fœtus in utero.<BR> E. गर्भ and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=237-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गार्भिण|गार्भिणं
गार्भिण n. (-णं) A number of pregnant woman.<BR> E. गर्भिणी a pregnant we-<BR>man, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=237-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गार्भिण्य|गार्भिण्यं
गार्भिण्य n. (-ण्यं) An assembly of pregnant women.<BR> E. गर्भिणी as above,<BR>and यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=237-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गार्हपत्य|गार्हपत्यः
गार्हपत्य m. (-त्यः) A sacred fire perpetually maintained by a household-<BR>er, received from his father, and transmitted to his descendants,<BR>and from which fires for sacrificial purposes are lighted.<BR> E. गृहपति a<BR>householder, (from गृह a house, and पति master,) and य्य referen-<BR>tial aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=237-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गार्हस्थ्य|गार्हस्थ्यं
गार्हस्थ्य n. (-स्थ्यं) The order or estate of a householder.<BR> E. गृहस्थ and यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=237-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गाल|गालः
गाल m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. Flowing, liquefying.<BR>	 2. Flowing, dropping.<BR>	 3. A flux.<BR>E. गल् to flow, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=237-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गालन|गालनं
गालन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Straining fluids.<BR>	 2. Fusing, liquefying, &c.<BR> E. गल् to<BR>flow, causal form, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=237-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गालव|गालवः
गालव m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. A tree, the bark of which is used in dying, Lodh,<BR>(Symplocus racemosa, Rox.)<BR>	 2. A pale species of the same: see<BR>लोध्र.<BR>	 3. A kind of ebony; also केन्दुक, (Diospyros glutinosa.)<BR>	 4. A<BR>particular Muni or saint, a disciple of VISWAMITRA.<BR> E. गाल flux,<BR>and व what prevents; referring to the astringent qualities of the<BR>Lodh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=237-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गालि|गालिः
गालि m. (-लिः) A curse, execration or imprecation.<BR> E. गल् in the causal<BR>from to cause to drop, and इन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=237-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गालित|गालितः
गालित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Melted, fused.<BR>	 2. Strained.<BR>	 3. Distilled, drop-<BR>ped.<BR> E. गल् to drop, causal form, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=237-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गालिन्
गालिन् mfn. (-ली-लिनी-लि)<BR>	 1. Fusing, liquefying.<BR>	 2. Distilling.<BR>	 3. Abusive,<BR>abusing.<BR>	 f. (-नी) A particular gesticulation or Mudra.<BR> E. गल to<BR>flow, causal form, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=237-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गालोड्य|गालोड्यं
गालोड्य n. (-ड्यं) The seed of the lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=237-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गाह|गाहः
गाह(ऊ)गाहू r. 1st cl. (गाहते)<BR>	 1. To churn, to stir or agitate.<BR>	 2. To<BR>penetrate.<BR>	 3. To destroy. With अव or वि prefixed, To bathe, to<BR>perform ablutions. With वि, to shake, to agitate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=237-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गाहित
गाहित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Shaking, trembling.<BR>	 2. Destroyed.<BR>	 3. Plunged<BR>into, immersed.<BR> E. गाह् to agitate, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=237-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गाहितृ
गाहितृ mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ)<BR>	 1. Shaking, agitating.<BR>	 2. Destroying, a destroyer.<BR>3. One who plunges into water, bathes, dives, &c.<BR> E. गाह् to agitate,<BR>तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=237-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गिर्
गिर् f. (-गोः)<BR>	 1. Speech, speaking.<BR>	 2. A name of SARASWATI the goddess<BR>of speech.<BR>	 3. Fame, celebrity.<BR> E. गॄ to sound, affix क्विप्, ऋ is<BR>changed to इर्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=237-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गिरण
गिरण n. (-णं) Swallowing.<BR> E. गॄ to swallow, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=237-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गिरा
गिरा f. (-रा) Speech. गॄ to sound, क and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=237-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गिरि|गिरिः
गिरि mfn. (-रिः-रिः-रि) Venerable, respectable worshipful.<BR>	 m. (-रिः)<BR>	 1. A<BR>mountain, a hill.<BR>	 2. A wooden ball with which children play.<BR>	 3. A.<BR>disease of the eyes.<BR>	 f. (-रिः)<BR>	 1. Swallowing.<BR>	 2. A small rat, a mouse.<BR>3. A title given to one order of the Dasnami Gosains.<BR> E. गॄ to<BR>swallow, &c. इ Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=237-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गिरिकण्टक|गिरिकंटक|गिरिकण्टकः
गिरिकण्टक m. (-कः) INDRA'S thunderbolt.<BR> E. गिरि a mountain, and कण्टक<BR>a thorn, tearing or splitting rocks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=237-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गिरिकदम्ब|गिरिकदंब|गिरिकदम्बः
गिरिकदम्ब m. (-म्बः) A species of Kadamba, (Nauclea cadamba.)<BR> E. गिरि,<BR>and कदम्ब the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=238-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गिरिकन्दर|गिरिकंदर|गिरिकन्दरः
गिरिकन्दर m. (-रः) A cave, a cavern.<BR> E. गिरि, and कन्दर a cave.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=238-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गिरिकदली
गिरिकदली f. (-ली) A species of plantain growing in hilly countries. E.<BR>गिरि, and कदली a plantain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=238-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गिरिकर्णिका|गिरिकर्ण्णिका
गिरिकर्णिका f. (-का) The earth.<BR> E. गिरि a mountain, and कर्ण an ear,<BR>affixes कन् and टाप्; the mountain-eared.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=238-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गिरिकर्णी|गिरिकर्ण्णी
गिरिकर्णी f. (-र्णी)<BR>	 1. A plant, commonly Jawasa, (Hedysarum alhaji.)<BR>2. A different plant, (Clitoria ternatea:) see अपराजिता.<BR> E. गिरि a<BR>mouse, and कर्णी an ear, affix ङीष्, the mouse-ear-leaved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=238-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गिरिका
गिरिका f. (-का) A small rat, a mouse.<BR> E. कन् added to गिरि the<BR>same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=238-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गिरिकाण|गिरिकाणः
गिरिकाण m. (-णः) A blind or one-eyed man, one blind from a particular<BR>disease.<BR> E. गिरि as above, and काण one-eyed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=238-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गिरिगुड|गिरिगुडः
गिरिगुड m. (-डः) A ball for playing with.<BR> E. गिरि, and गुड, each mean-<BR>ing the same thing, a ball.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=238-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गिरिज|गिरिजं|गिरिजः
गिरिज mfn. (-जः-जा-जं) Mountain-born, mountaineer. &c.<BR>	 m. (-जः) The<BR>Mahuwa tree, (Bassia.)<BR>	 f. (-जा)<BR>	 1. A name of goddes PARVATI, as<BR>the daughter of the personified HIMALAYA mountain 2. The Shad-<BR>dock or pumplemouce, (Citrus decumana.)<BR>	 3. A plant considered as<BR>a white species of Rasna: see राम्ना.<BR>	 4. The hill plantain.<BR>	 5. Jas-<BR>mine.<BR>	 6. A pebble, a small stone.<BR>	 n. (-जं)<BR>	 1. Talc.<BR>	 2. Benzoin or gum<BR>benjamin; it is also confounded with styrax, another gum resin.<BR>	 3.<BR>Bitumen.<BR>	 4. Iron.<BR> E. गिरि, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=238-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गिरिजामल|गिरिजामलं
गिरिजामल n. (-लं) Talc.<BR> E. गिरिज mountain-born, and अमल clear, clean;<BR>also गिरिज, and अमल severally.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=238-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गिरिज्वर|गिरिज्वरः
गिरिज्वर m. (-रः) The thunderbolt.<BR> E. गिरि a mountain, and ज्वर what<BR>burns.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=238-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गिरित|गिरितः
गिरित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Eaten.<BR>	 2. Swallowed.<BR> E. गॄ to swallow, affix क्त;<BR>also गिलित.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=238-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गिरिदुर्ग
गिरिदुर्ग n. (-र्गं) A hill fort or any stronghold amongst mountains. E.<BR>गिरि, and दुर्ग a place of difficult access.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=238-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गिरिधातु|गिरिधातुः
गिरिधातु m. (-तुः) Red chalk.<BR> E. गिरि, and धातु a mineral.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=238-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गिरिध्वज
गिरिध्वज m. (-जः) A thunderbolt.<BR> E. गिरि, and ध्वज a banner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=238-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गिरिपुष्पक|गिरिपुष्पकं
गिरिपुष्पक n. (-कं) Bitumen,<BR> E. गिरि, and पुष्प a flower; कन् affix of simili-<BR>tude.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=238-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गिरिपृष्ठ|गिरिपृष्ठः
गिरिपृष्ठ n. (-ष्ठं) The top of a hill.<BR> E. गिरि, and पृष्ठ back.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=238-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गिरिप्रिय
गिरिप्रिय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Fond of or frequenting mountains.<BR>	 f. (-या) The<BR>Yak.<BR> E. गिरि, and प्रिय fond of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=238-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गिरिभिद्
गिरिभिद् m. (-भित्) A plant, (Plectranthus scutellaroides.)<BR> E. गिरि, and<BR>भिद् what breaks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=238-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गिरिभू
गिरिभू mfn. (-भूः-भूः-भु) Mountaineer, mountain-born.<BR>	 f. (-भूः) PARVATI.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-भूः) A small stone.<BR> E. गिरि, and भू born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=238-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गिरिमल्लिका
गिरिमल्लिका f. (-का) A plant, (Echites antidysenterica:) see कुटज.<BR> E. गिरि<BR>a mountain, and मल्ली a jasmine, कन् affix of similitude.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=238-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गिरिमान|गिरिमानः
गिरिमान m. (-नः) A large and powerful elephant.<BR> E. गिरि a mountain,<BR>and मान measure, like a mountain in bulk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=238-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गिरिमृत्
गिरिमृत् f. (-मृत्)<BR>	 1. Red chalk.<BR>	 2. Mountain-soil.<BR> E. गिरि a mountain,<BR>and मृत् clay, earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=238-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गिरिमृद्भव|गिरिमृद्भवं
गिरिमृद्भव n. (-वं) Red chalk. गिरिमृत्, and भव produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=238-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गिरिमेद|गिरिमेदः
गिरिमेद m. (-दः) A foetid mimosa.<BR> E. गिरि, and मेद filth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=238-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गिरियक|गिरियकः
गिरियक m. (-कः) A ball for playing with.<BR> E. गिरि a ball, घ pleonastic affix,<BR>and कन् added; also गिरियाक the pen. being lengthened.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=238-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गिरियाक|गिरियाकः
गिरियाक m. (-कः) A ball; see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=238-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गिरिवासिन्
गिरिवासिन् mfn. (-सी-सिनी-सि) Living in the mountains, being or pro-<BR>duced in them.<BR>	 m. (-सी) A large kind of Arum.<BR> E. गिरि, and वासिन्<BR>what abides.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=238-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गिरिश|गिरिशः
गिरिश m. (-शः) A name of ŚIVA.<BR> E. गिरि a mountain, and शीञ् to sleep,<BR>affix ड; inhabiting mount Kailasa, or frequenting the Himālaya<BR>range.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=238-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गिरिशालिनी
गिरिशालिनी f. (-नी) A plant, (Clitoria ternatea.)<BR> E. गिरि, and शालिनी<BR>what grows in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=238-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गिरिशृङ्ग|गिरिशृंग|गिरिशृङ्गः
गिरिशृङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>	 1. A name of GANESA.<BR>	 2. A peak of a mountain. E.<BR>गिरि a mount, and शृङ्ग a peak, alluding to his bulk, or गिरि the<BR>mountain Kailasa, and शृङ्ग a peak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=238-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गिरिसार|गिरिसारः
गिरिसार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. The Malaya mountains, situated in the south of<BR>India.<BR>	 2. Iron.<BR>	 3. Tin.<BR> E. गिरि a mountain, and सार essence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=238-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गिरिसुता
गिरिसुता f. (-ता) PARVATI.<BR> E. गिरि Himālaya, and सुता daughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=238-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गिरीश|गिरीशः
गिरीश m. (-शः)<BR>	 1. A name of ŚIVA.<BR>	 2. A name of Himālaya, the snowy<BR>mountains on the north of Hindustan, or the range personified 3.<BR>A name of VṚHASPATI.<BR> E. गिरि a mountain, (or in the last mean-<BR>ing, गिर् speech,) and ईश lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=238-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गिल|गिलः
गिल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Who or what swallows.<BR>	 m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. The citron.<BR>2. Swallowing.<BR> E. गॄ to swallow, affix क, and र changed to ल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=238-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गिलग्राह|गिलग्राहः
गिलग्राह m. (-हः) A shark.<BR> E. गिल, and ग्राह who seizes, who swallows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=238-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गिलत्|गिलन्त्
गिलत् mfn. (-लन्-लन्ती-लत्) Swallowing, eating, devouring.<BR> E. गै to swal-<BR>low, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=238-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गिलन|गिलनं
गिलन n. (-नं) Swallowing; also गिरण. E. As before; र changed to ल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=238-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गिलि|गिलिः
गिलि f. (-लिः)<BR>	 1. Swallowing.<BR>	 2. Eating. E. See गिरि, र being changed<BR>to ल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=238-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गिलित|गिलितं
गिलित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Eaten.<BR>	 2. Swallowed. गॄ to swallow, affix क्त,<BR>गिरित, and र changed to ल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=238-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गिष्ण|गिष्णः
गिष्ण m. (-ष्णः)<BR>	 1. A Brahman versed in the Sama Veda, a chanter of<BR>that Veda, which is always to be so recited.<BR>	 2. An actor, a profes-<BR>sional singer.<BR> E. गै to sing, भिष्ण Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=238-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गीत|गीतं
गीत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Sung, chanted, sounded, &c.<BR>	 f. (-ता) A name often<BR>applied to books, as the Siva Gita, Rama Gita, Gita Govinda,<BR>Bhagavad Gita, which last is also often called Gita only.<BR>	 n. (-तं)<BR>Singing, song either general or particular.<BR> E. गॄ to sing, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=238-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गीतमोदिन्
गीतमोदिन् m. (-दी) A Kinnara or celestial chorister.<BR> E. गीत song or sing-<BR>ing, and मोदिन् who delights.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=238-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गीति|गीतिः
गीति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Sing, singing, 2. A kind of poetical metre, a form of<BR>the Aryya metre, in which the stanza consists of four lines of twelve<BR>and eighteen syllabic instants alternately.<BR> E. गै to sing, affix क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=238-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गीरथ|गीरथः
गीरथ m. (-थः) A name of VṚHASPATI.<BR> E. गी speech, and रथ a car, the<BR>conveyer of words.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=238-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गीर्ण|गीर्णः|गीर्ण्ण
गीर्ण mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-र्णं)<BR>	 1. Praised.<BR>	 2. Swallowed.<BR> E. गॄ to swallow or make<BR>known, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=238-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गीर्णि|गीर्णिः|गीर्ण्णि
गीर्णि f. (-र्णिः)<BR>	 1. Swallowing.<BR>	 2. Fame, celebrity.<BR>	 3. Praise, applause<BR>E. गृ to swallow, &c. affix क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=238-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गीर्देवी
गीर्देवी f. (-वी) The goddess SARASWATI.<BR> E. गी speech, and देवी a goddess,<BR>the goddess of language.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=238-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गीर्व्वाण|गीर्वाण|गीर्वाणः|गीर्व्वाणः
गीर्व्वाण m. (-णः) A deity, a god.<BR> E. गीः speech, and वाण an arrow or wea-<BR>pon in general, whose fiat or word is his weapon; or गी with वन<BR>to desire, affix अण्, desiring hymns, prayers, &c. it is also written<BR>गीर्ब्बाण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=238-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गीष्पति|गीष्पतिः
गीष्पति m. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. A name of VṚHASPATI, regent of JUPITER and<BR>preceptor of the gods.<BR>	 2. A Pandit or learned teacher.<BR> E. गिर् speech,<BR>in the nominative case, गीः and पति master, Visarga becomes स<BR>and स is here changed irregularly to ष the compound however is<BR>sometimes written differently, thus गीःपति, गीर्पति or गीस्पति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=238-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गु
गु(ओ, शि) r. 6th cl. (गुवति) To stool, to void excrement. (ङ) गुङ् r. 1st<BR>cl. (गवते) To sound inarticulately.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=238-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुग्गुल|गुग्गुलः
गुग्गुल m. (-लः) A gum resin: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=238-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुग्गुलु|गुग्गुलुः
गुग्गुलु m. (-लुः)<BR>	 1. A fragrant gum resin, Bdellium or the exudation of<BR>the Amyris agallochum.<BR>	 2. A species of morunga, (M. hyperanthe-<BR>ra.)<BR> E. गुज् (here said to mean) disease, and गुड to perfume, affixes<BR>क and उ, ड change to ल; also गुग्गुल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=238-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुच्छ|गुच्छः|गुछ
गुच्छ m. (-च्छः)<BR>	 1. A cluster of blossoms.<BR>	 2. A clump of grass.<BR>	 3. A neck-<BR>lace of thirty-two strings.<BR>	 4. A pearl necklace.<BR>	 5. A peacock's<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=239-a" target="_blank">Page239-a+ 60</a>]<BR>plumage or bundle of peacock's feathers.<BR>	 6. A bundle.<BR>	 f. (-च्छी) A<BR>species of Bonduz: see करञ्ज<BR> E. गु to sound, च्छ affix, or गुध् to play,<BR>and च्छक् affix, where bees, &c. sport.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=238-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुच्छक|गुच्छकं|गुच्छकः
गुच्छक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A cluster of blossoms.<BR>	 2. A clump of grass.<BR>	 3. A kind<BR>of necklace.<BR>	 4. A peacock's plumage, a bundle of peacock's feathers.<BR>E. कन् added to the preceding; also गुत्सक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=239-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुच्छपत्र|गुच्छपत्रः
गुच्छपत्र m. (-त्रः) The palm tree.<BR> E. गुच्छ a cluster, and पत्र a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=239-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुच्छफला
गुच्छफला f. (-ला)<BR>	 1. The plantain.<BR>	 2. The vine.<BR> E. गुच्छ a cluster, and फला<BR>fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=239-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुच्छार्द्ध
गुच्छार्द्ध m. (-र्द्धः) A necklace of thirty-four strings.<BR> E. गुच्छ a large neck-<BR>lace, and अर्द्ध a part; also गुत्सार्द्ध.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=239-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुच्छाल|गुच्छालः
गुच्छाल m. (-लः) A species of grass. (Andropogon schœnanthus.)<BR> E. गुच्छ<BR>and अल to fit for, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=239-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुज
गुज r. 1st cl. (गोजति) or (शि) r. 6th cl. (गुजति) or (इ) गुजि r. 1st cl. (गुञ्जति)<BR>To sound, to sound inarticulately, to buz, to hum, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=239-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुज्जरी
गुज्जरी f. (-री) One of the Rāgiṇīs, perhaps more correctly गुर्ज्जरी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=239-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुञ्ज|गुंज|गुंजः|गुञ्जः
गुञ्ज m. (-ञ्जः) A cluster of blossoms, a nosegay.<BR>	 f. (-ञ्जा)<BR>	 1. A small<BR>shrub, (Abrus precatorius,) bearing a red and black berry, which<BR>forms the smallest of the jeweller's weights.<BR>	 2. The berry which<BR>averages about 15-16 grains troy, or the artificial weight called by<BR>this name, weighing about 23. 16 grains: see रक्तिका &c.<BR>	 3. A kettle<BR>drum.<BR>	 4. A low murmuring sound.<BR>	 5. A tavern.<BR>	 6. Reflection,<BR>meditation.<BR> E. गुजि to sound, affix क where the bees buz.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=239-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुञ्जकृत्|गुंजकृत्
गुञ्जकृत् m. (-त्) A large black bee.<BR> E. गुञ्ज a low tone, and कृत् who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=239-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुञ्जत्
गुञ्जत् mfn. (-ञ्जन्-ञ्जन्ती-ञ्जत्) Buzzing, humming, making a low murmuring<BR>sound.<BR> E. गुजि to sound, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=239-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुञ्जन|गुंजन|गुंजनं|गुञ्जनं
गुञ्जन n. (-नं) Sounding low and deep, as buzzing, murmuring, &c. E.<BR>गुजि to sound, and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=239-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुञ्जिका|गुंजिका
गुञ्जिका f. (-का) The Ratti or Gunja seed, considered as equal to three<BR>barley-corns: see गुञ्जा<BR> E. गुञ्जा and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=239-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुञ्जित|गुंजित|गुंजितं|गुञ्जितं
गुञ्जित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Uttered in a low tone, murmured, &c.<BR>	 n. (-तं)<BR>Sounding, murmuring, buzzing.<BR> E. गुजि and क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=239-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुटिका
गुटिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. A pill, a bolus, any small globe or ball.<BR>	 2. A small<BR>pustule.<BR>	 3. The cocoon of the silk worm.<BR> E. गुड to surround, affix<BR>क्वुन्, ड changed to ट.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=239-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुठ
गुठ (इ) गुठि r. 10th cl. (गुण्ठयति) To surround, to envelope or enclose:<BR>with अव, to veil, to screen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=239-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुड|गुडः
गुड(शि) r. 6th cl. (गुडति) To defend, to guard or preserve. (इ) गुडि<BR>r. 1st and 10th cls. (गुण्डति गुण्डयति)<BR>	 1. To surround, to enclose, 2.<BR>To pound, to grind, to reduce to powder.<BR>	 3. (According to some<BR>authorities,) To preserve.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=239-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुड|गुडः
गुड mfn. (-डः-डा-डं) Round, globular, m. (-डः)<BR>	 1. A globe or ball.<BR>	 2.<BR>Treacle, molasses, the first thickening of the juice of the cane by<BR>boiling.<BR>	 3. An elephant's trappings or armour.<BR>	 4. A mouthful.<BR>	 f. (-डा)<BR>1. A plant, (Euphorbia tirucalli:) see स्नुही 2. Powder, pounded<BR>substance.<BR> E. गुङ् to sound, affix ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=239-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुडक|गुडकः
गुडक m. (-कः) A conserve, a drug prepared with treacle.<BR>	 n. (-कं) Treacle<BR>E. गुड and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=239-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुडकरी
गुडकरी f. (-री) One of the female personifications of the musical modes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=239-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुडची
गुडची f. (-ची) A plant, (Menispermum glabrum:) see गुडुची.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=239-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुडतृण|गुडतृणं
गुडतृण n. (-णं) Sugar cane.<BR> E. गुड raw sugar, and तृण grass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=239-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुडत्वच्
गुडत्वच् n. (-त्वक्) The aromatic bark of the Laurus cassia.<BR> E. गुड sugar,<BR>and त्वच् skin, bark, sweet-bark; also गुडत्वच.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=239-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुडत्वच|गुडत्वचं
गुडत्वच n. (-चं)<BR>	 1. Mace.<BR>	 2. Cassia bark.<BR> E. गुड sugar, sweet as sugar, त्वच्<BR>bark, and अच added in this form of the compound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=239-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुडदारु|गुडदारुः
गुडदारु m. (-रुः) Sugar cane.<BR> E. गुड raw sugar, and दारु wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=239-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुडधेनु|गुडधेनुः
गुडधेनु f. (-नुः) Sugar piled up for distribution at certain religious rites.<BR>E. गुड and धेनु a cow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=239-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुडपिष्ट
गुडपिष्ट n. (-ष्टं) A sort of sweetmeat, flour or rice and sugar, ground and<BR>boiled together.<BR> E. गुड and पिष्ट ground.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=239-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुडपुष्प|गुडपुष्पः
गुडपुष्प m. (-ष्पः) A kind of bassia, (B. latifolia.)<BR> E. गुड sugar, and पुष्प<BR>flower; the flowers being full of saccharine matter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=239-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुडफल|गुडफलः
गुडफल m. (-लः) A tree, commonly Pilu, (Careya arborea, &c.) see पीलु<BR>E. गुड and फल fruit, the fruit yielding Gur or saccharine matter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=239-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुडमिश्र
गुडमिश्र n. (-श्रं) A sort of cake or sweetmeat, flour or rice and coarse<BR>sugar ground and boiled together.<BR> E. गुड, and मिश्र mixed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=239-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुडमूल|गुडमूलः
गुडमूल m. (-लः) A kind of amaranth, (A. polygamus;) also अल्पमारिष.<BR>E. गुड, and मूल root; having a root as sweet as Gur.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=239-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुडल|गुडलं
गुडल n. (-लं) A spirituous liquor distilled from molasses, a sort of rum.<BR>E. गुड sugar, and ल what requires.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=239-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुडशर्क्करा|गुडशर्करा
गुडशर्क्करा f. (-रा) Sugar, refined sugar.<BR> E. गुड molasses, and शर्क्करा sugar or sand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=239-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुडशिग्रु|गुडशिग्रुः
गुडशिग्रु m. (-ग्रुः) A red sort of morunga: see शोभाञ्जन.<BR> E. गुड sugar, शिग्रु<BR>morunga.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=239-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुडाका
गुडाका f. (-का) Sloth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=239-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुडाकेश|गुडाकेशः
गुडाकेश m. (-शः)<BR>	 1. A name of ŚIVA.<BR>	 2. A title of ARJUNA.<BR> E. गुडा Eup-<BR>horbia, and केश the hair; the hair forming matted locks, resem-<BR>bling in shape the leaves of the Euphorbia: again, गुडिका sloth,<BR>and ईश paramount; subduing indolence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=239-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुडाशय|गुडाशयः
गुडाशय m. (-यः) A mountain Pilu: see गुडफल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=239-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुडिका
गुडिका f. (-का) A pill, a bolus.<BR> E. गुड to be round, वुन aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=239-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुडुची
गुडुची f. (-ची) A plant: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=239-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुडूची
गुडूची f. (-ची) A creeper, commonly called Guricha, (Menisperum glab-<BR>rum.)<BR> E. गुड to preserve, (from disease,) ऊचट् affix; also with pen.<BR>vowel short गुडुची.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=239-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुडेर|गुडेरः
गुडेर m. (-रः) A mouthful.<BR> E. गुड to surround, एरक् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=239-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुडेरक|गुडेरकः
गुडेरक m. (-कः) A mouthful.<BR> E. गुड to preserve, एरक् affix, and कन् add-<BR>ed; also गुडेर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=239-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुडोद्भवा
गुडोद्भवा f. (-वा) Sugar.<BR> E. गुड, and उद्भव produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=239-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुडौदन
गुडौदन n. (-नं) Boiled rice and coarse sugar.<BR> E. गुड, and ओदन rice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=239-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुण|गुणः
गुण r. 10th cl. (गुणयति)<BR>	 1. To invite.<BR>	 2. To advise.<BR>	 3. To multiply.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=239-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुण|गुणः
गुण m. (-णः)<BR>	 1. A quality, attribute, or property in general.<BR>	 2. A pro-<BR>perty of all created things; three are particularized, the Satwa,<BR>Raja and Tama, or principles of truth or existence, passion or foul-<BR>ness, and darkness or ignorance.<BR>	 3. A means of defence, one of six<BR>expedients in government, as, peace, war, a march, a halt, a stra-<BR>tagem, and recourse to protection: see सन्धि &c.<BR>	 4. Form, shape, &c.<BR>or property of the body.<BR>	 5. Knowledge, ignorance, &c. or quality<BR>of the mind.<BR>	 6. Heroism, valor, &c.<BR>	 7. White, black, &c. or the<BR>attributes of color.<BR>	 8. An organ of sense.<BR>	 9. A string in general.<BR>	 10.<BR>A bow-string.<BR>	 11. Abandoning, leaving.<BR>	 12. A cook.<BR>	 13. A name<BR>of Bhima.<BR>	 14. Secondary subordinate.<BR>	 15. Excellence, merit, free-<BR>dom from fault or blemish.<BR>	 16. (In arithmetic,) The given coeffici-<BR>ent of any number.<BR>	 17. (In geometry,) The chord of an arc.<BR>	 18.<BR>(In grammar,) The substitution of e, o, ar and al for i, u, ri, lri.<BR>	 19.<BR>(In rhetoric,) Consistency of plan, elegance of expression, &c. as<BR>the merits of a composition.<BR>	 20. In composition with numerals,<BR>multiplication, as द्विगुण twice, त्रिगुण thrice.<BR>	 f. (-णा) A plant of the<BR>fibers of which bow-strings are made: see मूर्व्वा.<BR> E. गुण to address or<BR>advice, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=239-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुणक|गुणकः
गुणक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A numerator, reckoner.<BR>	 2. (In arithmetic,) The mul-<BR>tiplier.<BR> E. गुण to count, क्कुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=239-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुणकार|गुणकारः
गुणकार mfn. (-रः-री-रं) Who counts, &c.<BR>	 m. (-रः) A name of BHIMASENA<BR>E. गुण and कार who makes; BHIMA performed the duties of a cook<BR>at the time when all the Pandava princes become servants to<BR>VIRAT.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=239-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुणगान
गुणगान n. (-नं) Panegyric, praise.<BR> E. गुण, and गान singing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=239-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुणग्रहण
गुणग्रहण n. (-णं) Acknowledging or appreciating merit.<BR> E. गुण, and<BR>ग्रहण taking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=239-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुणग्राहिन्
गुणग्राहिन् mfn. (-ही-हिनी-हि) Who judges or appreciates good qualities,<BR>E. गुण and ग्राहिन् who seizes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=239-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुणगृह्य
गुणगृह्य mfn. (-ह्यः-ह्या-ह्यं)<BR>	 1. Suited to good qualities.<BR>	 2. Admiring or<BR>attached to merit.<BR> E. गुण and गृह्य to be caught by.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=240-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुणघातिन्
गुणघातिन् mfn. (-ती-तिनी-ति) A detractor, a calumniator, envious, cen-<BR>sorious.<BR> E. गुण and घातिन् who destroys.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=240-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुणज्ञ|गुणज्ञः
गुणज्ञ mfn. (-ज्ञः-ज्ञा-ज्ञं) One who knows how to appreciate men or thing,<BR>knowing or judging of their merits.<BR> E. गुण, and ज्ञ who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=240-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुणतस्
गुणतस् ind.<BR>	 1. According to property or quality.<BR>	 2. According to desert.<BR>E. गुण, and तसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=240-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुणता
गुणता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Excellence, the possession of good qualities.<BR>	 2. Subs-<BR>tantiality, possession of attributes or qualities in general.<BR>	 3.<BR>Multiplication.<BR> E. गुण and तल् affix; also with त्व affix गुणत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=240-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुणत्रय
गुणत्रय n. (-यं) The three properties of nature; purity, passion, and<BR>darkness.<BR> E. गुण and त्रय triple; also गुणत्रितयं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=240-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुणदोषपरीक्षण
गुणदोषपरीक्षण n. (-णं) Test or investigation of merits and faults.<BR> E. गुण,<BR>दोष fault, परीक्षण trying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=240-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुणधर्म्म|गुणधर्म|गुणधर्मः
गुणधर्म्म m. (-र्म्मः) The virtue incident to the possession of certain<BR>qualities, as clemency is the virtue of royalty, &c.<BR> E. गुण a<BR>property, and धर्म्म virtue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=240-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुणन|गुणनं
गुणन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Describing, relating to qualities.<BR>	 2. Enumerating.<BR>	 3.<BR>Mulitiplication.<BR> E. गुण to number, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=240-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुणनिका
गुणनिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. Dance, the science or profession of dancing, acting<BR>&c.<BR>	 2. Determining the reading of a manuscript, &c.<BR>	 3. A cypher.<BR>4. The prologue or introduction to a drama. A necklace.<BR> E. कन्<BR>added to गुणनी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=240-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुणनी
गुणनी f. (-नी) Examining books, studying, collating, and correcting<BR>copies, &c.<BR> E. गुण to advise, affix ल्यट् and ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=240-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुणनीय|गुणनीयः
गुणनीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>	 1. To be advised.<BR>	 2. To be multiplied.<BR>	 3. To be<BR>enumerated.<BR>	 m. (-यः) Practice, practising any thing, but especially<BR>science or study.<BR>	 n. (-यं) The multiplicand.<BR> E. गुण to advise, &c.<BR>अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=240-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुणपूग
गुणपूग n. (-गं) Great merit.<BR> E. गुण, and पूग a head.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=240-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुणप्रकर्ष|गुणप्रकर्षः
गुणप्रकर्ष m. (-र्षः) Great merit, excellence.<BR> E. गुण and प्रकर्ष eminence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=240-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुणप्रिय
गुणप्रिय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Attached to merit, fond of excellence. E. and गुण,<BR>and प्रिय fond of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=240-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुणभ्रंश|गुणभ्रंशः
गुणभ्रंश m. (-शः) The loss of all good qualities.<BR> E. गुण good property,<BR>and भ्रंश fall, loss.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=240-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुणमय
गुणमय mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>	 1. Endowed with consisting of properties.<BR>	 2.<BR>Possessed of merit.<BR> E. गुण, and मयट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=240-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुणमहत्
गुणमहत् n. (-हत्) Great merit, superior qualities.<BR> E. गुण, and महत् great.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=240-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुणयुक्त
गुणयुक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं) Having virtues or properties.<BR> E. गुण, and युक्त<BR>joined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=240-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुणलक्षण
गुणलक्षण n. (-णं) Mark or indication of internal property.<BR> E. गुण, and<BR>लक्षण mark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=240-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुणलयनिका
गुणलयनिका f. (-का) A tent.<BR> E. गुण rope, ली to bind, ल्युट् and ङीप् affix,<BR>with कन् added; also गुणलयनी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=240-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुणलुब्ध
गुणलुब्ध mfn. (-ब्धः-ब्धा-ब्धं) Desirous of merit, attached to excellence. E.<BR>गुण, and लुब्ध covetous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=240-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुणवत्|गुणवन्त्
गुणवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>	 1. Possessing attributes.<BR>	 2. Endowed with<BR>good qualities.<BR>	 3. Tied, bound, &c.<BR> E. गुण quality, and मतुप् poss.<BR>aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=240-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुणवत्तम
गुणवत्तम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं) Excellent.<BR> E. गुणवन् and तमप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=240-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुणवत्तर
गुणवत्तर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Excellent.<BR> E. गुणवत् and तरप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=240-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुणवत्ता
गुणवत्ता f. (-त्ता) Excellence.<BR> E. गुणवत् and तल् affix; also with त्त्व, गुणवत्त्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=240-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुणवाचक|गुणवाचकः
गुणवाचक n. (-कं) An adjective or attributive noun.<BR> E. गुण, and वाचक a<BR>word.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=240-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुणवैशेष्य
गुणवैशेष्य n. (-ष्यं) Preeminence of merit or of any property.<BR> E. गुण, and<BR>वैशेष्य superiority.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=240-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुणवृक्षक|गुणवृक्षकः
गुणवृक्षक m. (-कः) A mast.<BR> E. गुण a rope, and वृक्ष a tree, कन् affix simi-<BR>litude; also गुणवृक्षः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=240-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुणश्लाघा
गुणश्लाघा f. (-घा) Praise, encomium.<BR> E. गुण, and श्लाघा praise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=240-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुणसम्पद्|गुणसंपद्
गुणसम्पद् f. (-पत् or -पद्) Great merit.<BR> E. गुण, and सम्पद् wealth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=240-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुणसङ्ग|गुणसंग|गुणसंगः
गुणसङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः) Association with properties or qualities.<BR> E. गुण, and सङ्ग<BR>combination.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=240-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुणसङ्ग्रह|गुणसंग्रह|गुणसंग्रहः
गुणसङ्ग्रह m. (-हः) A collection of merits or properties.<BR> E. गुण, and सङ्ग्रह<BR>collection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=240-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुणसागर|गुणसागरः
गुणसागर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Endowed with all good qualities.<BR>	 m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A<BR>name of BRAHMĀ.<BR>	 2. A form of BUDDHA, a Bauddha.<BR> E. गुण excell-<BR>ence, and सागर the ocean; an ocean of desert.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=240-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुणस्तुति|गुणस्तुतिः
गुणस्तुति f. (-तिः) Panegyric, encomium.<BR> E. गुण, and स्तुति praise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=240-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुणहीन
गुणहीन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>	 1. Void of merit.<BR>	 2. Free from properties.<BR> E. गुण,<BR>and हीन void of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=240-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुणाकर|गुणाकरः
गुणाकर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Possessing all excellences.<BR>	 m. (-रः) A name of<BR>BUDDHA the founder of the Bauddha sect.<BR> E. गुण attribute, espe-<BR>cially good, and आकर a mine; a mine of merit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=240-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुणातीत|गुणातीतः
गुणातीत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Freed from or beyond all properties.<BR> E. गुण, and<BR>अतीत passed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=240-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुणानुरोध|गुणानुरोधः
गुणानुरोध m. (-धः) Conformity or suitableness to good qualities, &c. E.<BR>गुण, and अनुरोध concurrence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=240-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुणान्तर
गुणान्तर n. (-रं)<BR>	 1. Species or sort of merit.<BR>	 2. Variety of property or<BR>quality.<BR> E. गुण, and अन्तर difference.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=240-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुणान्वित
गुणान्वित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Having attributes or qualities.<BR>	 2. Excellent,<BR>good, endowed with virtues.<BR> E. गुण, and अन्वित possessed of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=240-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुणापवाद|गुणापवादः
गुणापवाद m. (-दः) Detraction.<BR> E. गुण, and अपवाद reproach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=240-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुणाभास
गुणाभास m. (-सः) Semblance of qualities.<BR> E. गुण, and आभास appearance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=240-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुणाश्रय
गुणाश्रय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Virtuous, excellent, able, endowed with good<BR>qualities.<BR> E. गुण, and आश्रय a Anasylum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=240-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुणिगण
गुणिगण m. (-णः) A number of virtuous persons.<BR> E. गुणिन्, and गण a<BR>troop.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=240-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुणित|गुणितः
गुणित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Multiplied, (arithmetically.)<BR>	 2. Collected, hea-<BR>ped together.<BR> E. गुण to advise, &c. affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=240-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुणिद्वैध
गुणिद्वैध n. (-धं) Equality of merit on two sides.<BR> E. गुणिन् and द्वैध duality.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=240-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुणिन्
गुणिन् mfn. (-णी-णिनी-णि) Endowed with good qualities.<BR>	 m. (-णी) A bow.<BR>E. गुण a quality, &c. and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=240-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुणीभूत|गुणीभूतः
गुणीभूत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Made secondary or subordinate.<BR>	 2. Invested<BR>with attributes, &c.<BR>	 3. Varied according to its qualities.<BR>	 4. Hav-<BR>ing a certain force or application, (a word, &c.)<BR> E. गुण and भूत be-<BR>come, with च्वि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=240-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुणेश्वर|गुणेश्वरः
गुणेश्वर mfn. (-रः-री-रं) Having good qualities, &c.<BR>	 m. (-रः) The name<BR>of a mountain, according to some, Chitrakuta or Comptah in<BR>Bundelcund.<BR> E. गुण qualities, and ईश्वर master or possessor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=240-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुणोत्कर्ष|गुणोत्कर्षः
गुणोत्कर्ष m. (-र्षः) Excellence, endowment with superior qualities.<BR> E. गुण<BR>and उत्कर्ष abundance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=240-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुणोत्कीर्त्तन|गुणोत्कीर्तन|गुणोत्कीर्त्तनं
गुणोत्कीर्त्तन n. (-नं) Panegyric, eulogium.<BR> E. गुण and उत्कीर्त्तन celebrating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=240-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुणोत्कृष्ट
गुणोत्कृष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं) Superior in merit or in good qualities.<BR> E. गुण,<BR>and उत्कृष्ट best.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=240-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुणोपेत
गुणोपेत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Endowed with good qualities.<BR> E. गुण and उपेत<BR>possessed of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=240-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुणौघ|गुणौघः
गुणौघ n. (-घं) Superior or abundant merit.<BR> E. गुण and ओघ heap.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=240-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुण्ठित|गुंठित|गुण्ठितः
गुण्ठित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Pounded, ground, reduced to dust or powder.<BR>2. Covered with, surrounded.<BR> E. गुठि to surround, &c. affix क्त; also<BR>गुण्डित.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=240-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुण्ड|गुंडः|गुण्डः
गुण्ड m. (-ण्डः) A fragrant grass, (Scirpus kysoor.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=240-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुण्डक|गुंडक|गुंडकः|गुण्डकः
गुण्डक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. Dust, powder.<BR>	 2. Dirty meal.<BR>	 3. An oil vessel.<BR>	 3. A<BR>low tone.<BR> E. गुडि to surround, &c. affix ठुन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=240-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुण्डिक|गुंडिक|गुंडिकः|गुण्डिकः
गुण्डिक mf. (-कः-का) Flour, powder, meal.<BR> E. गुडि to pound, वुन् affix,<BR>and इ inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=240-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुण्डिचा
गुण्डिचा f. (-चा) The name of the place where the car of JAGANNATH<BR>stays for a weak at the Rath Yatra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=240-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुण्डित|गुंडित|गुण्डितः
गुण्डित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Pounded, ground.<BR>	 2. Covered with dust.<BR> E. गुड<BR>to grind or pound, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=240-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुण्य
गुण्य mfn. (-ण्यः-ण्या-ण्यं)<BR>	 1. To be enumerated.<BR>	 2. To be described as<BR>qualities, to be praised.<BR>	 3. To be multiplied, the multiplicand. E.<BR>गुण to count, क्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=241-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुत्स|गुत्सः
गुत्स m. (-त्सः)<BR>	 1. A cluster of blossoms, a nosegay.<BR>	 2. A clump of grass.<BR>3. A necklace of thirty-six strings.<BR>	 4. A perfume, commonly Gan-<BR>thiala: see ग्रन्थिपर्ण.<BR>	 5. A bundle.<BR> E. गुध् to enclose or surround,<BR>Uṇādi affix स; also गुत्सक-गुच्छ &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=241-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुत्सक|गुत्सकः
गुत्सक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A nosegay, a cluster of blossoms.<BR>	 2. A chowri, a cow<BR>tail.<BR> E. कन् added to the preceding; also गुच्छक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=241-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुत्सपुष्प
गुत्सपुष्प m. (-ष्पः) A plant, (Echites scholaris:) see सप्तपर्ण.<BR> E. गुत्स and पुष्प<BR>a flower: bearing its flowers in clusters.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=241-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुत्सार्द्ध
गुत्सार्द्ध m. (-र्द्धः) A necklace or garland of twenty-four strings.<BR> E. गुत्स a<BR>large garland, and अर्द्ध a part; also गुच्छार्द्ध्व.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=241-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुद|गुदं
गुद r. 1st cl. (गोदति) To play.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=241-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुद|गुदं
गुद n. (-दं) The anus.<BR> E. गुद् to play, affix क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=241-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुदकील|गुदकीलः
गुदकील m. (-लः) Piles.<BR> E. गुद the anus, कील a pin or bolt also with कन्<BR>added गुदकीलक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=241-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुदग्रह|गुदग्रहः
गुदग्रह m. (-हः) Constipation, flatulence, &c.<BR> E. गुद the anus, and ग्रह<BR>what takes or affects.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=241-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुदभ्रंश|गुदभ्रंशः
गुदभ्रंश m. (-शः) Prolapsus ani.<BR> E. गुद and भ्रंश loss.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=241-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुदाङ्कुर|गुदांकुर|गुदाङ्कुरः
गुदाङ्कुर m. (-रः) Piles.<BR> E. गुद the anus, and अङ्कुर a sprout.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=241-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुद्र
गुद्र r. 10th cl. (इ) गुद्रि (गुद्रयति) To lie, to speak falsely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=241-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुध
गुध r. 1st cl. (गोधते) To play. r. 4th cl. (गोध्यति) To surround, to encom-<BR>pass. r. 9th cl. (गोध्नाति) To be angry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=241-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुधित
गुधित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Surrounded, enclosed.<BR> E. गुध् to surround, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=241-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुधेर|गुधेरः
गुधेर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) A protector, a defender.<BR> E. गुध् to invest, एरक्<BR>Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=241-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुन्दल|गुंदल|गुंदलः|गुन्दलः
गुन्दल m. (-लः) The sound of a small oblong drum.<BR> E. गुद् to play, अलच्<BR>affix and नुम् inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=241-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुन्दाल|गुंदाल|गुंदालः|गुन्दालः
गुन्दाल m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. A kind of bird, (a sort of pheasant.)<BR>	 2. The barta-<BR>velle: see चकोर<BR> E. गुन्द्रा a kind of grass, and ल what takes or eats,<BR>र rejected; also read गुन्द्राल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=241-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुद्र
गुद्र m. (-न्द्रः) A kind of grass, (Saccharum sara.)<BR>	 f. (-न्द्रा)<BR>	 1. A fragrant<BR>grass, (Cyperus pertenuis; also C. rotundus.)<BR>	 2. A plant bearing<BR>a fragrant seed; also प्रियङ्गु<BR> E. गुद् to play, affix रक् and नुम् inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=241-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुन्द्राल|गुंद्राल|गुंद्रालः|गुन्द्रालः
गुन्द्राल m. (-लः) A sort of bird: see गुन्दाल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=241-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुप
गुप r. 1st cl. (जुगुप्सते)<BR>	 1. To conceal, to hide.<BR>	 2. To censure, to blame<BR>or despise, (this root takes सन् irregularly.) (उ) गुपू r. 1st cl.<BR>(गोपयति) To guard or protect. (इर) गपिर r. 4th cl. (गुप्यति)<BR>	 1. To<BR>be confused or disturbed.<BR>	 2. To disturb or perplex. गुप r. 10th cl.<BR>(गोपयति)<BR>	 1. To shine.<BR>	 2. To speak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=241-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुपिल|गुपिलः
गुपिल m. (-लः) A king, a prince.<BR> E. गुप् to protect, Uṇādi affix इलच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=241-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुप्त|गुप्तं|गुप्तः
गुप्त mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं)<BR>	 1. Preserved, protected.<BR>	 2. Hidden, concealed,<BR>secret.<BR>	 3. Joined, combined.<BR>	 4. Invisible, withdrawn from sight.<BR>n. adv (-प्तं) Privately, secretly.<BR>	 m. (-प्तः) An appellation forming<BR>especially the second member of the name of a Vaiśya or man of<BR>the third class.<BR>	 f. (-प्ता)<BR>	 1. Cowach.<BR>	 2. A woman who hides from<BR>her lover's endearments.<BR> E. गुप् to defend, &c. affix ऊ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=241-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुप्तगति|गुप्तगतिः
गुप्तगति m. (-तिः) A spy or secret emissary.<BR>	 f. (-तिः) Going privately or<BR>secretly.<BR> E. गुप्त and गति going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=241-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुप्तचर|गुप्तचरः
गुप्तचर mfn. (-रः-री-रं) Who or what goes secretly.<BR>	 m. (-रः) A name of<BR>BALARĀMA.<BR> E. गुप्त and चर who goes, or चरट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=241-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुप्ति|गुप्तिः
गुप्ति f. (-प्तिः)<BR>	 1. Concealing, hiding, concealment.<BR>	 2. Preserving, protec-<BR>ting.<BR>	 3. Restraint, check.<BR>	 4. A hole in the ground, a cavern, a<BR>sink, a cellar, &c. (a place of concealment.)<BR>	 5. A prison.<BR>	 6. The<BR>well or lower deck of a boat.<BR>	 7. Digging a hole in the ground.<BR>	 8.<BR>Fortification.<BR> E. गुप् to hide, &c. affix क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=241-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुफ
गुफ r. 6th cl. (गुफति) To string as a garland, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=241-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुफित|गुफितः
गुफित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Strung, tied on a string.<BR>	 2. Arranged in order.<BR>E. गुफ् to string, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=241-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुम्फ|गुंफ|गुंफः|गुम्फः
गुम्फ r. 6th cl. (गुम्फति) To string together as a garland, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=241-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुम्फ|गुंफ|गुंफः|गुम्फः
गुम्फ m. (-म्फः)<BR>	 1. Tying, stringing as a garland, &c.<BR>	 2. A bracelet.<BR>	 3. A<BR>whisker, a mustachio.<BR> E. गुम्फ to tie or string, affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=241-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुम्फित|गुंफित|गुम्फितः
गुम्फित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Tied, strung.<BR>	 2. Arranged, placed in order. E.<BR>गुम्फ to tie, affix क्त; also गुफित, and ग्रन्थित.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=241-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुर
गुर r. 1st cl. (गोरति) r. 6th cl. (-ई) गुरी (गुरते) To make an effort or exertion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=241-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुरण|गुरणं
गुरण n. (-णं) Effort, perseverance, great or continued exertion.<BR> E. गुर्<BR>to make an effort, affix ल्युट्; also गोरण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=241-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुरु|गुरुः
गुरु mfn. (-गुरुः-गुर्व्वी-गुरु)<BR>	 1. Heavy, weighty.<BR>	 2. Great, (large or eminent)<BR>3. Difficult, arduous.<BR>	 4. Important.<BR>	 5. Much, excessive.<BR>	 6. Best,<BR>excellent.<BR>	 7. Venerable, respectable.<BR>	 8. Dear, valuable, highly<BR>prized.<BR>	 9. Accented long, (as a foot or vowel.)<BR>	 mn. (-रुः-रु) The<BR>long vowel, a sound equal to two Matras or simple sounds.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-रुः)<BR>	 1. A spiritual parent, from whom the youth receives the in-<BR>itiatory Mantra or prayer, and who conducts the ceremonies<BR>necessary at various seasons of infancy and youth, up to the period<BR>of investiture with the characteristic thread or string; this per-<BR>son may be the natural parent or the religious preceptor.<BR>	 2. A<BR>religious teacher, one who explains the law and religion to his<BR>pupil, instructs him in Śāstras, &c.<BR>	 3. A name of VṚHASPATI,<BR>who is considered as the Guru or preceptor of the gods.<BR>	 4. A<BR>father or any venerable male relation.<BR> E. गृ to sound or speak, &c.<BR>Uṇādi affix कु and उ substituted for ऋ; declaring the mode of<BR>performing the rites, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=241-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुरुकार्य्य|गुरुकार्य
गुरुकार्य्य n. (-र्य्यं)<BR>	 1. A serious or momentous affair.<BR>	 2. The business or<BR>office of a spiritual teacher.<BR> E. गुरु as above, and कार्य्य business. &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=241-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुरुकोप
गुरुकोप m. (-पः) Violent wrath.<BR> E. गुरु much, and कोप anger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=241-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुरुक्रम|गुरुक्रमः
गुरुक्रम m. (-मः) Traditionary instruction.<BR> E. गुरु a teacher, and क्रम<BR>order.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=241-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुरुगत
गुरुगत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Being with or belonging to a spiritual teacher.<BR>E. गुरु and गत gone to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=241-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुरुघ्न|गुरुघ्नः
गुरुघ्न mfn. (-घ्नः-घ्नी-घ्नं) Destroying a spiritual parent.<BR>	 m. (-घ्नः) White<BR>mustard,<BR> E. गुरु and घ्न who or what destroys.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=241-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुरुजन|गुरुजनः
गुरुजन m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. An elder, a venerable person.<BR>	 2. The elders of a<BR>family, &c.<BR> E. गुरु and जन people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=241-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुरुण्टक|गुरुण्टकः
गुरुण्टक m. (-कः) A kind of bird, a sort of peacock: see नीलमयूर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=241-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुरुतल्पग|गुरुतल्पगः
गुरुतल्पग m. (-गः) A violator of his teacher's bed.<BR> E. गुरु as above तल्प a<BR>bed and ग who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=241-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुरुतल्पव्रत
गुरुतल्पव्रत n. (-तं) Penance for intercourse with the wife of a Gura. E.<BR>गुरु, तल्प a bed, (defiling, &c. understood,) and व्रत penance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=241-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुरुतल्पिन्
गुरुतल्पिन् m. (-ल्पी) One who has criminal intercourse with his teacher's<BR>wife.<BR> E. गुरु तल्प a bed, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=241-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुरुताप
गुरुताप m. (-पः) Excessive heat.<BR> E. गुरु and ताप heat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=241-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुरुत्व|गुरुत्वं
गुरुत्व n. (-त्वं)<BR>	 1. Sacredness, venerableness, respectability.<BR>	 2. Greatness,<BR>magnitude.<BR>	 3. Weight, heaviness.<BR>	 4. Burden, trouble.<BR> E. गुरु and त्व<BR>affix; also with तल्, गुरुता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=241-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुरुप्रमोद
गुरुप्रमोद m. (-दः) Happiness, delight.<BR> E. गुरु and प्रमोद pleasure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=241-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुरुरत्न|गुरुरत्नं
गुरुरत्न n. (-त्नं) A topaz.<BR> E. गुरु valuable, रत्न a gem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=241-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुरुदैवत|गुरुदैवतः
गुरुदैवत m. (-तः) The eight lunar constellation; also पुष्प<BR> E. गुरु and<BR>देवता deity. affix अण्; VṚHASPATI is the ruling deity of the cons-<BR>tellation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=241-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुरुपत्र|गुरुपत्रं
गुरुपत्र n. (-त्रं) Tin.<BR>	 f. (-त्रा) The tamarind tree.<BR> E. गुरु, and पत्र leaf;<BR>heavy or abundant in leaves.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=241-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुरुमर्द्दल|गुरुमर्दल|गुरुमर्दलः
गुरुमर्द्दल m. (-लः) A kind of drum or tabor.<BR> E. गुरु heavy or large, and<BR>मर्द्दल a small drum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=241-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुरुवत्
गुरुवत् ind. Like a Guru, as a Guru.<BR> E. गुरु, and वति aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=241-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुरुवद्वृत्ति
गुरुवद्वृत्ति f. (-त्तिः) Behaving to any one with as much respect as to a<BR>sacred teacher.<BR> E. गुरुवत्, and वृत्ति practice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=241-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुरुवर्च्चोघ्न|गुरुवर्चोघ्न|गुरुवर्चोघ्नः|गुरुवर्च्चोघ्नः
गुरुवर्च्चोघ्न m. (-घ्नः) The lime or citron.<BR> E. गुरु much, वर्च्चस् heat, and घ्न<BR>what removes; of cooling properties.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=241-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुरुशिंशपा
गुरुशिंशपा f. (-पा) A tree, (Dalbergia sisu:) see शिंशपा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=242-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुरुशुश्रूषा
गुरुशुश्रूषा f. (-षा) Service of a Guru.<BR> E. गुरु, and शुश्रूषा; also गुरुपूजा<BR>गुरुसेवा &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=242-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुरुसारा
गुरुसारा f. (-रा) See शिंशपा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=242-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुरुस्थिर
गुरुस्थिर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Very firm.<BR> E. गुरु and स्थिर steady.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=242-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुरुहन्
गुरुहन् m. (-हा) The murderer of his Guru or spiritual parent.<BR> E. गरु<BR>and हन् who kills, from हन् with क्विप् affix; this is the most hein-<BR>ous of all criminals, according to Hindu notions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=242-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुर्ज्जर|गुर्जर|गुर्जरः|गुर्ज्जरः
गुर्ज्जर m. (-रः) The name of a district, Gurjara or Guzrat. plu.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-राः) The people of Guzrat.<BR>	 f. (-री) One of the Rāgiṇīs or female<BR>personifications of music.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=242-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुर्द|गुर्द्द
गुर्द r. 1st. cl. (गुर्दते or गूर्दते) To play. r. 10th cl. (गुर्दयति or गूर्दयति)<BR>	 1. To<BR>dwell or inhabit.<BR>	 2. To invite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=242-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुर्व|गुर्व्व
गुर्व r. 1st cl. (ई)गुर्वी (गुर्वति) To endeavor, to aim or strive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=242-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुर्व्वर्थम्|गुर्वर्थम्
गुर्व्वर्थम् ind. For or on account of a Guru.<BR> E. गुरु, and अर्थ object.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=242-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुर्व्वङ्गना|गुर्वङ्गना
गुर्व्वङ्गना f. (-ना)<BR>	 1. The wife of a Guru.<BR>	 2. Any woman entitled to great<BR>respect.<BR> E. गुरु, and अङ्गना a female.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=242-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुर्व्विणी|गुर्विणी
गुर्व्विणी f. (-णी) A pregnant woman.<BR> E. गर्व्व to be proud, Uṇādi affix इनच्<BR>and ङीष् fem. affix, उ substituted for the radical अ; also गर्भिणी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=242-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुर्व्वी|गुर्वी
गुर्व्वी f. (-र्व्वीं)<BR>	 1. A pregnant woman.<BR>	 2. The wife of a Guru or spiritual<BR>teacher.<BR> E. गुरु heavy, &c. and ङीष् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=242-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुल|गुलः
गुल m. (-लः) Raw unrefined sugar, molasses.<BR>	 f. (-ला) A plant, (Euphor-<BR>bia tirucalli:) see स्नुही. (-ली) 1. A pill, a bolus, any small globu-<BR>lar substance.<BR>	 2. Small pox.<BR> E. गुड to surround, &c. affixes क and<BR>and टाप्, or ङीष्, ड changed to ल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=242-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुलञ्चकन्द|गुलञ्चकन्दः
गुलञ्चकन्द m. (-न्दः) An esculent root. commonly कुली.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=242-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुलिका
गुलिका f. (-का) A small ball.<BR> E. कन् added to गुली.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=242-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुलिकाक्रीडा
गुलिकाक्रीडा f. (-डा) Playing with a ball, bat and ball, golf, &c.<BR> E. गुलिका<BR>and क्रीडा play.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=242-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुलुच्छ|गुलुच्छः|गुलुछ
गुलुच्छ m. (-च्छः) A cluster of blossoms; also गुलुञ्छ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=242-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुलुञ्छ|गुलुंछ|गुलुंछः|गुलुञ्छः
गुलुञ्छ m. (-ञ्छः) A cluster of blossoms, nosegay.<BR> E. गुलु to preserve, affix<BR>क्विप्, and ड changed to ल, and उच्छ or इच्छि to gather. or glean,<BR>affix क; also with कन् added गुलुञ्छक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=242-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुल्फ|गुल्फः
गुल्फ m. (-ल्फः) The ankle.<BR> E. गल् to go, affix फक्, and उ substituted for<BR>the penultimate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=242-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुल्म|गुल्मं|गुल्मः
गुल्म m. (-ल्मः)<BR>	 1. The division of an army, a body of troops, consisting<BR>of nine platoons, or nine elephants, nine chariots, twenty-seven<BR>horse, and forty-five foot.<BR>	 2. The spleen.<BR>	 3. A shrub, a bush.<BR>	 4.<BR>A clump of grass, &c.<BR>	 5. A fort, an intrenchment.<BR>	 6. Disciplining<BR>an army, keeping it in a posture of defence.<BR>	 7. A wharf or stairs,<BR>a Ghat.<BR>	 8. A disease; according to some, a chronic enlargement of<BR>the spleen, but as variously situated, it is any glandular enlarge-<BR>ment in the abdomen, as that of the mesenteric gland, &c. so as<BR>to be perceived externally.<BR>	 f. (-ल्मी)<BR>	 1. A tent.<BR>	 2. Emblic myrobalan<BR>also आमलकी.<BR>	 3. Small cardamoms: see एला.<BR>	 4. A cluster or clump<BR>of trees, a multitude of thickets.<BR>	 5. A kind of plant, commonly<BR>Kurkavali.<BR> E. गुड to surround, मक् affix, ड changed to ल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=242-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुल्मकेतु|गुल्मकेतुः
गुल्मकेतु m. (-तुः) A small sort of cane or reed.<BR> E. गुल्म and केतु banner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=242-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुल्ममूल|गुल्ममूलं
गुल्ममूल n. (-लं) Ginger.<BR> E. गुल्म and मूल a root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=242-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुल्मिन्
गुल्मिन् mfn. (-ल्मी-ल्मिनी-ल्मि)<BR>	 1. Composed of different divisions, (a force,<BR>&c.)<BR>	 2. Growing, &c. in a clump or cluster.<BR>	 3. Having the spleen<BR>affected by it.<BR>	 f. (-नी) A spreading creeper or any creeping plant.<BR>E. गुल्म a clump, इनि and ङीष् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=242-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुल्य|गुल्यः
गुल्य m. (-ल्यः) Sweetness, a sweet or saccharine taste.<BR> E. गुड molasses,<BR>and क्यप् affix; ड changed to ल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=242-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुवाक|गुवाकः
गुवाक m. (-कः) The betelnut tree, (Areca faufel or catechu.)<BR> E. गु to<BR>stool, affix आक, and उ converted to उव irregularly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=242-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुह|गुहः
गुह r. 1st cl. (ऊ)गुहू(गुहति) To cover, to cover as with clothes. to wear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=242-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुह|गुहः
गुह m. (-ह)<BR>	 1. A name of KARTIKEYA.<BR>	 2. A name of VIṢṆU.<BR>	 3. A swift<BR>horse.<BR>	 4. The name of Nishada, ruler of Sringavera, the friend of<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=242-b" target="_blank">Page242-b+ 60</a>]<BR>RAMA.<BR>	 5. A name or title proper to persons of the writer caste.<BR>	 f.<BR>(-हा)<BR>	 1. A cave, a cavern.<BR>	 2. A pit, a hole in the ground.<BR>	 3. A<BR>plant, commonly Chakuliya: see सिंहपुच्छी.<BR> E. गुह to conceal, affixes<BR>अङ् and टाप.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=242-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुहागृह
गुहागृह n. (-हं) A cavern.<BR> E. गुहा, and गृह a house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=242-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुहामुख
गुहामुख mfn. (-खः-खी-खं) Wide mouthed, open mouthed.<BR> E. गुहा, and<BR>मुख mouth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=242-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुहाशय|गुहाशयः
गुहाशय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. A tiger.<BR>	 2. Any animal or man living in caverns.<BR>	 3.<BR>A name of VIṢṆU.<BR> E. गुहा a cave, and आशय abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=242-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुहिन|गुहिनं
गुहिन n. (-नं) A wood, a thicket.<BR> E. गुह् to hide, इनच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=242-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुहिल|गुहिलं
गुहिल n. (-लं) Wealth, property.<BR> E. गुह् to hide, &c. इलच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=242-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुहेर|गुहेरः
गुहेर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. An iron-smith.<BR>	 2. A guardian, a preserver.<BR> E. गुह to<BR>cover, एरक् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=242-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुह्य|गुह्यं|गुह्यः
गुह्य mfn. (-ह्यः-ह्या-ह्यं)<BR>	 1. Secret, solitary, retired.<BR>	 2. Private, concealable,<BR>to be kept hidden or secret.<BR>	 3. Mysterious, mystical.<BR>	 m. (-ह्यः)<BR>	 1. A<BR>tortoise.<BR>	 2. Hypocrisy.<BR>	 3. VIṢṆU.<BR>	 n. (-ह्यं)<BR>	 1. A privity, an organ<BR>of generation, &c.<BR>	 2. The anus.<BR> E. गुह् to cover, क्य affix, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=242-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुह्यक|गुह्यकः
गुह्यक m. (-कः) A kind of demigod attendant upon KUVERA the deity<BR>of wealth, and guardian of his treasures.<BR> E. गुह् to preserve or<BR>conceal, affix क्वुन् and य inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=242-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुह्यकेश्वर|गुह्यकेश्वरः
गुह्यकेश्वर m. (-रः) A name of KUVERA the Hindu PLUTUS.<BR> E. गुह्यक a<BR>demigod, (see the preceding,) and ईश्वर lord or master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=242-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुह्यगुरु|गुह्यगुरुः
गुह्यगुरु m. (-रुः) A name of ŚIVA.<BR> E. गुह्य secret, and गुरु a master;<BR>ŚIVA being considered as a teacher, especially of the Tantras<BR>or Hindu mystic and magical works.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=242-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुह्यदीपक|गुह्यदीपकः
गुह्यदीपक m. (-कः) The fire fly.<BR> E. गुह्य a solitary place, and दीपक the<BR>illuminer; from दीप् to light or inflame, and क्वन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=242-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुह्यनिष्यन्द|गुह्यनिष्यंद|गुह्यनिष्यन्दः
गुह्यनिष्यन्द m. (-न्दः) Urine.<BR> E. गुह्य and निष्यन्द what flows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=242-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुह्यभाषित|गुह्यभाषितं
गुह्यभाषित n. (-तं)<BR>	 1. A Mantra, a mystical prayer or incantation 2. A<BR>secret.<BR> E. गुह्य secret.<BR> E. भाषित spoken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=242-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गू
गू(ओ)ओगू r. 6th cl. (गूवति) To void by stool; also with a short vowel, गु<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=242-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गूढ|गूढं|गूढः
गूढ mfn. (-ढः-ढा-ढं) Hidden, concealed.<BR>	 n. (-ढं)<BR>	 1. A solitary or private<BR>place.<BR>	 2. A private part.<BR>	 3. A mystery.<BR> E. गुह् to hide, affix क्त.<BR>deriv. irregular.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=242-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गूढचार
गूढचार mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) One who goes about privately.<BR>	 m. (-रः) A secret<BR>emissary.<BR> E. गूढ and चार practice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=242-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गूढचारिन्
गूढचारिन् m. (-री) A secret emissary, a spy.<BR> E. गूढ and चारिन् who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=242-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गूढज|गूढजः
गूढज m. (-जः) The son of a concealed birth; born privately of a<BR>woman whose husband is absent, the real father being unknown;<BR>this is one of the twelve forms particularized in Hindu law.<BR> E. गूढ<BR>hidden, and ज born; also compound with पुत्त्र a son, गूढजपुत्त्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=242-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गूढनीड|गूढनीडः
गूढनीड m. (-डः) The wagtail.<BR> E. गूड secret, and नीड a nest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=242-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गूढपथ|गूढपथः
गूढपथ m. (-थः)<BR>	 1. Mind, intellect.<BR>	 2. A bye-path, a hidden way.<BR> E. गूढ<BR>secret, and पथ a road; whose path is unperceived.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=242-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गूढपाद्
गूढपाद् m. (-द् or त्) A snake.<BR> E. गूढ hidden, and पाद a foot, the final<BR>vowel rejected; also being retained गूढपाद nom. (-दः.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=242-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गूढपुरुष|गूढपुरुषः
गूढपुरुष m. (-षः) A spy, a secret emissary, a disguised agent, &c.<BR> E. गूढ<BR>concealed, and पुरुष a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=242-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गूढभाषित
गूढभाषित n. (-तं) Secret intelligence, private communication.<BR> E. गूढ<BR>secret, and भाषित what is said.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=242-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गूढमार्ग|गूढमार्गः
गूढमार्ग m. (-र्गः) A subterraneous passage, a defile, a bye-road, or secret<BR>way.<BR> E. गूढ concealed, and मार्ग a road.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=242-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गूढमैथुन|गूढमैथुनः
गूढमैथुन m. (-नः) A crow.<BR> E. गूढ secret, and मैथुन copulation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=242-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गूढवर्च्चस्|गूढवर्चस्
गूढवर्च्चस् m. (-र्च्चाः) A frog.<BR> E. गूढ hidden, and वर्च्चस् light, warmth;<BR>perhaps an idea is implied analogous to that of cold blooded<BR>animals: some explain it वर्च्चस् fœces, whose excrement is<BR>unknown.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=242-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गूढसाक्षिन्
गूढसाक्षिन् m. (-क्षी) A concealed witness, one placed by the plaintiff, so<BR>as to overhear what has been said by the defendant.<BR> E. गूढ and<BR>साक्षिन् a witness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=242-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गूढाङ्ग|गूढांग|गूढाङ्गः
गूढाङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः) A tortoise.<BR> E. गूढ, and अङ्ग body, hidden in his shell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=243-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गूढाङ्घ्रि|गूढांघ्रि|गूढाङ्घ्रिः
गूढाङ्घ्रि m. (-ङ्घ्रिः) A snake.<BR> E. गूढ and अङ्घ्रि foot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=243-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गूढोत्पन्न|गूढोत्पन्नः
गूढोत्पन्न m. (-न्नः) The son of concealed birth: see गूढज.<BR> E. गूढ privately,<BR>and उत्पन्न born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=243-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गूथ|गूथं|गूथः
गूथ m. (-थः) Fœces, ordure.<BR> E. गू to void by stool, and थक् Uṇādi<BR>aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=243-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गूथलक्त|गूथलक्तः
गूथलक्त m. (-क्तः) A small bird, considered to be a species of the Mayna,<BR>(Turdus salica.)<BR> E. गूथ ordure, and लक्त marked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=243-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गून|गूनः
गून mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Voided, (as ordure.)<BR> E. गू to stool, affix क्त deriv.<BR>irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=243-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गूर
गूर r. 10th cl. (गूरयते)<BR>	 1. To strive, to endeavor to make an effort or<BR>exertion.<BR>	 2. To eat. (ई) गूरी r. 4th cl. (गूर्य्यते)<BR>	 1. To hurt, to injure,<BR>as to wound, to kill, &c.<BR>	 2. To be decayed or old.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=243-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गूरण|गूरणं
गूरण n. (-णं) Effort, exertion.<BR> E. गूर् to strive, affix ल्युट्; also गुरण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=243-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गूर्द|गूर्दः|गूर्द्द
गूर्द r. 1st cl. (गूर्दते) To play. r. 10 cl. (गूर्दयति)<BR>	 1. To dwell or inhabit.<BR>	 2.<BR>invite; these roots are both written more usually with the short<BR>vowel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=243-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गूवाक|गूवाकः
गूवाक m. (-कः) The betelnut tree: see गुवाक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=243-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गूषणा
गूषणा f. (-णा) The eye in a peacock's tail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=243-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गूहमान
गूहमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Hiding, concealing.<BR> E. गूह् to hide, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=243-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गूहयित्वा
गूहयित्वा ind. Having concealed, hidden, disguised.<BR> E. गूह् to hide,<BR>causal form, क्त्वा aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=243-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृ
गृ r. 1st cl. (गरति) To sprinkle, to moisten or wet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=243-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृज
गृज r. 1st cl. (गर्जति) also (इ,) गृजि (गृञ्जति) To sound, to roar, to grum-<BR>ble, &c. also गर्ज.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=243-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृञ्जन|गृंजन|गृञ्जनं|गृंजनः|गृञ्जनः
गृञ्जन n. (-नं) Poisoned flesh, the meat of an animal destroyed by poi-<BR>son.<BR>	 m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. Garlic, or a small variety of it of a red colour.<BR>	 2.<BR>A turnip.<BR>	 8. The tops of hemp chewed as an inebriating substance<BR>the Ganja.<BR> E. गृजि to sound, and ल्युट् affix; applied to the latter<BR>as causing eructation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=243-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृणत्
गृणत् mfn. (-णन्-णन्ती-णत्)<BR>	 1. Speaking.<BR>	 2. Praising, flattering.<BR> E. गृ to<BR>speak, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=243-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृण्डीव|गृंडीव|गृंडीवः|गृण्डीवः
गृण्डीव m. (-बः) An animal of prey, considered as a large kind of jackal.<BR>E. गृ to sound, and डीव affix; deriv. irr.; also sometimes short<BR>गृण्डिव.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=243-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृत्स|गृत्सः
गृत्स m. (-त्सः) A name of KANDARPA.<BR> E. गृध् to be desirous, and स<BR>Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=243-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृध
गृध r. 4th cl. (उ)गृधु (गृध्यति) To covet, to desire greedily, to be greedy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=243-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृधु|गृधुः
गृधु m. (-धुः)<BR>	 1. The deity KĀMA^1 or love.<BR>	 2. A libidinous man.<BR> E. गृध्<BR>to desire, कु Uṇādi aff.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20260617. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/264.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=243-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृधू
गृधू m. (-धूः)<BR>	 1. Understanding.<BR>	 2. Air voided downwards.<BR>	 3. Bad,<BR>wicked.<BR> E. गृध and कू Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=243-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृध्नु|गृध्नुः
गृध्नु mfn. (-ध्नुः-ध्नुः-ध्नु) Covetous, cupidinous, greedy.<BR> E. गृध् to be<BR>greedy, क्नु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=243-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृध्नुता
गृध्नुता f. (-ता) Covetousness, greediness, extreme and illiberal desire.<BR>E. गृध्नु greedy, and तल् abstract aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=243-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृध्र|गृध्रः
गृध्र mfn. (-ध्रः-ध्रा-ध्रं) Desirous, greedy, covetous.<BR>	 m. (-ध्रः) A vulture. E.<BR>गृध् to desire, and क्रन् Uṇādi affix; it may also written गृद्ध्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=243-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृध्रनखी
गृध्रनखी f. (-खी)<BR>	 1. The jujube, (Zizyphus jujuba.)<BR>	 2. A wild kind of<BR>the same, (Zizyphus nepeca.)<BR> E. गृध्र a vulture, and नख nail, hav-<BR>ing thorns like a vulture's claws.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=243-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृध्रराज|गृध्रराजः
गृध्रराज m. (-जः) A name of JAṬĀYU.<BR> E. गृध्र and राज king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=243-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृध्रसी
गृध्रसी f. (-सी)<BR>	 1. Lumbago.<BR>	 2. Rheumatism, affecting the loins.<BR> E. गृध्र<BR>desire, सो to destroy, ड and ङीप् affixes; also sometimes written<BR>ग्रध्रसी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=243-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृष्टि|गृष्टिः
गृष्टि m. (-ष्टिः)<BR>	 1. A cow that has had one calf.<BR>	 2. A yam.<BR>	 3. The jujube<BR>(Zizyphus jujuba.)<BR> E. घृष् to grind, affix क्तिन् and घ changed to ग.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=243-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृह|गृहं|गृहः
गृह r. 1st cl. (ऊ,)गृहू(गर्हते) also r. 10th cl. (गृहयते) To take, to seize,<BR>to receive or accept; also ग्रह.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=243-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृह|गृहं|गृहः
गृह n. (-हं)<BR>	 1. A house, a mansion, a habitation in general.<BR>	 2. A wife:<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=243-b" target="_blank">Page243-b+ 60</a>]<BR>(in these senses the plural is always masculine, गृहाः)<BR>	 3. A name,<BR>an appellation.<BR> E. गृह् to receive or take, (grain, goods, &c.) affix क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=243-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहकच्छप|गृहकच्छपः
गृहकच्छप m. (-पः) A small flat oblong stone, used for grinding condi-<BR>ments, &c.<BR> E. गृह a house, and कच्छप a tortoise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=243-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहकन्या
गृहकन्या f. (-न्या) The aloe, (Aloes perfoliata;) also घृतकुमारी, कुमारी, &c.<BR>E. गृह a house, and कन्या a virgin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=243-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहकपोतक|गृहकपोतकः
गृहकपोतक m. (-कः) A pigeon, a tame or domestic pigeon.<BR> E. गृह a<BR>house, and कपोतक a dove or pigeon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=243-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहकरण
गृहकरण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Household affairs.<BR>	 2. House building.<BR> E. गृह, and<BR>करण making.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=243-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहकारक|गृहकारकः
गृहकारक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A house-builder.<BR>	 2. A thatcher.<BR> E. गृह, and कारक<BR>who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=243-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहकारिन्
गृहकारिन् m. (-री)<BR>	 1. A kind of wasp.<BR>	 2. A house-builder.<BR> E. गृह a house,<BR>and कारिन् who makes, building a nest or house of clay, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=243-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहकार्य्य|गृहकार्य
गृहकार्य्य n. (-र्य्यं) Household affairs.<BR> E. गृह, and कार्य्य business; also गृह-<BR>कर्म्म, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=243-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहगोधा
गृहगोधा f. (-धा) A small house lizard.<BR> E. गृह a house, and गोधा or गोधिका<BR>an iguana; hence also गृहगोधिका, or ध being changed to ल, गृह-<BR>गोलिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=243-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहगोलिका
गृहगोलिका f. (-का) A lizard: see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=243-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहचटक
गृहचटक m. (-कः) A house sparrow.<BR> E. गृह and चटक a sparrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=243-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहच्छिद्र|गृहछिद्र
गृहच्छिद्र n. (-द्रं)<BR>	 1. Private or family afflictions or troubles.<BR>	 2. A breach<BR>in a house.<BR> E. गृह, and छिद्र a hole; also गृहरन्ध्रं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=243-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहज
गृहज mfn. (-जः-जा-जं) Born in the house.<BR>	 m. (-जः) A slave born in the<BR>house.<BR> E. गृह, and ज born; also गृहजात.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=243-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहणी
गृहणी f. (-णी) Rice water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=243-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहतटी
गृहतटी f. (-टी) A terrace in front of a house, a threshold.<BR> E. गृह a house,<BR>and तट a bank.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=243-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहदास|गृहदासः
गृहदास mf. (-सः-सी) A domestic slave.<BR> E. गृह, and दास a slave.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=243-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहदीप्ति|गृहदीप्तिः
गृहदीप्ति f. (-प्तिः) A virtuous woman.<BR> E. गृह, and दीप्ति light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=243-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहद्वार
गृहद्वार m. (-रः) The door of a house.<BR> E. गृह, and द्वार a door.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=243-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहद्रुम|गृहद्रुमः
गृहद्रुम m. (-मः) A plant commonly Medhasringi: see मेढशृङ्गी<BR> E. गृह a<BR>house, द्रुम a tree, growing near dwellings.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=243-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहनाशन|गृहनाशनः
गृहनाशन m. (-नः) A pigeon.<BR> E. गृह, and नाशन who injures; defacing the<BR>walls of a house by building in and about it.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=243-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहनीड|गृहनीडः
गृहनीड m. (-डः) A sparrow.<BR> E. गृह and नीड a nest, who builds his nest in<BR>human dwellings.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=243-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहपति|गृहपतिः
गृहपति m. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. A house. holder, a man of the second class, or who<BR>after having finished his studies is married and settled.<BR>	 2. A house<BR>holder of particular merit, giving alms, and performing all the<BR>prescribed ceremonies, &c.<BR>	 3. Maintenance of a sacred and perpe-<BR>tual fire.<BR>	 4. Virtue, especially of a householder, as hospitality, &c.<BR>E. गृह a house. and पति lord or master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=243-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहपोतक|गृहपोतकः
गृहपोतक m. (-कः) The site of a habitation, the ground on which it<BR>stands, and which is attached to it.<BR> E. गृह, and पोत a young ani-<BR>mal, affix कन्, the rudiments of the house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=243-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहबलि|गृहबलिः
गृहबलि m. (-लिः) Offering of the reliques of a meal, or sacrifice to the<BR>spirits of the air, &c.<BR> E. गृह, and बलि offering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=243-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहबलिप्रिय|गृहबलिप्रियः
गृहबलिप्रिय m. (-यः) A kind of crane, the Vaca.<BR> E. गृह a house, बलि<BR>food offered in oblation, and प्रिय fond of: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=243-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहबलिभुज्
गृहबलिभुज् m. (-भुक्)<BR>	 1. A sparrow.<BR>	 2. A kind of crane. (Ardea nivea.)<BR>3. A crow.<BR> E. गृह a house or a wife, बलि grain, &c. used in obla-<BR>tions, or any edible grain, and भुज् who eats; that is, who eats the<BR>food of his female, or the fragments of offerings fallen in or about<BR>the house; also गृहबलिप्रिय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=243-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहभङ्ग|गृहभंग|गृहभङ्गः
गृहभङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>	 1. An exile, one who is driven from his house.<BR>	 2. Fa-<BR>mily decay.<BR>	 3. Breaking down or into a house.<BR> E. गृह, and भङ्ग<BR>breaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=243-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहभञ्जन
गृहभञ्जन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Breaking down or destroying a house.<BR>	 2. Causing<BR>the ruin or decay of a family.<BR> E. गृह, and भञ्जन breaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=243-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहभूमि|गृहभूमिः
गृहभूमि f. (-मिः) The site of a habitation.<BR> E. गृह a house, and भूमि ground.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=244-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहमणि|गृहमणिः
गृहमणि m. (-णिः) A lamp.<BR> E. गृह a house, and मणि a jewel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=244-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहमाचिका
गृहमाचिका f. (-का) A bat.<BR> E. गृह a house, and माचिका a fly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=244-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहमृग|गृहमृगः
गृहमृग m. (-गः) A dog.<BR> E. गृह a house, and मृग a deer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=244-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहमेधिन्
गृहमेधिन् m. (-धी) A householder.<BR>	 f. (-धिनी)<BR>	 1. A housewife, the wife of a<BR>householder.<BR>	 2. Natural sense or intelligence,<BR> E. गृह a house, मेध to<BR>to understand, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=244-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहयाप्य
गृहयाप्य m. (-प्यः) The householder, the master of a house or family. E.<BR>गृह to take, याप्य Uṇādi affix, and अय inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=244-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहयालु|गृहयालुः
गृहयालु mfn. (-लुः-लुः-लु) Disposed to seize or take.<BR> E. गृह to take, अय<BR>inserted, and आलच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=244-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहरन्ध्र
गृहरन्ध्र n. (-न्ध्रं)<BR>	 1. Private or family affairs, especially of an unpleas-<BR>ing nature.<BR>	 2. A breach in the wall of a house.<BR> E. गृह, and रन्ध्र a<BR>a hole; also गृहछिद्रं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=244-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहवाटिका
गृहवाटिका f. (-का) A garden or grove near a house.<BR> E. गृह a house, वट्<BR>to surround, affix ण्वुल्, and fem form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=244-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहव्यापार
गृहव्यापार m. (-रः) Household affairs, domestic economy.<BR> E. गृह and<BR>व्यापार practice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=244-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहस्तम्भ
गृहस्तम्भ m. (-म्भः) The pillar of a house.<BR> E. गृह, and स्तम्भ a post.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=244-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहस्थ|गृहस्थः
गृहस्थ m. (-स्थः) A householder, the man of the second class, or he who,<BR>after having finished his studies, and been invested with the sacred<BR>thread, performs the duties of the master of a house, and father of<BR>a family.<BR> E. गृह a house, and स्थ who stays or abides.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=244-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहस्थधर्म्म|गृहस्थधर्म
गृहस्थधर्म्म m. (-र्म्मः) The practice or duty of a householder.<BR> E. गृहस्थ and<BR>धर्म्म duty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=244-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहस्थाश्रम
गृहस्थाश्रम m. (-मः) The order of householder.<BR> E. गृहस्थ, and आश्रम order<BR>of life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=244-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहस्थूण|गृहस्थूणं
गृहस्थूण n. (-णं) The pillar of a house.<BR> E. गृह a house, and स्थूण a prop or<BR>pillar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=244-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहाक्ष|गृहाक्षः
गृहाक्ष m. (-क्षः) A loophole, an eyelet hole, a round or oblong window.<BR>E. गृह a house, and अक्ष for अक्षि an eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=244-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहागत|गृहागतः
गृहागत m. (-तः) A guest.<BR> E. गृह, and आगत come to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=244-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहाधिप|गृहाधिपः
गृहाधिप m. (-पः) The Grihastha or householder; see गृहस्थ.<BR> E. गृह a<BR>house, and अधिप a master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=244-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहाभिपालिन्
गृहाभिपालिन् mfn. (-ली-लिनी-लि) Watching, taking care of the house.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-ली) A watchman.<BR> E. गृह and अभि before पाल to protect, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=244-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहाम्ल|गृहाम्लं
गृहाम्ल n. (-म्लं) Sour gruel, made from the fermentation of rice water. E.<BR>गृह a house, अम्ल sour, the domestic acid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=244-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहायणिक
गृहायणिक m. (-कः) A householder.<BR> E. गृह a house, फिञ् derivative affix,<BR>and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=244-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहाराम|गृहारामः
गृहाराम m. (-मः) A garden, a grove, &c. near a house.<BR> E. गृह a house,<BR>and आराम a garden.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=244-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहालिका
गृहालिका f. (-का) A small lizard.<BR> E. गृह a house, आलि a scorpion, कन्<BR>affix of similitude.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=244-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहावग्रहणी
गृहावग्रहणी f. (-णी) The threshold, a raised ground or terrace in front of<BR>the door.<BR> E. गृह a house, and अव prefixed to ग्रह to take, affixes ल्युट्<BR>and ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=244-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहावस्थित
गृहावस्थित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Dwelling or living in a house.<BR>	 2. Lying in<BR>any place.<BR> E. गृह, and अवस्थित placed or situated in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=244-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहाशया
गृहाशया f. (-या) The betel tree, (Piper betel.)<BR> E. गृह a house, &c. आशय<BR>an asylum growing near dwellings.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=244-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहाश्मन्
गृहाश्मन् m. (-श्मा) A flat oblong stone, upon which condiments are<BR>ground together.<BR> E. गृह a house, and अश्मन् a stone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=244-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहिणी
गृहिणी f. (-णी) A wife.<BR> E. गृह a house, and इनि and ङीष् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=244-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहिन्
गृहिन् m. (-ही) A householder.<BR> E. गृह a house, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=244-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहीत|गृहीतं
गृहीत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Taken, attached, seized, caught.<BR>	 2. Obtained.<BR>3. Known, understood.<BR>	 4. Promised, agreed.<BR>	 5. Learnt, acquired.<BR>E. ग्रह् to take, affix क्त, र changed to ऋ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=244-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहीतविद्य
गृहीतविद्य mfn. (-द्यः-द्या-द्यं) Versed in science, learned, studied.<BR> E. गृहीत,<BR>and विद्या learning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=244-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहीतदिश्
गृहीतदिश् mfn. (-दिक्) Flown, escaped, retreated.<BR> E. गृहीत seized, and<BR>दिश् place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=244-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहीतवेतन
गृहीतवेतन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Paid, remunerated.<BR> E. गृहीत and वेतन wages.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=244-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहीतृ
गृहीतृ mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ) Taking, disposed to seize or take.<BR> E. ग्रह to seize,<BR>affix तृच् and ई inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=244-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहीत्वा
गृहीत्वा ind. Having taken.<BR> E. ग्रह to take, क्त्वा aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=244-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहोपकरण
गृहोपकरण n. (-णं) Any domestic utensil.<BR> E. गृह and उपकरण instrument.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=244-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहोत्पात|गृहोत्पातः
गृहोत्पात m. (-तः)<BR>	 1. A domestic nuisance, as vermin, &c.<BR>	 2. Family mis-<BR>fortune.<BR> E. गृह, and उत्पात calamity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=244-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहोलिका
गृहोलिका f. (-का) A small house lizard.<BR> E. गृह to take, and उल and कन्<BR>affixes: see गृहगोधिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=244-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृह्णत्
गृह्णत् mfn. (-ह्णन्-ह्णन्ती-ह्णत्) Taking, seizing, accepting, &c.<BR> E. ग्रह् to take,<BR>शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=244-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृह्य|गृह्यं|गृह्यः
गृह्य mfn. (-ह्यः-ह्या-ह्यं)<BR>	 1. Dependent, subservient.<BR>	 2. A partisan of or<BR>belonging to a side or party.<BR>	 3. To be taken or seized.<BR>	 4. To be<BR>trusted to, to be relied on.<BR>	 5. To be acknowledged or admitted, to<BR>be adopted as faith or belief.<BR>	 5. Domestic, of or belonging to a<BR>house.<BR>	 m. (-ह्यः) A tame or domesticated animal.<BR>	 n. (-ह्यं)<BR>	 1. The<BR>name of a book, containing directions for religious rites, a section<BR>or component treatise of the Sama Veda, by GOBHILA and others;<BR>which contains rules for the performance of domestic and other<BR>ceremonies: the ritual of the Vedas.<BR>	 f. (-ह्या) A suburb, a village ad-<BR>joining to a city, or a small village attached to a larger.<BR> E. ग्रह or<BR>गृह to take, affix क्यप्; or गृह a house, यत् affix; also with कन् add-<BR>ed गृह्यक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=244-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृह्यक|गृह्यकः
गृह्यक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Dependent, docile, not following one's own in-<BR>clinations.<BR>	 m. (-कः) A tame or domesticated animal, whether a bird<BR>or beast, &c.<BR> E. गृध् for ग्रह् to take, क्यप् affix, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=244-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृह्यगुरु
गृह्यगुरु m. (-रुः) A name of ŚIVA.<BR> E. गृह्य, and गुरु a teacher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=244-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृह्यसूत्र
गृह्यसूत्र n. (-त्रं) A precept of the Grihya or ritual of the Vedas.<BR> E. गृह्य,<BR>and सूत्र a rule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=244-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गॄ
गॄ r. 6th cl. (गिरति or गिलति) To swallow, to eat. r. 9th cl. (गृणाति) To<BR>sound, to sound intelligibly or articulately, to speak. r. 10th cl.<BR>(गीरयते)<BR>	 1. To know.<BR>	 2. To make known, to teach. With निर् or उत्<BR>prefixed, To reject, to vomit. With सम् and उत्, 1. To throw up.<BR>	 2.<BR>To cry aloud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=244-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गेण्डु|गेण्डुः
गेण्डु m. (-ण्डुः) A ball for playing with.<BR> E. गा to go, affix इण्डु, or<BR>with कन् added गेण्डुक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=244-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गेण्डुक|गेंडुक|गेंडुकः|गेण्डुकः
गेण्डुक m. (-कः) A ball; also गेण्डूक, the penultimate being made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=244-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गेप
गेप r. 1st cl. (ऋ)गेवृ (गेपते) 1. To shake or tremble.<BR>	 2. To move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=244-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गेय|गेयं|गेयः
गेय mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>	 1. A singer.<BR>	 2. A song or chant, what is to be sung<BR>or chanted.<BR>	 n. (-यं) Song, singing.<BR> E. गै to sing, affix यत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=244-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गेव
गेव r. 1st cl. (ऋ) गेवृ(गेवते) To serve, to gratify by service.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=244-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गेष
गेष r. 1st cl. (ऋ)गेषृ(गेषते) To seek, to search, to investigate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=244-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गेष्ण|गेष्णः
गेष्ण m. (-ष्णः)<BR>	 1. A professional singer, an actor, a mime, &c.<BR>	 2. A chanter<BR>of the Sama Veda.<BR> E. गै to sing, and इष्णच् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=244-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गेष्णु|गेष्णुः
गेष्णु m. (-ष्णुः)<BR>	 1. A singer.<BR>	 2. An actor.<BR>	 3. A chanter of the Sama<BR>Veda: see गेष्ण<BR> E. गै to sing, and इष्णुच् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=244-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गेह|गेहं
गेह n. (-हं) A house, a dwelling.<BR> E. ग a name of GANESHA इह् to desire,<BR>affix घञ्; that deity being usually invoked upon laying the found-<BR>ations of a house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=244-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गेहनर्द्दिन्
गेहनर्द्दिन् m. (-र्द्दी) A lazy or effeminate man, a cotquean.<BR> E. गेह a house,<BR>and नर्द्दिन् who makes a noise: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=244-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गेहशूर
गेहशूर m. (-रः) A slothful and trifling man, one who is unfit for con-<BR>cerns beyond those of the house, a cotquean, a house-hero.<BR> E. गेह a<BR>house, and शूर a hero.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=244-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गेहिन्
गेहिन् mfn. (-ही-हिनी-हि) Having a house, householder, &c.<BR> E. गेह, and<BR>इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=244-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गै
गै r. 1st cl. (गायति) To sound, to sing. With उद् or प्र prefixed; (उद्गायति<BR>प्रगायति) To sing, to chant, to sing out or aloud. (उद्गीयते प्रगीयते) To<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=245-a" target="_blank">Page245-a+ 60</a>]<BR>be sung or chanted. With वि (विगायति) To assert repeatedly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=244-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गैर
गैर mfn. (-रः-री-रं) Mountain, mountaineer, mountain-born.<BR> E. गिरि, and<BR>अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=245-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गैरिक|गैरिकं|गैरिकः
गैरिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Mountain, mountain-born or produced n. (-कं)<BR>	 1.<BR>Red chalk, or as sometimes applied, red orpiment.<BR>	 2. Gold.<BR> E. गिरि<BR>a mountain, affix ठक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=245-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गैरेय|गैरेयं
गैरेय mfn. (-यः-यी-यं) Mountain, mountaineer, mountain-born.<BR>	 n. (-यं)<BR>	 1.<BR>Bitumen.<BR>	 2. Red chalk.<BR> E. गिरि a mountain, affix ढक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=245-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गो
गो m. (-गौः)<BR>	 1. Heaven, Svarga or paradise.<BR>	 2. A bull.<BR>	 3. A ray of light.<BR>4. The thunderbolt.<BR>	 5. The moon.<BR>	 6. The sun.<BR>	 7. A kind of sacri-<BR>fice, the sacrifice of a cow.<BR>	 8. The moment of the sun's entering<BR>Taurus. mn (-गौः-गु)<BR>	 1. The hair of the body.<BR>	 2. Water: (in the last<BR>sense some confine it to the mas. plu. गावः and according to others,<BR>it is neuter in several other senses.)<BR>	 f. (-गौः)<BR>	 1. A cow.<BR>	 2. The eye.<BR>3. An arrow.<BR>	 4. quarter, as the east, west, &c.<BR>	 5. Speech; also identi-<BR>fied with the goddess of speech. SARASWATI.<BR>	 6. The earth.<BR>	 7. A<BR>mother.<BR> E. गम् to go, and करणे डो Uṇādi aff. गच्छति अनेन ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=245-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोकण्टक|गोकंटक|गोकण्टकः
गोकण्टक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. The name of a plant: see गोखुर.<BR>	 2. The print of a<BR>cow's hoof or spot so marked.<BR> E. गो the earth or a cow, &c. and<BR>कण्टक a thorn. गोः पृथिव्याः कण्टक इव ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=245-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोकर्ण|गोकर्णः
गोकर्ण m. (-र्णः)<BR>	 1. A span from the tip of the thumb to that of the little<BR>finger.<BR>	 2. A kind of deer, (the Nilgau)<BR>	 3. A mule.<BR>	 4. A class of<BR>demigods.<BR>	 5. A kind of snake.<BR>	 6. A snake in general.<BR>	 7. A place of<BR>pilgrimage on the Malabar coast.<BR>	 f. (-र्णी) A plant, (Aletris hyacin-<BR>thoides:) see मूर्व्वा.<BR> E. गो a cow, and कर्ण an ear, having ears like a<BR>cow, &c. गौः नेत्रं कर्णौ यस्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=245-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोकिराटिका
गोकिराटिका f. (-का) A bird, considered as one kind of the common<BR>Maina, (Turdus salica.)<BR> E. गो the earth, and किर a hog, अट who<BR>goes, with कन् added in the fem. form; resembling a hog, feeding<BR>on ordure, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=245-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोकिल|गोकिलः
गोकिल m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. A plough.<BR>	 2. A pestle.<BR> E. गो the earth, and किल् to<BR>go. affix क; also गोकील.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=245-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोकील|गोकीलः
गोकील m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. A pestle.<BR>	 2. A plough.<BR> E. गो the earth, and कील a pin<BR>or bolt. गोः पृथिव्याः कील इव ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=245-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोकुल|गोकुलं
गोकुल n. (-लं)<BR>	 1. A herd of kine, a multitude of cattle.<BR>	 2. A cow-house<BR>or station.<BR>	 3. A village or tract on the Jumna, the residence of<BR>NANDA and of KṚṢṆA during his youth.<BR>	 n. गो a cow, and कुल an<BR>assemblage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=245-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोकुलिक|गोकुलिकः
गोकुलिक mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>	 1. Squint-eyed.<BR>	 2. One who does not give help<BR>to a cow in the mud.<BR> E. गो the eye, &c. and कुल् to accumulate, affix ठक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=245-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोकृत|गोकृतं
गोकृत n. (-तं) Cowdung.<BR> E. गो a cow, and कृत made.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=245-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोक्षुर|गोक्षुरः
गोक्षुर m. (-रः) The name of a plant; also Gokhura, (Ruellia longifolia,<BR>Rox, it is also applied in Bengal to Tribulus lanuginosus.)<BR>	 n. (-रं)<BR>A cow's hoof.<BR> E. गो a cow, and क्षुर a hoof, the thorns getting be-<BR>tween the hoofs of cattle; also with कन् added गोक्षुरक, and with खुर<BR>a hoof, गोखुर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=245-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोक्षुरक|गोक्षुरकः
गोक्षुरक m. (-कः) See the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=245-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोखुर|गोखुरः
गोखुर m. (-रः) See गोक्षुर; also गोखुरि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=245-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोगोयुग|गोगोयुगं
गोगोयुग n. (-गं) A pair of oxen.<BR> E. गो, and गोयुग a pair. गवोर्द्वित्वम् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=245-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोगोष्ठ|गोगोष्ठं
गोगोष्ठ n. (-ष्ठं) A cattle shed.<BR> E. गो, and गोष्ठ a shed. गोः स्थानम् गा + स्थाने गोष्ठच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=245-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोगृष्टि|गोगृष्टिः
गोगृष्टि f. (-ष्टिः) A cow that has had one calf.<BR> E. गो a cow, and गृष्टि q. v.<BR>the same as the compound. सकृत् प्रमूतायां गवि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=245-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोग्रन्थि|गोग्रंथि|गोग्रन्थिः
गोग्रन्थि m. (-न्थिः)<BR>	 1. Dried cow-dung.<BR>	 2. A station for cows, a cow-yard<BR>or house, &c.<BR> E. गो a cow, ग्रन्थ् to arrange, and इन् aff. गोर्जातो ग्रन्थिः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=245-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोग्रह|गोग्रहः
गोग्रह m. (-हः) Spoil, booty, capture of cattle.<BR> E. गो, and ग्रह seizing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=245-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोग्रास|गोग्रासः
गोग्रास m. (-सः) The ceremony of presenting grass to the cow when<BR>making atonement.<BR> E. गो, and ग्रास a mouthful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=245-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोघ्न|गोघ्नः
गोघ्न mfn. (-घ्नः-घ्नी-घ्नं) Who or what kills kine.<BR>	 m. (-घ्नः) A guest.<BR> E. गो a<BR>cow, and घ्न what kills, from हन् with क affix; a cow being killed<BR>on the arrival of the latter, or being presented to him.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=245-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोघृत|गोघृतं
गोघृत n. (-तं)<BR>	 1. Rain.<BR>	 3. Ghee made from cow's milk.<BR> E. गो the earth,<BR>घृत what sprinkles, from घृ to sprinkle or wet, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=245-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोचर|गोचरः
गोचर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. An object of sense, as sound, shape, colour, &c.<BR>	 2. A.<BR>country, a district.<BR>	 3. The house or mansion of a planet, or its<BR>presence in any sign which is that of a person's nativity.<BR>	 4. Pas-<BR>turage.<BR> E. गो an organ of sense, &c. and चर what goes, from चर् to<BR>go, निपातने अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=245-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोचर्म्मन्|गोचर्मन्
गोचर्म्मन् n. (-र्म्म)<BR>	 1. A cow's hide.<BR>	 2. A hide of land, 300 feet long, by<BR>10 broad: it is also defined as that extent of land, the crop of<BR>which will support a man for a year.<BR> E. गो and चर्म्मन् skin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=245-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोचारक|गोचारकः
गोचारक m. (-कः) A cowhered.<BR> E. गो, चर to go, causal form णिच् ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=245-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोछाल|गोच्छाल|गोच्छालः
गोछाल m. (-लः) The palm of the hand with the fingers extended, &c.<BR>see अलम्बुष. गां भूमिम् आच्छादयति छद-णिच् अण् पृषोदरादित्वात् । भूकदम्बे ।<BR>चाकुलिया ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=245-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोजल|गोजलं
गोजल n. (-लं) Cow's urine.<BR> E. गो, and जल water. गवि जातं जलम् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=245-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोजागरिक|गोजागरिकं|गोजागरिकः
गोजागरिक m. (-कः) A prickly nightshade.<BR>	 n. (-कं) Happy, fortunate,<BR>auspicious.<BR> E. गो the earth, जागृ to wake or to be awake, affix ठक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=245-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोजिह्वा
गोजिह्वा f. (-ह्वा) A potherb growing wild. (Elephantophus scaber.)<BR> E. गो<BR>a cow, and जिह्वा a tongue: the leaves being so compared; also with<BR>कन् added गोजिह्वका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=245-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोडु
गोडु m. (-डुः) A lump of flesh on the navel.<BR> E. गुड् to be sound, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=245-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोडुम्ब|गोडुंब|गोडुंबः|गोडुम्बः
गोडुम्ब mf. (-म्बः-म्बा) The water melon.<BR>	 f. (-म्बा) A kind of cucumber,<BR>(Cucumis madras patanus.)<BR> E. गो the earth, तुवि to hurt, affix क<BR>and त changed to ड. गां भूमिं तुम्बति अर्दति । तुवि-क पृषोदराः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=245-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोणी
गोणी f. (-णी)<BR>	 1. Torn or ragged clothes.<BR>	 2. A sack.<BR>	 3. The measure of<BR>a Drona.<BR> E. गुण् to reckon, affixes घञ् नि-गुणः and ङीष् the deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=245-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोण्ड|गोंड|गोंडः|गोण्डः
गोऽण्ड mfn. (-ण्डः-ण्डा-ण्डं) A person with a prominent navel.<BR>	 m. (-ण्डः) A<BR>man of a low tribe, a mountaineer, especially inhabiting the eastern<BR>portion of the Vindhya range, between the Nerbudda and Krishna<BR>giving name to the province of Gondwana.<BR>	 2. A prominent navel,<BR>or a lump of flesh on the navel, &c.<BR> E. गुडि to enclose, &c. अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=245-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोतम|गोतमः
गोतम m. (-मः) The name of a sage belonging to the family of ANGIRAS<BR>father of SATANANDA; also गौतम. गोभिस्तमो ध्वस्तं यस्य पृषोदरादित्वात् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=245-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोतमान्वय|गोतमान्वयः
गोतमान्वय m. (-यः) A name of SAKYA or SAKYA MUNI, a Bauddha sage.<BR>E. गोतम a sage, and अन्वय lineage; the descendant of GOTAMA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=245-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोतल्लज|गोतल्लजः
गोतल्लज m. (-जः) An excellent cow.<BR> E. गो a cow, तल्लज implying excellence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=245-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोत्र|गोत्रं|गोत्रः
गोत्र n. (-त्रं)<BR>	 1. Family, race, lineage, kin.<BR>	 2. A name, an appellation.<BR>	 3. A<BR>forest.<BR>	 4. A field.<BR>	 5. A Chattra, an umbrella or parasol.<BR>	 6. A road.<BR>7. Knowledge of futurity, inspiration.<BR>	 8. A genus, a class or species<BR>9. A caste, a tribe or subdivision of it into families, as in that of<BR>the Brahman; twenty-four Gotras are reckoned, supposed to be<BR>sprung from and named after celebrated teachers, as SANDILYA,<BR>KAŚYAPA, GAUTAMA, BHARADWAJA, &c.<BR>	 10. Increase.<BR>	 11. Wealth.<BR>f. (-त्रा)<BR>	 1. The earth.<BR>	 2. A herd of kine.<BR>	 m. (-त्रः) A mountain.<BR> E. गु<BR>to sound, and त्र Uṇādi affix, or गो the earth, &c. and त्र what pre-<BR>serves, from त्रै with क aff. गां भूमिं त्रायते त्रैङ् पालने क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=245-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोत्रज|गोत्रजः
गोत्रज mf. (-जः-जा) A relation: in law, the term is nearly equivalent to<BR>the Gentile of Roman law, and is applied to kindred of the same<BR>general family, who are connected by offerings of food and water,<BR>and stands opposed to the Bandhu or cognate kin, who do not<BR>partake in the offerings to the common ancestors: see बन्धु.<BR> E. गोत्र<BR>as above, ज born. गोत्रे समाने वंशे जायते जन-ड ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=245-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोत्रभिद्
गोत्रभिद् m. (-भिद्- or भित्) A name of INDRA.<BR> E. गोत्र a mountain, and<BR>भिद् who splits, (with his thunderbolt.) गोत्रं पर्वतं मेघं वा भिनत्ति ।<BR>भिद्-क्विप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=245-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोत्ररिवथ
गोत्ररिवथ n. (-क्थं) Patrimony, inheritance.<BR> E. गोत्र, and रिवथ wealth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=245-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोद|गोदः
गोद mfn. (-दः-दा-दं) Who or what gives a cow.<BR>	 m. (-दः) The brain.<BR> E. गो<BR>light or a cow, and द what gives. गां नेत्रं दायति शोधयति दै-क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=245-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोदन्त|गोदंत|गोदन्तं
गोदन्त m. (-न्तः)<BR>	 1. Yellow orpiment.<BR>	 2. A cow's tooth.<BR>	 3. A fossile subs-<BR>tance of a white colour, apparently an earthy salt.<BR> E. गो a cow,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=246-a" target="_blank">Page246-a+ 60</a>]<BR>and दन्त a tooth, a cow's tooth, from its similar hardness,<BR>&c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=245-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोदा
गोदा f. (-दा) The Godavari river.<BR> E. गो water, and द who gives; see गोदावरी. गां स्वर्गं ददाति स्नानेन दा-क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=246-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोदान
गोदान n. (-नं) Gift of a cow.<BR> E. गो, and दान gift; or केशान्ताख्ये संस्कारभेदे<BR>also गोप्रदान गावः केशलोमानि वा दीयन्ते खण्ड्यन्ते अत्र । आधारे ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=246-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोदारण|गोदारणं
गोदारण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. A plough.<BR>	 2. A spade or hoe,<BR> E. गो the earth, and<BR>दारण what cuts or tears. गां भूमिं दारयति दृ-णिच्-ल्यु ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=246-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोदावरी
गोदावरी f. (-री) The name of a river in the peninsula, the Godavari.<BR>E, गो water, and द what gives, गोद and आवृ to cover or conceal;<BR>affixes अप् and ङीप्. गां स्वर्गं ददाति स्नानात् दा वनिप् ङीप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=246-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोदुग्ध
गोदुग्ध n. (-ग्धं) Cow's milk.<BR> E. गो, and दुग्ध milk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=246-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोदुह
गोदुह m. (-धुक्) A cowherd, a milkman.<BR> E. गो a cow, दुह to milk, and<BR>क्विप् affix; also with क affix गोदुह, nom. (-हः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=246-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोदोहनी
गोदोहनी f. (-नी) A milk pail.<BR> E. गो a cow, and दुह to milk, with भावे<BR>ल्युट् and ङीप् aff. आधारे ल्युट् गोदोहनकाले ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=246-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोद्रव|गोद्रवः
गोद्रव m. (-वः) Cow's urine.<BR> E. गो, and द्रव what runs from. गो + द्रु-अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=246-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोधन|गोधनं|गोधनः
गोधन n. (-नं) A herd of Cows, a multitude or number of cattle, especi-<BR>ally if considered as property.<BR>	 m. (-नः) A large headed arrow. E.<BR>गो a cow, and धन wealth. गवां धनं समूहः । गोसमूहे ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=246-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोधा
गोधा f. (-धा)<BR>	 1. A leathern fence worn by archers on the left arm, to<BR>prevent its being injured by the bowstring.<BR>	 2. An iguana, either<BR>the Gosap or the alligator.<BR> E. गुध् to surround, affixes घञ् and<BR>टाप्; see गोधिक. गुध्यते वेष्ट्यते बाहुरनया करणे घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=246-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोधापदिका
गोधापदिका f. (-का) Cissus pedata,<BR> E. कन् added to the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=246-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोधापदी
गोधापदी f. (-दी) A plant, (Cissus pedata.)<BR> E. गोधा, and पद for पाद a foot,<BR>affix ङीष्, the root being compared to an alligator's foot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=246-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोधि|गोधिः
गोधि m. (-धिः)<BR>	 1. The forehead.<BR>	 2. The Gangetic alligator.<BR>	 3. An igua-<BR>na.<BR> E. गो the eye or water, and धा to possess, with आधारे इन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=246-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोधिका
गोधिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. The Gangetic alligator.<BR>	 2. The iguana.<BR> E. कन् with<BR>the fem form added to गोधा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=246-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोधिकात्मज|गोधिकात्मजः
गोधिकात्मज m. (-जः) The iguana.<BR> E. गोधा An alligator, and आत्मज off-<BR>spring, here used to imply diminution: so गोधिकापुत्र, &c.<BR>षष्ठीतत्पुरुषः समासः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=246-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोधूम|गोधूमः
गोधूम m. (-मः) Wheat: see the next.<BR> E. गुध्-वा˚ उम ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=246-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोधूम|गोधूमः
गोधूम m. (-मः)<BR>	 1. Wheat.<BR>	 2. The orange.<BR>	 3. The name of a drug.<BR> E. गुध्<BR>to surround, and ऊम Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=246-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोधूमचूर्ण|गोधूमचूर्णं
गोधूमचूर्ण n. (-र्णं) Wheat flour.<BR> E. गोधूम, and चूर्ण powder. षष्ठीतत्पुरुषः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=246-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोधूमसम्भव|गोधूमसंभव|गोधूमसम्भवं
गोधूमसम्भव n. (-वं) Sour paste.<BR> E. गोधूम, and सम्भव produced. सम् + भू-<BR>अपादाने अप् गोधूमः सम्भवोऽस्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=246-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोधूलि|गोधूलिः
गोधूलि f. (-लिः) A period of the day, in the hot season when the sun is<BR>half risen; in the cold and dewy seasons, when the sun is full but<BR>mild; and in the three other seasons, sunset.<BR> E. गो, and धूलि dust.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=246-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोधेनु|गोधेनुः
गोधेनु (-नुः) A milch cow.<BR> E. गो a cow, and धेनु the same. सवत्सायां गवि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=246-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोधेर|गोधेरः
गोधेर mfn. (-रा-रं) A guardian, a protector, a preserver.<BR> E. गुध् एरच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=246-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोनन्दी|गोनंदी
गोनन्दी f. (-न्दी) The female of the Sārasa or Indian crane.<BR> E. गो water,<BR>नदि to be happy, अच् and ङीष् affs. गवि जले नन्दति । नन्द-अच् ङीष् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=246-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोनर्द|गोनर्दः|गोनर्द्द|गोनर्द्दं|गोनर्द्दः
गोनर्द m. (-र्दः) The Sārasa or Indian crane.<BR>	 n. (-र्दं) A fragrant grass,<BR>(Cyperus rotundus.)<BR> E. गो water, नर्द् to sound, affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=246-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोनर्द्दीय|गोनर्दीय|गोनर्दीयः|गोनर्द्दीयः
गोनर्द्दीय m. (-यः) A name of the saint PATANJALI, the founder of Yoga<BR>philosophy.<BR> E. गो heaven, नर्द्दीय to be sounded or celebrated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=246-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोनस|गोनसः
गोनस m. (-सः)<BR>	 1. A large kind of snake, by some considered to be the<BR>same with the Boa or Bor.<BR>	 2. A kind of gem.<BR> E. गो a cow, and नस<BR>a nose, cow-nosed; also गोनास.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=246-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोनाथ|गोनाथः
गोनाथ m. (-थः)<BR>	 1. A bull.<BR>	 2. A herdsman.<BR> E. गो, and नाथ master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=246-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोनास|गोनासं|गोनासः
गोनास mf. (-सः-सा) A snake: see गोनस.<BR> E. गोरिव नासा अस्य वा नसादेशः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=246-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोनिष्यन्द|गोनिष्यंद|गोनिष्यन्दः
गोनिष्यन्द n. (-ङ्गं) Cow's urine.<BR> E. गो, and निष्यन्द what oozes.<BR> E. गो +<BR>निष्यन्द-अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=246-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोप|गोपः
गोप mfn. (-पः-पा-पं)<BR>	 1. A helper, a friend or patron.<BR>	 2. A preserver, a<BR>cherisher.<BR>	 3. Who or what hides or conceals.<BR>	 m. (-पः)<BR>	 1. Superin-<BR>tendent of a district.<BR>	 2. The head of a cowpen.<BR>	 3. A herdsman, a<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=246-b" target="_blank">Page246-b+ 60</a>]<BR>cowherd, a milkman by caste and occupation.<BR>	 4. A king.<BR>	 5.<BR>A Myrrh: see गोपरस.<BR>	 f. (-पा or -पी) A plant, (Echites frutescens)<BR>f. (-पा) A milk-woman, a female cowherd.<BR>	 f. (-पी)<BR>	 1. A cowherd's<BR>wife, but especially applied to those of Brindaban, the compani-<BR>ons and objects of KṚṢṆA'S juvenile sports, and who are consid-<BR>ered sometimes as holy or celestial personages.<BR>	 2. A protectress.<BR>3. Nature, elementary nature.<BR> E. गो the earth &c. and प what<BR>preserves; also in some sense गुप् to hide, to protect, &c. affix क,<BR>fem. affix टाप् or ङीष्, गां भूमिं वा पाति रक्षति पा-क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=246-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोपक|गोपकः
गोपक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) One who guards or protects.<BR>	 m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. Myrrh.<BR>2. The Superintendent of a district.<BR> E. कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=246-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोपकन्या
गोपकन्या f. (-न्या)<BR>	 1. The daughter of a cowhered.<BR>	 2. A nymph of Brin-<BR>daban.<BR>	 3. A medicinal plant.<BR> E. गोप, and कन्या a daughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=246-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोपघोण्टा
गोपघोण्टा f. (-ण्टा) A wild sort of jujube, (Zizyphus nepeca.)<BR> E. गोप a cow-<BR>herd, and घोण्टा the jujube.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=246-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोपति|गोपतिः
गोपति m. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. A name of ŚIVA.<BR>	 2. Of INDRA.<BR>	 3. The sun.<BR>	 4. A king.<BR>5. A bull.<BR> E. गो the earth, &c. पति lord or master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=246-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोपतिचाप
गोपतिचाप m. (-पः) The rainbow.<BR> E. गोपति INDRA, and चाप a bow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=246-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोपदल|गोपदलः
गोपदल m. (-लः) The areca tree.<BR> E. गोप preserving, and दल a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=246-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोपन|गोपनं
गोपन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Protecting, guarding.<BR>	 2. Concealment, hiding, 3. Re-<BR>viling. abuse.<BR>	 4. Flurry, hurry, alarm.<BR>	 5. Light, lustre.<BR>	 6. The<BR>leaf of the Laurus cassia.<BR> E. गुप् to hide, भावे ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=246-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोपनीय|गोपनीयं
गोपनीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>	 1. Secret, mysterious, to be concealed or hid-<BR>den.<BR>	 2. To be preserved or protected.<BR> E. गुप to hide, &c. अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=246-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोपबधू
गोपबधू f. (-धूः)<BR>	 1. The wife of a cowhered.<BR>	 2. A plant, (Asclepias<BR>pseudosara)<BR> E. गोप. and बधू wife. षष्ठीतत्पुरुषः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=246-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोपबधूटी
गोपबधूटी f. (-टी) The youthful wife of a cowherd.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=246-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोपभद्र|गोपभद्रं
गोपभद्र m. (-द्रः) The fibrous root of a waterlily.<BR> E. गोप् a cowhered,<BR>and भद्र lucky, auspicious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=246-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोपभद्रिका
गोपभद्रिका f. (-का) The name of a tree: see गम्भारी.<BR> E. गोप a preserver.<BR>and भद्र auspicious, and संज्ञायां कन् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=246-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोपरस|गोपरसः
गोपरस m. (-सः) Gum myrrh.<BR> E. गोप secret, and रस juice exuding in a<BR>manner or place unknown.<BR> E. गां जलं पिवति पा-क गोपः रसोऽस्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=246-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोपवल्ली
गोपवल्ली f. (-ल्ली)<BR>	 1. A creeping plant, (Echites frutescens:) see श्यामलता<BR>2. Another plant, (Asclepias pseudosara.)<BR> E. गोप a cowherd, and<BR>वल्ली a pedicle, being used in medicines for cattle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=246-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोपाटविक
गोपाटविक m. (-कः) A cowherd.<BR> E. गो, and पाटविक clever.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=246-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोपानसी
गोपानसी f. (-सी)<BR>	 1. The wood of a thatch.<BR>	 2. A crooked beam which<BR>supports it.<BR>	 3. The bamboo frame work on which it rests.<BR> E. गवां<BR>किरणानां पानं शोषणं गोपानं तत्स्यति सो-क गौरादित्वात् ङीष् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=246-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोपायक
गोपायक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) A preserver, a cherisher, one who guards or<BR>protects.<BR> E. गुप् to preserve, आय + ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=246-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोपायित|गोपायितं
गोपायित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Preserved, protected, cherished.<BR> E. गुप् to pro-<BR>tect, affix आय-कर्मणि वाच्ये क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=246-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोपाल|गोपालः
गोपाल m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. A King, a sovereign.<BR>	 2. A cowherd.<BR>	 3. A name of<BR>KṚṢṆA.<BR> E. गो the earth, &c. and पाल who preserves or protects.<BR>गां भूमिं पशुभेदं वा पालयति पालि अण् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=246-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोपालक|गोपालकः
गोपालक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. ŚIVA.<BR>	 2. KṚṢṆA.<BR>	 3. A cow keeper or protector. E.<BR>गो a cow or the earth, पाल् to cherish, and ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=246-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोपालिका
गोपालिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. A kind of worm.<BR>	 2. A female cowherd: see गोपालक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=246-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोपाष्टमी
गोपाष्टमी f. (-मी) The eighth lunation of the light half of Kartik, on<BR>which KṚṢṆA became a cowherd; cows are to be worshipped. E.<BR>गोप, and अष्टम the eighth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=246-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोपिन्
गोपिन् mfn. (-पी-पिनी-पि) A protector, one who preserves or protects.<BR>	 f.<BR>(-नी)<BR>	 1. A creeping plant, (Echites frutescens.)<BR>	 2. Acowherd's<BR>wife.<BR> E. गुप् to preserve, णिनि and ङीप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=246-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोपिका
गोपिका f. (-का) A female cowherd, &c.: see गोपक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=246-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोपिल|गोपिलः
गोपिल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) One who preserves or protects.<BR> E. गुप, and इलच्<BR>unadi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=246-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोपीचन्दन
गोपीचन्दन n. (-नं) A species of white clay, said to be brought from<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=247-a" target="_blank">Page247-a+ 60</a>]<BR>Dwaraka and used by the worshippers of VIṢṆU to smear their<BR>faces with.<BR> E. गोपी, and चन्दन Sandal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=246-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोपीथ|गोपीथं|गोपीथः
गोपीथ m. (-थः) preserving, protecting.<BR>	 n. (-थ) A holy place, a place of<BR>pilgrimage.<BR> E. गोप preserving, and थक Uṇādi affix, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=247-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोपुच्छ|गोपुच्छः
गोपुच्छ m. (-च्छः)<BR>	 1. A cowtail.<BR>	 2. A sort of necklace, one of four or<BR>thirty-four strings.<BR>	 3. A sort of monkey.<BR> E. गो a cow, and पुच्छ a<BR>tail, resembling or possessing a cow's tail. गोः पुच्छ इव पुच्छो यस्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=247-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोपुटी
गोपुटी f. (-टी) Large cardamoms.<BR> E. गोरिव पुट मस्याः स्थू लैलायाम् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=247-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोपुटिक|गोपुटिकं
गोपुटिक n. (-कं) A temple or edifice consecrated to ŚIVA'S bull.<BR> E. गो a<BR>cow, and पुट् to enclose, affix इकन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=247-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोपुर|गोपुरं
गोपुर n. (-रं)<BR>	 1. A town gate.<BR>	 2. A gate in general.<BR>	 3. The ornamented<BR>gateway of a temple.<BR>	 4. A kind of grass, (Cyperus rotundus.) E.<BR>पर अग्रगमने क गवां पुरं गवा जलेन पूर्य्यते पॄ घञर्थे क वा ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=247-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोपुरीष|गोपुरीषं
गोपुरीष n. (-षं) Cow-dung.<BR> E. गो, and पुरीष dung.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=247-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोपेन्द्र|गोपेंद्र|गोपेन्द्रः
गोपेन्द्र m. (-न्द्रः) A name of KṚṢṆA or VIṢṆU.<BR> E. गोप a cowherd, and<BR>इन्द्र lord or chief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=247-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोपेश|गोपेशः
गोपेश m. (-शः)<BR>	 1. A name of SAKYA MUNI, a Buddha.<BR>	 2. A name of<BR>KṚṢṆA.<BR>	 3. A chief herdsman, the keeper or owner of kine.<BR>	 4. A<BR>name of NANDA.<BR> E. गोप cowherd, and ईश lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=247-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोप्तृ
गोप्तृ mfn. (-प्ता-प्त्री-प्तृ) A preserver, A protector, one who defends or<BR>cherishes.<BR> E. गुप् to preserve, &c. affix तृच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=247-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोप्य|गोप्यः
गोप्य mfn. (-प्यः-प्या-प्यं)<BR>	 1. To be cherished or preserved.<BR>	 2. To be kept<BR>secret or hidden.<BR>	 3. To be kept, to be taken care of.<BR>	 m. (-प्यः)<BR>1. A slave.<BR>	 2. The son of a female slave.<BR> E. गुप् to preserve, &c.<BR>कर्मणि यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=247-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोप्यक|गोप्यकः
गोप्यक m. (-कः) A servant or slave.<BR> E. कन् added to the proceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=247-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोप्याधि|गोप्याधिः
गोप्याधि f. (-धिः) A pledge, that is not be used, but to be carefully<BR>preserved.<BR> E. गोप्य to be preserved, and आधि a pledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=247-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोप्रकाण्ड|गोप्रकांड|गोप्रकाण्डं
गोप्रकाण्ड n. (-ण्डं) An excellent cow.<BR> E. गो a cow, and प्रकाण्ड excellent;<BR>the compound is always neuter. प्रशस्तो गौ नित्यसमासः परनिपातः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=247-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोप्रचार|गोप्रचारः
गोप्रचार m. (-रः) Pasturage ground.<BR> E. गो, and प्रचार going. प्रचरति अस्मिन्<BR>प्र + चर अधारे घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=247-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोफणा
गोफणा f. (-णा) A sling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=247-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोबध
गोबध m. (-धः) Killing a cow.<BR> E. गो, and बध killing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=247-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोबाल|गोबालः
गोबाल m. (-लः) The hair of a cow.<BR> E. गो, and बाल hair. षष्ठीतत्पुरुषः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=247-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोभण्डीर|गोभण्डीरः
गोभण्डीर m. (-रः) A water fowl.<BR> E. गो water, भटि to sound affix ईरन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=247-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोम
गोम r. 10th cl. (गोमयति) To smear, to anoint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=247-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोमक्षिका
गोमक्षिका f. (-का) A gadfly.<BR> E. गो, a cow, and मक्षिका a fly stinging<BR>cattle. गोः क्लेशदायिका मक्षिका (डांँस्) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=247-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोमण्डल|गोमंडल
गोमण्डल n. (-लं) The earth, the globe. गोसमूहे.<BR> E. गो, and मण्डल sphere.<BR>षष्ठीतत्पुरुषः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=247-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोमत्|गोमन्त्
गोमत् mfn. (-मान्-मती-मत्) Possessing herds, rich in cattle.<BR>	 f. (-मती) The<BR>name of a river, the Goomti, in the province of Oude.<BR>	 2. A<BR>prayer or formula of the Vedas to be repeated during expiation<BR>for killing a cow.<BR> E. गो a cow or water, and मतुप् aff. गौरस्ति अस्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=247-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोमतल्लिका
गोमतल्लिका f. (-का) A tractable and good cow.<BR> E. गो a cow, मतल्लिका excellent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=247-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोमध्यमध्य
गोमध्यमध्य mfn. (-ध्यः-ध्या-ध्यं) Slender in the waist.<BR> E. गो a cow &c. मध्य<BR>middle: repeated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=247-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोमन्त|गोमन्तः
गोमन्त m. (-न्तः)<BR>	 1. The name of a mountain.<BR>	 2. An owner of cattle.<BR>3. A herd of cattle.<BR> E. गो the earth, मन् to mind, झ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=247-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोमय|गोमयं|गोमयः
गोमय mn. (-यः-यं)<BR>	 1. Cowdung.<BR>	 2. The property or nature of a cow.<BR>E. गो a cow, and मयट् affix of relation or comprehension.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=247-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोमयच्छत्र|गोमयच्छत्रं|गोमयछत्र
गोमयच्छत्र n. (-त्रं) A mushroom, a fungus.<BR> E. गोमय cowdung, and छत्र a<BR>Chatta or parasol.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=247-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोमयच्छत्रिका|गोमयछत्रिका
गोमयच्छत्रिका f. (-का) A kind of fungus or mushroom.<BR> E. कन् and the<BR>fem. form added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=247-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोमयप्रिय|गोमयप्रियं
गोमयप्रिय n. (-यं) A sort of grass, (Andropogon schœnanthus.) भूतृणे,<BR>शिलीन्ध्रे<BR> E. गोमय cow-dung, and प्रिय favourable to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=247-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोमयोत्था
गोमयोत्था f. (-त्था) A kind of beetle found in cowdung.<BR> E. गोमय cow-<BR>dung, and उत्थ what rises or is generated. उद् + स्था-क टाप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=247-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोमयोद्भव|गोमयोद्भवः
गोमयोद्भव m. (-वः) Cassia fistula.<BR> E. गोमय, and उद्भव born, produced, re-<BR>quiring manure. गोमयादुद्भवति उद् + भू अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=247-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोमायु|गोमायुः
गोमायु m. (-युः)<BR>	 1. A jackal.<BR>	 2. A kind of Gandharba or celestial mu-<BR>sician.<BR>	 3. The bile or bilious humor of the cow.<BR> E. गो sound, &c.<BR>मा to measure, and उण् Uṇādi affix, य inserted, or गो a cow, and<BR>मायु bile. गां विकृतां वाचं मिनाति ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=247-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोमिथुन
गोमिथुन n. (-नं) A pair of cattle.<BR> E. गो, and मिथुन a couple.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=247-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोमिन्
गोमिन् mfn. (-मी-मिनी-मि) Rich in herds, &c.<BR>	 m. (-मी)<BR>	 1. The owner of<BR>cattle.<BR>	 2. A jackal.<BR>	 3. A worshipper.<BR>	 4. An attendant on a<BR>Buddha.<BR> E. गो a cow, &c. मिनि aff. गौरस्ति अस्य मिनि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=247-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोमिल
गोमिल m. (-लः) Name of a Muni.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=247-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोमीन|गोमीनः
गोमीन m. (-नः) A sort of fish, the bull-fish.<BR> E. गो, and मीन a fish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=247-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोमुख|गोमुखं|गोमुखः
गोमुख n. (-खं)<BR>	 1. A house build unevenly or crookedly, viz. with<BR>angles, projections, &c.<BR>	 2. A kind of musical instrument, (a sort<BR>of horn or trumpet)<BR>	 3. Spreading unguents, plastering, smear-<BR>ing.<BR>	 4. A hole in a wall made by thieves, &c. a breach.<BR>	 m. (-खः)<BR>1. A shark.<BR>	 2. A kind of Yakṣa; according to the Jainas, a<BR>demigod subservient to their deified saints.<BR>	 nf. (-खं-खी) A cloth-<BR>bag, containing a rosary into which the hand is thrust to count<BR>the beads.<BR>	 f. (-खी) The chasm in the Himālaya mountains through<BR>which the Ganges flows, erroneously conceived by the Hindus to<BR>be of the shape of a cow's mouth.<BR>	 2. A river in Bengal.<BR> E. गो a<BR>cow, and मुख face, having the face of a cow, &c. गोमुखमिव मुखमस्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=247-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोमूढ
गोमूढ mfn. (-ढः-ढा-ढं) Stupid as an ox.<BR> E. गो, and मूढ foolish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=247-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोमूत्र|गोमूत्रं
गोमूत्र n. (-त्रं) Cow's urine.<BR> E. गो, and मूत्र urine. षष्ठीतत्पुरुषः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=247-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोमूत्रिका
गोमूत्रिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. A kind of grass, described as growing in corn<BR>fields, of a reddish colour, and eaten by cattle, commonly Tam-<BR>bada (ताम्बड)<BR>	 2. A verse the second half of which repeats nearly<BR>all the syllables of the first.<BR>	 3. A form of calculation.<BR> E. गो, मूत्र<BR>urine, ठन् affix; operating on cows as a diuretic. गोर्मूत्रस्येव गतिरस्ति<BR>अत्र ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=247-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोमेद|गोमेदः
गोमेद m. (-दः) A yellow gem: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=247-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोमेदक|गोमेदकं|गोमेदकः
गोमेदक mn. (-कः-कं)<BR>	 1. A gem or precious stone brought from the<BR>Himālaya and Indus, described as of four sorts, white, pale<BR>yellow, red, and dark blue, perhaps varieties of a gate.<BR>2. A kind of poison: see काकोल.<BR>	 6. Smearing the body with un-<BR>guents.<BR> E. गो the eye, मिद् to anoint, &c. affix अच् and कन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=247-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोमेदसन्निभ|गोमेदसंनिभ|गोमेदसन्निभः
गोमेदसन्निभ m. (-भः) Chalcedony or opal.<BR> E. गोमेद, and सन्निभ what resem-<BR>bles.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=247-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोमेध|गोमेधः
गोमेध m. (-धः) The offering or sacrifice of a cow.<BR> E. गो a cow, and मेध<BR>sacrifice. मेध-वधे आधारे घञ् । षष्ठीतत्पुरुषः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=247-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोयान
गोयान n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. A cart.<BR>	 2. A carriage drawn by oxen.<BR> E. गो, and यान a<BR>vehicle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=247-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोयुग
गोयुग n. (-गं) A yoke of oxen.<BR> E. गो, and युग a pair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=247-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोरक्ष|गोरक्षः
गोरक्ष mfn. (-क्षः-क्षा-क्षं) A cow keeper, the cherisher or preserver of kine.<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>	 1. The orange.<BR>	 2. Keeping or tending cattle.<BR>	 3. A name of<BR>ŚIVA.<BR>	 f. (-क्षी) A small shrub.<BR> E. गो a cow, and रक्ष who preserves.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=247-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोरक्षक
गोरक्षक m. (-कः) A cow keeper, one who tends cattle.<BR> E. कन् added to<BR>the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=247-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोरक्षजम्बू
गोरक्षजम्बू f. (-म्बूः)<BR>	 1. Wheat.<BR>	 2. A plant, (Hedysarum lagopodioides;)<BR>also गाङ्गेरुकी.<BR>	 3. The fruit of the jujube.<BR> E. गोरक्ष, and जम्बू a rose-<BR>apple.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=247-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोरक्षण
गोरक्षण n. (णं) Tending or taking charge of cattle<BR> E. गो, and रक्षण protecting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=247-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोरक्षतण्डुला
गोरक्षतण्डुला f. (-ला) A plant, (Hedysarum lagopodioides.)<BR> E. गोरक्ष cow-<BR>preserving, and तण्डुल grain, used in medicines for cattle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=247-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोरक्ष्य
गोरक्ष्य n. (-क्ष्यं) Tending cattle.<BR> E. गो, and रक्ष्य to be preserved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=247-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोरङ्कु|गोरंकु|गोरङ्कुः
गोरङ्कु m. (-ङ्कुः)<BR>	 1. A water-fowl.<BR>	 2. A prisoner, a person or animal<BR>confined.<BR>	 3. A naked man, a mendicant, &c. wandering about<BR>without clothes.<BR> E. गो water, sky, &c. रङ्कु a kind of deer: as it were,<BR>the water deer, &c. गवा वाचा रङ्कुरिव ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=247-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोरण|गोरणं
गोरण n. (-णं) Effort, exertion.<BR> E. गुर् to make effort, affix ल्युट्; also गुरण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=248-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोरस|गोरसः
गोरस mn. (-सः-सं)<BR>	 1. Milk.<BR>	 2. Curdled or coagulated milk.<BR>	 3. Butter-<BR>milk.<BR> E. गो a cow, and रस juice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=248-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोरसज|गोरसजं
गोरसज n. (-जं)<BR>	 1. Butter-milk.<BR>	 2. Curds,<BR> E. गोरस, and ज produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=248-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोराज|गोराजः
गोराज m. (-जः) A bull.<BR> E. गो a cow, and राजन् a king, टच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=248-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोराटी
गोराटी f. (-टी) A small bird, (Turdus salica.<BR> E. गो speech, रट् to utter,<BR>affix अच्, feminine affix ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=248-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोरुत|गोरुतं
गोरुत n. (-तं) A measure of distance equal to two Crosa or Cos: see गव्यूतिः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=248-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोरोच|गोरोचं
गोरोच n. (-चं) Yellow orpiment.<BR> E. गो, and रोच what shines. गवा किरणेन<BR>रोचते रोच-अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=248-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोरोचना
गोरोचना f. (-ना) A bright yellow pigment prepared from the urine of a<BR>cow, or vomited in the shape of scibulæ by the animal; or accor-<BR>ding to some, found in the head of a cow; it is employed in paint-<BR>ing and dying, and is of especial virtue in marking the foreheads<BR>of the Hindus with the Tilaka or sectarial mark; it is also used in<BR>medicine as a sedative, tonic, and anthelmintic remedy, &c.<BR> E. गो a<BR>cow, रुचि to shine, affix ल्युट्. गोभ्यो जाता रोचना हरिद्रा ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=248-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोर्द्द|गोर्द|गोर्दः|गोर्द्दं
गोर्द्द n. (-र्द्दं) The brain.<BR> E. गुर् to endeavor, and दन् affix; also गोद.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=248-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोल|गोलं|गोलः
गोल mn. (-लः-लं) A circle, a ball, any thing round or globular.<BR>	 m. (-लः)<BR>1. A widow's bastard.<BR>	 2. Myrrh.<BR>	 3. A tree, (Vangueria spinosa.)<BR>4. A globe, celestial or terrestrial.<BR>	 5. Conjunction of planets, or<BR>the presence of several in one sign.<BR>	 f. (-ला)<BR>	 1. A globe. a sphere, a<BR>Mandala.<BR>	 2. A wooden ball with which children play.<BR>	 3. A woman's<BR>female friend.<BR>	 4. The Godavari river.<BR>	 5. A large water jar.<BR>	 6. Ink.<BR>7. Red arsenic.<BR>	 8. A name of the goddess DURGĀ.<BR> E. गो heaven,<BR>water, &c. and ल what gets or receives; again, गुड् to be round,<BR>&c. affix अच् and ड changed to ल. डलयोरैक्यात् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=248-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोलक|गोलकं|गोलकः
गोलक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A wooden ball for playing with, or any thing globu-<BR>lar, a sphere, a globe, &c.<BR>	 2. A widow's bastard.<BR>	 3. A water jar.<BR>4. Gum myrrh, 5. Pease.<BR>	 n. (-कं) The heaven of KṚṢṆA.<BR> E. कन्<BR>added to the preceding. गुड-ण्वुल् डस्य लः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=248-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोलाङ्गूल|गोलांगूल|गोलाङ्गूलः
गोलाङ्गूल m. (-लः) A kind of monkey, described as of a black colour,<BR>and having a tail like a cow.<BR> E. गो a cow, and लाङ्गूल a tail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=248-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोलाध्याय|गोलाध्यायः
गोलाध्याय m. (-यः) The division of mathematical science which treats<BR>of the spheres, spherics.<BR> E. गोल the globe, and अध्याय chapter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=248-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोलास|गोलासः
गोलास m. (-सः) A mushroom, a kind of fungus springing from cowdung.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=248-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोलिह|गोलिहः
गोलिह m. (-हः) A plant, commonly Ghantaparuli.<BR> E. गो a cow, and<BR>लिह to lick, affix क; upon which kine graze. गोभिर्लिह्यते लिह-घञर्थे क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=248-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोलीढ|गोलीढः
गोलीढ m. (-ढः) A plant: see the preceding.<BR> E. गो, and लिह as above,<BR>affix क्त. गोभिर्लिह्यते लिह क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=248-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोलोक|गोलोकं|गोलोकः
गोलोक n. (-कं) The heaven of KṚṢṆA.<BR> E. गो a cow, and लोक world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=248-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोलोमिका
गोलोमिका f. (-का) A kind of small shrub.<BR> E. गोलोमन् cow's hair, कन्<BR>affix, fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=248-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोलोमी
गोलोमी f. (-मी)<BR>	 1. A kind of bent grass, with white blossoms; also श्वेत-<BR>दूर्ब्बा.<BR>	 2. Root of sweet flag. Orris root.<BR>	 4. A whore. a harlot.<BR>	 5. A<BR>small shrub.<BR> E. गो the earth, &c. and लोमन् hair, the hair of the<BR>earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=248-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोवन्दनी
गोवन्दनी f. (-नी) A plant bearing a fragrant seed: see प्रियङ्गु<BR> E. गो the<BR>earth, and वन्दनी praising.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=248-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोवर्द्धन
गोवर्द्धन m. (-नः) A celebrated hill in Brindaban or the country about<BR>Mathura: it was upheld by KṚṢṆA upon one finger, to shelter<BR>the cowherds from a storm excited by INDRA, as a test of the for-<BR>mer's divinity.<BR> E. गो a cow, and वर्द्धन increasing; pasturing cattle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=248-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोवर्द्धनधर
गोवर्द्धनधर m. (-रः) A name of KṚṢṆA or VIṢṆU.<BR> E. गोवर्द्धन Gober-<BR>dhana, and धर who upholds: see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=248-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोवशा
गोवशा f. (-शा) A barren cow.<BR> E. गो a cow, and वशा barren.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=248-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोविन्द|गोविंद|गोविन्दः
गोविन्द m. (-न्दः)<BR>	 1. One of the most usual appellations of KṚṢṆA or<BR>VIṢṆU in that form.<BR>	 2. A name of VṚHASPATI, regent of<BR>JUPITER.<BR>	 3. A cow-keeper, one who protects, cherishes or owns<BR>cattle.<BR> E. गो language, here the language of the Vedas especially,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=248-b" target="_blank">Page248-b+ 60</a>]<BR>and विन्द who knows, from विद् to know, with श affix; also गो<BR>heaven, a cow, विद् to obtain, by whom heaven is obtained, or who<BR>obtains felicity by protecting kine. गां वेदमयीं वाणीं, भुवं धेनुं स्वर्गं वा<BR>विन्दति ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=248-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोविष्
गोविष् f. (-विट्) Cow-dung.<BR> E. गो a cow, and विष् ordure; also गोविष्ठा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=248-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोवृन्द|गोवृंद|गोवृन्दं
गोवृन्द n. (-न्दं)<BR>	 1. Property in cattle, possession of flocks and herds.<BR>	 2.<BR>A herd, a drove of cattle.<BR> E. गो a cow, and वृन्द a heap, a multitude.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=248-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोवृन्दारक|गोवृंदारक|गोवृन्दारकः
गोवृन्दारक m. (-कः) A capital cow.<BR> E. गो a cow, and वृन्दारक affix of<BR>pre-eminence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=248-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोवृष|गोवृषः
गोवृष m. (-षः) A bull. N. गो a cow, and वृष best, pre-eminent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=248-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोव्रज|गोव्रजः
गोव्रज m. (-जः) A station for cattle.<BR> E. गो and व्रज a pen. a fold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=248-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोशकृत्
गोशकृत् n. (-कृत्) Cow dung.<BR> E. गो a cow, and शकृत् ordure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=248-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोशाल|गोशालं
गोशाल mfn. sub. (-लः-ला-लं) A cow-house. adj. Born in a cow-house. E.<BR>गो a cow, and शाला a hall.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=248-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोशीर्ष|गोशीर्षं|गोशीर्षः
गोशीर्ष n. (-र्षं)<BR>	 1. A kind of Sandal, described as of the colour of brass,<BR>and of great fragrance.<BR>	 2. The head of a cow.<BR> E. गो a cow, and शीर्ष<BR>the head.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=248-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोशीर्षक|गोशीर्षकः
गोशीर्षक m. (-कः) A plant; also called Drona pushpa.<BR> E. कन् added to<BR>गोशीर्ष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=248-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोशृङ्ग|गोशृङ्गः
गोशृङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः) A tree; also Berbera.<BR>	 n. (-ङ्गं) The horn of a cow.<BR> E. गो,<BR>and शृङ्ग a horn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=248-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोष्ठ|गोष्ठं|गोष्ठः
गोष्ठ r. 1st cl. (गोष्ठते) To assemble, to collect, to heap together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=248-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोष्ठ|गोष्ठं|गोष्ठः
गोष्ठ mn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठं)<BR>	 1. A cowpen, a fold for cattle, any place where animals<BR>are kept.<BR>	 2. A station of cow-herds.<BR>	 f. (-ष्ठी)<BR>	 1. An assembly, a meet-<BR>ing.<BR>	 2. Conversation, discourse, dialogue, dispute.<BR>	 3. Family con-<BR>nexions, but especially the dependent or junior branches.<BR>	 4. A<BR>dramatic composition in one act.<BR> E. गो a cow, and ष्ठ from स्था to<BR>stay, with क affix; here meaning the place of abiding, or गोष्ठ to<BR>assemble, affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=248-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोष्ठवेदिका
गोष्ठवेदिका f. (-का) A mound or altar in a cowpen.<BR> E. गोष्ठ, and वेदिका a mound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=248-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोष्ठश्व|गोष्ठश्वः
गोष्ठश्व mfn. (-श्वः-श्वं-श्व) Malignant, censorious, envious: especially appli-<BR>ed to a person who stays at home, and slanders his neighbours. E.<BR>गोष्ठ a cowpen, in the first case used for abode in general, and श्वि to<BR>increase, affix ड, who magnifies himself in his own house.<BR>	 m. (-श्वः)<BR>A horse in a cowpen.<BR> E. गोष्ठ, and अश्व a horse, the form is irregular.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=248-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोष्ठाष्टमी
गोष्ठाष्टमी f. (-मी) A particular holiday: see गोपाष्टमी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=248-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोष्ठीपति|गोष्ठीपतिः
गोष्ठीपति m. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. The chief person in an assembly, a president.<BR>	 2.<BR>The master of a family.<BR> E. गोष्ठी, and पति master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=248-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोष्पद|गोष्पदं
गोष्पद n. (-दं)<BR>	 1. A spot frequented by kine.<BR>	 2. A measure, as much as<BR>a cow's footstep will hold.<BR>	 3. The mark or impression of a cow's<BR>foot.<BR>	 4. A cow's foot or hoof.<BR> E. गो a cow, and पद for पाद a foot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=248-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोस|गोसः
गोस m. (-सः)<BR>	 1. Gum myrrh.<BR>	 2. The last watch of the night, early<BR>morning or day-break.<BR> E. गो water, dew, and सो to destroy, to<BR>absorb; affix ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=248-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोसंख्य
गोसंख्य m. (-ख्यः) A herdsman, a cowherd.<BR> E. गो a cow, and सम् pre-<BR>fixed to ख्या to count, affix ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=248-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोसगृह
गोसगृह n. (-हं) The inner part of a house, an inner or sleeping room, a<BR>bed-chamber.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=248-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोसङ्ग|गोसंग|गोसङ्गः
गोसङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः) Dawn, day-break.<BR> E. गो a cow, and सङ्ग meeting, junc-<BR>tion; the herd assembling at that time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=248-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोसदृक्ष|गोसदृक्षः
गोसदृक्ष m. (-क्षः) The Gayal, (Bos gavæus.)<BR> E. गो a cow, and सदृक्ष like,<BR>from सदृश with स aff. गोः सदृक्षः । गोतुल्ये, गवये ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=248-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोसन्दाय|गोसंदाय|गोसन्दायः
गोसन्दाय m. (-यः) Ono who gives a cow.<BR> E. गो a cow, दा to give, with सम्<BR>prefixed, युक् augment, affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=248-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोसम्भव|गोसंभव
गोसम्भव mfn. (-वः-वा-वं) Produced from or by a cow.<BR> E. गो, and सम्भव born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=248-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोसर्ग|गोसर्गः
गोसर्ग m. (-र्गः) Dawn, day-break.<BR> E. गो a cow, and सर्ग going forth, the<BR>cattle then going forth to pasture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=248-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोसव|गोसवः
गोसव m. (-वः) The sacrifice of a cow, one of the grand sacrifices of the<BR>Hindus in former times, and not permitted in the present or Kali<BR>yuga age: see गोमेध.<BR> E. गो a cow, and सब sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=248-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोशशस
गोशशस m. (-शः) Myrrh: गवि जले शशति शश-वा असच् सप्तमी तत्पुरुषः ।<BR>वोलि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=249-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोस्तन|गोस्तनः
गोस्तन m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. The udder of a cow.<BR>	 2. A garland consisting of four or<BR>of thirty-four strings.<BR>	 3. A cluster of blossoms, a nosegay, &c.<BR>	 f.<BR>(-ना or -नी) A grape.<BR> E. गो a cow, and स्तन a breast, full or clustering<BR>like the udder of a cow. गोः स्तन इव गुच्छो यस्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=249-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोस्थान|गोस्थानं
गोस्थान n. (-नं) A cowpen, a station for cattle.<BR> E. गो a cow, and स्थान a<BR>place; also with कन् added गोस्थानक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=249-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोस्थानक|गोस्थानकं
गोस्थानक n. (-कं) See the proceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=249-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोस्वामिन्
गोस्वामिन् m. (-मी)<BR>	 1. The master or possessor of herds.<BR>	 2. A holy man,<BR>a religious personage and teacher; in common language, a<BR>Gossawami.<BR> E. गो kine, or an organ of sense, and स्वामिन् a lord or<BR>master. गवां स्वामिनि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=249-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोहत्या
गोहत्या f. (-त्या) Killing a cow.<BR> E. गो, and हत्या murder. गोहनने.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=249-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोहन्न|गोहन्नं
गोहन्न n. (-न्नं) Cow-dung<BR> E. गो, and हन्न ordure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=249-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोहरीतकी
गोहरीतकी f. (-की) Vilwa or Bel, (Ægle marmelos.) गोः हरितकीव हित-<BR>कारित्वात् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=249-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोहित|गोहितः
गोहित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Proper or fit for cattle.<BR>	 2. Cherishing or pro-<BR>tecting kine.<BR>	 m. (-तः)<BR>	 1. A creeping plant; also घोषा 2. The Bel<BR>tree.<BR> E. गो a cow, and हित suitable, &c. गवां हितं यस्मात् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=249-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोहिर|गोहिरं
गोहिर n. (-रं) The heel.<BR> E. गुह् to cover, इरच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=249-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोह्य|गोह्यं
गोह्य mfn. (-ह्यः-ह्या-ह्यं)<BR>	 1. To be covered or concealed.<BR>	 2. To be kept<BR>secret.<BR> E. गुह to cover, ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=249-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गौञ्जिक|गौंजिक|गौंजिकः|गौञ्जिकः
गौञ्जिक m. (-कः) A goldsmith.<BR> E. गुञ्जा the small weight especially used<BR>by goldsmiths, and ठक् aff. गुञ्जा तुलमानभेदः तद्ग्रहणं शीलमस्य । ठक् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=249-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गौड|गौडः
गौड m. (-डः) The district of Gaur, the central part of Bengal, extend-<BR>ing from Banga to Bhubaneshwar in Orrissa: the ruins of its capital,<BR>called by the same name, are still in existance.<BR>	 m. plu. (-डाः) The<BR>inhabitants of Gaur.<BR>	 f. (-डी)<BR>	 1. Rum or spirit distilled from Gur or<BR>molasses.<BR>	 2. One of the Rāgiṇīs.<BR>	 3. A style of poetry, the bold<BR>and spirited style,<BR> E. गुड to surround, or गुड raw sugar, and अण्<BR>affix, fem. affix ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=249-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गौडिक|गौडिकं|गौडिकः
गौडिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Of or relating to Gur or molasses.<BR>	 n. (-कं)<BR>Rum.<BR> E. गुड as above, affix of relation ठक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=249-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गौण|गौणः
गौण mfn. (-णः-णी-णं)<BR>	 1. Having qualities or attributes.<BR>	 2. Relating to<BR>multiplication or enumeration.<BR>	 3. Secondary, subordinate.<BR>	 4.<BR>Secondery as applied to the month, reckoned from full-moon to<BR>full-moon.<BR> E. गुण, and अण् aff. गुणमधिकृत्य प्रवृत्ता गौणी ततः आगतः अण् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=249-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गौणिक
गौणिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Having qualities, relating to or connected with<BR>them.<BR> E. गुण, and ठक् aff. गुणे रूपादौ साधुः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=249-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गौतम|गौतमः
गौतम m. (-मः)<BR>	 1. The name of a saint or sage and founder of the<BR>Nyaya philosophy.<BR>	 2. A legislator of the same name.<BR>	 3. A name<BR>of SAKYA Muni, the original Buddha or founder of the Bauddha<BR>sect.<BR>	 4. A name of the first pupil of the last Jaina.<BR>	 5. Name of a<BR>tribe or family of Brahmans descended from GOTAMA.<BR>	 6. A poison,<BR>one of the fixed kinds, or mineral, vegetable, &c.<BR>	 f. (-मी)<BR>	 1. A<BR>name of DURGĀ.<BR>	 2. A female Rākṣasa or goblin.<BR>	 3. A yellow dye:<BR>see गोरोचना 4. The Godavari river.<BR> E. गोतम a sage, and अण् patro-<BR>nomic affix, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=249-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गौधार|गौधारः
गौधार m. (-रः) An iguana.<BR> E. गोधा an alligator, and आरक् affix of des-<BR>cent; considered as the offspring of the alligator, on account of<BR>its smaller size, and similar shape; also गौधेय and गौधेर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=249-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गौधेय|गौधेयः
गौधेय m. (-यः) An iguana.<BR> E. गोधा, and ढक् affix: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=249-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गौधेर|गौधेरः
गौधेर m. (-रः) An iguana.<BR> E. गोधा, and ढक् affix; see गौधारः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=249-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गौपुच्छिक
गौपुच्छिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Of or belonging to a cow's tail, bought for a<BR>cow's tail, &c.<BR> E. गो, and पुच्छ a tail, affix ठञ्. गोपुच्छेन क्रीतम् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=249-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गौर|गौरं|गौरः
गौर mfn. (-रः-रा-री-रं)<BR>	 1. White.<BR>	 2. Yellow.<BR>	 3. Pale red: (or it may be<BR>used as a noun substantive mas. to imply either of these colours.)<BR>4. Clean, cleansed, pure.<BR>	 m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. white mustard.<BR>	 2. The moon.<BR>3. A tree, (Grislea tomentosa:) see धवः 4. A name of CHAITANA.<BR>	 n.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=249-b" target="_blank">Page249-b+ 60</a>]<BR>(-रं)<BR>	 1. The filament of a lotus.<BR>	 2. Gold.<BR>	 3. Saffron f. (-रा-री)<BR>	 1. A.<BR>name of the goddess PARVATI. (-री)<BR>	 2. A young girl, eight years<BR>old.<BR>	 3. Any young girl prior to menstruation, a maid, a virgin.<BR>	 4.<BR>The name of a river.<BR>	 5. The wife of the deity VARUṆA.<BR>	 6. The<BR>earth.<BR>	 7. Turmeric.<BR>	 8. A yellow dye called Gorochana.<BR>	 9. A plant:<BR>see रोचनी.<BR>	 10. A plant bearing a fragrant seed: see प्रियङ्गु.<BR>	 11.<BR>One of the female energies or Śaktis of the Bauddhas.<BR>	 12. A<BR>white kind of Durva or bent grass.<BR>	 13. Arabian jasmine.<BR>	 14. Sacred<BR>basil or Tulasi.<BR>	 15. One of the Rāgiṇīs.<BR> E. गुड to sound. and रन्<BR>Uṇādi affix, the deriv. is irregular; also गुरी to endeavour, धञ्<BR>affix, and derivative irr.; upon whom or what the mind exerts<BR>itself; again, गौर white, pure, &c. affix ङीष्, that which is white<BR>or brilliant, &c. which applies to the virgin, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=249-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गौरचन्द्र|गौरचन्द्रः
गौरचन्द्र m. (-न्द्रः) A name of the saint CHAITANYA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=249-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गौरव|गौरवं
गौरव n. (-वं)<BR>	 1. Reputation, respectability, venerableness or weight.<BR>2. Physical weight, heaviness.<BR> E. गुरु heavy, respectable, &c. and<BR>अण् affix, implying condition of being. गुरोर्भावः कर्म वा ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=249-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गौरवित|गौरवितः
गौरवित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Venerable, respectable.<BR> E. गौरव, and इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=249-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गौरवेरित
गौरवेरित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Praised, famed, celebrated.<BR> E. गौरव, fame, and<BR>ईरित declared.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=249-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गौरशाक|गौरशाकः
गौरशाक m. (-कः) A species of bassia; also मधुक.<BR> E. गौर pale white,<BR>and शाक a potherb. गौरः शाकः अस्य मधुकभेदे ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=249-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गौरसर्षप|गौरसर्षपः
गौरसर्षप m. (-पः)<BR>	 1. White mustard.<BR>	 2. The white mustard seed con-<BR>sidered as a measure of weight.<BR> E. गौर white, and सर्षप mustard,<BR>also गौर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=249-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गौराङ्ग|गौराङ्गः
गौराङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः) A name of CHAITANA.<BR> E. गौर pale, and अङ्ग body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=249-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गौरार्द्रक|गौरार्द्रकः
गौरार्द्रक m. (-कः) A kind of poison.<BR> E. गौर white, and आर्द्रक ginger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=249-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गौरास्य|गौरास्यः
गौरास्य m. (-स्यः) A black monkey with a white face.<BR> E. गौर, and आस्य<BR>face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=249-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गौरिका
गौरिका f. (-का) A virgin, a young girl, one eight years old, or in whom<BR>menstruation has not commenced.<BR> E. गौरी as above, and ठन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=249-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गौरिल|गौरिलः
गौरिल m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. White mustard.<BR>	 2. Iron or steel filings or dust. E.<BR>गौर pale white, and इलच् aff. गौरवर्णोऽस्ति अस्य वा इलच् । श्वेतसर्षपे ।<BR>लौहचूर्णे ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=249-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गौरीज|गौरीजं|गौरीजः
गौरीज m. (-जः) KARTIKEYA or GANESA.<BR>	 n. (-जं) Talc.<BR> E. गौरी, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=249-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गौरीपट्ट|गौरीपट्टः
गौरीपट्ट m. (-ट्टः) The horizontal plate of the Linga, typical of the female<BR>organ.<BR> E. गौरी, and पट्ट a layer. गौर्य्याः पट्टमिव स्थानम् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=249-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गौरीपति
गौरीपति m. (-तिः) A name of ŚIVA.<BR> E. गौरी, and पति husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=249-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गौरीपुत्त्र
गौरीपुत्त्र m. (-त्त्रः) A name of the deity KARTIKEYA.<BR> E. गौरी the goddess,<BR>and पुत्त्र a son, the son of GAURI.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=249-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गौरीललित|गौरीललितं
गौरीललित n. (-तं) Yellow orpiment.<BR> E. गौरी the goddess, or a young girl,<BR>and ललित loved, liked; this being used as a dye to stain the clo-<BR>thes of women, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=249-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गौरुतल्पिक|गौरुतल्पिकः
गौरुतल्पिक m. (-कः) A violator of the bed of a Guru.<BR> E. गुरु, तल्प a bed,<BR>and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=249-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गौलक्षणिक|गौलक्षणिकः
गौलक्षणिक m. (-कः) One who distinguishes the good marks of a cow. E.<BR>गो, लक्षण a mark, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=249-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गौल्य|गौल्यं
गौल्य n. (-ल्यं) Spirituous liquor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=249-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गौशतिक|गौशतिकः
गौशतिक m. (-कः) One possessing a hundred cows.<BR> E. गौ, शत a hundred, and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=249-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गौष्ठीन|गौष्ठीनं
गौष्ठीन n. (-नं) The site of an old and abandoned cowpen.<BR> E. गोष्ठ a cow-<BR>pen, and खञ् aff. पूर्वं भूतं गोष्ठं खञ् । भूतपूर्वगोष्ठे ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=249-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गौसहस्रिक
गौसहस्रिक m. (-कः) One who has a thousand cows.<BR> E. गो, सहस्र a thous-<BR>and, ठञ् aff. गोसहस्रमस्ति अस्य गौशतिकवत् ठञ् । गोसहस्रस्वामिनि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=249-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रथ
ग्रथ r. 1st cl. (इ) ग्रथि (ग्रन्थते) 1. To be crooked.<BR>	 2. To be crooked meta-<BR>phorically, to be wicked.<BR>	 3. To curve, to bend or make crooked.<BR>	 4.<BR>to string together, to arrange. r. 10th cl. (ग्रथयति) To bind or tie.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=249-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रथित|ग्रथितं
ग्रथित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Strung, tied together or in order.<BR>	 2. Collected.<BR>3. Arranged, classed.<BR>	 4. Overcome.<BR>	 5. Hurt, injured.<BR> E. ग्रथि to<BR>bind, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=249-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रन्थ|ग्रंथ|ग्रंथः|ग्रन्थः
ग्रन्थ r. 1st, 9th and 10th cls. (ग्रन्थति, ग्रथ्नाति ग्रन्थयति) To string, to tie to-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=250-a" target="_blank">Page250-a+ 60</a>]<BR>gether, to connect or arrange in a regular series. With उद् pre-<BR>fixed, To untie, to loosen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=249-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रन्थ|ग्रंथ|ग्रंथः|ग्रन्थः
ग्रन्थ m. (-न्थः)<BR>	 1. Stringing or tying together, (literally or metaphori-<BR>cally.)<BR>	 2. Wealth, property.<BR>	 3. A book or composition in prose or<BR>verse.<BR>	 4. A metre or measure of thirty two syllables.<BR> E. ग्रन्थ to dis-<BR>pose or arrange, affix भावे कर्मणि वा घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=250-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रन्थकर्त्तृ|ग्रन्थकर्तृ
ग्रन्थकर्त्तृ m. (-र्त्ता) An author.<BR> E. ग्रन्थ, and कर्त्तृ maker.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=250-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रन्थकार|ग्रंथकार
ग्रन्थकार m. (-रः) An author.<BR> E. ग्रन्थ, and कार who makes. ग्रन्थं करोति अण् उप० स० ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=250-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रन्थकुटी|ग्रंथकुटी
ग्रन्थकुटी f. (-टी) An office a study, a library.<BR> E. ग्रन्थ a book, and कुटी a<BR>house or room.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=250-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रन्थन|ग्रंथन|ग्रंथनं|ग्रन्थनं
ग्रन्थन nf. (-नं-ना) Arranging, stringing, tying or connecting together<BR>either as a chaplet or a book.<BR> E. ग्रन्थ to arrange, affix भावे ल्युट्<BR>or ग्रन्थ चुरा-युच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=250-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रन्थविस्तर|ग्रंथविस्तर|ग्रन्थविस्तरः
ग्रन्थविस्तर m. (-रः) A voluminous work.<BR> E. ग्रन्थ, and विस्तर extent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=250-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रन्थि|ग्रंथि|ग्रंथिः|ग्रन्थिः
ग्रन्थि m. (-न्थिः)<BR>	 1. The joint or knot of a reed or cane, &c.<BR>	 2. A tie,<BR>the knot of a cord, &c.<BR>	 3. A joint or articulation of the body, 4.<BR>A plant, commonly Ganthiala: see ग्रन्थिपर्ण.<BR>	 5. Crookedness, dis-<BR>tortion.<BR>	 6. A complaint, knotting of the vessels as in varicocele,<BR>&c.<BR> E. ग्रन्थ to connect, &c. Uṇādi affix इन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=250-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रन्थिक|ग्रंथिक|ग्रन्थिकं|ग्रंथिकः|ग्रन्थिकः
ग्रन्थिक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. An astrologer, a fortune teller.<BR>	 2. The youngest of<BR>the Pandus.<BR>	 3. A thorny plant: see करीर.<BR>	 n. (-कं)<BR>	 1. The root of<BR>long pepper.<BR>	 2. A kind of resin, Bdellium.<BR>	 3. A perfume: see ग्रन्थि-<BR>पर्ण.<BR> E. कन् added to the preceding, or ग्रन्थ a book, &c. and ठन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=250-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रन्थित|ग्रंथित|ग्रन्थितं
ग्रन्थित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Strung, tied.<BR> E. ग्रन्थ to tie, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=250-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रन्थिदूर्व्वा|ग्रन्थिदूर्वा
ग्रन्थिदूर्व्वा f. (-र्व्वा) A species of Durva grass.<BR> E. ग्रन्थि, and दूर्व्वा Panicum<BR>dactylon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=250-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रन्थिन्|ग्रंथिन्
ग्रन्थिन् mfn. (-न्थी-न्थिनी-न्थि)<BR>	 1. Bookish, read, learned.<BR>	 2. Relating or be-<BR>longing to a book, &c.<BR> E. ग्रन्थ, and णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=250-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रन्थिपर्ण|ग्रंथिपर्ण|ग्रन्थिपर्णं|ग्रन्थिपर्णः
ग्रन्थिपर्ण m. (-र्णः) A plant, and according to some authorities a perfume<BR>commonly called Ganthiala.<BR> E. ग्रन्थ a knot, and पर्ण a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=250-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रन्थिबन्धन|ग्रंथिबंधन
ग्रन्थिबन्धन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Tying a knot.<BR>	 2. A ligament.<BR>	 3. Tying together<BR>the garments of the bride and bridegroom at the marriage cere-<BR>mony.<BR> E. ग्रन्थि, and बन्धन binding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=250-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रन्थिमत्|ग्रंथिमत्|ग्रन्थिमन्त्
ग्रन्थिमत् m. (-मान्) A plant, (Heliotropium indicum;) also अस्थिसंहार. E.<BR>ग्रन्थि knot, and मतुप् poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=250-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रन्थिमूल|ग्रन्थिमूलं
ग्रन्थिमूल n. (-लं) Garlic.<BR> E. ग्रन्थि a knot, and मूल root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=250-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रन्थिल|ग्रंथिल|ग्रन्थिलं|ग्रन्थिलः
ग्रन्थिल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Knotted, knotty, &c.<BR>	 m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. A plant, com-<BR>monly Bainchi (Flacourtia sapida, Rox.)<BR>	 2. Karir, a thorny plant,<BR>capparis:) see करीर.<BR>	 n. (-लं)<BR>	 1. Green or undried ginger.<BR>	 2. Root<BR>of long pepper.<BR> E. ग्रन्थि a knot, and लच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=250-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रन्थिवर्हिन्
ग्रन्थिवर्हिन् m. (-र्ही) A plant: see ग्रन्थिपर्ण.<BR> E. ग्रन्थि a knot, वर्ह to cover,<BR>and णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=250-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रन्थिहर|ग्रंथिहर|ग्रन्थिहरः
ग्रन्थिहर m. (-रः) A counsellor, a minister.<BR> E. ग्रन्थि knot, and हर who<BR>removes; who unties the knots of business.<BR> E. ग्रन्थिं हरति हर-अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=250-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रन्थीक|ग्रन्थीकं
ग्रन्थीक n. (-कं) The root of long pepper: see ग्रन्थिक. पिप्पलीमूले ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=250-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रस
ग्रस r. 1st cl. (उ) ग्रसु (ग्रसते) 1. To eat.<BR>	 2. To swallow, to devour. r. 1st<BR>and 10th cls. (ग्रसति ग्रासयति) To take, to seize. भ्वा-आत्म-सक-सेट् ।<BR>चुरा-उभ० ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=250-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रसन|ग्रसनं
ग्रसन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Swallowing, eating.<BR>	 2. Taking, seizing.<BR> E. ग्रस् to take भावे ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=250-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रसमान
ग्रसमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>	 1. Swallowing, devouring.<BR>	 2. Receiving or listen-<BR>ing to any thing eagerly.<BR> E. ग्रस् to eat, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=250-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रसिष्णु
ग्रसिष्णु mfn. (-ष्णुः-ष्णुः-ष्णु) Eating, taking food.<BR> E. ग्रस् to eat, इष्णुच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=250-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रस्त|ग्रस्तं
ग्रस्त mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं)<BR>	 1. Inarticulately pronounced, slurred, uttered<BR>with the omission of a letter or syllable.<BR>	 2. Eaten.<BR>	 3. Taken,<BR>seized.<BR>	 4. Affected by.<BR>	 5. Commenced as an eclipse, eclipsed. E.<BR>ग्रस् to eat, affix कर्मणि क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=250-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रस्तास्त
ग्रस्तास्त mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं) Commenced and ended as an eclipse.<BR> E. ग्रस्त<BR>seized. अस्त set.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=250-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रह|ग्रहः
ग्रह r. 1st, and 10th cls. (ग्रहति-ग्रहयति) r. 9th cl. (उभ) ग्रहू (गृह्णाति गृह्णीते)<BR>1. To take, to seize, to receive or accept. With अनु, prefixed, To<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=250-b" target="_blank">Page250-b+ 60</a>]<BR>favour, to show kindness to. With अव, To oppose. With उत्, To<BR>deposit, to trust. With उप, To provide.<BR>	 2. To favour. With नि, 1.<BR>To take, to arrest.<BR>	 2. To punish.<BR>	 3. To restrain. With परि, To lay<BR>hold of, to seize. With प्रति, 1. To assent to, to receive as a precept<BR>or truth.<BR>	 2. To embrace, to enfold, to comprehend or contain.<BR>	 3.<BR>To subdue.<BR>	 4. To accept. With वि, To quarrel, to fight. With सम्,<BR>To collect, to assemble. क्न्या-उभ-सक-सेट् । आदाने वा चुरा-उभ पक्षे भ्वा-प ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=250-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रह|ग्रहः
ग्रह m. (-हः)<BR>	 1. Taking, whether by seizure or acceptance.<BR>	 2. An<BR>eclipse or seizure of the sun or moon, by RAHU, &c.<BR>	 3. A planet.<BR>4. The place of a planet in the fixed zodiac.<BR>	 5. A moveable point<BR>in the heavens.<BR>	 6. A name of RAHU, or the ascending node.<BR>	 7.<BR>An imp, one of a particular class, beginning with PUTANA, sup-<BR>posed especially to seize upon young children producing convul-<BR>sions.<BR>	 8. Effort in battle.<BR>	 9. Tenacity, perseverance.<BR>	 10. Purpose,<BR>design.<BR>	 11. Favor, patronage.<BR> E. ग्रह् to take, &c. affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=250-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रहकल्लोल|ग्रहकल्लोलः
ग्रहकल्लोल m. (-लः) A name of RAHU, the personified ascending node. E.<BR>ग्रह a planet, and कल्लोल an enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=250-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रहगण
ग्रहगण m. (-णः) The planets taken collectively.<BR> E. ग्रह, and गण a number.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=250-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रहण|ग्रहणं
ग्रहण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) A prisoner, captive, confined.<BR>	 n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Taking,<BR>seizure.<BR>	 2. Receiving, acceptance.<BR>	 3. Assent, agreement.<BR>	 4. Respect.<BR>5. The hand.<BR>	 6. An eclipse.<BR>	 7. Comprehension, the taking or<BR>receiving of instruction, or the acquirement of any science.<BR>	 8.<BR>Sound.<BR>	 9. An organ of sense.<BR>	 10. In grammar, Exception.<BR> E. ग्रह्<BR>to take, affix भावे ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=250-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रहणान्त|ग्रहणान्तः
ग्रहणान्त n. (-न्तं) Close of study, acquirement of science, &c.<BR> E. ग्रहण<BR>taking, and अन्त end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=250-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रहणान्तिक
ग्रहणान्तिक n. (-कं) Termination of holy study.<BR> E. ग्रहण, and अन्तिक final.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=250-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रहणि|ग्रहणिः
ग्रहणि f. (-णिः)<BR>	 1. Diarrhœa, dysentery.<BR>	 2. The vessels diffusing vital<BR>warmth.<BR>	 3. The small intestines, that part of the alimentary<BR>canal where the bile assists digestion.<BR> E. ग्रह् to seize, अनि Uṇādi<BR>affix; also with ङीप् added ग्रहणी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=250-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रहणीरुज्
ग्रहणीरुज् f. (-रुक्) Diarrhœa, dysentery.<BR> E. ग्रहणी the same (as above),<BR>and रुज् sickness, disease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=250-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रहणीय
ग्रहणीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) To be taken, to be seized, accepted, &c.<BR> E. ग्रह्,<BR>and अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=250-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रहणीहर|ग्रहणीहरं
ग्रहणीहर n. (-रं) Cloves.<BR> E. ग्रहणी diarrhœa, and हर what removes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=250-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रहनायक|ग्रहनायकः
ग्रहनायक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. The sun.<BR>	 2. The planet Saturn.<BR> E. ग्रह a planet,<BR>and नायक a chief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=250-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रहनाश|ग्रहनाशः
ग्रहनाश m. (-शः) A planet, (Echites scholaris)<BR> E. ग्रह taking, and नाश<BR>injury, producing pain in the bowels, &c. also ग्रहनाशन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=250-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रहनेमि|ग्रहनेमिः
ग्रहनेमि m. (-मिः) The moon.<BR> E. ग्रह a planet and नेमि the circumference<BR>of a wheel, from its shape,<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=250-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रहपति|ग्रहपतिः
ग्रहपति m. (-तिः) The sun.<BR> E. ग्रह a planet. and पति chief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=250-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रहपीडा
ग्रहपीडा f. (-डा) The influence of an unpropitious planet.<BR> E. ग्रह, and<BR>and पीडा pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=250-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रहपुष|ग्रहपुषः
ग्रहपुष m. (-षः) The sun,<BR> E. ग्रह, and पुष् to cherish, affix क; cherishing<BR>the planets with his light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=250-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रहपूजा
ग्रहपूजा f. (-जा) worship of the sun and the other planets.<BR> E. ग्रह, and<BR>पूजा worship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=250-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रहयाग|ग्रहयागः
ग्रहयाग m. (-गा) Worship of or offering to the planets.<BR> E. ग्रह, and याग<BR>sacrifice; also ग्रहयज्ञ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=250-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रहयालु
ग्रहयालु mfn. (-लुः-लुः-लु) Taking, receiving.<BR> E. ग्रह to take, आलुच् affix,<BR>अय inserted; also गृहयालु,<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=250-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रहराज|ग्रहराजः
ग्रहराज m. (-जः)<BR>	 1. The sun.<BR>	 2. The moon.<BR>	 3. The planet Jupiter or its<BR>regent.<BR> E. ग्रह a planet, and राज a king, a chief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=250-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रहविप्र|ग्रहविप्रः
ग्रहविप्र m. (-प्रः) An astrologer.<BR> E. ग्रह and विप्र a Brahman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=250-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रहाधार|ग्रहाधारः
ग्रहाधार m. (-रः) The constellation DHRUVA or the polar star.<BR> E. ग्रह<BR>planet, and आधार asylum; the star remaining fixed amidst the<BR>planetary movements.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=250-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रहाधीन
ग्रहाधीन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Subject to planetary influence.<BR> E. ग्रह, and अधीन dependent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=250-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रहामय|ग्रहामयः
ग्रहामय m. (-यः) Epilepsy, convulsions, demoniac possession which the<BR>complaint is supposed to be.<BR> E. ग्रह an imp, and आ मय sickness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=251-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रहाशिन्
ग्रहाशिन् m. (-शी) A plant, (Echites scholaris:) see ग्रहनाश.<BR> E. ग्रह taking,<BR>and अश् here meaning to hurt, affix इनि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=251-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रहीतव्य
ग्रहीतव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>	 1. To be taken or accepted.<BR>	 2. To be learned<BR>or acquired.<BR> E. ग्रह् to take, तव्य affix, and ई inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=251-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रहीतृ
ग्रहीतृ mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ) Taking, disposed to take.<BR> E. ग्रह् to take, तृच्<BR>affix, and ई inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=251-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्राम|ग्रामः
ग्राम m. (-मः)<BR>	 1. A village, a hamlet, an inhabited and unfortified place<BR>in the midst of fields and meadow land, where men of the servile<BR>class mostly reside, and where agriculture thrives.<BR>	 2. A scale in<BR>music.<BR>	 3. (In composition,) A multitude.<BR> E. गम् to go, affix घञ्,<BR>and deriv. irr. or ग्रस् to eat, Uṇādi affix मन् and आच् substituted<BR>for the radical final. ग्रस-मन् आदन्तादेशः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=251-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रामकुक्कुट|ग्रामकुक्कुटः
ग्रामकुक्कुट m. (-टः) A tame or domestic cock.<BR> E. ग्राम, and क्ककुट a cock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=251-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रामकूट|ग्रामकूटः
ग्रामकूट m. (-टः) A man of the fourth tribe, a Śūdra.<BR> E. ग्राम a village,<BR>and कूट a number, the crowd or population of the village. ग्रामस्य<BR>कूट इव वञ्चनाप्रघानत्वात् । शूद्रे ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=251-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रामग
ग्रामग mfn. (-गः-गा-गं) Who or what goes to a village.<BR> E. ग्राम, and गम्<BR>to go, ड aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=251-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रामगमिन्
ग्रामगमिन् mfn. (-मी-मिनी-मि) Going in or to a village.<BR> E. ग्राम, and गमिन्<BR>who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=251-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रामगृह्य
ग्रामगृह्य mfn. (-ह्यः-ह्या-ह्यं) Being or remaining outside the village. E.<BR>ग्राम, and गृह्य to be taken out. ग्राम-वाह्यार्थे क्यप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=251-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रामघात|ग्रामघातः
ग्रामघात m. (-तः) Plundering a village.<BR> E. ग्राम, and घात attacking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=251-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रामङ्गमिन्
ग्रामङ्गमिन् mfn. (-मी-मिनी-मि) Who or what goes to a village.<BR> E. ग्राम in<BR>the 2nd case, गमिन् what goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=251-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रामज
ग्रामज mfn. (-जः-जा-जं) Village, rustic, village-born or produced.<BR> E. ग्राम,<BR>and ज born; also ग्रामजात, &c. ग्रामे जायते जन-ड ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=251-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रामणी
ग्रामणी mfn. (-णीः-णीः-णि)<BR>	 1. Best, excellent.<BR>	 2. Chief, pre-eminent,<BR>superintendent.<BR>	 3. One who only thinks of enjoyment.<BR>	 m. (-णीः)<BR>A barber.<BR>	 f. (-णीः)<BR>	 1. A whore, a harlot.<BR>	 2. A female peasant or<BR>villager.<BR>	 3. The indigo plant.<BR> E. ग्राम a village, नी to get or obtain,<BR>affix क्विप्. ग्रामं समूहं नयति प्रेरयति स्वस्वकार्य्येषु ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=251-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रामणीपुत्र
ग्रामणीपुत्र m. (-त्रः) The son of a whore, a bastard.<BR> E. ग्रामणी, and पुत्र a<BR>son; also read ग्रामणिपुत्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=251-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रामतक्ष|ग्रामतक्षः
ग्रामतक्ष m. (-क्षः) The village carpenter.<BR> E. ग्राम a village, and तक्ष car-<BR>penter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=251-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रामतस्
ग्रामतस् ind. From the village.<BR> E. ग्राम and तसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=251-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रामता
ग्रामता f. (-ता) A multitude of villages.<BR> E. ग्राम, and तल् affix of multi-<BR>tude; also ग्रामत्वं with त्व aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=251-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रामदशेश
ग्रामदशेश m. (-शः) The head of ten villages.<BR> E. ग्राम, दश ten, and ईश<BR>chief; also ग्रामदशाधिपति, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=251-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रामभृत|ग्रामभृतः
ग्रामभृत m. (-तः) The village messenger or servant.<BR> E. ग्राम, and भृत sup-<BR>ported.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=251-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्राममद्गुरिका
ग्राममद्गुरिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. A kind of fish, (Silurus singio, HAM.)<BR>	 2. A riot,<BR>a fray, a village war, (ग्रामयुद्ध.)<BR> E. ग्राम, and मद्गुर a fish, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=251-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्राममुख|ग्राममुखः
ग्राममुख m. (-खः) A market town, a fair, a market.<BR> E. ग्राम a village, and<BR>मुख chief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=251-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्राममृग|ग्राममृगः
ग्राममृग m. (-गः) A dog.<BR> E. ग्राम, and मृग deer, the village deer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=251-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रामयाजक|ग्रामयाजकः
ग्रामयाजक m. (-कः) The village priest, one who conducts the ceremonies<BR>for any or all classes, and is consequently considered as a degrad-<BR>ed Brahman; it also applies to the attendant of an idol.<BR> E. ग्राम a<BR>village, यज् to sacrifice, in the causal form, affix वुन्; also with<BR>णिनि affix ग्रामयाजिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=251-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रामलुण्ठन|ग्रामलुंठन
ग्रामलुण्ठन n. (-नं) Plundering or pillaging a village.<BR> E. ग्राम, and लुण्ठन<BR>robbing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=251-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रामवास|ग्रामवासः
ग्रामवास m. (-सः)<BR>	 1. A villager.<BR>	 2. Living in a village.<BR> E. ग्राम, and वास<BR>abode; also ग्रामेवास.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=251-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रामवासिन्
ग्रामवासिन् m. (-सी) A villager.<BR> E. ग्राम, and वासिन् who inhabits; also ग्रामेवासिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=251-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रामविशेष|ग्रामविशेषः
ग्रामविशेष m. (-षः) Variety of the scales in music.<BR> E. ग्राम, and विशेष dif-<BR>ference.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=251-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रामशत
ग्रामशत n. (-तं) A hundred villages, a province.<BR> E. ग्राम and and शत a<BR>hundred.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=251-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रामशतेश
ग्रामशतेश m. (-शः) The governor of a province.<BR> E. ग्राम, शत and ईश chief<BR>also ग्रामशताधिपतिः, ग्रामशताध्यक्षः, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=251-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रामसङ्कर|ग्रामसंकर|ग्रामसंकरः
ग्रामसङ्कर m. (-रः) The common sewer or drain of a village.<BR> E. ग्राम and<BR>सङ्कर a narrow place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=251-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रामसङ्घ|ग्रामसंघ|ग्रामसंघः
ग्रामसङ्घ m. (-ङ्घः) A village corporation, a municipality.<BR> E. ग्राम, and सङ्घ<BR>assembly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=251-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रामस्थ|ग्रामस्थः
ग्रामस्थ mfn. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थं) Being or residing in a village, belonging to it<BR>&c.<BR>	 m. (-स्थः) A village.<BR> E. ग्राम, and स्थ what stays. ग्रामे तिष्ठति स्था-क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=251-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रामहासक|ग्रामहासकः
ग्रामहासक m. (-कः) A sister's husband.<BR> E. ग्राम a village, and हास who<BR>delights, from हस् to laugh, &c. and ण्वुल् aff. ग्रामं हासयति हम-णिच्.<BR>ण्वुल् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=251-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रामाधान|ग्रामाधानं
ग्रामाधान n. (-नं) Hunting.<BR> E. ग्राम a village, and आधान what supports.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=251-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रामाधिकृत|ग्रामाधिकृतः
ग्रामाधिकृत m. (-तः) The head man or chief of a village.<BR> E. ग्राम and अधि-<BR>कृत set over.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=251-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रामाधिपति|ग्रामाधिपतिः
ग्रामाधिपति m. (-तिः) Chief or head of a village.<BR> E. ग्राम, and अधिपति chief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=251-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रामाध्यक्ष|ग्रामाध्यक्षः
ग्रामाध्यक्ष m. (-क्षः) Superintendent or chief of a village.<BR> E. ग्राम and अध्यक्ष<BR>superior.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=251-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रामान्त|ग्रामांत|ग्रामान्तं|ग्रामान्तः
ग्रामान्त n. (-न्तं) Space near a village.<BR> E. ग्राम and अन्त a boundary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=251-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रामान्तीय
ग्रामान्तीय n. (-यं) Space near a village.<BR> E. ग्राम and अन्त end, छ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=251-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रामिक|ग्रामिकः
ग्रामिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>	 1. Village, rude, rustic.<BR>	 2. Chromatic.<BR>	 m. (-कः)<BR>1. The head-man of a village 2. A village.<BR> E. ग्राम and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=251-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रामिन्
ग्रामिन् mfn. (-मी-मिनी-मि) Village, villager.<BR>	 m. (-मी) The head-man of a<BR>village.<BR>	 f. (-मिनी) The indigo plant.<BR> E. ग्राम a village, इनि and ङीप्<BR>affixes; also ग्रामीणा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=251-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रामीण|ग्रामीणः
ग्रामीण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>	 1. A villager, a rustic.<BR>	 2. Produced in or pecu-<BR>liar to a village.<BR>	 3. Vulgar, rude. 4, Chromatic.<BR>	 m. (-णः)<BR>	 1. A dog.<BR>2. A crow.<BR>	 f. (-णा) The indigo plant.<BR> E. ग्राम and खञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=251-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रामीय|ग्रामीयः
ग्रामीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Belonging to a village, produced in or derived<BR>from it.<BR>	 m. (-यः) A villager.<BR> E. ग्राम and ढक् affix; also with कन् add-<BR>ed ग्रामीयक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=251-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रामेय
ग्रामेय mfn. (-यः-यी-यं) A villager, rustic, village-born, &c.<BR> E. ग्राम and ढक्<BR>affix; also with कन् added ग्रामेयक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=251-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रामेवास
ग्रामेवास m. (-सः)<BR>	 1. A villager.<BR>	 2. A village abode.<BR> E. ग्रामे seventh case,<BR>and वास abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=251-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रामेवासिन्
ग्रामेवासिन् m. (-सी) A villager.<BR> E. ग्रामे seventh case, वासिन् who dwells.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=251-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रामेश|ग्रामेशः
ग्रामेश m. (-शः) The head-man of a village.<BR> E. ग्राम and ईश a master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=251-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रामेश्वर|ग्रामेश्वरः
ग्रामेश्वर m. (-रः) The head-man or ruler over a village.<BR> E. ग्राम, and ईश्वर a<BR>master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=251-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्राम्य|ग्राम्यः
ग्राम्य mfn. (-म्यः-म्या-म्यं)<BR>	 1. Village-born, produced in or relating to a<BR>village.<BR>	 2. Vulgar, rude, rustic.<BR>	 3. Relating to a musical scale.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-म्यः) A hog, a tame or a village hog.<BR>	 n. (-म्यं)<BR>	 1. Rustic or homely<BR>speech.<BR>	 2. The Prakrit, and the other dialects of India, except the<BR>Sanskrit.<BR> E. ग्राम and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=251-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्राम्यकर्क्कटी|ग्राम्यकर्कटी
ग्राम्यकर्क्कटी f. (-टी) A pumpkin gourd.<BR> E. ग्राम्य village, and कर्क्कटी gourd.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=251-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्राम्यकन्द|ग्राम्यकन्दः
ग्राम्यकन्द m. (-न्दः) A common species of Arum.<BR> E. ग्राम्य, and कन्द root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=251-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्राम्यकुङ्कुम|ग्राम्यकुंकुम|ग्राम्यकुङ्कुमं
ग्राम्यकुङ्कुम n. (-मं) A yellow dye, safflower, (Carthamus tinctorius.)<BR> E. ग्राम्य<BR>and कुङ्कुम saffron, village saffron. कुसुम्भे ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=251-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्राम्यधर्म्म|ग्राम्यधर्म|ग्राम्यधर्मः|ग्राम्यधर्म्मः
ग्राम्यधर्म्म m. (-र्म्मः) Copulation.<BR>	 n. ग्राम्य and धर्म्म virtue, village virtue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=251-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्राम्यमद्गुरिका
ग्राम्यमद्गुरिका f. (-का) A kind of fish, (Silurus singio, HAM.) Also ग्राममद्गु-<BR>रिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=251-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्राम्यमांस
ग्राम्यमांस n. (-सं) Meat of tame animals.<BR> E. ग्राम्य rural, and मांस flesh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=251-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्राम्यमृग|ग्राम्यमृगः
ग्राम्यमृग m. (-गः) A dog.<BR> E. ग्राम्य and मृग a deer, the village deer; also<BR>ग्राममृग.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=251-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्राम्यराशि|ग्राम्यराशिः
ग्राम्यराशि f. (-शिः) A name of several of the signs of the zodiac.<BR> E. ग्राग्य,<BR>and राशि a sign.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=251-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्राम्यशूकर|ग्राम्यशूकरः
ग्राम्यशूकर m. (-रः) A village hog, a tame hog, a pig.<BR> E. ग्राम्य, and शूकर a hog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=251-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्राम्याश्व|ग्राम्याश्वः
ग्राम्याश्व m. (-श्वः) An ass.<BR> E. ग्राम्य, and अश्व a horse, the village horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=252-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रावन्
ग्रावन् mfn. (-वा-वा-व) Hard, solid.<BR>	 m. (-वा)<BR>	 1. A stone or rock.<BR>	 2. A<BR>mountain.<BR>	 3. A cloud.<BR> E. ग्रसते ग्रस ड ग्रः आवनति वन सम्भक्तौ विच् कर्म ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=252-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रास|ग्रासः
ग्रास m. (-सः) A mouthful or a quantity equivalent to a mouthful, a<BR>lump of rice, &c. of the size of a peacock's egg.<BR> E. ग्रस् to eat,<BR>affix कर्मणि घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=252-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रासाच्छादन
ग्रासाच्छादन n. (-नं) Bare subsistence, food and clothing.<BR> E. ग्रास, and<BR>आच्छादन covering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=252-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्राह|ग्राहं|ग्राहः
ग्राह m. (-हः)<BR>	 1. Taking, either by seizure or acceptance.<BR>	 2. A shark;<BR>according to some, the Gangetic alligator, (Lacerta Gangetica;)<BR>according to others, the water elephant, (the hippopotamus.)<BR>	 3.<BR>Any large fish or marine animal.<BR> E. ग्रह् to take, affix घञ् or ण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=252-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्राहक|ग्राहकः
ग्राहक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) One who takes or seizes, one who accepts or<BR>receives.<BR>	 m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A hawk, a falcon.<BR>	 2. A police officer, a cons-<BR>table, a bailiff.<BR> E. ग्रह् to take, णिच् ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=252-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्राहवत्|ग्राहवन्त्
ग्राहवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Containing or abounding with alligators. E.<BR>ग्रह्, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=252-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्राहिन्
ग्राहिन् mfn. (-ही-हिणी-हि)<BR>	 1. Taking, seizing, accepting, who or what<BR>takes.<BR>	 2. Astringent, binding, constipating.<BR>	 m. (-ही)<BR>	 1. A seda-<BR>tive, a narcotic.<BR>	 2. The elephant or wood apple: see कपित्थ.<BR>	 f.<BR>(-णी) A small kind of Jawasa, perhaps a species of Hedysarum.<BR>E. ग्रह् to take, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=252-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्राह्य|ग्राह्यः
ग्राह्य mfn. (-ह्यः-ह्या-ह्यं)<BR>	 1. To be seized, to be taken, to be accepted.<BR>	 2.<BR>To be accepted as a rule or a law, to be acknowledged or assented<BR>to.<BR>	 3. To be attended to or obeyed.<BR>	 4. To be admitted in evidence,<BR>&c.<BR>	 5. To be apprehended or arrested.<BR> E. ग्रह् to take, ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=252-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रीवा
ग्रीवा f. (-वा)<BR>	 1. The neck.<BR>	 2. The back part of the neck, the nape, the<BR>tendon of the Trepazium muscle.<BR> E. गॄ to swallow, वनिप् Uṇādi affix<BR>गिरति अनया गॄ वनिप् निपातने ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=252-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रीविन्
ग्रीविन् mfn. (-वी-विणी-वि) Long-necked, handsome-necked.<BR>	 m. (-वी) A<BR>camel.<BR> E. ग्रीवा a neck, and इनि poss. aff. दीर्घा ग्रीवा अस्ति अस्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=252-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रीष्म|ग्रीष्मः
ग्रीष्म mfn. (-ष्मः-ष्मा-ष्मं) Hot, warm.<BR>	 m. (-ष्मः)<BR>	 1. The hot season, compre-<BR>hending two months, about June July.<BR>	 2. Heat, warmth.<BR>	 f. (-ष्मी)<BR>Jasmin.<BR> E. ग्रस् to take, &c. मनिन् Uṇādi affix, and the deriv. irr.<BR>ग्रसते रसान् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=252-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रीष्मज
ग्रीष्मज mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>	 1. Produced by heat.<BR>	 2. Produced in the hot<BR>season.<BR>	 f. (-जा) A kind of fruit, (Annona reticulata.)<BR> E. ग्रीष्म the<BR>hot season, and ज produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=252-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रीष्मभव
ग्रीष्मभव mfn. (-वः-वा-वं) Produced by heat or in the hot season.<BR>	 f. (-वा)<BR>Double jasmine: see नवमल्ली.<BR> E. ग्रीष्म the hot season, and भव being,<BR>flourishing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=252-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रीष्मसुन्दरक|ग्रीष्मसुन्दरकः
ग्रीष्मसुन्दरक m. (-कः) A kind of potherb, (Chironia centauroides; it is<BR>also applied to Pharnaceum mollugo.)<BR> E. ग्रीष्म the hot season, and<BR>सुन्दर handsome, affix कन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=252-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रीष्महास|ग्रीष्महासं
ग्रीष्महास n. (-सं) The flocculent seeds, blown down, about in the<BR>air.<BR> E. ग्रीष्म the hot season, and हास a smile, considered from their<BR>white colour, as the smiles of the season.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=252-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रीष्मोद्भव
ग्रीष्मोद्भव mfn. (-वः-वा-वं) Produced by heat or in the hot season.<BR>	 f. (-वा)<BR>Double jasmine.<BR> E. ग्रीष्म, and उद्भव produced. ग्रीष्मकाले उद्भवति उद् +<BR>भू-अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=252-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रुच
ग्रुच (इर उ) इर ग्रुचु r. 1st. cl. (ग्रोचति) To steal or rob. भ्वा-पर-सक-सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=252-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रैव|ग्रैवं
ग्रैव mfn, (-वः-वी-वं) Belonging to the neck, &c.<BR>	 n. (-वं)<BR>	 1. A necklace, a<BR>close necklace or collar.<BR>	 2. A chain worn round the neck of an<BR>elephant, &c.<BR> E. ग्रीवा the necklace, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=252-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रैवेय|ग्रैवेयं
ग्रैवेय mfn. (-यः-यी-यं) Belonging to the neck.<BR>	 n. (-यं)<BR>	 1. A collar, a neck-<BR>lace.<BR>	 2. A chain on the neck of an elephant or horse.<BR> E. ग्रीवा, and<BR>ढक् affix; also ग्रैवेयक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=252-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रैवेयक|ग्रैवेयकं
ग्रैवेयक n. (-कं) A collar, an ornament for the neck.<BR> E. ग्रीवा and ढकङ्<BR>affix: see ग्रैव and ग्रैवेय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=252-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रैष्म
ग्रैष्म mfn. (-ष्मः-ष्मी-ष्मं) Belonging or relating to, or produced by heat or<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=252-b" target="_blank">Page252-b+ 56</a>]<BR>hot season. of. (-ष्मी) Double jasmine.<BR> E. ग्रीष्म the hot season, &c.<BR>affix अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=252-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्लपित
ग्लपित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Distressed, pained.<BR>	 2. Exhausted, overpower-<BR>ed.<BR> E. ग्लै to be weary, causal form, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=252-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्लस
ग्लस (उ) ग्लसु r. 1st cl. (ग्लसते) To eat: see ग्रस.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=252-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्लस्त|ग्लस्तः
ग्लस्त mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं) Eaten.<BR> E. ग्लस् to eat, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=252-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्लह|ग्लहः
ग्लह (उ) ग्लहु r. 1st and 10th cls. (ग्लहति-यति) To take, to receive or ac-<BR>cept: see ग्रह आदाने वा चुरा-उभ पक्षे भ्वा-सक-वेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=252-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्लह|ग्लहः
ग्लह m. (-हः) Gaming, playing with dice.<BR> E. ग्लह् to take, &c. affix अच्<BR>or it is derived irregularly from ग्रह, and with अप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=252-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्लान|ग्लानः
ग्लान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Wearied, languid, feeble, exhausted by fatigue,<BR>disease, &c.<BR> E. ग्लै to be feeble, and कर्त्तरि क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=252-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्लानि|ग्लानिः
ग्लानि f. (-निः) Langour, lassitude, fatigue of body or depression of<BR>mind.<BR> E. ग्ला or ग्लै to be weary, Uṇādi affix भावे नि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=252-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्लायत्
ग्लायत् mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्) Being exhausted, languid, faint, &c.<BR> E. ग्लै to<BR>be weary, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=252-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्लास्नु|ग्लास्नुः
ग्लास्नु mfn. (-स्नः-स्नुः-स्नु) Exhausted by disease or fatigue, wearied, lan-<BR>guid.<BR> E. ग्लै to be weak, affix स्नु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=252-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्लुच
ग्लुच (इर उ) इर ग्लुचु r. 1st cl. (ग्लोचति)<BR>	 1. To steal, to rob.<BR>	 2. To go;<BR>see ग्रुच. भ्वा-पर-सक-सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=252-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्लुञ्च
ग्लुञ्च (इर उ) इर ग्लुञ्चु r. 1st cl. (ग्लुञ्चति) To go, to move. भ्वा-पर-सक-सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=252-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्लेप
ग्लेप (ऋ) ग्लेपृ r. 1st cl. (ग्लेपते)<BR>	 1. To be poor or dependent.<BR>	 2. To shake<BR>to tremble.<BR>	 3. To move. सक-भ्वा-आ-सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=252-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्लेय|ग्लेयः
ग्लेय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) To be made weary or exhausted, exhaustible,<BR>fatiguable.<BR> E. ग्ला or ग्लै to be weary, affix यत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=252-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्लेव
ग्लेव (ऋ) ग्लेवृ r. 1st cl. (ग्लेवते) To serve, to worship, to gratify by<BR>service or devotedness. भ्वा-आ-सक-सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=252-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्लेष
ग्लेष (ऋ) ग्लषृ r. 1st cl (ग्लेषते) To inquire, to search, to investigate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=252-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्लै
ग्लै r. 1st cl, ग्लायति 1. To be languid or weary, to be exhausted,<BR>faded, &c.<BR>	 2. To yawn, this root is sometimes considered to be<BR>ग्ला. making ग्लायति as above, and in the causal form ग्लपयति or<BR>ग्लापयति. भ्वा-पर-अक-अनिट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=252-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्लैतृ
ग्लैतृ mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ) Wearied, exhausted.<BR> E. ग्लै to be weary, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=252-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्लौ
ग्लौ m. (-ग्लौः)<BR>	 1. The moon.<BR>	 2. Camphor.<BR> E. ग्ला to be weary, Uṇādi<BR>affix डा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=252-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घ|घः
घ The fourth consonant of the Sanskrit alphabet, being the aspirate<BR>of the preceding letter, and corresponding to Gh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=252-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घ|घः
घ m. (-घः)<BR>	 1. A bell.<BR>	 2. A rattling or gurgling sound.<BR>	 f. (-घा)<BR>	 1. A tin-<BR>kling ornament worn by women round the waist.<BR>	 2. Strikling, kill-<BR>ing.<BR>	 3. Wetting, sprinkling,<BR> E. हन् to kill, affix ड, and घ substi-<BR>tuted for the radical letter, or the same affix, with घृ to sprinkle,<BR>&c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=252-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घग्घ
घग्घ r. 1st cl. (घग्घति) To laugh, to laugh at or deride also; घघ<BR>and गग्घ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=252-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घघ
घघ r. 1st cl. (घघति) To laugh or to laugh at: see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=252-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घट|घटः
घट r. 1st cl. (घटते) To act, to strive or endeavour. r. 10th cl. (घाटयति)<BR>1. To unite or to put together.<BR>	 2. To injure or kill.<BR>	 3. To shine (इ)<BR>घटि r. 10th cl. (घण्टयति) To shine. घट भ्वा-आ-अक-सेट् घटादि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=252-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घट|घटः
घट m. (-टः)<BR>	 1. A large earthen water jar.<BR>	 2. The sign Aquarius.<BR>	 3. A<BR>measure; see कुम्भ.<BR>	 4. An elephant's frontal sinus.<BR>	 5. Suspending<BR>the breath as a religious exercise.<BR>	 6. A man who makes effort or exer-<BR>tion.<BR>	 f. (-टा)<BR>	 1. A troop of elephants assembled for martial purposes.<BR>2. Effort, endeavour.<BR>	 3. An assembly.<BR>	 4. A number, a collection,<BR>an assemblage.<BR>	 f. (-टी)<BR>	 1. The Ghari or Indian clock, a plate of<BR>iron or mixed metal on which the hours are struck.<BR>	 2. A small<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=253-a" target="_blank">Page253-a+ 60</a>]<BR>water jar, a ewer.<BR> E. घट् to endeavour, &c. affix अच् or अङ् and fem.<BR>affix टाप् or ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=252-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घटक|घटकः
घटक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A tree that produces fruit without apparent flowers.<BR>2. A match-maker, an agent who ascertains or invents genealogies,<BR>and negociates matrimonial alliances.<BR>	 3. A genealogist.<BR> E. घट् to<BR>endeavour, and णिच् ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=253-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घटग्रह|घटग्रहः
घटग्रह mfn. (-हः-हा-हं) Who or what takes a water pot.<BR> E. घट and ग्रह्<BR>to take, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=253-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घटदासी
घटदासी f. (-सी) A bawd or procuress.<BR> E. घट् effort, and दासी a slave or<BR>servant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=253-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घटन|घटनं
घटन nf. (-नं-ना)<BR>	 1. Effort, exertion.<BR>	 2. Assembling, bringing together.<BR>3. Joining, mixing.<BR>	 4. Occuring.<BR> E. घट् to strive, &c. affix युच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=253-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घटयोनि|घटयोनिः
घटयोनि m. (-निः) The saint AGASTYA.<BR> E. घट a water jar, and योनि place<BR>of birth; the saint being born from a water jar. see कुम्भसम्भव.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=253-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घटराज|घटराजः
घटराज m. (-जः) A large water jar of baked clay.<BR> E. घट् a jar, and राज<BR>king, chief. घटेन योजनेन राजते राज-अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=253-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घटस्थापन
घटस्थापन n. (-नं) Placing a water pot as a type of DURGĀ, an essential<BR>part of various Tantrika ceremonies.<BR> E. घट, and स्थापन placing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=253-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घटाटोप|घटाटोपः
घटाटोप m. (-पः) A covering for a carriage or any article of furniture.<BR>E. घट and आटोप pride.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=253-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घटिक|घटिकं|घटिकः
घटिक n. (-कं) The posteriors.<BR>	 f. (-का)<BR>	 1. The ankle; also घटिका.<BR>	 2. A<BR>Muhurta or thirtieth part of a day and night.<BR>	 3. A Danda or<BR>period of twenty-four minutes.<BR>	 m. (-कः) A waterman.<BR> E. घटी a clock.<BR>&c. affixes कन् and टाप् for the feminine; otherwise घट a jar and ठन्<BR>aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=253-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घटित
घटित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Devised, attempted.<BR>	 2. Made of.<BR>	 3. In contact<BR>with, contiguous, joined.<BR> E. घट् to make effort, णिच् क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=253-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घटिन्धम|घटिंधम|घटिंधमः
घटिन्धम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं) Who blows or sounds in a jar.<BR>	 m. (-मः) A potter<BR>E. घटी and ध्मा to blow, खश् aff. मुम् ह्रस्वश्च ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=253-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घटिन्धय|घटिंधय
घटिन्धय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Who drinks a Ghati, (in measure.)<BR> E. घटी and<BR>घै to drink, खश् aff. मुम् ह्रस्वश्च ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=253-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घटीकार|घटीकारः
घटीकार m. (-रः) A potter.<BR> E. घट कार who makes, with अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=253-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घटीग्रह
घटीग्रह mfn. (-हः-हा-हं) Who or what takes a small jar, &c.<BR> E. घटी and<BR>ग्रह who takes. अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=253-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घटीयन्त्र|घटीयंत्र|घटीयन्त्रं
घटीयन्त्र n. (-न्त्रं) The rope and bucket of a well, or any machine for rais-<BR>ing water.<BR> E. घट effort, and यन्त्र machine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=253-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घटोत्कच|घटोत्कचः
घटोत्कच m. (-चः) The son of BHIMA by the Rakshasi, named HIDIMBA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=253-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घटोत्कचान्तक|घटोत्कचान्तकः
घटोत्कचान्तक m. (-कः) A name of KARṆA, natural brother to the Pandus<BR>E. घटोत्कच a proper name, and अन्तक destroyer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=253-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घटोद्भव|घटोद्भवः
घटोद्भव m. (-वः) The sage AGASTYA.<BR> E. घट a jar, and उद्भव born, produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=253-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घट्ट|घट्टः
घट्ट r. 1st and 10th cls. (घट्टते or घट्टयति-ते) To move. With परि prefixed,<BR>To spread or diffuse. With वि, To rub gently, to scratch. भ्वा-आत्म-<BR>सक-सेट् । वा चुरा-उभ० ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=253-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घट्ट|घट्टः
घट्ट m. (-ट्टः) A Ghat, a quay or landing place, steps on the side of a<BR>river, &c. leading to the water's edge.<BR>	 f. (ट्टी) A small or inferior<BR>landing place, private stairs, &c.<BR> E. घट्ट् to go, affix घञ् and with<BR>ङीष् affix, implying diminution.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=253-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घट्टना
घट्टना f. (-ना)<BR>	 1. Going, moving.<BR>	 2. Practice, business, means of living.<BR>3. Rubbing or striking together.<BR> E. घट्ट् to go, affix युच् fem. टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=253-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घट्टजीविन्
घट्टजीविन् m. (-वी) An attendant at a landing place, who takes care of<BR>the clothes of the bathers, &c.<BR> E. घट्ट, and जीविन् who subsists. णिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=253-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घण
घण (उ,) घणु r. 8th cl. (घणुति or घणुते) To shine. तना-उभ-अक सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=253-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घण्ट|घंट|घण्टः
घण्ट m. (-ण्टः) A sort of sauce, vegetables made into a pulp with water,<BR>turmeric, mustard seeds and capsicums.<BR>	 f. (-ण्टा)<BR>	 1. A bell; also a<BR>plate of iron or mixed metal struck as a bell.<BR>	 2. A plant: see<BR>घण्टापाटली<BR> E. घन to strike, क्त affix, fem. टाप् and deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=253-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घण्टाक|घण्टाकः
घण्टाक m. (-कः) A plant: see घण्टा पाटली<BR> E. कन् added to the preceding;<BR>some copies read घण्टीक and घाण्टीक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=253-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घण्टाकर्ण|घण्टाकर्णः|घण्टाकर्ण्ण
घण्टाकर्ण m. (-र्णः) One of ŚIVA'S attendants, and is worshipped to pre-<BR>side over cutaneous complaints, and is worshipped for exemption<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=253-b" target="_blank">Page253-b+ 60</a>]<BR>from them in the month Chaitra.<BR> E. घण्टा, and कर्ण and ear; having<BR>ears as broad as a bell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=253-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घण्टाताड|घंटाताड|घण्टाताडः
घण्टाताड m. (-डः) A bell-man, one who strikes a bell or Ghadi.<BR> E. घण्टा,<BR>and ताड who beats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=253-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घण्टाताडन
घण्टाताडन n. (-नं) Striking a bell.<BR> E. घण्टा, and ताडन beating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=253-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घण्टानाद|घंटानाद|घण्टानादः
घण्टानाद m. (-दः) The sound of a bell, &c.<BR> E. घण्टा, and नाद sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=253-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घण्टापथ|घंटापथ|घण्टापथः
घण्टापथ m. (-थः) The chief road through a village, a highway.<BR> E. घण्टा a<BR>bell, and पथि a road, affix अच्; the bell-road, or that by which<BR>elephants, &c. decorated with tinkling ornaments, proceed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=253-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घण्टापाटली
घण्टापाटली f. (-ली) A plant commonly called by the similar name Ghan-<BR>taparuli, a species of the trumpet flower, (Bignonia suave-olens.) E.<BR>घण्टा a bell, &c. and पाटली the trumpet flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=253-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घण्टावाद्य
घण्टावाद्य n. (-द्यं) The sound of a clock.<BR> E. घण्टा and वाद्य playing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=253-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घण्टावीज
घण्टावीज n. (-जं) The croton nut.<BR> E. घण्टा, and वीज seed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=253-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घण्टारवा
घण्टारवा f. (-वा) Crotolaria of various species.<BR> E. घण्टा, and रव sound;<BR>the seed rattling within the husk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=253-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घण्टाशब्द|घंटाशब्द|घण्टाशब्दं|घण्टाशब्दः
घण्टाशब्द m. (-ब्दं)<BR>	 1. Bell-metal.<BR>	 2. The sound of a bell.<BR> E. घण्टा, and शब्द<BR>sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=253-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घण्टास्वन
घण्टास्वन m. (-नः) The sound of a bell or clock.<BR> E. घण्टा, and स्वन<BR>sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=253-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घण्टिका|घंटिका
घण्टिका f. (-का) The uvula or soft palate.<BR> E. घण्टा a bell, and कन् affix<BR>of similitude.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=253-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घण्टु|घंटुः|घण्टुः
घण्टु m. (-ण्टुः)<BR>	 1. A string of bells tied on an elephant's chest, &c. by<BR>way of ornament.<BR>	 2. Heat, light, &c.<BR> E. घटि to shine, Uṇādi affix<BR>उन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=253-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घण्टेश्वर|घण्टेश्वरः
घण्टेश्वर m. (-रः) A minor deity, the son of MARS.<BR> E. घण्टा, and ईश्वर lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=253-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घण्ड|घंडः|घण्डः
घण्ड m. (-ण्डः) A bee.<BR> E. घण वा-ड तस्य नेत्त्वम् । भ्रमरे ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=253-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घन|घनं|घनः
घन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>	 1. Material, solid.<BR>	 2. Coarse, gross.<BR>	 3. Compact.<BR>	 4.<BR>Hard, firm.<BR>	 5. Full, plum.<BR>	 6. Impenetrable.<BR>	 7. Vicid, thick, inspis-<BR>sated.<BR>	 8. Deep, (as sound)<BR>	 9. Very, much.<BR>	 10. Auspicious, fortu-<BR>nate.<BR>	 11. Permanent, eternal.<BR>	 m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. A cloud.<BR>	 2. An iron club.<BR>3. The body.<BR>	 4. A fragrant grass, (Cyperus rotundus.)<BR>	 5. A num-<BR>ber, an assemblage or quantity.<BR>	 6. Extension, diffusion.<BR>	 7. Hard-<BR>ness.<BR>	 8. Solidity, substance. matter.<BR>	 9. The cube of a number, (in<BR>arithmetic.)<BR>	 10. A solid, (in geometry.)<BR>	 11. Phlegm.<BR>	 12. Talc.<BR>	 n.<BR>(-नं)<BR>	 1. A cymbal, a bell, a Gong, &c. any brazen or composite<BR>metallic instrument, which is struck as a clock, &c.<BR>	 2. A mode of<BR>dancing, neither quick nor slow.<BR>	 3. Iron.<BR>	 4. Skin, rind, bark, &c. E.<BR>हन् to strike or be struck, affix अप् and ह changed to घ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=253-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घनकफ|घनकफः
घनकफ m. (-फः) Hail.<BR> E. घन a cloud, and कफ phlegm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=253-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घनकाल|घनकालः
घनकाल m. (-लः) The rainy season.<BR> E. घन a cloud, and काल time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=253-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घनगोलक|घनगोलकः
घनगोलक m. (-कः) An alloy of gold and silver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=253-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घनघनौघ
घनघनौघ m. (-घः) A gathering of dark clouds.<BR> E. घन thick, close, घनौघ<BR>cumulus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=253-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घनचय
घनचय m. (-यः) A collection of clouds, cumulus<BR> E. घन, and चय a heap.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=253-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घनजम्वाल
घनजम्वाल m. (-लः) A quantity of mire, a slough.<BR> E. घन much, a heap,<BR>and जम्वाल mud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=253-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घनजाल
घनजाल n. (-लं) A gathering of clouds.<BR> E. घन, and जाल multitude.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=253-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घनज्वाला
घनज्वाला f. (-ला) Lightning, a flash of lightning.<BR> E. घन a cloud, and<BR>ज्वाला flame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=253-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घनताल|घनतालः
घनताल mf. (-लः-ला) A bird: see घनतोल. घनतायां निविडतायाम् अलति पर्य्या-<BR>प्नोति अल्-अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=253-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घनतिमिर
घनतिमिर n. (-रं)<BR>	 1. The darkness of clouds.<BR>	 2. Great darkness.<BR> E. घन,<BR>and तिमिर dark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=253-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घनत्व
घनत्व n. (-त्वं)<BR>	 1. Firmness, compactness.<BR>	 2. Thickness, coarseness,<BR>solidity.<BR> E. त्व added to घन; also with तल्, घनता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=253-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घनतोल|घनतोलः
घनतोल mf. (-लः-ला) The Chataka, (Cuculus melanolencos.)<BR> E. घन a<BR>cloud, and तुल् to be equal, घनं मेघं तोलयति ऊर्द्ध्वं नयति आह्वानेन । तुल-<BR>उन्मितौ अण् उपमित समासः । who soars to the clouds in the rainy sea-<BR>son, which, according to the fable, is the only time when he gets<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=254-a" target="_blank">Page254-a+ 60</a>]<BR>water to drink; some books have घनताल from ताल tune, or sound;<BR>whose music is (from) the clouds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=253-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घनध्वनि|घनध्वनिः
घनध्वनि mfn. (-निः-निः-नि) Roaring, who or what makes such a sound.<BR>m. (-निः)<BR>	 1. A deep and loud tone, a roar.<BR>	 2. The muttering of<BR>thunder clouds.<BR> E. घन and ध्वनि sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=254-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घननाभि|घननाभिः
घननाभि m. (-भिः) Smoke.<BR> E. घन a cloud, and नाभि the navel or centre;<BR>smoke being supposed to be a principal ingredient in clouds.<BR>घनस्य मेघस्य नाभिरिव योनित्वात् । धूमे ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=254-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घननीहार|घननीहारः
घननीहार m. (-रः) Thick falling frost or snow.<BR> E. घन, and नीहार hoar-<BR>frost.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=254-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घनपदवी
घनपदवी f. (-वी) The sky.<BR> E. घन a cloud, and पदवी station.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=254-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घनपयोधर
घनपयोधर m. (-रः) A firm breast.<BR> E. घन, and पयोधर the female breast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=254-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घनपल्लव
घनपल्लव m. (-वः) A plant, (Hyperanthera; morunga:) see शोभाञ्जन<BR> E. घन<BR>abundance, and पल्लव a shoot or sprout. घना निविडाः पल्लवा अस्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=254-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घनपाषण्ड|घनपाषंड|घनपाषण्डः
घनपाषण्ड mf. (-ण्डः-ण्डा) A peacock.<BR> E. घन a cloud, and पाषण्ड a sectary;<BR>this bird is supposed to delight in cloudy and rainy weather. घनेन<BR>मेघध्वनिना पाषण्ड इव उन्मत्तत्वात् । मयूरे ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=254-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घनफल|घनफलः
घनफल m. (-लः) The contents of a solid, (in Geometry.)<BR> E. घन and फल<BR>fruit. घनानि निविडानि फलानि अस्य । विकङ्कटवृक्षे च ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=254-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घनमूल|घनमूलं|घनमूलः
घनमूल n. (-लं) Cube root, (in Arithmetic.)<BR> E. घन and मूल root. घनस्य<BR>समत्रिघातस्य मूलमाद्यम् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=254-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घनरव|घनरवः
घनरव m. (-वः) The roaring of clouds, thunder.<BR> E. घन and रव sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=254-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घनरस|घनरसः
घनरस mn. (-सः-सं) Water.<BR>	 m. (-सः)<BR>	 1. Camphor.<BR>	 2. Extract, decoction,<BR>&c.<BR>	 3. A plant, (Aletris hyacinthoides.)<BR>	 4. Thick or inspissated<BR>juice.<BR> E. घन a cloud or a heap, and रस juice, essence. घनस्य मेघस्य<BR>मुस्नकस्य वा रसो निष्यन्दः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=254-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घनवर्त्म
घनवर्त्म n. (-र्त्म) The sky.<BR> E. घन and वर्त्मन् path.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=254-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घनवल्लिका
घनवल्लिका f. (-का) Lightning.<BR> E. घन a cloud, and वल्लिका a creeper. घना<BR>निविडा वल्ली यस्याः कप् ह्रस्वः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=254-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घनवल्ली
घनवल्ली f. (-ल्ली) Lightning.<BR> E. घन and वल्ली a creeper. घनस्य मेघस्य वल्लीव । विद्यु ति ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=254-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घनवात|घनवातः
घनवात m. (-तः) One of the regions of hell.<BR> E. घन much, and वात wind;<BR>the region of storm. घनो निविडो वातोऽत्र ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=254-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घनवास|घनवासः
घनवास m. (-सः) A pumpkin gourd.<BR> E. घन a long time, and वास abiding.<BR>घनो वासो गन्धोऽस्य कुष्माण्डे ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=254-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घनवाहन|घनवाहनः
घनवाहन m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. A name of ŚIVA.<BR>	 2. A name of INDRA.<BR> E. घन a cloud<BR>and वाहन a vehicle; who rides in the clouds. घन इव शुभ्रं वाहनमस्य ।<BR>शिवे । घनो मेघो वाहनमस्य । इन्द्रे वा ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=254-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घनवीथि|घनवीथिः
घनवीथि f. (-थिः) A line of clouds.<BR> E. घन and वीथि a row. घनानां वीथिः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=254-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घनशब्द|घनशब्दः
घनशब्द m. (-ब्दः) The noise of clouds, thunder.<BR> E. घन and शब्द sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=254-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घनश्याम|घनश्यामः
घनश्याम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं) Black, deep black, as that of heavy clouds m.<BR>(-मः)<BR>	 1. RAMA.<BR>	 2. KṚṢṆA.<BR> E. घन and श्याम black. घनः मेघ इव श्यामः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=254-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घनसंवृत्ति|घनसंवृत्तिः
घनसंवृत्ति f. (-त्तिः) Profound secrecy.<BR> E. घन impenetrable, संवृत्ति secret<BR>purpose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=254-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घनस्वन|घनस्वनः
घनस्वन m. (-नः) Low thunder, the muttering of clouds.<BR> E. घन, and स्वन<BR>sound. घनेन तज्जलेन सुष्ठु अनिति अन्-अच् तृती-तत्पुरुषः । तण्डुलीयशाके ।<BR>मेघध्वनौच ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=254-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घनसमय|घनसमयः
घनसमय m. (-यः) The rainy season.<BR> E. घन a cloud, समय time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=254-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घनसार|घनसारः
घनसार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Camphor.<BR>	 2. Mercury, or some peculiar form of it.<BR>	 3.<BR>Water.<BR>	 4. A kind of tree.<BR> E. घन firm, &c. and सार essence. घनस्य मुस्त-<BR>कस्य सारः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=254-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घनाकर|घनाकरः
घनाकर m. (-रः) The rainy season.<BR> E. घन a cloud, and आकर a mine or<BR>place of producing. घनानामाकरः घनान् आकिरति आ + कॄ अच् वा । वर्षाकाले ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=254-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घनाघन|घनाघनः
घनाघन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>	 1. Mischievous, cruel.<BR>	 2. Even, uniform, with-<BR>out spaces or interstices.<BR>	 m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. A name of INDRA.<BR>	 2. A vici-<BR>ous elephant, or one in rut.<BR>	 3. A rainy cloud.<BR>	 4. Mutual collision.<BR>f. (-ना) A vegetable, (Solanum Indicum;) also काकमाची.<BR> E. घन as<BR>above, reiterated and the final of the first made long. हन-अच्<BR>निपातने ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=254-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घनात्यय|घनात्ययः
घनात्यय m. (-यः) The season succeeding the rains, autumn.<BR> E. घन a cloud<BR>and अत्यय disappearance, departure. घनानामत्ययोऽत्र । शरत्काले ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=254-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घनान्त|घनान्तः
घनान्त n. (-न्तं) Autumn, the end of the rains.<BR> E. घन a cloud, and अन्त<BR>end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=254-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घनामय|घनामयः
घनामय m. (-यः) The date tree, (Elate sylvestris.)<BR> E. घन a cloud, and<BR>आमय sickness, pining in the rains. घनो दृढः आमयो यस्मात् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=254-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घनामल|घनामलः
घनामल m. (-लः) A kind of potherb, (Chenopodium album:) see वास्तूक.<BR>E. घन much, and अमल clear, clean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=254-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घनाम्बु|घनांबु
घनाम्बु n. (-म्बु) Rain.<BR> E. घन, and अम्बु water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=254-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घनारुण
घनारुण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Deep red.<BR> E. घन, and अरुण red.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=254-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घनारुद्ध
घनारुद्ध mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं) Overcast, overspread with clouds.<BR> E. घन, and<BR>आरुद्ध obstructed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=254-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घनावरुद्ध
घनावरुद्ध mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं) Overcast, overspread with clouds.<BR> E. घन, and<BR>अवरुद्ध impeded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=254-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घनाश्रय|घनाश्रयः
घनाश्रय m. (-यः) Æther, the atmosphere or heaven.<BR> E. घन a cloud, and<BR>आश्रय asylum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=254-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घनीकृत
घनीकृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Hardened, compacted, made solid or firm.<BR>	 2.<BR>Congealed, thickened.<BR> E. घन and कृत made, with च्वि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=254-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घनोदधि|घनोदधिः
घनोदधि m. (-धिः) A division of hell.<BR> E. घन viscid, and उदधि an ocean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=254-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घनोपल|घनोपलः
घनोपल m. (-लः) Hail.<BR> E. घन a cloud, and उपल a stone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=254-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घनोपरुद्ध
घनोपरुद्ध mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं) Clouded, overcast.<BR> E. घन and उपरुद्ध obstructed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=254-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घनौघ|घनौघः
घनौघ m. (-घः) A gathering of clouds.<BR> E. घन, and ओघ a heap.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=254-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घम्ब
घम्ब r. 1st. cl. (घम्बति) To go to move. गतौ भ्वा-पर-सक-सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=254-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घर्घट|घर्घटः
घर्घट m. (-टः) A kind of fish, (Pimelodus gagora or P. tengara, HAM.)<BR>E. घर् an imitative sound, and घट् to endeavour, affix अच्; who<BR>makes such a sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=254-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घर्घर|घर्घरः
घर्घर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) One of the tones or notes in music.<BR>	 m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. The<BR>pass of a mountain.<BR>	 2. A door, a gate.<BR>	 3. An owl.<BR>	 4. The name of<BR>a river, the Gogra or Ghogra.<BR>	 5. Sound.<BR>	 6. Laughter, mirth.<BR>	 7. A<BR>fire of straw or chaff.<BR>	 f. (-रा or -री) A girdle of small bells or tin-<BR>kling ornaments worn by women.<BR>	 f. (-रा) A kind of lute.<BR> E. घर्घ<BR>here said to said to imply an inarticulate sound, gurgling, &c. and<BR>रा to give or take, affix क also with कन् added घर्घरक. घर्घेत्यनुकरणशब्दं<BR>राति । राक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=254-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घर्घरारव
घर्घरारव m. (-वः) A tinkling sound, the sound of small bells.<BR> E. घर्घरा<BR>and रव sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=254-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घर्घरिका
घर्घरिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. An ornament of small bells worn by women, horses,<BR>&c.<BR>	 2. The bow or stick of a viol, &c.<BR>	 3. A sort of musical instru-<BR>ment.<BR>	 4. Fried grain.<BR>	 5. The name of a river.<BR> E. घर्घरी as above,<BR>and ठन् added fem. form. घर्घरोऽस्ति अस्य ठन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=254-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घर्घूर्घा
घर्घूर्घा m. (-र्घा)<BR>	 1. A sort of insect. घृ-विच् घुर ध्वनौ क्विप् तौ हन्ति हन् ड निः<BR>तस्य घः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=254-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घर्ब|घर्ब्ब
घर्ब r. 1st cl. (-घर्बति) To go, to move. गतौ भ्वा-पर-सक-सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=254-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घर्म्म|घर्म|घर्मः|घर्म्मः
घर्म्म m. (-र्म्मः)<BR>	 1. Heat.<BR>	 2. The hot season.<BR>	 3. Sunshine.<BR>	 4. Sweat, pers-<BR>piration.<BR> E. घृ to sprinkle and मक् Uṇādi affix; what sprinkles the<BR>limbs. घरति अङ्गात् घृ सेके क्षेरणे कर्त्तरि मक्-निपातने । गुणः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=254-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घर्म्मचर्च्चिका|घर्मचर्चिका|घर्म्मचर्चिका
घर्म्मचर्च्चिका f. (-का) Eruptions from suppressed perspiration.<BR> E. घर्म्म and<BR>चर्च्चिका घर्मकृता चर्चिका । घामाचि इति ख्याते ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=254-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घर्म्मद्युति|घर्मद्युति|घर्मद्युतिः
घर्म्मद्युति m. (-तिः) The sun.<BR> E. घर्म्म and द्युति splendour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=254-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घर्म्मपयस्|घर्मपयस्
घर्म्मपयस् n. (-यः)<BR>	 1. Sweat, perspiration.<BR>	 2. Warm water.<BR> E. घर्म्म, and<BR>पयस् water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=254-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घर्म्मरश्मि|घर्मरश्मि
घर्म्मरश्मि m. (-श्मिः)<BR>	 1. The sun.<BR>	 2. Heat, radiance.<BR> E. घर्म्म, and रश्मि a ray.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=254-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घर्म्मविचर्च्चिका|घर्मविचर्चिका
घर्म्मविचर्च्चिका f. (-का) Cutaneous eruptions or pimples from suppressed<BR>perspiration.<BR> E. घर्म्म and विचर्च्चिका pustular eruption.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=254-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घर्म्मान्त|घर्मान्त|घर्मांत|घर्मान्तः|घर्म्मान्तः
घर्म्मान्त m. (-न्तः) The rainy season.<BR> E. घर्म्म and अन्त end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=254-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घर्म्मान्तकामुकी|घर्मान्तकामुकी
घर्म्मान्तकामुकी m. (-की) A small white bird; a kind of crane.<BR> E. घर्म्मान्त,<BR>and कामुकी who wishes for.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=254-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घर्म्मार्त्त|घर्मार्त
घर्म्मार्त्त mfn. (-र्त्तः-र्त्ता-र्त्तं) Suffering from heat.<BR> E. घर्म्म and आर्त्त pained<BR>by.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=254-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घर्म्माम्बु|घर्माम्बु|घर्मांबु
घर्म्माम्बु n. (-म्बु)<BR>	 1. Perspiration, sweat.<BR>	 2. Warm water.<BR> E. घर्म्म and अम्बु<BR>water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=254-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घर्म्मोदक|घर्मोदक
घर्म्मोदक n. (-कं)<BR>	 1. Perspiration.<BR>	 2. Warm water.<BR> E. घर्म्म and उदक water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=254-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घर्ष|घर्षः
घर्ष m. (-र्षः) Rubbing friction.<BR> E. घृष् to rub, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=255-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घर्षण|घर्षणं
घर्षण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Grinding, pounding.<BR>	 2. Rubbing, friction.<BR>	 f. (-णी) Tur-<BR>meric.<BR> E. घृष् to grind, affix भावे ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=255-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घर्षणाल|घर्षणालः
घर्षणाल m. (-लः) A roller or pestle for grinding, &c.<BR> E. घर्षण rubbing,<BR>and अल what is fit for. घर्षणाय अलति अल अच् । (नोडा) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=255-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घर्षित
घर्षित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Rubbed.<BR>	 2. Ground.<BR> E. घृष् to rub, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=255-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घष
घष (इ) घषि r. 1st cl. (घंषते) To render handsome or brilliant. क्षरणे भ्वा-<BR>आत्म-अक-सेट् इदित् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=255-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घस|घसः
घस (आ ऌ) औघसॢ r. 1st cl. (घसति) To eat: this root is in many tenses a<BR>substitute for अद and is itself imperfect in others. (इ) घसि r. 1st cl.<BR>(घंसते) To sprinkle or drop; this root is not generally admitted.<BR>भक्षणे भ्वा-पर-सक-अनिट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=255-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घसि|घसिः
घसि m. (-सिः) Food, victuals.<BR> E. घस् to eat, भावे इन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=255-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घस्मर|घस्मरः
घस्मर mfn. (-रः-री-रं) Gluttonous, voracious,<BR> E. घस् to eat, क्मरच् aff. मक्षण-<BR>शीले ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=255-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घस्र|घस्रं|घस्रः
घस्र mfn. (-स्रः-स्रा-स्रं) Mischievous, hurtful.<BR>	 m. (-स्रः) A day.<BR>	 n. (-स्रं)<BR>Saffron.<BR> E. घस् to eat, and रक् aff. घसति अन्धकारम् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=255-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घाट|घाटः
घाट mf. (-टः-टी) The nape or back of the neck.<BR> E. घट् to unite, affix<BR>अच्; the radical is of the 10th class of roots, whence the penul-<BR>timate is long. ग्रीवयोः पश्चाद्भागे अवटौ (घाड्) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=255-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घाटिका
घाटिका f. (-का) The nape of the neck.<BR> E. स्वाथ क added to the prece-<BR>ding. घाटायाम् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=255-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घाण्टिक|घांटिक|घांटिकः|घाण्टिकः
घाण्टिक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A bard, who sings in chorus, but especially in<BR>honour of the gods, and rings a bell in presence of their images.<BR>	 2.<BR>Datura fastuosa.<BR> E. घण्टा a bell affix ठक् घण्टया चरति ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=255-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घात|घातः
घात n. (-तं)<BR>	 1. Striking, wounding, killing.<BR>	 2. A bruise, a blow.<BR>	 3. An<BR>arrow.<BR>	 4. Product (of a sum in multiplication.)<BR> E. हन to<BR>to kill, घञ् affix, and the radical letters changed respectively, to<BR>घ and त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=255-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घातक|घातकः
घातक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) A murderer, a maimer, &c.<BR> E. हन् as above,<BR>with ण्वुल् aff. हननकर्त्तरि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=255-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घातन|घातनं|घातनः
घातन m. (-नं) A murderer, a killer.<BR>	 n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Killing, slaughter.<BR>	 2. Stri-<BR>king.<BR>	 3. Immolating victims.<BR> E. हन् to kill, ल्युट् affix, and घात sub-<BR>stituted for the radical. हस्त्यर्थत्वात् स्वार्थे णिच् भावे ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=255-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घातयत्
घातयत् mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्) Striking, hurting, killing.<BR> E. हन् to kill,<BR>causal form, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=255-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घातव्य
घातव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं) To be killed, what may be or ought to be<BR>killed &c.<BR> E. हन् to kill, तव्य affix, and घा substituted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=255-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घातस्थान
घातस्थान n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. A slaughter house.<BR>	 2. A place of execution.<BR> E. घात,<BR>and स्थान place. श्मशाने ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=255-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घाति|घातिः
घाति m. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Catching or killing birds, fowling.<BR>	 2. killing in gener-<BR>al.<BR>	 3. Striking.<BR> E. हन् to kill or hurt, affix इण्, and the radical<BR>changed: see घात.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=255-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घातिन्
घातिन् mfn. (-ती-तिनी-ति) Murderous, felonious, who or what strikes or<BR>kills.<BR> E. हन् to kill, णिनि aff. हन-ताच्छील्यार्थे णिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=255-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घातिपक्षिन्
घातिपक्षिन् mf. (-क्षी-क्षिणी) A hawk or falcon.<BR> E. घाति fowling, and पक्षिन् a<BR>bird. श्येनखगे ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=255-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घातुक|घातुकः
घातुक mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>	 1. Mischievous, hurtful.<BR>	 2. Cruel, savage. vio-<BR>lent, ferocious.<BR> E. हन् to kill, changed to घात, and उकञ् aff. हिंसे,<BR>क्रूरेच.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=255-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घात्य|घात्यं
घात्य mfn. (-त्यः-त्या-त्यं) Proper or fit to be killed.<BR> E. हन् and ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=255-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घार|घारः
घार m. (-रः) Sprinkling, wetting.<BR> E. घॄ to sprinkle, and घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=255-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घार्त्तिक|घार्तिक|घार्तिकः|घार्त्तिकः
घार्त्तिक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Pulse ground and fried with clarified butter. E.<BR>घृत ghee, and ठञ् aff. घृतप्रचुरे छिद्रबहुले पक्कान्नभेदे । (घिओड्) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=255-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घास|घासः
घास m. (-सः) Meadow or pasture grass.<BR> E. घस् to eat. कर्मणि घञ् affix;<BR>what is eaten by animals.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=255-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घासि|घासिः
घासि m. (-सिः) Fire or its deity.<BR> E. घस् to devour, and इण् Uṇādi aff.<BR>भक्ष्ये तृणादौ-त्रि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=255-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घिण
घिण r. 1st cl. (इ) घिणि (घिणते) To take, to seize or accept. ग्रहणे भ्वा-आ-<BR>सक-सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=255-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घु|घुः
घु 1st cl. (घवते) To sound. ध्वनौ भ्वा-आ-अक-अनिट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=255-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घु|घुः
घु m. (-घुः) Sound.<BR> E. घु to sound, aff. डु । घु-ध्वनौ वा डु ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=255-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घुट|घुटः
घुट r. 1st cl. (घोटते)<BR>	 1. To come back, to return.<BR>	 2. To barter or ex-<BR>change. r. 6th cl. (घुटति)<BR>	 1. To strike again or retaliate, to resist<BR>or oppose.<BR>	 2. To prevent.<BR>	 3. To protect or preserve. भ्वा-आत्म-<BR>सक-सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=255-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घुट|घुटः
घुट m. (-टः) The ankle.<BR> E. घुट् to resist, and क affix; also घुटि, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=255-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घुटि|घुटिः
घुटि f. (-टिः-टी) The ankle.<BR> E. घुट् to resist, affix इन् and वा ङीप् may be<BR>added, also with कन् added घुटिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=255-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घुटिक|घुटिकः
घुटिक mf. (-कः-का) The ankle, &c. see घुट and घुटि; also घुण्ट. घुट अस्त्यर्थे<BR>ठन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=255-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घुण|घुणः
घुण r. 1st and 6th cls. (घोणते घुणति) To roll, to whirl, to turn round,<BR>(इ) घुणि r. 1st cl. (घुणते) To take or accept. भ्वा-आ-सक-सेट् । तु-प-अक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=255-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घुण|घुणः
घुण m. (-णः)<BR>	 1. An insect that is found in timber.<BR>	 2. The pangolin or<BR>armadillo.<BR> E. घुण् to turn round, affix क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=255-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घुण्ट|घुंट|घुंटः|घुण्टः
घुण्ट m. (-ण्टः) The ankle.<BR> E. घुट् to resist, affix क and नुम् inserted; also<BR>with कन् added घुण्टक, or without the augment घुट &c. as above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=255-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घुण्टिक|घुंटिकं|घुण्टिकं
घुण्टिक n. (-कं) Cowdung found in thickets. घुण्ट-स्तदाकारोऽस्ति अस्य ठन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=255-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घुण्ड|घुंड|घुंडः|घुण्डः
घुण्ड m. (-ण्डः) A large black bee.<BR> E. घुण् to roll, Uṇādi affix ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=255-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घुर
घुर r.<BR>	 6. th cl. (घुरति)<BR>	 1. To be frightful or terrible.<BR>	 2. To sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=255-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घुर
घुर (ई) घुरी r. 4th cl. (घुर्य्यते)<BR>	 1. To be ignorant.<BR>	 2. To inquire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=255-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घुर्घुर|घुर्घुरः
घुर्घुर m. (-रः) A kind of worm borrowing in the skin, guinea worm,<BR>Dracunculus.<BR>	 f. (-री) The mole cricket.<BR>	 f. (-रा) Growling, as of<BR>dog or cat.<BR> E. घुर् imitative sound, and घुर् to sound, with क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=255-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घुष
घुष (इ) घुषि r. 1st cl. (घुंषते) To render beautiful or brilliant (इर) घुषिर<BR>r. 1st cl. (घोषति) To do any act except manifest sentiment by<BR>sound. r. 10th cl. (घोषयति)<BR>	 1. To manifest sentiment or thought by<BR>sound, to speak, to affirm, to declare or proclaim.<BR>	 2. To make<BR>various sounds.<BR>	 3. To praise. With आङ् prefixed, To weep in-<BR>cessantly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=255-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घुषित|घुषितं
घुषित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Manifested by sound, proclaimed.<BR> E. घुष् as above,<BR>affix क्त इट् augment; also घुष्ट.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=255-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घुष्ट|घुष्टं
घुष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं) Sounded, proclaimed,<BR> E. घुष् to sound, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=255-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घुष्टान्न
घुष्टान्न n. (-न्नं) Food given away by proclamation.<BR> E. घुष्ट and अन्न food.<BR>घुष्टं को भोक्ता इति उद्घुष्य देयमन्नम् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=255-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घुष्ट्र|घुष्ट्रं
घुष्ट्र m. (-ष्ट्रः) A car, a carriage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=255-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घुसृण|घुसृणं
घुसृण n. (-णं) Saffron.<BR> E. घुषि to beautify, ऋणक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=255-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घूक|घूकः
घूक m. (-कः) An owl.<BR> E. घू an imitative sound, and कै who sounds, from<BR>कै with क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=255-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घूकारि|घूकारिः
घूकारि m. (-रिः) A crow.<BR> E. घूक an owl, and अरि an enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=255-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घूर
घूर (ई) घूरी r. 4th cl. (घूर्य्यते)<BR>	 1. To kill, to hurt or injure.<BR>	 2. To become<BR>old, to decay. सक-जीर्णतायाम् अक-दि-आ-सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=255-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घूर्ण|घूर्णः|घूर्ण्ण
घूर्ण r. and 6th cls. (घूर्णते, घूर्णति) To roll, to whirl, to turn round.<BR>भ्रमणे अक-तु-उभ-सेट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=255-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घूर्ण|घूर्णः|घूर्ण्ण
घूर्ण m. (-र्णः)<BR>	 1. A kind of potherb, (Chironia centauroides:) see<BR>ग्रीष्मसुन्दरक 2. Turning round, whirling, rolling, &c.<BR> E. घूर्ण to roll,<BR>affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=255-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घूर्णन|घूर्णनं|घूर्ण्णन
घूर्णन n. (-नं) Revolving, whirling turning round.<BR> E. घूर्ण to whirl, भावे<BR>ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=255-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घूर्णायमान|घूर्णायमानः|घूर्ण्णायमान
घूर्णायमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Whirling, revolving, rolling, tossing<BR> E. घूर्ण<BR>and शानच् aff. घूर्णः भ्रान्त इव आचरति भृशा-च्वर्थे वा क्यङ् कर्त्तरि शानच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=255-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घूर्णि|घूर्णिः|घूर्ण्णि
घूर्णि f. (-र्णिः) Rolling, revolving, going round or over.<BR> E. घूर्ण and भावे<BR>इन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=255-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घूर्णित|घूर्णितः|घूर्ण्णित
घूर्णित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Rolling, turning, tossing.<BR> E. घूर्ण to turn round,<BR>affix कर्त्तरि क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=255-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घूर्ण्यमान|घूर्ण्यमानः
घूर्ण्यमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Agitated, set in motion, made to go round. E.<BR>घूर्ण to revolve, pass, voice, शानच् affix also घूर्णमान middle voice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=255-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घृ
घृ r. 1st, 3rd and 10th cls. (घरति जिघर्त्ति and घरयति)<BR>	 1. To sprinkle, to<BR>wet or moisten.<BR>	 2. To drop or distil.<BR>	 3. To shine. भासे-अक-सेके-सक-<BR>भ्वा-जु-पर अनिट् घृ सेके छादने च चु-उभ-सक-सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=255-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घृण|घृणः
घृण (उ) घृणु r. 8th cl. (घर्णोति घृणोति घर्णुते) To shine. (इ) घृणि r. 1st. cl.<BR>(घृणते) To take or accept. दीप्तौ तना-उभ-अक-सेट्. ग्रहणे भ्वा-आ सक-सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=256-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घृणा
घृणा f. (-णा)<BR>	 1. Reproach, blame, censure, &c.<BR>	 2. Compassion, tender-<BR>ness, pity.<BR> E. घृण् to shine, अङ् and टाप् affixes, or घृ to sprinkle,<BR>with नक् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=256-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घृणावास|घृणावासः
घृणावास m. (-सः) A pumpkin gourd. कूष्माण्डे ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=256-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घृणि|घृणिः
घृणि m. (-णिः)<BR>	 1. A ray of the sun or moon.<BR>	 2. The sun.<BR>	 3. Water. E.<BR>घॄण to shine, affix इन्; or घृ to sprinkle, Uṇādi नि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=256-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घृणित
घृणित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Abused, hated.<BR>	 2. Pitied<BR> E. घृणा pity इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=256-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घृणिन्
घृणिन् mfn. (-णी-णिनी-णि)<BR>	 1. Censorious, abusive.<BR>	 2. Compassionate. E.<BR>घृणा and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=256-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घृत|घृतः
घृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Sprinkled.<BR>	 2. Illumined.<BR>	 n. (-तं)<BR>	 1. Ghee, clarified<BR>butter, or butter which has been boiled gently, and allowed to<BR>cool: it is then used for culinary and religious purpose and is<BR>highly esteemed by the Hindus.<BR>	 2. Water.<BR>	 f. (-ता) The name of a<BR>tree: see घृतमण्डा.<BR> E. घृ to sprinkle Uṇādi affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=256-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घृतकुमारी
घृतकुमारी f. (-री) The aloe, (Aloes perfoliata)<BR> E. घृत ghee, to which the<BR>extact is compared, and कुमारी a virgin, which the plant is sup-<BR>posed to resemble in delicacy and elegance; also घृतकुमारिका. घुतमिव<BR>कुमारी सुन्दरी ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=256-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घृतकुम्भ
घृतकुम्भ m. (-म्भः) A jar of ghee.<BR> E. घृत and कुम्भ a jar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=256-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घृतदीधिति|घृतदीधितिः
घृतदीधिति m. (-तिः) The deity of fire.<BR> E. घृत ghee, and दीधिति light; of-<BR>ferings to fire, always comprehending clarified butter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=256-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घृतपशु|घृतपशुः
घृतपशु m. (-शुः) Ghee made into or supposed to resemble an animal to<BR>be offered at a sacrifice or eaten at a meal, for which it is substi-<BR>tuted.<BR> E. घृत, and पशु an animal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=256-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घृतपूर|घृतपूरः
घृतपूर m. (-रः) A sweetmeat composed of flour, milk, cocoanut and<BR>ghee, &c.<BR> E. घृत ghee, and पूर what is full of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=256-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घृतपूर्णक|घृतपूर्णकः|घृतपूर्ण्णक
घृतपूर्णक m. (-कः) A tree. (Caledupa arborea, &c.) see करञ्ज<BR> E. घृत ghee,<BR>and पूर्ण full, कप् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=256-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घृतप्राश|घृतप्राशः
घृतप्राश m. (-शः) Swallowing ghee.<BR> E. घृत and प्राश eating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=256-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घृतप्राशन
घृतप्राशन n. (-नं) Tasting or swallowing ghee.<BR> E. घृत and प्राश eating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=256-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घृतप्लुत
घृतप्लुत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Sprinkled or smeared with ghee,.<BR> E. घृत, and प्लुत<BR>bathed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=256-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घृतमण्डा
घृतमण्डा f. (-ण्डा) A tree; also वायसोली.<BR> E. घृत, and मण्ड scum; the scum<BR>of its infusion resembling ghee.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=256-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घृतलोलीकृत
घृतलोलीकृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Mixed with ghee, steeped in it or wet with<BR>it, &c.<BR> E. घृत लोल desirous. कृत made, च्वि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=256-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घृतवर|घृतवरः
घृतवर m. (-रः) A sweetmeat, or flour, &c. baked with ghee, and sugar.<BR>E. घृत and वर what excels.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=256-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घृतविक्रयिन्
घृतविक्रयिन् m. (-यी) A vender of ghee.<BR> E. घृत विक्रय to sell, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=256-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घृतस्पृश्
घृतस्पृश् mfn. (-स्पृक्) Who or what touches ghee.<BR> E. घृत स्पृश to touch, क्विन्<BR>aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=256-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घृताक्त
घृताक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं) Smeared with ghee.<BR> E. घृत and अक्त smeared.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=256-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घृताची
घृताची f. (-ची) One of the Apsaras or courtezans of Svarga.<BR> E. घृत ghee,<BR>अञ्च to worship, क्विप् and ङीप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=256-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घृताचीगर्भसम्भवा|घृताचीगर्भसंभवा|घृताचीगर्भ्भसम्भवा
घृताचीगर्भसम्भवा f. (-वा) Large cardamoms.<BR> E. घृताची गर्भ the womb, and<BR>सम्भव born from.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=256-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घृताभ्यक्त
घृताभ्यक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं) Smeared or anointed with ghee.<BR> E. घृत and<BR>अभ्यक्त anointed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=256-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घृताह्व|घृताह्वः
घृताह्व m. (-ह्वः) Turpentine.<BR> E. घृत ghee, and आह्वा and appellation, named<BR>from ghee.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=256-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घृतेली
घृतेली f. (-ली) A cock-roach.<BR> E. घृत ghee. इल् to go, अच् affix, र changed<BR>to ल fem. affix ङीष् । घृते स्नेहद्रव्ये इलति शेते इल शाये-अच् गौरा-ङीष् ।<BR>(तेलापोका) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=256-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घृतोद|घृतोदः
घृतोद m. (-दः) The sea of ghee surrounding Kusa Dwipa.<BR> E. घृत and<BR>उद water. घृतमिव स्वादु उदकमस्य । उदकस्य उदः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=256-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घृतोदङ्कः|घृतोदङ्क
घृतोदङ्कः m. (-ङ्कः) A leather vessel holding ghee.<BR> E. घृत उद up, अञ्च् to<BR>go, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=256-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घृष
घृष (उ) घृषु r. 1st cl. (घर्षति) To grind or pound. सक-पर-सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=256-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घृष्ट|घृष्टः
घृष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>	 1. Ground, rubbed, pounded.<BR>	 2. Frayed, grazed,<BR>rubbed off.<BR> E. घृष् to rub, कर्मणि क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=256-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घृष्टि|घृष्टिः
घृष्टि mf. (-ष्टिः) A hog; also गृष्टि f. (-ष्टिः)<BR>	 1. A plant, commonly Varaha-<BR>cranti, (Lycopodium imbricatum, Rox.)<BR>	 2. Grinding, pounding.<BR>	 3.<BR>Emulation, contest.<BR> E. घृष् to grind, affix कर्त्तरि क्तिच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=256-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घृष्टिला
घृष्टिला f. (ला) A plant: see पृश्निपर्णी<BR> E. घृष्टिं लाति लाक घर्षति भूमिं तुण्डेन ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=256-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घृष्वि|घृष्विः
घृष्वि mf. (-ष्विः-ष्वी) A hog.<BR> E. घृष् to rub, Uṇādi affix क्विन् घर्षति<BR>भूमिं तुण्डेन ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=256-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घेञ्चलिका
घेञ्चलिका f. (-का) An esculent root, (Arum orinense.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=256-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घोङ्क
घोङ्क (-ङ्क-ङ्का) mf. पक्षिभेदे ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=256-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घोङ्घ|घोंघः|घोङ्घः
घोङ्घ m. (-ङ्घः) Intermediate space.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=256-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घोट|घोटः
घोट m. (-टः) a horse: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=256-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घोटक|घोटकः
घोटक m. (-कः) A horse.<BR>	 f. (-टिका) A mare.<BR> E. घुट to strike again, (to<BR>spurn the ground,) अच् and कन् ण्वुल् वा affixes, or without the<BR>latter affix घोट.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=256-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घोणा
घोणा f. (णा)<BR>	 1. The nose.<BR>	 2. The nose or nostrils of a horse.<BR> E. घुण् to<BR>roll, to turn, and अच् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=256-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घोणिन्
घोणिन् m. (-णी) A hog.<BR> E. घोणा nose or snout, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=256-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घोण्टा|घोंटा
घोण्टा f. (-ण्ठा)<BR>	 1. The jujube, (Zizyphus jujuba.)<BR>	 2. The betelnut tree:<BR>see गुवाक.<BR>	 3. A timber tree, (Schrebera swietenioides.)<BR> E. घुट् to<BR>resist, affix अच् and नुम् inserted or घुण वा ट ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=256-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घोनस|घोनसः
घोन[ण्]स m. (-सः) A large kind of snake.<BR> E. घो for गो a cow, and नस a<BR>nose. see गोनस according to others the word is घोणस, from घुण् to<BR>roll, and असच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=256-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घोर|घोरं|घोरः
घोर r. 1st cl. (घोरति) To go as a horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=256-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घोर|घोरं|घोरः
घोर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Frightful, horrible, terrific.<BR>	 m. (-रः) A name of<BR>SHIVA.<BR>	 f. (-रा) Night.<BR>	 n. (-रं)<BR>	 1. Horror, horribleness.<BR>	 2. Poison. E.<BR>घुर् to be frightful, affix अच or गुर् substituted for हन् to injure or<BR>kill, and अच् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=256-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घोरदर्शन|घोरदर्शनः
घोरदर्शन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Terrific, of horrid or frightful appearance.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-नः) An owl.<BR> E. घोर as above, and दर्शन sight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=256-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घोरपुष्प|घोरपुष्पं
घोरपुष्प m. (-ष्पः) Bellmetal.<BR> E. घोर and पुष्प a flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=256-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घोररासन|घोररासनः
घोररासन m. (-नः) A jackal.<BR> E. घोर frightful, and रासन cry or sound,<BR>from रास् to sound, affix ल्युट.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=256-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घोररासिन्
घोररासिन् m. (-सी) A jackal. E. See the last, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=256-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घोररूप|घोररूपः
घोररूप mfn. (-पः-पी-पं) Frightful, hideous.<BR>	 n. (-पं) A hideous. appearance.<BR>E. घोर and रूप form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=256-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घोररूपिन्
घोररूपिन् mfn. (-पी-पिणी-पि) Frightful, horrible, hideous.<BR> E. घोररूप and<BR>णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=256-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घोरसङ्काश|घोरसंकाश
घोरसङ्काश mfn. (-शः-शा-शं) Dreadful, horrible.<BR> E. घोर, and सङ्काश like.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=256-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घोराकृति
घोराकृति mfn. (-तिः-तिः-ति) Frightful, hideous, of horrible aspect or<BR>form.<BR> E. घोर, and आकृति form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=256-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घोल|घोलं|घोलः
घोल n. (-लं) Buttelmilk.<BR> E. घुड substituted for हन् to strike, (i. e. with<BR>the churn,) and घञ् affix, ड changed to ल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=256-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घोष|घोषं|घोषः
घोष m. (-षः)<BR>	 1. A station of herdsmen.<BR>	 2. A herdsman.<BR>	 3. A creeping<BR>plant, commonly called by the same name Ghosha, and bearing<BR>white or yellow flowers, (Luffa pentandra and acutangula.)<BR>	 4.<BR>Bellmetal, tutenague, &c.<BR>	 5. Low thunder or the muttering of<BR>clouds.<BR>	 6. Sound.<BR>	 7. A proclamation.<BR>	 8. A gnat, a musquito 9. A<BR>term proper for the name of a Kayastha.<BR>	 f. (-षा) A kind of fennel,<BR>(Anethum sowa:) see मधुरिका.<BR> E. घुषि to shine, to sound, &c. affix.<BR>आधारे घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=256-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घोषक|घोषकः
घोषक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A cryer, a proclaimer.<BR>	 2. Ghosha, described as a cree-<BR>king plant, (Luffa pentangula, &c.)<BR> E. कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=256-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घोषकाकृति|घोषकाकृतिः
घोषकाकृति f. (-तिः) A plant commonly called Hatighosha, and perhaps<BR>a species of the preceding.<BR> E. घोषक Ghosha, and आकृति shape, ap-<BR>appearance of similar appearance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=256-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घोषण|घोषणं
घोषण nf. (-णं-णा)<BR>	 1. Speaking loud, making a great noise.<BR>	 2. Crying,<BR>proclaiming.<BR> E. घुष् to sound, affixes णिच् भावे ल्युट् and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=256-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घोषयित्नु|घोषयित्नुः
घोषयित्नु m. (-त्नुः)<BR>	 1. A Brahman.<BR>	 2. The Kokila or Indian cuckoo.<BR>	 3. A<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=257-a" target="_blank">Page257-a+ 50</a>]<BR>captive.<BR>	 5. A cryer, a herald.<BR> E. घोष sound, इत्नुच् affix, and य<BR>inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=256-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घोषवती
घोषवती f. (-ती) A lute, a Vina.<BR> E. घोष sound, and मतुप् poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=257-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घौर
घौर n. (-रं) Horror, horribleness.<BR> E. घोर and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=257-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घ्नत्|घ्नन्त्
घ्नत् mfn. (-घ्नत्-घ्नन्ती-घ्नत्) Striking, beating, hurting.<BR> E. हन् to strike,<BR>&c. शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=257-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घ्रति
घ्रति f. (-तिः) The nose.<BR> E. घ्रा to smell, डति aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=257-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घ्रा
घ्रा r. 1st cl. (जिघ्रति) To smell, to receive smell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=257-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घ्राण|घ्राणं|घ्राणः
घ्राण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Smelled.<BR>	 n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. The nose.<BR>	 2. Smell, odour.<BR>	 3.<BR>Smelling.<BR> E. घ्रा to smell, करणे ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=257-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घ्राणतर्पण|घ्राणतर्पणः
घ्राणतर्पण m. (-णः) Fragrance, odour, a fragrance, a perfume.<BR> E. घ्राण the<BR>smell, and तर्पण what satisfies.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=257-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घ्राणदुःखदा
घ्राणदुःखदा f. (-दा) Sneezing.<BR> E. घ्राण, and दुःखदा paining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=257-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घ्रात|घ्रातः
घ्रात mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Smelled.<BR> E. घ्रा to smell, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=257-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घ्रात्वा
घ्रात्वा ind. Having smelled.<BR> E. घ्रा to smell, क्त्वाच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=257-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घ्राति|घ्रातिः
घ्राति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. The nose.<BR>	 2. Smelling.<BR> E. घ्रा and करणे क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=257-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ङ|ङः
ङ The fifth consonant of the Sanskrit alphabet, and the nasal of the<BR>first class; the sound of this letter corresponds with that of the<BR>nasal N in Song, &c. or in the French word bon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=257-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ङ|ङः
ङ m. (-ङः)<BR>	 1. An object of sense.<BR>	 2. Desire, wish for any sensual object.<BR>E. ङु to sound, affix. ड । विषये विषयस्पृ हायां भैरवे च ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=257-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ङु
ङु (ङु) r. 1st cl. (ङवते) To sound. भ्वा-आत्म-अक-अनिट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=257-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

च|चः
च The twentieth letter of the alphabet, and first of the second or<BR>palatial class of consonants, having the sound of Ch in church.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=257-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

च|चः
च mfn. (चः-चा-चं)<BR>	 1. Seedless.<BR>	 2. Vile, base.<BR>	 m. (-चः)<BR>	 1. A name of<BR>SHIVA.<BR>	 2. The moon.<BR>	 3. A theif.<BR>	 4. A tortoise. Ind A particle and<BR>conjunction copulative or disjunctive. corresponding to.<BR>	 1. And.<BR>	 2.<BR>Also, 3. Moreover.<BR>	 4. Mutually.<BR>	 5. Equally.<BR>	 6. Otherwise.<BR>	 7. For,<BR>on account of.<BR>	 8. But. &c.<BR>	 9. An expletive.<BR> E. चर् to go, or चि to<BR>collect, &c. ड aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=257-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक
चक r. 1st cl. (चकते) To repel, to resist. To be satiated or satisfied.<BR>	 2.<BR>To shine. चक तृप्तौ प्रतिधाते च भ्वा-आ-अक-सेट् । भ्रान्तौ सौत्र-पर-अक-सेट्<BR>इदित् । चङ्कति ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=257-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चकास
चकास (ऋ) चकासृ r. 2nd cl. (चकास्ति) To shine. अदा जक्षा पर-अक-सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=257-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चकासयत्
चकासयत् mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्) Beautifying, illuminating.<BR> E. चकास to shine,<BR>causal form, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=257-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चकासित
चकासित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Illuminated, shining, splendid, beautiful. E.<BR>चकास, and क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=257-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चकित|चकितं
चकित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Timid, fearful.<BR>	 2. Frightened at, afraid of.<BR>	 n.<BR>(-तं) Timidity, groundless alarm.<BR>	 f. (-ता) A species of the Ashti<BR>metre.<BR> E. चक् to repel, affix भावे क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=257-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चकोर|चकोरः
चकोर m. (-रः) The bartavelle or Greek partridge, (Perdix rufa or Tetrao<BR>rufus.)<BR> E. चक् to be satisfied, ओरन् Uṇādi affix; also with कन् add-<BR>ed चकोरक; what is satisfied with the moonbeams, upon which the<BR>bird is fabulously said to subsist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=257-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चकोरक|चकोरकः
चकोरक m. (-कः) The Greek partridge: see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=257-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चकोरदृश्
चकोरदृश् mfn. (-दृक्) Fine-eyed.<BR> E. चकोर, and दृश् the eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=257-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्क
चक्क r. 10th cl. (चक्कयति) to give or inflict pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=257-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रस
चक्रस m. (-सः)<BR>	 1. Crookedness.<BR>	 2. Dishonesty,<BR> E. क्रस् to be crooked, अप्<BR>affix, and the root repeated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=257-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्र|चक्रं|चक्रः
चक्र m. (-क्रः)<BR>	 1. The ruddy or Brahmani goose, (Anas casarca.)<BR>	 n. (-क्रं)<BR>1. An army, a host.<BR>	 2. A realm, a region.<BR>	 3. A multitude, a heap<BR>4. A wheel.<BR>	 5. A potter's wheel.<BR>	 6. An oil mill, &c.<BR>	 7. A discus or<BR>sharp circular missile weapon.<BR>	 8. A whirlpool.<BR>	 9. A province, a<BR>number of villages, a district.<BR>	 10. A form of military array, a circular<BR>position.<BR>	 11. A diagram of various sorts for calculating nativities or<BR>foretelling events.<BR>	 12. A ring, circle or depression of the body for<BR>mystical, astrological or cheiromantic purposes; six such are enu-<BR>merated, or Muladhara the parts about the pubis, above that is<BR>the Swadhishthanam or umbilical region, and above that the<BR>Munipuram or pit of the stomach or epigastrium, Anahatam is the<BR>root of the nose, Visuddham the hollow between the frontal sin-<BR>uses, and the Ajnyakhyam the fontenelle or union of the coronal<BR>and sagittal sutures; various faculties and divinities are supposed<BR>to be present in these hollows.<BR>	 13. A cycle, a cycle of years.<BR>	 14.<BR>(In Astronomy,) A sphere or circle, as राशिचक्रं the zodiac; प्राक्चक्रं<BR>an epicycle.<BR>	 15. The horizon.<BR>	 16. The spiral marks of the Salagram<BR>or ammonite.<BR> E. कृ to do or make, with the reduplicate initial letter,<BR>affix क, or चक् to repel, &c. with रक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=257-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रक|चक्रकः
चक्रक m. (-कः) A logical form or proposition, arguing in a circle. E.<BR>कन् implying resemblance, added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=257-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रकारक|चक्रकारकं
चक्रकारक m. (-कः) A kind of perfume, apparently a dried shellfish: see<BR>नखी.<BR> E. चक्र a heap, and कारक what makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=257-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रकुल्या
चक्रकुल्या f. (-ल्या) A species of fern, commonly Chakuliya, (Hemionites<BR>cordifolia, Rox.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=257-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रगण्डु|चक्रगंडु|चक्रगण्डुः
चक्रगण्डु m. (-ण्डुः) A round pillow.<BR> E. चक्र, and गण्डु a pillow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=257-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रगुच्छ|चक्रगुच्छः
चक्रगुच्छ m. (-च्छः) A tree, (Jonesia asoca.)<BR> E. चक्र a wheel, and गुच्छ a<BR>cluster.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=257-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रजीवक|चक्रजीवकः
चक्रजीवक m. (-कः) A potter.<BR> E. चक्र a wheel, and जीवक who lives by;<BR>also चक्रजीविन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=257-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रदंष्ट्र|चक्रदंष्ट्रः
चक्रदंष्ट्र m. (-ष्ट्रः) A hog.<BR> E. चक्र and दंष्ट्र a tusk, having a curved tusk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=257-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रधर|चक्रधरः
चक्रधर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Having a wheel, &c.<BR>	 m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A village or<BR>common tumbler or juggler.<BR>	 2. One who holds a wheel, discus, &c.<BR>3. The manager or owner of many villages.<BR>	 4. A name of VIṢṆU<BR>or KṚṢṆA, who is represented as holding a discus in one hand.<BR>5. A snake.<BR> E. चक्र a wheel, &c. and धर who holds. धृ अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=257-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रनामन्
चक्रनामन् m. (-मा) A pyritic ore or iron: see माक्षिक.<BR> E. चक्र a wheel, &c.<BR>and नामन् appellation. चव्रवाके माक्षिकधातौ च ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=257-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रपद्माट|चक्रपद्माटः
चक्रपद्माट m. (-टः) Cassia tora: see चक्रमर्द्दक.<BR> E. चक्र a wheel, पद्म a lotus,<BR>and अट what goes or is अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=257-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रपर्णी|चक्रपर्ण्णी
चक्रपर्णी f. (-र्णी) A plant commonly Chakuliya, (Hemionites cordifolia,<BR>Rox.)<BR> E. चक्र a wheel, and पर्ण a leaf, the leaves being nearly round.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=257-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रपाणि|चक्रपाणिः
चक्रपाणि m. (-णिः) A name of VIṢṆU.<BR> E. चक्र and पाणि the hand, being<BR>always represented with a discus in one hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=257-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रपाद|चक्रपादः
चक्रपाद m. (-दः)<BR>	 1. A carriage, 2. An elephant.<BR> E. चक्र a wheel, and पाद<BR>a foot; also चक्रपादक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=257-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रपाल|चक्रपालः
चक्रपाल m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. Superintendent of a province.<BR>	 2. One who carries a<BR>discus.<BR>	 3. A circle.<BR>	 4. The horizon.<BR> E. चक्र and पाल who or what<BR>protects.<BR> E. पालि + अण् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=257-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रफल|चक्रफलं
चक्रफल n. (-लं) A missile weapon, a kind of discus.<BR> E. चक्र and फल<BR>fruit, bearing a discus as it were for fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=257-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रबान्धव|चक्रबांधव|चक्रबान्धवः
चक्रबान्धव m. (-वः) The sun.<BR> E. चक्र the ruddy goose, and बान्धव a friend;<BR>these birds being supposed to couple only in the day time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=257-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रभृत्
चक्रभृत् m. (-भृत्) A name of VIṢṆU.<BR> E. चक्र a discus, and भृत् who cher-<BR>ishes: see चक्रपाणि, &c. चक्रं विभर्त्ति भृ-क्विप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=257-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रभेदिनी
चक्रभेदिनी f. (-नी) Night.<BR> E. चक्र the ruddy goose, and भेदिनी what di-<BR>vides, (male and female;) these birds being condemned, according<BR>to the Hindus, to be separated at night. भिद-णिनि ङीप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=257-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रमण्डलिन्|चक्रमंडलिन्
चक्रमण्डलिन् m. (-ली) A large snake, (Boa constrictor.)<BR> E. चक्र a wheel,<BR>and मण्डल a circumference, implying either that the body of the<BR>snake, or the spots on the body may be compared to a wheel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=258-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रमर्द्द|चक्रमर्द|चक्रमर्द्दः
चक्रमर्द्द m. (-र्द्दः) Cassia tora.<BR> E. चक्र a wheel, here meaning figuratively<BR>a large leprous spot, and मर्द्द what cleanses or removes, from मृद्<BR>with अण् added; or with ण्वुल् affix चक्रमर्द्दक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=258-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रमर्द्दक|चक्रमर्दक|चक्रमर्द्दकः
चक्रमर्द्दक m. (-कः) See the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=258-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रमुख|चक्रमुखः
चक्रमुख m. (-खः) A hog.<BR> E. चक्र a discus, and मुख face; cutting the<BR>ground as it were with a sharp weapon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=258-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रयान|चक्रयानं
चक्रयान n. (-नं) Any wheel carriage.<BR> E. चक्र a wheel, and यान a carriage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=258-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्ररद|चक्ररदः
चक्ररद m. (-दः) A hog, a boar.<BR> E. चक्र and रद a tooth or tusk: see चक्रमुख.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=258-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रलक्षणा
चक्रलक्षणा f. (-णा) A plant, (Menispermum glabrum:) see गुडूची.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=258-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रला
चक्रला f. (-ला) A plant, (Kyllinga monocephala.)<BR> E. चक्र a wheel, and<BR>ल what gets. लाति ला-क । उच्चटायाम् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=258-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रवत्|चक्रवन्त्
चक्रवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>	 1. Circular, being in a ring or circle.<BR>	 2.<BR>Armed with a discus.<BR>	 3. Wheeled, &c.<BR>	 m. (-वान)<BR>	 1. The proprietor<BR>of an oil mill, or any one in which seeds are bruised.<BR>	 2. VIṢṆU.<BR>3. An emperor.<BR> E. चक्र a wheel. &c. मतुप् poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=258-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रवत्|चक्रवन्त्
चक्रवत् ind. In rotation, going round or revolving like a wheel.<BR> E. चक्र,<BR>and मतुप् aff. मस्य वः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=258-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रवर्त्तिन्|चक्रवर्तिन्
चक्रवर्त्तिन् m. (-त्तीं) An emperor, a sovereign of the world, the ruler of<BR>a Chakra or country described as extending from sea to sea;<BR>twelve princes beginning with Bharata are especially considered<BR>as Chakravartis.<BR> E. चक्र a reign, and वृत् to abide, affix णिच्<BR>वा णिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=258-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रवर्त्तिनी|चक्रवर्तिनी
चक्रवर्त्तिनी f. (-नी) A fragrant plant, commonly Chakawat.<BR> E. चक्र a heap,<BR>and वर्त्तिन् what abides or grows, fem. affix ङीप्,<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=258-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रवाक|चक्रवाकः
चक्रवाक m. (-कः) The ruddy goose. commonly called in India, the Brah-<BR>many duck or goose, (Anas casarca.)<BR> E. चक्र an imitative sound,<BR>and वाक speech. वच परिभाषणे कर्मणि घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=258-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रवाट|चक्रवाटः
चक्रवाट m. (-टः)<BR>	 1. Limit, boundary.<BR>	 2. A lamp stand.<BR>	 3. Engaging in<BR>any action.<BR> E. चक्र and वट् वेष्टने to surround, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=258-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रवाड|चक्रवाडं
चक्रवाड m. (-डः) See चक्रवाल. चक्रमिव वाडते वेष्टयति वाड-अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=258-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रवात|चक्रवातः
चक्रवात m. (-तः) A whirlwind, a hurricane.<BR> E. चक्र a circle, and वात wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=258-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रवाल|चक्रवालं|चक्रवालः
चक्रवाल m. (-लः) A range of mountains supposed to encircle the earth,<BR>and to be the limit of light and darkness.<BR>	 n. (-लं) The sensible<BR>horizon.<BR> E. चक्र a region, वल् to encompass, and अण् affix; girding<BR>the world; or वाड to emerge, &c. affix अच् what emerges (from<BR>darkness), in the shape of a wheel; ड changed to ल also चक्रवाड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=258-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रव्यूह|चक्रव्यूहः
चक्रव्यूह m. (-हः) The circular array of troops.<BR> E. चक्र and व्यूह array.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=258-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रवृद्धि|चक्रवृद्धिः
चक्रवृद्धि f. (-द्धिः) Compound interest.<BR> E. चक्र a wheel, वृद्धि increase.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=258-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रश्रेणी
चक्रश्रेणी f. (-णी) A plant bearing a crooked fruit: see अजशृङ्गी<BR> E. चक्र a<BR>wheel, and श्रेणी a line or row.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=258-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रसंज्ञ
चक्रसंज्ञ n. (-ज्ञं) Tin.<BR> E. चक्र and संज्ञा a name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=258-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रसंवर|चक्रसंवरः
चक्रसंवर m. (-रः) The name of a Bauddha deity; also हेरम्ब.<BR> E. चक्र a<BR>discus, and संवर who holds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=258-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रहस्त|चक्रहस्तः
चक्रहस्त m. (-स्तः) VIṢṆU.<BR> E. चक्र and हस्त hand: holding a discus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=258-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्राङ्की|चक्रांकी
चक्राङ्की f. (-ङ्की) A wild goose.<BR> E. चक्र a number, and अकि to go, affixes<BR>अच् and ङीष् flying in large flocks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=258-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्राङ्ग|चक्रांग|चक्राङ्गः
चक्राङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>	 1. A gander.<BR>	 2. A carriage.<BR>	 f. (-ङ्गी)<BR>	 1. A goose.<BR>	 2. A<BR>drug: see कटुकि.<BR>	 3. A potherb, (Hilancha repens:) see हिलमोचिका.<BR>E. चक्र a wheel, &c. and अङ्ग a limb or the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=258-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्राट|चक्राटः
चक्राट m. (-टः)<BR>	 1. A juggler, a snake-catcher, one who exhibits snakes<BR>and pretends to cure their bites.<BR>	 2. A knave, a cheat, a rogue.<BR>	 3.<BR>A gold coin or certain weight of gold, a Dinar.<BR> E. चक्र a number<BR>of villages, and अट who goes, i. e. a vagabond, &c. चक्राकारमटति अट-<BR>अण् उप-सः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=258-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्राण|चक्राणः
चक्राण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>	 1. Doing.<BR>	 2. Done.<BR> E. कृ to do, काणच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=258-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्राधिवासिन्
चक्राधिवासिन् m. (-सी) The orange tree.<BR> E. चक्र a heap, and अधिवस् to<BR>abide, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=258-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रावर्त्त|चक्रावर्त|चक्रावर्तः|चक्रावर्त्तः
चक्रावर्त्त m. (-र्त्तः) Turning round, whirling or rotatory motion.<BR> E. चक्र<BR>a wheel, and आवर्त्त revolving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=258-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रि|चक्रिः
चक्रि m. (-क्रिः) An agent, a maker, a doer.<BR> E. कृ to do, कि affix the<BR>root reduplicate and the deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=258-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रिका
चक्रिका f. (-का) The knee. चक्रं तदाकारोऽस्ति अस्य ठन् । जानुनि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=258-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रिन्
चक्रिन् mfn. (-क्री-क्रिणी-क्रि)<BR>	 1. Having or holding a discus, &c.<BR>	 2. Wheeled,<BR>having a wheel.<BR>	 3. Circular.<BR>	 m. (-क्री)<BR>	 1. A name of VIṢṆU.<BR>	 2. A<BR>potter.<BR>	 3. The ruddy goose.<BR>	 4. A snake.<BR>	 5. An informer.<BR>	 6. A tumb-<BR>ler, one who exhibits tricks with a discus or a wheel.<BR>	 7. An oil<BR>grinder.<BR>	 8. An emperor, a Chakravarti: see चक्रवर्त्तिन् 9. One who<BR>rides in a carriage.<BR>	 10. A crow.<BR>	 11. An ass.<BR>	 12. Cassia, (the tree.)<BR>E. चक्र a wheel, &c. and इनि poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=258-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रीवत्|चक्रीवन्त्
चक्रीवत् m. (-वान्)<BR>	 1. An ass.<BR>	 2. The name of a king.<BR> E. चक्र a wheel, वतु<BR>affix, and deriv. irr. rolling over like a wheel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=258-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रु|चक्रुः
चक्रु m. (-क्रुः) An agent, a maker, a doer.<BR> E. कृ to make or do, with the<BR>reduplicate initial, and कु Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=258-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रेश्वरी
चक्रेश्वरी f. (-री) A female deity peculiar to the Jainas, one of their<BR>Vidya Devis or goddesses of wisdom.<BR> E. चक्र the universe and ईश्वरी<BR>mistress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=258-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्ष
चक्ष (इङ्) चक्षिङ् r. 2nd cl. (चष्टे)<BR>	 1. To speak, to tell.<BR>	 2. To see; (in this<BR>sense आङ् is usually prefixed.)<BR>	 3. To eat. ख्या or कश are substitu-<BR>ted for the radical letters in several tenses of this verb. कथने त्यागे<BR>च अदा-आ-सक-सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=258-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्षण|चक्षणं
चक्षण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Eating a relish to promote drinking.<BR>	 2. Speaking,<BR>saying.<BR> E. चक्ष् to speak, to eat, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=258-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्षस्
चक्षस् m. (-क्षाः)<BR>	 1. A name of VṚHASPATI the preceptor of the gods.<BR>	 2.<BR>A spiritual teacher, an instructor in sacred science.<BR> E. चक्ष् to<BR>speak affix असि न ख्यादेशः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=258-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्षुःश्रवस्
चक्षुःश्रवस् m. (-वाः) A snake.<BR> E. चक्षुस् an eye, and श्रवस् an ear; whose<BR>eyes are ears. चक्षुषा शृणोति श्रु-असुन् चक्षुरेव श्रवः कर्णौ यस्य वा ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=258-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्षुर्दान
चक्षुर्दान n. (-नं) The ceremony of anointing the eyes of the image at<BR>the time of consecration.<BR> E. चक्षुस् and दान giving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=258-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्षुर्विषय|चक्षुर्विषयः
चक्षुर्विषय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. Presence, sight.<BR>	 2. An object of sight, any visible<BR>object.<BR>	 3. Visibility<BR> E. चक्षुस् and विषय object.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=258-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्षुष्मान्
चक्षुष्मान् mfn. (-ष्मान्-ष्मन्ती-ष्मत्)<BR>	 1. Having eyes, seeing.<BR>	 2. Having fine<BR>eyes.<BR> E. चक्षुस् and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=258-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्षुष्य|चक्षुष्यं|चक्षुष्यः
चक्षुष्य mfn. (-ष्यः-ष्या-ष्यं)<BR>	 1. Beautiful, pleasing or well looking.<BR>	 2. Fit<BR>or agreeable for the eyes.<BR>	 m. (-ष्यः)<BR>	 1. A flower, (Pandanus odora-<BR>tissimus.)<BR>	 2. A plant: see पुण्डरीक.<BR>	 3. collyrium or application to<BR>the eyes, extracted from the Amomum anthorhiza.<BR>	 f. (-ष्या)<BR>	 1. A<BR>blue stone, or according to some, the calx of brass used as coll-<BR>yrium.<BR>	 2. A pleasing or interesting woman.<BR> E. चक्षुस् the eye, affix<BR>यत् । चक्षुषे हितः यत् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=258-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्षुस्
चक्षुस् n. (-क्षुः) The eye.<BR> E. चक्ष् to speak, and करणे उसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=258-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्षूरोग|चक्षूरोगः
चक्षूरोग m. (-पः) Ophthalmia.<BR> E. चक्षुस् and रोग disease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=258-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चघ
चघ r. 5th cl. (चघ्नोति) To smite or slay. स्वा-सक-सेट् घातने ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=258-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चङ्कुर|चंकुर|चङ्कुरं|चंकुरः|चङ्कुरः
चङ्कुर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A car, a carriage.<BR>	 2. A tree.<BR>	 n. (-रं) Any vehicle. E.<BR>चकि a sautra root, to wonder, and उरच् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=258-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चङ्क्रमण|चंक्रमण|चंक्रमणं|चङ्क्रमणं
चङ्क्रमण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) who or what goes slowly or crookedly.<BR>	 n. (-णं)<BR>Going, proceeding, going tortuously or slowly.<BR> E. क्रम् to go,<BR>and the root reiterated. क्रम + यङ् ल्युट् यञोलुक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=258-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चङ्क्रमा|चंक्रमा
चङ्क्रमा f. (-मा) Going tortuously or slowly.<BR> E. क्रम् to go, root repeated,<BR>अङ् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=258-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चङ्क्रमावत्
चङ्क्रमावत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Who or what moves slowly or crookedly.<BR>E. चङ्क्रमा and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=258-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चङ्ग|चंग|चङ्गः
चङ्ग mfn. (-ङ्गः-ङ्गा-ङ्गं)<BR>	 1. Handsome, beautiful.<BR>	 2. Dexterous, clever.<BR>3. Sound, healthy.<BR> E. चं the moon, and ग what goes; what<BR>resembles the moon in beauty, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=258-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चचेण्डा
चचेण्डा f. (-ण्डा) A creeper, commonly Chichira.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=258-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चञ्च|चंच|चंचः|चञ्चः
चञ्च (उ) चञ्चु r. 1st cl. (चञ्चति) To go, to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=258-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चञ्चत्
चञ्चत् mfn. (-ञ्चन्-ञ्चन्ती-ञ्चत्)<BR>	 1. Going, moving.<BR>	 2. Unsteady, shaking. E.<BR>चञ्च् to go, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=259-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चञ्चत्क|चंचत्क
चञ्चत्क mfn. (-त्कः-त्का-त्कं) Trembling, moving.<BR> E. चञ्चत् the present parti-<BR>ciple of चञ्च् as above, affix कन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=259-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चञ्चरी|चंचरी
चञ्चरी f. (-री) A bee.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=259-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चञ्चरीक|चंचरीक|चंचरीकः|चञ्चरीकः
चञ्चरीक m. (-कः) A large black bee.<BR> E. चर् to go, reduplicated, नुम् in-<BR>serted, ईकन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=259-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चञ्चल|चंचल|चञ्चलं|चञ्चलः
चञ्चल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>	 1. Trembling, Shaking, moving, unsteady.<BR>	 2. Fickle,<BR>inconsiderate, inconstant, (unsteady, metaphorically.)<BR>	 m. (-लः)<BR>1. The wind.<BR>	 2. A lecher, a libertine, a lover.<BR>	 f. (-ला)<BR>	 1. Lightning.<BR>2. LAKṢMĪ or the goddess of the fortune.<BR>	 3. Long pepper.<BR> E. चल<BR>to go, in the reiterative form, नुम् inserted. चन्च अलच् । चञ्चं गतिं<BR>लाति ला क वा ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=259-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चञ्चलत्व
चञ्चलत्व n. (-त्व) Fickleness, inconstancy, unsteadiness.<BR> E. चञ्चल, and त्व<BR>affix; also with तल् affix चञ्चलता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=259-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चञ्चलहृदय
चञ्चलहृदय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Capricious, fickle, false hearted.<BR> E. चञ्चल, and<BR>हृदय the heart.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=259-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चञ्चा|चंचा
चञ्चा f. (-ञ्चा)<BR>	 1. A mat, a stool, &c. made of reeds or basket work.<BR>	 2. A<BR>puppet of grass or reeds, a man of straw.<BR> E. चञ्च् to go, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=259-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चञ्चु|चंचु|चञ्चुः
चञ्चु f. (-ञ्चुः) A beak; also चञ्चू.<BR>	 m. (-ञ्चुः)<BR>	 1. The castor oil plant.<BR>	 2. A<BR>kind of potherb.<BR>	 3. A deer.<BR> E. चञ्चु to go, to eat, affix उन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=259-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चञ्चुका|चंचुका
चञ्चुका f. (-का) A beak.<BR> E. कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=259-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चञ्चुभृत्|चंचुभृत्
चञ्चुभृत् m. (-भृत्) A bird.<BR> E. चञ्च a beak, and भृत् who possesses; also<BR>other similar compounds as चञ्चुमत्, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=259-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चञ्चुमत्|चंचुमत्|चञ्चुमन्त्
चञ्चुमत् mf. (-मान्-मती) A bird.<BR> E. चञ्चु a beak, and मतुप् poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=259-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चञ्चुर|चंचुर|चञ्चुरः
चञ्चुर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>	 1. Expert in, conversant with 2. Going to, repeat-<BR>edly.<BR> E. चर् to go, intensitive form, अच् aff. or चन्च उरच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=259-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चञ्चुसूचि|चंचुसूचि|चञ्चुसूचिः
चञ्चुसूचि m. (-चिः) The tailor bird, (Sylvia sutoria.)<BR> E. चञ्चु a beak, and<BR>सूचि a needle; having a sharp-pointed beak; also with कन् added,<BR>चञ्चुमूचिकम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=259-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चञ्चू|चंचू
चञ्चू f. (-ञ्चूः) A beak: see चञ्चु, the affix being ऊ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=259-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चञ्चूर्य्यमाण|चञ्चूर्यमाण
चञ्चूर्य्यमाण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Following evil practices, behaving ill, addict-<BR>ed to wickedness.<BR> E. चर् to go, intensitive form, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=259-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चट
चट r. 1st. and 10th cls. (चटति, चाटयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To break, to pierce.<BR>	 2. To<BR>kill, to injure. भ्वादि-पर-सक-सेट् । वधे भेदे च चुरा-उभ-सक-सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=259-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चटक|चटकः
चटक m. (-कः) A sparrow.<BR>	 f. (-का)<BR>	 1. A hen-sparrow.<BR>	 2. A young hen-<BR>sparrow.<BR>	 3. The root of long pepper: see चटकाशिरस् and चटिका.<BR>E. चट् to break, क्वुन् affix, braking corn, &c. चटति भिनत्ति धान्यादिकम् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=259-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चटकाशिरस्
चटकाशिरस् n. (-रः) The root of long pepper: see चटिकाशिरस्; also<BR>mas. चटकाशिरस् (-राः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=259-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चटिका
चटिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. The root of long pepper.<BR>	 2. A sparrow: see चटका,<BR>&c. चट-वा-इकन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=259-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चटिकाशिरस्
चटिकाशिरस् mn. (-राः-रः) The root of long pepper.<BR> E. चटका a sparrow,<BR>and शिरस् a head; resembling in colour the head of a sparrow; in<BR>other forms चटका, चटिकाशिरस् and चटकाशिरस्, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=259-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चटु|चटुः
चटु mn. (-टुः-टु)<BR>	 1. Scream, screech.<BR>	 2. Kind or agreeable discourse.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-टुः)<BR>	 1. The belly.<BR>	 2. A posture of devotion amongst ascetics. E.<BR>चट् to break, &c, Uṇādi affix उन्; also चाटु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=259-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चटुल|चटुलः
चटुल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>	 1. Tremulous, trembling.<BR>	 2. Shaking, moving.<BR>	 3.<BR>Beautiful.<BR>	 f. (-ला) Lightning.<BR> E. चट् to hurt, to break, and उलच्<BR>Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=259-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चटुलालस
चटुलालस mfn. (-सः-सा-सं) Pleased with or desirous of flattery.<BR> E. चटु,<BR>and लालस desirous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=259-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चटुलोल
चटुलोल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Tremulous and beautiful, beautiful as a soft<BR>swimming eye, &c.<BR> E. चटु beautiful, and लोल shaking, trembling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=259-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चड
चड (इ,) चडि r. 1st and 10th cls. (चण्डते and चण्डयति-ते) To be<BR>angry, to be wrathful or passionate. भ्वा-आ-अक-सेट् अथवा चुरा-उभ-<BR>अक-सेट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=259-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चण|चणः
चण r. 1st cl. (चणति)<BR>	 1. To give.<BR>	 2. To sound.<BR>	 3. To hurt or kill. भ्वा-पर-<BR>सक-सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=259-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चणक|चणकः
चणक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. Chick-pea, (Cicer arietinum.)<BR>	 2. The name of a sage.<BR>f. (-का) Linseed.<BR> E. चण् to be given, affix अच् and कन् added;<BR>what is given to horses, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=259-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चणकात्मज|चणकात्मजः
चणकात्मज m. (-जः) The name of a sage; also called VATSYAYANA. E.<BR>चणक, and आत्मज born; the son of CHĀNAKA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=259-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चणकाम्लक|चणकाम्लकं
चणकाम्लक n. (-कं) Pease with salt.<BR> E. चणक, and अम्ल acid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=259-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चणकाम्लवार्
चणकाम्लवार् n. (र्) Water drops on the leaves of the Cicer.<BR> E. चणकाम्ल,<BR>and वार् water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=259-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चण्ड|चंड|चण्डं|चण्डः
चण्ड mfn. (-ण्डः-ण्डा-ण्डं)<BR>	 1. Fierce, violent, passionate.<BR>	 2. Hot, warm.<BR>3. Pungent, acrid.<BR>	 m. (-ण्डः)<BR>	 1. The tamarind tree.<BR>	 2. A messenger<BR>of YAMA, 3. A Daitya, a demon.<BR>	 f. (-ण्डा)<BR>	 1. A perfume, commonly<BR>Chor.<BR>	 2. A kind of grass, (Andropogon aciculatum.)<BR>	 3. The name<BR>of a river in the east of Bengal.<BR>	 4. A goddess, peculiar to the<BR>Jainas.<BR>	 f. (-ण्डा-ण्डी) A name of the goddess DURGĀ, applied especial.<BR>ly to her incarnation for the purpose of destroying Mahisasura;<BR>this exploit forms the subject of a section of the Markandeya<BR>Puran, and is particularly celebrated in Bengal at the Durga Puja,<BR>or festival held in honour of the goddess, towards the close of the<BR>year, (Oct.-Nov.) (-ण्डी)<BR>	 1. A passionate woman.<BR>	 2. A mischievous<BR>or furious woman.<BR>	 3. A species of the Atijgati verse.<BR>	 n. (-ण्डं)<BR>	 1.<BR>Heat, warmth.<BR>	 2. Passion, wrath.<BR> E. चडि to be wrathful, अच् affix,<BR>and टा or ङीप् affixes of the feminine gender. चडि कोपे अच् चण दाने<BR>चमु अदने वा ड तस्य नेत्त्वम् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=259-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चण्डता
चण्डता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Warmth, pungency.<BR>	 2. Warmth of temper, passionate-<BR>ness.<BR> E. चण्ड angry, and तल् abstract affix; also with त्व, चण्डत्वम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=259-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चण्डनायिका
चण्डनायिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. The goddess DURGĀ.<BR>	 2. One of the eight Nayikas.<BR>E. चण्ड a demon, and नायिका mistress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=259-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चण्डरुद्रिका
चण्डरुद्रिका f. (-का) Knowledge of mystical nature, acquired by worship<BR>of the Nayikas.<BR> E. चण्ड, and रुद्र ŚIVA, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=259-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चण्डवत्|चंडवत्
चण्डवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Passionate, violent, warm.<BR>	 f. (-ती)<BR>	 1. A name<BR>or form of DURGĀ.<BR>	 2. One of her attendants.<BR> E. चण्ड anger, and<BR>मतुप् poss, aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=259-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चण्डात|चंडात|चंडातः|चण्डातः
चण्डात m. (तः) A fragrant plant, (Nerium odorum;) also प्रतीहास. E.<BR>चण्ड heat, and अत् to go or be, affix अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=259-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चण्डातक|चंडातक|चंडातकं|चण्डातकं|चंडातकः|चण्डातकः
चण्डातक mn. (-कः-कं) A short petticoat.<BR> E. चण्डा an angry woman, अत् to<BR>go, and ण्वुल् affix; it being described as the garb of women of some<BR>consequence, and therefore privileged to give themselves airs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=259-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चण्डाल|चंडाल|चण्डालः
चण्डाल m. (-लः) An outcaste, a Chandala, the generic name for a man<BR>of the lowest of the mixed tribes, born from a Śūdra father and<BR>Brahman mother.<BR> E. चण्ड angry, and अल able, or चण्ड् to be angry.<BR>and आलच् Uṇādi affix; proper to execute all vile or barbarous<BR>acts; also चाण्डाल<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=259-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चण्डालवल्लकी|चंडालवल्लकी
चण्डालवल्लकी f. (-की) A common or vulgar lute.<BR> E. चण्डाल an outcaste,<BR>and वल्लकी a lute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=259-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चण्डालिका|चंडालिका
चण्डालिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. A common lute.<BR>	 2. A name of the goddess DURGĀ.<BR>3. A plant.<BR> E. चण्डाल, and इकन् affix; or चण्ड a demon, &c. आली a<BR>line or troop, and कन् affix; hence also चण्डालिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=259-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चण्डांशु|चंडांशु|चण्डांशुः
चण्डांशु m. (-शुः) The sun.<BR> E. चण्ड hot, अंशु ray.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=259-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चण्डिका|चंडिका
चण्डिका f. (-का) The goddess DURGĀ.<BR> E. कण् added to चण्डी q. v. also<BR>चण्डा and चण्डी-चण्डी स्वार्थे क चडि कोपे ण्वुल् वा ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=259-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चण्डिल|चंडिल|चंडिलः|चण्डिलः
चण्डिल m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. A barber.<BR>	 2. A name of ŚIVA.<BR>	 3. A kind of potherb:<BR>see वास्तुक.<BR>	 f. (-ला) The name of a river.<BR> E. चडि to be wrathful, or<BR>to cause wrath, and इलच् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=259-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चण्डी|चंडी
चण्डी f. (-ण्डी) DURGĀ: see चण्ड. चण्ड-वह्वा-वा ङीष् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=259-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चण्डीकुसुम|चण्डीकुसुमः
चण्डीकुसुम m. (-मः) Red oleander.<BR> E. चण्डी, and कुसुम a flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=259-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चण्डु|चंडुः|चण्डुः
चण्डु m. (ण्डुः)<BR>	 1. A rat.<BR>	 2. A small monkey, (Simia erythrœa.)<BR> E. चडि<BR>to be passionate, उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=259-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चत
चत (ए) चते r. 1st cl. (चतति-ते) To ask, to beg, to solicit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=259-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चतुः|चतु
चतुः ind. Four times: see चतुर्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=259-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चतुःशाल|चतुःशालं
चतुःशाल nf. (-लं-ला) A square formed by four houses.<BR> E. चतुर् four, शाला<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=260-a" target="_blank">Page260-a+ 60</a>]<BR>a hall or house: the compound takes the neuter gender or the femi-<BR>nine, with टाप् affix; also with कन् added चतुःशालक चतसृणां शालानां<BR>समाहारः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=259-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चतुःषष्टि|चतुःषष्टिः
चतुःषष्टि f. (-ष्टिः)<BR>	 1. The number sixty-four.<BR>	 2. The Rig Veda.<BR>	 3. Art<BR>science collectively, supposed to comprise sixty-four branches. E.<BR>चतुर् four, and षष्टि sixty; before ष, र becomes Visarga. चतुरधिका<BR>षष्टिः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=260-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चतुर्
चतुर् mfn. plu. only, (चत्वारः चतस्रः चत्वारि) Four: in composition, and<BR>the last member of a compound, the numeral is inflected in all the<BR>numbers; thus प्रियचतुर् Who has four favorites, makes masc. and<BR>fem. (sing.) प्रियचत्वा (du.) त्वारौ (plu.) त्वारः and n. (sing.) प्रियचतुः (du.)<BR>चत्वारी (plu.) चत्वारि, &c. वहुवचनान्तः चत-उरन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=260-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चतुर|चतुरः
चतुर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>	 1. Dexterous, ingenious, clever.<BR>	 2. Visible, percepti-<BR>ble.<BR>	 m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A round pillow, one for the cheek.<BR>	 3. An elephant<BR>stable.<BR> E. चत् to ask, Uṇādi affix उरच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=260-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चतुरङ्ग|चतुरंग|चतुरङ्गं
चतुरङ्ग n. (-ङ्गं)<BR>	 1. An entire army, comprising elephants, cars, horse<BR>and foot.<BR>	 2. A sort of chess.<BR> E. चतुर्, and अङ्ग a member. चत्वारि<BR>अङ्गानि यस्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=260-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चतुरङ्गबल
चतुरङ्गबल n. (-लं) An entire army: see the last.<BR> E. चतुरङ्ग, and बल an<BR>army.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=260-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चतुरङ्गसैन्य
चतुरङ्गसैन्य n. (-न्यं) An entire army: see चतुरङ्ग.<BR> E. चतुरङ्ग, and सैन्य an army.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=260-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चतुरङ्गिन्
चतुरङ्गिन् mfn. (-ङ्गी-ङ्गिनी-ङ्गि) Having four parts or members.<BR>	 f. (-ङ्गिनी)<BR>An army.<BR> E. चतुरङ्ग and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=260-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चतुरङ्गुल|चतुरङ्गुलः
चतुरङ्गुल mfn. (-लः-ली-लं) Four fingers, (long, &c.)<BR>	 m. (-लः) A kind of<BR>Cassia. (Cassia fistula.)<BR> E. चतुर् four, and अङ्गुली a finger; the leaves<BR>being four fingers in length.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=260-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चतुरस्र|चतुरस्रः
चतुरस्र mfn. (-स्रः-स्रा-स्रं) Four cornered, quadrangular.<BR>	 n. (-स्रं) A square.<BR>E. चतुर् four, and अस्र a corner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=260-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चतुरानन|चतुराननः
चतुरानन m. (-नः) A name of BRAHMĀ.<BR> E. चतुर four, and आनन face;<BR>four-faced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=260-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चतुर्गति|चतुर्गतिः
चतुर्गति m. (-तिः) A tortoise.<BR> E. चतुर् four (feet), and गति motion; a<BR>quadruped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=260-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चतुर्गुण
चतुर्गुण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Four times, four-fold.<BR> E. चतुर्, and गुण multi-<BR>plication.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=260-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चतुर्थ|चतुर्थः
चतुर्थ mfn. (-र्थः-र्था or र्थी-र्थं) Fourth.<BR>	 f. (-र्थी) The fourth lunation. E.<BR>चतुर् four. डट् थुक् aff. चतुर्णी पूरणं डट् थुक् च ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=260-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चतुर्थकाल
चतुर्थकाल n. (-लं) The fourth season, implying especially the evening of<BR>every second day of a person's fasting,<BR> E. चतुर्थ, and काल time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=260-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चतुर्थफल
चतुर्थफल n. (-लं) (In astronomy,) The second inequality or equation of<BR>a planet.<BR> E. चतुर्थ, and फल quotient.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=260-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चतुर्थांश|चतुर्थांशः
चतुर्थांश m. (-शः) A quarter, a fourth part.<BR> E. चतुर्थ, and अंश part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=260-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चतुर्थिका
चतुर्थिका f. (-का) A Pala.<BR> E. कन् fem. form added to चतुर्थ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=260-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चतुर्दत्|चतुर्दन्त्
चतुर्दत् mfn. (-दन्-दती-दत्) Four-toothed.<BR> E. चतुर् four, दतृ substituted for<BR>दन्त a tooth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=260-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चतुर्दन्त|चतुर्दंत|चतुर्दन्तः|चतुर्द्दन्त|चतुर्द्दन्तः
चतुर्दन्त m. (-न्तः) INDRA'S elephant.<BR> E. चतुर् four, and दन्त a tooth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=260-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चतुर्दश|चतुर्द्दश
चतुर्दश min. (-शः-शी-शं) Fourteen.<BR>	 f. (-शी) The fourteenth lunation.<BR> E. चतु-<BR>र्दश, and टच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=260-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चतुर्दशन्|चतुर्द्दशन्
चतुर्दशन् mfn. plur. (-दश) Fourteen.<BR> E. चतुर् and दशन् ten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=260-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चतुर्दोल|चतुर्दोलः|चतुर्द्दोल|चतुर्द्दोलं
चतुर्दोल n. (-लं) A royal letter.<BR> E. चतुर् four, (supporters,) दोल a swing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=260-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चतुर्द्धा
चतुर्द्धा ind. Four times. four-fold.<BR> E. चतुर् and धा aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=260-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चतुर्भद्र|चतुर्भद्रं
चतुर्भद्र n. (-द्रं) The aggregate of four objects of human wishes, viz.<BR>virtue, love, wealth, and final beatitude.<BR> E. चतुर् four, and भद्र for-<BR>tunate, auspicious: see चतुर्वर्ग.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=260-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चतुर्भाग|चतुर्भागः
चतुर्भाग m. (-गः) Fourth part.<BR> E. चतुर् and भाग a share.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=260-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चतुर्भुज|चतुर्भुजः
चतुर्भुज m. (-जः)<BR>	 1. A name of VIṢṆU 2. An equilateral tetragon. E.<BR>चतुर् four, and भुज an arm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=260-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चतुर्मुख|चतुर्मुखः|चतुर्म्मुख|चतुर्म्मुखः
चतुर्मुख m. (-खः)<BR>	 1. The deity BRAHMĀ.<BR>	 2. A preparation of mercury.<BR>E. चतुर् and मुख a face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=260-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चतुर्युग|चतुर्युगं
चतुर्युग n. (-गं) The aggregate of the four Yugs or ages of the Hindus,<BR>a Mahayuga or 4,320,000 years.<BR> E. चतुर् four, and युग an age.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=260-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चतुर्वक्त्र|चतुर्वक्त्रः|चतुर्व्वक्त्रः
चतुर्वक्त्र m. (-क्तः) A name of BRAHMĀ.<BR> E. चतुर् four, and वक्त a face: see<BR>चतुर्मुख and other synonimous compounds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=260-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चतुर्वर्ग|चतुर्वर्गः|चतुर्व्वर्गः
चतुर्वर्ग m. (-र्गः)<BR>	 1. The four objects of human pursuit collectively see<BR>चतुर्भद्र.<BR>	 2. Any assemblage of four things.<BR> E. चतुर् four, and वर्ग class.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=260-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चतुर्वर्ण|चतुर्वर्णः
चतुर्वर्ण m. (-र्णः)<BR>	 1. The four classes of Hindus.<BR>	 2. Four principal colours.<BR>3. Four letters.<BR> E. चतुर्, and वर्ण tribe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=260-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चतुर्विद्य|चतुर्व्विद्यः
चतुर्विद्य m. (-द्यः) A priest who has studied the four Vedas.<BR> E. चतुर्<BR>four, विद्या knowledge: also चतुर्वेद, and with अण् added चातुर्वेद्य<BR>and चातुर्वेद.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=260-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चतुर्विध
चतुर्विध mfn. (-धः-धा-धं) Of four sorts or kinds, in four ways.<BR> E. चतुर्,<BR>and विध kind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=260-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चतुल|चतुलः
चतुल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Depositing, placing, fixing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=260-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चतुश्शाला
चतुश्शाला f. (-ला) A square of four houses, or a court enclosed by four<BR>buildings.<BR> E. चतुर्, and शाला a hall.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=260-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चतुष्क|चतुष्कं
चतुष्क mfn. (-ष्कः-ष्का-ष्कं) Four.<BR>	 f. (-ष्की)<BR>	 1. A large four-sided pond or<BR>tank.<BR>	 2. A bed or musquito curtain.<BR>	 3. A necklace of four strings.<BR>E. चतुर् four, कन् affix, and र is changed to ष. चतुरवयवं चत्वारोऽवयवा<BR>यस्य वा कन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=260-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चतुष्कोण|चतुष्कोणः
चतुष्कोण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Square, quadrangular.<BR>	 m. (-णः) A square, a<BR>tetragon.<BR> E. चतुर्. and कोण a corner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=260-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चतुष्टय|चतुष्टयं
चतुष्टय mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>	 1. Four.<BR>	 2. Four-fold.<BR>	 n. (-यं)<BR>	 1. A square.<BR>	 2. The<BR>centre of a circle.<BR>	 3. The aggregate of four.<BR> E. चतुर्, and तयप् aff.<BR>चत्वारोऽवयवा विधा अस्य तयप्र् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=260-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चतुष्पथ|चतुष्पथं|चतुष्पथः
चतुष्पथ m. (-थः) A Brahman.<BR>	 n. (-थं) A place where four roads meet. E.<BR>चतुर् four, and पथि a road, अच् aff. चत्वारः पन्थानः ब्रह्मचर्य्यादयः आश्रमा<BR>यस्य अच् समासः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=260-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चतुष्पद|चतुष्पदः
चतुष्पद nf. (-दं-दी) Verse, a metre of stanzas especially consisting of four<BR>Padas or lines.<BR>	 m. (-दः) An animal with four legs, a quadruped. E.<BR>चतुर् four, and पद for पाद a foot also read चतुष्पाद चत्वारि पदानि<BR>चरणा अस्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=260-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चतुष्पाटी
चतुष्पाटी f. (-टी) A river.<BR> E. चतुर् four (the four quarters), and पाटी what<BR>goes. चतस्रो दिशः पाटयति पाटि-अण् उप सः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=260-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चतुष्पाठी
चतुष्पाठी f. (-ठी) A school for Brahmans.<BR> E. चतुर् four, (the Vedas,) पाठ<BR>perusal. चतुर्णां चेदानां पाठोऽत्र गौरा-ङीष् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=260-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चतुष्पाणि|चतुष्पाणिः
चतुष्पाणि m. (-णिः) A name of VIṢṆU.<BR> E. चतुर् four, and पाणि a hand,<BR>four-handed. चत्वारः पाणयोऽस्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=260-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चतुष्पाद्
चतुष्पाद् mfn. (-पात्)<BR>	 1. A quadruped.<BR>	 2. A whole of four parts or quarters<BR>3. A judicial procedure, consisting of four processes, plea, defence,<BR>rejoinder, and sentence.<BR> E. चतुर् and पाद् a foot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=260-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चतुस्म
चतुस्म n. (-मं) An ungent of four ingredients, Sandal, agallochum,<BR>saffron, and musk.<BR> E. चतुर् four, and सम equal, same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=260-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चतुस्त्रिंशज्जातकज्ञ
चतुस्त्रिंशज्जातकज्ञ m. (-ज्ञः) A Bauddha, a Buddha saint.<BR> E. चतुस्त्रिंशत्<BR>thirty-four, जातक species, and ज्ञ who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=260-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चत्वर|चत्वरं
चत्वर n. (-रं)<BR>	 1. A levelled spot of ground prepared for a sacrifice.<BR>	 2.<BR>A courtyard.<BR> E. चत् to ask, Uṇādi affix ष्वरच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=260-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चत्वाल|चत्वालः
चत्वाल m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. A hole in the ground, &c. prepared for oblation with<BR>fire.<BR>	 2. The womb.<BR>	 3. Kusa grass.<BR> E. चत् to ask, वालच् affix, or<BR>with वालञ् affix, चात्वल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=260-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चद
चद r. 1st cl. (ए) चदे (चदति-ते) To ask or beg, to solicit. (इ) चदि (चंदति)<BR>1. To gladden.<BR>	 2. To shine. भ्वा-द्विक-उभ-सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=260-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चदिर|चदिरः
चदिर mf. (-रः-रा)<BR>	 1. An elephant.<BR>	 2. The moon.<BR>	 3. Camphor.<BR>	 4. A<BR>snake.<BR> E. चद् to shine, किरच् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=260-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन
चन r. 1st. and 10th cls. (चनति, चानयति) To hurt, to injure in any man-<BR>ner, to wound or kill, &c.<BR>	 2. To believe, to confide.<BR>	 3. To make<BR>a sound. भ्वा-पर सक-सेट् । चुरा-पर-सक-सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=260-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन
चन ind. A particle affixed to certain words, giving them an indefinite<BR>signification, as कदा when, कदाचन some, when, at sometime, कः<BR>who, कश्चन some one; see चित्<BR> E. कन् to sound, affix अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=260-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चनस्
चनस् n. (-नः) Food,<BR> E. च असुन् Uṇādi affix, and नुट् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=260-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन्द|चंद|चंदः|चन्दः
चन्द m. (-न्दः) The moon.<BR> E. चदि to shine, affix अच् see चन्द्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=260-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन्दक|चंदकः|चन्दकः
चन्दक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Pleasing, joy-inspiring.<BR>	 m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. The moon.<BR>2. Moonlight.<BR>	 3. A small silvery fish, of a genus allied to the<BR>Zeus, (Chanda, HAM)<BR> E. चन्द इव कायति कै क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=261-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन्दकपुष्प
चन्दकपुष्प n. (-ष्पं) Cloves.<BR> E. चन्दक, and पुष्प flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=261-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन्दन|चंदन|चंदनं|चन्दनं|चंदनः|चन्दनः
चन्दन mn. (-नः -नं) Sandal, (Sirium myrtifolium;) it implies either the<BR>tree, the wood, or the unctuous preparations of the wood, held in<BR>high estimation as perfumes.<BR>	 n. (-नं) Red Sandal wood: see रक्तच-<BR>न्दन.<BR>	 m. (-नः) A kind of ape.<BR>	 f. (-नी) The name of a river.<BR> E. चदि to<BR>gladden, to delight, affix णिच् ल्यु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=261-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन्दनाचल|चंदनाचल|चन्दनाचलः
चन्दनाचल m. (-लः) The Malaya mountain, part of the southern range<BR>of the Ghats, where Sandal wood is procured.<BR> E. चन्दन and अचल<BR>a hill, the Sandal hill; also similar names, as चन्दनाद्रि, चन्दन-<BR>पर्व्वत, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=261-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन्दिर|चंदिर|चंदिरः|चन्दिरः
चन्दिर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. An elephant.<BR>	 2. The moon.<BR> E. चदि to shine, &c. Uṇādi<BR>affix किरच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=261-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन्द्र|चंद्र|चन्द्रं|चन्द्रः
चन्द्र m. (-न्द्रः)<BR>	 1. The moon considered as a planet or a deity.<BR>	 2. Cam-<BR>phor.<BR>	 3. Water.<BR>	 4. Gold.<BR>	 5. A plant, (Crinum:) see रोचनी.<BR>	 6. (In<BR>composition) Pre-eminent, (as पुरुषचन्द्र an eminent man, a chief, a<BR>moon of men.)<BR>	 7. The edge in the peacock's tail.<BR>	 8. One of the<BR>eighteen minor Dwipas or divisions of the known continent.<BR>	 9.<BR>The mark of the soft aspirate.<BR>	 10. A pearl with a red tinge.<BR>	 11.<BR>Any thing giving pleasure.<BR>	 f. (-न्द्रा)<BR>	 1. An awning, a canopy.<BR>	 2.<BR>Small cardamoms: see एला.<BR> E. चदि to shine Uṇādi affix णिच् रक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=261-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन्द्रक|चंद्रक|चन्द्रकं|चंद्रकः|चन्द्रकः
चन्द्रक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. The moon.<BR>	 2. A ring, a circle, (like the moon.)<BR>	 3.<BR>The eye in a peacock's tail.<BR>	 4. A fingernail.<BR>	 5. A fish, (Chanda,<BR>HAM.)<BR>	 n. (-कं) Black pepper.<BR> E. चन्द्र the moon, and क affix of<BR>resemblance. चन्द इव कायति कै क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=261-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन्द्रकवत्|चंद्रकवत्|चन्द्रकवन्त्
चन्द्रकवत् m. (-वान्) A peacock.<BR> E. चन्द्रक the mark in his tail, मतुप्<BR>aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=261-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन्द्रकला|चंद्रकला
चन्द्रकला f. (-ला)<BR>	 1. A digit, or one-sixteenth of the moon's orb; each<BR>is personified as a female divinity, and worshipped in some Tan-<BR>trika ceremonies.<BR>	 2. A small drum.<BR>	 3. A fish commonly called<BR>Vacha or Bacha, (Pimelodus vacha, HAM.)<BR> E. चन्द्र the moon, and<BR>कला a digit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=261-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन्द्रकान्त|चंद्रकांत|चन्द्रकान्तं|चन्द्रकान्तः
चन्द्रकान्त m. (-न्तः) A fabulous gem, the moonstone, supposed to be<BR>formed of the congelation of the rays of the moon; a kind of<BR>crystal may perhaps be meant.<BR>	 mn. (-न्तः-न्तं)<BR>	 1. Sandal. 2, The<BR>white water lily.<BR>	 f. (-न्ता)<BR>	 1. Night.<BR>	 2. The wife of the moon.<BR> E. चन्द्र<BR>the moon, and कान्त splendid or beloved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=261-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन्द्रकिन्|चंद्रकिन्
चन्द्रकिन् m. (-की) A peacock.<BR> E. चन्द्रक the eye of the peacock's tail, and<BR>इनि poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=261-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन्द्रगुप्त|चन्द्रगुप्तः
चन्द्रगुप्त m. (-प्तः)<BR>	 1. The registrar of YAMA'S court.<BR>	 2. CHANDRAGUPTA<BR>a king of Pataliputra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=261-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन्द्रगोल|चंद्रगोल|चन्द्रगोलः
चन्द्रगोल n. (-लं) The orb or sphere of the moon.<BR> E. चन्द्र and गोल a ball.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=261-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन्द्रगोलस्थ
चन्द्रगोलस्थ m. (-स्थः) A deceased and defied progenitor.<BR> E. चन्द्रगोल and स्थ<BR>who stays or abides; an inhabitant of the lunar sphere.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=261-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन्द्रगोलिका|चंद्रगोलिका
चन्द्रगोलिका f. (-का) Moonlight.<BR> E. चन्द्रगोल the lunar orb, and कन् affix;<BR>derived from the moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=261-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन्द्रचञ्चल
चन्द्रचञ्चल mf. (-लः-ला) A small fish, (Chanda, HAM.)<BR> E. चन्द्र and चञ्चल<BR>trembling, quivering, and glistering like the moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=261-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन्द्रदार|चंद्रदार
चन्द्रदार plu.<BR>	 m. (-राः) The twenty-seven lunar mansions, which in<BR>mythology, are so many nymphs, daughters of DAKṢA, and wed-<BR>ded to CHANDRA, or the moon.<BR> E. चन्द्र and दार a wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=261-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन्द्रनिभ
चन्द्रनिभ mfn. (-भः-भा-भं) Like the moon, bright, handsome.<BR> E. चन्द्र and<BR>निभ what resembles.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=261-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन्द्रभागा|चंद्रभागा
चन्द्रभागा f. (-गा-गी) The name of a river, the Chennab, one of the five<BR>streams of the Punjab.<BR> E. चन्द्रभाग the name of a mountain, part<BR>of the Himālaya range, where the river is said to have its source,<BR>affix of derivation अण् hence also it may be read चान्द्रभागा-गी ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=261-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन्द्रप्रभ|चन्द्रप्रभः
चन्द्रप्रभ m. (-भः) The eight Jina or Jaina pontiff.<BR>	 f. (-भा)<BR>	 1. Moonlight.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=261-b" target="_blank">Page261-b+ 60</a>]<BR>2. A compound of various drugs used in jaundice, piles, &c. E.<BR>चन्द्र and प्रभा light. चन्द्रस्य प्रभा इव प्रभा अस्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=261-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन्द्रमणि|चंद्रमणि|चन्द्रमणिः
चन्द्रमणि m. (-णिः) The Chandrakanta or moon-gem: see चन्द्रकान्त. E.<BR>चन्द्र the moon, and मणि a gem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=261-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन्द्रमण्डल|चन्द्रमण्डलं
चन्द्रमण्डल n. (-लं) The orb or disc of the moon, the lunar sphere.<BR> E. चन्द्र<BR>and मण्डल circle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=261-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन्द्रमस्|चंद्रमस्
चन्द्रमस् m. (-माः) The moon.<BR> E. चन्द्र camphor, मा to mete or measure,<BR>and असुन् Uṇādi affix, मा देशः rendering all objects white like<BR>camphor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=261-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन्द्रमौलि|चंद्रमौलि|चन्द्रमौलिः
चन्द्रमौलि m. (-लिः) A name of ŚIVA.<BR> E. चन्द्र and मौलि a crest; this deity<BR>being represented with a half moon on his fore-head.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=261-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन्द्ररेखा|चंद्ररेखा
चन्द्ररेखा f. (-खा) A digit of the moon.<BR> E. चन्द्र and रेखा a line.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=261-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन्द्ररेणु|चंद्ररेणु|चन्द्ररेणुः
चन्द्ररेणु m. (-णुः) A plagiarist, a poetical thief, (काव्यचौर)<BR> E. चन्द्र the<BR>moon, and रेणु dust.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=261-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन्द्रलेखा|चंद्रलेखा
चन्द्रलेखा f. (-खा)<BR>	 1. A plant, (Serrantula anthelmintica:) see सोमराजी.<BR>2. A digit of the moon.<BR> E. चन्द्र and लेखा a line or mark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=261-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन्द्रलोक|चंद्रलोक|चन्द्रलोकः
चन्द्रलोक n. (-कं) The sphere or heaven of the moon.<BR> E. चन्द्र and लोक<BR>world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=261-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन्द्रलौह|चंद्रलौह
चन्द्रलौह n. (-हं) Silver.<BR> E. चन्द्र and लौह metal; also चन्द्रलौहकं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=261-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन्द्रवंश|चंद्रवंश|चन्द्रवंशः
चन्द्रवंश m. (-शः) The race of the moon. the second great branch of the<BR>Kṣatriya or royal dynasties, derived from the moon, through<BR>BUDDHA his son, and Pururavas his son.<BR> E. चन्द्र and वंश race.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=261-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन्द्रवंशिन्
चन्द्रवंशिन् m. (-शी) A member of the lunar dynasty.<BR> E. चन्द्रवंश and इनि<BR>aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=261-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन्द्रवल्लरी
चन्द्रवल्लरी f. (-री)<BR>	 1. A kind of asclepias, (A. acida:) see सोमलता.<BR>	 2. Rue.<BR>See ब्राह्मी.<BR> E. चन्द्र the moon, and वल्लरी a creeper. सोमलतायां माधवी-<BR>लतायाम् च ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=261-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन्द्रवाला
चन्द्रवाला f. (-ला) Large cardamoms.<BR> E. चन्द्र camphor, and वाला a child, a<BR>diminutive term in general.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=261-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन्द्रविहङ्गम|चन्द्रविहंगम|चन्द्रविहंगमः|चन्द्रविहङ्गमः
चन्द्रविहङ्गम m. (-मः) A kind of crane.<BR> E. चन्द्र the moon, (as white,) and<BR>विहङ्गम a bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=261-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन्द्रव्रत|चंद्रव्रत|चन्द्रव्रतं
चन्द्रव्रत n. (-तं)<BR>	 1. A regal property or virtue.<BR>	 2. A kind of penance.<BR>see चान्द्रायण.<BR> E. चन्द्र the moon, and व्रत religious observance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=261-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन्द्रशाला|चंद्रशाला
चन्द्रशाला f. (-ला)<BR>	 1. Moonlight.<BR>	 2. An upper room, an apartment on<BR>the top of the house.<BR> E. चन्द्र the moon, and शाला a hall. चन्द्रः शाला<BR>इव आधारो यस्याः । ज्योत्स्नायाम्, प्रासादोपरिस्थे गृहे (चिलेर घर) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=261-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन्द्रशालिका|चंद्रशालिका
चन्द्रशालिका f. (-का) A room on the top of a house.<BR> E. कन् affixed to<BR>the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=261-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन्द्रशेखर|चंद्रशेखर|चन्द्रशेखरः
चन्द्रशेखर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A name of ŚIVA.<BR>	 2. The name of a mountain; one<BR>so called is amongst the hills of Aracan.<BR> E. चन्द्र the moon, and<BR>शेखर a crest; whose crest is the moon. चन्द्रः चन्द्रकला शेखरे अस्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=261-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन्द्रसंज्ञ
चन्द्रसंज्ञ m. (-ज्ञः) Camphor.<BR> E. चन्द्र and संज्ञा a name: having all the<BR>synonyms of the moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=261-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन्द्रसम्भव|चन्द्रसंभव|चन्द्रसंभवः
चन्द्रसम्भव m. (-वः) Budha, the planet MERCURY.<BR> E. चन्द्र and आत्मज son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=261-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्द्रसम्भवा
सन्द्रसम्भवा f. (-वा) Small cardamoms.<BR> E. चन्द्र the moon, and सम्भव<BR>produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=261-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन्द्रसालोक्य|चंद्रसालोक्य
चन्द्रसालोक्य n. (-क्यं) Attainment of the lunar heaven.<BR> E. चन्द्र and सालोक्य<BR>domicile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=261-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन्द्रहास|चंद्रहास|चन्द्रहासं|चन्द्रहासः
चन्द्रहास m. (-सः)<BR>	 1. A scimitar.<BR>	 2. the sword of RAVANA.<BR>	 f. (-सा) Moon<BR>plant, (Menispermum glabrum.)<BR>	 n. (-सं) Silver.<BR> E. चन्द्र the moon,<BR>and हास what derides: outvieing the moon in brightness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=261-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन्द्राकृति
चन्द्राकृति mfn. (-तिः-तिः-ति) Moon-shaped, like the moon, (in roundness,<BR>whiteness, &c.)<BR> E. चन्द्र and आकृति form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=261-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन्द्रातप|चंद्रातप|चन्द्रातपः
चन्द्रातप m. (-पः)<BR>	 1. Moonlight 2. An awning.<BR> E. चन्द्र the moon, and<BR>आतप shining. चन्द्रस्य आतो गमनं ततः पाति-पा-क । चांँदोया ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=261-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन्द्रार्द्ध
चन्द्रार्द्ध n. (-र्द्धं) A half moon, a crescent.<BR> E. चन्द्र and अर्द्ध half.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=261-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन्द्रापीड|चंद्रापीड|चन्द्रापीडः
चन्द्रापीड m. (-डः) A name of ŚIVA.<BR> E. चन्द्र the moon, and आपीड a<BR>chaplet; who has the moon like a chaplet amidst his hair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=261-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन्द्राभास|चंद्राभास|चन्द्राभासः
चन्द्राभास m. (-सः) A false moon, an appearance like the moon.<BR> E. चन्द्र,<BR>and आभास resembling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=261-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन्द्रिका|चंद्रिका
चन्द्रिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. Moonlight.<BR>	 2. A small fish, commonly Chanda,<BR>(Chanda of var. species, HAM.)<BR>	 3. Large cardamoms.<BR> E. चन्द्र the<BR>moon, चन्द्रोऽस्ति अस्याः आश्रयत्वेन ठन् । चदि दीप्तौ रक् ततः स्वार्थे कवा ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=262-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन्द्रिकाद्राव|चंद्रिकाद्राव|चन्द्रिकाद्रावः
चन्द्रिकाद्राव m. (-वः) The moonstone.<BR> E. चन्द्रिका and द्राव what fuses;<BR>liquefying in moonlight. चन्दिकया द्रावो निष्यन्दो यस्य । चन्द्रकान्तमणौ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=262-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन्द्रिकापायिन्|चंद्रिकापायिन्
चन्द्रिकापायिन् m. (-यी) The Chakora or hill partridge.<BR> E. चन्द्रिका and<BR>पायिन् who drinks. चन्द्रिकां पिबति पा-णिनि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=262-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन्द्रिकाम्बुज|चंद्रिकांबुज|चन्द्रिकाम्बुजं
चन्द्रिकाम्बुज n. (-जं) The white lotus.<BR> E. चन्द्रिका and अम्बुज a lotus.<BR>चन्द्रिकेव शुम्रमम्बुजम् । सितोत्पले ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=262-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन्द्रिल|चंद्रिल|चंद्रिलः|चन्द्रिलः
चन्द्रिल m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. A name of ŚIVA.<BR>	 2. A barber.<BR>	 3. A potherb, (Cheno-<BR>podium album.)<BR> E. चन्द्र the moon or weapon, &c. bright as the<BR>moon, and इलच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=262-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन्द्रोदय|चंद्रोदय|चन्द्रोदयः
चन्द्रोदय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. An awning, a cloth spread over the large open<BR>courtyard of Hindu houses, upon festival occasions.<BR>	 2. Moon-rise<BR>3. A mercurial preparation used in medicine.<BR> E. चन्द्र the moon, and<BR>उदय rising, (of a planet, &c.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=262-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन्द्रोपल|चंद्रोपल|चन्द्रोपलः
चन्द्रोपल m. (-लः) Moongem; see चन्द्रकान्त.<BR> E. चन्द्र, the moon, and उपल a<BR>stone. चन्द्रप्रियः उपलः । चन्द्रकान्तमणौ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=262-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चप
चप r. 1st cl. (चपति) To caress, to coax, to soothe or console, r. 10th.<BR>cl. (चपयति-ते) To grind or pound. (इ) चपि r. 1st and 10th cls.<BR>(चम्पति, चम्पयति) To go, to move. भ्वा-पर-सक-सेट् चुरा-उभ-सक-सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=262-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चपट|चपटः
चपट m. (-टः) The palm with extended fingers: see चपेट.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=262-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चपल|चपलं|चपलः
चपल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>	 1. Trembling, tremulous, shaking.<BR>	 2. Wavering,<BR>unsteady.<BR>	 3. Inconsiderately criminal.<BR>	 4. Swift, expeditious;<BR>(also in this sense, or swiftly, adv.<BR>	 n. (-लं)<BR>	 5. Momentary,<BR>instantaneous.<BR>	 6. Agitated violently, overcome with alarm, &c.<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. Quicksilver.<BR>	 2. A kind of stone.<BR>	 3. A fish.<BR>	 4. A<BR>thief.<BR>	 f. (-ला)<BR>	 1. The goddess LAKṢMĪ or fortune.<BR>	 2. Light-<BR>ning.<BR>	 3. A whore.<BR>	 4. Long pepper.<BR>	 5. The tongue.<BR>	 6. Spirituous<BR>liquor.<BR>	 7. A species of the Āryā metre.<BR> E. चप् to go, affix अलच्<BR>or चुप् to move, Uṇādi affix कल and the radical vowel changed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=262-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चपलता
चपलता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Moving, trembling.<BR>	 2. Fickleness, inconstancy<BR> E. तल्<BR>added to the last, also with त्व, चपलत्वम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=262-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चपलात्मक
चपलात्मक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Of a fickle or inconstant nature<BR> E. चपल, आत्म<BR>self, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=262-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चपेट|चपेटः
चपेट m. (-टः) The palm of the hand with the fingers extended.<BR> E. चप्<BR>to go, affix अच्, चप trembling, and इट what goes or is, from इट्<BR>with क affix; also चपट and चर्पट.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=262-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चपेटाघात
चपेटाघात m. (-तः) A slap with the open hand.<BR> E. चपेट, and आघात a<BR>blow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=262-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चपेटिका
चपेटिका f. (-का) A slap with the open hand.<BR> E. चपेट, and वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=262-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चम|चमः
चम (उ) चमु r. 1st and 5th cls. (चमति, चम्नोति) To eat, to drink, to take<BR>any thing into the mouth, as food, whether solid or liquid. With<BR>आङ् prefixed, (आचामति) To sip as water. With वि, (विचमति) To eat.<BR>भ्वा-प-सक-सेट् स्वादि वा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=262-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चमत्करण|चमत्करणं
चमत्करण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Astonishing, producing wonder or surprise.<BR>	 2. Fes-<BR>tival.<BR>	 3. spectacle.<BR>	 4. High poetical composition.<BR> E. चमत् a sound<BR>of surprise, and करण making; also चमत्कार and चमत्कृति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=262-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चमत्कार|चमत्कारः
चमत्कार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Astonishment, surprise.<BR>	 2. Show, spectacle.<BR>	 3. Row,<BR>riot, festive or angry turbulence.<BR>	 4. Elaborate style or high poeti-<BR>cal composition.<BR>	 5. The name of a tree: see अपामार्ग<BR> E. चमत् a sound<BR>of surprise, and कार making. चमदित्यव्यक्तं क्रियते कृभावे घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=262-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चमत्कारिन्
चमत्कारिन् mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि) Unusual, surprising, astonishing. E.<BR>चमत्कार, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=262-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चमत्कृत
चमत्कृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Surprised, astonished.<BR> E. चमत्, and कृत made.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=262-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चमत्कृति|चमत्कृतिः
चमत्कृति f. (-तिः) Display, spectacle, &c.: see चमत्करण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=262-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चमर|चमरं|चमरः
चमर n. (-रं)<BR>	 1. A Chowri or long brush, most usually made of the<BR>tail-hairs of the Yak or Bos Grunniens, and employed to whisk off<BR>insects, flies, &c.<BR>	 2. The name of a demon, f. (-री) A compound<BR>pedicle.<BR>	 mf. (-रः-री) A kind of deer, or rather the Bos Grunniens,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=262-b" target="_blank">Page262-b+ 60</a>]<BR>erroneously classed by the Hidu writers amongst the deer.<BR> E. चम्<BR>to eat or be eaten, अरच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=262-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चमरपुच्छ|चमरपुच्छः
चमरपुच्छ m. (-च्छः) A small animal with a bushy tail; a squirrel.<BR>	 n.<BR>(-च्छं) A Chowri.<BR> E. चमर, and पुच्छ tail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=262-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चमरिक|चमरिकः
चमरिक m. (-कः) A species. of ebony, (Bauhinia variegata.)<BR> E. चमर a<BR>Chowri, and ठन् affix, growing in clusters, resembling a Chowri.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=262-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चमस|चमसं|चमसः
चमस mf. (-सः-सी) 1A vessel used at sacrifices for drinking the juice of<BR>the acid asclepias, a kind of ladle or spoon. 2, A cake made of<BR>barley, rice or lentils ground to meal.<BR>	 3. A plant, commonly<BR>Khetpapra, (Mollugo pentaphylla.)<BR>	 4. A sweetmeat, or flour,<BR>sesamum, &c. mixed up with sugar into a kind of cake, &c. E.<BR>चम् to eat, असच् Uṇādi affix, fem. affix ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=262-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चमू
चमू f. (-मूः)<BR>	 1. An army.<BR>	 2. A squadron, a division of an army con-<BR>sisting of 129 elephants, as many cars, 2187 horse, and 3685<BR>foot.<BR> E. चम् to eat or destroy, (the enemy.) and ऊ Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=262-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चमूचर|चमूचरः
चमूचर m. (-रः) A soldier, a warrior.<BR> E. चमू, and चर who marches.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=262-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चमूपति|चमूपतिः
चमूपति m. (-तिः) A general of division, any general.<BR> E. चमू, and पति<BR>master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=262-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चमूरु|चमूरुः
चमूरु m. (-रुः) A kind of deer.<BR> E. चम् to be eaten, ऊरच् affix, and उ<BR>final added. पृषोदरादित्वात् अत उत्त्वम् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=262-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चम्प|चंपः|चम्पः
चम्प r. 1st cl. (चम्पति) To go or move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=262-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चम्प|चंपः|चम्पः
चम्प m. (-म्प्रः) Mountain ebony, (Bauhinia variegata.)<BR>	 f. (-म्पा) The<BR>capital of KARṆA, the modern Bhagalpur, or a place in its vicini-<BR>ty.<BR> E. चपि to go &c. अच् and टाप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=262-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चम्पक|चंपक|चम्पकं|चंपकः|चम्पकः
चम्पक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A tree bearing a yellow fragrant flower, (Michelia<BR>champaca.)<BR>	 2. A division of the jack fruit.<BR>	 n. (-कं) The flower of<BR>the Champa.<BR>	 2. A variety of the banana or plantain, (the fruit.)<BR>E. चपि to shine, &c. affix ण्वुल्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=262-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चम्पकालु|चंपकालु|चंपकालुः|चम्पकालुः
चम्पकालु m. (-लुः) The Jack or Indian bread fruit tree, (Artocarpus in-<BR>tegrifolia.)<BR> E. चम्पक as above, and आलच् poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=262-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चम्पकोष|चम्पकोषः
चम्पकोष m. (-षः) The Jack: see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=262-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चम्पाधिप|चम्पाधिपः
चम्पाधिप m. (-पः) A name of KARṆA.<BR> E. चम्पा the city, and अधिप ruler.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=262-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चम्पापुरी
चम्पापुरी f. (-री) The city Champa: see चम्पा.<BR> E. चम्पा and पुर a city.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=262-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चम्पालु|चंपालु|चंपालुः|चम्पालुः
चम्पालु f. (-लुः) The Jack: see चम्पकालु.<BR> E. चम्प for चम्पक, and आलुच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=262-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चम्पावतो
चम्पावतो f. (-ती) The district of Champa: or Bhagulpur.<BR> E. चम्प the<BR>ebony tree, and मतुप् poss. affix, abounding in such trees.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=262-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चम्पू|चंपू
चम्पू f. (-म्पूः) A work in which the same subject is continued through<BR>alternations in the composition of prose and verse.<BR> E. चम् to eat<BR>or be eaten, ऊ affix प inserted; what is relished by persons of<BR>taste.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=262-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चम्पेश|चम्पेशः
चम्पेश m. (-शः) KARṆA the natural brother of the Pāṇḍus.<BR> E. चम्पा the<BR>city Champa, and ईश sovereign.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=262-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चम्पोपलक्षित|चम्पोपलक्षितः
चम्पोपलक्षित m. (-तः) The district of champa or Bhāgulpnr, or m. plu.<BR>(-ताः) The inhabitants.<BR> E. चम्प the ebony, and उपलक्षित designated:<BR>see चम्पावती.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=262-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चम्ब
चम्ब r. 1st cl. (चम्बति) To go, to move. भ्वा-पर-सक-सेट् गतौ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=262-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चय|चयः
चय r. 1st cl. (चयते) To go to or towards, to go, to move, भ्वा-आ-सक-सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=262-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चय|चयः
चय m. (यः)<BR>	 1. An assemblage, a multitude.<BR>	 2. A heap, a collection.<BR>	 3.<BR>A mound of earth, raised to form the foundation of a building.<BR>4. A rampart or mound of earth raised from the ditch of a fort.<BR>5. The gate of a fort.<BR>	 6. Any edifice.<BR>	 7. A seat, a stool.<BR>	 8. A<BR>cover, a covering.<BR> E. चि to collect, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=262-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चयन|चयनं
चयन n. (-नं) Collecting, gathering.<BR> E. चि to collect, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=262-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चयनीय
चयनीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) To be collected or gathered.<BR> E. चि to collect,<BR>अनीयर aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=262-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर|चरः
चर r. 1st cl. (चरति)<BR>	 1. To go.<BR>	 2. To eat.<BR>	 3. To behave or act, (in this<BR>sense आङ् is usually prefixed;) With अति, and आङ् prefixed, To<BR>transgress, to go astray. With अभि, 1. To deceive, to betray.<BR>	 2.<BR>To conjure.<BR>	 3. To attend. With अनु, 1. To follow, to attend.<BR>	 2. To<BR>imitate. With आङ् To practise. a duty. With उत्, (उच्चरते) 1. To<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=263-a" target="_blank">Page263-a+ 60</a>]<BR>transgress.<BR>	 2. To expel.<BR>	 3. (उच्चरति) To go up, to rise. With उप, 1.<BR>To approach.<BR>	 2. To worship. With परि, To serve. With प्र, 1. To<BR>prevail as a custom.<BR>	 2. To declare, to manifest. With वि and अभि,<BR>To go astray, to act wickedly. With सम् (सञ्चरते) 1. To ride upon.<BR>2. (सञ्चरति) To accompany. With सम् and आङ् 1. To perform.<BR>	 2.<BR>To announce. r. 10th cl. (चारयति)<BR>	 1. To doubt 2. To be free from<BR>doubt. With वि prefixed, To discuss, to dispute, to reason upon or<BR>respecting any doubtful points. भ्वा-पर-सक-सेट् । चु-उभ-सक-सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=262-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर|चरः
चर mfn. (-रः-रा or -री-रं)<BR>	 1. Moveable, locomotive.<BR>	 2. Trembling, shak-<BR>ing, unsteady.<BR>	 m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A spy, a secret emissary or agent.<BR>	 2. The<BR>planet Mars.<BR>	 3. A game played with dice and men, similar to<BR>backgammon.<BR>	 4. A wagtail.<BR>	 5. A cowri.<BR>	 6. The seventh Karana,<BR>(in Astrology.)<BR>	 7. The Karanas collectively.<BR>	 f. (-री) A young wo-<BR>man.<BR> E. चर् to go, affix अच् or टच् and in the latter case the fem.<BR>affix is ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=263-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चरक|चरकः
चरक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. The author of a treatise upon medicine: applied<BR>also to the work.<BR>	 2. A spy or secret emissary, &c.<BR> E. चर to go,<BR>Uṇādi affix. स्वार्थे क संज्ञायां कन् वा ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=263-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चरट|चरटः
चरट mf. (-टः-टी) A wagtail; also चर.<BR> E. चर वा अटच् । खञ्जनखगे ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=263-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चरण|चरणं|चरणः
चरण mn. (-णः-णं)<BR>	 1. A foot.<BR>	 2. The root of a tree. A race, a family.<BR>	 4.<BR>A portion of the Vedas, 5. Fixed or instituted observance.<BR>	 6.<BR>The peculiarity of condition or conduct implied by the English<BR>affix hood, as manhood, priesthood, &c.<BR>	 7. The fourth part of a<BR>stanza.<BR>	 4. (in Prosody,) A dactyl.<BR>	 n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Wandering, roaming,<BR>going round or about.<BR>	 2. Eating. E. to चर् go affix करणे ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=263-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चरणकिशलय
चरणकिशलय n. (-यं) The foot of a lover, or deity, &c.<BR> E. चरण and किशलय<BR>lotus filament.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=263-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चरणगत
चरणगत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Fallen at one's feet, prostrate.<BR> E. चरण and गत<BR>gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=263-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चरणग्रन्थि|चरणग्रंथि|चरणग्रन्थिः
चरणग्रन्थि f. (-न्थिः) The ankle.<BR> E. चरण the foot, and ग्रन्थि a joint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=263-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चरणपतन
चरणपतन n. (-नं) Prostration, falling at the feet.<BR> E. चरण and पतन falling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=263-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चरणपतित
चरणपतित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Prostrate, fallen at the feet.<BR> E. चरण and पतित<BR>fallen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=263-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चरणपात|चरणपातः
चरणपात m. (-तः) Tread, trampling, foot-fall.<BR> E. चरण and पात falling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=263-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चरणयुग
चरणयुग n. (-गं)<BR>	 1. Both the feet.<BR>	 2. Two lines of a stanza.<BR> E. चरण, and<BR>युग a pair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=263-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चरणसेवा
चरणसेवा f. (-वा) Service, devotion.<BR> E. चरण and सेवा service.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=263-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चरणार्द्ध
चरणार्द्ध n. (-र्द्धं)<BR>	 1. The half of the foot.<BR>	 2. Half of the fourth of a stanza<BR>E. चरण and अर्द्ध half.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=263-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चरणानमित
चरणानमित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Trodden down, bent or bowed under the<BR>feet.<BR> E. चरण and आनमित bowed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=263-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चरणाभरण
चरणाभरण n. (-णं) An ornament on the feet.<BR> E. चरण and आभरण orna-<BR>ment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=263-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चरणामृत
चरणामृत n. (-तं) The water in which the feet of a venerable Brahman<BR>or teacher have been washed.<BR> E. चरण and असृत nectar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=263-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चरणायुध|चरणायुधः
चरणायुध m. (-धः) A cock.<BR> E. चरण the foot, and आयुध a weapon, whose<BR>foot is his weapon.<BR> E. चरणम् आयुधं यस्य । कुक्वुटे ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=263-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चरणारविन्द|चरणारविंद
चरणारविन्द n. (-न्दं) The foot (of a deity, a lover, &c.)<BR> E. चरण and अर-<BR>विन्द a lotus; also many similar compounds, as चरणपद्मं, चरणकमलं,<BR>चरणनलिनं, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=263-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चरणास्कन्दन|चरणास्कंदन
चरणास्कन्दन n. (-नं) Trampling, trading on.<BR> E. चरण and आस्कन्दन going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=263-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चरणोदक
चरणोदक n. (-कं) Water in which the feet of a venerable Brahman or<BR>spiritual teacher have been washed.<BR> E. चरण and उदक water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=263-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चरणोपग
चरणोपग mfn. (-गः-गा-गं) In contact with the feet, at the feet.<BR> E. चरण.<BR>and उपग approached.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=263-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चरत्
चरत् mfn. (-रन्-रन्ती रत्) Going, going. to.<BR> E. चर् to go, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=263-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चरपुष्ट|चरपुष्टः
चरपुष्ट m. (-ष्टः) A mediator.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=263-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चरम|चरमः
चरम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>	 1. Last, ultimate, final.<BR>	 2. West, western. चर् to<BR>go, अमच् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=263-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चरमक्ष्माभृत्
चरमक्ष्माभृत् m. (-भृत्) The western mountain behind which the sun is<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=263-b" target="_blank">Page263-b+ 60</a>]<BR>supposed to set.<BR> E. चरम western, and क्ष्माभृत् a mountain; also<BR>चरमाचल, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=263-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चरमाचल|चरमाचलः
चरमाचल m. (-लः) See the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=263-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चरमाद्रि|चरमाद्रिः
चरमाद्रि m. (-द्रिः) See चरमक्ष्मामृत्; also other similar compounds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=263-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चराचर|चराचरं|चराचरः
चराचर mfn. (-रः-रा-री-रं)<BR>	 1. Moveable, locomotive.<BR>	 2. Shaking, trem-<BR>bling, unsteady.<BR>	 3. Wished, desired.<BR>	 4. Moveable and immove-<BR>able.<BR>	 n. (-रं)<BR>	 1. The world.<BR>	 2. Sky, atmosphere.<BR>	 3. Heaven, paradise.<BR>4. The aggregate of all things, whether inanimate or animate. E.<BR>चर् to go, affix अच् and the derivative reiterated, आङ् inserted;<BR>or चर what goes and अचर what does not go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=263-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चरि|चरिः
चरि m. (-रिः) An animal in general.<BR> E. चर locomotive, and इ Uṇādi<BR>aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=263-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चरित|चरितं
चरित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Gone, gone to, attained.<BR>	 n. (-तं) Fixed institute,<BR>proper or peculiar observance: see चरण.<BR>	 2. Story, adventures.<BR>	 3.<BR>Practice, behaviour.<BR>	 4. Nature.<BR> E. चर् to go, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=263-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चरितव्य
चरितव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं) To be followed or observed.<BR> E. चर and तव्य aff<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=263-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चरितार्थ|चरितार्थः
चरितार्थ mfn. (-र्थः-र्था-र्थं)<BR>	 1. Effected, accomplished.<BR>	 2. Successful. E.<BR>चरित and अर्थ object.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=263-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चरितगुणत्व
चरितगुणत्व n. (-त्वं)<BR>	 1. Accompaniment, assistance.<BR>	 2. Meritorious con-<BR>duct.<BR> E. चरित and गुणत्व faculty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=263-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चरित्र|चरित्रं
चरित्र n. (-त्रं)<BR>	 1. Instituted and peculiar observance or conduct.<BR>	 2.<BR>Story, adventures 3. Practice, habit, behaviour.<BR>	 4. Nature, dispo-<BR>sition.<BR>	 f. (-त्रा) The tamarind tree.<BR> E. चर् to go, इत्र Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=263-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चरित्रबन्धक|चरित्रबन्धकः
चरित्रबन्धक n. (-कं) A friendly pledge, one of unequal value to the loan.<BR>E. चरित्र and बन्धक a pledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=263-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चरिष्णु|चरिष्णुः
चरिष्णु mfn. (-ष्णुः-ष्णुः-ष्णु)<BR>	 1. Moveable, locomotive.<BR>	 2. Wandering about.<BR>E. चर् to go, and इष्णुच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=263-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चरीत्र|चरीत्रं
चरीत्र n. (-त्रं) Practice conduct behaviour: see चरित्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=263-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चरु|चरुः
चरु m. (-रुः)<BR>	 1. An oblation of rice barley, and pulse, boiled with<BR>butter and milk for presentation to the gods or manes.<BR>	 2. The<BR>vessel in which such an oblation is prepared.<BR> E. चर् to eat, उण्<BR>Uṇādi affix, what the gods feed upon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=263-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चरुव्रण|चरुव्रणः
चरुव्रण m. (-णः) A kind of cake.<BR> E. चर् to eat, उ affix, edible, and व्रण<BR>what is ground or pounded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=263-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चरुश्रपण
चरुश्रपण n. (-णं) Sprinkling an oblation of milk and ghee.<BR> E. चरु and<BR>श्रपण scattering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=263-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चरुस्थाली
चरुस्थाली f. (-ली) The vessel in which an oblation is prepared.<BR> E. चरु<BR>and स्थाली a pot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=263-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्घ
चर्घ r. 1st cl. (चर्घति) To go or move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=263-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्च|चर्चः|चर्च्च
चर्च r. 6th cl. (चर्चति)<BR>	 1. To speak or say.<BR>	 2. To abuse, to reprove,<BR>to censure or condemn.<BR>	 3. To injure or hurt.<BR>	 4. To inquire,<BR>r. 10th cl. (चर्चयति-ते) To read over, to peruse carefully, to study;<BR>also read चर्च्च. चुरा-उभ-सक-सेट् । तु-पर ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=263-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्चरी|चर्च्चरी
चर्चरी f. (-री)<BR>	 1. A festival, festive sport.<BR>	 2. A kind of song.<BR>	 3. Striking<BR>the hands to beat time. (In music).<BR>	 4. Curled or woolly hair.<BR>5. Musical symphony or, the recitation of scholars.<BR>	 6. The noise<BR>made at festivals, &c 7. Flattery, dishonest praise.<BR> E. चर्च् to<BR>speak, or say to sound, &c. अरन् and ङीष् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=263-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्चरीक|चर्चरीकः|चर्च्चरीकः
चर्चरीक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A form of ŚIVA.<BR>	 2. A potherb.<BR>	 3. Decorating or<BR>curling the hair.<BR> E. चर्चरी noise, &c. and क who utters, from कै to<BR>sound, affix ड; or चर्च ईकन् some authorities substitute बर्चरीक for<BR>this word.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=263-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्चा|चर्च्चा
चर्चा f. (-र्चा)<BR>	 1. Reflexion, consideration, the exercise of judgment or<BR>deliberation.<BR>	 2. Cleaning the person with fragrant unguents, 3.<BR>Inquiry, investigation.<BR>	 4. A name of the goddess DURGĀ.<BR> E. चर्च्<BR>to read, &c. affixes अच् and टाप् also चर्चिका &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=263-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्चिका|चर्च्चिका
चर्चिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. The goddess DURGĀ. or CHAMUNDA.<BR>	 2. Cleaning the<BR>person with perfumes.<BR>	 3. Deliberation, inquiry.<BR> E. चर्च् to ask,<BR>affix ण्वुल्; also चर्चा as above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=263-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्चित|चर्च्चितं
चर्चित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Perfumed, anointed, smeared with sandal, &c.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=264-a" target="_blank">Page264-a+ 60</a>]<BR>2. Sought, desired.<BR>	 3. Inquired into or after, investigated.<BR> E. चर्चा<BR>smearing, &c. and कर्मणि क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=263-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्च्च|चर्च|चर्चः
चर्च्च r. 1st and 10th cls. (चर्च्चते चर्च्चयते)<BR>	 1. To speak, to tell.<BR>	 2. To re-<BR>prove.<BR>	 3. To study: see चर्च.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=264-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्त्त्य
चर्त्त्य mfn. (-र्त्त्यः-र्त्त्या-र्त्त्यं)<BR>	 1. To be hurt or injured.<BR>	 2. To be strung or<BR>tied in order.<BR> E. चृत् to hurt, &c. and कर्मणि यत् affix from special.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=264-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्पट|चर्पटः
चर्पट m. (-टः)<BR>	 1. The open palm of the hand with fingers extended.<BR>	 2.<BR>A plant, (Mollugo pentaphylla.)<BR>	 3. A quantity of bubbles or specks<BR>(स्फारविपुल)<BR>	 f. (-टी) A thin cake or biscuit of flour.<BR> E. चर्प a Sautra<BR>root, to be low or flat, or चप् दीप्तौ; affix अटन् also चपट and चपेट.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=264-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्ब|चर्ब्ब
चर्ब r. 1st cl. (चर्बति) To go to move. भ्वा-पर-सक-सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=264-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्भट|चर्भटः
चर्भट m. (-टः) A kind of cucumber, (C. utilatissimus:) see इर्व्वारु.<BR>	 f. (-टी)<BR>The noise of merriment or festivity: see चर्च्चरी.<BR> E. चारु agreeable<BR>sound, and भट what makes, deriv. irr. चर क्विप् भट अच् कर्मधारय ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=264-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्म्म|चर्म|चर्मं|चर्म्मं
चर्म्म n. (-र्म्मं) A shield: see चर्म्मन्. चर्म साधनतया अस्ति अस्य अच् टिलोपः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=264-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्म्मकरण|चर्मकरण
चर्म्मकरण n. (-णं) Working in skins or leather.<BR> E. चर्म्म and करण making.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=264-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्म्मकषा|चर्मकषा
चर्म्मकषा f. (-षा) A plant, commonly called by a similar name Charmra-<BR>ksha or Charmagha.<BR> E. चर्म्म the skin, and कष what injures;<BR>also चर्म्मकसा. चर्म कषति कष-अच्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=264-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्म्मकार|चर्मकार|चर्मकारः|चर्म्मकारः
चर्म्मकार mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) The shoe-maker, a currier or worker in leather, the<BR>offspring of the Chandala woman by a man of the fisherman caste,<BR>or of a Vaideha female by a Nishadha.<BR>	 f. (-री)<BR>	 1. The plant Char-<BR>maghas: see the preceding.<BR>	 3. The wife of a Chamar.<BR> E. चर्म्म skin<BR>or leather, and कार who does or makes. चर्म तन्निमित्तं पादुकादि करोति<BR>कृ-अण् उपमित समासः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=264-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्म्मकारक|चर्मकारक|चर्मकारकः
चर्म्मकारक m. (-कः) A worker in leather.<BR> E. चर्म्म and कारक making.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=264-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्म्मकारिन्|चर्मकारिन्
चर्म्मकारिन् m. (-री) A currier, a worker in hides or leather.<BR> E. चर्म्म and<BR>कारिन् who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=264-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्म्मकार्य्य|चर्मकार्य
चर्म्मकार्य्य n. (-र्य्यं) Working in leather or skins.<BR> E. चर्म्म and कार्य्य<BR>business.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=264-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्म्मकील|चर्मकील|चर्मकीलः|चर्म्मकीलः
चर्म्मकील n. (-लं) A wart.<BR> E. चर्म्म and कील a bolt. चर्मणि कील इव ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=264-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्म्मकृत्|चर्मकृत्
चर्म्मकृत् n. (-कृत्) A shoe-maker: see चर्म्मकार.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=264-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्म्मचटका|चर्मचटका
चर्म्मचटका f. (-का) A bat.<BR> E. चर्म्म leather, and चटका a sparrow, the<BR>leather-winged sparrow; also चर्म्मचटिका चर्म्मचटी &c. चर्मणा चटका इव<BR>(चाम्चिका) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=264-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्म्मचटी|चर्मचटी
चर्म्मचटी f. (-टी) A bat.<BR> E. चर्म्म leather, and चट who hurts. चर्म चटति<BR>भिनत्ति चटभेदे अच् ङीष् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=264-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्म्मज|चर्मज|चर्म्मजं
चर्म्मज mfn. (-जः-जा-जं) Produced by or from the skin.<BR>	 n. (-जं)<BR>	 1. Hair.<BR>2. Blood.<BR> E. चर्म्म and ज born. चर्मणि जायते जन ड । रोमणि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=264-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्म्मण्वती|चर्मण्वती
चर्म्मण्वती f. (-ती)<BR>	 1. A river that runs across Bundelkhand into the<BR>Ganges, the modern Chambal.<BR>	 2. The plantain tree, (Musa sapien-<BR>tum.)<BR> E. चर्म्मन् skin, and मतुप् poss. affix; न is changed to ण it may<BR>also be dropped, and the word may be written चर्म्मवती.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=264-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्म्मतरङ्ग|चर्मतरङ्ग|चर्मतरङ्गः|चर्म्मतरङ्गः
चर्म्मतरङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः) A wrinkle, a fold of skin.<BR> E. चर्म्म and तरङ्ग a wave.<BR>चर्मणि तरङ्ग इव । जरया पलिते बलौ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=264-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्म्मदण्ड|चर्मदण्ड|चर्मदंड|चर्मदण्डः|चर्म्मदण्डः
चर्म्मदण्ड m. (-ण्डः) A whip.<BR> E. चर्म्म a leather (thong), and दण्ड a stick.<BR>चर्मणा कृतो दण्डः । कषायाम् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=264-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्म्मदूषिका|चर्मदूषिका
चर्म्मदूषिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. Leprosy.<BR>	 2. Cutaneous disease.<BR> E. चर्म्म and दूष् to<BR>vitiate, ण्वुल् aff. चर्म दूषयति ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=264-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्म्मन्|चर्मन्
चर्म्मन् n. (-र्म्म)<BR>	 1. Skin, hide, bark, &c.<BR>	 2. A shield.<BR>	 3. A student's hide,<BR>usually that of an antelope.<BR> E. चर् to go, to obstruct, Uṇādi affix<BR>मनिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=264-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्म्मनासिका|चर्मनासिका
चर्म्मनासिका f. (-का) A whip.<BR> E. चर्म्म, and नासिका the nose or end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=264-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्म्मपट्टिका|चर्मपट्टिका
चर्म्मपट्टिका f. (-का) A piece or strap of leather, for playing upon with<BR>dice, a leather backgammon board, &c.<BR> E. चर्म्म, and पट्टिका a fillet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=264-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्म्मपत्रा|चर्मपत्रा|चर्म्मपत्त्रा
चर्म्मपत्रा f. (-त्रा) A bat, the small house-bat.<BR> E. चर्म्म leather, and पत्र a<BR>wing, the fem. form implies diminutiveness. चर्म इव पत्रं पक्षोऽस्याः ।<BR>(चाम्चिका) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=264-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्म्मपादुका|चर्मपादुका
चर्म्मपादुका f. (-का) A leather shoe.<BR> E. चर्म्म and पादुका a slipper. चर्ममयी<BR>पादुका ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=264-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्म्मप्रभेदिका|चर्मप्रभेदिका
चर्म्मप्रभेदिका f. (-का) A shoe-maker's awl.<BR> E. चर्म्म leather, भिद् to pierce,<BR>with प्र prefixed, ण्वुल् affixed. चर्मं प्रभिनत्ति प्र + भिद-ण्वुल् टापि अत इत्त्वम् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=264-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्म्मप्रसेवक|चर्मप्रसेवक|चर्मप्रसेवकः|चर्म्मप्रसेवकः
चर्म्मप्रसेवक mf. (-वकः-विका) A bellows.<BR> E. चर्म्म leather, सिव् to sew, प्र<BR>prefix, and वुन् affix; what is sewn or made of leather.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=264-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्म्मवन्ध
चर्म्मवन्ध m. (-न्धः) A leather band or strap.<BR> E. चर्म्म and बन्ध band.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=264-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्ममय|चर्म्ममय
चर्ममय mfn. (-यः-यी-यं) Leather, made of leather.<BR> E. चर्म and मयट्<BR>aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=264-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्ममुण्डा|चर्ममुंडा|चर्म्ममुण्डा
चर्ममुण्डा f. (-ण्डा) A form of the goddess DURGĀ.<BR> E. चर्म a shield, and<BR>मुण्डा, a bald head whose head is round like a shield.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=264-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्मयष्टि|चर्मयष्टिः|चर्म्मयष्टि
चर्मयष्टि f. (-ष्टिः) A whip.<BR> E. चर्म, and यष्टि a stick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=264-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्मरु|चर्मरुः|चर्म्मरु|चर्म्मरुः
चर्मरु m. (-रुः) A shoe-maker, a worker in leather.<BR> E. चर्म leather, and रु<BR>to make a noise, affix क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=264-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्मसम्मवा
चर्मसम्मवा f. (-वा) Cardamoms: see एला.<BR> E. चर्म skin, and सम्भव produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=264-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्मसार|चर्मसारः|चर्म्मसार|चर्म्मसारः
चर्मसार m. (-रः) Lymph, serum.<BR> E. चर्म and सार essence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=264-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्माच्छादित|चर्म्माच्छादित
चर्माच्छादित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Covered with skin.<BR> E. चर्म and आच्छादित<BR>covered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=264-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्मावकर्त्तन|चर्मावकर्तन|चर्म्मावकर्त्तन
चर्मावकर्त्तन n. (-नं) Working in leather or skins. चर्म and अवकर्त्तन cutting<BR>off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=264-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्मावकर्त्तिन्|चर्मावकर्तिन्|चर्म्मावकर्त्तिन्
चर्मावकर्त्तिन् m. (-र्त्ती) A worker in leather or skins, a man of the lowest<BR>caste.<BR> E. चर्म and अवकर्त्तिन् who cuts off. चर्म अवकृन्तति स्वशिल्पनिर्वाहाय<BR>अव-कृती-छेदे णिनि । चर्मकारे ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=264-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्मावनद्ध|चर्म्मावनद्ध
चर्मावनद्ध mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>	 1. Covered with skin.<BR>	 2. Tied with leather, &c.<BR>E. चर्म and अवनद्ध bound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=264-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्मावृत|चर्म्मावृत
चर्मावृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Covered with skin or leather.<BR> E. चर्म and आवृत<BR>covered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=264-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्माम्भस्|चर्मांभस्|चर्म्माम्भस्
चर्माम्भस् n. (-म्भः) Lymph, serum.<BR> E. चर्म and अम्भस् water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=264-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्मार|चर्मारः|चर्म्मार|चर्म्मारः
चर्मार m. (-रः) A worker in leather.<BR> E. चर्म and ऋ to go, with अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=264-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्मिन्|चर्म्मिन्
चर्मिन् mfn. (-र्मी-र्मिणी-र्मि)<BR>	 1. Having a hide or skin.<BR>	 2. Leather, made of<BR>leather, &c.<BR>	 m. (-र्मी)<BR>	 1. A soldier armed with a shield, a shield<BR>bearer.<BR>	 2. A tree of which the bark is used for writing upon, &c.<BR>See भूर्ज a sort of birch.<BR>	 3. One of ŚIVAS doorkeeper: see भृङ्गरीट<BR>4. A plantain.<BR> E. चर्म skin, a shield, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=264-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्य्य|चर्य
चर्य्य mfn. (-र्य्यः-र्य्या-र्य्यं) To be gone, (in or by)<BR>	 nf. (-र्य्यं-र्य्या)<BR>	 1. Persever-<BR>ance in religious austerities.<BR>	 2. Due and regular observance of all<BR>rites or custom.<BR>	 3. Following the rules of studentship.<BR>	 4. Going.<BR>5. Eating.<BR>	 6. Practice usage.<BR>	 7. Behaviour.<BR> E. चर् to go, and यत्<BR>or ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=264-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्व|चर्व्व
चर्व r. 1st and 10th cls. (चर्वति चर्वयति-ते) To eat, to chew, to masticate.<BR>भ्रा-पर-सक-सेट् । चुरा उभ० ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=264-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्व्वण|चर्वण|चर्वणं|चर्व्वणं
चर्व्वण n. (-णं) Chewing, masticating.<BR> E. चर्व्व् to chew, and भावे ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=264-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्व्वन्|चर्वन्
चर्व्वन् m. (-र्व्वा) Striking with the flat of the hand.<BR> E. चर् to go, affix वुन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=264-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्व्वित|चर्वित|चर्व्वितं
चर्व्वित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Eaten.<BR>	 2. Chewed.<BR> E. चर्व्व् to eat, and कर्मणि क्त<BR>aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=264-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्व्वितपात्र|चर्वितपात्र
चर्व्वितपात्र n. (-त्रं) A spitting pot.<BR> E. चर्व्वित chewed, (pan or tobacco,)<BR>पात्र a vessel; also चर्व्वितपात्रकं. (पिकदानी) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=264-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्व्व्या
चर्व्व्या mfn. (-र्व्व्यः-र्व्व्या-र्व्व्यं) To be chewed.<BR>	 n. (-र्व्व्यं) Solid food, requiring<BR>mastication.<BR> E. चर्व्व् to chew, ण्यत् यत् वा affix; also चर्व्वणीय चर्व्वितव्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=264-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्षणि|चर्षणिः
चर्षणि m. (-णिः) A man. कृष-अनि आदेश्च चः उणादि । मनुष्ये ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=264-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चल|चलं|चलः
चल r. 1st. cl. (चलति) To tremble, to shake or totter. r. 6th cl. (चलति)<BR>To sport, to play. to frolic or wanton. r. 10th cl. (चालयति-ते) To<BR>cherish, to foster, (चालयति चालयते) To shake to cause to shake.<BR>With प्र, To fall as from a seat. भ्वा-पर-सक-सेट् । तुदा-पर-अक-सेट् ।<BR>चुरा-सक-उभ-सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=264-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चल|चलं|चलः
चल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Trembling tremulous, unfixed or unsteady.<BR>	 m. (-लः)<BR>Trembling, shaking.<BR>	 f. (-ला)<BR>	 1. The goddess of fortune, LAKṢMĪ.<BR>2. Lightning.<BR>	 3. Incense.<BR> E. चल् to go, affix अच् fem. affix टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=264-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चलकर्ण|चलकर्णः
चलकर्ण m. (-र्णः) The true distance of a planet from the earth.<BR> E. चल<BR>and कर्ण hypothenuse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=264-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चलचञ्चु|चलचंचु|चलचञ्चुः
चलचञ्चु mf. (-चञुः) The Greek partridge: see चकोर<BR> E. चल tremulous, and<BR>चञ्चु a beak. चला चञ्चुरस्य । चकोरे ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=264-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चलचित्त
चलचित्त mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं) Fickle, inconstant.<BR>	 n. (-त्तं) Fickleness, muta-<BR>bility.<BR> E. चल, and चित्त mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=265-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चलचित्तता
चलचित्तता f. (-ता) Fickleness, unsteadiness, inconstancy.<BR> E. तल् added<BR>to the last: also with त्व, चलचित्तत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=265-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चलत्
चलत् mfn. (-लन्-लन्तो-लत्) Going, moving.<BR> E. चल् to go, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=265-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चलत्पद
चलत्पद n. adv. (-दं) Moving, walking.<BR> E. चलत् and पद a step.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=265-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चलत्पूर्णिमा|चलत्पूर्ण्णिमा
चलत्पूर्णिमा f. (-मा) A small fish, (Chanda, HAM)<BR> E. चलत् trembling,<BR>and पूर्णिमा full moon, being of a white glistering colour, like that<BR>of the moon. चलन्ती पूर्णिमा तदुपलक्षितः चन्द्र इव ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=265-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चलदङ्ग|चलदङ्गः
चलदङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः) A fish, a sort of gilt-head.<BR> E. चलत् trembling, and अङ्ग<BR>body; also with कन् added चलदङ्गक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=265-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चलदल|चलदलः
चलदल m. (-लः) The holy fig tree.<BR> E. चल shaking, and दल a leaf. चलानि<BR>दलानि अस्य । अश्वत्थ-वृक्षे ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=265-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चलद्विष|चलद्विषः
चलद्विष m. (-षः) The Kokila or Indian cuckoo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=265-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चलन|चलनं|चलनः
चलन mfn. (-नः-ना-नी-नं)<BR>	 1. Who or what goes or moves.<BR>	 2. Trembling,<BR>tremulous, shaking.<BR>	 m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. A foot.<BR>	 2. A deer, an antelope.<BR>	 f.<BR>(-नी)<BR>	 1. A short petticoat worn by common women.<BR>	 2. The tye of<BR>an elephant.<BR>	 n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Wandering, roaming.<BR>	 2. Trembling, shak-<BR>ing.<BR>	 3. Going.<BR> E. चल् to go, affix भावे or करणे ल्युट् or युच् or कर्त्तरि ल्यु ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=265-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चलनक|चलनकं|चलनकः
चलनक n. (-कं) A short petticoat worn by women of some rank,<BR> E. चलन<BR>and कन् added. संज्ञायां कन् । चण्डातके ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=265-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चलमान
चलमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Going, moving, proceding.<BR> E. चल् to go शानच्<BR>aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=265-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चलस्
चलस् n. (-लः) Wood sorrel; see अम्ल.<BR> E. चल् to go, असुन् Uṇādi affi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=265-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चलसन्धि|चलसंधि|चलसन्धिः
चलसन्धि m. (-न्धिः) Moveable articulation of the bones, Diarthrosis. E.<BR>चल and सन्धि a joint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=265-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चलाचल|चलाचलः
चलाचल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>	 1. Tremulous, unsteady, unfixed.<BR>	 2. Moveable<BR>and stationary.<BR>	 m. (-लः) A cow.<BR> E. चल् to go, affix अच् deriv. re-<BR>iterated, and the first final vowel made long, or चल and अचल<BR>immoveable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=265-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चलि|चलिः
चलि m. (-लिः) A cover, a wrapper, a surtout: see निचोल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=265-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चलित|चलितं
चलित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Shaking, trembling.<BR>	 2. Gone, departed.<BR>	 3.<BR>Went, proceeded.<BR> E. चल् to go, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=265-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चलु|चलुः
चलु m. (-लुः) A handful of water, water taken up in the hollowed<BR>palm of the hand for rincing the mouth, &c.<BR> E. चल् to go, affix<BR>उन्, गण्डूषे ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=265-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चलुक|चलुकः
चलुक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. The hand hollowed as for holding a little water, &c.<BR>2. A small pot, a gallipot, &c.<BR>	 n. (-कं) A handful of water: see चलु<BR>E. चल् to go कन् affix: see चुलक । चलुना मीयते कन् । प्रसृतौ, भाण्डभेदे च ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=265-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चलेन्द्रिय|चलेंद्रिय
चलेन्द्रिय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Sensitive, sensual, not having subdued senses<BR>or passions.<BR> E. चल and इन्द्रिय organ of sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=265-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चवि|चविः
चवि f. (-विः-वी) The pepper plant or a kind of it.<BR> E. चर्व् to eat इन् affix;<BR>also sometimes ङीष्, deriv. irr. also चव्य and चविका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=265-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चविक|चविकं
चविक mf. (-कः-का or -की) A plant that yields a sort of long pepper,<BR>(Piper chavya.)<BR> E. चर्व् to eat, and क्कुन् affix, र rejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=265-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चव्य|चव्यं
चव्य nf. (-व्यं-व्या) A variety of pepper, (Piper chavya, Rox.)<BR>	 f. (-व्या)<BR>Orris root.<BR> E. चर्व् to be eaten, कर्मणि ण्यत् affix and deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=265-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चष
चष r. 1st cl. (चषति) To kill or hurt, (चषति-ते) To eat. भ्वा-उभ-सक-सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=265-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चषक|चषकं|चषकः
चषक mn. (-कः-कं)<BR>	 1. A vessel for drinking spirits with, a wine glass,<BR>&c.<BR>	 2. Any drinking vessel.<BR>	 3. Spirituous liquor.<BR>	 4. Honey.<BR> E. चष्<BR>to eat, करणे क्वुन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=265-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चषति|चषतिः
चषति m. (-तिः) Decay, infirmity.<BR> E. कृष् to plough, ति Uṇādi affix, and<BR>च substituted for the radical initials. चष-भक्षे बधे वा भावे अति ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=265-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चषाल|चषालः
चषाल m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. A wooden ring on the top of a sacrificial post.<BR>	 2. An<BR>iron ring at the base of the post.<BR>	 3. A hive.<BR> E. चष् to eat, &c. आलच्<BR>Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=265-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चह
चह r. 1st and 10th cls. (चहति, चहयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To be wicked, to commit<BR>wickedness.<BR>	 2. To cheat.<BR>	 3. To be proud, &c. r. 10th cl. (चहयति-ते)<BR>To grind or pound. भ्वा-पर-सक-सेट् । चुरा-उभ-सक-सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=265-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चाक्रिक|चाक्रिकः
चाक्रिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>	 1. Circular.<BR>	 2. Belonging to a wheel or discus.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=265-b" target="_blank">Page265-b+ 60</a>]<BR>3. Relating to a company or circle.<BR>	 m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A chorister, a<BR>bard who chants in chorus the praises of kings heroes, gods, &c.<BR>2. An oil maker.<BR>	 3. A coach-man, a driver.<BR> E. चक्र a multitude, &c.<BR>and ठक् aff. चक्रेण समूहेन यन्त्रभेदेन चक्रयुक्तशकटेन वा चरति ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=265-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चाक्षुष|चाक्षुषं|चाक्षुषः
चाक्षुष mfn. (-षः-षी-षं) Visible, perceptible, seen.<BR>	 m. (-षः) The sixth Manu.<BR>E. चक्षुष the eye, अण् aff. चक्षुषा गृह्यते ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=265-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चाङ्ग|चांग|चांगः|चाङ्गः
चाङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः) Whiteness or beauty of the teeth.<BR> E. चङ्ग handsome, affix<BR>ड । ची-ड चमङ्गमस्य । चाङ्गेय्याम् दन्तपटुत्वे च ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=265-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चाङ्गेरी
चाङ्गेरी f. (-री) Wood sorrel, (Oxalis monadelpha, Rox.)<BR> E. चाङ्ग as<BR>above, and इर् to send or cause, affixes अण् and ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=265-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चाचलि
चाचलि mfn. (-लिः-लिः-लि) Moving much or repeatedly.<BR> E. चल् to go,<BR>intents from, कि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=265-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चाञ्चल्य|चांचल्य|चांचल्यं|चाञ्चल्यं
चाञ्चल्य n. (-ल्यं)<BR>	 1. Tremulousness, unsteadiness.<BR>	 2. Transitoriness. E.<BR>चञ्चल, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=265-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चाट|चाटः
चाट m. (-टः) A cheat, a rogue, a peculator, one who makes away with<BR>money &c. entrusted to him.<BR> E. चट् to injure, affix अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=265-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चाटकैर|चाटकैरः
चाटकैर m. (-रः) A young sparrow.<BR> E. चटक a sparrow, and ऐरक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=265-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चाटु|चाटुः
चाटु mn. (-टुः-टु)<BR>	 1. Pleasing or grateful discourse.<BR>	 2. Distinct speech.<BR>3. Flattery.<BR> E. चट् to break, (anger,) Uṇādi affix ञुण्; also चटु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=265-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चाटुकार
चाटुकार mfn. (-रः-री-रं) Speaking agreeably or kindly.<BR>	 m. (-रः) A flat-<BR>terer.<BR> E. चाटु and कार who makes. चाटुं करोति ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=265-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चाटुपटु|चाटुपटुः
चाटुपटु m. (-टुः) A jester, a buffoon.<BR> E. चाटु agreeable speech, and पटु<BR>clever; also चाटुवटु. भण्डे । (भांँड) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=265-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चाटुलोल|चाटुलोलः
चाटुलोल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Elegantly tremulous.<BR> E. चाटु for चटु beautiful,<BR>and लोल trembling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=265-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चाटुवटु|चाटुवटुः
चाटुवटु m. (-टुः) A jester.<BR> E. चाटु wit and वटु who utters: see चाटुपटु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=265-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चाटुशत
चाटुशत n. (-तं) Repeated coaxing, a hundred entreaties.<BR> E. चाटु and शत<BR>a hundred.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=265-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चाटूक्ति|चाटूक्तिः
चाटूक्ति f. (-क्तिः)<BR>	 1. Service.<BR>	 2. Agreeable language.<BR>	 3. Flattery.<BR> E. चाटु<BR>agreeable speech, and उक्ति saying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=265-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चाणकीन|चाणकीनं
चाणकीन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Fit for or sown with the chickpea, (a field, &c.)<BR>E. चणक chickpea, and खञ् aff. चणकस्य भवनं क्षेत्रम् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=265-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चाणक्य|चाणक्यः
चाणक्य m. (-क्यः)<BR>	 1. A name of the sage VATSYAYANA.<BR>	 2. Name of a<BR>Brahman, the reputed author of a work on polity, and minister of<BR>CHANDRAGUPTA.<BR>	 n. (-क्यं) The work of Chanakya, detached stanzas<BR>original or compiled, on morals and polity.<BR> E. चणक a saint, and यञ्<BR>affix of descent. चणकस्य मुनेः गोत्रापत्यम् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=265-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चाणूर|चाणूरः
चाणूर m. (-रः) A wrestler in the service of KANSA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=265-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चाणूरसूदन|चाणूरसूदनः
चाणूरसूदन m. (-नः) KṚṢṆA.<BR> E. चाणूर and सूदन destroyer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=265-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चाण्डाल|चांडाल|चांडालः|चाण्डालः
चाण्डाल m. (-लः) A name of an impure or degraded tribe, a Chandala,<BR>a Pariah, an outcaste.<BR>	 f. (-ली) A woman of the same tribe.<BR> E. चडि<BR>to be angry, Uṇādi affix आलञ् and according to some अण् added<BR>also चण्डाल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=265-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चाण्डालिका|चांडालिका
चाण्डालिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. A vulgar lute.<BR>	 2. A name of DURGĀ.<BR>	 3. A kind<BR>of herb: see चण्डालिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=265-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चातक|चातकः
चातक m. (-कः) A bird, a kind of cuckoo, (Cuculus melanoleucus.) E.<BR>चत् to beg, affix कर्त्तरि ण्वुल्; begging water from the clouds, the<BR>supposed sole source of the fluid which this bird drinks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=265-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चातकानन्दन|चातकानंदन|चातकानन्दनः
चातकानन्दन m. (-नः) The rainy season.<BR> E. चातक and आनन्दन delighting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=265-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चातुर|चातुरः
चातुर mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>	 1. Perceptible, visible.<BR>	 2. Speaking well or amiably.<BR>3. Driving, one who drives, a driver, a charioteer, &c.<BR>	 4. Clever,<BR>able, ingenious.<BR>	 5. Relating to four.<BR>	 f. (-री) Dexterity, ability,<BR>cleverness.<BR>	 m. (-रः) A small round pillow for resting the cheek<BR>upon.<BR>	 n. (-रं) a four-wheeled carriage, a cart holding four people.<BR>E. चतुर dexterous, or चतुर् four, अण् affix; also with कन् added<BR>चातुरक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=265-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चातुरक|चातुरकः
चातुरक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) See the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=265-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चातुराश्रम्य|चातुराश्रम्यं
चातुराश्रम्य n. (-म्यं) The aggregate of the four orders of a Brahmana<BR>such as religious studentship, house-holder, mendicant and<BR>ascetic.<BR> E. चतुर् four, आश्रम order, ष्यञ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=265-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चातुरिक|चातुरिकः
चातुरिक m. (-कः) A charioteer, a coachman.<BR> E. चातुर a carriage, and<BR>ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=266-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चातुर्यक
चातुर्यक m. (-कः) A quartan ague.<BR> E. चतुर्य अण् affix, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=266-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चातुर्मास|चातुर्म्मास
चातुर्मास mfn. (-सः-सी-सं) Produced in four months.<BR> E. चतुर्मास, and अण्<BR>aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=266-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चातुर्मास्य|चातुर्मास्यं|चातुर्म्मास्य|चातुर्म्मास्यं
चातुर्मास्य n. (-स्यं) A sacrifice performed every four months.<BR> E. चतुर् and<BR>मास a month, यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=266-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चातुर्य्य|चातुर्य|चातुर्यं
चातुर्य्य n. (-र्य्यं) Dexterity, cleverness.<BR> E. चत्र and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=266-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चातुर्वर्ण्य|चातुर्व्वर्ण्यं
चातुर्वर्ण्य mfn. (-र्ण्यः-र्ण्या-र्ण्यं) Suited to the four tribes, belonging to them<BR>&c.<BR>	 n. (-र्ण्यं) The aggregate of the four original castes, the Brahman,<BR>Kṣatriya, Vaiśya and Śūdra.<BR> E. चतुर् four, and वर्ण a class, ष्यञ्<BR>aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=266-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चातुर्विध्य|चातुर्विध्यं
चातुर्विध्य n. (-ध्यं) Four kinds collectively.<BR> E. चतुर्विध and ञ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=266-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चातुर्वैद्य|चातुर्व्वैद्यः
चातुर्वैद्य m. (-द्यः) A priest, &c. versed in the four Vedas.<BR> E. चतुर four,<BR>वेद a Veda, and ष्यञ् affix; it is also derived from विद्या Know-<BR>ledge, and is optionally as here given, or चातर्विद्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=266-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चातुर्होतृक
चातुर्होतृक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Performed by four priests, read or sacrificed<BR>by, &c.<BR> E. चतुर् होतृ a priest, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=266-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चात्वाल|चात्वालं|चात्वालः
चात्वाल m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. A hollow made in the ground to receive, a burnt off-<BR>ering or sacrificial fire.<BR>	 2. Any hole in the ground.<BR> E. चत् to ask,<BR>(to solicit the gods) and वालञ् Uṇādi affix; also चत्वाल q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=266-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चान्दनिक|चांदनिक
चान्दनिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Made of or derived form Sandal, perfumed<BR>with it, &c.<BR> E. चन्दन, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=266-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चान्द्र|चांद्र|चान्द्रं|चान्द्रः
चान्द्र mfn. (-न्द्रः-न्द्री-न्द्रं) Lunar, relating to the moon, regulated by it,<BR>&c.<BR>	 m. (-न्द्रः)<BR>	 1. The Chandrakanta or moongem.<BR>	 2. A month, a<BR>lunar month.<BR>	 3. The light fortnight or half month, during which<BR>the moon is on the increase. (-न्द्रं) The Chandrayana observance:<BR>see चान्द्रायण f. (-न्द्री) Moonlight.<BR> E. चन्द्र the moon, and अण् affix of<BR>relation. चन्द्रस्य इदम् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=266-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चान्द्रक|चांद्रक|चांद्रकं|चान्द्रकं
चान्द्रक n. (-कं) Dried ginger.<BR> E. कन् added the last. शुण्ठ्यास् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=266-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चान्द्रभागा|चांद्रभागा
चान्द्रभागा f. (-गा) A river, the Chinab: see चन्द्रभागा; also चान्द्रभागी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=266-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चान्द्रमस|चांद्रमस|चान्द्रमसं|चान्द्रमसः
चान्द्रमस mfn. (-सः-सी-सं) Lunar, relating or belonging to the moon, &c.<BR>n. (-सं) The constellation Mrigasira: stars in Orion.<BR> E. चन्द्रमस् the<BR>moon, and अण् affix; the moon being its ruling deity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=266-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चान्द्रमसायन|चांद्रमसायनः|चान्द्रमसायनः
चान्द्रमसायन m. (-नः) A name of BUDDHA, regent of mercury, and son of<BR>CHANDRA or the moon.<BR> E. चन्द्रमस् the moon, फक् affix: or with<BR>फिञ् affix चान्द्रमसायनि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=266-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चान्द्रमास|चांद्रमास|चान्द्रमासः
चान्द्रमास m. (-सः) A lunar month, from new moon to new moon, when<BR>it is called Mukhya, and from full moon to full moon it is termed<BR>Gouna.<BR> E. चान्द्र lunar, मास month.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=266-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चान्द्रायण|चांद्रायण|चांद्रायणं|चान्द्रायणं
चान्द्रायण m. (-णः) A religious or expiatory observance regulated by the<BR>moon's age; diminishing the daily consumption of food every day,<BR>by one mouthful, for the dark half of the month beginning with fif-<BR>teen at the full moon, until is it reduced to one at the now moon,<BR>and then increasing it in like manner during the fortnight of the<BR>moon's increase: there are other forms of this penance.<BR> E. चन्द्र the<BR>moon, and स्वार्थे अण् aff. चन्द्रस्य अयनमिव अयनमत्र ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=266-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चान्द्रायणव्रत
चान्द्रायणव्रत n. (-तं) The penance called Chandrayana.<BR> E. चान्द्रायण as be-<BR>fore, and व्रत observance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=266-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चान्द्रायणविधान
चान्द्रायणविधान n. (-नं) The penance called Chandrayana.<BR> E. चान्द्रायण as<BR>before, and विधान rite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=266-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चाप|चापं|चापः
चाप m. (-पः)<BR>	 1. A bow.<BR>	 2. (In Geometry,) An arc or portion of a circle.<BR>3. Sagittarius, the ninth sign of the Zodiac.<BR> E. चप् to cast,<BR>(arrows,) affix अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=266-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चापपट|चापपटः
चापपट m. (-टः) A tree, (Buchanania latifolia, Rox.) See पियाल.<BR> E. चाप a<BR>bow, and पट what goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=266-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चापल|चापलं
चापल n. (-लं)<BR>	 1. Unsteadiness, (literally or metaphorically.)<BR>	 2. Transi-<BR>toriness.<BR> E. चपल trembling, अण् affix; also with यञ् affix चापल्य<BR>n. (-ल्यं.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=266-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चापलाश्रय
चापलाश्रय n. (-यं) Unsteadiness: transitoriness.<BR> E. चापल. and आश्रय support.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=266-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चापल्य|चापल्यं
चापल्य n. (-ल्यं) Unsteadiness: see चापल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=266-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चाबुका
चाबुका f. (-का) A small circular pillow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=266-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चामर|चामरं|चामरः
चामर nf. (-रं-रा or -री) A Chowri, the bushy tail of the Bos grunniens,<BR>used to whisk off flies, also as an emblem or insignia of princely<BR>rank.<BR> E. चमर the Yak or Bos grunniens, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=266-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चामरपुष्प|चामरपुष्पः
चामरपुष्प m. (-ष्पः)<BR>	 1. The betel-nut tree, (Areca faufel or catechu.)<BR>	 2. A<BR>kind of grass, (Saccharum cylindricum.)<BR>	 3. The mango tree.<BR>	 4. A<BR>flower, (Pandanus odoratissimus.)<BR>	 5. Ketaka plant.<BR> E. चामर a<BR>Chowri, and पुष्प a flower; whose flowers grow in clusters like the<BR>Indian chowri.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=266-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चामरपुष्पक|चामरपुष्पकः
चामरपुष्पक m. (-कः) A kind of grass: see काश.<BR> E. कन् added to the pre-<BR>ceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=266-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चामरिन्
चामरिन् m. (-री) A horse.<BR> E. चामर a Chowri, and इनि affix. Either allud-<BR>ing to his bushy tail, or the custom of whisking off flies, &c. from<BR>the animal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=266-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चामीकर|चामीकरं
चामीकर n. (-रं)<BR>	 1. Gold.<BR>	 2. The Dhutura plant. Gold.<BR> E. चमीकर said to<BR>mean a kind of mine, and अण् affix implying production.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=266-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चामुण्डा|चामुंडा
चामुण्डा f. (ण्डा)<BR>	 1. A terrific form of DURGĀ.<BR>	 2. One of the Matrikas.<BR>E. च the moon, and मुण्ड the head, having a head like the moon;<BR>or चा for चण्ड the name of a demon, and मुण्ड the skull; having<BR>seized the decapitated head of the demon: in either case the deriv.<BR>is irregular: see चर्ममुण्डा &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=266-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चाम्पिला|चांपिला
चाम्पिला f. (-ला) The champa river. (Probably the mordern Chambal).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=266-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चाम्पेय|चांपेय|चांपेयः|चाम्पेयः
चाम्पेय mn. (-यः-य)<BR>	 1. The Champaca, (Michelia champaca.)<BR>	 2. A plant<BR>commonly Nageshwar, or Naga kesara (Mesua ferrea.)<BR>	 3. The<BR>filament of flower.<BR>	 4. gold.<BR>	 5. Dhutura plant.<BR> E. चम्पा the district,<BR>and ढक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=266-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चाम्प
चाम्प n. (-म्पं) Food, &c.<BR> E. चम् to eat, ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=266-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चाय
चाय (ऋ) चायृ r. 1st cl. (चायति-ते)<BR>	 1. To worship, to revere.<BR>	 2. To discern,<BR>to perceive. भ्वा-सक-उभ-वेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=266-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चार|चारं|चारः
चार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Going in motion.<BR>	 2. A spy, a secret agent or emissary.<BR>3. Binding, a binding, a fetter, &c.<BR>	 4. A prison, a house of confine-<BR>ment.<BR>	 5. A kind of tree, the Piyal, (Buchanania latifolia, Rox.)<BR>see पियाल 6. Wandering about, travelling.<BR>	 n. (-रं) A factitious<BR>poison.<BR> E. चर going, &c. affix अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=266-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चारक|चारकः
चारक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A groom, a horseman, a cavalier.<BR>	 2. A binding, a<BR>fetter.<BR>	 3. An associate, a companion.<BR>	 4. A spy.<BR>	 5. A herdsman<BR>E. चर् to go, in the causal form, and णिच्-ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=266-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चारकाण्ड
चारकाण्ड n. (-ण्डं) Ascenscional difference, (in Astronomy.)<BR> E. चार and<BR>काण्ड part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=266-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चारचक्षुस्
चारचक्षुस् n. (-क्षुः) Espionage.<BR>	 m. (-क्षुः) One (a king, &c.) who employs<BR>spies.<BR> E. चार and चक्षुस् eye. चारश्चक्षुरस्य । नृपे ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=266-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चारचण
चारचण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Graceful in gait or motion.<BR> E. चार and चणप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=266-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चारचुञ्चु
चारचुञ्चु mfn. (-ञ्चुः-ञ्चुः-ञ्चु) Remarkable in walking, of graceful carriage.<BR>E. चार and चुञ्चुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=266-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चारज्या
चारज्या f. (-ज्या) The sine of the ascensional difference. (In astronomy.)<BR>E. चार, and ज्या sine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=266-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चारटी
चारटी f. (टी) A plant: see पद्मचारिणी.<BR> E. चर in the causal, what makes<BR>go or disperses, (disease,) अटन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=266-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चारण|चारणः
चारण m. (-णः)<BR>	 1. A dancer, a mime.<BR>	 2. An actor of note.<BR>	 3. A reader of<BR>scripture.<BR>	 4. A panegyrist of the gods.<BR>	 5. A bard, a herald.<BR>	 6. A<BR>celestial singer.<BR>	 7. A spy.<BR>	 8. A pilgrim.<BR> E. चर in the causal,<BR>to cause to go, to diffuse, (fame, &c.) and णिच् ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=266-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चारणदारा
चारणदारा f. plur. (-राः) Female dancers, actresses, &c.<BR> E. चारण and दारा<BR>wives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=266-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चारपथ|चारपथः
चारपथ m. (-थः) A meeting of two roads.<BR> E. चार a passenger, and पथिन् a<BR>road ष affix, which leaves final अच् समासान्तः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=266-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चारभट|चारभटः
चारभट m. (-टः) A hero, a chief or a warrior.<BR> E. चार diffusion, (of praise,<BR>&c.) and भट who desires.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=266-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चारयित्वा
चारयित्वा ind.<BR>	 1. Having enjoined or prescribed, having caused to<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=267-a" target="_blank">Page267-a+ 60</a>]<BR>observe.<BR>	 2. Having made to go.<BR> E. चर् to go, causal form, क्त्वा aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=266-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चारवायु|चारवायुः
चारवायु m. (-युः) Summer air, zephyr.<BR> E. चार causing to go, and वायु air<BR>or wind. चारेण रवेरुदग्गतिभेदेन कृतो वायुः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=267-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चारान्तरित|चारांतरित|चारान्तरितः
चारान्तरित m. (-तः) A secret emissary or spy.<BR> E. चार and अन्तरित con-<BR>cealed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=267-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चारिका
चारिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. A female attendant. A cockroach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=267-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चारित
चारित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Caused to go.<BR>	 2. Distilled.<BR> E. चर् to go, causal<BR>form क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=267-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चारिवाच्
चारिवाच् f. (-क्) A plant: see कर्क्कटशृङ्गी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=267-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चारित्र|चारित्रं
चारित्र n. (-त्रं)<BR>	 1. Peculiar observance or practice, peculiarity of customs<BR>or condition.<BR>	 2. Conduct.<BR>	 3. Reputation: see चरण f. (-त्रा) The<BR>tamarind tree.<BR> E. चर् to go णित्रन् Uṇādi affix; also चरित्र &c. चरित्र-<BR>मेव स्वार्थे अण् वा ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=267-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चारित्र्य
चारित्र्य n. (-त्र्यं) Becoming practices moral conduct or instituted obser-<BR>vance.<BR> E. चरित्र and स्वार्थे ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=267-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चारु|चारुः
चारु mfn. (-रुः-र्वी-रु)<BR>	 1. An agreeable, welcome, dear.<BR>	 2. Beautiful,<BR>elegant.<BR>	 m. (-रुः) A name of VṚHASPATI, regent of JUPITER,<BR>and preceptor of the gods.<BR> E. चर् to go, Uṇādi affix उण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=267-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चारुक|चारुकः
चारुक m. (-कः) The seed of the Sara cane.<BR> E. चारु + संज्ञायां कन् added to<BR>the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=267-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चारुगर्भ|चारुगर्भः
चारुगर्भ m. (-र्भः) A son of KṚṢṆA.<BR> E. चारु and गर्भ asylum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=267-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चारुगुप्त|चारुगुप्तः
चारुगुप्त m. (-प्तः) A son of KṚṢṆA.<BR> E. चारु and गुप्त preserved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=267-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चारुता
चारुता f. (-ता) Loveliness, beauty.<BR> E. तल् added to चारु; also with त्व<BR>added चारुत्वम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=267-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चारुदेष्ण|चारुदेष्णः
चारुदेष्ण m. (-ष्णः) The son of KṚṢṆA by RUKMIṆĪ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=267-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चारुधामन्
चारुधामन् m. (-मा) A plant: see शठी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=267-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चारुधारा
चारुधारा f. (-रा) A name of Sachi the wife of Indra.<BR> E. चारु beautiful,<BR>and धारा fame, splendor, &c. चारुं चारुतां धारयति धारि अण् । चार्वी<BR>धारा अस्या वा । शच्याम् । some authorities read चारुधामा, from चारु and<BR>abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=267-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चारुफला
चारुफला f. (-ला) A grape.<BR> E. चारु beautiful, and फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=267-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चारुमत्|चारुमन्त्
चारुमत् mfn. (-मान्-मती-मत्) Lovely, beautiful.<BR>	 f. (-ती) The daughter of<BR>KṚṢṆA by RUKMIṆĪ.<BR> E. चारु and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=267-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चारुलोचन|चारुलोचनः
चारुलोचन m. (-नः) A deer.<BR>	 f. (-ना) A woman with fine eyes.<BR> E. चारु<BR>beautiful and लोचन an eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=267-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चारुवर्द्धना
चारुवर्द्धना f. (-ना) A woman.<BR> E. चारु and वर्द्धन increasing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=267-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चारुबाहु|चारुबाहुः
चारुबाहु m. (-हुः) One of KṚṢṆA'S sons.<BR> E. चारु and बाहु an arm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=267-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चारुव्रता
चारुव्रता f. (-ता) A female who observes a month of fasting.<BR> E. चारु ele-<BR>gant, and व्रत religious observance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=267-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चारुशिला
चारुशिला f. (-ला) A jewel, a gem.<BR> E. चारु and शिला a stone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=267-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चारुशील
चारुशील mfn. (-ल-ला-लं) Lovely, beautiful.<BR> E. चारु and शील having.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=267-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चारुहासिन्
चारुहासिन् mfn. (-सी-सिनी-सि) Smiling sweetly.<BR> E. चारु and हासिन् smil-<BR>ing. चारु हसति हस-णिनि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=267-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चारेक्षण|चारेक्षणः
चारेक्षण m. (-णः) A statesman, a minister or king.<BR> E. चारु a spy, and<BR>ईक्षण seeing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=267-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चार्च्चिक्य|चार्चिक्य|चार्चिक्यं|चार्च्चिक्यं
चार्च्चिक्य n. (-क्यं)<BR>	 1. Perfuming the person, smearing it with Sandal,<BR>&c.<BR>	 2. An unguent<BR> E. चर्च् to beautiful, धात्वर्थे ण्वुल् affix, and चर्चिका<BR>एव स्वार्थे ष्यञ् added: see चर्चिका, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=267-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चार्म|चार्म्म|चार्म्मः
चार्म mfn. (-र्म-र्मी-र्मं)<BR>	 1. Covered with leather, (a car, &c.)<BR>	 2. Defended<BR>by a hide or skin.<BR>	 3. Shielded, having a shield.<BR> E. चर्म leather, and<BR>अण् aff. चर्मणा परिवृतो रथः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=267-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चार्मण|चार्म्मण|चार्म्मणं
चार्मण n. (-णं) A multitude of hides, or of shields, f. (-नी) covered with<BR>skin or leather &c.<BR> E. चर्मण् a hide. &c. and अण् affix of aggre-<BR>gation. चर्मणां समूहः । चर्मसमुदाये ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=267-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चार्मिक|चार्म्मिक
चार्मिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>	 1. Leather, made of leather.<BR>	 2. Belonging to<BR>the skin, &c.<BR> E. चर्म, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=267-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चार्मिण|चार्मिणं|चार्म्मिण|चार्म्मिणं
चार्मिण n. (-णं) A number of men armed with shields.<BR> E. चर्मिन् A shield-<BR>bearer, and अण् aff. चर्मिणां समूहः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=267-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चार्व्वङ्गी|चार्वङ्गी|चार्वंगी
चार्व्वङ्गी f. (-ङ्गी) A beauty.<BR> E. चारु, and अङ्ग the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=267-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चार्व्वाक|चार्वाक|चार्वाकः|चार्व्वाकः
चार्व्वाक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A sophist, a philosopher; one acquainted with the<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=267-b" target="_blank">Page267-b+ 60</a>]<BR>doctrines of the schools, a sceptic n many matters of Hindu faith,<BR>and considered by the orthodox as an atheist or materialist.<BR>	 2.<BR>Name of an old philosopher a pupil of Brihaspati who taught the<BR>rankest form of Atheism<BR> E. चारु good, beautiful, and वाक discourse.<BR>चारुः लोकसम्मतो वाको वाक्यं यस्य पृषो० । वृहस्पतिशिष्ये ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=267-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चार्व्वाघाट|चार्वाघाट
चार्व्वाघाट mfn. (-टः-टा-टं) Destructive of beauty.<BR> E. चारु, and हन् to des-<BR>troy, affix अण् and घट substituted for the radicals; also with घात,<BR>चार्व्वाघात । चारु आहन्ति आ + हन् चारुः वाहनोऽण् अन्त्यस्य च टः संज्ञायाम् चारौ वा<BR>वार्त्ति-अण् वा टान्तादेशः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=267-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चार्व्वी|चार्वी
चार्व्वी f. (-र्व्वी)<BR>	 1. A beautiful woman, a beauty.<BR>	 2. The wife of KUVERA.<BR>3. Understanding, intellect.<BR>	 4. Moonlight.<BR>	 5. Light, splendour. E.<BR>चारु beautiful, fem. affix ङीप्. चारु + गुणवचनत्वात् स्त्रियां ङीप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=267-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चाल|चालः
चाल m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. The thatch or roof of a house.<BR>	 2. The blue jay.<BR>	 3.<BR>Shaking, moving.<BR> E. चल् to go, affix ण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=267-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चालक|चालकः
चालक m. (-कः) A restive elephant.<BR> E. चल् to go, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=267-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चालन|चालनं
चालन nf. (-नं-नी) A sieve, a strainer.<BR>	 n. (नं)<BR>	 1. Causing to move or go.<BR>2. Muscular action.<BR> E. चल in the causal, to make go, (grain, &c.<BR>through its pores,) णिच् भावे ल्युट् and ङीप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=267-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चाष|चाषः
चाष m. (-षः)<BR>	 1. The blue jay, (Coracias Indica.)<BR>	 2. A kingfisher, (ac-<BR>cording to some.)<BR> E. चष् to injure, (fish. &c.) affix; स्वार्थे णिच् अच्<BR>also चास.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=267-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चास|चासः
चास m. (-सः)<BR>	 1. The blue jay.<BR>	 2. Sugar cane: see the preceding. चष्<BR>हिंसायां णिच् अच् पृषो० चाषखगे, इक्षुभेदे च ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=267-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चि
चि (चिञ) चिञ् r. 1st, 5th and 10th cls. (चयति-ते चिनोति चययति or चपयति)<BR>To collect, to gather together, to heap, to assemble, to accumulate,<BR>&c. With अप, To lose, to squander. With उप or सम्, To collect or<BR>acquire. With निर्, To determine. With वि and निर्, To deter-<BR>mine exactly (ईरण) ईरणिच् r. 1st cl. (चयति) to injure, (peculiar to<BR>the Vedas.) भ्वा उभ-अनिट् । चुरा-उभ । स्वा-उभ-द्विक-अनिट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=267-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिकरिषु
चिकरिषु mfn. (-षुः-षुः-षु) Desirous to cast or throw.<BR> E. कृ to throw, de-<BR>siderative form, उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=267-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिकर्त्तिषु|चिकर्तिषु
चिकर्त्तिषु mfn. (-षुः-षुः-षु) Desiring or intending to cut or cut off.<BR> E. कृत् to<BR>cut, desiderative form, उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=267-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिकित्सक|चिकित्सकः
चिकित्सक m. (-कः) A physician, a practiser in medicine.<BR> E. कित् to cure,<BR>affix स्वार्थे सन् ण्वुल् and the root reiterated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=267-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिकित्मन
चिकित्मन n. (-नं) Healing, practising medicine.<BR> E. कित् to relieve, rei-<BR>terative form, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=267-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिकित्सा
चिकित्सा f. (-त्सा) The practice of medicine, healing, curing, administer-<BR>ing or applying remedies.<BR> E. कित् to relieve, (disease,) in the redu-<BR>plicate form, affixes अ and टाप् । कित-स्वार्थे सन् भावे अ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=267-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिकित्सित|चिकित्सितं
चिकित्सित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Remedied, healed, physicked, cured.<BR>	 n. (-तं)<BR>Healing, remedying.<BR> E. कित, &c.: see the preceding, affix क्त स्वार्थे<BR>सन् कर्मणि क्त । भावे क्त वा ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=267-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिकिन|चिकिनः
चिकिन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Flat-nosed.<BR> E. नि preposition, इनच् affix in this<BR>sense, and नि changed to चिकः निनता नासिका इनच् ‘पिटाच्चिकचि च’<BR>वार्त्ति० इनच प्रकृतेश्च चिक्यादेशः । निनतनासिके (खांँदा) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=267-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिकिल|चिकिलः
चिकिल m. (-लः) Mud, mire.<BR> E. चिक् to obstruct, इलच् affix deriv. irr.<BR>चि वा इलच् कुक् च । पङ्के ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=267-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिकीर्षत्|चिकीर्षन्त्
चिकीर्षत् mfn. (-र्षन्-र्षन्ती-र्षत्) Wishing, purposing, meaning to do.<BR> E. कृ to<BR>do, desiderative form, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=267-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिकीर्षा
चिकीर्षा f. (-र्षा) Desire to do any thing.<BR> E. कृ to do, in the desiderative<BR>form, अ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=267-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिकीर्षित
चिकीर्षित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Wished, designed. purposed.<BR>	 n. (-तं) Purpose,<BR>intention.<BR> E. कृ to do, desiderative form, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=267-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिकीर्षु|चिकीर्षुः
चिकीर्षु mfn. (-र्षुः-र्षुः-र्षु) Desirous to do any thing.<BR> E. कृ to do, reiterated, and उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=267-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिकुर|चिकुरः
चिकुर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Rashly criminal, inconsiderately guilty, punishing<BR>or injuring others without consideration.<BR>	 m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Hair.<BR>	 2. A<BR>mountain.<BR>	 3. A snake, a reptile.<BR>	 4. A musk rat.<BR>	 5. A kind of bird.<BR>6. A kind of tree.<BR>	 f. (-रा) Moving.<BR> E. चि imitative sound, and कुर्<BR>to utter, affix क । चि इति अव्यक्तशब्दं कुरति कुर-क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=267-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिकुरपाश|चिकुरपाशः
चिकुरपाश m. (-शः) Abundance of hair.<BR> E. चिकुर &c. and पाश affix in this<BR>sense: see केशपाश; also with other affixes चिकुरपक्ष, and चिकुरहस्त, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=268-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिकूर|चिकूरः
चिकूर m. (-रः) Hair. E. See चिकुर; the vowel made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=268-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिक्क|चिक्कः
चिक्क r. 10th cl. (चिक्कयति-ते) To give pain. पीडने । चु-उभ-सक-सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=268-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिक्क|चिक्कः
चिक्क mfn. (-क्कः-क्की-क्कं) Flat-nosed.<BR>	 m. (-क्कः) A musk rat.<BR>	 f. (-क्का) A mouse.<BR>E. चिक् imitative sound, and क who utters, from कै with ड affix;<BR>or चिक्क् to give pain, and क affix; or in the last sense, नि preposi-<BR>tion changed. to चिक् and कच् added चिक् इति अव्यक्तेन शब्देन कायति कै<BR>क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=268-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिक्कण|चिक्कणं|चिक्कणः
चिक्कण mfn. (-णः-णा-णी-णं)<BR>	 1. Unctuous, greasy.<BR>	 2. Bland, emollient.<BR>	 3.<BR>Smooth, glossy.<BR>	 4. Slippery.<BR>	 m. (-णः) The betel-nut tree.<BR>	 nf. (-णं-णा<BR>or -णी)<BR>	 1. The betel nut.<BR>	 2. A good cow.<BR> E. चित् to think of, Uṇādi<BR>affix अच्, the final of the radical changed to क. or चिक्क-क्विप् चिक्<BR>तं कणति कण + शब्दे अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=268-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिक्कणता
चिक्कणता f. (-ता) Smoothness, greasiness, oiliness.<BR> E. तल् added to to the<BR>last; also with त्व चिक्कणत्वम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=268-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिक्कस|चिक्कसः
चिक्कस m. (-सः) Barley meal.<BR> E. चिक्क् to give pain, असच् aff. यवचूर्णे ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=268-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिक्किण
चिक्किण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>	 1. Unctuous, greasy.<BR>	 2. Bland, emollient.<BR>	 3.<BR>Glossy, shining, smooth.<BR>	 4. Slippery.<BR>	 f. (-णा) An excellent cow:<BR>see चिक्कण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=268-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिक्रंसा
चिक्रंसा f. (-सा) Wish to go or to approach.<BR> E. क्रम् to go, desiderative<BR>form, अङ् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=268-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिक्लिद|चिक्लिदं|चिक्लिदः
चिक्लिद n. (-दं) Moisture, freshness.<BR> E. क्लिद् to be wet, यङ लुक् अच् नि० ।<BR>affix, root redup. अतिशयक्लेदयुक्ते ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=268-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिङ्गेट
चिङ्गेट mf. (-टः-टी) A shrimp or prawn.<BR> E. चिङ्ग handsome, and अट what<BR>goes, the radical vowel changed; also चिङ्गड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=268-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिचिण्ड|चिचिंडः|चिचिण्डः
चिचिण्ड m. (-ण्डः) A sort of gourd, commonly Chichinda, (Trichosanthes<BR>anguinæ) चि-वा इण्डच् चुक् च ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=268-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिचीषत्
चिचीषत् mfn. (-षन्-षन्ती-षत्) Wishing to gather or collect.<BR> E. चि to collect<BR>desiderative form, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=268-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिञ्चा|चिंचा
चिञ्चा f. (-ञ्चा)<BR>	 1. The tamarind tree or its fruit.<BR>	 2. The gunja plant. E.<BR>चम् to eat, affix क्विप् and the radical vowel changed, चिम् then,<BR>चर् to go, with ड affix, and the fem. form what becomes edible.<BR>चिम् इति अव्यक्तं शब्दं चिनोति चि ड ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=268-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिञ्चाटक
चिञ्चाटक m. (-कः) A sort of grass, commonly Chenchra. चिञ्चा इव अटति अट<BR>ण्वुल् । (चेंच् को) तृणभेदे ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=268-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिञ्चाम्ल|चिञ्चाम्लं|चिञ्चाम्लः
चिञ्चाम्ल m. (-म्लः) An acid potherb, (Rumex vesicatorius.)<BR> E. चिञ्चा and<BR>अम्ल sour. चिञ्चा इव अम्लम् अम्लशाके (आमरुल्) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=268-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिञ्चासार|चिञ्चासारः
चिञ्चासार m. (-रः) A sort of potherb. (Rumex vesicatorius.)<BR> E. चिञ्चा<BR>and सार essence. चिञ्चाया इव सारोऽस्य । अम्लशाके (आमरुल्) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=268-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिट
चिट r. 1st and 10th cls. (चेटति चेटयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To be another's messenger<BR>or servant.<BR>	 2. To order as a servant भ्वा-पर-सक-चुरा-उभ वा सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=268-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित|चितः
चित (ई) चिती r. 1st cl. (चेतति) चित r. 10th cl. (चेतयति-ते) also (इ) चिति r.<BR>10th cl. (चिन्तयति) To think or reflect on, to be sensible or rational,<BR>to weigh, to remember, to consider, &c. भ्वा-पर-सक-सेट् । चु-आत्म-सक-<BR>सेट् । स्मृतौ चु-उभ-सक-सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=268-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्
चित् f. (-चित्) Intellect, understanding. ind. A particle and affix to<BR>words giving them an indefinite signification, as कश्चित् some one,<BR>कस्यचित् of some one, &c. see चन.<BR> E. चित् to remember, affix भावे क्विप्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=268-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित|चितः
चित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Covered, veiled, concealed.<BR>	 2. Collected, accum-<BR>ulated.<BR>	 3. Piled, heaped.<BR>	 f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. A funeral pile.<BR>	 2. A heap, an<BR>assemblage.<BR> E. चि to collect, &c. affix कर्मणि क्त; also चिति and चिती<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=268-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिताग्नि|चिताग्निः
चिताग्नि m. (-ग्निः) The funeral fire.<BR> E. चिता the pile, and अग्नि fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=268-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिताचूडक|चिताचूडकं
चिताचूडक n. (-कं) A mark where funeral pile has been, a mausoleum, a<BR>monument, &c.<BR> E. चिता a pile, and चूडक a crest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=268-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिति|चितिः
चिति f. (-तिः) Collecting, gathering. (-तिः-ती)<BR>	 1. funeral pile.<BR>	 2. A heap,<BR>a quantity.<BR>	 3. A pile, a stack.<BR>	 4. An oblong with quadrangular<BR>sides.<BR> E. चि to collect, affix आधारे क्तिन् and optionally ङीष् is<BR>added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=268-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चितिका
चितिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. A funeral pile.<BR>	 2. A small chain worn as an<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=268-b" target="_blank">Page268-b+ 60</a>]<BR>ornament round the loins.<BR> E. चित् to think of, इकन् affix and fem.<BR>form. चितिरिव कायति कै क वा चिति स्वार्थे क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=268-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्कार
चित्कार m. (-रः) A cry, a scream.<BR> E. चित् imitative sound, and कार<BR>making. चित् + कृ भावे यञ् । पृषो वा दीर्घः । Also चीत्कार.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=268-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्कारशब्द
चित्कारशब्द m. (-ब्दः) A cry, a scream.<BR> E. चित्कार the same, and शब्द sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=268-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्त|चित्तं
चित्त n. (-त्तं) The mind or faculty of reasoning, the heart considered as<BR>the seat of intellect.<BR> E. चित् to consider, and करणे क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=268-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्तकलित
चित्तकलित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Anticipated, expected, calculated.<BR>	 2.<BR>Known<BR> E. चित्त and कलित computed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=268-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्तजन्मन्
चित्तजन्मन् m. (-न्मा) Love.<BR> E. चित्त and जन्मन् birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=268-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्तनिर्वृत्ति
चित्तनिर्वृत्ति f. (-त्तिः) Contentment, happiness.<BR> E. चित्त and निर्वृत्ति repose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=268-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्तप्रशम|चित्तप्रशमः
चित्तप्रशम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं) Tranquil, content.<BR> E. चित्त and प्रशम calmness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=268-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्तप्रसन्नता
चित्तप्रसन्नता f. (-ता) Happiness, gaiety, joy.<BR> E. चित्त the heart, प्रसन्नता<BR>happiness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=268-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्तराग|चित्तरागः
चित्तराग mn. (-गः-गं) Passion, desire.<BR> E. चित्त and राग passion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=268-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्तवत्|चित्तवन्त्
चित्तवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Kind-hearted, amiable.<BR> E. चित्त and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=268-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्तविकार|चित्तविकारः
चित्तविकार m. (-रः) Change of thoughts or feelings.<BR> E. चित्त, and विकार<BR>alteration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=268-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्तविकारिन्
चित्तविकारिन् mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि) Changing a person's character or feel-<BR>ing.<BR> E. चित्त and विकारिन् causing change.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=268-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्तविप्लव|चित्तविप्लवः
चित्तविप्लव m. (-वः) Madness, insanity.<BR> E. चित्त the mind, and विप्लव afflic-<BR>tion. चित्तस्य विप्लवोऽनवस्थानं यस्मात् । उन्मादरोगे ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=268-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्तविभ्रम|चित्तविभ्रमः
चित्तविभ्रम m. (-मः) Madness, derangement.<BR> E. चित्त as above, and विभ्रम<BR>wandering, चित्तस्य विभ्रमो विशेषेण भ्रमणमनवस्थानं यम्मात् । उन्मादरोगे ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=268-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्तवृत्ति|चित्तवृत्तिः
चित्तवृत्ति f. (-त्तिः) Inward purpose, feeling, emotion.<BR> E. चित्त and वृत्ति<BR>being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=268-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्तवेदना
चित्तवेदना f. (-ना) Anxiety, affliction.<BR> E. चित्त, and वेदना pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=268-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्तभव
चित्तभव mfn. (-वः-वा-वं) Felt, perceived, being in the thoughts.<BR> E. चित्त,<BR>and भव being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=268-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्तभू
चित्तभू m. (-भूः) Love.<BR> E. चित्त, and भू born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=268-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्तभेद|चित्तभेदः
चित्तभेद m. (-दः) Inconsistency, contrariety of purpose or will.<BR> E. चित्त,<BR>and भेद difference.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=268-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्तसङ्ख्य|चित्तसंख्य
चित्तसङ्ख्य mfn. (-ङ्ख्यः-ङ्ख्या-ङ्ख्यं) Pervading the heart, penetrating, knowing<BR>the thoughts.<BR> E. चित्त, and सङ्ख्य what enumerates.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=268-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्तसमुन्नति|चित्तसमुन्नतिः
चित्तसमुन्नति f. (-तिः) Pride, arrogance, hauteur, haughtiness.<BR> E. चित्त the<BR>mind, समुन्नति elevation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=268-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्तसंहति
चित्तसंहति f. (-तिः) A multitude of thoughts, minds or emotions.<BR> E. चित्त,<BR>and संहति assemblage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=268-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्तहृत्
चित्तहृत् mfn. (-हृत्) Winning, fascinating.<BR> E. चित्त. and हृत् who takes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=268-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्तहारिन्
चित्तहारिन् mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि) Beautiful, agreeable, fascinating.<BR> E. चित्त,<BR>हारिन् what seizes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=268-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्तापहारिन्
चित्तापहारिन् mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि) Captivating, attractive.<BR> E. चित्त, and अप-<BR>हारिन् what takes away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=268-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्ताभोग|चित्ताभोगः
चित्ताभोग m. (-गः) Consciousness of pleasure or pain, the attention of<BR>the mind to its own sensations.<BR> E. चित्त the mind, and आभोग<BR>enjoyment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=268-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्तासङ्ग|चित्तासंग|चित्तासङ्गः
चित्तासङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः) Love, attachment, affection.<BR> E. चित्त and आसङ्ग devotion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=268-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्तैक्य
चित्तैक्य n. (-क्यं) Harmony, agreement, unanimity.<BR> E. चित्त and ऐक्य<BR>identity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=268-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्तोन्नति|चित्तोन्नतिः
चित्तोन्नति f. (-तिः) Pride, &c. see चित्तसमुन्नति.<BR> E. चित्त and उन्नति elevation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=268-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्य|चित्यं|चित्यः
चित्य n. (-त्यं) A monument, or any mark of the site of a funeral pile.<BR>E. चिता a pile, and भावे क्यप् affix.<BR>	 f. (-त्या) A funeral pile.<BR>	 m. (-त्यः)<BR>Fire.<BR> E. चि to collect, ण्यत् affix, and deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=268-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्याधिरोहण
चित्याधिरोहण n. (-णं) Burning with a husband's corpse.<BR> E. चित्या, and<BR>अधिरोहण ascending.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=268-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्यारोहण
चित्यारोहण n. (-णं) Ascending the funeral pile,<BR> E. चिति, and आरोहण<BR>mounting; also चितारोहण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=268-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्र|चित्रं|चित्रः
चित्र r. 10th cl. (चित्रयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To paint, to delineate, to colour with<BR>various colours, &c.<BR>	 2. To wonder.<BR>	 3. To cause wonder or be won-<BR>derful.<BR>	 4. To see a rare or wonderful sight. चु-उभ-सक-सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=268-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्र|चित्रं|चित्रः
चित्र mfn. (-त्रः-त्रा-त्रं)<BR>	 1. Variegated, spotted, speckled.<BR>	 2. Wonderful,<BR>surprising.<BR>	 m. (-त्रः) A name of YAMA.<BR>	 f. (-त्रा)<BR>	 1. A plant: see मूषिक-<BR>पर्णी.<BR>	 2. A kind of cucumber: see गोडुम्बा.<BR>	 3. A plant, commonly<BR>Danti: see दन्तिका.<BR>	 4. A name of SUBHADRA, the sister of JAGAN-<BR>NATHA.<BR>	 5. A star in the virgin's spike.<BR>	 6. A kind of snake.<BR>	 7. A<BR>name of river.<BR>	 8. Illusion, wordly unreality.<BR>	 9. The name of a<BR>nymph of Svarga.<BR>	 10. A form of metre. (त्रं)<BR>	 1. Wonder,<BR>surprise.<BR>	 2. Painting, delineation, writting, &c.<BR>	 3. Sky,<BR>heaven.<BR>	 4. A circular ornament, a sectarial mark on the<BR>forehead.<BR>	 5. White or spotted leprosy.<BR>	 6. Facetious conver-<BR>sation, conundrums, riddles, &c.<BR>	 7. Writing or arrange-<BR>ment of verses in mathematical or other fanciful figures.<BR>	 mn.<BR>(-त्रः-त्रं) Variegated colour.<BR> E. चि to accumulate. Uṇādi affix क्ति, or<BR>चित् the mind, and त्र what preserves, from त्रै with क affix, and the<BR>duplicate त rejected, or चित्र-भावे अच्, चि-ष्ट्रन् वा ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=269-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रक|चित्रकं|चित्रकः
चित्रक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. The Chita or small hunting leopard.<BR>	 2. A painter.<BR>3. The castor oil plant.<BR>	 4. A medical plant, (Plumbago zeylanica.)<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>	 1. A mark made with Sandal, &c. on the forehead.<BR> E. कन्<BR>added to the preceding. चित्रमिव कायति कै-क; चित्र-स्वार्थे क वा ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=269-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रकण्ठ|चित्रकंठ|चित्रकण्ठः
चित्रकण्ठ m. (-ण्ठः) A pigeon.<BR> E. चित्र variegated, speckled, and कण्ठ<BR>throat. चित्रः कण्ठोऽस्य । पारावते । तद्भेदे वनकपोते च (घुघु) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=269-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रकर|चित्रकरः
चित्रकर m. (-रः) A painter.<BR> E. चित्र colouring, and कर who makes. चित्रं<BR>लेख्यभेदं आश्चर्य्यं वा करोति ताच्छील्यादौ ट ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=269-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रकम्बल|चित्रकंबल|चित्रकम्बलः
चित्रकम्बल m. (-लः) A painted cloth used as an elephant's housings, &c.<BR>E. चित्र, and कम्बल a blanket.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=269-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रकर्म्मन्|चित्रकर्मन्
चित्रकर्म्मन् mfn. (-र्म्मा-र्म्मा-र्म्म)<BR>	 1. Astonishing, surprising, working wonders.<BR>2. Painting, variegating.<BR>	 m. (-र्म्मा)<BR>	 1. A magician.<BR>	 2. A painter.<BR>3. A tree, (Dalbergia ougeiniensis.)<BR>	 n. (-र्म्म)<BR>	 1. Painting, or a painting.<BR>2. Magic.<BR> E. चित्र surprising, and कर्म्मन् function. चित्रं कर्म अस्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=269-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रकर्म्मविद्|चित्रकर्मविद्
चित्रकर्म्मविद् m. (-विद्)<BR>	 1. A painter.<BR>	 2. A magician.<BR> E. चित्रकर्म्म, and विद्<BR>who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=269-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रकाय|चित्रकायः
चित्रकाय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. A tiger.<BR>	 2. A Chita.<BR> E. चित्र speckled, and काय body.<BR>चित्रः कायोऽस्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=269-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रकार|चित्रकारः
चित्रकार m. (-रः) A painter.<BR> E. चित्र, and कार who makes. चित्रं करोति<BR>कृ-अण्-उप-स० ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=269-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रकूट|चित्रकूटः
चित्रकूट m. (-टः) The name of a mountain in Bundelkhand, the modern<BR>Compteh, and first habitation of RAMA in his exile.<BR> E. चित्र wonder-<BR>ful, and कूट peak; it is an epithet of many hills. चित्रं कूटं शृङ्गं अस्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=269-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रकृत्
चित्रकृत् m. (-कृत्)<BR>	 1. A painter.<BR>	 2. A tree, (Dalbergia ougieniensis.)<BR> E. चित्र,<BR>and कृत् what makes. चित्रं करोति कृ-क्विप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=269-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रकोल|चित्रकोलः
चित्रकोल m. (-लः) A kind of lizard.<BR> E. चित्र speckled, and क्रोड haunch,<BR>deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=269-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रगत
चित्रगत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Painted, delineated, represented in a picture.<BR>2. Coloured, variegated.<BR> E. चित्र, and गत gone. चित्रे गतः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=269-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रगन्ध|चित्रगंध|चित्रगन्धं
चित्रगन्ध n. (-न्धं) Yellow orpiment.<BR> E. चित्र, and गन्ध smell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=269-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रगुप्त|चित्रगुप्तः
चित्रगुप्त m. (-प्तः)<BR>	 1. A name of YAMA, or rather one of the fourteen<BR>YAMAS.<BR>	 2. YAMA'S registrar, who records the vices and virtues of<BR>mankind.<BR> E. चित्र wonderful, and गुप्त preserving; or चित्र writing,<BR>and गुप्त as before.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=269-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रगो
चित्रगो mfn. (-गौः-गौः-गु) Having a brindled cow.<BR> E. चित्र, and गो a cow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=269-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रजल्प|चित्रजल्पः
चित्रजल्प m. (-ल्पः) Talking incoherently.<BR> E. चित्र, and जल्प prattle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=269-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रतण्डुल|चित्रतण्डुलं
चित्रतण्डुल mfn. subst. (-लः-ला-लं) A medicinal plant, said to possess<BR>anthelmintic virtues: see विडङ्ग.<BR> E. चित्र wonderful, and तण्डुल grain.<BR>चित्रः तण्डुलः अस्य । विडङ्गे ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=269-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रतल
चित्रतल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Painted or variegated on the surface, (as a<BR>floor, &c.)<BR> E. चित्र, and तल below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=269-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रत्वच्
चित्रत्वच् m. (-त्वक्) The birch or Bhurja tree.<BR> E. चित्र, and त्वच् bark. चित्रा<BR>त्वक् यस्य । भूर्जत्वचि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=269-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रदण्डक|चित्रदंडक|चित्रदण्डकः
चित्रदण्डक m. (-कः) The cotton plant.<BR> E. चित्र, and दण्डक stem. चित्रः दण्डः<BR>काण्डो यस्य (ओल्) शूरणे ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=269-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रन्नेत्रा
चित्रन्नेत्रा f. (-त्रा) A small bird, the Maina of the dialects.<BR> E. चित्र varie-<BR>gated, and नेत्र an eye. चित्रं नेत्रं यस्याः । शारिकायाम् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=269-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रपक्ष|चित्रपक्षः
चित्रपक्ष m. (-क्षः) The francoline partridge.<BR> E. चित्र surprising, and पक्ष<BR>a wing. चित्रौ पक्षौ अस्य । तित्तिरिखगे ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=269-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रपत्रिका
चित्रपत्रिका f. (-का) The name of a plant, commonly कपित्थानी.<BR> E. चित्र<BR>wonderful, and पत्र a leaf. चित्रं पत्रं यस्या कप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=269-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रपदक्रम
चित्रपदक्रम adv. ind. or n. (-मं) At a good pace.<BR> E. चित्र, पद a step, and क्रम going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=269-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रपदा
चित्रपदा f. (-दा)<BR>	 1. A creeper, (Cissus pedata.)<BR>	 2. A kind of metre.<BR> E. चित्र<BR>surprising, and पद foot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=269-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रपर्णिका
चित्रपर्णिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. A plant, commonly Chakuliya, (Hemionites<BR>cordifolia.)<BR>	 2. Bengal madar, (Bubia manjith.)<BR> E. कन् added to<BR>चित्रपर्णी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=269-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रपर्णी|चित्रपर्ण्णी
चित्रपर्णी f. (-र्णी)<BR>	 1. Chakuliya.<BR>	 2. M adra; also चित्रपर्णिका.<BR> E. चित्र writing<BR>or painting, and पर्ण leaf; the leaves being as it were painted: see<BR>the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=269-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रपादा
चित्रपादा f. (-दा) The Maina, a small bird so called.<BR> E. चित्र speckled,<BR>and पाद foot. चित्रौ पादौ यस्याः । शारिकायाम् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=269-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रपिच्छक|चित्रपिच्छकः
चित्रपिच्छक m. (-कः) A peacock.<BR> E. चित्र, and पिच्छ the tail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=269-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रपुङ्ख|चित्रपुंख|चित्रपुङ्खः
चित्रपुङ्ख m. (-ङ्खः) An arrow.<BR> E. चित्र wonderful, and पुङ्ख shaft.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=269-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रपृष्ठ|चित्रपृष्ठः
चित्रपृष्ठ m. (-ष्ठः) A sparrow.<BR> E. चित्र speckled, and पृष्ठ the back.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=269-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रफल|चित्रफलः
चित्रफल mf. (-लः-ला) A kind of cucumber, (C. utilatissimus.)<BR>	 m. (-लः) A<BR>kind of fish, (Mystus chitala, HAM.)<BR>	 f. (-ला-ली)<BR>	 1. Egg plant,<BR>(Solanum malongena.)<BR>	 2. Prickly nightshade, (Solanum jacquini.)<BR>3. Gourds of various sorts.<BR>	 4. A fish, (Mystus karpirat, HAM.) E.<BR>चित्र surprising, and फल fruit. चित्रं फलं फलकमिव आकारोऽस्ति अस्य-अच् ।<BR>(चितल्) मत्स्यभेदे ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=269-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रफलक|चित्रफलकः
चित्रफलक m. (-कः) A sort of fish: see the last.<BR> E. चित्र variegated,<BR>and फलक a scale.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=269-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रभानु|चित्रभानुः
चित्रभानु m. (-नुः)<BR>	 1. Fire.<BR>	 2. The sun.<BR>	 3. A name of BHAIRAVA, a form<BR>of ŚIVA.<BR>	 4. The marking-nut plant.<BR>	 5. Gigantic swallow wort. E.<BR>चित्र surprising, and भानु light. चित्राः भानवः यस्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=269-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रमृग|चित्रमृगः
चित्रमृग m. (-गः) The spotted antelope.<BR> E. चित्र, and मृग a deer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=269-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रमेखल|चित्रमेखलः
चित्रमेखल m. (-लः) A peacock.<BR> E. चित्र spotted, and मेखला a girdle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=269-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रयोधिन
चित्रयोधिन m. (-धी)<BR>	 1. A name of ARJUNA.<BR>	 2. A tree, (Pentaptera Arjuna.)<BR>3. Any hero.<BR> E. चित्र, and योधिन् a warrior. चित्रं युध्यति युध-णिनि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=269-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्ररथ|चित्ररथः
चित्ररथ m. (-थः)<BR>	 1. The sun.<BR>	 2. The chief of the Gandharbas or cho-<BR>risters of INDRA'S heaven.<BR> E. चित्र painted, and रथ a car; lord of the<BR>painted car. चित्रः रथः अस्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=269-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रल|चित्रलः
चित्रल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Variegated or spotted.<BR>	 m. (-लः) A variegated<BR>colour.<BR> E. चित्र painting, and ल what produces.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=269-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रलेखा
चित्रलेखा f. (-खा)<BR>	 1. A portrait, a picture.<BR>	 2. An Apsaras and friend<BR>of USHA.<BR>	 3. A form of metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=269-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रलिखित
चित्रलिखित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Represented, delineated, (as in a picture.) E.<BR>चित्र, and लिखित drawn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=269-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रलोचना
चित्रलोचना f. (-ना) The Maina, a small bird so called.<BR> E. चित्र variegated,<BR>and लोचन an eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=269-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रवदाल|चित्रवदालः
चित्रवदाल m. (-लः) A sheat fish, (Silurus pelorius.)<BR> E. चित्र variegated,<BR>and वदाल a sheat fish, the epithet being a pleonasm. चित्रवत् आ समन्तात<BR>अलति आ + अल-अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=269-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रवल्लिक|चित्रवल्लिकः
चित्रवल्लिक m. (-कः) A sheat fish. पाठीन मत्स्ये । (वोइयाल्) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=269-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रवृत्ति
चित्रवृत्ति f. (-त्तिः) Astonishing act or effort.<BR> E. चित्र and वृत्ति practice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=269-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रशिखण्डिज|चित्रशिखंडिज|चित्रशिखण्डिजः
चित्रशिखण्डिज m. (-जः) A name of BṚHASPATI.<BR> E. चित्रशिखण्डी one of<BR>the seven Rhishis, and ज born; being the son of ANGIRAS; also<BR>similar compounds, as चित्रशिखण्डिप्रसुत, &c. चित्रशिखण्डिनः अङ्गिरसः<BR>जायते जन-ड ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=269-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रशिखण्डिन्|चित्रशिखंडिन्
चित्रशिखण्डिन् m. plu. (-ण्डिनः) The seven sages or Ṛṣis, but especially<BR>as represented in the seven principal stars of the great bear; these<BR>sages are MARICHI, ATRI, ANGIRAS, PULAHA, PULASTYA, KRATU,<BR>and VASIṢṬHA.<BR> E. चित्र surprising, शिखण्ड a crest, and इनि affix;<BR>sing. nom. case, शिखण्डिन् (-ण्डी) चित्रः शिखण्डः अस्नि अस्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=269-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रशिखण्डिप्रसुत
चित्रशिखण्डिप्रसुत m. (-तः) VṚHASPATI.<BR> E. चित्रशिखण्डि, and प्रसुत born:<BR>see चित्रशिखण्डिज; there are other similar compounds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=270-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रश्री
चित्रश्री f. (-श्रीः) Great beauty, or the loveliness of variegated colours. E.<BR>चित्र, and श्री beauty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=270-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रसंस्थ
चित्रसंस्थ mfn. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थं) Pictured, painted.<BR> E. चित्र, and संस्थ fixed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=270-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रसर्प|चित्रसर्पः
चित्रसर्प m. (-र्पः) A large speckled snake.<BR> E. चित्र, and सर्प a snake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=270-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रसेन|चित्रसेनः
चित्रसेन m. (-नः) One of the judges or recorders of hell.<BR> E. चित्र, सेना an<BR>army. धृतराष्ट्रपुत्रभेदे, गन्धर्वभेदे च ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=270-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्राक्षी
चित्राक्षी f. (-क्षी) The Maina, (Turdus salica.)<BR> E. चित्र variegated, अक्ष an<BR>eye, fem. affix ङीष्, implying diminution.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=270-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्राङ्ग|चित्रांग|चित्राङ्गं|चित्राङ्गः
चित्राङ्ग mfn. (-ङ्गः-ङ्गी-ङ्गं) Painted, spotted, striped, (the body.)<BR>	 m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>1. A kind of snake.<BR>	 2. A plant, (Plumbago zeylanica.)<BR>	 n. (-ङ्गं)<BR>	 1.<BR>Yellow orpiment.<BR>	 2. Vermilion.<BR>	 f. (-ङ्गी)<BR>	 1. Mader.<BR>	 2. A worm,<BR>(Julus cornifex.)<BR> E. चित्र spotted or painted, &c. अङ्ग the body.<BR>धृतराष्ट्रपुत्रभेदे च ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=270-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्राङ्गद|चित्राङ्गदः
चित्राङ्गद m. (-दः)<BR>	 1. A Prince, a brother of Bichitrabirya father of<BR>DHRITARASHTRA and PĀṆḌU, and son of SANTANU.<BR>	 2. A judge<BR>and recorder in hell.<BR> E. चित्र अङ्ग body, and द who gives. शान्तनोः<BR>सत्यवत्यां जाते पुत्रभेदे ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=270-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्राङ्गदसू
चित्राङ्गदसू f. (-सूः) The mother of VYASA.<BR> E. चित्राङ्गद the name of a prince,<BR>uterine brother of VYASA, and सू mother. सत्यवत्याम् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=270-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्राटीर|चित्राटीरः
चित्राटीर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. The moon.<BR>	 2. The forehead, spotted with the blood<BR>of a goat, slain in the worship of the demon GHANTAKARṆA. E.<BR>चित्र spotted, &c. and अट् to go or be, and ईरच् aff. चित्रां नक्षत्रं अटति<BR>चित्रं वा अटति । अट-वा-ईरच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=270-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रान्न
चित्रान्न n. (-न्नं) Rice dressed with coloured condiments.<BR> E. चित्र and अन्न<BR>food. चित्रौदने । दध्योदनं हविश्चूर्णं मासिं चित्रान्नमेव च ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=270-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रापूप|चित्रापूपः
चित्रापूप m. (-पः) A cake.<BR> E. चित्र speckled, and अपूप a cake, a plum-cake.<BR>नित्यकर्मधारयः । पिष्टकभेदे ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=270-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रायस|चित्रायसं
चित्रायस n. (-सं) Steel,<BR> E. चित्र, and अयस् iron. कर्म० अच् समा । तीक्ष्णलौहे ।<BR>(इस्पात्) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=270-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रिक|चित्रिकः
चित्रिक m. (-कः) The month Chaitra or Cheyt, (March-April.)<BR> E. चित्र<BR>the star, and ठन् affix; also चैत्रिक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=270-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रित
चित्रित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Painted.<BR>	 2. Spotted, striped.<BR>	 3. Variegated. E.<BR>चित्र to paint, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=270-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रिन्
चित्रिन् mfn. (-त्री-त्रिणी-त्रि)<BR>	 1. Variegated.<BR>	 2. Wonderful.<BR>	 f. (-णी) One of<BR>the four kinds in which women are classed.<BR> E. चित्र, and इनि aff. or<BR>चित्र-णिनि वा ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=270-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रीयमाण
चित्रीयमाण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Astonishing, surprising, causing wonder or<BR>astonishment.<BR> E. चित्र with क्यच्, or used as a verb, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=270-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रेश|चित्रेशः
चित्रेश m. (-शः) The moon.<BR> E. चित्र the star, and ईश lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=270-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रोक्ति|चित्रोक्तिः
चित्रोक्ति f. (-क्तिः)<BR>	 1. A voice from heaven, that of an invisible speaker.<BR>2. A marvellous tale.<BR>	 2. Agreeable or eloquent discourse.<BR> E. चि<BR>miraculous, and उक्ति saying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=270-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रौदन|चित्रौदनं|चित्रौदनः
चित्रौदन n. (-नं) Boiled rice coloured with turmeric, &c.<BR> E. चित्र variegated,<BR>and ओदन boiled rice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=270-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिदात्मन्
चिदात्मन् m. (-त्मा) The intellectual soul, spirit.<BR> E. चित्, and आत्मन्<BR>soul.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=270-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिद्रूप|चिद्रूपः
चिद्रूप mfn. (-पः-पा-पं)<BR>	 1. Amiable, good-hearted.<BR>	 2. Wise, intelligent, of<BR>liberal or expansive mind.<BR>	 n. (-पं) The Supreme Being, as indenti-<BR>fiable with intellect or understanding.<BR> E. चित् mind, and रूप form.<BR>चिदेव रुपमस्य । आत्मस्फूर्त्तिमतिउ हृदयालौ च ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=270-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिन्तयत्
चिन्तयत् mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्) Reflecting, considering.<BR> E. चिति to think,<BR>and शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=270-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिन्तनीय
चिन्तनीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) To be considered or thought.<BR>	 2. To be compre-<BR>hended.<BR>	 3. To be meditated on.<BR> E. चिति to reflect, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=270-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिन्तयितव्य
चिन्तयितव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं) To be considered, to be reflected on.<BR> E. चिति<BR>to think, (10th cl.) तव्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=270-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिन्तयित्वा
चिन्तयित्वा ind. Having thought or considered,<BR> E. चिति to think, (10th cl.)<BR>क्त्वा aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=270-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिन्ता|चिंता
चिन्ता f. (-न्ता) Reflexion, consideration, recollection.<BR> E. चिति to reflect,<BR>affixes अङ् and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=270-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिन्ताकुल|चिंताकुल
चिन्ताकुल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Disturbed in thought or distracted by any<BR>idea.<BR> E. चिन्ता, and आकुल agitated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=270-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिन्तापर|चिंतापर
चिन्तापर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Thoughtful, anxious.<BR> E. चिन्ता, and पर engaged in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=270-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिन्तामणि|चिंतामणि|चिन्तामणिः
चिन्तामणि m. (-णिः)<BR>	 1. A fabulous gem, supposed to yield its possessor<BR>whatever may be required.<BR>	 2. A name of BRAHMĀ.<BR>	 3. A Jina or<BR>Jaina saint.<BR> E. चिन्ता, reflexion, and मणि a jewel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=270-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिन्त्यमान
चिन्त्यमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Reflecting, considering, meditating.<BR> E. चिति<BR>to think, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=270-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिन्तावत्|चिन्तावन्त्
चिन्तावत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Thinking, thoughtful.<BR> E. चिन्ता, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=270-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिन्तावेश्मन्|चिंतावेश्मन्
चिन्तावेश्मन् n. (-श्म) Council house or room.<BR> E. चिन्ता reflection, and वेश्मन्<BR>a house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=270-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिन्तिडी|चिंतिडी
चिन्तिडी f. (-डी) The tamarind tree. E. Irregularly changed from तिन्तिडी,<BR>q. v. also चिन्तिडीका, कन् being added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=270-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिन्तित|चिंतित|चिन्तितं
चिन्तित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Thought, considered.<BR>	 2. Reflecting, consider-<BR>ing.<BR>	 n. (-तं) Reflexion: see चिन्ता.<BR> E. चिति to think, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=270-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिन्तिति|चिंतिति|चिंतितिः|चिन्तितिः
चिन्तिति f. (-तिः) Consideration, reflexion.<BR> E. चिति to think, क्तिन् aff.<BR>चिति-क्तिन् वा इट् णिलोपश्च । चिन्तायाम् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=270-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिन्तिया|चिंतिया
चिन्तिया f. (-या) Reflexion, consideration, thinking.<BR> E. चिति, and इय<BR>aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=270-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिन्तोक्ति
चिन्तोक्ति f. (-क्तिः) Midnight cry or alarm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=270-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिन्त्य|चिंत्य
चिन्त्य mfn. (-न्त्यः-न्त्या-न्त्यं)<BR>	 1. To be considered.<BR>	 2. To be appreciated or<BR>conceived.<BR>	 3. To be thought of or meditated upon.<BR> E. चित् to think,<BR>कर्मणि यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=270-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिन्न|चिन्नः
चिन्न m. (-न्नः) A kind of grain, (Panicum miliaceum.) A various reading<BR>of चीन, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=270-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिन्वत्
चिन्वत् mfn. (-न्वन्-न्वन्ती-न्वत्) Gathering, collecting.<BR> E. चि to gather,<BR>(5th cl.) शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=270-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिपिट|चिपिटः
चिपिट mfn. (-टः-टा-टं) Flat-nosed.<BR> E. नि preposition, पिटच् किच्च affix<BR>in this sense, and नि changed to चि.<BR>	 m. (-टः) Rice or grain<BR>flattened.<BR> E. पिट् to flatten, क affix, the derivative reduplicated, and<BR>and ल substituted for the radical; also with कन् added चिपिटक;<BR>also the pen becoming उ, चिपुट.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=270-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिपिटक|चिपिटकः
चिपिटक m. (-कः) See the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=270-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिपुट|चिपुटः
चिपुट m. (-टः) See चिपिट.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=270-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिप्य
चिप्य n. (-प्यं) A whitlow. नखमांसमधिष्ठाय वातं पित्तं च देहिनाम् । करोति दाह-<BR>पाकौ च तं व्याधिं चिप्यमादिशेत् ॥ इत्युक्ते नखरोगभेदे ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=270-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिमि|चिमिः
चिमि m. (-मिः)<BR>	 1. A parrot.<BR>	 2. A plant, from the fibres of which coarse<BR>cloth and rope are made: see पट्ट.<BR> E. चि imitative sound, and मि to<BR>utter, affix क्विप्, with कन् added चिमिक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=270-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिमिक|चिमिकः
चिमिक m. (-कः) A parrot: see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=270-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिर|चिरं
चिर n. (-रं)<BR> E. चि-रक् । दीर्घकाले, तद्वर्त्तिनि पदार्थे । त्रि० लघ्वादौ त्रि कले गणे ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=270-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिरकारिन्
चिरकारिन् mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि) Dilatory, tedious, slow.<BR> E. चिर, and कारिन्<BR>who acts. चिरेण करोति कृ-णिनि । दीर्घसूत्रे, गौतमपुत्रभेदे च ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=270-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिरकाल|चिरकालः
चिरकाल n. (-लं) A long period.<BR> E. चिर long, and काल time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=270-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिरकालपालित
चिरकालपालित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Protected for a long time.<BR> E. चिरकाल, and<BR>पालित nourished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=270-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिकालोपार्ज्जित
चिकालोपार्ज्जित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Accumulated slowly or after a long time.<BR>E. चिरकाल, and उपार्ज्जित gained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=270-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिरक्रिय|चिरक्रियः
चिरक्रिय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Dilatory, tedious, slow.<BR> E. चिर long, and क्रिया<BR>business.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=270-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिरगत
चिरगत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Long absent, a long time gone.<BR> E. चिर, and गत<BR>gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=270-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिरचेष्टित
चिरचेष्टित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Long sought for, of rare occurence.<BR> E. चिर,<BR>and चेष्टित sought.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=270-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिरजीवक|चिरजीवकः
चिरजीवक m. (-कः) A tree: see जीवक<BR> E. चिर long, and जीवक lived.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=270-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिरचीविन्
चिरचीविन् mfn. (-वी-विनी-वि) Long-lived.<BR>	 m. (-वी)<BR>	 1. A name of VIṢṆU.<BR>2. A crow.<BR>	 3. The Jivaka: see the preceding.<BR>	 4. An epithet applied<BR>especially to eight chiefs or saints, viz. MARKANDEYA, ASWATTHAMA,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=271-a" target="_blank">Page271-a+ 60</a>]<BR>BALI, VYASA, HANUMANA, VIBHISHANA, KRIPA, and PARASURAMA.<BR>E. चिर for चिरम् long, and जीविन् living or lived; also चिरञ्जीविन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=270-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिरञ्जीविन्|चिरंजीविन्
चिरञ्जीविन् mfn. (-वी-विनी-वि) Long-lived.<BR>	 m. (-वी)<BR>	 1. A crow.<BR>	 2. VIṢṆU.<BR>E. See the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=271-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिरण्डी
चिरण्डी f. (-ण्डी)<BR>	 1. A woman married or single, who continues to reside<BR>after maturity in her father's house.<BR>	 2. A young woman.<BR> E. चिरम्<BR>long or late, and अट् to go, (from home,) affix अच् and deriv. irr.;<BR>also चिरिण्टी. चिरेण अटति पितृगृहात् भर्तृ गेहम् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=271-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिरतिक्त|चिरतिक्तः
चिरतिक्त m. (-क्तः) A kind of gentian, (Gentiana cherayta.)<BR> E. चिर long,<BR>and तिक्त bitter. चिरः तिक्तः रसो यत्र (चिराता) मूनिम्बे ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=271-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिरत्न|चिरत्नः
चिरत्न mfn. (-त्नः-त्नी-त्नं) Old, ancient, what has been or lasted long. E.<BR>चिर long, and त्न aff. चिरन्तने, पुराणे ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=271-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिरदिवसं
चिरदिवसं ind. For a long time.<BR> E. चिर. and दिवस a day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=271-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिरनिविष्ट
चिरनिविष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं) Long rested, long abided.<BR> E. चिर, and निविष्ट<BR>rested.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=271-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिरन्तन|चिरंतन|चिरन्तनः
चिरन्तन mfn. (-नः-नी-नं) Old, ancient, antiquated, long lasting.<BR> E. चिरम्<BR>long, and ट्युल् affix, with तुट् augment. चिरं भवार्थे ट्युल् तुट् च ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=271-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिरम्
चिरम् ind. A long time.<BR> E. चिर् to injure, and क affix: वा रमुक् । this<BR>word, and others evidently derived from it, are now considered as<BR>particles, and have accordingly appropriate, though strained ety-<BR>mologies; the derivatives however corresponding with the inflec-<BR>tions of the singular number of nouns masculine or neuter, it may<BR>have been originally an imperfect noun of the 1st declension, thus;<BR>nom. चिरः or चिरं acc. चिरं 1st abl. चिरेण dat. चिराय, 2nd abl. चिरात्,<BR>gen. चिरस्य, 3rd abl. चिरे; see these words severally.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=271-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिरप्रवासिन्
चिरप्रवासिन् mfn. (-सी-सिनी-सि) Dwelling a long time abroad.<BR> E. चिर and<BR>प्रवासिन् who is away from home.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=271-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिरमित्र
चिरमित्र n. (-त्रं) An old friend.<BR> E. चिर and मित्र a friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=271-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिरमेहिन्
चिरमेहिन् m. (-ही) An ass.<BR> E. चिर a long time, and मिह् to sprinkle or<BR>urine, affix णिनि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=271-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिरम्भण|चिरम्भणः
चिरम्भण m. (-णः) A kite.<BR> E. चि imitative cry, and रभि to commence,<BR>affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=271-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिररात्र|चिररात्रं
चिररात्र n. (-त्रं) A period of very many nights, a long time<BR> E. चिर long,<BR>and रात्र a night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=271-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिररात्राय
चिररात्राय ind. A long time<BR> E. चिररात्र as above, and अय् to go, affix अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=271-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिरलब्ध
चिरलब्ध mfn. (-ब्धः-ब्धा-ब्धं) Obtained after a long time, (as a son in old<BR>age.)<BR> E. चिर, and लब्ध gained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=271-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिरविल्व|चिरविल्वः
चिरविल्व m. (-ल्वः) The name of a plant: see करञ्ज.<BR> E. चिर a long time, विल<BR>to divide, and व affix; also चिरिविल्व. चिरं विलति विलभेदने वा । करञ्जवृक्षे ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=271-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिरसूता
चिरसूता f. (-ता) A cow that has borne many calves.<BR> E. चिर for a long<BR>time, and सूता prolific; also चिरसूतिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=271-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिरसेवक|चिरसेवकः
चिरसेवक m. (-कः) An old servant.<BR> E. चिर, and सेवक who serves.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=271-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिरस्थ
चिरस्थ mfn. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थं) Long continuing, enduring, lasting.<BR> E. चिर,<BR>and स्थ what is; also चिरस्थायिन्. चिरं तिष्ठति स्था-क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=271-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिरस्थायिन्
चिरस्थायिन् mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि) Of long continuance.<BR> E. चिर for चिर् and<BR>स्थायिन् what stays.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=271-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिरस्थित
चिरस्थित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Long enduring, lasting or remaining for a<BR>long time.<BR>	 2. Left behind for a long time.<BR> E. चिर, and स्थित stayed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=271-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिरस्य
चिरस्य ind. A long time.<BR> E. चिर a long time, अस् to be, affix ण्यत्: see<BR>चिरम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=271-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिराटिका
चिराटिका f. (-का) Hogweed, the white sort.<BR> E. चिरमटति अट-ण्वुल् कापि<BR>अत इत्त्वम् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=271-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिरातिक्त|चिरातिक्तः
चिरातिक्त m. (-क्तः) A sort of gentian: see चिरतिक्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=271-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिरात्
चिरात् m. (-रात्) A name of GARUḌA. ind. A long time.<BR> E. चिर for a long<BR>time, and अद् who eats, from अद् with क्विप् affix or चिर and आजि aff.<BR>चिरमतति अत-क्विप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=271-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिराय
चिराय ind. A long time.<BR> E. चिर a long time and अय् to go, affix अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=271-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिरायुस्
चिरायुस् mfn. (-युः-युः-यु) Long-lived.<BR>	 m. (-युः) A deity, a divinity.<BR> E. चिर<BR>long, and आयुस् life. चिरमायुर्यस्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=271-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिरारोध|चिरारोधः
चिरारोध m. (-धः) Blockade.<BR> E. चिर and आरोध obstruction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=271-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिराश्रित
चिराश्रित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Long maintained or protected.<BR> E. चिर, and<BR>आश्रित supported.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=271-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिरि|चिरिः
चिरि r. 5th cl. (चिरिणोति) To hurt, to injure, to wound or kill. स्वा-प<BR>सक-सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=271-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिरि|चिरिः
चिरि m. (-रिः) A parrot.<BR> E. चि imitative cry, and रा to utter, affix रिक्;<BR>or चि-वा-रिक् । शुकखगे ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=271-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिरिण्ठी
चिरिण्ठी f. (-ण्ठी)<BR>	 1. A woman staying in her father's house.<BR>	 2. A young<BR>woman. E. Irregularly derived from चिरि to hurt: see चिरण्टी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=271-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिरिविल्व|चिरिविल्वः
चिरिविल्व m. (-ल्वः) A tree: see चिरविल्व<BR> E. चिरि a parrot, and विल् to<BR>break, affix व.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=271-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिरु|चिरुः
चिरु n. (-रु) The shoulder joint.<BR> E. चिर् to hurt, affix उ; or चीयते-वा-<BR>रुक् । बाहुसन्धौ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=271-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिरे
चिरे ind. A long time: see चिरम्. चिरयति इ-विच् । दीर्घकाले ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=271-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिरेण
चिरेण ind. A long time: see चिरम्. चिर-अव्य-श वा एनप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=271-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिरोज्झित
चिरोज्झित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Long since abandoned or left.<BR> E. चिर, and<BR>उज्झित abandoned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=271-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिर्भिटी
चिर्भिटी f. (-टी) A kind of cucumber, (C. utilatissimus.) चिरेण भटति<BR>भट-अच् । गौ-ङीष् । कर्कट्याम् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=271-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिल
चिल r. 6th cl. (चिलति) To put on clothes. तु-प-अक सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=271-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिलमीलिका
चिलमीलिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. A necklace.<BR>	 2. A firefly.<BR>	 3. Lightning.<BR> E. चिर a<BR>long time, and र changed to ल, मील् to twinkle or glister, with ण्वुल्<BR>affix; and the fem. form. चिरं मिलति मीलति वा ण्वुल् रस्य लः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=271-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिलिचिम|चिलिचिमः
चिलिचिम m. (-मः)<BR>	 1. A kind of sprat, (Clupea cultrata.)<BR>	 2. A<BR>kind of prawn, (according to some.)<BR> E. चिल् to sport or play,<BR>affix कि, चिलि and reiterated, चिलिचि sport, pastime, मा to mete,<BR>to find, क affix, finding sport in marshy places amongst reeds, &c.;<BR>this word has various forms, being read as above, and चिलिचीम,<BR>चिलिमीनक, चिलीचिम, चिलिचिम, चिलीम, &c. चिल-इन् चिलिं वासं चिनोति<BR>चि-मक् [वेलेगुडगुडिया] मत्स्यभेदे ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=271-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिल्ल|चिल्लः
चिल्ल r. 1st cl. (-चिल्लति)<BR>	 1. To be loose, to be slack or flaccid.<BR>	 2. To in-<BR>dicate one's meaning.<BR>	 3. To act wantonly. भ्वा-प-अक-सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=271-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिल्ल|चिल्लः
चिल्ल mfn. (-ल्लः-ल्ली-ल्लं) Blear-eyed.<BR>	 m. (-ल्लः)<BR>	 1. The Bengal kite, (Falco<BR>cheela, Lath.)<BR>	 2. A bleared or sore eye.<BR>	 f. (-ल्ली)<BR>	 1. A potherb, said<BR>to be a small kind of Chenopodium: see वास्तुक.<BR>	 2. A cricket.<BR> E. चिल्ल्<BR>to be flaccid or loose, affix अच्ः see चुल्ल, or नि preposition, लच् in<BR>the second sense, and चिल् substituted for नि. or चिल्ल् अच् । पक्षिभेदे ।<BR>(चिल्) क्लिन्ने त्रि० ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=271-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिल्लका
चिल्लका f. (-का) A cricket: see चीलिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=271-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिल्लभक्ष्या
चिल्लभक्ष्या f. (-क्ष्या) A vegetable perfume: see हट्टविलासिनी.<BR> E. चिल्ल a kite,<BR>and भक्ष्य eatable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=271-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिल्लाभ|चिल्लाभः
चिल्लाभ m. (-भः) A petty thief, a shoplifter, a pick-pocket, &c.<BR> E. चिल्ल<BR>kite, and आभ resembling, from भा to shine, with आङ् prefix and<BR>ड affix, pouncing on his prize like a kite on its prey.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=271-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिवि|चिविः
चिवि m. (-विः) The chin.<BR> E. चीव् to take, कि affix, and the radical vowel<BR>shortened: see चिवु; or चीव्-इन् पृषो० । चिवुके ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=271-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिविट|चिविटः
चिविट m. (-टः) Flattened grain. A various reading of चिपिट, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=271-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिवु|चिवुः
चिवु m. (-वुः) The chin: see the next. चीव संवरणे उ-पृषो० ह्रस्वः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=271-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिवुक|चिवुकं|चिवुकः
चिवुक n. (-कं) The chin.<BR> E. चीव् to take or cover, कु affix, and कन् added;<BR>also चिवु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=271-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिह्न|चिह्नं
चिह्न Sautra root. 10th cl. (चिह्नयति-ते) To mark, to spot, to stamp. E.<BR>चु-उभ-सक-सेट् । सौत्रोऽयं धातुः इति केचित् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=271-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिह्न|चिह्नं
चिह्न n. (-ह्नं)<BR>	 1. A mark of any kind, a spot, stain, sign, symbol, &c.<BR>	 2.<BR>A banner, a standard.<BR>	 3. A symptom.<BR> E. च् to pound, affix नक्, and<BR>the radical vowel changed to इ, or चिह्न to mark, क aff. or चिह्न-अच्<BR>चह-न उपधाया इत्त्वम् वा ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=271-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिह्नकारिन्
चिह्नकारिन् mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>	 1. Spotting, marking.<BR>	 2. Hideous, frightful.<BR>3. Striking, killing.<BR> E. चिह्न, and कारिन् who or what makes. चिह्नं<BR>करोति कृ-णिनि । चिह्नकर्त्तरि, घोरदर्शने च ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=271-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिह्नधारिणी
चिह्नधारिणी f. (-णी) A plant, (Echites frutescens.)<BR> E. चिह्न a mark, and<BR>धारिणी possessing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=271-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिह्नित|चिह्नितः
चिह्नित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Marked, spotted, stained, stamped.<BR>	 2. Desig-<BR>nated.<BR>	 3. Known.<BR> E. चिह्न् to mark, and कर्मणि क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=272-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चीक
चीक r. 1st and 10th cls. (चीकति चीकयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To be patient, to suffer<BR>or endure.<BR>	 2. To be impatient.<BR>	 3. To touch.<BR> E. मर्षणे वा चु-उ पक्षे<BR>भ्वा-प-सक-सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=272-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चीन|चीनं|चीनः
चीन m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. A kind of deer.<BR>	 2. A sort of panic, (Panicum<BR>miliaceum.)<BR>	 3. A country, China.<BR>	 4. A sort of cloth 5. A thread.<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. A banner, (perhaps made of deer skin.)<BR>	 2. Lead.<BR> E. चि to<BR>collect, नक् affix, and the deriv. irr. पृषो दीर्घः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=272-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चीनक|चीनकः
चीनक m. (-कः) A sort of panic, (P. miliaceum.)<BR> E. कन् added to the<BR>preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=272-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चीनकर्पूर|चीनकर्पूरः|चीनकर्प्पूर
चीनकर्पूर m. (-रः) Camphor.<BR> E. चीन, and कर्पूर the same; the best is from<BR>China.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=272-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चीनज|चीनजं
चीनज n. (-जं) Steel.<BR> E. चीन, and ज produced. चीने जायते जः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=272-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चीनपिष्ट|चीनपिष्टं
चीनपिष्ट m. (-ष्टः)<BR>	 1. Minium or red-lead.<BR> E. चीन China, and पिष्ट cake;<BR>brought in lumps from the hills on the north-west of Bengal, and<BR>between it and China. चीनस्य सीसकस्य पिष्टं चूर्णं (चीनेर सिन्दुर) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=272-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चीनवङ्ग|चीनवंग|चीनवङ्गं
चीनवङ्ग n. (-ङ्गं) Lead, or more probably tutenague.<BR> E. चीन and वङ्ग zinc.<BR>सीसके ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=272-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चीनांशुक
चीनांशुक n. (-कं) China cloth, silk.<BR> E. चीन, and अंशुक cloth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=272-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चीब्
चीब् (ऋ) चीबृ r. 1st 10 cl. (चीवति-ते) (चीवयति-ते) To take: see चीव. भ्वा-उभ-सक-सेट् चु ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=272-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चीभ
चीभ (ऋ) चीभृ r. 1st cl. (चीभते) To coax, to commend, to flatter.<BR>	 2. To<BR>appropriate praise to boast, &c. some authorities substitute चीभृ<BR>for this root. भ्वा-आ-सक-सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=272-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चीय
चीय (ऋ) चीयृ r. 1st cl. (चीयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To take to receive.<BR>	 2. To wear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=272-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चीर|चीरं
चीर n. (-रं)<BR>	 1. Cloth, clothes.<BR>	 2. A rag, old and torn cloth.<BR>	 3. Bark,<BR>rind.<BR>	 4. A crest.<BR>	 5. A kind of garland.<BR>	 6. Lead.<BR>	 7. A line, a stroke.<BR>8. Writing.<BR>	 9. The dress of a Bouddha priest.<BR>	 f. (-री)<BR>	 1. A cricket.<BR>2. The ends or hem of a garment.<BR> E. चि to collect, Uṇādi affix क्रन्<BR>दीर्घश्च deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=272-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चीरवासस्
चीरवासस् mfn. (-साः-साः-सः) Clothed in tatters.<BR> E. चीर and वासस्<BR>vesture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=272-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चीरि|चीरिः
चीरि f. (-रिः) An eye cloth, a veil covering the eyes.<BR> E. चिर to hurt, and<BR>क्रि affix; the radical vowel lengthened. चि-वा क्रि दीर्घश्च ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=272-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चीरिका
चीरिका f. (-का) A cricket.<BR> E. कन् added to चीरी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=272-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चीर्ण|चीर्णं|चीर्ण्ण
चीर्ण mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-र्णं)<BR>	 1. Conversant, learned.<BR>	 2. Split, divided.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=272-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चीर्णपर्ण|चीर्णपर्णः|चीर्ण्णपर्ण्ण
चीर्णपर्ण m. (-र्णः)<BR>	 1. The Nimb: see निम्ब.<BR>	 2. The date tree, (Elate syl-<BR>vestris.)<BR> E. चीर्ण divided, and पर्ण a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=272-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चीलिका
चीलिका f. (-का) A cricked.<BR> E. चीरी imitative cry, and क who utters;<BR>also चिल्लका and झिल्लका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=272-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चीव
चीव r. 10th cl. (चीवयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To shine.<BR>	 2. To speak. (ऋ) चीवृ r. 1st cl.<BR>(चीवति-ते)<BR>	 1. To take.<BR>	 2. To wear. चु-उभ-सक-सेट् पक्षे भ्वादि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=272-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चीवर|चीवरं
चीवर n. (-रं) The tattered dress of a Bauddha mendicant, or of any<BR>mendicant.<BR> E. चि to collect, &c. and वरच् Uṇādi aff. चीव-अच् वा ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=272-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चीवरिन्
चीवरिन् m. (-री) A Bauddha or Jaina mendicant.<BR> E. चीवर a beggar's<BR>dress, and इनि aff. चीवरमस्ति अस्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=272-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुक्क|चुक्कं
चुक्क r. 10th cl. (चुक्कयति-ते) To inflict or suffer pain.<BR> E. चु-उभ-सक-सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=272-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुक्कार|चुक्कारः
चुक्कार m. (-रः) The roaring of a lion.<BR> E. चक्क pain, derived from चुक्व with<BR>भावे अच् affix, ऋ in the causal, to occasion, affix अच्; or चुक्कं पीड्न-<BR>माराति सम्यक् ददाति आ + रा-क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=272-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुक्र|चुक्रं|चुक्रः
चुक्र m. (-क्रः)<BR>	 1. Sorrel.<BR>	 2. Sourness.<BR>	 n. (-क्रं)<BR>	 1. Acid seasoning.<BR>	 2. Vine-<BR>gar made by the acetous fermentation of grain.<BR>	 f. (-का or -क्री)<BR>	 1.<BR>Indian sorrel, (Rumex vesicarius.)<BR>	 2. Hogplum.<BR>	 3. The tamarind.<BR>E. चक् to satisfy, Uṇādi affix रक्, and the radical vowel changed to<BR>उ; also with कन् चुक्रक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=272-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुक्रिका
चुक्रिका f. (-का) Indian sorrel, (Rumex vesicarius.)<BR> E. क्रन् added to the<BR>preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=272-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुचि|चुचिः
चुचि m. (-चिः) The female breast or bosom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=272-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुचुक|चुचुकं|चुचुकः
चुचुक mn. (-कः-कं) A nipple.<BR> E. चुष् to suck, and क affix, deriv. irr. or<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=272-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुचु
चुचु imitative sound, (such as a child makes in sucking,) and क<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=272-b" target="_blank">Page272-b+ 60</a>]<BR>what sounds; also चुचूक and चूचुक; चुचु इति अव्यक्तशब्दं कायति पीयमानः<BR>कै-क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=272-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुचू
चुचू m. (-चूः) A potherb, (Marsilea dentata, Rox.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=272-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुच्य
चुच्य (ई) चुच्यी r. 1st cl. (चुच्यति)<BR>	 1. To distil, to drop.<BR>	 2. To bathe. भ्वा-पर-सक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=272-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुञ्चु|चुंचु|चुञ्चुः
चुञ्चु m. (-ञ्चुः)<BR>	 1. The musk rat or shrew.<BR>	 2. A mixed caste, born of a<BR>Brahman father by a Vaideha female.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=272-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुञ्चुरी|चुंचुरी
चुञ्चुरी f. (-री) A game, a kind of hazard played with tamarind seeds in<BR>place of dice.<BR> E. चुञ्च substituted for चिञ्चा the tamarind, and र from<BR>रा to get or give, affixes ड and ङीष्, or with ल affix चुञ्चुली.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=272-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुट
चुट r. 1st cl. (चोटति) and 10th cl. (चोटयति-ते) To wane, to become small,<BR>low or shallow. r. 6th and 10th cls. (चुटति चोटयति-ते) To cut, to<BR>pierce or divide; (इ) चुटि r. 1st cl. (चुटति) To become low or shallow.<BR>r. 1st and 10th cls. (चुण्टति चुण्टयति-ते) To cut, &c.; also चुट्ट and चुड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=272-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुट्ट
चुट्ट r. 10th cl. (चुट्टयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To become small, low or shallow, as a river,<BR>&c.<BR>	 2. To collect. चु-उभ-अक-सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=272-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुड
चुड (इ) चुडि r. 1st cl. (चुण्डति) To become small, low or shallow. r. 10th<BR>cl. (चुण्डयति-ते) To cut, to pierce of divide. भ्वा-प-अक-सेट् । पक्षे चुरा-<BR>उभ-सक-सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=272-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुड्ड
चुड्ड r. 1st cl. (चुड्डति)<BR>	 1. To hint one's meaning.<BR>	 2. To dally, to wanton,<BR>to coquet, &c.<BR>	 3. To act. भ्वा-पर-सक-सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=272-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुण
चुण r. 6th cl. (चुणति) To cut, to pierce or divide. तु-पर-सक-सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=272-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुण्टा|चुंटा
चुण्टा f. (-ण्टा) A small well or reservoir near a well.<BR> E. चुडि to be low or<BR>shallow, affixes अङ् and टाप्; also चुण्डी, the fem. affix being ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=272-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुण्टी
चुण्टी f. (-ण्टी) A small well: see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=272-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुत|चुतः
चुत (इर) चुतिर r. 1st cl. (चोतति) To wet, to be wet or moist. भ्वा-प-अक-सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=272-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुत|चुतः
चुत m. (-तः) The anus.<BR> E. चुत् to be moist, affix क; also च्युत and चुति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=272-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुति|चुतिः
चुति f. (-तिः) The anus.<BR> E. चुत् to be wet. क्तिन् affix; also च्युति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=272-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुद
चुद r. 10th cl. (चोदयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To send, to direct, to throw or cast.<BR>	 2.<BR>To ask or interrogate. (इर, इ) इर चुदि r. 1st cl. (चुन्दति-ते) To<BR>sharpen. चु-उभ-सक-सेट् । पक्षे भ्वादि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=272-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुन्दी|चुंदी
चुन्दी f. (-न्दी) A procuress, a bawd.<BR> E. चुद् to inquire, affixes की and<BR>ङीष्, and नुम् inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=272-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुप
चुप r. 1st cl. (चोपति) To move slowly, to creep or steal along. भ्वा-प-सक-सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=272-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुब
चुब (इ) चुबि r. 1st cl. (चुम्बति) or implying reciprocity, To kiss<BR>r. 10th cl. (चुम्बयति-ते) To kill or hurt. भ्वा-प-सक-सेट् । पक्षे चुरादि उभ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=272-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुब्र|चुब्रं
चुब्र n. (-ब्रं) The face.<BR> E. चुब् to kiss, इन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=272-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुम्बक|चुंबक|चुंबकः|चुम्बकः
चुम्बक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A kisser, a lecher.<BR>	 2. A rogue, a cheat.<BR>	 3. The load-<BR>stone.<BR>	 4. A general scholar, one who knows parts in a variety of<BR>books.<BR>	 5. The upper part or middle of a balance.<BR> E. चुबि to kiss,<BR>affix ण्वुल्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=272-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुम्बत्
चुम्बत् mfn. (-म्बन्-म्बन्ती-म्बत्) Kissing.<BR> E. चुवि to kiss, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=272-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुम्बन|चुंबन|चुंबनं|चुम्बनं
चुम्बन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Kissing.<BR>	 2. A kiss.<BR> E. चुवि to kiss, affix भावे ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=272-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुम्बनदान
चुम्बनदान n. (-नं) Kissing.<BR> E. चुम्बन, and दान giving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=272-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुम्बित|चुंबित
चुम्बित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Kissed.<BR> E. चुबि to kiss, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=272-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुम्बितवत्
चुम्बितवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Kissing.<BR> E. चुबि, and क्तवतु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=272-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुर
चुर r. 10th cl. (चोरयति-ते) To steal, to rob: according to some it is<BR>also r. 1st cl. (चोरति) This root gives its name to the 10th class,<BR>which is thence called चुरादिः (ई) चुरी r. 4th cl. (चूर्य्यते) To burn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=272-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुरा
चुरा f. (-रा) Theft, stealing.<BR> E. चुर् to steal, affix क, fem. affix टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=272-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुरी
चुरी f. (-री) A small well.<BR> E. चुटि to be shallow, affixes क and ङीष्; ट्<BR>changed to र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=272-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुल
चुल r. 10th cl. (चोलयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To rise, to increase.<BR>	 2. To raise, to ele-<BR>vate.<BR>	 3. To dip or dive into. चु-उभ-सक-सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=272-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुलुक|चुलुकं|चुलुकः
चुलुक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. Mud, mire.<BR>	 2. A small vessel or pot, a gallipot, &c.<BR>3. The hand hollowed to hold water.<BR>	 n. (-कं) Water in which pulse<BR>has been steeped.<BR> E. चुल् to dip into, aff. उकक्ः see चलुक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=272-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुलुकिन्
चुलुकिन् m. (-की) A porpoise.<BR> E. चुलुक mud, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=272-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुलुम्प|चुलुंप|चुलुंपः|चुलुम्पः
चुलुम्प r. 1st cl. (चुलुम्पति)<BR>	 1. To cut.<BR>	 2. To disappear, to be lost. भ्वा-प-अक-सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=272-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुलुम्प|चुलुंप|चुलुंपः|चुलुम्पः
चुलुम्प m. (-म्प्रः) Fondling or nursing children, &c.<BR>	 f. (-म्पा) A she goat.<BR>E. चुलुम्प to cut, भावे घञ् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=272-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुलुम्पिन्
चुलुम्पिन् m. (-म्पी) The gangetic porpoise.<BR> E. चुलुम्प to cut, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=273-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुल्ल|चुल्लः
चुल्ल r. 1st cl. (चुल्लति)<BR>	 1. To manifest one's meaning.<BR>	 2. To dally, to<BR>wanton or coquet. भ्वा-प-अक-सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=273-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुल्ल|चुल्लः
चुल्ल mfn. (-ल्लः-ल्ला-ल्लं) Blear-eyed.<BR>	 m. (-ल्लः) A blear eye.<BR>	 f. (-ल्ली)<BR>	 1. A<BR>chimney, a fire place.<BR>	 2. A funeral pile.<BR> E. चुल्ल् to indicate mean-<BR>ing, affix इन् वा ङीप्; or नि proposition, लच् affix implying mois-<BR>ture of the eyes, and चुल् substituted for नि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=273-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुल्लक|चुल्लकः
चुल्लक m. (-कः) The palm of the hand hollowed as if to hold water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=273-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुल्लकी
चुल्लकी f. (-की)<BR>	 1. A porpoise.<BR>	 2. A water pot.<BR>	 3. The opposite bank of<BR>a river.<BR> E. चुल्ल् to dally, (in the water.) ण्वुल् affix, and fem. affix ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=273-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुल्लि|चुल्लिः
चुल्लि f. (-ल्लिः) A fire place, a chimney.<BR> E. चुल्ल् to manifest meaning, and<BR>इन् aff. वा ङीप् । चुल--वा-निक् वा ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=273-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुस्त|चुस्तं|चुस्तः
चुस्त n. (-स्तं)<BR>	 1. Friend meat, 2. Chaff, rind.<BR> E. चूष् to suck, क्त affix,<BR>deriv. irr. चु-क्त वा सुट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=273-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूचुक|चूचुकं
चूचुक mn. (-कः-कं) A nipple.<BR> E. चूष् to suck, and deriv. irr.; or चूचु<BR>imitative sound, (in sucking) and क what makes; also चुचुक, &c.<BR>चूष्यते चूष वा उकः पृषो-षस्य च । कुचाग्रे ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=273-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूडक|चूडकः
चूडक m. (-कः) A well,<BR> E. चुड् to become shallow, affix कन् and the<BR>vowel lengthened. चूडा अस्ति अस्य वा कन् । कूपे ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=273-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूडा
चूडा f. (-डा)<BR>	 1. A single lock of hair left on the crown of the head at<BR>the ceremony of tonsure.<BR>	 2. A peacock's crest.<BR>	 3. Any crest, plume,<BR>diadem, &c.<BR>	 4. The head.<BR>	 5. Top, summit.<BR>	 6. An upper house, a<BR>room on the top of a house, &c.<BR>	 7. A kind of bracelet.<BR>	 8. A small<BR>well.<BR>	 9. Tonsure; more commonly चूडाकरणं.<BR> E. चुल् to elevate, अङ्<BR>and टाप् affixes, ल changed to ड, and the vowel lengthened. चूल्<BR>अङ् चुल-समुच्छ्रये अङ् डस्य लः निः दीर्घः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=273-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूडाकरण|चूडाकरणं
चूडाकरण n. (-णं) Shaving the head all but one lock, considered as a<BR>religious, and purificatory rite; it should be performed in the<BR>first or third year.<BR> E. चुडा, and करण making.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=273-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूडाकर्म्मन्|चूडाकर्मन्
चूडाकर्म्मन् n. (-र्म्म) The rite of tonsure: see the last.<BR> E. चूडा, and कर्म्म<BR>act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=273-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूडामणि|चूडामणिः
चूडामणि m. (-णिः)<BR>	 1. A jewel worn in a crest or a diadem.<BR>	 2. The<BR>Gunja, (Abrus precatorius.)<BR> E. चूडा a crest, and मणि a jewel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=273-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूडाल|चूडालं
चूडाल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Crested, having a lock of hair on the crown of<BR>the head, &c.<BR>	 f. (-ला) A kind of grass, (Kyllinga monocephala.)<BR>n. (-लं) The head.<BR> E. चूडा a crest, and ल what has, from ला with ड<BR>affix, or लच् poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=273-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूडालक्षण
चूडालक्षण n. (-णं) Tonsure.<BR> E. चूडा, and लक्षण mark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=273-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूडावत्|चूडावन्त्
चूडावत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Crested, having a lock of hair, &c. on the<BR>top of the head.<BR> E. चूडा a crest, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=273-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूण
चूण r. 10th cl. (चूणयति-ते) To contract, to close or shrink.<BR> E. चु-उभ-सक-<BR>सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=273-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूत|चूतः
चूत m. (-तः)<BR>	 1. The mango, (Manjifera Indica.)<BR>	 2. The anus.<BR> E. चूष् to<BR>drink, affix क्त, deriv. irr. or चुत् to be moist, affix. अच् । चूष-क्त चोतति<BR>रसम्, चुत अच् वा ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=273-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूतक|चूतकः
चूतक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. The mango.<BR>	 2. A small or shallow well.<BR> E. कन् added<BR>to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=273-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूति|चूतिः
चूति f. (तिः) The anus: see चुति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=273-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूर
चूर (इ) चूरी r. 1st. cl. (चूर्य्यते) To burn.<BR> E. दिवा-आत्म-सक-सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=273-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूर्ण|चूर्णं|चूर्णः|चूर्ण्ण
चूर्ण r. 1st cl. (चूर्णयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To contract, to shrink, to close as an eye,<BR>to wink.<BR>	 2. Throw, to send or direct.<BR>	 3. To grind or pound. E.<BR>चुरा-उभ-सक-सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=273-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूर्ण|चूर्णं|चूर्णः|चूर्ण्ण
चूर्ण mn. (-र्णः-र्णं)<BR>	 1. Powder, any pulverulent or minute division of<BR>substance.<BR>	 2. Chalk, lime.<BR>	 3. Aromatic powder, pounded Sandal,<BR>&c.<BR>	 4. Pounded camphor.<BR>	 f. (-र्णी)<BR>	 1. A Cowri, the shell used as a<BR>coin.<BR>	 2. Selection of an unanswerable argument.<BR>	 3. A river in<BR>Bengal.<BR>	 4. The red powder scattered at the Holi festival.<BR>	 5. Dust:<BR>see चूर्णि<BR> E. चूर्ण् to pound, &c. affix. कर्मणि अच् । भावे अच् पेषणे ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=273-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूर्णक|चूर्णकं|चूर्णकः
चूर्णक m. (-कः) Grain fried and pounded.<BR>	 n. (-कं) Expounding in prose<BR>the purport of a foregoing verse, an order or interpretation in<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=273-b" target="_blank">Page273-b+ 60</a>]<BR>prose not abounding in compound words.<BR> E. कन् added to the<BR>preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=273-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूर्णकार|चूर्णकारः
चूर्णकार m. (-रः) A lime-burner, a maker of lime.<BR> E. चूर्ण, and कार who<BR>makes.<BR> E. चूर्णं करोति कृ-अण् उप-स ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=273-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूर्णकुन्तल|चूर्णकुंतल|चूर्णकुन्तलः
चूर्णकुन्तल m. (-लः) A lock of hair, a curl or curling hair.<BR> E. चूर्ण what<BR>contracts, and कुन्तल hair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=273-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूर्णखण्ड|चूर्णखंड|चूर्णखण्डं|चूर्णखण्डः
चूर्णखण्ड m. (-ण्डः) Pebble, gravel, hardened fragments of earth or brick<BR>lime-stone nodule, commonly known in India by the name of<BR>Kankar.<BR> E. चूर्ण dust, and खण्ड fragment. (कांँकड घुटिङ्) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=273-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूर्णता
चूर्णता f. (-ता) Pulverulence, comminution, the state of dust or powder.<BR>E. चूर्ण with तल् affix; also त्व, चूर्णत्वम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=273-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूर्णपारद|चूर्णपारदः
चूर्णपारद m. (-दः) Vermilion.<BR> E. चूर्ण, and पारद quicksilver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=273-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूर्णमुष्टि|चूर्णमुष्टिः
चूर्णमुष्टि f. (-ष्टिः) A handful of perfume or powder.<BR> E. चूर्ण and मुष्टि handful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=273-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूर्णि|चूर्णिः
चूर्णि m. (-र्णिः) A sum of 100 Cowries, the small shells used as coin.<BR>	 2.<BR>A selection or picking out of an unanswerable argument.<BR>	 2. The<BR>grammar of PATANJALA, a comment on PĀṆINI'S grammar.<BR> E. चर्<BR>to go, to pass, (current,) नि Uṇādi affix, and उ substituted for the<BR>radical vowel, or चूर्ण् to direct, &c. affix इन् । अशेषविदुषां तर्कं<BR>चूर्णयति । पतञ्जलिकृते महाभाष्ये ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=273-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूर्णिका
चूर्णिका f. (-का) Fried and ground rice.<BR> E. चूर्ण to pound, ठन् affix, and<BR>the feminine form. चूर्णश्चूर्णनमस्ति अस्याः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=273-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूर्णिकृत्
चूर्णिकृत् m. (-कृत्) An annotator, commentator, &c.<BR> E. चूर्णि selecting,<BR>picking out, (meanings or corroborative passages.) and कृत who<BR>makes. चूर्णिं महाभाष्यं करोति कृ-क्विप । महाभाष्यकारे ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=273-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूर्णित
चूर्णित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Ground, pounded, reduced to dust or powder.<BR>2. Squeezed, smashed.<BR> E. चूर्ण् to pound, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=273-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूर्णिन्
चूर्णिन् mfn. (-र्णी-र्णिनी-र्णि) Made or mixed up with any thing powdered<BR>or pounded.<BR> E. चूर्ण powder. and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=273-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूर्णीकृत
चूर्णीकृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Reduced to dust or powder, pounded, beaten to<BR>pieces.<BR> E. चूर्ण, and कृत made, च्वि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=273-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूर्त्ति|चूर्ति|चूर्तिः
चूर्त्ति f. (-र्त्तिः) Going.<BR> E. चर् to go, भावे क्तिन् affix, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=273-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूला
चूला f. (-ला)<BR>	 1. An upper room, a room on the top of a house.<BR>	 2. A<BR>crest.<BR> E. चूल् to rise, affixes अङ् and टाप्: see चूडा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=273-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूलिका
चूलिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. The root of an elephant's ear.<BR>	 2. The body of a<BR>drama, the inferior personages of the drama collectively.<BR>	 3. The<BR>crest of a peacock.<BR>	 n. (-कं) Flour-cakes fried with ghee.<BR> E. चूल् to<BR>be or make high, affix ण्वुल्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=273-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूष
चूष r. 1st cl. (चूषति) To drink or suck.<BR> E. भ्वा-पर-सक-सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=273-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूषा
चूषा f. (-षा)<BR>	 1. Sucking.<BR>	 2. A leathern girth.<BR> E. चूष् to drink, affix घञ्.<BR>चूष-घञर्थे क । चूष्यते पीयते पृष्ठमांसेन अदृश्यतां नीयते ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=273-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूष्य|चूष्यं
चूष्य mfn. (-ष्यः-ष्या-ष्यं) To be drunk or sucked.<BR>	 n. (-ष्यं) Any thing that<BR>can be eaten by sucking.<BR> E. चूष् to suck, ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=273-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चृत
चृत r. 1st and 10th cls. (चर्त्तति-चर्त्तयति-ते) To light, to kindle. (ई) चृती<BR>r. 6th cl. (चृतति)<BR>	 1. To hurt, to wound or kill.<BR>	 2. To tie or connect<BR>together.<BR> E. तुदा-सक-सेट् । चुरा-उभ० पक्षे-भ्वा-पर-सक-सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=273-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चृप
चृप r. 1st and 10th cls. (चर्पति, चर्पयति-ते) To light or kindle.<BR> E. चु-उभ-<BR>पक्षे भ्वा-प-सक-सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=273-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेक्रिय
चेक्रिय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Who does much or often, active, industrious.<BR> E. कृ to do, intens, form, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=273-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेट|चेटः
चेट m. (-टः) A servant, a slave.<BR>	 f. (-टी) A female servant.<BR> E. चिट् to<BR>serve, affix अच् also with कन् added चेटक.<BR>	 f. चेटिका; also चेड, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=273-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेटक|चेटकः
चेटक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A slave. A gallant: see the last.<BR>	 3. A servant, a<BR>minister, one who fulfils an appointed duty.<BR> E. चिट् to serve, ण्वुल्<BR>affix, or चेट with कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=273-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेड|चेडः
चेड m. (-डः) A servant.<BR>	 f. (-डी) A female servant or slave.<BR> E. चिट् to<BR>serve, अच् affix, and ट changed to ड; also चेट, &c. as above, and<BR>चेडक, चेडिका, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=273-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेत्
चेत् ind. If.<BR> E. चित् to think, to consider, affix. विच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=273-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेतक
चेतक mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>	 1. Suggesting, causing to think.<BR>	 2. What thinks<BR>or feels, sentient.<BR>	 f. (-की) The yellow myrobalan, (Terminalia<BR>chebula.)<BR> E. चित् to consider, affix, णिच् ण्वुल् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=273-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेतन|चेतनः
चेतन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Alive, living, feeling.<BR>	 m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. Soul, self.<BR>	 2. A<BR>man.<BR>	 3. A living and sentient being.<BR>	 f. (-ना) Understanding, in-<BR>telligence, wisdom, reflection.<BR> E. चित् to reflect, affix ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=274-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेतनावत्|चेतनावन्त्
चेतनावत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Living, sentient.<BR> E. चेतना, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=274-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेतय
चेतय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) A living and sentient being.<BR> E. चित् to think,<BR>श aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=274-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेतयमान
चेतयमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Sentient, reflecting, conscious.<BR> E. चित् to thing<BR>शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=274-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेतव्य
चेतव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं) To be collected, to be gathered.<BR> E. चि to collect<BR>तव्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=274-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेतस्
चेतस् n. (-तः) Mind, intellect, the faculty of reasoning or understand-<BR>ing.<BR> E. चित् to consider, Uṇādi affix असुन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=274-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेतोभू
चेतोभू m. (-भूः) Love.<BR> E. चेतस्, and भू born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=274-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेदार
चेदार m. (-रः) A lizard, a chamelion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=274-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेदि|चेदिः
चेदि m. (-दिः) The name of a country, perhaps the modern Chandail.<BR>m. plu. (-दयः) The inhabitants of Cedi. देशभेदे, सोऽभिजनोऽस्य अणः<BR>तद्राजाणश्च बहुत्वे लुक् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=274-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेदिपति|चेदिपतिः
चेदिपति m. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. A VASU named UPARICHARA.<BR>	 2. A name of SISU-<BR>PALA.<BR> E. चेदि, and पति master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=274-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेदिराज|चेदिराजः
चेदिराज m. (-जः) A name of ŚIŚUPĀLA a king killed by KṚṢṆA. E.<BR>चेदि the country, and राज a king; also चेदिपति, चेदिराज, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=274-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेय
चेय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) To be gathered or collected.<BR> E. चि to collect, कर्मणि<BR>यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=274-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेल|चेलं
चेल (ऋ) चेऌ r. 1st cl. (चेलति)<BR>	 1. To shake or tremble.<BR>	 2. To go or<BR>move. लौल्ये अक । गतौ सक-भ्वा-पर-सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=274-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेल|चेलं
चेल mfn. sub. (-लः-ली-लं) Cloth, clothes, raiment. adj. Vile, wicked,<BR>bad.<BR> E. चिल् to wear, affix, कर्मणि घञ्; also चेलक and चैल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=274-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेलप्रक्षालक|चेलप्रक्षालकः
चेलप्रक्षालक m. (-कः) A washer-man.<BR> E. चेल, and प्रक्षालक who washes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=274-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेलाल|चेलालः
चेलाल m. (-लः) A cucumber. चेलम् इव अलति अल-अच् । लतापनसे ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=274-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेलिका
चेलिका f. (-का) A corset, a boddice.<BR> E. चेल clothes, ण्वुल् aff. पट्टवसने ।<BR>(चेलिर कापड) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=274-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेलीम
चेलीम m. (-मः) A small kind of fish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=274-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेल्ल
चेल्ल r. 1st cl. (चेल्लति)<BR>	 1. To think.<BR>	 2. To go: this root is not usually<BR>admitted: see चेल.<BR> E. भ्वा-पर-सक-सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=274-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेवी
चेवी f. (-वी) One of the Rāgiṇīs or female personifications of music.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=274-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेष्ट|चेष्टं
चेष्ट r. 1st cl. (चेष्टते) To act or perform functions, duties, &c., to strive,<BR>to endeavour, to be busy or follow any particular avocation. E.<BR>भ्वा-आ-सक-सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=274-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेष्टन|चेष्टनं
चेष्टन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Making effort, who or what acts or attempts any<BR>act.<BR>	 n. (-नं) Effort, exertion.<BR> E. चेष्ट, and युच् or ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=274-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेष्टमान
चेष्टमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Active, moving.<BR> E. चेष्ट् to exert, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=274-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेष्टा
चेष्टा f. (-ष्टा) Effort, exertion, bodily effort.<BR> E. चेष्ट् to act, अङ् and टाप्<BR>affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=274-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेष्टानिरूपण
चेष्टानिरूपण n. (-णं) Observing a person's actions.<BR> E. चेष्टा, and निरूपण<BR>investigating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=274-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेष्टानाश|चेष्टानाशः
चेष्टानाश m. (-शः) The end of the world.<BR> E. चेष्टा, and नाश destruction.<BR>चेष्टायाः नाशः अत्र । प्रलयकाले ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=274-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेष्टित|चेष्टितं
चेष्टित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Exerted, done with effort.<BR>	 2. Done.<BR>	 n. (-तं)<BR>	 1.<BR>Going, motion.<BR>	 2. Bodily act or function.<BR>	 3. Action, behaviour.<BR>E. चेष्ट् to act, affix कर्त्तरि क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=274-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चैतन्य|चैतन्यं|चैतन्यः
चैतन्य n. (-न्यं)<BR>	 1. Soul, spirit, the deity considered as the essence of all<BR>being.<BR>	 2. Sense, consciousness.<BR>	 m. (-न्यः) A modern reformer of<BR>the Vaishnava faith, considered in Bengal as an Avatara of KṚṢṆA.<BR>E. चेतन intellect, and ष्यञ् aff. चेतनः एव चेतनस्य भावः वा--ष्यञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=274-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चैत्य|चैत्यं|चैत्यः
चैत्य m. (-त्यः) A sacred tree, a religious fig tree, &c. growing in a<BR>village or near it, and held in veneration by the villagers.<BR>	 n. (-त्यं)<BR>1. A place of sacrifice or religious worship, an altar, a shed kept<BR>for sacrifices, &c.<BR>	 2. A religious building peculiar to the Jainas, a<BR>Jaina temple.<BR>	 3. A Jaina or Bauddha image, &c.<BR>	 4. A monument<BR>a tomb-stone, a column, &c. erected in memory of some deceased<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=274-b" target="_blank">Page274-b+ 60</a>]<BR>person, or on the site of a funeral pile.<BR>	 5. A pile of stones form-<BR>ing a land-mark or boundary.<BR> E. चि to collect, deriv. irr.; or चित् to<BR>consider, affix क्यप्; चित्य and अण् aff. चित्तस्य इदम् अण् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=274-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चैत्यद्रु|चैत्यद्रुः
चैत्यद्रु m. (-द्रुः)<BR>	 1. The religious fig tree, (Ficus religiosa.)<BR>	 2. A large<BR>tree in a village.<BR> E. चैत्य as above, and द्रु a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=274-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चैत्यद्रुम|चैत्यद्रुमः
चैत्यद्रुम m. (-मः) A large tree in a village.<BR> E. चैत्य as above, and द्रुम a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=274-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चैत्यमुख|चैत्यमुखः
चैत्यमुख m. (-खः) A student's water pot.<BR> E. चैत्य place of sacrifice, and<BR>मुख principal. कमण्डलौ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=274-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चैत्यवृक्ष|चैत्यवृक्षः
चैत्यवृक्ष m. (-क्षः)<BR>	 1. The religious fig tree.<BR>	 2. A large tree in a village.<BR>E. चैत्य and वृक्ष a tree: see चैत्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=274-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चैत्र|चैत्रं|चैत्रः
चैत्र m. (-त्रः)<BR>	 1. The month Chaitra or Cheyte, (March-April.)<BR>	 2. One<BR>of the ranges of mountains dividing the continent into portions<BR>or Varṣas: see वर्ष.<BR>	 3. A Bauddha or Jaina religious mendicant.<BR>4. The son BUDHA by CHITRA.<BR>	 n. (-त्रं)<BR>	 1. A monument erected to<BR>the dead, a column or block of wood, a tree, &c. so considered.<BR>	 2.<BR>2. A small temple.<BR> E. चित्रा the star, or चित्र wonderful, &c. affix<BR>अण्, or चि-ष्ट्रन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=274-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चैत्रक|चैत्रकः
चैत्रक m. (-कः) The month Chaitra.<BR> E. कन् added to the preceding;<BR>also चैत्रिक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=274-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चैत्ररथ|चैत्ररथं
चैत्ररथ n. (-थं) The garden of the deity KUVERA.<BR> E. चित्ररथ a Gandharba<BR>in charge of the garden, affix अण्. चित्ररथेन निर्वृत्तम् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=274-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चैत्रावली
चैत्रावली f. (-ली) The day of full moon in Chaitra.<BR> E. चैत्र the month,<BR>and आवली a line, a series.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=274-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चैत्रि|चैत्रिः
चैत्रि m. (-त्रिः) The month Chaitra.<BR> E. चित्रा, and इञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=274-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चैत्रिक|चैत्रिकः
चैत्रिक m. (-कः) The month Chaitra.<BR> E. चित्रा the asterism, or lunar<BR>mansion for this month, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=274-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चैत्रिन्
चैत्रिन् m. (-त्री) the month Chaitra.<BR> E. चित्रा, and णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=274-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चैद्य|चैद्यः
चैद्य m. (-द्यः) A name of ŚIŚUPĀLA an adversary of KṚṢṆA, the son<BR>of DAMAGHOSHA, and sovereign of Cedi or Chandail.<BR>	 m. plu. (-द्याः)<BR>The inhabitants of Cedi.<BR> E. चेदि the country so called, and ज्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=274-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चैल|चैलः
चैल mfn. (-लः-ली-लं)<BR>	 1. Cloth, of cloth.<BR>	 2. Bred in clothes, (insects or<BR>lice, &c.)<BR> E. चेल cloth, कर्मणि घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=274-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चैलाशक|चैलाशकः
चैलाशक m. (-कः) An eater of lice, (a goblin so designated.)<BR> E. चैल an<BR>insect found in clothes, and अशक who eats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=274-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चोक्ष|चोक्षः
चोक्ष mfn. (-क्षः-क्षा-क्षं)<BR>	 1. Sung.<BR>	 2. Pure, clean.<BR>	 3. Clever, dexterous.<BR>	 4.<BR>Pleasing, delightful, beautiful.<BR>	 5. Sharp, pungent, keen, &c. E.<BR>चूष् to suck, affix ष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=274-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चोच|चोचं
चोच n. (-चं)<BR>	 1. Bark, rind.<BR>	 2. Skin.<BR>	 3. Cassia bark.<BR>	 4. Half eaten fruit<BR>of the palm.<BR>	 5. A banana or plaintain: see मोचा.<BR>	 6. A cocoanut.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=274-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चोचक|चोचकं|चोचकः
चोचक n. (-कं) Bark, rind.<BR> E. कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=274-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चोटी
चोटी f. (-टी) A petticoat.<BR> E. चुट् to be small, affixes अच् and ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=274-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चोड|चोडः
चोड m. (-डः)<BR>	 1. A bodice or jacket.<BR>	 2. A country: see चोल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=274-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चोदना
चोदना f. (-ना)<BR>	 1. A precept, a sacred ordinance or commandment.<BR>	 2.<BR>Sending, commanding, directing, &c.<BR>	 3. Enjoining, ordaining.<BR>	 4.<BR>Casting, throwing.<BR> E. चुद् to command, &c. affixes युच् and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=274-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चोदनागुड|चोदनागुडः
चोदनागुड m. (-डः) A ball for playing with.<BR> E. चोदना directing or throw-<BR>ing, and गुड a ball.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=274-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चोदित
चोदित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Informed, apprised.<BR>	 2. Ordered, directed.<BR>	 3.<BR>Appointed.<BR>	 4. Urged, impelled.<BR>	 5. Thrown, cast.<BR> E. चुद् to direct,<BR>क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=274-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चोद्य|चोद्यं|चोद्यः
चोद्य mfn. (-द्यः-द्या-द्यं) To be sent, thrown, or directed.<BR>	 n. (-द्यं)<BR>	 1. Sur-<BR>prise, wonderful or astonishing.<BR>	 2. Asking, an asking. a ques-<BR>tion, an objection &c.<BR> E. चुद् to send, to command, &c. affix ण्यत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=274-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चोपन|चोपनं
चोपन m. (-नः) Moving, moving slowly.<BR> E. चोप् to move, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=274-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चोर|चोरः
चोर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A thief, a robber.<BR>	 2. A perfume called commonly by<BR>the same name.<BR>	 f. (-रा) A plant: see चोरपुष्पी.<BR> E. चोर् to steal, affix<BR>अच्; also with कन् added चोरक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=274-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चोरकण्टक
चोरकण्टक m. (-कः) A kind of grass, commonly Chorcanta, (Andropo-<BR>gon aciculatum.)<BR> E. चोर, and कण्टक a thorn: the seeds clinging to<BR>the feet and clothes of those who walk amongst it.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=274-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चोरपुष्पी
चोरपुष्पी f. (-ष्पी) A kind of grass, (Andropogon aciculatum.)<BR> E. चोर a<BR>thief, and पुष्प a flower, fem. affix ङीष्ः see the last; also with कन्<BR>added चोरपुष्पिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=275-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चोरिका
चोरिका f. (-का) Theft, robbery: see चौरिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=275-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चोल|चोलः
चोल mf. (-लः-ली) A short jacket, a bodice.<BR>	 m. (-लः) or m. plu. (-लाः) A<BR>country, the modern Tanjore, the name is also supposed to apply<BR>to a part of Birbhum in Bengal.<BR> E. चुल् to be high or to elevate,<BR>affix अच् and ल being changed to ड चोड ut sup. or चोल a proper<BR>name, that of the king of the country applied to the country, or<BR>चुल कर्मणि घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=275-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चोलक|चोलकं|चोलकः
चोलक m. (-कः) A breastplate, a cuirass.<BR>	 n. (-कं) Bark, rind.<BR> E. चुल to<BR>elevate, affix वुन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=275-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चोलकिन्
चोलकिन् m. (-की)<BR>	 1. The shoot of the bambu.<BR>	 2. The wrist.<BR>	 3. The<BR>orange.<BR>	 4. A cuirassier, a soldier armed with a breastplate. E.<BR>चोलक armour, rind, &c. and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=275-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चोलोण्डुक|चोलोंडुक|चोलोंडुकः|चोलोण्डुकः
चोलोण्डुक m. (-कः) A diadem, a fillet for the head, a turban or tiara.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=275-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चोष|चोषः
चोष m. (-षः)<BR>	 1. Suction, sucking.<BR>	 2. Burning, (of the skin,) inflam-<BR>mation.<BR>	 3. Drying up.<BR> E. चूष् to suck, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=275-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चोषण|चोषणं
चोषण n. (णं) Sucking, suction.<BR> E. चूष् to suck, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=275-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चोस्क|चोस्कः
चोस्क m. (-स्कः) A horse of a particular and good breed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=275-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चौक्ष|चौक्षं
चौक्ष mfn. (-क्षः-क्षी-क्षं) Agreeable, pleasant.<BR> E. चोक्ष the same, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=275-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चौड
चौड mfn. (-डः-डी-डं)<BR>	 1. Crested, relating to a crest.<BR>	 2. Relating to<BR>to tonsure.<BR>	 n. (-डं) Tonsure.<BR> E. चूडा a crest, &c. and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=275-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चौडकर्म्मन्|चौडकर्मन्
चौडकर्म्मन् n. (-र्म्म) The rite of tonsure.<BR> E. चौड, and कर्म्मन् act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=275-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चौर|चौरः
चौर mf. (-रः-री)<BR>	 1. A thief, a robber, a pilferer.<BR>	 2. A plant: see चोरपुष्पी<BR>3. A perfume.<BR>	 f. (-री) Stealing, theft.<BR> E. चोर a thief, affix अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=275-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चौरतस्
चौरतस् ind. From theft.<BR> E. चौर, and तसि for the sign of the fifth case.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=275-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चौरहृत
चौरहृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Stolen, robbed.<BR> E. चौर, and हृत taken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=275-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चौरापहृत
चौरापहृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Carried off, stolen.<BR> E. चौर and अपहृत taken<BR>away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=275-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चौरिका
चौरिका f. (-का) Theft, robbing.<BR> E. चोर a thief, वुञ् affix, optionally<BR>चोरिका; or चौरी theft, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=275-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चौर्य्य|चौर्य|चौर्यं|चौर्य्यं
चौर्य्य n. (-र्य्यं) Theft, robbing.<BR> E. चोर a thief, ष्यञ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=275-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चौर्य्यार्ज्जित|चौर्यार्जित
चौर्य्यार्ज्जित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Acquired by plunder or robbery.<BR> E. चौर्य्य,<BR>and अर्ज्जित gained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=275-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चौल
चौल mfn. (-लः-ली-लं) Relating to a crest or top-knot, &c.<BR> E. चूला for<BR>चूडा, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=275-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चौलकर्म्मन्|चौलकर्मन्
चौलकर्म्मन् n. (-र्म्म) The ceremony of tonsure, cutting of all the hair<BR>from the head of a child three years old, except one lock on the<BR>crown.<BR> E. चौल or चोड relating to the चूडा or crest, and कर्म्मन्<BR>work, act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=275-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चोलुक्य
चोलुक्य m. (-क्यः) One of the Rajarshis or royal saints.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=275-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

च्यवन|च्यवनं|च्यवनः
च्यवन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Oozing, tricking, flowing.<BR>	 2. Going, moving.<BR>	 m. (-नः)<BR>The name of a RISHI.<BR> E. च्यु to go, ल्यट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=275-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

च्यु
च्यु (ङ) च्युङ् r. 1st cl. (च्यवते)<BR>	 1. To go or move.<BR>	 2. To flow, to drop. r.<BR>10th cl. (च्यावयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To laugh.<BR>	 2. To bear or suffer.<BR> E. भ्वा-आ-<BR>सक-अनिट् । चुरा-उभ-सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=275-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

च्युत|च्युतं
च्युत (इर) च्युतिर r. 1st cl. (च्योतति) To wet thoroughly, to moisten a<BR>little, to sprinkle, to drop, to exude.<BR> E. भ्वा-पर-अक-सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=275-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

च्युत|च्युतं
च्युत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Fallen, dropped, oozed out, &c.<BR>	 2. Fallen, from<BR>or off.<BR>	 3. Deviated from, erred, strayed.<BR>	 4. Broken, disordered.<BR>	 5.<BR>Lost.<BR> E. च्यु to go, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=275-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

च्युताचार
च्युताचार mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Deviating from duty.<BR> E. च्युत and आचार rite,<BR>usage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=275-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

च्युताधिकार
च्युताधिकार mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Dismissed, (from an office, &c.) deprived of,<BR>(as a right.)<BR> E. च्युत lost, and अधिकार function.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=275-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

च्युतोत्साह
च्युतोत्साह mfn. (-हः-हा-हं) Spent, exhausted, incapable of effort.<BR> E. च्युत<BR>and उत्माह exertion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=275-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

च्युति|च्युतिः
च्युति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Dropping, dripping, oozing.<BR>	 2. Falling, falling from.<BR>3. Deviating from.<BR>	 4. The vulva.<BR>	 5. The anus.<BR> E. च्यु to fall, &c,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=275-b" target="_blank">Page275-b+ 55</a>]<BR>affix क्तिन्; also with ङीष्, च्युती again with the radical vowel pro-<BR>tracted च्यूति, &c.; and without the semivowel चुति, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=275-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

च्युप|च्युपः
च्युप m. (-पः) The face.<BR> E. च्यु to laugh, प Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=275-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

च्युस
च्युस r. 10th cl. (च्वोसयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To laugh.<BR>	 2. To bear.<BR>	 3. To loose.<BR>	 4. To<BR>hurt or kill. चु-उभ-अक-सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=275-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

च्योत|च्योतं
च्योत n. (-तं) Sprinkling, pouring forth, or dropping falling as an<BR>unctuous substance, oozing, trickling, &c.<BR> E. च्युत् to wet or<BR>moisten, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=275-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

च्योत्र
च्योत्र mfn. (-त्रः-त्री-त्रं)<BR>	 1. A mover, a goer, one who moves or goes.<BR>	 2.<BR>Oviparous.<BR>	 3. Abandoned, wicked, void of virtue or purity.<BR> E. च्य<BR>to go, Uṇādi affix त्रण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=275-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छ|छं|छः
छ The aspirated letter corresponding to the preceding, and expressed<BR>by Ch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=275-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छ|छं|छः
छ mfn. (छः-छा-छं)<BR>	 1. Pure, clean.<BR>	 2. Trembling, tremulous, unsteady.<BR>m. (छः) Cutting, dividing.<BR>	 2. A part, a fragment.<BR>	 f. (छा)<BR>	 1.<BR>Covering, concealing.<BR>	 2. An infant, a child, any young animal.<BR>E. छो to cut, or छद् to cover, &c. affix ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=275-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छग|छगः
छग mf. (-गः-गा) A goat.<BR> E. छो to cut, गक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=275-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छगण|छगणं|छगणः
छगण mn. (-णः-णं) Dried cowdung.<BR> E. छ a fragment, and गण assemblage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=275-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छगल|छगलं|छगलः
छगल m. (-लः) A goat.<BR>	 f. (-ला-ली) A she goat.<BR>	 2. A kind of convolvulus<BR>(C. aegenteus,) or more probably (C. pes-capræ;) see ऋक्षगन्धा.<BR>	 n.<BR>(-लं) Blue cloth or garment.<BR> E. छो to cut or tear, Uṇādi affixes<BR>कलच् and गुक्, or ग substituted for क, ह्रस्वश्च ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=275-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छगलक|छगलकः
छगलक m. (-कः) A goat.<BR> E. कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=275-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छगलाङ्घ्री
छगलाङ्घ्री f. (-ङ्घ्री) A kind of convolvulus, (C. pes-capræ:) see छगला. E.<BR>छगल a goat, and अङ्घ्री a foot; also छगलान्त्री, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=275-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छगलाण्डी
छगलाण्डी f. (-ण्डी) A plant: see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=275-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छगलान्त्री
छगलान्त्री f. (-न्त्री) A kind of convolvulus: see छगलाङ्घ्री.<BR> E. छगल a goat.<BR>and अन्त्र a gut, an entrail; with कन् added, छगलान्त्रिका; also<BR>छगलाङ्घ्री.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=275-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छटा
छटा f. (-टा)<BR>	 1. Light, lustre, splendor.<BR>	 2. Assemblage, quantity.<BR>number.<BR>	 3. A straight or continuous mark or line.<BR> E. छो-अटन् किच्च ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=275-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छटाफल|छटाफलः
छटाफल m. (-लः) A palmyra tree.<BR> E. छटा a line, and फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=275-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छटाभा
छटाभा f. (-भा) Lightning.<BR> E. छटा a streak, and भा light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=275-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छत्र|छत्त्रं|छत्त्रः|छत्रं|छत्रः
छत्र n. (-त्रं) A parasol, and umbrella, the Indian chattah.<BR>	 f. (-त्रा)<BR>	 1.<BR>A kind of fennel, (Anethum sowa.)<BR>	 2. A pungent seed, coriander.<BR>3. A mushroom.<BR>	 4. Anise.<BR> E. छद् to cover, and णिच् and ष्ट्रन्<BR>Uṇādi affixes ह्रस्वश्च; hence the word and its derivatives are also<BR>written with a double त, छत्र &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=275-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छत्रक|छत्त्रकः|छत्रकः
छत्रक m. (-कः) A king-fisher 2. A mushroom.<BR>	 3. A shrub, commonly<BR>Kuliya-khara.<BR>	 4. A small vaulted temple, in honour of a deity.<BR>5. A beehive of a conical or umbrella form.<BR> E. कन् added to the<BR>preceding.<BR> E. छत्रम् इव कायति कै-क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=275-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छत्रचक्र|छत्त्रचक्रं
छत्रचक्र n. (-क्रं) An astrological diagram.<BR> E. छत्र, and चक्र a circle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=275-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छत्रधार|छत्त्रधारः|छत्रधारः
छत्रधार mfn. (-रः-री-रं) Bearing a parasol, having or possessing one. E.<BR>छत्र and धर who has or holds, affix अच् or अण्; also छत्रधर, छत्र-<BR>धारक, and छत्रधारिन् । छत्रं धरति धारयति वा अच् अण् वा ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=275-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छत्रधारण
छत्रधारण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Carrying a chatra.<BR>	 2. The carrying of one as a<BR>type of authority.<BR> E. छत्र, and धारण having.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=275-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छत्रपत्र|छत्त्रपत्त्रं|छत्त्रपत्त्रः|छत्त्रपत्र
छत्रपत्र n. (-त्रं) A plant, (Hibiscus mutabilis.)<BR> E. छत्र, and पत्र a leaf, um-<BR>brella-leaved; also छत्रपत्रक । छत्रम् इव पत्रम् अस्य । स्थलपाद्मे, भूर्जपत्रवृक्षे<BR>च ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=275-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छत्रभङ्ग|छत्त्रभङ्गः|छत्रभंग|छत्रभङ्गः
छत्रभङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>	 1. Widowhood.<BR>	 2. Wilfulness, independence.<BR>	 3. Sub-<BR>version of dominion, loss of empire, deposition, &c.<BR> E. छत्र a<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=276-a" target="_blank">Page276-a+ 60</a>]<BR>parasol, and भङ्ग a breaking; in the first two senses छत्र is<BR>used metaphorically, for any cover or defence, as a husband, &c.<BR>in the last it is used by synecdoche, a parasol being one of the<BR>ensigns of royalty.<BR> E. छत्रस्य भङ्गः यत्र । नृपनाशे, वैधव्ये, स्वातन्त्र्ये च ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=275-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छत्राक|छत्त्राकं|छत्त्राकः|छत्राकः
छत्राक n. (-कं) A mushroom.<BR>	 f. (-की) A plant, commonly Rasna: see<BR>रास्ला.<BR> E. छत्र a parasol, and अक् to go, to resemble; affixes अण् and<BR>ङीष् । छत्रा अतिछत्रा इव कायति कै-क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=276-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छत्रातिच्छत्र|छत्त्रातिच्छत्त्रः|छत्रातिछत्र
छत्रातिच्छत्र m. (-त्रः) A fragrant grass, described as growing in marshy<BR>ground.<BR> E. छत्र a mushroom, and अतिच्छत्र surpassing an umbrella,<BR>i. e. more like a chattah, than even a mushroom. छत्रम् अतिक्रम्य<BR>छत्रम् आवरणम् अस्ति अस्म्य अच् । छत्राकारे जलोद्भवे सुगन्धितृणमदे ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=276-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छत्रिका
छत्रिका f. (-का) A mushroom.<BR> E. छत्र-ठन् affix of resemblance, fem. form.<BR>छत्रं तदाकारं पुष्पं वा अस्ति अस्य ठन् । शिलीन्ध्रे, स्वेदजे शाकभेदे च ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=276-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छत्रिन्
छत्रिन् mfn. (-त्री-त्रिणी-त्रि) Bearing a parasol or umbrella.<BR>	 m. (-त्री) A<BR>barber.<BR> E. छत्र, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=276-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छत्वर|छत्वरः
छत्वर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A house, a dwelling.<BR>	 2. A bower, an arbour.<BR> E. छद् to<BR>cover, ष्वरच् Uṇādi affix, and त substituted for द.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=276-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छद|छदः
छद r. 1st and 10th cls. (छदति-ते छदयति-ते or more commonly छादयति-ते)<BR>1. To cover, to clothe, to veil, to hide, or remove from view:<BR>(आङ् is usually prefixed to the root in these senses.)<BR>	 2. To march.<BR>(इ) छदि r. 1st cl. (छन्दति) To live or breathe, to be or make strong;<BR>also. r. 1st and 10th cls. (छन्दति-ते छन्दयति-ते) To cover, &c. as above.<BR>E. चु-उभ-सक सेट् । भ्वा-उभ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=276-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छद|छदः
छद m. (-दः)<BR>	 1. A leaf.<BR>	 2. A wing.<BR>	 3. A plant: see ग्रन्थिपर्णी.<BR>	 4. A tree<BR>bearing dark blossoms: see तमाल.<BR> E. छद् to cover, &c. aff. घ, ह्रस्वश्च ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=276-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छदन|छदनं
छदन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. A leaf.<BR>	 2. A wing.<BR>	 3. A covering, a sheathe, a scabbard.<BR>4. Cassia.<BR> E. छद् to cover or hide, affix ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=276-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छदपत्र|छदपत्त्रः|छदपत्रः
छदपत्र m. (-त्रः) A tree, (Symplocos racemosa, Rox. See भूर्य्य.<BR> E. छद a<BR>cover or skin, and पत्र a leaf. छदार्थं पत्रम अस्य । भूर्जपत्रे ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=276-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छदिस्
छदिस् m. (-दिः) The thatch or roof of a house.<BR> E. छद् to cover, इसि<BR>Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=276-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छद्मतापस|छद्मतापसः
छद्मतापस m. (-सः) A religious hypocrite, a false brother.<BR> E. छद्म disguise.<BR>and तापस an ascetic. छद्मना छलेन त्रापसः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=276-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छद्मन्
छद्मन् n. (-द्म)<BR>	 1. Trick, deceit.<BR>	 3. Fraud, dishonesty.<BR>	 2. Plea, pretext.<BR>	 4.<BR>Masquerade, disguise of person, &c.<BR> E. छद a cloak, a covering, and<BR>मनिन् Uṇādi aff. छाद्यते स्वरूपमनेन ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=276-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छद्मवेशिन्
छद्मवेशिन् m. (-शी) Being in disguise, a player.<BR> E. छद्म, and वेशिन् who<BR>wears a dress, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=276-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छद्वर
छद्वर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A tooth.<BR>	 2. An arbour or bower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=276-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छन्च्छन
छन्च्छन ind. An imitative sound. expressive of sobbing, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=276-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छन्द|छंद|छन्दः
छन्द mfn. (-न्दः-न्दा-न्दं) Solitary, secret, private.<BR>	 m. (-न्दः)<BR>	 8. Meaning,<BR>intention, purport, opinion.<BR>	 2. Subjection.<BR>	 3. Poison.<BR>	 n. (-न्दं) Wish,<BR>desire.<BR> E. छद् to cover, affix अच्; see छन्दस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=276-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छन्दपातन|छन्दपातनः
छन्दपातन m. (-नः) A hypocrite, a pretended and false ascetic.<BR> E. छन्द<BR>subjection, (of all human beings,) and पातन obtaining, from पत् to<BR>go, affix ल्युट्; also छन्दकपातन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=276-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छन्दस्|छंदस्
छन्दस् n. (-न्दः)<BR>	 1. Poetical metre of every kind, but it is also applicable<BR>particularly to the metre of the Vedas.<BR>	 2. Meaning, purport, ob-<BR>ject, intention.<BR>	 3. Wish, desire.<BR>	 4. the Vedas or scripture.<BR>	 5.<BR>Wilfulness, independence, uncontrolled or unrestrained conduct.<BR>E. छदि to gladden, &c. and असुन् Uṇādi affix, च is changed to छ;<BR>also in some senses with a final vowel छन्द q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=276-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छन्दस्कृत|छंदस्कृत
छन्दस्कृत n. (-तं) A holy verse.<BR> E. छन्दस् and कृत made.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=276-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छन्दस्य|छंदस्य
छन्दस्य mfn. (-स्यः-स्या-स्यं) Made or done at will or according to one's<BR>wish.<BR> E. छन्दस् inclination, and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=276-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छन्दोग|छंदोग|छन्दोगः
छन्दोग m. (-गः) A reciter, or chanter of the Sama Veda.<BR> E. छन्दस् the<BR>metre of the Vedas, and ग who sings.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=276-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छन्दोनुवृत्त
छन्दोऽनुवृत्त n. (-त्तं) Humouring, indulgence.<BR> E. छन्दस् will, and अनुवृत्त con-<BR>forming to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=276-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छन्न|छन्नं|छन्नः
छन्न mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>	 1. Private, secret.<BR>	 2. Solitary.<BR>	 3. Covered.<BR> E. छद् to cover, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=276-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छप
छप (इ) छपि r. 1st and 10th cls. (छम्पति छम्पयति-ते) To go or. move. चु-<BR>उभ-पक्षे भ्वा-प-सक-सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=276-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छम
छम (उ) छमु r. 1st cl. (छमति) To eat: see चमु. भ्वा-प-सक-सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=276-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छमण्ड|छमंड|छमंडः|छमण्डः
छमण्ड m. (-ण्डः)<BR>	 1. An orphan, a fatherless son.<BR>	 2. A lad who has no<BR>kinsmen.<BR> E. छम् to eat, अण्डच् Uṇādi affix; also छेमण्ड ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=276-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छर्द|छर्दः|छर्द्द|छर्द्दं
छर्द r. 10th cl. (छर्दयति-ते) To vomit, to be sick.<BR> E. चु-उभ-सक-सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=276-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छर्द|छर्दः|छर्द्द|छर्द्दं
छर्द nf. (-र्दं-र्दी) Vomiting, sickness, retching.<BR> E. छर्द् to vomit, affix<BR>अच्; also with the affixes ल्युट् and इन्, छर्दन्, छर्दि, &c. ut infra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=276-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छर्दन|छर्दनं|छर्दनः|छर्द्दन|छर्द्दनं
छर्दन n. (-नं) Vomiting, reaching, sickness.<BR>	 m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. The Nimb tree:<BR>see निम्ब.<BR>	 2. The Rākṣasa, ALAMBUSHA.<BR> E. छृद् to be or make sick,<BR>affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=276-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छर्दि|छर्दिः|छर्द्दि|छर्द्दिः
छर्दि f. (-र्दिः) Vomiting. see छर्द.<BR> E. छृद् to be sick, इन् Uṇādi affix<BR>also with ङीष् added छर्दी, and with a further addition of कन्,<BR>छर्दिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=276-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छर्द्दिघ्न|छर्दिघ्न|छर्द्दिघ्नः
छर्द्दिघ्न m. (-घ्नः) The Nimb tree.<BR> E. छर्द्दि and घ्न what removes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=276-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छर्दिकारिपु|छर्द्दिकारिपुः
छर्दिकारिपु m. (-पुः) Small cardamoms.<BR> E. छर्दिका vomiting, and रिपु ene-<BR>my, anti-emetic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=276-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छर्दिस्
छर्दिस् f. (-र्दिः) Vomiting.<BR> E. छृद् to be sick, Uṇādi affix इसि; also छर्दि<BR>and छर्द.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=276-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छर्ष
छर्ष r. 1st cl. (छर्षति-ते) To kill, to wound, to hurt. भ्वा-सक-सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=276-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छल|छलं|छलः
छल n. (-लं)<BR>	 1. Wickedness.<BR>	 2. Fraud, circumvention, trick, stratagem.<BR>3. Design, device.<BR> E. छल to cut, अलच् affix, and the radical final<BR>rejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=276-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छलन|छलनं
छलन nf. (-नं-ना) Tricking, deceiving.<BR> E. छल nominal verb, णिच् and भावे<BR>ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=276-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छलनापर
छलनापर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Cunning, crafty, deceitful.<BR> E. छलना and पर ad-<BR>dicted to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=276-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छलयत्
छलयत् mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्) Deceiving, cheating.<BR> E. छल nom. verb to<BR>cheat, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=276-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छलिन्
छलिन् m. (-ली) A cheat.<BR> E. छल, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=276-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छल्लि|छल्लिः
छल्लि f. (-ल्लिः) Skin, bark, rind, &c.<BR> E. छद a cover, ला to give or get;<BR>with affix कि, द becomes ल; also with ङीप् added छल्ली.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=276-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छल्ली
छल्ली f. (-ल्ली)<BR>	 1. Skin, bark, rind, &c.<BR>	 2. Offspring, posterity.<BR>	 3. A<BR>spreading creeper.<BR>	 4. A kind of flower. E. See the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=276-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छवि|छविः
छवि f. (-विः)<BR>	 1. Beauty, splendor, brilliance.<BR>	 2. Light, lustre.<BR> E. छो to<BR>divide, (darkness, &c.) इन् affix, and the deriv. irr. or कित् च वा<BR>Uṇādi affix; also with ङीष् added छवी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=276-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छा
छा f. (छा) A young animal.<BR> E. छो to cut, डा aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=276-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छाग|छागः
छाग f. (-गः) A goat.<BR>	 f. (-गी) A she goat.<BR> E. छो to cut, Uṇādi affix गन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=276-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छागण|छागणः
छागण m. (-णः) A fire of dried cowdung.<BR> E. कर्मणि अच् affix of relation<BR>added to छगण् । छया छादनेन गण्यते गण कर्मणि अच् । छगण-स्वार्थे अण्<BR>वा करीषाग्नौ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=276-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छागभोजिन्
छागभोजिन् m. (-जी) A wolf.<BR> E. छाग, and भोजिन् who eats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=276-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छागरथ|छागरथः
छागरथ m. (-थः) AGNI or the deity of fire.<BR> E. छाग a goat, and रथ a car<BR>or any vehicle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=276-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छागल|छागलः
छागल m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. A goat: see छगल; also with कन् added छागलक.<BR>	 2. A<BR>proper name, the son of CHHAGALA or ATRI.<BR> E. छगल, and अण्<BR>affix; also with इञ् aff. छागलि or कन् added छागलक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=276-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छागलान्त्री
छागलान्त्री f. (-न्त्री) A plant, (Convolvulus pes-capræ:) see छगलान्त्री.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=276-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छागवाहन|छागवाहनः
छागवाहन m. (-नः) A name of AGNI or the deity of fire.<BR> E. छाग a goat,<BR>and वाहन a vehicle, the goat-born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=276-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छागिका
छागिका f. (-का) A she goat.<BR> E. कन् added to छागी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=276-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छात|छातः
छात mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Cut, divided.<BR>	 2. Thin, feeble, emaciated.<BR> E. छो<BR>to cut, affix क्त; also छित.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=276-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छात्र|छात्त्रः|छात्रं|छात्रः
छात्र m. (-त्रः) A scholar, a pupil, a disciple, a tyro or novice.<BR>	 n. (-त्रं)<BR>Honey.<BR> E. छत्र an umbrella, a screen or cover, affix ण । छत्रं गुरोः<BR>वैगुण्यावरणं शीलमस्य छत्रा० ण ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=276-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छात्रक|छात्रकं
छात्रक n. (-कं) Honey in the comb or hive.<BR> E. छत्रक a hive, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=276-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छात्रगण्ड|छात्रगंड|छात्रगण्डः
छात्रगण्ड m. (-ण्डः) An indifferent scholar in poetical composition; one<BR>citing imperfect portions only of a verse.<BR> E. छात्रः गण्डः इव ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=276-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छात्रदर्शन|छात्रदर्शनं
छात्रदर्शन n. (-नं) Oiled butter prepared from milk one day old. छात्रं मधु<BR>भेद इव दृश्यते दृश-कर्मणि ल्युट् । मधुतुल्यास्वादे हैयङ्गवीने, शिष्यस्य दर्शने च ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=277-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छाद|छादं
छाद n. (-दं) A thatch, a roof<BR> E. छद् to cover, affix अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=277-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छादन|छादनं|छादनः
छादन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Covering.<BR>	 2. A covering, a screen, &c.<BR>	 3. Hilling, con-<BR>cealing.<BR>	 4. A leaf.<BR> E. छद् to cover, affix ल्युट् and the vowel<BR>lengthened. भावे ल्युट् । छादने । करणे ल्युट् पत्रे । कर्त्तरि ल्यु छादके ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=277-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छादित|छादितः
छादित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Cut, divided.<BR>	 2. Covered.<BR>	 3. Hidden, conceal-<BR>ed.<BR> E. छो to cut, or छद् to cover, affix क्त । आछादिते ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=277-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छाद्मिक|छाद्मिकः
छाद्मिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Fraudulent, dishonest.<BR>	 m. (-कः) A rogue, cheat.<BR>E. छद्मन् knavery, ठक aff. छद्मना चरति व्यवहरति ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=277-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छान्दस|छांदस|छान्दसः
छान्दस mfn. (-सः-सी-सं) Relating to poetical metre, to the Vedas, &c.<BR>m. (-सः) A priest conversant with scripture.<BR> E. छन्दस्, and अण् aff.<BR>छन्दः अधीते वेत्ति वा पक्षे अण् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=277-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छान्दोग्य|छान्दोग्यं
छान्दोग्य n. (-ग्यं)<BR>	 1. The doctrine of the Vedas 2. A celebrated Upa-<BR>nishad of the Sama Veda.<BR> E. छान्दस belonging to the Vedas, ग who<BR>goes, and ञ्य affix of habitude or practice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=277-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छाया
छाया f. (-या)<BR>	 1. Shade.<BR>	 2. Shadow, reflected image.<BR>	 3. The wife of the<BR>sun.<BR>	 4. Beauty, splendor, lustre.<BR>	 5. Light.<BR>	 6. Nourishing, cherish-<BR>ing.<BR>	 7. A bribe.<BR>	 8. A straight or continuous line.<BR>	 9. A name of<BR>the goddess DURGĀ.<BR>	 10. Darkness, obscurity.<BR>	 11. The shadow of<BR>a Gnomon, especially as indicative of the position of the sun. E.<BR>छो to cut, (to cut off the light, &c.) and ण Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=277-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छायाकर|छायाकरः
छायाकर mfn. (-रः-री-रं) Shading, shadowing.<BR>	 m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A Chattah<BR>or umbrella bearer.<BR>	 2. A species of metre.<BR> E. छाया shade, and कर<BR>who makes. छायां करोति छत्रेण कृ-ट ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=277-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छायातनय|छायातनयः
छायातनय m. (-यः) A name of SATURN.<BR> E. छाया the wife of SŪRYA, and<BR>तनय a son; also similar compounds, as छायात्मज, छायासुत, &c. शनैश्चरे ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=277-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छायातरु|छायातरुः
छायातरु m. (-रुः) A large tree, one that gives shade or shelter.<BR> E. छाया,<BR>and तरु a tree. छायाप्रधानः तरुः । छायाप्रधाने वृक्षे ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=277-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छायात्मज|छायात्मजः
छायात्मज m. (-जः) SATURN: see छायातनय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=277-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छायापथ|छायापथः
छायापथ m. (-थः) Æther, the Akas or firmament.<BR> E. छाया light, and पथ<BR>a road. छायायुक्तः पन्थाः । आकाशस्थे ज्योतिश्चक्रमध्यवर्त्तिनि दक्षिणोत्तरायते<BR>तिरश्चीने आकाशस्थानभेदे ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=277-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छायाभृत्
छायाभृत् m. (-भृत्) CHANDRA or the moon.<BR> E. छाया light, and भृत् who<BR>possesses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=277-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छायामय
छायामय mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>	 1. Reflected.<BR>	 2. Casting a shadow.<BR> E. छाया, and<BR>मयट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=277-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छायामित्र|छायामित्रं
छायामित्र n. (-त्रं) A Chattah or parasol.<BR> E. छाया shade, and मित्र friend-<BR>ly. छायाया मित्रम् इव । आतपत्रे ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=277-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छायामृगधर|छायामृगधरः
छायामृगधर m. (-रः) The moon.<BR> E. छाया an image, मृग a deer, and धर who<BR>possesses; also छायाधर, and मृगधर, severally. छायारूपं मृगं धरति धृ-<BR>अच् । चन्द्रे ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=277-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छायासुत|छायासुतः
छायासुत m. (-तः) SATURN: see छायातनय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=277-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छि|छिः
छि m. (छिः) Abuse, reproach.<BR> E. छो to cut, कि aff. गर्हायाम् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=277-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छिक्कन
छिक्कन n. (-नं) Sneezing.<BR>	 f. (-नी) A small plant, (Artemisia sternutato-<BR>ria.)<BR> E. छिक्क nominal verb, to sneeze, ल्युट् aff. or छिक् इति अव्यक्तं<BR>नासिकाशब्दं कनति शब्दायते कन-अच् गौरा-ङीष् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=277-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छिक्का
छिक्का f. (-क्का) Sneezing.<BR> E. छिक् imitative sound, and क what utters,<BR>from कै with ड and टाप् affs. छिक् इति अव्यक्तं शब्दं करोति कृ-ड । क्षुते ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=277-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छिक्कक
छिक्कक mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>	 1. Sternutatory.<BR>	 2. Sneezing.<BR>	 f. (-का) A plant,<BR>(Artemisia sternutatoria.)<BR> E. छिक्क nominal verb, to sneeze, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=277-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छित|छितं
छित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Cut, divided.<BR> E. छो to cut, affix क्त deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=277-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छित्ति|छित्तिः
छित्ति f. (-त्तिः)<BR>	 1. Cutting, division.<BR>	 2. A plant, (Galedupa arborea:)<BR>see करज.<BR> E. छिद् to cut, affix कर्त्तरि क्तिच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=277-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छित्वर|छित्वरः
छित्वर mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>	 1. Roguish, fraudulent, knavish, a knave.<BR>	 2. Hos-<BR>tile, inimical, a foe.<BR>	 3. Cutting or fit for cutting, (a weapon, &c.)<BR>E. छिद् to cut, ष्वरप् Uṇādi affix, and त optionally substituted for the<BR>radical final, otherwise छिद्वर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=277-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छित्वा
छित्वा ind. Having cut or divided.<BR> E. छिद् to cut, क्त्वा aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=277-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छिद
छिद (औ, इर) औ छिदिर r. 7th cl. (छिनत्ति, छिन्ते) To divide to split, to cut,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=277-b" target="_blank">Page277-b+ 60</a>]<BR>&c. With the prefix आङ्, To seize, to lay hold of. With the prefix<BR>उत्, To slay or kill. रुधा-उभ-सक-अनिट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=277-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छिद्
छिद् mfn. (-द् or -त्) Cutting, destroying, who or what cuts.<BR> E. छिद् to<BR>cut, affix क्विप्. छेदनकर्त्तरि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=277-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छिदक|छिदकं
छिदक n. (-कं) INDRA'S thunderbolt.<BR> E. छिद् to cut or split, affix क्वुन्; also<BR>छिदिक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=277-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छिदा
छिदा f. (-दा) Cutting, dividing.<BR> E. छिद as above, affixes भावे अङ् and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=277-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छिदि|छिदिः
छिदि f. (-दिः) An axe.<BR> E. छिद् to cut, इन् Uṇādi affix and the radical<BR>vowel unchanged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=277-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छिदिर|छिदिरः
छिदिर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Fire.<BR>	 2. A rope, a cord.<BR>	 3. A sword.<BR>	 4. An axe, a<BR>hatchet.<BR> E. छिद् to cut, किरच् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=277-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छिदुर|छिदुरः
छिदुर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>	 1. Cutting, dividing, what cuts or divides.<BR>	 2. A<BR>knave.<BR>	 3. Hostile, a foe.<BR> E. छिद् to cut, and कुरच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=277-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छिद्र|छिद्रं
छिद्र r. 10th cl. (छिद्रयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To pierce, to bore, to perforate, to<BR>make openings or holes.<BR>	 2. To perforate the ear for rings &c. चु-<BR>उभ-सक-सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=277-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छिद्र|छिद्रं
छिद्र n. (-द्रं)<BR>	 1. A hole, a vacuity, a perforation, &c.<BR>	 2. Fault, defect,<BR>flaw (moral or physical.)<BR>	 3. A weak side.<BR>	 4. Infirmity.<BR> E. छिद् to<BR>pierce, Uṇādi affix रक्, or छिद्र अच्-वा ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=277-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छिद्रकर्ण
छिद्रकर्ण mfn. (-र्णः-र्णी-र्णं) Having the ears pierced.<BR> E. छिद्र, and कर्ण the<BR>ear, छिद्रयुक्तः कर्णः अस्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=277-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छिद्रानुसारिन्
छिद्रानुसारिन् mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि) Looking out for faults or flaws.<BR> E. छिद्र,<BR>and अनुसारिन् who pursues.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=277-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छिद्रान्तर्|छिद्रांतर्
छिद्रान्तर् m. (-न्तः) A reed.<BR> E. छिद्र, and अन्तर् within. छिद्रम् अन्तः मध्ये यस्य । नले ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=277-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छिद्रान्वेषिन्
छिद्रान्वेषिन् mfn. (-षी-षिणी-षि) Seeking for faults, malicious.<BR> E. छिद्र, and<BR>अन्वेषिन् searching.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=277-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छिद्रित|छिद्रितः
छिद्रित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Perforated, pierced, having holes or openings. E.<BR>छिद्र to pierce, affix कर्मणि क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=277-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छिद्वर
छिद्वर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) See छित्वर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=277-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छिन्न|छिन्नं
छिन्न mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं) Cut, divided.<BR>	 f. (-न्ना)<BR>	 1. A whore, a harlot.<BR>	 2. A<BR>tree: see गुडूची.<BR> E. छिद् to cut, affix क्त, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=277-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छिन्नक
छिन्नक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Cut a little, incised, not cut off.<BR> E. कन् added<BR>to छिन्न.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=277-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छिन्नकर्ण
छिन्नकर्ण mfn. (-र्णः-र्णी-र्णं) Having the ears cut off.<BR> E. छिन्न, and कर्ण the<BR>ear. छिन्नः कर्णोऽस्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=277-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छिन्नकेश
छिन्नकेश mfn. (-शः-शा-शं) Shorn, shaven.<BR> E. छिन्न, and केश the hair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=277-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छिन्नधन्वन्
छिन्नधन्वन् m. (-न्वा) A warrior whose bow has been cut or broken by his<BR>enemy's arrow.<BR> E. छिन्न, and धन्वन् a bow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=277-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छिन्ननासिक
छिन्ननासिक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Noseless, having had the nose cut off. E.<BR>छिन्न, and नासिका the nose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=277-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छिन्ननास्य
छिन्ननास्य mfn. (-स्यः-स्या-स्यं) Having the rope that passes through the<BR>nose of a draft ox broken.<BR> E. छिन्न, and नास्य the nose-rein.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=277-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छिन्नबन्धन
छिन्नबन्धन mfn. (-नः-नी-नं) Loosed, liberated.<BR> E. छिन्न, and बन्धन binding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=277-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छिन्नभिन्न
छिन्नभिन्न mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं) Cut up, destroyed, scattered.<BR> E. छिन्न, and भिन्न<BR>broken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=277-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छिन्नमस्त
छिन्नमस्त mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं) Decapitated.<BR>	 f. (-स्ता) A form of DURGĀ with-<BR>out her head.<BR> E. छिन्न, and मस्त the head; also with कन् added छिन्न<BR>मस्तक, छिन्नमस्तका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=277-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छिन्नरुहा
छिन्नरुहा f. (-हा) A tree, (Menispermum glabrum:) see गुडूची.<BR> E. छन्न cut,<BR>and रुहा what grows; growing again after being cut. छिन्नः सन्<BR>रोहति रुह-क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=277-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छिन्नवत्
छिन्नवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Having cut or cut off.<BR> E. छिन्न, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=277-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छिन्नवेशिका
छिन्नवेशिका f. (-का) A plant, commonly Akanadi, (Cissampelos hexan-<BR>dra.)<BR> E. छिन्न what is cut, (a wound,) and विश् to enter, कन् affix,<BR>and the fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=277-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छिन्नसंशय
छिन्नसंशय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Confirmed, confident, free from doubt.<BR> E. छिन्न,<BR>and संशय doubt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=277-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छुछुन्दरी|छुच्छुन्दरी
छुछुन्दरी f. (-री) The musk rat, or shrew. (छुंँचो) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=277-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छुट
छुट r. 6th and 10th cls. (छुटति, छोटयति-ते) To cut; also चुट्, चु० उभ०<BR>पक्षे तु० कुटादि० पर० सक० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=277-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छुड
छुड r. 1st and 6th cls. (-छोडति, छुडति) to cover.<BR> E. तुदा० पर० सक० सेट् ।<BR>भ्वा० पर० ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=278-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छुद्र|छुद्रं
छुद्र n. (-द्रं)<BR>	 1. Retaliating, returning, remedying.<BR>	 2. A ray.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=278-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छुप|छुपः
छुप (औ) औछुप r. 6th cl. (छुपति) To touch. तुदा-पर-सक-अनिट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=278-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छुप|छुपः
छुप m. (-पः)<BR>	 1. A small tree, a shrub, a bush.<BR>	 2. Touch, touching.<BR>	 3.<BR>Air, wind.<BR>	 4. War, combat.<BR> E. छुप् to touch, affix कर्त्तरि क, घञर्घेक<BR>वा । आधारे-क, युद्धे ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=278-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छुर
छुर r. 1st and 6th cls. (छोरति छुरति) To cut. भ्वा० पर० सक० सेट् । तदा०<BR>कुटादि० पर० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=278-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छुरा
छुरा f. (-रा) Lime.<BR> E. छुर् to cut, क and टाप् affs. (कलिचन्) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=278-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छुरिका
छुरिका f. (-का) A knife.<BR> E. छुर् to cut, क्वुन् affix, and the fem form; also<BR>with क and ङीष् affixes, छुरी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=278-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छुरित|छुरितं
छुरित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Cut.<BR>	 2. Inlaid, set, coated, spread.<BR>	 3. Blended<BR>intermingled.<BR> E. छुर् to cut, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=278-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छुरितोदर
छुरितोदर mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>	 1. Pierced, transpierced.<BR>	 2. Run through the<BR>belly.<BR> E. छुरित, and उदर the belly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=278-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छुरी
छुरी f. (-री) A knife: see छुरिका.<BR> E. छुर-क गौराः० ङीष् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=278-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छृद
छृद (उ and इर) उछृदिर r. 7th cl. (-छृणत्ति-छिंत्ते)<BR>	 1. To shine 2. To vomit.<BR>3. To play. (ई) छृदी r. 1st and 10th cls. (छर्दति छर्दयति-ते) To light to<BR>kindle. देवने दीप्तौ च अक वमने सक० रुधा० उभ० सेट् । सन्दोपने वा चु० उभ०<BR>पक्षे भ्वा० पर० सक० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=278-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छृप
छृप (ई) छृपी r. 1st and 10th cls. (छर्पति छर्पयति-ते) To light. to inflame or<BR>kindle. याचने द्विक० शब्दे अक वा चुरा० उभ० पक्षे भ्वा० पर० सक० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=278-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छेक|छेकः
छेक mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>	 1. Tame, domesticated as a bird or beast.<BR>	 2. Citizen<BR>town-bred, rakish, buckish, smart, trained in the acuteness and<BR>vice of towns.<BR> E. छो to cut, affix उकन्, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=278-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छेकोक्ति|छेकोक्तिः
छेकोक्ति f. (-क्तिः) Indirect speech, insinuation, double entendre, hint, &c.<BR>E. छेक city bred, and उक्ति saying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=278-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छेत्तव्य
छेत्तव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं) To be cut, to be cut off, &c.<BR> E. छिद् to cut, तव्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=278-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छेत्तृ
छेत्तृ mfn. (-त्ता-त्त्री-त्तृ)<BR>	 1. Who or what cuts.<BR>	 2. Solving, resolving,<BR>(doubts, &c.)<BR> E. छिद् to cut, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=278-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छेद|छेदः
छेद r. 10th cl. (छेदयति-ते) To cut, to cover, to divide, but especially into<BR>two parts. चरा० उभ० सक० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=278-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छेद|छेदः
छेद m. (-दः)<BR>	 1. Cutting, dividing.<BR>	 2. A part, a portion.<BR>	 3. Solving, dis-<BR>sipating, (as doubt.)<BR>	 4. The denominator of a fraction.<BR>	 5. The<BR>divisor.<BR> E. छिद् to cut, affix भावे घञ्, or अच् वा ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=278-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छेदकर|छेदकरः
छेदकर mfn. (-रः-रा-री-रं) Cutting.<BR>	 m. (-रः) A wood-cutter.<BR> E. छेद, and कर<BR>who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=278-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छेदन|छेदनं
छेदन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Cutting, dividing.<BR>	 2. A part, a portion.<BR> E. छिद् to cut, affix भावे ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=278-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छेदनीय|छेदनीयः
छेदनीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) To be cut or divided.<BR> E. छिद to cut, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=278-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छेदि|छेदिः
छेदि mfn. (-दिः-दिः-दि) Cutting, dividing, a cutter, &c.<BR> E. छिद् to cut,<BR>Uṇādi affix इन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=278-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छेदित|छेदितं
छेदित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Cut, divided.<BR> E. छिद् to cut, affix क्त, or छेदो<BR>जातोऽस्य तारकादित्वात् इतच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=278-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छेदितव्य
छेदितव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं) To be cut or divided.<BR> E. छिद् to cut, तव्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=278-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छेद्य
छेद्य mfn. (-द्यः-द्या-द्यं) To be cut or divided.<BR>	 n. (-द्यं) Amputation, exscis-<BR>sion.<BR> E. छिद् to cut, ण्यत् aff. छेत्तुं योग्यः कर्मणि योग्यार्थे ण्यत् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=278-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छेमण्ड|छेमंड|छेमंडः|छेमण्डः
छेमण्ड m. (-ण्डः) A fatherless son: see छमण्ड पृषोदरादित्वात् अतः एत्त्वम् ।<BR>मातृपितृहीनेवालके ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=278-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छेलु|छेलुः
छेलु m. (-लुः) A medicinal plant, (Conyza anthelmintica.)<BR> E. छो वा डेलु ।<BR>सोमराज्याम् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=278-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छैदिक|छैदिकः
छैदिक m. (-कः) A ratan, a cane.<BR> E. छेद cutting, ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=278-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छो
छो r. 4th cl. (छ्यति) To cut, to mow, to reap, &c. दिवा० पर० सक० अनिट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=278-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छोटिका
छोटिका f. (-का) Snapping the thumb and fore-finger together.<BR> E. छुट्<BR>to touch, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=278-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छोटिन्
छोटिन् m. (-टी) A fisherman.<BR> E. छुट् to cut, णिन् affix, deriv. irr. कैवर्त्ते ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=278-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छोरण|छोरणं
छोरण n. (-णं) Abandoning, leaving.<BR> E. छुर् to cut, affix मावे ल्युट् ।<BR>परित्यागे ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=278-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छोलङ्ग|छोलंगः|छोलङ्गः
छोलङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः) A citron, a lime.<BR> E. छुर् वा अङ्गच्, रस्य लः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=278-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छ्यु
छ्यु r. 1st cl. (छ्यवते) To go, to move or approach: see च्यु । भ्वा० आत्म०<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=278-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज|जः
ज The third letter of the second class of consonants, corresponding<BR>to the letter J in jet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=278-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज|जः
ज mfn. (जः-जा-जं)<BR>	 1. Speedy, swift.<BR>	 2. Eaten.<BR>	 3. Victorious, triumph-<BR>ant, conquering or a conqueror. (जः)<BR>	 1. A name of Siva.<BR>	 2. A<BR>name of VIṢṆU.<BR>	 3. Birth, production.<BR>	 4. A parent, a progenitor.<BR>5. Poison.<BR>	 6. Enjoyment.<BR>	 7. Light, Iustre.<BR>	 8. Speed.<BR>	 9. An imp-<BR>a goblin.<BR> E. जन् to bear or to born, जि to conquer, or other roots,<BR>and ड aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=278-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जकुट|जकुटं|जकुटः
जकुट m. (-टः)<BR>	 1. The Malaya mountain.<BR>	 2. A dog.<BR>	 n. (-टं) The egg-<BR>plant. (Solanum melongena.) जं जातं कटति कुट-क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=278-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जक्ष
जक्ष r. 1st cl. (जक्षिति) 3rd plu. जक्षति)<BR>	 1. To eat.<BR>	 2. To laugh. (इ) जक्षि<BR>(जंक्षते) 1. To give.<BR>	 2. To go भक्षे सक० हासे अक० जक्षादि स्वपादि पर० सेट् ।<BR>दाने भ्वा० इदित् आत्म० सक० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=278-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जक्षण|जक्षणं
जक्षण n. (-णं) Eating.<BR> E. जक्ष् to eat. affix भावे ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=278-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जक्षि|जक्षिः
जक्षि f. (-क्षिः) Eating.<BR> E. जक्ष to eat, कि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=278-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जक्षिवस्
जक्षिवस् mfn. (-वान्-क्षुषी-वत्) Eating, who eats.<BR> E. जक्ष् to eat, वसु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=278-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जक्ष्म|जक्ष्मः
जक्ष्म m. (-क्ष्मः) Consumption, decline: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=278-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जक्ष्मन्
जक्ष्मन् m. (-क्ष्मा) Consumption, phthisis.<BR> E. यक्ष् to worship, and मनिन्<BR>affix; ज is substituded for the semi-vowel; also यक्ष्मन्, and with a<BR>final vowel जक्ष्म.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=278-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जगच्चक्षुस्
जगच्चक्षुस् m. (-क्षुः) The sun.<BR> E. जगत् the universe, and चक्षुस the eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=278-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जगत्
जगत् mfn. (-गन्-गती-गत्) Moveable, loco-motive, transitory, nf. (-त्-ती)<BR>The world, the universe.<BR>	 m. (-त्) Air, wind.<BR>	 f. (-ती)<BR>	 1. The earth.<BR>	 2.<BR>people, mankind.<BR>	 3. A sort of metre, a stanza of forty-eight syl-<BR>lables variously disposed so as to form thirty varieties.<BR>	 4. A field<BR>of Jambu flowers.<BR> E. गम् to go, Uṇādi affix अति, जग substituted for<BR>the root, and ङीप् fem. affix, or गम् as before, and शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=278-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जगतीधर|जगतीधरः
जगतीधर m. (-रः) A mountain.<BR> E. जगती, and धर what holds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=278-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जगतीपति|जगतीपतिः
जगतीपति m. (-तिः) A kind, a prince.<BR> E. जगती, and पति lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=278-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जगतीपाल
जगतीपाल m. (-लः) A king.<BR> E. जगती, and पाल who protects.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=278-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जगतीरुह
जगतीरुह m. (-हः) A tree.<BR> E. जगती, and रुह what grows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=278-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जगत्कर्तृ|जगत्कर्त्तृ
जगत्कर्तृ m. (-र्ता) A name of BRAMHA.<BR> E. जगत्, and कर्तृ a maker, the<BR>creator of the world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=278-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जगत्कृत्स्न
जगत्कृत्स्न n. (-स्नं) The universe.<BR> E. जगत्, and कृत्स्न whole.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=278-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जगत्क्षय
जगत्क्षय m. (-यः) The destruction of the world.<BR> E. जगत्, and क्षय loss.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=278-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जगत्त्रय
जगत्त्रय n. (-यं) The three worlds, or heaven, earth, and hell.<BR> E. जगत्, and<BR>त्रय three.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=278-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जगत्पति|जगत्पतिः
जगत्पति m. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. A king.<BR>	 2. A deity.<BR> E. जगत्, and पति master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=278-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जगत्प्राण|जगत्प्राणः
जगत्प्राण m. (-णः) Air, wind.<BR> E. जगत् the universe, and प्राण breath or<BR>being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=278-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जगत्समग्र
जगत्समग्र n. (-ग्रं) The universe.<BR> E. जगत्, and समग्र whole.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=278-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जगत्सर्व|जगत्सर्व्व
जगत्सर्व n. (-र्वं) The whole world.<BR> E. जगत्, and सर्व whole.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=278-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जगत्साक्षिन्
जगत्साक्षिन् m. (-क्षी) The sun.<BR> E. जगत् the universe, and साक्षिन् witness,<BR>spectator.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=278-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जगत्स्रष्टृ
जगत्स्रष्टृ m. (-ष्टा) The creator of the world, BRAMHA.<BR> E. जगत्, and स्रष्टृ<BR>creator.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=278-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जगदन्त
जगदन्त m. (-न्तः) The end of the world.<BR> E. जगत्, and अन्त end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=278-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जगदम्बा|जगदंबा
जगदम्बा f. (-म्बा) A name of DURGĀ.<BR> E. जगत्, and अम्बा mother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=278-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जगदात्मक
जगदात्मक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Identical with the world.<BR> E. जगत्, and आत्मक<BR>same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=278-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जगदात्मन्
जगदात्मन् m. (-त्मा) The supreme spirit.<BR> E. जगत्, and आत्मन् the soul.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=278-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जगदाधार|जगदाधारः
जगदाधार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Air, wind.<BR>	 2. A stay or supporter of the universe.<BR>E. जगत् the world, and आधार support.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=278-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जगदीश|जगदीशः
जगदीश m. (-शः) An epithet of VIṢṆU.<BR> E. जगत् the universe, and ईश<BR>lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=278-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जगदेकपावन
जगदेकपावन mfn. (-नः-नी-न) Purifying or sanctifying the world<BR> E. जगत्-<BR>एक chief, and पावन purifying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=278-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जगद्गौरी
जगद्गौरी f. (-री) A name of MANASADEVI, the deified wife of the sage<BR>JARATKARU, and sister of VĀSUKI.<BR> E. जगत् the world,<BR>and गरी the goddess GAURI; a terrestrial GAURI; her rela-<BR>tionship to the snake breed is supposed to give her an influence<BR>over them, which is implored frequently by the Hindus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=279-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जगद्धातिन्
जगद्धातिन् mfn. (-ती-तिनी-ति) Destroying the world, destructive, hostile<BR>to mankind.<BR> E. जगत, and घातिन् who destroys.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=279-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जगद्धात्री
जगद्धात्री f. (-त्री) A name of DURGĀ.<BR> E. जगत्, and धात्री a nurse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=279-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जगद्बल|जगद्बलः
जगद्बल m. (-लः) Air, wind.<BR> E. जगत् the universe, and बल surrounding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=279-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जगद्योनि|जगद्योनिः
जगद्योनि m. (-निः)<BR>	 1. A name of ŚIVA.<BR>	 2. A name of VIṢṆU.<BR>	 f. (-निः)<BR>The earth.<BR> E. जगत् the universe, and योनि womb, or place of pro-<BR>duction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=279-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जगद्वहा
जगद्वहा f. (-हा) The earth.<BR> E. जगत् the universe, and वह what bears.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=279-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जगद्विनाश|जगद्विनाशः
जगद्विनाश m. (-शः) The expiration of a Yuga or period of the world's<BR>existence.<BR> E. जगत् the world, and विनाश destruction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=279-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जगनु|जगनुः
जगनु m. (-नुः)<BR>	 1. Fire or its deity.<BR>	 2. An animal or insect.<BR> E. गम् to<BR>go, deriv. irr. जगता नम्यते नम-वा कर्मणि डुवा ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=279-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जगन्नाथ|जगन्नाथः
जगन्नाथ m. (-थः) A form of VIṢṆU.<BR> E. जगत् the universe, and नाथ lord;<BR>a peculiar and celebrated idol of this name is worshipped on the<BR>Coromandal coast, in Orissa, and pilgrimages are made to the<BR>shrine of JAGANNATHA from all parts of India.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=279-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जगन्नाथक्षेत्र
जगन्नाथक्षेत्र n. (-त्रं) The shrine of JAGANNATHA and surrounding dis-<BR>trict.<BR> E. जगन्नाथ, and क्षेत्र holy place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=279-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जगन्निवास|जगन्निवासः
जगन्निवास m. (-सः)<BR>	 1. Worldly existence.<BR>	 2. A deity, as VIṢṆU, in<BR>whom the world exists.<BR> E. जगत्, and निवास abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=279-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जगन्नु|जगन्नुः
जगन्नु m. (-न्नुः)<BR>	 1. Fire.<BR>	 2. An animal.<BR> E. जगत्, and नु to send, डु affix;<BR>also जगनु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=279-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जगन्मातृ
जगन्मातृ f. (-ता) A name of DURGĀ.<BR> E. जगत्, and मातृ mother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=279-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जगन्वस्
जगन्वस् mfn. (-वान्-न्वुषी-न्वत्) Who or what goes.<BR> E. गम् to go, वसु affix,<BR>root repeated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=279-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जगर|जगरः
जगर m. (-रः) Armour, mail.<BR> E. जागृ to awaken, अच् affix, deriv. irr.;<BR>also जागर । जागर्त्ति युद्धे अनेन जागृ-अच् । कवचे ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=279-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जगल|जगलः
जगल m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. Vinous liquor for distilling.<BR>	 2. Armour: see the pre-<BR>ceding.<BR> E. गल् to ooze, अच् affix, and the root reduplicated; other-<BR>wise ल interchanged with रः see जगर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=279-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जग्ध|जग्धं
जग्ध mfn. (-ग्धः-ग्धा-ग्धं) Eaten.<BR>	 n. (-ग्धं) Food.<BR> E. अद् to eat, affix कर्मणि<BR>भावे वा क्त, and जग्ध substituted for the regular form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=279-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जग्धि|जग्धिः
जग्धि f. (-ग्धिः)<BR>	 1. Eating.<BR>	 2. Eating together or in company.<BR>	 3. Food,<BR>victuals.<BR> E. अद् to eat, क्तिन् affix, and जग्धि substituted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=279-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जग्मि|जग्मिः
जग्मि f. (-ग्मिः) Air, wind.<BR> E. गम् to go, किन् द्बित्वम् affix, root reiterated,<BR>and form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=279-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जग्मिवस्
जग्मिवस् mfn. (-वान्-ग्मुषी-वत्) Who or what goes.<BR> E. गम् to go, वसु affix,<BR>इट् inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=279-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जघन|जघनं
जघन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Mons veneris.<BR>	 2. The hip and loins.<BR> E. हन् to kill or hurt,<BR>जघन substituted for the radical, and अच् Uṇādi aff. वक्र हन्ति हन-यङ्<BR>अच् पृषो० ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=279-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जघनकूपक
जघनकूपक m. du. (-कौ) The hollows of the loins of a handsome woman.<BR>E. जघन the loins, and कूपक a well or pit. जघनस्य कूपः इव कायति कै-क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=279-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जघनचपला
जघनचपला f. (-ला)<BR>	 1. A woman active as in dancing.<BR>	 2. A species of<BR>the Aryaya metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=279-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जघनेफला
जघनेफला f. (-ला) Opposite leaved fig tree, (Ficus oppositi-folia, Rox.)<BR>E. जघन the haunch, &c. here put for the stem, and फल fruit;<BR>growing round the stem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=279-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जघन्य|जघन्यः
जघन्य mfn. (-न्यः-न्या-न्यं)<BR>	 1. Last, hindmost.<BR>	 2. Low, vile, base.<BR>	 3. Worst,<BR>vilest, lowest.<BR>	 n. (-न्यं) The penis.<BR>	 m. (-न्यः) A Śūdra or man of the<BR>fourth tribe.<BR> E. जघन tke loins, &c. and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=279-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जघन्यगुणवृत्तिस्थ
जघन्यगुणवृत्तिस्थ mfn. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थं) Vile, addicted to low pursuits.<BR> E. जघन्य<BR>vile, गुण quality, वृत्ति practice, and स्थ standing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=279-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जघन्यज|जघन्यजः
जघन्यज m. (-जः)<BR>	 1. A Śūdra.<BR>	 2. A younger brother or younger born. E.<BR>जघन्य last, and ज born. जघन्ये चरमे जायते जन-ड ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=279-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जघन्वस्
जघन्वस् mfn. (-न्वान्-नुषी-न्वत्) Who or what kills.<BR> E. हन् to kill वसु affix,<BR>root repeated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=279-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जघ्नि|जघ्निः
जघ्नि m. (-घ्निः) A sharp or offensive weapon.<BR> E. हन् to kill, affix किन्, द्वित्वञ्च, form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=279-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जघ्नु|जघ्नुः
जघ्नु mfn. (-घ्नुः-घ्नुः-घ्नु) Striking, beating, injuring, one who does so. E.<BR>हन् to hurt or kill, कु द्वित्वञ्च affix, and the radical reiterated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=279-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जघ्मिवस्
जघ्मिवस् mfn. (-वान्-घ्मुषी-वत्) Killing, who or what kills.<BR> E. हन to kill, वसु<BR>affix, root repeated, इट् inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=279-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जङ्गपूग
जङ्गपूग n. (-गं) Wickedness, sin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=279-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जङ्गम|जंगम|जङ्गमः
जङ्गम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं) Locomotive, moveable, that which has motion as<BR>opposed to that which is stationary.<BR> E. गम् to go affix यङ्-अच्<BR>the radical reduplicated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=279-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जङ्गमकुटी|जंगमकुटी
जङ्गमकुटी f. (-टी) A parasol, a Chattah or umbrella.<BR> E. जङ्गम moveable,<BR>and कुटी a house. जङ्गमा कुटी इव । छत्रे ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=279-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जङ्गल|जंगल|जङ्गलं|जङ्गलः
जङ्गल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Desert, solitary, waste, jungle, wild, &c.<BR>	 n. (-लं)<BR>Flesh.<BR> E. जङ्ग for जङ्गम moveable, and ल what brings, or takes, i. e.<BR>appertaining to moveable beings, as beasts birds, &c. गल-यङ्-अच्<BR>पृषोदरादित्वात् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=279-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जङ्गाल|जंगाल|जंगालः|जङ्गालः
जङ्गाल m. (-लः) A land mark, a limit, a boundary, a ridge of earth run-<BR>ning along the edge of a field for collecting water and forming a<BR>passage over it.<BR> E. जङ्ग locomotion, and ल what makes, आङ् pre-<BR>fixed, with the sense of limitation. गम-यङ् लुक् वा ड । जङ्गं कुटिलगतिं<BR>अलति वारयति अल् अण् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=279-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जङ्गुल|जंगुल|जंगुलं
जङ्गुल n. (-लं) Poison, venom.<BR> E. जङ्गु locomotive, (an animal), and ल<BR>what destroys, from लु to cut, affix ड । गम यङ् लुक् वा डुल । विषे ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=279-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जङ्घा|जंघा
जङ्घा f. (-ङ्घा) The leg.<BR> E. जन् to be born, जङ्घ substituted for the radical,<BR>and अच् aff. जङ्घन्यते कुटिलं गच्छति गत्यर्थकस्य हन्तेः कौटिल्ये यङ्लुकि अच्<BR>पृषो० ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=279-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जङ्घाकारिक|जंघाकारिक|जङ्घाकारिकः
जङ्घाकारिक m. (-कः) A courier, a runner, an express.<BR> E. जङ्घा a leg, and<BR>कर a toll, affix ठन्; who levies a toll by his legs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=279-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जङ्घात्राण|जंघात्राण|जङ्घात्राणं
जङ्घात्राण n. (-णं) Cuisses or greaves.<BR> E. जङ्घा the leg, and त्राण what pre-<BR>serves. त्रायते अनेन त्रै करणे ल्युट् । जङ्घासन्नाहे ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=279-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जङ्घाल|जंघाल|जङ्घालः
जङ्घाल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Quick, rapid, going quickly.<BR>	 m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. A<BR>courier.<BR>	 2. A deer, an antelope.<BR> E. जङ्घा the leg, and अल able, stout,<BR>or जङ्घा वेगवती अस्ति अस्य लच् । धावके ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=279-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जज|जजं|जजः
जज r. 1st cl. (जजति) also (इ) जजि (जंजति) To fight. भ्वा० पर० अक-सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=279-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जज|जजं|जजः
जज m. (-जः) A warrior.<BR> E. जज् to fight, and अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=279-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जजौजस्
जजौजस् n. (-जः) Prowess, valour.<BR> E. जज, and ओजस् power.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=279-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जञ्जपूक|जंजपूक|जञ्जपूकः
जञ्जपूक mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>	 1. Muttering repeatedly.<BR>	 2. Muttering evil<BR>prayers or charms.<BR>	 m. (-कः) An ascetic, a devotee, one who does so.<BR>E. जप् to mutter, reiterative form ऊक aff. जप-यङ् ऊक । अतिशयजपशीले<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=279-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जट
जट r. 1st cl. (जटति) To clot, to be entangled, as hair. भ्वा-प-अक सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=279-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जटा
जटा f. (-टा)<BR>	 1. The hair matted as worn by the god ŚIVA, and by<BR>ascetics; the long hairs occasionally clotted together, and brought<BR>over the head so as to project like a horn from the forehead, at<BR>other times allowed to fall carelessly over the back and shoulders.<BR>2. The root of a tree, a fibrous root.<BR>	 3. Spikenard: see जटामांसी.<BR>	 4.<BR>A plant, (Asparagus racemosa.)<BR>	 5. Cowach.<BR>	 6. Hedysarum, vari-<BR>ous species.<BR> E. जट् to entangle, अच् affix; or जन् to be produced,<BR>टन् Uṇādi affix, and the radical final rejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=279-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जटाजूट|जटाजूटः
जटाजूट m. (-टः)<BR>	 1. A quantity of clotted hair.<BR>	 2. ŚIVA'S hair.<BR> E. जटा,<BR>and जूट the same. जटानां जूटः बन्धः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=279-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जटाज्वाल|जटाज्वालः
जटाज्वाल m. (-लः) A lamp.<BR> E. जटा entangled hair, and ज्वाला flame.<BR>जटा इव ज्वाला अस्य । प्रदीपे ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=279-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जटाटङ्क|जटाटंक|जटाटङ्कः
जटाटङ्क m. (-ङ्कः) ŚIVA.<BR> E. जटा as above, टकि to bind, affix अच्, जटा टङ्कः<BR>इव अस्य । महादेवे ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=279-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जटाटीर|जटाटीरः
जटाटीर m. (-रः) ŚIVA.<BR> E. जटा as above, अट् to go, and ईरन् affix; some<BR>copies read जटाचीर । जटाम् अटति ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=279-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जटाधर|जटाधरः
जटाधर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A name of ŚIVA.<BR>	 2. A Jina or Jaina deified saint.<BR>3. Any mendicant wearing the braid of hair.<BR> E. जटा entangled<BR>hair, and धर possessor; also with धारिन्, जटाधारिन् (-री)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=279-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जटामांसी
जटामांसी f. (-सी) Indian spikenard, (Valeriana jatamansi.)<BR> E. जटा entan-<BR>gled hair or root, and मांसी the same plant. जटां मन्यते ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=280-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जटायु|जटायुः
जटायु m. (-युः)<BR>	 1. A fabulous bird, the son of ARUṆA, killed by<BR>RAVANA.<BR>	 2. Bdellium.<BR> E. जटा accumulation, आयु or आयुस् life;<BR>long-lived; hence also जटायुस् m. (-युः) जटां याति या-कु-जटा-ऊर्णा<BR>युच् वा, जट संहतौ अच्, जटं संहतम् आयुः अस्य वा ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=280-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जटाल|जटालः
जटाल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Wearing clotted hair.<BR>	 m. (-लः) The Indian fig<BR>tree.<BR>	 2. Zedoary.<BR>	 3. Bdellium.<BR>	 f. (-ला) Spikenard: see जटामांसी. E.<BR>जाट as above, and लच् affix of possession.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=280-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जटावत्|जटावन्त्
जटावत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Having clotted hair.<BR>	 f. (-ती) Spikenard,<BR>(Valeriana jatamansi.)<BR> E. जटा, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=280-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जटि|जटिः
जटि f. (-टिः)<BR>	 1. Waved-leaf fig tree, (F. venosa:) see जटिन्.<BR>	 2. Assem-<BR>blage, multitude.<BR>	 3. Clotted hair: see जटा.<BR> E. जट् to collect,<BR>affix इन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=280-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जटिन्
जटिन् mfn. (-टी-टिनी-टि) Having clotted hair, m. (-टी) Waved-leaf fig<BR>tree: see जटि.<BR> E. जटा as above, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=280-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जटिल|जटिलः
जटिल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Having any clotted or entangled hair.<BR>	 m. (-लः) A<BR>lion.<BR>	 f. (-ला)<BR>	 1. Indian spikenard.<BR>	 2. Long pepper.<BR>	 3. Orris.<BR> E. जटा,<BR>and अस्त्यर्थे इलच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=280-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जटी
जटी f. (-टी) Waved-leaf fig tree: see जटि.<BR> E. जट् to entangle, इ Uṇādi<BR>affix, and ङीष् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=280-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जटुल|जटुलः
जटुल m. (-लः) A freckle, a mark.<BR> E. जट् to accumulate, उलच् affix;<BR>also जडुल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=280-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जठर|जठरं|जठरः
जठर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>	 1. Hard, firm.<BR>	 2. Bound, tied.<BR>	 mn. (-रः-रं) The bel-<BR>ly.<BR> E. जम् to eat, अर् Uṇādi affix, and ठच् substituted for the radi-<BR>cal final.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=280-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जठरज्वाला
जठरज्वाला f. (-ला) Belly-ache, colic, enteritis.<BR> E. जठर, and ज्वाला<BR>burning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=280-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जठरनुद्
जठरनुद् m. (-नुत्) Cassia fistula.<BR> E. जठर the belly, and नुद् a laxative.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=280-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन|जनः
जन m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. Man, individually or collectively, a man, mankind.<BR>2. The universe.<BR>	 3. A division of the universe or Loka, the resi-<BR>dence of deified mortals: see जनलोक.<BR>	 3. A low man, a wretch.<BR>	 f.<BR>(-नी) A mother, &c. see जनि.<BR>	 f. (-ना) Birth, production.<BR> E. जन् to<BR>be born, affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=280-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनक|जनकः
जनक m. (-कः) A father, a progenitor.<BR>	 2. The name of a king, sover-<BR>eign of Mithila, and father of Sita.<BR> E. जन to be born, and णिच्<BR>ण्वुल aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=280-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनकता
जनकता f. (-ता) The property of generation, productiveness, paternity.<BR>E. जनक, and तल् affix; also with त्व, जनकत्वम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=280-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनकात्मजा
जनकात्मजा f. (-जा) A name of SITA the wife of RAMA.<BR> E. जनक as above,<BR>and आत्मजा daughter; also similar compounds, as जनकतनया, जन-<BR>कसुता, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=280-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनङ्गम|जनंगम|जनंगमः
जनङ्गम m. (-मः) A Chandala, a man of low or degraded tribe.<BR> E. जन<BR>a mean man, and गम् to go, खच् युम् च aff. जनेभ्यो गच्छति वहिः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=280-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनता
जनता f, (-ता)<BR>	 1. Mankind, a number of men.<BR>	 2. Manhood.<BR>	 3. Genera-<BR>tion, birth.<BR> E. जन a man, and तल् affix; also with त्व, जनत्वम् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=280-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनत्रा
जनत्रा f. (-त्रा) An umbrella or parasol.<BR> E. जन the person, and त्रा saving;<BR>from sun and rain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=280-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनन|जननं|जननः
जनन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Birth, production.<BR>	 2. Family, race, lineage.<BR>	 f. (-नी)<BR>	 1.<BR>A mother.<BR>	 2. Tenderness, compassion.<BR>	 3. A plant, commonly Chak-<BR>wat; also जननि and जनी.<BR>	 4. A bat.<BR>	 5. Arabian jasmine.<BR>	 6. Vale-<BR>rian.<BR>	 mf. (-नः-नी) A parent, a progenitor.<BR> E. जन् to bear or be born,<BR>affix भावे ल्युट्, and ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=280-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जननि|जननिः
जननि f. (-निः)<BR>	 1. A fragrant plant: see the preceding.<BR>	 2. Birth, pro-<BR>duction.<BR> E. जन् to be born, affix अनि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=280-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनपद|जनपदः
जनपद m. (-दः)<BR>	 1. Any inhabited country.<BR>	 2. Man, mankind<BR> E. जन man,<BR>and पद going. जनाः पद्यन्ते गच्छन्ति यत्र । पद आधारे घ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=280-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनप्रवाद|जनप्रवादः
जनप्रवाद m. (-दः) Rumour, report.<BR> E. जन man, and प्रवाद speech, from<BR>वद् to speak, with प्र prefixed, and घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=280-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनप्रिय|जनप्रियः
जनप्रिय mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>	 1. Agreeable to mankind.<BR>	 2. Philanthropic.<BR>	 m.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=280-b" target="_blank">Page280-b+ 60</a>]<BR>(-यः)<BR>	 1. Coriander seed.<BR>	 2. A tree, (Morunga hyperanthera.)<BR> E. जन,<BR>and प्रिय fond of. शोभाञ्जनबृक्षे, धन्याके, लोक प्रियमात्रे च ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=280-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनमेजय|जनमेजयः
जनमेजय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. The name of a king, son and successor to PARIK-<BR>SHIT.<BR>	 2. A son of PURU.<BR> E. जन in the second case, the world, एजृ<BR>to shine, affix णिच् and खश्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=280-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनयत्
जनयत् mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्) Begetting, engendering, producing.<BR> E. जन to<BR>be born, causal form, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=280-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनयितृ
जनयितृ mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ) Generating, begetting, producing, who or what<BR>does so.<BR>	 m. (-ता) A father, a progenitor.<BR>	 f. (-त्री) A mother.<BR> E. जन् in<BR>the causal form, to give birth, to engender, affix णिच् and तृच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=280-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनरव|जनरवः
जनरव m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. Rumour, report.<BR>	 2. Calumny, scandal.<BR> E. जन, and<BR>रव sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=280-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनलोक|जनलोकः
जनलोक m. (-कः) One of the seven Lokas or divisions of the world,<BR>the fifth, next above MAHARLOKA, where the sons of BRAMHA,<BR>and other pious men, reside.<BR> E. जन man and लोक a world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=280-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनवल्लभ|जनवल्लभः
जनवल्लभ mfn. (-भः-भा-भं) Kind to or fond of mankind.<BR> E. जन, and वल्लभ<BR>a friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=280-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनवाद|जनवादः
जनवाद m. (-दः) News, rumour, report.<BR> E. जन man, and वाद speech:<BR>see जनप्रवाद.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=280-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनश्रुति|जनश्रुतिः
जनश्रुति f. (-तिः) News, tidings, intelligence.<BR> E. जन mankind, and श्रुति<BR>that which is heard. जनेभ्यः श्रूयते श्रु-क्तिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=280-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनस्थान|जनस्थानं
जनस्थान n. (-नं) The forest Dandaka, (in the Deccan) the eastern part.<BR>of it.<BR> E. जन a world, and स्थान् a place; the resort of a world of<BR>demons.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=280-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनाचार|जनाचारः
जनाचार m. (-रः) Propriety, decorum, good conduct.<BR> E. जन mankind,<BR>and आचार moral observance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=280-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जगातिग
जगातिग mfn. (-गः-गा-गं) Superior, superhuman.<BR> E. जन, and अतिग going<BR>beyond.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=280-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनाधिनाथ|जनाधिनाथः
जनाधिनाथ m. (-थः)<BR>	 1. VIṢṆU.<BR>	 2. A king.<BR> E. जन, and अधिनाथ supreme<BR>lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=280-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनाव्
जनाव् m. (-नौः) A preserver or protector of mankind.<BR> E. जन, and अव् to<BR>preserve, क्विन् affix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=280-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनान्त|जनांत|जनान्तः
जनान्त m. (-न्तः) A district, an inhabited country.<BR> E. जन man, and अन्त<BR>boundary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=280-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनान्तिक|जनांतिक
जनान्तिक n. (-कं) Secret communication, whispering, speaking aside, &c.<BR>E. जन man, and अन्तिक near. त्रिपताककरेणान्यानपवार्य्यान्तरा क्वथा । अन्योन्या-<BR>मन्त्रणं यत् स्यात् जनान्ते तत् जनान्तिकम् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=280-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनार्दन|जनार्दनः|जनार्द्दन|जनार्द्दनः
जनार्दन m. (-नः) A name of VIṢṆU.<BR> E. जन mankind, and अर्दन worship-<BR>ing; whom men worship. जनैः अर्द्यते याच्यते पुरुषार्थलाभाय अर्द याचने<BR>कर्मणि ल्युट् । जनं जननम् अर्दति हिनस्ति ताडयति जनान् समुद्रवासिनः असुरभे-<BR>दान् अर्दयति वा कर्त्तरि ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=280-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनाशन|जनाशनः
जनाशन m. (-नः) A wolf.<BR> E. जन, and अशन food. जनान् अश्नाति अश भोजने ल्यु ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=280-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनाश्रय|जनाश्रयः
जनाश्रय m. (-यः) A temporary hall.<BR> E. जन man, and आश्रय an asylum.<BR>जनानां लोकानाम् आश्रयः । मण्डपे ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=280-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनि|जनिः
जनि f. (-निः-नी)<BR>	 1. A woman in general.<BR>	 2. A mother.<BR>	 3. Birth, pro-<BR>duction.<BR>	 4. The wife of a son, or brother's son, &c.<BR>	 5. A fragrant<BR>plant: see जतूका.<BR> E. जन् to be born or to bear, Uṇādi affix भावे इन्,<BR>and optionally वा ङीप् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=280-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनिक
जनिक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Producing.<BR>	 f. (-का) A woman, a wife, a mother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=280-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनित|जनितं
जनित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Engendered, begotten.<BR>	 2. Occasioned, occur-<BR>ring, produced.<BR> E. जन् to be born, causal form, णिच् क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=280-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनितस्वन
जनितस्वन m. (-नः) Sounding, making a noise.<BR> E. जनित, स्वन sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=280-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनितृ
जनितृ m. (-ता) A father.<BR>	 f. (-त्री) A mother.<BR> E. जन् to be born, (from<BR>whom) अन्तर्भूतण्यर्थे तृच् affix; and इट् inserted. पितरि मातरि च ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=280-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनितोद्यम
जनितोद्यम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं) Vigorous, energetic, making exertion. E.<BR>जनित, and उद्यम effort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=280-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनित्व|जनित्वः
जनित्व m. (-त्वः) A father.<BR>	 f. (-त्वा) A mother.<BR> E. जन् to be born, (from<BR>whom,) and णिच् इत्वन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=280-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनिमन्
जनिमन् m. (-मा) Birth, engenderment.<BR> E. जन् to be born, भावे मनिन्<BR>Uṇādi aff. जन्मनि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=280-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनीन
जनीन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Appropriate, good for, suitable.<BR> E. जन, and<BR>ख aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=281-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनु|जनुः
जनु f. (-नुः) Birth.<BR> E. जन् to be born, उ Uṇādi affix; also with ऊ affix<BR>जनू f. (-नूः)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=281-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनुस्
जनुस् n. (-नुः) Birth.<BR> E. जन् to be born, Uṇādi affix उसि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=281-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनेष्ट|जनेष्टः
जनेष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं) Desired or prized by mankind.<BR>	 f. (-ष्टा) Turmeric.<BR>E. जन, and इष्ट wished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=281-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनोदाहरण|जनोदाहरणं
जनोदाहरण n. (-णं) Fame, glory.<BR> E. जन mankind, and उदाहरण pre-<BR>eminence. जनैरुदाह्रियते उद् + आ + हृ-कर्मणि ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=281-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनौघ|जनौघः
जनौघ n. (-घं) A multitude, a mob.<BR> E. जन, and ओघ a heap.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=281-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन्तु|जंतु|जंतुः|जन्तुः
जन्तु m. (-न्तुः) Any animal, any being endowed with animal life; it<BR>is more usually applied however to beings of the lowest organiza-<BR>tion.<BR> E. जन् to be born, तुन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=281-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन्तुकम्बु|जंतुकंबु|जन्तुकम्बुः
जन्तुकम्बु m. (-म्बुः) A shell, a snail's shell, &c.<BR> E. जन्तु, and कम्बु a shell.<BR>जन्तुरूपः कम्बुः । कृमिशङ्खे ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=281-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन्तुका|जंतुका
जन्तुका f. (-का) Lac.<BR> E. क added to जन्तु. जन्तुभिः कायति कै क । लाक्षायाम् ।<BR>नाभिहिङ्गुनि च ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=281-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन्तुघ्न|जन्तुघ्नं|जन्तुघ्नः
जन्तुघ्न nf. (-घ्नं-घ्नी)<BR>	 1. A plant, and vermifuge: see विडङ्गः 2. Asafœtida.<BR>m. (-घ्नः) A citron.<BR> E. जन्तु an animal, (a worm) and घ्न what destroys.<BR>जन्तून् कृमीन् हन्ति हन-क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=281-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन्तुनाशन|जन्तुनाशनं
जन्तुनाशन n. (-नं) Asafætida.<BR> E. जन्तु, and नाशन destroying. जन्तून् नाशयति<BR>नश-णिच्-ल्यु । हिङ्गुनि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=281-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन्तुफल|जंतुफल|जन्तुफलः
जन्तुफल m. (-लः) Glomerous fig tree, (Ficus glomerata.)<BR> E. जन्तु an ani-<BR>mal, and फल a leaf; its leaves swarm with insects. जन्तवः फले अस्य ।<BR>उडम्बरे ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=281-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन्तुला
जन्तुला f. (-ला) A kind of grass, (Saccharum spontaneum.)<BR> E. जन्तु an<BR>animal or insect, and ला what gets. जन्तून् कीटान् लाति ला-क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=281-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन्म|जन्मं
जन्म mn. (-न्मः-न्मं) Birth: see जन्मन्.<BR> E. जन-वा-मन् । जन्मनि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=281-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन्मकील|जन्मकीलः
जन्मकील m. (-लः) VIṢṆU.<BR> E. जन्म birth, and कील the stay. जन्मनः कीलः इव<BR>रोधकत्वात् । विष्णौ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=281-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन्मद|जन्मदः
जन्मद m. (-दः) A father.<BR> E. जन्म birth, and द who gives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=281-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन्मन्
जन्मन् n. (-न्म) Birth, production.<BR> E. जन् to be born, and मनिन् Uṇādi<BR>affix, or with a final vowel जन्म.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=281-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन्मनक्षत्र
जन्मनक्षत्र n. (-त्रं) The planet or constellation under which a person is<BR>born, the natal star.<BR> E. जन्म, and नक्षत्र asterism.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=281-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन्मभूमि|जन्मभूमिः
जन्मभूमि f. (-मिः) Native country, birth place.<BR> E. जन्म, and भूमि land.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=281-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन्मवत्|जन्मवन्त्
जन्मवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Mortal, living.<BR> E. जन्म, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=281-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन्मवर्त्मन्
जन्मवर्त्मन् n. (-र्त्मः) The vulva. जन्म birth, and वर्त्मन् path or way.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=281-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन्मवैलक्षण्य
जन्मवैलक्षण्य n. (-ण्यं) Acting contrary to one's origin, unbecoming one's<BR>birth, &c.<BR> E. जन्म, and वैलक्षण्य inconsistency.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=281-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन्मशोधन
जन्मशोधन n. (-नं) Acquitting the obligations derived from birth.<BR> E. जन्म,<BR>and शोधन wiping away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=281-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन्मसाफल्य
जन्मसाफल्य n. (-ल्यं) Attainment of the object or end of existence. E.<BR>जन्म, and साफल्य fruitfulness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=281-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन्मान्तर|जन्मांतर|जन्मान्तरं
जन्मान्तर n. (-रं)<BR>	 1. The other world.<BR>	 2. Regeneration, another birth. E.<BR>जन्म, and अन्तर difference.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=281-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन्मान्ध|जन्मांध|जन्मान्धः
जन्मान्ध mfn. (-न्धः-न्धा-न्धं) Blind from birth.<BR> E. जन्म, and अन्ध blind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=281-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन्माष्टमी
जन्माष्टमी f. (-मी) The eighth lunation or dark half of Bhadra, the birth<BR>day of KṚṢṆA.<BR> E. जन्म, and अष्टमी eighth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=281-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन्मिन्
जन्मिन् m. (-न्मी) An animal, an existent being.<BR> E. जन्म birth, and इनि<BR>aff. जन्म अस्ति अस्य व्रीह्यादि इनि । प्राणिनि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=281-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन्मेजय|जन्मेजयः
जन्मेजय m. (-यः) The name of a prince: see जनमेजय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=281-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन्य|जन्यं|जन्यः
जन्य mfn. (-न्यः-न्या-न्यं)<BR>	 1. To be born or produced.<BR>	 2. Fit for or favourable<BR>to men.<BR>	 m. (-न्यः)<BR>	 1. A father.<BR>	 2. The friend, attendant, or companion<BR>of a bridegroom.<BR>	 f. (-न्या) The friend of a mother.<BR>	 2. The relation or<BR>companion of a bride, a bride's maid, &c.<BR>	 3. Pleasure, happiness.<BR>	 4.<BR>Affection.<BR>	 5. A mother.<BR>	 n. (-न्यं)<BR>	 1. War, combat.<BR>	 2. Rumour, report.<BR>3. A market, a fair.<BR>	 4. A portent, one occurring at birth.<BR> E. जन to<BR>be born, &c. affix णिच् कर्त्तरि यत् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=281-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन्यु|जन्युः
जन्यु m. (-न्युः)<BR>	 1. An animal, an existent. and sentient being.<BR>	 2. A name<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=281-b" target="_blank">Page281-b+ 60</a>]<BR>of BRAMHA.<BR>	 3. Fire or Agni.<BR> E. जन् to be born, &c. Uṇādi affix युच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=281-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जप|जपः
जप r. 1st cl. (जपति)<BR>	 1. To speak, to say or tell.<BR>	 2. To meditate, to<BR>speak internally, to say to one's self. With उप prefixed, to divide.<BR>भ्वा-पर-सक-सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=281-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जप|जपः
जप m. (-पः) Muttering prayers, repeating inaudibly passages from the<BR>scriptures, charms, names of a deity, counting silently the beads of<BR>a rosary, &c.<BR>	 f. (-पा) The China rose, the flower or plant; also जवा.<BR>E. जप् to repeat inaudibly, affix कर्त्तरि अच्; the flower is a sacred<BR>object.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=281-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जप्त्वा
जप्त्वा ind. Having repeated inaudibly.<BR> E. जप्, and क्त्वा affix: see जपित्वा;<BR>the omission of इट् is unusual.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=281-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जपन|जपनं
जपन n. (-नं) Inaudible repetition of prayers, &c.: see the last.<BR> E. जप्<BR>as before, affix भावे ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=281-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जपनीय
जपनीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) To be meditated on, to be repeated inaudibly. E.<BR>जप्, and अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=281-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जपपरायण|जपपरायणः
जपपरायण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Devoted to religious meditation, engaged<BR>in muttering prayers, &c.<BR> E. जप् as above, and परायण adhering or<BR>attached to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=281-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जपमाला
जपमाला f. (-ला) A rosary.<BR> E. जप, and माला a string of beads, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=281-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जपयज्ञ|जपयज्ञः
जपयज्ञ m. (-ज्ञः) Muttering prayers as a religious rite, or sacrifice.<BR> E. जप,<BR>and यज्ञ sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=281-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जपित्वा
जपित्वा ind. Having repeated inaudibly.<BR> E. जप्, and क्त्वा affix, इट् inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=281-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जपित
जपित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Repeated inaudibly.<BR> E. जप् to mutter prayers, and<BR>क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=281-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जप्य|जप्यः
जप्य mfn. (-प्यः-प्या-प्यं) To be repeated inaudibly, to be said over repeat-<BR>edly, (a prayer, &c.)<BR> E. जप्, and कर्मणि यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=281-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जभ्
जभ् r. 1st. cl. (जभति-ते) also (इ) जभि r. 1st cl. (जम्भति)<BR>	 1. To gape or<BR>yawn.<BR>	 2. To copulate. r. 10th cl. (जम्भयति-ते) To destroy, to efface.<BR>भ्वा-पर-सक-सेट् । चु० उभ० सक० इदित् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=281-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जम
जम (उ) जमु r. 1st cl. (जमति) To eat; also चम । भ्वा-पर-सक-सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=281-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जम
जम ind. A wife. It is used in composition: see जम्पती.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=281-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जमदग्नि|जमदग्निः
जमदग्नि m. (-ग्निः) A Muni, the father of PARASURAMA.<BR> E. जमन् प्रज्वलितः<BR>अग्निः इव ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=281-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जमन|जमनं
जमन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Eating.<BR>	 2. Food, victuals.<BR> E. जम् to eat, affix भावेल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=281-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जम्पति
जम्पति m. du. (-ती) Husband and wife.<BR> E. जं for जाया a wife, and पति<BR>a husband: see दम्पती &c. जाया च पतिश्च द्व० जायायाः जम् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=281-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जम्बाल|जंबाल|जंबालः|जम्बालः
जम्बाल mn. (-लः-लं)<BR>	 1. Mud, clay.<BR>	 2. An aquatic plant, (Vallisneria.)<BR>&c.<BR>	 m. (-लः) A fragrant plant, (Pandanus odoratissimus.)<BR> E. जल<BR>water, बल् to move, affix अण्, and the deriv. irr. or जम्ब-घञ् जम्बम्<BR>आलाति आदत्ते आ-ला-क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=281-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जम्बालिनी|जंबालिनी
जम्बालिनी f. (-नी) A river.<BR> E. जम्बाल mud, इनि and ङीष् affs. नद्याम् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=281-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जम्बिर|जम्बिरः
जम्बिर m. (-रः) A lime: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=281-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जम्बीर|जंबीर|जंबीरः|जम्बीरः
जम्बीर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Common lime, (Citrus acida;) the name seems to be<BR>applied to more than one species.<BR>	 2. A plant, called by some a<BR>sort of basil, with small leaves; also जम्भीर, and जम्बिर.<BR> E. जम् to eat,<BR>ईरन् affix, and वुक् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=281-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जम्बु|जंबु|जम्बुः
जम्बु mn. (-म्बुः-म्बु)<BR>	 1. Jambu Dwipa, said to be so named from the<BR>Jambu tree abounding in it, and implying, according to the<BR>Puranas the central division of the world, or the known world:<BR>according to the Bauddhas, it is confined to India.<BR>	 2. A fabulous<BR>river, said to flow from the mountain Meru.<BR>	 f. (-म्बुः) A fruit tree<BR>the rose apple, (Eugenia jambolana;) also applied to every species<BR>of Eugenia.<BR>	 fn. (-म्बुः-म्बु) The fruit.<BR> E. जम् to eat, वुक् augment, and<BR>कु or कू Uṇādi affix; hence it is also written जम्बू.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=281-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जम्बुक|जंबुक|जंबुकः|जम्बुकः
जम्बुक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A jackal.<BR>	 2. The deity of water, VARUṆA.<BR>	 3. A low<BR>man.<BR>	 4. The rose apple. जम् to eat, affix उकच् and वुक् augment,<BR>eating flesh, &c. or जम्बु as above, and क added the affix also being<BR>ऊकच्, जम्बूक । जम्बः इव कायति कै-क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=281-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जम्बुद्वीप|जंबुद्वीप|जम्बुद्वीपः
जम्बुद्वीप m. (-पः) One of the divisions of the world.<BR> E. द्वीप a continent,<BR>added to जम्बु । जम्बुवृक्षयुक्तः द्वीपः । भूमेः सप्तद्वीपान्तर्गते द्वीपभेदे ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=281-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जम्बुमत्|जम्बुमन्त्
जम्बुमत् m. (-मान्)<BR>	 1. A monkey.<BR>	 2. A mountain.<BR>	 f. (-मती) An Apsara or<BR>heavenly nymph.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=282-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जम्बू|जंबू
जम्बू f. (-म्बूः) See जम्बु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=282-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जम्बूक|जंबूक|जंबूकः|जम्बूकः
जम्बूक m. (-कः) See जम्बुक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=282-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जम्बूल|जंबूल|जम्बूलः
जम्बूल m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. A fragrant plant, (Pandanus odoratissimus.)<BR>2. The rose apple.<BR>	 n. (-लं) Jokes addressed to the bridegroom by<BR>his female relatives and friends.<BR> E. जम्बू as above, and ल what<BR>gets or is.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=282-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जम्बूलमालिका
जम्बूलमालिका f. (-का) Compliments or jokes addressed to the bride and<BR>bridegroom.<BR> E. जम्बूल, and मालिका a string.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=282-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जम्भ|जंभ|जंभः|जम्भः
जम्भ m. (-म्भः)<BR>	 1. A tooth.<BR>	 2. The lime.<BR>	 3. Food, victuals.<BR>	 4. The chin.<BR>	 5.<BR>A quiver.<BR>	 6. A part, a portion.<BR>	 7. The name of a demon.<BR> E. जभि to<BR>destroy, affix अच् and नुम् । दैत्यभेदे । करणे घञ् दन्ते । कर्मणि घञ् जम्बीरे ।<BR>भावे घञ् भक्षणे । कर्मणि घञ् अंशे । करणे घञ् तूणे हनौ च ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=282-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जम्भक|जंभक|जम्भकः
जम्भक mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>	 1. Who or what yawns, opens, expands, &c.<BR>	 2.<BR>Who or what kills or destroys.<BR>	 m. (-कः) A lime or citron.<BR>	 f. (-का)<BR>Yawning.<BR> E. जभि to yawn, &c. ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=282-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जम्भद्विष्|जंभद्विष्
जम्भद्विष् m. (-द्विट्) A name of INDRA.<BR> E. जम्भ a demon, and द्बिष् a foe;<BR>also similar compounds. जम्भम् असुरं द्वेष्टि द्विष-क्विप् । इन्द्रे ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=282-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जम्भभेदिन्|जंभभेदिन्
जम्भभेदिन् m. (-दी) INDRA.<BR> E. जम्भ as above, and भेदिन् destroying: see<BR>the last. जम्भम् असुरं भिनत्ति भिद-णिनि । इन्द्रे ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=282-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जम्भर|जंभर|जंभरः|जम्भरः
जम्भर m. (-रः) A lime or citron. E. See the next, ल being changed to र ।<BR>जम्भं भक्षणरुचिं राति ददाति रा-क । जम्बीरे ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=282-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जम्भल|जंभलः|जम्भलः
जम्भल m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. A lime or citron.<BR>	 2. A Jina or deified Jaina saint.<BR>	 f.<BR>(-ला) A female Rakshasi, the worship of whom is supposed to<BR>procure for women procreation.<BR> E. जभि to destroy, (sickness, sin,<BR>&c.) कलच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=282-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जम्भरि
जम्भरि m. (-रिः)<BR>	 1. INDRA'S thunderbolt.<BR>	 2. Fire or its deity.<BR>	 3. INDRA.<BR>E. जम्भ the demon, and अरि a foe. जम्भस्य भक्ष्यस्य असुरभेदस्य वा अरिः ।<BR>वह्नौ वज्रे च ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=282-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जम्भिन्|जंभिन्
जम्भिन् m. (-म्भी) A lime or citron.<BR> E. जभि to destroy, (disease,) affix णिनि<BR>and नुम् । जम्बीरे । जृम्मायुक्ते त्रि० ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=282-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जम्भीर|जंभीर|जंभीरः|जम्भीरः
जम्भीर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. The lime or citron, apparently of more than one<BR>species.<BR>	 2. A plant, considered to be a kind of basil with small<BR>leaves.<BR> E. जभि to destroy, (sickness,) ईरन् affix, and नुम् augment;<BR>also जम्बीर, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=282-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जय|जयः
जय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. Conquest, victory, triumph.<BR>	 2. A name of YuDHISH-<BR>ṬHIRA.<BR>	 3. A proper name, the son of INDRA.<BR>	 4. One of VIṢṆU'S<BR>door keepers.<BR>	 5. The name of a king; also विजयनन्दन.<BR>	 6. A kind of<BR>Mung or bean, (Phaseolus mungo.)<BR>	 f. (-या)<BR>	 1. A name of the goddess<BR>PARVATI.<BR>	 2. One of her female companions.<BR>	 3. The 3rd, 8th, or<BR>13th lunar day of either half month.<BR>	 4. Yellow myrobalan, (Ter-<BR>minalia chebula.)<BR>	 5. A plant: see जयन्ती.<BR>	 6. A tree, commonly<BR>Ganiyari, (Premna spinosa.)<BR>	 7. Hemp, (Cannabis sativa.)<BR>	 8. A<BR>banner, a flag.<BR> E. जि to conquer or excel, affixes भावे अच् and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=282-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जयकोलाहल|जयकोलाहलः
जयकोलाहल m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. A kind of dice.<BR>	 2. Shouts of victory.<BR> E. जय vic-<BR>tory, कोलाहल a noise. जयस्य कोलाहलः यस्मिन् । पाशकक्रीडाभेदे, जयध्वनौ च ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=282-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जयगर्व्व|जयगर्व
जयगर्व्व m. (-र्व्वः) Pride of conquest, exultation.<BR> E. जय, and गर्व्व pride.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=282-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जयत्|जयन्त्
जयत् mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्) Conquering, excelling.<BR> E. जि to conquer, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=282-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जयढक्का
जयढक्का f. (-क्का) A large kettle drum, beaten as a sign of victory. E.<BR>जय, and ढक्का a drum. जयसूचिका ढक्का । वाद्यभेदे ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=282-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जयदत्त|जयदत्तः
जयदत्त m. (-त्तः) The son of INDRA.<BR> E. जय victory, दत्त given, to whom<BR>victory is given by his enemies.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=282-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जयद्रथ|जयद्रथः
जयद्रथ m. (-थः) A chief in the army of DURYODHANA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=282-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जयन|जयनं
जयन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Armour for cavalry, elephants, &c.<BR>	 2. Conquering, sub-<BR>duing.<BR>	 f. (-नी) INDRA'S daughter.<BR> E. जि to conquer or excel, affixes<BR>करणे ल्युट् and ङीष् । हयादिसन्नाहे । भावे ल्युट् जये ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=282-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जयनयुज्
जयनयुज् mfn. (-युक्)<BR>	 1. Caparisoned, (as a war horse.)<BR>	 2. Victorious. E.<BR>जयन, and युज् having.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=282-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जयन्त|जयंत|जयंतः|जयन्तः
जयन्त m. (-न्तः)<BR>	 1. A hero and demigod, the son of INDRA.<BR>	 2. A name of<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=282-b" target="_blank">Page282-b+ 60</a>]<BR>ŚIVA.<BR>	 3. The moon.<BR>	 4. A name of BHIMA.<BR>	 f. (-न्ती)<BR>	 1. A tree,<BR>(Æschynomene sesban.)<BR>	 2. A name of the goddess DURGĀ.<BR>	 3. The<BR>daughter of INDRA.<BR>	 4. A flag, a banner, 5. A particular combina-<BR>tion in astronomy, or the rising of the asterism ROHINI at midnight,<BR>on the 8th of the dark half of Sravan, or in fact on the birth day<BR>of KṚṢṆA, which is then particularly sacred.<BR>	 6. Blades of barley<BR>planted at the commencement of the Dasahara, and plucked at its<BR>close.<BR> E. जि to conquer or excel, Uṇādi affix झच् fem. affix ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=282-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जयपत्र|जयपत्रं
जयपत्र n. (-त्रं) Record of victory or triumph; in law, the sealed and<BR>written award of the judge in favour of either party; in historical<BR>tradition, the label on the brow of a horse turned loose for the<BR>Aswamedha sacrifice.<BR> E. जय conquest, and पत्र a leaf; also with कन्<BR>added जयपत्रक । जयसूचकं पत्रम् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=282-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जयपाल|जयपालः
जयपाल m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. A name of BRAMHA.<BR>	 2. VIṢṆU.<BR>	 3. A king, a sover-<BR>eign; (it is also the appellation of several celebrated Hindu princes.)<BR>4. A tree, (Croton tiglium.)<BR> E. जय victory, पाल who nourishes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=282-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जयध्वनि
जयध्वनि m. (-निः) Shout of victory.<BR> E. जय, and ध्वनि sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=282-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जयपुत्रक|जयपुत्रकः
जयपुत्रक m. (-कः) A kind of dice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=282-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जयमङ्गल|जयमंगल|जयमङ्गलः
जयमङ्गल m. (-लः) The royal elephant.<BR> E. जय victory, and मङ्गल good<BR>fortune.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=282-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जययज्ञ|जययज्ञः
जययज्ञ m. (-ज्ञः) The Aswamedha or sacrifice of a horse, as a mark of<BR>dominion.<BR> E. जय, and यज्ञ sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=282-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जयवह
जयवह mfn. (-हः-हा-हं)<BR>	 1. Conferring victory.<BR>	 2. Victorious.<BR> E. जय and<BR>वह what bears.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=282-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जयवाहिनी
जयवाहिनी f. (-नी) The wife of INDRA.<BR> E. जय conquest, and वाहिनी who<BR>bears.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=282-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जयशब्द|जयशब्दः
जयशब्द m. (-ब्दः) A shout or song of victory, or the exclamation Jaya<BR>Jaya repeated like the Io of the Greeks, as जयदेवहरे, &c.<BR> E. जय<BR>and शब्द sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=282-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जयशील
जयशील mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Victorious, triumphant.<BR> E. जय and शील possessed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=282-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जयश्री
जयश्री f. (-श्रीः) Victory, glory.<BR> E. जय, and श्री splendor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=282-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जयान्तराय
जयान्तराय m. (-यः) An impediment or hindrance to victory.<BR> E. जय and<BR>अन्तराय obstacle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=282-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जयारव
जयारव m. (-वः) The Io or song of victory: see जयशब्द.<BR> E. जय and आरव sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=282-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जयावह
जयावह mfn. (-हः-हा-हं)<BR>	 1. Victorious.<BR>	 2. Conferring victory.<BR> E. जय and,<BR>आवह what gives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=282-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जयिन्
जयिन् mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि) Victorious.<BR> E. जय victory, शीलार्थे इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=282-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जयोद्धुर
जयोद्धुर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Victorious, conquering.<BR> E. जय and उद्धुर firm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=282-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जय्य|जय्यः
जय्य mfn. (-य्यः-य्या-य्यं) Able to conquer, victorious.<BR> E. जि to subdue, affix<BR>यत्, deriv. irr. जेतुं शक्यः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=282-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जय्यता
जय्यता f. (-ता) Victory, success, ability to conquer.<BR> E. जय्य and तल् affix;<BR>with त्व जय्यत्वम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=282-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जरठ|जरठः
जरठ mfn. (-ठः-ठा-ठं)<BR>	 1. Hard, solid.<BR>	 2. Herd-hearted, harsh, cruel.<BR>	 3.<BR>Pale, yellowish-white.<BR>	 4. Old, decayed, infirm.<BR>	 5. Bent, bowed<BR>down, drooping.<BR>	 m. (-ठः)<BR>	 1. A name of Pandu, father of the five<BR>Pandavas.<BR>	 2. Decrepitude.<BR> E. जॄ to become old or decayed, Uṇādi<BR>affix अठ्, and the deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=282-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जरण|जरणं|जरणः
जरण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Old, infirm, decayed.<BR>	 m. (-णः)<BR>	 1. Cuminseed.<BR>	 2.<BR>A plant yielding a pungent seed, (Nigella Indica.)<BR>	 3. A sort of<BR>salt, (Bit-laban.)<BR>	 4. Old age, becoming old and infirm.<BR>	 n. (-णं)<BR>Asafœtida.<BR> E. जॄ to become old, affix ल्यु ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=282-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जरण्ड|जरंड|जरण्डः
जरण्ड mfn. (-ण्डः-ण्डा-ण्डं) Old, decayed.<BR> E. जॄ to be old, अण्डच् Uṇādi<BR>aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=282-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जरत्|जरन्त्
जरत् mfn. (-रन्-रती-रत्)<BR>	 1. Old, ancient, advanced in years.<BR>	 2. Infirm,<BR>decayed.<BR>	 m. (-रन्) An old man.<BR>	 f. (-ती) An old woman.<BR> E. जॄ to be<BR>or become old, participial affix शतृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=282-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जरत्कारु|जरत्कारुः
जरत्कारु m. (-रुः) A celebrated Muni or sage so named.<BR>	 f. (-रुः) The<BR>wife of JARATKARU, the snake goddess MANASA.<BR> E. जरत् being old,<BR>and कारु a maker; a practiser of austerities in old age.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=282-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जरत्कारुप्रिया
जरत्कारुप्रिया f. (-या) The goddess MANASA, exercising a peculiar power<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=283-a" target="_blank">Page283-a+ 60</a>]<BR>over serpents, as the sister of VĀSUKI, the Naga.<BR> E. जरत्कारु as<BR>above, and प्रिया the beloved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=282-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जरद्गव|जरद्गवः
जरद्गव m. (-वः) An old ox.<BR>	 f. (-वी) An old cow.<BR> E. जरत् old, गो a cow,<BR>affix टच् fem. affix ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=283-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जरन्त|जरंत|जरन्तः
जरन्त m. (-न्तः)<BR>	 1. A buffalo.<BR>	 2. An old man.<BR> E. जॄ to be or become old,<BR>Uṇādi affix झच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=283-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जरसान|जरसानः
जरसान m. (-नः) A man.<BR> E. जॄ to grow old, असानच् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=283-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जरा
जरा f. (-रा)<BR>	 1. Decrepitude, the general relaxation and debility conse-<BR>quent upon old age, or old age itself.<BR>	 2. A tree, (Mimusops kauki,<BR>Rox.)<BR>	 3. A female demon or Rakshasi.<BR> E. जॄ to grow old, affixes<BR>अङ् and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=283-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जरातुर|जरातुरः
जरातुर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Infirm, decrepid, debilitated, old.<BR> E. जरा infirmi-<BR>ty and आतुर diseased, affected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=283-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जरापरिणत
जरापरिणत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Stooping, bent down with age or infirmity.<BR>E. जरा, and परिणत bent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=283-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जरापुष्ट|जरापुष्टः
जरापुष्ट m. (-ष्टः) A proper name: see जरासन्ध.<BR> E. जर a female Rakshasi,<BR>and पुष्ट fostered; assisted at his birth by a demon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=283-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जराभीरु|जराभीरुः
जराभीरु m. (-रुः) Love or the deity KĀMA^1.<BR> E. जरा decrepitude, and भीरु formidable.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20260617. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/264.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=283-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जरायणि|जरायणिः
जरायणि m. (-णिः) The sovereign JARĀSANDHA.<BR> E. जरा the Rakshasi,<BR>फिञ् affix of descent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=283-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जरायु|जरायुः
जरायु m. (-युः) The womb, the uterus.<BR> E. जरा infirmity, इण् to obtain,<BR>Uṇādi affix ञुण्, also with a final स, जरायुस् m. (-युः.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=283-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जरायुज|जरायुजः
जरायुज mfn. (-जः-जा-जं) Viviparous, born from the womb, as man and<BR>other animals.<BR> E. जरायु the womb, ज born. जरायौ जायते जन-ड ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=283-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जरासन्ध|जरासंध|जरासन्धः
जरासन्ध m. (-न्धः) A proper name, a celebrated king and warrior, sover-<BR>eign of Magadha, father-in-law to KANSA, and foe to KṚṢṆA;<BR>he was slain in single combat by BHIMA.<BR> E. जरा a female demon,<BR>and सन्ध connection, union; he was born in two halves, which<BR>were put together by the Rakshasi JARA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=283-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जरासन्धजित्|जरासंधजित्
जरासन्धजित् m. (-जित्) BHIMASENA, the third of the Pandu princes. E.<BR>जरासन्ध and जित् conqueror: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=283-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जरिन्
जरिन् mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>	 1. Old, ancient.<BR>	 2. Infirm, decayed.<BR>	 m. (-री) An<BR>old man.<BR> E. जॄ to become old, इनि aff. जरा अस्ति अस्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=283-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जरूथ|जरूथं|जरूथः
जरूथ n. (-थं)<BR>	 1. Flesh.<BR>	 2. Skinniness, flesh flaccid with old age.<BR> E. जॄ<BR>to become old, ऊथन् Uṇādi aff. मांसे, जरणीये च ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=283-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जर्च|जर्च्च
जर्च r. 6th cl. (जर्चति)<BR>	 1. To say, to speak.<BR>	 2. To reprove, to abuse or<BR>blame.<BR>	 3. To threaten. तुदा० पर० सक० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=283-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जर्च्छ
जर्च्छ r. 6th cl. (जर्च्छति) To say, to blame: see जर्च । तुदा० पर० सक० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=283-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जर्ज|जर्ज्ज
जर्ज r. 1st and 6th cls. (जर्जति)<BR>	 1. To say. To blame, to reprove.<BR>	 3. To<BR>kill or hurt. उक्तौ भर्त्सने च तुदा० पर० सक-सेट् । पक्षे भ्वा० ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=283-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जर्जर|जर्ज्जरः
जर्जर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>	 1. Old. infirm.<BR>	 2. Split, broken.<BR>	 3. Wounded, hurt.<BR>4. Divided in parts or pieces.<BR>	 5. Perforated.<BR>	 m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. INDRA'S<BR>banner or emblem.<BR>	 2. Benzoin.<BR>	 3. An aquatic plant, (Utricularia<BR>fasciculata.)<BR> E. जर्ज् to hurt, and अर affix; or जॄ to grow old, affix<BR>अच् the radical repeated, and the deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=283-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जर्जरीक|जर्ज्जरीकः
जर्जरीक mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>	 1. Ragged, perforated, full of holes.<BR>	 2. Old,<BR>decayed. E. See the last, ईकन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=283-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जर्जरीकृत|जर्ज्जरीकृत
जर्जरीकृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Wounded, disabled.<BR> E. जर्जर, and कृत made,<BR>च्वि inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=283-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जर्झ
जर्झ r. 6th cl. (जर्झति)<BR>	 1. To say or speak, 2. To blame.<BR>	 3. To threaten.<BR>तुदा० पर० सक० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=283-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जर्ण|जर्णः
जर्ण mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-र्णं) Old, decayed m. (-र्णः)<BR>	 1. The moon.<BR>	 2. A tree. E.<BR>जॄ to grow old, नन् Uṇādi affix, deriv. irr. जीर्णे, चन्द्रे, वृक्षे च ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=283-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जर्त्तिल|जर्तिल|जर्तिलः|जर्त्तिलः
जर्त्तिल m. (-लः) Sesamum growing wild.<BR> E. जन् to be produced, and तिल<BR>sesamum, deriv. irr.; also read जर्हिल or जॄ-विच् नित्यस० ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=283-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जर्त्तु|जर्तु|जर्तुः|जर्त्तुः
जर्त्तु m. (-र्त्तुः)<BR>	 1. The vulva.<BR>	 2. An elephant.<BR> E. जन् to be born, तु Uṇādi<BR>affix, and र inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=283-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जर्हिल|जर्हिलः
जर्हिल m. (-लः) Wild sesamum: see जर्त्तिल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=283-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जर्त्स
जर्त्स r. 1st cl. (जर्त्सति)<BR>	 1. To say or speak.<BR>	 2. To blame, to censure, to<BR>abuse. भ्वा० पर० सक० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=283-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जल|जलं|जलः
जल r. 1st cl. (जलति)<BR>	 1. To be sharp.<BR>	 2. To be wealthy. r. 1st and 10th<BR>cls. (जलति जालयति-ते) To cover, to hide or veil; to cover also as<BR>with a net, to encompass. भ्वा० अक० पर० सेट् । आच्छादने चुरा० उभ०<BR>सक० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=283-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जल|जलं|जलः
जल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Cold stupid, apathetic, idiotic, &c.<BR>	 n. (-लं)<BR>	 1.<BR>Water.<BR>	 2. A kind of perfume: see ह्रीवेर.<BR>	 3. The uterus of a cow.<BR>	 4.<BR>Frigidity, (moral, mental, or physical.)<BR>	 5. The constellation called<BR>Purvashada.<BR> E. जल् to hide, to encompass, &c. affix अच्; also ल<BR>being changed to its congener ड, जड q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=283-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलक|जलकं
जलक n. (-कं) A conch, a shell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=283-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलकण्टक|जलकंटक|जलकण्टकः
जलकण्टक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. An aquatic plant, (Trapa bispinosa.)<BR>	 2. A croco-<BR>dile.<BR> E. जल water, and कण्टक a thron. जले कण्टक इव । शृङ्गाटके<BR>कुम्भीरे च ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=283-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलकपि|जलकपिः
जलकपि m. (-पिः) The gangetic porpoise.<BR> E. जल, and कपि an ape, the<BR>water-ape. जले कपिरिव । शिशुमारे । (शोषक) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=283-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलकर|जलकरः
जलकर mfn. (-रः-री-रं) Making or shedding water.<BR>	 m. (-रः) Rent or tax<BR>derived from water, for fisheries, &c.<BR> E. जल, and कर tax or what<BR>makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=283-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलकरङ्क|जलकरंक|जलकरङ्कः
जलकरङ्क m. (-ङ्कः)<BR>	 1. A cocoanut.<BR>	 2. A shell or conch.<BR>	 3. A lotus.<BR>	 4. A<BR>cloud.<BR>	 5. A wave.<BR> E. जल water, and करङ्क a cup or receptacle. जलस्य<BR>करङ्कः इव आधारः । नारिकेले मेघे पद्मे च ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=283-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलकल्क|जलकल्कः
जलकल्क m. (-ल्कः) Mud, mire.<BR> E. जल water, and कल्क sediment. जले कल्क इव । जम्बाले ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=283-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलकाक|जलकाकः
जलकाक m. (-कः) The diver.<BR> E. जल, and काक a crow; the water-crow.<BR>जले काकः इव कृष्णत्वात् । (पान्कौडि).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=283-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलकाङ्क्ष|जलकांक्ष|जलकाङ्क्षः
जलकाङ्क्ष m. (-ङ्क्षः) An elephant.<BR> E. जल water, and काङ्क्ष desirous, from<BR>कांक्षि with अण् affix; also with इनि affix, ut inf. जलं काङ्क्षति काङ्क्ष-अण्<BR>उपमित समासः । हस्तिनि जलाभिलाषिणि च ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=283-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलकाङ्क्षिन
जलकाङ्क्षिन mfn. (-ङ्क्षी-ङ्क्षिणी-ङ्क्षि) Desirous of water, fond of water.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-ङ्क्षी) An elephant.<BR> E. जल, and काङ्क्षिन् wishing: see the last. जलं<BR>काङ्क्षति काङ्क्ष-णिनि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=283-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलकान्तार|जलकांतार|जलकान्तारः
जलकान्तार m. (-रः) A name of VARUṆA.<BR> E. जलकान्त the water-gem, the<BR>ocean, and अर who goes or rules. जलम् एव कान्तारो दुर्गमवर्त्म यस्य । वरुणे ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=283-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलकिराट|जलकिराटः
जलकिराट m. (-टः) A shark, or according to some, a large alligator. E.<BR>जल water, किर a hog, and अट who goes. जले किराट इव ग्राहे (हाङ्गोर) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=283-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलकुक्कुटी
जलकुक्कुटी f. (-टी) The black-headed gull: see गङ्गाचिल्ली.<BR> E. जल water, and<BR>कुक्कुटी a fowl. जले कुक्कुटी इव । (गां चिल्) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=283-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलकुक्कुभ|जलकुक्कुभः
जलकुक्कुभ m. (-भः) A sort of aquatic bird.<BR> E. जल water, and कुक्कुभ a wild<BR>fowl. जले कुक्कुभ इव (कोडा पाखि) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=283-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलकुन्तल|जलकुंतल|जलकुन्तलः
जलकुन्तल m. (-लः) An aquatic plant, (Vallisneria.)<BR> E. जल water, and<BR>कुन्तल hair. जलस्य कुन्तल इव । शैवाले ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=283-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलकुब्जक
जलकुब्जक m. (-कः) An aquatic plant, (Trapa bispinosa.)<BR> E. जल, कुब्ज to be<BR>crooked, affix क्वुन् । जले कुब्जः इव कायति कै-क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=283-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलकूपी
जलकूपी f. (-पी)<BR>	 1. A whirlpool.<BR>	 2. A pond, a pool.<BR>	 3. A spring, a well.<BR>E. जल water, कूप a well, ङीष् affix of diminution.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=283-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलकूर्म्म|जलकूर्म|जलकूर्मः|जलकूर्म्मः
जलकूर्म्म m. (-र्म्मः) The gangetic porpoise.<BR> E. जल, and कूर्म्म a tortoise, a<BR>water-tortoise. जले कूर्म इव । शिशुमारे ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=283-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलक्रिया
जलक्रिया f. (-या) A funeral ceremony, presenting water to the manes of<BR>the deceased.<BR> E. जल, and क्रिया ceremony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=283-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलकेश|जलकेशः
जलकेश m. (-शः)<BR>	 1. A plant, (Vallisneria.)<BR> E. जल, and केश hair; spread-<BR>ing over the water like dishevelled hair. शैवाले ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=283-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलक्रीडा
जलक्रीडा f. (-डा) Sporting or gamboling in water, bathing for pleasure<BR>or amusement. Splashing one another with water.<BR> E. जल, and<BR>क्रीडा pastime, play.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=283-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलगुल्म|जलगुल्मः
जलगुल्म m. (-ल्मः)<BR>	 1. A whirlpool.<BR>	 2. A turtle, a tortoise.<BR>	 2. A piece of<BR>water.<BR>	 3. A quadrangular tank, a lake.<BR> E. जल water, and गुल्म a<BR>lump like the spleen, or a cluster. जलस्य गल्मः इव । जलावर्त्ते (घुर्णो)<BR>कमठे जलचत्वरे च ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=283-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलङ्ग|जलंग|जलङ्गः
जलङ्ग mfn. (-ङ्गः-ङ्गा-ङ्गं) Aquatic, frequenting or going to water.<BR>	 m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>The colocynth.<BR> E. जल and ग what goes. जलं गच्छति गम-ड नि-मुम् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=283-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलङ्गम|जलंगम|जलङ्गमः
जलङ्गम m. (-मः) A Chandala, an outcaste.<BR> E. जल water, and गम who<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=284-a" target="_blank">Page284-a+ 60</a>]<BR>goes; who goes to fish for his subsistence; also जनङ्गम q. v.<BR> E. जलं<BR>गमयति स्पर्शात् गामि वा-ख । चण्डाले ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=283-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलचर|जलचरः
जलचर mfn. (-रः-री-रं) Aquatic, amphibious, going in or into water. E.<BR>जल and, and चर what goes. जले चरति चर-ठक् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=284-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलचारिन्
जलचारिन् mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि) Aquatic, living in or frequenting water.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-री) A fish.<BR> E. जल water, and चर् to go, affix णिनि. जले चरति चर<BR>णिनि ७ तत् स० ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=284-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलज|जलजं|जलजः
जलज mfn. (-जः-जा-जं) Water-born, aquatic.<BR>	 m. (-जः)<BR>	 1. A fish.<BR>	 2. Any<BR>aquatic animal.<BR>	 n. (-जं)<BR>	 1. A lotus.<BR>	 2. A shell.<BR>	 f. (-जा) A plant;<BR>said to be a sort of bassia growing in or near water.<BR> E. जल, and ज<BR>produced. जले जायते जल-ड ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=284-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलजन्तु|जलजंतु|जलजन्तुः
जलजन्तु m. (-न्तुः) A fish, or any marine, aquatic, or amphibious animal.<BR>E. जल water, and जन्तु animal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=284-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलजन्तुका|जलजंतुका
जलजन्तुका f. (-का) A leech.<BR> E. कन्, and टाप् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=284-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलजन्मन्
जलजन्मन् n. (-न्म) A lotus.<BR> E. जल, and जन्मन् birth. जले जन्म यस्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=284-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलजिह्व|जलजिह्वः
जलजिह्व m. (-ह्वः) A crocodile.<BR> E. जल cold, and जिह्व a tongue. जला जडा<BR>स्वादे असमर्था जिह्वा अस्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=284-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलडिम्ब|जलडिम्बः
जलडिम्ब m. (-म्बः) A bivalve shell.<BR> E. जल, and डिम्ब a young animal. जले<BR>डिम्ब इव । शम्बूके ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=284-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलतरङ्ग|जलतरंग|जलतरङ्गः
जलतरङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>	 1. A wave.<BR>	 2. A metal cup with water, so as to<BR>produce a harmonic note like a musical glass.<BR> E. जल, and तरङ्ग<BR>a wave.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=284-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलतापिक|जलतापिकः
जलतापिक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. The Hilsa or sable fish, (Clupanodon ilisha, HAM.)<BR>2. Another kind of fish, commonly Caouchhi, (Cyprinus cachius<BR>HAM.)<BR> E. जल water, तप to inflame, ठक् affix; also with णिनि affix<BR>जलतापिन् m. (-पी) The Hilsa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=284-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलताल|जलतालः
जलताल m. (-लः) The Ilisa or Hilsa fish: see the last.<BR> E. जल water, तल्<BR>to abide, affix अच् । जलतायै अलति पर्य्याप्नेति अल-अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=284-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलत्रा
जलत्रा f. (-त्रा) An umbrella.<BR> E. जल rain, त्रा defending, from त्रै, with ड<BR>and टाप् affs. or जलात् त्रायते त्रै-क । छचे, जङ्गमकुठ्याञ्च ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=284-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलद|जलदः
जलद mfn. (-दः-दा-दं) Giving or shedding water.<BR>	 m. (-दः)<BR>	 1. A cloud.<BR>	 2.<BR>A fragrant grass, (Cyperus rotundus.)<BR> E. जल water, and द what<BR>gives. जलं ददाति दा-क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=284-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलदपङ्क्ति
जलदपङ्क्ति f. (-ङ्क्ति) A line or succession of clouds.<BR> E. जलद, and पङ्क्ति a line.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=284-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलदसंहति
जलदसंहति f. (-तिः) Cloudiness, gathering of clouds.<BR> E. जलद, and संहति<BR>assemblage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=284-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलदागम|जलदागमः
जलदागम m. (-मः) The rainy season.<BR> E. जलद, and आगम arrival.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=284-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलदान
जलदान n. (-नं) Giving water.<BR> E. जल, and दान giving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=284-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलदाभ
जलदाभ mfn. (-भः-भा-भं) Dark, black.<BR> E. जलद a cloud, and आभ what<BR>resembles.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=284-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलदाशन|जलदाशनः
जलदाशन m. (-नः) The Saltree, (Shorea robusta.)<BR> E. जलद a cloud, and<BR>अशन imbibing, from अश् to eat, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=284-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलधर|जलधरः
जलधर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Holding or having water.<BR>	 m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A cloud.<BR>	 2.<BR>The ocean.<BR>	 3. A grass, (Cyperus rotundus.)<BR> E. जल water, and धर.<BR>containing, possessing, form धृ with अच् aff. जलं धरति ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=284-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलधरमाला
जलधरमाला f. (-ला)<BR>	 1. A row of clouds.<BR>	 2. A species of the Jagati metre.<BR>E. जलधर, and माला a garland.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=284-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलधि|जलधिः
जलधि m. (-धिः)<BR>	 1. The ocean.<BR>	 2. A large number, (a hundred lacs of<BR>crores.)<BR>	 3. The number “four”.<BR> E. जल water, धा to have. and<BR>आधारे कि aff. जलं धीयते अत्र ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=284-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलधिगा
जलधिगा f. (-गा) A river.<BR> E. जलधि the sea, गा going. जलधिं समुद्रं गच्छति<BR>गम-ड ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=284-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलधिजा
जलधिजा f. (-जा) A name of the goddess LAKṢMĪ.<BR> E. जलधि and जा<BR>produced, the ocean-born; appearing at the churning of the<BR>ocean, amongst the fourteen precious things recovered from it.<BR>जलधौ जायते जन-ड-टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=284-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलनकुल|जलनकुलः
जलनकुल m. (-लः) An otter.<BR> E. जल, and नकुल an ichneumon; the water-<BR>ichneumon. जले नकुल इव । (उद्विडाल) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=284-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलनिधि|जलनिधिः
जलनिधि m. (-धिः) The ocean.<BR> E. जल water and निधि a nest. निधीयते अस्मिन्<BR>नि-धा-आधारे कि उप स० ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=284-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलनिर्गम|जलनिर्गमः
जलनिर्गम m. (-मः) A drain, a water-couse, a pipe along a wall or build-<BR>ing for carrying off water, a waterfall, the descent of a spring,<BR>&c. into a river below.<BR> E. जल water, निर्गम transit or passage.<BR>जलानां निर्गमः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=284-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलनिवह
जलनिवह m. (-हः) A quantity of water.<BR> E. जल and निवह a quantity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=284-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलनीली
जलनीली f. (-ली) Vallisneria. Moss.<BR> E. जल and नीली a blue dye or<BR>indigo; imparting its own tinge to the stream. जलं नीलयति नील +<BR>तत्करोति णिच् अण् उप स गौरा ङीष् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=284-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलन्धर|जलंधर|जलन्धरः
जलन्धर m. (-रः) An Asura sprung from ŚIVA, and adopted by the ocean.<BR>E. जल, and धर who has. जलं धरति वा ख मुम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=284-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलपटल
जलपटल n. (-लं)<BR>	 1. A quantity of water.<BR>	 2. A cloud.<BR> E. जल, and पटल a<BR>quantity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=284-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलपति|जलपतिः
जलपति m. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. VARUṆA, the deity presiding over the watery ele-<BR>ment, the Hindu Neptune.<BR>	 2. The ocean.<BR> E. जल and पति lord or<BR>master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=284-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलपात्र
जलपात्र n. (-त्रं) A drinking vessel.<BR> E. जल, and पात्र vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=284-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलपान
जलपान n. (-नं) Drinking water: in Bengal, refreshment, luncheon. E.<BR>जल, and पान drinking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=284-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलपित्त|जलपित्तं
जलपित्त m. (-त्तः) Fire.<BR> E. जल, and पित्त bile; being as a dust to water as<BR>bile is to the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=284-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलपिप्पली
जलपिप्पली f. (-ली) An aquatic plant, (Commelina salicifolia, &c.) See<BR>जलभू.<BR> E. जल water, and पिप्पली long-pepper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=284-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलपृष्ठजा
जलपृष्ठजा f. (-जा) An aquatic plant, (Pistia stratiotes.)<BR> E. जल water, पृष्ठ<BR>back or surface, and ज produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=284-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलप्राय|जलप्रायं
जलप्राय n. (-यं) A country abounding with water.<BR> E. जल, and प्राय abund-<BR>ance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=284-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलप्रिय|जलप्रियः
जलप्रिय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Fond of water, frequenting water.<BR>	 m. (-यः)<BR>	 1.<BR>The Chataka, (Cuculus melanoleucos.)<BR>	 2. A fish.<BR> E. जल water, and<BR>प्रिय fond of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=284-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलप्लव|जलप्लवः
जलप्लव m. (-वः) An otter.<BR> E. जल water, and प्लव who goes or swims.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=284-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलप्लावन
जलप्लावन n. (-नं) An inundation, a deluge.<BR> E. जल, and प्लावन over-<BR>flowing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=284-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलबन्धक|जलबन्धकः
जलबन्धक m. (-कः) A dam, a dike, rocks or stones impeding a current.<BR>E. जल water, and बन्धक confining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=284-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलबन्धु|जलबंधु|जलबन्धुः
जलबन्धु m. (-न्धुः) A fish.<BR> E. जल water, and बन्धु a friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=284-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलबुद्वुद
जलबुद्वुद n. (-दं)<BR>	 n. A bubble of water.<BR> E. जल water, and वुद्बुद a bubble.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=284-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलब्रह्मी
जलब्रह्मी f. (-ह्यी) A kind of potherb, (Hilancha repens.)<BR> E. जल, and ब्रह्मी<BR>an asclepias.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=284-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलभू
जलभू mfn. (-भूः-भूः-भू) Aquatic, produced in or by water.<BR>	 m. (-भूः)<BR>	 1. A<BR>cloud.<BR>	 2. An aquatic plant, (Commelina salicifolia or bengalensis:)<BR>see कञ्चट<BR> E. जल water, and भू being or born. भवति अस्मात् भू अपादाने<BR>क्विप् ६ तत् स० ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=284-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलमक्षिका
जलमक्षिका f. (-का) A water insect.<BR> E. जल, and मक्षिका a fly. जलजाता मक्षिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=284-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलमद्गु|जलमद्गुः
जलमद्गु m. (-द्गुः) A kingfisher.<BR> E. जल and मद्गु another bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=284-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलमसि|जलमसिः
जलमसि m. (-सिः) A cloud.<BR> E. जल, and मसि ink; composed as it were<BR>of ink and water, alluding to its dark colour. जलंस्वस्थितं तोयं मस्यति<BR>छिनति सूक्ष्मांशतया भिनत्ति मस इन् ६ तत्-स० ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=284-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलमार्ग|जलमार्गः
जलमार्ग m. (-र्गः) A drain or issue from a pond, &c.<BR> E. जल water, and<BR>मार्ग a road, a water-course. जलस्य तद्वाहस्य मार्गः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=284-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलमार्जार|जलमार्जारः|जलमार्ज्जार
जलमार्जार m. (-रः) An otter.<BR> E. जल water, and मार्जार a cat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=284-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलमुच्
जलमुच् m. (-मुक्) A cloud.<BR> E. जल and मुच् from मुच् to set free, affix<BR>क्विप् liberating. जलानि मुञ्चति । मुच क्विप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=284-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलमूर्त्ति|जलमूर्ति|जलमूर्तिः|जलमूर्त्तिः
जलमूर्त्ति m. (-र्त्तिः) ŚIVA.<BR> E. जल and मूर्त्ति form; of whom one form is<BR>water; implying his omnipresence. जलं मूर्त्तिः अस्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=284-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलमूर्त्तिका|जलमूर्तिका
जलमूर्त्तिका f. (-का) Hail.<BR> E. जल and मूर्त्ति form, with कप् added; a form<BR>or condition of water. जलस्य मूर्त्तिः घनीभावः यत्र कप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=284-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलमोद|जलमोदं
जलमोद n. (-दं) A fragrant grass, (Andropogon muricatum.)<BR> E. जल and<BR>मोद what delights. जलेन मोदयति सेविनं मुद-णिच् अण् उप-स । उशीरे ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=284-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलम्बल
जलम्बल n. (-लं)<BR>	 1. A stream.<BR>	 2. Collyrium.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=284-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलयन्त्र|जलयंत्र
जलयन्त्र n. (-न्त्रं) A water-work, a machine for raising water, &c., any<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=285-a" target="_blank">Page285-a+ 60</a>]<BR>contrivance connected with that element.<BR> E. जल, and यन्त्र a ma-<BR>chine. जलानाम् उत्क्षेपणार्थं यन्त्रम् । (फोयारा) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=284-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलयन्त्रगृह|जलयंत्रगृह
जलयन्त्रगृह n. (-हं) A house or fabric erected in the midst of water, or<BR>subterraneous apartments constructed in the bank of a river, for<BR>retiring to in the hot season; a summer house, &c.<BR> E. जलयन्त्र a<BR>water-work, and गृह a house; also similar compounds, as जलयन्त्र-<BR>निकेतन, जलयन्त्रमन्दिर, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=285-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलरङ्क|जलरङ्कः
जलरङ्क m. (-ङ्कः) A kind of crane, (Ardea nivea.)<BR> E. जल, and रङ्क<BR>miserly, greedy of water; feeding on small fish chiefly, and<BR>therefore haunting swamps, &c. जले रङ्कः इव । वकपक्षिणि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=285-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलरङ्कु|जलरंकु|जलरङ्कुः
जलरङ्कु m. (-ङ्कुः) A gallinule.<BR> E. जल, and रङ्कु a sort of deer; the water-<BR>deer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=285-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलरञ्ज|जलरञ्जः
जलरञ्ज m. (-ञ्जः) The Vaka, (Ardea nivea.)<BR> E. जल, रञ्जि to be fond of,<BR>affix अच् । जले रञ्जति ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=285-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलरण्ड|जलरंड|जलरण्डः
जलरण्ड m. (-ण्डः)<BR>	 1. A whirlpool.<BR>	 2. A drop or a thin sprinkling of<BR>water.<BR>	 3. A snake.<BR> E. जल, and लडि to tremble, to play, &c. affix<BR>अच्, and ल becomes र । जलस्य रण्डः इव ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=285-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलरस|जलरसः
जलरस n. (-सं) Salt.<BR> E. जल water, and रस taste, essence. जलप्रधानः रसः<BR>अस्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=285-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलराशि|जलराशिः
जलराशि f. (-शिः) A piece of water, a quantity of water.<BR> E. जल, and<BR>राशि a heap.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=285-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलरुह्
जलरुह् m. (-रुट्) A lotus.<BR> E. जल water, रुह् to mount, affix क्विप्; also<BR>with क affix, जलरुह n. (-हं)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=285-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलरुप
जलरुप m. (-पः) The fish of KĀMADEVA.<BR> E. जल, and रूप form. जलस्य रूषम्<BR>इव रूपम् अस्य शुभ्रत्वात् । मकरे ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=285-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जललता
जललता f. (-ता) A wave, a billow.<BR> E. जल water, and लता a creeping<BR>plant. जलस्य लता इव सन्ततिमत्त्वात् । तरङ्गलेखायाम् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=285-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलवरण्ट|जलवरण्टः
जलवरण्ट m. (-ण्टः) A watery pustule, a sort of watery pox,<BR> E. जलप्रधानः<BR>वरण्टः (पानवसन्त) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=285-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलवल्कल|जलवल्कलः
जलवल्कल n. (-लं) An aquatic plant, (Pistia stratiotes.)<BR> E. जल, and वल्कल<BR>bark, rind. जलानां वल्कलः इव । कुम्भिकायाम् । (पाना) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=285-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलवायस|जलवायसः
जलवायस m. (-सः) A bird, the diver.<BR> E. जल, and वायस a crow, the water-<BR>crow; also जलकाक । जले वायसः इव कृष्णत्वात् (पानिकौडी) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=285-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलबालक|जलबालकः
जलबालक m. (-कः) The Vindhya mountain.<BR> E. जल water, बाड् to dive,<BR>and ण्वुल् affix; ड changed to ल; alluding to the many streams<BR>that rise in this range.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=285-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलबालिका
जलबालिका f. (-का) Lightning.<BR> E. जल water, and बालिका offspring,<BR>engendered at the rainy season.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=285-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलवाह|जलवाहः
जलवाह m. (-हः)<BR>	 1. A cloud.<BR>	 2. A water-carrier.<BR> E. जल, and वह् to bear,<BR>affix अण् । उप० स० । जलं वहति ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=285-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलवाहन|जलवाहनः
जलवाहन n. (-नं) Flowing of water.<BR>	 f. (-नी) A watercourse, an aqueduct.<BR>E. जल, and वाहन bearing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=285-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलविडाल|जलविडालः
जलविडाल m. (-लः) An otter.<BR> E. जल, and विडाल a cat; the water-cat. जले<BR>विडालः इव । (उद्विडाल) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=285-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलविन्दु
जलविन्दु f. (-न्दुः) A drop of water.<BR> E. जल, and विन्दु a drop.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=285-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलविल्व|जलविल्वः
जलविल्व m. (-ल्वः)<BR>	 1. A crab.<BR>	 2. A tortoise.<BR>	 3. A piece of water.<BR> E. जल,<BR>and विल्व a particular tree and fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=285-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलविषुव|जलविषुवं
जलविषुव n. (-वं) The autumnal equinox, the moment of the sun's enter-<BR>ing Libra.<BR> E. जल and विषुव equinox; the watery equinox occurring<BR>near the close of the annual rains.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=285-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलवृश्चिक|जलवृश्चिकः
जलवृश्चिक m. (-कः) A prawn or shrimp.<BR> E. जल water, वृश्चिक a scorpion.<BR>जले वृश्चिकः इव । (चिङ्गडिमत्स्ये) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=285-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलव्यध|जलव्यधः
जलव्यध m. (-धः) A kind of fish, (Esox cancila, HAM.)<BR> E. जल, and व्यध् to<BR>pierce, affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=285-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलव्याल|जलव्यालः
जलव्याल m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. A water-snake.<BR>	 2. A marine monster.<BR> E. जल, and<BR>व्याल a snake. जलस्थः व्यालः हिंस्रः (ढोडा साप).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=285-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलशय|जलशयः
जलशय m. (-यः) VIṢṆU.<BR> E. जल water, and शय who sleeps; he is suppos-<BR>ed to sleep borne by his serpent couch above the ocean, during<BR>the four months of the periodical rains in India; also during the<BR>intervals of the submersion of the world. जले शेते शी-अच् । ७ त० स० ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=285-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलशयन|जलशयनः
जलशयन m. (-नः) VIṢṆU.<BR> E. जल water, शी to sleep, affix ल्यु, see the<BR>preceding. जलं शयनम् अस्य । विष्णौ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=285-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलशायिन्
जलशायिन् m. (-यी) VIṢṆU.<BR> E. जल, and शायिन् who sleeps: see the<BR>preceding. जले समुद्रजले शेते शी-णिनि । नारायणे ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=285-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलशुक्ति|जलशुक्तिः
जलशुक्ति m. (-क्तिः) A bivalve shell.<BR> E. जल, and शुक्ति an oyster. जलस्य<BR>शुक्तिः इव । शम्बूके ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=285-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलशुचि
जलशुचि mfn. (-चिः-चिः-चि) Bathed, washed.<BR> E. जल, and शुचि cleansing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=285-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलशूक|जलशूकं
जलशूक m. (-कः) Vallisneria.<BR> E. जल, and शूक the beard of corn, &c. जलस्य<BR>शूकम् अग्रम् इव । शैवाले ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=285-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलशूकर|जलशूकरः
जलशूकर m. (-रः) A crocodile.<BR> E. जल and शूकर a hog, the water-hog.<BR>जलस्य शूकर इव । कुम्मीरे ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=285-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलसंसर्ग
जलसंसर्ग m. (-र्गः) Mixture with water, dilution.<BR> E. जल, and संसर्ग com-<BR>bination.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=285-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलसर्पिणी
जलसर्पिणी f. (-णी) A leech.<BR> E. जल water, सृप् to go or creep, affix णिनि,<BR>and ङीष्. जले सर्पति सृप्-णिनि । जलौकायाम् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=285-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलसूचि|जलसूचिः
जलसूचि m. (-चिः)<BR>	 1. A fish, a small sort of pike, (Esox cancila, HAM.)<BR>2. The Gangetic porpoise.<BR>	 3. A heron.<BR>	 4. An aquatic plant, (Trapa<BR>bispinosa.)<BR>	 f. (-चिः) A leech.<BR> E. जल water, and सूचि a needle. जलस्था<BR>सूचिः इव ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=285-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलस्थ
जलस्थ mfn. (-स्यः-स्था-स्थं) Being or abiding in water.<BR> E. जल, and स्थ who<BR>or what stays.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=285-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलह|जलहं
जलह n. (-हं) A small water (or summer) house.<BR> E. जल water, and हा<BR>to quit, affix डः see जलयन्त्रगृह, &c. जलेन हन्यते ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=285-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलहास|जलहासः
जलहास m. (-सः) Cuttlefish bone, considered as the indurated foam of<BR>the sea; also जलहासक.<BR> E. जल water, and हास laugh, smile; allud-<BR>ing to its white colour. जलानां हासः इव शुभ्रत्वात् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=285-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलाकर|जलाकरः
जलाकर m. (-रः) A piece of water, a spring, a fountain.<BR> E. जल, and<BR>आकर a mine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=285-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलाका
जलाका f. (-का) A. leech.<BR> E. जल, and अक् to go, अच् aff. जले आकायते प्रका-<BR>शते आ-कै-क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=285-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलाक्षी
जलाक्षी f. (-क्षी) An aquatic plant, (Commelina salicifolia.)<BR> E. जल, and<BR>अक्ष the eye, affix ङीष्ः see जलपिप्पली । जलम् अक्ष्णोति व्याप्नोति कारणतया<BR>अक्ष-अण् गौरा० ङीष् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=285-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलाखु|जलाखुः
जलाखु m. (-खुः) An otter.<BR> E. जल, and आखु a cat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=285-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलाञ्चल|जलांचल|जलाञ्चलं
जलाञ्चल n. (-लं) A natural water-course or channel.<BR>	 2. A plant, (Vallis-<BR>neria.)<BR> E. जल, and अञ्चल end of a garment. जलम् अञ्चति अञ्च-वा अलच्<BR>उत० स० ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=285-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलाञ्जलि|जलांजलि|जलाञ्जलिः
जलाञ्जलि f. (-लिः) A handful of water, or water held in the palms of<BR>the hand, as presented in oblation, &c.<BR> E. जल, and अञ्जलि saluta-<BR>tion. जलपूर्णः अञ्जलिः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=285-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलाटन|जलाटनः
जलाटन m. (-नः) A heron.<BR>	 f. (-नी) A leech.<BR> E. जल water, अट् to go,<BR>affixes ल्यु and ङीष् । जले अटति ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=285-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलाढ्य
जलाढ्य mfn. (-ढ्यः-ढ्या-ढ्यं) Watery, marshy.<BR> E. जल, and आढ्य rich,<BR>abounding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=285-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलाण्टक|जलांटक|जलाण्टकः
जलाण्टक m. (-कः) A shark, or according to some a large alligator, &c.<BR>see ग्राह.<BR> E. जल water, अटि to go, ण्वुल् पृषो० aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=285-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलाण्डक|जलाण्डकं
जलाण्डक m. (-कः) Small fry.<BR> E. जल water, अण्ड an egg, and क aff. जले<BR>अण्डः इव कायति कै-क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=285-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलात्मिका
जलात्मिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. A leech.<BR>	 2. A well.<BR> E. जल and आत्मा being, exist-<BR>ence, कप् aff. जलम् एव आत्मा अस्याम् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=285-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलादर्श
जलादर्श m. (-र्शः) Water reflecting any object, a watery mirror.<BR> E. जल,<BR>and आदर्श a mirror.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=285-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलाधार|जलाधारः
जलाधार m. (-रः) A pond, a lake, a reservoir, any piece of water.<BR> E. जल,<BR>and आधार a receptacle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=285-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलाधिदैवत|जलाधिदैवतः
जलाधिदैवत m. (-तः) A name of VARUṆA.<BR>	 n. (-तं) The asterism Purva-<BR>shadha.<BR> E. जल water, अधि over, and दैवत divinity; the possessor<BR>of divine supremacy over the element of water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=285-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलानुसार
जलानुसार m. (-रः) Going or acting like water.<BR> E. जल, and अनुसार agree-<BR>ing with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=285-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलाभिषेक
जलाभिषेक m. (-कः) Sprinkling with water.<BR> E. जल, and अभिषेक aspersion<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=285-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलाम्बिका|जलांबिका
जलाम्बिका f. (-का) A well.<BR> E. जल, and अम्बिका a mother; bearing water<BR>as it were in its womb: the word is sometimes read जलात्मिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=286-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलायुका
जलायुका f. (-का) A leech.<BR> E. जल water, अय to go, कप् aff. जलमायुरस्याः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=286-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलार्णव|जलार्णवः
जलार्णव m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. The rainy season.<BR>	 2. The sea of fresh water.<BR> E. जल<BR>water, and अर्णव a sea.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=286-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलार्थिन्
जलार्थिन् mfn. (-र्थी-र्थिनी-र्थि) Thirsty, desirous of water.<BR> E. जल, and अर्थिन्<BR>desirous of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=286-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलार्द्र|जलार्द्रः
जलार्द्र mfn. subst. (-र्द्रः-र्द्रा-र्द्रं) Wet cloth or clothes. adj. Wet, charged<BR>with aqueous moisture.<BR> E. जल water, and आर्द्र damp, moist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=286-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलालुका
जलालुका f. (-का) A leech.<BR> E. जल water, अल-उक affix; also जलायुका<BR>and जलालोका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=286-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलालोका
जलालोका f. (-का) A leech.<BR> E. जल water, आलोक to look or see, affix.<BR>घञ् । जले आलोक्यते । आ + लोक-कर्मणि घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=286-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलावर्त्त|जलावर्त|जलावर्तः|जलावर्त्तः
जलावर्त्त m. (-र्त्तः) An eddy, a whirlpool.<BR> E. जल water, and आवर्त्त turn-<BR>ing round. आ + वृत्-णिच् भावे अच् उत० स० । जलस्य स्वतः भ्रमणे ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=286-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलाविल
जलाविल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Stained or spotted with water.<BR> E. जल, and<BR>आविल muddy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=286-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलावुका
जलावुका f. (-का) A leech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=286-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलाशय|जलाशयं|जलाशयः
जलाशय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Stupid, dull, cold, apathetic.<BR>	 m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. A<BR>pond, a tank, a lake, a reservoir or any piece of water.<BR>	 2. The<BR>ocean.<BR>	 n. (-यं) A fragrant grass, (Androdgon muricatum.)<BR> E. जल<BR>water, and आशय an abode or receptacle, or जल for जड cold, and<BR>आशय disposition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=286-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलाशायिन्
जलाशायिन् mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि) Lying or sleeping in water as a penance.<BR>E. जल, and शी to sleep or lie, with आङ् prefixed, and णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=286-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलाश्रय|जलाश्रयः
जलाश्रय n. (-यं)<BR>	 1. A piece of water, a pond, a lake.<BR>	 2. A waterhouse. E.<BR>जल and आश्रय refuge, abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=286-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलाष्टीला
जलाष्टीला f. (-ला) A large square pond.<BR> E. जल water, स्था to abide, with<BR>आङ् prefixed, and अच् and ङीष् affixes. जलाष्टी and लच् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=286-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलाह्वय|जलाह्वयं
जलाह्वय n. (-यं) A lotus.<BR> E. जल, and आह्वय appellation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=286-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलिका
जलिका f. (-का) A leech.<BR> E. जल water, and ठक् affix: see जलौका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=286-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलुका
जलुका f. (-का) A leech.<BR> E. जस् to set free, (blood,) उक or ऊक Uṇādi<BR>affix, and स changed to ल; hence also, जलूका f. (-का) also<BR>जलौका, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=286-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलेचर|जलेचरः
जलेचर mfn. (-रः-रा-री-रं) Aquatic, living in or frequenting water.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-रः)<BR>	 1. A fish.<BR>	 2. Any kind of water fowl.<BR> E. जले in water, and<BR>चर who goes. जले चरति चर-ट वा अलुक् स ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=286-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलेच्छया
जलेच्छया f. (-या) A plant, (Heliotropium Indicum.)<BR> E. जलम् एति इ-क्विप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=286-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलेजात|जलेजातं
जलेजात n. (-तं) A lotus.<BR> E. जले the seventh case, in water, and जात<BR>born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=286-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलेन्द्र|जलेंद्र|जलेन्द्रः
जलेन्द्र m. (-न्द्रः)<BR>	 1. VARUṆA, the regent of water.<BR>	 2. A Jina or Jaina<BR>saint.<BR>	 3. The ocean of fresh water.<BR> E. जल water, and इन्द्र a ruler or<BR>chief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=286-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलेन्धन|जलेंधन|जलेन्धनः
जलेन्धन m. (-नः) Submarine fire.<BR> E. जल water, and इन्धन inflaming.<BR>जलानि इव इन्धनानि यस्य । वाडवानले ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=286-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलेवाह|जलेवाहः
जलेवाह m. (-हः) A diver, (by caste or business.)<BR> E. जले and वाह bearing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=286-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलेशय|जलेशयः
जलेशय m. (-यः) A fish.<BR> E. जले in the seventh case, in water, and शय<BR>who sleeps or abides, from शीङ् to sleep, affix अच् अलुक् समा० ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=286-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलेश्वर|जलेश्वरः
जलेश्वर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A name of the deity of water, VARUṆA.<BR>	 2. The ocean.<BR>E. जल, and ईश्वर sovereign.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=286-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलोका
जलोका f. (-का) A leech.<BR> E. जल water, and ओक a house; also जलौका,<BR>जलौकस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=286-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलोकिका
जलोकिका f. (-का) See the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=286-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलोच्छास
जलोच्छास m. (-सः) A drain or channel, made on purpose for carrying<BR>off an excess of water, or such a channel made naturally by the<BR>overflow of a river, &c.<BR> E. जल water, उत् up, and श्वास breath,<BR>breathing forth or expiration. जलानि उच्छसन्ति एभिः उत् + श्वस-घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=286-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलोदर|जलोदरं
जलोदर n. (-रः) Dropsy.<BR> E. जल, and उदर the belly. जलप्रधानम् उदरम् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=286-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलोद्भव
जलोद्भव mfn. (-वः-वा-वं) Aquatic, marine, born of or in water.<BR> E. जल, and<BR>उद्भव produced. जले उद्भवः अस्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=286-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलोरगी
जलोरगी f. (-गी) A leech.<BR> E. जल water, उरग a snake, diminutive affix<BR>ङीष् । जले उरगी इव ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=286-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलौकस्
जलौकस् f. (-काः) A leech.<BR> E. जल and ओकस् house; also जलौकस् with<BR>a final vowel. जलम् ओकः वसतिः आसाम् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=286-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलौकस|जलौकसः
जलौकस mfn. sub. (-सः-सा-सं) A leech. E. As before: see जलौकस्, अच्<BR>being added. जलम् ओकः स्थानम् अस्ति अस्याः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=286-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलौका
जलौका f. (-का) A leech. E. See the preceding; also जलोका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=286-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलौघ
जलौघ m. (-घः) A quantity of water.<BR> E. जल, and ओघ a heap.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=286-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जल्प|जल्पः
जल्प r. 1st cl. (जल्पते)<BR>	 1. To speak articulately, to say or tell.<BR>	 2. To<BR>prattle, to talk much or idly. (भ्वा-पर-सक-सेट् ।)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=286-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जल्प|जल्पः
जल्प m. (-ल्पः)<BR>	 1. Dissention, wrangling.<BR>	 2. Prate, babble.<BR>	 3. (In Logic.)<BR>Refutation of an advesary's arguments, and assertion of one's own.<BR>E. जल्प to speak, affix भाव घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=286-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जल्पक
जल्पक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) A chatterer, one who talks much or idly. E.<BR>जल्प to prate, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=286-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जल्पन|जल्पनं
जल्पन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Talking, saying.<BR>	 2. Chattering, prattling.<BR> E. जल्प, and<BR>भावे ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=286-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जल्पाक|जल्पाकः
जल्पाक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) A chatterer, talking much and foolishly, or<BR>improperly.<BR> E. जल्प to talk idly, षाक affix; also जल्पक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=286-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जल्पित|जल्पितं
जल्पित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Said, told, spoken.<BR>	 n. (-तं) Talking, babbling,<BR>gossiping.<BR> E. जल्प to talk, affix कर्मणि क्त । कथिते । भावे कथने ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=286-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जव|जवः
जव (इ) जवि r. 10th cl. (जंवयति) To shine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=286-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जव|जवः
जव mfn. (-वः-वा-वं) Swift, quick, expeditious.<BR>	 m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. Speed, velo-<BR>city.<BR>	 2. A runner, an express.<BR>	 f. (-वा) The China rose, (Hibiscus<BR>rosa sinensis;) also जपा.<BR> E. जु to move quickly, भावे अप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=286-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जवन|जवनं|जवनः
जवन mfn. (-नः-ना-नी-नं) Quick, fleet.<BR>	 m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. A courser, a fleet<BR>horse.<BR>	 2. A country, Ionia Greece: see यवन.<BR>	 3. A native of that<BR>country.<BR>	 4. A sort of deer.<BR>	 n. (-नं) Speed, velocity.<BR>	 f. (-नी)<BR>	 1. A<BR>screen surrounding a tent, a Kanat.<BR>	 2. A drug.<BR> E. जु to be quick<BR>affix ल्युट् or युच्, and fem. ङीष् or टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=286-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जवनाल|जवनालं
जवनाल n. (-लं) A sort of grain, (Andropogon bicolor:) see यवनाल.<BR>जवनाय अलति पर्य्याप्नोति अल-अच् । (जनार.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=286-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जवनिका
जवनिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. A wall or screen of cloth surrounding a tent, an<BR>outer tent, &c.<BR>	 2. A curtain, a screen in general.<BR> E. कन् added to<BR>जवनि सौ-जु करणे ल्युट् संज्ञायां कन् । (कानात्, चिक्) प्रभृतिव्यवधायकवस्त्रादौ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=286-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जवस|जवसं|जवसः
जवस m. (-सः) Meadow or pasture grass. जु to grow quick, असच् affix:<BR>see यवस.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=286-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जवादि
जवादि m. (-दिः) A perfume. मृगघर्मजाते कृत्रिमे गन्धद्रव्ये ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=286-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जवाधिक|जवाधिकः
जवाधिक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Very quick.<BR>	 m. (-कः) A fleet horse, a courser.<BR>E. जव speed, and अधिक exceeding. जवेन अधिकः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=286-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जवानिल|जवानिलः
जवानिल m. (-लः) A gale, a hurricane.<BR> E. जव fleet, अनिल wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=286-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जवापुष्प|जवापुष्पं
जवापुष्प m. (-ष्पः) The China rose, the plant or its flower.<BR> E. जवा as<BR>above, and पुष्प a flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=286-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जविन्
जविन् mfn. (-वी-विनी-वि) Quick or fleet expeditious.<BR>	 m. (-वी)<BR>	 1. A camel.<BR>2. A horse.<BR> E. जव speed, अस्त्र्यर्थे इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=286-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जष
जष r. 1st cl. (जषति-ते) To kill, to wound, to hurt or injure. भ्वा-उभ-सक-<BR>सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=286-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जस
जस (इर उ) इर् जसु r. 4th cl. (जस्यति) To liberate, to set free, to let loose.<BR>r. 1st and 10th cls. (जसति, जासयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To kill or injure.<BR>	 2. To<BR>slight or disregard, to treat irreverently.<BR>	 3. To strike, to punish<BR>with blows. (इ) जसि r. 1st and 10th cls. (जंसति जंसयति-ते) To pre-<BR>serve, to protect. मोक्षणे दिवा-पर-सक-सेट् । गतौ भ्वा-पर-सक-सेट् ।<BR>बधे अनादरे च चुरा-उभ-सक-सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=286-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जसुरि|जसुरिः
जसुरि m. (-रिः) INDRA'S thunderbolt.<BR> E. जस् to kill or hurt, Uṇādi<BR>affix उरिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=286-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जहक|जहकः
जहक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Abandoning, who leaves or abandons.<BR>	 m. (-कः)<BR>1. Time.<BR>	 2. A child.<BR>	 3. The slough of a snake.<BR> E. हा to quit, or<BR>abandon, क्वुन् Uṇādi aff. द्वित्वञ्च ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=286-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जहत्
जहत् mfn. (-हन्-हन्ती-हत्) Leaving, quitting, foregoing.<BR> E. हा to quit,<BR>शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=286-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जहत्स्वार्था
जहत्स्वार्था f. (र्था) The use of a word in a sense different from its ordi-<BR>nary one.<BR> E. जहत्, and स्वार्थ own meaning. जहन् स्वार्थः याम् । लक्षणाभेदे ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=287-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जहा
जहा f. (-हा) A plant, commonly Mundiri; also कदम्बपुष्पी, &c.<BR> E. हा to<BR>abandon, affixes ड and टाप्; shedding its leaves in spring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=287-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जहानक|जहानकः
जहानक m. (-कः) The period of the total destruction of the world E.<BR>हा to abandon, शानच् affix. and कन् added; also इ being substi-<BR>tuted for the vowel of reduplication, जिहानक as it is sometimes<BR>read.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=287-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जह्नु|जह्नुः
जह्नु m. (-ह्नुः)<BR>	 1. The name of a king or saint, son of KURU: see the<BR>next.<BR>	 2. A name of VIṢṆU.<BR> E. हा to abandon, (the world for devo-<BR>tion.) नु Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=287-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जह्नुतनया
जह्नुतनया f. (-या) The Ganges.<BR> E. जह्नु and तनया the daughter: the<BR>river in its course disturbed the devotions of the saint JANNHU,<BR>upon which he drank up its waters; having released them at the<BR>intercession of BHAGIRATHA, he is thus considered as the<BR>parent of the stream: see जाह्नवी; also जह्नुसुता, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=287-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जागर|जागरः
जागर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Walking, awake.<BR>	 mf. (-रः-रा) Waking, wakeful-<BR>ness, vigilance, &c.<BR>	 m. (-रः) Mail, armour.<BR> E. जागृ to wake, affix<BR>भावे घञ् गुणश्च ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=287-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जागरण|जागरणं
जागरण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Waking, watchfulness.<BR>	 2. Keeping watch, sitting<BR>up at night as part of a religious ceremony.<BR> E. जागृ to be awake,<BR>affix ण्वुल् गुणश्च ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=287-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जागरितृ
जागरितृ mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ) Wakeful, awake, vigilant.<BR> E. जागृ to wake,<BR>तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=287-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जागरिन्
जागरिन् mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि) Wakeful, awake.<BR> E. जागृ to wake, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=287-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जागरूक|जागरूकः
जागरूक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Wakeful, waking, watchful.<BR> E. जागृ to wake,<BR>ऊक aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=287-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जागर्त्ति|जागर्ति|जागर्तिः|जागर्त्तिः
जागर्त्ति f. (-र्त्तिः)<BR>	 1. Waking, vigilance.<BR>	 2. Keeping watch.<BR> E. जागृ to<BR>wake, भावे क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=287-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जागर्य्या|जागर्या
जागर्य्या f. (-र्य्या) Wakefulness, waking, watching.<BR> E. जागृ as above,<BR>भावे क्यप् aff. गुणश्च ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=287-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जागुड|जागुडं|जागुडः
जागुड n. (-डं)<BR>	 1. Saffron.<BR>	 2. A country so named. देशभेदे । सः अभिजन.<BR>अस्य अण् । तद्देशवासिनित्रि तत्र भवः अण् तद्देशभवेत्रि कुङ्कुमेन ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=287-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जागृ
जागृ r. 2nd cl. (जागर्त्ति) To wake, to be awake, or watchful. अदा-पर-<BR>अक-सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=287-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जागृवि|जागृविः
जागृवि m. (-विः) Fire or its deity.<BR> E. जागृ to wake. Uṇādi affix क्विन्, न<BR>गुणः । नृपे, तस्य स्वकार्य्ये अप्रमत्तत्वात् तथात्वम् । अग्नौ जागरणशीले च त्रि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=287-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाग्रत्
जाग्रत् mfn. (-ग्रन्-ग्रती-ग्रत्) Watching, being awake.<BR> E. जागृ to wake,<BR>Uṇādi affix शतृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=287-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाग्रिया
जाग्रिया f. (-या) Waking, watching.<BR> E. जागृ to wake, यत् affix, ऋ changed<BR>to its congener रि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=287-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाङ्गल|जांगल|जाङ्गलं|जाङ्गलः
जाङ्गल mfn. (-लः-ली-लं)<BR>	 1. Rural, picturesque, diversified with hill, vale,<BR>wood, and water, (country)<BR>	 2. Wild, jangali, barbarous, savage.<BR>3. Wild, (not tame, as an animal, &c.)<BR>	 m. (-लः) The francoline<BR>partridge.<BR>	 f. (-ली) Cowach, (Carpopogon pruriens.)<BR>	 n. (-लं)<BR>	 1. Flesh<BR>2. Game, the flesh of deer, &c.<BR> E. जङ्गल a wilderness, and अण् aff.<BR>जङ्गले भवः जङ्गलप्रायो वा ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=287-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाङ्गलि|जांगलिः|जाङ्गलिः
जाङ्गलि m. (-लिः) A snake-catcher.<BR> E. जङ्गल a wilderness, and इञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=287-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाङ्गुल|जांगुल|जांगुलं|जाङ्गुलं
जाङ्गुल n. (-लं) Poison, venom.<BR>	 f. (-ली)<BR>	 1. Knowledge of poisons, the<BR>possession of charms or drugs, and employment of them as anti-<BR>dotes.<BR>	 2. A potherb, (Luffa acutangula.)<BR> E. जङ्गुल poison, affix अण्<BR>or गम-यङ् लुक् वा डल् पृषो० दीर्घः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=287-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाङ्गुलि|जांगुलि|जांगुलिः|जाङ्गुलिः
जाङ्गुलि m. (-लिः) A snake-catcher, a dealer in antidotes.<BR> E. जङ्गुल, and<BR>इञ् aff. or गम-यङ् लुक् वा डुलि । विषवैद्ये ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=287-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाङ्गुलिक|जांगुलिक|जांगुलिकः|जाङ्गुलिकः
जाङ्गुलिक m. (-कः) A snake-catcher, a snake-doctor, one who pretends,<BR>chiefly by charms, to cure the bite of snakes or other venomous<BR>animals, a dealer in antidotes, &c.<BR> E. जङ्गुल poison, and ठञ् aff.<BR>जाङ्गुली विषविद्या ताम् अधीते वेद वा तया दीव्यति वा ठञ् । विषवैद्ये ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=287-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाङ्घनी
जाङ्घनी f. (-नी) The thigh.<BR> E. जङ्घा the leg, affixes अण् and ङीष्, नुम्<BR>augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=287-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाङ्घिक|जांघिक|जाङ्घिकः
जाङ्घिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Relating or belonging to the leg.<BR>	 m. (-कः)<BR>	 1.<BR>A courier, a running footman, an express.<BR>	 2. A camel.<BR> E. जङ्घा a<BR>leg, and ठञ् aff. जङ्घाभ्यां जीवति ठञ् । धावके उष्ट्रे च ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=287-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाजिन्
जाजिन् m. (-जी) A warrior, a combatant.<BR> E. जज् to fight, and णिनि aff.<BR>जजो योधे ताच्छील्ये णिनि । योधशीले ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=287-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाज्वल्यमान|जाज्वल्यमानः
जाज्वल्यमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Shining, flaming, blazing.<BR> E. ज्वल् to burn,<BR>intensitive form, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=287-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाटलि|जाटलिः
जाटलि mf. (-लिः-ली) A plant, (Bignonia suave-olens;) a various reading<BR>for पाटलि q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=287-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाड्य|जाड्यं
जाड्य n. (-ड्यं)<BR>	 1. Coldness, apathy.<BR>	 2. Folly, stupidity, dulness or cold-<BR>ness of intellect.<BR>	 3. Coldness, frigidity.<BR> E. जड cold, &c. ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=287-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जात|जातं|जातः
जात mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Born, engendered.<BR>	 2. A child, offspring.<BR>	 3. Ap-<BR>parent, manifest.<BR>	 4. Produced, caused, occasioned.<BR>	 5. Felt, enter-<BR>tained.<BR>	 6. Inspired with, affected by.<BR>	 n. (-तं)<BR>	 1. Kind, sort, class,<BR>species.<BR>	 2. Multitude, collection.<BR>	 3. Individuality, specific condi-<BR>tion.<BR>	 4. Birth, production.<BR> E. जन् to be born, aff. कर्त्तरि भावे वा क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=287-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातक|जातकं|जातकः
जातक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Born.<BR>	 m. (-कः) A mendicant.<BR>	 n. (-कं) Astrolo-<BR>gical calculation of a nativity.<BR> E. स्वार्थे क added to the pre-<BR>ceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=287-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातकध्वनि|जातकध्वनिः
जातकध्वनि m. (-निः) A leech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=287-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातकर्मन्|जातकर्म्मन्
जातकर्मन् n. (-र्म)<BR>	 1. A ceremony performed when the navel string is<BR>divided, touching the infant's tongue thrice with ghee, with ap-<BR>propriate prayers, &c.<BR>	 2. Delivery &c. of a newborn infant. E.<BR>जात born, and कर्मन् rite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=287-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातदन्त
जातदन्त mf. (-न्तः-न्ती) A child that has got a tooth.<BR> E. जात, and दन्त a tooth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=287-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातप्रत्यय
जातप्रत्यय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Confiding, believing, inspired with confidence.<BR>E. जात, and प्रत्यय trust.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=287-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातमर्ष
जातमर्ष mfn. (-र्षः-र्षी-र्षं) Enraged, vexed, angry.<BR> E. जात, and मर्ष wrath.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=287-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातमात्र
जातमात्र mfn. (-त्रः-त्री-त्रं) What is just born, or merely born.<BR>	 n. (-त्रं)<BR>As soon as born, the instant of birth.<BR> E. जात, and मात्रच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=287-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातरूप|जातरूपं
जातरूप mfn. (-पः-पी-पं) Embodied, assuming shape or form.<BR>	 n. (-पं)<BR>Gold.<BR> E. जात produced, and रूप form. जातं प्रशस्तं जात + प्रशस्ते रूपप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=287-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातवेदस्
जातवेदस् m. (-दाः) AGNI or fire.<BR> E. जात born, वेद a Veda, असुन्<BR>Uṇādi affix or जात kind, sort, and विद् to know, or comprehend,<BR>affix as before: one legend makes the Vedas to have issued from<BR>the mouth of AGNI. जातं सद्योजातं विन्दति प्राप्नोति विद-लाभे असुन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=287-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातश्रम
जातश्रम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं) Wearied, exhausted.<BR> E. जात, and श्रम fatigue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=287-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातस्पृह
जातस्पृह mfn. (-हः-हा-हं) Desirous, wishing for.<BR> E. जात, and स्पृहा wish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=287-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातहार्द्द|जातहार्द
जातहार्द्द mfn. (-र्द्दः-र्द्दी-र्द्दं) Becoming attached to or fond of.<BR> E. जात, and<BR>हार्द्द affection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=287-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातागस्
जातागस् mfn. (-गाः-गाः-गः) Offending, sinning, committing any fault. E.<BR>जात, and आगस् sin; also जातापराध, जातदोष, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=287-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातापत्या
जातापत्या f. (-त्या) A mother, a woman who has borne a child.<BR> E. जात<BR>born, (by whom,) अपत्य offspring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=287-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाताश्रु
जाताश्रु mfn. (-श्रुः-श्रुः-श्रु) Weeping, shedding tears.<BR> E. जात, and अश्रु a<BR>tear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=287-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाति|जातिः
जाति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Kind, sort, species, class, tribe.<BR>	 2. Birth, production.<BR>3. Lineage, race, family.<BR>	 4. A fireplace, a chimney.<BR>	 5. Emblic<BR>myrobalan, (Phyllanthus emblica.)<BR>	 6. A plant: see काम्पिल्ल.<BR>	 7. A<BR>kind of poetical metre.<BR>	 8. A rhetorical ornament.<BR>	 9. (In Arith-<BR>metic,) Assimilation, as विशेषजाति assimilation of the difference,<BR>शेषजाति of the remainder.<BR>	 10. Proximate cause or occurance of<BR>disease, &c.<BR>	 f. (-तिः or -ती)<BR>	 1. Great flowered jasmine, (J. grandi-<BR>florum.)<BR>	 2. Mace, nutmeg.<BR>	 f. (-तिः) The flower of the jasmine. E.<BR>जन् to be born, affix क्तिन् and occasionally ङीष added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=287-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातिकोश|जातिकोशं|जातिकोशः
जातिकोश n. (-शं) Nutmeg.<BR> E. जाति or जाती mace, and कोश or कोष<BR>sheathe; hence also जातिकोष, जातीकोश or जातीकोष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=287-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातित्व
जातित्व n. (-त्वं)<BR>	 1. Distinction or nature of caste or tribe.<BR>	 2. Special or<BR>generic property.<BR> E. त्व added to जाति; also with तल् जातिता ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=287-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातिधर्म्म|जातिधर्म|जातिधर्मः
जातिधर्म्म m. (-र्म्मः)<BR>	 1. The duty of caste, as sacred study of the Brah-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=288-a" target="_blank">Page288-a+ 60</a>]<BR>man, battle of the Kṣatriya, &c.<BR>	 2. Generic or specific property.<BR>E. जाति, and धर्म्म duty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=287-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातिफल|जातिफलं
जातिफल n. (-लं) Nutmeg.<BR> E. जाति or जाती mace, and फल fruit; also<BR>जातीफल; also जातिकोष, जाति or जाती and जातिपुष्पं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=288-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातिभ्रंश|जातिभ्रंशः
जातिभ्रंश m. (-शः) Loss of caste.<BR> E. जाति, and भ्रंश injury.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=288-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातिभ्रंशकर|जातिभ्रंशकरं
जातिभ्रंशकर mfn. (-रः-री-रं) Forbidden, improper, causing loss of caste.<BR>n. (-रं) Doing any act prohibited to a particular caste.<BR> E. जातिभ्रंश,<BR>and कर what makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=288-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातिमात्र
जातिमात्र n. (-त्रं)<BR>	 1. Species, genus.<BR>	 2. Caste only, not the performance<BR>of its especial duties.<BR> E. जाति, and मात्र only.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=288-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातिलक्षण
जातिलक्षण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Specific or generic distinction or characteristic.<BR>	 2.<BR>Mark of tribe or caste.<BR> E. जाति and लक्षण indication.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=288-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातिवैर|जातिवैरं
जातिवैर n. (-रं) Innate or instinctive hostility.<BR> E. जाति and वैर enmity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=288-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातिवैलक्षण्य
जातिवैलक्षण्य n. (-ण्यं) Inconsistency, incompatibility, conduct or qua-<BR>lity at variance with tribe or species.<BR> E. जाति, and वैलक्षण्य incon-<BR>sistency.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=288-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातिस्वभाव|जातिस्वभावः
जातिस्वभाव m. (-वः) Specific or generic character or nature.<BR> E. जाति and<BR>स्वभाव nature.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=288-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातिस्मर
जातिस्मर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) One who recollects his condition in a former<BR>life.<BR> E. जाति, and स्मर who remembers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=288-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातिहीन
जातिहीन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Outcaste, void of caste.<BR> E. जाति and हीन void of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=288-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातीपत्री
जातीपत्री f. (-त्री) Mace.<BR> E. जाति and पत्री a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=288-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातीय|जातीयः
जातीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Relating to any species, belonging to any tribe<BR>or order.<BR> E. जाति, and छ aff. जातौ भवः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=288-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातीरस|जातीरसं
जातीरस n. (सं) Gam myrrh.<BR> E. जाती nutmeg, and रस juice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=288-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातु
जातु ind.<BR>	 1. Sometimes, occasionally.<BR>	 2. A particle of prohibition.<BR>3. Of doubt, 4. Of contempt or abuse.<BR> E. जै to waste or decay, क्तुन्<BR>aff. जै क्षये जन वा क्तुन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=288-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातुक|जातुकं
जातुक n. (-कं) Asafœtida.<BR> E. जतुक the same, and अण् pleonastic aff.<BR>जातु गर्हितं कं जलम् अस्मात् । हिङ्गुनि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=288-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातुधान|जातुधानः
जातुधान m. (-नः) A Rākṣasa, an imp or goblin.<BR> E. जातु sometimes, धान<BR>possessing, from धा with ल्युट् or युच्; otherwise यातुधान, or जातु<BR>गर्हितं धानम् अभिधानम् अस्य । राक्षसे ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=288-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातुष|जातुषं
जातुष mfn. (-षः-षी-षं) Made, &c. of lac, any artificial form or condition<BR>of it.<BR> E. जतु lac, अण् affix, and मुक् augment. जतुनो विकारः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=288-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातेष्टि|जातेष्टिः
जातेष्टि f. (-ष्टिः) Rites performed at birth.<BR> E. जात and इष्टि sacrifice. जाते<BR>पुत्रजनने इष्टिः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=288-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातोक्ष|जातोक्षः
जातोक्ष m. (-क्षः) A bullock.<BR> E. जात born, उक्ष an ox. जातः प्राप्तदम्यावस्थः ।<BR>उक्षा टच् स ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=288-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जात्य|जात्यः
जात्य mfn. (-त्यः-त्या-त्यं)<BR>	 1. Well-born, legitimate, born of parents of the<BR>same caste.<BR>	 2. Best, excellent.<BR>	 3. Pleasing, beautiful.<BR>	 4. Rectangu-<BR>lar.<BR> E. जाति family, &c. यत् aff. जातौ भवः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=288-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जात्यन्तर
जात्यन्तर n. (-रं) Interval of difference of caste.<BR> E. जाति and अन्तर<BR>interval.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=288-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जात्यन्ध|जात्यंध|जात्यन्धः
जात्यन्ध mfn. (-न्धः-न्धा-न्धं) Born-blind.<BR> E. जाति birth, अन्ध blind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=288-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जानकी
जानकी f. (-की) A name of SITA.<BR> E. जनक the father of this lady affixes<BR>अण् and ङीष् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=288-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जानत्
जानत् mfn. (-नन्-नन्ती-नत्) Knowing, understanding.<BR> E. ज्ञा to know, aff.<BR>शतृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=288-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जानन
जानन n. (-नं) Knowing, understanding.<BR> E. ज्ञा to know, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=288-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जानपद|जानपदः
जानपद m. (-दः)<BR>	 1. Man, mankind.<BR>	 2. An inhabited country.<BR> E. जनपद<BR>the same, and अप् aff. जानेन उत्पत्त्या पद्यते पद-अप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=288-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जानु
जानु m. (-नुः) The knee.<BR> E. जन् to be produced, (walking, motion.) ञुन्<BR>Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=288-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जानुफलक
जानुफलक n. (-कं) The knee pan or patella.<BR> E. जानु, and फलक a layer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=288-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जानुसन्धि|जानुसंधि|जानुसन्धिः
जानुसन्धि f. (-न्धिः) The knee-joint.<BR> E. जानु, and सन्धि articulation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=288-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाप|जापः
जाप m. (-पः) Muttering prayers by beads, or reciting passages of the<BR>Vedas, &c. inaudibly.<BR> E. जप् to mutter, &c. affix घञ्, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=288-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जापक|जापकः
जापक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Muttering prayers, one who does so.<BR> E. जप and<BR>ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=288-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जापन|जापनं
जापन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Declining, rejection, dissent.<BR>	 2. Dismissing, complet-<BR>ing, finishing.<BR> E. जप् to speak, causal form भावे ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=288-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाप्य
जाप्य mfn. (-प्यः-प्या-प्यं) To be muttered, &c.<BR>	 n. (-प्यं) The muttering of<BR>prayers, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=288-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाबाल|जाबालः
जाबाल m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. The name of a saint.<BR> E. जबलाया अपत्यम् अण् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=288-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाबालि|जाबालिः
जाबालि m. (-लिः) The name of a Muni, one of the original teachers of<BR>the Vedas.<BR> E. जबल and इञ् patronymic affix; also with अण् जाबाल<BR>as before.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=288-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जामदग्न्य|जामदग्न्यः
जामदग्न्य m. (-ग्न्यः) A name of PARASURAMA.<BR> E. जमदग्नि a Muni so named<BR>and यञ् patronymic affix; the son of the saint JAMADAGNI.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=288-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जामातृ
जामातृ m. (-ता)<BR>	 1. A daughter's husband, a son-in law.<BR>	 2. A husband,<BR>a lord or master.<BR>	 3. A friend.<BR>	 4. The sunflower, (Helianthus<BR>annus.)<BR> E. जा for जाया a wife, मा to take, तृच् Uṇādi aff. जायां याति<BR>मिनोति मिमीते वा निपा ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=288-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जामि|जामिः
जामि f. (-मिः or -मी)<BR>	 1. A virtuous and respectable woman.<BR>	 2. A sister,<BR>&c.<BR> E. जै to decline or decay, affix मि; or जम् to eat, affix option-<BR>ally added इन् नि० वृद्धिः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=288-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जामेय|जामेयः
जामेय m. (-यः) A sister's son.<BR> E. जामि a sister, ढक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=288-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाम्बव|जांबव|जांबवं|जाम्बवं
जाम्बव n. (-वं)<BR>	 1. The rose apple, the fruit.<BR>	 2. Gold.<BR> E. जम्बु the tree,<BR>अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=288-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाम्बवौष्ठ
जाम्बवौष्ठ n. (-ष्ठं) A cauterising needle or probe.<BR> E. जाम्बवम् इव ओष्ठः अस्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=288-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाम्बबत्
जाम्बबत् m. (-वान्) A fabulous bear, father-in-law to KṚṢṆA.<BR> E. जाम्ब<BR>the Jambu tree, and मतुप् affix; also जाम्बुवत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=288-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाम्बूनद|जांबूनद|जांबूनदं|जाम्बूनदं
जाम्बूनद n. (-दं) Gold.<BR> E. जम्बुनदी a river flowing from mount Sumeru,<BR>the Indian Pactolus, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=288-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाम्बुनदमय
जाम्बुनदमय mfn. (-यः-यी-यं) Golden, made of gold.<BR> E. जाम्बूनद and मयट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=288-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जायक|जायकं
जायक n. (-कं) A yellow fragrant wood.<BR> E. जि to excel (all perfumes),<BR>and ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=288-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जायमान
जायमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Being born, coming into life.<BR> E. जन् to be born,<BR>शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=288-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाया
जाया f. (-या) A wife, one wedded according to the perfect ritual. E.<BR>जन् to be born, affix यक्; in whom a man is again born, that is to<BR>say, he is re-born in his children. जायते अस्याम् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=288-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जायाघ्न|जायाघ्नः
जायाघ्न m. (-घ्नः)<BR>	 1. A murderer of his wife.<BR>	 2. A mole or mark on the<BR>body, indicative of the death of a wife.<BR> E. जाया and घ्न what destroys.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=288-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जायाजीव|जायाजीवः
जायाजीव m. (-वः) An actor, a dancer.<BR> E. जाया a wife, and जीव who gets<BR>a livelihood. जायया तन्नर्त्तनवृत्त्या जीवति अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=288-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जायात्व
जायात्व n. (-त्वं) The character or attributes of a wife.<BR> E. जाया, and त्व aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=288-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जायानुजीविन्
जायानुजीविन् m. (-वी)<BR>	 1. An actor, a dancer, a mime, &c.<BR>	 2. A kind of<BR>crane, the Vaka (Ardea nivea.)<BR>	 3. A needy man, a pauper.<BR>	 4. The<BR>husband of a harlot.<BR> E. जाया a wife, अनु like or with, and जीविन्<BR>who gets a livelihood; who is supported by his wife. जायया अनुजी-<BR>वति अनु + जीव-णिनि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=288-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जायापती
जायापती m. du. (-ती) Husband and wife.<BR> E. जाया a wife, and पति hus-<BR>band.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=288-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जायु|जायुः
जायु m. (-युः) A medicine, a medicament.<BR> E. जि to subdue, (disease,)<BR>Uṇādi affix उण् । जयति रोगान् । औषधे जयशीले च ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=288-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जार|जारः
जार m. (-रः) A paramour, a gallant.<BR>	 f. (-री) A drug, a medicament. E.<BR>जॄ to grow infirm, करणे घञ् affix of agency, fem. ङीष्; weakening<BR>the affection of wives to their husbands, or diminishing the<BR>force of disease. जीर्य्यति अनेन ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=288-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जारज|जारजः
जारज mf. (-जः-जा) An adulterine, the child of a woman by her gallant.<BR>E. जार as above, and ज born. जारात् उपपतेः जायते जन-ड ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=288-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जारजात|जारजातः
जारजात mf. (-तः-ता) An adulterine.<BR> E. जार and जात born; also with कन्<BR>added, जारजातक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=288-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जारण|जारणं
जारण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Calcining or oxydizing metals.<BR>	 2. A condiment, a<BR>digester.<BR> E. जॄ to decay, causal form, ल्यु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=288-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जारभरा
जारभरा f. (-रा) An adulteress.<BR> E. जार, and भरा who cherishes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=288-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जारुत्थ
जारुत्थ m. (-त्थः) A sacrifice, thrice worshipping the sun in his southern<BR>declination.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=288-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाल|जालं|जालः
जाल n. (-लं)<BR>	 1. A net.<BR>	 2. A window, a lattice, an eyelet or loophole.<BR>3. A multitude, an assemblage.<BR>	 4. An unblown flower.<BR>	 5. Pride,<BR>arrogance.<BR>	 6. Magic, conjuring, illusion, supernatural deception<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. The Kadamba-tree.<BR>	 2. The young fruit of a gourd or<BR>cucumber.<BR>	 f. (-ली)<BR>	 1. A small cucumber, (Trichosanthes diœca,<BR>Rox.)<BR>	 2. Any medicament or drug.<BR> E. जल् to encompass, to hide<BR>or screen, affix अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=289-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जालक|जालकं|जालकः
जालक n. (-कं)<BR>	 1. A bud, a germ.<BR>	 2. An unblown flower.<BR>	 3. A nest.<BR>	 4. A<BR>net.<BR>	 5. Pride.<BR>	 6. A plantain, the fruit.<BR>	 7. Multitude, assemblage.<BR>m. (-कः) A window, a lattice, a loop or eyelet-hole.<BR>	 f. (-लिका)<BR>	 1.<BR>Armour, chain armour.<BR>	 2. A kind of cloth or raiment, woollen<BR>cloth.<BR>	 3. A leech.<BR>	 4. A window.<BR>	 5. Iron.<BR> E. जाल, and कन् added, or<BR>जल् to enclose, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=289-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जालकारक|जालकारकः
जालकारक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A spider.<BR>	 2. A net-maker.<BR> E. जाल a net, cobweb,<BR>and कारक a fabricator.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=289-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जालकिनी
जालकिनी f. (-नी) A sheep, an ewe.<BR> E. जालक woollen cloth, इनि and<BR>ङीष affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=289-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जालगणिका
जालगणिका f. (-का) A churning vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=289-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जालगर्द्दभ|जालगर्दभ|जालगर्दभः|जालगर्द्दभः
जालगर्द्दभ f. (-भः) A dull spreading pimple or boil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=289-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जालन्धर|जालंधर|जालंधरः|जालन्धरः
जालन्धर m. (-रः) The name of a country situated in the northwest of<BR>India, apparently part of Lahore, and perhaps the modern Jullun-<BR>dhar.<BR>	 m. plu. (-राः) The inhabitants of Jallandhara.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=289-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जालपाद्
जालपाद् m. (-त् or -द्) A goose.<BR> E. जाल a net, and पाद् a foot; web-footed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=289-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जालप्राया
जालप्राया f. (-या) Armour, iron net-work, or chain armour.<BR> E. जाल a net,<BR>and प्राय resembling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=289-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जालबद्ध
जालबद्ध mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं) Caught in a net, snared.<BR> E. जाल, and बद्ध bound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=289-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जालिक|जालिकः
जालिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) A cheat, a rogue, a vagabond, a conjuror or<BR>juggler.<BR>	 2. One who employs nets, &c. for a livelihood.<BR>	 m. (-कः) A<BR>spider.<BR>	 2. A fisherman.<BR>	 3. A hunter using nets.<BR> E. जाल a net, &c.<BR>affix ठक् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=289-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जालिन्
जालिन् mfn. (-ली-लिनी-लि)<BR>	 1. Having a net.<BR>	 2. Having a window. Illu-<BR>sory, deceptive.<BR>	 m. (-ली)<BR>	 1. A fisherman.<BR>	 2. a hunter using nets.<BR>3. A juggler.<BR>	 f. (-नी) A painting room.<BR> E. जाल a net, &c इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=289-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाल्म|जाल्मः
जाल्म mfn. (-ल्मः-ल्मा-ल्मं)<BR>	 1. Cruel, harsh, severe.<BR>	 2. Inconsiderate, rash,<BR>acting without thinking.<BR>	 m. (-ल्मः) A low man, one of a degraded<BR>tribe or business.<BR> E. जल् to screen or hide, affix मक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=289-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाषक|जाषकं
जाषक n. (-कं) A yellow fragrant wood.<BR> E. जष् to hurt, affix ण्वुल्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=289-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाह|जाहं
जाह m. (-हः) A termination affixed to nouns denoting parts of the<BR>body, such as कर्ण, अक्षि, &c. in the sense of “the root of” com-<BR>pare कर्णजाह.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=289-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाहक|जाहकः
जाहक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A cat 2. A pole-cat.<BR>	 3. A bed, a cot.<BR>	 4. A leech. E.<BR>हा to quit, affix ण्वुल्; radical initial doubled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=289-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाह्नवी
जाह्नवी f. (-वी) GANGA or the Ganges personified.<BR> E. जह्नु a saint, अण्<BR>affix of descent, fem. affix ङीष्, the daughter of JANHU: see<BR>जह्नुतनया.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=289-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जि|जिः
जि r. 1st cl. (जयति)<BR>	 1. To excel, to be pre-eminent, to surpass.<BR>	 2. To<BR>conquer, to reduce or overcome. With वि or परा prefixed, (विजयते<BR>पराजयते) To overcome, to conquer. भ्वा-पर-सक-अनिट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=289-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जि|जिः
जि mfn. (जिः-जिः-जि) Victorious, conquering, a victor.<BR>	 m. (-जिः) A<BR>demon.<BR> E. जि to conquer, कि aff. जयशीले पिशाचे च ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=289-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिगत्नु|जिगत्नुः
जिगत्नु m. (-त्रुः) Breath, life.<BR> E. गम् to go, to depart, कत्नुच् Uṇādi affix,<BR>and the radical repeated. प्राणवायौ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=289-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिगमिषत्
जिगमिषत् mfn. (-षन्-षन्ती-षत्) Wishing or endeavouring to go.<BR> E. गम् to<BR>go, desiderative form, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=289-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिगमिषा
जिगमिषा f. (-षा) Wish to go or move.<BR> E. गम् to go, desider. form, अङ्<BR>टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=289-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिगमिषु
जिगमिषु mfn. (-षुः-षुः-षु) Wishing to go.<BR> E. गम् to go, desiderative form, उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=289-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिगरिषु
जिगरिषु mfn. (-षुः-षुः-षु) Wishing to take, to lay hold of, to take away.<BR>E. गृ to seize, desiderative form, उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=289-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिगीषा
जिगीषा f. (-षा)<BR>	 1. Emulation, wish to excel or overcome.<BR>	 2. Eminence.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=289-b" target="_blank">Page289-b+ 60</a>]<BR>3. Usage, profession or habit of life.<BR> E. जि to conquer, in the desi-<BR>derative form, अङ् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=289-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिगीषु
जिगीषु mfn. (-षुः-षुः-षु) Striving to overcome, vieing or contending with.<BR>E. जि to conquer; desiderative form, affix उ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=289-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिघत्सत्
जिघत्सत् mfn. (-त्स्यन्-त्सन्ती-त्सत्) Wishing to eat.<BR> E. अद् to eat, desiderative<BR>form, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=289-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिघत्सा
जिघत्सा f. (-त्सा) Hunger.<BR> E. अद् to eat, in the desiderative form, अङ्<BR>and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=289-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिघत्सु|जिघत्सुः
जिघत्सु mfn. (-त्सुः-त्सु-त्सु) Hungry. E. See the preceding, affix उ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=289-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिघांसा
जिघांसा f. (-सा) Wish or intention to kill.<BR> E. हन् to kill, desiderative<BR>form, अङ् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=289-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिघांसु|जिघांसुः
जिघांसु mfn. (-सुः-सुः-सु) Mischievous, murderous, seeking to hurt or<BR>kill.<BR>	 m. (-सुः) An enemy.<BR> E. हन् to kill &c. in the desiderative form,<BR>form, उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=289-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिघांसत्
जिघांसत् mfn. (-सन्-सन्ती-सत्) Wishing to kill, murderous, felonious. E.<BR>हन् to kill, desiderative form, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=289-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिघांसियस्
जिघांसियस् mfn. (-यान्-यसी-यः) Very desirous or determined to kill, E.<BR>जिघांस, and ईयसुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=289-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिघृक्षत्
जिघृक्षत् mfn. (-क्षन्-क्षन्ती-क्षत्) Desirous to take, greedy, avaricious. E.<BR>ग्रह् to take, desiderative form, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=289-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिघृक्षा
जिघृक्षा f. (-क्षा) Greediness, covetousness, wish to seize or take.<BR> E. ग्रह् to<BR>take, desiderative form, सन् भावे अ and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=289-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिघृक्षु
जिघृक्षु mfn. (-क्षुः-क्षुः-क्षु) Wishing to seize or take.<BR> E. ग्रह् to take, desi-<BR>derative form, उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=289-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिघ्र|जिघ्रः
जिघ्र mfn. (-घ्रः-घ्रा-घ्रं) Smelling,<BR> E. घ्रा to smell, श affix, root reiterated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=289-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिघ्रत्
जिघ्रत् mfn. (-घ्रन् घ्रन्ती-घ्रत्) Smelling<BR> E. घ्रा to smell, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=289-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिङ्गशल्य
जिङ्गशल्य m. (-ल्यः) A tree, (Mimosa catechu:) see जिह्मशल्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=289-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिङ्घि
जिङ्घि f. (-ङ्घिः or ङ्घी) Bengal madder, (Rubia manjith, Rox.)<BR> E. इङ्ग going.<BR>from इगि to go, &c. added to जि to excel, fem. affix ङीष्; excelling<BR>all other plants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=289-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिजीविषु
जिजीविषु mfn. (-षुः-षुः-षु) Desirous of life.<BR> E. जीव् to live, desiderative<BR>form, उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=289-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिजीषत्
जिजीषत् mfn. (-षन्-षन्ती-षत्) Wishing or striving to overcome, emulous,<BR>ambitious, a warrior.<BR> E. जि to conquer, desiderative form, शतृ<BR>aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=289-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिज्ञापयिषु
जिज्ञापयिषु mfn. (-षुः-षुः-षु) Wishing or seeking to inform.<BR> E. ज्ञा to know,<BR>desiderative form of the causal. उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=289-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिज्ञासमान
जिज्ञासमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Inquiring, investigating.<BR> E. ज्ञा to know, desi-<BR>derative form, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=289-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिज्ञासा
जिज्ञासा f. (-सा)<BR>	 1. Asking, inquiring.<BR>	 2. Search, investigation.<BR> E. ज्ञा to<BR>know, desider. form, अङ् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=289-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिज्ञासित|जिज्ञासितः
जिज्ञासित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Asked, inquired, sought.<BR> E. ज्ञा to know, de-<BR>sid. form, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=289-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिज्ञासु|जिज्ञासुः
जिज्ञासु mfn. (-सुः-सुः-सु) Inquiring, inquisitive.<BR> E. ज्ञा to know, desid.<BR>form, उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=289-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जित्
जित् mfn. (-जित्) Who or what conquers or surpasses.<BR> E. जि to conquer,<BR>affix क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=289-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जित|जितः
जित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Conquered, subdued, surpassed, overcome.<BR>	 m. (-तः)<BR>One of the attendants upon a Jina or Jaina saint.<BR> E. जि to con-<BR>quer, aff. कर्मणि क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=289-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जितकाशि|जितकाशिः
जितकाशि m. (-शिः) The fist doubled. जित conquered, काश to shine,<BR>इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=289-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जितकाशिन्
जितकाशिन् mfn. (-शी-शिनी-शि) Victorious.<BR> E. जित conquered, and काशिन्<BR>who shines, from काशृ, with णिनि aff. जितेन जयेन काशते प्रकाशते ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=289-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जितक्रोध|जितक्रोधः
जितक्रोध mfn. (-धः-धा-धं) Of subdued passion, not to be provoked or<BR>made angry.<BR> E. जित, and क्रोध wrath. जितः क्रोधः येन ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=289-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जितनेमि|जितनेमिः
जितनेमि m. (-मिः) A staff made of the wood of religious fig tree. E.<BR>जित excelled, (by which,) and नेमि circumference of a wheel, (of<BR>any other wood.) जिता नेमिः अत्र ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=289-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जितशत्रु|जितशत्रुः
जितशत्रु mfn. (-त्रुः-त्रुः-त्रु) Victorious, triumphant.<BR>	 m. (-त्रुः) The father<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=290-a" target="_blank">Page290-a+ 60</a>]<BR>Ajita, the 2nd Jaina saint.<BR> E. जित, and शत्रु a foe: see other simi-<BR>lar compounds, जितामित्र, जितारि, &c. जितः शत्रुः येन ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=289-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जितश्रम
जितश्रम m. (-मः) One who is free from worldly cares, a stoic.<BR> E. जित,<BR>and श्रम fatigue, exertion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=290-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिताक्षर|जिताक्षरः
जिताक्षर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Reading well or readily.<BR> E. जित mastered, and<BR>अक्षर a letter. जितानि आयत्तीकृतानि अक्षराणि येन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=290-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जितात्मन्
जितात्मन् mfn. (-त्मा-त्मा-त्म) Self-subdued, void of passion.<BR> E. जित, and<BR>आत्मन् spirit. जितः वशीकृतः आत्मा इन्द्रियं मनः वा येन ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=290-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जितामित्र|जितामित्रः
जितामित्र mfn. (-त्रः-त्रा-त्रं) Triumphing, victorious over an enemy.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-त्रः) VIṢṆU.<BR> E. जित subdued, by whom, and अमित्र a foe. जितः<BR>अमित्रः येन ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=290-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जितारि|जितारिः
जितारि mfn. (-रिः-रिः-रि) Victorious, triumphant.<BR>	 m. (-रिः)<BR>	 1. A Jina or<BR>Jaina deified saint.<BR>	 2. The father of SAMBHAVA, the third of the<BR>Jaina pontiffs of this age.<BR>	 3. A conqueror.<BR> E. जित conquered, (by<BR>whom,) and अरि an enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=290-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिताहव|जिताहवः
जिताहव mfn. (-वः-वा-वं) Victorious, triumphant.<BR> E. जित conquered, and<BR>and आहव war, battle. जितः शत्रुः आहवे येन ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=290-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जितेन्द्रिय|जितेंद्रिय|जितेन्द्रियः
जितेन्द्रिय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Having subdued the senses, calm, unmoved.<BR>m. (-यः) An ascetic, a sage, one who has completely subdued his<BR>passions.<BR> E. जित subdued, इन्द्रिय an organ of sense. जितानि वशीकृतानि<BR>इन्द्रियाणि येन ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=290-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जितेन्द्रियत्व
जितेन्द्रियत्व n. (-त्वं) Continece, subjugation of the senses or passions.<BR> E. त्व added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=290-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जित्तम|जित्तमः
जित्तम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं) Most victorious, first of the victors.<BR>	 m. (-मः) The<BR>constellation, Gemini.<BR> E. जित, and तमप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=290-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जित्य|जित्यः
जित्य mfn. (-त्यः-त्या-त्यं) Conquerable, vincible.<BR>	 m. (-त्वः) A harrow.<BR>	 f. (-त्या)<BR>A ploughshare.<BR> E. जि to excel, क्यप् affix, तुक् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=290-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जित्वर|जित्वरः
जित्वर mfn. (-रः-री-रं) Victorious, triumphant.<BR>	 f. (-री) The city of<BR>Benares.<BR> E. जि to conquer or excel, क्वरप् affix, तुक् inserted, fem.<BR>affix ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=290-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जित्वा
जित्वा ind. Having conquered or excelled.<BR> E. जि to conquer, क्त्वाच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=290-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिन|जिनः
जिन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Victorious, triumphant.<BR>	 m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. A Jina,<BR>the generic name of the personage peculiar to the Jaina sect,<BR>who is ranked by them as superior to the gods of the other<BR>sects: a saint and teacher: twenty-four Jinas are supposed to<BR>flourish in an Avasarpiṇī or Jaina age, and their writers enumer-<BR>ate those of the ages past, present, and to come.<BR>	 2. A Buddha; a<BR>generic term applied to the chief saints of the Buddha sect, in<BR>the same manner as to those of the Jainas.<BR>	 3. A name of VIṢṆU.<BR>4. A very old man.<BR>	 5. A sage, one who is omniscient.<BR> E. जि to<BR>conquer or excel, नक् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=290-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिनयोनि|जिनयोनिः
जिनयोनि m. (-निः) A deer.<BR> E. अजिन the skin of a deer, and योनि a place<BR>of production; the initial of the first word rejected; also<BR>अजिनयोनि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=290-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिनसद्मन्
जिनसद्मन् n. (-द्म) A Jaina temple, or monastery.<BR> E. जिन a Jina, and सद्मन् abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=290-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिनेन्द्र|जिनेंद्र|जिनेन्द्रः
जिनेन्द्र m. (-न्द्रः) A Jaina or Jina saint.<BR> E. जिन a Jaina teacher, and<BR>इन्द्र a lord or master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=290-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिम
जिम (उ) जिमु r. 1st cl. (जेमति-ते) To eat: see जम भ्वा० प० सक० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=290-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिरि
जिरि r. 5th cl. but restricted to the Vedas (जिरिणोति) To injure, wound<BR>or kill. स्वा-प-सक-सेट् । अयं वैदिकधातुः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=290-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिव
जिव (इ) जिवि r. 1st cl. (जिन्वति)<BR>	 1. To please, to delight or charm.<BR>	 2. To<BR>be pleased, or charmed.<BR>	 3. To loose. भ्वा० प० सक० सेट् इदित् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=290-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिवाजिव|जिवाजिवः
जिवाजिव m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. A pheasant.<BR>	 2. The Chakora bird: see जीवञ्जीव.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=290-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिवि
जिवि r. 5th cl. (जिविनोति) To seek, to hurt or kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=290-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिव्रि|जिव्रिः
जिव्रि m. (-व्रिः)<BR>	 1. Time.<BR>	 2. A bird.<BR> E. जॄ to decay, Uṇādi affix रिक् रस्य वः<BR>and व substituted for the conversion of र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=290-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिष
जिष (उ) जिषु r. 1st cl. (जेषति) To sprinkle. भ्वा० प० सक० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=290-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिष्णु|जिष्णुः
जिष्णु mfn. (-ष्णुः-ष्णुः-ष्णु)<BR>	 1. Victorious, triumphant.<BR>	 2. Winning.<BR>	 3. Ex-<BR>celling m. (-ष्णुः)<BR>	 1. A name of VIṢṆU or KṚṢṆA.<BR>	 2. An epithet<BR>of INDRA.<BR>	 3. A name of ARJUNA.<BR>	 4. The sun.<BR> E. जि to conquer,<BR>ण्स्नु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=290-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिहान
जिहान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>	 1. Going, going to, attaining, obtaining.<BR>	 2.<BR>Abandoning, leaving.<BR> E. हा to go, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=290-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिहानक|जिहानकः
जिहानक m. (-कः) The destruction of the world: see जहानक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=290-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिहीर्षा
जिहीर्षा f. (-र्षा) Wish to take or seize.<BR> E. हृ to take, desiderative form,<BR>चङ् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=290-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिहीर्षु
जिहीर्षु mfn. (-र्षुः-र्षुः-र्षु) Wishing to take, seizing, carrying off.<BR> E. हृ to<BR>take, desiderative form, उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=290-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिह्म|जिह्मं|जिह्मः
जिह्म mfn. (-ह्मः-ह्मा-ह्मं)<BR>	 1. Morally Crooked.<BR>	 2. Dishonest.<BR>	 3. Slow, lazy.<BR>4. Dim, dark.<BR>	 5. Oblique, squint.<BR>	 m. (-ह्मः) A tree, (Tabernæmontana<BR>coronaria.)<BR> E. हा to quit, (a straight line,) मन् Uṇādi affix, and the<BR>root reduplicated, deriv, irr. हा मन् सन्वत् आलोपश्च ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=290-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिह्मग|जिह्मगः
जिह्मग mfn. (-गः-गा-गं) Going tortuously or lazily.<BR>	 m. (-गः) A snake. E.<BR>जिह्म as above, and ग what goes. जिह्मं कुटिलं मन्दं वा गच्छति गम-ड ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=290-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिह्मता
जिह्मता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Crookedness, curvature.<BR>	 2. Dishonesty.<BR> E. तल् added<BR>to जिह्म; also with त्व, जिह्मत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=290-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिह्ममोहन|जिह्ममोहनः
जिह्ममोहन m. (-नः) A frog.<BR> E. जिह्म slowly, and मोहन copulation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=290-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिह्मशल्य|जिह्मशल्यः
जिह्मशल्य m. (-ल्यः) The Khadira, (Mimosa catechu.)<BR> E. जिह्म crooked,<BR>शल्य a dart.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=290-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिह्मित
जिह्मित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Bent, bowed, curved.<BR>	 2. Turned away.<BR> E. जिह्म,<BR>and इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=290-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिह्व|जिह्वं|जिह्वः
जिह्व mf. (-ह्वः-ह्वा) The tongue.<BR> E. लिह् to lick, Uṇādi affix वन्, and the<BR>initial changed do ज.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=290-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिह्वल|जिह्वलः
जिह्वल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Greedy.<BR> E. जिह्वा the tongue, ल to take, क affix, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=290-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिह्वाग्र
जिह्वाग्र n. (-ग्रं)<BR>	 1. The tip of the tongue.<BR> E. जिह्वा, and अग्र end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=290-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिह्वानिर्लेखन|जिह्वानिर्लेखनं
जिह्वानिर्लेखन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Scraping the tongue.<BR>	 2. A tongue-scraper. E.<BR>जिह्वा, and निर्लेखन scraping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=290-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिह्वाप|जिह्वापः
जिह्वाप m. (-पः)<BR>	 1. A dog.<BR>	 2. A cat.<BR>	 3. A tiger.<BR>	 4. The hunting leopard.<BR>5. A bear.<BR> E. जिह्वा the tongue, and प who drinks, who laps. जिह्वया<BR>पिबति पा-क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=290-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिह्वामल|जिह्वामलं
जिह्वामल n. (-लं) The fur of the tongue.<BR> E. जिह्वा, and मल dirt, excretion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=290-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिह्वामूल
जिह्वामूल n. (-लं) The root of the tongue.<BR> E. जिह्वा, and मूल a root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=290-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिह्वामूलीय|जिह्वामूलीयः
जिह्वामूलीय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. A term applied to the Visarga before क, and ख,<BR>and also to the guttural class of consonant.<BR>	 2. A character substi-<BR>tuted for the Viserga as हरिःकाम्य, and with a like sound.<BR> E. जिह्वा-<BR>मूल, and छ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=290-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिह्वारद|जिह्वारदः
जिह्वारद m. (-दः) A bird.<BR> E. जिह्वा, and रद a tooth; whose tooth, (i. e.<BR>beak,) is like a tongue. जिह्वा रदः इव यस्य । पक्षिणि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=290-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिह्वालिह
जिह्वालिह m. (-लिट्) A dog.<BR> E. जिह्वा, and लिह् who licks or laps, from<BR>लिह् with क्विप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=290-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिह्वास्वाद|जिह्वास्वादः
जिह्वास्वाद m. (-दः) Licking, lapping.<BR> E. जिह्वा the tongue, and आस्वाद eating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=290-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिह्वाशत
जिह्वाशत n. (-तं) A hundred tongues.<BR> E. जिह्वा, and शत a century.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=290-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिह्वोल्लेखन
जिह्वोल्लेखन n. (-नं) Scraping the tongue.<BR>	 f. (-नी) A tongue-scraper, made<BR>of a thin piece of wood of the Mimusops Kauki or other trees.<BR>E. जिह्वा, and उल्लेखन scraping; also in the second sense. with कन्<BR>added, जिह्वोल्लेखनिका ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=290-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीन|जीनः
जीन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Old, aged.<BR> E. ज्या to become old, क्त affix, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=290-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीमूत|जीमूतः
जीमूत m. (-तः)<BR>	 1. A cloud.<BR>	 2. A mountain.<BR>	 3. A grass, (Andropogon<BR>serratus.)<BR>	 4. A name of INDRA.<BR>	 5. A nourisher, a sustainer.<BR>	 6. A<BR>plant: see घोषक.<BR>	 7. A species of the Dandaka metre.<BR> E. जि to<BR>excel or surpass, Uṇādi affix तन् and मूट् augment, or जी for जीव<BR>life, and मूत who urines. जयति नभः जीयते अनिलेन वा ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=290-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीमूतकुट
जीमूतकुट m. (-टः) A small hill near a mountain.<BR> E. जीमूत a mountain,<BR>and कुट a house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=290-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीमूतवाहन|जीमूतवाहनः
जीमूतवाहन m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. INDRA.<BR>	 2. The author of “Dayabhaga” a celebrated<BR>work on inheritance.<BR> E. जीमूत a cloud, and वाहन vehicle. जीमूतः मेघः<BR>वाहनम् अस्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=290-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीमूतवाहिन्
जीमूतवाहिन् m. (-ही) Smoke.<BR> E. जीमूत a cloud, and वह् to bear, affix णिनि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=290-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीर|जीरः
जीर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Cumin-seed.<BR>	 2. A sacrificial knife or sword, a scymitar.<BR>3. A sort of panic seed: see अणु.<BR> E. जु to go, or grow quickly, रक्<BR>Uṇādi affix, and the radical vowel changed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=290-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीरक|जीरकः
जीरक m. (-कः) Cumin seed.<BR> E. कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=291-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीर्ण|जीर्णं|जीर्णः
जीर्ण mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-र्णं)<BR>	 1. Old, ancient.<BR>	 2. Withered decayed.<BR>	 3. Digest-<BR>ed.<BR>	 m. (-र्णः)<BR>	 1. An old man.<BR>	 2. Cumin seed.<BR>	 n. (-र्णं) Benjamin. E.<BR>E. जॄ to become old or decayed, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=291-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीर्णज्वर|जीर्णज्वरः
जीर्णज्वर m. (-रः) Fever of some continuance and diminished intensity.<BR>E. जीर्ण, and ज्वर fever.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=291-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीर्णता
जीर्णता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Old oge.<BR>	 2. Infirmity, decay.<BR> E. जीर्ण and तल् affix;<BR>also with त्व, जीर्णत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=291-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीर्णदारु|जीर्णदारुः
जीर्णदारु m. (-रुः) A potherb, (Convolvulus argentaceus.)<BR> E. जीर्ण and<BR>दारु wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=291-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीर्णपर्ण|जीर्णपर्णः|जीर्णपर्ण्ण
जीर्णपर्ण m. (-र्णः) The Kadamba: see कदम्बक.<BR>	 n. (-र्णं) A withered leaf.<BR>E. जीर्ण old, withered, and पर्ण a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=291-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीर्णवज्र|जीर्णवज्रं
जीर्णवज्र n. (-ज्रं) A particular gem, said to be a sort of diamond.<BR> E. जीर्ण<BR>decayed, वज्र diamond.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=291-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीर्णवत्
जीर्णवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Old, decayed.<BR> E. जॄ to grow old, क्तवतु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=291-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीर्णवस्त्र|जीर्णवस्त्रं
जीर्णवस्त्र n. (-स्त्रं) Old, worn or tattered raiment.<BR> E. जीर्ण old, and वस्त्र<BR>cloth or clothes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=291-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीर्णवाटिका
जीर्णवाटिका f. (-का) A ruined mansion.<BR> E. जीर्ण, and वाटिका a house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=291-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीर्णब्रध्नक
जीर्णब्रध्नक m. (-कः) A fragrant grass, (Cyperus rotundus.)<BR> E. जीर्ण old,<BR>and ब्रध्न a root, affix कन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=291-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीर्णि|जीर्णिः
जीर्णि f. (-र्णिः)<BR>	 1. Old age, infirmity, decay.<BR>	 2. Digestion.<BR> E. जॄ to be-<BR>come old, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=291-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीर्णोद्यान
जीर्णोद्यान n. (-नं) A neglected garden.<BR> E. जीर्ण, and उद्यान a garden.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=291-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीर्णोद्धार|जीर्णोद्धारः
जीर्णोद्धार m. (-रः) Repairing, renewal, repairs.<BR> E. जीर्ण and उद्धार<BR>lifting up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=291-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीर्णोद्धृत
जीर्णोद्धृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Repaired, renewed.<BR> E. जीर्ण, and उद्धृत lifted up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=291-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीर्वि|जीर्विः
जीर्वि m. (-र्विः)<BR>	 1. An axe.<BR>	 2. A cart.<BR>	 3. The body.<BR> E. जॄ to decay, Uṇādi<BR>affix क्विन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=291-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीव|जीवः
जीव (ऋ) जीवृ r. 1st cl. (जीवति) To live. With आङ् To use or enjoy, to<BR>get a living. With उप, To be dependent on for a living. With सं or<BR>प्र To live agreeably. भ्वा० अक० प० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=291-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीव|जीवः
जीव mfn. (-वः-वा-वं)<BR>	 1. Life, the vital breath, existence.<BR>	 mf. (-वः-वा)<BR>	 1.<BR>Livelihood, profession, specific occupation.<BR>	 2. A tree: see जीवन्ती.<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. The sentient soul, the emanation of the deity, which<BR>is incorporated with the animal body, and gives it life, motion<BR>and sensation; hence also called जीवात्मन्; it is opposed to that<BR>abstract state of the soul परमात्मन् in which, by meditating upon<BR>its own divine nature and origin, the spirit is set at liberty from<BR>human feelings and passions.<BR>	 2. A name of VṚHASPATI.<BR>	 3. A<BR>name of the prince KARṆA.<BR>	 4. The constellation called Pushya.<BR>f. (-वा)<BR>	 1. A bow string.<BR>	 2. The earth.<BR>	 3. The tinkling of metallic<BR>ornaments.<BR>	 4. Orris root.<BR>	 5. (In Geometry.) The chord of an arc. E.<BR>जीव् to live, affix घञ् or क and fem. affix टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=291-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवक|जीवकः
जीवक mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>	 1. A servant, a slave, one who gets a livelihood<BR>by service.<BR>	 2. A snake-catcher, one whose business is catching<BR>snakes, curing their bites, &c.<BR>	 3. An usurer, or one who lives by<BR>lending money at high interest.<BR>	 4. A mendicant or one who lives by<BR>begging.<BR>	 5. One whose life is prolonged by blessings.<BR>	 m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A<BR>tree, (Pentaptera tomentosa:) see असन.<BR>	 2. A medicinal plant, com-<BR>monly called by the same name Jivaca, and considered as one of<BR>the eight principal drugs, classed together under the name अष्टबर्ग.<BR>3. An animal, any being endowed with life.<BR> E. जीव् to live, affix<BR>णिच् ण्वुल् or वुन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=291-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवग्राह|जीवग्राहः
जीवग्राह m. (-हः) A prisoner, one taken alive.<BR> E. जीव, and ग्राह capture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=291-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवजीव|जीवजीवः
जीवजीव m. (-वः) A kind of bird, supposed to be a a sort of pheasant:<BR>see जीवञ्जीव.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=291-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवञ्जीव|जीवंजीव|जीवञ्जीवः
जीवञ्जीव m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. A kind of bird, supposed to be a pheasant.<BR>	 2. The<BR>Chakora or Greek partridge.<BR>	 3. A kind of tree.<BR> E. जीव life, and जीव<BR>who lives, from जीव् with खच् affix, long lived.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=291-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवत्|जीवन्त्
जीवत् mfn. (-वन्-वन्ती वत्) Living, alive.<BR> E. जीव् to live, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=291-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवत्तोका
जीवत्तोका f. (-का) A woman whose children are living.<BR> E. जीवत् living,<BR>and तोक offspring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=291-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवत्पति|जीवत्पतिः
जीवत्पति f. (-तिः) A wife whose husband is alive.<BR> E. जीवत्, living, and<BR>पति a husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=291-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लीवत्पितृक
लीवत्पितृक m. (-कः) A son whose father is alive.<BR> E. जीवत्, and पितृ a<BR>a father, कप् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=291-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवथ|जीवथः
जीवथ mfn. (-थः-था-थं)<BR>	 1. Virtuous, pious.<BR>	 2. Long-lived.<BR>	 m. (-थः)<BR>1. Virtue, piety.<BR>	 2. Life, existence.<BR>	 3. A cloud.<BR>	 4. A peacock.<BR>5. A tortoise.<BR> E. जीव् to live, अथ Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=291-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवद|जीवदः
जीवद mfn. (-दः-दा-दं) Life-giving, who or what gives life.<BR>	 m. (-दः)<BR>1. A physician, a practitioner of medicine.<BR>	 2. An enemy.<BR> E. जीव<BR>life, and द in the first sense, from दा to give, in the second, from<BR>दो to destroy, affix क, जीवं जीवनं ददाति द्यति वा ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=291-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवधन|जीवधनं
जीवधन n. (-नं) Living property, live stock, wealth in flocks and herds.<BR>E. जीव alive, and धन wealth. जीव एव धनम् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=291-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवन|जीवनं|जीवनः
जीवन m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. A plant, commonly Jiuti, (Odina wodier.)<BR>	 2. A son.<BR>3. A living being, an animal.<BR>	 f. (-ना or -नी) A plant, commonly<BR>Jiyati: see जीवन्ती.<BR>	 f. (-नी)<BR>	 1. Jasmin.<BR>	 2. giving life.<BR>	 n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Life,<BR>existence.<BR>	 2. Livelihood, profession.<BR>	 3. Water.<BR>	 4. Butter of new one<BR>day-old milk.<BR>	 5. Marrow.<BR>	 6. Wind.<BR> E. जीव् to live, affix ल्यु or करणे<BR>वा भावे ल्युट्. ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=291-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवनक|जीवनकं
जीवनक m. (-कः) Food especially boiled rice.<BR> E. कन् added to the<BR>preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=291-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवनविडम्बन
जीवनविडम्बन n. (-नं) Disappointment of all hopes, living in vain. E.<BR>जीवन, and विडम्बन frustrating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=291-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवनयोनि|जीवनयोनिः
जीवनयोनि m. (-निः) Communication of vitality with body.<BR> E. जीवन, and<BR>योनि origin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=291-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवनहेतु|जीवनहेतुः
जीवनहेतु m. (-तुः) End or object of life, the cause of living.<BR> E. जीवन, and<BR>हेतु cause.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=291-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवनाघात|जीवनाघातं
जीवनाघात n. (-तं) Poison.<BR> E. जीवन life, and आघात destroying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=291-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवनान्त|जीवनांत|जीवनान्तः
जीवनान्त m. (-न्तः) Death.<BR> E. जीवन, and अन्त end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=291-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवनावास|जीवनावासः
जीवनावास m. (-सः) VARUṆA, regent of water.<BR> E. जीवन water, and आवास abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=291-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवनीय|जीवनीयं
जीवनीय n. (-यं) Water.<BR>	 f. (-या) Jiyati: see जीवन्ती.<BR> E. जीवन life, छ affix:<BR>being friendly or necessary to existence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=291-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवनोपाय|जीवनोपायः
जीवनोपाय m. (-यः) Livelyhood, means of subsistence.<BR> E. जीवन, and उपाय<BR>means.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=291-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवनौषध|जीवनौषधं
जीवनौषध n. (-धं) A drug to revive the dead.<BR> E. जौवन living, and औषध<BR>a medicament.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=291-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवन्त|जीवंत|जीवन्तः
जीवन्त mfn. (-न्तः-न्ती-न्तं) Living, existent.<BR>	 m. (-न्तः)<BR>	 1. Life, existence.<BR>	 2.<BR>A medicament, a drug.<BR>	 f. (-न्ती)<BR>	 1. The name of a tree, commonly<BR>Jiyati, (Celtis orientalis.)<BR>	 2. A plant, (Menispermum glabrum:)<BR>see गुडूची.<BR>	 3. The Sami or Saen tree, (Mimosa albida.)<BR>	 4. A para-<BR>site plant.<BR>	 5. Yellow myrobalan, (Terminalia chebula, Rox.)<BR> E. जीव्<BR>to live, affix कर्त्तरि, fem. affix ङीप्; also with कन् added जीवन्तिका, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=291-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवन्तिक|जीवंतिक|जीवंतिकः|जीवन्तिकः
जीवन्तिक m. (-कः) A fowler, a bird-catcher: see जीवान्तक.<BR>	 f. (-का)<BR>	 1. A<BR>parasite plant, (Epidendron tesseloides,) and other species.<BR>	 2. A<BR>plant, (Menispermum glabrum.)<BR>	 3. A kind of potherb.<BR> E. कन् add-<BR>ed to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=291-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवन्मुक्त|जीवन्मुक्तः
जीवन्मुक्त m. (-क्तः) A man purified by knowledge of BRAMHA, and exon-<BR>erated whilst living from future birth, and all ritual ceremonies. E.<BR>जीवन, and मुक्त freed. जीवन्नेव मुक्तः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=291-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवन्मुक्ति|जीवन्मुक्तिः
जीवन्मुक्ति f. (-क्तिः) Acquirement of spiritual knowledge, and consequent<BR>liberation from future birth, and ritual acts.<BR> E. जीवत्, and मुक्ति li-<BR>beration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=291-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवपुत्रक
जीवपुत्रक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A tree, commonly Ingua.<BR>	 2. A different plant<BR>bearing seeds which are used in rosaries, commonly (जिंँआपोती)<BR>Jiyaputa, (Nageia putranjiva.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=291-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवबध
जीवबध m. (-धः) Destruction of living beings.<BR> E. जीव, and बध killing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=291-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवमन्दिर|जीवमंदिर|जीवमन्दिरं
जीवमन्दिर m. (-रः) The body.<BR> E. जीव life, and मन्दिर mansion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=291-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवभूत
जीवभूत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Alive, endowed with life.<BR> E. जीव, and भूत become.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=291-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवलोक|जीवलोकः
जीवलोक n. (-कं)<BR>	 1. The world, the habitation of living beings.<BR>	 2. Man-<BR>kind.<BR> E. जीव, and लोक world. जीवानां लोकः भोगसाधनम् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=292-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवसाधन
जीवसाधन n. (-नं) Rice, grain, corn.<BR> E. जीव, and साधन means.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=292-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवसाफल्य
जीवसाफल्य n. (-ल्यं) Realisation of all one's wishes.<BR> E. जीव, and साफल्य fruit-<BR>fulness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=292-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवसू
जीवसू f. (-सूः) The mother of living offspring.<BR> E. जीव living, and सू bring-<BR>ing forth. जीवन्तं मूते सू-क्विप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=292-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवस्थान|जीवस्थानं
जीवस्थान n. (-नं) A joint, an articulation.<BR> E. जीव life, and स्थान place<BR>कर्मणि ल्यु ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=292-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवाजीवाधार|जीवाजीवाधारः
जीवाजीवाधार m. (-रः) The material and visible world.<BR> E. जीव animate,<BR>and अजीव inanimate, आधार a support.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=292-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवातु|जीवातुः
जीवातु mn. (-तुः-तु)<BR>	 1. A drug for reanimating the dead.<BR>	 2. Boiled rice,<BR>food.<BR>	 3. Life, existence.<BR> E. जीव life, णिच् कर्त्तरि आतु Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=292-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवात्मन्
जीवात्मन् m. (-त्मा) The vital principle or spirit; that spiritual essence<BR>which renders bodies susceptible of motion or sensation.<BR> E. जीव<BR>life, and आत्मन् soul or spirit. जीवति जीव अच् कर्म० ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=292-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवाधार|जीवाधारः
जीवाधार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. The world.<BR>	 2. Heart.<BR> E. जीव an animal, and आधार<BR>support. संसारे हृदये च ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=292-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवान्तक|जीवांतक|जीवान्तकः
जीवान्तक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A fowler, a bird-catcher.<BR>	 2. A destroyer of life, a<BR>slayer, a murderer.<BR> E. जीव a living being, and अन्तक a destroyer;<BR>also sometimes written जीवन्तिक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=292-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवाश
जीवाश mfn. (-शः-शा-शं) Hoping for life.<BR>	 f. (-शा) Hope of living.<BR> E. जीव,<BR>and आशा hope.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=292-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीविका
जीविका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. Livelihood, profession or occupation by which a<BR>subsistence is obtained.<BR>	 2. A tree: see जीवन्ती.<BR> E. जीव् to live, ण्वुल्<BR>and टाप् affixes: see जीवक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=292-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीविकापन्न
जीविकापन्न mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं) Having obtained subsistence.<BR> E. जीविका, and<BR>आपन्न obtained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=292-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीविकाप्राप्त
जीविकाप्राप्त mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं) Having obtained as a livelihood.<BR> E. जीविका,<BR>and प्राप्त obtained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=292-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवित|जीवितं
जीवित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Living, alive, existent.<BR>	 n. (-तं) Living, life, exist-<BR>ence.<BR> E. जीव, and भावे क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=292-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवितकाल|जीवितकालः
जीवितकाल n. (-लं) Period or duration of life, a life.<BR> E. जीवित existence,<BR>and काल time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=292-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवितज्ञा
जीवितज्ञा f. (-ज्ञा) An artery, a vessel of the body.<BR> E. जीवित, and ज्ञा who<BR>knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=292-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवितव्य
जीवितव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं) To be lived, to be kept alive.<BR> E. जीव, and<BR>तव्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=292-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवितव्यय|जीवितव्ययः
जीवितव्यय m. (-यः) Casting away life, sacrifice of life.<BR> E. जीवित, and व्यय expense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=292-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवितसंशय|जीवितसंशयः
जीवितसंशय m. (-यः) Fear of death.<BR> E. जीवित, and संशय doubt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=292-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवितहारिन्
जीवितहारिन् mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि) Destroying life.<BR> E. जीवित, and हारिन्<BR>what takes away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=292-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीविताशा
जीविताशा f. (-शा) Love of life.<BR> E. जीवित, and आशा hope.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=292-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवितेश|जीवितेशः
जीवितेश mfn. (-शः-शा-शं) Ruling life, a master of being, (applicable to<BR>objects either of reverence or affection.)<BR>	 m. (-शः)<BR>	 1. A name of<BR>YAMA, regent of death.<BR>	 2. The sun.<BR>	 3. The moon.<BR>	 4. A lover, a<BR>husband.<BR>	 5. Lord or master of existence.<BR>	 6. A drug to revive the<BR>dead.<BR> E. जीवित life, and ईश lord, ruler.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=292-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवोत्सर्ग|जीवोत्सर्गः
जीवोत्सर्ग m. (-र्गः) Abandonment of life, voluntary death.<BR> E. जीव, and<BR>उत्सर्ग leaving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=292-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीविन्
जीविन् mfn. (-वी-विनी-वि) Alive, living, animate, a living being.<BR> E. जीव,<BR>and णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=292-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जु
जु r. 1st cl. (जवति)<BR>	 1. To go or move quickly, to go rapidly.<BR> E. भ्वा० प०<BR>अक० अनिट् जुङ् (ङ) r. 1st cl. (जवते) To go or move. सौत्रधातुः आत्म०<BR>सक० अनिट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=292-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुकुट|जुकुटः
जुकुट m. (-टः)<BR>	 1. The Malaya range of mountains.<BR>	 2. A dog.<BR>	 n. (-टं)<BR>The egg plant, (Solanum melongena)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=292-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुग
जुग (इ) जुगि r. 1st cl. (जुंगति)<BR>	 1. To except, to exclude.<BR>	 2. To quit or<BR>abandon.<BR> E. भ्वा० प० सक० सेट् इदित् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=292-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुगुप्सन|जुगुप्सनं
जुगुप्सन n. (-नं) Censure, abuse, reproach, reviling.<BR> E. गुप् to censure,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=292-b" target="_blank">Page292-b+ 60</a>]<BR>affix स्वार्थे सन् भावे ल्यट्, or with अङ् and टाप् affixes जुगुप्सा; the root<BR>is always inflected in this sense, in the desiderative form. कर्त्तरि<BR>युच् । निन्दाशीले त्रि० ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=292-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुगुप्सा
जुगुप्सा f. (-प्सा) Censure, &c. See the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=292-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुगुप्सित
जुगुप्सित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Reviled, blamed, censured, abused.<BR> E. गुप् to<BR>censure, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=292-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुङ्ग|जुङ्गः
जुङ्ग mf. (-ङ्गः-ङ्गा) A potherb, (Convolvulus argenteus.)<BR> E. जुगि to quit,<BR>affix अच्, removing all blemishes; also with कन् added जुङ्गक<BR>m. (-कः.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=292-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुङ्गित|जुंगित|जुङ्गितः
जुङ्गित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Outcaste, deserted, injured, abandoned.<BR>	 m. (-तः)<BR>A man of a degraded caste, a Chandala, &c.<BR> E. जुगि to abandon,<BR>affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=292-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुटक|जुटकं
जुटक nf. (टकं-टिका)<BR>	 1. The matted hair of ŚIVA or of ascetics.<BR>	 2. Any<BR>knot or fillet of hair.<BR> E. जट् to collect, affix अच्, and सज्ञायां कन्<BR>पृषो० or ऊ inserted; see जटा; also जूट, जूटक’ &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=292-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुड
जुड r. 6th cl. (जुडति)<BR>	 1. To go, to move.<BR>	 2. To bind.<BR>	 3. To join, as in<BR>making or mending. r. 10th cl. (जोडयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To send, to cast or<BR>throw, to direct.<BR>	 2. To grind or pound.<BR> E. तु० कुटा० प० सेट् सक । चुरा०<BR>उभ० ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=292-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुत
जुत (ऋ) जुतृ r. 1st cl. (जोतते) To shine, &c.<BR> E. भ्वा० आत्म० अक० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=292-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुन
जुन r. 6th cl. (जुनति) To go, or move.<BR> E. तु० प० सक० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=292-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुर्
जुर् f. (-जूः)<BR>	 1. Speed, velocity.<BR>	 2. Motion in general.<BR> E. ज्वर् to make<BR>haste, affix क्विप्, and उठ् substituted for ब.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=292-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुल
जुल r. 10th cl. (जोलयति-ते) To reduce to powder.<BR> E. चु० उभ० सक०<BR>सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=292-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुर्व|जुर्व्व
जुर्व (ई) जुर्वी r. 1st cl. (जुर्वति) To hurt or kill.<BR> E. भ्वा० प० सक० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=292-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुष
जुष r. 1st and 10th cls. (जोषति जोषयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To reason, to think, to<BR>conceive or imagine, to investigate or examine.<BR>	 2. To injure, to<BR>hurt or kill.<BR>	 3. To like. (ञि ई) ञि जुषो r. 6th cl. (जुषते) To please.<BR>to gratify, to give satisfaction or delight, to serve.<BR> E. भ्वा० प० सक-<BR>सेट् । चुरा० उभ० अक तृप्तौ, सक तर्के । तुदा० आ० सेट् हर्षे अक०, सेवायां<BR>सक०<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=292-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुष्कक|जुष्ककः
जुष्कक m. (-कः) The water of boiled pulse, pease soup, porridge, &c.<BR>E. जुष् to please or satisfy, कक् affix, and deriv. irr. see जूष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=292-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुष्ट|जुष्टं
जुष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं) Served, obliged, worshipped, gratified by service.<BR>n. (-ष्टं) The crumbs or remnants of a meal or its leavings.<BR> E. जुष्<BR>to please, &c. affix कर्मणि क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=292-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुष्य|जुष्यः
जुष्य mfn. (-ष्यः-ष्या-ष्यं) To be served or worshipped.<BR> E. जुष् to please,<BR>aff. कर्मणि भावे वा क्यप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=292-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुहुवत्
जुहुवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत) Sacrificing, offering oblations.<BR>	 m. (-वान्) Fire.<BR>E. हु to sacrifice, क्तवतु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=292-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुहुवान|जुहुवानः
जुहुवान m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. Fire.<BR>	 2. A tree.<BR>	 3. A hard-hearted man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=292-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुहू
जुहू f. (-हूः) A wooden vessel, of the shape of a semicircle or crescent.<BR>used to pour sacrificial butter in to the fire.<BR> E. हु to sacrifice, Uṇādi<BR>affix क्विप्, the root reiterated, and the final made long also remain-<BR>ing short जुहु.<BR>	 f. (-हुः) |<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=292-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुहूवत्|जुहूवन्त्
जुहूवत् m. (-वान्) Fire, or the deity AGNI.<BR> E. जुह a sacrificial vessel,<BR>and मतुप् possessing; being the medium of (burnt) offerings; also<BR>जुहुवत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=292-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुहूराण|जुहूराणः
जुहूराण m. (-णः)<BR>	 1. The moon.<BR>	 2. Fire or its deity.<BR>	 3. An officiating<BR>priest<BR> E. हूर्च्छ to be crooked, to abandon, &c. Uṇādi affix आनच्;<BR>the root is reiterated, and the final छ rejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=292-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुह्वत्
जुह्वत् mfn. (-ह्वन्-ह्वती-ह्वत्) Sacrifice, offering oblations.<BR> E. हु to sacri-<BR>fice, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=292-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जू
जू f. (-जूः)<BR>	 1. Æther, heaven.<BR>	 2. A name of the goddess SARASWATI.<BR>3. A female demon or goblin.<BR>	 4. Speed, expedition, velocity.<BR>	 5.<BR>Going, motion.<BR>	 6. The atmosphere<BR> E. जू to go swiftly, affix क्विप्,<BR>and the final lengthened.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=292-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जूट|जूटः
जूट m. (टः)<BR>	 1. The matted hair of ŚIVA.<BR>	 2. The clotted hair of an as-<BR>cetic.<BR> E. जट् to collect, affix अच्, ऊ inserted; see जटा;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=293-a" target="_blank">Page293-a+ 60</a>]<BR>also with कन् added जूटक.<BR>	 n. (-कं) and with a short vowel जुटक q.<BR>v.; it is also used compounded with जटा in the same sense, as<BR>जटाजूट.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=292-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जूति|जूतिः
जूति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Speed, velocity.<BR>	 2. Going, proceeding, moving.<BR> E. जु to<BR>go swiftly, affix भावे क्तिन्, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=293-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जूर
जूर (ई) जूरी r. 4th cl. (जूर्य्यते)<BR>	 1. To hurt, to injure, to wound or kill.<BR>2. To be angry with (with a dat.)<BR>	 3. To be decayed, to decay or<BR>grow old.<BR> E. वयोहानौ अक० बधे सक-दिवा-आ-सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=293-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जूर्णाह्वय|जूर्णाह्वयः
जूर्णाह्वय m. (-यः) A kind of grain, (Andropogon sorghum:) see देवधान्य,<BR>जूर्णम् आह्वयते काण्डेन स्पर्द्धते आ + ह्वे वा श ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=293-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जूर्णि|जूर्णिः
जूर्णि f. (-र्णिः)<BR>	 1. Speed.<BR>	 2. The body.<BR>	 3. The sun.<BR>	 4. BRAMHA.<BR>	 5. Fever.<BR>E. ज्वर् to be feverish, Uṇādi affix नि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=293-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जूर्त्ति|जूर्ति|जूर्तिः|जूर्त्तिः
जूर्त्ति f. (-र्त्तिः) Fever, feverish or morbid heat.<BR> E. ज्वर् to be feverish, ऊठ् भावे क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=293-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जूर्व्व
जूर्व्व (-ई) जूर्व्वी (जूर्व्वति) To hurt or kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=293-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जूष|जूषं|जूषः
जूष r. 1st cl. (जुषति-ते) To kill or hurt.<BR> E. भ्वा-उभ सक-सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=293-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जूष|जूषं|जूषः
जूष n. (-षं) The water of boiled pulse, pease soup, porridge, &c.<BR> E. जूष्<BR>to satisfy, affix क and the radical vowel made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=293-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जूषण|जूषणं
जूषण n. (-णं) A plant, (Grislea tomentosa.)<BR> E. जूष् to hurt, affix ल्यु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=293-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जृ
जृ r. 1st cl. (जरति) To make short or low.<BR> E. भ्वा-प-सक-अनिट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=293-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जृभ
जृभ (ई) जृभी r. 1st cl. (जृभते) or more commonly r. 1st cl. (इ) जृभि (जृम्भते)<BR>To gape, to yawn. r. 10th cl. (जृम्भयति-ते) To fear, to dread. E.<BR>भ्वा-आ-अक-सेट् । जृम्भे गात्रशैथिल्ये च भ्वा-आ-अक-सेट् इदित् । चु-उभ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=293-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जृम्भ|जृंभ|जृंभं|जृंभः|जृम्भः
जृम्भ mfn. sub. (-म्भः-म्भा-म्भं)<BR>	 1. Gaping, yawning.<BR>	 2. Expansion, stretch-<BR>ing, expanding.<BR>	 3. Swelling, a puffing or blowing up.<BR>	 4. Blowing,<BR>blossoming.<BR> E. जृभि to gape, affix भावे घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=293-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जृम्भक|जृंभकः|जृम्भकः
जृम्भक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A subordinate deity.<BR>	 2. A yawner.<BR> E. जृभि, and ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=293-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जृम्भण|जृंभण|जृम्भणं
जृम्भण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Gaping, yawning.<BR>	 2. Blowing.<BR> E. जृभि to yawn, affix<BR>भावे ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=293-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जृम्भमाण
जृम्भमाण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>	 1. Yawning, gaping.<BR>	 2. Opening, blowing.<BR> E. जृभि to open, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=293-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जृम्भावत्|जृम्भावन्त्
जृम्भावत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Yawning, gaping.<BR> E. जृम्भा, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=293-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जृम्भिका|जृंभिका
जृम्भिका f. (-का) Gaping, yawning.<BR> E. जृम्भि and क्वुन् affix, fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=293-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जृम्भित|जृंभित|जृम्भितं
जृम्भित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Opened, expanded.<BR>	 2. Enlarged.<BR>	 3. Done,<BR>exerted.<BR>	 4. Opened, (as a flower,) blown.<BR>	 n. (-तं)<BR>	 1. Gaping, yawn-<BR>ing.<BR>	 2. Swelling, expansion.<BR>	 3. Bursting, opening.<BR>	 4. Wish, active<BR>wish or search for.<BR> E. जृभि to gape, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=293-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जृम्भिन्
जृम्भिन् mfn. (-म्भी-म्भिनी-म्भि)<BR>	 1. Who or what yawns or gapes.<BR>	 2. Expand-<BR>ing, blossoming.<BR>	 f. (-नी) A kind of Mimosa, (M. octandra.)<BR> E. जृम्भ<BR>bursting, budding and णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=293-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जॄ
जॄ r. 1st cl. (जरति) 4th cl. (जीर्य्यति) 9th cl. (जृणाति) and 10th cl. (जरयति-<BR>ते)<BR>	 1. To grow old, to be or become old or decayed.<BR>	 2. To be con-<BR>sumed, to perish.<BR>	 3. To be digested.<BR> E. भ्वा-अक-सेट् । दिवा-प-अक-सेट्<BR>इदित् । क्य्रादि-प्वादि-अक-सेट् । पक्षे चुरा-उभ० ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=293-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जेतव्य
जेतव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं) To be conquered or overcome, to be surpassed<BR>or excelled.<BR> E. जि to conquer, तव्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=293-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जेतृ
जेतृ mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ)<BR>	 1. Victorious, triumphant.<BR>	 2. Surpassing, excelling.<BR>3. An epithet of vishnu.<BR>	 m. (-ता) A victor, a conqueror.<BR> E. जि to<BR>conquer, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=293-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जेन्ताक|जेंताक|जेंताकः|जेन्ताकः
जेन्ताक m. (-कः) A dry hot bath, or heated chamber for inducing per-<BR>spiration in rheumatism, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=293-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जेमन|जेमनं
जेमन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Food, victuals Dinner.<BR>	 2. Eating.<BR> E. जिम् to eat, affix भावे ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=293-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जेय|जेयः
जेय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Conquerable, fit or subject to be conquered.<BR> E. जि<BR>to conquer, affix कर्मणि यत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=293-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जेष
जेष (ऋ) जेषृ r. 1st cl. (जेषते) To go or move.<BR> E. भ्वा-आ-सक-सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=293-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जेह
जेह (ऋ) जेहृ r. 1st cl. (जेहते)<BR>	 1. To resolve, to attempt resolutely, to<BR>endeavour diligently or perseveringly.<BR>	 2. To go, to move.<BR> E. भ्वा-आ-<BR>अक-सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=293-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जै
जै r. 1st cl. (जयति) To wane or decline.<BR> E. भ्वा-प-अक-अनिट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=293-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जैत्र|जैत्रं|जैत्रः
जैत्र mfn. (-त्रः-त्री-त्रं)<BR>	 1. Victorious, triumphant.<BR>	 2. Leading to victory.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-त्रः)<BR>	 1. A conqueror, a victor.<BR>	 2. Quicksilver.<BR>	 f. (-त्री) A tree, (Æs-<BR>chynomene sesban.)<BR> E. जेतृ to conquer or excel, प्रज्ञा० अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=293-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जैत्ररथ|जैत्ररथः
जैत्ररथ m. (-थः) A hero, a victor, a conqueror.<BR> E. जैत्र victorious, and रथ<BR>a car; whose chariot is triumphant जैत्रः रथः अस्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=293-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जैन|जैनः
जैन m. (-नः) A Jaina, a follower of the principles of a Jina or teacher<BR>of heterodox notions, the chief of which are, the supremacy of<BR>certain religious pontiffs over the gods of the Hindus, a denial of<BR>the divine authority of the Vedas, and a disregard of the distinc-<BR>tion of castes.<BR> E. जिन a Jina, and अण् aff. जिनः देवता अस्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=293-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जैपाल|जैपालः
जैपाल m. (-लः) A plant, (Croton tiglium): see जयपाल, the diphthong<BR>being considered as a substitute for the semivowel and vowels of<BR>the first members of the compound; it is most probably a corrup-<BR>tion borrowed from the dialects in which such a substitution is<BR>common.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=293-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जैमिनि|जैमिनिः
जैमिनि m. (-निः) The name of a celebrated saint and philosopher, the<BR>pupil of VYASA, and founder of the Purva Mīmāṃsā school, which<BR>is commented by Savaraswami.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=293-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जैवातृक|जैवातृकः
जैवातृक mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>	 1. Long-lived.<BR>	 2. Thin, spare.<BR>	 m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. The<BR>moon.<BR>	 2. A drug, a medicament.<BR>	 3. Camphor.<BR>	 4. A son.<BR>	 f. (की)<BR>	 1.<BR>Longlived.<BR>	 2. Thin, lean.<BR> E. जीव life, आतृ कन् Uṇādi affix, and<BR>the radical vowel changed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=293-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जैष्णव
जैष्णव mfn. (-वः-वी-वं) Relating to a conqueror, to ARJUNA, &c.<BR> E. जिष्ण<BR>as above, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=293-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जैह्म्य|जैह्म्यं
जैह्म्य n. (-ह्म्यं) Crookedness, moral or physical.<BR> E. जिह्म crooked, ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=293-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जोङ्गक|जोंगकं|जोङ्गकं
जोङ्गक n. (-कं) Alœ wood or Agallochum.<BR> E. जुगि to remove, ण्वुल् affix;<BR>dissipating bad smells.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=293-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जोङ्गट|जोंगट|जोंगटः|जोङ्गटः
जोङ्गट m. (-टः)<BR>	 1. Longing for, wishing earnestly or eagerly.<BR>	 2. The<BR>longings of a pregnant woman.<BR> E. जुगि to abandon, (all objects save<BR>that desired,) and अटन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=293-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जोटिङ्ग|जोटिंग|जोटिंगः|जोटिङ्गः
जोटिङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>	 1. A name of ŚIVA.<BR>	 2. A devotee, an ascetic, who sub-<BR>jects himself to the severest penances.<BR> E. जुट the braided hair of<BR>ŚIVA, ग who goes, from गम् to go, the form is irregular.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=293-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जोन्ताला
जोन्ताला f. (-ला) A kind of grain: see देवधान्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=293-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जोष|जोषं|जोषः
जोष n. (-षं) Happiness, felicity, pleasure, enjoyment, satisfaction.<BR>	 f.<BR>(-षा) A woman: see जोषा; also जोषित्, जोषिता, &c.<BR> E. जुष् to delight,<BR>affix भावे घञ् fem. affix टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=293-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जोषम्
जोषम् ind.<BR>	 1. Silently.<BR>	 2. In happiness, delightedly at ease, &c.<BR>	 3. Well,<BR>excellently.<BR>	 4. Excessively, beyond bounds.<BR> E. जुष् to please or be<BR>pleased, affix अमु, संज्ञायां कन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=293-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जोषिका
जोषिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. A bud, a germ.<BR>	 2. A woman.<BR> E. जुष् to please, affix कन्.<BR>and fem form; some copies have more accurately perhaps कोषिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=293-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जोषित्
जोषित् f. (-षित्) A woman.<BR> E. जुष् to delight, affix इति; also योषित,<BR>जोषिता, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=293-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जोषिता
जोषिता f. (-ता) A woman,<BR> E. जुष् to please, affix क्त; also योषित, योषिता, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=293-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञ|ज्ञः
ज्ञ A compound letter, considered to be composed of ज and ञ; it is<BR>usually expressed by jn or gn, but its peculiar nasal sound is not<BR>well conveyed by any combination of the Roman alphabet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=293-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञ|ज्ञः
ज्ञ mfn. (ज्ञः ज्ञा ज्ञं) Who or what knows.<BR>	 m. (ज्ञः)<BR>	 1. A wise and learned<BR>man; it especially applies to one possessed of sacred learning, and<BR>religious knowledge.<BR>	 2. A name of BRAMHA.<BR>	 3. The moon.<BR>	 4. Bu-<BR>dha, first of the line of the moon, and regent of the planet MER-<BR>CURY.<BR>	 5. The planet MARS or its regent.<BR>	 6. The Sentient soul. E.<BR>ज्ञा to know, to possess knowledge, affix क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=293-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञप
ज्ञप r. 10th cl. (ज्ञपयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To know.<BR>	 2. To cause to be known: see ज्ञा.<BR>3. To whet or sharpen.<BR>	 4. To beat.<BR>	 5. To please.<BR> E. चुरा० उभ० सक०<BR>सेट् घटादि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=293-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञपित|ज्ञपितः
ज्ञपित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Taught, expounded, made known.<BR> E. ज्ञप् to make<BR>known, affix क्त, नि-वा-इट् optionally inserted, otherwise ज्ञप्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=293-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञप्त|ज्ञप्तः
ज्ञप्त mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं) Made known: see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=293-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञप्ति|ज्ञप्तिः
ज्ञप्ति f. (-प्तिः) Understanding, comprehension, the exercise of the intel-<BR>lectual faculty.<BR> E. ज्ञप् to make known, affix भावे क्तिन्, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=293-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञा
ज्ञा r. 9th cl. (जानाति जानीते) To know, to understand. With अनु, prefix-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=294-a" target="_blank">Page294-a+ 60</a>]<BR>ed, 1. To assent or conform to.<BR>	 2. To acknowledge. With अप, To<BR>conceal. With अव, To disrespect, to despise. With उप, To deny<BR>knowledge of any thing. With परि, To ascertain. With प्र, To<BR>know well. With प्रति or सम्, To assent, to admit, to agree, to pro-<BR>mise. With प्रति and अभि, To recognise. With वि, To discriminate,<BR>to know. With सम्, To recollect or possess the power of knowing.<BR>(In combination, it usually takes the deponent form, as अनुजानीते,<BR>अपजानीते, &c.) r. 10th cl. (ज्ञापयतिते) To command, to direct; आङ् is<BR>usually prefixed in this sense. r. 1st cl. but occurring in the form of<BR>the causal, (ज्ञपयति)<BR>	 1. To slay.<BR>	 2. To gratify or please.<BR>	 3. To exhibit<BR>4. To sharpen.<BR>	 5. To praise. In these senses the root is, in general.<BR>combined with a prefix. क्र्या-प-सक-अनिट् । चु-उभ-सक-सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=293-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञात|ज्ञातं
ज्ञात mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Known, comprehended, understood fully.<BR> E. ज्ञा to<BR>know, affix कर्मणि क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=294-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञातव्य|ज्ञातव्यं
ज्ञातव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं) To be known or understood.<BR> E. ज्ञा, and तव्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=294-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञातसिद्धान्त|ज्ञातसिद्धांत|ज्ञातसिद्धान्तः
ज्ञातसिद्धान्त m. (-न्तः) A man completely versed in any science or Shastra.<BR>E. ज्ञात what is known, and सिद्धान्त completion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=294-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञातान्वय|ज्ञातान्वयः
ज्ञातान्वय m. (-यः) A name of Varddhamana, the last Jina or Jaina pon-<BR>tiff.<BR> E. ज्ञात known, and अन्वय lineage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=294-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञाति|ज्ञातिः
ज्ञाति m. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. A father.<BR>	 2. A kinsman in general.<BR>	 3. A distant kins-<BR>man, one who does not participate in the oblations of food or water<BR>offered to deceased ancestors.<BR> E. ज्ञा to know, affix कर्त्तरि करणे वा<BR>क्तिच्; who is known, an acquaintance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=294-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञातिकर्मन्|ज्ञातिकर्म्मन्
ज्ञातिकर्मन् n. (-र्म) Duty of kindred.<BR> E. ज्ञाति, and कर्म act; also ज्ञातिकार्य्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=294-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञातित्व
ज्ञातित्व n. (-त्वं) Relationship, kin.<BR> E. त्व added to ज्ञाति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=294-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञातृ
ज्ञातृ mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ) Knowing, wise, intelligent, who or what knows.<BR>E. ज्ञा to know, तृच् active aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=294-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञातेय|ज्ञातेयं
ज्ञातेय n. (-यं) Relationship, affinity.<BR> E. ज्ञाति a kinsmen, and ढक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=294-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञात्वा
ज्ञात्वा ind. Having known.<BR> E. ज्ञा to know, क्त्वाच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=294-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञान|ज्ञानं
ज्ञान n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Knowledge in general.<BR>	 2. Knowledge of a specific and<BR>religious kind, that which is derived from meditation, and the<BR>study of philosophy, which teaches man the divine nature and<BR>origin of his immaterial part, with the unreality of corporeal en-<BR>joyments or worldly forms, and which, separating him during<BR>life from terrestrial objects, secures him, after death, a final eman-<BR>cipation from existence, and reunion with the universal spirit.<BR>	 3.<BR>Cognizance, consciousness.<BR>	 4. The organ of intelligence, sense.<BR>	 5.<BR>Learning.<BR> E. ज्ञा to know, aff. भावे ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=294-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञानगम्य
ज्ञानगम्य mfn. (-म्यः-म्या-म्यं) Attainable by knowledge.<BR> E. ज्ञान, and गम्य<BR>attainable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=294-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञानचक्षुस्
ज्ञानचक्षुस् mn. (-क्षुः)<BR>	 1. (Intellect, intellectual vision.) A learned & wise-<BR>man.<BR> E. ज्ञान, and चक्षुस् the eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=294-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञानतपस्
ज्ञानतपस् n. (-पः) Cultivation of sacred knowledge.<BR> E. ज्ञान, and तपस्<BR>religious austerity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=294-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञानतस
ज्ञानतस ind.<BR>	 1. By or 2. Knowingly, intentionally, through knowledge.<BR>E. ज्ञान, and तसिल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=294-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञानदर्पण|ज्ञानदर्पणः
ज्ञानदर्पण m. (-णः) One of the Jaina saints.<BR> E. ज्ञान true knowledge, and<BR>दर्पण a mirror.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=294-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञानदीप
ज्ञानदीप m. (-पः) Knowledge, the lamp of knowledge.<BR> E. ज्ञान, and दीप a lamp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=294-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञाननिष्ठ
ज्ञाननिष्ठ mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठा-ष्ठं) Cultivating spiritual knowledge.<BR> E. ज्ञान, and<BR>निष्ठ engaged in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=294-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञानपर
ज्ञानपर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Versed in spiritual wisdom.<BR> E. ज्ञान, and पर attentive to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=294-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञानपूर्व|ज्ञानपूर्व्व
ज्ञानपूर्व mfn. (-र्वः-र्वा-र्वं) Preceded by the acquirement of divine wis-<BR>dom.<BR> E. ज्ञान, and पूर्व prior.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=294-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञानमय|ज्ञानमयः
ज्ञानमय mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>	 1. Consisting of knowledge, made up of it.<BR>	 2.<BR>Spiritual.<BR> E. ज्ञान, and मयट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=294-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञानमुद्र
ज्ञानमुद्र mfn. (-द्रः-द्रा-द्रं) Having the impress of wisdom, wise, making<BR>wise.<BR> E. ज्ञान, and मुद्रा a seal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=294-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञानमूल
ज्ञानमूल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Founded on spiritual knowledge.<BR> E. ज्ञान, and<BR>मूल root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=294-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञानलक्षण
ज्ञानलक्षण nf. (-णं-णा)<BR>	 1. Indication, sign, means of knowing or inferring.<BR>2. (In Logic.) Sign or proof of knowledge, or subsequent derived<BR>from antecedent knowledge.<BR> E. ज्ञान, and लक्षण indication.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=294-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञानवत्|ज्ञानवन्त्
ज्ञानवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Wise, especially in spiritual things.<BR> E. ज्ञान,<BR>and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=294-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञानविज्ञान
ज्ञानविज्ञान n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Sacred and profane knowledge.<BR>	 2. The Vedas and<BR>their subordinate parts, as medicine, war, &c.<BR> E. ज्ञान, and विज्ञान<BR>miscellaneous knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=294-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञानानुत्पाद|ज्ञानानुत्पादः
ज्ञानानुत्पाद m. (-दः) Folly, ignorance.<BR> E. ज्ञान, and अनुत्पाद nonproduction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=294-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञानावस्थित
ज्ञानावस्थित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Occupied by wisdom.<BR> E. ज्ञान, and अवस्थित<BR>placed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=294-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञानिन्
ज्ञानिन् mfn. (-नी-निनी-नि)<BR>	 1. Wise, intelligent.<BR>	 2. Knowing, who or<BR>what knows.<BR>	 m. (-नी)<BR>	 1. An astrologer, a fortuneteller, a man<BR>prescient of future events.<BR>	 2. A sage, one possessing religious<BR>wisdom or Jnan (ज्ञान) as above.<BR> E. ज्ञान knowledge, affix इनि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=294-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञानेन्द्रिय|ज्ञानेंद्रिय|ज्ञानेन्द्रियं
ज्ञानेन्द्रिय n. (-यं) An organ of preception or consciousness, the skin,<BR>tongue, eye, ear and nose (intellect.)<BR> E. ज्ञान, and इन्द्रिय an organ.<BR>ज्ञायते अनेन ज्ञा-करणे ल्युट् । ज्ञानसाधनम् इन्द्रियम् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=294-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञापक|ज्ञापकः
ज्ञापक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Making or causing to know.<BR>	 m. (-कः) An in-<BR>structor.<BR>	 2. A commander, a master.<BR>	 n. (-कं) A rub or precept imply-<BR>ing something not expressly mentioned or laid down (In Philspay)<BR>E. ज्ञा to know, causal form, णिच् ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=294-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञापन|ज्ञापनं
ज्ञापन n. (-नं) Making known, apprising, informing.<BR> E. ज्ञा to know,<BR>causal form, णिच् ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=294-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञाप्ति|ज्ञाप्तिः
ज्ञाप्ति f. (-प्तिः) Making known, informing.<BR> E. ज्ञा to know, causal form, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=294-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञीप्सा
ज्ञीप्सा f. (-प्सा) The desire of knowing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=294-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञेय|ज्ञेयं
ज्ञेय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) To be known, what may be or ought to be known.<BR>E. ज्ञा, and कर्मणि यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=294-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्यका
ज्यका f. (-का) The chord of an are.<BR> E. ज्या the same, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=294-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्या
ज्या r. 9th cl. (जिनाति) To decay, to be or become old. क्य्रा० प्वा० पर० अक० अनिट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=294-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्या
ज्या f. (ज्या)<BR>	 1. A mother.<BR>	 2. The earth, 3. A bowstring.<BR>	 4. The chord<BR>of an are.<BR> E. ज्या to become old, to decay, affixes अघ्न्या० यक् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=294-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्याघोष
ज्याघोष m. (-षः) Twang of a bow.<BR> E. ज्या, and घोष sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=294-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्यानि|ज्यानिः
ज्यानि f. (-निः)<BR>	 1. Old age, decay, infirmity.<BR>	 2. Abandoning, quitting,<BR>leaving.<BR>	 3. A river, a stream.<BR> E. ज्या to decay, &c. Uṇādi aff. नि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=294-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्यायस्
ज्यायस् mfn. (-यान्-यसी-यः)<BR>	 1. Very old.<BR>	 2. Very excellent, best.<BR>	 3. Su-<BR>perior, Elder, elder born.<BR>	 4. In law, one independent (come of age)<BR>and answerable for his own conduct.<BR> E. ज्या to be old, ईयसुन् affix.<BR>अतिशयेन प्रशस्यः वृद्धः वा ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=294-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्यु
ज्यु r. 1st cl. (ज्यवते) To go or approach.<BR> E. भ्वा-आ-सक-अनिट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=294-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्युत
ज्युत r. 1st cl. (ऋ) ज्युतृ (ज्योतते;) also (इर) ज्युतिर r. 1st cl. (ज्योतति) To<BR>shine. see द्युत । भ्वा० आ० अक० सेट् । भ्वा-पर-सक-सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=294-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्येष्ठ|ज्येष्ठः
ज्येष्ठ mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठा-ष्ठी-ष्ठं)<BR>	 1. Best, most excellent, pre-eminent.<BR>	 2. Very old,<BR>oldest.<BR>	 3. most senior Elder, elder born.<BR>	 f. (-ष्ठा)<BR>	 1. One of the aste-<BR>risms, considered as lunar mansions; the eighteenth, comprising<BR>three stars, of which one is a Scorpionis, figured by a ring or ear-<BR>ring.<BR>	 2. The middle finger.<BR>	 3. Misfortune, personified as a goddess.<BR>4. The Ganges, (-ष्ठा or ष्ठी) A small house lizard.<BR>	 m. (-ष्ठः) The<BR>month Jyeshtha or Jeyte, (May-June.)<BR>	 n. (-ष्ठं) Age, oldness.<BR> E. ज्या to<BR>decay, to grow infirm or old, affix इष्ठन्, fem. affixes टाप् and ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=294-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्येष्ठता
ज्येष्ठता f. (-ता) Seniority.<BR>	 2. Superiority.<BR> E. ज्येष्ठ, and तल् affix; also<BR>ज्येष्ठत्व.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=294-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्येष्ठतात|ज्येष्ठतातः
ज्येष्ठतात m. (-तः) A father's elder brother.<BR> E. ज्येष्ठ elder born, and तात<BR>a father; the usual order of composition is here irregularly<BR>inverted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=294-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्येष्ठभार्य्या|ज्येष्ठभार्या
ज्येष्ठभार्य्या f. (-र्य्या)<BR>	 1. An elder brother's wife.<BR>	 2. The elder or chief wife.<BR>E. ज्येष्ठ, and भार्य्या wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=294-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्येष्ठवर्ण|ज्येष्ठवर्णः
ज्येष्ठवर्ण m. (-र्णः) A Brahman.<BR> E. ज्येष्ठ elder born or best, वर्ण tribe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=294-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्येष्ठवृत्ति|ज्येष्ठवृत्तिः
ज्येष्ठवृत्ति f. (-त्तिः) The duties of age or seniority.<BR> E. ज्येष्ठ, and वृत्ति<BR>practice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=294-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्येष्ठावाप्य
ज्येष्ठावाप्य mfn. (-प्यः-प्या-प्यं) To be obtained by virtue or seniority, &c.<BR>E. ज्येष्ठ, and आवाप्य obtainable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=295-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्येष्ठश्वश्रू
ज्येष्ठश्वश्रू f. (-श्रू) A wife's elder sister.<BR> E. ज्येष्ठ elder, श्वश्रू mother-in-law.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=295-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्येष्ठसामन्
ज्येष्ठसामन् n. (-म)<BR>	 1. A portion of the Sama Veda.<BR>	 2. A religious rite<BR>of which its perusal is a part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=295-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्येष्ठांश|ज्येष्ठांशः
ज्येष्ठांश m. (-शः)<BR>	 1. The elder brother's share.<BR>	 2. The best share.<BR> E. ज्येष्ठ, and अंश a share.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=295-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्येष्ठामूलीय|ज्येष्ठामूलीयः
ज्येष्ठामूलीय m. (-यः) The month of Jyeshtha.<BR> E. ज्य्येष्ठा the constellation,<BR>(as above,) मूल root, origin, and छ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=295-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्येष्ठाम्बु|ज्येष्ठांबु
ज्येष्ठाम्बु m. (-म्बुः) The scum of boiled rice, or water in which grain has<BR>been washed.<BR> E. ज्येष्ठ, and अम्बु water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=295-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्यष्ठाश्रम
ज्यष्ठाश्रम m. (-मः)<BR>	 1. The order of the householder.<BR>	 2. A householder.<BR>E. ज्येष्ठ, and आश्रम order.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=295-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्येष्ठाश्रमिन्
ज्येष्ठाश्रमिन् m. (-मी) A householder, a man of the second order. E.<BR>ज्येष्ठ best, आश्रम order, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=295-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्यैष्ठ|ज्यैष्ठः
ज्यैष्ठ m. (-ष्ठः) The month Jyeshtha or Jeyte, (May-June.)<BR>	 f. (-ष्ठी)<BR>1. The day of full moon in Jeyshta.<BR>	 2. A house lizard. E.<BR>ज्यैष्ठा the mansion or asterism which the moon is in this month,<BR>and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=295-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्यैष्ठसामन्
ज्यैष्ठसामन् m. (-मा) A Brahman versed in that portion of the Sama<BR>Veda called Jyeshtha Sama. ज्येष्ठसामन् as above. aff. अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=295-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्यैष्ठिनेय
ज्यैष्ठिनेय mfn. (-यः-यी-यं) Born of the elder or principal wife.<BR> E. ज्यैष्ठा,<BR>and ढक् affix, इनङ् inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=295-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्यैष्ठ्य|ज्यैष्ठ्यं
ज्यैष्ठ्य n. (-ष्ठं) Seniority, age.<BR> E. ज्यैष्ठ, and यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=295-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्यो
ज्यो r. 1st cl. (ज्यवते)<BR>	 1. To advise or instruct.<BR>	 2. To order.<BR>	 3. To ob-<BR>serve a vow or any religious obligation.<BR> E. भ्वा-आ-सक-अनिट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=295-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्योतिःशास्त्र
ज्योतिःशास्त्र n. (स्त्रं)<BR>	 1. The science of Astronomy or astrology. E.<BR>ज्योतिस् and शास्त्र a Scripture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=295-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्योतिरिङ्ग|ज्योतिरिंग|ज्योतिरिङ्गः
ज्योतिरिङ्ग n. (-ङ्गं) A fire-fly.<BR> E. ज्योतिस् light, इगि to go, affix क; also<BR>with युच् affix, ज्योतिरिङ्गण n. (-णं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=295-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्योतिर्गण|ज्योतिर्गणः
ज्योतिर्गण m. (-णः) The heavenly bodies collectively.<BR> E. ज्योतिस् a planet, and गण a class.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=295-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्योतिर्विद्
ज्योतिर्विद् m. (-त्) An astrologer, an arithmetician.<BR> E. ज्योतिस्, and विद्<BR>who knows. ज्योतिषां मूर्य्यादीनां गत्यादिकं वेत्ति विद्-क्विप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=295-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्योतिर्विद्या
ज्योतिर्विद्या f. (-द्या) The science of computation, from arithmetic to as-<BR>tronomy and astrology.<BR> E. ज्योतिस्, and विद्या science.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=295-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्योतिर्वीज|ज्योतिर्व्वीजं
ज्योतिर्वीज n. (-जं) A fire-fly.<BR> E. ज्योतिस् light, and वीज seed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=295-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्योतिश्चक्र|ज्योतिश्चक्रं
ज्योतिश्चक्र n. (-क्रं)<BR>	 1. The zodiac.<BR>	 2. The lunar mansion.<BR> E. ज्योतिस्, pla-<BR>net, and चक्र a sphere.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=295-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्योतिष|ज्योतिषं|ज्योतिषः
ज्योतिष mfn. (-षः-षी-षं) Astrological, astronomical, relating to the hea-<BR>venly bodies.<BR>	 mf. (-षः-षी) An astrologer.<BR>	 n. (-पं) Mathemetical, as-<BR>tronomical and astrological science, astronomy.<BR>	 f. (-षी) A star, a<BR>planet, a asterism.<BR> E. ज्योतिस् light, especially of the heavenly<BR>bodies, affix अच्, fem. ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=295-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्योतिषिक|ज्योतिषिकः
ज्योतिषिक m. (-कः) An astrologer: see ज्योतिषिक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=295-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्योतिष्क|ज्योतिष्कः
ज्योतिष्क m. (-ष्कः)<BR>	 1. A planetary or heavenly body; the generic term<BR>for the sun, the moon, a planet, an asterism, a star: the word<BR>in the m. plu. (-ष्काः) implies all these five.<BR>	 2. A tree, the wood<BR>of which is used to produce fire by attribution: see गणिकारिका<BR>f. (-का) Heart-pea: see ज्योतिष्मती.<BR> E. ज्योतिस् light, and क what<BR>makes, from कृ, with ड aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=295-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्योतिष्कल्प
ज्योतिष्कल्प mfn. (-ल्पः-ल्पा-ल्पं) Blazing, radient, like flame or fire. E.<BR>ज्योतिस्, and कल्प affix, implying resemblance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=295-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्योतिष्टोम|ज्योतिष्टोमः
ज्योतिष्टोम n. (-मं) A particular sacrifice at which sixteen officiating<BR>priests are required. It is a sacrifice considered as the typical<BR>form of a whole class of sacrificial ceremonies.<BR> E. ज्योतिस् light,<BR>and स्तोम a sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=295-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्योतिष्मत्|ज्योतिष्मन्त्
ज्योतिष्मत् m. (-ष्मान्) The sun.<BR>	 f. (-ष्मती) Heart-pea, (Halicacabum cardios-<BR>permum)<BR> E. ज्योतिस् light or splendor, and मतुप् poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=295-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्योतिस्
ज्योतिस् n. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Light.<BR>	 2. A star.<BR>	 3. The pupil of the eye. The<BR>faculty of seeing.<BR>	 4. The light regarded as the supreme spirit.<BR>	 5.<BR>The lightening.<BR>	 6. A heavenly body.<BR>	 m. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. The sun.<BR>	 2. AGINI<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=295-b" target="_blank">Page295-b+ 60</a>]<BR>or fire.<BR> E. द्यत् to shine, to be or give light इसुन् Uṇādi affix, and<BR>ज substituted for the radical initial.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=295-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्योतिस्मात्
ज्योतिस्मात् ind. In flame or fire.<BR> E. ज्योतिस्, and साति aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=295-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्योतीरथ|ज्योतीरथः
ज्योतीरथ m. (-थः) The pole star, or in mythology DHRUVA, the son of<BR>UTTANAPADA.<BR> E. ज्योतिस् a star, and रथ a vehicle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=295-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्योत्स्ना
ज्योत्स्ना f. (-त्स्ना)<BR>	 1. Moonlight.<BR>	 2. Amoonlight night.<BR>	 3. A small cucum-<BR>ber: see ज्योत्स्नी.<BR> E. ज्योतिस् light, त affix, and the penultimate re-<BR>jected, deriv. irr. fem. affix टाप्; also with ङिष्, ज्योत्स्नी q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=295-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्योत्स्नाप्रिय|ज्योत्स्नाप्रियः
ज्योत्स्नाप्रिय m. (-यः) The Chakora or Greek partridge.<BR> E. ज्योत्स्ना moon-<BR>light, and प्रिय fond of; this bird is said to feed upon the moon-<BR>beams.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=295-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्योत्स्नावृक्ष|ज्योत्स्नावृक्षः
ज्योत्स्नावृक्ष m. (-क्षः) The tripod or tree of a lampstand, a candle-stick.<BR>E. ज्योत्स्ना moonlight, (put for lamp-light,) and वृक्ष a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=295-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्योत्स्नी
ज्योत्स्नी f. (-त्स्नी)<BR>	 1. A moonlight night.<BR>	 2. A small cucumber, (Tricho-<BR>santhes diæca;) it is also applied to Luffa acutangula, &c.<BR>	 3. A<BR>kind of perfume: see रेणुका. E. See ज्योत्स्ना.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=295-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्यौ
ज्यौ m. The planet Jupiter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=295-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्यौतिषिक|ज्यौतिषिकः
ज्यौतिषिक m. (-कः) An astrologer or astronomer.<BR> E. ज्योतिस् a star, affix<BR>ठक्; also the the vowel being unchanged optionally, ज्योतिषिक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=295-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्यौत्स्न|ज्यौत्स्नः
ज्यौत्स्न mfn. (-त्स्नः-त्स्नी-त्स्नं) Light, especially with moonlight, &c. E.<BR>ज्योत्स्ना moonlight, अण् affix: see ज्योत्स्नी and ज्यौत्स्निका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=295-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्यौत्स्निका
ज्यौत्स्निका f. (-का) A moonlight.<BR> E. ज्योत्स्नी, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=295-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्यौत्स्नी
ज्यौत्स्नी f. (-त्स्नी) A moonlight night, or a night on which the moon is<BR>full.<BR>	 2. A kind of cucumber: see ज्यीत्स्नी.<BR> E. ज्यौत्स्नी as above, and<BR>अण् pleonastic aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=295-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्रि
ज्रि r. 1st cl. (ज्रयति)<BR>	 1. To conquer, to reduce.<BR>	 2. To be conquered or<BR>reduced.<BR> E. भ्वा-प-सक-अनिट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=295-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्री
ज्री r. 1st cl. (ज्रिणाति) r. 1st and 10th cls. (ज्रयति-ज्राययति-ते) To grow old,<BR>to be or become old or decayed.<BR> E. क्र्या-प्वा-प-अक-अनिट् । भ्वा-वाचुरा-उभ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=295-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्वर|ज्वरः
ज्वर r. 1st cl. (ज्वरति) To be diseased, to be feverish, &c. भ्वा-प-अक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=295-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्वर|ज्वरः
ज्वर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Fever, intermitting or continued.<BR>	 2. Mental Pain, affli-<BR>ction, Distress.<BR> E. ज्वर to be feverish, affix भावेघ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=295-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्वरघ्न|ज्वरघ्नः
ज्वरघ्न mfn. (-घ्नः-घ्नी-घ्नं) Anti-febrile, febrifuge.<BR>	 f. (-घ्नी)<BR>	 1. A plant, (Men-<BR>ispermum glabrum.)<BR>	 2. A potherb, (Chenopocium album)<BR> E. ज्वर,<BR>and घ्न what destroys. ज्वरं हन्ति हन-ठक् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=295-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्वरनाशक
ज्वरनाशक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Febrifuge.<BR> E. ज्वर, and नाशक what destroys.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=295-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्वरहन्तृ
ज्वरहन्तृ mfn. (-न्ता-न्त्री-न्तृ) Febrifuge.<BR> E. ज्वर, and हन् what destroys;<BR>ज्वरहन् m. (-हा)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=295-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्वराग्नि|ज्वराग्निः
ज्वराग्नि m. (-ग्निः) Feverish heat, or the hot paroxysm of fever.<BR> E. ज्वर fever, and अग्नि fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=295-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्वरान्तक|ज्वरान्तकः
ज्वरान्तक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Febrifuge.<BR>	 m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A kind of Nimb from<BR>Nepal.<BR>	 2. Casia fistula.<BR> E. ज्वर, and अन्तक what removes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=295-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्वरापहा
ज्वरापहा f. (-हा) A plant, (Medicago esculenta.)<BR> E. ज्वर fever, अपहा removing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=295-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्वरित|ज्वरितः
ज्वरित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Febrile, feverish, affected with fever.<BR> E. ज्वर् to<BR>be feverish, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=295-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्वरिन्
ज्वरिन् mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि) Febrile, feverish, fevered.<BR> E. ज्वर, and इनि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=295-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्वल|ज्वलः
ज्वल r. 1st cl. (ज्वलति,) or with a prefix, r. 10th cl. (प्रज्वलयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To shine<BR>to blaze, to flame.<BR>	 2. To be ardent.<BR>	 3. To kindle<BR> E. भ्वा-प-अक-सेट्<BR>चु० उ० ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=295-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्वल|ज्वलः
ज्वल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Blazing, shining.<BR>	 m. (-लः) Flame, blaze, light.<BR> E. ज्वल् to blaze, affix अच्; also ज्वाल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=295-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्वलका
ज्वलका f. (-का) A large Flame.<BR> E. ज्वल् to blaze, affix वुन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=295-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्वलत्|ज्वलन्त्
ज्वलत् mfn. (-लन्-लन्ती-लत्)<BR>	 1. Burning, blazing.<BR>	 2. Shining, radient,<BR>brilliant.<BR> E. ज्वल् to burn, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=295-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्वलन|ज्वलनः
ज्वलन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Burning, blazing.<BR>	 2. The fire.<BR>	 m. (-नः) AGNI, or fire.<BR>3. The number “Three.”<BR> E. ज्वल् to blaze, affix ताच्छील्यादौ युच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=295-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्वलनाश्मन्
ज्वलनाश्मन् m. (-श्मा) The sun-stone.<BR> E. ज्वलन, and अश्मन् a stone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=295-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्वलन्मणि
ज्वलन्मणि mfn. (-णिः-णिः-णि) Blazing with jewels.<BR>	 m. (-णिः) A brilli-<BR>ant gem.<BR> E. ज्वलत्, and मणि a jewel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=295-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्वलयत्
ज्वलयत् mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्)<BR>	 1. Burning, blazing.<BR>	 2. Radient.<BR> E. ज्वल् to<BR>burn, r. 10th cl. शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=295-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्वलित|ज्वलितः
ज्वलित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Burnt.<BR>	 2. Blazing, flaming.<BR> E. ज्वल् to flame, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=295-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्वलितनयन
ज्वलितनयन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Fiery-eyed, looking angrily or fiercely. E.<BR>ज्वलित, and नयन the eye; also ज्वलितचक्षुस्, ज्वलितनेच, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=296-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्वलिन्
ज्वलिन् mfn. (-ली-लिनी-लि)<BR>	 1. Burning, flaming.<BR>	 2. Shining.<BR> E. ज्वल, and<BR>इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=296-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्वाल|ज्वालः
ज्वाल mfn. (-लः-ली-लं) Burning, blazing.<BR>	 mf. (लः-ला) Flame, blaze.<BR>	 f.<BR>(-ला) Burnt rice.<BR> E. ज्वल् to blaze, affix अण्, fem. affix टाप् or ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=296-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्वालाग्नि
ज्वालाग्नि m. (-ग्निः) Flame.<BR> E. ज्वाल, and अग्नि fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=296-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्वालजिह्व
ज्वालजिह्व m. (-ह्वः) AGNI, or fire.<BR> E. जाला, and जिह्वा a tongue; whose<BR>tongue is flame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=296-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्वालामुखी
ज्वालामुखी f. (-खी) A place where subterraneous fires break forth; an<BR>object of veneration to the Hindus: a celebrated Jwalamukhi<BR>exists in Punjab, to which pilgrimages are made; the soil abound-<BR>ing with carburetted hydrogen, which takes fire upon coming in<BR>contact with the external air; otherwise vents being made, a<BR>light is applied to the orifice, and flame being kindled, is fed by<BR>the stream of gas that escapes. The tongue of PARVATI is said to<BR>have fallen at this place.<BR> E. ज्वाला flame, and मुख chief, principal,<BR>fem. affix ङीष् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=296-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्वालिन्
ज्वालिन् mfn. (-ली-लिनी-लि)<BR>	 1. Flaming, blazing.<BR>	 2. An Epithet of Siva.<BR>E. ज्वल्, and णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=296-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झ|झः
झ The ninth consonant of the Deva Nagara alphabet; the aspirate<BR>of the preceding letter, and corresponding in power to Jh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=296-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झ|झः
झ mfn. (झः झा झं)<BR>	 1. Asleep, sleeping.<BR>	 2. Lost, destroyed.<BR>	 m. (झः)<BR>1. A name of VṚHASPATI, preceptor of the gods.<BR>	 2. A<BR>name of the chief of the Daityas or demons.<BR>	 3. Sound or a sort<BR>of sound like the splashing of water, or the clashing of cymbals,<BR>jangling, clanging, &c.<BR>	 4. High wind.<BR>	 5. A stray, a thing lost or<BR>mislaid.<BR>	 6. Playing a tune, beating time.<BR>	 f. (झा) The descent of<BR>a cascade, a water fall.<BR> E. झट to collect, affix ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=296-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झङ्कार|झंकार|झंकारः|झङ्कारः
झङ्कार m. (-रः) A low inarticulate sound, as the buzzing of bees, &c.<BR>E. झ, and कार a making. कृ-घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=296-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झञ्झन|झंझन|झंझनं
झञ्झन n. (-नं) An indistinct noise, like the jangling of metallic orna-<BR>ments, a ringing, a rattling, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=296-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झञ्झा|झंझा
झञ्झा f. (-ञ्झा)<BR>	 1. Wind, wind and rain, a hurricane, a gale.<BR>	 2. A sharp<BR>clanging sound, jangling.<BR>	 3. Raining in large drops.<BR>	 4. A stray,<BR>any thing lost. झमिति कृत्वा झटति झट-ड ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=296-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झञ्झानिल|झंझानिल|झञ्झानिलः
झञ्झानिल m. (-लः) Wind with rain, a high wind in the rainy season,<BR>a typhoon or the sort of tempest frequent during the south-west<BR>monsoon.<BR> E. झञ्झा heavy rain, and अनिल wind; also झञ्झा-<BR>मरुत्, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=296-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झञ्झावात|झंझावात|झञ्झावातः
झञ्झावात m. (-तः) Wind with rain, a storm, a squall.<BR> E. झञ्झा heavy<BR>rain, and वात wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=296-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झट
झट r. 1st. cl. (झटति) To clot, to be entangled, (as hair:) see जट. E.<BR>भ्वा-पर-अक-सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=296-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झटा
झटा f. (-टा) A plant, (Flacourtia cataphracta.)<BR> E. झट् to entangled,<BR>affix अत्र्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=296-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झटि|झटिः
झटि m. (-टिः) A small tree, a shrub, a bush.<BR> E. जट् to be entangled, इन्<BR>Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=296-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झटिति
झटिति ind. Quickly, speedily, instantly.<BR> E. झटि entangling, confusing,<BR>affix इन् क्तिन्; also जटिति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=296-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झनत्कार|झनत्कारः
झनत्कार m. (-रः) The clanging of metallic ornaments, &c.<BR> E. झनत् imi-<BR>tative sound, &c. कार making.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=296-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झम
झम (उ) झमु r. 1st cl. (झमति) To eat: see जमु, &c.<BR> E. भ्वा-प-सक-सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=296-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झम्प|झंप|झंपः|झम्पः
झम्प mf. (-म्पः-म्पा) Jumping, springing, plunging.<BR> E. झं imitative<BR>sound, and पत् to fall, affix ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=296-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झम्पाक|झंपाक|झंपाकः|झम्पाकः
झम्पाक m. (-कः) A monkey or ape.<BR> E. झम्प, and अक to go. झम्पेन आकायति<BR>आ + कै-क । वानरे ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=296-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झम्पारु|झंपारु|झंपारुः|झम्पारुः
झम्पारु m. (-रुः) A monkey, an ape.<BR> E. झम्प plunging, and अश् to go,<BR>उण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=296-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झम्पाशिन्
झम्पाशिन् m. (-शी) A kingfisher.<BR> E. झम्प plunging, and अश् to eat,<BR>affix णिनि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=296-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झम्पिन्|झंपिन्
झम्पिन् m. (-म्पी) A monkey, an ape.<BR> E. झम्प springing, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=296-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झर|झरः
झर m. (-रः)<BR>	 f. (-रा or -रिः-री) A cascade, a water-fall.<BR>	 f. (-री) A river.<BR>E. झॄ to waste or decay, affix अप्, fem. affix टाप्, इन् or ङीष्; also<BR>निर्झर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=296-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झर्च|झर्च्च
झर्च r. 6th cl. (झर्च्चति)<BR>	 1. To say.<BR>	 2. To blame, to abuse or menace;<BR>also झर्छ झर्ज, &c.<BR> E. तुदा० प० सक० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=296-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झर्छ
झर्छ r. 6th cl. (झर्छति)<BR>	 1. To say.<BR>	 2. To blame, to abuse or menace;<BR>also झर्च.<BR> E. तुदा-प-सक-सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=296-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झर्ज
झर्ज r. 6th cl. (झर्जति)<BR>	 1. To say, to speak.<BR>	 2. To censure, to blame.<BR>E. तुदा-पर-सक-सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=296-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झर्झ
झर्झ r. 1st and 10th cls. (झर्झति झर्झयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To speak or say.<BR>	 2. To<BR>censure or reprove. r. 1st cl. (झर्झति) To kill or hurt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=296-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झर्झर|झर्झरः
झर्झर mf. (-रः-री) A sort of drum.<BR>	 m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. The Kaliyuga, the pre-<BR>sent Yug or age of the world.<BR>	 2. The name of a river.<BR>	 3. A cane-<BR>staff.<BR>	 4. A cymbal f. (-रा) A whore.<BR>	 n. (-रं) A sound as of splashing<BR>or dropping.<BR> E. झर्झ an imitative sound like that of water splash-<BR>ing, &c. and र what makes, from रा with ड affix, or झर्झ to cen-<BR>sure, and करच् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=296-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झर्झरक|झर्झरकः
झर्झरक m. (-कः) The Kaliyug.<BR> E. कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=296-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झर्झरीक|झर्झरीकः
झर्झरीक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. The body.<BR>	 2. A country.<BR>	 3. A picture.<BR> E. झर्झ to<BR>injure or destroy, ईकन् affix, and र inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=296-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झलञ्झला
झलञ्झला f. (-ला) The flapping of an elephant's ears, or loose breasts,<BR>&c. the word is considered as merely imitative of the noise<BR>made.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=296-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झलरी
झलरी f. (-री)<BR>	 1. A sort of drum.<BR>	 2. A curl.<BR> E. झल imitative sound, र<BR>from रा to get or make, affixes ड and ङीप्; also झल्लरी and झल्ली.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=296-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झला
झला f. (-ला)<BR>	 1. A daughter, a girl.<BR>	 2. Sunshine, splendour, brilliant or<BR>glistering light.<BR>	 3. A cricket; also झाला.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=296-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झलि|झलिः
झलि f. (-लिः) The areca nut.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=296-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झल्ल|झल्लः
झल्ल m. (-ल्लः) A prize fighter, a cudgel player, a man of a tribe follow-<BR>ing such a profession; one of the degraded classes, being sprung<BR>from the outcaste Kṣatriya<BR> E. जल् to surround or embrace, ल<BR>added, and ज changed to झ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=296-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झल्लक|झल्लकं
झल्लक n. (-कं) Cymbals.<BR> E. झल्ल imitative sound, a clash, and क what<BR>emits, from कै to sound, affix ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=296-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झल्लकण्ठ|झल्लकंठ|झल्लकंठः|झल्लकण्ठः
झल्लकण्ठ m. (-ण्ठः) A pigeon.<BR> E. झल्ल imitative sound, and कण्ठ a throat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=296-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झल्लरी
झल्लरी f. (-री)<BR>	 1. A sort of drum.<BR>	 2. A curl, a lock of hair: see झलरी.<BR>	 3.<BR>A ball, &c. of perfumed substances used for cleaning the hair.<BR>	 4.<BR>Moisture.<BR>	 5. Purity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=296-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झल्लिका
झल्लिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. Light, splendour, lustre.<BR>	 2. A rag or cloth used for<BR>applying colour or perfumes.<BR>	 3. Dirt brought off the body by rub-<BR>bing it with perfumes.<BR> E. झर्झ ण्वुल् पृषो० ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=296-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झल्ली
झल्ली f. (-ल्ली) A kind of drum: see झलरी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=296-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झल्लोल|झल्लोलः
झल्लोल m. (-लः) A ball or protuberance at the lower end of a spindle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=296-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झष|झषं|झषः
झष r. 1st. cl. (झषति-ते)<BR>	 1. To kill or hurt.<BR>	 2. To take.<BR>	 3. To put on,<BR>to wear.<BR> E. भ्वा-पर-सक-सेट् । ग्रहणे पिधाने च भ्वा-उभ-सक-सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=296-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झष|झषं|झषः
झष m. (-षः)<BR>	 1. A fish.<BR>	 2. The sign “Pisces” of the Zodiac.<BR>	 3. Heat,<BR>warmth.<BR>	 4. A forest, a thicket.<BR>	 f. (-षा) A plant, (Hedysarum<BR>lagopodioides.)<BR>	 n. (-षं) Waste land.<BR> E. झष् to injure, affix कर्मणि घ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=296-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झषकेतन|झषकेतनः
झषकेतन m. (-नः) A name of KANDARPA.<BR> E. झष a fish, and केतन a ban-<BR>ner, who bears a fish on his banner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=296-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झषाङ्क|झषांक|झषाङ्कः
झषाङ्क m. (-ङ्कः) A name of Kandarpa झष, E. a fish and अङ्क a mark or<BR>symbol.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=296-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झषाशन|झषाशनः
झषाशन m. (-नः) The gangetic porpoise.<BR> E. झष fish, and अशन food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=296-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झषोदरी
झषोदरी f. (-री) An epithet of Satyabati the mother of the poet VYASA.<BR>E. झष a fish, and उदर the belly: born from the belly of a fish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=297-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झांकृत
झांकृत n. (-तं)<BR>	 1. A tinkling ornament worn on the toes or the feet.<BR>	 2.<BR>A gurgling or rattling noise.<BR> E. झां a jungling or jingling, and कृत<BR>made (by which.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=297-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झाट|झाटः
झाट m. (-टः)<BR>	 1. An arbour, a bower, a place overgrown with creepers.<BR>2. A wood, a thicket.<BR>	 3. Cleaning sores or wounds.<BR>	 f. (-टा-टी)<BR>	 1.<BR>Jasmine.<BR>	 2. A plant, (Flacourtia cataphracta:) see झाट n. (-टं) A<BR>wood, a thicket.<BR> E. झट् to be entangled, affix णिच् अच् । निकुञ्जे<BR>कान्तारे व्रणादीनां मार्ज्जने भूम्यामलक्यायां यूथिकायां च ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=297-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झाटाल
झाटाल m. (-लः) A kind of flower: see घण्टापाटलि.<BR> E. झट् to entangle,<BR>affix णिच् अलच ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=297-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झाटास्त्रक|झाटास्त्रकः
झाटास्त्रक m. (-कः) The water melon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=297-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झाटिका
झाटिका f. (-का) A plant, (Flacourtia cataphracta)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=297-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झामक|झामकं
झामक n. (-कं) A burnt or vitrified brick.<BR> E. झम् to eat, affix कर्मणि ण्वुल्<BR>being fed upon by fire. (झामा) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=297-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झामर|झामरः
झामर m. (-रः) A small whetstone, used chiefly by housewives for<BR>sharpening their spindles, needles, &c.<BR> E. झाम eating, wearing<BR>away, from झम् to eat, affix भावे घञ्, and र what gets, from रा<BR>with ड aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=297-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झार्झर|झार्झरः
झार्झर mf. (-रः-री) A tabor player, a drummer.<BR> E. झर्झर a cymbal, affix<BR>अण्; also with ठक् affix झार्झरिक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=297-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झालरी
झालरी f. (-री) A kind of drum or tabor.<BR> E. झलरी the same, अण् pleo-<BR>nastic aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=297-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झाला
झाला f. (-ला) See झला.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=297-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झालि|झालिः
झालि f. (-लिः) A sort of sour or unripe mangoes, fried with salt, mus-<BR>tard, and asafœtida.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=297-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झावु|झावुः
झावु m. (-वुः) A tree, (Tamarix Indica;) also with कन् added झावुक m.<BR>(-कः) and with a long final vowel झावू m. (-वूः) The words are con-<BR>sidered as irregular or foreign. झा-इति वाति गच्छति वा डु (झाउ) स्वार्थे<BR>कन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=297-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झिङ्गाक|झिङ्गाकं
झिङ्गाक n. (-कं) A sort of cucumber, (Luffa acutangula.) (भिङ्गा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=297-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झिङ्गिनी|झिंगिनी
झिङ्गिनी f. (-नी)<BR>	 1. A torch, a firebrand, The fire falling from heaven.<BR>	 2.<BR>A sort of cucumber (Luffa acutangula.) or the tree. लिगि-णिनि पृषो० ।<BR>जिङ्गिनीवृक्षे, उल्कायाम् च ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=297-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झिङ्गी
झिङ्गी f. (-ङ्गी)<BR>	 1. A cricket.<BR>	 2. The wick of a lamp.<BR>	 3. light, lustre.<BR>	 4.<BR>The Jhingine tree. see झिल्ली.<BR> E. लिगि अच् गौरा० ङीष् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=297-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झिञ्जिम
झिञ्जिम m. (-मः) A forest on fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=297-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झिण्टी|झिंटी
झिण्टी f. (-ण्टी) A shrub, (Barleria cristata.)<BR> E. झि imitative sound, रट्<BR>to utter, affix अच्, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=297-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झिरी
झिरी f. (-री) A cricket.<BR> E. झि imitative of the cricket's chirp, रा to<BR>make, affixes ड and ङीष्: also झिल्ली; भिरिका, and (कन् being add<BR>ed); also इ pen. being made long झिरीका, or changed to उ, झिरुका<BR>the first vowel also being lengthened झीरिका, and झीरुका, &c.<BR>झिरिति अव्यक्तशब्दोऽस्ति अस्या इन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=297-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झिरुका
झिरुका f. (-का) A cricket: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=297-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झिल्लि|झिल्लिः
झिल्लि f. (ल्लिः)<BR>	 1. Cymbals.<BR>	 2. A cricket.<BR>	 3. Membrane: see झिल्ली. चिल्लति<BR>चिल-अच् पृ-गौरा-ङोष् आतपरुचौ, कीटभेदे वर्त्त्याञ्च ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=297-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झिल्लिका
झिल्लिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. A cricket.<BR>	 2. The light of sunshine, strong light,<BR>splendour.<BR>	 3. Dirt taken off the body in rubbing it with perfumes.<BR>4. A cloth or rag used for applying colour, unguents, &c.<BR>	 5. A<BR>cricket's cry.<BR>	 6. Membrane, thin skin, parchment.<BR> E. झिल्ल for चिल्ल<BR>imitative sound, expressing the cricket's chirp, and ङीष् being<BR>added झिल्ली, and कन् again added झिल्लिका; also with the penulti-<BR>mate long झिल्लीका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=297-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झिल्ली
झिल्ली f. (-ल्ली)<BR>	 1. A cricket.<BR>	 2. Sunshine, light, lustre.<BR>	 3. The wick of<BR>a lamp.<BR>	 4. A cloth or rag for applying unguents, colour, &c.<BR>	 5. A<BR>musical instrument, cymbals.<BR>	 6. Membrane. E. See the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=297-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झिल्लीकण्ठ|झिल्लीकंठ|झिल्लीकण्ठः
झिल्लीकण्ठ m. (-ण्ठः) A pigeon.<BR> E. झिल्ली a cricket, and कण्ठ the throat,<BR>chirping as it were in the throat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=297-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झीरिका
झीरिका f. (-का A cricket: see झिरी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=297-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झीरुका
झीरुका f. (-का) A cricket: see झिरी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=297-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झु|झुः
झु r. 1st cl. (झवते) To go or move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=297-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झुण्ट|झुंट|झुंटः|झुण्टः
झुण्ट m. (-ण्टः)<BR>	 1. A tree.<BR>	 1. A shrub, a bush.<BR> E. झट् to be entangled,<BR>affix अच्, नुम् augment, and the vowel changed to उ. ल्युण्ठ अच्-पृ० ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=297-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झूणि|झूणिः
झूणि f. (-णिः)<BR>	 1. A kind of betel nut.<BR>	 2. Heavenly annunciation of<BR>misfortunes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=297-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झूमेरि
झूमेरि f. (-रिः) One of the Rāgiṇīs, or modes of music personified.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=297-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झूष
झूष r. 1st cl. (झूषति) To hurt or kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=297-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झॄ
झॄ r. 9th cl. (झॄणाति) (ष) झॄष् r. 1st cl. (झीर्य्यति) To grow old, क्य्रा० दिवा-<BR>प० अक० सेट् । to become infirm with age, &c. to decay.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=297-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झोड|झोडः
झोड m. (-डः) The betel nut tree,<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=297-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झ्यु
झ्यु r. 1st cl. (झ्यवते) To go or move. गतौ भ्वा० आ० सक० अनिट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=297-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ञ|ञः
ञ The nasal attached to the class of palatal letters, having some-<BR>thing like the sound of N in the French word Singe, and express-<BR>ed by the letter accented N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=297-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ञ|ञः
ञ m. (-ञः)<BR>	 1. A name of SUKRA, regent of Venus.<BR>	 2. An ox.<BR>	 3. A<BR>heretic, an apostate.<BR>	 4. Singing.<BR>	 5. Jingling or inarticulate sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=297-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ट|टं|टः
ट The 11th consonant of the Nagri alphabet, and first of the 3rd<BR>class or cerebrals. It corresponds in sound to the letter T pro-<BR>nounced far back in the mouth, or as in true, and is expressed<BR>in the roman character by the accented letter T.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=297-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ट|टं|टः
ट m. (-टः) Sound. a particular sound, like the twang of a bow<BR>string.<BR>	 2. A dwarf.<BR>	 3. A quarter, a fourth, n. (-टं) A hollowed<BR>cocoanut, f. (टा)<BR>	 1. The earth.<BR>	 2. An oath, confirming an asser-<BR>tion by ordeal, &c.<BR> E. टक् to bind, &c. affix ड<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=297-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

टक
टक (इ) टकि r. 1st and 10th cls. (टङ्कति टङ्कयति-ते) To bind, to tie. भ्वा०<BR>प० पक्षे चुरा० उभ० सक० सेट् इदित् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=297-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

टक्कादेशीय
टक्कादेशीय m. (-यः) A potherb, (Chenopodium album.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=297-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

टगर|टगरः
टगर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Squint-eyed.<BR>	 m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Borax.<BR>	 2. Wanton play or<BR>sport.<BR>	 3. Wandering of the mind, confusion, perplexity.<BR>	 4. An<BR>object of sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=297-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

टङ्क|टंक|टंकं|टंकः|टङ्कः
टङ्क mn. (-ङ्कः-ङ्कं)<BR>	 1. A kind of elephant or wood apple, नीलकपित्थ.<BR>	 2.<BR>Borax.<BR>	 3. A spade or hoe.<BR>	 m. (-ङ्कः)<BR>	 1. A hatchet or stone cut-<BR>ter's chisel.<BR>	 2. A sword, a scimiter, a sacrificial hatchet or knife.<BR>3. A scabbard, a sword-sheath.<BR>	 4. Anger, wrath.<BR>	 5. A weight of<BR>(silver) equal to four māṣas.<BR>	 6. A coin.<BR>	 7. Pride, arrogance.<BR>	 8. A<BR>cleft, a chasm.<BR>	 9. A peak.<BR>	 f. (-ङ्गा)<BR>	 1. The leg.<BR>	 2. The edge or side<BR>of a mountain.<BR> E. टकि to bind, affix अच् घञ् वा or ट imitative, कै<BR>to emit sound, affix ड, and नुम् augment. संज्ञायाम् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=297-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

टङ्कक|टंकक|टंककः|टङ्ककः
टङ्कक m. (-कः) A stamped coin, especially of silver.<BR> E. संज्ञायां कन् added<BR>to टङ्क a weight of silver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=297-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

टङ्ककपति|टंककपति|टङ्ककपतिः
टङ्ककपति m. (-तिः) The master of a mint or superintendent of the silver<BR>coin.<BR> E. टङ्कक, and पति master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=297-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

टङ्ककशाला|टंककशाला
टङ्ककशाला f. (-ला) A mint.<BR> E. टङ्कक, and शाला a hall.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=297-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

टङ्कटीक|टंकटीकः|टङ्कटीकः
टङ्कटीक m. (-कः) A name of ŚIVA.<BR> E. टङ्क an axe, and टीक who has,<BR>from टीक् to go or get, affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=297-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

टङ्कन|टंकन|टंकनं|टङ्कनः
टङ्कन mn. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Borax.<BR>	 2. m. (णः) A species of horse. Binding, tying.<BR>E. टकि to bind, affix ल्यु. पृषो० बा णत्वम् टङ्कण ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=298-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

टङ्कपति|टङ्कपतिः
टङ्कपति m. (-तिः) The master of the mint.<BR> E. टङ्क a weight of silver put<BR>for a coin, and पति master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=298-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

टङ्कशाला
टङ्कशाला f. (-ला) A mint.<BR> E. टङ्क see the last, and शाला a house or hall.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=298-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

टङ्कानक|टङ्कानकः
टङ्कानक m. (-कः) The mulberry, (Morus Indica.) (वामन गाछा)<BR> E. टङ्कं<BR>कोपमानयति उद्दीपयति अन-णिच् ण्वुल ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=298-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

टङ्कार|टंकार|टंकारः|टङ्कारः
टङ्कार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Surprise, wonder.<BR>	 2. Fame, notoriety.<BR>	 3. The twang<BR>of a bow string.<BR>	 4. A howl, a cry.<BR> E. टकि to bind, &c. affix आरक्;<BR>or ट twang, in the second case, कृ to make, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=298-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

टङ्ग|टंग|टंगं|टंगः|टङ्गः
टङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>	 1. A spade or hoe.<BR>	 2. An axe.<BR>	 3. The leg.<BR>	 4. Borax.<BR>	 5. A<BR>weight of four māṣas.<BR> E. टकि to bind, affix अच्. क changed to ग,<BR>otherwise टङ्क् as above; also with ल्युट् affix, टङ्गन n. (-नं)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=298-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

टङ्गिनी
टङ्गिनी f. (-नी) A plant, (Cissampelos hexandra.) टकि णिनि-पृ आकनादौ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=298-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

टट्टनी
टट्टनी f. (-नी) A house lizard.<BR> E. टट्ट imitative sound, and न what makes,<BR>from नी, affixes ड and ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=298-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

टट्टरी
टट्टरी f. (-री)<BR>	 1. A joke, a jest.<BR>	 2. A kettle drum.<BR>	 3. Any musical ins-<BR>trument.<BR> E. टट्ट imitative sound, and र what makes sound, and रा,<BR>with ड and ङीष् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=298-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

टट्टुर|टट्टुरः
टट्टुर m. (-रः) The sound of a drum.<BR> E. टट्टु imitative sound, tattoo,<BR>and र what gets or has.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=298-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

टल|टलः
टल r. 1st cl. (टलति) To be confused, to be disturbed by fear, anxie-<BR>ty, &c. भ्वा० पर० अक० सेट्-ज्वला० । विप्लवे ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=298-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

टलन|टलनं
टलन n. (-नं) Anxiety, Perturbation.<BR> E. टल् to be disturbed, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=298-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

टाङ्कर|टांकर|टांकरः|टाङ्करः
टाङ्कर m. (-रः) A black-guard, a lecher, a libertine.<BR> E. टां an oath, and<BR>कर who takes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=298-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

टाङ्कार|टांकारः|टाङ्कारः
टाङ्कार m. (-रः) A clang, a twang.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=298-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

टार|टारः
टार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. horse.<BR>	 2. A catamite.<BR> E. टां पृथ्वीमृच्छति ऋ-अण् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=298-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

टिक
टिक (ऋ) टिकृ r. 1st cl. (टेकते) To go or move. भ्वा-आत्म-सक-सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=298-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

टिटिभक|टिटिभकः
टिटिभक m. (-कः) A bird: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=298-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

टिट्टिभ|टिट्टिभः
टिट्टिभ m. (-भः) A bird, (Parra jacana or goensis.)<BR> E. टिट्टि imitative<BR>sound, भास् to utter, affix ड; also with स्वाथ कन् added, टिट्टिभक;<BR>also टिटिभक, टटिभक, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=298-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

टिण्डिश|टिण्डिशः
टिण्डिश m. (-शः) A kind of tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=298-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

टिप
टिप r. 10th cl. (टेपयति-ते) To direct, to send, to throw or cast: the<BR>act of throwing being considered analogous to that of sending or<BR>ordering. चुरा० उभ० सक० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=298-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

टिप्पनी
टिप्पनी f. (-नी) A gloss, a comment.<BR> E. टिप-क्विप् टिपा पन्यते स्तूयते पा घञर्थे क<BR>गौरा ङीष् । टीकायाम् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=298-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

टीक
टीक (ऋ) टीकृ r. 1st cl. (टीकते) To go or move. गतौ भ्वा-आत्म-सक-सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=298-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

टीका
टीका f. (-का) A commentary.<BR> E. टीक् to go, affixes घञ् and टाप् by<BR>which the sense of the text proceeds. टीक्यते मम्यते ग्रन्थार्थीऽनया टीक<BR>करणे घञ् घञर्थे क वा ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=298-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

टु|टुः
टु m. (-टुः)<BR>	 1. Gold.<BR>	 2. A Proteus, a changer of shapes at will, KĀMA^1<BR>or love.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20260617. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/264.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=298-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

टुण्टुक|टुंटुक|टुण्टुकः
टुण्टुक mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>	 1. Low, little, vile.<BR>	 2. Cruel, harsh.<BR>	 m. (-कः)<BR>1. A plant, (Bigonia Indica.)<BR>	 2. A black species of catechu.<BR>	 3. A<BR>small bird, (Silvia sutoria.)<BR>	 f. (-का) A plant, commonly Akanadhi:<BR>see टङ्गिनी.<BR> E. टुण्टु imitative sound, and क what utters.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=298-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

टेपन|टेपनं
टेपन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Sending.<BR>	 2. Throwing.<BR> E. टिप् to throw, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=298-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

टेर
टेर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Squint-eyed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=298-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

टेरक|टेरकः
टेरक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Spuint-eyed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=298-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

टौक
टौक m. (ऋ) टौकृ r. 1st cl. (टौकते) To go, or move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=298-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ट्वल
ट्वल r. 1st cl. (ट्वलति) To be disturbed or confused: see टल । भ्वा-प-अक-<BR>सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=298-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ठ|ठः
ठ The aspirate of the preceding letter, corresponding to Th.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=298-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ठ|ठः
ठ m. (-ठः)<BR>	 1. A name of ŚIVA.<BR>	 2. The disk of the sun or moon.<BR>	 3. A<BR>circle, a globe.<BR>	 4. A cypher.<BR>	 5. An object of sense.<BR>	 5. A loud<BR>noise.<BR>	 7. An imitative sound as of a metallic pot rolling down<BR>steps.<BR>	 8. An idol, a deity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=298-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ठक्कुर|ठक्कुरः
ठक्कुर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. An idol, a deity, an object of reverence or worship.<BR>	 2.<BR>An honorific title after the name of a distinguished person.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=298-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ठठम्
ठठम् ind. An imitative sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=298-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ठालिनी
ठालिनी f. (-नी) A girdle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=298-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ड|डः
ड The third letter of the cerebral class of consonants, having the<BR>sound of D, pronounced far back in the “head”: it is often con-<BR>founded in pronounciation with a hard R, or L, sounded as in<BR>the Northumbrian bur; it is written in the Roman character D.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=298-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ड|डः
ड m. (-डः)<BR>	 1. A name of ŚIVA.<BR>	 2. Fear.<BR>	 3. Sound.<BR>	 4. Submarine fire.<BR>5. A kind of drum or tabor.<BR>	 6. A kind of bird.<BR>	 f. (-डा)<BR>	 1. A kind<BR>of female imp or goblin.<BR>	 2. A basket, &c. carried by a sling: see<BR>डलक.<BR> E. डप to collect, affix, ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=298-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डङ्गरी
डङ्गरी f. (-री) A kind of gourd; also read डङ्गारी<BR> E. डं त्रासं गिरति गॄ-अच्<BR>गौरा ङीष् । कर्कटीभेदे ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=298-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डप
डप r. 10th cl (डापयते) (इ) डपि r. 1st and 10th cls. (डम्प-ते डम्पयते) To<BR>collect, to accumulate, to heap together. संहतौ वा-चुरा-आत्म-अक-सक-<BR>सेट् पक्षे भ्वा ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=298-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डब
डब r. 10th cl. (इ) डबि (डम्बयति-ते) To throw, to send, to order. With वि<BR>prefixed, to deceive, to disgrace. चुरा-उभ-प-आत्मप्रेरणे राशिकरणे<BR>च । सक-सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=298-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डभ
डभ (इ) डभि r. 1st and 10th cls. (डम्भति डम्भययि-ते) To collect, to heap.<BR>together. चुरा-उभ-पस-सक-सेट् पक्षे भ्वा । इदित् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=298-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डम|डमः
डम m. (-मः) A man of low caste, employed to clear away filth, &c. E.<BR>डं तासं माति मा-क । (डोम्)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=298-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डमर|डमरं|डमरः
डमर mf. (-रः-रा)<BR>	 1. An affray, a conflict without weapons.<BR>	 2. Terri-<BR>fying an enemy by shouts and gestures.<BR>	 3. Petty or predatory<BR>warfare, war carried on by detachments or by villagers, one in<BR>which kings are not engaged.<BR>	 4. Rout, riot.<BR>	 n. (-रं) Flight, running<BR>away through fear.<BR> E. डम् imitative sound, and अर what occasions,<BR>from ऋ to go, affix घञर्थे क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=298-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डमरु|डमरुः
डमरु m. (-रुः)<BR>	 1. A musical instrument, a sort of small drum, shaped<BR>like an hour-glass, and held in one hand usually carried by Kapa-<BR>likas.<BR>	 2. Any thing surprising, any strange occurence, &c.<BR> E. डम<BR>imitative sound, ऋ to go or get उण् affix and the vowel changed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=298-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डम्बर|डंबर|डम्बरः
डम्बर adj.<BR>	 f. (-रा)<BR>	 1. Famous, Renowned.<BR>	 2. (m) An assemblage, a mass.<BR>as in गेघडम्वर ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=298-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डयन|डयनं
डयन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. A car or litter carried upon men's shoulders, a Palan-<BR>quin, a Duli.<BR>	 2. Flying in the air, the flight of a bird.<BR> E. डी to fly<BR>aff ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=298-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डवित्थ|डवित्थः
डवित्थ m. (-त्थः) A wooden antelope.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=298-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डलक|डलकं
डलक n. (-कं) A sling, a basket, a duli carried on mens’ shoulders<BR>by means of a stick and ropes like the beam and strings of a<BR>balance; presents of fruit, sweetmeats, &c. are usually sent in<BR>this manner; also read डल्लक. (डालि)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=298-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डहु|डहुः
डहु m. (-हुः) A tree, (Artocarpus lacucha.)<BR> E. दह् to burn, affix उ, and<BR>deriv. irr.; also with ऊ affix डहू m. (-हूः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=299-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डाकिनी
डाकिनी f. (-नी) A kind of female imp or evil being. डाकानां समूहः इनि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=299-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डाङ्कृति|डांकृतिः
डाङ्कृति f. (-तिः) The clang of a bell, ding-dong.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=299-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डामर|डामरः
डामर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Affray, conflict without weapons, &c. See डमर.<BR>	 2.<BR>Rout, uproar, the bustle and the confusion of festivity or strife.<BR>3. Any surprising thing, sight or occurrence.<BR>	 4. A name common<BR>to six Tantras, as the Sivadamara, Yogadamara, Durgada mara,<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>	 1. Terrific.<BR>	 2. Beautiful.<BR>	 3. Variegated &c.<BR> E. डमर q. v. and<BR>अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=299-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डालिम|डालिमः
डालिम m. (-मः) A pomegranate: see दाडिम.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=299-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डाहल|डाहलः
डाहल m. (-लः) The name of a country; also Tripura: see त्रिपुर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=299-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डाहुक|डाहुकः
डाहुक m. (-कः) A gallinule.<BR> E. दह to consume, (disease,) उकञ् affix,<BR>the flesh being considered medicinal: the radical initial is changed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=299-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डिक्करी
डिक्करी f. (-री) A young woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=299-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डिङ्गर|डिंगर|डिंगरः|डिङ्गरः
डिङ्गर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Throwing, sending.<BR>	 2. A fat man.<BR>	 3. A servant, a<BR>slave.<BR>	 4. A rogue, a cheat.<BR>	 5. A low or depraved man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=299-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डिण्डिम|डिंडिम|डिंडिमः|डिण्डिमः
डिण्डिम m. (-मः)<BR>	 1. A musical instrument, a kind of small drum or<BR>tabor.<BR>	 2. A plant, bearing a small fruit, (Carissa carandas:)<BR>(पानआमला) see कृष्णपाक.<BR> E. डिण्डि imitative sound, a din, and म<BR>what emits, from मि, with ड aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=299-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डिण्डिर|डिंडिर|डिंडिरः|डिण्डिरः
डिण्डिर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Cuttle-fish bone, considered to be the foam of the<BR>sea.<BR>	 2. A foam in general also. डिण्डीर ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=299-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डिण्डिरमोदक|डिण्डिरमोदकं
डिण्डिरमोदक n. (-कं) Garlic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=299-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डित्थ|डित्थः
डित्थ m. (-त्थः)<BR>	 1. Wodden elephant.<BR>	 2. An agreeable man. “श्यामरूपो<BR>युवा विद्वान् सुन्दरः प्रियदर्शनः । सर्व्वशास्त्रार्थावेत्ता च डित्थ इत्यभिधीयते ॥<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=299-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डिप
डिप r. 4th cl. (इर) डिपिर (डिप्यति) r. 6th cl. (डिपति) and r. 10th cl. (डेप-<BR>यति-ते) To throw, to cast, to send or order, to direct प्रेरणे वा चुरा-उभ-<BR>पक्षे तुदा कुटा० पर-सक-सेट् । see टिप r. 10th cl. (डेपयति-ते) also (इ) डिपि<BR>r. 1st and 10th cls. (डिम्पति) and (डिम्पय-ति-ते) To collect, to heap<BR>to gether. संहतौ वा चुरा उभ, पक्षे भ्वा-आत्म-अक-सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=299-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डिब
डिब r. 10th cl. (इ) डिबि (डिम्बयति-ते) To cast, to throw. प्रेरणे वा चुरा उभ<BR>पक्षे भ्वा-पर-सक सेट् इदित् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=299-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डिभ
डिभ (इ) डिभि r. 1st and 10th cls. (डिम्भति and डिम्मयति-ते) To collect to<BR>heap together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=299-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डिम|डिमः
डिम m. (-मः) A dramatic entertainment, dramatic exhibition of battle<BR>or seige, such as the Tripurabadha, in which the destruction of<BR>the three cities of TRIPURA by ŚIVA is dramatised.<BR> E. डिम affray,<BR>and affix क 2. One of the ten kinds of drama, thus defined:--मायेन्द्र-<BR>जालसंग्रामक्रोधोद्भान्तादिचेष्टितैः । उपरागैश्च भूयिष्ठो डिमः ख्यातोऽतिवृत्तकः ॥<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=299-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डिम्ब|डिंब|डिम्बं|डिंबः|डिम्बः
डिम्ब m. (-म्बः)<BR>	 1. Affray, assault. conflict without weapons mutual de-<BR>fiance, petty and predatory war, &c. See डमर.<BR>	 2. Sound or noise<BR>occasioned by terror.<BR>	 3. An egg.<BR>	 4. A chrysalis.<BR>	 5. The bladder.<BR>6. The spleen.<BR>	 7. The uterus.<BR>	 8. Fear, terror.<BR>	 9. Any young ani-<BR>mal.<BR>	 10. A globe or ball.<BR> E. डिबि घञ् अच् वा ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=299-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डिम्बाहव|डिंबाहव|डिम्बाहवः
डिम्बाहव m. (-वः) Petty warfare, affray. skirmish, riot, &c.<BR> E. डिम्ब<BR>as above, and आहव war, battle; also डिम्बयुद्ध and other similar<BR>compounds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=299-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डिम्बिका|डिंबिका
डिम्बिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. A bubble.<BR>	 2. A kind of waterfly.<BR>	 3. A libidinous<BR>woman.<BR> E. डिम्ब the bladder, &c. कन् aff, or डिवि-ण्वुल् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=299-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डिम्प्र
डिम्प्र m. (-म्भः)<BR>	 1. Any young animal.<BR>	 2. A fool, an idiot, a blockhead.<BR>f. (-म्भा) An infant.<BR> E. डिभि to collect, affix अच्; कन् being added;<BR>also डिम्भक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=299-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डिम्भचक्र|डिम्भचक्रं
डिम्भचक्र n. (-क्रं) A diagram for telling fortunes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=299-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डी
डी (ङ) डीञ् r. 1st and 4th cls. (डयते डीयते)<BR>	 1. To fly, to pass through<BR>the air.<BR>	 2. To go, to move. With अव, prefixed, To fly down, to<BR>to alight. With उत्, To fly up, to soar. With परि, To fly round.<BR>With प्र, To fly well or swiftly. With सम्, To fly well or in flocks.<BR>With सम् and उत्, To fly up by degrees. नभोगतौ भ्वा० दिवा०<BR>आत्म० सक० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=299-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डीन|डीनं
डीन n. (-नं) Flying, the flight of a bird, to go.<BR> E. डी to fly, भ्वावे क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=299-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डीनडीनक|डीनडीनकं
डीनडीनक m. (-कः) Flying reiteratedly.<BR> E. डीन flying, reduplicated, कन्<BR>added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=299-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डीनावडीन|डीनावडीनं
डीनावडीन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Flying up and down.<BR>	 2. Flying ill.<BR> E. डीन, and<BR>अवडीन alighting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=299-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डुण्डु|डुण्डुः
डुण्डु m. (-ण्डुः) A kind of snake, (Amphisbæna)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=299-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डुण्डुभ|डुंडुभ|डुंडुभः|डुण्डुभः
डुण्डुभ m. (-भः) A kind of snake, not poisonous. (Amphisbæna) E.<BR>डुण्डु, and भ from भा to shine or resemble. डुण्डु इत्यनुकरणशब्दं भणति<BR>तेन भाति वा भण भा वा ड (ढोडासाप) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=299-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डुण्डुल|डुंडुलः|डुण्डुलः
डुण्डुल m. (-लः) A small owl.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=299-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डुन्दुक|डुंदुकः|डुन्दुकः
डुन्दुक m. (-कः) A gallinule: see डाहुक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=299-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डुलि|डुलिः
डुलि f. (-लिः)<BR>	 1. A small turtle.<BR>	 2. A female turtle: see टुलि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=299-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डुलिका
डुलिका f. (-का) A bird resembling a wagtail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=299-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डोर|डोरं|डोरः
डोर n. (-रं) A fillet of thread or cord tied round the arm or wrist;<BR>it is also applied to the string tying a packet or parcel; also with<BR>कन् added डोरक. दोष् रा-ड-पृषो ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=299-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ढ|ढः
ढ The aspirate of the preceding letter corresponding Dh: the use<BR>of this as an initial letter is very limited and several of the<BR>words in which it occurs can scarcely be regarded as pure<BR>Sanskrit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=299-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ढ|ढः
ढ m. (-ढः)<BR>	 1. A large drum.<BR>	 2. A dog.<BR>	 3. A dog's tail.<BR>	 4. Sound.<BR>	 5.<BR>A serpent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=299-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ढक्क|ढक्कः
ढक्क m. (-क्कः)<BR>	 1. The city or district Dhacca or Dacca.<BR>	 2. Coveting,<BR>disappearance.<BR>	 f. (-क्का) A large or double drum, a Dhak.<BR> E. ढक्<BR>imitative sound, and क what utters.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=299-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ढक्कारी
ढक्कारी f. (-री) The goddess TARINI, a Tantrika form of DURGĀ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=299-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ढगण
ढगण m. (-णः) मात्रावृत्ते त्रिमात्रिक प्रस्तावभेदे ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=299-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ढण्टी
ढण्टी f. (-ण्टी) वाक्यभेदे ढण्टीवाक्यस्वरूपा च ढकाराक्षररूपिणी ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=299-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ढामरा
ढामरा f. (-रा) A goose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=299-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ढाल|ढालं
ढाल n. (-लं) A shield.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=299-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ढालिन्
ढालिन् m. (ली) A warrior armed with a shield, a shield-bearer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=299-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ढुढ
ढुढ (इ) ढुढि Sautra root, (ढुण्ढति) To search, to seek. भ्वा-पर-सक-सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=299-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ढुण्ढन|ढुंढनं
ढुण्ढन n. (-नं) Seeking, investigating.<BR> E. ढुढि to search, ल्युट्. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=299-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ढुण्ढि|ढुंढि|ढुंढिः|ढुण्ढिः
ढुण्ढि m. (-ण्ढिः) A name of GANESHA.<BR> E. ढुढि to seek, कि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=299-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ढुण्ढित
ढुण्ढित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Sought, inquired.<BR> E. ढुढि to seek, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=299-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ढोल|ढोलः
ढोल m. (-लः) A Dhol or large drum. दोलायमानो वाद्यमाने वाद्यभेदे ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=299-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ढौक
ढौक (ऋ) ढौकृ r. 1st cl. (ढौकते) To go or move. प्रेरण गत्याञ्च भ्वा-आ-सक-<BR>सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=299-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ढौकन|ढौकनं
ढौकन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Offering.<BR>	 2. A present, a bribe.<BR> E. ढौक् to go, ल्यु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=299-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ण|णः
ण The nasal N belonging to the third or cerebral class of conso-<BR>nants; in derivation and inflection this is usually changed to न<BR>or to dental N, and hence the derivatives from the following re-<BR>dicals occur under that letter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=299-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ण|णः
ण m. (-णः)<BR>	 1. Knowledge.<BR>	 2. Certainty, ascertainment.<BR>	 3. A name of<BR>ŚIVA.<BR>	 4. Vindudeva, said to be a A Jaina deity.<BR>	 5. An orna-<BR>ment.<BR>	 6. A water or summer house.<BR>	 7. One without good<BR>qualities.<BR>	 8. A kind of sound, the sound of negation.<BR>	 9. Gift,<BR>giving.<BR> E. णी to guide, &c. affix ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=299-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

णक्ष
णक्ष r. 1st cl. (नक्षति, or with प्र prefixed प्रणक्षति) To go, to move;<BR>to approach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=300-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

णख
णख r. 1st cl. (नखति) also (इ) णखि r. 1st cl. (नंखति) To go, to move,<BR>also नख. गतौ भ्वा-पर-सक सेट् । णोपदेशत्वात् सति निमित्ते णत्वम् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=300-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

णट
णट r. 1st cl. (नटति प्रणटति)<BR>	 1. To dance.<BR>	 2. To dance as an actor, to<BR>gesticulate, to act; also नट.<BR>	 3. To hurt. भ्वा-पर-सक-सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=300-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

णद
णद r. 1st cl. (नदति प्रणदति) To sound Inarticulately, to roar as a river<BR>or a wild beast, to ring as a bell, &c. r. 10th cl.<BR>(नादयति-ते) To speak or tell, to shine. भासे चुरा-उभ-सक-सेट् । भ्वा-पर-अक-सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=300-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

णभ
णभ r. 1st cl. (नभते प्रणभते) 4th cl. (नभ्यति) and 9th cl. (नम्नाति)<BR>	 1. To kill,<BR>to injure.<BR>	 2. To be annihilated, to cease to be.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=300-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

णम
णम r. 1st cl. (नमति)<BR>	 1. To salute with reverence or respect.<BR>	 2. To<BR>bow down or bent, to bow down in homage or worship.<BR>	 3. To<BR>sound. With अव or आङ् or or सम् prefixed, To bend down, to<BR>decline. With प्र, to bow, to salute. With उत्, To lift up, to raise,<BR>to make straight or erect. शब्दे अक-नतौ सक भ्वा-पर-अनिट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=300-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

णय
णय r. 1st cl. (नयते प्रणयते)<BR>	 1. To go, to move or approach.<BR>	 2. To pres-<BR>erve, to protect, to defend. । भ्वादि-पर-सक-सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=300-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

णर्द|णर्द्द
णर्द r. 1st cl. (नर्दति प्रणर्दति) To sound; also नर्द-भ्वा-पर-अक-सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=300-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

णल
णल r. 1st cl. (नलति प्रणलति)<BR>	 1. To smell.<BR>	 2. To bind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=300-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

णश
णश r. 4th cl. (ऊ) णशू (नश्यति) To disappear, to cease to be, to perish,<BR>to be annihilated. अदर्शने नाशे च दिवा-पर-सक-सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=300-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

णस
णस r., 1st cl. (नसते (प्रणसते) 1. To be crooked, (literally or metaphorical-<BR>ly. ).<BR>	 2. To bend, to make curved or crooked. भ्वा-आत्म-अक-सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=300-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

णह
णह r. 4th cl. (औ) औनह (नह्यति नह्यते) To bind, to tie. With सम् pre-<BR>fixed, (सन्नाहति) To arm, to put on mail or military accoutrements.<BR>दिवा-उभ-सक-अनिट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=300-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

णास
णास (ऋ) णासृ r. 1st cl. (नसते प्रणासते) To sound in particular manner,<BR>to snore. भ्वा-आत्म-अक-सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=300-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

णिक्ष
णिक्ष r. 1st cl. (निक्षति प्रणिक्षति) To kiss: the change of the ण after a<BR>preposition is optional in the derivatives of this root. भ्वा-पर-सक-सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=300-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

णिज
णिज (इ) णिजि r. 2nd cl. (निंक्ते प्रणिंक्ते) To kiss; the cleanse, (औ, इर)<BR>औणिजिर r. 3rd cl. (नेनेक्ति नेनिक्ते)<BR>	 1. To nurture, to cherish or<BR>maintain.<BR>	 2. To purify, to cleanse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=300-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

णद
णद (इ) णिदि r. 1st cl. (निन्दति-ते प्रणिन्दति) also (ऋ) णिदृ r. 1st cl. (नेदति-<BR>ते, प्रणेदति)<BR>	 1. To abuse. to censure, to reproach, to reprove or revile,<BR>to despise or condemn, &c. (The second root means also)<BR>	 2. To<BR>approach, to come near. The change of ण after a preposition is op-<BR>tional in the derivatives of the first of these roots.<BR> E. कुत्सने भ्वादि-<BR>पर-सक-सेट् इदित् । सन्निधाने अक-निन्दने सक-भ्वा-उभ-सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=300-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

णिल
णिल r. 6th cl. (निलति)<BR>	 1. To misunderstand, to comprehend ill or im-<BR>perfectly.<BR>	 2. To be thick or impenetrable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=300-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

णिव
णिव (इ) णिवि r.<BR>	 1. cl. (निन्वति प्रणिन्वति) To wet, To moisten, to sprinkle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=300-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

णिश
णिश r. 1st cl. (नेशति प्रणेशति) To meditate profoundly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=300-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

णिष
णिष r. 1st cl. (उ) णिषु (नेषति) To sprinkle, to shed as water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=300-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

णिस
णिस (इ) णिसि r. 2nd cl. (निंस्ते प्रणिंस्ते) To kiss: the change of ण after a<BR>preposition is optional in the derivatives. अदा-अक-सेट् इदित् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=300-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

णी
णी (ञ) णीञ् r. 1st cl. (नयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To conduct, to drive or guide to<BR>cause progressive conveyance.<BR>	 2. To obtain, to get. The<BR>root is inflected as the deponent verb, implying, 1. Instruction,<BR>as नयते शास्त्रे he instructs in the Śāstra; 2. Worshipping, विष्णुं नयते<BR>he worships VIṢṆU; also with prepositions in the sense of; 1.<BR>Paying, भृत्यमुपनयते he pays the hire; 2. Paying as a debt, ऋणं<BR>विनयते he discharges the debt; 3. Casting or lifting up, दण्डमुन्नयते<BR>he lifts up the stick; 4. Giving, द्रव्यं विनमते he gives the things;<BR>and 5. Brahmanical Investiture, पुत्त्रमुपनयते he invests his son<BR>with the thread: it is also deponent, governing an incorporeal<BR>object existing in the agent, as क्रोधं विनयते he suppresses wrath;<BR>if the object is not in the agent the verb is active, as गुरोः क्रोधं<BR>विनयति he appeases his teacher's anger; as also if the object is<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=300-b" target="_blank">Page300-b+ 55</a>]<BR>corporeal, as गण्डं विनयति he turns away the cheek. The root occurs<BR>with many prefixes, and in a great variety of meanings; 1. With<BR>अनु, a To ask, to entreat. b To make like or resembling. c. To<BR>favour.<BR>	 2. With अप, a To take away, to remove. b. To attract.<BR>	 3.<BR>With अभि, a. To indicate by signs. b. To be kind or civil to.<BR>	 4. With<BR>आङ् To bring.<BR>	 5. With उत्, To raise up.<BR>	 6. With उप, To approach,<BR>to go near to (see also above.)<BR>	 7. With दुर्, To act or behave<BR>wickedly.<BR>	 8. With निर्, a. To get or obtain. b. To ascertain, to de-<BR>termine.<BR>	 9. With परि, a. To marry. b. To take cognizance of.<BR>	 10. With<BR>प्र, a. To punish. b. To love.<BR>	 11. With वि, a. To take away, to make<BR>remote or distant. b To behumble or modest.<BR>	 12. With वि and अप,<BR>To remove, to dispel, to disperse.<BR>	 13. With वि and निर्, To decide<BR>by law.<BR>	 14. With सम्, a. To collect. b. To discharge.<BR>	 15. With सम्<BR>and अनु, To entreat.<BR>	 16. With सम् and आङ्, To assemble to<BR>collect, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=300-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

णील
णील r. 1st cl. (नीलति प्रणीलति)<BR>	 1. To be blue.<BR>	 2. To make or dye blue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=300-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

णीव
णीव r. 1st cl. (नीवति प्रणीवति) To be large or corpulent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=300-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

णु
णु r. 3rd cl. (नौति-प्रणौति) To praise. With आङ् prefixed (आनुते) To<BR>utter a cry of regret. r. 6th cl. (नवति) To praise. अदा-पर सक-वेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=300-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

णुद
णुद r. 6th cl. (औ) औणुद (नुनति नुदते) 1. To cast, to command, to direct,<BR>to throw or send; the act of ordering being considered analogous<BR>to that of throwing.<BR>	 2. To go or proceed. With अप, To remove.<BR>With निर् 1. To throw out.<BR>	 2. To confess, to acknowledge. With वि,<BR>To be happy. With सं in the causal, To drive, (as horses.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=300-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

णू
णू r. 6th cl. (नुवति) To praise; also णु-तु-कु-पर-सक-सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=300-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

णेद
णेद (ऋ) णेदृ r. 1st cl. (नेदति-ते)<BR>	 1. To censure, to despise.<BR>	 2. To approach<BR>or come near; see णिद. उभ-सक-सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=300-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

णेष
णेष (ऋ) णेषृ r. 1st cl. (नेषते) To go, to move or approach. भ्वा-आत्म-सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=300-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ण्य|ण्यः
ण्य m. ब्रह्मलोकस्थे सरोवरभेदे ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=300-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्
त The first consonant of the fourth or dental class, corresponding to<BR>the letter T, in tongue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=300-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त|तं|तः
त m. (-तः)<BR>	 1. A thief.<BR>	 2. Nectar, the food of the immortals.<BR>	 3. An out-<BR>caste, a barbarian or Mleccha.<BR>	 4. The flank, the hip or haunch.<BR>5. A tail.<BR>	 6. The womb.<BR>	 7. A wicked man.<BR>	 8. A tree.<BR>	 9. A jewel.<BR>10. A Buddha.<BR>	 n. (-तं)<BR>	 1. Passing, crossing.<BR>	 2. Virtue, sancity. E.<BR>तृ to cross, &c. affix ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=300-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तक
तक r. 1st cl. (तकति)<BR>	 1. To laugh at or deride.<BR>	 2. To bear. With वि and<BR>अति prefixed, and implying reciprocity (व्यतितकते) To retort a<BR>laugh. (इ) तकि r. 1st cl. (तङ्कति) To live in distress to be in poverty<BR>or pain. (तंकते) To go to move. हसने सहने वा ड । हासे अक-सहने सक-<BR>भ्वा-पर-सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=300-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तक
तक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) That.<BR> E. तत् that कन् pleonasm added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=300-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तकिल|तकिलः
तकिल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Fraudulent, crafty, a rogue or cheat.<BR>	 f. (-ला) A<BR>medicament, a drug तक् to deride, affix इलच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=300-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तक्य|तक्यः
तक्य mfn. (-क्यः-क्या-क्यं)<BR>	 1. Laughable, ridiculous.<BR>	 2. To be borne or en-<BR>dured.<BR> E. तक् to laugh, यत् participial aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=300-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तक्र|तक्रं
तक्र n. (-क्रं)<BR>	 n. Buttermilk with a fourth part water.<BR> E. तक् to bear<BR>(sickness), Uṇādi affix रक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=300-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तक्रकूर्च्चिका|तक्रकूर्चिका
तक्रकूर्च्चिका f. (-का) Inspissated buttermilk.<BR> E. तक्र, and कूर्च्चिक । inspissat-<BR>ed milk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=300-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तक्रमांस|तक्रमांसं
तक्रमांस n. (-सं) Meat fried with ghee, turmeric and asafœtida, &c.<BR>eaten with buttermilk.<BR> E. तक्र, and मांस flesh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=300-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तक्राट|तक्राटः
तक्राट m. (-टः) A churning stick.<BR> E. तक्र buttermilk, and अट what goes or<BR>is, (from it)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=300-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तक्ष
तक्ष r. 1st cl. (तक्षति)<BR>	 1. To cover.<BR>	 2. To skin or peel. (ऊ) तक्षू of 1st cl.<BR>(तक्ष्णोति) To pare, to plane, to make thin, to cut off to chip or slice;<BR>used in any other sense, this root takes the regular form only,<BR>whether simple or compound, as with सम् prefixed, To censure,<BR>(सन्तक्षति,) &c. भ्वा-पक्षे स्वादि-पर-सक-सेट् (चाचा छोला) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=301-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तक्षक|तक्षकः
तक्षक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A carpenter.<BR>	 2. The Sutradhara, the manager and<BR>chief actor in the prelude of a drama.<BR>	 3. One of the principal<BR>Nagas or serpents of Pātāla.<BR>	 4. The divine artist, VISWAKARMA.<BR>5. The name of a tree.<BR> E. तक्ष् to chip, to peel or plane, &c. affix ण्वुल्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=301-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तक्षण|तक्षणं
तक्षण n. (-णं) Paring, peeling, planing, &c.<BR>	 f. (-णी) A carpenter's adze.<BR>E. तक्ष् to plane or pare, affixes भावे ल्युट् and ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=301-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तक्षशिला
तक्षशिला f. (-ला) The name of a city, the Taxila of Ptolemy in the<BR>Punjab.<BR> E. तक्ष paring, शिला stone, built of hewn stones.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=301-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तक्षन्
तक्षन् m. (-क्षा) A carpenter.<BR> E. तक्ष् to pare, Uṇādi affix कनिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=301-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तग
तग (इ) तगि r. 1st cl. (तङ्गति)<BR>	 1. To go or move.<BR>	 2. To quake, to shake or<BR>tremble.<BR>	 3. To trip, to stumble. भ्वा-पर-सक-सेट् इदित् । स्खलने कम्पेच अक०<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=301-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तगर|तगरं|तगरः
तगर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A shrub, (Tabernæmontana coronaria.)<BR>	 2. A thorny<BR>shrub, (Vangueria spinosa.)<BR>	 3. Another plant, commonly Tagara-<BR>mula. गॄ अच् । तस्य क्रोडस्य गरः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=301-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तगरपादिका
तगरपादिका f. (-का) A plant; also Tagaramula.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=301-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तङ्क|तंक|तंकः|तङ्कः
तङ्क m. (-ङ्कः)<BR>	 1. An axe, a crow, a stone cutter's chisel: see टङ्क.<BR>	 2. Grief<BR>upon separation from a beloved object.<BR>	 3. Fear, terror.<BR>	 4. Wearing<BR>cloth.<BR>	 5. Living in distress.<BR> E. तकि to be in distress, &c. affix अच्. भावे<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=301-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तज्ज
तज्ज mfn. (-ज्जः-ज्जा-ज्जं) Immediate, instantaneous.<BR> E. तत् that, (that<BR>moment,) and ज born. ततो जायते जन ड ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=301-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तञ्च
तञ्च (उ) तञ्चु r. 1st cl. (तञ्चति) To go, (ऊ) तञ्चू r. 7th cl. (तनक्ति) To shrink<BR>or contract; also तञ्ज.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=301-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तञ्ज
तञ्ज (ऊ) तञ्जू r. 7th cl. (तनक्ति) To shrink or contract.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=301-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तट|तटं|तटः
तट r. 1st cl. (तटति) To be elevated or high, to rise. r. 10th cl. (ताटयतिते) To beat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=301-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तट|तटं|तटः
तट mfn. sub. (-टः-टा-टी-टं) A shore or bank.<BR>	 n. (-टं) A field.<BR> E. तट to<BR>to rise or be high, affix अच्, fem. aff. ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=301-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तटस्थ|तटस्थं|तटस्थः
तटस्थ mfn. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थं)<BR>	 1. Indifferent, alien, neuter.<BR>	 2. Situated on<BR>the bank or shore.<BR>	 m. (-स्थः) An indifferent person, one neither a<BR>friend nor a foe.<BR>	 n. (-स्थं) That property which is distinct from<BR>the nature of any thing, yet is the faculty by which it is known:<BR>in other words, spiritual essence unconnected with bodily wants or<BR>passions.<BR> E. तट a bank, a weight, and स्थ who stands. तटे ममीपे तिष्ठति<BR>स्था-क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=301-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तटाक|तटाकं|तटाकः
तटाक m. (-कः) A pond deep enough for the lotus and other aquatic<BR>flowers.<BR> E. तट a band, and अक् to go, affix अच्; or तट-आकन् also<BR>तडाक; also ताटाक and तटीक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=301-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तटिनी
तटिनी f. (-नी) A river.<BR> E. तट a bank, and इनि poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=301-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तड
तड r. 10th cl. (ताडयतिते)<BR>	 1. To beat, to strike.<BR>	 2. To shine: (इ) तडि.<BR>r. 1st cl. (तण्डते) To strike or beat. चु० उभ० सेट । दीप्तौ अक० आहतौ<BR>सक० आहतौ भ्वा० आ० सक० सेट् इदित् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=301-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तडग|तडगः
तडग m. (-गः) A pond, a tank: see तडाग.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=301-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तडाक|तडाकः
तडाक m. (-कः) A pond or pool, one deep enough for the lotus.<BR>	 f.<BR>(-क्रा)<BR>	 1. A bank, a shore.<BR>	 2. A blow.<BR> E. तड् to beat, Uṇādi affix<BR>आक; also तटाक and तडाग.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=301-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तडाग|तडागं|तडागः
तडाग m. (-गः)<BR>	 1. A pond, a pool, deep enough for the growth of the<BR>lotus, &c. See the preceding.<BR>	 2. A trap for catching deer. E.<BR>तड् to beat, affix आग, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=301-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तडाघात|तडाघातः
तडाघात m. (-तः) A blow from an elephant's uplifted trunk.<BR> E. तडा a<BR>beating, and आघात a blow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=301-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तडित्
तडित् f. (-डित्) Lightning.<BR> E. तड् to strike or beat, Uṇādi affix इति striking the earth, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=301-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तडित्वत्|तडित्वन्त्
तडित्वत् mfn. (-त्वान्-त्वती-त्वत्) Lightning, emitting lightning, flashing.<BR>m. (-त्वान्) A cloud.<BR> E. तडित् lightning, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=301-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तडिल्लता
तडिल्लता f. (-ता) Forked lightning.<BR> E. तडित्, and लता a creeper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=301-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तण्डक|तंडक|तंडकः|तण्डकः
तण्डक mn. (-कः-कं) Complete performance or preparation.<BR>	 m. (-कः)<BR>1. A wag-tail.<BR>	 2. Froth, foam.<BR>	 3. The trunk of a tree.<BR>	 4. The up-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=301-b" target="_blank">Page301-b+ 60</a>]<BR>right post of a house.<BR>	 5. A compound word.<BR>	 6. A juggler. a<BR>cheat.<BR> E. तडि to beat or kill, affix ण्वुल्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=301-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तण्डु|तण्डुः
तण्डु m. (-ण्डुः) One of ŚIVA'S doorkeepers, and one of the original<BR>teachers of the arts of dancing and mimicry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=301-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तण्डुरीण|तंडुरीणः|तण्डुरीणः
तण्डुरीण m. (-णः)<BR>	 1. A worm, an insect.<BR>	 2. A fool, a blockhead.<BR>	 3. The<BR>water in which rice has been soaked or steeped.<BR> E. तण्डुल rice, &c.<BR>ख affix, and ल changed to र. or तण्डा अस्त्यर्थे उरच् तढ भवः खः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=301-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तण्डुल|तंडुल|तंडुलः|तण्डुलः
तण्डुल m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. Grain after threshing and winnowing, especially rice.<BR>2. A vermifuge plant: see विडङ्ग.<BR>	 3. A potherb, a sort of Ama-<BR>ranth, (A. polygonoides.)<BR> E. तड् to beat, Uṇādi affix उलच्, and नुम्<BR>inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=301-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तण्डुजाम्बु
तण्डुजाम्बु f. (-म्बुः) Rice water or gruel.<BR> E. तण्डुल, and अम्बु water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=301-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तण्डुलीक|तण्डुलीकः
तण्डुलीक m. (-कः) A sort of Amaranth.<BR> E. ईकन् added to the preceding;<BR>also तण्डुलीय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=301-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तण्डुलीय|तण्डुलीयः
तण्डुलीय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. A kind of Amaranth. (A. polygonoides.)<BR>	 2. Bidanga<BR>a vermifuge.<BR>	 3. A mineral, iron pyrites.<BR> E. तण्डुल grain, (to which<BR>the seeds, &c. are compared. and छ affix; also तण्डुलीयक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=301-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तण्डुलु|तण्डुलुः
तण्डुलु f. (-लुः) A plant of which the seeds are used as a vermifuge:<BR>see विडङ्ग.<BR> E. तडि to beat, affix उलु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=301-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तण्डुलेर|तण्डुलेरः
तण्डुलेर m. (-रः) A sort of Amaranth: see तण्डुलीय, &c.<BR> E. तण्डुल, and<BR>एरक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=301-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तण्डुलोदक|तण्डुलोदकं
तण्डुलोदक n. (-कं) Water in which rice has been boiled, rice gruel. E.<BR>तण्डुल, and उदक water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=301-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तण्डुलौघ|तण्डुलौघः
तण्डुलौघ m. (-घः) A prickly sort of bamboo, (Bambusa spinosa.)<BR>	 2. A<BR>heap of grain.<BR> E. तण्डुल grain &c. or (as derived from तडि to bent,<BR>to tear,) a thorn, ओघ a heap or quantity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=301-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तत्
तत् ind. Therefore, thence, the consequent or correlative to यत्.<BR> E. तन्<BR>to spread, or extend, affix क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=301-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ततःप्रभृति
ततःप्रभृति ind. Thenceforth.<BR> E. ततस्, and प्रभृति the rest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=301-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तत|ततं|ततः
तत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Spread, diffused, expanded.<BR>	 2. Stretched, extend-<BR>ed.<BR>	 m. (-तः) Air, wind.<BR>	 n. (-तं) Any stringed instrument.<BR> E. तन् to<BR>spread, &c. क्त affix, or Uṇādi aff. तन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=301-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ततचिह्न
ततचिह्न mfn. (-ह्नः-ह्ना-ह्नं) Distinctly marked.<BR> E. तत, and चिह्न a mark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=301-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ततपत्री
ततपत्री f. (-त्री) The plantain tree.<BR> E. तत spread, and पत्री leaf, broad-<BR>leaved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=301-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ततम|ततमः
ततम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं) That one, (of many.)<BR> E. तद् that, and डतमच् affix<BR>of the superlative degree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=301-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ततर|ततरः
ततर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) That one, (of two.)<BR> E. तद् that, and डतरच् affix of<BR>the comparative degree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=301-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ततस्
ततस् ind.<BR>	 1. Therefore, thence, consequently.<BR>	 2. From that, then.<BR>3. Then, how, (asking.)<BR>	 4. Then, further, after that (continuation.)<BR>5. Afterwards, subsequently.<BR>	 6. Thither, there.<BR> E. तद् that, affix<BR>तसि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=301-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ततस्ततस्
ततस्ततस् ind.<BR>	 1. Hither and thither.<BR>	 2. Then after that, what next;<BR>(asking impatiently.)<BR> E. ततस् reiterated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=301-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ततस्त्य|ततस्त्यं
ततस्त्य mfn. (-स्त्यः-स्त्या-स्त्यं) Of or relating to that, &c.<BR> E. ततस् as above,<BR>त्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=301-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तति|ततिः
तति mfn. plu. (ततयः ततयः ततीनि) So many.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=301-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तति|ततिः
तति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. A line, a row or range.<BR>	 2. A number, a crowd.<BR> E. तन् to<BR>spread, affix क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=301-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तत्कर
तत्कर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Obeying, serving, a servant.<BR> E. तत्, and कर who<BR>does.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=301-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तत्काल|तत्कालः
तत्काल m. (-लः) Present time, time being, or the time when an act<BR>occurs.<BR> E. तत् that, काल time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=301-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तत्कालधी
तत्कालधी m. (-धीः) A man wise or intelligent for the time being, one<BR>having presence of mind, &c.<BR> E. तत्काल time being, and धी under<BR>standing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=301-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तत्क्रिय|तत्क्रियः
तत्क्रिय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Working without hire or wages.<BR> E. तत् thence,<BR>क्रिया business.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=301-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तत्क्षण|तत्क्षणः
तत्क्षण n. (-णं) Time present, time being.<BR> E. तद् that, and क्षण moment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=301-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तत्त्व|तत्त्वं
तत्त्व n. (-त्त्वं)<BR>	 1. Essential nature, the real nature of the human soul,<BR>considered as one and the same with the divine spirit<BR>animating the universe: the philosophical etymology of this<BR>word best explains its meaning, तद् that, that divine being, and त्व<BR>thou, that very God art thou.<BR>	 2. The Supreme being, or BRAMHA.<BR>3. Truth, reality, substance, opposed to what is illusory or<BR>fallacious.<BR>	 4. An element or elementary property, differently<BR>enumerated in different system from the three which are<BR>the same with the three Gunas, to twenty-seven, which in-<BR>clude the elements, organs, faculties, matter, spirit, life, and God.<BR>5. A first principle, an axiom.<BR>	 6. Mind, intellect.<BR>	 7. Slow time in<BR>music.<BR>	 8. A musical instrument. E. As above, or तद् that, then &c.<BR>affix त्व; the word is properly, therefore, written तत्त्व, but in books<BR>one त is commonly rejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=302-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तत्त्वज्ञान|तत्त्वज्ञानं
तत्त्वज्ञान n. (-नं) Knowledge of divine truth.<BR> E. तत्त्व as above, and ज्ञान<BR>knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=302-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तत्त्वतस्
तत्त्वतस् ind. Truly, accurately, fully.<BR> E. तत्त्व, and तसिल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=302-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तत्त्वन्यास|तत्त्वन्यासः
तत्त्वन्यास m. (-सः) Touching different parts of the body in the worship<BR>of VIṢṆU.<BR> E. तत्त्व, and न्यास gesticulation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=302-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तत्त्वविद्
तत्त्वविद् mfn. (-वित्) Knowing the truth, knowing things as they are.<BR>E. तत्त्व, and विद् who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=302-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तत्त्वावबोध
तत्त्वावबोध m. (-धः) Knowledge of spirit.<BR> E. तत्त्व, and अवबोध ascertain-<BR>ment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=302-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तत्त्वाभियोग|तत्त्वाभियोगः
तत्त्वाभियोग m. (-गः) A positive charge or declaration.<BR> E. तत्त्व, and अमि-<BR>योग accusation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=302-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तत्पर|तत्परः
तत्पर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>	 1. Diligent, attending to any thing closely and an-<BR>xiously.<BR>	 2. Belonging to a principal object or intent of.<BR>	 m. (-रः)<BR>The thirtieth part of the time of the twinkling of the eye.<BR> E. तत्<BR>that, पर addicted to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=302-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तत्परायण|तत्परायणः
तत्परायण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Attached or addicted to some particular thing<BR>or person.<BR> E. तद् that, परायण attached to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=302-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तत्पूर्व|तत्पूर्व्व
तत्पूर्व mfn. (-र्वः-र्वा-र्वं) Prior, former.<BR> E. तत्, and पूर्व before.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=302-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तत्पुरुष|तत्पुरुषः
तत्पुरुष m. (-षः)<BR>	 1. That or a certain person.<BR>	 2. A form of composition,<BR>(in Grammar,) usually consisting of two nouns, the first of which<BR>was in any case except the nominative or vocative; sometimes<BR>the inflection of the case is retained.<BR> E. तत् that, and पुरुष man or<BR>person.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=302-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तत्फल|तत्फलः
तत्फल mfn. (-लः-ली-लं) Resulting from any particular act, &c.<BR>	 m. (-लः)<BR>1. The white water lily.<BR>	 2. A fragrant grass.<BR> E. तद्, and फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=302-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तत्र
तत्र (इ) तत्रि r. 10th cl. (तन्त्रयते)<BR>	 1. To spread, to extend or expand.<BR>2. To nourish or support a family, &c. चु० आ० सक० सेट् इदित् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=302-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तत्र
तत्र ind. There, therein, the relative to अत्र.<BR> E. तद् that, त्रल् affix, in lieu<BR>of the proper seventh case.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=302-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तत्रत्य|तत्रत्यः
तत्रत्य mfn. (-त्यः-त्या-त्यं) Produced there or in a certain place.<BR> E. तत्र, and<BR>त्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=302-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तत्रभवत्|तत्रभवन्त्
तत्रभवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Venerable, respectable, reverend.<BR> E. तत्र<BR>therein. (in all things) भवत् pre-eminent: see अत्रभवत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=302-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तत्व|तत्वं
तत्व n. (-त्वं) See तत्त्व.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=302-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तथा
तथा ind.<BR>	 1. So, like, correlative to यथा as, &c.<BR>	 2. Thus, (implying certain-<BR>ty.)<BR>	 3. So, so be it, (implying assent or promise.)<BR>	 4. Thus, then,<BR>therefore, (or reply.)<BR>	 5. And, so, in (conjunction.)<BR> E. तद् in that,<BR>थाल् affix, implying manner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=302-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तथागत|तथागतः
तथागत m. (-तः) A Jina or Buddha.<BR> E. तथा thus, (what really is,) and<BR>गत known, obtained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=302-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तथाच
तथाच ind. And so, thus, even so likewise.<BR> E. तथा with च and.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=302-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तथात्व|तथात्वं
तथात्व n. (-त्वं) Being so; the case or circumstance being admitted to be<BR>as stated.<BR> E. तथा, and त्व aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=302-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तथापि
तथापि ind. Nevertheless, yet, even.<BR> E. तथा, and अपि even.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=302-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तथाविध
तथाविध mfn. (-धः-धा-धं) Of such a sort or kind.<BR> E. तथा and विध sort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=302-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तथाराज|तथाराजः
तथाराज m. (-जः) A Jina or Buddha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=302-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तथैव
तथैव ind. So, even so, in the same manner.<BR> E. तथा, and एव thus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=302-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तथ्य|तथ्यं
तथ्य mfn. (-थ्यः-थ्या-थ्यं) True.<BR>	 n. (-थ्यं) Truth.<BR> E. तथा thus, (what is really<BR>so,) and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=302-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तद्
तद् Relative or third personal pronoun. (सः सा तद्) He, she, it, that<BR>man, that woman, that thing.<BR> E. तन् to extend or spread, Uṇādi<BR>affix अदि. डिच्च.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=302-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तद्
तद् (इ) तदि r. 1st cl. (तन्दते) To be content or happy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=302-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तदतिपात
तदतिपात mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Transgressing, going beyond the bounds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=302-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तदनन्तर
तदनन्तर n. adv. (-रं) Next, afterwards.<BR> E. तत् that, अनन्तर after.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=302-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तदन्त|तदंत
तदन्त n. adv. (-न्तं) To that end, just so far.<BR> E. तद्, and अन्त end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=302-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तदर्थ
तदर्थ mfn. (-र्थः-र्था-र्थं)<BR>	 1. On that account, with that object.<BR>	 2. Hav-<BR>ing such a meaning.<BR> E. तद्, and अर्थ sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=302-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तदर्पण
तदर्पण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. A thing returned.<BR>	 2. Delivering any article.<BR> E. तद्,<BR>and अर्पण delivery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=302-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तदा
तदा ind. Then, at that time.<BR> E. तद् that, दाच् affix, implying time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=302-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तदात्व|तदात्वं
तदात्व n. (-त्वं) Time being, time present.<BR> E. तदा then, त्व affix of the<BR>abstract.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=302-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तदानीम्
तदानीम् ind. Then, at that time.<BR> E. तद् that, दानीम् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=302-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तदाप्रभृति
तदाप्रभृति ind. Thenceforward.<BR> E. तदा, and प्रभृति the rest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=302-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तदामुख|तदामुखं
तदामुख n. (-खं) Commencement, beginning.<BR> E. तदा, and मुख beginning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=302-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तदीय
तदीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) That, that person, that thing.<BR> E. तद्, and छ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=302-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तद्दिनम्
तद्दिनम् ind.<BR>	 1. In the course of the day.<BR>	 2. Day by day.<BR>	 n. (-नं) On a<BR>certain day.<BR> E. तद् that, and दिन a day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=302-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तद्धन|तद्धनः
तद्धन mfn. (-नः-ना-न) Miserly, niggardly.<BR> E. तत् thence, धन wealth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=302-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तद्वत्|तद्वन्त्
तद्वत् ind. So, in like manner, the correlative to यद्वत् as.<BR> E. तद् that,<BR>वति aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=302-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तद्वला
तद्वला f. (-ला) A sort of arrow.<BR> E. तत् thence, वल strong.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=302-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तद्विध
तद्विध mfn. (-धः-धा-धं) In that manner, in such a manner, of such a<BR>kind or sort.<BR> E. तद्, and विध way.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=302-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तद्धित|तद्धितः
तद्धित m. (-तः) A derivative noun, as a patronymic or attributive of vari-<BR>ous kinds, &c.<BR>	 n. (-तं) The formation of such nouns.<BR> E. तत् that,<BR>(original noun,) हित what relates to or suits.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=302-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन|तनः
तन (उ) तनु r. 8th cl. (तनोति-तनुते) To expand, to spread, to extend, to<BR>diffuse, to dilate, &c. physically or morally. r. 1st and 10th cls.<BR>(तनति तानयतिते)<BR>	 1. To confide, to believe or have faith in.<BR>	 2. To aid,<BR>to assist.<BR>	 3. To be harmless.<BR>	 4. To sound.<BR>	 5. To pain or afflict with<BR>disease.<BR>	 6. (With a preposition,) To lengthen, to stretch, to expand,<BR>&c. as in the 8th cl.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=302-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनय|तनयः
तनय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. A son.<BR>	 2. A male descendant.<BR>	 f. (-या)<BR>	 1. A daughter.<BR>2. A plant: see चक्रकुल्या.<BR> E. तन् to spread, (to extend the family or<BR>name,) कयन् Uṇādi aff. तनोति कुलम् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=302-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनिष्ठ|तनिष्ठः
तनिष्ठ mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठा-ष्ठं)<BR>	 1. Smaller, less.<BR>	 2. Minute, delicate, small. E.<BR>तनु, and इष्ठन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=302-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनीयस्
तनीयस् mfn. (-यान्-यसी-यः)<BR>	 1. Smallest, least.<BR>	 2. Very small or delicate,<BR>&c.<BR> E. तनु, and ईयसुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=302-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनु|तनुः
तनु mfn. (-नुः-नुः or -न्वी or -नूः-नु)<BR>	 1. Small, minute.<BR>	 2. Delicate, fine, but<BR>with interestics.<BR>	 3. Thin, slender, emaciated.<BR>	 4. Little.<BR>	 f. (-नु<BR>नूः)<BR>	 1. The body.<BR>	 2. The skin.<BR>	 f. (-नुः)<BR>	 1. A woman.<BR>	 2. Point of<BR>conjunction, or sun's entrance into a new sign.<BR>	 f. (-नी)<BR>	 1. A deli-<BR>cate or slender woman.<BR>	 2. A stanza of four lines, and twenty-four<BR>syllables in each: a variety of the Sankriti metre.<BR> E. तन् to<BR>stretch or spread, Uṇādi affix उ; also तनू and तनुस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=302-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनुकूप|तनुकूपः
तनुकूप n. (-पः) A pore of skin.<BR> E. तनु, and कूप a well.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=302-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनुच्छद्
तनुच्छद् mfn. (-छत्) Covering (the body,) clothing, protecting.<BR>	 f. (-छत्)<BR>1. Armour.<BR>	 2. Attire.<BR> E. तनु, and छद् to cover, affix क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=302-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनुज|तनुजः
तनुज m. (-जः) A son.<BR>	 f. (-जा) A daughter.<BR> E. तनु body, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=302-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनुत्र|तनुत्रं
तनुत्र n. (-त्रं) Armour, mail.<BR> E. तनु the body, and त्र what preserves; also<BR>तनुत्राण n. (-णं.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=302-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनुत्रवत्|तनुत्रवन्त्
तनुत्रवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Armed, defended.<BR> E. तनुत्र, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=302-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनुत्याग
तनुत्याग mfn. (-गः-गा-गं) Niggardly, sparing, letting little go to be spent.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=303-a" target="_blank">Page303-a+ 60</a>]<BR>m. (-गः) Quitting the body, death.<BR> E. तनु little or the body, त्याग<BR>parting with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=302-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनुभस्त्रा
तनुभस्त्रा f. (-स्त्रा) The noise.<BR> E. तनु the body, and भस्त्रा a bellow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=303-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनुमत्|तनुमन्त्
तनुमत् mfn. (-मान्-मतो-मत्) Embodied, corporeal.<BR> E. तनु, and मतुप्<BR>aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=303-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनुमध्या
तनुमध्या f. (-ध्या)<BR>	 1. A woman with a slender or elegant waist.<BR>	 2. A<BR>species of the Gayatri metre.<BR> E. तनु, and मध्य middle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=303-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनुरस|तनुरसः
तनुरस m. (-सः) Perspiration, sweat.<BR> E. तनु the body, and रस juice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=303-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनुरुह|तनुरुहं
तनुरुह n. (-हं) The hair or down of the body.<BR> E. तनु, and रुह what<BR>grows: also with the final consonant. तनुरुह् n. (-रुट्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=303-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनुल|तनुलः
तनुल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Spread, expanded.<BR> E. तनु to spread, उलच् Uṇādi<BR>affix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=303-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनुवात|तनुवातः
तनुवात m. (-तः) A division of hell.<BR> E. तनु thin, small, and वात wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=303-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनुवार
तनुवार n. (-रं) Armour.<BR> E. तनु, वृ to defend, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=303-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनुवारभस
तनुवारभस m. (-सः) A warrior, a man in armour.<BR> E. तनुवार and भस who<BR>shines.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=303-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनुव्रण|तनुव्रणः
तनुव्रण m. (-णः) A pimple, a pustule, a boil.<BR> E. तनु slight, and व्रण a<BR>sore.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=303-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनुस्
तनुस् n. (-नुः) The body.<BR> E. तन् to stretch, Uṇādi affix उसि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=303-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनुसञ्चारिणी|तनुसंचारिणी
तनुसञ्चारिणी f. (-णी)<BR>	 1. A young woman, a girl, one of ten years old. E.<BR>तनु the body, सञ्चारिणी who makes perfect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=303-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनू
तनू f. (-नूः) The body.<BR> E. तन् to stretch, affix ऊः see तनु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=303-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनूकृत|तनूकृतः
तनूकृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Pared, made delicate or thin.<BR> E. तनु thin, कृत made,<BR>and उ rendered long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=303-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनूज|तनूजः
तनूज m. (-जः) A son.<BR>	 f. (-जा) A daughter.<BR> E. तनू, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=303-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनूजनि
तनूजनि m. (-निः) A son.<BR> E. तनू body, and जनि birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=303-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनून|तनूनः
तनून m. (-नः) The wind.<BR> E. तनू body, ऊन defective.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=303-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनूनप|तनूनपं
तनूनप n. (-पं) Clarified butter or ghee.<BR> E. तनु the body, and ऊन defici-<BR>ency, thinness, spareness of body, and प what cherishes; what<BR>fattens.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=303-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनूनपाद्
तनूनपाद् m. (-पाद् or पात्) Fire or its deity.<BR> E. तनूनप ghee, and अद् who<BR>eats, from अद with विच् affix, or तनू the body, न negative, and पा<BR>to preserve, deriv. irr. destroying other bodies, or consuming its<BR>own support or fuel, and ceasing to be.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=303-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनूरुह|तनूरुहं|तनूरुहः
तनूरुह mn. (-हः-हं)<BR>	 1. The hair of the body.<BR>	 2. The wing of a bird.<BR>m. (-हः) A son.<BR> E. तनु or तनू the the body, and रुह what grows or<BR>rises, from रुह् with क affix; also तनुरुह.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=303-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनूह्रद|तनूह्रदः
तनूह्रद m. (-दः) The anus, the rectum.<BR> E. तनू the body, and ह्रद a deep<BR>place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=303-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्ति|तंतिः|तन्तिः
तन्ति m. (-न्तिः) A weaver.<BR>	 f. (-न्तिः) Expantion, extension.<BR> E. तन् to<BR>stretch, affix क्तिच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=303-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्तु|तंतु|तंतुः|तन्तुः
तन्तु m. (-न्तुः)<BR>	 1. A thread.<BR>	 2. A shark.<BR>	 3. Offspring, race, descendants.<BR>E. तन् to spread or stretch, Uṇādi affix तुन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=303-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्तुक|तंतुक|तंतुकः|तन्तुकः
तन्तुक m. (-कः) Mustard seed.<BR>	 f. (-की) A vein or any tubular vessel:<BR>see तन्तुभ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=303-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्तुकाष्ठ|तंतुकाष्ठ|तन्तुकाष्ठं
तन्तुकाष्ठ n. (-ष्ठं) A piece of fibrous wood, or a brush used by weavers for<BR>cleaning the threads of the woof.<BR> E. तन्तु a weaver's thread, and काष्ठ<BR>a wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=303-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्तुकीट|तंतुकीट|तन्तुकीटः
तन्तुकीट m. (-टः) A silk-worm.<BR> E. तन्तु a thread, and कीट a worm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=303-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्तुण|तंतुणः|तन्तुणः
तन्तुण m. (-णः) A shark.<BR> E. तन् to spread, तुण aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=303-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्तुनाग|तंतुनाग|तन्तुनागः
तन्तुनाग m. (-गः) A shark.<BR> E. तन्तु, and नाग a snake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=303-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्तुनिर्य्यास|तन्तुनिर्यास|तंतुनिर्यास|तन्तुनिर्यासः
तन्तुनिर्य्यास m. (-सः) A palmyra tree.<BR> E. तन्तु thread, and निर्य्यास exudation,<BR>alluding to its stringy or adhesive nature.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=303-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्तुपर्व्वन्|तन्तुपर्वन्
तन्तुपर्व्वन् n. (-र्व्व) The full moon of Sravana, when KṚṢṆA is invested<BR>with the Brahmanical cord.<BR> E. तन्तु, and पर्व्वन् a festival.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=303-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्तुभ|तंतुभ|तन्तुभः
तन्तुभ m. (-भः)<BR>	 1. Mustard seed, (Sinapis dichotoma;) also sometimes<BR>तन्तुका.<BR>	 2. A calf.<BR> E. तन्तु a thread, and भा to shine, affix क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=303-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्तुर|तंतुर|तंतुरं|तन्तुरं
तन्तुर n. (-रं) See the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=303-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्तुल|तंतुल|तंतुलं|तन्तुलं
तन्तुल n. (-लं) The filaments or fibrous root of the lotus.<BR> E. तन्तु a thread,<BR>and ल what has; also with र, तन्तुर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=303-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्तुवाप|तंतुवाप|तन्तुवापः
तन्तुवाप m. (-पः)<BR>	 1. A weaver.<BR>	 2. A loom.<BR> E. तन्तु a thread वप् to weave,<BR>affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=303-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्तुवाय|तंतुवाय|तन्तुवायः
तन्तुवाय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. A weaver.<BR>	 2. A spider.<BR> E. तन्तु a thread, वे to weave,<BR>अण् affix; also तन्त्रवाय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=303-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्तुविग्रहा|तंतुविग्रहा
तन्तुविग्रहा f. (-हा) The banana or plantain.<BR> E. तन्तु a thread, and विग्रह a<BR>part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=303-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्तुशाला|तंतुशाला
तन्तुशाला f. (-ला) A weaver's shop.<BR> E. तन्तु weaving, and शाला a house or<BR>hall.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=303-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्तुसन्तत|तन्तुसंतत|तंतुसंतत|तन्तुसन्ततं
तन्तुसन्तत n. (-तं) Woven cloth.<BR> E. तन्तु a thread, and सन्तत collected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=303-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्तुसार|तंतुसार|तन्तुसारः
तन्तुसार m. (-रः) The betelnut tree; also तन्तुसारक.<BR> E. तन्तु a thread, and<BR>सार pith; having a stringy pith.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=303-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्त्र|तंत्र|तंत्रं|तन्त्रं
तन्त्र mfn. (-न्त्रः-न्त्रा-न्त्रं) Dependant, subservient.<BR>	 m. (-न्त्रः) A weaver.<BR>	 f.<BR>(-न्त्री)<BR>	 1. Any string or rope.<BR>	 2. The wire or string of a lute.<BR>3. Any tubular vessel of the body.<BR>	 4. A plant, (Menispermum<BR>glabrum:) see गूडुची.<BR>	 5. The name of a river.<BR>	 6. A young<BR>woman.<BR>	 n. (-न्त्रं)<BR>	 1. A Tantra, a religious treatise teaching<BR>peculiar and mystical formulæ and rites for the worship of the<BR>deities, or the attainment of superhuman power: it is mostly in the<BR>form of a dialogue between ŚIVA and DURGĀ, who are the peculiar<BR>gods of the Tantrikas: there is a great number of these works, and<BR>their authority, in many parts of India, seems to have, in a great<BR>measure, superseded that of the Vedas: according to one account,<BR>a Tantra comprises five subjects, the creation and destruction of<BR>the world, the worship of the gods, the attainment of all objects,<BR>magical rites for the acquirement of six (superhuman) faculties,<BR>and four modes of union with spirit by meditation; a variety of<BR>subjects are, however, introduced many of them, whilst some are<BR>limited to a single topic, as the mode of breathing in certain rites,<BR>the language of birds, beasts, &c.<BR>	 2. A branch of the Vedas, that<BR>which teaches Mantra or mystical and magical formulæ.<BR>	 3. Demon-<BR>stration, clear and right conclusion.<BR>	 4. Raiment, vesture.<BR>	 5. A me-<BR>dicament, a drug.<BR>	 6. A principal medicament, or perhaps a charm<BR>considered as producing medicinal effects.<BR>	 7. Providing for a fami-<BR>ly.<BR>	 8. A cause, a motive.<BR>	 9. Cause common to two or more results;<BR>the instruments or means of more than one effect.<BR>	 10. Necessary or<BR>indispensable act or provision; the right way of doing any thing.<BR>11. Chief, principal.<BR>	 12. A royal retinue, a court, a train.<BR>	 13. An<BR>army.<BR>	 14. A royal property: that of providing for the security and<BR>prosperity of the kingdom.<BR>	 15. A realm, a country.<BR>	 16. A thread,<BR>17. Subservience, service, dependence.<BR>	 18. Oath or ordeal.<BR>	 19. De-<BR>corations, hanging with trophies, garlands, &c.<BR>	 20. Heap, multitude.<BR>21. Wealth.<BR>	 22. A house.<BR>	 23. An implement or weaving a loom.<BR>24. Happiness, felicity.<BR> E. तन to spread or extend, affix ष्ट्रन्; or<BR>तत्रि to spread, to support a family, &c. affix क, fem. affix ङीप्; or<BR>तन्त्र with ई Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=303-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्त्रक|तंत्रक|तन्त्रकं|तंत्रकः|तन्त्रकः
तन्त्रक n. (-कं) New and unbleached cloth.<BR> E. तन्त्र the loom, and कन् affix,<BR>recently from the loom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=303-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्त्रकाष्ठ|तंत्रकाष्ठ|तन्त्रकाष्ठं
तन्त्रकाष्ठ n. (-ष्ठं) A fibrous stick for cleaning the woof, &c.<BR> E. तन्त्र weav-<BR>ing, and काष्ठ wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=303-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्त्रता|तंत्रता
तन्त्रता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Dependence, subservience.<BR>	 2. The quality or character<BR>of a Tantra.<BR>	 3. Comprehending several rites in one, performance<BR>of one ceremony or penance in lien of a number.<BR> E. तन्त्र, and तल् add-<BR>ed; also with त्व तन्त्रत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=303-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्त्रवाप|तंत्रवाप|तन्त्रवापः
तन्त्रवाप m. (-पः) A weaver.<BR>	 mn. (-पः-पं) A loom.<BR> E. तन्त्र a thread, and वप्<BR>to weave, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=303-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्त्रवाय|तंत्रवाय|तन्त्रवायः
तन्त्रवाय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. A weaver.<BR>	 2. A spider.<BR> E. तन्त्र a thread, a web,<BR>and वे to spin or weave, affix घञ्; also तन्त्रवाप and sometimes<BR>तन्द्रवाय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=303-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्त्रिका
तन्त्रिका f. (-का) A plant, Gurichi.<BR> E. कन् added to तन्त्री.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=303-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्त्रिन्|तंत्रिन्
तन्त्रिन् mfn. (-त्री-त्रिणी-त्रि)<BR>	 1. Spun, wove, made of threads.<BR>	 2. Chorded,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=304-a" target="_blank">Page304-a+ 60</a>]<BR>having chords or wires, (as an instrument.)<BR>	 3. A musician.<BR>	 4. Hav-<BR>ing a Tantra, following one, &c.<BR> E. तन्त्र and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=303-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्त्रिपालक|तन्त्रिपालकः
तन्त्रिपालक m. (-कः) A name of JAYADRATHA.<BR> E. तन्त्रि (derived from तन्त्र<BR>any, army, with इनि affix,) a general, and पालक who cherish<BR>or aids.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=304-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्द्रवाय|तन्द्रवायः
तन्द्रवाय m. (-यः) A weaver: see तन्त्रवाय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=304-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्द्रा|तंद्रा
तन्द्रा f. (-न्द्रा)<BR>	 1. Lassitude, exhaustion, weariness, syncope.<BR>	 2. Sleepi-<BR>ness, sluggishness.<BR> E. तदि a Sautra root, to be weary, affix<BR>भावे अ; also with किन् affix तन्द्रि f. (-न्द्रिः) and with ङीप् added तन्द्री.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=304-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्द्रालु|तंद्रालु|तन्द्रालुः
तन्द्रालु mfn. (-लुः-लुः-लु) Slothful, sluggish, overcome with sleep or fati-<BR>gue.<BR> E. तन्द्र sloth, and आलुच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=304-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्द्रि|तंद्रि|तंद्रिः|तन्द्रिः
तन्द्रि f. (-न्द्रिः)<BR>	 1. Sleepiness.<BR>	 2. Lassitude.<BR>	 3. Fainting, exhaustion:<BR>see तन्द्रा. E. As above, or तदि Sautra root, to be weary, and क्रिन्<BR>Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=304-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्द्रिका|तंद्रिका
तन्द्रिका f. (-का) Sloth, sleepiness.<BR> E. कन् added to तन्द्री.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=304-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्द्री|तंद्री
तन्द्री f. (-न्द्री)<BR>	 1. Drowsiness.<BR>	 2. Lasitude: see तन्द्रा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=304-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्नि|तन्निः
तन्नि f. (-न्निः) A plant: see चक्रकुल्या.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=304-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्मात्र|तन्मात्रं
तन्मात्र n. sub. (-त्रं) The archetype or subtile rudiment of elementary<BR>matter. adv. Merely that.<BR> E. तत्, and मात्र only, or element. तदेव<BR>एवार्थे मात्रच् सा मात्रा यस्य वा ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=304-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्यतु|तन्यतुः
तन्यतु m. (-तुः)<BR>	 1. Night.<BR>	 2. A musical instrument.<BR> E. तन् to spread,<BR>यतुच् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=304-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्वत्|तन्वन्त्
तन्वत् mfn. (-न्वन्-न्वन्ती-न्वत्) Spreading, extending.<BR> E. तन् to spread,<BR>शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=304-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तप|तपः
तप (औ) तपौ r. 1st cl. (तपति-ते) r. 4th cl. (तप्यति-ते) and r. 10th cl. (ताप-<BR>यति-ते)<BR>	 1. To heat or be hot, to burn; (hence figuratively,) to<BR>suffer mental or bodily pain.<BR>	 2. To have pre-eminent or super-<BR>human power: the deponent form only is used when the root<BR>with the prefix उत् or वि occurs intransitively, or governs as its<BR>object part of the body of the agent, as पाणिं वितपते warms the<BR>hand, (उत्तपते वितपते) shines, burns, &c. The root takes the pas-<BR>sive form also, when implying religious meditation, as तप्यते तपस्ता-<BR>पसः the devotee revolves religious thoughts. With अनु prefixed,<BR>(अनुतपते) To repent, to regret. With परि or सम् (परितपति सन्तपति,)<BR>1. To bear or inflict pain, anguish, heat, distress, &c.<BR>	 2. To be<BR>sorrowful, to repent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=304-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपःकर|तपःकरः
तपःकर m. (-रः) The mango fish: see तपस्विन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=304-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपःकृश
तपःकृश mfn. (-शः-शा-शं) Emaciated by austerities.<BR> E. तपस्, and कृश lean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=304-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपःक्लेशसह|तपःक्लेशसहः
तपःक्लेशसह mfn. (-हः-हा-हं) Patient of austerities.<BR> E. तपस् austere devo-<BR>tion, क्लेश fatigue, and सह bearing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=304-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपःस्थली
तपःस्थली f. (-ली) A name of Benares.<BR> E. तपस् religious austerities, and<BR>स्थल soil, place, fem. affix ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=304-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तप|तपः
तप m. (-पः)<BR>	 1. The hot season, summer.<BR>	 2. Heat, warmth.<BR>	 3. The sun.<BR>E. तप् to heat, affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=304-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपत्|तपन्त्
तपत् mfn. (-पन्-पन्ती-पत्)<BR>	 1. Heating or warming.<BR>	 2. Performing pen-<BR>ance.<BR> E. तप् to heat, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=304-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपती
तपती f. (-ती)<BR>	 1. A name of CHHAYA, wife of the sun.<BR>	 2. Also of the<BR>daughter of the sun, or the personified Tapti river, married to<BR>SAMVARANA of the Kuru family.<BR> E. तप heat or the sun, and अत<BR>who accompanies, fem. affix ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=304-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपन|तपनः
तपन m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. The sun.<BR>	 2. A division of hell.<BR>	 3. Heat, burning.<BR>	 4.<BR>Mental distress, pining, grieving.<BR>	 5. The hot season.<BR>	 6. the<BR>marking nut plant.<BR>	 f. (-नी) The Godavari river.<BR> E. तप् to inflame,<BR>affixes भावे ल्यु and ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=304-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपनकर|तपनकरः
तपनकर m. (-रः) A ray, a sunbeam.<BR> E. तपन, and कर a ray.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=304-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपनतनय|तपनतनयः
तपनतनय m. (-यः) KARṆA, &c.<BR>	 f. (-या)<BR>	 1. The Yamuna river.<BR>	 2. The<BR>Tapti river.<BR> E. तपन the sun, and तनय child.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=304-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपनमणि|तपनमणिः
तपनमणि m. (-णिः) The sun-stone.<BR> E. तपन, and मणि a gem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=304-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपनांशु|तपनांशुः
तपनांशु m. (-शुः) A ray of the sun, a sun-beam.<BR> E. तपन, and अंशु<BR>ray.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=304-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपनात्मजा
तपनात्मजा f. (-जा)<BR>	 1. The Godavari river.<BR>	 2. The Yamuna or Jumana<BR>river.<BR> E. तपन the sun, and आत्मजा a daughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=304-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपनीय|तपनीयं
तपनीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>	 1. To be heated.<BR>	 2. To be suffered or practised<BR>as penance.<BR>	 n. (-यं) Gold.<BR> E. तप् to heat, &c. अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=304-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपनीयक|तपनीयकं
तपनीयक n. (-कं) Gold.<BR> E. तपनीय, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=304-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपनेष्ट|तपनेष्टं
तपनेष्ट n. (-ष्टं) Copper.<BR> E. तपन, and इष्ट liked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=304-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपस्
तपस् m. (-पाः)<BR>	 1. The name of a month, Magha, (January February.)<BR>2. The cold or dewy season.<BR>	 3. The hot season.<BR>	 n. (-पः)<BR>	 1. Religi-<BR>ous austerity, penance, mortification, the practice of mental or perso-<BR>nal self-denial, or the infliction of bodily tortures.<BR>	 2. A world, the<BR>region above the Janaloka, inhabited by saints or devotees after<BR>death.<BR>	 3. Virtue, moral merit.<BR>	 4. Duty, the special observance of<BR>certain things: thus the Tapas of a Brahman is sacred learning;<BR>of a Kṣatriya, the protection of subject; of a Vaiśya, almsgiving<BR>to Brahmans; of a Śūdra, the service of the same tribe; and of a<BR>Ṛṣi or saint, feeding upon herbs and roots.<BR> E. तप् to heat or in-<BR>flame, affix असुन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=304-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपस|तपसः
तपस m. (-सः)<BR>	 1. The moon.<BR>	 2. A bird.<BR> E. तप् to heat, असच् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=304-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपस्तक्ष|तपस्तक्षः
तपस्तक्ष m. (-क्षः) A name of INDRA.<BR> E. तपस् austerity, and तक्ष who<BR>pares or makes thin; emaciating himself by his devotions.<BR> E. तपस्त-<BR>क्षति तक्ष-अण् उप० स० । इन्द्रे ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=304-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपस्य|तपस्यं|तपस्यः
तपस्य m. (-स्यः)<BR>	 1. The month Phalguna, (February-March)<BR>	 2. A name<BR>of ARJUNA.<BR>	 f. (-स्या)<BR>	 1. Devout austerity, religious penance.<BR>	 n. (-स्यं)<BR>The flower of the Kunda, (Jasminum pubescens.)<BR> E. तपस् the<BR>cold season, यत् aff. तपशि साधु यत् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=304-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपस्विन्
तपस्विन् mfn. (-स्वी-स्विनी-स्वि)<BR>	 1. Devout practicing austerities.<BR>	 2. Poor<BR>wretched, pitiable.<BR>	 m. (-स्वी)<BR>	 1. An ascetic, a religious<BR>man engaged in the practice of rigorous and devout penance.<BR>2. A name of NĀRADA^1.<BR>	 3. A mendicant, a pauper.<BR>	 4. The<BR>mangoe fish, (Polynemus risua.)<BR>	 f. (-स्विनी)<BR>	 3. A female devotee,<BR>a woman leading a religious life.<BR>	 2. Spikenard, (Valeriana<BR>jatamansi.)<BR>	 3. Another plant: see कटुरोहिणी.<BR> E. तपस् religious aus-<BR>terity, the hot season, &c. अस्त्यर्थेविनि aff.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20260517. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/225.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=304-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपस्समाधि
तपस्समाधि m. (-धिः) The practice of penance.<BR> E. तपस्, and समाधि obliga-<BR>tion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=304-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपात्मक
तपात्मक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Practicing austerities.<BR> E. तप and आत्मक self.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=304-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपात्यय|तपात्ययः
तपात्यय m. (-यः) The rainy season.<BR> E. तप the warm season.<BR> E. अत्यय des-<BR>troying; following the hot weather. तपस्य ग्रीष्मस्य अत्ययः अवसानं यत्र<BR>काले । वर्षाकाले ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=304-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपित|तपितं
तपित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Heated, burnt.<BR> E. तप् to heat, affix क्त, with इट् inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=304-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपुस्
तपुस् m. (-पुः)<BR>	 1. Fire.<BR>	 2. The sun.<BR> E. तप् to heat, Uṇādi affix उसि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=304-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपोधन|तपोधनः
तपोधन m. (-नः) A devotee, an ascetic, one who performs religious pen-<BR>ance.<BR>	 f. (-ना) A plant: see मुण्डीरी.<BR> E. तपस religious austerity, and<BR>धन wealth तपोधनं यस्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=304-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपोनुभाव|तपोनुभावः
तपोऽनुभाव m. (-बः) The influence of religious penance.<BR> E. तपस् and अनु-<BR>भाव authority.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=304-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपोनिष्ठ
तपोनिष्ठ mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठा-ष्ठं) Performing penance, practising austerities. E.<BR>तपस् and निष्ठ engaged in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=304-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपोमय|तपोमयः
तपोमय mfn. (-यः-यी-यं) Devout, practising austerities.<BR> E. तपस् and<BR>मयट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=304-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपोमूर्त्ति|तपोमूर्ति|तपोमूर्तिः
तपोमूर्त्ति m. (-र्त्तिः) An ascetic.<BR> E. तपस् and मूर्त्ति form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=304-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपोराशि|तपोराशिः
तपोराशि m. (-शिः) An ascetic.<BR> E. तपस् and राशि a heap.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=304-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपोवट|तपोवटः
तपोवट m. (-टः) A country, part of central India or holy land.<BR> E. तपस्<BR>religious austerity, and वट what surrounds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=304-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपोवन
तपोवन n. (-नं) A sacred grove, a place frequented by asceties.<BR> E. तपस्,<BR>and वन a wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=304-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तप्त|तप्तः
तप्त mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं)<BR>	 1. Heated, Inflamed, burnt.<BR>	 2. Scorched by pain or<BR>sorrow, distressed, afflicted.<BR>	 3. Inflamed with anger, incensed 4.<BR>Undergone or performed as penance.<BR>	 5. Fused, melted.<BR>	 6. Burnish-<BR>ed.<BR> E. तप् to heat, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=304-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तप्तकुम्भ|तप्तकुम्भः
तप्तकुम्भ m. (-म्भः) A hell.<BR> E. तप्त, and कुम्भ a jar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=305-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तप्तकृच्छ्र|तप्तकृच्छ्रः
तप्तकृच्छ्र n. (-च्छ्रं) A sort of penance, drinking hot water, milk, and ghee<BR>for three days each, and inhaling hot air for three days.<BR> E. तप्त<BR>heated, कृच्छ्र penance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=305-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तप्ततपस्
तप्ततपस् m. (-पाः) An ascetic.<BR> E. तप्त, and तपस् penance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=305-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तप्तपाषाणकुण्ड|तप्तपाषाणकुण्डं
तप्तपाषाणकुण्ड n. (-ण्डं) A hell.<BR> E. तप्त, पाषाण a stone, and कुण्ड a well.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=305-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तप्तबालुक|तप्तबालुकः
तप्तबालुक m. (-कः) A hell.<BR> E. तप्त, and बालुका sand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=305-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तप्तरूपक|तप्तरूपकं
तप्तरूपक n. (-कं) Silver.<BR> E. तप्त, and रूपक silver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=305-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तप्त्वा
तप्त्वा ind.<BR>	 1. Having heated.<BR>	 2. Having performed penance.<BR> E. तप, and<BR>क्त्वा aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=305-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तप्स्यत्
तप्स्यत् mfn. (-प्स्यन्-प्स्यन्ती-प्स्यत्) Practising or intending to practise aus-<BR>terities.<BR> E. तप् to perform penance. शतृ affix, future part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=305-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमःप्रवेश|तमःप्रवेशः
तमःप्रवेश m. (-शः)<BR>	 1. Groping in the dark.<BR>	 2. Mental indistinctness or<BR>aberration.<BR> E. तमस्, and प्रवेश entrance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=305-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमःस्थित
तमःस्थित n. (-तं) A hell, one of the lowest divisions of hell.<BR> E. तमस्, and<BR>स्थित placed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=305-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तम|तमं|तमः
तम (इर उ) इर्तमु r. 4th cl. (ताम्यति)<BR>	 1. To desire.<BR>	 2. To be distressed in<BR>body or mind.<BR> E. खेदे अक० इच्छायां सक-दिवा-प० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=305-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तम|तमं|तमः
तम m. (-मः) The quality of darkness incident to humanity: see तमस्.<BR>mf. (-मः-मा) A tree bearing black blossoms.<BR>	 n. (-मं)<BR>	 1. Darkness,<BR>gloom.<BR>	 2. The point of the foot.<BR>	 f. (-मा-मी) Night.<BR> E. तम् to be disturb-<BR>ed, to be fatigued, &c. affixes करणे घञर्थे संज्ञायां घ, and टाप् or ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=305-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमङ्गक|तमंगकः|तमङ्गकः
तमङ्गक m. (-कः) The flat and projecting roof of a house, a sort of bal-<BR>cony or terrace.<BR> E. तम् to desire, अङ्गक affix; pleasant, desirable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=305-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमत|तमतः
तमत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Desirous, cupidinous, longing or hankering after.<BR>2. Wished, desired.<BR> E. तम् to desire, affix अतच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=305-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमःप्रभ
तमःप्रभ mf. (-भः-भा) A hell, one of the lowermost divisions of the infer-<BR>nal regions.<BR> E. तम darkness, add प्रभ what is manifested.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=305-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमर|तमरं
तमर n. (रं) Lead.<BR> E. तम् to be disturbed, affix अरन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=305-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमराज|तमराजः
तमराज m. (-जः) A kind of sugar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=305-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमस्
तमस् n. (-मः)<BR>	 1. Third of the qualities incident to the state of humani-<BR>ty, the Tama guna, or property of darkness, whence proceed folly,<BR>ignorance, mental blindness, worldly delusion, &c.<BR>	 2. Darkness,<BR>gloom.<BR>	 3. Sin.<BR>	 4. Sorrow, grief.<BR>	 mn. (-माः-मः) Rahu or the personi-<BR>fied ascending node: see राहु.<BR> E. तम् to be disturbed, and असुन्<BR>Uṇādi affix; that property by which the mind is troubled, the<BR>world perplexed, &c.; also तमस and तम.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=305-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमस|तमसं|तमसः
तमस n. (-सं)<BR>	 1. Darkness.<BR>	 2. A city.<BR>	 f. (-सा) A river, the Tamasa or<BR>Tonse.<BR> E. तम् to be disturbed, (daylight, &c.) and असच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=305-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमस्कल्प
तमस्कल्प mfn. (-ल्पः-ल्पा-ल्पं) Like darkness, black, gloomy.<BR> E. तमस्, and<BR>कल्प aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=305-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमस्तति|तमस्ततिः
तमस्तति f. (-तिः) Great or diffusive darkness.<BR> E. तमस् darkness, and तति a spreading.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=305-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमस्विन्
तमस्विन् mfn. (-स्वी-स्विनी-स्वि) Dark, gloomy.<BR>	 f. (-नी)<BR>	 1. Night.<BR>	 2. Tur-<BR>meric.<BR> E. तमस् darkness, and विनि affix, fem. affix ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=305-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमाल|तमालं|तमालः
तमाल m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. The sectarial mark made with Sandal, &c. upon the<BR>forehead.<BR>	 2. The name of a tree bearing black blossoms, (Xantho-)<BR>cymus pictorios, Rox.)<BR>	 3. A sword, a scymitar or large sacrificial<BR>knife.<BR>	 4. A plant: see वरुण.<BR>	 5. A black kind of Mimosa.<BR>	 6. The<BR>bark of the bambu.<BR>	 n. (-लं) The leaf of the Laurus cassia. The bark<BR>or troubled, leaf of the Luarus cassia.<BR> E. तम् to be dark or troubled,<BR>Uṇādi affix कालन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=305-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमालक|तमालकं|तमालकः
तमालक n. (-कं)<BR>	 1. A sort of potherb, (Marsilea dentata, Rox.)<BR>	 2. The<BR>leaf of the Laurus cassia.<BR>	 mn. (-कः-कं)<BR>	 1. The bark of a bambu.<BR>	 2.<BR>The Tamala tree: see the preceding.<BR> E. कन् pleonasm, or implying<BR>some resemblance, added to तमाल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=305-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमालपत्र|तमालपत्रं
तमालपत्र n. (-त्रं)<BR>	 1. The Tamala tree: see तमाल.<BR>	 2. The Tilaka or sec-<BR>tarial mark on the forehead.<BR>	 3. The leaf of the Laurus cassia. E.<BR>तमाल, and पत्र a leaf: the leaf of the Tamala, either in fact or<BR>resemblance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=305-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमालिका
तमालिका f. (-का) A district of Bengal, the modern Tamluk.<BR> E. तमाल a<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=305-b" target="_blank">Page305-b+ 60</a>]<BR>Tamala tree, कन् affix, implying possession; also with an analo-<BR>gous affix इनि, तमालिनी abounding in Tamala trees.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=305-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमाली
तमाली f. (-ली) A medicinal plant: see ताम्रवल्ली.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=305-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमि|तमिः
तमि f. (-मिः) Night.<BR> E. तम् to be weary, इन् affix: see तम and तमी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=305-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमिन्
तमिन् mfn. (-मी-मिनी-मि) Desiring, desirous, wishing.<BR> E. तम् to desire,<BR>इन् or ङीप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=305-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमिस्र|तमिस्रं|तमिस्रः
तमिस्र m. (-स्रः) The dark half of the month, from the full to the change.<BR>f. (-स्रा)<BR>	 1. A dark night, or one during the wane of the moon.<BR>2. Great or extensive darkness.<BR>	 3. The night of the new moon.<BR>	 4.<BR>Any night.<BR>	 n. (-स्रं)<BR>	 1. Darkness.<BR>	 2. Anger, wrath.<BR> E. तमस् dark-<BR>ness, र added, and इ substituted for the penultimate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=305-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमिस्रपक्ष|तमिस्रपक्षः
तमिस्रपक्ष m. (-क्षः) The fortnight of the moon's wane.<BR> E. तमिस्र, and पक्ष<BR>a fortnight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=305-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमोगुण|तमोगुणः
तमोगुण m. (-णः) The quality of darkness or ignorance.<BR> E. तमस्, and गुण<BR>property.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=305-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमोघ्न|तमोघ्नः
तमोघ्न m. (-घ्नः)<BR>	 1. Fire.<BR>	 2. The sun.<BR>	 3. The moon.<BR>	 4. The legislator<BR>BUDDHA.<BR>	 5. VIṢṆU.<BR>	 6. ŚIVA.<BR> E. तमस् darkness, (physical or<BR>moral,) and घ्न destroyer. तमोऽन्धकारं मोहमज्ञानं वा हन्ति तम-ठक् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=305-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमोज्योतिस्
तमोज्योतिस् m. (-तिः) A fire-fly.<BR> E. तमस् darkness, and ज्योतिस् light.<BR>तमसि अन्धकारे ज्योतिरस्य । खद्योते ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=305-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमोनुद्
तमोनुद् mfn. (-नुद्) Dispersing darkness.<BR>	 m. (-नुद् or -नुत्)<BR>	 1. Fire.<BR>	 2. The<BR>sun.<BR>	 3. The moon.<BR>	 4. A lamp.<BR> E. तमस darkness, नुद् to send away<BR>or disperse, affix क्विप्; also with क affix तमोनुद । तमो नुदति खण्डयति<BR>नुद्-क्विप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=305-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमोनुद|तमोनुदः
तमोनुद mfn. (-दः-दा-दं) See the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=305-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमोपह|तमोपहः
तमोऽपह mfn. (-हः-हा-हं) Lightening, enlightening, removing darkness<BR>physical or moral.<BR>	 m. (-हः)<BR>	 1. The sun.<BR>	 2. The moon.<BR>	 3. Fire.<BR>	 4.<BR>A name of Buddha, the founder of Buddha sect.<BR> E. तमस् dark-<BR>ness, अपह removing, from the अप prefixed to हन् to kill or destroy,<BR>affix ड; also तमोहन्तृ mfn. (-न्ता-न्त्री-न्तृ) तमोऽपहन्ति अप-हन ड ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=305-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमोभिद्
तमोभिद् m. (-भिद् or -भित्) A fire-fly.<BR> E. तमस् darkness, and भिद् what pene-<BR>trates. तमो भिनत्ति भिद-क्विप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=305-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमोभूत
तमोभूत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Dark.<BR>	 2. Ignorant.<BR> E. तमस्, and भूत become.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=305-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमोमय|तमोमयः
तमोमय mfn. (-यः-यी-यं) Consisting of or composed of darkness, derived<BR>from it.<BR> E. तमस्, and मयट् aff. तम आत्मकं प्रचुरं वा ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=305-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमोमणि|तमोमणिः
तमोमणि m. (-णिः) A fire-fly.<BR> E. तमस् darkness, मणि a gem. तमसि<BR>मणिरिव ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=305-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमोलिप्ती
तमोलिप्ती f. (-प्ती) The district of Tumlook in Bengal.<BR> E. तमस् darkness<BR>or sin, and लिप्त soiled, affix ङीष्; a country of which the inhabi-<BR>tants are notoriously depraved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=305-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमोविकार|तमोविकारः
तमोविकार m. (-रः) Disease, sickness.<BR> E. तमस्, and विकार changed, pro-<BR>ceeding from the Tama guna.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=305-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमोवृत
तमोवृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Overcome with or influenced by rage, fear, &c.<BR>or any of the effects of the property of darkness.<BR>	 2. Obscured,<BR>clouded.<BR> E. तमस् as above, and वृत surrounded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=305-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमोहर|तमोहरः
तमोहर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Removing darkness, lightening.<BR>	 m. (-रः) The<BR>moon.<BR> E. तमस् darkness, and हर who removes. तमो हरति ह-<BR>अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=305-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तम्पा
तम्पा f. (-म्पा) A cow.<BR> E. तम् to desire, अप् affix; also प being changed<BR>to ब, तम्बा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=305-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तम्ब
तम्ब r. 1st cl. (तम्बति) To go or move.<BR> E. भ्वा-प-सक-सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=305-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तम्बा|तंबा
तम्बा f. (-म्बा) A cow: see तम्पा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=305-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तय|तयः
तय r. 1st cl. (तयते) To go or move.<BR>	 2. To guard or preserve.<BR> E. भ्वा-आ-<BR>सक-सेट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=305-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तय|तयः
तय mfn. (-यः-यी-यं) Who or what protects.<BR>	 m. (-यः) Protection.<BR> E. तय,<BR>and अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=305-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर|तरः
तर mfn. (-रः-रा-री-रं) Who or what passes over or beyond.<BR>	 m. (-रः)<BR>	 1.<BR>Passing over, crossing.<BR>	 2. A float, a raft.<BR>	 3. A road.<BR>	 4. A tree.<BR>	 f.<BR>(-री)<BR>	 1. A boat.<BR>	 2. A club.<BR>	 3. A clothes basket, a Pitara.<BR>	 4. Smoke.<BR>5. A small wooden baling vessel.<BR>	 6. The end of a garment.<BR> E. तॄ<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=306-a" target="_blank">Page306-a+ 60</a>]<BR>to cross, affix भावे अप्, fem. affix ङीष्; also with इन् affix तरि, q. v.<BR>कर्त्तरि अच् । कृशानौ पु० तरति अनेन करणे अप् । आतरे पणादौ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=305-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरक्षु|तरक्षुः
तरक्षु m. (-क्षुः) A hyena.<BR> E. तर a road, and क्षि to annoy, affix डु infesting<BR>the road; also with कन् added तरक्षुक m. (-कः) or with ड affix तरक्ष<BR>m. (-क्षः) but not common. तरं गतिं मार्गं वा क्षिणोति ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=306-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरङ्ग|तरंग|तरंगः|तरङ्गः
तरङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>	 1. Wave.<BR>	 2. Cloth or clothes.<BR>	 3. The gallop of a horse. E.<BR>तॄ to pass over or cross, Uṇādi affix अङ्गच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=306-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरङ्गिणी|तरंगिणी
तरङ्गिणी f. (णी) A river.<BR> E. तरङ्ग a wave, इनि and ङीष् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=306-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरङ्गित|तरंगित
तरङ्गित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Wavy, billowy, tossing with waves.<BR> E. तरङ्ग, and<BR>इतच् aff. तरङ्गः सञ्जातः अस्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=306-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरण|तरणं|तरणः
तरण m. (-णः)<BR>	 1. A raft, a float.<BR>	 2. Svarga or paradise.<BR>	 n. (-णं)<BR>1. Crossing over, passing, going across.<BR>	 2. Removing from an in-<BR>undation.<BR> E. तॄ to cross, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=306-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरणि|तरणिः
तरणि m. (-णिः)<BR>	 1. The sun.<BR>	 2. A ray of light.<BR>	 3. A float or raft.<BR>	 f. (-णिः-<BR>or -णी)<BR>	 1. A boat.<BR>	 2. The Socotrine aloe, (A perfoliata.)<BR>	 3. A plant,<BR>(Hibiscus mutabilis.)<BR> E. तॄ to cross, Uṇādi affix करणे कर्मणि भावे वा<BR>ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=306-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरणिपेटक|तरणिपेटकः
तरणिपेटक m. (-कः) An oval bowl or basin of wood, for baling a boat.<BR>E. तरणि, and पेटक a basket, the boat's basket.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=306-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरणिरत्न|तरणिरत्नं
तरणिरत्न n. (-त्नं) A ruby.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=306-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरण्ड|तरंड|तरंडं|तरंडः|तरण्डः
तरण्ड mfn. (-ण्डः-ण्डा or -ण्डी-ण्डं) A boat, a vessel.<BR>	 mn. (-ण्डः-ण्डं)<BR>	 1. A<BR>raft or float, made of bamboos, &c. tied together, and sometimes<BR>floated upon jars or hollow gourds inverted.<BR>	 2. The float of a finish-<BR>ing line.<BR>	 3. An oar.<BR>	 m. (-ण्डः) A country.<BR> E. तॄ to cross, अण्डन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=306-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरण्डपादा|तरंडपादा
तरण्डपादा f. (-दा) A boat.<BR> E. तरण्ड an oar, and पाद a foot, having oars<BR>for feet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=306-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरत्
तरत् mfn. (-रन्-रन्ती-रत्) Crossing, passing over.<BR>	 n. (-रत् or -रद्)<BR>	 1. A<BR>float or raft.<BR>	 2. A kind of duck.<BR> E. तॄ to cross, शतृ affix of the<BR>active participle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=306-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरत्सल
तरत्सल m. (-लः) Conflagration of chaff: see तृणाग्नि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=306-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरन्त|तरंत|तरंतः|तरन्तः
तरन्त m. (-न्तः)<BR>	 1. A fog.<BR>	 2. A hard shower, a torrent of rain.<BR>	 3. The<BR>ocean.<BR>	 f. (-न्ती) A boat.<BR> E. तॄ to cross, झच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=306-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरम्बुज|तरम्बुजं
तरम्बुज n. (-जं) A watermelon, (most probably borrowed from a Persian<BR>word.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=306-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरपण्य|तरपण्यं
तरपण्य n. (-ण्यं) Fare, freight.<BR> E. तर passing (a river), and पण्य price.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=306-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरल|तरलः
तरल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>	 1. Trembling, tremulous.<BR>	 2. Libidinous, lech-<BR>erous, wanton.<BR>	 3. Luminous, splendid.<BR>	 4. Hollow.<BR>	 5. Liquid,<BR>liquefied m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. The central gem of a necklace.<BR>	 2. A necklace.<BR>3. Bottom, depth, lower or under part.<BR>	 f. (-ला)<BR>	 1. Rice gruel.<BR>	 2.<BR>Wine, vinous or spirituous liquor.<BR>	 3. A bee.<BR> E. तॄ to pass, to go or<BR>move, affix अलच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=306-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरलता
तरलता f. (-ता) Tremulousness, unsteadiness.<BR> E. तल् added to the last;<BR>also with त्व, तरलत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=306-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरललोचना
तरललोचना f. (-ना) A woman with rolling or tremulous eyes.<BR> E. तरल<BR>trembling, and लोचन an eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=306-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरलायित|तरलायितः
तरलायित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Caused to tremble, agitated, undulating.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-तः)<BR>	 1. A large wave or surf.<BR>	 2. Fickleness.<BR> E. तरल used as a verb,<BR>क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=306-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरलित|तरलितं
तरलित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Shaken, trembling, tremulous.<BR> E. तरल trembling,<BR>and इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=306-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरवारि|तरवारिः
तरवारि m. (-रिः) A sword, a scymitar.<BR> E. तर passing, वॄ to effect, इन्<BR>affix; making its pass through the enemy, &c. also तरवारिक m. (कः)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=306-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरस्
तरस् n. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Speed, velocity.<BR>	 2. Strength.<BR>	 3. A bank.<BR>	 4. A float,<BR>a raft.<BR> E. तॄ to go, to go quick, &c. असुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=306-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरस|तरसं
तरस n. (-सं) Flesh.<BR> E. तरस् strength, affix अच्; in which there is<BR>strength.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=306-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरस्थान|तरस्थानं
तरस्थान n. (-नं) A landing place, a wharf or stairs.<BR> E. तर passing, ferry-<BR>ing, and स्थान place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=306-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरस्वत्|तरस्वन्त्
तरस्वत् mfn. (-स्वान्-स्वती-स्वत्)<BR>	 1. Quick, swift.<BR>	 2. Valiant.<BR> E. तरस्, and<BR>वतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=306-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरस्विन्
तरस्विन् mfn. (-स्वी-स्विनी-स्वि)<BR>	 1. Quick, swift.<BR>	 2. Strong, valiant.<BR>	 m. (-स्वी)<BR>1. A courier, an express, a runner.<BR>	 2. A hero.<BR>	 3. The bird of<BR>VIṢṆU.<BR>	 4. Air, wind.<BR> E. तरस् speed, &c. विनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=306-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरान्धु|तरांधु|तरांधुः|तरान्धुः
तरान्धु m. (-न्धुः) A large flat bottomed boat.<BR> E. तर crossing., अन्धु water;<BR>perhaps a various reading of the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=306-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरालु|तरालुः
तरालु m. (-लुः) A flat bottomed boat.<BR> E. तर passing over, आलुच् affix: see<BR>the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=306-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरि|तरिः
तरि f. (-रिः)<BR>	 1. A boat.<BR>	 2. A clothe's basket.<BR>	 3. The end of a cloth.<BR> E. तॄ<BR>to pass, Uṇādi affix इन्; also with ङीष् affix तरीः see तर, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=306-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरिक|तरिकः
तरिक n. (-कं) A raft, a float.<BR>	 m. (-कः) A ferry-man.<BR>	 f. (-का) A boat.<BR>E. तरि a boat, कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=306-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरिकिन्
तरिकिन् m. (-की) A ferry-man.<BR> E. तरिक a raft, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=306-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरित
तरित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Carried over or across.<BR>	 f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. The fore finger.<BR>2. Garlic, or perhaps hemp: see गृञ्जन.<BR> E. तॄ to cross, इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=306-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरिन्
तरिन् mfn. (-री-रिणी-णि) Who or what crosses.<BR>	 f. (-णी) a boat.<BR> E. तॄ to<BR>go, in the causal, affix इनि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=306-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरितृ
तरितृ mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ) What crosses, passes or carries over.<BR>	 f. (-त्री) A<BR>boat, a raft.<BR> E. तॄ to cross, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=306-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरिरथ|तरिरथः
तरिरथ m. (-थः) An oar, a paddle.<BR> E. तरि a boat, and रथ a car.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=306-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरीष|तरीषः
तरीष m. (-षः)<BR>	 1. The ocean.<BR>	 2. Heaven or paradise.<BR>	 3. Decorating,<BR>ornamenting.<BR>	 4. A raft, a float.<BR>	 5. Practice, business, profession.<BR>	 f.<BR>(-षी) The daughter of INDRA.<BR> E. तॄ to cross or cause to cross, Uṇādi<BR>affix ईषन्, in some of its senses this word and तबिष seem to be<BR>confounded; see तबिष and ताविष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=306-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरु|तरुः
तरु m. (-रुः) A tree.<BR> E. तॄ to proceed, Uṇādi affix उन्, what goes or<BR>grows; or from what flowers and fruits arise, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=306-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरुकूणि|तरुकूणिः
तरुकूणि m. (-णिः) A sort of bird.<BR> E. तरु a tree, and कुण् to contract, affix<BR>इन्; nestling in the tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=306-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरुज
तरुज mfn. (-जः-जा-जं) Borne, produced by a tree, (as a flower, fruit,<BR>&c.)<BR> E. तरु, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=306-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरुजीवन|तरुजीवनं
तरुजीवन n. (-नं) The root of a tree.<BR> E. तरु a tree, and जीवन living.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=306-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरुण|तरुणं|तरुणः
तरुण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>	 1. Young, juvenile.<BR>	 2. New, fresh, novel.<BR>	 m. (-णः)<BR>1. A young man, one of the virile age.<BR>	 2. The castor-oil-plant.<BR>3. Large cumin seed.<BR>	 f. (-णी)<BR>	 1. A young woman from 16 to 30<BR>years of age; generally however one about the first age.<BR>	 2. The<BR>alœ tree, (A. perfoliata.) A perfume, commonly Chira.<BR>	 4. A flower,<BR>the Indian white rose, (Rosa standulifera)<BR>	 n. (-णं) A kind of flow-<BR>er, that of the Achyranthes aspera (कुब्जपुष्प.)<BR> E. तॄ to pass away,<BR>उनन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=306-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरुणज्वर|तरुणज्वरः
तरुणज्वर m. (-रः) A fever that lasts a week.<BR> E. तरुण, and ज्वर fever.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=306-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरुणदधि
तरुणदधि n. (-धि) Curds five days old.<BR> E. तरुण, and दधि curds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=306-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरुणास्थि
तरुणास्थि n. (-स्थि) Cartilage, gristle.<BR> E. तरुण, and अस्थि bone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=306-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरुणीगण
तरुणीगण m. (-णः) A number of young woman.<BR> E. तरुणी, and गण a troop.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=306-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरुणीजन
तरुणीजन m. (-नः) A young woman.<BR> E. तरुणी, and जन person.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=306-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरुतल
तरुतल m. (-लः) The part under the branches of a tree, the ground<BR>about its root.<BR> E. तरु, and तल below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=306-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरुतूलिका
तरुतूलिका f. (-का) The flying fox.<BR>	 n.<BR> E. तरु a tree, and तूलिका scales,<BR>suspended like a balance from the branches of a tree; also read<BR>तरुदूलिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=306-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरुनख|तरुनखः
तरुनख m. (-खः) A thorn.<BR> E. तरु a tree, and नख a nail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=306-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरुपङ्क्ति
तरुपङ्क्ति f. (-क्तिः) A row of trees, an avenue.<BR> E. तरु, and पङ्क्ति a line.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=306-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरुभुज्
तरुभुज् m. (-क्) A parasite plant.<BR> E. तरु, and भुज् what enjoys.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=306-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरुमृग|तरुमृगः
तरुमृग m. (-गः) A monkey, an ape.<BR> E. तरु a tree, and मृग a deer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=306-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरुराग|तरुरागं
तरुराग m. (-गः)<BR>	 1. A bud, a blossom.<BR>	 2. A new sprout.<BR> E. तरु a tree, राग<BR>delight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=306-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरुविटप
तरुविटप m. (-पः) A branch or sprout.<BR> E. तरु, and विटप a shoot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=306-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरुराज|तरुराजः
तरुराज m. (-जः) The palmyra tree.<BR> E. तरु, and राज king, chief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=306-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरुरुहा
तरुरुहा f. (-हा) A parasite plant.<BR> E. तरु, and रुह what mounts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=306-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरुरोहिणी
तरुरोहिणी f. (-णी) A parasite plant.<BR> E. तरु, and रोहिणी what ascends.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=306-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरुशायिन्
तरुशायिन् m. (-यी) A bird.<BR> E. तरु a tree, and शीङ् to sleep, with णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=306-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरुसार|तरुसारः
तरुसार m. (-रः) Camphor.<BR> E. तरु a tree, and सार essence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=307-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरुस्थ
तरुस्थ mfn. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थं) Staying or being in a tree.<BR>	 f. (-स्था) A para-<BR>site plant.<BR> E. तरु, and स्थ what stays.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=307-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरुट|तरुटः
तरुट m. (-टः) The root of the lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=307-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्क|तर्कः
तर्क r. 10th cl. (तर्कयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To shine.<BR>	 2. To speak.<BR>	 3. To reason, to<BR>discuss.<BR>	 4. To doubt or apprehend. दीप्तौ अक० आकाङ्क्षायां वितर्के च सक०<BR>चुरा० उभ० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=307-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्क|तर्कः
तर्क m. (-र्कः)<BR>	 1. Doubt or disputation, discussion, reasoning.<BR>	 2. Wish.<BR>desire.<BR>	 3. Supplying an ellipsis.<BR>	 4. Cause, motive.<BR>	 5. The science<BR>of reasoning, logic.<BR>	 6. (In logic,) Reduction to absurdity, a con-<BR>clusion opposed to or disproving the premises.<BR> E. तर्क to infer, to<BR>reason, &c. affix भावे अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=307-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्कक|तर्ककः
तर्कक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A supplicant, a petitioner, an asker.<BR>	 2. A logician. E.<BR>तर्क to reason, and affix ण्वुल्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=307-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्कयत्
तर्कयत् mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्)<BR>	 1. Expecting, anticipating.<BR>	 2. Doubting. E.<BR>तर्क to doubt, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=307-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्कविद्या
तर्कविद्या f. (-द्या) The science of reasoning or logic.<BR> E. तर्क as above, and<BR>विद्या knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=307-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्काभास|तर्काभासः
तर्काभास m. (-सः) Apparent reduction to absurdity, or seeming not real,<BR>incompatibility of the conclusion with the premises.<BR> E. तर्क, and<BR>आभास fallacy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=307-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्कारी
तर्कारी f. (-री) A tree, (Æschynomene sesban.)<BR> E. तर्क reasoning, ऋ to<BR>go or affect, affixes अण् and ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=307-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्कित
तर्कित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Doubted, apprehended.<BR>	 2. Discussed.<BR> E. तर्क, to<BR>doubt, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=307-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्किन्
तर्किन् m. (-र्की) A logician, a disputant, a follower of the Tarka Śāstra.<BR>E. तर्क as above, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=307-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्किल
तर्किल m. (-लः) Cassia tora.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=307-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्कु|तर्कुः
तर्कु f. (-र्कुः) A spindle, an iron pin upon which the cotton is first<BR>drawn out; it also serves as the distaff, the cotton being next<BR>transferred from it to the wheel.<BR> E. कृत् to cut, Uṇādi affix उ, and<BR>the radical letters transposed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=307-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्कुट|तर्कुटं
तर्कुट n. (-टं) Drawing out the cotton upon the distaff or upon the<BR>wheel.<BR>	 f. (-टी) A spindle or a distaff: see तर्कु.<BR> E. कृत् to cut, &c.<BR>उटच् affix, and the radical letters transposed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=307-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्कुपिण्ड|तर्कुपिंड|तर्कुपिण्डः
तर्कुपिण्ड m. (-ण्डः) A ball of clay, &c. upon the lower end of the spin-<BR>dle to assist in giving it a rotatory motion.<BR> E. तर्कु as above, पिण्ड<BR>a lump.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=307-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्कुपीठी
तर्कुपीठी f. (-ठी) A ball at the lower end of a spindle: see the preced-<BR>ing.<BR> E. तर्कु a spindle, and पीठ a stool.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=307-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्कुलासक|तर्कुलासकः
तर्कुलासक m. (-कः) A concave shell or saucer in which the lower end<BR>of the spindle is placed, and whirled round.<BR> E. तर्कु a spindle, लस्<BR>to go, णिच् and ण्वुल् affs. तर्कुं लासयति चालयति । चरका ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=307-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्कुशाण|तर्कुशाणः
तर्कुशाण m. (-णः) A small whetstone, for sharpening spindles, &c.<BR> E. तर्कु<BR>a spindle, and शाण whetstone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=307-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्क्षु|तर्क्षुः
तर्क्षु m. (-र्क्षुः) A hyena.<BR> E. तर्ज् to give pain, affix कु; also तरक्षु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=307-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्क्ष्य|तर्क्ष्यः
तर्क्ष्य m. (-र्क्ष्यः) Nitre, saltpetre.<BR> E. तृक्ष-यत् वा गुणः । यवक्षारे ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=307-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्ज|तर्ज्ज
तर्ज r. 1st and 10th cls. (तर्जति तर्जयते) To blame, to censure, to reprove.<BR>भ्वा-प-सक-सेट् । चुर-आ-सक-सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=307-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्जन|तर्जनं|तर्ज्जन|तर्ज्जनं
तर्जन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Blaming, censuring.<BR>	 2. Pointing at, in ridicule, or<BR>contempt.<BR>	 3. Putting to shame, surpassing.<BR>	 4. Wrath, anger.<BR>	 f.<BR>(-नी) The forefinger.<BR> E. तर्ज् to abuse, to injure, affixes भावे ल्युट्<BR>and ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=307-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्जिक|तर्ज्जिक|तर्ज्जिकः
तर्जिक m. (-कः) The name of a country, perhaps to the north-west of<BR>India or Bokhara, &c. the country of the Tajics: also तायिक. E.<BR>तर्जलर्जनमस्ति अत्र ठन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=307-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्जित|तर्ज्जित
तर्जित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Blamed, reviled.<BR>	 2. Shamed, disgraced.<BR> E. तर्ज्<BR>to blame, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=307-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्ण|तर्णः
तर्ण m. (-र्णः) A calf.<BR> E. तृण to go, अच् affix; also with ण्वुल् added, तर्णक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=307-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्णक|तर्णकः
तर्णक m. (-कः) A calf: see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=307-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्णि|तर्णिः
तर्णि m. (-र्णिः)<BR>	 1. A raft, a float.<BR>	 2. The sun.<BR> E. तरति आकाशपद्धतिं तॄ-नि<BR>करणे नि वा ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=307-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्त्तरीक|तर्तरीक|तर्त्तरीकं
तर्त्तरीक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) A passenger, one who passes or crosses.<BR>	 n. (-कं)<BR>A boat, a raft, a vessel.<BR> E. तॄ to cross over, ईक aff. and deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=307-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्द|तर्द्द
तर्द r. 1st cl. (तर्दति) To kill or hurt.<BR> E. भ्वा-प-सक-सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=307-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्दू
तर्दू m. (-र्दूः) A wooden ladle.<BR> E. तर्द or तृद to go, Uṇādi affix ऊ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=307-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्पण|तर्पणं
तर्पण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Satisfaction given or received; either the act of<BR>pleasing, or the state of being pleased.<BR>	 2. Satiety, fulness.<BR>	 3. A<BR>religious rite, presenting water to the manes of the deceased or to<BR>the Pitṛs collectively; also to the gods either generally or in-<BR>dividually.<BR>	 4. Fuel used on sacrificial occasions.<BR>	 f. (-णी) A plant;<BR>also गुरुस्कन्ध.<BR> E. तृप् to satisfy or be satisfied, affixes णिच् and ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=307-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्पणेच्छु|तर्पणेच्छुः
तर्पणेच्छु mfn. (-च्छुः-च्छुः-च्छु) Desirous of satisfaction, or of receiving<BR>after death the presentation of water called Tarpana.<BR>	 m. (-च्छुः) A<BR>name of BHISHMA.<BR> E. तर्पण as above, इच्छु to wish, and उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=307-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्पित
तर्पित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Pleased, satisfied.<BR> E. तृप् to be pleased, क्त affix,<BR>with इट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=307-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्पिन्
तर्पिन् mfn. (-र्पी-र्पिणी-र्पि)<BR>	 1. Giving pleasure or satisfaction.<BR>	 2. Offering<BR>oblations to the manes, (who does so.)<BR>	 f. (-णी) A plant, (Hibiscus<BR>mutabilis.)<BR> E. तृप् to give pleasure, णिच्, णिनि and ङीप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=307-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्ब|तर्ब्ब
तर्ब r. 1st cl. (तर्बति) To go or move.<BR> E. भ्वा-प-सक-सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=307-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्बट|तर्बटः|तर्ब्बट
तर्बट m. (-टः) A year.<BR> E. तर्ब to go, अटन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=307-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्मन्|तर्म्मन्
तर्मन् n. (-र्म) The top or term of the sacrificial post.<BR> E. तॄ to pass up,<BR>and मनिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=307-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्ष|तर्षः
तर्ष m. (-र्षः)<BR>	 1. Thirst.<BR>	 2. Wish, desire.<BR>	 3. The ocean.<BR>	 4. A raft or<BR>float.<BR>	 5. The sun.<BR> E. तृष् to thirst, affix भावे घञ् or तॄ to pass over,<BR>कर्मणि करणे वा स । समुद्रे भेलके च ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=307-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्षण|तर्षणं
तर्षण n. (-णं) Thirst, thirsting: it is also used metaphorically.<BR> E. तृष्<BR>to thirst, affix भावे ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=307-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्षित|तर्षितः
तर्षित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Thirsting, a thirst, thirsty.<BR>	 2. Desiring, wish-<BR>ing for.<BR> E. तर्षो जातोऽस्य तारका० इतच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=307-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्हि
तर्हि ind. Therefore.<BR> E. तद् that, and र्हिल् aff. तस्मिन् काले.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=307-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तल|तलं|तलः
तल r. 1st and 10th cls. (तलति तालयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To be full or complete to.<BR>2. To fix, to found.<BR>	 3. To establish.<BR> E. चुरा० उभ० पक्षे भ्वा-पर-सक-सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=307-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तल|तलं|तलः
तल n. (-लं)<BR>	 1. Essential nature, (in composition especially, as महीतलं<BR>the earth itself, the very earth.)<BR>	 2. Depth, bottom, lowness, in-<BR>feriority of position, the place under or underneath.<BR>	 3. A wood,<BR>a forest.<BR>	 4. A hole, a pit, a chasm.<BR>	 5. Cause, origin, motive, the<BR>root or seed of events.<BR>	 6. Sole of the foot.<BR>	 7. A slap with the<BR>hand.<BR>	 nf. (-लं-ला) A leathern fence worn by archers on the left<BR>arm.<BR>	 m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. The palmyra tree.<BR>	 2. The palm with extended<BR>fingers.<BR>	 3. The hilt or handle of a sword, &c.<BR>	 4. Pressing the<BR>strings of a lute with the left hand.<BR>	 5. The stand or support of<BR>any thing, that which is under or below it.<BR>	 6. The fore arm.<BR>	 7. A<BR>span.<BR> E. तल् to fix, affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=307-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तलक|तलकं|तलकः
तलक n. (-कं) A large pond.<BR> E. तल a hole, a hollow, and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=307-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तलप्रहार|तलप्रहारः
तलप्रहार m. (-रः) A slap or blow with the palm of the hand.<BR> E. तल the<BR>open palm, प्रहार striking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=307-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तलवारण|तलवारणं
तलवारण n. (-णं) A sword.<BR> E. तल, and वारण opposing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=307-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तलसारक|तलसारकं
तलसारक n. (-कं) A martingale.<BR>	 2. A vessel from which horses are fed.<BR>E. तल below, सृ to go, in the causal form, कप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=307-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तलहृदय|तलहृदयं
तलहृदय n. (-यं) The centre of the sole of the foot.<BR> E. तल below, and हृदय<BR>heart.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=307-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तलाची
तलाची f. (-ची) A mat, one made of reeds or bamboos.<BR> E. तल below,<BR>अञ्च् to go, क्विप् affix, fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=307-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तलातल|तलातलं
तलातल n. (-लं) One of the seventh divisions of the infernal regions.<BR>E. तल below, reiterated, as down-adown.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=307-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तलिका
तलिका f. (-का) A martingale.<BR> E. तल् to fix, and ठन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=307-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तलित|तलितं
तलित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Fixed, placed, having a bottom.<BR>	 n. (-तं) Fried<BR>meat.<BR> E. तल् to be fixed or to satisfy, इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=307-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तलिन|तलिनं|तलिनः
तलिन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>	 1. Separate, having spaces or interstices.<BR>2. Clear, clean.<BR>	 3. Small, little.<BR>	 4. Delicate, thin, spare.<BR>	 5. below,<BR>situated under or underneath.<BR>	 n. (-नं) A bed, a couch or cot. E.<BR>तन् to fix or be fixed, Uṇādi affix इनन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=308-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तलिम|तलिमं
तलिम n. (-मं)<BR>	 1. Ground prepared for the site of a dwelling, &c. see<BR>कुट्टिम.<BR>	 2. A bed, a couch or cot.<BR>	 3. An awning.<BR>	 4. A scymitar, a<BR>large sacrificial sword or knife.<BR> E. तल् to fix, इमन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=308-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तलुन|तलुनः
तलुन m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. Air, wind.<BR>	 2. A youth.<BR>	 f. (-नी) A young woman.<BR> E. तल<BR>to fix, उनन् affix: see तरुण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=308-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तलेक्षण|तलेक्षणः
तलेक्षण m. (-णः) A hog.<BR> E. तल down, and ईक्षण looking. तले ईक्षणमस्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=308-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तलोदरी
तलोदरी f. (-री) A mistress or wife.<BR> E. कृशोदर्य्यां भार्य्यायाम् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=308-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तलोदा
तलोदा f. (-दा) A river.<BR> E. तल steep, down, उद water. तले उदकं यस्यां<BR>उदकस्य उदादेशः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=308-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तल्क|तल्कं
तल्क n. (-ल्कं) A wood, a forest.<BR> E. तल् to fix, कन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=308-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तल्प|तल्पं|तल्पः
तल्प mfn. (-ल्पः-ल्पा-ल्पं)<BR>	 1. A bed.<BR>	 2. An upper story, a room on the top of<BR>a house, a turret, a tower or keep.<BR>	 3. A wife.<BR> E. तल् to fix, Uṇādi<BR>affix पक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=308-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तल्पकीट|तल्पकीटः
तल्पकीट m. (-टः) A bug.<BR> E. तल्प a bed, and कीट an insect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=308-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तल्पज
तल्पज mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>	 1. Born of a wife, (as a son by an appointed<BR>substituted.)<BR>	 2. Produced in or from a bed, &c.<BR> E. तल्प and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=308-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तल्पन|तल्पनं
तल्पन n. (-नं) An elephant's back.<BR>	 2. The exterior muscles of the back.<BR>E. तल्प a nominal verb, to be as a bed, to be broad, &c. क्विप् and<BR>कर्त्तरि ल्यु affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=308-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तल्ल|तल्लं|तल्लः
तल्ल m. (-ल्लः) A reservoir, a large pond, a tank or Talao.<BR>	 f. (-ल्ला)<BR>	 1. A<BR>young woman.<BR>	 2. A boat.<BR>	 3. The wife of VARUṆA.<BR>	 n. (-ल्लं) A pit,<BR>a hole.<BR> E. तल deep, depth, and ल to be or have, from ली with ड aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=308-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तल्लज|तल्लजः
तल्लज m. (-जः) Excellence, happiness; also attributively, Excellent,<BR>happy: used in apposition as an epithet, the gender is not chang-<BR>ed, as कुमारीतल्लजः an excellent maiden.<BR> E. तत् that, (that which is<BR>every thing,) and लज् to attain, affix अच् । तत् प्रसिद्धं यथा तथा लजति<BR>लज कान्तौ अच् । प्रशस्ते ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=308-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तल्लिका
तल्लिका f. (-का) A key.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=308-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तल्व|तल्वं
तल्व n. (-ल्वं) Scent arising from the rubbing of fragrant substances.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=308-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तवक|तवकः
तवक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Thine.<BR> E. कन् added to तव to poss. case of त्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=308-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तवक्षीर|तवक्षीरं
तवक्षीर n. (-रं) Milk and water.<BR> E. तु-अच् । नित्यकर्म० ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=308-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तवराज|तवराजः
तवराज m. (-जः) A sort of sugar prepared from a species of Hedysa-<BR>rum.<BR> E. तु-अच् । तवः पूर्णः सन् राजते राज-अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=308-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तविष|तविषः
तविष m. (-षः)<BR>	 1. Heaven, paradise.<BR>	 2. The ocean.<BR>	 f. (-षी)<BR>	 1. A river.<BR>	 2.<BR>The daughter of INDRA.<BR>	 3. Strength, (in the dialect of the Vedas.)<BR>E. तव a Sautra root, टिषच् Uṇādi affix; also ताविष and तवीष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=308-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तवीष|तवीषः
तवीष m. (-षः)<BR>	 1. Heaven.<BR>	 2. The ocean.<BR>	 3. Gold. E. See the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=308-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तष्ट|तष्टः
तष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं) Pared, made thin.<BR> E. तक्ष् to pare, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=308-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तष्टृ
तष्टृ m. (-ष्टा)<BR>	 1. A carpenter.<BR>	 2. A name of VISWAKARMA.<BR>	 3. One of<BR>the twelve Adityas or suns; also तष्टृ.<BR> E. तक्ष् to pare, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=308-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तस
तस (इर उ) इरतसु r. 4th cl. (तस्यति) To throw, to toss, to direct, to send,<BR>(इ) तसि r. 1st and 10th cls. (तंसति तंसयति-ते) or with अव prefixed<BR>(अवतंसति अवतंसयति) To adorn to dress or decorate.<BR> E. चु० उभ० पक्षे<BR>भ्वादि० पर० सक० सेट् इदित् । दिवा-पर-सक-सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=308-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तसर|तसरः
तसर m. (-रः) A shuttle.<BR> E. तन् to stretch, क्सरन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=308-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तस्कर|तस्करः
तस्कर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A thief, a robber.<BR>	 2. The ear.<BR>	 3. A kind of potherb,<BR>(Medicago esculenta.)<BR>	 3. A tree, (Vangueria spinosa:) see मदन.<BR>	 f.<BR>(-री) A passionate woman.<BR> E. तत् that, used depreciatingly, and कर<BR>who does, सुट् substituted for the final of तत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=308-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तस्करता
तस्करता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Thievishness, thieving.<BR>	 2. Hearing, catching by the<BR>ear.<BR> E. तल् added to the last; also with त्व, तस्करत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=308-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताटङ्क|ताटंक|ताटंकः|ताटङ्कः
ताटङ्क m. (-ङ्कः) An ornament of the ear, a large sort of ear-ring: see<BR>ताडङ्क and तालपत्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=308-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताटस्थ्य|ताटस्थ्यं
ताटस्थ्य n. (-स्थ्यं)<BR>	 1. Indifference, disregard, exemption from attachment<BR>or aversion.<BR>	 2. Proximity.<BR> E. तटस्थ, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=308-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताड|ताडः
ताड m. (-डः)<BR>	 1. Beating, whipping, inflicting bodily chastisement.<BR>	 2.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=308-b" target="_blank">Page308-b+ 60</a>]<BR>Sound, noise.<BR>	 3. A handful of grass, corn, &c. a sheaf.<BR>	 4. A moun-<BR>tain.<BR>	 5. A kind of grass, (Andropogon serratus.)<BR>	 f. (-डि or -डी) A<BR>kind of palm, (Coripha talliera, Rox.) See ताली.<BR> E. तड् to give<BR>pain, to beat, &c. affix भावे अच् कर्मणि अच् वा ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=308-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताडका
ताडका f. (-का) A female demon, killed by RAMA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=308-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताडकाफल|ताडकाफलं
ताडकाफल n. (-लं) Large cardamoms.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=308-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताडङ्क|ताडंक|ताडंकः|ताडङ्कः
ताडङ्क m. (-ङ्कः) A kind of ear-ring: see तालपत्र.<BR> E. तड् to shine, अङ्कन्<BR>affix; also ड being changed to ट, ताटङ्क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=308-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताडघ|ताडघः
ताडघ mfn. (-घः-घा-घं) Beating with a whip or with strokes of any kind.<BR>E. ताड, and घ who strikes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=308-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताडघात|ताडघातः
ताडघात m. (-तः) An artificer who beats or hammers any thing.<BR> E. ताड,<BR>and घात a blow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=308-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताडन|ताडनं
ताडन n. (-नं) Beating, whipping, &c.<BR>	 f. (-नी) A whip.<BR> E. तड् to beat,<BR>भावे ल्युट् affix, fem. affix ङीष् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=308-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताडनीय
ताडनीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) To be beaten, punishable.<BR> E. तड् to beat, अनी-<BR>यर् affix; also ताड्य and ताडयितव्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=308-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताडपत्र|ताडपत्रं
ताडपत्र n. (-त्रं) An ornament of the ear.<BR> E. ताड the Tal tree, and पत्र<BR>a leaf, an earring resembling this: see तालपत्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=308-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताडयितृ
ताडयितृ mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ) Who or what beats or strikes.<BR> E. तड् to beat,<BR>तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=308-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताडयित्वा
ताडयित्वा ind. Having beaten.<BR> E. तड् to beat, क्त्वा aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=308-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताडित
ताडित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Struck, beaten.<BR> E. तड् to beat, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=308-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताडुल|ताडुलः
ताडुल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Beating, who or what beats or strikes.<BR> E. तड् to<BR>give pain, उल Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=308-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताड्य
ताड्य mfn. (-ड्यः-ड्या-ड्यं) To be beaten or chastised, what may or ought<BR>to be punished, punishable.<BR> E. तड् to beat, ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=308-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताड्यमान|ताड्यमानः
ताड्यमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Being beaten or struck.<BR>	 m. (-नः) A musical<BR>instrument, which is struck, as a drum, &c.<BR> E. तड् to beat or strike,<BR>शानच् affix, यक् inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=308-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताण्डव|तांडव|तांडवं|ताण्डवं|तांडवः|ताण्डवः
ताण्डव mn. (-वः-वं)<BR>	 1. Dancing, especially with violent gesticulation,<BR>and particularly applied to the frantic dance of the god ŚIVA,<BR>and his votaries.<BR>	 2. A sort of grass, (Saccharum procerum.)<BR>	 m.<BR>(-वः) In prosody, a tribrach or foot of three sort syllables.<BR> E. तण्डु<BR>the name of the Muni, by whom the style of dancing was first<BR>taught, affix अण्, or तडि to beat, and अव aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=308-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताण्डवतालिक|ताण्डवतालिकः
ताण्डवतालिक m. (-कः) A name of NANDI, one of ŚIVA'S principal<BR>attendants.<BR> E. ताण्डव ŚIVA'S dancing. and तालिक accompanied with<BR>music, from ताल tune or time, and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=308-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताण्डवप्रिय|तांडवप्रिय|ताण्डवप्रियः
ताण्डवप्रिय m. (-यः) A name of ŚIVA.<BR> E. ताण्डव dancing, and प्रिय<BR>fond of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=308-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताण्डि|तांडिः|ताण्डिः
ताण्डि f. (-ण्डिः) The science of dancing.<BR> E. तण्डु the teacher of this art,<BR>and इञ् off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=308-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तात|तातः
तात mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Venerable, reverend, respectable.<BR>	 m. (-तः)<BR>	 1. A<BR>father.<BR>	 2. A term of affection addressed to any person, but especi-<BR>ally to a junior or inferior, as हे तात oh! child, &c.<BR> E. तन् to extend,<BR>(his race or fame,) क्त affix, and the vowel made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=308-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तातगु|तातगुः
तातगु mfn. (-गुः-गुः-गु) Paternal, relating or belonging to the father.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-गुः) A paternal uncle.<BR> E. तात a father, गु who goes or is, from गम्<BR>to go, with डु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=308-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तातजनयित्री
तातजनयित्री f. du. always (-त्र्यौ) Father and mother, parents.<BR> E. तात<BR>father, and जनयितृ mother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=308-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताततुल्य|ताततुल्यः
ताततुल्य m. (-ल्यः) A paternal uncle, or the most respectable of the<BR>male relations.<BR> E. तात a father, and तुल्य like, equal to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=308-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तातन|तातनः
तातन m. (-नः) A wagtail. तातं प्रशस्तं नृत्यति नृत-ड । खञ्चनखगे ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=308-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तातल|तातलः
तातल m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. A fatherly relative, one who may be considered as a<BR>father.<BR>	 2. Sickness, disease.<BR>	 3. An iron club or spike.<BR>	 4. Cooking<BR>or maturing.<BR>	 5. Heat, physical or morbid.<BR> E. तापं लाति ला-क पृषो० ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=308-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताति|तातिः
ताति m. (-तिः) A son.<BR> E. ताय to spread, (the race,) क्तिच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=308-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तात्कालिक|तात्कालिकः
तात्कालिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Relating to any particular moment of time.<BR>E. तत्काल and ठङ् aff. ञिठ वा ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=308-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तात्पर्य्य|तात्पर्य|तात्पर्यं|तात्पर्य्यं
तात्पर्य्य n. (-र्य्यं)<BR>	 1. Object, purpose, intent, design.<BR>	 2. Meaning, purport.<BR>3. Explanation.<BR> E. तत्पर intent, ष्यञ् aff. तत्परस्य भावः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=309-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तात्पर्य्यार्थ|तात्पर्यार्थ|तात्पर्यार्थः
तात्पर्य्यार्थ m. (-र्थः) The meaning or purpose of a sentence.<BR> E. तात्पर्य्य pur-<BR>pose, and अर्थ meaning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=309-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तादर्थ्य|तादर्थ्यं
तादर्थ्य n. (-र्थ्यं)<BR>	 1. Sameness or precision of meaning.<BR>	 2. Identity of ob-<BR>ject.<BR> E. तदर्थ, ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=309-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तादात्म्य|तादात्म्यं
तादात्म्य n. (-त्म्यं) Identity, unity, sameness.<BR> E. तदात्म same, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=309-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तादृश्
तादृश् mfn. (-दृक्) Such like, like him or it, &c.<BR> E. तद् that, दृश् to see,<BR>affix क्विप्; also with ट affix तादृश mfn. (-शः-शी-शं) or with क्स affix,<BR>तादृक्ष mfn. (-क्षः-क्षा-क्षं.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=309-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तान|तानं|तानः
तान m. (-नः) A tune.<BR>	 n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Expanse, extension.<BR>	 2. An object of<BR>sense.<BR> E. तन् to extend, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=309-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तानव|तानवं
तानव n. (-वं) Thinness, spareness.<BR> E. तनु, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=309-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तानूर|तानूरः
तानूर m. (-रः) A whirlpool.<BR> E. तन् to spread, ऊरण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=309-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तान्त|तांत|तान्तः
तान्त mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं)<BR>	 1. Wearied, fatigued, distressed.<BR>	 2. Languid, lan-<BR>guishing.<BR>	 3. Faded, withered, blighted.<BR> E. तम् to be distressed,<BR>affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=309-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तान्तव|तांतव
तान्तव n. (-वं) Spinning, weaving.<BR> E. तन्तु a thread, अञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=309-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तान्त्र
तान्त्र mfn. (-न्त्रः-न्त्री-न्त्रं)<BR>	 1. Stringed, having wires or strings, (as a<BR>musical instrument.)<BR>	 2. Relating to the Tantras, &c.<BR> E. तन्त्र, and<BR>अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=309-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तान्त्रिक|तांत्रिक|तान्त्रिकः
तान्त्रिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>	 1. Relating to the Tantras, taught by them,<BR>following them, &c.<BR>	 2. Relating to a thread, &c.<BR>	 m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A<BR>scholar, a man completely versed in any science.<BR>	 2. A follower<BR>of the doctrine taught by the Tantras.<BR> E. तन्त्र truth, &c. and ठक् aff.<BR>तन्त्रं सिद्धान्तं वेत्ति शास्त्रमधीते वा ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=309-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तान्द्रन
तान्द्रन m. (-नः) Wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=309-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताप|तापः
ताप m. (-पः)<BR>	 1. Heat, burning, (moral or physical.)<BR>	 2. Pain, sorrow,<BR>distress.<BR> E. तप् to burn or inflame, affix घञ्.<BR>	 f. (-पी) A name of<BR>the Tapti or Surat river.<BR>	 2. A name of the Yamuna or Jamna<BR>river.<BR> E. तप the sun, affix of descent अच्, ङीष् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=309-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तापक|तापकः
तापक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Burning, inflaming, heating.<BR>	 m. (-कः) Fever,<BR>morbid heat.<BR> E. तप् to burn, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=309-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तापत्य|तापत्यः
तापत्य m. (-त्यः) ARJUNA.<BR> E. तपती, and ण्य affix of descent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=309-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तापन|तापनः
तापन mfn. (-नः-नी-नं) What heats or inflames.<BR>	 m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. The sun.<BR>2. Of KĀMA^1'S arrows, the inflamer.<BR>	 3. Sun-shine.<BR>	 4. Heating, in-<BR>flaming.<BR> E. तप् to heat, in the causal form, and णिच् and भावे<BR>ल्युट् affs. or तापि-कर्त्तरि ल्यु । सूर्य्ये ।<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20260617. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/264.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=309-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तापनीय
तापनीय mfn. (-यः-यी-यं) Golden, made of gold.<BR> E. तपनीय, and अण् aff.<BR>उपनिषद्भेदे च । यथा गोपालतापनीयः, नृसिंहतापनीयः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=309-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तापस|तापसं|तापसः
तापस mfn. (-सः-सी-सं) Performing penance, a practiser of devout aus-<BR>terities, a devotee, an ascetic.<BR>	 m. (-सः) A kind of crane, (Ardea<BR>nivea.)<BR>	 n. (-सं) The leaf of the Laurus cassia.<BR> E. तपस् penance, affix<BR>अण् । तपश्चरणं शीलमस्य छत्रादि० ण or तपोऽस्त्यस्य अण् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=309-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तापसक|तापसकः
तापसक m. (-कः) A contemptible devotee, one not long engaged in<BR>austerities.<BR> E. तापस, and कन् depreciative aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=309-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तापसतरु|तापसतरुः
तापसतरु m. (-रुः) A tree, commonly Ingua or Jiyaputa, (Nagelia pu-<BR>tranjiva.)<BR> E. तापस an ascetic, and तरु a tree; also similar com-<BR>pounds, as तापसद्रुम, तापसवृक्ष, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=309-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तापसप्रिय|तापसप्रियः
तापसप्रिय m. (-यः) A tree, (Chiranjia sapida:) see पियाल.<BR>	 f. (-या) A<BR>grape.<BR> E. तापस an ascetic, प्रिय beloved by. तापसानां प्रियः छाया-<BR>प्रदत्वात् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=309-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तापहर
तापहर mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>	 1. Cooling, removing heat.<BR>	 2. Consoling, alle-<BR>viating distress.<BR>	 f. (-री) A dish, a sort of soup, of pulse and grain,<BR>first fried with ghee and turmeric, and afterwards boiled with salt<BR>and sugar.<BR> E. ताप, and हर what removes. तापं हरति हृ-ट ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=309-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तापिच्छ|तापिच्छः
तापिच्छ m. (-च्छः) A tree bearing dark blossoms, the Tamala: see the<BR>next, तापिनं छादयति छद-ड पृषो० । तमालवृक्षे ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=309-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तापिञ्छ|तापिञ्छः
तापिञ्छ m. (ञ्छः) The Tamala tree, (Xanthocymus pictorius.)<BR> E. तापिन्<BR>a person heated, and छद what covers or shelters, ड affix, deriv.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=309-b" target="_blank">Page309-b+ 60</a>]<BR>irr. also the final being dropped तापिच्छ, and with जि to conquer<BR>or remove तापिञ्ज ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=309-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तापिञ्ज|तापिञ्जं|तापिञ्जः
तापिञ्ज m. (-ञ्जः) The Tamala tree.<BR>	 n. (-ञ्जं) Sulphate of iron: see the<BR>preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=309-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तापित
तापित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Inflamed.<BR>	 2. Distressed, pained.<BR> E. तप् to inflame,<BR>affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=309-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तापिन्
तापिन् mfn. (-पी-पिनी-पि) Oppressed by heat, morbid, moral or physical;<BR>any thing heated or growing.<BR>	 m. (-पी) One of the defied saints<BR>of the BAUDDHA.<BR> E. तप् to heat, affix णिनि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=309-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताप्य|ताप्यं
ताप्य mn. (-प्यः-प्यं) A mineral substance, sulphate of iron.<BR> E. तापी the<BR>river, and यत् affix; said to be procured from the Tapi river;<BR>also with कन् added ताप्यकम् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=309-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम|तामः
ताम m. (-मः) An object of terror.<BR>	 2. Fault, defect, vice.<BR>	 3. Anxiety,<BR>distress.<BR>	 4. Desire.<BR> E. तम् to be distressed, affix करणे भावे वा घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=309-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तामर|तामरं
तामर n. (-रं)<BR>	 1. Water.<BR>	 2. Ghee or oiled butter.<BR> E. ताम desire, and र<BR>from रा to get or have; desirable for drinking, &c. तामं ग्लानिं रवते<BR>हिनस्ति रुङ् बधे वा ड ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=309-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तामरस|तामरसं
तामरस n. (-सं)<BR>	 1. A lotus, (Nymphæa nelumbo.)<BR>	 2. Copper.<BR>	 3. Gold.<BR>4. A species of the Jagati metre.<BR> E. तामर water, सम् to abide, and<BR>ड affix; or ताम desire, and रस here implying object. तामरे जले सलि<BR>सस-ड ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=309-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तामलकी
तामलकी f. (-की) A plant, (Flacourtia cataphracta:) see मूम्यामलकी. E.<BR>तम् to desire, to be as it were, or resemble, आमलकी the Amalaki,<BR>तम णिच् क्विप् तान् कर्मधा० ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=309-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तामलिप्त|तामलिप्तं
तामलिप्त nf. (-प्तं-प्ती) A district in the south of Bengal, commonly Tam-<BR>look.<BR> E. ताम distress, trouble, and लिप्त smeared, affected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=309-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तामस|तामसं|तामसः
तामस mfn. (-सः-सी-सं)<BR>	 1. Affected by or appertaining to the third qua-<BR>lity, that of darkness or vice: belonging to it as a Purana, a sys-<BR>tem of philosophy, a ceremonial rite, &c.<BR>	 2. Dark, of or belong-<BR>ing to darkness.<BR>	 m. (-सः)<BR>	 1. A snake.<BR>	 2. An incendiary, a malignant<BR>and mischievous man, a villain.<BR>	 3. An owl.<BR>	 4. The fourth Menu.<BR>	 f.<BR>(-सी) A dark night.<BR>	 2. A name of the goddess DURGĀ.<BR>	 n. (-सं) The<BR>quality of darkness.<BR> E. तमस् the quality of drakness, &c. affix<BR>अण् । तमः अस्ति अस्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=309-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तामसिक|तामसिकं
तामसिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>	 1. Of belonging to the quality of darkness,<BR>derived from it, teaching lessons so characterised, &c.<BR>	 2. Of or be-<BR>longing to physical drakness.<BR> E. तमस्, and ठञ् aff. तमसा निर्वृत्तम् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=309-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तामिस्र|तामिस्रं|तामिस्रः
तामिस्र n. (-स्रं)<BR>	 1. Great darkness.<BR>	 2. A hell, that of deep gloom.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-स्रः) Indignation at being disappointed or slighted.<BR> E. तमिस्र, and<BR>अण् added. तमिस्रा तमस्ततिः अस्ति अत्र ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=309-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम्बूल|तांबूल|तांबूलं|ताम्बूलं
ताम्बूल nf. (-ल-ली)<BR>	 1. Areca, (Areca faufel or catechu.)<BR>	 2. Betel, (Piber<BR>betel,) or its pungent leaf, which together with the areca nut and<BR>catechu, and sometimes caustic lime and spices, is eaten very<BR>generally by the natives of the east.<BR>	 n. (-लं) The areca nut.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-लः) San, a plant, (Crotolaria juncea.)<BR> E. तम् to desire, affix ऊलच्<BR>and वुक् augment, the radical vowel made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=309-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम्बूलकरङ्क|तांबूलकरंक|ताम्बूलकरङ्कः
ताम्बूलकरङ्क m. (-ङ्कः) The Pan-dan or betel-box.<BR> E. ताम्बूल as above, and<BR>करङ्क a hollowed cocoanut, &c. which the Pan-box usually resem-<BR>bles. (पानेर डिपा) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=309-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम्बूलद|तांबूलद|ताम्बूलदः
ताम्बूलद m. (-दः) The betel-bearer; kings and great men being attended<BR>by an officer of this description.<BR> E. ताम्बूल betel, and द who gives.<BR>ताम्बूलं ददाति दा-क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=309-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम्बूलपेटिका|तांबूलपेटिका
ताम्बूलपेटिका f. (-का) A betel-box.<BR> E. ताम्बूल, and पेटिका a casket.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=309-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम्बूलराग|ताम्बूलरागः
ताम्बूलराग m. (-गः) A kind of pulse, (Ervum lens.)<BR> E. ताम्बूल betel, and<BR>राग colour. ताम्बूलकृतो रागः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=309-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम्बूलवल्ली|तांबूलवल्ली
ताम्बूलवल्ली f. (-ल्ली) A small plant bearing a pungent leaf, which with<BR>the areca nut, a small quantity of caustic lime (or Chunam) and<BR>catechu, and occasionally cloves, cardamoms, &c. form the Pan or<BR>betel of the Asiatic, (Piper betel.)<BR> E. ताम्बूल the same, and वल्ली root-<BR>stalk; also with कन् added ताम्बूलवल्लिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=309-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम्बूलवाहक|तांबूलवाहक|ताम्बूलवाहकः
ताम्बूलवाहक m. (-कः) A betel-bearer, a servant attached to men of rank<BR>to prepare the Pan, and carry the betel-box.<BR> E. ताम्बूल, and वाहक<BR>who carries; also ताम्बूलवाहिन् m. (-ही.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=310-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम्बूलिक|तांबूलिक|तांबूलिकः|ताम्बूलिकः
ताम्बूलिक mf. (-कः-की) A seller of betel.<BR> E. ताम्बूल, and ठक् aff. ताम्बूलं<BR>तद्रचनं शिल्पमस्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=310-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम्बूलिन्|तांबूलिन्
ताम्बूलिन् mfn. (-ली-लिनी-लि) Relating or belonging to a Pan having one,<BR>giving one, &c.<BR>	 m. (-ली) The Pan-bearer, a servant who prepares<BR>and furnishes the Pan.<BR> E. ताम्बूल as above, इनि aff. ताम्बूलं पण्यतया<BR>अस्ति अस्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=310-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम्यत्
ताम्यत् mfn. (-म्यन्-म्यती-म्यत्) Distressing, afflicting, annoying.<BR> E. तम् to<BR>distress, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=310-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम्र|ताम्रं|ताम्रः
ताम्र mfn. (-म्रः-म्री-म्रं) Of a coppery red colour.<BR>	 n. (-म्रं)<BR>	 1. Copper.<BR>	 2. A<BR>kind of sandal, represented as of a dark red colour, and smelling<BR>like a lotus.<BR>	 3. A dark or coppery red.<BR>	 m. (-म्रः) A leprosy with<BR>large red spots.<BR>	 f. (-म्री) A copper or metallic cup of prescribed<BR>capacity, and perforated by a small hole at the bottom, answering<BR>the purpose of an hour glass: it is put into a vessel of water;<BR>the water gradually filling it, and the cup sinking, marks the<BR>time that has elapsed.<BR> E. तम् to desire, Uṇādi affix रक्, and the<BR>vowel made long; or ताम्र copper, अण् and ङीष् affixes, implying<BR>analogy or derivation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=310-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम्रक|ताम्रकं
ताम्रक n. (-कं) Copper.<BR> E. ताम्र as above, and कन् pleonastic aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=310-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम्रकर्णी
ताम्रकर्णी f. (-र्णी) A name of the female elephant of the west.<BR> E. ताम्र<BR>coppery, and कर्ण ear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=310-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम्रकार|ताम्रकारः
ताम्रकार m. (-रः) A brazier, a copper-smith.<BR> E. ताम्र copper, and कार<BR>worker. ताम्रं ताम्रपात्रादिकं करोति कृ-अण् उप० स० ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=310-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम्रकिलि
ताम्रकिलि m. (-लिः) A small worm of a red colour.<BR> E. ताम्र red, and किलि<BR>a worm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=310-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम्रकुट्ट|ताम्रकुट्टः
ताम्रकुट्ट m. (-ट्टः) A brazier or copper-smith.<BR> E. ताम्रं कुट्टयति कुट्ट-अण् उप०<BR>स० ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=310-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम्रकुट्टक|ताम्रकुट्टकः
ताम्रकुट्टक m. (-कः) A brazier.<BR> E. ताम्र, and कुट्ट a point: the word is<BR>imitative of the foreign original, ण्वुल्प्रत्ययः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=310-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम्रकृमि|ताम्रकृमिः
ताम्रकृमि m. (-मिः) A kind of red insect.<BR> E. ताम्र red, and कृमि a<BR>worm. इन्द्रगोपकीटे ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=310-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम्रगर्भ|ताम्रगर्भं
ताम्रगर्भ n. (-र्भ) Blue vitriol or sulphate of copper.<BR> E. ताम्र copper, and<BR>गर्भ womb or source.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=310-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम्रचूड|ताम्रचूडः
ताम्रचूड m. (-डः) A cock.<BR> E. ताम्र, and चूडा a crest. ताम्रा रक्ता चूडा यस्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=310-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम्रतनु
ताम्रतनु mfn. (-नुः-नुः-नु) Having a ruddy or fair complexion, copper-co-<BR>loured.<BR> E. ताम्र, and तनु body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=310-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम्रपट्ट|ताम्रपट्टं|ताम्रपट्टः
ताम्रपट्ट n. (-ट्टं) A copper-plate, such as Hindu grants of land, &c. are<BR>frequently inscribed on.<BR> E. ताम्र copper, and पट्ट a cloth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=310-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम्रपर्णी
ताम्रपर्णी f. (-र्णी)<BR>	 1. A large point or lake.<BR>	 2. The name of a river in<BR>the peninsula, and of the district in its vicinity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=310-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम्रपत्र|ताम्रपत्रः
ताम्रपत्र n. (-त्रं) A plate of copper.<BR>	 m. (-त्रः) A potherb: see जीव.<BR> E. ताम्र,<BR>and पत्र a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=310-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम्रपाकिन्
ताम्रपाकिन् m. (-की) A tree: see गर्द्दभाण्ड.<BR> E. ताम्र red, and पाकिन् ripen-<BR>ing, the fruit being of this colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=310-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम्रपुष्प|ताम्रपुष्पः
ताम्रपुष्प m. (-ष्पः)<BR>	 1. A kind of ebony, (Bauhinia variegata.)<BR>	 2. A plant,<BR>(Kæmpfera rotunda.)<BR>	 f. (-ष्पा) Trumpet flower, (Bignonia suave-<BR>olens.)<BR>	 f. (-ष्पी)<BR>	 1. Lythrum or uticosum: see धातृ-पुष्पिका.<BR>	 2. Trumpet<BR>flower.<BR>	 3. Red Teori: see त्रिकृत्.<BR> E. ताम्र coppery red, and पुष्प a<BR>flower, bearing red blossoms. ताम्रं पुष्पं यस्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=310-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम्रफल|ताम्रफलः
ताम्रफल m. (-लः) A tree, (Alangium hexapetalum.)<BR> E. ताम्र copper, and<BR>फल fruit. ताम्रं रक्तं फलमस्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=310-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम्रफलक
ताम्रफलक n. (-कं) A copper-plate.<BR> E. ताम्र, and फलक a plank or board.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=310-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम्रमुख|ताम्रमुखः
ताम्रमुख mfn. (-खः-खी-खं) Copper-coloured, fair-complexioned.<BR>	 m. (-खः)<BR>A European.<BR> E. ताम्र, and मुख face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=310-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम्रमूला
ताम्रमूला f. (-ला) A plant: see ग्राहिणी.<BR> E. ताम्र copper, and मूल root. ताम्रं<BR>रक्तं मूलं यस्याः टाप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=310-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम्रमृग
ताम्रमृग m. (-गः) The red deer.<BR> E. ताम्र, and मृग deer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=310-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम्रवर्ण|ताम्रवर्णः
ताम्रवर्ण mfn. (-र्णः-र्णी-र्णं) Red, copper-coloured.<BR>	 f. (-र्णी) The blossom of<BR>sesamum.<BR> E. ताम्र, and वर्ण colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=310-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम्रवल्ली
ताम्रवल्ली f. (-ल्ली) Bengal madder, (Rubia manjith.)<BR>	 2. A medicinal<BR>plant used as an emollient in affections of the mouth and face;<BR>also called तमाली, ताली, मूक्ष्मवल्ली, &c.<BR> E. ताम्र copper, and वल्ली pedicle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=310-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम्रवीज|ताम्रवीजः
ताम्रवीज m. (-जः) A kind of vetch: see कुलत्थ.<BR> E. ताम्र copper, and वीज<BR>the seed. ताम्रं वीजं यस्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=310-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम्रवृक्ष|ताम्रवृक्षः
ताम्रवृक्ष m. (-क्षः) A sort of Sandal wood.<BR> E. ताम्र copper, and वृक्ष a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=310-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम्रवृन्त|ताम्रवृन्तः
ताम्रवृन्त mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं) A kind of vetch: see कुलत्थ<BR> E. ताम्र copper, or<BR>coppery, वृन्त foot-stalk. ताम्रं वृन्तमस्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=310-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम्रशिखिन्
ताम्रशिखिन् m. (-खी) A cock.<BR> E. ताम्र copper, शिखा a crest, and इनि affix.<BR>see ताम्रचूड. ताम्रा रक्ता शिखा अस्ति अस्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=310-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम्रसार|ताम्रसारं
ताम्रसार m. (रः) A red kind of Sandal, (Pterospermum santolinum.) E.<BR>ताम्र copper, and सार pith. ताम्रं रक्तं सारं अस्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=310-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम्राकु|ताम्राकुः
ताम्राकु m. (-कुः) One of the eighteen minor divisions of the known<BR>continent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=310-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम्राक्ष|ताम्राक्षः
ताम्राक्ष mfn. (-क्षः-क्षी-क्षं) Red-eyed.<BR>	 m. (-क्षः) The Koil or Kokila, the<BR>Indian cuckoo.<BR> E. ताम्र, and अक्षि an eye. ताम्रे अक्षिणी यस्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=310-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम्राभ|ताम्राभं
ताम्राभ n. (-भं) Red sandal wood.<BR> E. ताम्र copper, and resembling. ताम्रस्य<BR>आभा इव आभा यस्य । रक्तचन्दने ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=310-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम्रार्द्ध|ताम्रार्द्धं
ताम्रार्द्ध n. (-र्द्धं) Mixed or bell metal.<BR> E. ताम्र copper, and अर्द्ध part or half.<BR>ताम्रस्य अर्द्धः अंशभेद उत्पादकोऽस्य । कांस्ये ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=310-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम्रिक|ताम्रिकः
ताम्रिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Of copper, made of copper, &c.<BR>	 m. (-कः) A<BR>brazier, a copper-smith.<BR> E. ताम्र copper, and ठञ् affix.<BR>	 f. (-का) A<BR>copper-vessel for marking time.<BR> E. कन् added to ताम्री, q. v. ताम्रं<BR>तत्पत्रादिनिर्माणं शिल्पमस्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=310-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताय
ताय (ऋ) तायृ r. 1st cl. (तायते)<BR>	 1. To spread, to extend, to proceed in a<BR>continuous stream or line.<BR>	 2. To cherish or protect.<BR> E. भ्वा-आ-सक-<BR>सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=310-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तायिक|तायिकः
तायिक m. (-कः) A country; or plu.<BR>	 m. (-काः) 1ts inhabitants.<BR> E. ताय् to<BR>cherish, ठञ् aff. ताये वृद्धौ साधु ठञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=310-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तार|तारं|तारः
तार mfn. adj. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>	 1. High, as a note in music.<BR>	 2. Radiant, shin-<BR>ing, radiating.<BR>	 3. Clean, clear.<BR>	 4. Good, excellent, well flavoured,<BR>&c.<BR>	 m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A high note or tone in music.<BR>	 2. Elegance of a<BR>pearl.<BR>	 3. A clear or beautiful pearl.<BR>	 4. Crossing, passing over, &c.<BR>5. A wire, a cord.<BR>	 6. The mystic monosyllable Om.<BR>	 7. A mystical<BR>monosyllable in the Tantras.<BR>	 7. The name of a monkey chief, the<BR>son BALI. N. (-रं)<BR>	 1. Silver.<BR>	 2. A pearl.<BR>	 mfn. subst. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>	 1.<BR>The pupil of the eye.<BR>	 2. A star in general, a planet, as asterism,<BR>&c.<BR>	 f. (-रा) A female deity peculiar to the Bauddha sect.<BR>	 2. The<BR>wife of VṚHASPATI.<BR>	 3. The wife of the monkey king BALI.<BR>	 4.<BR>A name of the goddes DURGĀ.<BR> E. तॄ to pass or proceed; also in<BR>the causal, to cause to pass, and णिच्, अच् or घञ् aff. संसारार्णवात्<BR>तारयति स्वजापकान् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=310-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तारक|तारकं|तारकः
तारक mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>	 1. A protector, a preserver.<BR>	 2. One who causes or<BR>enables to pass or go over.<BR>	 n. (-कं)<BR>	 1. The eye.<BR>	 2. A Mantra, a<BR>formula addressed to Rama, as Ramaya namah.<BR>	 nf. (-कं-का)<BR>	 1. The<BR>pupil of the eye.<BR>	 2. A star.<BR>	 mn. (-कः-कं) A float or raft.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-कः) A pilot, a helmsman or steersman.<BR>	 2. The man of a demon<BR>or evil spirit destroyed by KARTIKEYA.<BR> E. तॄ to pass or cause to<BR>pass, and णिच् and ण्वुल् affixes; or कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=310-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तारकजित्
तारकजित् m. (-जित्) A name of KARTIKEYA.<BR> E. तारक a demon, and जित्<BR>conqueror: also similar names, as तारकारि, तारकहन्, तारकरिपु,<BR>&c. तारकं दैत्यं जयति जि-क्विप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=310-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तारकारि|तारकारिः
तारकारि m. (-रिः) The deity KARTIKEYA.<BR> E. तारक and अरि a foe: see<BR>the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=310-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तारकित|तारकितं
तारकित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Starry.<BR> E. तारक a star, इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=310-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तारकिन्
तारकिन् mfn. (-की-किणी-कि) Starry.<BR>	 f. (-णी) Night.<BR> E. तारक, and इनि<BR>aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=310-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तारण|तारणः
तारण mfn. (-णः-णी-णं) Who or what causes or enables to cross.<BR>	 m. (-णः)<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=311-a" target="_blank">Page311-a+ 60</a>]<BR>A raft, a float.<BR>	 n. (-णं) Carrying or conveying across.<BR> E. तॄ to<BR>cross, affix ल्युट् तारयति अनेन ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=310-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तारणि|तारणिः
तारणि f. (-णिः) A boat.<BR> E. तॄ to pass over, णि or अणि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=311-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तारतम्य|तारतम्यं
तारतम्य n. (-म्यं)<BR>	 1. More or less, the state or condition.<BR>	 2. Dependence<BR>of larger numbers on smaller in a progressive series.<BR> E. तर, and<BR>तम affixes of the comparative and superlative degrees, and ष्यञ्<BR>aff तरतमयोर्भावः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=311-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तारनाद
तारनाद m. (-दः) A loud sound or noise.<BR> E. तार, and नाद sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=311-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तारल|तारलः
तारल mfn. (-लः-ली-लं) Libidinous, dissipated, a lecher.<BR> E. तरल un-<BR>steady, affix अण् । तरल एव ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=311-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तारविमला
तारविमला f. (-ला) A sort of mineral said to be of the colour of silver.<BR>F. तार a star, and विमल pure, clean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=311-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तारशुद्धिकर|तारशुद्धिकरं
तारशुद्धिकर n. (-रं) Lead.<BR> E. तार silver, and शुद्धिकर what refines.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=311-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताराधिपति
ताराधिपति m. (-तिः) The moon.<BR> E. तारा a star, and अधिपति a ruler.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=311-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तारापथ|तारापथः
तारापथ m. (-थः) The atmosphere, the firmament, heaven or sky. E.<BR>तारा a star, and पथ for पथिन् a path. ताराणां पन्थाः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=311-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तारापीड|तारापीडः
तारापीड m. (-डः) The moon.<BR> E. तार a star, and आपीड a chaplet. ताराणां<BR>आपीडः भूषणमिव । चन्द्रे ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=311-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताराभूषा
ताराभूषा f. (-षा) Night.<BR> E. तारा, and भूषा ornament. तारा भूषा यस्याः । रात्रौ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=311-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताराभ्र|ताराभ्रः
ताराभ्र m. (-भ्रः) Camphor.<BR> E. तारा, and अभ्र talc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=311-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तारामण्डल|तारामंडल|तारामण्डलः
तारामण्डल m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. A large splendid temple.<BR>	 2. The region of the<BR>stars.<BR> E. तारा a star, and मण्डल a region; shining with gold and<BR>jewels as with stars.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=311-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तारारि|तारारिः
तारारि m. (-रिः) A pyritic ore of iron: see विट्माक्षिक.<BR> E. तारा the pupil<BR>of the eye, and अरि hostile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=311-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तारिक|तारिकं
तारिक n. (-कं) Fare, freight, toll.<BR>	 f. (-का)<BR>	 1. A star; also तारका.<BR>	 2. The<BR>juice of the palmyra tree, especially when become a spirit by<BR>spontaneous fermentation.<BR> E. तर fare, ठक् affix, of तारक fem. form<BR>or ताली and कन् added, ल changed to र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=311-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तारिन्
तारिन् mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि) Enabling or causing to cross or get over.<BR>	 f.<BR>(-णी)<BR>	 1. A goddess peculiar to the Jainas or Bauddhas.<BR>	 2. A<BR>name of DURGĀ.<BR> E. तॄ to cause to proceed, (life, fortune, &c.) and<BR>ङीष् aff. तारयति तॄ-णिच्-णिनि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=311-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तारीष
तारीष m. (-षः)<BR>	 1. Svarga or paradise.<BR>	 2. The ocean.<BR>	 3. Gold.<BR>	 f. (-षी)<BR>The daughter of INDRA.<BR> E. तॄ to cross, ईषन् affix, fem. affix ङीष्ः<BR>see तरीष and तरिष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=311-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तारुण्य|तारुण्यं
तारुण्य n. (-ण्यं) Youth.<BR> E. तरुण young, ष्यञ् aff. तरुणस्य भावः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=311-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तारेय|तारेयः
तारेय m. (-यः) The son of BALI, the monkey.<BR> E. तारा the wife of BALI,<BR>and ढक् aff. तारायाः अपत्यम् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=311-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तार्कव|तार्क्कव
तार्कव mfn. (-वः-वी-वं) Spun, made with or belonging to a spindle. E.<BR>तर्कु, and अण् aff. तर्कोर्विकारः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=311-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तार्किक|तार्किकः|तार्क्किक
तार्किक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Relating or attached to the science of reason-<BR>ing or logic.<BR>	 m. (-कः) A philosopher, a sophist, a follower of either<BR>of the six schools of Hindu philosophy.<BR> E. तर्क doubt, disputation,<BR>affix ठञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=311-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तार्क्ष|तार्क्षः
तार्क्ष m. (-र्क्षः) A name of KAŚYAPA.<BR> E. तृक्ष एव स्वार्थे अण् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=311-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तार्क्ष्य|तार्क्ष्यं|तार्क्ष्यः
तार्क्ष्य m. (-र्क्ष्यः)<BR>	 1. A horse.<BR>	 2. A name of GARUḌA, the bird and vehicle<BR>of VIṢṆU.<BR>	 2. A name of ARUṆA, or the dawn personified, consi-<BR>dered as the elder brother of GARUḌA.<BR>	 4. A car, a chariot.<BR>	 5. A<BR>snake.<BR>	 6. Gold.<BR>	 7. A tree, the Sal, (Shorea robusta.)<BR>	 n. (-र्क्ष्यं) A<BR>sort of collyrium.<BR>	 f. (-र्क्ष्यी) A wild creeper.<BR> E. तृक्ष् to go, घञ् affix<BR>तार्क्ष and यञ् added; again, तृक्ष or तार्क्ष considered as a name of<BR>KAŚYAPA the father of ARUṆA, &c. ष्यञ् or अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=311-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तार्क्ष्यध्वज|तार्क्ष्यध्वजः
तार्क्ष्यध्वज m. (-जः) A name of VIṢṆU.<BR> E. तार्क्ष्य GARUḌA, and ध्वज emblem<BR>or symbol. तार्क्ष्यः ध्वजः अस्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=311-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तार्क्ष्यनायक|तार्क्ष्यनायकः
तार्क्ष्यनायक m. (-कः) GARUḌA.<BR> E. तार्क्ष्य, and नायक leader.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=311-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तार्क्ष्यशैल|तार्क्ष्यशैलं
तार्क्ष्यशैल n. (-लं) A substance prepared from the calx of brass, or from<BR>the Amomum Anthorrhiza, and used as a medical application to<BR>the eyes: see रसाञ्जन.<BR> E. तार्क्ष्य a collyrium, and शैल derived from<BR>शिला a rock or stone. तार्क्ष्य शैले भवम् अण् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=311-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तार्य्य|तार्य
तार्य्य mfn. (-र्य्यः-र्य्या-र्य्यं) To be crossed or carried across, to be ferried<BR>over.<BR>	 n. (-र्य्यं) Toll, fare, freight.<BR> E. तॄ to cross. कर्मणि ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=311-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताल|तालं|तालः
ताल mfn. (-लः-ली-लं) Made of the palm wood.<BR>	 m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. Beating time<BR>in music, musical time or measure.<BR>	 2. A short span, one measur-<BR>ed by the thumb and middle finger.<BR>	 3. Slapping or clapping the<BR>hands together, or against the arms, &c.<BR>	 4. The open hand with<BR>the fingers extended, the palm.<BR>	 5. A musical instrument of bell<BR>metal or brass, (a sort of cymbal,) played with a stick.<BR>	 6. The<BR>hilt of a sword or sacrificial knife, &c.<BR>	 7. The palmyra tree or<BR>fan palm, (Borassus flabelliformis.)<BR>	 8. A lock, a bolt.<BR>	 9. In proso-<BR>dy, a trochee.<BR>	 n. (-लं)<BR>	 1. The throne of DURGĀ.<BR>	 2. Yellow orpiment:<BR>see हरिताल.<BR>	 3. The fruit of the palm tree.<BR>	 f. (-ली)<BR>	 1. A sort of key<BR>or pin.<BR>	 2. A species of the mountain palm, (Corypha taliera, Rox.)<BR>3. A plant, (Flacourtia cataphracta:) see झटा and अमला.<BR>	 4. A fra-<BR>grant earth: see तुवरिका.<BR>	 5. A plant, (Curculigo orchioides.)<BR>	 6.<BR>The spirituous juice of the palm, the common Tady.<BR> E. तल् to<BR>fix or तन् to spread, affix घञ्; or in the causal form, with अच्<BR>affix fem. affix ङीष्, न changed to ल; otherwise, तड् to beat, to<BR>overcome, (disease, &c.) अच् and ङीष् affixes, and ड changed to ल;<BR>the adjective is derived from the substantive by adding अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=311-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तालक|तालकं
तालक n. (-कं)<BR>	 1. A bolt, a latch, a kind of lock for fastening a door<BR>with.<BR>	 3. Yellow orpiment.<BR>	 3. A fragrant earth.<BR> E. कन् added to<BR>the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=311-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तालकाभ|तालकाभः
तालकाभ adj.<BR>	 mfn. (-भः-भा-भं) Green.<BR>	 m. (-भः) Green, the colour. E.<BR>तालक yellow orpiment, and आभ what resembles.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=311-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तालकी
तालकी f. (-की) Toddy, or the fermented exudation of the palm trees.<BR>E. ताल to palmyra, कन् aff. or तालकस्य इयम् अण्-ङीष् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=311-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तालजटा
तालजटा f. (-टा) The fibres of the palm tree under the outer bark. E.<BR>ताल, and जटा matted hair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=311-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तालध्वज|तालध्वजः
तालध्वज m. (-जः) A name of BALARĀMA.<BR>	 f. (-जा) The name of a city. E.<BR>ताल the palm, and ध्वज a banner. तालः ध्वजः अस्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=311-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तालपत्र|तालपत्रं
तालपत्र n. (-त्रं)<BR>	 1. A hollow cylinder of gold with or without a ring<BR>attached to it, thrust through the lobe of the ear, and worn as an<BR>ornament.<BR>	 2. The palm leaf.<BR> E. ताल the palmyra, and पत्र a leaf,<BR>pieces of the leaf of this tree being rolled up and used occasion-<BR>ally for the purpose or as a substitute.<BR>	 f. (-त्री) A plant: see मूषिक-<BR>पर्णी. E. As above; the leaves resembling those of the palm tree,<BR>or the palm of the hand. तालस्य पत्रमिव । कर्णभूषणभेदे ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=311-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तालपर्ण|तालपर्णं
तालपर्ण nf. (-र्णं-र्णीं)<BR>	 1. A kind of vegetable perfume: see मुरा.<BR>	 f. (-र्णी) A<BR>sort of anise, (Anethum pammorium, Rox.)<BR> E. ताल the palm, and<BR>पर्ण a leaf, palm-leaved. ताल इव खड्गमुष्टिरिव पर्णमस्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=311-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तालपुष्पक|तालपुष्पकं
तालपुष्पक n. (-कं) A medicinal application to the eyes.<BR> E. ताल the pal-<BR>myra, पुष्प a flower, and कप् affix; perhaps prepared from the blos-<BR>soms of the palmyra. तालः खड्गमुष्टिरिव पुष्पमस्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=311-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तालप्रलम्ब|तालप्रलम्बं
तालप्रलम्ब n. (-म्बं) The fibres that grow on the cocoanut and other palms<BR>under the outer rind and from which Coir a sort of cordage,<BR>prepared.<BR> E. ताल, and प्रलम्ब what depends. ताले वृक्षे प्रलम्बते प्र +<BR>लम्ब-अच् । तालवृक्षस्य जटायाम् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=311-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तालभृत्
तालभृत् m. (-भृत्) A name of BALARĀMA.<BR> E. ताल the palm, and भृत् who<BR>retains, (as his banner or symbol:) see तालध्वज, &c. तालं ध्वजरूपेण<BR>बिभर्त्ति भृ-क्विप् । वलदेवे ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=311-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तालमय
तालमय mfn. (-यः-यी-यं) Made of the palm, &c.<BR> E. ताल, and मयट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=311-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तालमूली
तालमूली f. (-ली) A plant, (Curculigo orchioides.)<BR> E. ताल the palm, and<BR>मूल a root, having a similar root; also with कन् added तालमूलिका f.<BR>(-का) तालस्य मूलमिव मूलमस्याः ङीप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=311-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तालयन्त्र|तालयंत्र
तालयन्त्र n. (-न्त्रं)<BR>	 1. A lock, a lock and key.<BR>	 2. A small pair of pincers.<BR>E. ताल, and यन्त्र instrument.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=311-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताललक्ष्मन्
ताललक्ष्मन् m. (-क्ष्मा) A name of BALARĀMA.<BR> E. ताल, and लक्ष्मन् a mark or<BR>sign: see तालध्वज.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=311-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तालवृन्त|तालवृंत|तालवृन्तं
तालवृन्त m. (-न्तः) A fan.<BR> E. ताल the palm of the hand, and वृन्त a root-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=312-a" target="_blank">Page312-a+ 60</a>]<BR>stalk, expanding from the hand like a leaf from its stem; also<BR>with कन् added तालवृन्तक, ताले करताले वृन्तं बन्धनमस्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=311-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तालवृन्तक|तालवृन्तकं
तालवृन्तक n. (-कं) A fan, a Pankha: see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=312-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तालवेचनक|तालवेचनकः
तालवेचनक m. (-कः) A dancer, an actor.<BR> E. ताल musical tone, विच् to ob-<BR>served, ल्यु affix, तालवेचन and कन् pleonasm added; also read<BR>तालरेचनक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=312-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तालाख्या
तालाख्या f. (-ख्या) A perfume: see मुरा.<BR> E. ताल the palmyra, and आख्या<BR>a name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=312-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तालाङ्क|तालांक|तालाङ्कः
तालाङ्क m. (-ङ्कः)<BR>	 1. A name of BALARĀMA.<BR>	 2. A saw.<BR>	 3. A book.<BR>	 4. A<BR>name of ŚIVA.<BR>	 5. A man marked with every fortunate spot or sign<BR>&c.<BR>	 6. A sort of vegetable.<BR> E. ताल the tree, and अङ्क mark or em-<BR>blem. तालः तालचिह्नितः अङ्कः ध्वजोऽस्य । वलरामे ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=312-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तालावचर|तालावचरः
तालावचर m. (-रः) A dancer, an actor.<BR> E. ताल musical time, अवचर to<BR>follow or perform, affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=312-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तालि|तालिः
तालि f. (-लिः) A kind of palm, (Corypha taliera:) see ताली. तल प्रतिष्ठायां<BR>णिच् and इन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=312-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तालिक|तालिकः
तालिक mf. (-कः-का) The open of palm of the hand.<BR>	 m. (-कः) A tie, a<BR>seal, a string, &c. binding a letter or parcel of papers.<BR>	 f. (-का) A<BR>plant: see तालमूली.<BR> E. ताल as above, and ठक् aff. तालेन करतालेन<BR>निर्वृत्तः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=312-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तालित|तालितं
तालित n. (-तं)<BR>	 1. Any musical instrument.<BR>	 2. Dyed or coloured cloth.<BR>3. A string, a tie.<BR> E. ताल musical time, &c. इतच् aff. or तड-क्त डस्य ल ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=312-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तालिश|तालिशः
तालिश m. (-शः) A mountain.<BR> E. ताल् to be fixed, ईश Uṇādi affix, the<BR>radical vowel made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=312-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तालीश|तालीशं
तालीश n. (-शं) A tree, commonly Talis or its leaf.<BR> E. ताल the corypha,<BR>ईश what resembles. तालीव रीगान् शवति शो-ड ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=312-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तालीशपत्र|तालीशपत्रं
तालीशपत्र n. (-त्रं)<BR>	 1. A plant, (Flacourtia Cataphracta.)<BR>	 2. A tree,<BR>Talisa or its leaf, which is used in medicine.<BR> E. तालीश as above,<BR>and पत्र a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=312-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तालु
तालु n. (-लु) The palate.<BR> E. तॄ to pass, to go, Uṇādi affix ञुण् । by<BR>which words, &c. proceed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=312-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तालुका
तालुका f. (-का) The palate.<BR> E. तालु, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=312-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तालुजिह्व|तालुजिह्वः
तालुजिह्व m. (-ह्वः)<BR>	 1. The uvula.<BR>	 2. A crocodile.<BR> E. तालु the palate, and<BR>जिह्वा the tongue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=312-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तालुपुप्पुट|तालुपुप्पुटः
तालुपुप्पुट m. (-टः) An indolent swelling of the palate.<BR> E. तालुगतरोगभेदे ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=312-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तालूर|तालूरः
तालूर m. (-रः) A whirlpool, an eddy.<BR> E. तल् to be deep, ऊरन् affix; also<BR>read तालुर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=312-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तावक
तावक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Thine.<BR> E. तवक, and अण् added युष्मद् + अण्-एकवचने तवकादेशः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=312-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तावकीन|तावकीनं
तावकीन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Thine.<BR> E. तवक for तव thine, and खञ् aff. तव इदं<BR>युध्मद् + खञ् एकवचने तवकादेशः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=312-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तावत्|तावन्त्
तावत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>	 1. So many, as many, as much.<BR>	 2. All. ind.<BR>So much, so far, so many, unto, until, the correlative to यावत्. E.<BR>तत् that, then, and डावत् affix: see यावत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=312-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तावतिक
तावतिक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Of so much, worth so much, &c. see the next.<BR>E. तावता क्रीतः संख्यात्वात् कन् वतोरिड् वा पा० वा इट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=312-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तावत्क
तावत्क mfn. (-त्कः-त्का-त्कं) Of so much, bought for so much, &c.<BR> E. कन्<BR>added to तावत्; also with इट् inserted तावतिक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=312-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तावत्काल
तावत्काल adv.<BR>	 n. (-लं) For so long a period, for such a time.<BR> E. तावत्, and<BR>काल time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=312-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तावद्द्वयस
तावद्द्वयस mfn. (सः-सी-सं) Measuring so much.<BR> E. तावत्, and द्वयसच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=312-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तावन्मात्र
तावन्मात्र mfn. (-त्रः-त्री-त्रं) So much.<BR> E. तावत्, and मात्रच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=312-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तावर|तावरं
तावर n. (-रं) A bow-string.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=312-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताविष|ताविषः
ताविष m. (-षः)<BR>	 1. Svarga or paradise.<BR>	 2. The ocean.<BR>	 f. (-षी) The daugh-<BR>ter of INDRA.<BR>	 2. A river.<BR>	 3. The earth.<BR> E. तव a Sautra root, Uṇādi<BR>affix टिषच्; also read तविष, तवीष, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=312-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तावुरि|तावुरिः
तावुरि m. (-रिः) The constellation Taurus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=312-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तास्कर्य्य|तास्कर्य|तास्कर्यं
तास्कर्य्य n. (-र्य्यं) Theft, robbery.<BR> E. तस्कर, and यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=312-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिक
तिक r. 1st cl. (ऋ) तिकृ (तेकते) To go or move. r. 5th cl. (तिक्नोति)<BR>	 1. To<BR>go.<BR>	 2. To assail, to assault.<BR>	 3. To seek to injure or kill: see तिग ।<BR>भ्वा-आ-सक-सेट् । आस्कन्दे बधे च स्वा० प० अक० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=312-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिक्त|तिक्तं|तिक्तः
तिक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>	 1. Bitter.<BR>	 2. Fragrant.<BR>	 m. (-क्तः)<BR>	 1. A bitter taste,<BR>bitterness.<BR>	 3. Fragrance, perfume.<BR>	 3. A medicinal plant, (Echites<BR>antidysenterica.)<BR>	 4. A tree, (Capparis trifoliata:) see वरुण.<BR>	 f. (-क्ता)<BR>Katuki, a medicinal plant.<BR>	 n. (-क्तं) A medicinal plant, (Mollugo<BR>pentaphylla.)<BR> E. तिज् to sharpen, (the appetite,) affix कर्त्तरि क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=312-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिक्तक|तिक्तकः
तिक्तक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A kind of gourd, (Trichosanthes diœca, Rox.)<BR>	 2. A<BR>sort of gentian, (G. cherayta.)<BR>	 3. A dark sort of the Khayar or<BR>Mimosa catechu.<BR> E. कन् added to तिक्त a bitter; alluding to the<BR>taste of these substances.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=312-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिक्तगन्धा
तिक्तगन्धा f. (-न्धा) A plant, (Lycopodium imbricatum, Rox.)<BR> E. तिक्त fra-<BR>grant, and गन्ध smell, fem. affix टाप्; also with कन् added, and the<BR>fem. form, तिक्तगन्धिका ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=312-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिक्ततुम्बी
तिक्ततुम्बी f. (-म्बी) A bitter gourd.<BR> E. तिक्त, and तुम्बी a gourd.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=312-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिक्तदुग्धा
तिक्तदुग्धा f. (-ग्धा) A medicinal kind of moon plant: see स्वर्णक्षीरी.<BR> E. तिक्त<BR>bitter, and दुग्ध milk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=312-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिक्तपत्र|तिक्तपत्रः
तिक्तपत्र m. (-त्रः) A cucurbitaceous plant, (Momordica mixta.)<BR> E. तिक्त bit-<BR>ter, and पत्र a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=312-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिक्तपर्व्वन्|तिक्तपर्वन्
तिक्तपर्व्वन् f. (-र्व्वा)<BR>	 1. A potherb, (Hiliancha repens.)<BR>	 2. A plant (Menis-<BR>permum glabrum.)<BR>	 4. Liquorice.<BR> E. तिक्त bitter, and पर्व्वन् a joint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=312-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिक्तभद्रक|तिक्तभद्रकः
तिक्तभद्रक m. (-कः) A kind of cucumber, (Trichosanthes diœca.)<BR> E. तिक्त<BR>bitter, and भद्रक auspicious, useful in medicine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=312-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिक्तरोहिणिका
तिक्तरोहिणिका f. (-का) A medicinal plant: see कटुकी.<BR> E. तिक्त bitter,<BR>and रीहिणी the same plant, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=312-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिक्तवल्ली
तिक्तवल्ली f. (-ल्ली) A plant, (Aletris hyacinthoides:)<BR> E. तिक्त bitter, and<BR>वल्ली a stalk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=312-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिक्तशाक|तिक्तशाकः
तिक्तशाक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A plant (Capparis trifoliata:) see वरुण.<BR>	 2. A kind<BR>of mimosa: see खदिर.<BR> E. तिक्त bitter, and शाक an esculent vegeta-<BR>ble; also तिक्तशाकक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=312-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिक्तसार|तिक्तसारं|तिक्तसारः
तिक्तसार m. (-रः) A sort of mimosa, (M. catechu:) see खदिर.<BR> E. तिक्त<BR>bitter, and स्तर pith.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=312-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिक्तिका
तिक्तिका f. (-का) A bitter gourd.<BR> E. तिक्त, and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=312-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिग
तिग r. 5th cl. (तिग्नोति)<BR>	 1. To go or move.<BR>	 2. To assail.<BR>	 3. To seek to<BR>injure, to attempt to kill, &c. also तिक.<BR> E. स्वा० प० सक० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=312-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिग्म|तिग्मं
तिग्म mfn. (-ग्मः-ग्मा-ग्मं)<BR>	 1. Hot.<BR>	 2. Pungent, acrid.<BR>	 3. Sharp, (as a weap-<BR>on.)<BR>	 4. Passionate, hasty.<BR>	 n. (-ग्मं) Heat; also the heat of spices,<BR>or pungency.<BR> E. तिज् to sharpen, Uṇādi affix मक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=312-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिग्मता
तिग्मता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Sharpness.<BR>	 2. Pungency.<BR>	 3. Heat.<BR>	 4. Passion, petu-<BR>lance.<BR> E. तल् added to तिग्म; also with त्व, तिग्मत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=312-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिग्मरुच्
तिग्मरुच् mfn. (-रुक्)<BR>	 1. Bright, shining.<BR>	 2. Hot.<BR>	 m. (-रुक्) The sun. E.<BR>तिग्म, and रुच् light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=312-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिग्मांशु|तिग्मांशुः
तिग्मांशु m. (-शुः) The sun.<BR> E. तिग्म hot, and अंशु a ray; also similar com-<BR>pounds, as तिग्मकर, तिग्मरश्मि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=312-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिघ
तिघ r. 5th cl. (तिघ्नोति) To strike, to hurt or kill.<BR> E. स्वा० प० सक० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=312-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिङ्गुद
तिङ्गुद m. (-दः) The name of a plant: see इङ्गुद.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=312-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिज
तिज r. 1st cl. (तितिक्षते) To bear, to endure, to suffer with patience. r.<BR>1st and 10th cls. (तेजते तेजयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To whet, to sharpen.<BR>	 2. To<BR>shine: see तेज । तिज क्षान्तौ स्वार्थे सन् निशाने न सन् । भ्वा-आ-सक-सेट् ।<BR>तीक्ष्णीकरणे चुरा० उभ० सक० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=312-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिजिल|तिजिलः
तिजिल m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. The moon.<BR>	 2. A Rākṣasa.<BR> E. तिज् to shine, and इलच्<BR>Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=312-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिण्ठी
तिण्ठी f. (-ण्ठी) A plant, commonly Teori, (Convolvulus turpethum.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=312-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तितउ|तितउः
तितउ mn. (-उः-उ) A sieve, a cribble.<BR> E. तन् to spread or scatter, (grain,<BR>&c.) उउ Uṇādi affix, and the radical reiterated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=312-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तितिक्षा
तितिक्षा f. (-क्षा) Patience, resignation, sufferance, endurance.<BR> E. तिज् to<BR>bear, भावे अ and टाप् affixes, and the root repeated. स्वार्थे सन् भावे अ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=312-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तितिक्षित|तितिक्षितः
तितिक्षित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Patient, resigned.<BR> E. तिज् to bear, affix इतच्,<BR>and the root reduplicate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=312-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तितिक्षु|तितिक्षुः
तितिक्षु mfn. (-क्षुः-क्षुः-क्षु) Patient, resigned.<BR> E. तिज् to bear, reduplicated,<BR>and स्वार्थे सन् and उ affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=312-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तितिभ|तितिभः
तितिभ m. (-भः) An insect, coccinella.<BR> E. तितीति भणति भण-ड । इन्द्रगोपकीटे ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=312-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तितिल|तितिलं
तितिल n. (-लं)<BR>	 1. One of the seven Karanas, or astronomical periods so<BR>called.<BR>	 2. A bowl or bucket.<BR>	 3. A sort of sweetmeat made of sesa-<BR>mum, ground and baked with sugar.<BR> E. तिल to go, affix क, and the<BR>radical reiterated: see तैतिल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=313-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तितीर्षा
तितीर्षा f. (-र्षा)<BR>	 1. Wish to cross.<BR>	 2. Wish to be freed from life.<BR> E. तॄ to<BR>cross, desid. form, अङ् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=313-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तितीर्षु
तितीर्षु mfn. (-र्षुः-र्षुः-र्षु)<BR>	 1. Desirous of crossing.<BR>	 2. Desirous of emancipa-<BR>tion from existence.<BR> E. तॄ to cross, desid. form affix उ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=313-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तित्तिर|तित्तिरः
तित्तिर m. (-रः) The francoline parridge: see the next.<BR> E. तित्ति इति शब्दं<BR>रौति रु-वा ड ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=313-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तित्तिरि|तित्तिरिः
तित्तिरि m. (रिः)<BR>	 1. The francoline parridge.<BR>	 2. The name of a Muni,<BR>and one of the early teachers of the Taittiri or Black Yajur Veda.<BR>3. The Yajur Veda named after its teachers.<BR> E. तित्ति an imitative<BR>sound, रा to make, affix कि; also with क affix तित्तिर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=313-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिथ|तिथः
तिथ m. (-थः)<BR>	 1. Fire.<BR>	 2. KĀMA^1 or love.<BR>	 3. Time.<BR> E. तिथ् to inflame,<BR>Uṇādi affix थक्, and the radical final rejected.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20260617. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/264.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=313-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिथि|तिथिः
तिथि mf. (-थिः-थिः or -थी) A lunar day, 1-30th of a whole lunation. E.<BR>अत् to go, to proceed, affix इथिन् and the radical initial rejected;<BR>also ङीष् being added तिथी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=313-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिथिक्षय|तिथिक्षयः
तिथिक्षय m. (-यः) Day of new moon.<BR> E. तिथि, and क्षय destruction. तिथीनां<BR>तिथ्युपलक्षितचन्द्रकलानां क्षयः क्षयारम्भो-यस्मिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=313-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिथिप्रणी
तिथिप्रणी m. (-णीः) The moon.<BR> E. तिथि a lunar day, प्र before, णी to get<BR>or obtain, affix क्विप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=313-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिनाशक|तिनाशकः
तिनाशक m. (-कः) A tree: see the next. तिनिशवृक्षे ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=313-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिनिश|तिनिशः
तिनिश m. (-शः) A tree, (Dalbergia ougenensis.)<BR> E. अति exceeding, निश्<BR>to meditate, affix क and the initial of the prefix rejected, deriv. irr.<BR>अतिशयेन नेशति अति + निश-क पृषो० अतेरकारलोपः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=313-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिन्तिड|तिंतिड|तिंतिडः|तिन्तिडः
तिन्तिड mf. (-डः-डी) The tamarind tree, (Tamarindous Indica.)<BR>	 m. (-डः)<BR>1. The name of a demon.<BR>	 2. Acid seasoning, sour sauce.<BR>	 3. An<BR>inauspicious period, the evil aspect of planets, &c.<BR>	 f. (-डी) Emblic<BR>myrobalan.<BR> E. तिम् to be damp or moist, अच् affix, the root redu-<BR>plicated, and ड substituted for the final म.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=313-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिन्तिडिका|तिंतिडिका
तिन्तिडिका f. (-का) The tamarind tree.<BR> E. कन् added to तिन्तिडी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=313-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिन्तिडीक|तिंतिडीक|तिन्तिडीकं|तिंतिडीकः|तिन्तिडीकः
तिन्तिडीक subst.<BR>	 mfn. (-कः-का-कं) The tamarind tree.<BR>	 n. (-कं)<BR>	 1. Acid sea-<BR>soning.<BR>	 2. The fruit of the tamarind.<BR> E. तिन्तिड as above, and इकन्<BR>Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=313-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिन्तिडीद्यूत
तिन्तिडीद्यूत n. (-तं) A kind of game, a sort of odd or even played with<BR>tamarind seeds.<BR> E. तिन्तिडी the tamarind, and द्यूत playing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=313-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिन्तिली|तिंतिली
तिन्तिली f. (-ली) The tamarind tree. E. See तिन्तिड, ल being substituted<BR>for ड; also कन् being added in the usual form, तिन्तिलिका or retain-<BR>ing the final तिन्तिलीका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=313-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिन्दु|तिंदु|तिंदुः|तिन्दुः
तिन्दु m. (-न्तुः) A species of ebony, from the fruit of which a kind of<BR>resin is obtained, that is used in India as pitch for caulking vessels,<BR>&c. (Diospyros glutinosa.)<BR> E. तिम् to be wet or moist, affix कु;<BR>also with कन् added, तिन्दुक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=313-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिन्दुक|तिंदुक|तिंदुकं|तिन्दुकं|तिंदुकः|तिन्दुकः
तिन्दुक mf. (-कः-की) A sort of ebony, (Diospyros glutinosa.)<BR>	 f. (-की) The<BR>resinous fruit of this tree: see the preceding. Also with इ substi-<BR>tuted for the final तिन्दुकि.<BR>	 n. (-कं) A Karṣa, the measure.<BR> E. तिन्दु,<BR>and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=313-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिन्दुल|तिंदुल|तिंदुलः|तिन्दुलः
तिन्दुल m. (-लः) A sort of ebony: see the preceding.<BR> E. लच् added to<BR>तिन्दु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=313-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिप
तिप (उ ऋ) उ तिपृ r. 1st cl. (तेपते) To sprinkle, to distil or drop, to ooze<BR>or leak.<BR> E. भ्वा-आ-सक-सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=313-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिम
तिम r. 4th cl. (तिम्यति) To be or become wet, damp, &c.<BR> E. दिवा० प०<BR>सक० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=313-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिम
तिम m. (-मः) A fish: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=313-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिमि|तिमिः
तिमि m. (-मिः)<BR>	 1. A whale, or a fabulous fish of an enormous size, said<BR>to be one hundred Yojanas long.<BR>	 2. The ocean.<BR> E. तम् to distress,<BR>इन् affix, and इ substituted for the radical vowel; otherwise तिम्<BR>to be wet or watery, affix कि, or with क affix तिम.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=313-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिमिकोष|तिमिकोषः
तिमिकोष m. (-षः) The ocean.<BR> E. तिमि a fish, as above, and कोष recepta-<BR>cle: also तिमिकोषक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=313-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिमिङ्गिल|तिमिंगिल|तिमिंगिलः|तिमिङ्गिलः
तिमिङ्गिल m. (-लः) A large fabulous fish: see तिमि.<BR> E. तिमि the fish so<BR>called, and गिल who swallows, (from गृ with क affix, र changed to<BR>ल) and मुम् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=313-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिमिङ्गिलगिल|तिमिंगिलगिल|तिमिङ्गिलगिलः
तिमिङ्गिलगिल m. (-लः) A fabulous fish larger than either of the preced-<BR>ing: see तिमि and तिमिङ्गिल.<BR> E. तिमिङ्गिल the fish so called, and गिल<BR>who devours.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=313-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिमित|तिमितः
तिमित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Wet, moist, moistened, damp.<BR>	 2. Steady, fix-<BR>ed, unmoved, unshaken.<BR> E. तिम् to be wet or damp, affix कर्त्तरि क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=313-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिमिर|तिमिरं|तिमिरः
तिमिर n. (-रं)<BR>	 1. Darkness.<BR>	 2. Gutta serena, total blindness from<BR>affection of the optic nerve.<BR> E. तिम् to be damp, or तम् to give pain,<BR>किरच् Uṇādi affix, in the latter case, इत् is inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=313-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिमिररिपु|तिमिररिपुः
तिमिररिपु m. (-पुः) The sun.<BR> E. तिमिर darkness, and रिपु an enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=313-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिमिष|तिमिषः
तिमिष n. (-षं)<BR>	 1. A kind of pumpkin gourd: see ग्राम्यकर्कटी.<BR>	 2. A water-<BR>melon.<BR> E. तम् to desire or be desired, इषक् affix, इत् inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=313-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिरश्चीन
तिरश्चीन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Sideways, awry, irregular.<BR> E. तिर्य्यच्, and ख aff.<BR>तिर्य्यगेव स्वार्थे ख ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=313-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिरस्
तिरस् ind.<BR>	 1. Indirectly, underhandedly, secretly, covertly.<BR>	 2. Crooked-<BR>ly, awry.<BR>	 3. A particle of abuse or depreciation.<BR> E. तॄ to go,<BR>असुक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=313-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिरस्करिणी
तिरस्करिणी f. (-णी)<BR>	 1. An outer tent, a Kanat, a wall or screen of cloth<BR>surrounding the principal tent.<BR>	 2. A veil.<BR>	 3. A curtain.<BR> E. तिरस्<BR>secret, and करिणी making; also with the antepen. vowel long,<BR>तिरस्कारिणी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=313-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिरस्कार|तिरस्कारः
तिरस्कार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Disrespect, abuse, reproach.<BR>	 2. Disappearance, con-<BR>cealment.<BR> E. तिरस् disrespect, and कार making. तिरस् + कृ-भावे घञ् ।<BR>कर्त्तरि अण् अवज्ञाकारके त्रि० ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=313-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिरस्कृत|तिरस्कृतः
तिरस्कृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Reviled, abused, reproached, censured.<BR>	 2.<BR>Veiled, hidden.<BR>	 3. Vanished, disappeared.<BR> E. तिरस्, and कृत made.<BR>तिरस् + कृ-कर्मणि क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=313-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिरस्क्रिया
तिरस्क्रिया f. (-या)<BR>	 1. Disrespect, contempt, reproach.<BR>	 2. Disappearance,<BR>concealment.<BR> E. तिरस् disrespect, and क्रिया action. तिरस् + कृ-<BR>भावे श ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=313-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिरिट
तिरिट m. (-टः) The sugar-cane.<BR> E. तॄ-वा क, इटक् । इक्षुग्रन्थौ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=313-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिरिम|तिरिमः
तिरिम m. (-मः) A kind of rice.<BR> E. तॄ-वा इमक् । शालिभेदे ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=313-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिरिय|तिरियः
तिरिय m. (-यः) A sort of rice.<BR> E. तॄ-वा इषक् । शालिभेदे ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=313-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिरीट|तिरीटं|तिरीटः
तिरीट m. (-टः) Pale Lodh, a kind of tree: see लोध्र.<BR>	 n. (-टं) A diadem,<BR>a tiara.<BR> E. तॄ to pass, इटक् Uṇādi aff. लोध्रवृक्षे ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=313-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिरोगत
तिरोगत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Disappeared, vanished, out of sight.<BR> E. तिरस्,<BR>and गत gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=313-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिरोधान|तिरोधानं
तिरोधान n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. A cover or concealment, a sheath, a veil, a cloth or<BR>cloak, any thing which withholds another from sight.<BR>	 2. Disap-<BR>pearance, the being hidden or the act of hiding or vanishing. E.<BR>तिरस् concealing, and धान having or holding. तिर + धा-भावे ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=313-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिरोहित|तिरोहितः
तिरोहित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Covered, concealed, hidden, removed or with-<BR>drawn from sight.<BR> E. तिरस् covering, धा to have, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=313-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिर्य्यक्|तिर्यक्
तिर्य्यक् ind. Crookedly, awry: see तिर्य्यच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=313-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिर्य्यक्स्रोतस्|तिर्यक्स्रोतस्
तिर्य्यक्स्रोतस् m. (-ताः) An animal, a beast or bird.<BR> E. तिर्य्यक् crookedly,<BR>and स्रोतस् motion. तिर्य्यक् स्रोतः आहारसञ्जारो यस्य । पशुपक्ष्यादौ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=313-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिर्य्यग्ज|तिर्यग्ज
तिर्य्यग्ज mfn. (-ग्जः-ग्जा-ग्जं) Born of an animal or insect.<BR> E. तिर्य्यच्,<BR>and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=313-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिर्य्यग्जाति|तिर्यग्जाति|तिर्यग्जातिः
तिर्य्यग्जाति mfn. (-तिः-तिः-ति) Of the brute species, born as an animal.<BR>	 f.<BR>(-तिः) The brute kind.<BR> E. तिर्य्यच्, and जाति species.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=313-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिर्य्यग्यवोदर|तिर्यग्यवोदर
तिर्य्यग्यवोदर n. (-रं) A barley corn.<BR> E. तिर्य्यच् curved, यव barley, उदर<BR>the interior.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=313-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिर्य्यग्यान|तिर्यग्यान|तिर्यग्यानः|तिर्य्यग्यानः
तिर्य्यग्यान m. (-नः) A crab.<BR> E. तिर्य्यक् crookedly, and यान motion,<BR>going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=313-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिर्य्यग्योनि|तिर्यग्योनि|तिर्यग्योनिः
तिर्य्यग्योनि mfn. (-निः-निः-नि) Born of or as an animal.<BR> E. तिर्य्यच्, and योनि<BR>place of birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=313-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिर्य्यग्योन्यन्वय|तिर्यग्योन्यन्वय
तिर्य्यग्योन्यन्वय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Of the brute kind.<BR>	 m. (-यः) The race or<BR>kind of animals, birds, &c.<BR> E. तिर्य्यग्योनि, and अन्वय race.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=314-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिर्य्यच्|तिर्यच्
तिर्य्यच् or तिर्य्यञ्च् mfn. (तिर्य्यङ् तिरश्ची तिर्य्यक्) Moving tortuously, going<BR>crookedly or awry, (the neuter is also used adverbially: see<BR>तिर्य्यक् m. (-र्य्यङ्)<BR>	 1. An animal, a quadruped.<BR>	 2. A bird, or any<BR>animal moving tortuously.<BR>	 f. (-र्य्यञ्ची) The female of an animal, a<BR>beast or bird.<BR> E. तिरस् crookedly, अञ्च् to go, affix क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=314-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिर्य्यञ्च्|तिर्यञ्च्
तिर्य्यच् or तिर्य्यञ्च् mfn. (तिर्य्यङ् तिरश्ची तिर्य्यक्) Moving tortuously, going<BR>crookedly or awry, (the neuter is also used adverbially: see<BR>तिर्य्यक् m. (-र्य्यङ्)<BR>	 1. An animal, a quadruped.<BR>	 2. A bird, or any<BR>animal moving tortuously.<BR>	 f. (-र्य्यञ्ची) The female of an animal, a<BR>beast or bird.<BR> E. तिरस् crookedly, अञ्च् to go, affix क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=314-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिल|तिलः
तिल r. 1st cl. (तेलति) To go. r. 6th cl. (तिलति) and 10th cl. (तेलयति-ते)<BR>1. To be unctuous or greasy.<BR>	 2. To oil or anoint.<BR> E. भ्वा० प० सक०<BR>सेट् । तुदा० प० अक० अनिट् । चुरा० उभ० अक० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=314-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिल|तिलः
तिल m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. A plant bearing an oily seed; the oil and seed being<BR>both much used in Oriental cooking, (Sesamum orientale.)<BR>	 2. A<BR>mole or spot, compared to a seed of sesamum.<BR>	 3. A small particle<BR>or portion.<BR> E. तिल् to be unctuous, affix क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=314-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिलक|तिलकं|तिलकः
तिलक mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>	 1. Spotted, freckled, a person having moles or<BR>spots.<BR>	 2. Chief, principal.<BR>	 mn. (-कः-कं) A mark or marks made with<BR>coloured earths or unguents upon the forehead, and between the<BR>eyebrows, either as an ornament or a sectarial distinction.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-कः)<BR>	 1. A freckle, a natural mark on the person.<BR>	 2. A kind of<BR>tree, commonly Tila.<BR>	 3. A sort of horse.<BR>	 4. A title, especially in<BR>composition, implying pre-eminence, as रघुवंशतिलकः the Tilaka of<BR>the race of RAGHU, a name of RAMA.<BR>	 n. (-कं)<BR>	 1. The bladder.<BR>	 2.<BR>Black Sochal salt, a factitious salt, containing sulphur and iron,<BR>&c.<BR>	 3. A disease, the appearance of dark spots on the skin, un-<BR>attended with inflammation.<BR>	 f. (-का) A kind of necklace.<BR> E. तिल<BR>sesamum, &c. कन् added, or तिल् to go or be unctuous, and<BR>क्वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=314-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिलकट|तिलकटः
तिलकट m. (-टः) The farina of sesamum.<BR> E. तिल्, and कटच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=314-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिलकल्क|तिलकल्कः
तिलकल्क n. (-ल्कं) Sesamum ground or bruised.<BR> E. तिल, and कल्क sedi-<BR>ment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=314-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिलकालक|तिलकालकः
तिलकालक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A mole, a spot on the body.<BR>	 2. A man so mark-<BR>ed.<BR> E. तिल sesamum seed, and काल black, कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=314-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिलकाश्रय|तिलकाश्रयः
तिलकाश्रय m. (-यः) The forehead.<BR> E. तिलक, and आश्रय asylum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=314-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिलकिट्ट|तिलकिट्टं
तिलकिट्ट n. (-ट्टं) The sediment or cake of sesamum after the oil is ex-<BR>tracted.<BR> E. तिल, and किट्ट sediment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=314-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिलकिन्
तिलकिन् mfn. (-की-किनी-कि)<BR>	 1. Marked with the Tilaka.<BR>	 2. Freckled,<BR>spotted.<BR> E. तिलक, and अस्त्यर्थे इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=314-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिलचूर्ण|तिलचूर्णं|तिलचूर्ण्ण
तिलचूर्ण n. (-र्णं) Sesamum ground or pounded.<BR> E. तिल, and चूर्ण powder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=314-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिलतण्डुलक|तिलतंडुलक|तिलतण्डुलकं
तिलतण्डुलक n. (-कं) An embrace, embracing.<BR> E. तिल sesamum, and तण्डुल<BR>grain, कन् affix, as agreeable as rice mixed with sesamum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=314-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिलतैल|तिलतैलं
तिलतैल n. (-लं) Sesamum oil.<BR> E. तिल, and तैलच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=314-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिलधेनु|तिलधेनुः
तिलधेनु f. (-नुः) Sesamum made up in the shape of a cow, for the<BR>purpose of being presented to Brahmans, &c.<BR> E. तिल sesamum,<BR>and धेनु a cow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=314-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिलपर्ण|तिलपर्णं|तिलपर्णः
तिलपर्ण n. (-र्णं)<BR>	 1. Sandal.<BR>	 2. The leaf of the Tila tree.<BR>	 m. (-र्णः) Turpen-<BR>tine.<BR> E. तिल, and पर्ण a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=314-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिलपर्णिका
तिलपर्णिका f. (-का) Red sandal: see the next.<BR> E. कन् added to तिलपर्णी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=314-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिलपर्णी|तिलपर्ण्णी
तिलपर्णी f. (-र्णी) Red sanders, (Pterocarpus santolinus.)<BR> E. तिल the<BR>sesamum plant, and पर्ण a leaf: also तैलपर्णी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=314-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिलपिच्चट|तिलपिच्चटं
तिलपिच्चट n. (-टं) A sort of sweetmeat, and chiefly of ground sesamum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=314-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिलपिञ्ज|तिलपिञ्जः
तिलपिञ्ज m. (-ञ्जः) Barren sesamum, bearing no blossom, or its seed<BR>yielding no oil.<BR> E. तिल sesamum, and पिञ्ज affix, in this sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=314-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिलपेज|तिलपेजः
तिलपेज m. (-जः) Barren sesamum: see the preceding.<BR> E. तिल sesamum,<BR>and पेज affix, with this sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=314-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिलमय
तिलमय mfn. (-यः-यः-यं) Made or composed of sesamum.<BR> E. तिल, and<BR>मयट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=314-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिलमयूर|तिलमयूरः
तिलमयूर m. (-रः) A kind of peafowl.<BR> E. तिल, and मयूर a peacock: marked<BR>with spots resembling the seed of the sesamum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=314-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिलरस|तिलरसः
तिलरस m. (-सः) Sesamum oil.<BR> E. तिल, and रस extract.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=314-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिलस्नेह|तिलस्नेहः
तिलस्नेह n. (-हं) Oil, especially from sesamum.<BR> E. तिल, and स्नेह grease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=314-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिलहोम|तिलहोमः
तिलहोम n. (-मं) Burnt offering of sesamum.<BR> E. तिल, and होम burnt<BR>offering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=314-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिलापत्या
तिलापत्या f. (-त्या) A plant, bearing a small pungent seed (Nigella In-<BR>dica.)<BR> E. तिल sesamum, and अपत्य offspring as it were, from the<BR>resemblance of the seeds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=314-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिलत्स
तिलत्स m. (-त्सः) A large snake, according to some, the same as the<BR>Gokhura, to others the Boa, (Boa constrictor.)<BR> E. तिलत् here said to<BR>imply motion, षो to destroy, and क affix, destroying life or<BR>loco-motion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=314-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिलोत्तमा
तिलोत्तमा f. (-मा) One of the courtezans of Svarga.<BR> E. तिल a mole, and<BR>उत्तम excellent, beautiful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=314-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिलोदक
तिलोदक n. (-कं) Sesamum seeds and water, as an oblation.<BR> E. तिल, and<BR>उदक water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=314-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिलौदन|तिलौदनं|तिलौदनः
तिलौदन n. (-नं) A dish of milk, rice, and sesamum.<BR> E. तिल sesamum,<BR>and ओदन boiled rice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=314-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिल्य|तिल्यं
तिल्य n. (-ल्यं) A field of sesamum.<BR> E. तिल with यत् aff. तिलानां भवनं<BR>क्षेत्रम् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=314-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिल्ल
तिल्ल r. 1st cl. (तिल्लति) To go or move.<BR> E. भ्वा-प-सक-सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=314-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिल्व|तिल्वः
तिल्व m. (-ल्वः) A pale sort of Lodh: see लोध्र.<BR> E. तिल् to anoint, and क<BR>affix; also with कन् added तिल्वक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=314-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिष्ठत्|तिष्ठन्त्
तिष्ठत् mfn. (ष्ठन्-ष्ठन्ती-ष्ठत्) Staying, abiding, standing, being.<BR> E. स्था to<BR>stay, &c. शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=314-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिष्ठद्गु|तिष्ठद्गुः
तिष्ठद्गु n. (-द्गु) Evening, sunset, the time which a cow stands to be<BR>milked, &c.<BR> E. स्था to sound, गौ a cow. तिष्ठन्त्यः गावः यस्मिन् काले ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=314-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिष्य|तिष्यः
तिष्य mfn. (-ष्यः-ष्या-ष्यं) Auspicious, fortunate, lucky.<BR>	 m. (-ष्यः)<BR>	 1. The<BR>eighth Nakshatra or lunar mansion, an asterism figured by an<BR>arrow, and containing three stars, of which one is Cancri.<BR>	 2. The<BR>month Pausha, (December-January.)<BR>	 3. The Kali Yuga, the fourth<BR>and present age.<BR>	 f. (-ष्या) Emblic myrobalan, (Phyllanthus emblica.)<BR>E. तुष् to please er delight, affix क्यप्, and इत् substituted for the<BR>penultimate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=314-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिष्यक|तिष्यकः
तिष्यक m. (-कः) The month Pausha: see the preceding.<BR> E. कन् added to<BR>तिष्य, the moon being then in that asterism.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=314-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिष्यपुष्पा
तिष्यपुष्पा f. (-ष्पा) Emblic myrobalan.<BR> E. तिष्य auspicious, and पुष्प a<BR>flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=314-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिष्यफला
तिष्यफला f. (-ला) Emblic myrobalan: see तिष्य.<BR> E. तिष्य auspicious, and<BR>फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=314-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिहन्
तिहन् m. (-हा)<BR>	 1. Sickness.<BR>	 2. Rice.<BR>	 3. A bow.<BR>	 4. A good disposition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=314-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीक
तीक (-ऋ) तीकृ r. 1st cl. (तिकते) To go or move.<BR> E. भ्वा० आ० सक०<BR>सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=314-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीक्ष्ण|तीक्ष्णं|तीक्ष्णः
तीक्ष्ण mfn. (-क्ष्णः-क्ष्णा-क्ष्णं)<BR>	 1. Hot, warm.<BR>	 2. Hot, pungent.<BR>	 3. Self-devoted,<BR>self-abandoning, committing suicide, &c.<BR>	 4. Zealous, active, warm.<BR>5. Keen, intelligent.<BR>	 6. Devout, ascetic, a devotee, a zealot.<BR>	 7.<BR>Sharp, (as a sword.)<BR>	 n. (-क्ष्णं)<BR>	 1. Heat, warmth.<BR>	 2. Poison.<BR>	 3. Iron.<BR>4. War, battle.<BR>	 5. Plague, pestilence, epidemic, destruction.<BR>	 6.<BR>Death, dying.<BR>	 7. Any weapon.<BR>	 8. Haste, hurry.<BR>	 9. Sea salt.<BR>	 10.<BR>The scrotum or testicles.<BR>	 11. Any metal.<BR>	 12. Pungency, the heat<BR>of pepper, &c.<BR>	 m. (-क्ष्णः) Nitre.<BR>	 f. (-क्ष्णा)<BR>	 1. Orris root.<BR>	 2. The cast<BR>skin of a snake.<BR> E. तिज् to sharpen or be sharp, Uṇādi affix<BR>क्स्न ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=314-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीक्ष्णक|तीक्ष्णकः
तीक्ष्णक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. The scrotum or the testicles.<BR>	 2. White mustard. E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=314-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीक्ष्णकण्टक|तीक्ष्णकण्टकः
तीक्ष्णकण्टक m. (-कः) Thorn apple, (Datura metel.)<BR> E. तीक्ष्ण sharp, and<BR>कण्टक a thorn. १ धुस्तूरे, २ वर्वुरे, ३ इङ्गुदीवृक्षे, ४ वंशे, ५ कन्थारीवृक्षे स्त्री-<BR>टाप् । ६ तीक्ष्णकण्टकयुक्ते त्रि०, ७ तीक्ष्णकण्टके पु० न० ।<BR> E. तीक्ष्णः कण्टकोऽस्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=314-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीक्ष्णकन्द|तीक्ष्णकंद|तीक्ष्णकन्दः
तीक्ष्णकन्द m. (-न्दः) The onion.<BR> E. तीक्ष्ण pungent, and कन्द root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=314-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीक्ष्णकर्म्मन्|तीक्ष्णकर्मन्
तीक्ष्णकर्म्मन् mfn. (-र्म्मा-र्म्मा-र्म्म) Active, zealous.<BR> E. तीक्ष्ण sharp, keen, and<BR>कर्म्मन् conduct.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=314-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीक्ष्णगन्ध|तीक्ष्णगन्धः
तीक्ष्णगन्ध m. (-न्धः)<BR>	 1. Morunga hyperanthera.<BR>	 2. The gum olibanum tree.<BR>3. Small cardamoms.<BR>	 4. A tree: see जियती.<BR>	 f. (-न्धा)<BR>	 1. Mustard<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=315-a" target="_blank">Page315-a+ 60</a>]<BR>seed.<BR>	 2. Orris root.<BR>	 3. Pandanus odoratissimus.<BR> E. तीक्ष्ण sharp, and<BR>गन्ध smell; also with कन् added तीक्ष्णगन्धक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=314-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीक्ष्णतण्डुला
तीक्ष्णतण्डुला f. (-ला) Long-pepper.<BR> E. तीक्ष्ण pungent, and तण्डुल grain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=315-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीक्ष्णतैल|तीक्ष्णतैलं
तीक्ष्णतैल n. (-लं)<BR>	 1. Resin.<BR>	 2. The milky juice of the Euphorbia.<BR>	 3.<BR>Spirituous or vinous liquor.<BR> E. तीक्ष्ण hot, pungent, and तैल oil,<BR>unguent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=315-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीक्ष्णदंष्ट्र|तीक्ष्णदंष्ट्रः
तीक्ष्णदंष्ट्र m. (-ष्ट्रः) A tiger.<BR> E. तीक्ष्ण sharp, and दंष्ट्र a tooth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=315-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीक्ष्णधार|तीक्ष्णधारः
तीक्ष्णधार mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Sharp-edged, sharp.<BR> E. तीक्ष्ण, and धारा edge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=315-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीक्ष्णपत्र|तीक्ष्णपत्रः
तीक्ष्णपत्र m. (-त्रः) Coriander.<BR> E. तीक्ष्ण pungent, and पत्र a leaf. तुम्बुरुवृक्षे ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=315-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीक्ष्णपुष्प|तीक्ष्णपुष्पं
तीक्ष्णपुष्प n. (-ष्प) Cloves.<BR> E. तीक्ष्ण pungent, and पुष्प flower. लवङ्गे ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=315-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीक्ष्णफल|तीक्ष्णफलः
तीक्ष्णफल m. (-लः) Coriander.<BR> E. तीक्ष्ण pungent, and फल fruit, bearing<BR>pungent seeds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=315-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीक्ष्णरस|तीक्ष्णरसः
तीक्ष्णरस m. (-सः) Saltpetre.<BR> E. तीक्ष्ण sharp, and रस juice. यवक्षारे ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=315-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीक्ष्णशूक|तीक्ष्णशूकः
तीक्ष्णशूक m. (-कः) Barley.<BR> E. तीक्ष्ण sharp, and शूक awn. यवे ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=315-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीक्ष्णाग्नि|तीक्ष्णाग्निः
तीक्ष्णाग्नि m. (-ग्निः) Heart-burn, dyspepsia.<BR> E. तीक्ष्ण, and अग्नि digestion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=315-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीक्ष्णायस|तीक्ष्णायसं
तीक्ष्णायस mfn. (-सः-सी-सं) Made of steel, sharp.<BR>	 n. (-सं) Steel.<BR> E. तीक्ष्ण,<BR>अयस् iron, टच् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=315-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीम
तीम r. 4th cl. (तीम्यति) To be wet or moist: see तिम । दिवा० प० अक०<BR>सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=315-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीर|तीरं|तीरः
तीर r. 10th cl. (तीरयति-ते) To finish or complete, to get through or<BR>over.<BR> E. चुरा० उत्र० अक० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=315-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीर|तीरं|तीरः
तीर n. (-रं)<BR>	 1. A shore, a bank.<BR>	 2. An arrow.<BR>	 m. (-रः) Tin.<BR>	 f. (-री) A<BR>kind of arrow<BR> E. तीर् to get through or over, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=315-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीरभक्ति
तीरभक्ति m. (-क्तिः) Tirhut, a province in the east of central Hindustan,<BR>lying on the north of Behar.<BR> E. तीर a bank, and भक्ति here<BR>signifying a limit: being bounded on the west and east by the<BR>Gandaki and Kausiki rivers, on the south by the Ganges, and on<BR>the north, by the skirts of the Himālaya mountains.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=315-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीराट
तीराट m. (-टः) Lodh: see तिरीट.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=315-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीरान्तर
तीरान्तर n. (-रं) The opposite bank or shore.<BR> E. तीर, and अन्तर beyond.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=315-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीरित|तीरितं
तीरित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Adjudged, settled, finished.<BR>	 n. (-तं)<BR>	 1. Completion<BR>of any act or affair.<BR>	 2. Corrupt or improper non-infliction of a sen-<BR>tence.<BR> E. तीर् to get through, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=315-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीर्ण|तीर्णः
तीर्ण mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-र्णं)<BR>	 1. Crossed, passed over.<BR>	 2. Spread, expanded.<BR>3. Surpassed, excelled.<BR> E. तॄ to pass, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=315-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीर्णपदी
तीर्णपदी f. (-दी) A plant: see तालमूली.<BR> E. तीर्ण spreading, and पाद foot<BR>or root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=315-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीर्णवत्
तीर्णवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Crossed, having crossed.<BR> E. तॄ to cross,<BR>affix क्तवतु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=315-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीर्थ|तीर्थं|तीर्थः
तीर्थ mn. (-र्थः-र्थं)<BR>	 1. Sacred science, or any of the branches of knowlege<BR>esteemed holy.<BR>	 2. A holy place of pilgrimage, as Benares, &c. but es-<BR>pecially particular sports along the course of sacred streams, as the<BR>Ganges, &c. and in the vicinity of some piece of water or sacred springs.<BR>3. Any piece of water.<BR>	 4. A Ghat or stairs of a landing place.<BR>	 5. A<BR>sacred preceptor, a Guru.<BR>	 6. Sacrifice.<BR>	 7. An Avatar or descent of<BR>a diety.<BR>	 3. A school of philosophy, a Darsana a sect.<BR>	 9. A coun-<BR>sellor, an adviser.<BR>	 10. An expedient, a means of success.<BR>	 11. The<BR>menses.<BR>	 12. Pudendum muliebre.<BR>	 13. A vessel.<BR>	 14. A royal vessel.<BR>15. Brahman.<BR>	 16. Ascertainment of disease.<BR>	 17. Fire.<BR>	 18. A part<BR>of the hand sacred to any deity, as between the thumb and finger<BR>to the manes, the root of the thumb to BRAMHA, &c.<BR> E. तॄ to pass<BR>over, थक् Uṇādi affix; by which persons are extricated from sin,<BR>difficulty, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=315-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीर्थकर|तीर्थकरः
तीर्थकर m. (-रः) One of the synonyms of a Jina or sanctified teacher of<BR>the Jaina sect.<BR> E. तीर्थ pure, purity, and कर who does or acts; also<BR>retaining the nasal. तीर्थङ्कर. तीर्थं शास्त्रं करोति कृ-ट ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=315-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीर्थकृत्
तीर्थकृत् m. (-कृत्) A Jina: see the preceding.<BR> E. तीर्थं शास्त्रं कोरति कृ-क्विप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=315-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीर्थध्वाङ्क्ष|तीर्थध्वांक्ष|तीर्थध्वाङ्क्षः
तीर्थध्वाङ्क्ष m. (-ङ्क्षः) An epithet of contempt, a crow, as it were, at a<BR>pilgrimage.<BR> E. तीर्थ, and ध्वाङ्क्ष a crow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=315-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीर्थराजी
तीर्थराजी f. (-जी) A name of Benares.<BR> E. तीर्थ a holy place, and राजी the<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=315-b" target="_blank">Page315-b+ 60</a>]<BR>assemblage: the most eminent of the Tirtthas or places of<BR>pilgrimage. तीर्थानां राजिरत्र । काश्याम् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=315-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीर्थवाक|तीर्थवाकः
तीर्थवाक m. (-कः) A curl of hair.<BR> E. तीर्थ, and वच् to speak, and affix<BR>घञ् । तीर्थस्य इव वाको वचनमस्य डत्तमाङ्गस्थित्या प्रशंसनीयत्वात् । केशे ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=315-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीर्थसेविन्
तीर्थसेविन् mf. (-वी-विनी)<BR>	 1. A pilgrim.<BR>	 2. A sort of crane, (Ardea<BR>nivea.)<BR> E. तीर्थ, and सेविन् who frequents. तीर्थं जलप्रान्तं सेवते । सेव-णिनि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=315-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीव
तीव r. 1st. cl. (तीवति) To be large, to be fat or corpulent.<BR> E. भ्वा० प०<BR>अक० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=315-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीवर|तीवरः
तीवर m. (-रः) The ocean.<BR>	 2. A hunter, one who lives by killing and<BR>selling game.<BR>	 3. A fisherman, one who lives by fishing.<BR>	 f. (-री) The<BR>wife of a hunter.<BR> E. तॄ to go, to pass or cross, ष्वरच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=315-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीव्र|तीव्रं|तीव्रः
तीव्र mfn. (-व्रः-व्रा-व्रं)<BR>	 1. Much, excessive, endless, unbounded, unlimit-<BR>ed.<BR>	 2. Pungent.<BR>	 3. Hot, warm.<BR>	 m. (-व्रः) A name of ŚIVA.<BR>	 f. (-व्रा)<BR>1. A medicinal plant, Katuki.<BR>	 2. Black mustard.<BR>	 3. A sort of<BR>Durva or bent grass, (गण्डदूर्व्वा)<BR>	 4. The name of a river in the east<BR>of Bengal; also the Chandi or Padmabati. adv.<BR>	 n. (-व्रं)<BR>	 1. Much,<BR>excessively, endless.<BR>	 2. Violently, fiercely. subst.<BR>	 1. A shore, a<BR>bank.<BR>	 2. Tin.<BR>	 3. Heat.<BR>	 4. Pungency.<BR> E. तीव् to be large, &c. रक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=315-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीव्रवेदना
तीव्रवेदना f. (-ना) Agony, excessive pain, the pain of damnation.<BR> E. तीव्र<BR>exceeding, and वेदना pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=315-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तु
तु r. 2nd cl. (तौति or तवति)<BR>	 1. To go or move.<BR>	 2. To thrive or increase.<BR>3. To injure, to hurt or kill.<BR>	 4. To become full. According to some<BR>authorities this is merely a Sautra root. वृत्तौ, वृद्धौ अक० हिंसायां जेतरि<BR>सक० अदा० प० अनिट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=315-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तु
तु ind. A particle, implying.<BR>	 1. Difference, (but, or.)<BR>	 2. Disjunction,<BR>(but, again, further, other.)<BR>	 3. Connection, (and, moreover.)<BR>	 4. As-<BR>severation, (indeed.)<BR>	 4. An expletive.<BR> E. तुद्-डु ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=315-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुकाक्षीरी
तुकाक्षीरी f. (-री) The manna of bamboos; also तुगा and तुगाक्षीरी. वंशरोचनायाम् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=315-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुगा
तुगा f. (-गा) The manna of bamboos. वंशरोचनायाम् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=315-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुगाक्षीरी
तुगाक्षीरी f. (-री) Bamboo manna वंशरोचनायाम् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=315-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुङ्ग|तुंग|तुङ्गः
तुङ्ग mfn. (-ङ्गः-ङ्गा-ङ्गं)<BR>	 1. High, elevated, lofty.<BR>	 2. Chief, principal.<BR>	 3.<BR>Passionate, hot.<BR>	 m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>	 1. A tree, (Rottleria tinctoria.)<BR>	 2. A<BR>mountain.<BR>	 3. The planet Mercury.<BR>	 4. The superior apsis or aphe-<BR>lion of a planet.<BR>	 5. Top, vertex, altitude.<BR>	 6. The cocoanut tree.<BR>	 f.<BR>(-ङ्गी)<BR>	 1. A kind of basil, (Ocymum gratissimum.)<BR>	 2. Turmeric.<BR>	 3.<BR>Night.<BR>	 f. (-ङ्गा) Bamboo manna.<BR> E. तुजि to guard, to dwell, to hurt,<BR>&c. affix घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=315-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुङ्गक|तुङ्गकः
तुङ्गक m. (-कः) A tree, (Rottleria tinctoria.)<BR> E. स्वार्थे कन् added to the<BR>preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=315-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुङ्गता
तुङ्गता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Loftiness.<BR>	 2. Passionateness.<BR> E. तल् added to तुङ्ग; also<BR>with त्व, तुङ्गत्वम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=315-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुङ्गभद्र|तुंगभद्र|तुङ्गभद्रः
तुङ्गभद्र m. (-द्रः) A restive elephant or one in rut.<BR>	 f. (-द्रा) A river in the<BR>Mysore country, the Toombhadra.<BR> E. तुङ्ग lofty, tall, &c. and भद्र<BR>auspicious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=315-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुङ्गशेखर|तुंगशेखर|तुङ्गशेखरः
तुङ्गशेखर m. (-रः) A mountain.<BR> E. तुङ्ग lofty, and शेखर crest or summit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=315-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुङ्गिन्|तुंगिन्
तुङ्गिन् mfn. (-ङ्गी-ङ्गिनी-ङ्गि) High, lofty.<BR>	 m. (-ङ्गी) A planet at the apex of<BR>its orbit, or of its position, with regard to others considered as-<BR>trologically.<BR> E. तुङ्ग, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=315-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुङ्गीपति|तुंगीपति|तुङ्गीपतिः
तुङ्गीपति m. (-तिः) The moon.<BR> E. तुङ्गी night, and पति master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=315-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुङ्गीश|तुंगीश|तुङ्गीशः
तुङ्गीश m. (-शः)<BR>	 1. A name of ŚIVA.<BR>	 2. The moon.<BR>	 3. The son.<BR>	 4. A name<BR>of KṚṢṆA.<BR> E. तुङ्गी night or तुङ्ग a mountain, &c. and ईश lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=315-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुच्छ|तुच्छं|तुच्छः
तुच्छ mfn. (-च्छः-च्छा-च्छं)<BR>	 1. Void, empty.<BR>	 2. Small, little.<BR>	 3. Abandoned,<BR>deserted.<BR>	 4. Low, contemptible.<BR>	 n. (-च्छं) Chaff.<BR> E. तुद-सम्प० क्विप् ।<BR>तुदा व्यथया छ्यति छो-क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=315-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुच्छधान्यक|तुच्छधान्यकं|तुच्छधान्यकः
तुच्छधान्यक n. (-कं) Straw.<BR> E. तुच्छ, and धान्यक grain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=315-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुच्छद्रु|तुच्छद्रुः
तुच्छद्रु m. (-द्रुः) The castor-oil tree.<BR> E. तुच्छ empty, pithless, द्रु a tree;<BR>having no sap.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=315-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुज्
तुज् m. (-तुक्) Offspring, children.<BR> E. तुज् to guard, affix क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=315-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुज|तुजः
तुज r. 1st cl. (तोजति) To kill or hurt. (इ) तुजि r. 1st cl. (तुञ्जति) To<BR>guard or protect. r. 1st and 10th cls. (तुञ्जति तुञ्जयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=316-a" target="_blank">Page316-a+ 60</a>]<BR>dwell, to abide.<BR>	 2. To be strong or vigorous.<BR>	 3. To give.<BR>	 4. To<BR>hurt, to injure or kill.<BR>	 4. To shine.<BR> E. प्रापणे हिंसायां च भ्वा० प० सक०<BR>बले इदित् सेट् । चुरा० उभ० अक० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=315-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुञ्ज|तुंज
तुञ्ज mfn. (-ञ्जः-ञ्जा-ञ्जं) Noxious, mischievous.<BR>	 m. (-ञ्जः) A Daitya, a de-<BR>mon.<BR> E. तुजि to hurt, affix अच् । दैत्ये वज्रे च ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=316-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुट
तुट r. 5th cl. (तुटति)<BR>	 1. To dispute, to quarrel, to wrangle.<BR>	 2. To hurt<BR>or injure.<BR> E. तुदा० कुटा० पर० अक० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=316-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुटुम|तुटुमः
तुटुम m. (-मः) A rat.<BR> E. तुट् to injure, affix उम.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=316-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुड
तुड (ऋ) तुडृ द्विधाकरणे (तोडति) also (इ) तुडि r. 1st cl. निष्पीडने (तुण्डते) also<BR>तुड r. 6th cl. भेदे (तुडति) 1. To tear, to break or cut, to pull to<BR>pieces, to hurt or kill.<BR> E. भ्वा० पर० सक० इदित् सेट् । तुदा० कुटा० पर०<BR>अक० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=316-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुड्ड
तुड्ड r. 1st cl. (तुड्डति) To disrespect.<BR> E. भ्वा० पर० सक० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=316-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुण
तुण r. 6th cl. (तुणति)<BR>	 1. To curve, to bend or make crooked.<BR>	 2. To act<BR>fraudulently.<BR> E. तुदा० पर० सक० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=316-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुणि|तुणिः
तुणि m. (-णिः) A timber tree: see तुन्न.<BR> E. तूण् to shrink or wrap, affix<BR>इन्, and the radical vowel made short.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=316-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुण्ड|तुंड|तुंडं|तुण्डं|तुण्डः
तुण्ड m. (-ण्डः) The mouth, the face.<BR> E. तुडि to tear, (food, &c.) affix अच्,<BR>and कन् being added तुण्डक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=316-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुण्डकेरी
तुण्डकेरी f. (-री) A cucurbitaceous plant, (Momordica monadelpha.) E.<BR>तुण्डक the mouth, ऋ to go, अण् and ङीष् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=316-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुण्डि|तुंडि|तुंडिः|तुण्डिः
तुण्डि mf. (-ण्डिः-ण्डी)<BR>	 1. The mouth, the face.<BR>	 2. A beak.<BR>	 3. The navel;<BR>(also तुन्दि.)<BR> E. तुडि to break or destroy, Uṇādi affix इन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=316-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुण्डिका
तुण्डिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. The naval.<BR>	 2. A plant, commonly Telakucha.<BR> E. कन्<BR>added to तुण्डी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=316-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुण्डिकेरी|तुंडिकेरी
तुण्डिकेरी f. (-री) The cotton plant.<BR>	 2. A sort of gourd, (Momordica mo-<BR>nadelpha.)<BR>	 3. A large boil or swelling on the palate.<BR> E. तुण्डिका the<BR>mouth or beak, ऋ to go, affixes अण् and ङीष्; also with कन्<BR>added तुण्डिकेरिका f. (-का) and with इन् fem. affix तुण्डिकेरि f.<BR>(-रिः) also तुण्डकेरी and तुण्डिकेशी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=316-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुण्डिकेशी
तुण्डिकेशी f. (-शी) A sort of gourd, commonly Telakucha: see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=316-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुण्डिभ|तुंडिभ|तुण्डिभः
तुण्डिभ mfn. (-भः-भा-भं)<BR>	 1. Having a prominent or elevated naval. E.<BR>तुण्डि the navel, भ affix; also तुण्डिम, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=316-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुण्डिल|तुंडिल|तुण्डिलः
तुण्डिल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>	 1. Having a prominent or elevated navel.<BR>	 2.<BR>Speaking harshly or severely.<BR> E. तुण्डि the navel, and ल affix; also<BR>तुन्दिल, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=316-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुत्थ|तुत्थं|तुत्थः
तुत्थ r. 10th cl. (तुत्थयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To screen, to veil, to cover.<BR>	 2. To spread.<BR> E. चुरा० उभ० सक० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=316-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुत्थ|तुत्थं|तुत्थः
तुत्थ m. (-त्थः) Fire.<BR>	 f. (-त्था)<BR>	 1. Indigo.<BR>	 2. Small cardamoms.<BR>	 n. (-त्थं)<BR>	 1.<BR>A collyrium extracted from the Amomum zanthorrhiza.<BR>	 2. Blue<BR>vitriol, sulphate of copper, especially medicinally considered as an<BR>Anjan, or application to the eyes.<BR> E. तुद् to pain, थक् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=316-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुत्थक|तुत्थकं
तुत्थक n. (-कं) Blue vitriol.<BR> E. कन् added to तुत्थ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=316-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुत्थाञ्जन|तुत्थांजन|तुत्थाञ्जनं
तुत्थाञ्जन n. (-नं) Blue vitriol, considered as a medicinal application to<BR>the eyes.<BR> E. तुत्थ the same, and अञ्चन a collyrium.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=316-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुद
तुद (औ) r. 6th cl. (तुदति-ते) To pain, to wound, to vex or harass, to<BR>tease, to torture or torment, (इ) तुदि r. 1st cl. (तुन्दति) To search,<BR>to seek.<BR> E. तुदा० उभ० सक० अनिट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=316-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुन्द|तुंद|तुंदं|तुन्दं|तुन्दः
तुन्द n. (-न्दं) The belly.<BR>	 f. (-न्दी) The navel: see तुण्डि.<BR> E. तुद् to torment,<BR>क affix, and नुम् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=316-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुन्दकूपी|तुंदकूपी
तुन्दकूपी f. (-पी) The navel.<BR> E. तुन्द the belly, and कूप a pit, a well, dim.<BR>affix ङीष्; also with कन् added तुन्दकूपिका f. (-का).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=316-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुन्दपरिमार्ज|तुंदपरिमार्ज|तुन्दपरिमार्ज्जः
तुन्दपरिमार्ज m. (-र्जः) A lazy man, a sloth, a sluggard: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=316-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुन्दपरिमृज|तुन्दपरिमृजः
तुन्दपरिमृज m. (-जः) A lazy man, a sluggard.<BR> E. तुन्द the belly, मृज to<BR>rub, with परि prefixed, and क affix; also with the affix घञ्, तुन्द-<BR>परिमार्ज as above; passing his whole time in stroking his sides.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=316-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुन्दवत्|तुंदवत्|तुन्दवन्त्
तुन्दवत् mfn. (-वान् वती-वत्) Corpulent, fat.<BR> E. तुन्द, and मतुप् aff. also<BR>from तुन्दि, तुन्दिवत् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=316-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुन्दि|तुंदि|तुन्दिः
तुन्दि n. (-न्दि) The belly.<BR>	 f. (-न्दिः) The navel.<BR>	 m. (-न्दिः) One of the<BR>Gandharbas or choristers of Svarga.<BR> E. तुद् to vex or harass, affix<BR>इन्, and नुम् inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=316-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुन्दिक|तुंदिक|तुन्दिकः
तुन्दिक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Having a large or prominent navel, fat, corpu-<BR>lent.<BR>	 f. (-का) The navel.<BR> E. तुन्दी the naval. कन् affix, or तुन्द with<BR>ठन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=316-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुन्दिकर|तुंदिकरः|तुन्दिकरः
तुन्दिकर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) See the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=316-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुन्दित|तुंदित|तुन्दितः
तुन्दित mfn. (तः-ता-तं) Having a large or prominent naval.<BR> E. तुन्द with<BR>इतच् affix; also तुन्दिक, तुन्दिल, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=316-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुन्दिन्|तुंदिन्
तुन्दिन् mfn. (-न्दी-न्दिनी-न्दि) Having a large or prominent navel.<BR> E. तुन्द<BR>with इनि affix; also तुन्दिक, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=316-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुन्दिभ|तुंदिभ|तुन्दिभः
तुन्दिभ See तुण्डिभ, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=316-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुन्दिल|तुंदिल|तुन्दिलः
तुन्दिल See तुण्डिल, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=316-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुन्न|तुन्नः
तुन्न mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>	 1. Tormented, vexed, injured.<BR>	 2. Cut, broken,<BR>cut down, &c.<BR>	 m. (-न्नः) Toon or Tuna, a tree of which the wood<BR>bears some resemblance to mahogany, and is used for furniture,<BR>&c. (Cedrela tunna.)<BR> E. तुद् to vex, affix क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=316-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुन्नवाय|तुन्नवायः
तुन्नवाय m. (-यः) A taylor.<BR> E. तुन्न cut, (cloth, &c.) and वे to sew, affix अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=316-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुन्नसेवनी
तुन्नसेवनी f. (-नी) A suture of the skull.<BR> E. तुन्न cut, and सेवनी a suture. तुन्नं<BR>छिन्नं सीव्यते अनया सिव-करणे ल्युट् ङीष् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=316-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुप
तुप r. 1st, 6th and 10th cls. (तोपति तुपति, तोपयति) (इ) तुपि r. 1st and<BR>10th cls. (तुम्पति, तुम्पयति-ते) To injure, to hurt or kill; also तुफ, तुम्ब,<BR>तुम्प, &c.<BR> E. भ्वा० पर० सक० सेट् । तुदा० बधे० सक० क्लेशे-मुचादि-पर-सेट् ।<BR>अदने चुरा० उभ-सक-सेट् इदित् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=316-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुफ
तुफ r. 1st, 6th and 10th cls. (तोफति, तुम्फति, तोफयति-ते) To hurt or kill.<BR>E. भ्वा-सक-सेट् । बधे सक-क्लेशे अक-तुदा-मुचा-पर-सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=316-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुब
तुब(इ)तुबि r. 1st and 10th cls. (तुम्बति तुम्बयति-ते) To kill or hurt. r. 10th<BR>cl. (तुम्बयति-ते) To disappear.<BR> E. भ्वा-पर-सेट् इदित् । पक्षे चुरा-उभ-सक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=316-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुभ
तुभ r. 1st cl. (तोभते) 4th cl. (तुभ्यति) 9th cl. (तुभ्नाति) To kill, to hurt, to<BR>injure in any manner.<BR> E. भ्वा-आत्म-लुङि उभ-सक-सेट् । दिवा-क्य्रा च पर-सक<BR>सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=316-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुमुर|तुमुरः
तुमुर mn. (-रः-रं) Mingled combat: see तुमुल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=316-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुमुल|तुमुलं|तुमुलः
तुमुल mn. (-लः-लं)<BR>	 1. Mingled or tumultuous combat.<BR>	 2. Uproar,<BR>clangour, tumult, tumultuous sound or noise.<BR>	 m. (-लः) Beleric<BR>myrobalan.<BR> E. तु a Sautra root, to kill, to injure, &c. मुलक् affix;<BR>or with the vowel long तुमूल.<BR>	 mn. (-लः-लं) and ल being changed to<BR>र, तुमुर as above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=316-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुम्प
तुम्प r. 1st and 6th cls. (तुफति, तुम्पति)<BR>	 1. To hurt or kill.<BR>	 2. To be<BR>distressed.<BR> E. भ्वा-सक-पर-सेट् । बधे सक-क्लेशे अक-तुदा-पर-सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=316-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुम्फ
तुम्फ r. 1st. cl. (तुफति, तुम्फति) To hurt or kill.<BR> E. भ्वा-पर-सक-सेट् । बधे सक-<BR>क्लेशे अक-तुदा-पर-सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=316-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुम्ब|तुंब|तुंबः|तुम्बः
तुम्ब mf. (-म्बः-म्बा or -म्बी) A long gourd, &c. See तुम्बि.<BR>	 f. (-म्बा) a cow<BR>disposed to be milked.<BR> E. तुबि to destroy, (bile, &c.) affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=316-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुम्बक|तुम्बकः
तुम्बक m. (-कः) A long gourd.<BR>	 n. (-कं) The gourd. कन् added to the<BR>preceding: see तुम्बि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=316-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुम्बि|तुंबि|तुंबिः|तुम्बिः
तुम्बि f. (-म्बिः or -तुम्बी) A long gourd, (Cucurbita lagenaris.)<BR> E. तुबि to<BR>destroy, (bile, sickness, &c.) अच् affix; fem. affix इन् or ङीष् also<BR>with कन् added तुम्बिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=316-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुम्बीपुष्प|तुम्बीपुष्पं
तुम्बीपुष्प n. (-ष्पं) The flower of the Cucurbita lagenaris.<BR> E. तुम्बी, and<BR>पुष्प a flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=316-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुम्बुरी
तुम्बुरी f. (-री)<BR>	 1. Coriander.<BR>	 2. A bitch: see तुम्बुरु.<BR> E. शम्यां धन्याके च ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=316-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुम्बुरु|तुंबुरु|तुंबुरुः|तुम्बुरुः
तुम्बुरु m. (-रुः)<BR>	 1. One of the Gandharbas or singers of heaven.<BR>	 2. A<BR>celestial inhabitant and attendant upon the sanctified Jaina teach-<BR>ers.<BR>	 n. (-रु) Coriander.<BR> E. तुबि to hurt, &c. उरन् affix; also with<BR>the pen. long तुम्बूरु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=316-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुर|तुरः
तुर r. 3rd cl. (तुतोर्त्ति) To go quick, to hurry, to make haste; this root<BR>is restricted to the Vedas: see त्वर जुहो० पर० अक० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=316-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुर|तुरः
तुर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Quick, swift.<BR> E. तुर् to make haste, क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=316-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुरग|तुरगः
तुरग m. (-गः)<BR>	 1. A horse.<BR>	 2. The mind.<BR> E. त्वर speed, velocity, and ग<BR>what goes, व changed to उ.<BR>	 f. (-गी)<BR>	 1. A plant, (Physalis flexuosa:)<BR>see अश्वगन्ध.<BR>	 2. A mare.<BR> E. ङीष् added to तुरग तुरेण वेगेन गच्छति गम-ड ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=316-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुरगगन्धा
तुरगगन्धा f. (-न्धा) A plant: see the preceding.<BR> E. तुरग a horse, and गन्ध<BR>smell, smelling like a horse; also अश्वगन्ध, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=316-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुरगब्रह्मचर्य्यक|तुरगब्रह्मचर्यक|तुरगब्रह्मचर्य्यकं
तुरगब्रह्मचर्य्यक n. (-कं) Necessary celibacy, leading a life of continence, in<BR>consequence merely of being without female society.<BR> E. तुरग a horse,<BR>and ब्रह्मचर्य्यक the practice of a religious student, one of whose<BR>duties is continence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=317-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुरगिन्
तुरगिन् mfn. (-गी-गिणी-गि) Equestrian, riding, mounted or carried in<BR>a horse.<BR>	 m. (-गी) A horse-man, cavalier, &c.<BR> E. तुरग a horse, and<BR>इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=317-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुरङ्ग|तुरंग|तुरंगः|तुरङ्गः
तुरङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>	 1. A horse.<BR>	 2. The mind, considerd as the seat of feeling<BR>as well as intellect, the heart.<BR> E. त्वर speedily, and ग what goes.<BR>	 f.<BR>(-ङ्गी)<BR>	 1. A plant: see तुरगी and तुरगगन्धा.<BR>	 2. A mare.<BR> E. ङीष् added<BR>to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=317-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुरङ्गक|तुरंगक|तुरंगकः|तुरङ्गकः
तुरङ्गक m. (-कः) A plant, a kind of Ghosha, commonly हस्तिधोष.<BR> E. तुरङ्ग<BR>a horse, and कन् affix analogy; coursing through the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=317-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुरङ्गद्विषणी|तुरंगद्विषणी
तुरङ्गद्विषणी f. (-णी) A she buffalo.<BR> E. तुरङ्ग, and द्विषणी disliking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=317-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुरङ्गप्रिय|तुरंगप्रिय|तुरङ्गप्रियः
तुरङ्गप्रिय m. (-यः) Barley.<BR> E. तुरङ्ग, and प्रिय fond of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=317-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुरङ्गम|तुरंगम|तुरंगमः|तुरङ्गमः
तुरङ्गम m. (-मः) A horse.<BR> E. तुर speed, and गम् to go, with खच् and मुम्<BR>affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=317-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुरङ्गयायिन्|तुरंगयायिन्
तुरङ्गयायिन् mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि) Going on horse-back.<BR> E. तुरङ्ग, यायिन् who<BR>goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=317-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुरङ्गवक्त्र|तुरंगवक्त्र|तुरङ्गवक्त्रः
तुरङ्गवक्त्र m. (-क्त्रः) A Kinnara or chorister of INDRA'S heaven.<BR> E. तुरङ्ग a<BR>horse, and वक्त्र a face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=317-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुरङ्गवदन|तुरंगवदन|तुरङ्गवदनः
तुरङ्गवदन m. (-नः) A celestial chorister.<BR> E. तुरङ्ग a horse, and वदन a face;<BR>these beings are described as having the bodies of men, and the<BR>heads of horse; also similar compounds, as तुरङ्गानन, तुरङ्गवक्त्र,<BR>तुरङ्गास्य, अश्ववक्त्र, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=317-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुरङ्गारि|तुरंगारि|तुरङ्गारिः
तुरङ्गारि m. (-रिः)<BR>	 1. A buffalo.<BR>	 2. Oleander.<BR> E. तुरङ्ग, and अरि foe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=317-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुरङ्गिन्|तुरंगिन्
तुरङ्गिन् m. (-ङ्गी)<BR>	 1. A horse-man, a rider.<BR>	 2. A groom.<BR> E. तुरङ्ग, and<BR>इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=317-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुरायण|तुरायणं|तुरायणः
तुरायण subst.<BR>	 mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Attachment to any object or pur-<BR>suit. adj Attached to any object or pursuit.<BR>	 m. (-णः) A particular<BR>sacrifice.<BR> E. तुर speed, haste, अय् to go, affix ल्यु; speeding towards<BR>a given end or in a certain cause: see परायण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=317-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुरासाह
तुरासाह m. (-षाट् or षाड्) A name of INDRA.<BR> E. तुर for त्वर haste, सह् to<BR>bear, in the causal form, and क्विप् affix, स being changed to ष in-<BR>flexion. हलादौ षत्वं । अजादौतु न षत्वम् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=317-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुरि|तुरिः
तुरि f. (-रिः) See the next; also तुलि.<BR> E. तुर-इन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=317-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुरी
तुरी f. (-री)<BR>	 1. A brush or a fibrous stick used by weavers to clean and<BR>separate the threads of the woof.<BR>	 2. A painter's brush, &c. see तुली.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=317-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुरीय|तुरीयं|तुरीयः
तुरीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Fourth, a fourth.<BR>	 m. (-यः) A fourth part, a quarter.<BR>n. (-यं) The divine being, or universal spirit. E. irr. derived from<BR>चतुर् four, with छ affix; also तूर्य्य and तुर्य्य । तुरीय-अच् । चतुर्णां पूरणः<BR>चतुर् + छ आद्यलोपश्च ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=317-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुरीयभाग
तुरीयभाग m. (-गः) A fourth part or share.<BR> E. तुरीय, and भाग share.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=317-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुरीयभाज्
तुरीयभाज् mfn. (-भाक्) A sharer of a fourth.<BR> E. तुरीय, and भाज् who<BR>divides.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=317-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुरीयवर्ण|तुरीयवर्णः
तुरीयवर्ण m. (-र्णः) The Śūdra or fourth tribe of the Hindus.<BR> E. तुरीय<BR>fourth, and वर्ण tribe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=317-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुरीयांश
तुरीयांश m. (-शः) A fourth part, a quarter share.<BR> E. तरीय, and अंश a share.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=317-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुरुष्क|तुरुष्कः
तुरुष्क m. (-ष्कः)<BR>	 1. Incense.<BR>	 2. A country, or m. plu. (-ष्काः) 1ts inhabit-<BR>ants; Turan or Turkestan, the original country of the Turks. E.<BR>तुर् to haste, (into smoke, &c.) affix उसिक्, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=317-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुर्य्य|तुर्य|तुर्य्यः
तुर्य्य mfn. (-र्य्यः-र्य्या-र्य्यं) Fourth. E. irr. derived from चतुर् four, with यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=317-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुर्व|तुर्व्व
तुर्व(ई)तुर्वी r. 1st cl. (तुर्वति) To hurt, to injure, to kill.<BR> E. भ्वा-पर-सक-सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=317-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुर्व्वसु|तुर्वसु|तुर्व्वसुः
तुर्व्वसु m. (-सुः) One of the sons of YAYATI, king of the south and<BR>eastern portion of India, reigning over the Mleccha tribes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=317-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुल
तुल r. 1st and 10th cls. (तोलति तुलति तोलयति-ते or irr. तुलयति) To weigh<BR>or measure.<BR> E. भ्वा-पर-सक-सेट् । पक्षे-चुरा-उभ० ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=317-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुलयित्वा
तुलयित्वा ind. Having weighed, having counterpoised, mode equal or like,<BR>&c.<BR> E. तुल् to weigh, क्त्वा. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=317-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुलसारिणी
तुलसारिणी f. (-णी) A quiver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=317-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुलसी
तुलसी f. (-सी) A small shrub held in veneration by the Hindus, Tulasi<BR>or holy basil, (Ocymum sanctum.)<BR> E. तुला resemblance, and षो to<BR>destroy, affixes ङ and ङीप्; being unparalleled: this plant is said<BR>to be a female metamorphosed. तुलां सादृश्यं स्यति सो-क गौरा० ङीष् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=317-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुला
तुला f. (-ला)<BR>	 1. Measure by weight.<BR>	 2. A measure or weight of gold and<BR>silver, 100 Palas, or about 145 ounces troy.<BR>	 3. Any balance, es-<BR>pecially a fine balance, goldsmith's or assay scales.<BR>	 4. The sign of<BR>the zodiac, Libra.<BR>	 5. Resemblance, likeness, equality, similarity.<BR>6. A vessel.<BR>	 7. Sloping beams or timbers in the roof of a house.<BR>E. तुल् to weigh or to resemble, affix अङ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=317-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुलाकोटि|तुलाकोटिः
तुलाकोटि f. (-टिः-टी)<BR>	 1. An ornament of the feet or toes.<BR>	 2. A certain<BR>weight.<BR>	 3. A hundred millions.<BR> E. तुला a balance, कुट् to measure,<BR>affixes अङ् and इन् or ङीप्; what is valued by weight, &c. or तुला<BR>a measure, &c. and कोटि Crore, or million. तुलया तुलां वा कोटयति कुट<BR>परितापे इन् वा ङीप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=317-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुलाकोश|तुलाकोशः
तुलाकोश m. (-शः) A sort of ordeal, in which the accused is tried by<BR>being weighed repeatedly in a scale: if he is lighter the second<BR>time he is pronounced innocent; if equipoised still, or heavier, he<BR>is guilty.<BR> E. तुला a scale, and कोश ordeal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=317-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुलाधट|तुलाधटः
तुलाधट m. (-टः)<BR>	 1. An oar, a paddle.<BR>	 2. The scale or cup of a balance. E.<BR>तुला, and धट a scale. तुलायै तोलनाय धटः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=317-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुलाधर|तुलाधरः
तुलाधर m. (-रः) The sun.<BR> E. तुला the sign, and धर who has or possesses.<BR>तुलाया मानदण्डस्य धरः धृ-अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=317-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुलाधार|तुलाधारः
तुलाधार mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) A trader, a dealer, trafficking, trading.<BR>	 m. (-रः)<BR>1. The sign Libra.<BR>	 2. The string of a balance.<BR>	 3. The beam.<BR> E. तुला<BR>the scales, &c. आधार what or who supports.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=317-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुलापरीक्षा
तुलापरीक्षा f. (-क्षा) Ordeal by the balance, the weight of the accused<BR>being first taken, certain prayers and ceremonies are performed,<BR>after which he is weighed again: if lighter, he is innocent, if heavy,<BR>or as at first, guilty.<BR> E. तुला, and परीक्षा test.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=317-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुलापुरुष|तुलापुरुषः
तुलापुरुष m. (-षः) A person weighed in a balance, or an effigy of him<BR>used as a weight.<BR> E. तुला, and पुरुष a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=317-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुलापुरुषदान|तुलापुरुषदानं
तुलापुरुषदान n. (-नं) Gift of gold or valuables of the weight of the donor.<BR>E. तुलापुरुष, and दान gift.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=317-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुलाप्रग्रह|तुलाप्रग्रहः
तुलाप्रग्रह m. (-हः) The string of a balance.<BR> E. तुला, and प्रग्रह holding; also तुलाप्रग्राह ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=317-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुलामान
तुलामान n. (-नं) Measure by weight.<BR> E. तुला, and मान measure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=317-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुलावीज|तुलावीजं
तुलावीज n. (-जं) The Gunja or berry of the Abrus precatorius, from<BR>which the goldsmith's or jeweller's weight in India is taken; the<BR>berry weighs about 1(5/16) grain troy, the factitious weight about<BR>2(3/16).<BR> E. तुला weight, and वीज seed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=317-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुलासूत्र
तुलासूत्र n. (-त्रं) The string of a balance.<BR> E. तुला, and सूत्र thread.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=317-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुलि|तुलिः
तुलि f. (-लिः or -ली)<BR>	 1. A fibrous stick or brush used by weavers for<BR>cleaning the threads of the woof.<BR>	 2. A painter's brush, or fibrous<BR>stick used for that purpose: see तूलिका,<BR> E. तुल् to resemble, &c. affix<BR>क, fem. affix इन् or ङीष्; also with ल changed to र, तुरि, तुरी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=317-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुलिका
तुलिका f. (-का) A small bird said to resemble the wagtail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=317-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुलित
तुलित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Made equal or like, equalled, compared.<BR>	 2.<BR>Weighed, counterpoised.<BR> E. तुल् to weigh, णिच् and कर्मणि क्त affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=317-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुलिफला
तुलिफला f. (-ला) The Simul or silk-cotton tree.<BR> E. तुलि for तूलि cotton,<BR>and फल fruit. तुलि तुलयुक्तं फलमस्याः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=317-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुल्य|तुल्यः
तुल्य mfn. (-ल्यः-ल्या-ल्यं) Like, resembling, equal or analogous to.<BR> E. तुला<BR>resemblance, and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=317-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुल्यता
तुल्यता f. (-ता) Likeness, sameness, equality.<BR> E. तल् added to the last;<BR>also with त्व, तुल्यत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=317-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुल्यपान|तुल्यपानं
तुल्यपान n. (-नं) Drinking together.<BR> E. तुल्य alike, and पान drinking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=317-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुल्यबल
तुल्यबल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Of equal strength.<BR> E. तुल्य, and बल strength.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=317-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुल्यभावन
तुल्यभावन n. (-नं) Combination of like series, (in calculation.)<BR> E. तुल्य, and<BR>भावन computing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=317-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुल्यरूप
तुल्यरूप mfn. (-पः-पा-पी-पं)<BR>	 1. Like, similar, analogous.<BR>	 2. Of like or equal<BR>form.<BR> E. तुल्य, and रूप nature, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=317-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुल्यवृत्ति
तुल्यवृत्ति mfn. (-त्तिः-त्तिः-त्ति) Following the same or similar occupation.<BR>E. तुल्य, and वृत्ति business.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=318-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुल्यशुद्धि
तुल्यशुद्धि f. (-द्धिः) Equal substraction, transposition, (in Arithmetic.) E.<BR>तुल्य, शुद्धि substraction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=318-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुल्याकृति
तुल्याकृति mfn. (-तिः-तिः-ति) Alike, of the same form.<BR> E. तुल्य, and आकृति<BR>form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=318-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुवर|तुवरः
तुवर mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>	 1. Astringent.<BR>	 2. Beardless.<BR>	 mn. (-रः-रं) An astringent<BR>taste.<BR>	 f. (-री)<BR>	 1. A fragrant earth.<BR>	 2. A kind of lentil, (Cytisus<BR>cajan:) see आढकी.<BR> E. तु a Sautra root, to remove, (disease, &c.)<BR>ष्वरच् and affix ङीष्; also कन् being added, in the fem. form तुवरिका<BR>f. (-का.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=318-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुवरीशिम्ब|तुवरीशिम्बः
तुवरीशिम्ब m. (-म्बः) A kind of cassia.<BR> E. तुवरी the pulse so called, and<BR>शिम्ब Cassia tora.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=318-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुवि|तुविः
तुवि f. (-विः) A long gourd: see तुम्बी ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=318-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुष|तुषः
तुष r. 4th cl. (ञि, औ) ञिऔतुष (तुष्यति) To be satisfied or content, to be<BR>pleased or delighted.<BR> E. दिवा-प-ऌदित् अक-सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=318-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुष|तुषः
तुष mf. (-षः-षा)<BR>	 1. The husk or chaff of rice, &c.<BR>	 2. Beleric myrobalan.<BR>E. तुष् to please or be pleased, affix क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=318-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुषग्रह|तुषग्रहः
तुषग्रह m. (-हः) Agni or fire.<BR> E. तुष chaff, and ग्रह who seizes. तुषेण गृह्यते<BR>गृह-कर्मणि अप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=318-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुषसार|तुषसारः
तुषसार m. (-रः) Agni or fire.<BR> E. तुष chaff, and सार who embraces, from<BR>सृ to go, with अण् aff. तुषं सरति अनुसरति ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=318-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुषानल|तुषानलः
तुषानल m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. A conflagration of chaff, or of the husk of corn.<BR>	 2.<BR>A capital punishment, burning; twisting dry straw, &c. round<BR>the limbs of a criminal, and setting it on fire.<BR> E. तुष, and अनल fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=318-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुषार|तुषारः
तुषार mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Cold, frigid, frosty.<BR>	 m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Frost.<BR>	 2. Cold.<BR>	 3.<BR>Thin rain, mist.<BR>	 4. Ice or snow.<BR>	 5. The name of a country.<BR> E. तुष्<BR>to please, Uṇādi affix आरन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=318-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुषारकण|तुषारकणः
तुषारकण m. (-णः)<BR>	 1. A dew drop.<BR>	 2. An icicle.<BR>	 3. Hoar frost.<BR> E. तुषार,<BR>and कण a particle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=318-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुषारकाल|तुषारकालः
तुषारकाल m. (-लः) Winter, the cold season.<BR> E. तुषार, and काल time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=318-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुषारपात
तुषारपात m. (-तः)<BR>	 1. Thin rain, a sprinkling, a shower.<BR>	 2. A fall of<BR>snow.<BR> E. तुषार, and पात falling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=318-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुषाराद्रि|तुषाराद्रिः
तुषाराद्रि m. (-द्रिः) The Himālaya mountain.<BR> E. तुषार, and अद्रि a moun-<BR>tain; also similar compounds, as तुषारपर्व्वत, तुषारशैल, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=318-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुषित|तुषितः
तुषित m. (-तः) A Tushita, a kind of subordinate deity, one of a class<BR>of thirty-six. F. तुष् to please, इतच् aff. तारका० इतच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=318-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुषोदक|तुषोदकं
तुषोदक n. (-कं) Rice gruel.<BR> E. तुष to satisfy, and उदक water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=318-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुष्ट|तुष्टः
तुष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं) Pleased, satisfied.<BR> E. तुष् to be pleased, कर्त्तरि क्त. ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=318-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुष्टि|तुष्टिः
तुष्टि f. (-ष्टिः)<BR>	 1. Pleasure, satisfaction, gratification, content.<BR>	 2. In-<BR>difference to every thing but that possessed or obtained.<BR>	 3. One<BR>of the Matris.<BR> E. तुष् to please, &c. affix भावे क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=318-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुष्टिकर
तुष्टिकर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Pleasing, satisfying.<BR> E. तुष्टि, and कर what makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=318-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुष्टिजनन
तुष्टिजनन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Gratifying, giving or producing satisfaction.<BR>E. तुष्टि, and जनन birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=318-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुष्टिद
तुष्टिद mfn. (-दः-दा-दं) Pleasing, ‘satisfying.’<BR> E. तुष्टि, and द what<BR>gives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=318-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुष्टु|तुष्टुः
तुष्टु m. (-ष्टुः) A jewel worn in the ears.<BR> E. तुष् to please, तुक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=318-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुष्ट्वा
तुष्ट्वा ind. Having pleased or gratified.<BR> E. तुष्, and क्त्वा aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=318-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुस|तुसः
तुस r. 1st cl. (तोसति) To sound.<BR> E. भ्वा-पर-सक-सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=318-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुस|तुसः
तुस m. (-सः) The husk of corn or rice: see तुष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=318-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुस्त|तुस्तं
तुस्त n. (-स्तं) Dust.<BR> E. तुस् to sound, affix क्तः see तूस्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=318-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुह
तुह (इर) तुहिर r. 1st cl. (तोहति) To hurt or give pain, to kill.<BR> E. भ्वा-पर-<BR>सक-सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=318-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुहिन|तुहिनं
तुहिन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Frost.<BR>	 2. Moonlight, moonshine.<BR> E. तुह् to give pain,<BR>इनन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=318-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुहिनशैल|तुहिनशैलः
तुहिनशैल m. (-लः) The Himālaya mountains.<BR> E. तुहिन, and शैल a moun-<BR>tain; also similar compounds, as तुहिनपर्व्वत, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=318-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुहिनांशु|तुहिनांशुः
तुहिनांशु m. (-शुः) The moon.<BR> E. तुहिन cold, अंशु a ray.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=318-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुहिनांशुतैल|तुहिनांशुतैलं
तुहिनांशुतैल n. (-लं) Camphor.<BR> E. तुहिनांशु, and तैल oil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=318-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुहिनाद्रि|तुहिनाद्रिः
तुहिनाद्रि m. (-द्रिः) The Himālaya mountains.<BR> E. तुहिन, and अद्रि a moun-<BR>tain; also तुहिनशैल, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=318-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तूण|तूणः
तूण r. 1st cl. (तूणयते) To fill, to fill up. (तूणयति) To shrink, to contract,<BR>to close as the eyelids or wink.<BR> E. पूरणे चुरा-आ । सङ्कोचे उभ-सक-सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=318-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तूण|तूणः
तूण mf. (-णः-णा or -णी) A quiver, &c.<BR>	 f. (-णी) Indigo.<BR> E. तूण् to be filled<BR>(with arrows, &c.) अच् and टाप् affixes, or कर्मणि घञ् and ङीष् ।<BR>तूण्यते बाणैः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=318-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तूणक|तूणकं
तूणक n. (-कं) A measure of verse, species of the अतिशर्करी metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=318-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तूणिन्
तूणिन् mfn. (-णी-णिनी-णि) Having a quiver, quivered.<BR>	 m. (-णी) The Tun<BR>tree.<BR> E. तूण, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=318-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तूणीर|तूणीरं|तूणीरः
तूणीर m. (-रः) A quiver.<BR> E. तूण to be filled (with arrows), ईरण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=318-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तूतक|तूतकं
तूतक n. (-कं) Blue vitriol.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=318-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तूनी
तूनी f. (-नी) Sharp pain in the perinœum and lower part of the abdomen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=318-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तूर्
तूर् f. (तूः) Speed.<BR>	 m. (तूः) A courier.<BR> E. तुर् to make haste, क्किप् affix,<BR>and the semivowel changed to ऊ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=318-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तूर|तूरं
तूर (ई) तूरी r. 4th cl. (तूर्य्यते) To go quick, to make haste.<BR>	 2. To kill, to<BR>hurt or injure.<BR> E. दिवा-आत्म हिंसायां सक० वेगे अक-सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=318-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तूर|तूरं
तूर n. (-रं) Any musical instrument.<BR>	 f. (-री) A trumpet.<BR> E. तूर् to speed,<BR>affix क । तूर्य्यते ताड्यते मुखमारुतेन तूर-घञर्थे कर्मणि क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=318-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तूर्ण|तूर्णं|तूर्ण्ण
तूर्ण mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-र्णं) Quick, expeditious n. adv. (-र्णं) Quick, swift,<BR>quickly.<BR> E. त्वर् to go swiftly, affix कर्त्तरि भावे वा क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=318-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तूर्णि|तूर्णिः
तूर्णि m. (-र्णिः)<BR>	 1. Speed, velocity, expedition.<BR>	 2. Dirt, excrement.<BR>	 3. A<BR>stanza.<BR>	 4. The mind.<BR> E. त्वर् to make haste, Uṇādi affix नि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=318-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तूर्य्य|तूर्य|तूर्यं|तूर्यः|तूर्य्यं
तूर्य्य mfn. (-र्य्यः-र्य्या र्य्यं) Fourth: see तुर्य्य.<BR>	 n. (-र्य्यं) Any musical instru-<BR>ment, the genus of which four species are reckoned, as wind ins-<BR>truments, stringed instruments, &c.<BR> E. चतुर् four, यत् deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=318-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तूर्य्यखण्ड|तूर्यखण्ड|तूर्यखण्डः|तूर्य्यखण्डः
तूर्य्यखण्ड m. (-ण्डः) A musical instrument, a sort of tabor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=318-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तूल|तूलं|तूलः
तूल r. 1st cl. (तूलति)<BR>	 1. To dismiss, to send forth or turn out.<BR>	 2. To<BR>ascertain quantity or weight; some make this a root of the tenth<BR>class (तूलयते.)<BR> E. भ्वा-पर-सक-सेट् । चु-आ-सक-सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=318-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तूल|तूलं|तूलः
तूल n. (-लं)<BR>	 1. The mulberry. (Morus Indica.)<BR>	 2. Æther, the heaven or<BR>atmosphere.<BR>	 mn. (-लः-लं) Cotton.<BR>	 f. (-ला-ली) The wick of a lamp, or<BR>cotton twisted into a similar form for applying unguents, &c.<BR>	 f.<BR>(-ली)<BR>	 1. Indigo.<BR>	 2. A weaver's fibrous stick or brush.<BR>	 3. A painter's<BR>brush, &c. see तुली and तुरी; also तूलि.<BR> E. तूल् to dismiss, to send<BR>forth, affix अच्, fem. affixes टाप् and ङीष् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=318-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तूलक|तूलकं
तूलक n. (-कं) Cotton.<BR> E. कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=318-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तूलकार्म्मुक|तूलकार्मुक|तूलकार्म्मुकं
तूलकार्म्मुक n. (-कं) A bow which is used for cleaning cotton.<BR> E. तूल<BR>cotton, and कार्म्मुक bow; also similar compounds, as तूलचाप,<BR>तूलधनुः, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=318-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तूलनाली
तूलनाली f. (-ली) A thick roll of cotton, from which it is drawn out in<BR>spinning.<BR> E. तूल cotton, नाल a tube, affixes अण् and ङीप्; also<BR>with कन् added तूलनालिका f. (-का.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=318-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तूलपिचु|तूलपिचुः
तूलपिचु m. (-चुः) Cotton.<BR> E. तूल cotton, and पिचु the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=318-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तूलशर्करा
तूलशर्करा f. (-रा) A pod or seed of the plant, any seed yielding a similar<BR>substance.<BR> E. तूल cotton, and शर्करा sand or gravel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=318-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तूलसेवन
तूलसेवन n. (-नं) Spinning.<BR> E. तूल cotton, सिव्-ल्युट् aff. तूलसूत्रकर्त्तने ।<BR>(काट्नाकाटा) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=318-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तूलि|तूलिः
तूलि f. (-लिः) A painter's brush, or a fibrous stick used as one, and for<BR>other purposes.<BR> E. तूल् to send forth or cut, affix इन्ः see तूल and<BR>तूली.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=318-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तूलिका
तूलिका f. (-का) A pencil, a painter's brush, or a stick with a fibrous<BR>extremity used as one.<BR>	 2. A mattress or quilt, a bed, a down or cot-<BR>ton bed.<BR>	 3. An ingot mould.<BR>	 4. A rod, &c. dipped into crucibles to<BR>try if their contents are in fusion.<BR>	 5. A wick or twist of cotton<BR>either for a lamp or for applying unguents, &c.<BR> E. तूली as above,<BR>and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=318-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तूलिनी
तूलिनी f. (-नी) The silk-cotton tree.<BR> E. तूल cotton, इनि and ङीष् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=318-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तूवर|तूवरः
तूवर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A bull without horns, though of an age to have them.<BR>2. A beardless man.<BR>	 3. A eunuch.<BR>	 4. An astringent taste.<BR>	 f. (-री)<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=319-a" target="_blank">Page319-a+ 60</a>]<BR>A fragrant earth.<BR> E. तू to injure, वरच् affix, and the vowel option-<BR>ally long, hence also तुवर and तुवरी; with कन् added तूवरिका and<BR>तूवरीका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=318-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तूष|तूषः
तूष r. 1st cl. (तूषति)<BR>	 1. To satisfy.<BR>	 2. To be satisfied or happy<BR> E. भ्वा-पर-<BR>सक-सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=319-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तूष्णीशील
तूष्णीशील mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Silent, taciturn.<BR> E. तूष्णीम् silent, and शील<BR>practising.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=319-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तूष्णीक|तूष्णीकः
तूष्णीक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Silent, taciturn.<BR> E. तूष्णीम् silent, कन् affix, and म<BR>dropped. तूष्णीं शीलं यस्य शीले अर्थे कन् मलोपश्च ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=319-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तूष्णीकाम्
तूष्णीकाम् ind. Silent, silently.<BR> E. तूष्णीम् silent, and काम् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=319-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तूष्णीम्
तूष्णीम् ind. Silent, silently.<BR> E. तुष् to please or be pleased, affix नीम्, and<BR>उ made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=319-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तूष्णीम्भूत|तूष्णींभूत
तूष्णीम्भूत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Silent.<BR> E. तूष्णीम्, and भूत become.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=319-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तूस्त|तूस्तं
तूस्त n. (-स्तं)<BR>	 1. Dust.<BR>	 2. Clotted hair.<BR>	 3. Sin.<BR>	 4. An atom, a very thin<BR>or delicate substance.<BR> E. तूस् to sound, Uṇādi affix तन्, and the ra-<BR>dical vowel made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=319-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृक्ष|तृक्षः
तृक्ष r. 1st. cl. (तृक्षति) To go, to move or approach.<BR> E. भ्वा-पर-सक-सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=319-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृख|तृखं
तृख n. (-खं) Nutmeg.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=319-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृढ
तृढ mfn. (-ढः-ढा-ढं) Hurt, injured, wounded.<BR> E. तृह् to hurt, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=319-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृण|तृणं
तृण (उ) तृणु r. 8th cl. (तर्णोति तर्णते or तृणोति तृणुते) To eat, especially<BR>grass, to graze.<BR> E. तना-उभ-सक-सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=319-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृण|तृणं
तृण n. (-णं) Grass, any gramineous plant.<BR> E. तृह् to hurt, Uṇādi affix णक्,<BR>and ह rejected; what is consumed by cattle, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=319-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृणकुङ्कम
तृणकुङ्कम n. (-मं) A short of perfume.<BR> E. तृण grass, कुङ्कुम saffron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=319-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृणकुटी
तृणकुटी f. (-टी) A hovel, a hut of grass, or straw.<BR> E. तृण grass, and कुटी a<BR>small house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=319-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृणकूर्म्म|तृणकूर्म|तृणकूर्म्मः
तृणकूर्म्म m. (-र्म्मः) A long gourd, (Cucurbita lagenaria.)<BR> E. तृण grass, and<BR>कूर्म्म a tortoise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=319-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृणकेतु|तृणकेतुः
तृणकेतु m. (-तुः) A bamboo.<BR> E. तृण grass, and केतु a banner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=319-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृणगोधा
तृणगोधा f. (-धा)<BR>	 1. A kind of newt.<BR>	 2. A chameleon.<BR>	 3. A worm.<BR> E. तृण<BR>grass, and गोधा a lizard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=319-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृणग्राहिन्
तृणग्राहिन् m. (-ही)<BR>	 1. Amber, &c. or any gem which being rubbed be-<BR>comes electrically attractive.<BR>	 2. Sapphire.<BR> E. तृण grass, and ग्राहिन्<BR>what seizes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=319-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृणजम्भ
तृणजम्भ mfn. (-म्भः-म्भा-म्भं)<BR>	 1. Graminivorous, one whose food is grass.<BR>	 2.<BR>Grass-toothed, having teeth of the colour of grass, &c.<BR> E. तृण grass,<BR>and जम्भ food, or a tooth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=319-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृणजाति|तृणजातिः
तृणजाति m. (-तिः) The vegetable kingdom.<BR> E. तृण, and जाति genus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=319-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृणता
तृणता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. A bow.<BR>	 2. The aggregate properties of grass or her-<BR>bage, gramineousness.<BR> E. तल् affix of the abstract, added to तृण;<BR>also तृणत्व n. (-त्वं.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=319-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृणद्रुम|तृणद्रुमः
तृणद्रुम m. (-मः) A palm tree, any of the various species, any of the<BR>various species, as the palmyra, cocoanut, date, &c.<BR> E. तृण grass,<BR>and द्रुम a tree; pre-eminent amongst gramineous plants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=319-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृणधान्य|तृणधान्यं
तृणधान्य m. (-न्यः) Grain growing wild or without cultivation.<BR> E. तृण<BR>grass, and धान्य grain, corn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=319-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृणध्वज|तृणध्वजः
तृणध्वज m. (-जः) A bamboo.<BR> E. तृण grass, and ध्वज a flag or banner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=319-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृणपूली
तृणपूली f. (-ली) A mat, a seat made of reeds or basket-work.<BR> E. तृण<BR>grass, पूल् to gather together, affixes अण् and ङीष् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=319-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृणमणि|तृणमणिः
तृणमणि m. (-णिः) A sort of gem, apparently amber.<BR> E. तृण grass, and<BR>मणि a gem; attracting straws, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=319-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृणमत्कुण|तृणमत्कुणः
तृणमत्कुण m. (-णः) A bail or surety.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=319-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृणराज|तृणराजः
तृणराज m. (-जः) A palmyra tree, (Borassus flabelliformis.)<BR> E. तृण grass,<BR>राजन् a sovereign, टच् affix, leaving a final vowel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=319-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृणविस्तर
तृणविस्तर m. (-रः) A heap of grass.<BR> E. तृण, and विस्तर expanse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=319-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृणशीत|तृणशीतं
तृणशीत n. (-तं) A fragrant grass, (Adropogon serratus.)<BR> E. तृण grass,<BR>and शीत here said to imply abundance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=319-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृणशून्य|तृणशून्यं
तृणशून्य mfn. subst. (-न्यः-न्या-न्यं) Arabian jasmine. adj. Free from or<BR>devoid of grass.<BR>	 n. (-न्यं) The flower of the Ketaki.<BR> E. तृण grass,<BR>शून्य void of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=319-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृणषट्पद|तृणषट्पदः
तृणषट्पद m. (-दः) A wasp.<BR> E. तृण grass, and षट्पद six-foot; an insect<BR>haunting meadows, &c. having six-feet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=319-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृणस
तृणस mfn. (-सः-सा-सं) Grassy, made, &c. with grass.<BR> E. तृण grass, and<BR>स aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=319-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृणसारा
तृणसारा f. (-रा) The plantain or banana.<BR> E. तृण grass, and सार essence,<BR>pith.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=319-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृणसिंह|तृणसिंहः
तृणसिंह m. (-हः) An axe.<BR> E. तृण grass, and सिंह a lion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=319-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृणहर्म्म्य
तृणहर्म्म्य m. (-र्म्म्यः) A hovel, a house or upper-room of grass or straw.<BR>E. तृण grass, and हर्म्म्य a mansion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=319-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृणाग्नि|तृणाग्निः
तृणाग्नि m. (-ग्निः)<BR>	 1. Conflagration of chaff.<BR>	 2. Burning a criminal<BR>wrapped up in straw.<BR> E. तृण grass, and अग्नि fire: see तुषानल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=319-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृणाञ्जन|तृणांजन|तृणाञ्जनः
तृणाञ्जन m. (-नः) A chameleon, a lizard.<BR> E. तृण grass, and अञ्जन a lizard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=319-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृणेक्षु|तृणेक्षुः
तृणेक्षु m. (-क्षुः) A kind of long grass, (Saccharum cylindricum.)<BR> E. तृण,<BR>and इक्षु sugar-cane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=319-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृणोद्भव|तृणोद्भवः
तृणोद्भव m. (-वः) Rice, &c. grow wild or without cultivation.<BR> E. तृण grass,<BR>and उद्भव produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=319-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृणोल्का
तृणोल्का f. (-ल्का) A firebrand made of a wisp of straw.<BR> E. तृण grass,<BR>उल्का a firebrand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=319-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृणौकस्
तृणौकस् n. (-कः) A hovel, a hut, a house of straw or mats.<BR> E. तृण grass,<BR>and ओकस् abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=319-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृणौषध|तृणौषधं
तृणौषध n. (-धं) A perfume, commonly Elaba luka.<BR> E. तृण, and औषध a<BR>drug; resembling grass in its appearance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=319-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृण्या
तृण्या f. (-ण्या) A heap or quantity of grass.<BR> E. तृण grass, यत् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=319-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृतीय|तृतीयः
तृतीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Third.<BR>	 f. (-या) The third lunation the third day<BR>of the fortnight.<BR> E. त्रि three, तीय affix, रि changed to the analogous<BR>vowel ऋ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=319-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृतीयक
तृतीयक m. (-कः) A tertian ague.<BR> E. कन added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=319-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृतीयकज्वर|तृतीयकज्वरः
तृतीयकज्वर m. (-रः) Tertian ague.<BR> E. तृतीय, and ज्वर fever.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=319-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृतीयप्रकृति|तृतीयप्रकृतिः
तृतीयप्रकृति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. A eunuch.<BR>	 2. The neuter gender: see तृतीयाप्रकृति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=319-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृतीयाकृत|तृतीयाकृतं
तृतीयाकृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Thrice ploughed, (a field, &c.<BR> E. तृतीय third,<BR>आकृत made, wrought.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=319-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृतीयाप्रकृति|तृतीयाप्रकृतिः
तृतीयाप्रकृति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. A eunuch.<BR>	 2. The neuter gender.<BR> E. तृतीय the<BR>third, प्रकृति nature; neither male nor female (whose or which) the<BR>compound if more regularly तृतीयप्रकृति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=319-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृतीयिन्
तृतीयिन् mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि) Having a third.<BR> E. तृतीय, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=319-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृद
तृद (औ इर्) औतृदिर् r. 1st, 7th and 10th. cls. (तृणत्ति तृन्ते तर्दति हिंसायाम्) ।<BR>1. To kill, to injure.<BR>	 2. To disregard.<BR>	 3. To give.<BR>	 4. To eat. E.<BR>रुधा-उभ-सक-सेट् । भ्वा-सक-सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=319-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृप
तृप r. 1st cl. (तर्पति) 4th cl. (ञि, उ) ञितृपु (तृप्यति) 5th cl. (तृप्नोति) 6th cl.<BR>(तृम्पति) and 10th cl. (तर्पयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To please, to satisfy, to<BR>content.<BR>	 2. To be pleased or satisfied, to be content or satiate.<BR>3. (In the 1st and 10th cls.) To light or kindle.<BR> E. भ्वा-पर-सक-सेट् ।<BR>दिवा-पर-सक-सेट् । स्वादि-पर-सक-सेट् । चुरा-उभ-तुदा-मुचादि-पर-सक-सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=319-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृपत्
तृपत् m. (-पत्)<BR>	 1. The moon.<BR>	 2. A parasol.<BR> E. तृप् to please, अति Uṇādi<BR>affix, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=319-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृपला
तृपला f. (-ला) A creeper or creeping plant.<BR> E. तृप् to please, कल Uṇādi<BR>aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=319-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृप्त|तृप्तः
तृप्त mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं) Contented, satisfied.<BR> E. तृप् to be pleased, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=319-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृपात्मन्
तृपात्मन् mfn. (-त्मा-त्मा-त्म) Contented, satisfied, tranquil.<BR> E. तृप्त, and<BR>आत्मन् self.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=319-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृप्ति|तृप्तिः
तृप्ति f. (-प्तिः) Satisfaction, content.<BR> E. तृप् to please, or be pleased, affix<BR>क्तिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=319-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृप्र|तृप्रः
तृप्र m. (-प्रः) Ghee or oiled butter.<BR> E. तृप् to satisfy, Uṇādi affix रक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=319-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृपालु
तृपालु mfn. (-लुः-लुः-लु) Having ghee, but not liking it or blending with<BR>it.<BR> E. तृप, and आलुच् possessive affix; but in this compound implying<BR>also aversion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=319-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृफ
तृफ r. 6th cl. (तृफति)<BR>	 1. To content, to please.<BR>	 2. To be pleased or con-<BR>tent.<BR>	 3. To hurt.<BR> E. तुदा-पर-सक-सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=319-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृफला
तृफला f. (-ला) The three myrobalans.<BR> E. तृ for त्रि three, फल a fruit,<BR>fem. affix टाप्; also त्रिफला.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=319-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृफू
तृफू m. (-फूः) A serpent in general, the serpent genus.<BR> E. तृफ् to hurt,<BR>or kill, ऊ Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=320-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृम्प
तृम्प r. 6th cl. (तृपति, तृम्पति)<BR>	 1. To content, to please.<BR>	 2. To be pleased<BR>तुदा-पर-सक-सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=320-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृम्फ
तृम्फ r. 6th cl. (तृफति, तृम्फति)<BR>	 1. To content, to please.<BR>	 2. To be pleased<BR>or content.<BR> E. तुदा-पर-सक-सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=320-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृष
तृष (ञि आ) ञितृषा r. 4th cl. (तृष्यति)<BR>	 1. To thirst.<BR>	 2. To thirst metaphori-<BR>cally, to desire, to long for.<BR> E. दिवा-पर-सक-सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=320-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृष्
तृष् f. (तृट्)<BR>	 1. Thirst.<BR>	 2. Thirst (metaphorical,) wish, desire, lust.<BR>	 3.<BR>The daughter of KĀMA^1, the deity of love.<BR> E. तृष् to thirst, affix<BR>क्विप्; also तृषा, &c.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20260617. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/264.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=320-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृषा
तृषा f. (-षा) Thirst.<BR>	 2. Wish, desire.<BR>	 3. The daughter of KĀMA^1: see the<BR>preceding.<BR>	 4. A plant, (Commelina salicifolia:) see लाङ्गलिकी.<BR> E. तृष्<BR>to thirst, affixes क and टाप्; also तृष्णा, तर्षा, &c.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20260617. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/264.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=320-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृषाभू
तृषाभू f. (-भूः) The bladder.<BR> E. तृषा thirst, and भू being; whence thirst<BR>arises.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=320-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृषार्त्त|तृषार्त
तृषार्त्त mfn. (-र्त्तः-र्त्ती-र्त्तं)<BR>	 1. Affected by desire.<BR>	 2. Thirsty, a thirst.<BR> E. तृषा,<BR>and आर्त्त pained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=320-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृषाह|तृषाहं
तृषाह n. (-हं) Water.<BR>	 f. (-हा) A kind of anise: see मधुरिका.<BR> E. तृष thirst,<BR>आङ् before, हन् to destroy or remove, affix ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=320-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृषित|तृषितः
तृषित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Thirsty, thirsting, (physically or metaphorically.)<BR>n. (-तं) Thirst, desire.<BR> E. तृष् to thirst, affix इतच् । तृषा जाता अस्य<BR>तारकादित्वात् इतच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=320-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृषितोत्तरा
तृषितोत्तरा f. (-रा) A plant, (Marsilea quadrifolia:) see असनपर्णी.<BR> E. तृषित<BR>thirst, and उत्तर answering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=320-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृष्णज्
तृष्णज् mfn. (-ष्णक्) Thirsty, (physically or metaphorically) desiring,<BR>longing for cupidinous.<BR> E. तृष् to thirst, न added, तृष्ण and नजिक्<BR>aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=320-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृष्णा
तृष्णा f. (-ष्णा)<BR>	 1. Thirst.<BR>	 2. Desire, wish.<BR> E. तृष् to thirst, न Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=320-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृष्णाक्षय|तृष्णाक्षयः
तृष्णाक्षय m. (-यः) Content, resignation, patience.<BR> E. तृष्णा greediness,<BR>thirst, and क्षय destruction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=320-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृष्यत्
तृष्यत् mfn. (-ष्यन्-ष्यती-ष्यत्)<BR>	 1. Thirsting, a thirst.<BR>	 2. Desiring.<BR> E. तृष् to<BR>thirst, and शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=320-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृह
तृह (उ) तृहु r. 6th cl. (तृहति) 10th cl. (तर्हयति-ते) also तृह r. 7th cl.<BR>(तृणेड्डि) To kill, to hurt, to injure in any manner. (इ) तृहि r. 1st cl.<BR>(तृंहति) To grow or increase.<BR> E. तुदा-पर-सक-सेट् । चुरा-उभ पक्षे रुधा-पर-<BR>सक-सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=320-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तॄ
तॄ r. 1st cl. (तरति)<BR>	 1. To pass over or across.<BR>	 2. To pass or float over,<BR>to navigate.<BR>	 3. To float or swim.<BR>	 4. To overcome, to surpass,<BR>With अव prefixed, To descend, as from heaven. With आङ्, To<BR>cross by a boat, &c. With उत्, a To pass over or above; b To<BR>answer; c To land, to arrive at the opposite shore. With दुर्, To<BR>cross with difficulty. With निर्, To cross safely, to obtain salvation.<BR>With प्र, To excel or surpass. With वि, a To pass from; b To relin-<BR>quish, to give, to give away, to give alms. With सम् To swim over.<BR>E. भ्वा-पर-सक-सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=320-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ते
ते ind. With or by thee.<BR> E. ते substituted for त्वया, but not to be con-<BR>founded with the optional inflection of the 4th and 6th cases of युष्मद्<BR>thou.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=320-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तेज|तेजः
तेज r. 1st cl. (तेजति) To guard, to cherish, to defend or protect.<BR>E. भ्वा-पर-सक-सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=320-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तेज|तेजः
तेज m. (-जः)<BR>	 1. Sharpness, pungency.<BR>	 2. Sharpness of a weapon.<BR>	 3.<BR>Brilliancy.<BR>	 4. Spirit.<BR> E. तिज् to sharpen, affix घञ्ः see तेजस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=320-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तेजन|तेजनं|तेजनः
तेजन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. A bamboo.<BR>	 2. Enlightening, making splendid or polish-<BR>ed.<BR>	 3. Sharpening.<BR>	 f. (-नी)<BR>	 1. A plant (Aletris hyacinthoides.)<BR>2. Heartpea.<BR> E. तिज् to sharpen, &c. affixes णिच् and ल्यु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=320-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तेजनक|तेजनकः
तेजनक m. (-कः) A kind of reed, (Saccharum sara.)<BR> E. कन् added to the<BR>preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=320-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तेजपत्र|तेजपत्रं
तेजपत्र n. (-त्रं) The leaf of the Laurus cassia.<BR> E. तेज sharp, pungent,<BR>and पत्र a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=320-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तेजल|तेजलः
तेजल m. (-लः) The francoline partridge.<BR> E. तिज् to sharpen, करणे<BR>कलच् । कपिञ्जलपक्षिणि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=320-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तेजवत्|तेजवन्त्
तेजवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>	 1. Sharp, pungent.<BR>	 2. Sharp as a weapon.<BR>	 3.<BR>Bright.<BR>	 4. Spirited, energetic.<BR>	 f. (-ती) An aromatic plant (Pothos<BR>officinalis:) see गजपिप्पली.<BR> E. तेज sharpness, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=320-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तेजस्
तेजस् m. (-जाः) A name of Agni or fire.<BR>	 n. (-जः)<BR>	 1. Splendour, light,<BR>lustre.<BR>	 2. Dignity, consequence.<BR>	 3. Srength, power.<BR>	 4. Ardour,<BR>spirit, energy.<BR>	 5. Semen virile.<BR>	 6. Fresh butter.<BR>	 7. Impatience, in-<BR>ability to bear or put up with.<BR>	 8. Gold.<BR>	 9. Bile, the bilious hu-<BR>mour.<BR>	 10. Marrow, the brain, &c.<BR>	 11. Fame, glory.<BR>	 12. Sharpness,<BR>(metallic.)<BR>	 13. Pungency.<BR>	 14. Heat.<BR>	 15. Bodily vigour.<BR>	 16. Viva-<BR>city.<BR> E. तिज् to sharpen or polish, affix भावे करणादौ असुन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=320-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तेजस्कर|तेजस्करं
तेजस्कर mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>	 1. Illuminating, making bright.<BR>	 2. Sharpening,<BR>whetting.<BR>	 3. Invigorating, tonic.<BR> E. तेजस् light, &c. and कर what<BR>makes. तेजः करोति कृ-हेत्वादौ ट ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=320-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तेजस्विन्
तेजस्विन् mfn. (-स्वी-स्विनी-स्वि)<BR>	 1. Famous, celebrated.<BR>	 2. Splendid, &c.<BR>see the preceding.<BR>	 f. (-स्विनी) Heartpea: see ज्योतिष्मती.<BR> E. तेजस्<BR>splendour, &c. विनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=320-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तेजित|तेजितः
तेजित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Sharpened, whetted, polished, burnished.<BR>	 2.<BR>Excited, invigorated, stimulated.<BR> E. तिज् to sharpen; णिच् and<BR>क्त affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=320-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तेजिष्ठ
तेजिष्ठ mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठा-ष्ठं)<BR>	 1. Very bright or splendid.<BR>	 2. Vigorous, power-<BR>ful.<BR> E. तेजस्, and इष्ठन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=320-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तेजीयस्
तेजीयस् mfn. (-यान्-यसी-यः)<BR>	 1. Very bright, radiant, splendid.<BR>	 2. Very<BR>powerful or vigorous.<BR> E. तेजस्, and ईयसुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=320-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तेजोमन्थ
तेजोमन्थ m. (-न्थः) A tree, (Premna spinosa:) see गणिकारी.<BR> E. तेजस् fire,<BR>light, and मन्थ friction; the friction of the wood engendering flame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=320-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तेजोमय
तेजोमय mfn. (-यः-यी-यं) Luminous, brilliant, consisting or made of<BR>light.<BR> E. तेलस्, मयट् made of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=320-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तेजोरूप|तेजोरूपं
तेजोरूप n. (-पं)<BR>	 1. The supreme spirit.<BR>	 2. The nature of light, &c. E.<BR>तेजस् light (divine), रूप form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=320-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तेजोवत्|तेजोवन्त्
तेजोवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>	 1. A Pungent.<BR>	 2. Sharp.<BR>	 3. Bright 4. Ener-<BR>getic.<BR>	 f. (-ती)<BR>	 1. A plant bearing a fruit resembling pepper: see<BR>गजपिप्पली.<BR>	 2. A kind of pepper, (Piper chavya, Rox.)<BR> E. तेजस् pun-<BR>gency, मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=320-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तेजोवृत्त
तेजोवृत्त n. (-त्तं) Superior brilliancy or power.<BR> E. तेजस्, and वृत्त<BR>being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=320-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तेन|तेनः
तेन ind. Therefore, thence, for that reason, on that account, the<BR>correlative to येन. E. The third case of तद् that, used as a particle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=320-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तेन|तेनः
तेन m. (-नः) A note or cadence introductory to a song, &c.<BR> E. ते said<BR>to mean GAURI and न ŚIVA; whose favour is secured by this word.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=320-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तेप
तेप (ऋ) तेपृ r. 1st cl. (तेपते)<BR>	 1. To sprinkle, to distil, to ooze or drop.<BR>2. To shake or tremble.<BR>	 3. To shine.<BR> E. भ्वा-आ-अक-सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=320-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तेम|तेमः
तेम m. (-मः) Wet, damp, moisture.<BR> E. तिम् to be wet, affix घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=320-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तैमन
तैमन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Wetting, moistening, moisture.<BR>	 2. A sauce or condi-<BR>ment.<BR>	 f. (-नी) A chimney, a fireplace.<BR> E. तिम् to be or become wet,<BR>affix ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=320-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तेव
तेव (ऋ) तिवृ r. 1st cl. (तेवते)<BR>	 1. To play, to sport.<BR>	 2. To weep or lament.<BR>E. भ्वा-आ-अक-सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=320-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तेवन|तेवनं
तेवन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. A garden, a pleasure garden or play-ground.<BR>	 2.<BR>Play, sport, pastime.<BR> E. तेव to play, affix भावे आधारे वा ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=320-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तैक्ष्ण्य|तैक्ष्ण्यं
तैक्ष्ण्य n. (-क्ष्ण्यं)<BR>	 1. Sharpness.<BR>	 2. Heat.<BR>	 3. Pungency.<BR>	 4. Fierceness,<BR>cruelty.<BR> E. तीक्ष्ण, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=320-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तैजस|तैजसं|तैजसः
तैजस mfn. (-सः-सी-सं)<BR>	 1. Of or relating to fire, fiery, splendid.<BR>	 2. Power-<BR>ful, vigorous, intense.<BR>	 n. (-सं)<BR>	 1. Ghee or oiled butter.<BR>	 2. Any metal.<BR>3. Intensity.<BR>	 4. Vigour, energy.<BR> E. तेजस् brilliance, affix अण् ।<BR>तेजसो विकारः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=320-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तेजसावर्त्तिनी
तेजसावर्त्तिनी f. (-नी) A crucible.<BR> E. तैजस metal, and आवर्त्तिनी stirring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=320-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तैतिल|तैतिलं|तैतिलः
तैतिल m. (-लः) A rhinoceros.<BR>	 n. (-लं) One of the astronomical periods<BR>called Karanas.<BR> E. अण् added to तितिल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=320-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तैत्तिर|तैत्तिरं|तैत्तिरः
तैत्तिर m. (-रः) A francoline partridge.<BR>	 n. (-रं) A flock of partridges. E.<BR>तित्तिर, and अण् affix of aggregation or pleonastic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=321-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तैत्तिरीय|तैत्तिरीयः
तैत्तिरीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Relating to the Tittiri portion of the Vedas,<BR>as a student, a text, teacher, section of, &c.<BR> E. तित्तिरि the Yajur<BR>Veda so called, and छ affix; or तित्तिरि a partridge, affix as before;<BR>the texts of this Veda being disgorged by YAJNYAWALKYA in a<BR>tangible form, and picked up by the rest of VAISAMPAYANA'S dis-<BR>ciples, who, for the purpose, assumed the shape of partridges.<BR>तित्तिरिणा प्रोक्तमधीयते छण् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=321-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तैत्तिरीयक|तैत्तिरीयकः
तैत्तिरीयक m. (-कः) A follower of the Tittiri branch of the Vedas. E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding; also इन् being added तैत्तिरीयिन्, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=321-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तैग्म्य
तैग्म्य n. (-ग्म्यं)<BR>	 1. Heat.<BR>	 2. Sharpness.<BR>	 3. Pungency.<BR> E. तिग्म, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=321-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तैल|तैलं
तैल n. (-लं)<BR>	 1. Oil, expressed oil, prepared from sesamum, mustard,<BR>&c.<BR>	 2. Storax, gum benzoin, incense.<BR> E. तिल sesamum, and अण् aff.<BR>तिलस्य तत्सदृशस्य वा विकारः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=321-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तैलक|तैलकं
तैलक n. (-कं) A small quantity of oil.<BR> E. तैल, and कन् diminutive<BR>affix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=321-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तैलकार|तैलकारः
तैलकार m. (-रः) An oil manufacturer.<BR> E. तैल, and कार who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=321-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तैलकिट्ट|तैलकिट्टं
तैलकिट्ट n. (-ट्टं) The oil cake, a cake made of the oily seed, after<BR>expression.<BR> E. तैल, and किट्ट sediment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=321-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तैलङ्ग|तैलंग|तैलंगः|तैलङ्गः
तैलङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः) The part of the peninsula south of Orissa to Madras,<BR>the modern Carnatic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=321-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तैलचौरिका
तैलचौरिका f. (-का) A cockroach.<BR> E. तैल oil, चुर् to steal, ण्वुल् affix; it<BR>is also sometimes read तैलाचारिका from चर् to go, with आङ् prefix-<BR>ed, and ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=321-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तैलद्रोणी
तैलद्रोणी f. (-णी) A bathing tub for an oil bath.<BR> E. तैल, and द्रोणी a<BR>bucket.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=321-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तैलपक|तैलपकः
तैलपक m. (-कः) A cockroach.<BR> E. तैल, and पच to digest, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=321-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तैलपर्णिक|तैलपर्णिकं
तैलपर्णिक n. (-कं) White Sandal wood.<BR> E. तिलपर्णी Sandal wood, affix कन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=321-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तैलपर्णी
तैलपर्णी f. (-र्णी)<BR>	 1. Sandal.<BR>	 2. Incense.<BR>	 3. Turpentine.<BR> E. तिल sesamum,<BR>and पर्ण a leaf, affixes अण् and ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=321-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तैलपा
तैलपा f. (-पा) A cockroach.<BR> E. तैल oil, and पा who drinks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=321-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तैलपायिका
तैलपायिका f. (-का) A cockroach.<BR> E. तैल oil, पा to drink, ण्वुल् affix, and<BR>यक् inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=321-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तैलपिपीलिका
तैलपिपीलिका f. (-का) The small red ant.<BR> E. तैल, and पिपीलिका an ant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=321-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तैलमाली
तैलमाली f. (-ली) A wick, the cotton of a lamp.<BR> E. तैल oil, माला a neck-<BR>lace, ङीप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=321-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तैलम्पात
तैलम्पात mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Blending with oil, &c.<BR>	 f. (-ता) Oblation to fire.<BR>E. तिल sesamum, पत् to go or alight, घञ् affix, and नुम् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=321-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तैलसाधन|तैलसाधनं
तैलसाधन n. (-नं) A fragrant substance, (Civet.)<BR> E. तैल oil, and साधन<BR>menstruum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=321-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तैलस्फटिक|तैलस्फटिकः
तैलस्फटिक m. (-कः) A sort of gem, (Amber.)<BR> E. तैल oil, and स्फटिक crystal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=321-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तैलाटी
तैलाटी f. (-टी) A wasp.<BR> E. तैल oil, and अट् to go, affixes अण् and ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=321-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तैलाम्बुका
तैलाम्बुका f. (-का) A cockroach.<BR> E. तैल oil, अम्बु water or drink, कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=321-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तैलिक|तैलिकः
तैलिक m. (-कः) An oilman.<BR> E. तैल, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=321-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तैलिन्
तैलिन् mfn. (-ली-लिनी-लि) Relating or belonging to oil only, &c.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-ली) An oil-man, an oil grinder or preparer.<BR>	 f. (-लिनी)<BR>	 1. The wick<BR>or cotton of a lamp.<BR>	 2. A kind of insect found in oil.<BR> E. तैल oil,<BR>affix इनि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=321-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तैलिशाला
तैलिशाला f. (-ला) An oil-mill.<BR> E. तैलिन् an oilman, and शाला a house or<BR>hall.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=321-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तैलीन|तैलीनं
तैलीन n. (-नं) A field of sesamum.<BR> E. तिल sesamum, and खञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=321-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तैष|तैषः
तैष m. (-षः) The month Pausha, (December-January.)<BR>	 f. (-षी) Day of<BR>full moon in Pausha.<BR> E. तिष्य the constellation, (in which the moon<BR>is full in this month,) and अण् affix; य is dropped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=321-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तोक|तोकं
तोक n. (-कं) A child, a son or daughter, male or female offspring. E.<BR>तु a Sautra root, to increase, affix क, deriv. irr. also तोकक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=321-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तोक्म|तोक्मं|तोक्मः
तोक्म m. (-क्मः)<BR>	 1. Green or unripe barley.<BR>	 2. Green, (the colour.)<BR>	 n.<BR>(-क्मं)<BR>	 1. The wax of the ear.<BR>	 2. A cloud.<BR> E. तक् to deride, म affix,<BR>and ओ substituted for the radical vowel; it is also written तोक्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=321-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तोटक|तोटकं|तोटकः
तोटक n. (-कं) A measure or verse, a stanza, each line containing<BR>twelve syllables.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=321-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तोड
तोड r. 1st cl. (ऋ) तोडृ (तोडति) To treat with disrespect.<BR> E. भ्वा-पर-सक-<BR>सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=321-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तोत्र|तोत्त्रं|तोत्रं
तोत्र n. (-त्रं)<BR>	 1. A stick or bamboo, with a sharp iron head, used for<BR>guiding an elephant.<BR>	 2. A goad or pike for driving cattle. E.<BR>करणे ष्ट्रन्; also तोदन ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=321-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तोत्रवेत्र
तोत्रवेत्र n. (-त्रं) A rod or wand carried by VIṢṆU.<BR> E. तोत्र a goad, and<BR>वेत्र a stick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=321-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तोद|तोदः
तोद m. (-दः)<BR>	 1. Pain, anguish, vexation, torture, uneasiness, (either of<BR>body or mind.)<BR>	 2. Sharp, shooting or pricking pain.<BR> E. तुद् to teaze<BR>or torment, affix भावे घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=321-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तोदन|तोदनं
तोदन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. A goad: see तोत्र.<BR>	 2. Pain, affliction from disease, &c.<BR>E. तुद् to give pain, affix करणे ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=321-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तोमर|तोमरं|तोमरः
तोमर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>	 1. An iron club or crow.<BR>	 2. A lance.<BR> E. तु Sautra<BR>root, to hurt, affix विच्, तु that which injures, मृ to die, affix<BR>करणे अच्, and the vowel of तु changed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=321-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तोमरग्रह
तोमरग्रह m. (-हः) A warrior armed with a club.<BR> E. तोमर, and ग्रह who takes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=321-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तोमरधर|तोमरधरः
तोमरधर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A name of Agni.<BR>	 2. A warrior armed with a club.<BR>E. तोमर an iron club, and धर having.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=321-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तोमरिका
तोमरिका f. (-का) A fragrant earth: see तुवरिका ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=321-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तोय|तोयं
तोय n. (-यं) Water.<BR> E. तु to surround, Uṇādi affix कोय or ताय to nourish,<BR>अच् affix, and आ changed irregularly to ओ or तु + विच् तवे पूर्त्त्यै याति<BR>या + क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=321-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तोयकाम|तोयकामः
तोयकाम m. (-मः) A sort of crane growing in or near water, (Calamus<BR>fasciculatus, Rox.)<BR> E. तोय water, and काम desiring, affecting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=321-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तोयकृच्छ्र|तोयकृच्छ्रं|तोयकृच्छ्रः
तोयकृच्छ्र m. (-च्छ्रः) A sort of penance, drinking nothing but water for a<BR>fixed period.<BR> E. तोय water, and कृच्छ्र penance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=321-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तोयडिम्भ|तोयडिंभ|तोयडिम्भः
तोयडिम्भ m. (-म्भः) Hail.<BR> E. तोय water, and डिम्भ young; also तोयडिम्भक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=321-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तोयद|तोयदः
तोयद mfn. (-दः-दा-दं) Who or what gives water.<BR>	 m. (-दः)<BR>	 1. A cloud.<BR>	 2.<BR>A fragrant grass, (Cyperus rotundus.)<BR>	 n. (-दं) Ghee or oiled butter.<BR>E. तोय water, and द yielding. तोयं ददाति दा + क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=321-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तोयधर|तोयधरः
तोयधर mfn. (-रः-रा-री-रं) Having or containing water.<BR>	 m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A<BR>cloud.<BR>	 2. A fragrant grass: see मुस्तक.<BR>	 3. A potherb. (Marsilia den-<BR>tata.)<BR> E. तोय water, and धर possessing. तोयं धरति धृ-अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=321-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तोयधि|तोयधिः
तोयधि m. (-धिः) The ocean.<BR> E. तोय water, and धि having.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=321-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तोयधिप्रिय|तोयधिप्रियं
तोयधिप्रिय m. (-यः) Cloves.<BR> E. तोयधि the sea, and प्रिय fond of; produced<BR>in maritime countries. लवङ्गे ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=321-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तोयनिधि|तोयनिधिः
तोयनिधि m. (-धिः) The ocean.<BR> E. तोय water, and निधि nest or receptacle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=321-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तोयपिप्पली
तोयपिप्पली f. (-ली) A plant, (Jussieua repens.)<BR> E. तोय water, and पिप्पली<BR>long pepper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=321-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तोयपुष्पी
तोयपुष्पी f. (-ष्पी) Trumpet flower.<BR> E. तोय water, and पुष्प a flower;<BR>flowering near water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=321-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तोयप्रसादन|तोयप्रसादनं
तोयप्रसादन n. (-नं) The clearing nut plant, (Strychnos potatorum.) E.<BR>तोय water, and प्रसादन clearing, cleansing; the nut being rubbed<BR>upon the inside of a water-jar, occasions the precipitation of the<BR>impurities of the water poured into it. (निर्माल्लि) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=321-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तोयप्रसादनफल|तोयप्रसादनफलं
तोयप्रसादनफल n. (-लं) The clearing nut: see the preceding.<BR> E. तोयप्रसादन<BR>as above, and फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=321-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तोयप्रष्ठा
तोयप्रष्ठा f. (-ष्ठा) The trumpet flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=321-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तोयवल्ली
तोयवल्ली f. (-ल्ली) A kind of gourd, (Memordica charantia.)<BR> E. तोय water,<BR>and वल्ली a creeper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=321-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तोयशुक्तिका
तोयशुक्तिका f. (-का) An oyster.<BR> E. तोय, and शुक्तिका an oyster.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=321-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तोयसूचक|तोयसूचकः
तोयसूचक m. (-कः) A frog.<BR> E. तोय water, and सूचक a spy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=321-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तोयाधिवासिनी
तोयाधिवासिनी f. (-नी) Trumpet flower.<BR> E. तोय water, अधि upon or near,<BR>वस् to abide, णिनि and ङीप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=321-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तोरण|तोरणं|तोरणः
तोरण mn. (-णः-णं)<BR>	 1. The ornamented arch of a door or gateway.<BR>	 2. An<BR>outer door.<BR>	 3. Decoration of the gate-post.<BR>	 3. A temporary and<BR>ornamented arch.<BR>	 5. A mound or raised mark near a bathing<BR>place.<BR>	 6. A triangle supporting a large balance.<BR>	 n. (-णं) The neck,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=322-a" target="_blank">Page322-a+ 60</a>]<BR>the throat.<BR> E. तुर् to hasten, affix आधारे ल्युट्; by which people<BR>pass or go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=321-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तोल|तोलं|तोलः
तोल mn. (-लः-लं) A Tola, a weight of gold or silver; it is stated in<BR>books at 16 Mashas of 5 Rettis or 6(1/2) grains each, and weighs<BR>therefore 105 grains troy; in practice it is calculated at 12<BR>Mashas jeweller's weight, and weighs nearly double, or 210 grains;<BR>but actually it is of the same weight as the Sicca or grs. 179(2/3.) E.<BR>तुल् to weigh, affix कर्मणि अच्; also with ण्वुल् affix तोलक mn. (-कः-कं.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=322-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तोलन|तोलनं
तोलन n. (-नं) Weighing.<BR> E. तुल् to weigh, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=322-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तोलयित्वा
तोलयित्वा ind. Having weighed.<BR> E. तुल् to weigh, causal form, क्त्वा aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=322-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तोष|तोषः
तोष n. (-षं) Pleasure, joy, happiness.<BR> E. तुष् to be pleased, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=322-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तोषित
तोषित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Pleased, appeased.<BR> E. तुष् to be pleased, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=322-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तौक
तौक (ऋ) तौकृ r. 1st cl. (तौकते) To go or move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=322-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तौक्षिक|तौक्षिकः
तौक्षिक m. (-कः) Sagittarius, the constellation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=322-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तौतिक|तौतिकं|तौतिकः
तौतिक n. (-कं) A pearl.<BR>	 m. (-कः) The pearl oyster.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=322-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तौर्य्य|तौर्य|तौर्यं|तौर्य्यं
तौर्य्य n. (-र्य्यं) The sound of musical instruments, harmony, &c.<BR> E. तूर्य्य<BR>an instrument, and अण् aff. तूर्य्ये मुरजादौ वाद्ये भवम् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=322-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तौर्य्यत्रिक|तौर्यत्रिक|तौर्य्यत्रिकं
तौर्य्यत्रिक n. (-कं) Symphony, union of song, dance, and instrumental<BR>music.<BR> E. तौर्य्य as above, त्रि three, कन् affix; triple or threefold<BR>melody.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=322-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तौल|तौलं
तौल n. (-लं) A balance.<BR> E. तुला, स्वार्थे अण् pleonasm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=322-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तौलिक|तौलिकः
तौलिक m. (-कः) A painter.<BR> E. तुलिका a brush, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=322-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तौलिकिक|तौलिकिकः
तौलिकिक m. (-कः) A painter.<BR> E. तुलिका a brush or pencil, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=322-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तौषार|तौषारं
तौषार n. (-रं)<BR>	 1. Snow.<BR>	 2. Cold.<BR> E. तुषार frost, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=322-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्यक्त|त्यक्तं
त्यक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं) Left, resigned, abandoned, deserted, &c.<BR> E. त्यज्<BR>to quit, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=322-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्यक्तजीवित
त्यक्तजीवित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Ready to die; willing to run all hazards,<BR>having relinquished the expectation of life as men on the forlorn<BR>hope.<BR> E. त्यक्त left, and जीवित life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=322-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्यक्तवत्
त्यक्तवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Leaving, abandoning.<BR> E. त्यज् to quit,<BR>क्तवतु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=322-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्यक्तव्य
त्यक्तव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं) To be left, abandoned, excepted, &c.<BR> E. त्यज्,<BR>and तव्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=322-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्यक्ताग्नि|त्यक्ताग्निः
त्यक्ताग्नि m. (-ग्निः) A Bramhan who has lost his household fire, one who<BR>neglects essential ceremonies.<BR> E. त्यक्त, and अग्नि fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=322-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्यक्तुकाम
त्यक्तुकाम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं) Wishing to leave.<BR> E. त्यक्तु for the infin, त्यक्तुं,<BR>and काम desiring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=322-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्यक्त्वा
त्यक्त्वा ind. Having left or abandoned.<BR> E. त्यज्, and क्त्वा aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=322-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्यज
त्यज r. 1st cl. (औ) त्यजौ (त्यजति) To quit, to abandon, to leave or resign,<BR>to part from, to give away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=322-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्यजन|त्यजनं
त्यजन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Leaving, quitting, abandoning.<BR>	 2. Excepting, exclu-<BR>sion.<BR>	 3. Giving.<BR> E. त्यज्, and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=322-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्यजनीय
त्यजनीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>	 1. To be left or abandoned.<BR>	 2. To be avoided.<BR>3. To be excepted.<BR> E. त्यज्, and अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=322-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्यद्
त्यद् pron. for तद् mfn. (-स्यः-स्या-तद्) That.<BR> E. त्यज् to quit, Uṇādi affix<BR>अदि, and the final of the radical rejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=322-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्याग|त्यागः
त्याग m. (-गः)<BR>	 1. Gift, donation.<BR>	 2. Abandoning, leaving, parting from,<BR>separation, deserting, &c.<BR>	 3. A sage, one who separates himself<BR>from worldly thoughts.<BR> E. त्यज् to abandon, भावे घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=322-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्यागशील
त्यागशील mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Generous, liberal.<BR> E. त्याग, and शील addict-<BR>ed to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=322-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्यागशीलता
त्यागशीलता f. (-ता) Generosity.<BR> E. त्यागशील, and तल् affix; also with त्व,<BR>त्यागशीलत्वम् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=322-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्यागिता
त्यागिता f. (-ता) Liberality, generosity.<BR> E. त्यागिन्, and तल् affix; also<BR>with त्व affix, त्यागित्वम् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=322-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्यागिन्
त्यागिन् mfn. (-गी-गिनी-गि) Who or what leaves, gives, excepts, &c.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-गी)<BR>	 1. A giver, a donor.<BR>	 2. A hero.<BR>	 3. An abandoner, a deserter,<BR>but chiefly applied to the religious ascetic, or him who abandons<BR>terrestrial objects, thoughts, passions, &c.<BR> E. त्याग as above, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=322-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्यागिम|त्यागिमः
त्यागिम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं) Left, abandoned.<BR> E. त्याग leaving, इमन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=322-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्याज्य|त्याज्यः
त्याज्य mfn. (-ज्यः-ज्या-ज्यं)<BR>	 1. To be left or avoided.<BR>	 2. To be abstained<BR>from.<BR>	 3. To be given.<BR>	 4. To be excepted.<BR>	 n. (-ज्यं) Part of an as-<BR>terism, or its duration considered as unlucky.<BR> E. त्यज् to leave,<BR>affix ण्यत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=322-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रक
त्रक (इ) त्रकि r. 1st. cl. (त्रङ्कते) To go or move. भ्वा० आ० सक० सेट् इदित् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=322-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रख
त्रख (इ) त्रखि r. 1st cl. (त्रङ्खति) To go or move. भ्वा० प० सक० सेट् इदित् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=322-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रग
त्रग (इ) त्रगि r. 1st cl. (त्रङ्गति) To go or move. भ्वा० प० सक० सेट् इदित् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=322-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रङ्ग|त्रङ्गः
त्रङ्ग mn. (-ङ्गः-ङ्गा) The city of HARISCHANDRA, suspended, it is supposed<BR>in the air.<BR> E. त्रगि to go, affix अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=322-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रद
त्रद (इ) त्रदि r. 1st cl. (त्रन्दति)<BR>	 1. To act, to perform functions.<BR>	 2. To<BR>endeavour, to strive.<BR>	 3. To be busy. भ्वा० प० अक० सेट् इदित् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=322-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रप
त्रप (ऊ, ष) त्रपूष् r. 1st cl. (त्रपते) To be modest, to be ashamed. भ्वा० आ०<BR>अक० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=322-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रप
त्रप mf. (-पः-पा) Shame, modesty, bashfulness.<BR>	 f. (-पा)<BR>	 1. An unchaste<BR>woman, (a shame, to her family.)<BR>	 2. Family, race.<BR>	 3. Fame,<BR>celebrity.<BR> E. त्रप् to be modest, affix भावे अङ्, fem. affix टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=322-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रपमाण
त्रपमाण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Being ashamed.<BR> E. त्रप् to be ashamed, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=322-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रपाक|त्रपाकः
त्रपाक m. (-कः) A barbarian of a certain description.<BR> E. त्रप् to be<BR>modest, आकन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=322-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रपानिरस्त
त्रपानिरस्त mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं) Shameless, impudent.<BR> E. त्रपा, and निरस्त<BR>expelled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=322-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रपान्वित
त्रपान्वित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Modest, bashful, ashamed.<BR> E. त्रपा, and अन्वित<BR>possessed of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=322-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रपाभर
त्रपाभर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Overcome with shame.<BR> E. त्रपा, and भर having.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=322-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रपायुक्त
त्रपायुक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं) Bashful, modest.<BR> E. त्रपा, and युक्त attached.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=322-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रपारण्डा|त्रपारंडा
त्रपारण्डा f. (-ण्डा) A whore, a harlot.<BR> E. त्रपा shame, लडि to affect, affixes<BR>अच् and टाप्, and ल changed to र ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=322-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रपावत्
त्रपावत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Modest, ashamed.<BR> E. त्रपा, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=322-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रपाहीन
त्रपाहीन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Immodest, impudent.<BR> E. त्रपा, and हीन void of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=322-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रपित
त्रपित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Modest, bashful, ashamed.<BR> E. त्रप् to be modest,<BR>क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=322-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रपिष्ठ|त्रपिष्ठः
त्रपिष्ठ mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठा-ष्ठं)<BR>	 1. Highly satisfied.<BR>	 2. Very much ashamed. E.<BR>तृप् to please, or त्रपा shame, and इष्ठन् affix, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=322-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रपीयस्
त्रपीयस् mfn. (-यान्-यसी-यः) Highly or excessively pleased or content.<BR>	 2.<BR>Very much ashamed.<BR> E. तृप् to be pleased, or तृपा, and ईयसुन् affix<BR>of the irr. superlative.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=322-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रपु|त्रपुः
त्रपु n. (-पु)<BR>	 1. Tin.<BR>	 2. Lead.<BR> E. त्रप् to be modest, Uṇādi affix उन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=322-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रपुल|त्रपुलं
त्रपुल n. (-लं) Tin.<BR> E. लच् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=322-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रपुष|त्रपुषं
त्रपुष nf. (-षं-षी) A cucumber.<BR>	 n. (-षं) Tin.<BR> E. त्रप् to be ashamed, &c.<BR>उसस् affix, fem. ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=322-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रपुस्
त्रपुस् n. (-पुः) Tin, or according to some, lead: see त्रपु.<BR> E. त्रप् to be<BR>ashamed, Uṇādi affix उस् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=322-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रप्स्य|त्रप्स्यं
त्रप्स्य n. (-प्स्यं) Thin or diluted curds.<BR> E. तृप् to be satisfied, deriv. irr.;<BR>also without the final य त्रप्स, n. (-प्सं) also द्रप्स्य and द्रप्सा ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=322-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रय|त्रयं|त्रयः
त्रय nf. (-यं-यी)<BR>	 1. The third.<BR>	 2. (In composition) Tree, as गुणत्रयं the<BR>three properties.<BR> E. त्रि, अयच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=322-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रयी
त्रयी f. (-यी)<BR>	 1. The three Vedas collectively, that is, omitting the<BR>Atharvan, which not being a text book for the customary reli-<BR>gious rites of the Hindus, is considered very commonly rather as<BR>an appendix to the other three, than a fourth work of equal<BR>authority.<BR>	 2. A matron, a married woman who has children living.<BR>3. Intellect, understanding.<BR>	 4. A plant, (Conyza serratula.)<BR> E. त्रि<BR>three, अयच् or टयप् substituted for the final, fem. affix ङीप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=322-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रयीतनु|त्रयीतनुः
त्रयीतनु m. (-नुः) The sun.<BR> E. त्रयी the three Vedas, and तनु diffusion;<BR>celebrated through these sacred books, or because the Sama Veda,<BR>and portions of the other Vedas, are said to have proceeded from<BR>the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=322-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रयीधर्म्म|त्रयीधर्म|त्रयीधर्मः|त्रयीधर्म्मः
त्रयीधर्म्म m. (-र्म्मः) Duty enjoined by the Vedas, modes of sacrifice, &c.<BR>prescribed by them.<BR> E. त्रयी the three Vedas, and धर्म्म virtue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=322-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रयीमुख|त्रयीमुखः
त्रयीमुख m. (-खः) A Bramhan.<BR> E. त्रयी the Vedas, and मुख the mouth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=322-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रयोदश|त्रयोदशः
त्रयोदश mfn. (-शः-शी-शं) Thirteenth.<BR>	 f. (-शी) The thirteenth day of the<BR>lunar fortnight: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=323-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रयोदशन्
त्रयोदशन् mfn. plu. (-श) Thirteen.<BR> E. त्रयस् for त्रि three, and दशन् ten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=323-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रस|त्रसं|त्रसः
त्रस (ई) त्रसी r. 1st and 4th cls. (त्रसति त्रस्यति)<BR>	 1. To fear, to be afraid.<BR>	 2.<BR>To run, to go quickly. (इ) त्रसि r. 1st and 10th cls. (त्रंसति त्रंसयति-ते)<BR>1. To speak.<BR>	 2. To shine. Also त्रस r. 10th cl. (त्रसयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To hold.<BR>2. To seize or take.<BR>	 3. To oppose to prevent or forbid.<BR>	 4. To<BR>frighten. भ्वा० दिवा० प० अक० सेट् । क्षुरा० उभ० अक० सेट् इदित् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=323-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रस|त्रसं|त्रसः
त्रस mfn. (-सः-सा-सं) Moveable, loco-motive.<BR>	 n. (-सं) A wood, a forest. E.<BR>त्रस् to go, affix अच् or आधारे घञर्थे क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=323-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रसर|त्रसरः
त्रसर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A shuttle.<BR>	 2. Weaving.<BR> E. त्रस् to go, affix अरन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=323-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रसरेणु|त्रसरेणुः
त्रसरेणु mf. (-णुः) An atom or mote visible in a sunbeam, especially con-<BR>sidered as an ideal weight, either of the lowest of nomination, or<BR>equal to three, or according to some, thirty invisible atoms.<BR>	 f.<BR>(-णुः) A wife of the sun.<BR> E. त्रस move, and रेणु dust; also read त्र्यसरेणु ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=323-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रसुर|त्रसुरः
त्रसुर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Timid, fearful.<BR> E. त्रस् to fear, उरच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=323-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रस्त|त्रस्तः
त्रस्त mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं)<BR>	 1. Timid, fearful.<BR>	 2. Frighted, alarmed.<BR>	 3. Quick.<BR>E. त्रस् to fear, affix क्त; also त्रस्नु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=323-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रस्तरूप
त्रस्तरूप mfn. (-पः-पा-पं) Fearful, terrified.<BR> E. त्रस्त; and रूप form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=323-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रस्नु|त्रस्नुः
त्रस्नु mfn. (-स्नुः-स्नुः-स्नु) Timid, fearful.<BR> E. त्रस् to fear, क्नु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=323-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रस्यत्
त्रस्यत् mfn. (-स्यन्-स्यन्ती-स्यत्) Fearing, apprehending.<BR> E. त्रस् to fear,<BR>शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=323-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रा
त्रा r. 2nd cl. (त्राते) To preserve, &c.: see त्रै० अदा० आ० सक० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=323-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्राण|त्राणं
त्राण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>	 1. Preserved, saved, guarded, protected.<BR>	 n. (-णं)<BR>1. Preserving, protection.<BR>	 2. A plant: see त्रायमाण.<BR> E. त्रै to preserve,<BR>affix क्त and ण optionally substituted त; also त्रात; again, त्रै to pre-<BR>serve, affix भावे ल्युट ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=323-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रात|त्रातं
त्रात mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Preserved, guarded, protected.<BR>	 n. (-तं) Preserving,<BR>protection: see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=323-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रापुष|त्रापुषं
त्रापुष mfn. (-षः-षी-षं) Made of tin.<BR> E. त्रपुस् tin, affix अण्, and षुक् aug-<BR>ment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=323-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रायत्
त्रायत् mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्) Preserving, protecting.<BR>	 f. (-न्ती)<BR>	 1. A plant:<BR>see the next.<BR>	 2. A protectress, &c.<BR> E. त्रै to preserve, affix शतृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=323-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रायमाण|त्रायमाणं
त्रायमाण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) A preserve, preserving.<BR>	 f. (-णा) A medicinal<BR>plant.<BR> E. त्रै to preserve, affix शानच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=323-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रास|त्रासः
त्रास m. (-सः)<BR>	 1. Fear, terror.<BR>	 2. A flaw or defect in a jewel.<BR> E. त्रस् to<BR>fear, affix भावे घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=323-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रासकर
त्रासकर mfn. (-रः-री-रं) Fearful, alarming.<BR> E. त्रास, and कर what makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=323-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रासदायिन्
त्रासदायिन् mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि) Terrifying, fear-exciting.<BR> E. त्रास fear, and<BR>दायिन् what gives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=323-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रासित
त्रासित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Frightened, alarmed.<BR> E. त्रास to fear, causal form,<BR>affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=323-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रि|त्रिः
त्रि plu. only, m. (त्रयः)<BR>	 f. (तिस्रः)<BR>	 n. (त्रीणि) Three. subst.<BR>	 m. sing. (त्रिः)<BR>plu. (त्रयः) Three times, a thrice.<BR> E. तॄ to pass, Uṇādi affix<BR>ड्रि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=323-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिंश|त्रिंशः
त्रिंश mfn. (-शः-शा-शं) Thirtieth.<BR> E. त्रिंशत्, and डट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=323-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिंशक|त्रिंशकः
त्रिंशक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Thirty collectively, a multitude of thirty. E.<BR>त्रिंशत् thirty, affix वुन् डिच्च ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=323-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिंशत्
त्रिंशत् f. sing. (-त्) Thirty, &c. du. (-तौ) Two thirties. plu. (-तः) many<BR>thirties.<BR> E. त्रिं for त्रि three, and शत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=323-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिंशत्पत्र|त्रिंशत्पत्रं
त्रिंशत्पत्र n. (-त्रं) The white esculent water lily.<BR> E. त्रिंशत् thirty, and पत्र<BR>a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=323-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिक|त्रिकं
त्रिक n. (-कं)<BR>	 1. The lower part of the spine.<BR>	 2. The aggregate of<BR>three, a trine, a triad.<BR>	 3. The three mystical words to be pro-<BR>nounced in daily prayer.<BR>	 4. A place where three roads meet.<BR>	 5. Three<BR>spices, three myrobalans, &c. collectively: see त्रिकटु, त्रिफल and<BR>the like.<BR>	 m. (-कः) A plant: see गोक्षुरक.<BR>	 f. (-का)<BR>	 1. A triangular<BR>frame or bar across the mouth of a well over which passes the<BR>rope of the bucket, or to which one end of it is tied to guard<BR>against its slipping.<BR>	 2. A wooden frame at the mouth of a well,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=323-b" target="_blank">Page323-b+ 60</a>]<BR>or the upper part of the well.<BR>	 3. A frame at the bottom of a well,<BR>on which the masonry rests.<BR>	 4. The cover or lid of a well.<BR> E. त्रि<BR>three, and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=323-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिककुद्
त्रिककुद् m. (-द् or -त्) A mountain with three peaks.<BR> E. त्रि three, and<BR>ककुद् a peak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=323-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिककुद
त्रिककुद mfn. (-दः-दा-दं) Having three humps or peaks.<BR> E. त्रि, and ककुद्<BR>a hump, and अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=323-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिकट|त्रिकटः
त्रिकट m. (-टः) A plant, (Ruellia Iongifolia,) &c. see गोक्षुरक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=323-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिकटु
त्रिकटु m. (-टुः) The aggregate of three spices, viz. black and long pep-<BR>per, and dry ginger.<BR> E. त्रि three, or threefold, and कटु pungent,<BR>(as a spice.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=323-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिकण्ट|त्रिकण्टं|त्रिकण्टः
त्रिकण्ट m. (-ण्टः)<BR>	 1. A plant, (Ruellia longifolia,) &c. त्रिकट.<BR>	 2. A sort of<BR>Euphorbia.<BR> E. त्रि three, and कण्ट a thorn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=323-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिकण्टक|त्रिकण्टकः
त्रिकण्टक m. (-कः) A sort of fish, (Silurus.)<BR>	 2. A plant: see the preced-<BR>ing.<BR> E. कन् added to त्रिकण्ट.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=323-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिकाय|त्रिकायः
त्रिकाय m. (-यः) A name of Buddha, the founder of the Bauddha<BR>sect.<BR> E. त्रि three, and काय a body, the three-bodied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=323-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिकालज्ञ|त्रिकालज्ञः
त्रिकालज्ञ mfn. (-ज्ञः-ज्ञा-ज्ञं) Omniscient.<BR>	 m. (-ज्ञः)<BR>	 1. A divine sage.<BR>	 2. A<BR>deity.<BR>	 3. A name of Buddha, the founder of the Bauddha sect. E.<BR>त्रि three, काल time, and ज्ञ who knows, acquainted with the past,<BR>present, and future; also similar compounds as the next, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=323-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिकालदर्शिन्
त्रिकालदर्शिन् mfn. (-र्शी-र्शिनी-र्शि) Omniscient.<BR>	 m. (-र्शी)<BR>	 1. A Ṛṣi of<BR>divine sage.<BR>	 2. A name of Buddha.<BR> E. त्रि three, काल time, and<BR>दर्शिन् who views: see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=323-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिकालविद्
त्रिकालविद् mfn. (-विद्-वित्) Omniscient.<BR>	 m. (-विद् or -वित्) A name of<BR>Buddha: see the preceding. E. As before, विद् who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=323-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिकूट|त्रिकूटं|त्रिकूटः
त्रिकूट m. (-टः) The name of a mountain in the peninsula; it is also<BR>applicable to any mountain with three peaks.<BR>	 n. (-टं) Sea-salt<BR>prepared by evaporation.<BR> E. त्रि three, कूट a peak, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=323-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिकूर्च्चक|त्रिकूर्चक
त्रिकूर्च्चक n. (-कं) A sort of knife with three edges.<BR> E. त्रि, and कूर्च्चक a<BR>bunch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=323-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिकोण|त्रिकोणं|त्रिकोणः
त्रिकोण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. The vulva.<BR>	 2. A triangle.<BR>	 3. Any triangular object.<BR>E. त्रि three, and कोण a corner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=323-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिख|त्रिखं
त्रिख (इ) त्रिखि r. 1st cl. (त्रिङ्खति) To go, to move or approach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=323-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिख|त्रिखं
त्रिख n. (-खं) A cucumber.<BR> E. त्रि three, and ख a cavity or space; also<BR>read sometimes तृख ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=323-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिखट्व
त्रिखट्व nf. (-ट्वं-ट्वी) The aggregate of three beds.<BR> E. त्रि three, खट्वा a<BR>bed, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=323-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिगण|त्रिगणः
त्रिगण m. (-णः) The aggregate of three human objects, or virtue,<BR>wealth, and desire.<BR> E. त्रि three, and गण a class: see त्रिवर्ग.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=323-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिगत
त्रिगत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Tripled.<BR>	 2. Gone or done in three ways.<BR>	 n.<BR>(-तं) The expression of different senses by the same word.<BR> E. त्रि,<BR>and गत gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=323-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिगर्त्त|त्रिगर्त|त्रिगर्त्तः
त्रिगर्त्त m. (-र्त्तः)<BR>	 1. A country in the north-west division of India, or m.<BR>plu. (-र्त्ताः) Its inhabitants: apparently part of Lahore, said, by<BR>Mr. WILFORD, to be the modern Tahora, but differently described<BR>in the Koshas: see जालन्धर and वालहीक.<BR>	 2. A form of calculation,<BR>(गणितान्तरे.)<BR>	 f. (-र्त्ता)<BR>	 1. A small worm.<BR>	 2. A lascivious woman, a<BR>wanton.<BR>	 3. A woman in general.<BR>	 4. A pearl.<BR> E. त्रि three, and गर्त्त<BR>a hole, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=323-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिगर्त्तक|त्रिगर्तक|त्रिगर्त्तकः
त्रिगर्त्तक m. (-कः) A country, the same as Valhika: see वाल्हीक.<BR> E. कन्<BR>added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=323-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिगुण|त्रिगुणं
त्रिगुण mfn. (-णः-णा-णी-णं)<BR>	 1. Thrice, three times, triple.<BR>	 2. Possessing<BR>the three Gunas or properties.<BR>	 n. (-णं) The aggregate of the three<BR>qualities incident to human nature.<BR> E. त्रि three, गुण a time or<BR>property.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=323-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिगुणाकृत|त्रिगुणाकृतं
त्रिगुणाकृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Thrice ploughed, (a field, &c.)<BR> E. त्रिगुण three<BR>times, and आकृत made, wrought.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=323-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिगूढ
त्रिगूढ n. (-ढं) The dancing or acting of a man in female attire.<BR> E. त्रि,<BR>and गूढ concealed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=323-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिचतुर
त्रिचतुर mfn. plur. (-राः-राः-राणि) Three or four.<BR> E. त्रि, and चतुर् four,<BR>अच added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=324-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिजातक|त्रिजातकं
त्रिजातक n. (-कं) Three spices collectively, mace, cardamoms, and<BR>cassia leaf.<BR> E. त्रि, and जातक species.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=324-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिज्या
त्रिज्या f. (-ज्या) A radius, a sine of three signs or ninety degrees.<BR> E. त्रि,<BR>and ज्या a sine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=324-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिण|त्रिणं
त्रिण n. (-णं) Grass, meadow grass. E. See तृण, ऋ being changed to रि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=324-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिणता
त्रिणता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. A bow.<BR>	 2. The state or abstract property of grass.<BR>E. त्रिण for तृण grass. and तल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=324-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिणाचिकेत|त्रिणाचिकेतः
त्रिणाचिकेत n. (-तं) A portion of the Yajur Veda.<BR>	 m. (-तः) A follower of<BR>that branch of the Vedas. It is also sometimes read तृणाचिकेत ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=324-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रितक्ष|त्रितक्षं
त्रितक्ष nf. (-क्षं-क्षी) An assemblage of three carpenters.<BR> E. त्रि three, तक्ष<BR>a carpenter, affix अच् समा० ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=324-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रितय|त्रितयं
त्रितय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Third.<BR> E. त्रि three, तयप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=324-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिदण्ड|त्रिदंड|त्रिदण्डः
त्रिदण्ड n. (-ण्डं)<BR>	 1. Three staves collectively.<BR>	 2. Triple subjection of<BR>words, thoughts, and acts; the state of a religious ascetic.<BR> E. त्रि<BR>three, दण्ड a staff, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=324-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिदण्डधारण
त्रिदण्डधारण n. (-णं) Carrying three staves tied together, (as done by<BR>some mendicants.)<BR> E. त्रिदण्ड, and धारण holding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=324-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिदण्डिन्|त्रिदंडिन्
त्रिदण्डिन् m. (-ण्डी)<BR>	 1. A wandering devotee, one who carries three long<BR>bamboo staves in his right hand.<BR>	 2. The religious man who has ob-<BR>tained a command over his words, thoughts, and actions, or mind,<BR>body, and speech.<BR> E. त्रि three, and दण्ड a punishment, a staff, &c.<BR>इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=324-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिदला
त्रिदला f. (-ला) A creeping plant, (Cissus pedata.)<BR> E. त्रि three, and दल<BR>a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=324-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिदश|त्रिदशः
त्रिदश m. (-शः) A god, a deity, an immortal.<BR> E. त्रि the third, and दशा<BR>state, being, (youth;) enjoying perpetual youth, or त्रि three, and<BR>दश state, subject as well as mortals to the three conditions, of<BR>birth, being, and destruction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=324-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिदश|त्रिदशः
त्रिदश mfn. (-शः-शा-शं) Thirteenth.<BR>	 f. (-शी) The thirteenth day of the<BR>fortnight; also त्रयोदश ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=324-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिदशदीर्घिका
त्रिदशदीर्घिका f. (-का) The heavenly Ganges.<BR> E. त्रिदश a deity, and दीर्घिका<BR>a long pool.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=324-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिदशन्
त्रिदशन् mfn. plu. (-श) Thirteen.<BR> E. त्रि three, and दशन् ten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=324-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिदशनदी
त्रिदशनदी f. (-दी) The heavenly Ganges.<BR> E. त्रिदश, and नदी a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=324-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिदशपति
त्रिदशपति m. (-तिः) INDRA.<BR> E. त्रिदश, and पति chief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=324-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिदशबधू
त्रिदशबधू f. (-धूः) A nymph of INDRA'S heaven.<BR> E. त्रिशद, and बधू wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=324-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिदशवनिता
त्रिदशवनिता f. (-ता) A nymph of INDRA'S heaven.<BR> E. त्रिदश, and वनिता<BR>a wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=324-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिदशाङ्कुश|त्रिदशांकुश
त्रिदशाङ्कुश n. (-शं) The thunderbolt.<BR> E. त्रिदश a deity, and अङ्कुश a goad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=324-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिदशाचार्य्य|त्रिदशाचार्य
त्रिदशाचार्य्य m. (-र्य्यः) The preceptor of the gods, VṚHASPATI.<BR> E. त्रिदश a<BR>deity, and आचार्य्य a teacher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=324-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिदशायुध|त्रिदशायुधं
त्रिदशायुध n. (-धं) The thunderbolt of INDRA.<BR> E. त्रिदश a deity, and आयुध<BR>a weapon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=324-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिदशारि|त्रिदशारिः
त्रिदशारि m. (-रिः) An Asura or infernal being hostile to the gods, a<BR>Titan, a Giant.<BR> E. त्रिदश a deity, and अरि a foe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=324-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिदशालय|त्रिदशालयः
त्रिदशालय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. Svarga, INDRA'S heaven or paradise.<BR>	 2. The moun-<BR>tain Sumeru.<BR> E. त्रिदश a deity, and आलय an abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=324-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिदशावास|त्रिदशावासः
त्रिदशावास m. (-सः) Svarga, the heaven of INDRA.<BR> E. त्रिदश a god, and<BR>आवास abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=324-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिदशाहार|त्रिदशाहारः
त्रिदशाहार m. (-रः) Amrita or ambrosia.<BR> E. त्रिदश a deity, and आहार food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=324-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिदालिका
त्रिदालिका f. (-का) A plant, commonly Charmaghasa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=324-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिदिन
त्रिदिन n. (-नं) Three days collectively.<BR> E. त्रि, and दिन a day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=324-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिदिनस्पृश्
त्रिदिनस्पृश् m. (-स्पृक्) Conjunction or concurrence of three lunations with<BR>one solar day.<BR> E. त्रिदिन, and स्पृश् contact.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=324-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिदिव|त्रिदिवः
त्रिदिव mn. (-वः-वं)<BR>	 1. Svarga or paradise.<BR>	 2. Sky, atmosphere, heaven.<BR>f. (-वा) The name of a river.<BR> E. त्रि the three, BRAMHA, VIṢṆU,<BR>and ŚIVA, दिव् to sport, affix क; the place where these three gods<BR>take divine pleasure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=324-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिदिवेश|त्रिदिवेशः
त्रिदिवेश m. (-शः) A god, a deity.<BR> E. त्रिदिव heaven, and ईश master or<BR>lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=324-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिदिवौकस्
त्रिदिवौकस् m. (-काः) A god, a celestial.<BR> E. त्रिदिव heaven, and ओकस्<BR>asylum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=324-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिदृश्
त्रिदृश् mfn. (-दृक्) Tri-ocular, three-eyed.<BR>	 m. (-दृक्) A name of ŚIVA. E.<BR>त्रि three, and दृश् an eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=324-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिदोष|त्रिदोषं
त्रिदोष n. (-षं) Disorder of the three humours of the body, vitiation of<BR>the bile, blood, and phlegm.<BR> E. त्रि three, and दीष a fault.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=324-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिदोषघ्न
त्रिदोषघ्न mfn. (-घ्नः-घ्नी-घ्नं) Correcting the vitiated state of the three hu-<BR>mours.<BR> E. त्रिदोष, and घ्न what destroys.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=324-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिदोषज|त्रिदोषजः
त्रिदोषज m. (-जः) Disease, &c. proceeding from disorder of the three hu-<BR>mours of the body.<BR> E. त्रिदोष, and ज produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=324-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिधा
त्रिधा ind. In three ways.<BR> E. त्रि, and धाच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=324-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिधातु|त्रिधातुः
त्रिधातु m. (-तुः) A name of GANESA.<BR>	 n. (-त) Three minerals, &c.<BR> E. त्रि<BR>three, and धातु mineral, &c. त्रीन् धर्मार्थकामान् दधाति पुष्णाति धा-तुन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=324-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिधामन्
त्रिधामन् mfn. (-मा-मा-म) Having three residences, &c.<BR>	 m. (-मा)<BR>	 1. A<BR>name of VIṢṆU.<BR>	 2. An appellation of ŚIVA.<BR>	 3. Agni or fire.<BR>	 4.<BR>Death.<BR> E. त्रि three (worlds,) and धामन् abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=324-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिनयन|त्रिनयनः
त्रिनयन mfn. (-नः-नी-नं) Three-eyed, tri-ocular.<BR>	 m. (-नः) A name of ŚIVA.<BR>E. त्रि three, and नयन an eye; this deity is represented with a<BR>third eye in his forehead; also similar compounds, as त्रिदृश्, त्रिनेत्र,<BR>त्र्यक्ष, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=324-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिनेत्र|त्रिनेत्रः
त्रिनेत्र mfn. (-त्रः-त्रा-त्रं) Tri-ocular.<BR>	 m. (-त्रः) ŚIVA.<BR> E. त्रि, and नेत्र eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=324-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिनेत्रचूडामणि|त्रिनेत्रचूडामणिः
त्रिनेत्रचूडामणि m. (-णिः) The moon.<BR> E. त्रिनेत्र ŚIVA, चूडा a crest, and मणि<BR>a gem; being worn by that deity as his crest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=324-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिपक्ष
त्रिपक्ष n. (-क्षं) A period of six weeks.<BR> E. त्रि, and पक्ष a fortnight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=324-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिषताक
त्रिषताक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. The forehead marked naturally with three horizon-<BR>tal lines.<BR>	 2. The hand with three fingers erect.<BR> E. त्रि three or three-<BR>fold, and पताका a banner, a symbol.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=324-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिपत्र|त्रिपत्रं|त्रिपत्रः
त्रिपत्र mfn. (-त्रः-त्रा-त्रं) Three-leaved trefoil.<BR>	 m. (-त्रः) A bell tree, (Ægle<BR>marmelos.)<BR> E. त्रि, and पत्र leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=324-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिपत्रक|त्रिपत्रकः
त्रिपत्रक m. (-कः) The Kiṃśuka tree, (Butea frondosa.)<BR> E. त्रि three, and<BR>पत्र a leaf; having three leaves on each stalk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=324-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिपथ|त्रिपथं
त्रिपथ n. (-थं)<BR>	 1. A place where three roads meet.<BR>	 2. Three ways or<BR>paths.<BR> E. त्रि, and पथ a road.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=324-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिपथगा
त्रिपथगा f. (-गा) The Ganges.<BR> E. त्रिपथ three roads, and गा who goes,<BR>flowing through earth, heaven, and hell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=324-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिपद
त्रिपद mfn. (-दः-दा-दी-दं)<BR>	 1. Three-footed.<BR>	 2. Having three lines or divi-<BR>sions, (a stanza.)<BR>	 3. (In Arithmetic,) Trinomial.<BR>	 n. (-दं)<BR>	 1. A<BR>tripod.<BR>	 f. (-दा) A verse of three lines, as the Gayatri.<BR>	 f. (-दी)<BR>	 1. A<BR>creeper, (Cissus pedata.)<BR>	 2. The girth of an elephant.<BR> E. त्रि three,<BR>and पद a foot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=324-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिपर्ण|त्रिपर्णः
त्रिपर्ण mfn. (-र्णः-र्णी-र्णं) Three leaved trefoil.<BR>	 f. (-र्णी) Wild cotton.<BR> E. त्रि<BR>three, and पर्ण a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=324-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिपाद्
त्रिपाद् m. (-पाद्)<BR>	 1. A name of VIṢṆU.<BR>	 2. Fever, (personified.)<BR> E. त्रि<BR>three, and पाद foot or part, three-footed, alluding to VIṢṆU'S<BR>three steps which paced the universe; and the demon of fever is<BR>described in the Puranas, with three feet, and three heads, allud-<BR>ing probably to its three stages of cold, hot, and sweating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=324-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिपिव
त्रिपिव m. (-वः) A long-eared goat.<BR> E. त्रि, and पिव who drinks, touching<BR>water with both ears as he laps.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=324-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिपिष्टप|त्रिपिष्टपं
त्रिपिष्टप n. (-पं)<BR>	 1. Heaven, Svarga or paradise.<BR>	 2. Sky, æther.<BR> E. पिष्टप<BR>a world, and त्रि three, or the third; also त्रिविष्टप ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=324-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिपिष्टपसद्
त्रिपिष्टपसद् m. (-सद्) A deity.<BR> E. त्रिपिष्ठप heaven, and सद् who goes,<BR>from सद् with क्विप् affix; also त्रिविष्ठपसद् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=324-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिपुट|त्रिपुटः
त्रिपुट m. (-टः)<BR>	 1. Pulse, pease of three kinds.<BR>	 2. A bank or shore.<BR>	 3.<BR>A kind of vetch, (Cicer arietinum.)<BR>	 4. A cubit.<BR>	 5. A plant,<BR>(Ruellia longifolia)<BR>	 f. (-टा-टी) A plant, (Convolvulus turpethum.)<BR>f. (-टा) Small cardamoms.<BR>	 2. Arabian jasmine.<BR>	 3. A goddess. E.<BR>त्रि three, and पुट skin or coat of a seed, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=324-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिपुटक|त्रिपुटकः
त्रिपुटक m. (-कः) A triangle.<BR> E. कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=325-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिपुटिन्
त्रिपुटिन् m. (-टी) The castor-oil plant.<BR> E. त्रि three, पुट the Seed vessel,<BR>and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=325-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिपुटीफल|त्रिपुटीफलः
त्रिपुटीफल m. (-लः) The castor-oil plant.<BR> E. त्रिपुटी as above, and फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=325-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिपुण्ड्र|त्रिपुंड्र|त्रिपुण्ड्रं
त्रिपुण्ड्र n. (-ण्ड्रं) Three curved horizontal marks, made across the fore-<BR>head with cowdung, &c.; they are worn especially by the fol-<BR>lowers of ŚIVA, or SAKTI, and are indispensable in proceeding to<BR>worship the former.<BR> E. त्रि three, triple, and पुण्ड्र a line; also with<BR>कन् added त्रिपुण्ड्रक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=325-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिपुण्ड्रक|त्रिपुण्ड्रकं
त्रिपुण्ड्रक n. (कं) See the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=325-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिपुर|त्रिपुरं|त्रिपुरः
त्रिपुर nf. (-रं-री)<BR>	 1. The three cities gold, silver and iron erected by the<BR>demon Maya and burnt down by ŚIVA.<BR>	 2. A district, the modern<BR>Tipperah, &c.<BR>	 m. (-रः) The name of an Asura, and king of<BR>Tripura.<BR> E. त्रि three, and पुर a city, the district and dominion of<BR>that Asura, consisting of three strong and famous cities.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=325-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिपुरदहन|त्रिपुरदहनः
त्रिपुरदहन m. (-नः) A name of ŚIVA.<BR> E. त्रिपुर the country of Tripura,<BR>and दहन burning, consuming; the Asura and his three cities<BR>being destroyed by MAHADEVA; also similar names, as त्रिपुरजित्,<BR>त्रिपुरसूदन, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=325-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिपुरमल्लिका
त्रिपुरमल्लिका f. (-का) A medicinal plant, apparently a kind of jasmine.<BR>E. त्रिपुर Tipperah, and मल्लिका jasmine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=325-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिपुरान्तक|त्रिपुरांतक|त्रिपुरान्तकः
त्रिपुरान्तक m. (-कः) A name of ŚIVA.<BR> E. त्रिपुर, and अन्तक ender, destroyer:<BR>see त्रिपुरदहन ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=325-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिपुरुष
त्रिपुरुष n. (-षं) Three generation collectively.<BR> E. त्रि three, पुरुष a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=325-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिपुरुषागत
त्रिपुरुषागत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Enjoyed or inherited through three genera-<BR>tions.<BR> E. त्रिपुरुष, and आगत come.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=325-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिपुषा
त्रिपुषा f. (-षा) Black Teori. त्रीन् वातादिदोषान् पुष्णाति पुष-क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=325-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिपौरुष
त्रिपौरुष mfn. (-षः-षी-षं) Relating or belonging to three persons or<BR>generations, offered to three, (the funeral cake, &c.) inherited from<BR>three, (an estate, &c.)<BR> E. त्रिपुरुष, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=325-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिपृष्ठ|त्रिपृष्ठः
त्रिपृष्ठ m. (-ष्ठः) A king, and one of the Vāsudevas, or descendants of<BR>VASUDEVA, according the Jainas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=325-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिफला
त्रिफला f. (-ला) The three myrobalans collectively.<BR> E. त्रि three, फल<BR>fruit, fem. affix टाप्; also with ङीष् affix त्रिफली ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=325-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिबलीक|त्रिबलीकं
त्रिबलीक n. (-कं) The anus.<BR> E. त्रि three, (the three humors,) तिस्रो<BR>बलो यत्र कप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=325-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिभण्डी
त्रिभण्डी f. (-ण्डी) A plant, (Convolvulus turpethum.)<BR> E. त्रि three,<BR>(ailments, or bile, phlegm, and fever,) भडि to oppose, affixes अण्<BR>and ङीष्. त्रीन् वातादिदोषान् भण्डति ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=325-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिभद्र|त्रिभद्रं
त्रिभद्र n. (-द्रं) Copulation, cohabitation.<BR> E. त्रि three, and भद्र pleasurable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=325-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिभुज
त्रिभुज m. (-जः) A triangle.<BR> E. त्रि, and भुज an arm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=325-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिभुवन|त्रिभुवनं
त्रिभुवन n. (-नं) Three worlds, or heaven, earth and hell.<BR> E. त्रि three, and<BR>भुवन a world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=325-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिमधु|त्रिमधुः
त्रिमधु m. (-धुः)<BR>	 1. A portion of the Rig Veda.<BR>	 2. A follower or student<BR>of the Trimadhu section of the Rig Veda.<BR>	 n. (-धु) Ghee, honey, and<BR>sugar.<BR> E. त्रि, and मधु honey.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=325-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिमार्गी|त्रिमार्ग्गी
त्रिमार्गी f. (-र्गी) The meeting of three roads.<BR> E. त्रि three, and मार्ग a road.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=325-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिमुकुट|त्रिमुकुटः
त्रिमुकुट m. (-टः) A mountain with three peaks.<BR> E. त्रि three, and मुकुट a<BR>crest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=325-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिमुख|त्रिमुखः
त्रिमुख mfn. (-खः-खी-खं) Having three faces.<BR>	 m. (-खः) A divine attendant<BR>upon a Jaina saint.<BR>	 f. (-खा) A female deity of the Jaina sect.<BR> E. त्रि<BR>three, and मुख a face, three-faced, or त्रि three (worlds,) and<BR>मुख principal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=325-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिमूर्त्ति|त्रिमूर्ति|त्रिमूर्तिः|त्रिमूर्त्तिः
त्रिमूर्त्ति m. (-र्त्तिः)<BR>	 1. A Jina or Jaina saint.<BR>	 2. The united form of BRAMHA,<BR>VIṢṆU, and ŚIVA, or the Hindu triad.<BR>	 3. One possessing three<BR>forms or modes of being.<BR> E. त्रि thee, and मूर्त्ति form, matter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=325-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिमूर्द्ध
त्रिमूर्द्ध mfn. (-र्द्धः-र्द्धी-र्द्धं) Three-headed.<BR> E. त्रि, and मूर्द्धन् the forehead, ष<BR>aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=325-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रियव
त्रियव n. (-वं) A Ratti or weight of three barley-corns.<BR> E. त्रि, and यव<BR>barley.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=325-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रियष्टि|त्रियष्टिः
त्रियष्टि m. (-ष्टिः)<BR>	 1. A medicinal plant.<BR>	 2. A necklace of three strings.<BR>(Mollugo pentaphylla.)<BR> E. त्रि three, and यष्टि a line; having three<BR>stalks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=325-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रियामक|त्रियामकं
त्रियामक n. (-कं) Sin.<BR> E. त्रि the three objects of life, and यामक impeder,<BR>from यम् with ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=325-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रियामा
त्रियामा f. (-मा)<BR>	 1. Night.<BR>	 2. The YAMUNĀ or Jumna river.<BR>	 3. Indigo.<BR>4. Black Teori, a plant so called.<BR>	 5. Turmeric.<BR> E. त्रि three (times, or<BR>past, present and future,) या to go, affix मन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=325-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रियूह|त्रियूहः
त्रियूह m. (-हः) A brown or chesnut horse. कपिलाश्वे ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=325-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिरात्र|त्रिरात्रं|त्रिरात्रः
त्रिरात्र n. (-त्रं) Three nights collectively, or the duration of three nights.<BR>E. त्रि three, and रात्रि night; compounded with a numeral रात्रि sub-<BR>stitutes अ for its final, and becomes neuter. तिसृणां रात्रीणां समाहारः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=325-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिरेख|त्रिरेखः
त्रिरेख m. (-खः) A conch.<BR> E. त्रि, and रेखा a line; this shell being mark-<BR>ed with three lines. तिस्रो रेखा यत्र । शङ्के ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=325-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिलोकी
त्रिलोकी f. (-की) The aggregate of the three worlds, or heaven, earth,<BR>and hell, collectively.<BR> E. त्रि three, and लोक a world, and ङीप्<BR>affix, with the sense of aggregation. त्रयाणां लोकानां समाहारः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=325-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिलोकेश|त्रिलोकेशः
त्रिलोकेश m. (-शः)<BR>	 1. The sun.<BR>	 2. God.<BR> E. त्रिलोक the three worlds or the<BR>universe, and ईश lord. त्रयाणां लोकानाम् ईशः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=325-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिलोचन|त्रिलोचनः
त्रिलोचन mfn. (-नः-नी-नं) Tri-ocular, three-eyed.<BR>	 m. (-नः) A name of<BR>ŚIVA.<BR>	 f. (-ना) A female deity of the Jainas.<BR>	 f. (-नी) A name of<BR>DURGĀ.<BR> E. त्रि three, and लोचन an eye: see त्रिदृश्, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=325-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिलोहक|त्रिलोहकं
त्रिलोहक n. (-कं) Gold, silver, and copper.<BR> E. त्रि, and लोहक metal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=325-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिवर्ग|त्रिवर्गः
त्रिवर्ग m. (-र्गः)<BR>	 1. Three human objects or pursuits as love, duty, and<BR>wealth.<BR>	 2. Three conditions of a king or state; prosperity, even-<BR>ness, and decay; or loss, gain, equality, &c.<BR>	 3. The three qualities<BR>of nature, purity, blindness, and depravity.<BR>	 4. The three myroba-<BR>lans.<BR>	 5. The three spices: see त्रिकटु.<BR>	 6. propriety, good behavior.<BR>E. त्रि three, and वर्ग a class; a class or aggregate of three.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=325-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिवर्गपारीण
त्रिवर्गपारीण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Having passed through the three condi-<BR>tions, or attained the three objects of life.<BR> E. त्रिवर्ग, and पारीण<BR>gone to the opposite shore.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=325-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिवर्णक|त्रिवर्णकं
त्रिवर्णक n. (-कं)<BR>	 1. The three myrobalans.<BR>	 2. The three spices.<BR>	 3. A<BR>plant, (Ruellia longifolia:) see गीक्षुरक.<BR> E. त्रि three, वर्ण a class, and<BR>कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=325-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिवर्षिका
त्रिवर्षिका f. (-का) A three years old heifer.<BR> E. त्रि, and वर्ष a year, affix ठन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=325-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिवली
त्रिवली f. (-ली) Three folds of skin on the abdomen, from obesity.<BR> E. त्रि,<BR>and वली a wrinkle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=325-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिविक्रम|त्रिविक्रमः
त्रिविक्रम m. (-मः) A name of VIṢṆU.<BR> E. त्रि, and विक्रम going; crossing<BR>over the three worlds in three steps, to the discomfiture of BALI.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=325-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिविद्या
त्रिविद्या f. (-द्या) Three branches of knowledge, especially that of the<BR>three Vedas.<BR> E. त्रि, and विद्या knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=325-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिविध
त्रिविध mfn. (धः-धा-धं) In three ways, of three kinds.<BR> E. त्रि, and विध sort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=325-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिविष्टप|त्रिविष्टपं
त्रिविष्टप n. (-पं)<BR>	 1. Heaven or paradise.<BR>	 2. The three worlds, or heaven,<BR>earth, and hell: see त्रिपिष्टप ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=325-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिविष्टपसद्
त्रिविष्टपसद् m. (-सद्) A deity; also त्रिपिष्टपसद् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=325-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिवृत्
त्रिवृत् mfn. (-वृत्) Triple, triform, threefold.<BR>	 m. (-वृत्)<BR>	 1. A plant of<BR>valuable purgative properties, commonly called Teori, and distin-<BR>guished into two species, white and black, (Convolvulus turpe-<BR>thum.)<BR>	 2. Combining any thing by three.<BR>	 3. A triple cord, a girdle,<BR>&c. of three strings.<BR>	 4. A kind of sacrifice.<BR> E. त्रि three, (three seed<BR>vessels,) वृ to cherish, affix क्विप्, and तुक् added: also with टाप्<BR>added त्रिवृता f. (-ता.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=325-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिवृत्करण|त्रिवृत्करणं
त्रिवृत्करण n. (-णं) Combining earth, water, and fire, in the proportion of<BR>half of one with a quarter of each of the others.<BR> E. त्रिवृत्, and करण<BR>making.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=325-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिवृत्पर्णी
त्रिवृत्पर्णी f. (-र्णी) A potherb, (Hilancha repens.)<BR> E. त्रिवृत् Teori, and पर्ण<BR>a leaf; having similar leaves.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=325-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिवेणी
त्रिवेणी f. (-णी) A name of the Ganges.<BR> E. त्रि three, वेणी a braid of hair:<BR>the name is especially applied to the river at Allahabad, where it<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=326-a" target="_blank">Page326-a+ 60</a>]<BR>receives the Jumuna, and is supposed to receive under ground the<BR>Sarasvatī; it is also that of a village in Bengal, above Hugli.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=325-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिवेद|त्रिवेदः
त्रिवेद n. (-दं) The three Vedas collectively.<BR> E. त्रि, and वेद a Veda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=326-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिवेदिन्
त्रिवेदिन् m. (-दी) A Bramhan acquainted with three Vedas.<BR> E. त्रिवेद, and<BR>इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=326-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिशङ्कु|त्रिशंकु|त्रिशङ्कुः
त्रिशङ्कु m. (-ङ्कुः)<BR>	 1. The name of a king of the solar race, famous for<BR>attempting to go to heaven in his mortal frame, by the aid of<BR>VISWAMITRA.<BR>	 2. A cat.<BR>	 3. A grasshopper.<BR>	 4. A bird, the Chataka,<BR>(Cuculus melanoleucos.)<BR>	 5. A fire-fly.<BR> E. त्रि three, शङ्कु a dart, ट aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=326-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिशङ्कुज|त्रिशंकुज|त्रिशङ्कुजः
त्रिशङ्कुज m. (-जः) A name of HARISCHANDRA, a prince.<BR> E. त्रिशङ्कु, and ज<BR>born, descended from TRISANKU.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=326-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिशङ्कुयाजिन्|त्रिशंकुयाजिन्
त्रिशङ्कुयाजिन् m. (-जी) VISWAMITRA, a celebrated sage and saint.<BR> E. त्रिशङ्कु<BR>the king so named, and याजिन् causing to worship; being the<BR>family priest of the monarch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=326-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिशरण|त्रिशरणः
त्रिशरण m. (-णः) A Jina, a sanctified teacher of the Jaina sect.<BR> E. त्रि<BR>three, (the three worlds,) and शरण protection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=326-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिशला
त्रिशला f. (-ला) The mother of VARDDHAMANA, the last of the Jaina<BR>pontiffs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=326-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिशिख|त्रिशिखं|त्रिशिखः
त्रिशिख mfn. (-खः-खा-खं) Three-crested, three-headed.<BR>	 n. (-खं)<BR>	 1. A crest,<BR>a tiara with three points.<BR>	 2. A trident, a three pronged spear.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-खः) The son of RAVANA, a demon with three heads.<BR> E. त्रि three,<BR>and शिखा a crest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=326-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिशिरस्
त्रिशिरस् mfn. (-राः-राः-रः) Three-headed.<BR>	 m. (-राः) A name of KUVERA.<BR>2. Fever personified as a demon with three heads: see त्रिपाद.<BR>	 3. A<BR>son of RAVANA.<BR> E. त्र three, and शिरस् a head.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=326-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिशीर्षक|त्रिशीर्षकं
त्रिशीर्षक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Three-headed.<BR>	 m. (-कः) A trident, tri-pointed<BR>spear.<BR> E. त्रि three, and शीर्ष a head, affix कन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=326-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिशूल|त्रिशूलं
त्रिशूल n. (-लं) A trident, a three-pointed pike or spear, especially the<BR>weapon of ŚIVA.<BR> E. त्रि three or Tri, and शूल a dar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=326-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिशूलिन्
त्रिशूलिन् m. (-ली) A name of ŚIVA.<BR> E. त्रिशूल, and इनि affix, armed with<BR>a trident.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=326-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिशृङ्ग|त्रिशृंग|त्रिशृङ्गः
त्रिशृङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>	 1. A hill with three peaks.<BR>	 2. A triangle.<BR> E. त्रि three,<BR>and शृङ्ग a horn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=326-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिशृङ्गिन्
त्रिशृङ्गिन् m. (-ङ्गी) A sort of fish, commonly Rohi, (Cyprinus rohita,<BR>HAM.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=326-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिषवण
त्रिषवण n. (-णं) The three ablutions to be performed in the day or at<BR>dawn, noon, and sunset.<BR> E. त्रि three, षवन bathing; also read<BR>त्रिसवन ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=326-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिषवणस्नायिन्
त्रिषवणस्नायिन् m. (-यी) A man performing regularly the prescribed ablu-<BR>tions, at morning, noon, and night.<BR> E. त्रि three, सवन time or period<BR>of ablution, and स्नायिन् who bathes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=326-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिष्टुभ्
त्रिष्टुभ् f. (-ष्टुप्) A form of metre, the stanza consisting of four lines of<BR>eleven syllables each, or of five lines, one of eleven and four of<BR>eight each, forming altogether forty-four syllables; there are other<BR>varieties.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=326-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिष्ठ
त्रिष्ठ mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठा-ष्ठं) Situated in three places.<BR> E. त्रि, and स्था to be, क<BR>aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=326-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिसन्ध्य|त्रिसंध्य|त्रिसन्ध्यं
त्रिसन्ध्य mfn. (-न्ध्यः-न्ध्या or न्ध्यी-न्ध्यं) The three periods of the day, or dawn,<BR>noon, and eve.<BR> E. त्रि three, and सन्ध्य either of the periods.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=326-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिसम|त्रिसमं
त्रिसम n. (-मं) An aggregate of three like or equal things.<BR> E. त्रि, and सम<BR>same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=326-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिसर|त्रिसरः
त्रिसर subst.<BR>	 mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) A dish of sesamum, rice, &c.<BR> E. त्रि three,<BR>threefold, and सर what is, from सृ to go or get, affix अप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=326-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिसवन|त्रिसवनं
त्रिसवन n. (-नं) Bathing thrice: see त्रिषवण ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=326-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिसीत्य|त्रिसीत्यं
त्रिसीत्य mfn. (-त्यः-त्या-त्यं) Thrice ploughed, (a field, &c.)<BR> E. त्रि thrice, and<BR>सीत्य ploughed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=326-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिसुपर्ण|त्रिसुपर्णः
त्रिसुपर्ण m. (-र्णः)<BR>	 1. A portion of the Rig and Yajur Vedas.<BR>	 2. A ob-<BR>servance enjoined by it.<BR>	 3. A Brahman following it.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=326-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिसुपर्णिक
त्रिसुपर्णिक m. (-कः) A Tri Suparna Brahman: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=326-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिस्रोतस्
त्रिस्रोतस् f. (-ताः)<BR>	 1. The Ganges.<BR>	 2. Another river.<BR> E. त्रि three, and<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=326-b" target="_blank">Page326-b+ 60</a>]<BR>स्रोतस् a river, the river of the three worlds, or one with three<BR>channels.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=326-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिहल्य|त्रिहल्यं
त्रिहल्य mfn. (-ल्यः-ल्या-ल्यं) Thrice ploughed, (a field, &c.)<BR> E. त्रि thrice, हल्य<BR>ploughed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=326-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिहायण
त्रिहायण mfn. (-णः-णी-णं) Three years, (old, &c.)<BR>	 f. (-णी) A three-years-<BR>old heifer.<BR> E. त्रि, and हायन a year; also read त्रिहायन ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=326-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रुट
त्रुट r. 4th cl. (त्रुट्यति) r. 6th cl. (त्रुटति) and 10th cl. (त्रोटयते) To cut,<BR>literally or metaphorically; to cut, (wood, &c.) to cut or solve,<BR>(difficulties, doubts, &c.) दिवा० तुदा० प० अक० सेट् । चुरा० आत्म० सक०<BR>सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=326-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिटि
त्रिटि f. (-टिः-टी)<BR>	 1. Cutting, breaking.<BR>	 2. Loss, destruction.<BR>	 3. Breaking<BR>a promise, &c.<BR>	 4. Small cardamoms, (Alpinia cardamomum).<BR>5. A short time, a moment.<BR>	 6. Doubt, uncertainty.<BR>	 7. (Always<BR>feminine, though used attributively.) Little, small.<BR>	 8. An<BR>atom, or a visible atom composed of three subtler elementary par-<BR>ticles.<BR> E. त्रुट् to cut or divide, affix इन् and ङीप् optionally added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=326-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रुटित
त्रुटित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Cut, broken, divided.<BR>	 2. Hurt, wounded.<BR> E. त्रुट,<BR>and क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=326-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रुटितवत्
त्रुटितवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Chapped, chafed, cut.<BR> E. त्रुट, and क्तवतु<BR>aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=326-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रुटिवीज|त्रुटिवीजः
त्रुटिवीज m. (-जः) An esculent root: see कचु.<BR> E. त्रुटि small, and वीज<BR>a seed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=326-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रुप
त्रुप r. 1st cl. (त्रोपति) To hurt, to injure or kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=326-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रुफ
त्रुफ r. 1st cl. (त्रोफति) To hurt, to kill or injure; also तुफ, तुम्फ, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=326-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रुम्प
त्रुम्प r. 1st cl. (त्रुम्पति) To hurt or injure: see तुप, तुम्प, &c. भ्वा० पर० सक०<BR>सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=326-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रुम्फ
त्रुम्फ r. 1st cl. (त्रुम्फति) To kill or injure; also त्रुफ, &c. भ्वा० पर० सक०<BR>सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=326-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रेता
त्रेता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. The second Yuga or age of the Hindus, consisting of<BR>1,296,000 years.<BR>	 2. The three sacred fires collectively, or the<BR>southern, household, and sacrificial fires.<BR> E. त्र preservation, &c.<BR>derived from त्रै to preserve, इत obtained, got.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=326-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रेताग्नि
त्रेताग्नि m. (-ग्निः) A man who has preserved the three sacred fires.<BR> E. त्रेता<BR>as above, and अग्नि fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=326-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रेतायुग|त्रेतायुगं
त्रेतायुग n. (-गं) The second or Treta age.<BR> E. त्रेता, and युग age.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=326-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रेधा
त्रेधा ind. Triple, threefold, in three ways.<BR> E. त्रि three, धा affix, and ए<BR>substituted for the vowel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=326-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रै
त्रै (ङ) त्रैङ् r. 1st cl. (त्रायते) To preserve, to protect, to cherish, to de-<BR>fend, &c.<BR> E. भ्वा० आ० सक० अनिट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=326-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रैगुणिक
त्रैगुणिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Giving three times, relating to thrice, three<BR>qualities, &c.<BR> E. त्रिगुण, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=326-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रैगुण्य|त्रैगुण्यं
त्रैगुण्य n. (-ण्यं)<BR>	 1. The quality of three Gunas or properties collectively.<BR>2. A trine, a multiplication by three.<BR> E. त्रिगुण, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=326-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रैदशिक
त्रैदशिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Sacred to the gods, belonging or relating to<BR>them. त्रिदश, and ठञ् aff. त्रिदशा देवता अस्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=326-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रैधम्
त्रैधम् ind. In three ways, threefold.<BR> E. त्रि three, धमञ् affix; also ड<BR>being added, the word becomes an attributive, and may be in-<BR>flected in the three genders, also त्रैध, mfn. (-धः-धी-धं) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=326-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रैपुर|त्रैपुरः
त्रैपुर m. (-रः) Tripura or Tipperah: see त्रिपुर.<BR> E. स्वार्थे अण् added to त्रिपुर ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=326-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रैराशिक|त्रैराशिकं
त्रैराशिक mf. (-कः-का) (In Arithmetic,) The rule of three: it is of two<BR>kinds क्रमत्रैराशिकः Rule of three direct, व्यस्त or विलोमत्रैराशिकः Rule<BR>of three inverse.<BR> E. त्रि three, राशि quantity, ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=326-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रैरूप्य
त्रैरूप्य n. (-प्यं) Three ways or forms.<BR> E. त्रि, रूप form, ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=326-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रैलोक्य|त्रैलोक्यं
त्रैलोक्य n. (-क्यं) The three worlds, or heaven, hell, and earth.<BR> E. त्रिलोक<BR>and ष्यञ् aff. त्रिलोकी एव स्वार्थे ष्यञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=326-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रैलोक्यविजया
त्रैलोक्यविजया f. (-या) A sort of hemp from which an intoxicating infu-<BR>sion, &c. is prepared.<BR> E. त्रैलोक्य and विजय subduing; alluding to<BR>its inebriating properties.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=326-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रैवर्गिक
त्रैवर्गिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Relating to the three objects of life.<BR> E. त्रिवर्ग,<BR>and ठञ् aff. त्रिवर्गाय हितम् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=326-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रैवर्णिक
त्रैवर्णिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Relating or belonging to three castes, the first<BR>three.<BR> E. त्रि, वर्ण cast, स्वार्थे ठञ् aff. त्रिषु वर्णेषु विहितः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=327-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रैवार्षिक
त्रैवार्षिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Triennial, three years old, &c.<BR> E. त्रिवर्ष three<BR>years, aff. ठञ् । त्रिवर्षे भूतो भवति वा ठञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=327-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रैविद्य|त्रैविद्यं|त्रैविद्यः
त्रैविद्य m. (-द्यः) A scholar in the three Vedas, or one who possesses<BR>three sciences.<BR>	 n. (-द्यं) A collection or assembly of learned Brahm-<BR>ans.<BR> E. त्रि three, विद्या knowledge, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=327-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रैविध्य|त्रैविध्यं
त्रैविध्य n. (-ध्यं) Three ways or kinds.<BR> E. त्रिविध, and यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=327-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रैवेदिक
त्रैवेदिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Scriptural, enjoined by the Vedas.<BR> E. त्रिवेद,<BR>and ठक् aff. त्रिषु वेदेषु तदध्ययनार्थं विहितः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=327-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रैष्टुभ
त्रैष्टुभ mfn. (-भः-भी-भं) Relating to or written in the Trishtubha metre.<BR>E. त्रिष्टुभ्, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=327-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रैस्वर्य्य|त्रैस्वर्य
त्रैस्वर्य्य n. (-र्य्यं) The three accents collectively.<BR> E. त्रि, and स्वर vowel<BR>sound, स्वार्थे ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=327-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रैहायण
त्रैहायण n. (-णं) A period or age of three years.<BR> E. त्रिहायण अण् affix;<BR>also read तैहायन. त्रिहायणस्य इदम् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=327-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रोटक|त्रोटकं|त्रोटकः
त्रोटक n. (-कं)<BR>	 1. Angry speech.<BR>	 2. A minor drama, such as the Vikra-<BR>morvasi.<BR> E. त्रुट् to cut, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=327-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रोटकी
त्रोटकी f. (-की) A Rāgiṇī or one female personifications of music.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=327-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रोटि|त्रोटिः
त्रोटि f. (-टिः or -टी)<BR>	 1. The beak or bill of a bird.<BR>	 2. A bird in general.<BR>3. A kind of pike, (Esox kankila.)<BR>	 4. A medicinal plant: see कट्फल.<BR>E. त्रुट् to cut, affix अच्, and fem. affix इन् or ङीप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=327-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रोटिहस्त|त्रोटिहस्तः
त्रोटिहस्त m. (-स्तः) A bird in general.<BR> E. त्रोटि a beak, and हस्त a hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=327-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रोत्र|त्रोत्रं
त्रोत्र n. (-त्रं)<BR>	 1. A goad.<BR>	 2. A weapon.<BR> E. त्रै to preserve, उत्र Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=327-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रौक
त्रौक (ऋ) त्रौकृ r. 10th cl. (त्रौकयते) To go, to move. चुरा० आ० सक० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=327-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्र्यंश|त्र्यंशः
त्र्यंश m. (-शः) Three-fourths, three shares.<BR> E. त्रि, and अंश part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=327-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्र्यक्ष|त्र्यक्षः
त्र्यक्ष mfn. (-क्षः-क्षी-क्षं) Tri-ocular.<BR>	 m. (-क्षः) A name of ŚIVA.<BR> E. त्रि three,<BR>अक्षि an eye, अच् substituted for the final: see त्रिदृश् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=327-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्र्यक्षर|त्र्यक्षरः
त्र्यक्षर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A genealogist, the Ghataka or person whose business it<BR>is to form alliances.<BR>	 2. A word, &c. of three letters.<BR> E. त्रि three,<BR>and अक्षर a letter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=327-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्र्यङ्गट|त्र्यंगट|त्र्यङ्गटं|त्र्यङ्गटः
त्र्यङ्गट mn. (-टः-टं)<BR>	 1. A sling or three strings like those of a balance,<BR>suspended to either end of a pole for the purpose of carrying<BR>burthens.<BR>	 2. A sort of collyrium.<BR>	 m. (-टः) A name of ŚIVA.<BR> E. त्रि<BR>three, अङ्ग body, and अट what goes, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=327-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्र्यञ्जन|त्र्यञ्जनं
त्र्यञ्जन n. (-नं) Combination of three, or Kalanjana, Pushpanjana,<BR>and Karañjana collyria.<BR> E. त्रि, and अञ्जन a collyrium.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=327-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्र्यधिष्ठान|त्र्यधिष्ठानः
त्र्यधिष्ठान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Situate in or affected by three places, (as body,<BR>mind, speech.)<BR> E. त्रि, and अधिष्ठान site.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=327-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्र्यध्वगा
त्र्यध्वगा f. (-गा) A name of the Ganges.<BR> E. त्रि three, अध्व a road, and ग<BR>what goes; going through the three worlds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=327-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्र्यब्द
त्र्यब्द n. (-ब्दं) A period of three years.<BR> E. त्रि, and अब्द a year.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=327-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्र्यम्बक|त्र्यंबक|त्र्यम्बकः
त्र्यम्बक m. (-कः) A name of ŚIVA.<BR> E. त्रि three, (the three Vedas,) अबि<BR>to speak or sound, and कन् added; or त्रि may mean the three<BR>letters, अ, उ, म, combined in the mystical word ओम् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=327-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्र्यम्बकसख|त्र्यंबकसख|त्र्यम्बकसखः
त्र्यम्बकसख m. (-खः) KUVERA the god of wealth.<BR> E. त्र्यम्बक ŚIVA, and<BR>सखि a friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=327-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्र्यवर
त्र्यवर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Having three inferiors or followers.<BR> E. त्रि, and अवर<BR>inferior.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=327-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्र्यसरेणु
त्र्यसरेणु m. (-णुः) A grass atom, one composed of three subtle atoms:<BR>see त्रसरेणु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=327-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्र्यस्र
त्र्यस्र n. (-स्रं) A triangle.<BR> E. त्रि, and अस्र an angle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=327-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्र्यह|त्र्यहः
त्र्यह n. (-हं) Three days collectively.<BR> E. त्रि, and अहन् a day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=327-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्र्यहस्पर्श|त्र्यहस्पर्शः
त्र्यहस्पर्श n. (-र्शं) Meeting of three lunations in one solar day.<BR> E. त्र्यह,<BR>and स्पर्श contact; also त्र्यहस्पृश् m. (-स्पृक्) and त्र्यहस्पृश.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=327-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्र्यहैहिक|त्र्यहैहिकः
त्र्यहैहिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Providing for three days.<BR> E. त्र्यह, and ऐहिक<BR>who makes an effort for.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=327-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्र्याहिक|त्र्याहिकः
त्र्याहिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>	 1. Produced or performed, &c. in three days.<BR>2. Quartan, (fever.)<BR> E. त्रि, and आहिक diurnal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=327-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्र्युषण|त्र्युषणं
त्र्युषण n. (-णं) The three spices collectively, or black pepper, long pep-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=327-b" target="_blank">Page327-b+ 60</a>]<BR>per, and dry ginger.<BR> E. त्रि three, and उषण a spice or pungent sub-<BR>stance; also with ऊषण the same, त्र्यूषण, n. (-णं) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=327-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्व|त्वं|त्वः
त्व mfn. (-त्वः-त्वा-त्वं) Other, different.<BR> E. तन् to divide or spread, and व<BR>substituted for the final letter of the radical.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=327-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वक्कूण्डुर
त्वक्कूण्डुर m. (-रः) A sore or wound.<BR> E. त्वक् the skin, कण्डु itching or<BR>irritation, and र what excites.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=327-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वक्क्षीरा
त्वक्क्षीरा f. (-रा) The manna of the bamboo.<BR> E. त्वच् the bark of the bam-<BR>boo, and क्षीर milk; also with ङीप् affix, त्वक्क्षीरी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=327-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वक्छद|त्वक्छदः
त्वक्छद m. (-दः) A plant, commonly Kṣirakanchuki.<BR> E. त्वक् bark, and<BR>छद a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=327-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वक्छेद|त्वक्छेदः
त्वक्छेद m. (-दः) A cut, a scratch.<BR> E. त्वक्, and छेद a cut.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=327-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वक्त्र
त्वक्त्र n. (-क्त्रं) Armour.<BR> E. त्वक् and त्र what preserves.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=327-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वक्पत्र|त्वक्पत्रं
त्वक्पत्र n. (-त्रं) Woody cassia.<BR>	 f. (-त्री) A medicinal and vegetable sub-<BR>stances: see हिङ्गुपत्री.<BR> E. त्वक् bark, and पत्र a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=327-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वक्परिपुटन
त्वक्परिपुटन n. (-नं) Desquamation, pealing of the skin.<BR> E. त्वक्, and परि-<BR>पुटन pealing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=327-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वक्पुष्प|त्वक्पुष्पं|त्वक्पुष्पः
त्वक्पुष्प n. (-ष्पं) Erection of the hairs of the body, horripilation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=327-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वक्पुष्प|त्वक्पुष्पं|त्वक्पुष्पः
त्वक्पुष्प nf. (-ष्पं-ष्पी) Blotch, scab, cutaneous eruption, &c.<BR> E. त्वक् the<BR>skin and पुष्प a flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=327-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वक्पुष्पिका
त्वक्पुष्पिका f. (-का) Scab, blotch: see the preceding.<BR> E. कन् added to त्वक्पुष्पी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=327-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वक्सार|त्वक्सारः
त्वक्सार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A bamboo.<BR>	 2. Woody cassia.<BR>	 f. (-रा) Bamboo manna.<BR>E. त्वक् bark, and सार essence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=327-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वक्सुगन्ध|त्वक्सुगंध|त्वक्सुगन्धः
त्वक्सुगन्ध m. (-न्धः) An orange.<BR>	 f. (-न्धा) A perfume, commonly Elabalu-<BR>ka.<BR> E. त्वक् skin or rind, and मुगन्ध fragrant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=327-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वग्भेद|त्वग्भेदः
त्वग्भेद m. (-दः) A flesh wound, a scratch.<BR> E. त्वच्, and भेद breaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=327-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वग्भेदक|त्वग्भेदकः
त्वग्भेदक m. (-कः) A stabber, a scratcher, one who draws blood from the<BR>skin.<BR> E. त्वच्, and भेदक who cuts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=327-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वक्ष
त्वक्ष (ऊ) त्वक्षू r. 1st cl. (त्वक्षति)<BR>	 1. To pare, to make thin.<BR>	 2. To be thin.<BR>3. To peel, to skin. भ्वा० सक० पर० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=327-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वग
त्वग (इ) त्वगि r. 1st cl. (त्वंगति) To go, to move. भ्वा० पर० सक० सेट् इदित् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=327-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वगङ्कुर|त्वगंकुर|त्वगङ्कुरः
त्वगङ्कुर m. (-रः) Erection of the hairs of the body.<BR> E. त्वच् or त्वक् skin,<BR>and अङ्कुर a sprout.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=327-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वगस्थिमात्रशेष
त्वगस्थिमात्रशेष mfn. (-षः-षा-षं) Reduced to a skeleton, to mere skin and<BR>bone.<BR> E. त्वच् skin, अस्थि bone, मात्र mere, and शेष end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=327-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वगाक्षीरी
त्वगाक्षीरी f. (-री) The manna of the bamboo.<BR> E. त्वक् bark, आङ् limitative,<BR>and क्षीरी milk, being of a milky colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=327-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वग्गन्ध|त्वग्गंध|त्वग्गन्धः
त्वग्गन्ध m. (-न्धः) An orange.<BR> E. त्वच् rind, गन्ध smell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=327-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वग्दोष|त्वग्दोषः
त्वग्दोष m. (-षः) Leprosy.<BR> E. त्वक्, and दोष fault.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=327-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वग्रोग|त्वग्रोगः
त्वग्रोग m. (-गः)<BR>	 1. Leprosy.<BR>	 2. Any cutaneous disease.<BR> E. त्वच्, and रोग<BR>disease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=327-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वङ्कार|त्वंकार|त्वंकारः
त्वङ्कार n. (-रं) The expression, ‘thou.’<BR> E. त्व, and कार making.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=327-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वङ्मय
त्वङ्मय mfn. (-यः-यी-यं) Made of bark or skin.<BR> E. त्वक् skin, and मयट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=327-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वच|त्वचं
त्वच r. 6th cl. (त्वचति) To cover, to clothe, to invest. तुदा-पर-सक-सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=327-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वच्
त्वच् f. (त्वक्)<BR>	 1. Skin.<BR>	 2. Bark, rind, peel, &c.<BR>	 3. Woody cassia.<BR> E. तन्<BR>to spread, to encircle or cover, Uṇādi affix चिक्, and व substituted<BR>for the final letters of the radical; also अच् being added त्वच and<BR>त्वचा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=327-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वच|त्वचं
त्वच nf. (-चं-चा)<BR>	 1. Skin.<BR>	 2. Bark, rind.<BR>	 3. Woody cassia: see the<BR>preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=327-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वचापत्र|त्वचापत्रं
त्वचापत्र n. (-त्रं) Woody cassia.<BR> E. त्वचा bark, and पत्र a leaf; also त्वक्पत्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=327-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वचिष्ठ|त्वचिष्ठः
त्वचिष्ठ mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठा-ष्ठं) Having abundant skin or bark. त्वच्, skin, इष्ठन्<BR>affix of the superlative; also with ईयसुन् and त्वचीयस् mfn. (-यान्-<BR>यसी-यः) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=327-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वचिसार|त्वचिसारः
त्वचिसार m. (-रः) A bamboo.<BR> E. त्वचि seventh case of त्वच् the bark, and<BR>सार strength, pith; also त्वक्सार ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=327-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वचिसुगन्धा
त्वचिसुगन्धा f. (-न्धा) Small cardamoms.<BR> E. त्वचि in the bark, सुगन्ध fragrance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=327-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वञ्च
त्वञ्च (उ) तञ्चु r. 1st cl. (त्वञ्चति) To go, move.<BR> E. भ्वा-पर-सक-सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=327-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वत्
त्वत् mfn. (त्वत्) Other, different: see त्व.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=327-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वत्क
त्वत्क mfn. (-त्कः-त्का-त्कं) Thine, your.<BR> E. त्वत् thine, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=327-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वदीय|त्वदीयं
त्वदीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Thine.<BR> E. त्वत् from त्वं thou, and ईय added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=327-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वर
त्वर (ञि आ) ञित्वरा r. 1st cl. (त्वरते) To hurry, to make haste, to go or<BR>move with speed, to do any thing readily or precipitately. भ्वा-आ-<BR>अक-सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=328-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वरण|त्वरणं
त्वरण n. (-णं) Making haste, speed, velocity.<BR> E. त्वर् to haste, and ल्युट्. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=328-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वरमाण
त्वरमाण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Hastening, making haste, going speedily. E.<BR>त्वर् to be quick, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=328-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वरा
त्वरा f. (-रा) Haste, speed.<BR> E. त्वर् to make haste, affixes अ and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=328-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वरान्वित
त्वरान्वित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Swift, quick.<BR> E. त्वरा haste, and अन्वित possess-<BR>ed of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=328-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वरायण
त्वरायण mfn. subst. (-णः-णा-णं) Adherence, attachment.<BR> E. त्वर to go, with<BR>speed, and युच् affix: see तुरायण ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=328-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वरायुक्त
त्वरायुक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं) Quick, expeditious.<BR> E. त्वरा, and युक्त having.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=328-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वरि|त्वरिः
त्वरि f. (-रिः) Haste, speed.<BR> E. त्वर् to make haste, affix इन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=328-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वरित|त्वरितं
त्वरित mfn. subst. (-तः-ता-तं) Quick, swift, expeditious.<BR>	 n. (-तं) Dispatch,<BR>haste. adv. Quickly, swiftly.<BR> E. त्वर् to make haste, affix क्त, and इट्<BR>inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=328-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वरितगति
त्वरितगति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Swift motion.<BR>	 2. A species of the Pankti metre. E.<BR>त्वरित, गति going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=328-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वरितोदित|त्वरितोदितं
त्वरितोदित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Spoken fast, hurried.<BR> E. त्वरित quickly, उदित<BR>said.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=328-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वष्ट|त्वष्टः
त्वष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं) Pared, made thin.<BR> E. त्वक्ष् to make thin, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=328-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वष्टि|त्वष्टिः
त्वष्टि f. (-ष्टिः) Carpentry.<BR> E. त्वक्ष् to plane, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=328-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वष्टृ
त्वष्टृ m. (-ष्टा)<BR>	 1. A carpenter.<BR>	 2. A name of VISWAKARMA, the artist of<BR>the gods.<BR> E. त्वक्ष् to pare, affix तृच्. The sun.<BR> E. तिष् to shine,<BR>Uṇādi affix तृच् and अ substituted for the radical इ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=328-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वाच
त्वाच mfn. (-चः-ची-चं)<BR>	 1. Cuticular, relating to the skin.<BR>	 2. Contagious,<BR>derived from touch.<BR> E. त्वच्, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=328-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वाचप्रत्यक्ष|त्वाचप्रत्यक्षं
त्वाचप्रत्यक्ष n. (-क्षं) Ascertainment of objects by contact.<BR> E. त्वाच, and प्रत्यक्ष<BR>perception.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=328-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वाष्ट्र|त्वाष्ट्रः
त्वाष्ट्र m. (-ष्ट्रः) The name of a demon, also called VRITRASURA.<BR>	 nf. (-ष्ट्रं-ष्ट्री)<BR>One of the lunar mansions, the fourteenth or Chitra.<BR>	 f. (-ष्ट्री)<BR>	 1. A<BR>wife of SŪRYA, or the sun; also called SANJNA, the daughter of<BR>VISWAKARMA.<BR>	 2. A small car.<BR> E. त्वष्टृ the sun, or a carpenter, अण्<BR>affix of relation or descent, and ङीप् fem. aff. त्वष्टा देवता अस्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=328-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्विष
त्विष r. 1st cl. (औ) औत्विष (त्विषति-ते) To shine. With अव prefixed, 1. To<BR>give.<BR>	 2. To dwell. भ्वा-उभ-अक-अनिट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=328-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्विष्
त्विष् f. (-त्विट्)<BR>	 1. Light.<BR>	 2. Splendour, beauty.<BR>	 3. Speech.<BR>	 4. Wish,<BR>desire.<BR>	 5. Custom, practice, usage.<BR> E. त्विष् to shine, affix क्विप्; also<BR>with टाप् added त्विषा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=328-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्विषा
त्विषा f. (-षा) Light: see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=328-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्विषाम्पति|त्विषांपति|त्विषाम्पतिः
त्विषाम्पति m. (-तिः) The sun.<BR> E. त्विषां gen. plu. of त्विष् light, and पति<BR>master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=328-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्विषि|त्विषिः
त्विषि m. (-षिः) A ray of light.<BR> E. त्विष् to shine, इन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=328-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्सर
त्सर r. 1st cl. (त्सरति) To proceed fraudulently or crookedly. भ्वा-पर-<BR>सक-सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=328-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्सरु|त्सरुः
त्सरु m. (-रुः) The hilt or handle of a sword, &c.<BR> E. त्सर् to go, Uṇādi<BR>affix उन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=328-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

थ|थं|थः
थ The seventeenth consonant of the Deva Nagri alphabet, and second<BR>of the dental class; the aspirate of the preceding letter, and express-<BR>ed by Th.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=328-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

थ|थं|थः
थ n. (थं)<BR>	 1. Auspiciousness.<BR>	 2. Fear, terror, 3. Preserving, preservation.<BR>m. (थः)<BR>	 1. A mountain.<BR>	 2. Eating.<BR>	 3. A disease.<BR> E. स्था to stand,<BR>affix ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=328-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

थुड
थुड r. 6th cl. (थुडति) To cover, to screen, to clothe or hide. तुदा-पर-<BR>सक-सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=328-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

थुत्कार|थुत्कारः
थुत्कार m. (-रः) The sound made in spitting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=328-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

थुथु
थुथु ind. Imitative sound of spitting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=328-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

थुध
थुध r. 4th cl. (थुध्यति-ते) To become pure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=328-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

थुर्व|थुर्व्व
थुर्व (ई) थुर्वी r. 1st cl. (थुर्वति) To kill, to injure or hurt. भ्वा-पर-सक-<BR>सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=328-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

थोडन|थोडनं
थोडन n. (-नं) Covering, clothing, wrapping up.<BR> E. थुड्, and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=328-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द|दं|दः
द The third letter of the dental class, and eighteenth consonant in<BR>the Deva Nagari alphabet, corresponding to the letter D.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=328-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द|दं|दः
द n. (-दं) A wife.<BR>	 nf. (दंदा)<BR>	 1. Gift, donation.<BR>	 2. Dividing, cutting,<BR>breaking, &c.<BR>	 f. (दा)<BR>	 1. Purifying, cleansing.<BR>	 2. Preserving, cherish-<BR>ing.<BR>	 3. Repentance.<BR>	 m. (दः)<BR>	 1. A donor, a giver.<BR>	 2. A mountain.<BR>3. A gift, a thing given.<BR> E. दा to give, or दो to cut, &c. affix ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=328-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंश|दंशः
दंश r. 1st cl. (दंशति) To bite, to sting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=328-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंश|दंशः
दंश m. (-शः)<BR>	 1. A gadfly.<BR>	 2. A tooth.<BR>	 3. Biting, stinging.<BR>	 4. Armour,<BR>mail.<BR>	 5. Cutting, dividing, tearing.<BR>	 6. Fault, defect.<BR>	 7. A joint, a<BR>limb.<BR>	 8. The sting of a snake.<BR>	 9. Pungency.<BR>	 f. (-शी) A small gadfly.<BR>E. दंश् to bite or sting, affix अच्, diminutive affix ङीष् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=328-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंशक|दंशकः
दंशक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) What bites or stings.<BR>	 m. (-कः) A gadfly.<BR> E. दंश-<BR>ण्वुल् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=328-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंशन|दंशनं
दंशन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Biting, stinging.<BR>	 2. Armour, mail.<BR> E. दंश् to bite, &c.<BR>भावे ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=328-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंशभीरु|दंशभीरुः
दंशभीरु m. (-रुः) A buffalo.<BR> E. दंश a gadfly, and भीरु afraid of; also with<BR>कन् added, दंशभीरुक m. (-कः) दंशात् भीरुः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=328-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंशमूल|दंशमूलः
दंशमूल m. (-लः) A plant, (Hyperanthera morunga.)<BR> E. दंश biting, and<BR>मूल a root; the root of this plant is substituted in Bengal for<BR>horseradish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=328-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंशित|दंशितः
दंशित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Armed, mailed.<BR>	 2. Bitten, stung.<BR> E. दंश armour,<BR>and इतच् affix, or दंश to bite, affix इतच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=328-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंशेर
दंशेर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Mischievous, noxious.<BR> E. दंश् to bite or sting,<BR>Uṇādi affix एरच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=328-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंष्ट्रा
दंष्ट्रा f. (-ष्ट्रा) A large tooth, a tusk.<BR> E. दंश् to bite, affix ष्ट्रन्, and टाप् fem.<BR>aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=328-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंष्ट्रिका
दंष्ट्रिका f. (-का) The beard.<BR> E. दंष्ट्रा a tooth, इकन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=328-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंष्ट्रिन्
दंष्ट्रिन् mfn. (-ष्ट्री-ष्ट्रिणी-ष्ट्रि)<BR>	 1. Biting or wounding with the teeth, (any<BR>animal, &c.)<BR>	 2. Tusked, having tusks or sharp teeth.<BR>	 3. Carnivo-<BR>rous.<BR>	 m. (-ष्ट्री)<BR>	 1. A hog.<BR>	 2. A snake.<BR> E. दंष्ट्रा a tooth, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=328-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंसन|दंसनं
दंसन n. (-नं) Armour, mail: see दंशन ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=328-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक|दकं
दक n. (-कं) Water. E. See उदक, the initial vowel being dropped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=328-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्ष|दक्षः
दक्ष r. 1st cl. (दक्षते)<BR>	 1. To grow or increase.<BR>	 2. To dispatch, to expedite,<BR>to do quickly.<BR>	 3. To go, to move.<BR>	 4. To hurt or kill. भ्वा-आ-अक-सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=328-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्ष|दक्षः
दक्ष mfn. (-क्षः-क्षा-क्षं) Clever, able, dexterous.<BR>	 m. (-क्षः)<BR>	 1. A Bramhadika;<BR>according to one legend, son of BRAMHA, born from the thumb of<BR>his right hand, for the purpose of peopling the world: according<BR>to another, he is the son of the Munis, called Prachetasas. DAKṢA,<BR>had sixty daughters, of whom twenty-seven are the nymphs who<BR>form the lunar asterisms, and wives of the Moon; one of his<BR>daughters also SATI or DURGĀ, the wife of ŚIVA; and seventeen<BR>were married to KAŚYAPA, and were the mothers of all created<BR>beings. DAKṢA was on one occasion decapitated by ŚIVA: see<BR>दक्षाध्वरध्वंसकृत्; he is sometimes regarded as an Avatara of Bramha<BR>himself.<BR>	 2. A Muni and legislator, who flourished in the beginning<BR>of the Treta Yuga.<BR>	 3. A kind of tree.<BR>	 4. The bull of ŚIVA.<BR>	 5. A<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=329-a" target="_blank">Page329-a+ 60</a>]<BR>cock.<BR>	 6. A scholar, a Pandit.<BR>	 7. A dexterous or clever man.<BR>	 8. ŚIVA.<BR>9. A name of Agni or fire.<BR>	 10. A general lover, one attached to<BR>many mistresses.<BR>	 f. (-क्षा) The earth.<BR> E. दक्ष् to grow or increase,<BR>affix कर्त्तरि अच ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=328-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षकन्या
दक्षकन्या f. (-न्या)<BR>	 1. A name of DURGĀ.<BR>	 2. Any lunar mansion.<BR> E. दक्ष,<BR>and कन्या the maiden, the daughter of DAKṢA, who in this case<BR>seems to be identified with Himālaya, the snowy mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=329-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षजा
दक्षजा f. (-जा)<BR>	 1. The goddes DURGĀ.<BR>	 2. A lunar asterism.<BR> E. दक्ष, and<BR>जा born: see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=329-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षजापति|दक्षजापतिः
दक्षजापति m. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. The moon.<BR>	 2. The deity ŚIVA.<BR> E. दक्षजा a lunar<BR>asterism or DURGĀ, and पति husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=329-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षता
दक्षता f. (-ता) Dexterity, cleverness.<BR> E. तल् added to दक्ष; also with<BR>त्व, दक्षत्वम् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=329-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षयज्ञ
दक्षयज्ञ m. (-ज्ञः) The sacrifice made by DAKṢA.<BR> E. दक्ष, and यज्ञ sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=329-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षयज्ञविनाशिनी
दक्षयज्ञविनाशिनी f. (-नी) DURGĀ.<BR> E. दक्षयज्ञ, and विनाशिनी destructress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=329-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षसावर्णि|दक्षसावर्णिः
दक्षसावर्णि m. (-र्णिः) The ninth Manu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=329-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षाध्वरध्वंसकृत्
दक्षाध्वरध्वंसकृत् m. (-कृत्) A name of ŚIVA.<BR> E. दक्ष the Bramhadika, as<BR>DAKṢA, अध्वर a sacrifice, ध्वंसकृत् subduer or disturber: DAKṢA<BR>having on one occasion made a sacrifice, to which he invited all<BR>the gods, except his son-in-law ŚIVA, and his wife SATI, the latter<BR>went unbid, and being received coolly, threw herself into the fire;<BR>This being informed siva, tore off a lock of his hair and cast it vio-<BR>lently on the ground. It started up into being a demon named<BR>Birbhadra who being ordered by siva proceeded against DAKṢA,<BR>and an affray ensued, in which the gods and Ṛṣis were maltreated<BR>and dispersed, and DAKṢA decapitated; he was restored to life,<BR>and the head of a ram substituted for the one he had lost.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=329-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षाय्य|दक्षाय्यः
दक्षाय्य m. (-य्यः)<BR>	 1. The bird of VIṢṆU, Garuḍa.<BR>	 2. A vulture.<BR> E. दक्ष् to<BR>hurt, आय्य Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=329-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिण|दक्षिणः
दक्षिण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>	 1. Candid, sincere, honest, upright.<BR>	 2. Right,<BR>(not left.)<BR>	 3. South, southern.<BR>	 4. Dependent, subject.<BR>	 5. Clever,<BR>able, dexterous.<BR>	 f. (-णा)<BR>	 1. A present to Brahmans, upon solemn<BR>or sacrificial occasions.<BR>	 2. The south.<BR>	 3. Completion of any rite,<BR>fixing or establishing any act or place.<BR>	 4. A form or figure of<BR>DURGĀ, in which the right side is said to be advanced.<BR>	 5. Dona-<BR>tion to Brahmans, personified as a goddess, said to be born from<BR>KṚṢṆA'S right side.<BR> E. दक्ष् to prosper, &c. Uṇādi affix इनन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=329-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणकालिका
दक्षिणकालिका f. (-का) A form of DURGĀ worshiped by the Tantrikas.<BR>E. दक्षिण, and कालिका a form of the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=329-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणतस्
दक्षिणतस् ind. Southward, southerly.<BR> E. तसि added to दक्षिण ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=329-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणापथ|दक्षिणापथः
दक्षिणापथ n. (-थं)<BR>	 1. The south.<BR>	 2. Southern road or course.<BR>	 3. Deccan. E.<BR>दक्षिण, and पथ for पथिन् path.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=329-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणपूर्वा|दक्षिणपूर्व्वा
दक्षिणपूर्वा f. (-र्वा) The south-east quarter.<BR> E. दक्षिण south and पूर्व east.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=329-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणस्थ|दक्षिणस्थः
दक्षिणस्थ mfn. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थं) Upon the right side, to the south, &c.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-स्थः) A charioteer.<BR> E. दक्षिण as above, and स्थ who stays or abides.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=329-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणाग्नि|दक्षिणाग्निः
दक्षिणाग्नि m. (-ग्निः) One kind of sacred fire. that which is taken from<BR>the domestic or consecrated fire, and is placed to the south.<BR>E. दक्षिण south, and अग्नि fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=329-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणाग्र
दक्षिणाग्र mfn. (-ग्रः-ग्रा-ग्रं) Pointing to the south, having the head or top<BR>to the south.<BR> E. दक्षिण, and अग्र end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=329-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणाचल|दक्षिणाचलः
दक्षिणाचल m. (-लः) The Malaya mountain.<BR> E. दक्षिण south, and अचल mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=329-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणाचार|दक्षिणाचारः
दक्षिणाचार m. (-रः) A worshipper of Śakti according to the purer or<BR>right-hand ritual.<BR> E. दक्षिण, and आचार observance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=329-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणात्
दक्षिणात् ind. Southward. E. The fifth case of दक्षिण, used as a participle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=329-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणात्यय|दक्षिणात्ययः
दक्षिणात्यय m. (-यः) A southern, or an inhabitant of South.<BR> E. दक्षिण,<BR>अत्यय who goes to or beyond.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=329-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणापथ|दक्षिणापथः
दक्षिणापथ m. (-थः) The south, the southern direction or quarter.<BR> E. दक्षिणा, and पथ for पथिन् path.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=329-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणापथजन्मन्
दक्षिणापथजन्मन् m. (-न्मा) A southern, or the Andhakas, Guhas, Pulin-<BR>das, Savaras, Chuchukas, and Madrapas, all outcaste or barbar-<BR>ous tribes.<BR> E. दक्षिणापथ, and जन्मन् birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=329-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणाप्रवण
दक्षिणाप्रवण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Declining, shelving or inclining to the<BR>south.<BR> E. दक्षिणा, and प्रवण declivity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=329-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणामुख|दक्षिणामुखः
दक्षिणामुख mfn. (-खः-खी-खं) Turning the face southwards.<BR> E. दक्षिण<BR>south, and मुख the face, with आङ् prefixed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=329-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणायन|दक्षिणायनं
दक्षिणायन n. (-नं) The suns progress towards the south of the equator,<BR>the winter solstice.<BR> E. दक्षिण, and अयन going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=329-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणारण्य
दक्षिणारण्य n. (-ण्यं) The peninsula, the great southern forest.<BR> E. दक्षिण,<BR>and अरण्य a wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=329-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणार्ह|दक्षिणार्हः
दक्षिणार्ह mfn. (-र्हः-र्हा-र्हं) Meriting a reward.<BR> E. दक्षिण a present, and अर्ह fit for.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=329-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणावर्त्त|दक्षिणावर्त|दक्षिणावर्तः
दक्षिणावर्त्त m. (-र्त्तः)<BR>	 1. A conch-shell with the valve opening to the right.<BR>2. Curved to the right.<BR>	 3. Turned towards the south.<BR> E. दक्षिण, and<BR>आवर्त्त a turn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=329-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणावर्त्तकी|दक्षिणावर्तकी
दक्षिणावर्त्तकी f. (-की) A line of bees.<BR> E. दक्षिण, and आवर्त्तक turning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=329-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणाशा
दक्षिणाशा f. (-शा) The south.<BR> E. दक्षिण, and आशा quarter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=329-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणाशापति|दक्षिणाशापतिः
दक्षिणाशापति m. (-तिः) A name of YAMA.<BR> E. दक्षिण south, आशा quarter,<BR>and पति master or regent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=329-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणीय|दक्षिणीयः
दक्षिणीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Meriting a reward.<BR> E. दक्षिण a present or reward, affix छ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=329-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणेन
दक्षिणेन ind. Southward, southerly. E. The third case of दक्षिण, used as<BR>a participle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=329-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणेर्म्मन्|दक्षिणेर्मन्
दक्षिणेर्म्मन् m. (-र्म्मा) A deer struck by a hunter.<BR> E. दक्षिण the right side,<BR>and इर्म्म wound, comp. irr. दक्षिणे ईर्मं व्रणं यस्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=329-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिण्य|दक्षिण्यः
दक्षिण्य mfn. (-ण्यः-ण्या-ण्यं) Meriting a reward.<BR> E. दक्षिण a present, and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=329-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दग्ध|दग्धं|दग्धः
दग्ध mfn. (-ग्धः-ग्धा-ग्धं)<BR>	 1. Burnt, scorched, consumed by fire.<BR>	 2. Tasteless.<BR>3. A term of abuse usually prefixed to the word it vilifies.<BR>	 f. (-ग्धा)<BR>1. The quarter where the sun is observable.<BR>	 2. An epithet of certain<BR>lunations, on which it is unlucky to do any thing, and religious<BR>rites are prohibited.<BR>	 n. (-ग्धं) A fragrant grass.<BR> E. दह् to burn,<BR>affix क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=329-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दग्धकाक|दग्धकाकः
दग्धकाक m. (-कः) A raven, or perhaps the carrion crow.<BR> E. दग्ध burnt,<BR>(black,) and काक crow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=329-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दग्धव्य
दग्धव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं) To be burnt.<BR> E. दह् to burn, तव्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=329-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दग्धिका
दग्धिका f. (-का) Scorched rice.<BR> E. दग्ध burnt, कन् depreciative affix, and<BR>the fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=329-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दग्धेष्टका
दग्धेष्टका f. (-का) A burnt or vitrified brick.<BR> E. दग्ध burnt, and इष्टक a brick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=329-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दग्धोदर
दग्धोदर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Hungry, starving.<BR>	 n. (-रं) The appetite, an empty<BR>or craving stomach.<BR> E. दग्ध, and उदर the belly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=329-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दग्ध्वा
दग्ध्वा ind. Having burnt.<BR> E. दह् to burn, क्त्वा aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=329-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दघ
दघ r. 1st cl. (इ) दघि (दंघति) 1. To quit or abandon.<BR>	 2. To cherish or<BR>protect. r. 5th cl. (दघ्नोति)<BR>	 1. To hurt or kill.<BR>	 2. To protect: some<BR>consider this root peculiar to the Vedas. भ्वा० प० सक० सेट् इदित् ।<BR>घातनार्थे स्वा० प० सक० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=329-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दध्न|दध्नः
दध्न f. (-ध्नी) A termination affixed to nouns to denote “reaching to” &c. “As high as.”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=329-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्ड|दंड|दंडं|दंडः|दण्डः
दण्ड r. 10th cl. (दण्डयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To punish, especially by fine.<BR>	 2. To fine,<BR>to amerce. चुरा० उभ० सक० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=329-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्ड|दंड|दंडं|दंडः|दण्डः
दण्ड mn. (-ण्डः-ण्डं) A stick, a staff.<BR>	 m. (-ण्डः)<BR>	 1. Punishment, castiga-<BR>tion, amercement, imprisonment or putting to death.<BR>	 2. A name<BR>of Yama, regent of the dead.<BR>	 3. An army.<BR>	 4. A form of array, a<BR>line or column of troops.<BR>	 5. A long measure, a pole of four<BR>cubits.<BR>	 6. A churning stick.<BR>	 7. A corner, an angle.<BR>	 8. A horse.<BR>	 9. A<BR>companion or attendant of the sun.<BR>	 10. A stem or stick of a<BR>tree.<BR>	 11. Subduing, subjecting.<BR>	 12. Pride, arrogance.<BR>	 13. A measure<BR>of time, a Danda, (1/60)th part of the day and night, or twenty-<BR>four minutes.<BR>	 14. Standing upright or erect, being like a staff.<BR>15. A son of IKSHWAKU.<BR> E. दम् to tame, and ड Uṇādi aff. or दण्ड to<BR>punish, affix अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=329-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्डक|दंडक|दंडकः|दण्डकः
दण्डक mn. (-कः-कं) A sort of metre, the stanza of which exceeds<BR>twenty-seven syllables, and may extend to 200.<BR>	 f. (-का) The penin-<BR>sula of India, from between the Narmada and Godaveri rivers to<BR>the south, the whole of which, in the days of RAMA, was a large<BR>forest.<BR> E. दण्ड a staff, &c. and स्वार्थे क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=329-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्डकारण्य
दण्डकारण्य n. (-ण्यं) The peninsula, the peninsular forest: see the last. E.<BR>दण्डक, and अरण्य a wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=330-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्डग्रहण|दंडग्रहण
दण्डग्रहण n. (-णं) Becoming a mendicant or ascetic.<BR> E. दण्ड the staff<BR>carried by the mendicant, and ग्रहण taking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=330-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्डघ्न
दण्डघ्न m. (-घ्नः) A fighter, one who commits personal violence.<BR> E. दण्ड a<BR>stick, and घ्न who strikes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=330-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्डजित
दण्डजित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Suppressed by punishment.<BR> E. दण्ड, and जित<BR>conquered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=330-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्डढक्का|दंडढक्का
दण्डढक्का f. (-क्का) A kettle drum.<BR> E. दण्ड a stick, and ढक्का a drum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=330-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्डताम्री
दण्डताम्री f. (-म्री) A perforated copper vessel, of given capacity, placed<BR>in a vessel of water; when filled with water, it sinks, marking a<BR>certain portion of time.<BR> E. दण्ड twenty-four minutes, and ताम्री<BR>(q. v.) a copper vessel, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=330-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्डदास|दंडदास|दण्डदासः
दण्डदास m. (-सः) A slave, a bondsman, one who has become so as a<BR>punishment or for debt.<BR> E. दण्ड, and दास a slave.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=330-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्डधर|दंडधर|दण्डधरः
दण्डधर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>	 1. Having a stick or staff.<BR>	 2. Having authority<BR>to punish.<BR>	 m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A name of YAMA.<BR>	 2. A king.<BR>	 3. A potter.<BR>4. A mendicant carrying a staff.<BR> E. दण्ड punishment, a stick, &c.<BR>and धर who holds or possesses; also दण्डधार m. (-रः) दण्डधारिन्,<BR>&c. दण्डं लगुडं वा धरति धर-अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=330-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्डधारण
दण्डधारण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Punishment.<BR>	 2. Carrying a staff.<BR>	 3. Following<BR>the order of a mendicant.<BR> E. दण्ड, and धारण having.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=330-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्डन|दंडन|दंडनं
दण्डन n. (-नं) Punishing, inflicting punishment.<BR> E. दण्ड to tame, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=330-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्डनायक|दंडनायक|दण्डनायकः
दण्डनायक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. General, a commander-in-chief.<BR>	 2. A magistrate, a<BR>head police officer.<BR> E. दण्ड a column of troops, and नायक a leader.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=330-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्डनीति|दंडनीति|दण्डनीतिः
दण्डनीति f. (-तिः) Polity, the system of civil and military administration<BR>taught by CHANAKYA and others.<BR> E. दण्ड (by) punishment or sub-<BR>jection, नी to get or obtain, and क्तिच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=330-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्डनीय|दंडनीय
दण्डनीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Punishable, deserving punishment.<BR> E. दण्ड to<BR>punish, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=330-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्डनीयत्व
दण्डनीयत्व n. (-त्वं) Demerit, desert of punishment.<BR> E. त्व added to the<BR>last; also with तल्, दण्डनीयता ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=330-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्डपांशुल|दंडपांशुल|दण्डपांशुलः
दण्डपांशुल m. (-लः) A porter, a warder or doorkeeper.<BR> E. दण्ड a staff, पा<BR>to cherish or bear, affix ड, दण्डपः again, अंशुल for अंशल strong,<BR>sturdy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=330-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्डपाणि|दंडपाणि|दण्डपाणिः
दण्डपाणि m. (-णिः)<BR>	 1. YAMA.<BR>	 2. A staff-bearer.<BR>	 3. One of ŚIVA'S atten-<BR>dants worshipped at Benares.<BR> E. दण्ड, and पाणि a hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=330-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्डपातिन्
दण्डपातिन् mfn. (-ती-तिनी-ति) Awarding punishment, fining.<BR> E. दण्ड,<BR>punishment and पातिन् causing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=330-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्डपारुष्य|दंडपारुष्य|दण्डपारुष्यं
दण्डपारुष्य n. (-ष्यं)<BR>	 1. Assault and battery, a title of jurisprudence.<BR>	 2.<BR>Infliction of cruel punishment, one of the seven vices of kings and<BR>rulers.<BR> E. दण्ड punishment, पारुष्य severity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=330-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्डपाल|दंडपाल|दण्डपालः
दण्डपाल m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. A doorkeeper, a porter.<BR>	 2. A small kind of fish,<BR>(Cyprinus danrica, HAM.) See अर्द्धसफर.<BR> E. दण्ड a staff, &c. and पाल<BR>who cherishes. दण्डं देहं पालयति भक्षणात् पालि-अण् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=330-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्डपालक|दंडपालक|दण्डपालकः
दण्डपालक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A sort of fish: see the preceding, which it is<BR>supposed to resemble.<BR>	 2. A doorkeeper.<BR> E. कन् implying likeness,<BR>or pleonastic added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=330-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्डपाशिक|दण्डपाशिकः
दण्डपाशिक m. (-कः) A hangman, an executioner.<BR> E. दण्ड, and पाश a<BR>noose, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=330-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्डप्रणयन
दण्डप्रणयन n. (-नं) Inflicting punishment.<BR> E. दण्ड, and प्रणयन leading.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=330-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्डभीति
दण्डभीति f. (-तिः) Fear of punishment.<BR> E. दण्ड, and भीति fear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=330-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्डभृत्|दंडभृत्
दण्डभृत् mfn. (-भृत्)<BR>	 1. Having a staff or stick.<BR>	 2. Inflicting punishment.<BR>m. (-भृत्)<BR>	 1. A potter.<BR>	 2. An epithet of Yama.<BR> E. दण्ड the stick or<BR>handle of his wheel, and भृत् who possesses or works with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=330-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्डमानव|दण्डमानवः
दण्डमानव m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. An ascetic, one who used a staff.<BR>	 2. A leader. E.<BR>दण्ड, and मानव a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=330-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्डयत्
दण्डयत् mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्) Punishing, amercing, chastising.<BR> E. दण्ड to<BR>punish, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=330-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्डयात्रा|दंडयात्रा
दण्डयात्रा f. (-त्रा)<BR>	 1. Subjection or conquest of a region or quarter.<BR>	 2. A<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=330-b" target="_blank">Page330-b+ 60</a>]<BR>bridal procession.<BR>	 3. Procession, moving in state or with attend-<BR>ants.<BR> E. दण्ड punishment, &c. and यात्रा going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=330-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्डयाम|दंडयाम|दण्डयामः
दण्डयाम m. (-मः)<BR>	 1. A name of YAMA.<BR>	 2. The saint AGASTYA.<BR>	 3. A<BR>day.<BR> E. दण्ड punishment, &c. यम् to refrain, in the causal form, and<BR>घञ् aff. दण्डेन यच्छति यम वा कर्त्तरि यम घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=330-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्डयोग
दण्डयोग n. (-गं) Infliction of punishment.<BR> E. दण्ड, and योग application.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=330-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्डलेश
दण्डलेश n. (-शं) A small fine.<BR> E. दण्ड, and लेश a little.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=330-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्डवत्|दंडवत्|दण्डवन्त्
दण्डवत् ind. Prostrate, falling or lying prostrate.<BR> E. दण्ड a stick, and<BR>वति aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=330-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्डवत्|दंडवत्|दण्डवन्त्
दण्डवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Having a stick, carrying a staff.<BR> E. दण्ड, and<BR>मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=330-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्डवादिन्|दंडवादिन्
दण्डवादिन् m. (-दी)<BR>	 1. A doorkeeper or a warder.<BR>	 2. One who threatens<BR>another with punishment or castigation.<BR> E. दण्ड castigation, and<BR>वद् to speak, to threaten, affix णिनि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=330-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्डवालधि
दण्डवालधि m. (-धिः) An elephant.<BR> E. दण्ड a stick, and वालधि a tail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=330-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्डवासिन्|दंडवासिन्
दण्डवासिन् m. (-सी)<BR>	 1. A doorkeeper, a warder, a chamberlain.<BR>	 2.<BR>The magistrate or the head of a village.<BR> E. दण्ड a staff or mace, or<BR>punishment, &c. वस् to abide, affix णिनि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=330-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्डविकल्प|दण्डविकल्पः
दण्डविकल्प m. (-ल्पः) Appropriate punishment or sentence.<BR> E. दण्ड, and<BR>विकल्प alternative.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=330-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्डविधि|दंडविधि|दण्डविधिः
दण्डविधि f. (-धिः) Criminal law, mode of punishment.<BR> E. दण्ड, and विधि<BR>rule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=330-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्डविशेष
दण्डविशेष m. (-षः) Kind or degree of punishment.<BR> E. दण्ड, and विशेष sort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=330-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्डविष्कम्भ|दंडविष्कंभ|दण्डविष्कम्भः
दण्डविष्कम्भ m. (-म्भः) A post or stake, round which plays the string that<BR>works the churning stick.<BR> E. दण्ड a stick, स्कम्भ to stop, with वि pre-<BR>fixed, and अण् aff. दण्डं मन्थानदण्डं विष्कभ्राति । (घोलमयार खुंँटि) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=330-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्डहस्त|दंडहस्त|दण्डहस्तं|दण्डहस्तः
दण्डहस्त m. (-स्तः)<BR>	 1. A staff-bearer.<BR>	 2. A doorkeeper.<BR>	 n. (-स्तं) A tree,<BR>(Tabernæmontana coronaria.)<BR> E. दण्ड, and हस्त the hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=330-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्डाजिन|दंडाजिन|दण्डाजिनं
दण्डाजिन n. (-नं) Deceit, fraud, cheating, roguery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=330-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्डादण्डि|दंडादंडि
दण्डादण्डि ind. Single stick, cudgelling, fighting with sticks or staves.<BR>E. दण्ड a stick, repeated, with आ inserted, and इच् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=330-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्डार|दंडार|दंडारः|दण्डारः
दण्डार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A carriage, a vehicle.<BR>	 2. A potter's wheel.<BR>	 3. A bow<BR>or any instrument for casting arrows or darts.<BR>	 4. An elephant in<BR>rut, a furious or intoxicated elephant.<BR> E. दण्ड a stick, ऋ to go, and<BR>अण् aff. दण्डं ऋच्छति ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=330-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्डाहत|दंडाहत|दण्डाहतं
दण्डाहत m. (-तः) Buttermilk.<BR> E. दण्ड a churning stick, and आहत struck,<BR>churned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=330-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्डिक|दंडिक|दंडिकः|दण्डिकः
दण्डिक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A mace-bearer, &c. one carrying a stick or staff.<BR>	 2.<BR>A fish, (Cyprinus dankena, HAM.)<BR> E. दण्ड a staff, and ठन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=330-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्डिका|दंडिका
दण्डिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. A kind of necklace.<BR>	 2. A string.<BR> E. दण्ड a measure,<BR>and इकन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=330-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्डित|दंडित|दण्डितः
दण्डित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Punished, chastised, sentenced, fined.<BR> E. दण्ड to<BR>punish, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=330-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्डिन्|दंडिन्
दण्डिन् mfn. (-ण्डी-ण्डिनी-ण्डि) Having a staff or stick.<BR>	 m. (-ण्डी)<BR>	 1. A door-<BR>keeper, a warder, a porter, a staff or mace-bearer.<BR>	 2. A name of<BR>YAMA.<BR>	 3. A man of the fourth order or beggar.<BR>	 4. A mendicant<BR>carrying a staff.<BR>	 5. A mendicant of a particular order, derived from<BR>SANKARACHARYA.<BR>	 6. A Jina or Jaina saint.<BR> E. दण्ड a staff, &c. and<BR>इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=330-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्डोत्पला
दण्डोत्पला f. (-ला) A small shrub; also सहदेवा । मत्स्यभेदे च ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=330-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्ड्य|दंड्य|दण्ड्यः
दण्ड्य mfn. (-ण्ड्यः-ण्ड्या-ण्ड्यं) Punishable, deserving punishment.<BR> E. दण्ड<BR>punishment, and कर्मणि यत् affix implying fitness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=330-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दत्|दन्त्
दत् m. (-दन्तः-दन्तौ-दन्तः) 2nd case plu. (दतः) A tooth: see दन्त; the nasal<BR>is dropped after the 2nd case.<BR> E. दम् to subdue, affix डत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=330-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दत्त|दत्तं|दत्तः
दत्त mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं)<BR>	 1. Given, presented, made over, assigned.<BR>	 2.<BR>Preserved, guarded, protected.<BR>	 m. (-त्तः)<BR>	 1. The name of a king.<BR>	 2.<BR>A saint; also दत्तात्रेय.<BR>	 3. A common surname or title of a man of<BR>the Vaiśya or third tribe, at present common to the Kayeth<BR>class.<BR>	 n. (-त्तं) A gift, a donation.<BR> E. दा to give, affix कर्मणि क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=330-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दत्तक|दत्तकः
दत्तक m. (-कः) A son given: see the next.<BR> E. कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=330-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दत्तकपुत्त्र
दत्तकपुत्त्र m. (-त्त्रः) A son given away by his natural parents, to persons<BR>engaging to adopt him; one of the twelve heirs acknowledged by<BR>the old Hindu law.<BR> E. दत्तक, and पुत्त्र a son; also simply दत्तक, and<BR>sometimes दत्त्रिम.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=331-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दत्तवत्|दत्तवन्त्
दत्तवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Gave, was giving.<BR> E. दा to give, क्तवतु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=331-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दत्तशुल्का
दत्तशुल्का f. (-ल्का) A bride for whom a sum of money has been paid to<BR>her father.<BR> E. दत्त, and शुल्क dower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=331-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दत्तात्मन्
दत्तात्मन् mfn. (-त्मा-त्मा-त्म) Self-given.<BR>	 m. (-त्मा) A youth or orphan, who<BR>gives himself to persons disposed to take the place of parents. E.<BR>दत्त given, and आत्मन् self.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=331-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दत्तात्रेय|दत्तात्रेयः
दत्तात्रेय m. (-यः) A sage, the son of ATRI given to him by three deities<BR>BRAMHA, VIṢṆU and ŚIVA.<BR> E. दत्त, and आत्रेय son of ATRI: also<BR>दत्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=331-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दत्तादत्त
दत्तादत्त mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं) Given and received.<BR> E. दत्त, and आदत्त taken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=331-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दत्तादर
दत्तादर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Treated with respect.<BR> E. दत्त, and आदर respect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=331-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दत्तानपकर्म्मन्|दत्तानपकर्मन्
दत्तानपकर्म्मन् n. (-र्म्म) Nonresumption of gifts.<BR> E. दत्त a gift, अन for अ neg.<BR>before अपकर्म्मन् resuming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=331-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दत्तापहृत
दत्तापहृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Given and taken again.<BR> E. दत्त, and अपहृत taken<BR>back.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=331-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दत्ताप्रदानिक|दत्ताप्रदानिकं
दत्ताप्रदानिक n. (-कं) Resumption of gifts; one of the eighteen titles of<BR>law.<BR> E. दत्त, and अप्रदानिक not giving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=331-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दत्तावधान
दत्तावधान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Attentive.<BR> E. दत्त and अवधान attention.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=331-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दत्तासन
दत्तासन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Having a seat given, requested to sit.<BR> E. दत्त,<BR>and आसन a seat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=331-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दत्ति|दत्तिः
दत्ति f. (-त्तिः) Gift, donation.<BR> E. दा to give, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=331-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दत्त्रिम
दत्त्रिम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>	 1. Given.<BR>	 2. Produced or effected by gifts.<BR>	 m. (-मः)<BR>1. A slave who is given by another.<BR>	 2. A son given by his parents.<BR>E. दा to give, क्त्रिम aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=331-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दत्तेय|दत्तेयः
दत्तेय m. (-यः) The deity INDRA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=331-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दत्त्वा
दत्त्वा ind. Having given.<BR> E. दा to give, क्त्वाच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=331-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दद
दद r. 1st cl. (ददते)<BR>	 1. To give.<BR>	 2. To relinquish. भ्वा० आ० सक० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=331-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ददत्
ददत् mfn. (-दन्-दती-दत्) Giving.<BR> E. दा to give, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=331-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दद
दद mfn. (-दः-दा-दं) Who gives or bestows.<BR> E. दद to give, and श aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=331-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ददन|ददनं
ददन n. (-नं) Gift, giving, donation.<BR> E. दद to give, affix भावे ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=331-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ददि
ददि mfn. (-दिः-दिः-दि) Who or what gives or bestows.<BR> E. दा to give,<BR>कि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=331-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ददिवस्
ददिवस् mfn. (-वान्-दुषी-वः) Giving, who or what gives.<BR> E. दा to give,<BR>वसु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=331-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ददृत्
ददृत् mfn. (-दृत्) Fearful, alarmed.<BR> E. दॄ to fear, क्विप् affix, and the radi-<BR>cal vowel made short.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=331-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ददृशिवस्
ददृशिवस् mfn. (-वान्-शुषी-वः) Seeing, looking.<BR> E. दृश् to see, वसु affix, इट्<BR>inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=331-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ददृश्वस्
ददृश्वस् mfn. (-श्वान्-शुषी-श्वः) Seeing, looking.<BR> E. दृश् to see, वसु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=331-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दद्रु|दद्रुः
दद्रु m. (-द्रुः) Cutaneous and herpetick eruptions; also दद्रूः or with कन्<BR>added दद्रुक m. (-कः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=331-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दद्रुघ्न|दद्रुघ्नः
दद्रुघ्न m. (-घ्नः) A kind of cassia, (C. tora.)<BR> E. दद्रु herpes, and घ्न destroy-<BR>ing, remedying; also दद्रूघ्न । हन्ति हन-टक् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=331-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दद्रण
दद्रण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Herpetick, afflicted with herpes.<BR> E. दद्रु, and न<BR>affix; also दद्रूण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=331-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दद्रुरोगिन्
दद्रुरोगिन् mfn. (-गी-गिणी-गि) Herpetick, diseased by herpes.<BR> E. दद्रु<BR>herpes, रोग a disease, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=331-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दद्रू
दद्रू m. (-द्रूः) Herpetick eruptions: see दद्रु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=331-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दद्रूघ्न|दद्रूघ्नः
दद्रूघ्न m. (-घ्नः) See दद्रूघ्न.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=331-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दद्रूण|दद्रूणः
दद्रूण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) See दद्रुण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=331-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दध
दध r. 1st cl. (दधते)<BR>	 1. To hold, to possess or retain.<BR>	 2. To give, to<BR>present, to assign or make over. (इ) दधि (दन्धति) To nourish.<BR>भ्वा० आ० सक० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=331-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दध
दध mfn. (-धः-धा-धं) Who has or possesses.<BR> E. धा to have, श aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=331-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दधत्
दधत् mfn. (-धन्-धती-धत्) Having, holding, possessing.<BR> E. धा to have,<BR>शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=331-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दधान
दधान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Having, holding, possessing.<BR> E. धा to have,<BR>शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=331-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दधि
दधि mfn. (-धिः-धिः-धि) Holding, having, who or what has or possesses.<BR>n. (-धि)<BR>	 1. Milk curdled or coagulated spontaneously by heat, or by<BR>the addition of buttermilk; it is an article of food of general use,<BR>and is held in high estimation amongst the Hindus, and is con-<BR>sidered, medicinally, as the remedy or preventative of most<BR>disorders.<BR>	 2. Resin, turpentine; (all the synonyms are common<BR>to these two senses.)<BR>	 3. A house, an abode.<BR> E. धा to have, कि affix,<BR>and the root reiterated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=331-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दधिकूर्च्चिका|दधिकूर्चिका
दधिकूर्च्चिका f. (-का) A mixture of boiled and coagulated milk, or of<BR>water and sour curds.<BR> E. दधि as above, and कूर्च्चिका inspissated<BR>milk. (छाना) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=331-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दधिचार|दधिचारः
दधिचार m. (-रः) The churning stick.<BR> E. दधि curdled milk, and चर् to<BR>move, in the causal form, affix णिच् अण् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=331-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दधिज|दधिजं
दधिज n. (-जं) Fresh butter.<BR> E. दधि curdled milk, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=331-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दधित्थ|दधित्थः
दधित्थ m. (-त्थः) The wood-apple: see कपित्थ.<BR> E. दधि, स्था to stand or be,<BR>affix ड; the root yielding a juice compared to curdled milk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=331-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दधिधेनु|दधिधेनुः
दधिधेनु f. (-नुः) A quantity of curds given away at any sacrifice.<BR> E. दधि,<BR>and धेनु a cow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=331-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दधिपुष्पिका
दधिपुष्पिका f. (-का) A flower, (Clitorea ternata.)<BR> E. दधि curdled milk, and<BR>पुष्प a flower, कन् added in the fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=331-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दधिफल|दधिफलः
दधिफल m. (-लः) The elephant or wood-apple; also दधित्थ.<BR> E. दधि curdled<BR>milk, and फल fruit, the fruit having the acid taste of Dahi or<BR>Dadhi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=331-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दधिभाण्ड
दधिभाण्ड n. (-ण्डं) A vessel for holding curds, a pail.<BR> E. दधि, and भाण्ड<BR>a vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=331-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दधिमण्ड|दधिमंड|दधिमण्डः
दधिमण्ड m. (-ण्डः) Whey.<BR> E. दधि, and मण्ड scum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=331-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दधिमण्डोद|दधिमण्डोदः
दधिमण्डोद m. (-दः) The sea of curds, or rather of whey.<BR> E. दधिमण्ड, and<BR>उद water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=331-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दधिशोण|दधिशोणः
दधिशोण m. (-णः) A monkey.<BR> E. दधि, and शोण crimson; of a colour<BR>composed of that of curdled milk and crimson.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=331-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दधिसक्तु
दधिसक्तु m. plu. always (-क्तवः) Barley meal mixed with curds.<BR> E. दधि,<BR>and सक्तु the meal of barley, after frying and grinding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=331-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दधिसर
दधिसर m. (-रः) The skim of coagulated milk; also सर only.<BR> E. दधि Dahi,<BR>and सर which goes on or upon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=331-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दधिसार|दधिसारं|दधिसारः
दधिसार m. (-रः) Fresh butter.<BR> E. दधि curdled milk, and सार essence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=331-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दधिस्नेह|दधिस्नेहः
दधिस्नेह m. (-हः) Skim of Dahi, or curdled milk whey.<BR> E. दधि curdled<BR>milk, and स्नेह oily substance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=331-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दधिस्वेद|दधिस्वेदः
दधिस्वेद m. (-दः) Buttermilk.<BR> E. दधि as above, and स्वेद exudation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=331-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दधीच|दधीचः
दधीच m. (-चः) The name of a Muni or saint, famous for having devoted<BR>himself to death, that the gods might be armed with his bones in<BR>the shape of thunderbolts; they being the only effective weapons<BR>against the demon VRITRA; also दधीचि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=331-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दधीचि|दधीचिः
दधीचि m. (-चिः) A Muni or saint: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=331-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दधीच्यस्थि
दधीच्यस्थि n. (-स्थि)<BR>	 1. The diamond.<BR>	 2. The thunderbolt.<BR> E. दधीचि a saint,<BR>and अस्थि a bone; the bones of the saint were converted into<BR>thunderbolts, which are of the same substance with the diamond,<BR>according to the Hindus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=331-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दधृच्
दधृच् mfn. (धृक्) Shameless, impudent.<BR> E. धृष् to be vain, affix क्विन्,<BR>deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=331-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दध्न|दध्नः
दध्न m. (-ध्नः) A name of YAMA.<BR> E. धा to have, reiterated, and न aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=331-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दध्याकर|दध्याकरः
दध्याकर m. (-रः) The sea of curds.<BR> E. दधि, and आकर a mine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=331-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दध्यानी
दध्यानी f. (-नी) A medicinal plant: see कटुकी.<BR> E. दधि curdled milk, नी<BR>with आङ् prefixed, affix क्विप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=331-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दध्याह्व
दध्याह्व m. (-ह्वः) The wood-apple.<BR> E. दधि, and आह्वा name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=331-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दध्युत्तर|दध्युत्तरं
दध्युत्तर n. (-रं) The skim of curdled milk, whey.<BR> E. दधि, and उत्तर upper<BR>part; also with कन् added दध्युत्तरक n. (-कं.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=331-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दध्युद|दध्युदः
दध्युद m. (-दः) The sea of curds.<BR> E. दधि, and उद water; that which has<BR>curds for water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=331-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दनु|दनुः
दनु f. (-नुः) A daughter of DAKṢA, wife of KAŚYAPA, and mother of<BR>the demons or Daityas, the Titans of Hindu mythology.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=332-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दनुज|दनुजः
दनुज m. (-जः) An Asura.<BR> E. दनु the mother of the giant race, and ज<BR>born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=332-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दनुजद्विष्
दनुजद्विष् m. (-द्विट्) A god, a deity.<BR> E. दनुज a demon, and द्विष् the hater.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=332-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दनुजारि
दनुजारि m. (-रिः) A god, a deity.<BR> E. दनुज, and अरि enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=332-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दनुसूनु|दनुसूनुः
दनुसूनु m. (-नुः) An Asura or infernal deity.<BR> E. दनु as above, and सूनु off-<BR>spring; also similar compounds, as दनुज, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=332-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्त|दंत|दंतः|दन्तः
दन्त m. (-न्तः)<BR>	 1. A tooth.<BR>	 2. The peak of a mountain.<BR>	 3. The side or<BR>ridge of a mountain.<BR>	 4. An arbour.<BR>	 5. Ivory, elephant's tooth.<BR>	 f.<BR>(-न्ती) A medicinal plant, commonly known by the same name Dan-<BR>ti, (Croton polyandrum.)<BR> E. दम् to subdue, तन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=332-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्तक|दंतक|दन्तकः
दन्तक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A crooked peak or projecting in a rock or mountain.<BR>2. A bracket, a pin or shelf projection from a wall.<BR>	 3. A tooth.<BR>कन् implying resemblance, added to दन्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=332-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्तकर्षण|दंतकर्षण|दन्तकर्षणः
दन्तकर्षण m. (-णः) The common lime, (Citrus acida.)<BR> E. दन्त a tooth, and<BR>कर्षण attracting, drawing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=332-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्तकाष्ठ|दंतकाष्ठ|दन्तकाष्ठं
दन्तकाष्ठ n. (-ष्ठं) A piece of stick, or of the small branch of a tree used<BR>as a tooth brush.<BR> E. दन्त, and काष्ठ wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=332-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्तच्छद|दंतच्छद|दन्तच्छदः
दन्तच्छद m. (-दः) A lip.<BR> E. दन्त a tooth, and छद a cover.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=332-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्तजात|दंतजात
दन्तजात mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Toothed, having teeth.<BR> E. दन्त, and जात produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=332-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्तधावन|दंतधावन|दन्तधावनं|दन्तधावनः
दन्तधावन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. A tooth brush, or a fibrous stick used for cleaning<BR>the teeth.<BR>	 2. Cleaning the teeth.<BR>	 m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. A tree yielding an<BR>astringent resin, (Mimosa catechu.)<BR>	 2. A plant, (Mimusops elengi)<BR>see वकुल.<BR> E. दन्त a tooth, and धाव् to clean, affix ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=332-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्तपत्र|दंतपत्र|दन्तपत्रं
दन्तपत्र n. (-त्रः) An ear-ring.<BR> E. दन्त a tooth, and पत्र a leaf or plate set<BR>with studs, resembling teeth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=332-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्तपत्रक|दंतपत्रक|दन्तपत्रकं
दन्तपत्रक n. (-कं) A kind of jasmine, (J. pubescens.)<BR> E. दन्त a tooth, and<BR>पत्र a leaf: the petals or leaves of the flower resembling teeth in<BR>colour and shape; this comparison is frequent among the poets.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=332-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्तपवन|दंतपवन
दन्तपवन n. (-नं) A dentifrice, or any thing taken to clean the teeth. E.<BR>दन्त, and पवन purifying. दन्तं पुनाति अनेन पू करणे ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=332-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्तपुप्पुटक|दन्तपुप्पुटकः
दन्तपुप्पुटक m. (-कः) Gum boil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=332-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्तपुष्प|दंतपुष्प|दन्तपुष्पं
दन्तपुष्प m. (-प्पः) A plant, the flower of which is compared to a tooth,<BR>(Strychnos potatorum.)<BR> E. दन्त a tooth, and पुप्प a flower. कुन्दे ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=332-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्तफल|दन्तफलं|दन्तफलः
दन्तफल m. (-लः) A plant: see the preceding.<BR> E. दन्त, and फल a fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=332-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्तभाग|दंतभाग|दन्तभागः
दन्तभाग m. (-गः)<BR>	 1. An elephant's front or forehead.<BR>	 2. Part of a tooth.<BR>E. दन्त the tusk, and भाग a part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=332-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्तमल|दंतमल|दन्तमलं
दन्तमल mn. (-लः-लं) The tarter of the teeth.<BR> E. दन्त a tooth, and मल dirt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=332-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्तमांस|दंतमांस
दन्तमांस n. (-सं) The gums.<BR> E. दन्त, and मांस flesh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=332-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्तमूलिका
दन्तमूलिका f. (-का) A plant: see दन्ती.<BR> E. दन्त, and मूल a root, कन् fem.<BR>form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=332-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्तवस्त्र|दंतवस्त्र|दन्तवस्त्रं
दन्तवस्त्र n. (-स्त्रं) A lip.<BR> E. दन्त a tooth, and वस्त्र a garment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=332-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्तवासस्|दंतवासस्
दन्तवासस् m. (-साः) A lip.<BR> E. दन्त a tooth, and वासस् vesture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=332-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्तव्यसन|दंतव्यसन
दन्तव्यसन n. (-नं) Fracture or decay of a tusk or tooth.<BR> E. दन्त, and व्यसन<BR>misfortune.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=332-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्तवेष्ट|दन्तवेष्टः
दन्तवेष्ट m. (-ष्टः) The gums.<BR> E. दन्त, and वेष्ट what incloses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=332-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्तशट|दन्तशटः
दन्तशट m. (-टः) A lime: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=332-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्तशठ|दंतशठ|दन्तशठः
दन्तशठ m. (-ठः)<BR>	 1. Elephant or wood-apple: see कपित्थ.<BR>	 2. Common<BR>lime, (Citrus acida.)<BR>	 3. A plant bearing an acid fruit, (Averhoa<BR>carambola,)<BR>	 4. An orange.<BR>	 5. Sourness, acidity.<BR>	 f. (-ठा) Wood-<BR>sorrel, (Oxalis monadelpha.)<BR> E. दन्त a tooth, and शठ noxious, bad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=332-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्तशर्करा|दंतशर्करा
दन्तशर्करा f. (-रा) Tarter of the teeth.<BR> E. दन्त tooth, and शर्करा sand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=332-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्तशाण|दंतशाण|दन्तशाणः
दन्तशाण n. (-णं) A dentifrice, composed chiefly of the powdered fruit<BR>of the chebulic myrobalan, and green sulphate of iron.<BR> E. दन्त a<BR>tooth, and शाण a whetstone; sharpening or polishing the teeth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=332-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्तशिरा
दन्तशिरा f. (-रा) The gum.<BR> E. दन्त, and शिरा a long vein or tubular vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=332-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्तशुद्धि
दन्तशुद्धि f. (-द्धिः) Cleaning the teeth.<BR> E. दन्त, and शुद्धि cleaning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=332-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्तश्लिष्ट
दन्तश्लिष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं) Entangled in or between the teeth.<BR> E. दन्त, and<BR>श्लिष्ट united.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=332-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्तसक्त
दन्तसक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं) Touched by the teeth; entangled in or be-<BR>tween the teeth.<BR> E. दन्त, and सक्त in contact.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=332-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्तहर्ष|दंतहर्ष|दन्तहर्षः
दन्तहर्ष m. (-र्षः) Tenderness of the teeth; intolerance of any rough, aus-<BR>tere, or acid substances.<BR> E. दन्त, and हर्ष delight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=332-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्तहर्षक|दंतहर्षक|दन्तहर्षकः
दन्तहर्षक m. (-कः) The lime, (Citrus acida.)<BR> E. दन्त a tooth, and हर्षक de-<BR>lighting, from हृष् to please, with वुन् affix; also with युच् affix दन्त-<BR>हर्षण.<BR>	 m. (-णः) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=332-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्ताघात|दंताघात|दन्ताघातः
दन्ताघात m. (-तः) A bite.<BR> E. दन्त, and आघात a wound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=332-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्तावल|दंतावल|दंतावलः|दन्तावलः
दन्तावल m. (-लः) An elephant.<BR> E. दन्त a tooth, वलच् affix, and the final<BR>of दन्त made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=332-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्तायुध|दंतायुध|दन्तायुधः
दन्तायुध m. (-धः) A hog.<BR> E. दन्त a tooth or tusk, and आयुध a weapon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=332-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्तार्व्वुद
दन्तार्व्वुद m. (-दः) A disease of the teeth or gums; gum boil, ulceration<BR>of the gums.<BR> E. दन्त a tooth, and अर्व्वुद a swelling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=332-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्तालिका|दंतालिका
दन्तालिका f. (-का) A horse's bridle.<BR> E. दन्त a tooth, अल भूषायाम् affix ण्वुल्<BR>and fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=332-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्तिका
दन्तिका f. (-का) A plant, commonly Danti, (Droton polyandrum.)<BR> E. कन्<BR>added to दन्ती; also read दन्तिजा f. (-जा.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=332-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्तिन्|दंतिन्
दन्तिन् mfn. (-न्ती-न्तिती-न्ति) Toothed, tusked.<BR>	 m. (-न्ती)<BR>	 1. An elephant.<BR>	 2.<BR>A mountain.<BR> E. दन्त a tooth, and इनि possessive aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=332-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्तिमद|दन्तिमदः
दन्तिमद m. (-दः) The temporal juice of the elephant.<BR> E. दन्ति and मद the<BR>effusion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=332-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्तीवीज|दन्तीवीजं
दन्तीवीज n. (-जं) A strongly purgative nut, the fruit of the croton. E.<BR>दन्ती, and वीज seed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=332-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्तुर|दंतुर|दन्तुरः
दन्तुर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>	 1. Having a large or projecting tooth.<BR>	 2. Waving,<BR>undulatory.<BR>	 3. Rising (a hair), bristling.<BR> E. दन्त a tooth, &c.<BR>affix उरच्, उन्नता दन्ताः सन्ति अस्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=332-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्तोद्भेद|दंतोद्भेद|दन्तोद्भेदः
दन्तोद्भेद m. (-दः) Dentition.<BR> E. दन्त, and उद्भेद out-break.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=332-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्तोलूखलिक|दन्तोलूखलिकः
दन्तोलूखलिक m. (-कः) One who eats grain without its having been<BR>threshed, an anchorite.<BR> E. दन्त a tooth, उलूखल a mortar, and ठन्<BR>affix; who winnows with his teeth. दन्ता एव उलूखलः कण्डनसाधनं<BR>विद्यते अस्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=332-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्त्य|दंत्य|दन्त्यः
दन्त्य mfn. (-न्त्यः-न्त्या-न्त्यं) Dental of or belonging to the teeth.<BR> E. दन्त, and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=332-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्दश|दंदश|दंदशः|दन्दशः
दन्दश m. (-शः) A tooth. E. Frequentative form of दश to bite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=332-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्दशूक|दंदशूक|दन्दशूकः
दन्दशूक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Mischievous, malignant, venomous.<BR>	 m. (-कः)<BR>	 1.<BR>A snake or serpent.<BR>	 2. A Rākṣasa, a demon or goblin. E.<BR>दश to bite, affix ऊक, the radical reiterated, and नुक् inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=332-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्द्रम
दन्द्रम n. (-मं) Going slowly or tortuously.<BR> E. द्रम् to go, root redup.<BR>घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=332-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्द्रमण
दन्द्रमण n. (-णं) Going slowly or tortuously.<BR>	 mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Who or<BR>what goes so.<BR> E. द्रम् to go, root redup. युच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=332-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दभ|दभः
दभ r. 10th cl. (दभयति-ते) also दभि (दम्भयति-ते) To order, to command.<BR>चुरा० उभ० सक० सेट् इदित् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=332-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दभ्र|दभ्रं|दभ्रः
दभ्र mfn. (-भ्रः-भ्रा-भ्रं) Little, small.<BR>	 m. (-भ्रः) The ocean.<BR> E. दन्भ-रक् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=332-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दम|दमः
दम r. 4th cl. (इर, उ) इरदमु (दाम्यति) 1. To tame or subject as an enemy<BR>to quiet or pacify, to tranquilize.<BR>	 2. To be tamed or tranquilized.<BR>दिवा० प० अक० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=332-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दम्
दम् ind. A wife.<BR> E. दम् to subject, affix क्विप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=332-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दम|दमः
दम m. (-मः)<BR>	 1. Punishing, chastisement, punishment.<BR>	 2. Taming, sub-<BR>duing.<BR>	 3. Self-command, endurance of the most painful austerities.<BR>4. Self-restraint, subduing the senses, suppressing the appetites,<BR>passions, &c.<BR>	 5. Mud, mire.<BR>	 6. (In the Vedas,) The hall of sacri-<BR>fice.<BR> E. दम् to tame or subdue, affix भावे घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=332-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दमक|दमकः
दमक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) A tamer, a subduer.<BR> E. दम् to tame, affix ण्वुल् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=332-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दमघोष|दमघोषः
दमघोष m. (-षः) A prince of the lunar race, king of Cedi, father of<BR>ŚIŚUPĀLA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=332-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दमघोषसुत|दमघोषसुतः
दमघोषसुत m. (-तः) A name of ŚIŚUPĀLA, a king and enemy of KṚṢṆA.<BR>E. दमघोष a proper name, the father of ŚIŚUPĀLA, and सुत a son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=332-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दमथ|दमथः
दमथ mn. (-थः-थं)<BR>	 1. Punishment, punishing, chastising.<BR>	 2. Self-control,<BR>endurance of rigorous austerities.<BR>	 n. (-थं) Taming, subduing. E.<BR>दम् to tame or subdue, Uṇādi affix अथच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=332-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दमथु|दमथुः
दमथु mn. (-थुः-थु)<BR>	 1. Punishment, restraint or subjection of others.<BR>	 2.<BR>Self-denial, subjection of oneself.<BR> E. दम् to tame, अथुच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=333-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दमन|दमनं|दमनः
दमन m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. A hero.<BR>	 2. A philosopher.<BR>	 3. A kind of flower, common-<BR>ly Dona, (Artemisia.)<BR>	 n. (-नं) Taming, subduing.<BR> E. दम् to tame,<BR>भावे ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=333-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दमनीय
दमनीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) To be tamed, subjected, or subdued.<BR> E. दम् to<BR>tame, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=333-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दमयत
दमयत mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्) Taming, restraining, chastising.<BR>	 f. (-न्ती)<BR>	 1.<BR>The wife of NALA.<BR>	 2. A kind of cucumber.<BR> E. दम् to subdue, parti-<BR>cipial affix शतृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=333-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दमस्वसृ
दमस्वसृ f. (-सा) DAMAYANTI.<BR> E. दम, स्वसृ sister of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=333-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दमित|दमितः
दमित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Tamed, subdued, patient of every suffering,<BR>exaction or privation.<BR> E. दम् to tame, affix क्त, with इट् inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=333-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दमिन्
दमिन् mfn. (-मी-मिनी-मि) A tamer, a dominator.<BR> E. दम with शीलार्थे<BR>घिनुण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=333-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दमुनस्
दमुनस् m. (-नाः)<BR>	 1. A name of Agni or fire.<BR>	 2. A name of SUKRA, regent<BR>of Venus.<BR> E. दम् to tame (all things), Uṇādi affix उनसि; also ऊनसि<BR>whence दमूनस् m. (-नाः.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=333-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दम्पति|दंपति
दम्पति m. du. (-ती) Husband and wife.<BR> E. दम् a wife, and पति a husband.<BR>जाया च पतिश्च द्वन्द्वे जायाशब्दस्य पक्षे दमादेशः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=333-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दम्भ|दंभ|दंभः|दम्भः
दम्भ r. 5th cl. (उ) दम्भु (दम्नोति) 1. To act deceitfully, to cheat, to impose<BR>upon, to trick or deceive.<BR>	 2. To split or divide. r. 10th cl. (दम्भयते)<BR>To collect, to gather, to arrange or string. स्वा० प० अक० सेट् । सङ्घाते<BR>चुरा० आ० ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=333-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दम्भ|दंभ|दंभः|दम्भः
दम्भ m. (-म्भः)<BR>	 1. Deceit, fraud, cheating.<BR>	 2. Hypocrisy.<BR>	 3. Sin, wicked-<BR>ness.<BR>	 4. Arrogance, pride.<BR> E. दम्भ to deceive, &c. affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=333-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दम्भिन्|दंभिन्
दम्भिन् mfn. (-म्भी-म्भिनी-म्भि)<BR>	 1. Hypocritical.<BR>	 2. Proud.<BR>	 3. Wicked.<BR>	 m. (-म्भी)<BR>A hypocrite, an impostor.<BR> E. दम्भ, and णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=333-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दम्भोलि|दंभोलि|दंभोलिः|दम्भोलिः
दम्भोलि m. (-लिः) INDRA'S thunderbolt.<BR> E. दम्भ to divide or split, affix<BR>उलि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=333-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दम्य|दम्यः
दम्य mfn. (-म्यः-म्या-म्यं) To be subjected or tamed.<BR>	 2. To be punished.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-म्यः) A steer, a young bullock.<BR> E. दम् to tame, यत् affix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=333-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दय|दयः
दय (ञ) ञिदय r. 1st cl. (दयते)<BR>	 1. To give.<BR>	 2. To move.<BR>	 3. To take.<BR>	 4. To<BR>protect.<BR>	 5. To hurt or kill. भ्वा० आ० सक० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=333-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दय|दयः
दय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Compassionate, tender-hearted.<BR>	 mf. (-यः-या) Tender-<BR>ness, compassion, clemency.<BR> E. दय् to preserve, affix अङ्, fem.<BR>affix टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=333-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दयमान
दयमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Preserving, protecting.<BR> E. दय, and शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=333-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दयाकर|दयाकरः
दयाकर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Kind, showing compassion.<BR> E. दया, and कर who<BR>makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=333-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दयाकूर्च्च|दयाकूर्च|दयाकूर्चः
दयाकूर्च्च m. (-र्च्चः) A Buddha, a Bauddha saint, or a form of BUDDHA,<BR>the founder of the sect.<BR> E. दया compassion, and कूर्च्च boasting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=333-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दयाकृत्
दयाकृत् mfn. (-त्) Compassionate.<BR> E. दया, and कृत् doing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=333-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दयान्वित
दयान्वित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Compassionate, charitable, kind.<BR> E. दया, and<BR>अन्वित possessed of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=333-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दयायुक्त
दयायुक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं) Compassionate, benevolent.<BR> E. दया, and युक्त<BR>joined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=333-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दयाल
दयाल m. (-लः) The breaking of a bank.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=333-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दयालु|दयालुः
दयालु mfn. (-लुः-लुः-लु) Tender, compassionate.<BR> E. दया compassion, आलुच्<BR>affix; also दयालुक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=333-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दयालुत्व
दयालुत्व n. (-त्वं) Tenderness, compassionateness.<BR> E. त्व added to the last;<BR>with तल् दयालुता ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=333-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दयावत्|दयावन्त्
दयावत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Merciful, tender,<BR> E. दया, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=333-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दयाशील
दयाशील mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Kind, compassionate.<BR> E. दया, and शील poss-<BR>essed of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=333-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दयित|दयितं|दयितः
दयित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Beloved, dear, desired.<BR>	 m. (-तः)<BR>	 1. A husband.<BR>	 2.<BR>A lover.<BR>	 f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. A woman.<BR>	 2. A wife or mistress.<BR> E. दय् to regard<BR>tenderly, affix क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=333-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दयिताधीन
दयिताधीन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Hen-pecked, subject to a wife.<BR> E. दयिता a wife,<BR>and अधीन subject.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=333-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर|दरं|दरः
दर mn. (-रः-रं)<BR>	 1. Fear, terror.<BR>	 2. A hole in the ground.<BR>	 n. (-रं) A conch-<BR>shell. ind. A little.<BR>	 f. (-रा-री)<BR>	 1. A natural or artificial excavation<BR>in a mountain, a cave, a cavern, a grotto, &c.<BR>	 2. A valley.<BR> E. दॄ<BR>to divide, to dread, &c. affix भावे अप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=333-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दरणि|दरणिः
दरणि m. (-णिः) An eddy, a current.<BR> E. दॄ to tear (down the banks),<BR>affix अनि; some books read दारणि, and others आरणि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=333-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दरद्
दरद् f. (-त्)<BR>	 1. Terror.<BR>	 2. A mountain.<BR>	 3. A precipice.<BR>	 4. The heart.<BR>	 5.<BR>A bank or mound.<BR>	 6. A tribe of barbarians.<BR> E. दॄ to divide or tear,<BR>अदि Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=333-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दरद|दरदं|दरदः
दरद mf. (-दः-दा) A country bordering on Kashmir, the mountains<BR>about Kashmir and above Peshawar.<BR>	 m. (-दः)<BR>	 1. Fear, terror.<BR>	 2. A<BR>tribe of barbarians.<BR> E. अच् added to the former.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=333-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दरविदलित
दरविदलित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Slightly or a little burst or opened.<BR> E. दर,<BR>and विदलित divided.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=333-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दरि|दरिः
दरि f. (-रिः) A cave: see दर.<BR> E. दॄ to divide, इन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=333-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दरित|दरितः
दरित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Frightened, terrified.<BR>	 2. Torn, rent, divided.<BR>E. दर fear, इतच् affix; or दॄ to divide, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=333-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दरिद्र|दरिद्रः
दरिद्र mfn. (-द्रः-द्रा-द्रं) Poor, needy, indigent, distressed.<BR> E. दरिद्रा to be<BR>poor, affix क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=333-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दरिद्रता
दरिद्रता f. (-ता) Poverty, indigence.<BR> E. दरिद्र, and तल् affix; also with त्व<BR>दरिद्रत्वम् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=333-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दरिद्रा
दरिद्रा r. 2nd cl. (दरिद्राति) 3rd plu. (दरिद्रति) To be poor or needy. अदा०<BR>पर० अक० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=333-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दरिद्रायक|दरिद्रायकः
दरिद्रायक mfn. (कः-का-कं) Poor, distressed.<BR> E. दरिद्रा, and ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=333-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दरिद्रित|दरिद्रितः
दरिद्रित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Poor, impoverished.<BR> E. दरिद्रा to be poor, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=333-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दरिद्रितृ
दरिद्रितृ mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ) Poor, needy.<BR> E. दरिद्रा, and तृच् affix; otherwise<BR>with ण्वुल् affix दरिद्रायक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=333-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दरीभू
दरीभू f. (-भूः) A cavern, a hollow.<BR> E. दरी, and भू a place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=333-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दरीभृत्
दरीभृत् m. (-भृत्) A mountain.<BR> E. दरी a cave, and भृत् what has.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=333-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दरोदर|दरोदरं|दरोदरः
दरोदर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A gamester.<BR>	 2. A stake.<BR>	 n. (-रं) Gambling: see<BR>दुरोदर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=333-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्दर|दर्दरः|दर्द्दरः
दर्दर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Cracked, flawed, slightly broken, (a vessel, &c.)<BR>m. (-रः) A mountain.<BR> E. दॄ to tear or break, affix अच्, and the root<BR>repeated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=333-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्दराम्र|दर्दराम्रः|दर्द्दराम्रः
दर्दराम्र m. (-म्रः) A sort of sauce or condiment; also मीनाम्रीण ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=333-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्दरीक|दर्दरीकः|दर्द्दरीकं|दर्द्दरीकः
दर्दरीक mn. (-कः-कं) A musical instrument.<BR>	 m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A cloud.<BR>	 2. A<BR>frog.<BR> E. दॄ to tear, Uṇādi affix ईकन्, and the radical reduplicate;<BR>what is struck, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=333-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्दुर|दर्दुरः|दर्द्दुर|दर्द्दुरं|दर्द्दुरः
दर्दुर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A frog.<BR>	 2. A cloud.<BR>	 3. A mountain.<BR>	 4. A sort or mu-<BR>sical instrument, a pipe or flute.<BR>	 n. (-रं) A number of villages.<BR>	 f.<BR>(-रा) A name of DURGĀ.<BR> E. दॄ to tear, Uṇādi affix उरच्, and the ra-<BR>dical repeated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=333-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्दुरपुट|दर्दुरपुटः
दर्दुरपुट m. (-टः) The mouth or extremity of a pipe.<BR> E. दर्दुर, and पुट<BR>a cup.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=333-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्द्रु|दर्द्रुः
दर्द्रु m. (-र्द्रुः) Herpetick eruption: see दर्द्रू.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=333-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्द्रू
दर्द्रू m. (-र्द्रूः) A cutaneous disease, herpes; also दर्द्रू.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=333-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दद्रू
दद्रू m. (-र्द्रूः) Cutaneous eruption, herpes.<BR> E. दरिद्रा to be poor, ऊ Una-<BR>di affix, the form is irregular: by substituting the short vowel,<BR>and omitting the first र, this word and its compounds appear in a<BR>variety of forms, as दद्रु, दद्रू, दर्द्रू; also omitting the second र, दर्द्रू,<BR>&c. &c. q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=333-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्द्रूघ्न
दर्द्रूघ्न m. (-घ्नः) Cassia, (tora:) also दद्रुघ्न and दर्द्रूघ्न.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=333-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दद्रूण|दद्रूणः
दद्रूण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Diseased with herpes, herpetick; also दर्द्रुण, दर्द्रूण,<BR>&c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=333-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्द्रूरोगिन्
दर्द्रूरोगिन् mfn. (-गी-गिणी-गि) Herpetic, afflicted with herpes; also दर्द्र<BR>रोगिन्, दर्द्रु रोगिन्, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=333-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्प|दर्पः
दर्प m. (-र्पः)<BR>	 1. Pride, arrogance.<BR>	 2. Musk.<BR>	 3. Heat.<BR> E. दृप् to be proud,<BR>to inflame, affix भावे घञ्, कर्त्तरि अच् वा ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=333-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्पक|दर्पकः
दर्पक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) What kindles, inflames, or excites, m. (-कः)<BR>A name of KĀMADEVA.<BR> E. दृप् to inflame, affix ण्वुल्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=333-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्पण|दर्पणं|दर्पणः
दर्पण m. (-णः) A mirror.<BR>	 n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. The eye.<BR>	 2. Kindling, inflaming. E.<BR>दृप् to excite, to shine, affix ल्यु ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=334-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्पध्मात
दर्पध्मात mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Puffed up or swelling with pride.<BR> E. दर्प, and<BR>ध्मात inflated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=334-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्पह
दर्पह mfn. (-हः-हा-हं) Humbling, humiliating, pride-destroying.<BR> E. दर्प,<BR>and ह what removes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=334-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्पारम्भ|दर्पारम्भः
दर्पारम्भ m. (-म्भः) Incipient pride, conceit.<BR> E. दर्प pride, आरम्भ commencement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=334-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्पोपशान्ति|दर्पोपशान्तिः
दर्पोपशान्ति f. (-न्तिः) Conciliating or subduing arrogance.<BR> E. दर्प, and उप-<BR>शान्ति allaying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=334-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्ब्ब|दर्ब
दर्ब्ब m. (-र्ब्बः)<BR>	 1. A Rākṣasa, an imp or goblin.<BR>	 2. A mischievous man<BR>or animal, &c.<BR> E. दॄ to tear, Uṇādi affix ब.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=334-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्ब्बट|दर्बट
दर्ब्बट m. (-टः) A constable, police officer set over a village, &c.<BR>	 2. A<BR>warder, a doorkeeper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=334-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्ब्बरीक
दर्ब्बरीक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. INDRA.<BR>	 2. Air, wind.<BR>	 3. A musical instrument.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=334-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्ब्बि|दर्बि
दर्ब्बि f. (-र्ब्बिः-र्ब्बी)<BR>	 1. A ladle or spoon.<BR>	 2. The expanded hood of a<BR>snake.<BR> E. दॄ to divide, Uṇādi affix बि; also with ङीप् added दर्ब्बी;<BR>some authorities made the final consonant the labial letter व, as<BR>as दर्व्वि, दर्व्वी; also दार्व्वी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=334-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्ब्बिक
दर्ब्बिक m. (-कः) A ladle, a spoon.<BR>	 f. (-का) A potherb: see दार्ब्बिका. E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=334-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्ब्बीकर
दर्ब्बीकर m. (-रः) A snake.<BR> E. दर्ब्बी the hood expanded, and कर who<BR>makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=334-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्भ|दर्भः
दर्भ m. (-र्भः)<BR>	 1. Kusa or sacrificial grass, (Poa cynosuroides.)<BR>	 2. A kind<BR>of reed, (Saccharum spontaneum.)<BR>	 3. Another species, (S.<BR>cylindricum.)<BR> E. दृभि to collect, to arrange, affix घञ्; or दॄ to<BR>tear, Uṇādi affix भ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=334-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्भट|दर्भटं
दर्भट m. (-टः) A private apartment or house, a retirement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=334-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्भपत्र|दर्भपत्रः
दर्भपत्र m. (-त्रः) A kind of grass, (Saccharum spontaneum.)<BR> E. दर्भ, and<BR>पत्र a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=334-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्श|दर्शः
दर्श m. (-र्शः)<BR>	 1. Sight, seeing.<BR>	 2. Day of new moon when it rises in-<BR>visible.<BR>	 3. Half monthly sacrifice, performed at the change of the<BR>moon, by persons maintaining a perpetual fire.<BR> E. दृश् to see, affix<BR>आधारे घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=334-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्शक|दर्शकः
दर्शक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Who or what shows, displays, explains, makes<BR>clear, &c.<BR>	 m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A doorkeeper, a warder.<BR>	 2. An exhibiter,<BR>one who points out or shows any thing.<BR>	 3. A skilful man, one who<BR>is conversant with any science or art, &c.<BR> E. दृश् to see, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=334-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्शत|दर्शतः
दर्शत m. (-तः)<BR>	 1. The sun.<BR>	 2. The moon.<BR> E. दृश् to see, कर्मणि अतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=334-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्शन|दर्शनं
दर्शन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Sight, seeing, looking.<BR>	 2. The eye.<BR>	 3. A Mirror.<BR>	 4. Show-<BR>ing.<BR>	 5. Aspect, appearance.<BR>	 6. Directing, instructing.<BR>	 7. A dream,<BR>a vision.<BR>	 8. Virtue, moral merit.<BR>	 9. Knowledge, especially religi-<BR>ous.<BR>	 10. Understanding, intellect.<BR>	 11. A Śāstra, one of six religi-<BR>ous or philosophical systems, the Patanjala, Sankhya, Vaiseshika,<BR>Nyaya, Mīmāṃsā, and Vedanta.<BR>	 12. Sacrifice.<BR>	 13. Colour.<BR>	 14. Vi-<BR>siting any sacred shrine, worshipping in the presence of any image.<BR>E. दृश् to see, affix भावकरणादौ ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=334-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्शनप्रतिभू
दर्शनप्रतिभू m. (-भूः) A surety for appearance.<BR> E. दर्शन, and प्रतिभू a surety.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=334-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्शनप्रातिभाव्य
दर्शनप्रातिभाव्य n. (-व्यं) Surety for appearance, bail.<BR> E. दर्शन, and प्रातिभाव्य<BR>surety.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=334-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्शनीय|दर्शनीयः
दर्शनीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>	 1. Beautiful, handsome, agreeable.<BR>	 2. Visible,<BR>to be seen.<BR> E. दर्श looking, and छ affix; or दृश् to see, and अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=334-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्शनीयमानिन्
दर्शनीयमानिन् mfn. (-नी-निनी-नि) Vain, conceited, thinking oneself hand-<BR>some.<BR> E. दर्शनीय, मन् to mind, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=334-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्शयामिनी
दर्शयामिनी f. (-नी) The night or new moon, on which it rises invisible.<BR>E. दर्श new moon, and यामिनी night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=334-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्शयितृ
दर्शयितृ mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ) Showing, displaying, who or what shows.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-ता)<BR>	 1. A warder, an usher, a doorkeeper.<BR>	 2. A show man, a<BR>guide, an exhibiter.<BR> E. दृश् to see, in the causal form, and तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=334-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्शयित्वा
दर्शयित्वा ind. Having shown, having made manifest.<BR> E. दृश् to see,<BR>causal form, क्त्वाच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=334-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्शयिष्यत्
दर्शयिष्यत् mfn. (-ष्यन्-ष्यन्ती-ष्यत्) Showing, explaining or proposing to show<BR>or explain.<BR> E. दृश् to see, causal form, शतृ affix, with a future<BR>sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=334-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्शविपद्
दर्शविपद् m. (-द्) The moon.<BR> E. दर्श day of new moon, and विपद् trouble.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=334-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्शित|दर्शितः
दर्शित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Visible, apparent.<BR>	 2. Shown, displayed.<BR>	 3.<BR>Explained.<BR>	 4. Seen.<BR>	 5. Understood.<BR> E. दृश् to see, in the causal<BR>form, affix णिच् and क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=334-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्शितवत्|दर्शितवन्त्
दर्शितवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>	 1. Having shown, showing, displaying.<BR>2. Explaining, teaching.<BR> E. दृश causal form, क्तवतु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=334-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दल|दलं|दलः
दल r. 1st cl. (दलति) r. 10th cl. (दालयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To cut, to divide, to split<BR>or pierce.<BR>	 2. To be cut, &c.<BR>	 3. To display.<BR>	 4. To wither. भ्वा० अक०<BR>भेदे सक० भेदने सेट् । भेदने चुरा० उभ० सक० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=334-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दल|दलं|दलः
दल mn. (-लः-लं) A leaf.<BR>	 n. (-लं)<BR>	 1. A part, a portion, a fragment.<BR>	 2.<BR>Dividing, tearing, cutting, splitting, &c.<BR>	 3. A sheath, a scabbard.<BR>4. An adulteration or alloy.<BR>	 5. A heap or quantity.<BR>	 6. The leaf<BR>of Tamala.<BR>	 7. A half.<BR> E. दल् to divide, to cut, &c. affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=334-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दलकपाट|दलकपाटः
दलकपाट m. (-टः) A folded petal or leaf.<BR> E. दल, and कपाट a door.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=334-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दलकोष|दलकोषः
दलकोष m. (-षः) A sort of jasmine, (J. pubescens.)<BR> E. दल a leaf, and<BR>कोष a sheath.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=334-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दलत्
दलत् mfn. (-लत्-लन्ती-लत्)<BR>	 1. Splitting, rending.<BR>	 2. Being torn or cut.<BR>E. दल् to cut or be pierced, affix शतृ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=334-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दलद्धृदय
दलद्धृदय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Broken-hearted, cut to the heart, &c.<BR> E. दलत्.<BR>and हृदय the heart.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=334-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दलन|दलनं
दलन mfn. (-नः-नी-नं) Breaking to pieces, cutting, dividing, (who or<BR>what does so.)<BR>	 n. (-नं) Tearing, rending, breaking, pulling to<BR>pieces.<BR>	 f. (-नी) A clod or clump of earth or mould.<BR> E. दल् to divide,<BR>affix करणे ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=334-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दलनिर्म्मोक|दलनिर्मोक|दलनिर्मोकः|दलनिर्म्मोकः
दलनिर्म्मोक m. (-कः) The Bhurjapatra, a tree of which the bark is used,<BR>for hookah snakes, &c.<BR> E. दल a leaf, and निर्म्मोक shedding, casting<BR>off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=334-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दलप|दलपः
दलप m. (-पः)<BR>	 1. Gold.<BR>	 2. A sacred or religious institute.<BR> E. दल् to be<BR>divided, Uṇādi affix कपन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=334-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दलपुष्पी
दलपुष्पी f. (-ष्पी) A fragrant plant, (Pandanus odoratissimus.)<BR> E. दल a<BR>leaf, and पुष्प a flower; the leaves surrounding the flower. केतक्याम् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=334-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दलसूचि|दलसूचिः
दलसूचि m. (-चिः) A thorn.<BR> E. दल a leaf, and सूचि a needle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=334-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दलस्नसा
दलस्नसा f. (-सा) The fibre or vein of a leaf.<BR> E. दल a leaf, and स्नसा a<BR>fibre. पत्रशिरायाम् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=334-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दलाढक|दलाढकः
दलाढक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. Sesamum growing wild or spontaneously.<BR>	 2. An<BR>aquatic plant, (Pistia stratiotes.)<BR>	 3. A plant commonly Nageshwara,<BR>(Mesua ferrea.)<BR>	 4. A tree, (Mimosa sirisha.)<BR>	 5. Red chalk.<BR>	 6. Cuttle<BR>fish bone.<BR>	 7. A moat, a ditch.<BR>	 8. A sort of jasmine, (J. pubescens.)<BR>9. An elephant's ear.<BR>	 10. The driver of an elephant.<BR>	 11. A hurri-<BR>cane, a high wind.<BR> E. दल as above, ढौकृ to go, with आङ् prefix-<BR>ed, affix अच्, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=334-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दलाढ्य|दलाढ्यः
दलाढ्य m. (-ढ्यः) Mud, but mud especially on the banks of a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=334-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दलामल|दलामलं
दलामल n. (-लं)<BR>	 1. A tree, (Vangueria spinosa:) see मरुवक.<BR>	 2. A plant,<BR>(Artemisia.)<BR> E. दल a leaf, and अमल clear, clean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=334-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दलाम्ल|दलाम्लं
दलाम्ल n. (-म्लं) Sorrel.<BR> E. दल the leaf, and अम्ल sour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=334-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दलि|दलिः
दलि mf. (-लिः-ली) A clod of clay or mould.<BR> E. दल् to be divided, (by<BR>the harrow or plough,) Uṇādi affix इ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=334-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दलिक|दलिकं
दलिक m. (-कः) Timber, wood.<BR> E. दल् to split, affix इकच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=334-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दलित|दलितं
दलित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Blown, full blown, expanded.<BR>	 2. Broken, split.<BR>3. Cut to pieces.<BR>	 4. Torn, rent.<BR>	 5. Scattered, driven apart, divid-<BR>ed.<BR>	 6. Opened, unfolded.<BR> E. दल् to split, affix क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=334-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दलेगन्धि|दलेगन्धिः
दलेगन्धि m. (-न्धिः) A plant, (Echites scholaris:) see सप्तपर्ण.<BR> E. दल in<BR>the seventh case दले, in the leaf, and गन्धि fragrance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=334-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दल्भ|दल्भः
दल्भ m. (-ल्भः)<BR>	 1. Fraud, dishonesty.<BR>	 2. Sin.<BR>	 3. The name of a Muni or<BR>saint.<BR>	 4. A wheel.<BR> E. दल् to divide, and भ Uṇādi affix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=334-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दल्मि|दल्मिः
दल्मि m. (-ल्मिः)<BR>	 1. A name of INDRA.<BR>	 2. INDRA'S thunderbolt.<BR> E. दल् to<BR>break or split, Uṇādi affix मि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=334-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दव|दवः
दव (इ) दवि r. 1st cl. (दन्वति) To go, to move. भ्वा० प० सक० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=335-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दव|दवः
दव m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. A wood on fire, a forest conflagration.<BR>	 2. A wood, a<BR>forest.<BR>	 3. Fire in general.<BR>	 4. Heat, (general or physical.)<BR> E. दु to<BR>agitate, affix अच्; also दाव ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=335-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दवथु|दवथुः
दवथु m. (-थुः)<BR>	 1. Anxiety, vexation, distress.<BR>	 2. Inflammation of the<BR>eye, &c.<BR> E. दु to be agitated, अथुच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=335-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दवयत्
दवयत् mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्) Removing, making remote, placing at a dis-<BR>tance.<BR> E. दव for दूर used as a verb, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=335-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दवाग्नि|दवाग्निः
दवाग्नि m. (-ग्निः) A wood on fire, or the conflagration of a forest.<BR> E. दव<BR>a wood, and अग्नि a fire; also दव and दाव ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=335-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दविष्ठ|दविष्ठः
दविष्ठ mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठा-ष्ठं) Very remote, very distant.<BR> E. दूर् far, affix इष्ठन्,<BR>and दव substituted for दूर्; also दवीयस् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=335-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दवीयस्
दवीयस् mfn. (-यान्-यसी-यः) Very remote or distant: see the preced-<BR>ing, the affix being the superlative affix ईयसुन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=335-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दश
दश (इ) दशि r. 1st and 10th cls. (दशति दंशयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To bite or sting.<BR>2. To arm, to put on armour.<BR>	 3. To see. r. 10th cl. (दंशयते) To<BR>shine. With उप, to be in trouble, to be reduced in circumstances.<BR>With सम्, to pinch, to nip, to bite. दीप्तौ चु० उभ० अक० सेट् इदित् ।<BR>दंशनार्थे चु० आत्म० and भ्वा० प० ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=335-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशक
दशक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Ten.<BR> E. कन् added to दश ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=335-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशकण्ठ|दशकंठ|दशकण्ठः
दशकण्ठ m. (-ण्ठः) A name of RAVANA.<BR> E. दश ten, and कण्ठ a neck: the<BR>ten-necked: also similar names, as दशग्रीव, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=335-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशकण्ठजित्|दशकंठजित्
दशकण्ठजित् m. (-जित्) A name of RAMA.<BR> E. दशकण्ठ RAVANA, and जित्<BR>the conqueror.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=335-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशकन्धर|दशकंधर|दशकन्धरः
दशकन्धर m. (-रः) RAVANA: see दशकण्ठ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=335-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशकामजव्यसन
दशकामजव्यसन n. (-नं) The aggregate of ten vices, proceeding from the<BR>the quality of desire, viz. hunting, gambling, sleeping during<BR>the day, abusiveness, lechery, drunkenness, dancing, singing, play-<BR>ing, and hypocrisy.<BR> E. दश ten, काम desire, ज born, व्यसन calamity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=335-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशगुण
दशगुण adv.<BR>	 n. (-णं) Ten times, ten-fold.<BR> E. दश, and गुण a time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=335-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशग्राम
दशग्राम n. (-मं) A district or collection of ten villages.<BR> E. दश, and ग्राम a<BR>village.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=335-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशग्रामपति|दशग्रामपतिः
दशग्रामपति m. (-तिः) A magistrate or chief of ten villages.<BR> E. दश, and<BR>ग्राम a village, पति master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=335-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशग्रामिन्
दशग्रामिन् m. (-मी)<BR>	 1. The head man of ten villages.<BR>	 2. Municipality<BR>or corporation of the same.<BR> E. दशग्राम, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=335-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशग्रीव|दशग्रीवः
दशग्रीव m. (-वः) RAVANA: see दशकण्ठ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=335-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशति|दशतिः
दशति f. (-तिः) A hundred.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=335-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशधा
दशधा ind. In ten ways.<BR> E. दश, and धाच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=335-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशन्
दशन् mfn. plu. (-श) Ten.<BR> E. दश् to bite, Uṇādi affix अन्, the nasal<BR>rejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=335-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशन|दशनं|दशनः
दशन mn. (-नः-नं) A tooth.<BR>	 m. (-नः) The peak of a mountain.<BR>	 n. (-नं)<BR>Armour, mail.<BR> E. दंश् to bite, affix भावे करणादौ ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=335-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशनवासस्
दशनवासस् n. (-सः) A lip.<BR> E. दशन tooth, and वासस् vesture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=335-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशनांशु|दशनांशुः
दशनांशु m. (-शुः) The whiteness or brightness of the teeth.<BR> E. दशन,<BR>and अंशु a ray.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=335-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशनाङ्क|दशनांक|दशनाङ्कः
दशनाङ्क m. (-ङ्कः) A bite, the mark of the teeth.<BR> E. दशन, and अङ्क a mark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=335-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशनाढ्या
दशनाढ्या f. (-ढ्या) A kind of sorrel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=335-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशनोच्छिष्ठ
दशनोच्छिष्ठ mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठा-ष्ठं) Toothless.<BR>	 m. (-ष्ठः)<BR>	 1. Breathing, breathing<BR>out, expiration.<BR>	 2. A lip.<BR>	 3. Kissing, a kiss.<BR> E. दशन a tooth, and<BR>उच्छिष्ठ expelled, ejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=335-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशपारमिताधर|दशपारमिताधरः
दशपारमिताधर m. (-रः) A Buddha or Bauddha saint.<BR> E. दश, पारमिता a<BR>particular work or scripture of this sect, धर who has.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=335-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशपुर|दशपुरं
दशपुर n. (-रं) A fragrant grass, (Cyperus rotundus:) see दाशपुर.<BR>	 2. A<BR>district, part of Malwa or Bundelkhand.<BR>	 3. A town or city.<BR> E. दश<BR>for दाश a fisherman, and पुर or पूर to nourish, affix दश; also दश<BR>ten, and पुर a city: district of ten cities.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=335-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशपूर
दशपूर n. (-रं) A fragrant grass: see the preceding; also दाशपूर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=335-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशबल|दशबलः
दशबल m. (-लः) A Buddha of Bauddha teacher.<BR> E. दश ten, (the ten<BR>worlds,) बल powerful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=335-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशभूमिग|दशभूमिगः
दशभूमिग m. (-गः) BUDDHA, the founder of the Bauddha sect, or a<BR>Buddha, the generic name of the sanctified teachers of that sect.<BR>E. दश ten, भूमि earth, and ग who goes; traversing the ten worlds;<BR>also दशभूमीश m. (-शः) Lord of the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=335-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशम|दशमः
दशम mfn. (-मः-मी-मं) Tenth.<BR>	 f. (-मी)<BR>	 1. The tenth day of the half<BR>month.<BR>	 2. The tenth or last stage of human life, the last ten<BR>years of a century.<BR> E. दशन् ten, and मट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=335-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशमहाविद्या
दशमहाविद्या f. (-द्या) DURGĀ.<BR> E. दश ten, (forms, or names,) महा great,<BR>and विद्या a name of DURGĀ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=335-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशमाल
दशमाल nf. (-लं-ली) A collection of ten garlands.<BR> E. दश ten, माला a<BR>garland, टच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=335-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशमिन्
दशमिन् mfn. (-मी-मिनी-मि) Very old or aged.<BR> E. दशमी the tenth, (stage<BR>of life,) and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=335-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशमीङ्गत|दशमींगत
दशमीङ्गत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Very old, above ninety.<BR> E. दशमी, and गत arrived at.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=335-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशमीस्थ|दशमीस्थः
दशमीस्थ mfn. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थं)<BR>	 1. Impotent.<BR>	 2. Very old, turned of ninety.<BR>	 3.<BR>Dying, on the point of death.<BR> E. दशमी the last stage of life, and<BR>स्थ who is.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=335-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशमुख|दशमुखः
दशमुख m. (-खः) A name of RAVANA.<BR> E. दश ten, and मुख a face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=335-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशमुखान्तक|दशमुखान्तकः
दशमुखान्तक m. (-कः) A name of RAMA.<BR> E. दशमुख RAVANA, and अन्तक<BR>destroyer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=335-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशमूल|दशमूलं
दशमूल n. (-लं) A tonic medicament prepared from the roots of ten<BR>plants.<BR> E. दश ten, and मूल a root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=335-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशरथ|दशरथः
दशरथ m. (-थः) A proper name, sovereign of Ayodhya or Oude,<BR>and father of RAMA.<BR> E. दश ten, and रथ a car; whose car bore<BR>him to the ten quarters of the universe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=335-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशरात्र|दशरात्रः
दशरात्र n. (-त्रं) A period of ten days and nights.<BR> E. दश, and रात्र for<BR>रात्रि night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=335-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशरूपभृत्
दशरूपभृत् mfn. (-भृत्) A name of VIṢṆU.<BR> E. दश ten, रूप forms, (Ava-<BR>taras,) and भृत् who assumes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=335-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशलक्षण
दशलक्षण n. (-णं) Ten marks or attributes.<BR> E. दश, and लक्षण a mark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=335-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशवाजिन्
दशवाजिन् m. (-जी) The moon.<BR> E. दश ten, and वाजिन् a horse, whose car<BR>is drawn by ten horses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=335-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशशत
दशशत n. (-तं) A thousand.<BR> E. दश, and शत a hundred.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=335-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशसहस्र
दशसहस्र n. (-स्रं) A myriad.<BR> E. दश, and सहस्र a thousand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=335-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशा
दशा f. (-शा) or m. plu. (-शाः)<BR>	 1. The ends of a piece of cloth, the end<BR>of a garment.<BR>	 2. A state, a condition, a period or time of life,<BR>as youth, age, manhood, &c.<BR>	 3. The wick of a lamp.<BR>	 4. The mind<BR>or faculty, of understanding.<BR>	 5. Aspect or position of the planets<BR>at birth.<BR> E. दश् to bite, to cut or divide, or be cut or divided,<BR>अङ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=335-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशाकर्ष|दशाकर्षः
दशाकर्ष m. (-र्षः) A lamp.<BR> E. दशा a wick, आकर्ष what possesses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=335-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशाकर्षिन्
दशाकर्षिन् m. (-र्षी) A lamp.<BR> E. दशा a wick, आङ् before, कृष् to make<BR>lines, affix इनि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=335-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशानन|दशाननः
दशानन m. (-नः) The giant RAVANA.<BR> E. दश ten, and आनन a face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=335-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशानिक|दशानिकः
दशानिक m. (-कः) A plant, commonly Danti, (Croton polyandrum.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=335-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशाफल
दशाफल n. (-लं) Result of circumstance of the condition of life.<BR> E. दशा,<BR>and फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=335-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशार्ण|दशार्णः
दशार्ण m. (-र्णः) A country, part of central Hindustan, lying on the<BR>south-east of the Vindhya mountains.<BR>	 f. (णा) A river rising in the<BR>Vindhya hills, the Dosarna of the ancients.<BR> E. दश ten, ऋण a<BR>fort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=335-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशास्थिति
दशास्थिति f. (-तिः) Condition.<BR> E. दशा, and स्थिति stay.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=335-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशार्ह|दशार्हः
दशार्ह m. (-र्हः)<BR>	 1. A Buddha or Jina.<BR>	 2. A country in the south of<BR>India, the kingdom of YADU.<BR>	 m. plu. (-र्हाः) The Yadavas or people<BR>of Dasarha.<BR> E. दश ten, and अर्ह proper, worthy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=335-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशावतार|दशावतारः
दशावतार m. (-रः) A name of VIṢṆU.<BR> E. दश ten, and अवतार descent;<BR>the deity of whom there are ten descents from heaven, for the<BR>purpose of protecting or punishing mankind: see अवतार ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=335-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशाविशेष
दशाविशेष m. (-षः) Excisting circumstances, peculiar condition.<BR> E. दशा,<BR>and विशेष sort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=335-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशाश्व|दशाश्वः
दशाश्व m. (-श्वः) A name of CHANDRA or the moon.<BR> E. दश ten, and अश्व a<BR>horse; driving ten horses in his carriage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=336-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशास्य|दशास्यः
दशास्य m. (-स्यः) A name of RAVANA.<BR> E. दश ten, and आस्य face, the ten-<BR>headed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=336-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशास्यजित्
दशास्यजित् m. (-जित्) RAMA.<BR> E. दशास्य as above, and जित् the conqueror.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=336-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशाह
दशाह n. (-हं) A period of ten days.<BR> E. दश, and अहन् a day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=336-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशेन्द्रिय
दशेन्द्रिय m. plu. (-याः) The ten organs of sense and action, viz, the<BR>skin, eye, tongue, nose, ear, organ of speech, hand, foot, anus,<BR>and pudendum.<BR> E. दश ten, and इन्द्रिय an organ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=336-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशिन्
दशिन् mfn. (-शी-शिनी-शि) Having ten of any thing.<BR>	 m. (-शी) The super-<BR>intendent of ten villages.<BR> E. दश, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=336-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशेन्धन|दशेंधन|दशेन्धनः
दशेन्धन m. (-नः) A lamp.<BR> E. दशा a wick, and इन्धन fuel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=336-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशेर|दशेरः
दशेर m. (-रः) A mischievous or venomous animal, a beast of prey, &c.<BR>E. दश् to bite, Uṇādi affix एरक् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=336-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशेरक|दशेरकः
दशेरक m. (-कः) A country destitute of water.<BR> E. कन् added to the pre-<BR>ceding: also दशेरुक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=336-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दष्ट
दष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>	 1. Bitten.<BR>	 2. Joining to, in contact with.<BR> E. दश्<BR>to bite, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=336-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दस
दस (इर्, उ) इरदसु r. 4th cl. (दस्यति)<BR>	 1. To lose.<BR>	 2. To throw or direct,<BR>to throw up or toss. r. 10th cl. (दसयते) To see. (इ) दसि r. 1st and<BR>10 cls. (दंसति, दंसयति)<BR>	 1. To bite or string.<BR>	 2. To see.<BR>	 3. To shine.<BR>दिवा० उत्क्षेपे, उपक्षये अपक्षये च अक० प० सक० सेट् । दर्शने दंशने च चु० आ०<BR>सक० सेट् इदित् । पक्षे भ्वा० प० ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=336-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दसन|दसनं
दसन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Throwing, tossing.<BR>	 2. Dismissing.<BR>	 3. Perishing.<BR> E. दस्<BR>to lose, affix ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=336-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दस्त
दस्त mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं)<BR>	 1. Lost, destroyed.<BR>	 2. Thrown, tossed.<BR>	 3. Sent<BR>away, dismissed.<BR> E. दस् to lose, &c. and क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=336-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दस्म|दस्मः
दस्म m. (-स्मः)<BR>	 1. A name of fire.<BR>	 2. A sacrificer, one who employs<BR>Brahmans in instituting a religious ceremony.<BR>	 3. A thief.<BR>	 4. A<BR>rogue, a knave.<BR> E. दस् to throw or send, मक् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=336-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दस्यु|दस्युः
दस्यु m. (-स्युः) An enemy.<BR>	 2. A thief.<BR>	 3. An oppressor, a violator, a<BR>committer of injustice, &c.<BR>	 4. A barbarian, an outcaste, or a Hindu<BR>who has become so by neglect of the essential rites.<BR> E. दस् to lose<BR>or be lost, Uṇādi affix युच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=336-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दस्युह
दस्युह m. (-हः) A name of Bali.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=336-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दस्र|दस्रं|दस्रः
दस्र m. (-स्रः)<BR>	 1. Either of the twin sons of AŚVINĪ, and physicians of<BR>Svarga; also collectively.<BR>	 m. du. (दस्रौ)<BR>	 2. An ass.<BR>	 n. (-स्रं) Thin<BR>rain, dew, frost.<BR> E. दस् to destroy, (disease, &c.) रक् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=336-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दस्रदेवता
दस्रदेवता f. (-ता) The lunar constellation AŚVINĪ.<BR> E. दस्र a divine physi-<BR>cian, and देवता a deity: he being the ruling genius of the asterism.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=336-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दस्रसू
दस्रसू f. (-सूः) A name of SANJNYA, a wife of the sun, and mother, ac-<BR>cording to one legend, of the twin physicians of INDRA'S heaven.<BR>E. दस्र as above, and सू mother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=336-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दह
दह (औ) दहौ r. 1st cl. (दहति) To burn or reduce to ashes. (इ) दहि r.<BR>10th cl. (दंहयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To shine.<BR>	 2. To burn. भ्वा० सक० प० अनिट् ।<BR>दीप्तौ अक० दाहे सक० चु० उभ० सेट् इदित् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=336-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दहत्
दहत् mfn. (-हन्-हन्ती-हत्) Scorching, burning.<BR> E. दह् to burn, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=336-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दहन|दहनं|दहनः
दहन n. (-नं) Burning, combustion.<BR>	 m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. Fire, or the deity AGNI.<BR>2. A bad man, one of evil dispositions.<BR>	 3. The marking nut plant.<BR>4. Lead wort, (Plumbago zeylanica, &c.)<BR> E. दह् to burn, affix ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=336-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दहनकेतन|दहनकेतनं|दहनकेतनः
दहनकेतन n. (-नं) Smoke.<BR> E. दहन fire, and केतन a banner or sign.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=336-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दहनप्रिया
दहनप्रिया f. (-या) A name of SWAHA, the wife of AGNI.<BR> E. दहन fire, and<BR>प्रिया the beloved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=336-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दहनबहुल
दहनबहुल m. (-लः) Fire.<BR> E. दहन, and बहुल much.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=336-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दहनाराति|दहनारातिः
दहनाराति m. (-तिः) Water.<BR> E. दहन, and अराति foe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=336-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दहनीय|दहनीयः
दहनीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) To be or what may be burnt, combustible. E.<BR>दह् to burn, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=336-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दहनोपल|दहनोपलः
दहनोपल m. (-लः) The Sun-gem, a crystal lens.<BR> E. दहन fire, and उपल a<BR>stone; fire-stone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=336-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दहर|दहरं|दहरः
दहर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Thin, small, fine.<BR>	 m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A rat, a mouse.<BR>	 2. A<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=336-b" target="_blank">Page336-b+ 60</a>]<BR>young animal.<BR>	 3. A younger brother.<BR>	 4. A child, an infant.<BR> E. दह्<BR>to burn, affix अर ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=336-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दह्यमान
दह्यमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Burnt, being burnt.<BR> E. दह् to burn, pass. v.<BR>शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=336-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दह्न
दह्न m. (-ह्नः)<BR>	 1. A name of AGNI or fire.<BR>	 2. The conflagration of forest.<BR>E. दह् to burn, रक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=336-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दा
दा (ण) दाण r. 1st cl. (यच्छति, or with सम् prefixed संयच्छते) also (डु ञ)<BR>डुदाञ् r. 3rd cl. (ददाति दत्ते) To give, to present. With आङ् prefixed<BR>(आदत्ते), To take, to accept or receive. With प्र, To give, to give to,<BR>With वि and आङ्, To open. With सम् and आङ्, To select. (प) दाप् r.<BR>2nd cl. (दाति) To cut. भ्वा० प० सक० सेट् ण इत् । जुहो० उभ० सक० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=336-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाक|दाकः
दाक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A donor, one who makes presents, especially to Brahm-<BR>ans.<BR>	 2. A sacrificer, one who pays all the expenses of the cere-<BR>mony, and employs the officiating priests.<BR> E. दा to give, क Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=336-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाक्षक|दाक्षकं
दाक्षक n. (-कं) A multitude of the descendants of DAKṢA.<BR> E. दक्ष, and<BR>and वुञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=336-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाक्षायण|दाक्षायणः
दाक्षायण mfn. (-णः-णी-णं) Of or relating of DAKṢA, a descendant, &c.<BR>n. (-णं) Gold, or a gold ornament, as an ear-ring, &c.<BR> E. दक्ष, and<BR>फक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=336-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाक्षायणिन्
दाक्षायणिन् mfn. (-णी-णिनी-णि) Having gold.<BR>	 m. (-णी) A Brahman student,<BR>wearing gold ear rings.<BR> E. दाक्षायण, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=336-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाक्षायिणी
दाक्षायिणी f. plu. (-यिण्यः) The twenty-seven lunar mansions, considered<BR>mythologically as the daughters of DAKṢA, and wives of the<BR>moon.<BR>	 f. sing. (-णी) A name of DURGĀ.<BR>	 2. The nymph and asterism<BR>ROHINI.<BR>	 3. A plant, commonly Danti, (Croton polyandrum.)<BR>	 4.<BR>A lunar asterism in general.<BR> E. दक्ष the son of BRAMHA, so called,<BR>फिञ् affix of descent, and ङीप् fem. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=336-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाक्षायिणीप
दाक्षायिणीप m. (-पः)<BR>	 1. CHANDRA.<BR>	 2. ŚIVA.<BR> E. दाक्षायिणी, and प who protects.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=336-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाक्षायिणीपति
दाक्षायिणीपति m. (-तिः) CHANDRA or the moon.<BR> E. दाक्षायिणी an asterism<BR>and पति husband: see the preceding; also similar compounds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=336-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाक्षायिणीरमण
दाक्षायिणीरमण m. (-णः) The moon: see the last.<BR> E. दाक्षायिणी, and रमण<BR>lover.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=336-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाक्षाय्य|दाक्षाय्यः
दाक्षाय्य m. (-य्यः) A vulture.<BR> E. दक्ष् to be quick, आय्य affix, and again,<BR>अण् affix of descent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=336-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाक्षिकन्था
दाक्षिकन्था f. (-न्था) A place in the north of India, in the country of<BR>Valhika or Balkh: see कन्थ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=336-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाक्षिकन्थीय
दाक्षिकन्थीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Produced or born, &c. in Dakshikantha; see<BR>the last,<BR> E. दाक्षिकन्थ, and छ affix; also similar compounds, as दाक्षि-<BR>नगरीय, दाक्षिग्रामीय ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=336-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाक्षिण
दाक्षिण mfn. (-णः-णी-णं) Relating or belonging to the south, to a gift to<BR>Brahmans, &c.<BR> E. दक्षिण, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=336-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाक्षिणात्य|दाक्षिणात्यः
दाक्षिणात्य mfn. (-त्यः-त्या-त्यं) Southerly, southern, belonging to or pro-<BR>duced in the south.<BR>	 m. (-त्र्यः) The cocoanut.<BR> E. दाक्षिण southern, and<BR>त्यक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=336-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाक्षिण्य|दाक्षिण्यं
दाक्षिण्य mfn. (-ण्यः-ण्या-ण्यं) Meriting a reward.<BR>	 n. (-ण्यं)<BR>	 1. Concord, har-<BR>mony, agreement.<BR>	 2. Cleverness, talent.<BR>	 3. Appeasing or restoring<BR>any one offended to good humour.<BR> E. दक्षिणा a gift, &c. affix ण्यत् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=336-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाक्षीपुत्त्र
दाक्षीपुत्त्र m. (-त्त्रः) The inspired grammarian PĀṆINI.<BR> E. दाक्षी a proper<BR>name, the mother of the saint, and पुत्त्र a son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=336-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाक्षेय|दाक्षेयः
दाक्षेय m. (-यः) A name of PĀṆINI.<BR> E. दाक्षी the mother of the Muni, and<BR>ढक् affix of descent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=336-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाक्ष्य|दाक्ष्यं
दाक्ष्य n. (-क्ष्यं) Cleverness, dexterity, ability.<BR> E. दक्ष, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=336-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाडक|दाडकः
दाडक m. (-कः) A tooth, a tusk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=336-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाडिम|दाडिमः
दाडिम subst.<BR>	 mfn. (-मः-मी-मं)<BR>	 1. The pomegranate tree, (or mf. the tree,<BR>n. the fruit.)<BR>	 2. Small cardamoms.<BR> E. दल् to divide, भावे घञ् दालेन<BR>निर्वृत्तः भावात् इमप् लस्य डः affix, the radical vowel made long, and<BR>ल changed to ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=336-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाडिमपुष्पक|दाडिमपुष्पकः
दाडिमपुष्पक m. (-कः) A medicinal plant, (Andersonia rohitaka.) E.<BR>दाडिम as above, पुष्प a flower, and कन् affix of resemblance; bearing<BR>flowers like those of the pomegranate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=336-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाडिमप्रिय|दाडिमप्रियः
दाडिमप्रिय m. (-यः) A parrot.<BR> E. दाडिम a pomegranate, and प्रिय fond of.<BR>दाडिर्म तत्फलं प्रियमस्य । शुकखगे, दाडिमप्रियमात्रे च ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=337-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाडिमभक्षण|दाडिमभक्षणः
दाडिमभक्षण m. (-णः) A parrot.<BR> E. दाडिम a pomegranate, and भक्षण<BR>eating. दाडिमं भक्षयितुं शीलमस्य ल्यु । शुकखगे दाडिमफलभक्षके । भक्ष-भावे ल्युट्<BR>दाडिमस्य भक्षणे न० ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=337-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाडिम्ब|दाडिंब|दाडिंबः|दाडिम्बः
दाडिम्ब m. (-म्बः) The pomegranate: see दाडिम ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=337-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाढा
दाढा f. (-ढा)<BR>	 1. A large tooth, a tusk.<BR>	 2. Wish, desire.<BR>	 3. A number,<BR>a multitude.<BR> E. दा to cut, ढ affix, fem. affix टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=337-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाढिका
दाढिका f. (-क्रा) The beard.<BR> E. दाढा a tooth, and कन् affix, implying<BR>propinquity, fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=337-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाण्ड|दांड
दाण्ड mfn. (-ण्डः-ण्डी-ण्डं)<BR>	 1. Relating to a stick or staff.<BR>	 2. Relating to<BR>punishment, &c.<BR> E. दण्ड a stick, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=337-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाण्डमाथिक
दाण्डमाथिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Churning with a straight stick or staff. E.<BR>दण्डमाथ a churning stick, ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=337-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाण्डाजिनिक|दांडाजिनिक|दाण्डाजिनिकः
दाण्डाजिनिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Fraudulent, dishonest.<BR> E. दण्डाजिन fraud,<BR>affix ठञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=337-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दात|दातं
दात mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Cut, divided.<BR> E. दा to cut, affix कर्मणि क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=337-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दातव्य
दातव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं) To be given, what may or ought to be given.<BR>E. दा to give, तव्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=337-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाति|दातिः
दाति f. (-तिः) Cutting, destroying.<BR> E. दा to cut, भावे क्तिच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=337-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दातृ
दातृ mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ) A donor, a giver, giving, bestowing.<BR> E. दा to give,<BR>तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=337-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दात्यूह|दात्यूहः
दात्यूह m. (-हः)<BR>	 1. A gallinule.<BR>	 2. The Chataka, a sort of cuckoo.<BR>	 2. A<BR>cloud.<BR> E. दाति destroying, ऊह to plan or arrange, affix अण्;<BR>also दात्यौह.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=337-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दात्यौह|दात्यौहः
दात्यौह mfn. (-हः-ही-हं) Of, relating to, or produced in the vehicle of a<BR>demon.<BR> E. दैत्य a demon, वह् to bear, affix घञ्, अण् added, and<BR>the first vowel, changed to आ by especial rule.)<BR>	 m. (-हः) A gallinule.<BR>E. See दात्यूह (the radical vowel being optionally changed,) with<BR>अण् affix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=337-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दात्र|दात्रं
दात्र n. (-त्रं) A sort of sickle, a large knife, a Da.<BR> E. दो to cut, त्रन्<BR>Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=337-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दात्व|दात्वः
दात्व m. (-त्वः) A giver, a donor.<BR> E. दा to give, त्वन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=337-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाद|दादः
दाद m. (-दः)<BR>	 1. A gift, a donation.<BR>	 2. Giving.<BR> E. दद to give, भावे घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=337-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दादद|दाददः
दादद m. (-दः) A donor, one who gives.<BR> E. दाद, and द who gives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=337-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दादिन्
दादिन् mfn. (-दी-दिनी-दि) Giving.<BR> E. दद to give, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=337-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाधिक|दाधिकं
दाधिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Made of or from Dadhi, or coagulated milk,<BR>mixed with it, sprinkled with it, &c.<BR> E. दधि, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=337-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दान|दानं|दानः
दान (उ) दानु r. 1st cl. irr. (दीदांसति-ते)<BR>	 1. To cut.<BR>	 2. To straighten or<BR>make straight.<BR>	 2. To be straight. भ्वा० उभ० सक० ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=337-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दान|दानं|दानः
दान n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Gift, giving, donation.<BR>	 2. The fluid that flows from the<BR>temples of an elephant in rut.<BR>	 3. Nourishing, cherishing.<BR>	 4. Purifi-<BR>cation.<BR>	 5. Cutting, dividing.<BR>	 6. A present, a special gift.<BR>	 7. Beat-<BR>ing, striking.<BR>	 8. Wild honey.<BR> E. दा to give, or दो to cut, affix ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=337-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दानकुल्या
दानकुल्या f. (-ल्या) The flow of an elephant's temporal ichor.<BR> E. दान, and<BR>कुल्या a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=337-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दानधर्म्म|दानधर्म|दानधर्मः|दानधर्म्मः
दानधर्म्म m. (-र्म्मः)<BR>	 1. Almsgiving, charity.<BR>	 2. The rules for making<BR>donations.<BR> E. दान, and धर्म्म virtue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=337-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दानपति|दानपतिः
दानपति m. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. A liberal or munificent man.<BR>	 2. A name of<BR>AKRURA, the kinsman of KṚṢṆA.<BR> E. दान giving, and पति eminent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=337-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दानप्रतिभाव्य
दानप्रतिभाव्य n. (-व्यं) Security for payment of a debt, &c.<BR> E. दान, and<BR>प्रतिभाव्य surety.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=337-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दानभिन्न
दानभिन्न mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं) Divided or made hostile by bribes.<BR> E. दान, and<BR>भिन्न broken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=337-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दानयोग्य
दानयोग्य mfn. (-ग्यः-ग्या-ग्यं) Fit for or meriting a donation.<BR> E. दान, and<BR>योग्य fit for.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=337-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दानव|दानवः
दानव m. (-वः) A demon, a Titan or giant.<BR> E. दनु the mother of these<BR>beings, and अण् affix of descent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=337-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दानवज्र|दानवज्रः
दानवज्र m. (-ज्रः) Vaiśya or man of the third tribe.<BR> E. दान, and वज्र<BR>diamond.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=337-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दानवर्षिन्
दानवर्षिन् m. (-र्षी)<BR>	 1. An elephant in rut.<BR>	 2. A liberal man.<BR> E. दान, and<BR>वर्षिन् showering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=337-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दानवारि|दानवारिः
दानवारि m. (-रिः) A deity.<BR> E. दानव a Titan, and अरि a foe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=337-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दानवीर|दानवीरः
दानवीर m. (-रः) A liberal man.<BR> E. दान, and वीर a hero.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=337-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दानव्यत्यास|दानव्यत्यासः
दानव्यत्यास m. (-सः) Gift under error, as giving to the wrong person,<BR>&c.<BR> E. दान, and व्यत्थास perversion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=337-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दानशील|दानशीलः
दानशील mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Liberal, munificent.<BR> E. दान giving, शील addict-<BR>ed to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=337-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दानशौण्ड|दानशौंड|दानशौण्डः
दानशौण्ड mfn. (-ण्डः-ण्डा-ण्डं) Liberal, bountiful, munificent.<BR> E. दान a gift,<BR>and शौण्ड intoxicated, attached to violently.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=337-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दानिन्
दानिन् mfn. (-नी-निनी-नि) Giving.<BR> E. दान, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=337-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दानीय|दानीयः
दानीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Worthy of having any thing given, or worthy or<BR>fit to be given.<BR>	 n. (-नं) Gift, donation.<BR> E. दा to give, अनीयर् affix<BR>of the future participle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=337-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दानु|दानुः
दानु m. (-नुः)<BR>	 1. A donor, a giver.<BR>	 2. A victor, a conqueror.<BR>	 3. Prosperity.<BR>4. Air, wind.<BR> E. दा to give, Uṇādi affix नु ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=337-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दान्त|दांत|दान्तः
दान्त mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं)<BR>	 1. Tamed, subdued, daunted.<BR>	 2. Bearing patient-<BR>ly privation, austerity, &c.<BR>	 3. Dental.<BR>	 m. (-न्तः)<BR>	 1. A donor, a giver.<BR>2. A well situated about the peak of a mountain.<BR> E. दम् to tame,<BR>to pacify, affix क्त, or दन्त a peak, &c. affix अण् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=337-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दान्ति|दांति|दांतिः|दान्तिः
दान्ति f. (-न्तिः)<BR>	 1. The patient endurance of religious austerities or<BR>privations.<BR>	 2. Subjection, humiliation.<BR> E. दम् to tame, &c. affix<BR>क्तिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=337-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दापयित्वा
दापयित्वा ind. Having fined.<BR> E. दा to give, causal form, क्त्वा aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=337-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दापित|दापितः
दापित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Condemned, adjudged, (the person.)<BR>	 2.<BR>assigned, awarded, (the thing.)<BR>	 3. The person to whom a fine, &c.<BR>is awarded or paid.<BR>	 4. Given, caused to be given.<BR>	 5. Purified. E.<BR>दा to give, in the causal form, and णिच् and क्रर्म्मणि क्त affix; also<BR>दायित ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=337-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाप्य
दाप्य mfn. (-प्यः-प्या-प्यं) To be fined, to be made to give or pay.<BR> E. दा to<BR>give, causal form, णिच् and कर्म्मणि यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=337-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाभ्य
दाभ्य mfn. (-भ्यः-भ्या-भ्यं) To be ordered, to be governed or ruled.<BR> E. दम् to<BR>order, ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=337-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दामन्
दामन् nf. (-म-मा) A string, a cord, a thread or rope.<BR> E. दो to cut or<BR>divide, &c. affix भावे करणे वा मनिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=337-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दामन
दामन mfn. (-नः-नी-नं) Relating to the Dona or Artemisia flower. E.<BR>दामन, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=337-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दामनपर्व्वन्|दामनपर्वन्
दामनपर्व्वन् n. (-र्व्व) The fourteenth of the light half of Chaitra, when<BR>the Dona flower is worshipped.<BR> E. दामन, and पर्व्व a holiday.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=337-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दामनी
दामनी f. (-नी) A string, a rope, especially for tying cattle.<BR> E. दामन् as<BR>above, अण् and ङीष् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=337-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दामलिप्त|दामलिप्तं
दामलिप्त n. (-प्तं) A country, the modern district of Tumlook. E. See<BR>तामलित, त being changed to द.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=337-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दामा
दामा f. (-मा) A rope, a string, a cord. E. See दामन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=337-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दामाञ्जन|दामांजन
दामाञ्जन n. (-नं) A foot-rope for horses, &c.<BR> E. दामा, and अञ्ज् to go,<BR>affix ल्युट्; also दामा, and अञ्चल end, दामाञ्चल, n. (-लं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=337-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दामोदर|दामोदरः
दामोदर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A name of KṚṢṆA.<BR>	 2. A Jina of the past age. E.<BR>दाम a rope, and उदर a belly; YASODHA his foster mother having<BR>in vain passed the folds of a rope round his body, whilst a child,<BR>to keep him in confinement. दाम बन्धनसाधनं उदरे यस्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=337-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाम्भिक|दांभिक|दाम्भिकः
दाम्भिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Hypocritical.<BR>	 m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A hypocrite.<BR>	 2. A<BR>kind of crane, (Ardea nivea.)<BR> E. दम्भ, and ठक् aff. दम्भेन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=337-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाय|दायः
दाय (ऋ) दायृ r. 1st cl. (दायते) To give. भ्वा० आ० सक० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=337-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाय|दायः
दाय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. Gift, donation.<BR>	 2. A special gift, as a nuptial present,<BR>alms to a student at his initiation, &c.<BR>	 3. Portion, inheritance.<BR>4. Loss, destruction.<BR>	 5. Breaking, dividing.<BR>	 6. A place, a site.<BR>7. Irony.<BR> E. दा to give, in the passive form, affix ण; that which<BR>is given; or दो to cut, &c. that which is divided. or दाय् to give,<BR>affix कर्मणि भावे वा घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=337-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दायक|दायकः
दायक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Liberal, giving, a donor.<BR> E. दा to give, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=337-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दायबन्धु|दायबंधु|दायबन्धुः
दायबन्धु m. (-न्धुः) A brother.<BR> E. दाय portion, बन्धु a friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=338-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दायभाग|दायभागः
दायभाग m. (-गः) Partition of heritage, apportioning inheritance, &c.<BR>E. दाय heritage, and भाग a part or portion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=338-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दायविभाग|दायविभागः
दायविभाग m. (-गः) Portioning or portion of inheritance, division of<BR>property amongst different heirs.<BR> E. दाय heritage, and विभाग a<BR>part or portion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=338-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दायाद|दायादः
दायाद m. (-दः)<BR>	 1. A son.<BR>	 2. A kinsman, near or remote.<BR>	 3. An heir.<BR>	 f.<BR>(-दा-दी) A daughter, an heiress.<BR> E. दाय a portion, आङ् prefixed to<BR>दा to take, affix क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=338-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दायादव
दायादव m. (-वः) An heir, a kinsman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=338-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दायापवर्त्तन|दायापवर्तन
दायापवर्त्तन n. (-नं) Privation, a forfeiture of property.<BR> E. दाय, and अप-<BR>वर्त्तन taking away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=338-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दायित|दायितः
दायित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Condemned, sentenced.<BR>	 2. Awarded, adjudged.<BR>3. The person to whom any thing is awarded, &c. see दापित. E.<BR>दायं दानं करोति दायि-कर्मणि क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=338-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दार|दारः
दार m. plu. (-राः) A wife.<BR> E. दॄ to take, to tear, (a husband,) affix अच्;<BR>also दारा । दारयति भ्रातॄन् दॄ-णिच्-दारि कर्त्तरि अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=338-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दारक|दारकः
दारक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) A breaker, a tearer.<BR>	 m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A son.<BR>	 2. A<BR>child, an infant or young animal.<BR>	 3. The charioteer of VIṢṆU.<BR>	 4.<BR>A village-hog.<BR>	 f. (-रिका)<BR>	 1. A daughter.<BR>	 2. A whore.<BR> E. दॄ to tear,<BR>affix ण्वुल् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=338-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दारकर्म्मन्|दारकर्मन्
दारकर्म्मन् n. (-र्म्म) Marriage.<BR> E. दार a wife, and कर्म्मन् a business; also<BR>दारक्रिया ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=338-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दारण|दारणं
दारण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. The clearing nut plant, (Strychnos potatorum.)<BR>	 2.<BR>Tearing, rending, dividing.<BR> E. दॄ to tear, affixes णिच् and युच् करणे<BR>ल्युट् वा ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=338-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दारद|दारदः
दारद m. (-दः)<BR>	 1. A sort of poison, one brought from the country<BR>named Darad.<BR>	 2. Quicksilver.<BR>	 3. Vermilion.<BR>	 4. The ocean.<BR> E. दरद a<BR>country, &c. affix अण् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=338-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दारपरिग्रह|दारपरिग्रहः
दारपरिग्रह m. (-हः) Marriage.<BR> E. दार, and परिग्रह taking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=338-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दारव
दारव mfn. (-वः-वी-वं) Wooden, made of wood.<BR> E. दारु, and अञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=338-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दारबलिभुज्
दारबलिभुज् m. (-भुक्)<BR>	 1. The Vaka, a sort of crane.<BR>	 2. A crow.<BR>	 3. A<BR>sparrow.<BR> E. दार a wife or female, बलि food, and भुज् who eats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=338-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दारसङ्ग्रह|दारसंग्रह|दारसंग्रहः
दारसङ्ग्रह m. (-हः) Marrying, marriage.<BR> E. दार, and सङ्ग्रह taking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=338-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दारा
दारा f. (-रा) A wife: see दार ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=338-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाराधीन
दाराधीन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Dependent upon a wife, subject to her, &c. E.<BR>दार, and अधीन subject.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=338-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दारि|दारिः
दारि f. (-रिः) Cutting, tearing, dividing.<BR> E. दॄ to tear, affixes णिच् and<BR>इन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=338-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दारिकादान
दारिकादान n. (-नं) Giving a daughter in marriage.<BR> E. दारिका, and<BR>दान gift.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=338-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दारित|दारितः
दारित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Torn, divided.<BR> E. दॄ to tear, to divide, affix क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=338-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दारिद्र|दारिद्रं
दारिद्र n. (-द्रं) Poverty.<BR> E. दरिद्र and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=338-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दारिद्र्य|दारिद्र्यं
दारिद्र्य n. (-द्र्यं) Poverty, indigence.<BR> E. दरिद्र poor, ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=338-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दारिन्
दारिन् m. (-री)<BR>	 1. A husband.<BR>	 2. A polygamist.<BR> E. दार, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=338-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दारु|दारुः
दारु mfn. (-रुः-र्वी-रु)<BR>	 1. Liberal, munificent, a giver, a donor.<BR>	 2. An<BR>artist.<BR>	 3. Tearing, rending, a tearer.<BR>	 mn. (-रुः-रु) Wood, timber.<BR>	 n.<BR>(-रु)<BR>	 1. A sort of pine, (Pinus devadaru.)<BR>	 2. Brass.<BR> E. दॄ to tear or<BR>split, Uṇādi affix उण्, or दा to give, रु Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=338-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दारुक|दारुकं|दारुकः
दारुक m. (-कः) A proper name, the charioteer of KṚṢṆA.<BR> E. दॄ to<BR>tear (his foes), affix उकञ्.<BR>	 n. (-कं) A pine, (Pinus devadaru.)<BR>	 f.<BR>(-का) A doll, a puppet.<BR> E. दारु wood, and स्वार्थे क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=338-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दारुकदली
दारुकदली f. (-ली) A wild uneatable plantain.<BR> E. दारु, and कदली a plan-<BR>tain. दारु इव कठिना कदली ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=338-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दारुगर्भा
दारुगर्भा f. (-र्भा) A doll, a wooden puppet.<BR> E. दारु wood, गर्भ place of<BR>birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=338-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दारुज|दारुजः
दारुज mfn. (-जः-जा-जं) Made of wood, wooden, &c.<BR>	 m. (-जः) A kind of<BR>drum.<BR> E. दारु wood, and ज produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=338-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दारुण|दारुणः
दारुण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Horrible, terrific, frightful. fearful.<BR>	 2. Dread-<BR>ful, shocking.<BR>	 mn. (-णः-णं) Horror, horribleness.<BR>	 m. (-णः) Lead-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=338-b" target="_blank">Page338-b+ 60</a>]<BR>wort, (Plumbago zeylanica.)<BR> E. दॄ to tear to pieces, Uṇādi affix<BR>उनन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=338-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दारुनिशा
दारुनिशा f. (-शा) A plant, (Curcuma zanthorrhizon.)<BR> E. दारु wood, and<BR>निशा turmeric.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=338-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दारुपुत्त्रिका
दारुपुत्त्रिका f. (-का) A wooden doll or puppet.<BR> E. दारु wood, and पुत्त्रिका<BR>an infant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=338-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दारुमय
दारुमय mfn. (-यः-यी-यं) Made of wood, woody, wooden.<BR> E. दारु, and<BR>मयट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=338-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दारुवह
दारुवह mfn. (-हः-हा-हं) What bears or carries timber.<BR> E. दारु, and वह<BR>what bears.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=338-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दारुस्त्री
दारुस्त्री f. (-स्त्री) A doll.<BR> E. दारु wood, and स्त्री a woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=338-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दारुहरिद्रा
दारुहरिद्रा f. (-द्रा) A kind of curcuma, (C. zanthorrhizon.)<BR> E. दारु wood,<BR>and हरिद्रा turmeric.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=338-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दारुहस्तक|दारुहस्तकः
दारुहस्तक m. (-कः) A wooden ladle.<BR> E. दारु wood, हस्त hand, and कन्<BR>affix of resemblance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=338-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दारोपसङ्ग्रह|दारोपसंग्रह|दारोपसंग्रहः
दारोपसङ्ग्रह m. (-हः) Marrying, taking a wife.<BR> E. दार, and उपसङ्ग्रह<BR>taking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=338-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दार्घसत्र|दार्घसत्रः
दार्घसत्र(-त्रः-त्री-त्रं) Performing a long continued sacrifice, &c.<BR> E. दीर्घसत्र<BR>a particular sacrifice, अण् affix of relation, and the vowel changed<BR>to आ by special rule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=338-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दार्ढ्य|दार्ढ्यं
दार्ढ्य n. (-र्ढ्यं) Hardness, fixedness, stability.<BR> E. दृढ hard, firm, ष्यञ्<BR>affix of the abstract. दृढस्य भावः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=338-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दार्द्दुर|दार्दुर|दार्दुरं|दार्दुरः|दार्द्दुरं
दार्द्दुर mfn. (-रः-री-रं) Relating to a cloud, a frog, &c.<BR>	 n. (-रं)<BR>	 1. A conch,<BR>the valve of which opens to the right.<BR>	 2. Lac.<BR>	 3. Water.<BR> E. दर्द्दुर a<BR>mountain, &c. अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=338-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दार्व्वट|दार्वट|दार्वटं|दार्व्वटं
दार्व्वट n. (-टं) A court or council-house.<BR> E. दारु timber, and अट् to go or<BR>be, affix अच् । दारु इव निश्चलतया निरुपणीयविषयनिश्चयार्थम् अटन्ति अत्र अट-<BR>घञर्थे क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=338-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दार्व्वण्ड|दार्वण्ड|दार्वंड|दार्वण्डः|दार्व्वण्डः
दार्व्वण्ड m. (-ण्डः) A peacock.<BR> E. दारु wood, and अण्ड an egg. दारु इव<BR>कठिनः अण्डोऽस्य । मयूरे ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=338-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दार्व्वाघाट|दार्वाघाट|दार्वाघाटः|दार्व्वाघाटः
दार्व्वाघाट m. (-टः) The woodpecker.<BR> E. दारु wood, हन् to injure, with<BR>आङ् prefixed, and अण् affix, घ is substituted for ह, and ट for न in<BR>place of त; also with त, दार्व्वाघात ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=338-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दार्व्वाघात|दार्वाघात|दार्व्वाघातः
दार्व्वाघात m. (-तः) The woodpecker: see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=338-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दार्व्विका|दार्विका
दार्व्विका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. A sort of collyrium prepared from an infusion of<BR>the Curcuma zanthorrhizon.<BR>	 2. A sort of potherb: see गोजिह्वा. E.<BR>दार्व्वी as below, and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=338-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दार्व्विपत्रिका|दार्विपत्रिका
दार्व्विपत्रिका f. (-का) Gojihwa, a sort of wild potherb.<BR> E. दार्व्वी Curcuma,<BR>पत्र a leaf, and ठन् aff. दार्व्व्या दारुहरिद्रायाः पत्रमिव पत्रमस्ति अस्याः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=338-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दार्व्वी|दार्वी
दार्व्वी f. (-र्व्वी)<BR>	 1. A sort of Curcuma, (C. zanthorrhizon.)<BR>	 2. A kind of<BR>pine: see देवदारु.<BR>	 3. Turmeric.<BR>	 4. Gojihwa, a potherb.<BR>	 5. A col-<BR>lyrium extracted from an infusion of the Curcuma zanthorrhizon.<BR>E. दॄ to tear or dissipate (disease,) उण् affix fem. affix ङीष्ः see<BR>दारु ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=338-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दार्षद|दार्षदः
दार्षद mfn. (-दः-दी-दं)<BR>	 1. Ground on a flat stone, (meal, &c.)<BR>	 2. Stony,<BR>of stone, mineral.<BR> E. दृषद् a stone or slab on which condiments<BR>are prepared, affix अण् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=338-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाल|दालं|दालः
दाल n. (-लं) Wild or unprepared honey.<BR>	 m. (-लः) A sort of grain, (Pas-<BR>palum frumentaceum.)<BR>	 f. (-ला) Colocynth.<BR> E. दल a sheath, affix<BR>अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=338-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दालन|दालनं
दालन n. (-नं) Toothache.<BR> E. दल् to tear, causal v. णिच् and ल्यु affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=338-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दालव|दालवः
दालव m. (-बः) A sort of poison.<BR> E. दल् to tear. in the causal form,<BR>अन् affix, and व added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=338-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दालिम|दालिमः
दालिम m. (-मः) The pomegranate: see दाडिम ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=338-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाल्मि|दाल्मिः
दाल्मि m. (-ल्मिः) A name of INDRA.<BR> E. दल् to tear or split, (mountains,)<BR>णिच् and मि affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=338-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाव|दावः
दाव m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. A forest.<BR>	 2. A forest on fire.<BR>	 3. Fire in general.<BR>	 4.<BR>Heat.<BR> E. दु to go or run, affix कर्त्तरि णः see दव ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=338-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दावाग्नि|दावाग्निः
दावाग्नि m. (-ग्निः) The conflagration of a forest.<BR> E. दाव a forest, and<BR>अग्नि fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=338-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दावानल|दावानलः
दावानल m. (-लः) Fire in a forest.<BR> E. दाव, and अनल fire: see the pre-<BR>ceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=339-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाविक|दाविकः
दाविक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Belonging, relating to, or produced in or<BR>near the river Devika or Deva.<BR> E. देविका the Deva, अण् affix,<BR>deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=339-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाश|दाशः
दाश (ऋ) दाशृ r. 1st cl. (दाशति-ते) 10th cl. (दाशयति-ते) To give 5th cl.<BR>(दाश्नोति) To hurt, to injure or kill: see दास । भ्वा० उभ० सक० सेट् ।<BR>चुरा० उभ० । स्वादि० प० ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=339-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाश|दाशः
दाश m. (-शः)<BR>	 1. A fisherman, the son of a Nishada by a woman of the<BR>Ayogava caste.<BR>	 2. A servant.<BR>	 f. (-शी)<BR>	 1. A female slave, &c.<BR> E. दाशृ<BR>to give, affix घञ् । see दास ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=339-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाशनन्दिनी|दाशनंदिनी
दाशनन्दिनी f. (-नी) The mother of VYASA: see दासनन्दिनी ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=339-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाशपुर|दाशपुरं
दाशपुर n. (-रं) A fragrant grass, (Cyperus rotundus:) see दशपुर; also<BR>दाशपूर, n. (-रं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=339-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाशरथ|दाशरथः
दाशरथ m. (-थः) A name of RAMA.<BR> E. दशरथ the father of RAMA,<BR>and अण् patronymic affix; also with इञ् affix दाशरथि m. (-थिः) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=339-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाशार्ह|दाशार्हः
दाशार्ह mfn. (-र्हः-र्ही-र्हं) Produced in Dasarha, (the country.)<BR>	 m. (-र्हः)<BR>A name of KṚṢṆA.<BR> E. दशार्ह a country or one of KṚṢṆA'S an-<BR>cestors, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=339-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाशेय|दाशेयः
दाशेय m. (-यः) A servant.<BR>	 f. (-यी) The mother of VYASA: see दासेय. E.<BR>दाश्या धीवर्य्या अपत्यम् ढक् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=339-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाशेर|दाशेरः
दाशेर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A servant.<BR>	 2. A camel: see दासेर.<BR> E. दास्या अपत्यम् ढ्रक् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=339-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाशेरक|दाशेरकः
दाशेरक m. (-कः) Malwa, the province. दाशेरकप्रधानः देशः संज्ञायां कन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=339-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाश्व|दाश्वः
दाश्व mfn. (-श्वः-श्वा-श्वं) Liberal, giving, a doner, a giver.<BR> E. दाश to give,<BR>वन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=339-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाश्वत्
दाश्वत् mfn. (-श्वन्-श्वती-श्वत्) Liberal, munificent.<BR> E. दा to give, श्वत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=339-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दास|दासः
दास (ऋ) दासृ r. 1st cl. (दासति-ते) To give; also दाश r. 5th cl. (दास्नोति)<BR>To hurt, to injure, to wound or kill: this and दाश, in the last<BR>sense, are restricted by some authorities to the Vedas. भ्वा० उभ०<BR>सक० सेट् । स्वा० पर० ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=339-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दास|दासः
दास m. (-सः)<BR>	 1. A fisherman.<BR>	 2. A servant, a slave.<BR>	 3. A Śūdra or man<BR>of the fourth tribe.<BR>	 4. A Śūdra affix or appellation.<BR>	 5. A person<BR>to whom it is proper to make gifts.<BR>	 6. A sage, one to whom it is<BR>proper nature of the soul is known.<BR>	 f. (-सी) A female servant or<BR>slave.<BR>	 2. The wife of a slave, a fisherman or Śūdra.<BR>	 3. A harlot.<BR>4. A plant, a sort of Barleria.<BR> E. दास् to give, affix घञ्, to whom<BR>wages, &c. are given; also दाश; otherwise, दश or दंश to bite, &c.<BR>Uṇādi affix ठन्, and the short vowel and nasal changed to आ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=339-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दासत्व
दासत्व n. (-त्वं) Slavery, servitude.<BR> E. दास, and त्व affix,; also with तल्<BR>affix, दासता ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=339-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दासनन्दिनी
दासनन्दिनी f. (-नी) A name of SATYAVATI, the mother of the poet<BR>VYASA.<BR> E. दास a fisherman, and नन्दिनी daughter; also दाशनन्दिनी ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=339-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दासदासी
दासदासी f. (-सी) The female slave of a slave.<BR> E. दास, and दासी the female.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=339-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दासपूर|दासपूरं
दासपूर n. (-रं) A fragrant grass, (Cyperus rotundus.)<BR> E. दास a fisher-<BR>man, and पूर what nourishes, from पृ to nourish, affix क also<BR>दाशपूर ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=339-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दासिका
दासिका f. (-का) A female servant or slave.<BR> E. कन् added to दासी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=339-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दासित
दासित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Thrown, lost.<BR>	 2. Lost, destroyed.<BR> E. दस् to<BR>toss, affix क्त, इट् inserted, and the vowel made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=339-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दासीपुत्त्र
दासीपुत्त्र m. (-त्त्रः)<BR>	 1. The son of a slave.<BR>	 2. A bastard.<BR> E. दासी a female<BR>slave, and पुत्त्र a son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=339-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दासीसभ|दासीसभं
दासीसभ n. (-भं) A multitude of female slaves.<BR> E. दासी a female slave.<BR>and सभा an assembly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=339-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दासेय|दासेयः
दासेय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Born of a slave, &c.<BR>	 m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. A servant or slave.<BR>2. A fisherman.<BR>	 f. (-यी) The mother of VYASA.<BR> E. दास as above,<BR>affix ढक्; also दाशेय ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=339-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दासेर|दासेरः
दासेर mfn. (-रः-री-रं) Born or sprung from a servant or slave.<BR>	 m. (-रः)<BR>1. A servant.<BR>	 2. A fisherman.<BR>	 3. A camel.<BR> E. दास as above, and ढ्रक्<BR>affix; also दाशेर, or with कन् added दासेरक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=339-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दास्य|दास्यं
दास्य n. (-स्यं) Slavery, servitude.<BR> E. दास a slave, affix ष्यञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=339-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाह|दाहः
दाह m. (-हः)<BR>	 1. Burning, combustion.<BR>	 2. Morbid heat.<BR>	 3. Actual or po-<BR>tential cautery.<BR> E. दह् to burn, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=339-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाहक|दाहकः
दाहक mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>	 1. Burning, inflammatory.<BR>	 3. Cauterising, caus-<BR>tic.<BR>	 m. (-कः) A plant, (Plumbago zeylanica.)<BR> E. दह् to burn, and<BR>ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=339-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाहज्वर|दाहज्वरः
दाहज्वर m. (-रः) Inflamatory fever.<BR> E. दाह, and ज्वर fever.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=339-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाहन|दाहनं
दाहन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Burning, reducing to ashes.<BR>	 2. Cauterising.<BR> E. दह् to<BR>burn. ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=339-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाहवत्|दाहवन्त्
दाहवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Burning, heated on fire.<BR> E. दाह, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=339-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाहसर|दाहसरः
दाहसर m. (-रः) A place where dead bodies are burnt.<BR> E. दाह, and सृ to<BR>go or be, affix अप्; also with असुन्, affix दाहसरस्, m. (-सः) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=339-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाहहरण|दाहहरणं
दाहहरण n. (-णं) The root of a fragrant grass, (Andropogon muricatum.)<BR>E. दाह heat, and हरण removing; this root being woven into<BR>screens, and kept wet, for the purpose of excluding or tempering<BR>the hot winds. दाहो ह्रियते अनेन हृ-ल्युट् and णिच् कर्त्तरि ल्यु वा ।<BR>वीरणमूले ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=339-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाह्य
दाह्य mfn. (-ह्यः-ह्या-ह्यं) To be burnt, inflammable.<BR> E. दह् to burn,<BR>ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=339-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिक्क|दिक्कः
दिक्क m. (-क्कः) A young elephant.<BR> E. दिक् an imitative sound, and क who<BR>utters, some books have धिक्क, and others विक्क in place of this<BR>word. दिक्षु कायति कै-क । विंशतिवर्षवयस्के करिशावके ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=339-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिक्कर|दिक्करः
दिक्कर mfn. (-रः-री-रं) Young, juvenile.<BR>	 f. (-री) A young woman.<BR> E. दिक्<BR>inflection of दिश् place, कर who makes; who is restlessly active,<BR>changing place continually.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=339-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिक्पति|दिक्पतिः
दिक्पति m. (-तिः) A regent of a quarter of the universe, as the sun of<BR>the east; Saturn of the west; Mars of the south; Mircury of<BR>the north; Venus of the south-east; Rahu of the south-west;<BR>Chandra of the north-west; and Jupiter of the north-east.<BR> E. दिश्,<BR>and पति master: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=339-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिक्पाल|दिक्पालः
दिक्पाल m. (-लः) A regent of a quarter of the universe, INDRA of the<BR>east; AGNI of the south-east; Yama of the south; NAIRRIT of<BR>the south-west; VARUṆA of the west; MARUTA of the north-west;<BR>KUVERA of the north; ISANA of the south-east.<BR> E. दिश्, and पाल<BR>who protects: this word applicable to the Dikpatis, (see the last,)<BR>as that term is to these also.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=339-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिक्शूल|दिक्शूलं
दिक्शूल n. (-लं) An inauspicious planetary conjunction, as for the Sun<BR>and Venus to be in the west, &c.<BR> E. दिश्, and शूल a spear or stake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=339-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिगन्त|दिगंत|दिगन्तः
दिगन्त m. (-न्तः) The horizon.<BR> E. दिक्, and अन्त end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=339-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिगन्तर|दिगंतर
दिगन्तर n. (-रं) Space, the atmosphere.<BR> E. दिक्, and अन्तर interval.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=339-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिगन्तराल
दिगन्तराल n. (-लं) The sky, the atmosphere, space.<BR> E. दिक्, and अन्तराल<BR>interval.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=339-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिगम्बर|दिगंबर|दिगम्बरः
दिगम्बर mfn. (-रः-रा-री-रं)<BR>	 1. Naked, unclad, unclothed.<BR>	 2. Dressed in,<BR>or enveloped by the atmosphere, clouds, &c.<BR>	 m. (-रं)<BR>	 1. A Bauddha<BR>mendicant, wearing coloured clothes, or going naked.<BR>	 2. Any<BR>mendicant not wearing clothes.<BR>	 3. Darkness.<BR>	 4. A name of ŚIVA,<BR>(from his being naked.)<BR>	 5. A Jain of one great division, which<BR>represents the images of their saints, either naked or plainly<BR>attired.<BR>	 f. (-री) A name of DURGĀ.<BR> E. दिक् inflection of दिश् space,<BR>अम्बर vestment; whose only garment is the atmosphere. दिक् शून्य-<BR>मम्बरं यस्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=339-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिग्गज|दिग्गजः
दिग्गज m. (-जः) An elephant of a quarter or point of the compass, one<BR>of eight attached to the north, north-east, &c. supporting the<BR>globe.<BR> E. दिश् a quarter, and गज an elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=339-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिग्दाह|दिग्दाहः
दिग्दाह m. (-हः) Preternatural redness of the horizon, as if on fire. E.<BR>दिश्, and दाह burning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=339-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिग्ध|दिग्धः
दिग्ध mfn. (-ग्धः-ग्धा-ग्धं) Smeared, anointed.<BR>	 m. (-ग्धः)<BR>	 1. A poison-<BR>ed arrow.<BR>	 2. A name of fire.<BR>	 3. Oil, unguent, oily substance.<BR>4. A tale, true or false.<BR> E. दिह् to smear or anoint, affix क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=339-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिग्वासस्
दिग्वासस् mfn. (-साः-साः-सः) Naked.<BR>	 m. (-साः) A name of ŚIVA.<BR> E. दिक्<BR>for दिश् space, and वासस् vesture: see दिगम्बर ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=339-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिग्विजय|दिग्विजयः
दिग्विजय m. (-यः) Subjugation of an extensive country, either in arms or<BR>controversy.<BR> E. दिश्, and विजय triumph.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=340-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिग्विजयक्रम
दिग्विजयक्रम m. (-मः) Invasion, going forth to conquer the world. E.<BR>दिग्विजय, and क्रम march.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=340-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिग्विभाग
दिग्विभाग m. (-गः) A quarter or point of the compass.<BR> E. दिक्, and विभाग<BR>division.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=340-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिग्विभावित
दिग्विभावित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Famous, celebrated, known in all quarters.<BR>E. दिक्, and विभावित made known.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=340-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिग्व्यापिन्
दिग्व्यापिन् mfn. (-पी-पिनी-पि) Spreading through all space.<BR> E. दिक्, and<BR>व्यापिन् what pervades.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=340-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिङ्क|दिङ्कः
दिङ्क m. (-ङ्कः) A nit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=340-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिङ्मण्डल|दिङ्मंडल
दिङ्मण्डल n. (-लं) The circle of the heaven, or any point of the compass.<BR>E. दिश्, and मण्डल sphere.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=340-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिङ्मुख
दिङ्मुख mfn. (-खः-खी-खं) Looking to, or facing any point or quarter.<BR>	 n.<BR>(-खं) Any part of the heavens.<BR> E. दिश्, and मुख face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=340-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिङ्नाग|दिङ्नागः
दिङ्नाग m. (-गः) An elephant of the quarter: see दिग्गज.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=340-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दित|दितं
दित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Cut, torn, divided.<BR> E. दी to cut, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=340-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिति|दितिः
दिति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. One of the wives of KAŚYAPA, and mother of the Dai-<BR>tyas or infernal race, opposer of the gods.<BR>	 2. Cutting, splitting,<BR>dividing.<BR>	 m. (-तिः) A king, a prince.<BR> E. दो to cut, affix क्तिच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=340-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दितिज|दितिजः
दितिज m. (-जः) An Asura, a sort of Titan or giant.<BR> E. दिति as above,<BR>and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=340-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दितिसूत
दितिसूत m. (-तः)<BR>	 1. Titan or giant.<BR> E. दिति as above, and सुत a son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=340-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दित्य|दित्यः
दित्य m. (-त्यः)<BR>	 1. Titan, a demon or giant.<BR> E. दिति as above, affix<BR>यत्, and the vowel unchanged: see दैत्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=340-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दित्सा
दित्सा f. (त्सा) Desire or purpose to give.<BR> E. दा to give, desid. form,<BR>अ and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=340-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दित्सु
दित्सु mfn. (-त्सुः-त्सुः-त्सु) Wishing to give.<BR> E. दा to give, desid. form,<BR>affs. सन् and उ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=340-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिदृक्षमाण
दिदृक्षमाण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Wishing to see.<BR> E. दृश् to see, desid. form,<BR>शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=340-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिदृक्षा
दिदृक्षा f. (-क्षा) Desire or wish to see.<BR> E. दृश् to see, desid. form, सन् भावे<BR>अ and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=340-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिदृक्षु
दिदृक्षु mfn. (-क्षुः-क्षुः-क्षु) Desirous of seeing.<BR> E. दृश् to see, desid. form,<BR>सन् and उ affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=340-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिदृक्षावत्
दिदृक्षावत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Wishing to see.<BR> E. दिदृक्षा, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=340-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिदेविषत्
दिदेविषत् mfn. (-षन्-षन्ती-षत्) Wishing to play or sport.<BR> E. दिव् to play,<BR>desid. form, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=340-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिद्युत्
दिद्युत् mfn. (-द्युत्) Shining, blazing, bright.<BR> E. द्यु to shine, शतृ affix,<BR>intens. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=340-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिद्योतिषु
दिद्योतिषु mfn. (-षुः-षुः-षु) Wishing to shine.<BR> E. द्यू to shine, desid. form,<BR>उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=340-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिधक्षमाण
दिधक्षमाण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Wishing to burn.<BR> E. दह to burn, desid. v.<BR>शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=340-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिधक्षयत्
दिधक्षयत् mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्) Desiring to burn.<BR> E. दह् to burn, desid. v. शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=340-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिधि|दिधिः
दिधि f. (-धिः) Firmness, stability, fixed state of mind or being.<BR> E. धा<BR>to have, affix कि, and the root reiterated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=340-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिधिषाय्य|दिधिषाय्यः
दिधिषाय्य m. (-य्यः) A pretended friend, an intimate.<BR> E. धा to have, Uṇādi<BR>affix आय्य, the root reduplicated, इट् and षुक् augments.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=340-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिधिषु|दिधिषुः
दिधिषु m. (-षुः) The second husband of a woman twice married.<BR>	 f. (-षुः)<BR>A virgin widow remarried.<BR> E. धा to have (sin), or धिष् to be re-<BR>proached, root reduplicate, affix कु or कू; in the first case, इट् and<BR>षुक् augments; also दिधिषू.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=340-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिधिषू
दिधिषू f. (-षूः)<BR>	 1. A virgin widow remarried: see the preceding; also<BR>दिधीषू.<BR>	 2. An elder sister unmarried, whose junior is a bride.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-षूः)<BR>	 1. The husband of a woman married a second time: see दिधिषु.<BR>2. Instability, want of firmness.<BR> E. दिधि firmness, षो to abandon, कू<BR>Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=340-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिधिषुपति
दिधिषुपति m. (-तिः) The husband of a woman remarried.<BR> E. दिधिषू as<BR>above, and पति a husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=340-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिन|दिनं|दिनः
दिन mn. (-नः-नं) A day.<BR> E. दी to waste, नक् affix, and the vowel made<BR>short; or दो to destroy, (darkness,) किनन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=340-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिनकर|दिनकरः
दिनकर m. (-रः) The sun.<BR> E. दिन day, and कर who makes, कृ-ट ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=340-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिनकरात्मजा
दिनकरात्मजा f. (-जा) The Yamuna or Jumna river.<BR> E. दिनकर the sun,<BR>and आत्मजा daughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=340-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिनकृत्
दिनकृत् m. (-कृत्) The sun.<BR> E. दिन, and कृत् who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=340-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिनकेशव|दिनकेशवः
दिनकेशव m. (-वः) Darkness.<BR> E. दिन day, and केशव hair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=340-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिनज्योतिस्
दिनज्योतिस् n. (-तिः) Sunshine, day-light.<BR> E. दिन day, and ज्योतिस् night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=340-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिनदुःखित|दिनदुःखितः
दिनदुःखित m. (-तः) The ruddy goose.<BR> E. दिन day, and दुःखित pained;<BR>regretting throughout the day, the approaching nocturnal separa-<BR>tion from its female.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=340-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिनप्रणी
दिनप्रणी m. (-णीः) The sun.<BR> E. दिन day, and प्रणी leading, bringing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=340-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिनबल|दिनबलः
दिनबल m. (-लः) A name of certain signs of the zodiac, the fifth to the<BR>eighth; also the eleventh and twelfth.<BR> E. दिन, and बल strong.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=340-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिनमणि|दिनमणिः
दिनमणि m. (-णिः) The sun.<BR> E. दिन day, and मणि jewel or gem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=340-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिनमूर्द्धन्
दिनमूर्द्धन् m. (-र्द्धा) The eastern mountain, behind which the sun is sup-<BR>posed to rise.<BR> E. दिन day, and मूर्द्धन् the forehead.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=340-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिनांश|दिनांशः
दिनांश m. (-शः) A portion of the day, a watch, an hour, or the three<BR>seasons of dawn, moon, and evening.<BR> E. दिन and अंश part or portion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=340-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिनादि|दिनादिः
दिनादि m. (-दिः) Dawn, day-break.<BR> E. दिन, and आदि commencement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=340-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिनान्त|दिनांत|दिनान्तः
दिनान्त m. (-न्तः) Evening, sunset, close of day.<BR> E. दिन day, and अन्त<BR>end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=340-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिनान्तक|दिनान्तकः
दिनान्तक m. (-कः) Darkness.<BR> E. दिन day, and अन्तक ender.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=340-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिनारम्भ|दिनारंभ|दिनारम्भः
दिनारम्भ m. (-म्भः) Morning.<BR> E. दिन, and आरम्भ beginning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=340-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिनावसान|दिनावसानं
दिनावसान n. (-नं) Evening, close of day.<BR> E. दिन day, and अवसान<BR>expiration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=340-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिनिका
दिनिका f. (-का) A day's wages, hire for a day or by the day.<BR> E. दिन a<BR>day, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=340-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिभ
दिभ (इ) दिभि r. 10th cl. (दिम्भयति-ते) To order, to direct. चुरा० उभ० सक०<BR>सेट् इदित् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=340-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिम्प
दिम्प r. 1st and 10th cls. (दिम्पति-ते दिम्पयति-ते) To order, to command.<BR>भ्वा० उभ० । चुरा० उभ० सक० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=340-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिम्भ
दिम्भ r. 10th cl. (दिम्भयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To command, to direct.<BR>	 2. To collect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=340-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिलीप|दिलीपः
दिलीप m. (-पः) The name of a king and ancestor of RAMA.<BR> E. दिली said<BR>to be the barbarous name of Hastinapur of the modern Delhi, and<BR>प who protects or rules.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=340-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिलीपराज्
दिलीपराज् m. (-राट्) King DILIPA: see the preceding.<BR> E. दिलीप as above,<BR>and राज् a king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=340-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिलीर|दिलीरं
दिलीर m. (-रः) A mushroom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=340-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिव|दिवं
दिव (उ) दिवु r. 4th cl. (दीव्यति)<BR>	 1. To play, to sport, to play with, to<BR>romp or gambol.<BR>	 2. To desire, to overcome, to be ambitious of<BR>surpassing, &c.<BR>	 3. To deal, to traffic, to buy or sell.<BR>	 4. To shine,<BR>to be splendid or beautiful.<BR>	 5. To praise.<BR>	 6. To be glad, to rejoice.<BR>7. To be mad, to be wild or inflated with pride, passion, &c.<BR>	 8.<BR>To be sleepy or sluggish.<BR>	 9. To love, to desire.<BR>	 10. To go. r. 10th<BR>cl. (देवयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To suffer pain.<BR>	 2. To ask, to beseech or beg.<BR>	 3.<BR>To move, to go.<BR>	 4. (-ति-ते) To lament, to wail, to mourn audibly.<BR>(इ) दिवि r. 1st cl. (दन्वति)<BR>	 1. To please.<BR>	 2. To be pleased. जिगीषायां<BR>व्रीडायां च अक० पणे व्यवहारे, इच्छायां स्तुतौ च सक० दिवा० पर० सेट् । चुरा०<BR>कूजने आत्मने० सक० सेट् । अर्दे चुरा० उभ० सक० सेट् । प्रीतौ भ्वा० पर० सक०<BR>सेट् इदित् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=340-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिव्
दिव् f. (द्यौः दिवौ दिवः)<BR>	 1. Heaven, paradise.<BR>	 2. Air, sky.<BR> E. दिव् to<BR>play, affix क्विप्, where sport immortals; also दिव ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=340-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिव|दिवं
दिव n. (-वं)<BR>	 1. Heaven, paradise.<BR>	 2. Heaven, sky, atmosphere.<BR>	 3. A day.<BR>4. A wood, a thicket.<BR> E. दिव् to play, to shine, &c. affix घञर्थे<BR>आधारे वा कः see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=340-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिवन्
दिवन् m. (-वा) A day.<BR> E. दिव् to play, Uṇādi affix कनिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=340-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिवस|दिवसः
दिवस mn. (-सः-सं) A day.<BR> E. दिव् to play, असच् Uṇādi aff. किच्च.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=340-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिवसकर|दिवसकरः
दिवसकर m. (-रः) The sun.<BR> E. दिवस day, and कर who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=340-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिवसमुख|दिवसमुखं
दिवसमुख n. (-खं) Dawn, day-break.<BR> E. दिवस day, and मुख beginning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=340-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिवसात्यय
दिवसात्यय m. (-यः) Evening, close of day.<BR> E. दिवस and अत्यय loss.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=341-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिवसावसान
दिवसावसान n. (-नं) Evening, close of day.<BR> E. दिवस, and अवसान end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=341-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिवस्पति|दिवस्पतिः
दिवस्पति m. (-तिः) A name of INDRA the Indian JOVE.<BR> E. दिवः of day,<BR>and पति lord, Divespiter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=341-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिवस्पृथिबी
दिवस्पृथिबी f. du. (-व्यौ) Heaven and earth.<BR> E. दिव heaven, and पृथिवी<BR>earth, स inserted for the sake of euphony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=341-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिबा
दिबा ind. By day, the day.<BR> E. दिव् to play, &c. affix का.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=341-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिवाकर|दिवाकरः
दिवाकर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. The sun.<BR>	 2. A crow.<BR>	 3. A flower, the sun-flower. E.<BR>दिवा the day, and कर who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=341-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिवाकीर्त्ति|दिवाकीर्ति|दिवाकीर्तिः|दिवाकीर्त्तिः
दिवाकीर्त्ति m. (-र्त्तिः)<BR>	 1. A man of a low or impure caste, a Chandala.<BR>2. A barber.<BR>	 3. An owl.<BR> E. दिवा by day, and कीर्त्ति credit, (the bar-<BR>ber is not allowed to operate at night,) or दिवा day, अकीर्त्ति dis-<BR>repute; the Chandala and owl coming abroad only in the dark.<BR>दिवा एव कीर्त्तिः कृत्यं यस्य रात्रौ क्षुरकर्मनिषेधात् नापिते चण्डाले पेचके च ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=341-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिवाकृत
दिवाकृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Done by day.<BR> E. दिवा, and कृत done.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=341-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिवाचर|दिवाचरः
दिवाचर mfn. (-रः-री-रं) Going about by day.<BR> E. दिवा, and चर who or<BR>what goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=341-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिवाटन|दिवाटनः
दिवाटन m. (-नः) A crow.<BR> E. दिवा by day, अट् to go, affix ल्यु ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=341-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिवातन|दिवातनः
दिवातन mfn. (-नः-नी-नं) Daily, diurnal, of or belonging to the day. E.<BR>दिवा by day, ट्यु aff. तुट् च ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=341-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिवानिश
दिवानिश n. (-शं) Day and night.<BR> E. दिवा, and निशा night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=341-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिवान्ध|दिवांध|दिवान्धः
दिवान्ध mfn. (-न्धः-न्धा-न्धं) Being blind by day.<BR>	 m. (-न्धः) An owl.<BR> E. दिवा<BR>by day, and अन्ध dark or blind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=341-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिवाभीत|दिवाभीतः
दिवाभीत m. (-ताः)<BR>	 1. An owl.<BR>	 2. A thief or housebreaker.<BR>	 3. The white<BR>lotus (कुमुदाकर;) perhaps any such flower, the petals of which<BR>open at night, and close in the day time.<BR> E. दिवा day, and भीत<BR>afraid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=341-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिवाभीति|दिवाभीतिः
दिवाभीति m. (-तिः) An owl.<BR> E. दिवा by day, and भीति fear: see the pre-<BR>ceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=341-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिवामणि|दिवामणिः
दिवामणि m. (-णिः) The sun.<BR> E. दिवा, and मणि a jewel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=341-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिवामध्य|दिवामध्यं
दिवामध्य n. (-ध्यं) Mid-day, noon.<BR> E. दिवा and मध्य middle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=341-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिवारात्र
दिवारात्र n. (-त्रं) A day and night.<BR> E. दिवा, and रात्र for रात्रि night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=341-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिवारात्रि
दिवारात्रि f. (-त्रिः)<BR>	 1. Day or night.<BR>	 2. A day and night.<BR> E. दिवा, and रात्रि<BR>night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=341-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिवास्वप्न|दिवास्वप्नः
दिवास्वप्न m. (-प्नः) A sleep by day.<BR> E. दिवा, and स्वप्न sleep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=341-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिवि|दिविः
दिवि m. (-विः) The blue jay.<BR> E. दिव् to play, affix कि । चाष खगे ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=341-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिविज|दिविजः
दिविज mfn. (-जः-जा-जं) Celestial, heavenly, of heavenly origin. E.<BR>दिवि in heaven, and ज born. दिवि जायते जन-ड अलुक् स० ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=341-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिविषद्
दिविषद् m. (-द्) A deity.<BR> E. दिवि in heaven, सद् to go, affix क्विप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=341-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिविष्ठ|दिविष्ठः
दिविष्ठ mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठा-ष्ठं) Celestial, heavenly, situated in heaven.<BR> E. दिवि<BR>in heaven, and स्थ what stays.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=341-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिवी
दिवी f. (-वी) A sort of insect; also उपजिह्विका.<BR> E. दिव् to play, वा ई affix,<BR>fem. affix ङीप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=341-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिवोकस्
दिवोकस् m. (-काः)<BR>	 1. A deity.<BR>	 2. A kind of cuckoo, the Chataka: see<BR>दिवौकस् । द्यौः स्वर्गः आकाशो वा ओको यस्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=341-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिवोदास|दिवोदासः
दिवोदास m. (-सः) DIVODASA, a king so named, king of Benares, and<BR>founder of the Indian school of medicine.<BR> E. दिवः of heaven, दास<BR>the slave. or दिवः स्वर्गात् दासो दानं यस्मै ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=341-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिवोद्भव
दिवोद्भव mfn. (-वः-वा-वं) Born or produced in heaven.<BR>	 f. (-वा) Cardamoms.<BR>E. दिव heaven, उद्भव born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=341-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिवौकस्
दिवौकस् m. (-काः)<BR>	 1. A deity.<BR>	 2. The Chataka, (Cuculus melanoleucos.)<BR>3. A deer.<BR>	 4. A bee.<BR>	 5. An elephant.<BR> E. दिव heaven either, ओकस्<BR>a mansion; also with the vowel unaltered दिवोकस् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=341-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिव्य|दिव्यं|दिव्यः
दिव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>	 1. Divine, celestial.<BR>	 2. Beautiful, agreeable,<BR>charming.<BR>	 m. (-व्यः)<BR>	 1. Barley.<BR>	 2. A fragrant resin, (Bdelliun.)<BR>	 3.<BR>The divine character or property.<BR>	 f. (-व्या) Emblic myrobalan.<BR>	 n.<BR>(-व्यं)<BR>	 1. Cloves.<BR>	 2. A sort of Sandal.<BR>	 3. An ordeal.<BR>	 4. An oath. E.<BR>द्यु the sky or heaven, and यत् aff. दिवि भवः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=341-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिव्यकारिन्
दिव्यकारिन् m. (-री) One who undergoes an ordeal.<BR> E. दिव्य, and कारिन्<BR>who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=341-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिव्यगन्ध|दिव्यगन्धं|दिव्यगन्धः
दिव्यगन्ध m. (-न्धः) Sulphur.<BR>	 n. (-न्धं) Cloves.<BR>	 f. (-धा) Large cardamoms.<BR>E. दिव्य, and गन्ध smell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=341-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिव्यगायन|दिव्यगायनः
दिव्यगायन m. (-नः) A Gandharba or singer of heaven.<BR> E. दिव्य divine,<BR>and गायन a singer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=341-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिव्यचक्षुस्
दिव्यचक्षुस् mfn. (-क्षुः-क्षुः-क्षुः)<BR>	 1. Beautiful-eyed.<BR>	 2. Blind.<BR>	 m. (-क्षुः)<BR>	 1. A<BR>sort of perfume.<BR>	 2. A monkey.<BR>	 n. (-क्षुः) The faculty of seeing what<BR>is invisible by the human eye.<BR> E. दिव्य divine, and चक्षुस् an eye.<BR>दिव्यं चक्षुः यस्मात् ५ ब० ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=341-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिव्यदोहद|दिव्यदोहदं
दिव्यदोहद mfn. (-दः-दा-दं) Fit for an offering or oblation.<BR> E. दिव्य divine,<BR>and दोहद wish, that which is the subject of a deity's desires.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=341-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिव्यधर्म्मिन्|दिव्यधर्मिन्
दिव्यधर्म्मिन् mfn. (-र्म्मी-र्म्मिणी-र्म्मि) Virtuous, agreeable.<BR> E. दिव्य, and धर्म्मिन्<BR>virtuous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=341-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिव्यपञ्चामृत|दिव्यपञ्चामृतं
दिव्यपञ्चामृत n. (-तं) A mixture of five articles, ghee, curd, milk, but-<BR>ter, and sugar.<BR> E. दिव्य divine, पञ्च five, and अमृत ambrosia.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=341-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिव्यरत्न|दिव्यरत्नं
दिव्यरत्न n. (-त्नं) The fabulous gem Chintamani.<BR> E. दिव्य divine, and<BR>रत्न jewel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=341-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिव्यरथ|दिव्यरथः
दिव्यरथ m. (-थः) The car or vehicle of any deity.<BR> E. दिव्य divine, and रथ a carriage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=341-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिव्यरस|दिव्यरसः
दिव्यरस m. (-सः) Quicksilver.<BR> E. दिव्य divine, and रस juice. पारदे,<BR>मनोज्ञे रसे, रुचिररसयुक्ते त्रि० ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=341-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिव्यवस्त्र|दिव्यवस्त्रः
दिव्यवस्त्र mfn. (-स्त्रः-स्त्रा-स्त्रं)<BR>	 1. Clothed or invested in celestial raiment.<BR>2. Handsomely dressed.<BR>	 m. (-स्त्रः) A plant, commonly Suryasobha,<BR>a sort of sun-flower.<BR> E. दिव्य divine, वस्त्र cloth or clothes. दिव्यं वस्त्रं<BR>यस्मात् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=341-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिव्यादिव्या
दिव्यादिव्या f. (-व्या) The heroine of a poem, as SITA, &c. of mixed origin<BR>or character, a demigoddess.<BR> E. दिव्य divine, अदिव्य not divine,<BR>partaking of both natures.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=341-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिव्योघ
दिव्योघ m. (-घः) A form of ŚIVA, worshipped by the Tantrikas.<BR> E. दिव्य,<BR>and ओघ heap.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=341-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिव्योदक|दिव्योदकं
दिव्योदक n. (-कं) Rain-water, dew, &c.<BR> E. दिव्य heavenly, and उदक water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=341-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिव्योपपादुक|दिव्योपपादुकः
दिव्योपपादुक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Divine, celestial, of heavenly birth or<BR>being.<BR> E. दिव्य divine, पद् to go, with उप prefixed, and उकञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=341-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिश|दिशः
दिश (औ) दिशौ r. 6th cl. (दिशति-ते)<BR>	 1. To show, to exhibit, to explain or<BR>make intelligible.<BR>	 2. To order, to command, to direct or send.<BR>	 3. To<BR>say, to speak.<BR>	 4. To give. With अप prefixed, To change, to dis-<BR>guise. With आङ्, 1. To order or command.<BR>	 2. To show.<BR>	 3. To<BR>summon. With उद्, 1. To proclaim, to make known or public.<BR>2. To show. With उप, To point out (literally or metaphorically),<BR>to show, to advise. With निर्, 1. To speak aloud.<BR>	 2. To specify,<BR>to show. With प्र, To appoint, to order. With प्रति and सम्, To<BR>command, to return, to send back. With वि and अप, To plead in<BR>excuse, to state as a plea or pretext. With वि and निर्, To declare.<BR>With सम्, 1. To exhibit, to show, &c.<BR>	 2. To communicate as<BR>news or information, With सम् and आङ्, To approve, to permit.<BR>With सम्, To point out at a distance, as with the finger. तु० उभ०<BR>सक० अनिट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=341-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिश्
दिश् f. (-दिक् दिशौ दिशः) Region, space, quarter, part.<BR> E. दिश् to show,<BR>affix क्विन्ः also with टाप् added, दिशा, f. (-शा) or with ङीप्, दिशी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=341-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिशस्
दिशस् f. (-शाः) Region, quarter.<BR> E. दिश्, and कसुन् affix: see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=341-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिश्य|दिश्यं
दिश्य mfn. (-श्यः-श्या-श्यं) Situated, bearing, lying in a particular tract<BR>or quarter, as पूर्व्वदिश्य eastern, bearing east.<BR> E. दिश् a quarter,<BR>यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=341-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिष्ट|दिष्टं|दिष्टः
दिष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>	 1. Shown, pointed out.<BR>	 2. Delineated, described.<BR>3. Counselled, advised, enjoined.<BR>	 m. (-ष्टः)<BR>	 1. Time.<BR>	 2. A sort of<BR>Curcuma: see दारुहरिद्रा.<BR>	 n. (-ष्टं) Fate, destiny, fortune, good or<BR>ill luck.<BR> E. दिश् to show, affix कर्मणि क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=341-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिष्टान्त|दिष्टांत|दिष्टान्तः
दिष्टान्त m. (-न्तः) Death, dying.<BR> E. दिष्ट fortune, and अन्त end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=341-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिष्टि|दिष्टिः
दिष्टि f. (-ष्टिः)<BR>	 1. Pleasure, happiness.<BR>	 2. A sort of measure.<BR> E. दिश् to<BR>point out, affix भावे क्तिन्, संज्ञायां कर्त्तरि क्तिच् वा ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=341-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिष्ट्या
दिष्ट्या ind. An exclamation, indicative of joy or auspiciousness, luckily,<BR>fortunately.<BR> E. दिश् pointing out, स्त्र्यै to sound, affix भावे क्विप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=341-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिष्णु|दिष्णुः
दिष्णु mfn. (-ष्णुः-ष्णुः-ष्णु) Giving, one who gives, a donor.<BR> E. दा to give.<BR>इष्णु Uṇādi affix: see देष्णु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=342-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिह
दिह (औ) दिहौ r. 2nd cl. (देग्धि दिग्धे)<BR>	 1. To increase, to augment, to<BR>accumulate.<BR>	 2. To smear. अदा० उभ० सक० अनिट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=342-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दी
दी r. 4th cl. (ओ ङ) ओदीङ (दीयते) To waste, to diminish, to be reduced,<BR>to decay. दिवा० आ० अक० अनिट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=342-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दी
दी f. (दीः) Wasting, destruction.<BR> E. दी to waste, क्विप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=342-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीक्ष
दीक्ष r. 1st cl. (दीक्षते)<BR>	 1. To be shaved.<BR>	 2. To perform a sacrifice.<BR>	 3.<BR>To initiate.<BR>	 4. To teach religious observances.<BR>	 5. To be selfres-<BR>trained भ्वा० आ० सक० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=342-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीक्षणीयेष्टि|दीक्षणीयेष्टिः
दीक्षणीयेष्टि f. (-ष्टिः) A particular sacrifice, that preceded by the Diksha;<BR>see the next.<BR> E. दीक्षा as below, छ affix, and इष्टि a sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=342-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीक्षा
दीक्षा f. (-क्षा)<BR>	 1. Sacrificing, offering oblations.<BR>	 2. Worshipping in<BR>general.<BR>	 3. Engaging in a course of austerities.<BR>	 4. Certain cere-<BR>monies preliminary to a cacrifice.<BR>	 5. Receiving the initiatory Man-<BR>tra or incantation.<BR> E. दा to give, (knowledge,) and क्षि to destroy,<BR>(sin;) deriv. irr. or दीक्ष् to initiate, &c. affixes अ and टाप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=342-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीक्षान्त|दीक्षांत|दीक्षान्तः
दीक्षान्त m. (-न्तः) A supplementary sacrifice, one made to atone for any<BR>defects in a preceding one.<BR> E. दीक्षा sacrifice, and अन्त completion,<BR>end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=342-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीक्षित|दीक्षितः
दीक्षित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Initiated.<BR>	 2. Performed, (as the Diksha cere-<BR>mony.)<BR>	 3. One by whom the preparatory ceremonies have been<BR>observed.<BR>	 m. (-तः)<BR>	 1. An assemblage of priests for peculiar cere-<BR>monies, or for any sacrifice.<BR>	 2. The pupil or an ascetick.<BR> E. दीक्ष् to<BR>perform a sacrifice or to be initiated, affix कर्त्तरि क्त or दीक्षा जाता<BR>अस्य तार० इतच् वा ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=342-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीक्षितृ
दीक्षितृ m. (-ता) A spiritual father, the communicator of the initiatory<BR>Mantra or prayer.<BR> E. दीक्ष to sacrifice, &c. तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=342-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीद
दीद mfn. (-दः-दा-दं) Destroying.<BR> E. दी, and द who or what gives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=342-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दौदिवि
दौदिवि mfn. (-विः-विः-वि) Risen, ascended.<BR>	 mn. (-विः-वि) Boiled rice.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-विः) A name of VṚHASPATI.<BR> E. दिव् to play, Uṇādi affix क्विन्, the<BR>radical reduplicate, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=342-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीधिति|दीधितिः
दीधिति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. A ray of light, a sun or a moonbeam.<BR>	 2. Light in<BR>general.<BR> E. दीधी to shine, affix क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=342-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीधी
दीधी (ङ) दीधीङ r. 2nd cl. (दीधीते)<BR>	 1. To shine.<BR>	 2. To play or sport. अदा०<BR>जक्षा० आ० सक० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=342-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीन|दीनं|दीनः
दीन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>	 1. Poor, indigent, needy, distressed.<BR>	 2. Afraid,<BR>frightened, timid.<BR>	 f. (-ना) A mouse or shrew.<BR> E. दी to waste or<BR>decay, affix क्त, deriv. irr. or दी as before, Uṇādi affix नक् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=342-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीनचेतन
दीनचेतन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Distressed, dejected.<BR> E. दीन, and चेतन feeling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=342-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीनमुख
दीनमुख mfn. (-खः-खी-खं) Down-cast, of melancholy aspect.<BR> E. दीन, and<BR>मुख mouth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=342-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीनार|दीनारः
दीनार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A gold ornament.<BR>	 2. A seal.<BR>	 3. A weight of gold,<BR>variously stated as two Kashthas, one Pala of thirty-two Rattis,<BR>and also as the large Pala or hundred and eight Suvernas.<BR>	 4. A<BR>coin, a Dinara.<BR> E. दीन a pauper, and ऋ to go; what is given to<BR>the poor; or दी to waste, Uṇādi affix आरक् and नुट् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=342-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीप|दीपः
दीप r. 4th cl. (ई ऋ) ऋदीपी (दीप्यते) To shine, to blaze, to be luminous<BR>or light. दिवा० आ० अक० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=342-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीप|दीपः
दीप m. (-पः) A lamp.<BR> E. दीप् to shine, affix, क, अच् or घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=342-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीपक|दीपकं|दीपकः
दीपक mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>	 1. Making luminous or beautiful.<BR>	 2. Kindling,<BR>inflaming.<BR>	 3. Exciting, rendering intense (a feeling, &c.)<BR>	 4. Tonic,<BR>stimulant.<BR>	 m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. An aromatic seed, (Ligusticum ajwaen,<BR>Rox.)<BR>	 2. Small cumin.<BR>	 3. Celosia cristata.<BR>	 4. Saffron.<BR>	 5. A lamp.<BR>6. A falcon.<BR>	 7. A name of KĀMA^1.<BR>	 8. One of the Ragas or modes of<BR>music.<BR>	 f. (-पिका)<BR>	 1. One of the Rāgiṇīs or female personifications<BR>of the musical modes.<BR>	 2. A title of various books, (the illustrator,<BR>the illuminator.)<BR>	 3. Moonlight.<BR>	 n. (-कं) A figure of rhetoric,<BR>dilating upon an idea, or accumulation of expressions tending to<BR>one object.<BR> E. दीप् to shine, in the causal form, affix ण्वुल् ।<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20260617. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/264.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=342-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीपकिट्ट|दीपकिट्टं
दीपकिट्ट n. (-ट्टं) Lamp black, soot.<BR> E. दीप a lamp, and किट्ट sediment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=342-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीपकूपी
दीपकूपी f. (-पी) The wick of a lamp.<BR> E. दीप a lamp, and कूप a well.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=342-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीपखोरी
दीपखोरी f. (-री) The wick of a lamp.<BR> E. दीप light, खुड् to divide, affix<BR>अच्, and ड changed to र ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=342-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीपध्वज|दीपध्वजः
दीपध्वज mn. (-जः-जं) Lamp black, the condensed smoke or soot of a<BR>lamp.<BR> E. दीप a lamp, and ध्वज symbol. दीपस्य ध्वज इव । कज्जले ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=342-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीपन|दीपनं|दीपनः
दीपन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>	 1. Inflaming, light or heat-exciting.<BR>	 2. Tonic,<BR>stimulant.<BR>	 n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Inflaming, lighting.<BR>	 2. Stimulating, exciting.<BR>3. A root, commonly Tagara.<BR>	 4. Saffron.<BR>	 mfn. (-नः-नी-नं) An<BR>aromatic seed, (Ligusticum ajwaen.)<BR>	 m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. A sort of potherb<BR>commonly Salincha, (Achyranthes triandra, Rox.)<BR>	 2. Celosia<BR>cristata.<BR>	 3. Cassia tora.<BR> E. दीप् to shine, in the causal form, and<BR>and युच् or ल्युट् aff. or दीपयति वह्निं दीप-णिच्-ल्यु ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=342-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीपनीय|दीपनीयः
दीपनीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>	 1. To be lighted, to be inflamed.<BR>	 2. To be<BR>excited or stimulated.<BR>	 m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. An aromatic seed, (Ligusticum<BR>ajwaen, Rox.)<BR>	 2. A stimulant drug, as pepper of various kinds, &c.<BR>E. दीप् to shine, अनीयर् aff. दीपनाय जठरानलोद्दीपनाय हितः छ ।<BR>यवान्याम् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=342-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीपपादप|दीपपादपः
दीपपादप m. (-पः) A lampstand, a candlestick.<BR> E. दीप and पादप a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=342-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीपपुष्प|दीपपुष्पः
दीपपुष्प m. (-ष्पः) The Champaca, (Michelia champaca.)<BR> E. दीप enkindling,<BR>(passion,) and पुष्प a flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=342-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीपमाला
दीपमाला f. (-ला) A row of lamps an illumination.<BR> E. दीप, and माला a<BR>garland; also दीपमालिका ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=342-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीपयत्
दीपयत् mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत) Illuminating, inflaming.<BR> E. दीप् to kindle,<BR>causal form, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=342-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीपवृक्ष|दीपवृक्षः
दीपवृक्ष m. (-क्षः) The stand or stem of a lamp, a candlestick.<BR> E. दीप a<BR>lamp, and वृक्ष a tree; also दीपवृक्षक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=342-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीपशिखा
दीपशिखा f. (-खा)<BR>	 1. Lamp black, especially considered as applicable to<BR>the eyes, to darken the lashes, &c.<BR>	 2. The flame of a lamp.<BR> E. दीप<BR>a lamp, and शिखा a crest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=342-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीपशृङ्खला|दीपशृंखला
दीपशृङ्खला f. (-ला) A row or string of lamps.<BR> E. दीप, and शृङ्खला a chain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=342-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीपान्विता
दीपान्विता f. (-ता) A festival: see the next.<BR> E. दीप, and अन्वित having.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=342-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीपाली
दीपाली f. (-ली)<BR>	 1. The day of new moon in the month Aswin or Kartik,<BR>(September-October,) a festival with nocturnal illuminations in<BR>honor of KARTIKEYA; the Diwali, as it usually termed.<BR>	 2. A row<BR>or range of lamps.<BR> E. दीप a lamp, and आली a line; also दीपावली<BR>the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=342-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीपित
दीपित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Illuminated, irradiated.<BR>	 2. Excited, inflamed.<BR>3. Manifested.<BR> E. दीप् to kindle, causal form, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=342-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीपितृ
दीपितृ mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ) An illuminator, an enlightener, shining, irradiat-<BR>ing.<BR> E. दीप् to kindle, &c. तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=342-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीप्त|दीप्तं|दीप्तः
दीप्त mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं)<BR>	 1. Luminous, splendid, radiant.<BR>	 2. Blazing, glow-<BR>ing.<BR>	 3. Burnt.<BR>	 n. (-प्तं)<BR>	 1. Gold.<BR>	 2. Asafœtida.<BR>	 m. (-प्तः)<BR>	 1. A lion.<BR>	 2.<BR>A lime.<BR>	 f. (-प्ता) A plant: see लाङ्गलिकी.<BR> E. दीप् to blaze, to shine,<BR>affix क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=342-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीप्तक|दीप्तकं|दीप्तकः
दीप्तक m. (-कः) Gold.<BR> E. कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=342-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीप्तजिह्वा
दीप्तजिह्वा f. (-ह्वा) A fox.<BR> E. दीप्त shining, fiery, and जिह्वा tongue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=342-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीप्तपिङ्गल|दीप्तपिङ्गलः
दीप्तपिङ्गल m. (-लः) A lion.<BR> E. दीप्त shining, and पिङ्गल tawny.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=342-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीप्तरस|दीप्तरसः
दीप्तरस m. (-सः) An earth-worm.<BR> E. दीप्त shining, and रस juice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=342-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीप्तलोचन|दीप्तलोचनः
दीप्तलोचन m. (-नः) A cat.<BR> E. दीप्त shining, and लोचन an eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=342-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीप्तलोह|दीप्तलोहं
दीप्तलोह m. (-हः) Bell metal.<BR> E. दीप्त shining, and लोह iron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=342-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीप्ताक्ष|दीप्ताक्षः
दीप्ताक्ष m. (-क्षः)<BR>	 1. A cat.<BR>	 2. A peacock.<BR> E. दीप्त glowing, and अक्ष the eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=342-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीप्ताग्नि|दीप्ताग्निः
दीप्ताग्नि mfn. (-ग्निः-ग्निः-ग्नि)<BR>	 1. Of good digestion.<BR>	 2. Kindled, fed, (as<BR>fire.)<BR>	 m. (-ग्निः) A name of the saint AGASTYA.<BR> E. दीप्त excited, and<BR>अग्नि fire, or the appetite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=342-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीप्ताङ्ग|दीप्तांग|दीप्ताङ्गः
दीप्ताङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः) A peacock.<BR> E. दीप्त, and अङ्ग body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=342-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीप्ति|दीप्तिः
दीप्ति f. (-प्तिः)<BR>	 1. Light, lustre, splendour.<BR>	 2. Beauty.<BR>	 3. The swift<BR>flight of an arrow.<BR>	 4. A property of women, extreme loveliness,<BR>brilliant beauty.<BR>	 5. Lac.<BR>	 5. Bell metal.<BR> E. दीप् to shine, affix भावे<BR>क्तिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=342-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीप्तिमत्|दीप्तिमन्त्
दीप्तिमत् mfn. (-मान्-मती-मत्) Shining, radiant.<BR>	 2. Blazing, flaming.<BR> E. दीप्त,<BR>and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=343-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीप्तोपल|दीप्तोपलः
दीप्तोपल m. (-लः) The sun-gem, crystalline lens.<BR> E. दीप्त shining, and<BR>उपल a stone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=343-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीप्य|दीप्यः
दीप्य mfn. (-प्यः-प्या-प्यं)<BR>	 1. To be kindled or inflamed.<BR>	 2. To be stimulated.<BR>m. (-प्यः)<BR>	 1. A plant, (Celosia cristata.)<BR>	 2. An aromatic seed,<BR>(Ligusticum ajwaen.)<BR> E. दीप, and यत् affix: see दीप; also with कन्<BR>added दीप्यकः see दीपक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=343-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीप्यमान
दीप्यमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Shining, radiant, irradiating.<BR> E. दीप् to shine,<BR>शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=343-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीप्र|दीप्रः
दीप्र mfn. (-प्रः-प्रा-प्रं) Light, luminous.<BR> E. दीप् to shine, affix र ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=343-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीप्रास्त्रधर
दीप्रास्त्रधर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Armed with shining weapons; well accoutred.<BR>E. दीप्र light, अस्त्र arms, धृ to hold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=343-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घ|दीर्घं|दीर्घः
दीर्घ mfn. (-र्घः-र्घा-र्घं) Long, applied either to space or time.<BR>	 m. (-र्घः)<BR>	 1.<BR>The Sal tree.<BR>	 2. A long vowel.<BR>	 3. The 5th, 6th, 7th or 8th sign of<BR>the zodiac.<BR> E. दॄ to divide or send, affix घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=343-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घकण्ठक|दीर्घकंठक|दीर्घकण्ठकः
दीर्घकण्ठक m. (-कः) A sort of crane, the Vaka, (Ardea nivea.)<BR> E. दीर्घ<BR>long, कण्ठ throat, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=343-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घकन्धर|दीर्घकंधर|दीर्घकन्धरः
दीर्घकन्धर m. (-रः) A sort of crane, (Ardea nivea.)<BR> E. दीर्घ, and कन्धर neck.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=343-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घकाल
दीर्घकाल n. (-लं) A long time, a long period.<BR> E. दीर्घ, and काल time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=343-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घकाष्ठ
दीर्घकाष्ठ n. (-ष्ठं) A spar, a beam, a long piece of timber.<BR> E. दीर्घ, and<BR>काष्ठ wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=343-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घकील|दीर्घकीलः
दीर्घकील m. (-लः) A tree, (Alangium hexapetalum.)<BR> E. दीर्घ long, कील a<BR>stem or stake; also with कन् दीर्घकीलक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=343-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घकेश|दीर्घकेशः
दीर्घकेश mfn. (-शः-शी-शं) Long-haired.<BR>	 m. (-शः) A bear.<BR> E. दीर्घ, and<BR>केश hair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=343-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घकोशिका
दीर्घकोशिका f. (-का) A cockle; also दीर्घकोशी, &c. see the next. (झिनुक्) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=343-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घकोषिका
दीर्घकोषिका f. (-का) A cockle.<BR> E. दीर्घ long, कोश or कोष a sheath or shell,<BR>affix ङीप्, दीर्घकोषी or दीर्घकोशी and कन् with the fem. form added,<BR>दीर्घकोशिका, -षिका ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=343-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घगति|दीर्घगतिः
दीर्घगति m. (-तिः) A camel.<BR> E. दीर्घ, and गति going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=343-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घग्रीव|दीर्घग्रीवः
दीर्घग्रीव m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. A camel.<BR>	 2. A kind of curlew.<BR> E. दीर्घ long, and ग्रीवा<BR>a neck.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=343-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घघाटिक|दीर्घघाटिकः
दीर्घघाटिक m. (-कः) A camel<BR> E. दीर्घ long, घाटा the neck, affix ठन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=343-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घजङ्गल|दीर्घजङ्गलः
दीर्घजङ्गल m. (-लः) A kind of fish, commonly Bhangan.<BR> E. दीर्घ long,<BR>and जङ्गल desert.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=343-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घजङ्घ|दीर्घजंघ|दीर्घजङ्घः
दीर्घजङ्घ mfn. (-ङ्घः-ङ्घा-ङ्घं) Long-thighed.<BR>	 m. (-ङ्घः)<BR>	 1. A crane.<BR>	 2. A camel.<BR>E. दीर्घ long, and जङ्घा a thigh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=343-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घजिह्व|दीर्घजिह्वः
दीर्घजिह्व m. (-ह्वः) A snake.<BR> E. दीर्घ long, and जिह्वा a tongue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=343-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घजीव
दीर्घजीव m. (-वः) Long life.<BR> E. दीर्घ, and जीव life; also दीर्घजीवित ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=343-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घजीविन्
दीर्घजीविन् mfn. (-वी-विनी-वि) Living or existing a long time.<BR> E. दीर्घ,<BR>and जीविन् who lives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=343-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घतनु
दीर्घतनु mfn. (-नुः-नुः-नु) Tall, long.<BR> E. दीर्घ, and तनु body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=343-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घतरु|दीर्घतरुः
दीर्घतरु m. (-रुः) The Tal or palm tree.<BR> E. दीर्घ long, and तरु a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=343-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घतिमिषा
दीर्घतिमिषा f. (-षा) A kind of cucumber: see कर्क्कटी ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=343-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घतुण्डा
दीर्घतुण्डा f. (-ण्डा) The musk shrew.<BR> E. दीर्घ, and तुण्डा a snout.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=343-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घदण्ड|दीर्घदण्डः
दीर्घदण्ड m. (-ण्डः) The castor oil tree.<BR> E. दीर्घ long, दण्ड a stick or stem;<BR>also with कन् added, दीर्घदण्डक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=343-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घदर्शिन्
दीर्घदर्शिन् mfn. (-र्शी-र्शिणी-र्शि) Far-seeing, provident, wise.<BR>	 m. (-र्शी)<BR>	 1.<BR>A wise or learned man, a scer, a prophet.<BR>	 2. A vulture.<BR>	 3. A bean.<BR>E. दीर्घ long, दृश् to see, affix णिनि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=343-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घदृष्टि|दीर्घदृष्टिः
दीर्घदृष्टि m. (-ष्टिः) A wise or provident man; also mfn. Wise, pro-<BR>vident, far-seeing.<BR> E. दीर्घ long, and दृष्टि sight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=343-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घद्रु|दीर्घद्रुः
दीर्घद्रु m. (-द्रुः) The palm tree.<BR> E. दीर्घ long, and द्रु a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=343-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घनाद|दीर्घनादः
दीर्घनाद m. (-दः) A conch shell.<BR> E. दीर्घ, and नाद sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=343-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घनिद्रा
दीर्घनिद्रा f. (-द्रा) Death.<BR> E. दीर्घ long, and निद्रा sleep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=343-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घनिश्वस्य
दीर्घनिश्वस्य ind. Sighing or having sighed deeply.<BR> E. दीर्घ, and निश्वस्य<BR>having sighed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=343-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घनिश्वास
दीर्घनिश्वास m. (-सः) A long or deep drawn sigh.<BR> E. दीर्घ, and निश्वास a<BR>sigh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=343-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घपक्ष|दीर्घपक्षः
दीर्घपक्ष m. (-क्षः) The fork-tailed shrike.<BR> E. दीर्घ, and पक्ष a wing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=343-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घपत्र|दीर्घपत्रः
दीर्घपत्र mfn. (-त्रः-त्रा-त्री-त्रं) Long-leaved longifolium.<BR>	 m. (-त्रः) Garlic.<BR>	 f.<BR>(-त्रा)<BR>	 1. A sort of Eugenia.<BR>	 2. A kind of Chakulya.<BR> E. दीर्घ long, and<BR>पत्र a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=343-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घपत्रक|दीर्घपत्रकः
दीर्घपत्रक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A thorny plant: see करीर.<BR>	 2. A kind of Bassia grow-<BR>ing in marshy places.<BR>	 3. Garlic.<BR> E. दीर्घ long, पत्र a leaf, and कन्<BR>added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=343-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घपर्ण
दीर्घपर्ण mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-णी-र्णं) long-leaved longifolium.<BR> E. दीर्घ, and पर्ण a<BR>leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=343-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घपल्लव|दीर्घपल्लवः
दीर्घपल्लव mfn. (-वः-वा-वी-वं) Having long shoots or tendrils.<BR>	 m. (-वः) The<BR>San plant, (Crotolaria juneca.)<BR> E. दीर्घ, and पल्लव a shoot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=343-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घपादप|दीर्घपादपः
दीर्घपादप m. (-पः)<BR>	 1. The cocoanut tree.<BR>	 2. The betelnut tree.<BR> E. दीर्घ,<BR>and पादप a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=343-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घपाद्
दीर्घपाद् m. (-द् or -त्) A heron.<BR> E. दीर्घ long, and पाद् for पद a foot;<BR>also with a final vowel दीर्घपाद m. (-दः) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=343-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घपृष्ठ|दीर्घपृष्ठः
दीर्घपृष्ठ m. (-ष्ठः) A snake.<BR> E. दीर्घ long, and पृष्ठ back.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=343-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घफल|दीर्घफलः
दीर्घफल n. (-लं) A plant, (Cassia fistula.)<BR> E. दीर्घ long, and फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=343-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घमारुत|दीर्घमारुतः
दीर्घमारुत m. (-तः) An elephant.<BR> E. दीर्घ long, and मारुत wind or breath.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=343-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घमुख
दीर्घमुख mfn. (-खः-खी-खं) Long-faced.<BR> E. दीर्घ, and मुख the face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=343-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घमूल|दीर्घमूलं|दीर्घमूलः
दीर्घमूल mfn. (-लः-ला-ली-लं) Having a long root.<BR>	 m. (-लः)<BR>	 m. (-लः) A kind<BR>of Bilwa tree.<BR>	 n. (-लं) A sort of sensitive plant.<BR>	 f. (-ला)<BR>	 1. A<BR>creeper, Echites frutescens:) see श्यामलता.<BR>	 2. A plant, (Hedysarum<BR>gangeticum;) also Salaparni.<BR>	 f. (-ली) A plant, (Hedysarum<BR>alhagi.)<BR> E. दीर्घ long, मूल a root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=343-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घरत|दीर्घरतः
दीर्घरत m. (-तः) A dog.<BR> E. दीर्घ long, and रत copulation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=343-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घरद|दीर्घरदः
दीर्घरद m. (-दः) A hog.<BR> E. दीर्घ long, and रद a tooth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=343-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घरसन|दीर्घरसनः
दीर्घरसन m. (-नः) A snake.<BR> E. दीर्घ long, and रसना a tongue. दीर्घा रसना<BR>जिह्वा अस्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=343-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घरात्र|दीर्घरात्रं
दीर्घरात्र n. (-त्रं) 1, A long period.<BR>	 2. A long night.<BR> E. दीर्घ long, and<BR>रात्र for रात्रि night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=343-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घराव
दीर्घराव mfn. (-वः-वी-वं) Making a long continued noise, yelling, howl-<BR>ing.<BR> E. दीर्घ, and राव cry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=343-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घरोगिन्
दीर्घरोगिन् mfn. (-गी-गिणी-गि) Being long ill.<BR> E. दीर्घ, and रोगिन्<BR>sick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=343-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घरोमन्
दीर्घरोमन् m. (-मा) A bear.<BR> E. दीर्घ long, रोमन् hair of the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=343-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घरोहिषक|दीर्घरोहिषकं
दीर्घरोहिषक n. (-कं) A fragrant sort of grass.<BR> E. दीर्घ, and रोहिषक an-<BR>other sort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=343-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घवंश|दीर्घवंशः
दीर्घवंश mfn. (-शः-शा-शं)<BR>	 1. Having a long staff or stick.<BR>	 2. Being of an<BR>ancient family.<BR>	 m. (-शः) A reed.<BR> E. दीर्घ, and वंश a race, a bamboo.<BR>दीर्घः वंश इव । नलतृणे सन्तते कुले च ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=343-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घवक्त्र|दीर्घवक्त्रः
दीर्घवक्त्र m. (-क्त्रः) An elephant,<BR> E. दीर्घ long, and वक्त्र face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=343-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घवर्च्छिका
दीर्घवर्च्छिका f. (-का) An alligator.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=343-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घवर्ण
दीर्घवर्ण m. (-र्णः) A long vowel.<BR> E. दीर्घ, and वर्ण a letter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=343-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घवर्त्मन्
दीर्घवर्त्मन् m. (-र्त्मा) A long road, a long journey.<BR> E. दीर्घ, and वर्त्मन् a path.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=343-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घवृन्त|दीर्घवृन्तः
दीर्घवृन्त m. (-न्तः) A plant, (Bignonia Indica.)<BR> E. दीर्घ long, and वृन्त<BR>stalk; with कन् added दीर्घवृन्तक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=343-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घवृन्तिका
दीर्घवृन्तिका f. (-का) A plant, (Mimosa octandra.)<BR> E. दीर्घ long, and वृन्त a<BR>stalk; कन् affix, with the fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=343-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घशाख|दीर्घशाखः
दीर्घशाख m. (-खः) The Sal tree, (Shorea robusta.)<BR> E. दीर्घ long, and शाखा<BR>a branch. दीर्घा शाखा यस्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=343-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घसक्थ|दीर्घसक्थं
दीर्घसक्थ mfn. (-क्थः-क्था-क्थं) Long-thighed.<BR> E. दीर्घ long, and सक्थि a<BR>thigh, affix अच्; figuratively used, the compound retains its<BR>proper final, as दीर्घसक्थि चक्रं a long-spoked wheel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=343-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घसत्र|दीर्घसत्रं|दीर्घसत्रः
दीर्घसत्र n. (त्रं)<BR>	 1. A sort of religious ceremony, one of long continuance.<BR>2. A place of pilgrimage.<BR> E. दीर्घ long, सत्र sacrifice, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=343-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घसन्ध्यत्व|दीर्घसंध्यत्व
दीर्घसन्ध्यत्व n. (-त्वं) Long-continued observance of the chief daily rites. E.<BR>दीर्घ and सन्ध्या the morning, noon, and evening oblation, त्व aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=343-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घसुरत|दीर्घसुरतः
दीर्घसुरत m. (-तः) A dog.<BR> E. दीर्घ long, and सुरत coition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=343-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घसूत्र|दीर्घसूत्रः
दीर्घसूत्र mfn. (-त्रः-त्रा-त्रं) Dilatory, slow, tedious.<BR> E. दीर्घ long, and सूत्र line<BR>or thread. दीर्घेण चिरकालेन सूत्रम् ईप्सितव्यापारो यस्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=343-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घसूत्रता
दीर्घसूत्रता f. (-ता) Dilatoriness, tediousness.<BR> E. दीर्घसूत्र, and तल् added; also<BR>with त्व दीर्घसूत्रत्वम् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=344-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घसूत्रिन्
दीर्घसूत्रिन् mfn. (-त्री-त्रिणी-त्रि) Dilatory.<BR> E. दीर्घ, and सूत्रिन् having a line or<BR>thread. दीर्घं कर्त्तव्यव्यापारोऽस्ति अस्य इनि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=344-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घस्वर
दीर्घस्वर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A long vowel.<BR>	 2. A long note, a minim or semi<BR>breve.<BR> E. दीर्घ, and स्वर a sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=344-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घाध्वग|दीर्घाध्वगः
दीर्घाध्वग mfn. (-गः-गा-गं) A letter carrier, a messenger, an express.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-गः) A camel.<BR> E. दीर्घ long, अध्वन् a road, and ग who goes. दीर्घमायतम-<BR>ध्वानं गच्छति गम-ड । ६ त० ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=344-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घाध्वन्
दीर्घाध्वन् n. (-ध्व) A long journey.<BR> E. दीर्घ, and अध्वन् a road.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=344-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घामय
दीर्घामय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Long ill.<BR> E. दीर्घ, and आमय sickness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=344-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घायुध|दीर्घायुधः
दीर्घायुध m. (-धः)<BR>	 1. A spear, a javelin.<BR>	 2. A hog.<BR> E. दीर्घ long, and आयुध<BR>weapon, or one so armed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=344-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घायुस्
दीर्घायुस् mfn. (-युः-युः-युः) Long-lived.<BR>	 m. (-युः)<BR>	 1. The saint MARKANDEYA.<BR>2. The silk-cotton tree, (Bombax heptaphyllum.)<BR>	 3. A crow.<BR>	 4. A<BR>tree.: see जीवक.<BR>	 n. (-युः) Long life.<BR> E. दीर्घ long, and आयुस् life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=344-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घायुष्य|दीर्घायुष्यः
दीर्घायुष्य mfn. (-ष्यः-ष्या-ष्यं) Long-lived.<BR> E. दीर्घ, and आयुष्य lived.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=344-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घिका
दीर्घिका f. (-का) A large and long pond.<BR> E. दीर्घ long, affix क, fem.<BR>form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=344-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्ण|दीर्णः
दीर्ण mfn. (-र्णाः-र्णा-र्णं)<BR>	 1. Torn, rent, sundered.<BR>	 2. Frightened, afraid. E.<BR>दॄ to tear, affix क्त, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=344-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीवि|दीविः
दीवि m. (-विः) The blue jay. E. See दिवि and किकीदिवि, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=344-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीव्यत्|दीव्यन्त्
दीव्यत् mfn. (व्यन्-व्यती-व्यत्) Playing, sporting.<BR> E. दीव् to play, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=344-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीव्यमान
दीव्यमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>	 1. Throwing, darting, shooting.<BR>	 2. Playing. E.<BR>दिव् to play, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=344-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दु|दुः
दु r. 1st cl. (दवति) To go, to move. (दुनीति) r. 5th cl. (ओ, दू) ओदुटु 1. To<BR>be in pain, to burn morally or figuratively.<BR>	 2. To cause pain,<BR>anxiety, &c.<BR>	 3. to burn, to heat. गतौ भ्वा० प० अक० अनिट् । उपतापे स्वा०<BR>प० सक० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=344-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुःख|दुःखं
दुःख r. 10th cl. (दुःखयति-ते) To give pain. चुरा० उभ० अक० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=344-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुःख|दुःखं
दुःख n. (-खं)<BR>	 1. Pain, sorrow. affliction, distress, unhappiness.<BR>	 2. The<BR>world.<BR>	 3. Difficulty, trouble.<BR> E. दुःख to give pain, affix अच्; or दु<BR>bad, and ख्या to call; or खन् to dig, ड aff. दुष्टानि खानि यस्मिन्, or दुष्टं<BR>खनति ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=344-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुःखकर
दुःखकर mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>	 1. Causing pain.<BR>	 2. Afflicting, occasioning sor-<BR>row or trouble.<BR> E. दुःख, and कर what makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=344-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुःखच्छिन्न|दुःखछिन्न
दुःखच्छिन्न mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>	 1. Cut with difficulty, tough, hard.<BR>	 2. Afflicted,<BR>pained, distressed.<BR> E. दुःख, and छिन्न cut.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=344-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुःखच्छेद्य|दुःखछेद्य
दुःखच्छेद्य mfn. (-द्यः-द्या-द्यं)<BR>	 1. To be cut with difficulty, tough, hard.<BR>	 3. To<BR>be overcome with difficulty.<BR>	 3. To be hurt or pained by, (afflic-<BR>tion, &c.)<BR> E. दुःख, and छेद्य to be cut.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=344-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुःखजीविन्
दुःखजीविन् mfn. (-वी-विनी-वि) Living in pain or distress.<BR> E. दुःख, and<BR>जीविन् living.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=344-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुःखदग्ध
दुःखदग्ध mfn. (-ग्धः-ग्धा-ग्धं) Afflicted, pained, distressed.<BR> E. दुःख, and दग्ध<BR>burnt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=344-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुःखदोह्या
दुःखदोह्या f. (-ह्या) A cow difficult to be milked.<BR> E. दुःख trouble, दोह्य to<BR>be milked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=344-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुःखप्राय
दुःखप्राय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Full of trouble or pain.<BR> E. दुःख, and प्राय abundant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=344-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुःखबहुल
दुःखबहुल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Painful, distressful, abounding with trouble,<BR>&c.<BR> E. दुःख, and बहुल much.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=344-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुःखभागिन्
दुःखभागिन् mfn. (-गी-गिनी-गि) Suffering pain, having pain as their portion.<BR>E. दुःख and भागिन् who shares.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=344-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुःखयोग|दुःखयोगः
दुःखयोग m. (-गः) Occurrence or incidence of trouble, pain, &c.<BR> E. दुःख,<BR>and योग union.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=344-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुःखलभ्य
दुःखलभ्य mfn. (-भ्यः-भ्या-भ्यं) To be obtained or effected with difficulty. E.<BR>दुःख, and लभ्य obtainable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=344-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुःखसंवर्द्धित
दुःखसंवर्द्धित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Reared with trouble and difficulty.<BR> E. दुःख,<BR>and संवर्द्धित raised.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=344-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुःखसंयोग
दुःखसंयोग m. (-गः) Accession or presence of pain, distress, &c.<BR> E. दुःख,<BR>and संयोग union.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=344-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुःखसंस्थिति
दुःखसंस्थिति mfn. (-तिः-तिः-ति) Wretched, poor, miserable.<BR> E. दुःख, and<BR>संस्थिति condition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=344-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुःखसागर|दुःखसागरः
दुःखसागर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Deep distress.<BR>	 2. The world.<BR> E. दुःख, and सागर<BR>an ocean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=344-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुःखहन्
दुःखहन् mfn. (-हा-हा-ह) Removing pain.<BR> E. दुःख, and हन् who or what<BR>destroys.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=344-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुःखातीत
दुःखातीत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Free from pain.<BR> E. दुःख, and अतीत passed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=344-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुःखान्वित
दुःखान्वित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Pained, afflicted, distressed.<BR> E. दुःख, and अन्वित<BR>having.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=344-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुःखार्त्त|दुःखार्त
दुःखार्त्त mfn. (-र्त्तः-र्त्ता-र्त्तं) Afflicted, pained, distressed.<BR> E. दुःख, and आर्त्त<BR>pained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=344-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुःखित|दुःखितः
दुःखित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Pained, suffering pain.<BR>	 n. (-तं) Pain, distress,<BR>trouble.<BR> E. दुःख to give pain, affix क्त or तारका० इतच ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=344-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुःखिन्
दुःखिन् mfn. (-खी-खिनी-खि)<BR>	 1. Suffering pain, sorrowing, afflicted.<BR>	 2.<BR>Difficult, painful.<BR> E. दुःख, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=344-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुःखोपेत
दुःखोपेत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Suffering distress, &c.<BR> E. दुःख, and उपेत gone to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=344-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुःप्राप
दुःप्राप mfn. (-पः-पा-पं) Difficult of attainment.<BR> E. दुर्, and प्राप obtain-<BR>ing; also दुष्प्राप ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=344-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुःप्राप्य
दुःप्राप्य mfn. (-प्यः-प्या-प्यं) Difficult of attainment.<BR> E. दुर्, and प्राप्य obtain-<BR>able; also दुष्प्राप्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=344-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुःशासन|दुःशासनः
दुःशासन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Ungovernable, ill managed, intractable. E.<BR>दुर्, and शासन an edict. दुःखेन शिष्यते असौ कर्मणि युच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=344-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुःशील
दुःशील mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) ill-behaved, reprobate, abandoned.<BR> E. दुर्, and<BR>शील behaviour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=344-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुःषमम्
दुःषमम् ind. Improperly, unseasonable, unfitly.<BR> E. दुर् bad. सम् equal<BR>to; स changed to ष ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=344-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुःषूति
दुःषूति m. (-तिः) A wicked son.<BR> E. दुर्, सूति progeny.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=344-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुःसन्धान|दुःसंधान
दुःसन्धान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Not coherent, difficult to be united or joined,<BR>E. दुर्, and सन्धान uniting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=344-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुःसम
दुःसम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं) Improper, unseasonable.<BR> E. दुर् bad, ill, सस<BR>same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=344-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुःसह
दुःसह mfn. (-हः-हा-हं) Intolerable, difficult to be borne.<BR> E. दुर्, and सह<BR>what is borne.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=344-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुःसाधिन्
दुःसाधिन् m. (-धी) A porter, a warder.<BR> E. दुर् ill, साध् to accomplish,<BR>affix णिनि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=344-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुःसाध्य|दुःसाध्यः
दुःसाध्य mfn. (-ध्यः-ध्या-ध्यं)<BR>	 1. Difficult, arduous, not easily accomplished<BR>2. Incurable or difficult of cure.<BR> E. दुर् ill, साध् to accomplish,<BR>affix यत् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=344-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुःस्थ|दुःस्थः
दुःस्थ mfn. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थं)<BR>	 1. Poor, ill conditioned, badly situated.<BR>	 2.<BR>Ignorant, unwise, a fool.<BR>	 3. Suffering pain or affliction, distressed,<BR>unhappy.<BR>	 4. Covetous.<BR>	 m. (-स्थः) Pain, trouble.<BR> E. दुर् bad, स्था to be<BR>or exist, affix ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=344-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुःस्थिति|दुःस्थितिः
दुःस्थिति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Unsteadiness, instability.<BR>	 2. Unhappiness, ill for-<BR>tune or condition.<BR> E. दुर् bad, &c. स्थिति staying, state.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=344-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुःस्पर्श|दुःस्पर्शः
दुःस्पर्श mfn. (-र्शः-र्शा-र्शं) Difficult or unfit to be touched.<BR>	 m. (-र्शः) A<BR>plant, (Hedysarum alhagi.)<BR>	 f. (-र्शा) A prickly sort of nightshade.<BR>E. दुर् bad, स्पृश् to touch, affix खल्, fem. affix टाप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=344-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुःस्फोट|दुःस्फोटः
दुःस्फोट m. (-टः) A sort of weapon.<BR> E. दुर् ill, स्फुट् to bear, affix अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=344-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुकूल|दुकूलं
दुकूल n. (-लं)<BR>	 1. Wove silk.<BR>	 2. Yery fine cloth or raiment.<BR> E. दु for दुर्<BR>ill, कूल् to cover, affix क; or दु to heat, to keep hot, उलच् affix, and<BR>कू or गू augment, whence also दुगूल ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=344-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुगूल
दुगूल n. (-लं) Wove silk: see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=344-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुग्ध|दुग्धः
दुग्ध mfn. (-ग्धः-ग्धा-ग्धं)<BR>	 1. Filled, full.<BR>	 2. Milked.<BR>	 n. (-ग्धं)<BR>	 1. Milk.<BR>	 2.<BR>Milking f. (-ग्धी) A medicinal plant; also क्षीरी.<BR> E. दुह् to milk,<BR>affix क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=344-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुग्धकूपिका
दुग्धकूपिका f. (-का) A sort of cake made of ground rice, and milk, &c.<BR>fried with ghee.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=344-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुग्धता
दुग्धता f. (-ता) Milkiness, the nature of milk.<BR> E. तल् added to दुग्ध; also<BR>with त्व दुग्धत्वम् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=344-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुग्धतालीय|दुग्धतालीयं
दुग्धतालीय n. (-यं) Milk and mangoes, mango fool.<BR>	 2. The froth of<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=345-a" target="_blank">Page345-a+ 60</a>]<BR>milk, syllabub.<BR>	 3. The skim of milk or cream.<BR> E. दुग्धता, लीङ् to<BR>embrace or adhere, affix छ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=344-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुग्धपाचन|दुग्धपाचनं
दुग्धपाचन n. (-नं) A vessel for boiling milk.<BR> E. दुग्ध milk, and पाचन<BR>cooking<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=345-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुग्धपुच्छी
दुग्धपुच्छी f. (-च्छी) A plant commonly Dugdhapeya.<BR> E. दुग्ध milk, and<BR>पुच्छ a tail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=345-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुग्धफेन|दुग्धफेनः
दुग्धफेन n. (-नं) The froth or skim of milk, syllabub, cream.<BR>	 f. (-नी) A<BR>small medicinal shrub, so called.<BR> E. दुग्ध milk, फेन froth, foam.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=345-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुग्धाक्ष|दुग्धाक्षः
दुग्धाक्ष m. (-क्षः) A sort of stone, (opal.)<BR> E. दुग्ध milk, and अक्ष a die, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=345-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुग्धाब्धि|दुग्धाब्धिः
दुग्धाब्धि m. (-ब्धिः) The sea of milk.<BR> E. दुग्ध, and अब्धि sea.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=345-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुग्धाब्धितनया
दुग्धाब्धितनया f. (-या) A name of LAKṢMĪ.<BR> E. दुग्धाब्धि, and तनया daughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=345-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुग्धिका
दुग्धिका f. (-का) A sort of Asclepias, (A rosea, Rox.) the Hindi deri-<BR>vative Dudhi, is also applied to Euphorbia hirta and thymifolia.<BR>E. दुग्ध milk, and ठन् affix, and the feminine form; the leaves, &c.<BR>yielding a milky sap.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=345-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुग्धिन्
दुग्धिन् mfn. (-ग्धी-ग्धिनी-ग्धि) Milky, having milk.<BR> E. दुग्ध, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=345-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुग्धिनिका
दुग्धिनिका f. (-का) A plant described as a red sort of Apang, (Achyranthes<BR>aspera.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=345-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुच्छक|दुच्छकः
दुच्छक m. (-कः) A kind of perfume: see मुरा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=345-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुडि|दुडिः
दुडि f. (-डिः) A small or female tortoise: see दुलि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=345-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुण्डक
दुण्डक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Fraudulent, dishonest, bad-hearted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=345-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुण्डुभ|दुंडुभ|दुंडुभः|दुण्डुभः
दुण्डुभ m. (-भः) A kind of snake, one which is described as not vene-<BR>mous.<BR> E. द्रुभ् to sink, Uṇādi affix उभ, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=345-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुद्
दुद् f. (दुत् or दुद्) Anxiety, uneasiness.<BR> E. दु to give pain, affix क्विप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=345-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुद्द
दुद्द mfn. (-द्दः-द्दा-द्दं)<BR>	 1. Giving pain.<BR>	 2. Wicked.<BR> E. दुद्, and द who or<BR>what gives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=345-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुद्युषु
दुद्युषु mfn. (-षुः-षुः-षु) Wishing to play with or brandish.<BR> E. दिव् to play,<BR>desid. form, irr., उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=345-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुद्रुम|दुद्रुमः
दुद्रुम m. (-मः) A green onion.<BR> E. दु bad, द्रुम tree; onions being prohi-<BR>bited food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=345-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुधूषत्
दुधूषत् mfn. (-षन्-षन्ती-षत्) Trying to shake.<BR> E. धु to tremble, desid. form,<BR>शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=345-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुन्दम|दुंदम|दुंदमः|दुन्दमः
दुन्दम m. (-मः) A sort of drum.<BR> E. दु bad, ill, दम् to subdue, affix अच्,<BR>नुम् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=345-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुन्दु|दुंदु|दुंदुः|दुन्दुः
दुन्दु m. (-न्दुः)<BR>	 1. A name of VASUDEVA, the father of KṚṢṆA.<BR>	 2. A<BR>kind of drum.<BR> E. दु difficult, दस् to tame, affix डु, and नुम् inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=345-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुन्दुभि|दुंदुभि|दुंदुभिः|दुन्दुभिः
दुन्दुभि m. (-भिः)<BR>	 1. A sort of large kettle drum.<BR>	 2. A name of VARUṆA,<BR>regent of the ocean.<BR>	 3. The name of a Daitya or demon.<BR>	 4. A pair<BR>or couple.<BR>	 f. (-भिः-भी)<BR>	 1. A die or dice.<BR>	 2. Twice three spots on a<BR>dice, or a pair of dice, with three spots on each.<BR> E. दुन्दु imitative<BR>sound, and भा to utter, affix कि or द्यौ heave, उभ् to fill, and<BR>deriv, irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=345-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुन्दुमार|दुंदुमारः|दुन्दुमारः
दुन्दुमार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A sort of red worm.<BR>	 2. The smoke of a house.<BR>	 3. A<BR>cat: other authorities have धुन्धुमार, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=345-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुन्वत्
दुन्वत् mfn. (-न्वन्-न्वती-न्वत्) Afflicting, injuring.<BR> E. दु to injure, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=345-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्
दुर् ind. A depreciative particle, implying, 1. Pain, trouble, (bad, diffi-<BR>cult, ill.)<BR>	 2. Inferiority, (bad, vile, contemptible.)<BR>	 3. Prohibition,<BR>(away, hold, forbear.) It corresponds in general to the English<BR>prefixes, in. un, &c. as in infamous, unbearable, and the like.<BR>E. दो to cut or divide, डुर affix. In composition, the final र is<BR>changed to visarga, and this to a sibilant optionally before<BR>the two first consonants of each class and the sibilants, as दुःकर,<BR>दुष्कर; and दुःसह, दुस्सह; or to र again before any other consonant<BR>or vowel, as दुर्ग, दुरतिक्रम, &c. q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=345-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुरक्ष|दुरक्षः
दुरक्ष n. (-क्षं) A loaded or fraudulent die or dice.<BR> E. दुर्, and अक्ष a die.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=345-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुरतिक्रम|दुरतिक्रमः
दुरतिक्रम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>	 1. Difficult to be suppressed or overcome,<BR>insuperable, unconquerable.<BR>	 2. Difficult of performance or<BR>accomplishment.<BR> E. दुर्, and अतिक्रम overcoming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=345-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुरत्यय
दुरत्यय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Difficult to be passed or overcome.<BR> E. दुर्, and<BR>अत्यय going over or beyond.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=345-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुरदृष्ट|दुरदृष्टं
दुरदृष्ट n. (-ष्टं) Bad luck, misfortune.<BR> E. दुर्, and अदृष्ट fortune.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=345-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुरधिगम
दुरधिगम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>	 1. Difficult to be traversed.<BR>	 2. Difficult to be<BR>read through or studied.<BR>	 3. Insurmountable, difficult to be over-<BR>come.<BR> E. दुर्, and अधिगम going over.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=345-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुरध्यय
दुरध्यय mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>	 1. Difficult of attainment or of acquirement.<BR>	 2.<BR>Difficult of perusal.<BR> E. दुर्, and अध्यय going over.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=345-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुरध्व|दुरध्वः
दुरध्व m. (-ध्वः) A bad road.<BR> E. दुर् bad, अध्वन् a road, अच् substituted for<BR>the final syllable of the last member of the compound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=345-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुरन्त|दुरंत
दुरन्त mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं) Ending ill, having a bad end.<BR> E. दुर्, and अन्त end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=345-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुरपचार
दुरपचार mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Difficult to be displeased or offended.<BR> E. दुर्, and<BR>अपचार offence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=345-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुरभिग्रह|दुरभिग्रहः
दुरभिग्रह mfn. (-हः-हा-हं) Difficult to be taken or laid hold of.<BR>	 m. (हः) A<BR>tree, (Achyranthes aspera.)<BR>	 f. (-हा) Cowach.<BR> E. दुर्, and अभिग्रह<BR>taking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=345-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुराक|दुराकः
दुराक m. (-कः) A barbarian.<BR> E. दुर् bad, vile, अक + संज्ञायां कर्त्तरि घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=345-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुराक्राम
दुराक्राम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>	 1. Difficult to be passed.<BR>	 2. Invincible.<BR> E. दुर्,<BR>and आङ् before, क्रम् to go, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=345-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुराचार|दुराचारः
दुराचार mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>	 1. Wicked, depraved, following evil practices.<BR>2. Disregarding or deviating from established practices.<BR>	 m. (-रः)<BR>Wickedness.<BR> E. दुर् bad, आचार observance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=345-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुराढ्य
दुराढ्य mfn. (-ढ्यः-ढ्या-ढ्यं) Poor, not rich.<BR> E. दुर्, and आढ्य rich.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=345-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुराढ्यकर
दुराढ्यकर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Who does any thing with difficulty though<BR>rich.<BR>	 2. What is done by one not rich.<BR> E. दुराढ्य, कृ to do, खल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=345-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुराढ्यसम्भव
दुराढ्यसम्भव mfn. (-वः-वा-वं)<BR>	 1. Proceeding from one not rich.<BR>	 2. Produced<BR>with difficulty by one who is rich.<BR> E. दुराढ्य, भू to be, खल् मुम् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=345-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुरात्मन्
दुरात्मन् mfn. (-त्मा-त्मा-त्म) Vile, wicked, bad.<BR>	 m. (-त्मा) A rascal, a scoun-<BR>drel, a villain.<BR> E. दुर्, and आत्मन् soul. दुष्टः आत्मा अन्तः करणं यस्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=345-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुराधर्ष|दुराधर्षः
दुराधर्ष mfn. (-र्षः-र्षा-र्षं) Haughty, intractable.<BR>	 m. (-र्षः) White mustard.<BR>E. दुर्, and आ + धृष अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=345-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुराधि|दुराधिः
दुराधि mfn. (-धिः-धिः-धि) Painful, distressing.<BR> E. दुर्, and आधि affliction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=345-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुराप
दुराप mfn. (-पः-पा-पं) Difficult of attainment.<BR> E. दुर्, आप to obtain, खल aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=345-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुरारोह|दुरारोहः
दुरारोह mfn. (-हः-हा-हं) Of difficult ascent.<BR>	 m. (-हः)<BR>	 1. The palm tree.<BR>2. The date tree.<BR>	 f. (-हा) The silk-cotton tree.<BR> E. दुर् with difficulty,<BR>आरोह to be ascended, from रुह् to rise, with आङ् prefixed, affixes<BR>खल् and टाप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=345-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुरालभ
दुरालभ mfn. (-भः-भा-भं)<BR>	 1. Unfit to be touched or taken, difficult of<BR>handling.<BR>	 2. Difficult of attainment.<BR>	 f. (-भा) A prickly plant, com-<BR>monly Jawasa, (Hedysarum alhagi.)<BR> E. दुर् bad, hardly, लभ् to<BR>attain, with आङ् prefixed, affix खल, fem. affix टाप्: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=345-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुरालम्भा
दुरालम्भा f. (-म्भा) A plant, Jawasa: see the preceding. E. As above, नुम्<BR>optionally inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=345-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुरालाप|दुरालापः
दुरालाप m. (-पः) Abuse, scurrilous or abusive language.<BR> E. दुर् bad, आलाप<BR>address.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=345-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुरालोक|दुरालोकः
दुरालोक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Painfully bright, dazzling, not to be looked<BR>at.<BR>	 m. (-कः) Great brightness or splendour.<BR> E. दुर्, and आलोक<BR>seeing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=345-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुराश्रय
दुराश्रय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Difficult of shelter or asylum.<BR> E. दुर्, and आश्रय<BR>resting place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=345-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुरास
दुरास mfn. (-सः-सा-सं) Difficult to be overcome or expelled,<BR> E. दुर्, and<BR>आस् to sit, खल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=345-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुरासद|दुरासदः
दुरासद mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>	 1. Difficult of attainment.<BR>	 2. Difficult of access.<BR>3. Unequalled, unrivalled.<BR>	 4. Intolerable.<BR> E. दुर् with difficulty,<BR>आङ् implying to or up to, सद् to go, affix कर्मणि खल् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=345-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुरित|दुरितं
दुरित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Sinful, wicked.<BR>	 n. (-तं) Sin.<BR> E. दुर् vile, bad, and<BR>इत gone, become. दुष्टम् इतम् गमनम् अस्मात् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=345-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुरिष्ठ|दुरिष्ठः
दुरिष्ठ mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठा-ष्ठं) Very bad, very wicked.<BR>	 n. (-ष्ठं) Great crime, ex-<BR>treme wickedness.<BR> E. दुर् bad, vile, and इष्ठन् superlative aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=345-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुरीषणा
दुरीषणा f. (-णा)<BR>	 1. Curse, cursing.<BR>	 2. An evil eye.<BR> E. दुर् bad, ईषणा<BR>seeing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=345-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुरुत्तर
दुरुत्तर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>	 1. Impassable, difficult to be crossed.<BR>	 2. Unanswer-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=346-a" target="_blank">Page346-a+ 60</a>]<BR>able.<BR> E. दुर्, and उत्तर going over. दुःखेन उत्तीर्य्यते असौ दुर् + उद् + तॄ<BR>कर्मणि खल् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=345-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुरुदाहर
दुरुदाहर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Difficult to be articulated or pronounced.<BR> E. दुर्,<BR>and उदाहर pronouncing. दुःखेन उदाह्नियते दुर + आ-हृ कर्मणि खल् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=346-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुरुद्वह
दुरुद्वह mfn. (-हः-हा-हं) Burthensome, unbearable.<BR> E. दुर्, and उद्वह up-<BR>bearing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=346-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुरुपक्रम
दुरुपक्रम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>	 1. Difficult of access or approach.<BR>	 2. Difficult of<BR>cure.<BR> E. दुर्, and उपक्रम approach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=346-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुरुपचार
दुरुपचार mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>	 1. Difficult of cure.<BR>	 2. Unmanageable.<BR> E. दुर्,<BR>and उपचार implement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=346-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुरुपस्थान
दुरुपस्थान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Unapproachable, unattainable.<BR> E. दुर्, and उप-<BR>स्थान proximity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=346-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुरोदर|दुरोदरं|दुरोदरः
दुरोदर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A gamester.<BR>	 2. A stake.<BR>	 n. (-रं) Playing, gaming. E.<BR>दुर् bad, reprehensible, उदर contest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=346-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्ग|दुर्गं|दुर्गः
दुर्ग mfn. (-र्गः-र्गा-र्गं)<BR>	 1. Difficult of access or approach, inaccessible, im-<BR>pervious, impermeable.<BR>	 2. Difficult of attainment, unattainable.<BR>	 n.<BR>(-र्गं)<BR>	 1. A fort, a strong hold, a Durga or hill fort.<BR>	 2. A pass, a<BR>defile, a difficult or narrow passage over a stream or a mountain,<BR>through a wood, &c.<BR>	 m. (-र्गः) The name of an Asura slain by<BR>DURGĀ.<BR>	 f. (-र्गा)<BR>	 1. The goddess DURGĀ, the wife of ŚIVA, and<BR>mother of KARTIKEYA, and GANESA; also called UMĀ,<BR>and PĀRVATĪ, &c.: as DURGĀ, she is a goddess of terrific<BR>form, and irascible temper, and particularly worshipped at the<BR>DURGĀ Pujā, held in Bengal in the month of Āswin, or about<BR>October.<BR>	 2. The indigo plant.<BR>	 3. A creeping shrub, (Clitotia ternata.)<BR>4. A singing bird, the Syama.<BR> E. दुर् bad, ill, with difficulty, गम् to<BR>go, affix ड; the etymology of goddess is thus given, दुर् with diffi-<BR>culty; गम् to be known; a knowledge of whom is obtained only<BR>by the severest austerities; or दुर् bad, गै to sing, who is especially<BR>hymned by the wicked; or दुर्ग the Asura slain by the goddess.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=346-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्गकर्म्म
दुर्गकर्म्म mn. (-र्म्मः-र्म्मं) Enterprize, difficult undertaking.<BR> E. दुर्ग, and कर्म्म<BR>act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=346-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्गकारक|दुर्गकारकं
दुर्गकारक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Making difficult or impassable.<BR>	 n. (-कं) The<BR>Bhurjpatra or birch.<BR> E. दुर्ग an impervious thicket, and कारक making.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=346-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्गत|दुर्गतः
दुर्गत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Poor, indigent, distressed.<BR>	 2. Suffering pain or<BR>affliction.<BR> E. दुर् ill, गत gone, become. दुर् + गम् कर्त्तरि क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=346-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्गति|दुर्गतिः
दुर्गति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Hell.<BR>	 2. Poverty, indigence.<BR>	 3. A difficult path or<BR>site.<BR> E. दुर् bad, ill, गति going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=346-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्गतिनाशिनी
दुर्गतिनाशिनी f. (-नी) DURGĀ.<BR> E. दुर्गति hell, नाशिनी who destroys.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=346-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्गनिवासिन्
दुर्गनिवासिन् mfn. (-सी-सिनी-सि) Staying in a stronghold.<BR> E. दुर्ग, and निवा-<BR>सिन् who abides.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=346-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्गन्ध|दुर्गंध|दुर्गन्धं|दुर्गन्धः
दुर्गन्ध mfn. (-न्धः-न्धा-न्धं) Ill-smelling, ill-scented.<BR>	 m. (-न्धः)<BR>	 1. Any Ill-<BR>smelling substance.<BR>	 2. The mango tree.<BR>	 n. (-न्धं) Soubarchala salt.<BR>E. दुर् bad, vile, and गन्ध smell. दुःस्थितः गन्धः अस्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=346-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्गन्धिन्|दुर्गंधिन्
दुर्गन्धिन् mfn. (-न्धी-न्धिनी-न्धि) Ill-smelling.<BR> E. दुर्गन्ध a bad smell, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=346-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्गपुर
दुर्गपुर n. (-रं) A fortified city.<BR> E. दुर्ग, and पुर a city.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=346-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्गपुष्पी
दुर्गपुष्पी f. (-ष्पी) A plant, commonly Kesapushpa.<BR> E. दुर्ग with difficulty,<BR>पुष्पी a flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=346-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्गम|दुर्गमः
दुर्गम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>	 1. Inaccessible, difficult of access or approach.<BR>	 2.<BR>Unattainable, difficult of attainment.<BR> E. दुर् with pain or difficulty,<BR>गम् to go, affix खल्; see दुर्ग । दुःखेन गम्यते दुर् + गम कर्मणि खल् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=346-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्गमार्ग
दुर्गमार्ग m. (-र्गः) A defile, a difficult pass or way.<BR> E. दुर्ग, and मार्ग a<BR>road.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=346-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्गलङ्घन|दुर्गलंघन|दुर्गलङ्घनः
दुर्गलङ्घन mfn. (-नः-नी-नं)<BR>	 1. Overcoming difficulties, making way through<BR>arduous passages or affairs, &c.<BR>	 m. (-नः) A camel.<BR> E. दुर्ग, and लङ्घन<BR>who traverses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=346-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्गव्यसन
दुर्गव्यसन n. (-नं) Defect in a citadel, its being ill-guarded, &c.<BR> E. दुर्ग,<BR>and व्यसन misfortune.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=346-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्गसञ्चर|दुर्गसंचर|दुर्गसञ्चरः
दुर्गसञ्चर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Progress or passage through an almost impervious<BR>or inaccessible spot.<BR>	 2. A bridge, &c. or any contrivance for pass-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=346-b" target="_blank">Page346-b+ 60</a>]<BR>ing a river, a defile, &c.<BR> E. दुर्ग a defile, &c. सञ्चर going; also with<BR>संचार, दुर्गसंचार m. (-रः) सम् + चर करणे अप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=346-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्गसम्पद्
दुर्गसम्पद् f. (-द् or -त्) Essential part of a fortress.<BR> E. दुर्ग, and सम्पद् wealth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=346-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्गाधिकारिन्
दुर्गाधिकारिन् m. (-री) The governor of a fort.<BR> E. दुर्ग, and अधिकारिन् who<BR>superintends.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=346-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्गाध्यक्ष|दुर्गाध्यक्षः
दुर्गाध्यक्ष m. (-क्षः) The governor of a fortress.<BR> E. दुर्ग, and अध्यक्ष super-<BR>visor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=346-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्गानवमी
दुर्गानवमी f. (-मी) The ninth of the light half of Kārtik, sacred to DURGĀ<BR>as JAGADDHĀTRI form.<BR> E. दुर्गा, and नवमी the ninth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=346-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्गावरोध
दुर्गावरोध m. (-धः) Investing or besieging a fortress.<BR> E. दुर्ग, and अवरोध<BR>investing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=346-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्गाश्रयण
दुर्गाश्रयण n. (-णं) Taking refuge in a fortress.<BR> E. दुर्ग, and आश्रयण seeking<BR>shelter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=346-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्घोष|दुर्घोषः
दुर्घोष (-षः-षा-षं) Harsh-voiced, roaring, bellowing.<BR>	 m. (-षः)<BR>	 1. A bear.<BR>2. A loud or disagreeable cry.<BR> E. दुर्, and घोष sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=346-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्जन|दुर्जनः
दुर्जन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>	 1. Bad, wicked, vile.<BR>	 2. Malicious, mischief-mak-<BR>ing.<BR>	 m. (-नः) A bad man.<BR> E. दुर् bad, vile, जन a man. दुष्टो जनः<BR>प्रा० स० ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=346-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्जनत्व|दुर्ज्जनत्व
दुर्जनत्व n. (-त्वं) Wickedness, villainy.<BR> E. त्व added to दुर्जन; also with<BR>तल् affix दुर्जनता ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=346-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्जय|दुर्जयः|दुर्ज्जय
दुर्जय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Invincible, difficult to be subdued or overcome,<BR>E. दुर्, and जय victory. दुःखेन जीयते दुर् + जि कर्मणि खल् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=346-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्जर|दुर्ज्जर
दुर्जर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Difficult of digestion, indigestible.<BR> E. दुर्, and जर<BR>digesting. दुःखेन जीर्य्यति जॄ-अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=346-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्जात|दुर्जातं|दुर्ज्जात
दुर्जात mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Inauspiciously born or produced.<BR>	 2. Improper.<BR>	 n.<BR>(-तं)<BR>	 1. Misfortune, calamity.<BR>	 2. Disparity, unconformity, impro-<BR>priety.<BR> E. दुर् bad, जात born. दुष्टं जातम् प्रा० स० ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=346-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्जाति|दुर्जातिः|दुर्ज्जाति
दुर्जाति mfn. (-तिः-तिः-ति)<BR>	 1. Vile, wicked.<BR>	 2. Low, outcaste.<BR> E. दुर्, जाति<BR>kind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=346-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्ज्ञेय|दुर्ज्ञेयः
दुर्ज्ञेय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Difficult to be known or understood.<BR> E. दुर्, and<BR>ज्ञेय to be known. दुःखेन ज्ञायते ज्ञा + कर्मणि यत् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=346-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्णय|दुर्णयः
दुर्णय m. (-यः) Want of conduct, impropriety, impolicy.<BR> E. दुर्, and नय<BR>policy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=346-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्णीत
दुर्णीत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Ill-behaved, ill-governed.<BR>	 2. Impolitic.<BR>	 n. (-तं)<BR>	 1.<BR>Misconduct.<BR>	 2. Impolicy.<BR> E. दुर and नीत conducted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=346-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्णीति
दुर्णीति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Impolicy.<BR>	 2. Misconduct.<BR> E. दुर्, and नीति policy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=346-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्दम
दुर्दम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं) Difficult to be subdued.<BR> E. दुर्, and दम taming.<BR>दुःखेन दम्यते असौ दुर + दम-कर्मणि खल् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=346-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्दर
दुर्दर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>	 1. Tearing.<BR>	 2. Distressing.<BR>	 m. (-रः) A kind of drug,<BR>Rishabha.<BR> E. दुर्, and दर what tears.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=346-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्दर्श|दुर्द्दर्श
दुर्दर्श mfn. (-र्शः-र्शा-र्शं) Dazzling painful to the sight.<BR>	 2. Difficult to be<BR>seen or met with.<BR> E. दुर्, and दृश seeing. दुःखेन दृश्यते असौ दुर् + दृश्-<BR>कर्मणि खल् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=346-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्दान्त|दुर्दांत|दुर्दान्तः|दुर्द्दान्त
दुर्दान्त mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं) Untameable, intractable, difficult to be res-<BR>trained or disciplined.<BR>	 m. (-न्तः)<BR>	 1. Strife, tumult.<BR>	 2. A caff.<BR> E. दुर्,<BR>and दान्त daunted. दुःखेन दान्तः दमितः दमि + क्त वा नि० ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=346-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्दिन|दुर्द्दिनं
दुर्दिन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. A dark or cloudy day.<BR>	 2. Rain, or cloudy and rainy<BR>weather.<BR> E. दुर् bad, vile, दिन a day. दुष्टं दिनम् प्रा० स० ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=346-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्दुरुट
दुर्दुरुट m. (-टः) An atheist.<BR> E. दुर् vile, repeated, अट् to go or be, affix<BR>घञ्, and उ substituted for the penultimate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=346-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्दृष्ट
दुर्दृष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>	 1. Ill seen, (literally or figuratively) ill-examined,<BR>imperfectly investigated.<BR>	 2. Looked at with an evil eye.<BR> E. दुर्<BR>bad, दृष्ट seen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=346-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्दैव|दुर्द्दैव
दुर्दैव n. (-वं) Bad luck, misfortune.<BR> E. दुर्, and दैव fate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=346-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्द्धरुट
दुर्द्धरुट m. (-टः) A pupil who obeys his teacher only after judging of the<BR>propriety or obedience.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=346-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्द्रिता
दुर्द्रिता f. (-ता) A creeping plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=346-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्द्रुम|दुर्द्रुमः
दुर्द्रुम m. (-मः) A green onion.<BR> E. दुर् bad, and द्रुम a tree: see दुद्रुम.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=346-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्द्धर्ष
दुर्द्धर्ष mfn. (-र्षः-र्षा-र्षं)<BR>	 1. Difficult of attainment or approach.<BR>	 2. Haughty,<BR>distant.<BR> E. दुर्, pride. दुःखेन धृष्यते असौ दुः + धृष-कर्मणि खल् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=346-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्धर|दुर्द्धरः|दुर्धरः
दुर्धर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>	 1. Difficult to be sustained or borne, troublesome,<BR>unbearable.<BR>	 2. Irresistible, difficult to be restrained.<BR>	 m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A<BR>division of hell.<BR>	 2. A kind of drug, commonly Rishabha.<BR>	 3. The<BR>name of an Asura or Titan.<BR> E. दुर् bad, ill, धर having, possessing;<BR>it is also written दुर्द्धर । दुःखेन धार्य्यते दुर् + धृ-कर्मणि खल् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=347-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्नामक|दुर्नामकं|दुर्नामकः
दुर्नामक n. (-कं) Hæmorrhoids.<BR> E. दुर्, bad नामन् a name, and कप् added;<BR>see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=347-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्नामन्
दुर्नामन् mf. (-मा-म्नी) A cockle.<BR>	 n. (-म) Piles or hæmorrhoids.<BR>E. दुर्, bad and नामन् a name, fem. affix, टाप् or ङीष्; also in the<BR>first sense, with a final vowel दुर्नामा.<BR>	 f. (-मा) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=347-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्निग्रह
दुर्निग्रह mfn. (-हः-हा-हं) Ungovernable, difficult of restraint.<BR> E. दुर्, and<BR>निग्रह restraint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=347-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्निवार
दुर्निवार mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>	 1. Difficult to be stopped, hindered, condradict-<BR>ed, &c. Invincible, unconquerable.<BR> E. दुर्, and निवार resistance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=347-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्निरीक्ष्य|दुर्न्निरीक्ष्य
दुर्निरीक्ष्य mfn. (-क्ष्यः-क्ष्या-क्ष्यं) Hard to be looked at, as the sun, &c. E.<BR>दुर and निरीक्ष्य to be seen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=347-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्ब
दुर्ब r. 1st cl. (इ) दुर्बी (दूर्बति) To hurt, to injure, to wound, to kill दूर्ब, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=347-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्बल|दुर्ब्बल|दुर्ब्बलः
दुर्बल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>	 1. Feeble, thin, emaciated.<BR>	 2. Weak, impotent.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-ल्) One who is circumcised, or whose glans penis is void of pre-<BR>puce.<BR> E. दुर् implying depreciation or diminution, and बल strong,<BR>potent. दुःस्थितं बलमस्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=347-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्बुद्धि
दुर्बुद्धि mfn. (-द्धिः-द्धिः-द्धि) Silly, ignorant.<BR> E. दुर्, and बुद्धि under-<BR>standing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=347-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्भक्ष्य
दुर्भक्ष्य mfn. (-क्ष्यः-क्ष्या-क्ष्यं) To be eaten with difficulty.<BR> E. दुर्, and भक्ष्य<BR>eating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=347-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्भगा
दुर्भगा f. (-गा)<BR>	 1. A wife not loved or liked by her husband.<BR>	 2. A<BR>bad or ill tempered woman.<BR> E. दुर् little or ill, भग affection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=347-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्भर
दुर्भर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Burdensome, troublesome, hard to be supported.<BR>E. दुर्, and भर what bears.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=347-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्भिक्ष|दुर्भिक्षं
दुर्भिक्ष n. (-क्षं) Dearth, famine.<BR> E. दुर्, and भिक्षा alms; when charity<BR>ceases.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=347-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्भाग्य
दुर्भाग्य mfn. (-ग्यः-ग्या-ग्यं) Unfortunate, unlucky.<BR> E. दुर्, and भाग्य fortune.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=347-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्भेद्य
दुर्भेद्य mfn. (-द्यः-द्या-द्यं)<BR>	 1. To be broken with difficulty.<BR>	 2. Firm, con-<BR>stant, not easily disunited.<BR> E. दुर्, and भेद्य to be broken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=347-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्मति|दुर्म्मति
दुर्मति mfn. (-तिः-तिः-ति) Silly, ignorant, simple, a blockhead.<BR> E. दुर्,<BR>and मति mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=347-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्मनस्|दुर्म्मनस्
दुर्मनस् mfn. (-नाः-नाः-नः) Sad, distressed, meditating or thinking sor-<BR>rowfully.<BR> E. दुर् distress, मनस् the mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=347-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्मर|दुर्म्मर
दुर्मर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Dying with difficulty, retentive of life: f. (-र्)<BR>Bent grass: see दूर्व्वा.<BR> E. दुर् with difficulty, मृ so perish, affix अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=347-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्मल्लिका|दुर्म्मल्लिका
दुर्मल्लिका f. (-का) A minor drama, a comedy, a farce.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=347-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्मुख|दुर्मुखः|दुर्म्मुख|दुर्म्मुखः
दुर्मुख mfn. (-खः-खा-खी-खं)<BR>	 1. Scurrilous, foul-mouthed.<BR>	 2. Hideous<BR>ugly.<BR>	 m. (खः)<BR>	 1. One of the monkey chiefs.<BR>	 2. One of the principal<BR>Nagas or serpents.<BR>	 3. A horse.<BR>	 4. An Asura.<BR> E. दुर् bad, ill, मुख<BR>mouth or face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=347-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्मूल्य|दुर्म्मूल्य|दुर्म्मूल्यं
दुर्मूल्य n. (-ल्यं) Any thing of high price or value.<BR> E. दुर्, and मूल्य price.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=347-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्मेधस्|दुर्म्मेधस्
दुर्मेधस् mfn. (-धाः-धाः-धः) Of little or contemptible understanding, dull,<BR>stupid, ignorant, uninformed.<BR> E. दुर् bad, मेधस् understanding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=347-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्योधन|दुर्योधनः|दुर्य्योधन|दुर्य्योधनः
दुर्योधन m. (-नः) The elder of the Kuru princes, and leader in the war<BR>against his cousins, the Pāndus and KṚṢṆA.<BR> E. दुर् vile, ill, युध्<BR>to make war, affix युच्; the author and leader of an unjust<BR>warfare.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=347-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्योनि
दुर्योनि mfn. (-निः-निः-नि) Of low or impure origin.<BR> E. दुर्, and योनि<BR>place of birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=347-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्लभ|दुर्लभः|दुर्ल्लभ
दुर्लभ mfn. (-भः-भा-भं)<BR>	 1. Difficult of attainment.<BR>	 2. Excellent, eminent.<BR>3. Dear, beloved.<BR>	 m. (-भः) A plant, (a sort of Hedysarum:) see<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=347-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुरालभा
दुरालभा f. (-भा) A prickly nightshade.<BR> E. दुर् difficult, लभ् to gain,<BR>affix खल् but without any nasal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=347-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्वच|दुर्व्वच|दुर्व्वचं|दुर्व्वचः
दुर्वच mfn. (-चः-चा-चं)<BR>	 1. Speaking ill or improperly.<BR>	 1. Speaking in<BR>pain.<BR>	 3. Difficult of utterance or articulation.<BR>	 4. What ought not<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=347-b" target="_blank">Page347-b+ 60</a>]<BR>to be spoken.<BR>	 n. (-चं)<BR>	 1. Abuse, censure.<BR>	 2. Evil or unlucky<BR>speech.<BR> E. दुर्, वच् to speak. दुःखेन उच्यते दुर् + वच्-कर्मणि खल् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=347-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्वचस्|दुर्व्वचस्
दुर्वचस् n. (-चः) Abuse, bad language.<BR> E. दुर् bad, वचस् speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=347-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्वर्ण|दुर्वर्णः|दुर्व्वर्ण|दुर्व्वर्णं
दुर्वर्ण mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-र्णं) Of a bad species or class.<BR>	 n. (-र्णं)<BR>	 1. Silver.<BR>	 2. A<BR>sort of perfume, commonly Elabāluka: see एलवालुक.<BR> E. दुर् bad,<BR>vile, and वर्ण species; the reduplication of the व is optional in<BR>this and the following words. हेमापेक्षया निकृष्टो वर्णोऽस्य । रजते ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=347-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्वर्णक|दुर्व्वर्णक|दुर्व्वर्णकं
दुर्वर्णक n. (-कं) Silver.<BR> E. दुर् inferior, वर्ण species, कन् pleonasm; in-<BR>ferior as compared with gold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=347-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्वह|दुर्व्वह
दुर्वह mfn. (-हः-हा-हं) Difficult to be borne or supported.<BR> E. दुर्, and वह<BR>bearing. दुःखेन उह्यते असौ दुर् + वह-कर्मणि खल् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=347-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्वाच्|दुर्व्वाच्
दुर्वाच् mfn. (-वाक्) An ill speaker, morally or physically.<BR>	 f. (-वा) Speak-<BR>ing ill, either inelegantly or abusively.<BR> E. दुर् ill, वाच् speech.<BR>गर्हिता वाक् प्रा० स० ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=347-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्वाच्य|दुर्व्वाच्य
दुर्वाच्य n. (-च्यं) Any unlucky or ill omened speech.<BR>	 2. censure, abuse.<BR>E. दुर् improperly, वाच्य to be spoken. दुष्टं निन्द्यं वाच्यम् प्रा० स० ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=347-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्वाद|दुर्वादः|दुर्व्वाद|दुर्व्वादः
दुर्वाद mfn. (-दः-दा-दं) One who speaks ill, (grammatically, &c.) or one<BR>who utters abusive or unbecoming language.<BR> E. दुर् ill, bad, वाद<BR>speaking. दुष्टो वादः प्रा० स० ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=347-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्वार|दुर्व्वार
दुर्वार mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Irresistible, not to be prevented or checked. E.<BR>दुर् and वार preventing. दुःखेन वार्य्यते असौ दुर् + वारि-कर्मणि खल् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=347-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्वासस्|दुर्व्वासस्
दुर्वासस् mfn. (-साः-साः-सः) Ill dressed.<BR>	 m. (-साः) The name of a Ṛṣi<BR>or saint, the son of ATRI, and an incarnation or portion of ŚIVA,<BR>famous for his choleric temperament.<BR> E. दुर्, and वासस् vesture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=347-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्विध|दुर्व्विध|दुर्व्विधः
दुर्विध mfn. (-धः-धा-धं)<BR>	 1. Poor, pauper, indigent.<BR>	 2. Wicked, melevo-<BR>lent.<BR>	 3. Foolish, stupid.<BR> E. दुर् bad, ill, विध habit, custom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=347-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्विनीत|दुर्विनीतः|दुर्व्विनीत|दुर्व्विनीतः
दुर्विनीत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Ill mannered, ill trained or behaved.<BR>	 m. (-तः)<BR>A restive horse.<BR> E. दुर् with difficulty, विनीत led, managed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=347-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्विभाव्य|दुर्व्विभाव्य
दुर्विभाव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं) Incomprehensible, inconceivable.<BR> E. दुर्, and<BR>विभाव्य to be observed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=347-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्विवाह|दुर्विवाहः|दुर्व्विवाह
दुर्विवाह m. (-हः) A bad mode or form of marriage.<BR> E. दुर् and विवाह<BR>marriage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=347-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्विषह|दुर्विषहः|दुर्व्विषह
दुर्विषह mfn. (-हः-हा-हं) Difficult to be sustained or supported.<BR> E. दुर्<BR>and वि before, सह to bear. दुःखेन विषह्यते असौ दुर् + वि + सह<BR>कर्मणि खल् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=347-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्वृत्त|दुर्व्वृत्तः
दुर्वृत्त mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं) Vile, wicked, leading a low or infamous life,<BR>following disreputable habits or business, a cheat, a juggler, a<BR>rogue, a blackguard, &c.<BR> E. दुर् bad, वृत्त to be or abide. दुष्टं वृत्तम्<BR>प्रा० स० ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=347-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्वृत्ति|दुर्वृत्तिः
दुर्वृत्ति f. (-त्तिः)<BR>	 1. Leading a disreputable life, following a degrading<BR>business, &c.<BR>	 2. Juggling, fraud.<BR> E. दुर्, and वृत्ति maintenance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=347-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्हन
दुर्हन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) What is killed with difficulty.<BR> E. दुर् before, हन्<BR>to kill. दुःखेन हन्यते असौ दुर् + हन-कर्मणि खल् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=347-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्हृद्
दुर्हृद् mfn. (-द् or -त्) Inimical, ill disposed.<BR>	 m. (-द् or -त्) An enemy. E.<BR>दुर् bad, हृद् heart. दुःस्थं हृद् हृदयमस्य प्रा० स० ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=347-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्हृदय|दुर्हृदयः
दुर्हृदय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Evil-minded, bad-hearted.<BR> E. दुर् bad, ill, हृदय<BR>the heart.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=347-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुल
दुल r. 10th cl. (दोलयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To raise, to throw up.<BR>	 2. To excite.<BR>	 3. To<BR>shake, to swing. चुरा० उभ० सक० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=347-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुलि|दुलिः
दुलि m. (-लिः) A Muni or saint.<BR>	 f. (-लि or -ली) A small or female<BR>tortoise.<BR> E. दुल् to throw up, (mud, &c.) affix कि fem. affix option-<BR>ally ङीष् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=347-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुश्चर|दुश्चरः
दुश्चर mfn. (-रः-रा-री-रं)<BR>	 1. Going with trouble of difficulty.<BR>	 2. Acting<BR>ill, behaving wickedly.<BR>	 3. Unattainable.<BR>	 m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A bivalve shell.<BR>2. bear.<BR> E. दुर् bad, चर् to go, अच् or टच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=347-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुश्चरित
दुश्चरित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Misbehaving, abandoned, wicked.<BR>	 m. (-तं)<BR>Misbehaviour, ill conduct, wickedness.<BR> E. दुर् and चरित conduct.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=347-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुश्चर्म्मन्|दुश्चर्मन्
दुश्चर्म्मन् m. (-र्म्मा) A circumcised man, or one whose prepuce is naturally<BR>or artificially wanting.<BR> E. दुर् bad, difficult, चर्म्मन् skin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=347-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुश्चेष्टित
दुश्चेष्टित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Misbehaving, doing or besieging evil.<BR>	 n. (-तं)<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=348-a" target="_blank">Page348-a+ 60</a>]<BR>Evil purpose or action, misconduct, error.<BR> E. दुर् and चेष्टित exerted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=347-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुश्च्यवन|दुश्च्यवनः
दुश्च्यवन m. (-नः) A name of INDRA.<BR> E. दुर् ill, च्यवन the name of a saint:<BR>INDRA having raised his arm to hurl his thunderbolt at Chyavana<BR>had it fixed in that position by the curse of the saint; other ety-<BR>mologies are given.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=348-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुश्छद
दुश्छद mfn. (-दः-दा-दं) Tattered, hardly covered.<BR> E. दुर् and छद covering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=348-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुश्शासन
दुश्शासन m. (-नः) One of the Kaurava princes.<BR> E. दुर्, and शासन<BR>government.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=348-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष
दुष (इर, औ) इरदुषौ r. 4th cl. (दुष्यति)<BR>	 1. To do or act wrong or impro-<BR>perly.<BR>	 2. To be impure. With प्र and आङ prefixed, To become<BR>manifest or apparent. दिवा० पर० अक० अनिट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=348-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्कर|दुष्करं
दुष्कर mfn. (-रः-रा-री-रं)<BR>	 1. Difficult to be done.<BR>	 2. One who behaves<BR>ill, does wrong, &c. wicked, bad.<BR>	 n. (-रं)<BR>	 1. Æthen atmo-<BR>sphere.<BR>	 2. Doing any thing with pain or difficulty. E.<BR>दुर् bad, and कर what does from कृ with कर्मणि खल् aff. दुःखेन<BR>क्रियते ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=348-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्कर्म्मन्|दुष्कर्मन्
दुष्कर्म्मन् n. (-र्म्म)<BR>	 1. Wickedness, sin.<BR>	 2. Any difficult or painful act. E.<BR>दुर् and कर्म्मन् act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=348-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्कुल
दुष्कुल n. (-लं) A low family or race.<BR> E. दुर bad, कुल race.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=348-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्कुलीन|दुष्कुलीनः
दुष्कुलीन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Of a low or degraded family.<BR>	 m. (-नः) A sort of<BR>perfume, commonly Chor.<BR> E. दुर् bad and कुलीन family or species.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=348-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्कृत|दुष्कृतं
दुष्कृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Done wrong or wickedly.<BR>	 2. Done with diffi-<BR>culty or pain.<BR>	 n. (-तं) Sin, crime, guilt.<BR> E. दुर् evil, कृत done, commit-<BR>ted. दुष्टं कृतम् प्रा० स० ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=348-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्कृतकर्म्मन्|दुष्कृतकर्मन्
दुष्कृतकर्म्मन् mfn. (-र्म्मा-र्म्मा-र्म्म) Wicked, reprobate.<BR>	 n. (-र्म्म) Wickedness. E.<BR>दुष्कृत, and कर्म्मन् act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=348-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्कृतवहिष्कृत
दुष्कृतवहिष्कृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Holy, free from sin. दुष्कृत, and वहिष्कृत<BR>excluded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=348-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्कृतिन्
दुष्कृतिन् mfn. (-ती-तिनी-ति) Wicked, an evil doer.<BR> E. दुष्कृत, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=348-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्क्रम
दुष्क्रम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>	 1. Difficult of access.<BR>	 2. Going ill or laboriously.<BR>2. Ill arranged, unmethodical.<BR> E. दुर्, and क्रम going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=348-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्क्रीत|दुष्क्रीतं
दुष्क्रीत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Dear, bought too dearly or unadvisedly.<BR> E. दुर्<BR>bad, क्रीत purchased: a bad bargain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=348-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्ख|दुष्खं
दुष्ख n. (-ष्खं) Pain in general: see दुःख ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=348-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्ट|दुष्टं|दुष्टः
दुष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>	 1. Low, vile, 2. Weak, impotent.<BR>	 3. Wicked,<BR>depraved.<BR>	 4. spoiled, injured.<BR>	 5. violated.<BR>	 6. Contaminated,<BR>degraded.<BR>	 7. Worthless.<BR>	 f. (-ष्टा) A harlot, a wanton.<BR>	 n. (-ष्टं) A<BR>kind of Costus, (C. speciosus:) see कुष्ठ.<BR> E. दुष् to be corrupt. &c.<BR>affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=348-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्टचारिन्
दुष्टचारिन् mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि) Wicked.<BR> E. दुष्ट, and चारिन् practising. दुष्टं<BR>चरति चर-णिनि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=348-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्टचेतस्
दुष्टचेतस् mfn. (-ताः-ताः-तः)<BR>	 1. Melevolent.<BR>	 2. Stupid.<BR> E. दुष्ट, and चेतस्<BR>the heart or mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=348-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्टता
दुष्टता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Wickedness, badness.<BR>	 2. Contamination, defilement.<BR>	 3.<BR>Violation.<BR> E. तल् added to दुष्ट; also त्वं दुष्टत्वम् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=348-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्टभाव
दुष्टभाव mfn. (-वः-वा-वं) Innately bad.<BR> E. दुष्ट, and भाव nature.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=348-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्टभावता
दुष्टभावता f. (-ता) Wickedness, innate depravity.<BR> E. दुष्टभाव, and तल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=348-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्टमति
दुष्टमति mfn. (-तिः-तिः-ति) Wicked, depraved.<BR> E. दुष्ट, and मति mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=348-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्टवृष|दुष्टवृषः
दुष्टवृष m. (-षः) A lazy ox.<BR> E. दष्ट as above, and वृष an ox.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=348-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्टव्रण|दुष्टव्रणः
दुष्टव्रण m. (-णः) A dull boil or sore, a sinus.<BR> E. दुष्ट bad, and व्रण sore.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=348-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्टान्वित
दुष्टान्वित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Defiled, rendered impure.<BR> E. दुष्ट, and अन्वित<BR>possessed of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=348-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्ठु|दुष्ठुः
दुष्ठु ind. Ill, bad.<BR>	 2. Improperly, incorrectly.<BR>	 mfn. (-ष्ठुः-ष्ठुः-ष्ठु) Ill<BR>behaved, unprincipled, depraved.<BR> E. दु ill, स्था to be, affix कु ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=348-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्पत्र|दुष्पत्रः
दुष्पत्र m. (-त्रः) Chor, a perfume.<BR> E. दुर् bad, पत्र a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=348-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्पर्श
दुष्पर्श mfn. (-र्शः-र्शा-र्शं) Not to be touched, unpleasant to the touch.<BR>m. (-र्शः) A plant, (Hedysarum alhaji:) see दुस्पर्श । दुर् + स्थल-कर्मणि<BR>खल् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=348-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्पान
दुष्पान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Difficult to be drunk.<BR> E. दुर्, and पान drinking.<BR>दुःखेन पीयते असौ खलर्थे कर्मणि युच् । भावे युच् वा ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=348-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्प्रकृति
दुष्प्रकृति mfn. (-तिः-तिः-ति) Of a bad nature or disposition.<BR> E. दुर्, and<BR>प्रकृति naure दुःस्था प्रकृतिरस्य प्रा० ब० ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=348-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्प्रधर्षणी
दुष्प्रधर्षणी f. (-णी) The egg plant, (Solanum melongena.)<BR> E. दुर् with<BR>difficulty, प्र before, धृष् to show, to guide, affix ल्युट्; also with<BR>णिनि affix दुष्प्रधर्षिणी ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=348-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्प्रधर्षा
दुष्प्रधर्षा f. (-र्षा) A plant, (Hedysarum alhaji.)<BR>	 2. The date tree. E.<BR>दुर्, and प्र before, धृष् to guide, affixes अङ् and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=348-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्प्रमय
दुष्प्रमय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Immeasurable, difficult to be measured.<BR> E. दुर्,<BR>and प्र before, मी to measure, खल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=348-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्प्रलम्भ
दुष्प्रलम्भ mfn. (-म्भः-म्भा-म्भं) Difficult of attainment.<BR> E. दुर्, and प्र before,<BR>लभ् to gain, खल् affix, नुम् inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=348-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्प्राप
दुष्प्राप mfn. (-पः-पा-पं) Difficult of attainment, difficult to be got or<BR>reached.<BR> E. दुर्, and प्राप obtaining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=348-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्प्राप्य
दुष्प्राप्य mfn. (-प्यः-प्या-प्यं) Remote, unattainable, difficult of approach<BR>or attainment.<BR> E. दुर्, and प्राप्य obtainable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=348-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्मन्त|दुष्मन्तः
दुष्मन्त m. (-न्तः) A prince of the lunar line, the husband of SAKUNTALĀ.<BR>E. दुर्, and झ affix, मुम्, aug; also read दुष्यन्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=348-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्यन्त|दुष्यंतः|दुष्यन्तः
दुष्यन्त m. (-न्तः) A prince: see that last.<BR> E. दुष् to do wrong, झ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=348-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुस्तर
दुस्तर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Difficult to be crossed.<BR> E. दुर्, and तर crossing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=348-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुस्त्यज
दुस्त्यज mfn. (-जः-जा-जं) Difficult to be relinquished or parted with. E.<BR>दुर् and त्यज abandoning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=348-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुस्सथ
दुस्सथ m. (-थः)<BR>	 1. A dog.<BR>	 2. A cock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=348-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुह
दुह (औ) दुहौ r. 2nd cl. (दोग्धि, दुग्धे) 3rd pers. plu. (दुहन्ति) To milk, (इर)<BR>दुहिर r. 1st cl. (दोहति)<BR>	 1. To hurt, to afflict, to give pain.<BR>	 2. To<BR>kill. अदा० उभ० द्विक० अनिट् । भ्वा० पर० सक० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=348-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुह
दुह m. (धुक्) A milker.<BR> E. दुह्, and क्विप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=348-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुहत्
दुहत् mfn. (-हन्-हन्ती-हत्)<BR>	 1. Relinquishing, parting with.<BR>	 2. Milking. E.<BR>दुह to milk, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=348-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुहितुःपति|दुहितुःपतिः
दुहितुःपति m. (-तिः) A son-in-law, a daughter's husband.<BR> E. दुहितृ a<BR>daughter, in the possessive case, and पति a husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=348-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुहितृ
दुहितृ(-ता) A daughter.<BR> E. दुह् to milk, (the mother,) Uṇādi affix तृच्,<BR>and इट् inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=348-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुह्य|दुह्यं
दुह्य mfn. (-ह्यः-ह्या-ह्यं) To be milked, milkable.<BR> E. दुह् to milk, affix क्यप्;<BR>also ण्यत्प्रत्ययं कृत्वा दोह्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=348-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दू
दू (ओ, ङ) ओदूङ r. 4th cl. (दूयते)<BR>	 1. To suffer or be consumed with<BR>pain.<BR>	 2. To inflict pain or anxiety. दिवा० आ० अक० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=348-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दू
दू f. (-दूः) Pain, distress.<BR> E. दू, and क्विप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=348-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूडभ|दूडभः
दूडभ mfn. (-भः-भा-भं) Unfortunate, distressed.<BR> E. दूर् difficult, दन्भ to<BR>deceive, deriv. irr. दुःखेन दभ्यते असौ दन्भ-कर्मणि खल् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=348-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूडाश|दूडाशः
दूडाश mfn. (-शः-शी-शं) Pained, afflicted.<BR> E. दुर bad, painful, दशि to hurt,<BR>deriv. irr. दुःखेन दाश्यते दुर् + दाश्-कर्मणि खल् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=348-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूढ्य|दूढ्यः
दूढ्य mfn. (-ढ्यः-ढ्या-ढ्यं) Bad, vile.<BR> E. दुर्, and ध्यै to meditate, क aff.<BR>दुष्टं ध्यायति दुर् + ध्यै-क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=348-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूणाश|दूणाशः
दूणाश mfn. (-शः-शी-शं) Destroyed or annihilated with trouble or difficul-<BR>ty<BR> E. दूर् before, णश् to destroy, deriv. irr. दुःखेन नाश्यते दुर् + नाशि-<BR>कर्मणि खल्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=348-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूत|दूतः
दूत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Sent, despatched.<BR>	 m. (-तः)<BR>	 1. A messenger or envoy,<BR>a news-carrier.<BR>	 2. An ambassador.<BR>	 f. (-तिः-ती) A female messenger,<BR>a confidante, a procuress, a go-between. &c.<BR> E. दु to go, Uṇādi affix<BR>क्त, and the vowel made long; or दू to suffer, affix क्त fem. affix क्तिन्<BR>or क्तिच् and optionally ङीप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=348-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूतघ्नी
दूतघ्नी f. (-घ्नी) A plant, resembling the Kadamba: see कदम्बपुष्पी.<BR> E. दूत<BR>a messenger, घ्नी what destroys. दूतं खेदं हन्ति हन-टक् । ङीप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=348-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूति|दूतिः
दूति f. (-तिः) See दूत दु-वा ति दीर्घश्च ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=348-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूतिका
दूतिका f. (-का) A female messenger, a confidante, &c. see दूत, &c.<BR> E. कन्<BR>added to दूति; also with the penultimate, vowel made long, दूतीका ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=348-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूत्य|दूत्यं
दूत्य n. (-त्यं)<BR>	 1. An embassy, a message.<BR>	 2. The abstract state or condi-<BR>tion of a message or a messenger.<BR> E. दूत a messenger, and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=348-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूद
दूद mfn. (-दः-दा-दं) Afflicting, harassing.<BR> E. दू, and द what gives or<BR>occasions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=348-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दून|दूनः
दून mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>	 1. Suffering pain or fatigue.<BR>	 2. Going, moving.<BR>	 3.<BR>Shaken, agitated.<BR> E. दु उपतापे to suffer, affix क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=349-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूनवत्
दूनवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>	 1. Being agitated or distressed.<BR>	 2. Gone,<BR>having gone.<BR> E. दू to be agitated, क्तवतु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=349-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूप्र
दूप्र mfn. (-प्रः-प्रा-प्रं) Strong.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=349-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूर|दूरं
दूर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Distant, remote.<BR>	 n. adv. (-रं) Far, far off.<BR>	 2. Widely.<BR>deeply.<BR> E. दुर with difficulty, इण् to go, Uṇādi affix रक्, deriv. irr.<BR>or दैप् शुद्धौ वा कू ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=349-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूरग
दूरग mfn. (-गः-गा-गं)<BR>	 1. Going afar or a long way.<BR>	 2. Remote.<BR> E. दूर, and<BR>ग what goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=349-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूरगामिन्
दूरगामिन् mfn. (-मी-मिनी-मि) Going far.<BR>	 m. (-मी) An arrow, &c.<BR> E. दूर,<BR>and गामिन् what goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=349-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूरतस्
दूरतस् ind. Afar, far off, from a distance, from afar.<BR> E. दूर, and तसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=349-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूरता
दूरता f. (-ता) Remoteness, distance.<BR> E. दूर, and तल्; also with त्वं<BR>दूरत्वम् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=349-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूरदर्शन|दूरदर्शनः
दूरदर्शन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Foresight.<BR>	 2. Long-sightedness.<BR>	 m. (-नः) A vulture.<BR>E. दूर, and दर्शन seeing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=349-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूरदर्शिन्
दूरदर्शिन् mfn. (-र्शी-र्शिनी-र्शि) Long-sighted, far-seeing, (literally or<BR>metaphorically.)<BR>	 m. (-र्शी)<BR>	 1. A Pandit, a learned man, a teacher.<BR>2. A prophet, a seer.<BR>	 3. A vulture.<BR> E. दूर far, and दर्शिन् who sees,<BR>from दृश् to see, with णिनि affix; also with क्विप् affix दूरदृश् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=349-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूरदृश्
दूरदृश् m. (-दृक्)<BR>	 1. A learned man.<BR>	 2. A vulture: see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=349-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूरदृष्टि|दूरदृष्टिः
दूरदृष्टि f. (-ष्टिः)<BR>	 1. Long-sightedness.<BR>	 2. Foresight.<BR> E. दूर, and दृष्टि sight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=349-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूरपातिन्
दूरपातिन् mfn. (-ती-तिनी-ति) Far going.<BR> E. दूर, and पातिब् who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=349-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूरभाज्
दूरभाज् mfn. (-क् or -ज्) Distant.<BR> E. दूर, and भाज् what shares.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=349-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूरभिन्न
दूरभिन्न mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं) Struck or wounded deeply.<BR> E. दूर, and भिन्न<BR>divided.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=349-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूरयायिन
दूरयायिन mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि) Going far.<BR> E. दूर, and यायिन् what goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=349-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूरवस्त्रक
दूरवस्त्रक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Naked, undressed.<BR> E. दूर, and वस्त्र clothes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=349-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूरवासिन्
दूरवासिन् mfn. (-सी-सिनी-सि) Residing in a foreign land, outlandish. E.<BR>दूर, and वासिन् who or what abides.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=349-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूरविभिन्न
दूरविभिन्न mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं) Unconnected by the ties of nature, of a differ-<BR>ent nature.<BR> E. दूर, and विभिन्न separated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=349-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूरवेधिन्
दूरवेधिन् mfn. (-धी-धिनी-धि) Missile, projectile, (weapons, &c.)<BR> E. दूर<BR>afar, and वेधिन् what pierces or wounds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=349-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूरसंस्थ
दूरसंस्थ mfn. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थं) Remote, distant.<BR> E. दूर, and संस्थ what stays.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=349-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूरसंस्थान
दूरसंस्थान n. (-नं) Being or residing at a distance.<BR> E. दूर, and संस्थान site.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=349-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूरस्थ
दूरस्थ mfn. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थं) Remote, far off.<BR> E. दूर, and स्थ what stays or<BR>is; also दूरस्थित, and दूरस्थायिन्, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=349-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूराप्लाव
दूराप्लाव mfn. (-वः-वा-वं) Jumping far.<BR> E. दूर, and आप्लाव a leap.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=349-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूरावस्थित
दूरावस्थित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Standing being or afar off.<BR> E. दूर, and अवस्थित<BR>situated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=349-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूरीकरण
दूरीकरण n. (-णं) Removing, placing at a distance.<BR> E. दूर, and करण<BR>making, च्वि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=349-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूरीकृत
दूरीकृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Removed, placed afar off.<BR> E. दूर, and कृत made, च्वि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=349-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूरीभूत
दूरीभूत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Remote, far off.<BR> E. दूर, and भूत become, च्वि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=349-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूरेत्य
दूरेत्य mfn. (-त्यः-त्या-त्यं) Far, distant.<BR> E. दूर, and एत्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=349-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूरेरितेक्षण|दूरेरितेक्षणः
दूरेरितेक्षण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Squint-eyed.<BR> E. दूर afar, ईरित sent, and ईक्षण sight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=349-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूर्वा|दूर्व्वा
दूर्वा f. (-र्वा) Bent grass, commonly Durbā, (Panicum dactylon.)<BR> E. दूर्व<BR>to hurt or be hurt, affix अच् or घञ्; fem. affix टाप् what hurts sin,<BR>or is injured by cattle. दूर्वति रोगान् अनिष्टं वा ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=349-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूर्वावण|दूर्व्वावण
दूर्वावण n. (-णं) A thicket of Durbā grass.<BR> E. दूर्वा and वन wood; also<BR>with the final unchanged, दूर्वावन ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=349-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूर्य्य|दूर्य|दूर्यं|दूर्य्यं
दूर्य्य n. (-र्य्यं) Fæces, ordure.<BR> E. दूर far, या to go, aff. यत् । पुरीषे, शट्याम् च ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=349-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूलाश
दूलाश m. (-शः) Which is to be injured with difficulty.<BR> E. दूडाश + डस्य<BR>वा लः । दःखेन हिंस्ये ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=349-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूश्य|दूश्यं
दूश्य n. (-श्यं) A tent. see दूष्य । दू-खेदे सम्पदा, भावे क्विप् तां श्यायते गमयति<BR>अन्तर्भूतण्यर्थे श्यै गतौ क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=349-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूष
दूष r. 4th cl. (दूष्यति)<BR>	 1. To be or become bad.<BR>	 2. To make bad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=349-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूषक|दूषकः
दूषक mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>	 1. Ill, low, contemptible, infamous.<BR>	 2. Spoiling,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=349-b" target="_blank">Page349-b+ 60</a>]<BR>corrupting, contaminating, who or what does so.<BR> E. दुष् to be<BR>vile, affixes णिच् and ण्वुल् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=349-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूषण|दूषणः
दूषण m. (-णः) Rākṣasa, the brother of RĀVAṆA.<BR>	 n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Blame,<BR>fault, defect, offence.<BR>	 2. Spoiling, ruining, vitiating. defiling.<BR>	 3.<BR>Violating, (as a girl.)<BR>	 4. Breaking, (as an agreement.)<BR> E. दूष् to<BR>become vile or wicked. affix भावे ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=349-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूषणारि|दूषणारिः
दूषणारि m. (-रिः) RĀMA.<BR> E. दूषण the brother of RĀVANĀ, and अरि<BR>a foe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=349-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूषयाण
दूषयाण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Vitiating, defiling, spoiling.<BR> E. दूष् to make bad,<BR>शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=349-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूषि|दूषिः
दूषि f. (-षिः-षी) The rheum of the eyes.<BR> E. दूष् to make bad, affix इन्<BR>or क with ङीष् added; also दूषिका and दूषीका ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=349-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूषिका
दूषिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. The rheum of the eyes.<BR>	 2. A pencil or painting<BR>brush.<BR> E. दूष् to make bad, (the eyes, &c.) affix ण्वुल्, or स्वार्थे क वा,<BR>fem. form; also दूषी, दूषि and दूषीका ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=349-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूषित|दूषितः
दूषित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Calumniated, falsely accused, especially of<BR>adultery.<BR>	 2. Contaminated, corrupted, spoiled.<BR>	 3. Violated.<BR>	 4.<BR>Blamed censured.<BR>	 f. (-ता) A girl who has been violated or deflower-<BR>ed.<BR> E. दूष् to become or make bad, affix क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=349-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूषीका
दूषीका f. (-का) The secretion or rheum of the eyes.<BR> E. दूष् to hurt, (the<BR>eyes,) Uṇādi affix ईकन्ः see दूषिका ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=349-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूषीविष|दूषीविषं
दूषीविष n. (-षं) Poison that may be overcome by drugs or charms, or<BR>that does not act upon the system.<BR> E. दूषी rheum, and विष venom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=349-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूष्य|दूष्यं|दूष्यः
दूष्य mfn. (-ष्यः-ष्या-ष्यं) Reprehensible, contemptible, vile, bad.<BR>	 f. (-ष्या)<BR>An elephant's leathern-girth.<BR>	 n. (-ष्यं)<BR>	 1. Clothes.<BR>	 2. A tent.<BR>	 3.<BR>Pus, matter.<BR> E. दूष् to be or become wicked or bad, यत् or ण्यत्<BR>affix, fem. affix टाप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=349-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृ
दृ r. 6th cl. usually with आङ् prefixed (आद्रियते) To reverence,<BR>to revere, to respect. r. 5th cl. (दृणोति) To hurt or kill. r. 1st and<BR>10th cls. (दरति दारयति-ते) To fear, to be afraid of. तुदा० आ० सक०<BR>अनिट् । स्वादि० पर० सक० अनिट् । भ्वा० पर० अक० सेट् । चुरा० उभ० ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=349-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृंहित
दृंहित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Grown, increased.<BR> E. दृहि to increase, क्त affix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=349-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृक|दृकं
दृक n. (-कं) A hole. दॄ विदारे कक् ह्रस्वश्च न कित्त्वम् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=349-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृकाण|दृकाणः
दृकाण m. (-णः) A demigod, presiding over the third part of a sign of<BR>the zodiac, (in Astrology.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=349-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृक्कर्ण|दृक्कर्णः
दृक्कर्ण m. (-र्णः) A snake.<BR> E. दृश् an eye, and कर्ण an ear; whose eyes<BR>are his ears in the opinion of the Hindus, the snake has no visible<BR>external ear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=349-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृक्काण|दृक्काणः
दृक्काण m. (-णः) See दृकाण ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=349-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृक्प्रिया
दृक्प्रिया f. (-या)<BR>	 1. Beauty.<BR>	 2. Splendor.<BR> E. दृश् and प्रिय amiable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=349-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृक्श्रुति|दृक्श्रुतिः
दृक्श्रुति m. (-तिः) A snake.<BR> E. दृश्, and श्रुति the ear; see दृक्कर्ण ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=349-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृगध्यक्ष|दृगध्यक्षः
दृगध्यक्ष m. (-क्षः) The sun.<BR> E. दृश् the sight, अध्यक्ष ruler.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=349-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृग्गोल|दृग्गोलः
दृग्गोल m. (-लः) A small circle on the axis of the earth, within the<BR>greater circle of the armillary sphere, and accompanying each<BR>planetary circle.<BR> E. दृश्, and गोल circle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=349-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृग्विष|दृग्विषः
दृग्विष m. (-षः) A serpent or other such venomous reptile.<BR> E. दृश् eye,<BR>and विष poison; whose eye is venomous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=349-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृङ्मण्डल
दृङ्मण्डल n. (-लं) A small circle within the great circles of the armillary<BR>sphere, accompanying each planetary circle or orbit.<BR> E. दृश्, and<BR>मण्डल sphere.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=349-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृडक|दृडकः
दृडक m. (-कः) A fireplace, or hole made in the ground for cooking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=349-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृढ|दृढं|दृढः
दृढ mfn. (-ढः-ढा-ढं)<BR>	 1. Much, exceeding; (in this sense it is also an<BR>adverb declinable in the neuter gender.)<BR>	 2. Hard, firm.<BR>	 3. Able,<BR>powerful.<BR>	 4. Bulky, massive, solid.<BR>	 5. Strong.<BR>	 6. Confirmed.<BR>	 n.<BR>(-ढं) Iron.<BR> E. दृह् to increase, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=349-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृढकण्टक|दृढकण्टकः
दृढकण्टक m. (-कः) A plant, commonly Dhaliākāra.<BR> E. दृढ much or many<BR>and कण्टक a thorn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=349-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृढकाण्ड|दृढकांड|दृढकाण्डं|दृढकाण्डः
दृढकाण्ड m. (-ण्डः) A bamboo.<BR> E. दृढ, and काण्ड a stem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=349-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृढकारिन्
दृढकारिन् mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि) Persevering, determined.<BR> E. दृढ and कारिन्<BR>who does, (any act.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=349-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृढगात्रिका
दृढगात्रिका f. (-का) Granulated sugar.<BR> E. दृढ firm, गात्र substance, affix कप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=350-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृढग्रन्थि|दृढग्रंथि|दृढग्रन्थिः
दृढग्रन्थि m. (-न्थिः) A bamboo.<BR> E. दृढ, and ग्रन्थि a knot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=350-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृढता
दृढता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Firmness, hardness.<BR>	 2. Steadiness.<BR>	 3. Solidity.<BR>	 4.<BR>Strength.<BR> E. तल् added to दृढ; also with त्वं दृढत्वम् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=350-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृढदंशक|दृढदंशकः
दृढदंशक m. (-कः) A shark.<BR> E. दृढ hard, दंशक a biter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=350-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृढधन्वन्
दृढधन्वन् m. (-न्वा) A good archer.<BR> E. दृढ, and धन्वन् a bow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=350-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृढधुर्
दृढधुर् mfn. (-धूः-धूः-धु) Strong, able to bear a weight or load.<BR> E. दृढ, and<BR>धुर् a burthen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=350-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृढनिश्चय
दृढनिश्चय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Certain, confirmed, corroborated, undoubted. E.<BR>दृढ, and निश्चय certainty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=350-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृढफल|दृढफलः
दृढफल m. (-लः) The cocoanut.<BR> E. दृढ hard, and फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=350-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृढबद्ध
दृढबद्ध mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं) Bound or tied tightly.<BR> E. दृढ, and बद्ध bound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=350-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृढबन्धिनी
दृढबन्धिनी f. (-नी) A creeper, (Echites frutescens.)<BR> E. दृढ firmly, बन्ध to<BR>bind, affixes णिनि, and ङीप्; winding closely round a tree or stem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=350-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृढभक्ति
दृढभक्ति mfn. (-क्तिः-क्तिः-क्ति) Faithful, devoted.<BR> E. दृढ and भक्ति faith.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=350-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृढमुष्टि|दृढमुष्टिः
दृढमुष्टि mfn. (-ष्टिः-ष्टिः-ष्टि) Miserly, niggardly close-fisted, m. (-ष्टिः) A<BR>sword, any weapon with a hilt or handle.<BR> E. दृढ firm, and मुष्टि a<BR>handle, a fist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=350-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृढमूल|दृढमूलः
दृढमूल m. (-लः) The cocoanut.<BR> E. दृढ, and मूल root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=350-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृढलोमन्
दृढलोमन् mfn. (-मा-मा-मं) Having coarse hair on the skin.<BR>	 m. (-मा)<BR>	 1. A<BR>wild hog.<BR>	 2. Coarse hair, bristles.<BR> E. दृढ firm, stiff, and लोमन् the<BR>hair of the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=350-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृढव्रत
दृढव्रत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Observing steadily a religious vow or obligation,<BR>E. दृढ, and व्रत a vow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=350-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृढसन्धि|दृढसंधि|दृढसन्धिः
दृढसन्धि mfn. (-न्धिः-न्थिः-न्धि)<BR>	 1. Strong knit, well fixed or compact, (the<BR>person, &c.)<BR>	 2. Close, compact, free from interstices.<BR>	 3. Closely<BR>connected or allied.<BR> E. दृढ firm, and सन्धि union, a joint, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=350-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृढसूत्रिका
दृढसूत्रिका f. (-का) A plant from the fibres of which bow strings are made:<BR>see सूर्व्वा.<BR> E. दृढ firm, and सूत्र a thread, a fibre, affix क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=350-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृढसौहृद
दृढसौहृद mfn. (-दः-दी-दं) Firm in friendship, constant.<BR> E. दृढ, and सौहृद<BR>friendship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=350-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृढस्कन्ध|दृढस्कन्धः
दृढस्कन्ध m. (-न्धः) A plant, a sort of Mimusops: see क्षीरिका.<BR> E. दृढ firm,<BR>and स्कन्ध stem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=350-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृढाङ्ग|दृढांग|दृढाङ्गं
दृढाङ्ग mfn. (-ङ्गः-ङ्गा-ङ्गी-ङ्गं) Firm-bodied, hard, strong.<BR>	 n. (-ङ्गं) A dia-<BR>mond.<BR> E. दृढ, and अङ्ग body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=350-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृढार्त्ति
दृढार्त्ति f. (-र्त्तिः)<BR>	 1. The end of a bow.<BR>	 2. Great pain.<BR> E. दृढ, and आर्त्ति<BR>end of a bow, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=350-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृढाभक्ति
दृढाभक्ति f. (-क्तिः) A faithful mistress or wife.<BR> E. दृढा fem. form, and भक्ति<BR>attachment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=350-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृढायुध|दृढायुधः
दृढायुध m. (-धः) A hero, one firm in battle.<BR> E. दृढ, and आयुध war.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=350-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृत|दृतः
दृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Respected, honoured.<BR>	 f. (-ता) Cumin.<BR> E. दृ to res-<BR>pect, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=350-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृति|दृतिः
दृति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. A bellows.<BR>	 2. A fish.<BR>	 3. A skin of leather, or a leather<BR>bag for holding water.<BR>	 4. Skin, hide.<BR> E. दृ to divide, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=350-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृतिधारक|दृतिधारकः
दृतिधारक m. (-कः) A plant, commonly Acanpātā.<BR> E. दृति a bellows, and<BR>धारक having; having leaved compared to a leather bellows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=350-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृतिहरि|दृतिहरिः
दृतिहरि m. (-रिः) A dog.<BR> E. दृति here said to mean skin in general, and<BR>हरि who steals, from हृ with इन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=350-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृतिहार|दृतिहारः
दृतिहार m. (-रः) A carrier of skins or bags, a water carrier, &c.<BR> E. दृति,<BR>and हृ to take, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=350-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृन्भू
दृन्भू m. (-न्भूः)<BR>	 1. The thunderbolt.<BR>	 2. The sun.<BR>	 f. (-न्भूः)<BR>	 1. A snake in<BR>general.<BR>	 2. A wheel.<BR> E. दृभ् to fear, Uṇādi affix कू, क्विप् and नुम्<BR>inserted; न being optionally changed to म, before भ, the word is<BR>also read दृम्भू ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=350-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृप
दृप r. 4th cl. (ञि ईर ऊ) ञि ईरदृपू (दृप्यति) 1. To be glad, to rejoice.<BR>	 2.<BR>To be arrogant. to be vain or proud. r. 6th cl. (दृपति) To pain,<BR>to inflict pain, to torture. r. 1st and 10th cls. (दर्पति दर्पयति-ते) To<BR>light, to kindle or inflame. हर्षे गर्वे च अक० दिवा० वेट् । तुदा० पर०<BR>सक० सेट्० । भ्वा० पर० । चुरा० उभ० ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=350-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृप्त|दृप्तः
दृप्त mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं) Proud, arrogant.<BR> E. दृप् to be proud, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=350-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृप्यत्
दृप्यत् mfn. (-प्यन्-प्यती-प्यत्) Being proud or arrogant.<BR> E. दृप् to be proud,<BR>शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=350-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृप्र|दृप्रः
दृप्र mfn. (-प्रः-प्रा-प्रं)<BR>	 1. Strong, powerful.<BR>	 2. Proud, arrogant.<BR> E. दृप् to<BR>be proud Uṇādi affix रक् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=350-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृफ
दृफ r. 6th cl. (दृम्फति) To pain, to hurt. तुदा० मुचादि० अक० पर० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=350-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृब्ध|दृब्धः
दृब्ध mfn. (-ब्धः-ब्धा-ब्धं)<BR>	 1. Strung, tied.<BR>	 2. Afraid, frightened.<BR>	 3. Pained,<BR>tortured.<BR> E. दृभ् to pain, to string, affix कर्मणि कर्त्तरि वा क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=350-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृभ
दृभ (ई) दृभी r. 6th cl. (दृभति)<BR>	 1. To string, to arrange.<BR>	 2. To give pain.<BR>r. 1st and 10th cls. (दर्भति दर्भयति-ते) To fear, to be afraid. तुदा० पर०<BR>सक० सेट् । भ्वा० पर० अक० । चुरा० उभ० ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=350-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृम्प
दृम्प r. 6th cl. (दृम्पति) To inflict pain, to torture. तुदा० पर० अक० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=350-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृम्फ
दृम्फ r. 6th cl. (दृम्फति) To pain, to torture. तुदा० पर० अक० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=350-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृम्फू|दृंफू
दृम्फू f. (-म्फूः) A snake, in general.<BR> E. दृम्फ to give pain, affix कूः see<BR>दृन्भू ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=350-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृम्भू
दृम्भू f. (-म्भूः) A snake, &c.: see दृन्भू ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=350-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृश
दृश (औ ईर) औदृशीर r. 1st cl. (पश्यति) To see. With उत् prefixed, 1. To<BR>see, to observe.<BR>	 2. To anticipate, to foresee.<BR>	 3. To doubt, to think<BR>doubtingly. भ्वा० पर० सक० अनिट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=350-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृश्
दृश् mfn. (दृक्)<BR>	 1. A seer, a looker.<BR>	 2. Wise, possessed of knowledge<BR>f. (-दृक्)<BR>	 1. The eye.<BR>	 2. Sight, seeing.<BR> E. दृश् to see, affix क्विप्ः<BR>also दृशा and दृशि, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=350-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृशद्
दृशद् f. (-शद्-शत्)<BR>	 1. A stone, a rock.<BR>	 2. A flat stone for grinding<BR>condiments upon.<BR> E. दॄ to divide, Uṇādi affix अदि, augment षुक्,<BR>and ष changed to श; the crude form may also be दृषत् or दृषद्, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=350-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृशद्वती
दृशद्वती f. (-ती)<BR>	 1. The name of a river which forms the eastern bound-<BR>ary of the Āryāvarta or holy land of the Hindus, running on<BR>the north-east of Delhi.<BR>	 2. A name of the goddess DURGĀ. E.<BR>दृशद् a stone or rock, and मतुप् poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=350-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृशा
दृशा f. (-शा) The eye. E. See दृश, टाप् being here added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=350-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृशाकाङ्क्ष्य|दृशाकांक्ष्य|दृशाकाङ्क्ष्यं
दृशाकाङ्क्ष्य n. (-ङ्क्ष्यं) A lotus, or rather a kind of nelumbium.<BR>E. दृश् the eye, काङ्क्ष्य to desire, with आङ् prefix, and यत् affix;<BR>desirable as an object of comparison to the eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=350-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृशान|दृशानं|दृशानः
दृशान n. (-नं) Light.<BR>	 m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. The name of an Asura; also VIROCHANA<BR>2. A holy or spiritual teacher.<BR>	 3. A king, a ruler, a protector or<BR>cherisher of the world.<BR>	 4. A Brāmhan.<BR> E. दृश् to see, आनच् Unādi<BR>affix; by whom or which, sight, &c. is enjoyed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=350-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृशि|दृशिः
दृशि f. (-शिः or -शी) The eye.<BR>	 2. A Sāstra.<BR> E. दृश् to see, affix कि, ङीष् is<BR>optionally added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=350-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृशोपम|दृशोपमं
दृशोपम n. (-मं) The white lotus, (Nelumbium speciosum.)<BR> E. दृशा the eye,<BR>उपमा resemblance; what resembles the eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=350-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृश्य|दृश्यं|दृश्यः
दृश्य mfn. (-श्यः-श्या-श्यं)<BR>	 1. Visible, to be seen.<BR>	 2. Beautiful, pleasing.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-श्यः) (In Arithmetic,) A given quantity or number.<BR> E. दृश् to<BR>see, क्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=350-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृश्यत्व
दृश्यत्व n. (-त्वं) Vision, sight.<BR> E. त्व added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=350-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृषद्
दृषद् f. (-पद् or -षत्)<BR>	 1. A stone or rock.<BR>	 2. A flat stone or plate on<BR>which spices, &c. are ground.<BR> E. दॄ to divide, Uṇādi affix अदि, and<BR>षुक् augment; also दृशद्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=350-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृष्ट|दृष्टं
दृष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं) Seen, visible, apparent.<BR>	 n. (-ष्टं) Obvious danger<BR>or calamity.<BR> E. दृश् to see, affix क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=350-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृष्टकूट
दृष्टकूट n. (-टं) A riddle, an enigma.<BR> E. दृष्ट seen, कूट trick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=350-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृष्टदोष
दृष्टदोष mfn. (-षः-षा-षं) Found out, exposed detected.<BR> E. दृष्ट, and दोष fault.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=350-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृष्टरजस्
दृष्टरजस् f. (-जाः) A girl arrived at puberty.<BR> E. दृष्ट seen, (by whom,)<BR>and रजस् the menstrual discharge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=350-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृष्टवन्
दृष्टवन् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Seeing, beholding, having seen.<BR> E. दृश् to see,<BR>क्तवतु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=350-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृष्टान्त|दृष्टांत|दृष्टान्तः
दृष्टान्त m. (-न्तः)<BR>	 1. A science, a Sāstra.<BR>	 2. An example, an illustration.<BR>3. Death, dying.<BR> E. दृष्ट obvious or seen, and अन्त end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=350-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृष्टि|दृष्टिः
दृष्टि f. (-ष्टिः)<BR>	 1. The eye.<BR>	 2. Sight, seeing.<BR>	 3. Knowledge, wisdom.<BR>	 4.<BR>The sight of the eye, the pupil.<BR>	 5. Aspect, (of the stars.)<BR> E. दृश् to<BR>see, affix भावे क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=350-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृष्टिकृत्
दृष्टिकृत् n. (-कृत्) A flower, (Hibiscus mutabilis.)<BR> E. दृष्टि the eye, कृ to<BR>make, affix क्विप् and तुक् added; also with क्त affix दृष्टिकृत n. (-तं)<BR>दृष्टिं करोति ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=351-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृष्टिगुण|दृष्टिगुणः
दृष्टिगुण m. (-णः) A butt, a mark for archers, &c.<BR> E. दृष्टि the eye, and गुण<BR>object.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=351-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृष्टिनिपात
दृष्टिनिपात m. (-तः) A look, a look at or on.<BR> E. दृष्टि, and निपात alighting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=351-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृष्टिपात|दृष्टिपातः
दृष्टिपात m. (-तः) A look, a glance.<BR> E. दृष्टि, and पात falling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=351-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृष्टिपूत
दृष्टिपूत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Kept pure by the sight, i. e. watched, that no<BR>impropriety is committed, or impurity contracted.<BR> E. दृष्टि, and पूत<BR>purified.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=351-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृष्टिबन्धु|दृष्टिबंधु|दृष्टिबन्धुः
दृष्टिबन्धु m. (-न्धुः) A fire-fly.<BR> E. दृष्टि sight, and बन्धु a friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=351-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृष्टिविक्षेप|दृष्टिविक्षेपः
दृष्टिविक्षेप m. (-पः) A leer, a side glance.<BR> E. दृष्टि the eye, विक्षेप casting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=351-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृष्टिविष|दृष्टिविषः
दृष्टिविष m. (-षः) A snake.<BR> E. दृष्टि, and विष poison, venomous in his look.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=351-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृष्ट्वा
दृष्ट्वा ind. Having seen.<BR> E. दृश् to see, क्त्रा aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=351-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृह
दृह r. 1st cl. (दर्हति) also (इ) दृहि r. 1st cl. (दृंहति) To grow, to increase,<BR>to prosper. भ्वा० पर० अक० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=351-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृहित|दृहितः
दृहित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Grown, increased, thriven.<BR> E. दृह् to grow, affix क्त<BR>with इट् inserted; also from दृहि, दृंहित ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=351-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दॄ
दॄ r. 9th cl. (दृणाति) To tear, to rend, to divide or pull to pieces. r. 1st<BR>cl. (दरति) To fear, to dread. क्या-प्वा० पर० अक० सेट् । भ्वा० पर० सक० सेट् ।<BR>दिवा० पर० सक० सेट् । दीर्य्यति ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=351-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दे
दे (ङ) देङ् r. 1st cl. (दयते) To preserve, to cherish or protect. भ्वा० आ०<BR>सक० अनिट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=351-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देदीप्यमान|देदीप्यमानः
देदीप्यमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Shining repeatedly or intensely, glowing,<BR>blazing.<BR> E. दोप to kindle, intense, form, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=351-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देय|देयं
देय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) To given, fit or proper for a gift.<BR> E. दा to give,<BR>कर्मणि यत् affix, and the vowel changed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=351-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देव|देवं|देवः
देव (ऋ) देवृ r. 1st cl. (देवते) To sport or play. भ्वा० आ० अक० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=351-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देव|देवं|देवः
देव m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. A deity, a god.<BR>	 2. A king, in poetical language.<BR>	 3.<BR>A husbands's brother: see देवृ.<BR>	 4. A cloud.<BR>	 5. A fool, a dolt.<BR>	 6. A<BR>child.<BR>	 7. A man following any particular line or business.<BR>	 8. A<BR>spear-man, a lancer.<BR>	 9. Emulation, wish to excel or overcome.<BR>10. Sport, play.<BR>	 11. A term or surname applicable to a Bramhan;<BR>also to a man of the kayestha class.<BR>	 n. (-वं) An organ of sense.<BR>	 f.<BR>(-वी)<BR>	 1. A flower, (Hibiscus mutabilis.)<BR>	 2. A plant, (Marsilea<BR>quadrifolia.)<BR>	 f. (-वी)<BR>	 1. A goddess, the wife of any deity of divine<BR>being.<BR>	 2. A name very commonly applied to the goddess DURGĀ.<BR>3. A queen, one who has been consecrated as well as the king,<BR>(in the theatrical language chiefly.)<BR>	 4. A respectful epithet or<BR>title applied to a woman of the first class.<BR>	 5. Worship, reverence.<BR>6. A plant, (Trigonella corniculata.)<BR>	 7. Another plant: see मूर्व्वा.<BR>E. दिव् to play, (in heaven, &c.) affix अच्, fem. affix टाप् or ङीष् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=351-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवक|देवकः
देवक mfn. (-कः-का-की-कं)<BR>	 1. Who or what sports or plays.<BR>	 2. Divine,<BR>celestial, like a deity.<BR>	 m. (-कः) A proper name, the maternal<BR>grandfather of KṚṢṆA.<BR> E. दिव् to play, ण्वुल् affix; or देव, and<BR>कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=351-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवकर्दम|देवकर्द्दम|देवकर्द्दमः
देवकर्दम m. (-मः) A fragrant paste of sandal, agallochum, camphor,<BR>and safflower.<BR> E. देव, and कर्दम mud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=351-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवकात्मजा
देवकात्मजा f. (-जा) The mother of KṚṢṆA.<BR> E. देवक as above, and<BR>आत्मजा daughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=351-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवकार्य्य|देवकार्य
देवकार्य्य n. (-र्य्यं) Worship of, or oblations to the gods.<BR> E. देव, and कार्य्य<BR>business.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=351-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवकाष्ठ|देवकाष्ठं
देवकाष्ठ n. (-ष्ठं) A kind of pine: (Pinus devadaru.)<BR> E. देव divine, and<BR>काष्ठ wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=351-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवकिरी
देवकिरी f. (-री) One of the female personifications of the modes of music.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=351-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवकी
देवकी f. (-की) DEVAKĪ, the daughter of DEVAKA, wife of VĀSUDEVA,<BR>and mother of KṚṢṆA.<BR> E. देवक, अञ् patronymic affix, fem. affix<BR>ङीष्; also with the vowel changed by the affix, दैवकी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=351-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवकीनन्दन|देवकीनंदन|देवकीनन्दनः
देवकीनन्दन m. (-नः) A name of KṚṢṆA.<BR> E. देवकी as above, and नन्दन a<BR>son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=351-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवकीय
देवकीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Divine, belonging or relating to a divinity. E.<BR>देव, and छ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=351-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवकीसूनु|देवकीसूनुः
देवकीसूनु m. (-नुः) The deity KṚṢṆA.<BR> E. देवकी as above, and सूनु a<BR>son; also similar compounds, as देवकीनन्दन, and देवकीपुत्र ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=351-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवकुण्ड|देवकुंड
देवकुण्ड n. (-ण्डं) A natural spring.<BR> E. देव, and कुण्ड a well.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=351-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवकुल|देवकुलं
देवकुल n. (-लं) A temple.<BR> E. देव a god, and कुल a house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=351-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवकुसुम|देवकुसुमं
देवकुसुम n. (-मं) Cloves.<BR> E. देव a deity, and कुसुम a flower fit for a deity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=351-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवखात|देवखातं
देवखात n. (-तं)<BR>	 1. A cave or hollow a midst mountains.<BR>	 2. A natural<BR>pond or reservoir.<BR> E. देव a deity, and खात dug; not the work of<BR>men.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=351-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवखातक|देवखातकं
देवखातक mn. (-कः-कं)<BR>	 1. A natural pond or one in front of a temple.<BR>2. A natural cavern, a grotto.<BR> E. देव a deity, खात dug, and कन्<BR>affix; dug by divine hands, or in honour of a god.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=351-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवखातविल|देवखातविलं
देवखातविल n. (-लं) A cavern, a chasm.<BR> E. देवखात, and विल a hole.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=351-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवगान्धारी
देवगान्धारी f. (-री) One of the Rāginis, or female personification of the<BR>modes of music.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=351-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवगायन|देवगायनः
देवगायन m. (-नः) A Gandharba, a celestial chorister.<BR> E. देव a god, and<BR>गायन a singer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=351-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवगिरी
देवगिरी f. (-री) One of the female personifications of the modes of music.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=351-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवगुरु|देवगुरुः
देवगुरु m. (-रुः) A name of VṚHASPATI.<BR> E. देव, and गुरु teacher; the<BR>preceptor of the gods.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=351-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवगृह|देवगृहं
देवगृह n. (-हं)<BR>	 1. A celestial or planetary sphere, the dwelling of the<BR>gods.<BR>	 2. A temple.<BR> E. देव, and गृह house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=351-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवचिकित्सक
देवचिकित्सक m. du. (-कौ) The two sons of ASWINĪ, and physicians of<BR>heaven.<BR> E. देव a god, and चिकित्सक a physician.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=351-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवच्छन्द|देवच्छंद|देवच्छन्दः
देवच्छन्द m. (-न्दः) A garland or necklace of pearls, &c. composed of 100<BR>strings.<BR> E. देव a deity, and छदि to cover, affix घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=351-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवजग्ध|देवजग्धं
देवजग्ध n. (-ग्धं) A fragrant grass.<BR> E. देव a deity, and जग्ध eaten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=351-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवजग्धक|देवजग्धकं
देवजग्धक n. (-कं) A fragrant grass.<BR> E. कन् pleonastic, added to the<BR>preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=351-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवट|देवटः
देवट mfn. (-टः-टा-टं) An artist, an artisan.<BR> E. दिव् to sport, अटन् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=351-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवट्टी
देवट्टी f. (-ट्टी) A sort of gull, (Larus ridibundus.) गङ्गाचिल्ल्याम् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=351-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवतरु|देवतरुः
देवतरु m. (-रुः) The holy fig tree.<BR>	 2. A tree of Svarga or paradise, the<BR>Mandāra tree.<BR>	 3. The tree of plenty.<BR>	 4. Any venerable and ancient<BR>tree: usually the place of assembling in a village.<BR> E. देव a deity,<BR>and तरु a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=351-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवता
देवता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. A god, a deity or divine being.<BR>	 2. Divinity; see देवत्व.<BR>E. देव divine, स्वार्थे तल् affix of the abstract: in the first case, अन्<BR>added; of whom the attribute is divinity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=351-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवतागार|देवतागारः
देवतागार m. (-रः) A temple.<BR> E. देवता, and आगार a house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=351-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवताड|देवताडः
देवताड m. (-डः)<BR>	 1. A kind of grass, (Andropogon serratus.)<BR>	 2. A name<BR>of Rāhu, the personified ascending node.<BR>	 3. A name or fire.<BR>	 4. A<BR>sort of creeper: see घोषक.<BR> E. देव a deity, &c. तड् to torment,<BR>affix अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=351-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवताडक|देवताडकः
देवताडक m. (-कः) A grass: see the preceding.<BR> E. कन् added to देवताड ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=351-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवताधिप|देवताधिपः
देवताधिप m. (-पः) A name of INDRA.<BR> E. देवता a deity, अधिप ruler or chief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=351-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवताभ्यर्च्चन|देवताभ्यर्चन
देवताभ्यर्च्चन n. (-नं) Worshipping an idol.<BR> E. देवता, and अभ्यर्च्चन wor-<BR>shipping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=351-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवतायतन
देवतायतन n. (-नं) A temple.<BR> E. देवता, and आयतन dwelling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=351-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवतीर्थ
देवतीर्थ n. (-र्थं) The part of the hand sacred to the gods, the tips of the<BR>fingers.<BR> E. देव, and तीर्थ a shrine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=351-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवत्व|देवत्वं
देवत्व n. (-त्वं)<BR>	 1. Divinity, the abstract attribute of divine being.<BR>	 2.<BR>Identification with a deity, deification.<BR> E. देव a deity, and त्व abs-<BR>tract affix; also with तल् देवता ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=351-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवदत्त|देवदत्तः
देवदत्त mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं) Given by the gods, god-given.<BR>	 m. (-त्तः)<BR>1. The younger brother of Buddha.<BR>	 2. The conch of<BR>ARJUNA.<BR>	 3. One of the vital airs that which is exhaled in yawning<BR>E. देव a deity, and दत्त given; the name is often used in gram-<BR>matical and other examples, in the place of some one, a certain<BR>person, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=351-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवदत्ताग्रज|देवदत्ताग्रजः
देवदत्ताग्रज m. (-जः) A name of Buddha.<BR> E. देवदत्त as above, and अग्रज<BR>elder born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=352-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवदानी
देवदानी f. (-नी) A sort of creeper, commonly Hātighoshā.<BR> E. देव a deity,<BR>and दान a gift, भावे ल्युठ् । fem. affix ङीष् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=352-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवदारु|देवदारुः
देवदारु mn. (-रुः-रु) A species of pine, (Pinus devadaru;) in Bengal it is<BR>usually applied to the Uvaria longifolia, and in the Peninsula to<BR>another tree, (Erythroxylon sideroxylloides.)<BR> E. देव a deity, and<BR>दारु timber.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=352-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवदासी
देवदासी f. (-सी) A courtezan, especially one employed as a dancer, &c.<BR>in a temple.<BR> E. देव a deity, and दासी a female slave.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=352-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवदीप|देवदीपः
देवदीप m. (-पः) An eye.<BR> E. देव an organ of sense, and दीप a lamp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=352-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवदूती
देवदूती f. (-ती)<BR>	 1. A female messenger of the gods.<BR>	 2. A sort of plant;<BR>also मधुकुक्कुटी.<BR> E. देव, and दूती a messenger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=352-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवदेव|देवदेवः
देवदेव m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. A name of BRAMHĀ.<BR>	 2. A name of ŚIVA.<BR> E. देव god,<BR>repeated; god of gods.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=352-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवद्रोणी
देवद्रोणी f. (-णी) The procession of a deity or idol.<BR> E. देव a deity, द्रुण्,<BR>to go, affixes घञ् and ङीप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=352-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवद्र्यञ्च्|देवद्र्यंच्
देवद्र्यञ्च् mfn. (-द्र्यङ्-द्रीची-द्र्यक्) Approaching or adoring a deity.<BR> E. देव<BR>an idol, अञ्च् to go to or to worship, affix क्विप्, and द्रि inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=352-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवधान्य|देवधान्यं
देवधान्य n. (-न्यं) A sort of grain cultivated in many parts of Hindustan,<BR>(Andropogon saccharatus.)<BR> E. देव a deity, and धान्य corn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=352-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवधूप|देवधूपः
देवधूप m. (-पः) A fragrant resin, (Bdellium,) used in the incense.<BR> E. देव<BR>a deity, and धूप incense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=352-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवन्
देवन् m. (-वा) A husband's brother.<BR> E. दिव् to play. अन् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=352-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवन|देवनं|देवनः
देवन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Sport, play, pastime, &c.<BR>	 2. Emulation, desire to excel<BR>or overcome.<BR>	 3. Affair, business, profession.<BR>	 4. Gaming.<BR>	 5. Splen-<BR>dour, lustre, beauty.<BR>	 6. Light.<BR>	 7. Praise.<BR>	 8. Motion.<BR>	 9. Grief,<BR>sorrow.<BR>	 10. A garden, a play or pleasure ground.<BR>	 11. A lotus.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-नः) A die or dice.<BR>	 f. (-ना)<BR>	 1. Service.<BR>	 2. Sport, wanton sport or<BR>pastime.<BR> E. दिव् to play, &c. affix ल्युट्, or युच्, fem. aff टाप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=352-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवनन्दिन्|देवनंदिन्
देवनन्दिन् m. (-न्दी) One of INDRA'S doorkeepers.<BR> E. देव a deity, and<BR>नन्दिन् who pleases.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=352-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवनल|देवनलः
देवनल m. (-लः) A kind of reed, (Arundo bengalensis)<BR> E. देव, and नल a<BR>reed; also read देवनाल ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=352-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवनारक
देवनारक m. (-कः) A superhuman being, also देवनामक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=352-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवनिकाय|देवनिकायः
देवनिकाय m. (-यः) A heaven, a paradise, the residence of a divinity.<BR>E. देव, and निकाय abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=352-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवनिन्दक|देवनिंदक|देवनिन्दकः
देवनिन्दक m. (-कः) A heretic, an unbeliever, a reviler of the gods. E.<BR>देव, and निन्दक a calumniator.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=352-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवनिन्दा
देवनिन्दा f. (-न्दा) Heresy, atheism.<BR> E. देव, and निन्दा abuse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=352-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवनिर्मित|देवनिर्म्मित
देवनिर्मित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Natural, created.<BR> E. देव, and निर्मित made by.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=352-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवपति|देवपतिः
देवपति m. (-तिः) A name of INDRA.<BR> E. देव a deity, and पति master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=352-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवपत्नी
देवपत्नी f. (-त्नी)<BR>	 1. The wife of a deity.<BR>	 2. Sweet potato.<BR> E. देव a deity,<BR>&c. and पत्नी wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=352-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवपथ|देवपथः
देवपथ f. (-थः) Heaven, the firmament, the celestial path or way.<BR> E. देव<BR>a deity, and पथिन् a road, final affix अ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=352-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवपद
देवपद n. (-दं) The royal presence.<BR> E. देव, and पद for पाद a foot; also<BR>देवपाद ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=352-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवपर
देवपर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>	 1. Addicted to play.<BR>	 2. Future, what will be,<BR>(predestined, &c.) see दैवपर ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=352-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवपशु|देवपशुः
देवपशु m. (-शुः) An animal consecrated to a deity.<BR> E. देव, and पशु an<BR>animal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=352-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवपुत्त्री
देवपुत्त्री f. (-त्त्री) A medicinal plant: see पृक्का.<BR> E. देव a deity, and पुत्त्री a<BR>daughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=352-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवपुर
देवपुर f. (-पूः) The capital of INDRA.<BR> E. देव a god, and पुर् a city.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=352-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवप्रतिमा
देवप्रतिमा f. (-मा) An idol.<BR> E. देव, and प्रतिमा image.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=352-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवप्रश्न|देवप्रश्नः
देवप्रश्न n. (-श्नं) Astrology, consulting the stars or gods.<BR> E. देव a deity,<BR>and प्रश्न asking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=352-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवबल्लभ
देवबल्लभ m. (-भः) A tree used in dying, (Rottleria tinctoria, Rox.) See<BR>पुन्नाम.<BR> E. देव a deity, and बल्लभ a friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=352-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवब्रह्मन्
देवब्रह्मन् m. (-ह्मा) A name of the Muni NĀRADA.<BR> E. देव a deity, ब्रह्मन्<BR>BRAMHĀ; BRAMHĀ amongst the saints and demigods.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=352-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवब्राह्मण|देवब्राह्मणः
देवब्राह्मण m. (-णः) A venerable Brahman, one esteemed by deities. E.<BR>देव, and ब्राह्मण a Brahman or देवपूजकः ब्राह्यणः । देवले ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=352-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवभवन|देवभवनं
देवभवन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. The holy fig tree.<BR>	 2. Paradise.<BR>	 3. A temple.<BR> E. देव a<BR>deity, and भवन a dwelling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=352-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवभाज्
देवभाज् mfn. (-क् or -ग्) Belonging to a god.<BR> E. देब, and भाज् what has.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=352-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवभू
देवभू m. (-भूः)<BR>	 1. A deity.<BR>	 2. Svarga or paradise.<BR> E. देव divine, and भू<BR>being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=352-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवभूति|देवभूतिः
देवभूति f. (-तिः) The Ganges of heaven.<BR> E. देव a deity, and भूति being,<BR>abiding. देवानामैश्वर्य्येच ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=352-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवभूय|देवभूयं
देवभूय n. (-यं)<BR>	 1. Divinity, godhead.<BR>	 2. Inferior deification or identifica-<BR>tion with a deity.<BR> E. देव a deity, and भूय being, becoming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=352-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवमञ्जर
देवमञ्जर n. (-रं) The jewel of KṚṢṆA suspended on his breast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=352-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवमणि|देवमणिः
देवमणि m. (-णिः)<BR>	 1. A name of ŚIVA.<BR>	 2. The jewel of KṚṢṆA.<BR>	 3. A<BR>twist of hair on a horse's neck.<BR> E. देव a deity, मणि a jewel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=352-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवमातृ
देवमातृ f. (-ता) A name of ADITI.<BR> E. देव, and मातृ a mother; the mother<BR>of gods.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=352-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवमातृक|देवमातृकः
देवमातृक mfn. (-कः-का-की-कं) Watered by rain, (corn, land, &c.)<BR> E. देव<BR>a cloud, मातृ a mother, and कप् affix; cherished by the clouds as<BR>by a parent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=352-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवमानक|देवमानकः
देवमानक m. (-कः) The jewel worn by KṚṢṆA: see कौस्तुभ.<BR> E. देव a<BR>deity, मान respect, affix कन्. or कप्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=352-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवमास|देवमासः
देवमास m. (-सः) The eighth month of pregnancy; also देवमासक.<BR> E. देव<BR>divine, and मास a month.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=352-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवयज्
देवयज् m. (-यक्) A worshipper of the gods.<BR> E. देव, and यज् to worship, क्विप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=352-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवयजि|देवयजिः
देवयजि m. (-जिः)<BR>	 1. A worshipper of the gods.<BR>	 2. A Muni.<BR> E. देव, and<BR>यजि who worships. देवं यजते यज्-इन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=352-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवयज्ञ|देवयज्ञः
देवयज्ञ m. (-ज्ञः) The Homa or burnt sacrifice.<BR> E. देव, and यज्ञ sacrifice;<BR>the sacrifice appropriated to the gods.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=352-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवयात्रा
देवयात्रा f. (-त्रा) The procession of a deity or idol, or sacred festival<BR>when the images are carried in procession.<BR> E. देव a god, and यात्रा<BR>going. देवानां यात्रा ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=352-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवयान|देवयानं
देवयान n. (-नं) The car or vehicle of god.<BR>	 f. (-नी) The daughter of<BR>SUKRA.<BR> E. देव a deity, and यान going. यायते अनेन या-करणे ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=352-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवयितृ
देवयितृ mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ) Sporting, playing.<BR> E. देव to play, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=352-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवयु|देवयुः
देवयु mfn. (-युः-युः-यु)<BR>	 1. Pious, righteous, virtuous.<BR>	 2. Frequenting holy<BR>festivals.<BR>	 m. (-युः) A deity.<BR> E. देव a deity, या to go, Uṇādi affix कु ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=352-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवयोनि|देवयोनिः
देवयोनि m. (-निः) A superhuman being, a demon or demigod.<BR> E. देव a<BR>deity, and योनि place of production.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=352-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवर|देवरः
देवर m. (-रः) A husband's brother, especially his younger brother. E.<BR>देव् to play, &c. affix अरच् । दीव्यते अनेन दिव-करणे अरच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=352-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवरथ|देवरथः
देवरथ m. (-थः) The car or vehicle of a deity.<BR> E. देव a deity, and रथ a<BR>carriage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=352-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवराज|देवराजः
देवराज m. (-जः) INDRA.<BR> E. देव a deity, राजन् a king, and टच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=352-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवरात|देवरातः
देवरात m. (-तः)<BR>	 1. A sort of crane.<BR>	 2. The name of a king; also Parikshit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=352-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवरूपिन्
देवरूपिन् mfn. (-पी-पिणी-पि) Godlike, of divine form.<BR> E. देव, and रूप form.<BR>इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=352-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवर्षि|देवर्षिः
देवर्षि m. (-र्षिः) A Ṛṣi, a saint of the celestial class, as NĀRADA, ATRI,<BR>MARĪCHĪ, BHARADWĀJA, PULASTYA, PULAHA, KRATU, BHRIGU,<BR>VASIṢṬHA, PRACHETAS; also BHARATA, TUMBURU, KANĀDA, and<BR>others.<BR> E. देव divine, and ऋषि a saint: see ऋषि, and राजर्षि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=352-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवल|देवलः
देवल m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. An attendant upon an idol; a Brahman of an inferior<BR>order, who subsists upon the offerings made to the images which<BR>he attends, and who conducts the ceremonies of all sorts of people<BR>for hire.<BR>	 2. A Muni; according to some authorities, a name of NĀ-<BR>RADA; to others, of a different saint, who is also a legislator, the<BR>son of ASITA and also named ASHTĀVAKRA.<BR>	 3. A husband's bro-<BR>ther: see देवर.<BR>	 4. A holy or virtuous man.<BR> E. देव a deity, ला to bring,<BR>and क aff. or देव-कलच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=352-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवलक|देवलकः
देवलक m. (-कः) The attendant on an idol: see the preceding.<BR> E. कन्<BR>added to देवल ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=353-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवलता
देवलता f. (-ता) Double jasmine.<BR> E. देव divine, and लता a creeper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=353-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवलोक|देवलोकः
देवलोक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. Heaven or paradise.<BR>	 2. Any one of the seven<BR>superior worlds, from earth to the highest or Satya loka, in op-<BR>position to those below the earth.<BR>	 3. The particular sphere or<BR>heaven of any divinity.<BR> E. देव, and लोक a world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=353-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देववक्त्र|देववक्त्रं
देववक्त्र m. (-क्त्रः) Fire or its deity AGNI.<BR> E. देव a deity, and वक्त्र a face,<BR>here implying, mouth; the mouth of the gods, eating or con-<BR>suming the oblations made to them.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=353-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देववल्लभ|देववल्लभः
देववल्लभ m. (-भः) A tree: see पुन्नाग ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=353-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देववर
देववर m. (-रः) A superior or supreme deity.<BR>	 n. (-रं) A divine boon or<BR>blessing.<BR> E. देव, and वर best.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=353-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देववर्द्धकि
देववर्द्धकि m. (-किः) A name of VIŚWAKARMĀ, the divine architect. E.<BR>देव a deity, वर्द्धकि a carpenter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=353-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देववृक्ष|देववृक्षः
देववृक्ष m. (-क्षः)<BR>	 1. A tree, (Echites scholaris.)<BR>	 2. A tree of heaven or<BR>paradise.<BR>	 3. A plant yielding a fragrant resin, (Bdellium.)<BR> E. देव<BR>a god, वृक्ष a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=353-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवव्रत|देवव्रतः
देवव्रत m. (-तः)<BR>	 1. A worshipper of the gods.<BR>	 2. A name of BHĪṢMA.<BR>n. (-तं) Any obligation or vow of a deity.<BR> E. देव a deity, and व्रत<BR>religious obligation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=353-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवश्रुत|देवश्रुतः
देवश्रुत m. (-तः) A god.<BR>	 2. A sacred treatise or branch of scripture.<BR>	 3. A<BR>name of NĀRADA.<BR> E. देव divine, and श्रुत heard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=353-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवसभा
देवसभा f. (-भा) An assembly of the gods.<BR> E. देव a deity, and सभा<BR>assembly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=353-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवसभ्य|देवसभ्यः
देवसभ्य m. (-भ्यः)<BR>	 1. A player, a gambler, a frequenter of clubs or assem-<BR>blies.<BR>	 2. An attendant on a deity.<BR> E. देव sport in general, or gam-<BR>bling, सभा an assembly, and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=353-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवसन्ध|देवसंध
देवसन्ध mfn. (-न्धः-न्धा-न्धं) Divine, relating to a deity.<BR> E. देव, and सन्ध con-<BR>nected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=353-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवसहा
देवसहा f. (-हा) A small shrub: see सहदेवा.<BR> E. देव a deity, सह् to bear,<BR>affixes टाप् and अञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=353-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवसात्
देवसात् ind. In or on a deity, becoming as a deity, appropriate or offer-<BR>ed to one.<BR> E. देव, and साति aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=353-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवसायुज्य|देवसायुज्यं
देवसायुज्य n. (-ज्यं)<BR>	 1. Inferior deification, the state or being of the infe-<BR>rior gods.<BR>	 2. Absorption into or identification with a deity.<BR> E. देव a<BR>god, स with युज् to join or be joined, affix क्विप्, देवसयुज् junc-<BR>tion with a deity, ष्यञ् added, implying the state or condition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=353-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवसृष्टा
देवसृष्टा f. (-ष्टा) Spirituous liquor.<BR> E. देव, and सृष्ट created, made by<BR>the gods.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=353-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवसेना
देवसेना f. (-ना)<BR>	 1. The daughter of INDRA.<BR>	 2. An army or host of celes-<BR>tials.<BR> E. देव Indra or any deity, and सेना an army.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=353-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवसेनापति|देवसेनापतिः
देवसेनापति m. (-तिः) A name of SKANDA.<BR> E. देवसेना as above, and पति<BR>ruler; commander of the hosts of heaven.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=353-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवस्व|देवस्वं
देवस्व n. (-स्वं) The property applicable to religious purpose, endowment,<BR>&c.<BR> E. देव divine, and स्व wealth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=353-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवाजीव|देवाजीवः
देवाजीव m. (-वः) An attendant upon an idol, a low Brahman, subsist-<BR>ing by attendance upon an image, and upon the offerings made to<BR>it.<BR> E. देव a deity, and आजीव who gets a livelihood; also इनि added<BR>देवाजीविन् m. (-वी.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=353-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवात्मन्
देवात्मन् mfn. (-त्मा-त्मा-त्म)<BR>	 1. One with or identified with a deity.<BR>	 2.<BR>Belonging to a deity, consecrated, sacred.<BR>	 m. (-त्मा) The holy,<BR>fig tree, (Ficus religiosa.)<BR> E. देव, and आत्मन् the self or soul.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=353-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवानाम्प्रिय|देवानांप्रिय|देवानाम्प्रियः
देवानाम्प्रिय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. A goat.<BR>	 2. An ascetic, one who relinquishes or<BR>abandons the world.<BR>	 3. A fool, an ideot.<BR> E. देव in the second case<BR>plural, and प्रिय beloved; the beloved of the gods.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=353-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवान्न
देवान्न n. (-न्नं) Rice or food that has been first presented to an idol. E.<BR>देव, and अन्न food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=353-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवापि|देवापिः
देवापि m. (-पिः) The son of PRATĪPA, supposed to be still alive, near<BR>the Sumeru mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=353-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवाभीष्ट
देवाभीष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं) Sacred, dedicated to a deity.<BR>	 f. (-ष्टा) Betel,<BR>(Piper betel.)<BR> E. देव, and अभीष्ट wished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=353-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवायतन|देवायतनं
देवायतन n. (-नं) A temple.<BR> E. देव, and आयतन abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=353-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवायुध|देवायुधं
देवायुध n. (-धं) The rainbow.<BR> E. देव, and आयुध a weapon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=353-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवालय|देवालयः
देवालय n. (-यं)<BR>	 1. A division of heaven, the residence of the gods.<BR>	 2. A<BR>temple.<BR> E. देव, and आलय an asylum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=353-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवाला
देवाला f. (-ला) One of the female personifications of the modes of<BR>music.<BR> E. देव a deity, and अल adopted to, fem. affix टाप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=353-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवार्ह|देवार्हं
देवार्ह mfn. (-र्हः-र्हा-र्हं) Divine, worthy of the gods.<BR> E. देव, and अर्ह fit for.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=353-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवावास|देवावासः
देवावास m. (-सः)<BR>	 1. A temple.<BR>	 2. The holy fig tree.<BR> E. देव a deity, and<BR>आवास abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=353-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवाश्व|देवाश्वः
देवाश्व m. (-श्वः) The horse of INDRA.<BR> E. देव a deity, and अश्व a horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=353-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देविक
देविक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Appertaining to or derived from a deity. E.<BR>देव, and ठन् affix; also देविय and देविल ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=353-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देविका
देविका f. (-का) The name of a river, the Saraju or Deva.<BR> E. देवी, and कन्<BR>affix, fem form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=353-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देविल|देविलः
देविल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>	 1. Virtuous, pious, just.<BR>	 2. Appertaining to a<BR>deity: see देविक.<BR> E. देव, and इलच् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=353-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवी
देवी f. (-वी) See देव ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=353-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवीकोट्ट
देवीकोट्ट m. (-ट्टः) A town, the city of VĀNA, probably DEVICOTTA, on<BR>the Coromandel coast.<BR> E. देवी a name of DURGĀ, and कोट्ट a house<BR>or abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=353-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवृ
देवृ m. (-वा)<BR>	 1. A husbands's brother, but especially his younger brother.<BR>2. The husband of a woman previously married.<BR> E. दिव् to play,<BR>Unādi affix ऋण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=353-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवेज्य|देवेज्यः
देवेज्य m. (-ज्यः) A name of VṚHASPATI.<BR> E. देव a deity, and इज्य a tea-<BR>cher, the Guru or spiritual preceptor of the gods.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=353-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवेष्ट|देवेष्टः
देवेष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं) Acceptable to the gods, wished for by them E.<BR>देव, and इष्ट wished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=353-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवोद्यान|देवोद्यानं
देवोद्यान n. (-नं) A sacred grove, one near a temple or consecrated to a<BR>deity.<BR> E. देव a deity, and, उद्यान a garden.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=353-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देश|देशः
देश m. (-शः)<BR>	 1. A country, a region, whether inhabited or uninhabited.<BR>2. A part, a portion.<BR>	 3. Institute, ordinance.<BR> E. दिश् to point, to<BR>show, affix घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=353-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देशक|देशकः
देशक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Who or what shows, points out, describes, &c.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A ruler, a governor.<BR>	 2. A guide.<BR>	 2. An instructor. E.<BR>दिश to command, affix ण्वुल् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=353-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देशकारी
देशकारी f. (-री) A mode of music, a Rāgini.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=353-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देशकालविद्
देशकालविद् mfn. (-विद्) Knowing what is suited to time and place.<BR> E. देश,<BR>काल time, and विद् who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=353-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देशकालव्यवस्थित
देशकालव्यवस्थित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Regulated by time and place.<BR> E. देश, and<BR>काल time, व्यवस्थित determined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=353-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देशदृष्ट
देशदृष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं) Considered locally, judged as to place,<BR> E. देश,<BR>and दृष्ट seen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=353-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देशधर्म्म|देशधर्म|देशधर्मः
देशधर्म्म m. (-र्म्मः) Local law, the law of usage of the country,<BR> E. देश, and<BR>धर्म्म moral merit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=353-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देशरूप|देशरूपं
देशरूप n. (-पं) Propriety, fitness.<BR> E. देश ordinance, रूप form, essence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=353-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देशव्यवहार|देशव्यवहारः
देशव्यवहार m. (-रः) Local usage, custom of the country.<BR> E. देश, and<BR>व्यवहार practice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=353-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देशान्तर|देशांतर|देशान्तरं
देशान्तर n. (-रं)<BR>	 1. foreign country.<BR>	 2. Longitude or difference of long-<BR>itude.<BR> E. देश, and अन्तर different.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=353-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देशापेक्ष
देशापेक्ष mfn. (-क्षः-क्षा-क्षं) Spying, searching out a land.<BR> E. देश, and अपेक्ष<BR>who inspects.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=353-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देशिक|देशिकः
देशिक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A traveller, a stranger, a so-journer.<BR>	 2. A Guru or<BR>spiritual teacher.<BR> E. देश a country, &c. ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=353-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देशित
देशित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Directed, commanded.<BR>	 2. Shown.<BR>	 3. Advised,<BR>instructed.<BR> E. दिश् to show, and क्त affix, with इट् inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=353-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देशिन्
देशिन् mfn. (-शी-शिनी-शि)<BR>	 1. Of or belonging to a country.<BR>	 2. Showing,<BR>instructing, guiding.<BR>	 f. (-नी) The index or fore-finger.<BR> E. दिश् to<BR>show, affix णिनि or देश्, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=353-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देश्य|देश्यं|देश्यः
देश्य mfn. (-श्यः-श्या-श्यं)<BR>	 1. What is proper to be proved or ordered.<BR>	 2.<BR>Local.<BR>	 3. Present at any transaction, on the spot.<BR>	 n. (-श्यं)<BR>	 1. The<BR>postulate, the statement or exhibition of a question or argu-<BR>ment.<BR>	 2. The fact or charge to be proved or substantiated.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-श्यं) An eyewitness of any thing, one who was on the spot.<BR>E. दिश् to show or command, affix ण्यत्; or देश, and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=354-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देष्णु|देष्णुः
देष्णु mfn. (-ष्णुः-ष्णुः-ष्णु)<BR>	 1. Difficult of subjection, untamable, intract-<BR>able, ungovernable, Liberal in giving, a donor.<BR>	 m. (-ष्णुः) A wash-<BR>erman.<BR> E. दा to give, &c. इष्णुच् Uṇādi affix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=354-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देह|देहं|देहः
देह mn. (-हः-हं) The body.<BR> E. दिह to collect together, affix घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=354-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देहकोष|देहकोषः
देहकोष m. (-षः)<BR>	 1. The skin.<BR>	 2. A feather, a wing.<BR> E. देह body, and कोष<BR>a sheath or covering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=354-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देहक्षय|देहक्षयः
देहक्षय m. (-यः) Disease, sickness.<BR> E. देह the body, and क्षय a wasting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=354-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देहच्युत
देहच्युत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Separated or detached from the body, (as excre-<BR>ment or the spirit, &c.)<BR> E. देह, and च्युत fallen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=354-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देहत्याग|देहत्यागः
देहत्याग m. (-गः)<BR>	 1. Voluntary death.<BR>	 2. Death in general.<BR> E. देह, and<BR>त्याग leaving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=354-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देहद|देहदः
देहद m. (-दः) Quicksilver.<BR> E. देह, and द what gives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=354-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देहधारक|देहधारकं
देहधारक n. (-कं) A bone.<BR> E. देह the body, and धारक sustainer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=354-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देहधि|देहधिः
देहधि m. (-धिः) A wing.<BR> E. देह the body, धा to have, and कि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=354-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देहधृज्
देहधृज् m. (-धृक्) Air, wind.<BR> E. देह the body, धृज् to pervade, क्विप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=354-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देहभृत्
देहभृत् mfn. (-भृत्)<BR>	 1. Living-being.<BR>	 2. Embodied, corporeal.<BR>	 m. (-त्)<BR>Life, vitality.<BR> E. देह the body, भृत् what has or supports.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=354-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देहयात्रा
देहयात्रा f. (-त्रा)<BR>	 1. Death, dying.<BR>	 2. Food.<BR> E. देह the body, यात्रा<BR>proceeding, (to or by which.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=354-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देहला
देहला f. (-ला) Spirituous liquor.<BR> E. देह the body, ला to seize, affix उ,<BR>and टाप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=354-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देहलि|देहलिः
देहलि f. (-लिः or ली)<BR>	 1. The threshold of a door, the lower past of the<BR>wooden frame of a door, or a raised terrace in front of it.<BR> E. देह<BR>here said to imply plastering of cow-dung, &c. ला to have or get,<BR>affix कि or क, and ङीष् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=354-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देहसार|देहसारः
देहसार m. (-रः) Marrow.<BR> E. देह, and सार essence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=354-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देहवत्|देहवन्त्
देहवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Corporeal, inhabiting a body.<BR> E. देह, and मतुप्<BR>aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=354-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देहात्मवादिन्
देहात्मवादिन् m. (-दी) A Chārvāka, a materialist. देह, and आत्मन् the<BR>soul, and वादिन् who maintains; asserting that the body and soul<BR>are one.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=354-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देहावरण
देहावरण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Armour.<BR>	 2. Dress.<BR> E. देह, and आवरण screening.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=354-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देहिका
देहिका f. (-का) A sort of insect, (a flea.)<BR> E. देह the body, affix ठन्,<BR>and ठाप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=354-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देहिन्
देहिन् mfn. (-ही-हिनी-हि)<BR>	 1. Corporeal, embodied, having body.<BR>	 2. Living,<BR>a living being.<BR>	 m. (-ही) The spirit.<BR> E. देह, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=354-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दै
दै (प) दैप् r. 1st cl. (दायति) To purify or cleanse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=354-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैतेय|दैतेयः
दैतेय m. (-यः) A demon, an Asur, the Titan or giant of Hindu mytho-<BR>logy.<BR> E. दिति the mother of the giants, and ढक् affix of descent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=354-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैत्य|दैत्यः
दैत्य m. (-त्यः) A Daitya or demon: see the preceding.<BR>	 f. (-त्या)<BR>	 1. A<BR>perfume, commonly Mura.<BR>	 2. A drug: see चण्डा.<BR>	 3. Spirituous<BR>liquor.<BR>	 4. The wife of a demon.<BR> E. दिति, and ण्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=354-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैत्यगुरु|दैत्यगुरुः
दैत्यगुरु m. (-रुः) A name of SUKRA, regent of Venus.<BR> E. दैत्य, and गुरु a<BR>teacher; the spiritual preceptor of the Daityas, or Titans.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=354-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैत्यदेव|दैत्यदेवः
दैत्यदेव m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. A name of VARUṆA, deity of the waters.<BR>	 2. Air or<BR>wind personified.<BR> E. दैत्य a demon, and देव a god.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=354-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैत्यपुरोधस्
दैत्यपुरोधस् m. (-धाः) A name of SUKRA.<BR> E. दैत्य, and पुरोधस् a family<BR>priest: see दैत्यगुरु ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=354-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैत्यपुरोहित
दैत्यपुरोहित m. (-तः) A name of SUKRA, regent of Venus.<BR> E. दैत्य, and<BR>पुरोहित a family priest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=354-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैत्यमातृ
दैत्यमातृ f. (-ता) A name of DITI, the mother of the Titanic race of<BR>Daityas.<BR> E. दैत्य, and मातृ a mother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=354-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैत्यमेदजा
दैत्यमेदजा f. (-जा) the earth.<BR> E. दैत्य, मेद marrow, ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=354-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैत्ययुग|दैत्ययुगं
दैत्ययुग m. (-गः) An age of the demons, consisting of 12,000 divine<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=354-b" target="_blank">Page354-b+ 60</a>]<BR>years, or the sum the four Yugs or ages of men.<BR> E. दैत्य a demon,<BR>and युग an age.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=354-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैत्यारि|दैत्यारिः
दैत्यारि m. (-रिः)<BR>	 1. A name of VIṢṆU.<BR>	 2. a deity in general.<BR> E. दैत्य,<BR>and अरि a foe; the enemy of the Daityas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=354-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैत्याहोरात्र|दैत्याहोरात्रं|दैत्याहोरात्रः
दैत्याहोरात्र m. (-त्रः) A day and night of demons, being a year of mortals.<BR>E. दैत्य a demon, अहन् a day, and रात्रि a night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=354-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैन|दैनं
दैन mfn. (-नः-नी-नं) Diurnal, daily, relating to a day.<BR>	 n. (-नं) Poverty,<BR>wretchedness.<BR> E. दीन or दिन and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=354-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैनन्दिन|दैनंदिन|दैनन्दिनं
दैनन्दिन mfn. (-नः-नी-नं) Diurnal, quotidian.<BR> E. दिनदिन day by day अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=354-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैनन्दिनप्रलय|दैनंदिनप्रलय|दैनन्दिनप्रलयः
दैनन्दिनप्रलय m. (-यः) Destruction of the world after fifteen years of<BR>BRAMHA'S age.<BR> E. दैनन्दिन, and प्रलय destruction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=354-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैनार|दैनारं
दैनार mfn. (-रः-री-रं) Bought with a Dinar, of the value of one, &c. E.<BR>दीनार, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=354-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैनिक
दैनिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Diurnal, of or relating to a day.<BR>	 f. (-की) A day's<BR>hire wages.<BR> E. दिन a day, affix ठञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=354-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैन्य|दैन्यं
दैन्य n. (-न्यं)<BR>	 1. Meanness, covetousness.<BR>	 2. Poverty, humbleness.<BR> E. दीन<BR>a pauper, &c. ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=354-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैप|दैपं
दैप mfn. (-पः-पी-पं) Relating or belonging to a lamp.<BR> E. दीप, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=354-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैर्घ्य|दैर्घ्यं
दैर्घ्य n. (-र्घ्यं) Length.<BR> E. दीर्घ long, ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=354-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैव|दैवं|दैवः
दैव mfn. (-वः-वी-वं) Of or relating to divinity or a deity, divine, celestial,<BR>&c.<BR>	 mn. (-वः-वं) Destiny, fate, fortune.<BR>	 n. (-वं)<BR>	 1. The part of the<BR>hand sacred to the gods; the tips of the fingers, (some exclude<BR>the thumbs.)<BR>	 2. One of the forms of marriage; the gift of a<BR>daughter at a sacrifice to the officiating priest.<BR>	 f. (-वी) a division of<BR>medicine, the medical use of charms, &c.<BR> E. देव a deity, and अण्<BR>affix of reference or relation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=354-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैवकर्म्मन्|दैवकर्मन्
दैवकर्म्मन् n. (-र्म्म) Burnt-offering, oblations to the gods.<BR> E. दैव, and कर्म्म rite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=354-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैवकी
दैवकी f. (-की) The mother of KṚṢṆA.<BR> E. दैवक father of the lady, affix<BR>of descend अण्, fem. affix ङीष्ः see देवकी ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=354-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैवकीनन्दन|दैवकीनन्दनः
दैवकीनन्दन m. (-नः) KṚṢṆA.<BR> E. दैवकी as above, नन्दन a son; also दैवकीनन्दन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=354-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैवकोविद
दैवकोविद mf. (-दः-दा) A conjuror or fortuneteller.<BR> E. दैव fortune, and<BR>कोविद skillful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=354-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैवचिन्तक|दैवचिंतक|दैवचिन्तकः
दैवचिन्तक m. (-कः) A fatalist.<BR> E. दैव, and चिन्तक who thinks of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=354-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैवचिन्ता
दैवचिन्ता f. (-न्ता) Fatalism, reliance on fate.<BR> E. दैव, and चिन्ता thinking<BR>also दैवचिन्तनम् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=354-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैवज्ञ|दैवज्ञः
दैवज्ञ mfn. (-ज्ञः-ज्ञा-ज्ञं) Prophetic, fore-telling, acquainted with fate.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-ज्ञः) An astrologer.<BR>	 f. (-ज्ञा) A female fortuneteller.<BR> E. दैव, and ज्ञ<BR>who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=354-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैवत|दैवतः
दैवत mfn. (-तः-ती-तं)<BR>	 1. Of or relating to a god.<BR>	 mn. (-तः-तं)<BR>	 1. A god, a<BR>deity.<BR>	 2. An idol.<BR>	 n. (-तं) A number of gods.<BR> E. देवता a deity, अण्<BR>pleonastic dor referential affix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=354-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैवदीप|दैवदीपः
दैवदीप m. (-पः)<BR>	 1. The eye.<BR>	 2. A heavenly lamp.<BR> E. देव, and दीप a lamp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=354-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैवदुर्विपाक|दैवदुर्विपाकः
दैवदुर्विपाक m. (-कः) Hardness of fortune, unpropitiousness of fate. E.<BR>दैव, and दुर्विपाक unfavourableness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=354-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैवपर|दैवपरः
दैवपर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>	 1. Fated, willed, predestined.<BR>	 2. Trusting to fate,<BR>a fatalist.<BR> E. दैव fate, &c. पर after, according to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=354-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैवप्रश्न|दैवप्रश्नः
दैवप्रश्न m. (-श्न) Astrology, fortune-telling.<BR> E. दैव fate. &c. प्रश्न asking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=354-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैवयुग|दैवयुगं
दैवयुग m. (-गः) An age of the gods or immortals: see दैत्ययुग ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=354-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैवयोग|दैवयोगः
दैवयोग m. (-गः) The occurrence of unforeseen event, the intervention of<BR>destiny.<BR> E. दैव, and योग juncture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=354-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैवलक|दैवलकः
दैवलक m. (-कः) The servant or worshipper of an evil spirit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=354-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैवलेखक|दैवलेखकः
दैवलेखक m. (-कः) An astrologer, a fortuneteller.<BR> E. दैव fate लिख to<BR>write, ण्वुल aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=354-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैववाणी
दैववाणी f. (-णी) A voice from heaven.<BR> E. दैव and वाणी speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=354-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैवाकरि|दैवाकरिः
दैवाकरि m. (-रिः)<BR>	 1. YAMA.<BR>	 2. SATURN.<BR>	 f. (-री) YAMUNĀ.<BR> E. दिवाकर the<BR>sun, and इञ् patron. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=354-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैवात्
दैवात् ind. By chance, by accident, unavoidably, fatally. E. The 5th<BR>case of दैव used as a participle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=354-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैवानुरोधिन्
दैवानुरोधिन् mfn. (-धी-धिनी-धि) Subject or obedient to the gods.<BR> E. दैव<BR>divine (will), अनुरोधिन् assenting to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=354-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैवायत्त
दैवायत्त mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं) Dependant upon destiny.<BR> E. दैव, and आयत्त<BR>subject to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=355-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैवासुर|दैवासुरं
दैवासुर n. (-रं) The natural enmity between the gods and Asurs.<BR> E. दैव,<BR>and असुर, with अण् added in this sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=355-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैवाहोरात्र|दैवाहोरात्रः
दैवाहोरात्र m. (-त्रः) A day of the gods, the human year: see दैत्याहोरात्र ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=355-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैविक|दैविकः
दैविक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Of or relating to the gods, divine, deific, &c.<BR>E. देव a deity, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=355-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैवोढा
दैवोढा f. (-ढा) A woman married according to the Daiva ritual.<BR> E. दैव,<BR>and ऊढा married.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=355-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैवोपहत
दैवोपहत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Ill-fated, unfortunate, unlucky.<BR> E. दैव, and<BR>उपहत struck by; also with कन्, दैवोपहतकः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=355-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैव्य|दैव्यं
दैव्य n. (-व्यं) Gate, fortune.<BR> E. देव a deity and यञ् affix: see दैव ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=355-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैशिक|दैशिकं|दैशिकः
दैशिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Provincial, national, belonging to a country,<BR>produced in it, &c. देश, and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=355-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैष्टिक|दैष्टिकः
दैष्टिक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Fated, predestined.<BR>	 m. (-कः) A predestinarian,<BR>a fatalist.<BR> E. दिष्ट fate, affix ठक् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=355-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैष्टिकता
दैष्टिकता f. (-ता) Fatalism, predestinarianism.<BR> E. तल् added to दैष्टिक;<BR>with त्व, दैष्टिकत्वम् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=355-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैहिक|दैहिकं
दैहिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Corporeal, bodily.<BR> E. देहे भवः तस्थ इदं वा ठक् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=355-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दो
दो r. 4th cl. (द्यति) To cut, to divide: अव is usually prefixed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=355-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोग
दोग m. (-गः) A bull.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=355-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोःशिखर|दोःशिखरं
दोःशिखर n. (-रं) The shoulder.<BR> E. दोस्, and शिखर crest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=355-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोःसहस्रभृत्
दोःसहस्रभृत् m. (-भृत्) The name of a king, also called KĀRTA-VĪRYA.<BR>E. दोस् an arm, सहस्र a thousand, and भृत् possessing: having a<BR>thousand arms.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=355-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोग्धृ
दोग्धृ mfn. (-ग्धा-ग्ध्री-ग्धृ)<BR>	 1. A milker, who or what milks.<BR>	 2. What<BR>yields milk.<BR>	 m. (-ग्धा)<BR>	 1. A poet, a panegyrist, one who writes<BR>verses for hire or reward.<BR>	 2. A calf.<BR>	 3. A cowherd.<BR>	 f. (-ग्धी) A<BR>cow.<BR> E. दुह् to milk, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=355-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोदुल्यमान|दोदुल्यमानः
दोदुल्यमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Swinging or being swung repeatedly or<BR>violently.<BR> E. दुल् to swing, intens, form, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=355-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोध|दोधः
दोध m. (-धः) A calf.<BR> E. दुह् to milk, घञ् affix, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=355-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोधक|दोधकः
दोधक n. (-कं) A form of metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=355-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोधूयमान|दोधूयमानः
दोधूयमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Shaking or trembling violently<BR> E. धू to shake,<BR>intens. form, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=355-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोरक|दोरकं|दोरकः
दोरक mf. (-रकः-रिका) A string for fastening the wires of a lute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=355-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोर्गडु|दोर्गडुः
दोर्गडु mfn. (-डुः-डुः-डु) Crooked-armed. having a cripple or crooked arm.<BR>E. दोस् an arm, and गडु a cripple.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=355-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोर्ग्रह|दोर्ग्रहः
दोर्ग्रह mfn. (-हः-हा-हं) Strong, powerful.<BR>	 m. (-हः) Pain in the arm. E.<BR>दोस् an arm, and ग्रह who takes or uses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=355-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोर्दण्ड|दोर्दंड|दोर्दण्डः
दोर्दण्ड m. (-ण्डः) The arm.<BR> E. दोस्, and दण्ड a stick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=355-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोर्मध्य|दोर्मध्यं
दोर्मध्य n. (-ध्यं) The middle of the arm.<BR> E. दोस् the arm, and मध्य the<BR>centre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=355-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोर्मूल|दोर्मूलं
दोर्मूल n. (-लं) The armpit.<BR> E. दोस् the arm, and मूल the root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=355-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोल|दोलः
दोल m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. Swinging.<BR>	 2. A festival on the 14th of Phālgun, the<BR>swinging of the juvenile KṚṢṆA.<BR>	 m. (-लः-ला or ली)<BR>	 1. A litter, a<BR>swinging cot, a dooly.<BR>	 2. A swing.<BR>	 f. (-ला) The indigo plant.<BR> E. दुल्<BR>to throw up or toss, to swing, affix अच्; fem. affix टाप् or ङीष् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=355-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोलायमान|दोलायमानः
दोलायमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>	 1. Swinging, being swung.<BR>	 2. Doubting,<BR>perplexed, vacillating.<BR> E. दुल् to swing, causal form, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=355-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोलिका
दोलिका f. (-का) A swing.<BR> E. कन् added to दोली ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=355-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोष|दोषः
दोष m. (-षः)<BR>	 1. Fault, defect, blemish.<BR>	 2. Sin, offence, transgression.<BR>3. Disorder of the humours of the body, or defect in the functions<BR>of bile, circulation, or wind.<BR>	 4. A calf.<BR> E. दुष् to be defective, affix<BR>घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=355-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोषक|दोषकः
दोषक m. (-कः) A calf.<BR> E. कन् added to दोष ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=355-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोषकल्पन
दोषकल्पन n. (-नं) Reprehending, condemning.<BR> E. दोष, and कल्पन<BR>attributing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=355-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोषग्राहिन्
दोषग्राहिन् mfn. (-ही-हिणी-हि) Malicious, malignant, censorious.<BR> E. दोष a<BR>fault, ग्रह् to take, affix णिनि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=355-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोषज्ञ|दोषज्ञः
दोषज्ञ mfn. (-ज्ञः-ज्ञा-ज्ञं) Knowing faults, &c.<BR>	 m. (-ज्ञः)<BR>	 1. A Pandit, a<BR>teacher, a sage.<BR>	 2. A physician.<BR> E. दोष fault, defect, and ज्ञ who<BR>knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=355-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोषत्रय|दोषत्रयं
दोषत्रय n. (-यं)<BR>	 1. Vitiation of the three humours, bile, wind, and phlegm.<BR>2. Any combination of three defects.<BR> E. दोष, and त्रय triad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=355-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोषप्रसङ्ग|दोषप्रसंग|दोषप्रसंगः
दोषप्रसङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः) Censure, condemnation.<BR> E. दोष, and प्रसङ्ग attribution.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=355-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोषभाज्
दोषभाज् mfn. (-भाक्) Wrong, faulty, doing wrong, being defective or<BR>to blame.<BR> E. दोष, and भाज् who or what shares.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=355-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोषवत्|दोषवन्त्
दोषवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>	 1. Faulty, defective.<BR>	 2. wicked.<BR> E. दोष, and<BR>मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=355-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोषा
दोषा f. (-षा)<BR>	 1. Night.<BR>	 2. The arm. ind. (-षा)<BR>	 1. By night, at night.<BR>	 2.<BR>At the beginning of the night.<BR> E. दम् to tame, ङीस् affix, and टाप्<BR>added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=355-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोषाकर|दोषाकरः
दोषाकर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Defective, faulty.<BR>	 m. (-रः) The moon.<BR> E. दोषा<BR>night, and कर a ray, or दोष and आकर a mine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=355-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोषातन|दोषातनः
दोषातन mfn. (-नः-नी-नं) Nocturnal, by night.<BR> E. दोषा by night, द्यु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=355-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोषातिलक|दोषातिलकः
दोषातिलक m. (-कः) A lamp.<BR> E. दोष night, and तिलक excellence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=355-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोषास्य|दोषास्यः
दोषास्य m. (-स्यः) A lamp.<BR> E. दोषा night, and आस्य a face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=355-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोषिक|दोषिकः
दोषिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Faulty, defective, bad.<BR>	 m. (-कः) Sickness,<BR>disease.<BR> E. दोष defect, ठन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=355-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोषिन्
दोषिन् mfn. (-षी-षिणी-षि)<BR>	 1. Faulty, defective.<BR>	 2. Wicked, bad.<BR> E. दुष् to<BR>be defective, affix णिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=355-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोषैकदृश्
दोषैकदृश् mfn. (-दृक्) Malevolent, censorious, discovering defects only.<BR>E. दोष a fault. एक one, alone, and दृष् seeing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=355-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोस
दोस m. (-दोः)<BR>	 1. The arm.<BR>	 2. The side of a triangle, or square, &c. E.<BR>दम् to subdue, affix डोम् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=355-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोस्क
दोस्क mfn. (-स्कः-स्का-स्कं) Worn, &c. on the arms.<BR> E. दोस् the arm, क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=355-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोस्थ|दोस्थः
दोस्थ mfn. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थं) Placed on the arm.<BR>	 m. (-स्थः)<BR>	 1. Play, sport.<BR>2. player, one who sports or plays.<BR>	 3. Service.<BR>	 4. A servant.<BR> E. दु<BR>bad, स्था to stay, ड affix दुस्थ, अण् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=355-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोह|दोहः
दोह m. (-हः)<BR>	 1. A milk-pail.<BR>	 2. Milk.<BR>	 3. Milking.<BR>	 4. Satisfaction,<BR>success.<BR> E. दुह् to milk, &c. affix घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=355-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोहज|दोहजं
दोहज n. (-जं) Milk.<BR> E. दोह milking, and ज produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=355-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोहडिका
दोहडिका f. (-कः) The Prakrit metre, commonly Doha; a stanza of<BR>four lines, containing thirteen and eleven syllabic instants alter-<BR>nately.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=355-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोहद|दोहदं|दोहदः
दोहद n. (-दं)<BR>	 1. Wish, desire.<BR>	 2. The longing of a pregnant woman,<BR>especially as a sign of impregnation.<BR> E. दोह here said to mean<BR>satisfaction, and द what gives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=355-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोहदलक्षण|दोहदलक्षणं
दोहदलक्षण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. The fœtus, the embryo, sometimes confounded<BR>with womb.<BR>	 1. The period of passing from one season of life to<BR>another, as from childhood to youth from youth to manhood. E.<BR>दोहद longing, and लक्षण a sign.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=355-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोहदवती
दोहदवती f. (-ती) A pregnant woman longing for any thing.<BR> E. दोहद as<BR>above, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=355-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोहदान्विता
दोहदान्विता f. (-ता) A pregnant woman longing for any thing.<BR> E. दोहद<BR>as above, and अन्वित attached or become inherent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=355-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोहन|दोहनं
दोहन nf. (-नं-नी) A milk vessel, a milkpail.<BR>	 n. (-नं) Milking.<BR> E. दुह् to<BR>milk, affix ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=355-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोहल|दोहलः
दोहल m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. Wish, desire.<BR>	 2. Longing.<BR>	 f. (-ली) The Asoka tree.<BR>E. दोह satisfaction, and ल what gets: see दोहद ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=355-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोहलवती
दोहलवती f. (-ती) A pregnant woman longing for any thing: see<BR>दोहदवती ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=355-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोहापनय|दोहापनयः
दोहापनय m. (-यः) Milk.<BR> E. दोह milking, अप below, णी to bring, affix अप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=355-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोहिन्
दोहिन् mfn. (-ही-हिणी-हि) Milking, a milker.<BR> E. दुह् to milk, घिनुण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=355-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोहीयस्
दोहीयस् mfn. (-यान्-यसी-यः) Yielding a great abundance of milk.<BR> E. दोह<BR>milk, ईयसुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=355-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोह्य|दोह्यं
दोह्य mfn. (-ह्यः-ह्या-ह्यं) To be milked, milkable.<BR> E. दुह to milk, ण्यत् affix,<BR>also दुह्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=355-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दौःसाधिक|दौःसाधिकः
दौःसाधिक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A sort of head borough or beadle, the superin-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=356-a" target="_blank">Page356-a+ 60</a>]<BR>tendent of a village.<BR>	 2. A door keeper, a warder, a porter.<BR> E. दुर्<BR>bad, difficult, साध् to accomplish, affix ठक् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=355-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दौकूल|दौकूलं|दौकूलः
दौकूल mfn. (-लः-ली-लं) Covered with silk, (a car, &c.)<BR> E. दुकूल wove<BR>silk, affix अण् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=356-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दौत्य|दौत्यं
दौत्य n. (-त्यं) An embassy or message.<BR> E. दूत a messenger, affix ष्यञ्:<BR>see दूत्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=356-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दौरात्म्य|दौरात्म्यं
दौरात्म्य n. (-त्म्यं) Wickedness, depravity.<BR> E. दुरात्मन् wicked, ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=356-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दौर्गन्धि
दौर्गन्धि n. (-न्धि) Fœtor, bad smell.<BR> E. दुर्गन्ध ill smelling, and इञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=356-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दौर्ग्य|दौर्ग्यं
दौर्ग्य n. (-र्ग्यं) Difficulty, Inaccessibility.<BR> E. दुर्ग and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=356-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दौर्जन्य|दौर्जन्यं|दौर्ज्जन्यं
दौर्जन्य n. (-न्यं) Wickedness, depravity, vileness.<BR> E. दुर्ज्जन and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=356-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दौर्बल्य|दौर्बल्यं|दौर्ब्बल्य|दौर्ब्बल्यं
दौर्बल्य n. (-ल्यं) Weakness, debility.<BR> E. दुर्बल and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=356-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दौर्भागिनेय|दौर्भागिनेयः
दौर्भागिनेय m. (-यः) The son of a woman disliked by her husband.<BR>	 f.<BR>(-यी) The daughter of such a woman.<BR> E. दर्भगा such a woman, ढक्<BR>affix and इनङ् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=356-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दौर्भाग्य|दौर्भाग्यं
दौर्भाग्य n. (-ग्यं) Ill-luck, misfortune.<BR> E. दुर् bad, भाग portion, ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=356-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दौर्मनस्य|दौर्मनस्यं|दौर्म्मनस्यं
दौर्मनस्य n. (-स्यं)<BR>	 1. Evil disposition or thought.<BR>	 2. Despair.<BR>	 3. Affliction,<BR>distress.<BR> E. दुर्मनस् and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=356-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दौर्वीण|दौर्वीणं|दौर्व्वीणं
दौर्वीण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. The sap or juice of bent grass.<BR>	 2. A clean leaf.<BR> E. दूर्वा<BR>bent grass, and खञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=356-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दौर्हृद|दौर्हृदं
दौर्हृद n. (-दं) Wish, desire, but especially the longing of pregnant<BR>women.<BR> E. दुर् pained, हृद् to heart, affix अण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=356-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दौलेय|दौलेयः
दौलेय m. (-यः) A turtle or tortoise.<BR> E. दूली a female tortoise. affix ढक् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=356-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दौल्मि|दौल्मिः
दौल्मि m. (-ल्मिः) A name of INDRA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=356-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दौवारिक|दौवारिकः
दौवारिक m. (-कः) A warder, a porter.<BR> E. दु bad, वार impediment, and<BR>ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=356-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दौश्चर्म्म्य
दौश्चर्म्म्य n. (-र्म्म्यं) Paraphymosis, circumcision.<BR> E. दुश्चर्म्म and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=356-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दौष्कुलेय|दौष्कुलेयः
दौष्कुलेय mfn. (-यः-यी-यं) Sprung of a bad or low family or race. E.<BR>दुष्कुल of a bad race, affix ढक् also दुष्कुलीन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=356-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दौष्ठव|दौष्ठवं
दौष्ठव n. (-वं) Badness, wickedness.<BR> E. दुष्ट and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=356-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दौष्मन्ति|दौष्मंति|दौष्मंतिः|दौष्मन्तिः
दौष्मन्ति m. (-न्तिः) A name of BHARAT, the first sole monarch of India.<BR>E. दुष्मन्त DUSHMANTA, husband of SAKUNTALĀ, and father to<BR>BHARAT, इञ् affix of descent; it is perhaps preferably read<BR>दौष्यन्ति from दुष्यन्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=356-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दौहित्र|दौहित्रः
दौहित्र m. (-त्रः) A daughter's son.<BR>	 f. (-त्री) A daughter's daughter. E.<BR>दुहितृ a daughter, affix अञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=356-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्यावाक्षमा
द्यावाक्षमा f. always dual, (-मे) Heaven and earth.<BR> E. द्यौ heaven, क्षमा the<BR>earth, form irr.; also similar compounds, as द्यावापृथिवी, द्यावा-<BR>भूमी, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=356-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्यावापृथिवी
द्यावापृथिवी f. always dual, (-व्यौ) Heaven and earth.<BR> E. द्यौ heaven, and<BR>पृथिवी the earth: see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=356-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्यावाभूमी
द्यावाभूमी f. always dual, (-भ्यौ) Heaven and earth.<BR> E. द्यौ, and भूमी the<BR>earth: see the two words preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=356-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्यु|द्युः
द्यु r. 2nd cl. (द्योति)<BR>	 1. To advance towards or against, to assail.<BR>	 2. To<BR>advance before or in front of, to approach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=356-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्यु|द्युः
द्यु m. (-द्युः) A name of AGNI or fire.<BR>	 n. (-द्यु)<BR>	 1. A day.<BR>	 2. Heaven, sky,<BR>æther.<BR>	 3. Heaven, paradise.<BR> E. द्यु to go to or towards, affix क्विप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=356-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्युक|द्युकः
द्युक m. (-कः) An owl.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=356-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्युकारि|द्युकारिः
द्युकारि m. (-रिः) A crow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=356-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्युग|द्युगः
द्युग m. (-गः) A bird.<BR> E. द्यु, and ग who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=356-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्युगण|द्युगणः
द्युगण m. (-णः) A given term of days, as a month, &c.<BR> E. द्यु, and गण a<BR>number.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=356-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्युत
द्युत r. 1st cl. (द्योतते) To shine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=356-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्युत्
द्युत् m. (द्युत्) A ray of light.<BR> E. द्युत् to shine, affix क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=356-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्युति|द्युतिः
द्युति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Light.<BR>	 2. Beauty or splendour.<BR>	 3. A ray of light.<BR>	 4.<BR>Stimulating, exciting.<BR> E. द्युत् to shine, affix कि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=356-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्युतिकर|द्युतिकरः
द्युतिकर mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>	 1. Shining, bright.<BR>	 2. Handsome.<BR>	 m. (-रः) The<BR>polar star, or in mythology, the divine sage DHRUVA.<BR> E. द्युति<BR>light, and कर who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=356-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्युतित|द्युतितं
द्युतित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Enlightened, illuminated, &c.<BR> E. द्युत् to shine,<BR>affix क्त; also with the vowel changed द्योतित्र ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=356-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्युतिमत्|द्युतिमन्त्
द्युतिमत् mfn. (-मान्-मती-मत्) Resplendent, bright.<BR> E. द्युति, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=356-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्युतिला
द्युतिला f. (-ला) A plant, (Hemionites cordifolia.)<BR> E. द्युति beauty, and<BR>ला to possess, affixes ड and टाप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=356-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्युनिवास|द्युनिवासः
द्युनिवास m. (-सः)<BR>	 1. Heavenly abode, heaven.<BR>	 2. A deity.<BR> E. द्यु, and<BR>निवास abiding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=356-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्युनिवासिन्
द्युनिवासिन् m. (-सी)<BR>	 1. A deity.<BR>	 2. A pious person.<BR> E. द्यु, and निवासिन्<BR>who abides.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=356-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्युनिश|द्युनिशं
द्युनिश n. (-शं) Day and night.<BR> E. द्यु a day, निशा night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=356-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्युपति|द्युपतिः
द्युपति m. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. The sun.<BR>	 2. A name of INDRA.<BR> E. द्यु, a day or<BR>paradise, and पति ruler.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=356-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्युमणि|द्युमणिः
द्युमणि m. (-णिः) The sun.<BR> E. द्यु a day, and मणि a gem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=356-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्युमयी
द्युमयी f. (-यी) The daughter of VISWAKARMĀ, and wife of the sun. E.<BR>द्यु a day, and मयट् affix of identity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=356-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्युम्र
द्युम्र n. (-म्रं)<BR>	 1. Wealth, property, substance.<BR>	 2. Strength, power. E.<BR>द्यु day, म्रा to remember or regard, affix क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=356-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्युवन्
द्युवन् m. (-वा)<BR>	 1. The sun.<BR>	 2. Heaven.<BR> E. द्यु to go (through the<BR>heavens,) Unādi affix कनिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=356-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्युषद्
द्युषद् m. (-षद् or -षत्)<BR>	 1. A god, a deity.<BR>	 2. A planet.<BR> E. द्यु heaven, षद्<BR>to go, affix क्विप्; it is also written द्युसद्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=356-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्यूत|द्यूतं|द्यूतः
द्यूत mn. (-तः-तं) Gaming, playing with dice, or any thing not possess-<BR>ing life.<BR> E. दिव् to play, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=356-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्यूतकर|द्यूतकरः
द्यूतकर m. (-रः) A gambler.<BR> E. द्यूत and कर who practises.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=356-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्यूतकार|द्यूतकारः
द्यूतकार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. The keeper of a gaming house.<BR>	 2. A gambler. E.<BR>द्यूत gaming, and कार who practises, also with कन् added,<BR>द्यूतकारक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=356-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्यूतकृत्
द्यूतकृत् m. (-कृत्) A gambler.<BR> E. द्यूत, and कृत् who practises: see the<BR>last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=356-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्यूतपूर्णिमा
द्यूतपूर्णिमा f. (-मा) The day of full moon in the month Kartic,<BR>(October-November,) the night of which is spent in games of<BR>chance, in honour of the goddess of fortune, LAKṢMĪ.<BR> E. द्यूत<BR>gaming, and पूर्णिमा day of full moon; also with अण् pleonastic<BR>affix added, and ङीष् fem. affix द्यूतपौर्णिमा, f. (-मी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=356-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्यूतप्रतिपत्
द्यूतप्रतिपत् f. (-पत्) The first day of the moon's increase in Kartic.<BR>when BALI is to be venerated.<BR> E. द्यूत, and प्रतिपद् the first lunation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=356-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्यूतवीज
द्यूतवीज n. (-जं) A Couri, a small shell used as a coin in most parts<BR>of India.<BR> E. द्यूत, gaming, and वीज seed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=356-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्यूतवृत्ति|द्यूतवृत्तिः
द्यूतवृत्ति m. (-त्तिः) A gambler.<BR> E. द्यूत<BR> E. वृत्ति, subsistence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=356-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्यूतसभा
द्यूतसभा f. (-भा) A gaming house or assembly.<BR> E. द्यूत and सभा an<BR>assembly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=356-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्यूताधिकारिन्
द्यूताधिकारिन् m. (-री) The keeper of a gaming house.<BR> E. द्यूत, and<BR>अधिकारिन् who superintends.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=356-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्यून|द्यूनं
द्यून mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Playing, sportive.<BR>	 n. (-नं) The seventh sign of<BR>the zodiac, reckoning from that which the sun enters.<BR> E. दिव् to<BR>play, &c. affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=356-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्यै
द्यै r. 1st cl. (द्यायति) To despise, to reprove, to treat or name with<BR>contempt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=356-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्यै
द्यै ind. Fie, for shame.<BR> E. द्यै, and क्विप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=356-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्यो
द्यो f. (-द्यौ)<BR>	 1. Heaven, paradise.<BR>	 2. Heaven, sky.<BR> E. दिव् to sport,<BR>Unādi affix डो आधारे; where the gods, &c. sport. द्योतन्ते देवा अत्र ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=356-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्योत|द्योतः
द्योत m. (-तः) Sun-shine, light, lustre, heat.<BR> E. द्युत् to shine, भावे घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=356-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्योतन|द्योतनं|द्योतनः
द्योतन mfn. (-नः-ना-नी-नं) Bright, shining.<BR>	 n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Sight, seeing.<BR>	 2.<BR>Making manifest.<BR>	 3. Illumination.<BR>	 4. An illumination.<BR>	 m. (-नः)<BR>A lamp.<BR> E. द्युत् to shine, affix भावे ल्युट् or शीलार्थेयुच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=356-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्योतमान
द्योतमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Shining, bright, radiant.<BR> E. द्युत् to shine,<BR>शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=356-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्योतयमान
द्योतयमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Enlightening, irradiating.<BR> E. द्युत् to shine,<BR>causal v. शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=356-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्योतित|द्योतितं
द्योतित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Enlightened, &c.<BR>	 2. Shining.<BR> E. द्युत् to light,<BR>affix क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=356-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्योतितप्रभ
द्योतितप्रभ mfn. (-भः-भा-भं) Resplendent.<BR> E. द्योतित, and प्रभा splendor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=356-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्योभूमि|द्योभूमिः
द्योभूमि m. (-मिः) A bird.<BR>	 f. du. (-मी) Heaven and earth.<BR> E. द्यो heaven,<BR>and भूमि the earth. द्यौराकाशो भूमिर्गतिस्थानं यस्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=357-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्योषद्
द्योषद् m. (-षद्-षत्) A deity, a celestial.<BR> E. द्यो heaven, षद् to go, affix क्विप् ।<BR>द्यवि सीदति ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=357-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्यौत्र|द्यौत्त्रं
द्यौत्र n. (-त्रं)<BR>	 1. Light, splendor, 2. Much or forked lightning.<BR> E. द्यु for<BR>दिव् to shine, Unādi affix ष्ट्रन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=357-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रगड|द्रगडः
द्रगड m. (-डः) A kettle drum.<BR> E. द्रेति गडति गड-अच । (दगड्काडा) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=357-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रङ्क्षण|द्रंक्षण|द्रङ्क्षणं
द्रङ्क्षण n. (-णं) A measure or weight, a Tolā. तोलके ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=357-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रङ्ग|द्रङ्गः
द्रङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः) A city, a town.<BR> E. द्रम् to go, affix गन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=357-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रढिमन्
द्रढिमन् m. (-मा) Firmness, hardness, heaviness.<BR> E. दृढ hard, firm, इमनिच्<BR>aff. दृढस्य भावः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=357-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रढिष्ठ|द्रढिष्ठः
द्रढिष्ठ mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठा-ष्ठं) Hardest, very hard or firm, &c.<BR> E. दृढ with the<BR>superlative affix, इष्ठन् and the liquid substituted for the vowel;<BR>also with ईयसुन् affix द्रढीयस् (-यान्-यसी-यः) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=357-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रप्स|द्रप्सः
द्रप्स mn. (-प्सः-प्सं) Thin or diluted curds.<BR> E. दृप् to please, affix क्स; also<BR>त्रप्स and द्रप्स्य । दृप्यति कफोऽनेन । (जलो दै) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=357-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रप्स्य|द्रप्स्यं
द्रप्स्य n. (-प्स्यं) Thin or diluted curds.<BR> E. दृप् to please, affix स्यः or it is<BR>derived from तृप् to be satisfied, त being changed to द ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=357-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रम
द्रम r. 1st cl. (द्रमति) To go, to move. भ्वा० प० सक० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=357-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रव|द्रवः
द्रव mfn. (-वः-वा-वं)<BR>	 1. Dropping, oozing.<BR>	 2. Flowing.<BR>	 3. Fluid, liquid.<BR>4. Fused, liquefied, melted.<BR>	 m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. Going, motion.<BR>	 2. Flight,<BR>retreat.<BR>	 3. Sport, amusement.<BR>	 4. Juice, essence, exudation.<BR>	 5.<BR>Fusion, liquefaction.<BR>	 6. Decoction.<BR>	 7. Dropping, distilling, trickl-<BR>ing.<BR> E. द्रु to go, to go out of, to drop, affix भावे अप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=357-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रबज
द्रबज m. (-जः) Treacle.<BR> E. द्रव, and ज born. द्रवात् जायते जन-ड ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=357-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रवण|द्रवणं
द्रवण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Going.<BR>	 2. Dropping, exuding.<BR>	 3. Heat.<BR> E. द्रु to go,<BR>affix ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=357-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रवत्|द्रवन्त्
द्रवत् mfn. (-वन्-वन्ती-वत्)<BR>	 1. Trickling, oozing.<BR>	 2. Running, flowing.<BR>	 3.<BR>Going.<BR>	 f. (-न्ती)<BR>	 1. A river in general.<BR>	 2. A medicinal plant, (An-<BR>thericum tuberosum.)<BR> E. द्रु to go, affix शतृ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=357-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रवत्व|द्रवत्वं
द्रवत्व n. (-त्वं)<BR>	 1. Fluidity, natural or artificial.<BR>	 2. Distillation.<BR>	 3. Fusion.<BR>E. द्रव, and त्व affix; also with तल् द्रवता । द्रवस्य भावः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=357-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रवरसा
द्रवरसा f. (-सा) Lac.<BR> E. द्रव, and रस juice. द्रवयुक्तो रसी यस्याः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=357-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रवाधार|द्रवाधारः
द्रवाधार m. (-रः) A small vessel, a receiver.<BR> E. द्रव juice, distillation, &c.<BR>and आधार what receives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=357-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रविड|द्रविडः
द्रविड m. (-डः) A man of an outcaste tribe, descended from a degraded<BR>Kṣatriya.<BR>	 f. (-डी) One of the Rāginis or female personifications<BR>of the modes of music.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=357-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रविण|द्रविणं
द्रविण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Wealth, property, thing, substance.<BR>	 2. Gold.<BR>	 3.<BR>Strength, power.<BR> E. द्रु to go, इनन् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=357-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रविणनाशन|द्रविणनाशनः
द्रविणनाशन m. (-नः) A plant, (Hyperanthera morunga.)<BR> E. द्रविण<BR>strength, and नाशन destroying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=357-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रविणोदास्
द्रविणोदास् m. (-दाः) AGNI.<BR> E. द्रविण, and दास् who gives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=357-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रवीकरण|द्रवीकरणं
द्रवीकरण n. (-णं) Liquefying, melting.<BR> E. द्रव fluid, करण making, च्वि<BR>augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=357-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रवीकृत
द्रवीकृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Melted, liquefied.<BR> E. द्रव, कृत made, च्वि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=357-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रवीभूत
द्रवीभूत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Fluid, liquefied, fused.<BR> E. द्रव, and भूत become, च्वि<BR>augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=357-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रवेतर
द्रवेतर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Hard, solid, congealed.<BR> E. द्रव, and इतर reverse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=357-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रव्य|द्रव्यं
द्रव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>	 1. Fit, proper, right, what is or ought to be.<BR>2. Derived from or relating to a tree.<BR>	 n. (-व्यं)<BR>	 1. Wealth, property.<BR>2. Substance, thing, the receptacle or substratum of properties, &c.<BR>3. Elementary substance, nine kinds of which are reckoned; viz.<BR>earth, water, fire, air, æther, time, space, soul, and intellect.<BR>	 4.<BR>Brass.<BR>	 5. A stake, a wager.<BR>	 6. A drug, a medicament, any thing.<BR>used in medicine.<BR>	 7. Anointing, plastering.<BR>	 8. Lac, the animal dye.<BR>9. Extract, gum, resin, &c. derived from vegetables.<BR>	 10. Modesty,<BR>propriety.<BR>	 11. Spirituous liquor.<BR> E. द्रु a tree, affix यत् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=357-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रव्यक|द्रव्यकः
द्रव्यक m. (-कः) A carrier or taker of any thing.<BR> E. कन् added to the<BR>last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=357-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रव्यप्रयोजन
द्रव्यप्रयोजन n. (-नं) Use or employment of any article.<BR> E. द्रव्य, and प्रयोजन<BR>purpose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=357-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रव्यमय
द्रव्यमय mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>	 1. Material.<BR>	 2. Having or holding any thing. E.<BR>द्रव्य, मयष्ट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=357-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रव्ययज्ञ
द्रव्ययज्ञ m. (-ज्ञः) Offering oblations, sacrifice, &c.<BR> E. द्रव्य, and यज्ञ sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=357-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रव्यवत्|द्रव्यवन्त्
द्रव्यवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Rich, wealthy.<BR> E. द्रव्य, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=357-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रव्यशुद्धि|द्रव्यशुद्धिः
द्रव्यशुद्धि f. (-द्धिः) Cleansing or purification of any soiled or defiled article.<BR>E. द्रव्य, and शुद्धि purity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=357-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रव्यसंस्कार|द्रव्यसंस्कारः
द्रव्यसंस्कार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Consecration of articles for sacrifice.<BR>	 2. Purification<BR>or cleansing of any articles soiled or defiled.<BR> E. द्रव्य, and संस्कार<BR>perfectioning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=357-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रव्यसञ्चय|द्रव्यसंचय
द्रव्यसञ्चय m. (-यः) Accumulation of property.<BR> E. द्रव्य, and सञ्चय collection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=357-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रव्यसिद्धि|द्रव्यसिद्धिः
द्रव्यसिद्धि f. (-द्धिः)<BR>	 1. Acquirement of wealth.<BR>	 2. Effecting any thing by<BR>wealth.<BR> E. द्रव्य, and सिद्धि completion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=357-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रव्यहस्त
द्रव्यहस्त mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं) Holding any thing in the hand.<BR> E. द्रव्य, and<BR>हस्त hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=357-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रव्यार्जन|द्रव्यार्ज्जन
द्रव्यार्जन n. (-नं) Gain, acquisition, acquiring property.<BR> E. द्रव्य, and अर्जन<BR>acquiring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=357-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रष्टव्य
द्रष्टव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं) To be seen, visible, apparent.<BR> E. दृश् to see, तव्य<BR>affix, and ऋ changed to र ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=357-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रष्टृ
द्रष्टृ mfn. (-ष्टा-ष्ट्री-ष्टृ) Who or what sees, a spectator.<BR> E. दृश् to see, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=357-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रा
द्रा r. 2nd cl. (द्राति)<BR>	 1. To fly, to run away.<BR>	 2. To be ashamed or<BR>spoiled. अदा० प० अक० अनिट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=357-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्राक्
द्राक् ind. Instantly, immediately, soon, shortly.<BR> E. द्रा to fly, कु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=357-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्राक्ष
द्राक्ष (इ) द्राक्षि r. 1st cl. (द्राङ्क्षति)<BR>	 1. To croke, to caw, &c. as a bird.<BR>	 2.<BR>To desire, to wish or long for. भ्वा० प० सक० सेट् इदित् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=357-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्राक्षा
द्राक्षा f. (-क्षा) A grape.<BR> E. द्राक्षि to desire, affix अ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=357-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्राख
द्राख (ऋ) दाखृ r. 1st cl. (दाखति)<BR>	 1. To be dry or arid.<BR>	 2. To adorn.<BR>	 3. To<BR>be able or competent.<BR>	 4. To prohibit, to prevent. शोषणे सक० अलमर्थे<BR>अक० भ्वा० पर० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=357-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्राघ
द्राघ (ऋ) द्राघृ r. 1st cl. (द्राघति)<BR>	 1. To be able or competent.<BR>	 2. To<BR>stretch, to lengthen.<BR>	 3. To tire, to be tired or fatigued. भ्वा० पर०<BR>अक० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=357-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्राघिमन्
द्राघिमन् m. (-मा) Length.<BR> E. दीर्घ, and इमनिच् affix, the first syllable<BR>changed. दीर्घस्य भावः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=357-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्राघिमवत्
द्राघिमवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Long, lengthy.<BR> E. द्राघिनन्, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=357-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्राघिष्ठ|द्राघिष्ठः
द्राघिष्ठ mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठा-ष्ठं) Longest, very long.<BR> E. दीर्घ long, इष्ठन् affix of<BR>the superlative, and द्राघ substituted for दीर्घ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=357-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्राघीयस्
द्राघीयस् mfn. (-यान्-यसी-यः) Very or exceeding long.<BR> E. दीर्घ, and ईयसुन्<BR>affix, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=357-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्राड
द्राड (ऋ) दाडृ r. 1st. cl. (द्राडते) To divide, to split, to pierce, to pull to<BR>pieces, &c. भ्वा-आ-सक-सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=357-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्राण|द्राणः
द्राण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Flown, run away, &c.<BR> E. द्रु to fly, affix कर्त्तरि क्त,<BR>deriv. irr. तस्य नः । भावे क्त । स्वप्ने पलायने च क्लीव० लि० ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=357-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्राप|द्रापः
द्राप m. (-पः)<BR>	 1. Mud, mire.<BR>	 2. Heaven, sky.<BR>	 3. A fool, an idiot 4. A<BR>cowri. -द्रा-णिच्-पुक्-अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=357-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रामिल|द्रामिलः
द्रामिल m. (-लः) The Muni CHĀNAKYA.<BR> E. द्रमिल a proper name, and<BR>अण् patronymic aff. द्रमिलो देशोऽभोजनोऽस्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=357-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्राव|द्रावः
द्राव m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. Flight, retreat.<BR>	 2. Speed, going quickly.<BR>	 3. Flowing,<BR>running.<BR>	 4. Fusion, liquefaction.<BR>	 5. Heat.<BR> E. द्रु to go, affix भावे घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=357-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रावक|द्रावकं|द्रावकः
द्रावक m. (-कः) A kind of stone, (a loadstone.)<BR>	 2. A wit, a wag, a sharp<BR>or clever man.<BR>	 3. A thief.<BR>	 4. A libertine, a lecher.<BR>	 5. A pursuer, a<BR>chaser, one who causes to fly.<BR>	 6. A sort of Ras or quality.<BR>	 n. (-कं)<BR>Bee's wax.<BR> E. द्रु to fly, affix ण्वुल् । द्रवति चन्द्रकरसम्पर्कात् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=357-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रावकर|द्रावकरं
द्रावकर n. (-रं)<BR>	 1. A kind of borax.<BR>	 2. A flux.<BR> E. द्राव fusion, and कर<BR>what makes. द्रावं द्रवं करोति स्वर्णादिकं स्वसम्पर्केण कृ-ताच्छील्ये ट ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=357-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रावण|द्रावणं
द्रावण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. The clearing nut.<BR>	 2. Causing to fly or retreat.<BR>	 3.<BR>Fusing.<BR>	 4. Distilling.<BR> E. द्रु to go or retreat, in the causal form<BR>णिच् and युच् affs. द्रावयति जलमलं स्वसंयोगात् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=357-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्राविका
द्राविका f. (-का) Saliva.<BR> E. द्रु to ooze out, ण्वुल् affix, and the fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=357-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्राविड|द्राविडः
द्राविड m. (-डः)<BR>	 1. A country, properly the coast of Coromandel from<BR>Madras to Cape Comorin, or the country in which Tamil is spoken.<BR>2. A native of Drāvira or Drāvida.<BR>	 3. A Brahman of Drāvira,<BR>of rather of the south five Drāviras being specified, or Drāvira,<BR>Karnāta, Gujrāta, Mahārashtra, and Tailanga.<BR>	 4. A particular<BR>number.<BR>	 5. Zedoary.<BR> E. द्रविड, and अण् aff. द्रविडो देशोऽभिजनोऽस्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=358-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्राविडक|द्राविडकं|द्राविडकः
द्राविडक m. (-कः) Zedoary, (Curcuma zerumbet.)<BR>	 n. (-कं) Black salt. E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding, growing in the country of Drāvira.<BR>द्रविडे भवः अण् संज्ञायां कन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=358-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्राविडभूतिक|द्राविडभूतिकः
द्राविडभूतिक m. (-कः) Zedoary.<BR> E. द्राविड the country, भूत being, affix<BR>कप्: see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=358-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रावित
द्रावित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Melted, liquefied.<BR>	 2. Softened, mollified.<BR>	 3.<BR>Driven, chased.<BR> E. द्रु to go, causal form, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=358-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्राव्य|द्राव्यं
द्राव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>	 1. To be set in motion, to be put to flight, &c.<BR>2. Fusible, liquefiable, to be made fluid.<BR> E. द्रु to go, ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=358-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्राह
द्राह (ऋ) द्राहृ r. 1st cl. (द्राहते)<BR>	 1. To wake.<BR>	 2. To deposit, to pledge.<BR>भ्वा-आ-अक-सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=358-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रु|द्रुः
द्रु r. 1st cl. (द्रवति)<BR>	 1. To go, to move, to run.<BR>	 2. To drop.<BR>	 3. To distil<BR>or ooze. r. 5th cl. (द्रुनुते-द्रुनोति) To hurt, to injure, to wound or<BR>kill. With अनु prefixed, To pursue, to follow. With अभि, To swim,<BR>to float, to descend. With आङ्, To flee. With उप, To oppress, to<BR>destroy. With प्र, To fly, to retreat, to run away. With वि, 1. To<BR>smite, to kill.<BR>	 2. To flee, to run away. With सम् and आङ् To run<BR>together. With सम् and उप, 1. To flee.<BR>	 2. To meet. भ्वा० प० सक०<BR>अनिट् । अनुतापे स्वा० पर० सक० अनिट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=358-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रु|द्रुः
द्रु m. (द्रुः) A tree.<BR>	 f. (द्रुः) Going, motion.<BR> E. द्रु to go (up), to grow,<BR>affix डु ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=358-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रुकिलिम|द्रुकिलिमं
द्रुकिलिम n. (-मं) A tree, a sort of pine: (Pinus devadāru.)<BR> E. द्रु a tree,<BR>किलिम the fir or pine, derived from किल् to send or cast, to give<BR>out (resin), and किमच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=358-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रुघण|द्रुघणः
द्रुघण m. (-णः)<BR>	 1. A mace, a mallet, an iron weapon made like a carpen-<BR>ter's hammer.<BR>	 2. An axe, a hatchet.<BR>	 3. A name of BRAMHĀ.<BR>	 4. A<BR>plant: see भूमिचम्पक.<BR> E. द्रु a tree, हन् to injure or demolish, affix<BR>अप्, and घन substituted for the radical; न is usually changed to ण,<BR>but the word is also written द्रुघन । द्रुः वृक्षः संसारगतिर्वा हन्यते अनेन ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=358-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रुड
द्रुड r. 6th cl. (द्रुडति) The sink. तुदा० कुटा० प० सक० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=358-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रुण|द्रुणं|द्रुणः
द्रुण r. 6th cl. (द्रुणति)<BR>	 1. To hurt, to injure.<BR>	 2. To go, to move, to ap-<BR>proach.<BR>	 3. To bind, to make crooked or curved. तुदा० कुटा० प० अक०<BR>सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=358-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रुण|द्रुणं|द्रुणः
द्रुण m. (-णः)<BR>	 1. A scorpion.<BR>	 2. A bee.<BR>	 3. A rogue, a cheat.<BR>	 f. (-णा) A<BR>bow-string.<BR>	 n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. A bow.<BR>	 2. A sword, a scimitar.<BR> E. द्रुण् to in-<BR>jure, affix क । द्रुणति हिनस्ति कुटिलीभवति वा द्रुण-क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=358-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रुणस|द्रुणसः
द्रुणस mfn. (-सः-सी-सं) Large-nosed.<BR> E. द्रु a tree, and नस for नास a nose.<BR>द्रुरिव दीर्घा नासिका अस्य अच् समा० नसादेशः पूर्वपदात् संज्ञायां णत्वम् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=358-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रुणह|द्रुणहः
द्रुणह m. (-हः) A scabbard, a sword sheath.<BR> E. द्रुण a sword, हा to kill<BR>or remove, affix क; the word is also द्रुनह ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=358-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रुणि|द्रुणिः
द्रुणि f. (-णिः-णी)<BR>	 1. An oval water basin of wood or stone, &c. shaped<BR>like a boat, and used for pouring water.<BR>	 2. A bucket, a basket.<BR>	 f.<BR>(-णी)<BR>	 1. A centipede.<BR>	 2. A small of female tortoise.<BR> E. द्रुण् to go,<BR>to hurt, affixes कि and ङीष् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=358-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रुत|द्रुतं|द्रुतः
द्रुत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Quick or swift.<BR>	 2. Melted, fused.<BR>	 3. Liquid, fluid.<BR>4. Flown, escaped, run away.<BR>	 5. Scattered, diffused.<BR>	 m. (-तः) A tree.<BR>n. (-तं) Quick time, (in music.) adv.<BR>	 n. (-तं) Quickly, swiftly.<BR> E. द्रु<BR>to go, affix क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=358-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रुतपद
द्रुतपद n. subs. (-दं) A quick pace or step. adv. Quickly.<BR> E. द्रुत, and<BR>पद a step.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=358-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रुनख|द्रुनखः
द्रुनख m. (-खः) A thorn.<BR> E. द्रु a tree, and नख nail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=358-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रुनह|द्रुनहः
द्रुनह m. (-हः) A scabbard: see द्रुणह ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=358-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रुम|द्रुमः
द्रुम m. (-मः)<BR>	 1. A tree in general.<BR>	 2. A tree of Svarga or paradise.<BR>	 3.<BR>A name of KUVERA.<BR> E. द्रु to go, म aff. द्रुः शाखा अस्वि अस्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=358-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रुमनख|द्रुमनखः
द्रुमनख m. (-खः) A thorn.<BR> E. द्रुम a tree, and नख a finger-nail: see द्रुनख ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=358-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रुमर|द्रुमरः
द्रुमर m. (-रः) A thorn.<BR> E. द्रुम a tree, रम् to sport, affix ड ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=358-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रमव्याधि
द्रमव्याधि m. (-धिः) Lac.<BR> E. द्रुम, and व्याधि disease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=358-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रुमशीर्ष|द्रुमशीर्षं
द्रुमशीर्ष n. (-र्षं) The upper part of a building or wall.<BR> E. द्रुम a tree, and<BR>शीर्ष a head, resembling the top of a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=358-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रुमश्रेष्ठ|द्रुमश्रेष्ठः
द्रुमश्रेष्ठ m. (-ष्ठः) The palm tree: see ताल.<BR> E. द्रुम a tree, and श्रेष्ठ best.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=358-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रुमामय|द्रुमामयः
द्रुमामय m. (-यः) Lac, the animal dye.<BR> E. द्रुम a tree, and आमय sickness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=358-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रुमारि|द्रुमारिः
द्रुमारि m. (-रिः) An elephant.<BR> E. द्रुम, and अरि a foe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=358-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रुमाश्रय|द्रुमाश्रयः
द्रुमाश्रय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Sheltering or dwelling in trees.<BR> E. द्रुम, and<BR>आश्रय abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=358-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रुमेश्वर|द्रुमेश्वरः
द्रुमेश्वर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. The palm tree: see ताल.<BR>	 2. The moon.<BR> E. द्रुम a tree,<BR>and ईश्वर sovereign.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=358-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रुमोत्पल|द्रुमोत्पलः
द्रुमोत्पल m. (-लः) A plant: see कर्णिकार.<BR> E. द्रुम a tree, and उत्पल a lotus,<BR>to which the flowers are compared.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=358-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रुवय|द्रुवयं|द्रुवयः
द्रुवय n. (-यं) Measure in general.<BR> E. द्रु a tree, and वय affix, implying<BR>measure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=358-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रुसल्लक|द्रुसल्लकः
द्रुसल्लक m. (-कः) A tree, (Chironjia sapida.)<BR> E. द्रु a thing or substance,<BR>सल्लका the olibanum plant: a resinous plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=358-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रुह|द्रुहः
द्रुह m. (ध्रुक्) An injurer.<BR> E. द्रुह to hate, affix क्विप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=358-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रुह|द्रुहः
द्रुह r. 4th cl. (द्रुह्यति) To bear hatred, to seek to hurt or injure. दिवा०<BR>प० सक० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=358-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रुह|द्रुहः
द्रुह m. (-हः) A son.<BR>	 f. (-ही) A daughter.<BR> E. द्रुह to hurt, affix क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=358-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रुहण|द्रुहणः
द्रुहण m. (-णः) A name of BRAMHĀ: see the next. द्रुं संसारगतिं हन्ति<BR>हन्-अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=358-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रुहिण|द्रुहिणः
द्रुहिण m. (-णः) A name of BRAMHĀ.<BR> E. द्रुह् to injure or hurt, (the<BR>wicked,) and इनन् affix, or द्रु a tree, (figuratively the universe,) हन्<BR>to destroy, इनि affix, destroyer of the world; न changed to ण;<BR>also द्रुहण ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=358-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रुह्यत्
द्रुह्यत् mfn. (-ह्यन्-हन्ती-ह्यत्)<BR>	 1. Attacking, assailing, defying.<BR>	 2. Tyrannis-<BR>ing over, oppressing.<BR> E. द्रुह् to hate, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=358-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रू
द्रू r. 9th cl. (ञ) द्रूञ् (द्रूणोति, द्रणुते, द्रूणाति, द्रूणीते) 1. To go, to move.<BR>	 2.<BR>To hurt, to injure, to wound or kill. स्वा० क्य्रा० उ० सक० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=358-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रू
द्रू m. (द्रूः) Gold.<BR> E. द्रु to go, क्विप् affix, and the vowel made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=358-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रूघण|द्रूघणः
द्रूघण m. (-णः)<BR>	 1. A name of BRAMHĀ.<BR>	 2. An iron club.<BR>	 3. A sort of<BR>hatchet.<BR> E. द्रु a tree, हन् to strike, affix अप्, घ and ण substituted<BR>for ह and न, and the vowel of द्रु made long; also optionally द्रुघण,<BR>द्रुघन, and द्रूघन ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=358-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रूण|द्रूणः
द्रूण m. (-णः) A scorpion; also द्रुण and द्रोण ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=358-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रेक
द्रेक r. 1st cl. (ऋ) द्रेकृ (द्रेकते) 1. To sound.<BR>	 2. To grow or increase.<BR>	 3.<BR>To manifest joy or elevation by noise. भ्वा० आ० अक० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=358-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रेक्क|द्रेक्कः
द्रेक्क m. (-क्कः) The regent of one-third of a planetary sign.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=358-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रेक्काण|द्रेक्काणः
द्रेक्काण m. (-णः) The regent of one-third of a planetary sign, the<BR>Decanus of European astrology, whence the word is probably<BR>derived.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=358-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रै
द्रै r. 1st cl. (द्रायति) To sleep; नि is usually prefixed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=358-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रोण|द्रोणः
द्रोण mn. (-णः-णं)<BR>	 1. A measure of capacity, the same as an Āḍhaka:<BR>see आढक.<BR>	 2. A measure of four Āḍhakas.<BR>	 3. In common use, a<BR>measure of thirty-two Seers, or rather more than sixty-four lbs.<BR>avoirdupois.<BR>	 4. The sixteenth part of a Khāri, or forty-eight gallons.<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>	 1. A proper name, the military preceptor of the Pāndus.<BR>2. A raven, or perhaps the carrion crow.<BR>	 3. A scorpion: see द्रुण.<BR>	 4.<BR>A large piece of water, one four hundred poles long.<BR>	 5. One of<BR>the principal clouds.<BR>	 6. A small tree bearing white flowers.<BR>	 f.<BR>(-णिः-णी)<BR>	 1. Any oval vessel made of wood, stone, &c. in the shape<BR>of a boat, and used for holding or pouring out water, as a bathing<BR>tub, a baling vessel, a bucket, a watering pot, &c.<BR>	 2. A trough or<BR>rack for feeding cattle.<BR>	 3. The name of country.<BR>	 4. The name of a<BR>mountain.<BR>	 m. (-णिः) The name of a river.<BR>	 f. (-णी)<BR>	 1. The indigo<BR>plant.<BR>	 2. The union of two mountains, the valley or chasm be-<BR>tween them.<BR>	 3. A sort of boat, implying the sort of water vessel,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=359-a" target="_blank">Page359-a+ 60</a>]<BR>probably described above.<BR>	 4. A measure of capacity equal to 128<BR>Seers.<BR> E. द्रु to go, न or नि Unādi affix, and ङीष् added to either<BR>form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=358-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रोणकाक|द्रोणकाकः
द्रोणकाक m (-कः) A raven.<BR> E. द्रोण the same, and काक a crow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=359-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रोणकाकल|द्रोणकाकलः
द्रोणकाकल m. (-लः) A raven.<BR> E. द्रोण as above, काकल here said to mean<BR>a crow, from का imitative sound, caw, and कल who utters.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=359-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रोणक्षीरा
द्रोणक्षीरा f. (-रा) A cow that yields a Dronā of milk.<BR> E. द्रोण the measure<BR>so called, and क्षीरा milk; also other analogous compounds, ut<BR>infra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=359-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रोणगन्धिका
द्रोणगन्धिका f. (-का) A plant: see रास्ना ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=359-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रोणघा
द्रोणघा f. (-घा) A cow that yields a Dronā of milk.<BR> E. द्रोण the measure,<BR>दुह् to milk, deriv irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=359-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रोणदुग्धा
द्रोणदुग्धा f. (-ग्धा) A cow that yields a Dronā of milk.<BR> E. द्रोण, and दुग्ध milk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=359-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रोणदुघा
द्रोणदुघा f. (-घा) See the last.<BR> E. द्रोण, and दुह to milk, affix कप्, and ह<BR>changed to घ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=359-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रोणपुष्पी
द्रोणपुष्पी f. (-ष्पी) A plant, known commonly by the same name; also<BR>गोशीर्षक.<BR> E. द्रोण the measure, and पुष्प a flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=359-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रोणमाना
द्रोणमाना f. (-ना) A cow yielding a Dronā of milk.<BR> E. द्रोण, and<BR>मान a measure: see द्रोणक्षीरा ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=359-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रोणमुख|द्रोणमुखं
द्रोणमुख m. (-खः) The capital of a district, the chief of four hundred<BR>villages.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=359-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रोणम्पच|द्रोणंपच|द्रोणम्पचः
द्रोणम्पच mfn. (-चः-चा-चं) Liberal in entertaining, one who cooks a<BR>Dronā.<BR> E. द्रोण, and पच् to cook, स्वच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=359-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रोणाचार्य्य|द्रोणाचार्य|द्रोणाचार्यः|द्रोणाचार्य्यः
द्रोणाचार्य्य m. (-र्य्यः) A proper name; Drona, the son of BHARADWĀJA,<BR>and the Achārya or teacher of the Pāndava princes. E.<BR>द्रोण as above, and आचार्य्य a preceptor; also with कन् added<BR>द्रोणाचार्य्यक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=359-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रोणिका
द्रोणिका f. (-का) The indigo plant.<BR> E. द्रोणी the same, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=359-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रोणीदल|द्रोणीदलः
द्रोणीदल m. (-लः) A flower, (Pandanus odoratissimus.)<BR> E. द्रोणी a water<BR>vessel, and दल a leaf, the leaves being boat-shaped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=359-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रोणीमुख|द्रोणीमुखं
द्रोणीमुख m. (-खः) The principal of four hundred villages: see द्रोणसुख ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=359-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रोह|द्रोहः
द्रोह m. (-हः)<BR>	 1. Mischief, malice, trespass, injury.<BR>	 2. Offence, wrong.<BR>3. Rebellion.<BR> E. द्रुह् to hurt or injure, affix भावे घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=359-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रोहचिन्तन|द्रोहचिंतन|द्रोहचिन्तनं
द्रोहचिन्तन n. (-नं) Injurious design, malice prepense; the wish, thought,<BR>or attempt to injure.<BR> E. द्रोह as above, and चिन्तन thinking,<BR>meditating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=359-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रोहाट|द्रोहाटः
द्रोहाट m. (-टः)<BR>	 1. A hunter, a deer-killer.<BR>	 2. A sort of metre the<BR>Doha or stanza of Hindī poetry.<BR>	 3. A religious impostor, a tar-<BR>tuffe, a hypocrite.<BR> E. द्रोह injury, mischief, and अट who goes or is.<BR>द्रोहेण अटति अट-अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=359-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रोहिन्
द्रोहिन् mfn. (-ही-हिणी-हि)<BR>	 1. Hurting, harming, endeavouring to hurt,<BR>malignant, malicious.<BR>	 2. Rebellious.<BR> E. द्रुह् to seek to hurt,<BR>घिनुण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=359-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रोणायण
द्रोणायण m. (-णः) A name of AŚWATTHĀMĀ, son of Drona.<BR> E. द्रोण as<BR>above, and फक् affix; also with फिञ् affix. द्रौणायणि, इञ् affix द्रौणि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=359-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रौणिक|द्रौणिकः
द्रौणिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Sown with a Dronā of grain, (fields, &c.)<BR>f. (की) A vessel holding a Dronā by measure.<BR> E. द्रोण the<BR>measure, ठञ् or ठन् affix; also with अण् and ङीष् affixes in the last<BR>sense. द्रौणी ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=359-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रौपदी
द्रौपदी f. (-दी) A proper name. DRAUPADĪ, the daughter of DRUPADA,<BR>king of Panchāla, and the common wife of the five Pāndava<BR>princes.<BR> E. द्रपद the father of this lady, and अण् and ङीप् affixes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=359-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वन्द|द्वंद|द्वन्दं|द्वंदः|द्वन्दः
द्वन्द m. (-न्दः) A clock or plate on which hours are struck.<BR>	 n. (-न्दं) A<BR>pair, a couple, (male and female especially:) see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=359-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वन्द्व|द्वंद्व|द्वंद्वं|द्वन्द्वं|द्वन्द्वः
द्वन्द्व n. (-न्द्वं)<BR>	 1. A pair, a brace.<BR>	 2. A couple of animals, or male and<BR>female.<BR>	 3. Union of the sexes or coupling.<BR>	 4. Strife, dispute.<BR>	 5. A<BR>secret.<BR>	 m. (-न्द्वः)<BR>	 1. A form of grammatical combination uniting two<BR>or more words in the same case, properly separated by a conjunc-<BR>tion, as रामलक्ष्मणौ RĀMA and LAKSHMANA; पाणिपादं hand and foot.<BR>2. A sign of the zodiac (Gemini.)<BR>	 3. A species of disease, a<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=359-b" target="_blank">Page359-b+ 60</a>]<BR>complication of two disorders, or compound affection of two<BR>humours.<BR> E. द्वि two, reduplicate, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=359-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वन्द्वचर|द्वंद्वचर|द्वन्द्वचरः
द्वन्द्वचर m. (-रः) The ruddy goose.<BR> E. द्वन्द्व a couple, and चर who goes;<BR>flying in couples.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=359-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वन्द्वचारिन्|द्वंद्वचारिन्
द्वन्द्वचारिन् m. (-री) The ruddy goose.<BR> E. द्वन्द्व, and चर् to go, affix णिनिः see<BR>the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=359-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वन्द्वज|द्वंद्वज|द्वन्द्वजः
द्वन्द्वज mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>	 1. Produced or proceeding from morbid affection<BR>of two humours.<BR>	 2. Proceeding from a pair, &c.<BR> E. द्वन्द्व, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=359-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वन्द्वदुःख|द्वंद्वदुःख
द्वन्द्वदुःख n. (-खं) Pain arising from alternation, as a heat or cold,<BR>pleasure or pain, &c.<BR> E. द्वन्द्व, and दुःख pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=359-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वन्द्वभिन्न|द्वंद्वभिन्न
द्वन्द्वभिन्न n. (-न्नं) Separation of the sexes.<BR> E. द्वन्द्व, and भिन्न broken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=359-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वन्द्वयुद्ध|द्वंद्वयुद्ध
द्वन्द्वयुद्ध n. (-द्धं) Sigle combat.<BR> E. द्वन्द्व, and युद्ध war. द्वयोर्द्वयोयुद्धम् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=359-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वन्द्वातीत|द्वंद्वातीत
द्वन्द्वातीत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Free from worldly affections.<BR> E. द्वन्द्व alternation<BR>(of pain and pleasure, &c.) and अतीत passed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=359-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वय|द्वयं
द्वय mn. (-यः-यं) A pair, a couple, two, chiefly used in composition, as<BR>पुरुषद्वयं two men.<BR> E. द्वि two, तयप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=359-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वयाग्नि|द्वयाग्निः
द्वयाग्नि m. (-ग्निः) A plant, (Plumbago zeylanica.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=359-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वयातिग|द्वयातिगः
द्वयातिग m. (-गः) A saint, a holy or virtuous man.<BR> E. द्वय a pair, the<BR>two bad qualities, passion and ignorance, अति beyond, and ग<BR>who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=359-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वाःस्थ|द्वाःस्थः
द्वाःस्थ m. (-स्थः)<BR>	 1. A warder, a porter.<BR>	 2. NANDI, one of ŚIVA'S door-<BR>keepers.<BR> E. द्वार् a door, and स्थ who stays; also द्वास्थ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=359-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वाःस्थित|द्वाःस्थितः
द्वाःस्थित m. (-तः) A doorkeeper, a warder.<BR> E. द्वार् a door, and स्थित<BR>staying; also द्वास्थित ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=359-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वाःस्थितदर्शक|द्वाःस्थितदर्शकः
द्वाःस्थितदर्शक m. (-कः) A warder, a porter, a chamberlain.<BR> E. द्वार् a door,<BR>स्थित staying, and दर्शक who shows, who introduces to the prince<BR>or great man to whom the mansion belongs; also द्वाःस्थित, and दर्शक<BR>severally; also द्वाःस्थितदर्शीन् m. (-र्शी.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=359-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वात्रिंशदक्षरिन्
द्वात्रिंशदक्षरिन् m. (-री) A book or composition.<BR> E. द्वात्रिंशत् thirty-two,<BR>अक्षर a letter, a consonant, इनि affix; formed of thirty-two letters.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=359-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वात्रिंशल्लक्षणोपेत|द्वात्रिंशल्लक्षणोपेतः
द्वात्रिंशल्लक्षणोपेत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Having thirty-two auspicious marks,<BR>illustrious, great.<BR> E. द्वात्रिंशत् thirty-two, लक्षण a mark, उपेत possess-<BR>ing, endowed with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=359-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वादश|द्वादशः
द्वादश mf. (-शः-शी) Twelfth.<BR>	 f. (-शी) The twelfth day of the half month<BR>E. द्वादशन्, and टच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=359-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वादशक
द्वादशक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Consisting of twelve, amounting to twelve, &c.<BR>E. कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=359-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वादशकर|द्वादशकरः
द्वादशकर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A name of VṚHASPATI.<BR>	 2. A name of KĀBTIKEYA.<BR>E. द्वादश twelve, and कर a hand or ray.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=359-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वादशन्
द्वादशन् mfn. plu. (-श) Twelve.<BR> E. द्वा for द्वि two, and दशन् ten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=359-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वादशपत्रक|द्वादशपत्रकं
द्वादशपत्रक n. (-कं) A particular religious observance.<BR> E. द्वादश, and पत्र leaf<BR>or part, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=359-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वादशलोचन|द्वादशलोचनः
द्वादशलोचन m. (-नः) The god KĀRTIKEYA.<BR> E. द्वादश twelve, and लोचन an<BR>eye; the twelve-eyed, or six-headed deity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=359-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वादशांशु|द्वादशांशुः
द्वादशांशु m. (-शुः) The deity VṚHASPATI, or planet Jupiter, over which<BR>he presides.<BR> E. द्वादश twelve, and अंशु a ray.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=359-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वादशाक्ष|द्वादशाक्षः
द्वादशाक्ष m. (-क्षः)<BR>	 1. The god KĀRTIKEYA.<BR>	 2. The deity or sage Buddha.<BR>E. द्वादश twelve, and अक्ष an eye: the word is sometimes read in<BR>the second sense, द्वादशाख्य m. (-ख्यः) the twelve named.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=359-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वादशाक्षरमन्त्र|द्वादशाक्षरमन्त्रः
द्वादशाक्षरमन्त्र n. (-न्त्रं) A prayer of twelve syllables, especially as address-<BR>ed to VIṢṆU, or Om, BHAGAVATE, VASUDEVAYA, RĀMĀYA. E.<BR>द्वादश, अक्षर a letter, and मन्त्र formulæ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=359-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वादशाङ्गुल|द्वादशांगुल|द्वादशाङ्गुलः
द्वादशाङ्गुल m. (-लः) A measure of twelve fingers.<BR> E. द्वादश, and अङ्गुल a<BR>finger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=359-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वादशात्मन्
द्वादशात्मन् m. (-त्मा) The sun.<BR> E. द्वादश twelve, and आत्मन् identity; being<BR>represented in and identified with the twelve Adityas, or the sun<BR>in each month of the year; also द्वादशात्मक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=359-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वादशायुस्
द्वादशायुस् m. (-युः) A dog.<BR> E. द्वादश twelve, (years,) and आयुस् life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=359-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वादशार्च्चिस्|द्वादशार्चिस्
द्वादशार्च्चिस् m. (-र्च्चिः) VṚHASPATI, regent of Jupiter, and precepter of<BR>the gods.<BR> E. द्वादश twelve, and अर्च्चिस् a ray of light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=359-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वादशास्र
द्वादशास्र nf. (-स्रं-स्री) A parallelopipedon, a dodecagonal figure.<BR> E. द्वादश,<BR>and अस्र an angle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=360-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वापर|द्वापरं|द्वापरः
द्वापर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. The third of the four Yugas or great periods, compris-<BR>ing 864,000 years.<BR>	 2. The age personified as a god.<BR>	 3. Doubt, un-<BR>certainty.<BR> E. द्वा for द्वि two, पर after.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=360-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वार्
द्वार् f. (-द्वाः)<BR>	 1. A door, a gate.<BR>	 2. A means, an expedient, a medium or<BR>way by which any thing takes place or is effected.<BR> E. द्वृ to cover<BR>or hold, in the causal form, affix विच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=360-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वार|द्वारं
द्वार n. (-रं)<BR>	 1. A door, a gate, or rather the door or gateway, a passage,<BR>an entrance.<BR>	 2. A way, a means, a medium or vehicle.<BR> E. द्वृ to<BR>cover, affix अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=360-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वारक|द्वारकः
द्वारक mf. (-कः-का) Dwarakā the capital of KṚṢṆA, supposed<BR>to have been submerged by the sea, but represented by a<BR>small island of the north part of the Malaber coast.<BR> E. द्वार a<BR>way, (to salvation,) affix कन्; also द्वारिका, द्वारवती, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=360-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वारकण्टक|द्वारकंटक|द्वारकण्टकः
द्वारकण्टक m. (-कः) A door, gate, the door itself.<BR> E. द्वार a doorway, and<BR>कण्टक a thorn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=360-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वारकेश|द्वारकेशः
द्वारकेश m. (-शः) A name of KṚṢṆA.<BR> E. द्वारक as above, and ईश master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=360-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वारपाल|द्वारपालः
द्वारपाल m. (-लः) A warder, a doorkeeper.<BR> E. द्वार a door, and पाल who<BR>protects; also with कन् added द्वारपालक, or with the radical finals<BR>dropped द्वारप ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=360-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वारपिण्डी|द्वारपिंडी
द्वारपिण्डी f. (-ण्डी) the threshold of a door.<BR> E. द्वार a door, and पिण्ड a ball.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=360-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वारयन्त्र|द्वारयंत्र|द्वारयन्त्रं
द्वारयन्त्र n. (-न्त्रं) A lock, a bolt.<BR> E. द्वार a door, and यन्त्र an instrument.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=360-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वारवती
द्वारवती f. (-ती) The city Dvārakā.<BR> E. द्वार a door, and मतुप् poss. affix;<BR>also द्वारावती ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=360-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वारवलिभुज्
द्वारवलिभुज् m. (-भुक्) The Vaka, a sort of crane, (Ardea nivea.)<BR> E. द्वार<BR>a door, वलि offal or fragments, and भुज् who eats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=360-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वारशाखा
द्वारशाखा f. (-खा) The leaf of a door.<BR> E. द्वार a door, and शाखा a branch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=360-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वारस्तम्भ|द्वारस्तम्भः
द्वारस्तम्भ m. (-म्भः) A door-post.<BR> E. द्वार, and स्तम्भ a post.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=360-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वारस्थ|द्वारस्थः
द्वारस्थ m. (-स्थः) A doorkeeper.<BR> E. द्वार a gate, and स्थ who stays.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=360-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वारावती
द्वारावती f. (-ती) Dvārakā: see द्वारवती, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=360-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वारिक|द्वारिकः
द्वारिक m. (-कः) A doorkeeper, a warder.<BR> E. द्वार a door, and ठक् affix f.<BR>(-का) Dvārakā, KṚṢṆA'S capital: see द्वारक.<BR> E. द्वार, and ठन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=360-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वारिन्
द्वारिन् m. (-री) A porter, a warder, a doorkeeper.<BR> E. द्वार, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=360-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वास्थ|द्वास्थः
द्वास्थ m. (-स्थः) A doorkeeper, a warder.<BR> E. द्वार् a door, स्थ who stays,<BR>and र rejected; also र being changed to Visarga, द्वाःस्थ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=360-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वास्थित|द्वास्थितः
द्वास्थित m. (-तः) A doorkeeper.<BR> E. द्वार, and स्थित who stays; also द्वाःस्थित;<BR>see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=360-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वास्थितदशक
द्वास्थितदशक m. (-कः) A doorkeeper: see द्वाःस्थितदर्शक, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=360-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वि|द्विः
द्वि dual only.<BR>	 mf. (-द्वौ)<BR>	 n. (-द्वे) Two.<BR>	 m. (-द्विः) Two, (of times, &c.) is<BR>only used in composition, as अतिद्वि a thing more than two, and<BR>inflected like other nouns in इः in composition with other nume-<BR>rals, it is changed to द्वा, as द्वादश twelve, द्वाविंशति twenty-two,<BR>द्वात्रिंशत् thirty-two, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=360-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विक|द्विकं|द्विकः
द्विक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A crow.<BR>	 2. The ruddy goose.<BR> E. द्वि two, and क the<BR>letter क, as in काक mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>	 1. Two.<BR>	 2. Twice.<BR>	 3. Two-fold.<BR>E. द्वि two, कन् pleonastic aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=360-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विककार|द्विककारः
द्विककार m. (-रः) A crow.<BR> E. द्वि two or twice, and ककार the letter क,<BR>as in काक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=360-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विककुद्
द्विककुद् m. (-द्) A camel.<BR> E. द्वि two, and ककुद् a hump.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=360-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विकर
द्विकर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Who or what makes two of any thing.<BR> E. द्वि and<BR>कृ to make, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=360-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विगु|द्विगुः
द्विगु m. (-गुः) A form of grammatical combination, that in which the<BR>first member of the compound is a numeral.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=360-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विगुण|द्विगुणं
द्विगुण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>	 1. Twice, two times.<BR>	 2. Multiplied by two,<BR>doubled.<BR> E. द्वि two, and गुण number.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=360-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विगुणाकृत|द्विगुणाकृतं
द्विगुणाकृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Twice ploughed.<BR> E. द्विगुणा twice, and कृत<BR>ploughed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=360-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विगुणित
द्विगुणित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Doubled, multiplied by two.<BR>	 2. Folded,<BR>doubled.<BR>	 3. Inverted, enveloped.<BR> E. द्वि, and गुण a time, इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=360-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विगुणीकृत
द्विगुणीकृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Doubled.<BR>	 2. Increased.<BR> E. द्विगुण twice, कृत<BR>made, च्वि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=360-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विगुणीभूत
द्विगुणीभूत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Doubled.<BR>	 2. Augmented.<BR> E. द्विगुण twice,<BR>भूत become, च्वि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=360-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विज|द्विजः
द्विज mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>	 1. Twice born.<BR>	 2. Oviparous.<BR>	 m. (-जः)<BR>	 1. A man of<BR>either of the three first classes, a Brahman, a Kṣatriya or a<BR>Vaiśya whose investiture with the characteristic string, at years<BR>of puberty, constitutes, religiously and metaphorically, their<BR>second birth.<BR>	 2. Any oviparous animal, as a bird, a snake, a fish,<BR>&c. first born in the shell, and in the second instance produced<BR>from it.<BR>	 3. A tooth.<BR>	 4. Coriander seed.<BR>	 f. (-जा)<BR>	 1. A sort of perfume<BR>also called Renukā.<BR>	 2. A plant. (Siphonanthus Indicus.)<BR>	 3.<BR>Kundur or gum olebanum.<BR> E. द्वि two, and ज born. द्विः जायते ।<BR>जन ड ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=360-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विजकुत्सित|द्विजकुत्सितः
द्विजकुत्सित m. (-तः) A tree, (Cordia myxa.)<BR> E. द्विज a bird, कुत्सित reviled,<BR>disregarded. द्विजैः कुत्सितः । (नोना आता) द्विजानां तद्भक्षण निषेधात् तथात्वम् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=360-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विजन्मन्
द्विजन्मन् mfn. (-न्मा-न्मा-न्म)<BR>	 1. Twice born, regenerate.<BR>	 2. Oviparous m.<BR>(-न्मा)<BR>	 1. A tooth.<BR>	 2. A Brahman.<BR>	 3. A bird.<BR>	 4. A man of the three<BR>first classes.<BR>	 5. Any oviparous animal: see द्विज.<BR> E. द्वि twice, जन्मन्<BR>birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=360-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विजदास|द्विजदासः
द्विजदास m. (-सः) A Śūdra or man of the fourth and servile tribe.<BR>E. द्विज a man of either of the three first castes, and दास a slave.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=360-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विजपति|द्विजपतिः
द्विजपति m. (-तिः) The moon.<BR> E. द्विज a Brahman, and पति master. १ चन्द्रे<BR>२ कर्पूरे ४ द्विजश्रेष्ठे ५ पक्षिश्रेष्ठे ६ गरुडे ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=360-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विजप्रपा
द्विजप्रपा f. (-पा) A trough near a well for watering birds, cattle, &c. E.<BR>द्विज a bird, &c. and प्र prefixed to पा to drink, affixes अङ् and टाप्.<BR>द्विजार्थं पक्षिणमुद्दिश्य प्रषा । आलवाले ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=360-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विजप्रिय
द्विजप्रिय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Acceptable or friendly to a man of the three<BR>first classes, or a Brahman especially.<BR>	 f. (-या) The moonplant,<BR>(Asclepias acida.)<BR> E. द्विज a Brahman, and प्रिय beloved, the acid<BR>juice being drank at certain sacrifices.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=360-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विजब्रुव|द्विजब्रुवः
द्विजब्रुव m. (-वः) A Brahman by birth only, one not studied or not<BR>practising the duties of his caste.<BR> E. द्विज a Brahman, and ब्रुव<BR>who speaks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=360-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विजराज|द्विजराजः
द्विजराज m. (-जः)<BR>	 1. The moon.<BR>	 2. The great serpent ANANTA.<BR>	 3. The<BR>bird and vehicle of VIṢṆU.<BR>	 4. Camphor.<BR> E. द्विज a snake or bird,<BR>and राज king. see द्विजपति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=360-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विजलिङ्गिन्|द्विजलिंगिन्
द्विजलिङ्गिन् m. (-ङ्गी)<BR>	 1. A Kṣatriya or man of the military tribe 2.<BR>An impostor, a pretended Brahman, wearing the distinguishing<BR>mark of that tribe without belonging to it.<BR> E. द्विज twice born,<BR>and लिङ्ग a mark, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=360-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विजवर्य्य|द्विजवर्य
द्विजवर्य्य m. (-र्य्यः) An excellent or superior Brahman.<BR> E. द्विज and वर्य्य excellent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=360-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विजब्रण
द्विजब्रण m. (-णः) Gumboil, toothache.<BR> E. द्विज a tooth, ब्रण a sore.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=360-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विजशप्त|द्विजशप्तः
द्विजशप्त m. (-प्तः) A sort of pulse; also called Rāja-māsh-kalai and<BR>Barbatti, (Dolichos catjang.)<BR> E. द्विज a Brahman, and शप्त cursed;<BR>it is a prohibited food on some occasions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=360-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विजशुश्रूषा
द्विजशुश्रूषा f. (-षा) Service of the three first classes, especially of the<BR>Brahmans, by the forth.<BR> E. द्विज and शुश्रूषा service.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=360-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विजसत्तम
द्विजसत्तम m. (-मः) A respectable Brahman.<BR> E. द्विज and सत्तम best; also<BR>द्विजवर द्विजप्रवर &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=360-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विजसेवक|द्विजसेवकः
द्विजसेवक m. (-कः) A Śūdra or man of the fourth and servile class. E.<BR>द्विज a man of the three first classes, and सेवक a servant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=360-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विजसेवा
द्विजसेवा f. (-वा) Service of the three first classes, especially of the<BR>Brahman by the fourth.<BR> E. द्विज, and सेवा service.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=360-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विजाग्र्य
द्विजाग्र्य m. (-ग्र्यः) A chief or respectable Brahman.<BR> E. द्विज, and अग्र्य<BR>first.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=360-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विजाङ्गी
द्विजाङ्गी f. (-ङ्गी) A medicinal plant; also कटुरोहिणी ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=360-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विजाति|द्विजातिः
द्विजाति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. A Brahman.<BR>	 2. A man of either of the three first<BR>classes.<BR>	 3. Any oviparous animal, as a bird, a snake, &c.<BR> E. द्वि<BR>two, जाति birth. द्विः जातिः जन्म यस्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=360-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विजानुलोम
द्विजानुलोम n. (-मं) The regular order or series of the three first classes.<BR>E. द्विज, and अनुलोम with the hair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=361-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विजायनी
द्विजायनी f. (-नी) The characteristic thread or cord which designates<BR>the three first classes of the Hindus.<BR> E. द्विज twice-born, ल्युट् affix,<BR>fem. affix ङीप् । द्विजः अय्यते ज्ञायते अनया । यज्ञोपवीते ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=361-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विजालय|द्विजालयः
द्विजालय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. The hollow of a tree.<BR>	 2. The residence of Brah-<BR>mans.<BR> E. द्विज a bird, or a Brahman, and आलय an asylum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=361-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विजिह्व|द्विजिह्वः
द्विजिह्व (mfn.) (-ह्वः-ह्वा-ह्वं) Double-tongued, (literally or figuratively.)<BR>	 m.<BR>(-ह्वः)<BR>	 1. A snake.<BR>	 2. An informer.<BR>	 3. A rogue, a scoundrel, a<BR>bad man.<BR>	 4. A thief.<BR> E. द्वि two, जिह्वा the tongue. द्वे जिह्वे यस्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=361-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विजिह्वता
द्विजिह्वता f. (-ता) Insincerity, dishonesty.<BR> E. तल् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=361-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विजोत्तम|द्विजोत्तमः
द्विजोत्तम m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. A Brahman.<BR>	 2. A superior or excellent Brahman.<BR>E. द्विज the twice-born, (three first classes,) and उत्तम best.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=361-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विज्या
द्विज्या f. (-ज्या) The sine or chord of an arc.<BR> E. द्वि, and ज्या sine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=361-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विज्यामार्ग
द्विज्यामार्ग m. (-र्गं) A horizontal line.<BR> E. द्विज्य, and मार्ग road.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=361-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विट्सेवा
द्विट्सेवा f. (-वा) Treachery.<BR> E. द्विष् a foe, सेवा service.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=361-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विट्सेविन्
द्विट्सेविन् n. (-वी) A traitor.<BR> E. द्विट् an enemy, and सेविन् who serves.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=361-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विठ|द्विठः
द्विठ m. (-ठः) Swāhā, the expression used with an oblation to fire. द्वौ<BR>ठकारौ लेखनाकारे यस्य । विसर्गे स्वाहायाम् । ठकारद्वये ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=361-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वितय|द्वितयं
द्वितय n. (-यं) A couple, a pair, two.<BR> E. द्वि two, तयप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=361-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वितीय|द्वितीयं|द्वितीयः
द्वितीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>	 1. Second.<BR>	 2. Two.<BR>	 m. (-यः) A son, a second or<BR>successor.<BR>	 f. (-या)<BR>	 1. A wife, according to the ritual, a woman<BR>wedded after the ceremony prescribed by the Vedas, a second self<BR>as it were.<BR>	 2. The second day of the fortnight.<BR> E. द्वि two, and तीय<BR>affix, fem. affix टाप्; also with कन् added, द्वितीयक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=361-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वितीयत्व
द्वितीयत्व n. (-त्वं) The circumstance or state of second.<BR> E. द्वितीय, and त्व<BR>affix; also with तल्, द्वितीयता ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=361-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वितीयत्रिफला
द्वितीयत्रिफला f. (-ला) A set of three fruits, the grape, the date, and the<BR>Gāmbhāri.<BR> E. द्वितीय second, त्रिफल three fruits.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=361-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वितीयाकृत|द्वितीयाकृतं
द्वितीयाकृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Twice ploughed, &c. (a field)<BR> E. द्वितीय a<BR>second time, and आकृत made.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=361-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वितीयाभा
द्वितीयाभा f. (-भा) A scitamineous plant, (Curcuma zanthorrhiza)<BR> E. द्वितीय<BR>second, आभा lustre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=361-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वितीयीक
द्वितीयीक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Second.<BR> E. द्वितीय, and ईकक pleonasm added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=361-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वित्र
द्वित्र mfn. plu. always (-त्राः-त्राः-त्राणि) Two or three.<BR> E. द्वि two and त्र for<BR>त्रि three.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=361-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विदत्|द्विदन्त्
द्विदत् mfn. (-दन्-दती-दत्) Two-toothed.<BR> E. द्वि two, दत् for दन्त a tooth;<BR>in marking age or period the compound is द्विदन्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=361-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विदन्त|द्विदन्तः
द्विदन्त mfn. (-न्तः-न्ती-न्तं) Old enough to have two teeth, &c.<BR> E. द्वि, and<BR>दन्त a tooth, see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=361-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विदण्डि|द्विदंडि
द्विदण्डि ind. Single stick, quarter staff, as द्विदण्डि प्रहरणं fighting with<BR>two sticks.<BR> E. द्वि, दण्ड a staff, इच् affix; also similar compounds,<BR>as द्विमुषलि, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=361-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विदश
द्विदश m. plu. (-शाः) Twenty, two tens.<BR> E. द्वि, and दश ten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=361-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विदाम्नी
द्विदाम्नी f. (-म्नी) A cow tied with two ropes.<BR> E. द्वि, and दामन् a rope.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=361-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विदेह|द्विदेहः
द्विदेह m. (-हः) A name of GANESA.<BR> E. द्वि two, and देह a body; having<BR>the head of an elephant, with the figure of a man. द्वाभ्यां देहोऽस्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=361-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विदैवत्या
द्विदैवत्या f. (-त्या) The constellation Viśākhā.<BR> E. द्वि two, दैवत a deity,<BR>and क्यप् affix; INDRA and AGNI jointly presiding over the<BR>asterism.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=361-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विघा
द्विघा ind. Of two kinds, in two ways.<BR> E. द्वि two, धा aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=361-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विधाकरण
द्विधाकरण n. (-णं) Dividing into two parts, arranging in two ways, &c.<BR>E. द्विधा, and करण making.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=361-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विधागति|द्विधागतिः
द्विधागति m. (-तिः) A crocodile.<BR> E. द्विधा of two sorts, गति going;<BR>amphibious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=361-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विधातु|द्विधातुः
द्विधातु mfn. (-तुः-तुः-तु) Having two natures, two roots, &c.<BR>	 m. (-तुः) A<BR>name of GANESA.<BR> E. द्वि two or double, धातु nature: see द्विदेह । द्वौ<BR>धातू यत्र । धातुद्बयघटिते कांस्यरैत्यादौ, गणेशे च ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=361-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विधात्मक|द्विधात्मकं
द्विधात्मक n. (-कं) A nutmeg.<BR> E. द्विधा two sorts, and आत्मक being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=361-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विधालेख्य|द्विधालेख्यः
द्विधालेख्य mfn. (-ख्यः-ख्या-ख्यं) To be written in two ways.<BR>	 m. (-ख्यः) The<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=361-b" target="_blank">Page361-b+ 60</a>]<BR>marshy date tree.<BR> E. द्विधा, and लेख्य to be written or described.<BR>द्विप्रकारे लेखनीये हिन्तालवृक्षे च ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=361-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विनग्नक|द्विनग्नकः
द्विनग्नक m. (-कः) A circumcised man, one having no prepuce.<BR> E. द्वि<BR>two, नग्न naked, कन् added; exposed either by want of clothes or<BR>skin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=361-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विनिष्क
द्विनिष्क mfn. (-ष्कः-ष्का-ष्कं) Bought, &c. with two Nishkas.<BR> E. द्वि, and<BR>निष्क a measure of value; also द्विनैष्किक mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=361-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विप|द्विपः
द्विप m. (-पः)<BR>	 1. An elephant.<BR>	 2. A plant, (Mesua ferrea.)<BR> E. द्वि two,<BR>and प who drinks, the elephant imbibing fluids by his trunk,<BR>and thence conveying them into his mouth. द्वाभ्यां मुखशुण्डाभ्यां पिबति<BR>पा-क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=361-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विपथ|द्विपथं
द्विपथ n. (-थं) A place where two roads meet.<BR> E. द्वि two, पथिन् a road.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=361-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विपद|द्विपदः
द्विपद mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>	 1. Two-footed.<BR>	 2. Having two parts.<BR>	 3. Binomial.<BR>m. (-दः) A biped, including four genera, gods, demons. men, and<BR>birds.<BR> E. द्वि, and पद for पाद a foot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=361-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विपदराशि|द्विपदराशिः
द्विपदराशि f. (-शिः) Either of the signs, Gemini, Libra, Aquarius, Virgo,<BR>and half of Sagittarius.<BR> E. द्विपद, and राशि a sign.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=361-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विपमद|द्विपमदः
द्विपमद m. (-दः) The elephant's temporal juice.<BR> E. द्विप, and मद the<BR>exudation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=361-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विपर्ण
द्विपर्ण mfn. (-र्णः-र्णी-र्णं) Two leaved, opposite-leaved.<BR> E. द्वि, and पर्ण a<BR>leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=361-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विपात्त्व
द्विपात्त्व n. (-त्त्वं) The having of two feet, two parts, &c.<BR> E. द्विपाद्, and<BR>त्व affix; also with तल्, द्विपात्ता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=361-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विपाद्
द्विपाद् mfn. (-पाद्-पती-पत्) Biped, two-footed.<BR> E. द्वि two, and पाद् for पाद<BR>a foot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=361-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विपाद्य|द्विपाद्यं|द्विपाद्यः
द्विपाद्य mfn. (-द्यः-द्या-द्यं) Bought, &c. with two quarters.<BR>	 n. (-द्यं) A<BR>double penalty, an amercement of twice the common amount. E.<BR>द्वि two, पाद a division, and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=361-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विपायिन्
द्विपायिन् m. (-यी) An elephant.<BR> E. द्वि two, and पायिन् who drinks: see<BR>द्विप.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=361-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विपृष्ट
द्विपृष्ट m. (-ष्टः) A proper name; also VASUDEVA. ब्रह्मसम्भवे राजभेदे ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=361-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विप्रतिक
द्विप्रतिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Bought, &c. with two Karṣas.<BR> E. द्वि, प्रति for<BR>कार्षापण, and ठन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=361-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विबाहु|द्विबाहुः
द्विबाहु mfn. (-हुः-ह्वी-हु) Two armed.<BR> E. द्वि, and वाहु an arm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=361-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विभुज|द्विभुजः
द्विभुज mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>	 1. Two armed.<BR>	 2. An angle or the lines which<BR>form it.<BR> E. द्वि two, and भुज an arm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=361-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विमय
द्विमय mfn. (-यः-यी-यं) Made or consisting of two, (parts of any thing.)<BR>E. द्वि, and मयट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=361-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विमातृज|द्विमातृजः
द्विमातृज mfn. (-जः-जा-जं) Having two mothers, born in two ways; it<BR>may be said of some of the deities, thus GANESA was the son of<BR>PĀRVATĪ, but not born in the usual way, being made of the scur<BR>of her body; see द्वैमातुर.<BR> E. द्वि two, मातृ a mother, and ज born.<BR>द्वाभ्यां मातृभ्यां जायते जन-ड ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=361-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विमुख|द्विमुखः
द्विमुख m. (-खः) A serpent.<BR>	 f. (-खा)<BR>	 1. A small water jar.<BR>	 2. A leech. E.<BR>द्वि, and मुख mouth; double-headed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=361-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विमुखाहि|द्विमुखाहिः
द्विमुखाहि m. (-हिः) A sort of serpent, (Amphisbœna.)<BR> E. द्वि two, मुख<BR>face, अहि a snake; the double-headed snake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=361-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विमुखोरग|द्विमुखोरगः
द्विमुखोरग m. (-गः) A sort of snake: see the last.<BR> E. द्विमुख as above,<BR>and उरग a snake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=361-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विमूर्द्ध
द्विमूर्द्ध mfn. (-र्द्धः-र्द्धा-र्द्धं) Two-headed.<BR> E. द्वि two, मूर्द्धन् the fore-head, and<BR>यच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=361-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विर|द्विरः
द्विर m. (-रः) A bee: see द्विरेफ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=361-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विरद|द्विरदः
द्विरद m. (-दः) An elephant.<BR> E. द्वि two, and रद a tooth, having tusks<BR>and teeth,<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=361-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विरदान्तक|द्विरदांतक|द्विरदान्तकः
द्विरदान्तक m. (-कः) A lion.<BR> E. द्विरद, and अन्तक destroyer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=361-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विरशन|द्विरशनं
द्विरशन n. (-नं) Eating twice a day.<BR> E. द्वि, and अशन् eating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=361-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विरसन|द्विरसनः
द्विरसन m. (-नः) A snake in general.<BR> E. द्वि two, रसना the tongue; double<BR>or forky-tongued.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=361-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विरात्र
द्विरात्र n. (-त्रं) A period of two nights.<BR> E. द्वि, and रात्र for रात्रि<BR>night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=361-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विराप|द्विरापः
द्विराप m. (-पः) An elephant.<BR> E. द्विर् for द्वि two, आङ् prefixed to पा to<BR>drink, affix ड; drinking with the trunk and mouth: see द्विप ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=362-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विरुक्त|द्विरुक्तः
द्विरुक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>	 1. Repeated, said twice.<BR>	 2. Said or told in two<BR>ways.<BR> E. द्वि, and उक्त said.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=362-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विरुक्ति|द्विरुक्तिः
द्विरुक्ति f. (-क्तिः)<BR>	 1. Tautology, repetition.<BR>	 2. Variety of narration,<BR>telling any thing in two ways.<BR>	 3. (In Grammar,) Repetition of a<BR>syllable.<BR> E. द्वि, and उक्ति saying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=362-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विरुढा
द्विरुढा f. (-ढा) A woman who has been twice married.<BR> E. द्वि two, उढ a<BR>married woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=362-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विरूप|द्विरूपः
द्विरूप mfn. (-पः-पा-पी-पं)<BR>	 1. Of two forms, having a different shape.<BR>2. Spelled or written in two ways.<BR>	 m. (-पः)<BR>	 1. A word that may<BR>be correctly spelled in two ways.<BR>	 2. Variety of interpretation or<BR>reading.<BR> E. द्वि, and रूप form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=362-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विरेफ|द्विरेफः
द्विरेफ m. (-फः) A large black bee.<BR> E. द्वि two, रेफ the letter र; having<BR>two rs, in the most common name, भ्रमर, Bhramara.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=362-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विरेफवृन्द
द्विरेफवृन्द n. (-न्दं) A flight or swarm of bees.<BR> E. द्विरेफ, and वृन्द a number.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=362-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विवर्ष
द्विवर्ष mfn. (-र्षः-र्षी-र्षं) Two years old, &c.<BR>	 f. (-र्षा) A cow two years old.<BR>E. द्वि two, वर्ष a year.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=362-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विवर्षिका
द्विवर्षिका f. (-का) A cow two years old.<BR> E. द्विवर्ष, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=362-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विवर्षीण|द्विवर्षीणः
द्विवर्षीण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Two years old, two years standing, &c.<BR> E. द्वि<BR>two, वर्ष a year, ख affix; also with ठञ् affix द्विवार्षिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>when futurity is implied, the first vowel is usually changed, as<BR>द्वैवार्षिक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=362-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विवाहिका
द्विवाहिका f. (-का) A swing, a swinging cot, a litter.<BR> E. द्वि two, वाह to<BR>bear, affix ण्वुल्; born usually by two men.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=362-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विविद|द्विविदः
द्विविद m. (-दः) The name of monkey, slain by RĀMA or VIṢṆU in<BR>that incarnation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=362-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विविदारि
द्विविदारि m. (-रिः) VIṢṆU.<BR> E. द्विविद as above, अरि the foe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=362-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विविध
द्विविध mfn. (-धः-धा-धं) Of two kinds, in two ways.<BR> E. द्वि, and विध sort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=362-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विवेशरा
द्विवेशरा f. (-रा) A kind of carriage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=362-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विशफ|द्विशफः
द्विशफ m. (-फः) Any cloven-footed animal.<BR> E. द्वि and शफ a hoof.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=362-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विशस्
द्विशस् ind. Two, respectively.<BR> E. द्वि two, and शस् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=362-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विशीर्षक
द्विशीर्षक m. (-कः) A name of AGNI.<BR> E. द्वि two, शीर्ष a head, and कन्<BR>added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=362-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विशूर्प्प|द्विशूर्प
द्विशूर्प्प mfn. (-र्प्प-र्प्पी-र्प्पं) Bought with two winnowing baskets of any-<BR>thing.<BR> E. द्वि, and शूर्प्प a basket; also with ठञ्, द्विशौर्प्पिक, mfn.<BR>(-कः-की-कं.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=362-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विशृङ्गिन्
द्विशृङ्गिन् m. (-ङ्गी) A sort of fish, commonly called Marmaka.<BR> E. द्वि two,<BR>शृङ्ग a horn, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=362-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विष|द्विषः
द्विष r. 1st cl. द्विषति also (औ) औद्विष r. 2nd cl. (द्वेष्टि-ष्टे) plu. (द्विषन्ति) To<BR>hate, to dislike, to be hostile or unfriendly. अदा० उभ० सक० अनिट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=362-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विष्
द्विष् mfn. (द्विट्) Inimical, hostile.<BR>	 m. (द्विट्) An enemy.<BR> E. द्विष् to hate,<BR>affix क्विप्; also with क affix द्विष m. (-षः) or mfn. (-षः-षा-षं.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=362-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विषत्|द्विषन्त्
द्विषत् mfn. (-षन्-षन्ती-षत्)<BR>	 1. Hating or detesting, hostile.<BR>	 2. Inimical,<BR>unfriendly.<BR>	 m. (-न्) An enemy.<BR> E. द्विष् to hate, participal aff. शतृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=362-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विषतीताप|द्विषतीतापः
द्विषतीताप mfn. (-पः-पा-पं) Vexing or harassing an enemy.<BR> E. द्विषत् and<BR>ताप who afflicts, with च्वि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=362-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विषन्तप|द्विषंतप|द्विषन्तपः
द्विषन्तप mfn. (-पः-पा-पं) Punishing or annoying an enemy, revenging,<BR>retaliating.<BR> E. द्विष an enemy, तप् to burn, affix खच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=362-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विष्ट|द्विष्टं
द्विष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं) Hated, dislike.<BR>	 n. (-ष्टं) Copper: see द्व्यष्ट.<BR> E. द्विष्<BR>to hate, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=362-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विष्ठ|द्विष्ठः
द्विष्ठ mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठा-ष्ठं) Staying in two shapes or places, &c.<BR> E. द्वि two,<BR>and स्थ what is or abides. द्वयो स्तिष्ठति स्था-क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=362-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विसप्ताह|द्विसप्ताहः
द्विसप्ताह m. (-हः) A fortnight.<BR> E. द्वि twice, सप्त seven, and अह a day.<BR>twice seven days.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=362-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विसम
द्विसम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं) Consisting of two equal portions, &c.<BR> E. द्वि two,<BR>सम equal. द्वि समे परिमाणमस्य ठञ् तस्य लुक् । द्विवर्षपरिमाणे.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=362-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विसमत्रिभुजा
द्विसमत्रिभुजा f. (-जा) An isosceles triangle.<BR> E. द्वि, सम equal, त्रिभुजा<BR>triangle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=362-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विसहस्राक्ष|द्विसहस्राक्षः
द्विसहस्राक्ष m. (-क्षः) The great serpent, sovereign of the snake race, and<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=362-b" target="_blank">Page362-b+ 60</a>]<BR>the couch of VIṢṆU.<BR> E. द्विसहस्र two thousand, and अक्षि an eye:<BR>the two thousand-eyed. द्विरावृत्तं सहस्रमक्षोणि यस्य, अनन्ते ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=362-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विसीत्य|द्विसीत्यं
द्विसीत्य mfn. (-त्यः-त्या-त्यं) Twice ploughed.<BR> E. द्वि twice, सीता a plough.<BR>and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=362-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विस्तन
द्विस्तन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Two-breasted, two-uddered.<BR> E. द्वि and स्तन breast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=362-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विहन्
द्विहन् m. (-हा) An elephant.<BR> E. द्वि two ways, with tusks and teeth,<BR>and हन् who kills.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=362-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विहल्य|द्विहल्यं
द्विहल्य mfn. (-ल्यः-ल्या-ल्यं) Twice ploughed.<BR> E. द्वि two, हल a plough,<BR>affix यत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=362-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विहायन
द्विहायन mfn. (-नः-नी-नं) Two years old.<BR>	 f. (-नी) A cow two years old. E.<BR>द्वि two, हायन a year, affixes अण् and ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=362-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विहृदया
द्विहृदया f. (-या) A pregnant woman.<BR> E. द्वि two, हृदय a heart; having,<BR>one of her own and one in the fœtus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=362-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विन्द्रियग्राह्य
द्विन्द्रियग्राह्य mfn. (-ह्यः-ह्या-ह्यं) Perceptible by two senses or forms, by<BR>sight and touch, &c.<BR> E. द्वि, इन्द्रिय an organ of sense, ग्राह्य to be<BR>seized.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=362-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वीप|द्वीपं|द्वीपः
द्वीप mn. (-पः-पं)<BR>	 1. An island, any land surrounded by water; the<BR>word is hence applied to the seven grand divisions of the<BR>terrestrial world, each of these being separated from the next, by<BR>a peculiar and circumambient ocean: the seven Dwīpas, reckon-<BR>ing from the central one are, Jambu, Kusa, Plaksha, Sālmalī,<BR>Krauncha, Sāka, and Pushkara: the central Dwīpa, or the known<BR>continent, is again portioned into ten divisions, likewise termed<BR>Dwīpas: viz. Kuru, Chandra, Varuna, Saumya, Naga, Kumārikā,<BR>Gabhastiman, Tāmrāpurna, Kaseru and Indra.<BR>	 2. A tiger's skin.<BR>E. द्वि two, (on both sides,) and आप water, आ dropped and इ made<BR>long. द्विर्गता द्वयो र्वा दिशोर्गता आपोऽत्र । अ० समा० ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=362-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वीपकर्पूरक
द्वीपकर्पूरक m. (-कः) China camphor.<BR> E. द्वीप and कर्पूर camphor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=362-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वीपवत्|द्वीपवन्त्
द्वीपवत् m. (-वान्) The ocean.<BR>	 mf. (-वान्-वती) A river.<BR>	 f. (-वती) The earth.<BR>E. द्वीप an island, मतुप् possessive aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=362-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वीपिन्
द्वीपिन् mfn. (-पी-पिनी-पि) Island, islander.<BR>	 m. (-पी)<BR>	 1. A tiger.<BR>	 2. An<BR>ounce or panther.<BR> E. द्वीप an Island, इनि affix; haunting the small<BR>woody islands that abound in the rivers in India, or द्वीप a tiger's<BR>spotted skin, derived from द्वि two; इ to go or be, प affix: and<BR>इनि as before.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=362-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वीपिशत्रु|द्वीपिशत्रुः
द्वीपिशत्रु m. (-त्रुः) A plant, (Asparagus racemosus.)<BR> E. द्वीपिन् a tiger, and<BR>शत्रु obnoxious. शतावर्य्याम् । द्वीपिनः व्याघ्रस्य शत्रुरिव ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=362-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वीप्य|द्वीप्यः
द्वीप्य mfn. (-प्यः-प्या-प्यं) Island, an islander, &c.<BR>	 m. (-प्यः)<BR>	 1. A sort of<BR>crow.<BR>	 2. A name of VYĀSA.<BR> E. द्वीप, and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=362-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वृ
द्वृ r. 1st cl. (द्वारति)<BR>	 1. To accept, to appoint.<BR>	 2. To cover.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=362-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वेधा
द्वेधा ind. In two ways: see द्विधा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=362-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वेष|द्वेषः
द्वेष m. (-षः) Hate, enmity.<BR> E. द्विष to hate, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=362-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वेषण|द्वेषणं|द्वेषणः
द्वेषण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Inimical, hostile.<BR>	 m. (-णः) An enemy.<BR>	 n. (-णं)<BR>Hate, enmity.<BR> E. द्विष् to hate, and ल्यु or युच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=362-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वेषिन्
द्वेषिन् mfn. (-षी-षिणी-षि) Hostile, inimical, adverse, obnoxious.<BR>	 m. (-षी)<BR>An enemy.<BR> E. द्विष् to hate, णिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=362-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वेष्टृ
द्वेष्टृ mfn. (-ष्टा-ष्ट्री-ष्टृ) Hating, inimical, an enemy.<BR> E. द्विष to hate, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=362-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वेष्य|द्वेष्यः
द्वेष्य mfn. (-ष्यः-ष्या-ष्य) Hateful, detestable.<BR> E. द्विष to hate, affix ण्यत् । द्वेष्टु-<BR>मर्हः यत् कर्मणि ण्यत् वा ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=362-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वेष्यता
द्वेष्यता f. (-ता) Aversion, dislike, detestableness.<BR> E. द्वेष्य and तल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=362-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वैगुणिक|द्वैगुणिकः
द्वैगुणिक m. (-कः) A usurer, a money lender.<BR> E. द्वि two, गुण number,<BR>affix ठक्; who requires cent. per cent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=362-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वैगुण्य|द्वैगुण्यं
द्वैगुण्य n. (-ण्यं)<BR>	 1. Duality.<BR>	 2. The possession of two out of the three<BR>qualities.<BR>	 3. Doubling.<BR> E. द्विगुण and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=362-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वैजात
द्वैजात mfn. (-तः-ती-तं) Twice-born.<BR> E. द्विजात, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=362-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वैत|द्वैतं
द्वैत n. (-तं)<BR>	 1. Duplication, doubling or being doubled.<BR>	 2. Duality, in<BR>philosophy, the assertion of two principles, as the distinctness of<BR>life and soul, spirit and matter, god and the universe.<BR> E. द्वि two<BR>तल् affix, द्वित double, two-fold, abstract affix अण्. द्विधा इतं द्वीतं तस्य<BR>भावः स्वार्थे वा अण् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=362-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वैतवादिन्
द्वैतवादिन् m. (-दी) A philosopher who asserts two principles.<BR> E. द्वैत,<BR>and वादिन् who asserts. द्वैतं जीवभेदं जीवेश्वरयोः भेदं वा वदति वद णिनि<BR>जीवभेदवादिनि जीवेश्वरयोः भेदवादिनि च नैयायिकादौ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=363-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वैतीयीक|द्वैतीयीकः
द्वैतीयीक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Second.<BR> E. द्वितीय second, pleonastic affix<BR>अण् and ईकक् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=363-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वैध|द्वैधं
द्वैध mfn. (-धः-धी-धं) Two-fold, of two sorts.<BR>	 n. (-धं)<BR>	 1. A double resource,<BR>a stratagem, a secondary arrangement or array, a reserve.<BR>	 2.<BR>Contest, dispute, difference.<BR>	 3. A two-fold form or state.<BR> E. द्वैधम्<BR>and ड added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=363-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वैधम्
द्वैधम् ind. In two ways.<BR> E. द्वि, and धमुञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=363-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वैधीकरण
द्वैधीकरण n. (-णं) Making two, separating, disuniting.<BR> E. द्वैध and करण<BR>making, च्वि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=363-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वैधीकृत
द्वैधीकृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Separated.<BR>	 2. made into two, sundered. E.<BR>द्वैध and कृत made, च्वि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=363-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वैधीभाव|द्वैधीभावः
द्वैधीभाव m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. Sowing dissension, causing tho separation of allies.<BR>2. Dividing into two.<BR>	 3. The nature or property of being two or<BR>distinct.<BR> E. द्वैध, and भाव property, च्वि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=363-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वैधीभूत
द्वैधीभूत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Being two, being separated or disunited.<BR> E. द्वैध<BR>and भूत become, च्वि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=363-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वैप|द्वैपः
द्वैप mfn. (-पः-पी-पं)<BR>	 1. Made of a tiger's skin.<BR>	 2. Island, islander.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-षः) A car covered or hung with a tiger's skin.<BR> E. द्वीप a tiger's<BR>skin, and अञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=363-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वैपायन्
द्वैपायन् m. (-नः) A name of VYĀSA, the author or compiler of the<BR>Vedas and Purānas.<BR> E. द्वीप an island, फक् affix; the island-born,<BR>the place of his nativity being a small island in Jamunā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=363-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वैप्य|द्वैप्यं
द्वैप्य mfn. (-प्यः-प्या-प्यं) Of or belonging to an island.<BR> E. द्वीप an island,<BR>यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=363-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वैमातुर|द्वैमातुरः
द्वैमातुर mfn. (-रः-री-रं) Having two mothers, or the natural mother and<BR>a step-mother.<BR>	 m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A name of GANESA.<BR>	 2. An epithet of<BR>JARĀSANDHA: see जरासन्ध.<BR> E. द्वि two, मातृ a mother, अण् affix, उ<BR>substituted for the penultimate: see द्विमातृज.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=363-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वैमित्रि
द्वैमित्रि mfn. (-त्रिः-त्री-त्रि) Born of two friends, the children, &c.<BR> E. द्वि,<BR>and मित्र a friend, इञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=363-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वैयह्निक
द्वैयह्निक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Of or belonging to two days.<BR> E. द्व्यहन्, and<BR>ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=363-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वैरथ|द्वैरथं|द्वैरथः
द्वैरथ m. (-थः) Single combat in chariots.<BR> E. द्विरथ two cars, अण्<BR>aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=363-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वैरात्रिक
द्वैरात्रिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Of or belonging to a period of two nights. E.<BR>द्विरात्र, and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=363-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वैवर्षिक
द्वैवर्षिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) After two years, of or belonging to two years<BR>to come.<BR> E. द्वि, वर्ष a year, ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=363-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वैविध्य|द्वैविध्यं
द्वैविध्य n. (-ध्यं) The state of being two-fold.<BR> E. द्विविध, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=363-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वैहायन|द्वैहायनं
द्वैहायन n. (-नं) The age of two years.<BR> E. द्विहायन, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=363-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्व्यंश
द्व्यंश m. (-शः) Two shares.<BR> E. द्वि, and अंश part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=363-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्व्यक्षर|द्व्यक्षरं|द्व्यक्षरः
द्व्यक्षर n. (-रं) A word of two syllables.<BR> E. द्वि, and अक्षर a syllable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=363-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्व्यङ्गुल|द्व्यंगुल|द्व्यङ्गुलं
द्व्यङ्गुल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Measuring two fingers.<BR>	 n. (-लं) Two fingers. E.<BR>द्वि two, अङ्गुलि a finger, if wood (काष्ठ) is implied, the fem. form<BR>is द्व्यङ्गुलि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=363-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्व्यञ्जल|द्व्यञ्जलं
द्व्यञ्जल mfn. (-लः-ली-लं) Measuring, &c. two Anjalis.<BR>	 m. (-लिः) Two<BR>Anjalis collectively.<BR> E. द्वि, and अञ्जलि a certain measure, टच् affix;<BR>also with the final retained द्व्यञ्जलि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=363-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्व्यणुक|द्व्यणुकं
द्व्यणुक n. (-कं) The aggregation of two atoms, the first step in the<BR>formation of substances, and when they become perceptible, The<BR>molecule of two atoms.<BR> E. द्वि and अणु an atom, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=363-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्व्यन्य|द्व्यन्यः
द्व्यन्य mfn. (-न्यः-न्या-न्यं) Accompanied, &c. by two others.<BR>	 n. (-न्यं) Two<BR>others collectively.<BR> E. द्वि, and अन्य another.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=363-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्व्यर्थ|द्व्यर्थः
द्व्यर्थ mfn. (-र्थः-र्था-र्थं)<BR>	 1. Having two senses, meaning two things.<BR>	 2.<BR>Having two objects.<BR>	 m. (-र्थः) Two-fold meaning, double-entendre.<BR>E. द्वि, and अर्थ sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=363-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्व्यष्ट|द्व्यष्टं
द्व्यष्ट n. (-ष्टं) Copper.<BR> E. द्वि two, (metals; gold and silvers.) अश to<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=363-b" target="_blank">Page363-b+ 54</a>]<BR>pervade, affix क्त; mixed as alloy with the fine metals; also the<BR>य being interchanged with its congener इ, द्विष्ट.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=363-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्व्यह|द्व्यहः
द्व्यह m. (-हः) Two days.<BR> E. द्वि two, and अह a day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=363-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्व्यहीन
द्व्यहीन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Of or belonging to two days.<BR> E. द्व्यह, and ख aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=363-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्व्यात्मक|द्व्यात्मकः
द्व्यात्मक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Comprising two, being two.<BR>	 m. (-कः) A sign<BR>of the zodiac, Gemini, Virgo, Sagittarius, and Pisces.<BR> E. द्वि, and<BR>आत्मन् self, कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=363-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्व्यामुष्यायण|द्व्यामुष्यायणः
द्व्यामुष्यायण m. (-णः) A boy who remains heir to his father though<BR>adopted by another.<BR> E. द्वि, and आमुष्यायण a certain person. अमुष्य<BR>प्रसिद्धस्यापत्यम् फक् आमुष्यायणः द्वयोरामुष्यायणः ६ तत् पु० स० ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=363-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्व्यायुष
द्व्यायुष n. (-षं) Two lives.<BR> E. द्वि, and आयुष् life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=363-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्व्याहिक|द्व्याहिकः
द्व्याहिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Produced, &c. in two days.<BR> E. द्व्यह, and ठञ्<BR>aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=363-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्व्येकान्तर
द्व्येकान्तर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Having two between, two off.<BR> E. द्वि, and<BR>एकान्तर an interval, a line.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=363-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध|धं|धः
ध The aspirated letter corresponding to the preceding, and expressed<BR>by Dh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=363-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध|धं|धः
ध m. (धः)<BR>	 1. A name of BRAMHĀ.<BR>	 2. A name KUVERA.<BR>	 3. Virtue, moral<BR>merit n. (-धं) Wealth, property.<BR> E. धा to have or possess, affix ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=363-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धक्क
धक्क r. 10th cl. (धक्कयति-ते) To destroy or annihilate. चुरा० उभ० सक० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=363-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धट|धटः
धट m. (-टः)<BR>	 1. A balance, a pair of scales.<BR>	 2. the sign Libra.<BR>	 3.<BR>Ordeal by the balance.<BR>	 f. (-टी)<BR>	 1. Old cloth or raiment.<BR>	 2. A piece<BR>of cloth worn over the privities.<BR> E. धण् to sound, and ट substi-<BR>tuted for ण, affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=363-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धटक|धटकः
धटक m. (-कः) A weight of forty-two Rattis.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=363-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धटिनी
धटिनी f. (-नी) A cotton tie or string, fastened round the loins<BR> E. धट<BR>a cloth, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=363-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धटीदान|धटीदानं
धटीदान n. (-नं) Giving old cloth to a woman after impregnation. E.<BR>धटी, and दान giving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=363-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धण
धण r. 1st cl. (धणति-ते) To sound. भ्वा० प० अक० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=363-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धत्तूर|धत्तूरः
धत्तूर m. (-रः) The thorn apple: see धुस्तर.<BR> E. धेट to drink, उरच् affix,<BR>or more correctly, धययि धातून् धा-ऊर-पृ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=363-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धन|धनं
धन r. 1st cl. (धनति) To sound. r. 3rd cl. (दधन्ति) To bear or produce,<BR>(grain, &c.): restricted to the Vedas. भ्वा० प० अक० सेट् । जुहो० ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=363-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धन|धनं
धन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. property of any description, thing, substance, wealth.<BR>2. Wealth in cattle, property in herds.<BR>	 3. A term of endearment<BR>4. (In Algebra,) The affirmative quantity or plus.<BR> E. धन to pro-<BR>duce, (a crop,) affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=363-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनकेलि|धनकेलिः
धनकेलि m. (-लिः) KUVERA, the Hindū Plutus; also धनकेलिक.<BR> E. धन<BR>wealth, and केलि who sports.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=363-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनगर्व्वित|धनगर्वित
धनगर्व्वित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) purse-proud.<BR> E. धन, and गर्व्वित arrogant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=363-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनच्छु
धनच्छु m. (-च्छुः) The Numidian crane.<BR> E. धन the wealth, (of fields,)<BR>and च्छो to destroy, affix टु Note; as a synonym of करेटुखगे this<BR>word would seem to mean the bird stated: the name itself is<BR>more analogous to the Dhanesa of the dialects or the Indian<BR>Buceros.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=363-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनजात
धनजात mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Springing from wealth.<BR> E. धन, and जात born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=363-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनञ्जय|धनंजय|धनंजयः|धनञ्जयः
धनञ्जय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. The deity of fire.<BR>	 2. A name of ARJUNA.<BR>	 3. One of<BR>the Nāgas or infernal serpents.<BR>	 4. One of the five vital airs, that<BR>which is supposed to fatten.<BR>	 5. A tree, (Pentaptera arjuna.)<BR> E. धन<BR>wealth, जि to conquer or possess, affix खच् मुम् च ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=363-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनतृष्णा
धनतृष्णा f. (-ष्णा) Covetousness.<BR> E. धन, and तृणा thirst.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=363-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनद|धनदः
धनद mfn. (-दः-दा-दं) Beneficent, liberal, who gives away pro-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=364-a" target="_blank">Page364-a+ 60</a>]<BR>perty, &c.<BR>	 m. (-दः) A name of KUVERA.<BR> E. धन wealth, देङ् to<BR>drink, or दा to give, affix क, or धनं दयते दे पालने ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=363-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनदण्ड|धनदंड|धनदण्डः
धनदण्ड m. (-ण्डः) Fine, amercement.<BR> E. धन and दण्ड punishment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=364-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनदर्प
धनदर्प m. (-र्पः) Pride of wealth.<BR> E. धन and दर्प pride.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=364-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनदानुज|धनदानुजः
धनदानुज m. (-जः) RĀVANA.<BR> E. धनद KUVERA अनुज younger brother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=364-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनदायिन्
धनदायिन् mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि) Liberal, munificent.<BR>	 m. (-यी)<BR>	 1. The deity of<BR>fire.<BR>	 2. A benefactor, a donor.<BR> E. धन wealth, दा to give, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=364-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनन्ददा|धनंददा
धनन्ददा f. (-दा) One of the Śaktis, or female personifications of Divine<BR>power peculiar to the Bauddhas<BR> E. धन wealth, दद to give, affix खश्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=364-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनपति|धनपतिः
धनपति m. (-तिः) The god of riches, KUVERA.<BR> E. घन wealth, and पति<BR>master or lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=364-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनपिचाशिका
धनपिचाशिका f. (-का) Avarice, thirst of wealth.<BR> E. धन wealth, पिचाशि a<BR>she-demon, affix कन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=364-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनपिशाची
धनपिशाची f. (-धी) Extreme desire of riches, avarice. E. See the<BR>preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=364-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनप्रिय
धनप्रिय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Fond of wealth.<BR>	 f. (-या) A vegetable, (Ardisia<BR>solanacea.)<BR> E. धन, and प्रिय dear to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=364-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनमद|धनमदः
धनमद mfn. (-दः-दा-दं) Proud, inflated with the pride of wealth,<BR> E. धन<BR>wealth, मद to be intoxicated, affix अप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=364-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनमूल
धनमूल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Proceeding from wealth.<BR>	 n. (-लं) Principal, capital<BR>E. धन, and मूल root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=364-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनलुब्ध
धनलुब्ध mfn. (-ब्धः-ब्धा-ब्धं) Miserly, avaricious, greedy of wealth, merce-<BR>nary.<BR> E. धन, and लुब्ध desirous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=364-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनलोभ|धनलोभः
धनलोभ m. (-भः) Desire of wealth, greediness, avarice,<BR> E. धन, and<BR>लोभ desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=364-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनवत्|धनवन्त्
धनवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Wealthy, opulent.<BR>	 f. (-वती) The constellation<BR>Dhaniṣṭhā.<BR> E. धन wealth, and मतुप् possessive aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=364-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनव्यय|धनव्ययः
धनव्यय m. (-यः) Expenditure, extravagance.<BR> E. धन and व्यय expense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=364-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनसम्पत्ति|धनसंपत्ति
धनसम्पत्ति f. (-त्तिः) Accumulation of wealth.<BR> E. धन, and सम्पत्ति acquire-<BR>ment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=364-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनसू
धनसू m. (-सूः) The fork-tailed shrike.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=364-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनस्थक
धनस्थक m. (-कः) A plant: see गोक्षुर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=364-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनहर|धनहरः
धनहर mfn. (-रः-रा-री-रं)<BR>	 1. Inheriting, an heir.<BR>	 2. Stealing, a thief.<BR>	 3.<BR>Taking wealth, &c.<BR>	 f. (-री) A sort of perfume, commonly called<BR>Chor.<BR> E. धन wealth, हृ to steal, affix अप् or ट.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=364-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनहारिन्
धनहारिन् mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि) A thief, a pilferer. E. See the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=364-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनहारिन्
धनहारिन् mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>	 1. Inheriting, an heir.<BR>	 2. A thief.<BR> E. धन and<BR>हारिन् who takes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=364-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनहीन
धनहीन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Poor, reduced to poverty.<BR> E. धन and हीन<BR>deprived of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=364-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनागम
धनागम m. (-मः) Accession of wealth.<BR> E. धन, and आगम coming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=364-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनादान
धनादान n. (-नं) Acceptance of money.<BR> E. धन and आदान taking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=364-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनाधिकारिन्
धनाधिकारिन् mf. (-री-रिणी-रि) An heir, an heiress.<BR>	 m. (-रीः) A treasurer,<BR>a collector.<BR> E. धन and अधिकारिन् having a right to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=364-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनाधिकृत
धनाधिकृत m. (-तः) A treasurer.<BR> E. धन and अधिकृत placed over.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=364-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनाधिप|धनाधिपः
धनाधिप m. (-पः)<BR>	 1. A name of KUVERA.<BR>	 2. A treasurer.<BR> E. धन riches<BR>and अधिप lord; also similar compounds, धनाधिपति, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=364-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनाध्यक्ष|धनाध्यक्षः
धनाध्यक्ष m. (-क्षः)<BR>	 1. A name of KUYERA.<BR>	 2. A treasurer.<BR> E. धन wealth,<BR>अध्यक्ष superintendent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=364-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनापहार|धनापहारः
धनापहार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Fine, amercement.<BR>	 2. Plunder.<BR> E. धन, and अपहार<BR>taking away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=364-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनार्च्चित|धनार्चित
धनार्च्चित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Wealthy, opulent.<BR> E. धन, and अर्च्चित respected by.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=364-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनार्ज्जन|धनार्जन
धनार्ज्जन n. (-नं) Acquisition of property.<BR> E. धन and अर्ज्जन acquiring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=364-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनार्थिन्
धनार्थिन् mfn. (-र्थी-र्थिनी-र्थि) Seeking for wealth, covetous, miserly.<BR> E. धन,<BR>and अर्थिन् who wants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=364-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनाशा
धनाशा f. (-शा) Thirst of wealth, longing after riches.<BR> E. धन wealth आशा<BR>hope, wish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=364-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनाश्री
धनाश्री f. (-श्री) One of the Rāginis.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=364-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनिक|धनिकः
धनिक mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>	 1. Pious, virtuous, excellent.<BR>	 2. Rich, opulent.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A wealthy man.<BR>	 2. A creditor.<BR>	 3. A husband.<BR>	 4.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=364-b" target="_blank">Page364-b+ 60</a>]<BR>Coriander.<BR>	 f. (-का)<BR>	 1. A virtuous or excellent woman.<BR>	 2. A wife.<BR>	 3.<BR>A young woman.<BR>	 4. A tree: see प्रियङ्गु.<BR> E. धन wealth, affix ठन्<BR>धनमादेयत्वेन अस्ति अस्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=364-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनिन्
धनिन् mfn. (-नी-निनी-नि) Wealthy, opulent.<BR>	 m. (-नी)<BR>	 1. A rich man.<BR>	 2.<BR>A creditor,<BR> E. धन wealth, इनि aff. धनमस्ति अस्य धन + इनि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=364-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनिष्ठा
धनिष्ठा f. (-ष्ठा) The twenty-fourth Nakshatra or lunar mansion, it com-<BR>prises four stars, and is figured by a drum or tabor.<BR> E. धन to<BR>produce, (as corn,) affix अच् and मतुप् added, धनवत् again, इष्ठन्<BR>added, and मतुप् rejected, fem. affix टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=364-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनीका
धनीका f. (-का) A young woman.<BR> E. धन wealth, ठक् affix, and the vowel<BR>made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=364-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनीयक|धनीयकं
धनीयक n. (-कं) Coriander-seed.<BR> E. धन to be produced, (as corn,) affix<BR>छ and कन् added see धन्याक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=364-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनु|धनुः
धनु m. (-नुः)<BR>	 1. A bow.<BR>	 2. The sign Sagittarius.<BR>	 3. A tree: see पियाल.<BR>	 4.<BR>A measure of four cubits.<BR> E. धन here meaning to cast as an arrow,<BR>Unādi affix उन् also धनुस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=364-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनुःकाण्ड|धनुःकांड
धनुःकाण्ड n. (-ण्डं) A bow and arrow.<BR> E. धनुस्, and काण्ड an arrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=364-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनुःखण्ड|धनुःखंड
धनुःखण्ड n. (-ण्डं) A bow, the stick or horns of the bow. धनुस् and खण्ड<BR>a part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=364-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनुःपट|धनुःपटः
धनुःपट m. (-टः) The Piyasal tree, (Buchanania latifolia, Rox.)<BR> E. धनुस् a<BR>bow, and पट width; bending like a bow. धनुष इव पटो विस्तारो दले यस्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=364-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनुःशाखा
धनुःशाखा f. (-खा) A plant, from the leaves of which a tough thread is<BR>extracted, of which bow strings were formerly made: see मूर्व्वा,<BR>(Sanseviera zeylanica, Rox. but called by Sir WM. JONES, Aletris<BR>hyacinthoides.)<BR> E. धनुस् a bow, शाखा a branch. धनुरवयव इव शाखा<BR>यस्याः । पियालतरौ, मूर्ब्बायाम् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=364-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनुःश्रेणी
धनुःश्रेणी f. (-णी) A plant: see the last.<BR> E. धनुस् a bow, and श्रेणी a line.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=364-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनुर्गुण|धनुर्गुणः
धनुर्गुण mf. (-णः-णा) A bow string.<BR>	 f. (-णा) A plant, from which bow<BR>strings are made: see the two last.<BR> E. धनुस् a bow, and गुण a string.<BR>धनुषो गुणो यस्याः सकाशात् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=364-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनुर्द्रुम|धनुर्द्रुमः
धनुर्द्रुम m. (-मः) A bamboo.<BR> E. धनुस् and द्रुम a tree. धनुषः साधनं द्रुमः ।<BR>वंशवृक्षे । ततएव धनुषो जननात् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=364-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनुर्धर|धनुर्धरः
धनुर्धर m. (-रः) An archer, a bowyer, one armed with a bow.<BR> E. धनुस् a<BR>bow, and धर who possesses. धनुर्धारयति धृ-अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=364-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनुर्धारिन्
धनुर्धारिन् m. (-री) An archer, a bowyer.<BR> E. धनुस् and धारिन् who has.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=364-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनुर्भृत्
धनुर्भृत् m. (-त्) An archer.<BR> E. धनुस् a bow, and भृत् who possesses: see<BR>the last. धनुर्भिभत्ति भृ कर्त्तरि क्विप् तुक् ६ तत् पु० स० ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=364-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनुर्मध्य|धनुर्मध्यं|धनुर्म्मध्य
धनुर्मध्य n. (-ध्यं) The middle part of a bow.<BR> E. धनुस् a bow, मध्य the<BR>centre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=364-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनुर्मार्ग|धनुर्मार्गः|धनुर्म्मार्ग
धनुर्मार्ग n. (-र्गं) A curve line.<BR> E. धनुस् an arc, मार्ग a road.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=364-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनुर्माला|धनुर्म्माला
धनुर्माला f. (-ला) A plant, from the leaves of which bow strings were<BR>made: see मूर्व्वा.<BR> E. धनुस् a bow, and माला a garland.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=364-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनुर्य्यास|धनुर्यास|धनुर्य्यासः
धनुर्य्यास m. (-सः) A plant, (Hedysarum alhagi.)<BR> E. धनुस् for धन्वन् a<BR>dry soil, and यास here said to mean effort; also धन्वयास धनुरिव<BR>यासः । दुरालभायाम् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=364-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनुर्लता
धनुर्लता f. (-ता) The moon plant. धनुरवयवयोग्या लता । सोमवल्ल्याम् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=364-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनुर्वृक्ष|धनुर्वृक्षः
धनुर्वृक्ष m. (-क्षः)<BR>	 1. A plant; also called Dhāminiya.<BR>	 2. A bamboo.<BR>	 3.<BR>A measure of four cubits.<BR>	 4. An are, a portion of the circum-<BR>ference of a circle.<BR> E. धनुस् bow, and वृक्ष a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=364-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनुष्कर|धनुष्करः
धनुष्कर m. (-रः) A bowyer, an archer.<BR> E. धनुस् a bow, and कर who<BR>makes or practises.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=364-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनुष्पट|धनुष्पटः
धनुष्पट m. (-टः) A tree: see धनुःपट.<BR> E. धनुस् a bow, पट breadth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=364-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनुष्पाणि
धनुष्पाणि mfn. (-णिः-णिः-णि) Armed with a bow.<BR>	 m. (-णिः) An archer.<BR>E. धनुस्, and पाणि hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=364-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनुष्मत्|धनुष्मन्त्
धनुष्मत् m. (-ष्मान्) An archer, a bowyer.<BR> E. धनुस् a bow, मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=364-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनुस्
धनुस् mfn. (-नुः-नुः-नु) Armed with a bow.<BR>	 mn. (-नुः-नु)<BR>	 1. A. bow.<BR>	 2.<BR>Sagittarius, the sign.<BR>	 m. (-नुः) The piyal tree, (Buchanania<BR>latifolia, Rox.)<BR> E. धन to produce, (as grain,) to throw forth,<BR>(darts, &c.) Unādi affix उसि; also with उ affix धनु, and with ऊ<BR>affix, धनू.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=364-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनू
धनू m. (-नूः) A bow: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=365-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनेयक|धनेयकं
धनेयक n. (-कं) Coriander: see धन्याक.<BR> E. धन grain, ढक् affix, and कन्<BR>added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=365-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनेश|धनेशः
धनेश m. (-शः) KUVERA.<BR> E. धन, and ईश lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=365-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनेश्वर|धनेश्वरः
धनेश्वर m. (-रः) KUVERA, the Hindū PLUTUS.<BR> E. धन wealth, ईश्वर lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=365-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनैषिन्
धनैषिन् mfn. (-षी-षिणी-षि) Wishing or claiming property.<BR>	 m. (-षी) A<BR>creditor.<BR> E. धन, and ऐषिन् who wishes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=365-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनोपचय
धनोपचय m. (-यः) Accumulation of wealth.<BR> E. धन, and उपचय assembling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=365-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धन्य|धन्यः
धन्य mfn. (-न्य-न्या-न्यं)<BR>	 1. Fortunate, well fated, lucky.<BR>	 2. Good, virtuous.<BR>m. (-न्यः)<BR>	 1. An infidel, an atheist.<BR>	 2. A virtuous or fortunate man.<BR>f. (-न्या)<BR>	 1. Emblic myrobalan.<BR>	 2. A nurse.<BR>	 3. Coriander.<BR>	 n. (-न्यं)<BR>Wealth.<BR> E. धन to produce, (grain, &c.) or धन wealth, and यत् affix<BR>of fitness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=365-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धन्यत्व
धन्यत्व n. (-त्वं) Luck, good fortune.<BR> E. धन्य, and त्व affix; also with तल्<BR>affix धन्यता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=365-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धन्याक|धन्याकं
धन्याक n. (-कं) A plant, bearing a small pungent seed used by the<BR>Hindus as a condiment, (Coriandrum sativum.)<BR> E. धन to produce,<BR>(as grain,) deriv. irr. धन्यते भक्ष्यार्थिभिः । धनिया इति ख्याते पदार्थे ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=365-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धन्व|धन्वं|धन्वः
धन्व n. (-न्वं) A bow: see धन्वन्. धन्व गतौ सौ० भ्वा० प० सक० सेट् । r. 1st cl.<BR>(धन्वति) To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=365-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धन्वदुर्ग|धन्वदुर्गं
धन्वदुर्ग n. (-र्गं) A desert.<BR> E. धन्व the same, and दुर्ग strong-hold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=365-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धन्वन्
धन्वन् mn. (-न्वा-न्वं) A bow.<BR>	 m. (-न्वा) A country scantily supplied with<BR>water, a desert, a waste.<BR>	 n. (-न्वं) A firm spot, land, ground.<BR> E. धन्वि<BR>Sautra root, to go or move, (by or on which,) and कनिन् Unādi<BR>affix; also with अच् affix धन्व.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=365-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धन्वन्
धन्वन् m. (-न्वः) A medicinal plant, commonly called Dhāminiya or<BR>Dhamin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=365-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धन्वन्तरि|धन्वंतरि|धन्वंतरिः|धन्वन्तरिः
धन्वन्तरि m. (-रिः)<BR>	 1. The physician of the gods, who was produced at<BR>the churning of the ocean.<BR>	 2. A celebrated physician; also<BR>काशिराज, being the same as the preceding in another existence:<BR>he appears to have been the founder of the Hindu medical school.<BR>3. The sun.<BR>	 4. A name of ŚIVA.<BR>	 5. One of the nine gems of the<BR>court of VIKRAMĀDITYA. धनोः तन्निमित्त शल्यस्य अन्तं पारं ऋच्छति ऋ गतौइन्<BR>किच्च । समुद्रोत्थिते देववैद्यभेदे ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=365-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धन्वन्तरिग्रस्ता
धन्वन्तरिग्रस्ता f. (-स्ता) A medicinal plant: see कटुकी.<BR> E. धन्वन्तरि, and ग्रस्त<BR>eaten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=365-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धन्वयवास|धन्वयवासः
धन्वयवास m. (-सः) A plant, (Hedysarum alhaji.)<BR> E. धन्व dry soil, यु to<BR>unite, आसच् affix; also with कन् added धन्वयवासक. मरुभवे यवास भेदे,<BR>दुरालभाभेदे ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=365-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धन्वयास|धन्वयासः
धन्वयास m. (-सः) A plant: see the last, alse simply यास, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=365-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धन्विन्
धन्विन् m. (-न्वी)<BR>	 1. An archer, a bow-man.<BR>	 2. A name of ARJUNA.<BR>	 3. A<BR>tree, (Pentaptera arjuna.)<BR>	 4. A wag, a wit, a sharp or shrewd<BR>man.<BR> E. धन्व a bow, इनि aff. धन्वं चापोऽस्ति अस्य धम ध्माने सौ० पर० सक०<BR>सेट् । धमति । To blow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=365-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धम|धमः
धम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं) One who blows a fire or a trumpet.<BR>	 m. (-मः)<BR>	 1. A<BR>name of the moon.<BR>	 2. KṚṢṆA.<BR>	 3. A name of Yama.<BR>	 4. BRAMHĀ,<BR>or the Supreme Spirit,<BR> E. ध्मा to blow, affix अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=365-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धमक|धमकः
धमक m. (-कः) A blacksmith.<BR> E. ध्मा to blow, (the forge.) क्वुन् Unādi aff.<BR>धमादेशश्च ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=365-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धमधमा
धमधमा ind. Blowing reiteratedly, or the sort of sound made by blow-<BR>ing with a bellows or a trumpet.<BR> E. धम + प्रकारे द्वित्वम् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=365-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धमन|धमनः
धमन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>	 1. One who blows a bellows, a trumpet, &c.<BR>	 2.<BR>Cruel.<BR>	 m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. A reed, (Arundo tibialis or karka.)<BR>	 2. Blowing,<BR>(a wind instrument.)<BR>	 f. (-निः or -नी)<BR>	 1. Any tubular vessel of the<BR>body, as a vein, a nerve, &c.<BR>	 2. The neck.<BR>	 3. Turmeric.<BR>	 4. A<BR>sort of perfume; also हट्टविलासिनी.<BR> E. धम from ध्मा to blow, &c. affix<BR>युच् fem. affix इन् or ङीष्; or ध्मा as before, Unādi affix अनि, and<BR>ङीप् optionally added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=365-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धम्मल|धम्मलः
धम्मल m. (-लः) The breast ornamented with gold or jewels: see धम्मिल्ल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=365-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धम्मिल्ल|धम्मिल्लः
धम्मिल्ल m. (-ल्लः) Braided and ornamented hair, tied round the head,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=365-b" target="_blank">Page365-b+ 60</a>]<BR>and intermixed with flowers, pearls, &c.<BR> E. धम a Sautra root, to<BR>breathe, affix विच्, मिल to meet, लच् or क affix, and the two<BR>conjoined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=365-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धया
धया mfn. (-यः-या-यी-यं) Who or what drinks.<BR>	 f. (-या) A little girl, female<BR>infant.<BR> E. धे to drink, affix श ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=365-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर|धरः
धर mfn. (-रः-रा-री-रं) Who or what has or holds.<BR>	 m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A mountain.<BR>2. A flock of cotton.<BR>	 3. The tortoise Avatāra.<BR>	 4. One of the demi-<BR>gods called VASUS.<BR>	 f. (-रा)<BR>	 1. The earth.<BR>	 2. The uterus or womb.<BR>3. Marrow.<BR>	 4. A vessel of the body.<BR>	 5. A golden globe or heap of<BR>valuables, representing the earth, and given to Brāhmans.<BR> E. धृञ्<BR>to have or hold, to contain or support. &c. affix अच्, or ट fem.<BR>affix टाप् or ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=365-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धरण|धरणं|धरणः
धरण mn. (-णः-णं)<BR>	 1. Holding, possessing, having.<BR>	 2. A sort of measure,<BR>a weight of ten Palās.<BR>	 3. A weight of silver, sixteen Māshās.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-णः)<BR>	 1. The Himālayā mountain considered as king of mountains.<BR>2. The sun.<BR>	 3. A world.<BR>	 4. A breast, a female breast.<BR>	 5. Rice.<BR>	 6. A<BR>ridge of land answering the purpose of a bridge, the edge of a<BR>river, the skirt of a mountain, a bridge.<BR>	 f. (-णी)<BR>	 1. The earth.<BR>	 2.<BR>The silk-cotton tree.<BR>	 3. A vessel of the body.<BR>	 4. An esculent root.<BR>E. धृ to hold, to uphold or support, affix युच्, भावे ल्युट्, fem, affix<BR>ङीप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=365-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धरणि|धरणिः
धरणि f. (-णिः) The earth.<BR> E. धृ to be contained, (animals, &c.) Unādi<BR>affix अणि; also धरणी as above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=365-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धरणिधर|धरणिधरः
धरणिधर m. (-रः) A name of VIṢṆU.<BR> E. धरणि the earth and धर who<BR>sustains; also धरणीधर, धरणीं धरति धृ-अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=365-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धरणिस्थ
धरणिस्थ mfn. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थं) Being or staying on earth.<BR> E. धरणि, and स्थ<BR>what stays or is.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=365-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धरणीकन्द|धरणीकन्दः
धरणीकन्द m. (-न्दः) An esculent root or bulb.<BR> E. धरणी the earth, कन्द<BR>a root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=365-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धरणीकीलक|धरणीकीलकः
धरणीकीलक m. (-कः) A mountain.<BR> E. धरणी the earth, कीलक a pin or<BR>bolt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=365-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धरणीधर|धरणीधरः
धरणीधर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. VIṢṆU.<BR>	 2. A mountain.<BR>	 3. A tortoise see धरणिधर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=365-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धरणीपूर|धरणीपूरः
धरणीपूर m. (-रः) The ocean.<BR> E. धरणी the earth, पूर to surround com-<BR>pletely, affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=365-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धरणीप्लव|धरणीप्लवः
धरणीप्लव m. (-वः) The ocean.<BR> E. धरणी the earth, and प्लव what swims; in<BR>which the earth floats. धरण्याः प्लवः यस्मात् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=365-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धरणीश्वर|धरणीश्वरः
धरणीश्वर m. (-रः) A name of ŚIVA.<BR> E. धरणी, and ईश्वर lord; lord of the<BR>world. शिवे, भूमिपतौ, विष्णौ च ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=365-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धरणीसुता
धरणीसुता f. (-ता) A name of SĪTĀ, the wife of RĀMA.<BR> E. धरणी the<BR>earth, and सुता daughter; the earth-born; being turned up from<BR>the soil by a plough, as JANAKA was ploughing a spot to prepare<BR>it for a sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=365-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धरसंस्थ
धरसंस्थ mfn. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थ) Like a mountain, as huge as, &c.<BR> E. धर, and<BR>संस्थ what is, or is like.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=365-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धराकदम्ब|धराकदम्बः
धराकदम्ब m. (-म्बः) The Kadamba tree, (Nauclea kadamba;) also<BR>धराकदम्बक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=365-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धरात्मज|धरात्मजः
धरात्मज m. (-जः) The planet Mars or its regent.<BR> E. धरा the earth, and<BR>आत्मज son, terræ-filius; also similar compounds, as धरासुत, धरापुत्त्र<BR>&c. मङ्गलग्रहे । तारकासुरे च ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=365-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धराधर|धराधरः
धराधर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A name of VIṢṆU.<BR>	 2. A mountain.<BR> E. धरा the<BR>earth, and धर who or what sustains. विष्णौ, पर्वते, अनन्ते च ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=365-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धराशय
धराशय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Sleeping on the ground.<BR> E. धरा, and शय who<BR>sleeps.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=365-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धरामर|धरामरः
धरामर m. (-रः) A Brāhman.<BR> E. धरा and अमर a deity. धरायाममर इव ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=365-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धरित्री
धरित्री f. (-त्री) The earth.<BR> E. धृ to contain, (beings.) इत्र Unādi affix,<BR>fem. affix ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=365-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धरिमन्
धरिमन् m. (-मा)<BR>	 1. Form, figure, semblance.<BR>	 2. A balance, a pair of<BR>scales.<BR> E. धृ to have or hold, Unādi affix इमनिच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=365-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धरिममेय
धरिममेय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Measurable by weight.<BR> E. धरिम, and मेय to be<BR>measured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=365-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धरुण|धरुणः
धरुण m. (-णः)<BR>	 1. A name of BRAMHĀ.<BR>	 2. Heaven, paradise.<BR>	 3. Water.<BR>4. Opinion, conception.<BR> E. धृ to hold or uphold, affix उनन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=366-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्त्तव्य|धर्तव्य|धर्त्तव्यं
धर्त्तव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>	 1. To be uphold or supported.<BR>	 2. To be had or<BR>possessed.<BR>	 3. To be placed or fixed.<BR>	 4. To be fallen or alighted by.<BR>E. धृ to hold, तव्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=366-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्त्तृ|धर्तृ
धर्त्तृ mfn. (-त्ता-र्त्त्री-र्त्तृ) Who or what has or holds.<BR> E. धृ to have, तृन्<BR>aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=366-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्त्र|धर्त्रं
धर्त्र n. (-र्त्रं)<BR>	 1. A house.<BR>	 2. Sacrifice.<BR>	 3. Virtue, moral merit.<BR> E. धृ to<BR>contain, Unādi affix त्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=366-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्म्म|धर्म|धर्मः|धर्म्मः
धर्म्म mn. (-र्म्मः-र्म्मं)<BR>	 1. Virtue, moral and religious merit, according to<BR>the law and the Vedas.<BR>	 2. Usage, practice, the customary<BR>observances of caste, sect, &c.<BR>	 3. Duty, especially that enjoined<BR>by the Vedas.<BR>	 4. Fitness, propriety.<BR>	 5. Nature, character, proper<BR>or natural state or disposition, 6. Innocence, innoxiousness.<BR>	 7.<BR>Resemblance.<BR>	 8. Any sacrifice.<BR>	 9. An Upanishad or theological<BR>portion of a Veda.<BR>	 10. Any peculiar or prescribed practice or<BR>duty; thus, giving alms, &c. is the dharma of a householder;<BR>administering justice, the dharma of a king; piety, that of a<BR>Brāhman; courage, that of a Kṣatriya, &c.<BR>	 11. Kind and virtuous<BR>speech or discourse.<BR>	 12. Law.<BR>	 m. (-र्म्मः)<BR>	 1. A name of YAMA, ruler<BR>of the lower regions, and judge of the dead.<BR>	 2. A drinker of the<BR>juice of the acid asclepias, at certain sacrifices.<BR>	 3. Virtue personified,<BR>born from the right breast of BRAMHĀ.<BR>	 4. A bow.<BR>	 5. Associating with<BR>the virtuous.<BR>	 6. The fifteenth of the twenty-four jaina pontiffs of<BR>the present age.<BR>	 7. A pious or virtuous man.<BR>	 8. The bull of ŚIVA,<BR>a personification or type or virtue.<BR> E. धृ to maintain or support,<BR>&c. Unādi affix मन्, what supports all men. ध्रियते लोकोऽनेन, धरति<BR>लोकं वा ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=366-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्म्मकर्म्मन्|धर्मकर्मन्
धर्म्मकर्म्मन् n. (-र्म्म) Acting according to some or any indispensable<BR>act of piety or duty.<BR> E. धर्म्म, and कर्म्मन् act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=366-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्म्मकाय|धर्मकाय|धर्मकायः|धर्म्मकायः
धर्म्मकाय m. (-यः) A jina or jaina deified saint.<BR> E. धर्म्म virtue, and काय<BR>body; virtue personified. धर्मार्थं कायोऽस्य, बुद्धे ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=366-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्म्मकार्य्य|धर्मकार्य
धर्म्मकार्य्य n. (-र्य्यं)<BR>	 1. Any indispensable act of religion, &c.<BR>	 2. Religious<BR>or virtuous conduct.<BR> E. धर्म्म piety, and कार्य्य act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=366-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्म्मकील|धर्मकील|धर्मकीलः|धर्म्मकीलः
धर्म्मकील m. (-लः) An edict, a royal order, decree, or grant.<BR> E. धर्म्म<BR>virtue, कील proper stay; also with कन् added धर्म्मकीलक m. (-कः)<BR>धर्मस्य कील इव । राजशासने ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=366-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्म्मकृत्य|धर्मकृत्य
धर्म्मकृत्य n. (-त्यं) Any moral or religious observance.<BR> E. धर्म्म and कृत्य to<BR>be done.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=366-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्म्मकेतु|धर्मकेतु|धर्मकेतुः|धर्म्मकेतुः
धर्म्मकेतु m. (-तुः) A jaina deified saint.<BR> E. धर्म्म virtue, केतु an emblem or<BR>banner. धर्मः अहिंसारूपकर्म केतुः यस्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=366-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्म्मकोष|धर्मकोष|धर्मकोषः
धर्म्मकोष m. (-षः) Store or treasure of virtue.<BR> E. धर्म्म, and कोष treasury.<BR>धर्मः कोष इव धर्मस्य कोषः समूहो वा ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=366-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्म्मक्रिया|धर्मक्रिया
धर्म्मक्रिया f. (-या)<BR>	 1. Righteous conduct, acting according to law.<BR>	 2. any<BR>religious act.<BR> E. धर्म्म, and क्रिया act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=366-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्म्मक्षेत्र|धर्मक्षेत्र|धर्मक्षेत्रः|धर्म्मक्षेत्रं
धर्म्मक्षेत्र n. (-त्रं) A plain in the north west of India near Delhi, the<BR>scene of the great battle between the Kurus and Paṇḍus.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-त्रः) A man of piety and virtue.<BR> E. धर्म्म. virtue, holiness, and क्षेत्र<BR>a field, literally or figuratively.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=366-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्म्मग्रहण
धर्म्मग्रहण n. (-णं) Observance of moral or religious institutes accepting<BR>or following the law.<BR> E. धर्म्म, and ग्रहण taking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=366-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्म्मघ्न|धर्मघ्न
धर्म्मघ्न mfn. (-घ्नः-घ्नी-घ्नं) immoral, unlawful, contrary to law or duty. E.<BR>धर्म्म, and घ्न what destroys.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=366-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्म्मचक्र|धर्मचक्र|धर्मचक्रः|धर्म्मचक्रः
धर्म्मचक्र m. (-क्रः) A Jaina deified saint.<BR> E. धर्म्म, and चक्र a wheel, &c. or<BR>धर्मसमूहे ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=366-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्म्मचक्रभृत्|धर्मचक्रभृत्
धर्म्मचक्रभृत् m. (-त्) A Jaina deified saint.<BR> E. धर्म्म virtue, चक्र a circle, and<BR>भृत् possessing. धर्मचक्रं विभर्त्ति भृ-क्विप तुक् । धर्म्मसमूहधारके त्रि० ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=366-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्म्मचारिन्|धर्मचारिन्
धर्म्मचारिन् mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि) Virtuous, moral, dutiful f. (-रिणी) A virtuous<BR>woman, an honest wife.<BR> E. धर्म्म duty and चर to follow, affixes णिनि<BR>and ङीष्. धर्म्मं तत्साधनकर्मे चरति ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=366-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्म्मचिन्तन|धर्मचिन्तन|धर्मचिंतन|धर्म्मचिन्तनं
धर्म्मचिन्तन n. (-नं) Virtuous reflection.<BR> E. धर्म्म, and चिन्ता reflection. चिन्ति<BR>भावे ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=366-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्म्मचिन्ता|धर्मचिन्ता|धर्मचिंता
धर्म्मचिन्ता f. (-न्ता) Virtuous reflection.<BR> E. धर्म्म, and चिन्ता reflection: see<BR>the last. चिन्ति भावे अ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=366-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्म्मजीवन|धर्मजीवन|धर्मजीवनः
धर्म्मजीवन m. (-नः) Brahman who lives according to rule: one who<BR>practises the outward acts of the law.<BR> E. धर्म्म, and जीवन living.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=366-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्म्मज्ञ|धर्मज्ञ|धर्म्मज्ञः
धर्म्मज्ञ mfn. (-ज्ञः-ज्ञा-ज्ञं) Knowing one's duty, conversant with virtue.<BR>E. धर्म्म, and ज्ञ who knows. धर्मं जानाति ज्ञा-क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=366-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्म्मज्ञान|धर्मज्ञान
धर्म्मज्ञान n. (-नं) Knowledge of moral, legal, and religious duty.<BR> E. धर्म्म<BR>and ज्ञान knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=366-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्म्मण|धर्मण|धर्म्मणः
धर्म्मण m. (-णः)<BR>	 1. A sort of tree, commonly Dhāminiya.<BR>	 2. A kind of<BR>large snake, not poisonous, commonly Dhamna. धर्माय नम्यते<BR>नम-वा-कर्मणि-ड । धामनि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=366-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्म्मतस्|धर्मतस्
धर्म्मतस् ind. Rightly, justly, righteously.<BR> E. धर्म्म and तसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=366-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्म्मत्व|धर्मत्व|धर्मत्वं|धर्म्मत्वं
धर्म्मत्व n. (-त्वं)<BR>	 1. Morality, piety.<BR>	 2. Inherent nature, peculiar property,<BR>&c.<BR> E. धर्म्म, and त्व aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=366-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्म्मद्रवी|धर्मद्रवी
धर्म्मद्रवी f. (-वी) The Ganges.<BR> E. धर्म्म virtue, द्रु to shed. affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=366-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्म्मद्रोहिन
धर्म्मद्रोहिन mfn. (-ही-हिणी-हि) Wicked.<BR>	 m. (-ही) A Rākshasa.<BR> E. धर्म्म, and<BR>द्रोहिन् rebellious. धर्माय परस्य धर्माचरणाय द्रुह्यति । द्रुह णिनि । ४ तं ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=366-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्म्मधातु|धर्मधातु|धर्मधातुः|धर्म्मधातुः
धर्म्मधातु m. (-तुः) A Jaina saint.<BR> E. धर्म virtue, धातु essence, root. धर्मं<BR>दधाति । धा-तुन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=366-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्म्मध्वजिन्|धर्मध्वजिन्
धर्म्मध्वजिन् m. (-जी) A religious hypocrite or imposter, one who makes a<BR>livelihood by assumed devotion.<BR> E. धर्म्म piety, ध्वज an emblem, इनि<BR>affix; having every outward mark of piety, matted hair, ragged<BR>garments, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=366-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्म्मनिबन्ध|धर्मनिबन्ध
धर्म्मनिबन्ध m. (-न्धः) Piety, virtue.<BR> E. धर्म्म, and निबन्ध attachment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=366-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्म्मनिबन्धिन्|धर्मनिबन्धिन्
धर्म्मनिबन्धिन् mfn. (-न्धी-न्धिनी-न्धि) Pious, holy, engaged in or conductive<BR>to virtue.<BR> E. धर्म्म, निबन्ध connexion, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=366-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मनिष्पत्ति|धर्मनिष्पत्तिः|धर्म्मनिष्पत्ति
धर्मनिष्पत्ति f. (-त्तिः) Duty, moral or religious observance, discharge or<BR>fulfilment of duty.<BR> E. धर्म, and निष्पत्ति completion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=366-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मपत्तन|धर्म्मपत्तन|धर्म्मपत्तनं
धर्मपत्तन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Pepper.<BR>	 2. The name of a district or city.<BR> E. धर्म<BR>virtue, पत्तन a city; pepper grows there, whence is said to be its<BR>name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=366-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मपत्नी|धर्म्मपत्नी
धर्मपत्नी f. (-त्नी) A man's first wife and of the same class.<BR> E. धर्म, and<BR>पत्नी a wife. धर्मार्थं पत्नी । निर्दोषायाम् पत्न्याम् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=366-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मपत्र|धर्म्मपत्र|धर्म्मपत्रं
धर्मपत्र (-त्रं) Glomerous fig tree, (Ficus glomerata)<BR> E. धर्म sacrifice,<BR>and पत्र leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=366-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मपर|धर्म्मपर
धर्मपर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Righteous, pious.<BR> E. धर्म, and पर addicted to.<BR>धर्मःपरो यस्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=366-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मपाठक|धर्मपाठकः|धर्म्मपाठक
धर्मपाठक m. (-कः) A teacher of law.<BR> E. धर्म, and पाठक who teaches.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=366-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मपुत्त्र
धर्मपुत्त्र m. (-त्त्रः)<BR>	 1. A name of the Pāndu prince, YUDHIṢṬHIRA.<BR>	 2. One<BR>so considered, as a son for piety or duty; also धर्मपुत्त्रक.<BR> E. धर्म<BR>a proper name, and पुत्त्र a son, the son of DHARMA or YAMA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=366-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मप्रधान|धर्म्मप्रधान
धर्मप्रधान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Eminent in piety.<BR> E. धर्म, and प्रधान chief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=366-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मप्रवक्तृ|धर्म्मप्रवक्तृ
धर्मप्रवक्तृ m. (-क्ता) A teacher or expounder of the law.<BR> E. धर्म, and<BR>प्रवक्तृ who explains. धर्मं सन्दिग्धार्थे अयं धर्म इति प्रवक्ति प्र + वच-तृच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=366-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मभागिनी|धर्म्मभागिनी
धर्मभागिनी f. (-नी) A virtuous and amiable wife.<BR> E. धर्म, and भागिनी<BR>who shares.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=366-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मभाणक|धर्मभाणकः|धर्म्मभाणक|धर्म्मभाणकः
धर्मभाणक m. (-कः) A lecturer, a public reader of the Mahābhārat<BR>and other sacred works which are read aloud, and explained to<BR>large assemblies of Hindūs at particular seasons.<BR> E. धर्म virtue,<BR>and भण् to utter, to speak, affix ण्वुल्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=366-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मभ्रातृ|धर्म्मभ्रातृ
धर्मभ्रातृ m. (-ता) A fellow religious student.<BR> E. धर्म, and भ्रातृ a brother.<BR>धर्मतः कृतो भ्राता ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=366-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मभिक्षुकः|धर्मभिक्षुक|धर्म्मभिक्षुक
धर्मभिक्षुकः m. (-कः) A mendicant Brāhman, one who is so, or has<BR>become so from meritorious motives.<BR> E. धर्म, and भिक्षुक a beggar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=366-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्ममय|धर्म्ममय
धर्ममय mfn. (-यः-यी-यं) Moral, righteous, made up or replete with<BR>virtue, &c.<BR> E. धर्म, and मयट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=366-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्ममूल|धर्म्ममूल|धर्म्ममूलं
धर्ममूल n. (-लं) The foundation of Hindu law and religion (the Vedas.)<BR>E. धर्म, and मूल root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=366-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मयु|धर्म्मयु|धर्म्मयुः
धर्मयु mfn. (-युः-युः-यु) Virtuous righteous.<BR> E. धर्म virtue, यु to go, affix<BR>क्विप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=367-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मयुज्|धर्म्मयुज्
धर्मयुज् mfn. (-युक्) Righteous, pious, just.<BR> E. धर्म virtue, युज् to join,<BR>affix क्विप् धर्मेण युज्यते युज-कर्मणि-क्विप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=367-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मराज|धर्मराजः|धर्म्मराज|धर्म्मराजः
धर्मराज m. (-जः)<BR>	 1. A Jain or deified saint, according to the Jaina sect.<BR>2. A name of YAMA, regent of the dead.<BR>	 3. A name of YUDHISH-<BR>THIRA.<BR>	 4. Also of ARJUNA.<BR>	 5. A king in general.<BR> E. धर्म virtue,<BR>Justice, and राज who shines, affix अच्; or राज from राजन् a king;<BR>lord of justice or धर्मेण राजते । राज-क्विप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=367-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मरोधिन्|धर्म्मरोधिन्
धर्मरोधिन् mfn. (-धी-धिनी-धि) Illegal, immoral.<BR> E. धर्म, and रोधिन्<BR>opposed to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=367-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मलक्षण|धर्म्मलक्षण
धर्मलक्षण n. (-णं) An essential ingredient in ethics or law, (as place,<BR>time, &c.)<BR> E. धर्म, and लक्षण mark. धर्मो लक्ष्यते ज्ञायते अनेन लक्ष-करणे<BR>ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=367-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मवत्|धर्मवन्त्|धर्म्मवत्
धर्मवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Virtuous, pious, upright, just.<BR> E. धर्म as<BR>above, मतुप् poss, aff. अस्त्यर्थे मतुप् । मस्य वः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=367-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मवासर|धर्मवासरः|धर्म्मवासर|धर्म्मवासरः
धर्मवासर m. (-रः) The day of full moon.<BR> E. धर्म virtue, and वासर a day;<BR>peculiar sacrifices being performed on this day. धर्मस्य तत्साधनस्य<BR>वासरः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=367-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मवाहन|धर्मवाहनः|धर्म्मवाहन|धर्म्मवाहनः
धर्मवाहन m. (-नः) A name of ŚIVA.<BR> E. धर्म the bull of this god, virtue<BR>typified, and वाहन a vehicle. धर्मं वाहयति प्रापयति नरान् । वाहि-ल्यू ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=367-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मविद्|धर्म्मविद्
धर्मविद् mfn. (-द् or -त्)<BR>	 1. Virtuous, pious, moral.<BR>	 2. Acquainted with<BR>the law.<BR> E. धर्म, and विद् who knows. धर्मं वेत्ति विद् क्विप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=367-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मविधि|धर्मविधिः|धर्म्मविधि
धर्मविधि f. (-धिः) Course of law, legal precepts or injunctions. E.<BR>धर्म, and विधि manner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=367-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मविप्लव|धर्मविप्लवः|धर्म्मविप्लव
धर्मविप्लव m. (-वः) Immorality, wickedness.<BR> E. धर्म, and विप्लव sub-<BR>mersion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=367-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मविवेचन|धर्म्मविवेचन
धर्मविवेचन n. (-नं) Judicial investigation.<BR> E. धर्म, and विवेचन delibera-<BR>tion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=367-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मशाला|धर्म्मशाला
धर्मशाला f. (-ला) A court of justice, a tribunal.<BR> E. धर्म justice, and<BR>शाला a hall. धर्मार्थं शाला । धर्मार्थमन्नादिदानाधिकरणशालायाम् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=367-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मशास्त्र|धर्म्मशास्त्र|धर्म्मशास्त्रं
धर्मशास्त्र n. (-स्त्रं)<BR>	 1. The body or code of Hindu law.<BR>	 2. Any work on<BR>the subject.<BR> E. धर्म virtue, and शास्त्र a treatise. शिष्यते अनेन शास<BR>करणे ष्ट्रन् । ६ त० स० ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=367-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मशील|धर्म्मशील|धर्म्मशीलः
धर्मशील mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Virtuous, just, pious.<BR> E. धर्म virtue, शील<BR>attached to. धर्मः धर्मसाधनं शीलमस्य, धर्मं शीलयति शील अण् वा ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=367-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मसंहिता|धर्म्मसंहिता
धर्मसंहिता f. (-ता) A code of laws, especially the work of some saint<BR>or divine person, as MANU, YĀJÑAVALKYA, &c.<BR> E. धर्म virtue,<BR>and सम् prefixed to धा, to have or possess, affix क्त, fem. affix टाप्;<BR>a compilation made for the purpose of teaching and maintaining<BR>virtue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=367-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मसङ्ग|धर्मसंग|धर्मसंगः|धर्म्मसङ्ग
धर्मसङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>	 1. Virtue.<BR>	 2. Hypocrisy.<BR> E. धर्म, and सङ्ग addiction to,<BR>real or seeming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=367-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मसन्तानसू|धर्म्मसन्तानसू
धर्मसन्तानसू mfn. (-सूः-सूः-सू) Virtuous, producing virtuous offspring or<BR>actions.<BR> E. धर्म, सन्तान progeny, सू who bears.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=367-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मसभा|धर्म्मसभा
धर्मसभा f. (-भा) A tribunal, a court of justice.<BR> E. धर्म justice, and सभा<BR>assembly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=367-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मसाधन|धर्म्मसाधन
धर्मसाधन n. (-नं) Any act or virtue essential to a system of duties.<BR>E. धर्म, and साधन instrument.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=367-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मसावर्णि|धर्म्मसावर्णि|धर्म्मसावर्णिः
धर्मसावर्णि m. (-र्णिः) The eleventh MANU.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=367-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मसुत|धर्म्मसुत|धर्म्मसुतः
धर्मसुत m. (-तः) A name of YUDHIṢṬHIRA.<BR> E. धर्म YAMA and सुत a<BR>son; also धर्मसूनु, धर्मात्मज, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=367-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मात्मन्|धर्म्मात्मन्
धर्मात्मन् m. (-त्मा) A saint, a pious or virtuous person<BR> E. धर्म virtue,<BR>आत्मन् self. धर्म आत्मा स्वभावोयस्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=367-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्माधर्मपरीक्षा|धर्म्माधर्म्मपरीक्षा
धर्माधर्मपरीक्षा f. (-क्षा) Ordeal by drawing lots or slips of black and<BR>white paper.<BR> E. धर्म, अधर्म iniquity, परीक्षा trial.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=367-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्माधिकरण|धर्माधिकरणः|धर्म्माधिकरण|धर्म्माधिकरणं|धर्म्माधिकरणः
धर्माधिकरण n. (-णं) A court of justice.<BR>	 m. (-णः) A judge.<BR> E. धर्म, and<BR>अधिकरण supervision. धर्मोऽधिक्रियते अत्र । अधि + कृ आधारे ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=367-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्माधिकरणिन्|धर्म्माधिकरणिन्
धर्माधिकरणिन् m. (-णी) A judge, a sovereign, an administrator of the<BR>law.<BR> E. धर्माधिकरण, and affix इनि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=367-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्माधिकार|धर्माधिकारः|धर्म्माधिकार
धर्माधिकार m. (-रः) The office of a judge.<BR> E. धर्म, and अधिकार office.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=367-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्माधिकारिन्|धर्म्माधिकारिन्
धर्माधिकारिन् m. (-री) A judge.<BR> E. धमाधिकार, and णिनि aff. धर्मं व्यवहारे<BR>तन्निर्णयमधिकरोति । अधि + कृ-णिनि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=367-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्म्माध्यक्ष|धर्माध्यक्ष|धर्माध्यक्षः|धर्म्माध्यक्षः
धर्म्माध्यक्ष m. (-क्षः) A magistrate, a judge, &c.<BR> E. धर्म justice, and अध्यक्ष<BR>superintendent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=367-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मानुष्ठान|धर्म्मानुष्ठान
धर्मानुष्ठान n. (-नं) Virtuous or moral conduct, behaviour according to<BR>law.<BR> E. धर्म, and अनुष्ठान act or condition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=367-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्म्मानुसार|धर्मानुसार|धर्मानुसारः
धर्म्मानुसार m. (-रः) Conformity to law or virtue, course or practice of<BR>duty.<BR> E. धर्म, and अनुसार following.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=367-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्म्मापेत|धर्मापेत
धर्म्मापेत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Wicked, immoral, unrighteous.<BR>	 n. (-तं) Im-<BR>morality, vice.<BR> E. धर्म, and अपेत deviated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=367-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्म्माभिमनस्|धर्माभिमनस्
धर्म्माभिमनस् mfn. (-नाः-नाः-नः) Virtuous.<BR> E. धर्म, अभि to or inclined to,<BR>मनस् the mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=367-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्म्मारण्य|धर्मारण्य|धर्म्मारण्यं
धर्म्मारण्य n. (-ण्यं) A forest into which DHARMA once retired.<BR> E. धर्म, and<BR>अरण्य a wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=367-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्म्मासन|धर्मासन|धर्म्मासनं
धर्म्मासन n. (-नं) The seat of the judge, the bench.<BR> E. धर्म, and आसन a<BR>seat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=367-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मिन्|धर्म्मिन्
धर्मिन् mfn. (-र्मी-र्मिणी-र्म्मि)<BR>	 1. Virtuous, pious, just.<BR>	 2. Endowed with a<BR>peculiar property or faculty.<BR> E. धर्म, and इनि poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=367-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मिष्ठ|धर्मिष्ठः|धर्म्मिष्ठ
धर्मिष्ठ mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठा-ष्ठं) Very pious or virtuous.<BR> E. धर्म, and इष्ठन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=367-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मीयस्|धर्म्मीयस्
धर्मीयस् mfn. (-यान्-यसी-यः) Very pious, moral, &c.<BR> E. धर्म, and ईयसुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=367-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मोपदेश|धर्मोपदेशः|धर्म्मोपदेश
धर्मोपदेश m. (-शः) Moral or religious instruction.<BR> E. धर्म, and उपदेश<BR>advice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=367-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मोपदेशक|धर्मोपदेशकः|धर्म्मोपदेशक|धर्म्मोपदेशकः
धर्मोपदेशक m. (-कः) A Guru or spiritual preceptor.<BR> E. धर्म virtue, उप<BR>before, दिश् to show, affix ण्वुल्; pointing out good and evil to<BR>his scholars.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=367-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मोपध|धर्म्मोपध
धर्मोपध mfn. (-धः-धा-धं) Hypocritical.<BR> E. धर्म, and उपधि fraud, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=367-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मोपेत|धर्म्मोपेत
धर्मोपेत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Virtuous, moral.<BR> E. धर्म, and उपेत possessed of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=367-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्म्य|धर्म्म्यः
धर्म्य mfn. (-र्म्यः-र्म्या-र्म्यं)<BR>	 1. Conformable or according to justice or<BR>morality.<BR>	 2. Obtainable by virtue or justice.<BR> E. धर्म as above,<BR>यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=367-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्म्यविवाह|धर्म्म्यविवाहः|धर्म्यविवाहः
धर्म्यविवाह m. (-हः) Legal marriage of five sorts, as the Brāhma, Daiva,<BR>Ārsha, Gāndharba, and Prājāpatya.<BR> E. धर्म्य, and विवाह marriage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=367-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्ष|धर्षः
धर्ष m. (-र्षः)<BR>	 1. Pride, arrogance.<BR>	 2. Contumely, overbearing.<BR>	 3. Impa-<BR>tience.<BR>	 4. Paralysing, rendering weak or impotent.<BR>	 5. Injury,<BR>wrong.<BR>	 6. Restraint.<BR>	 7. Copulation.<BR>	 8. A eunuch.<BR> E. धृष to be vain,<BR>affix भावे घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=367-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्षक|धर्षकः
धर्षक m. (-कः) A dancer, an actor, a mine.<BR> E. धृष् to be vain or pres-<BR>umptuous, affix ण्वुल् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=367-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्षकारिणी
धर्षकारिणी f. (-णी) A violated virgin.<BR> E. धर्ष, कृ to act, affix णिनि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=367-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्षण|धर्षणं
धर्षण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Disrespect, contumely, overbearingness, contempt.<BR>	 2.<BR>copulation.<BR>	 3. arrogance, vanity.<BR>	 f. (-णिः-णी) An unchaste woman.<BR>E. घृष् to be arrogant, &c. affix भावे ल्युट् or युच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=367-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्षवर
धर्षवर m. (-रः) eunuch superintending the women's apartments.<BR> E. धर्ष<BR>copulation, वृ to cherish, affix अप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=367-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्षित|धर्षितं
धर्षित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Proud, insolent.<BR>	 2. Unbearing, impatient.<BR>	 3.<BR>Overpowered, smitten.<BR>	 n. (-तं)<BR>	 1. Copulation, cohabitation.<BR>	 2. Con-<BR>tumely.<BR>	 3. Pride.<BR>	 f. (-ता) An unchaste woman.<BR> E. धृष् to be vain or<BR>impatient, affix, कर्मणि भावे वा क्त । इट् गुणश्च ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=367-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्षिन्
धर्षिन् mfn. (-र्षी-र्षिणी-र्षि)<BR>	 1. Proud, arrogant.<BR>	 2. Cohabiting.<BR>	 f. (-णी) A<BR>dishonest or unchaste woman.<BR> E. धर्ष cohabitation, ईनि and<BR>ङीष् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=367-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धलण्ड|धलण्डः
धलण्ड m. (-ण्डः) A small tree, commonly called Dhalākara; also<BR>धलण्डक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=367-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धव|धवः
धव (इ) धवि r. 1st cl. (धन्वति) To go or move: this is considered some-<BR>times as Sautra root. भ्वा० प० सक० सेट् इदित् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=367-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धव|धवः
धव m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. A husband.<BR>	 2. A man.<BR>	 3. A rogue, a cheat.<BR>	 4. A tree,<BR>(Grislea tomentosa.)<BR> E. धू to make tremble, (children, &c.) affix<BR>अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=367-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धवल|धवलः
धवल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>	 1. White.<BR>	 2. Handsome, beautiful.<BR>	 m. (-लः)<BR>	 1.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=368-a" target="_blank">Page368-a+ 60</a>]<BR>White, (the colour.)<BR>	 2. A capital ox.<BR>	 3. The Grislea tomentosa.<BR>	 4.<BR>Camphor.<BR>	 5. An inferior Rāga or mode of music.<BR>	 n. (-लं) White<BR>pepper.<BR>	 f. (-ला or -ली) A white cow, &c.<BR> E. धाव to be clean or pure,<BR>कलच् affix, and the radical vowel made short.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=367-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धवलपक्ष|धवलपक्षः
धवलपक्ष m. (-क्षः)<BR>	 1. A goose.<BR>	 2. The fortnight of the moon's increase.<BR>E. धवल, and पक्ष wing or fortnight. धवलौ पक्षौ यस्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=368-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धवलमृत्तिका
धवलमृत्तिका f. (-का) Chalk.<BR> E. धवल white. मृत्तिका earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=368-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धवलित
धवलित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) White, whitened.<BR> E. धवल, and इतच् aff. |<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=368-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धवलीकृत
धवलीकृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) White, made white.<BR> E. धवल, and कृत made, च्वि<BR>augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=368-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धवलीभूत
धवलीभूत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Become white.<BR> E. धवल, and भूत become, च्वि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=368-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धवलोत्पल|धवलोत्पलं
धवलोत्पल n. (-लं) The white esculent water lily.<BR> E. धवल white, and<BR>उत्पल a lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=368-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धवाणक|धवाणकः
धवाणक m. (-कः) Air, wind.<BR> E. धू to agitate, (the leaves or trees, &c.)<BR>and आणक Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=368-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धवित्र|धवित्रं
धवित्र n. (-त्रं) A Pankhā or fan, made of antelope's skin, and used<BR>especially for blowing a sacrificial fire,<BR> E. धृ to agitate, इत्र aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=368-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धा
धा (डु, ञ,) डुधाञ् r. 3rd cl. (दधाति-धत्ते)<BR>	 1. To hold or support.<BR>	 2. To<BR>nurture, to maintain.<BR>	 3. To give.<BR>	 4. To have, to possess. With अनु<BR>and सम् prefixed, To search after. With अपि, To cover. With अभि,<BR>1. To speak, to speak to or address.<BR>	 2. To promulgate.<BR>	 3. To show.<BR>With अभि and सम, To overcome. With अव, 1. To be careful.<BR>	 2. To<BR>attend to. With आङ्, To take, to receive. With उप and आङ्, To<BR>support. With उप, 1. To uphold.<BR>	 2. To do, to perform. With नि, 1.<BR>To take up or hold up.<BR>	 2. To place in or upon.<BR>	 3. To be born or<BR>produced.<BR>	 4. To hold. With परि, To assume, to put on, as clothes,<BR>&c. With प्र and नि, 1. To hold or support.<BR>	 2. To elevate or exalt,<BR>to dignify.<BR>	 3. To admit. With प्र, 1. To be chief or first.<BR>	 2. To<BR>send. With प्रति and वि, To do, to perform. With वि, 1. To do, to<BR>execute, to act.<BR>	 2. To act conformably to religious ordinances,<BR>to execute the precepts of the Vedas.<BR>	 3. To choose, to select.<BR>	 4. To<BR>provide.<BR>	 5. To order or direct 6. To promise.<BR>	 7. To give. With<BR>वि and अव, To hide, to veil, to conceal. With सम, 1. To place,<BR>to place firmly, to fix.<BR>	 2. To unite to combine, to hold together.<BR>3. To shoot at a mark. With सम and प्र, To doubt, to discuss; (also<BR>with प्रति and सम्) With आङ्, To instruct, to teach. With सम and<BR>नि, To place or have near at hand. In the causal with उप, To<BR>understand. जुहोत्या० उभ० सक० अनिट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=368-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धा
धा m. (-धाः)<BR>	 1. A possessor, a holder, a container, &c.<BR>	 2. A name of<BR>BRAMHĀ.<BR>	 3. VṚHASPATI.<BR> E. धा to have, affix विच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=368-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धाक|धाकः
धाक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. An ox.<BR>	 2. Food.<BR>	 3. Boiled-rice.<BR>	 4. A post.<BR> E. धा to have<BR>or hold, Unādi affix क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=368-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धाटी
धाटी f. (-टी) advancing towards or confronting an enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=368-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धाणक|धाणकः
धाणक m. (-कः) A weight of gold, a coin of metal, the division of a<BR>Dinār.<BR> E. धा to contain, Unādi affix आणक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=368-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धातकी
धातकी f. (-की) A tree, (Grislea tomentosa.)<BR> E. धा to have, affix ण्वुल्,<BR>तन् inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=368-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धातु|धातुः
धातु m. (-तुः)<BR>	 1. A principle or humour of the body, as phlegm, wind,<BR>and bile.<BR>	 2. Any constituent part of the body, as blood, flesh,<BR>&c.<BR>	 3. A primary or elementary substance, viz. earth, water, fire,<BR>air and Ākāsa or atmosphere.<BR>	 4. The property of a primary element<BR>viz. ordour, flavour, colour, touch, and sound.<BR>	 5. An organ of sense.<BR>6. A mineral, a fossil.<BR>	 7. A metal.<BR>	 8. A grammatical root; in<BR>Sanskrit this radical performs no other office, and cannot be used<BR>as a word without undergoing some change.<BR> E. धा to possess, to<BR>contain, (life, substance, &c.) तुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=368-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धातुकाशोश
धातुकाशोश n. (-शं) Red sulphate of iron.<BR> E. धातु mineral, and काशीश the<BR>green sulphate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=368-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धातुघ्न|धातुघ्नं
धातुघ्न n. (-घ्नं) Sour gruel, prepared from the fermentation of rice-water.<BR>E. धात chyle, and घ्न destroying; also similar compounds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=368-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धातुनाशन|धातुनाशनं
धातुनाशन n. (-नं) Sour gruel: see the last.<BR> E. धातु, and नाशन injuring.<BR>धातुं नाशयति नश-णिच्-ल्यु । स्वर्णादि धातुमारके, काञ्चिके च ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=368-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धातुप|धातुपः
धातुप m. (-पः) The alimentary juice or chyle.<BR> E. धातु an essential cons-<BR>tituent of the body, and प what cherishes. धातुं पाति पा-क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=368-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धातुपुष्पिका
धातुपुष्पिका f. (-का) A plant: see धातुपुष्पिका; also धातुपुष्पी ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=368-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धातुभृत्
धातुभृत् m. (-त्)<BR>	 1. A mountain.<BR>	 2. A robust man.<BR>	 mfn. (-भृत्) Promot-<BR>ing the animal secretions.<BR> E. धातु a mineral, and भृत what contains.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=368-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धातुमाक्षिक|धातुमाक्षिकं
धातुमाक्षिक n. (-कं) A mineral substance, a sulphurate of iron.<BR> E. धातु<BR>mineral, and माक्षिक the same substance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=368-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धातुमारिणी
धातुमारिणी f. (-णी) Borax.<BR> E. धातु a metal, मृ to perish, in the causal<BR>form, णिनि and ङीप् affixes; the borate of soda is generally used<BR>in India as a flux. धातुं मारयति मृ णिच् णिनि ङीप् (सोहागा)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=368-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धातुराजक|धातुराजकं|धातुराजकः
धातुराजक m. (-कः) Semen, the seminal fluid.<BR> E. धातु animal fluid, &c.<BR>राज chief, कन् added. धातुषु राजते राज-ण्वुल् धातुनां राजा टच् स० स्वार्थे<BR>क वा ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=368-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धातुवल्लभ|धातुवल्लभं
धातुवल्लभ n. (-भं) Borax.<BR> E. धातु, and वल्लभ a friend, a flux.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=368-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धातुवादिन्
धातुवादिन् m. (-दी) An assayer, a miner, a mineralogist.<BR> E. धातु a miner-<BR>al, वद् to speak or describe, affix णिनि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=368-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धातुवैरिन्
धातुवैरिन् m. (-री) Sulphur.<BR> E. धातु a metal, and वैरिन् an enemy;<BR>tarnishing metallic lustre, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=368-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धातुशेखर|धातुशेखरं
धातुशेखर m. (-रः) Green sulphate of iron, or green vitriol.<BR> E. धातु a<BR>mineral, and शेखर crest or chief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=368-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धातूपल|धातूपलः
धातूपल m. (-लः) Chalk.<BR> E. धातु a mineral, and उपल stone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=368-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धातृ
धातृ m. (-ता)<BR>	 1. A name of BRAMHĀ.<BR>	 2. A title of VIṢṆU.<BR>	 3. A father,<BR>a parent.<BR>	 f. (-त्री)<BR>	 1. A mother.<BR>	 2. A foster-mother, a nurse.<BR>	 3. The<BR>earth.<BR>	 4. Emblic myrobalan.<BR>	 mfn. (-त्रा-त्री-तृ)<BR>	 1. A cherisher, a<BR>protector, fostering, nourishing, 2. Having, containing, possess-<BR>ing, a possessor, &c.<BR> E. धा to have, to nourish, &c. affix तृच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=368-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धातृपुत्त्र
धातृपुत्त्र m. (-त्त्रः) A saint, also called SANATKUMĀRA.<BR> E. धातृ BRAMHĀ,<BR>and पुत्त्र the son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=368-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धातृपुष्पिका
धातृपुष्पिका f. (-का) A tree, (Grislea tomentosa, Rox.)<BR> E. धातृ cherish-<BR>ing, पुष्प a flower, ङीष् added, धातृपुष्पी and कन् added; also with-<BR>out the pleonasm, धातृपुष्पी f. (-ष्पी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=368-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धात्रिका
धात्रिका f. (-का) Emblic myrobalan.<BR> E. कन् added to धात्री ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=368-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धात्रीपुत्त्र
धात्रीपुत्त्र m. (-त्त्रः)<BR>	 1. An actor.<BR>	 2. A foster-brother.<BR> E. धात्री a nurse,<BR>and पुत्त्र a son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=368-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धात्रीफल|धात्रीफलं
धात्रीफल n. (-लं) The fruit of the emblic myrobalan.<BR> E. धात्री phyllan-<BR>thus emblica, and फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=368-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धात्रेयी
धात्रेयी f. (-यी)<BR>	 1. A sort of confidante, a foster-sister so employed.<BR>	 2. A<BR>wet-nurse,<BR> E. धातृ a nurse, ढक् affix, fem. affix ङीप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=368-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धाना
धाना f. plu. (-नाः)<BR>	 1. Fried barley or rice. sin (-नः)<BR>	 1. Coriander, (Corian-<BR>drum sativum)<BR>	 2. Grain fried, and reduced to powder.<BR>	 3. A bud,<BR>a shoot.<BR> E. धा to nourish, न Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=368-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धानाका
धानाका f. plu. (-काः) Fried barley or rice.<BR> E. धाना as above, कन्<BR>added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=368-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धानाचूर्ण|धानाचूर्णं
धानाचूर्ण n. (-र्णं) The meal or flour of fried barley, rice, &c.<BR> E. धाना<BR>fried grain, चूर्ण powder, dust.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=368-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धानी
धानी f. (-नी)<BR>	 1. Coriander.<BR>	 2. A granary. a receptacle.<BR>	 3. The site of<BR>a habitation.<BR>	 4. The name of a river.<BR>	 5. What has or contains,<BR>used in composition, as राजधानी a royal capital, having the king's<BR>presence, मत्स्यधानी a net, &c.<BR> E. धा to have, affix युच्, fem. affix.<BR>ङीप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=368-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धानुष्क|धानुष्कः
धानुष्क m. (-ष्कः) A bowyer, an archer.<BR> E. धनुस् a bow, ठक् affix.<BR>	 f.<BR>(-ष्का) A tree, (Achyranthes aspera.)<BR> E. धनुष्क an archer, अण् affix,<BR>and fem. affix टाप्, or धनुस् a bow, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=368-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धानुष्य|धानुष्यः
धानुष्य m. (-ष्यः) A bamboo.<BR> E. धनुस् as above, ञ्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=368-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धानेय|धानेयं
धानेय n. (-यं) Coriander, (Coriandrum sativum.)<BR> E. धन grain, &c. aff.<BR>स्वार्थे ढक्; also with कन् added, धानेयक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=368-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धान्धा|धांधा
धान्धा f. (-न्धा) Small cardamoms. एलायाम् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=368-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धान्य|धान्यं
धान्य n. (-न्यं)<BR>	 1. Corn in general, but especially rice, (Orizasativa.)<BR>	 2.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=369-a" target="_blank">Page369-a+ 60</a>]<BR>Coriander.<BR>	 3. A measure equal to four Seasamum seeds.<BR> E. धा<BR>to nourish (mankind), Unādi affix यत्, and नुट् augment. धाने<BR>पोषणे साधु यत् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=368-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धान्यक|धान्यकं|धान्यकः
धान्यक n. (-कं) Coriander, (C. sativum)<BR> E. कन् added to धान्य; also धन्याक<BR>and धान्याक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=369-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धान्यकल्क
धान्यकल्क n. (-ल्कं) Bran, chaff, straw.<BR> E. धान्य, and कल्क dirt or sediment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=369-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धान्यकोष्ठक|धान्यकोष्ठकं
धान्यकोष्ठक n. (-कं) A granary, a basket, A cupboard or small shed of<BR>matting, &c. for keeping rice.<BR> E. धान्य rice, कोष्ठ a granary, and कन्<BR>added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=369-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धान्यचमस|धान्यचमसः
धान्यचमस m. (-सः) Rice flattened by threshing after it has been steeped<BR>and fried in the husk.<BR> E. धान्य grain, and चमस a sort of cake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=369-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धान्यधेनु|धान्यधेनुः
धान्यधेनु f. (-नुः) A heap of rice to be presented to Brāhmans.<BR> E. धान्य,<BR>and धेनु a cow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=369-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धान्यमाय|धान्यमायः
धान्यमाय m. (-यः) A corn-seller, &c.<BR> E. धान्य grain, मा to measure, अण् aff.<BR>धान्यं माति मा-अण् युक् वा ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=369-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धान्यराज|धान्यराजः
धान्यराज m. (-जः) Barley.<BR> E. धान्य, and राजा king. यवे ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=369-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धान्यवत्|धान्यवन्त्
धान्यवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Abounding in corn, having abundance of it.<BR>E. धान्य, and मतुप् poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=369-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धान्यवर्द्धन
धान्यवर्द्धन n. (-नं) Lending grain at interest; receiving a usurious return<BR>for a loan of corn seed supplied to the peasants.<BR> E. धान्य corn,<BR>वर्द्धन increasing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=369-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धान्यवीज
धान्यवीज n. (-जं) Coriander.<BR> E. धान्य, and वीज seed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=369-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धान्यवीर|धान्यवीरः
धान्यवीर m. (-रः) A sort of pulse, (Phaseolus max.)<BR> E. धान्य, and वीर best.<BR>माषे (कलाई) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=369-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धान्वशीर्षक
धान्वशीर्षक n. (-कं) The ear or spike of corn.<BR> E. धान्य, with शीर्षक the top<BR>or head.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=369-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धान्यसंग्रह|धान्यसङ्ग्रह
धान्यसंग्रह m. (-हः) A store or magazine of grain.<BR> E. धान्य, and संग्रह col-<BR>lection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=369-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धान्यसार|धान्यसारः
धान्यसार m. (-रः) Grain after threshing.<BR> E. धान्य corn, and सार essence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=369-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धान्याक|धान्याकं
धान्याक n. (-कं) Coriander.<BR> E. स्वार्थे अण् added to धन्याक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=369-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धान्याचल|धान्याचलः
धान्याचल m. (-लः) A pile of grain for presentation to Brahmans.<BR> E. धान्य,<BR>and अचल a mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=369-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धान्याम्ल|धान्याम्लं
धान्याम्ल n. (-म्लं) Sour gruel made of the fermentation of boiled<BR>rice-water.<BR> E. धान्य rice, and अम्ल sour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=369-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धान्यारि|धान्यारिः
धान्यारि m. (-रिः) A rat<BR> E. धान्य, and अरि a foe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=369-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धान्यार्थ|धान्यार्थः
धान्यार्थ m. (-र्थः) Wealth in rice or gain.<BR> E. धान्य, and अर्थ wealth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=369-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धान्यास्थि
धान्यास्थि n. (-स्थि) Grain after threshing.<BR> E. धान्य, and अस्थि a bone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=369-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धान्योत्तम|धान्योत्तमः
धान्योत्तम m. (-मः) Rice.<BR> E. धान्य, and उत्तम best. धान्येषूत्तमः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=369-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धामन्
धामन् n. (-मः)<BR>	 1. The body.<BR>	 2. A house, a dwelling.<BR>	 3. Dignity, conse-<BR>quence, eminence.<BR>	 4. Spirit, pride, especially martial pride, hero-<BR>ism.<BR>	 5. Light, splendour, radiance.<BR>	 6. A ray of light.<BR>	 7. A place,<BR>a spot, a country.<BR>	 8. Birth.<BR> E. धा to contain, (life, a tenant, &c.)<BR>and मनिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=369-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धामनिधि|धामनिधिः
धामनिधि m. (-धिः) The sun.<BR> E. धाम light, निधि a nest or receptacle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=369-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धामनी
धामनी f. (-नी) Any tubular vessel of the body: see धमनी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=369-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धामवत्|धामवन्त्
धामवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>	 1. Splendid, luminous, 2. Eminent, exalted,<BR>illustrious.<BR>	 3. Heroic.<BR> E. धामन् and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=369-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धामार्गव|धामार्गवः|धामार्ग्गव
धामार्गव m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. A tree, (Achyranthes aspera.)<BR>	 2. A plant, a sort of<BR>Ghoshā, with white flowers.<BR> E. धामन् a dwelling, मार्ग a road, व<BR>to go or approach, affix क, deriv. irr. or धाम्नोऽर्गं वाति वा-क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=369-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धाय|धायः
धाय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Having, possessing, or who has or possesses.<BR> E. धा<BR>to have, ण aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=369-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धायस्
धायस् mfn. (-याः-याः-यः) An upholder.<BR> E. धा to have, &c. असुन् Unādi<BR>affix; also with a final vowel added, धायस.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=369-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धाय्य|धाय्यः
धाय्य m. (-व्यः) A Purohit or family priest.<BR>	 f. (-य्या) A prayer for exciting<BR>fire, upon the addition of fuel. E. Irregularly derived from धो to<BR>contain, with ण्यत् aff. or more correctly. धा-कर्मणि ण्यत्-युक् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=369-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धार|धारं|धारः
धार n. (-रं) Water derived from rain.<BR>	 m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A sort of stone.<BR>2. Debt.<BR>	 3. Slight sprinkling rain.<BR>	 4. Frost.<BR>	 5. End, bound, a line<BR>or limit.<BR>	 6. A deep place, a depth.<BR>	 f. (-रा)<BR>	 1. A horse's pace,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=369-b" target="_blank">Page369-b+ 60</a>]<BR>as the trot, canter, &c.<BR>	 2. The van of an army.<BR>	 3. The sharp<BR>edge of a sword or any cutting instrument.<BR>	 4. The flowing.<BR>running, oozing, or distilling &c. of any liquid, the motion of a<BR>fluid, stream, current, &c.<BR>	 5. Offspring.<BR>	 6. A leak, a flaw, a hole in<BR>pitcher &c.<BR>	 7. Excellence.<BR>	 8. The wheel of a carriage.<BR>	 9. A garden<BR>wall or fence, a hedge, &c.<BR>	 10. The edge of a mountain.<BR>	 11.<BR>Quantity, multitude.<BR>	 12. A heavy shower falling in large drops, or<BR>hail.<BR>	 13. Fame.<BR>	 14. Likeness.<BR>	 15. Custom, usage.<BR>	 16. The capital<BR>of BHOJA.<BR>	 17. Pouring a stream of water upon an image to get rid<BR>of a fever.<BR> E. धृ to fall, to uphold &c. in the cansal form, and णिच्<BR>and अच् affs. धाराया इदम् अण् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=369-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धारक|धारकः
धारक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Who or what holds or contains, a vessel or-<BR>receptacle of any kind.<BR>	 m. (-क.) A water pot.<BR> E. धृ to have, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=369-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धारण|धारणं
धारण n. (-णं) Holding, having, keeping, maintaining.<BR>	 f. (-णा)<BR>	 1. Con-<BR>tinuance in rectitude, keeping in the right way.<BR>	 2. Fortitude,<BR>firmness, steadiness, resolution.<BR>	 3. A particular religious exercise;<BR>keeping the mind collected, the breath suspended, and all natural<BR>wants restrained; steady, immoveable abstraction.<BR>	 4. Mental re-<BR>tention, memory.<BR>	 5. Understanding, intellect.<BR>	 6. Believing, con-<BR>viction.<BR>	 7. Certainty, conclusion.<BR>	 8. Positive precept or injunction.<BR>9. Debt.<BR>	 f. (-णी)<BR>	 1. Any tubular vessel of the body.<BR>	 2. A mystical<BR>verse or charm, or collection of such verses, among the Bauddhas<BR>3. A row or line.<BR> E. धृ to hold, (purpose, intent, virtue, &c.) affix<BR>ल्युट् or भावे युच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=369-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धारणक|धारणकः
धारणक m. (-कः) A debtor.<BR> E. धारण a debt, कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=369-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धारणीय
धारणीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) To be held or retained, to be adhered to.<BR> E. धृ<BR>to hold, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=369-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धारय|धारयः
धारय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Who or what has or possesses.<BR> E. धृ to have,<BR>causal form, श aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=369-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धारयत्
धारयत् mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्)<BR>	 1. Having, possessing.<BR>	 2. Acquainted with,<BR>versed in.<BR>	 3. Holding as doctrine, believing, maintaining.<BR> E. धृ to<BR>have, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=369-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धारयित्री
धारयित्री f. (-त्री) The earth.<BR> E. धृ to contain, in the causal form, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=369-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धाराकदम्बक
धाराकदम्बक m. (-कः) A sort of Kadamba tree. प्रावृट्काले पुष्पवति कदम्बभेदे ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=369-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धाराङ्कुर|धारांकुर|धाराङ्कुरः
धाराङ्कुर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Thin rain.<BR>	 2. Hail.<BR>	 3. Advancing before an army by<BR>way of defiance to an enemy.<BR> E. धारा rain, and अङ्कुर shoot or<BR>sprout.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=369-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धाराङ्ग|धारांग|धाराङ्गः
धाराङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>	 1. A sword, a scimitar.<BR>	 2. A place of pilgrimage. E.<BR>धारा the edge of a sword, &c. and अङ्ग body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=369-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धाराट|धाराटः
धाराट mf. (-टः-टा)<BR>	 1. The Chātaka, (Cuculus melanoleucos.)<BR>	 2. A horse.<BR>3. A cloud.<BR>	 4. A furious elephant.<BR> E. धारा rain, &c. अट who goes.<BR>affix अच् । धारायै अटति धारया वा अटति अट-अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=369-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धाराध्वनि
धाराध्वनि f. (-निः) The sound of falling rain or of the flowing of any<BR>fluid.<BR> E. धारा, and ध्वनि sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=369-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धाराधर|धाराधरः
धाराधर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A cloud.<BR>	 2. A sword.<BR> E. धारा rain or an edge, and धर what has.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=369-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धारायन्त्र|धारायंत्र
धारायन्त्र n. (-न्त्रं) A scent bottle, a sprinkling vase or ewer, a sort of<BR>censer.<BR> E. धारा, and यन्त्र an instrument. धारायाः प्रस्रवार्थं यन्त्रम् । (फोयारा)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=369-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धारावनि|धारावनिः
धारावनि mf. (-निः-निः) Air, wind.<BR> E. धारा thin rain, वन् to sound, affix इ.<BR>धाराया अवनिरिव । वायौ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=369-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धाराविष|धाराविषः
धाराविष m. (-षः) A crooked sword, a scimitar, a sabre.<BR> E. धारा, and विष<BR>poison; whose edge is as fatal as venom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=369-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धाराश्रु
धाराश्रु n. (-श्रु) A flood of tears.<BR> E. धारा, and अश्रु a tear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=369-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धारासम्पात|धारासंपात|धारासंपातः|धारासम्पातः
धारासम्पात m. (-तः) A hard shower, a heavy fall of rain.<BR> E. धारा rain,<BR>सम् implying quantity or accumulation, and पात falling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=369-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धारासार|धारासारः
धारासार m. (-रः) A heavy fall of rain, a large drop or shower.<BR> E. धारा<BR>and आसार sprinkling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=369-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धारिणी
धारिणी f. (-णी)<BR>	 1. The earth.<BR>	 2. The silk-cotton tree, (Bombax hepta-<BR>phyllum.)<BR> E. धृ, and णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=369-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धारित
धारित n. (-तं) A horse's trot; also धारितकंः see धौरितकं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=369-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धारिन्
धारिन् mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>	 1. Having, holding, keeping, possessing.<BR>	 2.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=370-a" target="_blank">Page370-a+ 60</a>]<BR>Edged.<BR>	 m. (-री) A sort of tree: see पीलु.<BR> E. धारा an edge, &c. णिनि<BR>aff. or धारं ऋणं शीध्यत्वेन अस्ति अस्य । स्त्रीयां ङीप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=369-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धारु|धारुः
धारु mfn. (-रुः-रुः-रु) Who drink, or sucks, a drinker, a sucker.<BR> E. धे to<BR>drink, रु affix, form special. पानशीले जटाधरः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=370-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धार्त्तराष्ट्र|धार्तराष्ट्र|धार्तराष्ट्रः|धार्त्तराष्ट्रः
धार्त्तराष्ट्र m. (-ष्ट्रः) A sort of goose, with black legs and bill.<BR>	 2. A kind<BR>of snake.<BR>	 3. DURYODHANA or any other descendant of DHRITA-<BR>RĀSHTRA.<BR> E. धृतराष्ट्र the name of a king or a bird, &c. and अण् affix<BR>of descent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=370-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धार्म्मिक|धार्मिक|धार्मिकः|धार्म्मिकः
धार्म्मिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Virtuous, pious, just.<BR> E. धर्म्म virtue, affix ठक् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=370-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धार्य्य|धार्य|धार्य्यं
धार्य्य mfn. (-र्य्यः-र्य्य-र्य्यं)<BR>	 1. To be born or upheld, to be contained. &c.<BR>2. To be kept or detained.<BR> E. धृ to hold, ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=370-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धार्य्यमाण|धार्यमाण
धार्य्यमाण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Being held, maintained, &c.<BR> E. धृ to uphold,<BR>pass. v. शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=370-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धार्य्यमाणत्व|धार्यमाणत्व
धार्य्यमाणत्व n. (-त्वं) Property.<BR> E. त्व added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=370-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धार्ष्ट्य|धार्ष्ट्यं
धार्ष्ट्य n. (-र्ष्ट्यं) Boldness, confidence, arrogance.<BR> E. धृष्टि bold, and<BR>ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=370-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धाव
धाव (उ) धावु r. 1st cl. (धावति-ते)<BR>	 1. To go or move.<BR>	 2. To run.<BR>	 3. To<BR>cleanse.<BR>	 4. To be clean or pure. With अनु.<BR>	 1. To know.<BR>	 2. To run<BR>after. With अभि prefixed. To approach, to come before. With आङ्,<BR>To alight. With परि, To run fast. With वि, To shed or sprinkle.<BR>With सम् and उप, To run to meet. जवे शुद्धौ अक० शुद्धिकरणे संमार्जने<BR>च सक० भ्वा० उभ० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=370-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धावक|धावकः
धावक mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>	 1. Running, going, swift, expeditious.<BR>	 2. Clean-<BR>ing, what cleans or cleanses.<BR> E. धाव to go. ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=370-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धावत्|धावन्त्
धावत् mfn. (-वन्-वन्ती-वत्) Running, going quickly.<BR> E. धाव् to go, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=370-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धावन|धावनं
धावन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Going, motion.<BR>	 2. Cleansing, purifying.<BR>	 f. (-निः or नी)<BR>A sort of creeping plant, (Hedysarum lagopodioides.)<BR> E. धाव् to go<BR>to cleanse, affix ल्युट् or अनि fem. affix ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=370-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धावनिका
धावनिका f. (-का) A prickly nightshade: se कण्टकारी.<BR> E. कन् added to<BR>धावनी implying similitude.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=370-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धावित|धावितः
धावित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Purified, Clean, cleansed.<BR>	 2. Gone, gone or run<BR>away.<BR>	 3. Run to, advanced to or against.<BR> E. धाव् to clean, affix क्त,<BR>with इट् augment, or without the augment धौत.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=370-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धासस्
धासस् m. (-साः) A mountain.<BR> E. धा to uphold, Unādi affix असुन् and षुट्<BR>augment; the word is considerd as peculiar to the Vedas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=370-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धि|धिः
धि r. 6th cl. (धियति) To have hold, to keep, to possess. तुदा० प० सक०<BR>अनिट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=370-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धिक्
धिक् ind. An interjection of reproach or menace, (fie, shame, shame,<BR>&c.)<BR> E. धक्क् to annihilate, डिकन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=370-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धिक्कार|धिक्कारः
धिक्कार m. (-रः) Disrespect, reproach, censure, contempt.<BR> E. धिक fie,<BR>and कार making.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=370-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धिक्कृत|धिक्कृतः
धिक्कृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Cursed.<BR>	 2. Reproached, reviled, censured,<BR>condemned.<BR> E. धिक् fie, and कृत made.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=370-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धिक्किया
धिक्किया f. (-या) Reproach.<BR> E. धिक् fie, and क्रिया making.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=370-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धिक्पारुष्य
धिक्पारुष्य n. (-ष्यं) Excessive abuse.<BR> E. धिक्, and पारुष्य violence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=370-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धिक्ष
धिक्ष r. 1st cl. (धिक्षते)<BR>	 1. To kindle.<BR>	 2. To be weary, 3. To live. सन्दीपने<BR>सक; क्लेशे जीवने अक० भ्वा० आ० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=370-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धिग्वण|धिग्वणः
धिग्वण mf. (-णः-णा) A man of a low caste sprung from a Brāhman,<BR>and a female of the tribe called Ayogava.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=370-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धिग्दण्ड|धिग्दंड|धिग्दण्डः
धिग्दण्ड m. (-ण्डः) Reprimand, censure.<BR> E. धिक, and दण्ड punishment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=370-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धिप्सु
धिप्सु mfn. (-प्सुः-प्सुः-प्सु) Deceptive, wishing to trick or deceive.<BR> E. दम्भ<BR>to cheat. desid. v. सन् उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=370-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धियाम्पति|धियांपति|धियाम्पतिः
धियाम्पति m. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. A Jina or Jaina deified saint.<BR>	 2. The soul.<BR> E. धी<BR>the understanding, in the seventh case, and पति master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=370-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धिव
धिव (इ) धिवि r. 1st and 5th cls. (धिनोति)<BR>	 1. To please, to satisfy.<BR>	 2. To<BR>be pleased or satisfied.<BR>	 3. To go or approach: this verb takes उ,<BR>and substitutes अ for the final, whence its unusual form for the<BR>first class, in the instance given. प्रीणने अक० गतौ च सक० स्वा० पर०<BR>सेट् इदित् । सार्वधातुके धिः आदेशः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=370-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धिष
धिष r. 3rd cl. (दिधेष्टि) To emit sound. जु० प० अक० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=370-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धिषण|धिषणः
धिषण m. (-णः)<BR>	 1. A name of VṚHASPATI.<BR>	 2. Any Guru or spiritual<BR>preceptor.<BR>	 f. (-णा) The understanding, the intellect.<BR> E. धृष् to be<BR>presumptuous, Unādi affix क्यु, and धिष substituted for the root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=370-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धिष्ट्य|धिष्ट्यं|धिष्ट्यः
धिष्ट्य See धिष्ण्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=370-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धिष्ठ्य
धिष्ठ्य See the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=370-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धिष्ण्य|धिष्ण्यं|धिष्ण्यः
धिष्ण्य n. (-ष्ण्यं)<BR>	 1. A place, a spot, a country.<BR>	 2. A house.<BR>	 3. A star, an<BR>asterism.<BR>	 4. Fire.<BR>	 5. Power. strength.<BR>	 m. (-ष्ण्यः) A name of AGNI,<BR>the deity of fire.<BR>	 2. A name of SUKRA, regent of VENUS.<BR> E. धृष् to<BR>be proud or overbearing, deriv. irr.; or more correctly. धृष-ण्य-नि०<BR>the word is also written धिष्ट्य or धिष्ठ्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=370-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धी
धी (ओ ङ) ओधीङ् r. 4th cl. (धीयते)<BR>	 1. To contain, to hold.<BR>	 2. To light,<BR>to disregard or despise.<BR>	 3. To accomplish. With अन्तर, To dis-<BR>appear, to become invisible. दिवा० आ० सक० अनिट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=370-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धी
धी f. (-धीः) Understanding, intellect.<BR> E. ध्यै to meditate, affix क्विप्, the<BR>final diphthong rejected, and the semi-vowel changed to its congen-<BR>er इ, which becomes long. धै-सम्प-भावे-क्किप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=370-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीत|धीतः
धीत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Drank, sucked.<BR> E. धे to drink, participal affix, क्त<BR>and the form irr. अनादृते आराधिते च ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=370-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीति|धीतिः
धीति f. (-तिः) Thirst.<BR> E. धे to drink, affix क्तिन्, and the radical vowel<BR>changed to ई.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=370-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीदा
धीदा f. (-दा)<BR>	 1. A virgin, a maiden.<BR>	 2. Understanding, intellect धियं<BR>ददाति दा-क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=370-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीन्द्रिय|धींद्रिय|धीन्द्रियं
धीन्द्रिय n. (-यं) An intellectual organ, as the mind, the eye, the ear,<BR>the nose, the tongue, and skin.<BR> E. धी the intellect, इन्द्रिय an organ<BR>of sense in general.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=370-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीमत्|धीमन्त्
धीमत् mfn. (-मान्-मती-मत्) Sensible, wise, learned.<BR>	 m. (-मान्) A name of<BR>VṚHASPATI, the preceptor of the gods.<BR> E. धी wisdom, understand-<BR>ing मतुप् possess. aff. धी अस्ति अस्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=370-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीर|धीरं|धीरः
धीर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>	 1. Wise, sensible, learned.<BR>	 2. Firm, steady, con-<BR>sistent, determined.<BR>	 3. Cool, collected.<BR>	 4. Head-strong, self-willed,<BR>uncontrollable.<BR>	 5. Lazy, dull, slow.<BR>	 6. Strong, powerful.<BR>	 7. Well-<BR>behaved, decorous, decent.<BR>	 8. Gentle, steady, (as a breeze.)<BR>	 9.<BR>Deep, (as a sound)<BR>	 m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A name of BALI, a celebrated prince.<BR>2. The ocean.<BR>	 mn. (-रः-रं) Saffron.<BR>	 f. (-रा)<BR>	 1. A drug;<BR>also काकोली.<BR>	 2. A woman who, although jealous of a husband or<BR>lover, suppresses all expression of resentment in his presence. E.<BR>धी understanding, रा to possess, क affix; or धी with ईर to go to,<BR>affix अण्; or धी to possess, क्तन् Unādi aff. धियं राति रा-क । धियमीरयति<BR>ईरअण् वा । उप० स ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=370-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीरत्व|धीरत्वं
धीरत्व n. (-त्वं)<BR>	 1. Firmness, fortitude.<BR>	 2. The feminine property of sup-<BR>pressing violent expression of jealousy.<BR> E. धीर firm, steady, affix<BR>त्व; also with तल् affix धीरता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=370-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीरप्रशान्त|धीरप्रशांत|धीरप्रशान्तः
धीरप्रशान्त n. (-न्तं) The hero of a poem or play who unites all good<BR>qualities.<BR> E. धीर, and प्रशान्त calm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=370-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीरललित|धीरललितः
धीरललित m. (-तः) The hero of a poem or play, who is firm and brave,<BR>but reckless and inconsiderate.<BR> E. धीर and ललित sportive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=370-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीरस्कन्द
धीरस्कन्द m. (-न्दः) A buffalo.<BR> E. धीर strong, स्कन्द a shoulder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=370-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीराधीरा
धीराधीरा f. (-रा) A mistress or wife, who having cause for jealousy,<BR>pursues a middle conduct between the suppression and expression<BR>of resentment.<BR> E. धीरा and अधीरा joined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=370-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीरोदात्त|धीरोदात्तः
धीरोदात्त m. (-त्तः) The hero of a poem or play whose characteristics<BR>are benevolence and fortitude.<BR> E. धीर, and उदात्त liberal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=370-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीरोद्धत|धीरोद्धतः
धीरोद्धत m. (-तः) The hero of a poem or play who is deficient in magn-<BR>animity.<BR> E. धीर and उद्धत haughty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=370-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीलटि|धीलटिः
धीलटि f. (-टि) A daughter. लट-बाल्योक्तौ इन्-धिया कर्मणा लटिः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=370-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीवन्
धीवन् m. (-वा)<BR>	 1. A brazier.<BR>	 2. A fisherman.<BR> E. धृ to hold, Uṇādi affix<BR>कनिन् and ऋ changed to ई.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=370-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीवर|धीवरः
धीवर m. (-रः) A fisherman.<BR>	 f. (-री)<BR>	 1. A fisherman's wife.<BR>	 2. A sort of<BR>harpoon for catching fish with.<BR> E. धी to hold or gain, (fish,)<BR>Unādi affix ष्वरच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=370-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीशक्ति|धीशक्तिः
धीशक्ति f. (-क्तिः) An intellectual faculty or power of the understanding,<BR>as attention, comprehension. &c.<BR> E. धी the intellect, and शक्ति<BR>power.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=371-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीसख|धीसखः
धीसख m. (-खः)<BR>	 1. A counsellor, an adviser, a minister.<BR>	 2. A tutor or<BR>friend.<BR> E. धी the understanding, and सखि a friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=371-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीसचिव|धीसचिवः
धीसचिव m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. A counsellor, a minister.<BR>	 2. A friendly or prudent<BR>adviser.<BR> E. धी the intellect, and सचिव a friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=371-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धु|धुः
धु (ञ) धुञ् r. 7th cl. (धुनोति-धुनुते) To shake, to agitate: see धू कम्पने अक०<BR>चालने सक० स्वादि० उभ० अनिट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=371-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धु|धुः
धु f. (-धुः) Shaking, trembling.<BR> E. धु to shake भावे डु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=371-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुक्ष
धुक्ष r. 1st cl. (धुक्षते)<BR>	 1. To kindle.<BR>	 2. To be weary.<BR>	 3. To live. भ्वा० आ०<BR>अक० अनिट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=371-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुत|धुतः
धुत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Abandoned, deserted, left.<BR>	 2. Shaken, agitated,<BR>(as leaves by wind, &c.)<BR> E. धु to shake, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=371-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुतपाप
धुतपाप mfn. (-पः-पा-पं) Purified from sin.<BR> E. धुत shaken, पाप sin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=371-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुनन
धुनन n. (-नं) Shaking, agitation.<BR> E. धु to shake, affix ल्यु also धूनन &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=371-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुनान
धुनान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Shaking, agitating.<BR> E. धु to shake, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=371-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुनि|धुनिः
धुनि f. (-निः) A river; see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=371-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुनी
धुनी f. (-नी) A river.<BR> E. धु to go, affix इन् fem. affix ङीप्; the affix is<BR>sometimes considered as निक् leaving नि, which makes धुनि ut sup.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=371-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुनीनाथ|धुनीनाथः
धुनीनाथ m. (-थः) The ocean.<BR> E. धुनी and नाथ lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=371-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुन्धुमार|धुंधुमारः|धुन्धुमारः
धुन्धुमार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. The name of a sovereign; also named Kuvalayāswa.<BR>2. An insect, (Coccinella.)<BR>	 3. The smoke of a house.<BR>	 4. A house.<BR>A house lizard<BR> E. धूम smoke reiterated, ऋ to go, affix अण्, deriv.<BR>irr. or धुन्धुं मारयति-मारि-अण्-उप-स० ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=371-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुन्वत्|धुन्वन्त्
धुन्वत् mfn. (-न्वन्-न्वन्ती-न्वत्) Shaking, agitating.<BR> E. धु to shake, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=371-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुन्वान
धुन्वान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Shaking, agitating.<BR> E. धु to shake, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=371-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुर्
धुर् f. (-धूः)<BR>	 1. The forepart of a carriage, the pole or the path where<BR>the yoke is fixed.<BR>	 2. Agitation, trembling.<BR>	 3. Reflection, recollec-<BR>tion.<BR>	 4. A spark of fire.<BR>	 5. A burthen, a load.<BR>	 6. A part, a portion.<BR>7. Wealth.<BR>	 8. A name of the Gānges.<BR> E. धुर्ब्ब hurt, affix क्विप्, and<BR>व rejected; also with टाप् added, धुरा ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=371-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुरन्धर|धुरंधर|धुरन्धरः
धुरन्धर mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>	 1. Bearing a burthen.<BR>	 2. Bearing, (figuratively,)<BR>laden with good qualities, heavy duties, &c.<BR>	 m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A beast<BR>of burthen.<BR>	 2. A man of business.<BR>	 3. A tree, (Grislea tomentosa.)<BR>E. धुर् a burthen, and धृ to have, affix खच् । खचिह्रस्वः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=371-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुरा
धुरा f. (-रा) A burthen, a load.<BR> E. धुर्व to hurt, affixes क and टाप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=371-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुरीण|धुरीणः
धुरीण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Bearing, (as a burthen.)<BR>	 2. Charged with,<BR>abounding with, (qualities, duties, &c.)<BR>	 m. (-ण)<BR>	 1. A beast of bur-<BR>then.<BR>	 2. A man of business.<BR> E. धुर a burthen, ख aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=371-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुरीय|धुरीयः
धुरीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>	 1. Fit for a load, suited to a burthen 2. Charged<BR>with important duties.<BR>	 m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. A beast of burthen.<BR>	 2. A man<BR>of business.<BR> E. धुर्, and छ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=371-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुर्य्य|धुर्य|धुर्यः|धुर्य्यः
धुर्य्य mfn. (-र्य्यः-र्य्या-र्य्यं) Fit for a burthen, adopted to it, &c.<BR>	 m. (-र्य्यः)<BR>1. A beast of burthen.<BR>	 2. minister, a charged affairs.<BR>	 3. A house.<BR>E. धुर् a burthen, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=371-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुर्व|धुर्व्व
धुर्व (इ) र्व्वि r. 1st. cl. (धुर्वति) To kill or hurt: भ्वा० प० सक० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=371-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुर्व्वह|धुर्वह
धुर्व्वह mfn. (-हः-हा-हं) Bearing a load, a burthen.<BR>	 m. (-हः)<BR>	 1. A beast of<BR>burthen.<BR>	 2. A minister, a charged affairs.<BR> E. धुर् and वह who<BR>bears; also धुरावह ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=371-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुबका
धुबका f. (-का) The introductory stanza to a song, forming afterwards<BR>the burthen of each verse. (धुया)<BR> E. धू to agitate, क्वुन् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=371-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुवन|धुवनः
धुवन m. (-नः) A title of AGNI.<BR> E. धू to agitate, affix क्युन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=371-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुवित्र|धुवित्रं
धुवित्र n. (-त्रं) A sort of fan made of deer skin, and used especially to<BR>excite a sacrificial fire.<BR> E. धू to agitate, इत्र affix also धवित्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=371-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुस्तुर|धुस्तुरः
धुस्तुर m. (-रः) Thorn apple, (Dhatura fastuosa:) see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=371-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुस्तूर|धुस्तूरः
धुस्तूर m. (-रः) Thorn apple, (Datura fastuosa:)<BR> E. धूष् to make hand-<BR>some, affix क्विप्, तूर् to be mischievous, affix क; elegant but deleteri-<BR>ous: the vowels are also both made short, as धुस्तुर, or both remain<BR>long, as in धूस्तूर also written धुत्तूर ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=371-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धु|धुः
धु[धू] (ञ) धूञ् r. 5th cl. (धूनोति-धूनुते) r. 6th cl. धूवति r. 9th cl. (धनाति धुनिते)<BR>r. 1st and 10th cls. धवति-ते-धावयति-ते or धूनयति) To shake or agitate,<BR>to make tremble; with अव, prefixed, 1. To abandon, to quit 2. To<BR>perceive. With निर् 1. To destroy.<BR>	 2. To go or move. With वि to<BR>make tremble or agitate. स्वा० क्य्रा० स्वादि० उभ० सक० अनिट् । उभ० पक्षे<BR>तुदा० कु० पर० सक० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=371-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूक|धूकः
धूक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. The air or wind.<BR>	 2. A rogue, a cheat.<BR>	 3. time.<BR> E. धु<BR>to agitate, कन् Uṇādi affix, and the vowel made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=371-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूक्ष
धूक्ष r. 1st cl. (धूक्षते)<BR>	 1. To live.<BR>	 2. To kindle.<BR>	 3. To be disinterested.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=371-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूत|धूतः
धूत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Shaken, agitated.<BR>	 2. Reproached, reviled.<BR>	 3.<BR>Abandoned, deserted.<BR>	 4. Judged, discriminated.<BR>	 f. (-ता) A wife.<BR>E. धू to shake, &c. affix क्त; this root also forms धून with the same<BR>aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=371-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूतपाप
धूतपाप mfn. (-षः-षा-षं) Pure, free from sin.<BR> E. धूत shaken, पाप sin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=371-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धून|धूनः
धून mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>	 1. Distressed by heat or thirst.<BR>	 2. Shaken, agitated.<BR>E. धू to shake, affix क्त, form irr. धू-क्त-ल्वादि० तस्य-नः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=371-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूनक|धूनकः
धूनक m. (-कः) Resin; it is sometimes read धूणक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=371-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूनन|धूननं|धूननः
धूनन n. (-नं) Shaking, agitating.<BR> E. धू to shake, affix भावे ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=371-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूनि|धूनिः
धूनि f. (-निः) Shaking, agitating.<BR> E. धू to agitate, affix क्तिन्, and त<BR>changed to न. धू-भावे क्तिन्-ल्वादि-तस्य नः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=371-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूप|धूपः
धूप r. 1st cl. (धूपायति) To heat. r. 10th cl. (धूपयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To speak.<BR>	 2. To<BR>shine. तापे अक० तापने सक० भ्वा० प० सेट् । दीप्तो चु० उभ० अक० दीपने<BR>सक० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=371-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूप|धूपः
धूप m. (-पः) Incense, the aromatic vapour that proceeds from the<BR>combustion of any fragrant gum or resin, the use of which is<BR>authorized by scripture.<BR> E. धूप् to heat, affix अच्. धपयति रोगान्<BR>दोषान् वा ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=371-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूपन|धूपनं|धूपनः
धूपन m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. Resin.<BR>	 2. Incense.<BR> E. धूप् to heat, affix ल्यु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=371-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूपवृक्ष|धूपवृक्षः
धूपवृक्ष m. (-क्षः) A species of pine, (Pinus longifolia.)<BR> E. धूप incense<BR>or resin so used, and वृक्ष a tree; also with कन् added, धूपवृक्षक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=371-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूपाङ्ग|धूपांग|धूपाङ्गः
धूपाङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः) Turpentine.<BR> E. धूप, and अङ्ग a part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=371-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूपायित|धूपायितः
धूपायित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Suffering pain or fatigue.<BR>	 2. Incensed, perfu-<BR>med with incense.<BR> E. धूप (to heat, &c.) affix क्त, आय inserted, or<BR>the passive form with the same aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=371-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूपिका
धूपिका f. (-का) Mist, fog.<BR> E. धूप incense, कन् affix of resemblance, fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=371-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूपित|धूपितः
धूपित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Suffering pain or fatigue.<BR>	 2. Scented, perfumed,<BR>incensed.<BR> E. धूप् to heat, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=371-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूम|धूमः
धूम m. (-मः)<BR>	 1. Smoke.<BR>	 2. Scent.<BR> E. धू to agitate, Unādi affix मक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=371-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूमकेतन|धूमकेतनः
धूमकेतन m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. KETU, the personified descending node.<BR>	 2. Fire or<BR>its deity.<BR> E. धूम smoke, and केतन a symbol.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=371-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूमकेतु|धूमकेतुः
धूमकेतु m. (-तुः)<BR>	 1. A comet or falling-star.<BR>	 2. Fire.<BR>	 3. The personified<BR>descending node.<BR> E. धूम smoke, and केतु a mark or symbol.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=371-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूमध्वज|धूमध्वजः
धूमध्वज m. (-जः) Fire.<BR> E. धूम smoke, and ध्वज a sign or symbol.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=371-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूमप्रभा
धूमप्रभा f. (-भा) A division of hell, the hell of smoke.<BR> E. धूम, and प्रभा<BR>what shines.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=371-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूममहिषी
धूममहिषी f. (-षी) Fog, mist.<BR> E. धूम smoke, महिषी a buffalo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=371-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूमयोनि|धूमयोनिः
धूमयोनि m. (-निः) A cloud.<BR> E. धूम smoke, and योनि womb; what is<BR>engendered from smoke or vapour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=371-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूमल|धूमलः
धूमल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Of a purple colour.<BR>	 m. (-लः) Purple, a colour<BR>compounded of black and red.<BR> E. धूम smoke, and ल what is, being<BR>of the hue of smoke. धूमं लाति ला-क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=371-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूमसंहति|धूमसंहतिः
धूमसंहति f. (-तिः) A cloud or quantity of smoke.<BR> E. धूम, and संहति<BR>collection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=371-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूमसी
धूमसी f. (-सी) A cake of pulse steeped in water, and dried in the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=371-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूमाकार
धूमाकार mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Of the form or appearance of smoke.<BR> E. धूम,<BR>and आकार form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=371-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूमाभ|धूमाभः
धूमाभ mfn. (-भः-मा-मं) Of a purple colour.<BR>	 m. (-भः) Purple.<BR> E. धूम smoke,<BR>and आभ resembling; of a smoky hue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=371-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूमावलि|धूमावलिः
धूमावलि f. (-लिः) A wreath or cloud of smoke.<BR> E. धूम, and आवलि a line.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=371-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूमिका
धूमिका f. (-का) Fog, vapour.<BR> E. धूम smoke, and ठन् affix of resemblance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=371-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूमोर्णा
धूमोर्णा f. (-र्णा) The wife of YAMA.<BR> E. धूम smoke, and ऊर्ण wool;<BR>of a smoky hue, and woolly-headed, a Caffree, Proserpine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=372-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूमोर्णापति|धूमोर्णापतिः
धूमोर्णापति m. (-तिः) YAMA, the ruler of the dead.<BR> E. धूमोर्णा as<BR>above, and पति husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=372-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूम्या
धूम्या f. (-म्या) A quantity of smoke.<BR> E. धूम with य affix, implying<BR>aggregation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=372-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूम्याट|धूम्याटः
धूम्याट m. (-टः) The fork-tailed shrike.<BR> E. धूम्या much smoke, and<BR>अट who goes,<BR> E. धूम्या इव अटति अट् अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=372-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूम्र|धूम्रः
धूम्र mfn. (-म्रः-म्रा-म्रं) Of a purple or smoky colour.<BR>	 m. (-म्रः) Purple,<BR>the colour; a compound of red and black.<BR>	 n. (-म्रं) Sin, vice,<BR>wickedness.<BR> E. धू smoke. रा to get, affix क, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=372-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूम्रक|धूम्रकः
धूम्रक m. (-कः) A camel.<BR> E. धूम्र smoky, कन् affix; of a smoky or tawny<BR>hue. धूम्र इव कायति कै-क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=372-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूम्रलोचन|धूम्रलोचनः
धूम्रलोचन m. (-नः) A pigeon.<BR> E. धूम्र dark, लोचन the eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=372-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूम्ररुच्
धूम्ररुच् mfn. (-रुक्) Of a purple colour.<BR> E. धूम्र, and रुच् to shine, affix<BR>क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=372-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूम्रवर्ण|धूम्रवर्णः
धूम्रवर्ण mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-र्णं) Of a smoky hue.<BR>	 m. (-र्णः) Incense.<BR>	 f. (-र्णा)<BR>Flame, or one of the seven tongues of AGNI or fire.<BR> E. धूम्र<BR>smoky or purplish, and वर्ण colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=372-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूम्राक्षि|धूम्राक्षिः
धूम्राक्षि m. (-क्षिः) A pearl of a bad colour.<BR> E. धूम्र smoky, अक्षि an eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=372-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूम्राट|धूम्राटः
धूम्राट m. (-टः) The fork-tailed shrike.<BR> E. धूम्र smoky, and अट who<BR>goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=372-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूम्राभ|धूम्राभः
धूम्राभ m. (-भः) Air, wind.<BR> E. धूम्र smoky, आभ who shines.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=372-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूम्रिका
धूम्रिका f. (-का) The Sisu tree.<BR> E. कन् added to धूम्र, fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=372-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूयमान
धूयमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Agitated, shaken.<BR> E. धू to shake, pass. v.<BR>शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=372-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूर
धूर (ई,) धूरी r. 4th cl. (धूर्य्यते)<BR>	 1. To kill or hurt.<BR>	 2. To move or approach.<BR>बधे गतौ च दिवा० आ० सक० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=372-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूर्ज्जटि|धूर्जटि|धूर्जटिः
धूर्ज्जटि m. (-टिः) A name of ŚIVA.<BR> E. धुर् a burthen, and जटि a colle-<BR>tion, from जट् to collect, and इन् affix; who collects or bears the<BR>burthen of the three worlds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=372-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूर्त्त|धूर्त|धूर्तः|धूर्त्तं|धूर्त्तः
धूर्त्त mfn. (-र्त्तः-र्त्ता-र्त्तं)<BR>	 1. Fraudulent, crafty, dishonest, knavish; &c.<BR>2. Mischievous, injurious.<BR>	 m. (-र्त्तः)<BR>	 1. A gamester.<BR>	 2. A rogue, a<BR>cheat.<BR>	 3. Thorn apple, (Dhutura.)<BR>	 n. (-र्त्तं)<BR>	 1. Rust or iron filings.<BR>2. Black salt.<BR> E. धुर्व्व to injure, Unādi affix तन्, deriv. irr. धूर वा क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=372-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूर्त्तक|धूर्तक|धूर्तकः|धूर्त्तकः
धूर्त्तक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A jackal.<BR>	 2. A cheat, a rogue, &c.<BR> E. धूर्त्त crafty, कन्<BR>added. धूर्त्त इव इवार्थे कन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=372-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूर्त्तकितव|धूर्तकितव|धूर्तकितवः
धूर्त्तकितव m. (-वः) A gamester.<BR> E. धूर्त्त, and कितव a knave.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=372-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूर्त्तकृत्|धूर्तकृत्
धूर्त्तकृत् mfn. (-कृत्) Dishonest, a knave, a rogue, a cheat.<BR>	 m. (-त्)<BR>Thorn apple: see धुस्तूर<BR> E. धूर्त्त mischievous, and कृत् who acts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=372-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूर्त्तजन्तु|धूर्तजन्तु|धूर्तजंतु|धूर्त्तजन्तुः
धूर्त्तजन्तु m. (-न्तुः) Man.<BR> E. धूर्त्त crafty, and जन्तु an animal; the subtlest<BR>of all animals.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=372-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूर्त्तता|धूर्तता
धूर्त्तता f. (-ता) Knavery, roguery, knavishness.<BR> E. धूर्त्त, and तल् affix;<BR>also with त्व, धूर्त्तत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=372-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूर्त्तमण्डल|धूर्तमण्डल
धूर्त्तमण्डल m. (-लः) A party of rogues or gamblers.<BR> E. धूर्त्त a cheat, and<BR>मण्डल a circle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=372-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूर्त्तमानुषा|धूर्तमानुषा
धूर्त्तमानुषा f. (-षा) A plant: see रास्ना.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=372-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूर्धर|धूर्धरः
धूर्धर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>	 1. Bearing a load or burthen.<BR>	 2. Managing affairs.<BR>m. (-रः) A beast of burthen.<BR> E. धूर् a burthen, and धर bearing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=372-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूर्व्वह|धूर्वह|धूर्वहः|धूर्व्वहः
धूर्व्वह mfn. (-हः-हा-हं) Bearing a load, who or what does so.<BR>	 2. Manag-<BR>ing affairs.<BR> E. धूर, and वह what bears.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=372-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूर्व्वी|धूर्वी
धूर्व्वी f. (-र्ब्बी) The forepart or pole of a carriage.<BR> E. धूर्व्व to injure, affix-<BR>es अच् and ङीष् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=372-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूलक|धूलकं
धूलक n. (-कं) Poison.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=372-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूलि|धूलिः
धूलि mf. (-लिः-लिः or -ली)<BR>	 1. Dust.<BR>	 2. A number.<BR> E. धू to agitate, affix<BR>लिक् वा ङीप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=372-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूलिका
धूलिका f. (-का) Fog or mist.<BR> E. धूलि dust, कन् affix of resemblance; the<BR>dust of the atmosphere. धूलिरिव कायति कै-क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=372-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूलिकुट्टिम
धूलिकुट्टिम n. (-मं) A mound, a rampart.<BR> E. धूलि dust or earth, and कृट्टिम<BR>prepared ground.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=372-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूलिकेदार|धूलिकेदारः
धूलिकेदार m. (-रः) A mound, a rampart of earth.<BR> E. धूलि dust, and<BR>केदार a field.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=372-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूलिगुच्छक|धूलिगुच्छकः
धूलिगुच्छक m. (-कः) The red vegetable powder thrown about at the<BR>spring festival called the Holi.<BR> E. धूलि dust, and गुच्छक a nose-<BR>gay; also धूलिगुच्छ m. (-च्छः)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=372-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूलिध्वज|धूलिध्वजः
धूलिध्वज m. (-जः) Air or wind.<BR> E. धूली dust, and ध्वज sign or symbol.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=372-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूलीकदम्ब|धूलीकदम्बः
धूलीकदम्ब m. (-म्बः)<BR>	 1. A species of the Kadamba tree, (Nauclea cordi<BR>folia.)<BR>	 2. Tila, a plant.<BR>	 3. A tree: see वरुण (Tapia cratæva.)<BR> E. धूली<BR>dust, and कदम्ब Kadamba, whose pollen perhaps resembles that of<BR>the Kadamba, or having a similar quantity of blossoms; also with<BR>कन् added धूलीकदम्बक; these words are also written with a short<BR>इ, as धूलिकदम्बक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=372-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूलीपटल|धूलीपटलः
धूलीपटल m. (-लः) A cloud of dust.<BR> E. धूली, and पटल a heap.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=372-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूश
धूश r. 10th cl. (धूशयति-ते) To make splendid or elegant; also धूष, and<BR>धूस । चुरा० उभ० सक० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=372-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूष
धूष r. 10th cl. (धूषयति-ते) to make splendid or elegant चुरा० उभ० सक०<BR>सेट् । also धूश and धूस ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=372-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूस
धूस r. 10th cl. (धूसयति-ते) To embellish, to make splendid or elegant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=372-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूसर|धूसरः
धूसर mfn. (-रः-री-रं) Grey, of that colour.<BR>	 m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Grey, (the colour,)<BR>2. A jack ass.<BR>	 3. An oilman.<BR>	 4. A camel.<BR>	 5. A pigeon.<BR>	 6. Any<BR>thing of a grey tint.<BR>	 f. (-री) A female Kinnara or chorister of<BR>heaven.<BR> E. धृ to agitate (the mind,) सर Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=372-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूसरछदा|धूसरच्छदा
धूसरछदा f. (-दा) A plant commonly Swetarāsna.<BR> E. धूसर grey, and छद<BR>a leaf, grey-leaved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=372-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूस्तूर|धूस्तूरः
धूस्तूर m. (-रः) The thorn apple, (Dhutura metel and fastuosa.)<BR> E. धूस्<BR>elegant, and तूर injurious: see धुस्तुर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=372-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृ
धृ (ङ) धृङ् r. 1st cl. (धरते) To fall. r. 6th cl. (ध्रियते)<BR>	 1. To continue, to<BR>remain.<BR>	 2. To have or hold, (ञ) धृञ् r. 1st cl. (धरति-ते) To have<BR>or hold, to keep, to maintain. r. 1st cl. (धरति) To sprinkle. r. 10th<BR>cl. (धारयति-ते) To hold. With अप or निर् prefixed, To verify, to<BR>make sure or certain. स्थितौ अक० धृतौ सक० उभ० भ्वा० अनिट् । तुदा० आ०<BR>अनिट् । चुरा० उभ० सक० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=372-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृज
धृज r. 1st cl. (धर्जति) also (इ) धृजि r. 1st cl. (धृञ्जति) To go or move. भ्वा०<BR>पर० सक० सेट् । इदित् च ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=372-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृत्
धृत् mfn. (धृत्) Who has, holds, possesses, &c.<BR> E. धृ to have, क्विप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=372-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृत|धृतः
धृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Possessed, held, contained.<BR>	 2. Cherished, sup-<BR>ported.<BR>	 3. Stood, stayed, standing.<BR>	 4. Alighted, gone down.<BR>	 5.<BR>Placed.<BR>	 6. Considered, weighed.<BR> E. धृ to hold, and क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=372-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृतकार्म्मुकेषु|धृतकार्मुकेषु
धृतकार्म्मुकेषु mfn. (-षुः-षुः-षु) Armed with bow and arrow.<BR> E. धृत, कार्म्मुक a<BR>bow, and इषु an arrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=372-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृतपट
धृतपट mfn. (-टः-टा-टं) Covered or overspread with a cloth, &c.<BR> E. धृत,<BR>and पट a cloth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=372-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृतराष्ट्र|धृतराष्ट्रः
धृतराष्ट्र m. (-ष्ट्रः) A proper name; DHRITARĀSHṬRA, the father of<BR>DŪRYODHANA, and uncle of the Paṇḍu princes.<BR>	 2. A good<BR>king.<BR>	 3. A Nāgā or serpent of the lower regions.<BR>	 4. A kind of<BR>bird, perhaps a short of goose: see धार्त्तराष्ट्र.<BR>	 f. (-री) A goose, the<BR>female bird only.<BR> E. धृत possessed, cherished, (by whom,) राष्ट्र a<BR>region.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=372-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृतवत्|धृतवन्त्
धृतवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>	 1. Held, was holding, 2. Having taken or<BR>conveyed. धृ to hold, क्तवतु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=372-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृतहेति
धृतहेति mfn. (-तिः-तिः-ति) Armed.<BR> E. धृत, and हेति a weapon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=372-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृतात्मन्
धृतात्मन् mfn. (-त्मा-त्मा-त्म) Firm, steady, calm, collected.<BR> E. धृत, and आत्मन्<BR>self.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=372-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृताम्भस्
धृताम्भस् mfn. (-म्भाः-म्भाः-म्भः) Full of water.<BR> E. धृत, and अम्भस् water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=372-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृति|धृतिः
धृति m. (-तिः) Sacrifice, offering, religious rite or ceremony.<BR>	 f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1.<BR>Holding, having.<BR>	 2. Steadiness, firmness.<BR>	 3. One of the astrological Yogas, see योग.<BR>4. Pleasure.<BR>	 5. Satisfaction, content.<BR>	 6.<BR>Happiness.<BR>	 7. A metre; a stanza of four lines of eighteen syllables each.<BR>8. The thirteenth Mātṛkā<BR> E. धृ to have &c. affix<BR>क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=372-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृतिमत्|धृतिमन्त्
धृतिमत् mfn. (-मान्-मती-मत्)<BR>	 1. Firm, steady, calm.<BR>	 2. content<BR> E. धृति, and<BR>मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=373-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृतिमुष्
धृतिमुष् mfn. (-मुट्) Discomposing, agitating.<BR> E. धृति firmness, and मुष्<BR>what steals.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=373-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृत्वन्
धृत्वन् m. (-त्वा)<BR>	 1. Virtue, morality.<BR>	 2. A Brāhman.<BR>	 3. The sea.<BR>	 4. The<BR>sky.<BR>	 5. A clever man 6. A name of VIṢṆU.<BR> E. धृ to hold, क्वनिप्<BR>affix, तुक् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=373-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृत्वरी
धृत्वरी f. (-री) The earth.<BR> E. धृ to hold, क्वरप् affix, and तुक् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=373-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृत्वा
धृत्वा ind. Having taken or held.<BR> E. धृ, and क्ता aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=373-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृष
धृष r. 5th cl. (ञि आ) ञिधृषा (धृष्णोति) To be proud, to be confident or<BR>presumptuous. r. 1st and 10th cls. (धर्षति धर्षयतिते) To overcome, to<BR>overbear, to resist impatiently, to be impatient. (उ) धृषु r. 1st cl.<BR>(धर्षति)<BR>	 1. To collect.<BR>	 2. To hurt or kill. (ङ) धृषङ् r. 10th cl.<BR>(धर्षयते) To neutralise, paralyse or make powerless. प्रागल्भ्ये स्वा०<BR>प० अक० सेट् । संहतौ अक० हिंसे सक० भ्वा० प० सेट् । क्रोधे अभिभवे च वा<BR>चुरा उभ० पक्षे भ्वा० प० सक० सेट् । सामर्थ्यबन्धने चुरा० आत्म० अक० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=373-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृषु|धृषुः
धृषु mfn. (-षुः-षुः-षु)<BR>	 1. A clever man.<BR>	 2. A proud one.<BR>	 3. A heap.<BR> E. धृष्<BR>to be confident. Unādi affix कु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=373-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृष्ट|धृष्टः
धृष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>	 1. Impudent, confident, bold, shameless.<BR>	 2. For-<BR>ward, intrusive, presumptuous.<BR>	 3. Secured, obtained.<BR>	 4. Profligate,<BR>abandoned.<BR>	 m. (-ष्टः) A faithless husband.<BR>	 f. (-ष्टा) A disloyal or un-<BR>chaste woman.<BR> E. धृष् to be confident, affix वैयात्ये क्त्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=373-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृष्णज्
धृष्णज् mfn. (-ष्णक्) Confident, impudent, shameless.<BR> E. धृष् to be confident<BR>नजिज् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=373-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृष्णि|धृष्णिः
धृष्णि m. (-ष्णिः) A ray of light.<BR> E. धृष् to be arrogant, नि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=373-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृष्णु|धृष्णुः
धृष्णु mfn. (-ष्णुः-ष्णुः-ष्णु)<BR>	 1. Confident, bold.<BR>	 2. Impudent, shameless.<BR>	 f.<BR>(-ष्णु) The branch of a bamboo.<BR> E. धृष् to be arrogant, affix क्नु ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=373-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धॄ
धॄ r. 9th cl. (धॄणाति) To be or grow old.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=373-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धे
धे r. 1st cl. (ट) धेट (धयति) also (ङ) धेङ् (धयते) To drink. भ्वा० प० सक०<BR>अनिट्० टित् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=373-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धेन|धेनः
धेन m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. The ocean.<BR>	 2. A male river.<BR>	 f. (-ना) A river.<BR> E. धे to<BR>drink, Unādi affix नन्-इच्च; what is drunk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=373-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धेनु|धेनुः
धेनु f. (-नुः) A milch cow, one that has lately calved.<BR> E. धे to drink,<BR>Unādi affix नु इच्च । धयति सुतान्, धीयते पीयते वत्सैर्वा ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=373-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धेनुक|धेनुकः
धेनुक m. (-कः) The name of an Asura or demon, killed by KṚṢṆA.<BR>f. (-का)<BR>	 1. A she-elephant.<BR>	 2. A milch cow.<BR> E. धेनु a cow and<BR>कन् aff. धेनुरिव “इवे प्रतिकृतौ” पा-कन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=373-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धेनुकसूदन|धेनुकसूदनः
धेनुकसूदन m. (-नः) A name of KṚṢṆA.<BR> E. धेनुक a demon, so called,<BR>and सूदन the destroyer, also similar compounds, as धेनुकहन्, धेनुकारि<BR>&c. सूदि-ल्यु ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=373-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धेनुकादुग्ध
धेनुकादुग्ध n. (-ग्धं)<BR>	 1. Cow's milk.<BR>	 2. A plant: see चिर्भिट<BR> E. धेनुका and<BR>दुग्ध milk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=373-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धेनुकारि
धेनुकारि m. (-रिः)<BR>	 1. KṚṢṆA.<BR>	 2. small tree, Nageshwar.<BR> E. धेनुक,<BR>and अरि a foe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=373-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धेनुष्या
धेनुष्या f. (-ष्या) A cow at the dairy or tied up to be milked.<BR> E. धेनु a<BR>milch cow, यत् affix, and षुक् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=373-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धेय
धेय mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>	 1. To be held.<BR>	 2. Denominated, called.<BR> E. धा to<BR>have, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=373-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धैनुक|धैनुकं
धैनुक n. (-कं) A herd of milch cows.<BR> E. धेनुका a milch cow, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=373-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धैर्य्य|धैर्य|धैर्यं|धैर्य्यं
धैर्य्य n. (-र्य्यं) Steadiness, firmness.<BR> E. धीर firm. ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=373-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धैर्य्यकलित|धैर्यकलित
धैर्य्यकलित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Steady, calm, assuming firmness or composure<BR>E. धैर्य्य and कलित made.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=373-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धैवत|धैवतः
धैवत m. (-तः) The sixth note of the gamut.<BR> E. धी intellect, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=373-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धोड|धोडः
धोड m. (-डः) A sort of snake, commonly called Dhonra, a kind of<BR>water-snake.<BR> E. धू to make tremble, ड aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=373-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धोर
धोर (ऋ) धोरृ r. 1st cl. (धोरति) To move well, to be quick or alert,<BR>or to have good paces. गतौ सक० चातुर्य्ये अक० भ्वा० प० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=373-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धोरण|धोरणं
धोरण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. A vehicle in general, any means of conveyance, as a<BR>horse, an elephant, a car, &c. A horse's trot.<BR>	 2. Going well or<BR>quickly.<BR> E. धोर् to move well or quickly, affix करणे भावे वा ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=373-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धोरणि|धोरणिः
धोरणि f. (-णिः) Tradition.<BR> E. धोर् to proceed, affix अनि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=373-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धोरित|धोरितं
धोरित n. (-तं) A horse's trot.<BR> E. धोर to go well, affix भावे क्त; also with<BR>कन् added, धोरितक n. (-कं) and with अण् again added, धौरितक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=373-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धौत|धौतं
धौत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Washed, cleaned, purified.<BR>	 2. Bright and shin-<BR>ing.<BR>	 3. White.<BR>	 n. (-तं) Silver.<BR> E. धाव् to make clean, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=373-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धौतकट|धौतकटः
धौतकट m. (-टः) A bag of coarse cloth, a sack.<BR> E. धौत washed and<BR>कट mat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=373-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धौतकोषज|धौतकोषजं
धौतकोषज n. (-जं) Bleached or wild silk.<BR> E. धौत pure or washed, कोष the<BR>cocoon, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=373-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धौतकौशेय|धौतकौशेयं
धौतकौशेय n. (-यं) Bleached or wild silk.<BR> E. धौत pure or washed, कोश a<BR>cocoon, and ढक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=373-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धौतशिल|धौतशिलं
धौतशिल n. (-लं) Crystal.<BR> E. धौत pure, शिला a stone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=373-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धौमक|धौमकः
धौमक m. (-कः) The name of a district.<BR> E. धूम smoke, वुञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=373-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धौरितक|धौरितकं
धौरितक n. (-कं) A horse's trot: see धोरितक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=373-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धौरेय|धौरेयः
धौरेय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Fit for burthen, capable of taking or bearing it,<BR>(either a vehicle or a beast. &c.) m, (-यः)<BR>	 1. A beast of burthen.<BR>2. A horse.<BR> E. धूर् a burthen, ढक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=373-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धौर्त्तिक|धौर्तिक|धौर्तिकं|धौर्त्तिकं
धौर्त्तिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Belonging to a cheat, knavish, fraudulent<BR>&c.<BR>	 n. (-कं) Fraud, dishonesty.<BR> E. धूर्त्त cheat, ठन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=373-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धौर्य्य|धौर्य|धौर्यं|धौर्य्यं
धौर्य्य n. (-र्य्यं) A horse's trot.<BR> E. धोर् to go well, affix ण्यत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=373-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्मा
ध्मा r. 1st cl. (धमति)<BR>	 1. To blow, as a wind instrument, to produce<BR>sound by blowing.<BR>	 2. To blow a fire, to excite fire by blowing.<BR>3. To apply fire.<BR>	 4. To excite sparks. अग्निसंयुतौ दीर्घश्वासहेतुके शब्द-<BR>भेदे अक० तादृशशब्देन वादने सक० भ्वा० प० अनिट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=373-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्माकार|ध्माकारः
ध्माकार m. (-रः) A blacksmith.<BR> E. ध्मा blowing, from ध्मा to blow, affix<BR>कर्त्तरि अण् and कार who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=373-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्माक्ष
ध्माक्ष (इ) r. 1st cl. (ध्मांक्षति)<BR>	 1. To desire.<BR>	 2. To crow or caw: see ध्राक्ष and<BR>ध्वाक्ष । आकाङ्क्षे सक०, धोररवे अक०, भ्वा० प० सेट् इदित् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=373-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्माक्ष
ध्माक्ष m. (-क्षः)<BR>	 1. Any aquatic bird.<BR>	 2. A crow, &c.<BR> E. ध्माक्ष् to crow or<BR>caw, अच् affix; more usually read ध्वाङ्क्ष, q. v. also read ध्वाक्ष ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=373-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्मात
ध्मात(-तः-ता-तं) 1. Inflamed, excited.<BR>	 2. Blown into or up, inflated.<BR>	 3.<BR>Blown by a bellows, (a fire, &c.)<BR> E. ध्मा to blow, &c. affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=373-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्मामन्
ध्मामन् m. (-मा)<BR>	 1. Measure.<BR>	 2. Light.<BR>	 3. Meditation.<BR> E. ध्मा to blow or<BR>breathe, Unādi affix मनिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=373-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्मायमान
ध्मायमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>	 1. Being melted or refined.<BR>	 2. Being inflated.<BR>E. ध्मा to blow, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=373-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्यात|ध्यातं
ध्यात mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Thought, meditated.<BR> E. ध्यै to meditate affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=373-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्यातव्य
ध्यातव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं) To be thought or reflected upon.<BR> E. ध्यै to think,<BR>तव्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=373-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्यान|ध्यानं
ध्यान n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Meditation, reflection, but especially that profound<BR>and abstract consideration which brings its object fully and un-<BR>disturbedly before the mind.<BR>	 2. Mental representation of the per-<BR>sonal attributes of the divinity to whom worship is addressed. E.<BR>ध्यै to meditate, affix भावे ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=373-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्यानयोग|ध्यानयोगः
ध्यानयोग n. (-गं) The performance of religious abstraction.<BR> E. ध्यान medi-<BR>tation, &c. योग a religious observance. ध्यानमेव योगः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=373-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्यानपर
ध्यानपर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Meditating, reflecting.<BR> E. ध्यान, and पर engaged<BR>in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=373-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्यानतत्पर
ध्यानतत्पर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Reflecting.<BR> E. ध्यान, and तत्पर absorbed in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=373-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्यानीय
ध्यानीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) To be meditated upon.<BR> E. ध्यै to think, and<BR>अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=373-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्याम|ध्यामं
ध्याम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं) Black.<BR>	 n. (-मं)<BR>	 1. A fragrant grass.<BR>	 2. A plant,<BR>(Artemisia.)<BR> E. ध्यै to think, कर्मणि मन् aff. गन्धतृणे, मदनवृक्षे, रोहिष-<BR>तृणेच ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=373-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्यामन्
ध्यामन् n. (-म) Meditation.<BR>	 m. (-मा) Measure.<BR> E. ध्यै to meditate, and भावे<BR>मनिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=373-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्याममूर्द्धज
ध्याममूर्द्धज mfn. (-जः-जा-जं) Having dishevelled hair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=373-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्यायत्
ध्यायत् mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्) Thinking of, meditating upon.<BR> E. ध्यै to think, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=373-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्येय|ध्येयः
ध्येय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) To be meditated or pondered.<BR> E. ध्यै to meditate,<BR>कर्मणि यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=373-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्यै
ध्यै r. 1st cl. (ध्यायति) To recollect, to call to mind, to meditate, to<BR>think; with the preposition नि, to see, to look, to look out for.<BR>भ्वा० प० सक० अनिट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=374-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्रज
ध्रज r. 1st cl. (ध्रजति) To go; also (इ) ध्रञ्जि r. 1st cl. (ध्रंजति) To go or<BR>move. भ्वा० प० सक० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=374-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्रण
ध्रण r. 1st cl. (ध्रणति) To sound, as a drum or other instrument. भ्वा० प०<BR>अक० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=374-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्रस
ध्रस r. 1st cl. (ध्रसयति) To throw or toss up. (उ) उध्रस r. 9th cl. (ध्रस्नाति)<BR>To glean: the root is by some authorities read उध्रस । चुरा० उभ०<BR>सक० सेट् । कणश आदाने क्य्रादि० पर० सक० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=374-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्राक्ष
ध्राक्ष (इ) ध्राक्षि r. 1st cl. (ध्रांक्षति)<BR>	 1. To utter the sound of birds or to<BR>crow, caw, &c.<BR>	 2. To desire: see ध्वाक्ष भ्वा० प० सक० सेट् इदित् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=374-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्राख
ध्राख (ऋ) ध्राखृ r. 1st cl. (ध्राखति)<BR>	 1. To be dry or arid.<BR>	 2. To adorn.<BR>	 3. To<BR>suffice, to be able or competent.<BR>	 4. To refuse, to prevent. भ्वा० प०<BR>सक० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=374-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्राघ
ध्राघ r. (ऋ) धघृ r. 1st cl. (ध्राघते) To be able or competent. भ्वा० आ० अक० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=374-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्राजि|ध्राजिः
ध्राजि f. (-जिः) A whirlwind, a gale.<BR> E. ध्रज् to go, मतौ वा भावे इन् Unādi<BR>affix, and the radical vowel made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=374-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्राड
ध्राड (ऋ) ध्राडृ r. 1st cl. (ध्राडति-ते) To divide, to split, to cut or pierce. भ्वा०<BR>आत्म० सक० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=374-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्राडि|ध्राडिः
ध्राडि m. (-डिः) gathering flowers.<BR> E. ध्राड् to divide, affix इन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=374-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृज
धृज r. 1st cl. (ध्रेजति) To go or move. भ्वा० प० सक० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=374-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्रियमाण
ध्रियमाण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>	 1. Being held or sustained.<BR>	 2. Being with-<BR>held, checked, suppressed, &c.<BR> E. धृ to hold, passive v. शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=374-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्रु
ध्रु r. 1st cl. (ध्रुवति) r. 6th cl. (ध्रुवति)<BR>	 1. To be firm or fixed.<BR>	 2. To go or<BR>move. गतौ भ्वा० प० अनिट् । तुदा० कु० प० अनिट् । स्थैर्य्ये अक० सर्पणे सक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=374-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्रुव|ध्रुवं|ध्रुवः
ध्रुव r. 6th cl. (ध्रुवति)<BR>	 1. To stand, firm.<BR>	 2. To go or move. ध्रु अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=374-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्रुव|ध्रुवं|ध्रुवः
ध्रुव mfn. (-वः-वा-वं)<BR>	 1. External.<BR>	 2. Fixed, stable, firm.<BR>	 3. Continual,<BR>permanent.<BR>	 4. Certain, ascertained.<BR>	 5. Spread, extended.<BR>	 m. (-वः)<BR>	 1.<BR>A name of BRAMHĀ.<BR>	 2. ŚIVA.<BR>	 3. VIṢṆU.<BR>	 4. The polar star or<BR>north pole itself; in mythology, personified by DHRUVA, the son of<BR>UTTĀNAPĀDA, and grandson of the first MANU.<BR>	 5. The pole of<BR>any great circle, particularly either of the celestial poles.<BR>	 6. (In<BR>Astronomy,) The distance of a planet from the beginning of the<BR>sydereal zodiac.<BR>	 7. Any epoch to which a computation of dates is<BR>referred.<BR>	 8. One of the demi-gods called VASUS.<BR>	 9. The trunk of a<BR>lopped tree.<BR>	 10. The Indian fig tree, (Ficus Indica.)<BR>	 11. One of the<BR>twenty-seven astronomical Yogas, or the Yoga star of the twelfth<BR>lunar asterism, supposed to be Leonis.<BR>	 12. A sort of bird: see<BR>शराटि.<BR>	 n. (-वं)<BR>	 1. Ascertainment, certainty.<BR>	 2. Logic, reasoning,<BR>discussion.<BR>	 3. Heaven.<BR>	 f. (-वा)<BR>	 1. A sacrificial vase made in the<BR>shape of the Indian fig leaf, and of the wood of the Flacourtia<BR>sapida.<BR>	 2. A plant, (Hedysarum gangeticum.)<BR>	 3. A small tree from<BR>the fibres of which bow strings are made: see मूर्ब्बा.<BR>	 4. The intro-<BR>ductory stanza of a song: it is distinct form the verses of the song,<BR>after each of which it is again repeated as a burden or chorus.<BR>	 5.<BR>A virtuous woman.<BR> E. ध्रु to be fixed affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=374-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्रुवक|ध्रुवकः
ध्रुवक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. The trunk of a lopped tree.<BR>	 2. Longitude.<BR>	 f. (-का) The<BR>introductory stanza and burden of a song: see ध्रुवा<BR> E. कन् added to<BR>the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=374-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्रू
ध्रू r. 6th cl. (ध्रुवति)<BR>	 1. To be firm, to stand fast.<BR>	 2. To go or move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=374-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्रेक
ध्रेक (ऋ) ध्रेकृ r. 1st cl. (ध्रेकते)<BR>	 1. To sound.<BR>	 2. To grow or increase.<BR>	 3.<BR>To be exhilarated or elevated with joy.<BR>	 4. To manifest elevation or<BR>hilarity by noise. भ्वा० आ० अक० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=374-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्रै
ध्रै r. 1st cl. (ध्रायति) To be satisfied or pleased. भ्वा० प० अक० अनिट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=374-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्रौव्य|ध्रौव्यं
ध्रौव्य n. (-व्यं) Firmness, fixedness.<BR>	 2. Duration.<BR> E. ध्रुव and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=374-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वंस|ध्वंसः
ध्वंस (उ) ध्वंसु r. 1st cl. (ध्वंसते)<BR>	 1. To fall down.<BR>	 2. To reduce to powder.<BR>3. To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=374-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वंस|ध्वंसः
ध्वंस m. (-सः) Loss, destruction.<BR>	 f. (-सी) A mote in a sun-beam.<BR> E. ध्वंस<BR>to fall, affix भावे घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=374-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वंसन|ध्वंसनं
ध्वंसन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Perishing, dying.<BR>	 2. Loss, destruction.<BR>	 3. Going.<BR>	 4.<BR>Falling.<BR> E. ध्वंस to fall down, affix भावे ल्युट् । णिच्-ल्यु ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=374-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वंसित
ध्वंसित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Lost, destroyed.<BR>	 2. Vexed, incensed.<BR> E. ध्वंस to<BR>fall down, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=374-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वंसिन्
ध्वंसिन् mfn. (-सी-सिनी-सि)<BR>	 1. Destructive, destroying, 2. Suffering loss,<BR>perishing.<BR>	 m. (-सी) A Pilu tree, said to grow in mountainous dis-<BR>tricts.<BR> E. ध्वंस to fall, and णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=374-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वज|ध्वजः
ध्वज r. 1st cl. (ध्वजति) also (इ) ध्वजि r. 1st cl. (ध्वंजति) To go, to move.<BR>भ्व० पर० सक० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=374-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वज|ध्वजः
ध्वज mn. (-जः-जं)<BR>	 1. A flag or banner.<BR>	 2. A mark, a sign or symbol.<BR>3. The penis.<BR>	 4. The upper part of a skull carried on a stick, as<BR>a penance for the murder of a Brāhman.<BR>	 5. A house situated to<BR>the east of any object.<BR>	 6. A flag-staff.<BR>	 7. (In Prosody,) An Iam-<BR>bic.<BR>	 m. (-जः)<BR>	 1. A distiller.<BR>	 2. Pride.<BR>	 3. Hypocrisy, fraud.<BR> E. ध्वज<BR>to go, affix अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=374-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वजद्रुम|ध्वजद्रुमः
ध्वजद्रुम m. (-मः) The palm tree.<BR> E. ध्वज a banner, द्रुम a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=374-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वजप्रहरण|ध्वजप्रहरणः
ध्वजप्रहरण m. (-णः) Air or wind.<BR> E. ध्वज a flag, and प्रहरण who seizes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=374-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वजभङ्ग|ध्वजभङ्गः
ध्वजभङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>	 1. Impotence.<BR>	 2. Fracture or fall of a banner<BR> E. ध्वज,<BR>and भङ्ग breaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=374-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वजवत्|ध्वजवन्त्
ध्वजवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Having a mark or sign.<BR>	 m. (-वान्)<BR>	 1. An en-<BR>sign, astandard-bearer.<BR>	 2. A distiller, a vender of spirituous liquors.<BR>3. A Brāhman who having slain another carries the skull of the<BR>murdered man with him to places of pilgrimage by way of pen-<BR>ance. E.<BR> E. ध्वज as above, मतुप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=374-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वजराजिन्
ध्वजराजिन् mfn. (-जी-जिनी-जि) Bearing or displaying ensigns.<BR> E. ध्वज,<BR>and राज् to shine, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=374-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वजांशुक
ध्वजांशुक m. (-कः) A flag.<BR> E. ध्वज, and अंशुक a cloth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=374-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वजिन्
ध्वजिन् mfn. (-जी-जिनी-जि) Having a flag or sign, &c.<BR>	 m. (-जी)<BR>	 1. A<BR>Brāhman.<BR>	 2. A mountain.<BR>	 3. A car or carriage.<BR>	 4. A snake.<BR>	 5. A<BR>horse.<BR>	 6. A peacock.<BR>	 7. A distiller or vender of spirituous liquors.<BR>8. A standard bearer.<BR>	 9. An armiger, one having an emblem or<BR>sign.<BR>	 f. (-नी) An army.<BR> E. ध्वज symbol, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=374-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वजीकरण|ध्वजीकरणं
ध्वजीकरण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Raising a standard.<BR>	 2. Taking an emblem &c.<BR>	 3.<BR>Making any thing a plea or setting up as a claim or right.<BR> E. ध्वज,<BR>and करण making, च्वि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=374-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वजोत्थान|ध्वजोत्थानं
ध्वजोत्थान n. (-नं) The twelfth day of the light half of Bhādra, a festival<BR>in honour of INDRA.<BR> E. ध्वज a flag, and उत्थान elevating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=374-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वण
ध्वण r. 1st cl. (ध्वणति) To sound. भ्वा० अक० पर० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=374-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वन|ध्वनः
ध्वन r. 1st cl. (ध्वनति) r. 10th cl. (ध्वनयति-ते ध्वानयति) To sound. भ्वा० प०<BR>अक० सेट् । अद-चुरा० उभ० सक० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=374-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वन|ध्वनः
ध्वन m. (-नः) Sound<BR> E. ध्वन् to sound, अच् affix: see ध्वान ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=374-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वनत्
ध्वनत् mfn. (-नन्-नन्ती-नत्) Sounding, making a noise.<BR> E. ध्वन् sound,<BR>शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=374-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वनमोदिन्
ध्वनमोदिन् m. (-दी) The humble bee.<BR> E. ध्वन sound, and मोदिन् who<BR>delights.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=374-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वनयत्|ध्वनयन्त्
ध्वनयत् mfn. (-यन्-यन्तो-यत्) Sounding, resounding, echoing with.<BR> E. ध्वन्<BR>to sound, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=374-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वनि|ध्वनिः
ध्वनि m. (-निः)<BR>	 1. Sound.<BR>	 2. Figurative or poetical style.<BR>	 3. The sound<BR>of a drum.<BR> E. ध्वन् to sound, इन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=374-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वनिग्रह|ध्वनिग्रहः
ध्वनिग्रह m. (-हः)<BR>	 1. The ear.<BR>	 2. Hearing.<BR> E. ध्वनि sound, ग्रह the<BR>recipient.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=374-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वनित|ध्वनितः
ध्वनित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Sounded, making a noise, as a drum, &c.<BR>	 2.<BR>Poetical, figurative, rhetorically expressed.<BR> E. ध्वन् to sound,<BR>affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=374-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वनिनाला
ध्वनिनाला f. (-ला)<BR>	 1. The Vina or lute.<BR>	 2. A pipe, a fife.<BR>	 3. A sort of<BR>trumpet.<BR> E. ध्वनि sound, and नाला a hollow tube.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=374-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वनिविकार|ध्वनिविकारः
ध्वनिविकार m. (-रः) Change of voice, through fear, grief, &c.<BR> E. ध्वनि<BR>sound, विकार change.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=374-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वस्त|ध्वस्तं
ध्वस्त mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं)<BR>	 1. Fallen, 2. Destroyed, perished, lost.<BR> E. ध्वंस to<BR>fall, affix कर्त्तरि क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=374-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वाक्ष
ध्वाक्ष (इ) ध्वाक्षि r. 1st cl. (ध्वांक्षति)<BR>	 1. To utter a cry peculiar to birds,<BR>as to croke, caw, &c.<BR>	 2. To desire. भ्वा० प० सक० सेट० इदित् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=375-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वाङ्क्ष|ध्वांक्ष|ध्वांक्षः|ध्वाङ्क्षः
ध्वाङ्क्ष m. (-ङ्क्षः)<BR>	 1. Any aquatic bird, as a crane, a gull, &c. feeding<BR>upon fish.<BR>	 2. crow.<BR>	 3. One of the Nāgas.<BR>	 4. A beggar.<BR>	 f. (-ङ्क्षी)<BR>	 1. A<BR>drug: see काकोली.<BR>	 2. A female imp or fiend.<BR> E. ध्वाङ्क्ष to cry. affix<BR>अच्; it and its derivatives, may also be read ध्माक्ष, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=375-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वाङ्क्षपुष्ट|ध्वांक्षपुष्ट|ध्वाङ्क्षपुष्टः
ध्वाङ्क्षपुष्ट m. (-ष्टः) The Kokila or Indian cuckoo.<BR> E. ध्वाङ्क्ष a crow, and पुष्ट<BR>fostered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=375-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वाङ्क्षराविन्
ध्वाङ्क्षराविन् mfn. (-वी-विनी-वि) Having a voice like a crow.<BR> E. ध्वाङ्क्ष a crow,<BR>and रव sound, affix णिनि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=375-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वाङ्क्षाराति|ध्वांक्षाराति|ध्वाङ्क्षारातिः
ध्वाङ्क्षाराति m. (-तिः) An owl.<BR> E. ध्वाङ्क्ष a crow, and अराति an enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=375-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वाङ्क्षाली
ध्वाङ्क्षाली f. (-ली) A medicinal plant: see काकोली.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=375-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वान|ध्वानः
ध्वान m. (-नः) Sound in general<BR> E. ध्वन् to sound, भावे घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=375-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वान्त|ध्वांत|ध्वांतं|ध्वान्तं
ध्वान्त n. (-न्तं) Darkness.<BR> E. ध्वन् to sound, क्त affix deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=375-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वान्तवित्त|ध्वांतवित्त|ध्वान्तवित्तः
ध्वान्तवित्त m. (-त्तः) The fire-fly.<BR> E. ध्वान्त darkness, and वित्त wealth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=375-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वान्तशात्रव|ध्वांतशात्रव|ध्वान्तशात्रवः
ध्वान्तशात्रव m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. A sort of Cassia, (C. fistula)<BR>	 2. The sun or any<BR>luminous body.<BR> E. ध्वान्त darkness, and शात्रव averse to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=375-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वान्ताराति|ध्वान्तारातिः
ध्वान्ताराति m. (-तिः) The sun or any luminous body.<BR> E. ध्वान्त darkness,<BR>and अराति an enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=375-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वान्तोन्मेष|ध्वांतोन्मेष|ध्वान्तोन्मेषः
ध्वान्तोन्मेष m. (-षः) The fire-fly.<BR> E. ध्वान्त darkness, and उन्मेष twinkling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=375-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वृ
ध्वृ r. 1st cl. (ध्वरति)<BR>	 1. To bend, to make crooked.<BR>	 2. To kill.<BR>	 3. To<BR>describe. भ्वा० पर० अक० अनिट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=375-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न|नं|नः
न The twentieth consonant of the Deva Nāgri Alphābet, correspon-<BR>ding with the letter N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=375-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न|नं|नः
न mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>	 1. Thin, spare.<BR>	 2. Vacant, empty.<BR>	 3. Identical, same,<BR>like.<BR>	 4. Unvexed, unwearied 5. Undivided, unbroken.<BR>	 m. (नः)<BR>	 1. A<BR>Bauddha, a follower of Buddha.<BR>	 2. Binding, tying.<BR>	 3. One who<BR>is praised.<BR>	 4. A name of GANESA.<BR>	 5. War.<BR>	 6. Giving, a gift.<BR>	 7.<BR>Good, welfare, prosperity.<BR>	 8. A jewel.<BR>	 f. (ना)<BR>	 1. The navel.<BR>	 2. A<BR>musical instrument.<BR>	 3. Knowledge. ind.<BR>	 1. No, not, a particle of<BR>prohibition.<BR>	 2. A particle of comparison.<BR>	 3. A particle of negation,<BR>annihilation, &c.<BR> E. नी to obtain, or नह् to bind, &c. ड aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=375-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नःक्षुद्र|नःक्षुद्रः
नःक्षुद्र mfn. (-द्रः-द्रा-द्रं) Small-nosed.<BR> E. नस् the nose, क्षुद्र small.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=375-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नंशुक|नंशुकः
नंशुक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Injurious, destructive.<BR> E. नश् to destroy, णुकन्<BR>Unādi affix and नुम् inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=375-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नंष्टृ
नंष्टृ mfn. (-ष्टा-ष्ट्री-ष्टृ) An injurious, destructive. नश् to destroy, affix<BR>तृच् and नुम् inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=375-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नकुट|नकुटं
नकुट n. (-टं) The nose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=375-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नकुल|नकुलः
नकुल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Disgraced, rejected from a family or race.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-लः)<BR>	 1. The Bengal mungoose, (Viverra ichneumon)<BR>	 2. A proper<BR>name, NAKULA, the fourth of the five Pāṇḍu princes.<BR>	 3. A son.<BR>4. A name of ŚIVA.<BR>	 f. (-ली)<BR>	 1. Silk cotton tree, 2. Indian spikenard.<BR>3. A sort of perfume: see शङ्क्षिनी. Saffron.<BR>	 4. The letter ह as used<BR>in the Tantras.<BR> E. न not, कुल race or heap, fem. affix ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=375-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नकुलेश|नकुलेशः
नकुलेश m. (-शः)<BR>	 1. A Bhairava, an attendant on or emanation from<BR>ŚIVA.<BR>	 2. The letter ह as used mystically in Tantras.<BR> E. नकुल, and<BR>ईश master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=375-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नकुलेष्टा
नकुलेष्टा f. (-ष्टा) A plant: see रास्ना.<BR> E. नकुल an ichneumon, and इष्ट wished;<BR>the mungoose, if wounded in a conflict with a poisonous snake, is<BR>supposed to prevent the effects of the venom by the use of this<BR>plant; also नकुलेष्टका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=375-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नक्क
नक्क r. 10th cl. (नक्कयति-ते) To destroy or annihilate. चुरा० उभ० सक० सेट्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=375-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नक्त|नक्तं
नक्त n. (-क्तं) Night.<BR> E. नज् to be ashamed, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=375-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नक्तक|नक्तकः
नक्तक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. Dirty or ragged cloth.<BR>	 2. A rag, a wiper, a hand-<BR>kerchief, &c.<BR> E. नज् to be ashamed or modest, affix तन् and कन्<BR>added; also लक्तक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=375-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नक्तचारिन्
नक्तचारिन् mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि) Going or moving about at night.<BR>	 m. (-री)<BR>1. A cat.<BR>	 2. An owl.<BR>	 3. A goblin.<BR>	 4. A thief.<BR> E. नक्त by night, चर्<BR>to go, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=375-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नक्तञ्चर|नक्तंचर|नक्तञ्चरः
नक्तञ्चर mfn. (-रः-री-रं) Going at night.<BR>	 m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A goblin, a demon.<BR>2. A tree, the Bdellium tree: see गुग्गुल.<BR>	 3. An owl, 4. A thief. E.<BR>नक्त by night, and चर who goes. नक्तं रात्रौ चरति चर-ट ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=375-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नक्तभोजन
नक्तभोजन n. (-नं) Supper.<BR> E. नक्त night, भोजन food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=375-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नक्तन्
नक्तन् ind. By night, at night.<BR> E. नज् to be ashamed, तनिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=375-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नक्तमाल|नक्तमालः
नक्तमाल m. (-लः) A tree, (Galedupa arborea, Rox.)<BR> E. नक्तम् by night,<BR>अल् to ornament, आङ् prefix and अच् affix; blossoming at night.<BR>करञ्ज वृक्षे । नक्तम् आ अलति अल-अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=375-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नक्तमुखा
नक्तमुखा f. (-खा) Night.<BR> E. नक्तम् by night, उख् to produce, affix क ।<BR>नक्तव्रताङ्गं मुखमाद्यभागोऽस्याः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=375-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नक्तव्रत|नक्तव्रतं
नक्तव्रत n. (-तं)<BR>	 1. Fasting by day and eating at night.<BR> E. नक्त and व्रत vow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=375-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नक्र|नक्रं|नक्रः
नक्र n. (-क्रं) The upper timber of a door-frame.<BR>	 nf. (-क्रं-क्रा) The nose.<BR>	 f.<BR>(क्रा) A string of bees or wasps m. (-क्रः) A crocodile.<BR> E. न not, क्रम् to<BR>go affix ड. न क्रामति दूरस्थानम् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=375-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नक्रराज्
नक्रराज् m. (-राट्) or नक्रराज m. (-जः) A shark, but applied also differ-<BR>ently: see ग्राह.<BR> E. नक्र a crocodile, and राज् or राज king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=375-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नक्षत्र|नक्षत्रं
नक्षत्र n. (-त्र)<BR>	 1. A star in general.<BR>	 2. An asterism in the moon's path<BR>or lunar mansion, of which twenty-eight, distinct in name, figure,<BR>and number of stars, are enumerated; the Pourānic and popular<BR>enumeration of those constellations is twenty-seven; Abhijit, the<BR>twenty-eighth, being considered as formed of portions of the two<BR>contiguous asterisms, and not distinct from them 2. A pearl. E.<BR>नक्ष् to go, Unādi, affix अत्रन् or क्षद Sautra root, to injure, or क्षर् to<BR>drop, or क्षी to waste or decay, with the negative prefix, and ष्ट्रन्<BR>affix; deriv. irr. न क्षीयते क्षरते वा ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=375-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नक्षत्रचक्र|नक्षत्रचक्रं
नक्षत्रचक्र n. (-र्क्र)<BR>	 1. A particular diagram for astrological calculations<BR>2. The lunar asterisms collectively.<BR> E. नक्षत्र and चक्र a circle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=375-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नक्षत्रनेमि|नक्षत्रनेमिः
नक्षत्रनेमि m. (-मिः)<BR>	 1. The moon.<BR>	 2. The pole-star.<BR>	 3. VIṢṆU.<BR>	 f. (-मिः)<BR>The last of the asterisms, Revatī, containing thirty-two stars. E.<BR>नक्षत्र a star, and नेमि circumference.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=375-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नक्षत्रप|नक्षत्रपः
नक्षत्रप m. (-पः) The moon.<BR> E. नक्षत्र and प who cherishes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=375-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नक्षत्रमाला
नक्षत्रमाला f. (-ला)<BR>	 1. A necklace containing twenty-seven pearls.<BR>	 2. The<BR>table of the asterisms in the moon's path.<BR>	 3. A kind of dance. E.<BR>नक्षत्र a constellation, and माला a garland.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=375-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नक्षत्रेश|नक्षत्रेशः
नक्षत्रेश m. (-शः)<BR>	 1. The moon.<BR>	 2. Camphor.<BR> E. नक्षत्र an asterism, and<BR>ईश lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=375-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नख|नखं|नखः
नख r. 1st cl. (नखति) To move. भ्वा० पर० सक० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=375-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नख|नखं|नखः
नख mf. (-खः-खी) A fingernail.<BR>	 m. (-खः) A part, a portion.<BR>	 nf. (-खं-खी)<BR>A perfume, a dried substance, of a brown colour, and of the<BR>shape of a nail; apparently, a dried shell-fish, used as a perfume.<BR>f. (-खी) A vegetable perfume, different from the one above,<BR>though known by the same name, NAKHI.<BR> E. न privative, ख<BR>sense; or नह् to bind ख Unādi affix, the radical ह rejected. नखम्<BR>छिद्रम् अत्र ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=375-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नखकुट्ट|नखकुट्टः
नखकुट्ट m. (-ट्टः) A barber.<BR> E. नख a nail, and कुट्ट who cuts, (barbers in<BR>India trim the nails, नखं कुट्टति कुट्ट-छेदे अण् उप० स० ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=375-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नखखादिन्
नखखादिन् mfn. (-दी-दिनी-दि) Who or what eats with nails or tal-<BR>ons.<BR> E. नख, and खादिन् eating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=375-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नखदारण|नखदारणः
नखदारण m. (-णः) A falcon.<BR> E. नख a nail, and दारण tearing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=375-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नखपद
नखपद n. (-दं) A scratch, the mark of a fingernail.<BR> E. नख, and पद a mark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=375-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नखभिन्न
नखभिन्न mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं) Torn, or torn off with a nail.<BR> E. नख, and भिन्न<BR>divided.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=375-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नखमुच|नखमुचं|नखमुचः
नखमुच m. (-चः) A bow.<BR> E. नख a nail, मुच् to let loose, क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=376-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नखम्पच|नखंपच
नखम्पच mfn. (-चः-चा-चं) What scalds the nail.<BR> E. नख, and पच् to cook,<BR>खश् aff. मुम् च ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=376-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नखर|नखरं|नखरः
नखर m. (-रः) A fingernail.<BR>	 f. (-री) A perfume: see नखी.<BR> E. न not,<BR>खन् to go, and डर affix; or नख a nail, रा to go or be, affix ड. or<BR>नखं-राति-रा + क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=376-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नखरञ्जनी|नखरंजनी
नखरञ्जनी f. (-नी) A nail-parer.<BR> E. नख, and रञ्जनी beautifying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=376-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नखरायुध|नखरायुधः
नखरायुध m. (-धः)<BR>	 1. A lion.<BR>	 2. Any beast of prey.<BR>	 3. A cook.<BR> E. नखर<BR>a nail, आयुध a weapon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=376-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नखलेखा
नखलेखा f. (-खा) A scratch<BR> E. नख, and लेखा a line.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=376-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नखविलेख
नखविलेख m. (-खः) A scratch.<BR> E. नख, and विलेखा a mark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=376-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नखविष्किर|नखविष्किरः
नखविष्किर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) What tears or rends, (as a bird of prey, &c.)<BR>E. नख, and विष्किर what scatters.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=376-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नखव्रण|नखव्रणः
नखव्रण n. (-णं) A scratch.<BR> E. नख, and व्रण a wound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=376-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नखशङ्ख|नखशंख|नखशङ्खः
नखशङ्ख m. (-ङ्खः) A small shell.<BR> E. नख a nail, शङ्ख a shell, one as small<BR>as a nail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=376-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नखांशु
नखांशु m. (-शुः) Elegance of the fingernails.<BR> E. नख, and अंशु a ray.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=376-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नखाङ्क|नखांक|नखाङ्कं|नखाङ्कः
नखाङ्क m. (-ङ्कः)<BR>	 1. A scratch, a mark of the nail.<BR>	 2. A sort of perfume.<BR>E. नख a nail, and अङ्क a mark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=376-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नखायुध|नखायुधः
नखायुध m. (-धः)<BR>	 1. A tiger.<BR>	 2. A lion.<BR>	 3. A cock.<BR>	 4. Any beast or bird<BR>having talons.<BR> E. नख, and आयुध a weapon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=376-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नखालि|नखालिः
नखालि m. (-लिः) A small.<BR> E. नख a nail, and आलि a line; also नखालिका<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=376-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नखाशिन्
नखाशिन् m. (-शी) An owl.<BR> E. नख a nail, and अशिन् who eats, using its<BR>claws in feeding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=376-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नखिन्
नखिन् mfn. (-खी-खिनी-खि) Nailed, clawed, having nails or talons. E.<BR>नख, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=376-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नग|नगः
नग m. (-गः)<BR>	 1. mountain.<BR>	 2. A tree.<BR> E. न not, गम् to go, affix ड, im-<BR>moveable; or दह् to burn, Unādi affix ग, ह rejected, and द changed<BR>to न.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=376-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नगज|नगजः
नगज mfn. (-जः-जा-जं) Mountain, mountaineer.<BR>	 m. (-जः) An elephant.<BR>E. नग a mountain, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=376-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नगणा
नगणा f. (-णा) Heart pea, (Cordiospermum halicacabum.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=376-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नगनन्दिनी|नगनंदिनी
नगनन्दिनी f. (-नी) The goddess DURGĀ.<BR> E. नग mountain, and नन्दिनी a<BR>daughter, being in one of her characters the daughter of Himā-<BR>laya, the snowy mountain personified.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=376-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नगपति|नगपतिः
नगपति m. (-तिः) Himālaya, the personified range of snowy mountains<BR>dividing India from Tārtāry, &c.<BR> E. नग mountain, and पति lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=376-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नगभिद्
नगभिद् m. (-द् or -त्)<BR>	 1. A plant, (Plectranthus scutellaroides.)<BR>	 2. An<BR>axe, a crow.<BR>	 3. INDRA.<BR> E. नग, and भिद्, what breaks. नगं भिनत्ति<BR>भिद-क्विप-६ त० स ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=376-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नगभू
नगभू mfn. (-भूः-भूः-भु) Mountain, mountaineer.<BR> E. नग, and भू born. नगे<BR>भवति-भू-क्विप् ७ त० स ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=376-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नगमूर्द्धन्
नगमूर्द्धन् m. (-र्द्धा) The crest or brow of a mountain.<BR> E. नग, and मूर्द्धन्<BR>forehead.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=376-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नगर|नगरं
नगर nf. (-रं-री) A town, a city.<BR> E. नग a tree, or according to some, a<BR>mountain, रल् affix; having trees or houses like mountains. नगा<BR>इव प्रासादाः सन्ति अत्र बा० र ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=376-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नगरघात|नगरघातः
नगरघात m. (-तः) An elephant,<BR> E. नगर a city, and घात who destroys or<BR>subverts. नगरं हन्ति अमनुष्य कर्त्तृ कत्वेन टकं बाधिन्वा अण् उप० स० । हस्तिनि<BR>हन-भावे घञ् ६ त० । नगरस्थलोकस्य हनने च ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=376-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नगरजन|नगरजनः
नगरजन m. (-नः) Towns-folk, citizen.<BR> E. नगर, and जन people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=376-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नगरस्थ|नगरस्थः
नगरस्थ mfn. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थं) City, citizen.<BR> E. नगर, and स्थ who or what stays.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=376-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नगरस्वरूपिणी
नगरस्वरूपिणी f. (-णी) A species of the Anushtubh metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=376-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नगरीवक|नगरीवकः
नगरीवक m. (-कः) A crow.<BR> E. नगरी, and वक a crane, the town-crane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=376-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नगरोपान्त|नगरोपांत|नगरोपान्तः
नगरोपान्त n. (-न्तं) Suburb, skirts of the town.<BR> E. नग, and उपान्त vicinity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=376-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नगरौषधि|नगरौषधिः
नगरौषधि (धी) f. (-धिः) The plantain.<BR> E. नगर a city, and औषधि a medica-<BR>ment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=376-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नगाटन|नगाटनः
नगाटन m. (-नः) A monkey.<BR> E. नग a mountain, अट् to go, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=376-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नगाधिप|नगाधिपः
नगाधिप m. (-पः) Himālaya; see नगपति.<BR> E. नग mountain, and अधिप a<BR>lord; also नगाधिराज, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=376-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नगाश्रय|नगाश्रयः
नगाश्रय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Living in or frequenting mountains.<BR> E. नग, and<BR>आश्रय abode. हस्तिकन्दवृक्षे, पर्वतवासिनि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=376-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नगोच्छ्राय|नगोच्छ्रायः
नगोच्छ्राय n. (-यं) The elevation of a mountain.<BR> E. नग and उच्छ्राय heighth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=376-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नगौकस्
नगौकस् m. (-काः)<BR>	 1. A bird in general 2. A lion 3. A fabulous animal:<BR>see शरभ.<BR>	 4. A crow.<BR> E. नग a tree, a mountain, and ओकस् a house<BR>or dwelling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=376-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नग्न|नग्नः
नग्न mfn. (-ग्नः-ग्ना-ग्नं) Naked.<BR>	 m. (-ग्नः)<BR>	 1. A naked mendicant.<BR>	 2. A<BR>Bauddha.<BR>	 3. A bard.<BR>	 f. (-ग्ना) A naked woman.<BR> E. नज् to be as-<BR>hamed, affix कर्त्तरि क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=376-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नग्नक|नग्नकः
नग्नक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Naked.<BR> E. कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=376-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नग्नजित्
नग्नजित् m. (-जित्) The name of a king, father of one of KṚṢṆA'S wives<BR>E. नग्न Bauddha, and जित् who conquers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=376-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नग्नत्व
नग्नत्व n. (-त्वं) Nudity, nakedness.<BR> E. त्व added to नग्न; also with तल्,<BR>नग्नता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=376-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नग्नहू
नग्नहू mn. (-हूः-हु) Ferment, a drug used to throw the mixture for<BR>spirituous liquor into fermentation.<BR> E. नग्न naked, and ह्वे to call,<BR>affix क्विप्, what is called for by the bare-faced, shameless, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=376-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नग्नाट|नग्नाटः
नग्नाट m. (-टः)<BR>	 1. A naked man, but especially a kind of religious men-<BR>dicant, who wanders about without clothes.<BR>	 2. A Bauddha.<BR>	 3. A<BR>Jain.<BR> E. नग्न naked, and अट who goes; also with कन् added नग्नाटक,<BR>नग्न एव अटति अट-अच् स्वार्थे क अट-ण्वुल् वा ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=376-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नग्निका
नग्निका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. A girl before menstruation or about ten years old.<BR>2. A naked woman.<BR> E. नग्न naked, संज्ञायां कन् added: and the fem.<BR>from, see नग्नक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=376-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नग्नीकरण
नग्नीकरण n. (-णं) Stripping, undressing.<BR> E. नग्न, and करण making, च्वि<BR>augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=376-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नग्नीकृत
नग्नीकृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Undressed, stripped, naked.<BR> E. नग्न, and कृत<BR>made, च्वि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=376-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नज
नज (ओ ई) ओनजी r. 6th cl. (नजते) also (इ, ओ) (ओनजि) r. 1st cl. (नञ्जते)<BR>To be ashamed, to be modest or bashful. तुदा० आ० अक० सेट् भ्वा०<BR>इदित् च ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=376-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नज्
नज् ind. A particle of negation, prohibition, &c. (no, not:) see अ and न ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=376-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नट|नटः
नट r. 1st and 10th cls. (नटति नाटयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To dance, to dance as an<BR>actor, to act.<BR>	 2. To drop or fall.<BR>	 3. To shake, to move slightly.<BR>	 4.<BR>To injure.<BR>	 5. To shine. भ्वा० प० चुरा० उभ० अक० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=376-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नट|नटः
नट m. (-टः)<BR>	 1. A dancer, a mime, an actor, a Nata, &c. in modern times:<BR>in caste, the son of a degraded Kṣatriya by a woman of the<BR>second caste.<BR>	 4. A sort of reed, (Arundo tibialis, or latterly called<BR>A. karka, Roxburgh's Catalogue;) also नड and नल, 5. A subordi-<BR>nate mode of music.<BR>	 f. (-टा) A sort of shrub, (Cæsalpinia bonduc-<BR>cella.)<BR>	 f. (-टी)<BR>	 1. A medicinal plant: see नली.<BR>	 2. A whore.<BR>	 3. A Nautch-<BR>girl, a dancer, an actress.<BR>	 2. Red arsenic: see नली.<BR>	 5. A Rāgini. E.<BR>नट् to dance, affixes अच्, and टाप् or ङीष्; otherwise, नश् to destroy<BR>Uṇadi affix डट, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=376-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नटन|नटनं
नटन n. (-नं) The art or act of dancing, pantomime, &c.<BR> E. नट् to dance<BR>affix भावे ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=376-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नटनारायण|नटनारायणः
नटनारायण m. (-णः) A Rāga or mode of music, according to some, the<BR>sixth, or to others, a subdivision of Dīpaka or of Megha.<BR> E. नट,<BR>and नारायण VIṢṆU: the supreme with dancers, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=376-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नटपर्ण
नटपर्ण n. (-णं) Skin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=376-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नटपत्रिका
नटपत्रिका f. (-का) The egg-plant (Solanum melongena.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=376-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नटमण्डन|नटमंडन|नटमण्डनं|नटमण्डनः
नटमण्डन m. (-नः) Yellow orpiment.<BR> E. नट an actor, and मण्डन adorning;<BR>dying theatrical raiment. नटं मण्डयति-मण्डि-ल्यु हरिताले ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=376-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नटवर|नटवरः
नटवर m. (-रः) A chief dancer or actor.<BR> E. नट, and वर best.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=376-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नटसंज्ञक
नटसंज्ञक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. Yellow orpiment, 2. An actor, a dancer, &c.<BR> E. नट<BR>an actor, संज्ञा a name, affix कन् । गोदन्ताख्यहरिताले ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=376-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नटश्रेष्ठ
नटश्रेष्ठ m. (-ष्ठः) A chief or excellent dancer or actor.<BR> E. नट, and श्रेष्ठ<BR>best.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=376-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नटान्तिका|नटांतिका
नटान्तिका f. (-का) Shame, modesty,<BR> E. टन dancing, and अन्त destroying,<BR>affixes कन् and टाप्; it is also read नटान्धिका ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=376-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नटेश्वर|नटेश्वरः
नटेश्वर m. (-रः) A name of ŚIVA,<BR> E. नट a dancer, and ईश्वर a deity, the<BR>god of the dancers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=377-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नड|नडं|नडः
नड r. 1st cl. (नडति) To be thick or impervious. r. 10th cl. (नाडयति-ते)<BR>To fall off or from. भ्रंशे भ्वा० प० चुरा० उभ० अक० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=377-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नड|नडं|नडः
नड (ल) m. (-डः or -लः)<BR>	 1. A sort of reed, (Arundo tibialis, or karka;) also<BR>नल.<BR>	 2. A particular tribe whose employment is making a sort of<BR>glass bracelets.<BR> E. नड् to be thick, affix अच् । नल वन्धे अच् वा डस्य-लः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=377-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नडकोय
नडकोय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Abounding in reeds, (a field, &c.)<BR> E. नड a reed,<BR>छ affix, and कुक् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=377-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नडप्राय|नडप्रायः
नडप्राय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Abounding in reeds.<BR> E. नड, and प्राय aboun-<BR>dance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=377-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नड|नडं|नडः
नड(ल)मीन m. (-नः) A small fish a kind of sprat haunting reedy places.<BR>E. नड a reed, and मीन a fish. “चिंडौ” मत्स्ये ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=377-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नडसंहति|नडसंहतिः
नडसंहति f. (-तिः) A quantity of reeds.<BR> E. नड, and संहति assemblage;<BR>also any analogous compound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=377-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नडह|नडहः
नडह mfn. (-हः-हा-हं) Lovely, beautiful, desirable.<BR> E. नड here said to be<BR>mental anxiety, derived form नड् to fall off or from, हन् to destroy,<BR>affix ड ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=377-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नड्या
नड्या f. (-ड्या) A quantity of reed.<BR> E. नड a reed, affix यत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=377-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नड्वन्
नड्वन् mfn. (-ड्वान्-ड्वती-ड्वत्) Reedy, abounding in reeds.<BR> E. नड, and<BR>नतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=377-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नड्वल|नड्वलः
नड्वल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Reedy, abounding in reeds.<BR> E. नड, and ड्वलच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=377-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नड्वाभू
नड्वाभू f. (-भूः) A house or hut of reeds.<BR> E. नड्व, and भू being, with आङ्<BR>prefixed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=377-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नत|नतं|नतः
नत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Bent, bowed, reclining.<BR>	 2. Crooked, curved.<BR>	 n.<BR>(-तं)<BR>	 1. The arc or distance of any planet from the Zenith.<BR>	 3. A<BR>plant or its root: see तगर and तगरमूल.<BR> E. नम् to bow or bend, affix<BR>कर्त्तरि-क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=377-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नतनाडिका
नतनाडिका f. (-का) Any hour of birth, after moon or before midnight.<BR>E. नत, and नाडिका a period of twenty-four minutes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=377-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नतनासिक|नतनासिकः
नतनासिक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Flat-nosed.<BR> E. नत bowed, and नासिक the nose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=377-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नतभाग
नतभाग m. (-गः) (In Astronomy,) Zenith distance.<BR> E. नत and भाग a part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=377-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नतभ्रु
नतभ्रु mfn. (-भ्रुः-भ्रुः-भ्रु) Frowning.<BR> E. नत, and भ्रु the brow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=377-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नतमुख
नतमुख mfn. (-खः-खी-खं) Down-faced, looking down.<BR> E. नत, and मुख the<BR>face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=377-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नतमूर्द्धन्
नतमूर्द्धन् mfn. (-र्द्धा-र्द्धा-र्द्ध) Looking down, hanging down the head.<BR> E. नत,<BR>मूर्द्धन् the forehead.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=377-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नतांश|नतांशः
नतांश n. (-र्शं) Zenith distance, (in Astronomy.)<BR> E. नत, and अंश a<BR>degree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=377-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नताङ्ग
नताङ्ग mfn. (-ङ्गः-ङ्गी-ङ्गं) Bent, curved, bowed, stooping.<BR>	 f. (-ङ्गी A woman<BR>E. नत, and अङ्ग the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=377-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नति|नतिः
नति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Bending, bowing, stooping.<BR>	 2. Curvature, crookedness.<BR>E. नम् to bow, भावे क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=377-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नत्युह
नत्युह m. (-हः) A gallinule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=377-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नद|नदः
नद r. 1st and 10th cls. (नदति, नादयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To speak or emit sound.<BR>	 2.<BR>To shine: see खद With वि and अनु, To fill with noise or sound;<BR>(दु इ,) दुनदि r. 1st cl. (नन्दति)<BR>	 1. To thrive, to be prosperous, 2.<BR>(Usually with आङ् prefixed,) To be happy, to be pleased or de-<BR>lighted. With अभि prefixed, 1. To wish for.<BR>	 2. To acknowledge or<BR>confess. With प्रति, To be thankful. भ्वा० प० सक० सेट इदित् । चुरा० ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=377-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नद|नदः
नद m. (-दः) A river, applied only to one of which the personification<BR>is male, as the Bramhaputra, Sone, Indus, &c.<BR>	 f. (-दी) A river in<BR>general; the common personification of rivers being female<BR> E. नद्<BR>to sound, affix अच्, fem. affix ङीप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=377-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नदत्|नदन्त्
नदत् mfn. (-दन्-दन्ती-दत्) Sounding, making a sound.<BR> E. नद् to sound,<BR>शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=377-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नदनदीपति
नदनदीपति m. (-तिः) The sea.<BR> E. नद, and नदी, and पति lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=377-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नदनु|नदनुः
नदनु m. (-नुः)<BR>	 1. A cloud.<BR>	 2. A lion.<BR> E. नद् to sound, अनुङ् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=377-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नदीकान्त|नदीकांत|नदीकान्तः
नदीकान्त m. (-न्तः)<BR>	 1. The ocean.<BR>	 2. A sort of tree, (Barringtonia acut-<BR>angula:) see हिज्जल.<BR>	 3. A small tree, (Vitex negundo.)<BR>	 f. (-न्ता)<BR>	 1.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=377-b" target="_blank">Page377-b+ 60</a>]<BR>A creeper.<BR>	 2. The rose apple, (Eugenia jambu.)<BR>	 3. A shrub, (Leea<BR>hirta.)<BR> E. नदी a river, कान्त loved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=377-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नदीकूल
नदीकूल n. (-लं) The bank or shore of a river.<BR> E. नदी a river, कूल a bank.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=377-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नदीकूलप्रिय|नदीकूलप्रियः
नदीकूलप्रिय m. (-यः) A short of reed, (Calamus rotang.)<BR> E. नदीकूल a river<BR>bank, and प्रिय fond of; growing on The banks of rivers. जलवेतसे<BR>जटाध० ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=377-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नदीज|नदीजं|नदीजः
नदीज mfn. (-जः-जा-जं) Aquatic, water-born.<BR>	 n. (-जं)<BR>	 1. Antimony.<BR>	 2. A<BR>lotus.<BR>	 m. (-जः)<BR>	 1. A sort of tree, (Pentaptera arjuna.)<BR>	 2. The marshy<BR>date tree.<BR>	 3. A name of BHĪṢMA.<BR> E. नदी a river, and ज born.<BR>अर्ज्जुनवृक्षे, यावनाल शरे, हिज्जलवृक्षे भीष्मे च ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=377-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नदीज्ञ
नदीज्ञ mfn. (-ज्ञः-ज्ञा-ज्ञं) One who knows the course of rivers, &c.<BR> E. नदी,<BR>and ज्ञ who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=377-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नदीतरस्थान|नदीतरस्थानं
नदीतरस्थान n. (-नं) A Ghāṭ, a landing place, a ferry.<BR> E. नदी a river,<BR>तर crossing, and स्थान place; also नदीतरस्थल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=377-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नदीतीर
नदीतीर n. (-रं) The bank of a river.<BR> E. नदी, and तीर a bank.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=377-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नदीन|नदीनः
नदीन m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. The ocean.<BR>	 2. The god of water, VARUṆA.<BR> E. नदी a<BR>river, and इन lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=377-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नदीमातृक|नदीमातृकः
नदीमातृक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Watered by rivers, (land, rice, &c.)<BR> E. नदी a<BR>river, मातृ a mother, कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=377-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नदीरय|नदीरयः
नदीरय m. (-यः) The stream or current of a river.<BR> E. नदी, and रय going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=377-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नदीवङ्क|नदीवंक|नदीवङ्कः
नदीवङ्क m. (-ङ्कः) The bend or arm of a river.<BR> E. नदी a river, and वङ्क a<BR>bend. (-वांँक ।)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=377-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नदीवेग
नदीवेग m. (-गः) The stream or current of a river.<BR> E. नदी, and वेग speed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=377-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नदीवेला
नदीवेला f. (-ला) The current or stream of a river.<BR> E. नदी, and वेला flow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=377-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नदीष्ण|नदीष्णः
नदीष्ण mfn. (-ष्णः-ष्णा-ष्णं)<BR>	 1. Bathing, &c. in a river.<BR>	 2. One who knows<BR>rivers, their depth, course, &c.<BR> E. नदी river, स्ना to bathe, ड affix;<BR>and स्न changed to ष्ण । नद्यां स्नातुं जानन्ति स्ना-क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=377-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नदीसर्ज|नदीसर्जः|नदीसर्ज्ज|नदीसर्ज्जः
नदीसर्ज m. (-र्जः) A tree, (Pentaptera arjuna.)<BR> E. नदी a river, and सर्ज<BR>the Sal tree. नद्या नृज्यते असौ सृज-कर्मणि-अप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=377-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नदेयी
नदेयी f. (-यी) A plant, (Premna herbacea, Rox.)<BR> E. नदी a river, ढक् affix;<BR>also नादेयी ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=377-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नद्ध|नद्धः
नद्ध mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>	 1. Bound, tied.<BR>	 2. Drawn up, raised.<BR> E. नह् to tye,<BR>affix कर्मणि क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=377-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नद्ध्री
नद्ध्री f. (-द्ध्री) A leather cord, a thong<BR> E. नह् to bind, करणे ष्ट्रन्-ङीप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=377-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ननन्दृ|ननंदृ
ननन्दृ f. (-न्दा) A husband's sister.<BR> E. न negative, नन्द to please, ऋत्<BR>Unādi affix; also the penultimate being made long, ननान्दृ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=377-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ननु
ननु ind.<BR>	 1. A particle of interrogation, (how, what.)<BR>	 2. Of affirmation,<BR>(certainly.)<BR>	 3. Of assent.<BR>	 4. A consolatory and kind expression.<BR>	 5.<BR>A vocative particle, (ho, hola.) or one implying kindness, concilia-<BR>tion, (pray, good friend, &c.)<BR>	 6. An inceptive particle, implying<BR>doubt or dissent, (may be, but, on the other hand.)<BR>	 7. A responsive<BR>particle.<BR>	 8. A particle of reproach.<BR> E. न negative, नुद् to send or<BR>command, affix डु ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=377-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ननुच
ननुच ind. An inceptive particle, implying doubt, dissent, or contra-<BR>diction.<BR> E. ननु as above, and च particle. अष्यय० ननु + च + स्रमा-द्व० ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=377-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्तव्य
नन्तव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं) To be saluted, to be revered or honoured.<BR> E. नम्<BR>to salute, तव्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=377-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्द|नंद|नंदः|नन्दः
नन्द mf. (-न्दः-न्दी) Happiness, pleasure, felicity.<BR>	 m. (-न्दः)<BR>	 1. One of<BR>KUVERA'S nine inestimable gems or treasure.<BR>	 2. The cow-<BR>herd NANDA, the foster father of KṚṢṆA.<BR>	 3. A name of<BR>VIṢṆU.<BR>	 4. A prince, the son of MAHĀNANDI.<BR>	 5. A flute, one<BR>eleven inches long.<BR>	 f. (-न्दा)<BR>	 1. An earthen water jar.<BR>	 2. The first,<BR>sixth, or eleventh day of the fortnight.<BR>	 3. Prosperity, increase.<BR>	 4.<BR>A husband's sister.<BR>	 f. (-न्दी) INDRA'S garden.<BR>	 f. (-न्दा or -न्दी) A name<BR>of DURGĀ.<BR> E. नदि to be prosperous or happy, affixes अच् and टाप्<BR>or भावे घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=377-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्दक|नंदक|नन्दकः
नन्दक mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>	 1. Rejoicing, making happy or delighted.<BR>	 2.<BR>Cherishing or rearing a family.<BR>	 m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. Happiness, pleasure.<BR>	 2.<BR>The sword of KṚṢṆA.<BR>	 3. The foster father of KṚṢṆA.<BR>	 4. A<BR>frog.<BR> E. नदि to make happy, affix ण्वुल् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=377-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्दकि|नंदकिः|नन्दकिः
नन्दकि f. (-किः) Long pepper.<BR> E. नन्द to delight, affix इन् वा कुक् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=378-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्दकिन्|नंदकिन्
नन्दकिन् m. (-की) KṚṢṆA.<BR> E. नन्दक, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=378-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्दगोपिता
नन्दगोपिता f. (-ता) A plant: see रास्ना ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=378-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्दथु|नंदथु|नंदथुः|नन्दथुः
नन्दथु m. (-थुः) Happiness, felicity.<BR> E. नदि to be happy, affix अथुच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=378-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्दन|नंदन|नन्दनं|नन्दनः
नन्दन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Delighting, rejoicing, making pleased or happy.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. A son.<BR>	 2. A frog.<BR>	 3. VIṢṆU.<BR>	 n. (-नं) INDRA'S pleasure<BR>ground, elysium.<BR>	 2. A species of the Dhritti metre.<BR>	 f. (-ना) A<BR>daughter.<BR> E. नदि to be or make happy, affix ल्यु ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=378-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्दनन्दन|नंदनंदन|नन्दनन्दनः
नन्दनन्दन m. (-नः) A name of KṚṢṆA.<BR> E. नन्द, and नन्दन a son; the<BR>Son of NANDA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=378-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्दनन्दनी
नन्दनन्दनी f. (-नी) A name of DURGĀ.<BR> E. नन्द the cowherd NANDA, and<BR>नन्दिनी a daughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=378-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्दन्त|नंदंत|नन्दन्तः
नन्दन्त m. (-न्तः)<BR>	 1. A son.<BR>	 2. A friend.<BR>	 3. A prince.<BR> E. नदि to make<BR>happy, झच् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=378-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्दनमाला
नन्दनमाला f. (-ला) A chaplet or garland made by KṚṢṆA.<BR> E. नन्दन<BR>delighting, माला a garland.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=378-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्दयत्
नन्दयत् mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्) Making happy, delighting.<BR> E. नदि to be<BR>happy, causal v. शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=378-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्दयन्त|नंदयंत|नन्दयन्तः
नन्दयन्त mfn. (-न्तः-न्ती-न्तं) Making happy, rejoicing, delighting.<BR> E. नदि<BR>in the causal form, with झच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=378-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्दपाल|नंदपाल|नन्दपालः
नन्दपाल m. (-लः) A name of VARUṆA<BR> E. नन्द KUVERA'S treasure, and पाल who guards.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=378-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्दपुत्री
नन्दपुत्री f. (-त्री) DURGĀ.<BR> E. नन्द the cowherd NANDA, and पुत्री a daught-<BR>er; the goddess becoming incarnate, as the infant daughter of<BR>NANDA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=378-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्दात्मज|नंदात्मज|नन्दात्मजः
नन्दात्मज m. (-जः) KṚṢṆA f. (-जा) DURGĀ as Yogamāyā.<BR> E. नन्द as<BR>above and आत्मज offspring: see नन्दनन्दन; also नन्दपुत्र, नन्दसुत, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=378-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्दि|नंदि|नंदिः|नन्दिः
नन्दि mn. (-न्दिः-न्दि)<BR>	 1. Gambling, gaming.<BR>	 2. Happiness.<BR>	 m. (-न्दिः)<BR>	 1.<BR>One of ŚIVA'S principal attendants.<BR>	 2. The speaker of the prologue<BR>or prelude to a drama.<BR>	 3. One who pronounces a benediction. E.<BR>नदि to make happy, and इन् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=378-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्दिक|नंदिक|नंदिकः|नन्दिकः
नन्दिक m. (-कः) Tun, a tree, the wood of which resembles mahogany,<BR>and is used for furniture, &c. (Cedrela tunna.)<BR>	 f. (-का)<BR>	 1. INDRA'S<BR>garden or pleasure ground.<BR>	 2. An earthen water pot.<BR>	 3. The first,<BR>sixth or eleventh day of a fortnight.<BR> E. नन्द, with कन् or ठन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=378-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्दिकेश्वर|नंदिकेश्वर|नन्दिकेश्वरः
नन्दिकेश्वर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. One of ŚIVA'S chief attendants.<BR>	 2. An inferior<BR>Purāna.<BR> E. नन्दिक INDRA'S garden, and ईश्वर master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=378-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्दिघोष|नंदिघोष|नन्दिघोषः
नन्दिघोष m. (-षः)<BR>	 1. The car of ARJUNA.<BR>	 2. The acclaim or proclam-<BR>ation of a panegyrist or herald.<BR> E. नन्दि happy, and धोष sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=378-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्दिन्|नंदिन्
नन्दिन् mfn. (-न्दी-न्दिनी-न्दि) Happy, rejoiced, delighted.<BR>	 m. (-न्दी)<BR>	 1. The<BR>name of one of ŚIVA'S chamberlains, and chief attendants.<BR>	 2. The<BR>Indian fig tree.<BR>	 3. Parspipal, (Hibiscus populneoides.)<BR>	 4. The<BR>speaker of the prelude or prologue to a drama.<BR>	 f. (-न्दिनी)<BR>	 1. A name<BR>of the goddess PĀRVATĪ.<BR>	 2. GANGĀ, the river goddess.<BR>	 3. A hus-<BR>band's sister.<BR>	 4. A fabulous cow, related to the cow of plenty, and<BR>the property of the sage VAŚISHṬHA.<BR>	 5. The Alakānanda river.<BR>6. The mother of the writer VYĀḌI.<BR> E. नन्द happiness, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=378-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्दिनीतनय|नन्दिनीतनयः
नन्दिनीतनय m. (-यः) A name of VYĀRI, author of a vocabulary.<BR> E. नन्दिनी<BR>as above, and तनय a son; also similar compounds, as नन्दिनीसुत,<BR>नन्दिनीपुत्त्र, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=378-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्दिवर्द्धन
नन्दिवर्द्धन m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. ŚIVA.<BR>	 2. The last day of either half of the month,<BR>the full or new moon.<BR>	 3. A son.<BR>	 4. A friend.<BR> E. नन्दि happiness,<BR>&c. and वर्द्धन increasing. वृध-णिच् ल्यु ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=378-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्दिवृक्ष|नन्दिवृक्षः
नन्दिवृक्ष m. (-क्षः) Tun tree.<BR> E. नन्दि pleasure, and वृक्ष a tree: also ङीष्<BR>being added to नन्दि, नन्दीवृक्ष; or with कन् added, नन्दिवृक्षक ।<BR>कोङ्कणदेश प्रसिद्धे सुगन्धवृक्षभेदे, अश्वत्थाकारे क्षीरयुक्ते वृक्षमेदे (तुंँद) गान्धीराख्य-<BR>तृणे, मेषशृङ्गीवृक्षे च ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=378-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्दीट
नन्दीट m. (-टः) A bald-headed man.<BR> E. नन्दि ŚIVA'S bald-headed atten-<BR>dant, and अट who resembles, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=378-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्दींमुखी
नन्दींमुखी f. (-खी) Sleep, drowsiness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=378-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्दीश|नंदीश|नन्दीशः
नन्दीश m. (-शः)<BR>	 1. name of NANDĪ, ŚIVA'S attendant.<BR>	 2. A name of<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=378-b" target="_blank">Page378-b+ 60</a>]<BR>ŚIVA.<BR>	 3. A species of musical rhythm.<BR> E. नन्दी INDRA'S garden,<BR>or नन्दि a proper name, ईश master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=378-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्दीश्वर|नंदीश्वर|नन्दीश्वरः
नन्दीश्वर m. (-रः) A name of ŚIVA, &c.: see the last.<BR> E. नन्दि ŚIVA'S cham-<BR>berlain, and ईश्वर master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=378-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्दीसरस्
नन्दीसरस् n. (-रः) A lake or pond in INDRA'S garden,<BR> E. नन्दी the garden,<BR>सरस् a piece of water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=378-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्द्यावर्त्त|नन्द्यावर्त|नन्द्यावर्तः|नन्द्यावर्त्तः
नन्द्यावर्त्त m. (-र्त्तः)<BR>	 1. A sort of temple.<BR>	 2. A tree, (Tabernæmontana<BR>coronaria:) see तगर.<BR>	 3. A peculiar diagram.<BR> E. नन्दी happiness,<BR>आवर्त्त abode. नन्दी आवर्त्तो यत्र ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=378-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्नम्यमान
नन्नम्यमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Bending or bowing very low.<BR> E. नम् to bow,<BR>intens. form, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=378-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नपुंसक|नपुंसकं|नपुंसकः
नपुंसक mn. (-कः-कं)<BR>	 1. A eunuch.<BR>	 2. An impotent or imbecile man.<BR>	 3.<BR>The neuter gender.<BR> E. न not. पुंसक male.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=378-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नप्तृ
नप्तृ m. (-प्ता) A grandson.<BR>	 f. (-प्त्री) A grand daughter.<BR> E. न not, पत् to fall,<BR>तृच् Unādi affix; propping or sustaining the family.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=378-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभ|नभः
नभ m. (-भः)<BR>	 1. The month Srāvana.<BR>	 2. Æther, atmosphere.<BR>	 f. (-भा)<BR>	 1.<BR>A spitting pot.<BR>	 2. The city of the sun.<BR> E. नह् to bind, affix भ; see<BR>नभस ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=378-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभःक्रान्तिन्|नभःक्रांतिन्
नभःक्रान्तिन् m. (-न्ती) A lion.<BR> E. नभस् a cloud, and क्रान्तिन् who goes;<BR>whose shape is seen in the clouds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=378-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभःप्राण|नभःप्राणः
नभःप्राण m. (-णः) Air, wind.<BR> E. नभस् atmosphere and प्राण life or<BR>breath.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=378-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभःसद्
नभःसद् m. (-सद्) A deity.<BR> E. नभस् heaven, and सद who travels, from सद्<BR>to go, with क्विप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=378-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभःसरित्
नभःसरित् f. (-रित्) The celestial Ganges.<BR> E. नभस् heaven, and सरित् a<BR>river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=378-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभःस्थ
नभःस्थ mfn. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थं) Celestial, ærial, heavenly, ethereal,<BR> E. नभस्,<BR>and स्थ what stays; also नभस्स्थ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=378-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभःस्थित|नभःस्थितः
नभःस्थित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Abiding in heaven or in the sky.<BR>	 m. (-तः) A<BR>division of the infernal regions, a hell.<BR> E. नभस् atmosphere, and<BR>स्थित a staying; also नभस्स्थित ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=378-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभश्चक्षुस्
नभश्चक्षुस् m. (-क्षुः) The sun.<BR> E. नभस् heaven, and चक्षुस् the eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=378-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभश्चमस|नभश्चमसः
नभश्चमस m. (-सः)<BR>	 1. The moon.<BR>	 2. A variegated cake.<BR>	 3. Conjuring. E.<BR>नभस् heaven, and चमस a short of ladle, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=378-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभश्चर|नभश्चरः
नभश्चर mfn. (-रः-री-रं) going in the air or heaven.<BR>	 m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A bird.<BR>2. A Vidyādhara or demi-god so called.<BR>	 3. A cloud.<BR>	 4. Air, wind.<BR>E. नभस् heaven, and चर who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=378-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभस्
नभस् m. (-भाः)<BR>	 1. The month Srāvana, (July-August)<BR>	 2. A cloud.<BR>	 3.<BR>The rains, rainy season.<BR>	 4. Smell.<BR>	 5. The fibres in the root of the<BR>lotus.<BR>	 6. A bird.<BR>	 7. A grey-headed man.<BR>	 n. (-भः) sky, atmosphere,<BR>ether or heaven.<BR> E. नभ् to injure, to be annihilated, (at the end of<BR>the world,) Unādi affix असुन्, or नह् to bind, and भ substituted<BR>for ह.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=378-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभस|नभसं|नभसः
नभस n. (-सं) Heaven, sky, &c. see the last.<BR> E. नभ as above, Unādi affix<BR>असच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=378-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभसङ्गम|नभसंगम|नभसंगमः|नभसङ्गमः
नभसङ्गम m. (-मः) A bird.<BR> E. नभस heaven, गम् to go, affix खच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=378-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभस्तल|नभस्तलं
नभस्तल m. (-लः) The atmosphere.<BR> E. नभस् sky, and तल below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=378-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभस्य|नभस्यः
नभस्य m. (-स्यः) The month Bhādra, (August-September.)<BR> E. नभस् a<BR>cloud or rain, and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=378-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभस्वत्|नभस्वन्त्
नभस्वत् m. (-स्वान्) Air, wind.<BR> E. नभस्, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=378-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभाक|नभाकं|नभाकः
नभाक n. (-कं) Darkness.<BR> E. नभ् to injure, आक Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=378-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभि|नभिः
नभि m. (-भिः) A wheel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=378-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभोगज|नभोगजः
नभोगज m. (-जः) A cloud.<BR> E. नभस् sky, and गज an elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=378-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभोगति|नभोगतिः
नभोगति f. (-तिः) Flying, soaring, going in the air.<BR> E. नभस् sky, and<BR>गति going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=378-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभोदुह|नभोदुहः
नभोदुह m. (-हः) A cloud.<BR> E. नभस् rain, दुह् to milk, affix क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=378-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभोद्वीप|नभोद्वीपः
नभोद्वीप m. (-पः) A cloud.<BR> E. नभस् rain, द्वीप an island.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=378-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभोधूम|नभोधूमः
नभोधूम m. (-मः) A cloud.<BR> E. नभस् sky, and धूम smoke.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=378-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभोनदी
नभोनदी f. (-दी) The celestial Ganges.<BR> E. नभस् heaven, and नदी a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=378-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभोमणि|नभोमणिः
नभोमणि m. (-णिः) The sun.<BR> E. नभस् sky, मणि a gem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=378-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभोम्बुप|नभोंबुप|नभोम्बुपः
नभोऽम्बुप m. (-पः) The Chātaka, (Cuculus melanoleucos.)<BR> E. नभस् sky,<BR>अम्बु water, and प who drinks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=379-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभोरजस
नभोरजस n. (-जः) Darkness.<BR> E. नभस् sky, and रजस् dust.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=379-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभोरेणु|नभोरेणुः
नभोरेणु f. (-णुः) Fog, mist, vapour.<BR> E. नभस् sky, and रेणु thin dust.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=379-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभोलय|नभोलयः
नभोलय m. (-यः) Smoke.<BR> E. नभस् sky, and लय abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=379-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभोलिह्
नभोलिह् mfn. (-लिट्) Lofty, towering, rising to the clouds.<BR> E. नभस्,<BR>and लिह् what touches.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=379-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभ्य|नभ्यं
नभ्य mfn. (-भ्यः-भ्या-भ्यं) Relating to the nave of a wheel, resembling it,<BR>&c.<BR> E. नभ for नाभि, and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=379-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभ्राज्
नभ्राज् m. (-भ्राट्) A cloud.<BR> E. न negative, भ्राज् to shine, affix क्विप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=379-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नम|नमः
नम r. 1st cl. (नमति) To bow, to pay obeisance. r. 10th cl. (नमयति-<BR>नामयति) To bend, to bow: see णम ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=379-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नमत्
नमत् mfn. (-मन्-मन्ती-मत्) Bending, stooping, bowed.<BR> E. नम् to bow, शतृ<BR>aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=379-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नमत|नमतः
नमत m. (-तः)<BR>	 1. A master, a lord.<BR>	 2. An actor, a mime.<BR>	 3. A cloud. E.<BR>नम to bow or bend, Unādi affix कर्मणि अतच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=379-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नमयत्
नमयत् mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्) Bending, directing downward, declining. E.<BR>नम् to bow. r. 10th cl. शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=379-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नमस्
नमस् ind.<BR>	 1. Gift, present.<BR>	 2. Bowing, bending, salutation, obeisance.<BR>3. An inarticulate cry.<BR>	 4. The term used in connexion with the<BR>name of a deity in the fourth case to signify veneration, as रामाय नमः<BR>salutation, glory or reverence to RĀMA.<BR> E. नम् to bend, and affix<BR>असुन-सच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=379-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नमस|नमसः
नमस m. (-सः) Agreement, concord.<BR> E. नम् to bow, affix असच् । अनुकूले च ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=379-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नमसित|नमसितः
नमसित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Reverenced, respected, worshipped.<BR> E. नमस्<BR>bowing, क्यप् affix, and क्त added, य rejected: see नमस्यित ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=379-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नमस्कार|नमस्कारः
नमस्कार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Respectful or reverential address or salutation.<BR>	 2.<BR>A sort of poison.<BR>	 f. (-री) A sensitive plant.<BR> E. नमस् bowing, and<BR>कार making, fem. affix अच० गौरा० ङीष्; or नमस् + कृ + घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=379-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नमस्कृत्वा
नमस्कृत्वा ind. Having saluted reverentially.<BR> E. नमस्, and कृत्वा having<BR>made.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=379-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नमस्य|नमस्यः
नमस्य mfn. (-स्यः-स्या-स्यं) Venerable, respectable, entitled to salutation<BR>or civility.<BR>	 f. (-स्या) Reverence, respect, worship, adoration.<BR> E. नमस्<BR>respect, क्यच् aff or नामधातुः नमस्य कर्मणि यत् अल्लोपयल्लोपौ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=379-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नमस्यत्
नमस्यत् mfn. (-स्यन्-स्यन्ती-स्यत्) Saluting reverentially, bowing to, paying<BR>adoration.<BR> E. नमस् nominal verb, to bow, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=379-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नमस्यित|नमस्यितः
नमस्यित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Reverenced, respected. worshipped.<BR> E. नमस् res-<BR>pect, affix क्यप्, and the participial affix क्त; also नमसित ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=379-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नमित|नमितः
नमित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Bowed, making salutation or obeisance.<BR>	 2.<BR>Bowed, bent down.<BR> E. नम् to bend, causal form, affix णिच् क्त वा<BR>ह्रस्वः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=379-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नमुचि|नमुचिः
नमुचि m. (-चिः)<BR>	 1. The deity of love.<BR>	 2. A demon so named.<BR> E. न nega-<BR>tive, मुच् to loose, and कि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=379-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नमुचिमूदन
नमुचिमूदन m. (-नः) A name of INDRA.<BR> E. नमुचि the demon, and सूदन des-<BR>troyer; also similar names, as नमुचिद्विष्, &c. नमुचिं सूदयति हिनस्ति<BR>सूदि-ल्यु ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=379-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नमेरु|नमेरुः
नमेरु m. (-रुः) The seed of the Elæocarpus.<BR> E. न not, मेरु the mountain<BR>Meru, or नम वा एरु ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=379-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नमोगुरु|नमोगुरुः
नमोगुरु m. (-रुः) A spiritual teacher.<BR> E. नमस् reverence, and गुरु a<BR>teacher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=379-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नम्ब
नम्ब r. 1st cl. (नम्बति) To go, to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=379-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नम्र|नम्रः
नम्र mfn. (-म्रः-म्रा-म्रं) Crooked, curved, bent, bowed.<BR> E. नम् to bow, affix र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=379-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नम्रक|नम्रकः
नम्रक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Bent or bowed, stooping.<BR> E. कत् added to the<BR>last. नम्र इव कायति कै-क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=379-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नम्रमुख
नम्रमुख mfn. (-खः-खी-खं) Looking down, having the head bent.<BR> E. नम्र,<BR>and मुख the face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=379-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नम्रमूर्त्ति|नम्रमूर्ति
नम्रमूर्त्ति mfn. (-र्त्तिः-र्त्तिः-र्त्ति) Bending down, stooping, bowed,<BR> E. नम्र, and<BR>मूर्त्ति form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=379-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नम्राङ्ग
नम्राङ्ग mfn. (-ङ्गः-ङ्गी-ङ्गं) Bent, bowed, stooping.<BR> E. नम्र, and अङ्ग the<BR>body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=379-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नय|नयः
नय r. 1st cl. (नयते) To go, to move: see णय and णी । भ्वा० आ० सक० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=379-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नय|नयः
नय mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>	 1. Fit, right, proper.<BR>	 2. Leading, conducting, (who<BR>or what does so.)<BR>	 m. (यः)<BR>	 1. Guiding, directing, (literally or figura-<BR>tively, as in morals, &c.)<BR>	 2. Polity, civil and military government.<BR>3. The theological part of the Vedas.<BR>	 4. A sort of dice or men<BR>for playing with.<BR>	 5. A guide, a conductor.<BR> E. नय् to go, affix घञ्,<BR>or णी to guide, &c. affix भावे अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=379-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नयत्
नयत् mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्)<BR>	 1. Leading, guiding.<BR>	 2. Tending or<BR>conducing to.<BR>	 3. Informing, certifying, giving in evidence.<BR>	 4.<BR>Obtaining.<BR> E. णी to obtain, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=379-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नयन|नयनं
नयन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. The eye.<BR>	 2. Leading, guiding, (literally or figuratively.)<BR>3. Attaining, obtaining.<BR>	 4. Bringing.<BR>	 f. (-ना) The pupil of the eye.<BR>E. णी to guide, affix करणे ल्युट् । नीयते वुद्धि वृत्तिः स्वसंयुक्तविषयान् अनेन ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=379-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नयनवारि
नयनवारि n. (-रि) Tears.<BR> E. नयन, and वारि water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=379-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नयनामोषिन्
नयनामोषिन् mfn. (-षी-षिणी-षि) Sight-stealing, blinding.<BR> E. नयन, and<BR>आमोषिन् what steals.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=379-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नयनोत्सव|नयनोत्सवः
नयनोत्सव m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. A lamp.<BR>	 2. Any lovely or desired object.<BR> E. नयन<BR>the eye, and उत्सव a festival.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=379-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नयनोपान्त|नयनोपांत|नयनोपान्तः
नयनोपान्त m. (-न्तः) The outer angle or canthus of the eye.<BR> E. नयन, and<BR>उपान्त extremity. अपाङ्गे ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=379-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नयनौषध|नयनौषधं
नयनौषध m. (-धः) Green sulphate of iron, or the salt in a state of par-<BR>tial decomposition by exposure to the atmosphere.<BR> E. नयन the eye,<BR>and औषध a medicament, being used as a collyrium. पुष्पकासीसे ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=379-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नयपीठी
नयपीठी f. (-ठी) The board or cloth on which dice are played. E.<BR>नय dice, पीठी a stool. (छक् ।)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=379-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नयप्रयोग|नयप्रयोगः
नयप्रयोग m. (-गः) Policy, political address.<BR> E. नय, and प्रयोग application.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=379-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नयविशारद|नयविशारदः
नयविशारद m. (-दः) A politician, a statesman.<BR> E. नय, and विशारद skilled<BR>in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=379-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नयसिद्धि
नयसिद्धि f. (-द्धिः) Political success, accomplishing any thing by good<BR>management.<BR> E. नय, and सिद्धि success.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=379-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नर|नरं|नरः
नर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Man, individually or generally.<BR>	 2. The Eternal, the<BR>divine imperishable spirit pervading the universe.<BR>	 3. A name of<BR>ARJUNA.<BR>	 4. VIṢṆU.<BR>	 5. A gnomon.<BR>	 6. A man or piece at chess,<BR>draughts, &c.<BR>	 7. A Muni, an incarnation of VIṢṆU.<BR>	 n. (-रं) A<BR>fragrant grass, commonly Rāmkappur.<BR>	 f. (-रौ) Woman in general:<BR>see नारी.<BR> E. नॄ or नृ to lead or guide, affix नये-अच् । गणितशास्त्रोक्ते<BR>छायाप्रमाण ज्ञानोपयोगिनि शङ्कौ च ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=379-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नरक|नरकं|नरकः
नरक mn. (-कः-कं) Hell, the infernal regions, including a number of<BR>places of torture of various descriptions.<BR>	 m. (-कः) The name of a<BR>Daitya or demon.<BR> E. नृ to guide or lead, affix वुन्, whither the<BR>wicked are conducted: It is sometimes read नारक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=379-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नरककुण्ड|नरककुंड|नरककुण्डं
नरककुण्ड n. (-ण्डं) A well or pit in Tartarus, eighty-six such are enu-<BR>merated.<BR> E. नरक, and कुण्ड a pit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=379-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नरकजित्
नरकजित् m. (-जित्) A name of VIṢṆU.<BR> E. नरक tke demon, and जित्<BR>subduing. नरकम् असुरभेदं जयति स्म । जि-भूते क्विप् ६ त० स० ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=379-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नरकदेवता
नरकदेवता f. (-ता) Misfortune, personified as a goddess.<BR> E. नरक, and<BR>देवता divinity. निऋतौ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=379-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नरकस्थ
नरकस्थ mfn. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थं) Living or being in Tartarus, who or what is<BR>there.<BR>	 f. (-स्था) The river of hell named “Baitarany”.<BR> E. नरक hell,<BR>स्थ who stays or abides, fem. affix टाप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=379-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नरकान्तक|नरकांतक|नरकान्तकः
नरकान्तक m. (-कः) VIṢṆU.<BR> E. नरक hell, and अन्तक destroyer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=379-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नरकामय|नरकामयः
नरकामय m. (-यः) The soul after death.<BR> E. नरक hell, and आमय sickness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=379-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नरकीलक|नरकीलकः
नरकीलक m. (-कः) The murderer of his spiritual preceptor.<BR> E. नर man-<BR>kind, and कील a stake, affix कन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=379-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नरङ्ग|नरंग|नरंगं|नरङ्गः
नरङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः) Pimples of the face.<BR>	 n. (-ङ्गं) The penis.<BR> E. नृ to guide or<BR>lead, Unādi affix अङ्गच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=379-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नरदेव|नरदेवः
नरदेव m. (-वः) A sovereign, a king.<BR> E. नर a man, and देव a deity,<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=379-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नरनारायण|नरनारायणः
नरनारायण m. dual. (-णौ) Two sages, incarnations of VIṢṆU,<BR>and born again, as KṚṢṆA and ARJUNA.<BR> E. नर, and नारायण,<BR>each severally the name of a sage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=379-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नरपति|नरपतिः
नरपति m. (-तिः) A king, a sovereign, a prince.<BR> E. नर man, पति lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=380-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नरप्रिय|नरप्रियः
नरप्रिय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Favourable or friendly to mankind.<BR> E. नर, and<BR>प्रिय fond of. नीलवृक्षे च ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=380-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नरभू
नरभू f. (-भूः) Bhārata Varṣa, India, or the central of the known conti-<BR>nent.<BR>	 2. The birth or birthplace of men.<BR> E. नर man, and भू land;<BR>also नरभूमि f. (-मिः)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=380-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नरमानिनी
नरमानिनी f. (-नी) A woman who has a beard.<BR> E. नर a man, मन् to re-<BR>gard or think, and णिनि affix; also with कन् affix in the feminine<BR>form, नरमानिका; these words are also written नरमालिनी, &c. नरं<BR>मन्यते मन-णिनि-ङीप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=380-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नरमाला
नरमाला f. (-ला) A string or girdle of skulls.<BR> E. नर, and माला a garland.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=380-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नरमालिनी
नरमालिनी f. (-नी) A woman with a beard.<BR> E. नर a man, माला a necklace,<BR>इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=380-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नरमेध|नरमेधः
नरमेध m. (-धः) A human sacrifice.<BR> E. नर, and मेध a sacrifice. मिध आधारे<BR>घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=380-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नरवाहन|नरवाहनः
नरवाहन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Borne or carried by men.<BR>	 m. (-नः) A name of<BR>KUVERA.<BR> E. नर a man, and वाहन a vehicle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=380-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नरवाहिन्
नरवाहिन् mfn. (-ही-हिनी-हि) Carried by men, (a vehicle.)<BR> E. नर, and<BR>वाहिन् what bears.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=380-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नरविष्वण|नरविष्वणः
नरविष्वण m. (-णः) An imp or goblin.<BR> E. नर man, विष्वण who devours.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=380-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नररूप
नररूप mfn. (-पः-पी-पं) Having the form of man.<BR>	 n. (-पं) The human form.<BR>E. नर, and रुप form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=380-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नररूपिन्
नररूपिन् mfn. (-पी-पिणी-पि) Having the human form.<BR> E. नररूप, and इनि<BR>aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=380-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नरसिंह|नरसिंहः
नरसिंह m. (-हः) VIṢṆU in his fourth Avatār or descent, the lion-<BR>headed man.<BR>	 2. A chief, a man of eminence or power.<BR> E. नर a man<BR>and सिंह a lion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=380-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नरहरि|नरहरिः
नरहरि m. (-रिः) VIṢṆU in his fourth Avatār. see the last.<BR> E. नर, and<BR>हरि a lion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=380-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नराधम|नराधमः
नराधम m. (-मः) A low or vile man, a wretch.<BR> E. नर, and अधम low.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=380-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नराधारा
नराधारा f. (-रा) The earth.<BR> E. नर man, आधार receptacle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=380-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नराधिप|नराधिपः
नराधिप m. (-पः) A king.<BR> E. नर and अधिप ruler.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=380-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नरान्तक|नरांतक|नरान्तकः
नरान्तक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. Death.<BR>	 2. A Rākshasa, a son of RĀVANA.<BR> E. नर,<BR>and अन्तक destroyer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=380-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नरायण|नरायणः
नरायण m. (-णः) A name of VIṢṆU.<BR> E. नर man, and अयण going; see<BR>नारायण ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=380-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नरेन्द्र|नरेंद्र|नरेन्द्रः
नरेन्द्र m. (-न्द्रः)<BR>	 1. A king, an anointed sovereign.<BR>	 2. A dealer in anti-<BR>dotes, a juggler.<BR> E. नर a man, इन्द्र chief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=380-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नरेश|नरेशः
नरेश m. (-शः) A king.<BR> E. नर, and ईश master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=380-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नरेश्वर|नरेश्वरः
नरेश्वर m. (-रः) A king.<BR> E. नर, and ईश्वर a sovereign.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=380-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नर्कुटक|नर्कुटकं
नर्कुटक n. (-कं) The nose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=380-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नर्त्तक|नर्तक|नर्तकः|नर्त्तकः
नर्त्तक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. An actor, a mime.<BR>	 2. A juggler, a dancer, a player of<BR>any description.<BR>	 3. A bard, a herald.<BR>	 4. An elephant.<BR>	 5. A reed,<BR>(Arundo karka, Rox.)<BR>	 6. A peacock.<BR>	 f. (-की)<BR>	 1. An actress, female<BR>dancer or singing girl.<BR>	 2. A female elephant.<BR>	 3. A peahen.<BR> E. नृत्<BR>to dance or act, ष्वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=380-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नर्त्तन|नर्तन|नर्तनः|नर्त्तनं
नर्त्तन n. (-नं) Dancing, gesticulating, acting.<BR> E. नृत् to dance, &c. affix<BR>भावे ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=380-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नर्त्तनप्रिय|नर्तनप्रिय|नर्तनप्रियः
नर्त्तनप्रिय m. (-यः) A peacock.<BR> E. नर्त्तन dancing, and प्रिय fond of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=380-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नर्त्तित|नर्तित
नर्त्तित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Danced, dancing.<BR> E. नृत् to dance, णिच् कर्मणि<BR>क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=380-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नर्द्द|नर्द
नर्द्द r. 1st cl. (नर्द्दति प्रनर्द्दति) To sound: the radical न is not convertible<BR>to ण after a preposition, &c. see णर्द्द । शब्दे अक० गतौ सक० भ्वा० पर०<BR>सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=380-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नर्द्दटक|नर्दटक|नर्दटकः|नर्द्दटकं
नर्द्दटक n. (-कं) A kind of metre, containing seventeen letters. “यदि<BR>भवतो नजौ भजजलागुरुर्नर्दष्टकम्” इत्युक्त लक्षणे सप्तदशाक्षरे छन्द्वोभेदे ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=380-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नर्द्दत्|नर्दत्
नर्द्दत् mfn. (-र्द्दन्-र्द्दन्ती-र्द्दत्)<BR>	 1. Sounding.<BR>	 2. Praising aloud, proclaiming.<BR>E. नर्द्द, and शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=380-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नर्द्दन|नर्दन|नर्दनं
नर्द्दन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Sounding, roaring, making a noise.<BR>	 2. Celebrating,<BR>praising aloud.<BR> E. नर्द्द to sound, affix भावे ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=380-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नर्द्दनीय|नर्दनीय
नर्द्दनीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>	 1. To be sounded.<BR>	 2. To be celebrated or praised<BR>aloud.<BR> E. नर्द्द sound, and अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=380-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नर्द्दित|नर्दित|नर्दितः
नर्द्दित mfn. (-तः-तः-तं)<BR>	 1. Sounded, made as a noise.<BR>	 2. Celebrated, prai-<BR>sed aloud.<BR>	 n. (-तं) Sound, roar, bellowing.<BR> E. नर्द्द to sound, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=380-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नर्द्धटक
नर्द्धटक n. (-कं) A stanza of four parts, having seventeen syllables in<BR>each.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=380-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नर्ब्ब|नर्ब
नर्ब्ब r. 1st. cl. (नर्ब्बति) To go, to move भ्वा० प० सक० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=380-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नर्म्मकील|नर्मकील|नर्मकीलः|नर्म्मकीलः
नर्म्मकील m. (-लः) A husband.<BR> E. नर्म्म amusement, कील a drop or stay.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=380-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नर्म्मगर्भ|नर्मगर्भ|नर्मगर्भः
नर्म्मगर्भ m. (-र्भः) A secret lover.<BR> E. नर्म्म, and गर्भ source.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=380-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नर्म्मट|नर्मट|नर्मटः|नर्म्मटः
नर्म्मट m. (-टः)<BR>	 1. The sun.<BR>	 2. A potsherd.<BR> E. नर्म्म, and अट what goes,<BR>deriv. irr. or नर्म अटन् पृषो० ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=380-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नर्म्मठ|नर्मठ|नर्मठः|नर्म्मठः
नर्म्मठ m. (-ठः)<BR>	 1. The nipple.<BR>	 2. A rake, a lecher, a libertine.<BR>	 3. Sport,<BR>amusement.<BR>	 4. Coition.<BR> E. नर्म्म pleasure, स्था to abide, ड affix, deriv.<BR>irr. or नर्मणि कुशलः नर्मन् + अठन ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=380-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नर्म्मद|नर्मद|नर्मदः|नर्म्मदः
नर्म्मद mfn. (-दः-दा-दं) Delighting, making happy, giving pleasure.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-दः) The associate or companion of a person's sports or amuse-<BR>ments.<BR>	 f. (-दा)<BR>	 1. The Narmadā river, which rising in the Vindhya<BR>mountains, runs westward to the gulf of Cambay.<BR>	 2. A plant: see<BR>पृक्का.<BR> E. नर्म्म pleasure, and द what gives. नर्म ददाति दा-क ६ त० स० ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=380-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नर्म्मद्युति|नर्मद्युति|नर्मद्युतिः
नर्म्मद्युति mfn. (-तिः-तिः-ति) Happy, merry.<BR>	 f. (-तिः) Enjoyment of a joke<BR>or any amusement.<BR> E. नर्म्म, and द्युति lustre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=380-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नर्म्मन्|नर्मन्
नर्म्मन् n. (-र्म्म)<BR>	 1. Sport, amusement, pastime, diversion.<BR>	 2. Jest, joke.<BR>3. Wit, humour.<BR> E. नृ to guide, affix मनिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=380-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नर्म्मसचिव|नर्मसचिव|नर्मसचिवः
नर्म्मसचिव m. (-वः) A companion, an associate, the promoter and parta-<BR>ker of a person's amusements, especially of a prince or man of<BR>rank.<BR> E. नर्म्मन, and सचिव a minister.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=380-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नर्म्मसाचिव्य|नर्मसाचिव्य
नर्म्मसाचिव्य n. (-व्यं) Superintendance or provision of a prince's amuse-<BR>ments, partaking a person's amusements.<BR> E. नर्म्मसाचिव, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=380-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नर्म्मस्फूर्ज्ज|नर्मस्फूर्ज|नर्मस्फूर्जः
नर्म्मस्फूर्ज्ज m. (-र्ज्जः) Happiness or amusement ending in alarm.<BR> E. नर्म्म,<BR>and स्फूर्ज्ज thundering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=380-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नर्म्मस्फोट|नर्मस्फोट|नर्मस्फोटः
नर्म्मस्फोट m. (-टः) Slight or inferior amusement.<BR> E. नर्म्म, and स्फोट opening.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=380-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नल|नलं|नलः
नल r. 10th cl. (नालयति)<BR>	 1. To shine.<BR>	 2. To bind or confine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=380-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नल|नलं|नलः
नल r. 10th cl. (-लः)<BR>	 1. A reed, (Arundo karka, Rox.)<BR>	 2. The name of a<BR>king, son of NISHADHA, and hero of several poetical works famous<BR>amongst the Hindus, especially the poem called Naishadha.<BR>	 3.<BR>Another prince, the son of VĪRASENA.<BR>	 4. A deified progenitor or<BR>Pitṛdeva.<BR>	 5. The name of a monkey chief.<BR>	 6. A demon.<BR>	 f. (-ली)<BR>Red arsenic.<BR>	 2. A perfume, commonly called by the same name<BR>of Nali.<BR>	 n. (-लं)<BR>	 1. The water lily, (Nelumbium speciosum.)<BR>	 2.<BR>Smell, odour.<BR> E. नल् to shine, affix अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=380-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नलक|नलकं
नलक n. (-कं) A bone of either of the extremities, any long bone. E.<BR>नल a reed, and कन् affix of resemblance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=380-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नलकिनी
नलकिनी f. (-नी) The knee cap or pan.<BR> E. नलक as above, and इनि affix;<BR>connecting the bones of the lower extremity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=380-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नलकील|नलकीलः
नलकील m. (-लः) The knee.<BR> E. नल a reed, or reed-like bone, and कील a<BR>pin or bolt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=380-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नलकूवर|नलकूवरः
नलकूवर m. (-रः) The son of KUVERA.<BR> E. नल a reed, कूवर a carriage yoke.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=380-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नलद|नलदं
नलद n. (-दं) Indian spikenard, (Valeriana jatamansi.)<BR>	 f. (-दा)<BR>	 1. The<BR>honey or nectar of a flower.<BR>	 2. The root of the Andropogon muri-<BR>catum.<BR> E. नल here said to mean, fragrance, and द what gives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=380-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नलपट्टिका
नलपट्टिका f. (-का) A sort of mat made with reeds, a coarse mat.<BR> E. नल a<BR>reed, and पट्ट a cloth, कन् affix of similitude.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=380-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नलमीन|नलमीनः
नलमीन m. (-नः) A kind of sprat of according to some, a shrimp or<BR>prawn.<BR> E. नल a reed, and मोन a fish; frequenting reedy spots. See<BR>नडमीन ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=380-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नलिका
नलिका f. (-का) A perfume: see नली.<BR> E. नली, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=380-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नलिन|नलिनं|नलिनः
नलिन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. A lotus or water lily, (Nelumbium speciosum, or Nym-<BR>phæa nelumbo.)<BR>	 2. Water.<BR>	 3. Indigo.<BR>	 m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. The Indian crane.<BR>2. A small fruit, Karonda.<BR>	 f. (-नी)<BR>	 1. An assemblage of lotus<BR>flowers.<BR>	 2. A place abounding in lotuses.<BR>	 3. The flexible stalk of a<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=381-a" target="_blank">Page381-a+ 60</a>]<BR>water lily.<BR>	 4. A pond in which the lotus grows or may grow.<BR>	 5.<BR>The Ganges of heaven.<BR>	 6. The fermented and intoxicating juice of<BR>the cocoanut.<BR> E. नल् to be bright, Unādi affix इनन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=380-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नलिनीरुह|नलिनीरुहं|नलिनीरुहः
नलिनीरुह m. (-हः)<BR>	 1. BRAMHĀ.<BR>	 2. n. (-हं) The fibres of the lotus stalk.<BR>E. नलिनी, and रुह what grows and क affix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=381-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नलिनेशय|नलिनेशयः
नलिनेशय m. (-यः) A name of VIṢṆU.<BR> E. नलिने in a lotus, and शय who<BR>sleeps. नलिने व्रह्मनाभिकमले शेते शी-अच् । अलुक़् स० ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=381-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नल्व|नल्वः
नल्व m. (-ल्वः) A furlong, a distance measured by four hundred cubits.<BR>E. नल् to be as a reed in length, and व aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=381-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नल्ववर्त्मगा
नल्ववर्त्मगा f. (-गा) The orange tree.<BR> E. नल्व as above, वर्त्म a road, and ग<BR>what goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=381-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नव|नवः
नव mfn. (-वः-वा-वं) New.<BR>	 m. (-वः) Praise, panegyric, celebration.<BR> E. नु<BR>to praise, &c. affix. कर्मणि भावे वा अप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=381-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवकारिक
नवकारिक f. (-का)<BR>	 1. A bride, a woman newly married.<BR>	 2. A new com-<BR>ment.<BR> E. नव new, and कारिका agent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=381-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवकालिका
नवकालिका f. (-का) A young woman, either one recently married or one<BR>in whom menstruation has lately commenced.<BR> E. नव new, काल time,<BR>कन् added with the fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=381-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवग्रहा
नवग्रहा m. plu. (-हाः) The nine planets, or sun, moon, five planets, and<BR>the ascending and descending nodes.<BR> E. नव for नवन्, and ग्रह a<BR>planet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=381-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवछात्र|नवच्छात्र|नवच्छात्रः
नवछात्र m. (-त्रः) A student, a novice.<BR> E. नव new, and छात्र a disciple.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=381-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवत|नवतः
नवत m. (-तः) An elephant's painted or variegated housings.<BR> E. नव new,<BR>तन् to spread, affix ङ or नू-अतच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=381-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवता
नवता f. (-ता) Novelty.<BR> E. तल् added to नव; also with त्व, नवत्वं;<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=381-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवति|नवतिः
नवति f. (-ति or -ती) Ninety.<BR> E. नव nine, and क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=381-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवतिका
नवतिका f. (-का) A painting brush.<BR> E. नवति ninety, (hairs,) कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=381-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवतिधा
नवतिधा ind. Ninety-fold.<BR> E. नवति, and धा aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=381-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवतिशस्
नवतिशस् ind. Ninety by ninety.<BR> E. नवति, and शस् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=381-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवदल|नवदलं
नवदल n. (-लं)<BR>	 1. The new leaf of a lotus.<BR>	 2. Any young leaf.<BR> E. नव new,<BR>and दल a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=381-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवदीधिति|नवदीधितिः
नवदीधिति m. (-तिः) Mars, the planet or its deified regent.<BR> E. नव nine,<BR>दोधिति a ray.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=381-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवदुर्गा
नवदुर्गा f. (-र्गा) The nine forms of DURGĀ.<BR> E. नव, and दुर्गा the<BR>goddess.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=381-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवदोला
नवदोला f. (-ला) A litter borne by nine men.<BR> E. नव, and दोल a litter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=381-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवद्वार
नवद्वार mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Having nine doors; an epithet applied to the<BR>body, which has nine inlets or outlets, as the nostrils, ears, mouth,<BR>&c.<BR> E. नव, and द्वार a door.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=381-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवधा
नवधा ind. Nine-fold, in nine ways.<BR> E. नव nine, and धा aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=381-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवन्
नवन् mfn. always plu. (-व) Nine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=381-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवनी
नवनी f. (-नी) Fresh butter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=381-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवनीत|नवनीतं
नवनीत n. (-तं) Fresh butter.<BR> E. नव new, and नीत procured from milk,<BR>&c.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=381-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवनीतक|नवनीतकं
नवनीतक n. (-कं) Clarified butter.<BR> E. कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=381-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवनीतधेनु|नवनीतधेनुः
नवनीतधेनु f. (-नुः) A quantity of butter as a present to Brāhmans. E.<BR>नवनीत, and धेनु a milch cow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=381-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवपल्लव
नवपल्लव n. (-वं) A new shoot or sprout.<BR> E. नव, and पल्लव a shoot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=381-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवफलिका
नवफलिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. A bride, a newly married woman.<BR>	 2. A girl in<BR>whom menstruation has recently begun.<BR> E. नव new, फल fruit, and<BR>ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=381-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवब
नवब(व)धू f. (-धूः) A bride, a newly married woman.<BR> E. नव, and बधू a<BR>wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=381-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवम|नवमः
नवम mfn. (-मः-मी-मं) Ninth.<BR>	 f. (-मी) The ninth day of a lunar half<BR>month.<BR> E. नव nine, and डढि-मट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=381-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवमल्लिका
नवमल्लिका f. (-का) Double jasmine: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=381-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवमालिका
नवमालिका f. (-का) Double jasmine, (J. Zambac.)<BR> E. नव excellent,<BR>praised, and मालिका or मल्लिका jasmine: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=381-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवयौवना
नवयौवना f. (-ना) A young woman.<BR> E. नव new, and यौवन young.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=381-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवरक्तक
नवरक्तक n. (-कं) A newly dyed garment.<BR> E. नव, रक्त red, and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=381-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवरङ्ग|नवरङ्गं
नवरङ्ग n. (-ङ्गं) Gift to five and acceptance by fours persons of the best<BR>Kayastha families.<BR> E. नव, and रङ्ग colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=381-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवरत्र
नवरत्र n. (-त्रं)<BR>	 1. Nine precious gems, or a pearl, ruby, topaz, diamond,<BR>emerald, lapis lazuli, coral, sapphire, and one called Gomedā.<BR>	 2.<BR>The nine men of letters at the court of VIKRAMĀDITYA, or DHAN-<BR>WANTARI, KSHAPANAKA, AMARASINHA, SANKU, VETĀLABHATTA,<BR>GHATAKARPARA, KĀLIDĀSA, VARĀHAMIHIRA, and VARARŪCHI.<BR>E. नव and रत्र a jewel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=381-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवरात्र|नवरात्रं
नवरात्र n. (-त्रं) The period of nine days, from the first of the light half<BR>of Aswin to the ninth; part of the time devoted to the worship of<BR>DURGĀ.<BR> E. नव, and रात्रि a night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=381-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नववरिका
नववरिका f. (-का) A newly married woman.<BR> E. नव new, वर a blessing,<BR>affix कन् added, fem. affix टाप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=381-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नववस्त्र|नववस्त्रं
नववस्त्र n. (-स्त्रं) New cloth.<BR> E. नव, new, and वस्त्र cloth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=381-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवशस्
नवशस् ind. Nine by nine.<BR> E. नव, and शस् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=381-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवशस्य
नवशस्य n. (-स्य) Grain of the year's harvest.<BR> E. नव, and शस्य grain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=381-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवशस्येष्टि
नवशस्येष्टि f. (-ष्टिः) A sacrifice performed on eating the new rice or<BR>grain of the year, नवशस्य, and इष्टि sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=381-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवशायक|नवशायकः
नवशायक m. (-कः) A name given to any of nine inferior classes, the<BR>cowherd, gardener, oilman, weaver, confectioner, betel seller,<BR>potter, blacksmith, and barber.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=381-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवश्राद्ध
नवश्राद्ध n. (-द्धं) The first series of Shrāddhas collectively, or funeral offer-<BR>ings on the first, third, fifth, seventh, ninth, and eleventh days<BR>after a person's demise.<BR> E. नव, and श्राद्ध obsequial rite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=381-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नधसूतिका
नधसूतिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. A milch cow.<BR>	 2. A woman recently delivered. E.<BR>नव new, and सूत offspring, and कन् affix, fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=381-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवांश|नवांशः
नवांश m. (-शः) A ninth, a ninth part.<BR> E. नव, and अंश share,<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=381-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवान्न|नवान्नं
नवान्न n. (-न्नं)<BR>	 1. New rice or grain.<BR>	 2. A ceremony observed on first<BR>eating the rice, &c. of the last harvest.<BR> E. नव, and अन्न food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=381-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवाम्बर|नवाम्बरं
नवाम्बर n. (-रं) New and unbleached cloth.<BR> E. नव new, and अम्बर cloth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=381-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवार्च्चिस्|नवार्चिस्
नवार्च्चिस् m. (-र्च्चिः) The planet Mars or its deified personification.<BR> E. नव<BR>nine, and अर्च्चिस् light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=381-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवाह|नवाहः
नवाह m. (-हः)<BR>	 1. A new day.<BR>	 2. The first day of the fortnight.<BR> E. नव<BR>new, and अह a day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=381-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवीकरण
नवीकरण n. (-णं) Renewing, doing or making anew,<BR> E. नव, करण making,<BR>च्वि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=381-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवीकृत
नवीकृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Renewed, revived, done or made anew,<BR> E. नव,<BR>and कृत made, च्वि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=381-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवीन|नवीनं
नवीन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) New.<BR> E. नव new, ख pleonasm, and the semi-vowel<BR>changed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=381-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवीभूत
नवीभूत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Renewed, revived.<BR> E. नव, and, भूत become, च्वि<BR>augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=381-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवै
नवै ind. Not so perhaps, a particle implying doubt.<BR> E. न not, वै<BR>expletive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=381-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवोढा
नवोढा f. (-ढा) A newly married woman, a bride.<BR> E. नव new, and ऊढा<BR>a wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=381-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवोद्धृत|नवोद्धृतं
नवोद्धृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Newly extracted or drawn up.<BR>	 n. (-तं)<BR>	 2. Fresh<BR>butter.<BR> E. नव new, उद्धृत made or drawn up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=381-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नव्य|नव्यं|नव्यः
नव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं) New, recent, young, modern. &c.<BR>	 m. (-व्यः) Praise,<BR>panegyric.<BR> E. नव new, and स्वार्थे यत् aff. रक्तपुनर्नवायाम् च ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=381-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नशाक|नशाकः
नशाक mf. (-कः-का) A bird, said to be a sort of crow.<BR> E. नश् to destroy,<BR>affix आक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=381-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नशितृ
नशितृ mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ) Destroying.<BR> E. णश to destroy, affix तृच् with इट्<BR>augment, else with a nasal augment नष्टृ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=381-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नश्यत्
नश्यत् mfn. (श्यन्-श्यन्ती-श्यत्) Perishing, decaying, wasting, being destroy-<BR>ed.<BR> E. नश् to perish, and शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=381-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नश्यत्प्रसूतिका
नश्यत्प्रसूतिका f. (-का) A female bearing a dead child.<BR> E. नश्यत्, प्रसूतिका a<BR>mother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=381-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नश्वर|नश्वरः
नश्वर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>	 1. Mischievous.<BR>	 2. Destructive, perishable.<BR> E. णशि<BR>to destroy, affix छरप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=381-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नष्ट|नष्टः
नष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं) Lost, destroyed, removed, annihilated.<BR> E. णश to<BR>perish, affix क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=382-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नष्टचन्द्र|नष्टचन्द्रः
नष्टचन्द्र m. (-न्द्रः) The moon on the fourth lunation of either half of<BR>Bhādra.<BR> E. नष्ट, and चन्द्र the moon: it is is very unlucky to see the<BR>moon on these days.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=382-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नष्टचेतन
नष्टचेतन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Fainted, insensible.<BR> E. नष्ट, and चेतन conscious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=382-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नष्टचेष्ट
नष्टचेष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं) Insensible, inert.<BR> E. नष्ट, and चेष्टा effort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=382-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नष्टचेष्टता
नष्टचेष्टता f. (-ता) Fainting, swooning, insensibility, proceeding either<BR>from joy or sorrow, &c.<BR> E. नष्ट lost, चेष्टता effort. हर्षशोकादिभिः सर्व-<BR>चेष्टाराहित्ये ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=382-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नष्टसंस्मृति
नष्टसंस्मृति mfn. (-तिः-तिः-ति) Unmindful, forgetful.<BR> E. नष्ट, and संस्मृति<BR>recollection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=382-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नष्टाग्नि|नष्टाग्निः
नष्टाग्नि m. (-ग्निः) A Brāhman or householder who has lost his conse-<BR>crated fire.<BR> E. नष्ट lost, and अग्नि fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=382-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नष्टाप्तिसूत्र|नष्टाप्तिसूत्रं
नष्टाप्तिसूत्र n. (-त्रं) Booty, plunder.<BR> E. नष्ट lost, आप्ति gain, and सूत्र thread<BR>or chain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=382-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नष्टार्थ
नष्टार्थ mfn. (-र्थः-र्था-र्थं) Reduced, become poor.<BR> E. नष्ट, and अर्थ wealth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=382-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नष्टेन्दुकला|नष्टेंदुकला
नष्टेन्दुकला f. (-ला) The day of new moon when it rises invisible.<BR> E. नष्ट,<BR>and इन्दुकला a digit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=382-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नस्
नस् f. (-नाः) The nose.<BR> E. नस् to sound, affix क्विप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=382-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नसा
नसा f. (-सा) The nose: see नासा and नासिका ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=382-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नस्त|नस्तः
नस्त m. (-स्तः) The nose.<BR>	 n. (-स्तं) A sternutatory, snuff, &c.<BR>	 f. (-स्ता) A<BR>hole bored in the septum of the nose.<BR> E. णस् to make crooked,<BR>affix संज्ञायां त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=382-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नस्तित|नस्तितः
नस्तित m. (-तः) An ox or any other draft animal, with a string through<BR>his nose, the sort of rein usually employed in India.<BR>	 f. (-ता)<BR>Nozzled.<BR> E. नस्त as above, the nose, formed into a nominal verb,<BR>and क्त added, nozzled or nose-led. णस्-तार-इतच् । (नाकफोडा) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=382-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नस्तोत|नस्तोतः
नस्तोत mf. (-तः) An ox led by a string through his nose: see the last;<BR>also नस्योत. नसि नासिकायां सम्यक् ऊतः आ + वे-क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=382-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नस्य|नस्यं
नस्य mfn. (-स्यः-स्या-स्यं) Nasal, relating or belonging to the nose.<BR>	 n.<BR>(-स्यं) A sternutatory, snuff.<BR>	 f. (-स्या) The nose.<BR> E. नसा the nose,<BR>यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=382-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नस्योत|नस्योतः
नस्योत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) An ox or other animal led by a string through<BR>the septum of the nose.<BR> E. नसा the nose, यत् affix of relation or<BR>fitness, and ऊत woven: see नस्तित । आ + वे + क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=382-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नह
नह (-औ) औनह r. 4th cl. (नह्यति-ते) To bind: see णह ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=382-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नहि
नहि ind. No, not.<BR> E. णह् to bind or tie, affix इन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=382-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नहुष|नहुषः
नहुष m. (-षः)<BR>	 1. The name of a Nāga or serpent.<BR>	 2. The name of a<BR>king, one of the lunar race, son of AYUS and grandson of PURŪ-<BR>RAVAS.<BR> E. णह् to bind, Unādi affix उषन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=382-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नहुषात्मज|नहुषात्मजः
नहुषात्मज m. (-जः) A king, also YAYĀTI.<BR> E. नहुष as above, आत्मज son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=382-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ना
ना ind. No, not (another form of न ।)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=382-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाक|नाकः
नाक m. (-कः) Heaven, paradise, æther. sky, atmosphere.<BR> E. न not<BR>with अक derived from क happiness, and the privative अ prefixed<BR>misery; in which there is no unhappiness. न कम् अकम् दुःखम् तत्<BR>नास्ति यत्र ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=382-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाकनाथ|नाकनाथः
नाकनाथ m. (-थः) A name of INDRA.<BR> E. नाक paradise, and नाथ lord;<BR>also with कन् added नाकनाथक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=382-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाकनायक|नाकनायकः
नाकनायक m. (-कः) INDRA.<BR> E. नाक, and नायक a chief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=382-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाकवनिता
नाकवनिता f. (-ता) A nymph of heaven.<BR> E. नाक, and वनिता a wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=382-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाकषेधक
नाकषेधक m. (-कः) INDRA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=382-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाकसद्
नाकसद् m. (-सत्) A deity.<BR> E. नाक, and सद् who dwells in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=382-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाकिन्
नाकिन् m. (-की) A deity, a god.<BR> E. नाक heaven, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=382-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाकु|नाकुः
नाकु m. (-कुः)<BR>	 1. An ant or mole hill, a burrow.<BR>	 2. A mountain.<BR>	 3. A<BR>name of a Muni or saint.<BR> E. न privative, अक् to go, affix उ, or नम्<BR>to be crooked or bowed, Unādi affix उ, and नाक substituted for<BR>the radical letters.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=382-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाकुल|नाकुलः
नाकुल mfn. (-लः-ली-लं) Relating or belonging to an ichneumon.<BR>	 f. (-ली)<BR>1. A plant; the ichneumon plant, a vegetable supposed to furnish<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=382-b" target="_blank">Page382-b+ 60</a>]<BR>the mungoose with an antidote, when bitten in a conflict with a<BR>snake, (Serpent ophioxylon)<BR>	 2. The root of the Simul tree,<BR>(कुक्कुटोकन्द) A sort of pepper, (Piper chavya)<BR> E. नकुल the ichneu-<BR>mon, affixes अण् and ङीष् । चविके, (चै) राम्नायां, यवतिक्तायां, श्वेत-<BR>कण्टकार्य्यां च ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=382-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाकुलान्ध्य
नाकुलान्ध्य n. (-न्धं) Weakness of sight<BR> E. नाकुल, and अन्ध्य blindness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=382-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाकुसद्मन्
नाकुसद्मन् m. (-द्मा) A snake.<BR> E. नाकु a mound of earth, सद्मन् a dwelling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=382-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाक्षत्र|नाक्षत्रं|नाक्षत्रः
नाक्षत्र mfn. (-त्रः-त्री-त्रं) Relating or belonging to the luner asterisms.<BR>	 n.<BR>(-त्रं) A month, one computed by the moon's passage through the<BR>twenty-seven mansions, or of thirty days of sixty Gharis each. E.<BR>नक्षत्र, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=382-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाक्षत्रिक|नाक्षत्रिकः
नाक्षत्रिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Relating or belonging to the lunar asterisms.<BR>m. (-कः) A month of twenty-seven days, each day being the period<BR>of the moon's passage through a luner asterism, f. (-की) The<BR>state or condition to which a person is subjected agreeably to the<BR>asterism presiding over his nativity.<BR> E. नक्षत्र as above, and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=382-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाग|नागं|नागः
नाग m. (-गः) Nāga or demi-god so called, having a human face, with<BR>the tail of a serpent, and the expanded neck of the Koluber Nāga;<BR>the race of these beings is said to have sprung from KADRU, the<BR>the wife of KĀSYAPA, in order to people Pātāla or the regions<BR>below the earth.<BR>	 2. A serpent in general or especially the specta-<BR>cle snake, or cobra capella, (Coluber Nāga.)<BR>	 3. An elephant.<BR>	 4. A<BR>cruel or tyrannical person.<BR>	 5. A cloud.<BR>	 6. (In composition,) Pre-<BR>eminent.<BR>	 7. A pin or nail projecting from a wall to hang any<BR>thing upon.<BR>	 8. A small tree, (Mesua ferrea.)<BR>	 9. A sort of grass,<BR>(Cyperus pertenuis.)<BR>	 10. A tree used in dying, (Rottleria tinctoria.)<BR>11. One of the airs of the body, that which is expelled by belching.<BR>12. Betel or Pān.<BR>	 13. The name of a country.<BR>	 14. A shark.<BR>	 n. (-गं)<BR>	 1.<BR>Tin.<BR>	 2. Lead.<BR>	 3. One of the astronomical periods called Karaṇas;<BR>it is one of those termed invariable, and always corresponds to<BR>the last half of Āmavasya or new moon.<BR>	 4. The effects of that<BR>period on any thing done or happening during it.<BR> E. नग a moun-<BR>tain, and अण् affix; living or produced in mountainous regions,<BR>&c. नगे पर्वते भवः अण् न गच्छति अगः न अगो वा ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=382-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागकेशर|नागकेशरः
नागकेशर m. (-रः) A small tree, commonly Nageshwar, (Mesua ferrea).<BR>E. नाग, and केशर synonymes of the same plant compounded; the<BR>word is also written नागकेसर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=382-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागगर्भ|नागगर्भं
नागगर्भ n. (-भं) Red lead.<BR> E. नाग lead. and गर्भ origin. सिन्दुरे ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=382-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागज|नागजं
नागज mfn. (-जः-जा-जं) Produced by or of a Nāga. &c.<BR>	 n. (-जं)<BR>	 1. Red<BR>lead.<BR>	 2. Tin.<BR> E. नाग lead, &c. and ज produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=382-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागजिह्वा
नागजिह्वा f. (-ह्वा) A plant, (Asclepias pseudosarsa:) see शारिवा<BR> E. नाग<BR>a snake, and जिह्वा a tongue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=382-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागजिह्विका
नागजिह्विका f. (-का) Red arsenic.<BR> E. नाग a snake, जिह्वा a tongue, कन्<BR>affix of comparison. मनःशिलायाम् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=382-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागजीवन|नागजीवनं|नागजीवनः
नागजीवन m. (-नः) Tin.<BR> E. नाग lead, जीवन proceeding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=382-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागदन्त|नागदंत|नागदन्तः
नागदन्त m. (-न्तः)<BR>	 1. Elephant's tooth or ivory; also the tooth of the ele-<BR>phant.<BR>	 2. A shelf, a pin or bracket projecting from a wall, and<BR>used to hang things upon.<BR>	 f. (-न्ती)<BR>	 1. A sort of sun-flower, (Helio-<BR>tropium Indicum.)<BR>	 2. A whore.<BR> E. नाग an elephant, and दन्त a tooth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=382-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागदन्तिक
नागदन्तिक m. (-कः) A wooden pin or bracket, projecting from a wall, a<BR>shelf.<BR> E. नागदन्त an elephant's tooth, and कन् affix of resemblance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=382-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागदन्तिका
नागदन्तिका f. (-का) A plant, commonly called Rāmadūtī, see विशल्या ।<BR>E. नागदन्ती a plant, and कन् affix of resemblance. (विछाति ।)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=382-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागदलोपम|नागदलोपमं
नागदलोपम m. (-मः) A sort of tree commonly Parusha.<BR> E. नाग one of<BR>the plants so called, दल a leaf, and उपमा resemblance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=382-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागद्रु|नागद्रुः
नागद्रु m. (-द्रुः) Euphorbia<BR> E. नाग a snake, and द्रु a tree; being used in<BR>offerings to the snake goddess MANASĀ. सि वृक्षे ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=382-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागनिर्य्यूह|नागनिर्यूह|नागनिर्यूहः|नागनिर्य्यूहः
नागनिर्य्यूह m. (-हः) A large pin or bracket, projecting from a wall like<BR>a shelf.<BR> E. नाग an elephant, and निर्य्यूह projection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=382-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागपाश|नागपाशः
नागपाश m. (-शः)<BR>	 1. A weapon of VARUṆA the regent of water.<BR>	 2. A<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=383-a" target="_blank">Page383-a+ 60</a>]<BR>sort of magical noose or knot, used in battle to entangle an<BR>enemy.<BR> E. नाग an elephant, and पाश a binding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=382-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागपुष्प|नागपुष्पः
नागपुष्प m. (-ष्पः)<BR>	 1. A tree in used in dyeing, (Rottleria tinctoria.)<BR>	 2.<BR>Nāgeshwar, (Mesua ferrea.)<BR>	 3. The Champaka, (Michelia champa-<BR>ca)<BR> E. नाग an elephant, and पुष्प flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=383-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागबन्धु|नागबंधु|नागबन्धुः
नागबन्धु m. (-न्धुः) The holy fig tree, (Ficus religiosa.)<BR> E. नाग an elephant<BR>and बन्धु friendly, liked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=383-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागबल|नागबलः
नागबल m. (-लः) A name of BHĪMA.<BR>	 f. (-ला) A creeping plant, (Hedy-<BR>sarum lagopodioides.)<BR> E. नाग an elephant, and बल strong. (गोरक्ष<BR>चाकुलिया ।)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=383-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागभिद्
नागभिद् m. (-भिद्) A sort of snake, (Amphisbæna.)<BR> E. नाग an elephant,<BR>and भिद् destroying; the word is sometimes written नागभृत्, from<BR>भृत् cherishing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=383-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागमल्ल|नागमल्लः
नागमल्ल m. (-ल्लः) The elephant of INDRA.<BR> E. नाग an elephant, and मल्ल a boxer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=383-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागमातृ
नागमातृ f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. A name of MANASĀ, a goddess supposed to preside<BR>over snakes.<BR>	 2. Red arsenic.<BR> E. नाग a snake, and मातृ a mother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=383-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाममार
नाममार m. (-रः) A sort of potherb; also केशराज<BR> E. नाग a snake, and<BR>मार destroying; considered as an antidote.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=383-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागयष्टि|नागयष्टिः
नागयष्टि f. (-ष्टिः) A piece of wood erected in a newly dug pond for<BR>showing the depth of water.<BR> E. नाग a snake, and यष्टि a staff; also<BR>नागयष्टिका ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=383-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागर|नागरं|नागरः
नागर mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>	 1. Clever, sharp, knowing, (as a buck, a blood,<BR>a wag. &c.)<BR>	 2. Town-born or bred, citizen.<BR>	 3. Nameless.<BR>	 4. Rela-<BR>ting to a city.<BR>	 5. Polite, civil 6. Bad, vile.<BR>	 n. (-रं)<BR>	 1. Dry ginger.<BR>2. A short of grass, (Cyperus pertenuis).<BR>	 3. A form of writing,<BR>the “Devanāgari alphabet.” m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A husband's brother.<BR>	 2. An<BR>orange.<BR>	 3. A lecturer.<BR>	 4. Denial of knowledge.<BR>	 5. Fatigue.<BR>	 6.<BR>Desire of final beatitude.<BR>	 f. (-री)<BR>	 1. A sort of Euphorbia.<BR>	 2. A<BR>clever or intriguing woman.<BR> E. नगर a city अण् aff. नगरे भवः अण् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=383-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागरक|नागरकः
नागरक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. The orange; see नागरङ्ग 2. A thief.<BR>	 3. An artist. E.<BR>नागर, and वुञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=383-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागरक्त|नागरक्तं
नागरक्त m. (-क्तः) Red lead.<BR> E. नाग mountain, and रक्त red. सिन्दुरे ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=383-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागरङ्ग|नागरंग|नागरङ्गः
नागरङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः) The orange; in India usually applied to the Sylhet<BR>orange, (Citrus aurantium.)<BR> E. नाग an elephant, रङ्ग to be sick,<BR>affix घञ्; on which elephants feed till they become ill; or नाग<BR>red lead, and रङ्ग colour, of the colour of red lead. (नाराङ्गी नेवु ।)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=383-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागरमुस्ता
नागरमुस्ता f. (-स्ता) A grass. (Cyperus.) नागरमुथा ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=383-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागराज|नागराजः
नागराज m. (-जः) ANANTA, the chief of the Nāgas.<BR> E. नाग, and राज king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=383-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागरीट|नागरीटः
नागरीट m. (-टः) A libertine, a debauchee, a rake, a blackguard. E.<BR>नागरी an intriguing woman, अट् to accompany, affix अच्, deriv. irr.<BR>or more appropriately नागरी-मेटति-इट-गतौ-क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=383-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागरुक|नागरुकः
नागरुक m. (-कः) The orange: see नागरङ्ग ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=383-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागरेणु|नागरेणुः
नागरेणु m. (-णुः) Red lead.<BR> E. नाग, and रेणु oxid. सिन्दुरे ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=383-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागरेयक|नागरेयकः
नागरेयक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) City, citizen.<BR> E. नगर a town, and ढकञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=383-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागलता
नागलता f. (-ता) The penis.<BR> E. नाग a snake, and लता a creeper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=383-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागलोक|नागलोकः
नागलोक m. (-कः) The Nāga regions below the earth.<BR> E. नाग a Nāga,<BR>and लोक world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=383-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागवल्लिका
नागवल्लिका f. (-का) The betel plant: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=383-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागवल्ली
नागवल्ली f. (-ल्ली) The betel plant, (Peper betel.)<BR> E. नाग the infernal<BR>Nāga, and वल्ली a creeper; the creeper of the lower regions; also<BR>with कन् added नागवल्लिका ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=383-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागवारिक|नागवारिकः
नागवारिक m. (-कः) Garuda, the bird of VIṢṆU.<BR>	 2. A peacock.<BR>	 3. A<BR>royal elephant.<BR>	 4. An elephant driver or keeper.<BR>	 5. The chief<BR>person in a court or assembly.<BR> E. नाग an elephant, वृ to cherish,<BR>&c. affix ठक् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=383-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागवीट|नागवीटः
नागवीट m. (-टः) A rake: see नागरीट ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=383-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागवीथी
नागवीथी f. (-थी) The path of Airāvata, “the milky way.”<BR> E. नाग the<BR>elephant, वीथी a road or path.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=383-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागसम्भव|नागसंभव|नागसम्भवं
नागसम्भव n. (-वं) Minium or red lead.<BR> E. नाग lead, and सम्भव pro-<BR>duction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=383-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागसुगन्धा
नागसुगन्धा f. (-न्धा) The ichneumon plant: see नाकुली.<BR> E. नाग a snake,<BR>and सुगन्ध perfume.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=383-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागाख्य|नागाख्यः
नागाख्य m. (-ख्यः) A plant: see नागकेसर.<BR> E. नाग an elephant, and आख्या<BR>a name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=383-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागाङ्ग
नागाङ्ग n. (-ङ्गं) Hastināpur.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=383-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागाञ्चला
नागाञ्चला f. (-ला) A stick or pole driven into a square piece of earth<BR>in the centre of a newly dug pond, a boring rod.<BR> E. नाग a snake,<BR>and अञ्चला end of a garment; it is also written नागाञ्चना f. (-ना)<BR>see नागयष्टि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=383-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागाधिप|नागाधिपः
नागाधिप m. (-पः) The great serpent ANANTA.<BR> E. नाग a serpent, and<BR>अधिप a king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=383-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागान्तक|नागांतक|नागान्तकः
नागान्तक m. (-कः) Garuda, the bird and vehicle of VIṢṆU.<BR> E. नाग a<BR>snake, and अन्तक a destroyer; this and similar compounds are<BR>also applied to the “Ardea Argala,” the peacock, and other birds<BR>who are natural enemies of the serpent genus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=383-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागारूढ
नागारूढ mfn. (-ढः-ढा-ढं) Mounted or riding upon an elephant.<BR> E. नाग,<BR>and आरूढ mounted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=383-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागाशन|नागाशनः
नागाशन m. (-नः) Garuda: see नागान्तक.<BR> E. नाग a snake, and अशन food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=383-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागाह्व|नागाह्वं|नागाह्वः
नागाह्व n. (-ह्वं) Hastināpur or ancient Delhi.<BR> E. नाग an elephant, and<BR>आह्वा a name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=383-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागोद|नागोदं
नागोद n. (-दं) Armour for the front or the belly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=383-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागोदर|नागोदरं
नागोदर n. (-रं) A breast plate, a cuirass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=383-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाचिकेतु|नाचिकेतुः
नाचिकेतु m. (-तुः) A name of fire; also नाचिकेतः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=383-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाट|नाटः
नाट n. (-टं)<BR>	 1. Dancing, acting.<BR>	 2. The Carnatic.<BR> E. नट् to dance, affix<BR>घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=383-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाटक|नाटकं|नाटकः
नाटक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) An actor, acting, dancing, &c.<BR>	 m. (-कः) a play,<BR>a drama: the first of the ten species of dramatic compositions of<BR>the first order.<BR>	 f. (-की) The court of INDRA.<BR> E. नट् to act or per-<BR>form, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=383-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाटकप्रपञ्च|नाटकप्रपञ्चः
नाटकप्रपञ्च m. (-ञ्चः) Course or arrangement of a drama.<BR> E. नाटक, and<BR>प्रपञ्च extent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=383-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाटकीय
नाटकीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Dramatic.<BR> E. नाटक, and छ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=383-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाटाम्र|नाटाम्रः
नाटाम्र m. (-म्रः) The Water melon, (Cucurbita citrullus.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=383-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाटार|नाटारः
नाटार m. (-रः) The son of an actress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=383-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाटिका
नाटिका f. (-का) A short or light comedy, the first of the Uparūpakas<BR>or dramas of the second order.<BR> E. नट् to dance, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=383-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाटेय|नाटेयः
नाटेय m. (-यः) The son of an actress.<BR> E. नटी and ढक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=383-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाटेर|नाटेरः
नाटेर m. (-रः) The son of an actress or dancing girl.<BR> E. नटी an actress,<BR>ढ्रक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=383-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाट्य|नाट्यं|नाट्यः
नाट्य n. (-ट्यं) The science or art of dancing or acting, or the union of<BR>song, dance, and instrumental music.<BR> E. नट् to dance, affix ण्यत्<BR>or ज्य, or नटानां कर्म ष्यञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=383-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाट्यधर्म्मिक
नाट्यधर्म्मिक m. (-कः) Rules of dramatic representation.<BR> E. नाट्य acting,<BR>धर्म्म rule, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=383-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाट्यप्रिय|नाट्यप्रियः
नाट्यप्रिय m. (-यः) A name of ŚIVA.<BR> E. नाट्य dancing, and प्रिय fond of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=383-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाट्यशाला
नाट्यशाला f. (-ला) A theatre, a building for dramatic exhibitions; accor-<BR>ding to some it should be built near the gate of a palace.<BR> E. नाठ्य<BR>and शाला a hall.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=383-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाट्योक्ति|नाट्योक्तिः
नाट्योक्ति f. (-क्तिः) Dramatic phraseology.<BR> E. नाठ्य and उक्ति expression.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=383-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाडि|नाडिः
नाडि f. (-डिः-डी)<BR>	 1. The stalk or stem of any plant.<BR>	 2. Any tubular,<BR>organ of the body, as an artery, a vein, an intestine, &c.<BR>	 3. The<BR>hollow stalk of a lotus, &c.<BR>	 4. A fistulous sore, a fistula, a sinus.<BR>5. A sort of bent grass.<BR>	 6. A juggling trick.<BR>	 7. Deception.<BR>	 8. An<BR>hour of twenty-four minutes.<BR>	 9. Any pipe or tube.<BR>	 10. The pulse,<BR>either at the hand or feet, &c.<BR> E. नड् to fall off or from, affix अच्<BR>and इन् or ङीष् optionally added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=383-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाडिका
नाडिका f. (-का) An Indian hour, or twenty-four minutes.<BR> E. नाडि the<BR>same, कन् pleonasm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=383-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाडिकेल|नाडिकेलः
नाडिकेल m. (-लः) The cocoanut: see नारिकेल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=383-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाडिचीर|नाडिचीरं
नाडिचीर n. (-रं) A small reed or tube round which the woof is wound;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=384-a" target="_blank">Page384-a+ 60</a>]<BR>it is then used as a shuttle.<BR> E. नाडि a tube, and चीर old<BR>cloth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=383-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाडिन्धम|नाडिंधम|नाडिंधमः|नाडिन्धमः
नाडिन्धम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>	 1. Terrifying.<BR>	 2. Moving the intestines.<BR>	 m. (-मः)<BR>A goldsmith.<BR> E. नाडि a tube, a hollow bamboo, &c. and धम who<BR>blows, from ध्मा with खश् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=384-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाडिन्धय|नाडिंधय|नाडिन्धयः
नाडिन्धय mfn. (-यः-यी-यं) Who or what drinks or sucks through a tube.<BR>E. नाडि a pipe, धे to drink, affix खश्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=384-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाडिपत्र|नाडिपत्रं
नाडिपत्र n. (-त्रं) An esculent root, (Arum colocasia.)<BR> E. नाडि a tube, पत्र<BR>a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=384-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाडिमण्डल|नाडिमंडल
नाडिमण्डल m. (-लं) The celestial equator.<BR> E. नाडि, and मण्डल a sphere.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=384-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाडीकेल|नाडीकेलः
नाडीकेल m. (-लः) The cocoanut: see नाडिकेल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=384-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाडीच|नाडीचः
नाडीच n. (-चं) An esculent root, (Arum colocasia.)<BR> E. नाडी a tube, चर्<BR>to go or grow, affix ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=384-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाडीचरण|नाडीचरणः
नाडीचरण m. (-णः) A bird in general.<BR> E. नाडी a tube, चरण foot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=384-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाडीजङ्घ|नाडीजंघ|नाडीजङ्घः
नाडीजङ्घ m. (-ङ्घः)<BR>	 1. A crow.<BR>	 2. The name of a holy teacher or saint.<BR>	 3.<BR>The name of a fabulous crane.<BR> E. नाडी a stalk, and जङ्घा a leg or<BR>thigh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=384-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाडीतरङ्ग|नाडीतरंग|नाडीतरङ्गः
नाडीतरङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>	 1. A sort of poison: see काकोल.<BR>	 2. An astrologer.<BR>	 3.<BR>A ravisher, a debaucher.<BR> E. नाडी an Indian hour, and तरङ्ग a wave;<BR>also नाडीतरङ्गक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=384-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाडीदेह|नाडीदेहः
नाडीदेह m. (-हः) BHRINGI, one of ŚIVA'S followers.<BR> E. नाडी a tube,<BR>and देह the body; as thin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=384-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाडीनक्षत्र|नाडीनक्षत्रं
नाडीनक्षत्र n. (-त्रं) The planet of a person's nativity.<BR> E. नाडी and नक्षत्र<BR>an asterism.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=384-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाडीविग्रह|नाडीविग्रहः
नाडीविग्रह m. (-हः) A name of BHRINGI, one of ŚIVA'S chief attendants.<BR>E. नाडी a pipe, and विग्रह the body; also नाडीदेह, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=384-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाडीव्रण|नाडीव्रणः
नाडीव्रण n. (-णं) An ulcer.<BR> E. नाडी a sinus, and व्रण a sore. (नालीघा ।)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=384-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाडीस्नेह|नाडीस्नेहः
नाडीस्नेह m. (-हः) A name of BHRINGI: see नाडीदेह ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=384-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाणक|नाणकं
नाणक n. (-कं) A coin, or any thing struck or stamped with an<BR>impression.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=384-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाणकपरीक्षा
नाणकपरीक्षा f. (-क्षा) Assaying.<BR> E. नाणक, and परीक्षा trial.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=384-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाणकपरीक्षिन्
नाणकपरीक्षिन् m. (-क्षी) An assayer.<BR> E. नाणक, and परीक्षिन् who tries.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=384-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नात्र|नात्रं|नात्रः
नात्र n. (-त्रं)<BR>	 1. Praise, eulogium.<BR>	 2. Surprise, wonder.<BR>	 m. (-त्रः)<BR>	 1. ŚIVA.<BR>2. A sage.<BR> E. नम् to bow, ष्ट्रण् affix, म is dropped, and the short<BR>radical vowel made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=384-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाथ|नाथः
नाथ (ऋ) नाथृ r. 1st cl. (नाथति-ते)<BR>	 1. To ask or beg.<BR>	 2. To bless.<BR>	 3. To<BR>destroy.<BR>	 4. To have wealth or power.<BR>	 5. To be deceased. उपतापे पर०<BR>आशिषि आत्म० ऐश्ये अर्थने च पर० भ्वा० सक० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=384-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाथ|नाथः
नाथ m. (-थः)<BR>	 1. A master, a lord.<BR>	 2. A name of ŚIVA, especially in the<BR>form of a Linga; it is usually compounded with some word relat-<BR>ing to the legendary history of the Linga, as Somanātha, the<BR>Linga set up by SOMA, &c.<BR>	 3. A name adopted by a class of Yogis,<BR>as GORAKSHANĀTHA, &c.<BR>	 4. A rope passed through the nose of a<BR>draft ox.<BR> E. नाथ् to ask, (from whom,) and अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=384-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाथवत्|नाथवन्त्
नाथवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Dependent, subservient, subject,<BR> E. नाथ<BR>master, and मतप् poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=384-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाथहरि|नाथहरिः
नाथहरि m. (-रिः) An animal bridled by the nose.<BR> E. नाथ the string,<BR>हृ to take, इन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=384-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाथहार
नाथहार mfn. (-रः-री-रं) Taking or carrying a master, &c.<BR> E. नाथ, हृ to<BR>take, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=384-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाद|नादः
नाद m. (-दः)<BR>	 1. Sound in general.<BR>	 2. A semicircle, used especially as<BR>an abbreviation or hieroglyphic in mystical works.<BR> E. नद् to<BR>sound, affix घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=384-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नादिन्
नादिन् mfn. (-दी-दिनी-दि) Who or what sounds.<BR> E. नद् to sound, aff णिनि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=384-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नादेय|नादेयं|नादेयः
नादेय mfn. (-यः-यी-यं) Ocean or river-born, marine, aquatic.<BR>	 n. (-यं)<BR>	 1.<BR>Sea salt.<BR>	 2. Antimony.<BR>	 f. (-यी)<BR>	 1. A sort of reed growing usually<BR>near water, (Calamus fasciculatus. Rox.)<BR>	 2. A plant, (Premna<BR>herbacea, Rox.)<BR>	 3. The orange.<BR>	 4. A tree see जयन्ती 5. The China<BR>rose.<BR> E. नद a river or the sea, and ढक् affix, fem. affix ङीप्; also<BR>with कन् added, in the fem. form नादेयिका f. (-का ।)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=384-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाध
नाध (ऋ) नाधृ r. 1st cl. (नाधते)<BR>	 1. To ask or beg.<BR>	 2. To bless.<BR>	 3. To des-<BR>troy.<BR>	 4. To have wealth or power, 5. To be deceased. भ्वा० आ०<BR>सक० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=384-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाना
नाना ind.<BR>	 1. Without, except.<BR>	 2. Many, various.<BR>	 3. Double or two-fold.<BR>E. नञ् negative, and नाञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=384-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नानाध्वनि|नानाध्वनिः
नानाध्वनि m. (-निः) A musical instrument of more than one tone. E.<BR>नाना various, and ध्वनि sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=384-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नानारस
नानारस mfn. (-सः-सा-सं) Of different flavours.<BR> E. नाना, and रस flavour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=384-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नानाराग
नानाराग mfn. (-गः-गा-गं) Variegated, of many colours.<BR> E. नाना, and राग<BR>colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=384-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नानारूप|नानारूपः
नानारूप mfn. (-पः-पी-पं) Multiform, various.<BR> E. नाना various, and रूप form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=384-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नानावर्ण|नानावर्णः
नानावर्ण mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-र्णं) Variegated, many-coloured.<BR> E. नाना, and<BR>वर्ण colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=384-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नानाविध|नानाविधः
नानाविध mfn. (-धः-धा-धं)<BR>	 1. In various ways.<BR>	 2. Of various sorts or<BR>kinds.<BR> E. नाना, and विध kind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=384-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नानुष्ठेय|नानुष्ठेयं
नानुष्ठेय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Improper, unusual, not right or customary. E.<BR>न not, अनु according to, ष्ठेय from स्था to be, to be fixed or deter-<BR>mined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=384-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नान्दिकर|नांदिकर|नांदिकरः|नान्दिकरः
नान्दिकर m. (-रः) The speaker of the prologue to a drama: see नान्दीकर ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=384-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नान्दी|नांदी
नान्दी f. (-न्दी)<BR>	 1. Eulogium of a king, or praise of a deity, recited in be-<BR>nedictory verses at the commencement of a religious ceremony,<BR>or the opening of a drama; it most usually signifies the kind of<BR>blessing pronounced as a prologue to a Nātaka or play.<BR>	 2. Pros-<BR>perity, thriving, increase.<BR> E. नदि to be happy, in the causal form,<BR>affix इन्, and ङीप्; delighting the gods, &c. or procuring happiness<BR>for mankind. नन्दन्ति देवा अत्र नन्द-घञ् पृषो० वृद्धिः ङीप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=384-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नान्दीक|नांदीकः|नान्दीकः
नान्दीक m. (-कः) A post in a door-way, set up for good luck,<BR> E. नान्दी<BR>prosperity, कृ to make, affix ड ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=384-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नान्दीकर|नांदीकर|नान्दीकरः
नान्दीकर m. (-रः) The speaker of the prologue or prelude of a drama.<BR>E. नान्दी as above, कर who makes; also with the vowel made short,<BR>नान्दिकर ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=384-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नान्दीपट|नांदीपट|नान्दीपटः
नान्दीपट m. (-टः) The lid or cover of a well.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=384-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नान्दीमुख|नांदीमुख|नान्दीमुखः
नान्दीमुख m. (-खः)<BR>	 1. The lid or cover of a well.<BR>	 2. The class of male<BR>progenitors to whom the Nāndi-mukha-shrāddha is addressed.<BR>f. (-खी) A female ancestor sharing in the same.<BR>	 n. (-खं)<BR>	 1. A speci-<BR>es of the Sarkari, metre.<BR>	 2. A Shrāddha or funeral obsequies per-<BR>formed on joyous occasions, as initiation, marriage, &c. in which<BR>nine balls of meat are offered to the deceased father, paternal<BR>grandfather, and great grandfather; to the maternal grandfather,<BR>great grandfather, and great great grandfather; and to the<BR>mother, paternal grandmother, and paternal great grandmother.<BR>E. नान्दी good fortune, मुख principal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=384-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नान्दीवादिन्|नांदीवादिन्
नान्दीवादिन् m. (-दी)<BR>	 1. The speaker of the prologue or introduction to<BR>a drama.<BR>	 2. A drummer, one who beats a drum at festivals, &c.<BR>E. नान्दी as above, and वादिन् who speaks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=384-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नापि
नापि ind. Not even.<BR> E. न not, and अपि even.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=384-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नापित|नापितः
नापित m. (-तः) A barber.<BR> E. न negative, आप् to obtain, (respect.) तन्<BR>Unādi affix, and इट् augment शूद्रायां क्षत्रियात् जाते सङ्कीर्णजातिभेदे ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=384-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नापितशाला
नापितशाला f. (-ला) A barber's shop,<BR> E. नापित, and शाला house; also<BR>with कन् added in the fem. form, नापितशालिका f. (-का ।)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=384-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नापित्य|नापित्यं|नापित्यः
नापित्य m. (-त्य) The business of a barber.<BR> E. नापित and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=384-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाभक|नाभकः
नाभक m. (-कः) A myrobalan, (Terminalia chebula.)<BR> E. नभ-ण्वुल्, वनतिक्तेवृक्षे ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=384-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाभि|नाभिः
नाभि f. (-भिः-भी)<BR>	 1. The nave of a wheel.<BR>	 2. Musk.<BR>	 mf. (-भिः or भी) The<BR>navel, m. (-भिः)<BR>	 1. An emperor, a sovereign, a lord, para-<BR>mount.<BR>	 2. The centre, focus, chief point.<BR>	 3. A king, a chief.<BR>	 4. A<BR>Kṣatriya or Hindu of the regal and military tribe.<BR>	 5. The son<BR>of PRIYAVRATA.<BR>	 6. A race, a family.<BR> E. नह् to bind, Unādi affix<BR>इञ्, and भ substituted for ह.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=384-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाभिकण्टक|नाभिकण्टकः
नाभिकण्टक m. (-कः) Ruptured or protruded navel.<BR> E. नाभि a navel,<BR>and कण्टक a thorn. (गांँड ।)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=384-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाभिगुड
नाभिगुड(ल)क m. (-कः) A prominent or ruptured navel.<BR> E. नाभि, and गुडक<BR>a ball or lump.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=385-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाभिगोलक|नाभिगोलकः
नाभिगोलक m. (-कः) A prominent or ruptured navel.<BR> E. नाभि, and गोलक<BR>a lump or ball.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=385-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाभिच्छेदन|नाभिछेदन
नाभिच्छेदन n. (-नं) Division of the umbilical cord.<BR> E. नाभि, and छेदन cut-<BR>ting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=385-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाभिज|नाभिजः
नाभिज m. (-जः) BRAMHĀ.<BR> E. नाभि navel, and ज born; BRAMHĀ appear-<BR>ing from the lotus which sprung from the navel of VIṢṆU.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=385-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाभिजन्मन्
नाभिजन्मन् m. (-न्मा) BRAMHĀ.<BR> E. नाभि the navel, and जन्मन् birth: see the<BR>last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=385-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाभिनाडी
नाभिनाडी f. (-डी) the umbilical cord.<BR> E. नाभि and नाडी a vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=385-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाभिनाला
नाभिनाला f. (-ला) The umbilical cord<BR> E. नाभि the navel, and नाला a<BR>string, a vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=385-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाभिभू
नाभिभू m. (-भूः) BRAMHĀ.<BR> E. नाभि, and भू born: see नाभिज.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=385-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाभिवर्द्धन
नाभिवर्द्धन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Division of the Umbilical cord.<BR>	 2. Umbilical hernia.<BR>3. Corpulency.<BR> E. नाभि, and वर्द्धन increasing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=385-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाभील|नाभीलं
नाभील n. (-लं)<BR>	 1. The groin of a woman.<BR>	 2. A prominent or ruptured<BR>navel.<BR>	 3. pain.<BR>	 4. The hollow of the navel.<BR> E. नाभि the navel, लच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=385-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाभ्य|नाभ्यं|नाभ्यः
नाभ्य mfn. (-भ्यः-भ्या-भ्यं) Umbilical, of or relating to the navel.<BR> E. नाभि the<BR>navel, and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=385-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाभ्यावर्त्त|नाभ्यावर्त|नाभ्यावर्तः
नाभ्यावर्त्त m. (-र्त्तः) The hollow or pit of the navel.<BR> E. नाभि a navel, आवर्त्त<BR>a round.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=385-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाम
नाम ind. A particle implying.<BR>	 1. Certainty.<BR>	 2. Possibility.<BR>	 3. Anger.<BR>4. Reproach.<BR>	 5. Consent, promise.<BR>	 6. Recollection.<BR>	 7. Surprise.<BR>	 8.<BR>Pretence, &c. as हिमालयो नाम नगाधिपः Himālaya, evidently the<BR>king of mountains, इह नाम सीता भविष्यति SITĀ will perhaps be<BR>here, &c.<BR> E. णम् to call or address, affix ड. deriv. irr. नाम्यते नामि-ड ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=385-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नामकरण|नामकरणं
नामकरण n. (-णं) Naming a child first after birth.<BR> E. नाम, and करण<BR>making.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=385-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नामग्रह|नामग्रहः
नामग्रह n. (-हं) Addressing by name,<BR> E. नाम and ग्रह taking; also नामग्रहण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=385-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नामद्वादशी
नामद्वादशी f. (-शी) A religious ceremony, worshipping DURGĀ daily<BR>under one of twelve appellations.<BR> E. नाम, and द्वादशी twelfth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=385-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नामधेय|नामधेयं
नामधेय n. (-यं) A name or appellation.<BR> E. नाम a name, and स्वार्थे धेय aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=385-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नामन्
नामन् n. (म) A name, an appellation.<BR> E. म्रा to be minded or remember-<BR>ed, मनिन् Unādi affix, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=385-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नामशेष|नामशेषः
नामशेष mfn. (-षः-षा-षं) Dead, deceased.<BR>	 m. (-षः) Dying, death.<BR> E. नाम a<BR>name, and शेष end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=385-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नामापराध|नामापराधः
नामापराध m. (-धः) Abusing a respectable object, as a pious man, a<BR>deity by name.<BR> E. नाम, and अपराध offence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=385-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नामित
नामित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Bent, bent down, bowed.<BR> E. णम् to bow, causal<BR>form, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=385-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाय|नायः
नाय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. Guiding, directing, (morally or physically.)<BR>	 2. Policy.<BR>3. Obtaining.<BR>	 4. Means, expedient.<BR> E. णी to guide, &c. affix ण or<BR>घञ्; also with अच् affix नय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=385-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नायक|नायकः
नायक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A guide, a leader, a conductor.<BR>	 2. A chief, a head,<BR>pre-eminent, principal.<BR>	 3. A general, a commander, 4. The cen-<BR>tral gem of a necklace.<BR>	 5. (In Erotic poetry,) The man, the<BR>husband or lover.<BR>	 f. (-यिका)<BR>	 1. mistress, a wife, the female in the<BR>amatory poetry of the Hindūs.<BR>	 2. A sort of goddess, an inferior<BR>form of DURGĀ, and attendant upon her: there are eight Nā-<BR>yikās.<BR> E. णी to guide, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=385-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नायकाधिप|नायकाधिपः
नायकाधिप m. (-पः) A king, a sovereign, a prince.<BR> E. नायक a chief, and<BR>अधिप lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=385-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नार|नारं|नारः
नार mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>	 1. Relating to men, human, mortal, &c.<BR>	 2. Spiri-<BR>tual.<BR>	 nf. (-रं-रा) Water.<BR>	 m. (-रः) A calf.<BR>	 n. (-रं) A multitude of men.<BR>E. नर, and अण् affix or न negative, ऋ to go, अप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=385-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नारक|नारकः
नारक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Infernal, hellish.<BR>	 m. (-कः) Hell or the infernal<BR>regions.<BR> E. नरक hell. अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=385-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नारकिन्
नारकिन् mfn. (-की-किनी-कि) Infernal, being in hell, condemned to or<BR>deserving it.<BR> E. नारक, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=385-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नारकीट|नारकीटः
नारकीट m. (-टः)<BR>	 1. A sort of worm.<BR>	 2. A deceiver, one who disappoints<BR>expectations excited by himself.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=385-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नारङ्ग|नारंग|नारङ्गं|नारंगः|नारङ्गः
नारङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>	 1. The juice of the pepper plant.<BR>	 2. An animal, one of<BR>twins.<BR>	 3. A catamite.<BR>	 4. The orange tree.<BR> E. नार many men, and<BR>ग who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=385-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नारद|नारदः
नारद m. (-दः) A name of NĀRADA, born from the hip of BRAMHĀ and<BR>one of the ten divine Munis or Ṛṣis; he is a friend of KṚṢṆA,<BR>a celebrated legislator, and inventor of the Vinā or lute. He is<BR>often described as engaged in conveying messages and causing dis-<BR>cord among gods and men.<BR> E. नार men, and दा to give, (instruc-<BR>tion,) ड affix; or नार water, and द who gives; offering sacrifices<BR>to the manes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=385-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाराच|नाराचः
नाराच m. (-चः)<BR>	 1. An iron arrow. (E. नार men, आङ् before, चम् to eat<BR>or consume, affix ड; destroying hosts of men.)<BR>	 2. A bad or cloudy<BR>day.<BR>	 3. A species of the Dhriti metre. (E. नार water, आचम् to<BR>spit, affix ड.)<BR>	 f. (-ची) A goldsmith's scales, a fine or assay balance.<BR>E. नाराच an iron arrow, and ङीष् diminutive affix; also with कन्<BR>added in the fem. from, नाराचिका f. (-का). or नरान् आचामति आ +<BR>चम-डि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=385-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नारायण|नारायणः
नारायण m. (-णः)<BR>	 1. A name of VIṢṆU, but especially considered as<BR>the deity who was before all worlds.<BR>	 2. A sage, and brother of<BR>नर । The two great sages, while practising penance at the<BR>Badarikāshram on the Himālaya, Indra being afraid lest he<BR>might be deprived of his throne sent Heavenly nymphs to disturb<BR>their devotions; But Nārāyana put these damsels to shame by<BR>creating a nymph (Urvashi by name) from his thigh far excelling<BR>Indra's nymph's in beauty.<BR>	 3. A valiant combatant.<BR>	 f. (-णी)<BR>	 1. A<BR>name of DURGĀ.<BR>	 2. A name of LAKṢMĪ, the goddess of prosperity,<BR>and wife of VIṢṆU.<BR>	 3. GANGĀ.<BR>	 4. A plant, (Asparagus racemosa.)<BR>E. नारा the primeval waters, derived from नर the spirit of God,<BR>whence they originated, and अयन place of coming or moving;<BR>he who moved over the waters before creation; the word has<BR>several etymologies, as नर the spirit or soul of the universe, अण्<BR>affix, नार appertaining to it, the actions or emotions of the soul,<BR>and अयन pervading, influencing; again नार multitudes, man kind,<BR>and अयन place; present amongst all men, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=385-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नारायणक्षेत्र|नारायणक्षेत्रं
नारायणक्षेत्र n. (-त्रं) Four cubits on either side of the stream of the<BR>Ganges,<BR> E. नारायण and क्षेत्र shrine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=385-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नारायणतैल|नारायणतैलं
नारायणतैल n. (-लं) An oil of great reputed efficacy in many complaints,<BR>expressed from a variety of plants.<BR> E. नारायण and तैल oil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=385-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नारायणप्रिय|नारायणप्रियः
नारायणप्रिय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Attached to KṚṢṆA or VIṢṆU.<BR>	 m. (-यः)<BR>ŚIVA.<BR> E. नारायण, and प्रिय fond of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=385-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नारायणास्त्र|नारायणास्त्रं
नारायणास्त्र n. (-स्त्रं) A weapon of undefined form and mystical nature.<BR>E. नारायण and अस्त्र weapon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=385-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नारिक
नारिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>	 1. Watery, aqueous.<BR>	 2. Spiritual.<BR> E. नर or नार<BR>and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=385-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नारिकेर|नारिकेरः
नारिकेर m. (-रः) The cocoanut: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=385-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नारिकेल|नारिकेलः
नारिकेल mf. (-लः-ली) The cocoanut.<BR> E. नारिक watery (place), ईर् to go<BR>or grow, affix क, and र optionally changed to ल; also with इन्,<BR>नारिकेलि, and ड being substituted for र, नाडिकेर, &c. नल-इन् नालिः<BR>केन वायुना जलेन वा इलति चलति, इल-क-कर्म-रलयोरैक्यम् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=385-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नारी
नारी f. (-री)<BR>	 1. A woman in general, a female.<BR>	 2. A species of the<BR>Madhya metre.<BR> E. नर a man, अञ् and ङीप् affs. or नृ + नर + वा जातौ<BR>ङीष् निपातने ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=385-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नारीकवच|नारीकवचः
नारीकवच m. (-चः) A king of the solar line, the son of ASMAKA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=385-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नारीकेल|नारीकेलः
नारीकेल mf. (-लः-ली) The cocoanut.<BR>	 f. (-ली) Fermented liquor made<BR>from the water of the cocoanut: see नारिकेल &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=385-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नारीच|नारीचं
नारीच n. (-चं) An esculent root, Arum colocasia: see नाडीच (नालिता)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=385-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नारीतरङ्गक|नारीतरंगक|नारीतरङ्गकः
नारीतरङ्गक m. (-कः) A catamite.<BR> E. नारी a woman, तरङ्ग capricious, and<BR>कन् affix of comparison. नारिं तरङ्गयति तरङ्ग + कृतौ-णिच्-ण्वुल् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=385-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नारीदूषण|नारीदूषणं
नारीदूषण n. (-णं) A vice or breach of duty in a woman, of which six<BR>cases are reckoned, drinking spirits, keeping bad company, quit-<BR>ting a husband, rambling abroad, and sleeping or dwelling in a<BR>strange house.<BR> E. नारी a woman, दूषण defect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=386-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नारीप्रसङ्ग|नारीप्रसंग|नारीप्रसंगः
नारीप्रसङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः) Libertinism, lechery.<BR> E. नारी, and प्रसङ्ग addiction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=386-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नारीयान
नारीयान n. (-नं) A litter or other conveyance for women.<BR> E. नारी, and<BR>यान a carriage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=386-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नार्य्यङ्ग|नार्यङ्ग|नार्यंग|नार्यंगः|नार्यङ्गः|नार्य्यङ्गः
नार्य्यङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः) The orange tree; also नागरङ्ग । नार्य्यं नरहितसम्बन्धिनं गच्छति<BR>गम-ड । मुम् च ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=386-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाल|नालं|नालः
नाल mfn. (-लः-ला or -ली-लं)<BR>	 1. A hollow or tubular stalk, the stalk of<BR>the water lily, &c.<BR>	 2. Any pipe or tube.<BR>	 3. A handle.<BR>	 n. (-लं) Yellow<BR>orpiment.<BR>	 f. (-ली)<BR>	 1. A stalk or culm..<BR>	 2. An instrument for perfora-<BR>ting an elephant's ear.<BR>	 3. A period of time, a Ghati, twenty-four<BR>minutes.<BR>	 4. Any tubular vessel of the body.<BR>	 5. The pulse.<BR> E. णल्<BR>to bind, affix ण, fem. affix टाप्, and ङीष्, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=386-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नालि|नालिः
नालि(ली) f. (-लिः or ली)<BR>	 1. Any tubular vessel of the body.<BR>	 2. A hollow<BR>stalk.<BR> E. ल interchanged with ड; see नाडि. नल-णिच्-इन् वा ङीप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=386-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नालिक|नालिकः
नालिक m. (-कः) A buffalo.<BR>	 n. (-कं) A lotus.<BR>	 f. (-का)<BR>	 1. A tubular stalk.<BR>2. An instrument for piercing an elephant's ear.<BR>	 3. A plant,<BR>commonly Charmaghās.<BR>	 4. A sort of potherb, (Hibiscus canna-<BR>binus.)<BR>	 5. Any plant growing on a hollow stem, as San, safflower,<BR>a mushroom, &c.<BR>	 6. A flute.<BR> E. नाली as above, and कन् aff. or नाल्या<BR>कायति कै-क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=386-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नालिकास्त्र
नालिकास्त्र n. (-स्त्रम्) Cannon.<BR> E. नालिक as above, and अस्त्र a missile weapon.<BR>(क्षुद्रनालिक means a pistol.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=386-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नालिकेर|नालिकेरः
नालिकेर m. (-रः) The cocoanut.<BR> E. नल् to bind, affix इन, नालि a leaf,<BR>&c. क air, wind, and इर what goes; fluttering in the wind. see<BR>नारिकेल ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=386-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नालिजङ्घ|नालिजङ्घः
नालिजङ्घ m. (-ङ्घः) A raven or the carrion crow.<BR> E. नालि a tube, and<BR>जङ्घा the leg.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=386-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नालिता
नालिता f. (-ता) An esculent root, (Arum colocasia.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=386-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नालीक|नालीकः
नालीक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. An arrow.<BR>	 2. A dart, a javelin, a pike.<BR>	 3. A lotus.<BR>4. The fibrous stalk of the lotus.<BR>	 n. (-कं) An assemblage of lotus<BR>flowers.<BR> E. नाली a fibrous stalk, affix ठन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=386-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नालीकिनी
नालीकिनी f. (-नी) A multitude of lotus flowers.<BR> E. नालीक, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=386-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नालीव्रण|नालीव्रणः
नालीव्रण m. (-णः) A fistulous or sinus sore; see नाडीव्रण, ल and ड being<BR>interchanged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=386-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नावमिक
नावमिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Ninth.<BR> E. नवम and, ठञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=386-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाविक|नाविकः
नाविक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Belonging to a vessel, or a boat, &c.<BR>	 m. (-कः)<BR>	 1.<BR>The helmsman of a vessel, the steersman, the pilot.<BR>	 2. A. sailor.<BR>E. नौ a boat, affix ठन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=386-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाव्य|नाव्यं
नाव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>	 1. Navigable.<BR>	 2. Belonging to a boat.<BR>	 n. (-व्यं)<BR>Newness, novelty.<BR> E. नौ a boat or vessel, and यत् affix; or नव new,<BR>ष्यञ् aff. नावा तीर्य्यते असौ, नवस्य भावः वा ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=386-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाश|नाशः
नाश m. (-शः)<BR>	 1. Annihilation, loss, destruction, disappearance, ruin.<BR>	 2.<BR>Death.<BR>	 3. Flight, retreat.<BR>	 4. Abandonment, desertion. (In Arith-<BR>metic.)<BR>	 5. Elimination.<BR> E. णश् to cease to be, affix भावे घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=386-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाशन
नाशन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Destruction, perishing.<BR>	 2. Removal, expulsion.<BR> E. णश्<BR>to perish, affix णिच्. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=386-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाशयत्
नाशयत् mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्) destroying annihilating.<BR> E. णश् to perish,<BR>causal form, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=386-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाशित
नाशित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Destroyed.<BR> E. नश् to perish, causal form. क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=386-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाशिन्
नाशिन् mfn. (-शी-शिनी-शि)<BR>	 1. Destructive, destroying, a destroyer.<BR>	 2.<BR>Perishing, being lost or destroyed.<BR> E. नश् to cease to be, in the<BR>causal from, affix इनि; or नाश, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=386-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाष्टिक|नाष्टिकः
नाष्टिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Belonging or relating to any thing lost.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-कः) The owner of any thing lost.<BR> E. नष्ट, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=386-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नासत्य
नासत्य m. du. (-त्यौ) The two sons of AŚHWINĪ, and physicians of<BR>Svarga.<BR>	 f. (-त्या) The constellation AŚHWINĪ.<BR> E. न not, असत्य<BR>impure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=386-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नासा
नासा f. (-सा)<BR>	 1. The nose.<BR>	 2. The upper timber of a door.<BR>	 3. The trunk<BR>of an elephant.<BR> E. णस् to sound, to stand, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=386-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नासाछिन्नी|नासाच्छिन्नी
नासाछिन्नी f. (-न्नी) A sort of bird; also पूर्णिका.<BR> E. नासा the nose, छिन्न<BR>cut, fem. affix ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=386-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नासादक्षिणावर्त्त|नासादक्षिणावर्त
नासादक्षिणावर्त्त m. (-र्त्तः) Wearing the nose-ring in the right nostril by<BR>women who have money and children.<BR> E. नासा the nose, दक्षिण<BR>the right, and आवर्त्त a turning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=386-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नासादारु|नासादारुः
नासादारु m. (-रुः) The upper timber of a door: see नासा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=386-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नासानाह|नासानाहः
नासानाह m. (-हः) Thickening of the membrance of the nose, stoppage<BR>of the nostrils.<BR> E. नासा, and नाह binding<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=386-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नासापरिस्राव|नासापरिस्रावः
नासापरिस्राव m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. Running at the nose.<BR>	 2. A running cold.<BR> E. नासा<BR>and परिस्राव flow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=386-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नासारन्ध्र|नासारंध्र
नासारन्ध्र n. (-न्ध्रं) The nostril.<BR> E. नासा, and रन्ध्र a hole.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=386-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नासालु|नासालुः
नासालु m. (-लुः) A plant, commonly Kāyaphal: see कट्फल.<BR> E. नासा<BR>the nose, and लु to cut, affix डु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=386-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नासावंश|नासावंशः
नासावंश m. (-शः) The bridge of the nose.<BR> E. नासा and वंश bamboo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=386-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नासावामावर्त्त|नासावामावर्त|नासावामावर्तः
नासावामावर्त्त m. (-र्त्तः) Wearing the nose-ring in the left nostril, a<BR>mark of sorrow or distress.<BR> E. नासा the nose. वाम the left side,<BR>आवर्त्त a turning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=386-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नासाशोष
नासाशोष m. (-षः) Dryness of the nostrils.<BR> E. नासा and शोष drying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=386-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नासिकन्धम|नासिकंधम|नासिकन्धमः
नासिकन्धम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं) Blowing or breathing through the nose,<BR>snoring, &c.<BR> E. नासिका the nose, ध्मा to blow &c. affix खश्. मुम्<BR>ह्रस्वश्च ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=386-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नासिकन्धय|नासिकंधय|नासिकन्धयः
नासिकन्धय mfn. (-यः-यी-यं) Drinking through the nose.<BR> E. नासिका, and घेट् to drink, affix. खञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=386-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नासिका
नासिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. The nose.<BR>	 2. The upper timber, or nose as it<BR>were, of a door.<BR>	 3. A name of the nymph AŚHwini.<BR> E. नासा as<BR>above, affix कन् fem. form. or नास शब्दे ण्वुल् । The same as नासा ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=386-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नासिकाग्र
नासिकाग्र m. (-ग्रं) The tip of the nose.<BR> E. नासिका, and अग्र end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=386-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नासिकामल|नासिकामलं|नासिकामलः
नासिकामल n. (-लं) The mucus of the nose, snot.<BR> E. नासिका, and मल<BR>excrement; it may also be नासामल । शिङ्घाणे ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=386-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नासिक्य|नासिक्यं|नासिक्यः
नासिक्य m. du. (-क्यौ)<BR>	 1. The two sons of Aśhwini.<BR>	 2. A nasal sound.<BR>n. (-क्यं) The nose.<BR> E. नासिका, and यत् affix of identity or descent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=386-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नासिक्यक|नासिक्यकं
नासिक्यक n. (-कं) The nose.<BR> E. कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=386-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नासीर|नासीरं
नासीर n. (-रं) Advancing or skirmishing in front of an army, leaving<BR>the line, and defying the enemy by shouts and gestures.<BR>	 m. (-रः)<BR>The van, or a champion who advances before the line.<BR> E. णास् to<BR>sound, affix ईरन्; or नासाय शब्दाय इर्त्ते इर-क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=386-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नास्ति
नास्ति ind. Nonexistence, not so, it is not.<BR> E. न negative, and अस्ति is,<BR>third person, singular, present tense of अस् to be.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=386-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नास्तिक|नास्तिकः
नास्तिक m. (-कः) An atheist, but applied by the orthodox Hindūs, to<BR>any one who denies the divine authority of the Vedas, or doubts<BR>the legends of the Purānas, or a future life or the existence of a<BR>ruler, or creator of the universe.<BR> E. नास्ति there is not (a god &c.)<BR>and ठन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=386-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नास्तिकता
नास्तिकता f. (-ता) Atheism, denial of the deity, of a future state, of<BR>the divinity of the Vedas; Buddhism, heresy, &c.<BR> E. तल् abs-<BR>tract affix added to the preceding: also with त्व नास्तिकत्व, or with<BR>यत् affix नास्तिक्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=386-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नास्तिक्य|नास्तिक्यं
नास्तिक्य n. (-क्यं) Infidelity, atheism, heresy.<BR> E. नास्तिक, and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=386-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नास्तित्व
नास्तित्व n. (-त्वं) Nonexistence.<BR> E. त्व added to नास्ति; also with तल् affix<BR>नास्तिता; ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=386-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नास्तिद|नास्तिदः
नास्तिद m. (-दः) The mango tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=386-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नास्य|नास्यं
नास्य n. (-स्यं) The rein of an ox passed through the septum of the<BR>nostrils.<BR> E. नासा the nose, शरीरावयवत्वात् यत् aff. नासायां भवम् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=386-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाह|नाहः
नाह m. (-हः)<BR>	 1. Binding, confinement.<BR>	 2. A trap, a snare for catching<BR>deer, &c.<BR>	 3. Obstruction in any organ or secretion of the body,<BR>as costiveness, &c.<BR> E. णह् to bind, affix भावे घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=386-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाहल|नाहलः
नाहल m. (-लः) A man of a barbarous or outcast tribe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=386-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाहुषि|नाहुषिः
नाहुषि m. (-षिः) The name of a king; also YAYĀTI.<BR> E. नहुष, and इञ्<BR>affix of descent. Also नाहुष ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=386-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःकारण
निःकारण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Causeless, unfounded.<BR> E. निर् neg. कारण<BR>cause.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=387-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःकासन
निःकासन n. (-नं) Expulsion, exile, turning out.<BR> E. निर्, and कस् to go,<BR>causal form, ल्युट् affix; also निःकाशन ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=387-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःकासित|निःकासितः
निःकासित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Turned out or forth, expelled, removed. E.<BR>निर् out, कस् to go, in the causal form, affix क्त; also निष्कासित,<BR>निःकाशित and निष्काशित ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=387-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःक्रामित|निःक्रामितः
निःक्रामित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Expelled, turned out.<BR> E. निः for निर् out,<BR>क्रामित caused to go, also निष्क्रामित ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=387-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःक्षत्र
निःक्षत्र mfn. (-त्रः-त्रा-त्रं) Having none of the military tribe, (in a city,<BR>&c.)<BR> E. निर् not, चत्र a Kṣatriya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=387-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःक्षिप्त
निःक्षिप्त mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं)<BR>	 1. Thrown or sent away.<BR>	 2. Spent.<BR>	 3. Passed. E.<BR>निर् before, क्षिप्त to throw, &c. affix क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=387-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःक्षिप्य
निःक्षिप्य ind.<BR>	 1. Having thrown or sent away.<BR>	 2. Having spent, (as<BR>time.)<BR>	 3. Having wiped away, (as tears,) &c.<BR> E. निर् before, क्षिप्<BR>to throw, and ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=387-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःक्षेप|निःक्षेपः
निःक्षेप m. (-पः)<BR>	 1. Throwing, sending, putting away.<BR>	 2. Spending. 3<BR>Passing, (as time.)<BR>	 4. Wiping away, (as tears)<BR> E. निर् and क्षिप् to<BR>throw, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=387-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःप्रभ|निःप्रभः
निःप्रभ mfn. (-भः-भा-भं) Gloomy, dark, obscured.<BR> E. निः for निर् priva-<BR>tive, and प्रभा light; also निष्प्रभ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=387-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःफल
निःफल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Fruitless, barren.<BR> E. निर् neg. फल fruit, more<BR>commonly निष्फल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=387-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःशंसय
निःशंसय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Undoubted.<BR> E. निः for निर्, शंसय doubt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=387-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःशङ्क
निःशङ्क mfn. (-ङ्कः-ङ्का-ङ्कं) Fearless.<BR> E. निर् and शङ्का apprehension.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=387-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःशलाक|निःशलाकः
निःशलाक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Solitary, private.<BR> E. निः for निर् privative, and<BR>शलाका the maina; not even frequented by birds; also निश्शलाक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=387-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःशब्द|निःशब्दः
निःशब्द mfn. (-ब्दः-ब्दा-ब्दं) Silent, voiceless.<BR> E. निः for निर्, and शब्द sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=387-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःशूक|निःशूकः
निःशूक m. (-कः) Rice without any awn or beard.<BR> E. निः for निर् and<BR>शूक beard of corn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=387-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःशेष|निःशेषं
निःशेष mfn. (-षः-षा-षं) Complete, entire.<BR> E. निः for निर् negative, and शेष<BR>remainder; also निश्शेष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=387-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःशोध्य|निःशोध्यं
निःशोध्य mfn. (-ध्यः-ध्या-ध्यं) Cleansed, cleared, purified.<BR> E. निः for निर्<BR>implying completion, and शोध्य pure; also निश्शोध्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=387-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःश्रयणी
निःश्रयणी f. (-णी) Wooden steps, a ladder, a staircase.<BR> E. निः for निर्<BR>out, forth, श्रि to go, affix ल्युट्; also with अच् affix, and इनि added,<BR>निःश्रयिणी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=387-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःश्रेणि|निःश्रेणिः
निःश्रेणि f. (-णिः-णी)<BR>	 1. A ladder or staircase, a flight of steps.<BR>	 2. The<BR>wild date tree.<BR> E. निः for निर् implying certainty, and श्रेणी a line<BR>also निश्श्रेणी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=387-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निश्रेयसः
निश्रेयसः n. (-यः)<BR>	 1. Final beatitude, the release of the soul from the<BR>body, and its reunion with the primary and universal spirit.<BR>	 2.<BR>Happiness, welfare.<BR>	 3. Knowledge, learning.<BR>	 4. Belief, faith,<BR>devotedness.<BR>	 5. Apprehension, conception.<BR>	 m. (-याः) A name of<BR>ŚIVA.<BR> E. निः for निर् implying eternity or certainty, श्रेयस् best, अच्<BR>added; also निश्श्रेयस.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=387-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःश्वसन|निःश्वसनं
निःश्वसन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Sighing, &c.<BR>	 2. Breathing out.<BR> E. निर् and श्वसन<BR>breathing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=387-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःश्वसित
निःश्वसित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Sighed, sig hing.<BR>	 2. Breathing out.<BR>	 n.<BR>(-तं)<BR>	 1. Expiration.<BR>	 2. Sighing.<BR> E. निर् and श्वस् to breathe, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=387-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःश्वस्य
निःश्वस्य ind. Having sighed.<BR> E. निर् and श्वस् to breathe, affix ल्यप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=387-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःश्वास|निःश्वासः
निःश्वास m. (-सः)<BR>	 1. Breathing out, expiration.<BR>	 2. Sighing.<BR> E. निर्, and<BR>श्वस् to breathe, भावे घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=387-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःश्वासपरम
निःश्वासपरम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं) Sorrowful.<BR> E. निःश्वास and परम best.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=387-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःषमम्
निःषमम् ind.<BR>	 1. A particle of reproof, (improperly, unseasonably.) 2<BR>A term of regret, (das!)<BR> E. निर् not, सम equal to, र is changed to<BR>Visarga, and स becomes ष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=387-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःसङ्ग|निःसंग|निःसंगः|निःसङ्गः
निःसङ्ग mfn. (-ङ्गः-ङ्गा-ङ्गं)<BR>	 1. Separated, unconnected.<BR>	 2. Regardless,<BR>indifferent, free from attachment or desire.<BR> E. निर् not, सङ्ग associa-<BR>tion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=387-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःसंज्ञ
निःसंज्ञ mfn. (-ज्ञः-ज्ञा-ज्ञं) Senseless, insensible.<BR> E. निर् not, संज्ञा sign of<BR>life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=387-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःसत्य
निःसत्य mfn. (-त्यः-त्या-त्यं) False, untrue.<BR> E. निर् neg. सत्य true.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=387-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःसत्यता
निःसत्यता f. (-ता) Insincerity, falsehood.<BR> E. निर् neg. सत्यता truth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=387-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःसत्व
निःसत्व mfn. (-त्वः-त्वा-त्वं)<BR>	 1. Weak, impotent.<BR>	 2. Insignificant, mean,<BR>low.<BR>	 3. Nonexistent.<BR>	 4. Insubstantial.<BR>	 n. (-त्वं)<BR>	 1. Insignificance,<BR>absence of power or consideration.<BR>	 2. Nonexistence.<BR> E. निर् neg.<BR>सत्व substance, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=387-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःस
निःस(ष)न्धि mfn. (-न्धिः-न्धिः-न्धि) Firm, well-knit, compact.<BR> E. निर् not, सन्धि<BR>junction; the joints of which are not perceivable. निष्क्रान्तः सन्धेः<BR>सुश्लिष्टित्वात् निरादिस० सुषमा-षत्वम् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=387-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःसम्पात|निःसंपात|निःसंपातः|निःसम्पातः
निःसम्पात m. (-तः)<BR>	 1. Without motion.<BR>	 2. Midnight.<BR> E. निर् neg. सम्पात<BR>going, from पत् to go, with सम् prefix, and घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=387-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःसरण|निःसरणं
निःसरण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Death, dying.<BR>	 2. A means or expedient.<BR>	 3. Exit, a<BR>going forth or out.<BR>	 4. Final beatitude.<BR>	 5. The entrance into a house<BR>or town, &c. the gate, the gate-way.<BR> E. निर् forth or out, सृ, to go,<BR>भावे ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=387-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःसह
निःसह mfn. (-हः-हा-हं)<BR>	 1. Intolerable, unbearable.<BR>	 2. Irresistible.<BR>	 3.<BR>Unable to support or bear.<BR> E. निर् neg. सह bearing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=387-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःसहत्व
निःसहत्व n. (-त्वं)<BR>	 1. Inability to bear or support.<BR>	 2. Impatience, unen-<BR>durance.<BR> E. निःसह, and त्व affix; also with तल् निःसहता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=387-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःसाध्वस
निःसाध्वस mfn. (-सः-सा-सं) Bold, fearless.<BR> E. निर् and साध्वस fear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=387-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःसार|निःसारः
निःसार mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>	 1. Sapless, pithless.<BR>	 2. Worthless, vain, insubs-<BR>tantial.<BR>	 m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A plant, (Trophis aspera.)<BR>	 2. Going forth.<BR>	 f. (-रा)<BR>The plantain.<BR> E. निर् privative, सार essence, pith; or निर् out, सृ<BR>to go, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=387-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःसारण|निःसारणं
निःसारण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Going forth or out.<BR>	 2. The entrance of a house or<BR>town, &c. the passage, the road of ingress and egress.<BR> E. निर् forth<BR>or out, and सृ to go णिच्ल्युट् aff; see निःसरण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=387-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःसारित|निःसारितः
निःसारित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Turned forth or out, expelled, dismissed. E.<BR>निर् out, and सारित caused to go. निर सृ-णिच् कर्मणि क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=387-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःसुख
निःसुख mfn. (-खः-खा-खं)<BR>	 1. Disagreeable, distressing.<BR>	 2. Unhappy. E.<BR>निर् neg. सुख pleasure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=387-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःसृत
निःसृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Gone forth or out.<BR> E. निर्, and सृ to go, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=387-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःस्नेह|निःस्नेहः
निःस्नेह mfn. (-हः-हा-हं)<BR>	 1. Dry, not greasy or unctuous.<BR>	 2. Cold, in-<BR>sensible, unfeeling.<BR>	 f. (-हा) Linseed, (Linum utilitissimum.) E.<BR>निर् forth, out, and स्नेह oil; whence oil is extracted or expressed,<BR>&c. or निर् privative, स्नेह oil or affection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=387-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःस्पृह
निःस्पृह mfn. (-हः-हा-हं)<BR>	 1. Free from desire.<BR>	 2. Disregarding, indiffer-<BR>ent to.<BR> E. निर् neg. स्पृहा wish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=387-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःस्राव|निःस्रावः
निःस्राव m. (-वः) The moisture or water of boiled rice.<BR> E. निर forth, and<BR>स्राव what is oozing or निर-स्रु-ण (फेन) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=387-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःस्व|निःस्वः
निःस्व mfn. (-स्वः-स्वा-स्वं) Poor, indigent.<BR> E. निर् not, nothing, स्व own property.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=387-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःस्वादु
निःस्वादु mfn. (-दुः-दुः-दु) Insipid, tasteless.<BR> E. निर् neg. स्वादु sweet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=387-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नि|निः
नि ind.<BR>	 1. In, within; on, upon: a particle and prefix.<BR>	 2. A negative<BR>or prohibitive particle.<BR>	 3. A particle implying certainty, affirma-<BR>tion, proximity, continuance, doubt, intensity, fulness, Lowness,<BR>order, skill, wrong, group, &c. see the following compounds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=387-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकट|निकटं|निकटः
निकट mfn. (-टः-टा-टं)<BR>	 1. Near, proximate.<BR>	 2. Kinless, solitary.<BR> E. नि,<BR>and कटच् affix; or नि prefixed to कट् to go to or towards, affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=387-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकर|निकरः
निकर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A flock or multitude.<BR>	 2. A heap, a bundle.<BR>	 3. Pith,<BR>sap, essence.<BR>	 4. Suitable or proper gift.<BR>	 5. A treasure, especially<BR>belonging to KUVERA: see निधि.<BR> E. नि in or upon, कॄ to throw,<BR>affix अप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=387-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकर्षण|निकर्षणं
निकर्षण m. (-णः)<BR>	 1. An open space or sort of play-ground in or near<BR>a town.<BR>	 2. A court at the entrance to a house.<BR>	 3. A neighbourhood.<BR>4. A plot of ground not ploughed.<BR> E. नि, with कर्षण ploughing; so<BR>prepared.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=387-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकष|निकषः
निकष(स) m. (-षः-सः) The touch-stone.<BR>	 f. (-षा) The mother of the imps or<BR>goblins.<BR> E. नि prefixed to कष् to injure, affix घ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=387-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकषा
निकषा ind.<BR>	 1. Near, proximate.<BR>	 2. In the middle, betwixt, between.<BR>	 3.<BR>The mother of a Rākshasha.<BR> E. नि prefixed to कष् to hurt, UNĀDI<BR>affix आ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=388-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकषात्मज|निकषात्मजः
निकषात्मज m. (-जः) A Rākshasa, a sort of goblin.<BR> E. निकषा the mother<BR>of the race, and आत्मज a son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=388-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकस|निकसः
निकस m. (-सः) A touch-stone: see निकष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=388-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकाम|निकामं|निकामः
निकाम n. adv. (-मं) Voluntarily, willingly, implying certainty.<BR> E. नि, काम<BR>will.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=388-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकाय|निकायः
निकाय m. (-यः) An assemblage of persons performing like duties, a<BR>congregation, an audience.<BR>	 2. A flock, a multitude.<BR>	 3. A butt, a<BR>mark.<BR>	 4. A house, habitation.<BR>	 5. The Supreme Being.<BR>	 6. The body.<BR>E. नि in or within, चि to collect, affix घञ्, and क substituted<BR>for the radical initial.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=388-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकाय्य|निकाय्यः
निकाय्य m. (-य्यः) A house.<BR> E. नि in or within, चि to collect, affix ण्यत्<BR>कुत्वम् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=388-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकार|निकारः
निकार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Opposition, contradiction.<BR>	 2. Injury, wrong, offence.<BR>3. wickedness; malice.<BR>	 4. Abuse, reproach, disrespect.<BR>	 5. Raising,<BR>tossing or lifting up.<BR>	 6. Piling or winnowing corn.<BR>	 7. Killing. E.<BR>नि depreciative prefix, कृ to make, or कॄ to throw, affix भावे घञ्<BR>or अप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=388-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकारण|निकारणं
निकारण n. (-णं) Killing, slaughter.<BR> E. नि prefixed to कॄ to injure, affix<BR>ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=388-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकाष|निकाषः
निकाष m. (-षः) Rubbing, Scratching.<BR> E. नि before, कष् to hurt, घञ् aff<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=388-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकास|निकासः
निकास(श) mfn. (-सः-सा-सं)<BR>	 1. Likeness. (in composition:)<BR>	 2. Proximity<BR>3. Appearance. See नीकास.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=388-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकुञ्चक|निकुञ्चकः
निकुञ्चक(न) m. (-कः) A measure of capacity equal to (1/4)th of a Kuḍava.<BR>E. नि before, कुचि to be small. affix क्कुन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=388-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकुञ्चित्र
निकुञ्चित्र mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Contracted.<BR> E. नि in, and कुञ्चित curved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=388-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकुञ्ज|निकुंज|निकुंजं|निकुञ्जं|निकुंजः|निकुञ्जः
निकुञ्ज mn. (-ञ्जः-ञ्जं) An arbour, a bower, a place overgrown with creep-<BR>ers and shrubs,<BR> E. नि expletive, and कुञ्ज an arbour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=388-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकुम्भ|निकुंभ|निकुंभः|निकुम्भः
निकुम्भ m. (-म्भः)<BR>	 1. The son of KUMBHAKARṆA, the brother of RĀVAṆA.<BR>2. A plant, (Croton polyandrum)<BR> E. कु the earth, भू to be, affix<BR>खच्, and नि prefixed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=388-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकुम्भिला|निकुंभिला
निकुम्भिला f. (-ला) A cave situated on the western part of ceylon, where<BR>offerings with fire are made.<BR> E. नि before, कुम्भ a jar, इलच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=388-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकुरुम्ब|निकुरुंब|निकुरुंबं
निकुरुम्ब n. (-म्बं) A flock or multitude: also निकुरुम्बक<BR> E. नि before, कुर्<BR>to divide or cut, affix अम्बच्, and उ substituted for the penultimate;<BR>also read निकुरुम्भ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=388-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकृत|निकृतः
निकृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Dishonest, wicked, perverse.<BR>	 2. Removed, set<BR>aside, dismissed.<BR>	 3. Tricked, cheated, deceived.<BR>	 4. Injured, afflicted.<BR>5. Low, base, vile.<BR> E. नि prefixed to कृत् to cut, affix क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=388-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकृति|निकृतिः
निकृति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Wickedness, dishonesty.<BR>	 2. Abuse, reproach.<BR>	 3. Re-<BR>jection, removal.<BR>	 4. Poverty, indigence.<BR> E. नि prefixed to कृत् to<BR>cut, affix कि. or नि + कृ-भावे क्तिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=388-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकृष्ट|निकृष्टः
निकृष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं) Outcast, despised, low.<BR> E. नि prefixed to कृष् to<BR>make furrows, to revile or despise, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=388-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकेचाय|निकेचायः
निकेचाय m. (-यः) Piling or collecting repeatedly.<BR> E. नि before, चि to<BR>gather, reit. v., घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=388-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकेत|निकेतः
निकेत m. (-तः) A house, a habitation.<BR> E. नि in, कित् to dwell, affix घञ्;<BR>also with युच affix निकेतन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=388-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकेतक|निकेतकः
निकेतक n. (-कः) A house, a dwelling.<BR> E. कन added to निकेत.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=388-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकेतन|निकेतनं|निकेतनः
निकेतन n. (-नं) A house, a habitation.<BR>	 m. (-नः) An onion E. see निकेत.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=388-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकोच
निकोच(ठ)क m. (-कः) A tree, (Allangium hexapetalum.)<BR> E. नि prefixed<BR>to कुच् to be crooked, affix वुन्; also derived from कुठ् to surround,<BR>निकोठक; also with अण् pleonasm added, निकौचक or नि + कुच + शब्दे<BR>वुन् । अङ्कोट वृक्षे ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=388-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निक्वण|निक्वणः
निक्वण m. (-णः)<BR>	 1. A musical tone or sound.<BR>	 2. Any sound.<BR> E. नि prefixed<BR>to क्कण् to sound, अप् affix; also with घञ् affix निक्वाण m. (-णः)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=388-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निक्ष
निक्ष r. 1st cl. (निक्षति) To kiss: see णिक्ष ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=388-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निक्षण|निक्षणं
निक्षण n. (-णं) Kissing.<BR> E. निक्ष् to kiss, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=388-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निक्षा
निक्षा f. (-क्षा) A nit.<BR> E. णिश् to meditate, Unādi affix अच् according to<BR>some a wrong form of लिक्षा ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=388-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निक्षिप्त|निक्षिप्तं
निक्षिप्त mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं)<BR>	 1. Rejected, abandoned, foregone, given or<BR>thrown away.<BR>	 2. Deposited, pawned, pledged.<BR>	 3. Thrust into,<BR>placed in.<BR>	 4. Sent, sent off or away.<BR> E. नि implying absolutely or<BR>internally, and क्षिप to throw क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=388-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निक्षिपत्
निक्षिपत् mfn. (-पन्-पन्ती-पत्) Throwing or placing in or upon.<BR> E. नि before,<BR>क्षिप् to throw, affix शतृ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=388-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निक्षेप|निक्षेपः
निक्षेप m. (-पः)<BR>	 1. A pledge, a deposit in general, or one which is count-<BR>ed or particularised in presence of the receiver, and left without<BR>cover or seal.<BR>	 2. Abandoning, parting with, throwing away.<BR>	 3.<BR>sending or putting away.<BR>	 4. Wiping, drying.<BR> E. नि prefixed to क्षिप<BR>to throw or reject, affix घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=388-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निक्षेप्तृ
निक्षेप्तृ mfn. (-प्ता-प्त्री-प्तृ) Who or what places or deposits.<BR>	 m. (-प्ता) A de-<BR>positor, a pawner or pledger.<BR> E. नि before, क्षिप् to throw, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=388-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निखर्व्व|निखर्व
निखर्व्व mfn. (-र्व्वः-र्व्वा-र्व्वं) Dwarfish, a dwarf.<BR>	 n. (-र्व्वं) A billion.<BR> E. नि<BR>certainly, verily खर्व्व short &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=388-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निखात
निखात mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Dug dug, up, excavated.<BR>	 2. Fixed in the<BR>ground as a snake.<BR> E. नि before खन् to dig, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=388-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निखिल|निखिलं
निखिल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) All, entire, complete.<BR> E. नि negative, खिल de-<BR>fective. निवृत्तं खिलं शेषो यस्मात् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=388-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगड|निगडः
निगड mn. (-डः-डं) Iron chain for the feet, a fetter, but especially the<BR>heel chains of an elephant.<BR> E. नि not, गड् to drop, (to drop off,)<BR>affix अच् । नि + गल + अच् । डलयोरैक्यात् डत्वम् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=388-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगडित|निगडितः
निगडित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Bound, tied, chained &c.<BR> E. निगड a chain,<BR>तार-इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=388-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगण|निगणः
निगण m. (-णः) The smoke of a burnt offering or sacrificial fire.<BR> E. नि<BR>implying certainty, prefixed to गण् to estimate, affix क; by which<BR>presence of fire is indicated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=388-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगद|निगदः
निगद m. (-दः)<BR>	 1. Speech, speaking, discourse.<BR>	 2. Audible recitation of<BR>prayers or charms.<BR> E. नि affirmative prefix, गद speech. अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=388-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगदत्
निगदत् mfn. (-दन्-दन्ती-दत्) Speaking, saying, speaking to, addressing.<BR>E. निगद to speak, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=388-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगदित
निगदित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Said, spoken,<BR> E. नि before गद् to speak, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=388-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगदितवत्
निगदितवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Speaking, having spoken.<BR> E. नि before,<BR>गद् to speak, क्तवतु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=388-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगम|निगमः
निगम m. (-मः)<BR>	 1. A town, a city.<BR>	 2. A market, a fair.<BR>	 2. Holy writ, the<BR>Vedas collectively.<BR>	 4. A road, a market road.<BR>	 5. Trade, traffic.<BR>	 6.<BR>A camp or caravan of itinerant dealers, as Bazaris, &c.<BR>	 7.<BR>Certainty, assurance.<BR>	 8. Logic.<BR> E. नि affirmative prefix, गम to go,<BR>affix घञ् by which people go, &c. निगम्यते अत्र अनेन वा नि + गम-घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=388-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगमन|निगमनं
निगमन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Certain or logical conclusion, the winding up of a<BR>syllogism.<BR>	 2. Quotations of words from the Vedas.<BR>	 3. The con-<BR>clusion in a syllogism, the deduction (the fifth member of a five-<BR>membered syllogism. (In logic.)<BR>	 4. Going.<BR> E. नि, and गमन going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=388-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निग
निग(गा)र m. (-रः) Eating, swallowing<BR> E. नि in, गॄ to swallow, affix अप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=388-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निग
निग(गा)रण n. (-णं) Eating, swallowing.<BR>	 m. (-णः)<BR>	 1. The throat, the gullet.<BR>2. Smoke of a burnt offering.<BR> E. नि prefixed to गॄ to swallow, affix<BR>ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=388-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगाद|निगादः
निगाद m. (-दः)<BR>	 1. Speech, discourse.<BR>	 2. A prayer recited aloud<BR> E. नि<BR>before गद् to speak, affix घञ्; also निगद ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=388-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगार|निगारः
निगार m. (-रः) Swallowing.<BR> E. नि prefixed to गॄ to swallow, affix घञ्;<BR>also निगर ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=388-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगा
निगा(ग)ल m. (-लः) Throat or neck of a horse.<BR> E. नि before, गल् to eat,<BR>affix घञ् or नि + गॄ + धञ् अप् वा-रस्य लः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=388-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगालवत्
निगालवत् m. (-वान्) A horse.<BR> E. निगाल as above, and अस्त्यर्थे मतुप् aff. मस्य-वः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=388-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगीत
निगीत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Sung, said.<BR> E. नि and गीत sung.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=388-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगु|निगुः
निगु m. (-गुः)<BR>	 1. A root.<BR>	 2. The mind, the faculty of feeling and<BR>reasoning.<BR>	 3. Painting.<BR>	 4. excrement<BR> E. नि affirmation, ग्रह to take,<BR>affix डु । रलोपश्च ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=388-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगूढ|निगूढः
निगूढ mfn. (-ढः-ढा-ढं)<BR>	 1. Profound, obscure.<BR>	 2. Hidden, concealed.<BR>3. Embraced, m. (-ढः) A sort of wild bean; see मुद्ग<BR> E. नि before, गुह्<BR>to hide or conceal, affix क्त. आलिङ्गिते, वनमुद्गे च ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=389-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगूढार्थ
निगूढार्थ mfn. (-र्थः-र्था-र्थं) Having a hidden sense or purpose.<BR> E. निगूढ,<BR>and अर्थ meaning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=389-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगूहनीय
निगूहनीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>	 1. To be hid or concealed.<BR>	 2. To be protected<BR>or defended.<BR> E. नि before, गुह् to conceal, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=389-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगृहीत
निगृहीत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Assailed, attacked.<BR>	 2. Harassed, spoiled.<BR>	 3.<BR>Seized, arrested.<BR>	 4. Restrained, subdued, checked.<BR> E. नि before, ग्रह्<BR>to take, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=389-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगृहीति|निगृहीतिः
निगृहीति f. (-तिः) Restraint, check, &c.: see निग्रह,<BR> E. नि before, ग्रह to<BR>take, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=389-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगृह्णत्
निगृह्णत् mfn. (-ह्णन्-ह्णन्ती-ह्णत्)<BR>	 1. Seizing, taking 2. Suppressing, restrain-<BR>ing.<BR> E. नि before, ग्रह् to take, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=389-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगृह्य
निगृह्य ind.<BR>	 1. Having taken.<BR>	 2. Having restrained or suppressed.<BR>	 3.<BR>Having arrested or confined.<BR> E. नि before, ग्रह् to take, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=389-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निग्रह|निग्रहः
निग्रह m. (-हः)<BR>	 1. Aversion, disfavour, discouragement, dislike.<BR>	 2.<BR>Abusing.<BR>	 3. Binding, confinement, capture, arrest, 4. A binding,<BR>a tie.<BR>	 5. Restraint, subjection.<BR>	 6. Suppression, putting down.<BR>	 7.<BR>A boundary, a limit.<BR>	 8. Administering medicine.<BR>	 9. Killing.<BR>	 10.<BR>A name of KṚṢṆA.<BR>	 11. Removing.<BR>	 12. A flaw in an argument.<BR>13. A handle.<BR> E. नि before, ग्रह् to take or seize, affix अप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=389-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निग्रहण
निग्रहण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Subduing, suppression.<BR>	 2. Defeat.<BR>	 3. Capture.<BR>	 4.<BR>Punishment in general.<BR> E. नि before ग्रह् to take, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=389-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निग्रहस्थान
निग्रहस्थान n. (-नं) Failure in logical argument.<BR> E. निग्रह, and स्थान place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=389-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निग्राह|निग्राहः
निग्राह m. (-हः) Aversion, &c. used as an imprecation, as, निग्राहस्ते भूयात्<BR>confusion seize you, &c.<BR> E. नि before, ग्रह् to seize, affix घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=389-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निघ|निघः
निघ m. (-घः)<BR>	 1. A round or circle, a ball, any thing whose height and<BR>circumference are equal.<BR>	 2. A tree.<BR>	 3. Sin.<BR> E. नि before, हन् to kill,<BR>affix क, deriv irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=389-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निघण्टु|निघंटु|निघंटुः|निघण्टुः
निघण्टु m. (-ण्टुः) A vocabulary, a collection of words or names.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=389-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निघस|निघसः
निघस m. (-सः)<BR>	 1. Food, victuals.<BR>	 2. Eating, Dining.<BR> E. नि before, अद् to<BR>eat, अप् affix, and घस् substituted for the root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=389-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निघाति|निघातिः
निघाति m. (-तिः) An iron club or mace.<BR> E. नि before, हन् to kill, इञ्<BR>Unādi affix, and घात substituted for the root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=389-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निघानिघ
निघानिघ mfn. (-घः-घा-घं) Of different forms or sizes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=389-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निघुष्ट|निघुष्टं
निघुष्ट n. (-ष्टं) Sound, noise.<BR> E. नि before, घुष् to sound, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=389-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निघृष्व|निघृष्वः
निघृष्व m. (-ष्वः)<BR>	 1. A hoof.<BR>	 2. A mule.<BR>	 3. A boar.<BR>	 4. A road.<BR> E. नि before,<BR>घृष् to pound, Unādi affix वन् or क्कन् । Der: Irreg.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=389-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निघ्न|निघ्नः
निघ्न mfn. (-घ्नः-घ्ना-घ्नं)<BR>	 1. Docile, subservient, domestic, dependant.<BR>	 2.<BR>Completing a quotient, (in Arithmetic.)<BR>	 3. Dependant on a sub-<BR>stantive (as an adjective.)<BR> E. नि before, हन् to injure or do mis-<BR>chief, घञर्थे क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=389-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निघ्नत्|निघ्नन्त्
निघ्नत् mfn. (-घ्नन्-घ्नन्ती-घ्नत्)<BR>	 1. Slaying. Destroying, overcoming.<BR> E. नि<BR>before, हन् to kill, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=389-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निघ्नान
निघ्नान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Slaying, killing.<BR> E. नि before, हन् to kill, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=389-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निचय|निचयः
निचय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. Heap, assemblage, collection.<BR>	 2. Certainty.<BR>	 3. An<BR>assemblage of parts constituting a whole.<BR> E. नि before, चि to<BR>collect, affix भावे अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=389-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निचयिन्
निचयिन् mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि) Having or containing a quantity, full of,<BR>redolent with, abounding.<BR> E. निचय, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=389-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निचिकी
निचिकी f. (-की) A capital cow: see नैचिकी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=389-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निचित|निचितं
निचित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. full, filled.<BR>	 2. Covered, overspread.<BR>	 3. Raised<BR>up.<BR>	 4. Narrowed.<BR> E. नि before, चि to collect, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=389-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निचुल|निचुलः
निचुल m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. A plant, (Barringtonia acutangula.)<BR>	 2. An upper and<BR>outer garment.<BR>	 3. A name of a poet.<BR> E. नि before, चुल् to lift up,<BR>affix क । हिज्जले तथा वेतसवृक्षे च ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=389-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निचुलक|निचुलकं
निचुलक n. (-कं) A breastplate, a cuirass.<BR> E. क्कुन् added to the preceding;<BR>also निचोलक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=389-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निचोल|निचोलः
निचोल mfn. (-लः-ली-लं) A cover, a wrapper, a veil, a surtout.<BR>	 2. A<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=389-b" target="_blank">Page389-b+ 60</a>]<BR>bed cover.<BR>	 3. The cover of a litter.<BR> E. नि before, चुल् to lift up, affix<BR>अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=389-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निचोलक|निचोलकः
निचोलक m. (-कः) A sort of jacket, but especially a soldier's jacket,<BR>or a body dress, serving as a cuirass or breastplate.<BR> E. कन् added<BR>to निचोल ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=389-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निच्छवि|निच्छविः|निछवि
निच्छवि m. (-विः) A district, the modern Tirhut.<BR> E. नि constantly, छवि<BR>light; or निकृष्टा छविरत्र ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=389-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निच्छिद्र
निच्छिद्र mfn. (-द्रः-द्रा-द्रं) Unimpeached.<BR> E. नि neg. छिद्र flaw.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=389-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निच्छिवि|निच्छिविः|निछिवि
निच्छिवि m. (-विः) A man of one of the degraded classes, born from the<BR>outcast Kṣatriya; the occupation of this caste is apparently<BR>public exhibition of tricks, prize-fighting, &c. being classed with<BR>the Jhallas, Mallas, and others.<BR> E. नि privative, छवि light or<BR>credit, इ substituted for the penultimate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=389-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निच्छेद|निच्छेदः
निच्छेद m. (-दः)<BR>	 1. Cutting off.<BR>	 2. Leaving no common measure.<BR>(In Arithmetic.)<BR> E. नि, and छेद cutting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=389-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निज|निजं
निज mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>	 1. Own.<BR>	 2. Perpetual, eternal.<BR>	 3. Peculiar.<BR>E. नि implying continuance, and ज what is produced. नितरां जायते<BR>नि + जन-ड ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=389-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निजिघृक्षयत्
निजिघृक्षयत् mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्) Desirous of making to excel.<BR> E. नि be-<BR>fore, ग्रह् to take, desid v., शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=389-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निजुह्नुषु
निजुह्नुषु mfn. (-षुः-षुः-षु) Wishing to conceal.<BR> E. नि before, ह्नु to hide,<BR>desid. v., उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=389-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निटल|निटलं
निटल n. (-लं) The forehead.<BR> E. नि before, टल् to be marked, (with<BR>frowns, &c.) affix अच्; also with घञ् added निटाल ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=389-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निटलाक्ष|निटलाक्षः
निटलाक्ष m. (-क्षः) A name of ŚIVA<BR> E. निटल the forehead, and अक्ष an eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=389-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निडीन|निडीनं
निडीन n. (-नं) The downward flight of a bird or a peculiar mode of<BR>flying.<BR> E. नि affirmative prefix and डीन flight, flying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=389-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निण्डिका
निण्डिका f. (-का) A plant commonly Teori.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=389-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नितम्ब|नितंब|नितंबः|नितम्बः
नितम्ब m. (-म्बः)<BR>	 1. A woman's buttock's.<BR>	 2. The buttocks or posteriors<BR>in general, or as it is sometimes applied, to the circumference of<BR>the hip and loins.<BR>	 3. The shoulder.<BR>	 4. The side of a mountain.<BR>	 5.<BR>The sloping bank or shore of a river.<BR> E. नि prefixed to तम्ब् to go,<BR>affix अच्; or तम् to go with ब aff. निभृतं तम्यते काम्यते कामुकैः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=389-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नितम्बिनी|नितंबिनी
नितम्बिनी f. (-नी) A woman with large and handsome posteriors. E.<BR>नितम्ब as above, इनि and ङीप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=389-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नितराम्
नितराम् ind.<BR>	 1. Always, continually, eternally.<BR>	 2. Especially, particu-<BR>larly.<BR>	 3. Hence.<BR> E. नि always, तरप् comparative affix, and आमु<BR>added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=389-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नितल|नितलं
नितल m. (-लः) One of the seven divisions of Pātāla or hell.<BR> E. नि not,<BR>(known,) तल depth. नितान्ते, एकान्ते च ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=389-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नितान्त|नितांत|नितान्तं
नितान्त adj.<BR>	 mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं) Much, excessive. adv.<BR>	 n. (-न्तं) much, ex-<BR>cessively.<BR> E. नि prefixed to तम् to desire, affix क्त, and the vowel<BR>made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=389-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नित्य|नित्यं|नित्यः
नित्य mfn. adj. (-त्यः-त्या-त्यं)<BR>	 1. Eternal, everlasting, continual, perpe-<BR>tual, past, present, and future.<BR>	 2. Regular, fixed, invariable.<BR>3. Ordinary.<BR>	 4. Necessary.<BR>	 n. adv. (-त्यं) Always, eternally, conti-<BR>nually. sub. Indispensable rite or act.<BR>	 m. (-त्यः) The ocean.<BR>	 f. (-त्या)<BR>1. A name of PĀRVATĪ.<BR>	 2. The goddess MANASĀ.<BR>	 3. A Saktī,<BR>a form of DURGĀ, or personified energy of ŚIVA.<BR> E. नि particle<BR>implying perpetually, and त्यप aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=389-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नित्यकर्म्मन्|नित्यकर्मन्
नित्यकर्म्मन् n. (-र्म्म) Indispensable act or ceremony, as observance of the<BR>five great sacrifices, or any daily and necessary rite.<BR> E. नित्य, and<BR>कर्म्म act; also नित्यक्रिया, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=389-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नित्यकृत्य
नित्यकृत्य n. (-त्यं) Regular and necessary act or ceremony.<BR> E. नित्य, and<BR>कृत्य to be done.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=389-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नित्यगति|नित्यगतिः
नित्यगति m. (-तिः) Air or wind.<BR> E. नित्य eternal, गति motion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=389-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नित्यता
नित्यता f. (-ता) Perpetuity, eternity.<BR> E. तल् added to नित्य; also with त्व,<BR>नित्यत्वं ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=389-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नित्यदान|नित्यदानं
नित्यदान ind. Always, constantly, and eternally.<BR> E. नित्य, and दाच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=389-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नित्यदान|नित्यदानं
नित्यदान n. (-नं) Daily alms.<BR> E. नित्य, and दान gift.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=389-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नित्यनैमित्तिक
नित्यनैमित्तिक n. (-कं) Any act or ceremony which though occasional is of<BR>irregular recurrence, as Srāddhas at fixed lunar periods.<BR> E. नित्य,<BR>and नैमित्तिक occasional; also नित्यनैमित्तिककर्म्मन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=390-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नित्यप्रलय|नित्यप्रलयः
नित्यप्रलय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. Sleep.<BR>	 2. The constant loss of living beings. E.<BR>नित्य and प्रलय destruction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=390-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नित्ययुक्त
नित्ययुक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं) Always busy or engaged in.<BR> E. नित्य and युक्त<BR>attached to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=390-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नित्ययौवन
नित्ययौवन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Ever or always young.<BR>	 f. (-ना) A name of<BR>DRAUPADI.<BR> E. नित्य always, and यौवन youth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=390-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नित्यशस्
नित्यशस् ind. Always, constantly, eternally.<BR> E. नित्य, and शसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=390-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नित्यसम|नित्यसमः
नित्यसम m. (-मः) An erroneous answer, one asserting perpetuity for<BR>perishable things.<BR> E. नित्य, and सम same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=390-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नित्यानध्याय|नित्यानध्यायः
नित्यानध्याय m. (-यः) A period when the perusal of the Vedas is invari-<BR>ably prohibited, as the day of full moon, new moon, the eighth<BR>and fourteenth days of the half month.<BR> E. नित्य always, अन् nega-<BR>tive prefix, अध्याय to be read.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=390-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नित्यानित्य
नित्यानित्य mfn. (-त्यः-त्या-त्यं) Eternal and perishable, permanent and tem-<BR>porary, &c.<BR> E. नित्य, and अनित्य transient.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=390-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निद|निदं
निद (इ) निदि r. 1st cl. (निन्दति) To reproach, to blame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=390-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निद|निदं
निद mfn. (-दः-दा-दं) Abusive.<BR>	 n. (-दं) Poison, venom.<BR> E. नि affirmative<BR>prefix, दो to destroy, affix ड or निदि-क, वा नलोपः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=390-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निदत्त
निदत्त mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं) Given, given absolutely.<BR> E. नि and दत्त<BR>given.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=390-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निदद्रु|निदद्रुः
निदद्रु mf. (-द्रुः-द्रुः) A man.<BR> E. निद poison, and द्रु tree, a living Upas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=390-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निदर्शन|निदर्शनं
निदर्शन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. An example or illustration.<BR>	 2. Injunction, precept.<BR>	 3.<BR>Tenour, purport.<BR>	 4. Authority, text.<BR>	 5. A sign.<BR>	 6. A scheme.<BR>	 7.<BR>View.<BR>	 8. Evidence.<BR> E. नि fully or certainly, दर्शन showing, or नि +<BR>दृश ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=390-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निदाघ|निदाघः
निदाघ m. (-घः)<BR>	 1. The hot season, (May and June.)<BR>	 2. Heat, warmth.<BR>2. Sweat, perspiration.<BR> E. नि always, दह् to burn, आधारे घञ् affix,<BR>न्यङ्क्वादि० कुत्वम् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=390-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निदाघकर|निदाघकरः
निदाघकर m. (-रः) The sun.<BR> E. निदाघ the hot season, and कर who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=390-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निदाघकाल|निदाघकालः
निदाघकाल m. (-लः) The hot season, two months previous to rains,<BR>about May and June<BR> E. निदाघ, and काल time or season.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=390-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निदाघसिन्धु|निदाघसिन्धुः
निदाघसिन्धु m. (-न्धुः) A river in the hot weather, one nearly dry. E.<BR>निदाघ, and सिन्धु a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=390-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निदान|निदानं
निदान n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. A first cause, a primary or remote cause.<BR>	 2. Diappear-<BR>ance, cessation or removal of a first cause.<BR>	 3. Purification purity,<BR>correctness.<BR>	 4. Asking for the recompense or objects of austere devo-<BR>tion.<BR>	 5. End, cessation.<BR>	 6. A rope for tying a calf.<BR>	 7. Ascertaining<BR>the causes of disease, study of symptoms with a view to trace the<BR>remote or proximate causes; hence this word is the name of a divi-<BR>sion of all works on medicine.<BR> E. नि always or certainly, देङ् to<BR>cherish affix पालने ल्युट्; by which all effects are produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=390-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निदिग्ध|निदिग्धं
निदिग्ध mfn. (-ग्धः-ग्धा-ग्धं) Smeared, anointed, plastered.<BR>	 f. (-ग्धा)<BR>	 1. Small<BR>cardamoms.<BR>	 2. Increasing.<BR> E. नि prefixed to दिह् to smear, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=390-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निदिग्धिका
निदिग्धिका f. (-का) A sort of prickly nightshade, (Solanum jacquini.) E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding. कण्टकारिकायाम् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=390-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निदिध्यासन|निदिध्यासनं
निदिध्यासन n. (-नं) Deep and repeated consideration, thinking of or<BR>recalling repeatedly.<BR> E. नि before, ध्यै in the reiterative form, affix ल्यु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=390-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निदिष्ट
निदिष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>	 1. Ordered, directed.<BR>	 2. Advised, enjoined.<BR>	 3.<BR>Explained, pointed out.<BR> E. नि implying certainty, दिश् to show,<BR>affix क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=390-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निदुश
निदुश m. (-शः) A fish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=390-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निदेश|निदेशः
निदेश m. (-शः)<BR>	 1. Order, command, direction, instruction.<BR>	 2. Speech,<BR>speaking, saying, relating.<BR>	 3. Vicinity, proximity.<BR>	 4. The word of<BR>command.<BR> E. नि verily, दिश् to show, affix घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=390-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निदेशिन्
निदेशिन् mfn. (-शी-शिनी-शि) Showing, directing, pointing out.<BR>	 f. (-नी)<BR>	 1.<BR>A quarter of space.<BR>	 2. A point of the compass.<BR> E. नि before, दिश् to<BR>show, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=390-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निदेष्टृ
निदेष्टृ mfn. (-ष्टा-ष्ट्री-ष्टृ) Who or what show or points out, explaining,<BR>advising, commanding, &c.<BR> E. नि before दिश् to show, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=390-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निद्रा
निद्रा f. (-द्रा)<BR>	 1. Sleep, sleepiness, sloth.<BR>	 2. Dream.<BR> E. णिद् to condemn<BR>or censure, Unādi affix रक्; or द्रै to sleep, affix क्विप् and नि pre-<BR>fixed. or more correctly. नि + द्रा भावे अ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=390-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निद्राण|निद्राणः
निद्राण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>	 1. Asleep, sleepy, drowsy.<BR>	 2. Shut up, closed.<BR>E. निद्रा as above, affix क्त । नि + द्रा-तस्य नः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=390-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निद्रात्
निद्रात् mfn. (-द्राण द्रान्ती-द्रात्) Sleeping.<BR> E. नि before, द्रा to go, affix शतृ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=390-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निद्राभङ्ग|निद्राभङ्गः
निद्राभङ्ग mfn. (-ङ्गः-ङ्गा-ङ्गं) Awaked, aroused from sleep.<BR> E. निद्रा, भङ्ग<BR>breaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=390-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निद्रायमाण
निद्रायमाण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Sleeping, asleep.<BR> E. नि before द्रै to sleep,<BR>शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=390-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निद्रालु|निद्रालुः
निद्रालु mfn. (-लुः-लुः-लु) Sleeping, sleepy, drowsy, slothful.<BR>	 m. (-लुः) A<BR>name of Viṣṇu.<BR>	 f. (-लुः) A sort of perfume, commonly नीली. E.<BR>निद्रा, and शीलार्थे आलु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=390-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निद्रावृक्ष|निद्रावृक्षः
निद्रावृक्ष m. (-क्षः) Darkness.<BR> E. निद्रा sleep, and वृक्ष a tree, (whose fruit<BR>is sleep.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=390-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निद्रासंजनन
निद्रासंजनन n. (-नं) Phlegm, phlegmatic humour.<BR> E. निद्रा sleep, and<BR>संजनन producing, occasioning. निद्रां संजनयति सम्-जन-णिच् ल्यु ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=390-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निधन|निधनं|निधनः
निधन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Poor.<BR>	 mn. (-नः-नं)<BR>	 1. Race, family.<BR>	 2. Loss, dis-<BR>appearance, annihilation, 3. Death, dying.<BR>	 4. The seventh asterism<BR>of the lunar mansions, reckoning from that under which a person<BR>is born.<BR>	 m. (-नः) The head of a family.<BR> E. नि before धा to cherish,<BR>affix अच्, or नि neg. धन wealth, or नि + धा + क्यु ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=390-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निधनकारिन्
निधनकारिन् mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि) Destroying, destructive.<BR> E. निधन and<BR>कारिन् making.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=390-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निधनता
निधनता f. (-ता) Poverty.<BR> E. निधन, and तल् added; also with त्व, निधनत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=390-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निधान|निधानं
निधान n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. A Nidhi or divine treasure, belonging especially to<BR>KUVERA the god of wealth.<BR>	 2. A receptacle, a place or vessel in<BR>or on which any thing is collected or deposited.<BR>	 3. Place of cessa-<BR>tion or rest.<BR>	 4. Property, possessions, wealth.<BR> E. नि in or on, धा to<BR>possess, Unādi affix क्यप् or according to others भावे ल्युट्ः see<BR>निधि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=390-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निधापक
निधापक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A weapon.<BR>	 2. Burnt timber, charcoal.<BR>	 3. The castor<BR>oil plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=390-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निधाय
निधाय ind. Having fixed or placed in or on.<BR> E. नि before धा to have,<BR>ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=390-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निधि|निधिः
निधि m. (-धिः)<BR>	 1. One of KUVERA'S Nidhis or divine treasures, nine of<BR>which are enumerated: viz. The Padma, Mahāpadma, Sankha,<BR>Makara, Kacchapa, Mukunda, Kunda, Nila, and Kharba: their<BR>nature is not exactly defined, though some of them appears to be<BR>precious gems; according to the Tāntrika system, they are per-<BR>sonified and worshipped as demi-gods, attendant either upon<BR>KUVERA or upon LAKṢMĪ, the goddess of prosperity.<BR>	 2. A recep-<BR>tacle, a place of asylum or accumulation, as a treasury, a granary,<BR>a nest, &c.; also figuratively, as गुणनिधिः a man who contains or is<BR>endowed with all good qualities.<BR>	 3. A treasure, any sum or quan-<BR>tity of wealth or valuables.<BR>	 4. A medicinal plant and perfume,<BR>commonly Jivaka.<BR>	 5. The ocean.<BR>	 6. An epithet of Viṣṇu<BR> E. नि in,<BR>धा to have, affix. आधारे कि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=390-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निधिनाथ|निधिनाथः
निधिनाथ m. (-थः) A name of KUVERA.<BR> E. निधि a divine treasure and<BR>नाथ lord; also similar compounds, as निधिप्रभु निधीश्वर, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=390-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निधीयमान
निधीयमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Being in the course of placing, depositing,<BR>&c.<BR> E. नि before, धा to have, causal form, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=390-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निधीश|निधीशः
निधीश m. (-शः) KUVERA.<BR> E. निधि as above, and ईश lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=390-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निधुवन|निधुवनं
निधुवन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Coition, copulation.<BR>	 2. Trembling, agitation.<BR>	 3. Plea-<BR>sure, enjoyment.<BR>	 4. Sport, play, pastime.<BR> E. नि before धू to shake or<BR>agitate, युच् aff. नितरां धुवनं हस्तपादादिचालनमत्र ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=390-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निधेय
निधेय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) To be placed in or on, to be deposited, &c.<BR> E. नि<BR>before धा to have, यत् aff. स्त्रियां टाप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=390-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निध्यान|निध्यानं
निध्यान n. (-नं) sight, seeing.<BR> E. नि before, ध्यै to think, affix भावे ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=391-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निधुवन|निधुवनं
निधुवन m. (-नः) Sound.<BR> E. नि before, ध्वन् to sound, affix भावे घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=391-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निनङ्क्षु|निनंक्षु
निनङ्क्षु mfn. (-ङ्क्षुः-ङ्क्षुः-ङ्क्षु) Wishing to kill.<BR> E. नि before, णश् to destroy,<BR>desid. v, उ affix, form irr. or correctly नश-सन्-उ नुम् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=391-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निनद|निनदः
निनद m. (-दः) Sound in general.<BR> E. नि before नद् to sound, affix भावे<BR>अप्; also निनाद.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=391-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निनयन|निनयनं
निनयन n. (-नं) Engaging in performance.<BR> E. नि before, णी to lead, ल्युट्<BR>aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=391-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निनाद|निनादः
निनाद m. (-दः) Sound in general.<BR> E. नि before नद् to sound, affix पक्षे<BR>घञ्; also निनद.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=391-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निनादित
निनादित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Sounded.<BR> E. नि before नद् to sound, causal v.,<BR>क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=391-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निनीषा
निनीषा f. (-षा) Desire to take or lead.<BR> E. णी to lead, desid. form, affixes<BR>अङ्. and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=391-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निनीषु
निनीषु mfn. (-षुः-षुः-षु) Desirous to take or lead.<BR> E. णी to lead, desid.<BR>form, उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=391-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निन्दक|निंदक|निन्दकः
निन्दक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Reproachful, abusive, scurrilous, censorious. E.<BR>निदि to abuse, ण्वुल् aff. or निन्द-वुञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=391-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निन्दत्
निन्दत् mfn. (-न्दन्-न्दन्ती-न्दत्) Abusing, blaming.<BR> E. निन्द to blame, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=391-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निन्दतल|निन्दतलः
निन्दतल mfn. (-लः-ली-लं) Having a maimed or defective hand: it is also<BR>sometimes read निम्नतक.<BR> E. निन्द as above, तल the fore-arm and<BR>कर्मणि घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=391-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निन्दन|निंदन|निंदनं|निन्दनं
निन्दन n. (-नं) Reproach, censure, blame.<BR> E. णिद्, to reprove, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=391-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निन्दा|निंदा
निन्दा f. (-न्दा)<BR>	 1. Censure, reproach, reproof, blame, abuse, reviling,<BR>defamation.<BR>	 2. Injury, injuring.<BR>	 3. Wickedness.<BR> E. णिद् to abuse,<BR>&c. affixes अङ् and टाप् or निन्दि भावे अ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=391-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निन्दास्तुति|निंदास्तुति|निन्दास्तुतिः
निन्दास्तुति f. (-तिः) Irony, ironical praise.<BR> E. निन्दा censure, and स्तुति praise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=391-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निन्दित|निंदित|निन्दितः
निन्दित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Abused, reviled, reproved, 2. Low, despi-<BR>cable, worthy of being reviled.<BR>	 3. Prohibited, forbidden.<BR> E. णिद् to<BR>abuse, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=391-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निन्दु|निंदु|निंदुः|निन्दुः
निन्दु f. (-न्दुः) A woman bearing a dead child.<BR> E. णिदि to abuse, affix<BR>कर्मणि उ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=391-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निन्द्य|निंद्य
निन्द्य mfn. (-न्द्यः-न्द्या-न्द्यं)<BR>	 1. Bad, vile despicable, reprehensible.<BR>	 2.<BR>Forbidden, Prohibited.<BR> E. निन्दा, and, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=391-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निप|निपं|निपः
निप mn. (-पः-पं) A water jar.<BR>	 m. (-पः) The Kadamba tree, (Nauclea<BR>cadamba.)<BR> E. नि continuative Particle, पा to drink, affix करणे<BR>घञर्थे क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=391-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निप|निपं|निपः
निप(पा)ठ m. (-ठः) Reading, studying or lecturing.<BR> E. नि before. पठ् to<BR>read, affix भावे अप् पक्षे घञ् वा; also with ल्युट् निपठनं ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=391-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निपठित
निपठित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Read, studied,<BR> E. नि पठ् to read, क्त. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=391-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निपठिति|निपठितिः
निपठिति f. (-तिः) Reading, study.<BR> E. नि पठ् to read, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=391-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निपतत्
निपतत् mfn. (-तन्-तन्ती-तत्)<BR>	 1. Falling, falling down, prostrating.<BR>	 2.<BR>Alighting.<BR> E. नि before पत् to fall, affix शतृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=391-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निपतन|निपतनं
निपतन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Falling.<BR>	 2. Alighting, descending.<BR> E. नि in or on, पत<BR>to go, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=391-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निपतित
निपतित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Fallen, fallen down.<BR>	 2. Alighted, descended.<BR>E. नि in or on, पत् to go, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=391-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निपत्य
निपत्य ind.<BR>	 1. Having fallen down, prostrate.<BR>	 2. Having alighted.<BR> E. नि<BR>before पत् to fall, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=391-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निपत्या
निपत्या f. (-त्या)<BR>	 1. A field of battle.<BR>	 2. Any plashy or slippery ground.<BR>E. नि in or on, पत् to fall, आधारे क्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=391-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निपाक|निपाकः
निपाक m. (-कः) Cooking, maturing, ripening.<BR> E. नि before पच् to cook,<BR>affix घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=391-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निपाठ|निपाठः
निपाठ m. (-ठः) Reading, study of the sacred books, or public perusal of<BR>popular poems.<BR> E. नि before, पठ् to read, affix घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=391-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निपात|निपातः
निपात m. (-तः)<BR>	 1. Death, dying.<BR>	 2. Falling, coming down, alighting.<BR>	 3.<BR>Irregularity, (in Grammar,)<BR>	 4. A particle, (in ditto.)<BR>	 5. Attack-<BR>ing.<BR>	 6. Casting.<BR>	 7. Accidental occurrence or mention.<BR> E. नि before,<BR>पत् to go, affix भावे घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=391-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निपातन|निपातनं
निपातन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Causing to descend or fall, throwing down.<BR>	 2. Bea-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=391-b" target="_blank">Page391-b+ 60</a>]<BR>ting, knocking down.<BR>	 3. Killing.<BR>	 4. (In Grammar,) Irregularity,<BR>exception.<BR> E. नि before, पत् to fall, it the causal form, णिच्-ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=391-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निपातित
निपातित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Beaten down, made to fall or descend.<BR>	 2.<BR>Killed.<BR>	 3. Irregular, excepted.<BR> E. नि before पत् to fall, causal form,<BR>affix क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=391-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निपान|निपानं
निपान n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. A trough or ditch near a well for watering cattle.<BR>	 2.<BR>A well.<BR>	 3. Any reservoir of water, a pool, a puddle.<BR>	 4. A milk-<BR>pail.<BR>	 5. Drinking off, imbibing.<BR> E. नि before. पा to drink, आधारे<BR>ल्युट् affix: also with कन् added निपानक n. (-कं ।)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=391-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निपीडन|निपीडनं
निपीडन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Squeezing, pressing.<BR>	 2. Embracing.<BR>	 3. Hurting,<BR>giving pain.<BR> E. नि before, पीड् to give pain, भावे ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=391-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निपीडित
निपीडित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Squeezed, pressed.<BR>	 2. Embraced.<BR>	 3. Pained,<BR>hurt.<BR> E. नि before, पीड् to give pain, affix क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=391-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निपीड्य
निपीड्य ind.<BR>	 1. Having pressed or squeezed, having pressed against or<BR>upon.<BR>	 2. Having embraced, 3. Having hurt.<BR> E. नि before, पीड् to<BR>pain and ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=391-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निपीत
निपीत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Drank, drank up.<BR>	 2. Absorbed, imbibed,<BR>dried up.<BR> E. नि before, पा to drink, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=391-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निपीतमान
निपीतमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Being drank.<BR> E. नि before, पा to drink, pass.<BR>form, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=391-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निपुण|निपुणः
निपुण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>	 1. Clever, skilful, conversant with.<BR>	 2. Skilled in.<BR>3. Kindly or friendly towards.<BR>	 4. Sharp, fine, delicate.<BR>	 5. Com-<BR>plete, perfect.<BR> E. नि before, पुण् to be pure, affix क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=391-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निफालन
निफालन n. (-नं) Seeing, sight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=391-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निबद्ध
निबद्ध mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>	 1. Bound, confined.<BR>	 2. Bound, costive.<BR>	 3. Fixed<BR>upon, fastened to.<BR>	 4. Checked, restrained, 5. Restricted to.<BR> E. नि<BR>before बध् to bind, and, affix क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=391-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निबन्ध|निबंध|निबन्धं|निबंधः|निबन्धः
निबन्ध m. (-न्धः)<BR>	 1. Epistasis suppression of urine or constipation.<BR>	 2.<BR>Commentary, explanation of technical rules.<BR>	 3. The Nimb tree:<BR>see निम्ब.<BR>	 4. Binding, confinement.<BR>	 5. Intentness on or attachment<BR>to.<BR>	 6. A grant of property, an assignment of cattle or money for<BR>support, a corrody.<BR>	 7. Fixed property, not moveable or fluctuating.<BR>8. A bond, a fetter.<BR>	 n. (-न्धं) Song, singing.<BR> E. नि before, बन्धि to<BR>bind, affix घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=391-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निबन्धदान
निबन्धदान n. (-नं) Grant of an assignment, gift of a corrody.<BR> E. निबन्ध,<BR>and दान gift.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=391-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निबन्धन|निबंधन|निबंधनं|निबन्धनं
निबन्धन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Cause, motive, origin.<BR>	 2. Binding, confining.<BR>	 3.<BR>Checking, restraining.<BR>	 4. Fastening.<BR>	 5. A grant, an assignment.<BR>6. A commentary.<BR>	 7. The tie or peg of a lute.<BR>	 8. Constructing,<BR>building.<BR>	 9. A receptacle.<BR>	 10. A bond, a fetter.<BR>	 11. Support.<BR>	 12.<BR>Syntax. (in gram.)<BR>	 13. Composing.<BR>	 14. Composition, a treatise.<BR>E. नि before, बधि to bind, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=391-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निबन्धित|निबन्धितः
निबन्धित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Bound, confined, tied.<BR> E. नि before, बन्ध् to bind affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=391-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निबन्धृ
निबन्धृ mfn. (-न्धा-न्ध्री-न्धृ) Who or what ties or binds.<BR>	 m. (-न्धा) An<BR>author, a commentator.<BR> E. नि affirmative, बन्ध् bind, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=391-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निभ|निभः
निभ mfn. (-भः-भा-भं) Like, resembling, similar.<BR>	 mn. (-भः-भं)<BR>	 1. fraud,<BR>trick, disguise, pretence.<BR>	 2. Light, manifestation, appearance.<BR> E. नि<BR>before, भा to shine, affix क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=391-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निभालन|निभालनं
निभालन n. (-नं) Sight, seeing.<BR> E. नि before भाल् to see, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=391-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निभूत|निभूतं
निभूत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Past, gone.<BR>	 f. (-ता) Quite frightened.<BR> E. नि affirm-<BR>ative, भूत been.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=391-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निभृत|निभृतः
निभृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Modest, humble, unassuming.<BR>	 2. Lonely, soli-<BR>tary.<BR>	 3. Placed down.<BR>	 4. Secret.<BR>	 5. Still, Silent.<BR>	 6. Firm.<BR>	 7. On<BR>the point of setting.<BR>	 8. Filled with.<BR> E. नि before, भृ to cherish,<BR>affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=391-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निभृतम्
निभृतम् ind.<BR>	 1. Privately, apart.<BR>	 2. Unobservedly in a corner.<BR>	 2. Cover-<BR>tly, in disguise or out of sight.<BR> E. नि before, भृ to cherish, affix क्त<BR>and मुट् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=391-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निम|निमः
निम m. (-मः) A pin, a stake.<BR> E. नि in, माञ् to plunge or stick, affix ड;<BR>stuck in the ground.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=391-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमग्न
निमग्न mfn. (-ग्नः-ग्ना-ग्नं)<BR>	 1. Plunged in, immersed.<BR>	 2. Gone down, set.<BR>	 3.<BR>Over whelmed.<BR> E. नि in, मस्ज to bathe, affix क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=392-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमज्जत्
निमज्जत् mfn. (-ज्जन्-ज्जन्ती-ज्जत्) Bathing, plunging in.<BR> E. नि before, मस्ज<BR>to bathe, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=392-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमज्जथु|निमज्जथुः
निमज्जथु m. (-थुः)<BR>	 1. Sleep, sleeping.<BR>	 2. The act of diving or entering<BR>into.<BR> E. नि in, मस्ज to bathe. भावे अथुच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=392-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमज्जन|निमज्जनं
निमज्जन n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Bathing.<BR>	 2. Immersion.<BR> E. नि before, मस्ज to bathe,<BR>भावे ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=392-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमन्त्रण|निमंत्रण|निमंत्रणं|निमन्त्रणं
निमन्त्रण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Summoning, calling.<BR>	 2. Inviting, invitation, 3.<BR>A summons.<BR> E. नि affirmative, मन्त्रण advising or नि + मन्त्र-भावे-ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=392-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमन्त्रित
निमन्त्रित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Summoned, convoked.<BR>	 2. Invited.<BR> E. नि be-<BR>fore मन्त्र to advise, affix क्त्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=392-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमय|निमयः
निमय m. (-यः) Barter, exchange.<BR> E. नि before, मि to measure, to mete,<BR>affix अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=392-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमातव्य
निमातव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं) To be exchanged or bartered.<BR> E. नि before,<BR>मा to measure, तव्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=392-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमि|निमिः
निमि m. (-मिः)<BR>	 1. Twinkling.<BR>	 2. A son of IKSHWAKU condemned to<BR>reside in the twinkle of the eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=392-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमित्त|निमित्तं
निमित्त n. (-त्तं)<BR>	 1. Cause, motive, instrumental cause.<BR>	 2. Mark, sign,<BR>spot, trace, token.<BR>	 3. Omen.<BR>	 4. A butt, a target.<BR>	 5. Pretext. E.<BR>नि before, मि to measure, क्त affix, also with कन् added निमित्तक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=392-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमित्तक|निमित्तकं
निमित्तक n. (-कं)<BR>	 1. Kissing, a kiss.<BR>	 2. Cause, &c. E. See the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=392-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमित्तकारण|निमित्तकारणं
निमित्तकारण n. (-णं) The instrumental cause, the material or the agent,<BR>especially the deity considered as the agent in creation.<BR> E. निमित्त<BR>the instrumental cause, कारण cause.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=392-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निनित्तकाल
निनित्तकाल m. (-लः) Any given or specific time.<BR> E. निमित्त, and काल time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=392-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमित्तत्व
निमित्तत्व n. (-त्वं) Causality, instrumentality.<BR> E. निमित्त, and त्व affix, also<BR>with तल् निमित्तता ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=392-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमित्तधर्म्म|निमित्तधर्म|निमित्तधर्मः
निमित्तधर्म्म m. (-र्म्मः)<BR>	 1. Expiation.<BR>	 2. Any occasional or special penance,<BR>rite, or obligation.<BR> E. निमित्त, and धर्म्म piety.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=392-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमित्तमात्र
निमित्तमात्र n. (-त्रं) The mere agent or instrument.<BR> E. निमित्त and मात्र<BR>alone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=392-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमित्तविद्
निमित्तविद् m. (-विद्) An astrologer.<BR> E. निमित्त a mark (lucky or un-<BR>lucky,) and विद् who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=392-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमित्तावृत्ति|निमित्तावृत्तिः
निमित्तावृत्ति f. (-त्तिः) Dependence upon a special cause or occasion. E.<BR>निमित्त and आवृत्ति revolving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=392-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमिष|निमिषः
निमिष m. (-षः)<BR>	 1. Twinkling of the eye.<BR>	 2. The twinkling of an<BR>eye considered as a measure of time.<BR>	 3. A name of VIṢṆU.<BR> E. नि<BR>before, मिष् to twinkle, affix क; also with घञ् affix निमेष, or निमि<BR>a proper name षद् to go, ड aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=392-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमिषत्
निमिषत् mfn. (-षन् षन्ती-षत्) Blinking, closing the eyelids.<BR> E. निमिष् to<BR>twinkle, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=392-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमिलत्
निमिलत् mfn. (-लन्-लन्ती-लत्) Twinkling, closing, (as the eye.)<BR> E. नि be-<BR>fore मील् to disappear, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=392-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमीलन|निमीलनं
निमीलन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Death, dying.<BR>	 2. Twinkling of the eye, shutting of<BR>the eyelids, winking.<BR>	 3. Total eclipse.<BR> E. नि before, मील् to dis-<BR>appear, &c. affix भावे ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=392-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमीलिका
निमीलिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. Fraud, trick, disguise.<BR>	 2. Twinkling of the eye,<BR>winking. blinking.<BR>	 3. Conniving at anything.<BR> E. नि before, मील<BR>to twinkle, affixes, वुन् and ठाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=392-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमीलित
निमीलित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Closed, (as the eyelid,) twinkled, blinked. E.<BR>नि before, मील् to disappear, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=392-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमेय|निमेयः
निमेय m. (-यः) Barter, exchange.<BR> E. नि before, मि to measure, affix यत् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=392-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमेष|निमेषः
निमेष m. (-षः)<BR>	 1. Twinkling of the eye.<BR>	 2. A momentary space of time,<BR>a twinkling of the eye considered as measure of time: see निमिष<BR>नि + मिष भावे घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=392-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमेषक|निमेषकः
निमेषक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. Twinkling of the eye.<BR>	 2. A firefly.<BR> E. कन् added to<BR>the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=392-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमेषकृत्
निमेषकृत् f. (-कृत्) Lightning.<BR> E. निमेष twinkling, and कृत् what makes.<BR>निमेषं करोति कृ-क्विप् तुक् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=392-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमेषरुच्
निमेषरुच् m. (-रुक्) A firefly.<BR> E. निमेष a twinkling, रुच् who shines.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=392-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निम्न|निम्नं
निम्न mfn. (-म्नः-म्ना-म्नं)<BR>	 1. Deep, profound, (literally or figuratively.)<BR>	 2.<BR>Low.<BR>	 3. Low land 4. A slope.<BR>	 5. A gap, a chasm in the ground.<BR>	 6.<BR>A depression.<BR> E. नि before, म्ना to mind, affix क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=392-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निम्नग
निम्नग mfn. (-गः-गा-गं) Deep, going deep.<BR>	 f. (-गा) A river.<BR> E. निम्न deep,<BR>and ग what goes. निम्नं गच्छति गम-ड ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=392-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निम्नता
निम्नता f. (-ता) Depth, profundity.<BR> E. निम्न with तल् affix; also with त्व,<BR>निम्नत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=392-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निम्नोन्नत
निम्नोन्नत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) High and low, up and down.<BR> E. निम्न, and उन्नत high.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=392-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निम्ब|निंब|निंबः|निम्बः
निम्ब m. (-म्बः) The Nimb or Neemb tree, (Melia azadiracta.)<BR> E. निबि to<BR>sprinkle, affix अच्; also with कन् added, निम्बकः these words are<BR>written with either व or ब, as निम्ब or निम्ब.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=392-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निम्बतरु|निम्बतरुः
निम्बतरु m. (-रुः) The coral tree, (Erythrina fulgens;) it is considered as<BR>one of the trees of paradise.<BR> E. निम्ब as above, and तरु a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=392-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निम्बूक|निम्बूकं|निंबूकः|निम्बूकः
निम्बूक m. (-कः) The common lime, (Citrus acida.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=392-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियत|नियतः
नियत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Self-governed, subdued, restrained.<BR>	 2. Attentive,<BR>fixed or intent upon.<BR>	 3. Constant, permanent.<BR>	 4. Ascertained,<BR>certain, fixed.<BR>	 5. Inevitable.<BR>	 6. Positive, definite.<BR>	 7. Permeable,<BR>what may be spread through or over.<BR>	 n. adv. (-तं) Always, cons-<BR>tantly. subst. Elementary or crude matter, the recipient of attri-<BR>butes or properties.<BR> E. नि before, यम् to restrain affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=392-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियतमानस
नियतमानस mfn. (-सः-सा-सं) Of subdued mind or spirit.<BR> E. नियत, and<BR>मानस the mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=392-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियतात्मन्
नियतात्मन् mfn. (-त्मा-त्मा-त्म) Self-regulated, self-controlled or restrained.<BR>E. नियत, and आत्मन् self.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=392-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियताहार
नियताहार mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Abstemious, moderate.<BR> E. नियत, and आहार<BR>food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=392-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियति|नियतिः
नियति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Destiny, luck, good or bad fortune.<BR>	 2. A religious<BR>duty or obligation.<BR>	 3. Self-command, self-restraint.<BR>	 4. A name<BR>of DURGĀ.<BR>	 5. Abidyā, or the will of god<BR> E. नि before, यम् to re-<BR>frain, affix करणे क्तिन् or क्तिच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=392-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियतेन्द्रिय|नियतेन्द्रियः
नियतेन्द्रिय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Of restrained or subdued passions.<BR> E. नियत<BR>controlled, इन्द्रिय an organ of sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=392-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियन्तव्य
नियन्तव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं) To be restrained, checked, controlled, &c. E.<BR>नि before, यम् to restrain, तव्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=392-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियन्तृ|नियंतृ
नियन्तृ mfn. (-न्ता-न्त्री-न्तृ) Who or what restrains, governs, or guides m.<BR>(-न्ता)<BR>	 1. A charioteer, a coachman.<BR>	 2. A ruler, a governor, a mas-<BR>ter.<BR>	 3. A punisher.<BR> E. नि before यम् to restrain, affix तृच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=392-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियन्त्रित|नियंत्रित|नियन्त्रितः
नियन्त्रित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Checked, restrained, governed, guided.<BR> E. नि<BR>affirmative particle, यम् to restrain or check, affix क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=392-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियम|नियमः
नियम m. (-मः)<BR>	 1. Agreement, contract, engagement, assent, promise.<BR>2. Any religious observance voluntarily practised, as fasting,<BR>watching, pilgrimage, praying, &c. voluntary penance, meritor-<BR>ious or supererogatory piety.<BR>	 3. A religious observance or<BR>obligation in general.<BR>	 4. Certainty, ascertainment.<BR>	 5. Rule, precept.<BR>6. Usage, practice.<BR>	 7. Common places in poetry, conventional<BR>expression, as notice of the Birch in describing the Himālaya, of<BR>the Sandal tree in describing the Malaya mountain, the white-<BR>ness of vesture, blackness of hair, the cry of the peacock in the<BR>rains, of the kokila in spring, &c,<BR> E. नि before, यम् to refrain, affix<BR>घञ् वा ह्रस्वः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=392-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियमन|नियमनं
नियमन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Precept, fixed practice or rule.<BR>	 2. Binding.<BR>	 3. Res-<BR>training, checking.<BR> E. नि before, यम् to restrain, affix भावे ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=392-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नितमपर
नितमपर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>	 1. Observing fixed rules.<BR>	 2. Relating to or<BR>corroborative of a rule.<BR> E. नियम, and पर attached to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=392-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियमित|नियमितः
नियमित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Regulated, prescribed.<BR>	 2. Governed, guided.<BR>3. Checked, restrained.<BR>	 4. Bound, confined.<BR> E. नि before, यम् to<BR>check, णिच्-कर्मणि क्त affix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=392-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियम्य
नियम्य ind. Having restrained.<BR>	 mfn. (-म्यः-म्या-म्यं) To be checked or res-<BR>trained.<BR> E. नि before, यम् to govern, ल्यप् or यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=392-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियातन|नियातनं
नियातन n. (-नं) Causing to fall or descend: see निपातन । नितरां यात्यते<BR>याति-ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=393-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियाम|नियामः
नियाम m. (-मः)<BR>	 1. Religious act, penance, fasting, &c. especially if an<BR>act of supererogation.<BR>	 2. Restraint.<BR> E. नि before, यम् to restrain,<BR>affix घञ्ः see नियम.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=393-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियामक|नियामकः
नियामक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Guiding, governing, what regulates or res-<BR>trains.<BR>	 m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A boatman, a sailor; but variously applied to<BR>one who rows, who steers, or who keeps a lookout from the mast<BR>head.<BR>	 2. A pilot, a helmsman.<BR>	 3. A charioteer.<BR> E. नि before, यम् to<BR>go or stop, affix णिच् ण्वु ल्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=393-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियुक्त|नियुक्तः
नियुक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>	 1. Engaged in, applying or attached to.<BR>	 2.<BR>Authorized, called, appointed.<BR>	 3. Directed, enjoined, commanded.<BR>4. Ascertained.<BR>	 5. Fastened or attached to.<BR> E. नि before, युज् to<BR>join, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=393-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियुञ्जान
नियुञ्जान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Authorizing, appointing.<BR> E. नि before, युज् to<BR>join, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=393-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियुज्य
नियुज्य ind.<BR>	 1. Having joined or attached to.<BR>	 2. Having put to or har-<BR>nessed.<BR> E. नि before, युज् to join, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=393-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियुत|नियुतं
नियुत mn. (-तः-तं)<BR>	 1. A million.<BR>	 2. A hundred thousand.<BR>	 3. Ten thou-<BR>sand krores.<BR> E. नि before, यु to join, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=393-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियुद्ध|नियुद्धं
नियुद्ध n. (-द्धं) Close fight, personal struggle.<BR> E. नि before, युद्ध fight, contest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=393-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियोक्तव्य
नियोक्तव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं) To be appointed or authorized.<BR> E. नि, युज् to<BR>join, affix तव्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=393-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियोग|नियोगः
नियोग m. (-गः)<BR>	 1. An order or command.<BR>	 2. Authority, appointment.<BR>3. Occupation, appointed duty.<BR>	 4. Effort, exertion.<BR>	 5. Ascertain-<BR>ment, certainty.<BR>	 6. Incidence, occurrence.<BR>	 7. The practise in<BR>ancient times by which a childless widow was permitted to have<BR>intercourse with the brother or any other near relative of her<BR>deceased husband to raise up issue to him.<BR> E. नि before, युज् to<BR>join, affix घञ् कुत्वम् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=393-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियोगप्रयोजन
नियोगप्रयोजन n. (-नं) The object of any appointment, authorized act or<BR>duty.<BR> E. नियोग, and प्रयोजन cause.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=393-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियोगविधि
नियोगविधि m. (-धिः) The form of appointing to any act or duty. E.<BR>नियोग and विधि rule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=393-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियोगार्थ
नियोगार्थ m. (-र्थः) The object of an authorized act or appointment E.<BR>नियोग and अर्थ object.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=393-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियोगिन्
नियोगिन् mfn. (-गी-गिनी-गि)<BR>	 1. Engaged in any pursuit, closely attached<BR>to it or engrossed by it.<BR>	 2. Appointed, authorized, entrusted with<BR>authority, &c.<BR>	 m. (-गी) A minister, a deputy, an agent, &c. E.<BR>नियोग and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=393-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियोग्य|नियोग्यः
नियोग्य mfn. (-ग्यः-ग्या-ग्यं) Fit to be appointed or authorized, able or fit<BR>for a duty.<BR>	 m. (-ग्यः) A master.<BR> E. नि before, युज् to join, अहार्थे<BR>कर्त्तरि ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=393-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियोजन|नियोजनं
नियोजन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Ordering, commanding, directing.<BR>	 2. Uniting,<BR>attaching to.<BR>	 3. Urging, impelling.<BR>	 4. Fasting.<BR> E. नि before, युज् to<BR>join, affix भावे ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=393-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियोजित
नियोजित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Entrusted with, appointed to.<BR>	 2. Directed,<BR>ordered.<BR>	 3. Impelled, urged to, instigated.<BR>	 4. Joined or attached<BR>to.<BR>	 5. Suited or adapted to, connected with, &c.<BR> E. नि before, युज्<BR>to join, क्त affix, with इट् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=393-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियोजनीय
नियोजनीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) To be attached or joined to.<BR> E. नि, युज् to<BR>join, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=393-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियोज्य|नियोज्यः
नियोज्य mfn. (-ज्यः-ज्या-ज्यं)<BR>	 1. To be attached to.<BR>	 2. To be appointed to<BR>or employed in.<BR>	 3. To be commanded, instigated, &c.<BR>	 m. (-ज्यः)<BR>A servant.<BR> E. नि before, युज् to join, शक्यार्थे कर्मणि ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=393-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियोद्धृ
नियोद्धृ m. (-द्धा)<BR>	 1. A cock.<BR>	 2. A combatant, a wrestler, a boxer,<BR> E. नि<BR>near, युध् to fight, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=393-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्
निर् ind.<BR>	 1. A particle and prefix implying certainty, assurance.<BR>	 2.<BR>Negation, privation.<BR>	 2. Outside, out, without, forth.<BR> E. नॄ to guide,<BR>affix क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=393-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरक्ष|निरक्षः
निरक्ष mfn. (-क्षः-क्षा-क्षं)<BR>	 1. Having no dice, &c.<BR>	 2. Having no latitude.<BR>m. (-क्षः) (In Astronomy.) The terrestrial equator.<BR> E. निर् and अक्ष<BR>a die, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=393-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरक्षदेश|निरक्षदेशः
निरक्षदेश m. (-शः)<BR>	 1. A first meridian, as Lankā, a place where the<BR>sun is always vertical and the days and nights are equal.<BR>	 2.<BR>The equatorial region.<BR> E. निर् and अक्ष latitude, देश a country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=393-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरग्नि
निरग्नि mfn. (-ग्निः-ग्निः-ग्नि) Having lost or neglected the consecrated<BR>fire.<BR> E. निर् अग्नि fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=393-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरङ्कुश|निरंकुश|निरङ्कुशः
निरङ्कुश mfn. (-शः-शा-श) Unchecked, uncontrolled, self-willed, indepen-<BR>dant<BR> E. निर् privative, अङ्कुश a hook for guiding an elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=393-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरङ्कुशत्व
निरङ्कुशत्व n. (-त्वं) Self-willed, wilfulness.<BR> E. त्व added to the foregoing;<BR>also with तल् निरङ्कुशता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=393-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरञ्जन|निरंजन|निरञ्जनः
निरञ्जन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>	 1. Void of passion or emotion.<BR>	 2. Unstained,<BR>unblackened.<BR>	 n. (-नं) The Supreme Being.<BR>	 f. (-ना) The day of full-<BR>moon.<BR>	 m. (-नः) An Epithet of Sīva.<BR> E. नि neg. रञ्जन affection; or<BR>निर् not, अञ्जन collyrium; figuratively, darkness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=393-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरत|निरतं
निरत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Engaged or interested in.<BR>	 2. Attached or devot-<BR>ed to.<BR> E. नि, and रत occupied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=393-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरत्यय
निरत्यय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Faultless, unblamable.<BR> E. निर् neg. अत्यय fault.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=393-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरनुक्रोश|निरनुक्रोशः
निरनुक्रोश mfn. (-शः-शा-शं) Hard-hearted, destitude of compassion. E.<BR>निर् and अनुक्रोश pity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=393-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरनुक्रोशता
निरनुक्रोशता f. (-ता) Cruelty, hard-hearted-ness.<BR> E. तल् added to the<BR>last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=393-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरनुरोध
निरनुरोध mfn. (-धः-धा-धं) Unkind unfavourable.<BR> E. निर् neg. अनुरोध<BR>favour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=393-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरन्तर|निरंतर|निरन्तरं
निरन्तर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>	 1. Coarse, gross, without interstices.<BR>	 2. Conti-<BR>nuous.<BR>	 3. Uninterrupted, continual.<BR>	 4. Unbounded.<BR>	 5. Identical,<BR>not different.<BR>	 6. Unconcealed, not hidden or vanished.<BR>	 7. Not<BR>external, &c.<BR> E. निर् not, अन्तर interval, difference, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=393-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरन्तराल|निरंतराल
निरन्तराल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Narrow, contracted.<BR> E. निर् neg. अन्तराल in-<BR>termediate space.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=393-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरन्ताभ्यास
निरन्ताभ्यास m. (-सः)<BR>	 1. Private study, reading to one's self the sacred<BR>works.<BR>	 2. Diligent and uninterrupted pursuit, exercise, practice.<BR>E. निर् not, अन्तर between, अभ्यास practice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=393-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरन्वय
निरन्वय mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>	 1. Childless, having no family, 2. Unconnected<BR>with, not belonging or related to.<BR>	 3. Done in one's absence, not done<BR>openly or visibly.<BR>	 4. Unmethodical, ill arranged.<BR> E. निर् neg. अन्वय<BR>descent, connexion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=393-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरप
निरप mfn. (-पः-पा-पं) Destitute of water.<BR> E. निर्, and अप water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=393-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरपत्रप|निरपत्रपः
निरपत्रप mfn. (-पः-पा-पं)<BR>	 1. Shameless, impudent.<BR>	 2. Bold, confident. E.<BR>निर् not, अपत्रप shame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=393-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरपराध|निरपराधः
निरपराध mfn. (-धः-धा-धं) Faultless, blameless.<BR> E. निर् neg. अपराध fault.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=393-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरपवर्त्त|निरपवर्त
निरपवर्त्त m. (-र्त्तः)<BR>	 1. Non-returning or turning back 2. (In Arithmetic,)<BR>Leaving no common measure.<BR> E. निर्, and अपवर्त्त returning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=393-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरपाय
निरपाय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Free from destruction or decay, eternal.<BR> E. निर्<BR>neg. अपाय loss.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=393-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरपेक्ष|निरपेक्षः
निरपेक्ष mfn. (-क्षः-क्षा-क्षं)<BR>	 1. Independent of, unconnected or unconcerned<BR>with.<BR>	 2. Careless, indifferent, negligent.<BR>	 3. Without purpose or<BR>hope.<BR> E. निर्, and अपेक्षा regard to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=393-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरब्भ्र
निरब्भ्र mfn. (-ब्भ्रः-ब्भ्रा-ब्भ्रं) Cloudless.<BR> E. निर्, and अब्भ्र a cloud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=393-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरय|निरयः
निरय m. (-यः) Hell.<BR> E. निर् out, beyond, अय good fortune.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=393-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरर्गल|निरर्गलः
निरर्गल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Unobstructed, unrestrained, unimpeded.<BR> E. निर्<BR>not, अर्गल a bolt or bar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=393-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरर्थक|निरर्थकं
निरर्थक mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>	 1. Vain, fruitless, unprofitable.<BR>	 2. Unmeaning.<BR>E. निर् not, अर्थ object, end, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=393-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरव|निरवः
निरव m. (-वः) Loss of voice.<BR> E. नि neg. and रव sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=393-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरवग्रह|निरवग्रहः
निरवग्रह mfn. (-हः-हा-हं) Self-willed, headstrong, independent, uncon-<BR>trolled.<BR> E. निर् neg. अवग्रह control.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=393-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरवद्य
निरवद्य mfn. (-द्यः-द्या-द्यं) Unobjectionable, unexceptionable.<BR> E. निर् neg.<BR>अवद्य not to be said.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=393-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरवशेषतस्
निरवशेषतस् ind. Fully, particularly, circumstantially.<BR> E. निर् neg.<BR>अवशेषतस् a remainder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=394-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरवसाद
निरवसाद mfn. (-दः-दा-दं) Animated, anxious, eager.<BR> E. निर् neg. अवसाद<BR>languor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=394-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरवहानिका
निरवहानिका f. (-का) A fence, a hedge, an outer wall.<BR> E. निर् out, with-<BR>out, and अवहानिका a fence. निर + अव + हन-ण्वुल ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=394-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरशन|निरशनं
निरशन n. (-नं) Fasting, going without food.<BR> E. निर् and अशन, eating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=394-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरस|निरसः
निरस mfn. (-सः-सा-सं)<BR>	 1. Dry.<BR>	 2. Insipid, tasteless.<BR>	 m. (-सः)<BR>	 1. Insi-<BR>pidity, want of flavour or passion.<BR>	 2. Dryness, want of juice.<BR> E. नि<BR>neg. रस juice, &c. also नीरस.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=394-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरसन|निरसनं
निरसन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) What removes, expels, subdues, checks, &c.<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>	 n. 1. Rejection, denial, contradiction, disallowance.<BR>	 2.<BR>Suppressing, checking.<BR>	 3. Appeasing.<BR>	 4. Expelling, ejecting, 5.<BR>Spitting, spitting out any thing with sickness or disgust.<BR>	 6. Kill-<BR>ing, destroying.<BR> E. निर् out or forth. अस् to throw ल्युट् affix or युच्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=394-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरस्त|निरस्तः
निरस्त mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं)<BR>	 1. Expelled, sent forth or out.<BR>	 2. Sent, thrown,<BR>cast, directed.<BR>	 3. Thrown off, (as from a horse.)<BR>	 4. Abandoned,<BR>deserted, left.<BR>	 5. Rejected, disallowed.<BR>	 6. Shot, (as an arrow,)<BR>	 7.<BR>Uttered ra pidly, hurried.<BR>	 8. Destroyed, 9. Gone, absent, what is<BR>not.<BR>	 10. Suppressed, checked.<BR>	 11. Torn or taken.<BR>	 12. Broken, (as<BR>an agreement.)<BR> E. निर् out or forth, अस् to throw or send, affix<BR>कर्मणि क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=394-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरस्य
निरस्य ind. Having ejected or thrown out.<BR>	 2. Having expelled, &c. E.<BR>निर् and अस् to throw. ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=394-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरस्यत्
निरस्यत् mfn. (-स्यन्-स्यन्ती-स्यत्)<BR>	 1. Ejecting, thrown out.<BR>	 2. Abandoning,<BR>neglecting.<BR>	 3. Expelling.<BR>	 4. Scattering.<BR>	 5. Destroying, &c.<BR> E. निर्<BR>out, अस् to throw, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=394-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरस्यमान
निरस्यमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>	 1. Being suppressed or checked.<BR>	 2. Being ab-<BR>andoned 3. Suppressing.<BR>	 4. Expelling.<BR>	 5. Scattering, &c.<BR> E. निर्<BR>before, अस् to throw, either a. or p. voice, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=394-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरहङ्कार|निरहंकार
निरहङ्कार mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Humble, free from pride.<BR> E. निर् neg. अहङ्कार<BR>pride.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=394-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निराकरण|निराकरणं
निराकरण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Obstruction, opposition, contradiction. rejection.<BR>2. Refutation, reply.<BR>	 3. Holding in consideration, making light of,<BR>contempt, disesteem.<BR>	 4. Expelling, turning out or away.<BR>	 5.<BR>Throwing out or off.<BR>	 6. Neglecting the chief sacrificial or religious<BR>duties.<BR> E. निर् privative particle, and आङ् before, कृ to do or make,<BR>affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=394-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निराकरिष्णु|निराकरिष्णुः
निराकरिष्णु mfn. (-ष्णुः-ष्णुः-ष्णु)<BR>	 1. Obstructive, obstructing.<BR>	 2. Disdaining,<BR>despising.<BR> E. निर्, and आङ् before कृ, affix शोलार्थे इष्णुच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=394-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निराकार|निराकारः
निराकार mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>	 1. Devoid of form or figure.<BR>	 2. Formless. 3<BR>Disguise.<BR>	 m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Heaven.<BR>	 2. VIṢṆU.<BR>	 3. SĪVA.<BR>	 4. The divine<BR>spirit, God.<BR>	 5. Reproach, censure.<BR> E. निर. implying negative or<BR>depreciation, and आकार shape, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=394-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निराकुल
निराकुल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Calm, steady, unperplexed, unconfused.<BR> E. निर्<BR>neg. आकुल agitated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=394-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निराकृत|निराकृतः
निराकृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Removed, rejected, set aside.<BR>	 2. Refuted,<BR>replied to.<BR>	 3. Made light of, contemned, despised.<BR>	 4. Expelled,<BR>turned out.<BR>	 5. Thrown from or off.<BR>	 6. Divorced.<BR> E. निरा, and<BR>कृत done, with आङ् prefixed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=394-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निराकृति|निराकृतिः
निराकृति mfn. (-ति-तिः-ति).<BR>	 1. A person who has not duly gone<BR>through a course of study, especially applied however to the<BR>religious student, who has not duly read the Vedas.<BR>	 2. One<BR>who neglects the five great religious obligations.<BR>	 3. Shapeless,<BR>formless, viewless.<BR>	 m. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Rejection, contradiction, opposi-<BR>tion, disallowance.<BR>	 2. Obstacle, impediment.<BR> E. निरा implying<BR>privation or obstruction, कृति making, causing; or निर् private<BR>and आकृति form. निर + आ + कृ क्तिन् or कर्त्तरि क्त्रिच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=394-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निराक्रोश
निराक्रोश mfn. (-शः-शा-शं) Unaccused, unreviled.<BR> E. निर्, and आक्रोश<BR>exclaiming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=394-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरागस्
निरागस् mfn. (-गाः-गाः-गः) Sinless, faultless,<BR> E. निर् neg. आगस् sin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=394-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निराचार|निराचारः
निराचार mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Lawless, corrupt, barbarian, depraved. E.<BR>निर् not, आचार moral ordinances: it is especially applied to those<BR>people who have not the ordinances of the Vedas or distinction<BR>of Casts, &c. and comprises all, therefore, except Hindūs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=394-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरातपा
निरातपा f. (-पा) Night.<BR> E. निर् not, none, and आतप sunshine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=394-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरादिष्ट
निरादिष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं) Given, paid, (as a debt) delivered.<BR> E. निर्,<BR>and आदिष्ट shown.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=394-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरादेश|निरादेशः
निरादेश m. (-शः) Payment, discharge, delivery.<BR> E. निर्, and आङ्<BR>before, दिश् to show, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=394-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरानन्द
निरानन्द mfn. (-न्दः-न्दा-न्दं) Causing no pleasure, undelighting.<BR> E. निर्<BR>neg. आनन्द happiness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=394-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरापद्
निरापद् mfn. (-द् or -त्) Prosperous, fortunate.<BR> E. निर् neg. आपद्<BR>misfortune.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=394-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निराबाध|निराबाधः
निराबाध mfn. (-धः-धा-धं) Frivolously or unreally vexatious, (as a<BR>cause of complaint.)<BR> E. निर् private, आङ् before, बाधा pain,<BR>annoyance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=394-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरामय|निरामयः
निरामय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Well, hale, recovered from sickness.<BR>	 m. (-यः)<BR>1. A wild goat.<BR>	 2. A hog, a boar.<BR> E. निर् not, आमय sickness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=394-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरामालु|निरामालुः
निरामालु m. (-लुः) The wood apple: see कपित्थ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=394-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरामिषाशिन्
निरामिषाशिन् mfn. (-शी-शिनी-शि)<BR>	 1. Living without meat.<BR>	 2. Free<BR>from sensual desires.<BR> E. निर्, आमिष flesh, अशिन् who eats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=394-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निराय|निरायः
निराय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Having no income or profit, yielding none<BR>&c.<BR> E. निर् neg. आय receipt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=394-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरायत
निरायत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Contracted, compact.<BR> E. निर् neg. आयत spread.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=394-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरायव्ययवत्
निरायव्ययवत् m. (-वान्) An idler who lives by clandestine means, has<BR>neither income nor expenditure.<BR> E. निर्, आय income, व्यय expense,<BR>मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=394-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरायास
निरायास mfn. (-सः-सा-सं) Not giving trouble, ready, easily attainable.<BR>E. निर् neg. आयास exertion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=394-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरायुध
निरायुध mfn. (-धः-धा-धं) Unarmed, defenceless.<BR> E. निर् neg. आयुध<BR>a weapon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=394-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरालम्ब|निरालंब
निरालम्ब mfn. (-म्बः-म्बा-म्बं)<BR>	 1. Self-supported, not relying on another.<BR>2. The supreme being.<BR> E. निर्, आलम्ब stay.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=394-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निराश|निराशः
निराश mfn. (-शः-शा-शं)<BR>	 1. Hopeless, despairing.<BR>	 2. Disappointed.<BR>E. निर्, and आश hope.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=394-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निराशिस्
निराशिस् mfn. (-शिः-शिः-शिः) Without a blessing.<BR> E. निर्, and आशिस्<BR>blessing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=394-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निराश्रय
निराश्रय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Without refuge, destitute.<BR> E. निर्, and आश्रय<BR>an asylum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=394-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरास|निरासः
निरास m. (-सः)<BR>	 1. Opposing, rejecting.<BR>	 2. Dispension.<BR>	 3. Ejecting.<BR>expelling.<BR>	 4. Removal.<BR>	 5. Abandonment.<BR>	 6. Vomitting.<BR> E. निर्<BR>out, and अस to be, भावे घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=394-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरासन|निरासनं
निरासन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Rejection, contradiction.<BR>	 2. Killing, destroy-<BR>ing.<BR>	 3. spitting out.<BR> E. निर् before, अस् to be, &c. with आङ्<BR>prefixed and ल्युट् affix; also निरसन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=394-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निराहार|निराहारः
निराहार mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Fasting through necessity or choice.<BR> E. निर्<BR>privative, आहार food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=394-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरास्पद
निरास्पद mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>	 1. Restless, anxious, unappeasable.<BR>	 2.<BR>Homeless, portionless.<BR> E. निर् neg. आस्पद station.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=394-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरिङ्गिणी
निरिङ्गिणी f. (-णी) A veil.<BR> E. निर् negative, अङ्ग a hint, इनि and ङीप्<BR>affs. निभृतमङ्गं निरङ्गं तदस्त्यस्या आच्छादत्वेन इनि ङीप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=394-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरिन्द्रिय|निरिंद्रिय|निरिन्द्रियः
निरिन्द्रिय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Imperfect, mutilated, maimed.<BR> E. निर्<BR>privative, इन्द्रिय an organ of sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=394-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरीक्षण|निरीक्षणं
निरीक्षण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Looking at, regarding, seeing.<BR>	 2. Expecting.<BR>E. निर्, and ईक्षण seeing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=394-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरीक्षत्
निरीक्षत् mfn. (-क्षन्-क्षन्ती-क्षत्)<BR>	 1. Looking at, regarding.<BR>	 2. Ex-<BR>pecting, hoping.<BR> E. निर्, and ईक्षत् seeing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=394-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरीक्षमाण
निरीक्षमाण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>	 1. Looking at, regarding.<BR>	 2. Hoping,<BR>expecting.<BR> E. निर् before, ईक्ष् to see, शनच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=394-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरीक्षा
निरीक्षा f. (-क्षा).<BR>	 1. Looking at, regarding.<BR>	 2. Hope, expectation.<BR>E. निर् before, ईक्ष् to see. अङ् and टाप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=395-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरीक्षामाण
निरीक्षामाण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Being regarded or looked at.<BR> E. निर् and<BR>ईक्ष to see, pass. शानच aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=395-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरोक्षित
निरोक्षित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Seen beheld, looked at.<BR>	 2. Hoped, ex-<BR>pected.<BR> E. निर्, and ईक्षित seen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=395-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरीश|निरीशं
निरीश(ष) n. (-शं) The body of a plough.<BR> E. ईश or ईष the shaft of the<BR>plough, and निर् forth or from, prefixed; hence also निरीष n.<BR>(-षं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=395-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरीह|निरीहः
निरीह mfn. (-हः-हा-हं) Indifferent, desireless, unanxious.<BR> E. निर् neg.<BR>ईह who seeks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=395-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरीहता
निरीहता f. (-ता) Indifference, absence of effort or wish to get any-<BR>thing.<BR> E. तल् added to the preceeding; also with त्व, निरीहत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=395-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरुक्त|निरुक्तं
निरुक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>	 1. Said, described.<BR>	 2. Obscure, obsolete.<BR>	 n.<BR>(-क्तं)<BR>	 1. One of the Vedāṇgas or works considered as supple-<BR>mentary to and connected with the Vedas, forming a part of<BR>the scriptural or sacred science: glossarial explanation of obscure<BR>terms especially those occurring in the Vedas.<BR>	 2. Explanation<BR>of the concord or disagreement of letters, &c.<BR>	 3. Separation<BR>or analysis of a derivative or compound word.<BR>	 4. The name of the<BR>Yāskās commentary on the Nighantus.<BR>	 5. Loud, Distinct.<BR> E. निर्<BR>negative or affirmative prefix, उक्त spoken, said.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=395-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरुक्ति|निरुक्तिः
निरुक्ति f. (-क्तिः) The Vedanga or portion of the scriptural science,<BR>which explains obscure and obsolete terms.<BR>	 2. Explanation of<BR>words.<BR>	 3. An artificial explanation of the derivation of a word; (In<BR>rhetoric). see the last.<BR> E. निर्, and उक्ति saying, or निर् + वच-क्तिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=395-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरुच्यमान
निरुच्यमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Being uttered or said.<BR> E. निर्, and उच्यमान<BR>being spoken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=395-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरुच्छास
निरुच्छास mfn. (-सः-सा-सं) Breathless.<BR>	 2. Narrow, contracted, crowded.<BR>E. निर् and उच्छास breathing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=395-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरुत्तर
निरुत्तर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Non-plussed, without an answer.<BR> E. निर्,<BR>and उत्तर an answer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=395-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरुत्साह|निरुत्साहः
निरुत्साह mfn. (-हः-हा-हं) Indolent, indifferent.<BR> E. निर् neg. उत्माह effort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=395-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरुत्सुक
निरुत्सुक mfn. (-कः-का-क) Unanxious, unregretting.<BR> E. निर् neg. उत्सुक<BR>sorrowing for.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=395-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरुद्ध|निरुद्धः
निरुद्ध mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>	 1. Stopped, checked, restrained, hindered.<BR>	 2.<BR>Confined, imprisoned.<BR> E. नि, and रुद्ध hindered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=395-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरुद्धप्रकष
निरुद्धप्रकष(स) m. (-षः or सः) Stricture of the urethra.<BR> E. निरुद्ध, and प्रकष<BR>what pains.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=395-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरुद्धशमवृत्ति
निरुद्धशमवृत्ति mfn. (-त्तिः-त्तिः-त्ति) Wearied, tired.<BR> E. निरुद्ध, and शमवृत्ति<BR>repose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=395-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरुद्द्राव
निरुद्द्राव mfn. (-वः-वा-वं) Immoveable, undecaying.<BR> E. निर्, and उद्द्राव<BR>going away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=395-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरुद्विग्न
निरुद्विग्न mfn. (-ग्नः-ग्ना-ग्नं) Sedate, free from perturbation.<BR> E. निर्, and<BR>उद्विग्न perturbed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=395-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरुद्योग|निरुद्योगः
निरुद्योग mfn. (-गः-गः-गं) Causeless, groundless.<BR> E. निर् negative,<BR>उद्योग cause.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=395-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरुन्धत्
निरुन्धत् mfn. (-न्धन्-न्धन्ती-न्धत्) Hindering, checking, suppressing.<BR> E. नि<BR>before, रुध to hinder, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=395-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरुन्धान
निरुन्धान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Hindering, opposing.<BR>	 2. Preventing, depriving<BR>of.<BR> E. नि before, रुध to hinder, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=395-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरुपद्रव|निरुपद्रवः
निरुपद्रव mfn. (-वः-वा-) Free from any national distress or affliction, free<BR>from tyranny.<BR> E. निर्, and उपद्रव violence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=395-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरुपप्लव
निरुपप्लव mfn. (-वः-वा-वं) Free from trouble or alarm.<BR> E. निर् and उपप्लव<BR>calamity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=395-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरुपम|निरुपमः
निरुपम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं) Unequalled, having no resemblance or likeness.<BR>E. निर्, and उपमा similitude.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=395-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरुपेक्ष|निरुपेक्षः
निरुपेक्ष mfn. (-क्षः-क्षा-क्षं) Honest, free from trick or fraud.<BR> E. निर्, and<BR>उपेक्षा trick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=395-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरूढ|निरूढः
निरूढ mfn. (-ढ-ढा-ढं)<BR>	 1. Conventional, accepted, (as the meaning of<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=395-b" target="_blank">Page395-b+ 60</a>]<BR>technical words or names in opposition to their etymological sense<BR>alone.)<BR>	 2. Unmarried 3. Inherent.<BR>	 m. (-ढः)<BR>	 1. The force or applica-<BR>tion of words, according to their natural or received meanings, (in<BR>Rhetoric)<BR>	 2. (In Logic,) The implied description of any property<BR>in the term designing it, (as of redness in the word red, &c.) E.<BR>नि affix, and रूढ ascended; or निर् neg. ऊढ married.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=395-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरूपण|निरूपणं
निरूपण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Sight, seeing.<BR>	 2. Doubt, discussion, investigation.<BR>3 Ascertaining, determining.<BR>	 4. Searching, looking for.<BR>	 5. Form,<BR>shape.<BR> E. नि implying certainty, रूप to have form, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=395-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरूपणीय
निरूपणीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>	 1. To be discussed, to be investigated.<BR>	 2. To<BR>be sought or looked for.<BR> E. नि before, रूप to have form, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=395-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरूपयत्
निरूपयत् mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्)<BR>	 1. Searching, looking for.<BR>	 2. Investigating,<BR>considering.<BR> E. नि, रूप to have form, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=395-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरूपित|निरूपितः
निरूपित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Seen, beheld.<BR>	 2. Ascertained.<BR>	 3. Discovered,<BR>found.<BR>	 4. Appointed, deputed, directed to do any thing.<BR>	 5. Con-<BR>sidered, weighed.<BR> E. नि before, रूप to have form, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=395-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरूप्य
निरूप्य mfn. (-प्यः-प्या-प्यं) To be seen or ascertained. ind. Having seen or<BR>considered,<BR> E. नि before, रूप to have form, यत् or ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=395-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरूप्यत्व
निरूप्यत्व n. (-त्वं) Ascertaining, determining.<BR> E. त्व added to the last:<BR>also with तल् निरूप्यता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=395-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरूह|निरूहः
निरूह m. (-हः)<BR>	 1. A complete sentence, one having no ellipsis.<BR>	 2.<BR>Certainty, ascertainment.<BR>	 3. Logic, disputation.<BR>	 4. An enema,<BR>one not of an oily kind.<BR> E. निर् privative, and ऊह reasoning, &c.<BR>करणे घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=395-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरूहण|निरूहणं
निरूहण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Ascertaining.<BR>	 2. Administering enemata not of an<BR>oily kind.<BR> E. निर before, ऊह to reason, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=395-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरृति|निरृतिः
निरृति mfn. (-तिः-तिः-ति) Free from violence, tyranny, &c.<BR>	 m. (-तिः) A<BR>demi-god and ruler of the south-west quarter: see नैरृति f. (-तिः)<BR>1. Misfortune, calamity.<BR>	 2. Security, prosperity, immunity<BR>from tyranny or violence.<BR> E. निर् implying reverse, ऋति good<BR>fortune, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=395-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरृथ|निरृथः
निरृथ m. (-थः) The Sāma Veda.<BR> E. निर्, ऋ to go, Unādi affix थक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=395-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरेभ
निरेभ mfn. (-भः-भा-भ) Silent, noiseless.<BR> E. नि neg. रेभ sounding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=395-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरोध|निरोधः
निरोध m. (-धः)<BR>	 1. Loss, destruction.<BR>	 2. Opposition, hindrance, check,<BR>restraint, prevention.<BR>	 3. A version, disfavour, dislike.<BR>	 4. Preserving.<BR>5. Confinement.<BR> E. नि before, रुध् to oppose, affix भावे घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=395-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्ग|निर्गः
निर्ग m. (-र्गः) Country, region, place or province.<BR> E. निर् forth, गम् to<BR>go, affix अधिकरणे ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=395-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्गत|निर्गतः
निर्गत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Gone out or forth.<BR>	 2. Expended, extinct, de-<BR>parted.<BR> E. निर् out, गत gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=395-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्गन्ध|निर्गंध|निर्गन्धं
निर्गन्ध mfn. (-न्धः-न्धा-न्धं) Inodorous, void of fragrance or smell.<BR> E. निर्<BR>neg. गन्ध smell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=395-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्गन्धन|निर्गंधन|निर्गंधनं|निर्गन्धनं
निर्गन्धन n. (-नं) Killing, slaughter.<BR> E. निर्, affirmative particle, गन्ध to<BR>hurt, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=395-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्गन्धपुष्पी
निर्गन्धपुष्पी f. (-ष्पी) The Simul or silk-cotton tree.<BR> E. निर्गन्ध, पुष्प a flower,<BR>ङीष् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=395-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्गम|निर्गमः
निर्गम m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. Going forth or out, exit.<BR>	 2. Total loss or departure.<BR>E. निर् out, गम going; also निर्गमन and निर्गति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=395-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्गुण|निर्गुणः
निर्गुण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>	 1. Void of all properties.<BR>	 2. Bad, worthless,<BR>having no good qualities.<BR>	 3. Stringless.<BR>	 m. (-णः) The Supreme<BR>Being, or any deity so considered.<BR> E. निर् privative, and गुण a<BR>property, an excellence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=395-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्गुणत्व
निर्गुणत्व n. (-त्वं) The state of being free from all qualities, an attribute<BR>especially of the Supreme Being.<BR> E. निर्गुण, and त्व affix; also with<BR>तल्, निर्गुणता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=395-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्गुण्ठी
निर्गुण्ठी f. (-ण्ठी)<BR>	 1. A shrub, (Vitex negundo.)<BR>	 2. Another plant,<BR>(नीलशेफालिका)<BR>	 3. The root of the lotus.<BR> E. निर् forth or out, गुठी or<BR>गुडि to surround, क affix, fem. affix ङीष्; hence also निर्गुण्डी f.<BR>(-ण्डी) निसिन्दावृक्षेच ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=395-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्गूढ|निर्गूढः
निर्गूढ m. (-ढः) The hollow of a tree.<BR> E. निर् in, गुह to hide, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=395-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्ग्रन्थ|निर्ग्रंथ|निर्ग्रन्थः
निर्ग्रन्थ m. (-न्थः)<BR>	 1. A saint, a devotee, one who has withdrawn from<BR>the world, and lives either as a beggar or a hermit.<BR>	 2. A religious<BR>character wandering about naked.<BR>	 3. A pauper, a beggar.<BR>	 4. An<BR>idiot, a fool.<BR>	 5. A gambler.<BR> E. निर not, ग्रन्थ a knot or tie, or<BR>figuratively, attachment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=396-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्ग्रन्थक|निर्ग्रन्थकः
निर्ग्रन्थक mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>	 1. Unattended, unaccompanied.<BR>	 2. Abandon-<BR>ed, deserted.<BR>	 3. Clever, expert, conversant.<BR>	 m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A religious<BR>mendicant.<BR>	 2. A naked devotee.<BR>	 3. A gambler.<BR> E. निर् not, ग्रन्थ tie<BR>or connection, affix कन्; also read निर्ग्रन्थिक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=396-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्ग्रन्थन|निर्ग्रंथनं|निर्ग्रन्थनं
निर्ग्रन्थन n. (-नं) Killing, slaughter.<BR> E. निर् privative, before ग्रन्थ to<BR>hurt or kill, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=396-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्घट|निर्घटं
निर्घट mfn. (-टः-टा-टं)<BR>	 1. A great collection of people, a fair, a market,<BR>&c.<BR>	 2. A free market or wharf, one where no toll is levied.<BR>	 3. A<BR>place where is no quay or stairs.<BR> E. निर् prefixed to घट to endea-<BR>vour, affix, अच् or निर्गतो घटो यस्मात् प्र० ब ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=396-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्घण्ट|निर्घंट|निर्घंटं|निर्घंटः|निर्घण्टः
निर्घण्ट m. (-ण्टः) A vocabulary, an index.<BR> E. निर् before, घटि to endea-<BR>vour, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=396-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्घर्षण|निर्घर्षणं
निर्घर्षण n. (-णं) Rubbing, friction,<BR> E. निर् before घृष् to rub, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=396-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्घर्षणक
निर्घर्षणक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Rubbing, a rubber.<BR> E. कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=396-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्घात|निर्घातः
निर्घात m. (-तः)<BR>	 1. A gust of wind, a hurricane, a whirlwind.<BR>	 2. The<BR>noise of contending vapours in the heavens.<BR>	 3. An earthquake.<BR>4. Destruction.<BR> E. निर् forth, हन् to drive, affix घञ्, घात substitu-<BR>ted for the radical.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=396-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्घूरिणी
निर्घूरिणी f. (-णी) A river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=396-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्घृण
निर्घृण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>	 1. Cruel, unmerciful.<BR>	 2. Shameless, immodest.<BR>E. निर् neg. घृणा mercy, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=396-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्घोष|निर्घोषः
निर्घोष m. (-षः) A sound in general.<BR> E. निर् before, घुष् to sound,<BR>affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=396-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्ज्जन|निर्जन|निर्ज्जनः
निर्ज्जन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Lonely, unpeopled, unfrequented.<BR> E. निर् neg.<BR>जन a person.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=396-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्जर|निर्जरं|निर्जरः|निर्ज्जर|निर्ज्जरः
निर्जर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Immortal, imperishable, undecaying.<BR>	 m. (-रः)<BR>A deity, an immortal.<BR>	 n. (-रं) Ambrosia, the food of the gods.<BR>	 f.<BR>(-रा)<BR>	 1. A plant: see गुडुची.<BR>	 2. A sort of perfume, commonly<BR>Mura.<BR> E. निर् not, जरा decrepitude or decay.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=396-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्जल|निर्जलः|निर्ज्जलः
निर्जल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Dry, desart, void of water.<BR>	 m. (-लः) A desart,<BR>a waste.<BR> E. निर् neg. and जल water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=396-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्जित|निर्ज्जितः
निर्जित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Conquered, subdued, overcome.<BR>	 2. Won,<BR>gained.<BR>	 3. Unconquered.<BR> E. निर् affirmative or neg. prefix, जित<BR>conquered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=396-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्जितेन्द्रिय|निर्जितेन्द्रियः
निर्जितेन्द्रिय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Of subdued passions or feelings.<BR> E. निर्जित,<BR>and इन्द्रिय an organ of sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=396-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्जितेन्द्रियग्राम|निर्ज्जितेन्द्रियग्रामः
निर्जितेन्द्रियग्राम m. (-मः) A Muni, a saint.<BR> E. निर्जितेन्द्रिय, and ग्राम ac-<BR>cumulation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=396-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्जीव|निर्ज्जीवः
निर्जीव mfn. (-वः-वा-वं) Lifeless.<BR> E. निर्, and जीव alive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=396-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्झर|निर्झरं|निर्झरः
निर्झर mf. (-रः-री) A cascade or torrent, the precipitous descent of<BR>water from mountains, &c., f. (-री) A river.<BR>	 m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A horse of<BR>the sun.<BR>	 2. A fire of chaff.<BR>	 3. An elephant.<BR> E. निर् before, झृ to<BR>waste, and अप् aff. (झरणा ।)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=396-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्झरिन्
निर्झरिन् m. (-री) A mountain.<BR>	 f. (-रिणी) A river.<BR> E. निर्झर a waterfall,<BR>इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=396-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्णय|निर्णयः
निर्णय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. Certainty, positive conclusion.<BR>	 2. Doubt, discussion,<BR>investigation.<BR>	 3. (In Law,) Sentence, decision.<BR>	 4. (In the Mi-<BR>mānsa.) The application of a conclusive argument.<BR>	 5. (In<BR>Logic,) Complete ascertainment.<BR> E. निर् affirmative prefix, णी<BR>to guide, affix, भावे अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=396-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्णयन|निर्णयनं
निर्णयन n. (-नं) Certainty, ascertainment, positive conclusion. E. See<BR>निर्णय. with ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=396-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्णयपाद|निर्णयपादः
निर्णयपाद m. (-दः) A sentence, a verdict, a decree, (in Law,)<BR> E. निर्णय,<BR>and पाद process.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=396-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्णर|निर्णरः
निर्णर m. (-रः) One of the horses of the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=396-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्णायक
निर्णायक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Causing or leading to certainty,<BR> E. निर्<BR>before, णी to guide, causal form, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=396-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्णायन|निर्णायनं|निर्ण्णायन
निर्णायन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Causing certainty.<BR>	 2. The outer angle of the ele-<BR>phant's eye.<BR> E. निर्णय certainty, फक् aff. or निर् + नी-णिच्-ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=396-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्णिक्त|निर्णिक्तं
निर्णिक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं) Cleaned, purified, cleansed.<BR> E. निर् before,<BR>निज to clean, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=396-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्णीत|निर्णीतं
निर्णीत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Ascertained, determined.<BR>	 2. Sentenced, de-<BR>creed.<BR> E. निर् before, णी to get, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=396-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्णेक|निर्णेकः
निर्णेक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. Cleansing, washing, cleaning.<BR>	 2. Ablution.<BR>	 3.<BR>Atonement, expiation.<BR> E. निर् before, निज to wash, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=396-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्णेजक|निर्णेजकः
निर्णेजक m. (-कः) A washerman.<BR> E. निर् before, निज to clean, affix ण्वुल्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=396-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्णेतृ
निर्णेतृ mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ) Certifying, verifying, leading to certainty,<BR>decisive.<BR>	 m. (-ता)<BR>	 1. A judge.<BR>	 2. A document. a voucher.<BR>	 3. A<BR>guide.<BR> E. निर् before, णी to lead, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=396-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्णेतृत्व
निर्णेतृत्व n. (-त्वं) Proof, verification,<BR> E. त्व added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=396-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्णेय
निर्णेय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) To be ascertained, what is or ought to be deter-<BR>mined.<BR> E. निर् before, णी to lead, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=396-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्द्दग्ध|निर्दग्ध
निर्द्दग्ध mfn. (-ग्धः-ग्धा-ग्धं)<BR>	 1. Burnt, burnt up.<BR>	 2. Unburnt.<BR> E. निर्<BR>and दग्ध burnt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=396-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्दट|निर्द्दटः
निर्दट mfn. (-टः-टा-टं)<BR>	 1. Unkind, unfeeling, unmerciful, devoid of<BR>pity or or charity 2. Unnecessary.<BR>	 3. Envious, slanderous, abu-<BR>sive.<BR>	 4. Mad, intoxicated.<BR>	 5. Violent.<BR>	 6. Rejoicing over the<BR>faults of others.<BR> E. निर् before, दो to cut, to hurt, affix अटच्,<BR>deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=396-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्दय|निर्द्दयः
निर्दय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Unkind, unmerciful, cruel, hard-hearted.<BR> E. निर्<BR>before, दया compassion, charity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=396-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्द्दर|निर्दर|निर्दरः|निर्द्दरं
निर्द्दर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>	 1. Harsh spoken.<BR>	 2. Shameless.<BR>	 n. (-रं) Much,<BR>excessively, subst.<BR>	 n. (-रं) Pith, essence.<BR> E. निर् not, दृ to respect,<BR>अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=396-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्द्दरि|निर्दरि|निर्दरिः
निर्द्दरि m. (-रिः) A cave.<BR> E. निर् before, द to rend, इन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=396-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्द्दरिवासिन्|निर्दरिवासिन्
निर्द्दरिवासिन् mfn. (-सी-सिनी-सि) Inhabiting a cave.<BR> E. निर्द्दरिन्, and<BR>वासिन् who abides in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=396-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्द्दशत्|निर्दशत्
निर्द्दशत् mfn. (-शन्-शन्ती-शत्) Biting, consuming.<BR> E. निर्, and दशत् biting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=396-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्दशन
निर्दशन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Toothless.<BR> E. निर् neg. दशन a tooth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=396-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्दहन|निर्द्दहनः
निर्दहन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Not burning, not caustic.<BR>	 n. (-नं) Marking<BR>nut.<BR> E. निर् affir. or neg. and दहन burning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=396-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्दहनी|निर्द्दहनी
निर्दहनी f. (-नी) A sort of creeper, from the fibres of which bowstrings<BR>are made, (Sanseviera zeylanica.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=396-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्द्दातृ|निर्दातृ
निर्द्दातृ mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ)<BR>	 1. A reaper, a husbandman.<BR>	 2. A Donor. E.<BR>निर्, before दो to cut, तृच् aff. निर् + दो खण्डने, दा-दाने, दै शोधने, तृच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=396-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्द्दारित|निर्दारित
निर्द्दारित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Torn, rent.<BR>	 2. Open, unclosed.<BR>	 3. Start-<BR>ing, (the eyes.)<BR> E. निर्, and दारित torn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=396-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्दिग्ध|निर्द्दिग्धः
निर्दिग्ध mfn. (-ग्धः-ग्धा-ग्धं)<BR>	 1. Stout, lusty.<BR>	 2. Anointed, smeared.<BR> E. निर्<BR>before, दिह to heap, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=396-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्दिश्य
निर्दिश्य ind. Having shown, explained, enjoined, &c.<BR> E. निर् before,<BR>दिश् to show, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=396-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्दिष्ट|निर्द्दिष्टः
निर्दिष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>	 1. Described, depicted, pointed out, shown.<BR>2. Ascertained, determined.<BR>	 3. Ordered, directed.<BR>	 4. Assigned.<BR>5. Asserted.<BR> E. निर् before दिश to show, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=396-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्देश|निर्देशः|निर्द्देशः
निर्देश m. (-शः)<BR>	 1. Order, command, authoritative instruction or direc-<BR>tion.<BR>	 2. Description, designation.<BR>	 3. Depicting, pointing out or<BR>exhibiting.<BR>	 4. Certainty, ascertainment.<BR>	 5. Saying, telling.<BR>6. Vicinity, proximity.<BR> E. निर् before, दिश to show, affix, भावे<BR>घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=396-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्देष्टृ
निर्देष्टृ mfn. (-ष्टा-ष्ट्री-ष्टृ) Who or what shows or explains.<BR>	 m. (-ष्टा)<BR>An authority, a guide.<BR> E. निर् before, दिश् to show, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=396-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्दोष|निर्द्दोषः
निर्दोष mfn. (-षः-षा-षं)<BR>	 1. Faultless, without defect or blemish.<BR>	 2. Not<BR>hostile, friendly.<BR> E. निर् negative, and दोष defect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=396-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्द्वन्द्व|निर्द्वंद्व
निर्द्वन्द्व mfn. (-न्दः-न्दा-न्दं)<BR>	 1. Not double.<BR>	 2. Free from either of two<BR>alternatives, neither glad nor sorry, &c.<BR>	 3. Not acknowledging<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=397-a" target="_blank">Page397-a+ 60</a>]<BR>two principles.<BR>	 4. Free from jealousy.<BR>	 5. Not dependant upon<BR>another.<BR> E. निर् neg. द्वन्द्व a pair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=396-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्ध
निर्ध(र्द्ध)न mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Poor, indigent.<BR>	 m. (-नः) An old ox.<BR> E. निर् priv.<BR>and धन wealth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=397-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्ध
निर्ध(र्द्ध)र्म्म mfn. (-र्म्मः-र्म्मा-र्म्मं)<BR>	 1. Impious, unrighteous, immoral, void of<BR>law or religion.<BR>	 2. Not acknowledging moral or religious institu-<BR>tions, but especially those of the Hindūs.<BR> E. निर् not, धर्म्म virtue,<BR>&c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=397-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्धा
निर्धा(र्द्धा)र m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Certainty, ascertainment.<BR>	 2. Particularising in-<BR>dividuals according to their degree of merit.<BR> E. निर् before, धृ to<BR>hold or have, affix णिच् + भावे-घञ्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=397-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्धा
निर्धा(र्द्धा)रण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Certainty, ascertainment.<BR>	 2. Specifying one out of<BR>many.<BR>	 3. Determining, settling.<BR> E. निर् before, धृ to have, affix<BR>णिच् + ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=397-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्धारणीय
निर्धारणीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>	 1. To be ascertained.<BR>	 2. Acting resolutely,<BR>irresistible.<BR> E. निर् affir. or neg. धृ to hold, अनीयर् affix; also<BR>निर्धारितव्य, and निर्धार्य्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=397-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्धारित|निर्धारितं
निर्धारित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Ascertained, determined.<BR> E. निर् affirmative,<BR>धृ to have, causal form, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=397-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्धा
निर्धा(र्द्धा)र्य्य mfn. (-र्य्यः-र्य्या-र्य्यं)<BR>	 1. Acting fearlessly.<BR>	 2. Active, energetic.<BR>3. Ascertainable, to be ascertained or determined.<BR> E. निर् neg.<BR>or affir. धृ to restrain, affix कर्मणि ण्यत्; it may also be written<BR>निर्द्धार्य्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=397-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्धूत|निर्धूतं|निर्धूतः
निर्धूत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Deserted, rejected.<BR>	 2. Removed, departed.<BR>	 3.<BR>Broken, divided.<BR>	 4. Refuted.<BR>	 5. Thrown out.<BR>	 6. Suffered, under-<BR>gone.<BR>	 7. Destroyed.<BR>	 m. (-तः) A man abandoned by his relatives<BR>or friends.<BR> E. निर् before, धू to shake, affix कर्मणि-क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=397-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्धौत|निर्धौतं
निर्धौत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Washed off.<BR>	 2. Bright, polished.<BR> E. निर् and<BR>धौत cleansed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=397-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्नमस्कार
निर्नमस्कार mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Uncourteous.<BR> E. निर् Neg. नमस्कार salutation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=397-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्नाथ
निर्नाथ mfn. (-थः-था-थं) Having no superior, master, or protector, &c. E.<BR>निर् neg. नाथ a lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=397-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्नाथता
निर्नाथता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Being without a master.<BR>	 2. Widow-hood.<BR> E. निर्<BR>neg. नाथता masterhood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=397-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्निमित्त
निर्निमित्त mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं) Causeless, groundless.<BR> E. निर् neg. निमित्त<BR>cause.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=397-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्ब्ब
निर्ब्ब(र्ब)न्ध m. (-न्धः)<BR>	 1. Intent, and pertinacious pursuit of any thing,<BR>urgency, importunity.<BR>	 2. Seizure, laying hold of any thing,<BR>literally or figuratively.<BR>	 3. Caprice, fancy, whim.<BR> E. निर् before,<BR>बन्ध to bind or tie, affix भावे घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=397-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्ब्ब
निर्ब्ब(र्ब)र्हण n. (-णं) Killing, slaughter.<BR> E. निर् before, वर्ह to slay, affix<BR>भावे ल्युट् also निर्बहण ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=397-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्ब्बल|निर्बल
निर्ब्बल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Weak, feeble, powerless.<BR> E. निर् neg. बल<BR>strength.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=397-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्ब्बुद्धि|निर्बुद्धि
निर्ब्बुद्धि mfn. (-द्धिः-द्धिः-द्धि) Ignorant, unwise.<BR> E. निर् neg. and दुद्धि under-<BR>standing; also निर्बोध.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=397-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्ब्बैर
निर्ब्बैर mfn. (-रः-री-रं) Free from hatred or enmity.<BR> E. निर् neg. बैर<BR>hostility.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=397-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्भग्न
निर्भग्न mfn. (-ग्नः-ग्ना-ग्नं) Broken down.<BR> E. निर्, and भग्न broken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=397-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्भट|निर्भटः
निर्भट mfn. (-टः-टा-टं) Hard, firm, compact.<BR> E. निर् before, भट् to main-<BR>tain, affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=397-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्भय|निर्भयः
निर्भय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Fearless, undaunted.<BR> E. निर् not, भय fear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=397-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्भर|निर्भरं|निर्भरः
निर्भर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>	 1. Much, excessive.<BR>	 2. Fearless.<BR>	 3. A servant<BR>employed without a pay.<BR>	 n. adv. (-रं) Much, excessively, subs.<BR>Pith, essence.<BR> E. निर् before, भृ to fill, affix अप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=397-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्भर्त्सन|निर्भर्त्सनं
निर्भर्त्सन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Wickedness, malignity.<BR>	 2. Abuse, blame.<BR>	 3.<BR>Lac.<BR>	 4. Threat, menace.<BR> E. निर् before, भर्त्स to abuse, affix ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=397-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्भर्त्सित|निर्भर्त्सितं
निर्भर्त्सित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Abused, reviled, despised.<BR> E. निर् before, भर्त्स<BR>to abuse, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=397-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्भाग्य|निर्भाग्यः
निर्भाग्य mfn. (-ग्यः-ग्या-ग्यं) Unlucky.<BR> E. निर् neg, भाग्य luck.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=397-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्भद्य
निर्भद्य ind. Having pierced or penetrated.<BR> E. निर् before, भिद् to break,<BR>ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=397-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्भिन्न
निर्भिन्न mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>	 1. Undistinguished, equal, like.<BR>	 2. Pierced,<BR>divided.<BR> E. निर्, भिन्न separated or pierced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=397-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्भुग्न
निर्भुग्न mfn. (-ग्नः-ग्ना-ग्नं) Straight, flat, not bent.<BR> E. निर्, and भुग्न curved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=397-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्म्मथ्य|निर्मथ्य
निर्म्मथ्य ind.<BR>	 1. Having discriminated or particularised.<BR>	 2. Having<BR>ground or churned.<BR> E. निर् before, मथि to churn, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=397-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्म्म
निर्म्म(र्म)द mfn. (-दः-दा-दं) Sober, quiet, unintoxicated.<BR>	 m. (-दः) An ele-<BR>phant after the frontal juice has ceased to exude, one out of rut.<BR>E. निर् priv. and मद madness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=397-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्म्मनुष्य|निर्मनुष्य
निर्म्मनुष्य mfn. (-ष्यः-ष्या-ष्यं) Uninhabited, desolate.<BR> E. निर्, मनुष्य a<BR>man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=397-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्म्मन्थन|निर्मन्थन|निर्मंथन|निर्मंथनं
निर्म्मन्थन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Separating, distinguishing, discriminating.<BR>	 2. Churn-<BR>ing.<BR>	 3. The wood used for kindling fire by friction.<BR> E. निर् before,<BR>मन्थ् to churn, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=397-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्म्मन्थ्य|निर्मन्थ्य|निर्मंथ्य
निर्म्मन्थ्य mfn. (-न्थ्यः-न्थ्या-न्थ्यं)<BR>	 1. To be rubbed or churned, &c.<BR>	 2. To be<BR>distinguished or discriminated.<BR> E. निर् affix. मन्थ्य to be rubbed,<BR>कर्मणि ण्यत् affix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=397-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्म्मम|निर्मम
निर्म्मम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं) Disinterested, claiming or wishing for nothing.<BR>E. निर्, and मम mine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=397-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्म्ममत्व|निर्ममत्व
निर्म्ममत्व n. (-त्वं) Disregard of wordly interests or possessions.<BR> E. निर्म्मम,<BR>and त्व affix; also निर्म्ममता, with तल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=397-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्म्म
निर्म्म(र्म)ल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>	 1. Clear, clean, free from dirt or impurities,<BR>(literally or figuratively.)<BR>	 2. Bright n. (-लं)<BR>	 1. The remains of an<BR>offering made to a deity.<BR>	 2. Talc.<BR> E. निर् priv. and नल<BR>dirt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=397-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्म्मलत्व|निर्मलत्व
निर्म्मलत्व n. (-त्वं) Purity, cleanness, (physical or moral.)<BR> E. त्व added to<BR>the last; also with तल, निर्म्मलता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=397-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्म्मा|निर्मा
निर्म्मा(र्मा)ण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Manufacture, production, making.<BR>	 2. Pith, mar-<BR>row, essence.<BR>	 3. Propriety, fitness.<BR> E. निर् before, मि to measure,<BR>affix भावे ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=397-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्म्माल्य|निर्माल्य|निर्म्माल्यं
निर्म्माल्य mfn. (-ल्यः-ल्या-ल्यं) Clear, clean.<BR>	 n. (-ल्यं)<BR>	 1. The remains of an<BR>offering presented to a deity.<BR>	 2. Faded flowers.<BR>	 3. Purity clean-<BR>ness, clearness.<BR>	 f. (-ल्या) A medicinal plant: see पृक्का.<BR> E. निर् not,<BR>मल dirt, impurity, affix ण्यत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=397-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्म्मि|निर्मि
निर्म्मि(र्मि)त mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Made.<BR>	 2. Fabricated, artificial.<BR> E. निर्<BR>before, मा to mete, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=397-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्म्मिति|निर्मिति|निर्मितिः|निर्म्मितिः
निर्म्मिति f. (-तिः) Making, manufacturing, artificial production. E.<BR>As above: see निर्म्मित, affix भावे क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=397-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्म्मुक्त|निर्मुक्त|निर्मुक्तः
निर्म्मुक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं) Loosed, set free, liberated, disjoined, sun-<BR>dered, separated, &c.<BR>	 m. (-क्तः) A snake who has lately cast his<BR>skin.<BR> E. निर् before, मुच् to let loose affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=397-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्म्मुट|निर्मुट|निर्मुटं|निर्मुटः
निर्म्मुट m. (-टः)<BR>	 1. A tree bearing apparent blossoms.<BR>	 2. The sun.<BR>3. A rogue.<BR>	 n. (-टं) A large, and free market or fair.<BR> E. निर्<BR>before, मुट् to press, &c. affix क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=397-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्म्मूल|निर्मूल
निर्म्मूल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>	 1. Baseless, unfounded.<BR>	 2. Eradicated.<BR> E. निर्<BR>and मूल a root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=397-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्मृष्ट
निर्मृष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं) Rubbed out.<BR> E. निर्, and मृज to rub affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=397-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्म्मोक|निर्मोक|निर्मोकः|निर्म्मोकः
निर्म्मोक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. The slough of a snake.<BR>	 2. Liberating, setting<BR>loose or free.<BR>	 3. Armour, mail.<BR>	 4. Sky, heaven, atmosphere.<BR>E. निर् forth, मुच् to let loose, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=397-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्यत्
निर्यत् mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्) Going forth or out, issuing.<BR> E. निर्, and यत्<BR>going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=397-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्य्यन्त्रण|निर्यन्त्रण|निर्यंत्रण|निर्यन्त्रणं
निर्य्यन्त्रण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Self-willed, unrestrained, uncontrolled,<BR>independent.<BR>	 n. (-णं) Independence, absence of restraint.<BR> E. निर्<BR>not, यन्त्रण restraining. निष्पीडने, यन्त्रणाशून्ये, निरर्गले, उच्छृङ्खलेच ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=397-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्यन्त्रित|निर्य्यन्त्रित
निर्यन्त्रित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Self-willed, uncontrolled, unrestrained.<BR> E. निर्<BR>neg. यन्त्रित restrained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=397-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्याण|निर्याणं|निर्य्याण
निर्याण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Going forth or out, exit, issue.<BR>	 2. Eternal eman-<BR>cipation, final beatitude.<BR>	 3. A rope for tying cattle, a foot-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=398-a" target="_blank">Page398-a+ 60</a>]<BR>rope.<BR>	 4. The outer corner of an elephant's eye.<BR>	 5. Vanishing.<BR>6. Death.<BR> E. निर् before, या to go, affix करणे ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=397-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्य्यात|निर्यात
निर्य्यात mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Gone out or forth, departed.<BR> E. निर्, and यात<BR>gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=398-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्यातन|निर्यातनं|निर्य्यातन
निर्यातन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Revenge.<BR>	 2. Gift, donation.<BR>	 3. Delivery of a<BR>deposit.<BR>	 4. Replacing any thing lost.<BR>	 5. Payment of a debt.<BR>6. Killing, slaughter.<BR> E. निर् before, यत् to endeavour, in the<BR>causal form, affix णिच्-ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=398-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्य्यातित|निर्यातित
निर्य्यातित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Taken away.<BR>	 2. Retaliated, requited. E.<BR>निर्, यत् to endeavour, causal v. क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=398-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्याम|निर्यामः|निर्य्याम
निर्याम m. (-मः) A sailor, a boatman.<BR> E. निर् before, यम् to refrain, affix<BR>घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=398-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्य्याय|निर्याय
निर्य्याय ind. Having gone out or departed.<BR> E. निर् out, याय having<BR>gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=398-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्यास|निर्यासं|निर्यासः|निर्य्यास
निर्यास m. (-सः)<BR>	 1. Extract, decoction, infusion.<BR>	 2. Any natural exu-<BR>dation of a plant, as gum, milk, extract, &c.<BR>	 3. Any thick fluid<BR>substance.<BR> E. निर् forth or out, यस् to endeavour, affix घञ्; it<BR>is also read निर्य्यास.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=398-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्य्युक्ति|निर्युक्ति
निर्य्युक्ति f. (-क्तिः)<BR>	 1. Disunion.<BR>	 2. Unfitness, inappropriateness, im-<BR>propriety.<BR>	 3. Want of connexion or government, (in Grammar.)<BR>E. निर् neg. युक्ति union, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=398-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्य्युक्तिक|निर्युक्तिक|निर्युक्तिकं
निर्य्युक्तिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>	 1. Detached, disunited.<BR>	 2. Unconnected,<BR>unmeaning.<BR>	 3. Inappropriate, improper.<BR> E. ठक् added to the<BR>preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=398-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्य्यूह|निर्यूह|निर्यूहः
निर्य्यूह m. (-हः)<BR>	 1. A chaplet, a crest, an ornament for the head.<BR>	 2.<BR>Extracted juice, or a decoction. &c.<BR>	 3. A door, a gate.<BR>	 4. A pin<BR>or bracket projecting from a wall to hang or place any thing<BR>upon.<BR>	 5. Wood placed in a wall for doves to build upon.<BR> E. निर्<BR>out, from, युह् to go, affix क, or according to Tarkabāchaspaty:--<BR>E. निर + ऊह-क-पृषो, मत्तवारणे ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=398-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्य्योगक्षेम|निर्योगक्षेम
निर्य्योगक्षेम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं) Free from care or anxiety about property. E.<BR>निर् neg. योगक्षेम property.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=398-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्लक्षण|निर्लक्षणः
निर्लक्षण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>	 1. Unmarked, unnoted, unspotted, &c.<BR>	 2.<BR>Undefined.<BR> E. निर् priv. and लक्षण a mark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=398-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्लज्ज
निर्लज्ज mfn. (-ज्जः-ज्जा-ज्जं) Impudent, shameless.<BR> E. निर् neg. लज्जा<BR>shame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=398-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्लिप्त|निर्लिप्तः
निर्लिप्त mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं)<BR>	 1. Unsmeared, unanointed.<BR>	 2. Undefiled, uncon-<BR>taminated, (by passion, &c.)<BR>	 m. (-प्तः)<BR>	 1. A name of Krishṇa.<BR>	 2.<BR>A sage.<BR> E. निर् neg. लिप to anoint and क्त affix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=398-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्लेप|निर्लेपः
निर्लेप mfn. (-पः-पा-पं)<BR>	 1. Anointed or smeared.<BR>	 2. Undefiled, (by pass-<BR>ion.)<BR>	 3. Stainless m. (-पः) A sage.<BR> E. निर् on, लेप plastering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=398-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्व्व
निर्व्व(र्व)चन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Silent.<BR>	 n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Explanation, declaration.<BR>	 2.<BR>Etymology.<BR>	 3. A proverb.<BR>	 4. Vocabulary, an index.<BR> E. निर् affix or<BR>neg. वचन speaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=398-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्व्वण|निर्वण
निर्व्वण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Bare, open, (a country)<BR> E. निर् neg. वन a wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=398-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्व्व
निर्व्व(र्व)पण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Gift, donation.<BR>	 2. Presentation of funeral offer-<BR>ings.<BR>	 3. Extinguishing, pulling out.<BR> E. निर् before, वप् to go, affix<BR>भावे ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=398-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्व्वयनी|निर्वयनी
निर्व्वयनी f. (-नी) The cast slough of a snake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=398-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्व्व
निर्व्व(र्व)र्णन n. (-नं) Sight, seeing, looking at, regarding.<BR> E. निर् before,<BR>वर्ण to class or colour, affix भावे ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=398-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वर्त्तन|निर्वर्तन|निर्वर्तनं|निर्व्वर्त्तन
निर्वर्त्तन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Leaving off, desisting from.<BR>	 2. Completing, ending.<BR>3. Limiting to, measuring by.<BR>	 4. Accomplishment.<BR> E. निर् before,<BR>वृत् to be ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=398-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्व्वर्त्य|निर्वर्त्य
निर्व्वर्त्य ind.<BR>	 1. Having finished, having done.<BR>	 2. Having ceased, E.<BR>निर् before, वृत् to be, ल्यप् aff. or निर् + वृत णिच्-कर्मणि-यत् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=398-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्व्व
निर्व्व(र्व)हण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. End, completion.<BR>	 2. Supporting, carrying on,<BR>maintaining.<BR>	 3. The catastrophe of a drama, the conclusion of<BR>the fable.<BR> E. निर् out, वह् to bear, affix भावे ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=398-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्व्वा|निर्वा
निर्व्वा(र्वा)च्य mfn. (-च्यः-च्या-च्यं)<BR>	 1. Unobjectionable, blameless, not to be<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=398-b" target="_blank">Page398-b+ 60</a>]<BR>found fault with or censured.<BR>	 2. Improper to be said.<BR> E. निर् neg.<BR>वाच्य to be spoken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=398-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्व्वा|निर्वा
निर्व्वा(र्वा)ण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>	 1. Liberated from existence.<BR>	 2. Dead, de-<BR>ceased.<BR>	 3. Gone out, extinguished, (as a fire).<BR>	 4. Set, as a planet.<BR>5. Immersed, plunged.<BR>	 6. Having no arrows.<BR>	 n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Eternal<BR>happiness, emancipation from matter, and reunion with the<BR>deity; it is especially employed in this sense by the Baudhas<BR>and Jains, understanding by it perfect and perpetual calm.<BR>	 2.<BR>Setting, disappearing, departure.<BR>	 3. Refraining, desisting, leav-<BR>ing off, cessation.<BR>	 4. Union, association, blending, confluence.<BR>	 5.<BR>Bathing or plunging of an elephant.<BR>	 6. Repose.<BR>	 7. Vacuity,<BR>vacuum or space.<BR>	 8. Instructing in science.<BR> E. निर् before, वाण् to<BR>blow, etc. affix क्त, deriv. irr. or निर् neg. वाण an arrow or निर् +<BR>वा-क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=398-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्व्वा|निर्वा
निर्व्वा(र्वा)णमस्तक m. (-कः) Liberation.<BR> E. निर्व्वाण and मस्तक head, chief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=398-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्व्वा|निर्वा
निर्व्वा(र्वा)त mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Calm, still, not windy, having ceased to<BR>blow.<BR>	 2. Sheltered from the wind.<BR>	 m. (-तः) A calm.<BR> E. निर् before,<BR>वात wind, air.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=398-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्ब्बा
निर्ब्बा(र्वा)द m. (-दः)<BR>	 1. Censure, blame, reproach.<BR>	 2. Bad rumour, or<BR>report, Scandal.<BR>	 3. Asseveration, affirmation, decision of a con-<BR>troversy.<BR>	 4. Absence of dispute or railing.<BR>	 5. Disrespect.<BR> E. निर्<BR>privat. prefix, and षाद speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=398-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्व्वा|निर्वा
निर्व्वा(र्वा)प m. (-पः)<BR>	 1. Putting out, as a fire or light.<BR>	 2. Gifts in honour<BR>of a deceased ancestor: see निवाप.<BR> E. निर् + वप-भावे-घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=398-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्व्वा|निर्वा
निर्व्वा(र्वा)पण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Putting out, as a fire or light, extinguishing,<BR>quenching.<BR>	 2. (In medicine,) Refrigerant.<BR>	 3. Killing, slaughter.<BR>4. Gift, giving.<BR>	 5. Presenting funeral oblations.<BR>	 6. Cooling, re-<BR>freshing.<BR> E. निर् before, वप् to go. &c, in the causal form, affix<BR>णिच्, वा णिच्-पुक्-ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=398-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्व्वा|निर्वा
निर्व्वा(र्वा)पित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Put out, quenched, extinguished.<BR>	 2.<BR>Allayed, cooled.<BR>	 3. Killed.<BR>	 4. Offered in oblation.<BR> E. निर्, वप् to go,<BR>causal v. क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=398-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्व्वा|निर्वा
निर्व्वा(र्वा)प्य ind.<BR>	 1. Having offered funeral cakes.<BR>	 2. Having delighted.<BR>3. Having quenched.<BR> E. निर् before, वप् to sow, affix ल्यप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=398-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वार्य्य|निर्वार्य|निर्व्वार्य्य|निर्व्वार्य्यः
निर्वार्य्य mfn. (-र्य्यः-र्य्या-र्य्यं)<BR>	 1. Acting fearlessly or determinately.<BR>	 2.<BR>Irresistible, not to be opposed or resisted.<BR> E. निर्, वृ to hinder,<BR>affix ण्यत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=398-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्व्वासन|निर्वासन|निर्वासनं|निर्व्वासनं
निर्व्वासन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Killing, slaughter.<BR>	 2. Hurting, injuring.<BR>	 3. Ba-<BR>nishment, expulsion.<BR> E. निर् out, forth, वस् to abide, causal form,<BR>and णिच्-भावे-ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=398-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्व्वासित|निर्वासित
निर्व्वासित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Expelled, banished.<BR> E. निर् out, वस् to abide,<BR>causal v., क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=398-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्व्वास्य|निर्वास्य
निर्व्वास्य mfn. (-स्यः-स्या-स्यं) To be banished.<BR> E. निर् out, वस् to abide,<BR>causal form णिच्-कर्मणि-यत् aff.; also निर्व्वासनीय, निर्व्वासितव्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=398-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्व्वा|निर्वा
निर्व्वा(र्वा)ह m. (-हः)<BR>	 1. Accomplishment, completion, end.<BR>	 2. Carrying<BR>on, supporting, maintaining.<BR>	 3. Providing means.<BR>	 4. Suf-<BR>ficiency, adequacy.<BR>	 5. Steadfastness.<BR> E. निर् before, वह् to bear,<BR>affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=398-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्व्वाहक|निर्वाहक
निर्व्वाहक n. (-कं) Application or connexion of cause and effect,<BR> E. निर्<BR>before, वह् to convey, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=398-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्व्वाहण|निर्वाहण|निर्व्वाहणं
निर्व्वाहण nf. (-णं-णा) Catastrophe of a drama: see निर्व्वहण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=398-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्व्विकल्प|निर्विकल्प
निर्व्विकल्प(क) n. (-कं) Knowledge, not depending upon or derived from<BR>the senses.<BR> E. निर् neg. विकल्प alternative, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=398-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्विकार|निर्विकारः|निर्व्विकार|निर्व्विकारः
निर्विकार mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Unchanged, unaltered, uniform.<BR> E. निर् neg.<BR>विकार change of form or state.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=398-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्विघ्न|निर्व्विघ्न
निर्विघ्न mfn. (-घ्नः-घ्ना-घ्नं) Unobstructed.<BR>	 n. subs. (-घ्नं) Absence of obs-<BR>truction or impediment. adv. Freely, unobstructedly.<BR> E. निर् neg.<BR>विघ्न obstruction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=398-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्विण्ण|निर्व्विण्ण|निर्व्विण्णः
निर्विण्ण mfn. (-ण्णः-ण्णा-ण्णं)<BR>	 1. Desponding, overcome with fear or sorrow.<BR>2. Humble.<BR>	 3. Abused, degraded.<BR>	 4. Fallen away, emaciate<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=399-a" target="_blank">Page399-a+ 60</a>]<BR>with grief.<BR>	 5. Decayed, impaired.<BR>	 6. Certain.<BR>	 7. Disgusted with<BR>anything.<BR> E. निर् private, विद् to know, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=398-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्विण्णचेतस्|निर्व्विण्णचेतस्
निर्विण्णचेतस् mfn. (-ताः-ताः-तः) Humble, resigned, meek.<BR> E. निर्विण्ण, and<BR>चेतस् mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=399-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्विन्ध्या|निर्विंध्या|निर्व्विन्ध्या
निर्विन्ध्या f. (-न्ध्या) The name of a river that rises in the Vindhya moun-<BR>tains.<BR> E. निर् out of, विन्ध्या the Vindhya hills, fem. aff. टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=399-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्विवर|निर्व्विवर
निर्विवर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Close, contiguous, without interval or inters-<BR>tice.<BR> E. निर् neg. विवर a space.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=399-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्विवेक|निर्व्विवेक
निर्विवेक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Foolish, undiscriminating.<BR> E. निर् neg. विवेक<BR>judgment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=399-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्विशङ्क|निर्विशंक|निर्व्विशङ्क
निर्विशङ्क mfn. (-ङ्कः-ङ्का-ङ्कं) Fearless, undaunted, confident.<BR> E. निर् neg.<BR>विशङ्क fearful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=399-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्विशत्|निर्व्विशत्
निर्विशत् mfn. (-शन्-शन्ती-शत्)<BR>	 1. Entering in or into.<BR>	 2. Engaged in.<BR>3. Attaining, obtaining.<BR>	 4. Marrying.<BR> E. निर् before, विश् to<BR>enter, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=399-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्विशेष|निर्विशेषः|निर्व्विशेष
निर्विशेष mfn. (-षः-षा-षं)<BR>	 1. Undiscriminating, making no difference.<BR>2. Same, like, indiscriminate.<BR> E. निर् neg. विशेष difference.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=399-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्विषा|निर्व्विषा
निर्विषा f. (-षा or -षी) A plant, (Curcuma zedoaria.)<BR> E. निर् opposite,<BR>(anti,) विष poison, antidote.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=399-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्विष्ट|निर्व्विष्ट|निर्व्विष्टः
निर्विष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>	 1. Attained, arrived at, Engaged out.<BR>	 2.<BR>Obtained, got (as wages).<BR>	 3. Engaged in, occupied by.<BR>	 4. Staying,<BR>being.<BR>	 5. Married.<BR>	 6. Earned, gained.<BR>	 7. Taken, received. E.<BR>निर् before, विश् to enter affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=399-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्व्वी
निर्व्वी(र्वी)ज mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>	 1. Seedless.<BR>	 2. Impotent.<BR> E. निर् neg. वीज<BR>a seed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=399-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वीर|निर्व्वीर|निर्व्वीरं
निर्वीर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Unheroic, cowardly.<BR>	 f. (-रा) A woman whose<BR>husband and children are dead, a childless widow.<BR> E. निर priva-<BR>tive, and वीर a hero, a champion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=399-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वीर्य्य|निर्वीर्य|निर्व्वीर्य्य
निर्वीर्य्य mfn. (-र्य्यः-र्य्या-र्य्यं)<BR>	 1. Tame, feeble, spiritless.<BR>	 2. Impotent. E.<BR>निर् not, वीर्य्य power.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=399-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वृत
निर्वृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Ended, terminated.<BR>	 2. Happy, content.<BR>	 3. Eman-<BR>cipated.<BR>	 4. Free from occupation or interest.<BR>	 n. (-तं) A house. E.<BR>निर्, and वृ to choose. क्त affix: see निवृत्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=399-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वृति|निर्वृतिः
निर्वृति f. (-ति)<BR>	 1. Final emancipation from existence.<BR>	 2. Death.<BR>	 3.<BR>Happiness.<BR>	 4. Rest, repose, tranquillity, ceasing or abstaining<BR>from.<BR>	 5. Setting, departure, disappearance.<BR>	 6. Completion, accom-<BR>plishment, conclusion.<BR> E. निर् affirmative particle, वृ to choose,<BR>affix भावे क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=399-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वृत्त|निर्वृत्तः
निर्वृत्त mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं) Finished, completely done, accomplished.<BR> E. निर्<BR>before, वृत् to be, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=399-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वृत्ति|निर्वृत्तिः
निर्वृत्ति mfn. (-त्तिः-त्तिः-त्ति) Desititute, having no occupation.<BR>	 f. (-त्तिः)<BR>	 1.<BR>Completion, termination, conclusion.<BR>	 2. Satisfaction.<BR>	 3. Final<BR>beatitude.<BR>	 4. Approach, advance.<BR> E. निर् neg. वृत् to be, affix भावे<BR>क्तिन्; or निर्, and वृत्ति business.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=399-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वेग
निर्वेग mfn. (-गः-गा-गं) Calm, (as the ocean.)<BR> E. निर्, and वेग agi-<BR>tation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=399-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वेद|निर्वेदः|निर्व्वेदः
निर्वेद mfn. (-दः-दा-दं) Not having the Vedas, infidel, unscriptural.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-दः)<BR>	 1. Humility, self-Humiliation.<BR>	 2. Being neglected or disre-<BR>garded by others.<BR>	 3. Indifference, disregard of worldly objects. E.<BR>निर् depreciative particle, विद् to know, affix भावे घञ्, or निर् neg.<BR>वेद the Vedas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=399-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वेश|निर्वेशः|निर्व्वेशः
निर्वेश m. (-शः)<BR>	 1. Wages, hire.<BR>	 2. Enjoyment.<BR>	 3. Eating.<BR>	 4. Fainting,<BR>swooning, syncope.<BR>	 5. Attaining, obtaining.<BR>	 6. Engaged or enter-<BR>ing in.<BR> E. निर् before, विश् to enter, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=399-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वेष्टन|निर्वेष्टनं|निर्व्वेष्टनं
निर्वेष्टन n. (-नं) A. small reed used as a shuttle.<BR> E. निर् without, वेष्टन<BR>surrounding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=399-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वैर
निर्वैर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Friendly, without enmity.<BR> E. निर् neg. वैर hostility.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=399-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्व्यथन|निर्व्यथनं
निर्व्यथन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. A hole, a chasm.<BR>	 2. Exemption from pain.<BR>	 3.<BR>Paining, afflicting.<BR> E. निर् affir. or neg. prefix, and व्यथन fear,<BR>dread.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=399-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्व्यपेक्ष
निर्व्यपेक्ष mfn. (-क्षः-क्षा-क्षं) Indifferent to, disregarding.<BR> E. निर् neg. व्यपेक्षा<BR>expectation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=399-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्व्यलीक
निर्व्यलीक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Undissembling, true,<BR> E. निर् neg. व्यलीक<BR>false.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=399-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्व्याज
निर्व्याज mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>	 1. Without deceit.<BR>	 2. Without obstruction.<BR>E. निर् neg. व्याज deceit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=399-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्व्यूढ|निर्व्यूढं
निर्व्यूढ mfn. (-ढः-ढा-ढं)<BR>	 1. Abandoned, left, deserted.<BR>	 2. Finished,<BR>completed.<BR>	 3. Grown, developed.<BR>	 4. Vindicated.<BR> E. निर् before, व्यूढ<BR>arranged. निर + वि-वह-क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=399-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्हरण|निर्हरणं
निर्हरण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Taking forth or out.<BR>	 2. Removing entirely.<BR>	 3. Set-<BR>ting apart.<BR>	 4. Burning dead bodies, or carrying them out to be<BR>burnt.<BR> E. निर् away, हरण taking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=399-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्हार|निर्हारः
निर्हार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Extracting, drawing out, rooting up, &c.<BR>	 2. Put-<BR>ting forth or out.<BR>	 3. Evacuation of any of the natural excrements<BR>of the fæces, urine, sweat, &c.<BR>	 4. Burning, combustion.<BR>	 5. Giving<BR>away, selling, exchanging, &c.<BR>	 6. Diffusive fragrance.<BR>	 7. Ac-<BR>cumulation of wealth, a hoard, a private purse.<BR> E. निर् out, हृ to<BR>take, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=399-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्हारिन्
निर्हारिन् mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>	 1. Taking forth or out.<BR>	 2. Diffusively<BR>fragrant, having a wide spreading odour.<BR>	 3. Having wealth. E.<BR>निर्, हृ to take, घिणुन् aff. or निर्हार, affix णिनि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=399-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्हृत
निर्हृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Taken or carried forth or out.<BR>	 2. Extracted.<BR>E. निर् out, हृत taken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=399-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्हृत्य
निर्हृत्य ind.<BR>	 1. Having taken forth or out.<BR>	 2. Having extracted. E.<BR>निर् before, हृ to take, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=399-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्हेति
निर्हेति mfn. (-तिः-तिः-ति) Unarmed.<BR> E. निर्, and हेति a weapon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=399-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्ह्राद|निर्ह्रादः
निर्ह्राद m. (-दः) A sound in general.<BR> E. निर् before, हृद् to sound, affix<BR>घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=399-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निलय|निलयः
निलय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. A house, a habitation.<BR>	 2. Abiding place, a den of<BR>animals.<BR> E. नि in, ली to embrace, affix आधारे अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=399-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निलयन|निलयनं
निलयन n. (-नं) Place, dwelling.<BR>	 2. Setting in a place.<BR> E. नि before, ली<BR>to endeavour, आधारे ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=399-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निलायिता
निलायिता f. (-ता) Dwelling, domesticality.<BR> E. निलायिन्, and तल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=399-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निलायिन्
निलायिन् mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि) Dwelling in, inhabiting.<BR> E. नि before, ली to<BR>embrace, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=399-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निलिम्प|निलिंप|निलिंपः|निलिम्पः
निलिम्प m. (-म्पः) A deity.<BR>	 f. (-म्पा) A cow.<BR> E. नि in or on, लिम्प to smear,<BR>affix खञ्, or according to others, नि + लिप-कर्त्तरि-श ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=399-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निलिम्पिका|निलिंपिका
निलिम्पिका f. (-का) A cow.<BR> E. कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=399-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निलीन|निलीनं
निलीन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>	 1. Encompassed, surrounded, shut or wrapt up,<BR>embraced.<BR>	 2. Destroyed, perished entirely.<BR>	 3. Transformed,<BR>changed.<BR>	 4. Fused in or into.<BR>	 5. Full.<BR> E. नि in or on, ली to<BR>embrace, affix क्त, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=399-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवपन|निवपनं
निवपन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Gifts in honour of deceased ancestors.<BR>	 2. Scattering,<BR>or throwing out.<BR>	 3. Sowing, also निवाप. नि + वप-भावे-ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=399-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवरा
निवरा f. (-रा) A virgin, a girl unmarried.<BR> E. नि priv. and वर a husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=399-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवर्त्तन|निवर्तन
निवर्त्तन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Returning or coming back.<BR>	 2. Bringing back.<BR>	 3.<BR>Reforming, repenting.<BR>	 4. Desisting from a work.<BR>	 5. Giving back,<BR>returning.<BR>	 6. Stopping, ceasing.<BR>	 7. A measure of land 20<BR>rods, or 200 cubits square.<BR> E. नि before वृत् to be, णिच्-भावे ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=399-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवर्त्तयितव्य|निवर्तयितव्य
निवर्त्तयितव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं) To be restrained, to be hindered or<BR>diverted.<BR> E. नि before, वृत् to be, causal v., तव्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=399-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवर्त्ता
निवर्त्ता ind.<BR>	 1. Having desisted or refrained from.<BR>	 2. Having turned<BR>back.<BR>	 3. Having repented.<BR>	 4. Having repaid.<BR> E. नि before, वृत् to<BR>be, aff. ल्यप्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=399-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवर्हण
निवर्हण nf. (-णं-णा)<BR>	 1. Killing, destroying.<BR>	 2. Removing.<BR> E. नि before,<BR>वर्ह to cover, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=399-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवर्हित
निवर्हित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Killed, destroyed.<BR>	 2. Removed, taken away.<BR>E. नि before, वर्ह to cover, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=399-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवसत्
निवसत् mfn. (-सन् सन्ती-सत्) Dwelling in, inhabiting.<BR> E. नि before,<BR>वस् to dwell, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=399-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवसति|निवसतिः
निवसति f. (-तिः) A house, a habitation.<BR> E. नि in, वस् to dwell, आधारे<BR>अतिच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=400-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवसथ|निवसथः
निवसथ m. (-थः) A village.<BR> E. नि in, वस् to dwell, aff. आधारे अथच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=400-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवसन|निवसनं
निवसन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. A house, a habitation.<BR>	 2. Cloth, clothes, raiment. E.<BR>नि in, वस् to dwell or wear, aff. आधारे ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=400-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवह|निवहः
निवह m. (-हः)<BR>	 1. A multitude, a quantity.<BR>	 2. One of the seven winds.<BR>E. नि always, वह to gain, घ or अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=400-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवात|निवातः
निवात mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Well armed, accoutred in strong mail.<BR>	 2.<BR>Secure, safe as in an asylum.<BR>	 3. Calm, not windy.<BR>	 4. Unhurt.<BR>5. Protected against the wind.<BR>	 m. (-तः)<BR>	 1. An asylum, a dwelling,<BR>&c.<BR>	 2. A calm.<BR>	 3. Strong armour.<BR> E. नि neg. वात wind, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=400-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवातकवच|निवातकवचः
निवातकवच m. (-चः) A demon, the grandson of HIRAṆYAKAŚIPU. E.<BR>निवात, and कवच a cuirass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=400-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवाप|निवापः
निवाप m. (-पः)<BR>	 1. Gifts in honour of a deceased parent or relative.<BR>2. Offering of water at Śrāddhas, or daily ablution to the manes.<BR>3. Gift, giving in general.<BR>	 4. Seed, grain.<BR> E. नि before, वप् to go,<BR>to give, &c. aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=400-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नि|निः
नि(नी)वार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Hindering, opposition, impediment.<BR>	 2. Name of<BR>the grain so called.<BR> E. नि prefix, वॄ to screen, घञ्. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=400-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवारण|निवारणं
निवारण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Hindering, opposing.<BR>	 2. An impediment.<BR>	 3.<BR>Contemning, holding light or worthless.<BR> E. नि prefix, वॄ to screen,<BR>णिच्-भावे-ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=400-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवारणीय
निवारणीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) To be checked, hindered, &c.<BR> E. नि before,<BR>वॄ to screen, aff. अनीयर्; also निवारितव्य and निवार्य्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=400-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवारयत्
निवारयत् mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्) Opposing, hindering.<BR> E. नि before, वॄ to<BR>screen, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=400-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवारित|निवारितः
निवारित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Hindered, checked, opposed.<BR> E. नि prefix, वॄ<BR>to screen, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=400-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवार्य्यमाण|निवार्यमाण
निवार्य्यमाण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) To be opposed or hindered.<BR> E. नि before,<BR>वॄ to screen, pass. v., शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=400-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवास|निवासः
निवास m. (-सः)<BR>	 1. A house, a dwelling.<BR>	 2. Passing the night.<BR> E. नि<BR>in, वस् to abide, aff. आधारे घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=400-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवासभूय
निवासभूय n. (-यं) Habitation or inhabiting.<BR> E. निवास, and भूय<BR>being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=400-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवासिन्
निवासिन् mfn. (-सी-सिनी-सि) Dwelling, abiding in, inhabiting.<BR> E. निवास,<BR>and णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=400-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निविड|निविडं
निविड mfn. (-डः-डा-डं)<BR>	 1. Coarse, large, gross, bulky, without spaces<BR>or interstices.<BR>	 2. Thick, impervious, impenetrable.<BR>	 3. Crooked-<BR>nosed.<BR> E. नि not, विल an interstice, ल changed to ड; or नि parti-<BR>cle, with विलच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=400-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निविरीस|निविरीसं
निविरीस mfn. (-सः-सा-सं)<BR>	 1. Coarse, gross.<BR>	 2. Crooked-nosed.<BR> E. नेर्वि-<BR>डज् विरीसची पा० विरीसच् दन्त्योच्चारणसामर्थ्यात् न षत्वम् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=400-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निविवृत्सत्
निविवृत्सत् mfn. (-सन्-सन्ती-सत्) Wishing to stop or return.<BR> E. नि before,<BR>वृत् to abide, desid. form, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=400-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निविशेष|निविशेषः
निविशेष mfn. (-षः-षा-षं) Alike, not different.<BR> E. नि neg. विशेष difference.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=400-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निविष्ट|निविष्टं|निविष्टः
निविष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>	 1. Entered, gone in or into.<BR>	 2. Seated, sit-<BR>ting upon.<BR>	 3. Situated or placed in or on.<BR>	 3. Arranged.<BR>	 4. Fixed<BR>on.<BR> E. नि before, विश् to enter, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=400-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवीत|निवीतं|निवीतः
निवीत mfn. subst. (-तः-ता-तं) A veil, a mantle, a wrapper.<BR>	 n. (-तं) The<BR>Brahmanical thread suspended round the neck, in which manner<BR>it is worn on some occasions.<BR> E. नि before, व्ये to cover, aff. क्त. or<BR>नि + अज क्त व्यादेशः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=400-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवीतिन्
निवीतिन् m. (-ती) A Brāhman with the cord suspended round his neck<BR>E. निवीत, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=400-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवृत|निवृतं|निवृतः
निवृत mfn. adj. (-तः-ता-तं) Surrounded, enclosed, encompassed. subst.<BR>A veil, a mantle, a wrapper.<BR> E. नि before, वृ to surround aff क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=400-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवृति|निवृतिः
निवृति f. (-तिः) Covering, enclosing.<BR> E. नि, वृ to be, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=400-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवृत्त|निवृत्तः
निवृत्त mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं)<BR>	 1. Ceased, stopped.<BR>	 2. Abstaining from worldy<BR>acts, &c.<BR>	 3. Abstracted from or independent of worldly motives.<BR>4. Desisting from or repenting of any improper conduct.<BR>	 5. Re-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=400-b" target="_blank">Page400-b+ 60</a>]<BR>turned, turned back.<BR>	 6. Gone, departed.<BR>	 7. Finished, complet-<BR>ed.<BR> E. नि prohibitory prefix, वृत् to be, aff. क्त; see निर्वृत्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=400-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवृत्तकारण|निवृत्तकारणः
निवृत्तकारण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Without further cause or motive.<BR>	 m. (-णः)<BR>A virtuous man, one uninfluenced by worldy desires.<BR> E. निवृत्त<BR>ceased, कारण cause.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=400-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवृत्तराग
निवृत्तराग mfn. (-गः-गा-गं) Of subdued appetite or passions.<BR> E. निवृत्त<BR>stopped, राग passion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=400-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवृत्तवृत्ति
निवृत्तवृत्ति mfn. (-त्तिः-त्तिः-त्ति) Quitting any practice or occupation. E.<BR>निवृत्त, and वृत्ति maintenance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=400-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवृतात्मन्
निवृतात्मन् m. (-त्मा)<BR>	 1. A sage.<BR>	 2. VIṢṆU.<BR> E. निवृत्त stopped, (from<BR>worldly acts, &c.) आत्मन् spirit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=400-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवृत्ति|निवृत्तिः
निवृत्ति f. (-त्तिः)<BR>	 1. Cessation, completion, leaving off, rest, repose.<BR>	 2.<BR>Discontinuance of worldly acts, cessation of emotions, separation<BR>from the world.<BR>	 3. Denial, refusal.<BR>	 4. Abolition, prevention.<BR>5. Returning.<BR> E. नि negative prefix, वृत् to be, aff. भावे क्तिन्ः see<BR>निर्वृत्ति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=400-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवेदन|निवेदनं|निवेदनः
निवेदन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Delivering, giving, entrusting, addressing, (either<BR>an article, a massage, or a speech.)<BR>	 2. Dedication.<BR>	 3. Oblation.<BR>4. An offering.<BR> E. नि before, विद् to know, causal form, aff.<BR>ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=400-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवेदित|निवेदितं
निवेदित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Given, entrusted, addressed, delivered.<BR>	 2.<BR>Represented, stated, told.<BR> E. नि before, विद् to know, aff. क्तः see<BR>निवेदन ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=400-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवेश|निवेशः
निवेश m. (-शः)<BR>	 1. Entrance, entering.<BR>	 2. Delivering, entrusting, de-<BR>positing.<BR>	 3. A camp. a place, the residence of a king or general.<BR>4. Any dwelling.<BR>	 5. Military array.<BR>	 6. Ornament, dress, decora-<BR>tion.<BR>	 7. Marriage.<BR>	 8. Encamping.<BR> E. नि before, विश् to enter, aff.<BR>भावे घञ्,<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=400-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवेशन|निवेशनं
निवेशन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Entering, entrance.<BR>	 2. A house, a habitation.<BR>	 3. A<BR>town or city.<BR>	 4. A camp.<BR> E. नि before, विश् to enter, aff आधारे ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=400-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवेशनीय|निवेशनीयः
निवेशनीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>	 1. To be entered.<BR>	 2. To be engaged in.<BR> E. नि<BR>before, विश् to enter, अनीयर् aff.; also निवेशितव्य and निवेश्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=400-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवेशयत्
निवेशयत् mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्) Sending in or into, causing to enter.<BR> E. नि<BR>before विश् to enter, causal form, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=400-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवेशित्
निवेशित् mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Entered into.<BR>	 2. Engaged in.<BR>	 3. Sent,<BR>directed.<BR>	 4. Placed in or upon.<BR>	 5. Turned to or towards, fixed<BR>upon.<BR> E. नि before, विश् to enter, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=400-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निव्यूढ|निव्यूढं
निव्यूढ n. (-ढं) Perseverance, resolution.<BR> E. नि, and व्यूढ arranged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=400-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निश्
निश् f. (-निट्)<BR>	 1. Night.<BR>	 2. Turmeric, see निशा. नितरां श्यति तनूकरोति<BR>व्यापारान् शो-क-पृषो० ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=400-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशठ|निशठः
निशठ m. (-ठः) The son of BALARĀMA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=400-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशमन|निशमनं
निशमन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Sight, seeing.<BR>	 2. Hearing.<BR>	 3. Becoming aware of.<BR>E. नि before, शम् to be quite, aff णिच्-ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=400-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशम्य
निशम्य ind. Hearing, having heard.<BR> E. नि, शम् to repose, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=400-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशमयत्
निशमयत् mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्) Hearing.<BR> E. नि before, शम् to rest, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=400-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशमय्य
निशमय्य ind. Having heard.<BR> E. नि before, शम् to repose, ल्यप् aff., and<BR>अय inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=400-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशा
निशा f. (-शा)<BR>	 1. Night.<BR>	 2. Turmeric, (Curcuma longa.)<BR>	 3. Another<BR>sort, (C. zanthorrhiza.)<BR> E. नि always, शो to waste or reduce,<BR>(mortals,) aff. क; or निश् to meditate, aff. क्विप्, and टाप added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=400-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशाकर|निशाकरः
निशाकर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. The moon.<BR>	 2. A cock.<BR>	 3. Camphire.<BR> E. निशा night,<BR>and कर who makes or marks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=400-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशाकेतु|निशाकेतुः
निशाकेतु m. (-तुः) The moon.<BR> E. निशा night, and केतु symbol.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=400-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशागण|निशागणः
निशागण m. (-णः) A number of nights.<BR> E. निशा a night, and गण a class,<BR>a troop.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=400-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशाचर|निशाचरः
निशाचर mfn. (-रः-रा-री-रं) Nocturnal, night walking, what goes or<BR>moves about by night.<BR>	 m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A Rākshasa, a fiend, an imp or<BR>goblin.<BR>	 2. A Jackal.<BR>	 3. An owl.<BR>	 4. A snake.<BR>	 5. The ruddy goose.<BR>6. A ghost, an evil spirit.<BR>	 7. A thief.<BR>	 f. (-री)<BR>	 1. A woman who<BR>goes to an assignation, a harlot, a whore.<BR>	 2. A she devil, a<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=401-a" target="_blank">Page401-a+ 60</a>]<BR>female fiend.<BR>	 3. A sort of perfume: see केशिनी.<BR> E. निशा night,<BR>and चर who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=400-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशाचर्म्मन्|निशाचर्मन्
निशाचर्म्मन् n. (-र्म्म) Darkness.<BR> E. निशा night, and चर्म्मन् skin or<BR>hide.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=401-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशाजल|निशाजलं
निशाजल n. (-लं)<BR>	 1. Frost, hoar frost.<BR>	 2. Dew.<BR> E. निशा night, and जल<BR>water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=401-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशाट|निशाटः
निशाट m. (-टः)<BR>	 1. An owl.<BR>	 2. A demon, a ghost.<BR> E. निशा night, and<BR>अट who goes; अच् aff. also with ल्यु aff. निशाटन m. (-नः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=401-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशात|निशातः
निशात mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Sharpened, polished, whetted, burnished. E.<BR>नि before, शो to cut or pare, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=401-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशाद|निशादः
निशाद m. (-दः) A man of a low caste: see निषाद.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=401-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशादत्व
निशादत्व n. (-त्वं) The state or condition of a man of low caste.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=401-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशादर्शिन्
निशादर्शिन् m. (-र्शी) An owl.<BR> E. निशा night, and दर्शिन् who sees.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=401-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशादि|निशादिः
निशादि f. (-दिः) Evening, twilight.<BR> E. निशा, and आदि beginning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=401-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशान्त|निशांत|निशान्तं|निशान्तः
निशान्त mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं) Quiet, tranquil, patient.<BR>	 n. (-न्तं)<BR>	 1. A house,<BR>a dwelling.<BR>	 2. The end of the night, or break of day.<BR> E. नि before,<BR>शम् to be quiet, aff. क्त; or निशा night, अम् to go, aff. क्त; or निशा as<BR>before night, and अन्त end or term.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=401-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशान्तनारी
निशान्तनारी f. (-री) A female, a housewife.<BR> E. निशान्त a house, नारी a<BR>a woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=401-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशान्ध|निशांध
निशान्ध mfn. (-न्धः-न्धा-न्धं) Blind at night.<BR> E. निशा, and अन्ध blind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=401-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशापति|निशापतिः
निशापति m. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. The moon.<BR>	 2. Camphor.<BR>	 3. An epithet of Siva.<BR>4. A name of Rāvana.<BR> E. निशा night, and पति master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=401-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशापुष्प|निशापुष्पं
निशापुष्प n. (-ष्पं)<BR>	 1. Hoar, frost.<BR>	 2. Dew.<BR>	 3. The white water lily which<BR>blossoms at night.<BR> E. निशा, and पुष्प a flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=401-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशाभङ्गा
निशाभङ्गा f. (-ङ्गा) A plant commonly Dugdhapeya.<BR> E. निशा night, भङ्गा<BR>breaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=401-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशामणि|निशामणिः
निशामणि m. (-णिः)<BR>	 1. The moon.<BR>	 2. Camphor.<BR> E. निशा night, and मणि a<BR>gem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=401-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशामन|निशामनं
निशामन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Sight, seeing.<BR>	 2. Looking at, beholding.<BR>	 3. Looking<BR>at repeatedly.<BR>	 4. Hearing.<BR>	 5. A shadow, a reflexion.<BR> E. नि before,<BR>शम् to quiet, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=401-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशामृग|निशामृगः
निशामृग m. (-गः) A Jackal.<BR> E. निशा night, and मृग a deer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=401-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशाम्य
निशाम्य ind.<BR>	 1. Having put out, (as a light)<BR>	 2. Having tranquillized.<BR>E. नि before, शम् to be quiet, causal form, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=401-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशारण|निशारणं
निशारण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Killing, slaying, slaughter.<BR>	 2. Night-combat.<BR> E. नि<BR>before, शृ to injure or kill, aff. स्वार्थे ल्युट्; or निशा night, and रण<BR>war.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=401-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशारत्र
निशारत्र m. (-त्रः)<BR>	 1. The moon.<BR>	 2. Camphor.<BR> E. निशा night, and रत्न a<BR>jewel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=401-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशारुक|निशारुकः
निशारुक n. (-कं) An air, a sort of musical composition, played as an<BR>accomplishment to dancing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=401-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशावृन्द|निशावृन्दं
निशावृन्द n. (-न्दं) A number of nights.<BR> E. निशा, and वृन्द a many.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=401-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशावेदिन्
निशावेदिन् m. (-दी) A cock.<BR> E. निशा night, and वेदिन् who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=401-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशाहस|निशाहसः
निशाहस m. (-सः) The white water lily.<BR> E. निशा, and हस what smiles;<BR>opening its petals at night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=401-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशाह्वा
निशाह्वा f. (-ह्वा) Turmeric.<BR> E. निशा, and आह्वा appellation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=401-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशित|निशितं|निशितः
निशित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Sharpened, whetted.<BR>	 2. Stimulated.<BR>	 n. (-तं)<BR>Iron.<BR> E. नि before, शो to pare, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=401-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशिपुष्पा
निशिपुष्पा f. (-ष्पा) A flower, (Nyctanthes tristis.)<BR> E. निशि by night,<BR>seventh case of निश्, and पुष्प flower, fem. affix टाप्; also with ङीप्<BR>affix निशिपुष्पी, and with कन् added निशिपुष्पिका the night-flowers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=401-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशीथ|निशीथः
निशीथ n. (-थं)<BR>	 1. Midnight.<BR>	 2. Night. (In general).<BR> E. नि always, शी<BR>to sleep, Unādi affix थक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=401-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशीथिनी
निशीथिनी f. (-नी) Night.<BR> E. निशीथ as above, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=401-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशीथिनीनाथ|निशीथिनीनाथः
निशीथिनीनाथ m. (-थः) The moon.<BR> E. निशीथिनी night, and नाथ lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=401-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशीथ्या
निशीथ्या f. (-थ्या) Night.<BR> E. निशीथ midnight, and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=401-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशुम्भ|निशुंभ|निशुंभः|निशुम्भः
निशुम्भ m. (-म्भः)<BR>	 1. Killing, slaughter.<BR>	 2. The name of a giant slain by<BR>DURGĀ.<BR> E. नि before, शुम्भ् to hurt or kill, aff. भावे घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=401-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशुम्भन|निशुंभन|निशुंभनं|निशुम्भनं
निशुम्भन n. (-नं) Killing, slaying, slaughter. E. See the last, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=401-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशुम्भमर्द्दिनी|निशुम्भमर्दिनी|निशुंभमर्दिनी
निशुम्भमर्द्दिनी f. (-नी) A name of DURGĀ.<BR> E. निशुम्भ an Asura or demon so<BR>named, and मर्द्दिनी the female destroyer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=401-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशुम्भिन्
निशुम्भिन् m. (-म्भी) An inferior deity of the Baudhas; also Heramba<BR>and Vajratika.<BR> E. नि not, शुम्भ injuring, aff. इनि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=401-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशोपशाय
निशोपशाय m. (-यः) Resting at night.<BR> E. निशा, and उपशाय rest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=401-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशैत|निशैतः
निशैत m. (-तः) The Vaka, a crane, (Ardea nivea.)<BR> E. निशा by night,<BR>इत gone, to his roost.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=401-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निश्चय|निश्चयः
निश्चय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. Certainty, ascertainment, positive, conclusion.<BR>	 2. A<BR>fixed intention, design, purpose, aim.<BR> E. निर affirmative particle,<BR>चि to collect, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=401-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निश्चल
निश्चल mfn. (-लः-ला-ली-लं)<BR>	 1. Immoveable, still, fixed.<BR>	 2. Invariable.<BR>	 f.<BR>(ला) The earth.<BR> E. निर् privat. चल what goes or moves.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=401-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निश्चलाङ्ग|निश्चलांग|निश्चलाङ्गः
निश्चलाङ्ग mfn. (-ङ्गः-ङ्गी-ङ्गं) Firm, immoveable.<BR>	 m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>	 1. A kind of<BR>crane, (Ardea nivea.)<BR>	 2. A mountain, a rock.<BR> E. निश्चल, and अङ्ग<BR>body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=401-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निश्चायक|निश्चायकः
निश्चायक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Who or what ascertains or determines.<BR> E. निर्<BR>before, चि to collect, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=401-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निश्चारक|निश्चारकं|निश्चारकः
निश्चारक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. Evacuation by stool.<BR>	 2. Air, wind.<BR>	 3. Obstinacy,<BR>wilfulness.<BR> E. निर् not, चर् to go, aff. ण्वुल्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=401-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निश्चित
निश्चित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Certain, ascertained, determined, con-<BR>cluded.<BR>	 2. Sentenced, pronounced.<BR>	 n. (-तं) Certainty, conclusion,<BR>E. निर् before, चि to collect, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=401-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निश्चित्य
निश्चित्य ind. Having ascertained,<BR> E. निर् aff. चि to collect, ल्यप्<BR>aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=401-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निश्चिन्त|निश्चिंत|निश्चिन्तः
निश्चिन्त mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं) Thoughtless, inconsiderate, void of reflex-<BR>ion.<BR> E. निर् neg. चिन्ता reflexion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=401-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निश्चीयमान|निश्चीयमानः
निश्चीयमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Being in the course of ascertainment or<BR>conclusion, being under investigation.<BR> E. निर् before, चि to col-<BR>lect, शानच् aff., यक् inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=401-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निश्चुक्वण
निश्चुक्वण n. (-णं) A sort of tooth-powder prepared of sulphate of<BR>iron &c., it destroys the tartar, but blackens the teeth.<BR> E. निर्<BR>before, चुक्क् to give pain, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=401-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निश्चेष्ट|निश्चेष्टः
निश्चेष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>	 1. Powerless, helpless.<BR>	 2. Incapable of effort.<BR>E. निर् neg. चेष्टा effort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=401-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निश्श्रेयस
निश्श्रेयस n. (-सं) Final emancipation: see निःश्रेयस.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=401-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निश्श्रेयसकर
निश्श्रेयसकर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Conferring final happiness or emancipa-<BR>tion.<BR> E. निःश्रेयस and कर what makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=401-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नि|निः
नि(श्)श्वसन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Breathing out, expiration.<BR>	 2. Sighing.<BR> E. निर्<BR>and असन breathing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=401-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नि|निः
नि(श्)श्वास m. (-सः)<BR>	 1. Breath expired, breathing out, expiration.<BR> E. निर्<BR>out, and श्वास breath.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=401-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष
निष (उ) निषु r. 1st. cl. (नेषति) To sprinkle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=401-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषङ्ग|निषंग|निषंगः|निषङ्गः
निषङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>	 1. A quiver.<BR>	 2. Union, meeting, association.<BR>	 3. At-<BR>tachment.<BR> E. नि before, सञ्ज् to embrace, aff. घञ्; a collection of<BR>arrows, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=401-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषङ्गथि|निषंगथि|निषंगथिः|निषङ्गथिः
निषङ्गथि m. (-थिः)<BR>	 1. Embracing, an embrace.<BR>	 2. A bowman.<BR>	 3. A<BR>charioteer.<BR>	 4. A car.<BR>	 5. Grass.<BR>	 6. The shoulder.<BR> E. नि before, सञ्ज्<BR>to embrace, Uṇadi aff. भावे गथिन्, कुत्वम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=401-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषङ्गिन्|निषंगिन्
निषङ्गिन् m. (-ङ्गी)<BR>	 1. An archer, a bowman.<BR>	 2. A quiver.<BR> E. निसङ्ग a<BR>quiver, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=401-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषद|निषदः
निषद m. (-दः) A musical note: see निषाद.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=401-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषद्या
निषद्या f. (-द्या)<BR>	 1. A market.<BR>	 2. A small bed or couch.<BR>	 3. A shop.<BR> E. नि<BR>before, षद् to go क्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=401-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषद्वर|निषद्वरः
निषद्वर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Mud, mire.<BR>	 2. The god of love.<BR>	 f. (-री) Night. E.<BR>नि before, सद् to go Unādi, aff. क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=401-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषध|निषधः
निषध m. (-धः)<BR>	 1. The name of a mountain or mountainous range,<BR>forming one of the principal ranges of the universe, and des-<BR>cribed as lying immediately south of Ilāvrata, and north of the<BR>Himālaya range.<BR>	 2. A country in the south-east division of India.<BR>3. The sovereign of Nishada.<BR>	 4. A musical note; also निषाद ।<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=402-a" target="_blank">Page402-a+ 60</a>]<BR>5. Hard, solid.<BR> E. नि before, सद् to go, aff. अच्, and द irregularly<BR>changed to ध.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=401-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषण्ण|निषण्णः
निषण्ण mfn. (-ण्ण-ण्णा-ण्णं)<BR>	 1. Placed in or on.<BR>	 2. Gone to.<BR>	 3. Rested,<BR>reclined.<BR> E. नि before, सद् to go, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=402-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषण्णक|निषण्णकं
निषण्णक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Seating, seated.<BR>	 n. (-कं) A seat.<BR> E. कन् added<BR>to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=402-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषन्नक
निषन्नक m. (-कः) A sort of potherb, (Marsilea dentata.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=402-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषाद|निषादः
निषाद m. (-दः)<BR>	 1. The last or the seventh note of the Hindu gamut,<BR>or more properly the highest of the scale.<BR>	 2. A man of a<BR>degraded tribe, or an outcaste, especially the son of a Brāhman<BR>by a Śūdra woman.<BR>	 3. A fisherman.<BR> E. नि before, सद् to go, aff.<BR>आधारे घञ्; pervading the mind, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=402-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषादिन
निषादिन mf. (-दी-दिनी)<BR>	 1. An elephant-keeper or driver.<BR>	 2. Sitting.<BR>E. नि before, सद् to go, aff. णिच्-णिनि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=402-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषिद्ध|निषिद्धं
निषिद्ध mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>	 1. Prohibited, forbidden.<BR>	 2. Prevented.<BR> E. नि<BR>priv. सिध् to complete, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=402-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषीदत्
निषीदत् mfn. (-दन्-दन्ती-दत्)<BR>	 1. Sitting, sitting upon.<BR>	 2. Standing or<BR>resting in or on.<BR> E. नि before, सद् to go, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=402-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषू
निषू(सू)दन n. (-नं) Killing, slaughter.<BR>	 m. (-दः) A killer.<BR> E. नि before, षद्<BR>to kill, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=402-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषेक|निषेकः
निषेक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. The ceremony performed upon impregnation taking<BR>place.<BR>	 2. Sprinkling, aspersion.<BR>	 3. Effusion.<BR>	 4. Seminal infusion.<BR>5. Irrigation.<BR>	 6. Dirty water.<BR> E. नि, and सिच् to sprinkle, aff.<BR>भावे घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=402-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषेदिवस्
निषेदिवस् mfn. (-वान्-वसी-वस्) Sitting, seated on or upon.<BR> E. नि before,<BR>सद् to go, क्वसु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=402-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषेध|निषेधः
निषेध m. (-धः)<BR>	 1. Prohibition, negation.<BR>	 2. Stop, discontinuance.<BR>	 3.<BR>Contrariety to or deviation from rule, irregularity, exception.<BR>4. Negation.<BR>	 5. A prohibitive rule or precept (In religious law).<BR>E. नि before, सिद to complete, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=402-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषेवन
निषेवन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Service.<BR>	 2. Observance, practice, adherence to.<BR>3. Worship.<BR>	 4. Enjoying.<BR>	 5. Familiarity with.<BR> E. नि before, सेव्<BR>to serve, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=402-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषेवणीय
निषेवणीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>	 1. To be served, to be obeyed.<BR>	 2. To be<BR>observed or followed.<BR> E. नि before, सेव् to serve, अनीयर aff.; also<BR>निषेवितव्य, and निषेव्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=402-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषेवित
निषेवित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Observed, practised.<BR>	 2. Served, obeyed.<BR>	 3.<BR>Frequented through respect.<BR> E. नि before, सेव् to serve, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=402-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्क|निष्कं|निष्कः
निष्क r. 10th cl. (निष्कयते) To measure or weigh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=402-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्क|निष्कं|निष्कः
निष्क mn. (-ष्कः-ष्कं)<BR>	 1. A weight of gold, applied however to different<BR>quantities: it is considered as synonimous with the Dināra of<BR>thirty-two small, or sixteen large Rattis; with the Karṣa or<BR>Suvarṇa of sixteen Māshās; with the Pala of four or five Suvar-<BR>ṇas; and with the larger Pala or Dināra, which is sometimes<BR>reckoned at 108, and other times at 150 Suvarṇas.<BR>	 2. Gold in<BR>general.<BR>	 3. Any ornament of the breast.<BR>	 4. An ornament of the<BR>neck.<BR>	 5. A weight of four Māshās.<BR>	 6. A weight of silver of four<BR>Suvarṇas.<BR>	 7. A value of sixteen Kāhons or Dramyas.<BR>	 8. A chan-<BR>dāla.<BR> E. नि before, सद् to go, Unādi aff. कन्, and the radical final<BR>rejected or निस् + कै-क or निष्क-अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=402-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कण्टक|निष्कंटक|निष्कण्टकः
निष्कण्टक mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>	 1. Without thorns.<BR>	 2. Free from trouble. E.<BR>निर् neg. कण्टक a thorn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=402-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कण्ठ|निष्कण्ठः
निष्कण्ठ m. (-ण्ठः) A plant, (Capparis trifoliata) &c.; see वरुणा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=402-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कर्म्मन्|निष्कर्मन्
निष्कर्म्मन् mfn. (-र्म्मा-र्म्मा-र्म्म) Exempt from or neglecting religious rites,<BR>worldly acts, &c.<BR> E. निर् neg. कर्म्मन् act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=402-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्करुण
निष्करुण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Cruel unpitying, unmerciful.<BR> E. निर् neg.<BR>करुण compassionate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=402-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कल|निष्कलं|निष्कलः
निष्कल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>	 1. Waned, diminished.<BR>	 2. Impotent, seedless,<BR>barren.<BR>	 m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. Pudendum muliebre.<BR>	 2. A name of BRAMHĀ.<BR>3. A fancied personification of BRAMHĀ, for religious cere monies.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=402-b" target="_blank">Page402-b+ 60</a>]<BR>f. (-ला or -ली) A woman past child bearing, in whom menstruation<BR>has ceased.<BR> E. निर् gone, lost, कल a part &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=402-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कर्ष|निष्कर्षः
निष्कर्ष m. (-र्षः)<BR>	 1. Certainty, ascertainment.<BR>	 2. Drawing out.<BR>	 3. The<BR>chief point.<BR>	 4. Measuring.<BR> E. निर् before, कृष् to plough, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=402-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्काम
निष्काम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं) Free from wish or desire.<BR>	 n. adv. (-मं) Un-<BR>willingly.<BR> E. निर् neg. काम desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=402-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कारण|निष्कारणं
निष्कारण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Causeless, groundless.<BR> E. निर् neg. कारण<BR>cause.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=402-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कारुष
निष्कारुष mfn. (-षः-षा-षं) Of a noble, not degraded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=402-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कालक|निष्कालकः
निष्कालक m. (-कः) A penitent, shaved and smeared with Ghee.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=402-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्काश|निष्काशः
निष्काश(स) m. (-शः or सः)<BR>	 1. A portico, a vārāndā.<BR>	 2. Exit, egress.<BR>	 3.<BR>Day break.<BR> E. निर् and कश् to go, भावे घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=402-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्काशित|निष्काशितः
निष्काशित mfn. (-तः -ता -तं)<BR>	 1. Expelled: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=402-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कासित|निष्कासितः
निष्कासित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Expelled, dismissed, turned out.<BR>	 2. Gone<BR>forth or out, issued.<BR>	 3. Placed, deposited.<BR>	 4. Placed over, appoint-<BR>ed, stationed.<BR>	 5. Reviled, reproached, 6. Opened out, blown,<BR>expanded.<BR> E. निर् out, कस् to go, in the causal form, aff. क्त, र be-<BR>comes ष or Visarga: see निःकासित; also निष्काशित.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=402-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कासिन्
निष्कासिन् mfn. (-सी-सिनी-सि) Who or what expels.<BR>	 f. (-नी) A female<BR>slave not restrained by her master.<BR> E. निर् forth, कस् to go,<BR>causal form, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=402-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कुट|निष्कुटः
निष्कुट m. (-टः)<BR>	 1. A pleasure grove near a house.<BR>	 2. A field.<BR>	 3. A door.<BR>4. The private apartments, the Zenana.<BR>	 5. The harem of a king.<BR>E. निर् without, कुट the house.<BR>	 f. (-टा, also -टिः or -टी) Large carda-<BR>moms.<BR> E. निर् out, कुट the shell or husk, aff. क, with टाप् fem.<BR>aff. or कि with ङीष् optionally added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=402-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कुम्भ|निष्कुम्भः
निष्कुम्भ m. (-म्भः) A plant, commonly Danti.<BR> E. निर् forth, ष्कुम्भ a<BR>Sautra root, to spread, aff. अच्; also निःकुम्भ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=402-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कुषित
निष्कुषित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Expelled, extracted, forced or drawn out. E.<BR>निर् neg. कुष् to extract, aff. निष्कर्षे-क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=402-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कुह|निष्कुहः
निष्कुह m. (-हः) The hollow of a tree.<BR> E. निर् affirmative prefix, कुह्<BR>to astonish, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=402-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कृत
निष्कृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Regardless, negligent.<BR>	 2. Disregarded,<BR>thought nothing of.<BR>	 3. Pardoned.<BR>	 4. Undone.<BR> E. निर् neg. कृत<BR>made.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=402-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कृति|निष्कृतिः
निष्कृति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Pardon, absolution.<BR>	 2. Expiration.<BR>	 3. Escaping<BR>from, avoiding the consequence of anything.<BR>	 4. Undoing, doing<BR>away.<BR>	 5. Disregarding, neglecting.<BR>	 6. Acquittance, compensation,<BR>discharge of a debt or obligation.<BR> E. निर् neg. कृ to do, क्तिन् affix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=402-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कोषन
निष्कोषन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Taking away.<BR>	 2. Extracting, extirpating.<BR>	 3. Hus-<BR>king, shelling.<BR> E. निर् before, कुष् to expel, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=402-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कोषितव्य
निष्कोषितव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं) To be taken away.<BR> E. निर् out, कुष् to<BR>expel, तव्य aff.; also निष्कोषणीय ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=402-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्क्रम|निष्क्रमः
निष्क्रम m. (-मः)<BR>	 1. Any intellectual faculty, as attention, comprehen-<BR>sion, &c.<BR>	 2. Degradation, baseness, inferiority of tribe, family, &c.<BR>3. Going out, exit.<BR>	 4. Intellectual faculty.<BR> E. निर् assuredly or<BR>forth, and क्रम going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=402-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्क्रमण|निष्क्रमणं
निष्क्रमण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Going forth or out.<BR>	 2. Taking a child for the<BR>first time out of the house, in the fourth month, considered as<BR>an essential ceremony, and accompanied by sacrifice, &c. E.<BR>निर् forth, क्रम to go, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=402-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्क्रम्य
निष्क्रम्य ind. Going forth,<BR> E. निर्, क्रम् to go, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=402-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्क्रय|निष्क्रयः
निष्क्रय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. Hire, wages.<BR>	 2. Reward.<BR>	 3. Barter.<BR>	 4. Price.<BR>	 5. Ran-<BR>som.<BR> E. निर् before, क्री to buy, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=402-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्क्रान्त|निष्क्रान्तः
निष्क्रान्त mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं) Gone out, gone, departed.<BR> E. निर् out, क्रम्<BR>to go, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=402-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्क्रिय|निष्क्रियं
निष्क्रिय mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>	 1. Abstaining from ceremonial rites.<BR>	 2. Idle,<BR>unoccupied.<BR>	 n. (-यं) BRAMHĀ or the Supreme Spirit.<BR> E. निर neg.<BR>क्रिया act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=402-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्क्वाथ|निष्क्वाथः
निष्क्वाथ m. (-थः) Broth, soup.<BR> E. निर् before, क्वथ् to decoct, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=402-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्ट्य|निष्ट्यः
निष्ट्य m. (-ष्ट्यः) A man of one of the outcast or barbarous tribes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=403-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्टप्त
निष्टप्त mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं)<BR>	 1. Well done, dressed or cooked.<BR>	 2. Burnished,<BR>made bright.<BR> E. निर्, and तप्त heated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=403-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्ठ|निष्ठः
निष्ठ mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठा-ष्ठं)<BR>	 1. Staying, being in, who or what stays or is<BR>in or on anything.<BR>	 2. Believing, faithful.<BR>	 3. Skilled in.<BR>4. Devoted to.<BR>	 f. (-ष्ठा)<BR>	 1. The catastrophe of a drama,<BR>the conclusion of a fable.<BR>	 2. Conclusion in general,<BR>end, termination.<BR>	 3. Disappearance, loss, destruction.<BR>	 4.<BR>Confirmation, completion.<BR>	 5. Asking, begging.<BR>	 6. Ordinary<BR>and uniform practice or profession.<BR>	 7. Good conduct, excellence.<BR>8. Religious practice, devout and austere exercise.<BR>	 9. Faith,<BR>belief.<BR>	 10. Condition, state.<BR>	 11. Fixed time of life, &c.<BR>	 12.<BR>Trouble, distress, anxiety.<BR>	 13. The technical term for the past<BR>participial affixes क्त and क्तवतु.<BR> E. नि completely, assuredly, स्था to<BR>stay or stop, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=403-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्ठान|निष्ठानं
निष्ठान n. (-नं) Sauce, condiment.<BR> E. नि before, स्या to stay, aff ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=403-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्ठित|निष्ठितं
निष्ठित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Firm, fixed.<BR>	 2. Certain, ascertained.<BR>	 3. En-<BR>gaged in, attached to, devoted to.<BR>	 4. Staying, being in or on. E.<BR>नि before, स्था to stay, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=403-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्ठिव
निष्ठिव m. (-वः) Spitting; see निष्ठेव.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=403-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्ठीवन|निष्ठीवनं
निष्ठीवन n. (-नं) Spitting, spitting out, ejecting any thing from the<BR>mouth.<BR> E. नि before, ष्ठिव to object, aff. ल्युट्; also निष्ठेवन and<BR>निष्ठीव ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=403-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्ठुर|निष्ठुरं
निष्ठुर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>	 1. Harsh, contumelious (as speech.)<BR>	 2. Hard,<BR>solid.<BR>	 3. Cruel.<BR>	 4. Severe.<BR> E. नि before, स्था to be, to be firm, aff.<BR>उरच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=403-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्ठुरता
निष्ठुरता f. (-ता) Harshness of speech, reviling, abuse.<BR> E. निष्ठुर, and तल्<BR>aff., also with त्व, निष्ठुरत्व.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=403-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्ठ्यूत|निष्ठ्यूतं
निष्ठ्यूत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Cast, thrown, sent, directed, despatched.<BR>	 2.<BR>Ejected from the mouth, spit.<BR> E. नि before, ष्ठिव् to eject, aff. क्त,<BR>deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=403-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्ठ्यूति|निष्ठ्यूतिः
निष्ठ्यूति f. (-तिः) Spitting, spitting out.<BR> E. नि before, ष्थिव् to eject from<BR>the mouth, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=403-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्ठेव|निष्ठेवं|निष्ठेवः
निष्ठेव subst.<BR>	 mfn. (-वः-वा-वं) Spitting, spitting out, ejecting any thing<BR>from the mouth.<BR> E. नि before, ष्ठिव् to eject, aff. घञ्; also निष्ठीव.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=403-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्ठेवन|निष्ठेवनं
निष्ठेवन n. (-नं) Spitting. E. See the last; also निष्ठीव.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=403-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्ण
निष्ण mfn. (-ष्णः-ष्णा-ष्णं) Skilful, &c. see the next.<BR> E. नि + स्ना + क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=403-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्णात|निष्णातः
निष्णात mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Skiful, clever, conversant, learned.<BR>	 2. Perfect,<BR>superior, supreme.<BR>	 3. (In law,) Agreed upon.<BR> E. नि before, स्ना to<BR>bathe, aff. कर्त्तरि-क्त; also with ड, निष्ण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=403-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्पक्क
निष्पक्क mfn. (-क्वः-क्वा-क्वं) Decocted, infused, boiled.<BR> E. निर् before, पक्व<BR>ripe or cooked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=403-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्पङ्क|निष्पंक
निष्पङ्क mfn. (-ङ्कः-ङ्का-ङ्कं) Pure, free from mud or filth.<BR> E. निर् neg. पङ्क<BR>mud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=403-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्पतत्
निष्पतत् mfn. (-तन्-तन्ती-तत्) Issuing, going forth or out.<BR> E. निर् before,<BR>पत् to go, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=403-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्पतन|निष्पतनं
निष्पतन n. (-नं) Going forth or out, issuing.<BR> E. निर्, and पतन going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=403-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्पत्ति|निष्पत्तिः
निष्पत्ति f. (-त्तिः)<BR>	 1. Completion, conclusion, termination, consumma-<BR>tion.<BR>	 2. Birth, production.<BR>	 3. Going forth or out.<BR> E. निर् negative,<BR>पद् to go, aff. क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=403-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्पत्राकृति|निष्पत्राकृतिः
निष्पत्राकृति f. (-तिः) Excessive bodily pain.<BR> E. निष्पत्र + डाच् + क-भावे क्तिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=403-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्पन्द|निष्पंद|निष्पन्दः
निष्पन्द mfn. (-न्दः-न्दा-न्दं) Motionless.<BR> E. निर् not, स्पदि to shake or move,<BR>aff: अच्; also निष्पन्न.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=403-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्पन्न|निष्पन्नः
निष्पन्न mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>	 1. Done, finished, concluded, completed.<BR>	 2.<BR>Born, produced.<BR>	 3. Motionless.<BR>	 4. Gone forth or out of.<BR> E. निर्<BR>affirmation or negation, and पन्न gone, from पद् to go, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=403-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्पराक्रम
निष्पराक्रम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं) Weak, destitute of power.<BR> E. निर् neg.<BR>पराक्रम valour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=403-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्परिग्रह|निष्परिग्रहः
निष्परिग्रह m. (-हः) An ascetic, one who has no family nor dependants.<BR>E. निर् neg. परिग्रह dependants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=403-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्पादन|निष्पादनं
निष्पादन nf. (-नं-ना)<BR>	 1. Doing, effecting, accomplishing.<BR>	 2. Concluding.<BR>3. Producing, causing, engendering.<BR> E. निर् forth, पद् to go,<BR>causal form, aff. युच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=403-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्पादित|निष्पादितं
निष्पादित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Done, effected, made, produced.<BR> E. निर् forth,<BR>पद् to go, causal form, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=403-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्पाद्य|निष्पाद्यं
निष्पाद्य mfn. (-द्यः-द्या-द्यं) To be done, to be effected or accomplished.<BR>E. निर forth, पद् to go, causal form यत् aff.; also निष्पादनीय<BR>and निष्पादयितव्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=403-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्पाद्यमान
निष्पाद्यमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Being done or made, in the course of com-<BR>pletion.<BR> E. निर् before, पद् to go, causal form, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=403-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्पान
निष्पान n. (-नं) Drinking.<BR> E. निर् before, पान drinking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=403-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्पाव|निष्पावः
निष्पाव mfn. (-वः-वा-वं) Certain, indubitable.<BR>	 m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. Winnowing,<BR>cleaning corn, &c.<BR>	 2. Wind, air.<BR>	 3. The wind of the winnowing<BR>sieve or basket.<BR>	 4. Straw, chaff.<BR>	 5. A legume, a pod.<BR>	 6. A sort<BR>of pulse, (Phaseolus radiatus.)<BR> E. निर् before, पू to purify,<BR>aff. करणे घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=403-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्पिष्ट|निष्पिष्टः
निष्पिष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>	 1. Ground, reduced to dust or powder.<BR>	 2.<BR>Beaten, oppressed.<BR> E. निर्, and पिष्ट ground.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=403-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्पुत्त्र
निष्पुत्त्र mfn. (-त्त्रः-त्त्रा-त्त्रं) Sonless,<BR> E. निर्, and पुत्त्र a son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=403-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्पुरुष|निष्पुरुषः
निष्पुरुष mfn. (-षः-षा-षं) Feminine, neuter, not male.<BR>	 m. (-षः)<BR>	 1. a<BR>eunuch or impotent man.<BR>	 2. A coward.<BR> E. निर् neg. पुरुष a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=403-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्प्रतिभ|निष्प्रतिभः
निष्प्रतिभ mfn. (-भः-भा-भं) Stupid, frigid, dull, apathetic, ignorant.<BR>E. निर् privative, प्रतिभ brilliance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=403-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्प्रत्यूह|निष्प्रत्यूहः
निष्प्रत्यूह mfn. (-हः-हा-हं) Unobstructed, unimpeded.<BR>	 n. adv. (-हं)<BR>Freely, without hindrance.<BR> E. निर् neg. प्रत्यूह obstacle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=403-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्प्रभ|निष्प्रभः
निष्प्रभ mfn. (-भः-भा-भं) Gloomy, dark, obscure.<BR> E. निर privative, and<BR>प्रभा light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=403-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्प्रयोजन|निष्प्रयोजनं
निष्प्रयोजन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Causeless, groundless.<BR> E. निर् negative,<BR>प्रयोजन, motive, cause.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=403-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्पृह
निष्पृह mfn. (-हृः-हा-हं) Content, not envying any person, nor covet-<BR>ing any thing.<BR>	 f. (-हा) A plant; also अमूला and विष्णुवल्लभा.<BR> E. निर्<BR>not, स्पृहा envy, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=403-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्प्रवाण|निष्प्रवाणं
निष्प्रवाण(णि) mfn. subst. (-णः-णी-णं) New and unbleached cloth.<BR> E. निर्<BR>gone, प्रवाणी here said to mean the weaver's brush; also निष्प्रवाणि<BR>mfn. (-णिः-णिः-णि) the forms are irregular.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=403-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्फल|निष्फलः
निष्फल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>	 1. Barren, unfruitful.<BR>	 2. Seedless, impotent.<BR>	 f.<BR>(-ला or -ली) A woman past child-bearing: one in whom menstrua-<BR>tion has ceased: see निष्कल.<BR> E. निर् priv. and फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=403-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निसम्प्रात
निसम्प्रात m. (-तः) Midnight; also निःसम्पात.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=403-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निसर्ग|निसर्गः
निसर्ग m. (-र्गः)<BR>	 1. The natural state, nature, peculiar character or<BR>condition.<BR>	 2. Form.<BR>	 3. Creation.<BR>	 4. Relinquishment, abandon-<BR>ing.<BR>	 5. Transfer, barter.<BR>	 6. Voiding excrement.<BR> E. नि before, सृज्<BR>to create, or to abandon, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=403-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निसर्गज
निसर्गज mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>	 1. Cognate, innate.<BR>	 2. Produced at crea-<BR>tion.<BR> E. निसर्ग, and ज produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=403-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निसिन्धु|निसिन्धुः
निसिन्धु m. (-न्धुः) A shrub, (Vitex negundo:) it is also read निसिन्ध,<BR>and with कन् added निसुन्धक; the words are considered as barbar-<BR>ous: see सिन्धुवार ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=403-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निसूदन|निसूदनं
निसूदन n. (-नं) Killing, slaughter.<BR> E. नि before, सूद् to kill, aff. भावे<BR>ल्युट्ः also निषूदन ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=403-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निसृता
निसृता f. (-ता) A plant commonly Teori.<BR> E. नि + सृ-क्त स्त्रियां-आप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=403-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निसृष्ट|निसृष्टं
निसृष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>	 1. Delivered, deposited.<BR>	 2. Centrical, middle.<BR>3. Permitted.<BR>	 4. Abandoned.<BR> E. नि before, सृज् to go, aff कर्मणि-क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=403-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निसृष्टार्थ|निसृष्टार्थः
निसृष्टार्थ m. (-र्थः) A messenger, an envoy, an ambassador: one who<BR>decides upon his own discretion, knowing the intents of both<BR>parties.<BR> E. निषृष्ट deposited, अर्थ meaning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=403-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्तनी
निस्तनी f. (-नी) A pill, a bolus, a sort of force-meat ball.<BR> E. नि before,<BR>स्तन a breast, ङीप् diminutive aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=403-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्तरण|निस्तरणं
निस्तरण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Going out or forth.<BR>	 2. Crossing over or pass-<BR>ing.<BR>	 3. Extraction, getting rid of or free from.<BR>	 4. Means of suc-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=404-a" target="_blank">Page404-a+ 60</a>]<BR>cess, an expedient, a plan,<BR> E. निर् before, तॄ to cross or pass over,<BR>aff. करणे ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=403-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्तब्ध
निस्तब्ध mfn. (-ब्धः-ब्धा-ब्धं)<BR>	 1. Paralysed, numbered.<BR>	 2. Stopped, fixed.<BR>E. नि before, स्तम्भ् to stop, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=404-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्तर्हण|निस्तर्हणं
निस्तर्हण n. (-णं) Killing, slaughter.<BR> E. निर् before, तृहू to kill or<BR>hurt, aff. भावे ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=404-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्तल|निस्तलं
निस्तल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>	 1. Round, globular.<BR>	 2. Trembling, shaking,<BR>moving.<BR>	 3. Down, below.<BR> E. निर् negative or affirmative, and<BR>तल a support or stay; or depth, bottom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=404-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्तार|निस्तारः
निस्तार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Getting over or across.<BR>	 2. Getting rid of, or away<BR>from, extraction, escape.<BR>	 3. Acquittance, requital.<BR>	 4. Means,<BR>expedient.<BR>	 5. Final liberation.<BR> E. निर्, and तॄ to cross, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=404-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्तारवीज
निस्तारवीज n. (-ञः) The cause of final liberation, faith in any deity.<BR>&c.<BR> E. निस्तार, and वीज seed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=404-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्तितीर्षत्
निस्तितीर्षत् mfn. (-र्षन्-र्षन्ती-र्षत्)<BR>	 1. Desirous or anxious to cross.<BR>	 2. Wishing<BR>for salvation, or to traverse the world.<BR> E. निर् before, तॄ to cross,<BR>desid. form, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=404-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्तुष
निस्तुष mfn. (-षः-षा-षं) Freed from the chaff, (corn, &c.)<BR> E. निर् neg.<BR>तुष chaff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=404-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्तुषक्षीर|निस्तुषक्षीरः
निस्तुषक्षीर m. (-रः) Wheat.<BR> E. निस्तुष, and क्षीर milk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=404-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्तुषरत्न|निस्तुषरत्नं
निस्तुषरत्न n. (-त्नं) Crystal.<BR> E. निस्तुष, and रत्न a gem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=404-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्तुषित|निस्तुषितं
निस्तुषित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Left abandoned, deserted.<BR>	 2. Skinned, peeled.<BR>3. Pared, made thin.<BR> E. निर् before, तुष् husk or skin, converted<BR>in to a nominal verb, and क्त participial aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=404-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्तेजस्
निस्तेजस् mfn. (-जाः-जाः-जः)<BR>	 1. Dull, obscure.<BR>	 2. Dull, spiritless.<BR>3. Powerless, impotent,<BR> E. निर् neg. तेजस् light, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=404-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्त्रंश
निस्त्रंश mfn. (-शः-शा-शं) Fearless, unapprehensive.<BR> E. निर् neg. त्रशि<BR>to fear, aff अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=404-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्त्रिंश|निस्त्रिंशः
निस्त्रिंश mfn. (-शः-शा-शं) Merciless, unfeeling, unpitying.<BR>	 m. (-शः) A<BR>scimitar, a sacrificial knife.<BR> E. निर् forth, त्रिंशत् thirty, ड aff; being<BR>of thirty finger's length, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=404-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्त्रिंशधारिन्
निस्त्रिंशधारिन् m. (-री) A soldier armed with a sword.<BR> E. निस्त्रिंश, and<BR>धारिन् who bears.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=404-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्त्रैगुण्य
निस्त्रैगुण्य mfn. (-ण्यः-ण्या-ण्यं) Destitute of the qualities, truth, passion,<BR>and darkness.<BR> E. निर् neg. त्रैगुण्य three qualities.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=404-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्नाव|निस्नावः
निस्नाव m. (-वः) The remainder of articles, &c. after a sale or market.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=404-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्पन्द|निस्पंद|निस्पन्दः
निस्पन्द mfn. (-न्दः-न्दा-न्दं) Still, steady, immoveable.<BR>	 m. (-न्दः) Thro-<BR>bbing, trembling.<BR> E. नि before, स्पद् to go, aff घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=404-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्पृह
निस्पृह mfn. (-हः-हा-हं) Content, unenvious.<BR>	 f. (-हा)<BR>	 1. A plant.<BR>(Gloriosa superba.)<BR>	 2. Contentment.<BR> E. नि neg. स्पृहा desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=404-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्यन्द|निस्यंदः|निस्यन्दः
निस्यन्द m. (-न्दः) Trickling, oozing, issuing.<BR> E. नि before, स्यन्द to ooze,<BR>aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=404-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्राव|निस्रावः
निस्राव m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. The scum of boiled rice.<BR>	 2. A torrent.<BR> E. नि before,<BR>स्रु to ooze or drop, aff घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=404-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्वन|निस्वनः
निस्वन m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. Sound.<BR>	 2. Silence,<BR> E. नि before, स्वन् to sound, aff. अप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=404-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्वान|निस्वानः
निस्वान m. (-नः) Sound.<BR> E. नि before, स्वन with घञ् aff.: see to last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=404-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निहत
निहत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Killed, slain.<BR> E. नि affir. हत killing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=404-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निहनन|निहननं
निहनन n. (-नं) Killing, slaughter,<BR> E. नि before, हन to kill, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=404-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निहन्तृ|निहंतृ
निहन्तृ mfn. (-न्ता-न्त्री-न्तृ) Murderous, who or what kills.<BR> E. नि before, हन्<BR>to kill, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=404-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निहन्यमान
निहन्यमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Killed.<BR> E. नि, हन to kill, pass. v. शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=404-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निहव|निहवः
निहव m. (-वः) Calling, calling to.<BR> E. नि before, ह्वे to call, अप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=404-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निहाका
निहाका f. (-का) An iguana or the Gangetic alligator.<BR> E. नि before, हा<BR>to quit, Unādi aff. कन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=404-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निह्यर
निह्यर m. (-रः) Frost, dew: see नीहार.<BR> E. नि + हृ + कर्मणि घञ् वा दीर्घः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=404-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निहिंसन|निहिंसनं
निहिंसन n. (-नं) Killing, slaughter.<BR> E. नि before, हिंस् to kill or hurt,<BR>aff. भावे ल्युट्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=404-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निहित|निहितं
निहित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Deposited, delivered, given, entrusted.<BR>	 2.<BR>Applied to, bestowed upon.<BR>	 3. Laid, (as dust by rain.)<BR> E. नि before,<BR>धा to have, aff. क्त; हिरादेशः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=404-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निहीन|निहीनः
निहीन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) A low man, an outcast.<BR> E. नि before, हीन<BR>abandoned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=404-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निह्नव|निह्नवः
निह्नव m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. Denial or concealment of knowledge, dissimulation,<BR>secrecy.<BR>	 2. Concealment in general.<BR>	 3. Mistrust, doubt, suspicion.<BR>4. Wickedness.<BR>	 5. A secret.<BR>	 6. Excuse.<BR> E. नि before, ह्नु to hide<BR>or secrete aff. अप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=404-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निह्नववादिन्
निह्नववादिन् m. (-दी) A defendant or witness who prevaricates or<BR>tries to hide the truth.<BR> E. निह्नव and वादिन् who speaks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=404-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निह्नवोत्तर
निह्नवोत्तर n. (-रं) An evasive reply or defence.<BR> E. निह्नव, and उत्तर<BR>answer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=404-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निह्नुत
निह्नुत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Concealed, secreted.<BR>	 2. Denied, evaded. E.<BR>नि before, ह्नु to secrete aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=404-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निह्नुति|निह्नुतिः
निह्नुति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Denial or concealment of knowledge, dissimulation,<BR>reserve, secrecy.<BR>	 2. Hiding, concealment.<BR> E. नि before, ह्नु to sec-<BR>rete aff. क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=404-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निह्नुवान
निह्नुवान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Insinuating, using double entendre.<BR> E. नि be-<BR>fore, ह्नु to secrete शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=404-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निह्नाद
निह्नाद m. (-दः) Sound.<BR> E. नि before, ह्रद् to sound aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=404-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निह्नादवत्
निह्नादवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती वत्) Sounding, making a noise.<BR> E. निह्राद and<BR>मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=404-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीक|नीकः
नीक m. (-कः) The name of a tree.<BR> E. नी to gain, Unādi aff. कक् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=404-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नी
नी(नि)कार m. (-रः) Disrespect, contempt, vilifying, degrading.<BR> E. नि<BR>before, कृ to make, aff. भावे घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=404-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नी
नी(नि)काश mfn. (-शः-शा-शं) (In composition) Like, resembling.<BR>	 m. (-शः)<BR>Certainty, ascertainment.<BR> E. नि before, काश् to shine, aff. घञ्<BR>and the vowel made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=404-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीच|नीचः
नीच mfn. (-चः-चा-चं)<BR>	 1. Low (in stature) short, dwarfish.<BR>	 2. Low,<BR>(in condition) vile, base, mean.<BR>	 3. Deep.<BR> E. न privative, ई good<BR>fortune, चि to obtain, aff. ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=404-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीचक|नीचकः
नीचक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Low, dwarfish, a dwarf.<BR>	 2. Vile, low.<BR>	 f. (-का)<BR>An excellent cow.<BR> E. कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=404-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीचकिन्
नीचकिन् m. (-की)<BR>	 1. The head or top of any thing.<BR>	 2. The owner of a<BR>good cow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=404-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीचकैस्
नीचकैस् ind. Low, below, little, vile, &c.<BR> E. नीचैस् low, अकच् inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=404-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीचग|नीचगं
नीचग mfn. (-गः-गा-गं) Low, vile, base.<BR>	 n. (-गं) Water.<BR>	 f. (-गा) A river.<BR>E. नीच low or deep, and ग who is going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=404-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीचभोज्य|नीचभोज्यः
नीचभोज्य m. (-ज्यः) An onion.<BR> E. नीच a low man, and भोज्य food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=404-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीचिका
नीचिका f. (-का) A good cow; also नीचिकी and नैचिकी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=404-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीचैस्
नीचैस् ind. Little, small, low.<BR> E. नि before, चि to collect, डैसि aff. and<BR>the vowel of नि made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=404-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीड|नीडं|नीडः
नीड mn. (-डः-डं)<BR>	 1. Nest 2. A place, a spot.<BR> E. नि before, इङ् to go,<BR>aff. घञ् or नि + इल-क, डस्य-लः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=404-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीडज|नीडजः
नीडज m. (-जः) A bird in general.<BR> E. नीड a nest, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=404-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीडोद्भव|नीडोद्भवः
नीडोद्भव m. (-वः) A bird.<BR> E. नीड a nest, and उद्भव born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=404-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीत|नीतं
नीत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Well behaved, correct, modest.<BR>	 2. Gained, ob-<BR>tained.<BR>	 3. Led, conducted.<BR>	 n. (-तं)<BR>	 1. Wealth.<BR>	 2. Corn, grain. E.<BR>नी to get &c. aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=404-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीति|नीतिः
नीति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Guiding, directing.<BR>	 2. Obtaining, acquirement, acquisi-<BR>tion.<BR>	 3. Polity, political science, treating especially of the ad-<BR>ministrating of government, including the practice of morality<BR>in private life, both by the sovereign and his subjects.<BR> E. नी<BR>to guide or gain, aff. क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=404-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीतिकथा
नीतिकथा f. (-था) Any work on polity or good government.<BR> E. नीति<BR>and कथा a tale.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=404-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीतिकुशल
नीतिकुशल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Politic, conversant with government and<BR>human affairs.<BR> E. नीति and कुशल able.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=404-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीतिघोष|नीतिघोषः
नीतिघोष m. (-षः) The car of VṚHASPATI.<BR> E. नीति guiding, and घोष sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=404-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीतिज्ञ
नीतिज्ञ mfn. (-ज्ञः-ज्ञा-ज्ञं) Knowing what is right especially in govern-<BR>ment, sagacious, politic.<BR>	 m. (-ज्ञः) A statesman, a politician.<BR> E. नीति<BR>and ज्ञ who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=404-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीतिमत्|नीतिमन्त्
नीतिमत् mfn. (-मान्-मती-मत्) Moral eminent for royal duties.<BR> E. नीति,<BR>and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=405-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीतिविद्या
नीतिविद्या f. (-द्या) Political science.<BR> E. नीति, and विद्या knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=405-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीतिशास्त्र
नीतिशास्त्र n. (-स्त्रं) The science of political ethics, or any work treat-<BR>ing of it.<BR> E. नीति, and शास्त्र a scripture. शिष्यते अनेन शास-त्रल् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=405-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीत्त
नीत्त mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं) Given, given away.<BR> E. नि before, दत्त given,<BR>form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=405-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीत्वा
नीत्वा ind.<BR>	 1. Having taken.<BR>	 2. Having passed or spent.<BR> E. णी to take,<BR>क्ता aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=405-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीथ|नीथः
नीथ m. (थः) A guider, a leader.<BR>	 n. (-थं) Water.<BR> E. नी to guide, क्थन्<BR>Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=405-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीध्र|नीध्रं
नीध्र(व्र) n. (-ध्रं-व्रं)<BR>	 1. The edge of a thatch or roof.<BR>	 2. A wood.<BR>	 3. The<BR>circumference of a wheel.<BR>	 4. The moon.<BR>	 5. The constellation<BR>Revatī.<BR> E. नि before, धृ to fall, &c. aff. क, and the vowel of the<BR>prefix made long: this is considered as a various reading also of<BR>नीव्र q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=405-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीप|नीपः
नीप m. (-पः)<BR>	 1. The Kadamba tree, (Nauclea Kadamba.)<BR>	 2. A spe-<BR>cies of Ixora, (I. bandhuca, Rox.)<BR>	 3. A sort of Aśoca or Nil<BR>Aśoka.<BR>	 4. The foot of a mountain.<BR> E. नी to obtain, (pleasure.) and<BR>प Uṇadi aff.; किच्च ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=405-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीयमान|नीयमानं
नीयमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>	 1. Being sought or obtained.<BR>	 2. Being taken<BR>away,<BR> E. नी to obtain, शानच् aff. यक् inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=405-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीर|नीरं
नीर n. (-रं)<BR>	 1. Water.<BR>	 2. Juice, liquor.<BR> E. नी to obtain, aff. रक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=405-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीरक्त
नीरक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं) Colourless, faded, having the colour taken<BR>out.<BR> E. निर् neg. रक्त red or dyed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=405-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीरज|नीरजं|नीरजः
नीरज mfn. (-जः-जा-जं) Aquatic.<BR>	 n. (-जं)<BR>	 1. A sort of Costus, (C. spe-<BR>ciosus.)<BR>	 2. A. lotus in general.<BR>	 m. (-जः) An otter.<BR> E. नीर water,<BR>and ज born, or produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=405-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीरजस्
नीरजस् mfn. (-जाः-जाः-जः)<BR>	 1. Free from dust.<BR>	 2. Having no pollen,<BR>(as a flower.)<BR>	 f. (-जाः) A woman not menstruating.<BR> E. निर् neg.<BR>रजस् dust &c. and इ made long before र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=405-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीरजीकारित
नीरजीकारित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Cleansed, made free from dust.<BR> E. नीरजस्<BR>and कारित caused, च्वि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=405-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीरत|नीरतः
नीरत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Indifferent, not taking pleasure in.<BR>	 2. Stop-<BR>ped, in stating.<BR> E. नि neg. or affir. रत engaged in, इ made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=405-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीरद|नीरदः
नीरद mfn. (-दः-दा-दं) Toothless.<BR>	 m. (-दः) A cloud.<BR> E. नीर water,<BR>द what gives, or नि neg. रद a tooth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=405-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीरदिन्
नीरदिन् mfn. (-दी-दिनी-दि) Cloudy.<BR> E. नीरद, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=405-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीरधि|नीरधिः
नीरधि m. (-धिः) The ocean.<BR> E. नीर water, and धि having.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=405-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीरनिधि|नीरनिधिः
नीरनिधि m. (-धिः) The ocean.<BR> E. नीर water, and निधि receptacle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=405-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीरन्ध्र|नीरंध्र|नीरन्ध्रं
नीरन्ध्र mfn. (-न्ध्र-न्ध्रा-न्ध्रं)<BR>	 1. Coarse, thick, gross, without interstices.<BR>2. Entire, having no holes, imperforate.<BR> E. नी for निर् negative<BR>prefix, रन्ध्र a hole.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=405-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीरस|नीरसः
नीरस mfn. (-सः-सा-सं) Dry, withered, insipid, devoid of taste, &c.<BR>morally or physically m. (-सः) The pomegranate.<BR> E. नी for निर<BR>negative or affirmative prefix, and रस juice, flavour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=405-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीराखु|नीराखुः
नीराखु m. (-खुः) An otter.<BR> E. नीर water, and आखु a cat; the water-<BR>cat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=405-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीराजन|नीराजनं
नीराजन nf. (-नं-ना)<BR>	 1. Lustration of arms; military and religious<BR>ceremony held or the 19th of Āshwin, by kings or generals<BR>for purifying the army before taking the field; it is still ob-<BR>served by some Hindu states, under the name of Dashahārā.<BR>	 2.<BR>Waving lights before an idol; but it may also be performed with<BR>a lotus, clean cloth, or the leaves of various sacred plants;<BR>prostration is also considered as the fifth kind of this sort of<BR>adoration.<BR> E. निर् completely, राज to shine, aff युच् or भावे ल्युट्;<BR>रलोपे पूर्वाणो दीर्घः or नीर water, and अजन going, sprinkling the<BR>arms, horses, &c. with water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=405-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीरिन्दु|नीरिन्दुः
नीरिन्दु m. (-न्दुः) A plant, (Trophis aspera.)<BR> E. नीर् water, इन्दु the<BR>moon; or नि + ईर् + क्विप् । (आस्श्याओडा) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=405-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीरुच्
नीरुच् mfn. (-रुक्) Dull, dim, faded.<BR> E. निर् neg. रुच् light, and इ made<BR>long, affix क्विप् । According to Turkabāchaspati:--निश्चितं रोचते<BR>निर + रूच-क्विप् रलोपे दीर्घः । नितान्तदीप्तिशीले ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=405-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीरुज्
नीरुज् mfn. (-रुक्) Convalescent, well, in health.<BR> E. नि private, रुज्<BR>disease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=405-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीरुज|नीरुजं|नीरुजः
नीरुज mfn. (-जः-जा-जं) Convalescent, well.<BR>	 n. (-जं) A sort of Costus,<BR>(C. speciosus.)<BR> E. नि implying opposition, (anti,) and रुज् disease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=405-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीरूप|नीरूपं|नीरूपः
नीरूप mfn. (-पः-पा-पं) Formless, shapeless.<BR>	 n. (पं) Heaven, æther.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-पं)<BR>	 1. Air, wind.<BR>	 2. GOD.<BR> E. निर् neg. रूप form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=405-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नील|नीलं|नीलः
नील mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Blue, dark blue or black.<BR>	 m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. Black or<BR>dark blue, (the colour.)<BR>	 2. The blue mountain, one of the princi-<BR>pal ranges of mountains, dividing the world into nine portions,<BR>and lying immediately north of Ilāvrata or the central division.<BR>3. One of the monkey chiefs.<BR>	 4. One of the Nidhis or divine<BR>treasures of KUVERA.<BR>	 5. A gem, (the sapphire.)<BR>	 6. A name of<BR>the Buddha MANJUGHOSHA.<BR>	 7. The blue or hill Maina, a bird<BR>so called.<BR>	 n. (-लं)<BR>	 1. Indigo, the dye.<BR>	 2. A mark, a characteristic<BR>mark.<BR>	 3. A medical plant, apparently distinct from the Indigo-<BR>fera.<BR>	 4. Blue vitriol.<BR>	 5. Black salt.<BR>	 6. Poison.<BR>	 7. Antimony.<BR>	 f.<BR>(-ला)<BR>	 1. A blue fly.<BR>	 2. A Rāgiṇī or mode of music, personified<BR>as the wife of the Rāga Mallār.<BR>	 f. (-ली)<BR>	 1. The indigo plant,<BR>(Indigofera tinctoria.)<BR>	 3. A complaint of the eyes, a darkening<BR>of the pupil.<BR>	 3. A bruise, a black and blue mark on the skin.<BR>E. नील to dye or tinge, Unādi aff. अच्; or नीली indigo, अन् aff.,<BR>implying being coloured or stained by it.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=405-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीलक|नीलकं|नीलकः
नीलक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. The Nil Gai or slate coloured antilope, (A. picta.)<BR>2. A tree, (Pentaptera tomentosa.)<BR>	 n. (-कं)<BR>	 1. Blue steel.<BR>	 2. Blue<BR>vitriol.<BR>	 3. Black salt.<BR> E. नील, स्वार्थे संज्ञायाम् कन् वा ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=405-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नी
नी(का)लकण्ठ m. (-ण्ठः)<BR>	 1. A name of SĪVA.<BR>	 2. Gallinule.<BR>	 3. A sparrow.<BR>4. A wagtail.<BR>	 5. A peacock.<BR>	 6. Morunga, (Hyperanthera morunga.)<BR>7. A blue necked jay.<BR> E. नील, blue or black, and कण्ठ the throat;<BR>also कालकण्ठ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=405-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीलकण्ठाक्ष|नीलकण्ठाक्षं
नीलकण्ठाक्ष n. (-क्षं) The Elœocarpus seed.<BR> E. नीलकण्ठ SĪVA, and अक्ष<BR>a seed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=405-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीलकमल|नीलकमलं
नीलकमल n. (-लं) The blue lotus.<BR> E. नील, and कमल a lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=405-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीलकुरुण्टक
नीलकुरुण्टक m. (-कः) Blue Barleria, (B. cærulea.)<BR> E. नील, and कुरुण्टक<BR>Barleria.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=405-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीलक्रौञ्च|नीलक्रौञ्चः
नीलक्रौञ्च m. (-ञ्चः) A sort of curlew or heron.<BR> E. नील blue, and क्रीञ्च a<BR>heron, &c. (काचवक) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=405-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीलग्रीव|नीलग्रीवः
नीलग्रीव m. (-वः) A name of MAHĀDEVA.<BR> E. नील blue, and ग्रीवा neck;<BR>the neck of SĪVA was stained blue by the acrimony of the poison,<BR>which, upon its production at the churning of the ocean, he<BR>swallowed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=405-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नील|नीलं|नीलः
नील(ला)ङ्गु m. (-ङ्गुः) An insect in general.<BR>	 2. A sort of worm.<BR>	 3. A Jackal.<BR>E. नि before, लिगि to go, Unādi aff. कु, and the इ of नि made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=405-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीलज|नीलजं
नीलज mfn. (-जः-जा-जं) Produced in the blue mountain, &c.<BR>	 n. (-जं)<BR>Blue steel.<BR> E. नील, and ज produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=405-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीलझिण्टी
नीलझिण्टी f. (-ण्टी) Blue Barleria.<BR> E. नील blue, and झिण्टी Barleria.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=405-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीलपङ्क|नीलपंक|नीलपङ्कं|नीलपङ्कः
नीलपङ्क mn. (-ङ्कः-ङ्कं)<BR>	 1. Darkness.<BR>	 2. Black mud.<BR> E. नील black, and पङ्क<BR>clay or mire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=405-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीलपटल
नीलपटल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Very dark or black.<BR> E. नील, and पटल<BR>abundance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=405-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीलपत्र|नीलपत्रं|नीलपत्रः
नीलपत्र mfn. (-त्रः-त्रा-त्रं) Having black or dark blue leaves.<BR>	 n. (-त्रं) The<BR>blue lotus.<BR> E. नोल blue, and पत्र a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=405-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीलपाचन
नीलपाचन n. (-नं) Steeping or maceration of indigo.<BR> E. नील, and पाचन<BR>cooking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=405-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीलपाचनभाण्ड
नीलपाचनभाण्ड E. (-ण्डं) An indigo vat.<BR> E. नीलपाचन, and भाण्ड a vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=405-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीलपद्म|नीलपद्मं
नीलपद्म n. (-द्मं) The blue lotus, (Nynphæa cærulea.)<BR> E. नील, and पद्म<BR>a lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=405-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीलपिच्छ|नीलपिच्छः
नीलपिच्छ m. (-च्छः) A falcon.<BR> E. नील blue, and पिच्छ a tail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=405-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीलपुष्प|नीलपुष्पं|नीलपुष्पः
नीलपुष्प m. (-ष्पः) A sort of Verbesina with blue flowers.<BR>	 f. (-ष्पी) A<BR>blue species of Rasan.<BR> E. नील blue, and पुष्प a flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=406-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीलपुष्पिका
नीलपुष्पिका f. (-का) The indigo plant.<BR> E. कन् added to नीलपुष्पी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=406-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीलपृष्ठ
नीलपृष्ठ m. (-ष्ठः)<BR>	 1. A sort of fish, commonly called Rohita, (Cyprinus<BR>denticulatus.)<BR>	 2. The fire.<BR> E. नील blue, पृष्ठ the back.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=406-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीलभ|नीलभः
नीलभ m. (-भः)<BR>	 1. The moon.<BR>	 2. A cloud.<BR>	 3. A bee.<BR> E. नील blue, or<BR>black, भा to show, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=406-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीलमणि|नीलमणिः
नीलमणि m. (-णिः)<BR>	 1. A gem of a blue colour, the sapphire.<BR>	 2. An epi-<BR>thet of Krishnā.<BR> E. नील blue, and मणि a jewel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=406-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीलमाधव|नीलमाधवः
नीलमाधव m. (-वः) A name of KṚṢṆA.<BR> E. नील and माधव VIṢṆU,<BR>being of a dark colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=406-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीलमीलिक|नीलमीलिकः
नीलमीलिक m. (-कः) A firefly.<BR> E. नील black or dark blue, मील् to<BR>twinkle, aff. ठक् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=406-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीलमृत्तिका
नीलमृत्तिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. Iron pyrites.<BR>	 2. Black mould.<BR>	 3. Black earth.<BR>E. नील and मृत्तिका earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=406-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीललोह|नीललोहं
नीललोह n. (-हं) Blue steel.<BR> E. नील blue, and लोह iron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=406-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीललोहित|नीललोहितः
नीललोहित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Purple, of a purple colour.<BR>	 m. (-तः)<BR>	 1. A<BR>name of SĪVA.<BR>	 2. A mixture of red and blue, purple.<BR>	 f. (-ता) A<BR>vegetable: see भूमिजम्बू<BR> E. नील blue or black, and लोहित red.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=406-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीलवर्ण
नीलवर्ण mfn. (-र्णः-र्णी-र्णं) Blue, of a blue colour.<BR> E. नील, and वर्ण colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=406-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीलवसन|नीलवसनः
नीलवसन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Wearing dark blue or black garments.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-नः) The planet Saturn.<BR> E. नील dark blue, and वसन vesture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=406-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीलवस्त्र|नीलवस्त्रः
नीलवस्त्र mfn. (-स्त्रः-स्त्रा-स्त्रं) Dressed in dark black vesture.<BR>	 n. (-स्त्रं)<BR>Dark coloured cloth.<BR>	 m. (-स्त्रः) A name of BALARĀMA.<BR> E. नील,<BR>and वस्त्र clothes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=406-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीलवासस्
नीलवासस् mfn. (-साः-साः-सः) Dressed in dark blue clothes.<BR>	 m. (-साः)<BR>A name of Saturn.<BR> E. नील dark blue, वासस् raiment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=406-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीलवृष|नीलवृषः
नीलवृष m. (-षः) A dark coloured bull.<BR> E. नील, and वृष a bull.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=406-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीलाक्ष|नीलाक्षः
नीलाक्ष m. (-क्षः) A goose.<BR> E. नील and अक्ष an eye, having dark blue<BR>eyes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=406-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीलाङ्ग|नीलांग|नीलाङ्गः
नीलाङ्ग mf. (-ङ्गः-ङ्गी)<BR>	 1. The Indian crane, or Sārasa.<BR>	 2. The blue<BR>jay.<BR> E. नील blue, and अङ्ग body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=406-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीला
नीला(ल)ङ्गु m. (-ङ्गुः)<BR>	 1. An insect in general.<BR>	 2. A sort of insect.<BR>	 3. A<BR>Jackal.<BR>	 f. (-ङ्गुः) A gad-fly. E. See नीलङ्गु; the penultimate being<BR>irregularly made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=406-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीलाञ्जन|नीलांजन|नीलाञ्जनं
नीलाञ्जन n. (-नं) Blue vitriol.<BR>	 f. (-ना) Lightning.<BR> E. नील blue, अञ्जन<BR>collyrium, &c. (तुंँते |)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=406-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीलाञ्जसा|नीलांजसा
नीलाञ्जसा f. (-सा)<BR>	 1. One of the Apsarās or courtezans of Svarga.<BR>2. The name of a river.<BR>	 3. Lightning.<BR> E. नील dark, अञ्जस quickly,<BR>affs. अच् and टाप्. अन्जि-णिच्-असच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=406-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीलाम्बर|नीलांबर|नीलाम्बरं|नीलाम्बरः
नीलाम्बर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Dressed in dark blue cloth.<BR>	 m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A<BR>name of BALARĀMA.<BR>	 2. A demon, A goblin.<BR>	 3. A name of SANI<BR>or Saturn.<BR>	 n. (-रं) Black or dark blue raiment.<BR> E. नील, and अम्बर<BR>clothing &c. तालीश पत्रे ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=406-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीलाम्बुजन्मन्|नीलांबुजन्मन्
नीलाम्बुजन्मन् n. (-न्म) The blue lotus.<BR> E. नील, and अम्बुजन्मन् a lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=406-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीलाभ
नीलाभ mfn. (-भः-भा-भं) Blue.<BR>	 m. (-भः) A cloud.<BR> E. नील, and आभ what<BR>shines.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=406-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीलाभ्र|नीलाभ्रः
नीलाभ्र n. (-भ्रं) A dark cloud.<BR> E. नील, and अभ्र cloud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=406-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीलाश्मन्
नीलाश्मन् m. (-श्मा) A blue stone, a sapphire.<BR> E. नील, and अश्मन् a<BR>stone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=406-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीलिका
नीलिका(नी) f. (-का) A plant, (Nyctanthes tristis;) a species with blue<BR>flowers.<BR>	 2. The indigo plant.<BR>	 3. A slight malady; black and<BR>blue marks in the body from bruises, &c. कन् added to नीली.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=406-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीलिनी
नीलिनी f. (-नी)<BR>	 1. Indigo, (Indigofera tinctoria.)<BR>	 2. A black species<BR>of Teori.<BR> E. नील black or dark blue, poss aff. इनि, fem. aff, ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=406-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीलीराग|नीलीरागः
नीलीराग m. (-गः)<BR>	 1. A firm and constant friend.<BR>	 2. Firm, unalterable<BR>attachment, (as that of RĀMA and SĪTĀ.)<BR>	 3. Dark blue.<BR> E. नीली<BR>indigo, and राग colour; as permanent as the dye of indigo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=406-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीलीसन्धान|नीलीसंधान
नीलीसन्धान n. (-नं) Fermentation or maceration of indigo.<BR> E. नीली,<BR>and सन्धान fermentation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=406-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीलीसन्धानभाण्ड|नीलीसंधानभाण्ड
नीलीसन्धानभाण्ड n. (-ण्डं) An indigo vat.<BR> E. नीलीसन्धान, and भाण्ड a vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=406-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीलोत्पल|नीलोत्पलं
नीलोत्पल n. (-लं) A blue lotus. (Nymphæa cærulea.)<BR> E. नील blue,<BR>and उत्पल a lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=406-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीलोत्पलिन्
नीलोत्पलिन् m. (-ली) One of the Jaina saints or teachers. called Manzughosa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=406-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीलोपल|नीलोपलः
नीलोपल n. (-लं) A blue stone, lapis lazuli.<BR> E. नील, and उपल a stone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=406-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीवर|नीवरः
नीवर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Trade, traffic.<BR>	 2. A place, &c. proper for the site<BR>of a habitation.<BR>	 3. A religious mendicant.<BR>	 4. A trader.<BR>	 n. (-रं)<BR>1. Water.<BR>	 2. Mud, mire.<BR> E. णी to obtain, &c. ष्वरच् Uṇadi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=406-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीवाक|नीवाकः
नीवाक m. (-कः) Increased demand for grains in times of dearth,<BR>scarcity.<BR> E. नि before, वच् to speak, aff. घञ्; creating alarm and<BR>causing conversation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=406-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीवार|नीवारः
नीवार m. (-रः) Rice growing wild or without cultivation.<BR> E. नि before,<BR>वृ to be, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=406-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीवि|नीविः
नीवि(वी) f. (-विः-वी)<BR>	 1. Capital, principal, stock.<BR>	 2. Stake, wager.<BR>	 3. A<BR>cloth round a woman's waist, or the ends of the cloth passed<BR>round the loins so as to hold the whole together; on being<BR>loosed the lower members are exposed: the tie of drawers worn<BR>by women, &c.<BR>	 4. The outer tie of a packet, in which the offer-<BR>ings of a Śūdra at funeral obsequies are presented.<BR> E. नि before,<BR>व्येञ् to cover, Unādi aff. इन् and ङीप् optionally added; the इ<BR>of नि is made long, and the radical finals rejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=406-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीव्र|नीव्रं
नीव्र(घ्र) n. (-व्रं-घ्रं)<BR>	 1. The edge of a thatch.<BR>	 2. The circumference of a<BR>wheel.<BR>	 3. A wood.<BR>	 4. The moon.<BR>	 5. The constellation Revatī.<BR>E. नि certainly, वृ to be, aff. क, deriv. irr.; also नीध्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=406-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीवृत्
नीवृत् mfn. (-वृत्) Any inhabited country.<BR> E. नि always, वृत to be, aff.<BR>क्विप्, and the vowel of the prefix made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=406-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीशार|नीशारः
नीशार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A warm cloth, blanket.<BR>	 2. Curtains, musquito-<BR>curtains.<BR>	 3. An outer tent or screen.<BR> E. नि before, शृ to hurt,<BR>&c. aff. घञ्, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=406-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीहार|नीहारः
नीहार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Frost, hoar-frost.<BR>	 2. Heavy dew.<BR>	 3. Evacuation.<BR>E. नि before, हृ to steal or take, aff. कर्मणि घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=406-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नु|नुः
नु ind.<BR>	 1. A particle of interrogation; 2. Of discrimination; 3.<BR>Of reflexion; 4. Of doubt; 5. Of contempt; 6. Of pretence;<BR>7. Of respect; 8. A particle implying cause or motive: (what,<BR>but, how, hum, or either, &c. will in general express it.)<BR> E. णुट्<BR>to go, or णु praise, &c. aff. डु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=406-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नु|नुः
नु m. (-नुः)<BR>	 1. A weapon.<BR>	 2. Time.<BR>	 3. A boat.<BR>	 4. The nasal mark<BR>above the line in neuter nouns, &c.<BR>	 f. (-नुः) Praise, eulogium,<BR>panegyric.<BR> E. णु to praise, &c. aff. क्किप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=406-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नुड
नुड r. 9th cl. (नुडति) To hurt or kill. तु-कु-पर-सक-सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=406-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नुत|नुतं
नुत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Praised, commended.<BR> E. णु to praise, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=406-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नुति|नुतिः
नुति f. (-निः)<BR>	 1. Praise, eulogium, panegyric.<BR>	 2. Worship, reverence.<BR>E. णु to praise, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=406-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नुत्त|नुत्तः
नुत्त mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं) Sent, ordered, despatched.<BR>	 m. (-त्तः) A plant:<BR>see लकुच.<BR> E. णुद to send, aff. क्त; also नुन्न.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=406-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नुनुत्सु
नुनुत्सु mfn. (-त्सुः-त्सुः-त्सु) Desirous of removing.<BR> E. णुद् to send, desid.<BR>v. उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=406-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नुन्न|नुन्नः
नुन्न mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं) Sent, thrown, despatched, cast, dismissed. E.<BR>णुद् to praise, aff. क्त, form irr.; also नुत्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=406-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नूत|नूतः
नूत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. New.<BR>	 2. Praised, eulogized, hymned.<BR> E. णु<BR>to praise, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=406-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नूतन|नूतनः
नूतन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>	 1. New, recent, fresh, young, &c.<BR>	 2. Present.<BR>3. Instantaneous.<BR>	 4. Modern.<BR>	 5. Curious.<BR> E. नव new, नू substituted<BR>for it, and तनप् aff. नुरादेशश्च ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=406-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नूततत्व
नूततत्व n. (-त्वं) Newness, novelty.<BR> E. त्व added to the last; also with<BR>तल्, नूतनता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=406-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नूत्न|नूत्नः
नूत्न mfn. (-त्नः-त्ना-त्नं) New.<BR> E. नू substituted for नव new, त्नप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=406-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नूद|नूदः
नूद m. (-दः) The mulberry tree, (Morus Indica.)<BR> E. णद् to send, क aff.<BR>and the deriv. irr. नुदति पापं; क-पृषो-दीर्घः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=406-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नूनम्
नूनम् ind.<BR>	 1. Certainly, assuredly.<BR>	 2. A particle of doubt or delibera-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=407-a" target="_blank">Page407-a+ 60</a>]<BR>tion.<BR>	 3. A reminiscent particle.<BR>	 4. An expletive.<BR> E. नू a particle,<BR>नम् to bow or bend, aff. विच् deriv. irr. or नु + ऊन-मि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=406-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नूपुर|नूपुरं|नूपुरः
नूपुर mn. (-रः-रं) An ornament for the toes and feet.<BR> E. णु to praise or<BR>be praised, aff. क्विप्; or नू an ornament, पुर् to precede, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=407-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नृ
नृ r. 1st cl. (नरति) 5th cl. (नृणाति) To lead, to conduct, to guide; phy-<BR>sically or morally. भ्वा० प० अक० अनिट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=407-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नृ
नृ n. (-ना)<BR>	 1. Man, individually or collectively, a man, mankind.<BR>	 2. A<BR>piece at chess, &c.<BR>	 3. A gnomon.<BR> E. णी to guide or gain, aff. दृन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=407-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नृकेशरिन्
नृकेशरिन् m. (-री) The Nrisinha or man-lion Avatār.<BR> E. नृ and केशरिन्<BR>a lion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=407-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नृग|नृगः
नृग m. (-गः) The name of a king, the son of IKSHWAKU.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=407-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नृचक्षस्
नृचक्षस् m. (-क्षाः) A demon, a Rākshasa, a goblin.<BR> E. नृ a man, and<BR>चक्षस् an eater; from चक्ष् to eat, असुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=407-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नृजग्ध
नृजग्ध m. (-ग्धः) A man-eater, a cannibal, a Rākshasa. E. (by whom,) नृ<BR>man, जग्ध is eaten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=407-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नृत
नृत (ई) नृती r. 4th cl. (नृत्यति) To dance, to dance as an actor, to gesti-<BR>culate, to act. दिवा० प० अक० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=407-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नृति|नृतिः
नृति f. (-तिः) Dancing, the science or practice.<BR> E. नृत् to dance, aff. कि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=407-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नृतू
नृतू m. (-तूः)<BR>	 1. A dancer, a mime, an actor.<BR>	 2. Earth.<BR>	 3. A worm.<BR>	 4.<BR>Length.<BR> E. नृत् to dance, and कू aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=407-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नृत्त|नृत्तं
नृत्त m. (-त्तं) Dancing.<BR> E. नृत् to dance, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=407-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नृत्य|नृत्यं
नृत्य n. (-त्यं) Dancing, acting, the actor's practice in general.<BR> E. नृत् to<BR>dance, aff. क्यप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=407-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नृत्यत्
नृत्यत् mfn. (-त्यन्-त्यन्ती-त्यत्) Dancing.<BR> E. नृत् to dance, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=407-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नृदेव|नृदेवः
नृदेव m. (-वः) A king.<BR> E. नृ and देव a divinity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=407-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नृधर्म्मन्|नृधर्मन्
नृधर्म्मन् mfn. (-र्म्मा-र्म्मा-र्म्म) Acting as a man, doing a man's duty, &c.<BR>m. (-र्म्मा) A name of KUVERA.<BR>	 n. (-र्म्म) Manly property or duty.<BR>E. नृ man, धर्म्म virtue, अनिच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=407-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नृप|नृपः
नृप m. (-पः) A king, a sovereign.<BR> E. नृ man, पा to protect, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=407-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नृपनीति
नृपनीति f. (-तिः) Royal policy.<BR> E. नृप, नीति policy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=407-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नृपति|नृपतिः
नृपति m. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. A name of KUVERA.<BR>	 2. A king, a sovereign.<BR> E. नृ<BR>man, and पति a master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=407-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नृपद्रुम|नृपद्रुमः
नृपद्रुम m. (-मः) A tree, (Cassia fistula.)<BR> E. नृप, and द्रुम a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=407-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नृपप्रिय|नृपप्रियः
नृपप्रिय m. (-यः) A thorny species of bamboo, (Bambusa spinosa.) E.<BR>नृप a king, and प्रिय fond of. (वेड्वांँश) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=407-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नृपमन्दिर|नृपमन्दिरं
नृपमन्दिर n. (-रं) A royal palace.<BR> E. नृप a king, and मन्दिर a residence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=407-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नृपमान
नृपमान n. (-नं) Sound of music, made to give warning to kings when<BR>eating or feasting.<BR> E. नृप, and मान measure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=407-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नृपलक्ष्मन्
नृपलक्ष्मन् n. (-क्ष्म)<BR>	 1. The royal umbrella.<BR>	 2. Any of the royal insignia.<BR>E. नृप, and लक्ष्मण a mark or sign.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=407-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नृपलिङ्ग|नृपलिंग
नृपलिङ्ग n. (-ङ्गं) Any emblem or mark of royalty.<BR> E. नृप, and लिङ्ग a mark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=407-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नृपलिङ्गधर|नृपलिङ्गधरः
नृपलिङ्गधर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>	 1. Assuming the insignia of sovereignty.<BR>	 2.<BR>Taking, (fraudulently,) the emblem or marks of the royal or mi-<BR>litary caste.<BR> E. नृपलिङ्ग, and धर who has.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=407-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नृपवल्लभ|नृपवल्लभः
नृपवल्लभ mfn. (-भः-भा-भं)<BR>	 1. A king's friend.<BR>	 2. A prepared oil or ghee<BR>containing medicinal properties.<BR>	 f. (-भा) A queen.<BR> E. नृप, and<BR>वल्लभ beloved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=407-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नृपसंश्रय
नृपसंश्रय m. (-यः) Service of princes.<BR> E. नृप, and संश्रय dependence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=407-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नृपसभ|नृपसभं
नृपसभ(भा) n. (-भं)<BR>	 1. An assembly of princes.<BR>	 2. A palace.<BR> E. नृप a king,<BR>and सभा an assembly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=407-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नृपांश
नृपांश m. (-शः) Revenue, the royal portion; of grain, a sixth, eighth,<BR>or twelfth; of fruits, &c. a sixth, and of merchandise a fiftieth.<BR>E. नृप, and अंश a part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=407-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नृपात्मज
नृपात्मज mfn. (-जः-जा-जं) Of royal birth.<BR>	 m. (-जः) A prince.<BR>	 f. (-जा)<BR>1. A bitter gourd.<BR>	 2. A princess.<BR> E. नृप a king, and आत्मज<BR>offspring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=407-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नृपाध्वर|नृपाध्वरः
नृपाध्वर m. (-रः) A sort of sacrifice; the Rājasūya, held by a lord pa-<BR>ramount, in which all the offices are performed by tributary<BR>princes.<BR> E. नृप a king, अध्वर a sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=407-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नृपाभीर|नृपाभीरं
नृपाभीर n. (-रं) Music played at the royal meals.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=407-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नृपामय|नृपामयः
नृपामय m. (-यः) Consumption.<BR> E. नृप, and आमय disease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=407-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नृपावर्त्त|नृपावर्त|नृपावर्त्तं
नृपावर्त्त n. (-र्त्तं) A kind of gem.<BR> E. नृप, and आवर्त्त what revolves.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=407-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नृपासन|नृपासनं
नृपासन n. (-नं) A throne.<BR> E. नृप a king, and आसन a seat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=407-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नृपोचित|नृपोचितः
नृपोचित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Kingly, princely, suited to a king.<BR> E. नृप, and<BR>उचित proper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=407-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नृयज्ञ|नृयज्ञः
नृयज्ञ m. (-ज्ञः) Hospitality.<BR> E. नृ a man, and यज्ञ sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=407-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नृवराह|नृवराहः
नृवराह m. (-हः) The third or the boar incarnation of VIṢṆU.<BR> E. नृ a<BR>man, वराह a boar; being delineated with the figure of a man, and<BR>the head of the wild boar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=407-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नृशंस|नृशंसः
नृशंस mfn. (-सः-सा-सं) Malicious, wicked, hurtful, injurious, mischievous,<BR>destructive.<BR> E. नृ man, शसि to hurt, aff. अण ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=407-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नृशंसवृत्त
नृशंसवृत्त mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं) Practising mischief.<BR> E. नृशंस, and वृत्त engaged<BR>in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=407-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नृसिंह|नृसिंहः
नृसिंह m. (-हः)<BR>	 1. Viṣṇu.<BR>	 2. The fourth Avatāra or descent of that<BR>deity, in the shape of a man, with the head and claws of a lion.<BR>3. A chief, a noble, a great or illustrious man, a great man.<BR> E. नृ a<BR>man, and सिंह a lion; applied in composition, also to signify<BR>preeminence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=407-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नृसेन|नृसेनं
नृसेन(ना) nf. (-नं-ना) An army of men.<BR> E. नृ a man, and सेना an army.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=407-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नृसोम|नृसोमः
नृसोम m. (-मः) An illustrious or great man, a prince or chief.<BR> E. नृ<BR>mankind, and सोम the moon, here implying superiority, or ex-<BR>cellence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=407-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नृहरि|नृहरिः
नृहरि m. (-रिः) VIṢṆU as the man-lion.<BR> E. नृ and हरि a lion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=407-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नेजक|नेजकः
नेजक m. (-कः) A washerman.<BR> E. णिज् to cleanse, aff. ण्वुल् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=407-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नेतव्य
नेतव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं) To be taken, to be carried or conducted.<BR> E. णी<BR>to take, तव्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=407-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नेतृ
नेतृ mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ) Leading, conducting, one who guides or leads,<BR>&c.<BR>	 m. (-ता)<BR>	 1. A master, an owner.<BR>	 2. A guide.<BR> E. णी to lead, aff.<BR>तृच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=407-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नेत्र|नेत्रं
नेत्र mfn. (-त्रः-त्री-त्रं) A leader, a guide, one who guides or leads.<BR>	 n. (-त्रं)<BR>1. The eye.<BR>	 2. The foot of a tree.<BR>	 3. Bleached or wove silk.<BR>	 4. A<BR>car, a carriage.<BR>	 5. The string of a churning rope.<BR>	 6. An enema-<BR>pipe.<BR>	 7. The number “two”.<BR>	 mn. (-त्रः-त्रं) Any tubular vessel.<BR>	 f.<BR>(-त्री)<BR>	 1. A river.<BR>	 2. The goddess LAKṢMĪ.<BR> E. णी to guide or gain,<BR>Unādi aff. ष्ट्रन्, fem. aff. ङीप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=407-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नेत्रज
नेत्रज n. (-जं) A tear.<BR> E. नेत्र, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=407-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नेत्रच्छद|नेत्रच्छदः
नेत्रच्छद m. (-दः) An eyelid.<BR> E. नेत्र the eye, छद् to cover aff. णिच्-क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=407-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नेत्रपर्य्यन्त|नेत्रपर्यन्त|नेत्रपर्यंत|नेत्रपर्यन्तः|नेत्रपर्य्यन्तः
नेत्रपर्य्यन्त mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं) As far as to the eye, up to the eye.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-न्तः) The outer angle of the eye.<BR> E. नेत्र, and पर्य्यन्त limita-<BR>tive अपाङ्गे ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=407-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नेत्रपिण्ड|नेत्रपिंड|नेत्रपिण्डः
नेत्रपिण्ड mf. (-ण्डः-ण्डी)<BR>	 1. A cat.<BR>	 2. The ball of the eye.<BR> E. नेत्र the<BR>eye, and पिण्ड a ball of flesh, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=407-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नेत्रयोनि|नेत्रयोनिः
नेत्रयोनि m. (-निः)<BR>	 1. INDRA.<BR>	 2. The moon.<BR> E. नेत्र an eye, and योनि<BR>the vulva; being covered with marks resembling that organ,<BR>through the curse of GAUTAMA, whose wife he had attempted<BR>to debauch; the sage afterwards relenting, changed these dis-<BR>graceful marks on the body of the deity to as many eyes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=407-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नेत्ररञ्जन|नेत्ररंजन|नेत्ररञ्जनं
नेत्ररञ्जन n. (-नं) Collyrium.<BR> E. नेत्र and रञ्जन delighting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=407-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नेत्ररोग|नेत्ररोगः
नेत्ररोग m. (-गः) Any disease of the eye.<BR> E. नेत्र, and रोग disease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=407-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नेत्रवस्त्र
नेत्रवस्त्र n. (-स्त्रं) A veil over the eye.<BR> E. नेत्र and वस्त्र clothes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=407-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नेत्रामय|नेत्रामयः
नेत्रामय m. (-यः) Ophthalmia, &c.<BR> E. नेत्र, and आमय sickness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=407-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नेत्राम्बु|नेत्रांबु
नेत्राम्बु m. (म्बुः) A tear.<BR> E. नेत्र an eye, and अम्बु water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=407-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नेत्रोत्सव|नेत्रोत्सवः
नेत्रोत्सव n. (-वं) Any pleasing or beautiful object.<BR> E. नेत्र, and उत्सव<BR>festival.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=407-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नेत्रौषध|नेत्रौषधं
नेत्रौषध n. (-धं)<BR>	 1. Green sulphate of iron considered as a collyrium.<BR>2. Collyrium in general.<BR>	 f. (-धी) A drug, commonly कोंगा.<BR> E. नेत्र<BR>the eye, and औषघ a medicament.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=407-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नेदयत्
नेदयत् mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्) Approximating, bringing near.<BR> E. नेद for<BR>अन्तिक nom. verb, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=407-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नेदिष्ठ|नेदिष्ठं
नेदिष्ठ mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठा-ष्ठं)<BR>	 1. Very near.<BR>	 2. Clever.<BR>	 m. (-ष्ठः) A tree; (Alan-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=408-a" target="_blank">Page408-a+ 60</a>]<BR>gium hexapetalum.)<BR> E. अन्तिक near, इष्ठन् affix of the superlative,<BR>and the form irr.; also नेदीयस् with ईयसुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=407-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नेदीयस्
नेदीयस् mfn. (-यान्-यसी-यः) Very near, nearest: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=408-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नेन्य
नेन्य mfn. (-न्यः-न्या-न्यं) Taking or obtaining frequently.<BR> E. णी to ob-<BR>tain, frequent. v., अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=408-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नेप|नेपः
नेप m. (-पः)<BR>	 1. The family priest.<BR>	 2. Water.<BR> E. णी to guide, Unādi<BR>aff. प.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=408-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नेपथ्य|नेपथ्यं
नेपथ्य n. (-थ्यं)<BR>	 1. A stage, or the part behind the scenes, the tiring<BR>room, &c.<BR>	 2. Ornament, decoration, embellishment.<BR> E. णी to<BR>guide, विच् aff. and the vowel changed, ने the eye, or a chief,<BR>पथ्य proper, agreeable, grateful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=408-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नेपाल|नेपालः
नेपाल m. (-लः) The country of Nepal.<BR> E. ने a chief: see the last,<BR>and पाल cherishing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=408-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नेपालिका
नेपालिका f. (-का) Arsenic.<BR> E. नेपाल, and ठन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=408-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नेम|नेमः
नेम m. (-मः)<BR>	 1. Time, period, season.<BR>	 2. Term, boundary, limit.<BR>	 3.<BR>Part, portion.<BR>	 4. A fence, a boundary wall or hedge.<BR>	 5. A hole,<BR>a chasm.<BR>	 6. Fraud, deceit.<BR>	 7. Acting, dancing.<BR>	 8. Other, dif-<BR>ferent.<BR>	 9. Evening.<BR>	 10. Up, above.<BR>	 11. A root.<BR>	 12. The founda-<BR>tion of a wall.<BR> E. णी to gain, Unādi aff. मन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=408-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नेमि|नेमिः
नेमि f. (-मिः-मी)<BR>	 1. The circumference of a wheel.<BR>	 2. The framework<BR>for the rope of a well.<BR>	 3. Edge, rim.<BR>	 4. A windlass.<BR>	 5. A thun-<BR>derbolt.<BR>	 6. The earth.<BR>	 m. (-मिः)<BR>	 1. The twenty-second Jina or<BR>Jaina pontiff.<BR>	 2. A sacred place, as Mathurā.<BR>	 mf. (-मिः-मी) A<BR>tree, (Dalbergia Oujeiniensis.)<BR> E. णी to gain or go, Unādi aff. मि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=408-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नेमिचक्र|नेमिचक्रः
नेमिचक्र m. (-क्रः) A prince descended from PARĪKSHIT, who is said<BR>to have removed the capital of India to Kausāmbi, after the<BR>inundation of Hastināpur.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=408-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नेमिन्
नेमिन् m. (-मी) A tree.<BR> E. नेमि the circumference of a wheel, इनि aff.<BR>the wood being used for its manufacture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=408-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नेष्टृ
नेष्टृ m. (-ष्टा) One of the sixteen officiating priests at a soma sacrifice.<BR>E. णी to lead or conduct the ceremonies, Unādi aff. तृन्, and षुक्<BR>augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=408-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैःश्रेयस
नैःश्रेयस mfn. (-सः-सी-सं) Relating to final emancipation, leading<BR>to it, effecting it, &c.<BR> E. निःश्रेयस्, and अण aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=408-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैःश्रेयसिक
नैःश्रेयसिक mfn. (-कः-कीकं) Relating to final emancipation, &c. E.<BR>निःश्रेयस, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=408-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैस्नेह्य
नैस्नेह्य n. (-ह्यं)<BR>	 1. Dryness, austerity.<BR>	 2. Coldness, want of affection.<BR>E. निःस्नेह, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=408-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैक|नैकः
नैक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Many, various.<BR> E. न neg. एक one.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=408-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैवटिक
नैवटिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Near, being near.<BR> E. निकट, and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=408-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैकट्य|नैकट्यं
नैकट्य n. (-ठ्यं) Proximity, vicinage.<BR> E. निकट and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=408-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैकभेद|नैकभेदः
नैकभेद mfn. (-दः-दा-दं) Various, multiform, manifold.<BR> E. नैक, and<BR>भेद kind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=408-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैकरूप
नैकरूप mfn. (-पः-पा-पं) Multiform.<BR> E. नैक, and रूप form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=408-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैकषेय|नैकषेयः
नैकषेय mf. (-यः-या) A Rākshasa, a fiend, goblin.<BR> E. निकशा the mother<BR>of the race, and ढक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=408-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैकृतिक
नैकृतिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>	 1. Morose, harsh-spoken.<BR>	 2. Wicked, bad.<BR>E. निकृति, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=408-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैगम|नैगमः
नैगम m. (-मः) An Upanishad or portion of the Vedas.<BR>	 2. A sectarian,<BR>not a heretic.<BR>	 3. A trader, a merchant.<BR>	 4. A citizen, a towns-<BR>man.<BR>	 5. Guiding, leading, directing.<BR>	 6. A road, a way<BR> E. निगम a<BR>religious obligation, aff. स्वार्थे अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=408-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैचिक|नैचिकं
नैचिक n. (-कं) The head of an ox.<BR>	 f. (-की) A capital cow.<BR> E. नीकैस्<BR>low, down, चर् to go, ठक् aff. and the radical finals rejected;<BR>also नीचिकी, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=408-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैज|नैजं
नैज mfn. (-जः-जी-जं) Own<BR> E. निज, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=408-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैत्य|नैत्यं
नैत्य n. (-त्यं) Eternity, perpetuity.<BR> E. नित्य + व्युष्टा-अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=408-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैत्यक
नैत्यक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Always, constant, indispensable.<BR> E. नित्य, and वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=408-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैत्यिक
नैत्यिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Invariable, constant, perpetual, indis-<BR>pensable.<BR> E. नित्य and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=408-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैद्र
नैद्र mfn. (-द्रः-द्री-द्रं) Sleepy, somniferous, relating or occurring in<BR>sleep.<BR> E. निद्रा, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=408-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैधान
नैधान mfn. (-नः-नी-नं) Relating to a treasure, a nest, &c.<BR>	 f. (-नी)<BR>A boundary where some articles are buried and dug up. E.<BR>निधान a treasure, अञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=408-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैपाल|नैपालः
नैपाल mfn. (-लः-ली-लं) Produced in Nepal.<BR>	 f. (-ली)<BR>	 1. Double jasmine.<BR>2. Red arsenic.<BR>	 3. Sephālica, (Nyctanthes tristis.)<BR>	 4. Indigo. E.<BR>नेपाल Nepal, अण् and ङीष् affs.; brought from thence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=408-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैपालिक|नैपालिकं
नैपालिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Produced in or brought from Nepal &c.<BR>	 n.<BR>(-कं) Copper.<BR> E. नेपाल, and ठेक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=408-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैपुण|नैपुणं
नैपुण n. (-णं) Dexterity, cleverness, skill.<BR> E. निपुण skilful, aff. अण;<BR>also with ष्यञ् aff., नैपण्य n. (ण्यं) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=408-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैपुण्य|नैपुण्यं
नैपुण्य n. (-ण्यं) Dexterity, cleverness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=408-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैमित्तिक|नैमित्तिकं|नैमित्तिकः
नैमित्तिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>	 1. Occasional.<BR>	 n. (-कं)<BR>	 1. An effect (opposite<BR>to “cause”)<BR>	 2. Occasional, periodical act or rite.<BR>	 m. (-कः) An astro-<BR>loger, a prophet.<BR> E. निमित्त cause, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=408-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नेमित्तिककर्म्मन्
नेमित्तिककर्म्मन् n. (-र्म्म) An occasional ceremony, such as should be<BR>observed on the birth of a child, &c.<BR> E. नैमित्तिक, and कर्म्म act;<BR>also नैमित्तिकक्रिया, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=408-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैमिष
नैमिष mfn. (-षः-षी-षं) Momentary, transient, in a twinkling.<BR>	 n. (-षं)<BR>The name of a forest. See नैमिषारण्य.<BR> E. निमिष, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=408-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैमिषारण्य|नैमिषारण्यं
नैमिषारण्य n. (-ण्यं) A wood celebrated as the residence of the Ṛshis,<BR>to whom Sautī related the Mahābhārat.<BR> E. निमिष a twinkling of<BR>an eye, in which the sage GAURAMUKHA destroyed a sort of<BR>Asuras, and अण् aff. and अरण्य a forest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=408-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैमेय|नैमेयः
नैमेय m. (-यः) Barter, exchange.<BR> E. नि before, मि to measure, यत् aff.<BR>and स्वार्थे-अण् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=408-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैयग्रोध|नैयग्रोधं
नैयग्रोध n. (-धं) The fruit of the Indian fig tree, &c.<BR> E. न्यग्रोध the fig<BR>tree, &c. and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=408-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैयङ्कव|नैयङ्कवं
नैयङ्कव mfn. (-वः-वी-वं) Made of the skin, &c. of the deer, called न्यङ्कु E.<BR>न्यङ्कु and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=408-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैयत्य|नैयत्यं
नैयत्य n. (-त्यं) Self-government or subjugation.<BR> E. नियत, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=408-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैयमिक
नैयमिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) According to rule, regular, enjoined, E.<BR>नियम, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=408-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैयायिक|नैयायिकः
नैयायिक m. (-कः) A logician, a follower of the Nyāya or logical<BR>philosophy.<BR> E. न्याय the Nyāya system, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=408-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैरन्तय्य
नैरन्तय्य n. (-र्य्यं) Compactness, closeness, contiguity.<BR> E. निरन्तर,<BR>and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=408-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैराश्या
नैराश्या n. (-श्यं) Despair.<BR> E. निराश, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=408-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैरुक्त|नैरुक्तं|नैरुक्तः
नैरुक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ती-क्तं)<BR>	 1. Obsolete, uncommon, belonging to the<BR>glossary of the Vedas 2. Acquainted with the terms of the Ve-<BR>das.<BR>	 3. A Philologist.<BR> E. निरुक्ति and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=408-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैरृत|नैरृतः
नैरृत m. (-तः)<BR>	 1. A demon, a fiend.<BR>	 2. The ruler of the south-west<BR>quarter.<BR>	 f. (-ती)<BR>	 1. The south-west quarter.<BR>	 2. An epithet of<BR>Durgā.<BR> E. निऋति said to be a proper name, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=408-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैर्गुण्य|नैर्गुण्यं
नैर्गुण्य n. (-न्यं) Absence of qualities or properties.<BR> E. निर्गुण, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=408-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैर्मल्य|नैर्मल्यं|नैर्म्मल्यं
नैर्मल्य n. (-ल्यं) Cleanness, purity.<BR> E. निर्मल, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=408-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैल्य|नैल्यं
नैल्य n. (-ल्यं) Blueness, darkness of colour.<BR> E. नील, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=408-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैवि
नैवि(ब)ड्य n. (-ड्यं)<BR>	 1. Thickness, substance.<BR>	 2. Closeness, compactness.<BR>3. Continued sound.<BR> E. निविड thick, &c. ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=408-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैवेद्य|नैवेद्यं
नैवेद्य n. (-द्यं) An offering of eatable articles presented to a deity, and<BR>may afterwards be distributed to his ministers or worshippers, es-<BR>pecially when it has been presented to any form of VIṢṆU. E.<BR>निवेद presenting, offering, ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=408-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैवेशिक|नैवेशिकं
नैवेशिक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) A present to a Brāhman who is a householder,<BR>a girl so given, or ornaments with her, &c.<BR> E. निवेश a house,<BR>aff. ठक् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=408-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैश|नैशं
नैश mfn. (-शः-शी-शं) Nocturnal, relating to the night; or a person,<BR>&c. doing any thing by night.<BR> E. निशा night, and अण् aff. also<BR>with ठञ् aff. नैशिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं ।)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=408-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैश्चित्य|नैश्चित्यं
नैश्चित्य n. (-त्यं)<BR>	 1. Certainty.<BR>	 2. A fixed festival; as at birth, investi-<BR>ture, marriage. &c.<BR> E. निश्चित certain, ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=409-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैषध|नैषधः
नैषध mfn. (-धः-धी-धं) Relating to NISHADHA.<BR>	 m. (-धः) A name of NALA.<BR>E. निषध the country so called, aff. अण् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=409-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैष्कर्म्म्य
नैष्कर्म्म्य n. (-र्म्म्यं)<BR>	 1. Abstinence or exemption from acts or their conse-<BR>quences.<BR>	 2. The salvation obtained by abstraction in opposition to<BR>that obtained by works.<BR> E. निष्कर्म्मन् and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=409-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैष्कशतिक
नैष्कशतिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Worth a hundred Nishkas, bought with<BR>them, &c.<BR> E. निष्क and शत a hundred, ठञ् aff.; also with सहस्र a thou-<BR>sand नैष्कसहस्रिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं ।)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=409-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैष्किक|नैष्किकः
नैष्किक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Bought with, made of, &c. a Nishka.<BR>	 m. (-कः)<BR>The mint-master.<BR> E. निष्क a weight of gold, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=409-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैष्कृतिक
नैष्कृतिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Wicked, evil-doing, malignant.<BR> E. निष्कृति,<BR>and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=409-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैष्ठिक|नैष्ठिकः
नैष्ठिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>	 1. Relating to state or condition.<BR>	 2. Belonging<BR>to the character or office of a perpetual student.<BR>	 3. Firm, fixed.<BR>4. Final.<BR>	 5. Highest, perfect.<BR>	 6. Completely versed in.<BR>	 7. Vowing<BR>perpetual abstinence and chastity.<BR>	 m. (-कः) The Brāhman who<BR>continues with his spiritual preceptor, and always remains in the<BR>condition of the religious student.<BR> E. निष्ठा certainty, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=409-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैष्ठुर्य्य|नैष्ठुर्य|नैष्ठुर्यं
नैष्ठुर्य्य n. (-र्य्य) Severity, cruelty.<BR> E. निष्ठुर, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=409-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैसर्गिक|नैसर्गिकः
नैसर्गिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Natural, innate.<BR> E. निसर्ग nature, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=409-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैस्त्रिंशिक|नैस्त्रिंशिकः
नैस्त्रिंशिक m. (-कः) A swordsman, a soldier armed with a sword. E.<BR>निस्त्रिंश a sword, aff. ठक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=409-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नो
नो ind. No, not.<BR> E. नह to command, aff. डो.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=409-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नोधस्
नोधस् m. (-धाः) The name of a saint.<BR> E. नु to praise, असि Unādi<BR>aff. and धुट augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=409-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नोपस्थातृ
नोपस्थातृ mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ) Remote, far off.<BR> E. न negative, उप near, स्था<BR>to be, aff. तृच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=409-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नौ
नौ f. (-नौः) A boat, a vessel in general.<BR> E. नुद् to send, Unādi aff. डौ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=409-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नौका
नौका f. (-का) A boat.<BR> E. कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=409-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नौकादण्ड|नौकादंड|नौकादण्डः
नौकादण्ड m. (-ण्डः) An oar, a paddle.<BR> E. नौका a boat, and दण्ड a stick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=409-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नौतार्य्य|नौतार्य|नौतार्य्यं
नौतार्य्य mfn. (-र्य्यः-र्य्या-र्य्यं) Navigable, to be gone to or traversed in a<BR>vessel.<BR> E. नौ, and तार्य्य to be crossed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=409-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नौयायिन्
नौयायिन् mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि) A passenger, a freight, who or what<BR>goes in a boat or vessel.<BR> E. नौ, and यायिन् who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=409-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यक्
न्यक् ind. A particle implying abuse or contempt when prefixed to कु<BR>or भू. E. The neuter of न्यञ्च used as a particle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=409-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यक्करण|न्यक्करणं
न्यक्करण n. (-णं) Treating with disrespect or contempt.<BR> E. न्यक्, and<BR>करण making.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=409-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यक्कार|न्यक्कारः
न्यक्कार m. (-रः) Contempt, disrespect.<BR> E. न्यङ् little, low, कृ to make,<BR>aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=409-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यक्कारुका
न्यक्कारुका f. (-का) An insect found in ordure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=409-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यक्ष|न्यक्षं|न्यक्षः
न्यक्ष mfn. (-क्षः-क्षा-क्षं)<BR>	 1. Whole, entire.<BR>	 2. Low, inferior.<BR>	 m. (-क्षः)<BR>	 1. A<BR>name of PARAŚURĀMA.<BR>	 2. A buffalo.<BR>	 n. (-क्षं)<BR>	 1. A kind of grass<BR>called mahishatrina.<BR> E. नि before, अक्ष a die &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=409-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यग्जाति
न्यग्जाति mfn. (-तिः-तिः-ति) Of mean or inferior race.<BR> E. न्यक्, and जाति caste.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=409-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यग्भावन
न्यग्भावन m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. Contempt.<BR>	 2. Defiling.<BR> E. न्यक्, and भावन con-<BR>ceiving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=409-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यग्रोध|न्यग्रोधः
न्यग्रोध m. (-धः)<BR>	 1. The Indian fig tree. (Ficus Indica.)<BR>	 2. A fathom<BR>measured by the arms extended.<BR>	 3. The Sami, (Mimosa albida)<BR>f. (-धी)<BR>	 1. A plant, (Salvinia cucullata, Rox.)<BR>	 2. A medical plant,<BR>commonly Mohānā.<BR> E. न्यक् short, रुध् to impede, aff. अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=409-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यग्रोधपरिमण्डला|न्यग्रोधपरिमंडला
न्यग्रोधपरिमण्डला f. (-ला) An elegant woman. In Vāchaspatya she is thus<BR>described: --स्तनौ सुकठिनौ यस्या नितम्बे च विशालता ।<BR>मध्ये क्षीणा भवेद्या सा न्यग्रोधपरिमण्डला ॥<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=409-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यङ्कु|न्यंकु|न्यंकुः|न्यङ्कुः
न्यङ्कु m. (-ङ्कुः)<BR>	 1. A deer.<BR>	 2. The name of a saint or Muni.<BR> E. नि<BR>always, अञ्च् to go, aff. कु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=409-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यङ्कुभूरूह
न्यङ्कुभूरूह m. (-हः) A tree, (Cassia fistula.)<BR> E. न्यङ्कु a deer, and भूरुह<BR>a tree. श्योनाकवृक्षे ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=409-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यङ्ग|न्यंगः|न्यङ्गः
न्यङ्ग n. (-ङ्गं) Low abuse.<BR> E. न्यङ्, and ग what goes or is. According to<BR>Vāchaspatya.--m. (-ङ्गः) नितरामञ्जने<BR> E. नि-अन्ज-घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=409-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यञ्च
न्यञ्च mfn. (न्यङ्-नीची-न्यक्)<BR>	 1. Short, dwarfish.<BR>	 2. Low, vile, con-<BR>temptible, base.<BR>	 3. Slow, lazy.<BR>	 4. Whole, entire.<BR> E. नि prefixed to<BR>अञ् to go, aff. क्विप्. निम्नतया अञ्चति, अञ्च-विच् । निम्ने क्विन् न्यच् तत्रार्थे<BR>त्रि० । शसादौ भत्वे च नीचः नीचा अन्यत्र कुत्वम् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=409-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यञ्चित|न्यंचित|न्यञ्चितं
न्यञ्चित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Thrown or cast down.<BR> E. नि before, अञ्चित gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=409-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यय|न्ययः
न्यय m. (-यः) Loss, expense, waste, destruction.<BR> E. नि before इ to go,<BR>aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=409-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यर्ण|न्यर्ण्ण
न्यर्ण mfn. (-र्ण्णः-र्ण्णा-र्ण्णं)<BR>	 1. Asked, solicited.<BR>	 2. Gone, 3. Injured.<BR> E. नि,<BR>अर्द्द् to ask, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=409-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यसन|न्यसनं
न्यसन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Delivering, Giving up.<BR>	 2. Depositing.<BR> E. नि before, अस्<BR>to throw ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=409-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यस्त|न्यस्तं
न्यस्त mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं)<BR>	 1. Deposited, consigned, delivered.<BR>	 2. Placed in<BR>or upon.<BR>	 3. Applied to.<BR> E. नि before, अस् to throw or send, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=409-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यस्तशस्त्र|न्यस्तशस्त्रः
न्यस्तशस्त्र mfn. (-स्त्रः-स्त्रा-स्त्रं) Unarmed, defenceless, having laid down or<BR>resigned weapons.<BR>	 m. (-स्त्रः) A deified progenitor.<BR> E. न्यस्त delivered,<BR>and शस्त्र a weapon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=409-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्याक्य|न्याक्यं
न्याक्य n. (-क्यं) Fried rice.<BR> E. नि + अकि-न्यत् बा० न लीपः । “मुडि” इति भाषा ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=409-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्याद|न्यादः
न्याद m. (-दः) Eating, feeding.<BR> E. नि before, अद् to eat, णः aff. न घसादेशः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=409-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्याय|न्यायः
न्याय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. Propriety, fitness.<BR>	 2. The Nyāya doctrine, logic, logi-<BR>cal philosophy.<BR>	 3. Apposite illustration.<BR>	 4. A complete argument<BR>or syllogism.<BR>	 5. Policy, good government.<BR>	 6. Method, way, man-<BR>ner, plan, rule.<BR>	 7. Virtue, honesty.<BR>	 8. Justice, law.<BR>	 9. A law-suit.<BR>12. Judgment.<BR>	 13. A universal rule, (In gram.)<BR>	 14. Likeness analo-<BR>gy.<BR>	 15. A vedic accent.<BR> E. नि certainly, इण to go, aff. भावकरणादौ घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=409-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यायता
न्यायता f. (-ता) Fitness, propriety.<BR> E. तल् added to न्याय; also with त्व<BR>न्यायत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=409-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यायसारिणी
न्यायसारिणी f. (-णी)<BR>	 1. A woman acting or judging rightly.<BR>	 2. Right<BR>behaviour.<BR> E. न्याय propriety, सारिणी proceeding. न्यायं सरति, सृ-णिनि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=409-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यायाचार
न्यायाचार m. (-रः) A virtuous man.<BR> E. न्याय, and आचार observance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=409-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यायाधार|न्यायाधारः
न्यायाधार m. (-रः) An example of virtue or propriety.<BR> E. न्याय, and आधार<BR>what uphelds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=409-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यायिन्
न्यायिन् mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि)<BR>	 1. Right, fit.<BR>	 2. Logical.<BR> E. न्याय, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=409-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्याय्य|न्याय्यं
न्याय्य mfn. (-य्यः-य्या-य्यं) Right, proper, fit.<BR> E. न्याय, and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=409-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यास|न्यासः
न्यास m. (-सः)<BR>	 1. A deposit, a pledge.<BR>	 2. Deserting, abandoning.<BR>	 3. De-<BR>livering, presenting.<BR>	 4. Mental delivering, consigning or entru-<BR>sting any thing to the mind.<BR>	 5. Mental appropriation or assi-<BR>gnment of various parts of the body to tutelary divinities. accom-<BR>panied with certain prayers and gesticulations.<BR>	 6. Painting,<BR>stamp, mark.<BR>	 7. Bringing forward.<BR>	 8. Seizing. (with the claws.)<BR>E. नि before, अस् to throw or cast away, aff. कर्मणि, भावे वा घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=409-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यासधारिन्
न्यासधारिन् m. (-री) The holder of a deposit, a mortgagee.<BR> E. न्यास,<BR>and धारिन् who has.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=409-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यु
न्यु(न्यू)ङ्ख m. (-ङ्खः)<BR>	 1. Six-fold repetition of the triliteral name of god.<BR>2. The Sāma Veda.<BR>	 3. Pleasing, agreeable charming, beautiful.<BR>E. नि before, उखि to go, aff. घञ्; it is also read न्यूङ्ख.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=409-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्युब्ज|न्युब्जं|न्युब्जः
न्युब्ज mfn. (-ब्जः-ब्जा-ब्जं)<BR>	 1. Crooked-backed, hump-backed, 2. Looking<BR>downwards.<BR>	 3. Bent, crooked.<BR>	 4. Convex.<BR>	 m. (-ब्जः)<BR>	 1. Disease,<BR>sickness, pain.<BR>	 2. A sort of ladle made of Kusa grass.<BR>	 3. The<BR>Nyagrodha tree.<BR>	 n. (-ब्जं)<BR>	 1. The fruit of the Kāmaranga, (Caram-<BR>bola averrhoa.)<BR>	 2. A vessel used at Shrāddhas.<BR> E. न्युब्ज् to be<BR>crooked, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=409-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्युब्जखड्ग|न्युब्जखड्गः
न्युब्जखड्ग m. (-ङ्गः) A sabre, a crooked sword.<BR> E. न्युब्ज crooked, and खड्ग a sword.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=409-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यून|न्यूनं
न्यून mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>	 1. Blamable, vile, wicked, despicable.<BR>	 2. Less,<BR>deficient, defective.<BR> E. नि before, ऊन less, affix अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=409-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यूनता
न्यूनता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Deficiency.<BR>	 2. Inferiority.<BR> E. तल् added to न्यून, also न्यूनत्व.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=409-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यूनधी
न्यूनधी mfn. (-धीः-धीः-धि) Ignorant, foolish,<BR> E. न्यून, and धी intellect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=409-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यूनपञ्चाशद्भाव|न्यूनपञ्चाशद्भावः
न्यूनपञ्चाशद्भाव m. (-वः) An idiot.<BR> E. न्यून, and पञ्चाशत् fifty, भाव property<BR>having but forty-nine properties of human nature.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=409-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यूनाङ्ग|न्यूनांग
न्यूनाङ्ग mfn. (-ङ्गः-ङ्गी-ङ्गं) Maimed, mutilated, imperfect.<BR> E. न्यून, and<BR>अङ्ग body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=410-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यूनाधिक
न्यूनाधिक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Unequal, more or less.<BR> E. न्यून, and अधिक more.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=410-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यूनाधिकविभाग
न्यूनाधिकविभाग m. (-गः) Unequal partition.<BR> E. न्यूनाधिक, and विभाग<BR>division.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=410-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यूनेन्द्रिय
न्यूनेन्द्रिय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Imperfect, wanting some organ; as blind,<BR>deaf, &c.<BR> E. न्यून. and इन्द्रिय an organ of sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=410-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्रस्थिमालिन्
न्रस्थिमालिन् m. (-ली) A name of SĪVA.<BR> E. नृ man, अस्थि a bone, माला<BR>a necklace, and इनि poss. aff.; ornamented with a garland of<BR>human skulls.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=410-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प|पं|पः
प The twenty-first consonant of the Deva Nāgri alphabet, corres-<BR>ponding to the letter P.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=410-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प|पं|पः
प m. (-पः)<BR>	 1. Air, wind 2. A prince, a ruler.<BR>	 3. A leaf.<BR>	 4. An egg.<BR>	 f.<BR>(-पा) (at the end of compounds).<BR>	 1. Drinking, (as in अनेकप)<BR>	 2.<BR>Guarding, Protecting, ruling. (As in गोप)<BR> E. पा to nourish, &c.<BR>aff. ड ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=410-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्कण|पक्कणः
पक्कण mn. (-णः-णं) The residence of low or outcast tribes.<BR> E. पच् to<BR>cook, कण् aff. and क substituted for च.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=410-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्तव्य
पक्तव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>	 1. To be cooked or dressed.<BR>	 2. To be matured.<BR>3. To be digested. पच् to cook, &c. तव्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=410-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्ति|पक्तिः
पक्ति f. (-क्तिः)<BR>	 1. Cooking.<BR>	 2. Ripening.<BR>	 3. Fame, respectability.<BR>	 4.<BR>Digestion.<BR> E. पच् to cook, aff. भावे-क्तिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=410-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्तिशूल|पक्तिशूलं
पक्तिशूल n. (-लं) Inflammation with violent pain of the bowels proceed-<BR>ing from indigestion, cholic.<BR> E. पक्ति, and शूल cholic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=410-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्तृ
पक्तृ mfn. (-क्ता-क्त्री-क्तृ) Who or what ripens or cooks.<BR>	 m. (-क्ता)<BR>	 1. The<BR>digestive faculty.<BR>	 2. Fire.<BR> E. पच् to cook, &c. तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=410-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्त्र|पक्त्रं
पक्त्र n. (-क्त्रं) The sacred fire to be maintained perpetually by the huse-<BR>holder.<BR> E. पच् to mature, Unādi aff. त्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=410-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्त्रिम|पक्त्रिमं
पक्त्रिम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं) Ripe, ripened, matured, cooked.<BR> E. पच् to cook,<BR>&c. aff. क्त्रि and मप् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=410-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्त्वा
पक्त्वा ind. Having cooked, dressed, matured, &c.<BR> E. पच् to cook, क्त्रा aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=410-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्व|पक्वं
पक्व mfn. (-क्वः-क्वा-क्वं)<BR>	 1. Mature, dressed, matured by nature or by art.<BR>2. Fully matured, on the eve of rottenness or decay.<BR>	 3. Perfect,<BR>come to perfection.<BR>	 4. Able, shrewd, experienced, mature (as the<BR>understanding.)<BR>	 5. Grey, (the hair.)<BR>	 6. Digested.<BR>	 7. Cooked, boiled.<BR>8. Baked, burned.<BR> E. पच् too cook or ripen, व substituted<BR>for क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=410-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्वकृत्
पक्वकृत् mfn. (-कृत्) Cooking, maturing, who or what does so.<BR>	 m. (-त्) The<BR>Nimba tree.<BR> E. पक्व ripe, and क्वत् what makes; the leaves of the<BR>plant are applied to phlegmonoid swellings, to induce suppuration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=410-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्वकेश
पक्वकेश mfn. (-शः-शी-श) Grey-haired.<BR> E. पक्व, and केश the hair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=410-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्वरस|पक्वरसः
पक्वरस m. (-सः) Wine or vinous liquor.<BR> E. पक्व matured, रस juice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=410-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्ववारि
पक्ववारि n. (-रिः)<BR>	 1. Rice-gruel.<BR>	 2. Boiling water.<BR>	 3. Distilled water.<BR>E. पक्व boiled, वारि water; also read पङ्कवारि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=410-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्वान्न|पक्वान्नं
पक्वान्न n. (-न्नं) Dressed or cooked food.<BR> E. पक्व, and अन्न food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=410-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्वाशय|पक्वाशयः
पक्वाशय m. (-यः) The abdomen, the stomach.<BR> E. पक्व, and आशय<BR>receptacle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=410-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्वेष्टका
पक्वेष्टका f. (-का) A burnt or baked brick.<BR> E. पक्व, and इष्टका a brick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=410-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्ष|पक्षः
पक्ष r. 1st and 10th cls. (पक्षति पक्षयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To take or accept.<BR>	 2. To<BR>take a part or side. भ्वा० चु० उभ० सक० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=410-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्ष|पक्षः
पक्ष m. (-क्ष-)<BR>	 1. The half of a lunar month or fortnight, comprising fif-<BR>teen days.<BR>	 2. A wing, a feather; (it is also neuter in this sense.)<BR>	 3.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=410-b" target="_blank">Page410-b+ 60</a>]<BR>The feather of an arrow.<BR>	 4. Partisan.<BR>	 5. friend.<BR>	 6. A side, a flank.<BR>7. An army, forces.<BR>	 8. A house.<BR>	 9. An argument, a thesis, a posi-<BR>tion advanced, doctrine to be maintained.<BR>	 10. Contradiction,<BR>opposition, rejoinder, reply.<BR>	 11. The subject of an inference.<BR>	 12.<BR>Alternative.<BR>	 13. A tribe, a class.<BR>	 14. The ash pit of a fire place.<BR>15. A royal elephant.<BR>	 16. (In composition with words signifying<BR>“hair”.) Quantity, as केशपक्ष much or abundant hair.<BR>	 17. A bird.<BR>18. A bracelet.<BR>	 19. Purity, perfection.<BR>	 20. A limb, a member.<BR>21. A tail.<BR>	 22. (In Arithmetic,) Side of an equation in a primary<BR>division.<BR>	 23. Condition.<BR>	 24. A wall.<BR>	 25. A party.<BR>	 26. The subject<BR>of a syllogism or inference.<BR> E. पक्ष् to take, aff. अच् or पण to tran-<BR>sact business, Unādi aff. स, and क substituted for the radical<BR>final.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=410-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षक|पक्षकः
पक्षक m. (-क)<BR>	 1. A private or back door.<BR>	 2. A side.<BR>	 3. A sidesman,<BR>an associate, a confederate or partisan.<BR> E. कन् added to the<BR>preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=410-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षचर|पक्षचरः
पक्षचर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. The moon.<BR>	 2. An elephant strayed from the herd.<BR>3. An attendant, a constant companion.<BR> E. पक्ष a fortnight, &c.<BR>चर who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=410-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षज|पक्षजः
पक्षज mfn. (-जः-जा-जं) Produced in a fortnight, &c.<BR>	 m. (-जः) The<BR>moon.<BR> E. पक्ष a fortnight, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=410-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षजन्मन्
पक्षजन्मन् m. (-न्मा) The moon.<BR> E. पक्ष, and जन्मन् birth: the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=410-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षता
पक्षता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. The nature or essential character of a proposition.<BR>2. The taking up a side of argument.<BR>	 3. Maintaining or defend-<BR>ing a thesis.<BR> E. तल् added to पक्ष; also with त्व, पक्षत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=410-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षति|पक्षतिः
पक्षति f. (-तिः-ती)<BR>	 1. The first day of the half month.<BR>	 2. The root or<BR>insertion of a wing.<BR> E. पक्ष a fortnight, &c. तिन् aff. and ङीष्<BR>optionally added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=410-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षद्वय
पक्षद्वय n. (-यं)<BR>	 1. A month.<BR>	 2. Both sides of an argument, &c.<BR> E. पक्ष,<BR>and द्वय two.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=410-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षद्वार|पक्षद्वारं
पक्षद्वार n. (-रं) A private entrance, an inner or back door.<BR> E. पक्ष a<BR>a side, and द्वार a door.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=410-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षधर|पक्षधरः
पक्षधर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Who or what has a part or side, a wing, &c.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. The moon.<BR>	 2. A bird.<BR>	 3. A partisan.<BR>	 4. An elephant<BR>strayed from the herd.<BR> E. पक्ष a half month, धर who has.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=410-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षपात|पक्षपातः
पक्षपात m. (-तः)<BR>	 1. Adopting a side or an argument whether right<BR>or wrong, partisanship.<BR>	 2. A partisan, an adherent, who or<BR>what sides with.<BR>	 3. The moulting of birds considered to proceed<BR>from fever.<BR> E. पक्ष, and पात who cause to go, or पक्ष a wing, and<BR>पात falling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=410-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षपातिता
पक्षपातिता f. (-ता) Adherence, friendship, fellowship.<BR> E. पक्षपातिन्,<BR>and तल aff.; also with त्व, पक्षपातित्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=410-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षपातिन्
पक्षपातिन् m. (-ती)<BR>	 1. A partisan, a friend, an adherent.<BR>	 2. Moving<BR>the wings.<BR> E. पक्षपात, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=410-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षपालि|पक्षपालिः
पक्षपालि m. (-लिः) A private or back door.<BR> E. पक्ष a side, and पालि a point, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=410-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षभाग|पक्षभागः
पक्षभाग m. (-गः)<BR>	 1. The side or flank of an elephant.<BR>	 2. The side,<BR>in general.<BR> E. पक्ष the side, and भाग a part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=410-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षमूल|पक्षमूलं
पक्षमूल n. (-लं) The root or articulation of a wing.<BR> E. पक्ष a wing,<BR>and मूल a root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=410-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षवत्|पक्षवन्त्
पक्षवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>	 1. Winged.<BR>	 2. Having a side or party. E.<BR>पक्ष, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=410-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षवाहन|पक्षवाहनः
पक्षवाहन m. (-नः) A bird.<BR> E. पक्ष a wing, and वाहन vehicle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=410-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षविन्दु
पक्षविन्दु m. (-न्दुः) A heron.<BR> E. पक्ष a feather, and विन्दु a spot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=410-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षस
पक्षस m. (-सः) A wing.<BR> E. पक्ष as above, असि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=410-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षसुन्दर|पक्षसुन्दरः
पक्षसुन्दर m. (-रः) A sort of tree, commonly Lodh.<BR> E. पक्ष a part, सुन्दर,<BR>handsome.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=410-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षाघात|पक्षाघातः
पक्षाघात m. (-तः)<BR>	 1. Refutation, containing.<BR>	 2. Palsy, hemiplegia.<BR> E. पक्ष,<BR>and आघात a blow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=410-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षान्त|पक्षांत|पक्षान्तः
पक्षान्त m. (-न्तः) The fifteen and last day of either half month, new or<BR>full moon.<BR> E. पक्ष a fortnight, and अन्त end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=410-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षान्तर|पक्षांतर
पक्षान्तर n. (-रं) Another side or part, another view of the argument. E.<BR>पक्ष, and अन्तर difference.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=411-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षाभास|पक्षाभासः
पक्षाभास m. (-सः)<BR>	 1. A seeming or fallacious argument.<BR>	 2. A false<BR>plaint.<BR> E. पक्ष, and आभास semblance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=411-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षालु|पक्षालुः
पक्षालु m. (-लुः) A bird.<BR> E. पक्ष a wing, आलुच् poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=411-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षावसर|पक्षावसरः
पक्षावसर m. (-रः) The last day of either half month, new or full<BR>moon.<BR> E. पक्ष a fortnight, and अवसर conclusion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=411-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षिन्
पक्षिन् mf. (-क्षी-क्षिणी) A bird.<BR>	 m. (-क्षी)<BR>	 1. An arrow.<BR>	 2. An epithet of<BR>Sīva.<BR>	 f. (-णी)<BR>	 1. A night and two days.<BR>	 2. Day of full moon.<BR>3. A female fiend, also called Pūtana.<BR> E. पक्ष a wing, and इनि<BR>poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=411-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षिपानीयशालिका
पक्षिपानीयशालिका f. (-का) A trough for watering birds, cattle, &c. E.<BR>पक्षिन् a bird, पानीय water, शाला a hall, and कन् diminutive aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=411-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षिराज
पक्षिराज m. (-जः) King of the birds, usually applied to Gadura. E.<BR>पक्षिन्, and राज for राजा a king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=411-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षिल|पक्षिलः
पक्षिल m. (-लः) A name of the saint VATSYĀYANA.<BR> E. पक्ष् to take,<BR>इलच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=411-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षिशावक|पक्षिशावकः
पक्षिशावक m. (-कः) A young bird.<BR> E. पक्षिन्, and शावक a young animal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=411-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षिशाला
पक्षिशाला f. (-ला) A nest, an aviary.<BR> E. पक्षिन् a bird, शाला a hall or<BR>house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=411-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षिसिंह|पक्षिसिंहः
पक्षिसिंह m. (-हः) A name of GARUḌA, the bird and vehicle of VIṢṆU.<BR>E. पक्षि for पक्षिन् a bird, सिंह pre-eminent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=411-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षिस्वामिन्
पक्षिस्वामिन् m. (-मी) GARUḌA.<BR> E. पक्षि, and स्वामिन् lord: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=411-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षोद्ग्राहिन्
पक्षोद्ग्राहिन् mfn. (-ही-हिणी-हि) Showing partiality, taking a side. E.<BR>पक्ष, and उट्ग्राहिन् taking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=411-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्ष्णु|पक्ष्णुः
पक्ष्णु mfn. (-क्ष्णुः-क्ष्णुः-क्ष्णु) Who or what cooks or matures.<BR> E. पच् to<BR>ripen, स्नु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=411-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्ष्मन्
पक्ष्मन् n. (-क्ष्म)<BR>	 1. An eyelash.<BR>	 2. The filament of a flower.<BR>	 3. The<BR>point of a thread.<BR>	 4. A wing.<BR> E. पक्ष् to take, मनिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=411-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्ष्य|पक्ष्यः
पक्ष्य mfn. (-क्ष्यः-क्ष्या-क्ष्यं)<BR>	 1. Produced or occurring in a fortnight.<BR>2. Belonging to a side, &c.<BR> E. पक्ष, and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=411-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पङ्क|पंक|पंकं|पंकः|पङ्कः
पङ्क mn. (-ङ्कः-ङ्कं)<BR>	 1. Mud, mire, clay.<BR>	 2. Sin.<BR> E. पचि to spread, aff.<BR>कर्मणि, करणे वा घञ् and च changed to क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=411-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पङ्ककर्व्वट|पङ्ककर्वट|पङ्ककर्वटः|पङ्ककर्व्वटः
पङ्ककर्व्वट m. (-टः) Soft mud, especially such as is left by the retiring<BR>of floods, or on the banks of a river, a marsh, a quagmire. E.<BR>पङ्क mud, कर्व्वट the capital of a district.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=411-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पङ्ककीर|पंककीर|पङ्ककीरः
पङ्ककीर mf. (-रः-री) A lap-wing.<BR> E. पङ्क mud, and कीर a parrot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=411-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पङ्कक्रीड|पंकक्रीड|पङ्कक्रीडः
पङ्कक्रीड mfn. (-डः-डा डं) Wallowing, sporting in mud.<BR>	 m. (-डः) A<BR>pig.<BR> E. पङ्क mud, and क्रीड who sports.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=411-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पङ्कगडक|पङ्कगडकः
पङ्कगडक m. (-कः) A small fish, (Macrognathus Pancalus, HAM.) E.<BR>पङ्क mud, and गडक another fish. (पांँकाल माछ) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=411-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पङ्कगति|पङ्कगतिः
पङ्कगति f. (-तिः) The Pancāl fish: see the last.<BR> E. पङ्क mud, and गति<BR>going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=411-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पङ्खग्राह
पङ्खग्राह m. (-हः) The makara, a marine monster.<BR> E. पङ्क mud, and<BR>ग्राह a shark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=411-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पङ्कज|पंकज|पङ्कजं|पङ्कजः
पङ्कज n. (-जं) A lotus.<BR> E. पङ्क mud, ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=411-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पङ्कजन्मन्|पंकजन्मन्
पङ्कजन्मन् n. (-न्म) A lotus.<BR> E. पङ्क mud, and जन्मन् birth; also पङ्कज,<BR>&c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=411-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पङ्कजिनी|पंकजिनी
पङ्कजिनी f. (-नी) A pool or pond where the lotus grows, or a place<BR>abounding with that flower.<BR>	 2. The flexible stalk of a water-<BR>lily.<BR> E. पङ्कज a lotus, इनि and ङीष् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=411-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पङ्कण|पंकण|पंकणः|पङ्कणः
पङ्कण m. (-णः) The residence of the lowest and most impure tribes.<BR>E. पचि to spread, युच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=411-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पङ्कता
पङ्कता f. (-ता) Muddiness, the nature or property of mud.<BR> E. तल् added<BR>to पङ्क; also with त्व, पङ्कत्व.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=411-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पङ्कधूम
पङ्कधूम m. (-मः) One of the divisions of hell.<BR> E. पङ्ग, and धूम smoke.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=411-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पङ्कप्रभा
पङ्कप्रभा f. (-भा) A hell, the hell of mud or mire.<BR> E. पङ्क, and प्रभा<BR>light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=411-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पङ्कभाज्
पङ्कभाज् mfn. (-क् or -ग्) Sunk in the mire<BR> E. पङ्क, and भाज् what<BR>shares.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=411-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पङ्घभारक
पङ्घभारक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Muddy, laden with mud.<BR> E. पङ्क, and भारक,<BR>burthened.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=411-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पङ्कमण्डुक|पंकमंडुक|पङ्कमण्डुकः
पङ्कमण्डुक m. (-कः) A brivalve-shell.<BR> E. पङ्क mire, मडि to ornament, aff. उक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=411-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पङ्करुह्|पंकरुह्
पङ्करुह् n. (-रुट्) A lotus.<BR> E. पङ्क mud, रुह् to grow, aff. क्किप्; also with क<BR>aff. पङ्करुह n. (-हं) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=411-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पङ्कवास|पंकवास|पङ्कवासः
पङ्कवास m. (-सः) A crab.<BR> E. पङ्क, and वास abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=411-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पङ्कशुक्ति|पङ्कशुक्तिः
पङ्कशुक्ति f. (-क्तिः) A cockle.<BR> E. पङ्क mud, शुक्ति an oyster.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=411-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पङ्कृसूरण
पङ्कृसूरण m. (-ण्णः) The fibrous root of a lotus.<BR> E. पङ्क mud, and सूरण a<BR>sort of root; also written पङ्कशूरण, and पङ्कषूरण्ण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=411-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पङ्कार|पंकार|पंकारः|पङ्कारः
पङ्कार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. An aquatic plant, (Vallisneria.)<BR>	 2. A bridge or rai-<BR>sed bank, forming a path amidst inundated fields.<BR>	 3. Stairs, steps.<BR>4. An aquatic plant, (Trapa bispinosa, Rox.)<BR> E. पङ्क mud, ऋ to go,<BR>अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=411-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पङ्किल|पंकिल|पङ्किलः
पङ्किल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Muddy, clayey.<BR>	 m. (-लः) A boat, a canoe.<BR> E. पङ्क mud, इलच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=411-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पङ्केज|पंकेज|पंकेजं|पङ्केजं
पङ्केज n. (-ज) A lotus.<BR> E. पङ्के in mud, and ज born; also पङ्कज.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=411-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पङ्केरुक्ष
पङ्केरुक्ष n. (-हं) A lotus.<BR>	 m. (-हः) The Indian crane.<BR> E. पङ्के in mud, and<BR>रुह what grows; also पङ्करुह.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=411-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पङ्क्ति|पंक्ति|पंक्तिः|पङ्क्तिः
पङ्क्ति f. (-ङ्क्तिः-ङ्क्ती)<BR>	 1. A line, a row or range.<BR>	 2. A sort of metre, a<BR>stanza of four lines, each line consisting of ten syllables.<BR>	 3. The<BR>number “ten,” (in composition, ut infra.)<BR>	 4. The earth.<BR>	 5. Fame,<BR>celebrity.<BR>	 6. Cooking, maturing.<BR>	 7. Associating with, eating or<BR>sitting with, especially with persons of the same caste.<BR>	 8. A com-<BR>pany, a society, an assembly.<BR> E. पचि to spread, to extended, to<BR>make evident, and क्तिन् aff. or पच् to cook, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=411-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पङ्क्तिग्रीव|पंक्तिग्रीव|पङ्क्तिग्रीवः
पङ्क्तिग्रीव m. (-वः) A name of RĀVANA.<BR> E. पङ्क्ति ten, ग्रीवा a neck,<BR>the ten-necked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=411-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पङ्क्तिचर|पंक्तिचर|पङ्क्तिचरः
पङ्क्तिचर m. (-रः) An ospray.<BR> E. पङ्क्ति, and चर who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=411-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पङ्क्तिदूषक|पंक्तिदूषक|पङ्क्तिदूषकः
पङ्क्तिदूषक m. (-कः) An improper person to associate with, an outcaste.<BR>E. पङ्क्ति, and दूषक who spoils.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=411-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पङ्क्तिपावन|पंक्तिपावन|पङ्क्तिपावनः
पङ्क्तिपावन m. (-नः) A respectable or eminent person.<BR> E. पङ्क्ति, and<BR>पावन who purifies.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=411-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पङ्क्तिरथ|पंक्तिरथ|पङ्क्तिरथः
पङ्क्तिरथ m. (-थः) DAŚARAṬHA, the father of RĀMA.<BR> E. पङ्क्ति ten,<BR>(sides) and रथ a car, whose car goes on all sides.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=411-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पङ्गु|पंगु|पङ्गुः
पङ्गु mfn. (-ङ्गु-ङ्गुः-ङ्गु) Lame, crippled, halt, one who has lost his<BR>legs, &c.<BR>	 m. (-ङ्गुः) The planet Saturn.<BR> E. पण् to engage in busi-<BR>ness, उ aff, and अङ्गु substituted for the radical final. खजि-कु-<BR>पगादेशः नुक् च ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=411-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पङ्गुल|पंगुल|पङ्गुलः
पङ्गुल m. (-लः) A horse of a glassy or silvery white colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=411-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पङ्गुग्राह|पंगुग्राह|पङ्गुग्राहः
पङ्गुग्राह m. (-हः) One of the signs of the zodiac: see मकर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=411-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पङ्गुता
पङ्गुता f. (-ता) Deformity, mutilation.<BR> E. तल् added to पङ्गु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=411-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पच|पचः
पच (डु, ष्) डुपचस् r. 1st. cl. (पचति) To mature by cooking or ripen-<BR>ing, to boil, to dress, to ripen; (इ) पचि r. 1st. and 10th. cls.<BR>(पचति-ते पचयति)<BR>	 1. To make evident or apparent.<BR>	 2. To represent,<BR>to state fully.<BR>	 3. To spread.<BR> E. पाके भ्वा० उभ० सक० अनिट् । व्यक्तीकारे<BR>भ्वा० आत्म० अनिट् । विस्तारे चु० उभ० सक० सेट् इदित् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=411-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पच|पचः
पच mfn. (-चः-चा-चं) Who or what cooks, matures, &c.<BR>	 m. (-चः) Cook-<BR>ing, maturing, &c.<BR> E. पच् to cook, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=411-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पचक|पचकः
पचक m. (-कः) A cook.<BR> E. पच् to cook, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=411-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पचत्
पचत् mfn. (-चन्-चन्ती-चत्) Cooking, ripening.<BR> E. पच् to cook, partici-<BR>pial aff. शतृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=411-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पचत|पचतः
पचत m. (-तः)<BR>	 1. The sun.<BR>	 2. Fire.<BR>	 3. A name of INDRA.<BR> E. पच् to<BR>cook or ripen, Unādi aff. अतच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=411-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पचतिकल्प|पचतिकल्पं
पचतिकल्प mfn. (-ल्पः-ल्पा-ल्पं) or adv.<BR>	 n. (-ल्पं) Almost cooked or ripened.<BR>E. पचति what cooks, and कल्प aff.; implying incompleteness;<BR>also in a similar sense, पचतिदेश्य and पचतिदेशीय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=411-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पचत्पुट|पचत्पुटः
पचत्पुट m. (-टः) A tree, (Hibiscus phæniceus.)<BR> E. पचत् here side to<BR>mean the sun, and पुट् to shine, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=411-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पचन|पचनं|पचनः
पचन mfn. (-नः-ना-नी-नं) What cooks or matures, &c.<BR>	 n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Cook-<BR>ing, dressing, boiling.<BR>	 2. Maturing.<BR>	 m. (-नः) Fire.<BR> E. पच् to<BR>cook, aff. युच् or कर्त्तरि-ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=411-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पचमान|पचमानः
पचमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Cooking, in the act of cooking or ripening.<BR>E. पच् to cook, &c. and शानच् aff., मुक् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=412-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पचम्पचा|पचंपचा
पचम्पचा f. (-चा) A species of Curcuma, (C. zanthorhizon.)<BR> E. पच् to<BR>cook, reiterated, अच् aff. and मुम् inserted; it is also read<BR>पचम्बचा. पचं पाचकं पचति पच-वा० खस्-मुम् । दारुहरिद्रायाम ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=412-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पचा
पचा f. (-चा) Cooking, dressing, maturing.<BR> E. पच् to dress, affs. अङ्<BR>and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=412-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पचि|पचिः
पचि m. (-चिः)<BR>	 1. Fire.<BR>	 2. Cooking, maturing.<BR> E. पच् to be cooked,<BR>(by it,) इन् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=412-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पचेलिम|पचेलिमः
पचेलिम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं) Fit to cook or ripen of itself.<BR>	 m. (-मः)<BR>	 1. The<BR>sun.<BR>	 2. Fire.<BR> E. पच् to dress or ripen, केलिम्न् aff. of the reflec-<BR>tive form, or Unādi aff. एलिमच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=412-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पचेलुक|पचेलुकः
पचेलुक m. (-कः) A cook<BR> E. पच, and एलुक aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=412-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पच्छस्
पच्छस् ind. Foot by foot, or stanza by stanza.<BR> E. पत् for पाद, and<BR>शस् aff. of several orders.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=412-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पच्यमान|पच्यमानः
पच्यमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Being in the act of ripening, cooking &c.<BR>E. पच् to cook, pass, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=412-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पज्ज|पज्जः
पज्ज m. (-ज्जः) A Śūdra.<BR> E. पत् for पाद a foot, and ज born, from the<BR>feet of BRAMHĀ. पद्भ्यां जायते जन-ड ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=412-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चक|पंचक|पञ्चकं|पञ्चकः
पञ्चक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Five or relating to five, made of five, bought<BR>with five, &c.<BR>	 m. (-कः) Any collection or aggregate of five, a<BR>five.<BR>	 n. (-कं) A field of battle.<BR> E. पञ्च five, and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=412-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चकपाल|पञ्चकपालः
पञ्चकपाल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) A particular ceremony in which ghee is<BR>offered in five cups.<BR> E. पञ्च five, कपाल a concave piece of<BR>pottery skull-shaped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=412-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चकर्म्मन्|पञ्चकर्मन्|पंचकर्मन्
पञ्चकर्म्मन् n. (-र्म्म) Five actions of the body, viz. vomiting, evacuation by<BR>bleeding or by stool, diseased excretion of fæces or purging, and<BR>blowing the nose.<BR> E. पञ्च five, कर्म्मन् an act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=412-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चकृत्वस्|पंचकृत्वस्
पञ्चकृत्वस् ind. Five times.<BR> E. पञ्च, and कृत्वसुच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=412-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चकोण|पंचकोण|पञ्चकोणः
पञ्चकोण m. (-णः) A pentagon.<BR> E. पञ्च, and कोण an angle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=412-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चकोल|पंचकोल|पञ्चकोलं
पञ्चकोल n. (-लं) The aggregate of five spices. viz. Long pepper, its<BR>root, Chai or Piper Chavya, Plumbago, and dry ginger.<BR> E. पञ्च<BR>five, and कोल pepper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=412-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चकोषा
पञ्चकोषा m. plu. (-षा) The five sheathes supposed to invest the soul, or<BR>the Annamaya kosha, that supported by food, the gross form; the<BR>Prānamaya kosha, the organs of action; the Manomaya Kosha,<BR>the organs of perception, with the manas or mind; Vijnānamaya,<BR>the same with the Buddhi or intellect; and the Anandamaya, con-<BR>sisting of the elements of identity and divine wisdom.<BR> E. पञ्च, and<BR>कोष a sheath.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=412-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चखट्व|पंचखट्व|पञ्चखट्वं
पञ्चखट्व nf. (-ट्व-ट्वी) A collection of five beds.<BR> E. पञ्च five, and खट्रा bed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=412-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चगव|पंचगव|पञ्चगवं
पञ्चगव n. (-वं) A collection of five cows.<BR> E. पञ्च, and गौ a cow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=412-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चगवधन|पञ्चगवधनः
पञ्चगवधन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Having five cows.<BR> E. पञ्चगव, and धन wealth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=412-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चगव्य|पंचगव्य|पञ्चगव्यं
पञ्चगव्य n. (-व्यं) Five articles derived from the cow; viz. milk, curds,<BR>clarified butter, cow's urine, and cow-dung.<BR> E. पञ्च five, and गव्य<BR>from गौ a cow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=412-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चगुण|पंचगुण
पञ्चगुण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Five times, five-fold.<BR> E. पञ्च, and गुण multiply-<BR>ing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=412-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चगुप्त|पंचगुप्त|पञ्चगुप्तः
पञ्चगुप्त m. (-प्तः)<BR>	 1. A tortoise, a turtle.<BR>	 2. The atheistical system of the<BR>Bauddhas.<BR> E. पञ्च five, (members, &c.) गुप्त concealed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=412-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चगो
पञ्चगो mfn. (-गौः-गौः-गु) Bought with five cows.<BR> E. पञ्च, and गो a cow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=412-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चचामर|पञ्चचामरं
पञ्चचामर n. (-रं) A form of metre, in which the line contains sixteen<BR>syllables.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=412-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चचीर|पञ्चचीरः
पञ्चचीर m. (-रः) A Bauddha saint and legislator; also named MANju-<BR>GHOSA, apparently the teacher of this doctrine in Nepal.<BR> E. पञ्च<BR>spreading, चीर rags.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=412-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चचूडा
पञ्चचूडा f. (-डा) One of the nymphs of heaven.<BR> E. पञ्च, and चूडा a top<BR>knot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=412-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चजन|पंचजन|पञ्चजनः
पञ्चजन m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. Man is general, a man.<BR>	 2. The name of a demon,<BR>whose bones became the Conch Pānchajanya, the shell of<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=412-b" target="_blank">Page412-b+ 60</a>]<BR>KṚṢṆA.<BR>	 f. (-नी) An assemblage of five persons<BR> E. पञ्च five,<BR>(elements,) and जन who is born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=412-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चजनीन|पंचजनीन|पञ्चजनीनः
पञ्चजनीन m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. An actor, a mimic, a buffoon.<BR>	 2. The chief of five<BR>men,<BR> E. पञ्च five, and जन a man, or पञ्चजन man, and ख aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=412-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चज्ञान|पंचज्ञान|पञ्चज्ञानः
पञ्चज्ञान m. (-नः) A Buddha or Bauddha sanctified teacher.<BR> E. पञ्च five<BR>(organs,) and ज्ञान knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=412-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चत्|पंचत्
पञ्चत् mfn. (-ञ्चत्) Five.<BR> E. पचि to spread, अति aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=412-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चतक्ष|पंचतक्ष|पञ्चतक्षं
पञ्चतक्ष nf. (-क्षं-क्षी) An assemblage of five carpenters.<BR> E. पञ्च, and तक्ष<BR>a carpenter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=412-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चतत्व|पंचतत्व
पञ्चतत्व mn. (-त्वः-त्वं)<BR>	 1. The five elements collectively.<BR>	 2. (In the Tan-<BR>tras,) The five essentials of certain rites; or wine meat, fish,<BR>sexual intercourse, and mystic gesticulations.<BR> E. पञ्च, and तत्व<BR>an element.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=412-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चतन्मात्र|पञ्चतन्मात्रं
पञ्चतन्मात्र n. (त्रं) The five subtile rudiments of the five elements. E.<BR>पञ्च, and तन्मात्र element.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=412-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चतपस्|पंचतपस्
पञ्चतपस् m. (-पाः) An ascetic, who in the hot weather, sits amongst<BR>four fires, and has the sun for the fifth.<BR> E. पञ्च, and तपस् penance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=412-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चतय|पंचतय|पञ्चतयं|पञ्चतयः
पञ्चतय mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>	 1. Having five parts or limbs.<BR>	 2. Five.<BR> E. पञ्च<BR>five, and तयप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=412-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चता|पंचता
पञ्चता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Death, dying, (i. e.) the separation of the five elements<BR>of whose aggregate the body consists.<BR>	 2. The nature or condition<BR>of five, the aggregate of five or five times.<BR>	 3. The five elements<BR>collectively, earth, air, fire, water, and Akās.<BR> E. पञ्च five, and तल्<BR>abstract aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=412-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चतीर्थी
पञ्चतीर्थी f. (-र्थी)<BR>	 1. Any five principal places of pilgrimage, especially<BR>Visrānti, Saukara, Naimisha, Prayāga and Pushkara.<BR>	 2. Bathing<BR>on the day of the equinox.<BR> E. पञ्च, and तीर्थ a shrine, affix ङीप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=412-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चत्व|पंचत्व|पंचत्वं|पञ्चत्वं
पञ्चत्व n. (-त्वं)<BR>	 1. Death.<BR>	 2. The state or being of five.<BR>	 3. The co-existence<BR>of the five elements.<BR>	 4. An aggregate, &c. of five.<BR> E. पञ्च five, and<BR>त्व aff.; see पञ्चता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=412-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चथु|पंचथु|पंचथुः|पञ्चथुः
पञ्चथु m. (-थुः)<BR>	 1. Time.<BR>	 2. The Kokila or Indian cuckoo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=412-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चदश|पंचदश|पञ्चदशः
पञ्चदश mfn. (-शः-शी-शं) Fifteen or fifteenth.<BR>	 f. (-शी) The fifteenth day<BR>of a half month, full or new moon.<BR> E. पञ्च five, दशन् ten, aff. डट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=412-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चदशन्|पंचदशन्
पञ्चदशन् mfn. plu. (-श) Fifteen.<BR> E. पञ्च five, and दशन् ten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=412-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चदीर्घ|पंचदीर्घ|पञ्चदीर्घं
पञ्चदीर्घ m. (-र्घः) Marks on five parts of the body, the arms, eyes, belly,<BR>nose, and breast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=412-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चधा|पंचधा
पञ्चधा ind. In five ways, five-fold.<BR> E. पञ्चन् five, and धा aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=412-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चन्|पंचन्
पञ्चन् mfn. plu. (-ञ्च) Five.<BR> E. पचि to spread, Unādi aff. कनिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=412-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चनख|पंचनख|पञ्चनखः
पञ्चनख m. (-खः)<BR>	 1. An elephant.<BR>	 2. A tortoise.<BR>	 3. A tiger.<BR>	 4. Any<BR>animal having five toes or claws.<BR>	 f. (-खी) A lizard.<BR> E. पञ्च five, नख<BR>a nail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=412-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चनद|पंचनद|पञ्चनदः
पञ्चनद m. (-दः) The Panjāb, or country of five rivers, viz. the Sata-<BR>drū, Vipāsā, Irāvati, Chandrabhāgā and Vitasthā.<BR> E. पञ्च,<BR>नदी a river, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=412-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चनिम्ब|पञ्चनिम्बं
पञ्चनिम्ब n. (-म्बं) Five parts of the Nimba tree:--the flowers, fruit,<BR>leaves, bark, and root.<BR> E. पञ्च five, and निम्ब the Nimba, tree,<BR>(Melia azadiracta).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=412-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चनी|पंचनी
पञ्चनी f. (-नी) A chequered cloth for playing at draughts, chess, &c.<BR>E. पञ्च five, नी to get, aff. क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=412-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चनीराजन|पंचनीराजन|पञ्चनीराजनं
पञ्चनीराजन n. (-नं) Waving four things before an idol; a lamp, a lotus,<BR>cloth, a mango or betel leaf, and then falling prostrate.<BR> E. पञ्च,<BR>and नीराजन presentation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=412-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चपञ्चनख
पञ्चपञ्चनख m. (-खः) Five kinds of animals allowed to be killed and<BR>eaten, the hare, porcupine, alligator, rhinoceros, and tortoise. E.<BR>पञ्च, and पञ्चनख a five-toed animal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=412-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चपल्लव|पञ्चपल्लवं
पञ्चपल्लव n. (-वं) The aggregate of five sprouts; six. of the spondias,<BR>rose-apple, Bel or marmelos, citron, and wood apple.<BR> E. पञ्च five,<BR>and पल्लव a new shoot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=412-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चपर्णी
पञ्चपर्णी f. (-र्णी) A small shrub.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=412-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चपात्र|पंचपात्र|पञ्चपात्रं
पञ्चपात्र n. (-त्रं)<BR>	 1. Five plates collectively.<BR>	 2. A Srāddha in which<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=413-a" target="_blank">Page413-a+ 60</a>]<BR>offerings are made in five vessels.<BR> E. पञ्च five, and पात्र a vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=412-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चप्राण|पंचप्राण
पञ्चप्राण m. plu. (-णाः) The five airs supposed to be in the body, and<BR>necessary to life. viz:--प्राण, अपान, व्यान, उदान, समान ।<BR> E. पञ्च, and<BR>प्राण vital air.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=413-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चप्रासाद|पञ्चप्रासादः
पञ्चप्रासाद m. (-दः) A temple with four pinnacles and a steeple. E.<BR>पञ्च, and प्रासाद a palace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=413-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चबन्ध|पञ्चबन्धः
पञ्चबन्ध m. (-न्धः) A fine equal to the fifth part of any thing lost or<BR>stolen.<BR> E. पञ्च five, and बन्ध binding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=413-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चभद्र|पञ्चभद्रः
पञ्चभद्र mfn. (-द्रःद्री-द्रं) A horse with five auspicious marks; or spotted<BR>on the chest, back, face, and flanks.<BR>	 n. (-द्रं) A sauce or condiment<BR>of five vegetables.<BR> E. पञ्च five, and भद्र fortunate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=413-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चभूत|पंचभूत|पञ्चभूतं
पञ्चभूत mn. (-तः-तं) The five elements; earth, air, fire, water, Ākās.<BR>E. पञ्च, and भूत an element.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=413-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चभूतात्मन्
पञ्चभूतात्मन् m. (-त्मा) Man as formed of the five elements.<BR> E. पञ्चभूत,<BR>and आत्मन् one with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=413-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चम|पंचम|पञ्चमं|पञ्चमः
पञ्चम mfn. (-मः-मी-मं)<BR>	 1. Fifth.<BR>	 2. Beautiful, pleasing.<BR>	 3. Dexterous, cle-<BR>ver.<BR>	 m. (-मः)<BR>	 1. The fifth note of the Hindu musical scale. It is<BR>called Panchama, from being said to be formed by air drawn<BR>from five places; the navel, the breast, the heart, the throat, and<BR>forehead.<BR>	 2. One of the RĀGAS or modes of music.<BR>	 f. (-मी)<BR>	 1.<BR>A name of DRAUPADĪ, the wife of the five Pāndus.<BR>	 2. A che-<BR>quered cloth for playing at draughts, &c. a chess board.<BR>	 3. The<BR>fifth day of a half month.<BR>	 4. The ablative case, (in gram.)<BR>	 n.<BR>(-मं)<BR>	 1. The fifth.<BR>	 2. Sexual intercourse.<BR> E. पञ्चन् five, and डटि aff.<BR>with मट augment; or पञ्चपतीन् मिनोति वध्नाति प्रेम्णा । मी-वन्धे ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=413-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चमकार|पंचमकार|पञ्चमकारं
पञ्चमकार n. (-रं) The five essentials of the left hand Tantra ritual;<BR>“Madya” wine, “Maṃsa” flesh, “Matsya” fish, “Maithuna” copu-<BR>lation, “Mudra” gesticulation.<BR> E. पञ्च, and मकार the letter M;<BR>all beginning with that letter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=413-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चमवत्|पञ्चमवन्त्
पञ्चमवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Having the fifth of any thing.<BR> E. पञ्चम,<BR>and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=413-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चमहापातक|पंचमहापातक
पञ्चमहापातक n. (कं) The five great sins. They are thus described in<BR>Vāchaspatya. viz:--<BR>ब्रह्महत्या सुरापानं स्तेयं गुर्वङ्गनागमः ।<BR>महान्ति पातकान्याहुः संसर्गश्चापि तैः सह ॥<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=413-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चमहायज्ञ|पंचमहायज्ञ
पञ्चमहायज्ञ m. plu. (-ज्ञाः) The five great sacraments of the Hindus,<BR>or the worship of spirits, progenitors, gods, Vedas, and man-<BR>kind, by offerings of perfumes and flowers, obsequial rites,<BR>oblations with fire, the study of the Vedas, and hospitality. E.<BR>पञ्च five, महा great, and यज्ञ sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=413-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चमार|पञ्चमारः
पञ्चमार m. (-रः) The son of BALADEVA. पञ्चविधकामे च ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=413-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चमाषिक
पञ्चमाषिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Of five Māshas, relating to, worth, amount-<BR>ing to five Māshas.<BR> E. पञ्च, माष a measure of silver, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=413-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चमास्य|पंचमास्य|पञ्चमास्यः
पञ्चमास्य m. (-स्यः) The Kokila or Indian cuckoo.<BR> E. पञ्चम, the musical<BR>note, and आस्य mouth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=413-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चमिन्|पंचमिन्
पञ्चमिन् mfn. (-मी-मिनी-मि) Being in the fifth year of one's age. E.<BR>पञ्चम, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=413-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चमुख|पंचमुख|पञ्चमुखः
पञ्चमुख m. (-खः)<BR>	 1. A name of SĪVA.<BR>	 2. A lion.<BR> E. पञ्च five, and मुख face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=413-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चमुद्रा
पञ्चमुद्रा f. (-द्रा) Five gestures to be made in the usual presentation<BR>of offerings to an idol.<BR> E. पञ्च, and मुद्रा gesture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=413-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चमूत्र|पञ्चमूत्रं
पञ्चमूत्र n. (-त्रं) The urine of the cow, goat, sheep, buffalo, and ass.<BR>E. पञ्च, and मूत्र urine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=413-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चमूल|पञ्चमूलं
पञ्चमूल n. (-लं) The assemblage of five roots, viz:--The Bel, Premna longi-<BR>folia, Cassia, Gmelian arborea, and the Trumpet flower.<BR>	 f. (-ली)<BR>A similar aggregate of five roots, considered as the similar one,<BR>viz:--Hedysarum gangeticum, H. logopodioides, Solanum melon-<BR>gena, S. Jacquini, and Tribulus lanuginosus.<BR> E. पञ्च five, मूल a<BR>root; the fem. aff. has a diminutive import.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=413-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चयज्ञ
पञ्चयज्ञ m. plu, (-ज्ञाः) The five rites of a house-keeper: see पञ्चमहायज्ञ ।<BR>E. पञ्च, and यज्ञ a sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=413-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चरत्न|पंचरत्न|पञ्चरत्नं
पञ्चरत्न n. (-त्नं) A collection of five precious objects; viz:--Gold, a<BR>diamond, a pearl, a ruby, an amethyst.<BR> E. पञ्च and रत्न a gem. For<BR>particulars see Vāchaspatya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=413-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चरसा
पञ्चरसा f. (-सा) Emblic myrobalan.<BR> E. पञ्च five, रस flavour, taste. (आम्लकी)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=413-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चलक्षण|पंचलक्षण|पञ्चलक्षणं
पञ्चलक्षण n. (-णं) A Purāna or mythological poem.<BR> E. पञ्च five, and<BR>लक्षण a mark; Puraṇa should comprehend five topics; the<BR>creation of worlds, their destruction and renovation, the genea-<BR>logy of gods and heroes, the reigns of the MANUS, and the ac-<BR>tions of their descendants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=413-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चलवण|पंचलवण|पञ्चलवणं
पञ्चलवण n. (-णं) Five kinds of salt.<BR> E. पञ्च, and लवण salt. viz:--<BR>काचकं सैन्धवं चैव सामुद्रं विडमेवच ।<BR>सौवर्चल तथा पञ्चलवणं परिकीर्त्तितम् ॥<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=413-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चलाङ्गलक|पञ्चलाङ्गलकं
पञ्चलाङ्गलक n. (-कं) Gift of land to the extent requiring five ploughs.<BR>E. पञ्च, लाङ्गल a plough, कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=413-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चलोह|पञ्चलोहं
पञ्चलोह n. (-हं) A metallic alloy containing five metals; copper, brass,<BR>tin, lead, and iron.<BR> E. पञ्च five, and लोह iron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=413-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चवक्त्र|पंचवक्त्र|पञ्चवक्त्रः
पञ्चवक्त्र m. (-क्त्रा)<BR>	 1. ŚIVA.<BR>	 2. A lion.<BR> E. पञ्च five, and वक्त्र a face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=413-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चवट|पञ्चवटः
पञ्चवट m. (-टः) The Brāhminical thread as worn across the breast; also<BR>पञ्चावट.<BR>	 f. (-टी)<BR>	 1. Five fig-trees, viz:--the Indian and the holy fig,<BR>the Bel, Grislea tomentosa, Rox. (धात्री) and Asoka, placed or plan-<BR>ted in several quarters; viz. east, west, north, south and south-<BR>east.<BR>	 2. Part of the great southern or Dandaka forest where<BR>the Godāvari rises.<BR> E. पञ्च, and वट the Indian fig.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=413-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चवर्ग|पञ्चवर्गः
पञ्चवर्ग m. (-र्गः) A class of five persons or things.<BR> E. पञ्च, and वर्ग<BR>a class.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=413-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चवल्कल|पंचवल्कल|पञ्चवल्कलं
पञ्चवल्कल n. (-लं) A collection of the bark of five trees, the Indian<BR>and the holy fig, the opposite-leaved fig, the wavy-leaved fig,<BR>and a sort of reed; other trees are sometimes taken.<BR> E. पञ्च five,<BR>and वल्कल a bark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=413-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चवाण|पंचवाण|पञ्चवाणः
पञ्चवाण m. (-णः) KĀMADEVA, The Indian Cupid.<BR> E. पञ्च five, and<BR>वाण an arrow; being armed with five arrows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=413-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चशर|पंचशर|पञ्चशरः
पञ्चशर m. (-रः) KĀMADEva.<BR> E. पञ्च five, and शर an arrow: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=413-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चशाख|पंचशाख|पञ्चशाखः
पञ्चशाख m. (-खः)<BR>	 1. The hand.<BR>	 2. An elephant.<BR> E. पञ्च five, शाखा a<BR>branch, the five-fingered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=413-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चशिख|पंचशिख|पञ्चशिखः
पञ्चशिख m. (-खः)<BR>	 1. A lion.<BR>	 2. The name of a Muni, the son of DHA-<BR>RMA by HINSĀ.<BR> E. पञ्च spreading, शिखा a crest or mane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=413-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चशैरीषक|पञ्चशैरीषकं
पञ्चशैरीषक n. (-कं) The bark of five trees.<BR> E. पञ्च, and शिरीष Mimosa<BR>sirisha, ठञ् aff. शिरीषवृक्षस्य पुष्पमूलफलपत्रवल्कलेषुच ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=413-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चष|पंचष
पञ्चष mfn. plu. (-षाः-षाः-षाणि) Five or six.<BR> E. पञ्च, and षष् six, with<BR>डच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=413-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चसुगन्धक|पञ्चसुगन्धकं
पञ्चसुगन्धक n. (-कं) The aggregate of five aromatic vegetable substances;<BR>cloves, nutmeg, camphor, aloe wood, and Kakkola.<BR> E. पञ्च five,<BR>सुगन्ध fragrance, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=413-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चसूना|पंचसूना
पञ्चसूना m. plu. (-नाः) The five things in a house by which animal life may<BR>be accidentally destroyed; viz:--the fire place, the slab on which<BR>condiments are ground, the broom, the pestle and mortar, and<BR>the waterpot.<BR> E. पञ्च five, and सूना place of slaughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=413-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चाग्नि|पंचाग्नि|पञ्चाग्निः
पञ्चाग्नि n. (-ग्नि)<BR>	 1. A collection of five fires, amidst which a devotee<BR>performs penance during the summer season; or four fires light-<BR>ed severally to the north, south, east and west, and the sun over<BR>head.<BR>	 2. Five mystic fires, supposed to be present in the body.<BR>m. (-ग्निः)<BR>	 1. A householder who maintains five fires, or the do-<BR>mestic one, and one for warming visitors in addition to the<BR>other three.<BR>	 2. One who is acquainted with the doctrine of the<BR>five mystic fires. viz:--अन्वाहार्य्य, पचन, गार्हपत्य, आहवनीय, सभ्य and<BR>आवसथ्य ।<BR> E. पञ्च five, and अग्नि fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=413-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चाङ्ग|पंचांग|पञ्चाङ्गं|पञ्चाङ्गः
पञ्चाङ्ग mfn. (-ङ्गः-ङ्गी-ङ्गं) Having five limbs or members, five parts<BR>or subdivisions, consisting of five things, &c.<BR>	 n. (-ङ्गं)<BR>	 1. Any<BR>aggregate of five parts or five things.<BR>	 2. Five modes of dovo-<BR>tion; viz:--silent prayer, burnt offering, libations, bathing idols,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=414-a" target="_blank">Page414-a+ 60</a>]<BR>and feeding Brāhmans.<BR>	 3. An almanack describing solar days,<BR>lunar days, and the periods of asterisms, Yogas and Karanas.<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>	 1. A tortoise.<BR>	 2. A species of horse with five spots on<BR>his body: see पञ्चभद्र.<BR>	 3. Reverence by extending the hands, bending<BR>the knees and head, and in speech and look.<BR> E. पञ्च five, अङ्ग body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=413-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चाङ्गगुप्त|पंचांगगुप्त|पञ्चाङ्गगुप्तः
पञ्चाङ्गगुप्त m. (-प्तः) A tortoise.<BR> E. पञ्च five, अङ्ग limb, and गुप्त hidden;<BR>covering his head and legs beneath his shell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=414-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चाङ्गुल|पंचांगुल|पञ्चाङ्गुलः
पञ्चाङ्गुल mfn. (-लः-ला-ली-लं) Measuring five fingers.<BR>	 m. (-लः) The<BR>castor-oil plant.<BR> E. पञ्च five, अङ्गुलि a finger, aff. अच्: the leaves<BR>having five lobes compared to fingers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=414-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चाङ्गुलि|पञ्चाङ्गुलिः
पञ्चाङ्गुलि mfn. (-लिः-लिः-लि) Having five fingers, or finger-like divisions.<BR>E. पञ्च five, अङ्गुलि a finger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=414-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चातपा
पञ्चातपा f. (-पा) Doing penance with five fires, or four fires and the sun.<BR> E. पञ्च, and आतप heat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=414-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चानन|पंचानन|पञ्चाननः
पञ्चानन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Very passionate.<BR>	 m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. A name of SĪVA.<BR>2. (With the mouth wide open) A lion.<BR>	 3. A title used at the end<BR>of the names of learned men to express veneration or high scho-<BR>larship.<BR> E. पञ्च five or spreading, आनन a face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=414-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चामृत|पंचामृत|पञ्चामृतं
पञ्चामृत n. (-तं)<BR>	 1. A mixture of milk, curds, sugar, ghee, and honey.<BR>2. The aggregate of any five drugs of supposed efficacy.<BR> E. पञ्च,<BR>and अमृत ambrosia.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=414-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चाम्नाय|पञ्चाम्नायः
पञ्चाम्नाय m. plu. (-याः) Five Shāstras supposed to have proceeded from<BR>the five mouths of SĪVA, constituting the basis of the Tantra<BR>ritual.<BR> E. पञ्च, and आम्नाय a scripture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=414-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चाम्ल|पञ्चाम्लं
पञ्चाम्ल n. (-म्लं) The aggregate of five acid plants; the jujube, prome-<BR>granate, sorrel, spondias, and citron.<BR> E. पञ्च five, and अम्ल sour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=414-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चारी
पञ्चारी f. (-री) A chequered cloth for playing draughts upon: see पञ्चाली.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=414-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चार्च्चिस
पञ्चार्च्चिस m. (-र्च्चिः) The planet Mercury.<BR> E. पञ्च five, अर्च्चिस् a ray.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=414-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चाल|पंचाल|पञ्चालः
पञ्चाल m. (लः)<BR>	 1. A country in the north of India.<BR>	 2. It may either be<BR>applied to its people or their king.<BR>	 f. (-ली)<BR>	 1. A chequered cloth for<BR>playing at draughts, &c.<BR>	 2. A doll, a puppet.<BR>	 3. A style of singing.<BR>E. पचि to spread, Unādi aff. कालन्; also with कन् added पञ्चालिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=414-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चावट|पञ्चावटं|पंचावटः|पञ्चावटः
पञ्चावट m. (-टः) The sacrificial cord, as worn crossed upon the breast,<BR>the ends hanging over the shoulders.<BR> E. पञ्च spreading, वट् to<BR>surround, aff. अच्, आङ् prefixed to the root; also पञ्चवट ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=414-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चावस्थ|पंचावस्थ|पञ्चावस्थः
पञ्चावस्थ m. (-स्थः) A corpse.<BR> E. पञ्च five, (elements,) अवस्था state or<BR>condition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=414-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चाशत्|पंचाशत्
पञ्चाशत् f. (-शत्) Fifty.<BR> E. पञ्च, with शत् aff. and आ augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=414-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चास्य|पंचास्य|पञ्चास्यः
पञ्चास्य mf. (-स्यः-स्या)<BR>	 1. A lion.<BR>	 2. SĪVA,<BR> E. पञ्च spreading, and आस्य a face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=414-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चेन्द्रिय|पंचेंद्रिय|पञ्चेन्द्रियं
पञ्चेन्द्रिय n. (-यं)<BR>	 1. The five organs of sense; the eye, ear, nose, tongue,<BR>and skin; or those of action, as hands, feet, windpipe, anus, and<BR>parts of generation.<BR> E. पञ्च five, and इन्द्रिय an organ of sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=414-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चेषु|पंचेषु|पञ्चेषुः
पञ्चेषु m. (-षुः) A name of KĀMADEVA, the Hindu Cupid.<BR> E. पञ्च five,<BR>इषु an arrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=414-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चेष्मन्
पञ्चेष्मन् m. plu. (-ष्माणः) The five digestive fires supposed to be in the body.<BR> E. पञ्च, and उष्मन् heat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=414-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प|पं|पः
प(पि)ञ्जर mn. (-रः-रं) A skeleton.<BR>	 n. (-रं)<BR>	 1. A cage, an aviary, a dove-cot.<BR>2. The ribs.<BR>	 m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. The body.<BR>	 2. The Kali age.<BR> E. पजि for<BR>पिजि to dwell, &c. Unādi aff. अरच्; also पिञ्जर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=414-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्जराखेट|पंजराखेट|पञ्जराखेटः
पञ्जराखेट m. (-टः) A sort of basket or wicker trap in which fish are<BR>caught.<BR> E. पञ्जर a cage, आखेट hunting. “पोलो” इति भाषा ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=414-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्जि|पंजि|पंजिः|पञ्जिः
पञ्जि(ञ्जी) f. (-ञ्जिः-ञ्जी)<BR>	 1. The ball or whisp of cotton from which thread is<BR>spun.<BR>	 2. A journal, a register.<BR>	 3. An almanack.<BR> E. पजि for पिजि<BR>to touch, &c. aff. इन् and ङीष् optionally added; also पिञ्जि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=414-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्जिका|पंजिका
पञ्जिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. The ball or skein of cotton from which thread is<BR>spun: see the last.<BR>	 2. A perpetual commentary.<BR>	 3. A calendar,<BR>an almanack.<BR>	 4. A journal, a register.<BR>	 5. The register or journal<BR>of YAMA, the record of human actions.<BR> E. स्वार्थेक added to पञ्जि;<BR>also पञ्जीका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=414-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्जिकाकारक|पञ्जिकाकारकः
पञ्जिकाकारक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A writer, a man of the Kāyastha tribe.<BR>	 2.<BR>An almanack-maker.<BR> E. पञ्जिका a journal, &c. and कारक who<BR>makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=414-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्जीकर|पञ्जीकरः
पञ्जीकर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. The Kāyastha or scribe.<BR>	 2. An almanack-maker. E.<BR>पञ्जी a journal, &c. कर who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=414-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पट|पटं|पटः
पट r. 1st cl. (पटति) To go, to move. r. 10th cl. (पटयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To string.<BR>2. To surround or encompass.<BR>	 3. To share, to portion, to distri-<BR>bute. (पाटयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To speak.<BR>	 2. To shine. With उत् prefixed,<BR>To pluck up, to eradicate, to destroy utterly. With वि, To fly,<BR>to run away. गतौ भ्वा० पर० सक० सेट् । दीप्तौ० चू० उभ० अक० सेट् ।<BR>वेष्टने, अद० चु० उभ० सक० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=414-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पट|पटं|पटः
पट mn. (-टः-टं)<BR>	 1. Fine cloth.<BR>	 2. Coloured cloth.<BR>	 3. A leaf or sheet<BR>of cloth, &c. on which any figures may be painted.<BR>	 4. A veil or<BR>screen.<BR>	 5. A tablet for writing or painting.<BR>	 m. (-टः)<BR>	 1. A<BR>kind of tree: see पियाल.<BR>	 2. Any thing well made or polished.<BR>	 f.<BR>(-टी)<BR>	 1. A particular sort of cloth, coarse thick cloth, canvas.<BR>	 2.<BR>A screen of cloth surrounding a tent, an outer tent.<BR>	 3. A<BR>coloured or chintz garment.<BR>	 n. (-टं) A thatch, a roof.<BR> E. पट to sur-<BR>round, aff. अच् fem. aff. ङीप्ः see पटि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=414-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पटक|पटकः
पटक m. (-कः) A camp, an encampment.<BR> E. पट to surround, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=414-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पटकार|पटकारः
पटकार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A weaver.<BR>	 2. A painter.<BR> E. पट cloth, and कार<BR>maker.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=414-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पटकुटी
पटकुटी f. (-टीः) A tent.<BR> E. पट cloth, कुटी a house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=414-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पटच्चर|पटच्चरं|पटच्चरः
पटच्चर n. (-रं) Old cloth.<BR>	 m. (-रः) A thief.<BR> E. पटत् imitative sound,<BR>and चर going. पटदिव वेष्टित इव चरति चर-अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=414-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पटमण्डप|पटमंडप|पटमण्डपः
पटमण्डप m. (-पः) A tent.<BR> E. पट cloth, and मण्डप a house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=414-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पटमय|पटमयं|पटमयः
पटमय mfn. (-यः-यी-यं) Made of cloth.<BR>	 n. (-यं)<BR>	 1. A tent, a canvas<BR>house.<BR>	 2. A petticoat.<BR> E. पट cloth, मयट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=414-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पटल|पटलं|पटलः
पटल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) A heap, a number, a quantity or multitude.<BR>nf. (-लं-ली)<BR>	 1. A chapter of a book.<BR>	 2. A tree.<BR>	 3. A stalk.<BR>	 mf.<BR>(-लः-ला) A roof, a thatch.<BR>	 n. (-लं)<BR>	 1. A cover, a coating, an enclo-<BR>sing or surrounding skin or membrance.<BR>	 2. A place, a spot,<BR>a circle or district.<BR>	 3. A mark on the forehead with Sandal wood<BR>4. A basket.<BR>	 5. Train, retinue.<BR>	 6. A coat or film over the eyes.<BR>E. पट् to go, कलच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=414-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पटलप्रान्त|पटलप्रांत|पटलप्रान्तं|पटलप्रान्तः
पटलप्रान्त m. (-न्तः) The edge of a thatch.<BR> E. पटल a thatch, and प्रान्त end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=414-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पटवाप|पटवापः
पटवाप m. (-पः) A tent.<BR> E. पट cloth, and वाप what is woven.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=414-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पटवास|पटवासः
पटवास m. (-सः)<BR>	 1. A tent.<BR>	 2. A petticoat.<BR>	 3. Perfumed powder. E.<BR>पट cloth, वास abode, or वस् to perfume, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=414-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पटवासक|पटवासकः
पटवासक m. (-कः) Perfumed powder.<BR> E. कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=414-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पटवेश्मन्
पटवेश्मन् n. (-श्म) A tent.<BR> E. पट, and वेश्मन् a house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=414-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पटह|पटहं|पटहः
पटह mfn. (-हः-हा-हं) A kettle-drum.<BR>	 m. (-हः)<BR>	 1. A war-drum, or one<BR>used in battle.<BR>	 2. Injury, killing, slaughter.<BR>	 4. Tumult.<BR> E. पट<BR>imitative sound, हा to quit or make, aff. ड ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=414-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पटाक|पटाकः
पटाक m. (-कः) A kind of bird.<BR>	 f. (-का) A flag, a banner.<BR> E. पट to go,<BR>आक Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=414-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पटालुका
पटालुका f. (-का) A leech.<BR> E. पट् to go, आलुच् aff., कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=414-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पटि|पटिः
पटि(टी) f. (-टिः or -टी)<BR>	 1. A kind of cloth.<BR>	 2. An aquatic plant: see<BR>कुम्भिका.<BR>	 3. The curtain of a stage.<BR>	 4. A screen of a cloth surround-<BR>ing a tent.<BR> E. पट् to surround, &c. aff. इन् or ङीप् । see पट and पटी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=414-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पटिका
पटिका f. (-का) Cloth.<BR> E. वुन् added to पटी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=414-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पटिष्ठ|पटिष्ठः
पटिष्ठ mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठा-ष्ठं) Very clever.<BR> E. पटु and irr. superlative.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=414-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पटीयस्
पटीयस् mfn. (-यान्-यसी-यः) Very clever or able.<BR> E. पटु clever, ईयसुन्<BR>aff. of the superlative.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=414-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पटीर|पटीरं|पटीरः
पटीर n. (-रं)<BR>	 1. Sandal-wood.<BR>	 2. A field.<BR>	 3. Bamboo manna.<BR>	 4. A<BR>radish.<BR>	 5. The belly.<BR>	 6. A sieve.<BR>	 7. Height.<BR>	 8. Khayar.<BR>	 9. Rheu-<BR>matism.<BR>	 m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. KANDARPA.<BR>	 2. A cloud.<BR> E. पट् to go, Unādi<BR>aff. ईरन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=414-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पटु|पटुः
पटु mfn. (-टुः-ट्वी-टु)<BR>	 1. Clever, dexterous, skilful.<BR>	 2. Diligent.<BR>	 3.<BR>Smart, sharp.<BR>	 4. Hale, healthy.<BR>	 5. Warm, hot.<BR>	 6. Blown, ex-<BR>panded.<BR>	 7. Cruel, ferocious, unmerciful, unfeeling.<BR>	 8. Harsh,<BR>contumelious, (speech, &c.)<BR>	 9. Fraudulent, crafty, a rogue or<BR>cheat.<BR>	 10. Loquacious, talkative.<BR>	 m. (-टुः)<BR>	 1. A small kind of<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=415-a" target="_blank">Page415-a+ 60</a>]<BR>cucumber. (Trichosanthes diœca.)<BR>	 2. The leaf of the Trichosanthes.<BR>n. (-टु)<BR>	 1. Salt.<BR>	 2. A mushroom.<BR> E. पट r. 10th cl. to speak,<BR>&c. Unādi aff. डु, and the radical vowel shortened. or पट-उन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=414-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पटुक|पटुकः
पटुक m. (-कः) A sort of gourd.<BR> E. कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=415-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पटुकल्प|पटुकल्पः
पटुकल्प mfn. (-ल्पः-ल्पा-ल्पं) Not so clever, a little less able, &c.<BR> E. पटु<BR>clever, and कल्प aff. of incompleteness; also in a similar sense<BR>पटुदेश्य, and पटुदेशीय ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=415-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पटुजातीय|पटुजातीयः
पटुजातीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Of a clever sort, &c.<BR> E. पटु as above, and<BR>जातीय aff. of kind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=415-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पटुत्व|पटुत्वं
पटुत्व n. (-त्वं)<BR>	 1. Cleverness.<BR>	 2. Eloquence.<BR> E. त्व added to पटु; also<BR>with तल्, पटुता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=415-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पटुपर्णी
पटुपर्णी f. (-र्णी) A medicinal sort of moon plant.<BR> E. पटु a sort of<BR>gourd, and पर्ण a leaf, fem. aff. ङीष्; also पटुपत्रक n. (-कं) and<BR>पटुपत्रिका f. (-का.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=415-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पटुरूप
पटुरूप mfn. (-पः-पा-पं) Very clever.<BR> E. पटु, and रूप here implying<BR>much.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=415-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पटोटज|पटोटजं
पटोटज m. (-जं) A tent.<BR> E. पट and उटज a house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=415-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पटोल|पटोलं|पटोलः
पटोल m. (-लः) A kind of cucumber, commonly Parwor, (Trichosanthes<BR>diœca.)<BR>	 n. (-लं) A sort of cloth, a kind of chintz.<BR>	 f. (-ली) A<BR>small cucumber, either the same as above, (Trichosanthes diœca,)<BR>or another kind, (Luffa acutangula.)<BR> E. पट् to go, in the causal<BR>form, aff. ओलच्; removing malady.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=415-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पटोलक|पटोलकः
पटोलक m. (-कः) An oyster.<BR> E. पटोल as above, and कन् aff. of res-<BR>emblance; compared to the shape of the Trichosanthes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=415-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पटोलिका
पटोलिका f. (-का) A small cucumber, (Trichosanthes diœca:) it is also<BR>applied to Luffa acutangula.<BR> E. कन् with the fem. form added to<BR>पटोली.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=415-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पट्ट|पट्टं|पट्टः
पट्ट m. (-ट्टः)<BR>	 1. Cloth.<BR>	 2. Coloured cloth, wove silk.<BR>	 4. A turban, &c.<BR>or cloth for that purpose.<BR>	 5. A coloured silk turban.<BR>	 6. A fillet<BR>bound round the head.<BR>	 7. A bandage, a ligature, a cloth bound<BR>round a sore, &c.<BR>	 8. An upper or outer garment.<BR>	 9. A plant, com-<BR>monly called Pāt, (Corchorus,) from the fibres of the bark of<BR>which, (called jute) a coarse sack-cloth and cordage are prepared.<BR>10. A stone for grinding with a mullar.<BR>	 11. A plate of metal<BR>for inscription or engraving.<BR>	 12. A royal grant or order written<BR>on copper, stone, &c.<BR>	 13. A shield.<BR>	 14. A place where four roads<BR>meet.<BR>	 15. A chair, a stool.<BR>	 n. (-ट्टं) A city, a town, a village, the<BR>Pettāh probably of the south.<BR>	 f. (ट्टा)<BR>	 1. An ornament of the fore-<BR>head.<BR>	 2. Red Lodh.<BR>	 3. A horse's girth.<BR> E. पट् to surround, क्त aff.<BR>and त changed to ट.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=415-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पट्टक|पट्टकः
पट्टक m. (-कः) Cloth, a bandage, &c.<BR> E. कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=415-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पट्टज|पट्टजं
पट्टज n. (-जं) A sort of cloth, probably a kind of canvas or sack-cloth.<BR>E. पट्ट as above, and ज produced; made from jute. कौशेयवस्त्रेच ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=415-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पट्टदेवी
पट्टदेवी f. (-वी) A principal queen.<BR> E. पट्ट a fillet or tiara, देवी a queen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=415-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पट्ट|पट्टं|पट्टः
पट्ट(त्त)न n. (-नं-नी) A city:<BR> E. पट(त)न्ति जना यत्र पट पत, वा तनन् नेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=415-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पट्टबन्धन
पट्टबन्धन n. (-नं) Crowing, binding the head with a fillet or tiara. E.<BR>पट्ट, and बन्धन binding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=415-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पट्टमहिषी
पट्टमहिषी f. (-षी) A principal queen.<BR> E. पट्ट a fillet or tiara, and महिषी<BR>a queen. (पाटराणी) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=415-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पट्टरङ्ग|पट्टरङ्गं
पट्टरङ्ग n. (-ङ्गं) A plant used in dying, (Cœsalpinia sappan.)<BR> E. पट्ट cloth,<BR>and रञ्ज to dye, aff. करणे घञ् (वकम्) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=415-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पट्टरञ्जन
पट्टरञ्जन n. (-नं) Sappen wood.<BR> E. पट्ट cloth, and रञ्जन colouring: with<BR>कन् added, पट्टरञ्जक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=415-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पट्टशाक|पट्टशाकं
पट्टशाक n. (-कं) A sort of potherb, commonly called Nālita, (Corchorus<BR>capsularis.)<BR> E. पट्ट Corchorus, and शाक a potherb; the leaves re-<BR>sembling to those of the Pāt. नालिता, वा पाटशाक् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=415-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पट्टारोहा
पट्टारोहा f. (-हा) A principal queen.<BR> E. पट्ट, and आरोह what mounts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=415-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पट्टिका
पट्टिका f. (-का) Lodh.<BR> E. पट्टी the same, कन् added: again with आख्या a<BR>name; it is read also पट्ठिकाख्य, mf. (-ख्यः-ख्या)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=415-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पट्टिन्
पट्टिन् m. (-ट्टी) Red Lodh; also पट्टी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=415-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पट्टिल|पट्टिलः
पट्टिल m. (-लः) A plant, (Cæsalpinia bonduccella.)<BR> E. पट्ट + अस्त्यर्थे -इलच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=415-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पट्टि
पट्टि(का)लोध्र m. (-ध्रः) A sort of tree, the bark of which is used as an<BR>astringent; the red species of the Lodh, (Symploces racemosa,<BR>Rox.)<BR> E. पट्टी the same plant, लोध्र the Lodh; also with कन्<BR>added पट्टिलोध्रक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=415-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पट्टिश|पट्टिशः
पट्टिश(स) m. (-शः -or -सः) A sort of weapon, a kind of axe.<BR> E. पट् to go,<BR>aff. टिश् or टिस्; whence it is also read पट्टिस.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=415-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पट्टोलिका
पट्टोलिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. A title deed, a Pāttā, a lease, &c.<BR>	 2. A written<BR>legal opinion.<BR> E. पट्ट a royal mandate, &c. ओलच् aff., कन् in the<BR>fem form added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=415-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पठ|पठः
पठ r. 1st. cl. (पठति) To speak articulately, to declaim, to recite or<BR>read. भ्वा० पर० सक० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=415-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पठत्
पठत् mfn. (-ठन्-ठन्ती-ठत्) Reading, reciting.<BR> E. पठ् to read, शतृ part.<BR>aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=415-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पठन|पठनं
पठन n. (-नं) Reading, reciting.<BR> E. पठ् to read, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=415-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पठनीय
पठनीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Readable, to be read.<BR> E. पठ् to read, अनीयर्<BR>aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=415-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पठमञ्जरी
पठमञ्जरी f. (-री) A Rāgīni, one of the wives of SRĪRĀGA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=415-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पठि|पठिः
पठि f. (-ठिः-ठी) Reading, perusal.<BR> E. पठ् to read, aff. इन्, ङीष् option-<BR>ally added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=415-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पटित
पटित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Read, studied.<BR>	 2. Recited, repeated.<BR> E. पठ्<BR>to read, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=415-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पठितव्य|पठितव्यं
पठितव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं) To be read, what may or ought to be read.<BR>E. पठ् to read, तव्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=415-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पठितृ
पठितृ mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ) Reading, reciting, a reader.<BR> E. पठ् to read, तृच्<BR>aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=415-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पठ्यमान
पठ्यमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Being read or recited.<BR> E. पठ् to read, poss.<BR>v. शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=415-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पड
पड (इ) पडि r. 1st. cl. (पण्डते) To go, to move. r. 1st. and 10th. cls.<BR>(पण्डति पण्डयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To destroy, to annihilate.<BR>	 2. To heap together,<BR>to accumulate. गतौ भ्वा० आ० सक०-सेट्-इदित् । राशीकरणे चु० उभ० सक०<BR>सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=415-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पण|पणः
पण r. 1st cl. (पणते) also 10th. cl. (पणयति)<BR>	 1. To negociate, to treat or<BR>transact business.<BR>	 2. To bet or stake at play. (पणायति) To praise.<BR>व्यवहारे स्तुतौच भ्वा० आ० सक० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=415-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पण|पणः
पण m. (-णः)<BR>	 1. Measure of account, in cowries or shells, twenty gandās<BR>or eighty cowries; also a weight of copper of similar value.<BR>	 2.<BR>Wages or hire.<BR>	 3. A stake at play, a bet, a wager.<BR>	 4. Gaming,<BR>playing.<BR>	 5. Playing with dice.<BR>	 6. Price.<BR>	 7. Wealth, property 8.<BR>A commodity for sale.<BR>	 9. Business.<BR>	 10. A distiller.<BR>	 11. A<BR>house, a dwelling.<BR>	 12. A stipulation, a treaty.<BR>	 13. A vendor.<BR>	 14.<BR>A shop.<BR> E. पण् to do business, aff. अप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=415-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पणग्रन्थि|पणग्रंथि|पणग्रन्थिः
पणग्रन्थि m. (-न्थिः) A fair, a market.<BR> E. पण a commodity, ग्रन्थि a knot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=415-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पणता
पणता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. The state or condition of a pledge or stake.<BR>	 2. Price,<BR>value.<BR> E. तल् added to पण; also with त्व, पणत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=415-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पणन|पणनं
पणन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Sale, selling.<BR>	 2. Betting.<BR> E. पण् to do business, aff. भावे ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=415-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पणव|पणवः
पणव mf. (-वः-वा) A sort of musical instrument; a small drum or<BR>tabor.<BR> E. पण् business or price, वा to sound, aff. क; it is also<BR>read प्रणव.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=415-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पणस|पणसः
पणस m. (-सः) A commodity, an article of sale or traffic.<BR> E. पण्<BR>to do business, Unādi aff. कर्मणि-असच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=415-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पणाङ्गना|पणांगना
पणाङ्गना f. (-ना) A prostitute, a whore,<BR> E. पण price, अङ्गना a woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=415-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पणाया
पणाया f. (-या) Business, affair, transaction, buying and selling, &c.<BR>2. Profits or receipts of trade.<BR>	 3. A market place.<BR>	 4. Gambling.<BR>5. Praise.<BR> E. पण् to negotiate, in the causal form, अच् and टाप्<BR>affs.; or पण, and आय income, it also occurs mas. (-यः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=415-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पणायित|पणायितः
पणायित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Praised.<BR>	 2. Transacted.<BR> E. पण् to praise,<BR>aff. स्वार्थे-आय-क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=415-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पणार्पण
पणार्पण n. (-णं) Agreement, engagement, contract.<BR> E. पण price,<BR>अर्पण delivering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=415-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पणस्थि
पणस्थि n. (-स्थि) The small shell used as coin, a Cowri.<BR> E. पण busi-<BR>ness, and अस्थि a bone; also with कन् added पणस्थिक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=416-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पणित|पणितं
पणित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Prasied.<BR>	 2. Transacted as business.<BR> E. पण to<BR>praise, aff. क्त; also पणायित.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=416-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पणितव्य|पणितव्यं
पणितव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>	 1. Vendible, fit or intended for sale.<BR>	 2. To be<BR>transacted, negotiable.<BR>	 3. To be praised.<BR> E. पण to deal, aff. तव्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=416-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पण्ड|पंड|पंडः|पण्डः
पण्ड mn. (-ण्डः-ण्डं)<BR>	 1. A catamite.<BR>	 2. An eunuch.<BR>	 f. (-ण्डा)<BR>	 1. Wisdom,<BR>understanding.<BR>	 2. Science, learning.<BR> E. पडि to go, aff. अच् or पण्<BR>to deal, Unādi aff. ड, तस्य नेत्वम्; also with कन् added पण्डक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=416-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पण्डापूर्व|पण्डापूर्व्व|पण्डापूर्व्वं
पण्डापूर्व n. (-र्वं) Non-occurrence of the results of fate or destiny. E.<BR>पण्ड, and अपूर्व unprecedented.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=416-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पण्डित|पंडित|पण्डितः
पण्डित m. (-तः)<BR>	 1. A scholar, a teacher, a Pandit, a learned Brāhman,<BR>or one read in sacred science, and teaching it to his disciples.<BR>2. Incense.<BR>	 3. Clever.<BR>	 4. Proficient.<BR> E. पण्डा learning, तार० इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=416-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पण्डितम्मन्य|पण्डितंमन्य|पंडितंमन्य|पण्डितम्मन्यः
पण्डितम्मन्य m. (-न्यः) An ignorant and vain person, a pedant, one who<BR>thinks himself a Pandit or scholar.<BR> E. पण्डित learned, मन् to think,<BR>खश् aff.; also with णिनि aff. पण्डितमानिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=416-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पण्डितमानिन्
पण्डितमानिन् m. (-नी) An arrogant and ignorant man: E. see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=416-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पण्डितायमान
पण्डितायमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Become wise from a state of ignorance.<BR>E. पण्डित used as a verb, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=416-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पण्य|पण्यं|पण्यः
पण्य mfn. (-ण्यः-ण्या-ण्यं)<BR>	 1. To be sold, salable, vendible.<BR>	 2. To be<BR>praised, 3. To be transacted as business.<BR>	 n. (-ण्यं)<BR>	 1. A ware.<BR>	 2.<BR>Price.<BR>	 3. Traffic.<BR>	 f. (-ण्या) Heart pea: see पिण्या.<BR> E. पण to deal, कर्मणि-<BR>यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=416-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पण्यफलत्व
पण्यफलत्व n. (-त्वं) Prosperity in trade, profit.<BR> E. पण्य, and फलत्व fruitfulness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=416-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पण्यमूल्य
पण्यमूल्य n. (-ल्यं) The price of a commodity.<BR> E. पण्य, and मूल्य price.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=416-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पण्यवीथी
पण्यवीथी f. (-थी)<BR>	 1. A stall, &c.<BR>	 2. A market: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=416-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पण्यवीथिका
पण्यवीथिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. A stall, a shop, a place of sale.<BR>	 2. A market. E.<BR>पण्य vendible, and वीथी a shop, &c. कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=416-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पण्यशाला
पण्यशाला f. (-ला)<BR>	 1. A market.<BR>	 2. A shop, a ware-room.<BR> E. पण्य vendible,<BR>and शाला a hall.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=416-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पण्यस्त्री
पण्यस्त्री f. (-स्त्री) A whore.<BR> E. पण्य vendible, and स्त्री a woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=416-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पण्याङ्गना|पण्यांगना
पण्याङ्गना f. (-ना) A prostitute, a whore.<BR> E. पण्य to be sold, अङ्गना a<BR>woman; also पणाङ्गना.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=416-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पण्यजीव
पण्यजीव m. (-वः) A trader.<BR>	 n. (-वं) A market, a fair,<BR> E. पण्य a vendible,<BR>and आजीव a livelihood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=416-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पण्याजीवक|पण्याजीवकं
पण्याजीवक n. (-कं) A market.<BR> E. कन् added to the last; also पण्यजीवकं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=416-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पण्यार्ह
पण्यार्ह mfn. (-र्ह-र्हा-र्हं) Salable, vendible.<BR> E. पण्य, and अर्ह fit for.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=416-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत|पतं|पतः
पत(ऌ)पतॢ r. 1st. cl. (पतति) r. 10th cl. (पतयति-ते or पातयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To go,<BR>to move, but especially downwards, as, to fall, to descend, to<BR>alight.<BR>	 2. To possess supreme or superhuman power. r. 4th cl.<BR>(पत्यते) To be rich or powerful. With अति prefixed. To excel or<BR>surpass. With अभि or अव, To descend. With आङ्, To arrive,<BR>to come. With उत्, To ascend. With नि 1. To gain or get.<BR>	 2. To<BR>happen. With निर, To abscond. With परि, 1. To go fast.<BR>	 2. To<BR>be valuable. With प्र and नि, To fall prostrate, to salute, to<BR>worship. With वि and निर, To turn, to turn back. With सम्, 1. To<BR>go with.<BR>	 2. To gain. With आङ्, To purify or cleanse. With सम्<BR>and उत्, To fly. With सम् and नि, To go forth or out. गतौ अद० चु०<BR>उभ० सक० ऐश्ये० अक सेट् । ऐश्ये दि० आ० अक० सेट् । गतौ भ्वा० पर० सक०<BR>ऐश्ये अक० ज्वला० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=416-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत|पतं|पतः
पत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Cherished, protected.<BR>	 m. (-तः)<BR>	 1. Going, 2. Fall-<BR>ing, alighting.<BR>	 3. Flying, flight.<BR> E. पत् to go, अच् aff. or a various<BR>reading of पात.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=416-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पतक|पतकः
पतक mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>	 1. Who or what falls, descends, &c.<BR>	 m. (-कः) An<BR>astronomical table.<BR> E. पत् to fall, to go, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=416-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पतग|पतगः
पतग m. (-गः) A bird.<BR> E. पत् to go, Unādi aff. अगच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=416-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पतङ्ग|पतंग|पतङ्गं|पतंगः|पतङ्गः
पतङ्ग mf. (-ङ्गः-ङ्गी)<BR>	 1. A grasshopper.<BR>	 2. A bird.<BR>	 3. A sort of rice.<BR>	 4. The<BR>sun.<BR>	 n. (-ङ्गं)<BR>	 1. Quicksilver.<BR>	 2. A kind of Sandal.<BR> E. पत् falling, गम्<BR>to proceed, aff.; खच्; or पत् to fall, अङ्गच् Unādi aff. also पतङ्गम ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=416-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पतङ्गम|पतंगम|पतंगमः|पतङ्गमः
पतङ्गम mf. (-मः-मा)<BR>	 1. A bird.<BR>	 2. A grasshopper.<BR> E. पत, and गम what<BR>goes; see the last. पतन् उत्प्लवन् सन् गच्छति गम-खच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=416-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पतङ्गिका|पतंगिका
पतङ्गिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. A sort of bee.<BR>	 2. A small bird.<BR> E. कन् implying<BR>resemblance, with the fem. form added to पतङ्ग ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=416-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पतञ्चिका|पतंचिका
पतञ्चिका f. (-का) A bow-string.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=416-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पतञ्ज
पतञ्ज(ञ्च)लि m. (-लिः)<BR>	 1. The name of a saint or Muni and teacher of the<BR>Yoga philosophy, thence called after him PĀTANJALA; also the<BR>author of Mahābhāshya or commentary on PĀṆINI.<BR>	 2. A name of<BR>the poet VARARUCHI.<BR> E. पत् falling, अञ्जलि the hands joined as a<BR>mark of respect; having fallen from heaven, it is said, in the<BR>shape of small snake, into the hands of the saint PĀṆINI as he<BR>was performing this act of reverence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=416-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पतत्|पतन्त्
पतत् mfn. (तन्-तन्ती-तत्) Falling, coming down, alighting, &c.<BR>	 m. (-तन्)<BR>A bird.<BR> E. पत् to go, to alight, participial aff. शतृ or अति<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=416-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पतत्र|पतत्त्रं|पतत्रं
पतत्र n. (-त्रं)<BR>	 1. A wing.<BR>	 2. A vehicle.<BR> E. पत् to go, अत्रन् करणे । Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=416-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पतत्रि|पतत्रिः
पतत्रि m. (-त्रिः) A bird.<BR> E. पत् to go, अत्रिन् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=416-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पतत्रिन्
पतत्रिन् m. (-त्री)<BR>	 1. A bird.<BR>	 2. An arrow.<BR>	 3. A horse.<BR> E. पतत्र a wing, इनि<BR>poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=416-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पतत्रिराज|पतत्रिराजः
पतत्रिराज m. (-जः) VIṢṆU'S bird, “Gadura.”<BR> E. पतत्रिन्, and राज king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=416-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पतद्ग्रह|पतद्ग्रहः
पतद्ग्रह m. (-हः)<BR>	 1. A spitting pot.<BR>	 2. The reserve of an army.<BR> E. पतत्<BR>what falls, and ग्रह what takes. (पिक्दानी) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=416-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पतद्भीरु|पतद्भीरुः
पतद्भीरु m. (-रुः) A hawk, a falcon.<BR> E. पतत् a bird, and भीरु fearful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=416-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पतन|पतनं
पतन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Who or what goes, falls, descending. &c.<BR>	 n.<BR>(-नं)<BR>	 1. Falling.<BR>	 2. Alighting, descending.<BR>	 3. Falling from dignity,<BR>virtue, &c.<BR>	 4. Sin.<BR>	 5. Going.<BR>	 6. Subtraction.<BR>	 7. The latitude of<BR>a planet.<BR> E. पत् to fall, युच् or भावे-ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=416-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पतम|पतमः
पतम m. (-मः)<BR>	 1. The moon.<BR>	 2. A bird.<BR>	 3. A grasshopper.<BR> E. पत् to<BR>go, अमच् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=416-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पतयालु|पतयालुः
पतयालु mfn. (-लुः-लुः-लु) Falling, liable or accustomed to fall.<BR> E. पत्<BR>to go, &c. in the causal form, आलुच् aff. तत्पर्युदानेन न णि लोपः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=416-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पतस|पतसः
पतस mfn. (-सः-सा-सं)<BR>	 1. A bird.<BR>	 2. The moon.<BR>	 3. A caterpillar.<BR> E. पत्<BR>to go, Unādi aff. असच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=416-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पताका
पताका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. A flag or banner.<BR>	 2. A flagstaff.<BR>	 3. An emblem<BR>carried as an ensign or banner, a symbol, a sign.<BR>	 4. A mark.<BR>	 5.<BR>An episode, or episodical incident in a drama.<BR>	 6. Good fortune,<BR>auspiciousness.<BR> E. पत् to go, अकन् Unādi aff. पत्यते ज्ञायते योधो अनया<BR>पत-णि-आक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=416-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पताकिन्
पताकिन् m. (-की)<BR>	 1. An ensign, a standard bearer.<BR>	 2. A scheme for<BR>casting a nativity.<BR>	 f. (-नी) An army.<BR> E. पताका a flag, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=416-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पतापत
पतापत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Who or what goes, &c. much or frequently.<BR>E. पत् to go, अच् aff. repeated, and आच् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=416-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पति|पतिः
पति m. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. A master, an owner.<BR>	 2. A husband.<BR>	 3. A root.<BR>4. Ruler 5. Going, motion.<BR> E. पा to nourish, Unādi aff. डति, or<BR>पत् to go, with the same aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=416-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पतिघ्नी
पतिघ्नी f. (-घ्नी)<BR>	 1. The murderess of her husband.<BR>	 2. A line on the<BR>hand, indicating that a woman will be faithless or treacherous<BR>to her husband,<BR> E. पति and घ्न who kills, fem. aff. ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=416-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पतिघ्नीलक्षण
पतिघ्नीलक्षण n. (-णं) Sign of a murderess of a husband.<BR> E. पतिघ्नी, and<BR>लक्षण a mark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=416-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पतित|पतितः
पतित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Fallen, alighted.<BR>	 2. Fallen from virtue,<BR>wicked, abandoned.<BR>	 3. Fallen in war, defeated, overthrown.<BR>4. Degraded, outcaste.<BR>	 5. Gone.<BR> E. पत् to go, aff. कर्त्तरि क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=416-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पतितसावित्रीक|पतितसावित्रीकः
पतितसावित्रीक m. (-कः) A man of the first three classes, whose investi-<BR>ture has not been duly performed.<BR> E. पतित, and सावित्री the mys-<BR>tical verse, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=416-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पतितेक्षित
पतितेक्षित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Looked at by an outcaste.<BR> E. पतित, and<BR>ईक्षित seen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=416-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पतितोत्पन्न
पतितोत्पन्न mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं) Born of an outcaste.<BR> E. पतित, and उत्पन्न<BR>born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=416-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पतित्व|पतित्वं
पतित्व n. (-त्वं) The conjugal state.<BR> E. पति, and त्व aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=416-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पतित्वा
पतित्वा ind. Having fallen or fallen down, having alighted, &c.<BR> E. पत्<BR>to fall, क्त्वा aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=417-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पतिप्राणा
पतिप्राणा f. (-णा) A faithful wife.<BR> E. पति, and प्राण life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=417-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पतिंवरा
पतिंवरा f. (-रा)<BR>	 1. A bride choosing her husband.<BR>	 2. A pungent seed,<BR>(Nigella Indica.)<BR> E. पति a husband, वृ to choose, खच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=417-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पतिवत्री
पतिवत्री f. (-त्री) A married woman, a wife whose husband is living. E.<BR>पति a husband, मतुप् aff. fem. form irr., नुक् being inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=417-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पतिव्रता
पतिव्रता f. (-ता) A good and virtuous wife.<BR> E. पति a husband, व्रत a<BR>religious obligation; who never violates her marriage vow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=417-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पतिसेवा
पतिसेवा f. (-वा) Devotion to a husband.<BR> E. पति, and सेवा service.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=417-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पतीयत्री
पतीयत्री f. (-न्ती) A woman wishing or fit for a husband.<BR> E. पति, and<BR>क्यच् added, aff. शतृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=417-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पतेर|पतेरः
पतेर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Going, moving, one who goes or moves.<BR>	 m. (-रः)<BR>1. A bird 2. An Arhaka, a measure so called.<BR>	 3. A hole.<BR> E. पत्<BR>to go, एरक् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=417-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्काषिन्
पत्काषिन् mfn. (-षी-षिणी-षि) Pedestrian, going on foot.<BR>	 m. (-षी) A<BR>footman, a foot soldier, &c.<BR> E. पत् for पाद foot, कष् to injure,<BR>णिनि aff. पदादेशः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=417-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्तङ्ग
पत्तङ्ग n. (-ङ्गं) Red sanders: see पत्रङ्ग, of which it appears to be a<BR>local corruption. (वकम्) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=417-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्तन|पत्तनं
पत्तन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. A town, a city.<BR>	 2. A sort of drum.<BR> E. पत् to go, तनन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=417-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्तनवणिज्
पत्तनवणिज् m. (-णिक्) A tradesman.<BR> E. पत्तन a city, वणिज् a trader.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=417-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्ति|पत्तिः
पत्ति m. (-त्तिः)<BR>	 1. A foot soldier.<BR>	 2. A hero.<BR>	 f. (त्ति)<BR>	 1. Going, moving,<BR>walking.<BR>	 2. A company, a platoon, consisting of one chariot, one<BR>elephant, three horse, and five foot.<BR> E. पद् to go, नि Unādi aff.<BR>or तिन् aff. for the feminine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=417-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्तिपङ्क्ति|पत्तिपंक्ति
पत्तिपङ्क्ति f. (-ङ्क्ति) A line of infantry.<BR> E. पत्ति, and पङ्क्ति a line.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=417-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्तिसंहति|पत्तिसंहतिः
पत्तिसंहति f. (-तिः) A body of troops.<BR> E. पत्ति, and संहति assemblage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=417-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्तूर|पत्तूरः
पत्तूर m. (-रः) A plant, commonly Salincha.<BR>	 n. (-रं) Red sanders.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=417-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्त्र
पत्त्र n. (-त्त्रं) Any vehicle or means of conveyance.<BR> E. पत् to go, ष्ट्रन् aff.;<BR>also पत्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=417-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्नी
पत्नी f. (-त्नी) A wife.<BR> E. पति a husband, ङीप् aff. and नुक् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=417-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्न्याट|पत्न्याटः
पत्न्याट m. (-टः) The Harem, the private or women's apartments. E.<BR>पत्री a wife, आट who goes, from अट, with घञ् affix, and आङ्<BR>prefix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=417-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्र|पत्त्रं|पत्रं
पत्र(त्त्र) n. (-त्रं)<BR>	 1. A leaf.<BR>	 2. A vehicle in general; as a car, a horse, a<BR>camel, &c.<BR>	 3. The wing of a bird.<BR>	 4. The feather of an arrow.<BR>5. The leaf of the Laurus cassia.<BR>	 6. The leaf of a book.<BR>	 7. Gold<BR>leaf, &c. any thin sheet or plate of metal.<BR>	 8. A letter.<BR>	 9. The<BR>blade of a weapon.<BR>	 10. Painting the person as a decoration.<BR>11. A knife, a dagger.<BR>	 12. The leaf of a flower.<BR>	 nf. (-त्रं-त्री) A letter,<BR>any written document or address.<BR> E. पत् to go, ष्ट्रन् aff. and one<BR>त rejected; also sometimes पत्त्र ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=417-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्रक|पत्रकं
पत्रक n. (-कं)<BR>	 1. A leaf.<BR>	 2. The leaf of the Laurus cassia.<BR>	 3. Staining<BR>the person with Sandal, &c. by way of decoration.<BR> E. पत्र with<BR>स्वार्थे-क added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=417-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्रकाहला
पत्रकाहला f. (-ला) The noise made either by the flapping of wings, or<BR>by the rustling of leaves.<BR> E. पत्र a leaf, a wing, &c. and काहल noise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=417-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्रकृच्छ्र|पत्रकृच्छ्रः
पत्रकृच्छ्र n. (-च्छ्रं) A sort of penance, drinking infusion of any leaves<BR>for a given time.<BR> E. पत्र a leaf, and कृच्छ्र a penance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=417-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्रगुप्त|पत्रगुप्तः
पत्रगुप्त m. (-प्तः) A species of Euphorbia, commonly Teykānta Sij.<BR>E. पत्र a leaf, and गुप्त hidden.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=417-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्रङ्गं|पत्रङ्ग
पत्रङ्गं n. (-ङ्गः) Red sanders, (Pterocarpus santalinus.) also पत्राङ्ग.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=417-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्रझङ्कार|पत्त्रझङ्कार|पत्रझङ्कारः
पत्रझङ्कार m. (-रः) The current of a river: other authorities have in<BR>place of this word, पुरसंस्कार, and पत्रसस्कार, of which the last<BR>appears to be most accurate. रायभटीवृक्षे च ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=417-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्रणा
पत्रणा f. (-णा)<BR>	 1. Trimming the feathered butt of an arrow.<BR>	 2. Pain-<BR>ting figures on the body as a decoration.<BR> E. पत्र the feather of an<BR>arrow, णी to get, aff. ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=417-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्रगण्डुला
पत्रगण्डुला f. (-ला)<BR>	 1. A woman.<BR>	 2. A kind of barley.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=417-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्रतरु|पत्रतरुः
पत्रतरु m. (-रुः) The fœtid Mimosa. दुष्खदिरे ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=417-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्रदारक|पत्रदारकः
पत्रदारक m. (-कः) A saw.<BR> E. पत्र a leaf, &c. and दृ to tear, ण्वुल् aff. (करात) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=417-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्रनाडिका
पत्रनाडिका f. (-का) The fibre or vein of a leaf.<BR> E. पत्र a leaf, नाडी a<BR>vessel, aff. कन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=417-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्रपरशु|पत्रपरशुः
पत्रपरशु m. (-शुः) A small file used by silversmiths, &c.<BR> E. पत्र a sheet<BR>of metal, परशु an axe; also with पर्शु the same, पत्रपर्शु m. (-र्शुः) (छेनी) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=417-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्रपाल|पत्रपालः
पत्रपाल m. (-ल) A large knife.<BR>	 f. (-ली) A pair of shears or scissors.<BR>E. पत्र a leaf, पाल् to nourish, aff. अच् (कांचि) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=417-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्रपाश्या
पत्रपाश्या f. (-श्या) An ornament of the forehead, a piece of gold leaf<BR>situated on the forehead, or a painted mark upon it.<BR> E. पत्र a leaf,<BR>पश् to bind, aff. ण्यत्. (टीका) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=417-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्रपिशाचिका
पत्रपिशाचिका f. (-का) A sort of cap or cover for the head, made of<BR>leaves.<BR> E. पत्र a leaf, पिशाचिका an imp. (टोका) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=417-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्रपुष्प|पत्रपुष्पः
पत्रपुष्प m. (-ष्पः) A plant, a red sort of Tulasi or Basil, (Ocymum pilo-<BR>sum.)<BR>	 f. (-ष्पा) Holy basil, (Ocymum sanctum.)<BR> E. पत्र a leaf,<BR>and पुष्प a flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=417-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्रपुष्पक|पत्रपुष्पकः
पत्रपुष्पक m. (-कः) A kind of birch, from the bark of which Hukka<BR>snakes, &c. are made: see भूर्ज्जपत्र<BR> E. पत्र a leaf, and पुष्प a flower,<BR>कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=417-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्रपूग
पत्रपूग m. (-गः) A shower of arrows.<BR> E. पत्र, and पूग a heap.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=417-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्रबन्ध|पत्रबन्धः
पत्रबन्ध m. (-न्धः) Adorning with leaves, flowers, &c. decorating with<BR>nosegays or garlands.<BR> E. पत्र a leaf, and बन्ध a binding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=417-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्रबाल|पत्रबालः
पत्रबाल m. (-लः) An oar, especially a large one used as a rudder.<BR> E. पत्र<BR>a leaf, बल् to be strong, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=417-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्रभङ्ग|पत्रभंग|पत्रभङ्गः
पत्रभङ्ग mf. (-ङ्गः-ङ्गी) Decorating the person by staining it with fragrant<BR>pigments of sandal, musk, &c.<BR> E. पत्र a leaf, भञ्ज to break, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=417-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्रयौवन|पत्रयौवनं
पत्रयौवन n. (-नं) A new leaf, a sprout.<BR> E. पत्र a leaf, यौवन youth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=417-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्ररथ|पत्ररथः
पत्ररथ m. (-थः) A bird.<BR> E. पत्र a wing, and रथ a vehicle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=417-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्ररञ्जन
पत्ररञ्जन n. (-नं) Embellishing a page, illuminating, gilding, &c.<BR> E. पत्र,<BR>and रञ्जन colouring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=417-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्रल|पत्रलं
पत्रल n. (-लं) Thin or skim milk.<BR> E. पत् to go, रल् aff. (पात्ला दै) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=417-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्रले
पत्रले(रे)खा f. (खा) Decoratien of the face or person, by means of<BR>fragrant pigments, consisting of Sandal, saffron, musk, &c. E.<BR>पत्र a leaf, and लेखा a line.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=417-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्रवल्ली
पत्रवल्ली f. (-ल्ली) Staining the person with Sandal, &c. by way of<BR>ornament.<BR> E. पत्र a leaf, and वल्ली a creeper; also पत्रावली, पत्रलेखा, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=417-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्रवाह|पत्रवाहः
पत्रवाह m. (-हः)<BR>	 1. An arrow.<BR>	 2. A bird.<BR>	 3. A postman, a letter<BR>carrier.<BR> E. पत्र a feather or a letter, and वाह bearing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=417-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्रशि
पत्रशि(सि)रा f. (-रा) The vein or fibre of a leaf.<BR> E. पत्र a leaf, and शिरा a<BR>tubular vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=417-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्रश्रेष्ठ|पत्रश्रेष्ठः
पत्रश्रेष्ठ m. (ष्ठः) The Bel tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=417-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्रसंस्कार
पत्रसंस्कार m. (-रः) The current of a river.<BR> E. पत्र a leaf, संस्कार making<BR>perfect; see पत्रझङ्कार.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=417-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्रसूचि|पत्रसूचिः
पत्रसूचि m. (-चिः) A thorn.<BR> E. पत्र a leaf, and सूचि a needle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=417-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्रहिम|पत्रहिमं
पत्रहिम n. (-मं) Cold, wintry weather.<BR> E. पत्र here said to mean<BR>falling, हिम frost or snow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=417-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्राख्य|पत्राख्यं
पत्राख्य m. (-ख्यः) The pungent leaf of the Laurus cassia.<BR> E. पत्र a<BR>leaf, and आख्या a name; the leaf, by way of distinction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=417-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्राङ्ग|पत्रांग|पत्राङ्गं
पत्राङ्ग n. (-ङ्गं)<BR>	 1. Red sanders (Pterocarpus santolinus)<BR>	 2. Red or<BR>sappan wood, (Cæsalpinia sappan.)<BR>	 3. Bhūrjapatra, a tree so<BR>called, a kind of Birch.<BR>	 4. Another plant: see पद्मक.<BR> E. पत्र a leaf,<BR>अङ्ग body or substance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=417-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्राङ्गुलि|पत्रांगुलि|पत्राङ्गुलिः
पत्राङ्गुलि f. (-लिः) Painting the forehead, throat, neck, &c. with<BR>coloured Sandal, saffron, or any other fragrant substance. E.<BR>पत्र a leaf and आङ्गुलि a finger, being applied with the finger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=417-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्राञ्जन|पत्रांजन|पत्राञ्जनं
पत्राञ्जन n. (-नं) Ink or blacking.<BR> E. पत्र a leaf, (of a book,) and अञ्ज्<BR>to tint, करणे-ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=417-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्राढ्य|पत्राढ्यं
पत्राढ्य n. (-ढ्यं)<BR>	 1. The root of a long pepper.<BR>	 2. A kind of grass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=417-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्राली
पत्राली f. (-ली) Coloured or ornamental marks on the face or person. E.<BR>पत्र, and आलि a row.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=417-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्रावलि|पत्रावलिः
पत्रावलि f. (लि)<BR>	 1. Red chalk.<BR>	 2. A row of leaves.<BR>	 3. Decorating the<BR>person.<BR> E. पत्र, and आवलि a line: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=418-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्रावली
पत्रावली f. (-ली)<BR>	 1. Drawing lines along the form; staining some<BR>parts of the body with coloured and fragrant pigments, as with<BR>saffron, sandal, &c.<BR>	 2. A mixture of young Aswattha leaves with<BR>barley and honey.<BR> E. पत्र a leaf, and आवली a line: see पत्रलेखा,<BR>पत्रक, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=418-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्रिका
पत्रिका f. (का) A leaf, a written leaf or page, a writing, a letter, &c. E.<BR>पत्र, and कन् added, fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=418-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्रिन्
पत्रिन् mfn. (-त्री-त्रिणी-त्रि)<BR>	 1. Winged.<BR>	 2. Feathered.<BR>	 3. Having a<BR>page or leaf.<BR>	 m. (-त्री)<BR>	 1. An arrow.<BR>	 2. A bird.<BR>	 3. A falcon.<BR>	 4. A<BR>tree.<BR>	 5. A mountain.<BR>	 6. A chariot.<BR>	 7. A rider in a car or car-<BR>riage.<BR>	 f. (-णी) A sprout, a shoot.<BR> E. पत्र a leaf, &c. इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=418-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्रोपस्कर|पत्रोपस्करः
पत्रोपस्कर m. (-रः) A tree, (Cassia esculenta.)<BR> E. पत्र a leaf, उपस्कर a<BR>condiment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=418-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्रोर्ण|पत्रोर्णं|पत्रोर्णः
पत्रोर्ण n. (-र्णं) Wove silk.<BR>	 m. (-र्णः) A plant, (Bignonia indica.)<BR> E. पत्र<BR>a leaf, ऊर्णा wool.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=418-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्रोल्लास|पत्रोल्लासः
पत्रोल्लास m. (-सः) A bud.<BR> E. पत्र, and उल्लास what delights.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=418-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्सल|पत्सलं|पत्सलः
पत्सल m. (-लः) A road.<BR> E. पत् to go, सर Unādi aff. र changed to ल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=418-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पथ|पथः
पथ r. 1st. cl. (पथति) to go, to move. r. 10th. cl. (पाथयति) To throw, to<BR>cast, to despatch or send; (इ) पथि, r. 1st. and 10th. cls. (पन्थति<BR>पन्थयति) To go, to proceed, to travel. गतौ भ्वा० पर० सक० सेट् । वा चुरा<BR>उभ० पक्षे भ्वा० पर० सक० सेट् इदित् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=418-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पथ|पथः
पथ m. (-थः) A road.<BR> E. पथ् to go, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=418-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पथत्|पथन्त्
पथत् mfn. (-थन्-थन्ती-थत्) Going, travelling.<BR>	 m. (-थन्) A road.<BR> E. पथ् to<BR>go, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=418-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पथिक|पथिकः
पथिक mfn. (-कः-का-की-कं) Knowing or going on a road.<BR>	 m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A<BR>traveller, a way-farer.<BR>	 2. A guide, one who knows the way. E.<BR>पथिन् a road, वुन् or कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=418-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पथिकसन्तति|पथिकसंतति|पथिकसंततिः|पथिकसन्ततिः
पथिकसन्तति f. (-ति) A line or range of travellers, a cafileh, a caravan.<BR>E. पथिक a traveller, सन्तति a range; also with संहति assemblage,<BR>पथिकसंहति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=418-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पथिद्रुम|पथिद्रुमः
पथिद्रुम m. (-मः) A sort of Khayar, (Mimosa alba.)<BR> E. पथिन् a road,<BR>and द्रुम a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=418-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पथिन्
पथिन् m. (पन्था)<BR>	 1. A road, a way.<BR>	 2. Sect, doctrine, path in morals<BR>or religion.<BR>	 3. A division of hell.<BR>	 4. A journey.<BR>	 5. Course of<BR>manner or action.<BR> E. पथ् to go, इन् Unādi aff.; the noun is irregu-<BR>larly inflected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=418-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पथिप्रज्ञ
पथिप्रज्ञ mfn. (-ज्ञः-ज्ञा-ज्ञं) Acquainted with roads.<BR> E. पथिन्, and प्रज्ञ<BR>who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=418-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पथिल|पथिलः
पथिल m. (-लः) A traveller, a way-farer.<BR> E. पथिन् a road, इलच् Unādi<BR>aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=418-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पथिवाहक|पथिवाहकः
पथिवाहक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A fowler, a bird-catcher.<BR>	 2. A porter, a burthen-<BR>carrier. Adj. Cruel.<BR> E. पथिन् a road, and वाहक who bears.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=418-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पथ्य|पथ्यं|पथ्यः
पथ्य mfn. (-थ्यः-थ्या-थ्यं) Proper, fit, suitable, agreeing with, but applied<BR>chiefly medically, with respect to diet, regimen, &c.<BR>	 mf. (-थ्यः-<BR>थ्या) Yellow Myrobalan, (Terminalia chebula.)<BR>	 n. (-थ्यं) Sea salt.<BR>E. पथ् to go, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=418-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पथ्यापथ्य|पथ्यापथ्यं
पथ्यापथ्य n. (-थ्यं) The class of things that are considered beneficial<BR>or hurtful in disease.<BR> E. पथ्य, and अपथ्य improper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=418-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पथ्याशिन्
पथ्याशिन् mfn. (-शी-शिनी-शि) Eating wholesome things.<BR> E. पथ्य, and<BR>अशिन् who eats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=418-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद|पदं|पदः
पद r. 4th. cl. (औ) पदौ (पद्यते) r. 10th. cl. (पदयते) to go, to move. (ए) पदे<BR>r. 1st. cl. (पदति) to stand fast. With अभि, prefixed, 1. To know,<BR>to understand.<BR>	 2. To see, to look. With अनु, To follow. With<BR>आङ्, 1. To happen, to befall.<BR>	 2. To gain.<BR>	 3. To suffer misfortune.<BR>4. To multiply.<BR>	 5. To produce.<BR>	 6. To come. With उत्, To be born<BR>or produced. With उप, 1. To gain.<BR>	 2. To be born.<BR>	 3. To be near or<BR>connected with. With उप, and सम्, To offer oblations. With प्र,<BR>1. To gain, to acquire.<BR>	 2. To commence. With प्र; and वि, To<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=418-b" target="_blank">Page418-b+ 60</a>]<BR>establish, to enact. With प्रति, 1. To gain.<BR>	 2. To assent, to agree or<BR>promise.<BR>	 3. To restore. With वि, To suffer misfortune or pain.<BR>With वि, and आङ्, To injure or kill. With वि and उत्, To discri-<BR>minate, to analyze. With सम्, 1. To thrive, to grow or increase.<BR>2. To do, to execute, to perform.<BR>	 3. To select. With सम्, and आङ्,<BR>1. To arrive.<BR>	 2. To finish. स्थैर्ये भ्वा० पर० सक० सेट् । गतौ दि० आ०<BR>सक० अनिट् पक्षे अद० चु० आत्म० सक० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=418-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्
पद् n. (-द् or -त्) A foot.<BR> E. पद् to go, aff. क्विप्; also पद; or it is<BR>considered as an irregular substitute for पाद.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=418-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद|पदं|पदः
पद n. (-दं)<BR>	 1. A foot.<BR>	 2. A footstep, the mark of a foot.<BR>	 3. A word.<BR>4. An inflected word.<BR>	 5. A crude word.<BR>	 6. A connected sentence.<BR>7. Subject, thing, matter.<BR>	 8. Preservation, defence 9. Industry,<BR>application.<BR>	 10. Disguise.<BR>	 11. Place, site 12. Rank, station,<BR>degree.<BR>	 13. A mark, a spot.<BR>	 14. A foot or rather line of a stanza.<BR>15. A mode of writing the Vedas, in which the several words are<BR>detached from one another.<BR>	 16. A business, an affair.<BR>	 17. (In<BR>Arithmetic,) Any one of a set of numbers the sum of which is<BR>required, or the last of the series, a square-root.<BR>	 18. To occupy.<BR>19. Step, pace, 20. A trace, a mark.<BR>	 m. (-दः) A ray of light.<BR> E. पद्<BR>to go, aff. अच् or घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=418-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पदक|पदकं|पदकः
पदक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A Brāhman knowing the verses of the Vedas.<BR>	 2. A<BR>Nishka, a weight of gold.<BR>	 3. An ornament of the neck.<BR>	 n. (-कं)<BR>1. Step.<BR>	 2. Position.<BR>	 3. Office.<BR> E. पद a verse, &c. and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=418-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पदकार|पदकारः
पदकार m. (-रः) One who divides or separates compound term. E.<BR>पद, and कार who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=418-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पदक्रम|पदक्रमः
पदक्रम m. (-मः)<BR>	 1. Step, pace.<BR>	 2. Walking.<BR> E. पद, and क्रम going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=418-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पदग|पदगः
पदग mfn. (-गः-गा-गं) Going with the feet.<BR>	 m. (-गः) A footman, a foot<BR>soldier, &c.<BR> E. पद् or पद a foot, and ग who goes; hence also पद्न.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=418-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पदगत
पदगत mfn. (-ता-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Gone on foot 2. Described or recorded in a<BR>line or stanza.<BR> E. पद, and गत gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=418-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पदन
पदन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Who or what goes or move.<BR> E. पद् to go, युच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=418-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पदन्यास|पदन्यासः
पदन्यास m. (-सः)<BR>	 1. Step, pace.<BR>	 2. Conduct, procedure.<BR>	 3. Position of<BR>the feet in a particular attitude.<BR>	 4. A plant; also गोक्षुर.<BR> E. पद,<BR>and न्यास gesticulation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=418-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पदपात|पदपातः
पदपात m. (-तः) Step, pace, foot-fall, tread.<BR> E. पद, and पात fall.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=418-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पदभञ्जन|पदभञ्जनं
पदभञ्जन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Explanation of obscure or obsolete words.<BR>	 2. Ety-<BR>mology.<BR>	 3. Separating the words of a line or sentence.<BR> E. पद a<BR>word, भञ्जन a breaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=418-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पदभञ्जिका|पदभंजिका
पदभञ्जिका f. (-का) A register, a journal, a calendar or almanack. E.<BR>पद a mark, &c. भञ्ज् to divide, aff. ण्वुल्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=418-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पदवि|पदविः
पदवि f. (-विः-वी)<BR>	 1. A road, a path, a way.<BR>	 2. Station, situation,<BR>degree, rank.<BR>	 3. Place, site.<BR> E. पद् to go, अवि aff.; fem. aff.<BR>optionally ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=418-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पदविक्षेप|पदविक्षेपः
पदविक्षेप m. (-पः)<BR>	 1. Step, pace, walking.<BR>	 2. A horse's paces.<BR> E. पद, and<BR>विक्षेप throwing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=418-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पदविष्टम्भ|पदविष्टम्भः
पदविष्टम्भ m. (-म्भः) Tread, step, stamp with the foot.<BR> E. पद, and विष्टम्भ<BR>fixing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=418-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पदष्टीव
पदष्टीव n. (-वं) The feet and knees.<BR> E. पद् a foot, and अष्ठीवत् the<BR>knee, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=418-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पदसङ्घात|पदसंघात|पदसंघातः
पदसङ्घात m. (-तः) A writer, an annotator, one who collects or classes<BR>words.<BR> E. पद, and सम् before, हन् to hurt, अण् aff.; also पदसङ्घाट.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=418-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पदाङ्क|पदांक|पदाङ्कः
पदाङ्क m. (-ङ्कः) Foot-mark, vestige.<BR> E. पद, and अङ्क a mark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=418-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पदाजि|पदाजिः
पदाजि m. (-जिः) A foot soldier.<BR> E. पद a foot, अज् to go, इन् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=418-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पदात|पदातः
पदात m. (-तः) A footman, a pedestrian.<BR> E. पद foot, अत् to go, aff. क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=418-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पदाति|पदातिः
पदाति m. (-तिः) A footman or foot soldier.<BR> E. पद foot, अत् to go, इन्<BR>Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=418-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पदातिक|पदातिकः
पदातिक m. (-कः) A peon, a footman or foot soldier.<BR> E. कन् added to<BR>the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=418-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पदानुराग|पदानुरागः
पदानुराग m. (-गः)<BR>	 1. A servant.<BR>	 2. An army<BR> E. पद, and अनुराग attachment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=418-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पदाम्भोज|पदांभोज
पदाम्भोज n. (-जं)<BR>	 1. The foot of a mistress, or a divinity; &c.<BR>	 2. A<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=419-a" target="_blank">Page419-a+ 60</a>]<BR>lotus-like foot.<BR> E. पद, and अम्भोज a lotus; also similar compounds,<BR>पदारविन्द, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=418-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पदार|पदारः
पदार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. The dust of the feet.<BR>	 2. A boat.<BR> E. पद a foot, ऋ to<BR>go, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=419-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पदारविन्द
पदारविन्द n. (-न्दं) The foot of a mistress, of a divinity, &c.<BR> E. पद, and<BR>अरविन्द a lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=419-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पदार्थ|पदार्थः
पदार्थ m. (-र्थः)<BR>	 1. Thing, substantial or material form of being.<BR>	 2. A<BR>category of predicament in Logic, of which seven are enumerated;<BR>viz:--substance, quality, action, identity, variety, relation and<BR>nonexistence or annihilation. They are sixteen according to<BR>Nyaya Philosophy six according to the Vaiseshika, twenty-five<BR>according to Sānkhya, twenty six according to Pātanjala,<BR>and two according to Vaidantica.<BR>	 3. The meaning of a word<BR>or sentence.<BR>	 4. A head, a topic.<BR> E. पद word, thing, and अर्थ<BR>meaning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=419-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पदासन|पदासनं
पदासन n. (-नं) A foot-stool.<BR> E. पद a foot, आसन a place of sitting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=419-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पदिक|पदिकः
पदिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Going on foot.<BR>	 m. (-कः) A foot soldier.<BR>	 n. (-कं)<BR>The point of the foot.<BR> E. पद a foot. aff. ष्ठन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=419-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पदेपदे
पदेपदे ind. Continually.<BR> E. पद a foot-step, seventh case repeated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=419-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्ग|पद्गः
पद्ग m. (-द्गः) A foot-soldier.<BR> E. पद् a foot, and ग who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=419-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्धति|पद्धतिः
पद्धति f. (-तिः-ती)<BR>	 1. A road.<BR>	 2. A line, a row or range.<BR>	 3. A ritual, a<BR>manual, a work upon any act or ceremony, detailing the mode<BR>of its performance, and collecting the texts connected with it.<BR>	 4.<BR>A family name, a surname or title.<BR> E. पद् a foot, हन् to strike,<BR>aff. क्तिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=419-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्धिम|पद्धिमं
पद्धिम n. (-मं) Coldness of the feet,<BR> E. पद् for पाद, and हिम frost or<BR>cold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=419-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्म|पद्मं|पद्मः
पद्म mn. (-द्मः-द्मं)<BR>	 1. A lotus, (Nelumbium speciosum;) it is often con-<BR>founded with the water lily, (Nymphæa.)<BR>	 2. A form of arraying<BR>army resembling to that of a lotus.<BR>	 3. One of KUVERA'S trea-<BR>sures or gems.<BR>	 4. A large number, ten billions.<BR>	 5. Coloured marks<BR>on the face and trunk of an elephant.<BR>	 6. A drug, also termed Pad-<BR>makāṣṭha.<BR>	 7. Lead.<BR>	 8. A name given to the six Chakras of the<BR>body, or to the mystical faculties present in them.<BR>	 9. The root<BR>of a lotus.<BR>	 m. (-द्मः)<BR>	 1. A Nāga or serpent of the lower regions.<BR>	 2.<BR>One of the twelve Chakravartis or paramount princes of the Jai-<BR>nas.<BR>	 3. One of the persons termed Sukla Balas by the Jains.<BR>	 4. A<BR>name of RĀMA.<BR>	 5. The personified treasures of KUVERA, as wor-<BR>shipped by the Tāntrikas.<BR>	 6. A particular mode of sexual enjoy-<BR>ment. The posture is thus described on Vāchaspatya:--<BR>हस्ताभ्याञ्च समालिङ्ग्य नारीपद्मासनोपरि ।<BR>रमेद्गाढं समाकृष्य बन्धोऽयं पद्मसंज्ञकः ॥<BR>f. (-द्मा)<BR>	 1. A name of LAKṢMĪ.<BR>	 2. A plant, (Hibiscus mutabilis.)<BR>3. A shrub, (Siphonanthus Indica.)<BR>	 4. A female serpent or Nāga,<BR>the goddess MANASĀ, and wife to the sage JARATKĀRU.<BR>	 5. The<BR>mother of the twentieth Jina or Jaina saint.<BR>	 6. The flower of<BR>the Carthamus or safflower.<BR> E. पद् to go, (on the water, &c.)<BR>Uṇādi aff. मन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=419-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्मक|पद्मकं
पद्मक n. (-कं)<BR>	 1. Coloured marks or spots on the face and trunk of<BR>an elephant.<BR>	 2. A sort of drug, commonly called पद्मकाष्ठ, 3. A<BR>kind of leprosy.<BR>	 4. An army arrayed in the form of a lotus-flower.<BR>E. कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=419-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्मकर|पद्मकरः
पद्मकर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. The sun.<BR>	 2. An epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR> E. पद्म, and कर<BR>hand, his image always holding a lotus in one hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=419-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्मकाष्ठ|पद्मकाष्ठं
पद्मकाष्ठ n. (-ष्ठं) A fragrant wood used in medicine, and described as<BR>cooling and tonic.<BR> E. पद्म a lotus, and काष्ठ wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=419-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्मकिन्
पद्मकिन् m. (-की)<BR>	 1. The Bhūrjapatra or birch tree, the bark is used<BR>for writing mantras upon, &c.<BR>	 2. An elephant.<BR> E. पद्मक, and<BR>इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=419-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्मकेशर|पद्मकेशरः
पद्मकेशर mn. (-रः-रं) The filament of a lotus.<BR> E. पद्म, and केशर the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=419-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्मखण्ड|पद्मखंड
पद्मखण्ड n. (-ण्डं) A quantity of lotuses, or spot abounding with them.<BR>E. पद्म a lotus, and खण्ड a portion or district.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=419-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्मगन्ध|पद्मगंध|पद्मगन्धं
पद्मगन्ध(न्धि) mfn. (-न्धः-न्धा-न्धं) Lotus-smelling; smelling like a lotus. E.<BR>पद्म, and गन्ध smell; also with इ substituted for the final, पद्मगन्धि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=419-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्मगर्भ|पद्मगर्भः
पद्मगर्भ m. (-र्भः)<BR>	 1. A name of BRAMHĀ.<BR>	 2. The sun.<BR>	 3. An epithet of<BR>Viṣṇu.<BR> E. पद्म a lotus, and गर्भ womb, born from the lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=419-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्मचारिणी
पद्मचारिणी f. (-णी) A small tree, (Hibiscus mutabilis.)<BR> E. पद्म a lotus, चर्<BR>to resemble, aff. णिनि, fem. aff. ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=419-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्मतन्तु|पद्मतंतु|पद्मतन्तुः
पद्मतन्तु m. (-न्तुः) The fibrous stalk of the lotus.<BR> E. पद्म, and तन्तु thread.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=419-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्मदर्शन|पद्मदर्शनः
पद्मदर्शन m. (-नः) The resin of the Pinus longifolia.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=419-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्मनाभ|पद्मनाभः
पद्मनाभ m. (-भः)<BR>	 1. A name of VIṢṆU.<BR>	 2. One of the Jinas of a fur-<BR>ture age.<BR> E. पद्म a lotus, and नाभि a navel, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=419-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्मनाभि|पद्मनाभिः
पद्मनाभि m. (-भिः) VIṢṆU is thus termed, because the lotus, contain-<BR>ing BRAMHĀ, sent to create the world, sprang from his navel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=419-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्मनाल|पद्मनालं
पद्मनाल n. (-लं) The stalk of a lotus.<BR> E. पद्म lotus, and नाल a hollow<BR>stalk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=419-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्मपत्र|पद्मपत्रं
पद्मपत्र n. (-त्रं) A sort of Costus, (C. specious.)<BR> E. पद्म a lotus, and पत्र<BR>a leaf; also पद्मपर्ण n. (-र्णं) from पर्ण a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=419-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्मपाणि|पद्मपाणिः
पद्मपाणि m. (णिः)<BR>	 1. A name of BRAMHĀ.<BR>	 2. The sun.<BR>	 3. A Buddha,<BR>a Bauddha sanctified teacher.<BR>	 4. An epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR> E. पद्म<BR>a lotus, and पाणि the hand holding a lotus in one hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=419-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्मपुष्प|पद्मपुष्पः
पद्मपुष्प m. (-ष्पः)<BR>	 1. A shrub, (Webera corymbosa:) see कर्णिकार.<BR>	 2. A<BR>sort of bird.<BR> E. पद्म a lotus, and पुष्प a flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=419-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्मप्रभ|पद्मप्रभः
पद्मप्रभ m. (-भः) The sixth Jina or Jaina pontiff.<BR> E. पद्म a lotus, and प्रभ<BR>who shines. कमलसदृशप्रभान्वितेच ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=419-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्मप्रिया
पद्मप्रिया f. (-या) The wife of the Muni JARATKĀRU.<BR> E. पद्म a lotus, and<BR>प्रिया fond of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=419-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्मबन्ध|पद्मबंध|पद्मबन्धः
पद्मबन्ध m. (-न्धः) The artificial arrangement of the words of a verse in<BR>a figure representing the leaves of a lotus; It is fully illustrated<BR>in Saraswatī Kanthābharana.<BR> E. पद्म, and बन्ध binding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=419-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्मबन्धु|पद्मबंधु|पद्मबन्धुः
पद्मबन्धु m. (-न्धुः)<BR>	 1. A bee.<BR>	 2. The sun.<BR> E. पद्म a lotus, and बन्धु the<BR>friend. अर्कवृक्षे च ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=419-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्मभू
पद्मभू m. (-भूः) BRAMHĀ.<BR> E. पद्म a lotus, and भू born, क्विप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=419-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्ममुखी
पद्ममुखी f. (-खी) A sort of prickly nightshade.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=419-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्मयोनि|पद्मयोनिः
पद्मयोनि m. (-निः) BRAMHĀ.<BR> E. पद्म, and योनि place of production.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=419-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्मराग|पद्मरागः
पद्मराग m. (-गः) A ruby.<BR> E. पद्म a lotus, and राग colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=419-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्मरेखा
पद्मरेखा f. (-खा) A lotus-figure on the palm of the hand, indicating the<BR>possession of great wealth.<BR> E. पद्म a large number, and रेखा a line.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=419-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्मलाञ्छन|पद्मलांछन|पद्मलाञ्छनः
पद्मलाञ्छन m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. A king, a sovereign.<BR>	 2. A name of BRAMHĀ.<BR>	 3.<BR>The sun.<BR>	 4. KUVERA, the god of wealth.<BR>	 f. (-ना)<BR>	 1. A name of<BR>LAKṢMĪ, 2. A name of SARASWATĪ.<BR>	 3. A title of TĀRĀ, one of<BR>the forms of DURGĀ.<BR> E. पद्म a lotus, a Chātā or parasol-shaped,<BR>like one, a fabulous gem, &c. and लाञ्छन a mark or designation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=419-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्मवर्णक|पद्मवर्णकं
पद्मवर्णक n. (-कं) A species of Costus, (C. speciosus.)<BR> E. पद्म a lotus, वर्ण<BR>a colour, कप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=419-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्मवासा
पद्मवासा f. (-सा)<BR>	 1. A name of LAKṢMĪ.<BR>	 2. Having the fragrance of a<BR>lotus-flower.<BR> E. पद्म a lotus, and वासा abode; abiding at the crea-<BR>tion within the petals of the lotus. or पद्मं वासो अस्याः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=419-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्मवी
पद्मवी(बी)ज n. (-जं) The seed of the lotus.<BR> E. पद्म a lotus, and वीज a seed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=419-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्मस्नुषा
पद्मस्नुषा f. (-षा)<BR>	 1. GANGĀ.<BR>	 2. LAKṢMĪ.<BR>	 3. GAURĪ or DURGĀ.<BR> E. पद्म<BR>a lotus, and स्नुषा a daughter-in-law.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=419-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्माकर|पद्माकरः
पद्माकर m. (-रः) A large deep tank or pond; one in which the lotus<BR>does or may grow.<BR> E. पद्म, and आकर a mine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=419-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्माक्ष|पद्माक्षं|पद्माक्षः
पद्माक्ष m. (-क्षः)<BR>	 1. The seed of the lotus.<BR>	 2. Lotus-eyed.<BR> E. पद्म a lotus,<BR>and अक्ष an eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=419-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्माट|पद्माटः
पद्माट m. (-टः) A sort of Cassia, (C. tora.)<BR> E. पड्म a lotus, and अट् to<BR>resemble, aff. अच्. चक्रमर्दवृक्षे, (दादमर्दनैति भाषा) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=419-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्मान्तर|पद्मान्तरः
पद्मान्तर m. (-रः) Petal of the lotus.<BR> E. पद्म, and अन्तर inside.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=419-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्मालया
पद्मालया f. (-या) A name of the goddess LAKṢMĪ.<BR> E. पद्म a lotus, and<BR>आलय an asylum. लवङ्गे च ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=419-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्मावती
पद्मावती f. (-ती)<BR>	 1. A name of the goddess manasā or the wife of the<BR>JARATKĀRU.<BR>	 2. The name of a river, the main stream of<BR>the Ganges, between the KĀSIMBĀZĀR river and the sea.<BR> E. पद्म<BR>a lotus, मतुप aff., fem. aff. ङीप्, and the antepen. made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=420-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्मावतीप्रिय|पद्मावतीप्रियः
पद्मावतीप्रिय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. The Muni JARATKĀRU.<BR>	 2. The Kalki avatāra.<BR>E. पद्मावती as above, and प्रिय beloved. शृगाल नृपेच ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=420-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्मासन|पद्मासनं|पद्मासनः
पद्मासन n. (-नं) A posture in religious meditation, sitting with the<BR>thighs crossed, one hand resting on the left thigh, the other held<BR>up with the thumb upon the heart; the eyes directed to the<BR>tip of the nose.<BR>	 2. A seat or throne made in the shape of a<BR>lotus, one especially on which idols are placed.<BR>	 m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. A<BR>name of BRAMHĀ.<BR>	 2. The sun.<BR> E. पद्म a lotus, and आसन sitting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=420-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्मिन्
पद्मिन् m. (द्मी-) An elephant.<BR>	 f. (-नी)<BR>	 1. A multitude of lotuses, or<BR>place abounding in them.<BR>	 2. A woman of one of the four classes<BR>into which the sex is distinguished; the first and the most<BR>excellent. She is thus described in Vāchaspatya:--<BR>भवति कमलनेत्रा नासिकाक्षुद्ररन्ध्रा ।<BR>अविरलकुचयुग्मा दीर्घकेशी कृशाङ्गी ॥<BR>मृदुचरणसुशीला गीतनृत्यानुरक्ता ।<BR>सकलतनुसुवेशा पद्मिनी पद्मगन्धा ॥<BR>3. A lotus, (Nelumbium speciosum.)<BR>	 4. A pool or pond, espe-<BR>cially one deep enough for the growth of the lotus.<BR>	 5. The<BR>fibrous stalk of a lotus.<BR>	 6. A female elephant.<BR> E. पद्म coloured<BR>marks. &c. or a lotus, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=420-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्मिनीकान्त|पद्मिनीकांत|पद्मिनीकान्तः
पद्मिनीकान्त m. (-न्तः) The sun.<BR> E. पद्मिनी a lotus, and कान्त beloved.<BR>अर्कवृक्षे च ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=420-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्मिनीखण्ड
पद्मिनीखण्ड n. (-ण्डं) A place abounding with lotuses, or a district in<BR>which they grow.<BR> E. पद्मिनी, and खण्ड division.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=420-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्मिनीबल्लभ
पद्मिनीबल्लभ m. (-भः) The sun.<BR> E. पद्मिनी a lotus, and बल्लभ a friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=420-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्मेशय|पद्मेशयः
पद्मेशय m. (-यः) A name of VIṢṆU.<BR> E. पद्म in or on a lotus, and शय<BR>who sleeps.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=420-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्मोत्तर|पद्मोत्तरः
पद्मोत्तर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Safflower.<BR>	 2. A proper name: see the next. E.<BR>पद्म, and उत्तर better.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=420-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्मोत्तरात्मज|पद्मोत्तरात्मजः
पद्मोत्तरात्मज m. (जः) One of the Jaina Chakravartis or emperors. E.<BR>पद्मोत्तर, and आत्मज son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=420-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्मोद्भव|पद्मोद्भवः
पद्मोद्भव m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. A name of BRAMHĀ.<BR>	 f. (-वा) The snake goddess<BR>MANASĀ.<BR> E. पद्म a lotus, and उद्भव born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=420-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्य|पद्यं|पद्यः
पद्य mfn. (-द्यः-द्या-द्यं) Hurting or coming in contact with the feet.<BR>	 n.<BR>(-द्यं)<BR>	 1. Metre, verse, a stanza.<BR>	 2. Wickedness, infamy.<BR>	 m. (-द्यः)<BR>	 1.<BR>A Śūdra.<BR>	 2. A part of a word.<BR>	 f. (-द्या)<BR>	 1. A road.<BR>	 2. Praise,<BR>eulogium.<BR> E. पद् to go, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=420-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्र|पद्रः
पद्र m. (-द्रः)<BR>	 1. A village.<BR>	 2. The entrance into a village.<BR> E. पद् to go,<BR>रक् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=420-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्व|पद्वः
पद्व m. (-द्वः)<BR>	 1. The abode or world of human beings.<BR>	 2. A car.<BR>	 3.<BR>A road.<BR> E. पद् to go, वन् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=420-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्वन्
पद्वन् m. (-द्वा) A road.<BR> E. पद् to go, वनिप् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=420-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पन
पन r. 1st. cl. (पनायति) To praise: this root and पण in the same<BR>sense, take आय before the Sārvadhātuka, and some of the<BR>Ārddhadhātuka, affixes. (पनते) To traffic, to buy and sell: see<BR>पण. स्तुतौ भ्वा० आत्म० सक० सेट् । स्वार्थे आय वा तत्र आत्म० ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=420-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पनस|पनसः
पनस m. ((सः)<BR>	 1. The bread-fruit or JACK tree, (Artocarpus integri-<BR>folia.)<BR>	 2. A thorn.<BR>	 3. The name of a monkey.<BR>	 f. (-सा)<BR>	 1. A malady,<BR>pustular and phlegmonoid inflammation of the skin or external<BR>organs.<BR>	 2. A she monkey.<BR>	 3. A female demon.<BR> E. पन् to praise<BR>or be praised, Uṇādi aff. असच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=420-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पनसना
पनसना(ता)लिका f. (-का) The bread-fruit or JACK.<BR> E. पनस, ठन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=420-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पन्थक|पंथक
पन्थक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Produced in or on the road.<BR> E. पथिन्, and वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=420-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पन्न|पन्नं|पन्नः
पन्न mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>	 1. Fallen, gone down or downwards.<BR>	 2. Gone.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-न्नः) Downward motion, falling, descending.<BR> E. पद् to go, aff. क्त,<BR>deriv. irr., otherwise पद् to go, Unādi aff. नन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=420-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पन्नग|पन्नगः
पन्नग m. (-गः)<BR>	 1. A snake.<BR>	 2. A drug: see पद्मकाष्ठ.<BR>	 f. (-गी) The snake<BR>goddess MANASĀ.<BR>	 n. (-गं) Lead.<BR> E. पन्न a fallen, ग who goes, or पद्<BR>a foot, न not, ग who goes,; moving without feet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=420-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पन्नगाशन|पन्नगाशनः
पन्नगाशन m. (-नः) A name of GARUḌA, the bird and vehicle of VIṢṆU.<BR>E. पन्नग a snake, and अशन food; the snake-eater.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=420-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पन्नद्धा
पन्नद्धा f. (-द्धा) A leather shoe or boot.<BR> E. पद् a foot, नह to bind, aff. क्त,<BR>deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=420-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पनद्ध्री
पनद्ध्री f. (-द्ध्री) A shoe, a boot.<BR> E. पद् a foot, नह् to bind, affs. ष्ट्रन्, or<BR>ङीष् optionally added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=420-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पपि|पपिः
पपि mfn. (-पिः-पिः-पि) Who or what drinks.<BR>	 m. (-पिः) The moon.<BR> E. पा<BR>to drink, कि aff. and the root repeated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=420-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पपिस्
पपिस् m. (-पीः)<BR>	 1. The moon.<BR>	 2. The sun.<BR> E. पा to drink, reiterated by<BR>special rule, Unādi aff. इस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=420-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पपीति
पपीति f. (-तिः) Mutual or reciprocal drinking, drinking alike or to-<BR>gether.<BR> E. पा to drink, in the reiterative form, aff. क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=420-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पपु|पपुः
पपु m. (-युः) A fosterer, a protector.<BR>	 f. (-पुः) A nurse, a fostermother.<BR>E. पा to cherish, कु aff. and the radical consonant repeated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=420-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पम्पा|पंपा
पम्पा f. (-म्पा)<BR>	 1. The name of a river, in the south of India.<BR>	 2. Name<BR>of a lake in the Dandaka forest.<BR> E. पा to drink, प Unādi aff., मन्<BR>inserted, and the radical vowel made short.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=420-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पय|पयः
पय r.<BR>	 1. st. cl. (पयते) To go, to move. भ्वा० आत्म० सक० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=420-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पयश्चय|पयश्चयः
पयश्चय m. (-यः) A piece of water.<BR> E. पयस् water, चय collection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=420-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पयस्
पयस् n. (-यः)<BR>	 1. Water.<BR>	 2. Milk.<BR>	 3. Semen virile.<BR>	 4. Boiled-rice.<BR>	 5.<BR>Night.<BR> E. पय् to go, असुन् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=420-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पयस
पयस n. (-सं)<BR>	 1. Water.<BR>	 2. Milk.<BR> E. पयस् the same, अच् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=420-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पयस्प
पयस्प m. (-स्पः) A cat.<BR> E. पयस् milk, and प who drinks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=420-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पयस्य|पयस्यं|पयस्यः
पयस्य mfn. (-स्यः-स्या-स्यं)<BR>	 1. Made from milk, (curds, butter, cheese, &c.)<BR>2. Relating to or connected with milk or water.<BR>	 3. A cat.<BR>	 f. (-स्या)<BR>1. A shrub, (Asclepias rosea.)<BR>	 2. A medicinal kind of moon plant.<BR>3. A drug: see क्षीरकाकोली.<BR>	 4. Curds of two milk whey.<BR>	 5. Any<BR>plant yielding a milky sap, as the Euphorbia, the Asclepias, &c.<BR>E. पयस् milk, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=420-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पयस्वल|पयस्वलः
पयस्वल m. (-लः) A goat.<BR> E. पयस्, वलच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=420-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पयस्विनी
पयस्विनी f. (-नी)<BR>	 1. A river.<BR>	 2. A milch cow.<BR>	 3. Night.<BR>	 4. A she-goat.<BR>E. पयस् water or milk, विनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=420-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पयोगड|पयोगडः
पयोगड(ल) m. (-डः or -लः) Hail.<BR>	 n. (-डं) An island.<BR> E. पयस् water, गड a drop.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=420-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पयोघन|पयोघनः
पयोघन m. (-नः) Hail.<BR> E. पयस् water. घन a lump.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=420-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पयोजन्मन्
पयोजन्मन् m. (-न्मा) A cloud.<BR> E. पयस् water, जन्मन् origin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=420-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पयोद|पयोदः
पयोद m. (-दः) A cloud.<BR> E. पयस्, and द what gives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=420-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पयोधर|पयोधरः
पयोधर m. (-रः) A woman's breast.<BR>	 2. A cloud.<BR>	 3. The sugarcane.<BR>	 4.<BR>The cocoanut.<BR>	 5. A sort of rush, (Scirpus kysoor.)<BR>	 6. A fragrant<BR>grass, (Cyperus rotundus, &c.)<BR>	 7. An udder.<BR>	 8. The back-bone.<BR>	 9.<BR>(In Prosody) A scolius.<BR> E. पयस् milk or water, and धर containing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=420-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पयोधस्
पयोधस् m. (-धाः)<BR>	 1. The ocean.<BR>	 2. A piece of water.<BR>	 3. A cloud E.<BR>पयस् water, धा to contain, Unādi aff. असि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=420-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पयोधि|पयोधिः
पयोधि m. (-धिः) The ocean.<BR> E. पयस्, and धा to have, कि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=420-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पयोधिक|पयोधिकं
पयोधिक n. (-कं) The cuttle-fish-bone.<BR> E. पयोधि, and कन् aff. समुद्रफेने ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=420-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पयोनिधि|पयोनिधिः
पयोनिधि m. (-धिः) The ocean.<BR> E. पयस्, and निधि a treasure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=420-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पयोमुच्
पयोमुच् m. (-मुक्) A cloud.<BR> E. पयस्, and मुच् what lets go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=420-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पयोर|पयोरः
पयोर m. (-रः) The Khayar, (Mimosa catechu.)<BR> E. पयस् water, रा to<BR>get, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=420-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पयोराशि|पयोराशिः
पयोराशि f. (-शिः) A piece of water.<BR> E. पयस्, and राशि a quantity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=420-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पयोव्रत|पयोव्रतः
पयोव्रत n. (-तं) Living upon milk for a month, which with prayer<BR>and residence in a cow house, is an expiation or receiving an<BR>unsuitable present; offering of milk to VIṢṆU, and subsisting<BR>upon it for twelve days; also for one or for three days is consi-<BR>dered as a religious act.<BR> E. पयस् milk, and व्रत religious observance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=420-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पयोष्णी
पयोष्णी f. (-ष्णी) A river that rises in the Vindhya mountain. The<BR>Narmadā according to some, the Tapti according to others.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=420-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर|परं|परः
पर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>	 1. Distant, removed, remote.<BR>	 2. Best, pre-eminent.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=421-a" target="_blank">Page421-a+ 60</a>]<BR>3. Subsequent, after, following.<BR>	 4. Other, different.<BR>	 5. Inimical,<BR>hostile, estranged, adverse.<BR>	 6. Addicted to, attached to, engaged<BR>in.<BR>	 7. More, exceeding, as परं शतं more than a hundred, परो लक्षः<BR>more then a Lac: these are also considered as distinct com-<BR>pounds, see the next.<BR>	 8. Higher, Superior.<BR>	 9. Beyond.<BR>	 10.<BR>Last, final.<BR>	 m. (रः)<BR>	 1. An enemy 2. The life of BRAMHĀ.<BR>	 n. ind.<BR>(-रं)<BR>	 1. Only, alone.<BR>	 2. After, afterwards. subst.<BR>	 1. Final beatitude.<BR>2. The Supreme spirit.<BR>	 3. (In Logic,) One species of common<BR>property; that which comprehends many objects, genus; or it<BR>is the same with existence, as the common property of all things.<BR>E. पॄ to fill, &c. aff. भावे अप् or कर्त्तरि अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=420-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परःशत|परःशतं
परःशत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) More than a hundred, many.<BR> E. पर more, and<BR>शत a hundred: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=421-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परःश्वस्
परःश्वस् ind. (-श्वः) The day after tomorrow.<BR> E. पर after, श्वस् tomorrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=421-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परःसहस्र|परःसहस्रं
परःसहस्र mfn. (-स्रः-स्रा-स्रं) More than a thousand.<BR> E. पर more, and<BR>सहस्र a thousand: see पर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=421-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परकलत्र
परकलत्र n. (-त्रं) Another's wife.<BR> E. पर, and कलत्र a wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=421-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परकलत्राभिगमन
परकलत्राभिगमन n. (-नं) Intriguing with another man's wife, adultery.<BR>E. परकलत्र another's wife, अभिगमन approaching.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=421-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परकीय|परकीयं
परकीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Another, belonging to another.<BR>	 f. (-या) The<BR>mistress or wife of another, one of the three objects of love,<BR>according to the Sringāra or amatory, doctrine.<BR> E. पर another,<BR>छ aff. कुक् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=421-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परक्षेत्र|परक्षेत्रं
परक्षेत्र n. (-त्रं)<BR>	 1. Another man's wife.<BR>	 2. Another's body.<BR>	 3. Another's<BR>field.<BR> E. पर another, क्षेत्र a field.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=421-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परग्रन्थि|परग्रंथि|परग्रन्थिः
परग्रन्थि m. (-न्थिः) An articulation, a finger-joint.<BR> E. पर after, ग्रन्थि a joining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=421-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परग्लानि|परग्लानिः
परग्लानि f. (-निः) Reduction or subjugation of an enemy.<BR> E. पर, and<BR>ग्लानि vexing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=421-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परछन्द|परच्छन्द|परच्छंद|परच्छन्दः
परछन्द mfn. (-न्दः-न्दा-न्दं) Dependant, subservient, subjected.<BR> E. पर<BR>another, छन्द inclination.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=421-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परछिद्र|परच्छिद्र|परच्छिद्रं
परछिद्र n. (-द्रं) A fault or defect in another.<BR> E. पर and छिद्र flaw.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=421-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परजात|परजातः
परजात mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Adopted, fostered, nourished by a stranger.<BR>2. Dependant, servile, subjected.<BR>	 m. (-तः)<BR>	 1. The kokila.<BR>	 2. A ser-<BR>vant.<BR> E. पर another, and जात born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=421-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परजित|परजितः
परजित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Nourished by a stranger.<BR>	 2. Conquered,<BR>or subdued by another.<BR>	 3. The kokila. पर another, and जित con-<BR>quered, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=421-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परञ्ज|परंज|परंजः|परञ्जः
परञ्ज m. (-ञ्जः)<BR>	 1. An oil press.<BR>	 2. Froth, foam.<BR>	 3. The blade of a<BR>sword or a knife.<BR>	 4. A sword or scimitar.<BR>	 f. (-ञ्जा) The sound of<BR>instruments at a festival.<BR>	 n. (-ञ्जं) The sword of INDRA.<BR> E. पर in<BR>the second case, another, and जि to conquer, aff. ड; some works<BR>have परज, and others पराञ्ज in place of this word.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=421-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परञ्जन|परंजन|परंजनः|परञ्जनः
परञ्जन m. (-नः) A name of VARUṆA, the regent of water.<BR> E. पर an-<BR>other, जि to conquer, deriv. irr; also परञ्जय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=421-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परञ्जय|परंजय|परंजयः|परञ्जयः
परञ्जय m. (-यः) VARUṆA: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=421-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परतन्त्र|परतंत्र|परतन्त्रः
परतन्त्र mfn. (-न्त्रः-न्त्रा-न्त्रं) Subservient, obedient, dependant.<BR> E. पर another, तन्त्र will.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=421-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परतम
परतम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं) Greatest.<BR> E. पर, and तरप् aff. of the superlative.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=421-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परतर
परतर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Greater, more.<BR> E. पर more, and तरप aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=421-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परतस्
परतस् ind.<BR>	 1. Afterwards.<BR>	 2. Behind.<BR>	 3. Otherwise, differently.<BR>	 4.<BR>From an enemy.<BR> E. पर or परा, and अतमुच् aff. According to<BR>Vāchaspatya:--1. From another.<BR>	 2. Dependence.<BR> E. पर + विभक्तर्थे-<BR>तसिल् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=421-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परत्र|परत्रं
परत्र ind.<BR>	 1. The next world, futurity.<BR>	 2. Further on, in the sequel.<BR>E. पर another, त्रल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=421-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परत्रभीरु|परत्रभीरुः
परत्रभीरु m. (-रूः) A pious man, one standing in awe of futurity. E.<BR>परत्र the next world, and भीरु timid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=421-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परत्व|परत्वं
परत्व n. (-त्वं)<BR>	 1. Difference, distinction, separateness.<BR>	 2. Hostility.<BR>	 3.<BR>(In Logic,) Priority of place or time, proximity, juvenility.<BR>	 4.<BR>The nature of common or generic property.<BR> E. त्व added to पर;<BR>also with तल्, परता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=421-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परदार|परदारः
परदार m. (-रः) Plu. Another's wife.<BR> E. पर, and दार a wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=421-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परदारगमन
परदारगमन n. (नं) Adultery, adulterous intercourse or intrigue.<BR> E. पर-<BR>दार, and गमन frequenting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=421-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परदाराभिमर्ष
परदाराभिमर्ष m. (-र्षः) Intriguing with another man's wife.<BR> E. परदार,<BR>and अभिमर्ष contact.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=421-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परदारोपसेवन
परदारोपसेवन n. (-नं) Intriguing with another's wife.<BR> E. परदार, and उप-<BR>सेवन frequenting; also परदारोपसेवा ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=421-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परदुःख|परदुःखं
परदुःख n. (-खं) The pain or sorrow of another.<BR> E. पर, and दुख pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=421-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परदेश|परदेशः
परदेश m. (-शः) A foreign country.<BR> E. पर, and द्रेश place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=421-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परदेशिन्
परदेशिन् mfn. (-शी-शिनी-शि) Foreign, exotic.<BR>	 m. (-शी)<BR>	 1. A foreigner.<BR>	 2.<BR>One residing abroad.<BR> E. परदेश, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=421-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परदेशसेविन्
परदेशसेविन् mfn. (-वी-विनी-वि) Living abroad, travelling, traveller.<BR> E. पर<BR>देश, and सेविन् who frequents.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=421-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परदोषकीर्त्तन
परदोषकीर्त्तन n. (-नं) Scandal, calumny, censoriousness.<BR> E. पर, दोष fault,<BR>कीर्त्तन proclaiming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=421-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परद्वेषिन्
परद्वेषिन् mfn. (-षी-षिणी-षि) Hostile, inimical, adverse.<BR> E. पर another,<BR>द्विष् to hate, घिणुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=421-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परद्रव्य
परद्रव्य n. (-व्यं) Another's property.<BR> E. पर, and द्रव्य thing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=421-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परद्रोहिन्
परद्रोहिन् mfn. (-ही-हिणी-हि) Tyrannising over another.<BR> E. पर, and<BR>द्रोहिन् injurious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=421-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परधन
परधन n. (-नं) Another's wealth.<BR> E. पर, and धन wealth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=421-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परधनास्वादनसुख
परधनास्वादनसुख n. (-खं) Feeding luxuriously at another's expense. E.<BR>परधन, आस्वादन eating, सुख pleasure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=421-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परधर्म्म|परधर्म|परधर्मः
परधर्म्म m. (-र्म्मः) Another's duty or business, the occupation of another<BR>caste.<BR> E. पर, and धर्म्म duty. उत्कृष्ट धर्मेच ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=421-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परध्यान|परध्यानं
परध्यान n. (-नं) Intent absorption or abstraction in the subject of medi-<BR>tation.<BR> E. पर, and ध्यान meditating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=421-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परन्तप|परंतप|परंतपः|परन्तपः
परन्तप mfn. (-पः-पा-पं) Vexing or annoying another, subduing a foe.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-पः) A conqueror.<BR> E. पर another, तप to heat or inflame, aff. खच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=421-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परपद|परपदं
परपद n. (-दं)<BR>	 1. Eminence, high station.<BR>	 2. Final felicity.<BR> E. पर<BR>supreme, पद, a place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=421-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परपरिग्रह|परपरिग्रहः
परपरिग्रह m. (-हः) The family or dependants of another.<BR> E. पर, and<BR>परिग्रह dependants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=421-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परपाक
परपाक m. (-कः) What is dressed or cooked by another, another's food.<BR>E. पर, and पाक cooking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=421-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परपाकनिवृत्त|परपाकनिवृत्तः
परपाकनिवृत्त m. (-त्तः) One who dresses his own food without observing<BR>the expiatory sacrifice for the five Sūnas, or places of destruction<BR>to animal life: see पञ्चसूना.<BR> E. पर another, पाक cooking, and निवृत्त<BR>ceased.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=421-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परपाकरत|परपाकरतः
परपाकरत m. (-तः) One who observes all the due ceremonies prepara-<BR>tory to cooking, but lives upon others.<BR> E. पर another, पाक cooking,<BR>रत constant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=421-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परपाकरुचि|परपाकरुचिः
परपाकरुचि m. (-चिः) A constant guest at other's tables.<BR> E. पर another,<BR>पाक cooking, and रुचि shining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=421-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परपिण्ड|परपिंड|परपिण्डः
परपिण्ड n. (-ण्डं) Food given by another.<BR> E. पर, and पिण्ड a ball of rice or meat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=421-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परपिण्डाद|परपिंडाद|परपिण्डादः
परपिण्डाद mfn. (-दः-दा-दं) Feeding at another's cost.<BR> E. परपिण्ड, and आद<BR>who takes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=421-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परपुरुष|परपुरुषः
परपुरुष m. (-षः)<BR>	 1. A name of VIṢṆU.<BR>	 2. Another man.<BR> E. पर supreme,<BR>or other, and पुरुष a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=421-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परपुष्ट|परपुष्टः
परपुष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्ठा-ष्टं)<BR>	 1. Fostered, nourished, &c. by a stranger.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-ष्टः) The Kokila or Indian cuckoo.<BR>	 f. (-ष्टा)<BR>	 1. A harlot, a whore.<BR>	 2.<BR>A parasite plant.<BR> E. पर another, पुष्ट cherished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=421-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परपुष्टमहोत्सव|परपुष्टमहोत्सवः
परपुष्टमहोत्सव m. (-वः) The mango.<BR> E. परपुष्ट the cuckoo, महा great, and<BR>उत्सव festival.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=421-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परपूर्व्वा|परपूर्वा
परपूर्व्वा f. (-र्व्वा) A woman formerly married.<BR> E. पर another, (husband,)<BR>पूर्व्व prior, fem. aff. टाप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=421-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परपूर्व्वापति|परपूर्वापति
परपूर्व्वापति m. (-तिः) The husband of a woman remarried.<BR> E. परपूर्व्वा,<BR>and पति a husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=421-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परप्रतिनप्तृ
परप्रतिनप्तृ m. (-प्ता) A great-great-grandson.<BR> E. पर subsequent, प्रति after,<BR>नप्तृ a grandson.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=421-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परप्रपौत्र|परप्रपौत्रः
परप्रपौत्र m. (-त्रः) A great-great-grandson.<BR> E. पर, subsequent, प्रपौत्र<BR>great-grandson.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=422-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परप्रेष्यत्व
परप्रेष्यत्व n. (-त्वं) Servitude, slavery.<BR> E. पर, and प्रेष्यत्व service.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=422-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परव्रह्मन्
परव्रह्मन् n. (-ह्म) The supreme Being.<BR> E. पर, and व्रह्म the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=422-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परभाग|परभागः
परभाग m. (-गः)<BR>	 1. Excellence, superior merit, supremacy.<BR>	 2. Good<BR>fortune, prosperity.<BR>	 3. The last part, residue, remainder.<BR> E. पर<BR>best, and भाग portion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=422-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परभाग्य
परभाग्य n. (-ग्यं) Another's wealth or prosperity.<BR> E. पर, and भाग्य good fortune.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=422-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परभुक्त
परभुक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं) Possessed or enjoyed by another.<BR> E. पर, and<BR>भुक्त enjoyed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=422-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परभुमि
परभुमि f. (-मिः) A foreign or an enemy's country.<BR> E. पर, and भूमि land.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=422-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परभूमिष्ठ
परभूमिष्ठ mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठा-ष्ठं) Living or being in a foreign or an enemy's<BR>country.<BR> E. परभूमि, and स्थ who stays.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=422-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परभूषण
परभूषण n. (-णं) Another's ornament.<BR>	 m. (-णः) Peace purchased by<BR>ceding the produce of lands.<BR> E. पर, and भूषण ornament.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=422-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परभृत्
परभृत् m. (-भृत्) A crow.<BR> E. पर another, (the cuckoo,) and भृत् who<BR>nourishes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=422-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परभृत|परभृतः
परभृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Cherished or nourished by a stranger, fostered,<BR>adopted.<BR>	 m. (-तः) The Indian cuckoo, which is supposed to leave<BR>its eggs in the nest of the crow to be hatched.<BR> E. पर another,<BR>and भृत nourished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=422-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परभेदक
परभेदक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Destroying or subduing a foe,<BR> E. पर, and भेदक<BR>who breaks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=422-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परम्
परम् ind. A particle of command.<BR>	 2. Of dismissal or refusal.<BR>	 3. Here-<BR>after, afterwards.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=422-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परम|परमः
परम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>	 1. Best, most excellent.<BR>	 2. Chief principal, preced-<BR>ing 3. First, chief part.<BR>	 4. Adequate. ind. (-मं)<BR>	 1. A term of<BR>assent, yes 2. A term of command.<BR> E. पर best, मा to mete, aff. ड<BR>or डम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=422-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परमगति|परमगतिः
परमगति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Chief object or refuge, as a god, protector.<BR>	 2.<BR>Final felicity.<BR> E. परम, and गति going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=422-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परमगव|परमगवः
परमगव mf. (-वः-वी) An excellent bull or cow.<BR> E. परम, and गो a cow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=422-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परमगहन
परमगहन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Very mysterious or profound.<BR> E. परम, and<BR>गहन thick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=422-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परमत|परमतः
परमत n. (-तं) A different opinion or doctrine.<BR> E. पर, and मत thought.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=422-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परमपद|परमपदः
परमपद n. (-दं)<BR>	 1. Eminence, high station.<BR>	 2. Final felicity<BR> E. परम, and<BR>पद station.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=422-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परमब्रह्मन्
परमब्रह्मन् n. (-ह्म) The Supreme Spirit.<BR> E. परम, and ब्रह्मन् the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=422-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परमराज|परमराजः
परमराज m. (-जः) A supreme monarch.<BR> E. परम, and राजन् a king, टच्<BR>aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=422-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परमर्षि|परमर्षिः
परमर्षि m. (-र्षिः) A Ṛṣi or divine sage, of a peculiar order or division,<BR>comprising the Muni BHELA and others.<BR> E. परम excellent, and<BR>ऋषि a divine sage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=422-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परमर्म्मज्ञ|परमर्मज्ञ
परमर्म्मज्ञ m. (-ज्ञः) One who knows another's character or disposition. E.<BR>पर, and मर्म्म a vital point, and ज्ञ who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=422-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परमस्वधर्म्मन्|परमस्वधर्मन्
परमस्वधर्म्मन् m. (-र्म्मा) A virtuous or pious man, one who attends scrupu-<BR>lously to the proper duties of his tribe or station.<BR> E. परम best,<BR>स्व own, धर्म्म virtue or duty, and अनिच् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=422-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परमहंस|परमहंसः
परमहंस m. (-सः) An ascetic, a religious man who has subdued all his<BR>senses by abstract meditation.<BR> E. परम best or first, हंस devotee.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=422-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परमागति
परमागति f. (-तिः) Final beatitude.<BR> E. परमा best, गति going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=422-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परमाङ्गना|परमांगना
परमाङ्गना f. (-ना) A beautiful woman.<BR> E. परम, and अङ्गना a woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=422-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परमाणु|परमाणुः
परमाणु m. (-णुः)<BR>	 1. An atom, the invisible base of all aggregate bodies;<BR>thirty of them are supposed to form a mote in a sunbeam;<BR>the lowest measure of weight; in Logic, six of them form the<BR>first perceptible object.<BR>	 2. A measure of time, the sun's passage<BR>past an atom of matter.<BR> E. परम first, and अणु an atom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=422-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परमाण्वङ्गक|परमाण्वङ्गकः
परमाण्वङ्गक m. (-कः) A name of VIṢṆU.<BR> E. परमाणु an atom, अङ्ग the<BR>body, कप् aff., deriv. irr.; smaller than the smallest; as he is<BR>larger than the largest, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=422-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परमात्मन्
परमात्मन् m. (-त्मा) The Supreme Being, considered as the soul of the<BR>universe.<BR> E. परम first, आत्मन् spirit or soul.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=422-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परमाद्वैत|परमाद्वैतः
परमाद्वैत n. (-तं) Pure unitarianism.<BR>	 m. (-तः) VIṢṆU, the only supreme.<BR>E. परम, and अद्वैत without duality.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=422-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परमान्न|परमान्नं
परमान्न n. (-न्नं) An oblation of rice to progenitors or gods, boiled with<BR>milk and sugar.<BR> E. परम best, and अन्न boiled rice; or परम the best,<BR>the supreme, (deities, &c.) and अन्न food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=422-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परमापम|परमापमः
परमापम m. (-मः)<BR>	 1. The inclination of a planet's orbit to the ecliptic.<BR>2. The sine of the sun's greatest declination.<BR> E. परम, and अपम<BR>declination.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=422-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परमायुष|परमायुषः
परमायुष m. (-षः) A particular tree: see असन ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=422-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परमायुस्
परमायुस् m. (-युः) The longest period of life, either in men or animals.<BR>E. परम and आयुस life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=422-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परमार्थ|परमार्थः
परमार्थ m. (-र्थः)<BR>	 1. Truth, fitness.<BR>	 2. Spiritual knowledge.<BR>	 3. Any excel-<BR>lent or important aim or object.<BR>	 4. The best sense.<BR>	 5. The best<BR>kind of wealth<BR> E. परम, and अर्थ object.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=422-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परमार्थविद्
परमार्थविद् m. (-वित्) A sage, a philosopher, one who knows the truth.<BR>E. परमार्थ, and विद् who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=422-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परमार्थविन्द्
परमार्थविन्द् mfn. (-न्दः-न्दा-न्दं) Who or what acquires knowledge of truth,<BR>the best kind of wealth, &c.<BR> E. परमार्थ, and विद् to acquire, श aff.<BR>मुम् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=422-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परमावधि
परमावधि f. (-धिः) Utmost term or limit.<BR> E. परम, and अवधि limit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=422-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परमार्हत|परमार्हतः
परमार्हत m. (-तः) A king and holy saint, apparently the same as SĀLI-<BR>BĀHANA.<BR> E. परम excellent, अर्हत a Jina.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=422-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परमृत्यु|परमृत्युः
परमृत्यु m. (-त्युः) A crow.<BR> E. पर another, and मृत्यु death; having many enemies.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=422-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परमेश्वर|परमेश्वरः
परमेश्वर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. The Supreme Being.<BR>	 2. SĪVA.<BR>	 3. VIṢṆU.<BR>	 f. (-री)<BR>DURGĀ.<BR> E. परम best, ईश्वर lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=422-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परमेष्ठ|परमेष्ठः
परमेष्ठ mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठा-ष्ठं) Supreme, superior.<BR>	 m. (-ष्ठः)<BR>	 1. BRAMHĀ.<BR>	 2. A<BR>deity.<BR> E. परमे, in heaven, and स्थ who stays or is.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=422-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परमेष्ठिन्
परमेष्ठिन् m. (-ष्ठी)<BR>	 1. A name of BRAMHĀ.<BR>	 2. A Jina or deified teacher<BR>of the Jaina sect.<BR>	 3. A kind of Sālagrām stone.<BR>	 4. A Guru or<BR>spiritual guide.<BR> E. परमे in the most exalted place, in heaven, स्था<BR>to be, Unādi aff. निन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=422-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परम्पद|परंपदं
परम्पद n. (-दं)<BR>	 1. Eternal felicity.<BR>	 2. The abode of VIṢṆU.<BR> E. पर् an-<BR>other, पद degree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=422-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परम्पर|परंपर|परंपरः|परम्परः
परम्पर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Successive, proceeding from one to another, from<BR>father to son, &c.<BR>	 m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A sort of deer.<BR>	 2. A great-great-grand-<BR>son.<BR>	 f. (-रा)<BR>	 1. Race, progeny, lineage.<BR>	 2. Order, method, continu-<BR>ous arrangement, regular series or succession.<BR>	 2. Hurting, killing,<BR>injury.<BR> E. पर subsequent, repeated, and the nasal augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=422-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परम्परतस्
परम्परतस् ind. Mutually.<BR> E. परम्पर, and तसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=422-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परम्पराक|परंपराक|परम्पराकं
परम्पराक n. (-कं) Immolating animals in sacrifice.<BR> E. परम्पर tradi-<BR>tionary or successive, and अक going or worshipping; or परम्<BR>much, पर the best, and अक going, custom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=422-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परम्परीण|परंपरीण|परम्परीणं
परम्परीण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>	 1. Hereditary, what has come by inheritance<BR>or descent.<BR>	 2. Traditional.<BR> E. परम् another, and पर again, another,<BR>ख aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=422-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पररु|पररुः
पररु m. (-रुः) A potherb, (Eclipta prostrata;) also केशराज.<BR> E. पर much,<BR>रुह् to grow, डु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=422-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पररूप
पररूप mfn. (-पः-पा-पं) परस्य रूपमिव रूपमस्य । स्वोत्तरवर्त्तिपरस्येव रूपवति “एङिपररूपम्” पानिनि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=422-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परलोक|परलोकं|परलोकः
परलोक m. (-कः) Heaven, paradise.<BR> E. पर another, and लोक world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=422-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परलोकगम|परलोकगमः
परलोकगम m. (-मः) Death, dying.<BR> E. पर another, लोक world, and गम<BR>going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=422-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परवत्|परवन्त्
परवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Dependent, subject.<BR> E. पर another, मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=422-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परवश|परवशः
परवश mfn. (-शः-शा-शं)<BR>	 1. Subservient, dependant, subject.<BR>	 2. Deceived.<BR>E. पर another, and वश subjection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=422-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परवाच्य
परवाच्य mfn. (-च्यः-च्या-च्यं) Reprehensible, blamable.<BR>	 n. (-च्यं) Fault,<BR>defect.<BR> E. पर, and वाच्य to be named, not to be spoken of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=422-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परवाणि|परवाणिः
परवाणि m. (-णिः)<BR>	 1. A Judge, a ruler.<BR>	 2. A year.<BR>	 3. The peacock on<BR>which the god KĀRTIKEYA rides.<BR> E. पर best, वा to go, णि aff,<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=422-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परव्रत|परव्रतः
परव्रत m. (-तः) A name of DHRITARĀSHTRA.<BR> E. पर best, व्रत, religi-<BR>ous observance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=423-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परश|परशं|परशः
परश m. (-शः) A kind of stone, the touch of which turns iron into<BR>gold, the philosopher's stone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=423-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परशव्य|परशव्यं
परशव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं) Fit or proper for a hatchet.<BR> E. परशु an axe, यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=423-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परशु|परशुः
परशु m. (-शुः) An axe, a hatchet.<BR> E. पर another, शु to injure, Unādi<BR>aff. कु, डिच्च ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=423-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परशुधर|परशुधरः
परशुधर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A soldier armed with an axe.<BR>	 2. A name of GANESA.<BR>3. PARASURĀMA: see the next.<BR> E. परशु an axe, धर who holds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=423-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परशुराम|परशुरामः
परशुराम m. (-मः) A hero and demigod; the first of the three RĀMAS,<BR>and the sixth Avatāra or descent of the deity VIṢṆU: who<BR>appeared in the world as the saint JAMADAGNI, for the purpose<BR>of repressing the tyranny and punishing the violence of the<BR>Kṣatriya, or military tribe; PARASURĀMA appears to typify<BR>the tribe of Brāmhans and their contests with the Kṣatrityas. E.<BR>परशु an axe, and राम who delights in; also with कन् added,<BR>परशुरामक; and with the first member, पर्शु, पर्शुराम, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=423-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परश्व|परश्वः
परश्व(स्व)ध m. (-धः) An axe, a hatchet.<BR> E. पर another, an enemy, श्व derived<BR>from श्वि, to grow or thrive; परश्व the prosperity of a foe, धे to<BR>drink, क aff.; what drinks the blood or destroys the life of an<BR>enemy; also पारश्वध and परस्वध.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=423-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परश्वस्
परश्वस् ind. The day after tomorrow.<BR> E. पर after, अवस् tomorrow; also परःश्वस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=423-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परस्
परस् ind. Beyond, further, more than, on the other side of, &c. (Not<BR>used by itself in classical Sanskrit.)<BR> E. पर, पञ्चम्याद्यर्थे बा असि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=423-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परसङ्गत|परसंगत
परसङ्गत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Associated with another.<BR>	 2. Fighting or<BR>engaged with another.<BR> E. पर, and सङ्गत gone with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=423-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परसंज्ञक
परसंज्ञक m. (-कः) The soul.<BR> E. पर best, संज्ञा name or title; aff. कप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=423-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परसम्बन्ध
परसम्बन्ध m. (-न्धः) Relation or connexion with another.<BR> E. पर, and<BR>सम्बन्ध connexion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=423-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परसम्बन्धिन्
परसम्बन्धिन् mfn. (-न्धी-न्धिनी-न्धि)<BR>	 1. Related to another.<BR>	 2. Belonging to<BR>another.<BR> E. परसम्बन्ध, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=423-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परस्तात्
परस्तात् ind.<BR>	 1. Subsequently, afterwards.<BR>	 2. Behind.<BR> E. पर, and<BR>अस्ताति aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=423-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परस्पर|परस्परं
परस्पर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Mutual, interchanging.<BR> E. पर another repeated:<BR>from one to another.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=423-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परस्परज्ञ|परस्परज्ञः
परस्परज्ञ m. (-ज्ञः) A friend, an intimate.<BR> E. परस्पर, and ज्ञ who know.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=423-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परस्परानुमति
परस्परानुमति f. (-तिः) Mutual concurrence or assent.<BR> E. परस्पर, and<BR>अनुमति agreement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=423-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परस्पराम
परस्पराम ind. Mutually.<BR> E. परस्पर, and आम् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=423-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परस्परोपकार
परस्परोपकार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Mutual assistance.<BR>	 2. Offensive and defensive<BR>alliance.<BR> E. परस्पर, उपकार aid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=423-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परस्परोपकारिन्
परस्परोपकारिन् m. (-री)<BR>	 1. An ally.<BR>	 2. An associate, a helper.<BR> E. इनि<BR>added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=423-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परस्मैपद|परस्मैपदं
परस्मैपद n. (-दं) The transitive or active verb.<BR> E. परस्मै to another, पद<BR>an inflected word.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=423-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परस्व
परस्व n. (-स्वं) Another person's property.<BR> E. पर, and स्व own.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=423-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परस्वत्व
परस्वत्व n. (-त्वं) Another's right.<BR> E. पर, and स्वत्व own right.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=423-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परस्वत्वापादन
परस्वत्वापादन n. (-नं) Conferring a right upon another as by gift, &c.<BR>E. परस्वत्व, and आपादन producing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=423-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परस्वध|परस्वधः
परस्वध m. (-धः) An axe: see परश्वध.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=423-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परस्वादायिन्
परस्वादायिन् mfn. (यी-यिनी-यि) Extortionary, extortioner.<BR> E. परस्व, and<BR>आदायिन् taking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=423-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परस्वोपजीविक
परस्वोपजीविक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Dependent, living on the property of<BR>others.<BR> E. परस्व, and उपजीविक subsisting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=423-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परहित
परहित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Friendly, benevolent.<BR>	 2. Good or profitable<BR>form for another.<BR> E. पर, and हित favourable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=423-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परा
परा ind. A participle and prefix implying, 1. Supremacy.<BR>	 2. Libera-<BR>tion.<BR>	 3. Inverted order.<BR>	 4. Pride, contumely.<BR>	 5. Encounter,<BR>mutual presence.<BR>	 6. Excess, exceeding.<BR>	 7. Overcoming, surpass-<BR>ing.<BR>	 8. Going.<BR>	 9. Killing, destroying, injuring. As पराक्रम supe-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=423-b" target="_blank">Page423-b+ 61</a>]<BR>rior power or valour; पराजय defeat; पराभव disgrace; परावर्त्त<BR>turning back, &c. see the following.<BR> E. पॄ to fill, aff. अप्, and आ<BR>added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=423-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराक्
पराक् ind. Crooked, crookedly.<BR> E. परा away, अच् to go, aff. क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=423-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराक|पराकः
पराक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A religious obligation of an expiatory kind, fasting<BR>for twelve days and nights, and keeping the mind attentive,<BR>and organs subdued.<BR>	 2. A sacrificial sword or scimitar.<BR> E. परा<BR>best, अक what goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=423-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराकरण|पराकरणं
पराकरण n. (-णं) Disdaining, disregarding, rejecting.<BR> E. परा before, कृ to do, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=423-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराकुर्व्वन्
पराकुर्व्वन् mfn. (-र्व्वन्-र्व्वन्ती-र्व्वत्) Throwing off or aside, rejecting, dis-<BR>daining.<BR> E. परा, and कुर्व्वन् making.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=423-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराकृत
पराकृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Rejected, set aside, thrown off, disdained. E.<BR>पर, and कृत made.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=423-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराक्रम|पराक्रमः
पराक्रम m. (-मः)<BR>	 1. Power, strength.<BR>	 2. Exertion.<BR>	 3. Valour, prowess.<BR>4. Going out or forth, exit or issue.<BR>	 5. Attacking an enemy.<BR>6. Attempt, enterprise.<BR>	 7. A name of Viṣṇu.<BR> E. परा supremacy,<BR>opposition, &c. and क्रम going, करणे घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=423-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराक्रमज्ञ
पराक्रमज्ञ mfn. (-ज्ञः-ज्ञा-ज्ञं) Knowing the power, (of the enemy.) E.<BR>पराक्रम, and ज्ञ who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=423-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराग|परागः
पराग m. (-गः)<BR>	 1. The pollen or farina of a flower.<BR>	 2. Dust.<BR>	 3. Fra-<BR>grant powder used after bathing.<BR>	 4. Sandal.<BR>	 5. The name of a<BR>mountain.<BR>	 6. Fame, celebrity.<BR>	 7. An eclipse of the sun or moon.<BR>8. Following one's own inclinations.<BR> E. परा implying supremacy,<BR>&c. and ग who goes, ड aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=423-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परागवत्
परागवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Laden with pollen.<BR> E. पराग, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=423-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परागत
परागत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Spread, expanded.<BR>	 2. Budded, blown.<BR> E. पर,<BR>and आङ् before, गम् to go, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=423-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परागिन्
परागिन् mfn. (-गी-गिणी-गि) Laden with pollen.<BR> E. पराग, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=423-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराङ्गद|परांगद|पराङ्गदः
पराङ्गद m. (-दः) A name of ŚIVA.<BR> E. पर another, (DURGĀ,) अङ्ग form<BR>and द who gives; forming with the goddess a deity, half male<BR>and half female; or better, पर an enemy, KĀMADEVA, अङ्ग body,<BR>and द who gives; restoring the body of that deity to shape, after<BR>having reduced it to ashes in a rage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=423-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराङ्गव|परांगव|परांगवः|पराङ्गवः
पराङ्गव m. (-वः) Ocean.<BR> E. पर another, (river,) अङ्ग substance, water,<BR>and व who receives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=423-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराङ्मुख|पराङ्मुखः
पराङ्मुख mfn. (-खः-खी-खं) Turning away, having the face averted. E.<BR>पराञ्च्, and मुख the face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=423-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराङ्मुखता
पराङ्मुखता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Turning away.<BR>	 2. Regardless of.<BR>	 3. Adverse<BR>from.<BR>	 4. Unfavourable.<BR> E. पराङ्मुख, and तल् aff.; also with त्व,<BR>पराङ्मुखत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=423-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराच्
पराच् mfn. (-ङ्ः-ची-क्)<BR>	 1. Situated beyond or on the other side.<BR>	 2. Dis-<BR>tant.<BR> E. परा + अञ्चति-क्किप्ः see परञ्च् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=423-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराचित|पराचितः
पराचित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Cherished or fostered by a stranger.<BR> E. पर<BR>another, आचित nourished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=423-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराचीन|पराचीनः
पराचीन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Turned away, having the face averted.<BR>	 2.<BR>Not minding, not caring about.<BR>	 3. Happening subsequently.<BR>	 4.<BR>Situated on the other side.<BR> E. पराञ्च् or पराच् turned away, ख aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=423-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराजय|पराजयः
पराजय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. Defeat.<BR>	 2. Overpowering.<BR>	 3. Loss, failure, (as in law<BR>suit.)<BR>	 4. The being overcome by, (with an ablative.)<BR> E. परा imply-<BR>ing encounter, contest, and जय victory.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=423-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराजयमाण
पराजयमाण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Overcoming, surpassing, defeating. E.<BR>पर before, जि to conquer, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=423-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराजित|पराजितः
पराजित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Conquered, defeated, overcome.<BR>	 2. Won at<BR>dice, &c.<BR> E. परा encounter, and जित conquered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=423-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराञ्च्|परांच्
पराञ्च् or पराच् mfn. (पराङ् पराची पराक्) Turned away, inverted,<BR>reversed.<BR> E. परा away, अञ्च् to go, aff. क्विन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=423-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराच्
परभूमिष्ठ mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठा-ष्ठं) Living or being in a foreign or an enemy's<BR>country.<BR> E. परभूमि, and स्थ who stays.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=422-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराञ्ज|परांजः|पराञ्जः
पराञ्ज m. (ञ्जः)<BR>	 1. An oil mill.<BR>	 2. Froth or foam.<BR>	 3. The blade of a<BR>sword or knife: see परञ्ज.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=423-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परात्पर|परात्परः
परात्पर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Superior to the best.<BR> E. पर in the fifth case,<BR>and repeated in the first.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=423-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परात्प्रिय|परात्प्रियः
परात्प्रिय m. (-यः) A kind of reed, (Saccharum spontaneum.) उल इतिभाषा ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=423-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परादन|परादनः
परादन mf. (-नः-ना) A horse of the Persian breed.<BR> E. परा exceeding, अदन<BR>food. (अरवी घोडा) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=424-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराधि|पराधिः
पराधि m. (-धिः) Hunting, the chase. अन्यस्याधौकर्म०, परममानसव्यथायाम्च ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=424-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराधिकार
पराधिकार m. (-रः) Another person's office or post.<BR> E. पर, and अधिकार<BR>superintendence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=424-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराधिकारचर्च्चा|पराधिकारचर्चा
पराधिकारचर्च्चा f. (-र्च्चा) Officiousness, interference with another's con-<BR>cerns.<BR> E. पराघिकार, and चर्च्चा searching.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=424-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराधीन|पराधीनः
पराधीन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Dependant, subject, subservient.<BR> E. पर another,<BR>and अधीन humble, docile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=424-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराधीनता
पराधीनता f. (-ता) Subjection, dependence.<BR> E. तल् added to the last;<BR>with त्य, पराधीनत्व n. (-त्वं)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=424-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परान
परान(ण)सा f. (-सा) The practice of medicine, administering remedies.<BR>E. परान् enemies, (disease,) षो to destroy, aff. ड; form irr; or<BR>correctly: परा + अन-करणे वा अस ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=424-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परान्न|परान्नं|परान्नः
परान्न mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं) Living at another's expense.<BR>	 n. (-न्नं)<BR>	 1. Food<BR>supplied by another.<BR>	 2. Food dressed or touched by or belonging<BR>to another.<BR> E. पर another, अन्न food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=424-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परान्नभोजिन्
परान्नभोजिन् mfn. (-जी-जिनी-जि) Living at another's cost.<BR> E. परान्न, and<BR>भोजिन् who eats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=424-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराप|परापं
पराप mfn. (-पः-पा-पं) A place, &c. whence water has retired.<BR> E. पर<BR>away, अप water; also परेप.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=424-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परापतत्
परापतत् mfn. (-तन्-तन्ती-तत्) Coming back quickly, returning hastily<BR>E. पर, and आङ् before, पत् to go, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=424-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परापर|परापरं|परापरः
परापर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Best and worst, prior and posterior, in front<BR>and behind, earlier and later, &c.<BR>	 n. (-रं) (In Logic,) Community<BR>of property intermediate between the greatest and smallest num-<BR>bers: a species, as being between genus and individual.<BR>	 m. (-रः)<BR>A Guru of an intermediate class, a term applied in the Tantras<BR>to the goddess DURGĀ.<BR> E. पर, and अपर another.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=424-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराभ
पराभ(भा)व m. (वः)<BR>	 1. Discomfiting, overcoming.<BR>	 2. Contempt, disres-<BR>pect, disgrace.<BR>	 3. Destruction.<BR>	 4. Mortification, humiliation. E.<BR>परा disgrace, भू to be, अप् aff. or rarely घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=424-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराभूत|पराभूतः
पराभूत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Defeated, discomfited, overcome.<BR>	 2. Degrated,<BR>humbled, treated with contempt.<BR> E. परा disgrace, and भू been,<BR>become, from भू with क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=424-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परामर्श|परामर्शः
परामर्श m. (-र्शः)<BR>	 1. Discrimination, discriminating, distinguishing,<BR>judgment.<BR>	 2. (In Logic,) Drawing conclusions from analogy or<BR>experience: knowledge of the existence of hetu in the Paksha.<BR>	 3.<BR>Seizing, pulling.<BR>	 4. Violence, assault, attack.<BR>	 5. Hindrance.<BR>	 6.<BR>Reflection, consideration, investigation.<BR> E. परा implying supre-<BR>macy, &c. मृश् to deliberate, भावे घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=424-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परामर्ष
परामर्ष m. (-र्षः) Forbearance.<BR> E. परा, and मृष् to bear, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=424-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परामृत|परामृतं
परामृत n. (-तं) Raining.<BR> E. पर best, अमृत water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=424-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परामृष्ट|परामृष्टः
परामृष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>	 1. Weighed, considered, Judged.<BR>	 2. Con-<BR>nected with.<BR>	 3. Touched or affected by.<BR>	 4. Borne, endured.<BR>	 5.<BR>Roughly handled, violated.<BR> E. पर, and आङ् before, मृश् to deliber-<BR>ate, or मृष् to bear, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=424-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परायण|परायणं
परायण mfn. subst. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>	 1. Adherence to any pursuit, attachment<BR>to any object.<BR>	 2. Dependence upon.<BR>	 3. Best refuge. adj.<BR>	 1. Adher-<BR>ing or attached to.<BR>	 2. Connected with, depending upon.<BR>	 3. Wish-<BR>ed, desired.<BR>	 n. (-णं) A religious order or division.<BR> E. पर only,<BR>(one object,) अयन going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=424-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परायत्त|परायत्तं
परायत्त mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं) Dependant, subject.<BR> E. पर another, आयत्त<BR>tame, humble.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=424-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परारि
परारि ind. The year before last.<BR> E. पर another, (last.) अरि aff. in this sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=424-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परारित्न|परारित्नः
परारित्न mfn. (-त्नः-त्ना-त्नं) Belonging to the year before last.<BR> E. परारि as<BR>above, and त्न aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=424-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परारु|परारुः
परारु m. (-रु.) A kind of gourd, (momordica charantia.)<BR> E. पृ to fill<BR>or satisfy, आरु aff. or परा + ऋ + उण् । (डच्छा) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=424-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परारुक|परारुकः
परारुक m. (-कः) A stone or rock.<BR> E. परारु a gourd, कन् aff. of comparison.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=424-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परार्थ|परार्थः
परार्थ mfn. (-र्थः-र्था-र्थं)<BR>	 1. Having another object or sense, &c.<BR>	 2.<BR>Designed or purposed by another.<BR>	 3. The highest interest.<BR>	 4.<BR>The chief meaning.<BR>	 n. (-र्थं) For the sake or good of another. E.<BR>पर, and अर्थ object.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=424-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परार्थवादिन्
परार्थवादिन् mfn. (-दी-दिनी-दि) Officious, intermeddling.<BR> E. परार्थ, and<BR>वादिन् who speaks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=424-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परार्द्ध|परार्द्धं
परार्द्ध n. (-र्द्धं)<BR>	 1. A great number, a lack of lacks of crores, or a number<BR>equal to half the term of BRAMHĀ'S life, or as many mortal days<BR>as are equal to fifty of his years.<BR>	 2. The other part, the latter<BR>half.<BR> E. पर, and अर्द्ध half.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=424-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परार्द्ध्य|परार्द्ध्यः
परार्द्ध्य mfn. (-र्द्ध्यः-र्द्ध्या-र्द्ध्यं)<BR>	 1. Excellent, chief, principal, best.<BR>	 2. Most<BR>costly.<BR>	 3. Most beautiful.<BR>	 4. Most exalted, highly esteemed.<BR>	 5.<BR>Most remote, most distant in number.<BR>	 n. (-र्द्ध्यं) An immense or<BR>infinite number; see the last.<BR> E. परा best, अर्द्ध part, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=424-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परावज्ञा
परावज्ञा f. (-ज्ञा) Indignity, insult, (received.)<BR> E. पर, and अवज्ञा disrespect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=424-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परावर
परावर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>	 1. Before and after, prior and subsequent, far and<BR>near, earlier and later, higher and lower.<BR>	 2. All including.<BR> E. पर,<BR>and अवर after.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=424-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परावर्त्त|परावर्त|परावर्तः|परावर्त्तः
परावर्त्त m. (-र्त्तः)<BR>	 1. Retreat, turning back.<BR>	 2. Exchange, barter.<BR>	 3.<BR>Reversal of a sentence.<BR>	 4. Restoration.<BR> E. परा, वृत् to be, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=424-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परावर्त्त्य
परावर्त्त्य mfn. (-र्त्त्यः-र्त्त्या-र्त्त्यं)<BR>	 1. To be turned back.<BR>	 2. To be exchanged.<BR>3. to be reserved, (as a sentence.)<BR>	 4. To be given back or restor-<BR>ed.<BR> E. परा, वृत् to be, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=424-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परावर्त्त्यव्यवहार
परावर्त्त्यव्यवहार m. (-रः) Appeal, (in law.)<BR> E. परावर्त्त्य to be reserved,<BR>व्यवहार judicial procedure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=424-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराविद्ध|पराविद्धः
पराविद्ध m. (-द्धः) A name of KUVERA.<BR> E. पर an enemy, आविद्ध frightened;<BR>or परा + व्यध-क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=424-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परावृत्त
परावृत्त mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं)<BR>	 1. Fled, retreated, turned back.<BR>	 2. Turned<BR>round, revolved.<BR>	 3. Exchanged.<BR>	 4. Reversed, (as a judgment.)<BR>5. Given back, restored. परा before. वृत् to be, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=424-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परावृत्ति|परावृत्तिः
परावृत्ति f. (-त्तिः)<BR>	 1. Returning, retreating, turning back.<BR>	 2. Revolving.<BR>3. Exchange, barter.<BR>	 4. Reversion of a judgment.<BR>	 5. Restoration<BR>of property.<BR> E. परा before, वृत् to be, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=424-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराशर|पराशरः
पराशर m. (-रः) The father of the poet VYĀSA and a great Hindu<BR>law-giver.<BR> E. पर best, शृ to complete, with आङ् prefixed, and अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=424-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराशरिन्
पराशरिन् m. (-री) A beggar, a wandering mendicant.<BR> E. पराशर the<BR>rules of PĀRĀSARA or VYĀSA, the founder of the tribe, and इनि<BR>aff.; also पाराशरिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=424-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराश्रय|पराश्रयः
पराश्रय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Dependent or relying upon another.<BR>	 m. (-यः)<BR>Dependence.<BR>	 f. (-या) A parasite plant.<BR> E. पर another, आश्रय asy-<BR>lum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=424-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराश्रित
पराश्रित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Subject, dependent.<BR> E. पर, and आश्रित having<BR>refuge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=424-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परासन|परासनं
परासन n. (-नं) Killing, slaughter.<BR> E. पर an enemy, अस् to throw or<BR>cast, aff. भावे ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=424-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परासिसिषु
परासिसिषु mfn. (-षुः-षुः-षु)<BR>	 1. Desirous to throw or send.<BR>	 2. Wishing to<BR>overcome.<BR> E. पर before, अस to throw, desid. v., उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=424-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परासु|परासुः
परासु mfn. (-सुः-सुः-सु) Dead, expired.<BR> E. पर away, remote, असु vital<BR>breath.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=424-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परासुता
परासुता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Death, extinction.<BR>	 2. Drowsiness, sleepiness. E.<BR>परासु, and तल् aff. or with त्व, परासुत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=424-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परास्कन्दिन्|परास्कंदिन्
परास्कन्दिन् m. (-न्दी) A thief, a robber.<BR> E. पर another's property, स्कन्द to<BR>steal, with आङ् prefix, णिनि aff. (डाकाइत) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=424-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परास्त|परास्तं
परास्त mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं)<BR>	 1. Thrown, tossed.<BR>	 2. Expelled, turned out.<BR>3. Defeated.<BR>	 4. Rejected.<BR> E. पर, and अस् to throw, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=424-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराह|पराहः
पराह m. (-हः) The next day.<BR> E. पर, and अह, for अहन् a day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=424-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराहत
पराहत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Assailed, attacked.<BR>	 2. Struck back.<BR>	 3. Re-<BR>pulsed.<BR>	 n. (-तं) A stroke.<BR> E. पर, आहत struck.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=424-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराह्ण|पराह्णः
पराह्ण n. (-ह्लं) The afternoon, the latter part of the day.<BR> E. पर after,<BR>(past,) अह a day. टच् अह्नादेशः णत्वञ्च ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=424-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परि
परि A particle and prefix to words implying, 1. Ubiquity, (all round,<BR>on every side.)<BR>	 2. Part, portion.<BR>	 3. Abandonment, (away.)<BR>	 4. End,<BR>term.<BR>	 5. Sickness, infirmity.<BR>	 6. Enforcement, stress, (even, very<BR>great.)<BR>	 7. Separateness, several distributions, (each by each, &c.)<BR>8. Embracing, encircling, (round, round about.)<BR>	 9. Depreciation,<BR>exposure of faults.<BR>	 10. Homage, respect.<BR>	 11. Rejection, turning<BR>off or away.<BR>	 12. Ornament.<BR>	 13. Diffusion, extension.<BR>	 14. Mark or<BR>sign.<BR>	 15. Sorrow.<BR>	 16. Cessation, stop, impediment.<BR>	 17. Truth.<BR>18. An exclamation of Pleasure or satisfaction. As परिकर्त्तुं, to<BR>adorn; परिक्षिप्नुं, to abandon; परिछेत्तुं, to divide; परिदेवितुं, to<BR>lament; परिरब्धुं, to embrace; परिव्रजितुं, to go about, to wander,<BR>&c.: see the following compound nouns.<BR> E. पॄ to complete, to<BR>satisfy, aff. इन्; in combination with roots forming nouns by घञ्,<BR>the इ of परि is sometimes optionally lengthened, as परी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=425-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिकथा
परिकथा f. (-या) A work of fiction, a tale, a story, the history or ad-<BR>ventures of any fabulous person.<BR> E. परि implying ornament,<BR>and कथा a tale.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=425-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिकम्प|परिकंप|परिकंपः|परिकम्पः
परिकम्प m. (-म्पः)<BR>	 1. Fear, terror.<BR>	 2. Trembling.<BR> E. परि very great, कम्प<BR>a trembling, करणे घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=425-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिकर|परिकरः
परिकर mfn. (-रः-री-रं) Who or what helps or assists.<BR>	 m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A<BR>sofa, a bed.<BR>	 2. Dependents, retinue, train.<BR>	 3. Multitude, numbers,<BR>a crowd.<BR>	 4. A firm girth, a waist, a zone or sash.<BR>	 5. Commence-<BR>ment.<BR>	 6. Discrimination, judgment.<BR>	 7. Covert or indirect inti-<BR>mation of wish or purpose, or of coming events in the plot of a<BR>drama. (In dramaturgy.)<BR>	 8. Unusual meaning or expression.<BR>9. Name of a figure of speech consisting in the employment of<BR>suggestive epithets (in rhetoric.)<BR> E. परि round about, कर making.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=425-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिकर्त्तन|परिकर्तन|परिकर्तनं
परिकर्त्तन n. (-नं) Cutting, cutting off or round, a circular incision. E.<BR>परि, and कृत् to cut, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=425-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिकर्त्तिका|परिकर्तिका
परिकर्त्तिका f. (-का) Sharp shooting pain, especially in the rectum. E.<BR>परि, and कृत् to cut, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=425-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिकर्त्तृ|परिकर्तृ
परिकर्त्तृ m. (-र्त्तृः) A priest who performs the marriage ceremony for a<BR>younger brother, whose elder brother is yet unmarried.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=425-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिकर्म्मन्|परिकर्मन्
परिकर्म्मन् n. (-र्म्म)<BR>	 1. Personal decoration, dressing, painting or per-<BR>fuming the body.<BR>	 2. Perfuming the person after bathing.<BR>	 3.<BR>Cleansing, purifying, (the body or the mind.)<BR>	 4. Arithmetical<BR>computation.<BR>	 5. Worship, adoration.<BR>	 m. (-र्म्मा) A servant, a<BR>slave.<BR> E. परि implying ornament, and कर्म्मन् business.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=425-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिकर्म्माष्टक|परिकर्माष्टक
परिकर्म्माष्टक n. (-कं) The eight rules of arithmetic.<BR> E. परिकर्म्म, and अष्टक<BR>eight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=425-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिकार्म्मिन्
परिकार्म्मिन् mfn. (-म्मी-र्म्मिणी-र्म्मि) Adorning, decorating.<BR>	 m. (-र्म्मी-र्म्मिणी)<BR>A slave, a servant,<BR> E. परिकर्म्म decoration, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=425-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिकल्कन|परिकल्कनं
परिकल्कन n. (-नं) Deceit, cheating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=425-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिकल्पन|परिकल्पनं
परिकल्पन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Contriving, making, inventing.<BR>	 2. Doing what<BR>is necessary, tending, providing food, rest, &c.<BR>	 3. Dividing.<BR>	 4.<BR>Settling, agreeing upon.<BR> E. परि, क्वष् to be able, ल्युट aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=425-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिकल्पित
परिकल्पित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Made, invented.<BR>	 2. Divided.<BR>	 3. Tended,<BR>waited upon, provided with all necessaries.<BR>	 4. Settled, agreed. E.<BR>परि before, कृप् to be able, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=425-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिकर्ष|परिकर्षः
परिकर्ष m. (-र्षः) Dragging out.<BR> E. परि, कष् to draw, भावे घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=425-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिकाङ्क्षित|परिकांक्षित|परिकांक्षितः|परिकाङ्क्षितः
परिकाङ्क्षित m. (-तः) A devotee, a religious ascetic.<BR> E. परि gone, काङ्क्षा<BR>wish, and इतच् aff.; having no earthly desires.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=425-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिकीर्ण
परिकीर्ण mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-णं)<BR>	 1. Spread, diffused, scattered around or<BR>about.<BR>	 2. Surrounded.<BR> E. परि about, कीर्ण scattered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=425-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिकीर्त्तन|परिकीर्तन|परिकीर्तनं
परिकीर्त्तन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Saying, telling.<BR>	 2. Talking of, boasting.<BR> E. परि<BR>before, कीर्त्तन celebrating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=425-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिकीर्त्तित|परिकीर्तित
परिकीर्त्तित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Said, declared, promulgated.<BR>	 2. Vaunted<BR>or boasted of.<BR> E. परि, and कीर्त्तित famed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=425-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिकट
परिकट n. (-टं) A barrier, a trench before the gate of a town, forming<BR>a sort of covered way.<BR> E. परि round, कट a fort or house. हस्तिनखेच ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=425-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिकृश
परिकृश mfn. (-शः-शा-शं) Emaciate, thin, wasted.<BR> E. परि, and कृश thin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=425-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिक्रम|परिक्रमः
परिक्रम m. (-मः)<BR>	 1. Walking, going.<BR>	 2. Walking round or about,<BR>circumambulating, going about.<BR>	 3. Roaming about.<BR>	 4. Series,<BR>order.<BR> E. परि about, around, क्रम going, भावे घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=425-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिक्रमसह|परिक्रमसहः
परिक्रमसह m. (-हः) A goat.<BR> E. परिक्रम going about, and सह who bears.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=425-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिक्रय|परिक्रयः
परिक्रय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. Redemption, purchasing or purchasing back.<BR>	 2.<BR>Giving up part of a treasure to preserve the rest.<BR> E. परि, क्री to<BR>buy, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=425-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिक्रामत्
परिक्रामत् mfn. (-मन्-मन्ती-मत्) Going, going round or about.<BR> E. परिक्रम् to<BR>go, round, &c. शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=425-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिक्रिया
परिक्रिया f. (-या)<BR>	 1. Enclosing, surrounding with a fence or ditch, &c.,<BR>intrenching.<BR>	 2. Attention.<BR> E. परि round about, क्रिया making.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=425-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिक्लिश
परिक्लिश m. (-शः) Vexation, trouble.<BR> E. परि much, क्लिश् to be vexed,<BR>क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=425-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिक्लिष्ट
परिक्लिष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं) Vexed, annoyed.<BR> E. परि before, क्लिश् to be<BR>wearied, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=425-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिक्षत
परिक्षत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Wounded, abraded, cut, scratched, &c.<BR> E. परि<BR>before, क्षत broken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=425-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिक्षति|परिक्षतिः
परिक्षति f. (-तिः) Wounding, lesion.<BR> E. परि before, क्षति rupture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=425-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिक्षय|परिक्षयः
परिक्षय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. Waste, decay, dissolution, destruction.<BR>	 2. Ruin,<BR>failure.<BR> E. परि before, क्षि to waste, भावे अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=425-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिक्षा
परिक्षा f. (-क्षा) Mud, dirt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=425-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिक्षित्
परिक्षित् m. (-क्षित्) The name of a king, the son of ABHIMANYU, and<BR>grand-son of ARJUNA; see परीक्षित्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=425-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिक्षिपक
परिक्षिपक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Who or what scatters, disperses, &c.<BR> E. परि<BR>before, क्षिप् to throw, वुञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=425-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिक्षिप्त|परिक्षिप्तं
परिक्षिप्त mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं)<BR>	 1. Surrounded, encircled, intrenched.<BR>	 2.<BR>Scattered, thrown about, diffused.<BR>	 3. Left, abandoned.<BR> E. परि<BR>round about, क्षिप् to throw, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=425-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिक्षीण
परिक्षीण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>	 1. Wasted, worn away, decayed.<BR>	 2.<BR>Diminished, exhausted, decreased.<BR>	 3. Lost, destroyed.<BR>	 4. (In<BR>Law,) Insolvent.<BR> E. परि, and क्षीण emaciate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=425-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिक्षीव
परिक्षीव mfn. (वः-वा-वं) Drunk.<BR> E. परि, and क्षीव drunk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=425-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिक्षेप|परिक्षेपः
परिक्षेप m. (-पः) Scattering, spreading, diffusion.<BR>	 2. Surrounding.<BR>	 3.<BR>A bandoning, leaving.<BR>	 4. Moving about.<BR>	 5. That by which any<BR>thing is surrounded.<BR> E. परि about, क्षेप throwing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=425-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिक्षेपिन
परिक्षेपिन mfn. (-पी-पिणी-पि) Who or what scatters or distributes, &c.<BR>E. परि about, क्षिप् to throw, विणुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=425-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिखा
परिखा f. (-खा) A moat, a ditch surrounding a fort or a town, &c. E.<BR>परि round, खन् to dig, aff. ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=425-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिखेद|परिखेदः
परिखेद m. (-दः) Fatigue, exhaustion. lassitude.<BR> E. परि, खेद depression.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=425-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिख्यात|परिख्यातः
परिख्यात mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Famous, celebrated.<BR> E. परि before, ख्यात said.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=425-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिख्याति|परिख्यातिः
परिख्याति f. (-तिः) Fame, reputation.<BR> E. परि on every side, ख्याति<BR>notoriety.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=425-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिगणित|परिगणितः
परिगणित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Reckoned, calculated.<BR> E. परि, and गणित<BR>counted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=425-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिगत|परिगतः
परिगत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Known, understood.<BR>	 2. Sought, inquired after.<BR>3. Obtained, gained.<BR>	 4. Forgotten.<BR>	 5. Diffused, spread.<BR>	 6. Obs-<BR>tructed, detained.<BR>	 7. Encircled, encompassed.<BR> E. परि about, &c.<BR>and गत gone, become.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=425-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिगम|परिगमः
परिगम m. (-मः)<BR>	 1. Surrounding.<BR>	 2. Seeking for.<BR>	 3. Knowing, ascertain-<BR>ing.<BR>	 4. Obtaining.<BR>	 5. Spreading, extending.<BR> E. परि before, गम्<BR>to go, क्त aff.; also with ल्युट् परिगमनं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=425-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिगमित
परिगमित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Brought, conducted, driven.<BR> E. परि, and गम्<BR>to go, causal v., क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=425-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिगलित
परिगलित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Flowing, fluid.<BR>	 2. Melted.<BR>	 f. (ता)<BR>	 1. Sunk.<BR>2. Dropped down, vanished.<BR> E. परि before, गल् to ooze, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=425-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिगर्हण|परिगर्हणं
परिगर्हण n. (-णं) Excessive blame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=425-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिगढ
परिगढ mfn. (ढः-ढा-ढं)<BR>	 1. Quite secret, very mysterious.<BR>	 2. Very difficult<BR>to understand.<BR> E. परि + गुह-क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=425-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिगृहीत
परिगृहीत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Taken, accepted.<BR>	 2. Assented, consented<BR>to.<BR>	 3. Obeyed.<BR>	 4. Opposed, checked.<BR>	 f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Grasped.<BR>	 2. Em-<BR>braced.<BR>	 3. Favoured.<BR>	 4. Obeyed.<BR> E. परि before, ग्रह् to take, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=426-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिगृह्य
परिगृह्य mfn. (-ह्यः-ह्या-ह्यं)<BR>	 1. To be taken or accepted.<BR>	 2. To be re-<BR>garded.<BR>	 f. (-ह्या) A married woman. ind.<BR>	 1. Having taken.<BR>	 2. Con-<BR>sidering, looking upon.<BR> E. परि encircling, ग्रह् to take; aff. यत्<BR>or ल्यप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=426-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिग्रह|परिग्रहः
परिग्रह m. (-हः)<BR>	 1. Acceptance, taking.<BR>	 2. Assent, consent.<BR>	 3. De-<BR>pendents, a family, a train or retinue.<BR>	 4. A wife.<BR>	 5. Root, origin.<BR>6. An oath.<BR>	 7. The reserve of an army, a corps posted with the<BR>general, four hundred yards in the rear of the line: see प्रतिग्रह.<BR>8. Maintaining, observing.<BR>	 9. Continued possession, continuance.<BR>10. Subjugation, making subservient or subject.<BR>	 11. Connexion,<BR>concern, business or interference with.<BR>	 12. Comprehension.<BR>	 13.<BR>The sun near the moon's node.<BR>	 14. Surrounding.<BR>	 15. Putting on<BR>(as a dress).<BR>	 16. Marriage.<BR>	 17. An epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR> E. परि<BR>intensitive prefix, or round about, &c. and ग्रह taking, अप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=426-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिग्राह|परिग्राहः
परिग्राह m. (-हः) A mound or place prepared for a burnt offering at<BR>a ceremony which requires three or four such places, placed to<BR>the north or east, &c. as उत्तरपरिग्राह, पुर्ब्बपरिग्राह.<BR> E. परि about,<BR>ग्रह् to take, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=426-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिग्नान
परिग्नान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Wearied out, exhausted.<BR>	 f. (-ना) Adverse<BR>from<BR> E. परि intensitive, ग्लान wearied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=426-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिघ|परिघः
परिघ m. (-घः)<BR>	 1. A bludgeon, a stick mounted with iron, or an iron<BR>club.<BR>	 2. Killing, striking, destroying.<BR>	 3. The nineteenth of the<BR>astronomical Yogas.<BR>	 4. The pin or bolt of a door.<BR>	 5. A glass<BR>vessel.<BR>	 6. A pike, a spear.<BR>	 7. A water jar.<BR>	 8. The outer door or<BR>gate of a palace.<BR>	 9. A house: see पलिघ<BR> E. परि round about, हन्<BR>to kill, अप् aff., घ substituted for the root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=426-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिघट्टित
परिघट्टित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Rubbed repeatedly.<BR>	 2. Much handled or<BR>touched.<BR> E. परि and घट्टित rubbed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=426-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिघात|परिघातः
परिघात m. (-तः)<BR>	 1. Killing, striking.<BR>	 2. A weapon.<BR> E. परि completely,<BR>हन् to kill, aff. घञ् and the root changed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=426-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिघातन|परिघातनं|परिघातनः
परिघातन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Striking, hurting killing.<BR>	 2. A staff or bludgeon<BR>armed with iron.<BR> E. परि before, हन् to kill, aff. स्वार्ये-णिच्-कर्त्तरि-ल्यु ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=426-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिघोष|परिघोषः
परिघोष m. (-षः)<BR>	 1. Sound.<BR>	 2. Improper or blamable discourse.<BR>	 3.<BR>The muttering or grumbling of clouds.<BR> E. परि intensitive or de-<BR>preciative prefix, and घोष sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=426-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिचय|परिचयः
परिचय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. Acquaintance, intimacy.<BR>	 2. Accumulation.<BR>	 3.<BR>Meeting with a friend.<BR>	 4. Study, Practice.<BR>	 5. Recognition.<BR> E. परि<BR>about, चि to gather, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=426-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिचयनीय
परिचयनीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>	 1. To be known.<BR>	 2. To be collected.<BR> E. परि<BR>before, चि to heap, aff. अनीयर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=426-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिचर|परिचरः
परिचर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A guard, a body-guard.<BR>	 2. An attendant, a com-<BR>panion, a servant.<BR>	 3. A commander-in-cheif.<BR> E. परि about, and चर<BR>who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=426-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिचर्य्या|परिचर्या
परिचर्य्या f. (-र्य्या)<BR>	 1. Service, dependence.<BR>	 2. Veneration, worship. E.<BR>परि about, चर् to go, aff. क्यप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=426-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिचाय्य|परिचाय्यः
परिचाय्य m. (-य्यः)<BR>	 1. A place for preparing or holding a sacrificial<BR>fire.<BR>	 2. Sacrificial fire in general.<BR>	 3. Raising the rent or re-<BR>venue of land.<BR> E. परि worship, &c. चि to collect, aff. ण्यत्, form<BR>specific.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=426-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिचारक|परिचारकः
परिचारक m. (-कः) A servant, an attendant.<BR> E. परि before, चर् to go, ण्वुल aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=426-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिवार्य्य|परिवार्य
परिवार्य्य mfn. (-र्य्यः-र्य्या-र्य्यं) To be served or obeyed, to be worshipped.<BR>E. परि before, चर् to go, ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=426-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिचित|परिचितः
परिचित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Known, acquainted with.<BR>	 2. Heaped, accu-<BR>mulated.<BR>	 3. Learnt, Practised.<BR> E. परि before, चि to collect, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=426-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिचेतव्य
परिचेतव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>	 1. To be known, fit or proper to be known as<BR>an acquaintance.<BR>	 2. To be collected together.<BR> E. परि, and चेतव्य to<BR>be gathered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=426-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिचेय|परिचेयं
परिचेय mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>	 1. To be collected all round, or from every side.<BR>2. To be known as an acquaintance.<BR> E. परि before, चि to collect.<BR>aff. ण्यत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=426-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिच्युत
परिच्युत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Lost, gone, deprived or devoid of.<BR> E. परि and<BR>च्युत fallen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=426-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिच्छद|परिच्छदः|परिछद
परिच्छद m. (-दः)<BR>	 1. Court, train, attendants, retinue.<BR>	 2. Family, depen-<BR>dents.<BR>	 3. Goods and chattels, personal property.<BR>	 4. Dress, parap-<BR>hernalia.<BR>	 5. Covering.<BR>	 6. Clothes.<BR> E. परि round, छद् to cover,<BR>aff. णिच्-घ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=426-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिच्छन्द|परिच्छंद|परिच्छंदः|परिच्छन्दः
परिच्छन्द m. (-न्दः) Retinue, train.<BR> E. परि around, छद to cover, aff.<BR>अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=426-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिच्छन्न|परिच्छन्नः|परिछन्न
परिच्छन्न mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>	 1. Covered, clothed.<BR>	 2. Invested, enclosed.<BR>	 3.<BR>Having a retinue or paraphernalia.<BR>	 4. Overlaid.<BR>	 5. Surrounded.<BR>E. परि before, छद् to cover, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=426-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिच्छित्ति|परिच्छित्तिः|परिछित्ति
परिच्छित्ति f. (-त्तिः)<BR>	 1. Partition, separation, &c.<BR>	 2. Accurate definition:<BR>E. परि + छिद्-भावे-क्तिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=426-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिच्छिन्न|परिच्छिन्नः|परिछिन्न
परिच्छिन्न mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्न)<BR>	 1. Detached, divided, cut off.<BR>	 2. Resisted,<BR>remedied.<BR>	 3. Limited, confined.<BR> E. परि before, छिद् to cut, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=426-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिच्छेद|परिच्छेदः|परिछेद
परिच्छेद m. (-दः)<BR>	 1. Segment, division, cutting or severing.<BR>	 2. Discri-<BR>mination.<BR>	 3. Limit, boundary.<BR>	 4. Obviating, remedying.<BR>	 5. The<BR>division of a book, a section or chapter.<BR>	 6. Moderation.<BR>	 7. Ac-<BR>curate distinction or definition.<BR>	 8. Exact determination.<BR> E. परि<BR>successively, severally, च्छेद cutting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=426-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिच्छेदन|परिच्छेदनं|परिछेदन
परिच्छेदन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Dividing, division.<BR>	 2. Discriminating.<BR>	 3. The<BR>division of a book.<BR>	 4. Laughter, expressive of joy,<BR> E. परि before,<BR>छिद to divide, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=426-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिजन|परिजनः
परिजन m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. Dependents, servants, family, followers.<BR>	 2. Train,<BR>retinue, Suit, (especially the maids of a lady).<BR> E. परि about, and जन<BR>a person.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=426-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिजल्पित|परिजल्पितं
परिजल्पित n. (-तं)<BR>	 1. The covert reproaches of a mistress neglected or<BR>ill-used by her lover.<BR>	 2. A servant's indication of his superiority<BR>by finding fault with his master.<BR> E. परि, and जल्पित prattling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=426-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिज्ञात
परिज्ञात mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Known, ascertained.<BR> E. परि, and ज्ञात known.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=426-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिज्ञातृ
परिज्ञातृ mfn. (-ता-त्री-त) Wise, intelligent, one who has knowledge. E.<BR>परि before, ज्ञा to know, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=426-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिज्ञान|परिज्ञानं
परिज्ञान n. (-नं) Knowledge, ascertainment, discrimination.<BR> E. परि,<BR>and ज्ञान knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=426-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिज्ञाय
परिज्ञाय ind. Having known or ascertained.<BR> E. परि, and ज्ञाय having<BR>known.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=426-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिज्वन्
परिज्वन् m. (-ज्वा)<BR>	 1. Moon.<BR>	 2. Fire.<BR> E. परि before, जु a sautra root,<BR>means to be quick, Unādi aff. कनिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=426-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिडीनक|परिडीनकं
परिडीनक n. (-क) The flight of a bird in circles.<BR> E. परि round, डीन<BR>or डीनक flying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=426-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिणत|परिणतं|परिणतः
परिणत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Ripe, mature.<BR>	 2. Bowed, bent.<BR>	 3. Aimed at,<BR>directed to, inclined to.<BR>	 4. Changed or transformed into.<BR>	 5. Di-<BR>gested.<BR>	 6. Full grown.<BR>	 7. Advanced, come to a close, ended.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-तः) An elephant stooping to strike with his tusks.<BR>	 n. (-तं)<BR>Capital, stock, wealth accumulated for the sake of profit. E.<BR>परि before, णम् to bend or bow, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=426-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिणति|परिणतिः
परिणति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Bending, bowing.<BR>	 2. Ripeness.<BR>	 3. Transformation.<BR>4. Fulfilment 5. Result, issue.<BR>	 6. Old age, 7. Conclusion, end.<BR>E. परि before, नम् to bow, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=426-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिणय|परिणयः
परिणय m. (-यः) Marriage.<BR> E. परि successively or individually, णी to<BR>take, अच् aff.; also with ल्युट aff. परिणयन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=426-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिणाम|परिणामः
परि(री)णाम m. (-मः)<BR>	 1. Change of form or state.<BR>	 2. Maturity, fulness,<BR>ripeness.<BR>	 3. End, last stage or state.<BR>	 4. Digestion.<BR>	 5. Result.<BR>6. A figure of speech closely resembling Rupaka and minutely<BR>distinguished by it; it consists in transferring the properties<BR>of any object to that with which it is compared.<BR> E. परि before,<BR>नम् to bend, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=426-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिणामदर्शिन्
परिणामदर्शिन् mfn. (-र्शी-र्शिनी-र्शि) Who looks forward or to the end.<BR>E. परिणाम, and दर्शिन् who sees.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=427-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिणामनिरोध
परिणामनिरोध m. (-धः) Human vicissitude; as birth, growth, death,<BR>&c.<BR> E. परिणाम and निरोध obstruction, (of final felicity.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=427-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिणामपथ्य
परिणामपथ्य mfn. (-थ्यः-थ्या-थ्यं) Suited to a future stage or condition.<BR>E. परिणामः and पथ्य good for.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=427-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिणामशूल|परिणामशूलः
परिणामशूल m. (-लः) Flatulence with pain or vomiting after eating,<BR>dyspepsia.<BR> E. परिणाम, and शूल colic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=427-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परि
परि(री)णाय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. Leading or taking round.<BR>	 2. Moving a piece<BR>at chess, draughts, &c.<BR> E. परि about, णी to take, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=427-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिणायक|परिणायकः
परिणायक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A husband.<BR>	 2. A leader.<BR> E. परि before, णी to take,<BR>ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=427-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिणाह|परिणाहः
परिणाह m. (-हः) Width, breadth.<BR>	 2. Circumference of a circle. E.<BR>परि extension, नह् to bind, aff. घञ् वा दीर्घः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=427-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिणिंसक
परिणिंसक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Who or what eats or feeds upon.<BR>	 2. Who<BR>or what kisses.<BR> E. परि before, निसि to kiss, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=427-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिणिंसा
परिणिंसा f. (-सा)<BR>	 1. Eating.<BR>	 2. Kissing.<BR> E. परि before, निसि to kiss,<BR>अङ् and टाप् affixes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=427-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिणिनंसु
परिणिनंसु mfn. (-सुः-सुः-सु) Seeking to take or lay hold of.<BR> E. परि, नश्<BR>to lose, उ aff. desid. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=427-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिणिष्ठा
परिणिष्ठा f. (-ष्ठा) Perfect skill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=427-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिणीत
परिणीत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Married.<BR> E. परि before, णी to take, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=427-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिणेतृ
परिणेतृ m. (-ता) A husband.<BR> E. परि before, णी to take, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=427-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परितर्पण|परितर्पणं
परितर्पण n. (-णं) Gratifying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=427-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परितस्
परितस् ind.<BR>	 1. Around, every way, all round.<BR>	 2. Towards.<BR> E. परि<BR>round, and तसिल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=427-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परि
परि(री)ताप m. (-पः)<BR>	 1. Pain, anguish.<BR>	 2. Sorrow.<BR>	 3. A division of hell.<BR>4. Heat, warmth.<BR>	 5. Fear.<BR>	 6. Trembling.<BR> E. परि exceeding, ताप<BR>burning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=427-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परितुष्ट|परितुष्टः
परितुष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं) Pleased, delighted.<BR> E. परि much, तुष्ट pleased.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=427-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परितुष्टि|परितुष्टिः
परितुष्टि f. (ष्टि) Contentment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=427-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परितोष|परितोषः
परितोष m. (-षः) Pleasure, satisfaction, delight.<BR> E. परि entirely, तोष<BR>pleasure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=427-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परित्यक्त
परित्यक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>	 1. Void or deprived of, left, quitted, abandon-<BR>ed.<BR>	 2. Let go, let fly, (as an arrow).<BR>	 3. Bereft of, (with an instru-<BR>mental.)<BR> E. परि, and त्यक्त left.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=427-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परित्यजन|परित्यजनं
परित्यजन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Distributing, dispersing.<BR>	 2. Abandoning.<BR> E. परि<BR>about, त्यज् to abandon, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=427-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परित्यज्य
परित्यज्य ind. Having abandoned.<BR> E. परि before, त्यज् to leave,<BR>ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=427-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परित्याग|परित्यागः
परित्याग m. (-गः)<BR>	 1. Abandonment, quitting, omission, desertion.<BR>2. Loss, privation.<BR>	 3. Liberality<BR> E. परि away, त्याग quitting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=427-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परित्यागिन्
परित्यागिन् mfn. (-गी-गिनी-गि) Abandoning, quitting.<BR> E. परि before, त्यज्<BR>to quit, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=427-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परित्याज्य
परित्याज्य mfn. (-ज्यः-ज्या-ज्यं) To be left or abandoned.<BR> E. परि before, त्यज्<BR>to leave, ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=427-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परित्रस्त
परित्रस्त mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं) Afraid.<BR> E. परि much, त्रस्त alarmed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=427-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परित्राण|परित्राणं
परित्राण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Warding a blow, self-defence.<BR>	 2. Preserving,<BR>rescue, deliverance, protecting.<BR> E. परि about, त्राण preserving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=427-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिदर|परिदरः
परिदर m. (-रं) Sponginess of the gums.<BR> E. परि, and दर rending.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=427-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिदहन|परिदहनं
परिदहन n. (-नं) Scorching, burning.<BR> E. परि, and दह् to burn, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=427-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिदान|परिदानं
परिदान n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Barter, exchange, returning any thing or its equi-<BR>valent.<BR>	 2. Donation.<BR>	 3. Restitution of a deposit.<BR> E. परि recipro-<BR>cally, दान giving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=427-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परि
परि(री)दाह m. (-हः)<BR>	 1. Burning.<BR>	 2. Pain, sorrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=427-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिदाहिन्
परिदाहिन् mfn. (-ही-हिनी-हि) Hot, scorching.<BR> E. परि before, दह् to<BR>burn, घिणुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=427-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिदेव|परिदेवः
परिदेव m. (-वः) Wailing, lamentation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=427-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिदेवक
परिदेवक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Who or what laments or complains.<BR> E. परि<BR>before, दिव् to play, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=427-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिदेवन|परिदेवनं
परिदेवन nf. (-नं-ना) Lamentation, complaint, bewailing.<BR>	 2. Fearing. E.<BR>परि implying grief, देवन showing, playing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=427-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिदेवित|परिदेवितं
परिदेवित n. (-तं)<BR>	 1. Lamentation.<BR>	 2. Repentance.<BR> E. परि before, देव् to<BR>play, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=427-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिदेविन्
परिदेविन् mfn. (-वी-विनी-वि)<BR>	 1. Lamenting.<BR>	 2. Fearing, apprehensive. E.<BR>परि before, दिव् to play, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=427-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिधान|परिधानं
परिधान n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. A lower garment.<BR>	 2. Vesture, clothes.<BR>	 3. Putting<BR>on, (a garment), dressing.<BR> E. परि about, round, धान having.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=427-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिधानीय|परिधानीयं
परिधानीय n. (-यं) An under-garment, also परिधेय ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=427-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिधाय|परिधायः
परिधाय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. Retinue, attendants.<BR>	 2. The posteriors.<BR>	 3. A piece of<BR>water.<BR> E. परि circling surrounding, धा to have, घञ् aff. and युक<BR>augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=427-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिधि|परिधिः
परिधि m. (-धिः)<BR>	 1. The circumference of a circle.<BR>	 2. The disk of the<BR>sun or moon.<BR>	 3. The periphery of a wheel.<BR>	 4. The horizon, circle<BR>surrounding the globe, a great circle.<BR>	 5. An epicycle.<BR>	 6. The<BR>branch of the tree to which the victim at a sacrifice is tied.<BR>7. A wooden frame round the hole in which a sacrificial<BR>fire is lighted.<BR>	 8. A wall, a fence.<BR> E. परि around, धा to have,<BR>कि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=427-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिधिस्थ|परिधिस्थः
परिधिस्थ m. (-स्थः)<BR>	 1. A guard, a body-guard.<BR>	 2. An aide-de-camp, an<BR>officer attendant on the king or general.<BR> E. परिधि around, (the<BR>king,) स्थ who stands.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=427-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिधूपित
परिधूपित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Perfumed.<BR> E. परि, and धूपित perfumed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=427-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिध्वंस|परिध्वंसः
परिध्वंस m. (-सः)<BR>	 1. Injury, destruction.<BR>	 2. A man of a mixed caste.<BR>3. Failure.<BR>	 4. Loss of caste.<BR> E. परि before, ध्वंस् to lose, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=427-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिनिर्वपन|परिनिर्व्वपन
परिनिर्वपन n. (-नं) Distributing, dispensing, giving.<BR> E. परि and निर्<BR>before, वप् to give, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=427-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिनिर्विवप्सा
परिनिर्विवप्सा f. (-सा) Liberality, wish to give.<BR> E. परि, and निर् before,<BR>वप् to give, desid. form, अङ् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=427-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिनिर्विवप्सु|परिनिर्व्विवप्सु
परिनिर्विवप्सु mfn. (-प्सुः-प्सुः-प्सु) Desirous of giving.<BR> E. परि, and निर्<BR>before, वप् to give उ aff. desid. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=427-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिनिष्ठित
परिनिष्ठित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Skilled in, acquainted with.<BR> E. परि, and<BR>नि before, स्था to stay, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=427-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिन्यास|परिन्यासः
परिन्यास m. (-सः) Completing the sense of a passage.<BR> E. परि, and न्यास<BR>position.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=427-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिपक्व
परिपक्व mfn. (क्कः-क्का-क्कं)<BR>	 1. Cooked, dressed.<BR>	 2. Mature.<BR>	 3. Shrewd,<BR>knowing.<BR>	 4. Digested.<BR>	 5. On the point of decay.<BR> E. परि before,<BR>पक्क ripe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=427-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिपक्कता
परिपक्कता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Being dressed or cooked.<BR>	 2. Maturity, perfection.<BR>3. Shrewdness.<BR>	 4. Digestion.<BR> E. तल् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=427-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिपण|परिपणं
परिपण(न) n. (-णं or नं) Capital, principal, stock<BR> E. परि severally, पण<BR>price.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=427-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिपणित
परिपणित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Pledged, plighted, agreed, promised.<BR> E. परि,<BR>and पण् to pledge, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=427-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिपदीन्
परिपदीन् m. (-दी) An enemy.<BR> E. परि against, पद् to go, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=427-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिपन्थक|परिपन्थकः
परिपन्थक m. (-कः) An enemy, an antagonist.<BR> E. परि opposition, पन्थक<BR>who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=427-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिपन्थिन्|परिपंथिन्
परिपन्थिन् mf. (-न्थी-न्थिनी)<BR>	 1. An enemy, an antagonist.<BR>	 2. A robber, a<BR>high-way-man, a bandit.<BR>	 f. (न्थिनी) Opposing, hindering.<BR> E. परि<BR>obstacle or opposition, पन्थिन् who goes the road.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=427-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परि
परि(री)पाक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. Being cooked or dressed.<BR>	 2. Maturity, perfec-<BR>tion.<BR>	 3. Cleverness, shrewdness.<BR>	 4. Digestion.<BR>	 5. The fruit or<BR>consequence of actions.<BR> E. परि before, पच् to cook or ripen, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=427-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिपाकिन्
परिपाकिन् mfn. (-की-किनी-कि) Who or what cooks, ripens, digests,<BR>&c.<BR>	 f. (-नी) A drug. (Convolvulus turpethum.)<BR> E. परि completely,<BR>पच् to ripen, aff. णिनि, fem. aff. ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=427-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिपाटि|परिपाटिः
परिपाटि(टी) f. (-टिः or टी)<BR>	 1. Order, method, arrangement.<BR>	 2. Arith-<BR>metic.<BR> E. परि several distribution, पाटि proceeding, from पट् to go,<BR>in the causal form, aff. इन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=427-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिपाठ|परिपाठः
परिपाठ m. (-ठः) Complete enumerations.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=427-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिपालन|परिपालनं
परिपालन n. (-नं) Protecting, cherishing.<BR> E. परि, and पालन the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=428-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिपालित
परिपालित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Protected, cherished.<BR> E. परि, and पालित<BR>protected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=428-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिपिष्टक|परिपिष्टकं
परिपिष्टक n. (-कं) Lead.<BR> E. परि + पिष्-क्त सज्ञायाम् कन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=428-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिपीडन|परिपीडनं
परिपीडन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Squeezing, pressing out.<BR>	 2. Injuring, hurting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=428-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिपुटन|परिपुटनं
परिपुटन n. (-नं) Peeling, desquamation, removing the bark, losing<BR>the bark.<BR> E. परि before, पुट् to reduce, and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=428-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिपुष्करा
परिपुष्करा f. (-रा) A sort of cucumber, (C. madraspatanus.) (गोमुक्) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=428-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिपूजन|परिपूजनं
परिपूजन n. (-नं) Worshipping, adoring.<BR> E. परि before, पूज् to worship,<BR>ल्युट् aff.; also परिपूजा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=428-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिपूजित
परिपूजित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Served, worshipped, adored.<BR> E. परि, पूज् to<BR>worship, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=428-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिपूत|परिपूतं
परिपूत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Pure, purified.<BR>	 2. Winnowed, threshed,<BR>freed from the chaff.<BR> E. परि, and पूत pure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=428-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिपूर्ण
परिपूर्ण mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-णं)<BR>	 1. Full, entire, complete.<BR>	 2. Self-satisfied,<BR>content.<BR> E. परि quite, पूर्ण full.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=428-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिपूर्णता
परिपूर्णता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Completion, entireness, fulness.<BR>	 2. Satiety or<BR>satisfaction.<BR> E. परि completely, पूर्णता fulness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=428-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिपूर्णत्व|परिपूर्णत्वं
परिपूर्णत्व n. (-त्वं) Completion, &c.; see the last.<BR> E. परि, and पूर्णत्व ful-<BR>ness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=428-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिपेल|परिपेलं
परिपेल n. (-लं) A fragrant grass, (Cyperus rotundus.)<BR> E. परि extension,<BR>पेल् to go, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=428-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिपेलव|परिपेलवं
परिपेलव fn. (-वा-वं) A grass.<BR>	 f. (-वा) Very fine, very delicate. See the<BR>last. E. As above, वन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=428-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिपोट|परिपोटः
परिपोट m. (-टः) A particular disease of the ear, (in medicine).<BR>Also परिपोटक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=428-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिपोषण|परिपोषणं
परिपोषण n. (-णं) Furthering, promoting nourishing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=428-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिप्रश्न|परिप्रश्नः
परिप्रश्न m. (-श्नः) Inquiry, interrogation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=428-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिप्रेप्सु
परिप्रेप्सु mfn. (प्सुः-प्सुः-प्सु) Desiring, seeking.<BR> E. परि, and प्र before,<BR>आप् to obtain, उ aff. desid. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=428-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिपेषण
परिपेषण n. (-णं) Abandoning, leaving, sending or putting away.<BR> E. परि<BR>before, प्रेष् to send, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=428-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिपेषित
परिपेषित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Abandoned, left, put or sent away.<BR> E. परि<BR>before, प्रेष् to send, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=428-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिप्लव|परिप्लवं|परिप्लवः
परिप्लव mfn. (-वः-वा-वं)<BR>	 1. Shaking, trembling.<BR>	 2. Unsteady, restless,<BR>moveable.<BR>	 3. Floating.<BR>	 m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. Bathing, wetting with water,<BR>immersing.<BR>	 2. Inundation.<BR>	 3. Oppression, tyranny.<BR>	 4. A boat. E.<BR>परि about, प्लव what goes, from प्लु to go, aff. अप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=428-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिप्लुत|परिप्लुतः
परिप्लुत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Immersed, inundated.<BR>	 2. Wetted, bathed.<BR>f. (-ता) Spirituous or vinous liquor.<BR>	 n. (-तं) A spring, a jump. E.<BR>परि every where, प्लु to go, aff. क्त. मैथुनवेदनायुक्ते, नार्य्यङ्गभेदेच ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=428-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिप्लुष्ट
परिप्लुष्ट f. (-ष्टा) Burnt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=428-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिबर्ह|परिबर्हः
परिब(-व)र्ह m. (-र्ह)<BR>	 1. Retinue, train.<BR>	 2. Insignia of royalty.<BR>	 3.<BR>Wealth.<BR>	 4. Thing, substance.<BR>	 5. Furniture.<BR> E. परि about, or a<BR>mark, a sign. वर्ह् to cover, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=428-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिबर्हण|परिबर्हणं
परिब(व)र्हण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Retinue, train.<BR>	 2. Fatigue, hardship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=428-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिबृंहण|परिबृंहणं
परिबृं(वृं)हण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Prosperity, welfare.<BR>	 2. Appendix, supplement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=428-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिबृंहित
परिबृं(वृं)हित fn. (-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Increased, augmented.<BR>	 2. Furnished with.<BR>n. (-तं) The roar of an elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=428-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिभङ्ग|परिभंग|परिभंगः|परिभङ्गः
परिभङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः) Breaking to pieces, shattering.<BR> E. परि, and भङ्ग a<BR>breaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=428-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिभव|परिभवः
परि(-री)भव m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. Disrespect, contempt, disgrace.<BR>	 2. Defeat, dis-<BR>comfiture.<BR> E. परि implying depreciation, and भव being; also परिभाव.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=428-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिभवपद
परिभवपद n. (-दं) Disgrace, a disgraceful situation.<BR> E. परिभव, and<BR>पद degree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=428-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिभवाष्पद
परिभवाष्पद n. (-दं) A situation of disgrace or defeat.<BR> E. परिभव, and<BR>आस्पद situation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=428-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिभविन्
परिभविन् mfn. (-वी-विनी-वि)<BR>	 1. Treating with contumely or disrespect.<BR>2. Suffering disrespect.<BR> E. परि before, भ to be, णिनि aff. der. irr.<BR>or परिभव, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=428-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिभाव|परिभावः
परिभाव m. (-वः) Disrespect: see परिभव.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=428-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिभाविन्
परिभाविन् mfn. (-वी-विनी-वि)<BR>	 1. Irreverent, disrespectful.<BR>	 2. Putting to<BR>shame, surpassing.<BR> E. परि before, भू to be, धिणुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=428-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिभावुक
परिभावुक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Who or what shames or humbles another.<BR>E. परि before, भू to be, उकञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=428-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिभाषण|परिभाषणं
परिभाषण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Reproof, abuse, ridicule, expression of censure or<BR>contempt.<BR>	 2. Addressing, discourse, conversing.<BR>	 3. Agreement,<BR>engagement.<BR>	 4. Rule, precept.<BR> E. परि exposure of faults, or<BR>mutually, &c., भाषण speaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=428-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिभाषणीय
परिभाषणीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>	 1. Reprehensible, liable to or deserving<BR>reproof.<BR>	 2. To be addressed or spoken to.<BR> E. परि before, भाष् to<BR>speak, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=428-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिभाषा
परिभाषा f. (-षा)<BR>	 1. A technicality, a conventional term in any science.<BR>2. (In Grammar,) A maxim given by the ancient grammarians<BR>as a summary interpretation of the rules of PĀṆINI.<BR>	 3. (In medi-<BR>cine,) Prognosis.<BR>	 4. Abuse, ridicule.<BR>	 5. A speech.<BR>	 6. Censure,<BR>blame.<BR> E. परि severally, and भाषा speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=428-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिभाषित
परिभाषित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Said.<BR>	 2. Formed or used technically. E.<BR>परि, भाष् to speak, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=428-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिभुक्त
परिभुक्त mfn. (क्त-क्ता-क्तं) Enjoyed, possessed, eaten.<BR> E. परि, and भुज् to<BR>enjoy, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=428-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिभुग्र
परिभुग्र f. (-ग्ना) Bowed, bent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=428-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिभूत|परिभूतं
परिभूत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Treated with contempt or disrespect, dis-<BR>regard, despised.<BR> E. परि exposure of fault, and भूत become.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=428-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिभूय
परिभूय ind. Disgracing, shaming, outvieing, having disgraced, &c. E.<BR>परि before, भू to be, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=428-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिभूषण|परिभूषणः
परिभूषण Peace obtained by cession of the revenue of a land.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=428-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परोभोक्तृ
परोभोक्तृ mfn. (-क्ता-क्त्री-क्त)<BR>	 1. One who uses another's property<BR>without leave.<BR>	 2. Possessing, one who possesses or enjoys.<BR> E. परि,<BR>and भुज् to enjoy, तच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=428-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिभोग|परिभोगः
परिभोग m. (-गः)<BR>	 1. Using or living upon another person's pro-<BR>perty without leave or improperly.<BR>	 2. Possession, enjoyment,<BR>especially sexual enjoyment.<BR> E. परि, भुज् to enjoy, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=428-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिभ्रंश|परिभ्रंशः
परिभ्रंश m. (-शः)<BR>	 1. Escape.<BR>	 2. Falling from.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=428-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिभ्रम|परिभ्रमः
परिभ्रम m. (-मः)<BR>	 1. Wandering, going about.<BR>	 2. Error.<BR>	 3. Rambling<BR>discourse. परि before, भ्रम् to roam, घञ् aff.; also with ल्युट्,<BR>परिभ्रमणं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=428-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिभ्रष्ट
परिभ्रष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं) Fallen, degraded, deprived of, void of, (with<BR>an ablative, or instrumental.)<BR> E. परि, and भ्रष्ट fallen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=428-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिमण्डल|परिमंडल|परिमण्डलं|परिमण्डलः
परिमण्डल n. (-लं) A ball, a globe, a circle.<BR>	 f. (-ला) Globular, circu-<BR>lar.<BR> E. परि round, and मण्डल a sphere or circumference.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=428-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिमण्डलता
परिमण्डलता f. (-ता) Rotundity, circularity.<BR> E. परिमण्डल, and तल् aff.;<BR>also परिमण्डलत्वं, with त्व aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=428-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिमण्डलित
परिमण्डलित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Rounded, made round or circular E.<BR>परिमण्डल, and इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=428-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिमन्थर|परिमंथर
परिमन्थर f. (-रा) Extremely slow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=428-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिमन्द|परिमंद
परिमन्द mfn. (-न्दः-न्दा-न्दं)<BR>	 1. Little, a little, not much.<BR>	 2. Slow.<BR>	 3. Dull.<BR>E. परि and मन्द slow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=428-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिमर|परिमरः
परिमर m. (-रः) Air, wind.<BR> E. परि + मृ-आधारे अप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=428-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिमर्द्दन|परिमर्दन|परिमर्दनं
परिमर्द्दन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Rubbing, grinding.<BR>	 2. Embracing, pressing.<BR>	 3.<BR>Trampling or destroying.<BR> E. परि, and मर्द्दन rubbing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=428-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिनल
परिनल m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. An exquisite scent, especially arising from the<BR>trituration of fragrant substances.<BR>	 2. The trituration of perfumes.<BR>3. Copulation.<BR>	 4. A meeting of learned men.<BR>	 5. Soil, stain, dirt. E.<BR>परि extension, मल् to increase, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=428-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिमलित
परिमलित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Soiled, despoiled of freshness or beauty.<BR>2. Perfumed.<BR> E. परिमल, and इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=428-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिमर्श|परिमर्शः
परिमर्श m. (-र्शः)<BR>	 1. Contact, propinquity.<BR>	 2. Friction.<BR> E. परि, and मश्<BR>to touch, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=428-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिमर्ष|परिमर्षः
परिमर्ष m. (-र्षः) Envy, dislike.<BR> E. परि before, मष् to bear, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=428-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिमार्ग|परिमार्गः
परिमार्ग m. (-र्गः)<BR>	 1. Friction.<BR>	 2. Touch.<BR>	 3. Cleaning, wiping.<BR> E. परि<BR>before, मृज् to clean, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=429-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिमार्गितव्य
परिमार्गितव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं) To be sought after.<BR> E. परि before, मार्ग्<BR>to search, तव्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=429-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिमार्ग्य|परिमार्ग्यं
परिमार्ग्य mfn. (-र्ग्य-र्ग्या-र्ग्य)<BR>	 1. To be cleaned or cleansed.<BR>	 2. To be<BR>rubbed.<BR> E. परि completely, मृज् to clean, ण्यत् aff.; also परिमृज्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=429-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परि
परि(री)माण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Measure.<BR>	 2. Measuring.<BR>	 3. Weight, number,<BR>value.<BR> E. परि completely, and माण measuring. परि + मा-ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=429-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिमाणीय
परिमाणीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) To be measured.<BR> E. परि before, मा to measure,<BR>अनीयर् aff.; also परिमातव्य and परिमेय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=429-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिमार्ज्जन|परिमार्जन|परिमार्जनं
परिमार्ज्जन n. (-नं) Cleaning, cleansing.<BR>	 2. A dish of honey and oil. E.<BR>परि completely, मृज् to cleanse, aff. भावे-ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=429-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिमित|परिमितं
परिमित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Joined.<BR>	 2. Meted, measured.<BR>	 3. Regulated. E.<BR>परि, मा to measure, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=429-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिमितभुज्
परिमितभुज् mfn. (-क्) Temperate, abstemious.<BR> E. परिमित, and भुज् who<BR>eats or enjoys.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=429-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिमिताहार
परिमिताहार mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Eating moderately.<BR> E. परिमित, and आहार<BR>food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=429-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिमिति|परिमितिः
परिमिति f. (-तिः) Measure, quantity.<BR> E. परि, मा to measure क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=429-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिमिलन|परिमिलनं
परिमिलन n. (-नं) Touch, contact.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=429-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिमुग्ध
परिमुग्ध f. (-ग्धा) Lovely yet simple, fascinating but foolish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=429-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिमृज्य|परिमृज्यं
परिमृज्य mfn. (-ज्यः-ज्या-ज्यं)<BR>	 1. To be cleaned.<BR>	 2. To be touched.<BR> E. परि<BR>before, मृज् to clean, aff. क्यप्; also परिमार्ग्यं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=429-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिमृदित
परिमृदित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Rubbed, ground.<BR>	 2. Embraced, clasped.<BR>E. परि before, मृद् to rub, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=429-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिमृष्ट
परिमृष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>	 1. Rubbed, touched.<BR>	 1. Embraced, clasped.<BR>	 3.<BR>Invested.<BR>	 4. Spread, pervaded.<BR>	 5. Washed, cleaned, purified. E.<BR>परि before, मृष् to rub, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=429-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिमृष्यत्
परिमृष्यत् mfn. (-ष्यन्-ष्यन्ती-ष्यत्)<BR>	 1. Envying.<BR>	 2. Rubbing.<BR> E. परि before,<BR>मृष् to bear, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=429-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिमेय|परिमेयं
परिमेय mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>	 1. Measurable, to be measured.<BR>	 2. Few, select.<BR>E. परि before, मा to measure, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=429-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिमोषिन्
परिमोषिन् m. (-षी) A thief, a robber.<BR> E. परि every where, मुष् to steal,<BR>aff. ताच्छील्ये-इनि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=429-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिमोहन|परिमोहनं
परिमोहन n. (-नं) Fascinating, beguiling.<BR> E. परि, and मोहन fascinating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=429-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिमोहिन्
परिमोहिन् mfn. (-ही-हिनी-हि) What is bewitching, fascinating, &c. E.<BR>परि before, मुह् to be foolish, घिणुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=429-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिम्लान
परिम्लान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>	 1. Soiled, stained.<BR>	 2. Waned, withered, faded.<BR>3. Diminished, impaired.<BR>	 n. (नं)<BR>	 1. Soil.<BR>	 2. Change of countenance<BR>by fear or grief.<BR> E. परि, and म्लान dirty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=429-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिरक्षण|परिरक्षणं
परिरक्षण n. (-णं) Guarding, defending, preserving.<BR> E. परि around,<BR>and रक्षण preserving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=429-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिरटन
परिरटन n. (-नं) Crying, crying aloud.<BR> E. परि before, रट् to cry, and<BR>ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=429-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिरब्ध
परिरब्ध mfn. (-ब्धः-ब्धा-ब्धं)<BR>	 1. Embraced.<BR>	 2. Encircled.<BR> E. परि before,<BR>रभ् to begin, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=429-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिरभमाण
परिरभमाण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Embracing.<BR> E. परि, and रभ् to begin,<BR>शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=429-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिरभ्यमाण
परिरभ्यमाण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Being embraced.<BR> E. परि everywhere,<BR>रभ् to go, pass. v., शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=429-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिरम्म
परिरम्म m. (-म्मः) Embrace, embracing.<BR> E. परि about, रभ् to begin,<BR>aff. घञ्, and नुम् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=429-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिरम्मण
परिरम्मण n. (-नं) Embracing.<BR> E. परि before, रभ् to begin, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=429-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिराटिन्
परिराटिन् mfn. (-टी-टिनी-टि) Crying, crying aloud, screaming, &c.<BR>E. परि before, रट् to cry, ताच्छील्ये धिणुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=429-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिरिसमान
परिरिसमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Wishing or trying to embrace.<BR> E. परिरभि<BR>to embrace, desid. v. शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=429-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिलुप्त
परिलुप्त mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं) Gone, lost,<BR> E. परि completely, लुप्त lost.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=429-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिलुप्तसंज्ञ|परिलुप्तसञ्ज्ञ
परिलुप्तसंज्ञ mfn. (-ज्ञः-ज्ञा-ज्ञं) Senseless.<BR> E. परिलुप्त, and संज्ञा sign of<BR>life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=429-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिलेख|परिलेखः
परिलेख m. (-खः) An outline, a sketch.<BR> E. परि + लिख-करणे घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=429-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिलोप|परिलोपः
परिलोप m. (-पः)<BR>	 1. Injury.<BR>	 2. Neglect, omission.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=429-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिवत्सर|परिवत्सरः
परिवत्सर m. (-रः) A year.<BR> E. परि end, वत्सर a year.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=429-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिवदन|परिवदनं
परिवदन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Reviling, accusing.<BR>	 2. Crying out, clamouring,<BR>screaming.<BR> E. परि, and वद् to speak, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=429-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिवर्जन|परिवर्जनं|परिवर्ज्जनं
परिवर्जन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Killing, slaughter.<BR>	 2. Quitting, abandonment.<BR>E. परि finally, वृज् to shun, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=429-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिवर्ज्जित|परिवर्जित
परिवर्ज्जित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Abandoned.<BR>	 2. Devoid of<BR> E. परि before, वृज् to shun, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=429-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परि
परि(री)वर्त्त m. (-र्त्तः)<BR>	 1. Going or turning back.<BR>	 2. Turning round,<BR>revolving.<BR>	 3. Flight, retreat, desertion.<BR>	 4. Exchange, barter.<BR>5. Requital, return.<BR>	 6. The end of a period of four ages, or<BR>destruction of the world.<BR>	 7. A chapter, a book, a canto, &c.<BR>	 8. The<BR>king of the tortoises, or the tortoise incarnation.<BR> E. परि severally,<BR>&c. वृत् to be, aff. भावे घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=429-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिवर्त्तक|परिवर्तक|परिवर्तकं
परिवर्त्तक mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>	 1. Who or what turns back or round.<BR>	 2.<BR>Who or what requites, exchanges, &c.<BR>	 3. Leaving off a thing<BR>begun for some other object.<BR> E. परि, and वृत् to be, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=429-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिवर्त्तन|परिवर्तन|परिवर्तनं|परिवर्त्तनं
परिवर्त्तन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Turning back or round, returning.<BR>	 2. Turning<BR>round, revolving.<BR>	 3. Barter, exchange.<BR>	 4. Requital, return.<BR>	 5.<BR>Inverting, taking or putting any thing in a wrong direction. E.<BR>परि around, वृत to be, भावे-ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=429-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिवर्त्तित|परिवर्तित
परिवर्त्तित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Turned round, revolved.<BR>	 2. Returned,<BR>retreated.<BR>	 3. Taken out but on in a wrong direction.<BR>	 4. Ex-<BR>changed.<BR> E. परि before, वृत् to be, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=429-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिवर्त्तिन्|परिवर्तिन्
परिवर्त्तिन् mfn. (-र्त्ती-र्त्तिनी-र्त्ति)<BR>	 1. Revolving, going round.<BR>	 2. Return-<BR>ing.<BR>	 3. Flying, retreating.<BR>	 4. Exchanging.<BR>	 5. Requiting, recom-<BR>pensing.<BR> E. परि, and वृत् to be, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=429-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिवर्द्धन
परिवर्द्धन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Growing, increasing.<BR>	 2. Rearing, breeding, (as<BR>of cattle.)<BR> E. परि, and वर्द्धन increasing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=429-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिवर्द्धित
परिवर्द्धित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Increased, augmented.<BR> E. परि before, वृद्ध to increase, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=429-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिवर्ह|परिवर्हः
परिवर्ह m. (-र्हः)<BR>	 1. Train, retinue, dependents.<BR>	 2. Royal insignia.<BR>E. परि around, वर्ह् to cover, घञ् aff.; also परिबर्ह.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=429-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिवसथ|परिवसथः
परिवसथ m. (-थः) A village.<BR> E. परि about, वस to abide, aff. आधारे अथच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=429-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिवह|परिवहः
परिवह m. (-हः) Name of the second of the seven courses of wind.<BR>E. परि + वह-अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=429-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिवाद|परिवादः
परिवाद m. (-दः)<BR>	 1. Abuse reproach, reproof.<BR>	 2. Charge, accusation.<BR>3. The bow or quill of the lute or fiddle.<BR> E. परि censure, &c. and<BR>वाद speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=429-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिवादक|परिवादकः
परिवादक m. (-कः) An accuser, a plaintiff, a complaint or calumnia-<BR>tor.<BR> E. परि implying censure, वद् to speak, वुञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=429-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिवादिन्
परिवादिन् mfn. (-दी-दिनी-दि)<BR>	 1. Who or what reproaches, accuses, &c.<BR>2. Censured, abused.<BR>	 3. Calling out, crying, screaming.<BR>	 m. (-दी)<BR>An accuser, a reprover; (in Law,) a plaintiff.<BR>	 f. (-नी) A lute or<BR>a vinā, with seven strings.<BR> E. परिवाद as above, इनि aff. or परि<BR>before, वद् to speak, ताच्छील्ये घिणुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=429-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिवाप|परिवापः
परिवाप m. (-पः)<BR>	 1. Shaving, shearing.<BR>	 2. A pool, a pond, a piece of<BR>water.<BR>	 3. Train, retinue.<BR>	 4. Sowing.<BR>	 5. Furniture.<BR> E. परि be-<BR>fore, वप् to shave, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=429-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिवापन|परिवापनं
परिवापन n. (-नं) Shaving, shearing.<BR> E. परि before, वप् to cut or<BR>shave, causal v. aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=429-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिवापित|परिवापितं
परिवापित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Shaven, shorn.<BR> E. परिवाप shaving, aff.<BR>इतच्. or परि + वप्-णिच्-क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=429-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिवार|परिवारः
परिवार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Dependent.<BR>	 2. Train or retinue.<BR>	 3. A scabbard, a<BR>sheath.<BR> E. परि round, वृ to be, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=429-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिवारता
परिवारता f. (-ता) Subjection, dependence.<BR> E. तल् added to परिवार.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=429-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिवारित
परिवारित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Surrounded, enclosed or begirt by.<BR> E. परि,<BR>and वारित impeded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=429-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिवास|परिवासः
परिवास m. (-सः) Abiding, abode.<BR> E. परि, and वस् to dwell, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=429-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिवासित
परिवासित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Respectfully attentive to superiors. E.<BR>परि respect, वस् to abide, aff. क्त, and इट inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=429-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परि
परि(री)वाह m. (-हः)<BR>	 1. An inundation, an overflowing, natural or arti-<BR>ficial.<BR>	 2. An water course or a drain to carry off excess of water.<BR>E. परि about, वह् to bear, aff. घञ्; also परीवाह.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=430-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिवाहवत्|परिवाहवन्त्
परिवाहवत् m. (-वान्) A pond or pool.<BR> E. परिवाह a drain, and मतुप्<BR>poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=430-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिवाहित
परिवाहित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Drained.<BR> E. परिवाह, and इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=430-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिविण्ण|परिविण्णः
परिविण्ण(न्न) m. (-ण्णः or न्नः) An unmarried elder brother whose junior is<BR>married.<BR> E. परि before, विद् to know, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=430-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिवित्ति|परिवित्तिः
परिवित्ति m. (-त्तिः) An unmarried elder brother, the younger being<BR>married and a householder.<BR> E. परि abandoning, and विद् to cover,<BR>affix क्तिच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=430-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिविन्दक|परिविंदक|परिविंदकः|परिविन्दकः
परिविन्दक m. (-कः) A younger brother married or become a house-<BR>holder before the elder.<BR> E. परि, विद् to possess, क्कुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=430-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिविन्दत्|परिविंदत्
परिविन्दत् m. (-न्दन्) An unmarried elder brother.<BR> E. परि before, विद्<BR>to know, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=430-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिविष्ट
परिविष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>	 1. Surrounded, enclosed 2. Offered, pre-<BR>sented.<BR> E. परि, and विष् to enter, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=430-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिविष्णु
परिविष्णु ind. Entirely or every where VIṢṆU.<BR> E. परि sound, विष्णु<BR>VIṢṆU.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=430-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिविह्वल
परिविह्वल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Agitated, bewildered.<BR> E. परि, and विह्वल agitated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=430-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिविह्वलता
परिविह्वलता f. (-ता) Bewilderment.<BR> E. परिविह्वल, and तल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=430-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिवीत
परिवीत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Surrounded, encompassed, invested.<BR>	 2.<BR>Overspread, pervaded.<BR>	 n. (-तं) The bow of BRAMHĀ.<BR> E. परि, and<BR>व्येञ् to surround, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=430-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिवृंहण|परिवृंहणं
परिवृंहण mfn. (-णः-णी-णं) Augmenting, enlarging, what enlarges or<BR>adds to.<BR>	 m. (-णः) An appendix, an additional work or section. E.<BR>वृहि to increase, with परि prefixed, and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=430-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिवृंहित
परिवृंहित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Increased, augmented.<BR>	 2. Improved,<BR>thriven.<BR>	 3. Sounded.<BR>	 4. Lightened, illuminated.<BR>	 5. Excited,<BR>stimulated.<BR> E. परि before, वृहि to augment, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=430-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिवृढ|परिवृढः
परिवृढ m. (-ढः) A master, an owner, a superior.<BR> E. परि exceeding, वृह<BR>to thrive, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=430-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिवृत|परिवृतः
परिवृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Encompassed, surrounded.<BR>	 2. Gained or<BR>received entirely.<BR>	 3. Known.<BR>	 4. Concealed.<BR>	 5. Overspread.<BR> E. परि<BR>before, वृ to be, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=430-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिवृत्त
परिवृत्त mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं)<BR>	 1. Gone round, revolved.<BR>	 2. Turned back,<BR>retreated, retired.<BR>	 3. Exchanged.<BR>	 4. Finished, ended.<BR>	 n. (-त्तं) An<BR>embrace.<BR> E. परि before, वृत् to be, aff क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=430-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिवृत्ति|परिवृत्तिः
परिवृत्ति f. (-त्तिः)<BR>	 1. Exchange, barter.<BR>	 2. Revolution, return.<BR>	 3. End,<BR>termination.<BR>	 4. An unmarried elder brother.<BR>	 5. Surrounding,<BR>encompassing.<BR>	 6. A striking exchange, one producing charm,<BR>considered as a figure of speech in rhetoric.<BR> E. परि mutually, वृत्<BR>to be, क्तिन aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=430-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिवृत्य
परिवृत्य ind.<BR>	 1. Having retreated or retired.<BR>	 2. Having turned round<BR>or revolved.<BR> E. परि before, वृत् to be, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=430-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिवृस्ति
परिवृस्ति m. (-स्तिः) An elder brother unmarried: see परिवित्ति ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=430-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिवृहित|परिवृहितं
परिवृहित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Increased, literally or figuratively,<BR>grown, thriven.<BR>	 2. Making effort, exerted.<BR> E. परि much, वृह् to<BR>grow, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=430-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिवेतृ
परिवेतृ m. (-ता) A younger brother married or become a householder<BR>before his elder.<BR> E. परि abandoning, (the usual practice,) विद् to<BR>know or possess, (a wife,) तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=430-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिवेदन|परिवेदनं
परिवेदन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Anguish, pain, misery.<BR>	 2. Marriage, (especially<BR>the marriage of a younger brother before the elder,) marrying.<BR>3. Discussion.<BR>	 4. Gain, acquisition.<BR>	 5. Keeping the household<BR>fire.<BR>	 6. Universal existence.<BR>	 f. (-ना)<BR>	 1. Shrewdness, wit.<BR>	 2. Fore-<BR>sight, prudence.<BR> E. परि before, विद् to know, &c. aff. ल्युट्, or युच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=430-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिवेदिन्
परिवेदिन् mfn. (-दी-दिनी-दि)<BR>	 1. Shrewd, knowing.<BR>	 2. Suffering pain.<BR>	 f.<BR>(-नी) The wife of a younger brother, the elder brother being<BR>unmarried.<BR> E. परि, and विद् to know, aff. घिणुन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=430-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिवेश|परिवेशः
परिवेश m. (-शः)<BR>	 1. Surrounding, encompassing.<BR>	 2. The circumference<BR>of a circle.<BR>	 3. The disk of the sun or moon, a halo round the<BR>sun or moon.<BR>	 4. Waiting at or serving up meals.<BR> E. परि round,<BR>विश् or विष् to encompass, aff. घञ्; hence also परिवेष ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=430-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिवेष|परिवेषः
परिवेष m. (-षः)<BR>	 1. Surrounding, encircling.<BR>	 2. The circumference of<BR>a circle.<BR>	 3. The disk of the sun or moon.<BR>	 4. Distributing rice, &c.<BR>to a party, serving up a meal: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=430-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिवेषण|परिवेषणं
परिवेषण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Surrounding, enclosing.<BR>	 2. Serving up dinner,<BR>distributing food to guests, &c.<BR>	 3. A halo round the sun or<BR>moon.<BR> E. परि round, वेषण encompassing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=430-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिवेष्टन|परिवेष्टनं
परिवेष्टन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Surrounding, encompassing.<BR>	 2. Circumference.<BR>E. परि before, वेष्ट् to surround, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=430-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिवेष्टित|परिवेष्टितं
परिवेष्टित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Enclosed, surrounded, encompassed.<BR>	 2.<BR>Covered, veiled.<BR> E. परि around, and वेष्टित surrounded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=430-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिव्यय|परिव्ययः
परिव्यय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. Best.<BR>	 2. Condiment, spices.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=430-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिव्याध|परिव्याधः
परिव्याध m. (-धः)<BR>	 1. A tree, (Pteros permum acerifolia.)<BR>	 2. A sort of<BR>reed growing in water, (Calamus fasciculatus.)<BR> E. परि much,<BR>व्याध pain. परि + व्यध्-कर्त्तरि-ण ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=430-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिव्रज्या
परिव्रज्या f. (-ज्या)<BR>	 1. Ascetic devotion, religious austerity, abandon-<BR>ment of the world.<BR>	 2. Leading the life of a mendicant.<BR> E. परि<BR>about, व्रज्या religious wandering. परि + व्रज्-भावे क्यप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=430-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिव्रढिमन्
परिव्रढिमन् m. (-मा) Masterhood, superiority.<BR> E. परिवृढ, and इमनिच्<BR>aff., ऋ changed to र ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=430-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिव्राज्
परिव्राज् m. (-ड् or ट्) The man of the last religious order, the mendi-<BR>cant devotee.<BR> E. परि about, व्रज् to go, aff. क्किप्, and the vowel<BR>made long; also with घञ् aff. परिव्राज.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=430-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिव्राज|परिव्राजः
परिव्राज m. (-जः) An ascetic: परि + व्रज्-सज्ञायां-कर्त्तरि घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=430-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिव्राजक|परिव्राजकः
परिव्राजक m. (-कः) A religious mendicant.<BR> E. परि about, व्रज् to<BR>wander, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=430-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिव्राज्य
परिव्राज्य n. (-ज्यं) The state or condition of an ascetic.<BR> E. परिव्राज् as<BR>above, and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=430-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिशङ्कनीय|परिशङ्कनीयः
परिशङ्कनीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) To be doubted, to be feared or apprehend-<BR>ed.<BR> E. परि completely, शकि to doubt, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=430-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिशाप
परिशाप m. (-पः) Cursing, reviling.<BR> E. परि before, शप् to curse, घञ्<BR>aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=430-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिशाश्वत
परिशाश्वत f. (-ती) Perpetually the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=430-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिशिष्ट|परिशिष्टं
परिशिष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>	 1. Left, remaining.<BR>	 2. Finished.<BR>	 n. (ष्टं) A<BR>supplement, an appendix.<BR> E. परि, and शिष्ट left. or परि + शिष्-क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=430-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिशीलन|परिशीलनं
परिशीलन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Intercourse, correspondence.<BR>	 2. Steady pursuit,<BR>study.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=430-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिशुद्ध
परिशुद्ध mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>	 1. Cleaned.<BR>	 2. Purified.<BR>	 3. Discharged,<BR>paid.<BR> E. परि before, शुघ् to be pure, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=430-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिशुष्क|परिशुष्कं
परिशुष्क mfn. (-ष्कः-ष्का-ष्कं) Dry, dried.<BR>	 n. (ष्कं) Meat fried, first with<BR>ghee, washed well with warm water, and dressed with spice, &c.<BR>E. परि much, शुष्क dried.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=430-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिशृत|परिशृतः
परिशृत m. (-तः) Ardent spirits.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=430-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिशेष|परिशेषः
परिशेष m. (-षः)<BR>	 1. Remainder.<BR>	 2. Completion.<BR>	 3. Supplement.<BR> E. परि,<BR>and शेष end. परि + शिष्-घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=430-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिशोध|परिशोधः
परिशोध m. (-धः)<BR>	 1. Cleansing, purifying, correcting.<BR>	 2. Discharging a<BR>debt or obligation.<BR> E. परि, and शोध purifying; also परिशोधन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=430-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिशोष|परिशोषः
परिशोष m. (-षः) Drying, evaporation.<BR> E. परि before, शुष् to be dry,<BR>घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=430-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिश्रम|परिश्रमः
परिश्रम m. (-मः)<BR>	 1. Labour, trouble, pain.<BR>	 2. Distress, fatigue. E.<BR>परि exceeding, श्रम weariness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=430-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिश्रय|परिश्रयः
परिश्रय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. An assembly, a meeting.<BR>	 2. An asylum.<BR> E. परि<BR>before, श्री to serve, &c. aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=430-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिश्रान्त|परिश्रान्तः
परिश्रान्त mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं) Overcome with distress or fatigue, ex-<BR>hausted, wearied.<BR> E. परि before, श्रम् to be weary, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=430-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिश्रान्ति|परिश्रांति|परिश्रांतिः|परिश्रान्तिः
परिश्रान्ति f. (-न्तिः)<BR>	 1. Labour, trouble.<BR>	 2. Fatigue, exhaustion.<BR> E. परि<BR>before, श्रम् to be weary, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=430-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिश्रत
परिश्रत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Heard.<BR> E. परि, and श्रुत heard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=431-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिश्लिष
परिश्लिष m. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं) Embraced, clasped.<BR> E. परि before, श्लिष् to<BR>embrace, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=431-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिश्लेष|परिश्लेषः
परिश्लेष m. (-षः) Embracing, an embrace.<BR> E. परि, and श्लेष embracing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=431-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिषत्त्व
परिषत्त्व n. (-त्त्वं) The formation or collection or functions of an<BR>assembly.<BR> E. त्त्व added to the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=431-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिषद्
परिषद् f. (षद् or षत्) An assembly, a meeting, an audience or congre-<BR>gation.<BR> E. परि around, सद् to go, aff. आधारे क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=431-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिषद|परिषदः
परिषद m. (-दः) A spectator at a play, one of an assembly or congre-<BR>gation.<BR> E. परिषद् as above, and अण् aff.; whence it is more usually<BR>परिषद । or परि + सद्-अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=431-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिषद्य|परिषद्यः
परिषद्य m. (-द्यः) One of a party or assembly, a spectator, a guest. E. See परिषद, यत् being added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=431-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिषद्वल|परिषद्वलः
परिषद्वल m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. An assistant in an assembly, an associate.<BR>	 2. A<BR>spectator, &c.<BR> E. परिषद as above, वलच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=431-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिष्क
परिष्क(स्क)न्द m. (-न्दः)<BR>	 1. A foster child, one nourished by a stranger.<BR>2. A servant. see परिस्कन्द ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=431-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिष्कन्न
परिष्कन्न(ण्ण) m. (-न्नः -or -ण्णः) A foster child, or one nourished by a<BR>stranger: see परिस्कन्न.<BR> E. परि + स्कन्द-क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=431-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिष्कार|परिष्कारः
परिष्कार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Decoration, embellishment.<BR>	 2. Cooking, dressing.<BR>3. Finishing, polishing.<BR>	 4. Initiation, purification by essential<BR>rites.<BR>	 5. Surrounding.<BR>	 6. Furniture.<BR> E. परि implying ornament,<BR>and कार making, स inserted, and changed to ष; also in the same<BR>sense परिस्कार.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=431-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिष्कृ
परिष्कृ(स्कृ)त mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Adorned, decorated, embellished.<BR>	 2.<BR>Highly finished or polished.<BR>	 3. Cooked, dressed.<BR>	 4. Purified by<BR>initiatory rites.<BR>	 5. Surrounded, encompassed.<BR> E. परि before, कृ to<BR>make, aff. क्त. see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=431-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिष्कृतभूमि|परिष्कृतभूमिः
परिष्कृतभूमि f. (-मिः) An altar, or ground prepared for a sacrifice,<BR>or for the victim and the untensils employed.<BR> E. परिष्कृत, and भूमि<BR>ground.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=431-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिष्कृति|परिष्कृतिः
परिष्कृति f. (-तिः) Finished, polishing, &c. see परिष्कार.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=431-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिष्टोम|परिष्टोमः
परिष्टोम m. (-मः) An elephant's coloured housings: see षरिस्तोम ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=431-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिष्ठल|परिष्ठलं
परिष्ठल n. (-लं) Surrounding place or site.<BR> E. परि, and स्थल place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=431-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिष्वङ्ग|परिष्वंग|परिष्वंगः|परिष्वङ्गः
परिष्वङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः) Embracing, an embrace.<BR> E. परि before, ष्वजि to<BR>embrace, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=431-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिष्वज्य
परिष्वज्य ind. Having embraced.<BR> E. परि, ष्कजि to embrace, ल्युप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=431-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिसङ्ख्या|परिसंख्या
परिसङ्ख्या f. (-ङ्ख्या)<BR>	 1. Total or complete enumeration or specification,<BR>implying exclusion of any other.<BR>	 2. Reckoning, enumerating. E.<BR>परि, and सङ्ख्या a number.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=431-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिसङ्ख्यात|परिसंख्यात
परिसङ्ख्यात mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Counted, enumerated.<BR>	 2. Reckoned up<BR>or specified exclusively of any more.<BR> E. परि, and सङ्ख्यात counted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=431-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिसङ्ख्यान|परिसंख्यान|परिसंख्यानं
परिसङ्ख्यान n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Exclusive enumeration or specification.<BR>	 2. Cor-<BR>rect judgment.<BR> E. परि, and सङ्ख्यान reckoning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=431-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिसञ्चर|परिसंचर|परिसंचरः
परिसञ्चर m. (-रः) Time of universal destruction.<BR> E. परि + सम-चर-अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=431-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिसभ्य|परिसभ्यः
परिसभ्य m. (-भ्यः) An assistant at an assembly.<BR> E. परि about, सभ्य a<BR>fellow guest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=431-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिसमापन|परिसमापनं
परिसमापन n. (-नं) Finishing entirely.<BR> E. परि, and सम् before, आप् to<BR>get, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=431-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिसमाप्त
परिसमाप्त mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं) Finished, done entirely.<BR> E. परि, and समाप्त finished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=431-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिसमाप्ति|परिसमाप्तिः
परिसमाप्ति f. (-प्तिः) Entire completion.<BR> E. परि, and सम before, आप् to<BR>obtain, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=431-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिसमूहन|परिसमूहनं
परिसमूहन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Heaping up.<BR>	 2. Sprinkling water round the sacri-<BR>ficial fire.<BR> E. परि + सम-उह-भावे-ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=431-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिसर|परिसरः
परिसर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Ground on the skirts of a river or mountain, or<BR>contiguous to a town, &c.<BR>	 2. Death, dying.<BR>	 3. Rule, precept,<BR>prescribed mode.<BR>	 4. Part, place, site.<BR>	 5. Width, breadth.<BR> E. परि<BR>about, or end, term, &c. सर going, from सृ to go, aff. अप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=431-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिसरण|परिसरणं
परिसरण n. (-णं) Running about.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=431-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिसर्प|परिसर्पः
परिसर्प m. (-र्पः)<BR>	 1. Encompassing, surrounding.<BR>	 2. Going, proceeding.<BR>3. following, pursuing.<BR> E. परि around, and सर्प going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=431-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिसर्पण|परिसर्पणं
परिसर्पण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Creeping about.<BR>	 2. Running to and fro.<BR>	 3. Cons-<BR>tantly moving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=431-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परि
परि(री)सर्य्या f. (-र्य्या)<BR>	 1. Perambulation, wandering round or about.<BR>	 2.<BR>Near approach.<BR>	 3. Service.<BR> E. परि about, सृ to go, भावे-क्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=431-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिसाधन
परिसाधन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Accomplishing, effecting.<BR>	 2. Determining, ascer-<BR>taining.<BR> E. परि before, साध् to accomplish, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=431-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिसार|परिसारः
परिसार m. (-रः) Wandering about.<BR> E. परि before, सृ to go, aff.<BR>अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=431-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिसारिन्
परिसारिन् mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि) Wandering.<BR> E. परि before, सृ to go,<BR>धिणुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=431-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिसीमन्
परिसीमन् m. (-मा) Boundary, extreme term or limit.<BR> E. परि and<BR>सीमन् a limit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=431-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिसेधत्
परिसेधत् mfn. (-धन्-धन्ती-धत्) Opposing.<BR> E. परि against, षिध् to effect,<BR>शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=431-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिसेसिचा
परिसेसिचा f. (चा) Frequent bathing or sprinkling.<BR> E. परि before,<BR>षिच् to sprinkle, frequent. v. अङ् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=431-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिस्कन्द|परिस्कंद|परिस्कन्दः
परिस्कन्द m. (-न्दः) A foster child, one nourished by a stranger.<BR>	 n. (-न्दं)<BR>Going round or about.<BR> E. परि about, स्कदि to go, aff. अच्; also स<BR>being optionally changed, परिष्कन्द.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=431-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिस्कन्दत्|परिस्कंदत्
परिस्कन्दत् mfn. (-न्दन्-न्दन्ती-न्दत्)<BR>	 1. Going round or about.<BR>	 2. Surround-<BR>ing, circumambulating.<BR>	 3. Wandering.<BR> E. परि, स्कदि to go, aff.<BR>शतृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=431-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिस्कन्न|परिस्कन्नः
परिस्कन्न m. (-न्नः)<BR>	 1. A foster or an adopted child.<BR>	 2. The Kokila or<BR>Indian cuckoo.<BR> E. परि before, स्कन्द् to go, aff. क्त; also परिष्कन्न.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=431-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिस्तृत
परिस्तृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Covered, spread over.<BR> E. परि, and स्तृत<BR>strewed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=431-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिस्तो
परिस्तो(ष्टो)म m. (-मः) An elephant's painted or coloured cloth or<BR>housings.<BR> E. परि around, स्तु to applaud, aff. क्त, irregular form, मन्<BR>being substituted for the proper termination; also परिष्टोम when<BR>considered as a compound of परि and स्तोम.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=431-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिस्थान|परिस्थानं
परिस्थान n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Fixedness, solidity.<BR>	 2. Fortitude, firmness.<BR> E. परि<BR>and स्थान place; also परिस्थिति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=431-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिस्पन्द|परिस्पंद|परिस्पंदः|परिस्पन्दः
परिस्पन्द m. (-न्दः)<BR>	 1. Beating, throbbing.<BR>	 2. Decoration of the hair,<BR>with flowers, &c.<BR>	 3. Train, retinue.<BR> E. परि around, स्पन्द् to go,<BR>aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=431-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिस्पन्दन|परिस्पन्दनं
परिस्पन्दन n. (-नं) Beating, throbbing.<BR> E. परि before, स्पदि to go, aff.<BR>ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=431-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिस्पन्दमान|परिस्पन्दमानः
परिस्पन्दमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>	 1. Moving tremulously, being gently<BR>agitated, shaking, trembling.<BR>	 3. Throbbing, beating,<BR> E. परि be-<BR>fore, स्पदि to go, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=431-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिस्फुट
परिस्फुट f. (-टा)<BR>	 1. Quite plain, very manifest.<BR>	 2. Fully developed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=431-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिस्फुरण|परिस्फुरणं
परिस्फुरण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Glancing, shooting.<BR>	 2. Budding.<BR> E. परि, and स्फुर्<BR>to expand, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=431-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिस्फुरत्
परिस्फुरत् mfn. (-रन-रन्ती-रत्)<BR>	 1. Budding, expanding.<BR>	 2. Bursting forth.<BR>3. Darting, glancing, moving quickly or suddenly.<BR>	 4. Gleam-<BR>ing.<BR> E. परि, and स्फुर् to expand, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=431-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिस्फुरित
परिस्फुरित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Glancing, gleaming.<BR>	 2. Opened, ex-<BR>panded.<BR>	 3. Shot, glanced.<BR> E. परि, and स्फुर् to expand, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=431-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिस्यन्द|परिस्यंद|परिस्यंदः|परिस्यन्दः
परिस्यन्द m. (-न्दः)<BR>	 1. Oozing, dropping.<BR>	 2. Decoration of the hair.<BR>	 3.<BR>Flow, stream.<BR>	 4. Train, retinue: see परिस्पन्द.<BR> E. परि around,<BR>स्यन्द to drop, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=431-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिस्यन्दन
परिस्यन्दन n. (-नं) Dropping, flowing, oozing.<BR> E. परि, and स्यदि to drop,<BR>ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=431-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिस्रव|परिस्रवः
परिस्रव m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. Flowing, streaming.<BR>	 2. A river, a torrent.<BR> E. परि + स्नु-<BR>भावे-अप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=431-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिस्राव|परिस्रावः
परिस्राव m. (-वः) Effluxion, efflux.<BR> E. परि + स्रु-णिच्-अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=431-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिस्रुत्
परिस्रुत् f. (स्रुत्)<BR>	 1. Vinous liquor.<BR>	 2. Dropping, flowing.<BR> E. परि<BR>before, स्रु to distil, aff. क्विप् and तल् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=431-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिस्रत
परिस्रत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Oozed, trickled, dropped, distilled.<BR>	 f. (-ता)<BR>Vinous or distilled liquor.<BR> E. परि before, स्रु to drop or ooze, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=431-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिहत
परिहत f. (-ता) Loosened.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=431-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिहरण|परिहरणं
परिहरण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Seizing, taking.<BR>	 2. Leaving, abandoning.<BR>	 3. Avoi-<BR>ding.<BR>	 4. Disappearing.<BR>	 5. Refuting, repelling.<BR> E. परि before, ह to<BR>take, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=432-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिहरणीय
परिहरणीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>	 1. To be shunned or avoided.<BR>	 2. To be<BR>taken away.<BR>	 3. To be confuted.<BR> E. परि, हृ to take, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=432-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिहरणीयता
परिहरणीयता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Disappearance, unattainableness.<BR>	 2. Refuta-<BR>tion.<BR> E. परिहरणीय to be taken away, तल् abst. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=432-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिहरत्
परिहरत् mfn. (-रन्-रन्ती-रत्)<BR>	 1. Illuding.<BR>	 2. Shunning, avoiding. E.<BR>परि, हृ to take, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=432-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिहरमाण
परिहरमाण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>	 1. Leaving, quitting.<BR>	 2. Taking, seizing.<BR>3. Confuting.<BR> E. परि before, हृ to take, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=432-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिहर्त्तव्य|परिहर्तव्य
परिहर्त्तव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>	 1. To be shunned or avoided.<BR>	 2. To be<BR>taken away.<BR>	 3. To be confuted.<BR> E. परि before, हृ to take, तव्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=432-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिहाणि|परिहाणिः
परिहाणि(नि) f. (-णि or नि) Decrease, loss.<BR>	 2. Waste, decay, decline.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=432-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परि
परि(री)हार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Disrespect.<BR>	 2. Seizing, surrounding, 3. Bounty,<BR>largess.<BR>	 4. Any thing or person objectionable.<BR>	 5. Leaving.<BR>	 6. Re-<BR>moving.<BR>	 7. Repelling.<BR>	 8. Omission.<BR>	 9. The common land round<BR>a village or town.<BR> E. परि, हृ to take away, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=432-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिहार्य्य|परिहार्य|परिहार्यः|परिहार्य्यः
परिहार्य्य mfn. (-र्य्यः-र्य्या-र्य्यं)<BR>	 1. To be shunned or avoided.<BR>	 2. To be<BR>taken off or away.<BR>	 m. (-र्य्यः) A bracelet: see परीहार्य्य.<BR> E. परि, हृ to<BR>take, कर्मणि-ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=432-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिहास|परिहासः
परिहास m. (-सः)<BR>	 1. Mirth, sport, pastime.<BR>	 2. Deriding. Ridiculing. E.<BR>परि much, हस् to laugh, aff. घञ्; also परीहास.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=432-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिहासवेदिन्
परिहासवेदिन् m. (-दी) A Jester, a wag, a wit.<BR> E. परिहास, and वेदिन्<BR>who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=432-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिहित
परिहित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Covered, invested, put on.<BR> E. परि, and हित<BR>placed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=432-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिहीण
परिहीण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>	 1. Waned, faded, wasted.<BR>	 2. Deserted by,<BR>deprived of.<BR> E. परि, and हीण quitted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=432-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिहृत|परिहृतः
परिहृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Avoided, quitted.<BR>	 2. Taken.<BR>	 3. Repelled,<BR>refuted.<BR> E. परि before, हृ to take, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=432-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परीक्षक|परीक्षकः
परीक्षक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Investigating acutely, trying, examining.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-कः)<BR>	 1. An experimenter, an assayer, a prover.<BR>	 2. An investigator,<BR>a Judge.<BR> E. परि well, closely, ईक्ष् to look or see, aff. ण्वुल्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=432-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिक्षण
परिक्षण n. (-णं) Trial, experiment, examination.<BR> E. परि about, ईक्ष् to<BR>see, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=432-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परीक्षणीय
परीक्षणीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) To be tried or investigated to be submit-<BR>ted to ordeal, &c.<BR> E. परि before, ईक्ष् to see, अनीयर् aff.; also<BR>परीक्षितव्य and परीक्ष्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=432-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परीक्षा
परीक्षा f. (-क्षा)<BR>	 1. Discrimination, investigation, examination, test,<BR>trial, experiment.<BR>	 2. Trial by ordeal of various kinds: see दिव्य.<BR>E. परि intensitive prefix, before, ईक्ष् to see, affs. अङ् and टाप्;<BR>looking into any thing or person closely and minutely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=432-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परीक्षित्
परीक्षित् m. (-क्षित्) The grandson of ARJUNA, to whom the Bhāgavat<BR>was related. He came to the throne of Hastināpura after<BR>Yudhishthira. The advent of the Kali age is placed at the<BR>commencement of his reign. He died of a snake-buite.<BR> E. परि<BR>before, क्षि to destroy, क्विप् aff. also with a final vowel परीक्षितः<BR>he was destroyed in his mother's womb, but reanimated by<BR>KṚṢṆA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=432-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परीक्षित|परीक्षितः
परीक्षित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Tried, examined, tested, proved.<BR>	 m. (-तः) A<BR>prince: see the last.<BR> E. परि before, ईक्ष् to see, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=432-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परीणाय|परीणायः
परीणाय m. (-यः) Moving a piece at chess, draughts, &c.<BR> E. परि<BR>before, णी to take, aff. घञ्. the vowel of the prefix is optionally<BR>made long; also परिणाय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=432-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परीत|परीतं
परीत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Surrounded, encompassed.<BR>	 2. Circumam-<BR>bulated.<BR>	 3. Addicted, affected by.<BR>	 4. Departed.<BR>	 5. Seized.<BR> E. परि<BR>round, and इत gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=432-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परोतत्
परोतत् mfn. (-तत्) Every way spread or extended.<BR> E. परि around,<BR>तन् to spread, aff. क्विप्, and the vowel of the prefix augmented.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=432-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परीत्य
परीत्य ind.<BR>	 1. Having passed round or circumambulated.<BR>	 2. Having<BR>encompassed.<BR> E. परि before, इण् to go, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=432-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परीधाविन्
परीधाविन् m. (-वी) The forty-first year of the Indian cycle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=432-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परीप्सा
परीप्सा f. (-प्सा)<BR>	 1. Desire of obtaining.<BR>	 2. Haste, hurry.<BR> E. परि + आप्-<BR>सन्-भावे अ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=432-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परीभाव|परीभावः
परीभाव m. (-वः) Disrespect. E. See परिभाव, the vowel of the prefix<BR>being here made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=432-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परीयमाण
परीयमाण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Being penetrated or pervaded by.<BR> E. परि<BR>before, इङ् to go, pass. v. शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=432-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परोर
परोर n. (-रं) Fruit.<BR> E. प to satisfy, Unādi aff. ईरन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=432-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परीरण|परीरणं
परीरण m. (-णः)<BR>	 1. A tortoise.<BR>	 2. A stick.<BR>	 3. A garment.<BR> E. परि + रण-अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=432-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परीरम्भ|परीरंभ|परीरंभः|परीरम्भः
परीरम्भ m. (-म्भः) An embrace: see परिरम्भ.<BR> E. परि + रम्भ-घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=432-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परीवर्त्त|परीवर्त|परीवर्तः|परीवर्त्तः
परीवर्त्त m. (-र्त्तः)<BR>	 1. Exchange, barter.<BR>	 2. The royal tortoise: See<BR>परिवर्त्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=432-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परीवाद|परीवादः
परीवाद m. (-दः)<BR>	 1. Reproof, censure, abuse.<BR>	 2. The bow or quill of a<BR>lute: see परिवाद.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=432-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परीवार|परीवारः
परीवार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. The sheath of a sword.<BR>	 2. Dependents, family, reti-<BR>nue.<BR> E. परि around, वृ to cover, aff. घञ् and the final of परि<BR>made long; also परिवार.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=432-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परीवाह|परीवाहः
परीवाह m. (-हः)<BR>	 1. A drain or channel made to carry off water from<BR>a pond that overflows.<BR>	 2. A natural inundation or overflow.<BR>	 3.<BR>Royal insignia.<BR>	 4. A sword-sheath, a scabbard.<BR> E. परि before, वह्<BR>to bear, aff. घञ् and the इ of परि is in consequence optionally<BR>long; also परिवाह.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=432-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परीष्टि|परीष्टिः
परीष्टि f. (-ष्टिः)<BR>	 1. Inquiry, research, especially philosophical.<BR>	 2. Ser-<BR>vice.<BR>	 3. Willingness, readiness.<BR>	 4. Homage, worship.<BR> E. परि<BR>much, इष्टि wish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=432-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परीसार|परीसारः
परीसार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Going round or about, wandering, perambula-<BR>tion.<BR>	 2. Near approach.<BR> E. परि about, सृ to go, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=432-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परीहार|परीहारः
परीहार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Disrespect.<BR>	 2. An open space for the pasturage<BR>of cattle near a village or town.<BR>	 3. Remedying or atoning for<BR>any improper action.<BR> E. परि disrespect, हृ to convey, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=432-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परीहास|परीहासः
परीहास m. (-सः) Mirth, sport, amusement.<BR> E. परि pleasure, हस् to<BR>laugh, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=432-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परु|परुः
परु m. (-रुः)<BR>	 1. A knot or joint in a reed.<BR>	 2. Paradise.<BR>	 3. The ocean.<BR>4. A mountain.<BR> E. पॄ to fill, aff. ड, also परुस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=432-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परुत्
परुत् ind. Last year.<BR> E. पर prior, उत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=432-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परुत्न
परुत्न mfn. (-त्नः-त्ना-त्नं) Of or belonging to last year.<BR> E. परुत् last year, त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=432-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परुद्वार|परुद्वारः
परुद्वार m. (-रः) A horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=432-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परुष|परुषं
परुष mfn. (-षः-षा-षं)<BR>	 1. Harsh, abusive, (speech.)<BR>	 2. Rough, rugged.<BR>3. Severe, cruel, unkind.<BR>	 4. Variegated in colour.<BR>	 5. Shaggy, rough<BR>to the touch.<BR>	 6. Sharp, piercing.<BR>	 n. (-षं)<BR>	 1. Harsh and contume-<BR>lious speech, abuse.<BR>	 2. Yellow Barleria.<BR>	 m. (-षः) A sort of<BR>tree, (Xylocarpus granatum.)<BR> E. पॄ to fill or satisfy, उषन्<BR>Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=432-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परुषवचन
परुषवचन n. (-नं) Harsh language, reproach, abuse.<BR> E. परुष, and वचन<BR>speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=432-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परुषवाच्
परुषवाच् mfn. (-क्) Harsh spoken.<BR>	 f. (-क्) Harsh or contumelious<BR>speech.<BR> E. परुष, and वाच् speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=432-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परुषोक्ति
परुषोक्ति f. (-क्तिः) Abusive or harsh language.<BR> E. परुष, and उक्ति speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=432-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परुषोक्तिक|परुषोक्तिकः
परुषोक्तिक m. (-कः) An abuser, one uttering harsh and scurrilous<BR>language.<BR> E. परुष abuse, and उक्ति speech, aff. कप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=432-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परुस्
परुस् n. (-रुः) The knot or joint of a cane or reed.<BR> E. पॄ to complete,<BR>Unādi aff. उसि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=432-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परूष|परूषं
परूष m. (-षः) The Parush tree: see परुष; also with कन् added परूषक.<BR> E. पॄ-ऊषन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=432-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परेत्
परेत् mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Dead, defunct.<BR>	 m. (-तः) A kind of goblin, a<BR>ghost, a spirit.<BR> E. पर another, (world,) इत gone. or परा + इ-क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=432-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परेतर
परेतर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Faithful, friendly.<BR> E. पर an enemy, इतर other,<BR>opposed to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=432-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परेतराज्
परेतराज् m. (-राट्) A name of YAMA.<BR> E. परेत a ghost, and राज who rules.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=432-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परेद्यवि
परेद्यवि ind. Next day, tomorrow.<BR> E. पर another, एद्यवि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=433-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परेद्युस्
परेद्युस् ind. (-द्युः) Next day.<BR> E. पर after, एद्युस् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=433-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परेप|परेपं
परेप mfn. (पः-पा-पं) Where water is lodged or retired, whence it has,<BR>(a place, &c.)<BR> E. पर, and अप water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=433-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परेष्टि|परेष्टिः
परेष्टि m. (-ष्टिः) BRAMHĀ.<BR> E. पर best, इष्टि worship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=433-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परेष्टुका
परेष्टुका f. (-का) A cow bearing many calves.<BR> E. पर best, इष् to go, तु<BR>aff., and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=433-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परैवित
परैवित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Nourished by a stranger.<BR>	 m. (-तः) The Kokila<BR>or Indian cuckoo.<BR> E. पर a stranger, एवित nourished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=433-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परोक्ष|परोक्षं|परोक्षः
परोक्ष mfn. (-क्षः-क्षा-क्षं)<BR>	 1. Invisible, imperceptible.<BR>	 2. Absent.<BR>	 3. Past.<BR>m. (-क्षः) An ascetic, a religious hermit.<BR>	 n. (-क्षं)<BR>	 1. Invisibility,<BR>absence, secrecy.<BR>	 2. (In Grammar,) Past time or tense.<BR> E. पर<BR>before, उक्ष् to sprinkle, aff. क; or पर away, अक्षि the eye,<BR>form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=433-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परोक्षभोग|परोक्षभोगः
परोक्षभोग m. (-गः) Enjoyment or possession of any thing in the<BR>absence of the proprietor.<BR> E. परोक्ष, and भोग enjoyment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=433-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परोक्षमन्मथ
परोक्षमन्मथ m. (-थः) Not experienced in love matters.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=433-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परोक्षवृत्ति|परोक्षवृत्तिः
परोक्षवृत्ति mfn. (-त्तिः-त्तिः-त्ति) One who does any thing whilst absent.<BR>E. परोक्ष, and वृत्ति practice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=433-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परोक्षार्थ
परोक्षार्थ n. (-र्थं) An absent or invisible object.<BR> E. परोक्ष, and अर्थ object.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=433-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परोत्कर्ष|परोत्कर्षः
परोत्कर्ष m. (-र्षः) Another's superiority.<BR> E. पर, and उत्कर्ष eminence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=433-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परोदित
परोदित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Said by an enemy, &c.<BR>	 n. (-तं) Clamour,<BR>menace.<BR> E. पर, and उदित said.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=433-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परोपकार|परोपकारः
परोपकार m. (-रः) Charity, benevolence, doing good to others. E.<BR>पर another, उपकार assistance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=433-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परोपकारिन्
परोपकारिन् mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि) Benevolent, charitable, good to others.<BR>E. परोपकार, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=433-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परोपकृत
परोपकृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Helped or befriended by another.<BR>	 2.<BR>Brought by another.<BR> E. पर, and उपकृत assisted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=433-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परोपजाप|परोपजापः
परोपजाप n. (-पं) The dissension of enemies.<BR> E. पर, and उपजाप<BR>dissension.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=433-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परोपदेश|परोपदेशः
परोपदेश m. (-शः) Giving advice, counselling, admonishing.<BR> E. पर, and<BR>उपदेश instruction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=433-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परोपरुद्ध
परोपरुद्ध mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं) Invested, besieged, blockaded.<BR> E. पर, and<BR>उपरुद्ध surrounded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=433-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परोवरीण|परोवरीणः
परोवरीण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Having both superior and inferior, prior<BR>and subsequent, &c.<BR> E. पर best, अवर lowest, खश् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=433-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परोष्णी
परोष्णी f. (-ष्णी) A cockroach.<BR> E. पर best, उष्णा warmth; it is also<BR>written परोष्टी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=433-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्कट|पर्कटः
पर्कट n. (-टं) Regret, anxiety.<BR>	 m. (-टः) A heron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=433-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्क्कटि|पर्कटि|पर्कटिः
पर्क्कटि f. (-टिः-टी) The waved-leaf fig tree, (Ficus infectiosa.)<BR> E. पृच्<BR>to touch, अटि aff., ङीष् optionally added; also with इन् added<BR>पर्क्कटिन्. (पाकुड) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=433-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्क्कटिन्|पर्कटिन्
पर्क्कटिन् m. (-टी) The waved-leaf fig tree: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=433-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्जनी|पर्ज्जनी
पर्जनी f. (-नी) A sort of Curcuma, (C. zanthorrhizon.)<BR> E. पृ to satisfy,<BR>aff. क्विप्, जन् to produce, aff. अच् and ङीष्. “दारुहरिद्रा” ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=433-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्ज्जन्य|पर्जन्य|पर्जन्यः|पर्ज्जन्यः
पर्ज्जन्य m. (-न्यः)<BR>	 1. A name of INDRA.<BR>	 2. A thundering cloud.<BR>	 3. The<BR>muttering of clouds or distant thunder.<BR>	 4. Any cloud.<BR>	 5. Rain.<BR>E. पृष्, to sprinkle, (rain,) Unādi aff. अन्य, and ज or य substituted<BR>for ष; also पर्य्यन्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=433-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्ण|पर्णं|पर्णः
पर्ण r. 10th cl. (पर्णयति-ते) To make or be green. अ-चु-उभ-सक-सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=433-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्ण|पर्णं|पर्णः
पर्ण n. (-र्णं)<BR>	 1. A leaf.<BR>	 2. The Pān or betel-leaf.<BR>	 3. A wine.<BR>	 4. The<BR>feather of an arrow.<BR>	 m. (-णः) The Palāsh tree, (Butea frondosa.)<BR>f. (र्णी)<BR>	 1. An aquatic plant, (Pistia stratiotes.)<BR>	 2. The leaf<BR>of the asafœtida.<BR> E. पॄ to please, and Unādi aff. न, fem. aff.<BR>ङीष्, or पर्ण् to be or make green, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=433-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्णकार|पर्णकारः
पर्णकार m. (-रः) A vender of Pān leaves<BR> E. पर्ण, and कार who<BR>makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=433-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्णकृच्छ्र|पर्णकृच्छ्रः
पर्णकृच्छ्र n. (-च्छ्रं) Living upon leaves and water for a limited term,<BR>as a religious obligation.<BR> E. पर्ण, and कृच्छ penance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=433-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्णखण्ड|पर्णखंड|पर्णखण्डः
पर्णखण्ड m. (-ण्डः)<BR>	 1. A tree without apparent blossoms.<BR>	 2. A tree<BR>in general.<BR>	 n. (-ण्डं) A multitude of leaves.<BR> E. पर्ण a leaf, खण्ड a<BR>part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=433-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्णचीरपट|पर्णचीरपटः
पर्णचीरपट m. (-टः) An epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=433-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्णचोरक|पर्णचोरकः
पर्णचोरक m. (-कः) A kind of perfume, called “chor.”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=433-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्णध्वत्
पर्णध्वत् mfn. (-ध्वत्) Causing the falling of leaves.<BR> E. पर्ण a leaf, ध्वंस् to<BR>fall, aff. क्विप्, and तुक् substituted for the final.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=433-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्णनर|पर्णनरः
पर्णनर m. (-रः) A man of leaves, an effigy stuffed with leaves, made<BR>to represent a person deceased, whose body cannot be found, and<BR>for whom obsequial rites are performed with this representative.<BR>E. पर्ण, and नर a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=433-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्णभेदिनी
पर्णभेदिनी f. (-नी) The priyangu creeper. पत्रभेदकमात्रेच ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=433-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्णभोजन|पर्णभोजनः
पर्णभोजन m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. A goat.<BR>	 2. Any animal eating leaves.<BR> E. पर्ण<BR>a leaf, and भोजन food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=433-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्णमाचाल|पर्णमाचालः
पर्णमाचाल m. (-लः) The Kāmrāngā, an acid fruit; (Averrhoa caram-<BR>bola.)<BR> E. पर्ण a leaf, मच् to be tall, aff. आलच्. According to<BR>Vāchaspatya:--कारवेल्लवृक्षे(उच्छा) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=433-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्णमुच्|पर्ण्णमुच्
पर्णमुच् m. (-क्) The winter. शिशिरकाले ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=433-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्णमृग|पर्णमृगः
पर्णमृग m. (-गः) Any wild animal lodging in the boughs of trees, as<BR>a monkey, a sloth, a squirrel.<BR> E. पर्ण, and मृग deer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=433-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्णरूह्
पर्णरूह् m. (-रुट्) The spring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=433-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्ण|पर्णं|पर्णः
पर्ण(र्णि)ल f. (-ला) Full of leaves, some authority places पल्वली instead of this word.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=433-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्णलता
पर्णलता f. (-ता) The betel plant.<BR> E. पर्ण, and लता a creeper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=433-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्णवल्ली
पर्णवल्ली f. (-ल्ली) A tree, (Butea frondosa.)<BR> E. पर्ण and वल्ली a pedicle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=433-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्णवीटिका
पर्णवीटिका f. (-का) Pieces of the areca-nut and other spices rolled up<BR>in betel leaves.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=433-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्णशाला
पर्णशाला f. (-ला) A hut of leaves and grass, a hermitage.<BR> E. पर्ण a<BR>leaf, and शाला a hall.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=433-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्णसन्तर
पर्णसन्तर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Sleeping on leaves.<BR> E. पर्ण and सन्तर a bed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=433-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्णसि|पर्णसिः
पर्णसि m. (-सिः)<BR>	 1. A lotus.<BR>	 2. A summer or water house.<BR>	 3. A vege-<BR>table.<BR>	 4. Decoration, toilet.<BR> E. पॄ to delight, Unādi aff. असि, and<BR>नुङ् inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=433-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्णाल|पर्णालः
पर्णाल m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. A boat.<BR>	 2. A spade or hoe.<BR>	 3. Single combat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=433-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्णाशन|पर्णाशनः
पर्णाशन m. (-नः) A cloud.<BR>	 n. (नं) Feeding on leaves.<BR> E. पर्ण a leaf,<BR>and अशन food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=433-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्णास|पर्णासः
पर्णास (सि) m. (-सः or सिः) A Tulasi tree with few leaves.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=433-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्णासि|पर्णासिः
पर्णासि m. (-सिः) A sort of Basil, (Ocymum sanctum,) with small<BR>leaves,<BR> E. पर्ण a leaf, असि to go, (beautiful,) aff. अच्, अस् or इन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=433-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्णिन्
पर्णिन् m. (-र्णी)<BR>	 1. A tree.<BR>	 2. The Butea frondosa.<BR> E. पर्ण a leaf, aff.<BR>इनि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=433-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्णोटज|पर्णोटजं
पर्णोटज n. (-जं) A hut of leaves, the residence of holy anchorets, a<BR>hermitage.<BR> E. पर्ण a leaf, and उटज a hut.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=433-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्द्द|पर्द|पर्दः|पर्द्दः
पर्द्द r. 1st. cl. (पर्द्दते)<BR>	 1. To fart, to break wind. भ्वा० आत्म० सक० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=433-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्द्द|पर्द|पर्दः|पर्द्दः
पर्द्द m. (-र्द्दः)<BR>	 1. A quantity of hair.<BR>	 2. A fart.<BR> E. पॄ to nourish, द<BR>Unādi aff., or पर्द्द् to fart, aff. भावे घञ् or ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=433-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्द्दन|पर्दन|पर्द्दनं
पर्द्दन n. (-नं) A fart, farting,<BR> E. पर्द्द् to fart, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=433-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्प|पर्पं|पर्पः
पर्प r. 1st. cl. (पर्पति) to go, to move. भ्वा० पर० सक० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=433-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्प|पर्पं|पर्पः
पर्प n. (-पं)<BR>	 1. A house.<BR>	 2. Young grass.<BR>	 3. A wheel chair, or one on<BR>which a cripple can move about.<BR> E. पॄ to be pleased, Unādi aff.<BR>प, or पर्प् to go, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=433-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्पट|पर्पटः
पर्पट m. (-टः) A medicinal plant with bitter leaves, (apparently the<BR>Oldenlandia biflora, though the Hindi name Pāpar is also applied<BR>to the Gardenia latifolia, Rox.)<BR>	 f. (-टी)<BR>	 1. A thin crisp cake made<BR>of any pulse.<BR>	 2. A red aluminous earth, apparently a sort of<BR>Bol, brought from Surāt or Saurāshtra.<BR> E. पर्प् to go, and अटन्<BR>Unādi aff. “क्षेतपापडा” ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=433-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्पटद्रुम|पर्पटद्रुमः
पर्पटद्रुम m. (-मः) Bdellium. कुम्मीवृक्षे ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=433-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्परीक|पर्परीकः
पर्परीक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. The sun 2. Fire.<BR>	 3. A piece of water.<BR> E. पॄ to<BR>nourish, ईकन् Unādi aff., the root repeated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=433-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्प्पिक|पर्पिक|पर्पिकः
पर्प्पिक mf. (-कः-की) A cripple that moves about by the aid of a chair<BR>of cradle.<BR> E. पर्प्प a chair, &c. aff. ष्ठन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=433-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्ब|पर्ब्ब
पर्ब r. 1st. cl. (पर्बति) To go, to move. भ्वा० पर० स० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=434-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्य्य|पर्य
पर्य्य(ल्य)ङ्क m. (-ङ्कः)<BR>	 1. A bed.<BR>	 2. A cloth thrown over the back, loins, and<BR>kneels, while seated upon the hams. The posture is thus des-<BR>cribed on Vāchaspatya, viz:--<BR>एकं पादमथैकस्मिन् विन्यस्योरौ तु मंस्थितम् ।<BR>इतरस्मिन् तथैवोर्द्धं वीरासन मिदं स्मृतम् ॥<BR>उत्तानिते करतले फरमुत्तानितं परम् ।<BR>आधायाङ्क गतं कृत्वा ध्यायेद्यस्तस्य सोऽन्तरम् ॥<BR>E. परि about, अकि to go, aff. अच्; also र being optionally chang-<BR>ed to ल, पल्यङ्क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=434-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्य्यङ्कबन्धन|पर्यङ्कबन्धन|पर्य्यङ्कबन्धनं
पर्य्यङ्कबन्धन n. (-नं) Binding a cloth round the knees, thighs, and back,<BR>as seated on the hams.<BR> E. पर्य्यङ्क, and बन्धन binding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=434-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्य्यटन|पर्यटन|पर्यटनं|पर्य्यटनं
पर्य्यटन n. (-नं) Wandering about, roaming.<BR> E. परि about, अटन going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=434-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्य्यनुयोग|पर्यनुयोग|पर्यनुयोगः|पर्य्यनुयोगः
पर्य्यनुयोग m. (-गः) Asking, inquiring, (with a view to contradict.)<BR>E. परि severally, अनु according to, योग fitness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=434-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्य्यन्त|पर्यन्त|पर्यंत|पर्यन्तः|पर्य्यन्तः
पर्य्यन्त m. (-न्तः)<BR>	 1. Limit, term, boundary, extent.<BR>	 2. End, termina-<BR>tion, close.<BR>	 3. Side, flank.<BR>	 n. (-न्तं) Far, (limitative,) as किंपर्य्यन्तं<BR>or कियत्पर्य्यन्तं, how much, how far.<BR> E. परि, and अन्त end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=434-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्य्यन्तभू|पर्यन्तभू|पर्यंतभू
पर्य्यन्तभू f. (-भूः) Ground contiguous to the skirts of a river or moun-<BR>tain, &c.<BR> E. परि about, अन्त term, भू earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=434-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्य्यन्तस्थ|पर्यन्तस्थ
पर्य्यन्तस्थ mfn. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थं) Limitative, boundary, confining.<BR> E. पर्य्यन्त,<BR>and स्थ what stays.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=434-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्य्यन्तस्थित|पर्यन्तस्थित
पर्य्यन्तस्थित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Bounding, confining.<BR> E. पर्य्यन्त, and स्थित<BR>placed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=434-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्य्यन्तिका|पर्यन्तिका|पर्यंतिका
पर्य्यन्तिका f. (-का) Loss of all good qualities, depravity.<BR> E. परि com-<BR>pletely, अन्त end, ठन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=434-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्य्यन्य|पर्यन्य|पर्य्यन्यः
पर्य्यन्य m. (-न्यः)<BR>	 1. A name of INDRA.<BR>	 2. A thunder cloud.<BR>	 3. The mut-<BR>tering of clouds.<BR> E. पृष् to sprinkle, अन्य Unādi aff., य substituted<BR>for ष; it is also read पर्ज्जन्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=434-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्य्यय|पर्यय|पर्ययः|पर्य्ययः
पर्य्यय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. Contrariety, opposition.<BR>	 2. Irregular or inverted<BR>order.<BR>	 3. Neglect of enjoined or customary observances.<BR>	 4. Re-<BR>volution, lapse, expiration.<BR>	 5. Change, alteration.<BR>	 6. Confusion.<BR>E. परि improperly, अय् to go or be, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=434-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्य्ययण|पर्ययण|पर्ययणं|पर्य्ययणं
पर्य्ययण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. A horse's saddle or housings.<BR>	 2. Walking round.<BR>E. परि about, अयण going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=434-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्य्यवदात|पर्यवदात
पर्य्यवदात f. (-ता) Quite pure or clean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=434-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्य्यवसान|पर्यवसान|पर्यवसानं
पर्य्यवसान n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. End, conclusion.<BR>	 2. Determination.<BR> E. परि, and<BR>अवसान end. परि + अव + सो-भावे ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=434-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्य्यवसित|पर्यवसित
पर्य्यवसित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Finished, completed, concluded.<BR>	 2.<BR>Perished.<BR> E. परि and अवसित ended.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=434-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्य्यवस्था|पर्यवस्था
पर्य्यवस्था f. (-स्था) Opposition, contradiction.<BR> E. परि opposition, अवस्था<BR>staying, station. परि + अव + स्था-अङ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=434-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्य्यवस्थातृ|पर्यवस्थातृ
पर्य्यवस्थातृ mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ) Opposing, obstructing, opposed to or<BR>against.<BR>	 m. (-ता) An antagonist, an opponent, an enemy.<BR> E. परि<BR>against, अव before, स्था to stand or be, aff. तृच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=434-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्य्यवस्थान|पर्यवस्थान|पर्यवस्थानं|पर्य्यवस्थानं
पर्य्यवस्थान n. (-नं) Opposition, resistance, contradiction.<BR> E. परि<BR>against, अव being, स्थान standing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=434-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्य्यवस्थित|पर्यवस्थित
पर्य्यवस्थित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Opposed to, siding with an enemy.<BR> E. परि<BR>adverse, अवस्थित staying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=434-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्य्यश्रु|पर्यश्रु
पर्य्यश्रु mfn. (-श्रुः-श्रुः-श्रु) Filled or suffused with tears.<BR> E. परि, and<BR>अश्रु a tear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=434-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्य्यवष्टब्ध|पर्यवष्टब्ध
पर्य्यवष्टब्ध mfn. (-ब्धः-ब्धा-ब्धं) Surrounded, invested.<BR> E. परि, and अवष्टब्ध<BR>stopped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=434-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्य्यवष्टम्मन
पर्य्यवष्टम्मन n. (-नं) Surrounding, investing.<BR> E. परि, and अवष्टम्मन obs-<BR>tructing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=434-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्य्यसन|पर्यसन|पर्यसनं
पर्य्यसन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Casting, sending.<BR>	 2. Putting off or away.<BR>	 3. Throw-<BR>ing.<BR> E. परि, and अस् to throw, भावे ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=434-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्य्यस्यत्|पर्यस्यत्
पर्य्यस्यत् mfn. (-स्यन्-स्यन्ती-स्यत्)<BR>	 1. Going forth, issuing.<BR>	 2. Investing,<BR>oversetting.<BR>	 3. Scattering.<BR> E. परि before, अस् to throw, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=434-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्य्यस्त|पर्यस्त|पर्य्यस्तः
पर्य्यस्त mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं)<BR>	 1. Fallen, descended, alighted.<BR>	 2. Thrown<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=434-b" target="_blank">Page434-b+ 61</a>]<BR>down or off.<BR>	 3. Overturned, upset.<BR>	 4. Struck, killed.<BR>	 5. Dismissed,<BR>laid aside.<BR>	 6. Bound, surrounded.<BR> E. परि round, &c. अस्त thrown.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=434-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्य्यस्तिका|पर्यस्तिका
पर्य्यस्तिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. A bed.<BR>	 2. Sitting upon the hams: (see पर्य्यङ्क)<BR>E. परि about, अस् to be, aff, क्तिन्, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=434-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्य्याकुल|पर्याकुल
पर्य्याकुल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Agitated, anxious.<BR>	 f. (ला)<BR>	 1. Turbid.<BR>	 2. Con-<BR>fused, disordered.<BR> E. परि, and आकुल agitated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=434-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्य्यागलत्|पर्यागलत्
पर्य्यागलत् mfn. (-लन्-लन्ती-लत्) Dropping, falling.<BR> E. परि, and आङ्<BR>before, गल् to fall, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=434-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्य्याचान्त|पर्याचान्त
पर्य्याचान्त mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं) Sipped, (as water, to rinse the mouth<BR>whilst eating.)<BR> E. परि, and आचान्त sipped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=434-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्य्याण|पर्याण|पर्याणं|पर्य्याणं
पर्य्याण n. (-णं) A saddle, a pack-saddle or cloth serving for one.<BR> E. परि<BR>about, इण् to go. form irr, or परि + वा-ल्युट्-पृषो ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=434-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्य्याप्त|पर्याप्त|पर्याप्तं|पर्य्याप्तं
पर्य्याप्त mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं)<BR>	 1. Obtained, gained.<BR>	 2. Able, adequate.<BR>	 3. All,<BR>complete, entire, enough, sufficient.<BR>	 n. adv. (-प्तं)<BR>	 1. Willing,<BR>readily.<BR>	 2. Ably, powerfully.<BR>	 3. Satisfactorily.<BR>	 4. Unwillingly.<BR>E. परि before, आप् to acquire, aff. भावे क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=434-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्य्याप्तभोग|पर्याप्तभोग
पर्य्याप्तभोग mfn. (-गः-गा-गं) Possessing or enjoying a sufficiency. E.<BR>पर्य्याप्त, and भोग enjoyment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=434-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्य्याप्ति|पर्याप्ति|पर्याप्तिः|पर्य्याप्तिः
पर्य्याप्ति f. (-प्तिः)<BR>	 1. Willingness, readiness.<BR>	 2. Obtaining, acquiring.<BR>	 3.<BR>Satisfaction, repletion, satiety.<BR>	 4. Entireness, fulness, sufficiency.<BR>5. Adequacy, competency, fitness.<BR>	 6. Discrimination or distinction<BR>of objects according to their natural properties.<BR>	 7. Preserving,<BR>guarding.<BR>	 8. Warding off a blow.<BR> E. परि exceeding, आप्ति obtain-<BR>ing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=434-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्य्याय|पर्याय|पर्यायः|पर्य्यायः
पर्य्याय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. Order, arrangement, regular and methodical dis-<BR>posal or succession.<BR>	 2. Manner, kind.<BR>	 3. Opportunity, occasion.<BR>4. Manufacture, preparation, artificial production.<BR>	 5. Property<BR>of substances, as bitter, cooling, &c.<BR>	 6. Generic or specific charac-<BR>ter.<BR>	 7. Comprehensiveness, aggregation.<BR>	 8. The text of a voca-<BR>bulary, or the order of the synonyms for any term.<BR> E. परि suc-<BR>cessively, अय् to go or proceed, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=434-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्य्यायशयन|पर्यायशयन|पर्य्यायशयनं
पर्य्यायशयन n. (-नं) Alternate sleeping and watching.<BR> E. पर्य्याय order,<BR>शयन sleeping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=434-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्य्यायान्न|पर्यायान्न
पर्य्यायान्न n. (-न्नं) Food that should have been given to some one else,<BR>as that of a Śūdra to a Brāhman, &c.<BR> E. पर्य्याय, and अन्न food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=434-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्य्याली|पर्याली
पर्य्याली Ind. A particle expressing “harm,” “injury.”<BR> E. परि + आ +<BR>अल्-इ ऊर्य्यादि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=434-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्य्यालोचन|पर्यालोचन|पर्यालोचनं
पर्य्यालोचन n. (-नं) Looking round or about.<BR>	 2. Considering, delibera-<BR>ting.<BR>	 3. Knowing, recognising.<BR> E. परि, and आङ् before, लोच् to<BR>see, aff. भावे ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=434-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्य्याविल|पर्याविल
पर्य्याविल f. (-ला) Very turbid, much soiled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=434-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्य्यास|पर्यास|पर्यासः|पर्य्यासः
पर्य्यास m. (-सः)<BR>	 1. Inverted order or position.<BR>	 2. End, conclusion.<BR>	 3.<BR>Rotation, revolution.<BR> E. परि before, अस् to be, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=434-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्य्याहार|पर्याहार|पर्याहारः
पर्य्याहार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Conveying, taking.<BR>	 2. A load.<BR>	 3. A yoke.<BR>	 4. Stor-<BR>ing hay or grain.<BR>	 5. An ewer, a pitcher.<BR> E. परि, and आङ् before,<BR>हृ to take, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=434-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्य्युक्षण|पर्युक्षण|पर्युक्षणं
पर्य्युक्षण n. (-णं) Sprinkling round water without uttering any mantras.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=434-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्य्युत्थान|पर्युत्थान|पर्युत्थानं
पर्य्युत्थान n. (-णं) Standing up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=434-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्य्युत्सुक|पर्युत्सुक
पर्य्युत्सुक mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>	 1. Afflicted, sorrowful, regretting.<BR>	 2. De-<BR>sirous, longing for.<BR> E. परि, and उत्सुक unhappy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=434-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्य्युदञ्चन|पर्युदञ्चन|पर्युदंचन|पर्युदंचनं|पर्य्युदञ्चनं
पर्य्युदञ्चन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Debt.<BR>	 2. Raising up, taking out.<BR> E. परि severally,<BR>उत् over, अञ्च् to go, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=434-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्य्युदस्त|पर्युदस्त|पर्य्युदस्तः
पर्य्युदस्त mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं)<BR>	 1. Prohibited, objected to, (as a ceremony.)<BR>2. Excepted, excluded.<BR> E. परि, and उद् before, अस to be, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=434-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्य्युदास|पर्युदास|पर्युदासः|पर्य्युदासः
पर्य्युदास m. (-सः) A prohibitive rule or precept.<BR> E. परि, and उद् before,<BR>अस् to throw or be, aff. घञ्; also पर्य्युदासन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=434-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्य्युपासन|पर्युपासन|पर्युपासनं
पर्य्युपासन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Joining in or concurrence with any act of reve-<BR>rence.<BR>	 2. Service, worship.<BR>	 3. Courtsey.<BR> E. परि, and उपासना<BR>worship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=434-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्य्युपासीन|पर्युपासीन
पर्य्युपासीन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Seated or sitting upon.<BR> E. परि, and उप<BR>before, आसीन seated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=434-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्य्युप्त|पर्युप्त
पर्य्युप्त mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं)<BR>	 1. Sown.<BR>	 2. Set as a gem in a ring,<BR> E. परि be-<BR>fore, वप् to sow, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=435-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्य्युषित|पर्युषित|पर्य्युषितं
पर्य्युषित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Stale, not fresh.<BR>	 2. Insipid.<BR>	 3. Stupid, vain.<BR>E. परि about, वस् to abide, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=435-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्य्युषितभोजिन्|पर्युषितभोजिन्
पर्य्युषितभोजिन् m. (-जी) The eater of stale viands, who will be regener-<BR>ated as a maggot or worm.<BR> E. पर्य्युषित stale, भोजिन् who eats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=435-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्य्येषणा|पर्येषणा
पर्य्येषणा f. (-णा)<BR>	 1. Research, investigation of duty by reasoning.<BR>	 2.<BR>Search, inquiry in general.<BR> E. परि severally, इष् to go, with युच्<BR>and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=435-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्य्येष्टि|पर्येष्टि|पर्येष्टिः
पर्य्येष्टि f. (-ष्टि) Search, inquiry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=435-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्व|पर्व्व
पर्व r. 1st. cl. (पर्वति) To fill. भ्वा० पर० सक० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=435-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्व्वक|पर्वक|पर्वकं|पर्व्वकं
पर्व्वक n. (-कं) The knee.<BR> E. पर्व्व for पर्व्वन् a joint, aff. कन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=435-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्व्वकारिन्|पर्वकारिन्
पर्व्वकारिन् m. (-री) A Brāhman who performs ceremonies for hire out<BR>of season.<BR> E. पर्व्व, and कारिन् who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=435-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्व्वगामिन्|पर्वगामिन्
पर्व्वगामिन् m. (-मी) A man who associates with his wife on festival<BR>or holy days.<BR> E. पर्व्व, and गामिन् who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=435-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्व्वणिका|पर्वणिका
पर्व्वणिका f. (-का) Specks with pain on the edge of the cornea of the<BR>eye.<BR> E. पर्व्वन्, and कन् added; also पर्व्वणीका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=435-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्व्वत|पर्वत|पर्वतः|पर्व्वतः
पर्व्वत m. (-तः)<BR>	 1. A mountain, a hill.<BR>	 2. A tree.<BR>	 3. A sort of potherb.<BR>4. A kind of fish, (Silurus pabda, HAM.)<BR>	 5. One of the divine<BR>Ṛṣis, a friend and rival of NĀRADA, and mentioned in the<BR>Mahābhārata.<BR>	 6. The number “Seven.”<BR> E. पर्व्व to fill, Unādi<BR>aff. अतच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=435-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्व्वतकाक|पर्वतकाक|पर्वतकाकः|पर्व्वतकाकः
पर्व्वतकाक m. (-कः) A raven.<BR> E. पर्व्वत a mountain, and काक a crow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=435-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्व्वतज|पर्वतज
पर्व्वतज mfn. (-जः-जा-जं) Mountain, mountain-born.<BR>	 f. (-जा) Ariver.<BR>E. पर्व्वत a mountain, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=435-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्व्वतवासिन्|पर्वतवासिन्
पर्व्वतवासिन् mfn. (-सी-सिनी-सि) Living, &c. in the mountains.<BR>	 f. (-नी)<BR>1. A name of DURGĀ.<BR>	 2. The Gayatrī.<BR> E. पर्व्वत, and वासिन् who<BR>dwells.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=435-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्व्वताधारा|पर्वताधारा
पर्व्वताधारा f. (-रा) The earth.<BR> E. पर्व्वत a mountain, and आधार a recep-<BR>tacle or stay.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=435-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्व्वतारि|पर्वतारि|पर्वतारिः|पर्व्वतारिः
पर्व्वतारि m. (-रिः) A name of INDRA.<BR> E. पर्व्वत a mountain, and अरि<BR>an enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=435-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्व्वताशय|पर्वताशय|पर्वताशयः|पर्व्वताशयः
पर्व्वताशय m. (-यः) A cloud.<BR> E. पर्व्वत a mountain, and आशय asylum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=435-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्व्वताश्रय|पर्वताश्रय|पर्वताश्रयः|पर्व्वताश्रयः
पर्व्वताश्रय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Mountaineer, living, &c. in mountains.<BR>m. (-यः) A fabulous animal, the Śarabha.<BR> E. पर्व्वत, and आश्रय<BR>abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=435-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्व्वतीय|पर्वतीय|पर्व्वतीयः
पर्व्वतीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Mountainous, mountaineer, &c.<BR> E. पर्व्वत moun-<BR>tain, छ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=435-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्व्वधि|पर्वधि|पर्वधिः|पर्व्वधिः
पर्व्वधि m. (-धिः) The moon.<BR> E. पर्व्व a day of the month, and धि who<BR>has.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=435-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्व्वन्|पर्वन्
पर्व्वन् n. (-र्व्वं)<BR>	 1. A knot, a joint in a cane or body, &c.<BR>	 2. A name<BR>given to certain days in the lunar month, as the full and change<BR>of the moon, and the 8th and 14th of each half month.<BR>	 3. Par-<BR>ticular periods of the year, as the equinox, solstice, &c.<BR>	 4. The<BR>moment of the sun's entering a new sign.<BR>	 5. A festival, a holy<BR>day.<BR>	 6. Opportunity, occasion.<BR>	 7. A chapter, a book, the divi-<BR>sion of a work.<BR>	 8. A moment, an instant.<BR>	 9. Step of a staircase.<BR>E. पॄ to fill or please, Unādi aff. वनिप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=435-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्व्वपुष्पी|पर्वपुष्पी
पर्व्वपुष्पी f. (-ष्पी) A plant, also called Rāmadūti.<BR> E. पर्व्व a joint, and<BR>पुष्प a flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=435-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्व्वपूर्णता|पर्वपूर्णता
पर्व्वपूर्णता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Preparations for an assembly or festival.<BR>	 2. Join-<BR>ing, uniting.<BR>	 3. Completion of a festival.<BR> E. पर्व्व a festival, and<BR>पूर्णता completion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=435-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्व्वयोनि|पर्वयोनि|पर्वयोनिः|पर्व्वयोनिः
पर्व्वयोनि m. (-निः) A cane or reed, the sugarcane, &c.<BR> E. पर्व्व a joint,<BR>and योनि place of production.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=435-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्व्वरीण|पर्वरीण|पर्व्वरीणं|पर्व्वरीणः
पर्व्वरीण n. (-णं) A festival, &c.: see पर्व्वन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=435-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्व्वरुह्|पर्वरुह्
पर्व्वरुह् m. (-रुट्) The pomegranate.<BR> E. पर्व्व a joint, and रुह what grows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=435-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्व्वसन्धि|पर्वसन्धि|पर्वसंधिः|पर्व्वसन्धिः
पर्व्वसन्धि m. (-न्धिः) The full and change of the moon, the junction of<BR>the 15th and 1st of a lunar fortnight, or the precise moment of<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=435-b" target="_blank">Page435-b+ 60</a>]<BR>the full and change of the moon.<BR> E. पर्व्व a joining of the month,<BR>and सन्धि union.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=435-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्व्वावधि|पर्वावधि
पर्व्वावधि m. (-धिः) A peculiar period, the end of a Parva, &c.<BR> E. पर्व्व<BR>as above, and अवधि limit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=435-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्व्वित|पर्वित|पर्वितः|पर्व्वितः
पर्व्वित m. (-तः) A sort of fish, (Silurus pabda, HAM.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=435-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्शु|पर्शुः
पर्शु m. (-र्शुः) An axe, a hatchet.<BR> E. पर an enemy, शृ to destroy, Unādi<BR>aff. कु, deriv. irr,; or स्पृश् to touch, changed to पृ, and शुन् Unādi<BR>aff.; also परशु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=435-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्शुका
पर्शुका f. (-का) A rib.<BR> E. पृ to fill, to complete, शुन् aff. and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=435-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्शुपाणि|पर्शुपाणिः
पर्शुपाणि m. (-णिः) A name of GAṆEŚA.<BR> E. पशु an axe, and पाणि the<BR>hand, holding an axe, in one hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=435-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्शुराम|पर्शुरामः
पर्शुराम m. (-मः) The first of three RĀMAS, being the sixth Avatār<BR>of VIṢṆU, as the son of the Muni JAMADAGNI.<BR> E. पर्शु an axe,<BR>and राम RĀMA; also परशुराम.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=435-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्श्वध|पर्श्वधः
पर्श्वध m. (-धः) An axe, a hatchet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=435-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्ष|पर्षः
पर्ष r. 1st cl. (पर्षते)<BR>	 1. To be kind or affectionate to.<BR>	 2. To be moist.<BR>भ्वा० आत्म० सक० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=435-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्षद्
पर्षद् f. (-षद् or षत्) An assembly, an audience.<BR> E. पृष् to please, Unādi<BR>aff. अदि; also परिषद्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=435-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्षद्वल|पर्षद्वलः
पर्षद्वल m. (-लः) An assistant at an assembly, a spectator, &c.<BR> E. पर्षद्<BR>as above, वलच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=435-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पल|पलं|पलः
पल r. 1st cl. (पलति) To go, to move. भ्वा० पर० सक० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=435-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पल|पलं|पलः
पल r. 1st cl. (पालयति-ते) To protect. चुरा० उभ० सक० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=435-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पल|पलं|पलः
पल n. (-लं)<BR>	 1. A weight of gold or silver equal to four Karṣas or<BR>Suvarnas; also of four or of eight Tolās, or in common use,<BR>of three Tolās, two Māshas, and eight Rattis.<BR>	 2. A moment, the<BR>sixtieth part of an Indian hour.<BR>	 3. Flesh.<BR>	 m. (-लः) Straw after<BR>threshing, &c.<BR> E. पल् to go, to move, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=435-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पलक्षार|पलक्षारः
पलक्षार m. (-रः) Blood.<BR> E. पल flesh, and क्षार what oozes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=435-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पलगण्ड|पलगंड|पलगण्डः
पलगण्ड m. (-ण्डः) A bricklayer, a plasterer.<BR> E. पल flesh or mortar,<BR>compared to it, and गण्ड a mark or spot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=435-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पलङ्कट|पलंकट|पलङ्कटः
पलङ्कट mfn. (-टः-टा-टं) Timid, fearful, frightened.<BR> E. पल flesh, कट्<BR>to go, aff. स्वच्; whose flesh shrinks with fear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=435-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पलङ्कर|पलंकर|पलंकरः|पलङ्करः
पलङ्कर m. (-रः) Bile.<BR> E. पल flesh, कर what makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=435-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पलङ्कष|पलंकष|पलंकषः|पलङ्कषः
पलङ्कष m. (-षः)<BR>	 1. A Rākshasa, an imp or goblin.<BR>	 mf. (-षः-षा) The<BR>Bdellium tree.<BR>	 f. (-षा)<BR>	 1. A plant, (Ruellia longifolia.)<BR>	 2. The<BR>ichneumon plant: see रास्ना.<BR>	 3. The Palāsh tree, (Butea frondosa.)<BR>4. Lac, the animal dye.<BR>	 5. A creeper: see मुण्डीरी.<BR> E. पल flesh,<BR>and कष what injures, aff. खच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=435-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पलभा
पलभा f. (-भा) The mid-day shadow of a gnomon, when the sun is<BR>in the equinoctial points.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=435-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पलल|पललं|पललः
पलल n. (-लं)<BR>	 1. Flesh.<BR>	 2. Mud, mire, clay.<BR>	 2. Oil-cake or sesamum<BR>seed.<BR>	 m. (-लः) A Rākshasa, a goblin or imp.<BR> E. पल् to go, Unādi<BR>aff. कलच्; or पल flesh, and ला to get, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=435-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पललज्वर|पललज्वरः
पललज्वर m. (-रः) Bile.<BR> E. पलल flesh, ज्वर heat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=435-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पललप्रिय|पललप्रियः
पललप्रिय m. (-यः) A raven.<BR> E. पलल, and प्रिय fond of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=435-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पललाशय|पललाशयः
पललाशय m. (-यः) Swelled neck, bronchocele.<BR> E. पलल flesh, आशय asylum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=435-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पलव|पलवः
पलव m. (-वः) A snare or basket of wicker work for catching fish. E.<BR>पल flesh, and वा to get, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=435-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पलाग्नि|पलाग्निः
पलाग्नि m. (-ग्निः) Bile, the bilious humour.<BR> E. पल flesh, अग्नि fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=435-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पलाङ्ग|पलांग|पलाङ्गः
पलाङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः) The Gangetic porpoise.<BR> E. पल flesh, गम् to go or get,<BR>aff. ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=435-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पलाण्डु|पलांडु|पलाण्डुः
पलाण्डु m. (-ण्डुः) An onion.<BR> E. पल् to preserve (from disease,) अण्डु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=435-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पलाद|पलादः
पलाद mf. (-दः-दा) A Rākshasa, male or female.<BR> E. पल flesh, अद who<BR>eats; also पलादन mf. (-नः-नी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=435-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पलाप|पलापः
पलाप m. (-पः)<BR>	 1. A halter.<BR>	 2. An elephant's temples.<BR> E. पल + आप-घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=435-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पलापहा
पलापहा f. (-हा) A collyrium: see कुलत्था.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=435-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पलायन|पलायनं
पलायन n. (-नं) Flight, retreat.<BR> E. परा from, अय् to go, ल्युट् aff. र<BR>changed to ल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=435-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पलायमान
पलायमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Running away.<BR> E. परा before, अय् to go, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=435-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पलायनपरायण
पलायनपरायण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Fugitive.<BR> E. पलायन, and परायण addic-<BR>ted to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=436-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पलायित|पलायितः
पलायित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Defeated, flown, run away, retreated. E.<BR>पलायन flying, इतच् aff., or परा + अय्गत्यर्थत्वात्-कर्त्तरि क्त रस्य लः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=436-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पलाल|पलालं|पलालः
पलाल mn. (-लः-लं) Straw.<BR> E. पल् to go, Unādi aff. कालन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=436-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पलालदोहद|पलालदोहदः
पलालदोहद m. (-दः) The mango tree.<BR> E. पलाल straw, दोहद wishing,<BR>requiring straw for manure, or from the fruit being sometimes<BR>ripened in straw.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=436-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पलाश|पलाशं|पलाशः
पलाश mfn. (-शः-शा-शं)<BR>	 1. Green.<BR>	 2. Unfeeling, unmerciful, cruel.<BR>	 n.<BR>(-शं) A leaf.<BR>	 m. (-शः)<BR>	 1. A tree bearing red blossoms, (Butea<BR>frondosa.)<BR>	 2. A demon, a goblin.<BR>	 3. A sort of Curcuma, (C. re-<BR>clinata, Rox.)<BR>	 4. Ancient Behār or Magadha.<BR>	 f. (-शी)<BR>	 1. Lac.<BR>2. A kind of creeper.<BR> E. पल going, or flesh, अश् to spread, to eat,<BR>aff. अण् or अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=436-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पलाशक|पलाशकः
पलाशक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. Curcuma reclinata.<BR>	 2. The Palāsh tree.<BR> E. कन्<BR>added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=436-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पलाशाख्य|पलाशाख्यः
पलाशाख्य m. (-ख्यः) Asafœtida.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=436-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पलाशाम्भा
पलाशाम्भा f. (-म्भा) Ajwaen: see गन्धपत्रा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=436-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पलाशिन्
पलाशिन् m. (-शी)<BR>	 1. A tree in general.<BR>	 2. A goblin.<BR>	 3. A sort of<BR>Mimusops, (M. kauki, Rox.)<BR> E. पलाश a leaf, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=436-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पलिक्नी
पलिक्नी f. (-क्नी)<BR>	 1. An old or greyheaded woman.<BR>	 2. A cow with<BR>calf.<BR> E. पलित grey hair, aff. ङीप्, and क्न substituted for तः see<BR>पलित.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=436-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पलिघ|पलिघः
पलिघ m. (-घः)<BR>	 1. A glass vessel.<BR>	 2. A water pot.<BR>	 3. The gate way of<BR>a building.<BR>	 4. A wall, a rampart.<BR>	 5. A cowpen.<BR>	 6. An iron club.<BR>E. परि completely, हन् to injure; घ substituted for the radical,<BR>and र changed to लः see परिघ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=436-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पलित|पलितं|पलितः
पलित mfn. (-तः-ता-ती-तं) Grey-haired, old.<BR>	 m. (-तः) An old man.<BR>	 f.<BR>(-ता) An old woman.<BR>	 n. (-तं)<BR>	 1. Greyness of the hair.<BR>	 2. Much or<BR>ornamented hair.<BR>	 3. Heat, burning.<BR>	 4. Mud, mire.<BR>	 5. Benzoin.<BR>E. पल् to go, (towards death,) Unādi aff. भावे क्त, or पल flesh, &c.<BR>and इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=436-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पल्यङ्क|पल्यंक|पल्यंकः|पल्यङ्कः
पल्यङ्क m. (-ङ्कः) A bedstead. E. See पर्य्यङ्क, र being changed to ल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=436-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पल्ययन|पल्ययनं
पल्ययन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. A saddle, a pack-saddle.<BR>	 2. A rein, a bridle.<BR> E. परि<BR>before, अयन going, र changed to ल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=436-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पल्युल
पल्युल r. 10th cl. (पल्युलयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To cut.<BR>	 2. To purify; also written<BR>पल्युल्ल and पल्यूल &c. अद० चुरा० उभ० सक० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=436-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पल्यूल
पल्यूल r. 10th cl. (पल्यूलयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To cut.<BR>	 2. To purify; also पल्युल and पल्युल्ल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=436-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पल्ल|पल्लः
पल्ल r. 1st cl. (पल्लति) To go. भ्वा० पर० सक० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=436-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पल्ल|पल्लः
पल्ल m. (-ल्लः)<BR>	 1. A large basket or matted shed used for keeping corn,<BR>&c.<BR>	 2. A large granary.<BR>	 f. (-ल्ली)<BR>	 1. A small village.<BR>	 2. A city, or<BR>rather an affix to words forming the name of a town; it is espe-<BR>cially used in the Dekhin, as in Trichinopoly or Trisira-palli,<BR>&c.<BR>	 3. A small house-lizard.<BR>	 4. A creeping plant.<BR> E. पल्ल् to go, aff.<BR>अच्; also with इन् aff. पल्लि. or पदं लाति ला-क, पादस्थाने पत् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=436-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पल्लव|पल्लवं|पल्लवः
पल्लव mn. (-वः-वं)<BR>	 1. A sprout, a shoot, the extremity of a branch<BR>bearing new leaves.<BR>	 2. A branch.<BR>	 3. Spreading, expansion.<BR>	 4. A<BR>wood.<BR>	 5. The red dye of lac or Alakta.<BR>	 6. Love, the sentiment<BR>or passion.<BR>	 7. A catamite.<BR>	 8. A bracelet.<BR>	 9. Unsteadiness, moral<BR>or physical.<BR> E. पद् the foot, लू to cut or break, अप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=436-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पल्लवक|पल्लवकः
पल्लवक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. The paramour of a harlot, a libertine.<BR>	 2. A kind<BR>of fish, (Cyprinus denticulatus.)<BR>	 3. A catamite.<BR>	 4. The Aśoka<BR>tree.<BR> E. पल्लव love, and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=436-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पल्लवद्रु|पल्लवद्रुः
पल्लवद्रु m. (-द्रुः) The Aśoka tree.<BR> E. पल्लव, and द्रु a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=436-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पल्लवाद|पल्लवादः
पल्लवाद m. (-दः) A deer.<BR> E. पल्लव a shoot, अद् to eat, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=436-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पल्लवाधार|पल्लवाधारः
पल्लवाधार m. (-रः) A branch.<BR> E. पल्लव a sprout, and आधार receptacle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=436-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पल्लवास्त्र|पल्लवास्त्रः
पल्लवास्त्र m. (स्त्रः) KĀMADEVA<BR> E. पल्लव a sprout or blossom, and अस्त्र a<BR>weapon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=436-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पल्लविक|पल्लविकः
पल्लविक mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>	 1. Amorous, desirous.<BR>	 2. A libertine 3. A<BR>catamite.<BR> E. पल्लव passion, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=436-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पल्लवित|पल्लवितं|पल्लवितः
पल्लवित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Having new sprouts.<BR>	 2. Spread, extended.<BR>	 3.<BR>Dyed red with Lac.<BR>	 m. (-तः) The red dye of the lac insect.<BR> E. पल्लव<BR>a sprout, &c. इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=436-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पल्लविन्
पल्लविन् m. (-वी) A tree.<BR> E. पल्लव a sprout, aff. इनि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=436-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पल्लि|पल्लिः
पल्लि(ल्ली) f. (-ल्लिः)<BR>	 1. A small village.<BR>	 2. Any village.<BR>	 3. A house.<BR>	 4. A<BR>number of houses.<BR>	 5. Any place or station.<BR>	 6. A house-lizard: see<BR>पल्ल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=436-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पल्लिका
पल्लिका f. (का)<BR>	 1. A House-lizard.<BR>	 2. A small village.<BR> E. पल्ली, and कन्<BR>added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=436-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पल्वल|पल्वलं
पल्वल mn. (-लः-लं) A small pond.<BR> E. पल् to go, Unādi aff. वल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=436-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पल्वलावास|पल्वलावासः
पल्वलावास m. (-सः) A tortoise.<BR> E. पल्वल a pond, and आवास abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=436-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पव|पवं|पवः
पव m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. Winnowing corn.<BR>	 2. A marsh.<BR>	 3. Air, wind.<BR>	 4. Puri-<BR>fication, purity.<BR>	 n. (-वं) Cow-dung.<BR> E. पू to purify, aff. अप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=436-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पवत्
पवत् mfn. (-वन्-वन्ती-वत्) Pure, purifying.<BR> E. पू to be pure, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=436-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पवन|पवनं|पवनः
पवन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Pure, clean.<BR>	 m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. Air, wind, physical or<BR>personified, as a deity.<BR>	 2. Winnowing grain.<BR>	 3. The domestic fire.<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. A potter's kiln.<BR>	 2. Water.<BR>	 3. Purifying, purification.<BR>E. पू to be or make pure, aff. ल्युट् or युच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=436-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पवनव्याधि|पवनव्याधिः
पवनव्याधि m. (-धिः)<BR>	 1. Uddhava, one of KṚṢṆA'S friends and advisers.<BR>2. Wind, as affected morbidly, or rheumatism, &c.<BR> E. पवन, and<BR>व्याधि sickness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=436-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पवनात्मज|पवनात्मजः
पवनात्मज m. (-जः)<BR>	 1. Hanumān, the monkey hero.<BR>	 2. Fire.<BR>	 3. A name<BR>of Bhima.<BR> E. पवन wind (the deity,) and आत्मज son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=436-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पवनाल|पवनालः
पवनाल m. (-लः) A kind of grain, (Andropogon saccharatus.) (देधान) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=436-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पवनाश|पवनाशः
पवनाश m. (-शः) A snake.<BR> E. पवन wind, and अश who eats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=436-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पवनाशन|पवनाशनः
पवनाशन m. (-नः) A snake.<BR> E. पवन wind, and अशन food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=436-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पवनाशनाश|पवनाशनाशः
पवनाशनाश m. (-शः)<BR>	 1. Garuda, the bird and vehicle of VIṢṆU.<BR>	 2. A<BR>peacock.<BR> E. पवनाशन a snake, and अश who eats; feeding on the<BR>serpent race.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=436-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पवनाहत
पवनाहत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Shaken by the wind.<BR>	 2. Rheumatic.<BR> E. पवन<BR>and आहत struck.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=436-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पवनेष्ट|पवनेष्टः
पवनेष्ट m. (-ष्टः) A large kind of Nimba tree. “महानिम्” ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=436-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पवनोम्बुज|पवनोम्बुजं
पवनोम्बुज m. (-जः) The Porush tree: see परुष.<BR> E. पवन air, अम्बु water,<BR>and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=436-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पवमान|पवमानः
पवमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Purifying.<BR>	 m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. Air, wind.<BR>	 2. Household<BR>fire or the sacred fire called Gārhapatya.<BR> E. पूञ् to purify,<BR>शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=436-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पवमानात्मज|पवमानात्मजः
पवमानात्मज m. (-जः) The householder's perpetual fire.<BR> E. पवमान, and आत्मज son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=436-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पवाका
पवाका f. (-का) A whirlwind.<BR> E. पू to purify, आक Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=436-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पवि|पविः
पवि m. (-विः) The thunderbolt of INDRA.<BR> E. पू to purify, Unādi aff. इ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=436-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पवित|पवितः
पवित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Purified, cleansed.<BR>	 n. (-तं) Black-pepper.<BR> E. पू to<BR>purify, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=436-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पवितृ
पवितृ mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ) Purifying, cleansing.<BR> E. पू to purify, तृन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=436-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पवित्र|पवित्रं|पवित्रः
पवित्र mfn. (-त्रः-त्रा-त्रं)<BR>	 1. Pure, clean, purified physically or morally.<BR>	 2.<BR>Who or what cleans, or purifies, &c.<BR>	 n. (-त्रं)<BR>	 1. Sacrifical grass,<BR>(Poa cynosuroides.)<BR>	 2. Copper.<BR>	 3. Water.<BR>	 4. Rain.<BR>	 5. Rubbing,<BR>cleansing.<BR>	 6. The vessel in which an Argha or libation or<BR>oblation is presented.<BR>	 7. The Brāhminical cord.<BR>	 8. Ghee.<BR>	 9.<BR>Honey.<BR>	 10. A couple of Kusa leaves a span long, used at<BR>sacrifices to present offerings upon, or to sprinkle Ghee, &c.<BR>	 11.<BR>Kusa grass used to clean or purify Ghee used in a sacrifice.<BR>	 12.<BR>A ring of Kusa grass worn on the fourth finger on some occa-<BR>sions.<BR>	 13. A text or Mantra of the Vedas.<BR>	 14. Any divinity, as<BR>Agni, &c.<BR>	 f. (-त्रा)<BR>	 1. Holy basil, (Ocymum sanctum.)<BR>	 2. The<BR>name of a river, a little to the north-west of Haridwār; the<BR>Pabar.<BR>	 3. The twelfth of the light fortnight of Srāvana, a<BR>festival in honour of VIṢṆU.<BR> E. पू to purify, aff. करणे इत्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=436-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पवित्रक|पवित्रकं|पवित्रकः
पवित्रक n. (-कं) Packthread, or a rope or net made of it.<BR> E. पवित्र<BR>pure, क aff. अश्वत्थवृक्षे, उदुम्बरवृक्षे, कुशे, दमनकवृक्षे, शणसूत्र निर्मिते<BR>जाले ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=436-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पवित्रारोपण|पवित्रारोपणं
पवित्रारोपण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Investiture with the Brāhminical cord.<BR>	 2. In-<BR>vesting the image of KṚṢṆA with it, on the twelfth of the light<BR>fortnight of Srāvana.<BR> E. पवित्र, and आरोपण placing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=437-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पवित्रारोहण|पवित्रारोहणं
पवित्रारोहण n. (-णं) The putting of the Brāhminical cord on images of<BR>DURGĀ on the eighth of the light half of Srāvana or Āshārh. E.<BR>पवित्र, and आरोहण mounting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=437-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पवित्रित|पवित्रितः
पवित्रित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Clean, pure, (literally or metaphorically.) E.<BR>पवित्र purifying, इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=437-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पवित्रीकरण
पवित्रीकरण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Purification, cleansing.<BR>	 2. The instrument or<BR>means of purifying.<BR> E. पवित्र, and करण making, च्वि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=437-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पवित्रीकृत
पवित्रीकृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Purified, cleansed.<BR> E. पवित्र, and कृत made, च्वि<BR>augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=437-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पवीनस
पवीनस m. (-सः) Name of an Asura said to be the destroyer of the<BR>child while in the womb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=437-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पवीर|पवीरं
पवीर n. (-रं)<BR>	 1. An weapon.<BR>	 2. The thunder.<BR>	 3. A plough-share. E.<BR>पवि, the thunderbolt, and स्वार्थे ईर aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=437-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पश
पश (ष-स) r. 1st cl. (पशति-ते) r. 10th cl. (पाशयति-ते पशयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To<BR>bind, to fetter.<BR>	 2. To knot or tie.<BR>	 3. To go, to move.<BR>	 4. To<BR>hinder or obstruct.<BR>	 5. To touch. बाधे भ्वा, पक्षे अद० बन्धे-चु-उभ-सक-सेट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=437-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पशव्य|पशव्यं
पशव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>	 1. Fit or advantageous for cattle, (meadow,<BR>pasturage; &c.)<BR>	 2. Possessed of or relating to a cattle.<BR>	 3.<BR>Brutish.<BR> E. पशु, and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=437-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पशु|पशुः
पशु m. (-शुः)<BR>	 1. An animal in general, a beast.<BR>	 2. A goat.<BR>	 3. A subor-<BR>dinate deity and one of SĪVA'S followers.<BR>	 4. Any living be-<BR>ing.<BR>	 5. A sacrifice, an oblation.<BR>	 6. The divine soul of the universe.<BR>7. The glomerous fig tree. ind. See, behold.<BR> E. दृश् to see, पश<BR>substituted, and कु Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=437-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पशुका
पशुका f. (-का) Any small animal.<BR> E. पशु, and कन् dimin. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=437-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पशुक्रिया
पशुक्रिया f. (-या)<BR>	 1. Copulation, coition.<BR>	 2. The act of animal sacrifice.<BR>E. पशु an animal, and क्रिया action.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=437-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पशुगायत्री
पशुगायत्री f. (-त्री) A parody of the holy verse of the Vedas, whispered<BR>into the ear of an animal about to be sacrificed.<BR> E. पशु, and<BR>गायत्री the Gāyatrī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=437-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पशुघात|पशुघातः
पशुघात n. (-तं) Slaughter of animals for sacrifice, &c.<BR> E. पशु, and घात killing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=437-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पशुता
पशुता f. (-ता) The condition or nature of an animal, bestiality, bru-<BR>tality.<BR> E. तल् added to पशु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=437-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पशुत्व
पशुत्व n. (-त्वं)<BR>	 1. Sacrifice of an animal.<BR>	 2. Nature of an animal,<BR> E. पशु,<BR>and त्व aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=437-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पशुधर्म्म|पशुधर्म|पशुधर्मः
पशुधर्म्म m. (-र्म्मः)<BR>	 1. Action, property, or treatment of animals.<BR>	 2. Pro-<BR>miscuous cohabitation.<BR>	 3. The marrying of widows.<BR> E. पशु, and<BR>धर्म्म office.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=437-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पशुपति|पशुपतिः
पशुपति m. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. A herdsman.<BR>	 2. A name of ŚIVA.<BR> E. पशु living<BR>creature, and पति the master, the creator, or preserver; or<BR>पशु SĪVA'S attendant, and पति master; or according to one<BR>legend, पशु an animal, which every deity acknowledged himself<BR>to be before his lord and master ŚIVA, when they solicited<BR>him to destroy the Asura TRIPURĀ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=437-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पशुपल्वल|पशुपल्वलं
पशुपल्वल n. (-लं) A fragrant grass, (Cyperus rotundus.) कैवर्त्तीमुस्तके ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=437-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पशुपाल|पशुपालः
पशुपाल m. (-लः) A herdsman.<BR> E. पशु, and पाल who cherishes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=437-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पशुपालन
पशुपालन n. (-नं) Tending or rearing cattle.<BR> E. पशु, and पालन protecting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=437-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पशुप्रेरण|पशुप्रेरणं
पशुप्रेरण n. (-णं) Driving cattle.<BR> E. पशु a beast, प्रेरण sending.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=437-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पशुयाग|पशुयागः
पशुयाग m. (-गः) Sacrifice of animals.<BR> E. पशु, and याग sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=437-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पशुरक्षण
पशुरक्षण n. (-णं) Tending cattle.<BR> E. पशु, and रक्षण preserving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=437-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पशुरक्षिन्
पशुरक्षिन् m. (-क्षी) A herdsman, a shepherd.<BR> E. पशु, and रक्षिन् who<BR>guards.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=437-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पशुरज्जु|पशुरज्जुः
पशुरज्जु m. (-ज्जुः) A string or tie for fastening cattle.<BR> E. पशु an animal,<BR>and रज्जु a rope.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=437-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पशुराज|पशुराजः
पशुराज m. (-जः) A lion.<BR> E. पशु a beast, and राज sovereign.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=437-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पशुरोमन्
पशुरोमन् n. (-म) The hair of an animal.<BR> E. पशु, and रोमन् hair of the<BR>body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=437-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पशुसम्मव
पशुसम्मव mfn. (-वः-वा-वं) Produced by an animal, (flesh, honey, butter,<BR>&c.)<BR> E. पशु, and सम्मव product.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=437-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पशुहरीतकी
पशुहरीतकी f. (-की) The hog plum.<BR> E. पशु an animal, हरीतकी myro-<BR>balan. आम्रातकफले ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=437-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पशुहव्य
पशुहव्य n. (-व्यं) Sacrifice of animals.<BR> E. पशु, and हव्य oblation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=437-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पश्चात्
पश्चात् ind. After, afterwards, behind, westward.<BR> E. पश्च, considered as a<BR>substitute for अपर, and आति aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=437-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पश्चात्ताप|पश्चात्तापः
पश्चात्ताप m. (-पः) Repentance.<BR> E. पश्चात् afterwards, ताप sorrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=437-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पश्चार्द्ध
पश्चार्द्ध mfn. (-र्द्धः-र्द्धा-र्द्धं) The remaining half or part of any thing. E.<BR>पश्च for अपर, and अर्द्ध a part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=437-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पश्चिम|पश्चिमं
पश्चिम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>	 1. West, western.<BR>	 2. Behind, after.<BR>	 mf. (-मः-मा)<BR>The region of VARUṆA, the west.<BR> E. पश्चात् behind, and डिमच्<BR>aff.; Hindus in their prayers, usually facing the east; and conse-<BR>quently having the west behind them.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=437-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पश्य
पश्य ind. An exclamation of wonder or admiration, (lo, behold,<BR>see.)<BR> E. दृश् to see, deriv. irr. also पश्यतु and पशु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=437-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पश्य
पश्य mfn. (श्यः-श्या-श्यं) Who or what sees.<BR> E. पश्य for दृश् to see, श aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=437-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पश्यत्
पश्यत् mfn. (-श्यन्-श्यन्ती-श्यत्)<BR>	 1. Looking, seeing.<BR>	 2. Remarking, consi-<BR>dering.<BR>	 f. (-न्ती)<BR>	 1. A harlot, a courtezan.<BR>	 2. A particular sound.<BR>E. दृश् to see, शतृ aff. of the present participle, and root irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=437-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पश्यतस्
पश्यतस् ind. Visibly, in sight.<BR> E. पश्य, and तसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=437-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पश्यतोहर|पश्यतोहरः
पश्यतोहर m. (-रः) A thief, a pilferer, but one who steals in presence<BR>of the parties, and proverbially applied to the goldsmith, &c. E.<BR>पश्यतस् in presence of, and हर who takes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=437-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पश्ववदान
पश्ववदान n. (-नं) Sacrifice of offering of animals.<BR> E. पशु, and अवदान<BR>oblation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=437-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पश्याचार
पश्याचार m. (-रः) Worship of DEVI.<BR> E. पशु, and आचार instituted<BR>observance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=437-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पष
पष r. 10th. cl. (पाषयति पषयति)<BR>	 1. To bind, to tie.<BR>	 2. To move.<BR>	 3. To<BR>oppose, to hinder.<BR>	 4. To touch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=437-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पस
पस r. 1st. and 10. cls. (पसति-ते पासयति पसयति)<BR>	 1. To bind, to fetter,<BR>to tie, to string.<BR>	 2. To touch.<BR>	 3. To oppose, to obstruct, to hinder.<BR>4. To go, to move.<BR>	 5. To injure or kill. (इ) पसि r. 1st and 10th.<BR>cls. (पंसति पंसयति-ते) To annul, to annihilate or destroy. चु-उभ-सक-<BR>सेट-इदित् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=437-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पस्त्य|पस्त्यं
पस्त्य n. (स्त्यं) A house,<BR> E. पस्-भावे क्तिन्, तत्र साधु यत् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=437-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पस्पश|पस्पशः
पस्पश m. (-शः) Name of the 1st Āhnika of the first chapter of<BR>Patanjalīs Mahābhāsya; (hence) An introductory chapter<BR>generally.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=437-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पह्नव|पह्नवः
पह्नव m. (-वः) The name of one of the degraded Kṣatriya races<BR>sentenced by SAGARA to wear beards, perhaps a Parthian.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=437-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पह्निका
पह्निका f. (-का) A plant, (Pistia stratiotes.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=437-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पह्लिक
पह्लिक m. plu. (-कः) Name of a people, (perhaps the Persians.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=437-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पांक्त
पांक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं) Linear, in or by line, or row.<BR> E. पंक्ति a line,<BR>aff. अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=437-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पांश
पांश(स)न mfn. (-नः-ना-नी-नं)<BR>	 1. Vitiating, spoiling.<BR>	 2. Wicked.<BR>	 f. (ना<BR>or नी; generally used at the end of a compound.)<BR>	 1. Disgraceful,<BR>dishonouring, as in कुलपांशन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=437-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पांश
पांश(स)व mf. (-वः-वी)<BR>	 1. Rock or fossile salt.<BR>	 2. Consisting of dust. E.<BR>पांशु dust, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=437-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पांशु|पांशुः
पांशु(सु) m. (-शुः or सुः)<BR>	 1. Dust.<BR>	 2. Manure.<BR>	 3. Landed property.<BR>	 4. A<BR>kind of camphor.<BR> E. पशि to bind, Unādi aff. कु; also पांसु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=437-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पांशुका
पांशुका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. A menstruous woman.<BR>	 2. A fragrant plant, (Panda-<BR>nus odoratissimus.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=437-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पांशुकासीस|पांशुकासीसं
पांशुकासीस n. (-सं) Sulphate of iron.<BR> E. पाशु dust, and कासीस the<BR>same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=437-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पांशुकुली
पांशुकुली f. (-ली) A principal road,<BR> E. पांशु dust, कुल a heap.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=437-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पांशुकूल|पांशुकूलं
पांशुकूल n. (-लं)<BR>	 1. A dust-heap.<BR>	 2. A black lease, a title deed,<BR>one not made out in any person's name.<BR> E. पांशु landed property,<BR>कूल a mound, (as it were.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=437-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पांशु|पांशुः
पांशु(सु)चत्वर m. (-रः) Hail.<BR> E. पांशु dust, चत्वर a level space.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=438-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पांशुचन्दन|पांशुचंदन|पांशुचन्दनः
पांशुचन्दन m. (-नः) A name of ŚIVA.<BR> E. पांशु dust, चन्दन Sandal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=438-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पांशुचामर|पांशुचामरः
पांशुचामर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A tent.<BR>	 2. A bank overgrown with Durbā grass.<BR>3. A Praise.<BR>	 4. A heap of dust.<BR>	 5. A small cucumber.<BR> E. पांशु<BR>dust, चामर a chowri.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=438-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पांशु|पांशुः
पांशु(सु)ज n. (-जं) Salt extracted from soil, rock or fossile salt.<BR> E. पांशु dust, ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=438-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पांशुपत्र|पांशुपत्रं
पांशुपत्र n. (-त्रं) A potherb, (Chenopodium.)<BR> E. पांशु dust, and पत्र leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=438-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पांशुमर्द्दन|पांशुमर्दन|पांशुमर्द्दनः
पांशुमर्द्दन m. (-नः) A channel or basin for water, near or about the<BR>root of a tree.<BR> E. पांशु dust, and मर्द्दन destroying. “केदारक्षेत्रेच” ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=438-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पांशुव
पांशुव m. (-वः) A cripple: see पीठसर्पिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=438-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पांशुर|पांशुरः
पांशुर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A gadfly.<BR>	 2. A cripple carried or moving about in a<BR>chair.<BR> E. पांशु dust, and रा to get, क or ड aff. (डांश)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=438-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पांशुल|पांशुलः
पांशुल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>	 1. Dusty, covered or spotted with dust.<BR>	 2.<BR>Sullied, defiled.<BR>	 3. Disgracing.<BR>	 m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. A name of ŚIVA.<BR>2. One of SĪVA'S weapons; a sort of pole armed at the upper<BR>end with transverse pieces, representing the breastbone and<BR>ribs adjoining, and surmounted by a skull; also खट्वाङ्ग.<BR>	 3. A<BR>paramour, a gallant.<BR>	 4. A kind of tree, (Cæsalpinia bonducella.)<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>	 1. An unchaste woman.<BR>	 2. A woman during mens-<BR>truation.<BR>	 3. The earth.<BR> E. पांशु dust, लच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=438-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पांशुवर्ष
पांशुवर्ष m. (-र्षः) A shower or fall of dust.<BR> E. पांशु, and वर्ष rain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=438-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पांसक
पांसक mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>	 1. Contemptible, vile.<BR>	 2. Vitiating, spoiling.<BR>E. पसि to destroy, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=438-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पांसन|पांसनः
पांसन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>	 1. Contemptible, wicked, bad, infamous.<BR>	 2.<BR>Vitiating, spoiling, destructive.<BR> E. पसि to destroy, &c. aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=438-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पांसु|पांसुः
पांसु m. (-सुः)<BR>	 1. Dust.<BR>	 2. Manure.<BR>	 3. A kind of camphor.<BR> E. पसि to<BR>bind, &c., aff. कु, also पांशु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=438-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पा
पा r. 1st. cl. (पिवति) To drink. r. 2nd. cl. (पाति) To cherish, to<BR>nourish, to protect or preserve. पाने, भ्वा-पर-सक-अनिट् । रक्षणे,<BR>अदा-पर-सक-सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=438-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पा
पा mfn. (पाः-पाः-पं)<BR>	 1. Who drinks.<BR>	 2. Who protects or cherishes.<BR>	 3.<BR>To feast on, (with the eyes or ears.)<BR>	 4. To absorb, to swallow up,<BR>to destroy.<BR> E. पा to drink, &c. क्विप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=438-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाक|पाकः
पाक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. Maturity, natural or artificial, as the state of being<BR>cooked or ripened.<BR>	 2. Cooking, baking, boiling, dressing food.<BR>	 3.<BR>A vessel in which any thing is dressed, a saucepan, a boiler,<BR>&c.<BR>	 4. Digestion, assimilation of food.<BR>	 5. Suppuration, ripeness<BR>of a boil.<BR>	 6. Greyness of the hair.<BR>	 7. General panic, or the sub-<BR>version of a country.<BR>	 8. Fear.<BR>	 9. An owl.<BR>	 10. The name of a<BR>demon.<BR>	 11. Completion.<BR>	 12. The consequence of an act done.<BR>13. Domestic fire.<BR>	 14. Grain, corn.<BR>	 15. Fruit, fruition.<BR>	 mf.<BR>(-कः-का) The young of animals.<BR> E. पच् to be or become ripe,<BR>aff. भावे-घञ्; or पा to nourish, Unādi aff. कन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=438-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाककृष्ण|पाककृष्णः
पाककृष्ण m. (-ष्णः) The Caronda tree, (Carissa carondas.)<BR> E. पाक ripen-<BR>ing, कृष्ण black; bearing a black fruit when ripe; also other<BR>similar compounds, पाककृष्णफल, कृष्णपाक, &c. “पानाम्ला” ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=438-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाकज|पाकजं
पाकज mfn. (-जः-जा-जं) Produced by cooking, maturing, &c.<BR>	 n. (-जं)<BR>1. Black-salt.<BR>	 2. Flatulence.<BR> E. पाक, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=438-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाकपात्र
पाकपात्र n. (-त्रं) A cooking utensil, a boiler, &c.<BR> E. पाक, and पात्र a vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=438-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाकपुटी
पाकपुटी f. (-टी) A potter's kiln.<BR> E. पाक backing, पुट् to heap, affs. क<BR>and ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=438-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाकफल|पाकफलः
पाकफल m. (-लः) The Caronda.<BR> E. पाक ripe, फल fruit, (black under-<BR>stood;) see पाककृष्णफल; also पाकफलकृष्ण, फलपाक, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=438-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाकभाण्ड|पाकभाण्डं
पाकभाण्ड n. (-ण्डं) A culinary utensil.<BR> E. पाक, and भाण्ड a vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=438-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाकमत्स्य|पाकमत्स्यः
पाकमत्स्य m. (-त्स्यः) Fish sauce.<BR> E. पाक cooking, मत्स्य fish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=438-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाकयज्ञ|पाकयज्ञः
पाकयज्ञ m. (-ज्ञः) An oblation offered on building a house, liberating<BR>a bull, &c. or a religious rite of four kinds, oblation to the<BR>VISWADEVAS, offerings to the spirits, the permanent obsequial<BR>rites, and hospitality.<BR> E. पाक, and यज्ञ sacrifice; the distribu-<BR>tion of food being a part of each of these ceremonies.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=438-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाकयज्ञिक|पाकयज्ञिकः
पाकयज्ञिक m. (-कः) The performer of the ceremony called Pāk-yajna,<BR>E. पाकयज्ञ, aff. ठञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=438-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाकरञ्जन|पाकरञ्जनं
पाकरञ्जन n. (-नं) The leaf of the Laurus cassia.<BR> E. पाक cooking, रञ्ज् to colour, aff. णिच्-ल्यु “तेजपत्रे” ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=438-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाकल|पाकलं|पाकलः
पाकल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>	 1. Producing maturity.<BR>	 2. Suppurative, pro-<BR>ducing suppuration in a boil.<BR>	 n. (-लं) A sort of Costus, (C. spe-<BR>ciosus.)<BR>	 m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. Fine.<BR>	 2. Wind.<BR>	 3. Fever in an elephant.<BR>f. (-ली) A sort of cucumber, (C. utilatissimus.)<BR> E. पाक ripeness,<BR>ला to get, aff. ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=438-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाकलि|पाकलिः
पाकलि m. (-लिः) A sort of plant, (Bauhinia candida.) रोहिणीवृक्षे ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=438-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाकशाला
पाकशाला f. (-ला) A kitchen.<BR> E. पाक cooking, शाला a hall.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=438-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाकशासन|पाकशासनः
पाकशासन m. (-नः) INDRA.<BR> E. पाक a demon, शासन ruling, overcoming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=438-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाकशासनि|पाकशासनिः
पाकशासनि m. (-निः)<BR>	 1. “Jayanta” the son of INDRA.<BR>	 2. A name of<BR>Vāli.<BR>	 3. A name of Arjuna.<BR> E. पाकशासन INDRA, इञ् aff. of<BR>descent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=438-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाकशुक्ला
पाकशुक्ला f. (-क्ला) Chalk.<BR> E. पाक cooking, burning, शुक्ल white.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=438-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाकस्थान|पाकस्थानं
पाकस्थान n. (-नं) A kitchen.<BR> E. पाक cooking, स्थान a place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=438-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाकिम|पाकिमं
पाकिम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं) Cooked, dressed, ripened, naturally or<BR>artificially.<BR> E. पाक cooking, इमनिच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=438-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाकुक|पाकुकः
पाकुक m. (-कः) A cook.<BR> E. पच् to cook, Unādi aff. उकञ्, चस्य कश्च ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=438-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाक्य|पाक्यं|पाक्यः
पाक्य mfn. (-क्यः-क्या-क्यं) What may or is to be cooked, matured, &c.<BR>n. (क्यं) Bit-Labana, a medicinal salt, impregnated with iron.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-क्यः) Nitre, salt-petre.<BR> E. पच् to cook, aff. कर्मणि ण्यत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=438-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाक्ष
पाक्ष mfn. (-क्षः-क्षी-क्षं)<BR>	 1. Belonging to a half month.<BR>	 2. Relating to a<BR>side or party, &c.<BR> E. पक्ष, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=438-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाक्षायण|पाक्षायणः
पाक्षायण mfn. (-णः-णी-णं) Belonging to or occurring in a Pakhsa or<BR>fortnight, &c.<BR> E. पक्ष half month, &c. and फक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=438-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाक्षिक|पाक्षिकः
पाक्षिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>	 1. Belonging to a bird, to a fortnight, to an<BR>argument, &c.<BR>	 2. Favouring a party or faction.<BR>	 3. Optional,<BR>allowed but not prescribed.<BR>	 m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A fowler, a bird-catcher.<BR>	 2.<BR>An alternative.<BR> E. पक्ष a fortnight, or पक्षिन् a bird, aff. ठञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=438-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाखण्ड|पाखंड|पाखंडः|पाखण्डः
पाखण्ड m. (-ण्डः) A heretic, a heterodox Hindu, adopting the<BR>exterior marks of the classes, but not respecting the ordinances<BR>of the Vedas.<BR> E. पा for पाल what nourishes, (mankind, as virtue<BR>may be said to do,) and खडि to subvert or destroy, aff. अण्; also<BR>पाषण्ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=438-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पांक्त्य|पाङ्क्त्य
पांक्त्य m. (-क्त्यः) A Brāhman who is or may be worthy to eat in a res-<BR>pectable society at sacrifices, &c.<BR> E. पंक्ति an assembly, and अञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=438-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाचक|पाचकं|पाचकः
पाचक mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>	 1. What produces maturity.<BR>	 2. What cooks<BR>or dresses.<BR>	 3. Digestive, tonic, what effects digestion.<BR>	 n. (-कं) The<BR>bile which assists in digestion.<BR>	 m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. Fire.<BR>	 2. A cook.<BR> E. पच्<BR>to ripen or concoct, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=438-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाचकस्त्री
पाचकस्त्री f. (-स्त्री) A she-cook.<BR> E. पाचक cooking, स्त्री a woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=438-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाचन|पाचनं|पाचनः
पाचन mfn. (-नः-नी-नं)<BR>	 1. What cooks or ripens, &c.<BR>	 2. Disgestive.<BR>Suppurative.<BR>	 n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. A medicinal preparation, an infu-<BR>sion, a decoction, &c. of various drugs, chiefly carminatives or<BR>gentle stimuli given to bring the vitiated humours in fever,<BR>&c. to maturity, a sort of diet drink.<BR>	 2. Penance, expiation.<BR>3. The act of cooking, or ripening.<BR>	 m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. Fire.<BR>	 2. Acidity,<BR>sourness.<BR>	 f. (-नी)<BR>	 1. A sort of myrobalan, (Terminalia, chebula.)<BR>2. Cooking, ripening,<BR> E. पच् to dress, in the causal form, aff.<BR>ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=438-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाचनक|पाचनकः
पाचनक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. Borax.<BR>	 n. (-कं) A sort of diet drink: see the last.<BR>E. पच् to mature, (metals,) in the causal form, ल्युट् aff., and कन्<BR>added. “सोहागा” ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=438-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाचल|पाचलं|पाचलः
पाचल n. (-लं) Cooking, maturing.<BR>	 m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. Fire.<BR>	 2. Wind.<BR>	 3. A<BR>thing dressed or matured without the aid of fire.<BR>	 4. What-<BR>ever ripens, cooks, causes digestion, &c.<BR> E. पच् in the causal<BR>form, णिच्वा-कलन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=438-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाचा
पाचा f. (-चा) Cooking, maturing.<BR> E. पच् to cook, causal v. अङ् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=438-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाचि|पाचिः
पाचि f. (-चिः) Cooking, maturing.<BR> E. पच् to cook, इञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=438-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाचिका
पाचिका f. (-का) Cooking, maturing.<BR> E. पच् to cook, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=439-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाजस्
पाजस् n. (-जः) Strength, power.<BR> E. पा to nourish, असुन् Unādi aff.,<BR>and जुट् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=439-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाञ्चकपाल|पांचकपाल|पाञ्चकपालः
पाञ्चकपाल mfn. (-लः-ली-लं) Relating to or part of that oblation which<BR>is offered in five cups.<BR> E. पञ्चकपाल, q. v. अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=439-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाञ्चजन्य|पांचजन्य|पांचजन्यः|पाञ्चजन्यः
पाञ्चजन्य m. (-न्यः)<BR>	 1. KṚṢṆA'S conch.<BR>	 2. A name of fire.<BR>	 3. Any<BR>shell.<BR>	 4. A sort of fish, commonly Garāi.<BR> E. पञ्चजन a demon,<BR>from whose bones the shell was made, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=439-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाञ्चजन्यधर|पांचजन्यधर|पाञ्चजन्यधरः
पाञ्चजन्यधर m. (-रः) A name of KṚṢṆA.<BR> E. पञ्चजन्य the conch, and<BR>धर who has.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=439-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाञ्चयाज्ञिक
पाञ्चयाज्ञिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Relating or belonging to, or included in<BR>the five great ceremonies.<BR>	 n. (-कं) Either of the five great sacra-<BR>ments.<BR> E. पञ्चयज्ञ, and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=439-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाञ्चभौतिक|पांचभौतिक
पाञ्चभौतिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Consisting or made of the five elements.<BR>E. पञ्चभूत, and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=439-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाञ्चलिका
पाञ्चलिका f. (-का) A doll, a puppet: see पाञ्चालिका ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=439-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाञ्चशब्दिक|पांचशब्दिक|पांचशब्दिकं|पाञ्चशब्दिकं
पाञ्चशब्दिक n. (-कं) Musical instruments in general, or of five sorts. E.<BR>पञ्च, शव्द sound, and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=439-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाञ्चार्थिक|पांचार्थिकः|पाञ्चार्थिकः
पाञ्चार्थिक m. (-कः) A follower or votary of ŚIVA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=439-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाञ्चाल|पांचाल|पाञ्चालं|पाञ्चालः
पाञ्चाल mfn. (-लः-ली-लं) Belonging to, dwelling in, ruling over, &c.<BR>the country of Panchāla.<BR>	 m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. The sovereign of Panchāla.<BR>plu. The people of that country.<BR>	 2. The company or association of<BR>five trades, the carpenter, weaver, barber, washerman, and<BR>shoemaker.<BR> E. पञ्चाल the country so called, and स्वार्थे अण् aff. &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=439-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाञ्चालिका|पांचालिका
पाञ्चालिका f. (-का) A doll, a puppet: see पाञ्चाली ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=439-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाञ्चाली|पांचाली
पाञ्चाली f. (-ली)<BR>	 1. A name of DRAUPADĪ, the wife of the five Pāṇḍu<BR>princes.<BR>	 2. A woman of the Panchālas.<BR>	 3. A puppet, a doll.<BR>4. Melodious combination of five or six words, (In rhetoric).<BR>E. पाञ्चाल the country so called, अण्, aff. of descent or reference,<BR>and fem. aff. ङीप्; coming from that region; also with कन् added<BR>पाञ्चालिका, and by making the second vowel short पाञ्चलिका ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=439-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाट्
पाट् ind. A vocative particle or interjection used in calling.<BR> E. पट्<BR>to go, in the causal form, aff. णिच् क्विप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=439-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाट|पाटः
पाट m. (-टः) Breadth, expanse, extension.<BR>	 f. (-टा) Regular or successive<BR>order, series, succession.<BR> E. पट् to spread, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=439-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाटक|पाटकः
पाटक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. The half of a village.<BR>	 2. A shore, a bank, a flight<BR>of steps leading to water.<BR>	 3. Casting dice.<BR>	 4. A musical instru-<BR>ment.<BR>	 5. A large span.<BR>	 6. Expense or loss of capital or stock.<BR>7. A splitter, a divider.<BR> E. पट् to go, ल्युल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=439-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाटच्चर|पाटच्चरः
पाटच्चर m. (-रः) A thief.<BR> E. पटच्चर the same, and अण् pleonastic aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=439-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाटन|पाटनं
पाटन n. (-नं) Cutting, breaking.<BR> E. पट् to go, causal form, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=439-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाटल|पाटलं|पाटलः
पाटल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Of a pink or pale-red colour.<BR>	 m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. Pale-red,<BR>rose colour.<BR>	 2. Rice ripening in the rains.<BR>	 f. (-ला)<BR>	 1. The Trumpet-<BR>flower, (Bignonia suave-olens.)<BR>	 2. Red Lodh.<BR>	 3. A name of<BR>DURGĀ.<BR>	 4. Pale-red.<BR>	 nf. (-लं-ला)<BR>	 1. The flower of the Bignonia<BR>snave-olens.<BR>	 2. Rice.<BR>	 3. Saffron.<BR> E. पाट extension, and ला to get,<BR>aff. ड; also पाटलि; or पट-णिच्-कलच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=439-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाटलि|पाटलिः
पाटलि mf. (-लिः) Trumpet-flower.<BR>	 m. (-लिः) Rice ripening in the rains.<BR>E. पाटल pale-red, aff. इन्. पट-णिच्-अलि “पारुल पुष्पे”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=439-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाटलित
पाटलित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Made red, tinted red, reddened.<BR> E. पाटल, and<BR>इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=439-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाटलिपुत्र
पाटलिपुत्र n. (-त्रं) The name of an ancient city, supposed to be the an-<BR>cient Palibothra, and the modern Pātnā; It was the capital of<BR>Magadha, situated near the confluence of the Sona and the<BR>ganges, and is also known by the name of Pushpapura in Sans-<BR>krit literature.<BR> E. पाटलि the trumpet flower, पू to be pure, त्रन्<BR>aff.; also with कन् added, पाटलिपुत्रक; it is also said to be<BR>named after its founder and sovereign, पाटलिपुत्र being a proper<BR>name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=439-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाटलोपल|पाटलोपलः
पाटलोपल n. (-लं) A ruby.<BR> E. पाटल, and उपल, a stone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=439-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाटव|पाटवं
पाटव mfn. (-वः-वी-वं) Clever, sharp, dexterous.<BR>	 n. (-वं)<BR>	 1. Cleverness,<BR>talent.<BR>	 2. Health.<BR>	 3. Eloquence.<BR> E. पटु clever, &c. aff. अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=439-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाटविक|पाटविकः
पाटविक mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>	 1. Cunning, crafty, fraudulent.<BR>	 2. Clever,<BR>dexterous.<BR> E. पटु clever, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=439-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाटहिका
पाटहिका f. (-का) A small shrub, (Abrus, precatorius.) see गुञ्जा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=439-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाटित|पाटितं
पाटित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Torn, broken, divided.<BR>	 2. Pierced.<BR> E. पट् to<BR>divide, in the causal form, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=439-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाटिन्
पाटिन् m. (-टी) A sort of fish described as having many teeth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=439-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाटी
पाटी f. (-टीः)<BR>	 1. Arithmetic.<BR>	 2. A kind of shrub called Bālā.<BR>	 3.<BR>Regular order.<BR> E. पट to go, इन् or ङीप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=439-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाटीर|पाटीरः
पाटीर m. (-रः) A field.<BR>	 2. A pungent root, a sort of radish.<BR>	 3. The<BR>pith or manna of the bamboo.<BR>	 4. A cloud.<BR>	 5. A sieve, a cribble.<BR>6. Tin.<BR>	 7. Disease arising from wind.<BR>	 8. Sandal.<BR> E. पट् to go, &c.<BR>in the causal form, ईरन् aff.; or पटीर + स्वार्थे अण् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=439-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाटूपट
पाटूपट mfn. (-टः-टा-टं) Going, who or what goes.<BR> E. पट् to go, अच् aff.<BR>and the root repeated, form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=439-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाठ|पाठः
पाठ m. (-ठः)<BR>	 1. Studying the Vedas scriptures, considered as one of<BR>the five great sacraments of the Hindus.<BR>	 2. Reading, perusal or<BR>study in general.<BR>	 f. (-ठा) A plant, commonly Akanādi.<BR> E. पठ् to<BR>read, aff. भावे घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=439-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाठक|पाठकः
पाठक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A lecturer, a public reader of the Puraṇās or<BR>other sacred works, or a Paṇḍit who declares what is the law<BR>or custom according to the scriptures.<BR>	 2. A spiritual preceptor.<BR>3. A reader, a student.<BR> E. पठ् to read, ण्वुल् aff., or पठ, causal v.<BR>वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=439-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाठन|पाठनं
पाठन n. (-नं) Lecturing, teaching.<BR> E. पठ् to read, causal v. भावे ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=439-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाठभू
पाठभू f. (-भूः) A place where the Vedas are read or studied.<BR> E. पाठ<BR>reading, (the Vedas,) and भू place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=439-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाठमञ्जरी
पाठमञ्जरी f. (-री) A small bird, commonly Sāri, (Gracula religiosa.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=439-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाठशाला
पाठशाला f. (-ला) A college, a school.<BR> E. पाठ study, शाला a hall.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=439-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाठशालिनी
पाठशालिनी f. (-नी) A small bird: see पाठमञ्जरी. पाठेन शलते, शल-णिनि-ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=439-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाठान
पाठान m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. Bdellium.<BR>	 2. kind of fish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=439-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाठित
पाठित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Instructed, taught, lectured.<BR> E. पठ् to read.<BR>causal v., क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=439-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाठिन्
पाठिन् m. (-ठी)<BR>	 1. A plant. (Plumbago zeylanica.)<BR>	 2. A Brāhman,<BR>especially one who has finished his sacred studies.<BR> E. पाठ perusal,<BR>and इनि aff.; the virtues of the plant are to be read of in medical<BR>works.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=439-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाठीन|पाठीनः
पाठीन m. (-नः) A sort of fish, (Silurus boalis, Ham.)<BR>	 2. A public<BR>reader or lecturer on the Purāṇās, &c.<BR>	 3. A tree: see गुग्गुल. E.<BR>पाठी a Brāhman, and ईन् added. “वोयाल” ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=439-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाठ्य|पाठ्यं
पाठ्य mfn. (-ठ्यः-ठ्या-ठ्यं) To be read or studied.<BR> E. पठ् to read, ण्यत् aff.; also पठनीय, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=439-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाडिनी
पाडिनी f. (-नी) An earthen pot or boiler.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=439-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाण|पाणः
पाण m. (-णः)<BR>	 1. Trade, traffic.<BR>	 2. A trader.<BR>	 3. An agreement.<BR>	 4.<BR>Praise.<BR>	 5. The hand.<BR> E. पण् to be of price, &c. भावे घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=439-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाणि|पाणिः
पाणि m. (-णिः) The hand.<BR>	 f. (-णिः) A place of sale, a shop, a market. E.<BR>पण् to be of price, &c. Unādi aff. इण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=439-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाणिका
पाणिका f. (-का) A sort of spoon or ladle.<BR> E. पाणि the hand, कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=439-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाणिगृहीती
पाणिगृहीती f. (-ती) A bride, one wedded according to the ritual. E.<BR>पाणि the hand, and गृहीत taken: see the next: when the com-<BR>pound means merely taken by the hand, the form is पाणिगृहीत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=439-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाणिग्रहण|पाणिग्रहणं
पाणिग्रहण n. (णं)<BR>	 1. Marriage.<BR>	 2. Laying hold of the hand.<BR> E. पाणि the<BR>hand, and ग्रहण taking, the junction of the hands of the bride and<BR>bridegroom, forming a part of this ceremony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=439-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाणिग्रहणिक
पाणिग्रहणिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Matrimonial.<BR> E. पाणिग्रहण, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=439-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाणिग्राह|पाणिग्राहः
पाणिग्राह m. (-हः)<BR>	 1. Laying hold of the hand.<BR>	 2. Marriage.<BR> E. पाणि,<BR>and ग्राह taking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=439-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाणिघ|पाणिघः
पाणिघ m. (-घः)<BR>	 1. A drummer, one who plays on a tabor, &c, with his<BR>hands.<BR>	 2. Playing upon a hand instrument.<BR>	 3. A workman, a<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=440-a" target="_blank">Page440-a+ 60</a>]<BR>handicraftsman.<BR> E. पाणि the hand, हन् to strike, ठक् aff. and घ<BR>substituted for the root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=439-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाणिघात|पाणिघातः
पाणिघात m. (-तः)<BR>	 1. Striking with the hands, boxing.<BR>	 2. A boxer, or<BR>one who strikes with his hand.<BR> E. पाणि the hand, and घात blow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=440-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाणिचापल्य
पाणिचापल्य n. (-ल्यं) Fighting with the hand, snapping the fingers,<BR>&c.<BR> E. पाणि the hand, चापल्य unsteadiness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=440-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाणिज|पाणिजः
पाणिज m. (-जः) A finger-nail.<BR> E. पाणि the hand, जन् to be born, aff. ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=440-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाणितल|पाणितलं
पाणितल n. (-लं)<BR>	 1. The palm of the hand.<BR>	 2. A measure of two Tolās.<BR>E. पाणि, and तल below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=440-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाणिन|पाणिनः
पाणिन m. (-नः) A name of Pāṇini: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=440-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाणिनि|पाणिनिः
पाणिनि m. (-निः) Pāṇini, a Muni and inspired grammarian.<BR> E. पाणिन्<BR>a proper name and इञ् aff. of descent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=440-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाणिनीय|पाणिनीयं|पाणिनीयः
पाणिनीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Connected with or derived from Pāṇini, the<BR>grammarian, (as a scholar, a rule, &c.)<BR> E. पाणिनि the saint, and<BR>छ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=440-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाणिधम
पाणिधम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>	 1. Who blows through the hands.<BR>	 2. Obscure.<BR>dark, (as a path, where a noise is made with the hands, to<BR>frighten away snakes, &c.)<BR> E. पाणि the hand, ध्मा to blow or<BR>breathe, aff. स्वञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=440-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाणिन्धय|पाणिंधय|पाणिन्धयः
पाणिन्धय mfn. (-यः-यी-यं) Who or what drinks from the hand.<BR> E. पाणि,<BR>and धे to drink, खश् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=440-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाणिपाद|पाणिपादं
पाणिपाद n. (-दं) The hands and feet<BR> E. पाणि the hand, and पाद the<BR>foot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=440-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाणिपीडन|पाणिपीडनं
पाणिपीडन n. (-नं) Marriage.<BR> E. पाणि the hand, पीडन paining, taking:<BR>see पाणिग्रहण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=440-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाणिभुज्
पाणिभुज् m. (-भुक्) The glomerous fig tree, (F. glomerata.)<BR> E. पाणि<BR>the hand, and भुज् what eats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=440-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाणिप्तत्
पाणिप्तत् mfn. (-मान्-मती-मत्) Possessed of hands.<BR> E. पाणि, and<BR>मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=440-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाणिमुक्त|पाणिमुक्तं
पाणिमुक्त n. (-क्तं) A missile weapon, one thrown with the hand, as a<BR>dart, a spear.<BR> E. पाणि the hand, and मुक्त loosed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=440-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाणिरुह्
पाणिरुह् m. (-रुट्) A finger-nail.<BR> E. पाणि, and रुह् to grow, क्विप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=440-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाणिवाद|पाणिवादः
पाणिवाद m. (-दः)<BR>	 1. A drummer, playing on a drum or tabor with<BR>the hand.<BR>	 2. Clapping the hands together.<BR> E. पाणि the hand, and<BR>वाद who sounds; also with कन् added पाणिवादक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=440-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाणिसर्ग्या
पाणिसर्ग्या f. (-र्ग्या) A rope, a cord.<BR> E. पाणि, the hand, सृज् to go,<BR>aff. कर्मणि-ण्यत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=440-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाणिस्थ
पाणिस्थ mfn. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थं) Held in the hand.<BR> E. पाणि, and स्थ what<BR>stays.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=440-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाणिहोम
पाणिहोम m. (-मः) Offerings made to Brāhmans where consecrated fire<BR>is not used.<BR> E. पाणि, and होम burnt offering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=440-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाणीतल|पाणीतलं
पाणीतल n. (-लं) A measure of two Tolās.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=440-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाणौकरण|पाणौकरणं
पाणौकरण n. (-णं) Marriage.<BR> E. पाणौ with the hand, and करण making.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=440-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाण्डर|पांडर|पाण्डरं|पाण्डरः
पाण्डर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Pale or yellowish white.<BR>	 m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Pale or<BR>yellowish white, (the colour.)<BR>	 2. A plant, commonly Marūa or<BR>Marūvaka.<BR>	 n. (-रं)<BR>	 1. Many-flowered jasmine.<BR>	 2. Red chalk. E.<BR>पडि to go, अर् Unādi aff., and the radical vowel made long; also<BR>पाण्डुर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=440-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाण्डरपुष्पिका
पाण्डरपुष्पिका f. (-का) A plant, commonly Sitalā, (perhaps phrynium<BR>dichotomum:) see शीतला.<BR> E. पाण्डर pale white, पुष्पी flower, aff. कप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=440-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाण्डव|पांडव|पांडवः|पाण्डवः
पाण्डव m. (-वः) A Pāṇḍava or descendant of PĀṆḌU; especially ap-<BR>plied to YUDHISṬHIRA and his four brothers.<BR> E. पाण्डु a proper<BR>name, and patronymic aff. ओरञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=440-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाण्डवाभील|पांडवाभील|पाण्डवाभीलः
पाण्डवाभील m. (-लः) A name of KṚṢṆA.<BR> E. पाण्डव a Pāṇḍava, and<BR>अभी courage, (not fear,) ल who gives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=440-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाण्डवायन|पांडवायनः|पाण्डवायनः
पाण्डवायन m. (-नः) A name of KṚṢṆA.<BR> E. पाण्डव a Pāṇḍava, and<BR>अयन going, accompanying; being the friend and ally of the<BR>Pāṇḍu princes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=440-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाण्डवेय|पांडवेय|पांडवेयः|पाण्डवेयः
पाण्डवेय m. (-यः) A descendant of Pāṇḍu<BR> E. पाण्ड, and ढक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=440-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाण्डित्य|पांडित्य|पांडित्यं|पाण्डित्यं
पाण्डित्य nf. (-थं-ती) Scholarship, learning.<BR>	 2. Dexterity, cleverness.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=440-b" target="_blank">Page440-b+ 60</a>]<BR>E. पण्डित a teacher, aff. ष्यञ् the semivowel rejected before the<BR>feminine aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=440-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाण्डु|पांडु|पाण्डुः
पाण्डु mfn. (-ण्डुः-ण्डुः-ण्डु) Pale of yellowish white.<BR>	 m. (-ण्डुः)<BR>	 1. Pale<BR>or yellowish white, (the colour.)<BR>	 2. the name of a sovereign of<BR>ancient Delhi, and nominal father of YUDHIṢṬHIRA and he<BR>other four Pāṇḍava princes; he was a son of Vyāsa by the<BR>wife of Bichitrabirya.<BR>	 3. The jaundice.<BR>	 4. A white elephant.<BR>f. (-ण्डुः) A plant, commonly Māshaparni, (Glycine debilis.) E.<BR>पडि to go, aff. कु, and the penultimate vowel made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=440-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाण्डक
पाण्डक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. The jaundice.<BR>	 2. A name of Pāṇḍu.<BR>	 3. Pale or<BR>yellowish white, (the colour.)<BR> E. कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=440-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाण्डुकम्बल|पांडुकंबल|पाण्डुकम्बलः
पाण्डुकम्बल m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. A sort of blanket or warm upper garment.<BR>2. A kind of stone, (Limestone or marble).<BR>	 3. The housings<BR>of a royal elephant.<BR> E. पाण्डु pale, and कम्बल blanket.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=440-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाण्डुकम्बलिन्
पाण्डुकम्बलिन् m. (-ली)<BR>	 1. A carriage covered with a sort of blanket.<BR>2. The housings of a royal elephant.<BR> E. पाण्डुकम्बल a blanket,<BR>and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=440-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाण्डुनाग|पाण्डुनागः
पाण्डुनाग m. (-गः) A plant, (Rottleria tinctoria.)<BR>	 2. A white elephant.<BR>3. A white species of serpent.<BR> E. पाण्डु pale, नाग a plant, a snake,<BR>or elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=440-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाण्डुपुत्र|पांडुपुत्र|पाण्डुपुत्रः
पाण्डुपुत्र m. (-त्त्रः) Either of the Pāṇḍava princes.<BR> E. पाण्डु, and पुत्त्र<BR>son; also similar compounds, as पाण्डुनन्दन, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=440-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाण्डुपृष्ठ|पाण्डुपृष्ठः
पाण्डुपृष्ठ mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठा-ष्ठं) Having unlucky marks on the back &c. E.<BR>पाण्डु pale, &c. and पृष्ठ back.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=440-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाण्डुभूम|पाण्डुभूमः
पाण्डुभूम m. (-मः) A country with a light-coloured soil.<BR> E. पाण्डु pale,<BR>and भूमि earth, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=440-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाण्डुमृत्
पाण्डुमृत् f. (-मृत्)<BR>	 1. A country in which the soil is of a whitish<BR>colour.<BR>	 2. Chalk.<BR> E. पाण्डु pale, and मृत् earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=440-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाण्डुमृत्तिका|पांडुमृत्तिका
पाण्डुमृत्तिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. The opal.<BR>	 2. A pale soil.<BR> E. पाण्डु pale, and<BR>मृत्तिका earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=440-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाण्डुर|पांडुर
पाण्डुर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Of a yellowish white colour.<BR>	 m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A pale<BR>or yellowish white.<BR>	 2. The jaundice.<BR>	 3. A tree: see मरुवक.<BR>	 n.<BR>(-रं) The white leprosy, vitiligo.<BR> E. पाण्डु pale, and र added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=440-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाण्डुरद्रुम|पाण्डुरद्रुमः
पाण्डुरद्रुम m. (-मः) A plant, (Echites antidysenterica.) “कुड्ची” ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=440-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाण्डुरपृष्ठ|पाण्डुरपृष्ठः
पाण्डुरपृष्ठ mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठी-ष्ठं) Having unlucky marks on the back, &c.<BR>E. पाण्डुर pale, and पृष्ठ the back.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=440-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाण्डुराग|पांडुराग|पाण्डुरागः
पाण्डुराग m. (-गः) Whiteness, pallor.<BR> E. पाण्डु, and राग colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=440-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाण्डुलेख|पांडुलेख|पाण्डुलेखः
पाण्डुलेख m. (-खः) A sketch made with chalk, a draft.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=440-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाण्डुलोमा
पाण्डुलोमा f. (-मा)<BR>	 1. A plant, (Glycine debilis.)<BR>	 2. Having white<BR>hair on the body, &c.<BR> E. पाण्डु pale, लोमन् hair or fibres: see<BR>पाण्डु. “माषपर्ण्याम्” ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=440-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाण्डुवर्ण
पाण्डुवर्ण mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-णं) White.<BR>	 m. (-र्णः) Whiteness.<BR> E. पाण्डु, and<BR>वर्ण colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=440-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाण्डुशर्क्क
पाण्डुशर्क्क(र्क)रा f. (-रा) Light-coloured gravel, (disease.)<BR> E. पाण्डु, and<BR>शर्क्करा sugar. सितानामक प्रमेह रोगे ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=440-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पण्डुशर्म्मिला
पण्डुशर्म्मिला f. (-ला) A name of DRAUPADI.<BR> E. पाण्डु a Pāṇḍu prince,<BR>शर्म्म fortune, aff. इलच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=440-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाण्डुसोपाक|पांडुसोपाक|पाण्डुसोपाकः
पाण्डुसोपाक m. (-कः) The offspring of a Caṇḍāla by a Vaidehī<BR>woman, a maker of mats, baskets, &c. a worker with bamboos,<BR>and reeds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=440-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाण्ड्य|पांड्य|पाण्ड्यः
पाण्ड्य m. (-ण्ड्य) plu.<BR>	 1. Name of a country and its inhabitants.<BR>	 2. Sing.<BR>A king of that country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=440-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाण्य|पाण्यः
पाण्य mfn. (-ण्यः-ण्या-ण्यं) Excellent, praise-worthy.<BR> E. पण् to praise, aff. ण्यत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=440-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाण्यास्य
पाण्यास्य m. (स्यः) A Brāhman who reads the Vedas upon receiving a<BR>gift at a Shrāddha.<BR> E. पाणि, and आस्य face or mouth, having his<BR>mouth in his hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=440-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पात्
पात् m. (-पात्)<BR>	 1. Falling.<BR>	 2. Sin, wickedness.<BR> E. पत् to fall, aff. क्किप,<BR>and the radical vowel made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=440-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पात्
पात् mfn. (-पान्-पान्ती-पात्) Who or what defends or preserves, a<BR>guardian, a protector, &c.<BR> E. पा to preserve, aff. शतृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=440-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पात|पातः
पात mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Preserved, protected.<BR> E. पा to preserve, aff. क्त.<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>	 1. Falling, alighting, descending.<BR>	 2. A name of Rāhu.<BR>3. The node of a planet's orbit.<BR>	 4. Flying, flight.<BR>	 5. A stroke, as<BR>in खड्गपात । 6. Shedding, emitting, discharging.<BR>	 7. An attack,<BR>an inroad.<BR>	 8. Happening.<BR>	 9. Failing, defect.<BR>	 10. Destruction,<BR>dissolution.<BR> E. पत् to fall, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=441-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पातक|पातकं|पातकः
पातक n. (-कं)<BR>	 1. Sin, crime.<BR>	 2. The cause of falling, literally or<BR>figuratively. For particulars see पञ्चपातक.<BR> E. पत् to fall or des-<BR>cend, (from virtue,) causal form, aff. ण्वुल्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=441-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पातकयोग
पातकयोग m. (-गः) Incurring guilt, acting sinfully.<BR> E. पातक, and योग<BR>accession.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=441-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पातकिन्
पातकिन् mfn. (-की-किनी-कि) Wicked, sinful, a sinner.<BR> E. पातक, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=441-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पातङ्कि
पातङ्कि m. (-ङ्किः)<BR>	 1. Saturn.<BR>	 2. Yama.<BR>	 3. Karṇa.<BR>	 4. Sugrīva.<BR> E. पतङ्ग<BR>the sun, इञ् aff. of descent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=441-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पातञ्जल|पातंजल|पातञ्जलं
पातञ्जल f. (-ली) Composed by Patanjali “पातञ्जले महाभाष्ये कृत भूरि<BR>परिश्रमः” Nagogibhatta.<BR>	 n. (लं) The Yoga system of philosophy.<BR>(It is an open question whether the author of the Mahā-<BR>bhāsya was identical with this Patanjali.)<BR> E. पतञ्जलि the sage<BR>by whom it was first taught, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=441-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पातन|पातनं
पातन n. (-नं) Bringing down, causing to fall.<BR>	 2. Lowering, humbling,<BR>3. Felling, knocking down.<BR>	 4. Nodding, (as in sleep.)<BR>	 5. Causing<BR>an abortion, as गर्भस्य पातनम्.<BR>	 6. Beating, as in दण्डस्य पातनम् &c.<BR>E. पत् to fall in the causal form, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=441-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पातव्य
पातव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>	 1. To be drunk.<BR>	 2. To be preserved or<BR>protected.<BR> E. पा to drink, to preserve, तव्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=441-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाताल|पातालं|पातालः
पाताल n. (-लं) The regions under the earth, and the abode of the<BR>Nāgas or serpents.<BR>	 2. A hole, a chasm.<BR>	 3. Submarine fire.<BR>	 4. The<BR>fourth sign from that in which the sun is present.<BR>	 m. (-लः) A<BR>sort of apparatus for calcining and subliming metals, formed<BR>of two earthen pots, the upper one inverted over the lower, and<BR>the two joined together by their necks with cement, and placed<BR>in a hole containing fire.<BR> E. पत् to alight, Unādi aff. आलञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=441-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पातालगङ्गा|पातालगंगा
पातालगङ्गा f. (-ङ्गाः) The ganges of the lower world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=441-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पातालनिलय|पातालनिलयः
पातालनिलय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. A demon, a Daitya.<BR>	 2. A Nāga or infernal<BR>serpent.<BR> E. पाताल hell, and निलय abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=441-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पातालौकस्
पातालौकस् m. (-काः) An Asur, a demon.<BR> E. पाताल hell, ओकस् a house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=441-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाति|पातिः
पाति m. (-तिः) A master, a lord, a husband.<BR> E. पा to nourish, Unādi<BR>aff. अति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=441-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पातिक|पातिकः
पातिक m. (-कः) The Gangetic porpoise.<BR> E. पात trembling, falling,<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=441-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पातित
पातित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Felled, struck down.<BR>	 2. Lowered, depressed,<BR>humbled.<BR> E. पत् to fall, causal v., क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=441-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पातित्य|पातित्यं
पातित्य n. (-त्यं) Loss of caste or position.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=441-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षातिन्
षातिन् mfn. (-ती-तिनी-ति) Going, going to, alighting, falling, pouring<BR>forth.<BR> E. पत् to go, घिणुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=441-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पातिली
पातिली f. (-ली)<BR>	 1. A trap or snare for catching deer.<BR>	 2. A small<BR>earthen vessel or pot, especially used by religious mendicants.<BR>3. A woman of a particular class.<BR> E. पात falling, इलच् aff. fem.<BR>aff. ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=441-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पातुक|पातुकः
पातुक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Falling frequently or habitually, disposed to<BR>fall.<BR>	 m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. The declivity of a mountain, a precipice.<BR>	 2. An<BR>aquatic animal of a large size; figuratively, the water-elephant.<BR>E. पत् to fall, aff. उकञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=441-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पातृ
पातृ mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ) Who or what protects or nourishes.<BR>	 m. (-ता) A<BR>plant, (Ocymum pilosum.)<BR> E. पा to nourish, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=441-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पात्य
पात्य mfn. (-त्यः-त्या-त्यं) To be fallen, to be alighted.<BR> E. पत् to fall,<BR>ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=441-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पात्र|पात्त्रं|पात्रं|पात्रः
पात्र n. (-त्रं) A preservative from sin, a preserver, a saviour.<BR> E. पात्,<BR>and त्र who or what saves.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=441-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पात्रता
पात्रता f. (-ता) The quality or property of a preservative from sin. E.<BR>पात, and तल् aff.; also with त्व, पातत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=441-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पात्र|पात्त्रं|पात्रं|पात्रः
पात्र mfn. (-त्रः-त्री-त्रं) A vessel in general, a plate, a cup, a jar, &c.<BR>	 n.<BR>(-त्रं)<BR>	 1. A sacrificial vase or vessel, comprising various forms of<BR>cups, plates, spoons, ladles, &c. so used.<BR>	 2. The channel of a<BR>river, or its course between the near and opposite bank.<BR>	 3. A<BR>king's counsellor or minister.<BR>	 4. Propriety, fitness.<BR>	 5. A leaf.<BR>	 6.<BR>The persons of a drama.<BR>	 7. An order, a command.<BR>	 8. The body.<BR>9. A fit or competent person.<BR>	 10. A measure of one Ārhaka<BR>or of eight Seers.<BR>	 11. A receptacle of any kind, what holds<BR>or supports.<BR>	 f. (-त्री) A small or portable furnace.<BR> E. पा to pro-<BR>serve or retain, aff. त्रन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=441-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पात्रट|पात्रटः
पात्रट mfn. (-टः-टा-टं) Spare, emaciate, thin.<BR>	 m. (-टः) Ragged gar-<BR>ments.<BR> E. पातेव पिवन्निव अटति, अट्-अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=441-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पात्रटीर|पात्रटीरः
पात्रटीर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. An able or competent minister.<BR>	 2. A vessel of<BR>metal, as silver, brass, &c.<BR>	 3. Rust of iron.<BR>	 4. Fire.<BR>	 5. A heron.<BR>6. A crow.<BR> E. पात्र a vessel, &c. and टीर aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=441-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पात्रता
पात्रता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Capacity, fitness.<BR>	 2. Appropriate state or circums-<BR>tance.<BR>	 3. The property or capacity of a cup or vessel.<BR>	 4.<BR>Dignity, honor.<BR> E. पात्र capable, and तल् aff. of the abstract,<BR>quality; also with त्व aff., पात्रत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=441-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पात्रपाल|पात्रपालः
पात्रपाल m. (-लः) A large oar used as a rudder.<BR>	 2. The rod of a<BR>balance.<BR> E. पात्र a vessel, (a boat,) and पाल what cherishes, affix. अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=441-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पात्रभूत
पात्रभूत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) The object of a present or of respectful treat-<BR>ment.<BR> E. पात्र fit, and भूत become.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=441-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पात्रभृत्
पात्रभृत् m. (-भृत्) A servant.<BR> E. पात्र, and भृत् who takes care of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=441-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पात्रसंस्कार|पात्रसंस्कारः
पात्रसंस्कार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. The current of a river.<BR>	 2. Cleaning a vessel<BR>that has been used.<BR> E. पात्र the channel, and संस्कार completion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=441-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पात्रिक
पात्रिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>	 1. Measured by a vessel, or the measure<BR>Pātra, sown with it, preparing it, &c.<BR>	 2. Fit, adequate, appro-<BR>priate.<BR>	 n. (-कं) A vessel, a cup, a dish.<BR> E. पात्र, and ष्ठन् aff.; also<BR>with घ aff. पात्रिय, and with यत्, पात्र्या, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=441-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पात्रिन्
पात्रिन् mfn. (-त्री-त्रिणी-त्रि)<BR>	 1. Having a vessel.<BR>	 2. Having fit or worthy<BR>persons.<BR> E. पात्र, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=441-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पात्रिय
पात्रिय f. (-या) Worthy to partake of a meal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=441-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पात्रीण
पात्रीण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Measured, sown, cooked, &c. by a Pātra. E.<BR>पात्र, and ख aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=441-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पात्रीय|पात्रीयं
पात्रीय n. (-यं) A sacrificial vessel.<BR> E. पात्र, the same, and छ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=441-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पात्रीर|पात्रीरं|पात्रीरः
पात्रीर(व) m. (-रः or -वः) An oblation.<BR> E. पात्र, a sacrificial vessel, ईर<BR>to go, क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=441-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पात्रेसमित|पात्रेसमितः
पात्रेसमित m. (-तः)<BR>	 1. A parasite, a person constant at dinners, or<BR>feasts, but good for nothing else.<BR>	 2. A connoisseur in eating.<BR>	 3.<BR>A hypocrite.<BR> E. पात्रे in a vessel, plate, &c and समित collected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=441-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पात्रोपकरण|पात्रोपकरणं
पात्रोपकरण n. (-णं) Decorations of an inferior class, as bells, chowris,<BR>&c.<BR> E. पात्र, and उपकरण instrument.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=441-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाथ|पाथं|पाथः
पाथ m. (-थः)<BR>	 1. The sun.<BR>	 2. Fire.<BR>	 n. (-थं) Water.<BR> E. पा to drink, and<BR>थक् aff.; the more usual form however is पीथ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=441-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाथस्
पाथस् n. (-थः)<BR>	 1. Water.<BR>	 2. Food.<BR>	 3. Air.<BR>	 4. Sky.<BR> E. पा to drink,<BR>Unādi aff. असुन, and थुक् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=441-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाथिस्
पाथिस् m. (-थि)<BR>	 1. The sea.<BR>	 2. The eye.<BR>	 n. (-थि) A blotch, a scab. E.<BR>पा to drink, Unādi aff. इसिन्, and थुक् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=441-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाथेय|पाथेयं
पाथेय n. (-यं)<BR>	 1. Provender, or provisions, &c. for a journey, viaticum.<BR>2. The sign Virgo of the Zodiac.<BR> E. पयिन् road, aff. ढञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=441-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाथोज|पाथोजं
पाथोज n. (-जं)<BR>	 1. A lotus.<BR>	 2. The conch.<BR> E. पाथस्, and ज produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=441-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाथोद|पाथोदः
पाथोद m. (-दः) A cloud.<BR> E. पाथस् water, दा to give, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=441-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाथोधर|पाथोधरः
पाथोधर m. (-रः) A cloud.<BR> E. पाथस् water, धर having.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=441-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाथोधि|पाथोधिः
पाथोधि m. (-धिः) The ocean.<BR> E. पाथस् water, and घा to have, aff. कि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=441-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाथोनिधि|पाथोनिधिः
पाथोनिधि m. (-धिः) The ocean.<BR> E. पाथस् water, and निधि receptacle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=441-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाद्
पाद् m. (-पाद् or -पात्) The foot.<BR> E. पद् to go, aff. णिच्-क्विप्, and the<BR>radical vowel made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=441-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाद|पादः
पाद m. (-दः)<BR>	 1. A foot.<BR>	 2. A quarter.<BR>	 3. A hill at the foot of a mountain.<BR>4. A ray of light.<BR>	 5. The root of a tree.<BR>	 6. The foot or line of a<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=442-a" target="_blank">Page442-a+ 60</a>]<BR>stanza.<BR>	 7. The line of a hymn or stanza of the Rig Vedas.<BR>	 8. The<BR>quadrant of a circle.<BR>	 9. The foot or leg of an inanimate object.<BR>E. पद् to go, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=441-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादकटक|पादकटकः
पादकटक m. (-कः) An ornament for the feet or toes.<BR> E. पाद a foot, and<BR>कटक bracelet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=442-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादकृच्छ्र|पादकृच्छ्रः
पादकृच्छ्र n. (-च्छ्रं) A sort of penance, eating once and fasting on<BR>alternate nights.<BR> E. पाद a quarter, and कृच्छ्र penance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=442-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादगण्डिर|पादगण्डिरः
पादगण्डिर m. (-रः) Morbid enlargement of the legs and feet.<BR> E. पाद<BR>the foot, गण्ड a swelling, इरन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=442-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादग्रहण|पादग्रहणं
पादग्रहण n. (-णं) Respectful obeisance, touching the feet of a Brāh-<BR>man or superior.<BR> E. पाद, and ग्रहण taking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=442-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादचत्वर|पादचत्वरः
पादचत्वर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A goat.<BR>	 2. A sand bank.<BR>	 3. The religious fig-tree,<BR>(Ficus religious.)<BR>	 4. Hail.<BR>	 5. A slanderer, a calumniator. E.<BR>पाद the foot, and चत्वर levelled ground.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=442-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादचापल्य
पादचापल्य n. (-ल्यं) Beating or shuffling with the feet.<BR> E. पाद a feet, &c.<BR>चापल्य unsteadiness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=442-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादचार|पादचारः
पादचार n. (-रं)<BR>	 1. The daily position of the planets.<BR>	 2. Going on foot.<BR>E. पाद, and चार going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=442-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादचारिन्
पादचारिन् m. (-री) A footman, a foot-soldier.<BR> E. पाद, and चर् to go,<BR>aff. णिनि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=442-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादज|पादजः
पादज m. (-जः) A Śūdra, or man of the fourth and servile tribe. E.<BR>पाद the foot, (of BRAMHĀ,) and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=442-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादजाह
पादजाह n. (-हं) The tarsus. पादस्य मूलं कर्णा० जाहच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=442-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादतल
पादतल n. (-लं)<BR>	 1. The sole or the lower part of the foot. adv. As low<BR>as, or under the feet.<BR> E. पाद, and तल below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=442-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादतस्
पादतस् ind.<BR>	 1. At the foot.<BR>	 2. By or with a quarter.<BR> E. पाद, and तसि<BR>aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=442-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादत्राण|पादत्राणं
पादत्राण n. (-णं) A boot, a shoe.<BR> E. पाद the foot, and त्राण preserving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=442-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाददारी
पाददारी f. (-री) A chap in the feet, a chilblain<BR> E. पाद, दृ to rend, अण्<BR>aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=442-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादप|पादपः
पादप m. (-पः)<BR>	 1. A tree.<BR>	 2. A foot-stool, a cushion, &c. for the feet.<BR>	 f.<BR>(-पा) A shoe, a slipper.<BR> E. पाद, a foot, or root, and पा to drink or<BR>preserve, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=442-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादपरिघट्टन
पादपरिघट्टन n. (-नं) Trampling, treading upon.<BR> E. पाद, and परिघट्टन<BR>friction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=442-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादपरुहा
पादपरुहा f. (-हा) A creeping or a parasite plant.<BR> E. पादप a tree, and<BR>रुह what mounts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=442-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादपाश|पादपाशः
पादपाश m. (-शः)<BR>	 1. A foot-rope for cattle or horses.<BR>	 2. An anklet of<BR>small bells, &c.<BR>	 f. (-शी)<BR>	 1. A chain for the feet, a fetter.<BR>	 2. A foot-<BR>carpet or mat.<BR> E. पाद the foot, and पाश a fetter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=442-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादपीठ|पादपीठं|पादपीठः
पादपीठ m. (-ठः) A foot-stool.<BR> E. पाद, and पीठ a stool.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=442-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादपीठिका
पादपीठिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. Any common or vulgar trade, as that of a bar-<BR>ber, &c.<BR>	 2. A white-stone.<BR> E. पादपीठ a foot-stool, a work bench,<BR>ङीप् depreciative aff., and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=442-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादपूरण
पादपूरण n. (-णं) An expletive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=442-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादप्रक्षालन|पादप्रक्षालनं
पादप्रक्षालन n. (-नं) Washing the feet.<BR> E. पाद, and प्रक्षालन washing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=442-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादप्रणाम|पादप्रणामः
पादप्रणाम m. (-मः) Bowing to the feet, prostration.<BR> E. पाद, and प्रणाम<BR>bowing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=442-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादप्रधारण|पादप्रधारणं
पादप्रधारण n. (-णं) A shoe.<BR> E. पाद, and प्रधारण defending.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=442-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादप्रहार|पादप्रहारः
पादप्रहार m. (-रः) A kick.<BR> E. पाद the foot, and प्रहार striking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=442-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादबन्धन|पादबंधन|पादबन्धनं
पादबन्धन n. (-नं) Stock of cattle.<BR> E. पाद a foot, and बन्धन binding,<BR>alluding to the foot-ropes with which cattle are tied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=442-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादमुद्रा
पादमुद्रा f. (-द्रा) A foot-print.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=442-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादमूल|पादमूलं
पादमूल n. (-लं) The heel.<BR>	 2. The tarsus.<BR>	 3. A polite designation of a<BR>person.<BR> E. पाद the foot, and मूल the root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=442-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादरक्षण|पादरक्षणं
पादरक्षण n. (-णं) A leather boot or shoe.<BR> E. पाद the foot, and<BR>रक्षण protecting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=442-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादरज्जु|पादरज्जुः
पादरज्जु f. (-ज्जुः) An elephant's heel-ropes.<BR> E. पाद, and रज्जु a rope.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=442-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादरथ
पादरथ mf. (-थः-था) A shoe, a slipper<BR> E. पाद the foot and रथ a vehicle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=442-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादरोहण|पादरोहणः
पादरोहण m. (-णः) The Indian fig-tree.<BR> E. पाद, and रोहण what rises.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=442-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादवन्दन|पादवंदन
पादवन्दन n. (-नं) Respect, respectful behaviour.<BR> E. पाद, and बन्दन<BR>saluting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=442-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादवल्मीक|पादवल्मीकः
पादवल्मीक n. (-कं) Morbid enlargement of the legs and feet.<BR> E. पाद<BR>the foot, वल्मीक a hillock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=442-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादविक|पादविकः
पादविक m. (-कः) A traveller, a way-farer.<BR> E. पदवी a road, aff. ठक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=442-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादविरजस्
पादविरजस् m. (-जाः) A god.<BR>	 f. (जाः) A shoe, a slipper.<BR> E. पाद the foot,<BR>वि privative, रजस् dust.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=442-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादशब्द
पादशब्द m. (-ब्दः) The sound or noise of the feet.<BR> E. पाद a foot, and<BR>शव्द sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=442-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादशाश्
पादशाश् ind.<BR>	 1. Verse by verse, stanza by stanza.<BR>	 2. Foot by foot.<BR>3. By a fourth.<BR> E. पाद a verse, शशि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=442-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादशाखा
पादशाखा f. (-खा) A toe.<BR> E. पाद a foot, शाखा a branch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=442-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादशैल|पादशैलः
पादशैल m. (-लः) A hill near a mountain.<BR> E. पाद the foot, and शैल a<BR>hill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=442-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादशोथ|पादशोथः
पादशोथ m. (-थः) Swelling of the feet, gout.<BR> E. पाद, and शोथ a swelling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=442-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादसेवन
पादसेवन n. (-नं) Service, duty.<BR> E. पाद, and सेवन waiting upon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=442-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादस्फोट|पादस्फोटः
पादस्फोट m. (-टः) Kibe, chilblain, a sore or ulcer on the foot.<BR> E. पाद<BR>the foot, and स्फोट a boil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=442-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादहत
पादहत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Trodden on, kicked, touched with the feet. E.<BR>पाद and हत struck.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=442-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादहर्ष|पादहर्षः
पादहर्ष m. (-र्षः) Tingling of the feet after pressure upon the crural<BR>nerves.<BR> E. पाद, and हर्ष pleasure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=442-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादहारक|पादहारकः
पादहारक m. (-कः) One who takes or steals any thing with his feet.<BR>E. पाद a foot, ह to take, aff. ण्वुल्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=442-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादाग्र|पादाग्रं
पादाग्र n. (-ग्रं) The point of the foot.<BR> E. पाद, and अग्र point or tip.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=442-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादाङ्गद|पादांगद|पादाङ्गदं
पादाङ्गद n. (-दं) An ornament for the feet or toes.<BR> E. पाद the foot, अङ्ग<BR>shape, beauty, and द what gives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=442-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादाङ्गुली
पादाङ्गुली f. (-ली) A toe.<BR> E. पाद a foot, अङ्गुली a finger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=442-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादाङ्गुष्ठ|पादांगुष्ठ|पादाङ्गुष्ठः
पादाङ्गुष्ठ m. (-ष्ठः) The great toe.<BR> E. पाद a foot, अङ्गुष्ठ the thumb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=442-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादाङ्गुष्टिका
पादाङ्गुष्टिका f. (-का) An ornament or ring worn on the great toe. E.<BR>पादाङ्गुष्ठ the great toe, aff. कन्, fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=442-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादात्
पादात् m. (-दात्) A foot-soldier, a footman.<BR> E. पाद foot, अत् to go,<BR>aff. क्किप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=442-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादात|पादातं|पादातः
पादात m. (-तः) A foot-soldier, a footman.<BR>	 n. (-तं) Infantry.<BR> E. पाद,<BR>and अत् to go, aff. अच्, or पदाति a foot-soldier, अण् collective aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=442-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादाति|पादातिः
पादाति m. (-तिः) A foot-soldier, a man on foot, or footman.<BR> E. पाद,<BR>with अत्, to go, aff. इन्; also पदाति; with कन् added, पादातिक<BR>m. (-कः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=442-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादाध्यास
पादाध्यास m. (-सः) Treading upon, kicking, spurning.<BR> E. पाद, and<BR>अध्यास placing upon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=442-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादानत
पादानत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Bowed down to the feet, prostrate.<BR> E. पाद,<BR>and आनत bowed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=442-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादारक|पादारकः
पादारक m. (-कः) The knees or ribs of a boat, supporting the deck on<BR>each side.<BR> E. पाद a foot, ऋ to go, aff. ण्वुल्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=442-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादार्घ्य
पादार्घ्य n. (-र्घ्यं) A donation to a Brāhman, or venerable persons. E.<BR>पाद foot, अर्घ्य a respectful offering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=442-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादार्द्ध
पादार्द्ध n. (-र्द्धं)<BR>	 1. An eighth.<BR>	 2. Half a line of a stanza.<BR> E. पाद, and अर्द्ध a half.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=442-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादालिन्द|पादालिंदः|पादालिन्दः
पादालिन्द mf. (-न्दः-न्दा -or -न्दी) A boat. पादैव अलिन्दो यस्याः गौरा० ङीष् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=442-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादावनेजन
पादावनेजन n. (-नं) Washing the feet.<BR> E. पाद, and अवनेजन washing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=442-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादावर्त्त|पादावर्त|पादावर्तः|पादावर्त्तः
पादावर्त्त m. (-र्त्तः) A machine for raising water from a well. E.<BR>पाद foot, and आवर्त्त revolving, worked by the feet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=442-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादावसेचन
पादावसेचन n. (-नं) Washing the feet.<BR> E. पाद, and अवसेचन<BR>sprinkling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=442-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादाविक|पादाविकः
पादाविक m. (-कः) A foot-soldier.<BR> E. पाद a foot, अव् to go, &c.<BR>aff. इक् or ठक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=442-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादासन
पादासन n. (-नं) A foot-stool.<BR> E. पाद, and आसन a seat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=442-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादास्फालन
पादास्फालन n. (-नं) Trampling, shuffling, or motion of the<BR>feet.<BR> E. पाद, and आस्फालन waving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=442-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादाहत
पादाहत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Kicked, trodden, touched by the foot.<BR>E. पाद, and आहत struck.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=442-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादिक
पादिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Fourth, a fourth.<BR> E. पाद a quarter, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=443-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादिन्
पादिन् mfn. (-दी-दिनी-दि)<BR>	 1. Footed, having feet.<BR>	 2. Having a<BR>fourth part or share.<BR>	 3. Having four parts, as a stanza, &c.<BR>m. (-दी)<BR>	 1. A footed aquatic animal, an amphibious animal.<BR>2. The heir of a fourth part of the estate.<BR> E. पाद, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=443-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादिन|पादिनः
पादिन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) A fourth part.<BR> E. पाद a quarter, घ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=443-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादु
पादु f. (-दुः) Walking.<BR> E. पद् to go, aff. उण् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=443-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादुक|पादुकः
पादुक mfn. (-कः-का-की-कं) Who or what does on foot or with<BR>feet.<BR>	 f. (-का) A shoe, a slipper.<BR> E. पद, and उकन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=443-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादुकाकार|पादुकाकारः
पादुकाकार m. (-रः) A shoemaker.<BR> E. पादुका a shoe, and कार who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=443-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादुकाकृत्
पादुकाकृत् m. (-कृत्) A shoemaker.<BR> E. पादुका a shoe, कृत् who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=443-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादू
पादू f. (-दूः) A shoe.<BR> E. पद् to go, Unādi aff. ऊ, णिच्च ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=443-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादूकृत्
पादूकृत् m. (-कृत्) A shoemaker.<BR> E. पादू a shoe, and कृत् who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=443-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादोदक|पादोदकं
पादोदक n. (-कं) Water for the feet, especially that in which the<BR>feet of a Brāhman have been washed.<BR> E. पाद, and उदक water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=443-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाद्य|पाद्यं
पाद्य mfn. (-द्यः-द्या-द्यं) Water, &c. for cleaning the feet.<BR> E. पाद<BR>the foot, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=443-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाद्यपात्र
पाद्यपात्र n. (-त्रं) A metal vessel for washing the feet.<BR> E. पाद्य, and<BR>पात्र a vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=443-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पान|पानं|पानः
पान n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Drinking.<BR>	 2. A drinking cup or vessel.<BR>	 3. Preserv-<BR>ing, protecting.<BR>	 4. A beverage.<BR>	 5. Sharpening.<BR>	 m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. Breath,<BR>breathing out, expiration.<BR>	 2. A distiller.<BR> E. पा to drink, &c.<BR>aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=443-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पानक|पानकं
पानक n. (कं) A drink.<BR> E. पानार्थं कायति-कै-क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=443-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पानगोष्ठिका
पानगोष्ठिका f. (-का) A dram shop, a place where people drink<BR>together.<BR> E. पान drinking, गोष्ठी a station, aff. कन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=443-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पानपर
पानपर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>	 1. Drinking, quaffing, who or what drinks<BR>assiduously.<BR>	 2. Looking at amorously.<BR> E. पान and पर intent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=443-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पानपात्र|पानपात्रं
पानपात्र n. (-त्रं) A glass, a drinking vessel.<BR> E. पान drinking, पात्र a<BR>vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=443-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पानबणिज्
पानबणिज् m. (-णिक्) A distiller, a vender of spirits.<BR> E. पान drinking,<BR>बणिज् a dealer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=443-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पानभाजन|पानभाजनं
पानभाजन n. (-नं) A drinking vessel, a glass, a goblet.<BR> E. पान, and<BR>भाजन a vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=443-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पानरत
पानरत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Drinking, drunken.<BR> E. पान, and रत engaged in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=443-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पानशौण्ड|पानशौंड|पानशौण्डः
पानशौण्ड m. (-ण्डः) A hard drinker.<BR> E. पान, and शौण्ड intoxicated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=443-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पानस|पानसं
पानस n. (-सं) A spirituous liquor prepared from the fruit of the Jack<BR>tree.<BR> E. पनस the Jack, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=443-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पानात्यय|पानात्ययः
पानात्यय m. (-यः) Morbid state after intoxication.<BR> E. पान, and अत्यय end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=443-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पानिक|पानिकः
पानिक m. (कः) A vendor of spirituous liquors.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=443-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पानिल|पानिलं
पानिल n. (-लं) A drinking vessel.<BR> E. पान drinking, and इलच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=443-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पानीय|पानीयं
पानीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>	 1. Drinkable, to be drunk.<BR>	 2. To be cherished,<BR>protected or preserved.<BR>	 n. (-यं) Water.<BR> E. पा to drink, अनीयर्<BR>participial aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=443-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पानीयनकुल|पानीयनकुलः
पानीयनकुल mf. (-लः-ला) An otter.<BR> E. पानीय water, नकुल an ichneumon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=443-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पानीयपृष्ठज|पानीयपृष्ठजः
पानीयपृष्ठज m. (-जः) An aquatic plant, (Pistia stratiotes.)<BR> E. पानीय<BR>water, पृष्ठ surface, ज born. “पाना” ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=443-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पानीयमूलक|पानीयमूलकं
पानीयमूलक m. (-कः) A plant, (Serratula anthelmintica:) see सोमराजी.<BR>E. पानीय water, मूल root, कप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=443-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पानियवर्णिका
पानियवर्णिका f. (-का) Sand. पानीयमिव वर्णवति-वर्णि-ण्वुल् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=443-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पानीयशालिका
पानीयशालिका f. (-का) A place where water, &c. is distributed. E.<BR>पानीय water, शाला a place, aff. स्वार्थे-क, कापि अत इत्त्वम् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=443-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पानीयामलक|पानीयामलकं
पानीयामलक n. (-कं) A fruit, (Flacourtia cataphracta.)<BR> E. पानीय water,<BR>and आमलक myrobalan. “पानिआम्ला” ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=443-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पान्थ|पांथ|पांथः|पान्थः
पान्थ mf. (-न्थः-न्था) A traveller.<BR> E. पथिन् a road, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=443-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाप|पापं|पापः
पाप mfn. (-पः-पा-पं)<BR>	 1. Mischievous, destructive, malignant.<BR>	 2. Vile,<BR>low, abandoned, vicious.<BR>	 3. Inauspicious.<BR>	 m. (-पः) A wicked<BR>man, a wretch, a profligate.<BR>	 n. (-पं)<BR>	 1. Sin, crime, wickedness,<BR>vice.<BR>	 2. Bad state, bad fortune.<BR> E. पा to preserve (from it,) and प<BR>Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=443-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पापक|पापकं|पापकः
पापक n. (-कं) Sin.<BR> E. कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=443-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पापकर
पापकर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Wicked, abandoned.<BR> E. पाप, and कर who does.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=443-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पापकर्त्तृ|पापकर्तृ
पापकर्त्तृ mfn. (-र्त्ता-र्त्त्री-र्त्तृ) Sinful, wicked, a sinner.<BR> E. पाप, and कर्चृ<BR>who does.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=443-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पापकर्म्मन्|पापकर्मन्
पापकर्म्मन् mfn. (-र्म्मा-र्म्मा-र्म्म) Wicked, sinful.<BR> E. पाप, and कर्म्मन् act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=443-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पापकृत्
पापकृत् mfn. (-कृत्) Sinful, wicked, a sinner.<BR> E. पाप sin, क्व to commit,<BR>aff. क्किप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=443-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पापगोचर
पापगोचर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Evidently involved in the consequences of<BR>sin.<BR> E. पाप, and गोचर visible object.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=443-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पापग्रह|पापग्रहः
पापग्रह m. (-हः) Any ill-omened aspect of the stars, as the conjunc-<BR>tion of the sun or Budha with the moon in its last quarter.<BR>	 2.<BR>Rāhu.<BR>	 3. Saturn.<BR>	 4. Mars.<BR> E. पाप, and ग्रह asterism.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=443-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पापघ्न|पापघ्नः
पापघ्न mfn. (-घ्नः-घ्नी-घ्नं) Removing sin.<BR> E. पाप, and घ्न destructive; or पापं<BR>हन्ति हन-टक् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=443-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पापचक
पापचक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Who or what matures or cooks often or<BR>much.<BR> E. पच् to cook, &c. frequent. v. ण्वुल् aff.; also पापाचक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=443-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पापचर्य्य|पापचर्य|पापचर्यः
पापचर्य्य m. (-र्य्यः)<BR>	 1. A sinner.<BR>	 2. A fiend, a Rākshasa.<BR> E. पाप, and चर्य्या<BR>practice, or चर्य्य to be gone (in or by.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=443-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पापचेतस्
पापचेतस् mfn. (-ताः-ता-त) Wicked, vile.<BR> E. पाप, and चेतस्र् understanding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=443-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पापचेली
पापचेली f. (-ली) A plant, commonly Ākanādi, (Cissampelos hexandra.)<BR>E. पच् to ripen, reiterated पापच, (rheumatism,) ईर् to dissipate,<BR>affs. अच् and ङीप्, and र changed to ल; also with कन् added in the<BR>fem. form पापचेलिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=443-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पापति
पापति mfn. (-तिः-तिः-ति) Who or what alights, goes or falls much or<BR>frequently.<BR> E. पत् to alight, &c. frequent. v., किन् aff. or पत-यङ्<BR>लुक्-इन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=443-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पापदर्शिन्
पापदर्शिन् mfn. (-र्शी-र्शिनी-र्शि) Malevolent, looking at faults.<BR> E. पाप, and<BR>दर्शिन् who sees.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=443-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पापदृश्वन्
पापदृश्वन् mfn. (-श्वा-श्वा-श्व) Conscious of guilt, knowing an act to be<BR>wicked.<BR> E. पाप, and दृश् to see, क्वनिप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=443-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पापनापित|पापनापितः
पापनापित m. (-तः) A vile, cunning or bad barber.<BR> E. पाप sinful, नापित a barber.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=443-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पापनाशिन्
पापनाशिन् mfn. (-शी-शिनी-शि) Purifying, sin-destroying<BR> E. पाप, and<BR>नाशिन् destroying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=443-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पापनिरति
पापनिरति mfn. (-तिः-तिः-ति) Wicked, villainous, a wretch.<BR>	 f. (-तिः)<BR>Wickedness.<BR> E. पाप, and निरति attachment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=443-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पापपति|पापपतिः
पापपति m. (-तिः) A paramour, a gallant.<BR> E. पाप wicked, and पति<BR>husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=443-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पापपुरुष|पापपुरुषः
पापपुरुष m. (-षः) A personification of all sin, or a male, whose head<BR>is Brāhmanicide, whose arms are theft, whose heart is wine<BR>drinking, &c.<BR> E. पाप, and पुरुष a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=443-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पापबुद्धि
पापबुद्धि mfn. (-द्धिः-द्धिः-द्धि) Evil-minded, wicked.<BR> E. पाप, and बुद्धि<BR>intellect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=443-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पापमति
पापमति mfn. (-तिः-तिः-ति) Of a corrupt mind, depraved.<BR> E. पाप, and<BR>मति mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=443-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पापमुक्त|पापमुक्तः
पापमुक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं) Freed from sin, liberated from all crime. E.<BR>पाप, and मुक्त set free.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=443-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पापभाज्
पापभाज् mfn. (-भाक्) Sinful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=443-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पापयोनि|पापयोनिः
पापयोनि f. (-निः) Birth in some inferior state, as an animal, &c.<BR>as the punishment of sin.<BR> E. पाप, and योनि womb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=443-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पापरोग|पापरोगः
पापरोग m. (-गः) A disease, considered as the punishment of sin in<BR>former life.<BR>	 2. Small box.<BR> E. पाप sin, and रोग disease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=443-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पापर्द्धि
पापर्द्धि f. (-र्द्धिः) Hunting, chase.<BR> E. पाप sin, and ऋर्द्धि thriving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=443-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पापल|पापलं
पापल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Giving or taking sin.<BR>	 n. (-लं) A measure. E.<BR>पाप, and लच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=443-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पापविनिग्रह|पापविनिग्रहः
पापविनिग्रह m. (-हः) Restraining or punishing wickedness.<BR> E. पाप, and<BR>विनिग्रह restraint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=443-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पापशमन
पापशमन mfn. (-नः-नी-नं) Palliating or removing crime.<BR>	 n. (-नं) A sin-<BR>offering.<BR> E. पाप, and शमन appeasing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=443-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पापसम्मित
पापसम्मित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Equal in sin, of like guilt.<BR> E. पाप, and<BR>सम्मित measured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=443-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पापात्मन्
पापात्मन् m. (-त्मा) A sinner, a reprobate, an evil-minded person, a<BR>wretch.<BR> E. पाप, and आत्मन् soul.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=444-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पापानुवसित
पापानुवसित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Addicted to sin.<BR> E. पाप, and अनुवसित<BR>dwelling with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=444-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पापापनुत्ति|पापापनुत्तिः
पापापनुत्ति f. (-त्तिः) Expiation.<BR> E. पाप, and अपनुत्ति removing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=444-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पापाशय
पापाशय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Wicked, sinful,<BR> E. पाप, and आशय abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=444-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पापिन्
पापिन् mfn. (-पी-पिनी-पि) Wicked, sinful, bad, a sinner.<BR> E. पाप, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=444-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पापिष्ठ
पापिष्ठ mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठा-ष्ठ) Very wicked.<BR> E. पाप, and इष्ठन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=444-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पापीयस्
पापीयस् mfn. (-यान्-यसी-यः) Very wicked.<BR> E. पाप, and ईयसुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=444-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाप्मन्
पाप्मन् m. (-मा) Sin, wickedness.<BR> E. पा to preserve (from it,) मनिन्<BR>Unādi aff., deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=444-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पामघ्न|पामघ्नः
पामघ्न m. (-घ्नः) Sulphur.<BR> E. पामन् scab, and घ्न destroying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=444-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पामन्
पामन् nf. (-म-मा) Cutaneous eruption, herpes, scab.<BR> E. पै to dry, aff.<BR>मनिन्. “खोस्पाच्डा” ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=444-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पामन|पामनः
पामन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Diseased with herpes.<BR> E. पामन् herpes, and<BR>न aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=444-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पामर|पामरः
पामर mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>	 1. Wicked, vile, low, base.<BR>	 2. Stupid, an idiot,<BR>fool.<BR>	 3. Poor, helpless.<BR>	 m. (-रः) A fool.<BR> E. पाम scab, and रा to get,<BR>क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=444-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पामरोद्धारा
पामरोद्धारा f. (-रा) A plant: see गुडुची.<BR> E. पामर here said to mean bile,<BR>उद् before, हृ to take away, affs. अण् and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=444-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पामारि|पामारिः
पामारि m. (-रिः) Sulphur.<BR> E. पामा scab, and अरि an enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=444-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाम्प
पाम्प mfn. (-म्पः-म्पी-म्पं) Belonging to the river, (Pampā.)<BR> E. पम्पा, and<BR>अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=444-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाय|पायं
पाय n. (-यं) Water.<BR> E. पा to drink, अच् aff. and युक् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=444-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पायना
पायना f. (-ना) Whetting, sharpening, (as a weapon).<BR> E. पा-णिच् भावे युच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=444-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पायस|पायसः
पायस mfn. (-सः-सी-सं) Made of or from milk or water.<BR>	 mn. (-सः-सं)<BR>1. An oblation of milk, rice, and sugar.<BR>	 2. Turpentine.<BR>	 n. (-सं)<BR>Milk.<BR> E. पयस् milk or water, aff. अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=444-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पायसिक
पायसिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Fond of or relating to a mixture of milk, &c.<BR>E. पायस, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=444-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पायिक|पायिकः
पायिक m. (-कः) A foot-soldier, a footman.<BR> E. पा to cherish, ण्वुल् aff.,<BR>and युक् and इट् augments.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=444-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पायु|पायुः
पायु m. (-युः) The anus.<BR> E. पा to preserve, Unādi aff. उण् and युक<BR>inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=444-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाय्य|पाय्यं
पाय्य mfn. (-य्यः-य्या-य्यं) Low, vile, reprehensible, contemptible.<BR>	 n. (-य्यं)<BR>1. Measure.<BR>	 2. Water.<BR>	 3. Drinking.<BR>	 4. Practice, profession.<BR> E. पा<BR>to drink, ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=444-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार|पारं|पारः
पार r. 10th cl. (पारयति-ते) To accomplish, to finish, to get through or<BR>over. अद० चु० उभ० सक० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=444-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार|पारं|पारः
पार n. (-रं) The further or opposite bank of a river.<BR>	 mn. (-रः-रं) The<BR>end, the extremity, the last.<BR>	 m. (-रः) Quicksilver.<BR>	 f. (-रा) The<BR>name of a river, said to flow from the Pariyatra mountains, or<BR>the centrical and western portion of the Vindhya chain.<BR>	 f. (री)<BR>1. A quantity of water.<BR>	 2. A rope for tying an elephant's feet.<BR>	 3.<BR>A small water jar.<BR>	 4. The pollen of a flower.<BR>	 5. A drinking vessel,<BR>a glass, a cup.<BR>	 6. A milk pail,<BR> E. पर another, ईर् to go to or<BR>towards; or पार to cross over; or प to fill aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=444-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारक|पारकः
पारक mfn. (-कः-का-की-कं)<BR>	 1. What purifies, protects, cherishes, pleases,<BR>&c.<BR>	 2. What enables one to cross, (a river or the world.)<BR>	 3. Ser-<BR>ving, delivering.<BR> E. पॄ to please, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=444-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारक्य|पारक्यं|पारक्यः
पारक्य mfn. (-क्यः-क्या-क्यं)<BR>	 1. An enemy, hostile, inimical.<BR>	 2. Alien,<BR>belonging to another.<BR>	 n. (-क्यं) Pious conduct, doing any thing<BR>for the sake of future happiness.<BR> E. परक or पारक, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=444-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारग|पारगः
पारग mfn. (-गः-गा-गं)<BR>	 1. Crossing, crossing over.<BR>	 2. Going over or<BR>beyond the world.<BR>	 3. Completely familiar or conversant with.<BR>	 4.<BR>Profoundly learned.<BR> E. पार the opposite bank, and ग who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=444-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारगत|पारगतः
पारगत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Crossed.<BR>	 2. Gone over the world, pure, holy.<BR>m. (-तः) A Jina or Jaina deified teacher.<BR> E. पार the further bank,<BR>(of the world,) and गत attained, gone to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=444-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारग्रामिक
पारग्रामिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Hostile, inimical.<BR> E. पर an enemy, ग्राम a<BR>number, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=444-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारज्
पारज् m. (-रक्) Gold.<BR> E. प to satisfy, Unādi aff. अजि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=444-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारजायिक|पारजायिकः
पारजायिक m. (-कः) An adulterer.<BR> E. पर another जाया wife, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=444-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारटीट|पारटीटः
पारटीट(न) m. (-टः or नः) A stone, a rock.<BR> E. पर across, and टीट aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=444-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारण|पारणं|पारणः
पारण m. (-णः)<BR>	 1. A cloud.<BR>	 nf. (-णं-णा)<BR>	 1. Eating or drinking after a fast,<BR>breaking a fast.<BR>	 2. Satisfying, satisfaction.<BR>	 3. Accomplishing.<BR>4. Reading through.<BR>	 5. Carrying across.<BR>	 6. Saving.<BR> E. पॄ to<BR>satisfy, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=444-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारत|पारतः
पारत(द) m. (-तः or दः) Quicksilver.<BR> E. पार fulness, (from पॄ to please,)<BR>and तन् to spread or diffuse, aff. ड, also पारद.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=444-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारतन्त्र्य|पारतंत्र्य|पारतंत्र्यं|पारतन्त्र्यं
पारतन्त्र्य n. (न्त्र्यं) Subservience, slavery, dependence.<BR> E. परतन्त्र depen-<BR>dent, aff. ष्यञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=444-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारत्रिक|पारत्रिकं
पारत्रिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Relating to the next world.<BR> E. परत्र, and<BR>ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=444-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारत्र्य|पारत्र्यं
पारत्र्य n. (-त्र्यं) Reward in a future state.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=444-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारद|पारदः
पारद(त) m. (-दः or तः) Quicksilver.<BR> E. पार as in पारत, and द what<BR>gives, from दा with क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=444-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारदण्डक|पारदण्डकः
पारदण्डक m. (-कः) The name of a country, a part of Orissa.<BR> E. पार be-<BR>yond, दण्डक the Dandaka forest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=444-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारदारिक|पारदारिकः
पारदारिक m. (-कः) An adulterer.<BR> E. पर another, दार wife, aff. ठक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=444-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारदार्य्य|पारदार्य|पारदार्यं
पारदार्य्य n. (-र्य्यं) Adultery.<BR> E. पर another, दार a wife, ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=444-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारदेशिक|पारदेशिकः
पारदेशिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Foreign, abroad.<BR>	 m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A traveller.<BR>2. A foreigner.<BR> E. परदेश, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=444-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारदेश्य|पारदेश्यः
पारदेश्य mfn. (-श्यः-श्यी-श्यं) Belonging to another country.<BR>	 m. (-श्यः)<BR>	 1.<BR>A traveller, one gone to a foreign country.<BR>	 2. A foreigner.<BR> E. पर<BR>another, देश country, ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=444-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारदृश्वन्
पारदृश्वन् mfn. (-श्वा-श्वा-श्व) Long-sighted, far-seeing, wise.<BR> E. पार, and<BR>दृश् to see, क्वनिप् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=444-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारधेनु|पारधेनुः
पारधेनु m. (-नुः) A particular and low cast, the Ayogava. Also, पारधेनुक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=444-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारभृत|पारभृतं
पारभृत n. (-तं) A present, an offering.<BR> E. पर, भृत prepared, अण् aff. Ac-<BR>cording to some it is a misreading of प्राभृत ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=444-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारभृतीय
पारभृतीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Belonging or relating to a present.<BR> E. पारमृत,<BR>and छ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=444-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारमहंस्य|पारमहंस्यं
पारमहंस्य n. (-स्यं) Most sublime asceticism.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=444-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारमार्थिक|पारमार्थिकः
पारमार्थिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>	 1. Preferable, best, most desirable.<BR>	 2. Re-<BR>lating to the spiritual knowledge.<BR>	 3. Real, true, existing.<BR>	 4.<BR>Loving truth.<BR> E. पारमार्थ chief object, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=444-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारमिक
पारमिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Supreme, chief, best.<BR> E. परम best, ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=444-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारमित
पारमित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Crossed, traversed.<BR>	 2. Transcendant, (as<BR>spiritual knowledge.)<BR> E. पारम् across, and इत gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=444-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारम्पर्य्य|पारम्पर्य|पारंपर्य|पारंपर्यं|पारम्पर्य्यं
पारम्पर्य्य n. (-र्य्यं)<BR>	 1. Traditional instruction, tradition.<BR>	 2. Continueous<BR>order or succession.<BR> E. परम्पर from one to another, aff. ष्यञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=444-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारम्पर्य्योपदेश|पारम्पर्योपदेश|पारंपर्योपदेश|पारंपर्योपदेशः|पारम्पर्य्योपदेशः
पारम्पर्य्योपदेश m. (-शः) Traditional instruction.<BR> E. पारम्पर्य्य, and उपदेश<BR>instruction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=444-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारय
पारय mfn. (यः-या-यं)<BR>	 1. Able, adequate, fit for.<BR>	 2. Satisfying.<BR> E. प to satisfy, श aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=444-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारयत्
पारयत् mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्)<BR>	 1. Satisfying, filling.<BR>	 2. Being able or com-<BR>petent to.<BR>	 3. Being alive, living.<BR> E. पॄ to satisfy, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=444-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारयिष्णु
पारयिष्णु mfn. (-ष्णुः-ष्णुः-ष्णु) Gratifying, pleasing, satisfying.<BR> E. पॄ<BR>to please, causal. v. इष्णु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=444-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारलौकिक
पारलौकिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Belonging or relating to the next world.<BR>E. परलोक another world, aff. ठक्, and both vowels changed by<BR>special rule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=444-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारवत|पारवतः
पारवत m. (-तः) A pigeon. See पारावत.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=444-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारशव|पारशवः
पारशव mfn. (-वः-वी-वं)<BR>	 1. Made or derived from an axe.<BR>	 2. Made of<BR>iron.<BR>	 m. (वः)<BR>	 1. The son of a Śūdra woman by a Brāhman.<BR>2. A son by another's wife, an adulterine, a bastard.<BR>	 3. An iron<BR>weapon.<BR> E. पर another, शव् to go, अच् aff. and अण् implying<BR>descent, added; or पार crossing, शव a corpse, a living corpse;<BR>or परशु an axe, aff. अञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=444-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारशीक|पारशीकः
पारशीक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. Persia.<BR>	 2. A native of Persia.<BR>	 3. A Persian horse.<BR>also पारसीक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=445-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारश्वध|पारश्वधः
पारश्वध m. (-धः) One armed with an axe, a hatchet-man, a pioneer,<BR>&c.<BR> E. परश्वध an axe, aff. अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=445-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारश्वधिक|पारश्वधिकः
पारश्वधिक m. (-कः) A soldier, or any other man armed with an axe. E.<BR>परश्वध an axe, ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=445-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारश्वय
पारश्वय m. (-यः) Gold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=445-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारसिक|पारसिकः
पारसिक m. (-कः) Persia; plu. The Persians also पारसीक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=445-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारसीक|पारसीकः
पारसीक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. The kingdom of Persia.<BR>	 2. A Persian, an inhabi-<BR>tant of Persia.<BR>	 3. A Persian horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=445-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारस्त्रैणेय|पारस्त्रैणेयः
पारस्त्रैणेय m. (-यः) An adulterine, the son of another's wife.<BR> E. पर<BR>another, स्त्री woman, ढञ् aff. of descent, and इणङ् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=445-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारा
पारा f. (-रा) Name of a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=445-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारापत|पारापतः
पारापत m. (-तः) A pigeon; also पारावत.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=445-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारापा
पारापा(वा)र m. (-रः) The ocean.<BR>	 n. (-रं) The two banks of a river. E.<BR>पार the further bank, and अपार near bank.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=445-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारायण|पारायणं
पारायण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Totality, entireness, completeness.<BR>	 2. Going over,<BR>reading or doing any thing completely.<BR>	 3. Going across.<BR>	 4. Reading<BR>a Purāna, or causing it to be read.<BR>	 f. (-णी)<BR>	 1. The goddess SARA-<BR>SWATĪ.<BR>	 2. Action, act.<BR>	 3. Considering, meditating.<BR>	 4. Light.<BR> E. पार<BR>the boundary or limit, and अयन going to, extending: when used<BR>attributively it remains always neuter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=445-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारायणिक|पारायणिकः
पारायणिक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A pupil, a scholar.<BR>	 2. A lecturer, a reader of<BR>the Purānas.<BR> E. पारायण reading through, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=445-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारारुक|पारारुकः
पारारुक m. (-कः) A rock.<BR> E. पार the further bank, ऋ to go to, aff.<BR>डकञ्. Also पारारुप ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=445-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारावत|पारावतः
पारावत m. (-तः)<BR>	 1. A dove, a pigeon.<BR>	 2. A monkey.<BR>	 3. A sort of ebony,<BR>(Diospyros glutinosa.)<BR>	 4. A mountain.<BR>	 f. (-ती)<BR>	 1. The name of a<BR>river in the peninsula.<BR>	 2. The fruit of the Annona reticulata.<BR>	 3.<BR>A form of song, peculiar to the cowherds.<BR> E. पर another, (life,<BR>&c.) अव् to go, to preserve, शतृ participial aff., and अण् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=445-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारावतपदी
पारावतपदी f. (-दी) Heart-pea: see पारावताङ्घ्रि । काकजङ्घायाम्च ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=445-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारावताङ्घ्रि|पारावतांघ्रि|पारावताङ्घ्रिः
पारावताङ्घ्रि f. (-ङ्घ्रि) Heart-pea, (Cardiospermum haliacacabum.) E.<BR>पारावत a pigeon, अङ्घ्रि a foot, the root being compared to a<BR>pigeon's foot; also similar compounds, as पारावतपदी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=445-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारावताङ्घ्रिपिच्छ|पारावताङ्घ्रिपिच्छः
पारावताङ्घ्रिपिच्छ m. (-च्छः) A pigeon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=445-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारावार|पारावारं|पारावारः
पारावार m. (-रः) The ocean.<BR>	 n. (-रं) The near and opposite banks of<BR>a stream.<BR> E. पार the further bank, वृ to surround, with आङ् pre-<BR>fix, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=445-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारावारीण|पारावारीणः
पारावारीण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>	 1. On both sides of a river, &c.<BR>	 2. One who<BR>goes to both sides.<BR> E. पार the opposite side, अवार this side,<BR>aff. खञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=445-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाराशर|पाराशरं|पाराशरः
पाराशर m. (-रः) A name of the poet VYĀSA.<BR>	 n. (-रं) The rules of<BR>PARĀSARA, or VYĀSA, the conduct of the mendicant orders. E.<BR>पराशर, and अण् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=445-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाराशरकल्पिक|पाराशरकल्पिकः
पाराशरकल्पिक m. (-कः) A follower of PARĀSARA, the institutor of<BR>rules for the mendicant order.<BR> E. पराशर the sage, कल्प aff., and<BR>ठक् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=445-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाराशरि|पाराशरिः
पाराशरि m. (-रिः)<BR>	 1. VYĀSA.<BR>	 2. An epithet of Sūkra.<BR> E. पराशर, and इञ् patronymic aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=445-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाराशरिन्
पाराशरिन् m. (-री)<BR>	 1. A recluse. Plu. The religious mendicant or<BR>Brāhman, who having passed through the three stages of<BR>student, house-holder, and ascetic leads a vagrant life, and<BR>subsists upon alms; or the class of ascetics who study the Shā-<BR>riraka Sutra of Vyāsa.<BR> E. पाराशर्य्य VYĀSA, the author of the rules<BR>of this order, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=445-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाराशर्य्य|पाराशर्य|पाराशर्यः|पाराशर्य्यः
पाराशर्य्य m. (-र्य्यः) The poet VYĀSA.<BR> E. पाराशर the father of the poet,<BR>and यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=445-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिकाङ्क्षिन्|पारिकांक्षिन्
पारिकाङ्क्षिन् m. (-ङ्क्षी)<BR>	 1. An ascetic, one who devotes his days to<BR>devout contemplation.<BR>	 2. The religious mendicant.<BR> E. परि imply-<BR>ing secession, (abandoning worldly wishes,) काङ्क्षि to desire,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=445-b" target="_blank">Page445-b+ 60</a>]<BR>and णिनि aff.; or पारि derived from पर, supreme felicity, and<BR>काङ्क्षिन् who desires.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=445-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिखेय
पारिखेय f. (-यीः) Surrounded by a ditch.<BR> E. परिखा, affix, ढक् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=445-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिजात|पारिजातः
पारिजात m. (-तः)<BR>	 1. Name of one of the five trees of paradise sup-<BR>posed to have been produced at the churning of the ocean.<BR>	 2.<BR>The coral tree, (Erythrina fulgens.)<BR> E. पारि said to mean, above,<BR>and जात produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=445-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिजातक|पारिजातकः
पारिजातक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A tree of paradise.<BR>	 2. The coral tree.<BR> E. कन्<BR>added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=445-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिणाय्य|पारिणाय्यं
पारिणाय्य mfn. (य्यः-य्यी-य्यं) Belonging to specifically or peculiarly.<BR>	 n.<BR>(-य्यं) Property received at the time of marriage by a woman.<BR>	 f.<BR>(य्यी)<BR>	 1. Relating to marriage.<BR> E. परि about, around, णी to get,<BR>aff. ष्यञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=445-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिणाह्य|पारिणाह्यं
पारिणाह्य n. (-ह्यं) Household furniture and utensils.<BR> E. परिणाह, and<BR>ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=445-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारितथ्या
पारितथ्या f. (-थ्या) A trinket worn on the forehead, where the hair<BR>is parted; or a string of pearls for binding the hair.<BR> E. परि every<BR>way (splendid), तथा there, ष्यञ् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=445-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारितोषिक|पारितोषिकं
पारितोषिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Delighting, making happy.<BR>	 n. (-कं) A<BR>reward, a gratuity.<BR> E. परितोष satisfaction, ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=445-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिध्वजिक|पारिध्वजिकः
पारिध्वजिक m. (-कः) A standard-bearer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=445-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिन्द्र|पारिंद्र|पारिंद्रः|पारिन्द्रः
पारिन्द्र m. (-न्द्रः) A lion: see परिन्द्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=445-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिपन्थिक|पारिपंथिक|पारिपंथिकः|पारिपन्थिकः
पारिपन्थिक m. (-कः) A robber, a thief, a highwayman.<BR> E. परि around,<BR>पथिन् the road, aff. ठक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=445-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिपाठ्य
पारिपाठ्य n. (-ठ्यं) Regularity, methodicalness, successiveness.<BR> E. परि-<BR>पाटी orderly course, ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=445-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिपात्र|पारिपात्रं|पारिपात्रः
पारिपात्र m. (-त्रः) The name of a mountain, apparently the centrical or<BR>western portion of the “Vindhya” chain, which skirts the province<BR>of Mālwā.<BR> E. परि every way, पा to cherish, ष्ट्रन् aff.; or with कन्<BR>added, पारिपात्रक; also read पारियात्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=445-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिपात्रक
पारिपात्रक m. (-कः) A mountain so called: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=445-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिपार्श्विक|पारिपार्श्विकः
पारिपार्श्विक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. An actor, who serves as a sort of chorus to<BR>the drama, and is one of the interlocutors in the prologue.<BR>	 2. An<BR>attendant.<BR> E. परि about, पार्श्व the side, (of the manager, &c.) aff.<BR>ठक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=445-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिपार्श्विका
पारिपार्श्विका f. (-का) A chamber-maid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=445-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिप्लव|पारिप्लवं|पारिप्लवः
पारिप्लव mfn. (-वः-वा-वं)<BR>	 1. Perturbed, troubled in mind.<BR>	 2. Trembling,<BR>tremulous, unsteady.<BR>	 3. Swimming, floating.<BR>	 m. (-वः) A boat. E.<BR>परिप्लव, and अण् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=445-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिप्लाव्य|पारिप्लाव्यः
पारिप्लाव्य m. (-व्यः) A goose.<BR>	 n. (-व्यं)<BR>	 1. Perplexity, agitation.<BR>	 2. Tre-<BR>mulousness.<BR> E. परिप्लव, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=445-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिवर्ह
पारिवर्ह m. (-र्हः) A wedding present.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=445-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिभद्र|पारिभद्रः
पारिभद्र m. (-द्रः)<BR>	 1. The coral tree, (Erythrina fulgens.)<BR>	 2. The Nimba<BR>tree.<BR>	 3. A sort of pine, (Pinus Devadāru.)<BR>	 4. The Sarala, also a<BR>sort of pine, (P. longifolia.)<BR> E. परि completely, भद्र auspicious, aff.<BR>अण्; also with कन् added, पारिभद्रक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=445-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिभाव्य|पारिभाव्यं
पारिभाव्य n. (-व्यं)<BR>	 1. Surety, security, bail.<BR>	 2. A drug, a sort of cos-<BR>tus, (C. speciosus.)<BR> E. परिभू a surety, or परिभव overcoming, (dis-<BR>ease) aff. ष्यञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=445-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिभाषिक|पारिभाषिकं
पारिभाषिक f. (-की)<BR>	 1. Current, common, universally received 2. Techni-<BR>cal, (as a word.)<BR> E. परिभाषा, and ठञ् affix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=445-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिमाण्डल्य|पारिमांडल्य|पारिमांडल्यं|पारिमाण्डल्यं
पारिमाण्डल्य n. (-ल्यं) An atom, as a measure of space, a mote in a sun<BR>beam.<BR> E. परिमण्डल a ball, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=445-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिमुखिक|पारिमुखिकः
पारिमुखिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Present, before or about the face.<BR> E. परि<BR>about, मुख the face, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=445-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिमुख्य|पारिमुख्यं
पारिमुख्य n. (-ख्यं) Presence, being before the face.<BR> E. परिमुख, and ष्यञ्<BR>aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=445-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारियात्र|पारियात्रः
पारियात्र m. (-त्रः) The name of one of the seven principal mountains:<BR>see पारिपात्र, also with कन् added, पारियात्रक, or with ठक aff.<BR>पारियात्रिक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=445-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारियानिक|पारियानिकः
पारियानिक m. (-कः) A travelling cart or carriage.<BR> E. पारि every way,<BR>यान going, aff. ठक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=446-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिरक्षक|पारिरक्षकः
पारिरक्षक m. (-कः) An ascetic or religious mendicant.<BR> E. पारि said<BR>to mean, future happiness, from परि and रक्षक who preserves.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=446-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिश|पारिशः
पारिश m. (-शः) A tree: see गर्द्धभाण्ड । पलाशपिपुल ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=446-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिशेष्य|पारिशेष्यं
पारिशेष्य n. (-यं) That which is left, remainder. [CDSL change from pAriSIla]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=446-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिषद|पारिषदः
पारिषद mfn. (-दः-दी-दं) Belonging or relating to an assembly.<BR>	 m. (-दः)<BR>1. A spectator, a person present at an assembly or congregation.<BR>2. A king's companion. plu. The retinue of a god.<BR> E. परिषद् an<BR>assembly, aff. अण्; or with ण्य aff. पारिषद्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=446-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिषद्य|पारिषद्यः
पारिषद्य m. (-द्यः) A spectator: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=446-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिहारिक|पारिहारिकः
पारिहारिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>	 1. Taking away, seizing.<BR>	 2. Surrounding.<BR>m. (-कः) A maker of garlands.<BR>	 f. (-की) A kind of riddle.<BR> E. परिहार<BR>seizure, ठक aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=446-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिहार्य्य|पारिहार्य|पारिहार्यः|पारिहार्य्यः
पारिहार्य्य m. (-र्य्यः) A bracelet.<BR>	 n. (-र्य्यं) Taking, seizure.<BR> E. परिहार,<BR>and ष्यञ् aff. also परिहार्य्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=446-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिहास्य|पारिहास्यं
पारिहास्य n. (-स्यं) Jest, joke, fun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=446-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारी
पारी f. (-री)<BR>	 1. A rope for tying an elephant's feet.<BR>	 2. A quantity of<BR>water.<BR>	 3. A drinking cup.<BR>	 4. A milk-pail.<BR> E. पा + क्किप्-रा-क-ङीष् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=446-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारीक्षित|पारीक्षितः
पारीक्षित m. (-तः)<BR>	 1. The name of a sovereign, to whom the Sri-Bhā-<BR>gavat, or life of KṚṢṆA, is supposed to have been addressed.<BR>2. The successor of the preceding; also JANAMEJAYA.<BR> E. परीक्षित्<BR>the king so called, and अण् pleonasm or patronymic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=446-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारीण|पारीणः
पारीण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>	 1. On the opposite side.<BR>	 2. Who goes or crosses<BR>to the other side.<BR>	 3. Completely versed in.<BR> E. पार the other side,<BR>aff. खञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=446-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारीणह्य|पारीणह्यं
पारीणह्य n. (-ह्यं) Household furniture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=446-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारीन्द्र|पारींद्र|पारींद्रः|पारीन्द्रः
पारीन्द्र m. (-न्द्रः)<BR>	 1. A lion.<BR>	 2. A large snake, (Boa.)<BR> E. पर another,<BR>(animal,) and इन्द्र lord, form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=446-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारीरण|पारीरणः
पारीरण m. (-णः)<BR>	 1. A tortoise.<BR>	 2. A stick, a staff. पार्य्यां रणति, रण + अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=446-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारु|पारुः
पारु m. (-रुः)<BR>	 1. The sun.<BR>	 2. Fire.<BR> E. पा or nourish, Unādi aff. रु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=446-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारुष्य|पारुष्यं|पारुष्यः
पारुष्य n. (-ष्यं)<BR>	 1. Abuse, reproach, scurrilous, opprobrious or un-<BR>friendly speech.<BR>	 2. The property of harshness, &c. in speaking.<BR>3. The forest or grove of INDRA.<BR>	 4. Aloe wood or Agallochum.<BR>5. Severity, violence, either in word or deed, as वाक्षारुष्यं defama-<BR>tion, abuse, or violence words, and दण्डपारुष्यं personal injury,<BR>assault or violence of blows.<BR>	 m. (-ष्यः) A name of VṚHASPATI. E.<BR>परुष harsh, contumelious, &c. aff. ष्यञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=446-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारेरक|पारेरकः
पारेरक m. (-कः) A sword, a scimitar.<BR> E. पार collectively, foes, from<BR>पर an enemy, ईर् to penetrate, aff. वुन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=446-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारोरर्य्य
पारोरर्य्य n. (-र्य्यं) Tradition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=446-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्घट|पार्घटं
पार्घट n. (-टं)<BR>	 1. Ashes.<BR>	 2. Dust.<BR> E. पार from पर another, घट् to<BR>endeavour, aff. अच्, and the final vowel of पार rejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=446-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्जन्य
पार्जन्य f. (-न्या) Belonging to rain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=446-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्ण|पार्णः
पार्ण f. (-र्णी) Relating to leaves.<BR>	 2. Raised from leaves (as a tax.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=446-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्थ|पार्थः
पार्थ m. (-र्थः)<BR>	 1. A king, a prince.<BR>	 2. A name of the Pāndu prince<BR>ARJUNA.<BR>	 3. A name of KĀRTAVĪRYA.<BR>	 4. A tree, (Pentaptera<BR>arjuna.)<BR> E. पृथा a proper name, अण् aff. of descent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=446-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्थक्य|पार्थक्यं
पार्थक्य n. (-क्यं) Severalty, individuality, difference.<BR> E. पृथक् separate,<BR>ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=446-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्थव|पार्थवं
पार्थव n. (-वं) Greatness, immensity.<BR> E. पृथु great, अण् aff.; also पृथुता,<BR>पृथुत्व, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=446-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्थिव|पार्थिवं|पार्थिवः
पार्थिव mfn. (-वः-वा or वी-वं)<BR>	 1. Earthen, made or derived from<BR>earth.<BR>	 2. Ruling or possessing the earth.<BR>	 3. Princely, royal.<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. A king, a prince.<BR>	 2. An earthen vessel.<BR>	 3. An inhabi-<BR>tant of the earth.<BR>	 f. (-वी)<BR>	 1. A name of ŚITA.<BR>	 2. An epithet of<BR>Lakshmi.<BR> E. पृथिवी the earth, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=446-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्पर|पार्परः
पार्पर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A name of YAMA.<BR>	 2. Consumption.<BR>	 3. A handful<BR>of rice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=446-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्य्यन्तिक|पार्यन्तिक|पार्यंतिक
पार्य्यन्तिक f. (-की) Final, conclusive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=446-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्व्व|पार्व
पार्व्व mfn. (-र्व्वः-र्व्वी-र्व्वं) Relating to a Parva, a particular day of the<BR>month, &c.<BR> E. पर्व्वन्, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=446-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्व्वण|पार्वण|पार्व्वणः
पार्व्वण mfn. (-णः-णी-णं)<BR>	 m. (-णः) A sort of deer.<BR>	 n. (-णं) The gene-<BR>ral funeral ceremony to be offered to all the manes at the<BR>Parva, or conjunction of the sun and moon, at which double<BR>oblations are offered; three cakes to the father, paternal grand-<BR>father, and great grandfather; and three to the maternal grand-<BR>father, his father, and grandfather; and the crumbs of each set<BR>to the remoter ancestors in each line.<BR>	 f. (-णी)<BR>	 1. Belonging or<BR>relating to a Parvan.<BR>	 2. Waxing, increasing.<BR> E. पर्व्व a knot, &c.<BR>aff. अण् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=446-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्व्वत|पार्वत|पार्व्वतः
पार्व्वत mfn. (-तः-ती-तं) Mountain, produced in the mountains.<BR>m. (-तः) A tree called the large Nīmb, (Melia sempervirens.)<BR>f. (-ती)<BR>	 1. A name of DURGĀ, in her capacity of daughter of<BR>HIMĀLAYA, the sovereign of the snowy mountains.<BR>	 2. DRAUPADĪ<BR>the wife of the Pāṇḍu princes.<BR>	 3. A female cowherd or Gopī.<BR>4. The olibanum tree, (Boswellia thurifera.)<BR>	 5. Another tree,<BR>(Celtis orientalis.)<BR>	 6. A red clay, commonly called Saurāshtri,<BR>or Surat earth.<BR>	 7. A name applied to several rivers.<BR> E. पर्व्वत a<BR>mountain, अण् aff. of descent or relation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=446-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्व्वतीनन्दन|पार्वतीनन्दन|पार्वतीनंदन|पार्वतीनन्दनः|पार्व्वतीनन्दनः
पार्व्वतीनन्दन m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. A name of KĀRTTIKEYA.<BR>	 2. A name of GANE-<BR>ŚHA.<BR> E. पार्व्वती the goddess, and नन्दन a son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=446-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्व्वतीय|पार्वतीय|पार्वतीयः
पार्व्वतीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Mountain, mountaineer.<BR>	 m. plu. Name of a<BR>mountain tribe.<BR> E. पर्व्वतीय, and अण् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=446-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्व्वतेय|पार्वतेय|पार्व्वतेयं|पार्व्वतेयः
पार्व्वतेय mfn. (-यः-यी-यं) Mountain or mountain-born, &c.<BR>	 n. (-यं)<BR>	 1.<BR>Antimony.<BR>	 2. A plant bearing a pungent fruit.<BR> E. पर्व्वत a moun-<BR>tain, and ढक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=446-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्व्वायनान्तीय|पार्वायनान्तीय
पार्व्वायनान्तीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Occurring at the end of a Parva or a<BR>solstice, (a sacrifice, &c.)<BR> E. पर्व्व, and अयन solstice, अन्त end,<BR>छण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=446-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्शव|पार्शवः
पार्शव m. (-वः) A warrior armed with an axe.<BR> E. पर्शु an axe, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=446-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्श्व|पार्श्वं|पार्श्वः
पार्श्व mfn. (-र्श्वः-र्श्वा-र्श्वं) Near, proximate, by the side of.<BR>	 mn. (-र्श्वः-र्श्वं)<BR>1. A side, the part of the body below the armpit.<BR>	 2. The curve<BR>or circumference of a wheel.<BR>	 3. Side of any square figure.<BR>	 n. (-र्श्वं)<BR>1. A multitude of ribs, the thorax.<BR>	 2. A fraudulent or crooked<BR>expedient.<BR>	 m. (-र्श्वः) The twenty-third Jina or Jaina pontiff. E.<BR>स्पृश् to touch, श्वण् Unādi aff., and पृ substituted for the root; or<BR>पर्शु a rib, aff. अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=446-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाश्वक
पाश्वक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A pilferer, a swindler, any one who seeks wealth or<BR>other objects, by dishonest or indirect means.<BR>	 2. A rib.<BR> E. पार्श्व<BR>a dishonest means, a side, and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=446-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्श्वगत
पार्श्वगत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Close to, beside.<BR> E. पार्श्व, and गत gone to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=446-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्श्वतस्
पार्श्वतस् ind. By or from the side of, &c.<BR> E. पार्श्व the side, and तसिल्<BR>aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=446-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्श्वतीय|पार्श्वतीयः
पार्श्वतीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Belonging to the side of.<BR> E. पार्श्वतस्, and छ<BR>aff.; the final अस् rejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=446-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्श्वपरिवर्त्तन|पार्श्वपरिवर्तन|पार्श्वपरिवर्त्तनं
पार्श्वपरिवर्त्तन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Turning round from one side to the other in a<BR>bed.<BR>	 2. A festival held in the eleventh day of the first half of<BR>Bhādra when VIṢṆU is supposed to turn upon the other side in<BR>his sleep.<BR> E. पार्श्व, and परिवर्त्तन turning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=446-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्श्वभाग|पार्श्वभागः
पार्श्वभाग m. (-गः) The side, the flank.<BR> E. पार्श्व the side, and माग part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=446-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्श्वशय
पार्श्वशय mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>	 1. Sleeping on.<BR>	 2. Sleeping beside the side. E.<BR>पार्श्व, and शी to sleep, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=446-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्श्वशूल|पार्श्वशूलः
पार्श्वशूल n. (-लं) Spasm of the chest, stitch.<BR> E. पार्श्व, and शूल sharp pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=446-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्श्वस्थ|पार्श्वस्थः
पार्श्वस्थ mfn. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थ्यं) Staying near or close to, or at the side.<BR>	 m.<BR>(स्थः)<BR>	 1. A sort of chorus to the Indian drama, an actor in the<BR>prelude, and interpreter of the plot.<BR>	 2. An associate, a compa-<BR>nion,<BR> E. पार्श्व the side, (of the manager, &c.) स्थ who stays.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=446-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्श्वाचान्त
पार्श्वाचान्त n. (-न्तं) Food not to be taken after one of the party has<BR>washed his mouth.<BR> E. पार्श्व, and आचान्त sipped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=446-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्श्वास्थि|पार्श्वास्थिः
पार्श्वास्थि n. (-स्थि) A rib.<BR> E. पार्श्व the side, and अस्थि a bone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=447-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्श्विक|पार्श्विकं|पार्श्विकः
पार्श्विक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Lateral, belonging to the side, &c.<BR>	 m. (-कः)<BR>	 1.<BR>A juggler.<BR>	 2. A partisan, a sidesman, an associate or companion.<BR>E. पार्श्व the side, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=447-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्श्वोदरप्रिय|पार्श्वोदरप्रियः
पार्श्वोदरप्रिय m. (-यः) A crab.<BR> E. पार्श्व the side, उदर the belly, and प्रिय fond of; going sidelong.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=447-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्षत|पार्षतः
पार्षत m. (-तः) A Pāṇḍu prince.<BR>	 f. (-ती)<BR>	 1. A name of DRAUPADĪ.<BR>2. Belonging to the spotted antelope.<BR>	 3. An epithet of DURGĀ.<BR>E. पृषत the name of a king, अण् aff. of descent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=447-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्षद|पार्षदः
पार्षद m. (-दः)<BR>	 1. A spectator, a person present in a congregation or<BR>assembly.<BR>	 2. A companion, an attendant.<BR>	 3. A retinue, a train.<BR>E. पर्षद an assembly, अण् aff.; also with ण्य aff., पार्षद्यः or derived<BR>from परिषद, पारिषद.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=447-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्ष्णि|पार्ष्णिः
पार्ष्णि mf. (-र्ष्णिः)<BR>	 1. The heel.<BR>	 2. The rear of an army.<BR>	 3. The back.<BR>4. Enquiry, asking.<BR>	 5. A kick.<BR>	 f. (-र्ष्णिः)<BR>	 1. A violent or licen-<BR>tious woman, one intoxicated literally or figuratively, &c.<BR>	 2. A<BR>name of KUNTĪ the mother of YUDHIṢṬHIRA.<BR> E. पृष् to sprin-<BR>kle, &c. Unādi aff. नि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=447-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्ष्णिग्राह|पार्ष्णिग्राहः
पार्ष्णिग्राह m. (-हः)<BR>	 1. An enemy in the rear.<BR>	 2. A commander in<BR>the rear of his army or reserve.<BR>	 3. An ally who supports a<BR>prince.<BR> E. पार्ष्णि the rear, and ग्राह who takes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=447-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्ष्णिवाह|पार्ष्णिवाहः
पार्ष्णिवाह m. (-हः) An outside horse.<BR> E. पार्ष्णि, वह to bear, aff. अण् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=447-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्ष्णित्र|पार्ष्णित्रं
पार्ष्णित्र n. (-त्रं) A reserve, a body of forces in the rear.<BR> E. पार्ष्णि the<BR>rear, and त्रा to preserve, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=447-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाल|पालः
पाल r. 1st and 10th cls. (पालयति-ते) To guard, to preserve or<BR>protect. चु० उभ० सक-सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=447-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाल|पालः
पाल mfn. (-लः-ली-लं) Who or what guards or preserves.<BR>	 m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. A<BR>nourisher, a protector.<BR>	 2. A spitting-pot.<BR>	 3. A herdsman.<BR>	 4. A<BR>king.<BR>	 f. (-ली)<BR>	 1. The sharp edge of a sword.<BR>	 2. A woman with a<BR>beard.<BR>	 3. A louse.<BR>	 4. A line, a row or range.<BR>	 5. A pot, a boiler.<BR>E. पाल् to nourish, aff. अच्; ङीष् added; also with इ aff. पालि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=447-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पालक|पालकः
पालक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Who or what protects, nourishes, &c.<BR>	 m. (-कः)<BR>1. A horse-keeper, a groom.<BR>	 2. A cherisher, a protector, a guar-<BR>dian.<BR>	 3. A prince.<BR>	 4. A horse.<BR>	 5. The chitraka tree.<BR> E. पाल् to<BR>nourish, aff. ण्वुल् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=447-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पालकाव्य
पालकाव्य m. (-व्यः) A name of a Muni or saint, a form of the divine<BR>physician DHANWANTARI, who promulgated the science of<BR>elephants.<BR>	 n. (व्यं) The science of elephants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=447-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पालघ्न|पालघ्नः
पालघ्न m. (-घ्नः) A mushroom.<BR> E. पाल earth, derived from पाल् to<BR>nourish, and ध्न destructive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=447-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पालङ्क|पालंकः|पालङ्कः
पालङ्क m. (-ङ्कः)<BR>	 1. The olibanum tree, (Boswellia thurifera.)<BR>	 2. A sort<BR>of beet root, (Peta bengalensis.)<BR>	 3. A hawk.<BR>	 f. (-ङ्की) Incense, the<BR>resin of the olibanum; also पालङ्क्या.<BR> E. पाल nourishing, अङ्क what<BR>goes or gives, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=447-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पालङ्क्या
पालङ्क्या f. (-ङ्का) Gum olibanum.<BR> E. पालङ्क the olibanum tree, ष्यञ् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=447-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पालन|पालनं
पालन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Preserving, guarding, protecting, cherishing,<BR>nourishing.<BR>	 2. The milk of a cow that has recently calved.<BR> E. पाल्<BR>to nourish, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=447-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पालयत्
पालयत् mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्) Protecting, cherishing.<BR> E. पाल् to protect, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=447-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पालयितृ
पालयितृ mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ) Protecting, cherishing, a protector, &c. E.<BR>पाल् to nourish, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=447-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पालाश|पालाशं|पालाशः
पालाश mfn. (-शः-शी-शं)<BR>	 1. Of a green colour.<BR>	 2. Belonging to the<BR>Palāsha tree, made of its wood, &c.<BR>	 m. (-शः) Green, (the colour.)<BR>E. पालाश a leaf, or the tree, aff. अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=447-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पालाशखण्ड|पालाशखंड|पालाशखण्डः
पालाशखण्ड m. (-ण्डः) A country in India, the western part of Bihar.<BR>E. पालाश belonging to the Palāsha tree, &c. खण्ड district; aboud-<BR>ing in the Butea frondosa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=447-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पालि|पालिः
पालि(ली) f. (-लिः or लीः)<BR>	 1. The sharp edge of a sword, or any cutting<BR>instrument.<BR>	 2. The tip of the ear.<BR>	 3. A line, a row or range.<BR>	 4. A<BR>mark, a spot, a stain.<BR>	 5. A louse.<BR>	 6. A woman with a beard.<BR>7. A boundary, a limit.<BR>	 8. A raised bank, a causeway, a bridge.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=447-b" target="_blank">Page447-b+ 60</a>]<BR>9. A circumference.<BR>	 10. Maintenance of a scholar during the<BR>period of his studies, by his teacher.<BR>	 11. Praise, eulogium.<BR>	 12.<BR>The hip or haunch.<BR>	 13. A Prastha or measure so called.<BR>	 14.<BR>The lap, the bosom.<BR> E. पाल् to nourish, इण् aff., and in most cases,<BR>ङीप् being optionally added, also पाली: see पाल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=447-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पालिका
पालिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. The sharp edge of a cutting instrument.<BR>	 2. A sort<BR>of ladle or knife for skimming milk, curds, &c.<BR>	 3. The lobe of the<BR>ear.<BR> E. पाली as above, with कन् added; see also पालक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=447-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पालित|पालितः
पालित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Cherished, nourished.<BR>	 m. (-तः) The Sākhota<BR>tree.<BR> E. पाल् nourish aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=447-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पालित्य|पालित्यं
पालित्य n. (-त्यं) Greyness of hair consequent on old age.<BR> E. पलित + ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=447-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पालिन्
पालिन् mfn. (-ली-लिनी-लि) Who or what nourishes or protects.<BR> E. पाल्<BR>to protect, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=447-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पालिन्द|पालिंदः|पालिन्दः
पालिन्द m. (-न्दः) A sort of jasmine, (J. pubescens.)<BR>	 f. (-न्दी) Teori; see<BR>the next.<BR> E. पाल् to nourish, (the bee,) aff. किन्दच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=447-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पालिन्धी
पालिन्धी f. (-न्धी) A plant, commonly Teori, (Convolvulus turpethum,)<BR>the black sort. E. See the last, aff. किन्धच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=447-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पावक|पावकः
पावक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Who or what renders pure, a purifier, purifica-<BR>tory.<BR>	 m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. fire, or its deified personification.<BR>	 2. Social<BR>fire, one lighted in common.<BR>	 3. A fire lighted on taking possession<BR>of a house.<BR>	 4. A saint, a person purified by religious abstraction.<BR>5. A tree, the wood of which is used to procure fire by attrition,<BR>(Premna, spinosa.)<BR>	 6. Leadwort, (Plumbago zeylanica.)<BR>	 7.<BR>Marking nut plant, (Semicarpus anacardium.)<BR>	 8. A vermifuge<BR>plant.<BR>	 9. A flash of lightning.<BR>	 10. The number “three”: see विडङ्ग.<BR>f. (-की) Wife of AGNI.<BR> E. पू to purify, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=447-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पावकारणि|पावकारणिः
पावकारणि m. (-णिः) A tree, the wood of which is used to procure fire<BR>by attrition.<BR> E. पावक fire, अरणि touch-wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=447-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पावकि|पावकिः
पावकि m. (-किः) A name of KĀRTTIKEYA.<BR> E. पावक, and इञ् aff.;<BR>indirectly this deity is the son of fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=447-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पावन|पावनं|पावनः
पावन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>	 1. Pure, purified.<BR>	 2. Purifying, expurgatory,<BR>purificatory.<BR>	 n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Water.<BR>	 2. Penace, expiation, purification<BR>by acts of austerity and devotion.<BR>	 3. Cow-dung.<BR>	 4. The Eleo-<BR>carpus seed.<BR>	 5. A kind of grass, (Costus.)<BR>	 m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. The inspired<BR>poet VYĀSA.<BR>	 2. Fire generally or for various ceremonial pur-<BR>poses.<BR>	 3. Incense.<BR>	 4. A Siddha.<BR>	 f. (-नी)<BR>	 1. Yellow myrobalan.<BR>2. A cow.<BR>	 3. The Ganges, or the goddess GANGĀ.<BR>	 4. Holy basil.<BR>E. पू to cleanse or purify, aff. णिच् ल्यु ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=447-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पावनध्वनि|पावनध्वनिः
पावनध्वनि m. (-निः) A conch-shell.<BR> E. पावन, and ध्वनि sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=447-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पावमान
पावमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Purificatory, purifying.<BR>	 f. (-नी) An expiatory<BR>text.<BR> E. पू to purify, शानच् + अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=447-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पावमानी
पावमानी f. (-नी) An epithet of particular Vedic hymns.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=447-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पावर|पावरः
पावर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. The side of a die which is marked with two points.<BR>2. A particular throw of the die.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=447-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पावित
पावित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Purified.<BR> E. पू to purify, causal v., क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=447-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाविन्
पाविन् mfn. (-वी-विनी-वि) Who or what purifies.<BR> E. पू to purify, घिणुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=447-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाव्य
पाव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं) What is to be or must be purified.<BR> E. पू to<BR>purify, ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=447-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाश|पाशः
पाश m. (-शः)<BR>	 1. A fetter, a chain, a tie, the string for fastening<BR>tamed animals, or the net or noose for catching birds, deer, &c.<BR>2. A noose as a weapon of combat.<BR>	 3. A die.<BR>	 4. In composition<BR>with words signifying “hair,” denotes quantity, as केशपाशः much<BR>or flowing hair.<BR>	 5. In composition with कर्ण, denotes “beauty,” as<BR>कर्णपाशः a handsome ear.<BR>	 6. in composition with छत्र and other<BR>words expresses “contempt” or “depreciation,” as छत्रपाशः an<BR>inelegant or shabby umbrella; भिषक् पाश् “a bad physician &c.”<BR>E. पश् to bind, aff. घञ्; where it is used in composition, it is<BR>in fact but a technical aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=447-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाशक|पाशकः
पाशक m. (-कः) A dice, particularly the long sort used in playing<BR>Chaupai.<BR> E. पश to bind, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=447-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाशन|पाशनं
पाशन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. A noose, a snare.<BR>	 2. Fettering, entrapping.<BR> E. पाशि,<BR>aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=448-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाशपाणि|पाशपाणिः
पाशपाणि m. (-णिः) A name of VARUṆA, the regent of water.<BR> E. पाश a<BR>sort of noose, and पाणि the hand, VARUṆA being represented as<BR>holding a cord in one hand, shaped like a sling or a noose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=448-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाशबद्ध
पाशबद्ध mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं) Noosed, snared, caught or bound.<BR> E. पाश, and<BR>वद्ध bound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=448-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाशबन्ध|पाशबंध|पाशबन्धः
पाशबन्ध n. (-न्धं) A noose, a snare, a halter, a net, &c.<BR> E. पाश, and बन्ध<BR>a binding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=448-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाशभृत्
पाशभृत् m. (-भृत्)<BR>	 1. VARUṆA.<BR>	 2. A soldier, &c. armed with a noose.<BR>E. पाश, and भृत् who has.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=448-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाशव
पाशव n. (-वं) A flock, a herd.<BR>	 f. (वी) adj. Relating to animals.<BR> E. पशु<BR>an animal, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=448-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाशवपालन|पाशवपालनं
पाशवपालन n. (-नं) Pasturage or meadow grass.<BR> E. पाशव, and पालन<BR>supporting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=448-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाशित|पाशितः
पाशित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Tied, fettered, bound.<BR> E. पाश a fetter, and इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=448-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाशिन्
पाशिन् m. (-शी)<BR>	 1. One armed with a net or noose.<BR>	 2. A deer-catcher<BR>or fowler, using a net or noose.<BR>	 3. A name of VARUṆA.<BR>	 4. A<BR>name of YAMA.<BR> E. पाश a fetter, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=448-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाशीकृत|पाशीकृतः
पाशीकृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Tied, fettered.<BR> E. पाश a fetter, कृत made, and<BR>ई substituted for the final of the first word.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=448-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाशुपत|पाशुपतः
पाशुपत m. (-तः)<BR>	 1. A follower and worshipper of ŚIVA, in one of his<BR>forms as the supreme deity of the Hindū triad.<BR>	 2. A followers<BR>of the doctrines of Paśupati, an old philosopher. A tree,<BR>(Æschynomene grandiflora.)<BR>	 n. (-तं) The teaching of Paśupati.<BR>E. पशुपति a name of ŚIVA, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=448-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाशुपतास्त्र|पाशुपतास्त्रं
पाशुपतास्त्र n. (-स्त्रं) ŚIVA'S trident.<BR> E. पाशुपत, and अस्त्र a weapon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=448-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाशुपाल्य|पाशुपाल्यं
पाशुपाल्य n. (-ल्यं) The business of a grazier, rearing and keeping cattle.<BR>E. पशु an animal, पाल nourishing, ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=448-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाश्चात्त्य
पाश्चात्त्य mfn. (-त्त्यः-त्त्या-त्त्यं)<BR>	 1. Behind, being behind.<BR>	 2. Subsequent.<BR>	 3.<BR>Western.<BR>	 n. (त्त्यं) The hinder part.<BR> E. पश्चाद् भवः त्यक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=448-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाश्या
पाश्या f. (-श्या) A number of nooses.<BR> E. पाश, and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=448-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाषक|पाषकः
पाषक m. (-कः) An ornament for the feet.<BR> E. पष to bind aff. ण्वुल् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=448-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाषण्ड|पाषंड|पाषण्डः
पाषण्ड m. (-ण्डः)<BR>	 1. A heretic, an impostor, one who not conforming<BR>to the orthodox tenets of Hindu faith, assumes the external<BR>characteristics of tribe or sect, a Jain, a Bauddha &c.<BR>	 2. Any<BR>sect not Hindu.<BR> E. पाप sin, षण् to give, ड aff., deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=448-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाषण्डक|पाषंडक|पाषंडकः|पाषण्डकः
पाषण्डक m. (-कः) A heretic, an impostor.<BR> E. कन् added to the preced-<BR>ing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=448-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाषण्डिन्|पाषंडिन्
पाषण्डिन् m. (-ण्डी) A heretic, &c.: see पाषण्ड.<BR> E. पाषण्ड, and इनि<BR>added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=448-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाषाण|पाषाणः
पाषाण m. (-णः) A stone in general.<BR>	 f. (णी) A small stone used as a<BR>weight.<BR> E. पिश् to grind, (condiments upon,) घञ् aff. आनच् added,<BR>and the deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=448-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाषाणदारक|पाषाणदारकः
पाषाणदारक m. (-कः) A sort of hatchet for cutting stones, a stone-<BR>cutter's chisel.<BR> E. पाषाण a stone, and दारक what tears or breaks;<BR>also पाषाणदारण, from दारण rending, tearing. “छेनी” ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=448-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाषाणदारण|पाषाणदारणः
पाषाणदारण m. (-णः) An instrument for cutting stones; see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=448-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाषाणभेदिन्
पाषाणभेदिन् m. (-दी) A plant, (Plectranthus scutellaroides.)<BR> E. पाषाण a<BR>stone, and भेदिन् dividing; growing amongst stones and rocks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=448-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाषाणसन्धि|पाषाणसन्धिः
पाषाणसन्धि m. (-न्धिः) A cave in a rock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=448-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाषाणहृदय
पाषाणहृदय Adj. Stone-hearted, cruel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=448-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाहात|पाहातः
पाहात m. (-तः) The mulberry tree, (Morus Indica.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=448-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पि
पि r. 1st cl (पियति) To go, to move. तु० सक० पर-अनिट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=448-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिक|पिकः
पिक m. (-कः) The Indian cuckoo, (Cuculus Indicus.)<BR>	 f. (-की) The<BR>female.<BR> E. पि imitative sound, कै to utter, aff. क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=448-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिकबन्धु|पिकबंधु|पिकबन्धुः
पिकबन्धु m. (-न्धुः) The mango tree.<BR> E. पिक the Kokila, and बन्धु friend;<BR>the favourite haunt of that bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=448-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिकराम
पिकराम m. (-मः) The mango tree.<BR> E. पिक, and राग fondness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=448-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिकवल्लम
पिकवल्लम m. (-मः) The mango tree,<BR> E. पिक, and वल्लभ beloved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=448-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिकाक्ष|पिकाक्षः
पिकाक्ष n. (-क्षं) A vegetable, and perfume, commonly Rochaṇi.<BR> E. पिक<BR>Kokila and अक्ष an eye; having red blossoms.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=448-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिकाङ्ग|पिकाङ्गः
पिकाङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः) A small bird, commonly called Chāṭaka.<BR> E. पिक<BR>the Kokila, and अङ्ग body or form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=448-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिकानन्द|पिकानंद|पिकानन्दः
पिकानन्द m. (-न्दः) The spring season.<BR> E. पिक the Kokila, and आनन्द<BR>delight. Also पिकबान्धव ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=448-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिक्व
पिक्व m. (-क्वः)<BR>	 1. A young elephant.<BR>	 2. An elephant twenty years<BR>old.<BR> E. पिक imitative sound, and कै to utter, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=448-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिङ्ग|पिंग|पिङ्गं|पिङ्गः
पिङ्ग mfn. (-ङ्गः-ङ्गा-ङ्गं) Of a tawny colour.<BR>	 m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>	 1. Tawny, (the<BR>colour.<BR>	 2. A rat.<BR>	 3. A buffalo.<BR>	 n. (-ङ्गं) A young animal.<BR>	 f. (-ङ्गा)<BR>	 1.<BR>A yellow dye: see गोरोचना.<BR>	 2. Asafœtida.<BR>	 3. A tubular vessel of<BR>the body, which according to the Yoga system, is the channel of<BR>respiration and circulation for one side.<BR>	 4. A name of DURGĀ.<BR>5. Turmeric.<BR>	 6. Bamboo manna.<BR>	 f. (-ङ्गी) A sort of Mimosa, (M.<BR>suma, Rox.)<BR> E. पिजि to colour, aff. अच्; or पिङ्ग tawny, aff. टाप्, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=448-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिङ्गकपिशा|पिंगकपिशा
पिङ्गकपिशा f. (-शा) A cockroach.<BR> E. पिङ्ग tawny, and कपिश brown.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=448-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिङ्गचक्षुस्|पिंगचक्षुस्
पिङ्गचक्षुस् m. (-क्षुः) A crab.<BR> E. पिङ्ग tawny, and चक्षुस् the eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=448-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिङ्गजट|पिंगजट|पिङ्गजटः
पिङ्गजट m. (-टः) ŚIVA.<BR> E. पिङ्ग tawny, and जटा braided hair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=448-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिङ्गल|पिंगल|पिङ्गलं|पिङ्गलः
पिङ्गल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Of tawny colour, brown, yellowish.<BR>	 m. (-लः)<BR>	 1.<BR>Tawny, (the colour,) a dull brown, or yellow.<BR>	 2. An attendant<BR>upon the sun.<BR>	 3. The sun.<BR>	 4. A fabulous being in the form of a<BR>Nāga or serpent of lower regions, to whom a treatise on<BR>prosody is ascribed; he hence considered as a Muni, or inspired<BR>and divine personage.<BR>	 5. A name of ŚIVA.<BR>	 6. One of KUVERA'S<BR>divine treasures.<BR>	 7. A monkey.<BR>	 8. Fire.<BR>	 9. An ichneumon.<BR>10. A sort of poison.<BR>	 11. A small owl.<BR>	 12. The 51st<BR>year of the Hindu cycle.<BR>	 n. (-लं)<BR>	 1. Brass.<BR>	 2. Yellow<BR>orpiment.<BR>	 f. (-ला)<BR>	 1. The female elephant of the south quarter.<BR>2. A pious whore, commemorated in the Bhāgavata.<BR>	 3. A<BR>particular vessel of the body, the right of three canals which<BR>run from the os-coccygis; to the head, and which are the chief<BR>passages of breath and air, according to the anatomy of the<BR>Yoga school of philosophy.<BR>	 4. An astrological house or period.<BR>5. The Sisu tree, (Dalbergia Sisu.)<BR>	 6. Heartpea.<BR>	 7. A kind of owl.<BR>8. A kind of metal.<BR> E. पिजि to colour, Unādi aff. अलच्; or<BR>पिङ्गल of a tawny hue, fem. aff. टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=448-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिङ्गलिका|पिंगलिका
पिङ्गलिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. A sort of crane.<BR>	 2. A kind of owl. see वलाक.<BR>E. पिङ्गल of a tawny colour, कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=448-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिङ्गसार|पिंगसार|पिङ्गसारः
पिङ्गसार m. (रः) Yellow orpiment. “हरिताले” ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=448-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिङ्गस्फटिक|पिंगस्फटिक|पिङ्गस्फटिकः
पिङ्गस्फटिक m. (कः) A kind of gem called “gomedh”.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=448-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिङ्गाक्ष|पिंगाक्ष|पिङ्गाक्षः
पिङ्गाक्ष mfn. (-क्षः-क्षी-क्षं) Red-eyed.<BR>	 m. (क्षः) A name of ŚIVA.<BR> E. पिङ्ग<BR>reddish brown, and अक्ष an eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=448-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिङ्गाश|पिंगाश|पिंगाशः|पिङ्गाशः
पिङ्गाश m. (-शः)<BR>	 1. A sort of fish, (Pimelodius pangasius, HAM.)<BR>	 2. The<BR>head man or proprietor of a village.<BR>	 n. (-शं) Virgin gold.<BR>	 f. (-शी)<BR>The indigo plant.<BR> E. पिङ्ग tawny, आश flesh, from अश् to eat aff.<BR>अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=448-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिङ्गास्य|पिङ्गास्यः
पिङ्गास्य m. (-स्यः) A fish: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=448-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिङ्गेक्षण|पिंगेक्षण|पिङ्गेक्षणः
पिङ्गेक्षण m. (-णः) A name of ŚIVA.<BR> E. पिङ्ग tawny, and ईक्षण eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=448-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिचण्ड|पिचंड|पिचंडं|पिचंडः|पिचण्डः
पिचण्ड m. (-ण्डः)<BR>	 1. The belly.<BR>	 2. The back of an animal.<BR> E. अपि<BR>certainly, चम् to eat, aff. ड, initial of the prefix rejected; also<BR>पिचिण्ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=448-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिचण्डिल|पिचंडिल|पिचण्डिलः
पिचण्डिल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Big-bellied, corpulent.<BR> E. पिचण्ड the belly,<BR>and इलच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=448-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिचण्डिका
पिचण्डिका f. (-का) The instep; also पिचिण्डिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=448-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिचव्य|पिचव्यः
पिचव्य m. (-व्यः) The cotton plant.<BR> E. पिचु cotton, and यत् aff. “कार्पासवृक्षे”.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=448-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिचिण्ड|पिचिंड|पिचिंडं|पिचिंडः|पिचिण्डः
पिचिण्ड m. (-ण्डः)<BR>	 1. The belly or abdomen.<BR>	 2. The back of an<BR>animal.<BR> E. अपि certainly, चम् to eat, aff. ड, and इ substituted<BR>for the radical vowel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=448-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिचिण्डिल|पिचिंडिल|पिचिण्डिलः
पिचिण्डिल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Big-bellied, corpulent, pot-bellied. E.<BR>पिचिण्ड a belly, and इलच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=448-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिवु
पिवु m. (-चुः)<BR>	 1. Cotton.<BR>	 2. The name of an Asura.<BR>	 3. A Karṣa or<BR>weight of two Tolās: see कर्ष.<BR>	 4. A sort of leprosy.<BR>	 5. One of the<BR>eight faces of BHAIRAVA.<BR> E. पिच Sautra root, means to rub,<BR>Unādi aff. उ; or पच-उ-पृषो० ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=449-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिचुक|पिचुकः
पिचुक m. (-कः) A plant, (Vangueria spinosa.)<BR> E. कन् added to the<BR>preceding. मदनवृक्षे ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=449-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिचुतूल|पिचुतूलं
पिचुतूल n. (-लं) Cotton.<BR> E. पिचु, and तूल both meaning the same, cotton.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=449-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिचुमन्द|पिचुमंद|पिचुमन्दः
पिचुमन्द m. (-न्दः) The Nimba tree, (Melia azadirachta.)<BR> E. पिवु a sort of<BR>leprosy, and मन्द to be slow, in the causal form, to make slow or<BR>check, aff. अच्; also पिचुमर्द्द.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=449-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिचुमर्द्द|पिचुमर्द|पिचुमर्दः|पिचुमर्द्दः
पिचुमर्द्द m. (-र्द्दः) The Nimba tree: see the last.<BR> E. पिचु as before, मृद् to<BR>destroy, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=449-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिचुल|पिचुलः
पिचुल m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. Cotton: also पिचु.<BR>	 2. The tamarisk, (T. Indica.)<BR>	 3.<BR>A plant, (Barringtonia acutangulā.)<BR>	 4. The diver or water-crow.<BR>E. पिचु cotton, ला to get, &c. aff. क. झावुकवृक्षे ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=449-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिच्च
पिच्च r. 10th cl. (पिच्चयति-ते) To cut, to divide. चु० उभ० सक० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=449-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिच्चट|पिच्चटं|पिच्चटः
पिच्चट m. (-टः) Inflammation of the eyes, ophthalmia.<BR>	 n. (-टं).<BR>	 1. Tin.<BR>2. Lead.<BR> E. पिच्च् to divide, aff. अच्, and टौक for ढोक to<BR>go, aff. ड; or पिच्च-अटन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=449-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिच्चा
पिच्चा f. (-च्चा) A particular measure of pearls.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=449-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिच्छ|पिच्छं|पिच्छः
पिच्छ r.<BR>	 6. th cl. (पिच्छति)<BR>	 1. To pain or torture.<BR>	 2. To hinder. r. 10th<BR>cl. (पिच्छयति) To cut, to divide. तु० पर० सक० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=449-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिच्छ|पिच्छं|पिच्छः
पिच्छ n. (-च्छं)<BR>	 1. The tail of a peacock.<BR>	 2. A crest.<BR>	 3. The feather<BR>of a tail.<BR>	 4. The feather of an arrow.<BR>	 m. (-च्छः) A tail in<BR>general.<BR>	 f. (-च्छा)<BR>	 1. The gum of the silk-cotton tree.<BR>	 2. A line,<BR>a row or range.<BR>	 3. A diseased affection of a horse's feet.<BR>	 4. The<BR>nut of the Areca, betel-nut.<BR>	 5. A plantain.<BR>	 6. The scum of<BR>boiled rice.<BR>	 7. A sort of body dress, or jacket.<BR>	 8. The venomous<BR>saliva of a snake.<BR>	 9. The Sisu tree, (Dalbergia Sisu.)<BR>	 10. A she-<BR>ath, a coat or cover.<BR>	 11. An armour.<BR>	 12. A multitude, a heap.<BR>13. The calf of the leg.<BR>	 14. The Indian cuckoo.<BR>	 15. The exudation<BR>of the Sālmalī tree.<BR> E. पिच्छ् to divide, aff. घञ् or अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=449-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिच्छल
पिच्छल f. (-ला) Slimy, slippery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=449-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिच्छलदला
पिच्छलदला f. (-ला) The jujube, (Zizyphus jujuba.)<BR> E. पिच्छल for पिच्छिल<BR>a tree, and दल a leaf. वदरोवृक्षे ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=449-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिच्छवत्
पिच्छवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Tailed, having a tail.<BR> E. पिच्छ, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=449-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिच्छवाण
पिच्छवा(बा)ण m. (-णः) A hawk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=449-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिच्छिका
पिच्छिका f. (-का) The feather of a peacock's tail tied in a bunch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=449-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिच्छितिका
पिच्छितिका f. (-का) The Sisu, (Dalbergia Sisu.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=449-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिच्छिल|पिच्छिलं|पिच्छिलः
पिच्छिल mfn. subst. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>	 1. Sauce mixed with rice gruel.<BR>	 2.<BR>Sauce, gravy, or condiments with water or Ghee.<BR>	 3. Broth, soup.<BR>4. Moist, and split pulse.<BR>	 f. (-ला)<BR>	 1. The silk-cotton tree,<BR>(Bombax heptaphyllum.)<BR>	 2. A potherb, (Basella rubra and<BR>lucida.)<BR>	 5. A timber tree, (Dalbergia Sisu.)<BR>	 4. The name of a<BR>river.<BR>	 5. An esculent root, (Arum Indicum.)<BR>	 6. Lubricous,<BR>slippery, smeary.<BR>	 m. (-लः) The tamarisk, (Tamarix Indica.)<BR>	 mfn.<BR>adj. (-लः-ला-लं) Having a tail.<BR> E. पिच्छा rice water, scum, &c. and<BR>इलच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=449-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिच्छिलत्वच्
पिच्छिलत्वच् m. (-त्वक्)<BR>	 1. An orange.<BR>	 2. Orange-peel.<BR> E. पिच्छिल said to<BR>mean an orange, and त्वच् skin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=449-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिज
पिज(इ)पिजि r. 2nd cl. (पिंक्ते)<BR>	 1. To tinge, to dye or colour, to<BR>impinge.<BR>	 2. To touch.<BR>	 3. To tinkle.<BR>	 4. To adore. r. 1st and<BR>10th cls. (पिञ्जति पिञ्जयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To kill or injure.<BR>	 2. To be strong.<BR>3. To give.<BR>	 4. To dwell.<BR>	 5. To speak.<BR>	 6. To shine. दीप्तौ वासे<BR>सामर्थ्येच अक० हिंसायां दानेच सक० चु० उभ० सेट् इदित् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=449-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिञ्ज|पिंज|पिञ्जं|पिञ्जः
पिञ्ज mfn. (-ञ्जः-ञ्जा-ञ्जं) Disturbed in mind, confused, confounded.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-ञ्जः)<BR>	 1. The moon.<BR>	 2. A kind of camphor.<BR>	 3. A heap.<BR>	 4. Killing,<BR>slaughter.<BR>	 n. (-ञ्जं) Strength, power.<BR>	 f. (-ञ्जा)<BR>	 1. Hurting, injuring,<BR>injury.<BR>	 2. Cotton.<BR>	 3. Turmeric.<BR>	 4. A sort of palm.<BR>	 5. A switch.<BR>E. पिजि to hurt or kill, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=449-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिञ्जट|पिंजट|पिंजटः|पिञ्जटः
पिञ्जट m. (-टः) The concrete rheum of the eyes.<BR> E. पिजि to give pain,<BR>अटन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=449-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिञ्जन|पिंजन|पिंजनं|पिञ्जनं
पिञ्जन n. (-नं) A bow-shaped instrument used for cleaning cotton.<BR>E. पिजि to touch, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=449-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिञ्जर|पिंजर|पिञ्जरं|पिञ्जरः
पिञ्जर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Yellow or tawny, reddish yellow.<BR>	 m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A<BR>sort of colour, tawny brown, a reddish yellow, or a mixture of red<BR>and yellow.<BR>	 2. A horse, probably a bay or chesnut horse.<BR>	 n. (-रं)<BR>1. Gold.<BR>	 2. Yellow orpiment.<BR>	 3. A cage.<BR>	 4. The ribs or the cavity<BR>formed by them, the thorax: see पञ्जर.<BR> E. पिजि to dye or tinge,<BR>अरच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=449-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिञ्जल|पिंजल|पिञ्जलं|पिञ्जलः
पिञ्जल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Confounded, overcome with terror or grief.<BR>m. (-लः) An army panic-struck, or in great disorder.<BR>	 n. (-लं)<BR>	 1.<BR>The leaf of the Kusa grass.<BR>	 2. Yellow orpiment.<BR>	 f. (-ली) Two<BR>blades of Kusa grass, used as a vessel, or to take up articles<BR>with, at sacrifices.<BR> E. पिजि to hurt, &c. aff. कलच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=449-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिञ्जाल|पिंजाल|पिंजालं
पिञ्जाल n. (-लं) Gold.<BR> E. पिजि, आलच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=449-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिञ्जिका|पिंजिका
पिञ्जिका f. (-का) A roll of cotton, from which the threads are spun. E.<BR>पिञ्जा cotton, कन् added in the fem. form. “पाइज” ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=449-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिञ्जूल|पिञ्जूलं
पिञ्जूल n. (-लं) The wick of a lamp.<BR> E. पिजि to hurt, &c. Unādi aff. ऊलव्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=449-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिञ्जूष|पिंजूष|पिंजूषः|पिञ्जूषः
पिञ्जूष m. (-षः) The wax of the ear.<BR> E. पिजि to stain, ऊषन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=449-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिञ्जेट|पिंजेट|पिंजेटः|पिञ्जेटः
पिञ्जेट m. (-टः) The excretion, or concrete rheum of the eyes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=449-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिञ्जोला|पिंजोला
पिञ्जोला f. (-ला) The noise, or rustling of leaves.<BR> E. पिजि, ओल aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=449-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिट|पिटं|पिटः
पिट r. 1st cl. (पेटति)<BR>	 1. To sound.<BR>	 2. To assemble or heap together.<BR>भ्वा० पर० अक० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=449-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिट|पिटं|पिटः
पिट m. (-टः)<BR>	 1. A basket for holding grain, a sort of cupboard or<BR>granary made of bamboos or canes.<BR>	 2. A basket, a box.<BR>	 n.<BR>(-टं)<BR>	 1. A house, a hovel.<BR>	 2. A roof.<BR> E. पिट् to collect, क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=449-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिटक|पिटकं|पिटकः
पिटक mfn. subst. (-कः-का-कं) A boil, an ulcer.<BR>	 m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A basket, a<BR>box.<BR>	 2. A large basket, or receptacle of basket work, for keeping<BR>grain, &c.; a granary.<BR>	 3. An ornament on Indra's banner.<BR> E. पिट्<BR>to collect, aff. क्कुन्; also पिट and पेटक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=449-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिटङ्काश|पिटङ्काशः
पिटङ्काश m. (-शः) A species of pike, (Esox scolopax.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=449-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिटङ्कीकी
पिटङ्कीकी f. (-की) Colocynth. इन्द्रवारुण्याम् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=449-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिटाक|पिटाकः
पिटाक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. The name of a saint.<BR>	 2. A basket, a box.<BR> E. पिट्<BR>to collect, and काक Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=449-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिट्टक|पिट्टकं
पिट्टक n. (-कं) The tartar or excretion of the teeth.<BR> E. पिट् to collect,<BR>aff. ण्वुल् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=449-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिठ|पिठः
पिठ r. 1st cl. (पेठति)<BR>	 1. To hurt or kill.<BR>	 2. To feel pain or affliction.<BR>क्लेशे अक० वधे सक० भ्वा० पर० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=449-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिठ|पिठः
पिठ m. (-ठः) Pain, distress.<BR> E. पिठ, and क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=449-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिठर|पिठरं|पिठरः
पिठर mf. (-रः-री) A pot, a pan.<BR>	 n. (-रं)<BR>	 1. A churning stick.<BR>	 2. A<BR>fragrant grass, (Cyperus rotundus.)<BR>	 3. A sort of building, a hut<BR>or watch box made of bamboos and mats, or as it is sometimes<BR>explained, a kind of store room or scullery.<BR> E. पिठ pain, रा to<BR>take, aff. क; or पिठ-करन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=449-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिठरक|पिठरकं|पिठरकः
पिठरक m. (-कः) A kind of serpent. E. see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=449-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिड
पिड(इ,)पिडि r. 1st and 10th cls. (पिण्डति-ते पिण्डयति-ते) To accu-<BR>mulate, to assemble, to heap together. राशीकरणे भ्वा० आत्म० सक०<BR>सेट्० इदित् । चुरादेरुभयपदी ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=449-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिडक|पिडकः
पिडक mf. (-कः-वा) A small boil, a pimple.<BR> E. पीड-ण्वुल् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=449-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिण्ड|पिंड|पिण्डं|पिण्डः
पिण्ड mn. (-ण्डः-ण्डं) A lump, a heap, a cluster, a quantity or collec-<BR>tion.<BR>	 mf. (-ण्डः-ण्डी) An oblation to deceased ancestors as a ball<BR>or lump of meat, or rice, mixed up with milk, curds, flowers,<BR>&c. and offered to the manes at the several Shrāddhas. by the<BR>nearest surviving relations.<BR>	 m. (-ण्डः)<BR>	 1. A ball, a globe.<BR>	 2. A<BR>mouthful, or roundish lump of food, considered as equivalent to a<BR>mouthful.<BR>	 3. Presenting water or cake to a deceased relation.<BR>	 4.<BR>The body.<BR>	 5. The side immediately below the armpit.<BR>	 6. A part of<BR>a house; a sort of portico or shed, in front of the door.<BR>	 7. Coarse,<BR>gross, thick, solid.<BR>	 8. Strength, power.<BR>	 9. Myrrh.<BR>	 10. Franki-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=450-a" target="_blank">Page450-a+ 60</a>]<BR>ncense.<BR>	 11. The China rose.<BR>	 12. Food.<BR>	 13. Flesh, meat.<BR>	 14. The<BR>projection of an elephant's frontal sinus.<BR>	 15. The embryo<BR>or fetus in an early stage of gestation.<BR>	 16. A sum, (in arith-<BR>metic.)<BR>	 17. Thickness, (In geometry.)<BR>	 18. (In astronomy,) The<BR>twenty-fourth part of the quadrant of a circle, or 30-45’.<BR>	 n.<BR>(-ण्डं)<BR>	 1. Livelihood, means, means of living.<BR>	 2. Iron.<BR>	 3. Fresh<BR>butter.<BR>	 4. Power, strength.<BR>	 5. An army.<BR>	 f. (-ण्डी)<BR>	 1. A long<BR>gourd, (Cucurbita lagenaria.)<BR>	 2. A sort of palm, (Phœnix dactyli-<BR>fera.)<BR>	 3. A flowering shrub, (Tabernæmontana coronaria flor.<BR>plen.)<BR>	 4. Performance of certain gesticulations, accompanying<BR>the silent repetition of prayers, &c. in meditation on real or<BR>divine knowledge.<BR>	 5. The nave of a wheel.<BR>	 6. A house.<BR>	 7. Solid,<BR>compact, close.<BR>	 8. The calf of the leg.<BR>	 9. A round mass.<BR> E. पिडि<BR>to heap, to gather, to collect, &c. aff. अच् fem. aff. ङीप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=449-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिण्डक|पिंडक|पिंडकं|पिण्डकं|पिंडकः|पिण्डकः
पिण्डक mn. (-कः-कं)<BR>	 1. Incense.<BR>	 2. Carrot.<BR>	 3. The calf of the leg.<BR>	 4. A<BR>lump of food.<BR>	 5. A lump or ball.<BR>	 m. (-कः) A goblin, a demon. E.<BR>पिण्ड as above, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=450-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिण्डकन्द|पिण्डकन्दः
पिण्डकन्द m. (-न्दः) See पिण्डालु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=450-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिण्डखर्ज्जूर|पिण्डखर्जूर|पिण्डखर्ज्जूरः
पिण्डखर्ज्जूर mf. (-रः-री) A sort of date tree.<BR> E. पिण्ड a lump, a cluster,<BR>and खर्ज्जूर the date. “छोहारा” ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=450-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिण्डगोस|पिंडगोस|पिण्डगोसः
पिण्डगोस m. (-सः) Gum myrrh; also पिण्ड, and गोस severally.<BR>“गन्धरसे” ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=450-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिण्डतैलक|पिंडतैलक|पिण्डतैलकः
पिण्डतैलक m. (-कः) Incense, olibanum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=450-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिण्डद|पिंडद|पिण्डदः
पिण्डद mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>	 1. Who or what gives the funeral cake to<BR>deceased ancestors.<BR>	 2. One who supports or feeds another.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-दः)<BR>	 1. The nearest male relation who offers the funeral cake.<BR>	 2.<BR>A patron, a master.<BR> E. पिण्ड, and द who or what gives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=450-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिण्डदान|पिंडदान
पिण्डदान n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Presentation of the obsequial cake.<BR>	 2. The<BR>funeral oblation made to deceased ancestors on the evening of the<BR>new-moon day.<BR> E. पिण्ड, and दान giving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=450-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिण्डन|पिंडन|पिंडनं|पिण्डनः
पिण्डन m. (-नः) A mound or bank.<BR>	 n. (-नं) Forming globes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=450-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिण्डनिर्वपन
पिण्डनिर्वपन n. (-नं) Presenting obsequial cake to the manes.<BR> E. पिण्ड,<BR>and निर्वपन offering funeral oblations.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=450-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिण्डपात|पिंडपात|पिण्डपातः
पिण्डपात m. (-तः) Collecting or giving alms.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=450-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिण्डपाद|पिंडपाद|पिण्डपादः
पिण्डपाद m. (-दः) An elephant.<BR> E. पिण्ड a lump of flesh, and पाद a<BR>foot: also पिण्डपाद्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=450-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिण्डपुष्प|पिंडपुष्प|पिण्डपुष्पं|पिण्डपुष्पः
पिण्डपुष्प mn. (-ष्पः-ष्पं)<BR>	 1. The flower of the Asoka tree, (Jonesia Asoca.)<BR>2. The China rose.<BR>	 3. A lotus.<BR>	 4. A flower, (Tabernæmontana<BR>coronaria.)<BR>	 5. The pomegranate.<BR> E. पिण्ड a cluster, and पुष्प a<BR>flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=450-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिण्डपुष्पक|पिण्डपुष्पकः
पिण्डपुष्पक m. (-कः) A potherb, (Chenopodium album.)<BR> E. पिण्ड a lump,<BR>पुष्प a flower, कन् added. वास्तूकशाके ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=450-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिण्डफला
पिण्डफला f. (-ला) A bitter gourd.<BR> E. पिण्ड a lump, फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=450-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिण्डभाज्|पिंडभाज्
पिण्डभाज् m. (-भाक्) Plu. The manes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=450-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिण्डभृति|पिंडभृति|पिण्डभृतिः
पिण्डभृति f. (-ति) Livelihood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=450-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिण्डमात्रोपजीविन्
पिण्डमात्रोपजीविन् mfn. (-वी-विनी-वि) Living, breathing, having no<BR>intellectual existence.<BR> E. पिण्ड, मात्र only, उपजीविन् subsisting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=450-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिण्डमुस्ता
पिण्डमुस्ता f. (-स्ता) A sort of grass, (Cyperus pertenuis.)<BR> E. पिण्ड a<BR>lump, and मुस्ता Cyperus. नागरमुस्तायाम् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=450-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिण्डमूल|पिंडमूल|पिण्डमूलं
पिण्डमूल n. (-लं) The carrot, (Daucus carota.)<BR> E. पिण्ड lump of flesh,<BR>and मूल a root; also with कन् added, पिण्डमूलक. “गांँजर” ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=450-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिण्डल|पिंडल|पिंडलः|पिण्डलः
पिण्डल m. (-लः) A bridge, a causeway, a passage over a stream or<BR>ravine, &c. or a mound raised to form a path across inundated<BR>fields.<BR> E. पिण्ड a heap, (of earth, &c.) and ला to get, aff. ड; or<BR>पिडि वा कलच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=450-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिण्डलेप|पिंडलेप|पिण्डलेपः
पिण्डलेप m. (-पः)<BR>	 1. The fragments of the obsequial cake which cling<BR>to the hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=450-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिण्डलोप|पिंडलोप|पिण्डलोपः
पिण्डलोप m. (-पः) Interruption in offering the funeral cakes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=450-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिण्डवीज
पिण्डवीज m. (-जः) A flowering shrub, (Oleander odorum.)<BR> E. पिण्ड, and<BR>वीज seed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=450-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिण्डस|पिंडस|पिंडसः|पिण्डसः
पिण्डस m. (-सः) A beggar, a mendicant living upon alms.<BR> E. पिण्ड a<BR>ball of rice, &c. सद् to go or get, aff. ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=450-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिण्डसम्बन्ध|पिंडसंबंध|पिण्डसंबन्ध|पिण्डसंबन्धः
पिण्डसम्बन्ध m. (-न्धः) Relationship between a living person and one<BR>deceased, near enough to qualify the former to offer the obsequial<BR>cake to the latter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=450-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिण्डात|पिंडात|पिंडातः|पिण्डातः
पिण्डात m. (-तः) Incense.<BR> E. पिण्ड the same, अत् to be, aff. मातत्ये-अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=450-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिण्डाभ्र|पिंडाभ्र|पिण्डाभ्रं
पिण्डाभ्र n. (-भ्रं) Hail.<BR> E. पिण्ड a lump, and अभ्र a cloud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=450-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिण्डायस|पिंडायस|पिण्डायसं
पिण्डायस n. (-सं) Steel.<BR> E. पिण्ड, and अयस iron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=450-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिण्डार|पिंडार|पिण्डारं|पिंडारः|पिण्डारः
पिण्डार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A keeper or attendant on buffaloes.<BR>	 2. A cow-<BR>herd.<BR>	 3. A beggar, a religious mendicant.<BR>	 4. The vikankata<BR>tree, (Trewia nudiflora.)<BR> E. पिण्ड a heap, ऋ to go, aff. अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=450-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिण्डालक्तक|पिंडालक्तक|पिण्डालक्तकः
पिण्डालक्तक m. (-कः) A red dye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=450-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिण्डाल
पिण्डाल m. (-लुः) An esculent and medical root, described as sweet,<BR>cooling, and diuretic.<BR> E. पिण्ड a lump, and आलु an esculent<BR>root. “गोलआलु” ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=450-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिण्डाश|पिंडाश|पिण्डाशः
पिण्डाश mfn. (-शः-शा-शं) A beggar.<BR> E. पिण्ड a piece of meat, आश who<BR>eats; also पिण्डाशनः, and पिण्डाशिन् m. (-शी ।)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=450-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिण्डि|पिंडि|पिंडिः|पिण्डिः
पिण्डि f. (-ण्डि)<BR>	 1. The have of a wheel.<BR>	 2. The Asoka tree, &c: see<BR>पिण्डी.<BR> E. पिडि to collect, (the spokes,) aff. इन्; also पिण्डी and<BR>पिण्डिका ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=450-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिण्डिका|पिंडिका
पिण्डिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. The nave of a wheel.<BR>	 2. The instep.<BR>	 3. A stool or<BR>seat of various shapes and dimensions.<BR> E. पिण्डी as above, and कन्<BR>added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=450-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिण्डित|पिंडित|पिण्डितं|पिण्डितः
पिण्डित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Multiplied, added.<BR>	 2. Counted, numbered.<BR>3. Thick, massy, lumpish.<BR>	 4. Collected, heaped together.<BR> E. पिण्ड<BR>a lump, a heap, and इतच् aff.; or पिडि-क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=450-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिण्डिन्|पिंडिन्
पिण्डिन् mfn. (-ण्डी-ण्डिनी-ण्डि) Having a Pinda or ball of food,<BR>(a ceremony, an ancestor, &c.)<BR>	 m. (-ण्डी)<BR>	 1. A beggar.<BR>	 2. An offerer<BR>of oblations.<BR> E. पिण्ड, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=450-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिण्डिल|पिंडिल|पिण्डिलः
पिण्डिल m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. A bridge, a mound, a causeway.<BR>	 2. An astrologer,<BR>an arithmetician, a calculator of nativities, &c.<BR>	 f. (-ला) A sort of<BR>cucumber, (C. madraspatanus.)<BR> E. पिण्ड a heap, &c. इलच् Unādi<BR>aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=450-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिण्डीकरण
पिण्डीकरण n. (-णं) Heaping, making up into a lump or ball.<BR> E. पिण्ड,<BR>and करण making, च्वि augm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=450-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिण्डीकृत
पिण्डीकृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Made into a lump or ball.<BR> E. पिण्ड, and कृत<BR>made, च्वि augm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=450-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिण्डीतक|पिण्डीतकः
पिण्डीतक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A tree, (Vangueria spinosa, Rox.)<BR>	 2. A shrub,<BR>(Tabernæmontana coronaria.)<BR>	 3. A plant, commonly marua: see<BR>मरुवक ।<BR> E. पिण्डी a plant, तन् to spread, to resemble, aff. ड and<BR>कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=450-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिण्डीतगर|पिण्डीतगरः
पिण्डीतगर m. (-रः) A plant, a species of Tabernæmontana.<BR> E. पिण्डी<BR>the same, and तगर T. coronaria.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=450-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिण्डीभूत
पिण्डीभूत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Lumped, heaped, made up in a lump or<BR>ball.<BR> E. पिण्ड, and भूत become, च्वि augm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=450-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिण्डीर|पिंडीर|पिण्डीरः
पिण्डीर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Sapless, juiceless, arid, dry.<BR>	 m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. The<BR>pomegranate.<BR>	 2. Cuttle-fish-bone considered to be the foam of<BR>the sea.<BR> E. पिण्ड a ball, &c. ईर to go, to resemble, aff. अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=450-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिण्डीशूर|पिंडीशूर|पिण्डीशूरः
पिण्डीशूर m. (रः) A cot queen, an effeminate braggart.<BR> E. पिण्ड a<BR>house, and शूर a hero.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=450-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिण्डोद्धरण|पिंडोद्धरण
पिण्डोद्धरण n. (-णं) Participating in obsequial offerings, presenting<BR>them to common ancestors.<BR> E. पिण्ड, and डद्धरण sharing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=450-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिण्डोलि|पिंडोलि|पिंडोलिः|पिण्डोलिः
पिण्डोलि f. (-लिः) Orts, leaving of a meal, or fragments dropped<BR>from the mouth.<BR> E. पिडि to heap, aff. ओलि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=450-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिण्या
पिण्या f. (ण्या) Heart-pea, (Cardiospermum haliacacabum.)<BR> E. पण्<BR>to praise, ण्यत् aff., and इ substituted for the radical vowel: see<BR>पण्या.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=450-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिण्याक|पिण्याकं|पिण्याकः
पिण्याक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. The sediments of seeds, &c. ground for oil; oil-<BR>cake, or the seeds after expression.<BR>	 2. Saffron.<BR>	 3. Asafœtida.<BR>4. Incense.<BR> E. पिषु to pound or bruise, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=450-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितामह|पितामहः
पितामह m. (हः)<BR>	 1. A paternal grandfather.<BR>	 2. A name of BRAHMĀ.<BR>the great father of all.<BR>	 f. (-ही) A paternal grandmother.<BR> E. पितृ<BR>a father, and डामह aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=451-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृ
पितृ m. (-ता) A father, dual, (-रौ) Mother and father, parents.<BR>plu. always, (-रः)<BR>	 1. Paternal ancestors.<BR>	 2. The manes, or the<BR>deceased and deified progenitors of mankind, inhabiting a<BR>peculiar region or heaven, or according to some, the orbit of the<BR>moon.<BR> E. पा to nourish, Unādi aff. तृच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=451-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृक|पितृकं
पितृक mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>	 1. Paternal, ancestral, parental, obsequial,<BR>relating or belonging to parents or progenitors.<BR> E. पितृ a sire,<BR>and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=451-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितॄक्थ
पितॄक्थ n. (-क्थं) Paternal property.<BR> E. पितृ, and ऋक्थ wealth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=451-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृकर्म्मन्|पितृकर्मन्
पितृकर्म्मन् n. (-र्म्म) Obsequial rites.<BR> E. पितृ, and कर्म्मन् act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=451-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृकार्य्य|पितृकार्य
पितृकार्य्य n. (-र्य्यं) Obsequial rites.<BR> E. पितृ, and कार्य्य to be done.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=451-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृकानन|पितृकाननं
पितृकानन n. (-नं) A cemetery.<BR> E. पितृ an ancestor, and कानन a<BR>wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=451-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृक्रिया
पितृक्रिया f. (-या) Obsequial rites.<BR> E. पितृ, and क्रिया ceremony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=451-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृगण|पितृगणः
पितृगण m. (-णः) A class of progenitors, the sons of the Ṛṣis or<BR>Prajāpatis: the principal classes are the Somasads descended<BR>from VIRĀT, the Agnishwattās from MARĪCI, Bārhishads from<BR>ATRI, Somapās from BHRIGU, Havishmats from ANGIRAS,<BR>Ājyapas from PULASTYA, Sukālins from VASHISTHA; there are<BR>also the Agnidaghas and Anagnidagdhas, Kavyas and Saumyas.<BR>E. पितृ father, (of mankind,) गण a troop.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=451-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृगामिन्
पितृगामिन् mfn. (-मी-मिनी-मि) Belonging to, or pertaining to a<BR>father.<BR> E. पितृ, and गामिन् what goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=451-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृगृह|पितृगृहं
पितृगृह n. (-हं)<BR>	 1. A paternal mansion.<BR>	 2. A burying ground, a<BR>cemetery.<BR> E. पितृ a deceased ancestor, and गृह a house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=451-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृघातक|पितृघातकः
पितृघातक m. (-कः) A parricide.<BR> E. पितृ and घातक a slayer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=451-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृतर्पण|पितृतर्पणं
पितृतर्पण n. (णं)<BR>	 1. The part of the hand between the middle<BR>finger and thumb, sacred to the manes.<BR>	 2. Gifts in honour of<BR>deceased relations, distributed at the Śrāddhas or funeral<BR>ceremonies.<BR>	 3. The act of throwing water out of the right hand<BR>at seasons of ablution, by way of offering to the manes or<BR>deceased ancestors in general.<BR> E. पितृ a father, a progenitor, and<BR>तर्पण satisfying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=451-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृतस्
पितृतस् ind. From or by the father.<BR> E. पितृ, and तसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=451-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृतिथि|पितृतिथिः
पितृतिथि m. (-थिः) Day of new moon, on which she rises invisible. E.<BR>पितृ a progenitor, and तिथि a lunar day, sacred to the manes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=451-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृतीर्थ|पितृतीर्थं
पितृतीर्थ n. (-र्थं)<BR>	 1. Gaya, the city so called, where the performance<BR>of funeral sacrifices is peculiarly efficacious and meritorious.<BR>	 2.<BR>The part between the forefinger and thumb, sacred to the<BR>manes.<BR> E. पितृ a progenitor, and तीर्थ a place of pilgrimage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=451-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृत्व
पितृत्व n. (-त्वं)<BR>	 1. Paternity.<BR>	 2. The state or condition of a Pitṛ, or<BR>deified progenitor.<BR> E. त्व added to पितृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=451-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृदान|पितृदानं
पितृदान n. (-नं) Gift in honour of deceased ancestors.<BR> E. पितृ a pro-<BR>genitor, and दान giving or gift; also with कन् added, पितृदानक<BR>n. (-कं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=451-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृदाय|पितृदायः
पितृदाय m. (-यः) Patrimony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=451-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितदैवत
पितदैवत n. (-तं) The tenth lunar asterism or Maghā.<BR> E. पितृ, and<BR>दैवत divinity, presiding over the asterism.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=451-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृपक्ष|पितृपक्षः
पितृपक्ष m. (-क्षः)<BR>	 1. The paternal side.<BR>	 2. The second half of the<BR>month of Bhādrapada peculiarly appointed for the celebration of<BR>obsequial rites to the manes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=451-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृपति|पितृपतिः
पितृपति m. (-तिः) YAMA, regent of the dead.<BR> E. पितृ a deceased pro-<BR>genitor, and पति lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=451-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृपद
पितृपद n. (-दं) The world or state of the manes.<BR> E. पितृ, and पद<BR>degree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=451-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृपात्र
पितृपात्र n. (-त्रं) A cup or vessel used at obsequial rites.<BR> E. पितृ, and<BR>पात्र a cup.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=451-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृपितृ
पितृपितृ m. (-ता) A paternal grandfather.<BR> E. पितृ a father, and पितृ the<BR>same, father's father.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=451-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृप्रसू
पितृप्रसू f. (-सूः)<BR>	 1. Twilight.<BR>	 2. A father's mother.<BR> E. पितृ a deceased<BR>progenitor, and प्रसू the parent; the first is the time when<BR>manes are abroad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=451-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृप्राप्त
पितृप्राप्त mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं)<BR>	 1. Received from a father.<BR>	 2. Inherited<BR>patrimonially.<BR> E. पितृ, and प्राप्त obtained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=451-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृबन्धु|पितृबंधु|पितृबन्धुः
पितृबन्धु m. (-न्धुः) A remote or cognate kinsman by the father's side,<BR>as the son of the paternal grandfather's sister, of the paternal<BR>grandmother's sister, and of the father's maternal uncle. E.<BR>पितृ, and बन्धु a kinsman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=451-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृबान्धव|पितृबान्धवः
पितृबान्धव m. (-वः) A remote kinsman of the paternal line: see the<BR>last.<BR> E. पितृ, and बान्धव a kinsman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=451-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृभक्ति
पितृभक्ति f. (-क्तिः) Filial duty to a father.<BR> E. पितृ, and भक्ति devotion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=451-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृभोजन|पितृभोजनः
पितृभोजन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Food offered to the manes.<BR>	 2. A father's food.<BR>3. A kind of pulse: see Māsha.<BR> E. पितृ, and भोजन food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=451-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृभ्रातृ
पितृभ्रातृ m. (-ता) A father's brother.<BR> E. पितृ, and भ्रातृ a brother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=451-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृमन्दिर|पितृमंदिर
पितृमन्दिर n. (-रं)<BR>	 1. The paternal mansion.<BR>	 2. A cemetery.<BR> E. पितृ,<BR>and मन्दिर a dwelling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=451-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृमेध|पितृमेधः
पितृमेध n. (-धं) Obsequial rites.<BR> E. पितृ, and मेध sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=451-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृयज्ञ|पितृयज्ञः
पितृयज्ञ m. (-ज्ञः)<BR>	 1. Obsequial rites.<BR>	 2. Oblations of water daily<BR>offered to the manes.<BR> E. पितृ a progenitor, and यज्ञ sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=451-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृयाण
पितृयाण n. (णं) The carriage of the manes, a car to convey holy<BR>persons after their decease to heaven.<BR> E. पितृ a progenitor, and<BR>यान a vehicle. पितरो यान्ति अनेन या-करणे ल्युट् संज्ञात्वात् णत्वम् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=451-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृराज
पितृराज m. (-जः) An epithet of Yama.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=451-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृरुप
पितृरुप m. (-पः) An epithet of SĪVA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=451-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृलोक|पितृलोकः
पितृलोक m. (-कः) The world or sphere of the manes: it is variously<BR>situated, but principally in Bhuva region or midheaven.<BR> E. पितृ,<BR>and लोक world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=451-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृवत्
पितृवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Having a father living, &c.<BR> E. पितृ, and<BR>मतुप् poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=451-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृवन|पितृवनं
पितृवन n. (-नं) A cemetery, a place where dead bodies are burnt or<BR>buried.<BR> E. पितृ a deceased progenitor, वन a wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=451-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृवनेचर|पितृवनेचरः
पितृवनेचर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. SĪVA.<BR>	 2. A goblin.<BR> E. पितृवन a cemetery, in the<BR>seventh case, and चर who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=451-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृवसति|पितृवसतिः
पितृवसति f. (-तिः) A cemetery.<BR> E. पितृ a deceased progenitor, and<BR>वसति an abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=451-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृवाक्पर
पितृवाक्पर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Obedient to parents.<BR> E. पितृ, वाच् speech,<BR>पर attentive to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=451-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृव्य|पितृव्यः
पितृव्य m. (-व्यः)<BR>	 1. A paternal uncle.<BR>	 2. Any elderly relation.<BR> E. पितृ<BR>a father, व्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=451-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृव्रत|पितृव्रतः
पितृव्रत m. (-तः) Who worships the manes.<BR>	 n. (-तं) Worship of<BR>ancestors, obsequial rites.<BR> E. पितृ, and व्रत obligation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=451-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृश्राद्ध
पितृश्राद्ध n. (-द्धं) The obsequial ceremony of a father.<BR> E. पितृ, and<BR>श्राद्ध the rite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=451-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृष्वसृ
पितृष्वसृ f. (-सा) A father's sister.<BR> E. पितृ father, and स्वसृ a sister, स<BR>changed to ष; the compound may also be पितुःष्वसृ, पितुःखसृ,<BR>and पितृस्वसृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=451-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृसन्निभ|पितृसंनिभ|पितृसन्निभः
पितृसन्निभ mfn. (-भः-भा-भं) Fatherly.<BR> E. पितृ, सन्निभ like.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=451-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृसामान्य
पितृसामान्य n. (-न्यं) Ancestors collectively.<BR> E. पितृ, and सामान्य uni-<BR>versality.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=451-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृमू
पितृमू f. (-मूः)<BR>	 1. Twilight.<BR>	 2. A father's mother.<BR> E. पितृ a ghost,<BR>and मू producing: see पितृपसू.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=451-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृस्थान|पितृस्थानः
पितृस्थान m. (-नः) A guardian, a protector.<BR>	 n. (-नं) The abode of the<BR>manes.<BR> E. पितृ, and स्थान like, or in place of; or a place, an abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=451-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृस्थानीय|पितृस्थानीयः
पितृस्थानीय m. (-यः) A guardian.<BR> E. पितृस्थान, and छ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=451-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृस्वस्रीय
पितृस्वस्रीय mf. (-यः-या) A maternal aunt's son or daughter.<BR> E. पितृ, and<BR>स्वस्रीय sister's son, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=451-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृहन्
पितृहन् m. (-हा) A parricide.<BR> E. पितृ, and हन् who kills.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=451-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पित्त|पित्तं
पित्त n. (-त्तं) Bile, the bilious humour.<BR> E. अपि certainly, दो to des-<BR>troy, or देङ् to nourish, aff. क्त, deriv. irr., or तप् to inflame, aff.<BR>क्त, and the radical letters transposed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=452-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पित्तघ्न
पित्तघ्न mfn. (-घ्नः-घ्नी-घ्नं) Anti-bilious.<BR>	 f. (-घ्नी) A plant, (Menispermum<BR>glabrum.)<BR>	 n. (घ्नं) Ghee.<BR> E. पित्त bile, and घ्न what destroys.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=452-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पित्तज्वर|पित्तज्वरः
पित्तज्वर m. (-रः) Bilious fever.<BR> E. पित्त bile, and ज्वर fever.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=452-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पित्तद्राविन्
पित्तद्राविन् mfn. (-वी-विणी-वि) Removing bile, causing it to flow.<BR> E. पित्त,<BR>and द्राविन् what disperses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=452-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पित्तरक्त|पित्तरक्तं
पित्तरक्त n. (-क्तं) Plethora. See रक्तपित्त.<BR> E. पित्त, and रक्त blood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=452-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पित्तल|पित्तलं
पित्तल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Bilious, relating to the bilious humour.<BR>	 n.<BR>(-लं)<BR>	 1. Brass.<BR>	 2. The Bhūrjapatra or Birch tree, of which the<BR>bark is used for writing upon, &c.<BR>	 f. (-ला) A plant, (Jussieua<BR>repens.)<BR> E. पित्त bile, ला to get, to resemble, (in colour,) aff. ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=452-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पित्र्य|पित्र्यं|पित्र्यः
पित्र्य mfn. (-त्र्यः-त्र्या-त्र्यं)<BR>	 1. Paternal, ancestral.<BR>	 2. Obsequial, relating<BR>to deceased progenitors.<BR>	 m. (-त्र्यः)<BR>	 1. An elder brother.<BR>	 2. The<BR>month of māgha.<BR>	 n. (-त्र्यं) The part of the hand between the<BR>forefinger and thumb, sacred to the manes.<BR>	 f. (-त्र्या)<BR>	 1. One of<BR>the lunar asterisms, called Maghā.<BR>	 2. Day of full moon.<BR>	 3.<BR>Ceremonies performed in honour of the deceased on the day of full<BR>or new moon.<BR> E. पितृ a father, and यत् aff., रीङ् substituted for ऋ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=452-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पित्सत्|पित्सन्त्
पित्सत् mfn. (-सन्-सन्ती-सत्)<BR>	 1. Habitually falling or coming down.<BR>	 2.<BR>Obtained, gained.<BR>	 m. (-सन्) A bird.<BR> E. पत् to fall or alight, शतृ<BR>aff., and desiderative form; the reduplicate syllable omitted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=452-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पित्सल|पित्सलं|पित्सलः
पित्सल n. (-लं) A road, a path, &c.<BR> E. पत् to go, Unādi aff. सल,<BR>form irr; or correctly पत् सन् पित्स + आधारे कलच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=452-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिदधत्
पिदधत् mfn. (-धन्-धन्ती-धत्) Covering, veiling, hiding.<BR> E. अपि before,<BR>धा to have, श तृ aff. and the initial rejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=452-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिधान|पिधानं
पिधान n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. A covering, a cover or concealment.<BR>	 2. A lid, a top<BR>or cover.<BR>	 3. A sheath.<BR>	 4. A wrapper, a cloak, &c.<BR> E. अपि<BR>certainly, धा to have or hold, (from sight,) ल्युट् aff., and the<BR>initial rejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=452-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिधानक|पिधानकं
पिधानक n. (-कं) A sheath, a scabbard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=452-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिधायक
पिधायक f. (का) Covering, hiding, concealing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=452-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिनद्ध|पिनद्धः
पिनद्ध mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>	 1. Clothed.<BR>	 2. Accoutred.<BR>	 3. Dressed.<BR>	 4. Con-<BR>cealed.<BR>	 5. Pierced.<BR> E. अपि, and नह् to bind, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=452-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिनस
पिनस m. (-सः) Cold, catarrh: see पीनस.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=452-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिनह्य
पिनह्य ind. Having put on or dressed.<BR> E. अपि before, नह् to tie, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=452-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिनाक|पिनाकं|पिनाकः
पिनाक mn. (-कः-कं)<BR>	 1. The bow of ŚIVA.<BR>	 2. A trident or three-pronged<BR>spear.<BR>	 3. The trident of ŚIVA.<BR>	 4. A shower of dust.<BR>	 f. (-की) A<BR>musical instrument, a sort of viol.<BR> E. पा to preserve, (the world,)<BR>Unādi aff. आकन्, the radical vowel changed to इ, and नुम्<BR>augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=452-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिनाकिन्
पिनाकिन् m. (-की) ŚIVA.<BR> E. पिनाक ŚIVA'S bow or trident, and<BR>इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=452-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिन्यास|पिन्यासं|पिन्यासः
पिन्यास n. (-सं) Asafœtida.<BR> E. अपि before, न्यस् (compounded of नि and<BR>अस् to throw,) to be given or placed in condiments, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=452-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिपतिषत्|पिपतिषन्त्
पिपतिषत् mfn. (-षन्-षन्ती-षत्) Inclined or addicted to falling repeatedly.<BR>m. (-षन्) A bird.<BR> E. पत् to come down, in the desiderative form,<BR>and शतृ participial aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=452-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिपतिषा
पिपतिषा f. (-षा) Wish or inclination to come down, to fall, &c.<BR> E. पत्<BR>to fall, desid. form, अङ् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=452-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिपतिषु|पिपतिषुः
पिपतिषु mfn. (-षुः-षुः-षु) Disposed to fall or descend.<BR>	 m. (-षुः) A bird.<BR>E. पत् to fall, desid. form, उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=452-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिपविषु
पिपविषु mfn. (-षुः-षुः-षु) Wishing to purify.<BR> E. पू to be pure, desid.<BR>v., उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=452-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिपासत्|पिपासन्त्
पिपासत् mfn. (-सन्-सन्ती-सत्) Thirsty, thirsting.<BR> E. पा to drink, desid.<BR>v., शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=452-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिपासा
पिपासा f. (-सा) Thirst.<BR> E. पा to drink, in the desiderative form, अङ्<BR>and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=452-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिपासित|पिपासितः
पिपासित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Thirsty, athirst.<BR> E. पिपासा thirst, and इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=452-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिपासु|पिपासुः
पिपासु mfn. (-सुः-सुः-सु) Thirsty, athirst.<BR> E. पा to drink, desid. form,<BR>and उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=452-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिपीतकी
पिपीतकी f. (-की) The twelfth of the month Vaisākha, when giving<BR>away water is an act of merit.<BR> E. पिपीतक the name of a Brāhman,<BR>said to have instituted the rite, ङीष् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=452-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिपीलक|पिपीलकः
पिपीलक m. (-कः) A large black ant.<BR>	 f. (-लिका) The common small<BR>red ant.<BR> E. अपि, पील to stop, ण्वुल् aff. and the initial rejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=452-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिपीलिक|पिपीलिकः
पिपीलिक m. (-कः) An ant.<BR>	 n. (कं) A kind of gold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=452-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिपृच्छिषु
पिपृच्छिषु mfn. (-षुः-षुः-षु) Wishing to ask.<BR> E. प्रच्छ् to ask, desid. v.,<BR>उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=452-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिप्पटा
पिप्पटा f. (-टा) A kind of sweetmeat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=452-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिप्पल|पिप्पलं|पिप्पलः
पिप्पल m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. The holy fig-tree, (Ficus religiosa.)<BR>	 2. A bird.<BR>3. The sleeve of a jacket or coat.<BR>	 4. A nipple.<BR>	 n. (-लं)<BR>	 1.<BR>Water.<BR>	 2. A berry of the holy fig-tree.<BR>	 3. A berry in general.<BR>	 4.<BR>Sensual enjoyment.<BR>	 f. (-ली) Long-pepper.<BR> E. पा to preserve, aff.<BR>कलच् and the root reiterated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=452-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिप्पलक|पिप्पलकं
पिप्पलक n. (-कं)<BR>	 1. A nipple.<BR>	 2. Sewing thread.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=452-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिप्पलि|पिप्पलिः
पिप्पलि f. (-लिः) Long-pepper: see पिप्पल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=452-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिप्पलीमूल|पिप्पलीमूलं
पिप्पलीमूल n. (-लं) The root of long-pepper.<BR> E. पिप्पली, and मूल the<BR>root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=452-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिप्पिका
पिप्पिका f. (-का) The tartar of the teeth.<BR> E. पाय् to increase, aff. इक,<BR>deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=452-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिप्लु|पिप्लुः
पिप्लु m. (-प्लुः) A freckle, a mark, a mole.<BR> E. अपि certainly, प्लुष् to<BR>burn or inflame, aff डु ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=452-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिब्दमाना
पिब्दमाना f. (-ना) Noising.<BR> E. अपि certainly, शब्द sound, and शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=452-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पियाल|पियालः
पियाल m. (-लः) A tree, called in Hindi also Chironji, (whence it has<BR>been named Chironjia sapida, Rox. in the catalogue it is<BR>termed Buchanania, latifolia, Rox.;) in Bengal, commonly Piya<BR>or Piyal.<BR> E. पीय a sautra root, to regard, Unādi aff. कालन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=452-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिल
पिल r. 10th cl. (पेलयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To throw, to cast or send.<BR>	 2. To incite.<BR>चु० उभ० सक० स्रेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=452-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिलुक|पिलुकः
पिलुक m. (-कः) A tree: see पीलु.<BR> E. पिल् to send, aff. कु, and कन्<BR>added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=452-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिलनी
पिलनी f. (-नी) A plant; see मूर्वा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=452-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिल्ल|पिल्लः
पिल्ल mfn. (-ल्लः-ल्ली-ल्लं) Blear-eyed.<BR>	 m. (-ल्लः) A bleared eye.<BR> E. पिल्ल<BR>considered as a substitute for क्लिन्न wet. &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=452-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिल्लका
पिल्लका f. (-का) A female elephant.<BR> E. पिल्ल blear-eyed, aff. कन्; the<BR>elephant's eye being usually moist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=452-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिव
पिव(इ,)पिवि r. 1st cl. (पिन्वति) To sprinkle, to wet or moisten. भ्वा० पर०<BR>सक० सेट्-इदित् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=452-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिव
पिव mfn. (-व-वा-वं) Who or what drinks.<BR> E. पा to drink, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=452-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिवत्
पिवत् mfn. (-वन्-वन्ती-वत्) Drinking.<BR> E. पा to drink, शत aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=452-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिश
पिश r. 1st. cl. (पिंशति)<BR>	 1. To be decomposed, to be reduced to consti-<BR>tuent parts.<BR>	 2. To be organised.<BR>	 3. To enlighten, to light. अवयवे<BR>समूहस्यांशभावे अक० दीपनायांसक० तुदा० मुचा० पर० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=452-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिश
पिश(स) mfn. (-शः-शा-शं) Free from sin.<BR>	 n. (शं) Having many forms. E.<BR>पिश to organise, aff. क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=452-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिशङ्ग|पिशंग|पिशङ्गः
पिशङ्ग mfn. (-ङ्गः-ङ्गा-ङ्गी-ङ्गं) Of a tawny or brown colour.<BR>	 m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>Tawny, (the colour.)<BR> E. पिश् to be a component part, अङ्गच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=452-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिशङ्गक|पिशंगक|पिशंगकः|पिशङ्गकः
पिशङ्गक m. (-क) An epithet of VIṢṆU.<BR> E. पिशङ्ग, स्वार्थे क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=452-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिशङ्गता
पिशङ्गता f. (-ता) Tawniness.<BR> E. तल् added to the last; also with त्व,<BR>पिशङ्गत्व ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=452-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिशङ्गिन्|पिशंगिन्
पिशङ्गिन् mfn. (-ङ्गी-ङ्गिनी-ङ्गि) Brown, tawny.<BR> E. पिशङ्ग, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=452-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिशाच|पिशाचः
पिशाच m. (-चः) A goblin, a fiend, a malevolent being something<BR>between an infernal imp and a ghost, but always described as<BR>fierce and malignant.<BR>	 f. (-ची) A female imp, a she-demon.<BR> E. पिश<BR>for पिशित flesh, and अश् to eat, aff. अण्, deriv. irr.; According to<BR>Vāchaspatya:--पिशितमाचामति आ + चम-बा-ड० पृषो० । also with कन्<BR>added, पिशाचक, पिशाचिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=452-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिशाचकिन्
पिशाचकिन् m. (-की) KUVERA, the god of wealth.<BR> E. पिशाच a demon,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=453-a" target="_blank">Page453-a+ 60</a>]<BR>इनि aff., and कुक् augment; the treasures of this deity being<BR>guarded by Pīṣāchas, and other malignant beings.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=452-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिशाचद्रु|पिशाचद्रुः
पिशाचद्रु m. (-द्रुः) A tree, (Trophis aspera.)<BR> E. पिशाच a goblin, and द्रु<BR>a tree; the favourite haunt of these beings.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=453-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिशाचवृक्ष|पिशाचवृक्षः
पिशाचवृक्ष m. (-क्षः) The Śākhoṭa tree: see the last.<BR> E. पिशाच, and वृक्ष a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=453-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिशाचभाषा
पिशाचभाषा f. (-षा) One of the lowest Prākrita dialects used in plays.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=453-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिशाचसभ|पिशाचसभं
पिशाचसभ n. (-भं)<BR>	 1. An assemblage of goblins or fiends.<BR>	 2. The<BR>place or hall of their assembly, pandemonium.<BR> E. पिशाच a goblin,<BR>and सभा assembly, but neuter in this compound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=453-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिशाचसञ्चार|पिशाचसंचारः
पिशाचसञ्चार m. (-रः) Demoniacal possession.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=453-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिशाचालय|पिशाचालयः
पिशाचालय m. (-यः) Phosphorescense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=453-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिशित|पिशितं
पिशित n. (-तं) Flesh.<BR>	 f. (-ता) Spikenard.<BR>	 m. (-तः)<BR>	 1. A goblin.<BR>	 2. A<BR>cannibal<BR> E. पिश् to be a component part, participial aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=453-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिशिताशन|पिशिताशनः
पिशिताशन mfn. (-नः-नी-नं) Eating meat.<BR>	 m. (-नः) A demon, a fiend, a<BR>cannibal.<BR> E. पिशित, and अशन food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=453-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिशिताशिन्
पिशिताशिन् mfn. (-शी-शिनी-शि) Eating flesh or meat, carnivorous.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-शी) A goblin, a cannibal.<BR> E. पिशित, and अश् to eat, aff. घिणुन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=453-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिशील|पिशीलं
पिशील n. (-लं) A shallow earthen dish.<BR> E. पिस, ईल aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=453-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिशुन|पिशुनं|पिशुनः
पिशुन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>	 1. Cruel, wicked.<BR>	 2. Vile, low, contemptible.<BR>3. Stupid, a fool.<BR>	 n. (-नं) Saffron.<BR>	 m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. A spy, an informer,<BR>a tale-bearer, a slanderer, a traitor.<BR>	 2. A name of NĀRADA.<BR>	 3.<BR>A crow.<BR>	 4. Cotton.<BR>	 f. (-ना) A gramineous plant, “पिडिङ्शाक”<BR>(Trigonella corniculata.)<BR>	 2. Indicating, making known, evincing.<BR>3. Calumniating, back-biting.<BR>	 4. unkind.<BR> E. पिश् to be a part, उनन्<BR>Unādi aff., and the vowel unchanged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=453-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिशुनवचन
पिशुनवचन n. (-नं) Evil speech, abuse, detraction, slander.<BR> E. पिशुन and वचन speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=453-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिशुनवाक्य
पिशुनवाक्य n. (-क्यं) Evil speech, bad report, detraction, slander. E.<BR>पिशुन, and वाक्य speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=453-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिष
पिष r.<BR>	 7. th cl. (पिनष्टि) To grind, to pound, to bruise or powder. r.<BR>10th cl. (पेषयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To injure.<BR>	 2. To give.<BR>	 3. To be strong.<BR>	 4.<BR>To dwell. r. 1st and 10th cls. (पेषति पेषयति-ते) To go or move.<BR>चूर्णने रु० पर० सक० अनिट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=453-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिष्ट|पिष्टं
पिष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>	 1. Ground, pounded, bruised.<BR>	 2. Clasped, (as the<BR>hands,) squeezed, rubbed together.<BR>	 3. Kneaded.<BR>	 n. (-ष्टं)<BR>	 1. Lead.<BR>2. The flour or meal of any thing that is ground.<BR> E. पिष् to<BR>pound or bruise, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=453-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिष्टक|पिष्टकं|पिष्टकः
पिष्टक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A cake made of the flour or meal of any grain.<BR>2. A disease of the eyes, opacity of the cornea.<BR>	 n. (-कं) Oil-cake.<BR>E. पिष्ट what is pound, कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=453-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिष्टप|पिष्टपं|पिष्टपः
पिष्टप mn. (-पः-पं) A world, a division of the universe.<BR> E. पिश् to go,<BR>अप् Unādi aff., and टन् augment; or विश-कप् dev. irr. also विष्टप.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=453-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिष्टपचन|पिष्टपचनं
पिष्टपचन n. (-नं) A boiler, a seether, a sauce-pan, a pan for parch-<BR>ing flour.<BR> E. पिष्ट meal, &c. and पचन cooking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=453-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिष्टपशु|पिष्टपशुः
पिष्टपशु m. (-शुः) A type or effigy of a victim, made with flour.<BR> E. पिष्ट,<BR>and पशु an animal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=453-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिष्टपाकभृत्
पिष्टपाकभृत् m. (-भृत्) A boiler.<BR> E. पिष्ट meal, पाक cooking, and भृत् what makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=453-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिष्टपाचक
पिष्टपाचक n. (-कं) A boiler.<BR> E. पिष्ट, and पाचक what cooks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=453-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिष्टपूर|पिष्टपूरः
पिष्टपूर n. (-रं) Meal, made up into a sort of cake with clarified<BR>butter.<BR> E. पिष्ट meal, and पॄ to complete, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=453-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिष्टपेषण
पिष्टपेषण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Grinding flour, (literally.)<BR>	 2. Vain repetition,<BR>useless occupation, (figuratively.)<BR> E. पिष्ट, पिष् to grind ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=453-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिष्टमय
पिष्टमय mfn. (-यः-यी-यं) Made of meal or flour, &c.<BR> E. पिष्ट that which<BR>is ground, मयट् transformative aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=453-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिष्टमेह|पिष्टमेहः
पिष्टमेह m. (-हः) A kind of urinary disease.<BR> E. पिष्ट, मिह् to pass<BR>as urine, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=453-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिष्टवर्त्ति|पिष्टवर्ति|पिष्टवर्तिः|पिष्टवर्त्तिः
पिष्टवर्त्ति m. (-र्त्तिः) A small cake, made of barley, rice or pulse ground<BR>to meal.<BR> E. पिष्ट meal, and वृत् to be, इन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=453-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिष्टसौरभ|पिष्टसौरभं
पिष्टसौरभ n. (-भं) Sandal.<BR> E. पिष्ट ground, and सौरभ fragrant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=453-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिष्टात|पिष्टातः
पिष्टात m. (-तः) Perfumed powder, for scenting rooms, garments, &c.<BR>especially the scented dust, which the Hindus sprinkle over each<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=453-b" target="_blank">Page453-b+ 60</a>]<BR>other at the Holi or spring festival.<BR> E. पिष्ट pounded, (saffron<BR>&c.) and अत् to go or be, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=453-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिष्टिक|पिष्टिकं
पिष्टिक n. (-कं) A cake made of rice flour.<BR>	 f. (-का) The meal of pulse<BR>steeped in water, peeled and ground.<BR> E. पिष्ट ground, ठन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=453-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिस
पिस(ऋ)पिसृ r. 1st cl. (पेसति) To go or move. r. 10th cl. (पेसयति-ते)<BR>	 1.<BR>To go.<BR>	 2. To be strong.<BR>	 3. To injure or hurt.<BR>	 4. To give.<BR>	 5. To<BR>dwell. (इ) पिसि r. 10th cl. (पिंसयति)<BR>	 1. To speak.<BR>	 2. To shine.<BR>	 3.<BR>To destroy. गतौ भ्वा० पर० सक० सेट् । दींप्तौ चु० उम० पक्षे भ्वा० पर० अक० सेट्-<BR>इदित् । वासे वलेच अक० वधे दाने गतौच सक० चुरा० उभ० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=453-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिसङ्ग
पिसङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः) Tawny (the colour): see पिशङ्ग.<BR> E. पिस, अङ्गच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=453-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिहित|पिहितं
पिहित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Covered, hidden, concealed.<BR>	 2. Filled with.<BR>3. Shut, barred.<BR> E. अपि before, धा to have, aff. क्त, and the initial<BR>of the prefix rejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=453-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पी
पी(ङ)पीङ् r. 4th cl. (पीयते) To drink. दि० सक० आत्म० अनिट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=453-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीच|पीचं
पीच n. (-चं) The lower jaw, the chin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=453-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीठ|पीठं
पीठ mfn. (-ठः-ठी-ठं)<BR>	 1. A stool, a seat, a chair.<BR>	 2. The seat of the reli-<BR>gious student, made properly of Kuśa grass.<BR>	 3. A place where<BR>some limb of PĀRVATĪ is supposed to have fallen, as after Daks-<BR>ha's sacrifice, her dead body was carried about by ŚIVA, and<BR>cut in pieces by the discus of VIṢṆU: there are fifty-one such<BR>places.<BR>	 4. Complement of a segment, (in Geometry.)<BR>	 5. A<BR>pedestal.<BR>	 6. A particular posture in sitting.<BR> E. पिठ् to be weary,<BR>to feel pain, aff. घञ्; deriv. irr. or पा-ठक् पिठ-क वा पृषो० दीर्घः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=453-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीठकेलि|पीठकेलिः
पीठकेलि m. (-लिः) A male confidant, a parasite.<BR> E. पीठ a seat, केलि<BR>sport.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=453-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीठगर्भ|पीठगर्भः
पीठगर्भ m. (-र्भः) The cavity in the Pedestal of an idol.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=453-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीठचक्र
पीठचक्र n. (-क्रं) A car or carriage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=453-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीठनायिका
पीठनायिका f. (-का) A girl of fourteen who personates Durgā on the<BR>occasion of the festival of that goddess.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=453-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीठभू
पीठभू f. (-भू) Basement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=453-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीठमर्द्द|पीठमर्द|पीठमर्दः|पीठमर्द्दः
पीठमर्द्द m. (-र्द्दः)<BR>	 1. A parasite, a companion.<BR>	 2. A dancing master<BR>who gives instruction in that art to courtezans.<BR> E. पीठ a seat,<BR>and मृद् to rub, aff. घञ्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=453-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीठसर्पिन्
पीठसर्पिन् m. (-र्पी) A cripple, who moves about on a wheeled chair,<BR>&c.<BR> E. पीठ a seat, and सर्पिन् who moves.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=453-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीठस्थान
पीठस्थान n. (-नं) A place where some limb of PĀRVATĪ is supposed to<BR>have fallen: see पीठ.<BR> E. पीठ, and स्थान place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=453-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीठिका
पीठिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. A bench.<BR>	 2. A festival.<BR>	 3. A chapter of a book.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=453-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीड
पीड(ऋ)पीडृ r. 10th cl. (पीडयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To give pain, to annoy, to<BR>hurt.<BR>	 2. To oppose or resist.<BR>	 3. To stir, to agitate.<BR>	 4. To<BR>squeeze or pinch.<BR>	 5. To cover with anything inauspicious.<BR>6. To press, (as corns.) बधे विलोडनेच चु० उभ० सक० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=453-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीडन|पीडनं
पीडन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Inflicting pain, paining, distressing.<BR>	 2. Devastation,<BR>laying a country waste.<BR>	 3. Squeezing, pressing, rubbing.<BR>	 4. Tak-<BR>ing, holding, as in पाणिपीडन “taking the hand” i. e. marrying.<BR>	 5.<BR>Threshing, (corn).<BR>	 6. An instrument for pressing.<BR>	 7. An eclipse,<BR>(In astronomy).<BR>	 8. A fault in the pronounciation of vowels. E.<BR>पीड् to give pain, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=453-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीडा
पीडा f. (-डा)<BR>	 1. Pain, anguish, suffering.<BR>	 2. Compassion, charity,<BR>pity.<BR>	 3. Devastation, laying waste.<BR>	 4. A chaplet, a garland for the<BR>head.<BR>	 5. The Saral tree, (Pinus longifolia.)<BR>	 6. Infraction, viola-<BR>tion.<BR>	 7. Damage, injury.<BR> E. पीड् to pain, अङ् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=453-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीडाकर
पीडाकर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Giving pain, afflicting, tormenting. Adj.<BR>Painful.<BR> E. पीडा, and कर who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=453-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीडाकरण
पीडाकरण n. (-णं) Torturing, tormenting.<BR> E. पीडा, and करण making.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=453-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीडित|पीडितं
पीडित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Bound, tied.<BR>	 2. Pained, suffering pain or dis-<BR>tress.<BR>	 3. Laid waste, destroyed, devastated.<BR>	 4. Rubbed, chafed.<BR>	 5.<BR>Squeezed, pressed.<BR>	 6. Espoused: see पीडन.<BR>	 7. Violated.<BR>	 8. Op-<BR>pressed, harassed.<BR>	 9. Eclipsed.<BR>	 n. (-तं)<BR>	 1. Injuring, harassing.<BR>	 2.<BR>A mode of sexual enjoyment.<BR> E. पीडा pain, इतच् aff. or पीड-क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=453-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीडितम
पीडितम It is used as an indeclinable in the sense of “fast,” “closely.”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=454-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीड्यमान
पीड्यमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>	 1. Being pained or afflicted.<BR>	 2. Suffering from.<BR>3. Being squeezed or pressed.<BR> E. पीड् to pain, pass. v., शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=454-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीत|पीतं|पीतः
पीत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Of a yellow colour.<BR>	 2. Drank, quaffed.<BR>	 m. (-तः)<BR>1. Yellow, the colour.<BR>	 2. Safflower.<BR>	 3. A topaz, a yellow gem.<BR>4. A yellow pigment, prepared from the urine of kine.<BR>	 n. (-तं)<BR>	 1.<BR>Drinking.<BR>	 2. Yellow orpiment.<BR>	 3. Gold.<BR>	 4. Sulphur.<BR>	 f. (-ता)<BR>	 1.<BR>Turmeric.<BR>	 2. A medical plant, commonly Ātāich, (Betula.)<BR>	 3.<BR>Saturated, steeped.<BR>	 4. Drunk.<BR> E. पा to drink, aff. क्त; imbibed,<BR>literally, or figuratively, by the eye sight, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=454-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीतक|पीतकं|पीतकः
पीतक n. (-कं)<BR>	 1. Yellow orpiment.<BR>	 2. Saffron.<BR>	 3. Aloe-wood.<BR>	 4.<BR>Brass.<BR>	 5. Honey.<BR>	 m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A sort of gentian, (G. Cherayta.)<BR>2. The Ṭun tree.<BR> E. पीत yellow, aff. कन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=454-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीतकदली
पीतकदली f. (-ली) A sort of Plantain.<BR> E. पीत yellow, कदली plantain.<BR>“चांपाकला” ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=454-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीतकन्द|पीतकंद|पीतकन्दं
पीतकन्द n. (-न्दं) The carrot.<BR> E. पीत yellow, and कन्द root. “गोंजर” ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=454-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीतकावेर|पीतकावेरं
पीतकावेर n. (-रं)<BR>	 1. Saffron.<BR>	 2. Brass.<BR> E. पीत yellow, कावेर vile shape<BR>or substance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=454-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीतकाष्ठ|पीतकाष्ठं
पीतकाष्ठ n. (-ष्ठं) Yellow sanders.<BR> E. पीत yellow, काष्ठ wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=454-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीतघोषा
पीतघोषा f. (-षा) A sort of creeper with yellow flowers.<BR> E. पीत, and<BR>घोषा the plant; yellow Ghosa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=454-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीतचन्दन|पीतचंदन|पीतचन्दनं
पीतचन्दन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. A yellow fragrant wood, considered as a yellow<BR>species of Sandal wood.<BR>	 2. Turmeric.<BR>	 3. Saffron.<BR> E. पीत yellow,<BR>and चन्दन Sandal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=454-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीतचम्पक|पीतचंपक|पीतचम्पकः
पीतचम्पक m. (-कः) A lamp.<BR> E. पीत yellow, चम्पक a flower, and कन् aff.<BR>of comparison; like the Champaka in colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=454-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीतता
पीतता f. (-ता) Yellowness.<BR> E. पीत, and तल् aff.; also with त्व, पीतत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=454-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीततुण्ड|पीततुंड|पीततुण्डः
पीततुण्ड m. (-ण्डः) The taylor bird, (Sylvia sutoria.) पीत yellow, and<BR>तुण्ड a beak; the whole bird is of a light yellow colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=454-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीततैला
पीततैला f. (-ला) A sort of creeper, a species of the heart-pea.<BR> E. पीत<BR>yellow, तैल oil. “ज्योतिष्मतीलतायाम्” ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=454-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीतदारु
पीतदारु m. (-रुः)<BR>	 1. A sort of pine, (P. Devadāru.)<BR>	 2. Another kind of<BR>pine, (Pinus longifolia.)<BR> E. पीत yellow, and दारु wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=454-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीतदुग्धा
पीतदुग्धा f. (-ग्धा)<BR>	 1. A cow tied up to be milked.<BR>	 2. Any milch cow. E.<BR>पीत drank, दुग्ध milk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=454-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीतद्रु|पीतद्रुः
पीतद्रु m. (-द्रुः)<BR>	 1. A sort of Curcuma, (C. zanthorrhizon.)<BR>	 2. A<BR>species of pine, (P. longifolia.)<BR> E. पीत yellow, and द्रु a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=454-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीतन|पीतनं|पीतनः
पीतन m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. The hog-plum, (Spondias mangifera.)<BR>	 2. A tree.<BR>(Pentaptera tomentosa.)<BR>	 3. The waved-leaf fig-tree.<BR>	 n. (-नं)<BR>	 1.<BR>Saffron.<BR>	 2. A sort of pine: see पीतदारु.<BR>	 3. Yellow orpiment. E.<BR>पीत yellow, णी to go, or be, aff. ड; or पीत, णिच्-ल्यु ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=454-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीतपर्णी
पीतपर्णी f. (-र्णी) A plant, commonly Bichati; a name applied to the<BR>nettle, or a plant of the same class, (Tragia involucrata.)<BR> E. पीत<BR>yellow, and पर्ण leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=454-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीतपादा
पीतपादा f. (-दा) A small bird, the Maina, (Turdus salica.)<BR> E. पीत yel-<BR>low, पाद a foot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=454-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीतपुष्प|पीतपुष्पं|पीतपुष्पः
पीतपुष्प m. (-ष्पः)<BR>	 1. A species of Karnikāra.<BR>	 2. A sort of Tabernæm-<BR>ontana.<BR>	 f. (-ष्पा-ष्पी) Yellow barleria.<BR> E. पीत yellow, and पुष्प a<BR>flower; it may also be applied to any plant with yellow flowers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=454-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीतफल|पीतफलः
पीतफल m. (-लः) A tree, (Trophis aspera.)<BR> E. पीत yellow, फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=454-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीतबालुका
पीतबालुका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. Turmeric.<BR>	 2. Yellow sand.<BR> E. पीत yellow, and<BR>बालुका sand or dust.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=454-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीतमणि|पीतमणिः
पीतमणि m. (-णिः) A yellow gem, a topaz.<BR> E. पीत yellow, and मणि a gem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=454-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीतमाक्षिक|पीतमाक्षिकं
पीतमाक्षिक n. (-कं) The common Pyritic iron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=454-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीतमस्तक
पीतमस्तक m. (-कः) A small bird, (Loxia philippensis.)<BR> E. पीत yellow,<BR>and मस्तक the head.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=454-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीतमुण्ड
पीतमुण्ड m. (-ण्डः) A gallinule.<BR> E. पीत yellow, मुण्ड the head.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=454-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीतमुद्ग|पीतमुद्गः
पीतमुद्ग m. (-द्गः) A sort of bean, a yellow variety of the phaseolus<BR>Mūng.<BR> E. पीत yellow, and मुद्ग Mūng.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=454-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीतमूलक|पीतमूलकं
पीतमूलक n. (-कं) The carrot.<BR> E. पीत, मूल the root, aff. कप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=454-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीतयूथी
पीतयूथी f. (-थी) Yellow jasmine.<BR> E. पीत, and यूथी jasmine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=454-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीतरक्त|पीतरक्तं
पीतरक्त n. (-क्तं) A yellow coloured gem, perhaps the topaz.<BR> E. पीत<BR>yellow, and रक्त coloured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=454-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीतराग|पीतरागं|पीतरागः
पीतराग m. (-गः)<BR>	 1. The fibres of the lotus.<BR>	 2. A yellow colour.<BR>	 n.<BR>(कं) Wax.<BR> E. पीत and राग colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=454-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीतल|पीतलः
पीतल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Of a yellow colour.<BR>	 m. (-लः) Yellow, the<BR>colour.<BR>	 n. (-लं) Brass.<BR> E. पीत, and लच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=454-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीतलक|पीतलकं
पीतलक n. (-कं) Brass.<BR> E. पीतल yellow, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=454-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीतलोह|पीतलोहं
पीतलोह n. (-हं) Yellow brass, queen's metal, or a mixed metal,<BR>resembling gold.<BR> E. पीत yellow, and लोह iron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=454-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीतवासस्
पीतवासस् mfn. (-साः-साः-सः) Dressed in yellow.<BR>	 m. (-साः) A name of<BR>KṚṢṆA<BR> E. पीत yellow, वासस् vesture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=454-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीतवृक्ष|पीतवृक्षः
पीतवृक्ष m. (-क्षः) A plant (Bignonia Indica.) “श्योनाकवृक्षे” ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=454-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीतशाल|पीतशालः
पीतशाल m. (-लः) A tree, (Pentaptera.)<BR> E. पीत yellow, and शाल the Sāl tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=454-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीतसार|पीतसारं|पीतसारः
पीतसार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Sandal.<BR>	 2. A yellow gem, a topaz.<BR>	 3. A tree,<BR>(Alangium hexapetalum.)<BR>	 n. (-रं) A yellow sort of Sandal wood.<BR>E. पीत yellow, and सार essence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=454-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीतसारि
पीतसारि n. (-रि) Antimony.<BR> E. पीत yellow, सार essence, aff. इन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=454-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीतसालक|पीतसालकः
पीतसालक m. (-कः) A tree, (Pentaptera tomentosa.)<BR> E. पीत yellow, सार<BR>essence, aff. क, and र changed to ल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=454-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीतसोम
पीतसोम m. (-मः) A Brāhman, by whom the juice of the acid asclepias<BR>is drank at a ceremony.<BR> E. पीत, and सोम the juice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=454-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीतस्कन्ध|पीतस्कंध|पीतस्कन्धः
पीतस्कन्ध m. (-न्धः) A hog.<BR> E. पीत for पीन large, and स्कन्ध a shoulder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=454-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीतस्फटिक|पीतस्फटिकः
पीतस्फटिक m. (-कः) A precious gem, the topaz.<BR> E. पीत yellow, and<BR>स्फटिक crystal. “पुष्परागमणौ” ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=454-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीतहरित
पीतहरित adj. Yellowish green.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=454-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीताब्धि|पीताब्धिः
पीताब्धि m. (-ब्धिः) The Muni AGASTYA.<BR> E. पीत drank, (by whom,) and<BR>अब्धि the ocean; the saint having on one occasion swallowed up<BR>the sea.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=454-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीताम्बर|पीतांबर|पीताम्बरः
पीताम्बर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Dressed in yellow clothes.<BR>	 m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. KṚṢṆA<BR>or VIṢṆU in that form.<BR>	 2. A dancer or actor.<BR>	 3. A religious<BR>mendicant, wearing yellow garments.<BR> E. पीत yellow, अम्वर<BR>vesture, raiment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=454-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीतारुण|पीतारुणः
पीतारुण adj. Yellowish red.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=454-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीताश्मन्
पीताश्मन् n. (-श्म) A topaz or any yellow gem.<BR> E. पीत, and अश्मन् a stone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=454-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीति|पीतिः
पीति m. (-तिः) A horse.<BR>	 f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Drinking.<BR>	 2. A dram shop.<BR>	 3. The<BR>Proboscis of an elephant.<BR> E. पा to drink, aff. क्तिच् or क्तिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=454-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीतिका
पीतिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. Turmeric.<BR>	 2. Yellow jasmine.<BR>	 3. Saffron.<BR> E. पीत<BR>yellow, णिच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=454-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीतिन्
पीतिन् m. (-ती) A horse.<BR> E. पा to drink, क्तिन् aff., इन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=454-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीतु|पीतुः
पीतु m. (-तुः)<BR>	 1. The sun.<BR>	 2. Fire.<BR>	 3. The chief elephant of a herd. E.<BR>पा to drink, (or dry up water,) and तुन् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=454-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीत्वा
पीत्वा ind. Having drank.<BR> E. षा to drink, क्त्वाच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=454-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीथ|पीथं|पीथः
पीथ m. (-थः)<BR>	 1. The sun.<BR>	 2. Fire.<BR>	 3. Time.<BR>	 n. (-थं) Water.<BR> E. पा to<BR>drink, Uṇadi aff. थक्, and the radical vowel changed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=454-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीथि|पीथिः
पीथि m. (-थिः) A horse: see पीति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=454-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीन|पीनः
पीन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Fat, bulky, corpulent, large, much, round,<BR>thick.<BR> E. प्यै to grow or enlarge, aff. क्त, form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=454-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीनस|पीनसः
पीनस m. (-सः)<BR>	 1. Cough, catarrh.<BR>	 2. Cold, affecting the nose, in-<BR>flammation of the schneiderian membrane.<BR> E. पीन fat, षो to<BR>destroy, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=454-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीनसिन्
पीनसिन् mfn. (-सी-सिनी-सि) Having a cold.<BR> E. पीनस, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=454-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीनोध्नी
पीनोध्नी f. (-ध्नी) A cow with full or large udders.<BR> E. पीन large, सधस् an<BR>udder, ङीप् aff. and अनङ् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=454-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीपर
पीपर r. 1st cl. (पीपरति) To beg. भ्वा० सक० पर० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=454-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीय
पीय r. 1st cl. (पीयति)<BR>	 1. To please.<BR>	 2. To injure. सौ-पर० सक० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=454-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीयु|पीयुः
पीयु m. (-युः)<BR>	 1. The sun.<BR>	 2. Time.<BR>	 3. An owl.<BR>	 4. A crow.<BR> E. पीय a<BR>Sautra root, to regard, Unādi aff. उ; or पा-कु; der. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=454-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीयूष|पीयूषं|पीयूषः
पीयूष n. (षं)<BR>	 1. The food of the gods, ambrosia, nectar.<BR>	 2. Milk.<BR>	 mn.<BR>(-षः-षं) The milk of a cow during the first seven days after calv-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=455-a" target="_blank">Page455-a+ 60</a>]<BR>ing.<BR> E. पीय Sautra root, to be kind or love, ऊषन् Unādi aff. In<BR>the last sense the word is also written पेयूष ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=454-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीयूषमहस्
पीयूषमहस् m. (-हाः)<BR>	 1. The moon.<BR>	 2. Camphor.<BR> E. पीयूष nectar, and<BR>महस् light; whose rays are filled with nectar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=455-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीयूषरुचि|पीयूषरुचिः
पीयूषरुचि m. (-चिः)<BR>	 1. The moon.<BR>	 2. Camphor.<BR> E. पीयूष nectar, and<BR>रुचि light: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=455-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीयूषवर्ष|पीयूषवर्षः
पीयूषवर्ष m. (-र्षः)<BR>	 1. A shower of water.<BR>	 2. The moon.<BR>	 3. Camphor. E.<BR>पीयूषं वर्षति करद्वारा-वृष-अण् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=455-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पील
पील r. 1st cl. (पीलति)<BR>	 1. To stop, to cease to be or do.<BR>	 2. To become<BR>stupid. भ्वा० पर० सक० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=455-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीलक|पीलकः
पीलक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. The large black ant.<BR>	 2. An opposer.<BR> E. पील् to<BR>stop; aff. ण्वुल् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=455-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीलु|पीलुः
पीलु m. (-लुः)<BR>	 1. The name of a tree, applied in some places to the<BR>Careya arborea, and in others to the Salvadora persica; it is<BR>very commonly assigned also to all exotic, and unknown trees.<BR>2. An elephant.<BR>	 3. An arrow.<BR>	 4. A flower.<BR>	 5. The blossom of the<BR>Saccharum sara.<BR>	 6. An atom.<BR>	 7. An insect.<BR>	 8. The metacarpus,<BR>the central part of the hand.<BR>	 9. The stem of the palm tree. E.<BR>पील् to stop, aff. उ; also with कन् added, पीलुक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=455-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीलुक|पीलुकः
पीलुक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A kind of worm.<BR>	 2. An ant. E. see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=455-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीलुनी
पीलुनी f. (-नी) A kind of creeper called murbā.<BR> E. पील, उन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=455-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीलुपर्णी
पीलुपर्णी f. (-र्णी)<BR>	 1. A plant: see पीलु.<BR>	 2. Bryonia grandis.<BR>	 3. A sort of<BR>drug.<BR> E. पीलु the tree, and पर्ण a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=455-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीलुमूल
पीलुमूल n. (-लं)<BR>	 1. A plant called shatamuli and shatābari. (Aspara-<BR>gus racemosus.)<BR>	 2. A shrub called shālaparni, (Hedysarum gange-<BR>ticum.)<BR>	 3. A plant called Ashwagandhā, (Physalis flexuosa.)<BR>	 4.<BR>A young cow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=455-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीव
पीव r. 1st cl. (पीवति) To be fat or corpulent. भ्वा० पर-अक० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=455-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीवन्
पीवन् mfn. (-वा-वा-व)<BR>	 1. Fat, large.<BR>	 2. Strong, robust.<BR>	 3. Full, fast,<BR>stout.<BR>	 m. (-वा) Air, wind.<BR> E. प्ये to swell or increase, Unādi<BR>aff. क्वनिप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=455-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीवर|पीवरः
पीवर mfn. (-रः-रा-री-रं) Fat large.<BR>	 f. (-रा-री) A plant, (Asparagus<BR>racemosus.)<BR>	 f. (-री)<BR>	 1. A young woman.<BR>	 2. A cow.<BR>	 m. (-रः) A tor-<BR>toise.<BR> E. प्यै to increase, Unādi aff. ष्वरच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=455-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीवरस्तनी
पीवरस्तनी f. (-नी)<BR>	 1. A cow with large udders.<BR>	 2. A woman with large<BR>breast.<BR> E. पीवर large, and स्तन a breast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=455-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीवा
पीवा f. (-वा) Water.<BR> E. पी to drink, वन् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=455-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुंध्वज
पुंध्वज m. (-जः)<BR>	 1. The male of any species of animal.<BR>	 2. A mouse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=455-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुंनाग|पुन्नाग|पुन्नागः
पुंनाग m. (-गः)<BR>	 1. A white elephant 2. A white lotus.<BR>	 3. A nutmeg.<BR>	 4.<BR>A name of the tree commonly called Nāgakesara, (mesua ferrea.)<BR>5. A distinguished man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=455-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुंयोग|पुंयोगः
पुंयोग m. (-गः) Association or cohabitation with men.<BR> E. पुम्, and योग union.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=455-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुंराशि|पुंराशिः
पुंराशि m. (-शिः) A male sign of the zodiac.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=455-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुंलिङ्ग|पुंलिङ्गं
पुंलिङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>	 1. The male organ.<BR>	 2. The masculine gender, (in<BR>grammar.)<BR> E. पुम् male, and लिङ्ग mark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=455-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुंवत्स|पुंवत्सः
पुंवत्स m. (-त्सः) A bull-calf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=455-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुंवृष|पुंवृषः
पुंवृष m. (षः) The musk-rat.<BR> E. पुम् male, and वृष a bull. “छुछुन्दरे” ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=455-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुंवेष
पुंवेष adj. Wearing male attire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=455-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुंश्चली
पुंश्चली f. (-ली) A harlot, an unchaste woman.<BR> E. पुंस् a man, and चल् to<BR>go, affs. अच् and ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=455-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुंश्चिह्न|पुंश्चिह्नं
पुंश्चिह्न n. (-ह्नं) The penis.<BR> E. पुंस् male, and चिह्न a mark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=455-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुंस
पुंस r. 10th cl. (-पुंसयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To punish, to pain.<BR>	 2. To crush, to<BR>grind. चु० उभ० सक० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=455-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुंसवन|पुंसवनं
पुंसवन n. (-नं) The first of the essential ceremonies of Hindu initia-<BR>tion; a religious and domestic festival held on a woman's per-<BR>ceiving the first signs of a living conception.<BR>	 2. Milk.<BR>	 3. Fetus.<BR>E. पुम् a male, सू to bear aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=455-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुंसानुज
पुंसानुज m. (-जः) Having an elder brother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=455-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुंस्कामा
पुंस्कामा f. (-मा) A woman wishing for a husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=455-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुंस्कोकिल|पुंस्कोकिलः
पुंस्कोकिल m. (-लः) A male cuckoo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=455-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुंस्त्व|पुंस्त्वं
पुंस्त्व n. (-स्त्वं)<BR>	 1. Semen virile.<BR>	 2. Manhood, virility.<BR>	 3. The masculine<BR>gender, (In gram.)<BR> E. पुम् man, and त्व aff. of the abstract; also<BR>with तल् aff., पुंस्ता f. (-स्ता.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=455-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुक्कश|पुक्कशः
पुक्कश(स) m. (-शः- or -सः) A Chaṇḍāla, an outcaste: see पुक्कस.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=455-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुक्कस|पुक्कसः
पुक्कस mfn. (-सः-सी-सं) Low, vile.<BR>	 m. (-सः) A Chaṇḍala, or man of an<BR>impure and degraded tribe or occupation, born of the Nishāda<BR>by a Śūdra female.<BR>	 f. (-सी)<BR>	 1. Indigo.<BR>	 2. A bud, a blossom.<BR>	 3. A<BR>woman of the Pukkasa tribe.<BR> E. पु for पुण्य purity, कु bad<BR>(understood,) कस् to go, aff. अच्, deriv. irr. or appropriately<BR>पुक् कुत्सतिं कसति कस-गतौ अच् पृषो० वा शः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=455-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुङ्ख|पुंख|पुंखं|पुंखः|पुङ्खः
पुङ्ख m. (-ङ्खः)<BR>	 1. The feathered part of an arrow.<BR>	 2. A falcon, a<BR>heron.<BR> E. पुम् man, खन् to destroy, aff. ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=455-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुङ्ग|पुंग|पुंगं|पुंगः|पुङ्गः
पुङ्ग mn. (-ङ्गः-ङ्गं) A heap, a collection, a quantity.<BR> E. पुं man, गम<BR>to go, aff. ड ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=455-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुङ्गल|पुंगल|पुंगलः|पुङ्गलः
पुङ्गल m. (-लः) The soul.<BR> E. पुं man, and गल् to pervade, aff. अच्; also read पुद्गल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=455-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुङ्गव|पुंगव|पुङ्गवः
पुङ्गव m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. A bull.<BR>	 2. A drug, commonly Mashāni.<BR>	 3. (In compo-<BR>sition,) Excellent, pre-eminent.<BR> E. पुं male, and गौ a cow, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=455-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुङ्गवकेतु
पुङ्गवकेतु m. (-तुः) An epithet of SĪVA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=455-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुच्छ|पुच्छं|पुच्छः
पुच्छ r. 1st cl. (पुच्छति) To err, to be careless or inattentive. भ्वा० पर० अक० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=455-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुच्छ|पुच्छं|पुच्छः
पुच्छ mn. (-च्छः-च्छं)<BR>	 1. A tail, the tail, the hinder part.<BR>	 2. A horse's<BR>tail.<BR>	 3. The tail of the peacock.<BR>	 4. Any hairy tail.<BR>	 5. The end<BR>of anything.<BR> E. पुच्छ to be careless, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=455-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुच्छकण्टक|पुच्छकंटक|पुच्छकण्टकः
पुच्छकण्टक m. (-कः) A scorpion. “वृश्चिके” ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=455-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुच्छजाह
पुच्छजाह n. (-हं) The root of the tail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=455-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुच्छटि|पुच्छटिः
पुच्छटि(टी) f. (-टि or टी) Snapping or cracking the fingers. E.<BR>पुच्छ-अटि वा ङीप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=455-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुच्छिन्
पुच्छिन् mfn. (-च्छी-च्छिनी-च्छि) Having a tail.<BR>	 m. (-च्छी) A cock.<BR> E. पुच्छ a tail, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=455-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुञ्ज|पुंज|पुंजः|पुञ्जः
पुञ्ज m. (-ञ्जः) A heap, a quantity, a collection.<BR> E. पुं man, जन् to be<BR>born, aff. ड; also पुङ्ग and पुञ्जि m. (-ञ्जिः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=455-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुञ्जिक|पुंजिक|पुंजिकः|पुञ्जिकः
पुञ्जिक m. (-कः) Hail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=455-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुञ्जित|पुंजित
पुञ्जित f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Heaped.<BR>	 2. Pressed together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=455-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुञ्जिष्ठ|पुञ्जिष्ठः
पुञ्जिष्ठ mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठा-ष्ठं) Heaped, accumulated.<BR> E. पुञ्जि, and स्थ who or what stays.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=455-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुट|पुटं|पुटः
पुट r. 1st cl. (पोटति) To rub, to press, to grind or pound. r. 6th cl.<BR>(पुटति) To embrace, to intertwine. r. 10th cl. (पोटयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To<BR>be or become small, or shallow.<BR>	 2. To shine.<BR>	 3. To speak.<BR>	 4. To<BR>reduce to powder, to grind. r. 10th cl. (पुटयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To<BR>fasten, to string, to bind together.<BR>	 2. To be in contact with. दीप्तौ<BR>अक० चूर्णने सक० चुरा० उभ० सेट् । श्लेषे तु० कु० पर० सक० सेट् । संसर्गे अद० चुरा०<BR>उभ० सक० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=455-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुट|पुटं|पुटः
पुट mfn. (-टः-टी-टं)<BR>	 1. A cover, a covering.<BR>	 2. A plate or vessel, made<BR>of leaves.<BR>	 3. A cloth worn to cover the privities.<BR>	 4. An eyelid.<BR>	 5.<BR>A cup or concavity, made of a leaf folded or doubled.<BR>	 6. A con-<BR>cavity, a shallow cup or receptacle, as the hollow of the hand.<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>	 1. A horse's hoof.<BR>	 2. A narrowing or contracting of any<BR>thing.<BR>	 3. A folding or doubling of any thing, so as to form a cup<BR>or concavity.<BR>	 4. A casket.<BR>	 n. (-टं)<BR>	 1. Two vessels joined together,<BR>the upper one inverted for the sublimation or digestion of<BR>medicaments.<BR>	 2. A nutmeg.<BR> E. पुट् to rub or bind, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=455-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुटक|पुटकं
पुटक n. (-कं)<BR>	 1. A lotus.<BR>	 2. A bag or vessel made of a leaf doubled<BR>over in a funnel-like shape.<BR>	 3. Any shallow cup or concavity.<BR>4. A nutmeg.<BR> E. पुट् to unite, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=455-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुटकिनी
पुटकिनी f. (-नी)<BR>	 1. An assemblage of lotus flowers.<BR>	 2. A lotus.<BR> E. पुटक, and इनि, aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=455-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुटग्रीव|पुटग्रीवः
पुटग्रीव m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. A pot, a jar, a pitcher.<BR>	 2. A brass or copper<BR>vessel or jug.<BR> E. पुट a contracting, from पुट, and ग्रीवा the<BR>neck; having a narrow neck.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=455-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुटपाक|पुटपाकः
पुटपाक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. Digesting, subliming.<BR>	 2. A method of preparing<BR>drugs; in it the various ingredients are wrapped up in leaves<BR>covered with clay and baked in fire.<BR> E. पुट, and पाक cooking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=455-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुटभेद|पुटभेदः
पुटभेद m. (-दः)<BR>	 1. The bend of, or an eddy in a river.<BR>	 2. A city,<BR>a town.<BR>	 3. A musical instrument.<BR> E. पुट a contraction, and भेद<BR>breaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=455-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुटभेदन|पुटभेदनं
पुटभेदन n. (-नं) A city.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=456-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुटिका
पुटिका f. (-का) Cardamoms.<BR> E. पुटमस्त्यस्याः ठन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=456-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुटित|पुटितं
पुटित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Sewn, stitched.<BR>	 2. Rubbed, ground.<BR>	 3. Con-<BR>tracted.<BR>	 n. (-तं) Closing or shutting the hands, (to hold anything;)<BR>the hollow of the hand.<BR> E. पुट rubbing, &c. and इतच्. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=456-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुटोटज
पुटोटज n. (-जं) A white umbrella or parasol.<BR> E. पुट a covering, and<BR>उटज a house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=456-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुटोदक|पुटोदकः
पुटोदक m. (-कः) The cocoanut.<BR> E. पुट a covering, and उदक water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=456-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुट्ट
पुट्ट r. 10th cl. (पुट्टयति-ते) To decrease, to diminish, to be or become<BR>small, low or shallow. चु० उभ० सक० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=456-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुड
पुड r. 6th cl. (पुडति)<BR>	 1. To leave, to quit.<BR>	 2. To discover.<BR>	 3. To emit.<BR>(इ) पुडि r. 1st cl. (पुण्डति)<BR>	 1. To rub.<BR>	 2. To grind or pound, to<BR>reduce to dust or powder.<BR>	 3. To adorn. मर्दने भ्वा० पर० सक०<BR>सेट्-इदित् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=456-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण
पुण r. 6th cl. (पुणति) To be pure or virtuous, to do a pious or holy<BR>act. तु० पर० सक० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=456-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्ड|पुंड|पुंडः|पुण्डः
पुण्ड m. (-ण्डः) A mark made with sandal &c. on the forehead.<BR> E. पुडि to adorn, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=456-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्डरिन्
पुण्डरिन् m. (-री) A drug, commonly Puṇderīya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=456-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्डरीक|पुंडरीक|पुंडरीकं|पुण्डरीकं|पुण्डरीकः
पुण्डरीक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. The elephant presiding over the south-east<BR>quarter.<BR>	 2. A leopard.<BR>	 3. A sort of snake called Rajila;<BR>(Amphisbœna.)<BR>	 4. A fragrant kind of mango.<BR>	 5. Fever affecting<BR>an elephant.<BR>	 6. A variety of the sugarcane.<BR>	 7. A silk worm,<BR>(कोषकार)<BR>	 8. A student's waterpot “Kamandalu.” 9. White,<BR>the colour.<BR>	 10. A sort of leprosy.<BR>	 11. A species of rice.<BR>12. Fire.<BR>	 13. A mark on the forehead with sandal, &c.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>	 1. A white lotus.<BR>	 2. A lotus in general.<BR>	 3. A white<BR>umbrella.<BR>	 4. A kind of drug.<BR> E. पुडि to grind; or according<BR>to some, to adorn, Unādi aff. ईक, and the form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=456-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्डरीकाक्ष|पुंडरीकाक्ष|पुण्डरीकाक्षं|पुण्डरीकाक्षः
पुण्डरीकाक्ष m. (-क्षः) A name of VIṢṆU.<BR>	 n. (-क्षं) A drug.<BR> E. पुण्डरीक<BR>a lotus, and अक्षि an eye, aff. षच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=456-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्डरीयक|पुण्डरीयकं
पुण्डरीयक n. (-कं)<BR>	 1. A flower, (Hibiscus mutabilis.) “स्थलपद्म.” 2.<BR>A drug, commonly Punḍerīya.<BR> E. पुण्डरिन् + आचारेक्यच् ततः ण्वुल् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=456-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्डर्य्य|पुण्डर्य|पुंडर्यं|पुण्डर्य्यं
पुण्डर्य्य n. (-र्य्यं) A creeper, a medicinal plant, used as a remedy for<BR>diseased eyes.<BR> E. पुडि to dissipate, (disease,) अर्य्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=456-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्ड्र|पुंड्र|पुंड्रः|पुण्ड्रः
पुण्ड्र n. (-ण्ड्रं)<BR>	 1. A red variety of the common sugarcane, (Saccharum<BR>officinarum.)<BR>	 2. The name of a Daitya or infernal being, consi-<BR>dered as incarnate in ŚISUPĀLA.<BR>	 3. A mark or line made on<BR>the forehead with Sandal, &c.<BR>	 4. A sort of creeper, (Gærtnera<BR>racemosa.)<BR>	 5. A worm.<BR>	 6. A white lotus.<BR>	 7. The name of a<BR>country, the greater part of Bengal and part of Behar.<BR>	 m. plu.<BR>(-ण्ड्राः) The inhabitants of that country.<BR> E. पुडि to rub, aff. रक् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=456-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्ड्रक|पुंड्रक|पुंड्रकः|पुण्ड्रकः
पुण्ड्रक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A creeper, (Gærtnera racemosa.)<BR>	 2. A mark on<BR>the forehead with Sandal, &c.<BR>	 3. A sort of sugarcane: see the<BR>last.<BR> E. कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=456-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्ड्रकेलि|पुंड्रकेलि|पुण्ड्रकेलिः
पुण्ड्रकेलि m. (-लिः) An elephant.<BR> E. पुण्ड्र sugarcane, and केलि pastime.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=456-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्य|पुण्यं
पुण्य mfn. (-ण्यः-ण्या-ण्यं)<BR>	 1. Virtuous, pure, righteous.<BR>	 2. Beautiful,<BR>pleasing.<BR>	 3. Fragrant.<BR>	 n. (-ण्यं)<BR>	 1. Virtue, moral or religious merit.<BR>2. A good action.<BR>	 3. Purity, purification.<BR>	 4. A trough for watering<BR>cattle.<BR>	 f. (-ण्या)<BR>	 1. Holy basil, (Ocymun sanctum.)<BR>	 2. Lucky,<BR>auspicious.<BR>	 3. Solemn, festive.<BR> E. पूञ् to be or make pure,<BR>यत् Unādi aff., and ण्वुक् augment; or appropriately पू-डुण्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=456-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्यक|पुण्यकं|पुण्यकः
पुण्यक n. (कं) A meritorious act or obligation of a religious nature,<BR>as fasting, praying, &c.<BR> E. पुण्य virtue, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=456-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्यकर्म्मन्|पुण्यकर्मन्
पुण्यकर्म्मन् mfn. (-र्म्मा-र्म्मा-र्म्म) Pious, virtuous.<BR> E. पुण्य, and कर्म्मन् act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=456-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्यकन्नत
पुण्यकन्नत n. (-तं) The worship of KṚṢṆA for a year, with daily<BR>presents, to be performed by a woman desirous of a son.<BR> E. पुण्यक,<BR>and व्रत religious obligation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=456-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्यकाल|पुण्यकालः
पुण्यकाल m. (-लः) An auspicious time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=456-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्यकीर्त्ति|पुण्यकीर्ति
पुण्यकीर्त्ति m. (-त्तिः) Celebrated, famous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=456-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्यकृत्
पुण्यकृत् mf. (-कृत्) Virtuous, pious.<BR> E. पुण्य virtue, and कृत् who acts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=456-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्यक्षेत्र
पुण्यक्षेत्र n. (-त्रं) Holy land or Āryābarta: see पुण्यमू ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=456-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्यगन्ध|पुण्यगंध|पुण्यगन्धः
पुण्यगन्ध m. (-न्धः) The Champaka, (Michelia champaca.) Adj. Sweet-<BR>scented.<BR> E. पुण्य pure, and गन्ध smell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=456-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्यगृह
पुण्यगृह n. (-हं)<BR>	 1. An alms-house.<BR>	 2. A temple.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=456-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्यजन|पुण्यजनः
पुण्यजन m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. A fiend, a goblin, a Rākshasa.<BR>	 2. A Yakṣa, a<BR>divine being attendant on KUVERA, the god of wealth.<BR>	 3. A<BR>pious or virtuous man.<BR> E. पुण्य virtuous, and जन man, ङीष् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=456-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्यजनेश्वर|पुण्यजनेश्वरः
पुण्यजनेश्वर m. (-रः) KUVERA, the Hindu deity of wealth.<BR> E. पुण्यजन a<BR>Yakṣa, and ईश्वर master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=456-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्यजित
पुण्यजित adj. Attained by good works.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=456-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्यतीर्थ
पुण्यतीर्थ n. (-र्थं) A holy shrine or place of pilgrimage.<BR> E. पुण्य, तीर्थ, sacred pool, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=456-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्यतृण|पुण्यतृणं
पुण्यतृण n. (-णं) White Kuśa grass.<BR> E. पुण्य, and तृण grass: it is much<BR>used in religious ceremonies.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=456-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्यदर्शन|पुण्यदर्शनः
पुण्यदर्शन m. (-नः) The blue jay.<BR>	 n. (-नं) Visiting holy shrines.<BR>E. पुण्य lucky, and दर्शन appearance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=456-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्यपुरुष|पुण्यपुरुषः
पुण्यपुरुष m. (-षः) A man rich in moral merit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=456-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्यप्रताप|पुण्यप्रतापः
पुण्यप्रताप m. (-पः) The efficacy of moral merit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=456-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्यफल|पुण्यफलः
पुण्यफल m. (-लः) A grove, a garden.<BR>	 n. (-लं) The reward or consequence<BR>of good actions.<BR> E. पुण्य handsome or virtue, and फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=456-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्यभाज्
पुण्यभाज् mfn. (-भाक्) Virtuous, addicted to virtue.<BR> E. पुण्य, and भाज्<BR>who possesses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=456-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्यभू
पुण्यभू f. (-भूः) The holy land of the Hindus; the central part of Asia,<BR>bounded on the north by the Himālaya, on the south by the<BR>Vindhya mountains, and on the east and west by the sea.<BR> E. पुण्य<BR>virtue, and भू land.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=456-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्यभूमि|पुण्यभूमिः
पुण्यभूमि f. (-मिः)<BR>	 1. The holy land or Āryāvarta: see the last.<BR>	 2.<BR>The mother of a male child.<BR> E. पुण्य virtue, and भूमि land.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=456-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्यरात्र|पुण्यरात्रः
पुण्यरात्र m. (-त्रः) A night on which any religious commemoration or<BR>ceremony is held.<BR> E. पुण्य, and रात्रि night, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=456-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्यलोक|पुण्यलोकः
पुण्यलोक m. (-कः) Heaven, paradise.<BR> E. पुण्य virtue, and लोक a world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=456-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्यवत्|पुण्यवन्त्
पुण्यवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>	 1. Fortunate, well-fated.<BR>	 2. Virtuous,<BR>pious, righteous.<BR>	 3. Happy.<BR> E. पुण्य virtue, &c. aff. मतुप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=456-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्यविजित
पुण्यविजित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Merited, acquired by merit.<BR> E. पुण्य, and<BR>विजित conquered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=456-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्यशकुन|पुण्यशकुनः
पुण्यशकुन m. (-नः) A bird of good omen.<BR>	 n. (-नं) An auspicious omen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=456-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्यशील
पुण्यशील mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Virtuous.<BR> E. पुण्य and शील having.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=456-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्यश्लोक|पुण्यश्लोकः
पुण्यश्लोक adj. Of good fame.<BR>	 m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A name of NALA.<BR>	 2. The<BR>epithet is also applied to YUDHISṬHIRA, and to VIṢṆU.<BR>	 f. (-का)<BR>1. A name of DRAUPADĪ.<BR>	 5. A name of SĪTA.<BR> E. पुण्य holy, श्लोक<BR>verse: who is celebrated in sacred poems.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=456-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्ययोग|पुण्ययोगः
पुण्ययोग m. (-गः) The influence or effect of virtuous actions.<BR> E. पुण्य,<BR>and योग union.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=456-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्यस्थान
पुण्यस्थान n. (-नं) A sacred place, a holy ground, a place of pilgrimage.<BR>E. पुण्य virtue, and स्थान a place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=456-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्यात्मन्
पुण्यात्मन् mfn. (-त्मा-त्मा-त्म) Holy, pious.<BR> E. पुण्य, and आत्मन् spirit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=456-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्याह|पुण्याहं
पुण्याह n. (-हं) A holy day.<BR> E. पुण्य holy, and अहन् a day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=456-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्याहवाचन|पुण्याहवाचनं
पुण्याहवाचन n. (नं) Repeating at sacrifices, &c. “This is a holy day,”<BR>three times.<BR> E. पुण्याह, and वाचन saying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=456-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्योदय|पुण्योदयः
पुण्योदय m. (-यः) Good fortune, as the result of virtuous acts in a<BR>former life.<BR> E. पुण्य, and उदय rise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=456-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्योद्यान
पुण्योद्यान adj. Having beautiful gardens.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=456-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्
पुत् n. (-पुत्) A hell to which the childless are condemned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=456-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्त
पुत्त r. 1st cl. (पुत्तति) To go. सौ० भ्वा-पर० सक० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=456-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्तल|पुत्तलः
पुत्तल mf. (-लः-ली)<BR>	 1. An idol, a puppet, a doll.<BR>	 2. A man of straw<BR>burnt in place of a lost corpse: see पर्णनर ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=456-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्तिका
पुत्तिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. A small bee.<BR>	 2. The white ant.<BR> E. पुत् to go, तिक<BR>Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=456-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्त्र
पुत्त्र(त्र) m. (-त्त्रः)<BR>	 1. A son.<BR>	 2. A child, in the language of the Vedas.<BR>3. The fifth mansion from the point of conjunction of the sun, and<BR>a zodiacal sign.<BR>	 f. (-त्त्री) A daughter. du. always, (-त्त्री) Son and<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=457-a" target="_blank">Page457-a+ 60</a>]<BR>daughter.<BR> E. पुत्, and त्रा to preserve, the hell, (from,) aff. क; or<BR>पूज् to purify, aff. त्त्र; one त may be rejected in writing this word,<BR>and its derivatives, leaving पुत्र. The word is thus derived by<BR>Manu. viz:--<BR>“पुन्नाम्नो नरकाद्यस्मात् पितरं त्रायते सुतः ।<BR>तस्मात्पुत्र इति प्रोक्तः खयमेव स्वयंभूवा ॥”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=456-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्त्रक
पुत्त्रक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A son.<BR>	 2. A son, as it were, used as a term of<BR>endearment.<BR>	 3. A fabulous animal with eight legs: see शरभ.<BR>4. A rogue, a cheat.<BR>	 5. A particular mountain.<BR>	 6. A sort of tree.<BR>7. A grasshopper, a locust.<BR>	 8. A doll, a puppet.<BR>	 f. (-त्रका or -त्रिका)<BR>1. A daughter.<BR>	 2. A puppet, a doll.<BR>	 3. Anything little of its<BR>kind, (when used at the end of a compound.)<BR> E. पुत्र a son, कन्<BR>pleonasm; in the feminine from the substitution of इ for the<BR>penultimate vowel is optional.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=457-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्त्रकन्दा
पुत्त्रकन्दा f. (-न्दा) A kind of drug. “लक्षणामूले” ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=457-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्त्रकाम्या
पुत्त्रकाम्या f. (-म्या) Wish or affection for progeny.<BR> E. पुत्त्र, and काम्यच् aff. अ being added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=457-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्त्रकार्य्य
पुत्त्रकार्य्य n. (-र्य्यं) Ceremony relating to a son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=457-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्त्रकृतक
पुत्त्रकृतक m. (-कः) Adopted as a son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=457-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्त्रजात
पुत्त्रजात Adj. One to whom a son is born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=457-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्त्रजीव
पुत्त्रजीव m. (-वः) A tree, from the fruit of which necklaces are made<BR>of supposed prolific efficacy, (Nagelia putranjiva, Rox.)<BR> E. पुत्त्र a<BR>child, and जीव life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=457-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्त्रञ्जीवक
पुत्त्रञ्जीवक m. (-कः) A plant; see the last.<BR> E. पुत्त्र a child, and जीव् to live,<BR>aff. खश् and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=457-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्त्रद
पुत्त्रद mfn. (-दः-दा-दं) Who or what confers offspring.<BR> E. पुत्त्र, and द, what gives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=457-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्त्रदार
पुत्त्रदार n. (-रं) Son and wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=457-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्त्रपौत्र
पुत्त्रपौत्र mn. (-त्रः-त्रं) Plu. Sons and grandsons.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=457-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्त्रपौत्रीण
पुत्त्रपौत्रीण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Descended from son to son.<BR> E. पुत्त्र, and पौत्र<BR>a grandson, खश् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=457-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्त्रपौत्रीणता
पुत्त्रपौत्रीणता f. (-ता) Perpetual descent from son to son, &c.<BR> E. पुत्त्रपौत्रीण, and तल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=457-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्त्रप्रतिनिधि
पुत्त्रप्रतिनिधि m. (-धिः) A substitute for a son, as an adopted son, &c. E.<BR>पुत्त्र, and प्रतिनिधि a substitute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=457-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्त्रलाभ
पुत्त्रलाभ m. (-भः) The obtaining of a son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=457-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्त्रवत्
पुत्त्रवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Having a son or offspring.<BR> E. पुत्त्र, and मतुप् poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=457-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्त्रवधू
पुत्त्रवधू f. (-धू) A daughter-in-law.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=457-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्त्रवल
पुत्त्रवल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Having a son or child.<BR> E. पुत्त्र, and वलच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=457-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्त्रश्रेणी
पुत्त्रश्रेणी f. (-णी) A plant, (Salvinia cucullata.) “मूषिकपर्ण्याम्” ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=457-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्त्रमख
पुत्त्रमख m. (-खः) One who is fond of children.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=457-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्त्रसू
पुत्त्रसू f. (-सूः) The mother of a son.<BR> E. पुत्त्र a son, and सू a parent. aff. क्विप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=457-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्त्रहीन
पुत्त्रहीन Adj. Childless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=457-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्त्राचार्य्य
पुत्त्राचार्य्य m. (-र्य्यः) A father instructed in sacred science by his son.<BR> E. पुत्त्र, and आचार्य्य a teacher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=457-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्त्रार्थिन्
पुत्त्रार्थिन् Adj. Wishing for a son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=457-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्त्रान्नाद
पुत्त्रान्नाद m. (-दः)<BR>	 1. One who is maintained by his son.<BR>	 2. A mendicant<BR>of a particular order.<BR> E. पुत्त्र a son, अन्न food, and आद who takes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=457-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्त्रिका
पुत्त्रिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. A daughter.<BR>	 2. A doll, a puppet.<BR>	 3. The cotton or<BR>pappus of the tamarisk.<BR> E. पुत्त्री a daughter, कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=457-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्त्रिकापुत्त्र
पुत्त्रिकापुत्त्र m. (-त्त्रः)<BR>	 1. The son of a daughter, appointed to raise issue<BR>for her father; one of the twelve heirs acknowledged by the old<BR>Hindu law.<BR>	 2. A daughter's son, who by agreement becomes<BR>the son of her father, (according to some interpretation.)<BR>	 3. A<BR>daughter who returns to her father's house being considered as<BR>his son, (according to other interpretation.)<BR>	 4. A grandson in<BR>general.<BR> E. पुत्त्रिका a daughter, and पुत्त्र a son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=457-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्त्रिकाभर्त्तृ
पुत्त्रिकाभर्त्तृ m. (-र्त्ता) A daughter's husband.<BR> E. पुत्त्रिका, and भर्त्तृ husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=457-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्त्रिकाप्रसू
पुत्त्रिकाप्रसू f. (-सूः) The mother of a daughter.<BR> E. पुत्त्रिका, and प्रसू a<BR>mother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=457-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्त्रिकासुत
पुत्त्रिकासुत m. (-तः) A daughter's son, a grandson.<BR> E. पुत्त्रिका, and सुत a son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=457-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्त्रिन्
पुत्त्रिन् m. (-त्त्री) The father of a son.<BR>	 f. (-णी)<BR>	 1. The mother of a son, or<BR>of children generally.<BR>	 2. A parasite plant.<BR>	 3. A plant, (Siphonan-<BR>thus Indica.)<BR> E. पुत्त्र a son or offspring, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=457-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्त्रीय
पुत्त्रीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Belonging or relating to a son, or child.<BR>	 2. Filial.<BR>f. (-या) The desire of a son.<BR> E. पुत्त्र, and छ aff.; also पुत्त्र्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=457-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्त्रीयत्
पुत्त्रीयत् mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्) Wishing for a son.<BR> E. पुत्त्र, and क्यच् aff. or<BR>nominal v., शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=457-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्त्रेप्सु
पुत्त्रेप्सु mfn. (-प्सुः-प्सुः-प्सु) Desiring a son.<BR> E. पुत्त्र, and इप्सु desirous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=457-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्त्रेष्टि
पुत्त्रेष्टि f. (-ष्टिः) A sacrifice performed for the purpose of obtaining<BR>children.<BR> E. पुत्त्र, offspring, and इष्टि sacrifice; also with कन् added<BR>in the feminine form, पुत्त्रेष्टिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=457-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्त्रैश्वर्य्य
पुत्त्रैश्वर्य्य n. (-र्य्यं) Resignation of property or power by a father to his<BR>son.<BR> E. पुत्त्र, and ऐशर्य्य masterhood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=457-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्त्र्य
पुत्त्र्य mfn. (-त्त्र्यः-त्त्र्या-त्त्र्यं) Belonging to a son, &c.<BR> E. पुत्त्र, and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=457-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुथ
पुथ r. 4th cl. (पुथ्यति) To hurt or kill. r. 10th cl. (पोथयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To shine.<BR>2. To speak. (इ) पुथि r. 1st cl. (पुन्थति)<BR>	 1. To hurt.<BR>	 2. To suffer pain<BR>or uneasiness. हिंसे दिवा० पर० सक० सेट् । वधे० सक० क्लेशे अक० भ्वा० पर० सेट०<BR>इदित् । दीप्तौ चु० उभ० सक० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=457-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुद्गल|पुद्गलः
पुद्गल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>	 1. Beautiful, handsome, of a handsome form or<BR>figure.<BR>	 2. Having form or property.<BR>	 m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. The body.<BR>	 2. The<BR>soul.<BR>	 3. An atom.<BR>	 4. An epithet of Śiva.<BR> E. पूर what fills, and गल<BR>what decays, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=457-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुनःपाक
पुनःपाक m. (-कः) Repeated boiling or cooking.<BR> E. पुनर्, and पाक dressing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=457-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुनःपुनर्
पुनःपुनर् Ind. Repeatedly, again and again.<BR> E. पुनर् again, repeated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=457-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुनःपुना
पुनःपुना f. (-ना) The Pumpā river in Bihar.<BR> E. पुनर् again, repeated,<BR>irrly.; perhaps from the meandering course of the river; or cor-<BR>rectly पुनः पुनाति पू-नक्-पृषो० ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=457-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुनःसन्धान
पुनःसन्धान n. (-नं) Reuniting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=457-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुनःसम्भव|पुनःसंभवः
पुनःसम्भव m. (-वः) Coming into existence again, metempsychosis.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=457-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुनःसंस्कार|पुनःसंस्कारः
पुनःसंस्कार m. (-रः) Repetition of any essential ceremony, as re-investi-<BR>ture with the sacrificial string of a Brāhman, who has forfeited<BR>it by unknowingly drinking spirits, &c.<BR> E. पुनर् again, संस्कार<BR>ceremony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=457-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुनर्
पुनर् Ind.<BR>	 1. Again, once more.<BR>	 2. But, on the contrary, neverthe-<BR>less, however.<BR>	 3. Assuredly, certainly.<BR>	 4. A particle indicating<BR>division or change of subject.<BR> E. पण् to praise, अर् aff., and the<BR>radical vowel changed to उ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=457-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुनरपि
पुनरपि Ind.<BR>	 1. Even, again, also.<BR>	 2. And, on the other hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=457-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुनरर्थिता
पुनरर्थिता f. (-ता) Repeated request.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=457-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुनरागत
पुनरागत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Come back, returned.<BR> E. पुनर्, and आगत come.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=457-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुनरागमन|पुनरागमनं
पुनरागमन n. (-नं) Returning, coming back.<BR> E. पुनर् and आगमन coming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=457-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुनराधान
पुनराधान n. (-नं) Renewing or replacing a consecrated fire.<BR> E. पुनर्,<BR>and आधान placing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=457-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुनरावर्त्त|पुनरावर्त|पुनरावर्तः
पुनरावर्त्त m. (-र्त्तः)<BR>	 1. Return, revolution.<BR>	 2. Repeated birth.<BR> E. पुनर्, and आवर्त्त revolving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=457-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुनरावर्त्तिन्|पुनरावर्तिन्
पुनरावर्त्तिन् mfn. (-र्त्ती-र्त्तिनी-र्त्ति)<BR>	 1. Returning.<BR>	 2. Subject to successive<BR>births.<BR> E. पुनरावर्त्त, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=457-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुनरावृत्
पुनरावृत् f. (-वृत्)<BR>	 1. Repetition.<BR>	 2. Revision.<BR>	 3. Return to mundane existence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=457-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुनरुक्त|पुनरुक्तं
पुनरुक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं) Repeated, said over again.<BR>	 n. (-क्तं) Tautology,<BR>repetition.<BR> E. पुनर्, and उक्त said.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=457-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुनरुक्तजन्मन्
पुनरुक्तजन्मन् m. (-न्मा) A Brāhman.<BR> E. पुनर् again, उक्त said, and जन्मन्<BR>birth; whose investiture is called a second birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=457-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुनरुक्तवदाभास
पुनरुक्तवदाभास m. (-सः) A figure of speech consisting in the appearance<BR>of tautology, the first impression being removed by a right<BR>understanding of the passage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=457-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुनरुक्ति|पुनरुक्तिः
पुनरुक्ति f. (-क्तिः)<BR>	 1. Repetition, tautology.<BR>	 2. Uselessness.<BR> E. पुनर्, and उक्ति saying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=457-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुनरुत्थान
पुनरुत्थान n. (-नं) Resurrection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=457-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुनरुत्पत्ति
पुनरुत्पत्ति f. (-त्ति)<BR>	 1. Reproduction.<BR>	 2. Metempsychosis.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=457-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुनरुपगम|पुनरुपगमः
पुनरुपगम m. (-मः) Return.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=457-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुनरुपोढा
पुनरुपोढा f. (-ढा) A woman remarried.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=457-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुनर्गम
पुनर्गम Ind. To go back.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=457-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुनर्जन्मन्
पुनर्जन्मन् mfn. (-न्मा-न्मा-न्म) Re-born, born again.<BR>	 n. (-न्म) Regeneration,<BR> E. पुनर्, and जन्म birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=457-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुनर्जन्मजय
पुनर्जन्मजय m. (-यः) Liberation, final emancipation, freedom from<BR>transmigration.<BR> E. पुनर्जन्म, and जय Victory.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=457-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुनर्दा
पुनर्दा Ind. To give back.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=458-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुनर्दारक्रिया
पुनर्दारक्रिया f. (-या) Taking a second wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=458-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुनर्न
पुनर्न(र्ण)व m. (-वः) A finger-nail.<BR>	 f. (-वा) Hog weed. (Boerhavia diffusa<BR>alata.)<BR> E. पुनर् again, and नव new.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=458-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुनर्भव|पुनर्भवः
पुनर्भव mfn. (-वः-वा-वं) Re-born, born again.<BR>	 n. (-वं) Regeneration.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-वः) A finger-nail.<BR> E. पुनर् again, and भव being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=458-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुनर्भविन्
पुनर्भविन् m. (-वी) The sentient soul.<BR> E. पुनर् again, भव being, and इनि<BR>possessive aff.; existing again after the dissolution of one body<BR>in another form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=458-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुनर्भू
पुनर्भू mfn. (-र्भूः-र्भूः-र्भु) Re-born, regenerated.<BR>	 f. (-र्भूः)<BR>	 1. A virgin widow<BR>re-married.<BR>	 2. Re-existence.<BR> E. पुनर् again, (a wife, &c.) भू being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=458-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुनर्यात्रा
पुनर्यात्रा f. (त्रा) Repeated procession.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=458-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुनर्वचन
पुनर्वचन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Repeated text or injunction.<BR>	 2. Saying anything<BR>again.<BR> E. पुनर, and वचन speaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=458-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुनर्वसु|पुनर्वसुः|पुनर्व्वसुः
पुनर्वसु m. (-सुः) The seventh of the lunar asterisms, containing accord-<BR>ing to some authorities two, and to others, four stars; (in this<BR>sense it is properly confined to the dual number पुनर्व्वसु, though<BR>in the Vedas it it used in the singular.)<BR>	 2. A name of VIṢṆU.<BR>	 3.<BR>The name of a saint, and grammarian; also KĀTYĀYANA.<BR>	 4. A<BR>name of ŚIVA.<BR>	 5. Commencement of wealth.<BR>	 6. A Loka or<BR>division of the universe.<BR> E. पनर् again, वस् to dwell, aff. उ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=458-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुनर्वसू|पुनर्व्वसू
पुनर्वसू m. du. (-सूः) An asterism; see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=458-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुन्नक्षत्त्र
पुन्नक्षत्त्र n. (-त्त्रं) An asterism under which males are procreated.<BR> E. पुं<BR>for पुमस्, and नक्षत्त्र asterism.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=458-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुन्नाग|पुंनाग|पुन्नागः
पुन्नाग m. (-गः)<BR>	 1. A tree, from the flowers of which a yellowish dye<BR>is prepared, (Rottleria tinctoria.)<BR>	 2. A white lotus.<BR>	 3. Nutmeg.<BR>4. A chief, a head or pre-eminent man.<BR>	 5. A white elephant.<BR> E. पुं<BR>male, नाग an elephant, or aff. or eminence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=458-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुपषत्
पुपषत् mfn. (-षन्-षन्ती-षत्) Wishing to cleanse or purify.<BR> E. पू to<BR>purify, desid. v., शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=458-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुपूषा
पुपूषा f. (-षा) Wish to cleanse or purify.<BR> E. पू to purify, desid. v., affs. अङ् and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=458-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुप्पुट
पुप्पुट m. (-टः) A kind of disease of the palate and gum severally.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=458-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुप्फुल|पुप्फुलः
पुप्फुल m. (-लः) Flatulence, wind in the bowels.<BR> E. फुल् to blow, form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=458-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुप्फुस|पुप्फुसः
पुप्फुस m. (-सः)<BR>	 1. The lungs.<BR>	 2. The pericarp of a lotus.<BR> E. स्फुर् to<BR>swell, deriv. irr. it is also written. फुप्फुस and पुप्पुस.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=458-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुमनुज
पुमनुज mfn. (-जः-जा-जं) Born after, like, or according to a man.<BR> E. पुं,<BR>and अनुज born after.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=458-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुमस्
पुमस् m. (-पुमान्) A man or male.<BR> E. पा to preserve, (his own duties,) Unādi aff. डुम and सुन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=458-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुवत्
पुवत् Ind. Manlily, like a man.<BR> E. पुं, and वति aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=458-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुर्
पुर् f. (-पूः) A city.<BR> E. पुर् to lead, क्विप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=458-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरःसर|पुरःसरः
पुरःसर mfn. (-रः-री-रं) One who goes first or before.<BR>	 m. (-रः) A<BR>leader, a preceder. Adv.<BR>	 n. (-रं) By or with, i. e. preceded by,<BR>attended with, as कोपपुरःसर with rage.<BR> E. पुरस् before, सर who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=458-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरःस्थायिन्
पुरःस्थायिन् Adj. Standing in front.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=458-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरःस्फुरत्
पुरःस्फुरत् mfn. (-रन्-रन्ती-रत्) Opening or becoming manifest before one.<BR>E. पुरस्, and स्फुरत् budding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=458-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुर|पुरं|पुरः
पुर r. 6th cl. (पुरति) To precede, to lead, to go before. तु० पर० सक० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=458-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुर|पुरं|पुरः
पुर nf. (-रं-री) A town, a city: a place containing large buildings<BR>surrounded by a ditch, and extending not less than one Krosha in<BR>length, is called a city, a pura or Nagara; if it extends not less<BR>than half a Krosha it is called a Kheṭa or town; if less than that,<BR>a Karvaṭa or small market town; and any cluster of houses<BR>less than that, is a Grāma or village.<BR>	 n. (-रं)<BR>	 1. A town.<BR>2. A fortress, a castle.<BR>	 3. The female apartments.<BR>	 4. A brothel.<BR>5. A house.<BR>	 6. Pāṭaliputra or modern Pātna.<BR>	 7. The body.<BR>8. The calyx of a flower, or any receptacle or cup formed of leaves.<BR>9. Skin.<BR>	 10. An upper story.<BR>	 11. A fragrant grass, (Cyperus.)<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A sort of resin, “bdellium.” 2. Yellow barleria.<BR>	 f. (-रा)<BR>1. The east.<BR>	 2. A perfume.<BR>	 3. An epithet of the Ganges.<BR> E. पुर् to<BR>precede, क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=458-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरकोट्ट
पुरकोट्ट n. (-ट्टं) A citadel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=458-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरग
पुरग f. (-गा) Adj. Favouribly inclined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=458-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरजित्
पुरजित् m. (-जित्) An epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=458-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरज्योतिस्
पुरज्योतिस् m. (-तिः) The region or world of AGNI or fire.<BR> E. पुर pri-<BR>mary, from पुर् to precede, with क aff., and ज्योतिस् light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=458-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरञ्जन|पुरंजन|पुरंजनः|पुरञ्जनः
पुरञ्जन m. (-नः) Life, the living principle.<BR>	 f. (-नी) Understanding. E.<BR>पुर the body, and जन what produces.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=458-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरञ्जय|पुरंजय|पुरञ्जयः
पुरञ्जय mfn. (-यः-यी-यं) Victorious, conquering cities.<BR>	 m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. The<BR>proper name of a king, the third of the race of the sun.<BR> E. पुर a<BR>city, जी to conquer, aff. खश्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=458-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरञ्जर|पुरंजरः
पुरञ्जर m. (-रः) The armpit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=458-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरट|पुरटं
पुरट n. (-टं) Gold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=458-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरण|पुरणः
पुरण m. (-णः) The ocean.<BR> E. प to fill, क्यु Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=458-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरतटी
पुरतटी f. (-टी) A market, a village or small fair.<BR> E. पुर a city, तट a<BR>bank, and ङीप् diminutive or depreciative aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=458-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरतस्
पुरतस् Ind. Before, in front of.<BR> E. पुर् to precede, aff. अतसुच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=458-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरतोरण
पुरतोरण n. (-णं) The outer gate of a city.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=458-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरदेवता
पुरदेवता f. (-ता) The tutelary deity of a town.<BR> E. पुर, and देवता deity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=458-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरद्वार|पुरद्वारं
पुरद्वार n. (-र) A city gate.<BR> E. पुर a city, and द्वार a gate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=458-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरद्विष्
पुरद्विष् m. (-द्विट्) A name of ŚIVA.<BR> E. पुर a name of Tripura, the<BR>demon, and द्विष् who hates.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=458-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरनिवेश|पुरनिवेशः
पुरनिवेश m. (-शः) The founding of a city.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=458-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरन्द|पुरंद
पुरन्द m. (-न्दः) INDRA.<BR> E. पुर a city, दो to destroy, ड aff. with the wower of स्व.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=458-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरन्दर|पुरंदर|पुरन्दरं|पुरंदरः|पुरन्दरः
पुरन्दर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A name of INDRA.<BR>	 2. An epithet of Sīva.<BR>	 3. An<BR>epithet of Agni.<BR>	 4. A thief, a housebreaker.<BR>	 n. (-रं) A sort of<BR>pepper, (Piper chavya.)<BR>	 f. (-रा) A name of the Ganges.<BR> E. पुर<BR>a city, दॄ to tear or rend, aff. स्वच्, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=458-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरन्ध्रि|पुरंध्रि|पुरंध्रिः|पुरन्ध्रिः
पुरन्ध्रि f. (-न्ध्रिः-न्ध्री) A woman, whose husband and children are living.<BR>E. पुर the body, धृ to uphold, aff. खच्, fem. aff. ङीप्, or the final<BR>is optionally short.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=458-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरपाल|पुरपालः
पुरपाल m. (-लः) The commandant of a fortress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=458-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरमार्ग|पुरमार्गः
पुरमार्ग m. (-र्गः) The street of a town.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=458-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुररक्षक|पुररक्षकः
पुररक्षक m. (-कः) A constable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=458-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुररोध|पुररोधः
पुररोध m. (-धः) The siege of a fortress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=458-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरला
पुरला f. (-ला) An epithet of Durgā.<BR> E. पुर-कलच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=458-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरवासिन्
पुरवासिन् mfn. (-सी-सिनी-सि) Inhabiting a city or town.<BR> E. पुर, and वासिन् inhabitant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=458-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरशासन|पुरशासनः
पुरशासन m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. An epithet of Sīva.<BR>	 2. A name of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=458-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरश्चरण|पुरश्चरणं
पुरश्चरण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. An introductory rite in Tantra shāstra.<BR>	 2. Repeti-<BR>tion of the name of a deity accompanied by burnt offering. E.<BR>पुरस्, चर to go, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=458-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरश्छद|पुरश्छदः
पुरश्छद m. (-दः) A sort of grass, (Saccharum cylindricum.)<BR>	 m. du. (-दौ) The nipples.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=458-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरस्
पुरस् Ind.<BR>	 1. Eastward.<BR>	 2. In front, before, in presence of, (with a<BR>genitive); in this sense it is often prefixed to कृ, भू and गम; hence<BR>such forms as पुरस्कत्य &c.<BR>	 3. Prior, first.<BR>	 4. Formerly.<BR> E. पुर् to<BR>precede, aff. असुक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=458-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरसंस्कार
पुरसंस्कार m. (-रः) The repairing of a castle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=458-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरस्करण|पुरस्करणं
पुरस्करण n. (-णं) Making perfect, &c.: see पुरस्कार.<BR> E. पुरस्, and करण doing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=458-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरस्करणीय
पुरस्करणीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) To be respected, &c.: see पुरस्कर्त्तव्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=458-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरस्कर्त्तव्य|पुरस्कर्तव्य
पुरस्कर्त्तव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>	 1. To be made complete or perfect.<BR>	 2. To<BR>be prepared, to be fitted out.<BR>	 3. To be set before.<BR>	 4. To be<BR>treated with deference or respect.<BR> E. पुरस्, कृ to make, तव्य aff.;<BR>also पुरस्करणीय and पुरस्कार्य्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=458-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरस्कार|पुरस्कारः
पुरस्कार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Making perfect or complete, finishing, polishing.<BR>2. Preparing, getting ready.<BR>	 3. Arranging, putting in array.<BR>4. Placing before.<BR>	 5. Honouring, respecting.<BR>	 6. Worshiping.<BR>7. Sprinkling with holy water.<BR>	 8. Promise.<BR>	 9. Accusation.<BR>	 10.<BR>Attacking, assailing.<BR>	 11. Anticipating, expecting.<BR> E. पुरस्, and<BR>कार making.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=458-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरस्कार्य्य|पुरस्कार्य
पुरस्कार्य्य mfn. (-र्य्यः-र्य्या-र्य्यं) To be prepared, to be fitted out, &c.: see<BR>पुरस्कर्त्तव्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=458-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरस्क्रिया
पुरस्क्रिया f. (-याः)<BR>	 1. A preparatory rite.<BR>	 2. Showing respect.<BR>	 3. Making<BR>perfect, &c.: see पुरस्कार.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=459-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरस्कृत|पुरस्कृतः
पुरस्कृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Made perfect, finished, polished.<BR>	 2. Pre-<BR>pared.<BR>	 3. Placed in front.<BR>	 4. Revered, adored, worshiped.<BR>	 5.<BR>Honoured, respected.<BR>	 6. Sprinkled with holy water, initiated,<BR>anointed.<BR>	 7. Promised, agreed.<BR>	 8. Accused, calumniated.<BR>	 9.<BR>Facing, and contending with an enemy.<BR>	 10. Distrest or haras-<BR>sed by an enemy.<BR>	 11. Anticipated.<BR> E. पुरस् before, and कृत made.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=459-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरस्तात्
पुरस्तात् Ind.<BR>	 1. Eastward.<BR>	 2. In front, before.<BR>	 3. Prior, first, preceding.<BR>4. Formerly.<BR>	 5. Further on, in the sequel.<BR> E. पुर to go before,<BR>अस्ताति aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=459-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरा
पुरा Ind.<BR>	 1. An ancient story.<BR>	 2. Old.<BR>	 3. Past.<BR>	 4. Long past, of yore.<BR>5. Near.<BR>	 6. Future.<BR>	 7. Proximate future.<BR> E. पुर् to precede, affs. क<BR>and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=459-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुराकथा
पुराकथा f. (-था) An old legend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=459-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुराकल्प|पुराकल्पः
पुराकल्प m. (-ल्पः)<BR>	 1. A former creation.<BR>	 2. An old story, a story of the past.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=459-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुराकृत|पुराकृतं
पुराकृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Done formerly or of old, done long ago.<BR>	 2.<BR>Done or observed precedingly.<BR>	 3. Begun, commenced.<BR> E. पुरा, कृत<BR>done.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=459-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुराट्ट|पुराट्टः
पुराट्ट n. (-ट्टं) A turret on a city wall.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=459-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुराण|पुराणं|पुराणः
पुराण r. 1st cl. (पुराण्यति) Legendary tale. यक् पर० सक० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=459-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुराण|पुराणं|पुराणः
पुराण n. (-णं) A Purāṇa or sacred poetical work, supposed to be<BR>compiled or composed by the poet VYĀSA; and comprising the<BR>whole body of Hindu theology: each Purāṇa should treat of five<BR>topics especially; the creation, the destruction and renovation of<BR>worlds; the genealogy of gods and heroes; the reigns of the<BR>Manus, and the transaction of their descendants: but great variety<BR>prevails in this respect and few contain historical or genealogical<BR>matter. There are eighteen acknowledged Purāṇas.<BR>	 1. BRAHMĀ.<BR>2. Padma, or the lotus.<BR>	 3. Brahmāṇḍa, or the egg of BRAHMĀ.<BR>4. Āgneya, or Agni, fire.<BR>	 5. VAISHNAVA, or of VIṢṆU.<BR>	 6. Garu-<BR>da.<BR>	 7. Brahmavaivarta, or transformations of BRAHMĀ, that is of<BR>KṚṢṆA, identified with the Supreme.<BR>	 8. SAIVA, or of ŚIVA.<BR>	 9.<BR>Linga.<BR>	 10. NĀRADĪYA.<BR>	 11. SKANDA.<BR>	 12. MĀRKAṆḌEYA, so called<BR>from a Muni of that name.<BR>	 13. Bhavishyat, or prophetic.<BR>	 14.<BR>Matsya, or the fish.<BR>	 15. Varāha, or boar.<BR>	 16. Kaurma, or of the<BR>Kurma or tortoise.<BR>	 17. Vāmana, or dwarf.<BR>	 18. Bhāgavat, or<BR>life of KṚṢṆA, which last is by some considered as a spurious<BR>and modern work: the Brahmavaivarta is also of very modern<BR>origin. The Purāṇas ars reckoned to contain four hundred<BR>thousand stanzas: there are also eighteen Upapurāṇas or similar<BR>poems of inferior sanctity, and different appellations: the whole<BR>constitute the popular or poetical creed of the Hindus, and some<BR>of them or particular parts of them, are very generally read, and<BR>studied.<BR>	 m. (-णः) A karsha or measure of silver equal to sixteen<BR>Paṇas of Cowries.<BR>	 mfn. (-णः-णा or -णी-णं) Old, ancient.<BR> E. पुरा old,<BR>and द्यु aff. or पुरा the same, णी to get or be, and ड aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=459-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुराणग|पुराणगः
पुराणग m. (-गः)<BR>	 1. A reader or reciter of the Purāṇas.<BR>	 2. BRAHMĀ.<BR>E. पुराण a sacred poem, and ग who goes or pervades.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=459-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुराणपुरुष|पुराणपुरुषः
पुराणपुरुष m. (-षः) VIṢṆU.<BR> E. पुराण old or primeval, and पुरुष man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=459-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुराणान्त|पुराणांत|पुराणान्तः
पुराणान्त m. (-न्तः) An epithet of Yama.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=459-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुराणोक्त
पुराणोक्त n. (-क्तं) Enjoined by the Purāṇas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=459-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरातन|पुरातनः
पुरातन mfn. (-नः-नी-नं)<BR>	 1. Old, ancient.<BR>	 2. Worn out.<BR>	 m. (-नः) An<BR>epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR> E. पुरा old, ठ्य, aff., and तुट् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=459-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरातल
पुरातल n. (-लं) The part below the seven worlds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=459-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुराव्यक्ष
पुराव्यक्ष m. (-क्षः) The governor or mayor of a city.<BR> E. पुर, and अध्यक्ष superintendant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=459-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुराधिप|पुराधिपः
पुराधिप m. (-पः) The governor of a town.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=459-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरायोनि|पुरायोनिः
पुरायोनि m. (-निः) An epithet of Śiva. Adj. Of ancient origin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=459-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरारि|पुरारिः
पुरारि m. (-रिः) ŚIVA.<BR> E. पुर the demon pura, or more properly Tripura,<BR>and अरि foe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=459-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरार्द्धविस्तार
पुरार्द्धविस्तार m. (-रः) Part of a town, a suburb, a ward, a division.<BR> E. पुर<BR>a city, अर्द्ध part, विस्तार extending.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=459-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरावसु|पुरावसुः
पुरावसु m. (-सुः) A name of BHĪṢMA.<BR> E. पुरा in former life, वसु a<BR>VASU or demigod, so called.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=459-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुराविद्
पुराविद् mfn. (-विद्) Knowing or acquainted with the past.<BR> E. पुरा, and विद् who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=459-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरावृत्त|पुरावृत्तं
पुरावृत्त n. (-त्तं)<BR>	 1. History, traditionary or heroic.<BR>	 2. Any old or legen-<BR>dary event.<BR> E. पुरा old, (time, or story,) and आवृत्त happened.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=459-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरावृत्तकथा
पुरावृत्तकथा f. (-था) An old story.<BR> E. पुरावृत्त and कथा tale; also<BR>पुरावृत्ताख्यान, and similar compounds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=459-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरासुहृत्
पुरासुहृत् m. (-हृत्) ŚIVA.<BR> E. पुर the demon. and असुहृत् and enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=459-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरि|पुरिः
पुरि f. (-रिः or री)<BR>	 1. A town, a city.<BR>	 2. A river.<BR>	 m. (-रिः) A king, a<BR>sovereign.<BR> E. पॄ to fill or to cherish, इ Uṇadi aff.: see पुर, and पुरी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=459-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरिश
पुरिश m. (-शः) A living being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=459-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरिशय
पुरिशय Adj. Reposing in a fortress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=459-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरी
पुरी f. (-री)<BR>	 1. A city.<BR>	 2. A stronghold.<BR>	 3. The body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=459-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरीतत्
पुरीतत् mn. (-तत्) An entrail, a gut.<BR> E. पुरि or पुरी for पुर body, and<BR>तन् to, spread, to stretch, aff. क्विप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=459-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरीमोह|पुरीमोहः
पुरीमोह m. (-हः) The thorn-apple, (Dhuturā): see धुस्तूर<BR> E. षुरी a town<BR>and मोह intoxicating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=459-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरीष|पुरीषं
पुरीष n. (-षं)<BR>	 1. Fæces, excrement, ordure.<BR>	 2. Rubbish, mould.<BR> E. पॄ<BR>to nourish or fill, (the body,) aff. ईषन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=459-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरीषण|पुरीषणः
पुरीषण m. (-णः) Fæces: see the last.<BR>	 n. (-णं) Evacuation by stool.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=459-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरीषनिग्रहण
पुरीषनिग्रहण n. (-णं) Obstructing the bowels.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=459-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरीषम|पुरीषमः
पुरीषम m. (-मः) The black kidney-bean, (Phaseolus mas. or P.<BR>radiatus.)<BR> E. पुरीष fæces, मा to mete or measure, ड aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=459-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरीषोत्सर्ग|पुरीषोत्सर्गः
पुरीषोत्सर्ग m. (-र्गः) Voiding excrement.<BR> E. पुरीष, and उत्सर्ग abandoning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=459-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरु|पुरुः
पुरु mfn. (-रुः-रुः-रु) Much, many, exceeding.<BR>	 m. (-रुः)<BR>	 1. The name of<BR>a king, the sixth monarch of the lunar line. He was the youngest<BR>son of king Yayāti and Sharmishthā, who consented to give<BR>his youth and beauty to his father in exchange for his infirmities.<BR>After a thousand years Yayāti restored to him his youth and<BR>made him king of Pratishthāna. He was an ancestor of the<BR>Kauravas and Pāndavas.<BR>	 2. Heaven, or the world and residence<BR>of immortals.<BR>	 3. The farina of a flower.<BR>	 4. The name of a Daitya.<BR>f. (-रुः) The name of a river said to run a little to the north-<BR>west of the Sarasvatī<BR> E. पॄ to cherish or fill well, Unādi aff. कु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=459-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुजित्
पुरुजित् m. (-जित्) A name of the king Kuntibhoja.<BR>	 2. An epithet of<BR>Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=459-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुद
पुरुद n. (-दं) Gold.<BR> E. पुरु much, दा to give, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=459-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुर्दशक
पुरुर्दशक m. (-कः) A goose.<BR> E. पुरु much, दंशक who bites.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=459-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुर्दशस्
पुरुर्दशस् m. (-शाः) A name of INDRA.<BR> E. पुरु much, दशि to destroy, असि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=459-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुरवस्
पुरुरवस् m. (-वाः) KUVERA: see पुरूरवस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=459-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुलम्पट|पुरुलंपट
पुरुलम्पट n. (-टं) Very lascivious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=459-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुष|पुरुषः
पुरुष m. (-षः)<BR>	 1. A man generally or individually, a male, man-kind.<BR>2. Representative of generation.<BR>	 3. An official, a functionary.<BR>	 4.<BR>The height of a man considered as a measure of length.<BR>	 5. The<BR>pupil of the eye.<BR>	 6. A person, (in gram.)<BR>	 7. The soul.<BR>	 8. God,<BR>the Supreme Being.<BR>	 9. VIṢṆU.<BR>	 10. BRAHMĀ.<BR>	 11. Life, the living<BR>principle.<BR>	 12. An atom.<BR>	 13. A follower of the Sānkhya philo-<BR>sophy, who believes in the twenty-fifth creation of the Sānkhya<BR>philosophy, the soul which according to them is neither a produc-<BR>tion nor a productive.<BR>	 14. A friend.<BR>	 15. A sort of tree: see पुन्नाग.<BR>16. A sort of tree, commonly Tila or Tilaka.<BR>	 n. (-षं) The mountain<BR>Meru.<BR> E. पुर the body, or षस् to abide, aff. क, and the vowel<BR>changed; or पुर् to precede, Unādi aff. कुषन्; also पुरूष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=459-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुषक|पुरुषकं|पुरुषकः
पुरुषक n. (-कं) Rearing as a horse, standing like a man on two feet.<BR>E. पुरुष, and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=459-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुषकार|पुरुषकारः
पुरुषकार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Manly act, virility.<BR>	 2. Effort, exertion.<BR>	 3. Any<BR>act of a man, manhood.<BR> E. पुरुष, and कार a doing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=459-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुषकुणप|पुरुषकुणपः
पुरुषकुणप mn. (-पः-पं) A human corpse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=459-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुषकेसरिन्
पुरुषकेसरिन् m. (-री) Man-lion or Viṣṇu in his fourth incarnation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=460-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुषज्ञान
पुरुषज्ञान n. (-नं) Knowledge of mankind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=460-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुषता
पुरुषता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Manhood, manliness.<BR>	 2. Valour.<BR> E. तल् added to पुरुष; also पुरुषत्व.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=460-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुषत्व|पुरुषत्वं
पुरुषत्व n. (-त्वं)<BR>	 1. Manhood, virility, manly nature or property.<BR>	 2.<BR>Valour, prowess.<BR> E. त्व added to पुरुष a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=460-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुषत्रा
पुरुषत्रा Ind. With or amongst men or mankind, worldly, &c.<BR> E. पुरुष<BR>mankind, and त्रा aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=460-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरूषदन्तिका
पुरूषदन्तिका f. (-का) A medicinal root; see मेदा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=460-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुषदध्न
पुरुषदध्न mfn. (-ध्नः-ध्नी-ध्नं) Of the height, or measure of a man.<BR> E. पुरुष a<BR>man, दध्नच् aff. in this sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=460-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुषद्वयस|पुरुषद्वयसः
पुरुषद्वयस mfn. (-सः-सा-सं) Of the height, or measure of a man.<BR> E. पुरुष a man, and द्वयसच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=460-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुषद्वेषिन्
पुरुषद्वेषिन् mfn. (-षी-षिणी-षि) Man-hating, misanthropic.<BR>	 f. (-णी) An ill-<BR>tempered, or fractious woman.<BR> E. पुरुष a man, and द्वेषिन् who hates.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=460-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुषनाय
पुरुषनाय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. A general, a commander.<BR>	 2. A king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=460-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुषपशु|पुरुषपशुः
पुरुषपशु m. (-शुः) A man, a human animal.<BR> E. पुरुष, and पशु beast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=460-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुषपुङ्गव|पुरुषपुंगव|पुरुषपुङ्गवः
पुरुषपुङ्गव m. (-वः) An eminent, or excellent man.<BR> E. पुरुष, and पुङ्गव a<BR>bull; the last implying pre-eminence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=460-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुषपुण्डरीक|पुरुषपुंडरीक|पुरुषपुण्डरीकः
पुरुषपुण्डरीक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. An excellent or superior man.<BR>	 2. The seventh<BR>of the nine persons called Vasudevās by the Jainas.<BR> E. पुरुष man-<BR>kind, and पुण्डरीक a lotus, or here used to signify pre-eminence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=460-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुषमात्र|पुरुषमात्रः
पुरुषमात्र mfn. (-त्रः-त्री-त्रं) Of the height, or measure of a man.<BR> E. पुरुष a<BR>man, and मात्रच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=460-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुषमेध|पुरुषमेधः
पुरुषमेध m. (-धः) A human sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=460-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुषर्षभ|पुरुषर्षभः
पुरुषर्षभ m. (-भः) An excellent man.<BR> E. पुरुष, and ऋषभ best.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=460-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुषवर|पुरुषवरः
पुरुषवर m. (-रः) Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=460-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुषवर्जित
पुरुषवर्जित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Desolate, destitute of human beings.<BR> E. पुरुष, and वर्जित void of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=460-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुषवाह|पुरुषवाहः
पुरुषवाह m. (-हः)<BR>	 1. Garuda.<BR>	 2. Kuvera.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=460-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुषव्याध्र
पुरुषव्याध्र m. (-ध्रः)<BR>	 1. A vulture.<BR>	 2. An eminent, or distinguished man.<BR>E. पुरुष a man, and व्याघ्र a tiger; here also implying pre-eminence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=460-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुषशार्द्दूल|पुरुषशार्दूल|पुरुषशार्दूलः
पुरुषशार्द्दूल m. (-लः) An eminent man.<BR> E. पुरुष, and शार्द्दल a tiger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=460-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुषसमवाय|पुरुषसमवायः
पुरुषसमवाय m. (-यः) A number of men.<BR> E. पुरुष, and समवाय assemblage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=460-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुषसिंह|पुरुषसिंहः
पुरुषसिंह m. (-हः)<BR>	 1. An eminent man.<BR>	 2. The fifth of the Vāsudevas,<BR>according to the Jains, and the son of ŚIVA.<BR> E. पुरुष mankind,<BR>and सिंह pre-eminent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=460-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुषसूक्त
पुरुषसूक्त n. (-क्तं) A name given to the 90th hymn of the tenth mandala of the Rigveda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=460-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुषाङ्ग|पुरुषांग
पुरुषाङ्ग mn. (-ङ्गः-ङ्गं) The male organ of generation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=460-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुषाद|पुरुषादः
पुरुषाद m. (-दः) A demon, a goblin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=460-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुषाद्य|पुरुषाद्यः
पुरुषाद्य m. (-द्यः)<BR>	 1. A name of the first Jaina pontiff of the present age,<BR>“ṚSHABHA.” 2. A name of VIṢṆU.<BR> E. पुरुष mankind, and आद्य first,<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=460-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुषाघम
पुरुषाघम m. (-मः) A low man, an outcaste.<BR> E. पुरुष a man, and अधम<BR>low, vile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=460-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुषाधिकार|पुरुषाधिकारः
पुरुषाधिकार m. (-रः) Manly office or duty.<BR> E. पुरुष, and अधिकार duty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=460-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुषान्तर|पुरुषांतर
पुरुषान्तर n. (-रं) Another man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=460-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुषायित
पुरुषायित n. (-तं)<BR>	 1. Manly conduct.<BR>	 2. A mode of sexual enjoyment. in which the woman acts the man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=460-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुषार्थ|पुरुषार्थः
पुरुषार्थ m. (-र्थः) A human object: as the gratification of desire, ac-<BR>quirement of wealth, discharge of duty, and final emancipation.<BR>n. (-र्थं) Adv. For, or on account of man.<BR> E. पुरुष, and अर्थ object.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=460-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुषायुस्
पुरुषायुस् m. (-युः) Life of man, human existence.<BR> E. पुरुष and आयुस् life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=460-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुषाशिन्
पुरुषाशिन् m. (-शी) A Rākshasa, a cannibal.<BR> E. पुरुष, and अशिन् who eats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=460-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुषास्थिमालिन्
पुरुषास्थिमालिन् m. (-ली) SīVA.<BR> E. पुरुष a man, अस्थि a bone, माला a<BR>necklace, and इनि poss. aff.; wearing a necklace of human skulls.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=460-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुषोक्ति
पुरुषोक्ति f. (-क्तिः) The name or title of a man.<BR> E. पुरुष, and उक्ति saying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=460-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुषोक्तिक
पुरुषोक्तिक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Destitute, having no friends.<BR> E. पुरुषोक्ति,<BR>and कन् aff. having only the name of man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=460-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुषोत्तम|पुरुषोत्तमः
पुरुषोत्तम m. (-मः) An excellent or superior man.<BR>	 2. VIṢṆU.<BR>	 3. A Jina,<BR>one of the generic terms for a deified chief of the Jaina sect.<BR>	 4.<BR>The fourth of the nine Vāsudevas of the jainas, the son of<BR>SOMA.<BR> E. पुरुष mankind, उत्तम best.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=460-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुह|पुरुहं
पुरुह mfn. (-हः-हा-हं) Much, many.<BR> E. पुरु many, हन् to destroy or<BR>surpass, aff. ड; also पुरुहु with डु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=460-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुहु
पुरुहु mfn. (-हुः-हुः-हु) Much, many. E. See the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=460-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुहूत|पुरुहूतः
पुरुहूत Adj. Invoked by many.<BR>	 m. (-तः) A name of INDRA.<BR> E. पुरु<BR>much, हूत worshiped or invoked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=460-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरूरवस
पुरूरवस m. (-वाः)<BR>	 1. The son of BUDHA and Ilā and the second king of<BR>the lunar dynasty. He was a prince renowned for liberality, devo-<BR>tion, love of truth and personal beauty. He fell in love with<BR>Urvashi while she was descending from heaven. Urvashi returned<BR>his love and became his wife. The king passed many happy days<BR>in her company and had one son by her. After some days the<BR>nymph returned to her home leaving the king to mourn her loss;<BR>but she repeated her visits five times successively and bore five<BR>sons to the king. Purūravas was not however, satisfied and longed<BR>for an inseparable union with her. This he secured by, celebrating<BR>many sacrifices. The story has its origin in a passage in<BR>Haribansha where Urvashī is represented as going to live with<BR>Purūravas on certain conditions, the accidental violation of<BR>which made her leave the king.<BR>	 2. A demigod, of the class of<BR>Viswadevas.<BR> E. पुरु much, रु to sound, Unādi aff. असि, form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=460-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरोग|पुरोगः
पुरोग mfn. (-गः-गा-गं)<BR>	 1. Going before, preceding.<BR>	 2. Chief, principal,<BR>pre-eminent.<BR> E. पुरस् before, and गम who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=460-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरोगत
पुरोगत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Preceded, gone before.<BR>	 2. Leading, chief.<BR> E. पुरस्, गत gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=460-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरोगति|पुरोगतिः
पुरोगति mfn. (-तिः-तिः-ति) Preceding, going before.<BR>	 m. (-तिः) A dog.<BR>	 f.<BR>(-तिः) Precedence, going before.<BR> E. पुरस् in front, and गति going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=460-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरोगम|पुरोगमः
पुरोगम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं) Going before, preceding.<BR> E. पुरस् before, and<BR>गम who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=460-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरोगमन
पुरोगमन n. (-नं) Going before, preceding.<BR> E. पुरस्, and गमन going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=460-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरोगामिन्
पुरोगामिन् mfn. (-मी-मिनी-मि) Going in front or before, preceding.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-मी) A dog.<BR> E. पुरस्, and गामिन् who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=460-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरोजन्मन्
पुरोजन्मन् Adj. Born before.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=460-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरोटि|पुरोटिः
पुरोटि m. (-टिः)<BR>	 1. The current of a river.<BR>	 2. The rustling of leaves.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=460-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरोडा
पुरोडा(श्)श m. (-शः)<BR>	 1. Ghee or clarified butter as offered in oblations<BR>to fire, with cakes of ground barley meal, that have been well<BR>steeped in it.<BR>	 2. The orts, or leavings of any substance, used in an<BR>oblation to fire.<BR>	 3. A sort of flat ladle or spoon, used for placing the<BR>cakes in the sacrificial fire.<BR>	 4. The juice of the acid asclepias<BR>drunk at certain sacrifices.<BR>	 5. A mantra, or prayer recited<BR>in offering oblations to fire.<BR> E. पुरस् first, दिश् to show, aff. अच्,<BR>deriv. irr.; the first ceremony on all sacred occasions; or accord-<BR>ing to Vāchaspatya:--पुरोदाश्यते दाश-दाने कर्म्मणि क्किप्, घञ् वा<BR>दस्य डः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=460-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरोडाशीय
पुरोडाशीय mf. (-यः-या-यं) Fit to be offered in oblations.<BR> E. पुरोडाश, and छ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=460-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरोडाश्य|पुरोडाश्यं
पुरोडाश्य mfn. (-श्यः-श्या-श्यं) Fit or proper for offering with Ghee in<BR>oblation to fire.<BR> E. पुरोडाश as above, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=460-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरोद्यान
पुरोद्यान n. (-नं) A city garden, a park.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=460-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरोद्भव
पुरोद्भव mfn. (-वः-वा-वं) Of former or prior origin.<BR>	 f. (-वा) A drug; also<BR>called Mahāmeda.<BR> E. पुरा formerly, उद्भव produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=460-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरोधस्
पुरोधस् m. (-धाः) The family or domestic priest.<BR> E. पुरस् before, धा to<BR>have, असि Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=460-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरोधान|पुरोधानं
पुरोधान n. (-नं) Priestly ministration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=460-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरोधिका
पुरोधिका f. (-का) A favourite wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=460-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरोपनीत
पुरोपनीत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Formerly had or possessed.<BR> E. पुरा, and उपनीत taken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=460-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरोभाग|पुरोभागः
पुरोभाग mfn. (-गः-गा-गं)<BR>	 1. Obtrusive.<BR>	 2. Fault-finding.<BR>	 m. (-गः)<BR>	 1. The.<BR>front part.<BR>	 2. Officiousness.<BR>	 3. Envy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=460-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरोभागिन्
पुरोभागिन् mfn. (-गी-गिनी-गि)<BR>	 1. Malevolent, censorious.<BR>	 2. Taking the<BR>first share.<BR> E. पुरस् first, भज् to serve, aff. घिणुन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=460-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरोमारुत|पुरोमारुतः
पुरोमारुत m. (-तः) Wind blowing in front.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=460-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरोवात|पुरोवातः
पुरोवात m. (-तः) See the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=460-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरोहित|पुरोहितः
पुरोहित Adj.<BR>	 1. Placed in front.<BR>	 2. Charged.<BR>	 m. (-तः) The purohita<BR>or family priest, conducting all the ceremonials and sacrifices<BR>of a house or family.<BR> E. पुरस् first, and हित् held, revered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=460-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुर्व|पुर्व्व
पुर्व r. 1st cl. (पुर्वति) To fill. r. 10th cl. (पुर्वयति)<BR>	 1. To dwell or inhabit<BR>2. To invite. भ्वा० पर० सक० सेट्, चु० ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=461-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुल|पुलः
पुल r. 1st cl. (पोलति) 6th cl. (पुलति) and 10th cl. (पोलयति-ते) To be great<BR>or large, to be lofty or high, to be heaped up or piled. महत्त्वे भ्वा०<BR>पर० उद्धृतौ चु० उभ० सक० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=461-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुल|पुलः
पुल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Vast, great, extensive.<BR>	 m. (-लः) Erection of the<BR>hairs of the body, considered as a proof of exquisite delight,<BR>horripilation.<BR>	 f. (-ला)<BR>	 1. One of the paces of a horse, the canter<BR>or gallop.<BR>	 2. The soft palate or uvula.<BR> E. पुल् to be great, क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=461-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुलक|पुलकं|पुलकः
पुलक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. Erection of the hairs of the body, considered as<BR>occasioned by internal pleasure or satisfaction.<BR>	 2. An insect of<BR>any class, affecting animals whether externally or internally.<BR>	 3.<BR>A sort of stone.<BR>	 4. Flaw or defect in a gem.<BR>	 5. A ball of bread<BR>and sweetmeats with which elephants are fed.<BR>	 6. Yellow orpiment.<BR>7. A Gandharba or heavenly chorister.<BR>	 8. A wine goblet or glass.<BR>9. A sort of mustard.<BR> E. पुल् to be great, कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=461-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुलकाङ्ग|पुलकांग|पुलकाङ्गः
पुलकाङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः) The noose or cord of VARUṆA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=461-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुलकालय|पुलकालयः
पुलकालय m. (-यः) KUVERA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=461-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुलकित
पुलकित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Having the hairs of the body erect.<BR>	 2. Joyful.<BR> E. पुलक, and इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=461-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुलकिन्
पुलकिन् mfn. (-की-किनी-कि) Having the down of the body erect.<BR>	 m. (-की)<BR>A sort of Kadamba, (Nauclea k.)<BR> E. पलक, and इनि aff. “धाराकदम्बे” ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=461-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुलकोद्गम|पुलकोद्गमः
पुलकोद्गम m. (-मः) Erection of the hairs of the body.<BR> E. पुलक the same,<BR>उद्गम arising.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=461-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुलस्ति|पुलस्तिः
पुलस्ति m. (-स्तिः) The name of one of the seven Ṛshis, and mind-<BR>born sons of BRAHMĀ.<BR> E. पुल् great, अस् to throw or cast down,<BR>Unādi aff. ति; otherwise with स्त्यै to collect, and क aff. पुलस्त्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=461-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुलस्त्य|पुलस्त्यः
पुलस्त्य m. (-स्त्यः) A Ṛshi so named: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=461-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुलह|पुलहः
पुलह m. (-हः) One of the seven divine sages, supposed to have born<BR>from the navel of BRAHMĀ.<BR> E. पुल् great, हा to abandon, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=461-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुला
पुला f. (-ला) The soft palate: see पुल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=461-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुलाक|पुलाकं|पुलाकः
पुलाक mn. (-कः-कं)<BR>	 1. Shrivelled or blighted grain.<BR>	 2. Rice-water,<BR>(according to some medical authorities.)<BR>	 3. A lump of boiled-rice.<BR>4. Brevity, compendium, abbreviation.<BR>	 5. Smallness, a little.<BR>	 6.<BR>Despatch, celerity.<BR> E. पुल् greatness, अक् to be or go, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=461-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुलाकिन्
पुलाकिन् m. (-की) A tree.<BR> E. पुलाक dry grain, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=461-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुलालिका
पुलालिका f. (-का) A kind of disease affecting the tip of the nose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=461-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुलायित|पुलायितं
पुलायित n. (-तं) A horse's gallop.<BR> E. पुल् to be great, &c. aff. क्यच्-क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=461-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुलिन|पुलिनं|पुलिनः
पुलिन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. An island of alluvial formation, or one from which<BR>the water has recently withdrawn, or a small island or bank left<BR>in the middle of a river, upon the falling of the waters.<BR>	 2. Any<BR>island.<BR> E. पुल to be great, इनन् Unādi aff. किच्च ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=461-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुलिनवती
पुलिनवती f. (-ती) A river.<BR> E. पुलिन an islet, &c. and मतुप् poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=461-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुलिन्द|पुलिंद|पुलिंदः|पुलिन्दः
पुलिन्द m. (-न्दः) A barbarian, a Mleccha, a savage or mountaineer,<BR>one who uses an uncultivated and unintelligible dialect.<BR> E. पुल् to<BR>be large, Unādi aff. किन्दच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=461-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुलिरिक|पुलिरिकः
पुलिरिक m. (-कः) A snake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=461-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुलोमजा
पुलोमजा f. (-जा) Sāchi the wife of INDRA and daughter of Puloman.<BR>E. पुलोमन् a demon so called, and जा born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=461-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुलोमजित्
पुलोमजित् m. (-जित्) INDRA.<BR> E. पुलोमन् as below, and जित् who conquers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=461-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुलोमद्विष्
पुलोमद्विष् m. (-द्विट्) INDRA.<BR> E. पुलोम, and द्विष् hostile; and other similar-<BR>compounds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=461-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुलोमन्
पुलोमन् m. (-मा) The name of a demon, the father-in-law of INDRA<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=461-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुलोमभिद्
पुलोमभिद् m. (-भित्) INDRA.<BR> E. पुलोम, and भिद् to tear or destroy; the god.<BR>destroyed his father-in-law to prevent his curse, for the violation<BR>of his daughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=461-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुलोमारि|पुलोमारिः
पुलोमारि m. (-रिः) The god INDRA.<BR> E. पुलोम the demon PULOMA, and<BR>अरि enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=461-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुल्कस|पुल्कसः
पुल्कस m. (-सः) An impure and degraded tribe born of the Brāhmana by Kṣatriya female.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=461-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुल्ल
पुल्ल mfn. (-ल्लः-ल्ला-ल्लं) Expanded, full-blown or spread.<BR>	 n. (-ल्लं) A flower. E.<BR>पुल् to be large, aff. क्त, form irr.: see फुल्ल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=461-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुल्वघ
पुल्वघ m. (-घः) A sort of deer who can eat much.<BR> E. पुरु much, अत्ति from<BR>अद् to eat, aff. अच्; र being interchanged with ल ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=461-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष
पुष r. 1st cl. (पोषति) पुष्टौ भ्वा० पर० अक० सेट् । 4th cl. (पुष्यति) and 9th cl.<BR>(पुष्णाति)<BR>	 1. To cherish or nurture, to rear, to bring up.<BR>	 2. To<BR>cause to thrive, to develop.<BR>	 3. To support, to maintain, to bear.<BR>4. To further, to augment, to enhance, to increase.<BR>	 5. To get, to<BR>possess, to have, to enjoy.<BR>	 6. To show, to display, to evince.<BR>	 7.<BR>To be increased. पुष्टौ अक० पोषणे सक० क्र्या० प० सेट् । (इर) पुषिर r. 4th cl.<BR>(पुष्यति) पुष्टौ दिवा० पर० अक० अनिट् । r. 10th cl. (पोषयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To<BR>put on, to wear.<BR>	 2. To promote.<BR>	 3. To maintain. धृतौ चु० उभ० सक०<BR>सेट् । With परि or सम् to cherish much, or bring up with care.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=461-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुषा
पुषा f. (-षा)<BR>	 1. Cherishing.<BR>	 2. The lāngali plant: see लाङ्गलिकी.<BR> E. पुष्<BR>to cherish, affs. क and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=461-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुषित|पुषितं
पुषित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Nourished, nurtured.<BR> E. पुष् to nourish, aff. क्त; also without the augment पुष्ट.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=461-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्क|पुष्कं
पुष्क n. (-ष्कं) To cherish,<BR> E. पुष-बा० भावे क किच्च आद्य कस्य नेत्त्वम् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=461-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्कर|पुष्करं|पुष्करः
पुष्कर n. (-रं)<BR>	 1. The sky, heaven, atmosphere.<BR>	 2. Water.<BR>	 3. A lotus,<BR>(Nelumbium speciosum, or Nymphæa nelumbo.)<BR>	 4. The tip of an<BR>elephant's trunk.<BR>	 5. The head of a drum, or place where any<BR>musical instrument is struck.<BR>	 6. A drug, (Costus speciosus.)<BR>	 7.<BR>The name of a celebrated place of pilgrimage, called Pushkara,<BR>about four miles from the city of Ajmere, consisting of a<BR>small town on the bank of a lake, whence its name.<BR>	 8. The<BR>blade of a sword.<BR>	 9. The sheath of a sword.<BR>	 10. One of the<BR>seven great Dwīpas or divisions of the universe.<BR>	 11. An arrow.<BR>12. The art or science of dancing.<BR>	 13. War, battle.<BR>	 14. Intoxica-<BR>tion.<BR>	 15. A cage.<BR>	 16. A part.<BR>	 17. Union.<BR>	 18. Water.<BR>	 m. (-रः)<BR>	 1.<BR>A pond or lake.<BR>	 2. A disease.<BR>	 3. The Indian crane.<BR>	 4. A sort of<BR>snake.<BR>	 5. The name of a king, the brother of NALA.<BR>	 6. The son of<BR>VARUṆA.<BR>	 7. The Sun.<BR>	 8. A kind or drum.<BR>	 9. One of the principal<BR>clouds, that which occasions dearth or famine.<BR>	 10. An inauspi-<BR>cious astrological combination or a lunation with an lucky day,<BR>and three-fourths of a lunar mansion.<BR>	 11. An epithet of Krishṇa.<BR>12. An epithet of Śiva.<BR>	 13. Name of a mountain which is situated<BR>on the Pushkara Dwīpa.<BR> E. पुष् to nourish, Unādi aff. करन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=461-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्करकर्णिका
पुष्करकर्णिका f. (-का) A shrub, (Hibiscus mutabelis.)<BR> E. पुष्करं पद्ममिव कर्णः<BR>पुष्पं यस्याः कप् कापि अत इत्त्वम् “स्थलपद्मिन्याम्” ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=461-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्करमूलक|पुष्करमूलकं
पुष्करमूलक m. (-कः) The root of the Costus speciosus.<BR> E. पुष्कर as<BR>above, and मूलक root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=461-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्करशिफा
पुष्करशिफा f. (-फा) The root of the lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=461-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्करस्रज्
पुष्करस्रज् n. du. (-जौ) The two sons of ĀshwiNĪ, and physicians of<BR>Svarga or paradise.<BR>	 f. (-स्रक् or स्रग्) A chaplet of lotuses.<BR> E. पुष्कर<BR>a lotus, and स्रज् a necklace or chaplet; wearing such.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=461-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्कराह्व|पुष्कराह्वः
पुष्कराह्व m. (-ह्वः) The Indian crane.<BR> E. पुष्कर a lotus, and आह्वा an<BR>appellation; whence also any name of the lotus is applicable to<BR>the bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=461-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्करिन्
पुष्करिन् m. (-री) An elephant.<BR>	 f. (-णी)<BR>	 1. A square or large pond.<BR>	 2. A<BR>piece of water, a lake.<BR>	 3. A pool, where the lotus does or may<BR>grow.<BR>	 4. The lotus plant.<BR>	 5. A female elephant.<BR> E. पुष्कर as above,<BR>इनि possessive aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=461-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्कल|पुष्कलं|पुष्कलः
पुष्कल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>	 1. Excellent, eminent, chief, best.<BR>	 2. Much,<BR>many 3. Full, filled, complete.<BR>	 4. Near, approached.<BR>	 5. Good,<BR>salutary.<BR>	 6. Possessed of all good things.<BR>	 7. Magnificent, splen-<BR>did.<BR>	 8. Resounding, resonant.<BR>	 n. (-लं) The mountain Meru.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-लः)<BR>	 1. The holy place Pushkara.<BR>	 2. The son of Varuṇa.<BR>3. A measure of eight Kunchis or sixty-four handfuls; in some<BR>places it means four times a double handful.<BR>	 4. Alms to the<BR>extent of four mouthfuls of food.<BR> E. पुष् to nourish, and कलच्<BR>Unādi aff.; otherwise पुष्कर as above, and ल interchanged with र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=461-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्क|पुष्कं
पुष्क(ष्य)लक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. The musk-deer.<BR>	 2. A bolt, a pin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=461-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्ट|पुष्टं|पुष्टः
पुष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>	 1. Nourished, cherished, 2. Thriving, strong.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=462-a" target="_blank">Page462-a+ 60</a>]<BR>3. Rich, amply provided.<BR>	 4. Complete, perfect.<BR>	 5. Full-sounding.<BR>E. पुष् to cherish, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=461-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्टाङ्ग
पुष्टाङ्ग mfn. (-ङ्गः-ङ्गी-ङ्गं) Fat, fattened.<BR> E. पुष्ट, and अङ्ग body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=462-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्टि|पुष्टिः
पुष्टि f. (-ष्टिः)<BR>	 1. Cherishing, nourishing.<BR>	 2. Increase, advance,<BR>thriving, prosperity.<BR>	 3. Wealth, property.<BR>	 4. Plumpness, fatness.<BR>5. Richness, perfection.<BR>	 6. One of the Mātṛkās or divine mo-<BR>thers, nourishment personified.<BR> E. पुष् to nourish, aff. क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=462-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्टिकर्मन्
पुष्टिकर्मन् n. (-र्म) A religious ceremony performed for the attainment<BR>of prosperity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=462-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्टिका
पुष्टिका f. (-का) An oyster, a bi-valve-shell.<BR> E. पुष्ट, and कन् added, fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=462-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्टिकान्त|पुष्टिकान्तः
पुष्टिकान्त m. (-न्तः) GAṆEŚA.<BR> E. पुष्टि prosperity, कान्त friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=462-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्टिद|पुष्टिदः
पुष्टिद mfn. (-दः-दा-दं) Nourishing, cherishing.<BR>	 f. (-दा)<BR>	 1. Increase,<BR>thriving.<BR>	 2. A plant, (Physalis flexuosa.)<BR> E. पुष्टि, and द what gives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=462-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्टिवर्द्धन
पुष्टिवर्द्धन m. (-नः) A cock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=462-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्प|पुष्पं
पुष्प r. 4th cl. (पुष्प्यति) To flower, to blossom. दि० पर० अक० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=462-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्प|पुष्पं
पुष्प n. (-ष्पं)<BR>	 1. A flower in general.<BR>	 2. The menses.<BR>	 3. Expansion,<BR>expanding.<BR>	 4. The vehicle or car of KUVERA.<BR>	 5. A disease of<BR>the eyes, specks on the eye, albugo.<BR>	 6. A topaz.<BR>	 7. Gallantry,<BR>politeness, (in erotic poetry.)<BR>	 f. (-ष्पा) The capital of KARṆA, or<BR>Bhāgalpur.<BR>	 m. (-ष्पः) Blossoming, blooming, expanding.<BR> E. पुष्प to<BR>flower, &c. अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=462-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पक|पुष्पकं
पुष्पक n. (-कं)<BR>	 1. Calx of brass used as collyrium.<BR>	 2. The chariot of<BR>KUVERA.<BR>	 3. A disease of the eyes, albugo, specks on the eye.<BR>4. A bracelet of diamonds or jewels.<BR>	 5. A cup or vessel of iron.<BR>6. A small earthen fireplace or furnace.<BR>	 7. Green vitriol.<BR>	 8. A<BR>flower.<BR> E. कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=462-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पकरण्डक|पुष्पकरण्डकं
पुष्पकरण्डक n. (-कं)<BR>	 1. Avantī or Oujein, or the grove in its vicinity<BR>considered as sacred to MAHĀDEVA.<BR>	 2. A basket on which flower<BR>is collected.<BR> E. पुष्प a flower, and करण्डक a basket.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=462-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पकरण्डिनी
पुष्पकरण्डिनी f. (-नी) Oujein: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=462-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पकाल|पुष्पकालः
पुष्पकाल m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. The spring.<BR>	 2. The time of the menstrual flux.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=462-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पकासीस|पुष्पकासीसं
पुष्पकासीस n. (-सं) The green sulphate of iron.<BR> E. पुष्प a flower, and<BR>कासीश green vitriol.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=462-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पकीट|पुष्पकीटः
पुष्पकीट m. (-टः)<BR>	 1. A large black bee.<BR>	 2. Any insect affecting flowers.<BR>E. पुष्प a flower, and कीट an insect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=462-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पकेतन|पुष्पकेतनः
पुष्पकेतन m. (-नः) The Hindu Cupid.<BR> E. पुष्प a flower, and केतन a symbol.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=462-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पकेतु|पुष्पकेतुः
पुष्पकेतु n. (-तुं) Calx of brass.<BR>	 m. (-तुः) The god of love.<BR> E. पुष्प flower<BR>and केतु mark or sign.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=462-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पगण्डिका
पुष्पगण्डिका f. (-का) Contrary purpose or effort of a man and woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=462-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पगिरि
पुष्पगिरि m. (-रिः) A fabulous mountain, the favourite resort of<BR>VARUṆA.<BR> E. पुष्प a flower, and गिरि a mountain, the hill of flowers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=462-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पवातक
पुष्पवातक m. (-कः) A bamboo.<BR> E. पुप flower, and घातक destroyer; the<BR>stem decaying after the plant flowers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=462-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पचय|पुष्पचयः
पुष्पचय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. A quantity of flowers.<BR>	 2. Gathering flowers.<BR> E. पुष्प and चय gathering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=462-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पचाप|पुष्पचापः
पुष्पचाप m. (-पः) KĀMADEVA, the Hindu Cupid.<BR> E. पुष्प a flower, and<BR>चाप a bow; who arms his bow with flowers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=462-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पचामर|पुष्पचामरः
पुष्पचामर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A plant, (Artemisia.)<BR>	 2. A fragrant plant, (Pan-<BR>danus odoratissimus.)<BR> E. पुष्प a flower, and चामर a Chowri, having<BR>a large bushy flower. वेत्रवृक्षे, मदनवृक्षेच ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=462-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पद|पुष्पदः
पुष्पद mfn. (-दः-दा-द) Who or what gives flowers.<BR>	 m. (-दः) A tree. E.<BR>पुष्प a flower, and द what gives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=462-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पदन्त|पुष्पदंत|पुष्पदन्तः
पुष्पदन्त m. (-न्तः)<BR>	 1. The elephant presiding over the north-west quarter.<BR>2. A chief of the Gandharbas or Vidyādharas, attendant upons<BR>ŚIVA, to whom is ascribed the authorship of the “Mahimna<BR>Stotra”.<BR>	 3. One of the Jinas or Jaina teachers.<BR>	 4. A Nāga or ser-<BR>pent of the infernal regions.<BR>	 m. dual. (-न्तौ) The sun and moon. E.<BR>पुष्प flower, and दन्त a tooth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=462-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पदन्तक|पुष्पदन्तकः
पुष्पदन्तक m. (-कः) A chief of the Gandharbas.<BR> E. कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=462-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पदामन्
पुष्पदामन् n. (-म)<BR>	 1. A garland of flowers.<BR>	 2. A kind of metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=462-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पद्रव|पुष्पद्रवः
पुष्पद्रव m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. The exudation or saccharine matter of flower.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=462-b" target="_blank">Page462-b+ 60</a>]<BR>2. An infusion of flowers, as rose water, &c.<BR> E. पुष्प, and द्रव<BR>oozing, distilling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=462-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पध|पुष्पधः
पुष्पध m. (-धः) The offspring of an outcaste Brāhmana.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=462-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पधन्वन्
पुष्पधन्वन् m. (-न्वा) KĀMADEVA.<BR> E. पुष्प, and धनु bow, अनङ् aff. otherwise<BR>पुष्पधनु; see पुष्पचाप.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=462-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पधारण|पुष्पधारणः
पुष्पधारण m. (-णः) An epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=462-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पध्वज|पुष्पध्वजः
पुष्पध्वज m. (-जः) The god of love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=462-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पनिकर
पुष्पनिकर m. (-रः) Throwing flowers.<BR> E. पुष्प, and नि before, कृ to throw, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=462-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पनिक्ष|पुष्पनिक्षः
पुष्पनिक्ष m. (-क्षः) A bee.<BR> E. पुष्प, and निक्ष who kisses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=462-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पनिर्यास|पुष्पनिर्यासः
पुष्पनिर्यास m. (-सः) Nectar of flowers.<BR> E. पुष्प, and निर्यास extract.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=462-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पनेत्र
पुष्पनेत्र n. (-त्रं) The tube of a flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=462-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पन्धय|पुष्पंधय|पुष्पंधयः|पुष्पन्धयः
पुष्पन्धय m. (-यः) A bee,<BR> E. पुष्प a flower, धे to drink, aff. खश्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=462-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पपत्रिन्
पुष्पपत्रिन् m. (-त्री) The god of love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=462-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पपथ|पुष्पपथः
पुष्पपथ m. (-थः) The vulva.<BR> E. पुष्प the menses, and पथिन् a road, अप aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=462-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पपुर|पुष्पपुरं
पुष्पपुर n. (-रं) Pātaliputra or Palibothra.<BR> E. पुष्प flower, and पुर a city.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=462-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पप्रचय|पुष्पप्रचयः
पुष्पप्रचय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. Gathering fruit or flower, &c. in any way except<BR>by the hand.<BR>	 2. Stealing flowers.<BR> E. पुष्प, and प्र before, चि to<BR>collect, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=462-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पप्रचाय|पुष्पप्रचायः
पुष्पप्रचाय m. (-यः) Gathering flowers with the hand.<BR> E. पुष्प, and प्र before, चि to collect, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=462-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पप्रस्तार|पुष्पप्रस्तारः
पुष्पप्रस्तार m. (-रः) A bed of flowers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=462-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पफल|पुष्पफलः
पुष्पफल m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. Elephant or wood apple.<BR>	 2. A pumpkin gourd.<BR> E. पुष्प a flower, and फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=462-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पबलि|पुष्पबलिः
पुष्पबलि m. (-लिः) An offering of flowers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=462-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पबा
पुष्पबा(-वा)ण m. (-णः) An epithet of the god of love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=462-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पभव|पुष्पभवः
पुष्पभव m. (-वः) Nectar of flowers.<BR> E. पुष्प and भव being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=462-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पमञ्जरिका|पुष्पमंजरिका
पुष्पमञ्जरिका f. (-का) The blue lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=462-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पमास|पुष्पमासः
पुष्पमास m. (-सः)<BR>	 1. The month of Chaitra.<BR>	 2. Spring.<BR> E. पुष्प flower, and मास a month or season.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=462-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्परक्त|पुष्परक्तः
पुष्परक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं) Dyed red with vegetable colour, as safflower,<BR>&c.<BR>	 m. (-क्तः) A shrub, (Hibiscus phæniceus.)<BR> E. पुष्प flower, and रक्त<BR>coloured, red. “सूर्य्यमणिवृक्षे” ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=462-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्परजस्
पुष्परजस् n. (-जः) The Pollen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=462-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्प|पुष्पं
पुष्प(ष्य)रथ m. (-थः) A car or carriage for travelling or pleasure, or any<BR>purpose except war.<BR> E. पुष्प a flower, and रथ a car.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=462-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्परस|पुष्परसः
पुष्परस m. (-सः) The nectar or honey of flowers.<BR> E. पुष्प, and रस juice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=462-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्परसाह्वय|पुष्परसाह्वयं
पुष्परसाह्वय n. (-यं) Honey, nectar,<BR> E. पुष्परस, and आह्वय a name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=462-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्परा
पुष्परा(ज)ग m. (-ज or गः) A topaz.<BR> E. पुष्प a flower, and राग colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=462-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्परेणु|पुष्परेणुः
पुष्परेणु m. (-णुः) The dust or farina of flowers.<BR> E. पुष्प, and रेणु dust.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=462-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्परोचन|पुष्परोचनः
पुष्परोचन m. (-नः) A plant, (Mesua ferrea.)<BR> E. पुष्प, and रोचन pleasing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=462-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पलक|पुष्पलकः
पुष्पलक m. (-कः) see पुष्यलक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=462-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पलाव|पुष्पलावः
पुष्पलाव m. (-वः) A flower-seller, a garland-maker.<BR>	 f. (-वी) A female<BR>flower-gatherer.<BR> E. पुष्प, and लाव who cuts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=462-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पलिक्ष|पुष्पलिक्षः
पुष्पलिक्ष m. (-क्षः) A bee.<BR> E. पुष्प a flower, लिह् to lick, स aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=462-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पलिह्
पुष्पलिह् m. (-लिट्) A large black bee.<BR> E. पुष्प, and लिह् to lick, क्विप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=462-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पवटुक
पुष्पवटुक m. (-कः) A gallant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=462-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पवत्|पुष्पवन्त्
पुष्पवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Having flowers, flowery.<BR>	 m. always dual.<BR>(-न्ती) The sun and moon.<BR>	 f. (-वती) A woman during menstruation.<BR>E. पुष्प a flower, or expansion as at rising, &c. and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=462-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पवन्त
पुष्पवन्त m. dual. (-न्ती) The sun and moon.<BR> E. पुष्प a flower, अव to<BR>prevent, झच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=462-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पवर्ष|पुष्पवर्षः
पुष्पवर्ष m. (-र्षः) A rain of flowers, flowers cast from heaven upon a<BR>hero or demigod, or on any great occasion.<BR> E. पुष्प, and वर्ष rain-<BR>ing; also पुष्पवर्षण, पुष्पवृष्टि, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=462-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पवाटिका
पुष्पवाटिका f. (-का) A flower-garden.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=462-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पवाटी
पुष्पवाटी f. (-टी) A flower-garden.<BR> E. पुष्प, and वाटी a garden.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=462-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पवृष्टि|पुष्पवृष्टिः
